inl zig_float_format () = Task ("ZIG-FLOAT-FORMAT", "Zig build time: std.fmt float printing adds ~0.4 s per program; a lean shortest-round-trip formatter matching the C oracle; 2026-10-10 measured on zig 0.17: the float arm is compiled only when a float is printed (an i32 print and a program that prints nothing both cold-build in about 9s; f32 and f64 cold-build in about 10-11s; a warm f64 after an i32 cache is about 2s). Printf still rejects a float argument, so no current program pays that cost. The printer is still unwritten.; 2026-10-13 18:05 Kino lane: Zig floats now print canonically (shortest round-trip via std.fmt {d}, .0 for integral values, NaN/Infinity/-Infinity) through sm'.show/format, asserted in sm' show_floats on zig; the build-time part (a lean formatter instead of std.fmt, ~0.4 s per program) is still open", TaskKind, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "backend,zig,performance", "current", "current")
