inl clean_generated_output () = Task ("CLEAN-GENERATED-OUTPUT", "Zero toolchain warnings and no comments in generated code across backends (Lean partial-def warnings suppressed by linters); 2026-10-08 13:3x measured C: the harness builds C with -w (all warnings suppressed); gcc -Wall -Wextra -fsyntax-only over the 208 committed main.c: 126 files warn (211 -Wunused-parameter, 180 -Wunused-but-set-variable); the 31 hard errors are expected (27 C-ABI samples linked with harness shims, 2 format_any lib arms deferred to the C compiler, 2 POSIX poll.h cube samples); fixes ((void)param for unused parameters, no set-but-unused temporaries) are in CodegenC = upstream section, so they go with COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION; then drop -w from the harness so warnings fail the native tier; 13:4x C -Wunused-parameter fixed: empty refcount bodies (ArrayDecrefBody, ClosureDecrefBody, heap DecrefBody) emit (void)x; (114 C outputs changed only by that line and one blank line; native unchanged); left: 180 -Wunused-but-set-variable (match results stored and never read: dead stores from peval, needs dead-store elimination), the // case comments on C switch labels (go with READABLE-GENERATED-NAMES); 18:4x fresh gcc -Wall -Wextra -fsyntax-only sweep over all 462 committed main.c: 382 clean, 31 hard errors (15 abi_external, 10 dynamic_array_growth/resize, the 2 format_any lib arms, the 2 POSIX cube samples, 2 native_managed_array_scc), 213 warnings in 49 files = 204 -Wunused-but-set-variable (was 180, new samples landed), 8 -Wunused-parameter, 1 -Wtautological-compare; two corrections to the record: the // case comments on C switch labels are gone (0 comment lines in the 462 main.c, and 0 across main.rs 402, main.pas 391, main.fsx 516, main.kt 246, main.swift 246, main.lean 135, main.wat 147, main.ts 117, main.lua 135, main.gleam 127, main.bend 120; the only comments left anywhere are the 11 main.zig build-header lines), and -Wunused-parameter is not fully fixed: the 8 remaining are closure body runtime parameters that the body never reads (closure_array v1, closure_depth v2, closure_heap v1, closure_mut v1, closure_return_heap v2, closure_return_text v2, method_depth v1, mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench_interned x), unlike the refcount bodies that already emit (void)x; the one -Wtautological-compare is ebpf_conv compiling its own m <= m source comparison (main.spi line 23), not a codegen defect; 19:4x fixed the closure-body half of the leftover: the C closure printer now void-casts exactly the domain arguments the body never reads (it collects the body's free variables once through the existing refc_used_vars walk and emits (void)vN; only for arguments absent from it), a three-line change in the shared CodegenC section that both cores build; the full-suite run single-flight-20261011-190603 regenerated the outputs with 7 files each gaining one (void)vN; line (closure_array v1, closure_depth v2, closure_heap v1, closure_mut v1, closure_return_heap v2, closure_return_text v2, method_depth v1) at 3774 jobs exit 0, native 2749 ran with 13 build-fail, oracle agree 2284, DISAGREE 0 and missing|regressed 0; re-sweeping the same 462 main.c gives 389 clean, 42 warning files, 206 warnings = 204 -Wunused-but-set-variable, the ebpf_conv tautological compare and 1 -Wunused-parameter, and that last one is the stale mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench_interned output that predates the 13:4x (void)x; fix (425 of 426 empty decref bodies carry it), and it did not clear in tonight's three full-suite runs: that sample is only in the suite as a Fsharp contracts job, its main.fsx refreshed at 20:47 with the same residual b00257ff342f6cce in rung 1 and in the restore, while its main.c still sits at 10-06 16:36, so no suite run regenerates its C file and clearing it needs a targeted C regeneration of that sample; 5 mega samples also drifted in that run (Rust impl Default blocks and the (v5)->refc++ parenthesization of earlier changes), pre-existing and benign; codegen proof ladder 2026-10-11 evening: rung 1 single-flight-20261011-190603, rung 2 hopac-20261011-195057, rung 3 the single-flight restore single-flight-20261011-204644, each 3774 jobs (contracts 669, examples 3052, frontier 48, mega 5), every run script exit 0 with native 2749 ran, 13 build-fail, oracle agree 2284, DISAGREE 0 and baseline missing|regressed 0; the restore reproduces rung 1 exactly, 0 of 3774 rows differ, so hopac left no residue behind and the void-cast fix reads back identically from both cores; across the cores 84 of 3774 rows differ and only in the emitted-text hash (83 rows over 32 samples and 13 backends, portable_math_rounding 11, portable_console_lines 11, portable_convert_parse 9) or in that one compile status (runaway_inline_match_recursion flips timeout in rung 1 to error under load in rung 2, non-ok in both), while compile, native, exit and stdout stay identical throughout; left: the 204 dead stores, which need dead-store elimination in peval; 2026-10-12: the gcc census used -fsyntax-only, which skips flow analysis: a real -O0 -c -Wall compile of 80 sampled main.c finds -Wreturn-type (control reaches end of non-void function) in 18 files, 42 of 48 warnings, from union switches whose cases all return; fix: the last case of a match with no fallback and one scrutinee is emitted as default (exhaustive in C, no builtin). Dead stores: new backend-agnostic DeadPureLetElision pass in CodegenUtils (backward liveness, drops TyLet of pure ops whose vars are dead, never Div/Mod/index/slice/macros/calls; memoized per body because RefcDecrTable keys statements by reference), applied to the main body and the CodegenAdapter method/closure bodies of both cores. Both unbuilt; verifier checks every changed output is a line subsequence of the old one; 2026-10-12 built and proven (single-flight-20261012-062458, 3,768 rows, DISAGREE 0, no regression): DeadPureLetElision + exhaustive default changed 268 rows, every one verified as a line deletion of the bless-time snapshot modulo the documented knock-ons (case->default relabel, (void)vN for a now-unused closure parameter, Gleam _v unused-parameter prefix, Delphi tmpN and Wasm $tN temp renumbering, blank-line placement); about 3,000 dead lines removed (C 1,199, Delphi 606, F# 535, Zig 554, Rust 298, TypeScript 96, Kotlin/Swift 46 each); gcc -O0 -c -Wall on the same 80-file sample: 48 warnings in 18 files -> 2 in 2 (-Wreturn-type gone, 2 dead stores the purity whitelist keeps); ladder single-flight-20261012-062458 / hopac-20261012-070019 / restore single-flight-20261012-080719: 3,768 rows each, 0 rows differ across cores or on restore (compile, residual hash, native, exit, stdout, oracle, baseline), DISAGREE 0; bless dev41 started 08:36 (main cache, then a reproduction pass); samples/string_ord joins the Wasm list (exit 0 like C, a $str_cmp forced to 0 exits 1); blessed dev41 2026-10-12 08:36 (single-flight-20261012-083637, 3,769 rows incl. the new string_ord Wasm row, agree 2,287, DISAGREE 0) with reproduction single-flight-20261012-090246: 0 of 3,769 rows differ, parity 3,769; 2026-10-12 compiler lane: Op.Dyn treated as pure, pureBlock/pureBranchingOp drop dead if/unbox/int-switch with pure branches; gcc -O0 -Wall set-but-unused over 464 main.c: 46 warnings in 12 files -> 31 in 2; remaining: folder_index_module macro let (won't fix: macro text opaque), omniledger runtime_native multi-destination let components (needs per-component rewrite) and single-variable chains kept live by something in the IR (next: IR dump); 2026-10-14 01:55 DeadPureLetElision now prunes dead components of multi-destination lets: a pure branching TyLet whose binder has some dead components keeps only the live ones in the binder and in every branch return (nested branch returns included), then re-elides the branches; mega_omniledger_erp_kernel/runtime_native gcc -O0 -Wall -Wextra warnings 29 -> 6; the 6 left are runtime_i64_add's raw C macro in the sample itself (opaque by design, like folder_index_module); outputs changed only on omniledger (F#, C, Rust, Delphi, Zig; native identical, stdout same); rung 1 single-flight-20261014-004129 clean; 2026-10-14 05:09 blessed with the Bend pack (single-flight-20261014-043715 reproduces rung 1, 0 of 4,094 differ); the pruning pass now elides each branch once (prune the unrewritten op, then rewrite) instead of twice, output-identical (proven by the bless reproduction); left: the two samples whose warnings come from their own raw C macros (folder_index_module, omniledger runtime_i64_add), opaque by design", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,codegen", "current", "current")
