inl spiral_independent () = Task ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", "Make spiral independent of polyglot, then split what remains of polyglot into descriptive repos; 2026-10-08: lib/spiral/*.fsx gone (FSX-FREE, spiral_runtime.fs instead), 4 compiler samples resolve their lib through spiral itself instead of deps/polyglot/deps/spiral (20 rows parity, residuals unchanged), apps/wasm builds natively on Windows; remaining polyglot mentions: env.ps1 and Kino core-package fallbacks (../polyglot), Kino polyglot_root option alias, docs; 23:2x dir-tree-html left spiral for its own repo; consumers reach it through spiral scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, not polyglot paths; 2026-10-12 inventory (code files only): what still ties spiral to polyglot is shallow, three steps: (1) naming: `namespace Polyglot` in spiral_compiler.fs, host Program.fs, runtime-compat PolyglotCommon.fs, RootNamespace in SpiralCompilerCore/SpiralCompiler fsproj and gear-dev.ps1, and two stack-trace filters matching \"Polyglot\" (spiral_compiler.fs ~133373, ~188068) -> rename to Spiral in one ladder; (2) consumers: dice and alphabet reach spiral as deps/polyglot/deps/spiral (init.ps1, package.spiproj packageDir, CI checkout) -> clone spiral directly as deps/spiral (mirror dice -> alphabet); (3) then drop the polyglot fallbacks: env.ps1:129-130 (VS Code Plugin core path), kino domain_compiler.ex:49, toolchain.ex:21, notebook.ex @lib_rels polyglot entries, kino.ex polyglot_root/SPIRAL_KINO_POLYGLOT_ROOT option; leave mentions in docs/history and the contract_*_polyglot_* sample names alone; step (2) is a multi-repo decision for the user: dice (and alphabet) use polyglot for far more than reaching spiral: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 in every build script, polyglot/lib/fsharp (Common.fs, Notebooks.livemd, open Polyglot), polyglot's parser app and init toolchains, polyglot/deps/hyperui css; cloning spiral directly in dice would leave two spiral copies (deps/spiral and polyglot/deps/spiral) unless polyglot stops vendoring spiral or the shared helpers move (core.ps1 into spiral or its own repo); step (1) and (3) can proceed independently; user decision 2026-10-12 19:05: once spiral no longer needs polyglot, split what remains into focused repos named for what they are and archive polyglot; 2026-10-13 22:59 the spiral-split gear splitter (scripts/gear-dev.ps1, bench-split.ps1, build-splitter.ps1, tmp/splitter, lanes/splitter) was removed at the user's request: idle since early October (234 runs Sep 26-Oct 1, then 21), built for gpt5parallel's 159k lines; use build.ps1 -Configuration Debug -CoreSource <copy> for candidates", Epic, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "", "repos,polyglot,main,lab-held,user-batch", "current", "current")
