and Delphi do run stack mutable layouts (native_layout_stack_mutable* exit 15), so their rejection of native_layout_stack_mutable_string_negative is the managed-string check behind a generic 'doesn't support stack mutable layout types' message; only C and F# lack stack_mut; after-bless scripts revised: wasm_fixture accepts the split exit only when both split runs exit cleanly, h2 drops only on a full bless (-Suite all, no -Filter), readme_apply writes a sample's edits only if all apply and keeps READMEs whose carrier is not live yet (needs h3 for abi_external_buffer_length_negative, expected_errors_check for the 6 ExpectedErrors samples); stacked on scratch copies: 117 READMEs deleted, harness parses, test.ps1 parses; 2026-10-14 03:40 lane 3: recursive_union_core.ps1 (recursive_union_multi_case gains packages: core-), brzozowski_negatives.ps1 (5 siblings re-export root names under root_*; 8 negatives reach their intended rejection: provisional texts; 30 ExpectedErrors entries; negative_antimirov_missing_finite_authority blocked: it needs the root prototype symbol_compare and the sibling at once), runbook %USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\after-bless\\RUNBOOK.md (11 ordered steps with dry-run, apply, verify filter and expected verdicts); all scripts stacked on a scratch tree: test.ps1 and matrix.psd1 parse, 36 ExpectedErrors entries; 2026-10-14 03:48 lane 3 revision: bend_arms and wasm_fixture now throw on a second apply (all after-bless scripts applied twice on a scratch tree: every second apply throws before writing or does nothing); readme_apply and brzozowski_negatives both add to an existing ExpectedErrors block, in either order (34 entries); brzozowski texts: 22 observed, skip_normalization and seal_unverified observed today, 4 provisional, the 2 negative_forge_* recorded after the first run; finding: antimirov_typed_slot_bound passes as its own row but lists 4 type errors in indexed_assignment.spi/injective_bound.spi when it is loaded as the depende