inl task_KINO_PARALLEL_CACHE () = Task ("KINO-PARALLEL-CACHE", "Kino stress notebook: N Spiral cells over one shared prefix run concurrently; measure per-cell compile time vs cold, require each cell's output identical to a single-cell run (catches cross-request state leaks like FRONTIER fix 57); if caching holds, migrate single-module samples to notebooks; 2026-10-08: Kino CompilerDaemon serializes every compile (GenServer handle_call -> one single-flight compiler process, warm after the first request), so concurrent cells queue instead of running in parallel; the experiment needs a compiler that serves parallel requests from one warm process, i.e. HOPAC-WARM-SERVER (fix 57: per-request join point state), then a daemon pool or async dispatch; 2026-10-08 17:0x unblocked differently: single-flight is warm-safe, so concurrency needs no hopac: a pool of K single-flight daemons (client-side, one port each); memory measured (tmp/kino-mem/warm-growth.ps1, one warm --batch process, 190 example compiles): ~530 MB after 189 compiles (~2.5 MB retained per compile), a single runaway sample (runaway_inline_match_recursion, FOR-D) spiked to 2 GB; the 5.5 GB Kino server seen this morning was a heavy compile's working set, not accumulated leaks; K=2-3 fits this 16 GB machine for normal cells; 17:4x implemented the pool: CompilerClient spreads compiles over SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILERS single-flight daemons (ports 13905..; default 1 = the old path exactly; least-busy pick through atomic ETS counters; ensure/retire/locks/logs per port; shutdown retires all); Kino tests 53/53; stress (tmp/kino-mem/stress.exs: 6 cells, fresh source copies, every daemon warmed first): pool 1 seq 16.9 s / par 9.4 s, pool 3 seq 17.5 s / par 6.7 s (1.4x over pool 1, 2.6x over sequential); outputs identical seq vs par and across pools; caches are per daemon (a repeated source is a cache hit only on the daemon that compiled it); cold daemon ~7 s first compile; 2026-10-14 01:16 lane 1 re-measure with today's daemon-side pool (one notebook = N cells over one shared prefix): lib/spiral/stream.spi (16 tests + prelude, host Rust, SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0, fresh daemon per config on private ports 13991-13994, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, through Invoke-Heavy, machine shared with other lanes): sequential (pool off, 1 cell) wall 420 s and 405 s on a repeat, warm compile median 3.4/2.6 s, cold first compile 28/55 s; 4 cells on one compiler wall 159 s (2.6x), compile median 5.6 s (+queue 128 s summed); 4 cells on pool 3 wall 144 s (2.9x over sequential, 1.1x over one compiler), compile median 3.9 s, cold first compile 21 s, each extra compiler pays its own cold prefix once; every config produced identical per-cell stdout and status (17/17 vs each other: no cross-request leak); the bottleneck in this notebook is the target build (rustc+run 162-205 s summed), not compile (50-90 s summed); next step unchanged: migrate single-module samples to notebooks, which belongs to the samples owner (main thread) since lanes must not touch apps/compiler/tmp/samples", Feature, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "HOPAC-WARM-SERVER,SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", "kino,compiler,cache,parallel", "current", "current")
