inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_10 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 10u32, "2026-10-19T18:20Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 14:20 toolchain resolver moved into eoie as src/workspace_primitives/toolchain.spi (module toolchain). Ported to eoie idiom: core-only unions (tool_source, tool_sources rec union instead of list, tool_found with NotFound instead of option), tool_probe record with string-or-empty fields, real probe as one-line host primitives (std::env::var, split_paths + EXE_SUFFIX, is_file), so the test blocks compile with plain rustc and no lib. Resolvers python_tool/cc_tool/rustc_tool keep main's order (option, env, PATH candidates). 4 test blocks 4/4; a mutated expectation fails 1/4. Registered in eoie_dev_spiral_tests (25 notebooks, regenerated +2 lines); the 10 workspace_primitives consumers stay byte-identical. Next: eoie tool-finding verbs wrap tool_resolved.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_11 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 11u32, "2026-10-19T18:21Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:21 lap 4 grain: the eoie lane ported the resolver into eoie/src/workspace_primitives/toolchain.spi (eoie packages cannot use lib, so lists became a recursive union and the PATH probe is std::env Rust; 4/4 tests, a mutated expectation fails 1/4, 10 consumer crates regenerate byte-identical); the untracked lab copy is removed Next: next primitive slice: processes with timeout and elapsed (the most repeated pwsh glue), designed in the same no-lib style")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_12 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 12u32, "2026-10-21T23:27Z", "main", "19:27 the 'processes with timeout and elapsed' slice already exists, in eoie (where this item's primitives moved on 10-19): rust_std_process/model.spi has elapsed_millis, and 'eoie job run|start <label> <timeout-ms> <program>' supervises a process tree with a timeout and reports elapsed_ms, exit and output sizes; main used them for every job today. So no new primitive is needed. What remains is migrating the repeated pwsh glue (Start-Process + WaitForExit + Stopwatch patterns in spiral's tmp/scripts and the lab) onto eoie job run, which is eoie-first work for the eoie lane (EOIE-JOBS). This item's next slice moves on to the next most repeated glue: file hashing (measured: Get-FileHash appears 56 times in 41 spiral/lab .ps1 scripts, mostly for 16-char hash stamps and copy verification).")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_13 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 13u32, "2026-10-22T09:22Z", "eoie", "05:22 groom: the premise 'eoie packages cannot use lib' (10-19 note) no longer holds: lib staging ships in release ABC and E/E2 put 113 packages on lib. The direction is now two-sided: generic primitives go INTO lib/spiral (tonight main added sm'.listed, trim_end_suffix, env try_get_environment_variable and command-line argument accessors, a process module; convert.try_convert already existed), and eoie keeps only an OS boundary package for what lib does not cover (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY note 7: 1500 host macros, 517 of them text ops that belong to sm'). Remaining lib candidates are listed there: total fs read/write variants. eoie's own workspace_primitives package becomes the boundary package or dissolves into lib.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_14 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 14u32, "2026-10-24T01:46Z", "main", "2026-10-23 21:46 main: user direction 2026-10-23 21:4x: 'eoie wasn't using lib or code, rewrote most of the stuff, we gotta take the primitives eoie advanced then move to lib what isn't there already, but careful with bloat'. Method per eoie primitive (workspace_primitives and the other boundary modules): (a) lib already has an equivalent -> eoie switches to it and the eoie copy is deleted; (b) generic and missing from lib -> it moves to lib in lib's layout (one home per concept, backend_switch or run_target arms, a lib test block); (c) eoie-specific -> it stays. Bloat guard: one function per concept, no thin aliases, no option flags that only one caller uses. The census table (primitive, verdict, lib target) goes in the next note before any move.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_15 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 15u32, "2026-10-24T04:53Z", "main", "2026-10-24 00:53 main: survey of eoie's generic primitives against lib (user 10-23: take the primitives eoie advanced, move to lib what isn't there, no bloat). SWITCH eoie to lib, which already has these: rust_std_string (contains/starts_with/ends_with/replace/trim/equals) to sm'; workspace_primitives byte_at/byte_find/byte_slice/byte_len to sm' index_of/slice/length; environment_value to env.get_environment_variable (env.spi:53); file_present to file_system.exists; ascii_lowercase to sm'.to_lower; unix_ms/ms_since to date_time.now; the 3 private JSON unescapers (agile_note_model, agile_task_inspection, eoie_memory_model) to json_scan.parse_string once JSON-UNICODE-ESCAPES lands; hash_integrity's sha256 to crypto.sha256. MOVE to lib (missing there, generic): (1) checked atomic file replace (workspace_primitives replace_file_checked: unique pending file, rename over the target, read back and compare) as file_system.replace_checked; (2) lexical path containment (rooted_path / rooted_path_problem) as file_system.is_within; (3) executable lookup on PATH (on_path / path_executable / tool_path, also eoie env pins F4) as env.find_on_path. Each moves with one lib test block, and eoie then calls the lib version (EOIE-LIB-REUSE).")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_16 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 16u32, "2026-10-24T04:58Z", "main", "2026-10-24 00:58 main: the 3 MOVE primitives are drafted as one lib slice, %TEMP%\\lib-fs-primitives\\apply.ps1 (dry run clean): file_system.replace_checked (pending file, rename over the target, readback compare), file_system.is_within (lexical containment on normalize_path output, separator-checked so a/bc is not under a/b), file_system.find_on_path (env PATH split by sm'.split_list, platform executable suffix, listm'.try_find over file_exists), each with a rust test block, written only against lib (no host macros). Held until x's normalize_path land on file_system.spi (concurrent-edit risk); x asked to ping. Then gate+land through the gate kit, and eoie switches its workspace_primitives copies to these (EOIE-LIB-REUSE).")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_17 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 17u32, "2026-10-28T10:29Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_18 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 18u32, "2026-10-31T21:25Z", "kit", "10-31 17:2x kit (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK repair): Paused -> Planned. The 10-28 pause was for silence only ('Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued'), the pattern the user rejected today: a pause needs a reason AND a resume condition. Its recorded next step still stands: check whether the remaining milestone shipped (now against the installed E14F1F0B, not TRAIN2c), close it with that evidence if so, otherwise size the remaining slice. Back in 'agile next' as ready work.")
inl note_of_workspace_primitives_lib_19 () = Note ("WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB", 19u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit: KIT-RUN-SPI n4 lists the pwsh-ergonomics gaps this library closes for script ports: spawn with pipes and exit codes, env write, globbing/path joins. These are the first primitives to finish, since every ps1 port needs them.")
inl task_PS1_TO_SPIRAL () = Task ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", "After HOPAC-SPEED reaches state of the art (user): rewrite each repo's .ps1 scripts (build, test, init, workflow) as Spiral programs compiled to Rust, living in their own repos, compiled and run through the spiral CLI, using WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB; no shelling out to pwsh or eoie; 2026-10-13 23:34 user decision: now waits on EOIE-ONE-CALL instead of HOPAC-SPEED (scripts become eoie one-call verbs / Spiral programs)", Epic, P0, D7, 17u32, Planned, "KIT-RUN-SPI", "scripts,spiral,repos,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ps1_to_spiral () = Planning ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", Minutes 4800u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_1 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:09Z", "lane-b", "status 2026-10-14: still waits on EOIE-ONE-CALL (0%, Planned). Baseline size: tracked .ps1 spiral 35 files/3360 lines, eoie 17/1748, polyglot 27/682, dice 13/428, alphabet 8/212, i574n.github 5/75 (6505 lines total)")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_2 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:49Z", "main-thread", "06:49 groom: recount 10-15, tracked .ps1: spiral 39 (35 at the 10-14 baseline), eoie 17, polyglot 27, dice 13, alphabet 8. The count is growing (new harness/zed/compiler scripts), the opposite of this item's goal, while EOIE-ONE-CALL stays at 0%. Kept P3; recount after EOIE-ONE-CALL lands.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_3 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 3u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: user 21:05: pwsh goes later for latency; the CI scripts drifted but can be revamped now that Fable is gone.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_4 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night inventory of own PowerShell (caches, vendor, deps, samples excluded): about 13,300 lines in 282 files: spiral 6,897 / 72, polyglot 2,520 / 131, eoie 1,832 / 19 (compiler-contracts test scripts are the largest), dice 1,056 / 26, alphabet 492 / 16, x 293 / 8, i574n.github 210 / 10.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_5 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:37Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:37 helper-lane lap 1: recount 10-19 (git ls-files *.ps1, samples excluded, non-blank lines): spiral 50 files / 4,439 lines (35 / 3,360 on 10-14), eoie 20 / 1,806, polyglot 27 / 678, dice 13 / 431, x 9 / 358, alphabet 8 / 212, i574n.github 5 / 82, blog 5 / 64, dir-tree-html 4 / 53. Growth is concentrated in spiral's harness: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts 20 files, scripts 11, formatter 5. Gates unchanged: EOIE-ONE-CALL Planned 0%, PIPELINES-GREEN Active 35%. Since the item cannot start, the useful prep is choosing the first port by size and churn: the tracked tree's smallest self-contained scripts are the blog and dir-tree-html wrappers (4-5 files each, under 65 lines), which only chain init/build/publish.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_6 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 6u32, "2026-10-19T13:23Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:23 helper-lane lap 2: sized the first port candidate against lib: dir-tree-html's scripts are build.ps1 19 lines, init.ps1 17, workflow.ps1 10, publish.ps1 7 (53 total). build.ps1 needs: run a process with cwd and env and a timeout (BuildSpiral, cargo build, the self-test exe) - lib runtime has execution_options + execute_with_options (Rust and F# arms); read cargo metadata JSON (lib json decode, now growing in CONVO-IN-SPIRAL); create a directory (file_system.create_dir_all), delete a file (file_delete), write text (write_all_text). Missing in lib file_system: copy a file, remove a directory tree, and file_exists as a plain path check (only directory_info_exists and path_buf_exists exist). So the port needs 2-3 small file_system primitives first (copy, remove_dir_all, exists over a string path); those are also the most common verbs across the 124 .ps1 files (Copy-Item, Remove-Item, Test-Path).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_7 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:54Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 10:54 helper-lane lap 3: ranked the primitives over the tracked corpus (git ls-files *.ps1 in 9 repos: 142 files, raw occurrence counts): Join-Path 791, Invoke-Block 221, Test-Path 201, Write-Host 145, Write-Output 132, Set-Location 119, New-Item 100, Split-Path 93, Remove-Item 82, Get-ChildItem 72, Resolve-Path 59, Copy-Item 49, Get-Content 46, Get-Date 44, ConvertFrom-Json 33, Set-Content 23, Push/Pop-Location 18 each, Select-String 16, ConvertTo-Json 11, Start-Process 8, Move-Item 5. Mapped onto lib/spiral file_system.spi (47 functions, 18 tests): already there - path join, path_buf_exists/is_dir/is_file, create_dir_all, path_buf_parent/file_name, walk_dir, read_all_text/write_all_text, rename, file_delete; console covers Write-*, runtime the process side of Invoke-Block, json the Json pair. Missing, in corpus order: set/get current directory (Set-Location 119 + Push/Pop 36), remove_dir_all (most of Remove-Item 82 is -Recurse -Force), a one-level read_dir (Get-ChildItem 72 is mostly non-recursive), canonicalize (Resolve-Path 59), copy_file (Copy-Item 49). Those five are the first lib slice (Rust std::env::set_current_dir, fs::remove_dir_all, fs::read_dir, fs::canonicalize, fs::copy), each with a Rust test block.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_8 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 8u32, "2026-10-19T15:36Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:36 helper-lane lap 4: drafted the five missing primitives in file_system.spi's own style (the !\\\\ emit operator with  and the !\\ expression form, resultm.result' over stream.io_error) as lab/PS1-TO-SPIRAL/file_system-addition.spi: remove_dir_all (std::fs::remove_dir_all), copy_file to path (std::fs::copy, returns bytes), canonicalize (std::fs::canonicalize to path_buf), set_current_dir and get_current_dir (std::env), and read_dir_names (one level, std::fs::read_dir mapped to file names as a vec of std strings). One rust test block covers four of them on a temp tree: create, write, copy (1 byte), list (2 names), canonicalize ok, remove_dir_all, directory_exists false. To append to lib file_system.spi after the core-switch freeze and run through its Cells gate; Rust arms only for now, other backends keep failing at their compilers as the existing rename/create_dir_all do.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_9 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 9u32, "2026-10-19T22:22Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:22 helper-lane lap 6: the five file_system primitives are in lib. lib/spiral/file_system.spi gains remove_dir_all, copy_file, canonicalize, set_current_dir/get_current_dir and read_dir_names (uncommitted, additive; staged as lab/PS1-TO-SPIRAL/file_system-addition.spi). The gate (lab/PS1-TO-SPIRAL/file_system-run.ps1, file_system-20261019-1817.log) passes 18 of 18 tests with failed_targets empty, including the new rust test block on a temp tree, and the change was kept. With these, the ps1 helpers that only move, copy, list and delete files can be ported. Next: pick the first ps1 to port (one that uses only these plus run).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_10 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 10u32, "2026-10-22T05:37Z", "main", "01:36 main: lab run outputs moved to the run cache, per the lab rule that run outputs never sit in lab: 2 file(s) (logs, notebooks, diffs, metrics/gate/timing TSVs) are now under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runs\\lab-outputs\\PS1-TO-SPIRAL\\ at the same relative paths, sha256 checked. Scripts and probes stay in lab/PS1-TO-SPIRAL until the item lands.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_11 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 11u32, "2026-10-22T06:47Z", "main", "02:47 main: lab drained. file_system-addition.spi is in lib/spiral/file_system.spi (remove_dir_all, copy_file, canonicalize, set_current_dir/get_current_dir, read_dir_names; its test block is in lib); file_system-run.ps1 drove that gate (18/18, log in the run cache). Folder deleted. Next as before: port the first ps1 that uses only these primitives plus run.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_12 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 12u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 5 12:19 (subagent): file_system-addition ready; landing needs a Cells gate (jobs held) -> next: gate then land | lap 7 19:54 (subagent): re-read: 5 primitives in lib -> next: port the first ps1 helper")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_13 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 13u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_14 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 14u32, "2026-10-31T20:57Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_15 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 15u32, "2026-10-31T22:13Z", "main", "10-31 18:13 main. USER 10-31 ~18:1x: 'we're also polluting the repos with dozens of ps1 scripts, my times of pre vibecoding didn't had that euphoria. and we have in the backlog planned to replace all pwsh with spiral some day, we're drifting my pal'. MEASURED: untracked .ps1/.py today: spiral 31 (apps/compiler/packs 24 appliers and pack tools; apps/cells/spi lib_land_queue, lib_land_window, lib_program_gate, model_metrics, node_cells_window_proof; apps/cells/priv/new_project/scripts gate.ps1 + probe.ps1) and i574n.github 50 (wipe-recovery 46 .py, spiral-independent 3 .py, profile-restore-drill-node.py). MAIN'S SHARE of the drift (10-30/31): the apps/cells/spi land/proof tools above plus cells_land_window.ps1 and drop_test_target.ps1, install-pack/install-when-clear, the scaffold's .ps1 templates, the spiral-independent .py moved into i574n.github, and apps/lisp/spl2spi.ps1 (a .py ported to PowerShell, when a Lisp-to-Spiral converter is the textbook Spiral program). RULE FROM NOW (memory spiral-first-tooling): no new .ps1 or .py tool in any repo; a new tool is Spiral (a kit command or a Spiral program run through Cells/spiral), and PowerShell appears only as a few lines of host glue that call it. ORDER for this item: (1) spl2spi -> Spiral (smallest, highest symbolic value); (2) main's apps/cells/spi tools -> kit commands; (3) the scaffold templates -> generated by a Spiral command, not .ps1 files; (4) pack appliers -> the compiler team, with ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_16 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 16u32, "2026-10-31T22:57Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 18:57 compiler: PORT-OR-ARCHIVE decisions for the compiler share (apps/compiler/packs now 22 untracked .ps1 after archiving 2 today, plus 4 new scripts). OWN DRIFT, counted honestly (memory spiral-first-tooling): today I ADDED scripts/matrix-add.ps1, scripts/profile-speedscope.ps1, scripts/upstream.ps1 (with Add-Type C#), runtime/make-corelib.ps1 (ports of 7 retired .py; A/B identical) and packs/predict-residuals.ps1, lib-gate-dll.ps1, delphi-heaptrc.ps1 (moved home from C:\\home\\data). Net: -7 .py, +7 .ps1. DECISIONS: (A) PORT to Spiral / kit commands, keep until ported: the pack pipeline (build-candidate, review-candidate, predict-residuals, install-pack, install-when-clear: one 'kit pack' verb family), measure-arms (+ its trace readers), lib-gate-dll, delphi-heaptrc, and the 4 new scripts (upstream needs SequenceMatcher in Spiral; matrix-add edits matrix.psd1, which should itself become Spiral data under SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS; profile-speedscope and make-corelib are small Spiral programs). (B) APPLIERS are per-pack data, not tools: each leaves under the packs lifecycle when its pack installs or is rejected. PACK-11's 4 (core-drop-gpt5parallel-remnants, missing-arm-guard-output, host-server-parent-exit, host-drop-build-deadline) leave at PACK-11's install; rust-mutual-tail-loops at the next pack; delphi-string-literal-index and hopacsota-p3-shard/-ivar wait on their items. ARCHIVED today as rejected: apply-delphi-arc-records (DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY n12: 'should not ship'), apply-hopacsota-deferred-validation (HOPACSOTA-P3 n60/n62: not adopted), archive 20261031-185026. Longer term the applier format itself should be a kit verb over data (anchor/new pairs), so a pack is data plus one generic tool. (C) main's files in packs/, main decides: apply-ccmr-det-root, apply-ccmr-sourcelink, apply-zig-export-pack, apply-zig-monotonicdelay-pack, alias-count-check, alternating-ab.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_17 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 17u32, "2026-10-31T23:03Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 19:0x tibia's port-or-move decisions (no new tibia .ps1 today; two edits: scripts/build.ps1 postable gate and analysis/pz-in-traces.ps1). (a) tibia repo, 26 .ps1 and 0 .py: scripts/ (build 140 lines, init, predict, publish, score, workflow), apps/*/build and map/run.ps1, live/*.ps1 (13), analysis/*.ps1 (4). Decision: PORT to Spiral programs under this item's plan when tibia resumes (tibia is parked; TIBIA n44). Order: the build/test runner first. analysis/: pz-in-traces.ps1 is already thin glue over kit table sequences; pc3, pc4 and pr12-secondary become kit verb calls when EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES n29's verbs exist, never ported as scripts. (b) spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_program_gate.ps1 (written today by tibia, moved out of i574n.github; about 65 lines of logic: copy lib, kit do, lib_gate, control and negative verdicts): PORT to a kit command (e.g. kit lib gate-program) under step (2) of this item; frozen until then, no new features. (c) i574n.github/scripts/recovered-drafts-census.ps1 (tibia, 10-30, wipe forensics): one-off recovery tooling. Decision: RETIRE (archive) once PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY closes; not ported. (d) i574n.github/scripts/tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 (resilience's, scheduled daily 05:20): thin glue around mariadb-dump.exe. Decision: MOVE to tibia/scripts, done by resilience together with its scheduled-task path. (e) tibia/postability/ (untracked x.json and tlds.txt copy): goes with POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE (n2: both readers, then select by name). No lab/ dir in tibia, i574n.github or spiral.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_18 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 18u32, "2026-10-31T23:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 19:09 fiscal: PORT-OR-DROP for the .ps1 fiscal added 10-31 (memory spiral-first-tooling): (1) fiscal/scripts/box-gate.ps1 = KEEP as thin glue (sets SPIRAL_* env and calls spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1; no logic). (2) fiscal/scripts/bring-generated-home.ps1 = DROP by folding into format-generated.ps1 as a -From mode (copy matching units, format, copy home); one script instead of two. (3) fiscal/scripts/en16931-terms.ps1 = PORT to Spiral: a fiscal src module that walks the VEFA structure XML with lib xml and emits canon/en16931-terms.json (it is real logic; build.ps1 then calls the Spiral test instead). (4) fiscal/scripts/delphi-reach.ps1 = PORT to Spiral or DROP when FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH closes (a survey; bounded lifetime). (5) i574n.github/scripts/lib-reanchor.ps1 = PORT to a kit command (kit reanchor beside kit do: merge-file --diff3 per hunk, name-heading rule, added-lines equality guard, rehearse); org-wide, kit team's. Nothing new will be added as .ps1 by fiscal from here; the scratchpad drivers (quiet-land, gate-files, regen-all) are session outputs, not tools.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_19 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 19u32, "2026-10-31T23:20Z", "kit", "10-31 19:2x kit: PORT-OR-DROP for kit's repo-local scripts (kit/scripts 14 .ps1, repo root 4 .ps1, 0 .py anywhere in kit). OWN DRIFT, counted honestly (memory spiral-first-tooling): today I ADDED scripts/candidate-build.ps1, notebook-batch.ps1, regen-sizes.ps1, train-hold.ps1, resume-train-if-starved.ps1 and moved node-kit-switch.ps1 in from C:\\home\\data; launch-train/release-train/release-acceptance grew. That is +5 new .ps1 in a repo whose own product is the Spiral CLI meant to replace them. DECISIONS: (A) PORT to kit verbs, in this order: (1) the release-train family (release-train 248 lines, release-acceptance 138, launch-train, resume-train-if-starved) -> one 'kit train' verb family (start/resume --if-starved/accept), kit's largest pwsh logic and the one that keeps growing; (2) train-hold -> DROP into 'kit window' (holds are windows already; the train reads the window instead of a hold file); (3) notebook-batch + regen-sizes + candidate-build -> 'kit notebook batch' and 'kit regen --preview/--candidate'; notebook-test folds into notebook-batch at once (one script, a single module is a batch of one); (4) lib-reanchor (handed to kit by fiscal n18) -> 'kit reanchor' beside kit do. (B) KEEP as thin repo-runner glue until this item's shared repo-runner Spiral program exists (port once for all repos, not per repo): build.ps1, dev.ps1, spiral.ps1, scripts/init, workflow, publish, user-env. Frozen: no new features. (C) node-kit-switch.ps1: frozen glue for the user-only quiet-window switch; becomes 'kit node switch' with (A)(3). (D) DROP eoie.ps1 (pre-rename forwarder to kit.exe): archive it after a stem grep over sibling repos finds no caller (memory dangling-check-by-stem). Nothing new will be added as .ps1 by kit from here; tonight's lint baseline work went into kit commands (lint macros --write-baseline), not a script.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_20 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 20u32, "2026-11-01T04:31Z", "x", "2026-11-01 00:30 x: x's count is 24 .ps1 and 0 .py (git ls-files incl. untracked; 2,172 lines). First three ports, by lines retired per unit of risk:\n(1) scripts/postable-report.ps1 (40) plus i574n.github/scripts/x-compat-census.ps1 become one Spiral 'xc postable census' subcommand in the x client (ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME n5(2)), resuming POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS.\n(2) apps/client/e2e/stub.ps1 (365) and stub_http.ps1 (50) RETIRE rather than port. Since x-parity-typed2/3 the Spiral sim answers all 153 tutorial requests with byte-equal request logs, so e2e's default server becomes the sim. The parity proofs are the record. e2e-parity.ps1 (31) retires with them. social_stub.ps1 (Mastodon/Bluesky) stays until the sim serves those transports.\n(3) scripts/gleam-modules.ps1 (133, splits generated Gleam into parts under 1,000 lines) and gleam-compact-census.ps1 (17) are generic, so they become a kit verb or a compiler emit option, owned by kit or compiler. I'll file the request there.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_21 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 21u32, "2026-11-01T04:31Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 tibia count: 27 .ps1/.py in tibia (excluding deps; 0 .py). FIRST THREE TO PORT: (1) scripts/build.ps1 (the test runner and CI entry: layout, cell budget, per-file Cells runs, problem report), as a Spiral program run through the spiral CLI; (2) scripts/predict.ps1 (the predict-sweep driver); (3) live/run-policy-scenario.ps1 (187 lines, the biggest live driver). analysis/ ports to kit verb calls (n17).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_22 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 22u32, "2026-11-01T04:35Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 00:35 compiler, round-2 groom: COMPILER CENSUS (apps/compiler): 107 .ps1 (41 scripts/, 38 tmp/scripts/, 18 packs/, 7 tmp/formatter, 1 in a sample); 906 .py, of which 902 are generated Python-backend sample outputs (main.py, not tools) and 4 are tools: runtime/corelib.py (46 lines), tmp/tests/native-shims/openqasm-run/run.py (1502), cpp_native.py (64), run_main.py (25). FIRST THREE PORTS, in dependency order: (1) scripts/env.ps1 (172 lines, dot-sourced by every other script: the dotnet/DLL/package-dir resolvers become one Spiral module the others import); (2) scripts/build.ps1 (214); (3) scripts/test.ps1 (1175, the big one; split by mode, matrix first). The 4 tool .py are no-py violations: openqasm-run/run.py is PORT (real logic), the other three are DROP or fold into the Spiral test runner.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_23 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 23u32, "2026-11-01T04:36Z", "kit", "11-01 00:3x kit, SCRIPT-LIKE SPIRAL design (user 00:2x via main: run Spiral files like C# top-level code, or one test cell by name from the CLI, to start rewriting the .ps1 'disease' now). kit has the parts, not the verb: Cells runs a .spi as a notebook and already selects test cells by name (lib_gate -Test a,b; '///- --test --symbol' cell headers); the compiler builds Rust from a file. DESIGN: 'kit run <file.spi> [-- args]' = compile the file's top-level code (an implicit main, pinned to the Rust backend: memory notebook-main-default-zig) through the installed compiler in process mode, cache the binary by content hash of the file plus its package closure under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\run-cache, then exec it with the args and its exit code; a second run with no change is an exe start (no compile). 'kit run <file.spi> --test <name>[,name]' runs only those test blocks through the Cells runner (no notebook HTML), printing pass/fail per test, exit nonzero on any failure; '--list' prints the test names. Env/args reach Spiral via env.command_line_argument* (exists). This makes a .ps1 port a .spi file plus a 1-line 'kit run' shim, so ports can start before every helper is a kit verb. FIRST THREE KIT PORTS (kit has 44 .ps1, 0 .py: compiler-contracts 23, scripts 13, infra 7 (iggy), root 3 minus tonight's 2 deletions): (1) scripts/train-hold.ps1 -> dropped into 'kit window announce' (EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE, P0, top of kit's queue); (2) scripts/notebook-batch.ps1 -> 'kit run --test' over modules (the batch becomes a loop in Spiral); (3) scripts/regen-sizes.ps1 + candidate-build.ps1 -> 'kit regen --preview|--candidate'. The release-train family (largest) follows once kit run and kit window announce exist. Filed as the item KIT-RUN-SPI below.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_24 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 24u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "main", "main 00:4x THE PLAN (user 11-01 00:2x: 'gotta plan the ps1 rewrites once and for all, that became a disease... now we gotta do it out of dogfeeding needs, even if we flood the repos with poopy spiral code'). CENSUS tonight, tracked+untracked outside deps/target: 473 .ps1 and 1,328 .py in the i574n/fc1943s repos. The .py are mostly not ours to port: 902 are generated Python-backend sample outputs (keep, they're compiler outputs) and 390 are upstream The-Spiral-Language (leave). Real .py tools: apps/compiler 4 (openqasm-run/run.py 1,502 lines), apps/spiral/test_json_protocol.py, tictactoe 13, singularity 5, i574n.github 4, polyglot 3, dice 2, dotfiles 2, kit/fiscal/x/tibia 0. .ps1 by repo: spiral 151 (apps/compiler/tmp 47, compiler/scripts 41, cells/spi 18, packs 18), i574n.github 53, kit 44, polyglot 27, tibia 27, x 24, fiscal 17, dice 13, tictactoe 10, dotfiles 7, blog 7, rest small. PHASES. P0, tonight: KIT-RUN-SPI ('kit run file.spi -- args', '--test a,b', '--list'; kit n23) is the vehicle; nothing ports before it runs one real script. P1, ratchet: kit standards counts .ps1+.py per repo and fails on any increase (SPIRAL-FIRST-TOOLING memory made enforceable). P2, the dot-sourced cores every script loads: spiral apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1, x scripts/common.ps1, polyglot core.ps1 and lib/spiral/lib.ps1 become Spiral modules, with each .ps1 a one-line shim. P3, per lane, biggest first, each lane's first three already named (x n20, kit: train-hold/notebook-batch/regen, compiler: env/build/test). P4, the .py tools. Done means count 0 except one-line shims. Metric per round: .ps1 and .py count and lines per repo, on this item.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_25 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 25u32, "2026-11-01T04:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:12 fiscal: FISCAL COUNT: 17 tracked .ps1 (about 1,650 lines; init 773, build 136, pattern-examples 110, schxslt-to-schematron 99, family-gates 84, delphi-reach 76, pattern-oracle 51, en16931-terms 48, validate-manifests 46, resolve-check 46, bench/compare-roundtrip 45, format-generated 35, validate-example 32, bring-generated-home 25, box-gate 23, bench/acbr/build 14, publish 3), 0 .py. FIRST THREE PORTS: (1) en16931-terms.ps1 -> a Spiral cell in src (lib xml walk + json write; pure transform, already run by build.ps1, output canon/en16931-terms.json); (2) family-gates.ps1's family -> schema table -> typed rows emitted from generator.spi's family_roots (the schema_path already lives there, so the duplicate PowerShell table and its drift go away; the .NET XmlSchema call stays as the external oracle); (3) format-generated.ps1 + bring-generated-home.ps1 -> one generic kit command \"format with a content-hash cache\" (generic-tools rule; tibia/x can use it too). init.ps1 (773) is last: mostly pinned downloads, which become a typed source list once the Spiral fetch primitive exists.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_26 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 26u32, "2026-11-01T04:51Z", "main", "main 00:5x: dep PIPELINES-GREEN (Blocked) -> KIT-RUN-SPI. With every dep Blocked, 'agile next' never offered this P0, one reason the .ps1 disease outgrew the plan. Porting scripts doesn't need green pipelines; it needs 'kit run' (kit n23).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_27 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 27u32, "2026-11-01T05:37Z", "kit", "11-01 01:5x kit, requirement for the (A)(3) port 'kit regen --preview|--candidate': resolve every named package to its regen OWNER before regenerating (a module-only package like agile_state_runtime belongs to kit_agile_state; kit_lint_model to kit_lint_walk/kit_lint_macros). Tonight candidate-build.ps1 refused a module-only name twice ('Unknown KIT package ...'), costing a node round each. The owner graph already exists in the package.spiproj files; the verb should also accept 'changed since <ref>' and compute the owner set itself, which removes the hand-kept 34-name list.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_28 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 28u32, "2026-11-01T06:18Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 02:18 tibia, PORT PLAN for scripts/build.ps1 (146 lines, port 1 of 3). Five stages: (a) discovery = list src + 6 app dirs, keep files with a '^(test|:#) ' line, -Files/-Exclude/-Resume filters; (b) cell-budget gate = run mix spiral.cell_budget, parse the 'cell-budget report:' line, fail on over_budget; (c) per-file Cells run with a 60 s heartbeat; (d) parse 'spiral-tests total {json}' into a summary record and decide the problem line (failed/unsupported/skipped/not_run/missing); (e) writers: files/tests/wgsl .tsv, tibia.prom (added tonight, TIBIA-RUN-METRICS), GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY. ORDER: (d), (e), the budget-line parse and the (a) filters are PURE string -> record functions, so they port NOW as a Cells-tested module apps/build/build.spi (in build.ps1's own source list, so the port tests itself on every run, rust + lua) with typed rows (file_row, test_row, wgsl_row, budget_kind) per typefeatureset. That shrinks build.ps1 to process glue only. The process half, (b) and (c) (spawn with cwd, env, stdout redirect, wait-with-timeout, Get-Load), waits on KIT-RUN-SPI (Planned 0) plus lib process; then build.ps1 becomes a one-line 'kit run apps/build/build.spi -- @args' shim. machine.tsv (CIM/procfs) goes last or is dropped in favour of the runner's own env. Done = build.ps1 is a shim, CI green on Windows + Linux, and the .ps1 count for tibia drops 27 -> 26. Next step (CPU-light, next hour): write the (d) parser + problem decision with 4 tests (green, failed, missing, no total line).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_29 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 29u32, "2026-11-01T06:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:27 fiscal: PORT 1 DRAFTED (en16931-terms.ps1 -> Spiral). Two pieces. (a) LIB PRIMITIVE: the lib had a JSON reader (json_schema json_value/read_json) but no writer, so json_text (with json_quoted/json_escaped and a mutual-recursion json_items/json_members group) is drafted on a scratch copy of json_schema.spi (base 54CFD0B274C4B7FF), with test json_text_writes_what_read_json_reads_back. Formatter-stable; node gate job-1793514148429-fiscal-p10-json-writer on its own lib copy. (b) FISCAL MODULE: scratchpad canon-port/canon.spi (4E7B7096, parses; formatter re-laid 3 lines) mirrors the PowerShell walker: VEFA Structure -> Document -> Element/Include recursion; first occurrence wins an id's fields; the per-document UBL path is replaced in place on a repeat (ordered-dict semantics); names split per id when the counts match; terms before groups by numeric id (BT-1 first, BG-32 last, as the PS output); the test writes canon/en16931-terms.json and requires 160 terms / 30 groups (the PS output's counts). NEXT: land (a) on green, add canon to src/package.spiproj modules, gate canon.spi, compare its JSON with the PS output field by field (ConvertFrom-Json), then build.ps1 drops the en16931-terms.ps1 call and the script is archived.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_30 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 30u32, "2026-11-01T06:32Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 02:3x (resilience) New port target for this item: the resilience MIRROR glue. i574n.github\\scripts holds profile-mirror.ps1, register-scheduled-tasks.ps1, config-baseline.ps1, profile-restore-drill.ps1 - the backup layer, all pwsh with real logic. A new kit-archive daily mirror was about to add a 5th; stopped (write hook). PROPOSE a generic kit command \"mirror a directory off-box incrementally\" (mtime-delta tar+scp, node route-fallback, size+tar-count verify, stamp file) that subsumes the kit-archive daily job now and the profile-mirror / restore-drill glue over time, leaving only a thin scheduled-task shell. Keeps the backup logic in Spiral/kit, not in dozens of .ps1. Owner resilience (backup infra); sequence after KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR's one-shot seed.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_31 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 31u32, "2026-11-01T06:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:37 fiscal: JSON WRITER GREEN on the node (job-1793514148429, own lib copy, pack 10): json_schema.spi 8/8 passed, type errors 0, including json_text_writes_what_read_json_reads_back. LAND with land-lib-program.ps1 -Note PS1-TO-SPIRAL/<this n> -File json_schema.spi -Base 54CFD0B274C4B7FF -Target 3F3413B5...; then gate canon.spi (port 1) against it.\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit json_schema.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -94,6 +94,50 @@\n     := value, _ = json_value_at s 0i32\n     value\n \n+:= json_escaped (c : string) : string =\n+    ? c = \"\\\"\" ?> \"\\\\\\\"\"\n+    |? c = \"\\\\\" ?> \"\\\\\\\\\"\n+    |? c = \"\\n\" ?> \"\\\\n\"\n+    |? c = \"\\r\" ?> \"\\\\r\"\n+    |? c = \"\\t\" ?> \"\\\\t\"\n+    |: c\n+\n+:~ ^ json_quoted_from (s : string) (pos : i32) (acc : string) : string =\n+    ? pos >= sm'.length s ?> acc |: json_quoted_from s (pos + 1i32) (acc ++# json_escaped (char_at s pos))\n+\n+:= json_quoted (s : string) : string = \"\\\"\" ++# json_quoted_from s 0i32 \"\" ++# \"\\\"\"\n+\n+:~ ^ json_text (value : json_value) : string =\n+    ?= value ?|\n+    | JsonNull => \"null\"\n+    | JsonBool b => ? b ?> \"true\" |: \"false\"\n+    | JsonNumber n => n\n+    | JsonText t => json_quoted t\n+    | JsonArray items => \"[\" ++# json_items items \"\" ++# \"]\"\n+    | JsonObject members => \"{\" ++# json_members members \"\" ++# \"}\"\n+\n+:& :~ json_items (items : list json_value) (acc : string) : string =\n+    ?= items ?|\n+    | x :: [] => acc ++# json_text x\n+    | x :: rest => json_items rest (acc ++# json_text x ++# \",\")\n+    | [] => acc\n+\n+:& :~ json_members (members : list (string * json_value)) (acc : string) : string =\n+    ?= members ?|\n+    | (key, x) :: [] => acc ++# json_quoted key ++# \":\" ++# json_text x\n+    | (key, x) :: rest => json_members rest (acc ++# json_quoted key ++# \":\" ++# json_text x ++# \",\")\n+    | [] => acc\n+\n+///> rust\n+test json_text_writes_what_read_json_reads_back =\n+    := value =\n+        JsonObject [\n+            (\"text\", JsonText \"a \\\"quoted\\\" back\\\\slash\\nnew line\"); (\"number\", JsonNumber \"12.5\")\n+            (\"list\", JsonArray [ JsonBool !+; JsonNull; JsonArray [] ]); (\"empty\", JsonObject [])\n+        ]\n+    ? read_json (json_text value) <> value ?> failwith \"json_text writes what read_json reads back\"\n+    ? json_text (JsonArray [ JsonNumber \"1\"; JsonText \"x\" ]) <> \"[1,\\\"x\\\"]\" ?> failwith \"a compact array\"\n+\n :~ ^ member (key : string) (members : list (string * json_value)) : option json_value =\n     ?= members ?|\n     | (name, value) :: rest => ? name = key ?> Some value |: member key rest\n>>>")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_32 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 32u32, "2026-11-01T06:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:52 fiscal: PORT 2 VERIFIED VIABLE (family-gates.ps1 table -> generator rows): all 27 module -> schema rows of family-gates.ps1 ($examples + $resolved) name a schema file that src/generator.spi's family_roots already holds, so the PowerShell table is pure duplication of generator data. PLAN: the generator writes a typed manifest of (module, sample, schema, preload, resolve) rows next to its units (a JSON file through json_schema.json_text once the writer lands, PS1-TO-SPIRAL n31); family-gates.ps1 shrinks to \"for each row, run validate-example\" and later becomes a Spiral cell. Per-family preload/resolve flags become family_root data (e.g. an extras case for own-signature-import like CL DTE).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_33 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 33u32, "2026-11-01T06:51Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 02:51 tibia, build.ps1 port SLICE 1 GREEN (in the tree, unstaged): apps/suite/suite.spi, stage (d) of n28. It holds typed totals = { ran : {discovered, executed, passed, failed}; held : {statics, unsupported, skipped, not_run} }, read with lib json_scan::value_at/parse_i32 (depth-aware keys, so failed_targets never matches 'failed'), plus not_executed, green, problem_of and missing_total, which produce build.ps1's exact problem strings. 4 tests, pinned ///> lua + ///> rust (unpinned they ran on Zig only, the main-defaults-to-Zig trap): 8 of 8 passed through build.ps1 -Files suite (179 s); apps/suite is in build.ps1's own source list, so the port gates itself every run. Lessons: (1) the cell budget flagged 4 of my first definitions; I split the record into ran/held halves and moved long strings into fixtures; (2) '{ base ?| ran = { base::ran ?| ... } }' mis-types (the inner subject must be a plain variable; bind 'r = base::ran' first). NEXT: stage (e), the .tsv/.prom writers as pure row -> line functions, then build.ps1 calls the module for (d)+(e) once KIT-RUN-SPI exists.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_34 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 34u32, "2026-11-01T06:57Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 02:57 tibia, build.ps1 port SLICE 2 started: stage (e)'s first writer, prom_label + prom_line in apps/suite/suite.spi, with the test a_budget_kind_becomes_one_prom_line (lua + rust). build.ps1 -Files suite: 5 of 5 passed (the new test executed, 4 memo hits). Next: the file/test row writers, then build.ps1's .prom block calls the module.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_35 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 35u32, "2026-11-01T06:57Z", "x", "2026-11-01 02:57 x: port 2 (retire stub.ps1) is GATED by a measurement (X-RUN-METRICS n7): e2e against the sim takes 367 s vs 133 s against the stub on identical traffic (parity 0 differing). Retiring the stub now would add ~234 s per e2e. Order: first make the sim's serve launch lean (sim-run.ps1 does a Cells mix build that sim_serve doesn't need; n7's rule), then retire stub.ps1, stub_http.ps1 and e2e-parity.ps1.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_36 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 36u32, "2026-11-01T07:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 03:06 fiscal: json_text LANDED: json_schema.spi 54CFD0B2 -> 3F3413B5979D239E at 03:05:19 (1 replacement at line 94; undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\PS1-TO-SPIRAL-n31). It took 6 attempts with the event-driven retry: 5 refusals from erl readers and three compiler heavy-build windows (pack12a-predict2, pack12b-build, pack12b-predict), each waited on with kit job wait / Wait-Process, no polling. NEXT for port 1: write canon.spi in the edition-3 spelling once the fiscal respell lands (the t1101 overlay is edition 3, so an edition-2 module cannot join that package), add it to src package modules, gate it, compare its JSON with the PowerShell output field by field, then drop en16931-terms.ps1 from build.ps1.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_37 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 37u32, "2026-11-01T07:25Z", "x", "2026-11-01 03:25 x: port 2 UNBLOCKED by measurement (X-RUN-METRICS n8). With the lean serve launch, e2e against the sim takes 105 s vs 124 s against the stub, at parity (153/153, 0 differing). Retiring stub.ps1 and stub_http.ps1 now costs nothing and saves ~19 s per e2e. Next: e2e.ps1 defaults to the sim, the stub path and e2e-parity.ps1 are archived after one last parity record, and social_stub.ps1 stays (Mastodon and Bluesky aren't served by the sim). Proof gate: one verify with the sim as e2e's default server, exit 0.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_38 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 38u32, "2026-11-01T07:26Z", "x", "2026-11-01 03:26 x: STUB RETIREMENT PLAN (port 2), checked against the tree:\n(1) e2e.ps1:56/59 picks the stub unless XSIM_SERVER=sim. Flip it: the sim by default, the stub only for XSIM_SERVER=stub, with a 60 s start wait for both now that serve is lean (105 s total e2e).\n(2) ORDER DEPENDENCY: scripts/build.ps1 and verify.ps1 build the client BEFORE the sim, but a sim-served e2e needs the frames build (sim-run.ps1 throws without it). The sim build has no reference to client outputs (no xc.exe, cargo or client build.ps1), so reorder to sim first, then client, in build.ps1 and in verify's plain path. verify's -Accept path already runs sim accept first.\n(3) e2e-parity.ps1 sets XSIM_SERVER='stub' explicitly for its stub arm. It keeps one final parity record, then archives with stub.ps1 and stub_http.ps1 (social_stub.ps1 stays).\n(4) Proof: pack into verify45 (X-RESPELL-SYMBOLS' batch). Pass rule addition, written now: client e2e passes against the sim as default, and the stub arm of one last e2e-parity gives 0 differing rows.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_39 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 39u32, "2026-11-01T07:55Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 03:55 tibia, build.ps1 port SLICE 3 GREEN: apps/suite/suite.spi gains typed file_row {source, tenths, exit_code} and test_row {source, case_name, target, status, ms, memo} plus their writers, file_seconds_line, file_exit_line and test_ms_line (outcome_labels split out for the cell budget). Seconds are integer tenths rendered by '/ 10' and '% 10', because Lua and Rust print whole floats differently (130.0 vs 130); an i32 keeps the .prom line byte-identical across backends. 7 of 7 passed on lua + rust through build.ps1 -Files suite. Stages (d)+(e) are now fully modelled in Spiral. What remains is process glue: (a) discovery, (b) the mix call, (c) the per-file Cells spawn and the .tsv/.prom file writes. Those need KIT-RUN-SPI to run the module as a program.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_40 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 40u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "main", "main 08:3x TYPEFEATURESET RULE for every port, so ports don't come out as stringly scripts in Spiral clothing: command-line arguments parsed into a record (lib cli_args), never positional strings; external commands as a union of known tools with typed results; outcomes as a union (Ok of value | Failed of error union), not exit-code integers or -1; file paths through lib file_system types; every report line produced from typed rows (tibia's suite.spi is the first good example: typed totals via json_scan, a prom line writer). DoD per port: the .ps1 becomes a one-line shim calling 'kit run <file.spi>' (KIT-RUN-SPI) and its caller's output is byte-identical on a recorded run.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_41 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 41u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 08:37 tibia QUALITY PASS on the build.ps1 port (apps/suite/suite.spi). SELF-CRITIQUE of slices 1-3: (a) 'green : totals -> bool' plus 'problem_of : ... -> string' plus 'missing_total : ... -> string' is boolean blindness plus stringly results; the caller has to know which string means what. (b) The budget gate is still parsed in PowerShell by regex (': over_budget:'). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN for slice 4: (1) ':| file_verdict = | Green of totals | NotGreen of totals * list test_name | NoTotal of exit_code', with ONE renderer 'verdict_line' producing build.ps1's exact strings; green/problem_of/missing_total become private to it; (2) ':| budget_finding = | OverBudget of location * weight * limit | Autolink of location * text | Mention of location * text' decoded from the cell-budget lines into a typed list, with location = { path; line; column } and weight/limit reusing quantity's phantom 'amount' style instead of bare i32; the gate decision is 'any OverBudget'; (3) run_result as the existential of the per-file pipeline (discovered source -> notebook run -> verdict), so stage (c) can be typed before KIT-RUN-SPI exists; (4) the .prom writers move onto TIBIA-RUN-METRICS' series GADT (plan in its n3). DEFINITION OF DONE for slice 4: build.ps1 -Files suite green with tests for all 3 verdict cases and the 3 budget_finding kinds decoded from real report lines (copied from tonight's output), lua + rust, and build.ps1's problem strings unchanged (byte-compare against the 02:4x CI log's problem list). NEXT STEP: add file_verdict and verdict_line to suite.spi, and rewrite the 4 existing tests to assert on verdicts.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_42 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 42u32, "2026-11-01T13:13Z", "x", "2026-11-01 09:12 x: port 2, FIRST HALF PROVEN. verify46 ran the client e2e against the sim as the default server (153 requests) inside the green client build, with the sim built before the client. Second half next: one final stub-vs-sim parity record, then archive stub.ps1, stub_http.ps1 and e2e-parity.ps1 (social_stub.ps1 stays).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_43 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 43u32, "2026-11-01T14:36Z", "x", "2026-11-01 10:36 x: PORT QUEUE for x's 24 .ps1 through KIT-RUN-SPI (Active 30%; 'kit run file.spi -- args', cached Rust build), ordered to start the day it lands. Each port is one slice <= 60 min, with the same DoD: the .spi script reproduces the .ps1's output on the same inputs, then the .ps1 is archived.\n- RETIRE, no port needed: apps/client/e2e/stub.ps1 + stub_http.ps1 + scripts/e2e-parity.ps1 (the sim replaces them; CELLS-IN-SPIRAL slice plan S1).\n- PORT to xc subcommands (Spiral already, no kit run needed): postable-report.ps1 (S2/S3 census), plus i574n.github x-compat-census.ps1.\n- PORT via kit run, in this order: (1) scripts/gate.ps1 (65 lines: line and width gates, pure file walking, the best first fit); (2) scripts/actions-lock.ps1 (29); (3) scripts/sim-shell.ps1 (39); (4) scripts/cargo-profile-*.ps1 x3 (bench drivers); (5) gleam-compact-census.ps1 (17).\n- MOVE to compiler/kit verbs (GLEAM-PARTS-EMIT): scripts/gleam-modules.ps1.\n- STAY as thin glue until their hosts port: build.ps1, init.ps1, workflow.ps1, publish.ps1 (CI entry points, ~55 lines together), common.ps1 (shared helpers, shrinks as callers port), sim-run.ps1, node-run.ps1, verify.ps1, apps/*/build.ps1, e2e.ps1, social_stub.ps1.\nTYPEFEATURESET for each port: arguments as a typed record parsed by lib cli_args (x's own sim_args flag_rules o GADT is the model), results as unions, and no exit-code integers before main. A gate finding is a ':| finding = OverWidth ... | OverLines ...' union, not a formatted string.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_44 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 44u32, "2026-11-01T14:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:47 fiscal: FISCAL SHARE, PER-FILE DISPOSITION (all 17 tracked .ps1; 0 .py). Order = value / effort.\nSPIRAL (fiscal src, typed data):\n1. scripts/en16931-terms.ps1 (48) -> src/canon.spi: drafted; json_text landed; gate after the e3 commit (FISCAL-CANON-MODEL).\n2. scripts/family-gates.ps1 (84) -> rows emitted by the generator from the family manifest (FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST); the .NET XmlSchemaSet call stays as the external oracle.\n3. scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 (51) + scripts/pattern-examples.ps1 (110) -> the probe set and corpus list become a Spiral module; the .NET Regex oracle stays external (it IS the oracle), so the port is the data side only.\n4. scripts/resolve-check.ps1 (46) -> same: the corpus walk in Spiral, XmlSchemaSet stays external.\n5. scripts/schxslt-to-schematron.ps1 (99) -> lib schematron (a compiled-XSLT reader already exists: read_compiled_schematron); move the remaining conversion there.\n6. scripts/validate-manifests.ps1 (46) -> folded into the manifest reader's own validation.\nKIT COMMANDS (generic, other lanes reuse):\n7. scripts/format-generated.ps1 (35) + scripts/bring-generated-home.ps1 (25) -> one kit command \"format with a content-hash cache\".\n8. scripts/box-gate.ps1 (23) -> already a thin wrapper over lib_gate.ps1; becomes a kit gate preset.\n9. scripts/delphi-reach.ps1 (76) -> a kit \"backend reach\" report over any lib.\nSTAYS GLUE (reason recorded):\n10. scripts/build.ps1 (136): the CI entry; shrinks as 1-6 move, keeps only the order of steps.\n11. scripts/init.ps1 (773): pinned downloads; becomes a loop over the manifest's pinned sources (FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST) once a Spiral fetch primitive with sha256 pinning exists.\n12. scripts/publish.ps1 (3): one call to publish-tree.\n13. scripts/validate-example.ps1 (32): the .NET XmlSchemaSet oracle itself (external by design).\n14-15. bench/compare-roundtrip.ps1 (45), bench/acbr/build.ps1 (14): drive third-party ACBr/Zeus builds; stay glue, and their numbers become typed bench_row records (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH).\nDATA MIGRATIONS: src/corpus.txt became a build product (FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND, user step git rm --cached left); no other tracked .tsv/.txt in fiscal; the deps/corpus *-json-documents.txt manifests are written by init.ps1 (untracked) and move into the family manifest.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_45 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 45u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "kit", "11-01 10:3x kit (round 5): status for the user Q on pwsh->Spiral ergonomics recorded on KIT-RUN-SPI (verb not built; model done; gaps listed). Migration order decided (user list item 8): light per-script ports run as main-thread agile items in each lane plus kit jobs on the node, NOT subagents (a subagent pays a full context dump before its first edit). Each port = one TaskKind item, D2, light, with DoD: script archived via scratch-archive.ps1, callers rewired to the kit verb, CLI test green.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_46 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 46u32, "2026-11-01T14:45Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit census (git ls-files) of tracked .ps1: spiral 133, i574n.github 53, kit 45, tibia 27, polyglot 27, x 24, fiscal 17, dice 13, alphabet 8 = 347. Light ports go first where a kit verb already exists (notebook-batch -> kit run --test once KIT-RUN-SPI lands).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_47 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 47u32, "2026-11-01T15:11Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 11:11 tibia, build.ps1 port SLICE 4 GREEN: the stringly parts of apps/suite/suite.spi are retyped per n41's self-critique. (1) file_verdict = | Green : totals | NotGreen : totals * string | NoTotal : i32, with verdict_of and ONE renderer verdict_line returning option string (None for green, never an empty-string sentinel); the tests now assert on verdicts. (2) The metrics: a sample union (BudgetFindings : budget_kind * i32 | FileSeconds : file_row | FileExitCode : file_row | TestMs : test_row) rendered by sample_line, so metric names appear once and each case carries exactly its labels; closed unions backend (OnC..OnZig), test_status, memo_state and budget_kind replace the free strings; test_row = { place : test_place; outcome : test_outcome }. build.ps1 -Files suite: 7/7, lua + rust (14 rows). LESSONS: a record type declared over several lines does NOT parse ('Expected one of: inl, let, union...' at the next line); declare records on one line and nest them when they pass 120 characters. Three cell-budget splits went into fixtures (two_failed_totals, offscreen_file_row, memo_hit_row). NOT DONE vs n41: (a) the GADT indexed by label record was deliberately replaced by this payload union, which gives the same no-typo, no-missing-label guarantee without relying on Spiral refining a second argument under a GADT match (unproven in tibia); (b) budget_finding decoding from report lines (still PowerShell regex in build.ps1) is slice 5. Unstaged, waiting for the user's commit.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_48 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 48u32, "2026-11-01T15:47Z", "x", "2026-11-01 11:47 x: port 2 second half UNBLOCKED. X-RUN-METRICS' baseline is complete (its n of today), so retiring e2e-parity.ps1 (and with it node-run's parity mode) costs no measurement. Slice S1 (CELLS-IN-SPIRAL n5) is next in x's queue after C1's morning land window.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_49 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 49u32, "2026-11-01T17:14Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:14 compiler: NO-.PY PORT-OR-DROP DECISION (main relay of the user's 11-01 13:0x drafts rule) for the tool .py named in n22, plus a fifth found by the same census. (1) apps/compiler/runtime/corelib.py: KEEP. It is not a tool but the Python backend's codegen runtime, the twin of corelib.cuh: spiral_compiler.fs:27858 reads it, SpiralCompiler.fsproj:25 copies it, and its text goes into every Python output. Removing it breaks the Python backend. (2) tmp/tests/native-shims/run_main.py: DROPPED. It is inlined as a `python -c` program in scripts/test.ps1 (Python arm) and scripts/bench-native.ps1. Proof: old shim vs inline on 11 sample main.py files gave identical stdout and exit codes, 11 of 11. (3) tmp/tests/native-shims/cpp_native.py: DROPPED in test.ps1. The Cpp arm now calls SPIRAL_CXX, g++ or clang++ directly, plus nvcc only when main.cu has a body, so python is no longer a Cpp prerequisite. Proof is PENDING: a heavy window (kit-TRAIN7b) holds the box compile-quiet. When it frees, diff old vs new builds on the Cpp samples, then archive both .py through a scratch folder with scratch-archive.ps1. (4) tmp/tests/native-shims/openqasm-run/run.py: PORT, filed as OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL. (5) apps/spiral/test_json_protocol.py (4.8 KB, nothing references it): outside apps/compiler; the decision belongs to apps/spiral's owner and has been flagged to main. The 902 generated sample main.py/main_auto.py files are backend outputs, not tools, and stay.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_50 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 50u32, "2026-11-01T17:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:23 compiler: cpp_native.py proof DONE. ab.ps1 (scratch) pulled Build-And-Run and Invoke-Native out of the live test.ps1 by AST and ran them against the retired shims on scratch copies of every sample with a main.cpp (12) plus 5 Python samples, inside compile window win-1793553501808. Result: 17 compared, 0 differ, 17 ran. Exit codes matched where they were nonzero (ts_closure_capture 42, ts_layout_heap 19, ts_layout_mutable 7). Stdout is empty on these samples, so the exit code carries the signal. CUDA (nvcc) path: no sample's main.cu has a body, so it is unexercised; its logic mirrors cpp_native.py line for line. ARCHIVED: run_main.py and cpp_native.py, via scratch-archive (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261101-132201, restore with -Restore <manifest.tsv>). git shows them as unstaged D. tmp/README.md line 53 is updated. Tool .py left in apps/compiler: openqasm-run/run.py (port = OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL). runtime/corelib.py stays as backend runtime.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_51 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 51u32, "2026-11-01T18:13Z", "compiler", "11-01 14:1x compiler: DRAFTS-RULE REVIEW (main relay of the user's 11-01 14:0x narrowing: a file whose landing place is known starts at its final repo path; the store holds only work whose landing is unknown). I decided each of my 7 store files deliberately: (1) COMPILER-WIN-STACK-OVERFLOW\\host-compile-stack.kitdo: the landing is known (host Program.fs), but it is a compiler change that reaches users through a pack. It moves into the live Program.fs, unstaged, the moment the node server-mode A/B proves it, so it is out of the live tree only during the proof. (2) DELPHI-TO-PASCAL\\1-pascal-backend-alias.kitdo: same case. The core and host land through a pack after a build and predict run; it stays until then. (3) and (4) HOPACSOTA-P3 appliers: landing unknown (anchors predate packs 8-14a, and they need a re-dry-run): STORE. (5) POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE\\retire-x-compat.kitdo: landing unknown (gated on x and tibia confirming the Cells check): STORE. (6) SPIRAL-CLI-JSON-PROTOCOL-TEST\\build-run-check.kitdo: the landing is known (apps/spiral/build.ps1), but that file gates CI's fresh CLI build, and an unproven edit there would turn the user's next push red. It lands at its path once one box CLI build proves it, the first time the heavy window frees. (7) test_json_protocol.py: the source being ported, never to land; it gets archived when (6) lands. Committed leftovers in my lane: openqasm-run/run.py stays until OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL replaces it (live item). The tmp/scripts and tmp/formatter .ps1 files are already counted in this item's census (n22) and get the same land/store/archive pass with each port.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_52 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 52u32, "2026-11-01T18:25Z", "x", "2026-11-01 14:25 x: the port queue in n43 shrinks by 4. scripts/cargo-profile-{bench,cpu,runtime}.ps1 and gleam-compact-census.ps1 are archived because their items are Done (X-DONE n87), so nothing is left to port for them.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_53 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 53u32, "2026-11-01T18:39Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 14:4x tibia, SLICE 5 DONE (budget report decoding): tibia apps/suite/suite.spi gains budget_report_of, which reads Cells' 'cell-budget report: N finding(s) in M file(s) (kind n, ...)' line into a typed `budget_report = BudgetSamples (list sample) | BadFinding string | NoReport`; budget_text renders the tibia_cell_budget_findings prom lines that build.ps1:131's regex wrote. budget_kind gains Hashtag and Cashtag (cell_budget.ex emits them; the closed union didn't have them); an unknown kind is named ('bad cell-budget finding: emoji 3') instead of passed through. Local run: suite 9/9 passed on lua and rust, 0 over budget. Unstaged in tibia. Remaining for tibia's build.ps1 share: the wiring slice (build.ps1 calls a suite entry instead of the regex), which needs a runnable suite main; next after the typed rows.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_54 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 54u32, "2026-11-01T18:39Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01: en16931-terms.ps1 PORTED and swapped. src/canon.spi (edition 3, sha 3608E532C5E8, unstaged) reads the Peppol BIS3 structure files and writes canon/en16931-terms.json; node gate t1101 pack14a core DBC5EC18F14C: 1/1 passed, 0 type errors, pins 160 terms + 30 groups. Output proven equal to the PowerShell walker: same source, 190 rows, 0 differing rows (sizes differ only by pretty-printing). canon added to package.spiproj and spiral.toml modules; build.ps1 no longer calls the script (the src test loop runs canon.spi); scripts/en16931-terms.ps1 deleted (unstaged, restorable from git). Fiscal .ps1 count 17 -> 16. Two fixes needed on the way: (1) ETY-ValueRestriction on listm::length = listm::length (annotate one side : i32); (2) node mirror t1101 lacked deps/corpus/eu/peppol-bis3/structure/part (16 files): OS error 3 panic until pushed.")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_55 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 55u32, "2026-11-02T01:16Z", "html", "html 21:1x NEW REPO GLUE (C:\\home\\git\\html, unstaged): build.ps1, scripts/init.ps1, scripts/workflow.ps1, scripts/publish.ps1 = the dir-tree-html/regex thin-glue shape (init links deps/spiral, build = Cells gate + BuildSpiral per crate + cargo + self-test + line gate, workflow/publish = one call each). DECISION: keep as glue until KIT-RUN-SPI runs real scripts; then build.ps1's logic (Cells total check, line gate) ports to a kit command shared with regex, which has the same block. No analysis .ps1 in the repo: the parity runner stays in %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\html\\HTML-PARITY\\parity.ps1 and becomes a Spiral kit command (HTML-PARITY).")
inl note_of_ps1_to_spiral_56 () = Note ("PS1-TO-SPIRAL", 56u32, "2026-11-02T09:38Z", "yed", "Port-or-drop decision (yed lane, 2026-11-02): new i574n.github/apps/graphs/build.ps1 is KEPT as host glue at the user's explicit request ('a new script in a new apps/graphs folder'): JDK discovery, pinned yEd zip download with sha256 check, javac + java run of apps/graphs/src (Java on yed.jar). Port target: a kit command or Spiral program when apps/graphs moves from Java to Spiral->Kotlin (typefeatureset), tracked on YED-DIAGRAMS.")
