inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_18 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 18u32, "2026-11-02T14:06Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByTest. QUESTION: The manual Zed check of gutter run buttons for test blocks. RULE (written before acting): PASS iff (a) runnables.scm (now at apps/zed/languages/spiral/runnables.scm, grammar wired at rev 3c76d3ed) captures 375/375 test headers over the 583-file corpus, (b) test-at-row.ps1 -DryRun on sampled header and body rows of math.spi and sm'_real.spir resolves the expected test names, and (c) an off-screen, muted Zed launch with the dev extension logs no runnables or grammar error. Otherwise reopen. BACKUP/UNDO: No source change. Fixes are left unstaged. OWNER: main. NEXT: Run (a)-(c) alongside TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL's check, then close. Set the assignee to agent. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl ci_after_spi_migration () = Task ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", "First CI runs after the 2026-10-12 commits (dc7b955c lib .livemd -> .spi with 370 test blocks, Kino from_spi/--livemd-path, DeadPureLetElision, Wasm str_cmp, canonical package dirs): spiral, dice, alphabet, polyglot must build lib from .spi with a compiler built from the same commit (an older compiler fails Package not loaded on test blocks); lib/spiral/build.ps1 runs 4 notebooks at once and was reaped locally at 16 GB, check runner memory and lower the throttle if needed; outputs are now <nb>.spi.ipynb/.spi.html; 2026-10-12 11:30 CI read: spiral ubuntu red on 2 runs (before and after the migration) in lib/spiral/near/wallet: gleam build --target javascript rejects the Erlang-only @external spiral_math_pow the Gleam integer prelude bundles (handed to the compiler lane); eoie ubuntu red: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/env.ps1:98 Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA null on Linux in Swift tool detection, fixed (guarded like BendMain, verified with LOCALAPPDATA unset); alphabet red (ALPHABET-CI-XELATEX); i574n.github red since 05:22; dice and spiral 10:44 runs in progress; 11:40: spiral run 38265092981 (10:44 push 52311f0a, first CI of the .spi lib) died differently: exit 143 (SIGTERM, not a script error) 26 min into lib/spiral/build.ps1 -sequential 1 with zero output in between (15:01:11 -> 15:27:49Z; the build buffered each notebook's log until the end), so the culprit notebook or memory pressure is unknowable from that log; lib/spiral/build.ps1 now prints start/done lines per notebook (exit, attempts, seconds) as they happen; the near_wallet Gleam pow failure would still follow later in that job; 11:58 dice 10:44 run red on windows in contract/: process_rust runs spiral_wasm through invoke-block -Linux (exit 127 on the Windows runner); already decided in CI-SPIRAL-WASM-NATIVE: the NEAR sandbox is Linux/macOS only (near-sandbox-utils), so it is WSL-last work, no skip switch; 12:05 correction: the fine-grained-cells hypothesis for the 26 min SIGTERM was wrong; the Kino lane measured per-test planning (sm' 195 -> 38 steps) at 374 s -> 369 s, math 87 -> 86 s: definition-only steps compile fast, the cost is test steps building once per ///> backend (gleam/fsharp/cuda dominate; sm' summed: target 552 s, compile 507 s, daemon queue 521 -> 303 s, rustc 44 s); my 622 s was contention; the SIGTERM cause stays open until the per-notebook progress lines show it; CI-time levers: per-backend batching of a file's tests (one gleam project per file), cached target builds, fewer targets in CI; 12:42 lib/spiral/build.ps1 done lines now also carry the test counts (spiral-tests JSON: passed/failed/skipped, failed test names, a total line) and available memory (MemAvailable on Linux), so the next 143 shows which notebook ran and whether memory was falling; hypothesis to confirm, not act on yet: runner memory exhaustion with Kino's default 4 concurrent cells building gleam/fsharp/cuda targets (SPIRAL_KINO_CELL_CONCURRENCY=2 in CI would be the lever); 14:20 spiral CI GREEN on feb8b9f7 (run 38280264212, 1h18m, ubuntu + windows, pages deployed): the NEAR wallet Gleam build passes with the target-neutral pow, lib/spiral/build.ps1 reports 39 files / 368 tests passed / 0 failed from .spi on ubuntu, slowest sm' 162 s, parsing 146 s, base 124 s; available memory on the runner never under 8.2 GB, so the earlier exit 143 stays unexplained (not memory in this run; possibly runner-side); my earlier \"parsing 33/40\" came from a text heuristic in my A/B script, the Kino report says 40/40; still to confirm on the next pushes: eoie ubuntu (env.ps1 LOCALAPPDATA fix lands when eoie CI clones spiral), alphabet xelatex (packages + diagnostics step, uncommitted), i574n.github (same near_wallet fix); 14:35 eoie run 38280533281 (12:50 commits incl. the eoie lane's in-progress typed-fields crates) fails on windows in agile_planning_rollup/tests/planning_cli.rs: mutating verbs refused with \"lease authority blocked mutating effect because should_wrap=1\" (tests depend on the fixture's lease clock), handed to the eoie lane; the env.ps1 LOCALAPPDATA fix is confirmed on the next eoie run; alphabet: root cause found (texlive-lang-greek), fix uncommitted; 2026-10-13 23:57 sweep lane: eoie run 38327253830 green on windows and ubuntu (env.ps1 LOCALAPPDATA fix confirmed); spiral 38389311114 and .github 38389289826 (push 8a89893a) red on ubuntu only in lib/spiral/near/wallet: lib build itself 39 files / 369 passed / 0 failed, but near_wallet.spi tests still called lustre.start without a DOM (let assert Ok panics under bun) once Kino dropped build_only; fixed by mirroring lustre.spi (init/update/view -> to_html -> expect_html exact HTML), landed in d94dc380 (23:49), CI 38508233036 / 38508243993 running; earlier xsim heavy-churn failure (runs 38312827285, 38295906353) has a test fix in 8a89893a with no CI evidence yet (later runs died before xsim); alphabet 38327247780 ubuntu green, windows red: tectonic cannot find font NanumGothicCoding for test.hangul.md.pdf (contradicts DOCUMENTS-TECTONIC Hangul check, which was local only); fix uncommitted in alphabet/scripts/init.ps1: on Windows, when C:/Windows/Fonts/NanumGothicCoding.ttf is missing, download naver/nanumfont VER2.5 NanumGothicCoding-2.5.zip (same files, same sizes as the local fonts tectonic uses), copy both ttf into the Windows fonts dir and register them in HKLM Fonts (download/extract dry-checked locally); dice 38265106556 ubuntu green, windows red only in the WSL-last contract; polyglot has no push since 10-09; 2026-10-14 00:22 push d94dc380 (incl. the near_wallet fix): spiral 38508233036 and .github 38508243993 red on ubuntu earlier, in apps/wasm: Kino now pins rustc +1.99.0 (kino.ex @rust_toolchain, new in d94dc380); the runner has only nightly-2025-05-09, rustup auto-installed 1.99.0 (3 components) while concurrent cells called rustc, and every attempt then failed error[E0463] can't find crate for std (rustup is not safe for concurrent installs; all 3 retries hit the same broken toolchain); fix (uncommitted, apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino.ex): before the first rustc through a rustup proxy, one cell under a :global lock checks rustup toolchain list and runs rustup toolchain install 1.99.0 --profile minimal --no-self-update if missing (rustup next to the rustc proxy, skipped when absent), cached in :persistent_term; kino compiles (private MIX_BUILD_PATH) and the rustup path/listing probe resolves locally; windows jobs of both runs were cancelled by fail-fast, so near_wallet, xsim and windows wasm still lack CI evidence; eoie 38508234661: ubuntu green, windows red in eoie_proxy_edit_contracts (runner temp path C:/Users/RUNNER~1 got quoted), fixed under EOIE-FRICTION-2026-10-12; next: commit kino.ex + alphabet init.ps1 + eoie, push, read the next spiral/.github/alphabet/eoie runs; 2026-10-14 00:25 near_wallet.spi (d94dc380) verified locally: run_notebook.ps1 --path lib/spiral/near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi (private MIX_BUILD_PATH, output to scratch): discovered 2, executed 2, passed 2 under gleam -t javascript; the rustc race is a hypothesis: spiral_wasm.livemd has 5 Kino cells, cell concurrency defaults to 4, the pin is the only change since the green wasm step in 38389311114, and rustc is the only caller of @rust_toolchain; if the next run still shows E0463 after the serialized install, preinstall 1.99.0 (rustup toolchain install 1.99.0 --profile minimal) in the workflows before any Kino step; 2026-10-14 04:29 review fixes (uncommitted): (1) apps/kino/lib/spiral/kino.ex ensure_rust_toolchain marked the toolchain ready even after a failed rustup install and ran the install unbounded inside :global.trans: now readiness is set only when rustup lists 1.99.0 or the install exits 0, both rustup calls go through Runner.run bounded by the cell's budget, and a failure returns a ProcessError with rustup's output tail (the next Rust cell tries again); prepare_rust_toolchain is public for tests; kino_test adds fake-rustup cases (already listed -> ok, install exit 0 -> ok, offline install exit 1 -> error naming the failed install and the offline text); proven in a private copy: that test passes and a real host-Rust notebook (convert.spi, rustup proxy, private port) 2/2; (2) alphabet scripts/init.ps1 font install no longer needs admin: it checks both %WINDIR%\\Fonts and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Fonts, installs into the per-user dir with HKCU Fonts values (full paths), and verifies the zip's SHA-256 (F4C9B108...619A3F) before extracting; proven by running the block with WINDIR/LOCALAPPDATA redirected to scratch (installs both ttf + HKCU values, second run is a no-op, the 2 HKCU values removed afterwards) and with a wrong hash (throws, nothing installed); tectonic and xelatex both find per-user fonts (a per-user-only font, Aller, renders under both; an unknown font fails)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY,PIPELINES-GREEN", "ci,lib,kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ci_after_spi_migration () = Planning ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Pair)
inl samples_to_test_blocks () = Task ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", "Folder samples (apps/compiler/tmp/samples, ~3,770 matrix rows) become test blocks in .spi files, the way lib/spiral did on 2026-10-12: one file per family, each test block names its backends (///> targets) and its expected exit/stdout inline; the matrix reads expectations from source instead of the cache-only EXPECTED.tsv; start with one low-signal family (heap_/closure_/union_ combinatorics, TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS) and measure suite time before/after; negative samples become test blocks expecting a diagnostic", Story, P1, D6, 40u32, Planned, "TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS,TEST-RUN-REPORT", "samples,tests,harness,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_samples_to_test_blocks () = Planning ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", Minutes 1800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
