inl note_of_configurable_oracle_3 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 3u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: Zig rows now 441 against C's 5,016 total harness rows (pack-1o).")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_4 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 4u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: correction of the previous note (5,016 was every backend's rows together): in the pack-1o bless single-flight-20261015-194349 C has 497 native rows and Zig 441.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_5 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-10-16T18:26Z", "main-thread", "14:26 main: implemented: test.ps1 -Oracle <backend> (C default; Zig, Rust, Delphi, Wasm, Lean, Gleam, Lua, TypeScript, Python, Kotlin, Swift allowed): the oracle column compares every other native row (C included) against that backend's row; a sample without one is no-<backend>. Neutral by default (pack-1x bless 140122 reproduced its expectation with it). Coverage measured on 125241: Zig rows exist for 454 of the 493 samples with a native C row; the 39 others are C-only (22) or written for one backend (17: ebpf_*, rust_*, ts_float_nan, ts_while_loop, wgsl_parallel_lanes, python_macro_annotations); Zig arms for ts_float_nan/ts_while_loop staged in pack-1y.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_6 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 6u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: full review scored with -Oracle Zig (single-flight-20261017-043743, candidate pack): agree 5,354 (5,383 under C), known 3, no-zig 67 (C 37, Bend 12, Rust 8, Ebpf 6, Python 2, Delphi 1, Wgsl 1), DISAGREE 5, all dynamic_array_bounds_negative: Zig exits 3 on the negative index like Lean and Bend while C, Delphi, Wasm, Kotlin and Lua read out of bounds and exit 0. Zig is the stricter oracle; a switch needs Zig rows for the 67 samples and a bounds-check decision for unchecked backends.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_7 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 7u32, "2026-10-17T19:55Z", "main-thread", "15:55 main-thread, user decision 2026-10-17: Zig becomes a SECOND oracle next to C (not a replacement): reviews compare against both C and Zig rows (C fallback where no Zig row exists), roughly two native tiers per review. Evidence: today's -Oracle Zig run agreed on 5,388 rows with DISAGREE 0. Next: a -Oracle C,Zig mode in test.ps1 (both oracles scoped in Known), a Zig bless, then make it the review default; native memo keeps the second tier cheap on reruns.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_8 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 8u32, "2026-10-17T20:21Z", "main-thread", "16:21 main-thread, user decision 2026-10-17: the first Zig bless runs in the next overnight run, after the -Oracle C,Zig harness change.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_9 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 9u32, "2026-10-17T23:07Z", "main-thread", "19:07 main-thread done (unstaged): test.ps1 -Oracle takes a list and now defaults to C,Zig; the second oracle is a pass over rows that agree with the first (DISAGREE on mismatch, or known via a Known entry scoped to that oracle). Full suite with memos in 117 s: DISAGREE 0, Zig ran 458 rows, the 4 dynamic_array_bounds_negative unchecked-backend rows are known vs Zig. No extra native time (Zig rows already run). Documented in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md. The next bless runs under C,Zig by default, which is the first Zig bless.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_10 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 10u32, "2026-10-19T12:38Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:38 helper-lane lap 1: verified the matrix half: test.ps1's -Oracle default @('C', 'Zig') is committed (a2abbe52, 10-18 01:03), so every accept since (123705 on 10-18, pack 3, pack 4 whose EXPECTED.tsv is dated 10-19 00:28) ran under C,Zig: the first Zig bless happened. Test-block half: Cells has no named reference backend; with agree on, cells.ex disagreement (lines 186-211) requires all targets of a test to print the same value and names the first two that differ (targets disagree: X printed ..., Y printed ...), with --no-agree reason as the escape (notebook.ex:120). All-agree already subsumes C-as-oracle for test blocks; the only missing piece is an expected-disagreement entry scoped to a reference backend (the matrix's Known with Oracle), e.g. dynamic_array_bounds_negative's checked vs unchecked split. Progress 65 -> 80.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_11 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 11u32, "2026-10-19T13:24Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:24 helper-lane lap 2: test-block form specified against the code it would touch: document.spi already parses header modes into ///- options (test_mode/agree_mode at 312/337, the no_agree reason at 450), and cells.ex disagreement (208-215) compares every target's shown output with the FIRST non-empty chunk. Spec: a header mode reference <backend> (test name reference zig =, cell option ///- --test --reference zig) makes disagreement compare each chunk with the reference backend's chunk instead of the first, names the reference in the message (targets disagree with the reference zig: ...), and still marks only the differing target as disagrees; combined with no_agree it stays off. Default without the mode: the first target, i.e. today's behaviour, so no existing test changes. Two code points: document.spi header parsing (one more agree_mode-like word) and cells.ex disagreement (pick the reference chunk). The matrix half stays as is (C,Zig).")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_12 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 12u32, "2026-10-19T14:56Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 10:56 helper-lane lap 3: drafted the Cells half as lab/CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE/patch.py (anchors --check OK on today's apps/cells, LF; not applied, lane 2 edits Cells): notebook.ex run options gain :reference from a cell option ///- --reference <target> (reference_target/1 beside build_only?/1, next to the existing :agree put at line 932); cells.ex disagreement (210) compares every non-empty chunk with the reference target's chunk when one is named and present, else with the first as today, and returns {reference, other}, so only the differing target is marked disagrees; the message becomes targets disagree with the reference zig: ... only when a reference is set, so the existing notebook_report_test assertion at 429 (targets disagree: lua printed ...) is unchanged. Left: the .spi header mode (test name reference zig =) in spi/document.spi beside agree_mode, and one ExUnit case (lua vs gleam, reference gleam: the lua target is the one marked).")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_13 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 13u32, "2026-10-19T15:37Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:37 helper-lane lap 4: the .spi half staged as lab/CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE/document_patch.py against apps/cells/spi/document.spi (4 anchors, --check OK): a header mode reference <target> (test name reference zig =) is accepted by flags_valid, becomes the cell option ///- --test --reference zig in test_options, and the reverse export (test_block_go) writes it back through reference_mode, so .spi -> cells -> .spi round-trips; word_after reads the target word with text.take_unicode_ident. Plus lab/CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE/reference_test.exs: round trip, the cell option, and a lua/gleam disagreement with reference gleam whose message names the reference and marks lua as the target that disagrees (helpers as in notebook_report_test: exit_when, a target callback). Both patches (cells.ex/notebook.ex from lap 3 and this one) plus the test are ready for one Cells change; lane 2 edits Cells, so they wait for a coordinated apply + mix test.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_14 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 14u32, "2026-10-19T21:40Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 17:40 helper-lane lap 6: patch.py (cells.ex and notebook.ex) and document_patch.py (spi/document.spi) dry runs both match apps/cells today. Applying them touches Cells files that lane 2 also edits, so that waits for coordination; reference_test.exs is the proof after apply.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_15 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 15u32, "2026-10-22T04:15Z", "main", "00:15 landing path found during the lab drain: neither half had landed (document.spi has no --reference; cells.ex has no reference message). document_patch.py's second anchor had drifted because the formatter split the header expression across lines; re-anchored to the current layout (++ reference_mode head as its own line), and its dry run matches again; patch.py (cells.ex, notebook.ex) still matches. Both, plus reference_test.exs inserted at the end of notebook_report_test.exs, join tonight's CELLS-PACK-NEXT run in an apps/cells copy (full mix test); they land in the tree with that pack if green.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_16 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 16u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 5 12:19 (subagent): Cells patches staged; coordinated apply with lane 2 pending -> next: apply + mix test | lap 7 19:54 (subagent): re-read: both patches dry-run clean on apps/cells -> next: Cells window + reference_test.exs")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_17 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 17u32, "2026-10-28T01:32Z", "main", "10-27 21:32 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_18 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 18u32, "2026-10-31T20:53Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl note_of_configurable_oracle_19 () = Note ("CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", 19u32, "2026-11-06T12:30Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: a matrix and test-block option names the reference backend (C by default); one suite run with another oracle (Rust) shows the same agree/disagree classification. Next step: find the option's remaining unwired consumer from its last note and run the Rust-oracle suite.")
inl kino_run_one_test () = Task ("KINO-RUN-ONE-TEST", "run_notebook.ps1 --test <name>: run only the prefix of a .spi up to that test block plus its body, report pass/fail and output; prerequisite of ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES and of fast single-test loops; done 2026-10-12: run_notebook --test <name>[,name] runs only those test cells, each carrying its definition prefix and earlier static prelude tests (regression: --test square_2 alone keeps open testing); evaluate/2 tests: [names]; per-test planning for .spi (plan: :tests) measured neutral on time (sm' 195 -> 38 steps, 374 -> 369 s) and kept", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,zed", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_run_one_test () = Planning ("KINO-RUN-ONE-TEST", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl notebooks_to_spi_siblings () = Task ("NOTEBOOKS-TO-SPI-SIBLINGS", "Repeat the lib/spiral migration in dice (lib/dice, contract, fsharp), alphabet (documents, hangul) and polyglot notebooks: to_spi_tested export, build scripts run .spi, Kino tests move from livemd round trips to parse_spi; mirror every dice change in alphabet; 2026-10-14 02:38 lane 1 (uncommitted): dice end to end: lib/dice.spi and contract/dice_contract.spi re-exported with their test blocks (run_notebook --path x.livemd --export-only --with-tests --spi-path x.spi: 24 and 8 test blocks); the compiler emits identical code with and without the blocks (dice.spi F# 325574 B and Rust 511961 B, dice_contract.spi Rust 184859 B, before/after compiled byte-identical); lib/build.ps1 and contract/build.ps1 run --path x.spi --output-path x.spi.ipynb and drop the livemd export step; runs from the .spi (private daemon, Invoke-Heavy): dice.spi 23/23 + prelude passed (397 s), dice_contract.spi 7/7 + prelude passed (489 s); lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp.livemd is an F# notebook (--no-spi, exported to .fs), nothing to migrate; README links -> dice.spi.html / dice_contract.spi.html; alphabet mirrored: apps/documents/documents.spi re-exported (2 test blocks, F# 634232 B and Rust 1014128 B byte-identical with/without), documents/build.ps1 runs the .spi, run 1/1 + prelude passed (198 s), README link -> documents.spi.html; apps/hangul is F# (--no-spi), nothing to migrate; Kino tests moved from livemd round trips to parse_spi for these sources (document_test: dice and alphabet .spi load and write back byte for byte via to_spi_tested, test counts; the CLI export comparison keeps only the F# notebooks), document_test 16/16; i574n.github profile README links updated; left for the user: git rm dice/lib/dice.livemd, dice/contract/dice_contract.livemd, alphabet/apps/documents/documents.livemd (lane rules forbid deleting tracked files; nothing reads them any more); polyglot in progress; 2026-10-14 02:49 polyglot (uncommitted): lib/math/math.spi (13 test blocks) and apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.spi (7) re-exported with tests, Rust output byte-identical with/without the blocks (292284 B, 86607 B); lib/math/build.ps1 runs Invoke-Notebook math.spi --output-path math.spi.ipynb, chat contract build.ps1 runs the .spi, both drop the livemd export; runs from the .spi: math 13/13 passed (197 s), chat_contract 6/6 + prelude passed (237 s); apps/spiral/temp/cube: cube.spi already equals the export, no tests, build.ps1 no longer re-exports it (the .spi is the source); README links -> math.spi.html, chat_contract.spi.html; not migrated, with reason: apps/perf/Perf.livemd and apps/scheduler/Tasks.livemd have no test cells but run output cells (benchmarks; Tasks has six-target ///! run cells) whose outputs a .spi cannot carry, so moving them means turning those run cells into test blocks (a design call: output-only tests), and their .spi files are already in sync with the livemd; the F#/pwsh/Elixir notebooks (lib/fsharp, parser, scripts, exercism) have no Spiral cells; left for the user: git rm of the migrated .livemd files (dice lib + contract, alphabet documents, polyglot lib/math, apps/chat/contract, apps/spiral/temp/cube); 2026-10-14 03:54 mirror check (dice -> alphabet): dice lib/build.ps1 and contract/build.ps1 (run the .spi, drop the livemd export) = alphabet apps/documents/build.ps1, same diff; dice README notebook links = alphabet README documents link; no counterpart: dice has two Spiral notebooks (lib, contract) against alphabet's one (documents), dice lib/fsharp and alphabet apps/hangul are both F# notebooks left as they are, and neither repo's scripts/ or .github/workflows reference .livemd or .ipynb names; reverse direction for information: the alphabet-only init.ps1 NanumGothicCoding install and the documents hangul code-fence fix have no dice counterpart (dice builds no PDFs)", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", "dice,alphabet,polyglot,kino", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_notebooks_to_spi_siblings () = Planning ("NOTEBOOKS-TO-SPI-SIBLINGS", Minutes 360u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl spir_interleaved_livemd () = Task ("SPIR-INTERLEAVED-LIVEMD", ".spi + _real.spir -> .livemd places real-mode cells before the rest, so sm'_real.spir does not round-trip byte for byte (the other 38 do); interleave by heading so the Livebook view of sm' matches the old notebook; done 2026-10-12: real-mode cells interleave by heading; repo-wide check sm'.spi + sm'_real.spir -> --livemd-path -> --export-only --with-tests gives both files byte-identical", TaskKind, P3, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,livemd", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spir_interleaved_livemd () = Planning ("SPIR-INTERLEAVED-LIVEMD", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
