inl note_of_lean_backend_1 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:32Z", "main-thread", "08:32 single-flight-20261014-073517: Lean 137 rows, 137 ran, 136 agree; the one non-agree is dynamic_array_bounds_negative, a Known row (C has no bounds check, Lean exits 3 as intended). Lean is at parity on its list; next is widening the list toward the Bend 344.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_2 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: Lean 137 rows, 136 agree, 1 known (pack-1h oracle). Nothing new; stays behind Zig.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_3 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 3u32, "2026-10-15T21:55Z", "main-thread", "17:55 Lean probe (main, single-flight-20261015-174746): 422 rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0; 276 new rows (native <= 6 s, Lean elaboration ~2-5 s) staged for pack-1n (Lean 137 -> 413). 39 build-fail rows are the next targets.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_4 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 4u32, "2026-10-15T22:06Z", "main-thread", "18:06 main: harness Lean list 137 -> 413 rows (probe single-flight-20261015-174746: 422 agree with C, DISAGREE 0, 39 build-fail, rows <= 6 s); in the pack-1n review.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_5 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 5u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: 442 of 443 Lean rows agree with C (1 known) in review 232243. Elaboration time per row (final review 023521, build + run under suite load): median 3,450 ms, p90 10,219, max 23,500 (array_union_heap_union_heap_pair_heaps), the most expensive per-row tier of all backends.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_6 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 6u32, "2026-10-17T18:24Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:24 resumable from the bundles: bundle-cleanup-backup-20260926\\bundle_spiral-samples_v20260926-alpha705.zip proof-export\\ holds Lean exports that are absent from today's repo (grep for derivativePreservesMatches/euclideanDivisionFromSerializedReplay finds nothing). (1) zeta-euclidean-v2: a structure-bearing Spiral replay transported to Lean (SerializedDivisionReplay, serializedDivisionReplaySound), elaborated by Lean 4.33.0-rc1; open boundary: general existence still uses Lean's Nat.div. (2) brzozowski-derivative: a Lean source with Derivative/DerivativeTrace/Matches, a normalization trace layer and a candidate derivativePreservesMatches proof, never kernel-elaborated (no lean in that container), plus an independent F# oracle and verify.fsx custody (active/trusted source byte identity + pinned hashes). (3) cic-strict-positivity. The optional\\lean gate stays nonblocking unless --require. A candidate first job for the Lean lane: elaborate these with today's Lean.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_7 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 7u32, "2026-10-19T12:35Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:35 lap 1 grain: today's pack 5 review: Lean 446 rows agree with C plus 1 known, 84 C samples without a Lean row (stack layouts, C macros, BackendSwitch records without a Lean key); the slow rows are lean --run's interpreter (BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS note 30), not codegen Next: measure lean -c + C compile on c_self_tail_loop_heap (17 s interpreted) to size a compiled Lean tier")
inl note_of_lean_backend_8 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 8u32, "2026-10-19T13:33Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:33 lap 2 grain, decides lap 1's compiled-tier question from today's review instead of a heavy probe: the 447 Lean rows sum to 742 s of native time, median 1.57 s per row, max 6.4 s (native_managed_tail_recursion), so lean --run is dominated by the ~1.5-2 s elaboration floor, not by interpretation. samples/c_self_tail_loop_heap, the 17 s case, has no Lean row at all (not on the Lean list; its 17 s was a hand probe). A compiled tier (lean -c, then leanc/clang) costs a C compile per row on top of elaboration, which is slower than 1.6 s for every row the matrix has today. Decision: no compiled Lean tier for the matrix; keep it only as an option for a future long-running Lean row (and then per sample, not per run). The open work is coverage: 84 C samples without a Lean row. Next: static scan of those 84 for constructs the Lean backend lacks (stack layouts, C-only macros, BackendSwitch records without a Lean key) to list the ones that should simply be added to the Lean list")
inl note_of_lean_backend_9 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 9u32, "2026-10-19T14:09Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:09 lap 3 grain: coverage gap re-counted on the accepted pack 5 run (single-flight-20261019-080524): 51 samples run natively on C but have no Lean row (lap 1's 84 counted non-native C rows too). Static scan of their sources: 30 use macro text (12 macros only, 6 with a BackendSwitch, 14 BackendSwitch + a family such as ebpf_/rust_/python_/abi/native_package, 10 macro + family), 1 is family-only, and 8 show no blocker: c_deep_list_decref, c_self_tail_loop_heap (the 17 s interpreted case: a Timeouts candidate), frontier_hopacsota_globals_order, mega_brzozowski_derivatives/runtime_bench (slow on every interpreter), mega_omniledger_erp_kernel/runtime_native, native_closure_union_rec, qualified_union_case_no_payload, typecheck_long_let_body (2,000 lets, which the pack-1y maxRecDepth option was made for). HEAVY QUEUE (main, matrix list edit between runs): add the 6 fast ones (all but c_self_tail_loop_heap and runtime_bench) to the Lean list and run test.ps1 -Mode single-flight -Backend C,Lean -Suite examples -Native (no accept); can share the C,Calyx,OpenQasm run. Next: per macro-only sample (12), check whether its macro has a Lean arm or needs one")
inl note_of_lean_backend_10 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 10u32, "2026-10-19T14:31Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:31 lap 4 grain: the 12 macro-only samples without a Lean row are all one family and C-only by construction: dynamic_array_* (geometric_growth, growth_union_managed/nested, reserve_zero, resize_alias/nested, resize_union_managed, string_resize/union, tuple_managed) and native_managed_array_scc(3)_tail_recursion call the C runtime's DynamicArrayReserve<n>/Resize<n>/Capacity<n> helpers through raw macro text, and today only C runs them (no Rust, Zig or other row either). So they are not a Lean gap but a portability gap of the samples: a portable version needs reserve/resize/capacity as core operations (or a BackendSwitch per backend), which is SAMPLES-STALE-OUTPUTS/portable-primitives territory, not codegenLean's. Lean's real addable set stays the 6 queued no-blocker samples; with the 14 BackendSwitch + family samples (written for one backend) and these 12, the remaining 51 are explained. Next: after the queued C,Lean run, look at the 6 BackendSwitch-only samples for missing Lean arms")
inl note_of_lean_backend_11 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 11u32, "2026-10-19T14:55Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:55 lap 5 grain: the 6 BackendSwitch-only samples without a Lean row, by their switch keys: native_cube_frame_reuse_direct already has a Lean arm (keys Delphi, Fsharp, Lean, Rust, Zig), so it only needs the list entry and joins the queued C,Lean run (row updated: 7 samples); lua_paren_statement (Lua, Zig) is a Lua-statement regression sample, not meant for Lean; native_float_nan_is (Delphi, Fsharp, Rust, Zig), ts_float_nan (CppHost, Delphi, Fsharp, Python, Rust, TypeScript, Zig), ts_while_loop (12 keys, no Lean) and wgsl_parallel_lanes (Delphi, Fsharp, Rust, Wgsl) need a Lean arm in the sample source (Lean: Float.isNaN for the two NaN samples, a repeat/break while for ts_while_loop), which is a sample edit for after the core switch window. So of the 51 missing rows: 7 addable now (queued), 4 need a small Lean arm each, the rest are C-only or single-backend by design")
inl note_of_lean_backend_12 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 12u32, "2026-10-19T15:20Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:20 lap 6 grain: the 7-sample no-blocker check is now a -Probe Lean run (no matrix edit, never accepted), filter on the 7 ids; queued after the switch window, replacing the matrix-edit row.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_13 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 13u32, "2026-10-19T15:53Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:53 lap 7 grain: drafted the Lean arms for the 4 switch-only samples as lab/LEAN-BACKEND/lean-arms.py (dry run: 6 anchors match once each). native_float_nan_is and ts_float_nan get Lean = (0.0 / 0.0 : Float32) / (0.0 / 0.0 : Float) next to the Zig arm; codegenLean writes NanIs as (Float32.isNaN x) / (Float.isNaN x), spiral_compiler.fs 165625. ts_while_loop gets Lean = !a := !b (Lean locals are let mut in do-notation). wgsl_parallel_lanes gets Lean = 0u32. Since BackendSwitch type-checks every arm on every backend, a wrong arm shows up as a compile error on all backends, and the probe review catches it. Queued for main between runs; the -Probe Lean run then covers them without a matrix edit.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_14 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 14u32, "2026-10-19T16:37Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:37 lap 8 grain: post-switch: lean-arms.py still matches all 6 anchors on the migrated samples (native_float_nan_is 2, ts_float_nan 2, ts_while_loop 1, wgsl_parallel_lanes 1). Checked the macro texts in real Lean instead of by reading: a do-block with let mut a : Float32 := (0.0 / 0.0 : Float32), b : Float := (0.0 / 0.0 : Float), and a := assignment on a let mut, testing Float32.isNaN and Float.isNaN, exits 0 under lean +leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc4 --run (the matrix toolchain). The wgsl_parallel_lanes arm 0u32 is a Spiral literal, not Lean text, so it needs no Lean check")
inl note_of_lean_backend_15 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 15u32, "2026-10-19T17:12Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:16 lap 9 grain: post-pack-7 stacking check on a scratch copy of the 4 samples: lean-arms.py --apply (6 edits) then OPENQASM3-BACKEND nan-arms.py --apply (4 edits) both succeed; the NaN switches read Zig, OpenQasm, Lean arms in that order, so main can apply the two scripts in one between-runs step in either order. Next: main applies lean-arms.py between runs, then the superseding -Probe Lean row (11 samples)")
inl note_of_lean_backend_16 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 16u32, "2026-10-19T17:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:40 lap 10 grain, latest-of-everything check: the Lean native tier pins leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc4, but v4.35.0 stable shipped 2026-10-12 (GitHub releases; v4.36.0-rc1 on 10-14 is a pre-release) and elan has only 4.34.1 and 4.35.0-rc4 installed. Staged lab/LEAN-BACKEND/lean-stable.py: moves all 7 pins (test.ps1:640, bench-native.ps1, apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md, apps/cells toolchain.ex:109 @lean_toolchain, apps/cells README x3; dry run counts match) to v4.35.0. Queue row: elan install, apply between runs, then the Lean rows of the next run. Next: main's go (test.ps1 and Cells files are not mine)")
inl note_of_lean_backend_17 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 17u32, "2026-10-19T17:55Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:55 lap 11 grain: risk read for the rc4 -> v4.35.0 pin move (lean-lang.org v4.35.0 release notes; GitHub's release page only links them): no change touches what codegenLean emits. Float/Float32 only gain fused multiply-add (#15024), UInt32 gains order instances (#15122), mutual and repeat/while changes are additive (invariants/termination measures, #14703, #14845 renames only the loop-invariant type, which the generated code never names), linter changes are new options; IO.Ref, String.Pos.Raw, partial def and lean --run are not mentioned. The breaking items are grind lemma sets and contract ensures syntax, unused by generated code. So lean-stable.py should leave every Lean row unchanged. Next: main's go for the queued lean-stable row")
inl note_of_lean_backend_18 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 18u32, "2026-10-19T18:25Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 14:25 lap 12: lean-arms.py turned out to be applied already (all 4 samples carry their Lean arm), while the script itself was not idempotent: the NaN anchors still matched, so a second apply would have duplicated the Lean arms in native_float_nan_is and ts_float_nan. The script now skips samples whose arm is present and writes only after every anchor checked; it reports already has its Lean arm for all 4. lean-stable.py still dry-runs (7 pins); v4.35.0 is not installed yet (elan has rc4 and v4.34.1)")
inl note_of_lean_backend_19 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 19u32, "2026-10-19T23:38Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 19:38 drive grain from main's Lean probe (single-flight-20261019-174154, 74 non-agreeing Lean rows; most are C-only helpers, negatives and backend switches without a Lean key): two real codegen failures share one cause, native_closure_union_rec and rust_static_closure_chain both stop at (kernel) arg #2 of 'U0.Cons' contains a non valid occurrence of the datatypes being declared, because a recursive union holding a closure that returns the union emits Cons : UInt64 → (Unit → IO U0) → U0, and U0 inside IO is not a positive occurrence. Staged lab/LEAN-BACKEND/boxed_closures.py (5 anchored edits to codegenLean, dry run by default, writes only after every anchor matched, refuses a re-apply): such a field becomes NonScalar, built with spiralBox and read back with spiralUnbox (opaque defs implemented_by unsafeCast, the same pattern as the existing IO.Ref default), emitted only when a program has such a field, so no other Lean output changes. Proven by hand on the probe's own main.lean files with exactly that emission, lean v4.35.0-rc4 --run: native_closure_union_rec exits 70 and rust_static_closure_chain 40, both C's exits. Other probe findings: frontier_hopacsota_globals_order fails because the sample's globals are C comments (// m1), sample-side, not the backend; mega_omniledger runtime_native times out. Next: main applies with the next pack and adds the 2 rows after the probe")
inl note_of_lean_backend_20 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 20u32, "2026-10-22T06:58Z", "main", "02:58 main: lab mostly drained. boxed_closures.py: landed ('already boxes Lean closure fields'); lean-arms.py: landed (ts_while_loop has its Lean arm); agents-note.py: was NOT applied, so I applied it now (tmp/AGENTS.md line 207: closure fields that return their own union are NonScalar via spiralBox/spiralUnbox; claims checked in the core: spiralBox 2, spiralUnbox 2, NonScalar 2). Those 3 are deleted. Kept: lean-stable.py, which moves the 7 pins v4.35.0-rc4 -> v4.35.0 (test.ps1, bench-native.ps1, tmp/AGENTS.md, Cells toolchain.ex, Cells README x3; dry run matches). v4.35.0 is the stable release of 2026-10-12, newer than rc4 (10-06); v4.36.0-rc1 (10-14) is a prerelease. Rule, fixed now: apply it after the PACK-AFTER-NIGHT install, with the contracts switch, in one -AcceptToolchain accept run; keep it if every Lean row keeps its verdict and the median Lean elaboration stays within 1.2x of rc4's (rc4 was chosen over 4.34.1 for 2 s vs 7 s).")
inl note_of_lean_backend_21 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 21u32, "2026-10-22T22:11Z", "main", "2026-10-22 18:11 main: staged in the post-install matrix bundle %TEMP%\\matrix-bundle\\bundle.ps1 (dry-run clean today), applied after PACK-NEXT-3b is accepted and installed; details and rule in ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY note 11.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_22 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 22u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 13 14:57 (subagent2): v4.35.0 downloaded (elan, eb6cafb); queue row done; lean-arms needs nothing (applied) -> next: main: lean-stable.py --apply between runs + the Lean rows | lap 14 15:03 (subagent2): v4.35.0 installed; lean-stable.py dry run 7 pins -> next: main applies lean-stable.py between runs | lap 16 16:06 (subagent2): ready: v4.35.0 installed, lean-stable.py 7 pins -> next: main applies between runs | lap 17 16:43 (subagent2): unchanged -> next: main | lap 19 18:56 (subagent2): lean-stable.py still dry-runs clean on today's test.ps1/bench-native/AGENTS/toolchain.ex/README (7 pins) -> next: main applies between runs (after pack 11's accept) | lap 21-drive 19:38 (subagent2): boxed_closures.py staged (recursive-union closure fields as NonScalar via spiralBox/spiralUnbox); hand-emitted Lean for native_closure_union_rec exits 70 and rust_static_closure_chain 40, as C -> next: main: next pack + Lean probe of the 2 samples | lap 22-drive 20:02 (subagent2): lab agents-note.py for the boxed closure fields (1 anchor, stacks with the Calyx/OpenQasm and eBPF doc scripts on one copy) -> next: main, with tomorrow's pack")
inl note_of_lean_backend_23 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 23u32, "2026-10-27T09:26Z", "main", "10-27 05:26 main: 10-27 05:25 main: Matrix-bundle review single-flight-20261027-042215 (-Suite all -Native -ReuseNative, 7,367 rows): DISAGREE 0 under both oracles; the one agree-fail is the long-known dynamic_array_bounds_negative Rust row (known vs C). Lean clause 1 (every row keeps its verdict) is GREEN: 458 of 458 rows have their baseline compile status and stdout. Lean clause 2 (median native_ms within 1.2x of rc4) is VOID on this run: all 458 Lean rows were native-reused. The memo key holds test.ps1's Lean clause (+leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0, unstaged vs HEAD's rc4), so those entries were really measured on stable, by single-flight-20261025-010749, the only run that executed all 458. Its rc4 counterpart single-flight-20261023-135519 (432 rows) gives a raw stable/rc4 ratio of 1.46 over the 432 shared rows (median per-row 1.435), over the threshold. But the C rows of the same two runs went 993 -> 3011 ms median (3.0x), so the 10-25 run was on a far busier box; against C in its own run, Lean went from 4.41x to 2.13x. Load confounds the clause, so it can't be decided from these runs. Decider (rule fixed before running): TEMP matrix-bundle/lean-ab.ps1, 24 evenly spaced of the 458 main.lean files x 3 rounds, rc4 vs stable interleaved per pair with alternating order, CPU = user+kernel over the process tree (Job Object), RED if any pair's exit or stdout differs, GREEN iff the median per-pair stable/rc4 CPU ratio is <= 1.2. Queued once kit's release lease on its tree clears.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_24 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 24u32, "2026-10-27T12:06Z", "main", "10-27 08:06 main: Lean speed clause GREEN on the node (job-1793101473069; elan with both toolchains installed there for it): 24 evenly spaced of the 458 main.lean files x 3 rounds, 72 interleaved pairs with alternating order, CPU = user+kernel over the process tree. Median CPU rc4 2.31 s, stable 2.31 s, median per-pair ratio stable/rc4 1.000 (rule: <= 1.2), and 0 pairs whose exit or stdout differs. With clause 1 already GREEN (458 of 458 verdicts kept), every clause of the bundle rule is GREEN. The remaining step is the rule's -Accept -AcceptToolchain run, which must reproduce single-flight-20261027-042215 row for row; it is queued next, locally, because the oracle lives in this box's cache.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_25 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 25u32, "2026-10-27T23:21Z", "main", "10-27 19:21 main: Bundle accept GREEN (accept-6, job-1793136844465, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 17:34 to 19:1x; ran in slot 2 against the TRAIN-frozen lib). test.ps1 exit 0; 7,367 rows accepted into spiral-bin baseline EXPECTED.tsv, with toolchain.tsv recorded (SPIRAL_CC pinned to scoop gcc 15.2). Against review single-flight-20261027-042215 under the n16/n17 rule (set before running): 2 differing cells, both ALLOWED, 0 blocking. samples/portable_convert_parse on Rust and on Lua is residual-only (same exit and stdout) and calls lib convert, which moved after the review (radix land 15:40). The accept-2 blocker is gone: mega_omniledger_erp_kernel/all_terminals [Fsharp] ran within the fixed budget (test.ps1's F# native paths now honour max(60, the job's TimeoutSec), so its matrix Timeouts 180 applies). The Zig coverage slice, the 620-row contracts on Zig and the Lean clauses of this bundle now stand as the oracle. Baseline backup in TEMP matrix-bundle/baseline-before-accept-20261027-173412. Unblocks: closing lab/ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY (spent; bundle.ps1 needs no re-apply now), the CCMR land (it waits on this plus TRAIN), and then the pack-5n install.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_26 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 26u32, "2026-10-30T23:42Z", "main", "10-30 19:4x main R3 groom (BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): next step, owner main: the title's 'BackendSwitch records without a Lean key' is now measured by BACKEND-SWITCH-PROTOTYPES's strict-blast run (scratch lib whose backend_switch makes a missing non-unit arm a Spiral-time error; C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1030\\backend-switch\\strict-blast.txt). Lean's current fallback is the unbound identifier backend_switch_has_no_Lean_arm_in_lib_spiral (found only by lake). From that census: list the reached functions without a Lean arm and add the arms worth having, smallest first.")
inl note_of_lean_backend_27 () = Note ("LEAN-BACKEND", 27u32, "2026-10-31T03:21Z", "main", "10-30 23:21 main: lab/LEAN-BACKEND is ARCHIVED (user, 10-30 22:5x: the lab dir didn't work and drifted; drafts don't live outside the repo). Archive 20261030-232045 under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive. Restore this folder with: pwsh i574n.github/scripts/scratch-archive.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab -Restore '%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045\\manifest.tsv' -Only 'LEAN-BACKEND\\*' -RestoreTo C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab. Resume this item's work in its real place in the repo, not in lab.")
