inl tree_sitter_spiral () = Task ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", "A real tree-sitter grammar for Spiral (both editions) to replace the borrowed tree-sitter-rust in apps/zed: top-level inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open, test blocks with ///> targets, doc runs, macros ($\"...\" $'...' !!!!), so highlights/outline/indents are exact and runnables.scm can tag each `test name =` for gutter run buttons; generate edition-3 symbol tokens from the same table as the compiler tokenizer (SPIRAL3-EDITIONS); 2026-10-14 01:25 lane 1 built the cheapest unblocking grammar (uncommitted, apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral: grammar.js, generated src/ parser.c ABI 14 with tree-sitter-cli 0.25.10, queries/highlights.scm, runnables.scm, outline.scm, test/corpus/test_headers.txt): every token is a whole line; kinds test_header (prec 6: test_keyword /test[ \\t]+/, test_name, test_signature as immediate tokens), target_directive (///>), doc_comment (///), line_comment (//), definition_line (inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open/and at column 0), indented_line, other_line; tree-sitter test 3/3; gate on the 583-file corpus (spiral lib+apps, eoie src, dice, alphabet, polyglot lib): 375 real test blocks, 375 headers found, 375 correct by row and name, recall 100%, precision 100%, files with parse errors 0 of 583 (the borrowed Rust grammar scored 71%/82%); highlighting lost vs the Rust-borrowed queries (corpus captures): keyword 18144, number 65914, operator 61920, punctuation 145808, string 8214 nodes covering 1.33 MB of the 3.35 MB corpus (40%: Spiral primes open Rust char literals, so most of it was wrong), string.escape 32452, type 11466, type.builtin 4701, boolean 465, variable.special 1128; the new queries capture test_keyword 375, test_name 375, target_directive 660, doc_comment 2042; the spiral-zed language server's semantic tokens (legend: variable, symbol, string, number, operator, unary_operator, comment, keyword, parenthesis, type_variable, escaped_char, unescaped_char, number_suffix, escaped_var, type; a Spiral-aware scanner with macros, (* *) comments, primes) cover keyword, type, string, escapes, number, operator, brackets, comment; not covered: builtin types (i32 etc. come back as variable), booleans (variable), delimiters as their own class; wiring left for after a commit: extension.toml [grammars.spiral] repository https://github.com/i574n/spiral, rev = the commit with apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, path = apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral; languages/spiral/config.toml grammar = spiral; replace languages/spiral/{highlights,outline}.scm with the grammar's queries, add runnables.scm, drop brackets.scm and indents.scm (they name Rust nodes); set languages.Spiral.semantic_tokens to combined; then the manual Zed check in apps/zed/README", Feature, P0, D6, 98u32, Blocked, "", "zed,grammar,editor,team:org,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tree_sitter_spiral () = Planning ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", Minutes 900u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_1 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:54Z", "lane-b", "wired (uncommitted): extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev 3c76d3ed path apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, grammar = spiral, grammar queries + runnables.scm, brackets/indents.scm emptied (old brackets query fails to compile on this grammar; user: git rm), .zed/settings.json semantic_tokens combined; generate reproduces src byte-identical, test 3/3, all 5 queries compile; left: Zed manual check")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_2 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 2u32, "2026-10-14T19:25Z", "lane-b", "checked against the compiler's own test-block authority (installed pack-1d --test-blocks): on 582 .spi/.spir files, Zed runnables.scm tags 420 rows, the compiler reports 420 test blocks, 420 equal, 0 false, 0 missed")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_3 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:48Z", "main-thread", "06:48 groom: 10-15: zed test-at-row now takes spans from the compiler (--source-blocks, pack-1g), so the grammar only drives highlighting/outline/runnables. Left: the manual gutter check in Zed (user).")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_4 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:35Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:35 lap 1 grain: unchanged since 10-15: grammar in apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, wiring waits for a commit rev (extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev) and the user's Zed check; nothing CPU-light left for agents beyond keeping the corpus test current Next: re-run the grammar's corpus parse over today's lib (401 test headers) to catch drift from new syntax (one light tree-sitter parse)")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_5 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:32 lap 2 grain, corrects lap 1 (wiring waits for a commit rev): apps/zed/extension.toml already pins [grammars.spiral] rev 3c76d3ed (2026-10-14 07:25), that commit is on github-i574n/main, its grammar.js has test_header, and git diff 3c76d3ed..HEAD over apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral is empty, so the pinned rev is the current grammar. Drift check without the tree-sitter CLI (not installed): the grammar is line-based and its test_header token is exactly ^test[ \\t]+ followed by a name of non-space non-= characters; over lib today that regex matches 402 lines in 40 files, the same 402 that ^test\\b matches (Grep count per file identical), so every compiler test header is a runnable and nothing new escapes it. Nothing CPU-light left for agents; what remains is the user's Zed check (ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES). Next: none for agents until the user reports the gutter check")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_6 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 6u32, "2026-10-19T15:23Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:23 lap 5 drift check widened from lib to every repo under C:\\home\\git: ^test\\b and the grammar's test_header shape ^test[ \\t]+[^ \\t=]+ both match 922 lines in the same 133 .spi/.spir files (lib, apps, lab, blog engine, dice, alphabet, eoie src, tibia, x, polyglot), so the pinned grammar rev 3c76d3ed still makes every test header in every consumer a runnable. Nothing else for agents; the user's Zed check stays (ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES, now incl. the worktree task gap).")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_7 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 7u32, "2026-10-19T15:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:40 lap 6 grain, the next grammar gap: outline.scm captures only test_header, because the grammar's definition_line is a single token (inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open/and plus the rest of the line) with no name field. Zed's outline panel and symbol search therefore list tests but none of the definitions (a lib file such as sm'.spi shows 42 tests and none of its functions). Proposed change: definition_line becomes seq(definition_keyword token, field name token.immediate([^\\s(:=]+), optional rest) at the same prec, and outline.scm gets (definition_line keyword @context name @name) @item, so definitions show up next to tests while the test headers stay exact. It needs tree-sitter generate (CLI not installed here), a grammar commit, and a new pinned rev in extension.toml, so it is the user's (or a CLI-equipped) step after the current gutter check.")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_8 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 8u32, "2026-10-19T16:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:40 lap 8 grain: the outline gap from lap 6 is staged as lab/TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL/definition_line.py (dry run by default; anchors ok): definition_line becomes seq(definition_keyword token at prec 2 that absorbs a leading and and a trailing rec, optional name field token.immediate of an identifier or a parenthesized operator such as (~#), optional definition_rest), the same shape as test_header; outline.scm gains a definition_line capture with keyword as context, skipping open via #not-match?; a corpus case covers open, inl rec, and inl, let, an operator and nominal. Regex check over lib: all 2,569 lines the current definition_line matches get a name under the new keyword+name pair, so no line falls into an error node. No query references definition_line today, so highlights are unaffected. Left: tree-sitter CLI (not installed) for generate + test, then a new grammar rev in extension.toml")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_9 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 9u32, "2026-10-19T17:15Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:16 lap 9 grain: definition_line.py proven with the real CLI on a scratch copy (npx tree-sitter-cli@0.25.10, the version of the committed parser.c, generate --abi 14). First run failed 2 of 4 corpus cases: the lexer preferred the longer definition_rest token over definition_name, and test_headers.txt still expected the old leaf definition_line. Fixed in the script: definition_name is token.immediate(prec(1, ...)) and the script rewrites that expectation (anchored once). Now: tree-sitter test 4/4, all 203 lib .spi/.spir files parse with 0 errors, outline query on am'_prototypes.spi yields item/context/name captures (array', a'). npm latest is 0.27.1 (ABI 15) = a separate bump after a Zed ABI check. Next: after the user's Zed check, definition_line.py --apply on apps/zed, generate --abi 14, test, new rev in extension.toml")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_10 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 10u32, "2026-10-19T17:41Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:41 lap 10 grain: definition_line.py now also appends highlights for the new nodes ((definition_keyword) @keyword, (definition_name) @function; guarded so it applies once). Rerun on a fresh scratch copy with tree-sitter-cli 0.25.10: generate --abi 14 ok, test 4/4, highlights/runnables/outline queries all run without query errors on lib testing.spi, and highlight captures go from 52 to 116 there (every inl/let/union/open line now colours its keyword and name; the outline keeps excluding open). Zed loads the grammar from extension.toml rev 3c76d3ed (on github-i574n/main, equal to the worktree grammar), so this change reaches Zed only through a commit + rev bump by the user. Next: user's Zed check, then --apply on apps/zed, generate, test, commit, rev bump")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_11 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 11u32, "2026-10-19T17:55Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:55 lap 11 grain, latest-of-everything for the grammar CLI: tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 (npm latest) generates the definition_line grammar with LANGUAGE_VERSION 15 and passes test 4/4 on a scratch copy; Zed main pins tree-sitter at git rev 43623ec (2026-08-20), 903 commits past v0.25.0, the release that introduced ABI 15, so Zed loads ABI 15 grammars. Decision for the apply step: regenerate with 0.27.1 (default ABI 15) instead of 0.25.10 --abi 14; the committed parser.c then moves from ABI 14 to 15 in the same rev bump. Next: after the user's Zed check, definition_line.py --apply, npx tree-sitter-cli@0.27.1 generate + test, commit, rev bump (user)")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_12 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 12u32, "2026-10-19T18:27Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 14:27 lap 12: corpus proof for definition_line.py on a scratch copy (cli 0.27.1, ABI 15): tree-sitter test 4/4, and parsing all 48 lib/spiral .spi files gives 1380 definition lines, every one with a definition_name, and 0 ERROR or MISSING nodes; the outline query on apps/cells console.spi lists the operator (~!\\\\), show_value, write_line and display. Ready to apply after the user's Zed check")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_13 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 13u32, "2026-10-22T04:17Z", "main", "00:17 applied in the tree (lab drain; uncommitted for the user): apply-grammar.ps1 -Apply ran definition_line.py on apps/zed, regenerated with tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 (parser.c LANGUAGE_VERSION 15) and tree-sitter test passed 4 of 4 (new corpus test/corpus/definitions.txt). Corpus recheck on the tree grammar: all 82 lib/spiral .spi files parse with 0 ERROR or MISSING nodes, 1,851 definition lines. Changed: grammar.js, src/grammar.json, node-types.json, parser.c, tree_sitter/array.h, outline.scm, test_headers.txt, new definitions.txt (highlights.scm shows a 4-line change the script did not check, possibly older). Left for the user: look in Zed, commit apps/zed, push, set extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev to that commit. Removed spiral/lab/TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL (2 files).")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_14 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 14u32, "2026-10-23T21:41Z", "main", "2026-10-23 17:41 main: lib grew today (erlang_process, otp_actor with new_with_init/new_with_self, otp_supervisor, step_runtime, sm' C arms, gleam_erlang 1.x process/platform), so the 0-ERROR corpus claim of 10-22 (82 files) needs a re-parse before the user commits apps/zed; tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 is no longer on this box (it lived in a pruned session scratch), so the re-parse waits for that CLI (a download, the user's call or the next session's). Still left for the user: the Zed look, commit apps/zed, push, set extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev.")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_15 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 15u32, "2026-10-24T04:38Z", "main", "2026-10-24 00:38 main: re-parse done. tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 (still the latest, published 10-08) reinstalled with npm install -g, so it no longer lives in a session scratch. All 104 lib/spiral .spi files (82 on 10-22) parse with the tree grammar in apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral (paths file, since sm'.spi breaks glob arguments): 2,591 definition_line nodes, every one with a definition_name (1,851 on 10-22). Correction to the earlier claims: '0 ERROR or MISSING nodes' proves nothing for this grammar. It is total by design (anything unrecognized is other_line), and junk text such as ')))' or 'inl f (((x' parses without ERROR (controls in scratch ts-broken*.spi), and --stat 'failed parses' does not count ERROR nodes either. The property that can fail is a definition_line without a name: control 'inl  = 3' gives 3 definition lines and 2 names, so 2,591 of 2,591 is a real pass. Left for the user: the Zed look, commit apps/zed, push, set extension.toml [grammars.spiral] rev.")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_16 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 16u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 3 10:09 (subagent2): blocked on the same user check; grammar current -> next: user check | lap 4 10:32 (subagent2): blocked: user's in-Zed check -> next: user check | lap 7 12:01 (subagent2): (no new grain beyond lap 6 outline proposal; needs the tree-sitter CLI) blocked on CLI + user check -> next: see lap 6 | lap 13 14:41 (subagent2): wider corpus for the definition_line grammar (scratch, cli 0.27.1): all 1159 sample main.spi files (incl. the mega samples) parse with 0 failures at ~6.9 MB/s, on top of lap 12's 48 lib files -> next: after the user's Zed check: apply, generate, rev bump | lap 14 15:03 (subagent2): corpus-proven (48 lib + 1159 samples, 0 errors); waiting -> next: user's Zed check | lap 15 15:10 (subagent2): staged lab apply-grammar.ps1: refuses if the grammar dir or outline.scm is dirty, runs definition_line.py, regenerates with the cached cli 0.27.1, runs tree-sitter test, prints the ABI and the user's commit + rev-bump step; dry run ok (found languages/spiral/tasks.json untracked, outside its guard) -> next: after the user's Zed check: apply-grammar.ps1 -Apply | lap 17 16:43 (subagent2): unchanged (apply-grammar.ps1 staged) -> next: user's Zed check | lap 19 18:56 (subagent2): unchanged (definition_line.py corpus-proven, apply-grammar.ps1 staged) -> next: user's Zed check | lap 20 19:05 (subagent2): tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 still npm latest (modified 10-08), so the ABI 15 regeneration plan stands -> next: user's Zed check")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_17 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 17u32, "2026-10-24T19:14Z", "main", "main 15:1x (edition 3 to the end, user 15:0x): grammar.js definition_keyword now also matches the edition-3 symbol spellings (:= :~ :== :| :! :? :+ :< :&, and ^ for rec) next to the words; tree-sitter generate (cli 0.27.1) ok in scratch ts-grammar; control file parses := g / :| shape / :~ ^ loop as definition_line with their definition_name. Next: parse the converted corpus (edition3-readiness/symbols) and require the same definition_name count as the words originals; then extension.toml rev bump with the user's commit.")
inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_18 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 18u32, "2026-10-24T20:33Z", "main", "main 16:4x: converted-corpus check done (scratch edition3-readiness/ts-names.ps1, query (definition_name) @name, cli 0.27.1, scratch ts-grammar with the symbol-aware definition_keyword): lib corpus 136 files, words 3,174 definition names vs symbols 3,171. The 3 missing are definitions added by lands after the 15:1x conversion (crypto.spi 16:21 hmac_sha1 and hmac_sha1_tag; xml.spi 15:39 zig_sequence_width), so the 134 files unchanged since have identical name sets in both spellings. The grammar is ready for edition-3 sources; the tree's apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral now holds only grammar.js (regenerate src/ with tree-sitter generate before the user's commit + extension.toml rev bump).")
