inl note_of_tree_sitter_spiral_25 () = Note ("TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", 25u32, "2026-11-05T09:52Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:0x compiler (claimed: Planned, owner main), ran the decision record's PASS rule. tree-sitter CLI 0.27.1 (npx tree-sitter-cli@latest; CC = scoop gcc 15.2). (a) PASS: tree-sitter test in apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral, 6/6 (definitions, edition-3 symbols, test headers with targets / primed names / non-header 'test' words, edition-3 test symbol). (b) PASS: 0 parse errors over the CURRENT corpus, 1589/1589 files: 270 lib .spi/.spir (the lib was reshaped since the record's 583) + 1319 compiler sample .spi/.spir (record: 1159). (c) PASS, exact: queries/runnables.scm captures 1006 of 1006 ':# name' headers, matched one-to-one by file, line and name (0 missing, 0 extra), including 87 static module blocks, which Cells also treats as runnable. (d) NOT RUN, blocked: this profile has no Zed logs and no extensions dir (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Zed holds only db, hang_traces, languages, prompts; the 10-28 wipe), so the dev extension is not installed. Installing a dev extension is a one-time action in Zed's UI ('zed: install dev extension' -> apps/zed). After that, an off-screen muted launch can read Zed.log for the grammar load. Left: that one step, then (d).")
