inl qualified_union_cases () = Task ("QUALIFIED-UNION-CASES", "Union cases cannot be qualified by module: `vitality.Slain _` in a pattern fails with \"The module does not have the key: Slain\" (apps/tibia/hunt.spi 2026-10-12), so every caller needs a local `open vitality`; decide per edition whether cases become module members (edition 3 candidate); user decision 2026-10-12 18:53: both: module.Case accepted in patterns and constructors (resolved through the module path like values), plus a clearer error when an unqualified case is ambiguous between opened modules; 02:34 module.Case done in patterns (constructors already worked) in both cores, uncommitted, rides pack-0004: a qualified PatNominal path that resolves on the term side to a union-case constructor (ho_fun -> nominal whose body is TyUnion) is typed as that case (scrutinee unified with the nominal, then the PatUnbox path), recorded by node identity in qualified_union_case_patterns, and Infer's fill pass rewrites it to PatUnbox so Prepass lowers a plain case test; plain nominal patterns (mod.num x) are untouched; probes on both cores (Debug): qualified case patterns with open exit 4, without open (qualified constructor + patterns) exit 6, qualified plain nominal exit 7; open: the clearer ambiguity error for an unqualified case shared by two opened modules; no harness sample added (standing no-new-samples rule; ask the user); 05:11 in pack-0004 Release (both suites DISAGREE 0, blessed); 06:22 also stable in pack-0005 (both cores parity); 07:02 regression sample added (user allowed regression samples 10-13): samples/qualified_union_case_pattern (two modules, qualified constructor + patterns without open, expected exit 6; C exit 6 on the pack-0005 DLL); enters the oracle at the next pack's bless", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,language", "current", "current")
