contracts 669, examples 3,069, frontier 50, mega 5; 0 missing/regressed, DISAGREE 0; hopac oracle agree 2,321), 27 new rows (WGSL union rows agree with C; FOR-D repros); sweep so far (hopac Debug builds of mechanical unifications): startParentWatcher, SpiralHub, main BUILD but are server/entry code whose hopac-only lines carry shutdown exit codes and diagnostics that the batch suites never exercise (HOPAC-WARM-SERVER territory), so they are review candidates, not applied; WDiffPrepass fails (needs hopac's PrepassNominal), Graph fails (SchemaPathId, 81 errors), Utils fails (duplicate module, 57 errors); 21:41 sweep results (hopac Debug builds of mechanical unifications, tmp/unify/try/summary.tsv): BUILD with single-flight text: startParentWatcher, SpiralHub, main, new_server (server/entry code; hopac-only shutdown/diagnostic lines the batch suites never exercise: review, not applied); FAIL: WDiffPrepass 12 (PrepassNominal), Graph 81 (SchemaPathId), Utils 57 and CodegenAdapter 70 (modules both cores define elsewhere), WDiff 28 (ConcurrentDictionary vs Dictionary), ServerUtils 43 (GraphPathId vs string), Prepass 22 (ConcurrentDictionary); pattern: the failures are two type families, interned ids (TermNameId/TypeNameId/GraphPathId/SchemaPathId vs string) and concurrent memo tables (ConcurrentDictionary vs Dictionary); plan (next step of HOPAC-WATER-OIL): one per-core adapter pair early in the file that defines those types and their few operations (single-flight: type TermNameId = string with identity Ops, MemoTable = Dictionary; hopac: the real interned ids and ConcurrentDictionary), after which most pairs share one text written against the adapter names; 00:22 classification: CodegenAdapter is a legitimate adapter pair (each side maps its core's PartEval result shapes, join-point cells, key tuples and memo tables onto the interface the shared codegens call), so it stays a pair by design: water-oil's target shape is shared text + per-core adapters like this one; Utils pair unification in a candidate (shared member-constrained get_default/memoize over TryGetValue/TryAdd for Dictionary and ConcurrentDictionary, one shared module Utils, hopac's private copy removed), Debug builds of both cores running; 00:34 Utils candidate (tmp/unify/utils) builds both cores in Debug with 0 errors; rides the next pack after the accept; 01:33 applied to spiral_compiler.fs (uncommitted, Debug builds of both cores 0 errors each, Release suites pending in the next pack): Utils shared; Graph -> GraphIdentity adapter pair + shared Graph; ServerUtils shared; WDiff shared (hopac-only DiagJson parse seeding moved behind observeParsedStatement: BlockParsingHopac became an adapter pair whose single-flight side observes nothing; IdentityAdapter gains termMapToModuleMembers/typeMapToModuleMembers identity converters and covers 7 id families; single-flight HopacExtensions gains sequential A/S array modules); pairs 14 -> 12 (+1 adapter pair); remaining real pairs: Infer, Prepass, PartEval, CodegenFsharp, SignalRSupervisor (3,480-line diff) + by-design adapters (CodegenAdapter, GraphIdentity, BlockParsingHopac); 01:44 startParentWatcher + SpiralHub shared behind a ServerHooks adapter pair (hopac: DiagJson/BigStack exits and diag_save_enabled trace gate; single-flight: Environment.Exit/Kill, trace files on), applied (both cores Debug 0 errors); main classified as a by-design entry pair (hopac's entry boots Progress88, BigStack terminal flow and the console HUD: the edge where hopac belongs); new_server candidate building (delivery ledger note behind ServerHooks.noteClientErrorsDelivered); 03:12 pack-0003 VERIFIED on both cores: single-flight-20261013-020515 and hopac-20261013-022459 each 3,822 parity + 8 Gleam residual rows (string prelude panic messages), DISAGREE 0: the Utils/Graph/ServerUtils/WDiff/ServerHooks/startParentWatcher/SpiralHub/new_server unification is behavior-neutral; pairs 14 -> 10 (by-design adapters: BlockParsingHopac, CodegenAdapter, GraphIdentity, ServerHooks, main; real pairs left: Infer, Prepass, PartEval, CodegenFsharp, SignalRSupervisor); 03:21 CodegenFsharp analysed (not applied): hopac text as shared fails single-flight with 94 errors; single-flight text as shared fails hopac with only 14: 4 id comparisons (union tag names via UnionTagIdOps.text, layout keys via LayoutFieldNameIdOps.matchesText, both exist in both cores once the CodegenAdapter pair moves above CodegenFsharp) and the method/closure join-point lookups; hopac's lookups are ~300 lines of fail-closed recovery each (EvalWorklist replay drain, sequential-authority retry, owner-missing aliasing), so the plan is: shared text = single-flight's CodegenFsharp, and the per-core lookup becomes an adapter hook codegenFsharpMethodBody/codegenFsharpClosureBody (hopac side = its current recovery block extracted verbatim, single-flight side = the plain dictionary read, no DeadPureLetElision so F# output stays byte-identical); then Infer/Prepass/PartEval/SignalRSupervisor remain; 2026-10-13 23:34 user decision: stays P0 while gpt5parallel lives (every shared-section change still costs double)", Feature, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "PACK-10", "compiler,hopac,maintenance,main", "current", "current")
