inl documents_tectonic () = Task ("DOCUMENTS-TECTONIC", "Use tectonic instead of xelatex everywhere (user decision 2026-10-12 18:53): alphabet apps/documents PDFs (crowbook) on Ubuntu, Windows CI and locally, replacing the apt texlive packages and the choco MiKTeX step; tectonic is one binary that fetches TeX packages on demand; check that crowbook can be pointed at it (or run crowbook --to tex then tectonic), keep the Hangul PDF working (font), and mirror any dice counterpart; run 38312799493 (17:47 commit): Ubuntu green, Windows still red in workflow.ps1; 20:24 Kino lane (uncommitted, alphabet): crowbook drives tectonic directly (--set tex.command tectonic): documents.livemd (edited with mix spiral.edit) adds it to the pdf args and to the no-args pdf fallback; documents.spi re-exported, documents.fsx/.rs regenerated by build.ps1 -fast (diffs ~9-10k lines, mostly compiler drift since their last regeneration, review before committing); gh-pages.yml: texlive apt packages removed (pandoc + fonts-nanum-coding stay), MiKTeX step -> wtfjoke/setup-tectonic@v3, diagnostics step -> tectonic; scripts/init.ps1: apt pandoc + fonts-nanum-coding, cargo binstall -y tectonic; local tectonic 0.17.0 via scoop; build.ps1 -fast passed (RUST-OK, exit 0; dist has nota.md.pdf, nota.hangul.md.pdf, README.md.pdf); Hangul page renders with NanumGothicCoding; dice has no TeX counterpart; CI verification pending on the next push; 06:23 done per the Kino lane handback (committed by the user in alphabet 10-12 20:26): documents.livemd, gh-pages workflow and init.ps1 use tectonic 0.17 via scoop; Hangul PDF checked; build.ps1 -fast RUST-OK", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "alphabet,ci,documents", "current", "current")
