inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_4 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 4u32, "2026-10-22T09:23Z", "eoie", "05:23 recount of the 06:55 groom's first targets: hand-written .rs islands without a .spi owner are down from 26 files to 0 outside tests; the 14 that remain are tests/*.rs (846 lines), tracked on EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS. So the rewrite starts from generated crates only: the GADT command algebra replaces rust_global blobs and host-macro clusters, guided by the EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY census (1500 macros, eoie_jobs 62 the largest).")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_5 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 5u32, "2026-10-22T22:09Z", "eoie-lane", "18:09 legacy-construct counts over src/*/*.spi (text counts, no compile). Live tree (644 files): rust_global 386, host blocks $'{ 176, concat5 1,172, Rc::<str>::from 616, lines with a host macro 1,502. GE2+H tree (682 files): rust_global 386 (unchanged), host blocks 168, concat5 556 (-52%), Rc wraps 570, host-macro lines 1,371 (-9%). The E2 heal wave halves string concatenation but does not touch rust_global, the largest block of non-idiomatic code (386 blobs). rust_global removal needs the OS boundary package (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY) as the place the remaining host code moves to. These counts are the baseline for measuring each later wave.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_6 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 6u32, "2026-10-23T23:24Z", "eoie", "19:24 eoie: design start, from apps/tibia's idiom (style reference only: tibia/src/readiness.spi). A private GADT 'ready group' can only be built by gate functions (attack_gate returns gate attack_group = Open (ready attack_group) | ClosedUntil ms), and commands take the proof (Strike : ready attack_group), so acting without passing the gate doesn't typecheck. eoie mappings where a recorded bug becomes a type error: (1) job gate: union private admitted resource = SlotAdmitted :: ticket -> admitted heavy_slot | WindowGranted :: window_id -> admitted machine_window; supervise's child start takes admitted heavy_slot * admitted machine_window, and the window request takes admitted heavy_slot, so window-before-slot (17 of 87 heavy jobs on the 10-21 binary, EOIE-WINDOW-LIVE-QUEUE note 4) can't be written. (2) agile mutation: state_written takes locked state_lock, minted only by the lock acquire, so an unlocked write is a type error. (3) release launch: land takes gates_passed stage, minted by the gate checks (today's typecheck-marker and O-installed gates). (4) tree writes: write verbs take lease_clear root, minted by the lease/window check (EOIE-TREE-READ-RECORD). First slice when this starts: (1) in eoie_job_gate, a pure-model change with the proofs in a model module and the gate loop returning them. Order: after the train's releases install, since eoie_job_gate is touched by HIJK/L.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_7 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 7u32, "2026-10-23T23:24Z", "eoie", "19:24 eoie: slice (1)'s pure model drafted (scratch f6/src/eoie_job_admission/model.spi). A private GADT admitted resource (SlotAdmitted :: ticket -> admitted heavy_slot | WindowGranted :: id -> admitted machine_window) is minted only by slot_gate and window_gate; window_gate takes an admitted heavy_slot, and child_start takes both proofs. Tests: the slot, then window, then start path carries both names; a later ticket and a full queue wait with reasons. Typecheck runs in the post-block batch; wiring into eoie_job_gate after the train installs.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_8 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 8u32, "2026-10-24T23:43Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 1800m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D8 at 0%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_9 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 9u32, "2026-11-01T18:18Z", "kit", "11-01 14:18 kit: raised P1 -> P0 under the user's 18:1x direction (typefeatureset to the max on kit itself, rewrite if needed). Its GADT command algebra is the in-crate half; KIT-TYPED-CRATES is the between-crates half (typed bindings, derived codecs, model crates built once). They are planned together after KIT-TYPED-CRATES S0 (the bootstrapping-model study).")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_10 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 10u32, "2026-11-03T08:20Z", "kit", "11-03 04:1x kit groom (user: kit keeps drifting; groom so it catches up). Its CLI-facing child is now KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE (S1..S7): verb families parse into typed command unions in x's apps/client shape (closed command union, flag/switch unions, draft record through result steps, typed exports, parse tests), plus GADT-indexed payloads. Measured: 1 typed command union in 506 packages.")
