inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_3 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 3u32, "2026-10-18T23:35Z", "claude", "Runner lab/EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC/one-call-runner.ps1 on build 1 (19:15): 12/34 green, exactly the target set 1 2 3 7 8 9 10 11 13 14 25 26. Next slice in build 3: crate eoie_do_facts (682 generated lines; sha2, regex, serde_json; globs via a new eoie_do_read_matching export) for hash (28), env + exists (19), nearest (18), json get (20), lines count by (22), files count by extension (17); fact union + grammar tests; eoie_do decode routes any fact verb to FactProgram; facts and read queries cannot share one program yet. Still red after it: run/stop/errors (6 15 16 24 33), git (12 23 31 32), dirs (4), diff (5), append (21), table (27), copy (29), job (30), lab audit (34).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_4 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 4u32, "2026-10-18T23:57Z", "claude", "Build 3 (19:50): runner 17/34 green, adding 17 18 19 20 28 (facts crate). 22 was red because the program tokenizer dropped the backslash of unknown escapes (\\w became w); build 4 keeps \\x unless x is a quote or backslash (regression test regex_escapes_survive_the_tokenizer). Build 4 also adds crate eoie_do_process (823 lines; sysinfo, regex; per-run job object so stops take the tree; clears NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath so cmd /c finds root scripts) for run/until/background/stop, tail output, search in output, errors in output by, processes where command ~; a scratch probe matched cases 6 15 16 33 byte for byte (15 depends on 5-digit pids: its header pads pid to the widest pid). table count by (27) joined the facts crate, probe matches. Left after build 4: 4 dirs, 5 diff, 12 23 31 32 git (need a setup grammar: git init/commit at/write/append line), 21 append, 24 edit+run in one program, 29 copy, 30 job in do, 34 lab audit.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_5 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 5u32, "2026-10-19T00:33Z", "claude", "Builds 4-6 (20:32): runner 24/34 green. Build 4: process crate live (6 15 16 33), table count by (27), tokenizer escape fix (22). Build 5b: pid column fixed at width 7 so the processes table no longer depends on pid length (spec case 15 header updated to it); runner rule: the spaces after a placeholder cell are flexible, since <HH:mm> and <pid> are padded at placeholder width in the spec; quoted run words keep their quotes. Build 6: edits then runs in one program (24): eoie_do validates and commits edits, then eoie_do_process_rejection (checked before any write) and eoie_do_process_after_edits (report, counts, failed) give one combined receipt; a failed edit runs nothing. eoie_do sits at 991 generated lines after part_at/printed became let; the next eoie_do feature needs a split. Still red: 4 dirs, 5 diff, 12 23 31 32 git (setup grammar), 21 append, 29 copy, 30 job, 34 lab audit.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_6 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 6u32, "2026-10-19T01:01Z", "claude", "Build 8b (21:01): runner 25/34 green; case 4 dirs/tag/count by landed in the facts crate (930 generated lines). A dirs line owns the tag and count lines below it; tag expressions combine <file> ~ \"re\" with and, or, not (or of ands). Build 7 had a panic: real program records carry empty fields, which the hand-encoded probe never had (lesson: probe with trailing empty fields). The test that nested a nullary constructor in a pattern (FactParsed DirsDetail) failed to parse; it now asserts through rejection_at. Still red (9): 5 diff, 12 23 31 32 git (setup grammar), 21 append, 29 copy, 30 job in do, 34 lab audit.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_7 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 7u32, "2026-10-19T01:05Z", "claude", "Case 5 diff (21:20) deferred to its own crate: written into eoie_do_facts it pushed the crate to 1,047 generated lines (gate 1,000). Profile: outcome_merged 160 and receipt_counts 92 lines, because each { state with ... } arm rebuilds a 30-field tally. A typed counter union over an Rc<RefCell<[u64; 30]>> barely helped (1,052): per-arm payload rebinding and one let per literal argument eat the savings, and inl->let on small helpers made it worse (1,065). Facts sources restored to the build 8b set (regenerates byte-identical). Plan: eoie_do_tables crate (diff by keys on columns; maybe absorb table count by) routed like facts. The primitive and grammar draft were tested to compile; the spec case 5 key column is one space wider than the spec's own widest-cell rule and needs the same whitespace correction as case 1.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_8 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 8u32, "2026-10-19T01:07Z", "claude", "Case 5 draft parked at lab/EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC/eoie_do_tables (crate eoie-do-tables, 330 generated lines, no extra deps; diff grammar test; scratch probe 21:07 printed the case 5 table and receipt rows a 3  b 4  changed 2  added 1  removed 0). To land: move it to src, add the workspace member and eoie_do dep, add diff to the program verbs and a TableProgram route in eoie_do decode/run (eoie_do is at 991 lines, so trim first, e.g. fold the per-crate *_run wrappers into one export call), refresh Cargo.lock offline, add the grammar notebook to the registry, and fix the spec case 5 key column (width 7, widest-cell rule).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_9 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 9u32, "2026-10-19T01:18Z", "claude", "Build 9 (21:18): diff landed as crate eoie_do_tables (330 lines), promoted from the lab draft (lab folder removed). Facts delegates any program containing diff to it, so eoie_do stays at 991 lines (one routing word added). Spec case 5 key column corrected to the widest-cell rule. Runner 26/34 green; read 5/5, ps 5/5, inherit-pipe PASS, timeout-tree 2/2. Red (8): 12 23 31 32 git (need a setup grammar), 21 append, 29 copy, 30 job in do, 34 lab audit. The next eoie_do-routed family must trim eoie_do first.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_10 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 10u32, "2026-10-19T07:31Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 03:31 eoie lane: 34/34 on a probe build of the regenerated eoie_do chain (was 26). New families, each its own crate under 1000 lines: eoie_do_write 684 (append with {clock:FMT}, copy <glob> to <dir> except ...; reads after writes go through new eoie_do_read rejection/report exports), eoie_do_git 880 (init, commit all at <iso>, history, status group by state, log count by day) plus search ... with git status in eoie_do_read, eoie_do_jobs 727 (job start/wait on real supervised eoie jobs through new eoie_jobs exports; wait resolves the newest job by label), eoie_do_lab 538 (lab audit against a backlog via agile list --json). eoie_do became a router (991 -> 270 lines) over a program_family union, with the edit engine moved to eoie_do_edit (862). The runner now runs setup blocks (eoie do programs grouped by family, or plain CLI lines); setups 12, 23 and 31 use append instead of the missing write/append-line verbs; cases 29 and 34 had one extra pad space against the +2 column convention of every other table, fixed in the spec. Release build with these is job eoie-release-install-4.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_11 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 11u32, "2026-10-19T09:40Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 05:40 eoie lane: 34/34 confirmed on the real debug build and the installed release eoie.exe (05:39). The spec cases now all run their setups through the runner. Next for the families: stale = last note older than 14 days (EOIE-LAB-AUDIT wording), gitignored files present in lab (not done yet), job notify beyond the printed line (not done yet).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_12 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 12u32, "2026-10-19T10:09Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 06:09 eoie lane: eoie.exe 06:08 has 34/34 on the installed binary. Fixed a clock-dependent bug the 06:00 release exposed: git log since <date> passed a bare date to git, which reads it as that date at the current time of day, so after 06:00 local a 10:00Z commit on the since day dropped out (case 31). A bare date now means midnight.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_13 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 13u32, "2026-10-21T10:00Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 06:00 eoie team: the one-call runner's case 30 (a job with a wall-clock timeout, cmd /c slow.cmd) starts job 'j1' in the user's real jobs home (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\jobs), so every runner pass leaves one: 40 j1 directories since 10-19, and every lane's job-change watcher reports them. Fix after the r26c release (the runner is one of its steps): the runner sets EOIE_JOBS_HOME to the case's temp directory, then the old j1 directories are deleted (they are runner fixtures by label, argv slow.cmd and cwd eoie-one-call-*).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_14 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 14u32, "2026-10-21T20:59Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:59 eoie team, progress review: 34 cases written, all green against every release today (the release gate requires >= 34); left: cases for the r30-r34 verbs (patch hunks, pattern rules, except, move, resume, views), written from real runs once those binaries exist, and the zed and grok habit shapes.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_15 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 15u32, "2026-10-21T22:35Z", "eoie-lane", "18:35 eoie team, decision on the 'zed and grok habit shapes' remainder: measured the client stores' newest writes: Zed (AppData\\Local\\Zed, 1.7 GB) 10-12 17:43, Grok (~\\.grok, 1.1 GB) 10-12 15:19, Gemini 10-11, OpenCode 10-12; Codex has no sessions in 14 days. Only Claude Code is in use (56 transcript files in 14 days). Mining dormant clients' shapes would tune the guide for nobody, so that part is deferred until a client is active again (the adoption verb in r35 reports per client and will show it). Left: tutorial cases for the r30-r34 verbs (patch hunks, pattern rules, except, move, resume, views), written from real runs after the r30-r33 install tonight (r34's after its release).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_16 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 16u32, "2026-10-22T18:27Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 14:27 the runner (lab/EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC/one-call-runner.ps1) also accepts direct-verb commands: when a command is not the do form, Get-DirectArguments tokenizes 'eoie <tokens>' with single- and double-quote groups. Setup parsing is unchanged. New TDD cases 38 (table sequences latency across two log files) and 39 (mirror check, an in-step file plus a left-only file; avoids timestamp-dependent results) are red until release I installs. Installed binary: 35/39 green (36 and 37 were already red on it). Incident while adding them: a PowerShell one-liner reused the names $t and $T (PowerShell names are case-insensitive) and wrote spec/one-call.md as 54 lines; it was restored byte-exact from release F's regen staging copy (the spec had not changed since 04:01), and the cases were re-appended with structure checks before writing. eoie-snapshot.ps1 now also covers spec, standards, compiler-contracts, docs and .github.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_17 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 17u32, "2026-10-22T20:29Z", "eoie-lane", "16:29 case 40 drafted (scratch one-call/apply-spec-case-40.ps1, applied after F's lease; dry run on copies: spec +20 lines, 0 removed, case count 39 -> 40). It is mined from today's habit: sync-lab, drain-after-F and the hook each hand-roll the lease check (list tree-leases, parse pid=, Get-Process, compare roots); the one call is 'eoie window claim <path>', with a setup 'window request tree-read 5 --label repo'. The same slice fixes a runner leak found while writing the case: the runner isolated EOIE_JOBS_HOME per case but not EOIE_WINDOWS_HOME, so any window case would have written the machine's shared window store (where every session's admissions live). It now sets EOIE_WINDOWS_HOME=<case>-windows and adds a <ms> placeholder for window ids. Green needs F's binary (tree-read class + window claim).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_18 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 18u32, "2026-10-22T21:17Z", "eoie-lane", "17:17 applied: spec case 40 (window claim) appended (39 -> 40 cases, additions only), and the runner isolates EOIE_WINDOWS_HOME per case and knows <ms>. Green after F installs.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_19 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 19u32, "2026-10-22T22:45Z", "eoie-lane", "18:45 case 40 does not run yet: its setup line starts with eoie (like commands do), but the runner passes setup tokens to eoie verbatim, so eoie sees the verb 'eoie'. The fix is drafted (one-call/apply-runner-setup-prefix.ps1: drop a leading eoie in setup statements) and applied after F2's lease. Dry run: the setup then reaches eoie, and the installed 10-21 binary answers 'unknown class tree-read', which F2's binary adds. Today's runner baseline on the installed binary: 35/40 green (36-37 wait for the new binary, 38-39 for release I, 40 for this fix plus F2). F2's runner gate needs 34.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_20 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 20u32, "2026-10-23T05:44Z", "eoie", "01:44 eoie: case 30 (job start slow.cmd as j1 timeout 2s notify; job wait j1) is load-flaky. It was red in F7's full runner pass at 00:00 under release load (Quiet mode keeps only the first output line, which matched), but green alone through the runner on the debug candidate at 01:44, and the installed binary's output matched the expected block line for line by hand. The other F7 reds are real gaps: 36 (do edit grammar), 38 (table query usage), 39 (mirror verb, release I), 40 (runner setup prefix, fixed in post-F). The release gate is greens >= 34, so one flake fits. Quiet mode should keep the first differing line instead of the first line, so a red under load says why.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_21 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 21u32, "2026-10-23T09:11Z", "eoie-lane", "05:11 install probe (spec case 40 claim): PASS. 40 green  | one-call spec: 1/1 green")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_22 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 22u32, "2026-10-23T12:50Z", "eoie", "08:50 red cases on the installed binary: 36, 38, 39 (37/40). 38 (table sequences) and 39 (mirror) are features in release I and turn green when it installs. 36 was the runner, not eoie: its setup 'do . '...'' (no eoie prefix, a quoted program spanning two lines) missed the grouped path that requires a leading 'eoie ', so it split at the line and sent an unterminated program. Fix drafted as scratch one-call/apply-runner-setup-do.ps1 (normalizes the eoie prefix before matching); on a copy of the runner and spec, 36 turns green (38/40). Applies to lab/ after HP-tail's tree lease ends.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_23 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 23u32, "2026-10-23T17:52Z", "eoie", "13:52 eoie: cases 41 and 42 added (spec/one-call.md). 41: a saved agile view (existing verbs; green on the installed binary). 42: 'job chain -- one ... -- two ...' from main's re-chaining habit (7-8 re-chains on 10-23), with expected receipts using <ms>/<pid> placeholders; red until release M installs job chain (TDD target). Not written as cases: ci parity and job doctor, whose output depends on this machine's toolchains and live processes; their acceptance lives in after-install-M instead. Runner: 39/42 (38 and 39 land with L and I, 42 with M).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_24 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 24u32, "2026-10-23T18:08Z", "eoie", "14:08 eoie: case 43 added, 'crate gate . --enforce --limit 4' over a fixture with two Spiral crates (3 and 5 generated lines): rows 'gate / tool tool.rs 3 lines ok' and 'gate / big big.rs 5 lines OVER 4', then the refused receipt. Row order traced through eoie_crate_gate's walker: dir_names reverses, the worklist fold reverses again, the final listm.rev gives tool then big. Red until L installs crate gate (TDD target). Runner: 39/43 (38 I+L, 39 I, 42 M, 43 L).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_25 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 25u32, "2026-10-23T21:00Z", "eoie", "17:00 eoie: case 47 drafted (scratch spec41/write-case47.ps1): 'eoie help env' must print env's own usage line. Today it answers with the do grammar, whose 'env <A,B>' fragment matches first, and help mirror has no line. Release O's direct-verb-lines slice makes it green. The spec can't be written now, because GE2's release holds a tree lease (since 15:47) and a repo write mid-run would block its publish. launch-O therefore appends case 47 itself, after its gates and before its snapshot, which is the one moment no release holds the tree; the case and its fix arrive together.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_26 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 26u32, "2026-10-24T01:46Z", "main", "2026-10-23 21:46 main: user direction 2026-10-23 21:4x: eoie gaps are 'reported for immediate fixes, then propagating the new usage with detailed tutorials'. So every landed eoie gap fix also adds a case here (provenance, the habit it replaces, fixture, command, exact expected output). That case is the tutorial the other lanes read, plus a one-line note to them that names it.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_27 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 27u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main: consolidated pendencies covered here (EOIE-CONSOLIDATED-INTAKE, class a): EDIT-10 (plan grammar and a minimal example in help), CLI-6 (every parse error with usage, valid values and a corrected example), CLI-4 (compact summary, full receipt). Tutorials for each new consolidated verb land here.. Spec text: Downloads/eoie-consolidated/agile_eoie.md.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_28 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 28u32, "2026-10-24T23:43Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 195m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D5 at 60%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_29 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 29u32, "2026-10-28T10:29Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_30 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 30u32, "2026-10-31T21:26Z", "kit", "10-31 17:2x kit (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK repair): Paused -> Planned. The 10-28 pause was for silence only ('Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued'), the pattern the user rejected today: a pause needs a reason AND a resume condition. Its recorded next step still stands: check whether the remaining milestone shipped (now against the installed E14F1F0B, not TRAIN2c), close it with that evidence if so, otherwise size the remaining slice. Back in 'agile next' as ready work.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_31 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 31u32, "2026-11-06T11:23Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_32 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 32u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries EDIT-10 (Plan schemas and examples are discoverable); CLI-4 (Compact output with full receipts); CLI-6 (Actionable errors). Why: 10-24 note #27: plan grammar + example in help, compact summary with full receipt, usage/valid/corrected on every parse error")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_33 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 33u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. EDIT-10 · Plan schemas and examples are discoverable · P0 · node, sbin, erp, ge2e, brz, ota · Partial / `fs-batch-write`, `fs-actions`, `patch` and `patch-matrix` advertise plans without exposing the grammar; agents recovered it from fixtures or runtime errors. Ship `patch example` / `plan init` and a minimal multi-file example in help, derived from the same schema the dispatcher uses. Make `fs-actions` column order self-describing: `copy_file` rows once ran in the reverse direction and overwrote freshly updated files with stale mirrors. *Now:* per-capability usage lines exist for every proxy verb; the plan grammar is still not in help. || CLI-4 · Compact output with full receipts · P2 · ota · Open / Stream a compact summary and store the full TSV as a receipt by default; `copy-tree` printed one row per file with no summary mode. || CLI-6 · Actionable errors · P0 · ge2e, ssam, brz, node, ota · Partial / `Not a directory`, `unsafe relative path`, `unknown help target` and arity errors cost several calls per transaction. Every parse or contract error includes the minimal usage, the inferred argument, valid values and a corrected example; validate the grammar before touching the filesystem. *Now:* top-level verbs print `intent / usage / valid / corrected`; proxy capabilities do not.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_34 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 34u32, "2026-11-09T08:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:0x local rig, the 10-28 next step answered: the remaining milestone (tutorial cases for the r30-r34 verbs, written from real runs) had NOT shipped: spec/one-call.md held 49 cases, none for patch hunks, pattern rules, except, move or resume. Added case 51 (edit patch hunks, from a real run of installed kit 5B9082C1: 2 replacements lines 1,3, and the stale rerun refusing with anchor not found + nothing written, exit 1) and case 50 (agile gap, red until KIT-GAP-INTAKE ships). Still owed from real runs: replace with a pattern rule, copy except, move (no overwrite, absolute roots), resume <backlog> --team. EDIT-10 (plan grammar in help) is now partly met: help do prints the whole do grammar incl. patch <<<hunks>>>; CLI-6 (usage on every parse error) met for agile verbs (agile add with no operands prints its shape), not for help <verb> <sub> (refused).")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_35 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 35u32, "2026-11-09T08:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:1x local rig: cases 52 (move + files, and the refused overwrite: already exists, failed files 0 moved, exit 1) and 53 (replace pattern all with a capture group, ${1}000ms) added from real runs; 53 also teaches the $1000ms trap: today it expands to nothing with exit 0, filed RIG-GAP-DO-REPLACE-PATTERN. copy except is case 29 already. resume NOT written: with an isolated KIT_JOBS_HOME its output is deterministic except free_mb=<n> (window list) and unix=<n> (resume receipt), which the runner has no placeholder for; next slice: runner placeholders <mb> and <unix>, then the resume case (fixture: init + 2 adds, resume backlog --team web). spec/one-call.md now 53 cases; 50 is red until agile gap ships, 51-53 match the installed binary.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_36 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 36u32, "2026-11-09T09:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:0x local rig: case 54 (resume backlog --team web) added from a real run with isolated KIT_JOBS_HOME and KIT_WINDOWS_HOME: next work (WSJF, team filter keeps a P0 of another team out, ~ marks a provisional estimate), empty jobs and windows sections, receipts. Spec header now documents the <ms>, <mb> and <unix> placeholders and the per-case jobs and windows homes. That closes the r30-r34 owed list (patch hunks 51, pattern rules 53, copy except 29, move 52, resume 54, views 41). kit guide renders 54 intents. Left on this item: EDIT-10 remainder (plan schema examples for proxy capabilities) and CLI-6 (help <verb> <sub>), plus a runner: none exists since the lab folder was lost, so cases are checked by hand from real runs.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_37 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 37u32, "2026-11-09T09:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "DoD: spec/one-call.md holds a case from a real run for every one-call verb family (do edit/read/facts/run/write/git/jobs/lab, table, mirror, window, agile views and gap, job chain, crate gate, grep notes, help, lint macros, resume), kit guide renders all of them, every top-level and agile parse error prints intent/usage/valid/corrected, and a runner (Spiral, in kit) rechecks every case against the installed binary in the release train. Next step: write the runner as a kit verb (spec check <file> --case n) so cases stop being checked by hand. TypeFeatures: a spec_case record (fixture, setup, command, expected) and a placeholder union (Hash, Commit, Pid, Clock, Ms, Mb, Unix) matched per cell.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_38 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 38u32, "2026-11-09T14:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:5x local rig, RUNNER CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): new package src/rig_spec_cases (cells.spi, pure, HostFree, standards 0). placeholder union with all nine spec placeholders (Elapsed, Clock, HourMinute, Hash, Commit, Pid, Ms, Mb, Unix); spec_cell union Literal text | Hole placeholder; cells_of splits an expected line at the earliest token; each hole has a typed class (Hash = exactly 64 hex, Commit = 7..40 hex, HourMinute = 5 of digits and colon, Pid/Ms/Mb/Unix = 1+ digits, Elapsed/Clock = free text up to the next literal) and is never empty; output_matches compares whole outputs line by line, CRLF tolerated, extra lines fail. The test uses real receipt shapes from the spec. NEXT STEP after the probe: case extraction (fixture/setup/command/expected fences from spec/one-call.md into a spec_case record) and the IO verb spec check <file> [--case n] that runs each case in a temporary root with KIT_*/SPIRAL_* unset.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_39 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 39u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The first probe was red and is fixed (unstaged): output_matches pinned listm.length to i32 (ETY-ValueRestriction) and uses filter instead of exists'; re-probed green. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_40 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 40u32, "2026-11-09T22:21Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:2x tibia (help pool): CASE EXTRACTION (the recorded next step) GREEN, ready for rig's train (kit is rig's; not applied). drafts\\kit\\KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC\\cells.spi (base 11599231089C) appends, pure: block_kind Fixture | Setup | Command | Expected; fixture_file { path; lines }; spec_case { title; fixture; setup : option string; command; expected }; cases_of spec folds the markdown lines with one pending block. Only '## <digits>.' headings open a case (the real spec has 54 '## ' headings for 33 cases); a fenced block attaches to the current case; fixture_of applies the spec's own path rule (no whitespace, and a '/' or a '.<letters>' tail; every other line is content of the last path); setup is None unless given. Tests: a two-case sample (Notes heading skipped; two fixture files with their lines; setup only on case 2; expected text kept line for line; a fixture-less case) and is_path on 3 paths and 5 content lines incl. '1.5', 'x.' and blank. Gate in rig's probe layout on ganymede (job tibia-spec2): Cells 3/3 (the runner core's test + both). Widths <= 120, kit bool spelling !+/!-. Trap met: 'open' is a Spiral keyword, so a record field named open fails to PARSE (first run). NEXT: the IO half: read spec/one-call.md, build each fixture in a temp root, run setup + command, output_matches against expected.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_41 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 41u32, "2026-11-09T22:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, CASE EXTRACTION BUILT (unstaged): src/rig_spec_cases/extract.spi, its own module. spec_case { number; title; fixture : list fixture_file; setup; command; expected } from \"## N. title\" headings and fixture / setup / command / expected fences; fixture blocks split by the spec's own path rule (no whitespace, and a / or a letters-only extension; v1.2 is not a path), every content line ending in LF. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (extract 1/1). NOTE: tibia drafted the same step in parallel (an append to cells.spi, 3/3) because rig did not claim before starting; rig keeps extract.spi (already in the tree and gated) and does not apply the duplicate. NEXT: the IO verb spec check <file> [--case n] (temp root per case, KIT_*/SPIRAL_* unset, output_matches), which adds a CLI verb, so after TRAIN43 snapshots.")
inl note_of_kit_one_call_spec_42 () = Note ("KIT-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 42u32, "2026-11-09T23:24Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:2x rig: parked on train:TRAIN44: the spec check verb is a new CLI verb (shared entry); case extraction is built and probe-green.")
