inl note_of_hopacsota_11 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 11u32, "2026-10-24T03:08Z", "main", "2026-10-23 23:08 main grooming: umbrella: last note was 10-20, but work moved on its parts (HOPACSOTA-P2, P3, P6 noted 10-22 and 10-23), and main-hopacsota-promotion is running now (chain B, behind rustls-check, am-any-gate and curried-main-probe).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_12 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 12u32, "2026-10-27T23:04Z", "main", "10-27 19:04 main: Groom 10-27 18:5x, the critical path to hopacsota SOTA, re-read from its parts: the single-threaded side is done and proven (P6: 7,352 rows match single-flight, apps/spiral byte-identical under inline, dfs, bfs and two random schedules). The open blocker is parallel determinism: the 10-25 waits census (finished, unread until now) shows policy=parallel gives a different output per run at 2, 4 and 8 workers (HOPACSOTA-P2 note). Order from here: (1) P2 determinism gate (1 hash per worker count, equal to single-flight), (2) localise and fix the order dependence, (3) speed (w4 is 0.68x of w1 today; w8 regresses on wait contention), (4) P6 promotion re-gated with the parallel policy included, then the user's call on deleting gpt5parallel. P3 (granularity cutoff) and P4 (diagnostics) don't gate promotion. The census sat unread for 2 days because nothing watched it after it was queued behind the quiet gate; lesson for this epic: every queued measurement gets a watcher that posts its reading.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_13 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 13u32, "2026-10-30T23:42Z", "main", "10-30 19:4x main R3 groom (BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): owner compiler (hopacsota is the compiler team's critical path: parallel determinism, per the 10-25 waits census in the 10-27 groom). main keeps only the install step after compiler's proofs.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_14 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 14u32, "2026-11-01T03:36Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 23:34 compiler, cadence groom (user 23:33: drift/stall check; no Active item silent >12 h): stays Active, progress today: P3's deferred validation measured twice on the node, the second with A/A (P3 n60, n62): waits cut 98-99%, wall inside the A/A spread, so NOT ADOPTED on speed; the w8 cost is claim transport, not waits. gpt5parallel fully retired (PACK-10 + PACK-11), so single-flight is the only reference. Next concrete step: HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH's design decision (below).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_15 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 15u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler, R5 MEASURABLE ANSWER PLAN (user: is upstream single-flight close to SOTA before the Rust/Gleam rewrite?). Metrics, all on installed single-flight, Normal priority, node, with an in-job A/A arm: (M1) phase split of the 7,413-row matrix compile and the 5 mega samples (lex/parse/infer/peval/codegen) via dotnet-trace; (M2) GC share of wall time (dotnet-counters time-in-gc); (M3) size scaling exponent per phase on agile.spi slices (shared with COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE); (M4) join-point memo hit rate and duplicate specializations; (M5) critical-path bound for parallel speedup (the P3 granularity data). VERDICT RULE written now: near-SOTA = GC < 15% of wall AND every phase exponent <= 1.1 AND no identified algorithmic fix worth >= 2x on any phase; otherwise the fixes are listed and done in F# BEFORE the rewrite so the rewrite ports the fast algorithm. External reference: fsc and ocamlopt check time per kloc on comparable code, reported for context only (different languages, not a gate). NEXT STEP: M2 + M1 on the 5 mega samples, one node job, after CHAR-ORDERING.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_16 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 16u32, "2026-11-03T07:30Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (41 h). Next: the R5 measurement plan M1-M3 (phase split, GC share, size exponent) on installed pack23, on the node with an in-job A/A arm.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_17 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 17u32, "2026-11-07T15:55Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler (groom): DoD: the hopacsota core compiles the full sample corpus with outputs byte-identical to single-flight and determinism by construction (no replay), and meets PLAN.md R5's near-SOTA rule on the LARGE-INPUT-SCALING inputs: GC under 15% of wall time and every phase's scaling exponent at most 1.1. Its phases P3-P7 are the steps.")
inl hopacsota_research () = Task ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", "hopacsota Phase 0 (no core code): R1 rest of Bend 2 (BendTT 6+, term_check/term_infer, emit_match/emit_task); R2 shared-state inventory with every access line; R3 per-specialization work/span from an instrumented single-flight copy on the mega roots + a scaling corpus (apps/spiral, all lib/spiral, generated N=10/100/1000 modules) -> the chains that make the span long and the D16 technique for each (parallel evaluation is required, R3 never decides whether); R4 Deferred DFS/BFS/random-seed worklist on single-flight, -Suite all residual hashes identical; gate numbers into spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md scoreboard; 2026-10-14 00:58 R1 done (BendTT pp. 7-10, 12 bend2 functions + checker bench: D12 +12 applied, 5 not applied) and R2 done (31 inventory rows, 0 without a line, 3/3 R2-decides resolved, 34/34 PartEval write lines covered, 5 proposed decision changes P1-P5 in PLAN.md); R3, R4 open; 2026-10-14 01:50 P1-P5 folded into the PLAN.md decision text (technical core facts 3-4, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7, D16; the Decision changes log kept as history); every PLAN.md line now <= 120 columns (inventory turned into a list); 2026-10-14 02:58 lane 3 R3/R4 patch scripts (not built; anchors checked once each against the current spiral_compiler.fs into scratch copies): %USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\hopacsota-p0\\r3_instrument.ps1 (-Target copy; SPIRAL_R3_DUMP=<path> TSV per specialization: run, id, kind, annotated, awaited, parent, offset_us, self_us, inclusive_us, outcome, note; awaited cache hits too), r3_simulate.py (W, S, greedy list scheduling at 1/2/4/8 workers, critical path, top 10 awaited chains with a D16 technique each; checked on a synthetic dump), r4_deferred.ps1 (SPIRAL_R4_POLICY=dfs|bfs|random:<seed>: closures and annotated methods go through a worklist, dfs runs them at once in the caller's context = single-flight, bfs/random drain after the root with D3 relative context unless SPIRAL_R4_CONTEXT=canonical; SPIRAL_R4_REPORT=<path> counts inline-depth and dynamic-if restarts, validating callers, relative-trace bodies, stack/inline/if stops)", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "HOPACSOTA", "compiler,hopacsota,research", "current", "current")
inl kit_agile_rename_id () = Task ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-ID", "eoie agile has no way to rename a task id (edit fields: title, kind, priority, difficulty, deps, tags, estimate, load, assignee); needed for the hopac -> gpt5parallel rename of HOPAC-* items; one call: rename <root> <old-id> <new-id> updating deps that point at it; 2026-10-13 22:47; 2026-10-14 03:58 lane 3 design: rename <old> to <new> as a typed agile do statement (Rename :: rename_request -> agile_statement agile_mutate rename_receipt): one write renames the Task id and inl name, its Planning and Note items, and every deps entry naming it (deps_rewritten listed), counting titles that mention the old id; fails with RenameTargetTaken or UnknownTask and then writes nothing; 2026-10-14 04:56 lane 2 done (uncommitted, eoie repo): eoie agile rename <root> <old-id> <new-id> in granular Spiral: crate agile_rename_rewrite (701 lines, line-wise rewrite of the Task line and inl name, the Planning row and planning_of_ name, each Note row and note_of_<id>_<seq> name, and every other task's deps entry equal to the old id; titles that mention it are counted and listed, not changed) and crate agile_task_rename (360, validation: the old id exists, the new id is upper-case letters, digits and - and not taken, not equal; one guarded write that refuses when state/agile.spi changed since it was read); receipt: eoie agile rename ok old= new= items= deps_rewritten= deps_in= titles_mentioning_old= titles_in= bytes_before= bytes_after= elapsed_ms=; proof on a copy of this backlog: EOIE-ONE-CALL -> EOIE-ONE-SHOT rewrote the task, its planning and a note plus deps in 11 tasks (EOIE-AGILE-BODY, EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC, ...), counted 1 title mention (PS1-TO-SPIRAL), 534 ms on the 504 KB file; taken, malformed and unknown ids rejected with nothing written; agile check build_attested=2 on the copy afterwards; tests in agile_note_receipts.rs: rename receipt and every rewritten item, plus a concurrent-writer test (EOIE_AGILE_TEST_PAUSE_MS pauses after the read; an outside write during the pause wins and the rename exits 2 writing nothing); not used on the real backlog (rename is proven on the copy only, as asked); 2026-10-14 05:20 review round: rename also refuses a new id whose inl name is already declared anywhere (e.g. MAIN collides with inl main) or that starts with a digit (2FA-LOGIN would give inl 2fa_login, not an identifier; agile add still accepts such ids, which is a separate gap), both tested with the state byte-identical; an expired lease blocks rename like every other mutation (tested); the concurrent-writer test waits for the pause marker; agile_note_receipts 5/5 against the new build; dev.ps1 staged run: see EOIE-AGILE-BODY note 4 (one eoie-contracts lib test fails only in the staged workflow, passes in the tree with the same binaries); left: deploy the new eoie.exe, renew owner growth and strict evidence, commit; 2026-10-14 05:55 final round: agile add now also rejects an id starting with a digit (agile add 2FA-LOGIN rejected: the id must start with a letter, so its inl name is a valid identifier; FA2-LOGIN still accepted), receipt test in agile_note_receipts.rs; the staged-only lease failure is fixed at its source: contracts.rs had been hand-patched (a743a92) with EOIE_LEASE_POLICY/EOIE_CONFIG_HOME isolation that contracts_entry/harness.spi never got, so every regeneration dropped it; harness.spi now carries env_remove EOIE_LEASE_POLICY + env_remove EOIE_LEASE_ROOT + EOIE_CONFIG_HOME=<root> on the 4 lease-sensitive commands and contracts.rs is regenerated from it; eoie dev.ps1 -Package (11 packages incl. agile-task-creation and eoie-contracts) -Publish passed end to end in 719 s: 11/11 owners emitted, cargo check ok, every package test ok: eoie-contracts lib 8/8 (7 ignored) incl. expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface, agile_note_receipts 6/6, agile_receipts 1/1, proxy_receipts 5/5, batch_completion 2/2; Published 0 changed owners, 11 unchanged (the tree already held the regenerated outputs); 2026-10-14 06:01 deployed in eoie.exe 44897B5C8234 (eoie build.ps1, release, published=True); rename still not used on the real backlog; left: commit, then renew-strict-evidence.ps1", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,agile,one-call", "current", "current")
inl hopacsota_p1 () = Task ("HOPACSOTA-P1", "hopacsota Phase 1: -Mode hopacsota + SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA, D10 seam hooks (single-flight code moved unchanged, projection-hash equal), hopacsota-lint.ps1 G1 size + G2 banned, Deferred worklist with D3 tables/D6 merge/D8 types, 4 frontier_hopacsota_* fixtures first; gate: -Suite all 0 diffs on Inline + Deferred DFS/BFS/3 seeds, Inline <=1.05x single-flight (spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md); 2026-10-14 02:15 lane 3 drafted 7 frontier fixtures in scratch (%USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\hopacsota-fixtures, README with expected single-flight outcomes derived from PartEval line by line, not yet compiled): recursion_unannotated (Recursive join points must be annotated, 163000), mutual_pending (exit 0, annotated pending key returns its type, 162999), globals_order (main.c lines m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2), two_errors (type error 'first body fails'), if_depth_across_fork (P1: EJP0040 only via the caller's depth 600 + leaf's 600), validation_global (P2: '// nested validation global' between g1 and g2, added once through the validation cache), pending_type_join_point (P3: recursive union read by ty_is_uninhabited, exit 0); the main thread compiles them after the bless", Story, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", "compiler,hopacsota", "current", "current")
