inl kit_agile_body () = Task ("KIT-AGILE-BODY", "eoie agile has no body/notes field: long context goes into title-append (HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH reached 2,123 title bytes on 2026-10-13); add a typed notes list (dated entries, one call: agile note <root> <id> <text>) and show it under the title; titles stay one line; 2026-10-14 03:58 lane 3 design (not compiled; %USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\eoie-do\\agile_model.spi + agile_cases.md): notes as a typed list (task_note: instant, author user|agent lane, text) stored as new inl items Note (id, seq, instant, author, text) beside Task/Planning; agile do statements note <id> [as lane] \"{clock:..} text\" and notes from-title <id> after \"; \" (MoveTitleToNotes) to migrate long title-append tails into dated notes; show <id> notes N prints the last N under a one-line title; 2026-10-14 04:56 lane 2: implemented and proven, evidence in this item's notes 1-3 (eoie agile show with the new build); 2026-10-14 06:01 lane 2: deployed eoie.exe 44897B5C8234 prints notes, agile check ok, dev.ps1 passed end to end (details in note 6); left: commit, then renew-strict-evidence.ps1", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "none", "kit,agile,dogfood", "current", "current")
inl spiral_formatter () = Task ("SPIRAL-FORMATTER", "Spiral formatter (user request 2026-10-13 23:48, plan only, later): probably inside the compiler to reuse its tokenizer/parser (a trivia-preserving pass over the same tokens, both editions, test blocks and ///> target lines kept), exposed as a compiler subcommand plus an eoie verb and a Zed format command; the style is the user's personal style in lib/spiral and the CLIs, mined from those files as measured rules (indentation, line breaks, operator and lambda spacing, match layout, blank lines), not invented; gates: formatting the user-authored corpus is a no-op (or only diffs the user approves), idempotent (format twice = once), and every reformatted file compiles to the same residual hash; open question for planning: which CLIs are user-authored vs agent-generated; 2026-10-13 23:48 user: the goal is to harden the 120-character line limit: every formatted line fits in 120 columns (a hard gate, with a deterministic break strategy for long applications, pipelines, records and match arms), checked by a lint over lib, CLIs and samples; 2026-10-14 01:32 style mined (read-only) from the user's own code, polyglot@bb856d13 (2025-01-12, 86 .spi/.spir, 14,683 non-blank lines; git authors cannot separate user from agents, so the split is by date, confirmed on pre-2025-09 blame lines of spiral lib/spiral and apps/spiral+apps/wasm): operators spaced 9,832/0, annotation colon spaced 4,265/0, +4 indent steps 3,871/7, multi-line body at +4 1,739/0, pipeline stages on their own lines aligned with the head 1,027/1, match arms at the match column 141/0, bare lambdas 1,168 vs 117 parenthesized, then-first if (if c / then a / else b) 107 vs 31, multi-line records with { ending the line, fields at +4 without ; 224/0, long definition heads as name / params at +4 / : type / = alone (44 vs 16 single-line heads over 120), one blank line between top-level definitions 1,923 of 2,105; 334 user lines exceed 120 but 272 of them hold a literal that cannot fit even alone, so a hard 120 gate needs a literal continuation or an allowlist (open question); rules, per-construct break strategy and open questions in %USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\formatter\\style-rules.md (scratch); 2026-10-14 01:40 refinement: of the 272 unbreakable-literal lines, 230 are plain strings that !!!!StaticStringConcat folds at compile time (split possible with the residual unchanged, given an always-in-scope concat operator), 42 are macros that need a tokenizer continuation or an allowlist; a spacing-only pass would change 29 of 14,689 user lines (22 trailing whitespace); 2026-10-14 02:23 plan written (not started): spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/formatter/PLAN.md in the hopacsota PLAN.md shape: facts with counts, decisions F1-F10 (inside the compiler on the Tokenize/BlockParsing tokens, measured style only, indentation is syntax, token-level spacing rules, deterministic outermost-first break order from the user's templates, semantics checked by token sequence + residual hash, untouched comments/literals/headers, both editions, pure function, content-keyed allowlist), a banned list, phases 0-4 with gates G1 idempotence, G2 user corpus formats to itself except the 29 listed lines, G3 residual hashes identical, G4 0 lines over 120 outside allowlist.tsv, G5 determinism, G6 banned lint; Q1-Q7 are decisions awaiting the user with a recommendation each (Q1: a compile-time core concat operator for plain strings plus a macro continuation, allowlist meanwhile; Q2: keep the author's breaks)", Feature, P0, D6, 95u32, Planned, "", "compiler,tooling,formatter,main,team:compiler", "current", "current")
