inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_4 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-10-14T23:28Z", "lane-b", "proof: a Spiral test block (Rust backend) drives eoie.exe agile edit+show --json on a temp root and passes via run_notebook in 9 s; a 361 control fails. Macro trap: \\\" and \\# unescape; raw strings need r\\#. Draft at lane-b tmp eoie-spiral-test")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_5 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-10-15T03:37Z", "lane-b", "23:37 lane B: planning_cli.rs converted to granular Spiral test blocks (draft tmp/lane-b/eoie-spiral-test/planning_cli.spi, not landed): typed fixture_root nominal, cli_run record, agile_call union (RootThen | ModeThenRoot), one small macro per concern (temp root, state read/write, spawn eoie with tab-split args, contains/count/offset), expect/accepted/rejected in Spiral; both former tests with every assertion are test blocks; run_notebook (Kino copy + scratch host, EOIE_BIN_UNDER_TEST=eoie.exe): 2/2 passed in 41 s; control with 361m/301m expectations: 2/2 failed with 'missing estimate=361m ... in: eoie agile edit ok ... estimate=360m'; macro trap: \\$'*!left == *!right' does not parse (ETY-MissingBody), (&*!left).eq(&*!right) does; next: land it in src/agile_planning_rollup beside planning_rollup.spi, wire a test-block phase into the eoie-dev workflow, then git rm tests/planning_cli.rs")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_6 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-10-15T04:52Z", "lane-b", "00:52 lane B: LANDED (uncommitted, eoie): src/agile_planning_rollup/planning_cli.spi (both planning_cli.rs tests as granular Spiral test blocks); runner = eoie-dev workflow (src/eoie_dev_model workflow.spi + host.spi, dev.rs regenerated with pack-1f): after cargo test succeeds, every registered notebook (typed registry union rec spiral_test_notebooks: cargo package + path) whose package is selected (or all when no --package) runs through Kino spi/run_notebook.ps1 with EOIE_BIN_UNDER_TEST = the freshly built target/debug/eoie, memo off (results depend on the binary), output target/spiral-tests/*.ipynb; Kino found via EOIE_SPIRAL_KINO, else EOIE_SPIRAL_BUNDLE/../../kino (test-regeneration sets it), else ../spiral/apps/kino; --dry-run prints 'spiral test blocks <path>'; proof: build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease -Package agile-planning-rollup: cargo tests ok, then spiral-tests 2/2 passed, memo_hits 0; CI (.github/workflows/eoie.yml): checkout i574n/The-Spiral-Language into spiral/deps (Kino cells link |core-), setup-beam OTP 27/Elixir 1.18, mix deps.get in spiral/apps/kino; user: git rm src/agile_planning_rollup/tests/planning_cli.rs once CI is green")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_7 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-10-15T07:00Z", "lane-b", "03:00 lane B: the phase runs Kino with SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process (no shared daemon left resident on 13905 beside renewals/cold budgets); proofs on pack-1g: build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease -Package agile-planning-rollup without any port env 2/2 with 0 daemons before/after; staged path test-regeneration -Package agile-planning-rollup -Test -SkipRelease 2/2 (Kino via EOIE_SPIRAL_BUNDLE); full build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease earlier: 267 cargo results ok + 2/2; CI's test-dev-workflow selects only its fixture package, so the phase never runs before the compiler build step")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_8 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 8u32, "2026-10-15T08:39Z", "lane-b", "04:39 lane B: renewal preflight caught eoie_dev at 1,016 lines (> 1000 gate) from the inlined phase; moved the phase into its own Spiral owner src/eoie_dev_spiral_tests (registry.spi typed notebook registry + selection, notebook.spi run_notebook spawn + dry-run announce, main.spi run loop + Export eoie_dev_spiral_tests_run; spiral_tests.rs 76 lines), eoie_dev_model calls it via one host macro line; dev.rs 701 (694 at HEAD); source-topology ok (crate max 995, file max 982); full build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease: 269 cargo results ok + Spiral tests 2/2")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_9 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 9u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: 2 of planning_cli.rs's tests now run as Spiral test blocks inside build.ps1 -Test (269 + 2/2, renewal 04:57 covers it). Next grain: the next hand-written tests/*.rs by size; planning_cli.rs git rm waits for the first green CI with the Kino step.")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_10 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 10u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: planning_cli.rs deleted after green CI 38725303020 (Spiral blocks 2/2 there); its 2 tests pinned ///> rust for the Kino zig default; eoie-dev-spiral-tests now declares test-requires-cli (its notebooks launch the CLI, so a stale binary passed before); 2 new registered notebooks (agile_todo_model model.spi 5 tests, todo_cli.spi 3).")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_11 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 11u32, "2026-10-19T23:00Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 19:00 eoie-lane: binary-driving Rust tests become Spiral notebooks on a shared harness package src/eoie_cli_harness (module cli: fixture roots, cli_args union, eoie_run/racing/closing-stdout runs, receipt normalizers, digests, symlink-or-skip, rustc_program for fake tools); notebooks include it with '///- --package ../eoie_cli_harness' + 'open cli' (a notebook compiles standalone, so this is how test code shares helpers). Ported and retired 9 Rust files (896 lines): agile_note_receipts, proxy_receipts, agile_receipts, batch_completion (eoie_contracts), agile_cache, agile_listing (eoie_agile_contracts), archive_publication, self_upgrade, eoie_cli tests/windows. New notebooks: agile_task_notes/notes_cli 6, eoie_contracts/receipts_cli 8, eoie_agile_contracts/agile_cli 9, archive_cli 3, upgrade_cli 2, eoie_cli/windows_cli 4 = 32 tests; each passed a mutation check (mutated expectations fail exactly the mutated tests); official eoie-dev run (build.ps1 -Test -SkipRelease, 5 packages, heavy job) green. Traps: a runtime (~) flag that picks between cli_args shapes makes the compile-time joined recursion diverge (EJP0011), keep shape flags static; Spiral string literals cannot hold a backslash before a quote, build it with char 92/34.")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_12 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 12u32, "2026-10-19T23:48Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 19:48 eoie-lane batch 2: native_paths.rs (4 binary tests -> eoie_coverage_prune/coverage_cli.spi with a rustc-built fake cargo; the pure eoie_coverage_jobs test -> a test block in coverage_prune_model/model.spi next to coverage_jobs_binding), evidence.rs -> eoie_coverage_prune/evidence_cli.spi (coverage-assess, prune-uncovered, coverage-export through proxy verbs, fake grcov), hygiene_confinement.rs sidecar half -> eoie_release_contracts/hygiene_cli.spi (junction helper with CREATE_NO_WINDOW). Kept in Rust on purpose: hygiene transient tests (prune-release-transients has no proxy verb; a test-only verb is not worth it), prune_transaction.rs (one case pre-creates a backup named after the test's own PID, which only collides in-process). False-pass trap found: through a binary, a refusal test passes on 'unknown proxy operation'; refusals now also assert that text is absent. Full gated release job-1792451451481 green with 34 notebooks / 99 Spiral tests, topology gate passed, eoie.exe 19:43 sha256 52FEFE97...; hand-written Rust test files 41 -> 30 (11 retired, 1 shrunk, 1,162 lines gone).")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_13 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 13u32, "2026-10-20T00:45Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 20:45 eoie-lane batch 3: hash_boundary.rs Windows/Linux test -> eoie_proxy_search/hash_cli.spi (proxy hash with EOIE_HASH_LIMIT_BYTES=3, junction ancestor), the Rust file keeps only the Linux FIFO test (36 lines). Flake found by the official run and fixed: the agile cache fixture read the clock twice for the lease start and deadline, and eoie rejects a 1 ms skew (deadline mismatch); the fixture now reads now_ms once. Pack 12 (unaccepted) was installed at 20:36, so the rerun skips regeneration (only notebooks and the harness changed, no generated output).")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_14 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 14u32, "2026-10-21T13:53Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 09:53 eoie team: inventory today: 26 eoie-owned hand-written Rust test files remain (9 [[test]] targets, 17 tests/*.rs; vendored crates excluded). command_spec_domain's help_catalog.rs (30 lines) is ported into the r30 command-spec slice's Spiral notebook as every_advertised_proxy_has_its_own_usage_and_unknown_names_get_none (catalog alignment, four exact usages, five unknown names). The .rs file is NOT deleted in r30: evidence/coverage/current.lcov and replay-seed.lcov list it as a source and state/evidence.spi hashes those files, so deleting it could trip the GPT-era evidence currentness checks; delete it in the release that next refreshes coverage evidence. Rule for the rest: port one file per slice into the slice's own notebook only when that slice already touches the crate.")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_15 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 15u32, "2026-10-21T20:35Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:35 eoie team: shipped in the combined r28+r29 release, installed 15:38 (one-call spec 34/34, all 67 notebooks green): the notebook phase lists every failure instead of stopping at the first.")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_16 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 16u32, "2026-10-22T09:23Z", "eoie", "05:23 remaining scope, measured on the live tree (vendor excluded): 14 hand-written tests/*.rs files, 846 lines, in 11 packages (eoie_bundle_manifest 3, rust_std_fs 2, eoie_agile_lease, eoie_compiler_discovery, eoie_coverage_prune, eoie_process_observation and 5 more with 1 each). These are the last .rs without a Spiral owner. Each converts to a Spiral test block in its package, std-only primitives only (crate-backed ones are covered end to end by the one-call runner, per spiral-macro-gotchas).")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_17 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 17u32, "2026-10-22T09:25Z", "eoie", "05:25 first conversion drafted, composed into release E: apply-test-portable-policy.ps1 turns eoie_bundle_manifest/tests/portable_policy.rs into the Spiral test archive_permissions_keep_executable_and_readonly_intent in bundle_manifest.spi (all four modes: 420/292/493/365 = 0o644/0o444/0o755/0o555), adds the package header and the registry notebook, deletes the .rs. The module's rust_global blob is reached only from main, so the plain-rustc test compile should not see it; E's preview and notebook phase confirm. 13 test files remain.")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_18 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 18u32, "2026-10-22T09:27Z", "eoie", "05:27 classification of the 13 remaining test files (after portable_policy): all are OS integration tests of Rust blob code against the real filesystem or processes: symlinks and renames (compiler_discovery identity, release_contracts hygiene_confinement, tree_copy, legacy path_mutation), a Linux FIFO child process (proxy_search hash_boundary), zip expansion limits (bundle_manifest archive_limits), Unicode and limit edges in directory listing (rust_std_fs directory_names), Windows-only behaviors (3 windows.rs), the lease package inputs and the coverage prune transaction. None tests a pure Spiral function, and Spiral test blocks compile with plain rustc without crate dependencies, so they cannot convert one-to-one. Path: each moves with its code. When the code under test becomes Spiral (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY / EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE), its test becomes a test block; until then the behavior is covered end to end as one-call runner cases, which run the real binary.")
inl note_of_kit_spiral_tests_19 () = Note ("KIT-SPIRAL-TESTS", 19u32, "2026-10-22T21:45Z", "eoie-lane", "17:45 inventory (no compile): 12 hand-written tests/*.rs remain in src (617 lines). portable_policy.rs (8 lines, a pure function test) migrates with GE2 (apply-test-portable-policy in apply-rE); the other 11 are the OS integration tests classified at 05:27. Outside src, compiler-contracts holds 9 test-*.ps1 contract scripts (1,148 lines); CI runs test-dev-workflow from them, which was red since 10-18 and is fixed in the tree today (EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW). After GE2: 11 .rs files, all needing OS boundaries (symlinks, FIFOs, zip limits, Windows-only behavior), so they move only with the OS boundary package (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY), where a Spiral test block can drive the primitive.")
