inl note_of_x_client_12 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 12u32, "2026-10-18T23:30Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 19:30 gate headroom (measured per crate): xc 973 -> 722 by making env_or a let (it was inlined at every environment read) plus failed/missing_bearer/reported as lets; args 994 -> 959 with one_value/other_command/write_command as lets (938 before delete-thread); view 999 -> 990 by timestamps via sm'.substring (drops the 61-line string_slice helper; post-text clipping keeps the UTF-8-safe slice); digest 998 -> 990 by a one-line Rust unescape; assemble back to 955 after gap detection (1,197) by Rust one-liners for the frame header (word_at/part_at), replied_to and the flattened page bundle. Lesson: an inl helper called from many places is the cheapest gate win; profile_rs per crate finds them")
inl note_of_x_client_13 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 13u32, "2026-10-21T03:15Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 23:15 pre-commit proof (eoie job x-precommit, 22:01-23:14): CI's own scripts/build.ps1 (no -fast) over the uncommitted tree exits 0 locally: actions-lock 8 actions locked, crate gate 16 crates 0 over 1000, x-compat 0 in 36 files, postable 1617 posts with 0 cells over one post, e2e tutorial and extra cases incl. delete-thread 34, Cells 35 of 35 notebook files with 0 failures, sim ExUnit 43/43 after the fixture guard, corpus commute on both schedules, real-Cells executor run, thread_run accepts the thread and rejects a tampered one. CI is red on HEAD 61b8fff only from the windows-2025 CLIXML e2e failure (run 39367603402) that the uncommitted e2e.ps1 ProgressPreference fix addresses, so the user's next commit of this tree is expected to turn ci green; D1 needs two consecutive green runs on main")
inl note_of_x_client_14 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 14u32, "2026-10-21T21:22Z", "x", "2026-10-21 17:22 x: grooming. Status Active -> Blocked so the stop gate's ready list stops offering it: x's part is verified (CI's own scripts/build.ps1 green locally on the uncommitted tree; 10-21 x-split-fix3 green after the post_id slice and the lib Gleam fixes). The remainder is the user's commit and push plus two consecutive green ci runs on main (X-DONE D1), which no agent can do. Unblock when the user commits.")
inl note_of_x_client_15 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 15u32, "2026-10-27T12:57Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:57 x: CI read (gh, read-only). ci on main failed for the user's last 3 pushes, including today's 9b90151 'tests' (run 40488607167). (1) xc-windows: \"couldn't find file apps\\client\\domains\\domains.rs\". The commit carried the WIP crates' .spi and Cargo.toml (domains, requests), but generated .rs were never put in the tree; I had wrongly left generated outputs to the verify. Fix in progress: x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part regen (job-1793105792101 via i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1) regenerates every client crate on the current tree with the pinned compiler, and the .rs that the WIP changes or adds (new crates; changed ones by the same-compiler base comparison) land in the tree unstaged. (2) build (ubuntu-24.04): the gate passed (28 crates), then e2e threw \"the Mastodon stub did not write its port\", because apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py is UNTRACKED: e2e.ps1 (committed) starts it, but the commit did not include it. Untracked files a commit needs today: apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py, apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt (untracked since 10-25 and compared by the sim build), apps/client/e2e/links.txt (new tutorial input), scripts/verify.ps1, plus the new crates' .rs once landed. Also added __pycache__/ to x/.gitignore (the Python stubs write it under e2e/). Only the user commits; this note is the list for that.")
inl note_of_x_client_16 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 16u32, "2026-10-28T12:20Z", "x", "2026-10-28 08:20 x: CI on the user's cc3bc3b (run 40677686892, 07:08) failed on both runners (windows-2025, ubuntu-24.04) at the same point: e2e.ps1:141 'the Mastodon stub did not write its port'. apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py is still untracked, so it is absent in CI. Every step before e2e passed on both runners. The remaining user commit for X-CLIENT is exactly 3 files: apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py (the Mastodon/Bluesky stub e2e starts), apps/client/e2e/links.txt (the tutorial's links-only step input) and apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt (a sim fixture). Everything else (scripts/verify.ps1, apps/sim/split, xsim_split, entities) was in cc3bc3b. Then X-REPO-TEMPLATE needs two green CI runs, and X-DONE closes.")
inl note_of_x_client_17 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 17u32, "2026-10-29T19:45Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:5x x groom (WIPE-REDO-LEDGER n41): load light, assignee user. What's left is the user's: commit apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py, apps/client/e2e/links.txt and apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt (CI red since 10-25 only because those are untracked), and re-issue ~/.secrets/x-api.env (lost in the 10-28 wipe; named only) for live posting. e2e runs entirely on the local stubs, so verifies don't need it.")
inl note_of_x_client_18 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 18u32, "2026-10-31T01:57Z", "x", "2026-10-30 22:0x x (user ask: no .py / .txt files in x): the commit list in n17 changed. apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py -> social_stub.ps1 (the side-by-side test of 30 requests matched the Python stub on every response and log row; self-test 17/17); e2e/links.txt -> links.md (byte-identical, tutorial step updated); apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt -> prelude.parity.json (mix xsim.parity now writes it through Xsim.Json, like the other fixtures; the two counts are dropped because they equal the map sizes). Old files are in C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\archive\\{social-stub-py,txt-fixtures}. Not compiled on the box (CPU 100%): verify38 is the proof, and its sim build regenerates prelude.parity.json and compares it byte for byte. postability/tlds.txt stays: the compiler (ReadAllLines) and Cells (split on newlines) read it by the name in x.json, so a new format needs a compiler and Cells change.")
inl note_of_x_client_19 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 19u32, "2026-10-31T03:16Z", "x", "2026-10-30 23:1x x: stub.py ported as well (user aim: no .py in x). e2e/stub.ps1 is the X API stub (world.json + includes, OAuth 1.0a HMAC-SHA1 check with the published example asserted at startup, X weights, search/timeline/lookup/following, refresh grant). e2e/stub_http.ps1 holds the HTTP plumbing shared with social_stub.ps1 (TcpListener on 127.0.0.1:0, one request per connection, Connection: close, like Python's HTTP/1.0 server). Proof on the box with the 10-25 xc.exe: e2e run A (stub.py) and run B (stub.ps1) gave the same 170 request-log rows (method, path, query, authorized, context, body) and the same step output; both stop at the Mastodon section because that exe predates XC_SITE. The weight function matched Python's x_weight on 367 texts (every world post plus emoji/keycap/flag/tag/URL edge cases), 0 differences. stub.py archived to C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\archive\\social-stub-py. CI keeps actions/setup-python for now: removing it changes a uses: line, so actions.lock must be regenerated, and the gh actions-lock extension needs the user's yes to reinstall. PRE-REGISTERED for verify38 (job-1793416530974, xqueue1, pack 8, -Accept, cap 14 h incl. queue): PASS = exit 0 with sim accept, client build, e2e accept, client notebooks and sim build all exit 0; the e2e log shows the X part plus 'mastodon post-thread' and 'bluesky post-thread' lines with exit 0 (first run of both PowerShell stubs against a current xc); 'xsim / accepted apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.json' is present and the landed file equals the hand-made one byte for byte (else land the regenerated one and say so); spiral.toml is read (X-EDITION3-RESPELL n17). A timeout red is rerun alone. A stub red: restore stub.py/social_stub.py from the archive and the two e2e.ps1 lines, then fix.")
inl note_of_x_client_20 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 20u32, "2026-10-31T07:05Z", "x", "2026-10-31 03:05 x: verify38 (job-1793416530974, 3 h 40 min, xqueue1, pack 8, -Accept) by n19's rule: PASS. Exit 0; x verify / sim accept, client build before accepting, e2e accept, client build and sim build all exit 0; all 43 client and 23 sim notebooks passed; x-compat 0 findings in 43 (client) and 29 (sim) files. The e2e ran on the PowerShell stubs (stub.ps1 + social_stub.ps1): 'mastodon post-thread / 17 statuses / exit 0', 'bluesky post-thread / 17 records / exit 0', bluesky refused sign-in exit 4 and delete-thread refused exit 2 as expected, 'RUST-OK x/apps/client / e2e: 37 tutorial steps and 5 extra cases', 153 requests to the X stub. 'xsim / accepted apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.json' present, and the land dry run (node-proof -Land x-verify38 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv38-out -Repo x) reports 0 to land, 0 conflicts, 113 unchanged, so the regenerated prelude.parity.json is byte-identical to the hand-made one, and every other accepted fixture equals the live tree. spiral.toml: the logs never name the project file, but the compiler prefers spiral.toml whenever it exists (spiral_compiler.fs spiproj_suffix line 184649; the x-compat edition check at 185022 does the same), and both packages carry one, so the build read them. Nothing to land. The .py stubs stay archived (C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\archive\\social-stub-py); CI still installs Python only until actions.lock can be regenerated (gh actions-lock extension missing, reinstall needs the user).")
inl note_of_x_client_21 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 21u32, "2026-11-04T01:12Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:11 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP, x's corner: open x items with no note in 48 h). Stays Blocked at 98. The client is green all day (x CI 2fe525a all jobs; e2e RUST-OK in every node run today). The blocker is the user's commit and push of the unstaged lands (git is the user's step). Owner x. Close when CI is green on a pushed tree.")
inl note_of_x_client_22 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 22u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:13 x: GROOM (user 11-04 00:1x via main). Stays Blocked at 98. Same blocker as X-DONE (CI on a pushed tree). Per the user (11-04): no commit asks; x notices the commit, then checks and heals CI.")
inl note_of_x_client_23 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 23u32, "2026-11-06T10:16Z", "x", "2026-11-06 06:1x x: groom. Stays Blocked at 98, and the step left is the user's: push the x and spiral trees (main's 11-05 codespace rehearsal: every red repo dies at the one spiral init-order bug, fixed unstaged). Resume and close: after the push, read x's CI run. From compiler's 06:12 lesson 1: spiral's compiler and cells-gate jobs run only on schedule/dispatch, so the Cells proof comes from the next SCHEDULED run's log, not the push run (it shows those jobs \"skipped\"). X-DONE follows from this.")
