inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_15 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 15u32, "2026-11-02T12:20Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x RETITLED and decomposed for the user (11-02). Children: CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD -> CIC-SYNTAX -> (CIC-SCOPE, CIC-UNIVERSES) -> CIC-SUBST -> CIC-REDUCE -> CIC-CONVERSION -> CIC-TYPING -> (CIC-INDUCTIVES, CIC-LEAN-ORACLE) -> CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY, CIC-BENCH; CIC-MEGA-ABSORB -> CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE. Three Lean tiers: T1 target agreement (///> lean pinned tests; needs a run-time kernel), T2 Lean kernel as verdict oracle (CIC-LEAN-ORACLE), T3 export replay. The 10-16 plan still holds (freeze the mega sample as the compiler oracle until archive, one module per layer, negatives as fails blocks, drop corrected_ prefixes). SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md.")
inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_16 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 16u32, "2026-11-02T14:13Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:1x RENAME FOR THE USER (11-02 ~09:2x: \"groom the backlog in a way that we're creating apps/kernel instead of cic, rename everywhere accordingly\").\n- Done: the titles, tags (cic dropped, kernel kept) and notes of the 14 CIC-* children plus SPS-PURPOSE now say spiral/apps/kernel, and so does this epic's title.\n- Not done: the IDs stay CIC-* until `kit agile rename` is usable (KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST). One rename of CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD ran 15 min and 424 s of CPU and then lost the optimistic-lock race (\"state/agile.spi changed since it was read; nothing written\"). After the fix, rename CIC-<X> to KERNEL-<X> for all 14 IDs.\n- Unchanged on purpose: \"CIC\" still names the calculus where the text means the calculus, and the legacy sample keeps its path (mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel).\n- DEP FIXES (fill-all-task-fields trap 1, a child depending on its own parent hides it from `agile next`): CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD no longer deps on LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS, and SPS-PURPOSE no longer deps on SPS-NOTEBOOKS.")
inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_17 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 17u32, "2026-11-02T14:37Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MIGRATION DONE RULE (user 11-02: \"make sure all these mega sample migrations have a definition of done so they don't spin forever again, and so we remove their code from the repo asap so we keep only latest code following the new style with test cells etc ... gotta transfer all the goodies before though, different than what regex did, only implemented a sliver then called it done\"). APPLIES TO all five: brzozowski (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB / REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION), lean_cic (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB / CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE), zeta (ZETA-TYPED-ARITH + ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE / ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE), omniledger (FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP / OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE), spiral_proves_spiral (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT + SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). (1) A migration is DONE only when the old sample is ARCHIVED out of the repo; a new home that works (regex published, CI green) is NOT done while absorption rows remain (the regex lesson: 9 of 71 legacy items absorbed at \"publishable\"). (2) Before the archive, every absorption-map row is resolved: (a) absorbed = a passing test in the new home in CI on both OSes, citing the legacy line; (b) lib = landed with lib tests; (c) compiler = a minimal regression sample with a matrix row; (d) dropped = a reason the map states. No row is left \"partial\". (3) ANTI-SPIN: the map is written first (one item, <= 4 h), then every (a)/(b) row is worked in priority order with the row count reported on the parent each groom round (absorbed / total); a week with no row closed raises the parent to P0 for the next round; a row blocked only by a compiler bug becomes its (c) regression sample plus a compiler item, and the archive may proceed with that row recorded as blocked-in-compiler (the goodie survives as the repro, in the new style). (4) The archive step runs in the SAME groom round the last row closes (scratch-archive.ps1, hash-verified, restore command in a note, dangling check by stem, user go), and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps its canary to the new home. (5) The parent item is set Done only after the archive note exists.")
inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_18 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 18u32, "2026-11-03T21:14Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:1x KERNEL EXISTS: spiral apps/kernel (unstaged) with 6 gated notebooks and 19 tests, wired into spiral CI (scripts/build.ps1): syntax (CIC-SYNTAX 80%), scope (CIC-SCOPE 60%), universes (CIC-UNIVERSES 40%), reduce (CIC-REDUCE 35%), conversion (CIC-CONVERSION 35%), typing (CIC-TYPING 30%); CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD Done. It already infers the polymorphic identity's dependent type and rejects ill-typed terms with named refusals. Next shared piece: the constants environment (delta in reduce/conversion, Const in typing), then inductives and the Lean oracle (CIC-LEAN-ORACLE).")
inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_19 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 19u32, "2026-11-09T17:26Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: this is an EPIC (2400m, D8) - a from-scratch CIC kernel rewrite - NOT a light-round leaf pull. Its design (note 1) already decomposes it into per-layer modules (sorts/universes, contexts, terms, substitution, conversion/defeq, inductives/iota, metas) each a notebook with test blocks + its negatives as Kino ///- --fails blocks; the first grain (sorts+contexts) is drafted. It needs STORY-level children (one per layer) to be pullable in rounds, which is a planning decision on a 40-hour user-requested epic. Parking on user (the epic's story decomposition + scheduling is the user's call; it is on their 2026-10-15/11-02 review list).")
inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_20 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 20u32, "2026-11-10T10:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 groom 11-10 (same user request; org2 owns this sample). MIGRATED, with test cells: CIC-SYNTAX, SCOPE, SUBST, REDUCE, UNIVERSES, CONVERSION, TYPING, INDUCTIVES, QUOTIENTS, LITERALS, LEAN-ORACLE, LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY, REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES and NOCONFUSION-BLOWUP are Done: 13 CIC modules with 92 tests in apps/kernel, Lean agreeing on the oracle corpus, and CIC-MEGA-ABSORB closed all 77 terminals (50 absorbed, 13 filled, 14 dropped with reasons). LEFT, as items: CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP (new: the 40 negatives were parked on CIC-TYPING n8 and the CIC modules have 0 fails blocks, so they still need a one-by-one map onto Rejected tests), CIC-BENCH (kernel vs Lean in Actions; needs REGEX-BENCH-PAGE; it is the measurement the compiler lane's kernel-vs-Lean plan needs), CIC-ENV-INDEX (P4 perf), KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS (team compiler), CI on a pushed commit (user push). DELETION PRECONDITION (CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE): CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP and KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS done, tests green on rust/gleam/lean in CI on a pushed commit; then drop its 59 matrix.psd1 rows and the bench-native entry, archive hash-verified")
inl note_of_lean_kernel_notebooks_21 () = Note ("LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS", 21u32, "2026-11-10T12:06Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2: the typefeatureset equilibrium question raised by CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP (9 forged-authority negatives dropped because kernel verdicts are public unions) is now its own item, CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY (P3, light), and is not a blocker for CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE")
inl test_fails_specific () = Task ("TEST-FAILS-SPECIFIC", "Negative test blocks matching only 'Unification failure' pass on any unrelated type error in the package (apps/spindle mutation: the module broke and the negative still passed); pin each to its own Got/Expected text, or have Kino require the diagnostic inside the test body. apps/tibia has 6 such tests", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,testing,negative-tests", "current", "current")
inl self_hosted_spiral () = Task ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", "Spiral rewritten in Spiral (user 2026-10-15 22:45): compiler targets Wasm (xsim comes for free), one set of core data structures shared by compiler and formatter; until then F# (formatter, hopacsota) and Elixir (Kino) stay interim code to be regenerated, and upstream-bound work is split from our own (some as PR candidates, some ours)", Epic, P1, D8, 0u32, Planned, "EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION,EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL,SPIRAL3-EDITIONS,GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX,CHAR-ORDERING,BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY,GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS,PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES,MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS,RUST-MOVE-ON-LAST-USE,RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION,RUST-FNMUT-CAPTURE-MOVE,DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY,BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS,STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS,GLEAM-ABYSSAL-SCALE,GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT,KINO-SOTA,WGSL-BACKEND,CALYX-BACKEND,OPENQASM3-BACKEND,BEND-BACKEND,EBPF-C-PROFILE,LEAN-BACKEND", "compiler,self-hosting,spiral,main,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_self_hosted_spiral () = Planning ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", Minutes 6000u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_1 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-10-19T12:25Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:25 lap 1 grain: first concrete anchor: the compiler already exposes its tokenizer as a CLI (TokensCli: tokens <file> | --stdin, one row per token with line, from, nearTo, class), and the formatter, Zed and edition work all sit on that tokenizer, so a Spiral tokenizer checked token-for-token against TokensCli output on the lib corpus is the natural first self-hosted slice (an oracle exists) Next: size the F# tokenizer (tokenize_line and its tables) in lines and list its data structures")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_2 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 2u32, "2026-10-19T13:01Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 09:01 lap 2 grain: sized the first slice: the /// ## Tokenize section runs from spiral_compiler.fs:42787 to the next section header at 45631 (2,845 lines, which also holds the parser's shared types: RawMacro, ParserErrors, BlockParsingEnv, ParseResult); the tokenizer's own data model is TokenKeyword, ParenthesisState, Parenthesis, MacroEnum, Literal, SemanticTokenLegend, SpiralToken, LexState (lex_state_init at 43109: triple_quotes, comment_depth, macro_close), TokenizerMacro, LineToken, LineComment, LineTokenErrors, LineTokens; module Tokenize starts at 43520; the oracle for a Spiral port is TokensCli (one row per token) Next: measure the module Tokenize body alone (43520 to its end) and map SpiralToken's cases to a Spiral union draft in lab/SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_3 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 3u32, "2026-10-19T18:40Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:40 lap 4 grain: corrected slice size: the /// ## Tokenize section proper is spiral_compiler.fs 42787-43523, 737 lines (the lap 2 figure of 2,845 ran to the next column-0 header, but section headers are indented, so it swallowed BlockSplitting and the parser types); it holds 12 types (TokenKeyword, ParenthesisState, Parenthesis, MacroEnum, Literal, SemanticTokenLegend, SpiralToken, LexState, TokenizerMacro, LineToken, LineComment, LineTokenErrors) and 152 let bindings, a realistic first self-hosting target Next: port the 12 types as Spiral unions/records in a lab package (no logic yet), with test blocks that build each case")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_4 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-10-19T20:46Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 16:46 lap 5 grain: first self-hosting slice in Spiral: lab/SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL/tokens.spi ports the tokenizer data model of spiral_compiler.fs 42793-43106 (token_keyword 31 cases, parenthesis and its state, macro_kind, literal with 13 typed payloads, semantic_token_legend as a union plus legend_code giving the F# enum values 0-13, spiral_token 22 cases, lex_state with in_triple) and the first logic, word_token, the keyword table of the F# var parser (42991-43009, including true/false as literals and the variable fallback); Cells gate 2/2 on c and rust, 0 type errors Next: next tokenizer function: the operator/symbol classifier (the ?: and ?| keyword operators at 43181) and a char-class predicate set (is_var_char_starting, is_var_char), each with test blocks mirroring the F# behavior")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_5 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 5u32, "2026-10-22T08:36Z", "main", "2026-10-22 04:35 main: char-class slice of the F# tokenizer in lab/SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL/tokens.spi (lexer_char Glyph/LineEnd, is_ascii_lower/upper, is_digit, is_letter, var-char starts, parenth open/close, is_operator_char, prefix/postfix/separator) gated by lib_gate: tests passed 3 of 3, type errors 0. Test char_classes_match_the_fsharp_tokenizer runs on rust + fsharp only: on C a char has no int conversion (sm'.convert_to_utf32 and convert.i32 on char both lack a C arm), and char supports only equality, so ranges compare via code. Precedence trap: 'a || b |> not' negates only b; the operator class is written as '(...) = false'. Next: promote tokens.spi into the self-hosted tree once its folder is decided, then the token union.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_6 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 6u32, "2026-10-22T09:00Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:00 main: promoted out of lab. Home: apps/compiler/spi/ (tokens.spi + package.spiproj, packageDir ../../../lib), following apps/cells/spi as a Spiral package inside its app; the F# compiler stays in apps/compiler. Gate in place: 3 of 3, 0 type errors. lab/SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL deleted after a hash match. Next: the token union (spiral_token cases with ranges) and tokenize_line over lexer_char, checked against TokensCli rows on the lib corpus.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_7 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 7u32, "2026-10-22T09:16Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:16 main: slice 2 in apps/compiler/spi/tokens.spi. Ports of the F# tokenizer's pure helpers: token_group (total, from token_groups; it replaces my partial token_legend, which wrongly gave bool literals the keyword legend: F# gives them number), lex_state_init, lex_state_error, comment_scan ((* nests, *) closes, (*) neither), edition3_symbol_token (all 30 edition-3 symbols), is_hex_digit. Modeling change: lex_state.macro_close is option char instead of F#'s '\\\\000' sentinel. Spiral's char lexer reads '\\\\0' as '0', and the option makes 'no macro open' a case. Gate: 6 tests, 15 target rows (c, rust, fsharp), all passed, 0 type errors. Traps hit: a top-level inl must be a function (lex_state_init ()), and ++# needs 'open sm'_operators'. Next: the Tokenizer cursor (peek/inc/skip over a line with LineEnd) and var/symbol/operator, checked against TokensCli rows.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_8 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 8u32, "2026-10-22T09:19Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:20 main: slice 3 in apps/compiler/spi/tokens.spi, a pure cursor tokenizer core. cursor {text; from}; peek_at returns LineEnd outside the text, as F#'s peek' returns lineParsersEol; advance; skip_while; skip_spaces; span {from; near_to}. Results are union lexed = Lexed of span * spiral_token * rest cursor | LexError of index * message, replacing F#'s mutable Tokenizer and Result list. Ported lexers: lex_var (keyword table via word_token, ': is not allowed directly after a var.'), lex_symbol (.name and .(op), with the ')' error at the skip_char index), lex_operator (edition-3 symbols; a trailing , or ; given back when the trimmed text is a keyword; unary when the previous char prefix-separates and the next does not postfix-separate). Expectations derived by hand from the F# code. Gate: 9 tests, 21 target rows, all passed, 0 type errors (lexers on rust + fsharp; C lacks char->int). Next: number (tokenizeNumber + suffixes), comment, strings/char_quoted, then tokenize_line and a TokensCli row comparison on lib files.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_9 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 9u32, "2026-10-22T09:24Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:25 main: slice 4 in apps/compiler/spi/tokens.spi. Two more lexers. lex_comment (state, cursor) -> lexed * lex_state: '//' plus doc/target markers ('///', '//! ', '///> ') then one required space, the text running to the line end; '(*' followed by a space or the line end goes to comment_scan, and the open depth is returned in the new lex_state, as F# sets LexCell.CommentDepth; '(*)' is no comment. lex_char_quoted: plain chars, escapes \\\\n \\\\r \\\\t \\\\b, any other escaped char as itself, errors at the F# positions. Gate: 11 tests, 25 target rows, all passed, 0 type errors. Traps (recorded for the Spiral gotchas): 'x |> f && y' parses as 'x |> (f && y)', so the lexers use a char_at_is helper; a char literal is not allowed as a union pattern payload ('| Glyph '\\\\\\\\' =>' fails with Expected: =>); use a when guard. Next: tokenizeNumber with suffixes, string/triple-quoted strings, macros, then tokenize_line and the TokensCli comparison.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_10 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 10u32, "2026-10-22T09:29Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:29 main: slices 5 and 6 drafted in apps/compiler/spi/tokens.spi (not gated: tibia live block 05:28-06:31; gate after 'block end'). Slice 5: lex_number (digit runs with underscores dropped; a minus is a sign only after a prefix separator; '1.' without digits fails at the char after the dot like F#'s committing opt; i/u/f suffixes parse through convert.try_convert and need a separator or operator char after them; F#'s 'uint8' wording kept). One deliberate deviation: F# consumes a partial width ('i1' then not '6') before reporting, and its error index lands later; the port reports at the width start. Slice 6: lex_bracket; lex_string_quoted (text chunks, escapes to TokEscapedChar / TokUnescapedChar); lex_triple_open and lex_triple_body (runs of 3+ quotes, six = empty, a shorter quote run is text, an unclosed body carries triple_quotes and ends its text in a newline). Design for slice 7, tokenize_line: F#'s alt tries the next lexer only when the failed one consumed nothing, and the error index is not the consumed position (var reports ': is not allowed' at the word start after consuming the word). So lexed/LexError must carry the cursor reached (committed vs not) before lexers can be chained in F#'s order: macro, triple, quoted, hex, number, var, symbol, raw string, char, comment, bracket, operator.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_11 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 11u32, "2026-10-22T09:41Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:41 main: slices 7-8 drafted and staged in the session scratchpad (%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--home-git\\5a6e53fb-7ff8-4098-adad-000b9fa45742\\scratchpad), to apply after tibia's block end. (1) slice7_committed_errors.py: LexError, LexFailure and NumberError carry 'committed' (true when F# had consumed input before failing), set at all 31 sites; dry run ok. (2) slice7_driver.spi: lex_string_raw (@\\\"...\\\"), lex_hex_number (0x, wrapping to i32 like Convert.ToInt32; over 32 bits is an error, where F# throws); token_step = Stepped (tokens, errors, rest, state) | Untouched | Committed, so or_else tries the next lexer only after an untouched failure; lex_plain_token in F#'s order; then one let rec group: line_from (stop rules from many_iter: an untouched failure must be at the line end, else 'end of line', plus 'Tabs are not allowed.'), lex_macro, macro_items (text, escapes with \\\\v as TokEscapedVar, '\\\\' at the line end continues via lex_state.macro_close), macro_expression (!x/\\\t/@t/#x vars with F#'s prime give-back rule, doubled start char, !(..) bodies tokenized as their own line with spans and errors shifted), and tokenize_line_body for comment, raw-string and macro continuations. Tests: 10 line cases and 9 macro cases, all expectations derived by hand. (3) after-block-tokens.ps1 gates slices 5-6, applies (1) and (2) only if green, gates again, and restores the gated file if slices 7-8 fail.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_12 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 12u32, "2026-10-22T09:45Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:45 main: review pass on the slices 7-8 draft before its gate. Constructor patterns with a bool literal (LexError (at, m, true)) became a bound 'committed' plus an if, since a char literal in that position failed tonight; a one-line 'match .. with A => .. | B => ..' became a block match. Queued as job-1792662286548-main-tokens-after-block: eoie window run compile --wait 140, blocked by tibia's live-gui window, so it starts at the block end on its own (gates slices 5-6, applies 7-8 if green, gates again, restores on failure).")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_13 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 13u32, "2026-10-22T10:11Z", "main", "2026-10-22 06:11 main: the queued gate job was granted a compile window in the gap between tibia's PR-21 and D21 live-gui windows (about 06:00-06:10), so it ran into tibia's block. Stopped it and released its window by hand (job stop left it held); no gate had finished, and tokens.spi and the lib copies are unchanged. Requeue only after tibia's explicit 'block end' (memory live-runs-alone, updated).")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_14 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 14u32, "2026-10-22T16:00Z", "main", "2026-10-22 12:00 main: tokens slices 5-6 gate (inside post-block-gates) reported 2/15 passed, but the raw output says \"Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed\": the box ran at 100% for 30 min (x-precommit-day6, eoie-release-F, tibia libmig jobs, my gates at BelowNormal). F# targets of slices 1-4, green on an earlier quiet gate, failed the same way. Reading rule from now on, for every gate in this batch: a failure whose raw output names the 300 s cell timeout is a load artifact and is rerun alone on a quieter box, never read as red; only a failure with a test message or a type error counts. Slices 7-8 were not applied (the script stops before them), so tokens.spi is unchanged.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_15 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 15u32, "2026-10-28T14:27Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-28 groom: estimate set 6000m (rough D8-epic placeholder vs QUERY-CACHE 6000 / UPSTREAM-ONION 3000; owner refines). No formal deps; BLOCKER = realistically sequenced after HOPACSOTA promotion (P6) + a mature Wasm backend -- it is a far-future epic, not startable until the F#/Elixir interim is replaceable. Not adding a dep edge without the owner.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_16 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 16u32, "2026-10-31T20:05Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:05 compiler (groom): USER RULE (10-31 15:4x): 'we should start the full rewrite only after all backends are sota, no memory problems, rc slowdowns, union hacks, recursions, ariths missing, etc.' plus 'edition3 gotta finish also' and 'gleam should be a top backend to test against to simulate abyssal codebases'. The deps now name every gate: edition 3 (EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION, EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL, SPIRAL3-EDITIONS); primitives/conversions (PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES, new BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY, GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS); shapes (BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS, STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS for the Rust/union hacks); recursion (MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS, GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); Rc/clone cost (RUST-MOVE-ON-LAST-USE, RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, RUST-FNMUT-CAPTURE-MOVE); memory (DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY); scale on Gleam (new GLEAM-ABYSSAL-SCALE); the concurrency design (GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT: Hopac + crossbeam + Gleam Subject under one interface); Cells speed (KINO-SOTA); and every other backend at full coverage (WGSL, eBPF, Calyx, OpenQASM 3, Lean). The tokenizer slices in apps/compiler/spi stay as the oracle-checked groundwork, but the FULL rewrite does not start until every dep is Done. Targets to test the self-hosted compiler against, in order: F# (bridge, diff vs the F# compiler), Rust (fast host), Gleam (abyssal scale), Wasm (stated target), with C/Zig as oracles.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_17 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 17u32, "2026-10-31T20:08Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:08 compiler GROOM, user direction (/btw 10-31 15:4x): the full rewrite starts only after EVERY backend is SOTA: no memory problems (DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY), no Rc slowdowns (RUST-MOVE-ON-LAST-USE, RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, RUST-FNMUT-CAPTURE-MOVE), no union hacks (BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS), no recursion limits (MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS), no missing arithmetic (GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS, PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES); GADT bugs (GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX) and conversion gaps (CHAR-ORDERING, new) are unacceptable now; edition 3 finishes first (EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION); Cells as fast as F# projects (KINO-SOTA); every backend's own item (WGSL, CALYX, OPENQASM3, BEND, EBPF). All are deps now and P0. TEST TARGETS for the rewrite: F# (the bridge: slices diffed against the F# original), Rust (native speed, deep recursion), Wasm (the stated target), Gleam (user: top target, simulates abyssal codebases), with the C/Zig-oracle matrix as the regression net. CONCURRENCY: the target design reuses Hopac, crossbeam and Gleam's Subject under one interface (folds into HOPACSOTA-P7's engine interface). Front-end slices (tokenizer, then block splitting and parser) may continue against oracles meanwhile; partial evaluation is last.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_18 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 18u32, "2026-10-31T20:09Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:09 compiler: deps MERGED (two grooms ran at once and the second deps write dropped 7): the union is 24 items, the fork's 22 (EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL, SPIRAL3-EDITIONS, BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY, STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS, GLEAM-ABYSSAL-SCALE, GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT, LEAN-BACKEND restored) plus CHAR-ORDERING and BEND-BACKEND.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_19 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 19u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 08:03 compiler, PRE-INFLUX LANE MAP (user 08:0x: main is reading an external conversation that will add many items; groom so new tasks MERGE into what's pending). Compiler team: 56 open after this groom (23 Active, 5 Blocked, 28 Planned). Each theme names its MERGE ANCHOR: a new task on that theme becomes a note or sub-item there, not a new parallel item.\n1 CORRECTNESS GATE (self-hosting, P0). Anchor BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY (op x type x backend census). Members: CHAR-ORDERING (55%, samples core switched; lib-core sweep running), GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (erasure plan), PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES 82%, STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS, SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD 95%.\n2 BACKEND COVERAGE. Anchor BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS (lib test targets: rust 427, gleam 205, zig 27, c 22, lean/wasm 0). Members: GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS 75% (arrays/refs ffi left), GLEAM-ABYSSAL-SCALE, GLEAM-PARTS-EMIT, WGSL/CALYX/OPENQASM3-BACKEND, EBPF-C-PROFILE, LEAN (merged into the anchor).\n3 RUST CODEGEN QUALITY. Anchor RUST-MOVE-ON-LAST-USE (85/kloc clones; next lever = borrow census for 497 Rc clones). Members: RUST-UNUSED-PATTERN-CLONES (P3 polish), RUST-FNMUT-CAPTURE-MOVE, RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE 90%, RUST-STRING-WRAPPER-INLINE, RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE (Blocked: push), EXPORT-STRING-PARAM-RC (Blocked 95%: push).\n4 READABLE CODEGEN (all backends). Anchor CODEGEN-READABLE-2. Members: GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE, RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE (shared).\n5 MEMORY / NATIVE RUNTIME. Anchor DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY 78% (step 2 retain/release next). Members: C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS (Blocked: Linux CI on push), MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER, MEGA-PARALLEL-JOIN-POINTS.\n6 HOPACSOTA / PARALLEL COMPILE. Anchor HOPACSOTA (epic). Members: HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH (decision entry written: caller-thread claims, gated), HOPACSOTA-P3 (shard+IVar A/B owed), P4, P5, P6 (promotion), P7, QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER, HEAVY-HOLD-DEADLOCK.\n7 EDITION 3 / SYNTAX. Anchor EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION. Members: EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL 85% (tree-sitter left), SPIRAL3-EDITIONS, LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION, LIST-SUGAR-DRIFT-GUARD, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS (Blocked), SPIRAL-FORMATTER (merge candidate with KEEP-BREAKS: same last 5%).\n8 PACKS / RELEASE FLOW. Anchor PACK-13 (ord defaulting + x-compat retirement, programs in apps/compiler/packs/pack13). Members: CI-LINUX-ENV-RESTORE-GUARD 90% (landed; needs post-push CI), CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE (Blocked), COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION.\n9 METRICS. Anchor BACKEND-METRICS-MODEL (first rows recorded). Members: DOTNET-ORACLE-COST.\n10 SELF-CHECKING / SAMPLES. Anchor SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES (advances via main's SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS).\n11 HYGIENE / ENV. Anchor COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE 80%. Members: DATA-DIR-HOME 70%, COMPILER-WIPE-DAMAGE 80%, SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON 90%, CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY 50% (box sm' gate owed).\n12 SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL itself: the umbrella; its deps are the gate list (themes 1, 2, 5 first, per the user's 10-31 rule).\nClosed in this groom: KIT-STATE-SPELLING-GUARD (both halves live). Since 10-31 18:00: PACK-12, MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS, BACKEND-BATCH, DELPHI-USES-UNITS.\nMERGE RULES for the influx: (a) search this map's anchor first (memory search-backlog-before-new); (b) a new task that restates an open item becomes a note there, citing its source; (c) a genuinely new theme gets one anchor item, not N siblings; (d) codegen text edits ship as kit do programs in apps/compiler/packs/pack<N>/ and batch into one candidate (BACKEND-BATCH rule).")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_20 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 20u32, "2026-11-01T12:07Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 08:07 compiler: MAP UPDATE (n19) for DIRECTION-1031's compiler children, merged into existing themes, no new anchors: CHECK-SILENT-DROP (P0) -> theme 1 correctness (in progress: --check already strict on pack12b; the build-path leak in same-package siblings is fixed in PACK-13 program 2). SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION and SPELLING-PROFILES -> theme 7 under EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION (both touch the formatter/parser; SPELLING-PROFILES generalizes the respell that already has headerSpelling/keywordSpelling tables in FormatterConvert). BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT -> theme 5 with MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER (its M0 = &[u8] input + a rebar runner; that's sample and runtime work first, compiler codegen later). Queue order for the compiler lane: CHECK-SILENT-DROP -> CHAR-ORDERING lib core (sweep running) -> SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION (480m, RFC with 13 acceptance tests) -> SPELLING-PROFILES (600m) -> BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT M0.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_21 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 21u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:40 compiler, R5 lane map add (1/4): theme PERFORMANCE gains COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE (P0, next after CHAR-ORDERING) and the HOPACSOTA near-SOTA verdict plan (M1-M5, rule: GC<15%, exponents<=1.1, no >=2x fix left).")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_22 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 22u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:40 compiler, R5 lane map add (3/4): theme EDITION3 gains EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL (:> entry + hardcoded-word census) and EDITION3-SAMPLES-RESPELL (P0 destructive respell under trap checks); theme FORMATTER gains FORMATTER-PARENS-MISSES.")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_23 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 23u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:40 compiler, R5 lane map add (2/4): theme LANGUAGE/TYPEFEATURESET gains SPIRAL-NAMEOF (typed nameof, cases_of, derived to_name/of_name) and its census SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL (runs first, CPU-light).")
inl note_of_self_hosted_spiral_24 () = Note ("SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", 24u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:40 compiler, R5 lane map add (4/4): theme RELEASE/CI gains SPIRAL-CI-COMPILER-BINARIES (6 RIDs incl. osx); packs folder retired (rule on COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE n48: drafts in apps/compiler/drafts, tools in scripts). New queue: CHAR-ORDERING, CHECK-SILENT-DROP close, COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE, BRZOZOWSKI M0, EDITION3-SAMPLES-RESPELL, SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION, SPELLING-PROFILES.")
inl fsx_from_spi () = Task ("FSX-FROM-SPI", "Generate F# (.fsx) from .spi notebooks instead of hand-writing it, for the formatter and hopacsota layers, with GADTs/existentials/HKTs/prototypes/reflection simulated by phantom data (user 2026-10-15 22:45)", Story, P1, D6, 15u32, Planned, "SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL", "fsharp,spiral,self-hosting,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fsx_from_spi () = Planning ("FSX-FROM-SPI", Minutes 720u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_1 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 1u32, "2026-10-19T12:11Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:11 helper-lane lap 1: measured the two targets in spiral_compiler.fs today: the Formatter section is lines 177553-180934 (about 3,380 F# lines, reads tokens and parse_block results only) and the hopacsota layer PartEvalSeamsHopacsota is lines 53397-53540 (about 143 lines, G1 142). Both are written against core F# types (tokens, RawExpr, PartEval dictionaries), so generated F# must name those types through macros or nominal stand-ins; the 143-line seams layer is the realistic pilot, the formatter the payoff. Still gated on SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL (0%).")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_2 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 2u32, "2026-10-19T13:04Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:04 helper-lane lap 2: found the concrete compiler gap: generated F# can only be a script today. Every samples/*/main.fsx is top-level lets ending in the program's value (closure_apply ends in if v2 then 0 else 1), with no module or namespace in any sample output, and the library entry op !!!!Export (Op union line 43683: a name and a function without runtime captures) is implemented only in CodegenRust (~163802), CodegenGleam (~167185) and CodegenTypescript (~172954); codegenFsharp has no Export arm. So generating the formatter or the hopacsota seams as F# that the compiler can link needs, first, F# Export (a module with named functions instead of a script body), the same contract the Rust/Gleam/TS arms already enforce (duplicate export check, closure without captures).")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_3 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 3u32, "2026-10-19T14:20Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 10:20 helper-lane lap 3: drafted F# Export as lab/FSX-FROM-SPI/patch.py (4 anchors, --check mode: anchors OK on today's spiral_compiler.fs, LF). It mirrors CodegenRust's arm: codegenFsharp gains exports/export_names/closure_of_var; TyJoinPoint(JPClosure) with no args records the var's closure tag; TyOp(Export, name, closure var) emits let name (v1 : t, ...) : range = f_cN () args (struct tuple for several params, the shape F# closures already take: closure_apply's let rec f_c0 () (v0 : int32)); exports land after the let rec group, before the script body. Probe lab/FSX-FROM-SPI/probe (add_one, add_pair) + use.fsx (#load main.fsx, open Main, expects FSX-EXPORT-OK). Heavy-queued to ride the next compiler pack; Fsharp residual-only changes expected: none (no sample uses Export on F#).")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_4 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 4u32, "2026-10-19T17:43Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 13:43 its pack 7 patch is in the accepted baseline (pack 7 ACCEPTED single-flight-20261019-125623 (7,020 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells vs review 124451, C rows unchanged)); the item stays open for its remaining scope.")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_5 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 5u32, "2026-10-19T21:45Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 17:45 helper-lane lap 6: the pack 7 F# Export patch never worked end to end. On the installed compiler, lab/FSX-FROM-SPI/probe fails with Non-standard functions are not supported in the F# backend. The cause: Export's peval retypes the exported function to FT_Pointer (single-flight 160392), and both the F# closure join point (163091) and F# tyv (162738) accepted only FT_Vanilla. Fix: lab/FSX-FROM-SPI/pointer_closure_patch.py, two arms that accept (FT_Vanilla | FT_Pointer), --apply gated. On a private-cache Debug candidate (pointer-run.ps1, 0 errors) the probe emits let add_one (v0 : int32) : int32 = closure0 () v0 and add_pair over a struct tuple, and dotnet fsi use.fsx prints FSX-EXPORT-OK, exit 0. The probe was also refreshed for core v1 (+ instead of +., packages |core-). Offered to main for pack 11. The item's bigger scope, generating the formatter and hopacsota layers as .fsx, is still ahead.")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_6 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 6u32, "2026-10-20T00:21Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 20:21 main: pack 11 ACCEPTED 20:21 (single-flight-20261019-191017: 7,276 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells vs the Release candidate review 190039); pointer_closure_patch.py is in: F# Export accepts FT_Pointer closures (helper lane 1 probe prints FSX-EXPORT-OK).")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_7 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 7u32, "2026-10-22T05:36Z", "main", "01:36 main: lab run outputs moved to the run cache, per the lab rule that run outputs never sit in lab: 3 file(s) (logs, notebooks, diffs, metrics/gate/timing TSVs) are now under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runs\\lab-outputs\\FSX-FROM-SPI\\ at the same relative paths, sha256 checked. Scripts and probes stay in lab/FSX-FROM-SPI until the item lands.")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_8 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 8u32, "2026-10-22T07:01Z", "main", "03:01 main: lab drained. Both patches have landed (patch.py's anchor and pointer_closure_patch.py's change are absent on a fresh copy of the core; pack 11, note 20:21). The F# Export probe is promoted as a check: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/export-check-fsharp.ps1 (-Dll optional; dotnet and package dir resolved as the other scripts do) with its probe in scripts/export-check-fsharp/ (main.spi exports add_one and add_pair; use.fsx loads the generated main.fsx and must print FSX-EXPORT-OK). Validated at the time of this note on the installed compiler: 405-byte main.fsx, FSX-EXPORT-OK, fsi exit 0; the output goes to the run cache and the tree folder stays clean. installed-run.ps1 and pointer-run.ps1 (one-off runners) are dropped. It pairs with RUST-EXPORT-TYPES' crate probes, which land in the same folder at the pack install. Folder deleted.")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_9 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 9u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 4 11:29 (subagent): blocked: F# Export patch rides main's pack 7 (about 14:00, after the switch accept) -> next: read pack 7's FSX-EXPORT-OK probe; then the module/namespace header option | lap 5 12:19 (subagent): batched in main's pack 7 (build about an hour out) -> next: read pack 7's FSX-EXPORT-OK probe | lap 7 19:54 (subagent): re-read: pointer_closure_patch.py in pack 11; FSX-EXPORT-OK proven on a candidate -> next: after the accept, rerun probe/use.fsx on the installed compiler")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_10 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 10u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 helper patch record folded from the deleted history folder: patch lab/FSX-FROM-SPI/patch.py, state 'rides pack 7 (main)', proof: probe/use.fsx prints FSX-EXPORT-OK")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_11 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 11u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_fsx_from_spi_12 () = Note ("FSX-FROM-SPI", 12u32, "2026-10-31T20:56Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
