inl note_of_toolchain_latest_1 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 1u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: pins in our workflows today: Rust nightly-2025-05-09 (gh-pages builds), nightly-2024-07-14 (NEAR contracts), nightly-2025-11-01 (app builds), 1.88.0 (eoie); setup-dotnet 9.0.202 while the compiler builds on .NET 11 rc; OTP 27, Elixir 1.18, Gleam 1.19.1, rebar3 3.24.0 (local OTP is 29); Python 3.12.10; zig 0.17.0 in CI vs 0.18-dev locally; Kotlin 2.4.21, Swift 6.4, Lean v4.35.0-rc4, playwright 1.44.0, trunk 0.21.14. Next grain: check release dates for each family, then bump one family per pack with a full suite.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_2 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 2u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: version matrix taken; .NET 11 rc.2 (11.0.100-rc.2.26504.105) installs in 63 s into a private cache and builds the compiler (145 s); a full review on that build (single-flight-20261017-034133) has 0 differing cells against bless 145428 on all 6,906 rows. install-dotnet.ps1 already takes the newest 11.0 preview, so only the shared local cache is behind (rc.1); move it as its own step after PACK-NIGHT-1017 is blessed, with a Tibia toolchain notice. Order: .NET rc.2, CI Rust nightlies to stable 1.99, CI OTP 27 to 29, scoop erl before choco on PATH.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_3 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 3u32, "2026-10-17T18:24Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:24 from the bundles (brzozowski alpha54, samples alpha705, spiral-bin alpha417; BUNDLE-WISDOM note 11): when moving toolchains, pin compiler identity as content fingerprints plus a mandatory capability probe, not one wrapper hash (identical spiral-compile wrappers sat on top of a good and a bad companion). Choose a new release by capability superset: an apparently latest lane was a functional subset of the stable one. Keep health per capability and history-aware (SDK ok / compiler attested / restore smoke failing as separate states). Use typed env profiles validated before launch (a malformed export produced SPIRAL_DOTNET=/dotnet). Preserve executable bits on rehydrate.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_4 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 4u32, "2026-10-18T09:05Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 05:05 main-thread local scoop status (manifests as of today): gleam 1.19.1 -> 1.19.2, elixir 1.19.4 -> 1.20.4, temurin-jdk 25.0.1 -> 27.0.0 (Kotlin native tier runs KotlinServer on JDK 25), pwsh 7.5.4 -> 7.6.6, rustup 1.28.2 -> 1.29.1, uv 0.9.21 -> 0.13.0, go 1.25.4 -> 1.27.2. Web: OTP 29.0 shipped 2026-05-13 (CI still pins 27). Not installed mid-run: every tool version is part of the native-memo key (a bump replays nothing) and peers share the binaries, so bump one family per quiet window with a full review.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_5 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:26Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:26 lap 1 grain: Rust family done today (RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE: nightly-2026-10-18 in every build script, the matrix, Cells and 8 CI workflows, every build verified, Linux rustix fixed by cfg); remaining families from the 10-18 scoop list: gleam 1.19.2, elixir 1.20.4, temurin 27, pwsh 7.6.6, rustup 1.29.1, uv 0.13, go 1.27.2, and OTP 29 in CI (still 27 in some workflows) Next: check which workflows still pin otp-version 27 vs 29 and gleam 1.19.1 vs 1.19.2; bump one family per quiet window with a full review")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_6 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 6u32, "2026-10-19T12:59Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:59 lap 2 grain: CI pins re-read across 10 repos: OTP 29, Elixir 1.20, Gleam 1.19.2 everywhere except tibia (OTP 27, Elixir 1.18, Gleam 1.19.1, tibia lane's tree, told); setup-dotnet pins 9.0.202 in spiral, dice, alphabet, polyglot, dir-tree-html, i574n.github while the compiler builds net11.0 (run_notebook installs .NET 11 itself), so the 9.0.202 pin is the next family to move Next: check what still needs the .NET 9 SDK in CI (fsi notebooks? dotnet tools) before bumping setup-dotnet to 11")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_7 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:03Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:03 lap 2 grain: found why CI still pins setup-dotnet 9.0.202: lib/spiral/lib.ps1 generates F# projects with TargetFramework net9.0 and runs the global dotnet publish (used by dice lib/build.ps1 and lib/fsharp/build.ps1), while the compiler, matrix and Cells already use their own .NET 11 SDK through Resolve-SpiralDotnet (env.ps1, install-dotnet.ps1); other direct dotnet calls are bench scripts (brzozowski bench.ps1, lib bench/parsing) and polyglot's temp cube; the only fsproj files left with net9.0 are vendored fable-library sources in polyglot Next: lib.ps1: generate net11.0 and publish with Resolve-SpiralDotnet, prove with dice lib/fsharp/build.ps1 (HEAVY QUEUE), then drop setup-dotnet from the gh-pages workflows (alphabet mirrors dice)")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_8 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 8u32, "2026-10-19T14:03Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:03 lap 2 grain: .NET step applied in the tree: lib/spiral/lib.ps1 PublishFsharp now generates net11.0 and publishes with the .NET 11 SDK from Ensure-SpiralCompiler (Resolve-SpiralDotnet) instead of the global dotnet, so dice lib/build.ps1 and lib/fsharp/build.ps1 no longer need CI's setup-dotnet 9.0.202 Next: HEAVY QUEUE 2: dice lib/fsharp/build.ps1 on net11; on green, remove setup-dotnet from the dice and alphabet workflows (and the other repos that only pin it for this)")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_9 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 9u32, "2026-10-19T14:51Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:51 proven: dice lib/fsharp/build.ps1 with the patched lib.ps1 (net11.0, .NET 11 SDK from Resolve-SpiralDotnet) publishes and runs: FSHARP-OK dice/lib/fsharp / result 72096518 (main heavy queue 2, 10:50-10:51). Remaining: setup-dotnet 9.0.202 in the gh-pages workflows is now unused by our builds; left in place until the next push shows no other step needs a global .NET 9 (removing it is then a one-line workflow edit in each repo, alphabet mirroring dice).")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_10 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 10u32, "2026-10-19T18:36Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:36 lap 4 grain: scoop status 14:3x, matrix-relevant tools behind latest: zig-dev 0.18.0-dev.146 -> dev.349 (Zig is now the first oracle), wasmtime 49.0.2 -> 49.0.3, temurin-jdk 25.0.1 -> 27.0.0 (the Kotlin server runs on JDK 25), pwsh 7.5.4 -> 7.6.7 (every script), rustup 1.28.2 -> 1.29.1, cmake 4.2.1 -> 4.4.4, uv 0.9.21 -> 0.13.1, git 2.52 -> 2.56, zed 1.23.2 -> 1.24.2; current: gleam 1.19.2, bun 1.4.3, erlang 29.1.2, elixir 1.20.4, .NET 11 rc.1; node 23.5.0 and python 3.12.10 are not scoop-managed and old (node 23 is an EOL odd line). Bumps change toolchain.tsv stamps, so they need one dedicated -AcceptToolchain pack, never mid-review Next: toolchain pack after pack 8b accepts: scoop update zig-dev wasmtime temurin-jdk pwsh rustup, rerun -Native (memo replays only the rows whose tool stamps changed), accept with -AcceptToolchain if DISAGREE 0")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_11 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 11u32, "2026-10-19T23:21Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 19:21 lap 6 grain: toolchain pack staged but moved to 10-20: scratchpad toolchain-job.ps1 updates wasmtime 49.0.2, temurin-jdk 25.0.1 and rustup 1.28.2 (scoop keeps the old versions, so scoop reset app@old rolls back) and reviews against the latest accept without accepting; zig-dev stays out of it (Zig is the first oracle, a dev-snapshot bump gets its own pack); tonight's matrix window went to packs 11 and 12; NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS needs the native Cells rustc (1.88.0-nightly) itself bumped to >= 1.93 for near-sys 0.2.14, a rustup self-update does not do that Next: run toolchain-job.ps1 first thing on 10-20, then a separate zig-dev pack, then the native rustc bump with the NEAR rerun")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_12 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 12u32, "2026-10-20T02:43Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 22:43 main: toolchain pack blocked by scoop itself: scoop config scoop_repo = https://github.com/i574n/Scoop-Core (branch main), which does not exist (also not under fc1943s), so every scoop update fails at Updating Scoop with Repository not found before touching an app; wasmtime, temurin-jdk and rustup stayed at 49.0.2, 25.0.1, 1.28.2; scoop status works only from local manifests (last core update 2023-03-08). Unblock (user decision, persistent tool config): point scoop_repo back at the upstream ScoopInstaller/Scoop or restore the i574n/Scoop-Core fork, then rerun scratchpad toolchain-job.ps1. The review it started is left to finish as a determinism check (stopping test.ps1 mid-compile can leave sample outputs empty).")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_13 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 13u32, "2026-10-20T03:10Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 23:10 main: scoop unblocked per the user: scoop_repo and the core clone now point at https://github.com/Ash258/Scoop-Core (main, archived but live; the original upstream of the missing i574n fork), scoop update succeeds again (core 52fe1646); Mold fixed to match in C:\\home\\git\\dotfiles\\dist\\windows\\install.ps1 (fresh clone of i574n/dotfiles for the user to commit): SCOOP_REPO -> Ash258/Scoop-Core, and the mold bucket URL i574n/mold.git (a rename redirect) -> i574n/dotfiles.git. The toolchain pack runs after pack 13 frees the matrix.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_14 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 14u32, "2026-10-21T03:26Z", "main", "23:26 scoop status (read-only) after last night's repo fix: matrix-relevant updates wasmtime 49.0.2 -> 49.0.4, temurin-jdk 25.0.1 -> 27.0.0-35, rustup 1.28.2 -> 1.29.1, zig-dev 0.18.0-dev.146 -> dev.349 (the first oracle, so its own pack), uv 0.9.21 -> 0.13.2, go 1.25.4 -> 1.27.2, cmake 4.2.1 -> 4.4.4, git 2.52.0 -> 2.56.0.2, pwsh 7.5.4 -> 7.6.7 (left to the user: the shell under every running session). Rewrote scratchpad toolchain-job.ps1: the scoop update of wasmtime, temurin-jdk and rustup takes the exclusive compiler-install window (other lanes may be running those tools), prints rollback commands (scoop reset app@old), then a -ReuseNative review that reruns only rows whose tool stamps changed. Runs after the evening pack install so its review has a fixed compiler.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_15 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 15u32, "2026-10-21T23:02Z", "main", "19:02 scoop status recheck (read-only): the matrix-relevant updates are unchanged since 10-21 03:26 (wasmtime 49.0.2 -> 49.0.4, temurin-jdk 25.0.1 -> 27.0.0-35, rustup 1.28.2 -> 1.29.1, zig-dev dev.146 -> dev.349 as its own pack since Zig is the first oracle, uv, go, cmake, git; pwsh 7.5.4 -> 7.6.7 stays with the user). Fixed the staged scratchpad toolchain-job.ps1 the same way as pack-night.ps1: its review baseline is now the newest run with >= 7,000 rows, not the newest dir (a -Filter rerun would have shown every row missing). Syntax-checked. Still queued behind the night-pack install (it needs the exclusive compiler-install window); not tonight, the window closes at 21:00.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_16 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 16u32, "2026-10-22T03:22Z", "main", "23:22 main (user 23:1x: update otp to latest, you have system permissions): upstream latest is OTP-29.1.2 (released 2026-10-14), already scoop's current; the drift was Chocolatey's erlang 26.2.5.5 plus rebar3 3.23.0, which resolved first on PATH (bare erl booted OTP 26 and crashed with load_failed: spiral/erl_crash.dump of 10-19, ERL-CRASH-DUMPS-IN-TREE). Done in an elevated shell: scoop install rebar3 (3.28.0, upstream release of 2026-10-21), choco uninstall rebar3 erlang, removed the orphan C:\\ProgramData\\chocolatey\\bin\\rebar3.cmd (15 bytes, pointed at the removed install). Now: erl = scoop OTP 29 erts 17.1.1, rebar3 = rebar 3.28.0 on OTP 29, elixir 1.20.4 (latest stable). Locally only CI workflows name rebar3 (setup-beam installs its own); running VMs were all scoop OTP 29, so none was affected.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_17 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 17u32, "2026-10-22T08:20Z", "main", "04:20 main: CI pin check against upstream (read only, gh api releases). rebar3 3.27.3 -> 3.28.0 (released 2026-10-21; local scoop already runs it) bumped in gh-pages.yml of spiral (3 jobs: build, compiler, cells-gate), polyglot, dice and alphabet; YAML parses; uncommitted for the user. Already current: gleam 1.19.2 (10-12), bun 1.4.3 (10-10), Elixir 1.20, OTP 29. Zig's 0.17.0 pin is newer than the GitHub mirror's 0.15.1, since Zig publishes on ziglang.org; zig-dev stays its own pack. The dotnet-version 9.0.202 pin (setup-dotnet) is not the compiler's SDK, because workflow.ps1 installs .NET 11 itself; 9.0.319 is the newest 9.0 patch, left for the user. The scratchpad toolchain-job.ps1 (wasmtime, temurin, rustup and zig-dev review job) now lives in %TEMP%\\toolchain-latest; it needs the compiler-install window.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_18 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 18u32, "2026-10-24T00:21Z", "main", "2026-10-23 20:21 main: upstream re-read (gh api releases/latest). gleam v1.19.2 (10-12), OTP-29.1.2 (10-14), elixir v1.20.4 and rebar3 3.28.0 are current. New: bun v1.4.4 (10-22; local ~/.bun is 1.4.3, while CI's setup-bun@v2.2.0 has no bun-version pin and takes the latest on its own) and wasmtime v50.0.0 (10-20; the job's scoop app). %TEMP%\\toolchain-latest\\toolchain-job.ps1 gains -Bun: bun upgrade inside the same compiler-install window, before/after logged with a rollback note. Bend rows depend on bun's 18 MB main-thread stack (BUN_JSC_maxPerThreadStackUsage), so the job's matrix review is the check. It needs the exclusive compiler-install window, so it runs after tonight's chains, not inside them (scratch next-session.md). Status corrected to Active: OTP/rebar3 and the CI pins moved on 10-22.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_19 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 19u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_toolchain_latest_20 () = Note ("TOOLCHAIN-LATEST", 20u32, "2026-10-30T01:58Z", "main", "10-29 21:58 main, groom (fill-all-task-fields): NO estimate basis. Paused, with no pre-registered milestones in the notes, so the estimate stays blank rather than guessed (estimates-from-rules). Sizing question for whoever resumes it: name 3 milestones with an expected size each; the estimate is then their sum.")
