inl note_of_fiscal_app_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-APP", 23u32, "2026-11-01T12:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:15 fiscal: MERGE RESULT for main's browser batch (DIRECTION-1031): nothing fiscal-scope to merge. The only fiscal-adjacent part (the Sigenius/Abu Dhabi business track) was dropped by the user and not filed. EXPECTED LATER: NAMING-LEXICON-RATCHET (a canonical function lexicon in standards.spi plus a ratchet in every repo). When it reaches fiscal, file its fiscal share as a child under cluster F (model quality, beside FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS and FISCAL-GRANULAR-280); it renames generated identifiers, so it is also gated on FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND.")
inl note_of_fiscal_app_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-APP", 24u32, "2026-11-01T14:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:55 fiscal: MERGE MAP UPDATE (groom round 5). New items: FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE (P0 epic: the user's \"super generic + provable\" target, with the measured baseline 46% per-country generator lines / 48% repeated generated lines and the two counters), with children FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST (P1: families as typed data, 0 per-country lines) and FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB (P1: insert/nth/sample_path -> am'.sort / listm'.try_item / one runtime unit). Placement: a new cluster I (GENERIC + PROOFS) gated on A (edition 3) and on XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES (B); FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES and FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE (B) are its dedup steps; FISCAL-LIFECYCLE-EVENTS (D) is re-baselined to 30% with the document-state GADT target. CII (FISCAL-CII-PROFILES) is the acceptance test of cluster I: the first family that must need 0 new generator code.")
