inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_37 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL", 37u32, "2026-11-10T04:42Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:5x microblog (help-pool groom, read-only): the 5 milestones of the 11-09 plan are all Done with proof in their last notes: M1 record/replay store (rig_convo_replay notebook gate green on ganymede), M2 JSON-lines persistence through the lib json codec (tibia draft applied, hash-equal, kit standards 0), M3 tool schemas (lib json.spi test tool_schema_describes_records_unions_options_and_arrays, c + rust), M4 type-directed decoder into the same record, M5 the .convo surface reader. So this epic looks finished, yet it still lists as ready Planned light work at 75% in every lane's pull. Next step (rig, owner): close it at 100% Done on that evidence, or name the useful Convo-Lang part still missing as a new milestone.")
inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_38 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL", 38u32, "2026-11-10T04:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 00:5x rig (owner), CLOSING on microblog's groom evidence, verified: CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M1..M5 are all 100 pct Done. Shipped: the lib parts (json.spi, json_scan.spi, json_schema.spi with the tool_schema test). In kit and NOT yet in an installed train: src/rig_convo_replay (untracked; record/replay store over a typed transcript, JSON-lines persistence, type-directed decoder, the .convo surface reader; notebook gate green on ganymede), which rides the train snapshots and is gated in their notebook phase. Left out on purpose (rare in the 290-file mine of 10-17: @edge routing 8 files, @on 8, @condition 7, components/RAG): not worth a milestone. Next step: none; the train verdicts cover rig_convo_replay.")
inl gadt_growing_index_hang () = Task ("GADT-GROWING-INDEX-HANG", "Compiler hang (both builds tested: candidate single-flight DLL of pack night-1017): a value of a recursive GADT whose case FIELD mentions the type at a grown index never finishes compiling (CPU-bound, ~230 MB, killed after 45-250 s). 8-line repro: nominal zero = (); nominal succ n = (); union rec transcript pending = | Done :: transcript zero | Call :: forall n. i32 * transcript (succ n) -> transcript n; inl main () : i32 = (inl t : transcript zero = Done) then 7i32. Same union defined but unused: compiles. Index kept the same (chain n -> chain n) or a non-recursive index change (box (succ n)): compile and run. Wrong programs over the full Call/Result transcript are rejected fast and correctly (Got transcript (succ zero) / Expected transcript zero), so type checking is fine; the suspect is the representation/reachable-cases closure of a GADT-indexed union (pack-1x: 'a GADT-indexed union holds only its reachable cases'), which expands transcript zero -> transcript (succ zero) -> ... without bound. Fix: compute reachable cases over the index modulo the case's quantified variables (a case whose field index grows is reachable for every instance, no expansion), or bound the closure and fall back to all cases; add the repro as the regression sample. Found while prototyping CONVO-IN-SPIRAL's type-level tool-call protocol (unanswered Call = type error).", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,gadt,bug", "current", "current")
inl lab_in_repo () = Task ("LAB-IN-REPO", "Experiments live in the repo, not in job tmp (user 2026-10-17: tmp overuse is drift; it also blocks continuing on another machine or in a cloud agent). Convention started in spiral/lab: one directory per backlog item named by its id lowercased (lab/convo-in-spiral, lab/lib-reactors, lab/hopacsota-hopac-depth, lab/hopacsota-lf-scheduling, lab/gadt-growing-index-hang), git-tracked sources only, one shared bounded runner lab/try.ps1 (60 s kill, shared DLL or SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL), run outputs in git-ignored lab/.runs; portable references only (nuget refs, repo-relative paths, no user-profile paths). Lifecycle: when the item is Done, its lab dir is promoted (lib/, apps/, samples/) or deleted in the same change; an item Paused/Planned keeps it. Measured drift it replaces: this job's tmp holds ~850 scripts in ~120 topic folders (packs, lanes, probes, benches) plus spiral-bin\\packs, all lost with the job and invisible to other machines; the heavy gate itself (tmp/shared/heavy.ps1 with the run ledger) lives there. Next: (1) EOIE-LAB-AUDIT; (2) move the reusable main-lane tools (heavy gate + ledger, compare-runs, kino-suite runner, pack scripts) into repo homes (apps/compiler/tmp/scripts or lab/<item>); (3) per-repo lab/ in eoie, i574n.github, polyglot as they need it.", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "process,lab,drift,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lab_in_repo () = Planning ("LAB-IN-REPO", Minutes 135u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kit_lab_audit () = Task ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", "eoie verb for lab lifecycle (eoie-first; one call): eoie lab audit <repo lab dir> <backlog root> lists every lab/<id> directory with its backlog item status and last note date, and flags: item missing (orphan lab), item Done (promote or delete now), no note for >14 days (stale), files ignored by .gitignore but present (run outputs outside .runs), absolute user-profile paths in sources (non-portable). Exit non-zero on orphan/Done so CI and the end-of-run check can gate on it. Written as granular Spiral in eoie, tests as Spiral test blocks. Consumer: LAB-IN-REPO.", Story, P3, D4, 60u32, Planned, "", "kit,lab,process,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_lab_audit () = Planning ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_1 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 1u32, "2026-10-17T14:48Z", "main-thread", "10:48 main-thread fork: TDD case written first (eoie/spec/one-call.md case 34, 'Audit lab directories against the backlog'): fixture with 3 lab dirs (one Paused item, one orphan, one Done item) and a source holding a C:\\Users nuget path; setup creates the 2 items with agile add/set as eoie do statements; command eoie do . 'lab audit lab against backlog'; exact expected table (lab, item, status, progress, verdict: keep / orphan: no backlog item OLD-PROBE / done: promote or delete), one non-portable line with file:line, receipt 'failed labs 3 keep 1 orphan 1 done 1 stale 0 non-portable 1'. Item id = lab dir name uppercased. Open in the spec: agile statements inside eoie do (the setup needs them) and the stale rule (last note older than 14 days at <clock>). Implementation is granular Spiral in eoie, not started (compiler-heavy builds wait for a free gate).")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_2 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 2u32, "2026-10-17T15:11Z", "main-thread", "11:11 main-thread fork: HANDOFF (lane paused): spec case 34 in eoie/spec/one-call.md is the TDD target; implementation not started.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_3 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 3u32, "2026-10-17T22:21Z", "main-thread", "18:21 main-thread: spiral/lab was emptied 2026-10-17 (every folder promoted to lib/samples/scripts/lanes or deleted, with a note on its item; lab/ is now created on demand). eoie/spec/one-call.md lines ~919-943 still cite lab/convo-in-spiral paths as audit fixtures; refresh those expected outputs when the audit verb is built.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_4 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 4u32, "2026-10-19T09:40Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 05:40 eoie lane: implemented as an eoie do statement, 'lab audit <dir> against <backlog>' (crate eoie_do_lab, 540 lines): per lab folder the backlog item, status, progress and a verdict (keep, orphan: no backlog item X, done: promote or delete, stale: no note for N days when the last note is older than 14 days), plus non-portable C:\\Users\\... and /home/<user>/ paths with file:line; exits 1 on any finding. Spec case 34 green on the installed eoie.exe. Not yet: gitignored files present in a lab folder.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_5 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 5u32, "2026-10-19T10:09Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 06:09 eoie lane: added the remaining finding: files ignored by .gitignore inside a lab folder (git status --ignored=matching), except under .runs, print as '<path>  ignored by .gitignore (run output outside .runs)' and add 'ignored N' to the receipt. Stale now means the item's last note is older than 14 days. The /home/<user>/ rule only matches at a token start, so C:/home/git paths are not flagged. On the real eoie repo: 5 labs, all keep, 0 findings. Installed in eoie.exe 06:08. Remaining from the item text: a top-level 'eoie lab audit' verb outside do (the do statement covers one-call use).")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_6 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 6u32, "2026-10-22T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:39 x: new consumer: LAB-SESSION-SWEEP (user 2026-10-21 21:4x: lab files live one session, then typed Spiral or pruned). Needed on top of the 10-17 spec case 34: --since <ISO time> lists only files created or changed after it (what one session must resolve), a carry marker read from the item's notes (a note naming the file path counts as the one allowed carry; a second session end over the same file flags 'carried twice'), run outputs flagged by extension (.log .tsv .pyc .bak dumps), and a receipt line the final report can paste: 'lab: promoted N, pruned M, carried K (paths)'. Consumer LAB-SWEEP-GATE calls it at the deadline.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_7 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 7u32, "2026-10-22T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:39 x: unpaused (Paused -> Planned, progress kept at 10): the user's 10-21 lab rule makes this the enforcement tool, so it is no longer optional; scheduling stays with the eoie team.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_8 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 8u32, "2026-10-22T01:46Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:46 x: two more verbs for the refined lab rule (LAB-SESSION-SWEEP note 2): eoie lab attic <repo> <ID> moves lab/<ID> to the repo's ignored attic (target/lab-attic/<day>/<ID>, or .cache/lab-attic for eoie), checking first that no live process command line names the folder; eoie lab restore <repo> <ID> [<day>] moves it back. Plus attic pruning past 14 days.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_9 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 9u32, "2026-10-22T01:52Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:52 x: withdraw note 8 (eoie lab attic / lab restore verbs): the attic lived under target/ or .cache/, which the user deletes to free disk, so it was drift (LAB-SESSION-SWEEP note 5). The audit's value now is finding which items hold lab folders, so they can be finished first.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_10 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 10u32, "2026-10-22T13:53Z", "eoie-lane", "09:53 eoie team: placement constraint found while picking this up. spec case 34 drives it as an eoie do statement ('lab audit lab against backlog'), so it parses in eoie_do_program, whose do_program.rs is at 988 lines. A new statement family cannot go there without a crate boundary first. Plan: G's do-verb family crate (eoie_do_verbs) is where statement families get classified; the audit itself becomes its own crate (eoie_do_lab_audit: walk lab dirs with lib file_system, look up items through the agile state crates, check non-portable paths) behind one export, and do_program gains only the word. Needs compiles, so it starts after GE2 is installed.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_11 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 11u32, "2026-10-23T14:10Z", "eoie", "10:10 eoie: progress corrected (15% Planned was stale). The do statement is installed and works on the current eoie.exe: eoie do . 'lab audit lab against <backlog>' on the eoie repo gives 14 labs, keep 14, orphan 0, done 0, stale 0, non-portable 18 (all in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22, the release-train lab copy of scratch scripts that name the scratch, regen-target and hook paths), exit 1, 2.96 s. Left: a top-level eoie lab audit verb (the 13:53 placement note: eoie_do_program is at 988 lines, so new words go behind a crate boundary after GE2), and x's LAB-SESSION-SWEEP needs (--since, carry marker, run-output extensions, paste-ready receipt).")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_12 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 12u32, "2026-10-24T07:11Z", "eoie", "03:11 audit of eoie's lab: 14 folders, all keep (their items are open), 0 orphan or stale. It fails only on 18 non-portable paths, all inside lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22: copies of session-scratch train scripts naming the scratchpad, spiral-bin and pack-next5d backup paths. Rule applied: a train night's lab folder drains only when every stage it holds has installed (GE2 onward is still in flight tonight), so it stays. The lasting fix is EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN's train-as-verbs, which turns these scripts into eoie commands with no session paths. Until then a non-portable path inside an archived night folder could count as a warning, not a failure.")
inl note_of_kit_lab_audit_13 () = Note ("KIT-LAB-AUDIT", 13u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
