inl note_of_kit_memory_model_14 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL", 14u32, "2026-11-09T16:20Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 15:2x rig groom: estimate -> 300 m = the sum of its open children (M1 120 + M2 120 + M3 60); the parent carries no work of its own, so it waits on its last child and leaves the ready list.")
inl kit_memory_verbs () = Task ("KIT-MEMORY-VERBS", "One-call verbs: eoie memory recall <query|ids> [--client <c>] (relevant memories for this task, ranked, with related links), eoie memory save <kind> <slug> <description> <body> (type-checked: feedback needs Why/How), eoie memory edit/forget, eoie memory check (subsumes EOIE-MEMORY-LINKS: backlog IDs, dangling links, Done items). Each verb ~20 ms native vs reading 56 files; Spiral test blocks", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", "kit,memory", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_memory_verbs () = Planning ("KIT-MEMORY-VERBS", Minutes 105u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kit_memory_adapters () = Task ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", "Client adapters (HKT-style interface, one instance per client): Claude (projects/*/memory md + MEMORY.md), Zed (AGENTS.md rules; threads db read-only), Codex (AGENTS.md), OpenCode (AGENTS.md/config; db read on a copy, never credential/account tables), Antigravity (.gemini/antigravity brain/annotations: format to study first), Grok (to find). Import (absorb once) and export (render each client's bootstrap or projection). No secrets ever enter the store (x-api-credentials stays a path reference)", Story, P2, D6, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,memory,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_memory_adapters () = Planning ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", Minutes 540u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_1 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 1u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "14:10 Claude Code items (measured): %USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\projects\\C--home-git\\memory = 56 item files + MEMORY.md; no other project dir has memory. Bytes: LF, no BOM, one final LF, no trailing spaces, 11 files non-ASCII (UTF-8), 783..11,214 B (sum 113,785; largest spiral-macro-gotchas). Frontmatter, fixed key order: name, description, metadata: {node_type: memory, type, originSessionId: uuid, modified: ISO-8601 ms Z} in 55 files (7 lines); inner-jev-autonomy has metadata: {type} only (4 lines). Then one blank line, then body. name equals filename stem in all 56. description max 206 chars: 48 YAML double-quoted (4 with backslash-escaped quotes), 8 plain (agent-sync-daily plain with raw Windows backslashes): keep a quote-style tag, never re-derive. Kinds: feedback 44, project 8, reference 4, user 0. All 52 feedback/project bodies hold **Why:** and **How to apply:** (51 line-initial, 1 inline); the 4 references hold neither. So the GADT why/how fields are sound, but bodies have prose around them: store body as ordered segments (text | why | how) so render is byte-exact. Links: 111 [[slug]] in 53 files, 39 distinct targets, 2 dangling: delete-dangling-freely (from dangling-check-by-stem) and corpus-check-before-packs (from kino-copy-lib-resolution; that is the MEMORY.md title of lib-smoke-before-syntax.md, a renamed slug: check should suggest it).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_2 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 2u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Claude index and loading: MEMORY.md = 56 lines + final LF, 9,151 B, no heading/frontmatter; every line is: - [Title](file.md) — hook (U+2014 em dash, single spaces), max 245 chars; all 56 items indexed, none missing. Title is free text, not the slug (Agent count -> max-three-agents.md, Corpus check before packs -> lib-smoke-before-syntax.md): a separate field, and index order is a list. Loading: the harness injects MEMORY.md into every session (seen verbatim in this agent's own context; documented cap first 200 lines), item files are read on demand; the agent writes all of it with file tools. Instructions: no ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, no ~/.claude/rules, no CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md at C:\\home\\git or any repo root; only in-repo docs (spiral/apps/compiler/AGENTS.md 931 B, its tmp/AGENTS.md 68,825 B) and upstream zed (.rules 12,651 B; CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md are 6-byte symlink-placeholder files reading .rules). In-repo AGENTS.md already sync through git: out of scope for import. ~/.claude/settings.json has no memory keys. Bootstrap: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (global, always on), 2-3 lines: memory lives in eoie, read the eoie memory tutorial first, record memories with eoie, not in this folder; and MEMORY.md shrunk to one pointer line so auto-memory stops growing a parallel store. Caution: Grok (compat.claude) and OpenCode (docs: fallback when no global AGENTS.md) also read ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, so keep that bootstrap client-neutral.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_3 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 3u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Zed: global rules = %APPDATA%\\Zed\\AGENTS.md (paths::agents_file = config_dir/AGENTS.md, zed/crates/paths/src/paths.rs:319), 908 B LF markdown, no frontmatter, one H2 section: Commit message (the customized built-in commit prompt, moved there by prompt_store/rules_to_skills_migration.rs, which appends Default Rules under ## title H2s and turns non-default Rules into ~/.agents/skills/slug/SKILL.md). Loaded into the native agent system prompt of every conversation (always on); no size cap found in crates/agent. Project rules: only the FIRST match of RULES_FILE_NAMES at a worktree root (.rules, .cursorrules, .windsurfrules, .clinerules, .github/copilot-instructions.md, AGENT.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md; prompts.rs:22). settings.json (2,575 B JSONC, // header) has no rules or profiles fields; its agent block is model/permissions/dock only: adapter never touches it. Legacy Rules LMDB AppData/Local/Zed/prompts/prompts-library-db.0.mdb is kept by the migration (not memory). ~/.agents absent. threads.db (copy, mode=ro, query_only): one table threads(id TEXT PK, summary, updated_at, data_type, data BLOB, parent_id, folder_paths, folder_paths_order, created_at), 8 rows, all zstd = transcripts. Zed has no memory store. Bootstrap: upsert an H2 section ## Memory with one pointer line into the global AGENTS.md; the adapter is a section-preserving edit keyed by H2 title so the Commit message section stays byte-identical.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_4 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 4u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "OpenCode: ~/.config/opencode holds only cli.json (v2 schema, UI prefs) and service.json. PRIVACY: service.json is a plaintext service password: never read or import it (deny by name). No opencode.json(c), no global AGENTS.md, no .opencode dir at C:\\home\\git. opencode.db (db+wal+shm copied; sqlite_master and non-sensitive schemas only): account, account_state, control_account, credential (never read), event, event_sequence, instruction_blob(hash PK, value), instruction_entry(session_id, key, value, removed, time_created, time_updated; PK session_id+key), instruction_state(session_id PK, epoch_start, through_seq, initial_values JSON, current_values JSON), kv, migration, permission, project, project_directory, session_inbox, session_message, session_pending, session_v2, workspace, worktree. instruction_* is a per-session content-addressed snapshot of system-prompt parts: the one state row maps core/codemode, core/skill-guidance, core/date, core/environment to 64-hex hashes into instruction_blob (5 blobs, 17..11,778 B); instruction_entry is empty. No memory feature: nothing to import. Loading (OpenCode docs, not verified on this v2 build): ~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md plus project AGENTS.md found walking up from cwd, falling back to ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md when no global file exists, plus opencode.json instructions globs; all always on. Bootstrap: create ~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md with the eoie pointer (this also stops the CLAUDE.md fallback double-load).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_5 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 5u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Antigravity (.gemini\\antigravity; antigravity-ide is a same-shape twin, plus antigravity-backup): no memory/knowledge store and no user rules on this machine. brain/conversation-uuid/ is per-conversation working state, not memory: .system_generated/{logs/transcript*.jsonl, messages/uuid.json, steps/n/*.txt tool outputs, tasks/*.log}, .user_uploaded/, scratch/ = conversation content, never import. annotations/uuid.pbtxt is protobuf text (title, last_user_view_time {seconds nanos}); antigravity_state.pbtxt holds onboarding/migration enums and installation_uuid; conversations/uuid.db and conversation_summaries.db are SQLite; agyhub_summaries_proto.pb binary. Rules per the bundled builtin/skills/agy-customizations docs: GEMINI.md and AGENTS.md (no frontmatter, always on) walked up from cwd or edited file to repo root; .agents/rules/*.md with frontmatter trigger: always_on or model_decision; workspace roots .agents/ .agent/ _agents/ _agent/; global ~/.gemini/config/ (here only config.json userSettings, projects/uuid.json, empty plugins and sidecars; no rule file; ~/.gemini/GEMINI.md absent). Limits: 24,000 B per rule file after @[label](path) include expansion, truncated on a line boundary; 20,000-token always-on rules budget, overflow demoted to path pointers. Bootstrap: one global rule under ~/.gemini/config/ (confirm the exact filename in the Customizations UI before the first write) with the eoie pointer. PRIVACY: ~/.gemini/oauth_creds.json and google_accounts.json: exclude.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_6 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 6u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Codex (.codex): config.toml (283 B: approval/sandbox/model, projects c:\\home\\git trust, windows sandbox) has no instruction keys; no ~/.codex/AGENTS.md or AGENTS.override.md; rules/default.rules is exec-policy Starlark prefix_rule(pattern=[...], decision=...) = command permissions, not memory. A memory feature exists but is empty: memories_1.sqlite (copy) has stage1_outputs(thread_id PK, source_updated_at, raw_memory, rollout_summary, rollout_slug, generated_at, usage_count, last_usage, selected_for_phase2, selected_for_phase2_source_updated_at) 0 rows, jobs 0, consolidation_progress 1, _sqlx_migrations 2; no ~/.codex/memories dir (the phase-2 output folder). skills/ holds only .system vendor skills. Loading (Codex docs): ~/.codex/AGENTS.md (AGENTS.override.md wins) plus AGENTS.md from git root down to cwd, always on, combined cap project_doc_max_bytes (default 32 KiB). Import: nothing today; when memories appear, stage1 raw_memory rows are per-thread drafts and the memories folder is the curated output (read that, never the db). Bootstrap: ~/.codex/AGENTS.md with the eoie pointer. PRIVACY: auth.json, .sandbox-secrets/, history.jsonl, sessions/: exclude.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_7 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 7u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Grok (.grok) HAS a memory store, memory-v2 (no memory key in config.toml: on via env or managed setting). Per scope (global/, workspaces/git-437d9324/): topics/*.md curated (11 workspace topics 722..16,945 B, 0 global; LF, no frontmatter: # Title, one-line summary, ## sections, - bullets); observations/_inbox/*.md pending (19; YAML frontmatter schema_version: 2, type, topic_hint, keywords, aliases, session_id, from_turn, through_turn, extraction_model, prompt_version, created_at epoch, job_id, observation_ordinal); archive/dream_hex/ consumed observations named session__tFROM-TO__nK.md (30-day retention); MEMORY.md generated, never write it; index.sqlite and memory_state.sqlite: leave alone. Loading (docs/user-guide/13-memory.md): both MEMORY.md indexes injected once per session, 8 KiB per scope; topics read on demand; capture after each turn into the inbox; /dream or auto-dream folds into topics; the model may edit topics/ and _inbox/ with file tools. Rules (12-project-rules.md, always on): ~/.grok/rules/*.md (absent), ~/.claude/rules and ~/.claude/CLAUDE*.md by compat.claude, [paths] extra_rule_dirs, then Agents.md, Claude.md, CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE.local.md, AGENT.md, AGENTS.md from repo root to cwd (cwd only outside git; needs folder trust). Import: topics as a topic kind (title, summary, sections), observations as an observation kind with provenance. Bootstrap: ~/.grok/rules/eoie-memory.md, and either set memory_v2.enabled = false or keep one global topic whose body is the eoie pointer.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_8 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 8u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Adapter interface proposal: a client is a record over a type-level carrier f (result with a per-client error union, later an io effect): import : root -> f (list stored); render : list stored -> f (list {path; text}); bootstrap : tutorial_ref -> f (list {path; edit}) with union edit = Replace text | UpsertSection {heading; text} | AppendLine text, so foreign content in Zed/Codex/Antigravity AGENTS.md files survives. stored = Stored :: forall k. memory k -> stored, and beside the kind GADT a source layout record, not part of the kind: {client; scope = Global | Workspace slug; path; quote = Plain | Double; meta = {node_type option; origin_session option; modified option}; body = list segment}. Renderers derive frontmatter from layout so bytes round-trip; normalization is a separate explicit verb. Kinds beyond user/feedback/project/reference: topic (Grok topics), observation (Grok inbox, with session/turn provenance), rule (an H2 section of an AGENTS.md). Indexes are derived: Claude MEMORY.md = ordered list of {title; file; hook}; Grok MEMORY.md is never rendered. Deny-list is a type: import walks only an allow-list of paths per client (Claude memory dir, Zed AGENTS.md, Grok topics and _inbox, Codex memories dir, OpenCode and Antigravity rule files); everything else is unrepresentable rather than filtered.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_9 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 9u32, "2026-10-17T18:12Z", "memory-formats", "Round-trip test blocks: (1) 56 Claude items render byte-identical; (2) MEMORY.md byte-identical, em dash and order kept; (3) inner-jev-autonomy keeps its 4-line frontmatter (no node_type/session/modified); (4) double-quoted descriptions with escaped quotes and the plain one with raw backslashes keep their quoting; (5) the 11 non-ASCII files keep UTF-8; (6) the one inline How to apply body survives; (7) a feedback without why fails to typecheck (negative), references without Why/How typecheck; (8) links: 111 parsed, 39 targets, exactly 2 dangling reported, corpus-check-before-packs gets lib-smoke-before-syntax suggested via its index title; (9) Zed AGENTS.md: UpsertSection Memory twice is idempotent and Commit message stays byte-identical; (10) the 11 Grok topics and 19 observations re-render byte-identical; (11) import, render, import is a fixed point; (12) an allow-list test: a tree seeded with service.json, auth.json, .credentials.json, oauth_creds.json yields zero items. Privacy flags: OpenCode service.json plaintext password; .claude/.credentials.json; .codex/auth.json and .sandbox-secrets; .grok/auth.json; .gemini/oauth_creds.json and google_accounts.json; OpenCode credential/account tables; Antigravity brain/ and every threads/sessions store are transcripts; Grok observations carry session ids and the agent-sync topic a scheduler id; Claude items carry originSessionId (fine in a private repo, strip before anything public); x-api-credentials stays a path pointer.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_10 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS", 10u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 720m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D6 at 0%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
