inl note_of_kit_lease_6 () = Note ("KIT-LEASE", 6u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_lease_7 () = Note ("KIT-LEASE", 7u32, "2026-11-06T10:52Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 06:5x kit, user ask (we are not on LLM browser tabs anymore; the time-boxed lease should not be on by default): DEFAULT FLIPPED in the tree (unstaged, proven by the next train). agile_lease_terms policy_name falls back to renewing, and agile_state_runtime_policy_domain reads only the exact word bounded as Bounded; anything else, including unset, is Renewing. Tests that exercise the blocking path (notes_cli strict and from_title, contracts_entry cli_driver x4) now set KIT_LEASE_POLICY=bounded explicitly instead of removing it. CONFIG NOW for the installed binaries: lease-policy file = renewing on the box (APPDATA kit), the wifi node (APPDATA kit, user alias) and europa (~/.config/kit); the box user env already had KIT_LEASE_POLICY=renewing. Why it mattered: under bounded an expired lease made every agile write fail with lease authority blocked mutating effect, in any process without the user env (SYSTEM tasks, node, europa). Bounded stays available as an opt-in time box.")
inl note_of_kit_lease_8 () = Note ("KIT-LEASE", 8u32, "2026-11-06T11:30Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-LEASE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_lease_9 () = Note ("KIT-LEASE", 9u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries LEASE-1 (New-turn rollover); LEASE-2 (Adopt an original clock); LEASE-3 (One lease authority); LEASE-4 (Wrap-safe closeout effect); LEASE-5 (Configurable budgets); LEASE-6 (A lease for any workspace); LEASE-8 (Pause on interruption); AGILE-6 (Lease timing aids). Why: 10-24 note #3 maps LEASE-1,2,3,5,6,8; title also names the WRAP write class (LEASE-4) and rollover; agile lease prints the lease (AGILE-6)")
inl note_of_kit_lease_10 () = Note ("KIT-LEASE", 10u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. LEASE-1 · New-turn rollover · P0 · ssam, brz · Open / An expired or wrapping lease inherited from a previous turn or a rehydrated bundle blocked writing its own successor (deadlock). Accept a host-supplied turn nonce that archives the predecessor and creates exactly one successor, is allowed while wrapping, and can never extend the same turn. Rehydrated predecessor leases must be frozen as history, not authority. When the user explicitly authorizes it, `lease-reset --explicit-user-override` records the old lease, the reason and the new deadline instead of a hand edit of `prompt.spi`. || LEASE-2 · Adopt an original clock · P1 · node, ge2e, brz, scp · Open / `agile begin --at <epoch>` / adopt-clock / recover-existing, so recovery inherits the budget already consumed instead of starting a fresh window, plus a durable start receipt that can be written before any tool runs. `agile begin` is not idempotent today (a second call restarts the deadline); add `begin-if-needed` or one immutable lease per prompt. Record unknown provenance when no clock survived. || LEASE-3 · One lease authority · P1 · sbin, ssam, ge2e, erp · Open / Status and mutation admission must share one lease token, root and monotonic clock (they disagreed near the guard), and lease writes must be monotonic (a timed-out capture once restored an older `prompt.spi` snapshot and made a fresh lease look expired). Bind every lease sidecar to the current root and refresh it on begin and rehydrate; never write runtime lease text into product files (it made sealed bundles stale). Name the lease root in diagnostics. || LEASE-4 · Wrap-safe closeout effect · P0 · sbin, ssam, ge2e, ota, node · Open / Once `should_wrap=1`, every write is blocked, including the state, ratings, handoff, evidence and checkpoint updates that closeout must perform. Add a closeout effect class: whitelisted state/report files, receipt renames and removals, checkpoint compression, bundle and verify, hash-receipted, unable to touch source. Classify read, validate and run separately from semantic mutation (formatting-only changes are not semantic work), and allow a post-closure note. || LEASE-5 · Configurable budgets · P1 · ota, ssam, ge2e, scp · Partial / Per-lease work/wrap/hard budgets (`--work-seconds`, `--guard-seconds`, `--deadline`, absolute start), separate reporting of each cutoff, and a warning when a release is attempted far before the useful-work budget. Sessions of 17 to 20 minutes still got an 85-minute lease. *Now:* `agile begin <root> <title>` fixes 75 + 10 minutes. || LEASE-6 · A lease for any workspace · P0 · node, erp, auth, scp, ota · Partial / `agile begin` rolled back on Rust-only and F#-first roots because it requires `package.spiproj`, `prompt.spi` and `agile.spi`. Separate a language-independent `lease begin/status/end` from the agile backend; agile consumes it. Allow a lease on an empty root during recovery, before rehydrate. *Now:* `agile init` scaffolds a backlog root. || LEASE-8 · Pause on interruption · P2 · ge2e · Open / The lease kept running while the user or the chat context was away, so continuations often resumed already inside the guard. Offer `agile pause/resume`, or a mode that counts active tool time with a separate wall-clock cap. || AGILE-6 · Lease timing aids · P2 · ssam · Open / `lease checkpoint` reporting elapsed time, freeze deadline and the next safe checkpoint, in one receipt.")
inl note_of_kit_lease_11 () = Note ("KIT-LEASE", 11u32, "2026-11-09T19:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, TIMING CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_agile_lease_time/lease.spi (pure, HostFree) covering four of the bundle findings at once. clock RunningSince | PausedAt, so ACTIVE time accrues only while running (LEASE-8 pause on interruption) under a separate wall-clock cap; lease_phase Working | Wrapping (active + wrap reserve reaches the budget) | Frozen (budget spent OR wall cap hit, even while paused); write_class WorkWrite | CloseoutWrite with allowed = closeout writes pass in EVERY phase, so closeout is never blocked (the WRAP write class), work writes only while Working; on_turn rolls the lease over when the user turn id changes (the stale lease that survived into the next turn 5+ times); checkpoint_of gives the AGILE-6 receipt: active ms, ms until wrap, ms until freeze, phase. Test: the three phases, closeout always allowed, work blocked at wrap, paused time not counted, the wall cap freezing a paused lease, resume, the checkpoint numbers, rollover. Ratchet clean. NEXT: agile begin/lease read and write this state (one time-box authority) and lease checkpoint prints the receipt.")
