inl note_of_kit_authority_audit_3 () = Note ("KIT-AUTHORITY-AUDIT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:57Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, MODEL BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_authority_audit/audit.spi (pure, HostFree). DoD: kit authority audit <rows> names every read of a fact from a source that is neither its owner nor a fresh mirror, plus facts read with no declared owner; Spiral test block. TYPEFEATURES: source_role Owns | Mirrors max-age-minutes; authority_finding WrongAuthority (site, fact, source, owner) | StaleMirror (site, fact, age, limit) | NoOwnerDeclared (site, fact). audit table readings judges each reading: owner passes, a mirror passes only within its age limit (memory status-files-need-age), any other source is WrongAuthority naming the real owner, and a fact with no Owns row is NoOwnerDeclared. Test rows are today's real cases: a remote job's exit is owned by the node's exit file, the box's placed-exit is a 30-minute mirror (KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE), reading the bare placement record is WrongAuthority (the stuck state=placed bug); a claim holder read from the last note author instead of claims state (the help-pool overlap of 11-09) is WrongAuthority; a train verdict read from a chat summary has no owner. Ratchet clean. NEXT STEP: the authority rows as a state file (fact, source, role) and the readings from a site census (the verbs that read each fact), then the one-call verb; milestone sizing replaces the provisional 240m once rows exist.")
inl note_of_kit_authority_audit_4 () = Note ("KIT-AUTHORITY-AUDIT", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_authority_audit_5 () = Note ("KIT-AUTHORITY-AUDIT", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:4x rig, THE AUTHORITY TABLE AS TYPED DATA (unstaged, inside src/rig_authority_audit/audit.spi): rather than a parsed rows file (which would be a fifth copy of the quote-split reader, see LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS), kit_authorities () is Spiral data: job-exit owned by the job exit file; remote-job-exit owned by the node exit file, mirrored by the box placed-exit for 30 min; job-liveness by the heartbeat file; claim-holder by claims state; item-wait by waits state, mirrored by the gate ready cache for 60 min; train-verdict by the node verdict files, mirrored by the box coordinator log for 15 min; installed-kit by the installed binary hash. kit_readings_11_09 () records today's real reads. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (audit module 2/2): three findings, the placed-forever job-list read (WrongAuthority, owner node-exit-file), the stop gate's ready list cached for 245 min (StaleMirror over 60), and the rename sweep reading source as if it were the installed binary (WrongAuthority); the fixed settle read, a fresh coordinator log and the claims read pass. NEXT: a site census that finds the readings in code (each verb's reads, tagged with fact and source), then the one-call verb; both TRAIN44 work.")
