inl note_of_kit_resume_compiler_11 () = Note ("KIT-RESUME-COMPILER", 11u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries CKPT-4 (Restart baton and resume summary); AGILE-4 (Handoff that degrades). Why: 10-24 note #6; kit resume <backlog-root> ships, item open at 40%")
inl note_of_kit_resume_compiler_12 () = Note ("KIT-RESUME-COMPILER", 12u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. CKPT-4 · Restart baton and resume summary · P1 · brz, sbin, ge2e · Partial / Write a baton automatically on every mutation and checkpoint (changed files with hashes, next commands, lease state), and offer one bounded command that reports the active lease, the newest checkpoint, files mutated since it, the newest receipts, toolchain identity and contradictions between sidecars and typed state, before new work opens. *Now:* `proxy restart-baton`, `incident-recovery snapshot|restore` and `agile handoff` exist; neither the automatic baton nor the summary does. || AGILE-4 · Handoff that degrades · P1 · ssam, brz, ge2e · Open / When `handoff.spi` is absent or partial, derive the handoff from typed state and receipts and say which field or section is missing, instead of failing the whole projection.")
inl note_of_kit_resume_compiler_13 () = Note ("KIT-RESUME-COMPILER", 13u32, "2026-11-09T19:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, AGILE-4 CORE BUILT (\"handoff that degrades\"; unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_handoff_degrade/degrade.spi (pure, HostFree; the legacy handoff_sections_projection_* units are string loops, untouched). handoff_part ActiveWork | OpenWaits | Evidence | NextSteps; provenance FromHandoff body | DerivedFromState text | MissingPart reason; project handoff typed_state takes option (list handoff_row) (None = handoff.spi absent) and, PER PART, uses the handoff row, else derives from typed state (Active items, wait rows, receipts), else names the gap with its reason, so the projection never fails whole; NextSteps is never derived (it lives only in the handoff); a blank row counts as missing; repeated titles are reported with the first kept (the legacy duplicate case). missing_titles lists the gaps for the \"say which section is missing\" line. Test: absent handoff (2 derived, 2 named gaps), partial handoff with a blank and a repeated title. Ratchet clean. NEXT: the resume verb reads handoff.spi + backlog state + receipts into these inputs and prints the projection with its provenance tags.")
