inl x_on_near () = Task ("X-ON-NEAR", "X rewritten as NEAR contracts with the sim as spec, driver and oracle (deferred, user 2026-10-18: too much for now): contract = SocialDB-style per-account storage (social.near) + NEP-145 storage deposits, Farcaster-style add/remove merge rules (remove wins, later timestamp wins, hash tie-break) as Spiral types; xc gains a NEAR site (free view reads over RPC, signed writes); feeds off chain in an indexer tested with the sim's reorder/duplicate faults, or on chain as paged views (NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW); copy designs not code (check licenses). Does not need SIM-IN-SPIRAL: the Elixir sim already emits the event stream (XSIM-EVENT-STREAM). Folds in X-NEAR-PROVENANCE", Epic, P4, D8, 0u32, Paused, "XSIM-EVENT-STREAM,NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS,NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW,NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES,X-FEDERATION-BRIDGES", "microblog,near,sim,social,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_on_near () = Planning ("X-ON-NEAR", Minutes 480u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_on_near_1 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 1u32, "2026-10-18T17:09Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:09 direction (user): iterate until feature parity with X while dogfooding everything (xc, sim, Cells, the compiler), keep a running list of NEAR gotchas as they surface, and stay Mastodon and Bluesky compatible (X-FEDERATION-BRIDGES), until a killer app arrives. Waits for the full machine: today CPU and memory go to spiral compiler maintenance, and the sandbox (near-workspaces/neard) needs WSL (NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE: WSL 3 bounded jobs, memory=6GB, wsl --shutdown after). Only NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS and XSIM-EVENT-STREAM run without WSL")
inl note_of_x_on_near_2 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 2u32, "2026-10-18T17:09Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:09 technical design (from the 2026-10-18 review): sim reuse = spec (typed events post/reply/quote/edit-as-revision/delete/like/unlike, idempotent per event, causal buffering, commute across orders), driver (xsim.world scenario -> contract calls) and oracle (same expected state as the X stub); on NEAR one contract's receipts run in one order and final blocks never roll back, so delivery faults move to the indexer/reader side. Prior art: social.near SocialDB (per-account key-value store, poster pays storage), NEP-145 storage_deposit/withdraw/unregister, Farcaster message sets (CastAdd/Remove, ReactionAdd/Remove, LinkAdd/Remove; remove wins, later timestamp wins, hash tie-break), AT Protocol (signed per-user repos, relays, app views). Approximate costs: storage ~1 NEAR per 100 KB (1,000 posts at ~400 B lock ~4 NEAR, refunded on delete), a simple write ~5 Tgas ~0.0005 NEAR, 300 Tgas ceiling per call. Shape: shared Spiral domain crates under the 1,000-line gate linked into one cdylib; xc reads/writes GADTs gain a NEAR site (view calls over RPC, signed function calls, key in a secrets env file). Phases: 1 domain types + merge-rule commutation tests, 2 contract (SocialDB layout + NEP-145), 3 native replay of sim scenarios in near-sdk's mock, 4 xc NEAR site, 5 feeds (NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW or an off-chain indexer tested with the sim's reorder/duplicate faults), 6 sandbox in CI Linux")
inl note_of_x_on_near_3 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 3u32, "2026-10-21T01:45Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 21:45 x-lane backlog refactor: Planned -> Paused to match the user's 2026-10-18 deferral, so it leaves the ready queue of agile next; back to Planned when the user starts NEAR work")
inl note_of_x_on_near_4 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 4u32, "2026-10-30T01:58Z", "x", "2026-10-30T02:00Z groom: filled the missing fields. assignee=agent; estimate=480 m for this epic's own integration only (like X-DONE, children carry their own estimates). Open children: NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS Active 40% (75 m), NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW Paused (240 m), NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES Active 10% (660 m), X-FEDERATION-BRIDGES Paused (720 m); XSIM-EVENT-STREAM Done. Stays Paused at P4 until those land.")
inl note_of_x_on_near_5 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 5u32, "2026-10-31T23:03Z", "x", "2026-10-31 19:03 x groom: Paused -> Planned at P4. 'Paused until children land' is dep gating, which agile next already does.")
inl note_of_x_on_near_6 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 6u32, "2026-11-01T06:37Z", "x", "2026-11-01 02:37 x: REVERTED my 10-31 19:03 groom move (Planned -> Paused again). I read only the last note and missed the user's deferral: X-ON-NEAR's title and n4 (10-20) record 'deferred, user 2026-10-18: too much for now', with the resume condition 'back to Planned when the user starts NEAR work'. This item is part of X-ON-NEAR (its child, fold-in or federation half), so it shares that reason and resume. The user's 11-01 00:2x remark that Cells will LATER live in NEAR contracts with zkVM receipts is direction, not a start. Lesson recorded: groom re-decisions read ALL notes and the title, not only the last note.")
inl note_of_x_on_near_7 () = Note ("X-ON-NEAR", 7u32, "2026-11-04T01:14Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:14 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (x's corner): stays Paused. Reason: the user's 10-18 deferral of NEAR work ('too much for now'). Resume condition: the user starts NEAR work. Owner x. The generic paged merge from this family now lives outside NEAR (X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND feed_merge, landed today).")
