inl xsim_event_stream () = Task ("XSIM-EVENT-STREAM", "Promote the sim's --save delivery logs to a documented, versioned event stream (post/reply/edit/delete/like/unlike with users, ids and revision sources, key-sorted JSON lines) plus a drift-guarded fixture in x, so any implementation replays the same scenario and compares with the sim's expected state: the NEAR contract mock, the Spiral sim port, other clients", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "x,sim,fixtures", "current", "current")
inl near_mocked_unit_tests () = Task ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", "Run NEAR contract logic natively on Windows through near-sdk's unit-testing mock (testing_env!, VMContextBuilder, env::used_gas) as Spiral test blocks, starting with dice and chat (mirror in alphabet): the fast loop needs neither the sandbox nor WSL, measures gas per method, and the sandbox runs stay on CI Linux (NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE)", Story, P1, D3, 85u32, Active, "", "near,dice,polyglot,testing,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_near_mocked_unit_tests () = Planning ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", Minutes 75u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_1 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 1u32, "2026-10-19T12:53Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:53 helper-lane lap 1: mapped the path for test blocks: both contracts pin near-sdk =5.11.0 (dice/contract and polyglot/apps/chat/contract Cargo.toml, borsh 1.5, indexmap =2.11.4), and near-sdk's mock (testing_env!, VMContextBuilder) needs the unit-testing feature. Cells passes ///> rust -d deps as --deps to the spiral CLI, whose cargo writer (apps/spiral/spiral.spi:309 and :912) turns name[feat] into name={version='*',features=[...]} and name=ver into a pinned version, but a token cannot carry both, so -d near-sdk[unit-testing] would resolve the newest near-sdk instead of the contracts' 5.11.0. Smallest unblock: accept name=version[features] in builders.ex parse_dep (Cells) and in spiral.spi's dep writer, then a first dice test block ///> rust -d near-sdk=5.11.0[unit-testing] -d borsh=1.5 calling roll_within_bounds under testing_env!.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_2 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 2u32, "2026-10-19T13:36Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:36 helper-lane lap 2: correction of lap 1 (no code change needed): Cells builders.ex dep_arg passes a -d token through raw when its version part starts with an opening brace or the token holds a quote, and apps/spiral/spiral.spi's cargo writer copies any token containing = verbatim into [dependencies] (lines 303-309). TOML accepts single-quoted literal strings, so a pinned crate with features is already expressible as one token without spaces: ///> rust -d near-sdk={version='=5.11.0',features=['unit-testing']} -d borsh=1.5, which becomes near-sdk={version='=5.11.0',features=['unit-testing']} in the generated Cargo.toml. The first dice mock test block can therefore be written today; what remains is the test itself (testing_env! with VMContextBuilder around roll_within_bounds) and its first cargo build of near-sdk, which is heavy.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_3 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 3u32, "2026-10-19T15:20Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:20 helper-lane lap 3: picked the first target by reading dice_contract.spi: roll_within_bounds is pure and already has two runnable test blocks, while new, contribute_seed and generate_random_number read near.random_seed, block_timestamp, signer_account_id and predecessor_account_id (lines 97-113), so generate_random_number is the first that needs a mocked context. Wrote it as lab/NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS/mocked_test_block.spi: ///> rust -c -d near-sdk={version='=5.11.0',features=['unit-testing']} -d near-token, a mocked () that calls near_sdk::testing_env with VMContextBuilder (random_seed [7u8; 32], a fixed block_timestamp; the macro bang written as a doubled bang inside the single-quoted macro), then two draws under the same context must be equal and positive. The explicit near-sdk token takes precedence, since apps/spiral adds near-sdk=5.11.0 only when no near-sdk dep is given (spiral.spi 293-301). run.ps1 appends the block to dice/contract/dice_contract.spi, runs only that test through Cells, and restores the file either way. HEAVY QUEUE (first near-sdk unit-testing build, about 10 min).")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_4 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-10-19T22:18Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:18 helper-lane lap 6: ran the queued row (lab/NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS/run.ps1; dice_contract.spi patched temporarily and restored, git status clean). The mocked test never compiled, because dice's contract itself no longer type-checks on the current tree: dice_contract.spi:117:12, [ ... ] |> am'.to_vec, Unification failure, Got array (vec u8) -> vec (vec u8), Expected array_base _ -> vec _. Since the core v1 switch, an array literal is the nominal array el, and lib am'.to_vec still takes array_base. Reported to main as a core-switch consumer breakage. It is blocked until dice (and its alphabet mirror) or lib am' is adapted.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_5 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-10-19T22:31Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:31 helper-lane: after main fixed the three am'.to_vec sites in dice_contract.spi, I reran with the process compiler (lab/NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS/contract-run.ps1, contract-gate-20261019-1829.log). All 7 contract tests fail at rust -c with the same type error, now in the mounted dice package: dice/lib/dice.spi 373-375, where main ;[] |> ignore in the Rust/Python/TypeScript arms fails with Got array _, Expected array_base string. It is the same core v1 array-literal migration, so it is not the contract build. The mocked test fails for the same reason. Reported to main; rerun after dice.spi is adapted.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_6 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-10-19T23:09Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 19:09 helper-lane: progress after main's dice migration. The contract gate passes 7 of 7 (contract-gate-20261019-1841.log). Three findings for the mocked test (lab/NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS/mocked_test_block.spi): (1) Cells' builder tokenizer strips quotes, so the crate spec must be quoted whole (-d near-sdk with its version and unit-testing feature inside double quotes). Done, and spiral rust now gets the exact spec. (2) As a contract (rust -c, wasm32), near_sdk::testing_env does not exist (E0433), as near-sdk gates its unit-testing helpers off wasm, so mocked tests need a native rust target. Done, the ///> line is now rust without -c. (3) The native path's toolchain is rustc 1.88.0-nightly, and near-sys 0.2.14 (pulled by near-sdk 5.11.0) requires rustc 1.93, so cargo refuses. Blocked on main's toolchain pack (rustup update), not on code. dice_contract.spi is restored after each run.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_7 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-10-19T23:11Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 19:11 helper-lane: unblock condition (per main): the rustc used by the native Cells/spiral rust path must itself go to 1.93 or later. That is the pinned 1.88.0-nightly toolchain, and a rustup self-update does not move it. Alternatively, pin near-sys below 0.2.14 in the test's -d specs (for example -d near-sys with a version below 0.2.14 next to near-sdk), if near-sdk 5.11.0 accepts that range. The toolchain pack moved to 2026-10-20.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_8 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 8u32, "2026-10-19T23:58Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 19:58 helper-lane: the near-sys pin route is closed. With -d near-sys pinned to =0.2.13 (run-20261019-1942.log), cargo reports near-sys 0.2.13 also requires rustc 1.93, so only bumping the native toolchain unblocks the test. The test block keeps the pin out of the next run (to be removed from mocked_test_block.spi). dice_contract.spi was restored by the run.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_9 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 9u32, "2026-10-22T05:37Z", "main", "01:36 main: lab run outputs moved to the run cache, per the lab rule that run outputs never sit in lab: 10 file(s) (logs, notebooks, diffs, metrics/gate/timing TSVs) are now under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runs\\lab-outputs\\NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS\\ at the same relative paths, sha256 checked. Scripts and probes stay in lab/NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS until the item lands.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_10 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 10u32, "2026-10-22T08:09Z", "main", "04:09 main: the 10-19 blocker is gone. dice/contract/dice_contract.spi type-checks and compiles to Rust on today's installed compiler (180 KB, exit 0; compiled into TEMP, and dice's tracked dice_contract.rs is unchanged). The 117:12 array vs array_base error was fixed in dice by the '|> am'.base' after the ;[ ... ] literal (commit 4218032, 10-19). This item's 'Blocked' reason (the contract not type-checking) no longer holds; its runners (contract-run.ps1, run.ps1, now writing into the run cache) can rerun when a Cells window is free.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_11 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 11u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 4 11:39 (subagent): blocked: run.ps1 (first near-sdk unit-testing build) queued -> next: read the mocked test result | lap 5 12:19 (subagent): run.ps1 queued -> next: read the mocked test | lap 7 19:09 (subagent): contract gate 7/7; mocked test fixed twice (quoting, native target), now blocked on native rustc 1.88 < near-sys 1.93 -> next: after the toolchain pack, rerun run.ps1")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_12 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 12u32, "2026-10-29T21:54Z", "main", "10-29 17:5x main: PROVISIONAL estimate 75m by the D-base rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS n2: base(D3) x (1 - 40%), floored at 30, rounded up to 15). A milestone-based sizing pass (estimates-from-rules) replaces it.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_13 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 13u32, "2026-10-31T03:21Z", "main", "10-30 23:21 main: lab/NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS is ARCHIVED (user, 10-30 22:5x: the lab dir didn't work and drifted; drafts don't live outside the repo). Archive 20261030-232045 under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive. Restore this folder with: pwsh i574n.github/scripts/scratch-archive.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab -Restore '%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045\\manifest.tsv' -Only 'NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS\\*' -RestoreTo C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab. Resume this item's work in its real place in the repo, not in lab.")
