inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_17 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 17u32, "2026-11-06T14:25Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:5x RESTORED in place (dice, unstaged): the archived lab block (20261030-232045, mocked_test_block.spi) is now the last cell of dice/contract/dice_contract.spi, ported to edition-3 locals and !+ booleans: ///> rust -d near-sdk 5.11.0 with unit-testing -d near-token; test generate_random_number_is_deterministic_under_a_mocked_context builds a VMContextBuilder context (random_seed [7; 32], fixed block_timestamp) through testing_env! and asserts that two draws of generate_random_number with max 2000 are equal and positive. No sandbox and no WSL. DoD: the cell passes in dice's own workflow on Linux CI and on the box, then gas per method (env::used_gas) for each contract method in a second cell. Next step: a dice codespace run with this file + the DICE-PAGES-404 publish change, checking the contract notebook's spiral-tests line.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_18 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 18u32, "2026-11-06T15:34Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:3x PROVEN ON LINUX: dice codespace run 3 (dice main + this cell + the publish change): contract/dice_contract.spi spiral-tests discovered 8, executed 8, failed 0 (the mocked cell generate_random_number_is_deterministic_under_a_mocked_context is one of them, with near-sdk unit-testing). No sandbox and no WSL were used. Next step: the same cell on the box (Windows, the item's point), when the box isn't saturated, then a gas-per-method cell (env::used_gas).")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_19 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 19u32, "2026-11-06T22:22Z", "main", "main 11-06 18:2x STATUS. (1) Linux CI (dice run 42255610569, after the user's 12:46 push of this cell): contract notebook 11 tests, 9 passed, 2 failed (contribute_seed and the mocked cell), both E0599 in append_seed: the committed spiral compiler (d86fd005, source A5FF832751C38A5C) lowers seeds : rust.ref (rust.mut' (am'.vec u8)) to &mut [u8], while the box's pack55d emits &mut Vec<u8>. Asked compiler whether a later pack fixes it (then the next spiral push turns dice CI green). (2) Windows box: the contract build first failed E0463 (no wasm32-unknown-unknown for the contract toolchain nightly-2024-07-14). main installed that target (box upkeep), and the contract now compiles to wasm under pack57, but running -c cells goes through spiral_wasm -> WSL ('WSL 2 requires an update'): the known NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE gap. The gate then fails every cell of the file, so the mocked cell's Windows verdict is still pending. Next step: run the mocked cell alone on Windows (a notebook holding only non -c cells), then add the drafted gas cell (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\dice\\NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS\\gas-cell.spi).")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_20 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 20u32, "2026-11-06T22:53Z", "main", "main 11-06 18:5x WINDOWS IS BLOCKED UPSTREAM (box, pack57, a notebook holding only the mocked cells, all -c cells stripped): near-sdk 5.11's unit-testing feature pulls near-vm-runner 0.29.2, whose src/cache.rs:307 does `use rustix::fs::{Mode, OFlags}` unconditionally. rustix 0.38.44 has no fs module on Windows, so the mocked VM cannot compile there at all (E0432/E0433). The item's 'native Windows fast loop' is impossible with near-sdk unit-testing until near-vm-runner gates that import. FIXES ON THE WAY: (a) my mocked cell passed `near.new_vector` (a vector u8) where generate_random_number takes `ref (mut' (vec u8))`. The committed compiler let that through to rustc (part of dice CI's red); pack57 rejects it at type check. It now uses empty_seeds () |> rust.to_ref_mut, like the contract's own tests. (b) The gas cell (env::used_gas around generate_random_number, asserting 0 < gas < 300 Tgas) is appended to dice_contract.spi, unstaged. DoD AMENDED: the mocked cells pass on Linux (dice CI and a codespace); Windows is recorded as blocked upstream (near-vm-runner cache.rs rustix::fs). A codespace run of the contract notebook (dice-cs5) is proving (a)+(b) on Linux now.")
inl note_of_near_mocked_unit_tests_21 () = Note ("NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS", 21u32, "2026-11-06T23:34Z", "main", "main 11-06 19:3x PROVEN ON LINUX (codespace dice-cs5: dice main 3c50872 plus an overlay of the unstaged dice_contract.spi and manifests, building spiral's COMMITTED compiler like CI; codespace deleted, verified gone): contract notebook 12 discovered, 12 executed, 11 passed, 1 failed. PASS: generate_random_number_is_deterministic_under_a_mocked_context (with the empty_seeds fix) and the NEW generate_random_number_reports_its_gas_under_a_mocked_context (env::used_gas around one call, 0 < gas < 300 Tgas). FAIL: only contribute_seed, the committed compiler's &mut [u8] lowering of seeds; the box's pack55d+ emits &mut Vec<u8>, and compiler expects the next spiral push to fix it ('likely yes, not confirmed'). Windows stays blocked upstream (near-vm-runner rustix::fs). DoD (amended n20): mocked cells pass on Linux = MET, plus gas per method for generate_random_number. Remaining before Done: dice CI green after the user pushes spiral then dice; gas for the other methods (contribute_seed once it builds).")
inl near_feed_paged_view () = Task ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", "Gas-limit spike for an on-chain home feed: a minimal contract (post, follow, feed view) where the feed is a k-way merge over the followed accounts' post indices computed in bounded view-call steps with a typed resumable cursor (a GADT step indexed by its phase, the per-step budget computed at compile time from gas measured in the mock); view calls cost the reader nothing, so the client pages; compare with fan-out on write as a resumable job queue or NEP-519 yield/resume; replay XSIM-EVENT-STREAM scenarios and report gas per page and follows per page", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS,XSIM-EVENT-STREAM", "near,microblog,gadt,feed,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_near_feed_paged_view () = Planning ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_1 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 1u32, "2026-10-18T17:09Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:09 design detail: views are free for the reader but each call still has a gas ceiling, so the merge must be resumable: cursor = per-followed-account position (or a timestamp watermark plus offsets) returned with each page; the step is a typed state machine (GADT indexed by merge phase) whose per-step item budget is a compile-time constant derived from gas measured in the mock; fan-out on write = a queue drained by later transactions (or NEP-519 promise_yield_create/resume) for accounts with many followers; report gas per page, follows per page and storage per post")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_2 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 2u32, "2026-10-19T12:56Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:56 helper-lane lap 1: dep check: XSIM-EVENT-STREAM is Done, NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS (Planned 0%) is the real gate, since the per-step budget must come from gas measured in the mock. Found an existing in-tree instance of the same unbounded-view problem, so the spike's paging can be proven without a new contract first: polyglot/apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.rs get_alias_map(alias) returns the whole HashMap<String, (u64, u32)> of an alias in one view call (plus a borsh twin), so a popular alias would hit the view gas ceiling exactly like an unpaged feed. A paged get_alias_map(alias, cursor, limit) with a typed cursor is the smallest rehearsal of the feed's resumable view, measurable in the mock once NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS lands.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_3 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 3u32, "2026-10-19T13:38Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:38 helper-lane lap 2: modelled the resumable feed view off-chain first (lab/NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW/paged_merge.spi, CPU-only): a k-way merge over per-account post timestamps (newest_head picks the newest head, drop_head consumes it) where page feeds budget returns up to budget items plus the remaining feeds as the cursor, and all_pages resumes from that cursor until a page is empty. Check: three accounts (8 posts) paged by 3 give 3 pages whose order checksum equals one unbounded page's, i.e. resuming from the cursor loses or reorders nothing; C exit 3 via try.ps1 + Invoke-Heavy. On-chain, the cursor would shrink to per-account positions instead of the remaining lists, and budget is the compile-time constant from the mock's gas per item.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_4 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 4u32, "2026-10-19T15:24Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:24 helper-lane lap 3: wrote the on-chain cursor shape as lab/NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW/paged_offsets.spi (unrun until main's freeze all-clear): the feeds stay immutable (each account's post index, newest first, read by position as a vector would be), and the cursor is one i32 offset per followed account instead of the remaining lists; newest_at scans the heads at the current offsets, bump advances only the winning account's offset, page returns up to budget items plus the new offsets, all_pages resumes from them. Same check as the list version: 3 accounts, 8 posts, budget 3 must give 3 pages whose order checksum equals one unbounded page (expect exit 3). The cursor is now O(follows) integers, which is what a view call can return and take back as its argument.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_5 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 5u32, "2026-10-19T16:01Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 12:01 helper-lane lap 5: the cursor is now the title's typed resumable step (lab/NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW/paged_offsets.spi, unrun until the freeze all-clear): a GADT cursor phase with Fresh and Paused offsets indexed scanning and Exhausted indexed exhausted, next_page accepting only a cursor scanning and returning More (items, cursor scanning) or Last items (it peeks whether any head remains, so the last page is marked without an extra empty call), and drain resuming until Last. Same equality check as before (expect exit 3: 3 pages of the 8 posts equal one unbounded page). paged_exhausted_negative.spi passes Exhausted to next_page and must be rejected at compile time - the type, not a runtime check, stops a client from paging a finished feed.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_6 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 6u32, "2026-10-19T17:42Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 13:42 helper-lane: probe run: paged_offsets.spi with the phase-indexed cursor GADT exits 3 as predicted (3 pages resumed through Paused offsets equal one unbounded page). The compile-time negative (paging Exhausted) is still to run.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_7 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 7u32, "2026-10-22T04:08Z", "x", "2026-10-22 00:08 x: open decision for the user (asked 10-21 22:4x, no answer yet). spiral/lab/NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW holds 3 probes from 10-19 (paged_merge.spi 1,445 B, paged_offsets.spi 2,968 B, paged_exhausted_negative.spi 2,806 B), and NEAR work is paused by the user since 10-18. Under the lab rule they have no place to land while the item is paused. Options: land them now as Spiral test blocks of a paged-feed module (they test merge, offsets and exhaustion of a paged view, which needs no NEAR contract), or keep them parked here until NEAR resumes. Until the user decides, they stay where they are; nothing is moved or deleted.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_8 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 8u32, "2026-10-22T13:34Z", "x", "2026-10-22 09:34 x: DECIDED by rule, replacing the 00:08 'open decision for the user' (memory decide-autonomously: open calls are mine, never a user list). Rule, written before checking: a lab probe whose item the user paused lands where its tested logic belongs today. If no live module owns that logic, the probe stays in place until the item resumes, and the resume is the landing trigger. Probes are never deleted before landing (lab rule). Check: the probes test a k-way merge of followed accounts' post indices with a resumable cursor (a GADT phase: Fresh/Paused offsets vs Exhausted). x's only paging module, apps/client/paging.spi, walks X API next_token pages (paged/all_pages over a pager), which is different logic, and no other x module has a merge cursor. Outcome: the 3 probes stay in spiral/lab/NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW until NEAR resumes. Then they become the test blocks of the contract's feed-view module, and paged_exhausted_negative.spi (still unrun) becomes a compile-time rejection test there.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_9 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 9u32, "2026-10-23T11:08Z", "x", "2026-10-23 07:08 x: grooming: status Planned -> Paused. Its parent X-ON-NEAR is paused by the user, and note 8's rule keeps it until NEAR resumes, so it must not show as ready work.")
inl note_of_near_feed_paged_view_10 () = Note ("NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW", 10u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 4 11:39 (subagent): blocked: paged_offsets.spi written, bounded jobs frozen -> next: after the all-clear: run (expect 3) | lap 6 13:42 (subagent): GADT cursor probe PASS (3) -> next: run the Exhausted negative | lap 6 13:49 (subagent): Exhausted negative rejected at compile time (cursor scanning vs exhausted) -> next: gas mock (needs NEAR-MOCKED) | lap 7 19:54 (subagent): re-read: GADT cursor PASS 3 + negative -> next: next page op")
