inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_1 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 1u32, "2026-10-20T02:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 22:33 user request 2026-10-19 21:4x (main-thread recorded it): Every i574n repo gets the Open in GitHub Codespaces button (README badge plus a working .devcontainer so the codespace boots with the toolchains the repo needs).")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_2 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T09:39Z", "main", "10-27 05:39 main: 10-27 05:39 main groom: fresh census (stale since the 10-19 laps), README codespaces.new links vs .devcontainer, across the 59 git repos under C:\\home\\git. With the button: alphabet, dice, dotfiles, i574n.github, polyglot, spiral, tapas2, vault. i574n-owned repos without it (12): tibia and tictactoe already have a .devcontainer, so each needs only its README line. azeroth, blog, dir-tree-html, fiscal, i574n.github.io, kit and x have no devcontainer, so they need the devcontainer first (button without one = a bare default image). Out of scope by rule: cargo-outdated and The-Spiral-Language (forks of public projects, no-public-project-interaction), eoie (a junction to kit), and every other-owner repo (zed, wasmer, nearcore, leptos and the rest). fc1943s's 11 repos are the backup dump, never edited. Next concrete step: tictactoe's one-line README badge. Tibia's goes to the tibia team; each other repo's devcontainer goes to its team.")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_3 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 3u32, "2026-10-29T06:18Z", "main", "10-29 02:2x main: tictactoe's step is already DONE in the working tree (unstaged, from before the wipe): README.md:5 carries the badge [![...](https://github.com/codespaces/badge.svg)](https://github.com/codespaces/new?hide_repo_select=true&ref=main&repo=487648852), and gh api repos/i574n/tictactoe returns id 487648852, so the link opens the right repo. Its .devcontainer (devcontainer.json, Dockerfile, .env) exists. The README diff rewrites every line (line endings plus the badge line), and the repo also has staged renames (.yaml -> .yml) and a staged FUNDING.yml, both the user's (user-stages-mid-run), so nothing was touched. Left: tibia's README line (tibia team), and a devcontainer first, then the badge, for azeroth, blog, dir-tree-html, fiscal, i574n.github.io, kit and x (each repo's team). A devcontainer is only proven by booting a codespace, which this box can't do offline.")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_4 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 4u32, "2026-10-30T14:55Z", "main", "10-30 10:55 main: main's 3 repos DONE in the working tree (unstaged, for the user's commit): blog, dir-tree-html and i574n.github.io. Each gets .devcontainer/{devcontainer.json, Dockerfile}, byte-copied from the shared sibling standard (dice/alphabet/i574n.github use the same 601 B + 220 B files: universal:dev image + powershell, Spiral extension, ports 13805/13806; hash-checked equal), plus the README badge line under the title in dice's exact form, with each repo's numeric id from gh api (blog 1422846800, dir-tree-html 1411208249, i574n.github.io 637595591) and ref=main (gh api default_branch = main for all 3). README diffs are +2 lines each, LF kept, and no staged files were touched (dir-tree-html's unstaged shared.spi/tree.spi edits are left alone). NOT proven: booting a codespace, which needs the user's GitHub session after the push; that's the check. LEFT, per team: tibia (README line only; it has a .devcontainer) for team tibia; fiscal, kit and x (devcontainer + badge) for teams fiscal, kit and x, copying the same sibling files. azeroth is the user's own repo (banned-words n3 lists it as user prose), so it's left for the user to decide.")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_5 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 5u32, "2026-10-31T00:06Z", "main", "10-30 20:06 main: tibia is DONE (its README badge is in). Left: kit, fiscal and x (devcontainer + badge each, byte-copied from the sibling standard as in n4). Tagged kit, fiscal and x so each team's agile next hands out its repo (the item was tagged main only, so none of them saw it).")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_6 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 6u32, "2026-10-31T00:10Z", "x", "2026-10-30 20:1x x: x's repo DONE in the working tree (unstaged, for the user's commit). x/.devcontainer/{devcontainer.json 601 B 3623A9C2A0F9, Dockerfile 220 B AFD7905604D7} byte-copied from dice, the hashes main's 3 repos and i574n.github carry (alphabet and tibia have a 617 B variant; dice's is the majority standard). README badge at line 3, under '# x', in the siblings' exact form, with repo=1421538869 and ref=main (gh api repos/i574n/x: id 1421538869, default_branch main). README diff +2 lines, LF kept; nothing staged touched. NOT proven: booting a codespace needs the user's GitHub session after the push. Left: kit and fiscal (their teams).")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_7 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 7u32, "2026-10-31T07:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 03:25 fiscal: fiscal's repo DONE in the working tree (unstaged, for the user's commit): fiscal/.devcontainer/{devcontainer.json 601 B 3623A9C2A0F9, Dockerfile 220 B AFD7905604D7} byte-copied from dice (the majority standard per x's n6); README badge at line 3 under '# fiscal' in the siblings' exact form with repo=1429627019 and ref=main (gh api repos/i574n/fiscal: id 1429627019, default_branch main, public). README diff +2 lines, LF kept; nothing staged. NOT proven: booting a codespace needs the user's GitHub session after the push. Left: kit (its team), then azeroth, blog, dir-tree-html, i574n.github.io per main's n2 census.")
