inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_14 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 14u32, "2026-11-01T12:44Z", "kit", "11-01 08:5x kit (Blocked rule). blocked by: user, push the unstaged fiscal and kit changes, then open one codespace from a repo's badge with the user's GitHub session so it boots (x 10-31 23:37); azeroth stays without the button by the user's call.")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_15 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 15u32, "2026-11-01T14:21Z", "main", "main 10:1x: the devcontainers this item added asked for storage 64gb, which made codespaces impossible on every i574n repo (no 32 GB machine qualifies; CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS). Lowered to 32gb in all 16 files, unstaged. The badge only works after the user commits that.")
inl note_of_codespaces_button_all_repos_16 () = Note ("CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS", 16u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
