inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_1 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 1u32, "2026-10-20T02:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 22:33 user request 2026-10-19 21:4x (main-thread recorded it): Finish edition 3 and migrate every Spiral source in every repo to its symbols (the edition-3 symbol table), getting closer to x sim compatibility.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_2 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 2u32, "2026-10-24T18:53Z", "main", "main 15:0x (user 14:5x: considering edition 3 symbols + automatic translation next; answer: heals are not made moot, edition 3 is lexical and the converter cannot touch macro text, so granular code translates better; land the ~13 queued anchored slices first, then migrate, then EDITION3-280-SPLIT). State found in the core: both cores already LEX the edition-3 symbols (edition3_symbol_token, Tokenize section ~43180); FormatterConvert (~179405) respells keyword and bool tokens to Symbols or Words per line outside macros, re-lexes each converted line and keeps it only when the token identities are unchanged (else Rejected); format-corpus convert measures a corpus (lines converted/rejected, round trip back to words byte-identical, parse-same vs parse-differs) and writes the symbol text to --out. Missing for the real migration: an in-place verb (format --spelling symbols|words <paths>, editions from package.spiproj) and the edition-3 spelling of test blocks and #. Readiness measurement running now over every tracked .spi/.spir in spiral (minus samples), eoie, x, dice, alphabet, fiscal, polyglot, blog (scratch edition3-readiness: corpus.tsv, listing.txt, symbols/).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_3 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 3u32, "2026-10-24T18:59Z", "main", "main 15:0x user 15:0x: \"advance edition3 thru the end, toml and everything, we have backups; remain upstream compatible, mostly core only; dogfood with the memoization; mechanical, all projects benefit\". Plan (decided, no poll): (1) sources: every tracked .spi/.spir in spiral (lib, apps, samples), eoie, x, dice, alphabet, fiscal, polyglot, blog respelled to edition-3 symbols with the compiler's own FormatterConvert (format --spelling symbols, guarded per line by re-lexed token identity); the upstream core package (deps/The-Spiral-Language VS Code Plugin core, |core-) stays edition-2 words so the fork remains upstream compatible; (2) manifests declare their edition; (3) tooling: tree-sitter grammar (TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL) and the Zed extension/config .toml files learn the symbols; a package.spiproj -> TOML manifest is a compiler package-format change, done after the source migration as its own step; (4) proof by memoization: lexical respelling must leave every residual byte-identical, so the compile memo/matrix and Cells gates on converted copies must report 0 residual differences; (5) land per repo after the in-flight anchored lib slices land, with backups (git history plus a scratch snapshot). Step 1 in flight: readiness measurement over 956 files (format-corpus convert) and the in-place verb candidate (pack-spelling, job main-serial-pack-spelling, round trip on a lib copy).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_4 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 4u32, "2026-10-24T19:52Z", "main", "Readiness 15:3x: 956 files over 8 repos respelled to symbols with 0 rejected lines (47,015 lines converted); 932 round-trip byte-identical, 23 differ (lib 2, eoie 16, x 5), all 40 lines one class: the anti-fusion guard spelled false; as !- ; (the lexer already splits a trailing ; or , off a symbol), so the words round trip came back false ;. Fix packed into pack-spelling: convertLine tries the original gaps first and inserts the space only when the re-lex changes token identities. Residual proof: lib + apps/spiral with 108 converted files compile to byte-identical F# (DA79215DB24E7AFF, 941,591 B) and Rust (51AF983545824F1F, 1,561,366 B). Next: candidate build + lib round trip 0 differs, then land lib via land.ps1 with a snapshot.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_5 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 5u32, "2026-10-24T20:42Z", "main", "main 16:5x, land rule written before the proof runs: the queued pack-spelling job (main-serial-pack-spelling, build-probe.ps1) builds the verb with the tight-first respelling, then on a lib + apps/spiral copy: format --spelling symbols, the installed formatter must change 0 symbol files (land.ps1 formats touched files), apps/spiral F# and Rust residuals must equal the original's, and format --spelling words must restore every file byte for byte. It writes %TEMP%\\lib-gate-kit\\verdict-EDITION3-LIB-SYMBOLS.txt and does NOT land. The land (land.ps1 -Name EDITION3-LIB-SYMBOLS -ApplyScript %TEMP%\\lib-edition3-symbols\\apply.ps1: full snapshot to %TEMP%\\edition3-backup-lib-<stamp>, then respell every file not in hold.txt) is queued by hand only when (1) the verdict is GREEN, (2) x, tibia and eoie have each answered the 16:4x message with 'no pending lib chains' or a hold list (memory reformat-peer-repos-ask-first; silence is not agreement, held files go to hold.txt), and (3) my own queued lib slices (async-roundtrip, zig-lua-gaps, channel-spawn, date-time-span-2b, sm-roundtrip, crypto/trace) have landed or been withdrawn, since their anchors are spelled in words. Other repos follow one by one under the same rule; the upstream core stays words.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_6 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 6u32, "2026-10-24T20:47Z", "main", "main 16:5x: peer answers so far. tibia holds process.spi (3 pending chains: process-handle-land, process-replace-apply, process-delete-apply) and file_system.spi (Lua file_exists arm, gate RED). x holds file_system.spi (normalize-prefix + GRANULAR-HEAL FS-1..4 serial chain), sm'.spi (regexp ///> directive fix) and listm'.spi (part B skip_/chunks_); I chose x's option (a) for all three, so x lands on edition-2 text. hold.txt has the 4 files; the apply dry run respells 106 lib files, 4 held. Held files join a second respelling pass once their owners report them landed (one verb call, no redraft). eoie has not answered yet. Not touched: package.spiproj (tibia's chains edit its module list).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_7 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 7u32, "2026-10-24T21:32Z", "main", "main 17:3x: the land is one step once its rule holds. %TEMP%\\lib-edition3-symbols\\ready.ps1 checks the rule's machine-checkable conditions: proof verdict GREEN and no main lib-slice runner running (sm-roundtrip, zig-channel-2, heal-gates, lands). It prints the hold list and, when ready, the job start line for land.json (land.ps1 + apply.ps1: snapshot, 106 files, 4 held). At 17:3x it prints NOT READY (no verdict yet; zig-channel-2 and sm-roundtrip running), which is also its positive control. All 3 peer teams have answered. After the land, message eoie, which holds HIJK until then; held files get a second pass when x and tibia report their chains landed. The proof now also respells apps/spiral, so its GREEN covers the apps/spiral land as a follow-up.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_8 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 8u32, "2026-10-24T21:34Z", "main", "main 17:4x: the respelling is idempotent, checked with the pack-spelling candidate on copies of json.spi, step_runtime.spi and xsd_regex.spi: the first pass changed 3 files, a second symbols pass changed 0 and every hash stayed the same. So the second pass for held files is just: empty their lines from hold.txt and run land.json again. The real output shows the tight-first fix: step_runtime now reads 'draining = mut !-;' (it was '!- ;').")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_9 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 9u32, "2026-10-24T21:39Z", "main", "main 17:3x: proof fix before it runs. proof.ps1 ran the installed formatter on the symbol text and only then compared the words round trip, so any lib file that was not format-clean to begin with would have turned the verdict RED for a reason that is not the respelling's (land.ps1 formats touched files anyway). Both copies are now normalized with the installed formatter first, so the formatter-neutral, residual and round-trip checks measure only the respelling. Script parses; it starts when its heavy slot frees.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_10 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 10u32, "2026-10-24T21:57Z", "main", "main 17:5x: proof GREEN (main-edition3-lib-proof, verdict 17:56). On copies of the current lib + apps/spiral: (1) the format baseline normalized 2 files per copy first, so the 17:3x fix was needed: without it the verdict would have been a false RED; (2) 110 of 110 lib files and apps/spiral respelled, 0 errors; (3) the installed formatter changes 0 symbol files; (4) apps/spiral residuals are identical, F# B02DDE307115EFD6 and Rust 6B00A44CA5FFF387 on both sides (new hashes because lib changed since 15:3x); (5) the words round trip restores every file, 0 differ. Land rule: conditions 1 (verdict) and 2 (peer answers) hold; condition 3 does not yet (main-serial-zig-channel-2 still running), so ready.ps1 says NOT READY and the land waits for it.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_11 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 11u32, "2026-10-24T23:45Z", "main", "2026-10-24 19:45 groom: x reports its held lib files landed on edition-2 text (listm'.spi part B 17:58, sm'.spi regexp-directive 18:06, file_system.spi normalize-prefix + fs-heal-1..3 18:28; runner job-1792875049850-x-lib-held-files exit 0). fs-heal-4 is not landed and will come later as an edition-3 chain, so it does not block. Second-pass rule: once tibia also reports process.spi/file_system.spi done, drop listm'.spi and sm'.spi from hold.txt and respell them in the land or a follow-up pass. x also flags sm'.spi:737 spiral_sm_find_trailing (Gleam) missing gleam_erlang/gleam/dynamic imports (X-SIM-FRAMES-GLEAM-IMPORTS).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_12 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 12u32, "2026-10-24T23:45Z", "main", "2026-10-24 19:45 groom: 55%. The respell verb is built, the lib proof is GREEN (17:56), tree-sitter handles symbols, and x's holds are released. Left: the lib land (ready.ps1 -> land.json), the held-file second pass, then the other repos (956 files already proven to round-trip).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_13 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 13u32, "2026-10-25T00:18Z", "main", "2026-10-24 20:18 main: the land waits on eoie's CLEAN release (eoie 20:1x: HIJK..R folded into one CLEAN release on the current edition-2 lib). Its preflight job-1792887334696-eoie-clean-preflight reads the live lib through a junction (~30-40 min), and CLEAN reads lib until it prints 'lib-free:'. Rule: queue land.json only after CLEAN prints lib-free; the land's reader guard watches that marker. My own lib runners have all finished (zig-channel-2 exit 0).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_14 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 14u32, "2026-10-25T00:49Z", "main", "2026-10-24 20:49 main: LIB LANDED and verified live. job-1792888956522-main-serial-edition3-land (20:42-20:44): 108 lib files respelled to symbols, 0 errors, process.spi and file_system.spi held for tibia, snapshot %TEMP%\\edition3-backup-lib-20261024-204332 (restore: robocopy <snapshot> C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral /E). The installed formatter then touched only otp_supervisor.spi. Live check job-1792889210868-main-edition3-live-check-2 GREEN: apps/spiral over the live lib and over the live lib with the snapshot's words files laid back gives identical F# 21292B1B6F2BF31D and Rust 490A23161B25CA8C. (Its first run was a false RED: the snapshot holds only .spi/.spir files, so the words copy lacked package.spiproj.) Left: tibia's 2 held files, the other 8 repos one at a time after their lanes answer, the spelling verb shipping in 5j, spiral.toml.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_15 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 15u32, "2026-10-25T00:53Z", "main", "2026-10-24 20:53 main groom, lessons from the land: (1) apply.ps1's snapshot holds only the .spi/.spir files (110), so a check that rebuilds 'the pre-land lib' from it has to overlay those files on a full copy (live-check.ps1 does now); its first run was a false RED. (2) Read a check's own output before trusting its verdict: 'none' on one side is a setup failure, not a mismatch. (3) A land window opens when the owner of the long readers says so: eoie's CLEAN preflight read the live lib through a junction, and its launcher's failure is what freed the window.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_16 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 16u32, "2026-10-25T01:14Z", "main", "2026-10-24 21:14 main: the proof had a gap. It checked residuals, the formatter and the round trip, but never ran the lib's test blocks through Cells, whose keyword-prefix classifier doesn't know the symbols (CELLS-EDITION3-KEYWORDS, P0, fix drafted). Rule for every future repo land: one Cells gate on a respelled file with a top-level :! and test blocks, before the land. Pass 2 (process.spi, file_system.spi, released by tibia and x) was queued under a new name whose verdict file didn't exist, so it waited; the verdict now states its basis (the 17:56 proof covered all 110 files, and live-check-3 follows the apply).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_17 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 17u32, "2026-10-25T01:48Z", "main", "2026-10-24 21:48 main: a second respell bug, found by that scan. format --spelling respelled two test NAMES that are keywords: listm' 'test forall =' became 'test \\* =' and 'test exists print_code =' became 'test \\? print_code ='. Cells reads those as malformed headers, so listm' got 29 test cells for 27 headers. The token guard missed it because \\* lexes to the same keyword token as forall, but a test header is free text the compiler skips. Fixed: the two lib headers are restored, and %TEMP%\\pack-next5j\\test-header-words.ps1 (anchor 1/1, in compose.ps1) makes convertLine leave a column-0 test header unchanged; the tree mirror apps/compiler/tmp/formatter/Convert.fsx has the same arm. RULE for every remaining repo land: run the Cells round-trip scan (lib-trip-all.exs over the repo's .spi files) before and after the respell, and require identical failure sets.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_18 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 18u32, "2026-10-25T03:20Z", "main", "2026-10-24 23:20 main: SPREAD (user 23:0x: 'if the lib experiment passed we gotta spread edition3 around everything'). Generic tool %TEMP%\\edition3-spread\\respell-repo.ps1: works on copies; test headers put back verbatim until 5j; the words round trip must be byte-identical; the installed formatter goes on top, and its changes are checked as pre-existing on a words copy; Cells round-trip scan on the original and symbols copies with identical failure sets. Applied: dir-tree-html 1, blog 10 (4 pre-existing formatter normalizations; Cells 1/1), dice 16 (0/0), alphabet 2 (0/0), polyglot 5 (Perf.spi not idempotent on both sides). x, tibia and eoie reported no drafts on these repos. Owner lanes respell their own repos: tibia is landing (51 files GREEN, terrain.spi excluded as generated), x after verify-landing8, eoie after its hand crate splits and release. Left for main: spiral apps (dry run in progress, excluding lib and compiler samples), the compiler samples (1,145; they feed the matrix, own step), fiscal (untracked; with FISCAL-ROOT-PATHS), then EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_19 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 19u32, "2026-10-25T03:38Z", "main", "2026-10-24 23:38 main: spiral apps LANDED, 31 files (job-1792898860281-main-edition3-spiral-apps). apps/spiral F# 21292B1B6F2BF31D, Rust 490A23161B25CA8C and the Cells domain Gleam 2614043FA6663EA5 are identical before and after. Excluded: lib (done), compiler samples (own step), the formatter fixtures (byte-exact edge cases) and lab (each lane's drafts). apps/zed/fixtures is held until I check whether the Zed tests pin columns. Tool fixes: -Exclude split on commas, the round trip compares words(respelled) with words(original), errors anchored at line start; x added the final-newline tolerance. x is GREEN on copies (44 files) and lands after verify8; tibia is landing 51.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_20 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 20u32, "2026-10-25T03:53Z", "main", "2026-10-24 23:53 main: x LANDED, 44 files, spelling only (formatter skipped: it would push 28 cells past 280), gate job-1792900302663-x-verify-landing9. eoie is still on its crate splits (5 of 16) and respells after its release.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_21 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 21u32, "2026-10-25T04:27Z", "main", "2026-10-25 00:27 main: tibia LANDED 51 files (arena compiled Lua 9/9 byte-identical, build.ps1 green with memo off; src/terrain.spi excluded as generated). tibia's trap: scripts that find Spiral definitions by word-keyword regex go silently blind (its arena build matched ^inl main \\(\\) and found no probes). Swept every repo I landed: fixed apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 (5 patterns, plus :# for test headers), apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1 and fiscal scripts/candidate-gate.ps1 (memo.ex and cells.ex were fixed earlier). Control on the census pattern: the old pattern finds 2,015 definitions in the words snapshot and 0 in the live edition-3 lib, which is the silent failure; the new pattern finds 2,021 live (+6 landed since). Remaining hits match Cells-generated words text or Swift, so they're fine. RULE for every remaining land: grep the repo's scripts for '\\^(inl|let|open|nominal|union|type|and) ' and StartsWith('inl ' patterns first, and give each a symbol alternative with a positive and a negative control.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_22 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 22u32, "2026-10-25T04:43Z", "main", "2026-10-25 00:43 main: apps/zed/fixtures respelled (ok/main.spi, bad/main.spi). The hold was unneeded: apps/zed/test.ps1 only needs ok to compile and bad to fail, the manual test wants exactly one diagnostic, and no test pins lines or columns. The words round trip is byte-identical; originals are in %TEMP%\\edition3-spread\\zed-fixtures\\original.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_23 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 23u32, "2026-10-25T12:52Z", "eoie", "08:52 eoie: dry run GREEN for eoie with main's respell-repo.ps1 on the 5l' candidate (-Compiler copy, -SymbolTestHeaders, no -Apply): 844 files, 843 respelled, errors 0, words round trip differs 0, installed formatter normalizes 476 more files (1319 changed in all). It applies right after SLATE installs, as its own release before KIT-RENAME. Pre-apply checks: (1) a sample of the 476 formatter-only diffs against the keep-breaks rule (no joined authored lines, re-lay only over 120); (2) the untracked new packages are in the file list; (3) after -Apply, a full no-publish regen of every crate (all at or under 1000, cargo check green), then the release.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_24 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 24u32, "2026-10-25T13:49Z", "eoie", "09:49 eoie: read respell-repo.ps1 before the keep-breaks review. The respell itself enforces equal line counts (line 44, an error otherwise), but the formatting pass on top (line 55) runs the INSTALLED compiler (5j today) on the symbols copy that -Apply lands, and nothing checks its line counts. So the 476 formatter changes are where joins could hide, and the apply must run after 5l' is installed, so the same formatter that ships is the one normalizing. Check script: scratch clean\\respell\\keep-breaks-check.ps1 (final symbols copy versus original: files with fewer lines, files still over 120), run on the re-done dry run under %TEMP%\\respell-repo\\eoie.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_25 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 25u32, "2026-10-25T14:22Z", "eoie", "10:22 eoie pre-apply check 1 PASSED: re-ran the dry run with the fixed tool (copies under %TEMP%\\respell-repo\\eoie; same result: 843 respelled, round trip differs 0, 476 formatter changes, GREEN) and compared the final symbols copy with the originals (scratch clean\\respell\\keep-breaks-check.ps1). 4 files have one line fewer; all 4 are a removed blank line (3 leading, 1 between definitions), with no joined authored lines. 109 files still have lines over 120 after the format: legacy long lines the formatter leaves alone, not created by the respell. Oddity for main: in src/eoie_tree_copy/terminal.spi the definition emit_runtime, whose body opens a raw triple-quoted rust_global block, keeps its word spelling (inl), while its neighbour rust_global becomes ':='. The round trip still holds, so it is cosmetic, but symbols mode leaves one word-spelled definition there. Check 2 (untracked packages in scope) passed earlier: they are staged, so inside the 844. Ready to -Apply once SLATE installs, on the installed 5l' formatter.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_26 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 26u32, "2026-10-25T18:25Z", "eoie", "14:25 kit: runbook for the eoie respell release (it follows SLATE; edition-3 spellings, test headers as :#). Rules written before running:\n1. Start only after SLATE has installed and its after-install checks passed (after-install-SLATE-extra.ps1 11/11 plus CLEAN's), with no tree lease and no eoie release queued or running.\n2. Dry run on the installed 5l'' (SpiralCompiler.dll under spiral-bin\\bin\\single-flight, core MVID 7fd00bff-...):\n   respell-repo.ps1 -Name eoie -Root C:\\home\\git\\eoie -Compiler <dll> -SymbolTestHeaders (no -Apply). It must report GREEN, and keep-breaks-check must show only the 4 known removed blank lines.\n3. -Apply, then regenerate all 234 crates in one workspace with SLATE's make/merged-check scripts on the respelled tree.\n   Gate: every crate's .rs is byte-identical to SLATE's published .rs, since respelling changes syntax, not meaning. Any diff stops the release; the crate is investigated, and the respell is reverted from the respell work folder's original copy.\n4. If identical: the release job builds and installs as SLATE did (notebooks plus after-install checks). The diff is source-only, so the release is mostly the formatter-visible text.\n5. Then KIT-RENAME (kit-rename.ps1, dry run already green: 693 files, 149 folders, 0 leftovers), then the post-rename queue: splits (HAND-CRATE-UNITS notes 13-14), the list-sugar heal (DO-SLOP-GATE note 6, same byte-identical gate), the lint CLI, the CI fixture fix.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_27 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 27u32, "2026-10-25T19:44Z", "eoie", "15:43 kit: respell runbook (note 26), new step 0. Land clean\\standards-edition3\\declared-edition3.do (EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET note: eoie standards reads ':=' and ':~' rows) before running respell -Apply. Otherwise the respelled standards.spi files declare nothing to the installed checker, and every package reads as clean.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_28 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 28u32, "2026-10-25T21:00Z", "eoie", "17:00 kit: the respell release job is generated and tested. scratch clean\\respell\\make-RESPELL.ps1 derives release-build-job-RESPELL.ps1 from SLATE's job: log, lease and notebook-tag names renamed (rRESPELL-, candidateRESPELL), the same 234-crate filter, plus the byte-identical gate.\n- The gate hashes every src crate's .rs before the regen and compares after it; any difference means 'release not published', listing the changed files, with restore from the before-release-RESPELL snapshot.\n- Checks: job-script-check ok (136 commands), parse ok. Gate logic exercised on a fake tree: 2 files hashed, target excluded; unchanged tree 0 changed; one edited crate exactly 1 changed.\n- Launch order after SLATE (note 26 plus step 0): land the standards fix, run respell -Apply, take a snapshot labelled before-release-RESPELL, then job start --heavy with the RESPELL job.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_29 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 29u32, "2026-10-25T21:04Z", "eoie", "17:04 kit: correction to note 28. Step 0's standards fix really changes eoie_standards' generated code, so the gate now has an explicit intended list (rsIntended = eoie_standards) and every other crate must stay byte-identical. Gate test, 4/4 pass: baseline hashes 2 crate files with target excluded; unchanged tree 0; a change in the intended crate is excluded; a change anywhere else is reported by name. The job is regenerated; job-script-check ok, 137 commands.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_30 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 30u32, "2026-10-25T22:22Z", "eoie", "18:22 kit: respell tool smoke on the installed 5l'' (core CDD68DC3), on a scratch git repo holding eoie_job_serial: GREEN, 2 files respelled, 0 errors, words round trip differs 0, installed formatter changes 0, 39 s (mostly .NET startup per format pass). So the launcher's respell step works on this box's installed compiler. The full-tree run is in the worker-node proof (job-1792966042350-renameproof), still respelling at 18:20 node time on a node at 100% CPU.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_31 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 31u32, "2026-10-26T05:29Z", "x", "2026-10-26 01:3x x: the next full migration round also respells member access: SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX (P0, user 10-26) decided '..' (st..head) by rule ACCESSOR-1; respell gains the pair Symbols '.x' -> '..x' / Words '..x' -> '.x' beside the keyword pairs (spiral_compiler.fs:180490), so the same launcher run, words round trip and byte-identical gate cover it. Run it in the same round as EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML's 'format --manifest toml', and include lib's .livemd Spiral cells, or the next spiral.edit regen writes '.x' back.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_32 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 32u32, "2026-10-26T05:52Z", "x", "2026-10-26 01:52 x: ROUND SCOPE (user 10-26 ~01:4x: 'in this conversion round we should find more things to clear so we review everything at the same time, convert the remaining livemd files, etc'). Inventory over 11 repos (git-tracked, target/e2e/deps excluded; script %TEMP%\\x-simland-0214\\round_inventory.ps1). One round, one review, these classes: (1) manifests: 1,705 package.spiproj (spiral 1,251, eoie 435, tibia 7, x 2, dice 2, alphabet 2, polyglot 3, fiscal 1, blog 1, dir-tree-html 1), 0 spiral.toml yet -> EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML 'format --manifest toml'; (2) member access '.x' -> tight '::x' (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, ACCESSOR-2 pending): 23,689 attached + 132 standalone symbols outside strings/macros; (3) word keywords still spelled as words: line-start inl/let/type/... 31,438 (spiral 28,318, eoie 3,112, tibia 4, polyglot 2, alphabet 1, dir-tree-html 1) and if/then/else/match/with/fun ~21,800 (spiral 14,427, eoie 3,319, tibia 46, fiscal 21, polyglot 12, x 3) -> respell Symbols, edition 3 per package; (4) 'Cons (' -> 'x :: xs' sugar: 415 (spiral 230, eoie 113, blog 55, tibia 17); (5) .livemd: 21 left. Three are twins whose .spi is exported from Spiral.Cells.eval! cells (spiral/apps/spiral/spiral.livemd 143 KB -> spiral.spi, spiral/apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.livemd, polyglot/apps/perf/Perf.livemd; spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1:27 --export-only): make the .spi the source, delete the .livemd and the export step, or the respell is undone by the next export. 11 are F#-only/mostly F# (dice/lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp, alphabet/apps/hangul/hangul, polyglot apps/parser x2 + lib/fsharp x8, Perf's F# cells): port to Spiral .spi or retire, decided per file by whether anything still builds or reads them. 3 Elixir-only (spiral apps/cells/notebooks/spiral, apps/lisp/lisp, polyglot examples/elixir/exercism) and 2 pwsh-only (polyglot scripts/build, init) need no Spiral conversion; (6) idiomatic forms for raw '!!!!' macros (x 51, spiral 3,580, eoie 803, tibia 23, polyglot 15, dir-tree-html 8, dice 4; by name EQ 1,369, Export 431, LayoutToHeap 395, LayoutIndex 390, ArrayIndexSet 102, ArrayIndex 94, ArrayCreate 90, Global 58, Add 50, BackendSwitch 43, GT 42, Conv 35): lib wrappers where missing (x already proved an inl export wrapper gives byte-identical Rust; (~!) for LayoutIndex, core &&& ||| ^^^ <<< >>> and conv for arithmetic); (7) formatter-only: lines > 120 (eoie 2,354, spiral 136, x 9, polyglot 8), comment lines (eoie 29, spiral 6), trailing whitespace (polyglot 57, spiral 18, eoie 4). Order inside the round: manifests, then lexer-level respells (keywords, '::', Cons sugar), then macro wrappers, then formatter, so each step's byte-identical gate checks one class.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_33 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 33u32, "2026-10-26T06:39Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:38 x: user 10-26 ~02:1x: 'let's prioritize these migrations, groom the backlog then notify every respective lane so they can be started there'. Round raised to P0 with this item as the umbrella; per-team parts: X-EDITION3-RESPELL (x), TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND (tibia), FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (fiscal), EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND (eoie), LIB-EDITION3-ROUND (main: spiral repo + dice/alphabet/polyglot/blog/dir-tree-html), NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE (main); compiler prerequisites SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX (:: accessor), SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES (@@/##), SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT (U+200B), plus EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML (converter), EDITION3-280-SPLIT, BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP, LIB-LIST-SUGAR-REST, all P0. A team can start its manifest/keyword/Cons/formatter classes now; the '::' and '@@/##' classes wait for the compiler's respell pairs.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_34 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 34u32, "2026-10-26T08:46Z", "x", "2026-10-26 03:0x x: CORRECTION to note 32's keyword counts (kit found them inflated by host-macro text). Recount over 2,520 .spi/.spir with $'' macros, plain and triple-quoted strings and // comments stripped (scratch keyword_census.ps1). Line-start word keywords (inl let open union nominal type instance prototype), code-only vs raw regex: spiral 28,216 vs 28,322; eoie 106 vs 3,112; tibia 4; alphabet 1; x, dice, fiscal, polyglot, blog 0. Flow keywords (if then else elif match with fun function): spiral 12,752 vs 14,968; eoie 11 vs 3,550; all others 0 (tibia's 78 and fiscal's 26 were Lua/host text). Cons (: spiral 226, eoie 113, blog 55, tibia 12. Raw !!!!: spiral 3,580, eoie 766, x 51 (0 once job-1792997503468 lands), tibia 23, polyglot 14, dice 4. blog's 55 Cons ( have no team item in the round yet.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_35 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 35u32, "2026-10-26T15:28Z", "main", "10-26 11:28 main: plan and rules for the compiler-samples respell, written before 5n installs (11:3x). The 06:06 dry run (job-1792998563870, GREEN: 1,248 of 1,251 files respelled, 0 errors, 0 word-round-trip differences, 9 formatter normalizations) was made on the compiler installed before 5m'. 5n changes the lexer (:: dcolon, macro-sigil respell, zero-width space), and respelling depends on the installed compiler and formatter, so that result is not reused. Steps, after install-5n reports its reviewed core: (1) rerun TEMP edition3-samples/dry.ps1 on the 5n compiler; it must be GREEN with 0 errors and 0 word-round-trip differences, and if the changed-file count differs from 1,248 by more than the 9 formatter files, read why before going on. (2) The apply writes about 1,257 files under apps/compiler/tmp/samples, which other lanes' matrix and gate jobs read, so it runs only inside an announced window, after messaging every lane, never during a live block. (3) A full matrix on the respelled samples. (4) Re-accept rule, written now: the respell moves 54,132 line lengths, so diagnostic columns in error samples' expected outputs shift. A DISAGREE row is re-accepted only when its new expected differs from the old one in column numbers alone (same file, line, error code and message text) and the same row agrees on both cores. Any other difference blocks the accept and is investigated. The accept itself follows the accept-autonomously rule: single-flight, reviewed rows, both cores DISAGREE 0, determinism check.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_36 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 36u32, "2026-10-26T15:31Z", "main", "10-26 11:31 main: correction to the previous note's rule (4), checked against the oracle at 11:3x. spiral-bin baseline/EXPECTED.tsv (7,353 rows) records compile, residual hash, native, exit and stdout hash. Its 510 compile-error rows carry only compile=error, with no message text and no residual. So diagnostic column shifts cannot show up in the matrix at all, and a column-only exception would only open a loophole. The rule becomes stricter: the respelled samples must reproduce EXPECTED with DISAGREE 0 on both cores, with no re-accept. Every DISAGREE is a real behavior change of the respell (e.g. generated code that embeds source text or positions), blocks the apply, and is investigated; the apply is rolled back from the dry run's original/ copies.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_37 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 37u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "main", "10-29 22:00 main, groom (WIP rule, 3 days with no note): Active -> Paused, progress kept at 65%. Last note 2026-10-26, before the 10-28 profile wipe interrupted every lane, and no live job. Resume when picked; it is not abandoned, and it keeps its priority P0.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_38 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 38u32, "2026-10-30T19:37Z", "compiler", "10-30 15:37 compiler: STEP (1) of the 10-26 compiler-samples plan is MET on today's compiler. The plan's TEMP edition3-samples/dry.ps1 was lost in the 10-28 wipe (the recovery folder holds 0 files), so its successor ran: i574n.github/scripts/respell-repo.ps1 -Name e3-samples -Root apps/compiler/tmp/samples -Compiler <installed pack 8, core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52> (box job job-1793388631493, 6 min, copies only). Result GREEN: 1,255 files, 1,252 respelled, errors 0, word round-trip differences 0, installed formatter normalizations 9 (5 named: inventory_indexed_model, mega_lean_cic main, mega_omniledger main + one negative, mega_spiral_proves main). Against the plan's rule ('if the changed count differs from 1,248 by more than the 9 formatter files, read why'): +4, inside the tolerance, and consistent with the samples added since 10-26 (e.g. rust_host_move_only_branch). NEXT, unchanged from the plan: (2) the apply writes about 1,252 files under apps/compiler/tmp/samples, so it needs an announced window with every lane told and no live matrix/gate jobs; (3) a full matrix on the respelled samples must reproduce EXPECTED (now 3D3409C99008220F, pack 8) with DISAGREE 0, with NO re-accept (n36's stricter rule); any DISAGREE rolls back from the dry run's original/ copies (%TEMP%\\respell-repo\\e3-samples\\original). Asked main for that window. If the dry-run copies go stale (a new compiler or sample change), rerun this dry run first.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_39 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 39u32, "2026-10-30T19:37Z", "main", "10-30 15:37 main: steps (2)+(3) SCHEDULED, with the rule fixed before the run. Slot: the next exclusive QUIET box slot after tibia's K4 window (tibia-k4-box, by ~17:55 at the latest), TONIGHT; if the user's TRAIN5 OK arrives first, TRAIN5 goes first and this moves to tomorrow. Quiet means no live matrix, gate, Cells or train job, because today's loaded gates gave 9 load-only reds that would muddy the read. PASS LINE (n36 rule): after compiler's apply of the ~1,252 respelled samples (from its 15:0x dry run with respell-repo.ps1: 1,255 files, 1,252 respelled, 0 errors, 0 word round-trip diffs, 9 formatter normalizations), the full -Suite all on installed pack 8 reproduces EXPECTED 3D3409C99008220F with DISAGREE 0 and NO re-accept. Anything else means a full rollback from the dry run's original/ copies plus a hash check of every restored file. The apply and the rollback are one compiler-prepared command; compiler takes a 90-min kit window when main announces the slot. FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS's HEAD redo follows (n71).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_40 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 40u32, "2026-10-30T20:25Z", "main", "10-30 16:25 main: e3 run 1 (job-1793389808307, run single-flight-20261030-155334) FAILED the pre-registered line and ROLLED BACK cleanly (1,255 restored, 0 hash mismatches, both windows released). Read: DISAGREE 0, timeouts 0, 7,382/7,385 parity; 3 NATIVE-DIFF, all [C]: dynamic_array_bounds_negative (the agreed UB noise) plus abi_external_buffer_length_negative and managed_string_invalid_utf8_slice. Both new rows have UNCHANGED generated hashes (ba105aa7a0009590, ea2685a8403f2fa5 = EXPECTED); only the exit went 3 -> -1073740791 (0xC0000409). Cause: the run's CC was scoop mingw 16.2.0 (gcc first on PATH) against the baseline's scoop gcc 15.2.0 (toolchain.tsv), the pin-spiral-cc trap. e3-run.ps1 pinned SPIRAL_FPC but not SPIRAL_CC. So the respell is NOT implicated. Rerun requested with SPIRAL_CC = scoop gcc 15.2.0, same pass line.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_41 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 41u32, "2026-10-30T21:18Z", "compiler", "10-30 17:18 compiler: COMPILER-SAMPLES RESPELL LANDED AND VERIFIED (steps 2+3 of the 10-26 plan), unstaged in apps/compiler/tmp/samples. Driver C:\\home\\data\\e3-samples\\e3-run.ps1 (job-1793392350746): durable snapshot + sha256 manifest of all 1,255 sample sources at C:\\home\\data\\e3-samples (rollback: e3-samples-window.ps1 -Rollback, hash-checked); respell-repo.ps1 -Apply on installed pack 8 (core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52) changed exactly the dry run's 1,252 files (incl. 9 formatter normalizations); then test.ps1 -Suite all -Native with SPIRAL_CC = scoop gcc 15.2 and SPIRAL_FPC = FPC 3.3.1 trunk (the baseline toolchain.tsv's compilers). Run single-flight-20261030-163636: 7,385 rows, compile timeouts 0, baseline parity 7,384, NATIVE-DIFF 1 (the agreed UB row dynamic_array_bounds_negative [C], residual 8264f723 unchanged), DISAGREE 0. VERDICT PASS by n36's stricter rule: EXPECTED 3D3409C99008220F reproduced row for row, NO re-accept. Every respelled sample compiles to the identical residual. History: the first attempt (16:00, run single-flight-20261030-155334) failed the same rule only because the wrapper hadn't pinned SPIRAL_CC (PATH gave mingw 16.2, so 2 C rows with unchanged residuals changed exit). It rolled back cleanly (1,255 files, 0 mismatches) and filed TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD. LEFT for this epic: the other repos' rounds (deps X/TIBIA/FISCAL/EOIE/LIB-EDITION3-ROUND, NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE); for FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS the lib respell (LIB-EDITION3-ROUND) still precedes the HEAD reformat (n71). The user reviews and commits the 1,252 respelled files (never committed by agents).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_42 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 42u32, "2026-10-30T21:18Z", "main", "10-30 17:18 main: steps (2)+(3) DONE, PASS on the pre-registered line. Rerun job-1793392350746 (run single-flight-20261030-163636), SPIRAL_CC = scoop gcc 15.2 and SPIRAL_FPC = trunk pinned: 7,385 rows; 7,384 baseline parity; 1 NATIVE-DIFF = the agreed UB row dynamic_array_bounds_negative [C] (residual 8264f723); DISAGREE 0; timeouts 0; no re-accept. EXPECTED 3D3409C99008220F reproduced. The 1,252 respelled sample sources STAY applied (unstaged, for the user's commit); the snapshot + sha256 manifest is at C:\\home\\data\\e3-samples. Context: it passed on a fully loaded box (fiscal's predicate chain and kit's build ran beside it after the windows were released), which supports the 10-30 rule that correctness runs don't need a quiet box. Run 1 failed only on the unpinned C toolchain (n40). Next: FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS's HEAD redo (n71), team compiler.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_43 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 43u32, "2026-10-31T20:02Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:01 compiler GROOM (user direction via /btw, 10-31 15:4x): the self-hosted rewrite (SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL) starts only after EVERY backend is SOTA: no memory problems, no Rc slowdowns, no union hacks, no recursion limits, no missing arithmetic; GADT bugs and conversion gaps are 'unacceptable by now'; edition 3 finishes first; Gleam is a top test target (abyssal codebases) with F#, Rust and Wasm; Cells as fast as F# projects. This item is now on that gate (priority -> P0, status -> Active).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_44 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 44u32, "2026-10-31T20:05Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:05 compiler (groom): user (10-31 15:4x): 'edition3 gotta finish also'. Gate for SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL, together with EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL and SPIRAL3-EDITIONS (both raised to P0 today).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_45 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 45u32, "2026-11-01T04:46Z", "main", "main 00:4x (user 11-01 00:2x: 'since we have backups we gotta stop waiting for windows for doing migrations, a lot of codebases have their styles pending to be changed to the new dialect, gotta push and push so we stop relying on things like the difuse'). Respell = SpiralCompiler format <dirs> --spelling symbols, which is formatter work with no compile and git as the backup, so a repo's respell needs no heavy window. Status per repo tonight: tibia respelled (cell budget 0 over, 9 Lua-in-macro autolinks left); fiscal re-derived its e3 respell (node proof job-1793506463392); x's sources show 0 findings, so they're already compliant; lib/spiral still dotted (511 autolinks in the Cells check), and lib is shared, so it goes through a lib land window with readers drained, as one land; kit, dice, alphabet, blog, i574n.github: not started. Order: each lane respells its own repo this round (CPU-light), lib lands next, then the dot-defusing in x's poster can go. Upstream core compatibility: the respell keeps '.' accepted (it's an alternate spelling), so upstream core still parses.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_46 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 46u32, "2026-11-01T05:12Z", "main", "main 01:1x RESPELL TRAP (tibia found it): format --spelling symbols also rewrites 'test' to ':#', so any script that finds test files with '^test ' silently matches none after a respell, and a gate that runs zero files passes vacuously (tibia's build.ps1 matched 0 of 56). Cells itself accepts both (accept.ex:93, memo.ex:400), and kit's sources are already respelled. Grep across repos found: spiral apps/cells/spi lib_sweep.ps1:8, ci_gate.ps1:10, lib_program_gate.ps1:39 (FIXED by main to '^(test|:#) ', parse-checked, probe on a respelled file matches); apps/compiler/scripts lib-usage-consumers.ps1:11/13 and lib-usage-census.ps1:47 (sent to compiler); x/apps/sim/build.ps1:114 (sent to x); tibia's fixed by tibia. RULE before any repo respell: grep the repo's scripts for '\\^test' and make them accept ':#'. A gate should also fail when it finds 0 test files.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_47 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 47u32, "2026-11-01T05:13Z", "main", "main 01:2x, trap widened (compiler found open -> ':<'): the respell maps every keyword with a symbol spelling, so any source-text regex anchored on a keyword goes blind. Sweep over every repo's .ps1/.ex/.exs/.py for anchored open/inl/let/type/union/nominal/prototype/instance. Already dual: Cells cells.ex:650, memo.ex:532/548, zed test-at-row.ps1, tibia arena/canary build.ps1, compiler lib-usage-census (fixed tonight). Keyword-only, sent to owners: compiler coverage-buckets.ps1:16 ('^\\s*union'), alias-count-check.ps1:11 ('^type '); fiscal sefaz candidate-gate.ps1:29 ('^inl xsd_table_'); kit renew-cold-rebuild.ps1:113 and migrate-native-rust.py:29/31; backlog parsers ('^inl note_of_', dangling-census.ps1:8) if the backlog state were ever respelled (kit: guard it or make kit agile the only parser). Rule: before a repo respell, grep its scripts for anchored keywords, not just '^test'. Better long-term: tools read Spiral through the compiler's tokens (format/parse_block) or KIT-RUN-SPI, never regexes; PS1-TO-SPIRAL removes this whole class.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_48 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 48u32, "2026-11-01T05:14Z", "main", "main 01:2x, correction to n47: compiler fixed coverage-buckets.ps1:16 ('(?m)^\\s*(?:union\\b|:\\|\\s)'). alias-count-check.ps1:11 is NOT affected: it reads the compiler's generated F# (.fsx), not Spiral source, so drop it from the sweep list. Lesson for the sweep: classify each hit by what the regex reads (Spiral source vs generated output vs tool logs) before calling it a trap.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_49 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 49u32, "2026-11-01T05:16Z", "main", "main 01:3x: kit side done. renew-cold-rebuild.ps1 takes '(?:inl|:=)' (tested both); migrate-native-rust.py had no caller, archived and removed (kit's .py count is now 0); dangling-census.ps1 accepts both. Biggest exposure: kit agile's own state parsers key on 'inl ' at 251 sites in 69 files, so a respelled agile.spi would blind the backlog tool for every lane. Guard filed: KIT-STATE-SPELLING-GUARD (P0: check and write preflights refuse a respelled state, plus 'kit agile unspell'). Formatter side sent to compiler: skip state modules on --spelling, or honor a '///- --no-respell' header (kit's preference).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_50 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 50u32, "2026-11-01T06:49Z", "main", "main 02:4x LIB RESPELL MEASURED on a scratch copy (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\scratch\\lib-respell; live lib untouched): 'format <lib> --spelling symbols' rewrote 98 of 114 files in 60 s, exit 0, no errors. Cell-budget check before -> after: autolink 511 -> 116, mention 151 -> 97, hashtag 60 -> 52, cashtag 63 -> 59, over_budget 1187 -> 1177. The 116 left are mostly host text inside macros, which the respell correctly leaves alone (benchmark.run x15, listm.map x11, solutions.map x8, optionm.map x7, spiral_io_threaded.io x6, calendar.Date x5), so those need macro-side renames or granular Spiral instead of host text (GRANULAR-STATS). Before landing lib's respell: the '^test'/'^open' script traps are fixed in spiral (n46-n48), and fiscal's sefaz gate is still open; land as one lib window with readers drained.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_51 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 51u32, "2026-11-01T12:04Z", "main", "main 08:1x, compiler lane map anchor (SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL n19): two new items from DIRECTION-1031 belong to this theme and stay separate only because each has its own definition of done: SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION (one .spi, real/~> per statement, 13 acceptance tests) and SPELLING-PROFILES (Words/Symbols as bijective data profiles, corpus round-trip in CI).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_52 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 52u32, "2026-11-01T13:17Z", "main", "main 08:5x: a real edition-3 codegen bug blocks fiscal's respell: EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN (P0, team:compiler, routed to compiler 08:5x). Rust emits 'st = Group94::M97(v6, v10);' without 'let' only under edition 3 (rustc E0425); fiscal's resolves_* tests pass in edition 2. Every repo respell should run its Rust tests under edition 3 before landing, which is how fiscal caught it.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_53 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 53u32, "2026-11-01T13:23Z", "main", "main 09:0x CORRECTION to n52: EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN is not an edition-3 bug. compiler's root cause: a PACK-12 regression, where the mutual-tail group loops leaked their 'inside a group' state into methods first emitted from a group body, so a tail call became 'st = GroupN::M..(..)' in a function with no 'st' (rustc E0425). Edition 3 only changes emission order, which is why it showed up there. The fix is pack14a (apps/compiler/packs/pack14/1-group-loop-scope.kitdo). The rule from n52 still stands: run a repo's Rust tests after a respell.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_54 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 54u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler, R5 children: EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL (pick :> for the entry, plus the census of hardcoded English words) and EDITION3-SAMPLES-RESPELL (compiler samples/tests destructive respell under trap checks).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_55 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 55u32, "2026-11-01T14:47Z", "main", "main 10:4x LIB RESPELL LANDING (user 11-01: 'since we have backups we gotta stop slacking in all destructive migrations'). Fresh copy respelled with 'format --spelling symbols': 98 files changed, 0 format errors; landing through lib_land_window with all 98 drafts and their base hashes (refuses any file a lane changed since; close = 14 signatures + document_test + type_probe; undo on red). Started 10:43, waiting on live lib readers. The '.' spelling stays accepted, so consumers that still use it keep compiling. The trap fixes (n46-n49) are in for spiral's scripts. Result note follows.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_56 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 56u32, "2026-11-01T15:19Z", "main", "main 11:2x: the lib respell land did NOT happen; it gave up after 30 min, touching nothing ('live lib readers still present'). The readers were MAIN's own hung 'gh codespace ssh' sessions from codespace attempts 1-2: their command lines contain 'spiral' and 'lib_gate', and they outlived both the codespaces (Shutdown) and the stopped background tasks. Stopped 11:18 (verified own by command line; 0 left). Retry plan: after compiler lands its convert.spi guard (ZIG-EXPECTED-SEMICOLON-REGRESSION), respell a FRESH lib copy (convert.spi's base changes) and land again with the trap checks; consumer builds (apps/spiral, x, tibia, fiscal) must be part of the check this time (lesson from CONVERT-ZIG-UNATIVEINT n9).")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_57 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 57u32, "2026-11-01T15:50Z", "main", "main 12:0x LIB RESPELL ATTEMPT 2: closed RED and undid itself cleanly (lib restored; the only lib diff left is compiler's unstaged convert.spi guard). Close steps: signatures 2 'changed' (spelling only: resultm.result' -> resultm::result'), consumers OK (apps/spiral compiles), document_test 22/22, type_probe FAIL 10 of 95 modules. ROOT CAUSE, a respell bug: the respeller rewrites module paths in open statements (':< rust.rust_operators' -> ':< rust::rust_operators'), which open doesn't resolve, so everything the open brings in goes unbound (leptos/ui/toggle.spi: event, label, attr_fn; 18 errors; text_input 7). Sent to compiler with the repro copy (scratch lib-respell3). BLOCKED until the respeller leaves open paths dotted or open accepts '::'. The trap list from n46-n49 grows: open paths. Lesson: the land window's undo did its job; landing destructive migrations through it is safe.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_58 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 58u32, "2026-11-01T15:58Z", "main", "main 12:1x CORRECTION to n57: the 'respell bug in open paths' diagnosis was WRONG. compiler showed (a) putting ':< rust::rust_operators' back to the dotted form gives identical errors, (b) '::' between open path segments already parses (the lexer makes '::x' the same token as '.x'), (c) the LIVE, un-respelled lib already fails type_probe on 22 of 23 leptos/ui + leptos/svg modules. The 10 red modules were pre-existing failures that the land had to probe because the respell touched them. I blamed the change without checking the baseline. compiler made lib_land_window's type_probe close baseline-aware (only NEW failures block; pre-existing ones print as 'already failed before this land, not blocking') and filed LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED for the 22. Rerunning the land now.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_59 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 59u32, "2026-11-01T18:56Z", "main", "main 11-01 14:53 LIB RESPELLED TO :: AND LANDED GREEN (attempt 5; 98 files from %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\scratch\\lib-respell3, each guarded by its base hash). It waited for kit-TRAIN7c's notebook readers to clear (13:41), then the close ran 72 min: signatures 14 unchanged (the spelling-normalized compare from attempt 3's fix), consumer apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe 85/95 with the same 10 leptos/ui failures as before (LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED), no new ones. Undo: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-132117. Tool defect found and fixed: the tree-write window was a fixed 30 min and expired 40 min before the close ended, so another lane could have written lib mid-close. lib_land_window.ps1 now sizes it at 45 + 10 per 10 files (98 files -> 145 min). Next: lanes re-base any lib-derived drafts and anchors (anchors-stale-across-respell), then tibia/fiscal/x/kit consumers confirm green on their next gate.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_60 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 60u32, "2026-11-01T22:26Z", "fiscal", "fiscal consumer proof 11-01 (node t1101 synced to box spiral 504e1e07, lib confirmed :: spelled, compiler core DBC5EC18F14C, job-1793562713871): GREEN. src canon 1/1, corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4, corpus_checks 26/26 (one apparent red traced to a stale mirror copy pinning 23; the box file pins 24, which CI confirms), generator 23/23 (16:37-18:22). Regeneration: 81 units, 0 changed, so generated units are byte-identical under the :: lib. The edition-2 consumer generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 passes 2/2. x-compat 0 everywhere. No red traces to the respell.")
inl note_of_edition3_symbols_migration_61 () = Note ("EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", 61u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (33 h; last note fiscal, consumer proof green). Owner compiler. Next: list the repos and sources still on edition-2 symbols and pick the next respell.")
