inl note_of_x_done_85 () = Note ("X-DONE", 85u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "x", "2026-11-01 08:03 x: LANE INVENTORY for merging the incoming batch (user 11-01 08:0x: main is reading an external conversation that will bring many items; match new items against these clusters before filing). 34 open x items:\nA. IN FLIGHT, proof running (verify46, job-1793529002122): X-RESPELL-SYMBOLS 70 (test -> :#, 72 files), LIST-SUGAR-DRIFT-GUARD 40 (x share applied; kit share + formatter rule open), SIM-X-FEATURE-PARITY 95 (lands with verify46), PS1-TO-SPIRAL port 2, first half (e2e defaults to the sim), X-RUN-METRICS 85 (baseline run 3 pending; raw-pair rows live), BEAM-GUARD-ALL-INVOCATIONS 35 (x's launchers guarded; the box-wide cap is resilience's).\nB. MORNING LAND WINDOW, runbook ready (CELLS-TYPED-DIRECTIVES n5): CELLS-SPI-LIB 80 + CELLS-TYPED-DIRECTIVES 85 (+ cell.wrap typed).\nC. CELLS-IN-SPIRAL epic 10: main's slices CELLS-DOCUMENT-TYPED, CELLS-MANIFEST-SOURCEMAP-SPIRAL, CELL-BUDGET-NAMING 80 (main), CELLS-XCOMPAT/CELL-BUDGET-SPIRAL (main). Cells census and backend map: CELLS-CENSUS (Done) n2/n3.\nD. POSTABILITY / CELL BUDGET: POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE 70 (TLD generator deferred), POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS 45 (xc postable census: design + census.spi draft), ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME (x share decided n5).\nE. GENERATED SIZE / BUILD UNITS: X-HAND-UNITS 60 (resume FIRED: Gleam parts 945/954 of 1000), GLEAM-PARTS-EMIT (compiler-side alternative), X-PARALLEL-BUILD, X-PARALLEL-CENSUS (Blocked on HAND-UNITS), GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE, RUST-UNUSED-PATTERN-CLONES, X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP 40 (decoder-hoist rule n11), X-FAILURE-TEXT-DEDUP (Paused with a written condition), X-LAMBDA-PARENS.\nF. SPEED / BACKENDS: X-PRECOMMIT-SPEED 70 (notebooks are ~48 of 61 CI min, serial with cold compilers), X-BACKEND-SWITCHES (re-scoped Gleam vs Rust), BACKEND-BALANCE 80, GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT 55.\nG. WAITING ON THE USER: X-DONE 90, X-CLIENT 98 (x-api.env), X-REPO-TEMPLATE 82, CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS 90. SOCIAL-PROFILES-LOCAL 95 moved to Active today (its user step is met; it closes on an all-green CI, and windows only had a hex.pm outage).\nH. CROSS-TEAM EPICS (x's part done): GRANULAR-HEAL, CELLS-EVERYWHERE, DATA-DIR-HOME.\nI. USER-DEFERRED (Paused until the user starts NEAR work): X-ON-NEAR, NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW, X-FEDERATION-BRIDGES, X-NEAR-PROVENANCE.\nMerge rule for the batch: a new item that names a cluster's subject becomes a note or a child there, never a parallel item (tonight's X-CI-NOTEBOOK-SPEED duplicate of F is the counter-example). Typefeatureset and Gleam/Rust balance apply to every new slice (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCE n6, BACKEND-BALANCE).")
inl note_of_x_done_86 () = Note ("X-DONE", 86u32, "2026-11-01T17:13Z", "x", "2026-11-01 13:13 x: CI has been red since 08a49e2, also bcbca2d, on both OSes, with \"No .NET 11 SDK found\" at spiral apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1:84 under apps/sim/build.ps1. Cause: 08a49e2 put sim's build ahead of client's. Sim resolved .NET and the compiler DLL itself, while client's BuildSpiral goes through lib.ps1 Ensure-SpiralCompiler, which installs .NET 11 and builds the DLL when either is missing. So sim worked only while client ran first. Fix (unstaged): apps/sim/build.ps1 dot-sources spiral lib.ps1 and calls Ensure-SpiralCompiler, keeping Get-SpiralPackageDir from env.ps1. Box smoke test: same dotnet and DLL paths. Proof: the next push's ci run. Lesson: reordering build steps can drop provisioning that an earlier step did implicitly. Also, I missed 08a49e2's red run when it happened; verify-ci-after-user-push now applies to every push.")
inl note_of_x_done_87 () = Note ("X-DONE", 87u32, "2026-11-01T18:25Z", "x", "2026-11-01 14:25 x: JUNK TRIAGE under the narrowed drafts rule (11-01 14:0x). Each committed x file that might be junk got a deliberate decision.\nARCHIVED (kit archive 20261101-142407, unstaged deletes): scripts/cargo-profile-{bench,cpu,runtime}.ps1, whose item X-CARGO-BUILD-PROFILE is Done and whose verdict and method are in n1/n8, and scripts/gleam-compact-census.ps1, whose item GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT is Done and whose method is in n6. Nothing references any of them outside backlog notes.\nKEPT UNDER LIVE ITEMS: postability/tlds.txt and postability/x.json (POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE, x's DoD in n19); scripts/postable-report.ps1 (CELLS-IN-SPIRAL S2/S3 census); apps/client/e2e/stub.ps1, stub_http.ps1 and scripts/e2e-parity.ps1 (S1, unblocked); apps/client/e2e/social_stub.ps1 (S4).\nKEPT AS FIXTURE OR GLUE: e2e/links.md (the post-thread dry-run input in the README tutorial), plus the build, verify, workflow, gate, node-run, sim-run and sim-shell glue.\nDRAFTS STORE: spiral\\CELLS-TYPED-DIRECTIVES keeps the applier and 3 .spi files. They replace live spiral/apps/cells files under main's churn, so they wait for the land window. Its 2 discriminate*.ps1 probes are archived (the bug is fixed with a helper).")
inl note_of_x_done_88 () = Note ("X-DONE", 88u32, "2026-11-01T23:32Z", "x", "2026-11-01 19:32 x: CI RED AGAIN on 837a84b (the user's 17:12 commit of x's day). X-DONE n86's .NET fix WORKED (the sim build now runs), and a NEW red follows: 'x/apps/sim/spi / cell-budget report: 5 finding(s) in 30 file(s) (autolink 5)' -> CELL-BUDGET throw. Cause: Cells' cell_budget (73e4d863) now reports AUTOLINK findings, domain-like tokens such as tweet.read, xsim.world and the test input \"go x.com now\". Measured on the node against spiral b3fd292b: sim 5 and client 15 (defuse/posted/reading/splitter test inputs, wire app.bsky.feed.post, e2e.bsky.social handles). Cells exits 0 on them, since only over_budget fails (CELL-BUDGET-NAMING n2), and cell_weight already charges each link 23. x's Assert-CellBudget was stricter, failing on ANY finding, because when it was written over_budget was the only kind. FIX (unstaged, scripts/common.ps1): fail on a nonzero exit or an 'over_budget N' kind, and print other kinds as 'advisory only', since x's own splitter defuses these dots when it posts (posted_as on_x -> defused_dots_by). PROOF x-budget-advisory1 (node), rule written before the run: client and sim PASS with advisory lines, and a scratch tree with one over-budget definition THROWS 'over budget'.")
inl note_of_x_done_89 () = Note ("X-DONE", 89u32, "2026-11-01T23:40Z", "x", "2026-11-01 19:40 x: x-budget-advisory1 (node, 339 s, spiral b3fd292b) by n88's rule: PASS. The client prints 'advisory only: cell-budget report: 15 finding(s) in 43 file(s) (autolink 15)' and passes, and the sim prints its 5 and passes. A scratch tree with one 480-weight definition prints 'over_budget: weight 480 > 273' and '(over_budget 1)' and THROWS 'over budget (exit 1)'. So the gate fails exactly where Cells does. scripts/common.ps1 is unstaged and ready for the user's commit, and that push's CI is the end-to-end proof (the build runs past the cell budget into the sim notebooks for the first time since 08a49e2). The 20 autolinks themselves are a postability-quality follow-up: spell the domain-like test inputs by concatenation and rename the xsim.world/xsim.events labels, after x-verify47's outputs land so no sim source moves under its manifest.")
inl note_of_x_done_90 () = Note ("X-DONE", 90u32, "2026-11-02T02:23Z", "x", "2026-11-01 22:23 x: CI on 4b27709 (the user's 20:19 commit of the advisory gate + sim_run header): the SIM BUILD 2026-11-01 22:23 PASSES in CI. The cell budget is advisory as designed, and the sim notebooks ran, so the 08a49e2/bcbca2d/837a84b chain of reds is cleared up to the client. The next red is the client gate (scripts/gate.ps1 -Enforce): the COMMITTED splitter.spi is the record-of-closures design, whose posted/weights/chunks generate 1211/1297/1549 Rust lines (X-SOTA-MODEL n9). The fix is the unstaged V3 splitter (555/764/583, x-platform-size3), now inside x-verify48b. Expected after the user commits splitter.spi + sim_serve.spi + simframes.spi + the staged headers: CI passes the client gate and reaches e2e.")
inl note_of_x_done_91 () = Note ("X-DONE", 91u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:13 x: GROOM (user 11-04 00:1x via main). Stays Blocked at 90. D1 needs two consecutive green CI runs on a pushed tree, and the user said 11-04 they won't commit for now (no asks). When a commit appears, x checks and heals CI; until then x keeps accumulating finished items. Blocker: the next user commit; owner x.")
