inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_1 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 1u32, "2026-10-21T11:01Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 07:01 eoie team: state at 07:00. The hook script was rewritten at 06:59:55 (not by eoie): 13 lines, no sleep loop, exits 0 when stop_hook_active, a global disarm file ~/.claude/autonomous/disarmed, immediate block with a fixed reason. Still open: (3) settings.json hooks.Stop timeout is 600 s; a few seconds would cap any regression. That is the user's config, so I left it for the user rather than changing it on a peer relay. (4/5) arm/disarm as an eoie verb with a test notebook, so the gate is dogfooded. eoie's own session file was removed at the deadline.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_2 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 2u32, "2026-10-21T11:01Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 07:01 eoie team: duplicate of AUTONOMOUS-STOP-GATE (main lane owns the hook and says nothing is needed from eoie). Paused here; an eoie arm/disarm verb would only come back if main asks for it.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_3 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 3u32, "2026-10-25T06:05Z", "fork-git", "fork-git team, 2026-10-25 02:1x: the light list (autonomous-gate.ps1:160-166) reads only C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\docs\\backlog with --team <team>, so a team whose items live in a repo-local eoie root (fork-spiral-patch/docs/backlog holds FORK-SPIRAL and FORK-SPIRAL-SPI, moved there at the user request) always gets an empty list and a generic take-the-next-one block. Second trap: team names are matched as backlog tags, so registering 84b53718=fork handed this session UPSTREAM-FORK-START (tag fork, a main item about the language fork) until the team was renamed fork-git. For the eoie verb: read the session team light list from every registered root (agile roots) or a root named next to the team in standing.txt, and reject a team name that already tags another team items.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_4 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 4u32, "2026-10-29T22:32Z", "main", "10-29 18:3x main: PROVISIONAL fields filled while the item is Blocked or Paused (fill-all-task-fields): estimate 120m (D-base rule: base(D3) x (1 - 0%)); load light (default); assignee agent (default). The owner corrects them on resume.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_5 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 5u32, "2026-11-01T03:38Z", "kit", "10-31 23:4x kit groom, Paused P1 re-decided: STAYS PAUSED. Reason: duplicate of main's AUTONOMOUS-STOP-GATE; the hook is main's and works (kit edited it 10-31 for wake sources and the Paused P0/P1 line). Resume condition (event): PS1-TO-SPIRAL reaches its hooks step (hook logic as kit verbs instead of pwsh), or main asks for 'kit autonomous arm|disarm|gate'.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_6 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 6u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit: resume condition met in part: the gate logic now has a typed home (agile_cadence idle_verdict, KIT-GROOM-ROUND n4 spec). Stays Paused until the 3-verdict model is node-proven; then this item becomes the verb wiring (kit groom gate) and KIT-GROOM-ROUND keeps the model.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_7 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 7u32, "2026-11-01T20:12Z", "kit", "11-01 16:12 kit RE-DECIDED (stop gate ask): resume -> Planned. The resume condition is met: the 3-verdict gate model (agile_cadence gate_verdict: PullItem|KeepWaiting|MayStop, anti-spin) passed 6/6 on the node and was green in TRAIN7c's 56/56 notebooks (installed A25B8FBD). This item is now the verb wiring: kit groom gate <root> --team t, read by autonomous-gate.ps1 instead of its own list logic.")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_8 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 8u32, "2026-11-06T11:25Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-AUTONOMOUS-GATE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_autonomous_gate_9 () = Note ("KIT-AUTONOMOUS-GATE", 9u32, "2026-11-09T06:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:0x local rig, requirements from tonight's live hook work (GATE-ROTATE-PAST-STUCK, Done) for the verb that replaces the PowerShell hook's list logic: (1) TEAM IDENTITY: the hook mapped sessions to teams by a hand file (autonomous/teams.txt) that went stale at the 11-08 renames (kit, main, x, resilience matched 0 ready items, so those lanes were offered an EMPTY list all night); the verb resolves team from lane aliases (lane-aliases.txt already maps rig=kit) instead. (2) ROTATION and SPLIT-ME are now hook state (gate-stamps/<session>.offers.json, .split.txt); the verb owns them as typed state (offer record { item; reason : TopReady | Rotated | NoneLeft }, split hint per over-240 m item). (3) BUDGET: the hook calls agile list --json and agile next in parallel under a 15 s cap; on a 9.9 MB state next takes 4.8-8.4 s and list 6.4 s, so under load the hook timed out and printed no items (seen tonight); one in-process verb parses the state once, so it fits the cap. (4) PAUSED re-decide line and the box-CPU line stay. Code for TRAIN43; the hook stays until the verb ships.")
