inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 1u32, "2026-10-21T13:16Z", "main", "2026-10-21 09:16 main: two variants staged in the scratchpad; the gate is sefaz-shared-chain.ps1 -Variant <file> (restores the accepted DFA generator 240C6A248B819314 on red). Variant 1, generator.shared.spi: one state function per distinct pattern, 128-state cap. Variant 2, generator.shared512.spi (15CCDE51F60A7723): the same with a 512-state cap, so all 196 patterns are direct-coded, including the 7 QR-code ones (max 494). Accept rule, fixed before measuring: family gate 17/17 and 13 examples at 0 .NET messages; the generated total under run 7's 11,081 KB for variant 1; for variant 2, at most variant 1's total + 15%, and no Cells VM above 16 GB private (MACHINE-WATCH hog line). Order: variant 1, then variant 2, after tibia's PR-17 and PR-18 blocks (about 13:30).")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 2u32, "2026-10-21T17:42Z", "main", "13:42 variant 1 (generator.shared.spi, 3837A07766BC5B79) accepted by the pre-written rule: family gates 17/17 green, 13 examples at 0 .NET validation messages, generated total 10,098 KB (< 11,081 KB, -9%). Job main-sefaz-shared-v1 took 73 min in total. The accepted generator and generated modules are saved in scratchpad sefaz-v1-accepted; a red variant 2 now restores those (the chain's -Fallback). Variant 2 (generator.shared512.spi) runs next, after the sm'.spi lib gate in the same job (they share MIX_BUILD_PATH), with a sampler for the Cells VM private-memory peak.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 3u32, "2026-10-21T18:14Z", "main", "14:14 variant 2 (generator.shared512.spi, 512-state cap) rejected by the pre-written memory rule: 10 min into its family gates, its Cells VM (erl 120700, job main-libgate-sefaz-v2) reached 21,875 MB private (> 16 GB) with 443 MB free, and Claude Code reaped two of my idle watchers. I stopped the job (eoie job stop), the VM was gone after 5 s, and free memory recovered to 8.2 GB. The lab was restored from sefaz-v1-accepted (generator 3837A07766BC5B79, 10,098 KB, 0 files differing). Variant 1 stays. The 7 patterns over 128 states must not be direct-coded at 494 states: next is a table-driven DFA for those 7 (part 2 of this item). Lessons: the chain's peak sampler matched erl by session id and missed this VM (it saw 71 MB), so the cap must follow the job tree, and the 16 GB rule should be enforced inside the chain (stop at 16 GB) instead of read afterwards.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 4u32, "2026-10-21T18:18Z", "main", "14:18 variant 3 staged (part 2: the 7 patterns over 128 states): scratchpad xsd_regex.table.spi adds dfa_table (records = per state an accept char, a 6-hex move count and moves as 6-hex low/high/target; offsets = 6 hex per state) with table_matches and the encoder dfa_table_of, plus tests table_matches_like_dotnet_on_every_probe (all 196 patterns) and table_keeps_xsd_semantics. generator.table.spi = variant 1 + for DFAs over 128 states (within 4096) an inl xsd_table_<fnv>_<len> constant checked with xsd_regex.table_matches, with the derivative matcher only when no DFA exists. Job sefaz-table-job.ps1 runs the chain under lab/MACHINE-WATCH/memory-cap.ps1, which sums private memory over the chain's descendant tree and stops that tree above 16,000 MB (smoke-tested: capped a 335 MB tree at 200 MB). Accept rule, fixed before measuring: 17/17 green incl. both new tests, 13 examples at 0 messages, generated total <= 10,098 KB x 1.15 = 11,613 KB, never capped, and the generated modules have no xsd_regex.pattern_matches left (all 196 patterns DFA-backed). Red or capped: back to sefaz-v1-accepted (now also holds xsd_regex.spi 0A7681A0543F2709). Order: after the night-pack install + review and the control-workers rerun (WSJF: x is blocked on the install).")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 5u32, "2026-10-22T00:42Z", "main", "20:42 pre-gate code review of variant 3 (scratchpad xsd_regex.table.spi lines 288-452, read only): correctness holds by construction. table_target's early exit (c below a move's low gives -1) needs each state's moves ascending and disjoint: interval_starts starts from [0] and insert_point keeps the starts sorted and unique, state_moves walks them in order with high = next start - 1, add_move only merges adjacent ranges with the same target, and reverse_moves restores ascending order; the list matcher move_target uses the same exit, so table and list agree by design (and the 196-pattern .NET test checks it). Start state = index 0 = the compiled pattern (build_states 0 [r] 1). 6-hex fields cover code points to 0x10FFFF and record offsets to 16.7M chars; the encoder writes lowercase and table_hex_value reads only lowercase, consistent. Performance risks for the gated run, not bugs: state_index is a linear rx_compare scan and with_state appends at the end, so building n states is O(n^2) structural compares (16M at the 4096 cap); table_of_rows and table_moves_text build records with ++# appends, quadratic in the record length (fine at about 500 states, about 1.5M chars near the cap). If the gate is slow, a map from rx to index and a list-then-concat encoder are the fixes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 6u32, "2026-10-22T06:12Z", "main", "02:12 main: variant 3 (DFA tables for the 7 patterns over 128 states) moved out of my session scratchpad, which would have lost it at session end, into the sefaz repo. C:\\home\\git\\sefaz\\candidates\\dfa-table\\{generator.spi, xsd_regex.spi} hold scratchpad generator.table.spi and xsd_regex.table.spi with the lab paths rewritten. The rewrite mapping (lab corpus/ to deps/corpus/, generated/ and samples/ to the repo folders, everything else to src/) reproduces all 15 files of sefaz/src from the scratchpad's accepted-v1 snapshot byte for byte, so sefaz/src IS the accepted v1 and the snapshot is redundant. The chain became one gate, sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1 -Candidate <dir>. It snapshots src/*.spi to TEMP, copies the candidate modules in, and runs family-gates.ps1 under apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/memory-cap.ps1 (16,000 MB). It passes only with >= 17 green modules, 0 validation messages and no cap, and restores the snapshot otherwise. The accept rule of note 14:18 is unchanged; it adds 'generated total <= 11,613 KB' and 'derivative fallbacks left 0', which the gate prints. Run: candidate-gate.ps1 -Candidate candidates\\dfa-table as a heavy job when the machine has room (not tonight: free memory is about 3 GB with 2 heavy jobs; tibia live block 05:30-06:30). Superseded scratchpad variants (orig, dfa, next, shared, shared512) are recorded in notes 10-20 and 10-21.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 7u32, "2026-10-22T15:49Z", "main", "2026-10-22 11:49 main: reconciled with today's FISCAL-GENERIC table work, one record per fact. Two table encodings existed: this item's variant 3 (fiscal/candidates/dfa-table: records + offsets strings, 6-hex fields, dfa_table record type) and today's self-indexing format (lib-xsd copy xsd_regex: dfa_table_text, one string whose move targets are the character offsets of their state lines, plus table_matches, also used for the value-set catalogs via dfa_of_values). Rule, fixed before choosing: keep the encoding with fewer moving parts that serves both uses. That is today's (one string, no separate offset table, no record type), and generator.spi already emits it for patterns between 128 and 4096 states (part 2 of this item). Variant 3's strong part, its test, is ported: fiscal corpus_checks gains table_matches_like_dotnet_on_every_probe (all 196 corpus patterns through dfa_of_pattern -> dfa_table_text -> table_matches against .NET's expected rows). Part 1 (one state function per distinct pattern per module) is already in fiscal/src, since unique_emitted dedupes the hash-named functions. The accept rule of 10-21 14:18 carries over to the fiscal regen after the lib landing: 17/17 green, 0 validation messages, generated total <= 11,613 KB, no xsd_regex.pattern_matches left. fiscal/candidates/dfa-table is retired once the new format lands and passes that rule; it stays as reference until then.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 8u32, "2026-10-25T15:30Z", "fiscal", "11:29 fiscal: the 10-22 20:42 performance risk is real and worse than O(n^2). parse_quant unrolls {n,m} into repeat_n + optional_chain, a chain m nodes long, so every DFA state is an O(m) regex and every rx_compare in the linear state_index scan walks O(m) of shared suffix: building R{1,m} is O(m^3). Measured with a faithful Python mirror of build_states (session scratchpad xsd-regex-repeat/mirror.py): compare steps grow 8x per doubling of m unrolled, 4x with a counted node; for FatturaPA's [\\p{IsBasicLatin}\\p{IsLatin-1Supplement}]{1,1000} that projects to 1.2e10 steps unrolled vs 9e6 counted. Second defect found on the way: \\p{...} block escapes are not parsed (escape_ranges 'p' is a literal p), so that class became the ~18 literal characters of 'p{IsBasicLatin}p{IsLatin-1Supplement}' and FatturaPA's validators reject ordinary text such as 'Mario Rossi'; the BR census (FISCAL-APP n5) had 0 \\p, and patterns.txt holds only BR patterns, so no oracle saw it (FISCAL-PATTERN-ORACLE-FAMILIES). Fix drafted as lib slice xsd-regex-repeat/apply.py (base AB61AE5FA83FDCA5): RxRepeat (atom, low, high) with derivative d(R)R{low-1,high-1} through a counted smart constructor (high <= 0 -> eps, {1,1} -> atom; no nullable normalization, so example_with output is unchanged); {n} and {n,m} go through it, {n,} = R{n,n}R*; block escapes IsBasicLatin, IsLatin-1Supplement, IsLatinExtended-A/B, \\P negated, unknown names fail to compile; tests block_escapes_read_code_point_ranges and bounded_repeats_build_one_state_per_count ({1,1000} -> 1001 states). Differential before compiling (differential.py): 400 random patterns incl. nullable atoms under bounded counts x 255 probes vs Python re, 0 disagreements. Gate job-1792941953660-fiscal-lib-gate-xsd-2. Accept rule, fixed now: xsd_regex tests green AND fiscal corpus_checks' 5 .NET pattern tests (196 BR patterns, derivative + DFA + table) at 0 disagreements against the patched lib -> land with reader guard AB61AE5FA83FDCA5.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 9u32, "2026-10-25T18:00Z", "fiscal", "13:59 fiscal: XSD-SLICES LANDED in the tree lib by job-1792950895715 (kit land.ps1 + the staged apply): xsd_regex 528907A279636CC1, xsd_emit 5C364F8DA3287371, xsd_resolve 170A91102936C86C, xsd 5CF595CEF83FE12C, byte-identical to the GREEN candidate (the kit's post-land format was a no-op). The lib now has: counted RxRepeat + XSD block escapes (xsd_regex); match-based enumerations, URI case names and list sugar in emitted code (xsd_emit); namespace-qualified type names with collision tags (xsd_resolve); parenthesized tuple-slot list patterns (xsd); tests interleaved. The same job then applied fiscal-post-land (271-pattern oracle derived from deps, KSeF known_defect None, gitignore and README) and is waiting for a test-suite window for the full fiscal build, which checks KSeF's example: it must now pass with no pin.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 10u32, "2026-10-27T07:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:30 fiscal: estimate set to 390m remaining, from its two milestones: the counted RxRepeat and block escapes landed (XSD-SLICES, note of 10-25 14:00), so what remains is (1) one direct-coded state function per distinct pattern per module: the staged generator.shared.spi predates today's landings and must be re-derived on the live tree, then gated (family gates + examples at 0 + module sizes) 150m; (2) the 7 patterns over 128 states (NF-e QR-code URLs, up to 494 states) get a table-driven DFA: design, implementation, tests against the 271-pattern oracle 240m.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 11u32, "2026-10-30T15:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:09 fiscal: GROOM R3 (silent >= 3 d): Active -> Paused, progress kept. The design stands, but its code changes the generator/emitter, whose text the edition-3 respell is about to change (FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, draft proving on e3lv). Rule anchors-stale-across-respell: land the respell first, then write against the respelled tree. Dep added: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND; resume (Active) when that lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 12u32, "2026-10-31T23:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 19:09 fiscal: RE-DECIDED: stays Paused. REASON (true today): its remaining steps rewrite generator/emitter output, which FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (95%, held behind EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL) will respell; writing against the pre-respell tree stales every anchor. RESUME CONDITION: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND reaches Done; then resume as Planned and re-derive the shared-state-function step on the respelled live tree.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 13u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:51 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). MEASURED 11-01: shared DFA pattern functions are the largest repeated code in generated/ (xsd_pattern_f653e85e_247 206 lines x 14 units, xsd_pattern_f009c066_169 145 x 16, ...; part of the 453k repeated lines). DONE WHEN: every distinct pattern is emitted once (a shared patterns module per schema system) and units import it; repeated xsd_pattern_* lines across units = 0; the pattern oracle tests stay at 0 disagreements; rustc time of the 4 CT-e units is reported before/after. NEXT STEP: merge with FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES' shared-module mechanism (same module_package dependencies), patterns first because they are content-addressed already (xsd_pattern_<hash>). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a pattern is identified by its content hash (a nominal \":! pattern_id = string\" from the hash), so two units can never emit diverging copies of the same pattern; the certified table (XSD-CERTIFIED-MATCHER) is the pattern's only implementation.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 14u32, "2026-11-03T22:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:47 fiscal: RE-DECIDED: Paused -> Planned. The recorded resume condition is MET (FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND Done since 11-01 14:4x; the live xsd_emit is edition 3 and today carries group_part + nominal records, both landed through lib_land_window). ORDER: every step here rewrites every generated unit, so it starts after XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES lands (codec proof job-1793743680574-fiscal-codec is running) and before XSD-DECODE-RESULT, one emitter change per regen so drifts never compound. Anchors must be re-derived on the live xsd_emit E9BDA3EE (or its codec successor), not on the 10-31 notes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 15u32, "2026-11-04T00:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 20:49 fiscal: ANCHORS RE-DERIVED on the live xsd_emit 5E485076 (after group_part, nominal and codec landed): pattern_function_name :361-362 ('xsd_pattern_' ++ fnv hex of the pattern ++ '_' ++ its length: already content-addressed, the plan's pattern_id); pattern_checks :464 is where every unit gets its own copy: a direct-coded DFA becomes an 'emitted' item (state function + certificate_item, :469-480), otherwise a table string '<name>_table' (:484-500), each added to acc::functions of THAT unit. The shared-module step therefore changes exactly these two branches: emit the item once into a per-schema-system patterns module (keyed by pattern_function_name) and leave only the reference in the unit, plus a module dependency in the unit's package.spiproj (the generator writes those; see FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES' module_package mechanism). Order unchanged: next emitter change after the codec land, one regen proof.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 16u32, "2026-11-07T15:53Z", "fiscal", "11-07 groom DoD (restating the 11-01 DONE WHEN as the marker): one direct-coded state function per distinct pattern per module (content-addressed, shared across types), and the 7 patterns over 128 states (NF-e QR-code URLs, up to 494 states) table-driven; module sizes back near their pre-DFA size; the affected units' Cells gates green and the pattern oracle 0 disagreements.")
inl note_of_fiscal_xsd_patterns_large_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE", 17u32, "2026-11-07T15:55Z", "fiscal", "DoD: one direct-coded state function per distinct pattern per module (content-addressed, shared across types), the 7 patterns over 128 states (NF-e QR-code URLs, up to 494 states) table-driven, module sizes back near their pre-DFA size, the affected units' Cells gates green and the pattern oracle at 0 disagreements.")
inl kit_notebook_workers () = Task ("KIT-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS", "The release notebook phase runs N notebooks at once (EOIE_NOTEBOOK_WORKERS, default 2) instead of one by one (63 notebooks, about 35 of a release's 60-70 minutes): spawn through the jobs host child API (kill-on-close container, tree stop on timeout), print each notebook's logs when it ends, list all failures", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", "kit,dev,release", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_notebook_workers () = Planning ("KIT-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS", Minutes 60u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl gleam_string_linear () = Task ("GLEAM-STRING-LINEAR", "Gleam string search and slicing are O(n) per call, so lib substring loops go O(n^2) (x sim hit 16 GB on 10-21)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "gleam,lib,compiler,perf,main,lab-held", "current", "current")
inl kit_job_stop_windows () = Task ("KIT-JOB-STOP-WINDOWS", "eoie job stop leaves windows held by a 'window run' inside the stopped tree (main hit it 10-21 14:14: compile window held 163 min after the job stopped)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,window,job", "current", "current")
inl kit_job_memory_cap () = Task ("KIT-JOB-MEMORY-CAP", "eoie job start --max-private-mb: stop a job whose process tree (incl. detached Cells VMs it spawned) exceeds a private-memory cap, with the peak in job status", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,job,memory", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_job_memory_cap () = Planning ("KIT-JOB-MEMORY-CAP", Unestimated, Load Medium, Unassigned)
inl kit_init_lease_file () = Task ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", "agile init leaves a root where attested writes fail: state/package.spiproj lists the prompt module, but init writes no state/prompt.spi, so any typecheck-attested mutation (groomed add, set) fails with 'Missing check input: state/prompt.spi' until a lease begins", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_init_lease_file () = Planning ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_1 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 1u32, "2026-10-21T18:35Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 14:35 eoie team: found by the combined r28+r29 release. notes_cli's agile_add_lands_a_groomed_item_in_one_call ran on a fresh 'agile init' root and failed the attestation. Real roots (the shared backlog, eoie/state) carry a prompt.spi, so day-to-day use is unaffected. The test fixture now writes a lease file like the shared backlog's. Product fix to decide: init writes a closed lease file, or the state package lists prompt only once a lease exists. Lease-root detection keys on prompt.spi, so measure both before choosing.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_2 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 2u32, "2026-10-21T19:41Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 15:41 eoie team, rule set before measuring (measurements run after tibia's live block, because they typecheck). Option A: init writes state/prompt.spi with a closed lease (PromptLease ... LeaseClosed), so the state package it declares is complete from the start and begin replaces the lease. Option B: init lists only the agile module, and begin adds prompt to the manifest when it writes the lease. On scratch roots, choose A if all of these hold: (1) init, then a groomed add (--estimate/--note --as) passes under the default lease policy and under renewing; (2) agile begin afterwards still opens a lease and later mutations pass; (3) agile lease/status on an init-only root reports the closed lease, not an error. Otherwise B, measured the same way. Ties go to A (smaller: one more scaffold file, no manifest rewriting).")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_3 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 3u32, "2026-10-21T21:20Z", "eoie-lane", "17:20 eoie team, measured on scratch roots with the installed r28+r29 binary (init-lease-measure.ps1, then 4 lease-file variants). (1) holds for baseline and option A: a groomed add (--estimate/--note --as) on a bare init root now passes under the default and renewing policies (validation=runtime-attested, compiler not required), so the item's premise (attestation fails without prompt.spi) no longer reproduces. (2) holds for both: begin opens a lease and later adds pass. (3) fails for both: baseline (= option B) 'agile lease' on an init-only root prints a raw OS error (prompt.spi not found, exit 2); option A's closed lease is rejected ('PromptLease shape/status rejected fields=7'), because the lease reader accepts only LeaseActive. Nothing in src writes LeaseClosed. An all-zero LeaseActive file is read but reported as phase=running, 497949h ago, which misleads. The rule did not cover both options failing; decision: neither A nor B. The remaining defect is the lease reader: a missing prompt.spi should give a no-lease receipt (exit 0, hint 'eoie agile begin'), and LeaseClosed should be read as closed. The reader is a Rust blob in agile_state_runtime/state_terminal.spi, so the fix goes with that blob's granular migration (next in the order after the handoff render), not as blob growth. Priority lowered to P3: day-to-day roots carry a lease file.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_4 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 4u32, "2026-10-22T07:40Z", "eoie", "03:40 groom: the row now matches note 3's decision (P3; the item's premise no longer reproduces, the remaining lease-reader defect rides the state_terminal.spi blob migration).")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_5 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 5u32, "2026-10-22T13:46Z", "eoie-lane", "09:46 eoie team, decided by reading the code (measuring was the open step): lease readback accepts only LeaseActive (agile_prompt_lease_status_code maps everything else to unknown, which the shape binding rejects) and checks deadline = started + budget + guard. Attested writes need only the file (the shared backlog's lease expired on 10-08 and its writes still pass). So a 'closed lease' file would fail readback, and the working shape is an expired active lease, the one the shared backlog and the notes fixture carry. Fix (apply-init-lease.ps1, in G before E's heal): scaffold_file gains LeasePrompt; init writes state/prompt.spi as PromptLease ('init', ..., 4500000, 600000, now-5100000, now, LeaseActive), which is never live; init refuses when prompt.spi already exists; the receipt says files=3. notes_cli test: a fresh init root takes a groomed add with no hand-written lease, and a second init fails.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_6 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 6u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 30m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D2 at 60%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_7 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 7u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_8 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 8u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_9 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 9u32, "2026-11-06T11:35Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-INIT-LEASE-FILE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_10 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 10u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries AGILE-3 (Generic record and check). Why: agile init leaves a root where attested writes fail: same bootstrap-absent-ledgers and one-attestation-policy intent (was parked 10-24)")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_11 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 11u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. AGILE-3 · Generic record and check · P1 · node, sbin, ota, ge2e · Open / `agile record` required EOIE migration ledgers (`history`, `ratings`, `bench`, `migration`). Bootstrap absent ledgers atomically, support generic project ratings, report legacy/unknown receipts and orphan state modules as a non-blocking compatibility class, keep one attestation policy across `set`, `record`, `add` and `check` (a runtime-attested mutation made `check` demand compiler attestation), and offer a scoped check that does not demand compiler attestation for unrelated historical state.")
inl note_of_kit_init_lease_file_12 () = Note ("KIT-INIT-LEASE-FILE", 12u32, "2026-11-09T14:31Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "proof: 11-09 10:3x microblog groom, the step from n7/n8 (did it ship?), on the installed kit (11-08) over a fresh scratch root. 'agile init <root>' -> files=3: state/agile.spi, state/package.spiproj AND state/prompt.spi. 'agile lease <root>' -> 'kit agile lease status ... phase=running policy=renewing ... remaining=0s', exit 0: the expired-active-lease shape n5 chose, read back without the raw OS error n3 saw. A groomed 'agile add ... --estimate 10 --note ... --as ...' on that init-only root -> ok (planned=estimate, notes=1). So the n3 defect (lease on an init-only root failed) and the original premise (attested writes fail without prompt.spi) are both gone. The scratch root was deleted. Done; the dump's AGILE-3 ledger bootstrap (n10) is a separate intent and stays with KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM. pass.")
