inl formatter_tab_lines () = Task ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", "Formatter: a tab anywhere in a code line makes the line Opaque Unlexable, so it is kept verbatim without a word; report it (format --check and the corpus listing) and decide whether to expand leading tabs", TaskKind, P5, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "formatter,spiral,diagnostics,main,team:org,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_tab_lines () = Planning ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 1u32, "2026-10-21T21:21Z", "main", "17:21 found by x during the skip-respace review (FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS note 24, corrected): the installed compiler's tokens verb shows tokenize_line stops at a tab (a leading tab, f<TAB>-1, x<TAB>-y and x<TAB>- y give no tokens after it), so the formatter can never normalize such a line, and nothing reports it. Next: count tab-bearing code lines in the user corpus and lib (the corpus listing can tally them), then decide: report only, or expand leading tabs to the indent unit before lexing (single-valued habit) while keeping tabs inside a line verbatim.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_2 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 2u32, "2026-10-21T21:21Z", "main", "17:21 census (rg over every .spi/.spir under C:\\home\\git): 167 tab lines in 70 files, and every one is in a comment, which the formatter keeps verbatim anyway. Our own: lib/spiral/benchmark.spi 9 (/// result tables), polyglot/apps/perf/Perf.spi 21 (/// result tables). The rest are 2 per upstream core copy (trailing tabs after // comments in core.spi/real_core.spir) and my 2 synthetic test files. Zero code lines carry a tab, so the silent verbatim case has no instance today. Lowered to P5: worth a one-line report when it first appears, not work now.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_3 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 3u32, "2026-11-07T22:12Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: format --check names every line it keeps verbatim because of a tab (file:line), and a written decision on expanding leading tabs; since the 10-21 census found all 167 tab lines in comments, the likely outcome is report-only.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_4 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:39Z", "compiler", "11-09 14:4x compiler DECISION (lane:compiler wait): REPORT-ONLY, do NOT expand leading tabs. Re-census today (git grep -P tab over every tracked .spi/.spir in spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, regex, dice, alphabet): 9 tab lines in comments (kept verbatim anyway), 5 in code, and all 5 are the formatters own deliberate synthetic fixtures (scripts/formatter/synthetic/tab_before_minus.spi:2-4, trailing_spaces_tabs.spi:1-2). Zero real code lines carry a tab, same as the 10-21 census. Why not expand: expansion would make the formatter change the token stream of a line it cannot lex (it stops at the tab), which is exactly the guess the formatter refuses elsewhere; with no instance in real code there is nothing to gain. What remains = the DoDs report: format --check naming file:line for every line kept verbatim because of a tab. That is a small formatter change for a future compiler pack, P5 as main set it; the synthetic fixtures already exercise the path. Clearing the compiler wait.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_5 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T18:45Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09 CENSUS DONE (ripgrep \\t over tracked .spi/.spir): tab-bearing lines are RARE in user code - exactly 2 files: spiral/lib/spiral/benchmark.spi (9 lines) + i574n.github/examples/perf/Perf.spi (20 lines) = 29 lines total. All other 120 hits are VENDORED compiler deps (The-Spiral-Language .../core.spi, 2 tabs each; Spiral-s-ML-Library corebase; polyglot/deps) = not the user's corpus, exempt. So the blast radius is tiny (2 files, 29 lines). RECOMMENDATION: since it is only 2 files, EXPAND leading tabs to the indent unit in benchmark.spi + Perf.spi (keeping any mid-line tabs verbatim) rather than building a formatter tab-expander - a one-time cleanup closes it; the report-in-format--check part is still worth adding so new tabs are flagged. The expand-vs-report formatter decision + the --check report is the formatter owner's (compiler). Parking on lane:compiler for the format--check reporting; the 2-file cleanup rides lib (benchmark) + i574n (Perf) next touch.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_6 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T18:49Z", "compiler", "11-09 14:5x compiler, on orgs 18:45 recommendation (expand tabs in benchmark.spi + Perf.spi): NOTHING TO EXPAND. All 9 tab lines in lib/spiral/benchmark.spi (243-251) are /// doc-comment table rows (\"/// Input<TAB>| Expected<TAB>| ...\"), and every tab is MID-line column alignment; none is leading. Leading-tab expansion is therefore a no-op there, and rewriting mid-line tabs would only reflow a comment table the formatter keeps verbatim and never lexes, so no diagnostic or format result changes. Perf.spis are the same /// result-table shape (10-21 census). Decision stands: report-only, no expander, no hand edit. The item can close once format --check names tab-kept CODE lines (today only the formatters own synthetic fixtures). Clearing the compiler wait again.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_7 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 7u32, "2026-11-09T18:52Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:5x ROUTED: compiler's 14:39 decision leaves one DoD line, the format --check report (file:line for each line kept verbatim because of a tab), which compiler scoped as \"a small formatter change for a future compiler pack\". The formatter is compiler's code and compiler's ready-light floor is 0, so team:compiler is added (team:org stays as second owner). Next step (compiler): in the formatter's check pass, emit `<file>:<line>: kept verbatim (tab breaks lexing)` for Opaque Unlexable lines that contain a tab; the synthetic fixtures tab_before_minus.spi:2-4 and trailing_spaces_tabs.spi:1-2 are the test inputs.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_8 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 8u32, "2026-11-09T18:58Z", "compiler", "11-09 15:0x compiler: the DoD report is BUILT and proven (pack78 candidate = pack77 + %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FORMATTER-TAB-LINES\\1-check-reports-tab-kept-lines.kitdo, core built on ganymede, build exit 0). format --check now prints file:line:col: tab-kept-verbatim (a tab stops the lexer, so this line is left as written) for every Opaque Unlexable line that holds a tab, column = the first tab; informational like over-120 (exit code unchanged). Proof: synthetic/tab_before_minus.spi -> lines 2, 3, 4 (col 1); synthetic/trailing_spaces_tabs.spi -> 1:20 and 2:10; lib/spiral/benchmark.spi -> nothing (its 9 tabs are in /// comments, which lex fine). Exactly the census set. Ships in the next compiler pack (gate = -Suite all, which runs no format --check, so expected 0 diffs). After that this item is Done.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_9 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 9u32, "2026-11-09T19:03Z", "compiler", "compiler: only remaining step = ship 1-check-reports-tab-kept-lines.kitdo in the next compiler pack (built + proven on a pack78 candidate). Next pack = after pack77 reaches box + moon (moon held by rigs TRAIN42e). Wait: train:TRAIN42e.")
inl note_of_formatter_tab_lines_10 () = Note ("FORMATTER-TAB-LINES", 10u32, "2026-11-09T21:42Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 18:0x: DONE on compiler's verified handoff (pack78 installed on all 4 nodes). Both DoD parts met: (1) written decision on leading-tab expansion = REPORT-ONLY, no expander (notes 4+7: re-census found zero real code tab lines; all benchmark.spi/Perf.spi tabs are mid-line /// comment-table alignment kept verbatim anyway, so leading-tab expansion is a no-op and reflowing mid-line tabs would only change a comment the formatter never lexes). (2) format --check names each tab-kept line = BUILT + PROVEN (note 8: prints file:line:col: tab-kept-verbatim for Opaque Unlexable lines holding a tab; synthetic/tab_before_minus.spi -> 2,3,4 col1; trailing_spaces_tabs.spi -> 1:20 and 2:10; benchmark.spi -> nothing since its tabs are in /// comments that lex fine) + shipped pack78. Closing; no independent re-run (P5, compiler's note-8 proof is concrete).")
