inl kit_release_train () = Task ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", "The eoie release train as eoie verbs: today's releases ran on session-scratch scripts (apply-rNN, preview-at, notebook-check, check-rNN, release-build-job-NN, chain-rNN waiting on tails and windows), which vanish with the session and repeat the same go rule by hand. One call per step: eoie release check <tree> --crates <regex> (preview + notebook typecheck + cargo check, go-rule receipt), eoie release run --after <job> (apply, build, publish, install, tail), with the go rule as typed data", Story, P1, D5, 45u32, Planned, "KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS", "kit,jobs,release,wipe-redo,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_release_train () = Planning ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_release_train_1 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 1u32, "2026-10-21T21:50Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 17:50 filed while handing off: the r34 chain, the r35 drafts and every release script lived only in the session scratchpad. Scripts move to lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN after tonight's install (not before: the release's publish step refuses inventory changes). Evidence of the cost today: a wrong script name and a polluted PowerShell return lost r28; a lab write mid-release blocked publish; three stale tests surfaced only in the release.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_2 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 2u32, "2026-10-21T22:29Z", "eoie-lane", "18:29 lesson for the verb's design: a check tree must be rebuilt from the live tree plus the release's apply scripts every time the live tree changes. Tonight r34-tree predated three live test fixes (window_model row_blocks argument, notes_cli lease fixture, census assertion), so r34's and r35's notebook checks showed a false type error in window_model.spi and a false runtime failure in notes_cli. Fix tonight: r34-rebuild.ps1 (mirror live src/spec, apply every slice with -Src, then preview, notebooks, cargo check in one chain via job start --after-ok). Second lesson: when a slice changes a shared record or function, grep every consumer of the record before checking (the analysis row mask missed eoie_table_test, which builds the same scope record; the earlier where_clauses grep had shown it).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_3 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 3u32, "2026-10-21T22:32Z", "eoie-lane", "18:32 design from tonight's scripts, for the first slice. Typed data: a release is a union of steps (Mirror tree, Apply slice, Preview crates, Typecheck notebooks, CargoCheck packages, Build, Publish, Install) and a go rule is a list of typed checks (PreviewExit0, NoFileOver 1000, NoParserErrors, NoTypeErrors, CargoPassed) evaluated over receipts, never over grepped logs. Verbs, one call each: 'eoie release tree <name> --from live --slices <file>' (mirror src/spec only with the size guard, apply every slice with -Src, receipt per slice); 'eoie release check <name> --crates <regex> [--notebooks auto]' (preview + notebook typecheck + cargo check --locked of the touched packages and their placeholders, runtime failures reported separately from type errors, line counts per generated file); 'eoie release run <name> --after <job> --go <rule>' (apply to live, build, publish, install; inventory lock while it runs so lab writes wait instead of breaking publish). Consumers of a changed record or function are found by the tool (spiproj package graph + grep of the changed names), not by memory. Tonight's scripts that this replaces: r34-rebuild, r35-early, preview-at, notebook-check, check-rNN(-inner), chain-rNN, release-build-job-NN, after-install.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_4 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 4u32, "2026-10-21T22:49Z", "eoie-lane", "18:49 queue state for the next session: r30-r33 building since 18:46 (install ~19:56). r34 (12 slices) green on a tree rebuilt from live: preview exit 0 (max do_program.rs 988), cargo check of 35 crates passed, notebooks without type errors (recheck r34f running). r35 (10 slices) green on top of r34: previews exit 0, 12 notebooks typecheck. r36 (grep split) previews clean on top of r35. Order: main's compiler install after r30-r33, then r34 (re-check on the new compiler), r35, r36. Scripts land in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN and per-item lab folders after tonight's install (lab-handoff.ps1).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_5 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 5u32, "2026-10-21T23:23Z", "eoie-lane", "19:23 another script-train trap for the verb's design: a cargo-check wrapper passed -TimeoutSec 900 to test-regeneration.ps1 (its range ends at 600); the parameter error left $LASTEXITCODE unset, the wrapper's 'exit $LASTEXITCODE' exited 0 and 'window run' reported exit=0. Only the go rule's text match ('regeneration passed') would have caught it. The verb must carry typed outcomes (CheckPassed | CheckFailed reason) end to end, never exit codes read through shell layers.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_6 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 6u32, "2026-10-21T23:27Z", "eoie-lane", "19:27 cargo check of the r35 and r36 trees failed in eoie-agile-mutation (E0432: use eoie_handoff::handoff_render_owned), which is not an r35/r36 defect: the live tree has r30-r33's .spi and Cargo changes applied but still the old committed .rs until the release publishes, and a check that regenerates only its own owners compiles stale neighbours (here pulled in through eoie-cli). Rule: cargo-check a tree rebuilt from live only after the release in flight has published; after-install-r33.ps1 now chains r34 rebuild -> r35 -> r36 -> cargo checks. The verb should regenerate every owner whose source differs from its committed .rs, not only the filtered ones.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_7 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 7u32, "2026-10-22T00:11Z", "eoie-lane", "20:11 next-session opening checklist (scripts in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN and the per-item lab folders once tonight's install runs lab-handoff.ps1; they still reference the old scratchpad path, so re-home them first). 1) Confirm r30-r33 installed (r33-tail 'release install done'); if not, read r33-tests.log and the cells daemon log (requests from the release's notebook process). 2) Ask main whether its compiler install ran; r34 re-checks on the new compiler. 3) Rebuild check trees from live AFTER the install published: r34-rebuild.ps1 -> r35-early.ps1 -> r36-early.ps1, then cargo check r35/r36 (r35-early-cargo.ps1, r36-early-cargo.ps1; TimeoutSec max 600) and the ratchet (eoie standards --ratchet standards/census.spi <tree>\\src, one call per tree). 4) Release r34 (12 slices), then r35 (13), then r36 (7), each with its plan file; r34 unblocks tibia's last 6 experiment imports. 5) Then the patch prune per EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION's plan (positional codes already removed by r35's descriptor slice). 6) After each install, capture the spec cases (spec-cases-r33/capture-cases.ps1) and regenerate docs/one-call-guide.md.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_8 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 8u32, "2026-10-22T00:12Z", "eoie-lane", "20:12 handoff rule set before the deadline: if r30-r33 has not installed by 20:50, the session's scripts and drafts go to C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\lab\\<item>\\ (lab-handoff.ps1 -Lab, outside the eoie repo so the release's inventory check is untouched) and move into eoie/lab next session; if it installs first, after-install-r33.ps1 copies them into eoie/lab directly.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_9 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 9u32, "2026-10-22T00:13Z", "eoie-lane", "20:13 safety copy made early (the 20:50 rule's fallback, done at 20:13 because it is only a copy outside eoie): 76 files in C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\lab\\<item>\\ (EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN 24, EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION 13, EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE 11, MACHINE-WATCH 8, MEMORY-VERBS 7, TABLE-TEST 7, GREP-FILE-ROOT 5, JOBS 4, others). after-install-r33.ps1 still copies the same set into eoie/lab when the release installs; next session keeps the eoie/lab copy and deletes the i574n.github/lab one (uncommitted, user's git).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_10 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 10u32, "2026-10-22T00:26Z", "eoie-lane", "20:26 checklist update: step 1 is now 'relaunch r30-r33': the live tree already holds the r30-r33 sources, their published .rs (19:19) and the resume_cli test fix (20:24), so the relaunch is only release-build-job-33.ps1 (lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN) with no applies. Before it, per the new memory release-candidate-cli-run, build a candidate binary and run the CLI notebooks of the r30-r33 crates against it. Scripts are in eoie/lab (78 files copied 20:24); the temporary i574n.github/lab copy was removed after the eoie copy was verified.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_11 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 11u32, "2026-10-22T00:37Z", "eoie-lane", "20:37 post-publish checks: r35 cargo check --locked passed for 16 owners on a tree rebuilt from live after the 19:19 publish (so the earlier eoie-agile-mutation E0432 was the stale-tree artifact, as diagnosed). r35/r36 previews exit 0 on that tree. Candidate binary (the release's own r30-r33 debug build, 19:19) runs the r30-r33 CLI notebooks for real: resume_cli (with the fix), edit_cli, receipts_cli, notes_cli pass so far; todo_cli, views_cli, grep_cli running. r36 cargo check running.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_12 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 12u32, "2026-10-22T00:38Z", "eoie-lane", "20:38 post-publish chain complete: r36 cargo check --locked passed for 8 owners, including the three new crates (eoie_grep_query, eoie_memory_store, eoie_memory_save) and their sorted lock entries; r35 passed earlier (16 owners). So r34, r35 and r36 have each passed preview, notebook typecheck and cargo check on trees rebuilt from the live tree after the 19:19 publish. Candidate CLI run: todo_cli passes too (5 of 7; views_cli and grep_cli finishing).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_13 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 13u32, "2026-10-22T00:41Z", "eoie-lane", "20:41 candidate CLI run complete: all 7 r30-r33 CLI notebooks pass against the release's own r30-r33 debug binary (resume_cli with the fix, edit_cli, receipts_cli, notes_cli, todo_cli, views_cli, grep_cli). The relaunch next session should therefore clear the notebook phase that failed tonight, barring infra (the cells daemon retiring under low memory; prefer a quiet machine for the release).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_14 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 14u32, "2026-10-22T00:45Z", "eoie", "20:45 candidate check for r34 started (job-1792629732157-eoie-candidate-cli-r34): debug eoie-cli from r34-tree into scratch candidate-target, then 6 r34 CLI notebooks against it. Script and result land in eoie/lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (candidate-cli-r34.ps1, nbcheck-candidate34.txt). Any fail blocks r34 next session.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_15 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 15u32, "2026-10-22T00:54Z", "eoie", "20:54 candidate-cli-r34 result is INVALID, not an r34 bug: table_test_cli 2 fails (where <= refused as unknown column; whole-table one-sample refused 'needs --arms'), but r34-tree's generated .rs are stale (table_test.rs 13:48 vs table_test.spi 20:25), so cargo built pre-r34 code. Proof: candidate 'table query --where foreign<=0' works (query crate unchanged), the old guard text lives only in stale table_test.rs:543. Next session: regenerate the tree's .rs with the Spiral build before 'cargo build -p eoie-cli' (and assert every .rs is newer than its .spi), then rerun candidate-cli-r34.ps1. Repro fixtures: scratch repro34/. The r33 candidate run was valid (live tree .rs regenerated by the release build).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_16 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 16u32, "2026-10-22T00:58Z", "eoie", "20:58 open question for next session, check BEFORE trusting the r34/r35/r36 'cargo check green': r34-tree/eoie/src/eoie_table_test/table_test.rs is the 13:48 live copy, so a cargo check run directly on a check tree compiles copied .rs, not the patched .spi. Verify which .rs check-r34-inner.ps1, r35-checks-cargo.ps1 and r36-early-cargo.ps1 compiled (preview output vs tree copy). If tree copies: regenerate each tree's .rs, redo the cargo checks and candidate runs. Mtime staleness counts on trees (93-109 crates) are mostly mirror-copy noise; in live every .rs is newer than its .spi except eoie_resume (20:23 test fix, regenerated by the next release).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_17 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 17u32, "2026-10-22T00:58Z", "eoie", "20:58 note 16 answered: check-r34-inner.ps1 (and the r35/r36 cargo checks) call test-regeneration.ps1 -Filter <all touched crates> -CargoCheck, which regenerates those crates before checking without writing .rs back into the tree (table_test.rs stays 13:48). So the r34-r36 cargo checks compiled the patched code and stay valid; only the candidate build read the tree's copied .rs. Fix for candidate-cli-r34.ps1: regenerate the touched crates into the tree first (or build eoie-cli from test-regeneration's output), then rerun.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_18 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 18u32, "2026-10-22T00:59Z", "eoie", "20:59 candidate fix route: test-regeneration.ps1 has -KeepStaged (params: EoieRoot, Filter, Package, TargetDirectory, CargoCheck, Test, SkipRelease, Offline, KeepStaged). Next session: run the r34 check with -KeepStaged, then cargo build -p eoie-cli from the kept staged dir and point candidate-cli-r34.ps1's -Eoie at that binary. No tree write-back needed.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_19 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 19u32, "2026-10-22T02:30Z", "eoie", "22:30 chain change: apply-r35.ps1 no longer runs apply-recall-coverage (memory drift hold, EOIE-MEMORY note), so the r35 check tree must be rebuilt and rechecked before release; r36 ships only apply-grep-split + apply-grep-regex (memory-split/save/forget/default-store/edit held). memory_cli expectations 104/105 from recall-coverage no longer apply.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_20 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 20u32, "2026-10-22T03:10Z", "eoie", "23:10 run to 07:00 (user: 'iterate until 7am autonomously'), rules written before measuring. R1 release A = live tree (r30-r33 + tonight's generic teams/fixtures) launches only after a candidate CLI run, built from regenerated code (test-regeneration -KeepStaged), passes every touched notebook; a failure is fixed and the candidate rerun before launch. R2 no src/ or lab/ writes in eoie while a release runs; drafts go to scratch trees. R3 after A installs: ask main for its compiler-install window; if no answer in 20 min, r34 proceeds on the current compiler. R4 release B = r34 + neutral fixtures, same candidate rule. R5 release C = r35 (no recall) + r36 grep + ratchet fixes + lib link/pilot, each slice proven on a fresh check tree; a slice that fails its check is dropped from C, not debugged in the slot. R6 drop order when time runs short: am'.any lib fix, then C's lib link, then C's ratchet slice; nothing launches after 05:15 unless it finishes by 06:45. R7 a reaped job is retried with lower parallelism (retry-after-memory-kills); a tibia live block pauses compiles.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_21 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 21u32, "2026-10-22T03:12Z", "eoie", "23:12 release A launched (job-1792638704456-eoie-release-A, heavy): release-build-job-A.ps1 = r33's job with logs rA-* plus a fail-fast candidate step after the debug build (12 touched CLI notebooks against src/target/debug/eoie.exe from the freshly published .rs; any runtime-fail or TYPE-ERROR stops before the long test phase). Live tree = r30-r33 + tonight's generic teams and neutral fixtures. No eoie writes until it ends (R2).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_22 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 22u32, "2026-10-22T03:20Z", "eoie", "23:20 R2 slip during release A: I fixed lab/EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION/apply-help-coverage.ps1 (r35 help payload still wrote '--team main|x|tibia|eoie'; now '--team <team>'). test-regeneration -Publish hashes every workspace file incl. lab/, so I restored the lab copy's exact bytes (same LF, no BOM as its siblings) within minutes; the r35 chain runs the scratch copy, which keeps the fix. After A: reapply to the lab copy. Also confirmed: Get-WorkspaceEntries throws on reparse points, so a src/spiral junction would break regeneration (EOIE-HEAL-LIB-LINK deferral stands).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_23 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 23u32, "2026-10-22T03:36Z", "eoie", "23:36 release C check tree (rC-tree = r34-tree + r35 minus recall + grep-split + grep-regex + census-lib-metrics + gate-queue, 15 slices) applies cleanly; preview compile exit 0 for all 15 touched crates. Sizes: command_spec 962, machine watch 954, job_control 855, run 885, windows 897, census 783 (+25 for 4 probes), gate.rs 1000 exactly after reworking gate-queue to fixed 5 s waits (the backoff version with a pause parameter was 1011). Unit tests: probes.spi passes on a dry copy; neutral-fixture model tests pass on the r34 tree.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_24 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 24u32, "2026-10-22T03:45Z", "eoie", "23:45 R8 (written before deciding): the pending slices predate tonight's style contract and add drift (r34: +52 host macros, +15 Rc wraps, +7 let-blocks; release C: +64, +32, +14). They still ship (live bug fixes: gate window hoarding, job-stop windows; requested features: tibia's table test, grep regex), but releases B and C no longer re-baseline the census at install, so the ratchet and the edit hook keep flagging those packages until each is healed (touching heals). Release A's job was already running with its re-baseline step, so A's own drift (r30-r33 + tonight) is absorbed; noted as debt on EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_25 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 25u32, "2026-10-22T04:06Z", "eoie", "00:06 R9 (written before acting): main takes compiler-install windows 01:15-01:50 (after A) and 06:30-07:00; tibia has a live block 05:30-06:30 (no compiles). Sequential B then C would end ~05:20 with no retry room, so B and C merge into one release BC (apply-r34 then apply-rC on live, which reproduces the checked rC tree built on r34), launched after main's 'install done' or 01:55. BC's candidate step covers both lists (17 CLI notebooks). If BC fails, bisect: ship B alone, then C. Nothing launches after 05:15 unless it ends by 05:30.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_26 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 26u32, "2026-10-22T04:11Z", "eoie", "00:11 release A FAILED at publish after 59 min: 'Checkout changed during validation; generated outputs were not published: lab/EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION/apply-help-coverage.ps1'. My 23:2x restore of that file was not byte-identical; regeneration, cargo check of all 197 outputs passed otherwise. R10 (written before relaunch): relaunch as ONE release ABC = live (r30-r33 + tonight) + apply-r34 + apply-rC, saving a full cycle; candidate step covers A's 12 + BC's 16 notebooks (deduplicated); no re-baseline (A's drift now also shows as debt); the job holds a tree lease (PreToolUse hook blocks Edit/Write under eoie) and I make no shell writes under eoie during the run. Main's compiler install moves to right after ABC. If ABC fails in candidate or tests, bisect with A alone; nothing launches after 05:15 unless it ends by 05:30 (tibia live block).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_27 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 27u32, "2026-10-22T04:23Z", "eoie", "00:23 ABC prepared on live while main installs the night pack (00:30-01:05): night handoff copied into lab, apply-r34 (snapshot 001242) and apply-rC incl. gate-queue, lib staging, regeneration lease (snapshot 001654) applied cleanly; live src equals the checked rC tree except the two intended lib-pilot files (agile_task_query), Cargo.lock and the test registry identical. Launch of release-build-job-ABC (21 candidate notebooks, tree lease, no re-baseline) waits for main's 'install done'.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_28 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 28u32, "2026-10-22T04:44Z", "eoie", "00:44 release ABC launched (job-1792644209539-eoie-release-ABC, heavy, 21 candidate notebooks, tree lease, no re-baseline) on main's new compiler (single-flight DA88EFB13FF61151); queued behind main-fmt-fix4 and main-cells-pack holding both heavy slots. Release D prepared and checked in the scratch tree rD (apply-tree-read: tree-read window class 0 MB never clashing + eoie window claim <path> in new crate eoie_window_claim on the eoie_tree_lease model + a claims CLI test; apply-job-slot-split: heavy-slot queue moved to new crate eoie_job_slot, gate.rs 1005 -> 854): preview exit 0 for all touched crates (windows 977, claim 407, gate 854, slot 216, launch 897), window_model and lease unit tests pass. D launches after ABC only if it can end by 05:30 (tibia live block).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_29 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 29u32, "2026-10-22T05:07Z", "eoie", "01:07 release D trimmed to fit before 05:30: its regeneration filters to the 8 crates whose Spiral packages inline the changed ones (closure over package.spiproj deps from eoie_machine_windows, eoie_job_gate, eoie_job_slot, eoie_window_claim, eoie_tree_lease): eoie_job_gate, eoie_job_slot, eoie_machine_watch, eoie_machine_windows, eoie_process_table, eoie_window_claim, eoie_window_query, eoie_window_run (eoie_jobs/eoie_job_launch/eoie_cli call them through exports, no inlining). Saves ~30 min of the 200-output regen. Candidate step: 5 CLI notebooks incl. the new claim test and ps_cli. Check after ABC publishes: a brand-new crate's .rs (eoie_grep_query in ABC) gets published although it was not in the start snapshot; D relies on the same for claim.rs and slot.rs.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_30 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 30u32, "2026-10-22T05:07Z", "eoie", "01:07 confirmed from test-regeneration.ps1:230-233: publish writes every regenerated output (Set-EoieGeneratedFile Source -> declared Original) whether or not the file existed, so new crates' .rs (eoie_grep_query in ABC; eoie_window_claim and eoie_job_slot in D) are published.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_31 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 31u32, "2026-10-22T05:19Z", "eoie", "01:19 release D final scope (3 slices, all applied cleanly to a fresh mirror of live): apply-tree-read (tree-read window class + eoie window claim in new crate eoie_window_claim on eoie_tree_lease + claims CLI test + registry entry for lease.spi), apply-job-slot-split (heavy-slot queue -> new crate eoie_job_slot; gate.rs 1005 -> 854), apply-standards-host-free (new standards rules HostFree and LibReferenced, declared by eoie_tree_lease and eoie_window_claim; AGENTS.md then points at the declarations and the central healed.spi goes, one record per fact). Checks: preview exit 0 (windows 977, claim 407, gate 854, slot 216, standards 680), unit tests pass for rules.spi, window_model.spi, lease.spi. Regen filtered to 9 crates; candidate step 6 notebooks. Launch after ABC only if it can end by 05:30.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_32 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 32u32, "2026-10-22T05:20Z", "eoie", "01:20 R11 (written before ABC ends): release D launches only if ABC has installed AND the launch time is 03:50 or earlier (D estimate 1h30-1h40 with its 9-crate regeneration, so it ends by 05:30, when tibia's live block starts). If ABC fails, D does not launch; the time goes to bisecting ABC (A alone) instead. If ABC installs after 03:50, D waits for the next session with its scripts in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN. ABC progress at 01:20: regeneration 51/200, no failures.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_33 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 33u32, "2026-10-22T05:43Z", "eoie", "01:43 ABC regeneration has slowed to ~1 output/min under machine load (113/200 at 01:25, 122 at 01:36, 131 at 01:42): projected regen end ~02:50, install ~04:20, so by R11 release D most likely waits for the next session (built and checked; its scripts go to lab with lab-handoff-D.ps1). From now on the eoie lane runs no compile jobs of its own until ABC ends, to give it every cycle.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_34 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 34u32, "2026-10-22T05:59Z", "eoie", "01:59 carry decision (lab rule: drain lab, at most one named carry): the night's pending work goes to ONE folder, lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22 (35 files: D's three slices + apply/job/launch, E's heal slices + heal-crate.ps1 + window-held marker + apply-rE, the helper scripts notebook-check/preview-at/eoie-snapshot, the scratch models f1-owner/f2-lease/tree-read and the memory-feature designs, the morning report draft), with every scratchpad path rewritten to that folder so it runs after this session. lab-handoff-D.ps1 does it after ABC publishes; per-item duplicate copies dropped (one record per fact). The folder empties as D and E land.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_35 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 35u32, "2026-10-22T06:13Z", "eoie", "02:13 ABC regeneration at 160/200, ~0.6 outputs/min under saturation (8 cores busy: main-sm-combined ~2.5 cores, tibia-pf1-run4 ~1, x-precommit ~0.5, sessions + compiler servers): projected regen end ~03:20, install ~05:00. By R11, D does not launch tonight (install after 03:50); it carries to next session in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22. Asked main whether new heavy/compile work can wait until ABC's regeneration ends, so ABC clears tibia's 05:30 live block.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_36 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 36u32, "2026-10-22T06:14Z", "eoie", "02:14 R12 (written before it applies): tibia's live block starts 05:30 and its live-gui window is exclusive, so a running ABC would hold it back. At 05:15: if ABC has not reached its release build (the final ~10 min after tests), I stop job-1792644209539-eoie-release-ABC myself (my own job, process tree stopped), release its windows, and relaunch it next session from lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (live tree keeps r34 + rC applied). If ABC is in its release build at 05:15, it finishes.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_37 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 37u32, "2026-10-22T06:24Z", "eoie", "02:24 ABC regeneration complete: 200/200 emitted, no failures (it sped up from ~0.6 to several outputs/min once main and tibia held heavy work). Now in the staged cargo check, then debug build, candidate step (21 notebooks), full test suite, release build. Main told it can resume heavy work; lib/spiral stays unchanged until 'release done'.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_38 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 38u32, "2026-10-22T07:17Z", "eoie", "03:17 ABC candidate check: 2/21 notebooks fail so far, so ABC will exit 'release not published: candidate'. (1) notes_cli notes_from_title_moves_each_tail_into_a_dated_note is deterministic: ABC's note-local-time slice appends ' (HH:MM -04:00)' to note lines and this test still expects the bare UTC line; test-only fix apply-notes-local-test.ps1 asserts the UTC stamp prefix + note text suffix (timezone-independent). (2) windows_cli a_heavy_job_waits_for_a_live_window_and_releases_its_own timed out (3000 ms job timeout, 21.8 s elapsed) with 5 heavy-build windows held machine-wide plus my scratch preview in a concurrent compile window: load flake; I stopped my preview and released its window. Rule R13, written before the rerun: if ABC fails ONLY at the candidate notebooks, launch release-build-job-ABC-tail.ps1 instead of a new full release: it reuses ABC's published regen and built candidate, requires 21/21 rows from ABC's check, reruns only the failed notebooks (after the test-only fix), then runs ABC's own parity, ratchet, Spiral tests, runner, e2e, window/orphan checks, release build and install verbatim. A notebook failing again in the tail is genuine: no further rerun, carry to the next session. R12 still applies (05:15: stop it unless in its release build). R11 is moot: D carries to the next session either way. My scratch previews stay off while the tail runs notebooks.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_39 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 39u32, "2026-10-22T07:23Z", "eoie", "03:23 third candidate failure: eoie_table_test/table_test_cli.spi line 38 closes its Arg chain with 12 parens for 11 opens (ParserErrors at col 215, so the cell drops and spiral_cells_test goes unbound); it came from my apply-whole-table slice (fixed there too). I skipped the paren scan my own memory prescribes before queuing test edits; a full-tree scan now finds no other real surplus (11 other hits are multi-line closers under a line ending in ','). Test-only fix apply-table-test-paren.ps1 joins apply-notes-local-test.ps1 in launch-ABC-tail.ps1; R13 covers any number of test-only fixes, each dry-run on a copy first.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_40 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 40u32, "2026-10-22T07:26Z", "eoie", "03:26 third test-only fix for the tail: windows_cli's gated heavy job had a 3000 ms timeout that must cover a cold pwsh gate wrapper; the test checks window waiting and release, not the timeout, so it now gets 30000 ms (safe even if the clock started at job start: the test's whole wait is ~10-15 s). Sequence at ABC's end (end-of-abc.ps1): message main, lab handoff into lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22 while no release holds the tree, then launch-ABC-tail.ps1 (three dry-run test fixes, then the tail job).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_41 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 41u32, "2026-10-22T07:48Z", "eoie", "03:48 ABC ended 03:42 exactly as diagnosed: candidate notebooks 18/21 (notes_cli, windows_cli, table_test_cli), 'release not published: candidate'. R13 applied: main told; lab handoff copied the carry set into lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22; the 3 test-only fixes applied; tail job-1792654976840-eoie-release-ABC-tail started 03:42:57 in heavy slot 1 (main yielded its queued Cells pack so the tail wasn't queued past R12). Main holds its lib/spiral landing (sm', env, process.spi) until the tail reaches its release build, because the tail's Spiral tests read tree lib through agile_task_query's spiral- reference.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_42 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 42u32, "2026-10-22T07:51Z", "eoie", "03:51 R14, written before deciding: the tail is queued behind tibia-p29-build2 (slot 1, still running at 94 min) and x-precommit-night2 (first ticket, queued 60 min); main-fmt-fix5b holds slot 2 until ~05:00. The tail needs ~75 min from its slot to its release build, so it must hold a slot by 04:00 to beat R12 (05:15), and 05:30-06:30 is tibia's live block (no compiles). Rule: if at 04:00 the tail's slot file still says 'waiting', stop the tail (my job) so its heavy-build window and queue ticket free up for the lanes ahead, and carry it: next session runs launch-ABC-tail.ps1 unchanged (ABC's regen stays published in the tree; the 3 test fixes are already applied, so the launcher's fix scripts must be skipped: they throw on a missing anchor, which is the expected 'already applied' state). If it holds a slot by 04:00, it continues under R12. No queue jumping in either case.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_43 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 43u32, "2026-10-22T08:17Z", "eoie", "04:17 composition check (text only) on a src+spec copy of the live tree after tonight's post-04:00 edits (3 test fixes, generic drift): D's three slices (tree-read, job-slot split, standards host-free) and then all of E apply cleanly, the same 4 near-gate crates skipped. So next session's order ABC tail -> D -> E needs no re-drafting; only E's compile preview and gate numbers remain, measured on the live tree after the tail installs.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_44 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 44u32, "2026-10-22T09:13Z", "eoie", "05:13 tonight's two release lessons are now code, not just memory: prelaunch-check.ps1 dry-runs a release's slices on a src copy of the live tree, paren-scans every changed .spi line (a seeded copy of ABC's table_test_cli bug is caught at :38:215), and refuses when both heavy slots are held unless -Queue is passed. launch-D.ps1 and launch-ABC-tail.ps1 call it first (via pwsh -Command, because pwsh -File does not split a comma list into an array). D's slices pass it now.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_45 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 45u32, "2026-10-22T09:14Z", "eoie", "05:14 verb design from tonight's scripts (one call each, no plan files, per EOIE-ONE-CALL): (1) eoie release check <slice-script>... [--queue]: today's prelaunch-check.ps1 (dry-run on a src copy, surplus-paren scan of changed lines, heavy-slot queue refusal). (2) eoie release start <label> --slices <...> --notebooks <...>: today's launch-X + release-build-job-X (tree lease with pid, regen -Publish, debug build, candidate notebooks, parity, ratchet, Spiral tests, runner, e2e checks, release build, install), as one supervised job whose steps are a typed union, not a script. (3) eoie release resume <label> --from candidate-notebooks: today's tail (R13): reuse a published regen and a built candidate, rerun only the failed notebooks, continue. (4) eoie release status <label>: the step reached, failures, queue position (today read from job tail and nbcheck files). (5) deadlines as flags (--slot-by HH:MM, --release-build-by HH:MM) so R12/R14 stop rules are enforced by the job, not by crons. Evidence: R11-R14 and the tail cost about 20 scripts tonight; each step already exists as a scratch script carried in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_46 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 46u32, "2026-10-22T09:20Z", "eoie", "05:20 hazard closed in the carried scripts: the lab handoff rewrites the scratch path to the night folder, so release-build-job-D, the ABC tail, notebook-check, preview-at, prelaunch-check and the E/E2 previews would have written logs, notebook outputs and whole src copies into lab/ inside the repo, which during D's regeneration -Publish is release A's failure again (a workspace file changing mid-run). Every output now goes to work = %LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\release-work when the script runs from inside C:\\home\\git (scratch behavior unchanged); inputs and script paths still come from the night folder. Verified: running the carried prelaunch-check from lab left the lab folder byte-identical.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_47 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 47u32, "2026-10-22T09:34Z", "eoie", "05:34 lab drain rule (memory lab-in-repo 10-22: drain before new work, delete only after landing), written before checking: a lab folder is deleted when (1) its backlog item is Done, (2) none of its files is git-tracked (no history lost), and (3) no file outside the folder (eoie src, scripts, compiler-contracts, spec, standards, other lab folders' scripts) references the folder path. Candidates now: lab/CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE (3 files), lab/EOIE-TABLE-TEST (7), lab/EOIE-CORE-OPERATORS (10). Active and Planned items keep their folders until they land.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_48 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 48u32, "2026-10-22T09:34Z", "eoie", "05:34 lab drain applied: lab/CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE, lab/EOIE-TABLE-TEST and lab/EOIE-CORE-OPERATORS deleted (items Done, 0 tracked files; the only outside mention is eoie_repo_state's test fixture string '? lab/EOIE-CORE-OPERATORS/sweep.ps1', sample git-status text that needs no file). 19 lab folders remain, all for Active/Planned items; the night carry is lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_49 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 49u32, "2026-10-22T10:46Z", "eoie", "06:46 lab drain by landing check (rule: an untracked apply slice is drained when it defines at least 2 Spiral names and every one exists in live src): drained 6 slices that shipped via ABC: EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE apply-adoption + apply-guide-parent, EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION apply-descriptor-named + apply-proxy-tokens + apply-status-reflection, EOIE-JOBS apply-job-list-live. Kept (undecidable by names: slices that only edit text, 0-1 defined names; or partial: apply-ps-cores 2/4, apply-run-holder 4/5, likely renamed later): next session checks those by anchor. EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS' five held string-store slices stay unlanded by design.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_50 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 50u32, "2026-10-22T10:47Z", "eoie", "06:47 the two partial cases resolved: their missing names were the OLD anchors each slice replaces (apply-ps-cores replaces the process_table header and listing_count; apply-run-holder renames orphaned_job_window to orphaned_window, which is in live eoie_machine_windows), so absence proves landing. Both drained: 12 landed slices in total tonight.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_51 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 51u32, "2026-10-22T10:49Z", "eoie", "06:49 three text-only slices verified by their effect and drained: apply-gate-queue (gate.spi has the 5000 ms waits and slot_gate before windowed_gate), apply-lib-staging (test-regeneration.ps1 has its exact spiralLib staging line), apply-regen-lease (its own guard refuses when test-regeneration.ps1 mentions tree-leases, and it does). 15 landed slices drained tonight. Remaining undecided text slices: note-local-time, authority-reflection, help-coverage, lib-pilot, machine-watch 1+2, census-lib-metrics, plus the release-train composition scripts (apply-r34/r35/rC, neutral fixtures, resume test fix).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_52 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 52u32, "2026-10-22T10:51Z", "eoie", "06:51 five more drained after checking their effect in live src: apply-note-local-time (let local_stamp in agile_note_model), apply-machine-watch and apply-machine-watch-2 (crate eoie_machine_watch with its jobs_watch module), apply-lib-pilot (agile_task_query lists spiral-), apply-census-lib-metrics (all four probe words top-level-macro, rc-wrap, let-block, std-string-use in probes.spi). 20 landed slices drained tonight. Still undecided: authority-reflection, help-coverage, and the release-train composition scripts.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_53 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 53u32, "2026-10-22T10:52Z", "eoie", "06:52 last two checked: apply-help-coverage landed (its guide and memory help lines are in command_spec_domain/model.spi), apply-authority-reflection landed if its two effects are present (union_reflection in authority_state_domain/package.spiproj: 1, authority-state-domain notebook in the registry: 1). Drained what holds. Lab now holds only unlanded material (r36 drafts, held memory string-store slices, the release-train composition scripts and the night carry).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_54 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 54u32, "2026-10-22T10:53Z", "eoie", "06:53 end of the 10-21/22 night run. State for the next session: no eoie release installed tonight; installed eoie.exe is still the r28+r29 binary. Live tree holds ABC's published regeneration (r30-r35) plus the 3 test-only fixes, generic drift and the gh-pages verify step, all uncommitted. Order: (1) launch-ABC-tail.ps1 (prelaunch check first; needs a free heavy slot, ~1h20), (2) launch-D.ps1, (3) preview-E-live.ps1 staying in the turn while it runs, then E, preview-E2-live.ps1, E2. Everything is in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22 (final-summary.md first); carried scripts write to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\release-work. No job, window, lease or process of the eoie lane is live.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_55 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 55u32, "2026-10-22T11:19Z", "eoie", "07:19 new run until 21:00 (user 07:0x). Rule written before launching: D and the new job host (EOIE-JOB-HOST, user request) ship as ONE release DH instead of ABC tail + D: the tree already holds ABC's published regeneration, so a filtered regen of the D + host crates (job gate/slot, machine watch/windows, process table, window claim/query/run, standards, job host, jobs, job launch, job control, dev spiral tests) plus the full candidate/parity/tests/runner/e2e gates installs r30-r35 + D + host together. Applied to the live tree 07:1x (snapshot before-release-D), Cargo.lock updated by cargo metadata --offline, job host model tests 3/3 in place, Spiral preview of the 3 host crates clean (host_run.rs 365, launch.rs 891, jobs.rs 745). Candidate notebooks: D's 6 + notes_cli + table_test_cli. After install, a job host acceptance step starts 3 short jobs and reports how many supervisors are parented by the host. Queued behind main-pack-review2; I stay in the turn while it runs (tonight's reap lesson).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_56 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 56u32, "2026-10-22T11:42Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-22 07:42 rule (set before DH ends): the shared live block (tibia PR-22+PR-23, ~2.5 h) starts once eoie-release-DH, x-precommit-day4 and main-pack-review3 finish, so any heavy job or compile I start after DH delays it. From DH's exit until tibia posts 'block end': no heavy job, no compile window, no cargo; only CPU-free work (drafts, reading, notes). Release F (window admission split, staggered admission, bench) is next once block end shows in eoie window list, then E preview, E, E2 preview, E2. Tie-break: if the block hasn't started 30 min after the last of the three jobs ends, ask main before starting F (a message, not a job).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_57 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 57u32, "2026-10-22T11:54Z", "eoie-lane", "07:54 release F scope (apply-rF.ps1, dry-run clean on a live src copy): window admission split + staggered admission, bench class, --slot-within, and the job host exiting with its home. Runs after tibia's block end (rule in note 56).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_58 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 58u32, "2026-10-22T12:10Z", "eoie-lane", "08:10 DH ended exit 1 after 49 min, not published: candidate notebooks 7/8. stop_cli failed killing_only_the_supervisor... and after_waits..., both on the job host gap (EOIE-JOB-HOST note 5): every start paid the 5 s fallback. Regen and gate were fine (0 files over 1000, max 994 eoie_memory), and the debug build passed. The live tree keeps ABC+D+host sources and DH's published .rs. Installed eoie.exe is unchanged. Next: release F = everything since the last install (ABC, D, host + zero-pid fix, F slices) with 9 candidate notebooks and the stricter host acceptance, launched after tibia's block end. Before launching, a candidate pre-run of stop_cli and windows_cli on F's tree (one compile window, after the block).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_59 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 59u32, "2026-10-22T12:33Z", "eoie-lane", "08:33 train after DH, all dry-run clean on the live tree in order F -> G -> E2. F = host zero-pid fix, window admission split + staggered admission, bench class, --slot-within, host exit with its home, census --baseline-merge. Release script: 9 candidate notebooks, then a candidate host probe right after the debug build (job start in a scratch home must take under 3 s and write host.pid, else blocked before the notebook phase; this is what DH lacked), then the stricter installed-host acceptance. G = E + do-verb family crate and wiring + binomial-band + machine crowding (apply-rG.ps1), preview first for the gate numbers (do_program.rs 988, do_edit.rs 976, experiments.rs 949, analysis.rs 965). E2 = 24-package heal wave after G's preview. Everything is carried in the lab night folder.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_60 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 60u32, "2026-10-22T13:04Z", "eoie-lane", "09:04 G release script ready (release-build-job-G.ps1, carried). The regen filter is the 102 crates whose package graph reaches the 105 packages G changes, computed on the F-applied tree (g-regen-crates.txt; recompute if F changes, and from 'eoie repo affected' once G installs). It runs the 20 CLI notebooks of touched crates and keeps the candidate host probe. Regen timeout is 2400 s for the near-full regen. G doubles as its own preview: regen and the line/topology gate run before any notebook, so a separate preview job would only add CPU. If the gate fails, restore the live tree from the pre-G snapshot (eoie-snapshot.ps1). prelaunch-check now refuses removed-but-used definitions and changed paren balance; it passes on F, G and E2 together.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_61 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 61u32, "2026-10-22T13:20Z", "eoie-lane", "09:20 rule for the afternoon (written before any launch): launch-F at tibia's 'block end' (the watcher reports live-gui gone, or main's message). Launch G only after F ends: if F installed, G applies on top; if F failed on a candidate test, fix the test or slice and relaunch F before G; if F failed in regen or gate, restore before-release-F, fix, relaunch. E2 after G by the same rule. Hard stop for new launches: 19:00 (a release takes 60-100 min, so anything later could not end before 21:00). After 19:00 only reruns of a failed candidate step, never a new regen. Each launch runs its prelaunch-check (slices on a live copy, paren balance, removed-but-used definitions, both heavy slots busy = refuse) and snapshots before applying. Staged in the lab night folder: launch-F/G/E2.ps1 and release-build-job-F/G/E2.ps1 (G 102 regen crates, 21 notebooks; E2 88 crates, 21 notebooks).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_62 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 62u32, "2026-10-22T13:43Z", "eoie-lane", "09:43 rule change, written before any launch: after F, launch GE2 (G plus the E2 heal wave in one release: launch-GE2.ps1, release-build-job-GE2.ps1) instead of G then E2. Measured overlap: G regenerates 111 crates and E2 88, union 118, so E2 adds 7 crates and 3 notebooks (26 total) and saves one full release cycle (~1.5 h of the box) on an afternoon with a 19:00 launch cutoff. If GE2 fails on a candidate test or gate finding inside an E2-only package, drop the wave: restore before-release-GE2, launch G alone, and leave E2 for the next session. A failure elsewhere gets fixed in place and GE2 relaunched.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_63 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 63u32, "2026-10-22T13:51Z", "eoie-lane", "09:51 release H staged (apply-rH.ps1, after GE2): CLI harness adoption (test-only) and the eoie_log_sequences crate as a standalone crate with its two test blocks registered, so its list, listm.rev and GADT idioms get compiled before the table sequences verb is built on them. F1 kill --mine joins H once GE2 is installed, because its anchors are the post-heal text of process_table and launch. H's prelaunch runs on the post-GE2 live tree.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_64 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 64u32, "2026-10-22T13:58Z", "eoie-lane", "09:58 GE2 gate forecast (live generated .rs, no compiler): 19 crates sit at 900+ lines and all are in GE2's regen set. eoie_memory 994, eoie_do_program 988, agile_todo_lines 986, eoie_agile_mutation 981, agile_task_listing 979, agile_task_next 978, eoie_machine_windows 977 (713 after F's split), eoie_do_edit 976, eoie_memory_query 975, eoie_experiment_analysis 965, command_spec_domain 962, eoie_machine_watch 954, eoie_experiments 949, and six more under 947. Expected movement: do_program and do_edit shrink (pipe table and has_run macro become one extern call each); analysis and experiments grow by one test kind (about +10); watch grows by the crowding call and the compile-hold class arms (about +10); the heal waves skip crates at 950+ by guard. The risk is crates that only regenerate because a dependency changed, eoie_memory at 994 above all. Rule, written now: if GE2's line gate lists any crate over 1000, put an export at a crate boundary (the 10-21 fixes: row-mask, job-state, grep split), never trim; check it with a filtered preview of that crate only, then relaunch GE2. Do not drop the wave for a gate overrun.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_65 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 65u32, "2026-10-22T15:57Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 11:34: prelaunch-check gains a typed-boundary guard. sm'.split returns array_base while am'.length/index/try_item take the nominal array; F's census slice passed split output on unwrapped (a type error the paren and removed-definition checks cannot see). Fixed with '|> array' before F started; the same flaw was fixed in GE2 repo-affected and the log-sequences drafts. F requeued as job-1792683581652.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_66 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 66u32, "2026-10-22T16:18Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 12:20 rule, written before the rerun: a regen crate timeout while the box is loaded (another heavy slot held, or free memory under 5 GB), on a crate whose earlier regens took under 15 s and whose code compiled elsewhere in the same run, counts as load, not code. Requeue the release once with the per-crate limit raised to 1200 s. A second timeout of the same crate is a hang: compile that crate alone in a compile window before any further requeue. Case: F, eoie_window_run timeout at 615 s (DH: 2.9 s; the same requested/verdict_text code compiled in eoie_machine_windows in 46 s), with x-precommit-day6 holding the other slot and 2.7-4.6 GB free.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_67 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 67u32, "2026-10-22T17:49Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 13:49 rules for the rest of today, written before the runs: (1) F requeues when tibia's live block releases live-gui (a watcher does it). (2) If F installs and its after-install-F.ps1 probes pass, launch-GE2.ps1 runs at once, provided the launch starts by 19:00; otherwise GE2 carries to the next session. (3) H (launch-H.ps1) needs GE2 installed and never launches today after 19:00. (4) Before GE2 launches, the GE2+H preview of modified crates (stopped at tibia's block start) reruns; any crate at 950+ lines or any type error blocks the launch and gets a crate-boundary fix. (5) After F's spiral tests line, main gets 'past lib reads' for their second landing (write_error_line, am' sort fix, last_write_ms); I, J and K (table sequences, mirror, env) wait for that landing.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_68 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 68u32, "2026-10-22T18:05Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 14:05 lab drain: 36 superseded files deleted from lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN's root (10-21 release scripts for A, B, C, BC and r33-r36, their plans, check outputs and a post-install message draft). Stem check with the Grep tool across all repos: the only references outside the old scripts were night-folder scripts naming their own copies of notebook-check.ps1, eoie-snapshot.ps1 and preview-at.ps1, plus backlog history. Both slice scripts among them had landed (resume_cli no longer asserts 'eoie job list ok'; table logs and experiments fixtures use the neutral words). lab-handoff.ps1's EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN entry was trimmed so a later handoff cannot restore them. Kept: lab-handoff.ps1, the two 10-21 reports, and the night-2026-10-22 folder (today's live tooling).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_69 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 69u32, "2026-10-22T19:16Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 15:16 rule for F after x's run 8, written before the outcome: (1) on x's 'run 8 end', the GE2+H preview reruns first (a few minutes, compile window). (2) If tibia has said no block today, F requeues at once (main's review may share the other heavy slot). (3) If tibia's PR-25 block is on, F requeues at once only if tibia agrees to start PR-25 after F ends; otherwise F waits for tibia's 'block end' and launches only if that comes by 19:00 (the no-new-launch-after-19:00 rule). Failing that, F carries to the next session. (4) GE2 and H do not launch today in any branch, since F cannot finish before ~18:30.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_70 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 70u32, "2026-10-22T21:02Z", "eoie-lane", "17:02 typed release pipeline drafted and tested as a pure model (scratch f5/src/eoie_release_model, HostFree + LibReferenced; F5's release half). The GADT typestate release_run planned -> regenerated -> checked -> published means publish takes only a checked run, so a release without a candidate phase does not type-check (memory release-candidate-cli-run). Each step returns advance next = Advanced run | Stopped reason, and stop_reason encodes today's lessons: RegenIncomplete emitted/selected, CrateOverLimit name/lines (F's eoie_job_launch at 1065), NoCandidateNotebooks (a candidate phase that ran nothing proves nothing), CandidateFailed count. 2 test blocks (the happy path for 'release F' with 18 owners, plus each stop). Cells: 2/2 pass after one parse fix (a record update must start from a variable, now in memory); standards 0 findings. This is the model the 'eoie release start' verb would drive in place of today's per-release launch and job scripts.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_71 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 71u32, "2026-10-22T21:11Z", "eoie-lane", "17:11 F failed (job-1792697313050, exit 1, 98 min): all 18 owners regenerated, then the regen cargo check failed with E0433 in eoie_window_run. eoie_machine_windows/windows.spi calls eoie_window_admission::eoie_window_verdict in a host macro; eoie_window_run opens that package, so the call is expanded into window_run's generated Rust, but window_run's Cargo.toml had no path dependency on eoie_window_admission (the admission split added it only to machine_windows). Nothing was published. Fix applied to the live tree (window_run gains [dependencies] eoie-window-admission). The generated-.rs scan over the staging copy finds no other missing edge, and a compile job verifies the fix in the staging tree. Relaunch rule, written before deciding: F relaunches now only if start + 95 min (today's measured run) ends by 18:15, when x's retry starts (x was promised the slot after F). Otherwise F waits for x's 'retry end' and launches only if that arrives before 19:00 (the no-launch-after-19:00 rule); else it moves to tomorrow's session. Applied at 17:11 : 17:11 + 95 min is past 18:15, and x estimates its retry ends ~19:20, so F moves to tomorrow.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_72 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 72u32, "2026-10-22T21:15Z", "eoie-lane", "17:15 the rule from note 71 is unchanged, but its premise moved: x's retry started at 17:14 (main's review let it run), and x expects 'retry end' about 18:20. So per the rule, F launches when 'retry end' arrives, if that is before 19:00, not tomorrow (note 71's last sentence used x's earlier ~19:20 estimate). Also found by the generated-Rust scan (scratch crate-deps-check.ps1 -Generated): the live tree is not cargo-buildable right now. F's slices are applied but its regeneration never published, so src/eoie_job_launch/launch.rs is the old pre-split file (it still calls eoie_job_gate and eoie_job_after) while launch's Cargo.toml already moved those deps to eoie_job_supervise. F's relaunch regenerates launch.rs and resolves it; until then nobody should cargo-build or commit src/eoie_job_launch alone.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_73 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 73u32, "2026-10-22T21:18Z", "eoie-lane", "17:18 process fix from F's failure: today's composed-tree previews ran test-regeneration without -CargoCheck, so they proved Spiral -> Rust and the line gate, but not Cargo edges. A host macro calling another crate's export lands in every crate that expands it, so the needed path dependencies follow package opens, not the crate's own .spi. preview-ge2h.ps1 and preview-integer.ps1 now pass -CargoCheck (whole staged workspace, the check F failed 70 min in). crate-deps-check.ps1 -Generated scans generated Rust for export calls without a path dependency. It needs regenerated .rs: on a partial preview, a crate outside the filter keeps its stale .rs and is flagged as a false positive (eoie_job_launch's pre-split launch.rs in two of today's previews).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_74 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 74u32, "2026-10-22T21:21Z", "eoie-lane", "17:21 measured and dropped: a static check that follows package.spiproj opens transitively and collects export calls from the opened packages' .spi reports 89 possible missing edges on the live tree and 114 on the GE2+H tree. The live tree's only real gap was the window_run edge (the generated-Rust scan of F's staging tree finds just that one), so about 99% are opened-but-not-expanded false positives, and adding those dependencies would create Cargo cycles (job_gate <-> job_control). Kept: the -CargoCheck preview plus crate-deps-check -Generated over regenerated output. The reach script was deleted.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_75 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 75u32, "2026-10-22T21:31Z", "eoie-lane", "17:31 GE2+H checked for F's failure class with no compile: the generated-Rust scan over only the .rs files today's previews actually regenerated (newer than each staging copy) finds no missing path dependency in the 18-crate GE2+H preview (13a9...), the kill split (1d1a...) or the amend split (711a...). Crates those filters did not regenerate are covered by tomorrow's -CargoCheck preview.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_76 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 76u32, "2026-10-22T21:42Z", "eoie-lane", "17:42 stopped my optional staging-tree cargo check (job-1792703730290) after 26 min: one rustc held 1 GB and tibia stopped a Cells run at 829 MB free. F's own regen cargo check gives the same answer in about an hour, so the early warning was not worth the memory. Rule kept: no extra compile of mine runs beside F.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_77 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 77u32, "2026-10-22T22:07Z", "eoie-lane", "18:07 close rule for F's install, written before any result. after-install-F.ps1 prints one PASS/FAIL row per probe: EOIE-JOB-STOP-WINDOWS, MACHINE-WINDOWS bench, JOBS slot-within and done-within, JOB-MEMORY-CAP, JOB-HOST, standards unknown-rule, GREP-FILE-ROOT, MACHINE-WATCH, RESUME-COMPILER v2, GENERIC-DRIFT team word, TABLE-TEST-WHERE, TABLE-LOGS-VALUES quiet, spec case 40. An item whose only remaining condition is its install probe is set Done (100) on PASS, with the probe row as the note (TABLE-TEST-WHERE, TABLE-LOGS-VALUES, JOB-MEMORY-CAP, GREP-FILE-ROOT, JOB-STOP-WINDOWS, MACHINE-WATCH, GENERIC-DRIFT). Items with work beyond the probe (JOBS, MACHINE-WINDOWS, JOB-HOST, RESUME-COMPILER) get the PASS row as a note and keep their status. A FAIL row is noted on its item, which stays open with the failing output. If F itself fails, nothing closes, and tomorrow starts with F.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_78 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 78u32, "2026-10-22T22:17Z", "eoie-lane", "18:17 F's second run passed regeneration and published at 18:15 (regen exit 0; line gate 0 files over 1000; topology ok, widest crate eoie_memory 994). The window_run dependency fix held. The live tree is cargo-consistent again (crate-deps-check -Generated clean; launch.rs regenerated at 601 lines). The debug build and spiral tests follow.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_79 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 79u32, "2026-10-22T22:32Z", "eoie-lane", "18:32 F's candidate phase found a failure: src/eoie_machine_windows/windows_cli.spi test shared_classes_coexist_and_memory_gates_admission expects 'reason=low-memory free_mb=1000 need_mb=3072' but gets 'free_mb=0'. Cause: F's staggered admission (window_model free_after_settling: a held window counts its needed_mb against free until settle_ms passes, 90 s for heavy-build and test-suite) subtracts the two windows the test granted moments before (1024 + 3072 > 1000), so effective free is 0. The model tests already pin that behavior (free_after_settling 3000 4096 = 0); the CLI expectation predates it and was not updated by the slice. F refuses to publish on any candidate failure, so this run ends at the candidate step without installing. Rule, written before F's exit: if the candidate failures are only expectations made stale by an intended F behavior (checked against the model tests), the expectations are fixed after F's lease ends and F relaunches if the launch is before 19:00, else tomorrow. Any other candidate failure is investigated first, with no relaunch today.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_80 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 80u32, "2026-10-22T22:35Z", "eoie-lane", "18:35 grep of every *_cli.spi for free_mb/need_mb/low-memory assertions (the outputs of the computation the settling change touched) finds 3 lines, all in eoie_machine_windows/windows_cli.spi. Line 35 is a first request on an empty store (nothing settling, 8000 stays right; it passed in F), line 173 is window list (raw free_mb, not admission), and line 59 is the one stale expectation, fixed by windows-cli-settling.do. So windows_cli is the only candidate the settling change breaks.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_81 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 81u32, "2026-10-22T22:36Z", "eoie-lane", "18:36 tail rule, written before F's candidate phase ends (memory release-candidate-cli-run: if only candidate notebooks fail, rerun just those after test-only fixes and continue the remaining steps instead of relaunching regeneration). F continues today as a tail job if all of these hold: (a) F's candidate failures are only expectations made stale by intended F behavior (today: windows_cli line 59); (b) after windows-cli-settling.do, the failed notebooks pass against F's own candidate binary (src/target/debug/eoie.exe, built from the published tree), checked inside the tail before anything else; (c) the tail starts by 19:15. The tail holds a tree lease and runs F's remaining steps unchanged: parity, ratchet, spiral tests, runner, e2e checks, release build, install, host acceptance. The 19:00 no-launch rule targets new regenerations; a tail of an already regenerated and built release is ~60 min with no regen. Peers: tibia's second lib landing moves from 'F end ~19:00' to the tail's spiral-tests line (~19:45); main's combined landing (~20:00+) is not delayed. If (b) fails or the start slips past 19:15, F moves to tomorrow as written in note 79.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_82 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 82u32, "2026-10-22T23:01Z", "eoie-lane", "19:01 GE2+H chain re-checked on today's live tree (after F's publish, the window_run dependency, the host-home and windows_cli fixes, the spec and AGENTS edits): prelaunch-check over apply-rG, apply-rE2-wave and apply-rH passes (anchors apply, paren balance unchanged, no removed definition still in use, new crates covered by GE2's and H's baseline merges). Tooling fix on the way: the removed-definition check matched bare names across unrelated packages. H's harness adoption removes the test helper state_write from agile_planning_rollup, and the check flagged the agile_note_model union of the same name. Uses now count only inside the defining package or packages that list it (which keeps the real catch it was built for: the window functions that job gate and window query still called). -ReleaseScript takes several scripts, for a chained check.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_83 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 83u32, "2026-10-22T23:03Z", "eoie-lane", "19:03 F2 (job-1792708845541) regenerated eoie_job_host and published it, passed the line gate, debug build and the host-home check ('candidate host after its home was removed: alive=False', so the fix works). But its host probe took 4074 ms against a 3000 ms bound (F's run: 518 ms). Each probe copies the 44 MB debug binary into a fresh probe home, under cargo I/O. That marks host-probe as blocked, which skipped the candidates, and F2 cannot publish. Recovery under memory installed-is-done: stop F2 and launch F3 = F2 without regen (the tree already holds F2's output; F3 checks the host-home fix is in host_run.spi). F3's probe gate is structural: host.pid present, the probe job's supervisor (a 5 s ping job) parented by that host, and start under 5000 ms (the detached fallback's delay, the real sign of the dead primary path); the time is reported. Today's rule note 81 (tail by 19:15) is met: launch ~19:05.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_84 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 84u32, "2026-10-22T23:07Z", "eoie-lane", "19:07 F3 (19:03) stopped at 19:06. Its probe proved parentage (supervisor 101612 parented by host 36276), but my probe change created two artifacts: a cold start in a fresh probe home took 13569 ms (first start copies the 44 MB debug supervisor binary, and the copy cost swings: 518, 4074, 13569 ms today), and a 5 s ping child was still running when the home was removed, so the host correctly kept serving (alive=True). F4's probe: a warm-up start first, then a timed start (ping 3 s) that must be under 5000 ms with its supervisor parented by the host, then wait for that job, remove the home, and allow 3 s for the host to exit. Run standalone against the candidate binary before launch: warm-up 496 ms, probe 853 ms, supervisor 96236 parent 45400 = host, host exited after its home was removed: no block. F4 launched at 19:07 (job-1792710435076).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_85 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 85u32, "2026-10-22T23:22Z", "eoie-lane", "19:22 F4 progress: 3/9 candidates pass (machine_windows windows_cli with the settling fix, eoie_cli windows_cli, window_run run_cli); stop_cli (the job-host notebook) is next. My F4 waiters were stopped by Claude Code's low-memory guard at ~19:20 while the session was idle (memory heavy-gate-lessons: idle sessions' background shells get reaped). They are not restarted per the notice; F4 itself runs under the eoie job host, unaffected.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_86 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 86u32, "2026-10-22T23:27Z", "eoie-lane", "19:27 residue found: every release's host probe left its probe home with the 44 MB supervisor copy (the copy was still locked when the probe removed the home, before the host exited). Three such folders (F2-F4) removed by hand just now. The template fix for the next release script: retry the probe home's removal once after the host has exited.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_87 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 87u32, "2026-10-22T23:55Z", "eoie-lane", "19:55 GE2+H re-checked after tonight's tree edits (the kill fix in eoie_process_table/host.spi and the supervisor cache in eoie_jobs/host.spi): prelaunch-check over apply-rG, apply-rE2-wave and apply-rH still passes (anchors, paren balance, removed definitions, baseline merges). Main holds its combined lib landing for my 'past lib reads' after F5's spiral tests.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_88 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 88u32, "2026-10-22T23:58Z", "eoie-lane", "19:58 speedup found while waiting: every regen's -CargoCheck runs cold (~20-25 min: F 17:46-18:12, the verify job 19:48-), because test-regeneration stages into a new eoie-regeneration/<guid> folder and defaults the target directory inside it. test-regeneration.ps1 already takes -TargetDirectory, so release scripts can pass one persistent folder (e.g. spiral-bin\\eoie-regen-target) and cargo check becomes incremental across releases. Rule for adopting it: the next release passes it, and the change is kept if that release's cargo check takes under half the cold time with an identical result.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_89 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 89u32, "2026-10-23T00:08Z", "eoie-lane", "20:08 plan for the next session, in order (each release recovers the same day if it fails: memory installed-is-done): (1) if F5 has not installed: rerun F5 from its failing step, and nothing else is launched first. (2) After the install: post-F.ps1 (runner fix, install probes plus close preview, tree-read probes, lab drain and sync, model previews, parentless audit); close items by the note-77 rule. (3) GE2 preview with -CargoCheck plus crate-deps-check -Generated -Since, then a candidate pre-run of every touched CLI notebook against the preview binary, then GE2. (4) H (claim live rows, host-home gate, process-kill split, log sequences). (5) The console heal as its own wave, then I after main's combined lib landing. Release-script improvements before (3): a persistent -TargetDirectory for regen cargo checks; the probe-home removal retried after the host exits.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_90 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 90u32, "2026-10-23T00:28Z", "eoie-lane", "20:28 F5 queued as job-1792715270554-eoie-release-F5 with --heavy --after-ok job-1792712662424-eoie-kill-verify, so it starts by itself when the verify job ends, whether or not this session is active (my schedule ends at 21:00). F5 = F4's script with no regen (it checks the published process_table.rs holds the kill fix), the validated probe, and stop_cli first among the 9 candidates; any candidate failure blocks publish. Main stopped its three queued heavy jobs and requeues them with --after F5. Expected install ~22:10. The next session starts with post-F.ps1 (probes, close preview, parentless audit) if F5 installed, else with F5's failing step.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_91 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 91u32, "2026-10-23T00:47Z", "eoie-lane", "20:47 the kill-fix verify job (job-1792712662424) hit its own 60-minute wall-clock limit at 20:44, still in the regen's cold cargo check (194 crates on 2 jobs under contention; the windows crate alone took ~6 min). Nothing was published, and F5 (queued --after-ok on it) was skipped. Recovery under installed-is-done: both regenerated files from verify's staging copy (eoie_process_table/process_table.rs with the kill fix, eoie_job_host/host_run.rs with the shared supervisor cache; regen had emitted 2/2) were published into src with test-regeneration's own Set-EoieGeneratedFile (20:46). F6 (job-1792716408661, 20:46) = F5's script; its full debug build re-checks every crate, stop_cli runs first, and any failure blocks the install. Lesson: a verify job that wraps a cold regen needs more than 60 min, or the persistent -TargetDirectory (note 88).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_92 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 92u32, "2026-10-23T00:57Z", "eoie-lane", "20:57 end of run: F6 (job-1792716408661) passed its debug build (exit 0, so the published kill and supervisor-cache fixes compile) and its job-host probe (warm-up 1142 ms, probe start 1948 ms, supervisor 23164 parented by host 127592, host ended after its home was removed). It is now in its 9 candidates (stop_cli first), then spiral tests, release build, install and host acceptance, unattended. Next session: read F6's tail. If it installed: post-F.ps1, then close-after-install.ps1 -Apply after reading the preview, then the parentless audit. If it failed: fix and rerun that step first (installed-is-done). Main's next5 review holds slot 1, with next4, cells-pack and hopacsota serialized after it.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_93 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 93u32, "2026-10-23T03:06Z", "eoie-lane", "23:06 F6 status: debug build, host probe and 9/9 candidates passed (stop_cli included). Its first spiral-tests run failed at 21:50 on a timing assertion under load (eoie_process_observation windows test stdout_consumer_timeout_closes_descendant_pipes, elapsed < 10 s); the retry's cargo tests passed (22:08). Its 81-notebook Cells batch was still running at 23:05, while the shared Cells daemon (cells-13905) logged 'retire requested; the queue is drained' and a new daemon started at 23:00 (not mine). The retry's -TimeoutMs 3600000 is likely to expire. Rule, written before F6 ends: if F6 ends blocked only on tests (candidates passed), launch F7 = F6's steps from the spiral tests on (release-build-job-F7.ps1: lease, tests with -TimeoutMs 7200000, runner, e2e checks, release build, install, host acceptance), unattended. Any other block is investigated first.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_94 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 94u32, "2026-10-23T03:09Z", "eoie-lane", "23:09 the user extended the autonomous run to 07:00 (deadline file re-armed). Main confirmed nobody sent the Cells retire: the shared daemon retires itself below 4096 MB free (compiler_daemon.ex @default_retire_free_mb, env SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_RETIRE_FREE_MB), and free memory sat at 3.6-4.0 GB all evening. F7's script now sets SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_RETIRE_FREE_MB=2048, which applies if its batch starts the daemon. Main holds all its Cells jobs until our spiral-tests batch ends. Night plan in order: F6/F7 install, post-F.ps1 plus the close step plus the parentless audit, then note 89's plan (GE2 preview with -CargoCheck and a candidate pre-run, GE2, H, the console heal, I).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_95 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 95u32, "2026-10-23T03:35Z", "eoie", "23:35 eoie: F6 cannot finish inside its 4 h job limit (child started 20:47, limit ~00:47). The supervisor reads timeout_ms once at child start (eoie_job_supervise supervise.spi:57), so it can't be extended. F6's retry passed the cargo tests, but its 81-notebook batch, running since 22:08, is ~30 done at 2-3 min each, because the shared Cells daemon keeps retiring: free memory ~4000 MB against its 4096 floor, restarts seen at 23:22 and 23:27, cold compile open 45 s. A timeout prints no 'release not published' line, so F7's gate would have refused. F7 now accepts a stopped F6 with 9/9 candidates and no other blocker, and it reuses F6's tests only when F6 passed them and no src/lib source changed after the test run began (scan over 2507 files: 0 changed). The gate block was run standalone against the live F6 and refuses correctly while F6 runs. Tibia was asked to release its night-block window so F7 is admitted first. Lesson: a release job's limit must cover a cold Cells notebook batch under memory pressure; size it from the slowest measured batch, not the warm one.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_96 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 96u32, "2026-10-23T04:16Z", "eoie", "00:16 eoie: F7 failed in 13 s at the spiral tests, both runs: 'build.ps1 -TimeoutMs 7200000' was refused by eoie-dev ('--timeout-ms must be between 1 and 3600000'). My error: job-script-check validates literal arguments against the callee script's ValidateRange, and build.ps1 declared 1..86400000, wider than the eoie-dev binary it calls. Fixed: build.ps1 now declares 1..3600000; positive control: job-script-check flags F7's line 33, and GE2/H/I/F8 pass. F7's lab steps passed (runner 35/40, read 5/5, ps 5/5, hidden window 2/2, timeout tree 2/2, orphan wait 3/3). F8 (job-1792728931011, launched 00:15) is F7 with -TimeoutMs 3600000, a 6 h job limit, and the heavy watchdog aligned to it (heavy-cap-align.ps1, simulated end to end). Its window waits on tibia's live-gui request; tibia asked to release again. Lesson: a wrapper's declared parameter range must equal what its callee accepts, or the static check vouches for values that fail at run time.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_97 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 97u32, "2026-10-23T05:10Z", "eoie", "01:10 eoie: throughput rule, written before any preview. Tonight a release takes ~3 h on this box (cargo tests ~35 min, 81-notebook batch ~2.5 h at ~2 min per notebook under 2-4 GB free, then lab steps, release build, install), and the train behind F is GE2, H, I, J, K: five slots, about two days. Rule: (1) GE2 goes alone and first after F (it carries EOIE-JOB-ENV, P0). (2) H, I, J and K combine into one release HIJK when all of these hold: the chained dry run is clean (prelaunch-check over G, E2, job-env, H, I, J, K), one compile preview of the combined tree regenerates every touched crate under 1000 lines, and the candidate pre-run of the union of their touched CLI notebooks passes. (3) If any of those fail, the failing release drops out and the rest still combine; a candidate failure caught later costs the combined slot, which is the accepted risk. Deadline: decide when GE2 installs.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_98 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 98u32, "2026-10-23T05:36Z", "eoie", "01:36 eoie: HIJK prep. H's hand filter (15 crates) misses what J and K touch (agile_task_query/listing/next, agile_subcommand_domain, eoie_jobs, eoie_job_control, eoie_window_admission/run/query), and K's job start change reaches every package that opens eoie_jobs. Per the transitive-graph rule, the combined filter comes from 'eoie repo affected' over the union of changed packages, a verb that ships with GE2. So the HIJK job script is written after GE2 installs, from that verb's output, not from a hand union. Known inputs: candidates H (ps_cli, todo_cli, planning_cli, windows_cli), I (sequences_cli, mirror_cli, env_cli), J (next_cli, a list CLI notebook, stop_cli), K (windows_cli, stop_cli); new-package baseline merges H (eoie_log_sequences, eoie_process_kill) and I (eoie_table_sequences, eoie_mirror, eoie_env_pins).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_99 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 99u32, "2026-10-23T06:06Z", "eoie", "02:06 eoie: F8 progress. Notebook batch at 41 of 81 at 02:03 (70 min in). 26 of the remaining 40 are CLI notebooks (1.5-7 min each; notes_cli took 7), so the batch ends ~03:35, then lab steps (~6 min), release build (1-5 min incremental), install ~03:50-04:00. The Cells daemon retired once at 01:45 (free under its 2048 floor) and restarted cold. tibia's night block (give-up 04:40) starts when F8 and main's next5d release their heavy windows.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_100 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 100u32, "2026-10-23T06:25Z", "eoie", "02:25 eoie: GE2 launch checklist for the morning, written now. (1) After tibia's block (~06:15): libgate-copy.ps1 on main's landed lib (env snapshot/restore, last_write_ms, append_all_text; -RawOut kept), then lib_land.ps1 with the recorded tree hashes. (2) GE2 preview: regen of GE2's filter with -CargoCheck into the persistent target, crate-deps-check -Generated -Since, every crate under 1000 lines. (3) Candidate pre-run, per the memory rule, in compile windows outside the heavy slot: build the candidate from the preview tree and run the touched CLI notebooks, stop_cli first (it carries the env test), then windows_cli and the probe block (host priority Normal, env). (4) launch-GE2.ps1 only when (2) and (3) pass. This runs past 07:00, so the morning report says where it stands.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_101 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 101u32, "2026-10-23T06:54Z", "eoie", "02:54 eoie: F8 result. Spiral tests 268 of 269 (cargo tests all green, 80 of 81 notebooks): stop_cli after_waits_for_the_named_job_and_after_ok_skips_when_it_failed failed with 'missing state=queued ... state=finished', because the first job slept only 1500 ms and, under load, starting the second and third jobs took longer than that. The same test passed in F6's candidate run. The failed test also left its fixture home and host behind (EOIE-JOB-HOST note 21). F8's rule then started a full 2.5 h retry. Decision (memory R13 recovery: rerun only what failed after a test-only fix, then continue): stopped F8 at 02:50, changed the first job's sleep to 8000 ms in stop_cli.spi, and queued F9 (job-1792738426322). Its gate requires F8's log to show exactly one failure, in stop_cli, with no cargo failure, and no src change since F8's test run except that file (tested standalone: 1 of 269, 0 cargo, only stop_cli.spi changed); then it reruns stop_cli on the candidate and does F8's lab steps, release build and install. Stopping F8 released its window, and tibia's live-gui request (waiting since 00:16, older than anything new) was granted at 02:50. Any release after F8 was behind that request, and F8's own retry would have run past tibia's 04:40 give-up, so F9 now starts at block end (~05:00-05:45); tibia chose to keep the block since its live runs had begun.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_102 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 102u32, "2026-10-23T07:19Z", "eoie", "03:19 eoie: prelaunch over the whole chain (G, E2, job-env, host priority, host cwd, container breakaway, H, J, K; I waits for main's lib) caught two surplus ')' in tonight's test lines: the window-wait CLI test and K's job floor test. Both fixed; the line-level paren scan (scratch paren-lines.ps1) over all 19 slices drafted tonight is now clean. The one remaining finding is expected: the new crate eoie_window_wait needs '--baseline-merge' in the release script that carries K (HIJK's script, written after GE2 per note 98). K also gained the unknown-option refusal promised on EOIE-JOBS note 45 ('unknown option --x' for a label, and 'the program cannot start with --'), with two CLI test lines.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_103 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 103u32, "2026-10-23T07:22Z", "eoie", "03:22 eoie: HIJK drafted for the combine rule (note 97), to use only if GE2 installs and the rule's preview and candidate pre-run pass. launch-HIJK.ps1 refuses unless no release is running, no exclusive window holds or waits, the installed eoie answers 'repo affected' (GE2 installed), and the lib has write_error_line, last_write_ms, append_all_text and environment_restored. It then runs job-script-check and prelaunch over H, I, J, K, snapshots, hashes src before and after the four chains to find the changed packages, and computes the regen filter with 'eoie repo affected src <changed>' (package directory names, verified in affected.spi) into hijk-filter.txt. release-build-job-HIJK.ps1 is H's tested script with that filter, the six new-package baseline merges (log_sequences, process_kill, table_sequences, mirror, env_pins, window_wait) and 14 candidate notebooks covering what the four releases touch.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_104 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 104u32, "2026-10-23T07:26Z", "eoie", "03:26 eoie: morning checklist, step (2) scripted: preview-GE2.ps1 copies src, spec and compiler-contracts (no target, .cache) to a scratch root, applies GE2's six slices, regenerates GE2's filter with -CargoCheck into the persistent target (-KeepStaged), and lists generated files over 1000 lines. It refuses until lib env.environment_restored has landed. Run it as a heavy job after main's lib landing and my lib gate; read preview-GE2.log for the line counts if the staging copy differs from the root. Full order: block end -> F9 -> post-F (host hygiene, probes, closes, drains) -> main lands lib -> libgate-copy -> lib_land -> preview-GE2 (heavy) -> candidate pre-run -> launch-GE2.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_105 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 105u32, "2026-10-23T07:34Z", "eoie", "03:34 eoie: tonight's tail decisions are now typed, as a first step toward release verbs. The release model (scratch f5/src/eoie_release_model) gains predecessor_end (Installed | BlockedOn step | StoppedOrTimedOut), test_record (failed, failing_files, cargo_failed, changed_beyond_fix) and tail_plan (NothingToDo | ReuseTests | RerunFailedNotebooks | RerunAllTests | RefuseTail reason), with tail_plan_of choosing exactly what F7, F8 and F9 decided by hand. Test block: F6 stopped mid-tests -> rerun all; F8 one failing file -> rerun failed notebooks; passed tests -> reuse; two failing files -> rerun all; changed tree -> refuse; a non-test stop -> refuse; installed -> nothing. Cells check in post-F's model previews. Next: a release tail verb computes test_record from the predecessor's log, as F9's gate does now in PowerShell.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_106 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 106u32, "2026-10-23T08:09Z", "eoie", "04:09 eoie: full-chain prelaunch is clean at 04:09. Ten slices on a live copy: G, E2, job-env, host priority, host cwd, container breakaway, host no-inherit, H, J, K. Paren balance is unchanged everywhere, no removed definition is still in use, and the new-package baseline requirement is met by release-build-job-HIJK.ps1 (window_wait among its six merges). I still waits for main's lib landing, then joins the HIJK check.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_107 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 107u32, "2026-10-23T09:07Z", "eoie", "05:07 after-install-HIJK.ps1 written (fixture backlog, jobs home and windows home only): EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG, agile --words, job amend --timeout on a queued job, order-free start options (--max-private-mb before --after keeps the label), window events.log, window --min-free-mb (1 MB granted, 999999 MB with --wait 0 not granted), window wait-clear. Negative control on a scratch copy of the installed 10-21 binary: 0/7 pass. The first draft had 2 vacuous passes (the old binary refused my label case for another reason, and silently ignores unknown window flags), both reshaped before the control was accepted. after-install-GE2.ps1 gained GE2's core probes (job env adoption, pipe release, breakaway) on the installed binary; post-F runs them against F9's binary as their positive control (all three must FAIL there).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_108 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 108u32, "2026-10-23T09:33Z", "eoie", "05:33 formatter rebase built and proven (scratch fmt-rebase/fmt-rebase.ps1). main's 05:08 formatter pass (user's rules, 71 eoie files) broke my slice anchors: 21 of the files my GE2..K chain edits were reformatted, 17 with token changes. Rebase: slices apply to the unformatted equivalents (main's backup originals for GE2; the previous stage's raw output for later stages), the same formatter DLL (main's command, byte-identical with the next composite) formats only the files the slices changed, untouched formatted files stay live, and -Land writes only files whose live hash still equals the copy's (snapshot-relative deltas; never removes a file the slices didn't). GE2 dry run 05:3x: 7 slices clean, 20 files re-formatted, delta 323 writes, 1 removal, no formatter refusals. Determinism: format(original) == live for 2 untouched files; slot.spi's diff is exactly the heal change. launch-GE2 now runs prelaunch with -Originals and lands through fmt-rebase -Land after the snapshot. HIJK: fmt-rebase -Stage HIJK -RawFrom GE2 once GE2 has landed (it refuses if live moved from GE2's final hashes).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_109 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 109u32, "2026-10-23T09:48Z", "eoie", "05:48 HIJK composes on GE2 through the rebase (dry, -Live = GE2's rebased tree): H, J and K apply clean, 6 formatted files changed and were re-formatted, delta 54 writes, 0 removals. I stops at apply-mirror-check's guard (lib file_system.last_write_ms has not landed yet), as designed; rerun the full H,I,J,K dry once my lib lands (~06:55, after main's fiscal gate).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_110 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 110u32, "2026-10-23T10:16Z", "eoie", "06:16 release L scripted and composed: release-build-job-L.ps1 (from HIJK's: 3 candidate notebooks grep_cli, accept-review review.spi, notebook progress model; baseline-merge of the 2 new crates; job-script check ok) and launch-L.ps1 (refuses unless HIJK is installed, i.e. window wait-clear exists; prelaunch -Originals HIJK raw; lands via fmt-rebase -Stage L -RawFrom HIJK). Dry chain: GE2 -> H,J,K -> L applies clean (L: 3 slices, 2 formatted files re-formatted, delta 19 writes, 0 removals). Found and fixed on the way: the grep-hint slice anchored on the pre-G text, but G's heal had already turned grep.spi's receipt line into ++# and added open sm'_operators; it now anchors on the healed form, which is what it meets after GE2. Release I's slices stay unproven until the lib lands (apply-mirror-check guards on last_write_ms).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_111 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 111u32, "2026-10-23T10:18Z", "eoie", "06:18 after-install-L.ps1 written (fixture files and dirs only): accept-review (literal-only exit 0, boolean flip exit 1 naming line 3 BOOLEAN), grep regex hint (literal alternation hints, --regex matches 2 without a hint), notebook progress (a fake run_notebook.ps1 batch with --path x2 and --output-dir holding one fresh report: machine watch must print 'pid <n> notebook batch: 1 of 2 written'). Negative control on the installed binary: 0/3, each for the right reason; the fake batch process is stopped afterwards. close-after-install.ps1 gains -Stage L (closes all three on PASS).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_112 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 112u32, "2026-10-23T10:40Z", "eoie", "06:40 GE2 preview running (job-1792751959794-eoie-preview-GE2, heavy slot, host-parented). Left for the next session: read its log (preview-GE2.log; regen exit, cargo check, crates over 1000 lines), then the candidate pre-run and launch-GE2; and the full H,I,J,K dry rebase on GE2 now that last_write_ms is in the lib (I's mirror-check guard passes).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_113 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 113u32, "2026-10-23T11:59Z", "eoie", "07:59 measured on hotfix HP: test-regeneration -Filter '^(eoie_job_host)$' regenerated the one crate in 38 s, but its -CargoCheck then checked the whole workspace (CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, under load), 45+ min, while main waited on the slot. Rule for the next small release: the regen's cargo check covers only the filtered crates plus their dependents ('eoie repo affected' gives the list once GE2 installs; until then the filter crates and eoie-cli), and the full-workspace check stays in the big releases. Drafted as a change to the release scripts, not to test-regeneration.ps1's default.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_114 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 114u32, "2026-10-23T12:25Z", "eoie", "08:25 formatter change (main 08:2x, user-flagged): the next5d DLL joins authored leading then lines onto their if line, and the user wants authored then placement kept, so 5d must not run again. fmt-rebase.ps1 now reads its DLL from fmt-rebase/formatter.txt and refuses when it is missing or names pack-next5d. Plan agreed with main: after HP's lease ends, main re-formats from the pre-05:08 originals with 5e only the eoie files still byte-equal to its 5d output and sends the list; I configure the 5e DLL, re-format host_run.spi (landed by HP through 5d) myself, and re-record the rebase's expected hashes from the live tree before GE2.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_115 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 115u32, "2026-10-23T12:42Z", "eoie", "08:42 mistake to keep: I stopped HP (probe artifact) after queueing HP-tail, assuming main's waiting jobs were chained --after HP and so held no slot ticket. main-am-any-gate already held an older ticket and took slot 2 at once; HP-tail waits behind it. heavy-gate-lessons already says a stop hands the slot to the oldest waiting request; the check I skipped: read every waiting job's slot file (waiting ticket=...) before stopping, and only count on a slot when no older ticket exists.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_116 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 116u32, "2026-10-23T13:29Z", "eoie", "09:29 lesson from three restarts of HP in one morning: each candidate gate that rested on ONE timing sample (a 3-s probe job vs a CIM lookup, a 20-s pipe limit, a 5-s start budget) failed under load while the property it guards held (verified each time with the same binary). Rule for every timing gate in release scripts: assert the property, not a single duration; when a duration is the property, take a second sample before blocking and report both. Applied to the HP-tail script; carry it into GE2, HIJK and L before they launch.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_117 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 117u32, "2026-10-23T13:31Z", "eoie", "09:31 carried HP's lessons into the waiting releases before any of them launched: release-build-job-GE2, -HIJK and -L now probe with a 30-s job, report a vanished supervisor as gone (never parent 0), stop the probe job instead of waiting it out, and retry one slow start sample before blocking. Also found: all three still read the host pid at jobs/host.pid, which HP moves to jobs/shell-host/pid, so every post-HP candidate probe would have found no host and blocked; now shell-host\\pid. All three parse and pass the job-script check.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_118 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 118u32, "2026-10-23T14:58Z", "eoie", "11:05 eoie: release M drafted after L (scratch launch-M.ps1, release-build-job-M.ps1). Slices: ci-parity (eoie ci parity), agile-records (formatted-agile reader at 18 load sites), job-rechain (job after + job chain); the window-backfill slice was withdrawn (EOIE-MACHINE-WINDOWS note 32). Launch gates: L installed (crate gate verb), lib gaps landed (lib-gaps/apply-lib-gaps.ps1, after main's lib land). New candidate gate: agile-records/byte-identity.ps1 (6 read verbs plus note and set give the same answers on a raw and a 5e-formatted backlog copy; refuses unless the formatted copy spans more lines); its positive control on the current binary runs after tibia's block, since it formats a 5 MB file. Candidate notebooks 12, baseline merges for the 3 new crates. after-install-M: 3 checks, positive control 0/3 on the installed binary.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_119 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 119u32, "2026-10-23T15:09Z", "eoie", "11:09 eoie: the train's stage-to-stage rule is now typed data in the release model (scratch f5/src/eoie_release_model): train_decision_of (installed stage, acceptance tally, machine state, following stage) -> TrainStopped reason | WaitForMachine holder | LaunchNext stage | TrainComplete. The rules: only a full tally launches, an empty tally proves nothing, and an exclusive window waits. Test the_train_launches_only_after_full_acceptance_on_a_free_machine. It is the spec of today's scratch chain-next.ps1 (GE2 -> HIJK -> L -> M, each launched by the previous stage's after-install pass), which a future eoie release train verb replaces; the notebook check runs after tibia's block.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_120 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 120u32, "2026-10-23T16:38Z", "eoie", "12:38 eoie: GE2 preview 1 (11:38-12:34, compile class) stopped at regen: cargo check --locked refused because GE2 adds crates and the preview copy never refreshed Cargo.lock (release scripts do: 'cargo metadata --offline' first). The chain gate worked: 'GE2 preview regen did not pass; GE2 not launched'. Fixed in preview-GE2.ps1 (lock refresh on the preview src before regen) and requeued 12:37. Lesson for the release-check verb: the lock refresh is part of applying slices, not of the release build.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_121 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 121u32, "2026-10-23T17:48Z", "eoie", "13:48 eoie: GE2 preview 2 PASSED (12:37-13:46, compile class; job-1792773461098): 4 slices onto the unformatted equivalents of 28 formatted files, 19 changed and re-formatted by 5e, tree delta 322 writes and 1 removal; lock refresh exit 0; regen plus cargo check exit 0; 0 generated files over 1000 lines. The chain (job-1792775390563, 8 h limit) now waits for main's review job (main asked no Normal compiles beside its full matrix), then launches GE2, then chain-next runs GE2's acceptance before HIJK.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_122 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 122u32, "2026-10-23T18:00Z", "eoie", "14:00 eoie: release M's slices checked on the tree they will land on (scratch m-on-l.ps1: fmt-rebase/L-dry2/work, the full post GE2, HIJK and L tree), not only the live tree. Two would have failed at launch: ci-parity anchored its usage line on 'adoption [--days n] [--out <file.tsv>]', which L's adoption-habits slice extends with [--habits], and job-rechain anchored on the end of job_usage, which J's job amend extends. Fixed (scratch fix-m-anchors.ps1): ci parity's usage goes after 'machine watch [--sample-seconds n]' (stable through L), and job after/chain is inserted at the start of job_usage, stacking with job doctor's in either order. All 4 M slices now apply on both trees; post-L unions read JobStop, JobAfter, JobChain, JobAmend, JobDoctor and VerbResume, VerbCi, VerbCrate, VerbEnv, VerbMirror. Rule for later releases: dry-run each release's slices on its predecessor's work tree before calling it ready.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_123 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 123u32, "2026-10-23T18:02Z", "eoie", "14:02 eoie: release N drafted (scratch launch-N.ps1, release-build-job-N.ps1, after-install-N.ps1; derived from M by derive-n.ps1). Slices: apply-heal-lines.ps1 (8 packages onto lib line primitives; dry run clean on the post-M tree) and agile-records/apply-agile-records.ps1 (formatted-agile reader). Launch gates: M installed (job doctor answers), lib has am'.push_back, sm'.nonempty_line_at and the typed concat_array (lib-gaps landed after main's lib land). Candidate: byte-identity gate (needs a formatter that formats agile.spi: main's 5f; 5e fails on the one astral character), 15 notebooks (records model, 6 agile CLI notebooks, the 8 healed packages' notebooks), baseline merge for eoie_agile_records. Acceptance: byte identity on the installed binary, one-call spec >= 39, shared backlog list. Not chained yet: chain-next's order stays GE2, HIJK, L, M until 5f and the lib landing exist; the positive control of after-install-N waits for main's matrix end.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_124 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 124u32, "2026-10-23T19:39Z", "eoie", "15:39 eoie: requirement from today's evidence (memory recompile-drafts-after-compiler-change): when the installed compiler changed after a queued release's last compile, the train must run a regen + cargo check preview of that release's crates on the current compiler before landing it. Case: H's stamp_in compiled on 10-22 13:50, and by 10-23 15:29 a codegen regression (RUST-FNMUT-CAPTURE-MOVE, main) made it a Rust E0507. HIJK would have landed, then failed at regen, leaving a broken live tree and a stopped train. Shape for the verb: 'eoie release preview <stage>' records the compiler hash it compiled with; 'release launch' refuses when that hash differs from the installed one. Until then, a manual HIJK preview is queued after main's install.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_125 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 125u32, "2026-10-23T22:02Z", "eoie", "18:02 eoie: rule written before acting. A time-boxed live block outranks a release build without a deadline. tibia requested a 4-stage live-gui block at 18:0x (latest start 20:00, ends 21:00). GE2's release is mid-regen (61/120 crates at 18:01, about 90 min of regen left, then cargo check, build, tests and acceptance), so its heavy-build window would hold the machine past 21:00 and tibia's block would never start. Action: stop my eoie-preview-L-dry2 and eoie-release-GE2 jobs (both mine). GE2's sources stay landed in the tree; only build and publish rerun. A plain waiter job requeues release-build-job-GE2 (heavy, 361 min) and chain-next GE2 -> HIJK once no live-gui window is held or waiting and no tibia-block job runs, the same condition chain-next uses. Cost: about 2.2 h of regen CPU redone overnight.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_126 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 126u32, "2026-10-23T22:23Z", "eoie", "18:23 eoie: release Q added (derive-q.ps1). It carries heal wave 1 (eoie_receipt, eoie_job_supervise open, workspace_primitives measured_sizes), heal wave 2 (heal-crate on eoie_experiment_amend and eoie_machine_crowding, both leaf packages with 0 dependents; control: the same query finds 19 dependents of eoie_jobs) and do write <file> [overwrite] <<< >>>. The train order is now GE2, HIJK, L, M, O, N, Q, P; P rebases on Q and stays last behind its gate. Q's slices are not typechecked yet (no compiles during tibia's block); the rule is that Q launches only after its 5 candidate notebooks pass on a post-N scratch tree, and failing that, Q's slices leave the train before N installs. after-install-Q control on today's eoie: 1/5 (append receipt PASS, which confirms the expected format on the current binary; the 3 write checks fail with 'unsupported statement: write'; spec 39 < 41 until L/M/O).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_127 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 127u32, "2026-10-23T22:45Z", "eoie", "18:45 eoie: composition check of the train's tail, file operations only. On a copy of the post-M tree with O's 3 slices applied, N's slices (heal-lines, agile-records) apply cleanly. agile-records touches agile_task_notes and agile_note_edit, which O's note-as-first had just changed, and its anchors hold. Then Q's 3 slices and P's slice apply cleanly on that post-N copy. So O -> N -> Q -> P compose in train order; each launch's prelaunch check still re-verifies on the real raw output. HIJK's prelaunch passed on the real post-GE2 tree at 18:0x. L and M were composed on the L-dry2 chain earlier; their real check comes at launch.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_128 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 128u32, "2026-10-23T22:47Z", "eoie", "18:47 eoie: the GE2 requeue waiter had a dead predicate. Its function was named Clear, PowerShell resolves aliases before functions, so it ran Clear-Host (16 KB of cursor errors on stderr) and was never true, and GE2 would not have requeued tonight. I caught it from the job's growing stderr byte count, stopped it (exit 143), renamed the predicate MachineClear, tested it both ways (False with tibia's live-gui held, True on empty scratch stores), and restarted it as job-1792795583492. eoie-first follow-up: once K installs, these waiters become one call, 'eoie window wait-clear live-gui,compiler-install --settle 10', so no hand-written loop is left to get wrong. Memory check-scripts-by-data-flow records the lesson.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_129 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 129u32, "2026-10-23T23:16Z", "eoie", "19:16 eoie: found and fixed two train failures that my dry trees had hidden. Every dry run since 08:09 used fmt-rebase/L-dry2, built at 05:30, before HP's host rewrite (07:09) and GE2's 15:00 landing. New tool, scratch chain-emulate.ps1: it copies the live tree, overlays GE2's raw equivalents of its formatted files (exactly what fmt-rebase gives HIJK), then applies every stage's slices in train order, stopping on any anchor refusal or nonzero exit; no formatter is needed, so it runs during a live block. First run: HIJK, L, M, N and P apply; O's direct-verb-lines failed (its captured help region didn't exist; the real one is 5,348 chars and the real union has 22 verbs, including VerbProcess from L's start-under-shell), and Q's do-write failed (the raw run.spi keeps empty_write_tally on one line). Fixes: make-blocks takes -Tree and gained VerbProcess (22 verbs print 19 lines), with blocks regenerated from the emulated post-M tree; do-write's tally swap accepts both layouts. Second run: all 30 slices of HIJK..P apply on the real base. q-typecheck now typechecks on the emulated q-live tree, not the stale m-on-l. Lesson: dry-run on an emulation of the real raw chain, rebuilt after every landing or install, never on a tree older than the last landing.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_130 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 130u32, "2026-10-23T23:21Z", "eoie", "19:21 eoie: verb design distilled from the scratch scripts the train ran on today. Each verb replaces one script, and the bugs each script grew today are listed as tests. (1) 'eoie release emulate <stage>... [--from <raw-stage>]': chain-emulate (live tree plus the previous stage's raw/ overlay, then each stage's slices in order); FAIL on an anchor refusal or nonzero exit; receipt stages=N slices=M failed=K. Test: a tree older than the last landing is refused, because it hid 2 broken anchors today. (2) 'eoie release preview <stage>': regen plus cargo check over the stage's affected crates. It records the compiler hash and --timeout is capped at regen's max (today's 2400 > 1800 died silently), and it exits nonzero on failure (today's script exited 0). (3) 'eoie release launch <stage>': gates (no release queued, no exclusive window, predecessor installed, typecheck marker, lib needs), then snapshot, rebase, land, filter, then the heavy job under window run tree-read. Refuses on a compiler hash mismatch with the preview. (4) 'eoie release accept <stage>': runs the stage's acceptance checks; n/n is required. (5) 'eoie release chain <stage>...': the train as data, one queued job per stage, after-ok on the previous one; waiting uses 'window wait-clear live-gui,compiler-install --settle 10' (no hand-written predicate: today's Clear-alias bug). (6) 'eoie release yield <stage>': stop a running release for a time-boxed block and requeue it after the block (today's 18:02 manual sequence). Stage definitions (slices, notebooks, acceptance, gates) live in one typed record per stage, not in derive-x.ps1 string rewrites, so adding stage Q is one record and not a 40-line derive script.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_131 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 131u32, "2026-10-23T23:21Z", "eoie", "19:21 eoie: first piece of the verb design drafted as a pure model (scratch f6/src/eoie_release_stages/model.spi): a stage record (name, raw_from, slices, notebooks, acceptance, gates as a stage_gate union) and chain validation into a chain_problem union (ChainEmpty, WrongPredecessor, NoSlices, NoAcceptance, RepeatedStage). Tests: tonight's GE2..P train validates; the hand-made mistake from today (N still rebasing on M after O was inserted) is named 'N rebases on M but follows O'; empty stage and empty train are named. Typecheck after the block.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_132 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 132u32, "2026-10-23T23:48Z", "eoie", "19:48 eoie: do-split joins release Q (its slices are now heal wave 1, heal wave 2, do write, do split); q-typecheck probes eoie_do/run.spi too (10 rows). after-install-Q gains 2 checks. 'do mixes edits and writes': one program edits mixed.txt, appends to it and writes made.txt, and all three effects must show. 'a failed edit skips the writes': a missing anchor must leave never.txt unwritten. The second one alone passes even on today's eoie, which refuses mixed programs outright, so it only counts together with the first, and Q's acceptance needs both. Re-emulation on the real base: all slices of HIJK..P apply in train order, do-split included.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_133 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 133u32, "2026-10-24T00:56Z", "eoie", "20:57 Q typecheck (post-block, 20:41) FAILED and the gate kept Q from launching. Two causes:\n(1) Harness, not Q: chain-emulate trees had no src\\spiral lib link. Cells mounts siblings only, so all 8 spiral- notebooks died with 'Package ...cells-mounts/<hash>/spiral is not loaded' before compiling. chain-emulate now junctions the live lib after the slices run. A first version made the link before the slices; lib write times since 20:40 show nothing touched.\n(2) A real Q bug: do-write-file\\apply-do-write-file.ps1 lost the trailing newline of two here-string replacements, merging the 'write_parsed' head into its first body line (grammar.spi:63) and 'read_run' likewise (run.spi). Fixed with + newline; backup .before-newline-fix.\nchain-emulate now prints a FAIL row for any merged definition line (positive control: 2 sites in the old post-train tree; live tree: 0), so this class can't slip through again. Rerun job-1792803027880-eoie-q-typecheck-2 is queued after the edit-where typecheck.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_134 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 134u32, "2026-10-24T02:35Z", "eoie", "22:35 GE2 release FAILED 21:58 (job-1792803641786, exit 1, chain skipped) on the topology gate: agile_task_listing 1084, eoie_experiment_analysis 1030, eoie_job_supervise 1062, eoie_memory 1040 generated lines (note 64 forecast 19 crates at 900+). They grew from GE2's 15:00 source landing (typed status unions etc.); nothing was published, but the live tree's generated .rs are from the refused regen. No waiter was armed, so it surfaced only in the 22:1x process audit. Next: split the 4 crates at crate boundaries (heal-crate 950 rule), regen + cargo preview on the 22:27 compiler, relaunch GE2. Also fixed a real HIJK bug: tree-read\\apply-heavy-one-limit.ps1 (via apply-rH) left heavy_wrapper's concat5 with 4 arguments (string -> string where string was expected); the Q typecheck caught it in crowding.spi. Found with a new chain-emulate -Watch <file>, which names the slice that changes a file. Backup: .before-arity-fix.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_135 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 135u32, "2026-10-24T02:51Z", "eoie", "22:51 progress on the GE2 stall. The Q typecheck now PASSES (10/10 notebooks, 22:42, main's 22:27 compiler) after the heavy-one-limit arity fix. Edit-where typechecks: scope.spi 2/2 pass, and program.spi has only an unlinked-crate E0433; my gate flags it as 'hard' because only probe rows are exempt, which is a gate gap, not a code error. Crate splits for GE2's topology gate: eoie_job_supervise is drafted (crate-splits\\supervise-split.do + -files.do). job_environment_adopted moves into a new 4-file crate eoie_job_env, called across the crate boundary; that function alone was 121 of supervise.rs's 1062 generated lines, so the expected result is ~940. The other three (agile_task_listing 1084: JSON/table printing ~250; eoie_experiment_analysis 1030: analyzed_plan 226; eoie_memory 1040: memory_run 153 + rendering) need splits along domain seams, then a regen + cargo preview on the new compiler before GE2 relaunches.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_136 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 136u32, "2026-10-24T02:58Z", "eoie", "22:58 crate splits: eoie_memory drafted (crate-splits\\memory-split.do + -files.do). memory_import + identical_count move into a new crate eoie_memory_import (lib-referenced, concat5 migrated to ++#), called as eoie_memory_import::eoie_memory_import(dir, data); expected memory.rs ~820 from 1040. Both splits apply on the post-train tree. Still open: eoie_experiment_analysis 1030 (the median path is only 44 lines, which reaches 986, under the gate but over the 950 margin; the real seam is a measurement crate for tallied/early_rows/values_of/terms_of/arm_counts, ~290 lines, returning a typed tuple like eoie_table_rows_kept does) and agile_task_listing 1084 (printing ~250). Each needs a regen to confirm the counts.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_137 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 137u32, "2026-10-24T04:16Z", "eoie", "00:16 which items install with tonight's chain (IDs cited by each stage's slices, wrappers expanded): GE3 GE2-CRATE-SPLITS; HIJK AGILE-FIND, JOB-AMEND, MACHINE-WINDOWS, NEXT-FITS-NOW (part 1), SHOW-NOTE-FILTER, UNION-REFLECTION, WINDOW-LIVE-QUEUE, WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR; L ACCEPT-REVIEW, ADOPTION-HABITS, CRATE-GATE, EXPERIMENTS, GREP-REGEX-HINT, HEAL-BOUNDARY, NEXT-FITS-NOW (part 2), SLOT-FILE-SETTLED, START-UNDER-SHELL; M CI-PARITY, JOB-RECHAIN, JOBS-DOCTOR, ONE-CALL, SHOW-NOTE-FILTER, STANDARDS-CHECKS; O AGILE-ROOT-FLAG, LOG-SEQUENCES, UNION-REFLECTION; N AGILE-FORMATTED-WRITER; Q EDIT-BATCH, LIB-REUSE; P QUEUED-JOBS-IN-HOST; R JOB-START-SETTLE, SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE (all EOIE- prefixed). An item whose only remaining work is its install should not be re-drafted; check its stage's after-install verdict (chain-<stage>.txt) instead.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_138 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 138u32, "2026-10-24T05:37Z", "eoie", "01:3x whole-train regen + cargo check (train-cargo-check.ps1 over the emulated post-R tree, current compiler) found 6 crates that would fail their stage's release regen; none of them showed up in emulation or notebook typechecks. Causes and fixes, all made in the slice sources before their stages launch (tonight's chain is at GE3):\n(1) L notebook-progress: the draft project in f5 already listed 'progress', and the slice added it again -> 'Duplicate name'. Now added only if missing.\n(2) L next-fits: fitting_loads used concat5 in query.spi, which (since GE2) opens sm'_operators only -> unbound. Now '++#'.\n(3) M job-rechain: copies after.spi wholesale from a stale f6 draft that predated after.spi's move to lib -> 'open rust_std_string' unbound, and it would have undone the migration. f6 copy converted (open sm'_operators, 3 concat5 -> ++#), keeping its re-read-the-after-file logic; backup .before-lib-merge.\n(4) N agile-records, agile_title_notes: its write check used 'raw', which only from_title_entry defines; title_moved now takes ~raw and the call passes it.\n(5) N agile-records, eoie_resume: records_text was called unqualified in a file that doesn't open agile_task_text.model; now agile_task_text.model.records_text.\n(6) eoie_table_test: broken by my own GE3 split, which changed analysis.median_terms to take two floats while table_test passes a band string. GE3 had already landed and its release regen covers eoie_table_test, so a live hotfix (crate-splits\\analysis-median-api.do: band-string median_terms restored as a wrapper over median_terms_between) went in at 01:26, before GE3 got a slot. Verified by regenerating both crates from live: both ok, analysis 986 lines. analysis.spi is not in GE3's formatted set, so HIJK's hash guard is unaffected.\nProcess fixes: train-cargo-check now closes over reverse dependencies from package.spiproj (dependents of a changed API compile with it) and names each failing crate's first error. The rerun with all fixes is job-1792819874751.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_139 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 139u32, "2026-10-24T07:07Z", "eoie", "03:07 next train scaffolded during tibia's compile-free block (scratch next-train\\PLAN.md): S1 jobs/processes (owner-parented hosts, doctor --unwatched; job-expect joins after its typecheck), S2 windows/tables (window announce, table empty cells), S3 hygiene/agile (standards duplicate-entry rule, note-edit guards rebased onto post-R, adoption label). Per stage: a slice wrapper that applies on post-R and is idempotent, launch/build scripts derived from R's, and an acceptance script negative-controlled on today's binary (S1 0/5, S2 1/5 with one regression guard, S3 0/4). One check of mine passed vacuously at first (doctor erroring = no 'unwatched' line); it now requires doctor's receipt.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_140 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 140u32, "2026-10-24T07:11Z", "eoie", "03:1x design for train-as-verbs, mapped from the scratch scripts that actually carried tonight's train. Each verb replaces one script, and each script earned its place by catching a real failure tonight.\n- eoie train plan <root>: reads stage records (name, raw-from, slices, notebooks, acceptance, order) from one state file. Replaces launch-<X>.ps1 slice lists plus chain-next's $order. Model: f6 eoie_release_stages (typed stages, chain validation; its parse errors are fixed, recheck pending).\n- eoie train emulate [--from S] [--to S] [--watch file,...]: live tree + the last landed stage's raw, then each stage's slices in order. FAIL on refusals and on merged definition lines; the lib link is added after the slices. Replaces chain-emulate.ps1 (it caught 2 broken anchors, a merged line, and with -Watch found the slices behind 7 failures).\n- eoie train check [--stages ...]: regen + cargo check over every crate the stages change plus reverse dependents, naming each failing crate's first error and every crate over 950 lines. Replaces train-cargo-check.ps1 (it caught 6 crates that would have failed mid-train, including one my own split broke in a dependent).\n- eoie train typecheck <spec>: draft programs (.do or .ps1) applied on the emulated tree, probes, package headers, notebook verdicts (pass / link-only / type-error / rust-error). Replaces drafts-typecheck.ps1.\n- eoie train launch <stage>: fmt-rebase landing plus the release job with its acceptance chained after-ok; refuses while a live-gui window is held or waiting. Replaces launch-<X>.ps1 + start-<X>.ps1 + chain-next.ps1.\n- eoie train status: stage, job states, last acceptance verdict, which items install with which stage (tonight's map, computed from slice receipts). Replaces train-watch.ps1 and the hand-made map in note 137.\nContract: every verb is one call; stage records are typed rows, not script text; acceptance scripts stay per stage, negative-controlled on the installed binary before a train starts. Order: emulate and check first (they guard everything else), then typecheck, plan, launch, status.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_141 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 141u32, "2026-10-24T09:56Z", "eoie", "05:5x eoie: GE3's release was starving. Its regen finished 25 of 122 crates in 2 h 15 m (single crates took 9-17 min against 10-30 s in my whole-train check), on a box at 100% CPU with 1.4 GB free. Invoke-Heavy runs heavy jobs at BelowNormal (heavy-gate-lessons), while every compile-class job from the four lanes runs at Normal, so a saturated machine gives the heavy slot almost nothing. At that pace GE3 would hit its 361-min limit (09:40) around crate 60 and the whole train would stall behind it. Rule, written before acting: a heavy job of mine that projects past its own deadline goes up to Normal (a fair share), never above. Applied at 05:56 to GE3's tree only (supervisor child 131960: release pwsh, regen pwsh, current dotnet). Later dotnet children inherit Normal from the regen pwsh. Re-measure the crate rate at the next check-in. Follow-up for the gate owner: BelowNormal holds up while the box is idle and fails under 4-lane saturation; heavy jobs need a deadline-aware boost or compile admission capped while a heavy slot is held.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_142 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 142u32, "2026-10-24T13:45Z", "eoie", "eoie: GE3 finished at 09:27 with exit 1 and did not publish. Spiral tests failed twice, 6/287, all in eoie_do_program/program.spi: rustc E0433, 'cannot find crate eoie_do_verbs'. Cause: the do-verbs wire slice (10-22, landed 10-23 15:00, after F8's green tests) put a host call to another crate, eoie_do_verbs::eoie_do_verb_family, into program.spi's step_at, which every parser test reaches. A notebook test build links no sibling crates. ranking.spi's agile_task_query call survives only because no test reaches it. Fix (scratch ge3-fix/do-verb-boundary.do): the parser takes the verb recognizer as a parameter (program_of known text); compiled.spi, the cargo entry that does link eoie_do_verbs, passes the crate call; tests pass a search-only recognizer, plus one new test that a known verb becomes a query step. Scratch notebook test passes. Rerun as GE3b: regen of eoie_do_program only, the same gates, and a 'lib-free' stdout line after the spiral tests for main's lib guard; then chain-next -Done GE3 -Next HIJK. Gap in my gates: the whole-train check did a regen plus cargo check but no notebook tests of changed packages; it will run spiral tests for every package a slice touches.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_143 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 143u32, "2026-10-24T14:02Z", "eoie", "eoie: GE3b started at 10:02 as job-1792850533961-eoie-release-GE3b, with the chain to HIJK queued after-ok (job-1792850534804). Scratch proof before launch: regen plus cargo check passed, the eoie_do_program notebook passes, and do_program.rs is 999 lines (54,700 to 55,179 bytes). That is one line under the gate, so the next change to eoie_do_program has to split it first: the parser and the encoder go in separate crates at the compiled-records boundary. A snapshot was taken (before-release-GE3b.zip) and the fix applied live (3 files, 22 replacements). The release scripts for GE3b and HIJK through R now print 'lib-free: ...' after their spiral tests, and main's land guard releases on that line.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_144 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 144u32, "2026-10-24T20:51Z", "eoie", "16:51 GE3b passed and installed at 11:46, and after-install acceptance passed 12/12. The chain then stopped at 11:48 because launch-HIJK's prelaunch refused to run while both heavy slots were held by main's gates. chain-next now retries every 2 minutes while the slots are busy, until its deadline. HIJK is held on purpose until main lands the edition-3 respelling of lib/spiral (user-directed). Before relaunching: one eoie regen plus notebook check against the edition-3 lib. The lib checks in the launch scripts for HIJK, L, M, N and S1 now match on names only, so they don't depend on keyword spelling. My 4 lib drafts (env.command_line_arguments_from, env.process_id, console.read_to_end, sm'.char_code) get respelled in edition 3 after main lands.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_145 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 145u32, "2026-10-24T20:56Z", "eoie", "16:56 Main replied: the installed compiler already reads edition-3 lib (editions are set per package.spiproj). The land respells 106 lib files and holds 4 (process, file_system, sm', listm'). It lands after main's queued lib slices, possibly after 18:00. Main offered an edition-2 relaunch now. Rule, written before checking the queue: relaunch HIJK on edition-2 lib now only if a heavy slot is free and HIJK could reach lib-free before 18:00; otherwise hold for the land. Checked at 16:56: both heavy slots are held by main serial runners, with 8 main/x jobs queued ahead (edition3-proof among them), so HIJK is held. That costs no idle CPU because the machine is already full. After main's land message: name-only prelaunch checks, regen and notebook check on the edition-3 lib, re-anchor the 4 lib drafts (sm'.char_code targets a held file), then relaunch HIJK.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_146 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 146u32, "2026-10-24T23:45Z", "eoie", "19:45 groom: EOIE-JOB-ENV and EOIE-GE2-CRATE-SPLITS closed after GE3b's install. EOIE-QUEUED-JOBS-IN-HOST (waits on release P) and EOIE-HEAVY-ONE-LIMIT (waits on HIJK) now list this item as a dependency, so the block is a field and not only a note.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_147 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 147u32, "2026-10-25T00:08Z", "eoie", "20:08 HIJK picked up the pending-heal patch: replace_file_checked removes its .pending copy when the rename fails (new case RenameFailedTemporaryKept when even that fails), and view-add registers views in state/package.spiproj. 49 crates are affected, all already in the agile/proxy family HIJK regenerates. HIJK's notebook list now includes agile_task_views\\views_cli.spi. The orphan agile.spi.76908.pending, left by a failed 19:44 rename, was deleted at 19:57 after confirming the retry had landed the same edit.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_148 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 148u32, "2026-10-25T00:13Z", "eoie", "20:13 User direction (20:1x): 'update our compiled eoie version so we start on a clean slate; you're getting too clogged, bad release management'. Change: the remaining eight serial stages (HIJK, L, M, O, N, Q, P, R) become one release, CLEAN, built from all their slices in train order. It gets one rebase, one regen of every affected crate, one build, one spiral test run, the union of the stages' CLI notebooks, one install, and the union of their after-install checks. The edition-3 hold is dropped, because main offered an edition-2 relaunch; main's land waits for CLEAN's lib-free line. Rules, written before measuring: (1) a slice that no longer applies, or whose regen or cargo check fails, comes out of CLEAN and gets a note on its own item, as long as no later slice needs it. CLEAN never waits on a fix longer than one short repair pass. (2) The preflight is chain emulation plus the whole-train regen and cargo check; CLEAN launches only after both pass. (3) After CLEAN installs, nothing new parks in scratch: verified work lands in the repo tree and ships in the next release.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_149 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 149u32, "2026-10-25T00:39Z", "eoie", "20:39 CLEAN stopped: the preflight failed, and its starter refused to launch as designed. Two blockers. (1) eoie_machine_watch calls eoie_notebook_batch_line(cmd, age) with two arguments, but the export is curried (string -> u64 -> string compiles to fn(&str) -> Rc<dyn Fn(u64)>); the fix is the tupled form, (fun (command, age_minutes) => ...) : string * u64 -> string. This error has failed every whole-train check since 07:38. (2) The real clog: 17 generated crates come out over the 1,000-line topology limit, which publishing enforces. Live tops out at 1000 (eoie_agile_mutation). Each stage pushes at least one crate over, even HIJK alone (eoie_agile_mutation 1646, eoie_job_launch 1512). The worst are eoie_ci_parity 1956 (new, M), eoie_job_host 1852 (L/P/R), eoie_log_sequences 1743 (new, HIJK/O) and eoie_jobs_doctor 1435 (new, M). So none of the eight stages could have published, and the train kept queueing them because the per-stage 'over 950' lines were report-only. The installed eoie.exe (GE3b, 11:46) matches the live source, so work does not wait on a release. Next: the 33 parked slices become backlog work gated on crate size (the module-level output in SPIRAL-SHARED-SPECIALIZATIONS, or crate splits), and no slice is queued again before its crates fit.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_150 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 150u32, "2026-10-25T00:41Z", "eoie", "20:41 x relayed the user's ruling: no automatic splitting or deduplication in the compiler. Model by hand and export, as eoie does, and sharpen that method: whole verbs into sibling crates, calls across crates through exports, shared types in Spiral-only packages, let/inl chosen by measured size. So the 17 over-limit crates in note 149 are fixed by hand splits, not by waiting on compiler work.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_151 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 151u32, "2026-10-25T06:11Z", "eoie", "02:11 I dry-applied the parked next-train stages S1-S5 (scratch next-train\\apply-stage-S*.ps1) on a copy of the current tree. All five fail on anchors from before tonight's crate splits: S1 owner-parent.do, S2 window-announce.do, S3 needs lib console.read_to_end landed first, S4 heal-stdout-line.do, S5 job-chain-serial.do. So they do not ride in SLATE, which ships what is in the tree now: the 33 landed slices, the 16 splits, the registry fix and the views/pending-file fixes. After SLATE installs, each S slice is rebased onto the post-split layout as its own small change landed in the repo (no new parked train), starting with the P0s (EOIE-JOB-CHAIN-SERIAL, EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT) and with the lib drafts re-anchored on edition-3 text first. The release script is ready: scratch release-build-job-SLATE.ps1 and clean\\slate\\launch-SLATE.ps1 (full regen of every Spiral crate in two batches on the installed compiler, the 54 candidate notebooks with moved paths mapped, 111 registered spiral tests, the 17 new crates added to the census merge). It launches after 5k is installed and the new modules' notebooks are green.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_152 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 152u32, "2026-10-25T07:00Z", "eoie", "03:00 Parked S stages rebased onto the post-split tree, all dry-run clean on live src (scratch clean\\s-rebase): doctor-unwatched (model now in eoie_jobs_doctor_model; 5 over-120 lines wrapped), heal-stdout-line (do_git/do_write host moved to *_host packages; 20 replacements), window-announce (admission.spi was re-laid by the formatter, so its anchors were rewritten; 6 over-120 lines wrapped; 23 replacements). adoption-days-back, standards-duplicate-entry, table-empty-cells, heal-number-text(+tail), heal-stderr-line and note-edit-expect-rebased apply unchanged; the earlier failures came from a stale scratch copy. Still parked: owner-parent (S1), which needs a design against the eoie_job_queue split; its last notebook run had probe_paths_typecheck failing. These land after SLATE as one serial job.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_153 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 153u32, "2026-10-25T07:53Z", "eoie", "03:53 Changed plan for the parked S stages (pack-queued-builds rule, written before measuring): a stage ships inside SLATE only if, before 5k is installed, its affected crates measure at or under 950 on 5k, cargo check is green and its notebooks pass; otherwise it lands after SLATE. All 10 programs applied to live src after snapshot 20261025-034824-before-s-stages.zip (68 files, 96 replacements); the preflight covers 90 affected crates in two regen batches, with the 7 unpublished split crates in both, plus 10 notebooks. Snapshot fix on the way: scratch eoie-snapshot.ps1 walked src/target with Get-ChildItem -Include (46 min at 10-24 21:06); .NET enumeration lists the same 1482 files in 18 s, and the whole snapshot now takes 3.5 min. launch-SLATE uses the same script, so SLATE's snapshot step is fast too. Queued for the next regen: the job start flag-order fix (EOIE-JOB-START-FLAG-ORDER) and the host-free false positive for macro text inside string literals (eoie_standards rules.spi).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_154 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 154u32, "2026-10-25T10:29Z", "eoie", "06:29 S-stage SLATE decision, applied mechanically per note 153. The regen of all 90 affected crates plus the new ones on 5k was cargo check green in both batches, and all 10 notebooks passed. Size rule: each stage's affected crates must be at or under 950. Pass: table-empty-cells, adoption-days-back. note-edit-expect fails only via eoie_cli (1034), which is a SLATE blocker of its own (below); it gets re-measured after that fix. Deferred until after SLATE and reverted from the tree: doctor-unwatched (eoie_jobs_doctor 1097), heal-stdout-line, heal-number-text, heal-number-text-tail and heal-stderr-line (they touch 81 crates, and sm'.format adds format_real plus a helper, +14 lines each, which pushes crates already at 950-989 over, e.g. eoie_standards 1056 and agile_todo_lines 998), window-announce (eoie_machine_windows 975), standards-duplicate (eoie_standards 1056). The revert uses generated inverse programs (scratch clean\\s-rebase\\inverse\\*.undo, dry-run clean) plus a snapshot restore for the two regex-edit stages, verified by hash. Pre-existing SLATE blockers this preflight found, independent of the S stages: (1) eoie_cli 1034: per-verb help made direct_verb_usage a 136-line fold inlined into eoie_cli; fix: command_spec_domain exports eoie_direct_verb_usage (scratch clean\\cli-usage\\verb-usage-export.do). (2) agile_task_listing at 989 published with no margin; fix: the eoie_agile_list_args crate takes argument parsing and status validation (scratch clean\\list-split\\apply-list-split.ps1; the status filter becomes OnlyStatus : string, dropping the reflection fold). Each is kept only if all its crates end at or under 950 with cargo check green.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_155 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 155u32, "2026-10-25T10:36Z", "eoie", "06:36 Gate added before SLATE, written before measuring (release-preflight rule): SLATE launches only after a full no-publish regen of every Spiral crate on 5k (scratch clean\\slate\\full-measure.ps1, 2 batches) shows every crate at or under 1000 and cargo check green in both batches. Why: on 5k, crates regenerate 11-25 lines above their published size (5j/5k codegen versus the pre-5j publish), and three published crates no earlier measurement covered sit near the line: eoie_do_program 999, patch_compat_driver 982, eoie_repo_accept_review 973. A crate over 1000 found mid-release would fail SLATE late, so the full measure runs first; any crate over 1000 gets a hand split before launch. Also queued: eoie_agile_list_args added to make-SLATE's census merge; job-script-check ok.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_156 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 156u32, "2026-10-25T11:03Z", "eoie", "07:03 5k will never be installed (main 07:0x): its base check refused it after the tree core moved to 17D970FE (x's x-compat change). The closure fix ships in pack 5l' (composite 0C48169521E5384F: 17D970FE + 5k closure guard + EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL stage 3 + tibia LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS + C !!!!PrimToString; review job-1792926015134). Gate amended (rule from note 155, unchanged except the compiler): the full no-publish measure runs on 5l', either the installed compiler or its candidate DLL if main sends the path, and SLATE launches after it passes. The 5k measurements stay as an approximation; drafts get re-proved on 5l' (recompile-drafts rule).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_157 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 157u32, "2026-10-25T13:38Z", "eoie", "09:38 Full measure on the 5l' candidate (core 0C48169521E5384F, copied DLL): all 234 Spiral crates regenerate, every one at or under 1000 (largest eoie_do_program 999, then patch_compat_driver 982, agile_todo_lines 983, eoie_do_edit 981, eoie_memory_query 981). The per-batch cargo checks both failed, for structural reasons and not code: (1) my split-check took a crate's first name= line, which is a [lib] name in eoie_dev and eoie_predicate_lift (fixed: the name now comes from the [package] section); (2) each batch's staged workspace holds only its own regenerated Rust, so crates depending on new split crates regenerated in the other batch see no .rs (eoie_job_start_args from batch 1's side). The same flaw was in SLATE's own two-batch -CargoCheck -Publish, which would fail or check against stale published Rust. Decided: SLATE regenerates all 234 in one batch (one workspace; the regen timeout is not a whole-run limit, since 117 crates ran for 60 min under 1800 s); make-SLATE and launch-SLATE are updated, and job-script-check is ok. Running now: cargo check of all 234 in one merged workspace (batch 1 outputs copied into batch 2's), the last piece of the gate.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_158 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 158u32, "2026-10-25T13:42Z", "eoie", "09:42 SLATE gate PASSED on the 5l' candidate: all 234 Spiral crates regenerate at or under 1000 (largest 999) and cargo check of all 234 in one merged workspace exits 0. SLATE is ready: the single-batch job script is regenerated and job-script-check is ok; launch-SLATE refuses while a release, an exclusive window or a tree lease is live. It launches once main installs 5l' (the installed compiler must be the measured one). After install: after-install checks (CLEAN's HIJK..R plus the four job start flag orders, the job chain --serial live run, and the supervisor console count), then the edition-3 respell release, then KIT-RENAME.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_159 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 159u32, "2026-10-25T14:01Z", "eoie", "10:01 SLATE post-install checks for the new behavior are written and negative-controlled: scratch clean\\slate\\after-install-SLATE-extra.ps1 (11 checks): job start in four flag orders (heavy/after-ok both ways, heavy/quiet both ways), a repeated lead flag refused by name, job chain --serial returning one job id, note-edit refusing a wrong --expect-at with nothing written and editing with the right one, agile next --load and --fits. On today's installed binary: 7 FAIL, each through its own bug (timeout-ms misread when --heavy leads, quiet-needs-heavy before --heavy is seen, chain --serial unknown, note-edit 8 operands refused, next --load/--fits unknown), and 4 PASS for behavior that already holds. Every queued heavy test job is stopped by the script. Runs right after SLATE installs, beside CLEAN's after-install; SLATE counts as done at 11/11.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_160 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 160u32, "2026-10-25T14:33Z", "eoie", "10:33 Base changed again: 5l' will not be installed (its review found a Lua build failure from tibia's LUA-FUNCTION-LIMITS). 5l'' = tree 17D970FE + 5k closure guard + EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL stage 3 + C-PRIM-TO-STRING (composite 34519B923366CCEC, review job-1792938510698-main-pack5l2-review). Main expects the 5l' gate result to carry over (only Lua codegen differs), but the rule is to measure what ships, so one unattended chain is armed (scratch clean\\slate\\slate-5l2-chain.ps1): wait for the 5l'' candidate (dll.txt plus a core-hash check in the review log), copy it, run the 234-crate measure and the single-workspace cargo check, gate (none over 1000, check green, all 234 measured), then watch the installed SpiralCompilerCore MVID (main's install rebuilds, so file hashes differ; the MVID survives) and launch SLATE on a match. It stops on any other core hash.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_161 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 161u32, "2026-10-25T18:14Z", "eoie", "14:14 kit: the SLATE gate passed on the 5l'' candidate (core 34519B923366CCEC, from main's review run single-flight-20261025-123908):\n- 234 crates measured, 0 over 1000, max eoie_do_program 999. Ten are over the 950 margin (HAND-CRATE-UNITS note 12; split designs in notes 13-14).\n- The merged single-workspace cargo check exits 0.\n- Chain b4318959l now waits for the installed SpiralCompilerCore MVID 7fd00bff-ba14-fc03-1b62-5a896ccd06ed (main's install job-1792950541607, waiting for a compiler-install window), then launches SLATE.\n- After the install: after-install-SLATE-extra.ps1 (11/11 required) plus CLEAN's after-install.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_162 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 162u32, "2026-10-25T18:30Z", "eoie", "14:30 kit: SLATE launched.\n- Timeline: 5l'' installed (main's job-1792950541607 at 14:14; MVID 7fd00bff-... confirmed by main, SpiralCompilerCore CDD68DC3EE829A67 = the reviewed candidate), install window released at 14:19, launch at 14:21.\n- Pre-release snapshot: 20261025-142222-before-release-SLATE.zip, 1,485 files.\n- Job: job-1792952822294-eoie-release-SLATE (heavy, 8 h budget, a single 234-crate regen filter). It was queued at 14:27 with free memory at 1.3 GB, so admission may hold it.\n- Watcher: scratch slate\\watch-SLATE.ps1 (its settled branch was exercised on a finished job first).\n- The first chain (b4318959l) died on a PowerShell (try {...}) expression in its post-match branch; that's recorded in the gotchas memory, and launch-SLATE now uses an explicit Set-Content -Path.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_163 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 163u32, "2026-10-25T20:42Z", "eoie", "16:42 kit: after SLATE, in order. One list; each step names where its detail lives.\n1. post-install-SLATE.ps1 (scratch clean\\slate): installed eoie.exe equals the release build, SLATE-extra 11/11, CLEAN all pass. Any failure stops here.\n2. Re-measure the baselines on the installed binary: supervisor consoles (SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE note 4: new supervisors own 0); adoption --days-back works (AGENT-GUIDE note 24); eoie_crate_gate's own size from the published .rs (CRATE-GATE-HARDEN).\n3. Copy infra/k3s-iggy finals over the drafts and check the hashes (IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE notes 9-10); unstaged for the user.\n4. Tell kit2 the tree is free (CI fixture fix plus worker-node reproduce, EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW note 11).\n5. Respell release (EDITION3 notes 26-27):\n   step 0, land the standards ':=' fix (STYLE-RATCHET note 34);\n   respell dry run, then -Apply, then regen;\n   gate: every .rs byte-identical to SLATE's.\n6. union_cases_find experiment, arms B and C, in one regen job (UNION-REFLECTION notes 38-39).\n7. KIT-RENAME release (notes 6-11): quiescent window announced to all lanes; kit-rename.ps1; hooks args; machine-watch's 4 edits; tibia's 3 scripts via table; memory paths; after the job, kit-state-move.ps1 -Apply; the folder move last.\n8. Post-rename: splits of eoie_do_program and eoie_experiment_analysis (HAND-CRATE-UNITS notes 13-14), the list-sugar heal (DO-SLOP-GATE note 6, byte-identical gate), the slop gate (note 7), the lint CLI (GRANULAR-LINT note 6, rename the draft first), the batched planning export (AGILE-CALL-LATENCY note 5).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_164 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 164u32, "2026-10-25T20:50Z", "eoie", "16:50 kit: the three deferred S stages still apply to the live tree after today's changes. do-dry dry runs on copies of their targets: doctor-unwatched ok (2 files, 5 replacements); heal-stdout-line ok (20 files, 20 replacements); window-announce ok (6 files, 23 replacements, Cargo.toml member included). They ride the first release after SLATE whose crate budget fits them, re-measured under the 950 rule as before (each was deferred for line cost, not for broken anchors).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_165 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 165u32, "2026-10-25T22:16Z", "eoie", "18:16 kit: SLATE close-out map. Each item closes (100, Done) the moment its post-install check passes on the installed binary, with the check line quoted in the closing note. No other judgement is needed.\n- after-install-SLATE-extra.ps1:\n  - 'job start heavy before after-ok', 'after-ok before heavy', 'heavy before quiet', 'quiet before heavy' and 'a repeated lead flag is refused by name' close EOIE-JOB-START-FLAG-ORDER (70%);\n  - 'job chain --serial starts one job' closes EOIE-JOB-CHAIN-SERIAL (85%);\n  - 'note-edit refuses a wrong --expect-at and writes nothing' and 'note-edit with the right --expect-at edits' close EOIE-NOTE-EDIT-EXPECT (80%);\n  - 'agile next accepts --load' and 'agile next accepts --fits and names the loads' close EOIE-NEXT-FITS-NOW (85%).\n- after-install-CLEAN.ps1 stages, whose Verdict lines name their items:\n  - R closes EOIE-SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE (80%; also needs the live count of 0 consoles on supervisors started after the install, note 4) and EOIE-JOB-START-SETTLE (50%; fail/ok/skip verdicts);\n  - L closes EOIE-ACCEPT-REVIEW;\n  - N closes the formatted-state read (EOIE-AGILE-FORMATTED-WRITER reader half);\n  - Q closes the failed-edit-skips-writes item;\n  - P re-runs HP's live-parent checks (6/6).\n- Items that stay open after SLATE: EOIE-QUEUED-JOBS-NO-PROCESS (13 queued supervisors remain until its own change), CRATE-GATE-HARDEN (split first), GRANULAR-LINT (CLI wiring after the rename).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_166 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 166u32, "2026-10-27T23:36Z", "eoie", "19:4x eoie: the queue for after TRAIN (TRAIN = job-1793137570729, in its candidate notebooks since 18:00). Every entry is a scratchpad draft that applied on copies; the regens were proven on the node.\nLib window first (after 'TRAIN window closed'; through lib-guarded-do.ps1, then a lib gate):\n- lib-gaps-3 (4 programs)\n- lib-dotnet\\join-rust-arm.do: join', map' and parallel_map Rust arms; a rustc probe printed 'a!, b!, c!'\n- lib-clip\\lib-clip.do: sm'.clip, first_line, after_first_line, with fsharp+rust test blocks; rustc probe OK\nNext kit release (regen against that lib):\n- agile-trim\\seal\\apply-seal.ps1 (agile seal; byte-identical to the hand trim)\n- wip-merge\\apply-wip.ps1 (agile wip; its warm/cold rule is still open)\n- heal-boundary: argument-count.do, argument-after-flag.do, argument-at.do\n- uses-lib\\window-watch-to-lib.do\n- lib-clip\\kit-clip.do and kit-lines.do: 17 host copies retired, all consumers byte-identical, plus the note-edit replaced= receipt (agile_note_edit 855)\n- job-settle\\settle-receipt.do (kit_job_launch 714)\n- jobs-doctor\\stage (new crate kit_jobs_doctor_servers 502) plus orphan-servers.do (doctor 917)\nNot queued: agile-weight\\p0-weight.do. Its 10-24 acceptance rule rejects it (EOIE-AGILE-P0-WEIGHT note 2).\nAfter TRAIN publishes: post-install-TRAIN.ps1 (queued-no-process, heavy-held, dry-run, agile-guard, owner-parent, show-archive), granular-lint\\activate.ps1, then close CRATE-GATE-HARDEN and EOIE-AGENT-GUIDE. Update 20:0x: lib window also takes lib-clip\\lib-text.do (sm'.decimal_text, sm'.char_text); the kit release also takes lib-clip\\kit-text.do (19 host copies retired, 45 crates byte-identical on the node). TRAIN itself went red (note 167), so 'after TRAIN' now means after TRAIN2. Update 20:3x: lib window also takes lib-dotnet\\average-rust-arm.do (rustc probe OK). Update 20:3x: and lib-dotnet\\transpose-rust-arm.do (rustc probe OK). Update 03:5x, lib window plan. 8 programs apply together on the live lib (checked on a copy at 03:57): the lib-gaps-3 trio (char-code-and-stdin, env-arguments-and-pid, try-append; lib-batch.do is just their union), join-rust-arm, average-rust-arm, transpose-rust-arm, lib-clip and lib-text. They touch sm', am', env, console and file_system. Landing goes through lib-guarded-do.ps1 on 'P2 installed', which takes seconds. Gates run on the node, on a mirror synced after the land with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL pinned to the box's P2 DLL, so the box stays quiet through tibia's 08:25-09:30 block. A red gate undoes its program.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_167 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 167u32, "2026-10-28T00:00Z", "eoie", "20:0x kit: TRAIN (job-1793137570729) ended at 19:50 without publishing. Everything up to the notebooks passed: regen skipped (fresh), topology max 999, debug build, the fixed host probe (host 122208, dies with its home), byte identity 8/8, release-wait. Candidate notebooks: 60/66, and all 6 reds are among the 12 notebooks this train added. (1) 5 can never run as standalone notebooks because their modules have no '///- --package' prelude: evidence, workspace_primitives/files and kit_job_slot type-error on their own package modules; ceremonies and crate_largest pass their test, then rustc reports 'main function not found'. Not regressions; filed as KIT-UNRUN-TEST-BLOCKS. make-TRAIN.ps1 now leaves them out (61 rows). (2) census_cli: a real red, and mine. The 10-27 census-probes.do patterns used lookaround (GadtCase '(?!.*=>)', RustGlobal '(?<![\\w.])'). I checked them with .NET regex, but the census matches with Rust's regex crate, which rejects lookaround, so Regex::new failed and every count was 0 (gadt-case=0, rust_global missing). Fixed in the live tree by census-probes-rust-regex.do: GadtCase '^\\s*\\|\\s*[A-Z]\\w*\\s*::[^=]*$' and RustGlobal '(^|[^\\w.])(rust_global\\b|global\\s*(\\(|\\x22))'. A cargo probe with regex 1.13.1 confirms it: the old patterns don't compile; the new ones count gadt 2 on the fixture, 0 on list-cons arms, and 3 globals with foo.global( and my_global( excluded. TRAIN2: the lib is moving tonight (main's cli_args, tibia's 13 slices, fiscal's 8), and module-freshness can't see lib changes, so TRAIN2 regens in full (plus census.rs for the probe fix), once, on main's pack-5n compiler after it installs, with a window announced first. Lesson recorded: test regexes in the engine that ships them.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_168 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 168u32, "2026-10-28T00:04Z", "eoie", "20:0x kit: TRAIN2 start rule, written before any of its inputs arrive. TRAIN2 queues once (a) main reports pack-5n installed and verified, or 2026-10-28 06:00 passes, whichever comes first (after 06:00 it regens on the installed compiler), and (b) no lib land job (land, lib-guarded) has been running or queued for 15 min. Before queueing: run each candidate notebook once on the live tree (61 rows), dry-run the release script's candidate checks, announce the window to main, fiscal, x and tibia, and force a full regen (module-freshness can't see the lib).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_169 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 169u32, "2026-10-28T00:30Z", "eoie", "20:3x kit: TRAIN2 notebook preflight is done ahead of time. make-TRAIN.ps1 lists 67 candidate rows. The 6 modules that went red now have the notebook prelude and '///> _' above main (live tree, KIT-UNRUN-TEST-BLOCKS) and pass alone; wheres and files are newly added and pass. census_cli passes only after the regen, because its CLI binary carries census.rs. The other 60 passed in TRAIN. Live-tree changes since the 17:20 regen that TRAIN2's full regen picks up: probes.spi (Rust-regex fix) and the 6 test-prelude edits. Test blocks and directives don't emit Rust, so only kit_style_census should differ.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_170 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 170u32, "2026-10-28T01:44Z", "eoie", "21:4x kit: amendment to the TRAIN2 start rule (note 168), at main's request. 5n was installed at 21:43, but the installed SpiralCompilerCore (7A6C1445) differs from the reviewed one (295C72E1), so main is reviewing it in full (ETA 23:30-23:45). TRAIN2 starts only after main sends 'cleared' (regen on 5n) or 'rolled back to 5m'' (regen on that), and then after 15 min with no lib land. The 06:00 fallback no longer picks a compiler on its own: with no message by 06:00, ask main first. Also riding TRAIN2: the EOIE-AGILE-P0-WEIGHT draft (live tree; ranking.spi added to the candidate list, 68 rows). Preflight step added (x via main, 21:5x): right before queueing, check that no Cells compiler daemon is listening on 139xx (Get-NetTCPConnection -State Listen, local ports 13900-13999). If one exists from an earlier compiler build, wait for it to exit (or, if it's mine, quit it) so TRAIN2's notebooks start a fresh daemon on the cleared compiler. No Cells runs from me before 'cleared'.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_171 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 171u32, "2026-10-28T03:10Z", "eoie", "23:07 kit: TRAIN2 queued (job-1793156965914-kit-release-TRAIN, front ticket, snapshot 20261027-230728-before-release-TRAIN.zip), on 5n (cleared 22:49). Start rule met: 5n cleared; lib quiet 15 min (last write file_system.spi 22:51:20, x's final test-only land, hash DCE66AEE unchanged at queue time); main, tibia, fiscal and x all confirmed their holds; nothing listening on 139xx. Full regen of all 242 spiral crates (train-regen-crates.txt), then 68 candidate notebooks and tests.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_172 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 172u32, "2026-10-28T05:01Z", "eoie", "01:0x kit: TRAIN2 (job-1793156965914) went red at the very last step, the tests (00:57). Everything before passed: regen exit 0 for 242 crates on 5n (23:09-23:57), line gate 0 over, topology max 999 (kit_do_program), host probe, byte identity 8/8, release-wait, candidate notebooks 68/68 (incl. tonight's 6 prelude modules and ranking.spi), one-call spec 36/49 (report-only), read/ps e2e 5/5, window/timeout/orphan checks green. The style ratchet (report-only) shows 108 regressions: packages missing from the 38-package baseline that the fixed probes now count; the baseline needs a refresh (EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET). The red: kit_agile_lease tests/package_inputs.rs bounded_inputs_reject_oversized_sources still set an 8 MiB + 1 file, but this train raised the per-file limit to 64 MiB (agile-guard-64.do). My miss; fixed to 64 MiB + 1 (guard-test-64.do), 6/6 pass. cargo test stops at the first failing binary, so a --no-fail-fast workspace run is going now before the re-run. TRAIN2b = the same release without a regen: train-regen-crates.txt emptied (the 242-crate list is kept as .done-2357.txt), train-regen-done.txt = regen start 23:09; 0 module inputs newer; lib hash set snapshotted (lib-hashes-train2.tsv, 116 files, digest 1FA7C7155C4D72D9) and rechecked before queueing.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_173 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 173u32, "2026-10-28T07:56Z", "eoie", "03:5x kit: TRAIN2b (job-1793163848922) passed cargo tests and 68/68 candidate notebooks, then went red in build.ps1 -Test's notebook sweep. That sweep covers 111 files and 365 tests; 4 failed, all in agile_todo_model/model.spi, and the first run and the retry were identical. Cause: this train split the marker fields into the agile_todo_fields crate, which left model.spi's finding_json calling agile_todo_fields::kit_agile_todo_fields through a host macro. A standalone notebook's rustc can't link that crate (E0433), so the whole file failed. Behind that, todo_blocks_keep_their_spiral_lines_and_ids still expected JSON without the new fields:{} entry. Fix (todo-fields-injected.do, todo-fields-test.do): findings, findings_from and finding_json take fields_of : string -> string -> string. agile_todo_lines passes linked_marker_fields (the host call), the tests pass marker_fields_json (the in-package marker_fields Spiral), and the expectation is updated. The model.spi notebook passes 11/11. Regen check: agile_todo_lines goes 907 -> 923; agile_todo_scan, fields, paths, roots and sources are byte-identical. TRAIN2c queued at 03:55 (job-1793174128919), regenerating agile_todo_lines only; the lib digest is unchanged (1FA7C7155C4D72D9). Plan after it closes: main installs P2 (about 15 min), then the lib window opens about 06:30, pauses its gates 08:25-09:30 for tibia's live block, and resumes at 09:30. My 5 drafts go first, then main's 3 slices if they fit.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_174 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 174u32, "2026-10-28T09:46Z", "eoie", "05:4x kit: lib window. All 8 programs landed live through lib-guarded-do (05:36-05:44): char-code-and-stdin, env-arguments-and-pid, try-append, join-rust-arm, average-rust-arm, transpose-rust-arm, lib-clip, lib-text (log: scratchpad clean\\lib-window-land.log). Two refusals were resolved first: main's morning-runner (Cells) started at 05:37 and was stopped; tibia's orphaned Cells daemon on port 13985 was stopped by tibia. Gates run on the node with the box's P2 SpiralCompiler.dll pinned (A4E480202BD4, staged at C:\\home\\remote-stage\\spiral-bin-p2): job-1793180751198 (mirror kit-libwin-a) gates am', env, console and file_system; job-1793180849277 (mirror kit-libwin-b) gates sm'. A red gate undoes its program. Next kit release: kit-clip, kit-lines, kit-text, settle receipt, doctor servers crate, seal, wip, boundary slices, the P0-weight revert and KIT-LINT-DOLLAR-LITERAL, regenerated against this lib.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_175 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 175u32, "2026-10-28T10:49Z", "eoie", "06:4x kit: lib window closed. Node gates (P2 DLL pinned): am' 16/17, env 6/9, console 3/3, file_system 28/28, sm' 55/67. Two reds are mine and reproduce locally on F#: average_divides_the_sum_by_the_count ('Cannot parse the literal as: i32', the f64 literals in my test) and clip/first_line (a compile-time 'UTF-8 string slice ... does not preserve codepoint boundaries' on F#). By the window rule I undid both programs live at 06:49 (undo-average-rust-arm.do, undo-lib-clip.do; checked on a copy first, main's temp-copy land.ps1 exempted). The other node reds pass locally (env.spi 9/9; sm' builder_*, format and show 4/4): those are node toolchain gaps, not regressions. Kept live: char-code-and-stdin, env-arguments-and-pid, try-append, join-rust-arm, transpose-rust-arm, lib-text. Knock-on: kit-clip.do and kit-lines.do (which need sm'.clip/first_line) and the note-edit replaced= receipt wait for the fixed lib-clip; kit-text.do (decimal_text/char_text) can ride the next release.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_176 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 176u32, "2026-10-28T11:20Z", "eoie", "07:2x kit: release queue for today. TRAIN3 (09:45): kit-text, settle-receipt, the doctor servers crate, seal, argument-count/after-flag/at, window-watch-to-lib (all 8 apply together on a tree copy; the node regen-compare is job-1793185548220), plus what's already in the live tree: the P0-weight revert, the lint dollar-literal fix and the census baseline refresh. Land window (about 14:00): lib-clip and average-rust-arm fixed forward (local gates green). TRAIN4 (about 16:00): kit-clip, kit-lines (fresh regen-compare first, since clip's Rust body changed) and x's kit lint shadows (%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--home-git\\b7595ac3-963d-4714-be58-0267aa270947\\scratchpad\\kit-lint-shadows; wiring.do applies 4/5 on copies). Later candidate: main's BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP census puts 622 raw !!!!Export sites in kit/src onto lib's wrapper, a mechanical slice to prove by byte-identical regen.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_177 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 177u32, "2026-10-28T11:54Z", "eoie", "07:5x kit: TRAIN3 preflight. Module notebooks for every changed package pass 20/20 on the live tree (job-1793187198471). The node regen-compare passes (102 crates, 0 failures, 0 over 1000). Launch dry run: all preconditions hold, 244-crate full regen, 69 candidate notebooks. Queues at 09:45, after tibia's live block.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_178 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 178u32, "2026-10-28T12:23Z", "eoie", "08:2x kit: TRAIN4 content, built by scratchpad clean\\train4\\build-train4-copy.ps1 on top of the live tree: kit-clip and kit-lines (need the fixed lib-clip landed in the 14:00 window), waits-column (agile list --blocked shows waits <deps>), kit-part-at (needs lib split_nth, same window), rename-retry (40x50 ms rename retries in replace_file_checked), text-replace-cas (proxy text-replace refuses on a concurrent change), and x's kit lint shadows (core crate plus run crate, dispatched through kit_lint_macros). Node regen-compares running: job-1793189767176 (65 crates, without the shadows slice) and job-1793189966231 (the shadows slice, 7 crates). Lib window at 14:00, in order: lib-clip (fixed), average-rust-arm (fixed test), lib-split-nth. All three pass local gates on a lib copy. Not in TRAIN4: the export rewrite (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP; byte-identity compare job-1793188973244 still running), next release.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_179 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 179u32, "2026-10-28T13:31Z", "eoie", "09:3x kit: TRAIN4 regen compare v2 is green (job-1793189767176, P2 DLL A4E480202BD4, 65 crates reaching the TRAIN4 programs): 0 compile failures, 0 crates over 1000. Differences are all explained by the programs: +19 lines in 17 crates (agile_planning_migration, agile_planning_revision, agile_task_creation, agile_task_notes, agile_task_rename, agile_task_revision, agile_task_views, agile_title_notes, agile_todo_record, agile_todo_roots, kit_evidence, proxy_text_replacement and others) from renamed_within in workspace_primitives.replace_file_checked (rename-retry.do); proxy_text_replacement also gets the changed-since-read refusal (text-replace-cas.do); agile_task_census 471 -> 563 and agile_task_listing 978 -> 988 from waits-column.do; agile_note_edit 845 -> 874 and agile_note_seal 584 -> 604 from the retry plus kit-lines; kit_memory, kit_memory_import, kit_memory_query and agile_task_next differ at equal length from clip's borrowing Rust arm (lands in the lib window). Every other crate, including the kit_do_* family (kit-part-at.do), is byte-identical. Closest to the gate: kit_memory_query 996, agile_todo_scan 993, kit_do_edit 992, kit_experiment_analysis 992. The x shadows compare (job-1793189966231) was clean earlier: 8 crates, 0 failures, 0 over 1000. TRAIN4 content is ready for preflight once the lib window lands clip, split_nth and the rest.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_180 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 180u32, "2026-10-28T13:44Z", "eoie", "09:4x kit: land-window lib set gated green (job-1793194573270, compile slot, process compiler). On a fresh copy of the live lib, all 7 programs apply in landing order: lib-clip (fixed), average-rust-arm, lib-split-nth, lib-all-digits, lib-bytes-between, lib-read-text-or-empty, lib-set-env. The new test blocks all pass with 0 type errors and no failed targets: sm' all_digits_accepts_only_nonempty_ascii_digit_runs, sm' bytes_between_slices_utf8_bytes_or_gives_empty, env set_environment_variable, file_system read_text_or_empty_reads_a_file_or_gives_empty. clip, average and split_nth were gated green earlier on the libfix copy. Gate script: scratch clean/lib-clip/gate-window-set.ps1. These are kit's lib writes for the land window that opens when TRAIN3 publishes; the kit halves (kit-all-digits, kit-bytes-between, kit-read-text-or-empty, kit-ticket-adopted) follow in the release after. Landing is one call: scratch clean/lib-clip/land-window-set.ps1 -Land runs the 7 programs in order through lib-guarded-do and stops at the first refusal, printing the undos for what landed, newest first. Rehearsed at 09:51 on a fresh copy of the live lib: all 7 applied, then their generated undos (anchor swap, reverse order), and all 4 touched files (sm', am', env, file_system) hashed back to live.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_181 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 181u32, "2026-10-29T14:05Z", "kit", "10-29 10:0x kit: TRAIN3 retry, first run (job-1793275863025, the new repo-tracked scripts/release-train.ps1): regen 08:11-09:01 ok (10 owners changed, 245 unchanged, 0 errors); debug candidate kit.exe E883AFA0; positive control kit_lcov pass; notebooks 09:07-10:01, 66/73 pass, STOP, nothing installed (kit.exe still A5B55974). The 7 reds: 3 were runner bugs of mine, now fixed in release-train.ps1. (a) The candidate was built under target/candidate, which broke kit_checkout()'s fixed-depth layout (kit_cli/windows_cli handoff test). (b) Any .spi mentioning the binary was selected, including 10 crate entries with no test blocks: 3 failed to compile as notebooks (kit_coverage_smoke/smoke, kit_patch_mutation_contracts/main, kit_proxy_edit_contracts/main) and 7 passed with 0 tests; test blocks are now required. 4 were real, all fixed in the live tree (kit-drafts\\train3-reds): seal.spi had test blocks without a notebook header, so its tests never ran (KIT-UNRUN-TEST-BLOCKS). stop_cli's a_job_over_its_memory_cap test predates TRAIN3's 2 s start settle, which correctly reports the capped job at start, so it now passes --settle-ms 0. ps_cli kill --mine is a REAL regression since TRAIN2c's owner-parent: mine_verdict allowed any pid in my session before checking the job author, and every job is in-session now, so another author's job was killed; ownership is checked first now, with a regression test. These 2 reds (stop_cli memory cap, ps_cli kill --mine) are exactly yesterday's TRAIN3 reds, which closes the WIPE-REDO-LEDGER row for the lost 67/69 run record. Evidence kept: the env-guard e2e test passed; tibia's table_cli and table_test_cli passed. Next: regen and publish agile_note_seal, kit_process_table and kit_process_kill (job-1793282672180), then rerun with -SkipRegen, then install.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_182 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 182u32, "2026-10-29T15:39Z", "kit", "10-29 11:3x kit: TRAIN3 PUBLISHED 11:35, kit.exe CD2F0D1A (was A5B55974). Path, with scripts/release-train.ps1 (repo-tracked; it replaces the lost per-train launchers): run 1 (job-1793275863025) regen of all 255 owners plus 73 notebooks, 66/73; rerun (job-1793282979350, -SkipRegen) 64/65 after the three runner fixes and the four real fixes; final (job-1793286715057) seal-only 1/1, then the release build hit kit-dev's default 15 min cargo cap; final-2 (job-1793287768387, -TimeoutMs 3600000 now passed by the runner) built, checked schema and topology, published and passed the smoke. The candidate behind every notebook verdict is C9EE1592; the seal target-marker fix was codegen-neutral (0 owners changed). The lane copy %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe was swapped to CD2F0D1A once its running instance exited (the runner now stages kit.exe.next for that case). Closeout on the installed binary, 7/7 (C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\train3-closeout.ps1, with an A5B55974 control): closed KIT-LINT-DOLLAR-LITERAL, EOIE-JOB-START-SETTLE, EOIE-JOBS-DOCTOR. Next: the lib window (after fiscal's 8): re-merge merged-lib (preview vs main's landed env guard: env.spi merges cleanly, both kept), land sm'/env/file_system plus the delete-guard slice and gate them; then restore merged-m5 (73 files), apply the post-TRAIN3 drafts (universal roots, the 5 headers and the headerless rule, path-tag, LPT leaves, the kit_schedule crate and wiring, BANG as a phase), and run TRAIN4.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_183 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 183u32, "2026-10-29T15:58Z", "kit", "10-29 11:5x kit: TRAIN4 tree STAGED in kit/src (unstaged, WIP in place; 136 entries). (a) The m5-commit-bundle restore, re-merged at 11:57 against the current tree: 73 files, 0 conflicts (26 new in 7 crates: agile_todo_cache, agile_todo_merge, kit_do_commit, kit_do_store, kit_lint_shadows, kit_lint_shadows_core, kit_remote_status; 47 take-theirs). (b) Batch A, proven 7/7 by notebooks (job-1793288690204): 5 notebook headers, the path-tag re-layout, env-guard universal roots. (c) After the restore: lpt-leaves.do, standards-headerless-tests.do (rule 2), wire-schedule.do (re-anchored: the restore changed the lint help line, so the anchor moved to before ':= help_line_for') and the kit_schedule crate. (d) DELETE-ROOT-GUARD (5): kit_process session files never get remove_dir_all. Blocked on: the lib half (sm'.clip fixed, split_nth, all_digits, bytes_between, read_text_or_empty, set/remove_environment_variable), because kit-clip, kit-lines and part-at call it. The lib window comes after fiscal's 8, x's 2 and main's delete guard. Then: release-train full regen + candidate notebooks + install. BANG: its node proof is on the TRAIN3-era src, so it rides either as a pre-regen apply re-proven by a node compare of the TRAIN4 tree, or as TRAIN5, decided once TRAIN4's own regen is green.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_184 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 184u32, "2026-10-30T01:59Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T01:59 kit groom: progress 30 -> 45. Releases no longer run on session-scratch scripts: TRAIN3 and TRAIN4 (TRAIN4b-4e, installed C528BE4D 10-29 18:35) ran on the repo-tracked kit/scripts/release-train.ps1. Its phases are regen, the new early 'crate gate --enforce' (it stopped TRAIN4d in 40 min, not after notebooks), candidate, positive control, notebooks with per-worker build slots, release and smoke, plus -SkipRegen/-NotebooksOnly/-Only for preflights. Still open: making it a kit verb (not a script), the -Environment fix for the $env race (TRAIN5), and the deps (EOIE-HAND-CRATE-UNITS).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_185 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 185u32, "2026-10-30T10:25Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T10:25 kit groom: TRAIN5 (job-1793335928930, started 00:52 on pack 7) was LOST at about 01:26: state=lost exit=125, 'the supervisor stopped beating: it was killed with its caller'. The job was host-held by kit's claude session (host_home 42472-...), and that session ended, taking the train with it. It got through regen (8 owners, 01:18), the crate gate (255 crates, 0 over 1000), the candidate (kit.exe 01FDAB64) and 13 of 92 notebooks (positive control passed; 0 'Waiting for lock' lines), then nothing was published. Installed kit is still C528BE4D. No train processes are left. The kit tree still holds TRAIN5's applied src edits (unpublished). Rerun needs a new heavy slot (it was ordered before PACK-8 review); launch it so it survives the caller session (detached supervisor, not host-held), or keep the launching session alive for the full 2h05.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_186 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 186u32, "2026-10-30T10:27Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T10:27 kit: CORRECTION to n185's cause. The BOX CRASHED at 01:26 (unexpected shutdown, rebooted 06:09, per main); kit's session ending and the host-held supervisor were consequences, not the cause. Post-crash tree check (stopping-jobs-that-mutate): C:\\home\\git\\kit is CONSISTENTLY at the TRAIN5-applied state, not half-applied. All 8 edited files match the post-apply sha256 that kit do printed at 00:51:55 (host.spi dd8979e8, check_runtime.spi 9fc17ffa, kit_agile_state/Cargo.toml 1a2cbf78, root Cargo.toml 30991d56, legacy_terminal.spi 5b388055, kit_legacy_operations/Cargo.toml 3a9e6010, commit.spi 11afc61f, native_compiler.rs 4db824cb); release-train.ps1 is cdc6e8dc. Both new crates are whole (kit_delete_guard 6 files/802 .rs lines, agile_planning_gaps 6 files/640; 0 empty files, 0 NUL bytes). Cargo.lock (00:51) lists kit-delete-guard and agile-planning-gaps. Regen had published its 8 owners at 01:18 before the crash; notebooks only read the tree. So no restore is needed: a rerun can use -SkipRegen-style resume, or run whole. Per main: no TRAIN5 restart before 07:00 (crash cause unknown; heavy load is plausible); it goes in the morning queue after the user's report.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_187 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 187u32, "2026-10-30T10:30Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T10:30 kit: TRAIN5's regen output also survived the 01:26 crash. The only generated files written between 00:52 and 01:27 are the 8 published owners' outputs (agile_planning_gaps, kit_agile_state, kit_contracts, kit_delete_guard, kit_job_create, kit_legacy_operations, kit_lint_shadows, kit_lint_shadows_core), with 0 empty files and 0 NUL bytes. The split_list consumers are exactly the node-predicted sizes (kit_lint_shadows 777, kit_lint_shadows_core 731), so regen ran against the landed sm' F8378BD6937F. Option for the morning rerun: release-train.ps1 -SkipRegen starts from the crate gate and saves about 26 min (≈1h40 total). A full rerun is still the conservative choice if the crash cause turns out to involve disk writes. Box queue: only this lost record; node: git-a6's compiler-concurrency running, 32 GB free; nothing of kit's is dangling.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_188 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 188u32, "2026-10-30T17:33Z", "kit", "10-30 13:3x kit: TRAIN5 CONTENT UPDATE. The TRAIN5 rerun (waiting on the user's OK and the laptop on AC) will now also carry today's unstaged kit work, all regenerated with pack 8 on the post-window lib (13:02 close) and proven on a candidate kit.exe built from the live tree with 'cargo build --locked -p kit-cli' (95DC5104).\n- Features and fixes (item, then what changes):\n  - EOIE-DO-APPEND-PARENTS: append creates parent folders; --dry-run previews appends.\n  - GRANULAR-LINT: main's census rules; 0 false flow rows on lib.\n  - EOIE-MACHINE-WINDOWS: job status names the memory-floor wait.\n  - EOIE-AGILE-NOTE-STDIN: 'note -' and 'note-edit -' read stdin.\n  - KIT-NEXT-SKIPS-USER-BATCH: 'next' skips user-batch items.\n  - KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD: agent sessions commit only fixture repos.\n  - EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES F2d/F2e: git status 'staged' row; the do walker in Spiral, skipping .cache.\n  - EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH M1: correct CPU via kit_machine_sample.\n- New crates: kit_lint_flow, kit_lint_flow_constructs, kit_lint_flow_idioms, kit_machine_sample, kit_do_walk. Cargo.lock gains only those packages plus the kit-do -> kit-do-file-steps edge.\n- Acceptance 14/14: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\agent-commit-guard\\candidate-acceptance.ps1 (11 rows), plus append dry-run, copy skipping .cache, and machine watch cores against Windows counters (1.67 read, 1.61 true).\n- Registry: 7 new test notebooks (lint x5, git_cli, sample, walk) join the notebook phase.\n- Closeout after install: rerun the acceptance script against the installed kit, then close the items above.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_189 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 189u32, "2026-10-30T18:04Z", "kit", "10-30 14:2x kit: TRAIN5 RUNNER AND PYTHON PINNED. Compiler's verdict: the lib is fine (the old runner passes 9/9 of the sm' tests on the post-window lib; 7 of the 9 earlier failures were load). The new runner F1DD2E34 hangs nondeterministically in show_floats [zig]/[delphi], so it's reverted, and TRAIN5 keeps 2E5F532E73EEAF14. The 5 sm' cuda rows depend on which python comes first on PATH, not on the lib. So launch-train5.ps1's train stage now refuses unless C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe hashes to 2E5F532E73EEAF14, and puts SPIRAL_PYTHON's folder (scoop python312, numpy 2.5.4) first on the process PATH. Process-only, no machine config. It parses; the runner is 2E5F532E; python resolves to python312 with numpy. Compiler's morning run with python312 first was 72/72, so the cuda rows are expected green. TRAIN5 is ready apart from the user's OK (and the laptop on AC).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_190 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 190u32, "2026-10-30T18:20Z", "kit", "10-30 14:2x kit: TRAIN5 launcher, one more process-only setting, from main's Cells window close (apps/cells mix test 327 passed): SPIRAL_CELLS_SHELL_LAUNCHER = the installed kit.exe, so the train's Cells daemons start under explorer.exe through 'kit process start-under-shell' (present on C528BE4D) and can't be orphaned under a dead cmd. The daemon port moved to 13905 + 8k, still inside 139xx, so the 'nothing listens on 139xx' preflight still covers it. Launcher parses.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_191 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 191u32, "2026-10-30T18:25Z", "kit", "10-30 14:2x kit: TRAIN5 content grew after n188. It adds 'kit memory save | edit | forget' (EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS, new crate kit_memory_save) and M2's reused-pid parent rule in kit_machine_sample (EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH n11). candidate-acceptance.ps1 now has 16 rows (+memory save refusal, save, edit hook, forget/restore, kernel parent kept), and 16/16 pass on the current candidate. Closeout after install: run that script with -Candidate set to the installed kit. New crates since n188: kit_memory_save. Regen list (C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\regen-after-lib-window.tsv) has 27 crates for any later lib change.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_192 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 192u32, "2026-10-30T18:33Z", "kit", "10-30 14:3x kit: TRAIN5 launcher pins SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_PORT=13977 in its process, per main: the new default daemon port is per compiler BUILD, so every node mirror on one DLL shares it. It refuses if 13977 is already listening (free at 14:3x); 13977 is inside 139xx, so the preflight still covers it. Daemons are stopped by pid or owner, never by port.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_193 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 193u32, "2026-10-30T19:16Z", "kit", "10-30 15:2x kit (EOIE-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE): the frozen GPT-era backlog kit/state/agile.spi maps PORT-STRICT-RELEASE to this item. Their remaining intent is this item's scope; no separate work is carried over. Table: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\legacy-state-triage.tsv.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_194 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 194u32, "2026-10-30T19:53Z", "kit", "10-30 15:4x kit: runner split until TRAIN5 publishes. Node runner = F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (compiler swapped it after kit's 'node ok'; smoke byte-identical, SPIRAL_PYTHON honoured; old one kept as spiral.exe.replaced-runner-F1DD2E34). Box runner stays 2E5F532E73EEAF14, which TRAIN5's launcher pins. CLOSEOUT STEP: when TRAIN5 publishes, message compiler to swap the box to F1DD2E34; the next train's launcher then pins F1DD2E34 on both machines and can drop the python312-first PATH workaround.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_195 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 195u32, "2026-10-31T00:30Z", "kit", "10-30 20:3x kit: what the next kit train carries (all unstaged in kit/src, on top of TRAIN5's items), and the acceptance that proves an install. CONTENTS: table query --median, plus the kit_table_filter split (EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES n26-27); table sequences --count/--count-in/--in-set for tibia's pz-in-traces (n29-30), plus the kit_table_sequences split (verb 976 -> 125); machine health verb with leftovers, history and stall rule, M1-M3 (EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH n13-14); lint baseline fix for unnamed rows, plus kit/standards/lint-macros*.rows (GRANULAR-LINT n35-36); rc_str adoption, agile next about 6x faster (EXPORT-STRING-PARAM-RC n9); start-under-shell console-window fix for the visible erl windows the user reported (EOIE-START-UNDER-SHELL n6). ACCEPTANCE: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\agent-commit-guard\\candidate-acceptance.ps1 now has 23 rows, 5 new for the list above; candidate 6E4F7AB5: 23/23 PASS (20:30). After install, rerun it against the installed kit.exe: every row must pass, and the 5 new rows fail on today's installed C528BE4D, so they are real controls. Open, not blocking the train: 6 census-ratchet regressions recorded on EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET n42.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_196 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 196u32, "2026-10-31T00:39Z", "kit", "10-30 20:4x kit: final candidate for the next train: 7C8DD692 (pinned C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\launch-no-window\\kit-final-7C8DD692.exe; adds the watch skip-idle fix to n195). Acceptance 23/23 PASS. The git-status-vs-installed rows now retry up to 3 times, because other sessions write into C:/home/git/spiral between the two calls (499 vs 500 untracked once; it passed on attempt 3). The live kit tree equals the candidate's scratch workspace (0 mismatches, apart from TRAIN5's two drafted crates), and nothing is staged.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_197 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 197u32, "2026-10-31T09:10Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 05:1x kit: starved trains now finish instead of restarting (unstaged, scripts/). release-train.ps1 got two changes. (a) A serial retry pass: notebooks whose log says 'Spiral cell timed out' rerun once at throttle 1 after the parallel phase. (b) -Resume reuses .cache/release-tree/<Name>. It stops if the rebuilt candidate's hash differs from the earlier run's, reruns only the non-passing rows of notebooks-verdicts.txt over the saved notebooks.txt, and refreshes the live repo kit.exe like -Snapshot does. launch-train.ps1 passes -Resume through. The new scripts/resume-train-if-starved.ps1 -Name <n> resumes only when the train's last STOP is 'candidate notebooks are not green' and every red log timed out. Negative control: on train5d (crate-gate stop) it answered 'stopped for another reason ... a resume can't help', exit 1. It is chained after TRAIN5e as job-1793437771344-kit-train5e-resume-gate (after_mode=any). TRAIN5e at 05:06 had 94/140 notebooks done, and all 7 reds are timeouts (kit_experiment_stats, kit_experiments x2, kit_handoff_render, kit_job_slot, kit_jobs model, kit_lint_model).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_198 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 198u32, "2026-10-31T09:36Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 05:3x kit: TRAIN5e was not stopped by its reds. It hit its job's 5 h wall-clock cap (18,000,000 ms) at 05:31, with 99 of 140 notebooks done, and was killed mid-phase, so it never wrote notebooks-verdicts.txt or a STOP line. The chained gate correctly answered 'did not stop; nothing to resume' and exited 0. FIX (unstaged): release-train -Resume without a verdicts file now rebuilds the passes from the earlier run's per-notebook logs, using the same rule as the verdict (the total line has failed 0, passed = executed, unsupported 0, and there is no type error or timeout). resume-train-if-starved also resumes a train that ended with neither STOP nor DONE. LIVE: resumed at 05:35 as job-1793439312086-kit-train5e-20261031. Cargo found the candidate fresh (D269D3E1, same as 00:47:57), so the hash check passed, and 93 of 140 passes were recovered from the logs. kit_notebook_progress's train line: model.spi 5/5 on the live tree, regen published (progress.rs 814).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_199 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 199u32, "2026-10-31T09:43Z", "kit", "10-31 05:4x kit: test-regeneration.ps1 -Package now accepts folder names and underscores. After owner selection it replaces -Package with the selected owners' crate names, which Get-KitOwners already resolves, so the cargo --package arguments and build.ps1 -Test -Package get real crate names. Proof: -Package 'kit_notebook_progress' -CargoCheck printed 'Checking kit-notebook-progress' and 'KIT regeneration passed for 1 selected owners'. Before, cargo was handed the folder name, and a regen had to pass hyphenated names (a trap noted in the 10-30 summary).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_200 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 200u32, "2026-10-31T12:19Z", "kit", "10-31 08:0x kit: TRAIN5e INSTALLED kit.exe E14F1F0B at 07:43, after a 5 h cap, two resumes and a restart onto a lib snapshot. 140/140 notebooks; 7 load timeouts cleared on retry or resume. The binary swap was retire-then-move, so running lanes kept working. release-acceptance.ps1 passed 23/23 at 07:44. NEW ROW (24th): 'memory import round-trips and recall ranks by words'. It imports the copied memory folder to memory.spi (214 memories, index_identical=yes) and recalls 'stopped session wake heartbeat'; the top hit must be idle-needs-wake-source. It passes on E14F1F0B. A rerun at 08:0x gave 23/24: the timing row 'agile next on the live backlog under 4 s' measured 10.2 s, against 2.6 s at 07:44, while TRAIN6's full regen held the box at 100% CPU. That threshold is wall time and fails under load without measuring the binary (no-quiet-machine-wait). Fix next: time with the receipt's elapsed_ms (kit's own clock), not wall time.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_201 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 201u32, "2026-10-31T12:30Z", "kit", "10-31 08:3x kit: HOLD before TRAIN7 (main's request). After TRAIN6 (job-1793447760143) ends, start no train until main messages that two waiters are done: Cells window 6 (apps/cells and 4 lib .spir files; train notebooks run the live Cells app, which the lib snapshot doesn't cover) and the compiler pack 10 install (it swaps the installed SpiralCompiler that notebooks use). Both start on their own once no *train* job is running; expect about 15 min plus 30-60 min. The queued kit-train6-resume-gate only resumes train6 itself, never a new train. GAP FOUND: the installed kit has no 'window announce' verb (only request/release/list/check/claim/wait-clear/run/remote), so main can't reserve this gap in a form trains would respect, and today it rests on a message. Candidate: let a train check for a held or announced 'cells-edit'/'compiler-install' window before its notebook phase. ALSO SEEN LIVE: this note's first attempt was refused with 'state/agile.spi changed since it was read; nothing written', which is KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES's compare-and-swap on the installed E14F1F0B catching a concurrent lane write instead of overwriting it.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_202 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 202u32, "2026-10-31T13:19Z", "kit", "10-31 09:2x kit: the train's full regen is now its long pole. TRAIN6 regenerates every owner one at a time, at about 45 s each on the shared box (regen.log rows: kit_job_state 49.9 s, kit_os_launch 38.0 s, kit_remote_status 45.4 s), and had done 165 of 268 owners after 80 min: about 3.4 h of regen before a 2-3 h notebook phase, which guarantees the 5 h cap (resume-train-if-starved is chained to absorb it). File modification times can't skip owners: 53 packages have .spi newer than their .rs, but Set-KitGeneratedFile leaves unchanged outputs untouched, so an older .rs may still be current. NEXT (an incremental regen): key each owner by a hash of its inputs (its .spi files plus its transitive package deps' .spi, as Get-PackageInputs already walks for the narrowed lease, plus the compiler DLL hash and the lib snapshot hash), store the hash beside the published output, and regenerate only owners whose key changed. A train after a few edits would then regen a handful of owners in minutes instead of 268 in hours.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_203 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 203u32, "2026-10-31T13:35Z", "kit", "10-31 09:3x kit: two train tools landed (unstaged). (1) INCREMENTAL REGEN: test-regeneration.ps1 -Incremental keys each owner by SHA-256 over the compiler DLL hash, every lib .spi/.spir/package.spiproj, and every .spi/.spir/package.spiproj/Cargo.toml in the owner's package plus its transitive package deps (the same walk as the narrowed lease). After a successful -Publish it stores '<key> <published .rs hash>' in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\regen-keys\\<owner>.key. Next run, an owner whose key matches AND whose live .rs still hashes to the stored value skips the compiler; its current output still goes through cargo check and the publish compare. PROOF on kit_notebook_progress: run 1 compiled (44.9 s) and recorded the key; run 2 printed 'unchanged inputs; compile skipped' (whole run 101 s against 209 s). NEGATIVE CONTROL: with one byte appended to progress.spi it compiled again (50.1 s); the file was restored and hash-checked. release-train's regen now passes -Incremental. TRAIN7 compiles everything once and records keys; later trains then regen only owners whose inputs changed, instead of 268 x ~45 s. (2) TRAIN HOLDS: kit/scripts/train-hold.ps1 -Holder <name> [-Minutes n] [-HolderPid p] [-Release] writes %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\train-holds\\<name>.hold. launch-train.ps1, and so the resume gates, waits up to -HoldWaitMinutes (default 240) while any hold is live (until not passed, or holder pid alive). Tested: a 2-min hold refused a 0-min-wait launch with 'trains are held (probe-hold until ...)', and after -Release the same check passed. This is the reservation main lacked tonight (no 'kit window announce' verb).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_204 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 204u32, "2026-10-31T17:00Z", "kit", "10-31 13:0x kit: TRAIN6 hit its 5 h job cap at 12:57 with 19+/140 notebooks done (a slow box), and the chained gate behaved as designed: it found no STOP or DONE and launched the resume, and launch-train waited on main's train holds (cells-window-6 until 18:06, pack10-install until 19:38). DEADLOCK FOUND AND BROKEN: main's waiters start when no job labelled *train* is running, and the waiting gate was itself a running job named kit-train6-resume-gate. It was stopped and restarted under kit-r6-holds-then-resume (job-1793465946953). RULE: a helper that waits for others must not carry the word 'train' in its label. Chain gates with labels like kit-r<n>-... ; only the real train job is kit-train<n>-<date>. The resume gives up after -HoldWaitMinutes 240 (about 16:57); main was asked to -Release its holds when done. While main's Cells and compiler work runs, kit runs no notebooks or regens either, because both use the live Cells app and the installed compiler.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_205 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 205u32, "2026-10-31T17:36Z", "kit", "10-31 13:3x kit: TRAIN7 MANIFEST, everything unstaged in kit since the TRAIN6 snapshot (07:57) or not covered by it, with how each is accepted once installed. BINARY CHANGES: (1) Done path: agile_todo_scan skips the comment parse for files without the id (KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS n17; accept: a live Done set under 10 s wall, roots_cli refusal still fires). (2) kit do copy with a literal file (EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL; acceptance row 25). (3) lint shadows --opens plus the new kit_lint_opens crate (EOIE-OPEN-SHADOW-LINT; acceptance row 26). (4) kit standards checks subfolder entries (KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS; CLI case subfolder_entries_of_the_package_are_checked_too). (5) 112 string respells across 9 files, plus duplicate-helper removals in kit_agile_mutation, kit_agile_routes and agile_task_revision, and kit_table_query's ++# with its sm'_operators import (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY n32; notebooks). Also whatever landed after 07:57 that TRAIN6 lacks: check its snapshot time against EOIE-LOG-SEQUENCES' typed count_spec, KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES' replace_records_unchanged and KIT-RENAME's team-tag match. SCRIPT CHANGES (no install needed, live on next use): incremental regen, train holds, -Resume from logs, resume-train-if-starved, the lib snapshot (SPIRAL_CELLS_LIB), narrowed regen leases with retried removal, -Package folder names, notebook-batch.ps1, and release-acceptance rows 24-26 with kit-clock timing. VERIFICATION IN FLIGHT: node mirror kit-verify (spiral + kit synced, digests OK) runs 13 touched-module notebooks as job-1793467903613-kit-verify-batch, while the box gap belongs to main (Cells window 6, pack 10). Launch TRAIN7 only after main releases its holds; it must also run a full regen, because pack 10 changes the compiler hash and so invalidates every incremental key.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_206 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 206u32, "2026-11-01T01:07Z", "kit", "10-31 21:1x kit: train resume reused stale notebook verdicts. On resume, release-train.ps1 counted any clean notebook log in the train folder as a pass (\"from the earlier run's log\") without comparing it to the candidate, so a resume that rebuilt the candidate after a source change kept passes the new code never earned. Seen: train5e and train6 both list todo_cli.spi as such a pass, while the TRAIN7 preview found the --tagged prefilter regression in that same notebook (KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS n18). FIX (scripts/release-train.ps1, the reuse loop): a log is reused only if it is newer than the candidate kit.exe ($built) and newer than the notebook's source in the release tree; otherwise the notebook re-runs. Parse-checked; it takes effect on the next train. Script is frozen glue under PS1-TO-SPIRAL (A)(1) 'kit train'; the port must keep this freshness rule.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_207 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 207u32, "2026-11-01T03:38Z", "kit", "10-31 23:4x kit groom, NEXT NODE-RUNNABLE ITEM: the TRAIN7 node pre-proof. On mirror kit-verify: candidate-build with the full set of owners changed since TRAIN6 (the 30 of job-1793492637691 plus agile_todo_scan/kit_lint_walk/kit_lint_macros as already published), then notebook-batch over every module touched since TRAIN6 (not the 30-module subset), and write a sha256 manifest of the generated crates so the box train can run -SkipRegen (memory node-proof-skips-regen). Longest wait today: TRAIN6 stopped at its 10:57 cap and then sat behind cells-window-6 and pack10-install holds until the 14:31 resume, about 3.5 h.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_208 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 208u32, "2026-11-01T12:38Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD for TRAIN7 (the next train): (a) node pre-proof: candidate-build of every owner changed since TRAIN6 (34 + tonight's packages) green, notebook-batch over every module touched since TRAIN6 with 0 RED, and a sha256 manifest of the generated crates written next to it; (b) the box train runs with -SkipRegen only after its own tree matches that manifest (a missing or mismatched manifest means a full regen), resumes reuse a notebook log only if newer than the candidate and its source (fix in the tree since 10-31); (c) installed binary hash recorded and acceptance rows green; longest hold wait during the train < 30 min (HEAVY-HOLD-DEADLOCK). NEXT STEP: the pre-proof job on node mirror kit-verify (full owner list per memory remote-kit-worker-node; never re-sync between regen and build), then the manifest check as a 'kit regen --verify-manifest <file>' call the train makes before -SkipRegen. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN for the 'kit train' port: train phases as a GADT typestate (Snapshot -> Regen|SkipRegen -> CrateGate -> Candidate -> Notebooks -> Release, indexed by phase so 'release' before 'notebooks' does not typecheck); resume evidence as a union (FreshLog | StaleLog | NoLog) instead of a log-text match; manifest rows typed (crate, file, sha256 nominal), compared as sets.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_209 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 209u32, "2026-11-01T13:17Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit groom: this item is the kit train PORT and the train history (208 notes); each concrete train now gets its own item so it can close: KIT-TRAIN7 filed (DoD from n208). Future trains follow the same pattern.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_210 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 210u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 42 h ago by kit, progress kept at 45%. Resume from that note: 11-01 09:1x kit groom: this item is the kit train PORT and the train history (208 notes); each concrete train now gets its own item so it can close: KIT-TRAIN7 filed (DoD from n208). Future trains follow the same pattern.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_211 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 211u32, "2026-11-03T10:14Z", "kit", "11-03 06:2x kit: TRAIN14c INSTALLED 06:08 (kit.exe 5B9082C1; regen 284 owners, 0 changed; crate gate 284/284 under 1000; 58/58 notebooks; release build with schema and topology checks). It carries decline-on-release (live-proven), whole-word job liveness, kit window list announced blocks, the lint classifier fixes, and resilience's BEAM-GUARD set. NODE SWAPPED the versioned way (main asked; the node is never idle): the new binary read the live job store first, then C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe went AD5A8A62 -> 5B9082C1 with the old kept at C:\\home\\bin\\kit-AD5A8A62.exe, and a fresh-process smoke passed (exit 0); running jobs were untouched. EUROPA: its Linux kit (remote-machines eoie /home/remote/git/kit/src/target/debug/kit) is still pre-TRAIN14c; the rebuild from the TRAIN14c tree is next when europa is free (also moves supervisor copies off the 1.7 GB /tmp tmpfs). Lessons from TRAIN14/14b: memory train-snapshot-takes-peer-wip.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_212 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 212u32, "2026-11-03T16:13Z", "kit", "11-03 12:3x kit: TRAIN15 STOPPED, nothing installed: 40/51 notebooks. Of the 11 failures, 8 were TYPE-ERROR rows all pointing at c:/home/git/spiral/lib/spiral/file_system.spi:1050 (tibia's 10:42 live-lib break), and 3 were NOT-RUN. ROOT CAUSE IN KIT: train notebooks never read the -Lib snapshot. Cells' find_spiral_lib walks the notebook's ancestors before it reads SPIRAL_LIB, and the walk from .cache/release-tree/<TRAIN>/src reaches C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral. So 'notebooks read the lib at <snapshot>' has been false since the snapshot was added. FIX (tree): release-train.ps1 mirrors the -Lib snapshot to <snapshot>/deps/spiral/lib/spiral, which the walk finds first, and stops the train if the copy fails. PROOF: an error injected only into that copy surfaced via a cells-mount when a notebook ran from TRAIN15's snapshot; probe artifacts removed. NEXT: TRAIN16 once the europa proof of the current WIP (CI heal + entry slices + export codemod + nameof heals) is green.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_213 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 213u32, "2026-11-03T18:56Z", "kit", "11-03 16:4x kit: TRAIN16 LAUNCHED (job-1793732042113-kit-TRAIN16). It's the first train whose notebooks read the snapshot lib, through <snapshot>/deps/spiral/lib/spiral. PINS: (1) runner -RunnerHash 9FF45F124306B5EC (spiral.exe was rebuilt at 09:08 by another lane; pinned to the current hash, not 'any', so another mid-train change still stops the train); (2) SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL = a private copy of the pack24 compiler (6B30D2F5...), because pack25/26 regressed: count_scan.spi fails 3/4 with rustc E0507 (moves a closure-captured string in am'.vec_fold') on the current DLL and passes 4/4 on pack24 (same-input A/B on the box); reported to main for compiler. Content: today's kit WIP (CI heal: Windows batch chunking + sysinfo process liveness; KIT-ENTRY-X S1-S7 slices; 630-site export codemod; 16 reflected word maps; baseline-only-shrinks merge refusal; tree-window path guard; train lib isolation). Linux side: europa round 8 runs the same tree with the export byte-identity A/B and the Linux CLI checks.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_214 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 214u32, "2026-11-03T19:32Z", "kit", "11-03 17:2x kit: TRAIN16 was STOPPED (mine, during regen, before any publish). Its snapshot carried an agile_claim_store parse error: a 9-tuple parameter whose type annotation was continued onto its own line, plus a stray ')' left by an export rewrite. Fixed: applied_claims now takes a claim_application record of 9 primitive fields (all-primitive records cross a link directly), and a box compile+cargo check of agile_claim_lease/request/store/cli passed before relaunch. TRAIN16b LAUNCHED (job-1793733696136) with the same pins: runner 9FF45F124306B5EC, SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL = the private pack24 copy (compiler's E0507 fix isn't confirmed; main says keep the pin). New in TRAIN16b: kit_lint_args, a linked unit that parses the lint flags once for macros/shadows. LESSON: run a compile-only check of every package touched since the last proof before a long round or a train; three rounds today died on one-line slips.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_215 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 215u32, "2026-11-05T10:47Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 06:5x kit: TRAIN28 RED at regen cargo (node job-1793871811335, pack44 dll E441B6B3, 53 min): the single error in the whole regen is E0308 at kit_agile_sprint_show\\show.rs:250 (expected agile_note_listing::UH0, found UH0: a local list string in a Mut1 loop state typed with the linked crate's list union). Compiler bug reported to compiler with the shape. kit workaround (unstaged): show.spi last_note_line uses an array split (sm'.split + am'.index_base), so the crate builds no list of its own. Box --check ok. Node pre-flight running: job-1793875512132-kit-size-split (kept regen of kit_proof_scope_imports, kit_proof_scope, agile_task_next, kit_agile_sprint_state, kit_agile_sprint_show), then cargo check -p on the kept tree before TRAIN29.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_216 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 216u32, "2026-11-05T12:53Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 09:0x kit: TRAIN29 RED at regen cargo (node, pack44 dll E441B6B3, launched 07:39, regen ended 08:44). The TRAIN28 fix held (show.rs clean). The train's gate showed one error, E0425 kit_ingest_frontier\\ingest_frontier.rs:317 (a shape alias for a struct nested in a host-global mod). LESSON: cargo stops scheduling crates after the first failure, so each train shows one error at a time. A full 'cargo check --workspace --keep-going --message-format short' on the kept regen tree (node kit-regeneration\\dbc0f5f92bd545b480e17065cea9067c, 41 s warm) found 13 errors in 4 crates, all compiler-side: the E0425 above plus the TRAIN28 E0308 linked-list-union class in kit_window_query (query.rs:93-104), kit_exec_jobs (jobs.rs:260-271) and kit_run_cli (run.rs:184-195). Full list sent to compiler, which has both fixes in pack48 (fix 3 closed shapes, fix 4 generated-structs-only). kit does NOT work around these. NEXT: when pack48's candidate bin exists, run a full regen with it + keep-going cargo check before TRAIN30; then TRAIN30 carries everything (TRAIN29 snapshot + kit_job_slot/kit_job_host/kit_job_control heals proven since). Memory pack-preflight-regen-cargo-probe updated.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_217 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 217u32, "2026-11-05T14:25Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 10:2x kit: TRAIN30 LAUNCHED 10:25 (box job-1793888708235, node mirror train25), on pack49 (host A1BF06EB, core 0BA4A608; node = box per main 09:39). GATE before launch: a full kit regen with the pack48 candidate (same core) + cargo check --workspace --keep-going = 348 owners, 0 errors (node job-1793883435492). The six kit_mirror* crates added after that gate's snapshot passed their own kept regen + cargo check -p (job-1793888353021, 0 errors after adding sha2 to two Cargo.toml files). Carries since TRAIN29: kit_job_slot/host/control heals, the kit_proof_scope budget refactor, KIT-REMOTE-SYNC v2, and everything from TRAIN29's snapshot. Pending on the node.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_218 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 218u32, "2026-11-05T16:09Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 12:1x kit: TRAIN30 RED at the CRATE GATE only. Its regen phase passed for the first time since TRAIN21: every owner regenerated (293 published, 60 unchanged) and the full cargo check was clean on pack49. Four crates over 1000: kit_job_slot 1311, kit_job_host 1090, kit_job_control 1105 (all three are this morning's GRANULAR heals of host one-liners into Spiral list/sort code, never sized: my slip; memory size-every-inliner updated) and agile_claim_rank 1025 (999 at HEAD; it inlines agile_task_next, where the Blocked-dependents task_waits added a second reflection pass). FIXES (unstaged, box --check ok, standards ok): NEW linked crate kit_job_ticket (ticket helpers out of slot: node-sized slot 491, ticket 945); NEW linked crate kit_job_names (earliest_ending = fold-min with comp/lt_is instead of a full am'.sort, newest_labeled) used by host and control; task_waits = task_open || status equals the Blocked case text (no reflection loop). Comprehensive node probe of every crate changed since TRAIN30 (28 named + missing-.rs deps added automatically now): job-1793894928791. TRAIN31 launches when it is clean. Node = box on pack51 (core E190545B, per main 12:01).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_219 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 219u32, "2026-11-05T16:44Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 12:4x kit: TRAIN31 LAUNCHED 12:43 (box job-1793896999040, node mirror train25) on pack51 (host A1BF06EB, core E190545B; node = box per main 12:01). Pre-launch proof: every crate changed since TRAIN30 (plus all dependencies without committed generated .rs, now added by the probe script itself) regenerated and cargo-checked on the node with ERRORS=0 CARGO-EXIT=0 and every crate under 1000: kit_job_slot 491 + new kit_job_ticket 945; kit_job_host 924 + kit_job_control 794 + new kit_job_names 675 (earliest_ending / newest_labeled / live_items); agile_claim_rank 726 (was 1002 even at HEAD under pack51; its job-liveness scan moved into kit_job_names); the memory/table/experiment/queue/supervise typed-link heals all under 1000 (largest memory_query 999). Reverted for size: the Blocked-dependents ranking fix (archived; needs a ranking split first).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_220 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 220u32, "2026-11-06T11:26Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_221 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 221u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries BNDL-11 (Binary staging and promotion). Why: build, smoke, guarded copy-back and profile record of kit's own release binary are the train's verbs")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_222 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 222u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. BNDL-11 · Binary staging and promotion · P2 · sqlt, ota · Open / One operation that builds (by profile and codegen backend), copies, strips, chmods, renames atomically, hashes and smoke-tests a release binary, records which profile produced it (release vs dev-stripped), and never claims release evidence for a debug build.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_223 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 223u32, "2026-11-07T19:45Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: TRAIN37 (launched 14:12 on pack61 E3F33F3766EE6EDA, node half job-1794075557718) STOPPED in regen at 15:42 on a pack61 Rust codegen bug, not kit code: generated cold_proof_domain/cold_proof.rs:78 string_concat(&[&*v1, ...]) references an unbound v1 (E0425). Trigger: an inline := path (root) (relative) = root ++# \"/\" ++# relative called with a literal second argument. Repro and details sent to compiler; nothing installed; the installed kit stays TRAIN33. The train itself proved S4 (node half via kit job start --on) and STALE-PIN (fresh pin equal to parity) live. NEXT STEP: relaunch as TRAIN38 on the fixed pack (or pack60 if compiler rolls back), carrying everything TRAIN37 had plus drift-retire batch 1, the per-test TestTargets rules, CratesOnTest and the dialect respell.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_224 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 224u32, "2026-11-08T04:31Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 00:3x kit, TRAIN39 RECOVERY and a resume gap. The node half ended 195/196 (agile_task_split/split_cli.spi did not parse: a := value continued on the next line with ++#). release-train -Resume on the node refused: it needs the snapshot of an earlier -Snapshot run, but node trains run against the mirror with -NotebooksOnly and never write one. Worked path: fix the file, write it into the node mirror and the box snapshot (same sha256), rerun release-train -NotebooksOnly -SkipRegen -Only split_cli on the node (candidate D866369B unchanged, cargo found it fresh; same core 65DEE79C; 1/1 pass, 15 s), then the box half via launch-train -NodeStage -ResumeNodeJob <that job> as a box kit job. GAP TO FIX: node-train resume should rerun only the non-passed notebooks against the existing candidate without a box snapshot (the verdicts file and the candidate hash are enough), and launch-train should offer it as one flag. Also the precheck has no guard for a continuation line that starts with ++# under a := binding; add it.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_225 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 225u32, "2026-11-08T04:57Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 00:5x kit, TRAIN39 VERDICTS REBUILT (for audit). The -Only split_cli rerun overwrote the node's notebooks-verdicts.txt with 1 row, and the box half fetched that file; release-train on the box would then refuse (verdicts miss 195 of 196), a safe failure but no install. All 196 per-notebook logs were still on the node (195 from the full 22:26-00:22 run, split_cli from the 00:29 rerun), all on candidate D866369B with core 65DEE79C. A scratch script rebuilt the rows with release-train's own pass rule (clean spiral-tests total, no ETY, ParserErrors, type error or timeout), mapping each log back to its notebook by computing the log name of every src .spi in the mirror: 196 rows, 196 pass, 0 unmapped. Written as notebooks-verdicts-merged.txt on the node and copied over the box's node-verdicts.txt before the box half read it; the 1-row file is kept beside it as node-verdicts.txt.one-row-<time>. GAP (same as note 224): a node rerun of failed notebooks should merge into the earlier verdicts, not replace them.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_226 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 226u32, "2026-11-08T14:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 10:1x rig: TRAIN40 NODE HALF GREEN (node job-1794140052966-kit-TRAIN40, pack61b core 65DEE79CF2CF8B9F pinned start and end): regen 20 changed owners (353 unchanged) in 48 min, crate gate ok crates=373 over=0, candidate kit.exe D5D22429, notebooks 66/66 pass (module notebooks of the 29 packages changed since TRAIN39 shipped manifest; positive control kit_lcov pass), 20 regenerated outputs fetched by hash and copied back to the live tree. Box half started as job-1794147257405-kit-TRAIN40 on the heavy gate (installs on the box). Correction: rig note headers on 11-08 labeled 10:0x to 10:5x were written before 10:14 local and ran ahead of the clock; the at stamps on each note are the true times.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_227 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 227u32, "2026-11-08T18:16Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 14:1x rig: TRAIN41 LAUNCHED 14:12 after i574n posted node ready (node pack62 core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE, Cells runner 2A8B15580CA7F5B6 incremental=false); box watcher job-1794161595649-kit-TRAIN41-node; parity ok dll 9011B777 core 4524F0D8 rustc 1.101.0-nightly. Content: the R3 respell (287 rig_ crates, identifiers and Cargo names), AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE (agile_waits_hold, routing, CLI test), JobPlaced, SPIRAL_CELLS_ROOT resolver (coordinator, release-train, init), config_choice, gleam build/zig-out skip, taplo repo-then-TAPLO_CONFIG, installed-train.txt writer. Full notebook set expected (every package path changed). TWO LAUNCHER BUGS found at launch: (1) the precheck passes every touched file on one command line; 1150 files exceeded the Windows limit, and kit --args-from does not help because it relaunches itself with the same argv; (2) launch-train treats any unexpected precheck output as unavailable and SKIPS the guards. Covered by hand: the precheck run in chunks of 150 found 1907 rows, all pre-existing (inside raw blocks, or equal to their HEAD line after mapping rig_ back to kit_ under the old path), 0 real. Fix (chunked precheck, unknown output refuses instead of skipping, the HEAD-mapping excuse already in) lands after TRAIN41 ends, since the running watcher executes launch-train.ps1 from the live tree.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_228 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 228u32, "2026-11-08T18:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 14:5x rig: LEAK FOUND AND HEALED: every train snapshot under .cache/release-tree kept its own src/target (4-5.5 GB each); 13 snapshots from train5c to TRAIN39 held 57.5 GB of regenerable Cargo output, removed today (sources, results and logs kept; TRAIN40 and TRAIN41 untouched); C: free 210 GB after. FIX (lands after TRAIN41 ends, the running watcher uses the live scripts): release-train removes the snapshot target after a successful install and after a refused one, keeping only the newest installed snapshot target for -Resume. Measured for the storage question: TRAIN40 box half spent 38 of 38.5 min in cargo (debug candidate 10, release 28) rebuilding a tree the node had already built; a shared content-addressed artifact cache is the lever (tibia storage ask, KIT-BUILD-PROFILE).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_229 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 229u32, "2026-11-08T19:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 15:1x rig: LAUNCHER FIXES IN (while no train runs): (1) launch-train sends the touched files to kit lint precheck in chunks of 150 (1150 files broke the Windows argv limit; --args-from relaunches with the same argv, so it cannot help); (2) the precheck fails CLOSED: a chunk with neither ok nor refused output refuses the launch, and the old skipped line is gone; (3) a refused row is excused when its text, mapped back from rig_ to kit_, equals a line of the HEAD file at the old path (rename-aware unchanged check); (4) release-train removes the regenerable src/target of every older snapshot after an install, keeping the current one for -Resume (the 57.5 GB leak). All parse 0. TRAIN41 relaunch is chained on fiscal's box watcher job-1794164344603-fiscal-nfe4-watch (uncontended node run, about 45-75 min).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_230 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 230u32, "2026-11-08T19:45Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 15:4x rig: TRAIN41 RELAUNCHED 15:43 after fiscal's uncontended node run ended (15:37), box watcher job-1794167025173-kit-TRAIN41-node. First use of the fixed launcher: the precheck ran in chunks and passed (1712 rows excused inside raw blocks, 195 on lines unchanged since HEAD under the rename-aware check, 1151 touched files; about 6 min for the precheck).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_231 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 231u32, "2026-11-08T22:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 18:2x rig: TRAIN41 NODE HALF (node job-1794167408476-kit-TRAIN41, pack62 pinned start and end, 15:50-18:11): regen ok (18 changed owners published, 356 unchanged), crate gate ok crates=374 over=0, candidate kit.exe 4F197B31, notebooks 289/292 (all 723 changed packages, since every path changed). 3 failures, none in generated code: (1) rig_jobs/model.spi labels_become_safe_directory_names and (2) rig_notebook_progress/model.spi a_release_train_command_names_its_train_and_root were respell artifacts inside string literals (the identifier rule renamed an expected value but not its input, or the input but not the expected value after an underscore); test-only fixes in the live tree, the box snapshot and the node mirror (hash-equal); (3) rig_units/model.spi was my unfinished RIG-UNITS-U1 module, swept into the snapshot because the train takes the whole live tree; archived out of the TRAIN41 snapshot and the node mirror (kept in the live tree for TRAIN42). Test blocks do not feed codegen, so candidate 4F197B31 stands. Rerun of the 2 notebooks as TRAIN41r on the node, then the verdicts merge and the box half (release-train -Resume -Verdicts) as for TRAIN39.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_232 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 232u32, "2026-11-08T22:21Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 18:3x rig: TRAIN41 rerun TRAIN41r (node job-1794176111752) 2/2 pass on the SAME candidate 4F197B31 (cargo fresh), pack62 pinned. Because the node watcher threw on the 3 failures, its step that fetches regenerated outputs never ran; redone by hand (scratchpad train41-finish.ps1): node mirror vs box snapshot .rs hashes, 18 fetched and hash-verified (= the 18 published owners), 18 copied back to the live tree, 0 conflicts. Verdicts merged: 291 rows, 291 pass (rig_units dropped with its snapshot removal). Box compiler confirmed pack62 core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE before start (compiler holds pack63c on the box until this installs). Box half started: job-1794176472454-kit-TRAIN41 (heavy gate, release-train -Resume -Verdicts).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_233 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 233u32, "2026-11-08T23:01Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:1x rig: TRAIN41 box half STOPPED at the release build (18:45): rig_dev hand-kept dev.rs still passed --package kit-cli (the dev tool is not regenerated from Spiral, so the R3 Cargo rules, which covered Cargo.toml and .spi only, missed its .rs literals). Same class found in rig_dev_spiral_tests registry and 11 more files: a package-literal pass built from the 257 real renamed Cargo packages (bin names kit-dev and kit-lift-predicate excluded) renamed 227 literals in 12 files, live tree and snapshot; 10 remaining kit-* registry labels are test-group labels, not Cargo packages (unchanged in HEAD, cosmetic, R3b). USER RULE now (via org): no compute on the box during non-autonomous periods; org approved: TRAIN41 release build runs on MOON (the only Windows node, same toolchain) in the TRAIN41 mirror with the pinned pack62 compiler, then a hash-verified COPY install on the box. 13 post-snapshot files copied to the moon mirror, hashes equal. Moon job: job-1794178853992-rig-TRAIN41-release. Moon window note for org: this build runs now, ahead of fiscal shard 0, per org.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_234 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 234u32, "2026-11-09T13:53Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:5x local rig, TRAIN42e notebooks phase (moon, still running at 66/277): 2 REGRESSIONS vs TRAIN41 (both green there). (1) src/agile_task_tree/epic_tree.spi: FatalError, ParserErrors (main.spi) line 2 char 4-6 \"Failed to parse this token\", \"The package of main has blocks that fail to tokenize or parse\". Every sibling notebook (agile_quality_facts, agile_quality_lint, agile_task_parents x3) is green and regen compiled all 374 units, so the parse failure is in a harness-generated main, likely the stub for this notebook's two link: units (agile_quality_facts, agile_task_listing; task_listing has no notebook of its own, so this is its only cells compile). Between TRAIN41 and TRAIN42e both linked units changed only by formatter respell (one-branch-per-line guards; union_case_where with its lambda arguments one per line). (2) src/agile_task_notes/notes_cli.spi: the cells runner crashed, ErlangError {:invalid_byte, 129} in json.erl encode_list while encoding a test result: a lone UTF-8 continuation byte, the signature of child output truncated inside a multibyte character; the local change there is only a host-literal reflow. Full red list and owner routing after the phase ends.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_235 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 235u32, "2026-11-09T14:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 10:5x local rig, TRAIN42e notebooks at 84/277 on moon: 2 more reds, both the kit->rig respell crossing the command-line rule (receipts say rig; command lines a reader must RUN keep kit until R4, the binary is kit.exe). (3) src/rig_agile_gate/gate.spi the_gate_names_ready_work_...: ready_line printed \"rig agile claim <root> <ID> --as <lane>\", which does not run; FIXED IN CODE back to \"kit agile claim\" (the test already expected kit). (4) src/rig_adoption/classify.spi commands_split_into_kit_habit_and_other_calls: the committed test expected \"rig read src/x.spi\" to count as a kit call, but rig_named (host.spi:60) matches only the kit binary name, which is the only one that exists; FIXED IN TEST back to \"kit read\". R4 must extend rig_named to both names in the same change that ships a rig binary. Both fixes unstaged, ride TRAIN43 (probe list). Still red from earlier: epic_tree (harness main.spi parse) and notes_cli (runner invalid_byte 129); two more notebooks were still running.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_236 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 236u32, "2026-11-09T15:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:5x local rig, TRAIN42e PROJECTION: notebooks 118/277 at 11:49 (moon local). Pace fell from ~0.5/min (09:43-11:15) to ~0.18/min (11:15-11:49) as moon took four concurrent jobs at 100 pct CPU and 7.8 GB free (tibia-libland5, fiscal-g6a-b3-gate, x-verify-client-r2w, kit-TRAIN42e); the remaining CLI notebooks also each build their own binaries. At the current pace the phase ends well after the 21:00 run deadline, so the post-train steps (box install, the 37-notebook probe batch of today's unprobed models, TRAIN43) move to the next run. Not preempting other lanes' jobs. Capacity fix filed for org: NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET (ganymede had free cores all day; node-proof can only reach moon). Reds so far: 7 red or unfinished (2 fixed in code for TRAIN43: rig_agile_gate claim command, rig_adoption test; 2 open: epic_tree harness main.spi parse, notes_cli runner invalid_byte 129).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_237 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 237u32, "2026-11-09T15:52Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 14:0x local rig, DIAGNOSIS of the notes_cli red (invalid_byte 129): every notes_cli test builds its backlog in a fixture root named \"agile notes ü <label>\"; in the OEM console code page (CP437/850) ü is byte 0x81 = 129, the exact byte the cells runner's JSON encoder rejected. So child output carrying the fixture path reached the runner OEM-encoded, most likely from a FAILING test's message (the fixture is unchanged since TRAIN41, which was green), and the runner crash hides which test failed. Routed to compiler (cells harness): decode captured output lossily and still name the failing test; also the epic_tree harness main.spi parse failure. rig follow-up after the harness fix: rerun notes_cli to name the real failure.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_238 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 238u32, "2026-11-09T18:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:0x local rig, TRAIN42e projection REVISED: notebooks 189/277 at 14:03 moon local (118 at 11:49: ~0.53/min since; moon now runs 3 jobs: fiscal-g6a-b5-gate, x-verify-sim3, kit-TRAIN42e). At this pace the notebook phase ends near 16:50, so the post-train steps (box install, the probe batch of today's unprobed models, then TRAIN43) can start before the 21:00 deadline after all; TRAIN43 itself would finish in the next run.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_239 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 239u32, "2026-11-09T18:54Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:3x rig TRAIN PLAN after TRAIN43 (today's accepted cross-package rewrites, grouped so a red names one family): TRAIN44 = the agile-family argv rewrite: LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH (86 prelude copies -> lib argv_view) with KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE-M2 (the same sites) and LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT's 8 one-line swaps; TRAIN45 = typed records: KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-H2 step 1 (records as array_base, 21 records_text callers) with the DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC fold of the 23 two-guard bindings; TRAIN46 = repo-wide hygiene: KIT-USES-LIB-M1 batch 1 (62 manifests gain the lib reference, byte-identical regen required) with KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT's MagicNumber census word. Each train snapshots only after the previous one installs (train-snapshot-takes-peer-wip). TRAIN43 itself carries today's ~50 unprobed models, admitted per the probe batch, with reds held out by the snapshot swap.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_240 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 240u32, "2026-11-09T20:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:3x rig, TRAIN43 PRE-CHECK READ (rig-regen1109 on ganymede, job-1794218773195; it FINISHED this morning with exit 1, but the box record still says placed, the exact KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE bug; read by hand from /root/.cache/kit/jobs/<id>/exit). Regen 378 units: TWO REDS, both fixed unstaged on the box and synced to ganymede's tree (hashes match): (1) rig_drafts/entry.spi moved: resultm.is_err on file_system.rename's result' (a nominal, not the result union) -> ETY-NominalInPatternUnbox, which also failed rig_cli (main). Fix: resultm.unbox' then Ok/Error arms, the rig_job_ticket.renamed precedent. (2) crate gate over=1: agile_task_creation 1076 lines (largest agile_add_entry_0 567), up from 992. Cause: the rename sweep changed variable_or_empty \"KIT_AUTHOR\" to variable_twin \"AUTHOR\"; variable_or_empty ALREADY routes KIT_/RIG_ names through variable_twin, so the edit changed nothing in behaviour and cost 84 generated lines (a runtime concatenation instead of a folded literal). Fix: variable_or_empty \"RIG_AUTHOR\" (reads RIG_AUTHOR, then KIT_AUTHOR; same as before). Other 376 units ok, crates=378. Not re-run: ganymede is saturated by another lane's cells gate (load ~4 on 4 cores) and TRAIN43 itself regenerates and gates both units; if TRAIN43's gate still shows agile_task_creation over, fall back to the literal \"KIT_AUTHOR\" (the committed 992-line spelling).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_241 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 241u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 21:2x rig, TRAIN42e RESULT: NOT INSTALLED. Coordinator exit 1 at 16:59 local; the node half (moon, job-1794221916075) hit its 10 h wall-clock timeout (exit 124) inside the notebook phase at 270 of 277 notebooks, so no verdict file was written. Before that: regen ok (1 changed owner, 373 unchanged), crate gate ok (374, over 0), candidate kit.exe 134714D1. 9 RED notebooks, ONE ROOT CAUSE for six: rig_cli_check/cli.spi joined and twinned were := ^ (INLINE recursion); twinned (added by the rename sweep, 11-08) branches on starts head \"KIT_\", a host macro and so always a runtime bool, which makes the cli_args list shape dynamic, so joined unrolled to EJP0011 (10000 nested applications) in every CLI test module using it: rig_agile_contracts agile_cli, rig_contracts_receipts cli, rig_coverage_prune coverage_cli, rig_machine_windows windows_cli, rig_release_contracts hygiene_cli, rig_jobs stop_cli. FIX (unstaged): both are :~ ^ join points now (runtime recursion); grep shows no other site. The other 3 reds were already fixed after the 06:58 snapshot (rig_adoption, rig_agile_gate) or are compiler's receipt rerun (agile_task_tree epic_tree). NEXT TRAIN: TRAIN43 with the node-half timeout raised (277 notebooks needed > 10 h on a shared moon; TRAIN43 carries more) or the notebook set split across moon and ganymede; its pre-check reds (rig_drafts type error, agile_task_creation 1076 lines) are fixed. ALSO: 33 of today's 41 new pure models are probe-green on ganymede (/root/rig-probe), 8 more fixed by that probe; their waits are cleared.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_242 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 242u32, "2026-11-09T21:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 21:3x rig, TRAIN43 READY TO LAUNCH, HELD for a quiet moon: fiscal's build took moon at 17:16 local right after TRAIN42e released it (fiscal-erp build.ps1, rustc and erl processes, CPU 100%), and a train needs the node alone. launch-train.ps1 now takes -NodeTimeoutHours (default 10, unchanged behaviour; it sets the node job timeout and the coordinator's give-up horizon; parse 0, unstaged) because TRAIN42e hit the hard 10 h cap at 270/277 notebooks. EXACT LAUNCH (box, PowerShell, when moon is quiet): & $env:LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe job start kit-TRAIN43-node 72000000 pwsh -NoProfile -File C:\\home\\git\\kit\\scripts\\launch-train.ps1 -Name TRAIN43 -Node node -NodeMirror train25 -SshHost laptop-ts -NodeStage -CellsPort 13977 -NodeTimeoutHours 18 (TRAIN42e's exact arguments plus the timeout; 20 h box job over an 18 h node half). Expect ~340 notebooks at ~2.2 min each on a shared node. The snapshot takes the live tree, which carries today's fixes (rig_cli_check join points, rig_drafts unbox, agile_task_creation RIG_AUTHOR, 9 probe-found model fixes) and the 41 probed models; the post-TRAIN43 rewrites (TRAIN44-46) are still NOT in the tree.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_243 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 243u32, "2026-11-09T22:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 18:45 local rig, TRAIN43 LAUNCHED: job-1794264326952-kit-TRAIN43-node (box coordinator, 20 h) with the recorded command (TRAIN42e's arguments + -NodeTimeoutHours 18), after fiscal released moon at 18:40 (moon load 22% at launch) and promised no moon jobs until TRAIN43 releases it. First lines: parity ok (dll 99EADCD9, core F4148639 = pack78), node disk ok (14.3 GB free). The live tree carries today's fixes and the probe-green models; post-TRAIN43 rewrites and drafts (TRAIN44-46, tibia's KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE wiring and KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2) are applied only after the snapshot line. Watched by a background file check every 5 min (never a remote wait).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_244 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 244u32, "2026-11-09T23:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:5x rig, TRAIN44 MANIFEST (one list for the next session; TRAIN43 is in regen on moon since 18:52, notebooks not started). ALREADY IN THE LIVE TREE (applied after TRAIN43's snapshot, unproven until TRAIN44): rig_jobs/jobs.spi placed-exit read side (KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE); 6 lib read swaps (LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT: rig_experiments ledger_host, proxy_text_replacement, rig_do_write_host, rig_guide, agile_lease_terms, cold_proof_domain); rig_memory_adapters AGENTS.md adapter (KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2, tibia); probe-green model growth (rig_memory_typed kind GADT + heading-aware reasons, rig_lane_work rows, rig_tfs_queue census, rig_experiment_ledger rows, rig_handoff_degrade inputs + renderer, rig_authority_audit table, rig_spec_cases extract, rig_convo_replay surface + nested decode, rig_do_algebra write + external, rig_standards_repo repo_io, rig_memory_check). DRAFTED, NOT APPLIED: tibia's slop wiring (drafts\\kit\\KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M1: rig_do_edit + Cargo + lock, crate at 951 lines). NEEDS A NODE FIRST (Cargo dependency + lock + regen): kit resume Handoff section (KIT-RESUME-COMPILER-M2), the slop wiring, LINK-WITHOUT-MANIFEST's derived path deps. DESIGNED, ride the agile-family rewrite: LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH + KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE-M2, KIT-AGILE-FIND --notes (3 crates through rig_query_passes), agile next skipping parents with children (KIT-NEXT-STARVATION). CENSUS WORDS (shared census code): string-tag-compare (KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT), comment-lines (COMMENT-LINT-GATE), MagicNumber/DrivePath/PosixPath/ExeSuffix (KIT-STANDARDS-PORTABILITY, microblog's draft). Suggested split to keep reds bisectable: TRAIN44 = applied tree changes + slop wiring + resume section (one node prep); TRAIN45 = agile-family rewrite; TRAIN46 = census words + DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC fold + KIT-USES-LIB-M1.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_245 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 245u32, "2026-11-10T00:04Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:0x rig, TRAIN43 STOPPED AT REGEN (19:54; coordinator exit 1), NOTHING INSTALLED. 9 of 378 owners failed, TWO root causes, both rig's, both fixed in the live tree: (1) rig_style_census/census.spi:239 ETY-ModuleIndexFailed (no key toml_run): rig had replaced the shipped src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi (typed verdicts + git/taplo calls + toml_run + its export) with a smaller pure model this morning; RESTORED byte for byte from HEAD (the model is archived under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\rig-standards-toml-model-20261109); memory new-model-must-not-replace-tracked-file. (2) rig_experiments/experiment_gates.spi:43 ETY-TermError (gate vs reading, 8 owners cascading: rig_experiments, _stats, _import, _amend, _analysis, rig_table_test, rig_cli_routes): the fold lambda left c unannotated so the record type was inferred from field names; now (c : checked). A full check of every model package for the same overwrite: only rig_os_process and agile_split_plan are tracked AND modified, both small additive edits. RELAUNCHED as TRAIN43b at 20:0x: job-1794269055477-kit-TRAIN43b-node, the same arguments and -NodeTimeoutHours 18; it shares moon with microblog's x verify chain (running since 18:40, as TRAIN43 did), and its snapshot also carries the TRAIN44 manifest's in-tree changes (placed-exit read side, 6 lib read swaps, sm'.quoted_fields switch), so a red there is attributed by package.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_246 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 246u32, "2026-11-10T00:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:1x rig, NEW TRAIN PREFLIGHT (unstaged, scripts/launch-train.ps1, parse 0; the running TRAIN43b loaded the old copy and is unaffected): Get-UnresolvedReferences scans every src .spi for package.module.name references (rig_ / agile_ / kit_ / rust_std_ / union_ / workspace_ packages) and checks each name has a definition in that module (:= / :~ / :| / :== / :! heads, inl / let / union / nominal, or a union case); the launcher throws \"refusing a node train\" BEFORE the snapshot when any is unresolved, and prints \"references ok\" otherwise. It targets exactly the break that stopped TRAIN43 after 1 h 10 min of regen (rig_style_census calling rig_standards_toml.toml.toml_run, which a rewrite had removed): proof: live tree 1,055 references, 0 unresolved; negative control (the archived model toml.spi beside census.spi) reports rig_standards_toml.toml.toml_run. A few seconds of text scan on the box, CPU-light.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_247 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 247u32, "2026-11-10T00:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:2x rig, train preflight WIDENED (scripts/launch-train.ps1, unstaged, parse 0): Get-UnresolvedReferences now also checks host-macro cross-crate calls (crate::function inside $'...' bodies) against the callee crate's surface = its own .spi plus every package its package.spiproj lists under packages: (export \"x\", pub fn / pub use / pub const|static in global blocks; e.g. rig_agile_state's agile_*_owned come from agile_state_runtime/owned_runtime.spi), and it skips :# test blocks (fixture strings that look like calls). Iterations: 104 -> 22 -> 13 -> 1 -> 0 false findings as multi-line exports, pub fn globals, included source packages and test blocks were learned. Proof: live tree 1,055 Spiral + 320 host references, 0 unresolved, 12 s on the box; negative control with BOTH planted breaks (the archived toml model beside census.spi; agile_begin_owned renamed in a copy of owned_runtime.spi) reports exactly rig_agile_state::agile_begin_owned and rig_standards_toml.toml.toml_run.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_248 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 248u32, "2026-11-10T00:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:33 rig, TRAIN44 manifest addition: src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi = HEAD plus a TAPLO_CONFIG-first taplo_config (a stray repo .taplo.toml no longer overrides the canonical one), probe-green 2/2 on ganymede; toml_run and its export unchanged, the reference preflight reports 0 unresolved.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_249 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 249u32, "2026-11-10T01:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 21:0x rig, TRAIN43b STOPPED AT REGEN (21:04), NOTHING INSTALLED: 8 of 378 owners, ONE cause, rig's incomplete fix: rig_experiments/experiment_gates.spi:59 ETY-TermError (stake vs bool in binding_met), the same unannotated-fold-lambda inference as line 43; lines 59 (binding_met) and 64 (next_step) are now annotated (e : expectation, b : branch), no unannotated two-argument lambda left in the file (unstaged, kit standards checked). NOT relaunched: the rig run window closed at 21:00. Next train: relaunch TRAIN43 as TRAIN43c with the same arguments (-NodeTimeoutHours 18); the new reference preflight runs first. Lesson: when a fix is for an inference pattern, sweep the whole file for that pattern, not the reported line.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_250 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 250u32, "2026-11-10T02:55Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:55 rig: TRAIN43c LAUNCHED (job-1794279304906-kit-TRAIN43c-node; same arguments, -NodeTimeoutHours 18; moon idle at 6 pct, 13.9 GB free). The new reference preflight ran for the first time and passed in 16 s (\"references ok\"), then the snapshot started. Fixes since TRAIN43b, probed off-train on ganymede against the full dependency closure: experiment_gates.spi lines 59/64 annotated plus a test-block local renamed from the keyword then (5/5 green; the then trap would have failed the notebook phase, not regen); a keyword-local sweep over all 188 changed/new .spi found nothing else. Unprovable off-train: the whole-CLI notebooks experiments_cli (unchanged from HEAD) and table_test_cli (one string literal split with the committed ^^ operator); they run in this train. Also in the snapshot: rig_agile_side_rename (new pure package, 3/3) and the rig_standards_toml TAPLO_CONFIG-first edit (2/2).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_251 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 251u32, "2026-11-10T03:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:1x rig, TRAIN44 manifest addition: src/rig_style_measure/measure.spi census line-count fix (test region ends at the next top-level line, not only at main; 144 kit packages and fiscal/src were undercounted, see FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS). Off-train unprovable (linked unit); its notebook must be read in the TRAIN44 verdicts, and the census baseline lines for those 144 packages will rise once the fixed kit is installed.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_252 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 252u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:2x rig groom. Next step: read TRAIN43c's verdict when its coordinator exits (watcher on job-1794279304906); green means hash-verified install of rig.exe plus kit.exe on the box and a smoke run, then compiler told DONE; red means fix by root file, sweep every changed file for the same pattern, and relaunch as TRAIN43d. TRAIN44 (manifest notes 244-251) follows the install.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_253 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 253u32, "2026-11-10T03:51Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 00:0x rig, TRAIN44 manifest addition: agile rename side-file pass (src/agile_task_rename task_rename.spi + package.spiproj include of rig_agile_side_rename; src/agile_task_notes/notes_cli.spi rename test now asserts the wait row moves). Off-train: side package 4/4, reference preflight 0 unresolved; the verb and the CLI notebook are read in TRAIN44's verdicts.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_254 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 254u32, "2026-11-10T04:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 00:3x rig: TRAIN43c PASSED REGEN (all owners) and STOPPED AT THE CRATE GATE: 6 crates over 1000. ROOT CAUSES, three different silent inlinings plus two thin overs: (1) rig_cli 3787 (HEAD 905): rig_cli_model links rig_units and rig_drafts, but the app crate rig_cli/package.spiproj did not list them under packages:/link:, so the compiler inlined their whole CLI bodies into kit.rs (zero rig_units::/rig_drafts:: calls; rig_hook/rig_heal_nameof, which rig_cli does list, link fine). FIXED in the live tree (both lists). (2) rig_do_edit 1500: rig_do_replacement.group_problem was a CURRIED export, and curried args inline (memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes); now takes a tuple, call site updated; rig_do_replacement probe 2/2. (3) rig_units 1792 and rig_drafts 1196 are over on their own: need a split (model unit) before they can ship. (4) rig_agile_mutation 1015: agile_argument_count was an inline := expanded at 31 sites; now a :~ join point. (5) agile_task_creation 1012: variable_or_empty's KIT_/RIG_ twin expands ~25 lines at its call site; the call now uses a new rust_std_env.model.variable_either \"RIG_AUTHOR\" \"KIT_AUTHOR\" (about 8 lines). A one-expression host primitive was tried first and refused by the style contract (120 chars, host-block ratchet). TRAIN43d LAUNCHED 00:19 (job-1794284334153; node half job-1794284845514): TRAIN43c's tree + fixes (4) (5) and the rig_do_replacement tuple, with a HOLD-OUT verified on the snapshot: rig_units, rig_drafts and their wiring (direct_verbs cases, rig_cli_model arms/links, rig_cli Cargo+spiproj, workspace members, lock entries) and rig_do_edit at HEAD (951 lines, deps unchanged since HEAD), plus the train-only-provable edits (agile rename side pass, its CLI test, the census fix) at their TRAIN43c copies. Lock precheck 0, reference preflight ok, keyword sweep 0. Live tree restored after \"node half started\": 15 files, 0 hash mismatches, lock check 0. Next step: read TRAIN43d's verdict; held work returns in TRAIN44 once units/drafts are split.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_255 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 255u32, "2026-11-10T05:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 01:5x rig: TRAIN43d regen OK (Published 7 changed owners, 369 unchanged) and the size fixes WORKED: crate gate over=0 (agile_task_creation and rig_agile_mutation now under 1000). It still stopped: \"3 crate(s) have no generated output\" = agile_task_verify, rig_do_slop, rig_job_liveness, rig's own untracked packages from 11-09 morning that carry a Cargo.toml but are NOT workspace members, so regen never owns them while the gate counts every Cargo.toml dir (TRAIN43c had the same gap, masked by its over-limit stop). TRAIN43e LAUNCHED 01:51 (job-1794289839586; node half job-1794290082654) = TRAIN43d's exact tree minus those 3 dirs: the live tree was diffed against TRAIN43d's snapshot (16 changed files restored to the snapshot copy, 39 new files moved out, including tonight's rig_drafts split and the portability rules), snapshot verified (none of the 6 held packages present), live tree restored (55 files, 0 hash mismatches, lock check 0). Hold manifest: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\rig\\TRAIN43e-hold\\manifest.txt. Also: rig_style_probes with the portability rules is probe-green 2/2. Next step: TRAIN43e verdict; the 3 non-member crates need workspace membership + lock (or no Cargo.toml) before they ship.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_256 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 256u32, "2026-11-10T05:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 02:0x rig, TRAIN44 prep for the 3 crates TRAIN43d's gate found without output: agile_task_verify and rig_job_liveness export nothing (pure models, like rig_job_settle which has no Cargo.toml), so their premature Cargo.toml files are ARCHIVED (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\premature-crate-manifests-20261110), not made crates; rig_do_slop exports and is the slop wiring already in the TRAIN44 manifest, so it is now a workspace member with its lock entry (cargo update --offline --workspace; cargo metadata --locked exit 0). Unstaged; TRAIN43e's snapshot was taken before this and is unaffected.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_257 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 257u32, "2026-11-10T06:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 02:1x rig, TRAIN44 manifest addition: rig_crate_gate names the failing crates and reports both failure classes in one run (GATE-HEALS-1101 note 24); train-gated notebook.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_258 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 258u32, "2026-11-10T07:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 03:1x rig: TRAIN43e PASSED REGEN AND THE CRATE GATE (first of the TRAIN43 series to do so) and entered the notebook phase at 03:08: 331 notebooks (48 use the binary; module notebooks of 483 changed packages), positive control rig_lcov pass at 03:11. Expect hours (TRAIN42e ran about 270 in 10 h; this train has an 18 h node budget). Next step: read its verdicts when the coordinator exits; green means install rig.exe + kit.exe (R2), then R4's window.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_259 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 259u32, "2026-11-10T09:51Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 05:5x rig: TRAIN43e ENDED 05:34, exit 1, nothing installed, but it was the furthest of the series: regen ok (376 unchanged), crate gate ok (376 crates, over=0), candidate kit.exe CB404279 built, notebooks 330/331. The one red: src/rig_contracts/receipts_cli.spi text_replace_receipts_count_matches_and_bytes, expected \"corrected: kit proxy text-replace ...\" while the binary now prints \"corrected: rig proxy text-replace ...\" (a kit->rig rename leftover in a test expectation). Fixed (one line). A sweep for other \"kit <verb>\" test expectations found more (rig_patch_mutation_contracts \"corrected: kit help patch\", rig_spec_cases fixture lines, usage strings), but those match what their verbs still print, so only the proven one changed. TRAIN43f LAUNCHED 05:45 (job-1794303822783; node half job-1794304223915) = TRAIN43e's exact tree + that fix, built by the snapshot diff (18 changed restored, 51 new moved out; the fix verified in the snapshot; live tree restored, 69 files, 0 mismatches, lock 0). Next step: TRAIN43f verdict (about 4 h: regen, gate, 331 notebooks); green installs rig.exe (R2).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_260 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 260u32, "2026-11-10T12:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 08:5x rig: TRAIN43f GREEN ON THE NODE, the first green of the TRAIN43 series. Regen ok, crate gate ok (376 crates, over 0), candidate kit.exe 4CB754D1, notebooks 331/331 pass (06:51-08:46 on moon), coordinator exit 0. The box half is RUNNING now: job-1794314931750-kit-TRAIN43f (release-train.ps1 -Resume, heavy slot 1 granted after 6 s; the user is away until 21:00, so the box may take it). It reuses the snapshot and the 331 node verdicts, re-ran the crate gate on the box (ok) and is building the candidate, then the release build and install. Next step: when the box half exits green, hash-verify and smoke the installed rig.exe + kit.exe, tell compiler DONE, then run R4's window checklist; moon is FREE again, so regen-sizes for the rig_drafts and rig_units splits can run there.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_261 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 261u32, "2026-11-10T13:39Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 09:3x rig: regen-sizes on moon (job-1794316507301-rig-split-sizes, kit e7de0e33 tree) measured the splits. ok: rig_drafts 107 (from 1196), rig_drafts_list 553, rig_drafts_put 539, rig_drafts_promote 658, rig_units_edges 652, rig_units_layout 800, rig_do_edit 958, rig_cli 946. OVER: rig_units 1211 (from 1792), so the first split was not enough. Done now: a third linked unit rig_units_manifest (manifest.spi = the parser + the directory walk; exports rows_under root -> array_base unit_row and members_under root -> array_base string, the shapes array_base carries across a link). rig_units keeps only host_call_deps + the receipt; check.spi calls the three linked units. members/lock updated, pre-split archived at kit\\archive\\rig-units-before-manifest-split-20261110. Probe of manifest.spi + the thinned model.spi is running on ganymede. Next step: when the probe is green, regen-sizes of rig_units + rig_units_manifest on moon (the consumer rig_units is only provable on a train), then it rides TRAIN44.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_262 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 262u32, "2026-11-10T13:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 09:5x rig: the rig_units split now FITS. regen-sizes on moon (job-1794318802229-rig-units-sizes2): rig_units 416 (was 1792, then 1211), rig_units_manifest 924, rig_units_edges 652, rig_units_layout 800; 0 over 1000. With the 09:25 run, every rig split package measured ok. ganymede probe: rig_units_manifest/manifest.spi 1/1 and rig_units/model.spi 1/1. The consumer rig_units/check.spi (three linked units) is only provable on a train: it rides TRAIN44. Next step: when the TRAIN43f box half installs, TRAIN44 with the hold list plus this split.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_263 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 263u32, "2026-11-10T15:04Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 11:0x rig: TRAIN43f box half STOPPED in the release phase by a TIMEOUT, not a code red: build.ps1 -TimeoutMs 3600000 (release-train.ps1:273, already the validator maximum) ran out at 10:55 with cargo still compiling (release.log 54 KB of a normal ~95 KB). The box was at 100% from several concurrent sessions (no single hog); the debug candidate alone took 59 min (08:50-09:49) where past trains took about 30. Installed kit.exe is unchanged. Node half stays green (331/331). RELAUNCHED the box half: job-1794323012525-kit-TRAIN43f-r2 (release-train.ps1 -Name TRAIN43f -Resume, heavy gate); cargo keeps the crates already built, so the release resumes past the halfway mark. Follow-up for the train script: a release timeout should be a retryable state (resume once automatically) rather than a STOP, and the 1 h cap should scale with box load. Next step: when r2 exits green, hash-verify and smoke rig.exe + kit.exe, then R4.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_264 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 264u32, "2026-11-10T15:21Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 11:2x rig: r2 (job-1794323012525) STOPPED at start, nothing built: -Resume would mix compilers. The compiler lane installed a new live core at 09:24 (DE4EE5A21040E965); the train pinned F414863971EB2A2C at 06:4x and the node half ran all 331 notebooks with it. The guard (release-train.ps1:57) runs only when SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL is unset, so r3 sets it to the train pin (.cache\\release-train\\TRAIN43f\\compiler\\SpiralCompiler.dll): the release is built with the same compiler as the verdicts, which is the consistent choice, not a mix. r3 = job-1794323852351-kit-TRAIN43f-r3, queued at the heavy window (box free 573 MB < 1024 MB needed; it starts when memory frees). Follow-up for the script: a box-half resume should default to the train pin, and refuse only when no pin exists.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_265 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 265u32, "2026-11-10T22:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 18:5x rig, CRASH RECOVERY (box BSOD 11:51, down to 18:28): r3 (job-1794323852351-kit-TRAIN43f-r3) was LOST mid-release (exit file: lost, supervisor stopped beating); release.log 44.7 KB at 11:52, cargo still compiling, so nothing was published and installed kit.exe is unchanged (93BDD93F). Node half stays green (331/331, moon). Files rig wrote today were checked after the reboot: 24 files (new packages rig_scratch, rig_scratch_cited, rig_ready_rank, rig_units_manifest, the rig_units/rig_cli/verb wiring, Cargo.toml/lock, the release-train draft and its base, the gate hook) have no NUL bytes, end cleanly, and the recorded hashes match (cited.spi FE3122E7BA7D, rank.spi ADB876EF56B9, draft base 86B9772358C7); both scripts parse. KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN-D1 finished its interrupted close (Done, released). Next step: r4 = the same pinned resume, launched when the box is under 70% CPU (the user is present after a crash, so the box stays light until then); cargo keeps the crates r1 to r3 built.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_266 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 266u32, "2026-11-10T23:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 19:1x rig, MOVED OFF EARTH (user 19:0x via org2: nodes idle while earth sits at 100%, the condition under which both BSODs happened): TRAIN43f's release build now runs on MOON, job-1794351784230-rig-release-43f: build.ps1 on C:\\home\\remote\\train25\\kit (the exact tree the node half verified: newest source write 05:48, before the 331/331 run) with the train pin (core F414863971EB2A2C), so the binary matches the verdicts. Earth's part becomes light: fetch kit.exe, compare its sha with the moon log, then the install swap (retire the old copy, move the new one in) and the smoke, the same steps release-train.ps1 does after its release phase. No box r4.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_267 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 267u32, "2026-11-10T23:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 19:4x rig: TRAIN43f VERDICT: UNSHIPPABLE, superseded by TRAIN44. The moon release (job-1794351784230) BUILT fine (cargo release 22 min 52 s on moon, so the release belongs on a node) but the candidate source-topology check refused: rust_file_max=1792, the pre-split rig_units/check.rs in the 43f snapshot. The box half would have hit the same check at its end even without the 10:55 timeout, the 09:24 pack and the 11:51 BSOD; the node half was green only because notebooks and the crate gate do not run that check. Lesson: run the source-topology check in the node half, before notebooks. The live tree carries the fix (rig_units in 4 linked units, max 924; rig_drafts 107), and both stale .rs files are rewritten by the next regen. NEXT: TRAIN44 from the live tree with -NodeOnly (new launch-train switch: the node half ends at the verdicts and no box half starts; the release then runs on moon and earth only installs), plus the applied release-train.ps1 draft (TRAIN-ON-NODE-D1 candidate skip, KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN-D1 resume on the pin and a timeout retry).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_268 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 268u32, "2026-11-10T23:51Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 19:5x rig: LOAD CAPS in release-train.ps1 (live, unstaged, parse 0), after org2 found moon starved at 19:37 (sshd sent no banner; earth is the same hardware and both BSODs came under sustained 100%): every train now sets CARGO_BUILD_JOBS to half the cores unless the caller set it, and drops its own process to BelowNormal priority on Windows (children inherit the class, so cargo, the regen compilers and the Cells notebooks all yield to sshd and interactive work); the train log prints the caps. TRAIN44 launching node-only now (snapshot of the live tree: the rig_units, rig_drafts and task_creation splits, today's models and verbs, the typefeatureset wording, the train-script changes).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_269 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 269u32, "2026-11-10T23:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:0x rig: TRAIN44 RUNNING node-only. Node half: remote job job-1794354233106-kit-TRAIN44 on moon (started 19:43, snapshot of the live tree, 418 generated files, load caps in effect). Box coordinator: job-1794355142404-kit-TRAIN44-node (detached; it resumed the node half at 19:59). Launch slip, recovered: the launch line carried -NodeStage (copied from a summary), which skipped the reference preflight and ran the coordinator inside the agent shell; the in-shell launcher was stopped and a detached coordinator resumed the same node job via -ResumeNodeJob (memory launch-train-from-powershell-not-bash updated). The preflight did not run, so an unresolved reference would show up as a regen failure on the node. Next step: on green, release on moon with the pin and caps, install on earth by sha, smoke, then KIT-NEXT-NAME R2.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_270 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 270u32, "2026-11-11T00:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:5x rig: TRAIN44 RED at the crate gate (node, 20:27; regen ok in 44 min, Published 25 changed owners, 362 unchanged): rig_standards_layers_model/scan.rs 1433 lines OVER 1000 (it grew today with the Prim-binding scanner; HEAD was 970). FIX: a new linked unit rig_standards_prim_bindings (the switch scanner, prim_binding union and its texts, plus the code-scan helpers code_of, own_macros and module_opened, all called across the link with one or tuple arguments; the model keeps one-line wrappers and its end-to-end test, the unit has its own tests). Measured on moon (job-1794357608300): layers_model 827, prim_bindings 828, layers 781, 0 over. The precheck then refused 5 over-width lines (agile_task_creation 115, rig_agile_routes 135 = a peer's uncommitted edit, reflowed only, rig_units/model 17, agile_task_creation_text 44, rig_ready_rank 120): reflowed. TRAIN44b LAUNCHED node-only (precheck ok, 251 touched files): coordinator job-1794357928714-kit-TRAIN44b-node, node half job-1794358085382-kit-TRAIN44b on moon (started 20:48). Held out of the snapshot and restored after node half started, hash-verified 15/15: the five unprobed pure models (rig_bench_model, rig_do_move_model, rig_boundary_census, rig_quiet_forecast, rig_store_key), so their first tests cannot turn this train red. Known non-blocker: the census flags agile_task_creation_text for a tab literal that is its string escaper (spi_escaped), not row encoding.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_271 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 271u32, "2026-11-11T01:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 21:5x rig: TRAIN44b passed every gate that stopped tonight's trains and is in its notebook phase on moon (start 21:45, positive control rig_lcov pass 21:46). Reaching notebooks means regen ok, the crate gate ok (the prim_bindings split fixed TRAIN44's 1433-line crate), the debug candidate built, and the node-half source-topology check passed (the 1792-line rig_units/check.rs that made TRAIN43f unshippable is gone). All under the load caps (CARGO_BUILD_JOBS half, BelowNormal; RustDesk kept Normal). Next step (the next session): when the coordinator job-1794357928714-kit-TRAIN44b-node exits green, build the release on moon with the train pin and caps, fetch kit.exe to earth and compare its sha, swap it in with retire, smoke it, then KIT-NEXT-NAME R2 (rig.exe) and R4.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_272 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 272u32, "2026-11-11T04:14Z", "rig", "11-11 00:10 TRAIN44b node half 346/347: regen, crate gate, candidate, topology all ok; the one red was command_spec_domain/direct_verbs.spi shared_lines_print_once, a stale help-line count after the units, drafts and scratch verbs joined the union (35 verbs, 32 lines). Test fixed in the live tree, the box snapshot and the moon mirror (only diff vs snapshot). Moon job job-1794370454538-rig-release-44b reruns that one notebook on the TRAIN44b compiler pin (TRAIN44b-r1), then builds the release in place; log C:/home/remote-stage/rig-release-moon-44b.log. Next: fetch kit.exe by hash, swap with retire, smoke, then R2.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_273 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 273u32, "2026-11-11T04:27Z", "rig", "11-11 00:26 rig: TRAIN44b INSTALLED on earth: kit.exe D80FDBD7 (27264000 B), built on moon by build.ps1 on the TRAIN44b pin in 7m17s, schema and topology checks passed; the rerun TRAIN44b-r1 passed 1/1 and cargo found the debug candidate 144A2B8B already fresh, so the change was test-only. Fetched by sha256, swapped into the repo and lane copies, old binaries kept in kit/retired as repo-kit and lane-kit-20261111002558029.exe. shipped-manifest (1974 rows) is from the TRAIN44b snapshot; last-installed and installed-train now name TRAIN44b. Smoke: job list, agile list, lint precheck, the help lines of units, drafts and scratch, and scratch cited all ok; output now prints rig. Every train:TRAIN44 wait (32) and older now reads answered. Next: KIT-NEXT-NAME R2 (rig.exe), then R4-R7, then the train for the models written after the snapshot.")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_274 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", 274u32, "2026-11-11T05:17Z", "rig", "11-11 01:1x rig: KIT PULLED FROM ORIGIN (user 11-11: pull without invasive git, back up, fix conflicts, leave unstaged for review). origin had 1 commit, 56fb201 'tests' (178 files, agile_state_fs and agile_state_spelling, elapsed_ms timing on agile verbs); 60 of its files overlapped local work. Steps: (1) backup at C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local/kit/archive/pull-kit-20261111-010528: 548 files with a sha256 manifest (all verified), the index as tree b7c60114, staged.patch, unstaged.patch, status, old-head e7de0e3. (2) only the 60 overlapping files back to HEAD. (3) git merge --ff-only origin/main. (4) git merge-file per file: ours = backup, base = e7de0e3, theirs = 56fb201. Results: 22 clean (every hand-written .spi, both manifests, README, test-regeneration.ps1); 1 hand-resolved (rig_agile_lint/lint_cli.spi: kept origin's elapsed_ms and agile_state_fs reader plus rig's retired-prefix report and rig usage word); 37 generated .rs kept origin's version (resolution.txt in the backup), regenerated by the next train from the merged .spi. Seven over-width lines in origin's code reflowed (agile_note_model, rig_agile_lint, rig_agile_mutation; the AgileInit and AgileDialect hBchost routes moved unchanged); precheck of all 9 merged .spi ok. Checks: 488 of 488 non-overlap backed-up files untouched; main = origin/main. The user staged 151 more files during the run, each identical to the work tree; the 3 staged overlap files (README.md, rig_window_run/run.rs, rust_std_env/package.spiproj) now hold the merged result UNSTAGED (their old staged copies are in index tree b7c60114). TRAIN45 runs on a pre-pull snapshot; the merged tree first regenerates in TRAIN46.")
inl pack_after_night () = Task ("PACK-AFTER-NIGHT", "Compiler pack after the 10-21 night pack: formatter skip-respace, GADT union-nesting guard (EJP0041), record-with expected base, Rust Export record returns, retype census (inert)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,pack,main", "current", "current")
