inl note_of_kit_ledger_one_file_2 () = Note ("KIT-LEDGER-ONE-FILE", 2u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 240m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D4 at 0%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_ledger_one_file_3 () = Note ("KIT-LEDGER-ONE-FILE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T11:35Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-LEDGER-ONE-FILE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_ledger_one_file_4 () = Note ("KIT-LEDGER-ONE-FILE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T20:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, MODEL BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_experiment_ledger/ledger.spi (pure, HostFree). Measured first: rig_experiments stores FIVE files per entry, not two (record_path ledger id registration | amendments | disclosures | verdict | addenda; experiments.spi:37-90). One-file shape, the backlog's state/agile.spi pattern: one append-only list of ledger_row = Registered (id, at, plan) | Amended | Disclosed | Concluded | Addendum, and appended rows row returns Appended rows or Refused reason, so the ledger ENFORCES the pre-registration order the five files only implied: one registration per id, nothing before registration, and after a verdict only addenda (no late amendment, no second verdict); entry_of rebuilds the five-part view the current show prints. Test: two entries interleaved in one file, the E-1 view, the three refusals, an open entry. Ratchet clean. NEXT STEP: render/parse rows as inl lines in one ledger.spi (the agile state codec), a one-shot import of existing five-file entries (rig_experiment_import is the precedent), then experiment register/amend/conclude write through appended.")
inl note_of_kit_ledger_one_file_5 () = Note ("KIT-LEDGER-ONE-FILE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_ledger_one_file_6 () = Note ("KIT-LEDGER-ONE-FILE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T23:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, ROW CODEC BUILT (unstaged): src/rig_experiment_ledger/rows.spi, the recorded next step's first part. ledger_text writes one inl line per row, named by position (inl ledger_row_<n> () = Registered (\"ID\", \"at\", \"plan\") / Amended / Disclosed / Concluded / Addendum (\"ID\", \"text\")), so an append-only file never collides on names and keeps its order; quotes inside a field become ' (the state files' rule, which keeps the split-on-quote reader exact); rows_of_text reads the lines back, ignoring anything else. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (rows 1/1): position names, four rows back in order, the inner quotes rule, the verdict surviving the round trip into entry_of, other lines ignored. kit standards 0, ratchet clean. NEXT: the one-shot import of existing five-file entries (rig_experiment_import is the precedent) and experiment register/amend/conclude writing through appended + ledger_text; both edit the experiment verbs, so TRAIN44.")
inl kit_memory_features () = Task ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", "Mine every memory for eoie functionality that uses the type feature set, then implement it (user 2026-10-21 22:3x: 'pick from each memory what could be turned into an eoie functionality that leverages the typefeatureset then implement it to give even more value to claude, not to stuff everything into unformatted strings, drift')", Story, P1, D7, 55u32, Planned, "", "kit,memory,gadt,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_memory_features () = Planning ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", Minutes 330u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_1 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 1u32, "2026-10-22T02:30Z", "eoie", "22:30 pivot (to plan with more intelligence later, per the user): classify each memory as (a) enforceable behavior eoie can own (a verb, a check, a refusal, a typed default), (b) guidance that stays prose, (c) obsolete. Implement (a) with GADTs/existentials/reflection, then shrink the memory to a pointer at the feature. Precedents already in the tree or queue: read-clock-before-timestamps -> note-local-time (eoie stamps notes itself), decide-by-prewritten-rules -> experiment preregistration, no-sleep-polling/monitor-every-long-run -> job verbs with timeout and watcher (EOIE-JOBS). Candidates: stop-only-own-processes -> ps kill refuses PIDs outside its own job tree (OwnedPid|ForeignPid), copy-eoie-src-only -> a typed copy guard, pin-spiral-cc -> a toolchain profile type, 1000-line gate -> a standards check, eoie-generic-no-external -> a literal census check. Reflection can then list which memories are embodied by which verb and flag those still prose. Not a byte-identical string store.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_2 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 2u32, "2026-10-22T02:44Z", "eoie", "22:44 user 22:4x: 'return back the memories that can't be absorbed into eoie but are still useful to keep, don't lose useful stuff'. Checked: nothing was lost; the 17:11 import copied, all 75 imported memories are still in ~/.claude/projects/C--home-git/memory (none shrank, 10 grew, 7 new since). Rule for the pivot: a memory leaves the client folder only after its eoie feature exists and is installed; class (b) guidance stays in the client memory as is.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_3 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 3u32, "2026-10-22T03:13Z", "eoie", "23:13 classification of all 83 memories (draft in scratch memory-features/classification.md; moves to lab/EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES after release A): six feature families. F1 job supervision (retry-after-memory-kills, no-sleep-polling, monitor-every-long-run, stop-only-own-processes, sweep-leftover-shells, offscreen-muted-gui-runs...): job_outcome Exited|Reaped|TimedOut|Silent, retry_policy, pid_owner OwnedPid|ForeignPid, run_mode Visible|OffscreenMuted. F2 tree safety (cells-reads-live-tree, copy-eoie-src-only, dangling-check-by-stem): TreeRead lease refusing do edit, copy_scope, delete_clearance Cleared|Blocked refs. F3 standards rules indexed by language with an existential rule pack (lib-first, generic, 1k lines all languages, PowerShell glue, actions.lock). F4 toolchain profiles (pin-spiral-cc, kino-mix-erlang-path). F5 decision records (prewritten rules as typed items, release pipeline with a mandatory candidate phase). F6 mirrored repos (alphabet-mirrors-dice). 8 already embodied (read-clock -> note-local-time, ...), 43 stay as guidance, 2 to re-check (one-entry-no-native-wrappers, agent-sync-daily). Order by WSJF: F2 > F1 > F3 > F5 > F4 > F6.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_4 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 4u32, "2026-10-22T03:47Z", "eoie", "23:47 F2 tree lease designed in detail (scratch memory-features/f2-tree-lease.md): tree_use ReadsTree|ShapesTree, a TreeRead window class as the lease store (reuses holder-alive cleanup), tree_claim TreeFree|TreeHeld lease, edit_verdict EditAllowed|EditRefused lease. Releases (test-regeneration -Publish) and job start --reads-tree take the lease; do edit/write/replace/move refuse under it naming the holder; the edit hook checks the same registry; eoie tree copy with copy_scope SourceOnly|WithSpec; do delete takes only a Cleared value from eoie refs <stem>. Would have stopped tonight's mid-release lab edit and the earlier lab probe that cost a release.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_5 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 5u32, "2026-10-22T03:54Z", "eoie", "23:54 F2 started: the tree-lease model is written and green in the scratchpad (f2-lease/eoie_tree_lease/lease.spi, 3 Spiral test blocks pass via Cells): tree_use, tree_lease record, tree_leases list, tree_claim TreeFree|TreeHeld, edit_verdict EditAllowed|EditRefused, claim_of/edit_verdict_of/verdict_text. Lib-first, zero host macros (sm'.to_lower/replace/starts_with/ends_with/format, ++# from sm'_operators). Lessons: Cells finds lib/spiral by searching the notebook's ancestors (deps/polyglot/..., spiral/lib/spiral), so a package outside C:\\home\\git needs packageDir; string concat is ++# with open sm'_operators; a record update needs a bound base. Moves into eoie (lab then src) after release A; then the window-class store and the do-edit refusal.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_6 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 6u32, "2026-10-22T03:59Z", "eoie", "23:59 F2 model upgraded to the typefeatureset and green (3 tests): tree_lease is a GADT indexed by reads|shapes (ReadLease :: terms -> tree_lease reads, ShapeLease -> tree_lease shapes), a forall converter makes runtime rows (StoredRead|StoredShape), so only typed read handles can produce a blocking row. Census: gadt-case 2, forall 1, indexed-union 2, host-macro 0, string-concat 0. An existential registry was tried and dropped: existentials can't cross into runtime lists (Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var); runtime data stays plain unions.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_7 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 7u32, "2026-10-22T04:00Z", "eoie", "00:00 F2 integration point found: eoie_do_edit/host.spi:32 commits every pending write in one Rust block (temporaries + rename), fed by decode.spi's record_list (Rc<Vec<Vec<Rc<str>>>> split on bytes 30/31: legacy encoded rows). Slice after release C: (1) land eoie_tree_lease (lab -> src, spiral- package), (2) a TreeRead window class in eoie_machine_windows as the lease store (holder-alive cleanup reused), (3) before the commit, claim_of over the stored leases for each pending path; EditRefused stops the whole batch with verdict_text, (4) test-regeneration -Publish takes a TreeRead lease on the repo root for its run. The commit blob itself is migration debt for EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION (encoded rows + a let-block).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_8 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 8u32, "2026-10-22T04:02Z", "eoie", "00:02 F2 store decision: reuse the window registry (a TreeRead class with the existing holder-alive cleanup and run-holder union from r35) instead of a new lease store; the lib's file_system.read_dir_names returns a Rust-only am'.vec of std_string, so a fresh store would mean lib-internal iteration for no gain.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_9 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 9u32, "2026-10-22T04:09Z", "eoie", "00:09 F2 interim protection installed (decided autonomously): a PreToolUse hook on Edit|Write|MultiEdit (~/.claude/hooks/eoie-tree-lease.ps1, settings backup in scratch) blocks an edit under any root named by a live lease file in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\tree-leases (root=, pid=, holder=, since=); a lease whose pid is dead is stale and removed. Release BC's job writes such a lease with its own pid for its whole run (regeneration hashes and notebook tests both read the tree). Tested: inside root blocked (exit 2, case/separators normalized), sibling prefix allowed, dead lease ignored and deleted, no leases allowed. Not covered: writes from shell commands (PowerShell WriteAllText) — the typed path (TreeRead window class + eoie_tree_lease crate + do-edit refusal + test-regeneration taking the lease generically) replaces this interim.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_10 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 10u32, "2026-10-22T04:59Z", "eoie", "00:59 lease hook extended to shell commands (the path of tonight's release-A-killing write): the PreToolUse matcher is now Edit|Write|MultiEdit|PowerShell|Bash; a command that names a leased root and contains a write verb (Set-Content, WriteAllText, Copy-Item, Remove-Item, robocopy, redirect...) is blocked while the lease is live. Tested 8 cases: Edit inside, WriteAllText into root and redirect into root blocked; read-only Get-Content, eoie verbs run from the root, writes elsewhere, -gt comparisons and lease-free sessions pass. Known gap: eoie's own write verbs (do edit) inside the root pass until the typed TreeRead path (release D) refuses them.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_11 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 11u32, "2026-10-22T05:02Z", "eoie", "01:02 lease hook made cheap and proven live: settings now run it as cmd /c if exist %LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\tree-leases\\*.lease pwsh ..., so sessions pay pwsh startup only while a lease exists. Release ABC started 00:53 and holds two live leases (its job, pid 6572, and the regeneration -Publish, pid 71396), so both lease writers work. Against those real leases the hook blocks a PowerShell write into C:\\home\\git\\eoie (exit 2) and passes a read (exit 0).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_12 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 12u32, "2026-10-22T05:09Z", "eoie", "01:09 F1 job supervision designed in detail (scratch memory-features/f1-job-supervision.md, to lab after ABC): job_outcome Exited|Reaped|TimedOut|Stopped|Lost from the existing exit lines; liveness Progressing|Silent minutes with job start --silent-limit (busy-but-silent is a hang); retry_policy NoRetry|RetryWhen with job start --retry-reaped n exporting EOIE_RETRY_ATTEMPT; pid_owner OwnedBy|OtherJob|NoJob so ps kill refuses other authors' and job-less processes unless --theirs names the job; job sweep --mine; run_mode Visible|OffscreenMuted. Order: pid_owner > liveness > retry > sweep > run_mode.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_13 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 13u32, "2026-10-22T05:21Z", "eoie", "01:21 F5 decision records designed (scratch memory-features/f5-decision-records.md): decision_rule record (condition, check, tie-break, deadline) added with agile rule add before measuring and kept immutable; check_kind Measured|ThresholdAt|BeforeTime|AllOf; rule_outcome Applied|Waived|Expired via agile decide; agile rules lists open ones and the Stop gate blocks on rules past deadline without an outcome; a typed release_step sequence where Publish needs an Applied Candidate. Case study: tonight's R1-R11 lived as free-text notes and two were applied late (R2 broken by a shell write, R8 after a re-baseline).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_14 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 14u32, "2026-10-22T05:21Z", "eoie", "01:21 F4 and F6 sketched (scratch memory-features/f4-f6.md): F4 profiles as user-owned Spiral data (tool pins, env, PATH prefix), eoie env <profile> -- <cmd>, eoie env check with pin_drift Matches|Shadowed|Missing, job start --profile; F6 mirror pairs as data, eoie mirror check with mirror_state InStep|LeftAhead|RightAhead|Diverged. All six families now have designs; F2 is built (release D), the rest wait for build slots.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_15 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 15u32, "2026-10-22T05:23Z", "eoie", "01:23 F1 first piece built and green (scratch f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner/owner.spi, 2 test blocks via Cells, passed first run): process_row/job_record records, pid_owner OwnedBy|OtherJob|NoJob by walking parents up to a job supervisor (64-hop guard), kill_verdict KillAllowed|KillRefused with --theirs <job> as the only override and refusal texts naming the owner. Lib-first (++#), no host macros. Next F1 piece: liveness Progressing|Silent.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_16 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 16u32, "2026-10-22T05:25Z", "eoie", "01:25 F1 second piece green (scratch f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner/liveness.spi, 2 tests): output_watch from byte-count samples, liveness Progressing|Silent minutes, silence_verdict KeepRunning|StopSilent at a --silent-limit (0 = report only). Design corrected: no new job_outcome union, eoie_jobs already has job_settled (JobFinished|JobTimedOut|JobStopped|JobSpawnFailed|JobSkipped|JobLost|JobMemoryCapped); retry_policy NoRetry|RetryWhen n decides over it (JobLost from a reaped supervisor and JobMemoryCapped retry). Retry and wiring go into eoie_jobs itself, not a parallel type.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_17 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 17u32, "2026-10-22T05:27Z", "eoie", "01:27 F4 core built and green (scratch f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner/pins.spi, 1 test block, 5 cases): tool_pin record, found_paths in PATH order, pin_drift Matches|Shadowed first|Missing decided by the first copy on PATH (case and separators normalized), drift_text naming the shadowing copy (the mingw 16.2 vs scoop gcc 15.2 case from pin-spiral-cc).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_18 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 18u32, "2026-10-22T05:29Z", "eoie", "01:29 F6 core built and green (scratch f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner/mirror.spi, 5 cases): mirrored_file records with both hashes, mirror_state InStep|LeftAhead files|RightAhead files|Diverged, refuses_commit for anything but InStep (alphabet-mirrors-dice). Tonight's scratch models, all lib-first, no host macros, Spiral tests green: F2 lease (built into release D), F1 owner + liveness, F4 pins, F6 mirror; they move to lab/EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES with the D handoff and into real packages per family next.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_19 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 19u32, "2026-10-22T05:32Z", "eoie", "01:32 F5 core built and green (scratch f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner/decision.spi, 2 tests): rule_check AtMost|AtLeast|BeforeTime, decision_rule record with written and deadline times, rule_outcome Applied|Declined|Expired|Premature (a measurement older than the rule is refused; a decision after the deadline expires), outcome_text. Every family now has a green core model in the scratchpad (F1 owner + liveness, F2 lease, F4 pins, F5 decision, F6 mirror); F3 ships as standards rules in D.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_20 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 20u32, "2026-10-22T05:34Z", "eoie", "01:34 release E plan (next session; F1 pid ownership into ps kill): (1) job start records an author file from EOIE_AUTHOR or --as (job records carry no author today, so 'my jobs' cannot be decided); (2) eoie_process_table's stop path (stops_from -> stop_refusal_of Allowed pid) adds an ownership step: process rows from the existing listing host + job records (id, author, supervisor pid from the jobs registry) -> owner_of -> kill_verdict_of, refusing OtherJob and NoJob unless --theirs <job> names it; (3) eoie_pid_owner lands in src (lib-first package, standards.spi declaring HostFree + LibReferenced). Liveness wiring (job status/list print progressing|silent N min; job start --silent-limit) follows in the same release.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_21 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 21u32, "2026-10-22T08:14Z", "eoie", "04:14 F1 integration design, sized before drafting: eoie_process_table/process_table.rs is at 828 lines, so the owner walk (process rows + job records + parent walk, about 100-150 Rust lines) cannot be inlined into ps kill. Shape: the green scratch models (f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner: owner, liveness, pins, decision, mirror) become their own exporting crate eoie_pid_owner with one primitive boundary in the domain's words: eoie_pid_owner_of(pid, author) -> owner word (mine / other:<job id> / none). ps kill: stop_refusal gains OtherJob : string (refusal text names the owning job and its author), checked after OwnProcess/OwnAncestor; a --force flag is NOT added (killing another lane's job goes through that lane). Job records: job start writes an author file from env.try_get_environment_variable EOIE_AUTHOR (main landed it 04:0x; None leaves the file absent and the job counts as unowned, so old jobs stay killable by anyone, as today). Tests: ps_cli kill of a fixture job with another author is refused, own author allowed, unowned allowed. Needs: crate scaffold + owner growth row + compile preview; release F after D and E. Draft models carried in lab/EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN/night-2026-10-22/f1-owner.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_22 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 22u32, "2026-10-22T09:16Z", "eoie", "05:16 integration designs for the green F4/F5/F6 models (scratch f1-owner/eoie_pid_owner, carried in the night folder). F5 decision rules: tonight's R11-R14 were prewritten as free-text notes and applied by hand plus crons; as eoie: agile rule <root> <id> <rule-id> <check> [--by HH:MM] stores a typed decision_rule (check AtMost/AtLeast/BeforeTime, written_ms, deadline_ms) as its own state record (a backlog state schema addition, so it needs the state migration path, not note text), and agile decide <root> <id> <rule-id> <measured> evaluates it with the model's outcome_of: refuses a measurement older than the rule, expires after the deadline, and appends the outcome as a note. F4 pins (memory pin-spiral-cc: SPIRAL_CC must be scoop gcc 15.2 while mingw 16.2 is first on PATH): a pin check reading the first PATH hit per tool against a declared pin, reported by eoie machine watch and refused by the release prelaunch check (eoie release check, EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN note 45). F6 mirror (memory alphabet-mirrors-dice): mirror check <left-root> <right-root> <glob> hashes both sides and reports one-sided changes; the model's refuses_commit makes it a pre-commit refusal. Placement: each as a small exporting crate with a word boundary (owner, pin drift, mirror state), never inlined into near-gate crates (process_table 828, machine_watch 954).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_23 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 23u32, "2026-10-22T09:32Z", "eoie", "05:32 decision rule, written before checking (memory decide-autonomously: no user-decision lists; one-record-per-fact): an untracked file that copies another store's facts as strings is deleted when (1) the user called that shape drift, (2) the source of truth still holds every fact, and (3) a stem grep across eoie (src, scripts, compiler-contracts, spec, standards, lab) and the backlog finds no consumer. Subject: eoie/memory/claude.spi (213 KB, untracked, every Claude memory as a Memory GADT row of 8 strings, written 10-21 17:11 by the memory string-store slice r36, which was held as drift). If any check fails, keep it and record why.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_24 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 24u32, "2026-10-22T09:33Z", "eoie", "05:33 rule applied: all three conditions held, so eoie/memory/claude.spi was deleted (the untracked memory/ folder held only it). (1) the string-store shape was called drift by the user on 10-21; (2) ~/.claude/projects/C--home-git/memory still holds every fact; (3) no consumer: the only code that would read it is the default_store from lab/EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS/apply-memory-default-store.ps1, which never reached src (the r36 string-store slice was held), and the memory verbs take an explicit <data.spi> path. The typed direction stays EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES (F1-F6 models + verbs), not an imported copy.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_25 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 25u32, "2026-10-22T13:36Z", "eoie-lane", "09:36 eoie team, F1 wiring decided (stop-only-own-processes as one call, opt-in so no lane's plain kill changes): job start records the caller's EOIE_AUTHOR (any word; eoie names no lane) in jobs/<id>/author. 'eoie kill --mine <pid>...' allows a pid when it descends from the caller's agent session (the ps --mine scope that already exists) or when owner.spi's job_above finds a job whose author equals the caller's EOIE_AUTHOR. Otherwise it refuses with owner.spi's texts, unless --theirs <job-id> names the owning job. Plain kill is unchanged. With F's job host, supervisors hang under the host and not under the agent session, which is why the author field is needed (the session walk alone would refuse an agent's own detached job trees). Placement: the verdict lives in eoie_pid_owner as an export (process_table.rs is at 828; the owner fold plus job records would push it toward the gate), and process_table calls it once per pid. It lands after E2, with the harness adoption.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_26 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 26u32, "2026-10-22T13:56Z", "eoie-lane", "09:56 eoie team: F1 kill --mine, first half drafted as an anchor-safe slice in release H (apply-f1-ownership.ps1: new module eoie_process_table/ownership.spi; job_owner YourJob | TheirJob | NoOwningJob, mine_verdict, a 6-case test block registered; spiproj gains the module and spiral- when E's heal has not added it). It reuses machine watch's existing owner_walk (supervisor command line 'job supervise <id>') for the job lookup, so the lab owner.spi's parallel ancestry model stays as reference only. The second half (run.spi flags --mine/--theirs, rows sampled once, EOIE_AUTHOR written by job start) anchors on post-heal text and is written once GE2 is installed.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_27 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 27u32, "2026-10-22T15:57Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 11:50: F2 tree-lease hook gap. A session started before the hook was installed (10-22 01:01) never loads it, so two edits landed under release F's lease. The hook itself blocks correctly (2-3 s, through its cmd wrapper). Typed follow-up: the tree-read window claim (release D) should also be checked by eoie's own write verbs, so the guard does not depend on a session's hook snapshot.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_28 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 28u32, "2026-10-22T17:14Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 13:14 F6 integration drafted (scratch, synced to lab with the night folder): eoie mirror check <left-root> <right-root> <path>... as its own lib-only crate eoie_mirror (HostFree). The model is retyped from the 01:29 core: file_side Missing | Present (content, last_write_ms) replaces the empty-hash convention, which made an empty file look missing, plus file_drift SameOnBoth | LeftOnly | RightOnly | LeftNewer | RightNewer and mirror_state over a core list. Content equality replaces hashing (the lib crypto path's sha2 version is unproven in eoie). Directories are walked with an explicit worklist in sorted order. Exits 0 in step and 1 otherwise; model and CLI notebooks are registered. Dry run on the post-I tree is clean. Waits on lib file_system.last_write_ms (offered to main as apply-lib-last-write.ps1) and console.write_error_line (main's second landing).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_29 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 29u32, "2026-10-22T17:20Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 13:20 F4 integration drafted: eoie env check <tool>=<pinned-path>... as a lib-only crate eoie_env_pins (HostFree). PATH comes from env.get_environment_variable split by platform.is_windows, and each tool is looked up as tool + platform.get_executable_suffix. pin_drift is Matches | Shadowed first | Elsewhere first | Missing; Elsewhere is new and separates 'only other copies' from 'none'. Exits 1 on drift. Model and CLI notebooks set the child's PATH over fixture tool stubs. Dry run clean in either order with F6's mirror slice. Waits only on lib console.write_error_line.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_30 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 30u32, "2026-10-22T18:28Z", "x", "2026-10-22 14:28 x: candidate feature from memory ci-parity-toolchains (written today). Verb: 'eoie ci parity <repo>' reads the workflow's setup-* pins (setup-zig version, setup-beam otp/elixir/gleam, setup-rust channel or rust-toolchain.toml, setup-python). It compares them with what the local test harness resolves: the harness's own env override (SPIRAL_ZIG, SPIRAL_RUSTC, ...), else PATH through scoop shims (read the .shim target), and rustup's toolchain for the directory the harness runs in. It prints one row per tool (ci, local, match) and exits 1 on a mismatch, with the env line that would make a run match CI. Typed: a tool union (Zig | Rust | Otp | Elixir | Gleam | Python), each with its pin reader and local resolver. Evidence: today all local Cells runs used zig-dev 0.18 and rustc 1.88-nightly, while x CI pins 0.17.0 and nightly-2026-10-18 (X-PRECOMMIT-SPEED notes 32-33). Generic, with no repo names in the code: any repo whose workflow uses those actions.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_31 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 31u32, "2026-10-22T20:51Z", "eoie-lane", "16:51 F5 pure model drafted and tested (scratch f5/src/agile_decision_model; model only, like eoie_tree_lease, with standards.spi declaring HostFree and LibReferenced). rule_check AtLeast | AtMost | Before | Recorded is checked against measurement Number | Clock | Text: a kind mismatch is Unmeasurable, never a silent pass. The GADT typestate decision undecided -> decided (OpenRule/ClosedRule; decide and waive take only an undecided rule) stops a rule being decided twice, and stored_decision is the runtime row. rule_outcome is Applied (verdict, measurement) | Waived reason | Expired (decided after its deadline). overdue_rules is the fold the Stop gate needs. Its 3 test blocks use today's real rules: the sentinel-probe rule (10 against at least 14 fails; 14 holds) and 'no release launch after 19:00' (a late decision expires; a waived rule is not overdue). Cells notebook check: 3/3 pass on the first compile and again after re-laying lines over 120; eoie standards: 0 findings; census ratchet: no new-package problem. Next, a compile-release item: agile rule add/decide/rules over these rows, plus the Stop-gate reading.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_32 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 32u32, "2026-10-22T21:06Z", "eoie-lane", "17:06 F5 CLI placement, read from the code: an agile verb is a union case plus its spec record in agile_subcommand_domain/subcommand.spi (reflection-driven names and usage) and two arms in eoie_agile_mutation/agile_mutation.spi (the mutates table and the dispatch to a crate export). agile_mutation.rs is at 981 lines, so three verbs (rule add, decide, rules) do not fit as three cases. Plan: one family case AgileRule ('rule', shape 'add <root> <item> <id> --when <text> --check at-least|at-most|before|recorded <value> [--by HH:MM] | decide <root> <item> <id> --measured <value> | waive ... | list <root> [--overdue]'), which costs about 2 dispatch lines, routed to one export of a new crate agile_decision_rules. That crate opens agile_decision_model and parses its own sub-verbs, so agile_mutation never grows per sub-verb. Storage: typed rows in <root>/state/rules.spi (a Spiral data module like standards/census.spi: one 'inl rule_<id> () = DecisionRule (...)' per rule, outcome rows appended, never edited), so the Stop gate reads overdue rules with one 'eoie agile rule list <root> --overdue' call. Ordering: after GE2 and H (both touch agile crates), as its own release with candidate notebooks for the rule CLI.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_33 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 33u32, "2026-10-23T00:37Z", "x", "2026-10-22 20:37 x: correction to note 30, plus a measured expected table for the 'ci parity' verb. The Rust half of note 30 is WRONG and would bake today's 15:18 failure into the tool. A plain 'rustc --version' shows rustup's default toolchain, but a harness may pass its own +toolchain to the rustup proxy (Cells does: rustc_args adds +nightly-2026-10-18 when rustc's path contains /.cargo/bin/ or /rustup/). So the local resolver must model the harness's argument building, not the tool's --version. Never suggest an env override that swaps the proxy for a direct rustc: the harness then passes '+nightly...' as a file name ('multiple input filenames provided'). Expected rows for the x repo on this box, 10-22 20:1x (ci / local / verdict): zig 0.17.0 / 0.18-dev from the PATH shim / MISMATCH, fixed by SPIRAL_ZIG=<scoop zig 0.17.0>; rust nightly-2026-10-18 (setup-rust x2 + rust-toolchain.toml) / the same through the proxy's +arg / match; otp 29 / 29.1.2 / match; elixir 1.20 / 1.20.4 / match; gleam 1.19.2 / 1.19.2 / match; python 3.12.10 / 3.15.0 on PATH, 3.12.10 under scoop python312 / MISMATCH, which matters only where python runs (x: the e2e stub; proof = run it on 3.12.10). Version matching is prefix-wise: a CI '29' matches a local '29.1.2'.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_34 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 34u32, "2026-10-23T15:58Z", "eoie", "11:58 eoie: re note 33 (x): the eoie ci parity draft now follows it: Rust is resolved the way a harness sees it (rust-toolchain file channel if installed, else rustup default; never 'swap the proxy' advice), Python is a tool, matching is prefix-wise at a dot (no dev build stands in), and mismatches print a fix line (SPIRAL_ZIG=<scoop zig 0.17.0> for x's zig row). Details on EOIE-CI-PARITY; ships in release M.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_35 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 35u32, "2026-10-23T18:11Z", "eoie", "14:11 eoie: today's memory lessons mined for features. (1) search-backlog-before-new (5 slips on 10-23: a mirror verb already in release I, a backfill rule already settled, do raw payloads already in the usage, plus 2 earlier) -> EOIE-AGILE-FIND (drafted) should also search the verb usage text and the scratch slice scripts, not only titles and notes: 'agile find <root> <words> --usage --slices <dir>', so one call answers 'is this already built, drafted or decided?'. (2) check-scripts-by-data-flow, extended today with 'a positive control must fail for the reason under test, through the bug's own path' -> the experiment ledger (EOIE-EXPERIMENTS) gains a typed control arm: a rule is not registrable until a control run on the old binary or fixture has failed with the expected verdict. (3) job run vs job start (agent-sync trick) -> eoie job doctor --env (drafted, release M) runs the detached path so nobody needs to remember the trick.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_36 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 36u32, "2026-10-23T21:36Z", "eoie", "17:36 eoie: mined today's new memory recompile-drafts-after-compiler-change into a typed feature: a release preview records the compiler hash it compiled with, and release launch refuses when the installed compiler differs (union preview_state = PreviewCurrent of hash | PreviewStale of old * new | NoPreview; the launch decision is total over it). Specified on EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN note 124, from today's case: a codegen regression made H's stamp_in a Rust E0507 hours after its last preview. Memory to eoie link: recompile-drafts-after-compiler-change -> EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (EOIE-MEMORY-LINKS).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_37 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 37u32, "2026-10-24T00:02Z", "eoie", "20:02 eoie: mined memory window-coordination ('read queue + announced blocks before heavy work') into EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE: announced exclusive blocks become typed rows in the window store (class, from, until, latest start), read by admission, release yield and wait-clear, instead of living only in peer messages. Evidence: tonight's 18:02 manual yield to tibia's block.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_38 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 38u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main: consolidated pendencies covered here (EOIE-CONSOLIDATED-INTAKE, class a): JOB-4 (F1 retry-reaped with lower parallelism), TOOL-1 (F4 env profiles), EVID-7 (F6 mirror check). Spec text: Downloads/eoie-consolidated/agile_eoie.md.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_39 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 39u32, "2026-10-24T23:43Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 720m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D7 at 40%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_40 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 40u32, "2026-10-25T00:44Z", "eoie", "20:44 Lab drain: lab/EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES/classification.md moved into this note verbatim (the file is deleted; this note is the record):\n# EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES: classification of the 83 memories (2026-10-21 23:2x)\n\n(a) = eoie can enforce or do it, built on the type system; (b) = guidance that stays in the client memory; (c) = candidate obsolete, re-check before touching.\n\n## (a) Feature families\n\n### F1 Job supervision (eoie job / ps)\nMemories: retry-after-memory-kills, no-sleep-polling, parallel-while-waiting, monitor-every-long-run, sweep-leftover-shells, stop-only-own-processes, offscreen-muted-gui-runs, cmd-cwd-search-off, heavy-gate-lessons.\nTyped sketch:\n- `union job_outcome = Exited : i32 | Reaped | TimedOut | Silent : u32` (Silent = no output for N minutes: busy-but-silent is a hang).\n- `union retry_policy = NoRetry | RetryReaped : u8 * parallelism_step` drives `job start --retry-reaped`.\n- `union pid_owner = OwnedPid : job_id | ForeignPid` so `ps kill` refuses foreign PIDs by type.\n- `union run_mode = Visible | OffscreenMuted` for GUI clients (separate desktop, audio off).\n- `job sweep --mine` lists and stops leftovers owned by the caller's session.\n- Already embodied: windows, heavy gate, env_remove of NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath.\n\n### F2 Tree safety (do edit / copy / delete)\nMemories: cells-reads-live-tree, copy-eoie-src-only, dangling-check-by-stem, user-stages-mid-run, live-runs-alone.\nTyped sketch:\n- a `TreeRead` lease class held by test runs and releases; `do edit` returns `EditRefused (TreeLeased holder)` while it is held.\n- `copy_scope = SourceOnly | WithSpec` (never .cache/target) for scratch copies.\n- `delete_clearance = Cleared | Blocked : refs` from a cross-repo stem search; `do delete` takes only a Cleared value.\n- staged files reported as `StagedByUser` in `do git` output, never touched.\n\n### F3 Standards rules (eoie standards / edit hook)\nMemories: no-comments-self-explanatory, lib-first-all-projects, eoie-generic-no-external, eoie-granular-spiral, line-gate-all-languages, spiral-macro-gotchas (PowerShell glued statements, here-string traps), actions-lock-on-workflow-edits, code-era-quality, no-readme-for-comments.\nTyped sketch: `rule lang` indexed by language (Spiral, Rust, Gleam, PowerShell, Workflow) with an existential `rule_pack = exists lang. rule lang * lang_files lang`; findings carry the lib function to use. Feeds EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET and EOIE-HEAL-EDIT-HOOK.\n\n### F4 Toolchain profiles (eoie env)\nMemories: pin-spiral-cc, kino-mix-erlang-path, latest-of-everything (version check part).\nTyped sketch: `profile` record (compiler paths, PATH prefix, env overrides) named per task (matrix, kino); `eoie env <profile> -- <cmd>`; a profile check reports drift (mingw 16.2 first on PATH, choco OTP 26 first).\n\n### F5 Decision records (eoie agile)\nMemories: decide-by-prewritten-rules, decide-autonomously, release-candidate-cli-run, autonomous-stop-gate, backlog-always-has-cpu-light.\nTyped sketch: `decision_rule = { condition; check; tie_break; deadline }` stored on an item before measuring; `agile decide <id>` records the measured outcome against the rule; a release pipeline type with a mandatory candidate phase.\n\n### F6 Mirrored repos\nMemory: alphabet-mirrors-dice. Typed sketch: declared mirror pairs (data, generic) + `eoie mirror check <a> <b>` diffing plumbing files; refuses to report clean when one side changed alone.\n\n## Already embodied (memory can shrink to a pointer after the next install)\nread-clock-before-timestamps (note-local-time, r34), eoie-memory-symbiosis (agile links), scheduling-discipline (agile next roles), generic-tools-not-per-experiment (table/experiment verbs), eoie-one-call-tdd (spec/one-call.md + runner), agile-team-term (agile vocabulary), lab-in-repo (EOIE-LAB-AUDIT planned), one-record-per-fact (experiment import, partly).\n\n## (b) Guidance that stays in the client memory\nno-polls-during-runs, autonomous-e2e-fixing, experiment-until-sota, decisions-are-not-go, inner-jev-autonomy, decision-rounds-one-at-a-time, max-three-agents, classic-agents-visible, main-thread-works, use-full-timebox, trace-drift-before-pivoting, tokens-abundant-cpu-scarce, backlog-review-depth, pack-queued-builds, standardize-with-siblings, no-public-project-interaction, slide-with-spiral-main, fc1943s-dump-i574n-destructive, workspace-folder-stays, bold-native-goals, spiral-direction-2026-10, backend-targets-2026-10-07, core-migration-direction, priority-order, gpt5parallel-hopacsota, self-checking-samples-direction, regression-samples-allowed, accept-autonomously, lib-smoke-before-syntax, kino-copy-lib-resolution, formatter-keep-breaks, phantom-data-in-fsharp, x-compat-naming, x-api-credentials (secrets pointer: never into eoie), tibia-dogfood-project, tibia-other-session, lane-roles, agent-sync-daily, no-wsl-until-workflow-passes, backlog-in-eoie, eoie-first, eoie-embodied-memory, user-stages-mid-run (rule part).\n\n## (c) Candidates to re-check\none-entry-no-native-wrappers (F#/Fable entry may be moot under bold-native-goals' no-Fable direction), agent-sync-daily (agent-sync.md still read?).\n\n## Order (WSJF: weight = how often the rule is broken or costs a run, size = typed surface)\nF2 tree lease (broke releases twice) > F1 outcome/ownership (rustc kill hit main, reaped jobs) > F3 rules (feeds the hook) > F5 decision records > F4 profiles > F6 mirrors.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_41 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 41u32, "2026-10-30T14:22Z", "kit", "10-30 10:3x kit groom (R3, silent 5.6 d): the source survives the wipe. Note #40 holds the full classification (F1-F6, WSJF order) verbatim, so nothing needs rewriting. EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS's five unlanded patches (next-release\\memory-verbs) are LOST: heal's copies are noise (checked 10:2x). NEXT (owner kit): F2 tree lease first, as #40's order says. Step 1 is CPU-light: a milestone sizing note on F2 (TreeRead lease class, EditRefused (TreeLeased holder), copy_scope, delete_clearance) that names which pieces already ship (kit_delete_guard in TRAIN5, copy-eoie-src-only), replacing the provisional 720m estimate. Then the memory-verbs patches are rewritten from EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS's notes, re-proved on the current tree.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_42 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 42u32, "2026-10-30T15:45Z", "kit", "10-30 11:5x kit: F2 (tree safety, first in #40's order) sized by milestone against what ships, the step #41 named.\nSHIPPED (in the installed kit):\n- F2a tree lease: window class tree-read (readers share a path, writer preference, a dead holder refuses nothing), kit_tree_lease's EditRefused (TreeLeased terms), and 'kit window claim <path>' refusing writes under a held tree-read root. Tests: windows_cli a_tree_read_window_refuses_edits_under_its_root_and_never_blocks_compiles, kit_tree_lease lease.spi verdict tests.\n- F2b partly: kit_delete_guard refuses relative paths and protected roots (TRAIN5).\nREMAINING, each a milestone with its own size (estimates-from-rules base: D2=90m, D3=180m):\n- F2c delete clearance (D3, 180m): 'do delete' takes only a Cleared value from a cross-repo stem search (dangling-check-by-stem as a type: Cleared | Blocked refs).\n- F2d copy scope (D1, 30m): 'do copy' already takes exclusions (copies_run's excluded list); what's missing is a SourceOnly default that drops .cache and target (copy-eoie-src-only).\n- F2e staged files in 'do git' output as StagedByUser, never touched (D2, 90m; user-stages-mid-run, never-commit-leave-unstaged).\nF2 remaining = 300m. F1, F3-F6 keep the provisional split until each is sized the same way when its turn comes. Next: F2d (smallest), then F2e, then F2c.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_43 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 43u32, "2026-10-30T15:46Z", "kit", "10-30 11:5x kit: F2d resized after a probe, which corrects n42. Installed kit, scratch tree src/{.cache/deep/big.bin, target/debug/out.rlib, pkg/a.spi, b.spi}, 'kit do . \"copy src/** to out\"': 3 files copied, INCLUDING out/.cache/deep/big.bin, while target/ was skipped. The walker (kit_do_read host.spi:34, 'let skip = [\".git\", \"target\", \"node_modules\", \"_build\", \"deps\"]') skips nested build folders but not .cache. The glob base itself is never skipped, so 'files .cache/**' stays possible. That makes the fix a one-token addition. But the list sits inside a legacy host blob (the whole walk is one $'{ ... }' macro), and AGENTS says touching it means migrating it. So F2d is really: migrate kit_do_read's walk to Spiral over lib (read_dir, glob match, exclusions), with a typed skipped-folder list that adds .cache. D3, 180m, not 30m. F2 remaining: 180 + 180 + 90 = 450m. Order now: F2e (90m), then F2d (migration), then F2c.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_44 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 44u32, "2026-10-30T16:55Z", "kit", "10-30 12:5x kit: F2e LANDED UNSTAGED (n43's order put it first). 'kit do \"git status <repo> group by state\"' now lists the index's staged paths in their own 'staged' row, between modified and untracked, so an agent session can see what the user has staged (and so leave it alone, per never-commit-leave-unstaged). It's computed in Spiral (staged_from over the porcelain lines: index column not ' ' and not '?') in kit_do_git_reports (456 -> 518 lines), without touching the legacy porcelain_paths blob. Counts are unchanged ('changed' still counts every tracked change). Proof on a candidate kit.exe, test repo with 'M  b.txt' staged, ' M a.txt' unstaged and '?? c.txt': the candidate prints modified 2 (a, b), staged 1 (b.txt), untracked 1; the installed kit (control) has no staged row. Draft: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\agent-commit-guard\\git-status-staged.do. F2 left: F2d (walker migration with .cache skip, 180m) and F2c (delete clearance, 180m).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_45 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 45u32, "2026-10-30T17:24Z", "kit", "10-30 13:0x kit: F2d LANDED UNSTAGED. The walk behind every 'kit do' read/files/grep/copy (kit_do_read host.spi files_matching, one 33-line legacy $'{ ... }' blob) is migrated to Spiral in a new crate, kit_do_walk (730 lines). wildcard, the ** glob matcher, segments and the stack walk are Spiral; the host part is one-expression primitives (read_dir entries with dir/symlink flags, a BTreeSet path buffer that keeps output sorted and unique). The skipped folders are a Spiral list that now includes .cache: .git, target, node_modules, _build, deps, .cache. An explicit base (files .cache/**) is still walked. kit_do_read stays 948 lines (its blob is now one call).\nPROOF:\n- Cells tests 2/2: wildcard, ** spans and segments; and a temp-tree walk with .cache and target skipped, masks, exclusions, an explicit .cache base, and a missing path echoed back.\n- Differential on a candidate kit.exe: 'files <glob>' prints byte-identical rows and receipts to the installed kit for 9 globs over kit, spiral and i574n.github (up to 847 rows).\n- This morning's repro: 'copy src/** to out' now copies 3 files (b.spi, pkg/a.spi, pkg/tmp.log) where the installed kit copied 4, including .cache/deep/big.bin; 'except *.log' still skips 1.\nDrafts: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\do-walk\\. F2 left: F2c (delete clearance).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_46 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 46u32, "2026-10-30T17:54Z", "kit", "10-30 13:5x kit: F2c (delete clearance) DESCOPED for now, by rule rather than taste. kit has no 'do delete' verb; deletion is 'kit proxy fs-remove-tree <root> <relative>', which TRAIN5's kit_delete_guard already makes refuse relative paths and protected roots. The standing rule archive-never-delete (cleanup places or archives; only build outputs are removed directly) means agents don't delete source trees at all, so a cross-repo stem clearance (dangling-check-by-stem) would gate a path the rules already close. Revisit only if a 'do delete' or 'do archive' verb is built; then 'archive' takes a Cleared value from the stem search. F2 is therefore complete apart from that conditional piece: F2a (lease), F2b (guard), F2d (walker + .cache) and F2e (staged row) all landed or shipped.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_47 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 47u32, "2026-11-01T03:36Z", "kit", "10-31 23:4x kit groom (main 23:33, user: cadence/drift): Active -> PLANNED. No note in over 12 h, so nobody is working it this week; Planned keeps it in agile next at its priority (never auto-Paused, R3). First step when picked = the next step in its latest note.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_48 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 48u32, "2026-11-06T11:26Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_49 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 49u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries JOB-4 (Stop, retry and parallelism policies); TOOL-1 (Named environment profiles). Why: 10-24 note #38: F1 retry with lower parallelism, F4 env profiles; F4 shipped only the pin check (kit env check), named profiles still open")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_50 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 50u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. JOB-4 · Stop, retry and parallelism policies · P2 · sbin, ota · Open / On the first semantic failure, cancel undispatched work and let running siblings finish, recording the failure frontier. Retry only timed-out units, with an escalated budget. Run batches as one cumulative gate and bisect automatically on failure. Lower parallelism automatically after child-node crashes (MSBuild `MSB4166`) while reusing completed artifacts. || TOOL-1 · Named environment profiles · P0 · sqlt, ota, sbin, ssam, brz, erp, ge2e · Open / Every gate repeated `PATH`, `CARGO`, `RUSTC`, `RUSTDOC`, `RUSTFMT`, `CARGO_HOME`, `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`, `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and runtime settings such as `RUST_MIN_STACK` (or `DOTNET_ROOT`, `SPIRAL_DOTNET`). Bind a typed profile to a tool identity, compose toolchain and system `PATH` (the linker `cc` vanished when only the toolchain path was set), validate it before launch, actively unset obsolete or ambient variables (`PLATFORM` broke MSBuild; a global `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` broke .NET ICU), pass it transitively to `agile check`, patch providers and helpers, carry required build properties, and refuse profile substitution for gates. Give each gate named source-root bindings instead of process-global variables.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_51 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 51u32, "2026-11-09T14:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "MILESTONES: F2d (smallest remaining F2 slice) 60 m; F2e 90 m; F2c 120 m; F2 close-out and the memory notebook 30 m; size F1 and F3-F6 into their own milestones 60 m.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_52 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 52u32, "2026-11-09T14:30Z", "kit-split", "split into 4 chained children by kit agile split")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_53 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 53u32, "2026-11-09T14:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:0x rig CORRECTION of my 10:30 MILESTONES note: it named F2 slices from a stale line, but F2 is complete (F2a-b, d-e landed; F2c descoped by rule, 10-30). Source search today: F1 pid_owner exists (ps kill --mine/--theirs, rig_process_table/ownership.spi), F4 exists (rig_env_pins check), F6 exists (rig_mirror check), F3 is KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM (split today), F5 is KIT-EXPERIMENTS (tibia drafting the ledger spec). The real remaining work is four F1 pieces, now the children: M1 liveness --silent-limit 120 m, M2 retry --retry-reaped 90 m, M3 job sweep --mine 60 m, M4 run_mode OffscreenMuted 60 m.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_features_54 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES", 54u32, "2026-11-09T16:20Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 15:2x rig groom: estimate -> 330 m = the sum of its open children (F1 children M1 120 + M2 90 + M3 60 + M4 60); the parent carries no work of its own, so it waits on its last child and leaves the ready list.")
inl tree_pages_v2 () = Task ("TREE-PAGES-V2", "Tree pages v2 (from the 10-21 review, TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO note 24): publish exactly the tracked files (git checkout-index) instead of the rsync allowlist that leaks build outputs on Linux and drops whole languages on Windows; a separate pages job per repo, independent of tests; deploy via actions/deploy-pages (no gh-pages history) or force_orphan; a pinned renderer release instead of building dir-tree-html main in every CI; the post-deploy check landed from lab; dir_tree_html.rs split under 1,000 lines", Story, P1, D4, 88u32, Planned, "", "ci,pages,dir-tree-html,team:org,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tree_pages_v2 () = Planning ("TREE-PAGES-V2", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_1 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 1u32, "2026-10-22T02:38Z", "x", "2026-10-21 22:38 x: filed from the review; measurements are in TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO note 24. Order by value: (a) checkout-index publish in spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 (one script; every repo calls it), (b) the separate pages job, (c) deploy-pages or force_orphan, (d) renderer release + pin, (e) post-deploy check, (f) the crate split. (a) alone fixes the content of all 10 pages on their next deploy.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_2 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 2u32, "2026-10-22T03:59Z", "x", "2026-10-21 23:59 x: step (a) drafted and tested, not applied (spiral/scripts is main's). Draft: %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--home-git\\b7595ac3-963d-4714-be58-0267aa270947\\scratchpad\\publish-tree-v2.ps1, a drop-in for spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 with the same parameters. git checkout-index -a -f --prefix=dist/ exports the index; -Exclude patterns now drop any tracked path with a matching segment (eoie's '.cache' keeps working); -Include patterns now add untracked files with a matching name (polyglot '*.png', tibia '*.tsv','*.txt','*.lua','*.xml' keep their meaning); symlinks are dropped; dotfile renaming and the renderer-failure guard are unchanged; rsync, the 41-pattern allowlist, CYGWIN=noglob and the default exclude list are gone. Piping paths into checkout-index --stdin fails on Windows (pwsh appends CR: 'is not in the cache'), hence -a plus removal of excluded paths. Results with the local renderer: x 132 tracked files -> dist (0 .beam where the live page has 351 build outputs; all 19 .ex, which the allowlist drops on Windows), 4 s; spiral 10,234 files (534 .c, 467 .zig), 73 s on Windows, index.html 1,563 KB; a probe repo confirmed Exclude drops skipme/s.spi, Include adds an untracked b.tsv, an untracked c.beam stays out, and .gitattributes becomes _gitattributes. Note: the spiral test deleted a pre-existing, gitignored spiral/dist (an earlier local publish output; publish-tree itself wipes dist on every run).")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_3 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 3u32, "2026-10-22T04:01Z", "main", "00:01 main landed step (a) in spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 (uncommitted for the user): x's git checkout-index draft with two mechanical fixes (the literal NUL byte in the exclusion split became the backtick-0 escape so git diffs it as text; CRLF to LF); token sequence identical to the draft x tested (424 tokens), so x's results stand (x 132 files in 4 s, spiral 10,234 in 73 s, Include/Exclude semantics on a probe repo).")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_4 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 4u32, "2026-10-22T04:02Z", "x", "2026-10-22 00:02 x: main landed step (a) as spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 (uncommitted; NUL literal fixed to the backtick-0 escape, LF line endings). Rechecked the landed file on x: same result as the draft (132 tracked files + index.html, 0 .beam, 19 .ex). Live pages change on each repo's next deploy after the user commits spiral.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_5 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 5u32, "2026-10-22T06:29Z", "x", "2026-10-22 02:29 x: x's .github/workflows/ci.yml push job gets main's deploy check, copied verbatim from spiral's gh-pages.yml: echo GITHUB_SHA > gh-pages/_deploy.txt before peaceiris, then a pwsh step that GETs https://i574n.github.io/x/_deploy.txt (cache-busting query) every 15 s for up to 6 min until it equals GITHUB_SHA, then requires the README section and viewport meta in the index. No new uses: (scripts/actions-lock.ps1: 8 actions locked, passes); YAML parses; today's live x page already carries both marks. Uncommitted, for the user.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_6 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 6u32, "2026-10-22T10:00Z", "main", "2026-10-22 06:00 main: deciding (b), (c) and (d) myself (memory decide-autonomously), by one rule: pick the option that needs no repository-settings change and no new action dependency, with a tie going to the smaller workflow diff. (c) force_orphan: true on the existing peaceiris step. The alternative, actions/deploy-pages, needs each repo's Pages source switched to GitHub Actions in its settings, plus a new 'uses:' and actions.lock regeneration in every repo. Checked: all 10 tree-pages workflows (spiral, polyglot, dice, alphabet, x/ci, eoie, tibia, blog, i574n.github, dir-tree-html) pass only github_token and publish_dir (no keep_files, no destination_dir). peaceiris already replaces the whole page content, so force_orphan only stops the gh-pages branch from accumulating history. (d) pin the renderer by commit SHA in the checkout step, not by a release, since cutting a release is a push and git actions belong to the user; it is bumped deliberately. (b) the separate pages job stays as it is, a push job that needs build. Pages still deploy only after the build, which keeps a broken tree off the page. Revisit only if a red build ever blocks a needed page.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_7 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 7u32, "2026-10-22T10:01Z", "main", "2026-10-22 06:01 main: (c) APPLIED: force_orphan: true added after publish_dir in all 10 tree-pages workflows (spiral, polyglot (4-space YAML, indent 18), dice, alphabet, x/ci, eoie (no tree lease live), tibia, blog, i574n.github, dir-tree-html), one match per file. pyyaml check: each push job's peaceiris step now has force_orphan True. Uncommitted, for the user. (d) DEFERRED by a mechanical condition: the renderer is cloned at main only in CI (spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 builds when no exe exists), and dir-tree-html has staged, uncommitted renderer changes while origin/main is c1363bb (10-19). publish-tree v2 was tested against a local renderer that may include them, so a pin now could break the next deploy. Resume condition: when 'git -C dir-tree-html status' is clean and main equals origin/main, add 'git -C \\ checkout --quiet <that sha>' right after the clone in dir-tree-html.ps1, then bump the SHA with every renderer commit.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_8 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 8u32, "2026-10-22T11:40Z", "x", "2026-10-22 07:40 x: step (f) can close without a compiler change. x's scripts/rust-modules.ps1 (column-0 item parser; private fns go to <stem>_partN.rs with use super::*; types, pub fns and fn main stay in the root) splits dir-tree-html's generated dir_tree_html.rs, 2,774 lines, into a 33-line root plus parts of 950, 727, 379 and 701 lines. Every non-blank line is kept exactly once. Tested on %TEMP% copies, nothing in the repo touched: cargo check 0 errors 0 warnings; the dev builds of the split and unsplit copies both pass --self-test and render byte-identical HTML for x/scripts (4 KB) and x's 132 tracked files (19.6 KB). To apply: one line after BuildSpiral in dir-tree-html/build.ps1, pwsh -File <x>/scripts/rust-modules.ps1 -Source dir_tree_html.rs (or copy the script into spiral/scripts, since dir-tree-html has spiral, not x, as a dep). dir-tree-html and spiral/scripts are main's; x leaves the call to main.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_9 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 9u32, "2026-10-23T12:35Z", "main", "2026-10-23 08:35 main: (d) still deferred by its own condition: dir-tree-html has staged gh-pages.yml and dir_tree_html.spi (HEAD = origin/main c1363bb), so the renderer pin waits for the user's commit. (f) decided: no per-repo post-processing script. x's scripts/rust-modules.ps1 would be a second copy of a method that GENERATED-OUTPUT-MODULES (P1, compiler: one entry's output written as several files under 1,000 lines) puts in the compiler, where every Spiral repo gets it (rule generic-tools-not-per-experiment). dir-tree-html's 2,774-line dir_tree_html.rs is listed there as a consumer, and this item's (f) closes when that lands.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_10 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 10u32, "2026-10-25T09:58Z", "main", "10-25 05:58 main: (d) APPLIED by its resume condition (dir-tree-html clean, HEAD = origin/main = a643950e, 10-25 01:52). spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 checks out $rendererCommit = 'a643950e0628bc57005c94a9db83edc05a4c66ea' right after the CI clone, with a throw on a failed checkout; it parses with 0 errors. Bump that SHA with each renderer commit. A local checkout that already exists is left as is. (f) re-decided under the 10-24 rules: no compiler or script splitting (5j removed the output splits; memory hand-modeled-build-units). dir_tree_html.rs (2,774 lines) meets the 1k gate by splitting dir_tree_html.spi by hand into units with exports, so (f) is a dir-tree-html authoring task, not GENERATED-OUTPUT-MODULES.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_11 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 11u32, "2026-10-25T17:03Z", "main", "10-25 13:03 main: (f) first unit drafted on x's hand-unit method (X-HAND-UNITS: crates split by hand, linked through !!!!Export with typed host calls by name). %TEMP%\\dir-tree-units\\split.ps1 -Root <repo> [-Apply] cuts dir_tree_html.spi (739 lines) into: shared.spi (the ++ operator, find_nl), markdown/markdown.spi (the markdown renderer, 314 lines; main exports dtl_markdown : string -> string; crate dtl_markdown) and the root (428 lines; readme_html calls dtl_markdown::dtl_markdown through one typed host call). It also adds the Cargo workspace member and dependency, the modules entries, and a BuildSpiral line. Rule, written before the run: GREEN iff the unsplit (reference) and split scratch copies both build and pass --self-test (which renders a README through the new crate boundary), every generated .rs is at most 1,000 lines, and the split binary writes byte-identical HTML to the reference for spiral/scripts, x/scripts and the dir-tree-html checkout. If a unit is still over 1,000, cut it next (inline renderer vs blocks) by the same method. Not in this cut, recorded for after: dir-tree-html builds against the compiler's samples core (packageDir deps/spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples), against lib-first, and that path breaks at COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE step 1; host_listing is a multi-statement Rust blob (GRANULAR-HEAL scope).")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_12 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 12u32, "2026-10-25T19:12Z", "main", "10-25 15:12 main: (f) cut 1 by n11's rule: RED on size, GREEN on behaviour (job-1792949174944). Both builds pass --self-test, which renders a README through the new dtl_markdown crate. The split binary writes byte-identical HTML to the unsplit one for spiral/scripts (52CD6D8E), x/scripts (F511E825) and dir-tree-html (EB1866D2). But root dir_tree_html.rs is 1,403 lines and markdown.rs 1,359 (2,774 before), so per n11 the units are cut again by the same method. Cut 2 plan: crates dtl_inline (escape, inline links/images/badges, render_inline; exports dtl_escape and dtl_render_inline), dtl_markdown (block parsing, calling dtl_inline by name), dtl_tree (listing parse, sort, sizes, the HTML chain; exports dtl_tree_html, dtl_tree_bytes, dtl_size_label) and the root (host I/O, CLI, self-test, page assembly). A shared Spiral-only module holds ++, <., the Rust emit operator, find_nl, copied_run, digit/show_i64 and doc_head/doc_close. Same gate as n11.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_13 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 13u32, "2026-10-25T21:22Z", "main", "10-25 17:22 main: (f) cut 2 GREEN by n11's rule, proven on the node by kit2 (offload of the stuck local job; the node is output-validated). Generated units: dir_tree_html.rs 920, inline.rs 901, markdown.rs 481, tree.rs 625, all at most 1,000. HTML byte-identical to the unsplit build for spiral/scripts 52CD6D8E, x/scripts F511E825 and the dir-tree-html checkout (same hashes as this box's cut-1 run). LANDED unstaged in dir-tree-html (split2.ps1 -Apply on the clean HEAD a643950): shared.spi, inline/, markdown/, tree/ (crates dtl_inline, dtl_markdown, dtl_tree with Cargo.toml and [package.metadata.spiral]), the workspace members and dependencies, the modules list and 3 BuildSpiral lines. The repo's own build (regenerates the .rs, --self-test, line re-count) is queued as main-dir-tree-repo-build. Still open from n11: the samples-core packageDir (lib-first) and host_listing's multi-statement Rust blob (GRANULAR-HEAL).")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_14 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 14u32, "2026-10-25T23:12Z", "main", "10-25 19:12 main: lib-first port measured on the node (self-served). split3 (cut 2 + packageDir deps/spiral/lib with |core- and spiral-) is RED with genuine type errors, as predicted: the fork core's sm has no concat (shared.spi ++), and the samples core's dotted operators (%., /., +., -., *., =.) don't exist in lib. (The first split3 run, by kit2, had failed earlier on a missing deps junction: scp does not carry junctions.) split4 = split3 + a mechanical rewrite (%TEMP%\\dir-tree-units\\make-split4.ps1): 244 dotted operators made plain across the 5 files, and (++) defined over lib's ++# with shared opening sm'_operators. sm.index, sm.length and sm.slice exist in the fork core unchanged. split4 BUILDS on the node (RUST-OK); the full proof (same rule as n11: --self-test, 4 units at most 1,000 lines, byte-identical HTML for the 3 dirs) is running as node job-1792969904454. If GREEN, land split4 over the cut-2 landing (the delta is the spiproj plus the operator rewrite), which retires dir-tree-html's dependency on apps/compiler/tmp/samples (COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE step 1).")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_15 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 15u32, "2026-10-25T23:15Z", "main", "10-25 19:15 main: split4 GREEN on the node by n11's rule (job-1792969904454): units dir_tree_html.rs 990, inline.rs 912, markdown.rs 491, tree.rs 670 (all at most 1,000; root within 10 lines of the gate, since the fork core emits more than the samples core); --self-test passes; HTML byte-identical for spiral/scripts 52CD6D8E, x/scripts F511E825, dir-tree-html 0633BD8B. LANDED unstaged over the cut-2 landing, after verifying the repo held exactly cut 2 (0 of 11 files differing): 6 files updated (the 5 .spi with dotted operators made plain and ++ over lib's ++#, plus package.spiproj now packageDir deps/spiral/lib with |core- and spiral-). The queued repo build (main-dir-tree-repo-build) now regenerates and re-checks this lib-first version. Next for (f): if the root unit grows past 1,000, cut host I/O out of the root.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_16 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 16u32, "2026-10-26T00:24Z", "main", "10-25 20:24 main: status by part. (a) checkout-index publish: landed 10-22 in spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1. (b) decided 10-22 06:00: stays a push job that needs build. (c) force_orphan: applied in all 10 workflows. (d) renderer pinned by commit a643950e in spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1. (e) post-deploy check: in spiral's gh-pages.yml and x's ci.yml. (f) split4 lib-first, 4 units of at most 1,000 lines, landed unstaged 10-25 19:15. Nothing is left to build. Done needs the live check (memory installed-is-done): after the user commits spiral, the 10 workflows and dir-tree-html, each repo's next deploy must pass its _deploy.txt = GITHUB_SHA check and its page must list only tracked files. Next for main: at the next session with those commits pushed, read each repo's latest pages run and spot-check one leak path per repo (spiral: no .beam or target/ files in the page tree). One more: when dir-tree-html's split4 is committed, bump rendererCommit to that SHA.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_17 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 17u32, "2026-10-26T00:24Z", "main", "10-25 20:24 main: checked the pin bump's risk. The lib-first split4 renderer needs deps/spiral/lib, but CI clones dir-tree-html without the gitignored deps. dir-tree-html.ps1 runs the renderer's scripts/init.ps1 before build.ps1, and init.ps1:14-21 clones spiral beside it when missing and links deps/spiral to it, so packageDir deps/spiral/lib resolves in CI. Bumping rendererCommit to the split4 commit needs no other change.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_18 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 18u32, "2026-10-26T01:28Z", "main", "10-25 21:28 main: root cut drafted. The root's 990 generated lines are 724 in spiral_main: Spiral inlines non-recursive definitions, so self_test, its fixtures and run all land in one body. The cut that pays is therefore self_test plus fixtures into their own unit, not 'host I/O'. %TEMP%\\dir-tree-root-cut\\apply.ps1 -Root <repo> [-Apply] splits dir_tree_html.spi into top-level definitions and routes each by name (an unknown or missing name throws, and every original line must land exactly once): 15 into shared.spi (the crate wrappers markdown, tree_html and tree_bytes, the host primitives, readme_html, page, last_sep, parent_text and host_write; clash-checked against the inline, markdown and tree units: only size_label collides, tree.spi has its own, so its wrapper stays out of shared), 13 into a new selftest/selftest.spi unit (size_label's wrapper, the fixtures, self_test; exported as dtl_self_test : i32 -> i32, with a dummy arg because unit-arg Rust exports are the compiler lane's open RUST-EMIT-UNIT-ARG), and the root keeps host_arg_count, host_arg, flag_at, argument, run and main plus a one-line self_test calling dtl_self_test::dtl_self_test(0i32). Also: workspace member selftest, root dependency dtl_self_test, selftest/Cargo.toml depending on dtl_markdown and dtl_tree, a build.ps1 BuildSpiral step before the root's, and a package.spiproj module entry after tree/. Dry run on the repo: clean. Proof queued (main-dir-tree-root-cut-proof): n11's rule (byte-identical HTML for 3 dirs, --self-test through the new crate, every unit at most 1,000 lines) plus the new root size. Composes with the tree heal (it touches tree.spi only). After both, the cli_args port (CLI-ARGS-STYLE n17) has room.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_19 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 19u32, "2026-10-26T01:36Z", "main", "10-25 21:36 main: main-dir-tree-repo-build GREEN (finished 21:08): the repo's lib-first split4 working tree builds as 4 hand-split units, --self-test passes, every generated .rs is at most 1,000 lines. The landed split4 is verified in place; the root cut and cli_args proofs build on it.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_20 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 20u32, "2026-10-26T04:35Z", "main", "10-26 00:35 main: root cut and cli_args port both GREEN on the worker node and LANDED unstaged in dir-tree-html. Root-cut proof (node job-1792988595174): HTML byte-identical for 3 dirs, no unit over 1,000, root dir_tree_html.rs 990 -> 293 lines. Cut+port proof (node job-1792988608182): byte-identical HTML, root 353 lines, and a run without --dir exits 2 with 'error: missing --dir <value>'. Landed: selftest/ (selftest.spi + Cargo.toml) new; dir_tree_html.spi, shared.spi, Cargo.toml, build.ps1 and package.spiproj updated, with the root's run/main over cli_args. The tracked generated .rs files are stale until the queued main-dir-tree-repo-build-2 (after the tree-heal chain, so one build covers cut, port and heal). Its size check now covers every generated .rs; it named the 4 split4 units, which would have skipped selftest.rs.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_21 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 21u32, "2026-10-26T14:30Z", "main", "10-26 10:30 main: order for the remaining dir-tree work, 10:3x. repo-build-2 (00:34-01:22, exit 0) regenerated the tracked .rs before this morning's tree.spi heal landed (09:0x), so tree.rs is stale again against tree.spi. Next: the args/clock heal proof (job-1793018349662-main-dir-tree-args-lib-proof-2, queued; it copies the live repo, so it builds tree heal + args heal together). On GREEN, apply TEMP dir-tree-args-lib/apply.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html -Apply, then run repo-build-3 (TEMP dir-tree-units/repo-build.ps1, local: it rewrites the tracked .rs), so one build regenerates the units for both heals. The proof's size check already covers every generated .rs.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_22 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 22u32, "2026-10-26T18:20Z", "main", "10-26 14:20 main: 10-26 14:0x main: dir-tree-args-lib GREEN (job-1793018349662: HTML byte-identical, no unit over 1,000 lines, 0 host args/stderr code left in dir_tree_html.spi, same error path). LANDED as an unstaged layer over the user's staged dir_tree_html.spi and shared.spi. Anchors re-matched on the live tree first (dry run at 14:0x). Live hashes after the land equal the proven healed copies: dir_tree_html.spi 95EF329B2E316C70, shared.spi 8CCF65F8E60A70E7, selftest/selftest.spi 08DECBE175C74612. Undo copies in TEMP dir-tree-args-lib/pre-land: dir_tree_html 985BFA257A2B2E2D and shared 6EB5A937CED77F58 from the live tree; selftest FAB8C6DDF2685164 from the proof's reference, which equals git's index version. My backup loop used a wrong path for selftest (it lives in selftest/), so that copy came from the reference and was verified against the index. The landing rule's last step, the repo build (dir-tree-html build.ps1 + --self-test + 1k units, main-serial-dir-tree-repo-build-3), is registered in the post-rename requeue. Kit's pause would stop it now.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_23 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 23u32, "2026-10-27T14:08Z", "main", "10-27 10:08 main: status re-measured part by part against the title (10-27 10:1x). DONE: (1) publish exactly the tracked files: spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 (shared by every repo's scripts/publish.ps1) builds dist with git checkout-index -a -f --prefix=dist/ over git ls-files, with per-repo Exclude and Include, and no rsync anywhere (census of 13 i574n repos' workflows: rsync 0). (2) force_orphan deploy: peaceiris actions-gh-pages force_orphan in blog, dir-tree-html, eoie/kit, fiscal, i574n.github, tibia and x. (3) post-deploy check: the 'verify the deploy is live' step (e.g. x ci.yml). (4) dir_tree_html.rs split under 1,000 lines (10-26, root 293 lines). PARTIAL: (5) pinned renderer: spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 pins rendererCommit a643950e, but still clones and BUILDS dir-tree-html in every CI run. A prebuilt release download needs a dir-tree-html GitHub Release to exist, and publishing releases is outward-facing, so it's the user's decision before anything is set up. OPEN: (6) a pages job independent of tests: the generated push job still has needs: build (workflows come from i574n.github/scripts/pins/workflows.spi). Splitting it means a pages job that runs publish.ps1 itself, not one that downloads the build matrix's artifact. Light design work in workflows.spi; any new uses: needs gh actions-lock.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_24 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 24u32, "2026-10-27T14:09Z", "main", "10-27 10:09 main: dependency found while designing (6): in every generated gh-pages workflow (workflows.spi lines 21-225: plain repos, notebook builds, spiral's build and the x/tibia variants), publish.ps1 runs INSIDE the build job, which already sets up the toolchains the renderer needs: dir-tree-html.ps1 clones and cargo-builds the renderer when no binary is present. A pages job independent of tests would have to repeat that Rust setup plus a renderer build in its own job, costing more CI minutes, not fewer, unless it can download a prebuilt renderer. So (6) waits on (5): with a released dir-tree-html binary the pages job is checkout + spiral's scripts + download + publish-tree.ps1, a few minutes and independent of tests. BLOCKER for both: the user's decision to publish dir-tree-html GitHub Releases (an outward-facing action). Proposed shape for that decision: dir-tree-html's own CI attaches the Linux and Windows binaries to a release per tagged commit, and spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 downloads the release matching rendererCommit, falling back to today's build when none exists.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_25 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 25u32, "2026-10-28T11:15Z", "main", "10-28 07:15 main: Groom 10-28 07:1x: Active -> Blocked, user decision. Step (6), a pages job independent of tests, waits on (5), a released dir-tree-html binary the job can download instead of building the renderer (n.10-27 10:09). (5) is a GitHub release, i.e. publishing, which is the user's call (listed as an open decision since 10-27). Unblocks on: the user approves the dir-tree-html release, then (5) and (6) are agent work (about 60 min).")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_26 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 26u32, "2026-10-30T02:01Z", "main", "10-29 22:01 main, groom: re-verified Blocked: still the USER's approval of a dir-tree-html GitHub release (publishing), step (5). Steps (5) and (6) are then about 60 min of agent work.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_27 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 27u32, "2026-10-30T14:12Z", "main", "10-30 10:12 main, BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030 R1: the only blocker is approving the dir-tree-html GitHub release (publishing). Now assignee=user + user-batch; grooms stop re-verifying it, and it moves when the user acts.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_28 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 28u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Publish a dir-tree-html GitHub release so the independent pages job can download the renderer? RULE (written before acting): Default without publishing: pin the renderer by dir-tree-html commit SHA (cargo install --git --rev <sha>) with an actions/cache keyed on the SHA. That gives step (6), a pages job independent of tests, with no release. It is reversible, stays inside the user's repos, and leaves the pinned release as a later swap behind one workflow input. The workflow edits plus actions.lock are left unstaged for the user's push. BACKUP/UNDO: The workflow edits are unstaged and the old job is kept until the new one is green. Revert = git checkout of the workflow files by the user. OWNER: main. NEXT: Draft the pinned-SHA pages job for one repo (x), regenerate actions.lock, and node-prove it before rolling it out to the rest. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_29 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 29u32, "2026-11-03T08:52Z", "main", "main 11-03 04:2x RETARGETED: the renderer part of this item ('a pinned renderer release instead of building dir-tree-html main in every CI', and x's 11-02 ByDefault pin by commit) now means html's release (HTML-CI-RELEASE), adopted through the shim (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS), since dir-tree-html left the org 11-03. The publish-tree.ps1 mechanics (git checkout-index of exactly the tracked files, a separate pages job, deploy-pages or force_orphan, the post-deploy check) are unaffected and stay here.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_30 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 30u32, "2026-11-06T12:47Z", "main", "main 11-06 10:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: tree pages publish exactly the tracked files (git checkout-index) plus the regenerated notebook pages, in every adopted repo, with html as the renderer. Next step: HTML-ADOPT-REPOS's shim switch after the user's html push.")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_31 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 31u32, "2026-11-09T11:52Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 fiscal evidence for the renderer switch: fiscal's live pages (i574n.github.io/fiscal, deploy 518c4abe) are STILL dir-tree-html: README.md is served raw (no .md.html page), and the index links target/ci-metrics/reports.md as a raw file. html's renderer already covers what fiscal publishes (html_pages/file_views.spi: Prose for .md, Delimited tables for .tsv such as gate-cost/growth/modeling-ceiling, Source for .spi), so fiscal needs no change of its own when HTML-ADOPT-REPOS flips the shim. Wait: item HTML-ADOPT-REPOS")
inl note_of_tree_pages_v2_32 () = Note ("TREE-PAGES-V2", 32u32, "2026-11-09T18:24Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:3x tibia (help pool): no work to take. The item is 88 pct and its next step is HTML-ADOPT-REPOS's shim switch after the user's html push (DoD note, 11-06; fiscal's 11-52Z evidence agrees). That wait was only PROSE (\"Wait: item HTML-ADOPT-REPOS\"), which the gate cannot read, so the item kept surfacing in every empty lane's help pool. It now has a structured wait row (item:HTML-ADOPT-REPOS) and leaves the pool until that item moves.")
inl kit_lib_reuse () = Task ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", "Rework eoie onto lib/spiral and granular Spiral (user 2026-10-21 22:4x: 'gotta rework everything'; 'we have the damn sm in spiral lib, eoie should be reusing lib as much as possible instead of duplicating code everywhere')", Epic, P1, D8, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-HEAL-LIB-LINK,SPIRAL-LIB-AM-ANY,KIT-STYLE-RATCHET,KIT-HEAL-EDIT-HOOK,KIT-AGENT-GUIDE,KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY,KIT-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", "kit,style,lib,epic,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_lib_reuse () = Planning ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", Minutes 1122u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_1 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 1u32, "2026-10-22T02:41Z", "eoie", "22:41 baseline: eoie 47.4 KLOC Spiral, 29.6 host macros/KLOC, 12.1 Rc::<str>::from/KLOC, 3.3 $'{ let blocks/KLOC; tibia 0/0/0; x 16.3 macros confined to boundary modules. 0 eoie packages reference lib/spiral; x, polyglot, dice, alphabet and Spiral samples all do (packageDir + spiral-). Plan: (1) wire lib/spiral into eoie's build (workspace.ps1 makes a git-ignored src/spiral junction to the Spiral checkout's lib/spiral, the same shape the Cells mount uses) and into Cells runs; (2) a gate: no $' outside one eoie OS boundary package, no $'{ blocks, no Rc::<str>::from outside it, failing the build (EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET becomes a hard check); (3) shrink rust_std_string into calls of sm'/am' and then delete it; missing generic primitives go into lib/spiral, never into eoie; (4) migrate crate by crate after the r30-r36 train lands (pending slices anchor on today's text; migrating first breaks every anchor), each crate done when it has no macros outside the boundary and its tests pass. Pilot on agile_task_query started 22:38 (sm'.to_lower/to_upper/index_of/trim/split/starts_with + am'.any replacing three macros).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_2 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 2u32, "2026-10-22T02:43Z", "eoie", "22:43 pilot PASSES under Cells (query.spi unit tests 4/4): agile_task_query with spiral- as a plain sibling package (no packageDir: Cells resolves packageDir from its cells-mounts junction, so ../../../spiral/lib breaks; the mount already links spiral next to the package) and sm'.to_lower/to_upper/index_of/replace/starts_with replacing three host macros (6 -> 3 left: query_token, expect, i32 text). am'.any fails in rustc (SPIRAL-LIB-AM-ANY), worked around with sm'.index_of. Not left live: eoie's own build has no src/spiral, so the r30-r33 relaunch would break; live files restored, pilot saved in lab/EOIE-LIB-REUSE (apply-lib-pilot.ps1 refuses until src/spiral exists). Next: workspace.ps1 creates a git-ignored src/spiral junction to <bundle>/../../../lib/spiral (+ /src/spiral in .gitignore, census/harvest scans skip it), apply the pilot, test-regeneration -Filter agile_task_query -CargoCheck, check the generated .rs against the 1000-line gate.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_3 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 3u32, "2026-10-22T05:12Z", "main", "01:12 main: am'.any is portable now in tree lib/spiral/am'.spi, so it works on any backend that has array length and index_base. Test block for rust, fsharp and typescript; lib gate 11/11, 0 type errors (job main-am-any-gate). Next: sm'.listed and sm'.trim_end_suffix (sm'.contains already exists), gated as main-helpers-gate.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_4 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 4u32, "2026-10-22T05:26Z", "main", "01:26 main: sm' helpers gate, same harness fault (copy folder not named spiral); rerunning. Rule: on the same run as the tree baseline, every target passing on the tree passes on the copy, and listed_compares_trimmed_parts and trim_end_suffix_removes_every_trailing_copy pass on rust, fsharp and gleam. Then both land in tree lib/spiral/sm'.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_5 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 5u32, "2026-10-22T05:39Z", "main", "01:39 main: eoie's 4th lib gap is answered. env.get_environment_variable (env.spi:53) is already a runtime read on 7 backends (Rust std::env::var). What's added is env.try_get_environment_variable var : option string, a portable wrapper (None when unset or empty), test try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset on gleam, lua, fsharp, rust and typescript. Job main-env-gate runs after main-sm-gates; rule as for the sm' helpers (copy passes everything the tree passes, plus the new test). Landing in tree lib/spiral waits for eoie's 'release done' (ABC reads lib/spiral).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_6 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 6u32, "2026-10-22T05:46Z", "main", "01:46 main: second invalid run, now understood. Cells finds the lib and its real prelude (testing, rust_type) by looking for lib/spiral and similar paths under an ancestor of the file (notebook.ex @lib_rels), so a copy at <copy>\\spiral loses the prelude and every test fails with main_real.spir 'open testing' unbound. The tree baselines from the same runs pass: sm'.spi 43/43, env.spi 2/2. Copies are now <copy>\\lib\\spiral. lib_gate.ps1 throws on any other -Lib shape. Reruns: main-sm-gates2 (concat, helpers), then main-env-gate2.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_7 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 7u32, "2026-10-22T06:06Z", "main", "02:06 main: gates PASS on correct copies (job main-sm-gates2): balanced concat 43/43, 0 type errors, the same as the tree baseline; sm' helpers 45/45 (the tree's 43 plus listed_compares_trimmed_parts and trim_end_suffix_removes_every_trailing_copy), 0 type errors. Combined into the helpers copy (sm' E812C7BE301E6EC1). Slip: this was applied while main-env-gate2 was already running on that copy, so that env gate saw either sm' version. Both passed alone and env.spi uses neither change. Final check: main-sm-combined gates the combined sm'.spi after it. Landing into tree lib/spiral waits for eoie's 'release done'.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_8 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 8u32, "2026-10-22T06:11Z", "main", "02:11 main: env.try_get_environment_variable PASSES (job main-env-gate2 on the helpers copy): env.spi 3/3, 0 type errors (the tree's 2 plus try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset on gleam, lua, fsharp, rust and typescript). It lands in tree lib/spiral with the sm' helpers after eoie's 'release done' and the combined sm' gate (main-sm-combined).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_9 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 9u32, "2026-10-22T06:18Z", "eoie", "02:18 measured progress (live tree -> scratch tree rE after releases ABC + D + E apply): packages on lib/spiral 1 -> 70 (of 374), on rust_std_string 116 -> 51, declaring HostFree 0 -> 22, concat5 uses 1165 -> 717. E carries the 67 healed crates and still needs its compile preview and the 1000-line gate check before it ships next session.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_10 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 10u32, "2026-10-22T06:18Z", "main", "02:18 main: the combined gate PASSES (job main-sm-combined, helpers copy with balanced concat + listed + trim_end_suffix + env.try_get_environment_variable): sm'.spi 45/45, env.spi 3/3, 0 type errors. Only sm'.spi (+50/-7) and env.spi (+17) differ from the tree, and the tree's sm'.spi still equals the gated base (F7D95B8A8410F714). Landing is %TEMP%\\land-lib.ps1, which refuses if either tree file changed since. It runs on eoie's 'release done' (ABC reads lib/spiral).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_11 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 11u32, "2026-10-22T06:43Z", "eoie", "02:43 heal-crate bug caught by an audit before any release: when a file's only open sm'_operators sat inside its 'test X static' block, the tool deleted the top-level open rust_std_string.model and its presence check matched the indented open, leaving 15 files using ++# with no top-level operator open (would have failed E's regen). Fix: the top-level open is replaced in place by open sm'_operators and dropped only when nothing uses ++#; the check is anchored at column 0. The E preview was rebuilt from the D tree in 20 s (apply-rE.ps1 now takes -Src): 0 files lack the open; the only other diffs are two block-string files the old preview had mangled. New hand-healed slice apply-heal-do-verbs.ps1: eoie_do_model gains query_verb_word/query_verb_named (reflection over the existing query_verb union); do read's verb if-chain, its two option pipe tables and its option record-update chain become query_option/query_filler unions with query_option_applied; do write reuses query_verb_named instead of re-listing the verbs. 74 crates healed in E. Compile check waits for a quiet machine (ABC release build running).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_12 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 12u32, "2026-10-22T07:03Z", "eoie", "03:03 E preview: two more heal-crate bugs fixed before any release: (1) a call whose only newlines sit inside a triple-quoted block was laid out multi-line with indent taken from inside the block (++# at column 0, ParserErrors in agile_note_model and agile_planning_model); layout now masks block literals. (2) eoie_agile_mutation reached 1004 .rs lines after the ++# heal (gate 1000): per the prewritten rule its heal-crate step is dropped from E, its planning-field pipe table still becomes a reflection over agile_planning_model.planning_field. Root cause sent to main: each ++# lowers to its own Rc::from(format!) binding on Rust, concat5 was one; fix belongs in codegen (inline single-use macro bindings) or a lib n-ary concat. New slice apply-heal-agile-words.ps1: agile list's status filter holds an agile_status, agile_status_open lives in agile_mutation_policy, ranking's open check reflects over it. Duplicate found: eoie_agile_mutation declares its own validation_result next to workspace_primitives.outcome's.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_13 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 13u32, "2026-10-22T08:01Z", "main", "04:01 main: LANDED in tree lib/spiral (uncommitted for the user): sm'.listed, sm'.trim_end_suffix, env.try_get_environment_variable, the balanced sm'.concat_list, and the new process module. Gates: sm'.spi 45/45 combined, env.spi 3/3, process.spi 5/5.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_14 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 14u32, "2026-10-22T08:06Z", "eoie", "04:06 main landed sm'.listed, sm'.trim_end_suffix, env.try_get_environment_variable in tree lib (04:0x). heal-crate.ps1 now maps trim_end_matches -> sm'.trim_end_suffix (same semantics: every trailing copy, empty suffix is a no-op) and pipe_member -> sm'.listed only over a whitespace-free string literal list (listed trims parts, pipe_member compares exactly; computed lists are refused for review). Hand slice apply-heal-comma-lists.ps1: table diff keys and planning tally deps become sm'.listed with a comma separator (trimmed comma lists, the behavior agile next's listed_in already implements by hand; listed_in itself stays because agile_task_next is at 993 lines). E rebuilt from the D tree: concat5 1165 -> 488 uses, packages on rust_std_string 116 -> 39, on lib 1 -> 82, pipe tables 22 -> 4 (command_spec_domain's positional route lists, hand-only), 4 near-gate crates skipped. Compile preview of E waits for the next session (no compiles from 04:00 through tibia's live block).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_15 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 15u32, "2026-10-22T08:09Z", "eoie", "04:09 preview caveat: the scratch D tree holds stale .rs for crates ABC regenerated or created (eoie_machine_watch watch.rs empty there, 954 live; eoie_do_write 683 vs 785; eoie_table_query 304 vs 534; eoie_read_query 939 vs 632), and heal-crate's 950 guard plus gate measurements read those files. No healed crate crosses 950 between the two, but eoie_do_write's healed size projects to ~963 from the live base. Next session builds E's preview from a copy of the live tree after the ABC tail installs. eoie_machine_watch stays on concat5 (954 live).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_16 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 16u32, "2026-10-22T08:10Z", "eoie", "04:10 one of the 4 remaining pipe tables: agile_subcommand_domain/subcommand.spi agile_subcommand_shape joins every spec name and shape into two strings and pipe_lookups by position, duplicating agile_subcommand_of right above it. Typed heal: match agile_subcommand_of input with AgileKnown subcommand -> (agile_subcommand_spec subcommand).shape, AgileUnknownName -> empty (and agile_subcommand_of's equals becomes =). Held: the package compiles into its consumers (agile_task_query, eoie_agile_mutation) and a 25-arm match costs more Rust than one pipe_lookup, with eoie_agile_mutation at 981 lines; do it with the near-gate set after main's codegen pack. The other 3 are command_spec_domain's positional route lists (hand-only, see spiral-macro-gotchas).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_17 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 17u32, "2026-10-22T08:26Z", "eoie", "04:26 census of the 39 packages still on rust_std_string in a composed copy (live + D + E, real .rs sizes): 21 heal now with tonight's mappings (wave E2, apply-rE2-wave.ps1, its own preview after E's); 12 near-gate skips (950-1000: job_gate 1000, memory 994, do_program 988, todo_lines 986, agile_mutation 981, task_listing 979, task_next 978, do_edit 976, memory_query 975, experiment_analysis 965, command_spec_domain 962, machine_watch 954); 3 unmapped names (agile_subcommand_domain pipe_lookup, authority_state_domain, eoie_experiment_stats); 2 computed lists (agile_memory_links, agile_todo_model). Rejected idea, measured: a static growth predictor (extra lines = ++# operators - concat5 calls) misses by -30..+148 lines against tonight's previews (do_write +178 measured vs +30 predicted; eoie_dev -28 vs +2), because sm' calls pull lib helpers and reflection lookups expand per call site. The compile preview stays the only gate measurement; the 950 rule stays the pre-filter.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_18 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 18u32, "2026-10-22T08:29Z", "eoie", "04:29 heal-crate fix: a file whose only rust_std_string open sits inside its test static block (authority_state_domain, eoie_experiment_stats) was refused because the open handling required a column-0 open; it now handles an open at any indent (replaced by open sm'_operators, dropped when nothing uses ++#; a top-level operator open is still inserted wherever ++# appears). Both join wave E2 (23 packages).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_19 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 19u32, "2026-10-22T08:31Z", "eoie", "04:31 wave E2 is 24 packages: the 21 from the census, authority_state_domain and eoie_experiment_stats (after the indented-open fix) and agile_memory_links (hand slice apply-heal-memory-links.ps1: memory slugs come from kebab-case file names, so sm'.listed's trimming changes nothing). agile_todo_model stays: it is a package compiled into agile_todo_lines (986 lines). The whole wave dry-runs clean on a composed copy of live + D + E.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_20 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 20u32, "2026-10-22T08:55Z", "eoie", "04:55 composition check (text only) on a fresh D-tree copy: apply-rE.ps1 then apply-rE2-wave.ps1 (24 packages + decimal parse 13 + string length 7 + path kind 8) compose cleanly. Totals after E+E2: concat5 1165 -> 232 uses, packages on rust_std_string 116 -> 14, packages on lib/spiral 1 -> 111. Gate numbers come only from previews (E first, then E2) on the live tree after the ABC tail installs.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_21 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 21u32, "2026-10-22T09:08Z", "eoie", "05:08 E's gate preview is scheduled for 06:32, after tibia's live block: preview-E-live.ps1 copies the live src (which already holds ABC's regenerated .rs, so sizes are real), applies D then E, and previews the 100 touched packages in a compile window (~18 min), reporting every .rs against 1000/950. Its text half was dry-run just now (D + E apply, 100 touched).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_22 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 22u32, "2026-10-22T09:16Z", "eoie", "05:16 preview scripts fixed before use: a touched set built only from packages whose own .spi changed misses the crates that compile a changed crate-less package (workspace_primitives, eoie_do_model, agile_mutation_policy...). preview-E-live.ps1 and the new preview-E2-live.ps1 add every crate whose package.spiproj lists a touched package; E's set grows 100 -> 120 (about 22 min in a compile window). E2's script applies E first and previews only what E2 changes on top.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_23 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 23u32, "2026-10-22T10:29Z", "eoie", "06:29 tibia's live block ended 06:28 (live-gui released, confirmed by tibia); E's gate preview started (preview-E-live.ps1: live src copy + D + E, about 120 touched crates and consumers, one compile window). Results go here and into the 07:00 report.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_24 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 24u32, "2026-10-22T10:33Z", "eoie", "06:33 E's gate preview was reaped by Claude Code's low-memory guard at about 06:31, after 5 of ~120 crates: at block end every lane started heavy work at once (x pre-commit, tibia gpu sim, four main jobs), free memory fell to 3.7 GB with both heavy slots held. Cleaned up: its compile window released (pid gone), the live src copy and the staged regeneration folder (verified mine by eoie_do_records, no process using it) removed. Not retried tonight, though retry-after-memory-kills says retry: the preview needs ~22 min, 27 min remained, and the machine stays saturated by six other heavy jobs, so a retry would be reaped again or miss 07:00. Next session: run preview-E-live.ps1 first thing, before heavy lanes start, or after the ABC tail; gate numbers stay pending until then.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_25 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 25u32, "2026-10-22T10:35Z", "eoie", "06:35 correction to note 24: the reap was not only the block-end stampede. I had taken the Stop gate's idle-stop path (three tool-free stops) while the preview ran, and the low-memory reaper only kills background shells of an idle session. Recorded in memory heavy-gate-lessons: while a job of mine runs, stay in the turn with light tool work.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_26 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 26u32, "2026-10-22T22:16Z", "eoie-lane", "18:16 next heal drafted (scratch apply-heal-console.ps1, text dry run on a GE2+H copy): 25 packages each define their own stdout helper as a println host macro, and lib console.write_line's Rust arm is exactly println of the value, so the helper becomes 'let name (~x : string) : () = console.write_line x' plus spiral- in the spiproj. Dry run: 23 packages healed; eoie_do_edit (976) and eoie_machine_watch (954) skipped by the near-gate rule; 16 inline println uses (not helpers) left for package-by-package healing. eprintln (12 copies) waits for main's console.write_error_line in the combined landing. Placement: its own wave after H, previewed with -CargoCheck over the 23 owners, since it touches crates GE2 and H do not regenerate. Also measured: workspace_primitives already holds stdout_line, stderr_line and unix_ms for 47 packages; the heal goes to lib, not there, because lib is the single source (lib-first).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_27 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 27u32, "2026-10-22T22:21Z", "eoie-lane", "18:21 apply-heal-console.ps1 now also covers the 12 eprintln helpers, behind a lib check: they move onto console.write_error_line only when lib console.spi defines it (main's combined landing). Dry runs on GE2+H copies: with today's lib the 12 stay as they are (reported); with a stand-in console.spi that defines write_error_line, all 12 heal. So the slice is correct before and after the landing, and needs no edit when the landing arrives.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_28 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 28u32, "2026-10-23T16:23Z", "eoie", "12:23 eoie: next heal drafted, scratch apply-heal-lines.ps1, from a census of host-macro helpers still copied across packages on the live tree (stdout_line 24, argument_count 22 and argument 18 were already covered by the console, argv, decimal-parse and integer-text heals; left: line_count 10, line_at 8, text_between 5, file_text 4, option_value 4). The line helpers come in two semantics (all lines, or the empty ones filtered out) and two return types. Lib gains sm'.line_count/line_at/nonempty_line_count/nonempty_line_at as named Rust one-expression primitives (the exact scanning expressions the copies use), plus sm'.lines/nonempty_lines (split once) for real per-package migrations; test blocks for both, in the lib-gaps slice. A first version mapped the copies onto sm'.lines plus am'.length/try_item, but callers use these helpers in loops (do_lab checks line_count every recursion step, lcov walks by line_at), so per-call array building would have turned those loops quadratic in allocations; the heal now maps onto the scanning primitives instead. Dry run on a src copy: 15 definitions in 8 packages (dev_spiral_tests, do_git, do_jobs, do_lab, do_write, handoff_render, lcov, repo_state), each keeping its semantics and return type; eoie_machine_watch (954) skipped by the near-gate rule; eoie_grep_query's multi-line copy is left for package-level healing. Lands after lib-gaps, in its own heal wave.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_29 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 29u32, "2026-10-23T17:50Z", "eoie", "13:50 eoie: lib-gaps gate with a tree baseline (job-1792773558090, process compiler, own MIX_BUILD_PATH, box at 100%). Tree sm'.spi (untouched lib) failed MORE targets than the copy: format and show and replicate_3 on rust, format_fixed_avoids_ties gleam, show_floats typescript. Copy sm'.spi with the lib gaps: 49/51, and the 2 reds (format_fixed_avoids_ties zig, show_floats zig, with delphi/lean not run) also fail on the tree (zig-dev locally vs 0.17.0 in CI). Tree env.spi 5/5, where the copy's earlier run had one typescript red in get_environment_variable: so these reds differ run to run under load. Every added test passes: process.try_capture_combined_list (rust), am'.growable/push_back, sm'.concat_array join, sm'.lines/nonempty_lines/line_count/line_at and nonempty variants, env.current_executable, testing.expect. Ready to land after main's lib land, with one more gate run on an idler box.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_30 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 30u32, "2026-10-23T21:51Z", "eoie", "17:51 eoie: from EOIE-USES-LIB's close check (live tree, after GE2's landing): 32 packages still list rust_std_string. 10 are named by a queued slice (H, J, K, heal-lines, agile-records, job-rechain, note-append); that is an upper bound, since being named doesn't mean the slice removes the dependency. 22 are covered by nothing queued: agile_note_model, agile_todo_lines, agile_todo_model, command_spec_domain, eoie_do_edit, eoie_do_facts, eoie_do_git, eoie_do_process, eoie_do_program, eoie_experiment_amend, eoie_experiment_analysis, eoie_experiments, eoie_job_supervise, eoie_machine_crowding, eoie_machine_watch, eoie_memory, eoie_memory_model, eoie_memory_query, eoie_receipt, eoie_style_census, eoie_table_query, workspace_primitives. Those are this item's next heal wave. Order by the 950-line gate (crates near 1000 lines first need a crate boundary, as with do_program at 988).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_31 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 31u32, "2026-10-23T22:08Z", "eoie", "18:08 eoie: heal wave 1 drafted (scratch heal-wave-1/apply-heal-wave-1.ps1; dry run clean and idempotent; typecheck waits for tibia's live block to end, since no compiles run during a block). eoie_receipt moves onto lib (++#, console.write_line, lib testing.expect, sm'.contains; spiral- added). eoie_job_supervise drops an unused open of rust_std_string.model. workspace_primitives measured_sizes uses ++#, with byte-identical output. replace_file_checked keeps its concat5 until lib has a process-id primitive, since touching it would mean migrating its pid host blob. Selection rule applied: packages whose own or inlining crates sit at 950+ generated lines are skipped (eoie_memory 994, do_program 988, do_edit 976, memory_query 975, experiment_analysis 965, machine_watch 954; eoie_table_query is inlined into analysis.rs at 965), because each ++# adds a Rust binding until RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE lands. Package listings stay until a dependents check (transitive resolution).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_32 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 32u32, "2026-10-23T22:18Z", "eoie", "18:18 eoie: measured with heal-crate.ps1 (its built-in gate rule: own or consumer crate projected within 5% of 1000 lines) over the 17 remaining uncovered packages on a post-O copy. Only 2 heal now: eoie_experiment_amend (1 file rewritten, spiral- referenced, HostFree + LibReferenced declared) and eoie_machine_crowding (0 rewrites, standards declared). 15 are skipped: own crates do_edit 976->1054, do_facts 937->973, do_process 903->987, do_program 988, experiment_analysis 965, experiments 949, machine_watch 954, memory 994, memory_query 975, style_census 923->986, agile_todo_lines 986; consumers agile_note_model and eoie_table_query (via experiment_analysis 965), agile_todo_model (via agile_todo_lines 986), eoie_memory_model (via eoie_memory 994). So the heal wave is blocked on RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE (main's codegen: inline single-use bindings, so a ++# chain costs what concat5 costs), not on drafting. Plan: wave 2 = heal-crate on those 2 plus heal wave 1, in the release after O; the rest re-run heal-crate the day RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE installs (the tool re-projects, so no per-package work is lost).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_33 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 33u32, "2026-10-24T00:09Z", "eoie", "20:09 eoie: lib-first heal of the most repeated host blob: stdout_line as $'println!(\"{}\", &*!text)' occurs once in each of 23 packages. A generated eoie do program (scratch heal-do-host/heal-stdout-line.do, one edit block per file with expect files 1 replacements 1) turns 20 of them into console.write_line text: ok files 20 replacements 20 in 54 ms on a copy of the real post-P tree. The 3 packages without spiral- (eoie_do_edit, eoie_do_facts, eoie_machine_watch) wait for a step that adds the lib reference; console.write_line compiles to the same println, so near-gate crates don't grow. heal-jobs-host.do dropped its own stdout rule (now 4 rules), so the two programs compose (both ok in sequence; a third, overlapping program refused fail-safe and was deleted). Typecheck tomorrow; ships after the train with the boundary work.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_34 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 34u32, "2026-10-24T00:10Z", "eoie", "20:10 eoie: second mass heal: the number-to-text one-liners count_text, decimal_text, i32_text and u64_text (to_string host blobs repeated across packages) become sm'.format value. sm'.format prints integers as bare digits (lib test: 8i32 shows as 8), and eoie's sequences receipts already rely on it. Generated program scratch heal-do-host/heal-number-text.do: 17 files, 17 replacements, ok in 40 ms, applied on top of heal-stdout-line and heal-jobs-host, so all three compose. Skipped: eoie_do_program and eoie_machine_watch (no spiral- reference) and eoie_jobs (its decimal_text sits in heal-jobs-host.do). Census method for the next ones: exact duplicate host one-liners (inl/let name ... = $'...' : type) grouped by text, highest counts first; all_digits (4x) is next and needs a lib sm'.all_digits or a fold over to_char_list.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_35 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 35u32, "2026-10-24T00:13Z", "eoie", "20:13 heal-do-host\\heal-stderr-line.do: 11 generated edit blocks swap the copied stderr_line host macro (eprintln through Rc str) for console.write_error_line text; every target package already lists spiral-; eoie_jobs left out because heal-jobs-host.do carries its copy. Applied on the compose copy after stdout-line + number-text: ok files 11 replacements 11 in 33 ms. Typecheck with the other heal programs after the train.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_36 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 36u32, "2026-10-24T00:16Z", "eoie", "20:16 heal-do-host\\heal-number-text-tail.do: the first number-text program only matched the .to_string().as_str() spelling; a regex census over integer-to-text one-liners with the plain (!value).to_string() spelling found 9 more packages, now sm'.format value. Composes on the compose copy after the other three programs (ok files 9 replacements 9). Left out: u64_parsed (2, parse without trim, try_convert goes through i64 so values above i64 max would differ), own_pid (2, lib has no process id: lib gap), text_between (4, total get vs lib substring that slices unchecked).")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_37 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 37u32, "2026-10-24T00:17Z", "eoie", "20:17 correction to note 36: the tail program is 6 packages, not 9. eoie_do_program (compiled.spi) and eoie_machine_watch (jobs_watch.spi, run.spi) list only core- and rust_std_string, so sm'.format would not resolve. Dropped those 3 blocks and reverted them on the compose copy with the inverse program. A spiral- audit over all five heal programs now shows none targeting a package without spiral-.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_38 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 38u32, "2026-10-24T07:18Z", "eoie", "03:18 the five heal programs (stdout_line 20, number-text 17 + tail 6, stderr_line 11, eoie_jobs host 4 rules) still apply on the emulated post-R tree and form next-train stage S4 (scratch next-train\\apply-stage-S4.ps1, launch/build derived). Emulating the full chain HIJK..R + S1..S4 gives 37 ok, 0 FAIL. The post-block whole-train check regenerates and cargo-checks every crate they touch plus dependents before anything launches.")
inl note_of_kit_lib_reuse_39 () = Note ("KIT-LIB-REUSE", 39u32, "2026-10-29T23:23Z", "main", "10-29 19:23 main, fill-all-task-fields: estimate set to 1122 min by the epic rule (the sum of each open child's estimate x (100 - progress)%, all children estimated): EOIE-HEAL-LIB-LINK 24, EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET 24, EOIE-HEAL-EDIT-HOOK 3, EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY 99, EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION 972; the other 2 children are Done. Re-derive it when a child's estimate or progress moves. Epic progress stays at its owner's value.")
