inl kit_heal_boundary () = Task ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", "One thin OS boundary package for eoie (process, fs, env, clock, path) as named one-expression primitives, x-style (glyphs/wire/net); rust_std_string becomes calls into sm'/am' and is then deleted; generic gaps go to lib/spiral with backend_switch and lib tests", Story, P1, D4, 45u32, Planned, "", "kit,lib,heal,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_heal_boundary () = Planning ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_1 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 1u32, "2026-10-22T02:57Z", "eoie", "22:57 after EOIE-HEAL-LIB-LINK; the boundary is the only place a host macro may live.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_2 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 2u32, "2026-10-22T03:36Z", "eoie", "23:36 design input from a census of eoie's directory walks: 55 read_dir sites (47 plain listings, 6 recursive walks, 2 extension-filtered listings) in 39 files, none link-aware. One boundary module gives: entries <dir> -> list of a typed entry (FileEntry name | DirEntry name | LinkEntry name, never followed), a recursive walk built in Spiral over entries with a skip predicate (target, .cache, links), and an extension filter in Spiral. Host code stays one read_dir primitive. Scanners first (census, standards, source topology, grep/search, do read/facts/lab), then the rest; this unblocks EOIE-HEAL-LIB-LINK. Also eoie_job_gate sits at 1000 lines after tonight's gate fix: split the slot queue into its own crate before the next gate change.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_3 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 3u32, "2026-10-22T04:54Z", "eoie", "00:54 rust_std_string retirement map (89 of 637 eoie .spi files open it; counts are upper bounds, same-named locals included): concat5 1164 uses/134 files -> ++# chains (open sm'_operators); equals 185/46 -> =; replace 162/44 -> sm'.replace from into text (argument order flips); contains 134/42 -> LIB GAP (sm' has no contains; index_of >= 0 meanwhile); starts_with 76/39 and ends_with 34/14 -> sm'.starts_with/ends_with value text (order flips); trim 46/23 -> sm'.trim; pipe_member 28/16, pipe_lookup 3, pipe_index 1 -> LIB GAP (delimited membership, blocked on SPIRAL-LIB-AM-ANY); trim_end_matches 4/3 -> LIB GAP (suffix trim; sm'.trim_end takes chars). Order: add the three gaps to lib/spiral first (backend_switch + tests), then rewrite crate by crate with the argument-order flips checked by each crate's tests; measure concat5 -> ++# generated size on one crate first (concat5 is one host call; a ++# chain may inline more lines against the 1000 gate).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_4 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 4u32, "2026-10-22T05:05Z", "eoie", "01:05 correction from main: sm'.contains already exists (all 8 backends), so contains (134 uses) maps today, not a lib gap; my 00:5x grep missed it. sm'.listed separator item text and sm'.trim_end_suffix suffix text are drafted by main as portable compositions with lib tests (rust, fsharp, gleam) and gate after the am'.any gate (main-helpers-gate); they land in tree lib/spiral and ship in main's next pack. The retirement map now has no open lib gaps once that gate passes.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_5 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 5u32, "2026-10-22T05:36Z", "eoie", "01:36 lib gap 4 (sent to main): lib/spiral env has no runtime environment read for Rust (environ_get is Python-only, get_environment_variable_comptime is option_env!). eoie has 132 std::env::var(_os) host reads that would move onto a portable env.var key : option string; release E (job author from EOIE_AUTHOR) needs it first.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_6 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 6u32, "2026-10-22T05:38Z", "eoie", "01:38 correction from main: lib/spiral env.get_environment_variable key : string (env.spi:53) reads at runtime on Rust, F#, Zig, Gleam, Lua, TypeScript and Python ('' when unset), so eoie's 132 std::env::var(_os) host reads can move onto it today and release E can record the job author from EOIE_AUTHOR. Main adds env.try_get_environment_variable : option string after release ABC ends (ABC reads lib/spiral, so main won't change its inputs mid-run). Second lib function I wrongly reported missing tonight (after sm'.contains): my lookups listed '^inl name' lines instead of searching the lib for the operation.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_7 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 7u32, "2026-10-22T08:33Z", "eoie", "04:33 census of eoie host macros (live src, read-only): 1500 macros in 123 packages. By surface: text ops 517 (split/trim/parse/format: lib sm' territory, not OS), other 387, fs 161, cross-crate extern calls 153 (legitimate boundaries), env 110, path 86, process 63, clock 23. Most-copied bodies across packages: args().nth(n) 20 pkgs, number to Rc<str> 20+18, args().count() 15, args().skip(2).count() 14, len() as i32 12, trim().parse::<u64>().unwrap_or(0) 12, the record decoder 10 (eoie_do_records in E absorbs it), Path::is_dir/is_file 9+9. Lib already covers: sm'.obj_to_string (numbers), sm'.length, file_system.path_buf_is_dir/is_file. Lib gaps (offered to main): command-line arguments (count, nth) in env, and a decimal parse returning option in sm'. Plan: the boundary package should hold only fs/env/process/clock/path primitives; the 517 text macros go to sm' instead (heal-crate-style mapping per recurring body). Top packages by macro count: eoie_jobs 62, eoie_cli_harness 51, eoie_machine_watch 47, eoie_do_edit 44, eoie_table_query 42.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_8 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 8u32, "2026-10-22T08:34Z", "eoie", "04:34 macro-to-lib mapping table for a future heal-macros tool (each row needs its semantics proven by a preview before use): (1) Path::new(x).is_dir() / .is_file() : bool -> file_system.path_buf_is_dir|is_file (file_system.new_path_buf (sm'.to_std_string x)): same std calls (PathBuf::from instead of Path::new), safe. (2) x.len() as i32 -> sm'.length x: UNVERIFIED, sm'.length delegates to core sm.length; must confirm it is byte length on Rust (str::len) before mapping, else non-ASCII text changes. (3) Rc::<str>::from(x.to_string()) -> sm'.obj_to_string x: type-directed in lib (string is identity, numbers via format); only for numeric x, which a text tool cannot see: map by hand per site or via a typed helper. (4) args().nth/count/skip(2).count and trim().parse::<u64>().unwrap_or(0): wait for main's lib answer (offered 04:33). (5) the record decoder: done by eoie_do_records (E).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_9 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 9u32, "2026-10-22T08:46Z", "eoie", "04:46 correction from main: the decimal parse is NOT a lib gap. convert.try_convert : string -> option u (Rust arm (x).trim().parse::<u64>().ok(), plus Gleam/Lua/F#/Python/C/Delphi) with optionm'.default_value 0u64 reproduces the unwrap_or(0) helpers exactly (my census searched sm'/env/file_system only and missed convert.spi; lib-first means searching the whole lib for the operation). Slice apply-heal-decimal-parse.ps1 (in wave E2, after the heal loop) rewrites the trimmed helper bodies in 13 packages with the 950 guard (untrimmed sites in bundle_retention and dev_model stay: try_convert trims, so they would get more lenient). argv: main drafted env.command_line_argument_count () : i32, try_command_line_argument (index) : option string and command_line_argument index (index 0 = first user argument); mappings args().nth(n) -> try_command_line_argument (n - 1), args().count() -> command_line_argument_count () + 1, args().skip(2).count() -> command_line_argument_count () - 1; lands after its gate (before 05:30 or after 06:30).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_10 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 10u32, "2026-10-22T08:47Z", "eoie", "04:47 mapping (2) verified in the compiler source: core sm.length is !!!!StringLength, which spiral_compiler.fs lowers to .len() on Rust (line 164419) and to UTF-8 GetByteCount on F# (163422), i.e. byte length on both, the same as str::len(). So x.len() as i32 -> sm'.length x is exact when x is a string parameter; it must NOT be applied to .len() on vectors (record_list, token_list, hunk_list: those stay boundary primitives or move to am'.length on typed arrays).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_11 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 11u32, "2026-10-22T08:49Z", "eoie", "04:49 slice apply-heal-string-length.ps1 (wave E2): the 7 string byte-length helpers (eoie_cli_harness byte_count, eoie_guide/eoie_memory_model/eoie_table_logs/eoie_table_query text_length, eoie_table_measures text_bytes, workspace_primitives byte_len) become sm'.length over their string parameter; only string-typed parameters match, vector .len() macros are untouched. Generated code should be the same .len() call.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_12 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 12u32, "2026-10-22T08:52Z", "eoie", "04:52 slice apply-heal-path-kind.ps1 (wave E2): the 11 Path::new(x).is_dir()/is_file() helpers over a string parameter become file_system.path_buf_is_dir|is_file (file_system.new_path_buf (sm'.to_std_string x)); rule written before applying: this mapping grows each inl call site by about 2 Rust lines (String + PathBuf instead of a borrowed Path), so its guard is 900 lines instead of 950 (skips agile_todo_scan at 946). 8 packages heal on the E tree; the guard reads live sizes at release time.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_13 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 13u32, "2026-10-22T08:57Z", "eoie", "04:57 mapping (3) narrowed: 37 helpers turn an INTEGER-typed parameter into text via Rc::from(x.to_string()); lib sm'.obj_to_string routes non-nominal types to format_debug_real ({:?}), identical to Display for integers but NOT for floats (1.0 vs 1), so the one f64 site is excluded. Slice apply-heal-integer-text.ps1 drafted (matches integer parameter types only, 950 guard) and kept OUT of the waves until a compile confirms the Rust arm a plain integer reaches is {:?} (the nested typecase in sm'_real.spir is not conclusive by reading); the CLI notebooks would catch any printing change.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_14 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 14u32, "2026-10-22T08:58Z", "eoie", "04:58 argv mapping prepared for main's env API (not landed yet): 18 helpers wrap args().nth(i).unwrap_or_default(). nth counts the program name as 0, while env.try_command_line_argument starts at the first user argument, so the body becomes optionm'.default_value empty-string (env.try_command_line_argument (i - 1i32)) and is exact only when i >= 1. No call passes a literal 0; 22 calls pass a computed index (e.g. index + 1i32 while walking flags), which a slice must check by eye (they start at 2 or 3 in the verb parsers) before mapping. Slice to be written when env.spi lands.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_15 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 15u32, "2026-10-22T09:00Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:00 main: lib env.spi gained command_line_argument_count () : i32, command_line_argument (index : i32) : string, try_command_line_argument (index : i32) : option string (index 0 = first user argument; Rust, F#, TypeScript, Python arms), landed EB6944E216A8EB3A after a 4 of 4 gate on a copy. Decimal parse needs nothing new: convert.try_convert : string -> option u64 already trims and parses on every backend.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_16 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 16u32, "2026-10-22T09:03Z", "eoie", "05:03 main landed env.command_line_argument_count / command_line_argument / try_command_line_argument in tree lib (index 0 = first user argument; gate 4/4 on rust, fsharp, python, typescript). Slice apply-heal-argv.ps1 (wave E2, after path kind): nth(i) helpers -> optionm'.default_value empty (env.try_command_line_argument (i - 1i32)) (all 22 computed call indices start at the verb parsers' offsets 2 or 3, none can be 0); args().count() helpers -> command_line_argument_count () + 1i32; args().skip(2).count() helpers -> user count minus 1 clamped at 0 (skip(2) never goes negative). Dry-run: 31 packages heal, the 3 near-gate crates skip. Risk for E2's preview: workspace_primitives has no crate of its own; its inl argument helpers expand inside consumer crates, near-gate ones included, which the per-package guard cannot see, so the preview must check every consumer. 61 other args() shapes (collect, skip(2).collect, any) remain for a later slice.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_17 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 17u32, "2026-10-22T09:10Z", "eoie", "05:10 fs census (161 fs macros, few repeats): read_to_string(..).unwrap_or_default() in 5+3 packages, create_dir_all(..).is_ok() in 4, write(..).is_ok() in 3, remove_dir_all/remove_file treated as success when the path is gone in 3+3. Lib file_system.read_all_text / write_all_text are NOT drop-in: their Rust arms unwrap (panic on error), while eoie needs total versions (empty text, or a success bool). Lib candidates for main's queue, low priority (about 21 sites): try_read_all_text : string -> option string, and write/create_dir/remove variants returning bool or a result. Until then these stay boundary primitives; the bigger fs wins are per-package boundary consolidation, not lib mapping.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_18 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 18u32, "2026-10-22T18:11Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 14:11 mapping (3), integer to text, traced through lib source: sm'.obj_to_string x for a plain integer type takes obj_to_string_rust (show_composite_real is false), then sm'_real.spir obj_to_string_rust_real (not char, string or nominal), then format_debug_real's Rust arm (no option, tuple, array, list, seq or record case matches), then format_debug_other_rust, which for prim_type_is emits Rc::<str>::from(format!({:?}, x)). Debug and Display agree for i8..u64, so Rc::from(x.to_string()) -> sm'.obj_to_string x is exact for integer parameters; the f64 site stays excluded ({:?} prints 1.0, Display prints 1). apply-heal-integer-text.ps1 can join a wave after one preview compile confirms the emitted line in a generated .rs.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_19 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 19u32, "2026-10-22T22:10Z", "eoie-lane", "18:10 sizing input (text classification of the 1,502 live .spi lines carrying a host macro; a line can fall in several classes). Text work (Rc wraps, split, trim, replace, lines, lowercase, format) 670; numeric casts and parses 287; filesystem 262; collections (Vec, maps, RefCell, iter) 210; console io 138; env and args 137; process 79; clock 47; regex 31; unclassified 374. Text, numeric and collections (~60%) are not OS surface at all: they are lib/spiral's job (sm', convert, am', listm'), so the heal waves remove them. The real boundary is the fs + env + process + clock + console set (~660 lines, many duplicates across packages), which is what one OS boundary package must offer as named primitives. That is the target size for its first cut, not 1,502.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_20 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 20u32, "2026-10-22T22:11Z", "eoie-lane", "18:11 duplication measured: 491 single-quoted host macros touch an OS surface; with splice names normalized they are 338 distinct bodies. The top repeats are println (27x), argv nth (20x), argv count (15x and 15x with skip 2), eprintln (12x), is_dir (9x), so ~10 named primitives (stdout_line, stderr_line, argument n, argument_count, is_directory, file_text, ...) cover ~120 of the 491 uses at once. Many of the 338 are one-off composite blobs (read + parse + format in one macro), which split into a primitive plus lib code when their package is healed. First cut of the boundary package: the top ~25 bodies by count, then the rest package by package with the heal waves.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_21 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 21u32, "2026-10-23T12:32Z", "eoie", "08:32 scope decision by measurement (no compile): the top repeated OS bodies from the 18:11 count (println 27x, argv nth 20x, argv count 30x, eprintln 12x, is_dir 9x, ~100 uses) all have lib equivalents in the live lib today: console.write_line, console.write_error_line (main's 04:40 landing), env.try_command_line_argument, env.command_line_argument_count, file_system.directory_exists, plus file_exists and read_all_text. The packages healed tonight (eoie_crate_gate, eoie_table_text, eoie_notebook_progress, accept-review) use exactly these with no host macro. So the boundary package's scope shrinks to what lib/spiral lacks: process spawning with creation flags and job objects (eoie_jobs, eoie_job_host: CreateProcessW, parent attribute), process sampling (sysinfo), file times beyond last_write_ms, OS-specific job-object limits. Everything else heals by switching to the lib call package by package (the heal waves), not into a new eoie package. Next concrete cut: name those few primitives in one eoie_os package (one-expression each) and point eoie_job_host's launch at it.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_22 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 22u32, "2026-10-23T13:33Z", "eoie", "09:33 next cut drafted for release L, after start-under-shell: scratch start-under-shell/apply-host-uses-os-launch.ps1 replaces eoie_job_host's own 40-line CreateProcessW block (as HP lands it) with one call into eoie_os_launch::eoie_shell_parented_start, plus the Cargo dependency, so the job host and eoie process start-under-shell share one implementation. Dry run on HP's raw host_run.spi applies. Also verified: host_run.spi formatted by 5e equals the live file, so HP's landing needs no re-format (main's 5e pass found the other 46 eoie files unchanged too).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_23 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 23u32, "2026-10-24T00:03Z", "eoie", "20:03 eoie: census snapshot of the live tree, post-GE2 landing (eoie standards --census src, 381 packages, 13 s): host-macro 721, wide-host-macro 187, let-block 175, rc-wrap 527, with host macros in 116 of 381 packages. Ranked by host + 3 x wide + 2 x let-block, the boundary work pays most in: eoie_jobs (39/14/11), eoie_cli_harness (24/13/14, test-only), eoie_do_edit (18/12/15, at 976 lines, so it needs a crate split first), rust_std_process (22/8/7, already a boundary-style package to absorb), eoie_do_process (14/9/7), eoie_do_facts, eoie_do_read, eoie_machine_windows (20/4/4), eoie_do_lab, agile_memory_links. Rule for picking the next boundary slice: the highest-ranked package whose crates sit under 950 lines, so eoie_jobs first (its blobs cover process liveness, file reads and env). Its first slice moves the process_alive, parent_pid and relaunched_as blobs into the boundary package's process module, as named one-expression primitives. Baseline kept for the ratchet: next session compares against these totals.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_24 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 24u32, "2026-10-24T00:06Z", "eoie", "20:06 eoie: first eoie_jobs heal written as an eoie do program, the first slice authored that way from the start (scratch heal-jobs-host/heal-jobs-host.do, 5 replace-once rules in one edit block with expect files 1 replacements 5). argument becomes env.try_command_line_argument (index - 1), the same mapping as eoie_do's host. decimal_i32 becomes convert.try_convert with default -1. decimal_text becomes sm'.format. stdout_line and stderr_line become console.write_line and write_error_line. Applied to a copy of the real post-P eoie_jobs: ok files 1 replacements 5 in 4 ms. jobs.rs is at 759 lines, well under the gate. The rest of host.spi (process_alive, parent_pid, container and job-object calls, newest_directories, supervisor_executable) are true OS calls and go to the boundary package. Typecheck tomorrow; it ships in the first release after the train, since HIJK..P all touch eoie_jobs.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_25 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 25u32, "2026-10-24T23:43Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 180m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D4 at 30%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_26 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 26u32, "2026-10-27T19:31Z", "kit", "kit 15:3x: env inventory for the boundary, read from the post-TRAIN tree. 27 std::env macros outside rust_std_env, in 20 packages, reduce to 7 shapes: (1) argument at an absolute index, args().nth(i): kit_cli_model, kit_evidence, kit_jobs. NOT the same as rust_std_env.argument_owned, which counts after skip(2), so each call site needs its index shifted by 2: a per-site change, not a regex. (2) argument count, args().skip(k).count(): agile_task_creation, agile_task_listing, kit_agile_routes, kit_machine_watch. (3) flag present, args().skip(k).any(== flag): agile_memory_links, agile_todo_scan, kit_agile_mutation, kit_evidence, kit_read_query, kit_standards. (4) value after a flag, skip_while(!= flag).nth(1): kit_experiments, kit_machine_windows (kit_lint_macros already does it in Spiral via value_after). (5) variable or empty: agile_lease_terms, kit_command_line (rust_std_env.variable_or_empty fits as is). (6) host facts: temp_dir, EXE_SUFFIX, current_exe (kit_cli_check, inspection_negative, kit_jobs). (7) set_var SPIRAL_HEAVY_TICKET (kit_job_slot). Plan: rust_std_env gains four named one-expression primitives, argument_at (absolute), argument_count_after k, flag_present k flag and value_after flag, plus host_temp_dir, exe_suffix and current_exe_is. Then each package migrates in its own slice, proven by its CLI notebook (shapes 1-4 change argv parsing, so a proof must cover flags in every position). Shape 5 can move now with no index risk: 2 sites.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_27 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 27u32, "2026-10-27T19:35Z", "kit", "kit 15:4x: shape 5 (variable or empty) is drafted as a lib-first slice, staged for the release after TRAIN: scratch clean/heal-boundary/env-variables-to-lib.do. agile_lease_terms.environment_text and kit_command_line.pathext become env.get_environment_variable, whose Rust arm is the very expression they inlined (Rc::<str>::from(std::env::var(..).unwrap_or_default())), so behavior is identical by construction. It is a :~, so it is emitted once per crate. Both packages already reference spiral-. Compiled on the post-TRAIN rehearsal, before vs after: agile_lease_terms 675 -> 679 and kit_command_line 564 -> 568 (+4 each, the shared fn). Two host macros fewer; the other six shapes wait for the four rust_std_env primitives in note 26.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_28 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 28u32, "2026-10-27T20:11Z", "kit", "kit 16:1x: shapes 1-5 of note 26 are done or staged. Shapes 3 and 5 (flag present; variable or empty) ride TRAIN as next-train steps 5i and 5j, already applied to the live tree. Shapes 1, 2 and 4 are drafted against the post-train live tree for the release after TRAIN (scratch clean/heal-boundary: argument-at.do, argument-count.do, argument-after-flag.do). Each adds one named one-expression primitive to rust_std_env (argument_at, absolute index; argument_count_after skip; argument_after_flag), with exactly the expression the call sites inlined, so behavior is unchanged by construction. Package edges added: kit_cli_model, kit_jobs, kit_machine_watch, kit_experiments, kit_machine_windows. Compiled on a copy of the live tree: agile_task_creation 958, agile_task_listing 978, kit_machine_watch 932, kit_evidence 428, kit_experiments 787, kit_machine_windows 964, kit_job_host 991, kit_experiment_analysis 992 and kit_cli 971 are all unchanged; kit_agile_routes 670 -> 686 (sm'.show for the operand count). Left as is: kit_jobs.arguments_from (a newline-joined row protocol, which goes to typed columns, not the boundary); temp_dir (file_system.get_temp_path strips the trailing separator that std::env::temp_dir keeps, so it is not equivalent); EXE_SUFFIX (test harness only); current_exe (one site, with an empty-string edge). 14 env macros leave non-boundary packages in all.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_29 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 29u32, "2026-10-28T13:22Z", "eoie", "09:2x kit: shape 7 of note 26 (set_var), lib-first. The one site is kit_job_slot.ticket_adopted (unsafe std::env::set_var for SPIRAL_HEAVY_TICKET). lib env.spi has get_environment_variable on every backend but no setter, so the primitive goes to lib first: scratch clean/heal-boundary/lib-set-env.do adds set_environment_variable (var, value) with Rust (unsafe std::env::set_var, the expression the kit site inlines), F# (System.Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable), TypeScript (process.env[var] = value) and Gleam (envoy.set, the module get already imports) arms; other targets failwith by name, since Lua 5.1 has no setenv. Its test block sets a probe variable and reads it back through get_environment_variable on gleam, fsharp, rust and typescript. Then kit-ticket-adopted.do makes the kit site env.set_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_HEAVY_TICKET\" name (kit_job_slot already references spiral-). Both dry-run clean (lib against the live lib, kit against the TRAIN4 copy). Order: gate the lib slice, land it in the 13:10 window, then the kit line rides TRAIN4 or the release after it. Shape 6 stays as note 28 decided (temp_dir is not equivalent; EXE_SUFFIX is test-only; current_exe is one site with an empty-string edge). With this, every std::env macro outside rust_std_env is migrated or deliberately kept.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_30 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 30u32, "2026-10-30T19:16Z", "kit", "10-30 15:2x kit (EOIE-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE): the frozen GPT-era backlog kit/state/agile.spi maps MAPPING-FILESYSTEM-TRANSACTION, PHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING to this item. Their remaining intent is this item's scope; no separate work is carried over. Table: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\legacy-state-triage.tsv.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_31 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 31u32, "2026-10-31T15:12Z", "kit", "10-31 11:0x kit: STATE, measured on the live tree (probes excluded). (1) The env slice is DONE: lib env.spi has set_environment_variable (env.spi:79, with its test at :117), and kit_job_slot.ticket_adopted calls env.set_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_HEAVY_TICKET\" name, so n31's two drafts landed. (2) rust_std_string: 298 refs in 44 files outside its package: concat5 121, equals 53, bare model 48, contains 21, replace 14, pipe_member 11, starts_with 11, ends_with 8. (3) read_dir: 65 sites in 50 files outside rust_std_fs (kit_bundle_retention 4, contracts_entry 4, kit_jobs 3, parallel_search_contract 3; EOIE-READ-QUERY's --depth needs the last of these). NEXT SLICE, chosen for risk: the mechanical string respells (equals -> '=', and contains/starts_with/ends_with/replace -> the sm' functions): 107 sites with one-to-one semantics, checked per package with the census ratchet and an in-place regen with cargo check. concat5 (121) waits: it is the size-saving form the style hook explicitly allows near the 1000-line gate, so respelling it to ++# can push crates over (KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS headroom first). Then the read_dir boundary primitive (n2's typed entries list plus a Spiral walk).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_32 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 32u32, "2026-10-31T15:44Z", "kit", "10-31 11:4x kit: n31's NEXT SLICE is DONE in the tree (unstaged); VERIFICATION is queued until TRAIN6 frees the CPU. 112 one-to-one string respells across 9 files: agile_todo_model/model.spi 66, command_spec_domain 8, agile_todo_scan 8, agile_task_text 7, agile_todo_model/roots 6, agile_task_next/ranking 6, kit_machine_watch_model 5, agile_note_model 3, agile_task_creation 3. Rules: rust_std_string.model.equals a b -> (a = b); starts_with/ends_with/contains text x -> sm'.<f> x text (sm' takes the needle FIRST); replace text from into -> sm'.replace from into text. Applied with a scratch rewriter that only touches sites whose arguments are whole tokens (string literals as atoms, identifiers, balanced groups), plus two passes for nested calls and multi-line forms (split-line equals becomes an infix '<a>' line and '= <b>'). The few multi-line sites were fixed and read by hand. Every diff hunk was reviewed for argument order. Census ratchet ok on all 8 packages. agile_task_text was rebaselined for ONE pre-existing host macro, the kit_agile_records_unchanged crate call added 10-31 00:3x for KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES, which the respell's ratchet run surfaced. VERIFY NEXT (after TRAIN6): notebooks for agile_todo_model/model.spi, agile_task_next/ranking.spi, kit_machine_watch_model/model.spi and command_spec_domain/model.spi, then an in-place regen with cargo check of the 9 owners plus their dependents (crate sizes checked against the gate), or let TRAIN7's full regen and notebooks carry it. rust_std_string after this slice: concat5 121 and pipe_member 11 remain, plus the bare 'model' opens.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_33 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 33u32, "2026-10-31T17:54Z", "kit", "10-31 13:5x kit: the node verification (mirror kit-verify, job-1793468530547-kit-verify-batch2, run while the box gap is main's) CAUGHT A BREAK in n32's respell. agile_task_next/ranking.spi went red 6/6 with 'ETY-UnboundVariable: Unbound term variable: sm''. In the definition: spi_escaped' (agile_task_text/model.spi). Cause: three respelled packages never referenced the lib: agile_task_text, agile_note_model and agile_task_creation had no 'spiral-' in package.spiproj (pre-contract packages; AGENTS requires every package to reference the lib). Fixed by adding spiral- to all three, the contract fix rather than a revert. Passed already: agile_todo_model/model.spi 11/11 and agile_todo_model/roots.spi 2/2. The rest of the batch is running; ranking and the agile_note_model module get rerun on a re-synced mirror. agile_task_creation is at 990/1000 lines, so its crate size must be checked at the next regen. RULE for respells into sm': first confirm the package lists spiral- (the census LibReferenced row), or the respell compiles nowhere.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_34 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 34u32, "2026-10-31T18:22Z", "kit", "10-31 14:2x kit: pipe_member (11 sites) is scoped and deferred. Every site tests membership in a '|'-joined CONSTANT (\"--help|-h\", \"spi|spir\", hash_family_names (), vendor_directory_names (), proxy_*_route_names ()), which is an encoded row by the census's own definition. The typed fix turns each constant into a list literal and tests membership with a lib list function. The two hosts are library packages inlined into crates at the gate (agile_todo_model -> agile_todo_scan 993/1000; command_spec_domain 889), and list literals generate more Rust than one split, so this waits for the same headroom work as concat5 (KIT-HAND-CRATE-UNITS: split agile_todo_scan first). Node verification of n32 so far: 11/13 touched-module notebooks pass on mirror kit-verify; the 2 reds (ranking, agile_note_model) are the lib-less packages fixed in n33 and are being rerun.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_35 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 35u32, "2026-10-31T18:24Z", "kit", "10-31 14:3x kit: NODE VERIFICATION COMPLETE, 13/13 touched-module notebooks green. Box CPU was reserved for main's Cells/compiler gap, so they ran on the node: mirror kit-verify (spiral fd70dccf + kit 7ac6aa05 working trees, REMOTE-SYNC-OK digests). batch2 (job-1793468530547): agile_todo_model/model 11/11, agile_todo_model/roots 2/2, kit_machine_watch_model 7/7, command_spec_domain 2/2, kit_lint_shadows_core/shadows 6/6, kit_lint_opens/opens 1/1, kit_do_file_steps/steps 1/1, kit_log_counts/count_scan 4/4, kit_notebook_progress/model 5/5, kit_do_program/program 8/8, kit_standards/rules 8/8. It also caught n33's break: ranking and agile_note_model red (lib-less packages). batch3 (job-1793470794683), after spiral- was added: agile_task_next/ranking 6/6, agile_note_model/model 1/1. Tool: kit/scripts/notebook-batch.ps1 -Module a,b,c (new, unstaged) runs run_notebook serially with the spiral next to the kit tree (SPIRAL_CELLS_LIB pinned to it), so it works the same on a node mirror and on the box. Its comma-joined -Module handling exists because string[] arguments reach the node's cmd as one string (batch1 failed exactly so). Still to verify only with a built candidate (TRAIN7): the CLI notebooks (sequences_cli --count, standards_cli subfolders, roots_cli Done refusal) and the acceptance rows for copy-literal and --opens.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_36 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 36u32, "2026-11-01T22:59Z", "main", "11-01 19:0x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). Lib targets for this item's SWITCH list now exist as filed items, and one n21 assumption is corrected: date_time.now is not a replacement for workspace_primitives unix_ms/ms_since (it returns a chrono naive local date_time and pulls the chrono crate); LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK adds typed unix_now_ms/ms_since to date_time for that. Related per-package copies outside rust_std_*/workspace_primitives, which this item does not list, are filed with exact sites: LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE (argument/argument_count/argument_owned in ~45 packages under 3 argv offsets, stdout_line/stderr_line, decimal_u64/decimal_of, own_pid; deletes the rust_std_env argument family), LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT (11 read-or-empty copies vs file_system.read_text_or_empty), LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS (i32_text/u64_text/decimal_text/count_text, padded, lines_joined, unquoted), LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE (kit_receipt local_offset_minutes, three host macros inlining Hinnant civil math, agile_note_model civil_of_days). Either lane may land them; they say they ride this item if kit prefers.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_37 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 37u32, "2026-11-03T07:34Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 33 h ago by main, progress kept at 45%. Resume from that note:  padded, lines_joined, unquoted), LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE (kit_receipt local_offset_minutes, three host macros inlining Hinnant civil math, agile_note_model civil_of_days). Either lane may land them; they say they ride this item if kit prefers.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_38 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 38u32, "2026-11-06T11:26Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_heal_boundary_39 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", 39u32, "2026-11-09T05:42Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:5x rig MEASURED the rust_std_string retirement: 11 definitions; 43 packages list it in package.spiproj, 34 files open it with :< rust_std_string.model; 127 qualified call sites across 6 functions (concat5 104, pipe_member 12, trim 8, pipe_index, pipe_lookup, trim_end_matches 1 each) plus unqualified calls in the 34 opening files: 430 concat5 lines in all, of which 179 pass only atoms (string literals or plain names) and can become a ++# chain mechanically; the other 251 have parenthesised arguments and need an application-aware rewrite (or a hand pass). agile_task_views keeps its own local concat5 (a ++# b ++# c ++# d ++# e), the shape every call should inline to. trim maps to sm'.trim. PLAN (TRAIN43, one fleet-sized respell, so sample diff first per mass-respell-show-sample-first): (1) the 179 atom-only concat5 calls -> chains, dropping the empty-string arguments; (2) trim and trim_end_matches -> sm'; (3) pipe_member/index/lookup -> named lib functions (check sm' and listm' first, else add to lib/spiral with a backend_switch and lib test); (4) the parenthesised 251 by a Spiral-parse-based rewrite; (5) remove rust_std_string from 43 spiprojs and delete the package; census host-statement counts must only fall. Next step: (1) with a 10-file sample diff.")
inl generated_output_modules () = Task ("GENERATED-OUTPUT-MODULES", "SUPERSEDED by SPIRAL-SHARED-SPECIALIZATIONS (not delivered): Compiler: write one entry's generated output as several files, each under 1,000 lines, so the user's 10-21 rule (1,000 lines per file in every language but Spiral) can hold for generated code: Gleam as granular packages, each with its own gleam.toml and path deps, built in parallel (SIM-GLEAM-PACKAGES; module parts of one package were drift, flagged 10-24), Rust as mod files inside one crate, the same for other backends; the split follows the function graph (helpers and specializations grouped by their callers), with a stable order so outputs stay diffable", Story, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "X-PARALLEL-BUILD,XSIM-GLEAM-SPLIT-BENCH", "compiler,codegen,gleam,rust,gate,main", "current", "current")
