inl note_of_kit_window_held_marker_6 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-HELD-MARKER", 6u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_window_held_marker_7 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-HELD-MARKER", 7u32, "2026-11-06T11:32Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-WINDOW-HELD-MARKER (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_window_held_marker_8 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-HELD-MARKER", 8u32, "2026-11-11T00:05Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:1x rig: the HEAVY half is written (unstaged; base archived at kit\\archive\\window-held-marker-bases-20261110). The window half already shipped (rig_window_run exports RIG_WINDOW_HELD and KIT_WINDOW_HELD to its child). Now rig_machine_windows/windows.spi heavy_wrapper writes $env:RIG_HEAVY_HELD = $env:KIT_HEAVY_HELD = '1' INSIDE the Invoke-Heavy block, so the marker exists only while the slot is held and a nested --heavy request in a wrapper can see it and skip waiting on itself. The function moved off the legacy concat5 to lib ++# in the same change (AGENTS.md: touching a legacy function migrates it). The windows_cli CLI test now also asserts the marker in the written heavy-wrapper.ps1; that test drives the kit binary, so its proof is TRAIN44 or the next train. NEXT STEP: once a train installs it, a wrapper that already holds a heavy slot reads RIG_HEAVY_HELD and runs inline instead of re-requesting (the spiral heavy.ps1 Invoke-Heavy honoring it is the compiler side: ask compiler).")
inl note_of_kit_window_held_marker_9 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-HELD-MARKER", 9u32, "2026-11-11T00:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:1x rig correction + markers: the heavy-marker edit landed after TRAIN44's 19:43 snapshot, so it rides TRAIN45 (not TRAIN44). DoD: a job started with --heavy runs its command with RIG_HEAVY_HELD=1 and KIT_HEAVY_HELD=1 set only inside the held slot, proven by the windows_cli test reading the written wrapper and by one live heavy job printing the variable. TYPEFEATURES: none needed; the wrapper is boundary text at the OS edge (a PowerShell script), built from lib ++# pieces.")
inl kit_pages_verify () = Task ("KIT-PAGES-VERIFY", "eoie gh-pages.yml verifies its own deploy like spiral/polyglot/dice/alphabet: the push job writes GITHUB_SHA to gh-pages/_deploy.txt before peaceiris, then a pwsh step polls https://i574n.github.io/eoie/_deploy.txt (cache-busted, up to 6 min) until it equals GITHUB_SHA and checks the index's README section and viewport meta", TaskKind, P3, D1, 50u32, Planned, "", "kit,ci,pages,team:rig", "current", "current")
