inl note_of_kit_pages_verify_1 () = Note ("KIT-PAGES-VERIFY", 1u32, "2026-10-22T06:29Z", "eoie", "02:29 from main (TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO's last row): copy the last 3 steps of spiral/.github/workflows/gh-pages.yml; no new uses:, so actions.lock stays valid. Edit after release ABC releases its tree lease.")
inl note_of_kit_pages_verify_2 () = Note ("KIT-PAGES-VERIFY", 2u32, "2026-10-22T06:30Z", "eoie", "02:30 slice ready (apply-pages-verify.ps1 + pages-verify-step.yml, in the night carry folder): writes GITHUB_SHA to gh-pages/_deploy.txt before peaceiris and appends spiral's 'verify the deploy is live' step verbatim; dry run keeps 8 uses: lines (actions.lock valid). eoie publishes through spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1, the same generator whose index passes spiral's README/viewport check. Apply after ABC releases its lease; the first eoie push proves it.")
inl note_of_kit_pages_verify_3 () = Note ("KIT-PAGES-VERIFY", 3u32, "2026-10-22T10:02Z", "eoie", "06:02 applied to the live workflow at 04:0x (uncommitted). main later added force_orphan: true to the same peaceiris step (TREE-PAGES-V2 step c). The two compose: the orphan push publishes only the current gh-pages/ folder, which includes the _deploy.txt written just before it, so the verify step still compares the live _deploy.txt with GITHUB_SHA. uses: count still 8 (no actions.lock in eoie). First real check: the next push to main.")
inl note_of_kit_pages_verify_4 () = Note ("KIT-PAGES-VERIFY", 4u32, "2026-10-22T20:10Z", "eoie-lane", "16:10 no push since a831bad (10-19), so the verify step has not run yet. The push job runs even after a red build ('needs: build' with 'if: !cancelled()'; pages-build-deployment succeeded after each red run since 10-18), so the next push exercises the verify step whatever the build result. The red build itself is EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW.")
