inl kit_do_verb_family () = Task ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", "one program_verb union in eoie_do_model names every eoie do verb and its program_family", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "KIT-DO-RECORDS", "kit,lib-reuse,heal,domain,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_do_verb_family () = Planning ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_1 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 1u32, "2026-10-22T07:19Z", "eoie", "03:19 design from the night census: eoie_do/decode.spi already has union program_family (Edits Reads Facts Runs Writes Git Jobs Labs), but which verb belongs to which family lives in 4 copies: Rust string arrays inside has_fact/has_run/has_write/has_git/has_job/has_lab macros, eoie_do_program's 27-word pipe table (query_verb_known), do write's read-verb list (healed tonight to reuse query_verb) and a files special case (files with a fact flag counts as Facts). Shape: union program_verb in eoie_do_model (one case per verb, query_verb nested as ReadVerb : query_verb so do read keeps its union), let program_verb_named (reflection, let not inl: 27 cases), inl program_verb_family (match, one arm per case), and eoie_do's dispatch classifies each record once with a family priority list instead of 7 macro scans. Gate risk: a 27-case reflection fold is ~160 Rust lines; do_program and eoie_do are small (check sizes first), so place the lookup there, never in a near-gate do crate. Accept: preview 0 errors, eoie do one-call notebooks unchanged, every touched crate under 950.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_2 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 2u32, "2026-10-22T07:59Z", "eoie", "03:59 design refined by a size check: eoie_do_program.rs is at 948 lines, so a 27-case reflection lookup cannot live there (~160 Rust lines), and moving the unknown-verb rejection to eoie_do would change which error wins in a multi-error program ('unsupported statement: X' is raised in statement order). So the verbs become their own exporting crate eoie_do_verbs with a primitive boundary in the domain's own words: eoie_do_verb_family(word) -> family word ('reads' 'facts' 'runs' 'writes' 'git' 'jobs' 'labs', '' unknown). Consumers: do_program's query_verb_known = family <> '' (one extern call), eoie_do classifies each query record by family (replaces the 6 has_* macro scans; the 'files with a fact flag' rule stays in eoie_do), do write's read-after = family 'reads'. Draft model (granular: fact_verb/run_verb/write_verb unions + ReadVerb : query_verb, lookups as let, test block) in the carry set: do-verb-family/eoie_do_verbs/verbs.spi. Still needed: move union program_family from eoie_do/decode.spi into eoie_do_model, the crate scaffold (Cargo.toml, lib export, cargo metadata --offline, owner growth row), and a compile preview.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_3 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 3u32, "2026-10-22T08:20Z", "eoie", "04:20 crate draft complete and dry-run clean on a composed copy (live tree + D + E): apply-do-verbs-crate.ps1 installs do-verb-family/eoie_do_verbs (verbs.spi with the eoie_do_verb_family export and a test block, Cargo.toml, package.spiproj on spiral-/union_reflection/eoie_do_model), moves union program_family from eoie_do/decode.spi into eoie_do_model (eoie_do opens it), adds the workspace member and the registry notebook. Next session: cargo metadata --offline (lock), owner growth row, compile preview; then a second slice wires do_program (query_verb_known), eoie_do (family per record) and do write (read-after) to the export.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_4 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 4u32, "2026-10-22T12:24Z", "eoie-lane", "08:24 eoie team: the wiring slice is drafted (apply-do-verbs-wire.ps1, carried in lab night folder). It applies cleanly after F + E + E2 + apply-do-verbs-crate, and the paren scan is clean. (1) The family words live once in eoie_do_model (program_family_word plus program_family_named via reflection); verbs.spi drops its local copy. (2) eoie_do_verbs exports eoie_do_program_family(encoded): query records fold into a families_seen record; files with a count word is Facts (field_index ... count, as the old macro); the first family in a typed priority list Cons (Runs, Jobs, Labs, Git, Writes, Facts, Reads) wins, else Edits. 7 expectations in a test block via records_from_bars. (3) eoie_do/decode.spi drops 7 host macros (has_query..has_lab) for one export call plus a match (Runs with an edit stays Edits). (4) eoie_do_edit drops its has_run macro for runs_in encoded. (5) do_program's 27-word pipe table becomes verb_family_word <> ''. Cargo deps eoie-do-verbs in eoie_do, eoie_do_program, eoie_do_edit. Net 8 fewer host macros. Gate: do_program.rs 988 and do_edit.rs 976 must shrink or hold in the preview, else the slice waits. Ships with E (release G) after its preview.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_5 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 5u32, "2026-10-24T01:17Z", "x", "2026-10-23 21:17 x: consumer finding from the user's lane-lands-lib direction (atomic batched patches so all lanes can patch shared code). A lib change that ADDS modules and EDITS existing files (2 new .spi + crypto/sm'/resultm/package.spiproj edits) cannot be one eoie do program: \"program rejected: edit and write statements cannot share one program yet; run them as two calls\". So the change isn't atomic. x's workaround orders the calls copy-then-edit, so a failed edit leaves only unlisted (never compiled) new files; edit-then-copy would list missing modules. Ask: let copy/write and edit share one program with the same all-or-nothing validation (validate every statement first, then write), so a mixed change lands atomically.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_6 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 6u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_7 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 7u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
