inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_9 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 9u32, "2026-11-09T19:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, CLOSE-OUT CHECK (the recorded first step: did the remaining milestone ship?): YES. Evidence in the live tree: src/rig_do_verbs/verbs.spi holds union program_verb (ReadVerb query_verb | FactVerb | RunStepVerb | WriteVerb | ToolVerb), program_verb_family, the named lookups and a test block (search/tail reads, hash/diff facts, processes runs, move writes, git, lab; replace and edit are no query verb), exporting rig_do_verb_family and rig_do_program_family; program_family itself lives once in rig_do_model (program_family_word / program_family_named by reflection). Consumers all call the exports: rig_do_program/compiled.spi:51 (verb_family_word), rig_do/decode.spi:11 and rig_do_edit/decode.spi:4 (program family). The four copies the 10-22 census found are gone: no has_fact/has_run/has_write/has_git/has_job/has_lab macro and no verb word list remain in any rig_do* package (grep 0). Placement differs from the title on purpose (verbs in their own crate, per the 10-22 03:59 size refinement: the program crate was at 948 lines). DONE.")
inl note_of_kit_do_verb_family_10 () = Note ("KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY", 10u32, "2026-11-09T19:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the installed kit (box, TRAIN41) classifies and runs a read verb through these exports: kit do <kit> --dry-run with a search statement printed \"ok files 1 searched 1 matched matches 3\" and exit 0 (the search verb is resolved by program_verb_named / rig_do_verb_family before it runs). Grep proof of the single source: 0 has_* macros and 0 verb word lists in rig_do*.")
