inl kit_window_wait_clear () = Task ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", "eoie window wait-clear <class,...> [--settle <n>] [--max <min>]: block until no window of the given classes is held or waiting for n samples in a row, then print the list; and job status shows the windows held during a job (a contended flag), so agents stop writing their own window-sampling loops", Story, P3, D2, 75u32, Planned, "", "kit,gate,windows,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_window_wait_clear () = Planning ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_1 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 1u32, "2026-10-22T18:02Z", "x", "2026-10-22 14:02 x: filed from two scratch scripts I wrote today instead of verbs (eoie-first). (1) block_end_watch.ps1 samples 'eoie window list' every 90 s until no live-gui or compiler-install window has been held or waiting for 2 samples in a row, so a background shell notifies the agent when a block ends. A block is often several live-gui windows back to back, hence the settle count. (2) run8_watch.ps1 samples 'eoie window list' every 5 min during a heavy job to classify the run as quiet or contended (any compile window held), because timing rules (X-PRECOMMIT-SPEED notes 27-28: --timeout thresholds of 135 s quiet vs 150 s contended) depend on it, and eoie keeps no window history. Proposed: 'window wait-clear' as in the title (exit 0 when clear, 1 at --max), and an append-only window event log (request, grant, release with timestamps) from which 'job status' derives windows_overlapping=<kinds:count>. Both are generic: no lane or project names. Until it ships, the scratch scripts stay in the session scratchpad only.")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_2 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 2u32, "2026-10-22T21:27Z", "eoie-lane", "17:27 pure model drafted and tested (scratch f5/src/eoie_window_settle_model, HostFree + LibReferenced), from x's two watcher scripts. settled forall sample. folds any sample_series with a busy predicate; sample_busy over window rows and watched classes is the window-list instance. settle_terms {clear_samples_needed; max_samples}, verdicts KeepWaiting | ClearNow | GaveUp, and run_contention Quiet | Contended busy_samples comes from the same pass, which is the 'contended flag' for job status. Tests: a one-sample gap between back-to-back live-gui blocks is not the end; a compile window does not count for a block watch; the watch gives up at its limit and reports Contended 3; a live window does not contend with a compile-only watch. Cells: 2/2 pass after annotating the recursive forall (ETY-ExpectedAnnotation on the first try); standards 0 findings. Next (compile release): 'eoie window wait-clear <class,...> [--settle n] [--max min]' sampling window list rows through this fold, and job status reading the contention.")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_3 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 3u32, "2026-10-23T06:17Z", "eoie", "02:17 eoie: verb drafted for release K (scratch window-wait/apply-window-wait.ps1, chained after the event log in apply-rK; dry run clean on the post-K tree). New crate eoie_window_wait (HostFree, LibReferenced, like eoie_window_claim): settle.spi is the Cells-checked model, and wait.spi samples live_rows every --every seconds (default 30), counts a sample busy when any row's class is in the comma list, and runs observed/verdict_of until the clear streak reaches --settle (default 2, exit 0) or --max minutes pass (default 60, exit 1). Unknown classes are refused. The receipt carries samples and quiet or contended busy_samples: x's contended flag for a heavy run. Wired into window_run's dispatch and usage, with eoie_machine_windows' Cargo edge and the workspace member. wait_cli tests a block that ends during the wait (busy, then cleared) and the unknown-class refusal. job status reading the contended flag from the event log comes after the log ships (EOIE-WINDOW-LIVE-QUEUE note 6).")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_4 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-23, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_5 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 5u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_6 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 6u32, "2026-11-06T11:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_7 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 7u32, "2026-11-09T13:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 10:0x microblog groom, the step from n4/n5 (did it ship?), on the installed kit (11-08). (1) window wait-clear SHIPPED and works: 'window wait-clear live-gui --settle 2 --every 2 --max 1' -> 'kit window wait-clear ok classes=live-gui samples=2 quiet', exit 0; an unknown class is refused with the valid class list (live-gui|test-suite|heavy-build|compile|compiler-install|tree-read|bench|compile-hold|tree-write). (2) NOT shipped: the title's second half. job status shows no windows held during a job and no contended flag (job status on job-1794225846973 prints only state/exit/elapsed/bytes/label). The model has it (run_contention Quiet | Contended busy_samples, n2), and the wait receipt prints quiet/contended, but job status does not record it. next: job supervise samples window list at the job's start and end (or reads the window event log for its span) and job status prints contended=<n> or quiet. dod: job status of a job that overlapped a compile window says contended; one that did not says quiet.")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_8 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 8u32, "2026-11-09T13:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "typefeatures: run_contention union (Quiet | Contended of busy_samples) from eoie_window_settle_model already exists; job status gains a field of that union, no new types.")
inl note_of_kit_window_wait_clear_9 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOW-WAIT-CLEAR", 9u32, "2026-11-09T18:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:5x tibia (help pool): STATUS CHECKED on the installed kit. Part 1 SHIPPED: `kit window` usage lists `wait-clear <class,...> [--settle <n>] [--every <seconds>] [--max <minutes>]` (package src/rig_window_wait: settle.spi model, wait.spi, wait_cli.spi). Smoke: `kit window wait-clear tree-write --settle 1 --max 1` -> \"kit window wait-clear ok classes=tree-write samples=1 quiet\", exit 0. Part 2 NOT shipped: the \"contended flag in job status\" (windows held during a job) appears only in rig_window_wait's receipt; `kit job list`/status rows carry state/exit/elapsed/bytes/label/placement, no contended field (grep \"contended\" over src: only rig_window_wait). The remaining slice is a job-host change (record the windows sampled during the job, show quiet|contended on its row): rig's.")
