inl kit_accept_review () = Task ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", "Review verb for Cells accept runs: compare a test file against its pre-accept copy and pass only when every changed line differs in numeric literals alone (same tokens otherwise, no true/false token changed, no comparison operator touched, same line count); print each changed line with its kind (literal, BOOLEAN, COMPARISON, SHAPE). Requested by tibia 2026-10-22 after a Cells --accept refresh of model pins, where accept would also have flipped a failing boolean property; scratch prototype f34-review.ps1 did it by hand.", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,cells,review,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_accept_review () = Planning ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_1 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 1u32, "2026-10-23T09:54Z", "eoie", "05:54 pure model drafted: scratch f5/src/eoie_accept_review_model (HostFree + LibReferenced, formatted with the reviewed formatter, typecheck running). A char scanner (sm'.index) splits each line into words, numbers (digits, optional fraction, type suffix like i32/f64), operator runs of <>=! and single marks. A changed line takes its worst kind: literal (only number tokens differ) < BOOLEAN (true/false flipped) < COMPARISON (an operator run with a comparison changed) < SHAPE (anything else, incl. token count; an identifier with digits like x1 -> x2 is SHAPE, not literal). accept_review(before, after) refuses a line-count change and passes only when every changed line is literal; the report lists 'line <n> <kind>: <after line>'. Next: the verb 'eoie cells accept-review <before> <after>' as its own small crate (read both files via lib file_system), after GE2.")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_2 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 2u32, "2026-10-23T09:59Z", "eoie", "05:59 model passes its 3 test blocks (notebook check models3). First typecheck failed with a constraint error: Spiral's <=/>= don't take char, so the scanner now classifies u32 code points via lib xml.code_point_at/code_point_width like lib xpath.spi does, which also makes it UTF-8 safe (non-ASCII letters count as word chars). Next: verb wiring (own crate reading both files through lib file_system), after GE2.")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_3 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 3u32, "2026-10-23T10:01Z", "eoie", "06:01 verb drafted: scratch accept-review/apply-accept-review.ps1 creates crate eoie_repo_accept_review (review.spi = the passing model, accept.spi = lib-only entry: env args, file_system.read_all_text, console) and wires 'eoie repo accept-review <before> <after>' as one more elif after release G's 'affected' branch, plus the usage text, the spiral-tests registry, eoie_cli's Cargo deps and the workspace. Exit 0 = literal-only, 1 = refused (each changed line listed with its kind), 2 = usage or missing file. Dry run on GE2's rebased tree: applies. Ships after GE2 (its anchors are G's output), via fmt-rebase, with a --baseline-merge line in its release script.")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_4 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 4u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 30m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D2 at 50%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_5 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 5u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_6 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 6u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_7 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 7u32, "2026-11-06T11:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-ACCEPT-REVIEW (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_accept_review_8 () = Note ("KIT-ACCEPT-REVIEW", 8u32, "2026-11-09T17:33Z", "tibia", "Evidence: 11-09 13:4x tibia (help pool; tibia filed the original request 10-22). The verb SHIPPED: the installed kit's usage lists `repo accept-review <before> <after> (passes when every changed line differs in numeric literals only)`, from package src/rig_repo_accept_review (review.spi + accept.spi), wired in rig_cli_routes/routes.spi and the spiral-tests registry. SMOKE on the installed kit.exe (scratch files): literal-only change 42i32 -> 43i32 => \"line 1 literal ... accept-review ok\", exit 0; boolean flip true -> false => \"line 2 BOOLEAN ... refused\", exit 1; dropped line => \"SHAPE: line count 3 -> 2 ... refused\", exit 1. That matches the DoD (pass only on numeric-literal-only changes; each changed line printed with its kind). Proof: those three runs.")
inl kit_bench_verb () = Task ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", "eoie bench: repeat a command n times on a fresh copy of its target and emit a TSV of elapsed_ms (from the eoie receipt, else wall time) that experiment analyze reads directly; today a per-measurement script did it (state-scale write cost)", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,experiments,dogfood,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_bench_verb () = Planning ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_1 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 1u32, "2026-10-22T21:48Z", "eoie-lane", "17:48 friction: measuring agile write latency for EOIE-STATE-SCALE meant a throwaway PowerShell loop (copy the state, run show/note/set n times, parse elapsed_ms, compute p50/p95). Generic-tools rule: the method should be one verb, e.g. 'eoie bench <n> [--copy <dir>] -- <eoie args>', which writes run<TAB>elapsed_ms rows so 'eoie experiment analyze' or 'table stats' gives the medians. Typed: bench_source Receipt | WallClock, and a copy scope so a write probe never touches the live target.")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_2 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 2u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main: consolidated pendencies covered here (EOIE-CONSOLIDATED-INTAKE, class a): BENCH-1 (paired A/B under the same conditions, alternating order), BENCH-3 (one timeout per cell), BENCH-5 (performance ratchet with rollback). Spec text: Downloads/eoie-consolidated/agile_eoie.md.")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_3 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 3u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 120m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D3 at 0%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_4 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 4u32, "2026-11-06T08:23Z", "tibia", "11-06 04:24 tibia (cross-lane, from the star exchange; owner kit): when built, the bench verb should hold three guards that tibia, x and compiler each paid for by hand. (1) Refuse to time a run with a nonzero exit or an output-parity mismatch. A mingw AVX crash dropped stdout, and a crash got timed as \"3x faster\", which VOIDed a node square. (2) Record load-before for each round and drop rows above a threshold (tibia used 40%). (3) Run the A/A or A/B arms inside one job (x #7). Relates to EOIE-JOB-QUIET-START.")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_5 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 5u32, "2026-11-06T10:18Z", "tibia", "11-06 06:19 tibia (adds to my 04:24 note): (4) when the max quiet wait runs out, SKIP the round; never run it loaded. tibia's tf8 sweep waited about 900 s and then ran anyway: 9 of 12 rounds were VOID and it hit its 11,054 s wall cap. (5) Print the budget, rounds x (run + max wait) + setup, and refuse to launch with a smaller timeout. Reference implementation: tibia's tf9-sweep.ps1 (node tibia-tf6, sha F3E5FA834A40).")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_6 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 6u32, "2026-11-06T11:33Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-BENCH-VERB (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_7 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 7u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries BENCH-1 (Paired A/B with lifecycle control); BENCH-3 (Serial matrices with per-cell budgets); BENCH-5 (Performance-aware promotion). Why: 10-24 note #2: paired A/B alternating order, per-cell timeout, ratchet with rollback")
inl note_of_kit_bench_verb_8 () = Note ("KIT-BENCH-VERB", 8u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. BENCH-1 · Paired A/B with lifecycle control · P0 · ssam, brz, ota · Open / The control and candidate must be measured under the same conditions: clean the process family before every sample, bypass or reset caches per stage (or bust them without changing semantics), alternate order, bind both source hashes, compare against the sealed control and the best current state with a threshold, roll back by hash automatically, and report cache/warm state separately (and warm-state labels must match). || BENCH-3 · Serial matrices with per-cell budgets · P2 · ssam, brz · Partial / One timeout per cell, not per matrix, so a stalled cell cannot waste the rest; resource-tagged exclusive execution for scarce tools; concurrency from observed pressure rather than CPU count; templates for the matrix TSV schema. *Now:* `command-capture-matrix` with parallel chains exists. || BENCH-5 · Performance-aware promotion · P2 · ssam · Open / `patch gated` runs a project-defined ratchet and rolls back when the configured delta is exceeded, and a generic progress gate accepts monotonic improvement (a count strictly decreases and the worst case does not regress) instead of demanding the final target in one promotion.")
