inl matrix_rustc_codegen_units () = Task ("MATRIX-RUSTC-CODEGEN-UNITS", "Matrix Rust rows compile with -C codegen-units=1 if a quiet-box A/B confirms it is faster for single-file programs", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "team:org,matrix,rust,performance,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_matrix_rustc_codegen_units () = Planning ("MATRIX-RUSTC-CODEGEN-UNITS", Minutes 30u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_matrix_rustc_codegen_units_1 () = Note ("MATRIX-RUSTC-CODEGEN-UNITS", 1u32, "2026-10-23T06:42Z", "main", "2026-10-23 02:42 main: first A/B on a loaded box (8 hashed-random samples, 7 building, second of 2 rounds, rustc +nightly-2026-10-18 -C opt-level=2 as test.ps1:725): default 39,288 ms, -C codegen-units=1 28,787 ms (-27%), -C linker=rust-lld 39,834 ms (no gain), debuginfo=0 plus strip 37,351 ms. Rule fixed before the rerun: on a quiet box with 20 samples and 2 orders, adopt codegen-units=1 in test.ps1 only if the total is at least 10% lower in both orders and no run output changes. Rust rows are 474 of the matrix at a 1.7 s native median, so 27% would save about 3.7 min of compile per full run.")
inl note_of_matrix_rustc_codegen_units_2 () = Note ("MATRIX-RUSTC-CODEGEN-UNITS", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:16Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: an A/B on an idle machine (8 hashed-random samples, 2 rounds) of -C codegen-units=1 vs default; adopt in test.ps1's Rust rows only if faster by more than noise. Next step: rerun the 10-23 A/B on europa (idle CPU) with the 11-05 nightly, after the spiral pin pass.")
inl note_of_matrix_rustc_codegen_units_3 () = Note ("MATRIX-RUSTC-CODEGEN-UNITS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T14:31Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~14:2xZ: IDLE-BOX A/B DONE -> DO NOT ADOPT. europa (idle, load 0.36 at launch), rustc pinned nightly-2026-10-18, 20 hashed-random single-file matrix samples (of 502 single-file candidates), 2 orders, identical emitted .rs + pin + opt-level=2, only -C codegen-units=1 differs. ORDER1 default 5616ms vs cgu1 5320ms (B 5.3% lower); ORDER2 default 7400ms vs cgu1 6652ms (B 10.1% lower); run-output identical on all 20 (0 diffs). Rule (B >=10% lower in BOTH orders + no output change) NOT met -> DO NOT ADOPT at test.ps1:1172. The large between-order variance (default 5616 vs 7400) says the single-compile signal is noisy. CAVEAT: the prior loaded-box run showed -27%, so the benefit is LOAD-DEPENDENT (codegen-units=1 cuts per-compile thread overhead, which helps most under core contention). Production compiles 474 Rust rows IN PARALLEL (-ThrottleLimit), so an idle single-compile A/B likely UNDERSTATES the real benefit; a parallel-batch A/B (compile N rows concurrently, default vs cgu1) is the production-representative test. Did not run it: europa load rose to 1.4 mid-session (another lane), and a core-saturating bench would contaminate + disturb. RECOMMEND a parallel/loaded A/B follow-up if the ~3.7 min/run potential saving is worth it. Idle-box DoD as written: MET, verdict DO NOT ADOPT.")
