inl kit_grep_regex_hint () = Task ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", "eoie grep hints at --regex when a literal needle with regex syntax matches nothing", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,grep,friction,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_grep_regex_hint () = Planning ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", Minutes 20u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_1 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 1u32, "2026-10-23T10:07Z", "eoie", "06:07 friction measured on myself: eoie grep over the backlog state with the needle 'single-use binding|codegen pack' (and 'near-gate|zzz') answered 'ok ... 0 matched', because the needle is literal without --regex, while 'near-gate' alone matched 12 times; I nearly concluded absence. Rule: when a search ends with 0 matches, no --regex was given, and the needle holds a pipe, .*, brackets, ^ or $, the receipt adds 'hint: the needle is literal; pass --regex to use it as a pattern'. No other behavior change. Test: a grep CLI notebook case with an alternation needle over a fixture that holds both words.")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_2 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 2u32, "2026-10-23T10:10Z", "eoie", "06:10 slice drafted: scratch grep-hint/apply-grep-regex-hint.ps1 (typed needle_hint union NoNeedleHint | LiteralLooksLikePattern, hint only when total is 0 and --regex is absent; eoie_grep_query gains spiral- for sm'; grep_cli test with 'needle|three' literal -> hint, --regex -> matches 3 and no hint). Anchors are on main's pre-format originals (grep.spi is in the 05:08 formatted set), so it lands through fmt-rebase; prelaunch with -Originals is clean. Ships with the small post-GE2 release (accept-review, notebook progress), not HIJK.")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_3 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 3u32, "2026-10-23T10:17Z", "eoie", "06:17 re-anchored: the slice now matches the post-G healed grep.spi (receipt line with ++#, open sm'_operators already present, added only if missing). Composes in the release L dry chain on GE2 -> H,J,K. Ships in release L (launch-L.ps1).")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_4 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 4u32, "2026-10-23T18:10Z", "eoie", "14:10 eoie: TDD case written, spec/one-call.md case 44 (eoie grep notes.txt 'one|two' over a two-line fixture). On the installed binary it is red at exactly the hint ('ok  files 1 searched  0 matched  matches 0  2ms ...' vs the same with '  hint: the needle is literal; pass --regex to use it as a pattern'), so the rest of the receipt already matches byte for byte; it turns green when L installs the slice.")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_5 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 5u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-23, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_6 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 6u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_7 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 7u32, "2026-11-06T11:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-GREP-REGEX-HINT (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_grep_regex_hint_8 () = Note ("KIT-GREP-REGEX-HINT", 8u32, "2026-11-09T12:41Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "proof: 11-09 08:41 microblog, installed kit.exe (11-08 build) on the box over a scratch fixture holding one, needle, three. kit grep <dir> 'needle|three' -> 'ok files 1 searched 0 matched matches 0 hint: the needle is literal; pass --regex to use it as a pattern'. With --regex -> 2> needle, 3> three, matches 2, and no hint. Source: kit/src/rig_grep_query/grep.spi needle_hint (NoNeedleHint | LiteralLooksLikePattern), CLI case in rig_read_query/grep_cli.spi:122. Landed and green; DoD met.")
