inl kit_job_cells_gate () = Task ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", "eoie job start waits, instead of failing, while another team's Cells notebook run is active (a 'cells' slot or --wait-free <process pattern>), so agents stop hand-rolling busy loops around run_notebook.ps1", Story, P3, D3, 20u32, Planned, "", "kit,jobs,cells,friction,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_job_cells_gate () = Planning ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_1 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 1u32, "2026-10-23T13:52Z", "x", "2026-10-23 09:52 x: friction measured today. To keep my Cells checks off other teams' runs I wrote three ad-hoc gates: cells_when_free.ps1 (poll every 60 s, give up after N min), cells_chain.ps1 (poll, retry on refusal, and a named mutex after two of my own chains started in the same second at 09:18:40-41), and cells_check.ps1, which refuses with exit 75 when a run_notebook.ps1 outside its own process tree is alive (the 07:52 overlap with eoie's notebook check is why). eoie job start --compile does not know about Cells runs started outside eoie jobs (tibia's and main's run_notebook calls), so a queued job either overlaps them or fails with 75 and stops the --after-ok chain. Wanted: job start waits in its queue while a run_notebook.ps1 / spiral.notebook process not in its own tree is alive (re-checked on each slot grant), shows 'waiting: foreign Cells run pid N (label)' in job status and machine watch, and has a --slot-within deadline as today. Then every agent's Cells check is one 'eoie job start --compile' call, and these scripts are deleted.")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_2 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 2u32, "2026-10-23T15:57Z", "x", "2026-10-23 11:57 x: measured cost today. I queued 21 compile-class jobs right after tibia's 11:22 block end, each running a Cells notebook through a foreign-run refusal (exit 75). eoie admitted them while other teams' run_notebook.ps1 were alive (eoie's own f6 scratch notebooks among them), so 19 of 21 finished as exit 75 within ~30 min without testing anything. Only the non-Cells xc compile and one early prelude run did real work. Workaround now: a detached self-gating chain (poll until no foreign runner, a named mutex, retry on 75), i.e. the hand-rolled gate this item asks eoie to own. With the requested wait-in-queue behaviour, the 21 jobs would have run in sequence with no resubmission.")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_3 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 3u32, "2026-10-23T18:21Z", "eoie", "14:21 eoie: design chosen and pure model drafted (scratch f6/src/eoie_wait_free; typecheck queued behind main's matrix). Of the item's two options, a box-wide exclusive 'cells' window class would serialize every team's notebook runs, which is a policy change for main and tibia. '--wait-free <pattern,...>' is opt-in and generic, so it comes first: job start writes the patterns to the job file; the supervisor's gate samples processes (eoie_machine_watch's sysinfo rows) every 5 s and stays queued while a process OUTSIDE the job's own tree has a command line containing any pattern; job status shows 'waiting free of a foreign run pid=N (command)' (with EOIE-JOBS-DOCTOR's waiting_for); --slot-within keeps its deadline. Model: wait_free_state_of (rows, own root pid, patterns) -> MachineFree | ForeignRun (pid, command), with tree membership by bounded parent walk; tests: a foreign run_notebook.ps1 holds the job, the job's own run never does, comma pattern lists, and empty patterns never wait. Then x's three scripts become 'eoie job start --compile --wait-free run_notebook.ps1,spiral.notebook <label> ...'. Placement: the flag goes into K's typed start-option fold, so this lands after K. Today's cost, from x: 19 of 21 queued Cells jobs ended exit 75 without testing anything.")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_4 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-23, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_5 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 5u32, "2026-10-31T09:59Z", "kit", "10-31 06:0x kit groom (WIP limit, dangling rule 'no Active silent > 3 d'): Active -> Planned at 20%. No note for about 3 days, so this item isn't in progress. Planned keeps it in 'agile next --team kit' as ready work (Paused would park it out of the queue). Kit had 42 Active items, with Active meaning anything ever touched rather than being worked now. The progress and notes stay; whoever pulls it next sets it Active again.")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_6 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 6u32, "2026-11-06T11:34Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-JOB-CELLS-GATE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_7 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T18:30Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:3x tibia (help pool): STATUS + EVIDENCE for rig's prioritisation. --wait-free has NOT shipped: no wait-free in `kit job` / `kit job start` usage and no wait_free package in src (the 10-23 model draft never landed). Today's friction data: tibia ran ~25 Cells/compile gates on ganymede via `kit job start --on ganymede --compile` (lib gates, regex gates, verify-edits, BC steps 11-15), and none failed with the 10-23 refusal exit 75; the node's 2 compile slots plus the job queue serialised them. The remaining cost was QUEUEING behind another lane holding both slots (~40 min, see GATE-HEALS-1101 tibia note), not foreign-run overlap. Reading: the 10-23 box-centric case (run_notebook.ps1 started outside kit next to kit jobs) is mostly retired now that Cells gates run as node jobs. The item still matters for Cells runs launched OUTSIDE kit (e.g. lib_land_window's document_test on the box). Suggest lowering to P3 unless a lane reports a fresh exit-75 overlap.")
inl note_of_kit_job_cells_gate_8 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-CELLS-GATE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T18:39Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig groom: P1 -> P3 on tibia's field data: --wait-free never shipped, yet today's 25 node gates had 0 exit-75 overlaps, so the overlap this item guards against is not happening in practice. Revisit if exit 75 reappears.")
