inl note_of_kit_do_move_range_3 () = Note ("KIT-DO-MOVE-RANGE", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries EDIT-5 (Template and scaffold cloning); EDIT-6 (Structural refactors: move, split, rename, delete ranges); EDIT-7 (Language-aware edits). Why: title cites EDIT-5..7: move range/definition, rename, bounded delete, folder-family clone, split plan; do move <a> to <b> ships the rename part")
inl note_of_kit_do_move_range_4 () = Note ("KIT-DO-MOVE-RANGE", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. EDIT-5 · Template and scaffold cloning · P0 · erp, ge2e · Open / Projects repeatedly generated families of 7 to 11 near-identical crates. Add a transaction that clones a directory family, renames paths and files, applies checked substitutions with per-file preconditions, and merges into an existing tree without overwriting. `fs-copy-tree` correctly refuses merges, so it currently takes one call per crate. || EDIT-6 · Structural refactors: move, split, rename, delete ranges · P0 · sqlt, ota, scp, ge2e, sbin · Open / Rename a file or directory as one transactional step (today it is copy plus remove); move a line range or symbol into a new file; delete a bounded range with boundary preflight (scp quarantined dead code in comments because no range delete existed); extract a block or test module into a new crate while updating workspace members and dependencies; rename symbols and paths in a batch (allow/deny globs, expected hashes, changed-path report); move many files while rewriting guarded `Cargo.toml` target paths, checking collisions and rolling back. A split planner must predict the physical size before and after, using the same measurement function as the post-apply gate, and refuse transformations with no gain (generated wrappers pushed files back over the ceiling after rustfmt). When a module moves, leave a one-line forwarding shim so retained parents that still `#[path]`-include it keep compiling. Re-key path-based hash manifests after moves. || EDIT-7 · Language-aware edits · P1 · ota, sqlt, ge2e · Open / Symbol read/replace, brace-aware method moves across files, AST-local edits (add a struct field, update every initializer), scoped import edits. Lower priority than EDIT-3; an exact-text transaction covers most cases.")
inl kit_scratch_copy () = Task ("KIT-SCRATCH-COPY", "eoie scratch copy: one call makes a disposable copy of a repo from declared includes (src and spec, minus target and .cache), each path declared real copy or junction, with an identity receipt (source hash, state) and recreate-on-failure; gates and benches run there, never on the live tree (FS-1, FS-6, FS-7, EVID-8, BENCH-2, FIXT-4)", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-HEAL-BOUNDARY", "kit,fs,consolidated,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_scratch_copy () = Planning ("KIT-SCRATCH-COPY", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_scratch_copy_1 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-COPY", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "Replaces session scripts: cells-root.ps1 (copy root with dice/alphabet junctions), lib-gate-kit copies, %TEMP% eoie copies (copy-eoie-src-only: 2 runaway 5.5 GB copies on 10-21), verify-drafts-on-scratch-copies. kino-copy-lib-resolution is the case for per-path real-vs-junction. Milestones: model + tests 90 m, host copy with junctions 90 m, receipt + identity check 60 m, tutorial 30 m, release 30 m.")
