inl note_of_kit_scratch_copy_3 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-COPY", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries FS-1 (Import from outside the root, hash-checked); FS-6 (Explicit destination semantics); FS-7 (Copies are independent unless asked otherwise); EVID-8 (Worktree identity); BENCH-2 (Sandboxed gates); FIXT-4 (Typed replay profile). Why: title cites all six: disposable declared copy, real-vs-junction per path, identity receipt, recreate on failure, gates never on the live tree; do copy with absolute paths covers plain external import")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_copy_4 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-COPY", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. FS-1 · Import from outside the root, hash-checked · P0 · ge2e, ssam, node, brz, scp · Open / `fs-copy` accepts only paths relative to one root, so receipts, logs and uploaded artifacts produced outside the workspace needed shell `cp`. Add an explicit external-source import (file or directory, from an absolute path or a host-mounted upload) that records source path, bytes and hash, checks the expected destination hash, and works for binaries. || FS-6 · Explicit destination semantics · P1 · node, ssam, scp, ge2e · Open / Extract, rehydrate and copy should state up front whether the destination must be absent, empty or mergeable, and offer `--replace-empty`, `--replace --expect-old-hash` and an idempotent reset for resumable extraction. State whether extracted files keep archive mtimes: restored historical mtimes let Cargo reuse newer artifacts in a shared target that no longer matched the source bytes. `fs-copy` needs a replace-existing mode with an overwrite precondition. || FS-7 · Copies are independent unless asked otherwise · P0 · ota, ge2e · Open / `copy-file-preserve` kept hardlink identity, so editing a promoted file silently changed its source too. Make independent copies the default, record inode and link count, and offer explicit copy-on-write clones (reflink) and shadow trees with excludes for cheap disposable workspaces, refusing hardlink shadows when any writer is not atomic. Give each shadow a receipt identity and recreate it after a failure instead of silently reusing a stale one (a reused shadow made a second run report an empty selection). || EVID-8 · Worktree identity · P2 · ge2e · Open / A partially built working root was reused as if it were a clean baseline and nearly caused a false diagnosis. Give every worktree an identity receipt (source hash and state: clean corpus, healed, overlaid, built), and make baseline cloning require it. || BENCH-2 · Sandboxed gates · P0 · ssam · Open / Gates must never mutate canonical source (a burn-in gate restored its control source over an in-progress candidate and erased it): run in a sandbox forked from current with a neutral lease, then import only allowed receipts. Gates own cleanup of their output paths. || FIXT-4 · Typed replay profile · P2 · node · Open / Cold replay in an isolated tree (fresh cache, home and target) bound to a source identity, with byte and vendor-hash verification, invalidated by any later source change, and with an identity-checked disposable lifecycle.")
