inl note_of_kit_tree_diff_3 () = Note ("KIT-TREE-DIFF", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries READ-4 (File-level and symbol-level diff); BNDL-7 (Bundle and tree diff); MERGE-4 (Overlays and layered reconstruction). Why: title cites READ-4, BNDL-7, MERGE-4: hash-first tree/file diff, --stat, owned-source filter")
inl note_of_kit_tree_diff_4 () = Note ("KIT-TREE-DIFF", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. READ-4 · File-level and symbol-level diff · P0 · ssam, ota, sbin, scp, ge2e · Partial / `product-diff` is root-oriented and noisy. Add a hash-first `file-diff <left> <right>` with bounded context, an archive-member-to-file diff, a per-function/module diff, a sorted path-set diff, `--stat --owners` summaries, and an owned-source filter (exclude receipts, build output, vendor, state) with a separate full mode. *Now:* `do diff` compares TSVs by key. || BNDL-7 · Bundle and tree diff · P1 · ge2e, sbin, ota · Open / `bundle diff <a.zip> <b.zip>` classified as product / test / state / environment; `bundle compare <workspace> <rehydrated>` (file count, path set, byte hashes); a filtered tree-state diff against the last bundle for recovery. || MERGE-4 · Overlays and layered reconstruction · P2 · ge2e · Open / Base + authority layer + overlay with per-layer hashes and authority-aware ordering; overlay manifests that can also delete and rename; a changed-only overlay built by diffing against the base; mailbox patches applied commit by commit with excludes; a compile-closure check that applies the overlay to a clean baseline before emitting it; reconstruction of a full tree through copy-on-write or hardlinks; and source gates that declare which root kind they need (bundle, overlaid repo, input corpus).")
