inl note_of_kit_remove_plan_4 () = Note ("KIT-REMOVE-PLAN", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. FS-4 · Safe removal: trees, batches, prune plans · P0 · sqlt, ota, erp, ge2e, scp, node · Partial / Removal needs a dry-run plan (selected paths, bytes recovered, protected-source rules), a root/name guard and a receipt stored outside the target subtree; `remove-many` with all-or-nothing preflight; chunked, resumable removal of very large trees; symlink awareness (unlink runtime links before recursing); configurable version-name patterns for pruning stale transient state; and `--missing-ok` that really returns success for an absent path. *Now:* `fs-remove-tree [--missing-ok]` and no-follow unlink exist; there is no plan, batch or chunked mode.")
inl kit_job_expect () = Task ("KIT-JOB-EXPECT", "eoie job start --expect-exit <codes> --expect-line <regex> --expect-file <path>: a job settles failed when a predicate misses and Deferred on a declared resumable code, because exit 0 lies (PROC-1, PROC-4)", Story, P1, D3, 50u32, Planned, "KIT-JOBS", "kit,jobs,consolidated,team:rig", "current", "current")
