inl note_of_kit_job_expect_7 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-EXPECT", 7u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries PROC-1 (Wrapper success is never child success); PROC-4 (Typed outcomes and expected exit codes). Why: title cites PROC-1, PROC-4: --expect-exit/--expect-line/--expect-file, Deferred on resumable codes (50%)")
inl note_of_kit_job_expect_8 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-EXPECT", 8u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. PROC-1 · Wrapper success is never child success · P0 · auth, ota, node, ge2e, scp · Open / `command-capture` prints `ok` and exits 0 whatever the child returned (confirmed in source). Add a mode that propagates the child exit, put the child status first in every summary, and let callers supply completion predicates (a required output line or artifact), because exit 0 alone was observed to lie: a cancelled MSBuild returned 0, and a compiler returned 0 without writing its binary. Verify declared outputs exist before reporting success. || PROC-4 · Typed outcomes and expected exit codes · P0 · ota, sbin, brz, node, scp, ge2e · Partial / Distinguish `completed`, `failed`, `semantic_failure`, `time_budget`, `yielded_with_checkpoint`, `external_blocked`, `killed_without_receipt`, `child_completed_but_caller_hung`, `spawn_failed`, and setup failure versus product failure. Let callers declare expected nonzero exits (an expected-reject status 5; `diff` and `grep` returning 1 for 'different' / 'no match') and resumable codes (an installer's deliberate 75). A spawn failure names the path and environment it tried. Partial results (a timed-out hygiene snapshot) are typed as partial and never promoted. *Now:* process-exit receipts carry `wrapper_status`, `child_exit`, `signal`, `timeout`, `stderr_digest` and `retryability`; jobs report finished / timed out (tree stopped, survivors counted) / lost / spawn failure. There is no expected-code declaration.")
inl kit_job_requeue () = Task ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", "eoie job requeue <id>...: jobs record argv, cwd, environment names and their after-chain, so stopped or failed jobs restart with the same chain in one call (PROC-3)", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-JOB-RECHAIN", "kit,jobs,consolidated,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_job_requeue () = Planning ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_1 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "Evidence 10-23 18:28: main stopped 7 queued jobs when a live block began and saved their argv by hand (scratch saved-argv) to requeue them at block end. Milestones: argv/cwd/env record at start 45 m, requeue verb keeping chain order 60 m, tutorial 30 m, release 15 m.")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_2 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 2u32, "2026-10-24T02:53Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:53 main: the record already exists. Each job folder under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\jobs\\<id> holds argv, argv.inner (the real command when heavy-wrapper.ps1 wraps it), label, timeout_ms, after (predecessor plus ok|any) and cwd. Main requeued 9 chained jobs at 22:5x by reading those files (scratch requeue-lib-tail.ps1: check every job is still queued, stop all, requeue in order with --after). So the verb is that script plus --timeout overrides; milestone 1 (recording) is done. Re-estimate: 90 m.")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_3 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 3u32, "2026-10-24T05:37Z", "main", "2026-10-24 01:37 main: spec from the working stopgap (scratch main-queue.ps1 -Action Stop|Requeue|Show, used for tibia's PR-27 block). Algorithm: (1) Stop: take the queued jobs of a set (label prefix, team, or listed ids), record each folder's label, argv.inner (or argv), timeout_ms, heavy (heavy-wrapper.ps1 present), window-class, and after (predecessor id TAB ok|any), sorted by job id = creation order, into one manifest, then job stop each. (2) Requeue: walk the manifest in order; a predecessor that is itself in the manifest maps to its NEW id; a predecessor outside it keeps its id only while unsettled (a settled one drops the --after); keep --after vs --after-ok from the mode; relaunch with the same shape, label, timeout and argv; print 'requeued <label> as <new id> after <id>'. Plumbing for the eoie team: a new crate eoie_job_requeue (control.rs is already ~46 KB, so the verb must not grow it); a new export on eoie_job_launch that takes the shape and after mode (eoie_job_launched_text covers only PlainStart); JobRequeue in eoie_jobs.model job_command plus usage; dispatch in eoie_jobs/jobs.spi. Re-estimate stays 90 m for the Spiral, plus the train's new-crate steps.")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_4 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 4u32, "2026-10-24T06:09Z", "main", "2026-10-24 02:09 main: a gap the stopgap hit. 'job list' without a count shows a bounded window (unsettled first, up to 120), and my stop pass parsed it for queued main jobs: 3 old queued jobs (otp-single gate/land, dictm-land-2, created 22:52/22:59) were missed and stayed live. One of them was --after a stopped job, so it was free to take a heavy slot ahead of tibia's live block. Fixed in the stopgap with 'job list 1000'. The verb needs a direct query: 'job list --queued [--label-prefix p]' (or a state filter) that never truncates, so 'requeue' and 'doctor' can rely on it.")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_5 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T11:28Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-JOB-REQUEUE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_6 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 6u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries PROC-3 (Full argv and environment in receipts). Why: title cites PROC-3: jobs record argv, cwd, env names")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_7 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 7u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. PROC-3 · Full argv and environment in receipts · P1 · ota, ssam, node · Open / Receipts record the program, cwd and environment names but not the argument vector (confirmed in source), so commands had to be reconstructed. Record normalized argv, the named profile (TOOL-1), the manifest/cwd relationship and the executable hash.")
inl note_of_kit_job_requeue_8 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-REQUEUE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T06:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:1x local rig, premise re-check: PROC-3's gap (receipts lack argv) is CLOSED: every local job dir now holds argv, cwd, timeout_ms, label, path-first, exit, peak_private_mb, stdout/stderr logs, and after (tab: predecessor id and mode) for chained jobs (seen in job-1794204246091-kit-unstaged-backup). STILL MISSING: the verb (no requeue in src). DESIGN: job requeue <id>... re-creates each job with the recorded argv, cwd, timeout and label (label suffixed -r1, -r2), re-links its after-chain to the new ids in order, and prints the new ids; refuses a job still running. ENV: the env snapshot is deleted on adoption by design (it can hold secrets), so a requeue runs with the caller's environment and records only the variable NAMES the original had, printing a diff of names; never store values. Remote (--on) records keep remote-bin, so requeue forwards to that machine. DoD: requeue of a 3-link chain recreates all three in order (CLI test); a running job is refused. TypeFeatures: requeue_plan list of (old id, new label, after link) built before any write. Code for TRAIN43.")
