inl kit_verdict_ledger () = Task ("KIT-VERDICT-LEDGER", "eoie verdicts: a gate verdict is keyed by its input hashes plus tool identity (compiler DLL, eoie binary, toolchain pins) and goes stale when any of them changes; land and install scripts ask eoie verdict check instead of hand-made verdict files (EVID-1, EVID-2, CARGO-4, PROC-10)", Feature, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-EXPERIMENTS", "kit,evidence,consolidated,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_verdict_ledger () = Planning ("KIT-VERDICT-LEDGER", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_verdict_ledger_1 () = Note ("KIT-VERDICT-LEDGER", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "Replaces: pack-fmt-only gate-verdict.txt (PASS <core hash>), lib-gate-kit verdict files, recompile-drafts-after-compiler-change, release-candidate-cli-run (an old binary hid a failure). Milestones: verdict record model 60 m, record/check verbs 90 m, stale reasons named 60 m, tutorial 30 m, release 60 m.")
inl note_of_kit_verdict_ledger_2 () = Note ("KIT-VERDICT-LEDGER", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:28Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-VERDICT-LEDGER (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_verdict_ledger_3 () = Note ("KIT-VERDICT-LEDGER", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries PROC-10 (Release-aware execution); EVID-1 (Evidence ingest, union and certificates); EVID-2 (Source freshness and build-scope attestation); CARGO-4 (Stale binaries never count). Why: last note cites all four: verdicts keyed by input hashes + tool identity, stale binaries never count")
inl note_of_kit_verdict_ledger_4 () = Note ("KIT-VERDICT-LEDGER", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. PROC-10 · Release-aware execution · P2 · erp · Open / Prefer optimized binaries for heavy passes, and refuse a stale binary after a failed build (see CARGO-4). || EVID-1 · Evidence ingest, union and certificates · P0 · ge2e, node · Open / Hash-bound import of receipts produced outside the workspace, as one transaction keyed by one source fingerprint, into declared canonical/current aliases, with role and schema checks, allowed during closeout. Scope-indexed so a targeted run cannot overwrite broad authority; publish before scratch cleanup, never after. Declarative certificates list required receipts and structured TSV predicates instead of matching literal phrases, so evidence unions don't need a new crate each time. Failing gates write their diagnostic receipt before exiting nonzero. || EVID-2 · Source freshness and build-scope attestation · P2 · ge2e · Open / Commit a content-addressed source fingerprint from a successful captured build/test plan without replaying the pipeline; bind every gate receipt to the final fingerprint and reject receipts older than the last edit; hand an attestation to sibling runs that share the fingerprint. Keep a verdict ledger keyed by input hash plus tool identity (`fresh_pass`, `historical_pass`, `timeout_nonreject`, `known_invalid`) with a `restore-known-good` that restores source and derived artifacts together, and key derived-artifact caches (and negative receipts) by input digest plus the identity of every generator and post-processor, so a changed tool invalidates stale verdicts. || CARGO-4 · Stale binaries never count · P1 · ota, node, ge2e · Open / Record manifest, cwd, target dir and executable hash before running; mark an executable stale when its inputs are newer (a green `cargo test` left the runnable binary stale); resolve a package to its binary path; refuse to run a binary after a failed build.")
inl kit_build_phases () = Task ("KIT-BUILD-PHASES", "eoie job phases: compile, link, test and run phases read from output patterns, a timeout classified by phase with the last unit named, and the load-versus-code rule for regen timeouts typed (CARGO-1, CARGO-2, CARGO-3, JOB-2)", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-JOB-EXPECT", "kit,jobs,consolidated,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_build_phases () = Planning ("KIT-BUILD-PHASES", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_build_phases_1 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PHASES", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN 10-22 12:20 wrote the load-versus-code rule by hand. Milestones: phase patterns per tool 60 m, phase in job status 60 m, timeout classification 60 m, tutorial 30 m, release 30 m.")
inl note_of_kit_build_phases_2 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PHASES", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:34Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-BUILD-PHASES (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_build_phases_3 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PHASES", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries JOB-2 (Chains, composite gates and graph sharding); CARGO-1 (One Cargo gate runner); CARGO-2 (Distinguish compile from test); CARGO-3 (Owner gates, shards and TDD cycles). Why: title cites all four: compile/link/test phases, timeout classified by phase; job chains themselves ship (KIT-JOB-RECHAIN Done, job --after)")
inl note_of_kit_build_phases_4 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PHASES", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. JOB-2 · Chains, composite gates and graph sharding · P1 · node, erp, ge2e, ota · Partial / Chain jobs that pass receipts forward, stop on the first failing prerequisite, distinguish setup failures from product failures, and expose per-stage receipts for one composite gate (fmt, test, clippy, freshness). Shard a build graph (Cargo crates or a .NET project graph), or a large file set weighted by size with heavy files isolated, into nodes that each fit the budget, with per-node receipts and resume of only the missing nodes; a fail-closed rollup decides the gate. Check nested budgets before launch: a suite once declared 640 s of run budgets inside a 420 s window. *Now:* `do` programs can run steps and stop; there is no persisted chain. || CARGO-1 · One Cargo gate runner · P1 · sqlt, ota, erp, ge2e · Partial / fmt, test, doctest, clippy `-D warnings`, release build and smoke, under one toolchain profile (TOOL-1), offline and locked, with a shared target, phase receipts, independent per-phase timeouts and a compact summary. Prove cwd, config and vendor before spawning (a wrong cwd made Cargo use the registry). Scope fmt and clippy to the changed packages, never let fmt walk path-dependency vendor, keep the full subcommand grammar (a clippy wrapper rejected several `-p`) and validate the argv shape before spending a window (a test run with two filters failed only after compiling), resolve the fmt fallback chain (`cargo fmt` → `cargo-fmt` → `rustfmt`), take the edition from the manifest (a first pass formatted with 2021 instead of 2024) and record which executable ran, resolve which lib/bin/test targets a package actually has before invoking (`--lib` on a bin-only package wasted gates), select profile and codegen backend as typed options, and diagnose a stale `Cargo.lock` in the receipt. *Now:* `proxy toolchain <root> cargo-check|cargo-test|cargo-clippy|cargo-fmt-check|cargo-build` exist; check package scoping and phase receipts. || CARGO-2 · Distinguish compile from test · P0 · ota, sbin, ge2e · Open / Report compile, link and test-run phases separately, classify a timeout as `cold_compile` / `link` / `test_execution` (or timeout after the artifact was already produced, which is not a build failure) and name the last crate compiling; persist completed-crate checkpoints and resume until the lease boundary; refuse a gate whose worst-case time crosses the cutoff; never blindly repeat a fingerprint that already exceeded its budget without producing anything (allow one incremental resume, then turn a second failure into a backlog item); keep check and link progress apart so a green check does not hide a second full link; reject zero-test green runs and print the test path that actually ran. || CARGO-3 · Owner gates, shards and TDD cycles · P2 · ota, ge2e · Open / Prefer the smallest gate that reaches the real owner before monolithic links; compile tests without linking a monolithic harness; shard workspace tests automatically and aggregate receipts; serialize only the harnesses that mutate process-global state (environment variables); per-owner timeouts with a typed partial-success receipt; and a `cargo-tdd-cycle` (manifest path, package, filter, expected red then green, non-zero test contract).")
