inl note_of_kit_table_jsonl_3 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-JSONL", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom of the old eoie dump (KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM; source drafts/kit/KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM/agile_eoie.md, 2026-10-22): this item also covers dump entries TABLE-3 (Structured-file contract gates); TABLE-5 (JSONL query). Why: title cites TABLE-3, TABLE-5; do json <file> get covers file-based JSON query")
inl note_of_kit_table_jsonl_4 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-JSONL", 4u32, "2026-11-07T14:14Z", "main", "INLINE TEXT of the old agile_eoie dump entries (user 11-07: keep the lessons inline so the dump file link can be lost). Source: eoie-consolidated agile_eoie.md (2026-10-22, status measured at eoie a831bad), copies at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM\\ and i574n.github\\recovered\\agile-eoie\\from-des073\\eoie-consolidated\\; verdicts from KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM n3. Verdict Covered by this item. TABLE-3 · Structured-file contract gates · P2 · sqlt, ge2e · Open / Assert absent sections, required fields and status-dependent filename rules over generated TOML/JSON sidecars; file-based JSON query and projection; capture a command's JSON output straight into a typed receipt; JSON-to-TSV summaries with a schema and hashes; round-trip gates proving a parser and renderer preserve identity columns and counts. || TABLE-5 · JSONL query · P0 · scp, ota · Open / Runtime traces were diagnosed with Python or jq in nearly every spiral-compiler-parallelization round. Validate JSONL framing (malformed and torn rows, sequence continuity, rows inside a ZIP), filter and group by field, count kinds, take latest-by-kind and first/last windows, build timelines by a typed key, join events across kinds in time order, measure cadence (inter-arrival), and project fields into small deterministic receipts.")
inl note_of_kit_table_jsonl_5 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-JSONL", 5u32, "2026-11-09T19:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, FRAMING CORE BUILT (TABLE-5's \"validate JSONL framing\"; unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_table_jsonl/framing.spi (pure, HostFree). row_frame WholeRow | BlankRow | NotAnObject | TornRow depth; frame_of scans brace/bracket depth OUTSIDE strings (escapes honoured), so a row is whole only when it starts with {, ends with }, returns to depth 0, never closes below 0 mid-row (a \"}}{\" splice is torn, not whole) and does not end inside a string; counts_of tallies every row once and names the FIRST bad row's line number. Test: whole, braces in strings, escaped quote, a row cut mid-write (depth 2), an early close, an array row, a blank row, and the per-file counts with first_bad. FIELD QUERIES (filter, group, latest-by-kind) need a tolerant field reader: lib json.decode is type-directed with no failure case, and json_scan's value_at / text_between are module-private (:~). NEXT: a lib slice exposing a field_text key row -> option string over json_scan (lib lane, rides a train), then filter/group/latest-by-kind here.")
inl note_of_kit_table_jsonl_6 () = Note ("KIT-TABLE-JSONL", 6u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
