inl note_of_kit_gap_intake_7 () = Note ("KIT-GAP-INTAKE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T07:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:4x local rig, REAUTHORED (the 10-24 draft agile_gap_intake never landed and is gone with the wipe): new package src/rig_agile_gap (not in TRAIN42, written after its mirror sync). gap.spi = pure model: gap_flag union with flag words by reflection (--verb --exit --argv --cwd --as), gap_request record, request_from + request_checked refusals (title, verb, lower-case verb words, team from --as first word, numeric exit), id <TEAM>-GAP-<VERB WORDS> with the first free -N against raw state (Task (ID, headers are one line), tags rig,gap,<first verb word>,team:<team>, note FAILED CALL: verb exit cwd argv plus DoD/Next step/TypeFeatures markers; 3 test blocks. intake.spi = entry over lib env.command_line_arguments and file_system.read_text_or_empty, files through agile_task_creation agile_add (TaskKind P1 D2, 30m light agent), export rig_agile_gap_run. Wiring: AgileGap in agile_subcommand_domain (spec + WritesState), dispatcher arm in rig_agile_mutation through link (no host macro; style hook green), Cargo member + dep. kit standards rig_agile_gap: 0 findings, HostFree+LibReferenced declared. Evidence the one call already works today with agile add: scratch backlog copy, add with every planning field + failed-call note in one call, exit 0. LEFT: notebook probe of gap.spi on moon after TRAIN42 (moon at 100 pct now), Cargo.lock refresh offline, TRAIN43 regen (rig_agile_mutation is 992 generated lines: watch the 1000 gate), then a spec/one-call tutorial case. Real gap found while testing: kit help agile add is refused (help takes one verb); agile add with no operands does print its usage.")
inl note_of_kit_gap_intake_8 () = Note ("KIT-GAP-INTAKE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T07:52Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:0x local rig: src/Cargo.lock refreshed offline for the new member (cargo update --workspace --offline: Adding rig-agile-gap, +9 lines, deps agile-task-notes + rig-agile-records), so TRAIN43's lock precheck passes. spec/one-call.md case 50 written red (TDD): setup init + one earlier WEB-GAP-HELP-AGILE-ADD, command kit agile gap backlog <title> --verb help agile add --exit 2 --as web-1, expected receipt rig agile add ok id=WEB-GAP-HELP-AGILE-ADD-2 ... notes=1 bytes_before=956 bytes_after=2361 (bytes measured with the equivalent agile add on a scratch root); agile lint on that root passes the gap-shaped item (only the bare setup item fails PlanningFields/DoD/NextStep).")
inl note_of_kit_gap_intake_9 () = Note ("KIT-GAP-INTAKE", 9u32, "2026-11-09T09:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:1x moon probe rig-probe1109j (job-1794214742546): src/rig_agile_gap/gap.spi GREEN 3/3. Left: TRAIN43 regen of rig_agile_gap intake (agile_add inlined through agile_task_creation) and rig_agile_mutation (gate check), then the CLI case 50.")
inl note_of_kit_gap_intake_10 () = Note ("KIT-GAP-INTAKE", 10u32, "2026-11-09T10:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "DoD: kit agile gap <root> <title> --verb <verb> --as <lane> files a TaskKind P1 D2 item (30m light agent) with id <TEAM>-GAP-<VERB WORDS>[-N], tags rig,gap,<verb>,team:<team> and a FAILED CALL note carrying the lint markers, in one call from the installed binary; spec/one-call.md case 50 green; refusals before any write. TypeFeatures: gap_flag (reflected flag words), gap_request record, request_read and flag_parse unions.")
