inl note_of_kit_legacy_state_triage_1 () = Note ("KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "Open rows include PUBLIC-BINARY-PROFESSIONALISM 62%, DOMAIN-AGILE 22%, QUARRY-FINAL-MINING, CONFINED-IO-CODECS, PARALLEL-READINESS-REASSESSMENT 70%, CANONICAL-PLAN-IR, COMPILER-UNIT-TAIL-RETURN, SPIRAL-NATIVE-DEVELOPER-WORKFLOW 40%. Rule: a row maps to an open item here (note there), or is GPT-era governance (Dropped, reason), or is a live gap (new item).")
inl note_of_kit_legacy_state_triage_2 () = Note ("KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE", 2u32, "2026-10-30T19:16Z", "kit", "10-30 15:2x kit: TRIAGE DONE, all 41 open rows of kit/state/agile.spi decided by n1's rule (38 Active/Planned, 3 Paused). Table with a reason per row: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\legacy-state-triage.tsv.\n- map 8, each noted on its target: EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION <- SPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-BURNDOWN, AUTH-NO-DIRECT-RUST, SPIRAL-NATIVE-SOURCE-OWNERSHIP; EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY <- MAPPING-FILESYSTEM-TRANSACTION, PHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING; EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN <- PORT-STRICT-RELEASE; EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW <- SPIRAL-NATIVE-DEVELOPER-WORKFLOW, PORT-LINUX-LOCAL.\n- drop-fixed 2, verified today: COMPILER-UNIT-TAIL-RETURN (generated tail-recursive unit loops now end in 'return ();'), COMPILER-MISSING-SYMBOL-DIAGNOSTIC (errors name the unbound symbol with file:line:col).\n- drop 31: GPT-era governance or umbrella epics with no consumer (autopoietic loop, sensor policy, causal delta store, formal retirement ceremony...), retired eras (bundles, smoke inventory, ZIP-by-PID promotion), or shipped in substance (CANONICAL-PLAN-IR: kit_do_program tokenizes into typed steps).\n- No new item was needed: no row was a live gap without a home.\nRETIREMENT: the file is only read when someone passes C:\\home\\git\\kit as a backlog root (the src hits for 'state/agile.spi' are kit's generic per-root path). Retiring it means moving a tracked file in the kit repo, a change the user reviews, so it is proposed here, not done: move kit/state/agile.spi to kit/state/archive/agile-gpt-era.spi (archive, never delete).")
inl note_of_kit_legacy_state_triage_3 () = Note ("KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE", 3u32, "2026-10-31T12:32Z", "kit", "10-31 08:3x kit: THE FULL TABLE now lives in this note; the C:\\home\\data path in n2 no longer exists. The TSV was archived when kit-drafts was emptied on 10-30 (restorable: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-230011, blob CB824E46..., 3799 B), and a backlog note must not depend on a side file (research-lives-in-backlog). 41 rows:\nPUBLIC-BINARY-PROFESSIONALISM: drop (GPT-era umbrella; CLI safety now lives in concrete items (KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD, DELETE-ROOT-GUARD, receipts on every verb))\nSPI-RUNTIME-DRIFT-BURNDOWN: map -> EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION (rust_global drift burn-down is that epic's scope)\nFORMAL-RETIREMENT-CEREMONY: drop (GPT-era release governance; the release train (EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN) is the rule)\nSPI-SAMPLE-STUDY: drop (GPT-era prototype study; GADT/existential work lives in EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES and lib items)\nSPI-ADAPTER-INVENTORY: drop (99% GPT-era inventory; superseded by GRANULAR-LINT census and HAND-CRATE-UNITS)\nMAPPING-FILESYSTEM-TRANSACTION: map -> EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY (granular typed fs mapping = the OS boundary package item)\nSPI-SHARED-PACKAGES: drop (99% GPT-era; package reuse is the lib-first rule (AGENTS))\nAUTH-NO-DIRECT-RUST: map -> EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION (no hand Rust = AGENTS style contract + granular migration)\nDOMAIN-AGILE: drop (GPT-era epic; kit agile is shipped and tracked by its own items (EOIE-SCRUM-XP etc.))\nDOMAIN-BUNDLE: drop (bundles retired (EOIE-CONSOL-BUNDLE-ERA Paused: no consumer))\nDOMAIN-PROXY: drop (proxy verbs shipped; remaining OS work = EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY)\nSTATE-TYPED-REDESIGN: drop (GPT-era; typed state is the style contract (unions/records), enforced by kit standards)\nSOTA-FOUR-PILLARS: drop (GPT-era umbrella over patch/agile/bundle/proxy)\nCOMPILER-RUST-BACKEND: drop (compiler gaps belong to the compiler team's backlog (packs))\nE2E-COLD-FOUNDATION: drop (99% GPT-era; cold proofs = release train candidate + notebooks)\nCOVERAGE-FLOOR-RECOVERY: drop (GPT-era coverage checkpoint; not a current gate)\nCANONICAL-PLAN-IR: drop (done in substance: kit_do_program tokenizes into typed steps (no line reparsing))\nAUTOPOIETIC-LOOP-DENOMINATOR: drop (GPT-era autonomy theory, no consumer)\nINTERNAL-AGENT-AUTHORITY: drop (GPT-era; authority = user-only rules + peer-cannot-grant-escalation)\nSENSOR-POLICY-FEEDBACK: drop (GPT-era, no consumer)\nTOOL-CAPABILITY-ACTIONS: drop (GPT-era, no consumer)\nCOLD-SELF-PROMOTION: drop (GPT-era; promotion = release train + user install gates)\nCAUSAL-DELTA-STORE: drop (GPT-era, no consumer)\nPORT-STRICT-RELEASE: map -> EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (staged distribution = the release train)\nSPIRAL-NATIVE-SOURCE-OWNERSHIP: map -> EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION (no hand-written Rust artifacts)\nSPIRAL-NATIVE-DEVELOPER-WORKFLOW: map -> EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW (native dev workflow + its CI)\nCOMPILER-UNIT-TAIL-RETURN: drop-fixed (verified 10-30: generated tail-recursive unit loops end in 'return ();' (kit_machine_sample rows_from))\nCOMPILER-MISSING-SYMBOL-DIAGNOSTIC: drop-fixed (verified 10-30: compile errors print 'ETY-UnboundVariable: Unbound term variable: <name>' with file:line:col)\nONBOARDING-DOCTOR-ORIENT-TUTORIAL: drop (kit guide + job doctor ship; GPT-era tutorial scope has no consumer)\nIMMUTABLE-JOURNAL-RECEIPTS: drop (every kit verb prints a receipt; journal staging is GPT-era)\nCONFINED-IO-CODECS: drop (no consumer for base64/gzip/xz stdin codecs)\nQUARRY-FINAL-MINING: drop (GPT-era oracle mining)\nPARALLEL-READINESS-REASSESSMENT: drop (superseded by the gpt5parallel/hopacsota work)\nPHYSICAL-BOUNDARY-HARDENING: map -> EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY (OS boundary hardening)\nAUTONOMOUS-WORKSTREAM-LEASES: drop (GPT-era; leases = kit tree/window leases (shipped))\nMETA-STATE-REFLECTION: drop (GPT-era, no consumer)\nDOGFOOD-SMOKE-INVENTORY: drop (legacy smoke era; tests are Spiral notebooks + CLI notebooks)\nDOGFOOD-GROWTH-PREDECESSOR-STAGE: drop (GPT-era release mechanism (ZIP by PID); release train replaced it)\nPORT-LINUX-LOCAL: map -> EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW (Linux runs = CI's ubuntu job (test-dev-workflow on both OSes); WSL waits per no-wsl-until-workflow-passes)\nPROMOTION-CANDIDATE: drop (self-described archaeology only)\nPROMOTION-EXCLUSIVE-CUTOVER: drop (self-described superseded)\nLEFT (why 90%, not Done): 'retire the file by rule'. kit/state is a Spiral package and agile.spi is a module in its package.spiproj, next to live data (evidence.spi and others), so retiring means removing the module from package.spiproj and checking every consumer of the state package (typecheck, regen, kit agile check on the kit root). That is a targeted change for a quiet tree, not a groom-time archive.")
