inl note_of_kit_legacy_state_triage_6 () = Note ("KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T18:19Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 14:2x microblog (help pool), the consumer census the 'retire by rule' step needed, read-only: kit/state/agile.spi is 164,318 bytes, 355 inl/let rows, last touched c28f318 (10-18). (1) PACKAGES: no package depends on the kit/state package. The four package.spiproj files that mention 'state' (rig_agile_sprint_state, rig_agile_state, rig_job_state, rig_repo_state) list their OWN module named state, not ../state. (2) SCRIPTS and CI: no kit build.ps1, scripts/*.ps1 or workflow references kit/state, 'state' as a package, or state/agile. (3) The many 'state/agile.spi' strings in src are the generic <root>/state/agile.spi path every backlog root uses, not this file. So retiring is: drop the 'agile' line from kit/state/package.spiproj modules, and move state/agile.spi to the archive (archive-never-delete), leaving evidence.spi and the other live modules. Checks after: kit agile check and typecheck on any root still green (they don't load kit/state), plus one kit standards run over state. Not applied (rig's repo; asked rig). dod: the module is out of package.spiproj, the file is archived, and the checks are green.")
inl note_of_kit_legacy_state_triage_7 () = Note ("KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T18:21Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:5x rig APPLIED microblog's last step (owner's go, applied by the owner; unstaged). Re-verified first: no kit package, script, workflow or contract reads kit/state/agile.spi (every state/agile.spi reference in src is a BACKLOG root's state file, a different file); git log shows its content unchanged since c28f318 (2026-10-18; the 11-07 mtime is a checkout touch). Done: archived to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\kit-state-agile-legacy-20261109\\agile.spi (hash-verified copy, plus package.spiproj.before), dropped the agile line from kit/state/package.spiproj (git diff: 1 deletion, nothing else), removed state/agile.spi from the tree (git: D). evidence.spi and every other live state module stay. It rides the next train's regen, which compiles the state package without it.")
inl note_of_kit_legacy_state_triage_8 () = Note ("KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T18:21Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 14:2x rig APPLIED it (unstaged): the module line is dropped from kit/state/package.spiproj (1 deletion), and state/agile.spi is archived hash-verified under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\kit-state-agile-legacy-20261109 and removed from the tree; rig re-checked the census. PENDING: the compile proof is the next train's regen of the state package (TRAIN43); close on its green.")
