inl note_of_lib_otp_factory_supervisor_1 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-FACTORY-SUPERVISOR", 1u32, "2026-10-24T10:23Z", "x", "From the 10-24 agent survey of Erlang/OTP patterns worth modelling in Gleam (lib has erlang_process subject/pid/monitor/selector, otp_actor builder/next/started, otp_supervisor static). Needed for per-connection and per-job workers, e.g. the x sim runner shell (SIM-IN-SPIRAL).")
inl note_of_lib_otp_factory_supervisor_2 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-FACTORY-SUPERVISOR", 2u32, "2026-10-24T10:37Z", "x", "10-24 06:37 x: API read from the pinned gleam_otp 1.3.0 source (gleam/otp/factory_supervisor.gleam, 463 lines). Planned lib surface, mirroring otp_supervisor/otp_actor and one call per primitive: nominals factory a d = factory_supervisor.Supervisor(a, d), factory_builder a d = Builder(a, d), factory_message a d = Message(a, d); worker_child / supervisor_child (template : a -> otp_actor.start_result d, passed as a closure VALUE, as otp_actor.on_message already does, so no closure body sits in a macro); named (builder, erlang_process.name (factory_message a d)), which builds on LIB-OTP-NAME; restart_tolerance, timeout, restart_strategy (otp_supervisor's restart union); start -> start_result (factory a d); supervised -> child spec, so a factory can sit under a static supervisor; start_child (factory, argument) -> start_result d; count_children -> i32; get_by_name (name) -> factory a d. Gleam test: a named factory starts 3 echo workers, count_children = 3, each worker answers a call. First consumer: the x sim runner shell's per-job executors (SIM-IN-SPIRAL).")
inl note_of_lib_otp_factory_supervisor_3 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-FACTORY-SUPERVISOR", 3u32, "2026-11-07T22:15Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: lib wraps gleam_otp 1.3.0's factory_supervisor (dynamic children, simple_one_for_one) beside the static supervisor, with a test that starts 3 dynamic children and survives one crashing. Next step: write the planned surface from x's 10-24 API read as a draft module. TypeFeatures: the child-spec as a nominal over the child's message type.")
