inl note_of_lib_otp_ets_1 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-ETS", 1u32, "2026-10-24T10:23Z", "x", "From the 10-24 agent survey of Erlang/OTP patterns worth modelling in Gleam (lib has erlang_process subject/pid/monitor/selector, otp_actor builder/next/started, otp_supervisor static). The standard fix when one process becomes a read bottleneck. Check overlap with Cells' ETS use (CELLS-ETS-OWNER) before designing.")
inl note_of_lib_otp_ets_2 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-ETS", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:15Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: lib ets with new/insert/lookup/delete as one-call typed primitives over table k v, with a Gleam test sharing reads between 2 actors without copying through a mailbox. Next step: read gleam's erlang ETS bindings (gleam_erlang or a hex package) for the FFI surface. TypeFeatures: table k v as a nominal so keys and values cannot be mixed across tables.")
