inl planning_of_lib_otp_statem () = Planning ("LIB-OTP-STATEM", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_otp_statem_1 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-STATEM", 1u32, "2026-10-24T10:23Z", "x", "From the 10-24 agent survey of Erlang/OTP patterns worth modelling in Gleam (lib has erlang_process subject/pid/monitor/selector, otp_actor builder/next/started, otp_supervisor static). The long-term, most distinctive layer.")
inl note_of_lib_otp_statem_2 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-STATEM", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:15Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: actor_ref state msg where only messages valid in the current state type-check, demonstrated by a door state machine whose illegal transitions are compile errors (control: one illegal send fails to type). Next step: prototype the state-indexed ref with phantom types on the deterministic arm first. TypeFeatures: state-indexed references (phantom state parameter), session-type style.")
inl note_of_lib_otp_statem_3 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-STATEM", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:15Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:1x: waiting - lib/spiral shared-lib item (state-indexed actor_ref via a phantom state param, session-type style). Next step = prototype the state-indexed ref on the deterministic arm. Like GRANULAR, a lib/spiral edit is window-gated (do not edit outside the lib_land_window per the file_system.spi lesson; a train snapshots WIP) and needs consumer verification - a dedicated lib-land effort, not light-round standalone.")
inl lib_otp_code_change () = Task ("LIB-OTP-CODE-CHANGE", "lib/spiral: typed hot code upgrade: a state_vN -> state_vN+1 migration hook (Erlang code_change) for supervised actors", Story, P3, D4, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-OTP-NAME", "lib,gleam,otp,backends,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_otp_code_change () = Planning ("LIB-OTP-CODE-CHANGE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_otp_code_change_1 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-CODE-CHANGE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T10:23Z", "x", "From the 10-24 agent survey of Erlang/OTP patterns worth modelling in Gleam (lib has erlang_process subject/pid/monitor/selector, otp_actor builder/next/started, otp_supervisor static). Rarely modelled, but one of the reasons to pick BEAM (BACKEND-BALANCE's G5).")
inl note_of_lib_otp_code_change_2 () = Note ("LIB-OTP-CODE-CHANGE", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:15Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: a supervised lib actor upgrades state_v1 -> state_v2 through a typed migration hook (Erlang code_change) in a Gleam test that hot-loads the new module and keeps serving. Next step: check whether gleam_otp exposes code_change at all; if not, record the Erlang FFI needed. TypeFeatures: the migration as a function state_v1 -> state_v2 whose types make a missed field a compile error.")
inl formatter_then_below () = Task ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", "apps/spiral/spiral.spi still has `then` laid on the line below its if: find whether the formatter fix was never reapplied there or the formatter still emits it, fix the source, re-lay the file (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 60u32, Blocked, "FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", "formatter,apps,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_then_below () = Planning ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:02Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:02 main: found and healed. The installed formatter (5f) keeps `if c then` + block intact (stdin probe), but it also keeps an authored LONE `then` line (`if c` / `then` / block), because it never joins authored breaks. Those lone-then lines are artifacts of the 10-20 formatter runs: 2 in the 10-02 lib+apps/spiral, 37 now (33 at HEAD plus 4 in spiral.spi's unstaged diff). Healed by a token-neutral join (%TEMP%\\lib-lone-then\\apply.ps1: `if/elif cond` + lone `then` -> one line when it fits in 120; whitespace-only, checked per file): apps/spiral/spiral.spi 4 sites now; lib 27 sites in 8 files through the land guard (main-serial-lone-then). async, base, sm', sm'_real and trace come after their heal slices land. Formatter rule for the next formatter pack: a lone `then` line whose previous line is an if/elif condition at the same indent joins it when the result fits, the only case where the formatter joins an authored break (lone then is never an authored habit: 2 in the whole 10-02 corpus).")
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_2 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 2u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_3 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 3u32, "2026-10-31T20:56Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_4 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:12Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:4x re-measured: lone 'then' lines = 0 in spiral (*.spi, *.spir). The defect came back in edition-3 form, a lone '?>' under '? cond': spiral 76 (apps/compiler 33, lib 23, apps/cells 20; 66 of 67 fit in 120 when joined), kit 238, fiscal 73, others 1-3. Waits on FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN (compiler, filed now): one formatter rule instead of hand heals across 5 repos. Next step: when it lands, format spiral lib + apps through the land guard and recount; the other lanes format their own repos.")
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_5 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 5u32, "2026-11-06T15:39Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:3x the rule exists: compiler's pack55d (box 11:2x, node 11:33) formatter joins a lone then/?> onto its condition when it fits in 120 (FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN, lib corpus parse-same 154/154, 0 lines over 120 created). Per compiler's fleet rule, no lane reformats with it until the user's spiral push carries the core (CI formats with the committed compiler, so reformatting early turns CI red); then each lane reformats its tree in one pass (spiral 638, kit 873, fiscal 109 lines at compiler's census) and this item closes on a recount of 0. Resume when the user's push lands.")
