inl lib_format_automation () = Task ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", "Unformatted code still lands in lib: automate formatting at land time (gate kit and lib_land run the formatter on touched files) and measure its cost so it does not clog the queue (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D3, 60u32, Active, "", "formatter,lib,tooling,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_format_automation () = Planning ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_1 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:55Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:55 main: measured: the installed formatter checks all of lib in 22 s on 2 threads (SPIRAL_FORMAT_PARALLEL=2), so it cannot clog the queue. Today 18 files would change, and 86 over-120 lines are strings and macros the formatter leaves alone (sm'_real 51, benchmark 12, trace 5). Automation: the gate kit's land.ps1 now hashes every lib file before the apply and formats exactly the files the apply touched, with the installed formatter, which is token-neutral by its own corpus gate. Every land therefore leaves its files formatted, and no file outside the slice is reflowed under another team's pending anchors. The files no pending slice edits (csv, conversation, cursor_walk, date_time, float_text, lustre, parsing, near_wallet) are formatted by a guarded land now (main-serial-format-idle). The other 10 (env, file_system, json_schema, oauth, otp_actor, otp_supervisor, resultm, sm', xpath_eval, xsd_emit) get formatted by their pending lands. oauth and otp_* are x drafts, so they wait for x.")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_2 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 2u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_3 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 3u32, "2026-10-31T20:57Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_4 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:47Z", "main", "main 11-06 10:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: lib_land_window and the kit gate run the formatter on touched lib files, and a land with an unformatted file is refused or auto-formatted; proven by one land. Next step: check whether lib_land_window's format --check (respell drift) covers layout, not only spelling.")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_5 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 5u32, "2026-11-07T22:14Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. TypeFeatures: none; a gate step. The land window's respell_drift already refuses one class of unformatted text (it caught sm'.char_code today); the formatter run is the missing half.")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_6 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 6u32, "2026-11-11T00:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 MEASURED + design. The formatter exists (SPIRAL-FORMATTER 95%): SpiralCompiler.dll format-corpus check|format [--out dir] <file.spi>... (not --format, which the CLI parses as an output path). On the box, one lib file (json.spi, 263 lines, a copy): check exits 1 in 2.8 s and reports over-120 lines; format writes the formatted file in 10.7 s, both dominated by dotnet start and the parse. Live evidence the gap is real: formatting json.spi changes 2 places, one being the test org2 landed tonight through lib_land_window (JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS: [\"x\"; \"y\"] where the formatter wants [ \"x\"; \"y\" ]) and one pre-existing over-120 assertion line split onto a pipeline line. lib_land_window.ps1 has no format step today (respell_drift is the only text check). DESIGN: step 0 of the land window, before the round trip and every gate, runs format-corpus format on each touched draft (into a temp dir) and REFUSES the land when the formatted bytes differ from the draft, printing the diff, so the author re-formats the draft (rather than the window rewriting bytes after they were proven, which would land unproven text). Cost per land: about 3 s per touched file for check, against a land window of several minutes, so it does not clog the queue. TYPEFEATURES: none (a gate step). Next step: draft the step in spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 (a .ps1 edit to an existing script, not a new one), plus a formatted json.spi as its first proof")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_7 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 7u32, "2026-11-11T00:27Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 ROLLOUT FACT: formatting all 149 lib/spiral/*.spi in one format-corpus process (on the box, 312 s of one core; next whole-lib run goes to a node) finds 14 files whose formatted text differs today: bench_model, event_log, json_scan, json (2 of them from org2 land tonight), regex_certificate, sm-prime (sm), ui_dom_ts, ui_dom, ui_signals, ui_view, unicode, xsd_emit, xsd_regex, xsd_resolve. So the refuse-unformatted land step cannot be switched on first: it would block the next land touching any of those 14, for every lane. ORDER: (1) one dedicated land that reformats those 14 (formatter output only, proven through lib_land_window like any land, gates green); (2) then add the step 0 check to lib_land_window.ps1 with a -SkipFormat escape for formatter bugs (FORMATTER-PARENS-MISSES is open). Cost after rollout: ~3 s per touched file. Next step: run format-corpus format over the 14 on ganymede and stage them as one lib land")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_8 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 8u32, "2026-11-11T00:29Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 the 14 split by what the formatter changes (whitespace stripped and compared): WHITESPACE-ONLY (8, safe to land as layout): event_log, json, regex_certificate, sm-prime (sm), ui_dom_ts, unicode, xsd_regex, xsd_resolve. TOKENS CHANGE (6, held): bench_model (40 lines), json_scan (19), ui_dom (214), ui_signals (38), ui_view (74), xsd_emit (89). In json_scan the formatter drops the parentheses of (conv (digits64 ...) : u32) after |: in a conditional, which can move what the : u32 annotation binds to, and FORMATTER-PARENS-MISSES is still open, so token-changing reformats need that fix plus a per-file review before landing. Phase A: one lib land of the 8 whitespace-only files (formatter output from box bytes), proven on ganymede. Phase B: the 6 after FORMATTER-PARENS-MISSES. Then the step 0 check")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_9 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 9u32, "2026-11-11T01:04Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 PHASE A LANDED on the box (unstaged), proof: ganymede org2-fmta (lib_land_window -PrivateLib closed green, 26 passed, mirror digest 9E619EA011BF7CC2; json 19/19). The box copy-land took the -ProvenLog path with a digest mismatch (the mirror carried an unrelated mirror-only land of erlang_port/process from ERLANG-PROCESS-SOTA), so the fast checks reran on the box and passed; box digest after: FC4C149FB8C5E5D8, undo C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261110-205926. 8 whitespace-only reformats now formatter-clean: event_log, json, regex_certificate, sm-prime, ui_dom_ts (1F25778F6763), unicode, xsd_regex, xsd_resolve (sm-prime 8F62DB1E387D). Lanes were told to rebase drafts on those files. Phase B (6 token-changing files) still waits on FORMATTER-PARENS-MISSES; then the step-0 check")
inl platform_bound_tsv () = Task ("PLATFORM-BOUND-TSV", "apps/compiler/tmp/tests/platform-bound.tsv: find why it exists and whether it is drift (TSVs are a slippery slope); move the facts into typed Spiral or the matrix table, delete the TSV (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,tests,drift,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_platform_bound_tsv () = Planning ("PLATFORM-BOUND-TSV", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl compiler_tmp_retire () = Task ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", "Retire apps/compiler/tmp: every script, test and lane folder moves to its proper place (or into Spiral programs), no new folders under tmp (tests/families went in wrongly), tmp/scripts and its new subfolders shrink to zero without losing code; lanes/hopacsota/research and other script euphoria folded or deleted by rule (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Epic, P1, D7, 85u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,tmp,drift,structure", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_tmp_retire () = Planning ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:12Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:12 main: from FLAT-FOLDERS: the samples move (apps/compiler/tmp/samples -> top-level samples/, 9,882 files losing 2 levels) is this epic's first and largest step. test.ps1/matrix.psd1 paths, CI and EXPECTED.tsv ids (samples/<name>) are written to keep their `samples/...` ids, so the oracle needs no re-accept beyond the path root.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-25T14:06Z", "main", "10-25 10:06 main: inventory (10,015 tracked files under apps/compiler/tmp) and destination rules, written before any move (rule: decide by pre-written rules).\n(1) samples/ (9,855): to top-level samples/ per FLAT-FOLDERS, keeping 'samples/<name>' ids so EXPECTED.tsv only changes its path root. Precondition: no matrix reader live (the 5l' review/install/accept done) and an exclusive window, since test.ps1, matrix.psd1 and CI paths change in the same edit.\n(2) compiler/ (host, core, lib, runtime-compat, Directory.Build.props; 13): product code, so it goes to apps/compiler/host etc., next to spiral_compiler.fs. Precondition: build.ps1 and env.ps1 paths updated in the same edit, and a candidate build proves an identical DLL hash (deterministic build).\n(3) tests/ (matrix.psd1, native-shims 31, rust-exports 5): to apps/compiler/tests/.\n(4) scripts/ (62): each script is classified once by rule: an entry point (build.ps1, test.ps1, env.ps1, probe.ps1) moves to apps/compiler/; a method used by several sessions becomes an eoie verb (memory: generic tools, not per-experiment scripts) and the script is deleted once the verb ships; a script with no caller in any repo or CI and no backlog reference newer than 10-20 is deleted by the dangling-check rule (grep the stem in all repos plus consumer builds, with a positive control).\n(5) formatter/ (30 F#/Python prototype files): the formatter lives in the compiler's '/// ## Formatter' section now. Each file is deleted once a grep shows no caller and its function exists in 'SpiralCompiler format' (format.ps1 corpus modes: check format-corpus covers them first).\n(6) lanes/ (14 docs: hopacsota PLAN.md etc.): facts go into backlog notes on the lane's items (memory: research lives in backlog), then the files are deleted.\nOutside references to update in the same edits: .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml, apps/cells (README.md, compiler_daemon.ex, run_notebook.ps1, run_suite.ps1), apps/lisp (lisp.livemd, membership*.spl), apps/zed (fixtures package.spiproj x2, tasks/test-at-row.ps1), scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1, scripts/workflow.ps1. Order: (6) and (5) first (docs and dead code, no readers), then (4) by class, (3), (2), and (1) last in its own window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-25T14:19Z", "main", "10-25 10:19 main: step (5), formatter/ classified, with a correction to the plan's method. The repo grep alone was WRONG for 4 files: candidate-gate.ps1 showed no callers in any repo, yet %TEMP%\\pack-next4\\review.ps1:46 calls it on every pack review, and it runs extract-corpus.ps1, fitting_lines_kept.py and complaints_probe.py. Those are LIVE (the pack review's formatter gate). Also live: report.ps1 (CI: scripts/workflow.ps1), corpus.ps1 (scripts/parser-corpus-gate.ps1), format.ps1 and lint.ps1 (documented entry points in tmp/AGENTS.md). Rule amended: the dangling check also greps %TEMP% pack/gate/serial scripts and follows live callers one level down (memory dangling-check-by-stem). Dead: the 8 F# prototypes (Check, Convert, Flatten, Format, Layout, Lexed, Parsed, Spacing .fsx). They form a closed #load cluster rooted at Format.fsx, which nothing outside the cluster loads, and only lanes/formatter/PLAN.md mentions them. Their function lives in 'SpiralCompiler format'. Deletion waits for the %TEMP% caller scan. The live formatter tooling then moves with step (4) to its proper place (probably apps/compiler/formatter/), not deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-25T15:11Z", "main", "10-25 11:11 main: step (5) part 1 DONE. Deleted the 8 dead F# formatter prototypes (Check, Convert, Flatten, Format, Layout, Lexed, Parsed, Spacing .fsx; unstaged, copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\formatter-fsx). The rule held on every source: no caller in any of 9 repos, CI or the top-level scripts of 144 %TEMP% job folders (453 scripts; positive control: the same scan finds 13 callers of candidate-gate.ps1); a closed #load cluster rooted at Format.fsx; their function lives in 'SpiralCompiler format'. lanes/formatter/PLAN.md still names them as history, and it goes with step (6). Left in formatter/: the live gate tooling (candidate-gate, extract-corpus, fitting_lines_kept, complaints_probe, report, corpus, format, lint) and synthetic/, all moving with step (4).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-25T15:16Z", "main", "10-25 11:16 main: step (6) started. lanes/bend/w64.bend deleted (a hand-written Bend probe of the w64 helpers; 0 references in the repo; copy in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\lanes), and the empty bend/ folder with it. single-flight/README.md's one unique fact is now CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS; the rest repeats tmp/AGENTS.md. RUST_LIBRARY_PLAN.md is finished history (all steps done 09-28). gpt5parallel/README.md's unique fact is the run-log location + 'Select-String runtime_exception_captured'. These three, plus tmp/NEXT.md, which links to them (NEXT.md:168/185/786, AGENTS.md:124), go together in ONE doc pass so no link dangles: facts to backlog notes, AGENTS.md:124 repointed to FRONTIER.md, then the files deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-25T15:18Z", "main", "10-25 11:18 main: lanes/hopacsota/research/ (untracked, 9 per-experiment scripts r3_*/r4_*/tree_paths, 56 KB, all stamped 10-22 00:05, i.e. a lab-drain copy) DELETED; copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\hopacsota-research. Rule basis: per-experiment scripts are not kept (memory generic-tools-not-per-experiment); their findings are cited in backlog notes (r4_deferred 7 lines, r3_simulate 6, r3_instrument 5); the R4 edits they applied are in the tree core (R4 gate met 10-15, seams installed); no job script in %TEMP% calls research/; the only tracked mentions are 2 historical lines in lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md ('job scratch ...r4_deferred.ps1'), which goes in the doc pass.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 7u32, "2026-10-25T15:29Z", "main", "10-25 11:29 main: step (6) doc pass 1 DONE: tmp/NEXT.md (838 lines, frozen since 10-18), lanes/gpt5parallel/README.md, lanes/single-flight/README.md and RUST_LIBRARY_PLAN.md deleted (unstaged, copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\docs; the files stay in git history). Folded first. NEXT.md's 'Open, in order' entries 0-3 were done or obsolete and entry 4 was overtaken (gpt5parallel met the promotion criterion 10-01); entries 5 and 6 became MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS and DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY. The single-flight README's gap is CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS, and the gpt5parallel README's run-log facts are a sentence in tmp/AGENTS.md's gpt5parallel paragraph. Links repointed: AGENTS.md (3), README.md (1, now pointing at the backlog), FRONTIER.md (6), all citing NEXT.md@47d1e562 so they still resolve. Left: one code comment in spiral_compiler.fs:186146 mentions NEXT.md; strip it in the next pack (no-comments rule). Still to fold: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md (85 KB), lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (92 KB), lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (90 KB), hopacsota hop-probes, formatter/allowlist.tsv.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 8u32, "2026-10-25T16:26Z", "main", "10-25 12:26 main: step (6) doc pass 2 DONE: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md (813 lines) and allowlist.tsv (25 rows) deleted (unstaged; copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\docs\\lanes-formatter), with the empty lanes/formatter/ folder. Folded first: the measured user style, F1-F10, the keep-breaks additions, the G6 banned list, G1-G7 and the process rules are one note on SPIRAL-FORMATTER. The user decisions were already notes (SPIRAL-FORMATTER 1, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS 1). Scoreboards and the decision-change log are history, kept at PLAN.md@0ec501fb. Dangling check: 0 readers of allowlist.tsv or lanes/formatter in the 9 repos, CI, the compiler, or 858 %TEMP% job scripts (positive control: candidate-gate.ps1 found 19 times). tmp/AGENTS.md:147 now points at the backlog notes plus PLAN.md@0ec501fb. Left in step 6: lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (92 KB, the live hopacsota contract that memory and AGENTS.md cite, so it is folded last, after its readers are repointed), lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (90 KB), hopacsota hop-probes.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 9u32, "2026-10-25T16:30Z", "main", "10-25 12:30 main: lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (1,045 lines, last edit f5e487e0 10-18) is NOT folded yet, by rule (links must resolve): 23 comments in spiral_compiler.fs cite its fix numbers ('FRONTIER.md fix 22/33-47/50/55'; lines 10746, 15806, 55149, 57317, 83125, 87117, 129890, 135213, 137838, 137863, 137926, 146883, 147687, 149237, 149245, 152779, 157437, 157525, 158919, 186182, 186197, 186243, 188866), as do tmp/AGENTS.md:12 and :89 and 13 backlog notes. Order: (a) the pack after 5m strips those comments (the no-comments rule; the code keeps its meaning in names), together with the NEXT.md comment at :186146; (b) AGENTS.md's citations become FRONTIER.md@f5e487e0; (c) the fix list's still-live facts (the fast loop; fixes 22, 57 and 58 named in AGENTS.md) go into notes on HOPACSOTA items; (d) the file is deleted. Backlog notes citing 'FRONTIER.md fix N' stay readable through the pin.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 10u32, "2026-10-25T16:47Z", "main", "10-25 12:47 main: step (a) of the FRONTIER order is staged for pack 5m: %TEMP%\\pack-next5m\\strip-doc-citations.ps1 -Target <core> [-Apply]. It finds by content every pure line-comment block that cites tmp/NEXT.md or lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (24 blocks, 86 lines on today's tree core, including the NEXT.md one at :186146), refuses a block holding a directive or marker, and proves that every non-comment line is unchanged and in order. On a copy, pair-drift found 0 pairs touched on one side only (8 pairs, 2 touched since HEAD by the user's staged work). Proof in the pack review: a comment-only edit, so residuals must be identical (the review's DISAGREE 0 and 0 differing cells cover it). After 5m installs: AGENTS.md:12/:89 citations become FRONTIER.md@f5e487e0, the live facts move to HOPACSOTA notes, and the file is deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_11 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 11u32, "2026-10-25T17:03Z", "main", "10-25 13:03 main: an outside reference missing from step 1's list: dir-tree-html/package.spiproj has packageDir: deps/spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples (it builds on the samples core). Step 1 must repoint it, or better, move dir-tree-html to lib/spiral first (TREE-PAGES-V2).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_12 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 12u32, "2026-10-25T23:15Z", "main", "10-25 19:15 main: dir-tree-html no longer builds against apps/compiler/tmp/samples. Its package.spiproj is lib-first now (TREE-PAGES-V2 n15; landed unstaged, proven on the node). The outside reference from n11 is resolved for step 1 once the user commits it.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_13 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 13u32, "2026-10-26T00:29Z", "main", "10-25 20:29 main: consumer inventory for the samples core. Of the 393 package.spiproj files with a packageDir in spiral, eoie, x, fiscal, polyglot, alphabet, dice, dir-tree-html, i574n.github and blog (deps, target, _build and .cache excluded), 332 resolve into apps/compiler/tmp, all in spiral. 328 are inside tmp itself (the samples, which move with it). The 4 outside: apps/zed/fixtures/ok and bad (the spiral-zed probe fixtures; ok uses the samples core's +. operator), lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/rename_probe and lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (labs of open items; they follow their items). dir-tree-html left with split4 on 10-25 (step 1). The Zed port is drafted: %TEMP%\\zed-fixtures-lib\\apply.ps1 -Fixtures <dir> [-Apply] checks the 3 files' exact current text first, then gives both fixtures packageDir ../../../../lib with |core- and spiral-, and ok uses + instead of +.. Gate: %TEMP%\\zed-fixtures-lib\\verify.ps1 applies it to a copy (with a lib junction at the same relative depth) and runs the installed dist\\spiral-zed.exe --probe: ok must exit 0, bad nonzero. That is one compiler process per fixture, so it runs after tibia's PR-28 block, then lands unstaged. After that, no product outside tmp needs the samples core.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_14 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 14u32, "2026-10-26T04:35Z", "main", "10-26 00:35 main: Zed fixtures on lib, GREEN (main-zed-fixtures-lib-verify, 00:19: the installed dist/spiral-zed.exe --probe gives ok exit 0 and bad exit 1 on the copy) and LANDED unstaged in apps/zed/fixtures (both package.spiproj files plus ok/main.spi). No product outside apps/compiler/tmp now needs the samples core; the 2 remaining packages are labs of open items.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_15 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 15u32, "2026-10-26T10:45Z", "main", "10-26 06:45 main: inventory (scratchpad tmp-scripts-inventory.ps1, one pass over every repo's tracked text files, backlog state excluded; %TEMP%\\tmp-scripts-inventory.tsv). apps/compiler/tmp holds 9,999 tracked files: samples 9,854, scripts 62, tests 37, formatter 22 (21 MB, fixtures), compiler 13 (the host), lanes 8, plus AGENTS.md, README.md and .gitignore. Of the 43 script files (.ps1/.py/.fsx): (A) 7 with readers outside tmp: build.ps1 (95 outside references, alphabet's documents build among them), env.ps1 (17, eoie's compiler contracts), install-dotnet.ps1 (7), test.ps1 (6, one CI workflow), test-rust-exports.ps1 (3), heavy.ps1 (3, agent-sync docs), probe.ps1 (2, a Cells test). (B) 13 read only from inside tmp (pair-drift, hopacsota-lint, projection-hash, fast-tier, upstream.py, ...). (C) 23 with no tracked reader. They are on-demand tools, not dead: test-blocks.ps1 ran tonight and rebuild-determinism.ps1 is a 5n repro file; their uses live in backlog notes and job scripts, which the scan doesn't count. So (C) is not a deletion list. Plan, in order, each step one gate: (1) a dangling check by stem over the backlog and the %TEMP%/scratchpad job scripts splits (C) into used tools and dead ones, and only the dead ones go; (2) (B) and the used (C) tools move with their callers into a non-tmp home; (3) (A) moves last, because its 125 outside references need one batch update plus a grep proof that no old path is left. The destination folder is a structure decision; I propose apps/compiler/scripts, the sibling of tmp, so that tmp can go away. Not started.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_16 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 16u32, "2026-10-26T11:36Z", "main", "10-26 07:36 main: step 1 of the n15 plan done; it finds no dead script. The scratchpad tmp-unread-check.ps1 was narrowed: the first version read every .ps1/.json under %TEMP% to depth 4 and was still silent after 40 min, so it was stopped (read-only, nothing to restore). It now reads top-level %TEMP% scripts, %TEMP% folders written in the last 14 days to depth 1 (2,752 scripts under 1,530 folders), session scratchpads to depth 3, and every kit job's argv. All 23 (C) scripts are used. Uses come from backlog notes and items (try.ps1 68, bench-native 11, test-blocks 7, rebuild-determinism 7, machine-watch 7, ...), from job scripts, and from job argv (try.ps1 39, capped-run 23, test-blocks 6). Positive control: test-blocks.ps1, run tonight, reads as used, with 7 backlog, 2 script and 6 job references. So the plan's delete step frees nothing, and every (B) and (C) tool moves in step 2 with its references. Step 2 is still a path decision: the destination folder (proposed apps/compiler/scripts), plus a batch update of the backlog text and the job scripts that name tmp/scripts. Most of the (C) uses are backlog notes, which are history, so step 2 only has to rewrite live callers: job scripts and tracked files.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_17 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 17u32, "2026-10-27T10:32Z", "main", "10-27 06:32 main: drift found by POLYGLOT-RETIRE's phase-2 census (10-27 06:3x): two functions are defined twice with different bodies inside tmp/scripts. Get-FileSha256 in env.ps1 and in test.ps1 (test.ps1 dot-sources env.ps1, so its own copy shadows the shared one), and Resolve-Results in ci-classify.ps1 and compare-runs.ps1. Both should become one definition in the scripts' shared module when the scripts move to their proper place.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_18 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 18u32, "2026-10-27T11:01Z", "main", "10-27 07:01 main: ownership settled (compiler 10-27 07:0x): the Get-FileSha256 and Resolve-Results dedup is the compiler team's, folded into its CCMR apply, which already holds anchored edits on env.ps1 and test.ps1. Keep env.ps1's Get-FileSha256 and drop test.ps1:367; move Resolve-Results into env.ps1, called by ci-classify.ps1 and compare-runs.ps1. This item's relocation of tmp/scripts is sequenced AFTER CCMR plus dedup lands and moves the files unchanged, so the two files have one writer at a time.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_19 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 19u32, "2026-10-27T16:54Z", "main", "10-27 12:54 main: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts census DONE (session scratchpad tmp-scripts-census.ps1, output TEMP tmp-scripts-census.tsv). The first version never finished: Get-ChildItem -Recurse walked kit's 5.5 GB .cache and the other skipped folders before filtering them, then ran one Contains per script per file, and after 43 CPU-minutes it hadn't finished the walk. Rewritten with a stack walk that prunes .git/target/.cache/deps/samples/_build and similar folders before entering them, plus one compiled alternation regex per file: 3,426 files from 12 repos plus TEMP's first-level scripts, walked in 9 s and scanned in 28 s. Result over the 45 scripts: ENTRY 4 (build, test, env, probe), LIVE-OUTSIDE 23, LIVE-INTERNAL 1, BACKLOG-ONLY 17, DEAD-CANDIDATE 0. Positive controls: results-path.ps1 LIVE-OUTSIDE (first caller TEMP matrix-bundle/accept.ps1), try.ps1 LIVE-OUTSIDE (11 outside callers), compare-runs.ps1 LIVE-OUTSIDE (16). The old control (candidate-gate*) no longer matches any script, so it checked nothing and was replaced. Caveat that changes the reading: BACKLOG-ONLY does not mean dead. bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1 is BACKLOG-ONLY (no file names it) yet runs right now as E1, launched from a kit job's argv; scripts launched by hand or by job never appear in a file corpus. So the retirement MOVES all 17 BACKLOG-ONLY scripts with their notes (bench-cells-vs-matrix, capped-run, ci-classify, cost-report, coverage-blockers, coverage-buckets, coverage-probe-queue, ebpf-dual-profile, ebpf-kernel-load, lib-usage-census, lib-usage-consumers, lib-usage-delete-unused.py, machine-watch, matrix-add-backend-to-groups.py, matrix-add-to-list.py, parser-corpus-gate, spiral-processes) and deletes none; nothing here is provably redundant. No file moved yet: scripts are moved only in a window when no job runs them (E1 runs bench-cells-vs-matrix now, and accept-3 queues test.ps1).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_20 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 20u32, "2026-10-27T18:37Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-27: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts PLACEMENT PLAN (n19 census, 45 scripts; plan only, no moves). \"You know that tree best\" ask.\n\nRECOMMENDED STRUCTURE (lowest churn): move the WHOLE tmp/scripts/ folder up one level to apps/compiler/scripts/ (sibling of the retiring tmp). Every intra-folder call is $PSScriptRoot-relative (entries dot-source env.ps1, build.ps1 calls hopacsota-lint/pair-drift/projection-hash, test.ps1 calls fast-tier/compare-runs, probe.ps1 calls profile-summary.py, etc.), so a WHOLE-FOLDER move leaves all of them unchanged -- only the ~125 OUTSIDE references update (main n15 step 3: one batch rewrite + a grep-proof no old path remains). This empties tmp/scripts and lets tmp retire. Keeps entries WITH their helpers (no entry/helper relative-path split).\nALTERNATIVE (main n2 step 4): hoist the 4 ENTRY to apps/compiler/ (public API at the compiler root), tools to apps/compiler/scripts/. Cleaner conceptual split BUT every entry<->tool relative path inside the scripts changes (build/test/probe <-> their helpers), adding churn + a second path-rewrite surface. RECOMMEND the whole-folder move unless the API separation is wanted.\n\nPER-CLASS DESTINATION (all -> apps/compiler/scripts/ under the recommended move):\n- ENTRY (4): build.ps1, test.ps1, env.ps1, probe.ps1 -> apps/compiler/scripts/ (recommended) OR apps/compiler/ (alternative).\n- LIVE-INTERNAL (1): profile-summary.py (probe.ps1's helper) -> apps/compiler/scripts/ (stays beside probe.ps1).\n- LIVE-OUTSIDE (23): .gitignore*, bench-native, bench-pair, ci-runs, compare-runs, export-check-fsharp, export-check-rust, fast-tier, heavy, hopacsota-g3, hopacsota-lint, install-dotnet, lib-usage-references, memory-cap, pair-drift, profile-thread.py, projection-hash, rebuild-determinism, results-path*, test-blocks, test-rust-exports, try, upstream.py -> apps/compiler/scripts/.\n- BACKLOG-ONLY (17, MOVE WITH NOTES, delete none -- n19 caveat: BACKLOG-ONLY != dead; bench-cells-vs-matrix runs now as E1 from job argv): bench-cells-vs-matrix, capped-run, ci-classify, cost-report, coverage-blockers, coverage-buckets, coverage-probe-queue, ebpf-dual-profile, ebpf-kernel-load, lib-usage-census, lib-usage-consumers, lib-usage-delete-unused.py, machine-watch, matrix-add-backend-to-groups.py, matrix-add-to-list.py, parser-corpus-gate, spiral-processes -> apps/compiler/scripts/.\n\nSPECIAL CASES (NOT a plain file move):\n- .gitignore (tmp/scripts/.gitignore): merge its rules into apps/compiler/.gitignore (or the repo root .gitignore); it is not a script and does not \"move\".\n- results-path.ps1: it currently holds the deduped Resolve-Results (ci-classify.ps1 + compare-runs.ps1 source it). main n18 proposes folding Resolve-Results into env.ps1 instead -> then results-path.ps1 is DELETED (both callers use env.ps1's). So: if n18 is taken, results-path.ps1 is absorbed, not moved; confirm with the dedup landing (the CCMR apply already holds the env.ps1/test.ps1 anchors but currently only the Get-FileSha256 dedup, not Resolve-Results -- reconcile before the move).\n- Get-FileSha256 dedup (n18): env.ps1 keeps it, test.ps1:367 drops its copy -- already folded into the staged CCMR apply.\n\nEOIE-VERB CANDIDATES (move to apps/compiler/scripts/ now; convert later as separate work, per n2 \"a method used by several sessions becomes an eoie verb, the script deleted once the verb ships\"): the generic cross-session tools -- memory-cap, capped-run, machine-watch, spiral-processes, lib-usage-census/consumers/delete-unused. Flag only; this move keeps them as scripts.\n\nSEQUENCING (hard constraints from n18/n19): (1) runs AFTER CCMR + the dedup land, so env.ps1/test.ps1 have one writer at a time, and the move then carries the files UNCHANGED. (2) Move only in a window when NO job runs these scripts (accept-3 runs test.ps1; E1 runs bench-cells-vs-matrix) -- a quiet exclusive window like the samples move. (3) Batch-update the ~125 outside references in the same edit + grep-proof no old apps/compiler/tmp/scripts path remains (positive control, dangling-check-by-stem). The 17 BACKLOG-ONLY scripts' backlog-note references are history (not rewritten live), but any LIVE caller (job scripts, tracked files, CI, AGENTS.md, README.md) is.\n\nNET: one new folder (apps/compiler/scripts), 43 files moved unchanged + .gitignore merged + results-path.ps1 absorbed-or-moved per n18; 0 deletions; tmp/scripts -> empty. Destination for tests/ (apps/compiler/tests, n2 step 3) and compiler/ host (apps/compiler/host, n2 step 2) are separate steps already ruled.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_21 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 21u32, "2026-10-27T18:40Z", "main", "10-27 14:40 main: Decision on n20's placement plan (main, technical call; it stays inside apps/compiler, so it isn't new top-level structure): (1) WHOLE-FOLDER move: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/ becomes apps/compiler/scripts/ as one unit. Every intra-folder call is $PSScriptRoot-relative and stays valid unchanged; only the ~125 outside references get the batch rewrite. Hoisting the 4 entries separately would also churn every entry-to-tool relative path. All 45 scripts move, the 17 BACKLOG-ONLY ones with their notes, and none are deleted. .gitignore merges into apps/compiler/.gitignore. (2) CORRECTION to n18: results-path.ps1 is NOT absorbed into env.ps1. env.ps1:2 sets Set-StrictMode -Version 3.0, and Resolve-Results' body (the Leaf plus nested single-flight-* search) trips StrictMode; that is why it lives in its own strictness-free file, sourced by ci-classify.ps1:7 and compare-runs.ps1:3 (and by main's TEMP matrix-bundle/compare-accept.ps1). It moves with the folder as a separate module. The Get-FileSha256 dedup into env.ps1 is unaffected, since that function is StrictMode-clean and already in the CCMR apply. (3) Sequencing unchanged: after CCMR and the dedup land, in a window when no job runs these scripts, with file contents unchanged by the move. Outside references in main's TEMP harnesses (matrix-bundle accept/compare-accept, rmd-wildcard, chain manifests) are part of the rewrite list. (4) The eoie-verb candidates n20 flags (memory-cap, capped-run, machine-watch, spiral-processes, lib-usage-*) are converted later, each as its own item.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_22 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 22u32, "2026-10-28T11:35Z", "main", "10-28 07:35 main: Reference census for the n21 whole-folder move (tmp/scripts/ to apps/compiler/scripts/), main 10-28 07:3x, Grep across the repos (no moves). Live callers outside the folder: spiral scripts/workflow.ps1 (5, the CI workflow), apps/cells README.md (1) and priv/new_project/scripts/probe.ps1 and gate.ps1 (1 each, the new-project scaffold); lab/ 53 refs in 44 files (they move or retire with their items, so rewrite them in the same batch); i574n.github/scripts serial-runner.ps1, respell-repo.ps1 and remote.ps1 (1 each); kit FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md (1, prose). x, fiscal and tibia: 0. Backlog notes (agile.spi 62, done-notes 12) are history and stay as written. Also unknown: each lane's TEMP and scratchpad scripts (this session's matrix-bundle, pack-*, lib-gate-kit, and the compiler and kit scratch dirs). They break at the cutover, so the move needs a heads-up to every lane plus one release of overlap. Cutover plan: (1) a window with no tmp/scripts process running (no test.ps1, build.ps1 or env.ps1 consumer; kit TRAIN-free, compiler not building); (2) move the folder, then rewrite the 8 live repo refs plus the 3 org scripts plus lab in one pass, each rewrite an exact path replace with a count check; (3) leave a tiny forwarding env.ps1 at the old path that warns and dot-sources the new one, for one day, so lanes' TEMP scripts keep working while they update. Avoid a junction, since git on Windows would see a second tree. Candidate window: 20:00-21:00 today after TRAIN4, or tomorrow morning. Estimate 60 min.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_23 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 23u32, "2026-10-28T11:36Z", "main", "10-28 07:36 main: CORRECTION to n21 (main's 10-27 14:40 decision), found 10-28 07:3x before any move. 'Every intra-folder call is $PSScriptRoot-relative and stays valid' is true for script-to-script calls only. 12 scripts reach SIBLING folders or fixed depths through '..', and those break when scripts/ moves up a level: (1) env.ps1:4 $script:BundleRoot = Split-Path $PSScriptRoot -Parent, which is the root every script uses for samples, tests, compiler/host and target. After the move it would resolve to apps/compiler instead of apps/compiler/tmp. CCMR's det-root and PathMap are keyed on BundleRoot, so the move could also change core DLL bytes (compiler team: re-check by hash). (2) Sibling-relative paths: bench-native.ps1:15-16 ('../samples', '../tests/native-shims'), bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1:3 ('..\\tests\\families'), coverage-probe-queue.ps1:7 and ci-classify.ps1:24 ('../tests/matrix.psd1'), test.ps1:855 ('../tests/native-shims/kotlin-server'), ebpf-kernel-load.ps1:2 ('../samples'), parser-corpus-gate.ps1:21 ('..\\formatter\\corpus.ps1'). (3) Depth-relative paths that change by one level: try.ps1:23 and lib-usage-consumers.ps1:9 ('../../../..' to the repo root, which becomes '../../..'), pair-drift.ps1:2 ('../../spiral_compiler.fs' becomes '../spiral_compiler.fs'), env.ps1:129 ('../../runtime' becomes '../runtime'), machine-watch.ps1:3 ('../../../../../kit/kit.exe' loses one level). Revised plan: in the same cutover, env.ps1 sets BundleRoot explicitly to apps/compiler/tmp (while samples, tests, compiler and formatter still live there), the sibling paths go through $BundleRoot instead of '..', and the depth paths shift by one, each an exact replace with a count check. The compiler team confirms CCMR by-hash at the default det-root after the move: a rebuild of the installed core must still give 05E94769. That cross-check is part of the move's done rule. Without (1)-(3) the move would break test.ps1, build.ps1 and every bench at once.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_24 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 24u32, "2026-10-28T11:38Z", "main", "10-28 07:38 main: Mover drafted (TEMP tmp-retire/move.ps1, dry by default): the 14 corrected path edits from n23 (BundleRoot pinned to tmp; sibling paths through ../tmp; depth paths up one), each an exact replace with an exactly-once check. Dry run 10-28 07:3x: all 14 anchors match once in 12 scripts. Then a folder move plus a forwarding env.ps1 at the old path that warns and dot-sources the new one. Weakness found in the dry run: its 'in use' guard (a process command line naming tmp/scripts) saw 0 while main's speed A/B was running build.ps1, because dot-sourced env.ps1 and child builds don't carry the path in their command line. So the guard is advisory only. The real precondition is coordination: announce the window, then require 'no runs' acks from compiler, kit and x (the test.ps1 and build.ps1 users) and kit job list showing no running matrix, build or train job. Still to add before -Apply: the rewrite of the 8 live outside refs (scripts/workflow.ps1 x5, apps/cells README and the two new_project scaffold scripts), the 3 org scripts (serial-runner, respell-repo, remote) and lab's 53, plus the compiler team's by-hash rebuild check (05E94769) as the done rule.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_25 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 25u32, "2026-10-28T11:40Z", "main", "10-28 07:40 main: Mover complete for its dry run (10-28 07:3x, TEMP tmp-retire/move.ps1): 14 path anchors match once in 12 scripts, and 51 callers (48 in spiral: scripts/workflow.ps1, apps/cells README and the 2 new_project scaffold scripts, 44 lab files; plus 3 i574n.github/scripts) each hold at least one reference, rewritten by an exact slash-preserving regex. Compiler team review: pinning BundleRoot to apps/compiler/tmp is CCMR-safe. PathMap's left side is literally $BundleRoot, so the unchanged source location keeps mapping to /_b/. The scripts' own location never enters a build. The core bytes depend only on the det-root. DONE RULE (set before the move): after the move, rebuild single-flight at the default det-root and require BOTH the core SpiralCompilerCore.dll == 05E94769A86A9B9C AND the host SpiralCompiler.dll == A4E480202BD40D80 (today's installed hashes). The host hash is the one that catches a BundleRoot mistake, because the core is protected by the det-root and would pass anyway. Plus test.ps1 -Suite smoke passing from the new path. Window: 20:00-21:00 today (compiler confirms no builds then; kit TRAIN4 ends at 20:00). Precondition: 'no runs' acks from compiler, kit and x, since the process guard can't see dot-sourced env.ps1.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_26 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 26u32, "2026-10-28T11:46Z", "main", "10-28 07:46 main: Mover update (10-28 07:4x). (1) x made the 3 shared org scripts (serial-runner, respell-repo, remote) dual-path: each resolves apps/compiler/scripts first and falls back to tmp/scripts, so they need no rewrite and are dropped from callers.txt (48 callers left, dry run clean). (2) Gap found via x: serial-runner calls heavy.ps1, and the plan's env.ps1-only forwarder would have broken every old-path call of test.ps1, build.ps1, heavy.ps1 and the rest. Fixed: after the move, every moved .ps1 gets a stub at the old path. env.ps1's stub dot-sources the new one; every other stub runs `& <new> @args` then `exit $LASTEXITCODE`, after a warning. Probe (scratch stub-probe): named params, a string array and a switch pass through, and the exit code passes through both via pwsh -File (7) and an in-process & (7). Under pwsh -File a comma list arrives as one string, exactly like a direct pwsh -File call, so the stubs change nothing for callers. Acks for 20:00 so far: compiler, kit, x, tibia, fiscal (each sends 'no runs' at 20:00; kit warns if TRAIN4 runs long).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_27 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 27u32, "2026-10-28T22:48Z", "main", "10-28 18:5x main: tonight's 20:00 retire window is OFF. The move tool (%TEMP%\\tmp-retire\\move.ps1 + callers.txt, dry run clean at 09:4x: 14 path anchors in 12 scripts, 48 callers) was lost in the profile wipe (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY), and every lane is paused or logged out. Rebuild the move script from note n23's design (env.ps1 BundleRoot pin, sibling ../tmp paths, depth paths up one level, stubs that dot-source or forward @args + exit code) and re-run its dry run before any window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_28 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 28u32, "2026-10-29T01:48Z", "main", "10-28 21:4x main: mover dry run REBUILT after the wipe, now in the repo so a TEMP loss can't take it again: spiral lab/COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE/move.ps1 (unstaged; dry run only, writes just callers.txt beside it). Rebuilt from n23-n26: the 14 exact anchor replaces (BundleRoot pinned to apps/compiler/tmp, sibling paths through ../tmp, depth paths up one level) match exactly once in 12 scripts, as at 09:4x. Caller census regenerated with git grep --untracked over spiral, i574n.github and kit (backlog notes stay as history; kit FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md is kept as written): 53 to rewrite, 3 org scripts already dual-path. NEW since the 07:3x census, and missing from the lost callers.txt: apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 and run_suite.ps1, apps/compiler/AGENTS.md, apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, and one more lab file; the old tool would have broken them. Stubs planned: 39 .ps1 at the old path. Still to write before a window: the apply stage (folder move, the stubs per n26, and the slash-preserving caller rewrite), then this dry run again, then n25's hash done rule.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_29 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 29u32, "2026-10-29T05:42Z", "main", "10-29 01:4x main: mover APPLY and UNDO written and rehearsed (spiral lab/COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE, unstaged: move.ps1 [-Apply|-Undo], rehearse.ps1, kit-dual-path.ps1, kit-rehearse.ps1). Three gaps in the pre-wipe design (n23-n26), found and fixed: (1) 7 more upward-relative paths that n23 missed: coverage-blockers.ps1:4 and coverage-buckets.ps1:4 ('..' is the bundle), bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1:85 ($scripts '..\\..\\..\\..'), and 4 Python files (lib-usage-delete-unused parents[4]; matrix-add-backend-to-groups and matrix-add-to-list parents[1]/tests; upstream.py '..','..'). There are 21 anchors now; each must match exactly once AND resolve to the same target from the new folder (positive control: a New left at the old relative path fails 2 rows). (2) 23 callers DOT-SOURCE heavy.ps1 or tree-cpu.ps1. n26's stub ('& new @args; exit') would have exited the caller and defined none of its functions. Stubs now dot-source when InvocationName is '.', and they print their notice on stderr, because Write-Warning lands on stdout under pwsh -File and would corrupt parsed output. (3) Bundle-relative callers ($bundle + 'scripts/...') are invisible to a tmp/scripts grep: spiral lib/spiral/lib.ps1 (5 refs) and lib/spiral/bench/parsing/bench.ps1 are rewritten to ../scripts; kit has 8 refs in compiler-contracts/workspace.ps1, test-regeneration.ps1, spiral.ps1 and scripts/workflow.ps1 (CI). Also 3 in-tmp formatter scripts dot-source ..\\scripts\\env.ps1 and are rewritten. Apply refuses while kit refs are still single-path, while the target or an undo dir exists, or while a kit job is running or queued. It copies every touched file to undo\\ with before/after hashes, moves the folder, writes 41 stubs, rewrites 76 files, and re-runs the census (0 old-path callers). Undo refuses if any file changed after the apply, restores by hash and archives the stubs. Rehearsal on a scratch copy (129 files): 11/11 PASS (BundleRoot and the runtime dir are identical via the new path and via the stub; heavy.ps1 defines the same functions via the stub; the -File, & and dot-source stubs match direct calls, exit code 7 included), and the undo leaves 0 differences. kit-dual-path.ps1 (10 anchors; dry on the real kit 10/10, parse-clean) adds Get-KitSpiralScript to workspace.ps1 (tries ../scripts, then scripts) and $spiralScripts to workflow.ps1; kit-rehearse is 8/8 PASS on both layouts and rejects an empty bundle. Window steps: kit applies kit-dual-path.ps1 (or acks main applying it), then compiler, kit and x ack no runs, then move.ps1 -Apply, then n25's done rule (re-read the installed core and host hashes at the window, rebuild by hash, test.ps1 -Suite smoke from the new path). Left outside the tool: the prose in tmp/AGENTS.md and tmp/README.md that names scripts/ relative to tmp.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_30 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 30u32, "2026-10-29T06:12Z", "main", "10-29 02:1x main: CORRECTION to n28-n29: the move tools no longer live in spiral lab/COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE. Creating a new lab folder broke the user's 10-24 rule (stop the lab pattern; experiments go in their committable place). They moved to apps/compiler/packs/tmp-retire/ (with the other anchored appliers; untracked, not ignored): move.ps1, rehearse.ps1, kit-dual-path.ps1, kit-rehearse.ps1 and callers.txt, with their roots one folder deeper and the census self-exclusions repointed. Re-proven there: move.ps1 dry run unchanged (21/21 anchors, 53 callers, 3 dual-path, 3 in-tmp siblings, 6 spiral bundle refs, 8 kit refs, 39 stubs), rehearse 11/11 PASS with undo leaving 0 differences over 129 files, kit-rehearse 8/8 PASS. spiral/lab no longer has a COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE folder.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_31 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 31u32, "2026-10-29T10:44Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: n29's 'left outside the tool' doc prose, counted: apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md has 22 bare scripts/<file> references on 20 lines (13 distinct, 6 of them 'pwsh scripts/...' command lines), and apps/compiler/tmp/README.md has 13 on 13 lines (5 distinct, 7 command lines). Both docs are written for a cwd of tmp, so after the move each becomes ../scripts/<file>. That is the same exact-replace shape as the in-tmp sibling class the mover already handles ('..\\scripts' -> '..\\..\\scripts'), so the next mover revision can take these two files as a fourth class (count checked, undo-copied) instead of leaving them to a hand edit.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_32 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 32u32, "2026-10-29T10:45Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: the doc class is IN the mover (apps/compiler/packs/tmp-retire/move.ps1, unstaged). tmp/AGENTS.md and tmp/README.md get scripts/ -> ../scripts/ (pattern (?<![\\w./-])scripts/, so an already-relative ../scripts or apps/compiler/scripts is untouched); the post-rewrite check requires 0 bare references left, and both files are undo-copied like every other rewrite. Dry run on the real tree: 2 files, 36 references; every other count is unchanged (21/21 anchors, 53 callers, 3 dual-path, 3 in-tmp siblings, 6 bundle refs, 39 stubs). Rehearsal (rehearse.ps1, now copying both docs): apply rewrites 78 files, 12/12 PASS (new: tmp AGENTS.md has 0 bare scripts/ left and 22 ../scripts/), and the undo leaves 0 differences over 131 files. n29's 'left outside the tool' list is now empty.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_33 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 33u32, "2026-10-29T13:04Z", "main", "10-29 09:0x main: rehearsal RE-RUN on today's tree (after kit's dual-path commit 05da38a and pack 6's appliers): packs/tmp-retire/rehearse.ps1 on a scratch copy of 131 files. Positive control fails (exit 1, 2 FAIL rows, as designed). Dry run: 21/21 anchors match exactly once across 18 scripts; 53 callers to rewrite; 0 kit bundle-relative refs still single-path (kit's half is done); 41 stubs planned. Apply: 78 files rewritten, 0 callers left on the old path, every stub check PASS (dot-source, pwsh -File, & in process, exit code forwarded, notice on stderr only); lib.ps1, the formatter and tmp AGENTS.md re-pointed. Undo: 78 restored by hash, 0 differences vs the snapshot. The window is READY; it opens after the pack-6 install (which waits for kit's TRAIN3 publish), as the first heavy-free slot after that. It needs no lib or Cells reader freeze, only no compiler-tmp runs.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_34 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 34u32, "2026-10-29T16:30Z", "main", "10-29 12:3x main: APPLIED (unstaged), right after the pack-6b install, with git-a6's GO (nothing of the compiler lane ran locally against tmp/scripts). Live dry run first: anchors 21/21 match exactly once; 59 callers to rewrite (up from the 09:0x rehearsal's 53, now including 5 in apps/compiler/packs); 0 kit single-path refs; 39 stubs planned. The first -Apply was REFUSED by its own guard because kit jobs were running. The only one was the long-lived node-watch, verified to be i574n.github/scripts/node-watch.ps1, which never references compiler/tmp, so the rerun used -IgnoreJobs. Result: folder moved to apps/compiler/scripts, 39 forwarding stubs, 84 files rewritten (undo copies in packs/tmp-retire/undo), anchors present 21/21, 0 callers still on the old path. Consumer proof: lib.ps1's BuildSpiral through the moved env.ps1 compiles lib/spiral/near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi to Gleam byte-identically to the committed near_wallet.gleam (on the pack-6b install), and dot-sourcing the old-path stub tmp/scripts/env.ps1 still defines the functions. Left: git-a6's build-candidate dry path as the second consumer check; retiring the stubs later, once callers are confirmed migrated (the stubs print a notice on stderr).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_35 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 35u32, "2026-10-29T16:53Z", "main", "10-29 12:5x main: one caller the mover could NOT rewrite. kit src/kit_jobs/host.spi:27 (generated into kit_job_create/create.rs:71) searches ancestors for spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1, built from JOINED path segments (join(\"tmp\").join(\"scripts\")), a shape kit-dual-path's text match does not see. It works through the stub, but every kit --heavy job prints the stub's 'moved ... update this caller' notice on stderr (found by git-a6). Handed to kit for TRAIN5 (kit's tree is mid-TRAIN4): look for apps/compiler/scripts/heavy.ps1 first and keep the old path as a fallback. Lesson for the later stub retirement: before removing any stub, grep for joined-segment forms as well as path strings.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_36 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 36u32, "2026-10-29T17:35Z", "main", "10-29 13:35 main: fixed the stubs' exit codes (sweep-4 hazard). The 12:3x stub form ended in `exit $LASTEXITCODE`, so a moved script that did not call exit returned the last native command's code: under `pwsh -File` a script whose last native call failed (exit 3) came back 3 through the stub but 0 directly, a false RED for test.ps1-style callers. All 39 stubs in apps/compiler/tmp/scripts now branch three ways. Dot-source: `. new @args; return`. Launched as the `pwsh -File` target (checked against [Environment]::GetCommandLineArgs, not call-stack depth, which misfires under -Command): relaunch the new script as a child `pwsh -NoProfile -File` and `exit $LASTEXITCODE`, exactly the direct semantics. Otherwise in-process: `& new @args; if (-not $?) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }`, so an `exit N` still sets $? false for the caller. Matrix (scratchpad tmp-retire/stub-exit-test2.ps1): 6 probe scripts (native fail without exit, exit 7, ok, throw, soft Write-Error last, native fail then exit 0) under -File, -Command and in-process, plus array args in-process and nested, -File with params, dot-source without leaked variables: 0 mismatches. Consumer check: hopacsota-lint.ps1 via stub vs direct, identical output and exit (0/0 real core, 1/1 missing core as the positive control); env.ps1 dot-sourced via stub defines the same functions and BundleRoot. Note for kit --heavy: heavy.ps1 launched with -File through the stub now runs as a child pwsh inside the same job tree (one extra process, same job object). Undo copies: scratchpad tmp-retire/restub-undo. Still to do: commit apps/compiler/scripts together with the stubbed tmp/scripts (untracked new folder that CI workflow.ps1 calls; user's commit).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_37 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 37u32, "2026-10-29T20:46Z", "main", "10-29 16:5x main: old-path census across repos (ripgrep; Get-ChildItem -Recurse was too slow because it walks kit's 5.5 GB .cache before filtering). sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1:18 is FIXED by fiscal (now apps/compiler/scripts/memory-cap.ps1; FISCAL-GENERIC n120). x/scripts: 0. kit: src/kit_jobs/host.spi plus its generated kit_job_create/create.rs (the joined-segment heavy.ps1 lookup), fix in TRAIN5. i574n.github/scripts has 4 DELIBERATE dual-path fallbacks, each new path first then old: serial-runner.ps1:4 (heavy.ps1), node-regen-compare.ps1:11 (env.ps1), respell-repo.ps1:29 (env.ps1), remote.ps1:70 (the node's old env.ps1). They are right while the node's spiral checkout predates the move. STUB-RETIRE GATE: (1) the user commits apps/compiler/scripts plus the 39 stubs; (2) git-a6's node checkout update (remote.ps1 sync) lands the new folder on the node; (3) TRAIN5 is installed; (4) drop the 4 fallbacks above; (5) a cross-repo grep for both the path string and joined-segment forms finds 0; only then archive the stubs. ADDENDUM 17:4x: a second joined-segment caller, found by git-a6 through the stub's own stderr warning in a run log: apps/compiler/packs review-candidate.ps1 built tmp + scripts\\test.ps1. It is FIXED now (runs apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1). The stub warnings are the backstop that catches what text greps miss, so keep the stubs until a full day of run logs shows none.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_38 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 38u32, "2026-10-30T02:48Z", "compiler", "10-29 22:4x compiler: a LIVE caller of the old path, found from the stub's stderr in every kit --heavy job ('apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1 moved ...; update this caller'): kit's heavy-gate discovery hardcodes base/spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1 in kit src/kit_jobs/host.spi:27 and the generated src/kit_job_create/create.rs:71 (KIT_HEAVY_GATE unset, so it walks cwd ancestors). It works through the forwarding stub. Fix in kit: join apps/compiler/scripts/heavy.ps1, ideally trying the new path first and the old one second, as i574n.github/scripts/serial-runner.ps1:4 already does. Routed to kit (via main) for TRAIN5. The stub must stay until that kit release is installed. Other hits are undo copies under packs/tmp-retire/undo and backlog prose.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_39 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 39u32, "2026-10-31T07:24Z", "compiler", "10-31 03:24 compiler: packs/ CLEANUP after the user's 01:5x 'ain't this drift? ... a shit ton of ps1 files ... we're losing quality'. Rule now in memory: packs/ holds only PENDING appliers plus the build/review/install tools; an applier leaves the repo when it is installed, rejected or diagnostic-only; its record is the backlog/PLAN entry; no .txt/.tsv/.py there and no parked samples. Moved out by verified move (copy + sha256 + remove) to C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-31\\spiral-packs, 21 appliers + the guard sample folder. INSTALLED, proven by dry-run DONE or by every 'new' text present in the live core/host: bend-float-math, formatter-repad-closer, gleam-compact-arms, hopacsota-d4-restart, hopacsota-p2-alias-order, rust-derive-inference, codegen-lf-lines, delphi-fpu-mask, delphi64-noregvar, export-rc-str-opt-in, fsharp-isnan-qualified, hopacsota-d4-restart-host. REJECTED or diagnostic-only, records in PLAN.md/HOPACSOTA-P3: hopacsota-control-workers, hopacsota-p3-control-workers, hashcons-striped, hopacsota-bridge-trace, -bridge-split, -wait-log, -wait-keys, -worklist-trace, host-batch-foreign-entry-diagnostics. Live references checked first (rg over all repos): none outside the appliers and tmp-retire's undo manifest. LEFT (23), each needing a per-item verdict, not a guess: PENDING by dry-run: delphi-arc-records, missing-arm-guard, rust-mutual-tail-loops, hopacsota-deferred-validation (p3 stack), hopacsota-p3-shard, hopacsota-p3-ivar, host-related-diagnostics-closure (pack 9), delphi-string-literal-index. AMBIGUOUS (no idempotency guard, and 0 of their 'new' texts in the tree, or not parseable): char-nul-escape, check-parse-errors, codegen-lf-headers, global-fragment-single-line, host-gen0-reexec, rust-postpass-idioms, rust-ureq-move-only, ccmr-det-root (1/7), ccmr-sourcelink, zig-export-pack, zig-monotonicdelay-pack, export-string-rc (likely superseded by rc-str-opt-in), formatter-operator-dehang, openqasm-tanh, rust-emit-unit-arg. Still in the repo and owned here: packs/tmp-retire/undo (~75 copied files incl. 5 .py, the undo set of the tmp move) and spiral/lab leftovers (~20 files the undo set names). Both go when this item closes.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_40 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 40u32, "2026-10-31T07:28Z", "compiler", "10-31 03:28 compiler: 4 more out (same verified move): openqasm-tanh and global-fragment-single-line shipped in PACK-7 (Done; its title lists OpenQasm tanh and global-fragment dedup); rust-emit-unit-arg (RUST-EMIT-UNIT-ARG Done); export-string-rc (superseded by the installed rc_str opt-in, EXPORT-STRING-PARAM-RC). Proof: neither their old anchors nor their new texts are in the live tree any more, so a later change rewrote those regions. 19 appliers left; formatter-operator-dehang has no backlog item at all and stays until its author rules on it.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_41 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 41u32, "2026-10-31T11:37Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 07:37 compiler: SWEEP (main's all-lanes request; the compiler lane has no tracking item, so the record is here). PROCESSES: none of mine left. One orphan tree seen and NOT stopped (owner unproven, rule stop-only-own): dotnet 21660 -> 18736, a Cells compiler daemon from 10-30 22:06 (--server-tcp spiral-cells-6828-1380.sock, --stall-seconds 120). Its erl parent 6828 and its socket file are gone, yet it is still alive ~9 h later with 41 s CPU, so --stall-seconds did not retire it (evidence for CELLS-DAEMON-RETIRE-STOP / CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT). Also a bare pwsh 11252 from 10-30 06:10 with its parent gone (not mine). JOBS: box has 0 running or held compiler jobs (pack10 build, pack10 predict and gpt5retire-hopacsota-build are finished and read); node has 0 compiler jobs; 0 compiler windows held. BACKLOG (10 min): CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION marked superseded by GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE, deps -> PACK-10; GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE gate fixed (user decision replaces promotion), step 2 written out, deps -> PACK-10; HOPACSOTA-P6 got the user's decision recorded; SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD's stale gpt5parallel-side note corrected, deps +PACK-10; PACK-9 marked subsumed by PACK-10; PACK-10 got its gate result (n2) and was handed to main. CORRECTION 10-31 09:57: '--stall-seconds did not retire it' was wrong. In the host (Program.fs:960-981, 1021) --stall-seconds is a compile-stall watchdog that runs only while a compile request is outstanding; an idle --server-tcp daemon blocked in AcceptSocket() has no exit condition, so outliving its erl client is by design. The gap is lifecycle: nothing ties the daemon to its client process.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_42 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 42u32, "2026-10-31T12:12Z", "main", "10-31 08:10 main: apps/compiler/packs/tmp-retire's undo set (callers.txt, manifest.json) names files under spiral/lab/COMPILER-PACK-SPEED-AB, HOPACSOTA-P2 and SPIRAL-TO-YAML. Those folders are now archived as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-080801 (spiral/lab is gone). If the undo is ever run, restore them first with scratch-archive.ps1 -Restore that manifest.tsv -RestoreTo C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_43 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 43u32, "2026-10-31T15:03Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 11:03 compiler: (1) packs/tmp-retire ARCHIVED (scratch-archive.ps1, dry-run first, 90 files, 0 verify failures) as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-105334. It held the finished tmp/scripts -> apps/compiler/scripts move tool (move.ps1, rehearse.ps1, kit-dual-path.ps1, kit-rehearse.ps1), callers.txt (a .txt in packs/) and the undo copies; the folder was untracked, and only its own scripts and backlog notes name it. To undo the move: restore that archive (and main's lab archive 20261031-080801, per n42) and run move.ps1 -Undo. (2) The 39 files in tmp/scripts are all forwarding stubs ('moved to apps/compiler/scripts/...; update this caller'). Remaining callers of the old path: kit src/kit_jobs/host.spi:27-28 now tries apps/compiler/scripts/heavy.ps1 FIRST and the old path second (staged in kit; kit.exe reinstalled 10-31 07:43); i574n.github/scripts serial-runner.ps1:4, respell-repo.ps1:29, node-regen-compare.ps1:11 and remote.ps1:70 all try new-then-old (the old path covers node mirrors with the old layout). The stubs can go once a kit --heavy job runs without the stub's stderr line AND the node mirror has apps/compiler/scripts. (3) packs/ applier census vs the live tree: apply-formatter-operator-dehang's new text is in the live core, so it SHIPPED; archived as 20261031-110306. Pending and clean (all anchors 1x): delphi-arc-records (17), delphi-string-literal-index (1), hopacsota-p3-shard (8), host-related-diagnostics-closure (4), host-server-parent-exit (3), missing-arm-guard (2), retire-gpt5parallel, rust-mutual-tail-loops (3). Stacked (fail on live by design, they need an earlier applier first): missing-arm-guard-output (on PACK-10), hopacsota-deferred-validation (on p3keys). STILL UNCLASSIFIED, anchors fail on live and the census couldn't read their new text: char-nul-escape, check-parse-errors, codegen-lf-headers, rust-postpass-idioms, rust-ureq-move-only, host-gen0-reexec (COMPILER-GEN0-BUDGET), hopacsota-p3-ivar. main's (not touched): ccmr-det-root, ccmr-sourcelink, zig-export-pack, zig-monotonicdelay-pack, alias-count-check, alternating-ab. CLASSIFIED 10-31 11:09: SHIPPED and ARCHIVED as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-110906 (hash-verified moves, 0 verify failures): char-nul-escape (its lexer text is in the single-flight half; the old anchor still matches once on the gpt5parallel half until PACK-10), check-parse-errors (the unindented 'let rec files' listing is in the live host), codegen-lf-headers (0 text.AppendLine left in codegenKotlin/Swift/OpenQasm/Ebpf), rust-postpass-idioms (captureFreeCache live), rust-ureq-move-only (the ureq regex live), host-gen0-reexec (reexecWithGen0Budget live; COMPILER-GEN0-BUDGET's host half is installed). PENDING: hopacsota-p3-ivar (9 anchors 1x, the HOPACSOTA-P3 D5 IVar waits). packs/ now has 15 appliers: 9 pending/clean, 2 stacked, 4 main's.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_44 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 44u32, "2026-10-31T16:15Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 12:15 compiler: .py HELPERS RETIRED from apps/compiler (user: no .py in the repos), each A/B-checked on identical inputs before retiring; all 6 archived as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-120731. (1) scripts/matrix-add-to-list.py + matrix-add-backend-to-groups.py -> ONE scripts/matrix-add.ps1 (-List <name> | -Backend <b> -After <a>, -Samples a,b, -Apply, optional -Matrix): 9 cases (dry runs, applies, already-listed, missing sample, bad list, missing after-key, sample not in the table) give identical printed output and identical matrix.psd1 bytes. (2) scripts/profile-summary.py + profile-thread.py -> ONE scripts/profile-speedscope.ps1 (-View Summary|Thread): on a real dotnet-trace profile, Thread view 52/52 lines identical; Summary differs only at ties, where the python itself is nondeterministic (two python runs on the same file differ in 32 lines because its set order is hash-seeded; as multisets the two agree except 2 lines at the top-45 cutoff). probe.ps1:84, a live caller of profile-summary.py that builds the path with Join-Path, now calls it; probe -Profile re-checked end to end. tmp/AGENTS.md's profile-thread line updated. (3) tmp/formatter/complaints_probe.py + fitting_lines_kept.py -> functions Get-FormatComplaints / Get-FittingLinesKept inside formatter/candidate-gate.ps1 (its only caller): census 13/13 lines identical over 31,357 authored lines with all 4 kinds firing; complaints 31/31 identical with the fail verdict (crafted file with join heads, off-grid indents and a macro block), plus a passing set with the same exit. LEFT: scripts/upstream.py (plan on COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION) and the target-language files, which stay by design: runtime/corelib.py and make_corelib.py (the Python backend's runtime), tests/native-shims/*.py and openqasm-run/run.py (they run the Python and OpenQASM backends' rows).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_45 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 45u32, "2026-10-31T17:24Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 13:24 compiler: runtime/make_corelib.py (a hand-run generator, no callers; not target runtime as first classified) -> runtime/make-corelib.ps1 [<stock>] [-Out]. A/B on the stock corelib.cuh at fork 0cb0fda0: the generated corelib.cuh is byte-identical to the python's AND to the committed runtime/corelib.cuh. The printed delta patch now comes from 'git diff --no-index --no-prefix': the same hunks (20 added, 1 removed lines), with git's 'diff --git'/'index' headers and function context in the @@ lines instead of difflib's bare ones; it is informational (stdout) and applies the same. Archived as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive (make-corelib-py). .py left under apps/compiler: only target-language files (runtime/corelib.py, tests/native-shims/*.py, openqasm-run/run.py). CORRECTION 13:25: tests/native-shims/cpp_native.py is TOOLING too (test.ps1:772 runs it to build the Cpp+Cuda native tier with g++/nvcc), not target runtime. Port it to a PowerShell function in test.ps1's Cpp block, but NOT today: tests/native-shims is part of every native-memo key (tmp/AGENTS.md), so touching the folder makes every lane's next -ReuseNative run redo the whole native tier (~20 min); do it together with the next planned harness change after the PACK-10 review, A/B on the Cpp rows' exit and stdout. Truly target-language and staying: runtime/corelib.py (the Python backend's runtime), native-shims/run_main.py (imports and runs the generated Python module). openqasm-run/run.py (46 KB) is the OpenQASM backend's simulator, i.e. its toolchain like wasmtime; porting it is a separate job (Spiral or F# would dogfood best), not a helper port.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_46 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 46u32, "2026-10-31T22:58Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 18:58 compiler: PRE-NIGHT SWEEP (main's all-lanes request). (1) GROOM: the compiler team has 0 Paused items (FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS is Blocked on LIB-EDITION3-ROUND with that resume condition; MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER and RUST-STRING-WRAPPER-INLINE back to Planned, 20:29Z). Ready CPU-light: GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS (P0, math half settled n30; next: the .mjs arrays/refs applier), MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS (P0, review met n14; next: ship with the next pack + its sample), CHAR-ORDERING (P0, decided by main, checklist n7). READY NODE-RUNNABLE: the Gleam JavaScript digits check (GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS n30: the matrix's tanh/sin/cos samples built for the JS target with gleam_community_maths, run with bun/node on the node, stdout vs C). (2) PROCESSES/JOBS: no compiler job running or queued on box or node, no compiler window held; node work dirs cleared (C:\\home\\remote-stage\\p3ab, p11speed, both zips); box temp restores removed (runner-restore, guard-restore). (3) DRIFT: per-file port-or-archive decisions for the compiler's 22 packs/.ps1 + today's 4 new scripts are on PS1-TO-SPIRAL n16 (own drift counted: -7 .py, +7 .ps1 today); 2 rejected appliers archived (20261031-185026). No lab/ dirs (spiral/lab is gone). Misrouted: kit's iggy-fixtures fix (LIB-IGGY-CLIENT, a kit/eoie-team item) sent back for routing.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_47 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 47u32, "2026-11-01T12:36Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 08:36 compiler, ROUND 4 QUALITY SPEC: FIELDS: tag team:compiler; est 2400 stays (epic-sized), light. DEFINITION OF DONE: apps/compiler/tmp holds no scripts (git ls-files apps/compiler/tmp/*.ps1 = 0 outside samples and tests/native-shims), every former tmp script either moved under apps/compiler/scripts or ported to a kit command (PS1-TO-SPIRAL first three: env.ps1, build.ps1, test.ps1), and AGENTS.md/README references updated (grep 'tmp/scripts' = 0). NEXT STEP: list the 38 tmp/scripts/*.ps1 with their callers (grep each stem across sibling repos, memory dangling-check-by-stem) and classify each move/port/archive. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN (for the kit ports): a script's inputs become a typed record of options with UNIONS for modes (e.g. 'Mode = SingleFlight | Hopacsota', 'Suite = Smoke | Examples | Contracts | All') instead of string ValidateSet parameters; results.tsv rows parse into the BACKEND-METRICS-MODEL row type, so test.ps1's port shares one row model with the metrics item.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_48 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 48u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler, R5 PACKS LIFECYCLE RULE (user: what is the packs folder, do I commit it): apps/compiler/packs was an untracked staging folder (0 tracked files) the compiler lane invented for pack candidates. RULE: (1) an INSTALLED pack is archived (scratch-archive), never kept: its code lives in spiral_compiler.fs (unstaged for the user) and its regression samples were already copied to tmp/samples; (2) PENDING programs (.kitdo, and the 2 legacy .ps1 appliers until ported) live in ONE tracked place, apps/compiler/drafts/; (3) the pack TOOLS are scripts like any other and live in apps/compiler/scripts/; (4) nothing else, and no packs folder. ACTED this round: moved build-candidate, install-pack, predict-residuals, review-candidate, install-when-clear, lib-gate-dll, measure-arms, alternating-ab, alias-count-check, delphi-heaptrc to apps/compiler/scripts (siblings, so every PSScriptRoot-relative path still resolves); retire-x-compat.kitdo + apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar/shard.ps1 to apps/compiler/drafts; archived pack12b, pack13, pack14 and the 6 installed appliers (19 files) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261101-103706 (verify 0 failures; restore with -Restore that manifest.tsv); removed the empty packs dir. Callers: appliers named to build-candidate/install-pack resolve against the script dir, so pass ..\\drafts\\apply-x.ps1 now. Answer for the user: commit apps/compiler/drafts (3 files) and the moved scripts; there is no packs folder to commit. NEXT: port the 2 hopacsota appliers to .kitdo when HOPACSOTA-P3 resumes.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_49 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 49u32, "2026-11-03T07:30Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (41 h). Next: apply the packs rule to the installed packs 19-23 (archive the candidates under spiral-bin-candidates), then move the next tmp script to its home.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_50 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 50u32, "2026-11-03T11:13Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:1x compiler: CANDIDATE CACHES FREED (order 5, delete after a check). %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates: removed cache\\ (build output: SpiralCompiler bins, obj, R2R; byte-reproducible from source\\ via build.ps1 per tmp/AGENTS.md) of 49 candidates whose source\\spiral_compiler.fs is present, via safe-delete.ps1 Remove-TreeSafely -Under the candidates root; 3.22 GB freed; no process referenced the folder. Kept: every source\\ (the per-pack core snapshots, 2-13 MB each), pack23 and pack24 whole (rollback/live), runner-* cargo targets (no CACHEDIR.TAG), and folders without a source\\. Box C: had 231.9 GB free before.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_51 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 51u32, "2026-11-04T09:28Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:2x compiler: packs rule applied to installed packs 23-32 (box): removed each candidate's cache\\ (regenerable build output) where source\\spiral_compiler.fs is present, via safe-delete Remove-TreeSafely scoped to spiral-bin-candidates; no process referenced the folder; 354 MB freed. Kept: every source\\ (hashes printed in the run), pack33 (rollback) and pack34 (live) whole, and heapmove (no source\\). Node side: my 42 stale stages were removed at 02:3x (10.4 GB).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_52 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 52u32, "2026-11-04T13:21Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:2x compiler: node upkeep (same rule): removed 23 finished review stages of today and last night under C:\\home\\remote-stage (bendsafe 1-5, splitu 1-9r, heapmove2, heaptrc, megaprobe, grnat, gleamrec, zigalloc, pack34d, rustrev) via safe-delete Remove-TreeSafely -Under C:\\home\\remote-stage; no process ran from them; their scripts and programs stay in the box scratchpad and their logs in the kit job store. 3.14 GB freed, node C: 21.5 GB free. Kept: compiler-pack34f (base source and control bin for every review), the running delphiarc/bendsafe6/splitu10, and gleamarr (proof not landed yet).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_53 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 53u32, "2026-11-05T07:32Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:3x compiler: PACKS RULE APPLIED (the item's recorded next step). The 85 pack candidate folders of installed or superseded packs (pack6-pack40, the compiler-*-box/-node review arms, and the small probe candidates gadt*, p3*, guard*, mutualtail*, zigexp* ...) were archived with scratch-archive.ps1 -Root %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates -ListFile (dry run first; 8352 files, 1.27 GB, blob verify failures 0) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261105-032848 (195 MB) and removed. Restore with -Restore '...\\20261105-032848\\manifest.tsv' -RestoreTo <dir>. The dry run's duplicate store copy was deleted (same 8352-line manifest). Kept: pack41 (installed box + node), pack42 (installing), pack43 (queued), plus pack8-kit-delta and runner-3f1b7588 / runner-cuda1030, which may be other lanes' builds. Box and node undo for installed packs stays in spiral-bin\\compiler-installs. apps/compiler/tmp now holds compiler (host), formatter, lanes, samples, target, tests; no scripts left in tmp.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_54 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 54u32, "2026-11-05T15:04Z", "compiler", "11-05 11:0x compiler: PACKS RULE applied again. Candidates of installed or superseded packs pack41, pack42, pack43, pack44 and pack48 were archived with scratch-archive.ps1 -Root %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates -ListFile (dry run first: 5 folders, 619 files, 0.16 GB, blob verify failures 0) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261105-110353 and removed. Restore: -Restore '...\\20261105-110353\\manifest.tsv' -RestoreTo <dir>. The dry run's duplicate store 20261105-110332 (same 619 rows) was deleted. Kept: pack49 (node + europa live), pack50 (box live), pack8-kit-delta, runner-3f1b7588, runner-cuda1030 (possibly other lanes'). Box/node undo stays in spiral-bin\\compiler-installs.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_55 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 55u32, "2026-11-06T12:22Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:2x compiler: PACKS RULE applied again. pack50 and pack51 candidates (superseded by pack52, installed box + node) archived with scratch-archive.ps1 -Root %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates -ListFile (dry run first: 2 folders, 74 files, 0.06 GB, blob verify failures 0) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261106-082047 and removed; the dry run's duplicate store 20261106-082010 removed with Remove-TreeSafely. Restore: -Restore '...\\20261106-082047\\manifest.tsv' -RestoreTo <dir>. Kept: pack49 (europa live), pack52 (box + node live), pack53/53b/53c (under review), pack8-kit-delta, runner-3f1b7588, runner-cuda1030.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_56 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 56u32, "2026-11-06T14:54Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:5x compiler: STEP DONE: apps/compiler/tmp/formatter -> apps/compiler/scripts/formatter (plain filesystem move, unstaged; 37 files incl. the untracked dll/ pin and synthetic/ fixtures). Rule: the compiler's scripts live in apps/compiler/scripts; the formatter gate tooling is scripts, and its synthetic fixtures stay beside the gate that reads them. Repath: env.ps1 in candidate-gate, format, report (..\\..\\scripts -> ..); the repo-root depth is unchanged (still 4 levels: corpus.ps1 and report.ps1 untouched; lint.ps1's ..\\..\\spiral_compiler.fs still resolves). External callers updated: scripts/parser-corpus-gate.ps1 (formatter\\corpus.ps1), spiral scripts/workflow.ps1 (CI: ../apps/compiler/scripts/formatter/report.ps1), tmp/AGENTS.md mention. Checks: all 7 scripts parse 0; corpus.ps1 from its new home lists the same corpus (kit 1109, lib 154, samples 1327, apps 81); git grep tmp/formatter = 0 tracked hits; %TEMP% job scripts (depth 2) call none. Left in tmp: compiler (host), lanes, samples, target, tests.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_57 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 57u32, "2026-11-06T15:39Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:4x compiler: tmp/target REMOVED: an empty, gitignored folder (spiral_Eval/, 0 files, last written 09-28); the core's Eval path recreates <workspaceRoot>/target/spiral_Eval on use, and tmp/.gitignore keeps covering it. Removed with Remove-TreeSafely. tmp now holds only compiler (host), lanes, samples, tests. lanes/ is NOT deletable yet under rule (6) (facts to backlog first): lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (116 KB, the live hopacsota plan: P3-P7, HOPAC-DEPTH) and hopac-probes/*.fsx (6 probes; HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH n11 queues their idle-machine rerun before Gate 3, and PLAN.md cites their numbers). NEXT STEP: a doc pass folding PLAN.md's still-open sections into the HOPACSOTA-* items, then delete lanes/ with the probes' rerun recorded or moved into a kit bench. Order after that, per the 10-25 rules: tests and compiler (host) by class, samples last in its own window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_58 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 58u32, "2026-11-06T16:12Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:1x compiler: lanes/ RE-DECIDED (rule 6 applied to a LIVE plan). Section map of lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (116 KB) against item states: history, folded already in Done items: Phase 0 (HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH Done), Phase 1 (P1 Done), Phase 2 (P2 Done), Phase 6 (P6 Done today), \"Why gpt5parallel drifted\" (GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE). LIVE design reference for open items: Decisions D1-D16 (23.7 KB), Shared state inventory (18.6 KB), Decision changes (40.7 KB), Scoreboard (9.8 KB), Phases 3/4/5/7, and the Hopac 0.5.1 caveats. These are what HOPACSOTA (25%), P3 (40%), P4/P5/P7 (0%) and HOPAC-DEPTH (40%) work from, and hopac-probes/ holds HOPAC-DEPTH's queued rerun. Folding them into notes now would freeze a working plan into history mid-work. DECISION: lanes/hopacsota stays until the HOPACSOTA epic closes. Resume when: HOPACSOTA is Done (then fold the decisions into its Done note and delete lanes/). The remaining tmp steps are window-bound: tests/ and compiler/host move together with build.ps1/env.ps1/build-candidate/install-pack paths (needs a no-pack window), and samples/ goes last in its own exclusive window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_59 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 59u32, "2026-11-06T16:15Z", "compiler", "11-06 12:2x compiler: Planned -> PAUSED. Reason: every remaining step needs an exclusive window. tests/ + compiler/host move together with the build.ps1 / env.ps1 / build-candidate / install-pack paths, which the pack pipeline reads mid-install (two installs ran today), and samples/ goes last in its own window with no matrix reader live; lanes/ waits on the HOPACSOTA epic (12:1x note). Resume when: a no-pack window is agreed with main (no install chain or review running on the box or node), or HOPACSOTA closes (for lanes/).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_60 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 60u32, "2026-11-06T17:13Z", "compiler", "11-06 13:1x compiler (re-decide): stays PAUSED. Reason unchanged and live: pack57 (AE1 + AE2 + RUST-GROUP-ARM-STRING-FOLD) is building and installs next, so the box has an install chain today. Resume when: a no-pack window is agreed with main after pack57 ships, or HOPACSOTA closes (for lanes/).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_61 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 61u32, "2026-11-06T21:12Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:1x compiler (re-decide): stays PAUSED, condition sharpened. pack57 and pack58c both shipped (16:38 / 16:49 node, europa 14:36 / 16:50), so the original 'after pack57 ships' part is met, but a candidate (ae3a, AUTO-EXPORT-3) is building today and would need its own install, and the tests/ + compiler/host move rewrites the paths build-candidate / install-pack read. Resume when: the first no-pack window of 11-07 (no candidate building, no install chain or review on box or node), agreed with main at the start of that window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_62 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 62u32, "2026-11-07T18:58Z", "compiler", "11-07 15:0x compiler (re-decide): stays PAUSED. Reason: the 11-07 window had pack61 (installed 13:51, fleet 14:0x) and now the pack62 candidate (CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS + LITERAL-SUFFIX-WARN) is gating on the node; the tests/ + compiler/host move rewrites the paths build-candidate, review-candidate and node-proof jobs read, so it must not land mid-gate. Resume when: pack62 is installed fleet-wide and no candidate is building; then the move goes first, before the next candidate.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_63 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 63u32, "2026-11-09T03:50Z", "compiler", "11-09 00:3x compiler (re-decide): Paused -> PLANNED. The resume condition is met: pack62 and then pack63c are installed fleet-wide (box, moon, vultr, ganymede; 11-08) and no compiler candidate is in flight. Next step: move tests/ and compiler/host out of tmp/ in one batch and update every path that reads them in the same edit (build-candidate.ps1, review-candidate.ps1, install-pack.ps1 (just gained -FromStore/-FromUrls, reads tmp/compiler for the fsproj deps hash), node-proof jobs, test.ps1, AGENTS.md), then a node-proof dry run before any new pack.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_64 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 64u32, "2026-11-09T12:00Z", "compiler", "11-09 12:0x compiler (re-check): stays Planned, not started -- pack75 is a candidate in flight (gate on ganymede, Windows pair pending on moon), and this move rewrites the paths build-candidate, review-candidate, install-pack (tmp/compiler fsproj deps hash = the oort base key!) and test.ps1 read. Note for the move: changing where the 4 compiler fsproj live changes Get-StoreKeys deps hash, so the oort base layer must be re-put after the move. Wait: when pack75 is installed fleet-wide and no candidate is building.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_65 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 65u32, "2026-11-09T12:01Z", "compiler", "Correction to note 64: Get-StoreKeys hashes each fsprojs file NAME + content, not its path, so a pure move keeps the oort deps hash; it changes (and the base layer needs a re-put) only if the move edits relative paths inside the fsproj files.")
inl spiral_script_tests () = Task ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", "Prototype Spiral test blocks as script replacements: a .spi file whose filtered test cells do what a pwsh script does today (run steps, check outputs), driven by Cells/eoie with parameters to filter execution, so compiler tooling dogfoods Spiral and its backends instead of dotnet scripting; measure against one real tmp/scripts script (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "pwsh-free,cells,dogfood,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_script_tests () = Planning ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_script_tests_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:37Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is PWSH-FREE; recorded here instead of as a dep (sole dep on an unfinished parent epic hid it from 'agile next'; AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT).")
inl note_of_spiral_script_tests_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:18Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: one real pwsh script (e.g. html build.ps1's steps) replaced by a .spi whose filtered test cells do the same steps under Cells, with identical outputs. Next step: pick the script and list its steps as test-cell names.")
inl note_of_spiral_script_tests_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:18Z", "org-f33af161", "D1 slice done (authoring): html/build.ps1 steps mapped to test-cell names, draft at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\html\\SPIRAL-SCRIPT-TESTS\\build-steps-as-cells.md. Next concrete step (the gate): write html/build.spi with the 9 named cells, record build.ps1 clean-tree stdout as the oracle, diff the cells combined stdout against it (export-oracle pattern). Inner --gate (unit notebooks own cells) stays; build.spi replaces only the outer orchestration.")
inl spiral_notebook_files () = Task ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", "Spiral files as large subject notebooks: one file per subject organized by sections, tests next to the code they test (never all at the end), merge needlessly split lib/product files; check every repo for distanced tests and fix them; the 1k split stays only for compiled crates. Try first on the XSD files (one file instead of many underscored ones), spread destructively only if it works (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D5, 15u32, Planned, "", "lib,structure,tests,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_notebook_files () = Planning ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", Minutes 960u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:30Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:30 main: test placement census (scratch test-placement-census.ps1: share of test blocks after a file's last definition, i.e. clustered at the end). lib: 46 files with tests, 450 tests, 17% at the end; 9 files fully clustered (process, xsd, erlang_process, unicode, ...). The user's interleaving habit holds in most of lib, and the clustered files are agent-era. eoie: 68 files, 266 tests, 77% at the end, 27 files fully clustered (model.spi 10/10, notes_cli 9/9, window_model 8/8, program 7/7): the main offender. x: 34% (cli.spi 20/20 at the end), tibia: 50% (lua.spi, block_plan), fiscal: 27%. Rule from here: a test block sits right after the definition it tests; the lint (GRANULAR-LINT verb) reports files above 50%. Healing order: my lib files first (xsd, unicode, erlang_process; process is tibia's replace), then eoie by team (EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION slices move tests while touching each file), x cli.spi with X-GRANULAR-HEAL. The one-file-per-subject trial (XSD modules into one file organized by sections) goes after the XSD heal slices land, so their anchors are not broken mid-queue.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 2u32, "2026-10-25T13:57Z", "main", "10-25 09:57 main: applied to new code before it lands: lib cli_args.spi (CLI-ARGS-STYLE) now carries its tests next to the functions they test instead of at the end; the reorder kept the sorted line multiset identical and the livemd round trip ok. Rule for my new lib files from here: a test goes right after the definition it tests, and a fixture type goes right before its first test.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 3u32, "2026-10-25T14:02Z", "main", "10-25 10:02 main: lib census redone today: 51 files with 2+ tests, 482 tests, 87 after the file's last definition (18%). 17 files are fully clustered. Excluded: the XSD set (xsd, xsd_regex, xsd_resolve, xpath, xpath_eval; the fiscal team's pending slices) and process/unicode (under LIB-LIST-SUGAR-REST's anchors; process is tibia's). The other 10 go in one slice: %TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1 moves each trailing test right after the last top-level definition its body references, and throws if a file's sorted line multiset changes. Dry run: 26 tests moved, 0 left trailing. Gate + land job-1792936954610 (after the list-sugar chain).")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 4u32, "2026-10-25T14:06Z", "fiscal", "10:06 fiscal (XSD set, at main's 10:0x handoff): the lib slices now end with main's interleaver (%TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1 -Files xsd.spi,xsd_resolve.spi,xsd_emit.spi -Apply) plus a formatter pass, inside lib-gate-xsd.ps1. Dry run on the patched copies: xsd 6, xsd_resolve 3 (the new namespace test included) and xsd_emit 1 trailing tests move right after the last definition they use, 0 stay, exact line multiset kept. xsd_regex, xpath and xpath_eval are untouched by these slices and keep their trailing tests until the fiscal team next edits them.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 5u32, "2026-10-25T15:32Z", "fiscal", "11:3x fiscal: lib-test-interleave (%TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1) Defined-Names did not read ':& :~ name' lines, so a test that uses a member of a recursive group (xsd_resolve references_in) was placed after the group's predecessor and failed with ETY-UnboundVariable. Fixed in place: the name regex takes an optional ':& ' prefix; chunking is unchanged (':& ' lines still extend their group's chunk), so a test now lands after the whole group. Found by lib gate 1 of XSD-NAMESPACE-NAMES.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 6u32, "2026-10-26T00:51Z", "main", "10-25 20:51 main: lib-wide distanced-test census (dry run of %TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1 per file over all 108 lib/spiral .spi, nothing written): 47 files still hold trailing tests that would move (86 tests), 0 stay, 0 errors. 10 of them are the held main-serial-test-interleave chain (erlang_term, decimal, json_schema, otp_actor, lustre, json_scan, cursor_walk, csv, oauth, benchmark). The other 37, largest first: process 6, physics 5, unicode 5, base 4, xpath 3, listm' 3, xpath_eval 2, file_system 2, sm' 2, then 28 files with 1 (xsd_emit, xsd_regex, routes, schematron_run, schematron, step_runtime, resultm, util, xsd_constraints, testing, reflection, array_dim, xsd_resolve, parsing, otp_supervisor, optionm', ...). Rule, written before batching: a file with a slice pending against it gets its interleave inside that slice, as fiscal's XSD slices do, so no anchor ever clashes. That covers process (tibia's process heal), unicode (x's code-points patch), xsd*/xpath*/schematron* (fiscal's XSD set), listm' (main's list-sugar-rest), file_system (main's fs-link-length) and json_scan (in the held chain). Every other file goes into ONE batch-2 interleave slice, composed after the held chain lands, gated like batch 1 (exact line multiset kept; Cells tests of each touched file; a test after a recursive group's last member, the 15:32 fix). The pending set is re-read from the gate-kit work folders and the job list at compose time, not from this note.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 7u32, "2026-10-26T00:52Z", "main", "10-25 20:52 main: product-repo half of the census (the same per-file dry run; spiral/apps without the compiler, dice, alphabet, polyglot, dir-tree-html; 9 .spi files hold tests). Clean: dice (2 files), alphabet (1), dir-tree-html (0). Distanced: (1) apps/cells/priv/new_project/src/PROJECT_NAME.spi, 4 trailing tests: the spiral.new template, so every new project starts with tests at the end; it matters most and goes first. Cells reads it live (mix spiral.new), and CELLS-NEW-PROJECT's tests may pin the template text, so it is a Cells slice gated on those tests, not a tree edit. (2) polyglot apps/scheduler/Tasks.spi, 1 test: polyglot is the user's repo, so interleave and leave it unstaged for the user's commit. (3) apps/cells/tmp/Spiral.Cells.NotebookTargetsTest/.../bare.spi: a fixture a Cells test run wrote under tmp, not source; no change.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 8u32, "2026-10-26T00:53Z", "main", "10-25 20:53 main: CORRECTION to n6/n7's counts. The interleaver's 'N trailing tests moved' counts every trailing test that has a target, including tests whose target is already the file's LAST definition, where they already sit (the spiral.new template's 4 'moves' were 1 trivial reorder). Recounted with scratchpad distanced-tests.ps1, which loads the interleaver's own Split-Chunks/Defined-Names/Is-Test, so the chunking is identical: a test counts as distanced only when its last-referenced definition precedes the file's final definition; distance = lines between that definition and the final one. Result over 108 lib files plus the 2 product hits: 19 files, 40 tests, 3,937 lines of distance in all, concentrated in physics 4 tests/900 lines, listm' 2/802, sm' 1/524, date_time 1/475, json_scan 2/244, xpath_eval 1/208, json_schema 2/175, process 4/154, base 2/142, unicode 4/134, xpath 2/87, then 8 files at 22 lines or fewer. spiral.new template: 3 tests 6 lines away (trivial, low value). polyglot Tasks.spi: 0, nothing to do. So batch 2's value sits in physics, date_time, base and sm' (no pending slice on those except sm'), and the n6 rule still applies to the rest. The interleaver should print the corrected metric; that fix rides batch 2.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 9u32, "2026-10-26T00:55Z", "main", "10-25 20:55 main: the interleaver's count fixed in place (%TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1): 'moved' now counts only tests whose target definition precedes the file's last one, so it reports real relocations. The reorder itself is unchanged, and so is the message text (no script under %TEMP% parses it; checked). It now agrees with distanced-tests.ps1 on 3 probes: spiral.new template 3, physics 4, polyglot Tasks 0. Parse 0 errors. n8's 'fix rides batch 2' is done.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 10u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "main", "10-29 22:00 main, groom (WIP rule, 3 days with no note): Active -> Paused, progress kept at 15%. Last note 2026-10-26, before the 10-28 profile wipe interrupted every lane, and no live job. Resume when picked; it is not abandoned, and it keeps its priority P1.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 11u32, "2026-10-31T20:58Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 12u32, "2026-11-07T22:18Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: per repo, files merged into subject notebooks where the split was needless, tests next to the code they test; measured by a count of files with tests only at the end, falling to 0. Next step: pick html's units as the pilot (they were just reshaped by the parser move). TypeFeatures: none new; organisation.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 13u32, "2026-11-09T17:52Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: 960m over-budget, inherently DISTRIBUTED. The test-placement census is DONE (lib 17pct-end/9 clustered files, eoie 77pct the main offender, x 34pct, tibia 50pct, fiscal 27pct). Healing is per-lane: lib's clustered files (xsd/unicode/erlang_process) are main/lib's, eoie by team (EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION), x cli.spi (X-GRANULAR-HEAL), tibia, fiscal each own theirs; the one-file-per-subject XSD trial goes AFTER the XSD heal slices land (so anchors are not broken mid-queue). The ENFORCEMENT (files >50pct tests-at-end flagged) is rig's GRANULAR-LINT verb. Parking on lane:rig (the test-placement lint); the per-lane test-moves ride each owner's next touch.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 14u32, "2026-11-09T20:19Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig PROGRESS on the test-placement lint (the enforcement this item waits on; the lane:rig row stays until the verb is wired): src/rig_test_placement/placement.spi (pure, HostFree; unstaged, unprobed, in rig's probe batch). block_kind TestBlock (:# name =) | DefinitionBlock | ModuleHeader (:# name static =); placement_verdict TestsBesideCode (trailing, total) | TestsClusteredAtEnd (trailing, total) | NoTests; a file is flagged when its trailing run of test blocks holds at least 2 tests AND more than half of all its tests (org's >50pct rule; a lone trailing test after a one-definition file is beside its code). Test: interleaved, clustered, single, none. SAME RULE MEASURED on kit/src today (text pass): 353 files with tests, 109 clustered at the end (31pct); top agile_todo_model/model.spi 13/13, rig_machine_windows/window_model.spi 13/13, agile_task_notes/notes_cli.spi 12/12, rig_lint_model/model.spi 10/10, rig_standards/rules.spi 10/10, rig_coordinator_actor/actor.spi 10/10. NEXT (rig): wire it as a kit standards rule (TestsBesideCode, opt-in per package like the other rules, plus a census word so the ratchet refuses growth); that edits the shared census code, so it rides after TRAIN43 snapshots, with COMMENT-LINT-GATE's census word.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 15u32, "2026-11-09T20:24Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig correction to note 14's NEXT: the test-placement rule routes through KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB (kit lint smells beside kit lint macros, one linked unit for all four smell models), not inline in kit standards: rig_standards is at 906 of 1000 generated lines. Still after TRAIN43; the lane:rig wait stays until the rule fires.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 16u32, "2026-11-09T21:26Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig progress: rig_test_placement is probe-green (Cells notebook gate on ganymede, off-train). The lane:rig wait stays until KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB wires the rule into kit lint smells after TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 17u32, "2026-11-10T13:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 09:5x rig: the lane:rig wait is now item:KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB, the precise target every earlier rig note already named (that verb routes this rule to every lane, and it waits on train TRAIN43f, node-green 331/331 at 08:46 with the box install running). The wait clears itself when the verb is Done, so this item stops showing up as waiting on rig in the gate.")
inl bang_macro_cleanup () = Task ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", "Code relying on !!!! intrinsics is ugly: inventory !!!! uses in lib and products, replace them with upstream core aliases (reuse upstream's names) or lib wrappers (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P0, D4, 70u32, Planned, "KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN", "lib,core,macros,granular,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_bang_macro_cleanup () = Planning ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_1 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:18Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:18 main: inventory of !!!! uses outside core (lib, eoie src, x, tibia, fiscal; lab and deps excluded), with the core alias each one has. Export 596: no core alias; eoie's crate exports. Proposal: one lib `export` wrapper (named, typed), then a mechanical rewrite in eoie (eoie team). Global 107: core base `global (x : string)` exists, so rewrite to `global`, mechanical. StaticStringConcat 18: the `^^` operator form, decided by CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's rule. Array intrinsics ArrayCreate 10, ArrayIndex 5, ArrayIndexSet 6, ArrayLength 6: core base has the prototype instances create/index/set/length on `array`, so rewrite to those (this is also the prototype usage TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCE wants). Conv 5: core `conv`. StringLength 4: core `sm.length`. LTE 6, Sub 3, Add 2: the operators `<=`, `-`, `+`. Without a core alias (keep as primitives until core grows one): Indent 6, NominalCreate 4, UnionToRecord 4, SymbolToString 3, RecordTypeFoldBack 2, Unbox 2. Order: Global (107) and the arithmetic/array/string ones (about 47) are mechanical rewrites, then the Export wrapper with the eoie team, and the rest wait for core aliases (upstream fork, UPSTREAM-FORK-START).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_2 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 2u32, "2026-10-26T00:41Z", "main", "10-25 20:41 main: re-census (tracked .spi; deps, target, _build, .cache and lab excluded; apps/compiler excluded because its samples exercise the intrinsics on purpose). lib: json_scan 27 (StaticStringConcat 8 at :32/128/130/133/268-271, array intrinsics 19 over raw array_base), array_dim 4 (its own create/index/set/length over the intrinsics: a wrapper, which is the target shape), base 2 (Add/Sub are the operator definitions themselves, so they stay), float_text 1 (has a land pending; untouched), rust/testing 1 ((++) = StaticStringConcat, used inside global (...)). apps: cells StaticStringConcat 5. eoie src: Global 107 (eoie team, frozen until KIT-RENAME). x Conv 5, tibia arrays 23 (their teams), polyglot Conv 4. Order: StaticStringConcat (lib 9, cells 5) waits on CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's fold probe (queued), since its target form (++# or ^^) is that rule's output. json_scan's array intrinsics are not mechanical: core's create/index/set/length are prototype instances over the array nominal, and json_scan's API passes raw array_base i32, so moving it changes types. That goes as a typed slice through the gate kit after the probe. Next: after the probe, one lib slice for json_scan (concat form plus arrays through the array nominal, gated with its tests).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_3 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 3u32, "2026-10-26T05:19Z", "main", "10-26 01:19 main: CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN decided (DOES-NOT-FOLD): the target form for !!!!StaticStringConcat is ^^, the compile-time concat. Sites: lib json_scan.spi 8 (:32, 128, 130, 133, 268-271), rust/testing.spi 1 (the (++) used inside global (...), where only ^^ keeps the literal global accepts), cells 5. Note json_scan's :128-133 concat run-time values (prefix, text_between results), where StaticStringConcat behaves as a plain concat; those become ++#, and only literal-only sites become ^^. Next: one lib slice over json_scan and rust/testing, classifying each site by literal-only (^^) or run-time operand (++#), gated on json_scan's tests.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_4 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 4u32, "2026-10-26T05:48Z", "main", "10-26 01:48 main: lib concat slice drafted per CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's verdict: %TEMP%\\lib-static-concat\\apply.ps1 (10 anchored edits, each exactly once, 0 lines over 120, no StaticStringConcat left in either file). json_scan.spi: all 8 sites have a run-time operand (key, prefix, the text_between results, piece, and the test's unicode.char_of values), so they become ++#, and json_scan gains ':< sm'_operators' (json_schema opens it the same way; package order allows it). rust/testing.spi's (++) builds global (...) text, where only a compile-time literal works, so it becomes 'a ^^ b'. Queued main-serial-static-concat after the test-interleave chain, because json_scan.spi is one of that chain's files (the interleave moves tests without changing lines, so these line anchors stay unique). Gate on json_scan.spi and rust\\testing.spi; every lib test runs through testing, so the ^^ change gets exercised. Remaining: cells 5 StaticStringConcat, then the array intrinsics as the typed array-nominal refactor.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_5 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 5u32, "2026-10-26T07:21Z", "eoie", "03:21 eoie: eoie's Global part drafted, with one coupling found. Census on the renamed tree: !!!! intrinsics 768 (Export 604, Global 107, StaticStringConcat 11, the rest single digits). All 100 Global wrappers are the same copy-pasted line ':= rust_global (x : string) : () = !!!!Global(x)', duplicating core base's 'inl global (x : string) : () = !!!!Global(x)' (base.spi:22); x and tibia already call bare global. Converter: kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\global-wrapper.ps1, string and macro aware. Dry run on a tree copy: 110 files, 100 local definitions removed, 256 call sites renamed to core global, and no string or macro body touched (a tests.spi string holding 'rust_global (' as rewriter input stays). Left by design: 7 direct !!!!Global(triple-quote) test calls, and the variant wrapper rust_global_transport (1 definition, 3 calls), which should fold in too. COUPLING, blocking a plain rename: eoie's drift tools key on the token rust_global: the style census token (kit style model.spi:135, probes.spi:87 RustGlobal), the ratchet rule 'a new package carries rust_global' (census.spi:183), and the authority census counting 'rust_global (quote)' sites inside host code (terminal.spi:118/155). Renamed call sites would make all of them blind to host blocks, and the ratchet would pass new drift written as global. So the class lands as one change: the rename, plus those detectors counting a global macro call as the same host-block marker, plus their fixtures updated. Gate: every regenerated product crate byte-identical (inl wrapper to inl wrapper), and the census numbers unchanged before and after on the same tree.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_6 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 6u32, "2026-10-26T07:32Z", "eoie", "03:32 eoie: the census coupling, measured. Probe counts over eoie src (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\probe-delta.ps1), before the Global cleanup and after it (dry-run tree copy). Old RustGlobal probe (the bare token rust_global): 381 before, 25 after. The rename alone would report a 93% drop in host-code drift while migrating nothing. Drafted probe (clean\\list-sugar\\census-probes.do, kit_style_census/probes.spi): a host-block call in either spelling, (?<![\\w.])(rust_)?global\\s*( paren or quote ), gives 363 before and 263 after, exactly the 100 removed definitions, and no longer counts Rust identifiers such as stats.rust_global_sites. Gate for the class, written now: with the new probe, RustGlobal falls by exactly the number of removed wrapper definitions, every other probe is unchanged on the same tree, and every regenerated crate is byte-identical. The probe change lands first (or in the same change); the authority census counter (kit_source_topology_core terminal.spi, counting 'rust_global (quote)' inside host code) and the ratchet's 'a new package carries rust_global' rule need the same either-spelling form.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_7 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 7u32, "2026-10-26T07:34Z", "main", "10-26 03:34 main: tibia is landing am'.create_base n (!!!!ArrayCreate) and am'.set_base ar i v (!!!!ArrayIndexSet) beside index_base (tibia-serial-heals, for terrain.spi's 23 raw array ops; probed on Rust and C). Follow-up for main once it lands: json_scan.spi's raw ArrayIndexSet sites (:162, :211) move to set_base, as a separate slice after main-serial-static-concat lands (same file), with no second wrapper. Rule for every lane: a raw !!!! whose lib wrapper exists is replaced by the wrapper. A missing wrapper is added once in lib, beside its siblings.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_8 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 8u32, "2026-10-26T08:01Z", "main", "10-26 04:01 main: raw !!!! in main's small repos (tracked .spi): dir-tree-html 8 (7 Export, 1 LT in shared.spi's char (<.)), dice 4 (all Export, contract/dice_contract.spi), polyglot 15 (6 Export in chat_contract.spi, plus apps/spiral/temp/cube/cube.spi: Sin, Cos, 2 Conv, 4 Printf), blog 0, alphabet 0. Plan, with order rules: (1) Export (17 sites) waits for x's base.export (job-1792997503468-x-serial-lib-export: ':= export \\* t. (name : string) (f : t) : () = !!!!Export(name, f)', which x proved byte-identical on Rust), then reuses x's generic %TEMP%\\x-simland-0214\\export_migrate.ps1 -Root per repo. No second tool. Per-repo proof: dir-tree-html's build with .rs byte-identical; dice and polyglot contract wasm export lists identical. Ordering: chat_contract.spi after the alias heal (job-1793000241647); dir-tree-html's tree.spi after the tree heal (main-serial-reland-fs). (2) cube.spi's Sin/Cos/Conv wrappers become core sin/cos/conv (core.spi:96-100 already wraps them); Printf has no lib or core wrapper, so it stays until BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP adds one beside console.write. (3) dir-tree-html's (<.) on char: core '<' is {number}-only, so a lib char comparison would be the home; low value, last.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_9 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 9u32, "2026-10-26T08:46Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:52 x: first wrapper, Export. lib/spiral/base.spi gets ':= export \\* t. (name : string) (f : t) : () = !!!!Export(name, f)' next to emit (base- is included unprefixed, so consumers call it bare: export \"xc_refs\" ((\\ x => refs_of x) : refs_args -> refs_reply)). Proof on the node (job-1792992991779-x-export-proof): all 51 x sites in 23 entries rewritten by export_migrate.ps1 (multi-line sites keep their authored breaks), and every entry compiles to byte-identical output, 22 Rust + simframes Gleam, 0 differ. Queued as job-1792997503468-x-serial-lib-export: lib gate on base.spi, land.ps1 (GREEN verdict + reader guard), then the x migration (refuses unless the live lib has export, rolls back on failure). eoie's 604 sites can use the same wrapper; x is now free of !!!! (exsss.spi moved to ^^^/&&&/|||/<<</>>>/conv, posts.spi to (~!) p).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_10 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 10u32, "2026-10-26T09:24Z", "main", "10-26 05:24 main: LIB-STATIC-CONCAT landed 05:21 (main-serial-static-concat, gate GREEN then a land through the mutex-held kit): json_scan.spi 9C2DBF8E3FCE19D3 (8 StaticStringConcat -> ++# plus ':< sm''_operators') and rust\\testing.spi A33B2BEF370CE01C ((++) = a ^^ b, compile-time concat for global). Neither file has a !!!!StaticStringConcat left. The json_scan follow-up (ArrayIndexSet at :162/:211 -> am'.set_base) waits only on tibia's create_base/set_base land now, since this one is in.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_11 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 11u32, "2026-10-26T09:25Z", "main", "10-26 05:25 main: json_scan.spi has 19 raw array intrinsics, not 2: ArrayLength x5, ArrayIndex x4, ArrayIndexSet x4, ArrayCreate x6 (lines 163-245 after the static-concat land). am' has index_base and init_base; tibia's pending slice adds create_base and set_base beside index_base; there's no length_base. Plan: after tibia's land, one gate-kit slice adds am'.length_base beside the landed wrappers (anchored on their landed text, so the two lands can't collide) and moves all 19 sites onto length_base, index_base, set_base and create_base. Rule for the gate: Rust and Gleam outputs of json_scan's tests stay identical in behavior, with 0 candidate-only reds.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_12 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 12u32, "2026-10-26T11:50Z", "x", "2026-10-26 07:50 x: the lib export gate waited 4.9 h for a local heavy slot (05:36-10:3x) without starting, so it moved to the node: local chain job-1792997503468 stopped while still waiting (gate.ps1 never ran, no writes), node gate job-1793015478185 runs the node lib-gate-kit against a fresh spiral mirror (xgate). On GREEN, the verdict is copied into the local kit and a local serial job runs only land.ps1 (stage + reader guard + mutex) and x-migrate.ps1 (manifest serial-x-lib-land.json); both are non-heavy and write live trees, so they stay local.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_13 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 13u32, "2026-10-26T12:03Z", "main", "10-26 08:03 main: json_scan array slice drafted and proven on a lib copy: %TEMP%\\lib-json-scan-arrays\\apply.ps1 -Lib <lib\\spiral> [-Apply]. am'.spi gets length_base (`ar |> array |> length`, the same form as index_base) right after tibia's set_base, plus a ///> rust test, base_wrappers_round_trip (create_base 3, set_base, then [length; index] = [3; 7]). json_scan.spi moves all 19 raw sites, each pattern at its exact expected count: 4 ArrayLength -> am'.length_base, 7 ArrayCreate -> am'.create_base (the element type comes from each site's annotation or return type), 4 ArrayIndexSet -> am'.set_base, 3 ArrayIndex -> am'.index_base. 0 raw array intrinsics left; 0 lines over 120. Type check first: the wrappers take `int`, and a --check probe shows int is i32 (`(x : i32) : int = x` accepted; the negative twin `(x : i64) : int = x` rejected), so json_scan's i32 counts need no conv. Proof (proof-check.ps1): a robocopy of lib, tibia's exact LIB-ARRAY-BASE text simulated from their apply script (their script itself not run), then this slice, then --check of a probe that calls json_scan.parse_i32_array and both wrappers: exit 0. Negative control: a string planted as index_base's index in the copy is rejected (exit 5), so the check reads the copy, not the live lib. The slice refuses until am'.spi carries tibia's set_base line, since it anchors on that landed text. Next: when LIB-ARRAY-BASE lands (tibia's 'gaps' part), run the gate kit on am' and json_scan (Cells tests on both backends, 0 candidate-only reds), then land.ps1.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_14 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 14u32, "2026-10-26T13:49Z", "x", "2026-10-26 09:49 x: GREEN at last on the node (attempt 3, job-1793016941188), using tibia's node gate (-Tree/-Gate against the mirror's lib_gate.ps1, mix deps.get first, EOIE_EXE set). Attempts 1-2 were VOID because the plain gate ran no test rows in a fresh mirror. Verdict GREEN 20261026-0817: baseline red 39, 10 candidate-only reds (join_body_unit_3/gleam, from_pair*) all passed when rerun alone (5 of 5), 0 type errors. Gated base.spi hash 4E28EB421DBB5F8F equals live, so the verdict was copied into the local kit; local land+migrate job-1793021989909-x-serial-lib-land runs land.ps1 (stage, reader guard, mutex) then x-migrate.ps1.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_15 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 15u32, "2026-10-26T13:55Z", "x", "2026-10-26 09:55 x: LANDED. lib base.spi gained export (land.ps1 09:53, base.spi 8C92D23BA51E50A5, waited 11 min for a Cells run to clear). Then x-migrate rewrote 51 sites in 23 files under x/apps to call lib export (backup %TEMP%\\x-lib-export\\x-backup-20261026-095402). x .spi files now hold 0 '!!!!' sites. Compile proof of the migrated x tree rides on the next full x verify.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_16 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 16u32, "2026-10-26T14:36Z", "main", "10-26 10:36 main: apps/cells' 5 StaticStringConcat sites, looked at 10:3x: each of cell.spi, directives.spi, document.spi, notebook.spi and text.spi opens with its own ':= (++) (left : string) (right : string) : string = !!!!StaticStringConcat(left, right)', applied to run-time strings. By CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's verdict (run-time operands: ++#, literal-only: ^^) the target is lib's ++#. The 5 local copies go, replaced by one shared operator rather than 5 renamed aliases. Ordering rule, written now: this slice starts only after install-5n has run, because install-5n.ps1 hash-guards directives.spi (FFE782851366145F) and applies x's structural-names apply_host_cells.ps1 to Cells inside the install window, so an earlier edit would make the P0 install refuse. The slice is drafted after 5n lands, anchored on the post-install text, with the Cells mix tests as its gate.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_17 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 17u32, "2026-10-26T14:36Z", "main", "10-26 10:36 main: correction to the previous note: apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj lists only |core- (no spiral-), so lib's ++# (sm'_operators) is not reachable from Cells, which is likely why each module keeps a local (++). The slice's choice, by the same post-5n rule: either core's own run-time string concat, if core has one (check core before drafting), or one shared Cells module (text.spi is first in the package order) holding the single definition that the other 4 open. Adding spiral- to the Cells package is out of scope, since Cells must build before lib.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_18 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 18u32, "2026-10-26T19:37Z", "main", "10-26 15:37 main: 10-26 15:3x main: the Cells StaticStringConcat slice's open check (n17) is resolved by reading, and its shape is decided. (1) Core has NO run-time string concat: the fork core's sm.spi defines only index, length and slice; its concat functions are arraym.concat and listm.concat (arrays and lists). So the core-alias option is out. (2) apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj order is text, cell, directives, document, notebook, targets, main (|core- only). Each of the 5 modules defines its own '(++) ... = !!!!StaticStringConcat(left, right)' on line 1 and opens nothing.\nShape, by lib's existing idiom (sm'_operators, rust.rust_operators): a new operators-only module apps/cells/spi/text_operators.spi, first in the package, holds the single (++); all 5 modules replace their line-1 definition with ':< text_operators'. Rejected alternative: ':< text' from the other 4 would open every text definition unqualified (notebook calls text.replace and text.next_line by qualified name), risking shadowing, whereas an operators-only module exposes just the operator.\nResult: 5 !!!! sites become 1 (the operator's own body, an irreducible intrinsic with no core alias); 0 renamed aliases. Ordering unchanged: draft after install-5n (it guards directives.spi) and after fiscal's fidelity and keep_docs lands (document.spi, directives.spi). Gate: Cells mix test, failures equal to the 3-known baseline, plus a corpus notebook run.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_19 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 19u32, "2026-10-26T19:40Z", "main", "10-26 15:40 main: 10-26 15:4x main: lib census re-run by intrinsic: 40 '!!!!' sites in 6 files, down from the 10-24 inventory. Classified, by n1's rule (core alias, else lib wrapper, else irreducible): base.spi 6 (Add/Sub/Mult/Div/Do/Export) ARE the lib wrappers, the irreducible single definitions everyone else calls; backend.spi 8 (BackendSwitch x2, Indent x6) is the dispatch machinery itself; array_dim.spi 4 are the array primitive wrappers; console.spi 2 (Printf in write_line_bend, the Bend backend's only output route) have no core alias (the fork core has no printf), and a lib wrapper would only move them one level down, so irreducible; float_text.spi 1 (StaticStringConcat) sits in fiscal's pending LIB-TARGET-GAP landing, re-checked after it lands; json_scan.spi 19 (array intrinsics) wait on tibia's LIB-ARRAY-BASE, as recorded. So lib has 0 sites left that main can heal today; the remaining reducible ones are float_text (fiscal, after its land), json_scan (tibia's array base), and the Cells 5 to 1 slice (n18, after 5n).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_20 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 20u32, "2026-10-26T19:46Z", "main", "10-26 15:46 main: 10-26 15:5x main: product census of '!!!!' in main's repos: dice contract 4 Export; polyglot apps/chat/contract 6 Export, plus apps/spiral/temp/cube Conv/Cos/Sin/Printf (cube-core-math's own heal); dir-tree-html 7 Export (tree 3, inline 2, markdown 1, selftest 1) plus shared.spi's '(<.)' over !!!!LT; alphabet 0; blog 0. The LT is irreducible for now: Spiral char has no ordering, so lib would need a char comparison first.\nThe 17 Export sites move to lib base.spi's export (x landed it 09:53; x migrated its own 51 sites) through x's converter (TEMP x-simland-0214/export_migrate.ps1: balanced parens, string-aware). Dry run on copies of all 6 files: 17 sites, 0 left. Single-line '!!!!Export(\"n\", f)' becomes 'export \"n\" f'; multi-line forms become 'export' with the name and lambda indented on the following lines (offside application).\nRunner TEMP main-export-migrate/run.ps1, one generic tool for all three repos: lib guard (base.spi has export), backup plus hashes, conversion on a staged copy first (nothing written if the converter fails), then the repo's own consumer build. Rule, written before the runs: GREEN iff that build exits 0 AND 0 '!!!!Export(' is left; otherwise restore every file, verified by hash. Builds: dice/contract/build.ps1 (full, incl. notebook tests and export check); polyglot apps/chat/contract/build.ps1; dir-tree-html via repo-build.ps1 (build + --self-test + 1k units).\nOrdering: the dir-tree migration is step 2 of the repo-build-3 serial manifest, so the two dir-tree builds never share the live tree concurrently; dice and polyglot-chat are standalone requeue extras. All three are queued after kit's rename finalize.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_21 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 21u32, "2026-10-26T23:15Z", "main", "10-26 19:15 main: 10-26 19:15 main: json_scan.spi's 19 array intrinsics are unblocked: tibia landed LIB-ARRAY-BASE (am'.create_base, set_base, index_base; gated GREEN ~17:5x). The 08:00 slice (TEMP lib-json-scan-arrays/apply.ps1: am'.length_base + a round-trip test, and json_scan's 19 sites through am') now dry-runs clean on live lib, its set_base anchor present once, 0 raw intrinsics left, 0 lines over 120. proof-check.ps1 updated to skip its LIB-ARRAY-BASE simulation when lib already has create_base; on a fresh lib copy, --check exit 0 (TYPECHECKS) through parse_i32_array -> item_positions -> record_start. The real gate (json_scan's rust/gleam/c test blocks and am''s new test) is queued as requeue extra main-serial-json-scan-arrays (gate -> land, kit gate-kit), AFTER job-1793030605331-main-serial-am-try-item, because both edit am'.spi and each gate must gate the bytes it lands on (pause-requeue.ps1 gained an optional After field for this). When it lands, lib's '!!!!' count drops 40 -> 21, all classified irreducible or held (n19).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_22 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 22u32, "2026-10-26T23:16Z", "main", "10-26 19:16 main: 10-26 19:16 main: CORRECTION to n21's count, measured on live lib now: lib has 43 '!!!!' sites in 8 files, not 40. Since the 15:40 census (n19): am'.spi +2 (tibia's create_base and set_base bodies, the array wrappers themselves) and sm'.spi +1 (PrimToString in obj_to_string_c, the C backend's only primitive-to-string route). Both are irreducible single definitions by n1's rule, like base.spi's 6. So the json_scan slice takes lib 43 -> 24: backend 8, base 6, array_dim 4, am' 2, console 2, sm' 1 (all wrappers or dispatch machinery) and float_text 1 (held for fiscal's LIB-TARGET-GAP).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_23 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 23u32, "2026-10-27T06:41Z", "main", "10-27 02:41 main: 10-27 02:41 main: the polyglot apps/chat/contract export migration (job-1793062387257, 20:54-00:14) went RED, but not because of the migration. Its build failed one test, generate_cid on rust, and tibia's fresh baseline on the restored, untouched tree fails it the same way: chat_contract.spi:74:8 ETY-TermError, where the test pipes ;[] straight into am'.to_vec, which takes array_base (red since about 10-24 23:19). The migration's runner restored its file by hash. tibia fixes the test (tibia-polyglot-cid-test-fix: ;[] |> am'.base |> am'.to_vec, the crypto.spi idiom) and then reruns its generate_cid heal (cid-land7, --after-ok). The polyglot export migration requeues AFTER cid-land7, on a copy of the tree rather than in place, because the in-place run overlapped tibia's baseline build for ~3 h. The dice export migration is unaffected.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_24 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 24u32, "2026-10-27T06:41Z", "main", "10-27 02:41 main: 10-27 02:41 main: dice's export migration LANDED (unstaged). job-1793062386837 went GREEN: 1 file in dice/contract migrated from !!!!Export to lib export, dice/contract build.ps1 exit 0, contract tests all passed, NEAR sandbox tests passed on dist/dice.wasm (backup in TEMP main-export-migrate). Of n19's 17 product Export sites, dice's are done; polyglot chat waits on tibia's cid-land7 (n23), and dir-tree-html's are in main-serial-dir-tree-repo-build-3.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_25 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 25u32, "2026-10-27T06:44Z", "main", "10-27 02:44 main: 10-27 02:43 main: polyglot chat's export migration is UNBLOCKED, not yet run. tibia landed the generate_cid test fix (6/6) and its heal (cid-land7: rebuild exit 0, notebook tests 6/6, all 9 exports identical) as an unstaged layer in polyglot, so the baseline is green now. Next run, in this order: (1) change TEMP main-export-migrate/run.ps1 so the convert-then-build proof runs on a copy of the repo (cargo workspace and deps links included), and only a GREEN verdict writes the live tree, as promised to tibia after the 3 h overlap. (2) Run it on polyglot apps/chat/contract, anchored on tibia's new chat_contract.spi bytes. The pass rule is unchanged: build exit 0 AND 0 sites left; otherwise nothing is written. Deferred tonight because main's standing run ended at 21:00 and the runner change is real work.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_26 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 26u32, "2026-10-27T07:21Z", "main", "10-27 03:21 main: 10-27 03:21 main: json_scan's 19 array intrinsics LANDED (json-scan-arrays chain, re-chained behind the new am-try-item; gate and land exit 0). lib's '!!!!' count should now be 24 (n22's projection); re-measure next run. With dice's export migration (n24), the open product sites are polyglot chat's (n25, deferred) and dir-tree-html's (migrated in repo-build-3, GREEN).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_27 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 27u32, "2026-10-27T09:45Z", "main", "10-27 05:45 main: 10-27 05:45 main: lib re-measured, 24 '!!!!' sites in 7 files, n26's projection exactly. ALL 24 are inside lib wrapper definitions, so lib is at its floor. am' create_base/set_base and array_dim create/index/set/length are the array primitives. base.spi has export, do and the arithmetic operators (+ - * /). float_text has concat. backend.spi holds backend_switch itself (2) and its 6 Indent helpers. console.spi:57-58 is write_line_bend, the Bend arm of console printing. sm'.spi:226 is obj_to_string's C path. Each wraps exactly one intrinsic, and callers use the wrapper. The item's open work is products only: polyglot apps/chat/contract's export sites (unblocked since cid-land7; runner change next) and dir-tree-html's (migrated in repo-build-3, GREEN). Then a product census for the other intrinsics.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_28 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 28u32, "2026-10-27T10:26Z", "main", "10-27 06:26 main: polyglot chat's export migration is QUEUED (job-1793096715870), with the runner change promised to tibia on 10-27 02:44 done. TEMP main-export-migrate/run-copy.ps1 copies apps/chat plus scripts and lib into a work folder, recreates deps links, and re-points every absolute link that pointed back into the live repo into the copy (apps/chat/contract/lib -> C:\\home\\git\\polyglot\\lib was one). It refuses (VOID) if any link in the copy still points into the live repo, then converts and builds apps/chat/build.ps1 (the contract, then its tests) inside the copy, with cargo's target in a main-owned cache. It writes the live tree only on GREEN, and only if every site file still has the hash read at the start (else VOID: nothing written). The copy stage was tested alone with -CopyOnly: 394 MB, 1 link re-pointed, 0 escaping, then removed links-first with the live lib and spiral intact. The pass rule is unchanged from n24: build exit 0 AND 0 sites left. The old in-place run.ps1 is kept for reference and no longer used.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_29 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 29u32, "2026-10-27T12:00Z", "main", "10-27 08:00 main: polyglot chat migration (job-1793096715870) is RED by its rule, and the live tree is untouched as designed: the copy, the link re-point and the conversion all worked (6 sites in 1 file, 0 left). The build failed for ENVIRONMENTAL reasons, not the migration. (1) The contract step runs spiral_wasm through WSL, which failed with Wsl/Service/ERROR_TIMEOUT under the box's 100% load. (2) chat_contract.spi's 6 rust test cells all exceeded Cells' 300 s timeout (slowest 624 s, headroom 2.08). The runner had no control, so it couldn't tell the two failure kinds apart. Fix before the next run: run-copy.ps1 also builds an UNCONVERTED copy (the control). Converted GREEN is GREEN; converted RED with control GREEN is RED (the migration broke it); both RED is VOID (environment), with the failing step of each named.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_30 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 30u32, "2026-10-27T15:53Z", "main", "10-27 11:53 main: chat-2 (job-1793103260833) VOID, and the cause was my harness, not the migration. Both the converted and the unconverted control copy failed the same 6 chat contract tests the same way (the failure lines differ only by a thread id): the WSL spiral_wasm binary panicked on 'No such file or directory' reading target/spiral/spiral_contract/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/spiral_<hash>.wasm. Cargo had built all 6 artifacts fine (exit 0; a failed build prints 'cargo error', not 'wasm error'), but into the per-side CARGO_TARGET_DIR that run-copy.ps1 set (LOCALAPPDATA main-cargo-target/export-migrate-<side>, where all 6 top-level .wasm files sit). apps/spiral/spiral.spi:327 hard-codes the wasm path under the workspace's own target/, so it never finds output redirected by CARGO_TARGET_DIR. A race between parallel test steps was ruled out: there are 6 distinct hashes, one per test. Both sides generate identical hashes, so the isolation bought nothing. run-copy.ps1 now sets CARGO_TARGET_DIR only when -CargoTarget is passed (default off). Re-queued as chat-3: job-1793116323641 (heavy, 8 h cap counting the queue). Product defect for later, owner whoever next needs wasm runs under a redirected target: spiral rust's wasm_path (spiral.spi:327) and its cleanup paths (spiral.spi:392) should resolve against CARGO_TARGET_DIR when it is set, so a caller's redirection doesn't break the run.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_31 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 31u32, "2026-10-27T20:18Z", "main", "10-27 16:18 main: Inventory of main's other products (blog, dice, alphabet, dir-tree-html; grep !!!!\\w+ over their .spi): exactly 1 site outside chat, dir-tree-html/shared.spi:4 ':= (<.) (left : char) (right : char) : bool = !!!!LT(left, right)', used once at tree/tree.spi:58 (left_ch <. right_ch) to order tree entries. It's a lib gap, not a shortcut: lib has no char ordering (no char compared with < anywhere in lib/spiral), and the compiler docs note that char 'only supports equality' where it isn't a number (the eBPF profile). Fix: a lib slice adding char ordering in the char/sm' operators, written over the existing code-point conversion so no host text is needed, with test blocks per backend; then dir-tree-html drops its local (<.) and uses it. After TRAIN publishes, per kit's lib cut-off. Chat's 6 Export sites stay with chat-3 (job-1793116323641, running). The blog (55 Cons/Nil sites converted to list sugar 16:0x, node proof running), dice and alphabet have 0 Cons/Nil and 0 !!!! sites.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_32 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 32u32, "2026-10-28T00:07Z", "main", "10-27 20:07 main: dir-tree-html's last !!!!LT drafted, TEMP dir-tree-char-less/apply.ps1 (dry run clean on the live repo). It drops shared.spi:4's (<.) operator, which wraps !!!!LT, and replaces its only use, tree.spi:58 in cmp_at, with (conv left_ch : u32) < (conv right_ch : u32). That's the lib idiom at xsd_regex.spi:911. Rust orders char by scalar value, which is the u32 order, so the render must be byte-identical. Proof: proof.ps1, the dir-tree-heal harness. It builds reference and healed copies with their --self-test and requires HTML byte equality over spiral/scripts, x/scripts and dir-tree-html, no unit over 1,000 lines, and 0 host macros in tree.spi. Queued as job-1793145529520 and stopped at 20:1x before it built, to give the box to the CCMR A/B. It requeues on 'CCMR landed'. Other !!!!LT sites seen in the scan are in kit (another team), the archived backlog and the Spiral-s-ML-Library/VS Code plugin cores (older eras).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_33 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 33u32, "2026-10-28T11:19Z", "main", "10-28 07:19 main: Inventory (main, 10-28 07:1x, Grep over the live trees, excluding deps and target). lib/spiral: 55 uses in 10 files. 31 are in .spir real-dialect modules (sm'_real 19, routes_real 7, json_real 5), where intrinsics are the dialect's primitives (out of scope). The 24 in plain .spi are each a single named wrapper, the target shape: am' create_base and set_base; base Export, Do, Add, Sub, Mult, Div; array_dim create, index, set, length; backend BackendSwitch dispatch (2) and Indent (6); console Printf (2, in a typecase); float_text concat (StaticStringConcat; could become sm' ++#, a one-line follow-up); sm' PrimToString in show's fallback. So lib is healed. Products: x 0, fiscal 0, dice 0, blog 0; dir-tree-html's last !!!!LT has its slice drafted (dir-tree-char-less, proof pending a slot); tibia 4 (terrain 3 and hunting_pack 1), already scheduled in TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND onto am'.create_base, index_base and set_base. kit/src holds the bulk: 683 uses in 226 files, of which !!!!Export is 622 (91%), then StaticStringConcat 11, Global 7, LTE 6, NominalCreate 4, StringLength 4, UnionToRecord 4, SymbolToString 3, and a small tail. lib already wraps Export once (base.spi:17), so kit's 622 raw Export sites are one mechanical rewrite to that wrapper (kit's code, so kit's team: a kit-side slice, verified by byte-identical regen), and the remaining 61 are a small hand pass. Remaining scope: kit Export rewrite (kit), dir-tree char proof (main), tibia's 4 (tibia), float_text concat (main, trivial).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_34 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 34u32, "2026-10-28T11:51Z", "eoie", "07:5x kit: the kit/src slice is drafted. scratchpad clean\\bang-export\\rewrite-exports.ps1 rewrites every single-line !!!!Export(name, f) into lib's wrapper, export name (f) (base.spi:17, the form x already uses), with a paren- and string-aware argument split. It also adds spiral- to the package.spiproj of any touched package that lacks it, since export comes from lib's base-. On a tree copy: 578 sites in 200 files, 64 packages linked; the 47 multi-line or non-literal sites are left for a second pass. Byte-identity regen-compare on the node: job (kit-bang-export-regen), 205 crates, P2 DLL pinned. If it's 205/205 identical, it rides the release after TRAIN4.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_35 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 35u32, "2026-10-28T12:01Z", "eoie", "08:0x kit: the rewriter also handles the stacked multi-line form now: export, then the name on its own line, then the parenthesized body, all at the original indentation. That makes 623 of 625 kit sites in 215 files (2 non-literal sites left) and 64 packages given spiral-. The 578-site compare was stopped and replaced by job-1793188973244 (214 crates, P2 DLL pinned).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_36 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 36u32, "2026-10-28T13:43Z", "main", "10-28 09:43 main: dir-tree-html part DONE (10-28 09:3x-09:43). Proof GREEN (job-1793194605722, TEMP dir-tree-char-less proof.ps1): reference and healed copies both build and pass --self-test; HTML byte-identical on 3 trees (spiral/scripts 52CD6D8E, x/scripts EE3FFFD5, dir-tree-html B3226587); no Rust unit over 1,000 lines (largest inline.rs 912); 0 host macros in tree.spi. First attempt RED (job-1793194267634): '(conv left_ch : u32)' has no char instance (tree.spi:58 ETY-ConstraintError); the heal now uses lib sm'.char_code (a backend_switch, Rust arm u32::from), equivalent to the old char '<' because Rust orders char by code point. Landed into C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html at 09:43 (unstaged): shared.spi drops ':= (<.) ... = !!!!LT(left, right)', tree/tree.spi:58 becomes '|? sm'.char_code left_ch < sm'.char_code right_ch ?> -1i32'; both files byte-identical to the proven healed copies (6754BC0C, 3DEEF7ED). dir-tree-html now holds 0 '!!!!' sites (7 .spi files searched per folder, positive control sm'.char_code found 1). Remaining for the item: kit's !!!!Export regen and tibia's 4 sites. Also fixed: proof.ps1's Rust line census no longer recurses over the whole repo copy (source folders only).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_37 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 37u32, "2026-10-29T06:08Z", "main", "10-29 02:2x main: post-wipe census (git grep -F --untracked '!!!!' over *.spi per repo; compiler samples/tests, deps, backlog and target excluded; positive control: a scratch repo with one untracked !!!!Probe reports 1). First pass without --untracked read the control as 0, so every 'tracked-only' count misses lab and scratch files; counts below include untracked files. kit 688 sites in 232 files (Export 636, Global 7, StaticStringConcat 7, LT 5, UnionToRecord 4, EQ 4): the n34-n35 Export rewriter (623 of 625 sites) lived in kit's TEMP scratchpad and was LOST in the wipe (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY), as was its regen-compare job state; it must be rebuilt from n34-n35 (paren- and string-aware split, stacked multi-line form, spiral- added to touched spiprojs). tibia 4 (ArrayCreate, ArrayIndex, ArrayIndexSet, BackendSwitch; tibia team). polyglot 15 in 2 files (Export 6, Printf 5, Conv 2, Sin, Cos). spiral 404, of which 336 are untracked lab copies (SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS 320, mostly LayoutToHeap/LayoutIndex in copied mega families; they drain with their items), and the tracked rest is apps/compiler 36, lib/spiral 24 (lib is where wrappers legitimately hold the intrinsic) and apps/cells 8. 0 in x, dice, alphabet, dir-tree-html, fiscal, blog and i574n.github. Product work left: kit (rebuild the rewriter, then the 214-crate byte-identity regen), tibia 4, polyglot 15, cells 8, and the compiler's own .spi 36 after a per-site read (some may be the compiler's own intrinsic tests).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_38 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 38u32, "2026-10-29T06:16Z", "main", "10-29 02:2x main: the kit-slice Export rewriter, lost with kit's TEMP, is REBUILT as a generic org codemod (committable home, since it applies to any repo): i574n.github/scripts/bang-export-rewrite.ps1 -Root <repo or copy> [-Apply] (untracked). It rebuilds n34-n35's design. A paren-, bracket-, string-, char- and comment-aware scan finds each !!!!Export( call and splits it at the first top-level comma. Single-line calls become export \"name\" <f> (f kept as is when it is already one parenthesized group, so the output is x's exact form, e.g. export \"iggy_job_started\" ((\\ ...) : T)). The stacked form (!!!!Export( / name line with comma / body / closing-paren line) becomes export / name line / body at the original indentation, with the closing line dropped. Code after the closing paren, a non-literal name, and any file that defines export itself (lib base.spi, cells main.spi) are skipped and reported. Packages without spiral- get it inserted right after |core-, so every later, more specific package still shadows lib names as before; the 151 src packages that already list spiral- resolve lib the same way, with no packageDir. Dry run on the real kit: 218 files, 634 sites rewritten (261 single-line, 373 stacked) in 217 files, 64 packages given spiral-, 2 skipped (src/typed_predicate/model.spi:64 and :67, non-literal item.name). That matches n35's 64 packages and its 2 non-literal sites exactly. Applied to a scratch copy (1,319 .spi/.spiproj files): 281 files change (217 .spi, 64 .spiproj), only those 2 sites remain, 0 files gain CRLF, and the diffs are the forms above. NOT yet proven: a parse check (SpiralCompiler format --check on the copy, after main's oracle run, to keep its timeouts clean) and n35's byte-identity regen of every touched crate with the P2 DLL pinned (heavy: kit team or the node, which is still blocked on the key). Nothing written to kit.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_39 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 39u32, "2026-10-29T06:44Z", "main", "10-29 02:4x main: the codemod now also rewrites the 2 'non-literal' sites (src/typed_predicate/model.spi:64 and :67, !!!!Export(item.name, ...)). A name that is an identifier path is accepted, because export is an inline definition (lib base.spi), so the macro sees the same term, and the same module already passes a field path as a plain argument (line 70: inspected item.name). Dry run on the real kit: 636 of 636 sites in 218 files (263 single-line, 373 stacked), 65 packages given spiral- (typed_predicate is the 65th), 0 skipped. Still to prove, after main's oracle runs: the parse check (format --check, before and after) and the byte-identity regen.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_40 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 40u32, "2026-10-29T08:00Z", "main", "10-29 04:0x main: two product slices LANDED (unstaged), each proven byte-identical first. (1) apps/cells/spi: the 5 local '(++) ... = !!!!StaticStringConcat(left, right)' wrappers (cell, directives, document, notebook, text) become 'left ^^ right' (CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN: ^^ is the parser's StaticStringConcat). Copies compiled with --backend Gleam give the same domain.gleam before and after (7A2CC6E9E03AC97C, also the live file's hash), and after landing mix's spiral_domain compiler regenerated domain.gleam at 03:59 to the same hash. cells spi has 1 '!!!!' left: main.spi's local export wrapper (the package lists only |core-, no lib). (2) polyglot apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.spi: 6 stacked !!!!Export sites go through i574n.github/scripts/bang-export-rewrite.ps1; copies compiled with --backend Rust give the same chat_contract.rs (EE7B10970DD4B2CE, 1,387 lines); polyglot now has 0 !!!!Export (cube.spi's Sin/Cos/Conv/Printf stay: a deliberately intrinsic-only benchmark). CORRECTION to n39's plan: SpiralCompiler format --check is NOT a parse gate. A deliberately broken .spi gives exit 0 and no 'format error' (the formatter keeps unparsable blocks as written), so the kit copy's '0 format errors before and after' is VOID. kit's only proof is n35's byte-identity regen (kit team, or the node once the key works).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_41 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 41u32, "2026-10-29T12:51Z", "kit", "10-29 08:5x kit: the byte-identity proof for the kit slice is running on the node: job-1793277020393-kit-bang-identity. The rewrite was applied to a copy of the live kit/src: 624 sites in 215 files (252 single-line, 372 stacked), 65 spiprojs given spiral-, 0 skipped. draft-regen-bundle.ps1 reached 214 crates plus the agile_note_listing control; bundle sha256 1BC33285E8B4; P2 DLL A4E480202BD4, equal to the box's installed compiler. Scope, reconciled with main's 636/218 (02:4x, whole kit root): today the root has 635 sites in 217 files. The 11 sites in 2 files outside src are infra/a/iggy-client/codec/encode.spi (10) and decode.spi (1); they're outside the shipped crates and need their own identity check (their own build, or a second bundle root) before the rewrite touches them. The remaining 1 site and 1 file is kit_job_env/env_adopt.spi, already moved to lib export by the env guard. Plan (agreed with main): if the compare is identical, the rewrite rides TRAIN4 as a phase that re-applies it to the TRAIN4 tree and re-proves identity in that train's full regen; the iggy codec pair waits for its own check.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_42 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 42u32, "2026-10-29T14:09Z", "kit", "10-29 10:0x kit: PROVEN byte-identical on the node (job-1793277020393, 99 min, finished exit 0; compiler pinned explicitly: spiral-bin-p2 core 05E94769A86A9B9C / host A4E480202BD40D80, the box's install, so unaffected by the node's stale default compiler). bang-export-rewrite.ps1 -Apply on a copy of live kit/src: 624 sites in 215 files, 65 spiprojs given spiral-. Result: 215 of 215 crates identical=True (214 reached plus the agile_note_listing control), 0 candidate crates over 1000 lines. The one compile failure is path_tag_contract, which fails identically on base and cand ('ParserErrors' at model.spi:15, 'Expected one of: inl, let, union ...'), the same pre-existing failure GRANULAR-HEAL n87 recorded; it needs its own look. Plan (agreed with main): TRAIN4 gets a phase that re-applies the rewrite to the TRAIN4 tree, and that train's full regen re-proves identity. The 11 iggy codec sites (infra/a/iggy-client/codec) still need their own check.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_43 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 43u32, "2026-10-29T14:32Z", "kit", "10-29 10:3x kit: the iggy codec pair is PROVEN identical too, which completes the kit slice's proof: all 635 sites in 217 files (src's 624/215 in n42, plus these 11/2). infra/a/iggy-client/codec was copied base/cand (packageDir pointed identically at the node mirror kit-depstest's lib, because the node's own C:\\home\\git\\spiral checkout has no iggy.spi; the first attempt, job-1793284170409, was VOID with 'Unbound module iggy' on both sides). The rewrite took 11 sites (10 single-line, 1 stacked) in 2 files, 0 spiprojs. Node job job-1793284289184 (-RequireCore 05E94769A86A9B9C, P2 DLL A4E480202BD4): encode 348 lines and decode 916 lines, identical=True for both. Side finding: the node's own spiral checkout is stale (no iggy.spi), so node jobs must use a synced mirror's lib, never C:\\home\\git\\spiral there. Plan unchanged: the rewrite lands as a TRAIN4 phase on the TRAIN4 tree, re-proven in that train's full regen; the codec files are re-applied together with it.")
