inl note_of_duplicate_code_tool_1 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-TOOL", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02: first cheap census for \"drift like rust_std_env in other lanes\": top-level defs in each lane repo whose NAME matches a lib top-level def (>= 6 chars; a name match is a lead, not proof). kit 106, x 69, tibia 26, regex 22, cells 20, graphs 2, fiscal 0, dice 0. Clear duplicates on sight: arguments_from (lib env) in kit and tibia; digits_from (lib decimal) in tibia, regex and cells; first_line (lib sm') in tibia and cells; control_escape/controls_from (lib json) in x; contains/collect/length (lib listm'/am') in regex and cells. DoD for this item now includes: the AST/shingle tool confirms or clears each name match, and each confirmed one is replaced by the lib import in the owning lane.")
inl note_of_duplicate_code_tool_2 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-TOOL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:45Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia healed main's 3 clear duplicates, unstaged. (1) arguments_from + arguments in apps/offscreen/offscreen.spi were deleted; the caller now uses env::command_line_arguments (), which is the same function. (2) first_line in apps/host/world_executor.spi now delegates as trimmed_first_line = sm'::trim (sm'::first_line text): it trims, so it keeps its own, distinct name. (3) No change for digits_from in apps/arena/combat_text.spi (an int digit run returning the stop index) or apps/map/map.spi (a quote-terminated byte run): both differ from lib decimal::digits_from, a decimal parser. Proof: node job tibia-dup-heal-3, offscreen 7/7 and world_executor 2/2 green.")
