inl note_of_upstream_fork_start_1 () = Note ("UPSTREAM-FORK-START", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:33Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:33 main: state found. There are TWO checkouts of the fork, and they diverge. (a) spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language, cloned by spiral's scripts/init.ps1 (HEAD cc1b12ac, merged mrakgr/master): the one every compile resolves |core- against, holding the consolidated core of 10-19 (15 core .spi files). (b) C:\\home\\git\\The-Spiral-Language, the standalone fork checkout (HEAD 7423e39e) where the post sits untracked: its VS Code Plugin/core still has 18 files, and only 2 are byte-identical to (a), so the core switch never reached it. \"Nothing touched in the fork yet\" is true for (b). Plan, by rule: (1) one fork checkout. (b) becomes the single source and spiral's deps points at it (junction or init.ps1 path), so core work lands where it can be pushed. Git operations stay the user's: I copy (a)'s core into (b)'s working tree uncommitted, and the user commits. (2) Then the compiler-side moves the 10-06 direction asked for (\"move everything spiral-compiler into the upstream fork\"), starting with what upstream maps one-to-one (the core library, then upstream-mapped compiler sections), each as a reviewed pack, the post staying in posts/. (3) No PR or outward step by me (no-public-project-interaction). Step (1) is CPU-light and next in my queue after the current lands; it needs a matrix run to prove compiles unchanged when deps switches, queued as a heavy step.")
inl note_of_upstream_fork_start_2 () = Note ("UPSTREAM-FORK-START", 2u32, "2026-10-24T13:37Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:37 main: correction to note 1: the fork IS spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language (current master, origin i574n), so step (1) is not a core copy. C:\\home\\git\\The-Spiral-Language is a stale 2023 checkout. The post now lives in the real fork (UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA note 30). Next fork steps: the compiler moves of the 10-06 direction, as reviewed packs.")
inl note_of_upstream_fork_start_3 () = Note ("UPSTREAM-FORK-START", 3u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_upstream_fork_start_4 () = Note ("UPSTREAM-FORK-START", 4u32, "2026-10-31T20:59Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
