inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_1 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "main", "main 00:3x WHY IT DIDN'T STICK: the item had 0 notes in 8 days because it depended on CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS, which is Blocked on user steps. A README badge isn't needed to run a codespace, so 'agile next' never offered this item. Dep removed, raised to P0 (user 11-01 00:2x: 'i asked before to always use our gh codespaces quota for dogfood but it seems it didn't stick'). Next step, CPU-light on our side: (1) gh api user/codespaces and the billing endpoint to read the quota left this month; (2) one codespace on i574n/spiral (its .devcontainer exists) running the Cells lib gate for one file, timed against the node's number for the same file (lib-sweep 10-31: am'.spi 86 s); (3) if it holds, a kit verb to send node-shaped jobs to a codespace as a third worker (KIT-EXEC-METRICS records its numbers). Owner main until kit takes the verb.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_2 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T04:48Z", "main", "main 00:4x step 1 hit a WIPE LOSS: the gh token on the box (login fc1943s, re-created after the 10-28 wipe) lacks the 'codespace' and 'user' scopes. 'gh api user/codespaces' returns 403 'needs the codespace scope', and the billing usage endpoint returns 404 'needs the user scope'. So no lane could have used codespaces even if the item had been pulled. USER STEP (interactive device flow): gh auth refresh -h github.com -s codespace,user. After that, main runs steps 1-3 the same session. Item set Blocked on that step only.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_3 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T14:07Z", "main", "main 10:0x UNBLOCKED: the user refreshed gh (scopes now codespace, gist, read:org, repo, user, workflow). Step 1 done: 0 codespaces exist; October's whole codespaces usage was 0.0386 core-hours + storage on dir-tree-html (10-20 probe), net \\ (free allowance); November 0 so far. Step 2 started: a 4-core standardLinux32gb codespace on i574n/spiral main (devcontainer: universal image + PowerShell, hostRequirements 4 cpu/16 GB/64 GB), --idle-timeout 30m --retention-period 1h, running scripts/init.ps1 then lib_gate -File am'.spi (node: 86 s) with /usr/bin/time; the driver stops the codespace at the end. Driver and log: main scratchpad codespace-gate.ps1 / codespace-gate.log.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_4 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 4u32, "2026-11-01T14:07Z", "main", "main 10:0x BLOCKED on a user step, again, now account-side. 'gh codespace create -R i574n/spiral -b main -m standardLinux32gb' returned 'Available machines: []' and created nothing. The machines API returns an empty list for every repo tried: i574n/spiral, i574n/dir-tree-html (which got a 2-core codespace on 10-20) and the personal fork fc1943s/spiral. Both the account (fc1943s) and the org (i574n) are on the free plan, and the free allowance is nearly unused (October 0.04 core-hours). So it's an account or org setting, not quota and not the repo's hostRequirements (spiral's 4 cpu/16 GB/64 GB would also need fixing later, since 64 GB storage implies the 8-core tier). USER STEP: check https://github.com/settings/codespaces (access and spending limit) and the i574n org's Codespaces policy (org settings > Codespaces). Main reruns codespace-gate.ps1 right after, with a 2-core machine first if spiral's hostRequirements still filter it out.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_5 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 5u32, "2026-11-01T14:21Z", "main", "main 10:1x ROOT CAUSE FOUND (not the account, not the org): the REST create endpoint says 'No valid machine types are available ... or by host requirements defined in your dev container configuration'. Every i574n devcontainer (16 files; CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS copied spiral's) requires cpus 4, memory 16gb, storage 64gb, and the account's machines (basicLinux32gb 2-core and standardLinux32gb 4-core) have 32 GB disks, so no machine qualified anywhere. Control: i574n/tictactoe (no hostRequirements) lists both machines, and 'Codespaces usage for this repository is paid for by fc1943s' confirms the org allows it. FIX (local, unstaged, needs the user's commit + push to take effect): storage 64gb -> 32gb in the 16 devcontainer.json files (alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, eoie/kit, fc1943s.github, fiscal, i574n.github, i574n.github.io, mechahaze-album1, polyglot, spiral, tapas2, tibia, vault, x). MEASURING NOW without waiting for that commit: a 4-core codespace on i574n/tictactoe that clones i574n/spiral and runs init + lib_gate am'.spi (driver codespace-gate.ps1, log codespace-gate.log).")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_6 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 6u32, "2026-11-01T14:47Z", "main", "main 10:4x: attempts 1-2 ran on a tictactoe codespace (4 cores, 15 GB, 32 GB disk) and cloned spiral fine, but PowerShell never installed: apt failed, and 'dotnet tool install' exited 127 because gh codespace ssh runs a non-login shell without the image's PATH. Attempt 3 wraps every remote command in 'bash -lc' and gates async.spi (node 36 s). LESSON: the driver's 'gh codespace stop' in finally did NOT take effect; both codespaces stayed Available ~25 min (~1.7 core-hours) until 'too many codespaces running' blocked attempt 3, so main stopped them by name. The driver must confirm Shutdown via 'gh codespace list' after stopping. Note: -R i574n/tictactoe resolved to fc1943s/tictactoe in the codespace list.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_7 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 7u32, "2026-11-01T14:58Z", "main", "main 10:5x: attempts 1-3 failed for a reason that wasn't PATH: tictactoe's devcontainer is ALPINE Linux 3.23 (os-release), so there's no apt, no dotnet and no ICU; the PowerShell 7.6.9 tarball runs only with DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=1, and spiral's toolchain on musl would fight us. Attempt 4 uses i574n/dotfiles, which has no devcontainer, so it gets GitHub's default universal image (Ubuntu), with the PowerShell tarball plus an invariant fallback. All earlier codespaces are Shutdown (checked by name). The driver now verifies shutdown.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_8 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 8u32, "2026-11-01T15:11Z", "main", "main 11:1x RESULT of attempts 4-6 (i574n/dotfiles, default universal image: Ubuntu 24.04, 4 cores, 15 GB, 32 GB disk with 12 GB free, .NET 10.0.403). PowerShell 7.6.9 from the release tarball works; clone 22 s; spiral's scripts/init.ps1 ran 7.5 min and stopped at Playwright's missing browser libs (dice e2e only). The lib gate did NOT run, and that is the finding: (a) lib_gate.ps1 assumes \\%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local (Windows-only), so it dies on Linux at line 10 (filed as LIB-GATE-LINUX-PORTABLE); (b) init.ps1 installs no Erlang/Elixir on Linux, because CI gets them from setup-beam, so 'mix' is missing. Restarting a stopped codespace to rerun one step takes 40-80 s, reusing its disk. Quota used today: ~3 codespaces x 4 cores for a few minutes each, plus the ~25 min idle earlier; all codespaces confirmed Shutdown by name. CONCLUSION: the right fix is a spiral devcontainer that reproduces CI's toolchain (.NET 11 rc, BEAM/Elixir, Rust, Zig, Lean) in its postCreateCommand, so a codespace equals a CI runner; until then codespaces can't run Cells gates. Filed SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_9 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 9u32, "2026-11-01T22:43Z", "main", "main 18:4x FIRST USEFUL CODESPACE RUN (in progress): a Linux full lib sweep for cross-OS parity with the node's Windows sweep of the same post-respell tree. Codespace bookish-space-goggles-6qj775x47fxv7 (i574n/dotfiles, default universal image: Ubuntu 24.04.5, 4 cores, 15 GB; spiral cloned inside, plus a tar of the box's 131 unstaged files). Setup that works (drafts store CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS\\codespace-lib-sweep.sh + -stage2.sh): pwsh 7.6.9 tarball; spiral init.ps1 7.5 min; install-dotnet.ps1; OTP 29.1.2 from builds.hex.pm with ./Install -minimal <its own dir> (it installs IN PLACE, which my first try got wrong); Elixir 1.20.5 zip; gleam 1.19.2, zig 0.18.0-dev.738, bun 1.4.4; lua5.1 needs sudo apt-get update first; cargo is in ~/.cargo/bin (not on PATH); the compiler builds in 81 s. Lessons: (1) spiral's own codespace came up in the ALPINE RECOVERY container, so its devcontainer build fails (SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY n2); (2) gh codespace cp right after create times out, so retry; (3) gh codespace ssh polls can hang indefinitely, so the driver must time-box them (the first driver wedged 45 min); (4) idle-timeout stops the codespace while a nohup job runs, because nohup work doesn't count as activity, and restarting resumes the disk. Sweep at 16 files after ~8 min.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_10 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 10u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "main", "main 19:4x FIRST USEFUL CODESPACE RUN DONE, codespace deleted. A Linux full lib sweep of the post-respell tree: 77 files, 647 passed, 3 failed, 0 type errors, 48 min of sweep after ~10 min of setup (4 cores). It gives Windows-vs-Linux parity data (LIB-SWEEP-1031-RED n4) that neither box nor node could produce. Results fetched to the drafts store (cs-lib-sweep.tsv, cs-sweep.log, cs-run2.log) before deletion; gh codespace list = []. Cost: one standardLinux32gb (4 cores) for ~2 h 40 min including setup, retries and an idle-stop. Lessons for the next batch: a driver with time-boxed ssh polls; ./Install of OTP in place; apt-get update before apt; cargo on PATH; keep the codespace active (any ssh resets idle). x-dumps proved codespaces as remote.ps1 machines ('remote.ps1 codespaces refresh' -> cs-<name>), so the next run can be a plain 'remote.ps1 cs-<name> job start'. NEXT: make the setup a reusable script (or fix spiral's devcontainer, SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY), then batch the regex benches (REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) and Linux parity gates per codespace.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_11 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 11u32, "2026-11-02T00:06Z", "main", "main 20:0x SECOND USEFUL RUN DONE, codespace deleted: regex's pre-registered benchmark on reimagined-succotash (EPYC 7763, 4 cores), provisioned by main's reusable setup script codespace-spiral-setup.sh (drafts store; ~11 min to SETUP-DONE: pwsh, spiral init, dotnet, OTP 29.1.2, Elixir 1.20.5, gleam, zig, bun, lua, rust, compiler build, Cells deps, ~/spiral-env.sh). One job: 4 A/A arms 0.997-1.007, 6 arms with equal counts (regex crate as oracle), ratios vs minimal DFA: Brzozowski 1.06-1.77, Antimirov 1.26-2.09, eager DFA 1.00-1.02 (REGEX-BENCH-PAGE n7). Pattern proven: provision, hand a worker the machine, delete on its signal; gh codespace list = [].")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_12 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 12u32, "2026-11-05T06:58Z", "main", "11-05 02:58 main THIRD USEFUL RUN, codespace deleted (gh codespace list empty): miniature-meme-x7jqqp6pp3v957, ~35 min. (1) Fresh-runner proof of the spiral init fix before the user's push: no Rust/sccache/binstall, rustup like setup-rust, then the fixed init.ps1 exit 0, CLI run check green (rust 42 was the CI red). (2) The quiet control that no shared machine could give tonight: file_system.spi 41/41 and 42/42 where europa and the node had shown 6 and 2 load-induced failures. New use pattern: a codespace as the quiet tie-breaker for reds from overloaded machines, and as the fresh runner for init/CI-order changes.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_13 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 13u32, "2026-11-05T20:19Z", "main", "main 11-05 16:2x QUOTA MEASURED (gh api users/fc1943s/settings/billing/usage): November so far 5.92 h on 4-core = 23.7 core-hours, net $0 (all included), storage 0.06 GB-h; October 0.04 h on 2-core. Against the free personal 120 core-hours/month that leaves ~96 core-hours (~24 h of 4-core) until 12-01: under-used. FOURTH RUN STARTED: a pre-push CI REHEARSAL of the box's unstaged spiral tree. HEAD faf422c9's CI has been red at init since 11-05 03:18 (the sccache-before-CLI order, fixed unstaged and fresh-runner-proven in run 3), so nothing after init has run against the 1732 modified + 126 untracked files. One standardLinux32gb codespace, CI's pins (OTP 29, Elixir 1.20, gleam 1.19.2, rebar3 3.28, zig 0.17.0, bun, rust nightly-2026-10-18 + rust-src), clone HEAD + overlay the delta, then the compiler job (workflow.ps1 -Compiler -Suite all, own bin cache) and the cells-gate job (workflow.ps1 -Compiler, model fetch, ci_gate lib/spiral,apps/transformer). Driver: scratchpad ci-rehearsal/drive.ps1, deletes the codespace in finally. Verdict pending.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_14 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 14u32, "2026-11-05T22:35Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:4x FOURTH RUN DONE (codespace deleted, gh codespace list empty): the CI rehearsal of the unstaged spiral tree took 1 h 50 min (setup 11 min, compiler job 19 min, cells-gate job 72 min) on one standardLinux32gb, about 7.5 core-hours. A first attempt died in 15 min on two setup bugs of mine (no /usr/bin/time on the image; no rustup) and now has a toolchain guard. VALUE: found that ci_gate never failed on failed tests (fixed), plus 1 new red the push would ship (json_schema, routed to fiscal) and 2 hidden pre-existing reds (process ping -n on Linux; reactors C clock); all on PIPELINES-GREEN n58. Pattern confirmed: a codespace is the pre-push CI for the box's unstaged tree. Driver: scratchpad ci-rehearsal/drive.ps1 + remote.sh (move into i574n.github/scripts when it runs again). Quota: ~31 core-hours used of 120 in November.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_15 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 15u32, "2026-11-05T22:59Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:0x: correction to n14's 'move the driver into i574n.github/scripts': no new .ps1 in repos. The rehearsal driver now lives in the kit drafts store beside the earlier codespace scripts: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS\\ci-rehearsal-drive.ps1 + ci-rehearsal-remote.sh (drive.ps1 expects remote.sh next to it as 'remote.sh'). The long-term home is a kit verb ('kit ci rehearse'), not a script.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_16 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 16u32, "2026-11-05T23:40Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:4x FIFTH RUN DONE (codespace deleted): a targeted Linux proof, 35 min (tools 7, tree 2, workflow.ps1 -Compiler 19, two single-file gates 2 + 1.5), about 2.3 core-hours. It validated ci_gate's new RED path and the process deadline test fix on Linux (PIPELINES-GREEN). europa had failed the same proof (ld bus error under its memory cap, no 'python'), so for Linux gates a codespace is the reliable quiet machine. November total about 33 of 120 core-hours. Driver variant: scratchpad ci-rehearsal/drive-proc.ps1 (the pattern: tools, tree overlay, upload a draft, one targeted step).")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_17 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 17u32, "2026-11-06T00:03Z", "main", "main 11-05 20:0x SIXTH RUN DONE (codespace deleted): regex's own CI workflow beside the unstaged spiral tree, 20 min wall (tools 5, tree 2, regex workflow 11), ~1.3 core-hours: 93/93 green, which settled REGEX-SYNTAX's lost gate and proved a consumer repo passes init with spiral's fix. November ~35 of 120 core-hours. Driver: scratchpad ci-rehearsal/drive-regex.ps1 (any consumer repo: clone it as a sibling of ~/spiral and run its workflow.ps1).")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_18 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 18u32, "2026-11-06T00:34Z", "main", "main 11-05 20:3x SEVENTH RUN DONE: dice/alphabet/blog workflows in one codespace, 30 min: blog green, dice VOID (840 s bound), alphabet VOID (needs CI's setup-tectonic/apt steps; a rehearsal of a repo whose workflow uses setup actions must replicate them first). ~2 core-hours; November ~37 of 120. Lesson for the rehearsal kit: read the repo's gh-pages.yml uses: steps and install their equivalents before running workflow.ps1.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_19 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 19u32, "2026-11-06T10:48Z", "resilience", "DELEG-ROUTER routing rule (SMART-DELEGATION): Linux CI gates -> codespace (free on public-org repos), never the 3.4GB europa (ld bus error under MemoryMax, no python - main/compiler lesson). Codespace is a first-class delegation target.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_20 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 20u32, "2026-11-06T12:04Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:2x lint fill: DoD: a reusable codespace driver (create, tools, clone + overlay, steps, fetch logs, delete) proven on 3+ repos, with the quota use per run recorded; today it ran physics, the fork posts and the CI rehearsals of 11-05. Next step: fold the driver into a kit verb (kit codespace run) instead of scratch scripts.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_21 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 21u32, "2026-11-06T13:18Z", "main", "main 11-06 12:2x USAGE today (standardLinux32gb, 4 cores, each codespace deleted by its driver's finally): 6 finished runs = 7079 s wall = 1.97 h = 7.9 core-hours (physics notebook 3 runs, fork posts 2, blog 1), plus 2 in flight now (physics 4th run, dice publish). Monthly quota is 120 core-hours, about 37 used before today. What they caught that the box couldn't (box at 100% CPU, node holding tibia's quiet timing sweep): the fork's shared cargo target, the blog engine's root-absolute links, the physics show_chart concat/array/inline-recursion bugs, the live 0-SVG baseline. Next step unchanged: fold the driver (create, tools, clone + overlay, steps, fetch, delete) into a kit verb.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_22 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 22u32, "2026-11-06T20:01Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:0x: the driver fold is handed to kit as KIT-CODESPACE-RUN (spec + 9 proven drivers in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS, now durable rather than in the session scratchpad). Correction learned today: the physics 43/43 (logs4, 13:04Z) predates physics v2, so v2's frame path was never codespace-proven; the box gate found zig reds there. A run's verdict must be tied to the source hash it ran.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_23 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 23u32, "2026-11-07T23:36Z", "main", "main 11-07 19:4x USAGE today (standardLinux32gb, 4 cores, each deleted by its driver's finally): 6 finished CI rehearsals = 8,665 s wall = 2.4 h = 9.6 core-hours (dice rerun still running). What they caught that box/node/europa couldn't (box at 99-100%, node saturated by 5 lanes):\n- blog: NoFileTarget on origin Cells -> PUSH ORDER spiral first; the pack61 E0425 in CI; the create_temp_dir rename miss (blog CI's actual red);\n- blog green after the fixes; regex 93/93 on nightly-11-05;\n- alphabet: needs tectonic (env), toolchain fine;\n- dice: the driver's staged-file blind spot (git ls-files -m vs HEAD), now fixed.\nNew driver at main scratchpad cs-pair\\drive.ps1 -Repo <r>: origin spiral + the box spiral delta + the repo delta (staged + unstaged + deletions), then the repo's scripts/workflow.ps1. KIT-CODESPACE-RUN (kit) should absorb this pair driver as its \"consumer with spiral overlay\" mode.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_24 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 24u32, "2026-11-08T05:56Z", "main", "main 11-08 01:5x usage data point: tonight's cs-pair rehearsals were 3 codespace runs on standardLinux32gb, each created and deleted by the driver (retention 1h, 'after delete: gone' confirmed): regex 23:4x-00:17 (1827 s, 77/77), regex 01:20-01:50 (1793 s, 64/64), plus the earlier nightly rehearsal (93/93). Per run: ~12 min tools install, ~4 min tree, ~10 min Cells run. The tools step (pwsh, OTP, elixir, gleam, zig, bun, two rust nightlies) is ~40 percent of each run's cost; a prebuilt devcontainer image or a cached tools tarball would roughly halve core-hours per rehearsal. Next step: measure the monthly core-hour quota left (gh api user/codespaces billing) and decide on prebuilds.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_25 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 25u32, "2026-11-09T03:27Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 23:2x QUOTA MEASURED (gh api users/fc1943s/settings/billing/usage, org3's delegated comet-quota dimension): November = 85.1 core-hours of 120 free (71% used), net 0 (all included), storage 0.25 GB-h, as of 2026-11-09T03:21Z. ~34.9 core-h left (~8.7h of 4-core) until the 12-01 reset. BURN TREND: ~37 used at 11-07 19:36 -> 85.1 now = ~48 core-h in ~2 days (~24/day, from tibia's 4-core codespace + CI rehearsals). AT THIS RATE the free quota exhausts ~11-10/11-11, well before 12-01; so the 'how much work advances until quota' answer is ~1.5 more days of current cadence. org3's saturation-monitor alerts at 110 (10 reserve) = ~25 core-h headroom before the alert; past 120 is a USER call, never a lane's. PREBUILD DECISION (n24's open question): the tools install (pwsh/OTP/elixir/gleam/zig/bun/2 rust nightlies) is ~40% of each run (~12 min); a cached tools TARBALL (tar the installed trees once, store as a release asset, overlay at create) would ~halve per-run core-hours and extend the 35h runway - recommended, but it itself costs one codespace so schedule it deliberately. NOT acting on the user-gated pieces (tictactoe .devcontainer; the devcontainer 64gb->32gb storage fix needs the user commit+push) - pending user.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_26 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 26u32, "2026-11-09T05:40Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 01:4x COMET DELETED (rig, ~01:37): the active codespace animated-umbrella (which drove the 88.9 core-h) was deleted by rig (idle, load 0.13); gh codespace list now []. So comet quota is FROZEN at ~89/120 (~31 free), NO active codespace - the creep I was tracking (87.1->88.9) stops here because the codespace is gone, not from burn pausing. It will hold ~89 until a new codespace is created, so the 110 USER-alert is further off. The 01:30 teardown watchdog MISFIRED (rig): its gh codespace list took 2.5min in the scheduled-task context, returned empty, logged 'already gone' and SKIPPED the delete while the codespace stayed Available = ~7 extra min billed (in the ~89). LESSON (rig owns, -> KIT-CODESPACE-RUN): a teardown must treat an empty/failed list as UNKNOWN and RETRY, never as gone - same class as my drift-watch 'unreachable != ok' fix (a failed probe must not read as a clean state).")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_27 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 27u32, "2026-11-09T05:51Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 01:4x MONITOR FIX (false-0-on-query-fail): saturation-monitor.sh read comet as 0.0 core-h this beat - a FALSE 0 from a transient gh billing query failure (2>/dev/null + add//0 masked the empty response to 0), which reads as 'lots of quota' and could HIDE the 110 alert. Confirmed the real quota is ~89/120 (ran the exact filter directly = 88.95; SKUs = Codespaces compute 2-core/4-core). FIX: the monitor now separates the raw gh call from the parse; a failed/empty/invalid-JSON response reports 'comet quota UNKNOWN (retry next beat)', NOT 0 - only a valid billing response yields a number. The gh billing endpoint is flaky/slow under repeated+scheduled calls (rig: 2.5min in scheduled-task context). Same failed-query-isn't-a-clean-value class as the drift-watch unreachable fix + rig's comet-teardown empty-list-isn't-gone. Real comet state: codespace DELETED (rig+compiler ~00:28-01:37), quota frozen ~89/120, no active codespace.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_28 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 28u32, "2026-11-09T08:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 05:5x NEXT STEP DONE (quota measured + prebuild decision). Quota: org3's 01:4x reading = ~89 of 120 core-h used this cycle, ~31 free, no codespace alive (comet deleted by rig 01:37), monitor reports UNKNOWN on a failed billing query instead of 0. DECISION: NO prebuilds. A prebuild is itself a billed codespace build plus prebuild storage, re-run on every push to the configured branch, so it spends the very quota it is meant to save; with ~31 core-h left that is the wrong trade. INSTEAD: a cached tools tarball (pwsh, OTP, elixir, gleam, zig, bun, the two rust nightlies) built once on a node, stored in oort, and unpacked at codespace start; it removes most of the ~12 min tools step (~40 percent of each ~30 min run). Arithmetic at standardLinux32gb (8 cores; ~0.5 h per run = ~4 core-h): today ~7 more runs fit in 31 core-h; with the tarball (~18 min, ~2.4 core-h) ~12 fit. Past the free quota = billing = the user's call (unchanged). Next step: rig's KIT-CODESPACE-RUN driver gains a tools-tarball step (fetch from oort, verify sha256, unpack), proven on one regex rehearsal with its core-h recorded.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_29 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 29u32, "2026-11-09T12:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:5x rig (the lane:team:rig wait): tools-bundle step DRAFTED in the regex rehearsal driver (drafts/i574n.github/CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS/ci-rehearsal-remote.sh, backup .before-tools-bundle): tools-bundle <presigned url> <sha256> = curl --retry 3, sha256sum -c (exit 65 on mismatch), tar --zstd -xf into ~, then requires pwsh erl elixir mix gleam rebar3 zig bun rustc on PATH or exits 66 so the driver falls back to the tools step; bash -n clean, LF only. Uses tibia's oort toolchain bundle v2 (519 MB, keyless presigned GET). Asked tibia for the bundle's internal layout (PATH must match) and the presign recipe + full sha256. Then: the drive.ps1 passes url+sha, one regex rehearsal on basicLinux32gb within the free quota (core-h recorded), compared with the ~12 min tools step. The wait stays on rig until that rehearsal.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_30 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 30u32, "2026-11-09T12:53Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:5x local rig: step finished against tibia's real bundle facts (v2 sha 991395b8..., 518,836,373 B, made from /): the remote step now extracts with sudo tar --zstd -xf -C / (the bundle's usr/local/bin symlinks are absolute and OTP embeds ROOTDIR=/opt/beam/otp, so -C ~ would break erl), verifies sha256 first, then installs the three tools the bundle lacks (rebar3, bun, rust nightly) on their usual lines; the script-wide PATH gains /opt/microsoft/powershell/7, /opt/beam/{otp,elixir}/bin and /usr/local/bin. Driver variant drafts/.../ci-rehearsal-drive-regex-bundle.ps1: presigns on the box (oort-presign.ps1 New-OortUrl, 15 min), uploads the URL as a FILE (no quoting through bash -lc), runs tools-bundle with a fall back to the tools step, defaults to basicLinux32gb (2 cores), delete + verify in finally. Checks before spending quota: presign 404-char URL, 1-byte range GET of the bundle = 206. REHEARSAL LAUNCHED 08:5x on basicLinux32gb (est. ~1.5 core-h; last reading ~31 core-h free): result, tools-step minutes vs the ~12 min baseline and core-h follow.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_31 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 31u32, "2026-11-09T13:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:0x local rig, BUNDLE REHEARSAL RESULT 1 (standardLinux32gb: i574n/spiral offers no basic machine): the bundle fetch, sha256 check and unpack to / took 8 s (12:58:17 to 12:58:25Z), versus the ~12 min tools step. rebar3 2 s, bun 2 s, rustup + nightly 66 s. ONE GAP: zig was not found on PATH. The bundle's /usr/local/bin/zig symlink points into /root/.cache/spiral-bin/toolchains, which the codespace user cannot traverse (/root is 0700). FIX (in the remote script, applies to the next run): after unpacking, chmod o+x on /root, /root/.cache and /root/.cache/spiral-bin, plus o+rX recursively on the toolchains dir. The rebuilt bundle should not ship toolchains under /root (tibia: build them under /opt). This run fell back to the tools step and continues to the tree and regex steps; core-h follows.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_32 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 32u32, "2026-11-09T13:19Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:2x local rig, BUNDLE REHEARSAL RESULT (proof: regex REGEX-JOB exit 0, discovered 64 executed 64 passed 64 failed 0; codespace humble-happiness-* deleted, list after delete: gone). Machine standardLinux32gb, 4 cores (i574n/spiral offers no basic machine). Timeline (UTC on the codespace): bundle fetch 518 MB + sha256 + unpack to / 12:57:49-12:58:25 (36 s); rebar3 + bun 4 s; rustup + nightly 66 s; zig missing (root-only toolchain dir, fixed for next time); fallback tools step 12:59:59-13:01:37 only 38 s because it skips tools already present; tree overlay 159 files; regex 594 s. TOOLS PHASE: about 2.5 min with the bundle versus about 12 min without (the 11-08 baseline), about 9.5 min saved per run. Whole run 1461 s wall on 4 cores = 1.6 core-h (free quota had ~31 core-h left before this). Driver: drafts/.../ci-rehearsal-drive-regex-bundle.ps1 + ci-rehearsal-remote.sh tools-bundle step (now with the chmod fix). Remaining for tibia's next bundle build: put toolchains under /opt, not /root/.cache, so no chmod is needed.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_33 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 33u32, "2026-11-09T17:53Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:5x local rig: second codespace use today, the STORE-LINUX-PACK-PULL rehearsal: run 1 ~1.8 core-h (pull proven, launch check refused under the image's own dotnet), run 2 ~0.94 core-h (all green after compiler's Resolve-SpiralDotnet fix and rig's late bundle-URL mint). Today's total: 1.6 (regex bundle) + 1.8 + 0.94 = ~4.3 core-h of the ~31 free at the start of the day.")
inl note_of_codespaces_quota_runs_34 () = Note ("CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS", 34u32, "2026-11-09T19:57Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 15:5x: waiting CODESPACES on rig. The driver DoD (reusable codespace driver proven on 3+ repos, quota-per-run recorded) is MET - 9 proven drivers in LOCALAPPDATA/kit/drafts/i574n.github/CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS, many logged runs. Remaining standalone step = the durable kit-verb fold, handed to rig as KIT-CODESPACE-RUN (note 20). The user's standing wish (use the quota for dogfood) is operationalized via the DELEG-ROUTER rule (note 19: route a lane Linux CI gate to a codespace), so the quota gets used by routed lane work, not by this item as standalone runs. Not launching a speculative multi-hour codespace run with no imminent push or known-red CI to action. Clears when rig lands the verb or a lane needs a routed Linux gate.")
inl backends_sota_score () = Task ("BACKENDS-SOTA-SCORE", "Standing 0-1000 score of how far all backends are from SOTA, recomputed in every report from a fixed rule (matrix agree share, sample coverage, codegen quality checks) and dogfooding agile weights (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "backends,metrics,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backends_sota_score () = Planning ("BACKENDS-SOTA-SCORE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl cells_history_review () = Task ("CELLS-HISTORY-REVIEW", "Look up in the session history how the Cells idea came to be, how progress went, whether it drifted from the original version, and why it is not finished; write the findings and the remaining path (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,history,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_history_review () = Planning ("CELLS-HISTORY-REVIEW", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl banned_words_scan () = Task ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", "Scan all repos for words the user does not want (harness, ...), heal drift, keep the list as a lint rule (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D1, 85u32, Planned, "", "drift,words,lint,team:org,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_banned_words_scan () = Planning ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_1 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 1u32, "2026-10-24T11:52Z", "main", "2026-10-24 07:52 main: scan done (tracked and untracked; deps, target and _build excluded). spiral has 0 (the compiler rename of 10-18 holds). eoie has the real drift: a package named eoie_cli_harness, which 30+ `*_cli.spi` headers name in `///- --package ../eoie_cli_harness`, plus eoie/standards/census.spi (13), state/bench.spi (4) and lab copies. Decision: fold the rename into KIT-RENAME, since that rename touches every package name anyway (eoie_cli_harness -> kit_cli_runner or similar; eoie team), so names are not renamed twice. tibia has README.md:232 (`live/` \"the live arena harness\") and docs/BENCHMARK.md (8 lines), for the tibia team. Kept: Cargo's `harness = false` (a Cargo key) and the user's own quote \"keep harnessing OTClient\" in three paused tibia titles. Done-item titles in the backlog are history and stay. Still open: the lint rule (word list) goes with GRANULAR-LINT's eoie verb.")
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_2 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 2u32, "2026-10-25T23:52Z", "main", "10-25 19:52 main: re-scan with the Grep tool, one call per repo (rg is not on this shell's PATH, so a shell rg loop prints 0 for every repo: a silent false negative, which is why each 'absent' needs a positive control). Found what the 10-24 scan missed: spiral/lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR (10-19 files), with 16 uses in rust-check, gleam-check, export-check and reprove-cuda-cpp.ps1 (a \\ variable, harness.rs, Build-Harness) and proven.tsv ('4 harness cases'). Healed: \\, runner.rs, Build-Runner, 'runner cases'; all 4 scripts parse with 0 errors; 0 hits left in the folder (unstaged, for the user's commit). x, fiscal: 0. eoie: eoie_cli_harness is gone (no *_cli.spi header names it any more). Left for KIT-RENAME (eoie source frozen): src/eoie_ci_verdict/verdict.spi:124 (a test message, 'names the harness variable'), FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md:606, and recorded bench and burnin receipt strings in state/ (bench.spi 122/197/221/239, burnin_receipts.spi:9). eoie_predicate_lift/Cargo.toml 'harness = false' is a Cargo key and stays. Backlog hits (agile.spi, 290) are history in done items and notes.")
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_3 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 3u32, "2026-10-29T05:45Z", "main", "10-29 01:5x main: re-scan after the wipe, git grep -P per repo over all 55 repos under C:\\home\\git (tracked + untracked; backlog, deps, target, _build and Cargo `harness =` keys excluded), with a positive control (a scratch repo whose one file says 'harness' reports 1 hit, so 0 elsewhere means absent). New since 10-25: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/tests/families/export_family.spi:5 (a comment, 'harness that links an exe'), healed to 'runner' (unstaged); tibia README.md:26 ('the client harness live/run-hunt.ps1', written by the 10-28 first live block), for the tibia team with README.md:246 and docs/BENCHMARK.md (11 lines) and results/path-check-pc1.txt:10. Unchanged and still waiting on KIT-RENAME: kit (and the stale eoie clone) FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md:606, src/kit_ci_verdict/verdict.spi:123, state/bench.spi 122/197/221/239, state/burnin_receipts.spi:9. Not drift, kept: upstream forks and vendored trees (zed 201, wasmer, rustix, nearcore, leptos, The-Spiral-Language, forgottenserver item names) and the user's own prose and data (vault, Trading-Journal, azeroth, singularity). BLOCKER for the rest of this item: the word list beyond 'harness' (the '...' of the 10-24 06:56 review list) was never written into a note or memory, so only 'harness' can be scanned; the lint rule still goes with GRANULAR-LINT's verb.")
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_4 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 4u32, "2026-10-30T10:32Z", "git-51", "10-30 06:3x git-51: re-scan after the 06:19 restarts, same method as n3 (git grep -P per repo, 55 repos, tracked + untracked, same exclusions, Cargo 'harness =' keys dropped), positive control 1 hit. Delta vs n3: NONE. spiral 0 (export_family heal holds); kit and the stale eoie clone the same 7 lines (FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md:606, verdict.spi:123, bench.spi 122/197/221/239, burnin_receipts.spi:9; :371 is the quoted Cargo key 'harness = false', not drift), waiting on KIT-RENAME; tibia the same 14 lines (README 26/246, BENCHMARK.md 11, path-check-pc1.txt:10), for the tibia team. Nothing healed (read-only pass). The n3 blocker still stands: the word list beyond 'harness' was never written down.")
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_5 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 5u32, "2026-10-30T14:32Z", "main", "10-30 10:32 main: the LINT RULE part is DONE as an org tool: i574n.github/scripts/banned-words-scan.ps1 (new, unstaged). It takes -Words (default 'harness'; add the rest when the user restates them), -SkipRepos (the n3 upstream and user-prose list), -ExcludePaths (deps/target/_build/node_modules/backlog) and -AllowLine (Cargo 'harness = false' keys, plain or quoted), and -FailOnHit exits 1 so it can gate. A BUILT-IN positive control runs first: a temp repo with one probe line and one Cargo key must give exactly 1 hit, or the scan throws (the 10-25 silent-rg trap). First run, 10:3x: 44 repos, 29 hits, matching n4 except tibia, now 15 lines (BENCHMARK.md has 12, n4 counted 11). Who owns what is left: (1) kit: src/kit_ci_verdict/verdict.spi:123 (a test message) and FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md:606. KIT-RENAME is finalized, so these are kit's to heal after TRAIN5 (kit source is frozen until then). state/bench.spi x4 and state/burnin_receipts.spi:9 are recorded receipt data, kept by respell-skips-state-data. The eoie folder is the stale pre-rename clone (the same 7 lines). (2) tibia: README 26/246, docs/BENCHMARK.md x12, results/path-check-pc1.txt:10, for team tibia (held under the user's direct STOP). (3) THE USER: the rest of the word list (the '...' in the 10-24 06:56 review list), never written down and lost with the transcripts.")
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_6 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 6u32, "2026-10-30T14:41Z", "main", "10-30 10:41 main: CORRECTION to n5 (and n3/n4's 'stale eoie clone'). C:\\home\\git\\eoie is a JUNCTION to C:\\home\\git\\kit (the same HEAD, 7ac6aa05), not a clone, so kit's 7 lines were counted twice. banned-words-scan.ps1 now skips junctioned repo folders, and the rerun reports the true total.")
inl note_of_banned_words_scan_7 () = Note ("BANNED-WORDS-SCAN", 7u32, "2026-10-30T22:56Z", "heal", "10-30 19:0x heal (git-51): the lost word list (the '...' after 'harness') is NOT recoverable; the n5 user blocker is final. Searched: (a) all 51 backlog notes tagged '(user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)' in agile.spi and done-notes.spi: none names another word (this item's title is the only one, 'harness, ...'); (b) the deleted-file MFT catalog: no record of the pre-wipe ~\\.claude\\history.jsonl (the user's prompt log), and every .claude.json copy is TRIMmed noise; (c) the live history.jsonl starts 10-28 17:26, after the wipe; (d) transcripts: the 890 carved lines are post-wipe only. Next step is the user's: restate the words; then pass them to banned-words-scan.ps1 -Words.")
