inl note_of_kit_no_claude_names_3 () = Note ("KIT-NO-CLAUDE-NAMES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T10:17Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 06:3x local rig, MEASURED: 28 case-insensitive claude mentions in 15 kit src .spi files (+28 in spec/one-call.md provenance lines, 3 in scripts/release-acceptance.ps1). Classified: (A) LEGIT client adapters, keep: rig_adoption ClaudeCode beside Codex in a client union (each client's transcript store and tool-call shape), process ancestry fixtures (rig_os_launch owner test), commit-trailer fixtures (rig_hook_verbs lease_verbs). (B) AGENT DETECTION by one client's env (CLAUDECODE beside AI_AGENT in agile_task_notes, rig_do_git and their tests): fold into one agent_markers list (AI_AGENT first) so a new client is one row. (C) NAMED CASES that should be generic: rig_machine_watch_model ClaudeSession (label claude:<pid>) -> AgentSession carrying the client word; rig_process_table agent_named = claude or codex plus its ps --mine message -> the same client list. (D) COUPLING to this machine's private setup, the one real defect: rig_machine_window_watch gate_summary reads ~/.claude/autonomous/gate.log in a host block; it should take the path from RIG_GATE_LOG (KIT_ twin) and print nothing when unset; behavior change for machine watch readers (org lanes), so it lands with a note to them. Next step: (D) then (C), each with its test updated. DoD: no claude literal outside the client-adapter union and fixtures. TypeFeatures: an agent_client union shared by adoption, machine watch and ps.")
inl note_of_kit_no_claude_names_4 () = Note ("KIT-NO-CLAUDE-NAMES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:31Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 12:5x local rig, (D) RESOLVED BY REMOVAL (unstaged; no notebook covers these packages, so the TRAIN43 regen + crate gate compile them). Checked before migrating: the Stop gate (~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1) no longer writes any gate.log, and the file does not exist on the box, so gate_summary read a file nobody produces and machine watch always printed \"== stop gate: no gate.log\". Removed the whole path instead of re-pointing it: rig_machine_window_watch gate_summary (a 14-line $'{...}' host block holding the ~/.claude path) and its export rig_machine_gate_summary, and in rig_machine_watch/jobs_watch.spi the extern wrapper plus the gate lines; machine watch now prints jobs then \"== windows\". Ratchet ok on both packages (a host block gone). That removes the one coupling to this machine's private setup. Next: (C) rig_machine_watch_model ClaudeSession -> AgentSession and rig_process_table agent_named via one agent_client union, then (B) the CLAUDECODE detection folded into an agent_markers list.")
inl note_of_kit_no_claude_names_5 () = Note ("KIT-NO-CLAUDE-NAMES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T15:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:0x local rig, (B) DONE (unstaged; notebooks queued: rig_do_git git_cli + grammar, agile_task_notes task_notes): one agent rule in rust_std_env/model.spi: agent_markers () = [ AI_AGENT; CLAUDECODE ] (AI_AGENT first: the generic marker; a new client is one more row) and agent_session (), a join point so it does not inline into callers. Both production copies now call it: agile_task_notes unnamed_choice (was variable_set AI_AGENT || variable_set CLAUDECODE; the now-unused variable_set helper with its inline sm'.trim is removed, shrinking the crate) and rig_do_git (its own agent_session copy over env.get_environment_variable is removed; package gains rust_std_env). CLAUDECODE now appears in production code only as that one adapter row; the test fixtures that set or clear it stay as fixtures. Ratchet ok on all three packages. Left: (C) the AgentSession/agent_client union for machine watch and ps.")
inl note_of_kit_no_claude_names_6 () = Note ("KIT-NO-CLAUDE-NAMES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T15:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:1x local rig, (C) DONE (unstaged; notebooks queued: rig_machine_watch_model model, rig_process_table ps_cli). One agent_client rule in rig_machine_watch_model/model.spi: agent_clients () = [ claude; codex ] and agent_client name. process_owner ClaudeSession : u64 is now AgentSession : string * u64 (client word, pid); owner_text renders \"<client>:<pid>\", so the claude:42 label is unchanged and a codex session now reads codex:9 (machine watch previously treated a codex process as unowned). rig_machine_watch host builds AgentSession for any listed client; rig_process_table drops its own agent_named copy and calls agent_client; the ps --mine message is built from the same list and renders the identical text the ps_cli test asserts. Ratchet ok on all touched packages. STATE vs DoD (no claude literal outside the client-adapter data and fixtures): production code now names clients only in three adapter rows: agent_clients (process names), agent_markers (env markers) and rig_adoption's client union (transcript stores and tool-call shapes); the rest are test fixtures and spec provenance. Remaining check before Done: the post-train probe of these notebooks.")
