inl note_of_kit_agile_superseded_1 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-SUPERSEDED", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:35Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-AGILE-SUPERSEDED (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_agile_superseded_2 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-SUPERSEDED", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:13Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:2x tibia (help pool): MEASURED the overstatement this item removes. Over state/agile.spi + archive/*.spi: 1216 tasks are Done. Only 2 carry the SUPERSEDED title prefix the item describes, but 134 items have a note saying \"superseded by\" / \"folded into\" / SUPERSEDED, and 83 of those are Done. So up to 83 of 1216 Done items (6.8 pct) were closed by folding, not delivery (an upper bound: some notes describe a superseded approach rather than a fold). Examples: BACKLOG-LAPS, CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST, COMPILER-SERVE-PER-REQUEST-ISOLATION, CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION, CRATE-GATE-HARDEN. SHAPE (for rig, who owns the schema): agile_activity model.spi's task_status union gains `| Superseded` and its move union a `Supersede` (Planned|Active|Blocked -> Superseded) with a required successor id; agile set ... Superseded --by <ID> writes the link and repoints dependents' deps to the successor; delivered counts (rollups, light floor, wsjf done-rate) exclude Superseded while \"closed\" includes it. A one-off migration can then re-label the 83 by their fold notes (reviewed, not automatic). Not drafting in rig's packages: adding a status case touches every exhaustive status match in kit.")
