inl kit_build_profile () = Task ("KIT-BUILD-PROFILE", "Measure eoie's build cost per crate and the release profile options (cargo --timings, thin LTO and codegen-units, rust-lld, sccache) and adopt what wins", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,build,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_build_profile () = Planning ("KIT-BUILD-PROFILE", Minutes 180u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_build_profile_1 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PROFILE", 1u32, "2026-10-25T00:59Z", "eoie", "20:59 Filed from x's build research (X-PARALLEL-BUILD notes 5-6). eoie today: 226 Cargo.toml, 572 generated .rs, 211,527 lines, median file 206 lines, 281 files under 200 lines; [profile.release] sets nothing. Measure: (1) cargo build --timings on the workspace, per-crate fixed cost (metadata decode of everything upstream, which Zed measured at over 400 ms per crate late in the graph) against codegen time, to find crates below break-even; (2) thin LTO with codegen-units 16 against the defaults; (3) rust-lld against link.exe on Windows; (4) sccache, which caches lib crates only and needs incremental off. Reuse x's rule from X-CARGO-BUILD-PROFILE. Rule, written before measuring: adopt a setting only if the clean release build wall time drops at least 15% over 3 runs each with identical test results; a regression in any test rejects it. Feeds EOIE-HAND-CRATE-UNITS (which crates are too small to pay their fixed cost).")
inl note_of_kit_build_profile_2 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PROFILE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:35Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 07:4x kit, KIT-RENAME: renamed from EOIE-BUILD-PROFILE (item IDs follow the tool name; older notes keep the old ID as history).")
inl note_of_kit_build_profile_3 () = Note ("KIT-BUILD-PROFILE", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 21:0x rig groom: a BASELINE data point from tonight, for when this runs: TRAIN43f's full release build (kit-cli and kit-dev, default [profile.release], CARGO_BUILD_JOBS unset = 8 jobs) took 22 min 52 s on moon (8 cores, otherwise idle), against more than 60 min on earth under multi-lane load the same day (it hit the 1 h build timeout at about half the crates). Trains now cap CARGO_BUILD_JOBS at half the cores and run BelowNormal (release-train.ps1, 11-10), so the A/B must pin CARGO_BUILD_JOBS explicitly in both arms or the caps confound it. The workspace has grown since 10-25 (387 crates in TRAIN44). Still a node run (3 clean builds per setting): wait set until a node is free.")
