inl note_of_kit_generated_profile_1 () = Note ("KIT-GENERATED-PROFILE", 1u32, "2026-10-25T01:03Z", "x", "10-24 21:03 x: gap hit while doing X-HAND-UNITS. eoie has crate gate counts (EOIE-CRATE-GATE) and source-topology, but no per-item profile of generated code, so x wrote a stopgap measuring script in %TEMP%\\x-units\\measure.ps1 (BuildSpiral on a scratch copy, then per-item heads and the specialization sum). What it found today: thread's 3 export closures each re-inlined wire.describe_failure (~75 lines; write and users carry 4 copies each), found by counting a literal's repeats per crate. The verb should report exactly that: items by size, and literal/body blocks repeated within one output. Fold it into CRATE-GATE-HARDEN n14 (largest fn report) if that's the same record.")
inl note_of_kit_generated_profile_2 () = Note ("KIT-GENERATED-PROFILE", 2u32, "2026-10-31T00:36Z", "main", "10-30 20:36 main groom (BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030 group C): the measurement script this item's latest note cites, %TEMP%\\x-units\\measure.ps1, is GONE (10-28 wipe; Test-Path false). The next step must rewrite it, preferably as a kit command or a committed script (generic-tools rule) rather than in TEMP.")
