inl note_of_kit_generated_profile_4 () = Note ("KIT-GENERATED-PROFILE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T19:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, PROFILE CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_generated_profile/profile.spi (pure, HostFree), shaped on a real generated crate (rig_agile_records/agile_records.rs: column-0 fn headers, items closed by a column-0 brace, specializations named method<N> / closure<N>, 8 of them there; generated Gleam keeps the same column-0 rule). item_kind Specialization | NamedItem (a specialization only when the prefix is followed by a digit, so methods_total is named); items_of gives { name; kind; first_line; lines; body } per item; profile_report = items, total lines, specialized lines (the specialization share), and repeated blocks = groups of items whose bodies are byte-identical apart from the header (the repeated-literal-block signal, names ignored). Test: four items, 6 of 14 lines specialized, the prefix trap, and one three-member identical-body group. Ratchet clean (the style hook first refused a records-only version; the union is the fix). NEXT: the IO half, kit profile <entry.spi | crate.rs> --top N, reading the generated file the build already wrote.")
inl note_of_kit_generated_profile_5 () = Note ("KIT-GENERATED-PROFILE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The first probe was red and is fixed (unstaged): open is a keyword (local renamed) and sm'.length pinned to i32 (ETY-ValueRestriction); re-probed green. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
