inl lib_cells_roundtrip_rest () = Task ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", "The 15 lib files whose Cells .livemd round trip is not byte-identical, which keeps DocumentTest 'lib .spi files load as notebooks' red; the same on words and edition-3 text: no blank line before a ///> target line (decimal, float_text, json_schema, schematron, schematron_run, xpath, xpath_eval, xsd_constraints, xsd_regex), a test right after the header line (dictm, json_scan), a heading moved or dropped (file_system remove_dir_all, reflection get_union_fields_untag), a test name losing its trailing underscore (listm' map4_ -> map4), and xml.spi mangled and not idempotent", Story, P1, D3, 30u32, Planned, "", "lib,cells,roundtrip,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest () = Planning ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_1 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 1u32, "2026-10-25T01:48Z", "main", "2026-10-24 21:48 main: decision rule, written before fixing. Where Document only normalizes layout (the blank line before ///>, a test right after the header), fix the lib text toward Document's canonical form, the same rule LIB-SM-ROUNDTRIP used. Where Document loses information (map4_ -> map4, a dropped or moved heading, xml.spi's mangled text), fix Document, because a round trip must never change a name or drop text. xml.spi first: its string literals hold '<?', '?>' and '<!--', and the round trip turns code into a /// heading. Scan to rerun: scratch sm-rt/lib-trip-all.exs with TRIP_LIB.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_2 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 2u32, "2026-10-25T03:20Z", "main", "2026-10-24 23:20 main: the most common shape is cross-repo. Document drops a 'test <name> static =' header that sits on line 2, right under the ///- package line: lib dictm and json_scan, blog engine/html.spi, and all 33 of tibia's failing files (tibia's respell scan, e.g. src/wire.spi line 2 -> ''). Fix Document for this one first: one fix clears about 36 files across 3 repos.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_3 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 3u32, "2026-10-25T06:26Z", "main", "2026-10-25 02:26 main: option B drafted (tibia's diagnosis; tibia handed it back): %TEMP%\\cells-document-tight\\apply.ps1. emit_spi puts no blank line after a lone one-line ///- --package cell (anchor 1/1, dry run clean). Apply when no Cells run reads the tree (x's verify-landing10 and main's lib gate are running now). In the same land, lib float_text.spi and blog engine/style.spi drop their blank line after the package line; fiscal's generator emitters follow in the fiscal lane. The proof is the lib-trip-all scan before and after: dictm and json_scan leave the failing set, and nothing joins it.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_4 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 4u32, "2026-10-25T12:52Z", "main", "10-25 08:54 main: shape found by livemd-from-spi on polyglot apps/perf. Markdown after the LAST code cell of a .spi is dropped by spi -> livemd -> spi: first the empty trailing heading '/// ## hasAnyPairCloseToEachotherTests' was lost; with that heading removed, the 31 trailing '/// Ranking / Test case' lines before it were lost instead. So any trailing markdown run is dropped, not just an empty heading. The heading-removal workaround was wrong and is reverted (Perf.spi restored byte for byte). Perf.livemd stays in edition-2 words until this is fixed, and polyglot apps/perf/build.ps1 exports livemd -> Perf.spi, so its next build would revert Perf.spi to words. Cells fix: emit and parse a trailing markdown cell after the final code cell, with a DocumentTest case ending in prose.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_5 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 5u32, "2026-10-25T12:59Z", "main", "10-25 08:59 main: cause of the trailing-markdown shape: apps/cells/spi/document.spi export_text wraps its cells in keep_docs, which drops the LAST cell when it is markdown (rationale not recorded; its only history is the squashed 10-17 commit). Batch job-1792933087976 (cells-trailing-docs\\run.ps1): waits for no Cells readers; snapshots; runs the lib round-trip scan before; removes keep_docs (call site and definition); adds a DocumentTest case ending in prose and a trailing empty heading; scans after; runs the suite; restores on any new suite failure or newly failing scan file. It also shows how many of the 15 currently failing lib round-trip files this fixes. Once green: regenerate polyglot apps/perf/Perf.livemd with livemd-from-spi.ps1.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_6 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 6u32, "2026-10-25T17:05Z", "fiscal", "13:0x fiscal: xsd_regex.spi leaves this list once XSD-SLICES lands: the kit's livemd round trip shows the tree xsd_regex.spi 'differs' and the candidate 'ok' (verdict 20261025-1218), most likely via the test interleave (6 trailing tests moved next to their definitions). Re-read the list after the land (job-1792947423678).")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_7 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 7u32, "2026-10-26T15:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 11:04 fiscal: fresh sweep of all 76 lib/spiral .spi through the kit round trip: 17 differ. (a) 8 differ only by the missing blank line before '///> rust': decimal, float_text, json_schema, schematron, schematron_run, xpath, xpath_eval, xsd_constraints (xsd_regex has left this list). (b) The 9 others change content: am'_prototypes, backend, dictm, file_system, json_scan, listm' (map4_ -> map4), reflection, runtime, xml (line 1 becomes string-literal text). The list in this item's body was missing am'_prototypes, backend and runtime. Measured rule: a blank line before EVERY '///>' line is WRONG. On copies it fixed the 8 but turned 15 ok files into differs (base, benchmark, common, conversation, crypto, date_time, guid, json, parsing, platform, reactors, routes, sm', threading, trace). So the gap is applied only to the 8 named files, which go differs -> ok with nothing else touched. Landing ready (fiscal session scratchpad landings/target-gap: apply.ps1 runs target_gap.py on the live version of each file, so it stacks after the XSD release, R8 and R9; gate-only.ps1 = kit gate LIB-TARGET-GAP). It runs after those three land. Also fixed in the kit: roundtrip.exs crashed on a file new to the candidate, giving false 'tree new' rows (see FISCAL-TYPEFEATURE-DRIFT note 102). The release gate 20261026-1016 shows 'tree ok' rows after the new xsd_certificate.spi with the fix.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_8 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 8u32, "2026-10-26T15:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 11:08 fiscal: map4_ diagnosis (document.spi). heading_test_name = strip_underscores (test_name_go ...), and test_name_go never ends on a separator. So NO heading can yield a test name ending in '_'. name_tested writes '#### map4_ (test)', which reads back as 'map4'. Do not simply stop stripping trailing underscores; that stripping is load-bearing: lib seq 'test take_while_3' sits under '/// ### take_while_' (third use of base take_while; without the strip it derives take_while__3), and polyglot lib/math 'test test_zeta_at_1' sits under '/// ## test_zeta_at_1___'. Do not rename the lib test either: listm' defines both map4 and map4_ (same body, inner loop := vs :~), 'test map4_' is map4_'s only test, and 15 of listm''s 29 tests share their function's name, which is the convention. Per main's rule (Document loses information -> fix Document), the fix is an explicit name channel used only when a heading can't carry the name. Shape: name_tested checks 'heading_test_name heading_source = name'. If that fails, it adds a '///- --name <name>' option line to the test cell, and test_block_go / name_tests take '--name X' over the derived name (test_block_go already folds every '///-' line into options). This is a Cells change, so it needs DocumentTest cases (a trailing-underscore name, plus take_while_3 unchanged) and the lib round-trip scan before and after.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_9 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 9u32, "2026-10-26T15:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 11:15 fiscal: drafted the map4_ Document fix (fiscal session scratchpad cells-name/name_transform.py; drafts in cells-name/draft). document.spi 462F60C7 -> C93DCC80: helpers head_and_tail / explicit_name / with_name; name_tests and index_tests take '--name X' from a test cell's first line over the derived name; name_tested adds ' --name <name>' to the cell's first line only when heading_test_name of the emitted heading differs from the name, inserted before any ' --fails ' clause (the clause runs to the end of the line) and never first (real_marker checks starts_with '///- --real'). directives.spi FFE78285 -> DB5E7955: pair accepts Token ('--name', Token (_, rest)). Without that, the runner's ParseBad 'flag' would reject every renamed cell. document_test.exs 2043DEE7 -> 7E33338C: two cases (map4_ round-trips via --name and is idempotent; a test named 'take' under '### take_' keeps the heading name with no --name). Proof queued locally after the R7+R8 gate: job-1793027697435 = A/B on %TEMP% copies (never the live tree), with 6 Cells suites per variant plus the 76-file lib round-trip scan per variant. Pass rule, written before it runs: b has no suite failure that a lacks, b's two new cases pass, b's failing scan set = a's minus listm'.spi with nothing added.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_10 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 10u32, "2026-10-26T15:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 11:25 fiscal: xml.spi cause found, and it is in the Elixir side (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/document.ex). render_cell writes each spiral cell's metadata as '<!-- livebook:<json> -->' with the full source in attrs.source. markdown_part strips comments with the non-greedy '<!-- livebook:.*?-->', so the first '-->' inside the JSON ends the comment early (xml.spi read_nodes holds the literal '-->'). The rest of the JSON parses back as a markdown cell at the top. The parse side never reads the JSON (source comes from the elixir fence via eval_source), so the fix is render-only: attrs |> String.replace('-->', '--\\u003e'). It stays valid JSON with an identical decoded value. Simulated over all 76 lib files: only xml.spi's livemd bytes change, and escaping every '>' would have rewritten nearly every livemd. xml.spi also needs one layout fix (a blank line between test measures_the_shape_of_a_schema and := element_children, line 219/220). With both, xml.spi round-trips byte for byte (simulated: plain false, fixed true). Both are added to the same queued A/B (job-1793027697435, still queued): b also gets the document.ex draft, the xml.spi blank line, and a DocumentTest case ('a cell source holding --> stays inside its livebook comment'). Amended pass rule, written before it runs: b's failing scan set = a's minus listm'.spi AND xml.spi, with nothing added; no suite failure in b that a lacks; b's 3 new cases pass.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_11 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 11u32, "2026-10-26T16:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:13 fiscal: first A/B run VOID (job-1793027697435): variant b never compiled. 'Package .../b/spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin/core is not loaded': apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj takes |core- from the spiral root's deps, and the copies had no deps/. Variant a got through only by reusing cached compiled output for its unchanged .spi; its results match the baseline (3 known DocumentTest failures: alphabet, dice, lib load; 17 lib files differ). The runner now copies the 19-file core package into each variant. Rerun with the same pass rule: job-1793031122436.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_12 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 12u32, "2026-10-26T16:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:37 fiscal: A/B rerun (job-1793031122436) result, read against the pre-written rule. Suites: b's failures (dice, alphabet, lib-load DocumentTests) are a subset of a's (the same 3, plus a NotebookReportTest flake in a), and the 3 new cases pass in b. Scan: xml.spi LEFT the failing set (17 -> 16) and nothing joined. listm'.spi still differed, so the rule as written ('minus listm'') was NOT met. Cause: a SECOND, layout-only difference (a test runs straight into '/// ### try_find'' at line 209/210; same class as reflection's). map4_ itself round-trips via --name (its new case passes). With one lib blank line each, listm' and reflection round-trip ok on b's copy. Landing shape now: (1) lib layout = LIB-TARGET-GAP extended to 11 files (the 8 '///>' gaps + blank_before.py anchored inserts for listm', reflection, xml; verified on a copy: exactly those 11 change), gated by the kit gate.ps1; (2) Cells fidelity fix (document.spi C93DCC80, directives.spi DB5E7955, document.ex 1959BB90, document_test.exs 897DA489). Its gate is the A/B with the rule ENCODED in the runner (cells-name/ab.ps1, which writes verdict-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-FIDELITY.txt to the kit): no new suite failure in b, the 3 cases pass, b = a + 3 tests, no file joins the failing set, and all 11 layout / fidelity files leave it. Expected remainder: 6 (am'_prototypes, backend, dictm, file_system, json_scan, runtime: keep_docs plus option-B shapes). Running: job-1793032596876.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_13 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 13u32, "2026-10-26T16:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:45 fiscal: fidelity gate run 1 (job-1793032596876) came back RED on a MEASUREMENT bug only. Every substantive condition held: b's failing scan set = exactly the expected 6 (am'_prototypes, backend, dictm, file_system, json_scan, runtime; 17 -> 6, nothing joined), b has no suite failure a lacks, and the 3 new cases did not fail. The red reason was 'test counts -1': this suite uses a custom formatter whose summary is 'Result: P/T passed' (a 76/79, b 79/82, so b = a + 3 as required), not ExUnit's 'N tests, M failures'. The parser is fixed (checked on both logs: totals 79 and 82), and the gate is rerunning so a run decides, not my reading: job-1793033043935. Landing prepared: session scratchpad landings/cells-fidelity (4 frozen files, byte-identical to the gated b: document.spi C93DCC80, directives.spi DB5E7955, document.ex 1959BB90, document_test.exs 897DA489; base-pinned to live 462F60C7 / FFE78285 / 913A272E / 2043DEE7, all-or-nothing, dry run ok; land.ps1 -Name CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-FIDELITY -Target/-GuardedTree apps/cells -Include *.spi,*.ex,*.exs). It lands on a GREEN verdict. The 11-file lib layout landing (LIB-TARGET-GAP) is gated AFTER the XSD release and R8 land, because it touches their files, so its gate must see the bytes it will land on.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_14 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 14u32, "2026-10-26T16:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:48 fiscal: backend.spi (trailing markdown dropped by keep_docs) is the last CONTENT-losing file of the 6. Main's batch job-1792933087976 (%TEMP%/cells-trailing-docs/run.ps1, 10-25) edited the LIVE tree and restored its snapshot on RED; keep_docs is still in document.spi, so it went RED (its job record is gone). Likely a false RED: its known-failure list names 2 tests, but today's baseline fails 3 (alphabet, dice, lib-load), so alphabet and dice would count as 'new'. That is the same class as my fidelity gate's parser miss. The change itself is unproven, so it is redrafted over the fidelity draft with main's exact anchors (session scratchpad cells-trailing/draft: document.spi 0E208D63 over C93DCC80, keep_docs call + definition removed, 0 left; document_test.exs E4051116 over 897DA489 with main's 'markdown after the last code cell survives the round trip' case). Proof plan, rule fixed now: an A/B on copies (never the live tree) after the fidelity fix lands; b = a + 1 test; no b failure a lacks; the new case passes; the failing scan set shrinks by exactly backend.spi with nothing joining. If any other file joins, keep_docs protected something and the cause is traced before going on.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_15 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 15u32, "2026-10-26T16:59Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:59 fiscal: fidelity gate GREEN 20261026-1258 (job-1793033043935, rule encoded in the runner): suites a 79 / b 82 tests (+3), the same 3 known failures (alphabet, dice, lib-load), and the 3 new cases pass; lib round trip a 17 -> b 6 differ, exactly the expected remainder (am'_prototypes, backend, dictm, file_system, json_scan, runtime), nothing joined. LANDING now via land.ps1 -Target/-GuardedTree apps/cells (the reader guard waits for any live Cells run; main's Nil batch is running one): job-1793033954641. Pins pre-checked (dry run ok). After it lands: the keep_docs A/B (cells-ab tool, spec cells-trailing/spec.json), then the 11-file LIB-TARGET-GAP gate once main's Nil batch and the XSD release / R8 have landed, so the layout gate sees the bytes it lands on. Main told about the S2d / layout overlaps with its Nil batch.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_16 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 16u32, "2026-10-26T18:52Z", "main", "10-26 14:52 main: 10-26 15:0x main: Cells package-subdirectory namespace fix DRAFTED and unit-proven (TEMP cells-dir-open). fiscal confirmed (15:0x) that it doesn't overlap its fidelity/keep_docs files (document.spi, directives.spi, document.ex, document_test.exs) and that it stays main's.\nShape: apps/cells notebook.ex execute/4, right after decode_plan |> attach_source and BEFORE Memo.context, so memo keys include the change and no cached pre-fix failure is replayed. Each step's program goes through the new Notebook.directory_open(program, opts[:path]). When the cell's '///- --package <root>' header names a root that strictly contains the source file's directory, it inserts ':< <dir.as.dotted>' right after the header. Skipped when that open is already present (lib's rust/near), when there is no header or no path, and for modules at the package root or outside every package. The drive-letter comparison is case-insensitive.\nTest: new test/spiral/cells/notebook_directory_open_test.exs, 5 cases. A standalone elixir run of the drafted helper passes 5/5. Positive control: an identity stand-in (today's behavior) fails exactly the 3 open-expecting cases (2/5 pass), so the suite sees the fix.\nLanding rule, written now: after fiscal's 'landed' (job-1793033954641), (1) apply to a fresh apps/cells copy that postdates it; (2) mix test on the copy, full suite, with failures equal to fiscal's recorded baseline set (3 known: alphabet, dice, lib-load) and the 5 new cases passing; (3) blog scripts/build.ps1 with the patched Cells: the reference must go from the recorded 'Unbound term variable: html' to exit 0; (4) the lib subdirectory-module gates (rust/near, rust/testing) unchanged. Then land through the reader-guarded land path fiscal uses for apps/cells, unstaged. Then rerun blog-list-sugar-proof unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_17 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 17u32, "2026-10-26T18:52Z", "main", "10-26 14:52 main: Correction to note 16: its text says '10-26 15:0x', and fiscal's confirmation also came at 14:4x-14:5x, not 15:0x. The note was written at 14:52 local (its stamp, 18:52Z, is right; only the prose time was wrong).")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_18 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 18u32, "2026-10-26T19:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 15:40 fiscal: the fidelity landing (job-1793033954641, verdict GREEN 20261026-1258, staged, NOTHING written) changed blockers: from tibia's Cells run to kit's release train ('kit-release-FOLLOWUP reads the live lib in its notebook-check and spiral-tests phases'), which can run up to 8 h. The landing's own cap ends ~17:59, so it will most likely time out still waiting. That is a safe outcome (the reader guard never released, so no file changed), not a failure. kit also needs fiscal 'clear' (no running or queued local job) at its rename pause, so the real path is the requeue recorded in the fiscal session scratchpad requeue-after-rename.txt, after kit's 'rename finalized'. At that point re-check the 4 apps/cells bases (462F60C7 / FFE78285 / 913A272E / 2043DEE7) before requeuing: if a base moved, re-run the cells-ab fidelity gate first (verdicts carry bases).")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_19 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 19u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "main", "10-29 22:00 main, groom (WIP rule, 3 days with no note): Active -> Paused, progress kept at 30%. Last note 2026-10-26, before the 10-28 profile wipe interrupted every lane, and no live job. Resume when picked; it is not abandoned, and it keeps its priority P1.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_20 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 20u32, "2026-10-31T20:57Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_21 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 21u32, "2026-11-07T22:14Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. Today's state: document_test's 'lib .spi files load as notebooks' passes again (26/26, after x's blank-line fix and main's near_wallet/dice fixes). DoD: every lib/spiral .spi round-trips byte-identically through Cells' .livemd writer (the 15 named here re-measured; any left listed with its cause). Next step: run Document round trip over every lib file and diff the list against the 15 named. TypeFeatures: none new; a round-trip law per file (see TFS-CONVERSION-LOSS-LAWS: spi -> livemd -> spi is a Retraction).")
inl note_of_lib_cells_roundtrip_rest_22 () = Note ("LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST", 22u32, "2026-11-10T15:17Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~15:1xZ: DoD RE-MEASUREMENT DONE. Ran Document round-trip (spi->livemd->spi) over all 174 REAL lib/spiral modules (excluded generated bench/target subtrees - the raw **/*.spi glob otherwise processes ~34 generated cells_after cells and MISSES the real modules). Result: 173 canonical, ONLY 1 non-canonical = array_prototypes.spi (canonical false, fixpoint TRUE). The \"15 named\" is down to 1: the lambda-parens + heading-cleanup + Cells-fidelity waves that landed since the 15 were named fixed the other 14. CAUSE (array_prototypes.spi): a blank line at line 2, between the \"/// ### array\" heading comment (-> markdown cell) and the first := def (-> code cell); the livemd writer canonical form omits that separator, so the round-trip drops it (7 lines -> 6). Same layout-normalization class as the already-landed xml/listm/reflection fixes. fixpoint TRUE = the writer output round-trips to itself, so removing line 2 (source := writer canonical) yields byte-identity with NO writer change - proven safe. FIX DRAFTED (unstaged, NOT applied to live src per restore-on-red): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-CELLS-ROUNDTRIP-REST\\array_prototypes.spi (6-line) + .base (live 7-line). Lands via the Cells round-trip / lib-land gate like the others. HARNESS NOTE for whoever lands it: use mix run --no-start --no-compile spi/lib_roundtrip.exs <lib> <out> [files] - plain mix run fails on the app Spiral recompile (base.spi:275 !!!!EQ); --no-compile runs against the built BEAM. Only the gated land remains.")
inl gleam_compact_output () = Task ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", "Compiler (Gleam codegen): emit single-expression case arms without a brace block and fold 'let vN = x' followed by a bare 'vN' into the expression, so generated Gleam is ~15% shorter (measured on x sim probes: g_split 1159 -> ~1000, g_world 4899 -> ~4120). Output compaction, not splitting.", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "PACK-7", "compiler,gleam,codegen,x", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gleam_compact_output () = Planning ("GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT", Minutes 180u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl x_edition3_respell () = Task ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", "x: respell every x .spi (apps/client, apps/sim's Spiral) to edition-3 symbols with %TEMP%\\edition3-spread\\respell-repo.ps1 -Name x -Root C:\\home\\git\\x. The tool works on copies and applies only when green: test headers verbatim, word round trip byte-identical, installed formatter on top. Gate: the Cells round-trip scan on the original and symbols copies must give identical failure sets.; reopened for the 10-26 round (one review): spiral.toml for its 2 package.spiproj, member access .x -> ::x (2,233 symbols), macro sigils @@/##, 51 raw !!!! -> lib wrappers (Export first: an inl export wrapper gave byte-identical Rust on refs.spi), 9 lines > 120, 280-weight split, then X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY", Story, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "x,edition3,format", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_edition3_respell () = Planning ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", Minutes 120u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_edition3 () = Task ("TIBIA-EDITION3", "Respell the tibia repo to edition 3 (user directive 10-24 23:0x via main): respell-repo on copies, round-trip scan, guarded land with compiled-Lua identity and a memo-off build; then the map generator and src/terrain.spi once a spelling-capable formatter is installed", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,edition3,spelling", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_edition3 () = Planning ("TIBIA-EDITION3", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl edition3_test_symbol () = Task ("EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL", "Edition-3 symbol for test headers: :# (the scheme puts : before every top-level form; echoes Rust #[test]; 0 uses of :# in spiral, x and tibia; # is an operator char, so :# lexes as one operator token). The lexer maps :# to TokVar (\"test\", variable), so blockParsingIsTest, the header check and the test modes work unchanged. Rollout: (1) 5j lexer arm (test-symbol-lexer.ps1, staged); (2) Cells reads and writes :# headers keeping each header's spelling across the .livemd round trip (document.spi 374/533/574, memo.ex @test_header, accept.ex header regex, document_test.exs ^test regex) and tree-sitter recognizes :#; (3) only then format --spelling writes :# for column-0 test headers (convertLine), and a mechanical pass converts every repo", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "edition3,cells,tree-sitter,team:compiler,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_edition3_test_symbol () = Planning ("EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl lib_generated_cost () = Task ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", "Shrink the Rust that two generic lib helpers generate per crate: file_system.file_delete's traced error path and union_reflection's per-case closures", Story, P2, D4, 70u32, Planned, "", "lib,rust,crates,kit,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_generated_cost () = Planning ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_1 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 1u32, "2026-10-25T05:59Z", "eoie", "01:59 Measured while hand-splitting eoie crates (EOIE-HAND-CRATE-UNITS). (1) file_system.file_delete: on Rust, the Error arm calls trace Critical, which pulls in the trace state machinery. One call cost about 200 generated lines in eoie_job_host (held_released 117 + new_trace_state 87); a one-call std::fs::remove_file primitive removed them. (2) union_reflection.cases.union_case_where and union_cases_fold build one closure per union case: dropping one small union_case_where lookup saved 46 lines in eoie_ci_probe, and union_cases_fold over the 25 agile subcommands costs 202 lines (agile_subcommand_of) plus 347 (agile_subcommand_shape) in every crate that inlines them. Rule, written before changing anything: keep the APIs and their meaning (one record per fact stays: the union is the table); a change lands only if the lib tests and Cells pass and the generated size of a probe crate drops by at least 25% for that helper, measured on the same compiler. Options to measure: file_delete returns or ignores the error without a trace on Rust (the caller decides); union reflection generates a single match or if-chain instead of nested closures.")
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_2 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 2u32, "2026-10-25T06:15Z", "main", "2026-10-25 02:15 main: (1) file_delete MEASURED by the item's rule on a one-call probe (main calls file_system.file_delete once; installed 5j, Rust): live lib 517 generated lines with 13 trace mentions; patched 78 lines with 0, an 85% drop against the 25% bar. The patch: the Rust Error arm uses console.write_error_line (sm'.(++#) \"file_system.file_delete: \" error') instead of trace Critical. console comes before file_system in lib's module order. The other backends already report nothing (Zig catch {}, Gleam, Lua). The binary was checked: a missing file deletes nothing and exits 0; a file locked with no sharing prints \"file_system.file_delete: Os { code: 32 ... }\" to stderr and exits 0, as before (non-fatal). The slice is %TEMP%\\lib-file-delete-cheap\\apply.ps1 (anchor 1/1), gated by the lib kit on file_system.spi, then landed, as job-1792908815992. (2) union_reflection's per-case closures are next, by the same rule.")
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_3 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 3u32, "2026-10-25T06:23Z", "main", "2026-10-25 02:23 main: (2) union_reflection probe (installed 5j, Rust; a 25-case union plus a spec function returning (name, shape), in eoie's agile_subcommand_shape form). Variant A, union_cases_fold with the step inlined per case: 335 generated lines, and the binary prints the right shape. Variant B, cases folded into a list at compile time, made runtime with dyn, then listm'.try_find: EJP0040 (more than 1,000 nested dynamic ifs). try_find is a recursive inl, so it still unrolls over a dyn list; B needs a real runtime loop (a let rec or join point over the list, or an array with one indexed loop) so that spec compiles to one 25-arm match instead of 25 inlined copies. Next: write that variant and measure it against A's 335 by the 25% rule. Probes are in %TEMP%\\lib-generated-cost\\union-*.")
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_4 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 4u32, "2026-10-25T06:26Z", "main", "2026-10-25 02:26 main: (2) MEASURED, union lookup on 25 cases (installed 5j, Rust, the binary prints the right shape): union_cases_fold with the step inlined per case: 335 lines. Cases folded once into a list, made runtime with dyn, searched by a let rec loop (spec becomes one runtime match): 248 lines, a 26% drop, so it clears the 25% bar. The listm'.try_find variant hits EJP0040, because the recursive inl unrolls even over a dyn list. The helper this points to: lib reflection gets union_cases_find (a runtime loop over the dyn case list, written with list sugar per memory list-sugar-not-cons: | v :: rest =>, never Cons). Callers like eoie's agile_subcommand_of and agile_subcommand_shape switch to it. Expected gain per crate is about 26% of those helpers' 202 + 347 lines. Not landed yet; the next step is the helper plus a lib test, gated by the kit.")
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_5 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 5u32, "2026-10-25T07:15Z", "eoie", "03:15 eoie measurement for the union_cases_find design, on 5k with baseline and trial in one job: making agile_subcommand_shape go through agile_subcommand_of (union-returning fold plus a match), instead of its own string fold, moved eoie_agile_routes from 692 to 816 (+124). No other consumer of agile_subcommand_domain changed (agile_task_query 685, command_spec_domain 693, eoie_agile_mutation 723, eoie_command_help 865). Reverted under the prewritten rule. Read: per-case unrolling costs more when the fold's accumulator is a union than when it is a string, so a find helper returning option t may pay that cost per call site. Measure union_cases_find on routes (shape only) as well as on the of form before switching both.")
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_6 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 6u32, "2026-10-25T07:40Z", "main", "10-25 03:40 main: both slices from the cost probes LANDED in the tree lib, uncommitted. file_system.file_delete's Rust error arm now prints one stderr line (one-call probe: 517 -> 78 generated Rust lines). Gate job-1792908815992 GREEN: file_system.spi 19/22, the same 3 reds as the unchanged tree lib. reflection.union_cases_find (fold-backed): gate job-1792909796496 GREEN 10/10. Its first land hit a transient 'file in use' on reflection.spi; the retry, job-1792913813496, landed. eoie told.")
inl note_of_lib_generated_cost_7 () = Note ("LIB-GENERATED-COST", 7u32, "2026-10-25T22:52Z", "eoie", "18:52 kit: the lib batch for S1 owner-parent (scratch lib-gaps-3\\lib-batch.do: env.command_line_arguments_from plus env.process_id, sm'.char_code/of_char, console.read_to_end, file_system.try_append) still applies to the live lib after the day's lib lands by other lanes. do-dry on copies, root lib\\spiral: ok, 4 files, 5 replacements (env.spi lines 205 and 241, sm'.spi 1063, console.spi 116, file_system.spi 1645). It lands through the lib gate right after the rename, then S1 owner-parent builds on it (EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT).")
