inl lib_iggy_client () = Task ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", "lib/spiral iggy client and typed message model for every project: one Spiral GADT family (job, lease, slot, step, health and toolchain-inventory events) with byte-identical Rust and Gleam codecs; Rust over the iggy crate (TCP 8090), Gleam over iggy HTTP (3000); lib test blocks on both backends; consumers are kit's remote executor, the compiler matrix shards, lib gates and lane watchers (IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE note 11, lessons L9-L15)", Story, P0, D5, 75u32, Planned, "IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE", "lib,iggy,remote,gleam,rust,typefeatureset,eoie-team,kit,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_iggy_client () = Planning ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_1 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 1u32, "2026-10-26T05:14Z", "eoie", "Created 10-26 after the user asked to prioritize iggy across every project and lib. Starts now: lib/spiral is outside the eoie feature freeze. Milestones, pre-registered: M1 120m the GADT message family with a round-trip test on rust and gleam (byte-identical encodings asserted against one fixture); M2 120m Rust producer and consumer against the node's iggy over the ssh -L tunnel (10,000 messages, 0 missing, ordered, like the fork's verify.ps1); M3 120m Gleam HTTP consumer with token persistence; M4 120m a job-event watcher replacing one ssh-polling watcher (L12) end to end. Rule: done when M4 replaces a real watcher and its events match the job's own receipt. Risk carried from note 7: size iggy memory_pool below the pod limit before any load test.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_2 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 2u32, "2026-10-26T06:32Z", "eoie", "02:32 eoie: M2 step 1 done. An independent Rust reference codec of the frozen M1 wire format (envelope seq u64 BE, machine string, tag u8, fields in declared order; i32 4 bytes BE; strings u32 BE length plus UTF-8) encodes all 10 of the compiler lane's per-tag fixtures byte for byte and decodes them back. It refuses truncated input, trailing bytes and an unknown tag instead of misreading them. 3/3 tests, built as a dependency-free single-file test (kit scratch clean\\iggy-m2\\src\\wire.rs, fixtures.tsv). Split per the compiler lane: it owns M1 (the lib/spiral codec, which must match these same bytes) and M3; kit owns M2 and M4. Next for M2: the producer and consumer on iggy SDK 0.11.0 (stable, published 2026-09-18 with server 0.9.0; 0.11.1 is edge only), 10,000 events round-tripped against the node's server, then the same over the ssh -L tunnel from this box.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_3 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:51Z", "eoie", "03:51 eoie: M2 round trip PASSED on the worker node. A Rust producer and consumer on iggy SDK 0.11.0 (direct producer, batches of 1,000; standalone consumer from offset 0, auto-commit off) against the node's iggy 0.9.0 at 127.0.0.1:8090, credentials read from secret iggy/iggy-root into the process env and never printed: 'M2-OK sent 10000 in 354 ms, received 10000, missing 0, duplicates 0, out_of_order 0, not_byte_identical 0, undecodable 0' (fresh topic kit-m2/events-1793001050582). Every payload is a JobStep event in the frozen M1 wire format, decoded and re-encoded byte-identical; the codec's 3 fixture tests pass on the node too. Code: kit scratch clean\\iggy-m2 (src/wire.rs, src/main.rs, node-m2.ps1). Left for M2's done rule: the same run from this box through the ssh -L tunnel (needs a local build of the SDK tree; queued for a quieter box), and switching wire.rs to the compiler lane's lib/spiral/iggy.spi codec once M1 lands, asserting the same bytes.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_4 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 4u32, "2026-10-26T07:53Z", "eoie", "03:53 eoie: M4 design (kit owns M4), written before building. Target: replace one real ssh-polling watcher (kit scratch clean\\respell\\watch-node-log.ps1, which polls a node log every 120 s over ssh and greps for DONE or STOP; lessons L12-L13: stale markers fooled it twice tonight). Shape: (1) node side, a publisher wrapping any node job: it runs the job's script, maps each Say line that is a verdict (step results, the 'notebooks done' totals, DONE or STOP) to a typed event (JobStarted at launch, JobStep with exit and detail per step, JobDone with the exit, or JobStop with the reason), and publishes to stream kit-jobs, one topic per job label, with seq monotonic per job; (2) review box side, a consumer over the ssh -L tunnel that subscribes to the topic from offset 0 and returns when it sees JobDone or JobStop for that job id. No log grep and no marker files: a stale marker cannot match because each event carries the job id and a seq. Milestones: M4a the publisher as a node-side Rust bin reusing iggy-m2's codec and producer; M4b the consumer bin on this box (local build when the box is quieter); M4c one real node proof run under the new watcher, its events checked against the job's own log (every Say verdict has exactly one event, same order). Done rule: M4c passes, and the watcher reports the job's end within 5 s of its last event (the polling watcher's latency was up to 120 s).")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_5 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 5u32, "2026-10-26T08:00Z", "eoie", "04:00 eoie: M4a and M4b work on the worker node (kit scratch clean\\iggy-m2: src/bin/publish.rs wraps a job script, echoes its output and publishes each verdict line as a typed event; src/bin/follow.rs follows one job's topic from offset 0 and exits 0 on JobDone with exit 0, 1 on a failed JobDone, 2 on JobStop, 3 on timeout). Test (node-m4.ps1): (a) a sample job run to DONE, with the follower started BEFORE the topic existed; it received JobStarted, the four verdict steps in order (regen, debug build, positive control, notebooks done) and JobDone exit 0, and reported the end 30 ms after the job ended (done rule: within 5 s; the ssh-polling watcher took up to 120 s). (b) a sample ending in STOP: the follower got the failing step and the stop reason and exited 2. First run's bug, fixed: the follower died at startup when its topic did not exist yet (exit 1, empty output); it now retries consumer init each second until the topic appears or its deadline passes, and its stderr is captured. Next: M4c, one real node proof run under the publisher with the follower as its watcher, events checked against the job's own log.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_6 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 6u32, "2026-10-26T08:15Z", "eoie", "04:15 eoie: M4 DONE by its rule. M4c ran a real node proof (the 10-notebook arity run) wrapped by the publisher with the follower as its watcher: the job log had 5 verdict lines and the follower received 5 step events with identical text, same order; JobDone arrived and the follower exited 0 138 ms after the job ended (rule: within 5 s; the ssh-polling watcher took up to 120 s). The run's notebook verdict itself is void (stale binary, IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE L21), which does not affect the event check: events matched the job's own log exactly. M4 status: publisher and follower work on the node; the review-box consumer over the ssh -L tunnel is the remaining step when this box is quieter.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_7 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 7u32, "2026-10-26T09:09Z", "eoie", "05:09 eoie: M4's last step done, with no compile on this box. The follower the node built (follow.exe, x86_64 Windows, 9.9 MB) was fetched and run here over an ssh -L tunnel to the node's iggy (kit scratch clean\\iggy-m2\\review-box-follow.ps1: it reads secret iggy/iggy-root over ssh into the process env, never printed; waits for the tunnel port; stops the ssh tunnel by its own PID in finally). Three checks: (1) the finished M4c topic m4c-arity-040401 replayed from offset 0 with all 5 step events and done exit 0 (10.8 s including ssh connect); (2) negative control: a nonexistent topic gave exit 3 after the 1 min deadline, and no tunnel was left behind; (3) live: a node job wrapped by the new generic node wrapper (clean\\iggy-m2\\node-publish-job.ps1 -Label -Script, other args passed through to the script) with this box following before the topic existed: 4 step events and done exit 0, the whole run 33 s wall, the follower ending 2.6 s after it connected. Next: every node proof run goes through node-publish-job.ps1 with review-box-follow.ps1 as its watcher, replacing watch-node-log.ps1 (L12). Left for M2's done rule: the 10,000-event run from this box, which needs a producer binary; the node builds that too and this box fetches it.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_8 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 8u32, "2026-10-26T09:12Z", "eoie", "05:12 eoie: M2's tunnel run PASSED from this box, again with no local compile (node-built iggy-m2.exe fetched; review-box-follow.ps1 now runs any fetched tool: -Tool iggy-m2 -ToolArguments 10000): 'M2-OK sent 10000 in 4523 ms, received 10000, missing 0, duplicates 0, out_of_order 0, not_byte_identical 0, undecodable 0' (topic kit-m2/events-1793005941884; 12.7 s wall with the ssh connect). Sending is 4.5 s through the tunnel against 354 ms on the node itself: each 1,000-message batch waits one round trip over ssh. For lane watchers (a few events per job) this does not matter; a bulk producer on this box should batch larger or run on the node. M2 left only on the codec swap: wire.rs becomes the compiler lane's lib/spiral/iggy.spi output when M1 lands, with the same 10 fixtures asserted.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_9 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 9u32, "2026-10-26T10:47Z", "eoie", "06:47 eoie: review of the compiler lane's M1 codec (their scratch iggy.spi; encode plus decode, round trip verified by them on the node with rustc -O). Encode matches the frozen wire format. Decode gaps against kit's reference codec (clean\\iggy-m2\\src\\wire.rs, 3 tests): (1) the default arm decodes any unknown tag (10-255) as Toolchain instead of refusing; (2) no bounds checks: truncated input panics on am'.index, and a bad length in read_str_at reads garbage; (3) trailing bytes are accepted. Asked for decode to return a result (event, or truncated at / unknown tag / trailing bytes), since stream bytes are untrusted. Their test block asserts only the Health fixture; pointed them at the 10 per-tag fixtures (clean\\iggy-m2\\fixtures.tsv) so the rust and gleam byte-identity gate covers every tag. Rule for the wire.rs swap, set now: swap when decode returns a result and all 10 fixtures pass on Rust; until then the M2 and M4 binaries keep wire.rs.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_10 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 10u32, "2026-10-26T13:13Z", "compiler", "M1 compiler-lane progress (lib/spiral/iggy.spi, scratch; lands post-5n). decode REDESIGNED to kit's wire.rs contract: returns decode_result = | Decoded event | Truncated | UnknownTag u8 | NotUtf8 | TrailingBytes i32 (NotUtf8 was missing from the first cut; Truncated is nullary not an offset). Overflow-safe bounds (need i w len = i>=0 && w>=0 && i<=len && w<=len-i). Proven GREEN on the node Cells gate (rust, real backend): encode_health_fixture (byte-exact Health), malformed_input_is_refused (Truncated on a dropped byte, TrailingBytes 1 on an appended byte, UnknownTag 42 on a bad tag, + JobDone round-trip), and codec_round_trip_2/_3 (round-trips Lease/Lease/SlotAdmitted and SlotReleased/Health/Toolchain). Remaining: codec_round_trip_1 (JobStarted/JobStep/JobStop) -- decode is sound for these by field-order review (same rd_str/rd_i32 machinery as the 7 proven tags), it only hit infra (300s cell timeout under contention, now raised to `///- --timeout 600000`; and a transient directive-adjacency slip that mis-routed it to zig, fixed). Re-running under kit's preflight3 load; will confirm all-10 green when the node is quieter. So the swap rule (decode returns a result + all 10 fixtures on Rust) is met except the last block's gate confirmation. Will ping when fully green. Also: filed codegenZig Export (the kit rename-release blocker's proper fix) on BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS note 41 with a dry-run-verified apply draft for pack 5n.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_11 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 11u32, "2026-10-26T22:23Z", "kit", "18:23 kit: progress set to 50% Active by the pre-registered milestones. Done: M2 (Rust producer and consumer round trip, 10,000 messages, 0 missing, on the node and through the review-box tunnel) and M4 (a job-event watcher replacing an ssh-polling watcher, judged done by its rule). It is in daily use: every node proof today was followed through review-box-follow.ps1. Open: M1 (the compiler lane's lib/spiral iggy.spi codec, decode result union proven green on the node, lands after pack 5n, which waits for the rename finalize) and M3 (Gleam HTTP consumer, compiler lane).")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_12 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 12u32, "2026-10-27T08:35Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-27: M1 GREEN (the swap rule is met). Ran the full iggy codec gate on THIS box -- apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 -File iggy.spi, rust backend, memo off (SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0), per-run MIX_BUILD_PATH, installed compiler 4FD712E9E357 (10-26 08:19): tests passed 5 failed 0 of 5, type errors 0. The 5 blocks cover all 10 tags: encode_health_fixture; codec_round_trip_1 (JobStarted/JobStep/JobStop -- the one unconfirmed cell, now GREEN); codec_round_trip_2 (LeaseAcquired/LeaseReleased/SlotAdmitted); codec_round_trip_3 (SlotReleased/Health/Toolchain); malformed_input_is_refused (JobDone round-trip + Truncated on a dropped byte + TrailingBytes 1 on an appended byte + UnknownTag 42). So note 9's swap rule -- decode returns a result + all 10 fixtures pass on Rust -- is MET.\n\nRan on a LOADED box, no wait for a quiet node (the user's 2026-10-27 no-quiet-machine rule): codec_round_trip_1's only prior failure was an infra timeout under node contention, never an assertion, so CPU load could only slow it, not change the result. A generous cell timeout covers the slowness; a quiet box was never needed.\n\niggy.spi is landed UNSTAGED at C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral\\iggy.spi (the user's WIP-in-repo practice), reviewable there. M1 (compiler-lane codec) is complete. REMAINING on the item: the wire.rs swap (kit's -- now unblocked), and M3 (Gleam HTTP consumer + the portable bytes->string decode that is an M1 stub in rd_str_utf8's Gleam arm, marked with a // TODO: LIB-IGGY-CLIENT in iggy.spi). Progress moved 50% -> 75% (M1+M2+M4 done of M1-M4; M3 open) -- kit, correct if your milestone weighting differs.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_13 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 13u32, "2026-10-27T09:03Z", "kit", "05:1x kit: wire.rs swap PROVEN in a throwaway probe (%TEMP%\\iggy-codec-probe). kit's Rust client keeps wire.rs's API (Body, Event, DecodeError) as a thin adapter over Spiral-generated encode/decode from lib iggy.spi; its 3 tests pass 3/3 (all 10 tags encode to the frozen bytes, every frozen string decodes back, Truncated/TrailingBytes 1/UnknownTag 42 refused), with no hand codec left. FFI: arrays cross as Rc<RefCell<Vec<u8>>>; decode exports a flat 12-field primitive tuple. Size against the 1000-line crate gate: as written 3,127 lines for a 2-export wrapper. With :~ on the codec defs, 1,602 for all 11 exports; with a :~ cat helper replacing array ++ (which inlines a copy loop per use), 1,242. Hand-split into encode (348) and decode (916) units, both under the gate. Waiting on: (1) the compiler lane registers iggy in lib/spiral/package.spiproj (now ETY-UnboundModule from a consumer) and applies the :~/cat edits for real; (2) kit-release-SLICES frees the kit tree. Then kit lands the two codec units at infra/a/iggy-client/codec (codec.spi WIP there now, marker in wire.rs) and swaps wire.rs.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_14 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 14u32, "2026-10-27T09:05Z", "kit", "05:1x kit, assessment of how far the current iggy implementation can go (written for the user's question). Payoff order: (1) replace every polling watcher with event followers (removes stale-marker false verdicts); (2) the kit job supervisor publishes typed events itself instead of a wrapper parsing printed lines; (3) one cross-machine heavy queue from slot and lease events, where a hung slot holder shows as missing heartbeats; (4) a remote executor (matrix shards and lib gates on topics, consumer groups on either box), which is the real use-both-machines goal; (5) the agile event log (EOIE-AGILE-EVENT-LOG). Ceilings: one server on the node behind an ssh tunnel (watchers go blind when sshd is starved, so job exit files stay the record of truth and events are the fast path); one ssh round trip per batch; NO VERSION FIELD on the wire, and decode refuses unknown tags, so adding a tag breaks every consumer not yet updated; client 0.11.0 against server 0.9.0. Proposed rule before consumers multiply: tags are append-only, and a consumer treats UnknownTag as skip-and-count, never fatal (follow.rs prints and continues).")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_15 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 15u32, "2026-10-27T09:34Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-27: M1 codec CLOSED (5/5 green on the size-optimized form). Re-gate of lib/spiral/iggy.spi after adopting kit's :~/cat size edits (encode 348 / decode 916 lines, under the crate gate) + registering iggy in package.spiproj + adding ///- --timeout 600000 to the 5 rust cells: tests passed 5 failed 0 of 5, type errors 0. The earlier codec_round_trip_2/_3 failures were purely the 300s default cell timeout under a loaded box (slowest_ms 365930), NOT a codec change -- raising the budget to 600000 (per the no-quiet-machine rule) passes all 5. kit re-proved the swap against the LIVE lib (`:< iggy` from a packageDir=spiral/lib package, no copy): wire.rs 3/3, both units under gate. So M1 (compiler-lane codec) is done end to end: registered lib module, 10-tag byte-identical encode/decode, size-optimized, consumer-verified. Remaining on the item: wire.rs swap (kit, lands when its tree lease frees) and M3 (Gleam HTTP consumer + portable bytes->string, the rd_str_utf8 Gleam stub, mine). Progress stays 75% (M1+M2+M4 done; M3 open).")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_16 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 16u32, "2026-10-27T09:47Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-27 (M3 consumer policy, agreeing with kit n14 + one refinement). Forward-compat rule for the Gleam HTTP consumer (M3) and any iggy consumer: tags are APPEND-ONLY (never renumber or remove a tag 0-9), and a consumer never crashes on a decode_result that isn't Decoded. iggy delivers one encoded event per message, so the consumer has message boundaries and does not need an in-band length prefix (the wire format has none) -- it skips the whole message and continues. Policy per decode_result: Decoded e -> handle e; UnknownTag t -> skip + unknown_count++ (forward-compat: a newer producer added a tag; expected, benign); Truncated / NotUtf8 / TrailingBytes -> skip + error_count++ (real corruption; non-fatal so one bad message never kills a long-lived watcher, but surfaced in metrics). So decode stays a total function returning decode_result (already is); the never-fatal handling lives in the CONSUMER (M3 Gleam, M4 watcher), not in decode. M3 (mine, build-bound) will implement this + the portable bytes->string decode that is the rd_str_utf8 Gleam stub today.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_17 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 17u32, "2026-10-27T10:42Z", "kit", "06:4x kit: the wire.rs swap LANDED (unstaged) in kit infra/a/iggy-client. codec/encode.spi and codec/decode.spi (packageDir ../../../../../spiral/lib, :< iggy from the live lib) generate src/codec_encode.rs (348 lines) and src/codec_decode.rs (916), byte-identical to the 05:3x proof. src/wire.rs is now an adapter over them (#[path] modules; Body/Event/DecodeError API unchanged; no hand codec left). Its 3 tests pass 3/3 run from the landed files (all 10 tags encode to the frozen bytes, every frozen string decodes back, the malformed refusals). Hashes: codec\\encode.spi=A788458DF3C2 codec\\decode.spi=70EBDC3B1CC3 src\\codec_encode.rs=78074A7DFF67 src\\codec_decode.rs=B69518863C58 src\\wire.rs=2708798F532B. Not yet run: a rebuild of the publish/follow/iggy-m2 binaries against the adapter (they need the iggy SDK build, last done on the node); next node build of iggy-client does it. Remaining on the item: M3 (Gleam consumer, compiler lane).")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_18 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 18u32, "2026-10-27T12:14Z", "kit", "08:1x kit: the generated codec is proven end to end on the real transport. On the node (the iggy-m2 stage project, src replaced by the landed adapter plus codec_encode/decode.rs; hand wire.rs kept as wire.rs.hand-20261027): the full client builds (release, exit 0; publish, follow and iggy-m2 rebuilt 08:05), the 3 wire tests pass, and the M2 round trip against the node's iggy gives 'M2-OK sent 10000 in 1060 ms, received 10000, missing 0, duplicates 0, out_of_order 0, not_byte_identical 0, undecodable 0' (topic kit-m2/events-1793103149794). Sending is about 3x slower than the hand codec (354 ms), likely from the Rc<RefCell<Vec<u8>>> round trips at the FFI edge; irrelevant for watcher traffic, and noted in case a bulk producer appears. kit's M2/M4 plus the swap are done; M3 (Gleam consumer) is the compiler lane's.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_19 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 19u32, "2026-10-30T23:42Z", "main", "10-30 19:4x main R3 groom (BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): owner kit. Same tag gap as IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE (eoie-team only); tag kit added 19:4x. Its last note (codec proven end to end on the node's iggy, M2 round trip OK) leaves the adapter land on the live lib as the next step.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_20 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 20u32, "2026-10-31T04:08Z", "main", "10-31 00:08 main: heal recovered 5 Rust HTTP SDK files from a node job (main 10-30 scratchpad): C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\from-node\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--home-git\\5a6e53fb-7ff8-4098-adad-000b9fa45742\\scratchpad\\iggy-sdk-http (consumer_offsets.rs, messages.rs, streams.rs, topics.rs, users.rs). They belong to kit's client work; kit decides whether they land.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_21 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 21u32, "2026-11-01T00:00Z", "kit", "10-31 20:0x kit: frozen wire bytes for every tag now live in lib iggy.spi's test blocks (the fixtures task compiler handed to kit; the duplicate infra/a/iggy-client/fixtures.tsv was archived earlier tonight, DATA-ROWS-TYPED). Before: only Health had frozen bytes (a hand-traced array whose comment cited the .tsv); all 10 tags were round-trip tested, which cannot catch an encoder and decoder that drift together. After: hex_upper (bytes -> upper-case hex, sm'.concat_list since iggy opens no sm'_operators) plus frozen_bytes_1 and frozen_bytes_2 (5 tags each, the 300 s per-cell budget split the round-trip blocks use), asserting encode against the same 10 hex strings as kit's wire.rs mod fixtures frozen(). PROOF: node job-1793490844975-kit-node-iggy-gate4, lib_program_gate on mirror kit-verify, base 526EE12F4B1E5351 (= live) -> B438384D08C9E048: \"tests: passed 2 failed 0 of 6\", type errors 0. (Gate 2 caught an unbound ++# in the first draft.) Land: land-lib-program.ps1 -Note LIB-IGGY-CLIENT/<this note> -File iggy.spi -Base 526EE12F4B1E5351 -Target B438384D08C9E048.\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):edit iggy.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -63,15 +63,43 @@ test iggy static =\n :~ encode (e : event) : array u8 =\n     cat (put_u64 e.seq) (cat (put_str e.machine) (cat ;[ body_tag e.body ] (body_bytes e.body)))\n \n-// Health{cpu=63,mem=7500,disk=84}, seq=1, machine=\"node\" -> 29 bytes (hand-traced; matches kit fixtures.tsv).\n+/// ### hex_upper  (a[0..i] as upper-case hex, prepended to acc)\n+:~ ^ hex_upper (a : array u8) (i : i32) (acc : string) : string =\n+    ? i < 0i32 ?> acc\n+    |:\n+        := b : u64 = conv (am'.index i a)\n+        := digit (n : u64) = sm'.substring (conv n : i32) 1i32 \"0123456789ABCDEF\"\n+        hex_upper a (i - 1i32) (sm'.concat_list \"\" [ digit (b >>> 4i32); digit (b &&& 15u64); acc ])\n+\n ///- --timeout 600000\n \n ///> rust\n-test encode_health_fixture =\n-    := ~ev : event = { seq = 1u64; machine = \"node\"; body = Health { cpu = 63i32; free_mem_mb = 7500i32; free_disk_gb = 84i32 } }\n-    := ~expected : array u8 =\n-        ;[ 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 1u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 4u8; 110u8; 111u8; 100u8; 101u8; 8u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 63u8; 0u8; 0u8; 29u8; 76u8; 0u8; 0u8; 0u8; 84u8 ]\n-    _assert_eq expected (encode ev)\n+test frozen_bytes_1 =\n+    := frozen (body : event_body) (expected : string) =\n+        := bytes = encode { seq = 1u64; machine = \"node\"; body }\n+        _assert_eq expected (hex_upper bytes ((conv (am'.length bytes) : i32) - 1i32) \"\")\n+    (\n+        frozen (JobStarted { job = \"j1\"; label = \"build\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F646500000000026A31000000056275696C64\",\n+        frozen (JobStep { job = \"j1\"; step = \"compile\"; exit = 0i32; detail = \"ok\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F646501000000026A3100000007636F6D70696C6500000000000000026F6B\",\n+        frozen (JobDone { job = \"j1\"; exit = 0i32 }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F646502000000026A3100000000\",\n+        frozen (JobStop { job = \"j1\"; reason = \"memory\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F646503000000026A31000000066D656D6F7279\",\n+        frozen (LeaseAcquired { tree = \"eoie\"; owner = \"compiler\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F64650400000004656F696500000008636F6D70696C6572\"\n+    )\n+\n+///- --timeout 600000\n+\n+///> rust\n+test frozen_bytes_2 =\n+    := frozen (body : event_body) (expected : string) =\n+        := bytes = encode { seq = 1u64; machine = \"node\"; body }\n+        _assert_eq expected (hex_upper bytes ((conv (am'.length bytes) : i32) - 1i32) \"\")\n+    (\n+        frozen (LeaseReleased { tree = \"eoie\"; owner = \"compiler\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F64650500000004656F696500000008636F6D70696C6572\",\n+        frozen (SlotAdmitted { slot = 1i32; owner = \"compiler\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F6465060000000100000008636F6D70696C6572\",\n+        frozen (SlotReleased { slot = 1i32; owner = \"compiler\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F6465070000000100000008636F6D70696C6572\",\n+        frozen (Health { cpu = 63i32; free_mem_mb = 7500i32; free_disk_gb = 84i32 }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F6465080000003F00001D4C00000054\",\n+        frozen (Toolchain { tool = \"perl\"; version = \"5.42.3\"; path = \"p\"; mtime = \"2026-10-26\" }) \"0000000000000001000000046E6F646509000000047065726C00000006352E34322E3300000001700000000A323032362D31302D3236\"\n+    )\n \n // --- decode: untrusted bytes -> decode_result. Big-endian raw readers + overflow-safe bounds. ------------\n \n>>> LANDED 20:03:57 on live lib: iggy.spi 526EE12F4B1E5351 -> B438384D08C9E048 (undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\LIB-IGGY-CLIENT-n21). Reader guard: the 3 readers present were fiscal's box gate g21, exempted by ancestry after tracing its deps\\spiral junction to its own scratch lib copy (g21\\lib), so live lib/spiral was not being read.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_22 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 22u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: lib/spiral/iggy.spi's tests pass on the Rust target in the lib gate (frozen_bytes_1/2, codec_round_trip_1..3, malformed_input_is_refused: 6/6, landed 11-01 00:03, node gate 2/2 for the frozen blocks) AND the Gleam arm decodes the same 10 frozen hex fixtures to equal events (M3: today the Gleam string read is a stub); kit's infra/a/iggy-client wire.rs and lib agree byte for byte (the frozen strings are the shared contract). NEXT STEP: M3 = portable bytes->string in lib for Gleam (bit_array.to_string), then a Gleam test block over the same frozen hex strings. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN (in code): event body as a closed union with one record per tag (JobStarted ... Toolchain), decode_result a union mapping Rust Result<Event, DecodeError> (Decoded | Truncated | UnknownTag of u8 | NotUtf8 | TrailingBytes of i32), rd as a union threading value+offset (no -1 offsets); next: index tags by a phantom per body kind so encode/decode tables cannot drift (one GADT body_tag kind, tag byte derived from the kind).")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_23 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 23u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 43 h ago by kit, progress kept at 75%. Resume from that note: M3 = portable bytes->string in lib for Gleam (bit_array.to_string), then a Gleam test block over the same frozen hex strings. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN (in code): event body as a closed union with one record per tag (JobStarted ... Toolchain), de")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_24 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 24u32, "2026-11-03T07:47Z", "tibia", "11-03 03:4x tibia, PROPOSAL for the event family (main's 11-03 order 6: arena runs and GPU rentals are a natural fit). tibia's two cross-machine progress streams today are ssh-polled logs: (a) batched-evolution lane runs (lane i of plan p scores s; a full-plan run is 1,789 s on lavapipe, a rented GPU will run many in parallel), (b) live arena blocks (competitor, run, experience, cleared_ms, deaths per hunt). Proposed cases, appended after tag 9 so frozen fixtures stay valid: LaneScore : { run : string; plan : string; lane : i32; score : i32 } (tag 10) and ArenaHunt : { block : string; competitor : string; run : i32; experience : i32; cleared_ms : i32; deaths : i32 } (tag 11), each with a round-trip test like the existing ten. The consumer is a follower that turns LaneScore into the C-vs-WGSL parity check (lane scores must be equal across backends) and ArenaHunt into the results/rows table, instead of ssh + log scraping. tibia will write the producer side (the WGSL runner's lane lines -> events) once the cases exist; no wire change is made by tibia.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_25 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 25u32, "2026-11-03T07:50Z", "resilience", "11-03 03:5x resilience (order-6 iggy adoption, resilience-consumer scoping): resilience's three ssh-polling monitors are candidate iggy followers, but with a prerequisite the current client lacks. MONITORS -> EVENTS: (a) node-utilization-monitor (ssh-polls node cpu/mem/jobs) -> follow Health events; (b) heartbeat-staleness-guard (reads schedules\\*.last.log mtimes) -> largely box-local, stays file-based, but node-side staleness could follow Health; (c) profile-mirror-monitor (ssh-polls newest tgz mtime on the node) -> a mirror-landing step/health event. GAP: M4's publisher (publish.rs) is PER-JOB (wraps a job, emits JobStep/JobDone); there is NO continuous node-HEALTH publisher yet, so (a)/(c) can't just follow a stream - the enabler is a node-side daemon sampling cpu/mem/jobs+mirror-age and publishing Health events (reuse kit_machine_sample + the frozen Health tag). SEQUENCE when the box frees (builds gated on TRAIN14c + kit owns the client): 1) node health publisher (Health events on a kit-health stream, one topic per machine); 2) resilience monitors become followers (review-box-follow pattern), ssh-poll stays the fail-open fallback when sshd/iggy is starved (kit n14 ceiling: events are the fast path, exit/status files the record of truth). Not urgent (the ssh-polling monitors work + caught real failures); this is the order-6 \"if it pays off, land it\" path. Asking kit (client owner): is a continuous Health publisher planned, or should resilience build it as its first iggy core-logic landing?")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_26 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 26u32, "2026-11-05T12:18Z", "x-dumps", "Cross-check (x-dumps, user double-check 2026-11-05): lib/spiral/iggy.spi reviewed - high-typefeatureset (typed event_body union 10 variants, event record, universally-quantified rd decode monad RTrunc/RUtf8, bounds-checked need/rd_*, decode_result union, backend_switch Rust/Gleam). Rust arm COMPLETE + frozen-tested (encode+decode, frozen_bytes_1/2 hex fixtures). GAP confirmed = M3: the Gleam arm of rd_str_utf8 is STUBBED (Gleam => RD empty-string) so Gleam cannot decode strings yet -> NOT full-SOTA on Gleam; Rust-SOTA done. Matches the 75% / M3-pending state. Also: this is the event CODEC; a full Spiral transport client (connect/login/poll) is still Rust-only (xarchive/events.rs), pending the Spiral port.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_27 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 27u32, "2026-11-05T13:29Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:1x x: M3 GAP DRAFTED, the Gleam arm of rd_str_utf8 (was the stub 'Gleam => RD (\\\"\\\", i + 4 + n)', so Gleam decoded every string as empty). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-IGGY-GLEAM-UTF8\\iggy.spi 92B9E9D4CFB3 on live D1636359D59A (the LIB-NO-COMMENTS land of 07:34). Gleam: rd_str_utf8_gleam slices the n bytes as Rust does, turns them into a native list (am'::to_list_base'), then into a BitArray through an Erlang external (erlang:list_to_binary, declared in a global like sm''s percent_encode_gleam), then bit_array.to_string as resultm::result' string (), so Ok -> RD and Error -> RUtf8, the same UTF-8 refusal as Rust. Rust: the arm moved unchanged into := rd_str_utf8_rust (inlined, so the generated Rust is unchanged); rd_str_utf8 is now a flat two-arm switch. TESTS: codec_round_trip_1/2/3 gain ///> gleam next to ///> rust (all 10 event bodies round-trip on both), and a new test a_string_that_is_not_utf8_is_refused on rust + gleam (machine name byte 0xFF -> NotUtf8). The frozen_bytes and malformed tests stay rust-only. Round trip canonical + fixpoint + byte-exact, 0 comment lines, europa --check exit 0 on pack48. PROOF rides x-next10 (lib_gate iggy.spi on the node, reported on its own line). Then a lib_land_window land. If Gleam's encode side has gaps of its own, that gate shows them.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_28 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 28u32, "2026-11-05T14:24Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:3x x: CORRECTION, scope of my europa --check claims today. My checks picked the compiler with 'ls compiler-installs/*/single-flight-bin | sort -V | tail -1', which returns the newest '*-src-before' dir, and those dirs are not the named packs. Measured cores: pack44-src-before ea36ca047fa29828, pack48-src-before 96df7d2a78a2469e, pack49-src-before dc49ffdc170199df (= europa's installed core). None equals the box or node pack cores (pack44 657DA4B173F9D3D3, pack48/49 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3). So where my notes say 'europa --check exit 0 on pack44' or 'on pack48', read 'on europa's older installed compiler (core shown above)'. They are type-check evidence on a recent compiler, not a proof on the land compiler. The node runs (pinned compiler, core read at launch) remain the proof, unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_iggy_client_29 () = Note ("LIB-IGGY-CLIENT", 29u32, "2026-11-05T19:46Z", "x", "2026-11-05 15:3x x: M3 GAP LANDED: lib iggy.spi D1636359D59A -> 92B9E9D4CFB3, the Gleam arm of rd_str_utf8 (bit_array.to_string over the n bytes; Error -> RUtf8, the same refusal as Rust), the Rust arm moved unchanged into a := helper, codec_round_trip_1/2/3 on rust + gleam, and the new a_string_that_is_not_utf8_is_refused on both. lib_gate iggy.spi 7/7 on the node. lib_land_window closed green (3 drafts round-trip, 2 consumer-used signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe 3/3 PASS, 0 respell drift; lib digest F0EC3B7F2A44E351; undo lib-land-undo\\20261105-152932). Proof: x-next10 lib gates on the node (job-1793894849167, pinned pack51 core E190545B5F30A7B4). So Gleam decodes event strings now (was: every string read as empty).")
inl x_defuse_links_only () = Task ("X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY", "x splitter defuses only what X would link or tag (x.json domain_pattern + tlds.txt + the two-letter rule, and the mention/hashtag/cashtag regexes), not every label.letter dot: after the '::' migration the rest is foreign text in strings, macros and doc lines (about 700 sites across all repos: main.rs, Gleam @external, C #include, PowerShell $env), and SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT makes those defusals copy-paste exact; tests in splitter.spi for a TLD dot (defused), a mention in a string (defused), a macro .unwrap (kept), and a pasted-back cell that compiles", Story, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "team:microblog,x-compat,postable", "current", "current")
