inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_1 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: round scope EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION note 32; X-compliance layers SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX notes 10-11. Classes in order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), lexer respells (keywords, ::, Cons sugar, macro sigils), macro wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP lib helpers), formatter, 280 split (EDITION3-280-SPLIT); one identical-output gate per class.")
inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-26T06:55Z", "eoie", "02:55 eoie: inventory remeasured on the working tree (the KIT-RENAME release already applied the edition-3 respell to 843 files tonight; the round's counts came from git HEAD at 01:52). Scripts: kit scratch clean\\respell\\edition3-left.ps1, keyword-sample.ps1, keyword-sample2.ps1.\n- Line-start keywords: 3,112 by the round's regex, but 2,927 of them are Rust 'let' inside multi-line host macro blocks, not Spiral and out of scope for a respell (they leave with GRANULAR-HEAL host-block migration). Of the 185 real inl/union/type lines: 85 are fixture text inside triple-quoted strings (they mimic agile state rows; leave them); about 100 are real Spiral the respell skipped: every one is a binding whose right side opens a triple-quoted string (inl kinds = triple-quote, inl emit_runtime () : () = rust_global triple-quote). A respell gap, reported on SPIRAL-FORMATTER.\n- Flow keywords: 2,662 by a rough regex, likely inflated the same way (Rust if/match in host blocks); recount with macro text excluded before planning.\n- Cons ( : 119. Raw !!!! : 767. Lines over 120: 2,332. Comment lines: 5. package.spiproj: 431, spiral.toml: 0.\nSequencing: all classes start after KIT-RENAME publishes (eoie feature freeze; the tree is under the release lease now). Order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), the ~100 respell-gap sites once the respell handles them, Cons sugar, !!!! wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP), formatter; each class through the identical-output gate (rsIntended plus the regen manifest, proven on the worker node first).")
inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:05Z", "eoie", "03:05 eoie: Cons class ready. The existing converter (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar.ps1, balanced-paren aware, rewrites Cons (a, b) as a :: b) dry-ran on a copy of the renamed and respelled tree: 113 sites in 19 files across 15 packages (kit_repo_affected 36, kit_log_sequences 21, kit_mirror 17, kit_env_pins 9, kit_do_verbs 8, ...), 0 skipped, 0 left, 0 doubled parens. Gate: list sugar is syntax for the same constructor, so every touched crate must regenerate byte-identical. Node proof script ready (clean\\respell\\node-sugar.ps1: convert on a mirror, regen the touched crates, compare every .rs hash before and after; verdict 'codegen-neutral' only at 0 changed). It runs when the node's strict notebook chain finishes (node at 100% CPU now), and the class lands right after KIT-RENAME publishes.")
inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-26T07:08Z", "eoie", "03:08 eoie: keyword class recounted with macro bodies, triple-quoted strings and plain strings stripped (kit scratch clean\\respell\\keyword-recount.ps1): line-start word keywords 106 (the respell-gap bindings, SPIRAL-FORMATTER note 85), flow keywords 9 (then 3, if 3, with 3). So eoie's real keyword work is about 115 sites, not the round inventory's 3,112 plus 3,319; the rest was Rust inside host macros and string fixtures. The class waits only on the respell handling bindings whose right side opens a triple-quoted string.")
inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_5 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-26T07:28Z", "eoie", "03:28 eoie: the Cons class's node proof caught a converter bug: 13 of 14 touched crates regenerated, but kit_crate_gate/gate.spi:44 did not type-check (Got: list string, Expected: string). 'Cons (dir </> name, acc)' had become 'dir </> name :: acc', which parses as dir </> (name :: acc) because the custom operator binds looser than ::. Fixed: the converter parenthesizes a head with any top-level infix operator, and a tail with any operator other than :: (right-associative, so chains stay bare). Test 9/9 (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar-test.ps1: the path operator, ++#, ++ in the tail, a negative literal, a comma in a string, glued member access, a pattern). Proof rerunning on the node (job kit-sugar-proof-3).")
inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_6 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-26T07:33Z", "eoie", "03:33 eoie: Cons class PROVEN codegen-neutral on the worker node. With the precedence-fixed converter (heads with a top-level infix operator and tails with an operator other than :: get parens; test 9/9), all 113 Cons ( sites in 19 files were converted on a mirror of the renamed tree, the 14 touched crates regenerated (ok), and 0 of 260 generated .rs changed. The class is ready to land right after KIT-RENAME publishes: run clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar.ps1 -Root src -Apply, then the identical-manifest check.")
inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_7 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-26T08:21Z", "eoie", "04:21 eoie: status of the two waiting classes. The compiler lane's edition-3 lexer core (9E1F72AB) built clean on the worker node at about 04:1x (single-flight Debug, 0 errors): the :: member access, the macro sigil respell (@@ and ##) and the ZWSP strip/remap all compile; behavioral probes are next on their side. When their respell pairs land (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT), eoie's '.x to ::x' and sigil classes run through the same identical-output gate as the Cons class: convert on a node mirror, regenerate the touched crates, require 0 changed generated .rs. Ready now (after KIT-RENAME lands): Cons (proven), the Global wrapper cleanup with its census probe (drafted, gate written), stop_cli and harness fixes (node proof running). Waiting: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter, main), the ~106 keyword sites (SPIRAL-FORMATTER note 85 respell gap).")
