inl note_of_kit_edition3_round_9 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-ROUND", 9u32, "2026-11-11T00:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:4x rig groom: its three deps are Done, so it surfaces as ready, but its first and largest part (member access .x -> ::x over kit/src) IS KIT-EDITION3-RESPELL, which runs in its own train after TRAIN44 and shows the user a sample first (user 11-07 mass-respell rule). The rest of the round (spiral.toml for the package.spiproj files, word keywords, Cons -> :: sugar, macro sigils, raw !!!! -> lib wrappers, formatter widths) must be measured on the respelled tree, not the current one, or every count and byte-identity gate moves under it. NEXT STEP: after the respell lands, re-count each class on the respelled tree and slice the round per class (one review per class, rsIntended gate per crate). Wait set to item:KIT-EDITION3-RESPELL.")
