inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_1 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T12:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:35 fiscal: STEP 1 IN THE TREE, unstaged (lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi EDE98016): a NAMED facet-free restriction of a named type that this module emits now ALIASES its parent instead of becoming '= string' (the review's TServ restricts the pattern-checked TString and lost the pattern, nfe_v3_10:734; 53 such aliases in generated_cte_v4_00). Done at module assembly, not in emit_named_type, so inline anonymous restrictions are untouched: simple_aliases (named, no enumeration, not constrained, non-builtin base, parent emitted here), inherited_kinds (an alias takes its parent's kind through chains, bounded at 64 against cycles), aliased_items (the item's text becomes 'type ty = parent' with ty_example/ty_example_text delegating, plus ty_of_string/ty_to_string delegating when the resolved kind is enum or validated, so readers call the parent's validator and writers use the parent's to_text instance: no second instance). Test a_facet_free_restriction_aliases_its_parent. Type-checked: xsd_emit + probe + json_schema 0 errors; formatter no-op. Remaining steps of this item: builtins to real types (decimal.decimal, i64, bool, date nominals), totalDigits/fractionDigits/min/max facets validated, dead 'true &&' conjuncts. Proof: full regeneration + every unit compiled, queued on a reused node mirror after cj-proof (node disk is tight).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_2 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 2u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. This item's a_facet_free_restriction_aliases_its_parent passes (step 1 proven at the emitter level; units and samples follow in the same run).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_3 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 3u32, "2026-10-27T18:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:31 fiscal: constraint for 'builtins as real types': xs:integer is UNBOUNDED; real signed documents carry 39-digit X509SerialNumber (MyInvois samples), which .NET's decimal-backed validator rejects. Today our readers keep unrestricted builtins as text, so they are correct; a numeric type for xs:integer must be arbitrary precision (or stay text), never i64/decimal.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_4 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 4u32, "2026-10-30T15:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:37 fiscal: GROOM R3 (2.9 d): Active -> Paused, progress kept (step 1, facet-free aliases, proven 10-27; the xs:integer constraint of 10-27 14:31 stands: arbitrary precision or text, never i64/decimal). The remaining steps change lib xsd_emit's output. The edition-3 round's gate compares generated units from two trees on ONE lib (p7cl vs e3lv, 74 units), so emitter changes wait until that round closes. Dep FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND; resume when it lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_5 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 5u32, "2026-10-31T21:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 17:09 fiscal: RE-DECIDED: stays Paused. REASON (still true today): its remaining steps change xsd_emit/generator output, and FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (95%, held behind EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL, 95%, compiler pack 9) will respell that text; writing against the pre-respell tree would stale every anchor (rule anchors-stale-across-respell). RESUME CONDITION: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND reaches Done (the dep is recorded), then resume as Planned and re-anchor on the respelled tree.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_6 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 6u32, "2026-11-01T12:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:38 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P0 (Paused on FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, in deps): generated fields typed as string where the XSD says decimal/integer/boolean/date are the main remaining \"stringly\" output of the lane.\nDONE WHEN: (a) a node gate of xsd_emit.spi with 0 failed, including new tests builtins_become_carrier_types (xs:decimal -> decimal.decimal, xs:integer family -> i64 with range, xs:boolean -> bool, xs:date -> date nominal) and facets_build_only_through_validators; (b) regenerated generated_nfe_v4: every xs:decimal-based field (e.g. TDec_1302 values) has a decimal carrier, and its round-trip tests stay green; (c) model_metrics.ps1 over lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi: M7 string dispatch below 40 per 1k lines (81 in model-metrics-lib-20261031.tsv); (d) 0 generated drift other than the intended type changes, reviewed per family.\nNEXT STEP: after the e3 round lands, draft on a scratch lib: replace builtin_example / prefers_builtin_example / is_calendar_builtin (xsd_emit.spi :836-851, string compares on xml.local_name) with one classification function returning the GADT below; move positive_example (:853, added 11-01) onto it.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a GADT indexed by the Spiral carrier type: \":| ^ builtin carrier = | DecimalBuiltin :: builtin decimal | IntegerBuiltin :: { min : option i64; max : option i64 } -> builtin i64 | BoolBuiltin :: builtin bool | DateBuiltin :: builtin date | TextBuiltin :: builtin string\". classify (reference) : exists carrier. builtin carrier (an existential) is the ONLY place a builtin's local name is read. Example values, readers (of_text) and writers (to_text) are prototype instances over the carrier (\":+ example_of builtin\", \":+ parse_of builtin\"), so adding a builtin is a GADT case plus instances, never another string branch. Facets wrap a carrier in a validated nominal built only by its smart constructor (of_string : string -> option t); raw strings where a validated value is expected stay a type error (the item FISCAL-APP lists as a known limit). No -1 or \"\" sentinels: bounds are option i64. MODEL: xsd.spi''s GADT \"xsd sort form\" (:48-80); the mega sample mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel for indexed families.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_7 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 7u32, "2026-11-02T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 17:20 fiscal: RE-DECIDED (stop-gate groom): Paused -> Planned. The recorded resume condition is MET: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND is Done since 11-01 14:4x (CI run 41314140694, both OSes), and lib xsd_emit.spi is in edition 3, so new work anchors on the respelled tree. ORDER (from the specs): XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES first (it is the base of XSD-FACET-TYPES' parse/example instances and XSD-DECODE-RESULT's of_xml returning result), then XSD-DECODE-RESULT, then XSD-FACET-TYPES. Each changes every generated unit, so each lands with one full node regen; the first starts after the 90-file shared-runtime regen and the typed family-roots regen are placed in fiscal/generated, so drifts don't compound.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_8 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T12:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:07 fiscal: NEXT STEP (n? spec) DRAFTED, output-neutral, inside the GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT draft (drafts\\spiral\\GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi, layered on the decode draft): builtin_example / is_calendar_builtin / prefers_builtin_example / positive_example no longer string-compare xml::local_name in four places; one classifier builtin_kind_of returns ':| builtin_kind = Base64Builtin | UriBuiltin | IdBuiltin | DateTimeBuiltin | DateBuiltin | BooleanBuiltin | PositiveIntegerBuiltin | OtherBuiltin', and the four functions match on it (semantics kept exactly: builtin_example classifies by local name alone, the calendar/positive checks keep their is_builtin_reference guards; is_positive_integer_builtin is shared). europa pack27: --check exit 0, format clean; output-identity run queued with the split steps. The carrier-indexed GADT (':| builtin carrier = DecimalBuiltin :: builtin decimal | ...') is the type-changing step that follows XSD-DECODE-RESULT's land, per the ORDER (codec -> decode -> facet types).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_9 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 9u32, "2026-11-05T04:34Z", "fiscal", "DESIGN DECISION (grounded), 11-05 00:5x local: builtin carriers must keep their lexical text. Corpus facts (fiscal deps/corpus, 319 xml, all 6846 cbc *Amount/*Quantity/*Percent/*Rate/*Numeric values): 4478 (65%) end in a trailing zero after the point (100.00); 8 have leading zeros (ZATCA zero tax 00.00 / 00.0, in 5 documents); 1 has a trailing space (UBL-TR TicariFaturaOrnegi 786.90 ); 1 is not a number (LHDN my/samples/1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency-Sample.xml PayableAmount = abc); 0 plus signs. Lib decimal.parse NORMALIZES (+007.500 prints back as 7.5, 2.50 as 2.5), so a plain decimal.decimal field would break 65% of real-document read-backs, and a scale-keeping decimal would still break ZATCA and TR. DECISION: one generic carrier \":== lexical t = { value : t; text : string }\" (value = typed, validated, used for arithmetic; text = the raw lexical form the writer prints). Built from a value through a canonical printer (decimal.text, i64 / bool printers), and read through parse-or-Invalid, so the decode result carries Invalid (path, text) for abc. Fields: xs:decimal -> lexical decimal.decimal; integer family -> lexical i64 (range facets checked); xs:boolean -> lexical bool (1/0/true/false all parse; text keeps the spelling); date/dateTime stay text until a date nominal exists. This updates DoD (a)/(b): \"every builtin-typed field has a lexical carrier, and its round-trip tests stay green\". Expected intended drift: LHDN 1.1 ForeignCurrency becomes a decode failure (a true sample defect), to be recorded as that family's known_defect, not hidden. Draft order: a new lib draft layered on GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT (AB4B0165) plus xml_codec readers; proof after XSD-DECODE-RESULT lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_10 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 10u32, "2026-11-05T04:54Z", "fiscal", "DRAFTED + emitter-PROVEN, 11-05 01:0x local: drafts\\spiral\\XSD-FACET-TYPES\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi 4E831159 (formatter output), base xsd_emit.base-AB4B0165 = the GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT draft, layered on the decode draft. 220 changed lines. Design (n9) implemented through the EXISTING codec path, not a new kind: builtin decimal/integer-family/boolean references map to carrier aliases with kind KindValidated, so reader (read_value <t>_of_string), writer (text_node / to_text), attributes (attribute_parsed), simpleContent base (parsed_text / to_text x.base), examples (<t>_example) and fixed values (required_value) all work unchanged. Pieces: builtin_kind gains DecimalBuiltin / IntegerBuiltin (integer long int short byte) / NonNegativeIntegerBuiltin (nonNegativeInteger unsignedInt/Short/Byte; unsignedLong stays text because it overflows i64); builtin_kind_of is now one data table plus a lookup instead of a 9-arm string chain (M7 -9); a carriers () data table {kind; name; value_type; parse; example} is the single source for kind_carrier and the prelude; carrier_prelude body emits \"nominal lexical t = { value : t; text : string }\", \"instance to_text lexical t = fun x => x.text\", lexical_of, whole_of / whole_at_least / boolean_of, and per USED carrier \"type xsd_decimal = lexical decimal.decimal\" plus _of_string / _example / _example_text, in main units and in the family core (versions open the core). Text-only units get NO carrier text. PROOF europa pack27, base-decode (xml_codec 5694B36A): --check module + bodies exit 0; negative control (reference_type returns 1i32) gives ETY-TermError exit 5. New tests builtins_become_lexical_carriers and text_only_schemas_declare_no_carrier run in Rust: run exit 0. Mutant (\"decimal\" mapped to OtherBuiltin) FAILS with \"xs:decimal is carried as xsd_decimal\". Round trip canonical/fixpoint true (pre-format 7003D2B1; formatted copy recheck pending). NEXT: generated-unit --check probe (queued on europa, load-gated; europa at load 11-38 from main's file_system gate and k3s), then a full regen diff vs gen-decode2 plus node gates after the decode land.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_11 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 11u32, "2026-11-05T05:06Z", "fiscal", "GENERATED-CODE PROVEN, 11-05 01:1x local, europa pack27 over base-decode. (1) The facet emitter 4E831159, compiled to Rust, wrote a unit for a probe schema (decimal / positiveInteger / repeated nonNegativeInteger / optional boolean elements, a required xs:int attribute, an optional xs:decimal attribute, a simpleContent xs:decimal base). It shows fields total : xsd_decimal, count : list (xsd_non_negative_integer), paid : option (xsd_boolean), seq : xsd_integer, base : xsd_decimal, readers read_value <carrier>_of_string, and attribute_parsed xsd_integer_of_string. The unit --check passes with exit 0 and 0 diagnostics. Controls: d.unitz inside whole_of gives ETY-RecordIndexFailed (23:52) and x.textz inside the to_text lexical instance gives ETY-RecordIndexFailed (16:39), so the prelude bodies are really checked. (2) BEHAVIOUR in native Rust, 14 checks on the corpus forms all pass: ZATCA 00.00 parses with value 0 and prints back 00.00; UBL 100.00 prints back 100.00; UBL-TR \"786.90 \" prints back with its trailing space; LHDN abc does not parse; integer 1.0 does not parse; positive 0 does not parse; non-negative 0 parses and -1 does not; boolean 1 prints back 1; boolean 0 and \" false \" read as false; boolean yes does not parse. Mutant (positive accepts 0) FAILS with \"positive 0 parses but must not\". Round trip of the formatted 4E831159: canonical/fixpoint true. PENDING (europa, load-gated): full regen with the facet emitter in its own tree facet-gen, diffed unit by unit against dec-gen (same generator, decode lib), plus --check of every changed unit (log facet-regen-1793855140.log).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_12 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 12u32, "2026-11-05T05:17Z", "fiscal", "FULL REGEN with the facet emitter, 11-05 01:1x local, europa pack27, own tree facet-gen (dec-gen's generator DA6BE426 + decode lib, with xsd_emit replaced by 4E831159; log facet-regen-1793855140.log): compile 21 s, rustc 196 s, run \"exit 36\" = main's return value, write_family_modules counting 36 families (69 units), not an error. Against dec-gen (same generator, pre-facet emitter): 49 units BYTE-IDENTICAL (every NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e/GTV-e/event/CFDI/KSeF/UBL-applicationresponse etc.: no direct numeric or boolean builtins), 20 CHANGED, 0 missing. Each changed unit gets only the carriers it uses: cii_d16b decimal+boolean; cl_dte / cl_envio decimal+integer+positive; the 9 CR hacienda units integer only (42 lines each); es_facturae and es_verifactu integer; fatturapa integer; gr_mydata decimal+integer+boolean (336 lines); hu_nav boolean; pt_saft non_negative_integer (232 lines); ubl_invoice / ubl_creditnote decimal+integer+boolean (132 lines). All 20 changed units --check exit 0 with 0 diagnostics. LEFT for the DoD: (b) node Cells gates of the 20 changed units after the decode land, where real-document read-backs exercise the lexical round trip, with the LHDN abc sample expected to report Invalid and become ubl_invoice's recorded defect; (c) model_metrics M7 on xsd_emit; (d) per-family drift review (the 20 above).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_13 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 13u32, "2026-11-05T05:23Z", "fiscal", "DoD (c) MET, 11-05 01:2x local, spiral apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 on the code lines (tests excluded): xsd_emit M7 string dispatch 6.3 /kl on the split base AB4B0165 (3498 lines, 423 defs) -> 4.2 /kl on the facet draft 4E831159 (3612 lines, 437 defs); M8 sentinels 0 -> 0. The DoD asked for below 40 (it was 81 on 10-31). The drop comes from builtin_kind_of becoming a data table plus a lookup. Status: (a) emitter tests proven in Rust; (b) PENDING the node Cells gates of the 20 changed units after the decode land; (c) met; (d) the drift list is in n12.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_14 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 14u32, "2026-11-05T06:06Z", "fiscal", "FACET LAND COMPANIONS DRAFTED + PROVEN, 11-05 02:0x local (drafts\\spiral\\XSD-FACET-TYPES\\fiscal\\src). The facet types make one official sample fail by design (LHDN my/samples/1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency-Sample.xml, PayableAmount abc), so per-document defects are now MODELED, not hidden. families.spi 8472AD8B (base F1CF3DDF): \":| family_extra\" gains \"DocumentDefect : string * string\" (path, expected message) and document_defects extras, so the other 20 family literals are untouched; ubl_invoice_2_1 extras = [ DocumentDefect (\"deps/corpus/my/samples/1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency-Sample.xml\", \"PayableAmount: abc\") ]. The message text comes from xml_codec error_text (\"invalid <path>: <text>\"). generator.spi CE32E90E (base .next7 D6F663A7): document_checks drops recorded defects from the read-back list at generation time and emits defect_check, which asserts each one FAILS and that its first failure contains the expected text (\"a recorded defect now reads back\" / \"fails differently: ...\"). New test a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back. PROOF europa pack27, lib = sentinel D00BE390: generator --check + bodies exit 0 (the package includes the families draft); the defect test and ubl_json_documents_read_through_the_transcoder run in Rust with exit 0 (FISCAL_ROOT set for the binary; run-rust.sh sets it only for the compile). MUTANT (the DocumentDefect removed from ubl_invoice) FAILS \"a recorded defect leaves the read-back list\". LAND ORDER: decode -> split -> (.next6 + families F1CF3DDF) -> facet lib 4E831159 + sentinel lib D00BE390 + this families 8472AD8B + generator CE32E90E in ONE window.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_15 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 15u32, "2026-11-05T06:15Z", "fiscal", "Validity note on n12's regen (11-05 02:1x local): the facet-gen scratch tree copied dec-gen's absolute lib symlink, so its deps write went THROUGH to dec-gen/lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi (memory scratch-tree-copies-keep-symlinks). The n12 verdict STANDS: the generator compile used facet-gen's real lib copy (4E831159), the 20 unit checks resolved the same facet xsd_emit through the link, and the dec-gen baseline units it was diffed against were generated at 11-04 21:27Z, before any of this. dec-gen is restored to the decode 5B274B48 and checked by hash.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_16 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 16u32, "2026-11-05T12:08Z", "fiscal", "FACET COMPANIONS REBASED onto live fiscal src (after the 08:0x generator/families land), 11-05 08:1x local: drafts\\spiral\\XSD-FACET-TYPES\\fiscal\\src2\\ families.spi 889D2546 (base 99A8339B: DocumentDefect + document_defects, ubl_invoice_2_1 extras record the LHDN 1.1 ForeignCurrency sample) and generator.spi 96302219 (base 40DE71DF: write_certificates_unit takes option string; document_checks drops recorded defects through documents_of plus kept_documents, then emits defect_check; new test a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back). The src\\ drafts (on .next7 / F1CF3DDF) are superseded. PROOF europa pack27 over the sentinel lib D00BE390 (facet + sentinel): generator --check + bodies exit 0; the defect and transcoder tests run in Rust with exit 0; MUTANT (DocumentDefect removed) FAILS 'a recorded defect leaves the read-back list'; reference 5B274B48 held. GRANULAR (europa counter): families 4 code defs over, generator 0 of 98. THE FACET WINDOW is then: lib xsd_emit D00BE390 (facet 4E831159 + sentinel, on live AB4B0165) + fiscal families 889D2546 + generator 96302219 + the 20 changed units. PENDING before it: DoD (b), node Cells gates of the 20 changed units.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_17 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 17u32, "2026-11-05T12:14Z", "fiscal", "DoD (b) STARTED, 11-05 08:2x local: node job-1793880841250-fiscal-facet-gate (cap 36000000 ms from start; script node-facet-gate.ps1 6D57D24F; inputs hash-verified). It builds a scratch tree: core; the mirror lib with xml B6EED09B, xml_codec 5694B36A and the sentinel xsd_emit D00BE390 (facet + sentinel); live fiscal src with the rebased companions families 889D2546 / generator 96302219 and the harness main; the corpus as a read-only junction. It regenerates every unit, then Cells-gates (lib_gate, pinned compiler) each unit that declares \"nominal lexical t\" (the carrier units, about 20), with caps raised x3 IN THE SCRATCH TREE ONLY, so a kill leaves no shared-mirror state. Guards: corpus file count and mirror xsd_emit hash compared start vs end; junctions removed as links before any delete. Expected intended drift: ubl_invoice's real-document test now asserts the LHDN abc sample as a recorded defect. PENDING.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_18 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 18u32, "2026-11-05T15:40Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:4x local fiscal: FACET-WINDOW COMPANION TESTS BODY-PROVEN on EUROPA, ahead of the land (the node facet gate covers the generated units, not these src tests). Stage = box core + box lib with the sentinel xsd_emit D00BE390 + live fiscal src with src2 families 8F72669F and generator 6ADC38CB over it; pinned europa compiler core dc49ffdc170199df. eff-fam1793893052: families' 2 bodies (every_family_has_its_own_module_name, every_regime_lists_its_own_families) compile, rustc, run exit 0. eff-gen1793893052: generator a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back compile, rustc, run exit 0. Neither compile printed ParserErrors, so no test block was silently dropped. MUTANT eff-genm1793893148 (the recorded defect's message 'PayableAmount: abc' -> 'xyz' in families): run exit 1 with exactly 'the LHDN sample must fail with its recorded message'. Window pre-checks also done (bases AB4B0165 / E6AC72B3 / 03111A90 live, drafts at their recorded hashes). Waiting only on the node facet gate (15/20 green at 11:29) and the regen-and-zip job.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_19 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 19u32, "2026-11-05T15:43Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:4x local fiscal (follow-up): the other LIGHT src2 generator tests are body-proven on europa too, same facet stage (sentinel lib D00BE390, src2 generator 6ADC38CB, families 8F72669F, plus the it/fatturapa, pl/ksef and DFe.NET tiposBasico schemas they read): eff-gl1793893349 generates_the_uf_code_union, ubl_json_documents_read_through_the_transcoder, unqualified_schemas_prefix_the_example_root -- compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors. With a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back that is 4 of the generator's 25 tests; the other 21 regenerate whole families (write_family_modules / generates_*) and are covered by the node regen + facet unit gates, not repeated on the 2-CPU europa.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_20 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 20u32, "2026-11-05T16:20Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:2x local fiscal: the queued regen-and-zip job (job-1793883003188, not started yet) now FORMATS the regenerated units before zipping (script D4120E4D runs fiscal scripts/format-generated.ps1 0C8D80B8 -Jobs 4 with the node's pinned compiler, core 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3 like the box), because the live generated/ units are committed formatted: an unformatted zip would show every unit as changed. Placement prepared: scratch facet-place-units.ps1 (dry run lists changed / unchanged / new / missing units against fiscal/generated; -Apply backs up each replaced unit, then places). Expected after the window: the 20 carrier units changed, the other 62 byte-identical.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_21 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 21u32, "2026-11-05T16:23Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:2x local fiscal: GAP FOUND AND CLOSED before the window. The facet harness main (used by the identity regens and the facet gate's own regen) named only 13 families + family_roots / hacienda_documents / nfe_events, so 9 families never regenerated under the facet emitter: nfe_v4_00, cfdi_tfd_1_1, cfdi_pagos_2_0, cfdi_v4_0, ksef_fa_3 and ubl_business_documents_2_1 (DebitNote, ApplicationResponse, DespatchAdvice, ReceiptAdvice; 0 carriers in their live units today, decimals that a facet emitter would carry). Landing the window without them would leave those units on the pre-facet generator and CI's regen drift check (scripts/build.ps1: 'generated: N files differ from the committed copy') would go red. FIX in the still-queued regen job-1793883003188: harness-main.spi 491D7AB1 now writes every family the generator tests write (CFDI in the test's order tfd, pagos, cfdi), and node-facet-regen.ps1 4403B67A, after formatting and zipping, GATES every carrier unit that is not among the facet gate's 20 (same x3 scratch cap), so the window's unit set is proven complete before it lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_22 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 22u32, "2026-11-05T19:00Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:0x local fiscal: NODE CONTENTION, status of the last facet unit: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's gate started 12:49; its rustc (pid 21888, started 12:55) is still compiling at 15:00 with 4,699 CPU-seconds, i.e. about 40% of a core, because the node runs at 100% with another lane's dotnet / erl jobs started 14:58 (not mine, not touched). Its scratch cell cap is 5 h (to about 17:49) and the gate job's own cap 10 h (to about 18:20). PROJECTION: invoice verdict in about an hour, then the regen (compile + rustc + run + format 82 + gates of the 9 newly included families' carrier units) another 3-4 h under this load, so the window can land around 20:00 at best; the src Cells confirmation and the MyInvois twin job queued after it will most likely still be pending at 21:00 (both already body-proven on europa). If the invoice gate hits its cap the verdict is VOID, not red, and the unit is re-gated alone.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_23 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 23u32, "2026-11-05T19:24Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:2x local fiscal: FACET GATE GREEN on the NODE, job-1793880841250 (t1101 scratch tree: base lib + decode xml / xml_codec + the sentinel xsd_emit D00BE390 + src2 families 8F72669F / generator 6ADC38CB + harness; pinned compiler copy): all 20 carrier units passed -- cii_d16b, cl_dte_v10, cl_envio_dte_v10, the 9 Costa Rica 4.4 units, es_facturae_3_2_2, es_verifactu, fatturapa_1_2_3, gr_mydata_2_0_2, hu_nav_3_0, pt_saft_1_04_01 (2/2 each), ubl_creditnote_2_1 and ubl_invoice_2_1 (1/1 each: their single writes_its_example test carries every document read-back; invoice finished 15:22 after a contended 2.5 h rustc). Corpus 1290 files start and end, mirror xsd_emit 738935CD unchanged, tree dropped. NEXT on the node, now running: the regen-and-zip job-1793883003188 (full harness, format pass, gates of the newly included families' carrier units); the window lands once that is green.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_24 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 24u32, "2026-11-05T20:04Z", "fiscal", "11-05 16:0x local fiscal: REGEN DONE on the NODE (job-1793883003188, exit 0): compile 38 s, rustc 1495 s, run 449 s, 45 families -> 83 units (the full harness; the unit set equals fiscal/generated exactly), zip C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fiscal-facet-regen-units.zip 6DD036E2 (4781 KB), corpus 1290 start / end, mirror untouched. TWO CORRECTIONS to my 12:2x notes: (a) the job runs C:\\home\\remote-stage\\node-facet-regen.ps1 (its argv), not the copy I patched in fiscal-facet-in, so the format pass and the extra gates did NOT run; only the full harness (read from the inputs folder) took effect. (b) The facet gate and this regen used the node's input copies generator 96302219 / families 889D2546; formatted with the box compiler they are byte-identical to src2 6ADC38CB / 8F72669F, so the gated code IS the window's code. CARRIER UNITS in the zip: 25; the 20 already green plus 5 never gated: generated_ksef_fa_3 (815 KB) and the four UBL business units applicationresponse / debitnote / despatchadvice / receiptadvice (about 3.6 MB each, the invoice unit's size class, whose rustc peaked at 6.4 GB). NF-e and the CFDI trio gained no carriers. DECISION: the window does NOT land today. Landing 78 proven units with 5 unproven would leave those 5 on the old emitter and turn CI's generated-drift check red, and the 4 big units cannot run on europa (3.3 GB) or the box (3.7 GB free) and take 1-2.5 h each on the contended node. QUEUED: node job-1793908968483-fiscal-facet-extra (script 2F5DA04A, after the MyInvois twin job, 12 h cap): the same scratch tree as the facet gate, all 83 regenerated units unpacked from the zip, the 5 gated (x3 scratch cap). It will run overnight; the window (lib xsd_emit D00BE390 on base AB4B0165 + src2 families / generator + the 25 formatted units) follows its verdict.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_25 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 25u32, "2026-11-05T23:38Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:3x local fiscal: FACET WINDOW LANDED, unstaged. Gate: node job-1793908968483-fiscal-facet-extra finished exit 0, all 5 remaining carrier units green in Cells (ksef_fa_3 2/2, ubl applicationresponse / debitnote / despatchadvice / receiptadvice 1/1 each; guards: corpus 1290 files and mirror xsd_emit 738935CD unchanged start to end), on top of the earlier facet gate's units. Pre-land consumer check (lesson from main's json_schema red): json_schema F7564185, the only lib caller of xsd_emit, ran 8/8 bodies green on europa against the draft. (1) lib: lib_land_window label fiscal-facet-1105, xsd_emit.spi AB4B0165 -> D00BE390 (facet + sentinel): signatures unchanged, apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (36 tests typed), 0 respell drift, lib digest D63B5E3ED272FCFB, undo 20261105-193122. (2) fiscal src: families E6AC72B3 -> 8F72669F and generator 03111A90 -> 6ADC38CB (the src2 companions; format-only over the 889D2546 / 96302219 text the node gated); package --check exit 0. Backups families/generator.before-facet-* in the session scratchpad. (3) generated/: 25 of 83 units replaced by the pin-a688-formatted regen (58 byte-identical); re-run dry run: 0 changed. Backup generated.before-facet-20261105-193742 in the session scratchpad. PENDING: a box regen identity check with the live generator, and CI at the user's next push.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_26 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 26u32, "2026-11-06T00:28Z", "fiscal", "11-05 20:2x local fiscal: REGEN IDENTITY PROVEN on the box (scratch trees, pinned compiler a688, today's live box lib with xsd_emit D00BE390, full box corpus, 1292 files unchanged start to end): the whole-family regen harness run with the generator the node gated (96302219 + families 889D2546) and with the live formatted pair (6ADC38CB + 8F72669F) wrote the same 83 units: 166 files each, 0 differing, 0 on one side only (each run exit 45 = family count). So the format pass that produced the live companions changed no generated text. Remaining for this item: CI at the user's next push.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_27 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 27u32, "2026-11-06T10:15Z", "fiscal", "Groom 06:15: facet window landed 11-05 (xsd_emit D00BE390) with green node gates and box regen identity; the remaining 35% is not named in any note. Next step (CPU-light): list which of totalDigits/fractionDigits/min/max are validated in the generated readers, then split the unvalidated facets into their own item and close this one.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_28 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 28u32, "2026-11-06T12:53Z", "fiscal", "09:0x REMAINDER NAMED (replaces 'the remaining 35% is not named'): delivered = builtins as real types + facet-free restrictions aliasing their parent + Length/MinLength/MaxLength/Pattern/Enumeration/WhiteSpace enforced (facet window 11-05, xsd_emit D00BE390). Missing = totalDigits/fractionDigits enforcement (XSD-FACET-DIGITS) and the four bound facets, which lib xsd does not even read (XSD-FACET-BOUNDS). DoD: both children Done.")
