inl note_of_xsd_typed_rules_1 () = Note ("XSD-TYPED-RULES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:06 fiscal: GROOM (pre-merge inventory): this item had no notes. STATE: Planned, not started; its title is the spec. GATE: it changes xsd_emit/generator output, so it waits for FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND to land (the same reason as the Paused XSD-FACET-TYPES / XSD-DECODE-RESULT / XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES), then one regeneration per change. NEXT: write a design note against the edition-3 emitter before any code.")
inl note_of_xsd_typed_rules_2 () = Note ("XSD-TYPED-RULES", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:51 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). DONE WHEN: the EN 16931 UBL rules (104 rules, 981 asserts, validation-1.3.17) compile to typed predicates over the generated UBL Invoice type, and on the 5 CEN examples plus the mutated invoices of corpus_checks cen_rules_catch_mutated_invoices their verdicts equal the schematron engine's (0 disagreements), with the count of rules not yet compilable reported per reason. NEXT STEP: after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS, pick the 10 simplest BR-* rules (single-path existence/equality) and compile them through the field descriptors; diff the verdicts with schematron_run on the CEN examples. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: \":| ^ rule doc = | Rule :: { id : rule_id; flag : rule_flag; check : doc -> verdict } -> rule doc\" indexed by the generated document type, so a UBL rule cannot be applied to a CII document; \":! rule_id = string\" from the rule's id attribute; \":| verdict = | Holds | Fails : list decode_path\"; \":| rule_flag = | Fatal | Warning\". XPath text is parsed once at generation time (lib xpath) into the predicate; no XPath strings are evaluated at run time. key/unique constraints become the same rule type.")
