inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source: cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts; mirror thegreenter/ubl-validator@980bad9412eab51516e4879b06d8d2e723c62f0d src/xsd/2.1/ (header says UBL 2.1 CS1: diff against fiscal's OASIS os copy first). Rules are XSL; official XSL UNVERIFIED.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 2u32, "2026-10-27T19:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:01 fiscal: sourcing: UBL 2.1 mandatory since 2019-03-01 (RS 164-2018). Official per-document XML guides are PDFs under cpe.sunat.gob.pe/sites/default/files/inline-files/ (factura, boleta, nota de debito). The portal pages answer scripted requests with 403 (bot protection), so the XSD set, the samples and the SFS validation XSLT (SUNAT's rules) are not reachable from init. NEEDS: a browser download of SUNAT's XSD + SFS package once, then init pins it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 3u32, "2026-10-27T23:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:36 fiscal: sourcing: cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts. greenter's parser fixtures are UBL 2.0 / customization 1.0 (pre-2018 format; one looks like a real retail receipt): rejected. Most code-search hits carry real RUCs: skipped. Chosen: project-openubl/xhandler-java (Apache-2.0) @9b0af749 xbuilder e2e/homologacion: 58 SUNAT homologation cases (28 Invoice, 15 CreditNote, 15 DebitNote; UBL 2.1, customization 2.0; test RUC 12345678912), unsigned. Their ONLY schema fault is the empty signing slot (ExtensionContent): 58/58 valid without it. init drops that slot (throws if any ExtensionContent has content), like GST's nulls; no signature is faked.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 4u32, "2026-10-27T23:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:37 fiscal: IN THE TREE: init block deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion (58 pinned files). Manifests: invoice 127 -> 155, creditnote 6 -> 21, debitnote 3 -> 18; all 58 schema-valid (validate-manifests); no BOM; set-proof stage includes them. Open: SUNAT's own rule XSLs (official site 403s scripts).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 5u32, "2026-10-28T08:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 04:16 fiscal: RUNTIME: its real UBL documents are among the 155 invoices that read back unchanged through the generated UBL Invoice reader/writer on the node (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357, generator with the count-type fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 6u32, "2026-10-28T10:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: BLOCKED on user download: SUNAT's current validation XSL package (ValidaExprReg*.xsl etc. from cpe.sunat.gob.pe, which answers 403 to scripts). Documents are done: 58 homologation cases round-trip on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 7u32, "2026-10-30T14:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:18 fiscal: GROOM: stays agent (mixed blockers, so not R1). (a) Your download of SUNAT's validation XSL package (cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts; Chrome extension not connected 10-30), and (b) XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS, whose end-to-end evidence is fiscal-p7-set-ublj2 (running 10-30, on generated_ubl_invoice_2_1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 8u32, "2026-10-31T13:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 09:36 fiscal: GROOM R1 -> user-batch. Blocker (b) is gone: XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS closed 10-30 (namespace claim re-proven on the live lib; see FISCAL-SA-ZATCA's groom note). The only open step is (a), yours: download SUNAT's current validation XSL package (ValidaExprReg*.xsl etc.) from cpe.sunat.gob.pe, which answers 403 to scripts, into fiscal/deps/corpus/pe/sunat/ (the 58 homologation documents already round-trip). Then the agent wires it like the other rule-set profiles (DIAN/ZATCA/RO pattern, CPU-light + one box gate). Assignee agent -> user, tag user-batch added.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 9u32, "2026-10-31T22:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 18:10 fiscal: the download gate is lifted (user 10-31 ~18:00), so this is agent work again, but cpe.sunat.gob.pe still answers 403 to scripts. Leads: SUNAT publishes its validation rules as XSLT inside the SFS (Sistema de Facturacion Electronica, the free Facturador SUNAT) package; esolutions/xml (packagist) says its rules are extracted from those XSLTs; greenter/validator and Kembec/facturacion-electronica-sunat-sdk are related tools. Next: fetch the official SFS distribution (or an archive.org snapshot of it) and take the ValidaExprReg*.xsl files from it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 10u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:49 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). TODAY: cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts, but the project-openubl xbuilder homologation cases are already in deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion (init.ps1). DONE WHEN: the SUNAT UBL 2.1 customization reads through the EXISTING generated UBL units (no new family code): every homologation case reads back with 0 drift as one corpus_checks test pinning the count, and the SUNAT customization rules (from the openubl rule set, pinned) run as a profile with pinned findings. NEXT STEP: count the cases in deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion, add the read-back test beside ubl_tr_samples_keep_their_main_schematron_findings. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: Peru is a ubl_profile case (PeSunat) with its rules as typed schematron patterns; catalog codes (SUNAT catalogs 01-59) become validated nominals from their published lists, never raw strings.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 11u32, "2026-11-03T20:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:34 fiscal: DoD part 1 (the count test) WRITTEN, unstaged in fiscal src/corpus_checks.spi: test every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit pins the 58 project-openubl homologation cases (deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion, all XML) as 28 Invoice, 15 CreditNote and 15 DebitNote entries of the init-written UBL manifests, which ARE the documents the existing generated UBL units read back (no new family code, as the DoD asks). Typed: ':| ubl_kind = InvoiceKind | CreditNoteKind | DebitNoteKind' with ':| ubl_syntax = UblXml | UblJson' select the manifest (ubl_manifest), and entries_under prefix kind syntax counts a country's entries; the MyInvois test (FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS) now uses the same reader, so one function serves every country. PROVEN on europa (pack27): corpus_checks --check with bodies exit 0; both tests compiled --backend Rust against the box's 4 real manifests run exit 0; MUTATION (one SUNAT debit note removed from its manifest) exits 1. LEFT for the DoD: the read-back verdict per case comes from the UBL units' own reads_its_documents tests (the next full regen gate); the SUNAT customization rules as a pinned profile (openubl rule set) and the catalog nominals.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 12u32, "2026-11-04T01:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 21:37 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793754211554-fiscal-corpus-checks, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2, one compiler): with scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write run first (src/corpus.txt 580 lines) and the box manifests, the live corpus_checks.spi is 28/28 -- incl. every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes, every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit, and models_the_corpus_census / resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet (the 2 rows VOID this afternoon; the NotFound root cause is confirmed).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:13 fiscal: CATALOG 07 AS A TYPED GADT (new fiscal src/sunat.spi 06BA8C08, registered in package.spiproj + spiral.toml after profiles; unstaged). SOURCE PINNED, not memory: project-openubl/xbuilder main xbuilder/src/catalogs.rs (blob 6f73783d32b75e16001fb2bcd398a06a4458d8d3, 23,678 bytes, fetched as data): Catalog7 codes 10-17 Gravado, 20-21 Exonerado, 30-36 Inafecto, 40 Exportacion -- and Catalog7::group maps 40 to EXONERADO (not its own group), which the model follows. Model: phantom groups gravado/exonerado/inafecto, ':| igv_affectation g' (18 cases each indexed by its group), ':| affectation = Taxed | Exempt | Unaffected' for parsing (one typed case per group), affectation_code / affectation_of / code_of / is_onerosa, and igv_line rate (line : igv_affectation gravado) base: charging IGV on a non-taxed line is a COMPILE error. Grounded in the corpus: the 58 homologation cases use TaxExemptionReasonCode 10, 11, 12, 13, 20, 21, 30, 31 (all parse); InvoiceTypeCode is catalogo01 '01' on the 28 invoices. Tests: every_catalog_07_code_round_trips_through_its_group, the_homologation_cases_use_known_codes, only_taxed_lines_charge_igv, an_exempt_line_cannot_charge_igv fails 'Unification failure' (europa: fails with 'Got igv_affectation gravado, Expected igv_affectation exonerado'). PROOF europa pack27: format clean, --check module + bodies exit 0, the 3 bodies to Rust exit 0. LEFT: other catalogs the corpus uses (01 document type, 05 tax scheme, 09/10 note reasons, 16 price type) the same way, then the openubl rule set as a profile.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 14u32, "2026-11-04T07:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:19 fiscal: CATALOGS 01, 09, 10 added to sunat.spi (36BDD4C5), same pinned source (openubl catalogs.rs blob 6f73783d): document_type (01 Factura, 03 Boleta, 07 NotaCredito, 08 NotaDebito, 09 GuiaRemisionRemitente), credit_note_reason (catalog 09, 10 cases), debit_note_reason (catalog 10: 01 InteresPorMora, 02 AumentoEnElValor, 03 PenalidadOtrosConceptos); each with an exhaustive code match and a parser from one all_* list via the generic coded lookup. UPSTREAM DEFECT FOUND: openubl maps DevolucionPorItem to '06' (same as DevolucionTotal) and never emits '07', in a list otherwise contiguous 01-10; a code table must be injective, so fiscal uses 07 and the test pins unique codes 01..10 (worth an upstream issue, but no public-project interaction from here). Corpus: the 30 note ResponseCode values are all '01'. Test catalogs_01_09_10_have_unique_codes_that_round_trip. PROOF europa pack27: format clean, module + bodies exit 0, the negative still fails 'Got igv_affectation gravado', all 4 bodies to Rust exit 0. LEFT: catalogs 05/16 as needed, the openubl rule set as a profile.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 15u32, "2026-11-04T07:22Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:22 fiscal: CATALOG 05 + the 07->05 mapping added (sunat.spi 8A0EBE17), ported from the pinned source's Catalog7::tax_category, not inferred: tax_scheme (1000 IGV, 1016 IVAP, 2000 ISC, 9995 EXP, 9996 GRA, 9997 EXO, 9998 INA, 7152 ICBPER, 9999 OTROS), tax_category over the group-indexed igv_affectation (onerosa lines get their own scheme; every free transfer, retiro or gratuita, gets 9996 GRA; IVAP 17 -> 1016), scheme_code_of for a parsed affectation. FIX found by the same read: is_onerosa had missed GravadoIvap (17), which openubl's onerosa marks true. Grounded: the corpus's TaxScheme IDs (multi-line XML) are 1000 x142, 2000 x36, 9996 x122, 9997 x22, 9998 x22, all parse. Test every_affectation_has_the_tax_scheme_openubl_assigns. PROOF europa pack27: format clean, module + bodies exit 0, negative still 'Got igv_affectation gravado', all 5 bodies to Rust exit 0.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 16u32, "2026-11-04T07:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:25 fiscal: RULE-SET SOURCE CHECKED (DoD part 3): project-openubl ships NO pinnable SUNAT rule set. Its active repos (xhandler-rust, xhandler-java, ublhub, xbuilder catalogs) contain no .xsl/.xslt/.sch files: openubl encodes SUNAT knowledge as code (catalogs.rs, enrich rules), which fiscal has now ported as typed catalogs (01, 05, 07, 09, 10 in sunat.spi). SUNAT's own rules are its published validation XSLs (the 'validaciones' packages on cpe.sunat.gob.pe), and that host answers 403 to scripts (n?). OPTIONS for the profile: (a) fetch the SUNAT validation package once through the user's browser (Chrome tooling) and pin it by sha256 in init.ps1 under deps/corpus/pe/sunat-validaciones; (b) derive a typed rule subset from the ported catalogs (e.g. every line's TaxScheme = tax_category of its TaxExemptionReasonCode; a credit note's ResponseCode parses as catalog 09) and check it over the 58 homologation cases -- runnable now, no download. Next: (b), as a corpus_checks test pinning 0 findings over the homologation cases.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 17u32, "2026-11-04T07:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:32 fiscal: RULE (b) DONE AND HELD BY THE CORPUS (sunat.spi B3AC871C): every TaxCategory that carries a TaxExemptionReasonCode must carry the TaxScheme ID that openubl's Catalog7::tax_category assigns (category_findings/findings_within walk any UBL document; scheme_finding names the line). Tests: a_tax_category_carries_the_scheme_of_its_affectation (synthetic: a retiro under 9996 passes, code 10 under 9996 and an unknown 99 are findings) and the_homologation_cases_carry_the_scheme_of_each_affectation: over the 58 SUNAT homologation cases (pe/ lines of the 3 UBL manifests) 233 TaxCategory elements are checked and 0 findings -- 233 also matches an independent grep of the lines carrying TaxExemptionReasonCode, so the walk misses none. PROOF europa pack27 (with the pe corpus + manifests staged): module + bodies exit 0, negative still fails as typed, all 7 bodies to Rust exit 0; MUTATION (code 11 retiro -> IGV) fails the suite (caught first by the mapping test). DoD part 3 is met in the typed form (option b); the SUNAT XSL package (option a) stays optional. LEFT: the read-back verdict per case at the next full regen gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 18u32, "2026-11-04T07:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:46 fiscal: catalog 16 (price type: 01 PrecioUnitarioIncluyeIgv, 02 ValorReferencialUnitarioEnOperacionesNoOnerosas; same pinned source) added to sunat.spi (DF106C6C) with price_type_of; corpus PriceTypeCode values are 01 x133, 02 x100. A per-line '02 iff non-onerosa' rule was NOT asserted: the counts show lines carry both prices, so it needs a per-line study first. PROOF europa pack27: format clean, --check exit 0, all 7 bodies to Rust exit 0 (corpus rule still 233 checked, 0 findings).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 19u32, "2026-11-04T07:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:51 fiscal: SECOND CORPUS RULE (sunat.spi E76F8F3C): a line's PriceTypeCode follows its affectation's onerosa flag (01 PrecioUnitarioIncluyeIgv for onerosa, 02 ValorReferencial for free transfers). Studied before asserting (the aggregate counts had looked inconsistent): per line, the 58 cases give exactly 133 lines 'prices=[01] onerosa' and 100 lines 'prices=[02] non-onerosa', nothing else. Test every_homologation_line_prices_by_its_onerosa_flag: synthetic (a 21 line priced 01 is the only finding) + corpus 233 lines checked, 0 findings. PROOF europa pack27: format clean, --check exit 0, all 8 bodies to Rust exit 0; MUTATION (code 11 marked onerosa) fails the suite (first at the onerosa-flags assertion; the corpus test would also fail on the code-11 lines). Six SUNAT catalogs typed (01, 05, 07, 09, 10, 16) and two rules held over the full homologation set.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 20u32, "2026-11-06T08:19Z", "fiscal", "Groom 11-06: 85%; shares the UBL 2.1 signature path with MyInvois; check after FISCAL-MYINVOIS-SIGNATURE-TWIN whether the SUNAT sample has the same ds:Signature twin gap.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 21u32, "2026-11-09T07:17Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 TWIN CHECK (note 20's question) ANSWERED: NO GAP. FISCAL-MYINVOIS-SIGNATURE-TWIN closed 11-09 (the twin rule in lib xml_codec handles an XMLDSig ds:Signature inside UBLExtensions/ExtensionContent). Scanning all 58 SUNAT homologation samples under deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion: 0 carry an XMLDSig block; they carry only the UBL cac:Signature party reference, which is plain UBL and already round-trips (corpus_checks every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit: 28 invoices, 15 credit notes, 15 debit notes, green in the 11-09 30/30 run). So the twin shape cannot arise for this corpus. Remaining for this item: DoD part 3, SUNAT's own validation XSLs (cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts, note 16); a signed SUNAT sample, if one is ever pinned, then goes through the same twin path as MyInvois.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 22u32, "2026-11-10T02:41Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 21:xx (user: download things pending) SUNAT VALIDATION XSLs DOWNLOADED AND PINNED. cpe.sunat.gob.pe/guias-y-manuales now answers 200 to plain clients (it was 403 to scripts on 10-27..11-04). Pinned in fiscal scripts/init.ps1 (unstaged, new block deps/corpus/pe/sunat-validaciones): the UBL 2.1 XSL archive 'XSL Actualizado al 06092022' (sha256 03A8DEC89D8BEB00..., 15 ValidaExprReg*-2.0.1.xsl incl. Factura 495268 B, Boleta, NC, ND, Guia, Liquidacion) into xsl/, and the published XSD set (5CAC9D9353521340..., 105 files) into xsd/; placed locally with both pins verified. Also downloaded, NOT pinned (92 MB, a Java app, nothing executed): SFS v2.5 (www2.sunat.gob.pe/facturador/SFS_v-2.5.zip, sha256 6F59BF9AC8646CC3...), whose sunat_archivos/sfs/VALI/commons holds the complete 265-XSL set the Greenter guide recommends over the published archive; kept at C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\fiscal-pending-dl\\sunat for comparison. NEXT STEP: DoD part 3, run the ValidaExprReg XSLs (XSLT 1.0) over the 58 homologation cases and turn their rule codes into typed findings next to rule (b).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 23u32, "2026-11-10T13:54Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 10:4x DoD PART 3 RUN: SUNAT's own ValidaExprReg rules executed over all 58 homologation cases. Engine and rules are SUNAT's: SFS 2.5 (SFS_v-2.5.zip; facturadorApp-2.5.jar is a fat jar carrying SAXON-HE 9.7.0.1J, build 2015-11-27) running SFS's OWN rule copies (sunat_archivos/sfs/VALI/commons/xsl/validation/2.X), the only mapping being SFS's install-root and local:/// include paths to the extracted VALI. FINDING: the PUBLISHED xsl-ubl21 2.0.1 rules do NOT compile under a strict XSLT processor (single-argument concat() in Factura/Boleta, out-of-scope variables in NC/ND, duplicated sibling variables, XPath 2.0 matches() under a 1.0 header), and Saxon itself rejects the published Factura for the concat(); SFS ships corrected copies with the same version label (Factura 5,781 lines vs 6,600+ published). The rules read the submitted file name from the stylesheet parameter nombreArchivoEnviado (RUC-TT-SERIE-NUMERO.xml), built per case from the issuer RUC, the type code and cbc:ID as SFS names its files. RESULT: 58/58 ACCEPTED. NEGATIVE CONTROL: the same run without the file name rejected all 58 with errorCode 1034 (file-name RUC vs content), so the engine evaluates rules and acceptance is a verdict. Runner: session scratchpad sunat-runner\\run-sunat-saxon.ps1 (rejectCall overridden to emit REJECT|code|message so a rejection yields its code). Next step: pin SFS_v-2.5.zip (94 MB, from SUNAT) in fiscal scripts/init.ps1 with its sha256 so the run is reproducible, and decide whether a CI leg may run Java (else the 58/58 stays recorded evidence rather than a gate).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 24u32, "2026-11-10T14:07Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 11:0x SFS PINNED for reproducibility: https://www2.sunat.gob.pe/facturador/SFS_v-2.5.zip (SUNAT's own host; HTTP 200, application/zip, 93,978,756 bytes, Last-Modified 2026-10-01) downloaded fresh and byte-identical to the copy used for the 58/58 run (sha256 6F59BF9AC8646CC32F1738703AA9CB5D3AE5020DC78F5A25551B08817AA93EDF). Pinned in fiscal scripts/init.ps1 as deps/corpus/pe/sunat-sfs (unstaged; parse clean) and placed locally. Next step: user decision on whether CI may run Java for a SUNAT-rules leg (recorded on the item; until then the 58/58 with its 1034 negative control is recorded evidence, not a gate).")
