inl note_of_x_backend_switches_1 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:43Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:41 x: carved out of X-BACKEND-MAP so the finished map stops blocking GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT. Rules: X-BACKEND-MAP notes 2 (shell), 13 (corpus) and 6-7 (batch dry-run), all registered in x/target/ledger. Blockers per switch: the shell needs a gleam run launcher (staged in x-world shell-launch) and a quiet box; the corpus needs SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY's shared cell parser for its parity gate; the sampler needs EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH's shared process-table walk.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_2 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 2u32, "2026-10-27T17:05Z", "x", "2026-10-27 13:05 x: the shell switch's 'quiet box' blocker is dropped under the user's 10-27 rule (no waiting for a quiet machine; benches must hold under load). Its bench is redesigned like X-PRECOMMIT-SPEED's: both arms in one loaded run, alternating order, median ratio, cpu% reported beside the number. The other blockers stand: a gleam run launcher for the shell, SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY's cell parser for the corpus parity gate, and EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH's process-table walk for the sampler.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_3 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 3u32, "2026-10-29T13:38Z", "x", "2026-10-29 10:2x x: blocker review. X-BACKEND-MAP is Done; EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH is still Planned (blocks only the sampler switch). Shell switch: the gleam run launcher staged in %TEMP%\\x-world\\shell-launch was LOST in the 10-28 wipe (WIPE-REDO-LEDGER batch 4); it's a redo from xsim_shell_entry.spi, and the X-SHELL-SWITCH rule survives in x/target/ledger. The bench design from n2 holds (both arms in one loaded run). Corpus switch: still needs SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY's cell parser for parity. Overlap to watch: SIM-IN-SPIRAL S1 (n76) moves xsim.run's fake path to Spiral's sync runner; the shell switch compares Elixir's Runner with the Gleam OTP shell on replay. Different questions, same Runner, so run the shell switch BEFORE S5 deletes the Elixir Runner.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_4 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 4u32, "2026-10-29T13:40Z", "x", "2026-10-29 10:3x x: wipe redo of the shell launcher DRAFTED in a tracked place: x/scripts/sim-shell.ps1 [shell args...]. It uses the sim build's toolchain resolution (honours a pinned SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL), writes a gleam package xsim_shell under target/build/sim-shell (git-ignored, outside the line gate), BuildSpiral's apps/sim/spi/xsim_shell_entry.spi -Backend Gleam into it, then 'gleam run --target erlang -- <args>' and exits with its code. UNPROVEN: first run is 'sim-shell.ps1 --replay apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.events.jsonl' on the node after verify29 (expect 'settled' and exit 0), with a negative 'sim-shell.ps1 --replay no-such-file' (expect the usage/refusal path and exit != 0).")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_5 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 5u32, "2026-10-29T18:47Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:0x x: the shell launcher (wipe redo, x/scripts/sim-shell.ps1) is PROVEN on the node (x-queue2 job-1793297885276, pack-6b): positive replay of apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.events.jsonl exit 0, negative --replay of a missing stream exit 1. The first run failed with 'No module ... actor', because the generated gleam.toml lacked gleam_otp; it now declares the same 7 Gleam deps Cells pins for notebooks (targets.ex @gleam_deps), so the shell runs with the deps its Cells tests passed with. Next for the shell switch: the X-SHELL-SWITCH bench (x/target/ledger rule) when the node has an hour.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_6 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 6u32, "2026-10-30T02:01Z", "x", "2026-10-30T02:01Z groom: deps re-checked. X-BACKEND-MAP Done since 10-27; the remaining dep is EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH (Planned 0, kit team). n5's 'X-SHELL-SWITCH bench when the node has an hour' is restated under no-quiet-machine-wait: bench under load with an in-job A/A row instead of waiting for a quiet hour. Stays Planned 0 because of the dep.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_7 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 7u32, "2026-11-01T06:31Z", "x", "2026-11-01 02:31 x: RE-DECIDED after SIM-IN-SPIRAL (Done 10-31). Two of the four switches lost an arm:\n(1) Shell switch, Elixir Runner vs Gleam OTP shell: VOID. S5 deleted apps/sim's Elixir (n3 had said to run it before S5; it wasn't run, partly because the wipe took the launcher until 10-29). No measurement is possible and none is needed: the Gleam engine is the only engine, at parity with Elixir's recorded behaviour (SIM-IN-SPIRAL n117).\n(2) Corpus run, Elixir vs Rust vs Rust+par: re-scoped to Gleam vs Rust. The sim's pure engine (sync_run, scheduler, invariants) is backend-neutral Spiral with rust and gleam test blocks. Only cells_executor is BEAM. The measure is now built in: X-RUN-METRICS' x_sim_deliveries_per_second, emitted per schedule since tonight's clock_ms (proof x-parity-metrics1 running). Rule, written now: run the same seed/schedule ladder through the fake executor on both backends in ONE node job, alternating order, 3 rounds each, with an in-job A/A row (memory ab-needs-in-job-aa). Switch the corpus driver to Rust iff its median rate is >= 2x Gleam's AND rows are identical (XSIM stable fields). Otherwise Gleam stays (BACKEND-BALANCE tie rule).\n(3) Batch dry-run: folded into POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS' 'xc postable census' (Rust already, R2).\n(4) Native tree sampler: still blocked on EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH, which only it needs.\nNext node-runnable: (2) once X-RUN-METRICS' rate row is proven. A Rust launcher for the fake corpus run is the one new piece, a cli_run-equivalent export compiled to Rust.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_8 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 8u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "x", "2026-11-01 08:37 x: ITEM UPGRADE (round 4). Fields: tags gain team:x; 240 / heavy / agent stand (the node runs both arms). DEFINITION OF DONE: n7's corpus switch decided by its rule (Rust median rate >= 2x Gleam AND identical XSIM stable fields -> switch, else Gleam stays), measured in ONE node job with an in-job A/A, 3 rounds alternating. Artifact: medians and the verdict on this item, and BACKEND-BALANCE updated. NEXT CONCRETE STEP: a Rust launcher for the fake corpus run, an export mirroring simframes' cli_run but with the fake executor only (sim_run.simulated, already backend-neutral), compiled with --backend Rust into a small crate under target/build. It reads x_sim_run_ms and x_sim_deliveries_total from both arms.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the arm is a phantom index on the run record, so results can't be mixed. ':! on_rust = ()' and ':! on_gleam = ()', with the measured row typed 'arm_run b = { rows : list (metric count); ms : metric milliseconds }' over X-RUN-METRICS' 'metric u'. The comparison takes 'arm_run on_rust' and 'arm_run on_gleam' as distinct parameters, so swapping arms is a type error. Stable-field identity compares typed run_shape records, not printed XSIM lines (stringly diffing is what the ladder parity was replaced with).")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_9 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T01:12Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:11 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP, x's corner: open x items with no note in 48 h). Owner x, heavy. Next step unchanged (n7's corpus switch rule on the node), after the real-profile replay frees the node.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_10 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 10u32, "2026-11-06T08:26Z", "x", "2026-11-06 04:2x x: groom: READY. Both deps (X-BACKEND-MAP, X-RUN-METRICS) are Done. Heavy; node-first.")
inl note_of_x_backend_switches_11 () = Note ("X-BACKEND-SWITCHES", 11u32, "2026-11-10T12:06Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 08:2x slice-on-demand check: NOT sliced, because the next step is a node RUN (no authoring step to draft). Structured wait row added so the slice prompt stops offering it: when:quiet-node-slot (ganymede or moon after TRAIN43f).")
