inl planning_of_runner_stale () = Planning ("RUNNER-STALE", Minutes 75u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_runner_stale_1 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 1u32, "2026-10-29T14:13Z", "compiler", "10-29 10:1x compiler: filed from the compiler lane's node upkeep (assigned by main 10:1x). Cells resolves the runner as opts[:spiral] || SPIRAL_EXE || default_spiral() (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/toolchain.ex:42). Both machines run a runner older than apps/spiral HEAD, and the two differ from each other: box workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe built 2026-10-26 06:28, sha16 7CEC582FD5E29728 (no SPIRAL_EXE, default path); node SPIRAL_EXE = the same path, built 2026-10-25 17:28, sha16 04C10A363AC987E1. apps/spiral changed at 3f1b7588 (2026-10-27 05:43): spiral.spi +/-200 lines, spiral.rs regenerated (10,061+/13,309-), spiral.livemd removed, plus an unstaged apps/spiral/build.ps1 edit. So box and node Cells verdicts can differ by runner, and neither runs HEAD's runner. Visibility added now: i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1 status prints node runner/compiler and box runner/compiler sha16 + build time side by side (unstaged; verified: compilers match 05E94769A86A9B9C, runners differ). SEQUENCE (main): (1) kit's 'TRAIN3 published'; (2) the pack-6(b) install; (3) broadcast to all lanes and check for live Cells readers (lib-guarded-do's reader rule), then rebuild the box runner as a singleton (cargo --release in workspace), smoke one cell, rename-swap the old exe aside, log; (4) ship to the node by stage + smoke + rename-swap, then verify with remote.ps1 status (runner lines equal) and -RequireCore; (5) then COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE. A swap under a running notebook is the failure mode to avoid.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_2 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 2u32, "2026-10-29T14:37Z", "compiler", "10-29 10:37 compiler: scope widened (main, kit's REMOTE-LAPTOP-LANE n19): the node's own C:\\home\\git\\spiral checkout is stale too, at d095f13d with 112 lib .spi/.spir files vs the box's cec8840c with 236 (no lib\\spiral\\iggy.spi), so anything on the node resolving the lib from its checkout gets an old lib. remote.ps1 status now prints a checkout line (HEAD + lib file count + names/sizes digest) for node and box beside the runner and compiler lines. The quiet-window pass refreshes the node checkout too: mirrors link deps\\ from it (agent-sync.md), so check for live mirror jobs first (memory unlink-mirror-junctions-first).")
inl note_of_runner_stale_3 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 3u32, "2026-10-29T16:52Z", "compiler", "10-29 12:52 compiler: STAGED, not swapped (main: no swap until kit's 'TRAIN4 published', so the whole train sees one runner). Built HEAD's committed apps/spiral/spiral.rs (3f1b7588, which already carries the mimalloc allocator line) with cargo +nightly-2026-10-18 --profile release-unwind --package spiral into a SEPARATE CARGO_TARGET_DIR (no tree write, no contention with TRAIN4's workspace target): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\runner-3f1b7588\\target\\release-unwind\\spiral.exe, sha16 2E5F532E73EEAF14, 5m38s (job-1793292311432). Smoke: --help exit 0 with the same 6 commands as the live 7CEC582F; a real Rust cell (samples/closure_pair/main.rs via 'spiral.exe rust --rs-path') exit 0 on both, identical output. Deliberately NOT regenerated spiral.rs with the pack-6b compiler: RUNNER-STALE's goal is the runner = HEAD's apps/spiral; regenerating belongs to the normal apps/spiral build. SWAP PLAN after TRAIN4: broadcast + live Cells reader check, then move the live workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe aside (a running exe can be renamed on Windows, so in-flight cells keep the old one), copy the staged exe in, smoke again; then node-ship.ps1 the same exe to the node's SPIRAL_EXE path, then the node checkout update.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_4 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 4u32, "2026-10-29T22:42Z", "compiler", "10-29 18:4x compiler: SWAPPED on kit's 'TRAIN4 published' (18:35:54, kit confirmed nothing of its own was using the old runner). BOX workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe 7CEC582FD5E29728 (10-26, stale) -> 2E5F532E73EEAF14 (HEAD 3f1b7588 build, release-unwind); old archived hash-verified at C:\\home\\data\\runner-archive-2026-10-29\\spiral.exe.7CEC582FD5E29728. NODE: node-ship 04C10A363AC987E1 (10-25) -> 2E5F532E73EEAF14, digest verified, previous kept as .replaced-runner-2E5F532E. SMOKE NOTE: the swap script's check (stdout must contain the program's 'runner-smoke 42') FAILED on the new runner, and its auto-restore could not run (the file was briefly held). Running the archived OLD runner on the identical 'rust --rs-path' smoke gave the same behavior (exit 0, the same 3 trace lines, no program text), so the criterion was wrong for both runners and the new one has behavioral parity; kept. Next swap: parity with the old runner is the criterion. 'runner swapped' sent to main and kit. Left: node checkout sync, deferred (other lanes' jobs on the node; 14 node-only files archived).")
inl note_of_runner_stale_5 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 5u32, "2026-10-30T16:55Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:55 compiler: RUNNER READY TO SWAP (staged, not swapped). Built on the BOX from C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace with the landed spiral.spi + spiral.rs (5ECE8F9946287738), cargo +nightly-2026-10-18 release-unwind in a private target seeded from the 10-29 warm target: 4 min, exe F1DD2E34F1E816C8, staged at C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\runner-F1DD2E34.exe. Why the box and not the node proof's exe (EB706BDE, built from the identical spiral.rs and Cargo.lock): spiral.rs reads env!(CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR) at 4 sites, so the proof exe's cells report code_path under c:/home/remote/pack8 (a mirror). A swap runner must be built from the real checkout path (memory runner-bakes-manifest-dir). The node's checkout has the same path, so this box exe ships to the node as on 10-29. Smoke: --help exit 0 (13 lines, same as live). A rust --rs-path cell (closure_pair) exits 0 with output byte-identical to the live 2E5F532E (1,437 B, 46ED123B03DE33A7, code_path included). Cuda: SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312 (numpy 2.5.4) exit 0 with the ok line; SPIRAL_PYTHON = a nonexistent path exits 1 'cannot find the path', so the runner takes its interpreter from SPIRAL_PYTHON. The no-numpy control ran on the node (n5). Swap script C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\runner-swap.ps1 (10-29's, re-parameterized): dry run ok, live 2E5F532E, 0 users. Waiting on main + kit's go, then node-ship.ps1 for the node, then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 sm' cuda rows on both machines.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_6 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 6u32, "2026-10-30T18:04Z", "compiler", "10-30 14:04 compiler: SWAP REVERTED by a pre-registered rule; the box is back on 2E5F532E73EEAF14 (hash-verified, smoke exit 0); the node was never shipped. Sequence: box swap to F1DD2E34 at 13:0x (main + kit go), then kit's sm' gate on the new lib under kit's failing condition (numpy-less python 3.15 first on PATH, SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312): 63/72. Kit's 5 cuda failures (to_char_array, format, show, to_char_array_2, concat_array) PASS, so the cuda fix works. But 9 others failed. A quiet-box rerun of the 9 alone (job-1793382555570), same lib (sm' A683500F), per arm: NEW F1DD2E34 7/9, failing show_floats [zig] and show_floats_in_python_repr_layout [delphi] with 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed' (the slowest passing cell took 79 s, so this is a hang); OLD 2E5F532E 9/9. The other 7 were load (tibia saw the same file's load reds on the node this morning). The hang's target moved between runs (loaded: delphi/zig the other way round), so it's nondeterministic. Rule (agreed with main before the read): new fails and old passes = runner, so restore. F1DD2E34 is kept at C:\\home\\data\\runner-archive-2026-10-30\\spiral.exe.F1DD2E34F1E816C8. Checked so far: the child-process pipe sites (wait/BufReader) have the same shape in the committed (old) and regen (new) spiral.rs, so it's not an obvious pipe-order change. NEXT (box time needed, queued behind tibia's smoke and main's Cells window): (1) repeat the 2 tests 3x per arm to rule out a flake; (2) if it holds, run show_floats on the new exe under a CPU sampler (busy hang vs blocked wait); (3) build a runner from HEAD spiral.spi (no cuda edit) with the installed compiler. If that hangs too, it's a pack-7 Rust codegen regression in the regen, not the cuda edit; then bisect the 13,926-line regen diff by function. 2) Workaround for kit's cuda cells: scoop python312 first on PATH (72/72 this morning).")
inl note_of_runner_stale_7 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 7u32, "2026-10-30T18:48Z", "compiler", "10-30 14:48 compiler: RUNNER CLEARED on follow-up, re-swap deferred to after TRAIN5 (kit's call). After n6's revert: (1) flake check, show_floats + show_floats_in_python_repr_layout ALONE, 3 rounds alternating new/old (job-1793384471396, quiet box, CPU sampler log C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\flake\\cpu-samples.tsv): all 6 runs 2/2, no timeout. (2) the original 9 together with the order REVERSED, old first (job-1793385454471): old 9/9, new 9/9, 4.1 min each. Tally for the two show_floats tests: new runner 1 failure in 8 runs (its first cold run, 9 cells in flight), old 0 in 5. The daemon-port confound is ruled out: lib_gate -Compiler process sets SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER=process, which skips the warm daemon (spiral.notebook.ex:26, notebook.ex:776, cells.ex:765). main's caveat stands: the old runner also passed cold and first, so the new runner's first-run path stays slightly suspect at n=8. PLAN: after TRAIN5 publishes (TRAIN5's launcher pins 2E5F532E and puts python312 first, so its cuda cells pass without the swap), re-swap the box to F1DD2E34 with runner-swap.ps1, then node-ship.ps1. Guard: one show_floats warm-up before a train's notebooks; on a no-load recurrence, revert and bisect (HEAD-spi pack-7 regen on the node, job-1793383855225, for the churn diff).")
inl note_of_runner_stale_8 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 8u32, "2026-10-30T19:52Z", "compiler", "10-30 15:52 compiler: NODE RUNNER SWAPPED to F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (kit confirmed TRAIN5 is box-only, so the node could move now; the box stays on 2E5F532E until TRAIN5 publishes). node-ship.ps1 -Label runner-F1DD2E34. Pre-swap smoke on the node (the swap runs only on SMOKE-OK): a closure_pair rust --rs-path cell's JSON output from the staged new exe is byte-identical to the node's live old runner's, code_path included (the exe was built from C:\\home\\git\\spiral on the box, the same path as the node checkout). Digest 4DAB82B4CC4A96DF verified after the copy; the previous runner is kept as spiral.exe.replaced-runner-F1DD2E34. Post-swap cuda test on the node through the live runner, with numpy-less Programs\\Python312 FIRST on PATH: control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset) exit 1 'No module named numpy' (the bug's own path); fixed (the node's User SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312) exit 0 with the ok line. So the node half of CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY is done. LEFT: the box swap after TRAIN5 publishes (runner-swap.ps1, byte-equal smoke + auto-restore), then the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar; the 5 cuda cells already passed on F1DD2E34 on the box at 13:3x).")
inl note_of_runner_stale_9 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 9u32, "2026-10-30T23:10Z", "compiler", "10-30 19:10 compiler: DRIFT NOTE for the post-TRAIN5 box swap. main's LIB-CANON-NAMES (19:05, runtime.spi retired, consumers renamed to process / rust/clap) edited apps/spiral/spiral.spi again (now blob 8028a925; the cuda_python edit is intact; 0 'runtime.' refs left), but the landed apps/spiral/spiral.rs is still the pre-rename regen 5ECE8F9946287738. So the tree's .rs no longer matches its .spi. The rename is behaviour-neutral, so the node's F1DD2E34 stays fine, but the BOX swap after TRAIN5 must use a runner regenerated from the CURRENT spiral.spi: regen spiral.rs with the installed compiler (the mimalloc tail appended as build.ps1 does), cargo release-unwind from C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace (private target, warm seed runner-cuda1030), the same byte-equal smoke vs the live runner, then swap box and node to that one hash so both machines match again. Land the new spiral.rs with it.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_10 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 10u32, "2026-11-02T23:54Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:5x orphan sweep round 4: Active with no note for over 48 h and no lane driving it this week, so Active -> Planned at 90% (an Active status that nobody touches lies to agile wip). The next step stays the one in the latest note; it is back in agile next at its priority.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_11 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 11u32, "2026-11-05T07:43Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:5x compiler: a concrete reason to rebuild: the box and node spiral.exe (box built 11-03 09:08) do not contain SPIRAL_PYTHON (byte scan), although spiral.spi has had it since 11-02 00:38; see SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON's 11-05 note. A rebuild via apps/spiral/build.ps1 (box, then ship to the node) unblocks CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_12 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 12u32, "2026-11-06T12:47Z", "main", "main 11-06 10:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: the Cells runner spiral.exe on box and node is built from apps/spiral HEAD, and both have the same hash. Next step: rebuild via apps/spiral/build.ps1 on the node when it is quiet (not during tibia's timing sweep), ship it to the box, and compare hashes.")
inl note_of_runner_stale_13 () = Note ("RUNNER-STALE", 13u32, "2026-11-08T16:49Z", "i574n", "11-08 16:4x (compiler): the node's live C:\\home\\git\\spiral is at commit 98e51d32 with spiral.spi from 11-02, so running apps/spiral/build.ps1 there would rebuild a STALE runner; its current runner 9FF45F124306B5EC equals the box's previous one (copied from the box earlier). Plan for 11-08 (incremental=false): in the gap after fiscal's shards, compiler copies the box's checked runner 2A8B15580CA7F5B6 to the node (old exe kept aside) and verifies hash + --help + one rust cell run whose workspace Cargo.toml must show incremental = false; restore the aside copy on any start failure (print the exit code in hex first). Root cause to fix later: runners should ship like compiler DLLs (box-built, checked, hashed, copied), never be built from a host's own stale checkout. europa (Linux) needs its own build from the box's source.")
