inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_1 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 1u32, "2026-10-30T04:29Z", "main", "10-30 00:29 main, from x's full-suite run (box, env imported, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, on pack 7, after fiscal's spiral.toml Cells land): 321/325. The 4 failures are intermittent: re-run alone, those 4 files go 73/73. Main's own post-land run earlier showed only the 2 postability failures (since fixed by x), so these 4 appear with load or concurrency, not deterministically. Priority within the item: DocumentTest's 'compiler blew up' is an uncaught compiler crash, not a timeout, so capture its stderr (lib_gate -RawOut-style) in a full-suite run and check whether it reproduces on pack 6b (the backup at C:\\home\\data\\compiler-installs\\pack7-20261029-221710). Method: run the full suite N times under the same load with an A/A row, and count per-test failure rates (no-quiet-machine-wait).")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_2 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 2u32, "2026-11-01T01:24Z", "x", "2026-10-31 21:24 x: evidence from an IDLE node mirror (xqueue3, nothing else running in it), tests run alone, 6 runs each, during CELLS-SPI-LIB's discriminating check (its n5-n6):\n- targets_test.exs:321 'gleam cells with the same manifest run in a warm package whose src is replaced' failed 6 of 6. That is not load: it fails deterministically on the node, so either a real bug or a node environment gap in the warm Gleam package.\n- cells_test.exs:698 'a missing pinned Rust toolchain is installed once' failed 3 of 6, alone and idle. A real flake, not only under load.\nBoth are independent of apps/cells/spi's package reference. I'm not fixing either, since they're main's Cells tests. Recorded so the next suite comparison treats :698 as noise and :321 as a known red on the node.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_3 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 3u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM, evidence since n2: four more LOAD reds on a saturated node, each disproved by a discriminator. x-cells-c3-pre1 (suite 1,216 s) gave MemoTest \"an unqualified name resolves in opened modules...\"; x-cells-c3-memo1 then passed it 26/26 three times. x-cells-c4-pre1 (suite 2,117 s) gave MemoTest \"a target run is reused when the generated code is the same\", MemoDepsTest \"editing a dependency module the program never reaches keeps the key\", and TargetsTest \"a Gleam cell runs from the notebook's directory\"; x-cells-c4-domain1 showed byte-identical domain.gleam. node_cells_window_proof -Tests (scoped suites) is the current mitigation. The CELLS-PORT-* oracles inherit this list, so a red from it needs a discriminator, not a revert.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_4 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. Likely mechanism, from fiscal n4: concurrent Cells runs on one mirror share %TEMP%\\spiral_cells and the mirror lib, and that produced os error 3 rows and locked files there. That fits the load reds listed in n3, which all came from saturated nodes with other Cells work present. Discriminator to run next, rule written now: the same scoped suite twice on an idle node, (A) alone and (B) beside a second Cells gate on the same mirror. The hypothesis holds iff A has 0 of n3's reds and B reproduces at least one.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_5 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 5u32, "2026-11-07T22:08Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: the scoped suite passes twice on an idle node alone (A) and beside a second Cells gate on the same mirror (B); if B fails, each concurrent run gets its own %TEMP%\\spiral_cells and lib mount, and B passes. Next step: x's discriminator run (A/B) the next time the node is under 50% load.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_6 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 6u32, "2026-11-09T19:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 15:5x microblog, ARM (A) EVIDENCE from the europa per-test runs (Linux, quiet node: tibia's QAT had ended, load ~1, no other Cells work on the mirror; full suite, --max-cases 2; logs archived in the microblog scratchpad europa-suite/runs.tgz): 5 full runs over 4 tree states plus a HEAD bf5cc30a control (338/398 with a mixed snapshot, 387/401, 395/401, 395/398, control 381/395). 0 of the 7 load-red tests named in this item (n0 + n3: MemoTest package-file key, MemoTest unqualified name, MemoTest target-run reuse, MemoDepsTest never-reaches, DocumentTest lib .spi as notebooks, TargetsTest kept lock, TargetsTest gleam directory) failed in any run; every red was deterministic and is explained in CELLS-PORT-PER-TEST-PROTOCOL n16. This supports the shared-TEMP/mirror concurrency hypothesis (n4) on the A side. Arm (B), the same suite beside a second Cells gate on the same mirror, is still unrun, so the DoD is not met. Caveat: Linux only; the original reds were on Windows boxes and nodes.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_7 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 7u32, "2026-11-09T20:01Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 16:0x microblog, ARM (B) STARTED, rule pre-registered before the result: job-1794254498329-x-cells-flaky-arm-b on europa (quiet, load 0.3): a fresh mirror /home/remote/cellsflaky (the box's tracked Cells + lib, hash-identical except test scratch), two full suites started together (--max-cases 2 each), private MIX_BUILD_PATH per side (compiled first, so a build race can't masquerade as the hypothesis), SHARED TMPDIR (/tmp/spiral_cells) and SHARED mirror lib. RULE (n4): the concurrency hypothesis HOLDS iff B reproduces >= 1 of the 7 listed tests (arm A today: 0 in 5 runs). If B shows none, the hypothesis is not supported on Linux and the item's next step is a Windows A/B, because the original reds were on Windows. Reds outside the list are reported separately, never counted for the hypothesis. Only the 3 known mirror gaps (Lisp x2, CLI export) are expected on both sides.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_8 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 8u32, "2026-11-09T20:08Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 16:0x microblog, ARM (B) RESULT, read by the rule pre-registered in n7: job-1794254647086-x-cells-flaky-arm-b2, two full suites CONCURRENT on one europa mirror (verified overlap: both began after compile at ~20:04:19Z and finished 20:06:11Z / 20:06:16Z, 110.7 s and 115.6 s vs ~95 s solo, so contention was real). Shared /tmp/spiral_cells and mirror lib, private build paths. BOTH sides 395/398: only the 3 known mirror gaps (Lisp x2, CLI export), 0 of the 7 listed tests. VERDICT: the concurrency hypothesis is NOT SUPPORTED on Linux (A 0/5 runs, B 0/2 sides). NEXT STEP (pre-registered): the same A/B on a Windows node, since every original red came from Windows boxes or nodes (%TEMP% semantics, file locking, os error 3 rows). Logs: microblog scratchpad europa-suite/flaky-arm-b.tgz. Mirror torn down (deps symlink unlinked first, shared deps intact).")
inl spiral_cuda_runner_python () = Task ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", "spiral cuda (apps/spiral process_cuda) runs the first python on PATH and ignores SPIRAL_PYTHON, so Cells cuda rows fail with ModuleNotFoundError numpy wherever a numpy-less python wins PATH; resolve the interpreter from SPIRAL_PYTHON (fallback python) for the run and the pip install", TaskKind, P1, D2, 90u32, Blocked, "RUNNER-STALE", "team:compiler,compiler,runner,cuda,python,cells", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python () = Planning ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", Minutes 60u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 1u32, "2026-10-30T05:06Z", "compiler", "10-30 01:0x compiler: ROOT CAUSE from kit's raw stderr on the base side (via main, 00:5x): spiral.rs:20438 'spiral.process_cuda / child failed'; main.py:141 numpy.empty(3, dtype=object) gives ModuleNotFoundError numpy. Code: apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1213 Pip runs the literal python \"<path>\", and :1202 runs the PATH pip install. Measured by main: its shell resolves python312 first (numpy 2.x), so 72/72; kit's resolves scoop python 3.15.2 (no numpy), so 67/72 on the same lib, failing the 5 cuda rows of sm' (to_char_array, format, show, to_char_array_2, concat_array). NOT a compiler or lib bug: pack 7 vs 6b Python+Cuda codegen of to_char_array is byte-identical. FIX drafted: C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\apply-spiral-cuda-python.ps1, 3 anchored edits: := python = SPIRAL_PYTHON or python; Pip install = <python> -m pip install -r requirements.txt; Pip run = <python> <path>; Poetry unchanged. Proof running on the node (job-1793336805393): build spiral.exe from the patched source in a private CARGO_TARGET_DIR, then spiral cuda --py-path on a numpy script with a numpy-less python first on PATH. The control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset) must fail on numpy; the fixed run (SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312) must print. Ships through the runner rebuild (RUNNER-STALE). Related, NOT fixed here: SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR n11, the Pip deps transform writes Poetry-style lines (numpy='*') that pip rejects.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 2u32, "2026-10-30T10:25Z", "compiler", "10-30 06:2x compiler (groom): node proof job-1793336805393 is VOID, not a fail of the fix. The applier applied (3 edits) on the pack8 mirror, but compiling apps/spiral/spiral.spi with the installed pack 7 returned 'BuildFile returned no code and no diagnostic arrived', so no spiral.rs carried the fix and the cuda test never ran. Next: re-run the compile with TRACE_DIAGNOSTICS and the mirror's own build.ps1 compile path (BuildSpiral), then the same control/fixed test. Status Active 30 (fix drafted + anchors proven, proof pending).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 3u32, "2026-10-30T10:41Z", "compiler", "10-30 06:4x compiler: VOID CAUSE FOUND, a bug in my draft, not the runner. Inside process_cuda the record parameter { py_path env deps } binds a field named env (the Pip/Poetry choice), which SHADOWS the env module, so env.get_environment_variable there type-checks as a field access on a cuda_env value. TRACE_DIAGNOSTICS showed it: 'Expected: (cuda_env : *) In the definition: run.' The first run printed no diagnostic. FIX REVISED: the applier now adds a top-level ':= cuda_python () : string' (SPIRAL_PYTHON, else 'python') above process_cuda, which only calls 'cuda_python ()'. Re-run job-1793356308358 on the node: spiral.spi now COMPILES (spiral.rs 1,480,375 B); cargo build and the control/fixed numpy test are in progress. Lesson for probes: a lib module name can be shadowed by a record field of the same name inside a function.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 4u32, "2026-10-30T11:10Z", "compiler", "10-30 07:1x compiler: PROOF PASSED (node job-1793356308358, exit 0). The pack8 mirror's spiral.spi reset to its checkout (= the box's clean HEAD file) + the revised applier (3 edits; top-level cuda_python, because the record field env shadows the env module inside process_cuda) compiled with installed pack 7 to spiral.rs 1,480,375 B; cargo release-unwind in a PRIVATE target dir (31 min cold) gave spiral.exe EB706BDE50B84FA4. Test: 'spiral cuda --py-path' on a numpy.empty(3, dtype=object) script, with Programs\\Python312 (no numpy) FIRST on PATH. Control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset): exit 1, ModuleNotFoundError numpy (the bug's own path). Fixed (SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312): exit 0, the ok line printed. LEFT: land the source edit in apps/spiral/spiral.spi (do+undo, a small text edit) after healing's all-clear; then the runner swap (RUNNER-STALE) and CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's done rule (the 5 sm' cuda rows on box and node). Applier: C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\apply-spiral-cuda-python.ps1.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 5u32, "2026-10-30T14:30Z", "compiler", "10-30 10:3x compiler: SOURCE LANDED (unstaged). Applied apply-spiral-cuda-python.ps1 to the live C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\apps\\spiral\\spiral.spi. The pre-land blob baba6978 equals the node proof mirror's checkout, and the post-land blob 6a1b8a73 is byte-identical to the file the node compiled and ran in job-1793356308358. Diff: 8+/2-. format --check exits 0. Undo copy: scratchpad cuda-land\\spiral.spi.undo. spiral.rs was NOT regenerated in the tree: the committed .rs comes from a pre-pack-7 compiler, so any regen churns about 14k lines. The regen goes with the runner rebuild. The proof's exe EB706BDE is NOT shippable, because its mirror (pack8) predates 4 lib lands: sm', xpath, xpath_eval, xsd_emit. Rebuild started from a fresh mirror of the current tree (runner1030, REMOTE-SYNC-OK digest 15B10991A48EB8CD, head cec8840c), job-1793370467510-compiler-runner1030: regen spiral.rs, cargo release-unwind in a private target, smoke (--help, a closure_pair Rust cell), and the cuda control/fixed test. LEFT: read that job; bring its spiral.rs into the tree; swap the runner on box+node, coordinated with main/kit as on 10-29 (RUNNER-STALE); then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 sm' cuda rows on both machines.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 6u32, "2026-10-30T15:46Z", "compiler", "10-30 11:46 compiler: spiral.rs LANDED (unstaged) to match the landed spiral.spi. The fresh-mirror regen (node runner1030, current box tree, installed pack 7 core 9C899B30) is 1,480,455 B, 5ECE8F9946287738, BYTE-IDENTICAL to the proof's spiral.rs. So the 4 lib lands after the pack8 mirror (sm', xpath, xpath_eval, xsd_emit) do not reach apps/spiral, and the proof's cargo build (exe EB706BDE, control exit 1 / fixed exit 0) already built exactly this file. Diff: 13,926 lines, mostly the pre-pack-7 -> pack-7 regen; 1 SPIRAL_PYTHON line, mimalloc tail kept. Undo copy: scratchpad cuda-land\\spiral.rs.undo (= HEAD blob). The runner1030 cargo build (job-1793370467510) is still running as the re-proof. LEFT: its smoke, then the runner swap on box+node coordinated with main/kit (RUNNER-STALE), then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 rows.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 7u32, "2026-10-30T16:55Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:55 compiler: RUNNER READY TO SWAP (staged, not swapped). Built on the BOX from C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace with the landed spiral.spi + spiral.rs (5ECE8F9946287738), cargo +nightly-2026-10-18 release-unwind in a private target seeded from the 10-29 warm target: 4 min, exe F1DD2E34F1E816C8, staged at C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\runner-F1DD2E34.exe. Why the box and not the node proof's exe (EB706BDE, built from the identical spiral.rs and Cargo.lock): spiral.rs reads env!(CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR) at 4 sites, so the proof exe's cells report code_path under c:/home/remote/pack8 (a mirror). A swap runner must be built from the real checkout path (memory runner-bakes-manifest-dir). The node's checkout has the same path, so this box exe ships to the node as on 10-29. Smoke: --help exit 0 (13 lines, same as live). A rust --rs-path cell (closure_pair) exits 0 with output byte-identical to the live 2E5F532E (1,437 B, 46ED123B03DE33A7, code_path included). Cuda: SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312 (numpy 2.5.4) exit 0 with the ok line; SPIRAL_PYTHON = a nonexistent path exits 1 'cannot find the path', so the runner takes its interpreter from SPIRAL_PYTHON. The no-numpy control ran on the node (n5). Swap script C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\runner-swap.ps1 (10-29's, re-parameterized): dry run ok, live 2E5F532E, 0 users. Waiting on main + kit's go, then node-ship.ps1 for the node, then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 sm' cuda rows on both machines.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 8u32, "2026-10-30T18:04Z", "compiler", "10-30 14:04 compiler: SWAP REVERTED by a pre-registered rule; the box is back on 2E5F532E73EEAF14 (hash-verified, smoke exit 0); the node was never shipped. Sequence: box swap to F1DD2E34 at 13:0x (main + kit go), then kit's sm' gate on the new lib under kit's failing condition (numpy-less python 3.15 first on PATH, SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312): 63/72. Kit's 5 cuda failures (to_char_array, format, show, to_char_array_2, concat_array) PASS, so the cuda fix works. But 9 others failed. A quiet-box rerun of the 9 alone (job-1793382555570), same lib (sm' A683500F), per arm: NEW F1DD2E34 7/9, failing show_floats [zig] and show_floats_in_python_repr_layout [delphi] with 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed' (the slowest passing cell took 79 s, so this is a hang); OLD 2E5F532E 9/9. The other 7 were load (tibia saw the same file's load reds on the node this morning). The hang's target moved between runs (loaded: delphi/zig the other way round), so it's nondeterministic. Rule (agreed with main before the read): new fails and old passes = runner, so restore. F1DD2E34 is kept at C:\\home\\data\\runner-archive-2026-10-30\\spiral.exe.F1DD2E34F1E816C8. Checked so far: the child-process pipe sites (wait/BufReader) have the same shape in the committed (old) and regen (new) spiral.rs, so it's not an obvious pipe-order change. NEXT (box time needed, queued behind tibia's smoke and main's Cells window): (1) repeat the 2 tests 3x per arm to rule out a flake; (2) if it holds, run show_floats on the new exe under a CPU sampler (busy hang vs blocked wait); (3) build a runner from HEAD spiral.spi (no cuda edit) with the installed compiler. If that hangs too, it's a pack-7 Rust codegen regression in the regen, not the cuda edit; then bisect the 13,926-line regen diff by function. 2) Workaround for kit's cuda cells: scoop python312 first on PATH (72/72 this morning).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 9u32, "2026-10-30T19:52Z", "compiler", "10-30 15:52 compiler: NODE RUNNER SWAPPED to F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (kit confirmed TRAIN5 is box-only, so the node could move now; the box stays on 2E5F532E until TRAIN5 publishes). node-ship.ps1 -Label runner-F1DD2E34. Pre-swap smoke on the node (the swap runs only on SMOKE-OK): a closure_pair rust --rs-path cell's JSON output from the staged new exe is byte-identical to the node's live old runner's, code_path included (the exe was built from C:\\home\\git\\spiral on the box, the same path as the node checkout). Digest 4DAB82B4CC4A96DF verified after the copy; the previous runner is kept as spiral.exe.replaced-runner-F1DD2E34. Post-swap cuda test on the node through the live runner, with numpy-less Programs\\Python312 FIRST on PATH: control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset) exit 1 'No module named numpy' (the bug's own path); fixed (the node's User SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312) exit 0 with the ok line. So the node half of CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY is done. LEFT: the box swap after TRAIN5 publishes (runner-swap.ps1, byte-equal smoke + auto-restore), then the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar; the 5 cuda cells already passed on F1DD2E34 on the box at 13:3x).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 10u32, "2026-10-31T15:19Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 11:19 compiler: BOX SWAP READY, gated on train6 (not TRAIN5 any more). TRAIN5 has published, but kit-train6-20261031 is running now (holds heavy-build), and a release train exercises the runner, so the swap waits for train6 to finish, by the same reason as the old gate. Tooling: runner-swap.ps1 and runner-F1DD2E34.exe were archived with C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python (20261031-094304) and restored to %TEMP%\\runner-restore\\cuda-python; the script's archive dir moved from C:\\home\\data\\runner-archive-2026-10-30 to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runner-archive\\2026-10-31 (C:\\home\\data is closed). Dry run now: live 2E5F532E73EEAF14, staged F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (hash re-verified), 0 live users. The swap keeps its byte-equal smoke (closure_pair rust --rs-path, new vs old JSON identical) and auto-restore. After it: the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 11u32, "2026-10-31T17:05Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 13:05 compiler: BOX RUNNER SWAPPED to F1DD2E34F1E816C8. train6 ended (its job hit the wall-clock cap at 12:5x), and its resume gate is held behind cells-window-6 (to 18:06) and pack10-install (to 19:38), so no train will run on the old runner for hours. runner-swap.ps1 -Apply: live had 0 users; the old 2E5F532E73EEAF14 is archived at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runner-archive\\2026-10-31\\spiral.exe.2E5F532E73EEAF14; smoke 'rust --rs-path samples/closure_pair/main.rs' gave new exit 0 (1437 B) and old exit 0 (1437 B), identical: SMOKE-OK; live is now F1DD2E34F1E816C8. Box and node now run the same runner. LEFT for Done: the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 12u32, "2026-10-31T20:21Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:21 compiler: the box sm' cuda gate (job-1793474272154, 'scoop python' 3.15 numpy-less FIRST on PATH, SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312, runner F1DD2E34, sm' D3FCCD791E27FED1) is VOID: it hit my 60 min cap (exit 124) on a box at 100% (train6 + PACK-11 builds) before lib_gate printed its summary; cells were compiling, not hung (one-shot compiler processes at 4-7 s CPU per 5 s, 15:36). The cap was too tight for the load (memory job-timeout-counts-queue-wait). Rerun with a 3 h cap AFTER tibia lands its test-only sm' change (D3FCCD79 -> 94A51BB5; tibia's land waits for this gate as the only live sm' reader), so the gate proves the new base and doesn't block tibia again.")
