inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 15u32, "2026-11-03T07:30Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (43 h). Closes with CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's box gate, no separate work.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 16u32, "2026-11-05T07:43Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:5x compiler: EVIDENCE the deployed runners are stale for SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON. The source fix is in apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1143 (':= python = \"SPIRAL_PYTHON\" |> env.get_environment_variable', spiral.spi last changed 11-02 00:38) and in the generated spiral.rs:20612. But neither deployed binary contains the string SPIRAL_PYTHON (byte scan): box C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe (built 11-03 09:08) False; node, same path, False. So Cells cuda rows still run the first python on PATH on both machines, and the fix needs a runner rebuild (apps/spiral/build.ps1, RUNNER-STALE, main's, heavy) before CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's box gate means anything.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 17u32, "2026-11-06T15:50Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:5x compiler: Planned -> BLOCKED, with the blocker written as a dep (main's star #5: a prose condition is invisible to the Blocked-deps sweep). Re-checked: the box runner C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe is still the 11-03 09:08 build (5.8 MB), and a byte scan finds no SPIRAL_PYTHON, so the source fix (apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1143) is not deployed. Blocked on: RUNNER-STALE (main's: rebuild apps/spiral on a quiet node, ship to the box, hashes equal). Resume when: RUNNER-STALE is Done; then the byte scan finds SPIRAL_PYTHON in both runners and CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's box gate closes this.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_18 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 18u32, "2026-11-09T06:50Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:5x compiler: LINUX ROOT CAUSE found via org2 (html shim proof on ganymede, 9 run-check cases panicking at spiral.rs:19642 'spiral.process_cuda / child failed / No such file or directory'): cuda_python() defaulted to the executable 'python', which Linux nodes don't have (only python3), so the child spawn hit ENOENT and process_cuda's failwith panicked; the cuda/protocol run-check cases are plain Python scripts, not CUDA. FIX (unstaged, apps/spiral/spiral.spi cuda_python): SPIRAL_PYTHON if set, else 'python' on Windows, else 'python3'. Proof queued on ganymede (chain2: apps/spiral/build.ps1 compile + cargo + full run check), and the regenerated spiral.rs comes back to the box after it passes. This does not touch the Windows box runner staleness (RUNNER-STALE) this item is blocked on.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_19 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 19u32, "2026-11-09T07:03Z", "compiler", "11-09 03:0x compiler: CLI FIX PROVEN on ganymede (Linux, no python executable, SPIRAL_PYTHON unset): apps/spiral/build.ps1 (compile + cargo + full run check) exit 0; cuda exit 0 spiral-check-cuda 42, protocol-level-{unset,Verbose,Debug,Info,Warning,Critical} exit 0 child output quoted, protocol-child-exception and protocol-cuda-driver fail as expected. The regenerated apps/spiral/spiral.rs (564c0eb0, same spiral.spi, mimalloc footer kept) is copied back to the box (unstaged; 58 lines differ after normalizing variable numbers: today lib + compiler changes + the python3 default).")
inl cuda_cells_fleet_parity () = Task ("CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY", "Cells cuda target works on every machine without depending on PATH order: the runner uses SPIRAL_PYTHON, every machine sets SPIRAL_PYTHON to a numpy python, and cuda cells are validated on the numpy path (no CUDA>=11 GPU in the fleet: both K1100M Kepler)", Story, P1, D2, 50u32, Planned, "SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON,RUNNER-STALE", "team:compiler,compiler,runner,cuda,python,cells,node", "current", "current")
