inl note_of_cuda_cells_fleet_parity_1 () = Note ("CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY", 1u32, "2026-10-30T11:04Z", "compiler", "10-30 07:1x compiler: filed on the user's order ('put in the backlog so this cuda thing is solved autonomously; you have admin there; things work here, replicate there'). No user decision is needed; the rules below decide everything.\nFACTS (census 07:0x, C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\cuda-census.ps1, read-only on both machines). BOTH machines have an NVIDIA Quadro K1100M (Kepler, compute capability 3.0); the box driver is 25.21.14.2678 (426.78, CUDA 10.1), the node driver is 23.21.13.8908 (older). Box: SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312 3.12.10 (numpy 2.5.4, cupy 14.2.0); scoop python 3.15.2 has NO numpy. In main's and my shells python312 comes first on PATH (cells pass, 72/72); in kit's shell 3.15 comes first (67/72). Node: SPIRAL_PYTHON was UNSET; PATH-first python312 3.12.9 has numpy 2.2.3 and cupy 13.3.0, and Programs\\Python312 has no numpy.\nDONE 07:1x: node User env SPIRAL_PYTHON = C:\\Users\\alias\\scoop\\apps\\python312\\current\\python.exe (verified: numpy.empty(3, dtype=object) works), replicating the box.\nDECISION RULES. (1) The cuda runner must not depend on PATH order: SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON (dep) makes spiral cuda run SPIRAL_PYTHON for both the run and pip install. (2) No GPU kernel can run on this fleet. CUDA 11 dropped compute capability 3.x, and every cupy release for Python 3.12 (13.x, 14.x) needs CUDA 11.2 or later, so no package install fixes it. cuda cells are validated on their numpy (CPU) path, and a test that needs a real kernel is Known with the reason 'no CUDA>=11 GPU in the fleet'. Do NOT chase an old CUDA 10 cupy (it would need Python <= 3.8/3.9). (3) A Python that the runner can pick must have numpy: keep numpy in every python312 that SPIRAL_PYTHON names, and never point SPIRAL_PYTHON at scoop python 3.15 until it has numpy.\nDONE RULE: after the runner swap (RUNNER-STALE), on BOTH box and node, with the 3.15 shim FIRST on PATH and SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312, the sm' cuda rows (to_char_array, format, show, to_char_array_2, concat_array) pass, and the full sm' Cells gate parses 'tests: passed 72 failed 0' (lib_gate exits 0 even on red). Run the box half only after healing's undelete all-clear (no large box writes until then).")
inl note_of_cuda_cells_fleet_parity_2 () = Note ("CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY", 2u32, "2026-10-30T19:52Z", "compiler", "10-30 15:52 compiler: NODE RUNNER SWAPPED to F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (kit confirmed TRAIN5 is box-only, so the node could move now; the box stays on 2E5F532E until TRAIN5 publishes). node-ship.ps1 -Label runner-F1DD2E34. Pre-swap smoke on the node (the swap runs only on SMOKE-OK): a closure_pair rust --rs-path cell's JSON output from the staged new exe is byte-identical to the node's live old runner's, code_path included (the exe was built from C:\\home\\git\\spiral on the box, the same path as the node checkout). Digest 4DAB82B4CC4A96DF verified after the copy; the previous runner is kept as spiral.exe.replaced-runner-F1DD2E34. Post-swap cuda test on the node through the live runner, with numpy-less Programs\\Python312 FIRST on PATH: control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset) exit 1 'No module named numpy' (the bug's own path); fixed (the node's User SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312) exit 0 with the ok line. So the node half of CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY is done. LEFT: the box swap after TRAIN5 publishes (runner-swap.ps1, byte-equal smoke + auto-restore), then the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar; the 5 cuda cells already passed on F1DD2E34 on the box at 13:3x).")
