inl fiscal_canon_model () = Task ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", "fiscal canonical document model: EN 16931 semantic terms widened by Peppol PINT, every family as a typed projection with measured loss", Epic, P1, D7, 72u32, Active, "FISCAL-CII-PROFILES,FISCAL-PEPPOL-PINT", "team:fiscal,fiscal,generic,canon,en16931,typefeatures,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_canon_model () = Planning ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", Minutes 1080u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 1u32, "2026-10-31T02:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 22:26 fiscal (user 10-30 ~22:20: 'start planning the canon fiscal modeling'): a canonical fiscal document model that every family maps into and out of, anchored on the EN 16931 semantic model (BT/BG terms; UBL and CII are its two syntaxes) widened by Peppol PINT's international terms, with the national families (NF-e, CFDI, FatturaPA, KSeF, DTE, CR, myDATA, NAV, SAF-T, GST JSON) as typed projections. Criterion kept from FISCAL-CII-PROFILES n2: count dimensions, not countries. Dimensions fiscal already expresses: versions (BR), runtime complements (CFDI), cross-namespace names (KSeF), signing stages (XSD-SIGNING-STAGES), JSON documents (GST), rule-set profiles over UBL (Peppol, ZATCA, RO, TR, MY, CO, PE). Missing for a canon: same semantics in a second syntax (CII), a non-EU semantic spine (PINT), the profile lattice (CII), and document lifecycle as its own model (FISCAL-LIFECYCLE-EVENTS). Milestones, CPU-light first: (1) term inventory: EN 16931 BT/BG list + PINT's additions as data in fiscal (no runs) 120m; (2) mapping census for three unlike families (UBL invoice, NF-e 4.00, CFDI 4.0): per family, which canon terms it supplies, which of its fields map to none, measured from the generated types 240m; (3) design note: canon as a GADT indexed by capability (profile lattice reused), projections generated per family, loss reported per field 120m; (4) generator emits to_canon/of_canon for the three, proven by round trip on their real documents 600m.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 2u32, "2026-10-31T03:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 23:13 fiscal: DESIGN SKETCH for milestone 3 (for review; nothing generated yet), built only from mechanisms fiscal already proves. (a) The canon is a family of record types keyed by EN 16931 term ids (BT-n fields, BG-n groups), so a canon field's name IS its standard id and every mapping is checkable against the binding. (b) It carries the indices fiscal already uses: the signing stage s (xsd_emit's staged s / stage witness, so canon_invoice unsigned and canon_invoice signed are distinct types) and, from FISCAL-CII-PROFILES, a profile index p (MINIMUM < BASIC WL < BASIC < EN16931 < EXTENDED) under which a field exists only from some profile up, as phantom-typed availability. (c) Each family gets two generated functions: to_canon (family_doc s -> canon_doc s p * loss) and of_canon (canon_doc s p -> result (family_doc s) missing). loss lists the family fields that map to no canon term (data kept beside the canon, never dropped silently), and missing lists the canon terms a family requires but the canon value lacks. (d) Proof per family, same rule as the readers: every real document satisfies of_canon (to_canon doc) = doc (xml.first_difference), and the loss list is pinned like the regional findings (a pin change is read before re-pinning). (e) National fields with no EN 16931 term (NF-e's ICMS groups, CFDI complements, FatturaPA's regional data) go to per-regime extension groups, BG-X-<regime>-n, so the canon stays one model and the extensions are typed, not strings. (f) Lifecycle (FISCAL-LIFECYCLE-EVENTS) attaches as events targeting a canon document id, not as fields of the document. Milestone order unchanged: (1) term inventory from OpenPeppol's BIS 3.0.20 structure/syntax bindings (fetch block in init.ps1, awaiting the user's OK to download), (2) census on UBL invoice / NF-e 4.00 / CFDI 4.0, then this sketch becomes the design note.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 3u32, "2026-10-31T22:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 18:08 fiscal: MILESTONE 1, EN 16931 HALF DONE (the user lifted the download gate 10-31 ~18:00: 'stop asking for my oks for things like downloads'). (1) SOURCE pinned in scripts/init.ps1: OpenPeppol peppol-bis-invoice-3 v3.0.20 structure/syntax, ubl-invoice.xml + ubl-creditnote.xml AND their 16 transitively included part/*.xml files (the first version of the block fetched only the 2 top files; the guard now tests the part folder, so CI and existing trees pick the parts up). (2) TOOL scripts/en16931-terms.ps1 walks the nested <Element> tree (each part's root is itself an Element) and writes canon/en16931-terms.json: 160 business terms + 30 groups, each with id, name, data type, cardinality (default 1..1) and its UBL path per document (ubl-invoice / ubl-creditnote); combined references (BT-31, BT-32 on one element) split into separate rows with their names. Spot checks: BT-1 ubl:Invoice/cbc:ID [1..1]; BT-31 .../cac:AccountingSupplierParty/cac:Party/cac:PartyTaxScheme/cbc:CompanyID; BG-24 [0..n]; BG-25 INVOICE LINE [1..n]. LEFT for milestone 1: Peppol PINT's added terms (fetch the PINT structure the same way), then milestone 2 (mapping census for UBL invoice, NF-e 4.00, CFDI 4.0 against this inventory). 0 -> 10.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 4u32, "2026-11-01T12:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:43 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P1 epic: the canon is what makes fiscal generic (one semantic model over every country''s syntax) rather than 40 unrelated generators.\nDONE WHEN (milestone 1): (a) src/canon.spi (PS1 port 1, drafted in scratchpad canon-port) writes canon/en16931-terms.json from Spiral, 160 terms and 30 groups, equal field by field (ConvertFrom-Json) to the PowerShell output it replaces; (b) a coverage table per family (target/ci-metrics/canon-coverage.tsv): for each EN 16931 term, whether the family''s generated type has a typed accessor for it; UBL Invoice and CreditNote reach 100% of the mandatory (1..1) terms; (c) PINT-only terms added with their source.\nNEXT STEP: after the e3 round, re-derive canon.spi in edition-3 spelling, add it to src package modules, gate it on the node, and diff its JSON with the PS output.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: term ids are nominals, not \"BT-12\" strings: \":! bt_id = i32\" and \":! bg_id = i32\", parsed once at the structure boundary. A GADT indexed by what a term holds: \":| ^ canon_term kind = | Term :: { id : bt_id; name : string; data_type : canon_type } -> canon_term value | Group :: { id : bg_id; name : string; members : list (exists k. canon_term k) } -> canon_term group\". Groups hold existentially quantified members. data_type is a union (\":| canon_type = | Amount | Quantity | Text | Code | Identifier | Date | Percentage | BinaryObject\"), never the raw \"Amount\" string. A family binding is a prototype \":+ term_value family\" from a canon term to an option of the family''s typed field, using XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS'' field GADT as the reflection layer, so coverage is computed from types, not grepped paths. The draft canon.spi uses a term_row record with a group : bool and string ids; that is the pass-1 port, and it is rewritten onto this model in milestone 2 (said here so nobody builds on the bool). MODEL: mega_omniledger_erp_kernel (ledger terms as indexed families) and xsd.spi''s GADT.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 5u32, "2026-11-01T18:40Z", "fiscal", "Term table landed as typed Spiral: src/canon.spi (term_row record, en16931_terms) replaces scripts/en16931-terms.ps1; gate 1/1 on node, JSON equal to the walker (190 rows, 0 diffs). See PS1-TO-SPIRAL note of 11-01. Draft copies archived: kit archive run 20261101-143904. Next step: widen term_row by the Peppol PINT layer (rules 70/assertions 170 already read by corpus_checks pint_rules_read_fully) and give term_row a phantom document-kind index.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 6u32, "2026-11-01T19:47Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 15:47: TYPEFEATURESET step on src/canon.spi (unstaged, sha 822014D1717E). The term identity is now a union \":| term_id = | BusinessTerm : i32 | BusinessGroup : i32\" instead of \"id : string\" + \"group : bool\". Two fields that had to agree are now one value, so a group/term mismatch cannot be represented. The ID is parsed once (term_id_of via sm'::decimal_i32, None on malformed input), and ordering matches on the union instead of re-parsing digits with the old index_of trick, which gave garbage on non-digits. The placeholder template record (id = \"\") is gone: add_terms builds each row whole. Node gate: 1/1, 0 type errors, x-compat 0, JSON BYTE-IDENTICAL to before (9DBC4B63F0CA), so the refactor changed the model, not the output. Next: phantom document-kind index on term_row (invoice vs creditnote UBL paths), then the PINT widening.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 7u32, "2026-11-01T20:58Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 16:57: second typed step on src/canon.spi (sha 1CA241F20E1C, unstaged). UBL documents are a union \":| ubl_document = | UblInvoice | UblCreditNote\" instead of the strings \"ubl-invoice\"/\"ubl-creditnote\" threaded through 6 functions. term_row::ubl is list (ubl_document * string). The string exists only at the edges: ubl_document_name for the structure file name and the JSON key. Node gate: 1/1, 0 type errors, x-compat 0, JSON byte-identical again (9DBC4B63F0CA). Remaining typed step: a phantom index tying each UBL path to its document kind (path ubl_document), worth it once a consumer selects paths per document.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 8u32, "2026-11-02T16:04Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 12:04 typefeatureset survey: 'every family as a typed projection with measured loss' is a higher-kinded shape. project \\* (f : * -> *) {loss} (doc : family_doc) : f canon_doc, with f = identity for an exact family and f = with_losses (a canon_doc plus the list of dropped terms) for a lossy one, so measured loss is in the type rather than a side count. fiscal has 0 HKT uses today (lib 1.3 per kloc; tibia views.spi:8 decide_all is the in-house example). First child: FISCAL-CANON-TYPED-TERMS.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 9u32, "2026-11-02T19:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 15:25 fiscal: RE-PINNED ON PACK17 (core E556D773EB123175, job-1793647287613-fiscal-canon17, node t1102): canon 2/2 and en16931-terms.json 9DBC4B63F0CA (52,597 bytes) byte-identical to the pre-typing baseline, so the typed term_row (data_type union, presence/bound cardinality, ubl_path nominal) holds on pack17. A first run in job-1793646614590 died with os error 3 because mirror t1102 lacked deps/corpus (VOID, environment); t1102 now has deps junctions to t1101.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 10u32, "2026-11-03T21:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 17:00 fiscal: FIRST HKT IN FISCAL (the 11-02 survey's plan, n?: 'every family as a typed projection with measured loss is a higher-kinded shape'), unstaged in fiscal src/document.spi 198816DD: views ':! exact a = a' and ':! with_losses a = a * list string' with prototypes ':? content f a : f a -> a' and ':? losses f a : f a -> list string' (instances per view, the lib fixed_views 'mapped' pattern), and 'measured \\* (f : * -> *) {content; losses}. (view : f canon_document) : bool * i32' (BT-109 + BT-110 = BT-112 on the content, plus the loss count), written once for any view. Projections: exactly (manual_invoice -> exact canon_document, no loss) and receipt_view (a new cash_receipt family with no buyer -> with_losses canon_document, losing BT-44), so a family's loss is in its projection's TYPE, not a side count. Tests: a_projection_carries_its_measured_loss_in_its_type ((true, 0) exact, (true, 1) receipt, losses = [BT-44]); negative an_option_is_not_a_measured_view fails 'does not have the prototype content' (europa: option has neither content nor losses; a bare record gives only a structural Unification failure, so the option case is the one that proves the prototype guard). PROVEN on europa (pack27): check with bodies exit 0, all 3 negatives exit 5, 3 Rust bodies exit 0; p2p and posting re-checked against it exit 0. The confirm-landed2 node job now gates this version (document 6/6). NEXT: generated-family instances (exact for NF-e/UBL/CFDI where every core term maps; with_losses with the measured dropped terms otherwise).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 11u32, "2026-11-05T14:29Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:4x local fiscal: MILESTONE 1(b) MEASURED + a canon cardinality defect found. (1) COVERAGE (scratch walk, no runs: each term's UBL path from canon/en16931-terms.json followed step by step through the generated units' field GADT cases, <Owner>Type_field_<ns>_<Element> :: x_<owner>_type_field (<child>), wrapped cases and namespace-qualified owners like CommonAggregateComponents_2_LocationType included): generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 reaches 190/190 terms with a typed field at every step; generated_ubl_creditnote_2_1 reaches 189/190, the gap being BT-11 Project reference, which the Peppol credit-note structure does not bind at all (no BT-11 reference in ubl-creditnote.xml or its parts). So DoD (b)'s 'UBL Invoice and CreditNote reach 100% of the mandatory terms' already holds by measurement; what is left for (b) is emitting it as target/ci-metrics/canon-coverage.tsv from Spiral. (2) DEFECT: the JSON's cardinality is the element's OWN attribute (default 1..1), not the term's: cbc:ID of BT-11 is 1..1 inside cac:ProjectReference 0..1, so BT-11 read as required. Of 160 BT rows, 79 read 1..1 but only 24 are required once ancestors count (BT-1 2 3 5 23 24 27 34 40 44 49 55 106 109 110 111 112 115 126 129 131 146 151 153, the Peppol BIS binding's mandatory core); 33 rows with the groups. FIX (in place, unstaged; backup canon.before-effective-8F34F43B.spi): term_row gains effective : cardinality, computed while walking (within outer own: required only if every step is, bounds multiply, n absorbs), threaded through visit_element / read_children / read_child / included_terms from exactly_once at the Document root; the JSON keeps 'cardinality' (own) and adds 'effective'. Tests: en16931_terms_are_written_to_the_canon now also pins 24 required terms and BT-11 (1..1 own, 0..1 effective); new a_cardinality_within_its_ancestors_is_their_product. Box: format clean, --check exit 0 (58 s, --timeout-ms under box load 100%). PENDING on EUROPA: eff-1793888925 (self-contained stage D55AD9D1 = box core + box lib + fiscal src + the Peppol structure, pinned copy of europa's installed compiler): check, all bodies to Rust, rustc -O under a 2200M scope, run, and the regenerated JSON fetched back for a field diff vs the committed one.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 12u32, "2026-11-05T14:34Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:5x local fiscal: EFFECTIVE CARDINALITY PROVEN on EUROPA (eff-1793888925; self-contained stage D55AD9D1 = box core + box lib + fiscal src incl. canon.spi 39CE1621 + the Peppol structure; pinned copy of europa's installed compiler, core dc49ffdc170199df): --check exit 0, 5 bodies compiled to Rust exit 0, rustc -O exit 0 (2200M scope), run exit 0 ('en16931 terms: 160 terms, 30 groups'). MUTANT (24 -> 23 in the pin, eff-mut1793889158): run exit 1 with exactly '24 business terms are required once their optional ancestors count', so the harness fails when a pin is wrong. OUTPUT: the regenerated JSON EF0D3594 (56,207 bytes) equals the committed one field by field apart from the new 'effective' (190 rows, 0 differing via ConvertFrom-Json), its effective values agree 190/190 with an independent scratch walker of the structure files, and with the effective fields stripped it is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the 11-02 Spiral baseline 9DBC4B63F0CA (52,597 bytes; +3,610 = 190 x 19 bytes for ',\"effective\":\"x..y\"'). Required: 24 BT, 33 rows. NOTE: the committed canon/en16931-terms.json (70,842 bytes, pretty-printed, CRLF) is not the Spiral writer's output byte-wise (compact, LF), and CI's drift check covers only generated/, so it is left untouched; the canon test rewrites it on every run. Node Cells confirmation follows in the queued job-1793886615820 (that job carries the pre-effective canon from the nameof zip; the effective version needs its own Cells run after it).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 13u32, "2026-11-05T14:37Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:0x local fiscal: NEXT for DoD (b), the Spiral half (the measurement is done and needs no generated-text parsing): canon walks each term's UBL path through the resolved UBL 2.1 schema set (maindoc UBL-Invoice-2.1.xsd / UBL-CreditNote-2.1.xsd + the CommonAggregate/CommonBasic imports in deps/corpus/eu/ubl21), the same model xsd_emit generates the field GADT cases from, and writes target/ci-metrics/canon-coverage.tsv (term, document, own, effective, reached, first missing step). It should reuse the generator's schema-set loading rather than a second resolver, and land as a canon test pinned to today's scratch numbers: invoice 190/190, credit note 189/190 (BT-11 unbound), required 24 BT / 33 rows. Progress 30 -> 35 (term table typed + effective cardinality proven; coverage measured; TSV emission, PINT terms (c), and milestones 2-4 open).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 14u32, "2026-11-05T14:40Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:1x local fiscal: RESEARCH for milestone 1(c), PINT's added terms (web, no downloads). Current release: Peppol PINT BIS Billing 1.1.3 (release date 5 Jun 2026, breadcrumb on docs.peppol.eu/poac/pint/pint/). Unlike BIS 3, OpenPeppol publishes NO machine-readable structure for PINT: no structure/syntax XML on the docs site, no public GitHub repo found, and the resources.zip that scripts/init.ps1 already pins (corpus eu/peppol-pint) holds only codelists (14 per transaction), the preprocessed schematron (.sch/.xslt) and 4 PDFs. Terms are IBT-nnn / IBG-nn (+ suffixed sub-terms like IBT-018-1, IBT-031-1); roughly 195 base IBT + ~27 sub-IBT + 37 IBG (hand tally of the semantic-model page); each syntax node shows cardinality and its UBL element, and the full path is only encoded in the node's link slug (e.g. cac-AccountingSupplierParty/cac-Party/cbc-EndpointID). The semantic model marks terms Shared / Aligned / blank, NOT 'PINT-only' (Aligned examples: IBT-168 issue time, IBT-178 payment instructions id, IBT-187 terms payment instructions id, IBT-200 tax inclusive pricing). OPTIONS for (c): (1) pin the syntax page docs.peppol.eu/poac/pint/pint/trn-invoice/syntax/ (and trn-creditnote) in init.ps1 like resources.zip, and read term id + slug path + cardinality from its node links in canon.spi (HTML, so a narrow reader over the anchor list, not xml::read_xml); (2) the schematron already in the corpus names IBT ids in its assertions, but only for asserted terms, so it cannot be the inventory. (1) is the only complete source; the IBT <-> BT mapping is by number for the EN 16931 core (IBT-001 = BT-1) and 'PINT additions' = IBT numbers with no BT row in canon/en16931-terms.json.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 15u32, "2026-11-05T14:53Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:5x local fiscal: SECOND CANON DEFECT FIXED, found while measuring PINT: canon dropped every term bound to an XML ATTRIBUTE, because read_child visited only <Element> and <Include>, never <Attribute>. In the Peppol BIS 3 structure that is BT-82 Payment means text (cbc:PaymentMeansCode/@name, usage=Optional) and BT-130 Invoiced quantity unit of measure (cbc:InvoicedQuantity/@unitCode and CreditedQuantity/@unitCode in the credit note), so the '160 terms' count was 2 short (the other gaps in BT-1..165 are BT-4, which EN 16931 does not define, and BT-21, which BIS 3 does not bind). FIX (in place, unstaged; backup canon.before-attributes-39CE1621.spi): read_child gains an Attribute arm -> attribute_terms (defined ahead of the visit_element mutual group so the group stays one), path '<parent>/@<term>', own cardinality 0..1 for usage=Optional else 1..1, effective through within as for elements. canon.spi 39CE1621 -> 052142D9 (formatted). Pins: 162 terms / 30 groups, 25 required BT (BT-130 is 1..n under the lines), BT-130's two paths and 1..n. PROVEN on EUROPA (eff-a1793890196): check exit 0, 5 bodies, rustc -O, run exit 0 ('162 terms, 30 groups'); JSON 60FA5155 (56,780 bytes) = the previous EF0D3594 plus exactly 2 rows (BT-82, BT-130), 0 rows changed, effective 192/192 equal to the independent scratch walker. MUTANT eff-m1793890196 (Attribute arm disabled): run exit 1 with exactly the 162-terms message, and its JSON is EF0D3594 byte for byte, so the arm is the only change. The node job-1793886615820 (still queued) now carries this src (zip 35B5A52D) for the Cells confirmation.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 16u32, "2026-11-05T15:07Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:1x local fiscal: MILESTONE 1(c) DONE AS DATA: PINT terms read from Spiral. (1) SOURCE pinned in scripts/init.ps1 (edited in place, unstaged; backup init.before-pint-syntax-8BEE0062.ps1): new block deps/corpus/eu/peppol-pint/syntax/ fetches the PINT Billing 1.1.3 syntax pages for trn-invoice and trn-creditnote from docs.peppol.eu with SHA256 pins (0B3DE3A6..., 066108AB...; byte-stable across fetches, Last-Modified 7 Sep 2026), own guard so existing trees pick it up; the box corpus has both files at those hashes. (2) NEW src module pint_terms.spi 46C57FC7 (unstaged): pint_id = PintTerm : i32 * option i32 (IBT-034-1 = sub-term 1) | PintGroup : i32; pint_row { id; name; slug; own; semantic; effective } read by a narrow scanner over the page's '<tr id=SB-...>' rows (6 cells: id, semantic cardinality, name, syntax cardinality; the href slug is the path); effective = canon::within (parent slug's effective) own, so PINT terms get the same effective cardinality as the EN 16931 rows; slug steps decode cac-X -> cac:X, cac-X-1 -> cac:X[1] (PINT's numbered variants), bare -> @attribute. 'Additions' = base IBT numbers with no BT row in canon's table. Tests: a_slug_step_becomes_its_ubl_name; pint_invoice_terms_are_read_from_the_syntax_page (362 rows = 195 IBT + 24 sub-terms + 36 IBG + 107 structural; 33 additions incl. IBT-168 issue time, not IBT-130), which writes canon/pint-terms.json (source, 255 terms with semantic / own / effective / ubl path, additions). PROVEN on EUROPA eff-p1793891012: run exit 0, JSON A1E99F94 (47,075 bytes) equal in all 6 fields for all 255 terms to an independent scratch parser, same 33 additions; MUTANT eff-q1793891012 ([n] -> (n)) run exit 1 with exactly the slug-test message. Found on the way: --check passed while the Rust body compile failed with ETY-ValueRestriction (listm::length fed straight to the polymorphic obj_to_string has no fixed result type), fixed by binding the counts as list i32. canon/pint-terms.json placed (new, unstaged). Node Cells confirmation queued in job-1793886615820 (pint_terms added; script 08F02E06, zip AE4FC438). LEFT for (c): the credit-note page is pinned but not yet read (same reader, root ubl:CreditNote).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 17u32, "2026-11-05T15:16Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:2x local fiscal: (c) now covers BOTH PINT transactions. pint_terms.spi DF1AAA83 (unstaged; supersedes 46C57FC7 of the previous note): pages keyed by canon::ubl_document (transaction_of = 'trn-' + case label, root_of = 'ubl:' + case name without Ubl; canon's ubl_document_name made public for the JSON keys, canon.spi 052142D9 -> 32B2BFA1, visibility only), document_terms per document, merged_terms (one row per id, invoice order first), and canon/pint-terms.json now has the EN 16931 file's shape with the syntax binding PER DOCUMENT: { id, name, semantic, ubl: { ubl-invoice: { path, cardinality, effective }, ubl-creditnote: {...} } } + additions. Per-document cardinality is needed: IBT-009 Payment due date binds once at cbc:DueDate (0..1) in the invoice but under cac:PaymentMeans (0..n) in the credit note. Credit-note tree: 357 rows (191 IBT, 24 sub-terms, 35 IBG), 250 terms, none absent from the invoice; invoice-only: the prepaid-payment group IBG-35 with IBT-179..182. New test pint_terms_are_written_to_the_canon (250 / 255 and IBT-009's credit-note binding). PROVEN on EUROPA eff-p1793891601: 3 bodies, rustc -O, run exit 0; JSON AF1E89EC (87,862 bytes) with 0 field differences over 255 terms and both documents' bindings vs the independent scratch parser, 33 additions equal. MUTANT eff-q1793891601 (merge without the id check): run exit 1 with exactly the '250 credit-note terms ... 255 in all' message. Found on the way: a lambda whose body is a tuple, once the formatter breaks it over lines, typed as a field-access tuple (Unification .slug vs .effective); a named local function with parenthesized tuple fixed it. canon/pint-terms.json replaced with AF1E89EC (my own A1E99F94 was the only prior copy). Node job-1793886615820 still queued, zip 651CCD8B carries this src. Milestone 1 (c) DONE pending Cells; (b)'s TSV emission is what is left of milestone 1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 18u32, "2026-11-05T15:19Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:2x local fiscal: PROBE for (b)'s Spiral coverage walk (scratch module, europa eff-u1793891935, not in the repo): lib xsd_resolve::load_schema_tree on deps/corpus/eu/ubl21/maindoc/UBL-Invoice-2.1.xsd loads and finalizes the whole UBL set (complex type names include the generator's collision forms, e.g. CommonAggregateComponents-2_LocationType / CommonBasicComponents-2_LocationType). But InvoiceType's content items are element REFERENCES: tag text keeps the document prefix (cbc:ID, cac:AccountingSupplierParty) with type_ref None, while the global elements in schema::elements carry UNPREFIXED names with their types (WitnessParty : PartyType). So a walk must resolve each ns:Local reference to the global element OF THAT NAMESPACE, and schema::elements has lost the namespace exactly where cac and cbc both define a local name (Location, and others the generator disambiguates). DESIGN for the next step: either (i) keep the namespace on global elements in xsd_resolve (a lib change: element tag as the qualified {uri}local or the prefixed form, with a lib test), or (ii) walk the generator's own per-type field model, the one xsd_emit turns into the <Owner>Type_field_<ns>_<Element> GADT cases, so coverage measures exactly the generated types. (ii) avoids a second resolver and matches the DoD's wording ('measured from the generated types'); it needs xsd_emit to expose its field list per type. Medium, not light: left for a planned window. Also seen: the probe's first console line (a list i32 of counts) did not print while the next ones did; not chased (scratch only).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 19u32, "2026-11-05T15:23Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:3x local fiscal: (b) option (ii) located. The field list per generated type already exists inside lib xsd_emit (live AB4B0165): the Writing prototype instance builds one witness { case; t; field; fragment } per element (element_witness, xsd_emit.spi ~2199), choice (choice_witness) and any (any_witness) of each owner type, and witness_union prints them as the '<Owner>_field r' GADT cases (~1875). So the lib change for (ii) is a public 'type_witnesses schema : list (owner * list witness)' (or a describe instance of the same prototypes) with a lib test, after which canon walks term paths owner -> witness field -> witness t, exactly the generated types. Sequence it AFTER the facet window (it touches xsd_emit, which that window replaces with D00BE390). Pre-checks for that window done now, all matching the plan: live lib xsd_emit AB4B0165 (base), sentinel draft D00BE390 = the split plus facet+sentinel (+217/-47 vs live; +1207/-707 vs the pre-split 5B274B48 undo copy, live itself +1024/-694), live families E6AC72B3 / generator 03111A90, src2 families 8F72669F / generator 6ADC38CB.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 20u32, "2026-11-05T15:53Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:5x local fiscal: GRANULAR on today's fiscal src changes (europa ~/cell-budget/cell-budget --granular, kit's nominal-constructor rule; a finding anchored at a '///> rust' line is a test block). Before (this morning's backups): canon 2 code overages (read_child 287, term_json 279). Today's additions had raised them (read_child 444 with the Attribute arm, term_json 347 with 'effective') and pint_terms had 3 of its own (row_of 491, step_text 284, binding_json 329). SPLIT: canon read_child now matches a typed ':| structure_part = IncludePart | ElementPart | AttributePart | OtherPart' from structure_part_of / tagged_part (the tag tests in one place, outside the visit_element mutual group); term_json takes cardinality_fields; pint_terms gets row_record, is_prefixed / prefixed_step / variant_suffix, binding_object. AFTER: canon 0 code overages (was 2), pint_terms 0, corpus_checks / reports / document code findings unchanged (their only new findings are my test blocks). Behaviour unchanged, re-proven on europa eff-cn1793893886 / eff-pt1793893886: run exit 0 and the regenerated JSONs are BYTE-IDENTICAL to before the split (en16931-terms 60FA5155, pint-terms AF1E89EC), no ParserErrors. canon.spi E0900687, pint_terms.spi 9EFD3E4B, formatted. Node zip re-shipped while job-1793886615820 is still queued.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 21u32, "2026-11-05T15:55Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:5x local fiscal: README updated in place (unstaged; backup in the session scratchpad): the outputs list says en16931-terms.json carries own + effective cardinality and adds canon/pint-terms.json (PINT 1.1.3 IBT/IBG terms with invoice and credit-note bindings, plus the PINT-only additions); the file table adds src/pint_terms.spi (PINT terms from the published syntax trees pinned by scripts/init.ps1). New untracked files for the user's commit: src/pint_terms.spi, canon/pint-terms.json; edited: src/canon.spi, scripts/init.ps1, README.md.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 22u32, "2026-11-05T16:50Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:4x local fiscal: MILESTONE 1 (b) DONE IN SPIRAL: new src module canon_coverage.spi 75E13DC3 (unstaged; README file table updated). It loads the UBL 2.1 maindoc schema through lib xsd_resolve::load_schema_tree, dereferences element references with the PUBLIC lib xsd_emit::dereferenced_parts (the same step the generator takes before emitting the field GADTs, so no second resolver and no generated-text parsing), and walks every canon term's UBL path: element steps by local name to their type_ref, @attribute steps through own attributes and the Derived base chain (BT-130's unitCode lives on the CCTS QuantityType base). ':| reach = Reached | MissingStep : string | Unbound'. Test every_ubl_term_is_reached_in_the_generated_types writes target/ci-metrics/canon-coverage.tsv (Term, Document, Effective, Reach; 384 rows) and pins: invoice 0 misses over all 192 terms, credit note 1 miss = 'BT-11 unbound'; a_path_reaches_through_references_and_attribute_bases pins one reference path, one inherited attribute and one undeclared element. EUROPA: compile, rustc, run exit 0 ('misses (invoice, credit note): 0, 1'), no ParserErrors, under two compiler builds (core dc49ffdc170199df, then the newer installed 6b7af90b041bfc78). MUTANT (no base chain for attributes): run exit 1 with exactly 'an element reference and an inherited attribute are both reached'. GRANULAR 0 code overages (walk split into attribute_reach / next_owner / missing_at, own_attributes into attribute_name). Added to the queued node Cells job-1793886615820. With (a) the typed term table and (c) PINT, MILESTONE 1 IS COMPLETE pending the node Cells run; milestones 2-4 (mapping census for NF-e / CFDI, design, generated to_canon / of_canon) open.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 23u32, "2026-11-05T17:15Z", "fiscal", "11-05 13:0x local fiscal: MILESTONE 2 STARTED (mapping census), NF-e 4.00 first. (1) canon_coverage.spi B303959A generalized: schema_model_of (path) for any schema, and the walk now goes over type DEFINITIONS (element_hit { type_ref; inline }), so inline local types (NF-e's ide / det / prod) and named ones (TEnderEmi) both resolve, and a final step only needs the element to be declared (NF-e leaves are simple types). UBL result unchanged (misses 0 / 1). (2) NEW src/canon_nfe.spi AF1D9965: a typed binding table (canon::term_id * NF-e path), 29 rows in header / seller / buyer / totals / line / item tables: BT-1 ide/nNF, BT-2 ide/dhEmi, BT-9 cobr/dup/dVenc, BT-22 infAdic/infCpl, BT-27/28/30/35/37/38/39 emit (xNome, xFant, CNPJ, enderEmit xLgr/xMun/CEP/UF), BT-44/47/50/52/53/54 dest, BT-106 ICMSTot/vProd, BT-107 vDesc, BT-112 vNF, BT-115 cobr/fat/vLiq, BT-126 det/@nItem, BT-129..131 / 146 / 153 / 157 / 158 det/prod (qCom, uCom, vProd, vUnCom, xProd, cEAN, NCM). Terms needing a conversion or a computation are deliberately not bound (BT-40/55 country: NF-e's cPais is a BACEN code, not ISO 3166; BT-110: a sum of NF-e tax totals; BT-5: BRL is implicit). Tests: every_nfe_binding_reaches_a_declared_field (all 29 reach a declared field of deps/corpus/DFe.NET/.../nfe_v4.00.xsd, and an undeclared field is not reached) and nfe_supplies_13_of_the_25_required_terms; it prints the required terms NF-e lacks: BT-3, 5, 23, 24, 34, 40, 49, 55, 109, 110, 111, 151 -- these are milestone 3's design input (derived terms vs per-regime extension groups vs loss). EUROPA: both modules compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors (compiler core e9c77ce35244454d); GRANULAR 0 code overages in both after splits (leaf_reach / step_reach / rooted_reach; binding tables split by role). README updated; both added to the queued node Cells job-1793886615820 (zip F3A9F370). NEXT: the same census for CFDI 4.0.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 24u32, "2026-11-05T17:47Z", "fiscal", "11-05 13:4x local fiscal: MILESTONE 2 census for the three unlike families DONE (UBL, NF-e, CFDI). Shared census helpers moved into canon_coverage.spi ACE8AA44 (is_bound, is_required_term, required_ids, unreached_terms, absent_required) and used by canon_nfe EAB79CB1 and the NEW src/canon_cfdi.spi 93277719: 20 typed bindings against deps/corpus/mx/cfdi/cfdv40.xsd, all attributes of the inline Comprobante tree (BT-1 @Folio, BT-2 @Fecha, BT-5 @Moneda, BT-25 CfdiRelacionados/CfdiRelacionado/@UUID, BT-27/31 Emisor @Nombre/@Rfc, BT-44/48 Receptor @Nombre/@Rfc, BT-53 Receptor/@DomicilioFiscalReceptor, BT-106 @SubTotal, BT-107 @Descuento, BT-110 Impuestos/@TotalImpuestosTrasladados, BT-112 @Total, BT-129/130/131/146/153/155/158 Conceptos/Concepto @Cantidad/@ClaveUnidad/@Importe/@ValorUnitario/@Descripcion/@NoIdentificacion/@ClaveProdServ; LugarExpedicion deliberately NOT bound as the seller's post code: it is the place of issue). Tests every_cfdi_binding_reaches_a_declared_field (+ an undeclared attribute is not reached) and cfdi_supplies_13_of_the_25_required_terms. RESULT, the design input for milestone 3: UBL Invoice reaches 192/192 terms (credit note 191, BT-11 unbound); NF-e 4.00 and CFDI 4.0 each bind 13 of the 25 required terms directly. Absent in BOTH: BT-3 (type code: NF-e finNFe / CFDI TipoDeComprobante use national code lists), BT-23 / BT-24 (process and specification ids: none), BT-34 / BT-49 (electronic addresses: none), BT-40 / BT-55 (country: NF-e BACEN code, CFDI implicit MX), BT-109 / BT-111 (totals without tax / tax in accounting currency: derived), BT-151 (VAT category code: national tax codes). NF-e only lacks BT-5 (BRL implicit) and BT-110 (a sum of ICMS/IPI/... totals); CFDI only lacks BT-115 (no amount due) and BT-126 (no line number). So milestone 3 needs: per-regime code-list mappings (BT-3, BT-151, BT-40/55), derived terms (BT-109, BT-111, NF-e BT-110), implied constants (BT-5 for NF-e, BT-40 MX), and a typed 'not carried' loss for BT-23/24/34/49. EUROPA: all three modules compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors (core e9c77ce35244454d); GRANULAR 0 code overages in all three. README updated; added to the queued node Cells job-1793886615820 (zip 7A479E39). Progress 60 -> 65.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 25u32, "2026-11-05T18:03Z", "fiscal", "11-05 14:0x local fiscal: MILESTONE 3 first piece, BT-3 from the national document types. NEW src/canon_codes.spi 8E10BAB0 (unstaged; README updated): ':| invoice_type = CommercialInvoice | CreditNote | DebitNote' with its UNTDID 1001 codes 380 / 381 / 383; ':| cfdi_voucher = Ingreso | Egreso | Traslado | Nomina | Pago' (I/E/T/N/P) and ':| nfe_purpose = NormalIssue | Complementary | Adjustment | GoodsReturn | CreditNoteIssue | DebitNoteIssue' (1..6) as code tables; cfdi_invoice_type / nfe_invoice_type map to option invoice_type (I -> 380, E -> 381; NF-e 1 -> 380, 4 and 5 -> 381, 6 -> 383; complementar / ajuste / traslado / nomina / pago carry no EN 16931 invoice type: None, a typed loss, not a guess); generic code_of / of_code / bt3_of. Test the_national_code_lists_are_the_schemas_own reads the enumerations FROM THE SCHEMAS (catCFDI.xsd c_TipoDeComprobante; nfe_v4.00.xsd -> TFinNFe) and requires the unions to list exactly them. FINDING it made on its first run: the generator's leiauteNFe_v4.00.xsd TFinNFe has SIX values, not four (5 = Nota de credito, 6 = Nota de debito, the 2025 tax-reform additions next to tpNFDebito / tpNFCredito; the enumeration annotation still says 1-4, the finNFe element's documentation lists all six), while the Homologacao and prod_ copies still list four. Test bt_3_comes_from_each_regimes_document_type pins all eleven mappings and an unknown code. EUROPA (core e9c77ce35244454d): compile, rustc, run exit 0 (the first run exited 1 with exactly 'nfe_purpose lists TFinNFe: 1,2,3,4,5,6', i.e. the schema check is live), no ParserErrors; GRANULAR 0 code overages. Added to the queued node Cells job-1793886615820 (zip 97B2C4D9).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 26u32, "2026-11-05T18:12Z", "fiscal", "11-05 14:1x local fiscal: MILESTONE 3 second piece, IMPLIED regime constants (terms a regime fixes instead of writing): canon_nfe 0AD26B89 nfe_implied = BT-5 BRL (NF-e amounts are in reais) and BT-40 BR (the issuer is a Brazilian taxpayer); canon_cfdi 22A058FE cfdi_implied = BT-40 MX (CFDI already carries BT-5 as @Moneda, so nothing implied there). Tests nfe_implies_its_currency_and_seller_country / cfdi_implies_its_seller_country: an implied term is never one the binding table carries, and with them NF-e supplies 15 and CFDI 14 of the 25 required terms. EUROPA: 3 bodies each, compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; GRANULAR 0 code overages. Left for milestone 3: code-list mappings BT-151 (NF-e CST / CFDI ObjetoImp + TipoFactor -> UNCL5305), BT-55 (NF-e BACEN cPais, CFDI ISO-3 ResidenciaFiscal -> ISO 3166-1 alpha-2), derived BT-109 / BT-111 / NF-e BT-110, a typed 'not carried' for BT-23 / 24 / 34 / 49, then the canon projection design. Node zip re-shipped while job-1793886615820 is still queued.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 27u32, "2026-11-05T18:27Z", "fiscal", "11-05 14:3x local fiscal: MILESTONE 3 third piece, the gap analysis is now TYPED AND COMPLETE. canon_coverage 1DEF40F8 adds ':| gap = NotCarried | Derived | NationalCode : string' with ids_of / gap_ids / unaccounted. canon_nfe B78573E2: nfe_gaps = BT-3 NationalCode finNFe (mapped by canon_codes), BT-55 NationalCode 'cPais (BACEN)', BT-151 NationalCode CST, BT-23 / 24 / 34 / 49 NotCarried, BT-109 / 110 / 111 Derived. canon_cfdi 8014BB35: BT-3 TipoDeComprobante, BT-55 c_Pais, BT-151 ObjetoImp, BT-23 / 24 / 34 / 49 NotCarried, BT-109 / 111 / 115 / 126 Derived. Tests every_required_term_is_bound_implied_or_a_typed_gap_in_nfe / _in_cfdi: each of the 25 required terms is accounted EXACTLY ONCE by bindings + implied constants + gaps (NF-e 13 + 2 + 10, CFDI 13 + 1 + 11). EUROPA: 4 bodies per module, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; MUTANT (BT-151 dropped from nfe_gaps): run exit 1 with exactly 'each required term is accounted exactly once for NF-e: BT-151'. GRANULAR 0 code overages in all three (two first findings were blank lines missing between my inserted defs, which the counter reads as one block). Node zip E697C543 re-shipped while job-1793886615820 is still queued. Milestone 3 now has its typed inputs; left: the canon projection design (to_canon / of_canon per family over these tables) and the code-list conversions behind the NationalCode gaps.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 28u32, "2026-11-05T18:31Z", "fiscal", "11-05 14:3x local fiscal: MILESTONE 3 DESIGN, the canon projection, built on today's typed tables (for review before code). (1) WHAT A FAMILY PROVIDES is already data per family: bindings (term_id * path, each proven to reach a declared field of its schema), implied constants (term_id * value) and gaps (term_id * gap), with a test that the three account for every required term exactly once. (2) THE PROJECTION is per family 'to_canon : family_doc -> with_losses canon_document', generated from those tables, not hand-written per term: each binding becomes a typed read through the family's generated accessor (the same <Owner>_field GADT case canon_coverage walks to), each implied constant a literal, each gap a typed loss entry; document.spi's existing 'with_losses' HKT view (measured loss in the type) is the carrier, so loss is counted, never silent. (3) GAPS GET A RESOLVER EACH, by kind: NationalCode n -> a typed code mapping like canon_codes (BT-3 done for finNFe and TipoDeComprobante; next BT-151 from NF-e CST / CFDI ObjetoImp + TipoFactor to UNCL5305, BT-55 from BACEN cPais / CFDI c_Pais alpha-3 to ISO 3166 alpha-2, both needing a pinned code table in deps/corpus), Derived -> a formula over already-projected terms with its own law test (BT-109 = BT-106 - BT-107 + BT-108; BT-111 = BT-110 when one currency; NF-e BT-110 = sum of ICMSTot taxes; CFDI BT-115 = BT-112 - BT-113; BT-126 = line position), NotCarried -> stays a loss forever, named in the report. (4) of_canon (the reverse) only for UBL first, since its 192/192 coverage makes it lossless by construction; NF-e and CFDI reverse needs the NationalCode resolvers to be bijective, which BT-3 is not (complementar / ajuste have no UNTDID code), so their reverse projections return result _ (list missing) as planned in the 10-30 sketch. (5) PROOF per family stays the read-back rule: every real document of the family projects with exactly its pinned loss list. Order: BT-109 / 111 formulas (pure, light) -> BT-151 / 55 tables (need pinned code lists) -> generator emission of to_canon from the tables (heavy: regen + gates, a node window).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 29u32, "2026-11-05T18:44Z", "fiscal", "11-05 14:5x local fiscal: MILESTONE 3 fourth piece, the first DERIVED resolver with a real-document law. NEW src/canon_derived.spi (unstaged; README updated): bt109 lines allowances charges = lines - allowances + charges, reconciles bt109 bt110 bt112 = (bt109 + bt110 = bt112), and a typed CFDI totals reader (cfdi_totals { subtotal; discount; taxes; total } from Comprobante @SubTotal / @Descuento / @Total and Impuestos/@TotalImpuestosTrasladados). Tests: bt_109_is_lines_minus_allowances_plus_charges (1000.00 - 25.00 + 10.00 = 985.00; 985.00 + 189.15 = 1174.15 reconciles, one cent off does not) and a_stamped_cfdi_reconciles_through_its_derived_bt_109 on the corpus's real stamped CFDI (mx/stamped/cfdiutils-cfdi40-valid.xml): BT-109 = 3824.15 - 956.04 = 2868.11 and 2868.11 + 458.90 = 3327.01 = Total, so CFDI's BT-109 gap resolves by formula and the EN 16931 BR-CO-15 style law (BT-112 = BT-109 + BT-110) holds on it. EUROPA: compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; MUTANT (discount ignored): run exit 1 with exactly 'BT-109 = SubTotal - Descuento: 3824.15'; GRANULAR 0 code overages (cfdi_totals_from split out). Node zip BF59658F + gate list (canon_derived added) re-shipped while job-1793886615820 is still queued. Progress 70 -> 72.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 30u32, "2026-11-05T19:34Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:3x local fiscal: INDEPENDENT REVIEW of today's canon modules (a fresh reviewer agent given the files and domain facts, not my conclusions): 13 findings, verified against the schemas and structure files before acting. FIXED now (re-proof running on europa): (1) canon with_document kept the LAST path when a term is referenced twice in one document, so BT-18 / BT-128 bound to the qualifier cbc:DocumentTypeCode and BT-90 lost the seller PartyIdentification path; it now keeps the FIRST, pinned (BT-18 = .../cac:AdditionalDocumentReference/cbc:ID in both documents). (5) CFDI @Total is AFTER withholding (SubTotal - Descuento + traslados - retenidos per cfdv40.xsd), i.e. BT-115, not BT-112: @Total now binds BT-115, BT-112 is Derived (BT-109 + traslados); canon_derived reads TotalImpuestosRetenidos and pins a synthetic service CFDI with 106.67 withheld (BT-112 1160.00, BT-115 1053.33 = @Total) plus the real stamped one. (6) NF-e vProd (line and total) is Valor bruto and vDesc / CFDI Descuento sum LINE discounts, so BT-131 and BT-106 are Derived and BT-107 (document-level allowance) is no longer bound. (7) NF-e uCom is free text, not UN/ECE Rec 20: BT-130 is a NationalCode gap. (8) NF-e dest/email is a buyer electronic address: BT-49 now bound. (9) finNFe 4 (devolucao / retorno, often issued by the buyer, or goods coming back) no longer maps to 381. (12) the census counts only required implied terms and gaps. (13) PINT ids with two sub-parts are rejected; the 24 sub-terms are pinned. New counts: NF-e 11 bound + 2 implied + 12 gaps, CFDI 11 + 1 + 13. DEFERRED, recorded: (2) effective cardinality is kept once per term though BT-9 differs per document (invoice 0..1, credit note 0..n under PaymentMeans): needs a per-document effective in term_row. (3) BT-111 counts as required because the structure tags BT-110 and BT-111 on ONE TaxAmount inside a 1..2 TaxTotal; PINT has IBT-111 0..1, so the true required count is 24; the fix needs a rule for combined references, likely PINT's semantic cardinality as the presence source. (4) PINT slug variants become positional [1]/[2] while the printed qualifier (TaxScheme = VAT etc.) is dropped, so IBT-090 reads as the first PartyIdentification; no consumer yet. (10) BT-11 unbound in the credit note reflects the BIS structure's tagging (PINT binds IBT-011 at AdditionalDocumentReference-2/cbc:ID). (11) CFDI BT-1 is the optional @Folio (the fiscal id is the TFD UUID), and NF-e CNPJ -> BT-30 vs CFDI RFC -> BT-31 is inconsistent.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 31u32, "2026-11-05T19:55Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:5x local fiscal: REVIEW FIXES PROVEN on EUROPA (compiler core e9c77ce35244454d, all with no ParserErrors): canon 5 bodies (162 terms / 30 groups; the new pin BT-18 = .../AdditionalDocumentReference/cbc:ID passes), canon_nfe 4 (11 bound, 13 with BRL / BR implied, every required term accounted exactly once), canon_cfdi 4 (11 bound, 12 with MX), canon_derived 3 (incl. the synthetic CFDI with 106.67 withheld: BT-112 = 1160.00, BT-115 = 1053.33 = @Total, and ignoring the withholding no longer matches), canon_codes 2 (finNFe 4 -> no invoice type), reports 5 (census rows NF-e 11 / 2 / 5 / 4 / 3, CFDI 11 / 1 / 6 / 3 / 4), pint_terms 3 (sub-terms pinned at 24; JSON AF1E89EC byte-identical), canon_coverage 2 (misses 0 / 1). The regenerated canon JSON 3F8AD2AD differs from the previous run's 60FA5155 in exactly the 3 rows the review named: BT-18 and BT-128 now bind cbc:ID (not the cbc:DocumentTypeCode qualifier) in both documents, BT-90 binds the seller PartyIdentification (its first binding) instead of the payee's. canon/en16931-terms.json now holds this regenerated file (it had been the 10-31 pretty-printed version without 'effective' / BT-82 / BT-130 / these fixes, i.e. stale and misleading; backup en16931-terms.before-review-*.json in the session scratchpad). GRANULAR: 0 code overages in all seven touched files. Node zip D742F390 re-shipped while job-1793886615820 is still queued.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 32u32, "2026-11-05T20:47Z", "fiscal", "11-05 16:5x local fiscal: review finding (2) FIXED: effective cardinality is now kept PER DOCUMENT. canon.spi 6C66D6C6: term_row gains effective_by : list (ubl_document * cardinality) (first occurrence per document, like the paths; with_document is now generic over the paired value; merged_row does the update), effective_in row document reads it, and the JSON adds an effective_by object beside the unchanged cardinality / effective (invoice-first) fields. canon_coverage 4AF6D28E: the coverage TSV prints each document's own effective. Pin in en16931_terms_are_written_to_the_canon: BT-9 is 0..1 in the invoice, 0..n in the credit note. EUROPA: canon 5 bodies and canon_coverage 2 run exit 0 (misses 0 / 1), no ParserErrors; the regenerated JSON 6E922C32 (68,650 bytes) with effective_by stripped is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the previous 3F8AD2AD, and BT-9 is the only one of 192 rows whose effective differs by document (the reviewer's claim confirmed). GRANULAR 0 code overages. canon/en16931-terms.json updated to 6E922C32; node zip re-shipped while reports-gate2 is queued. Deferred findings left: (3) BT-111 presence, (4) PINT variant qualifiers, (10) BT-11 tagging, (11) CFDI BT-1 / BT-30 vs 31.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 33u32, "2026-11-05T21:02Z", "fiscal", "11-05 17:0x local fiscal: review finding (3) FIXED, data-driven: a term is REQUIRED for the census only if the BIS binding requires it (effective presence) AND the semantic model does not mark it optional. canon_coverage 653A0B13: semantically_optional () reads PINT 1.1.3's semantic cardinality column (pint_terms::document_terms) and required_ids drops base IBT-n terms marked 0..x. Measured first: of canon's 25 binding-required terms exactly ONE disagrees with PINT's semantic model, BT-111 (binding 1..2 because the structure tags BT-110 and BT-111 on one TaxAmount inside a 1..2 TaxTotal; PINT IBT-111 0..1). So the required set is now 24 terms; canon's own test still pins 25 as the binding fact. BT-111 left the NF-e and CFDI gap tables; supply / accounting tests and the census moved to 24 (census NF-e 11 / 2 / 4 / 4 / 3, CFDI 11 / 1 / 5 / 3 / 4; NF-e 11 + 2 + 11, CFDI 11 + 1 + 12). EUROPA: canon_coverage 2, canon_nfe 4, canon_cfdi 4, reports 5 bodies run exit 0, no ParserErrors; GRANULAR 0 code overages. Node zip re-shipped. Deferred findings now: (4) PINT variant qualifiers, (10) BT-11 credit-note tagging, (11) CFDI BT-1 @Folio vs TFD UUID and BT-30 / 31 choice.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 34u32, "2026-11-05T22:25Z", "fiscal", "11-05 18:2x local fiscal: review finding (4) FIXED, PINT variant qualifiers. pint_terms rows now carry the full UBL path built from the parent row, and a variant step takes the printed qualifier from the element cell (e.g. cac:PartyIdentification[...] per variant) instead of a positional suffix. canon/pint-terms.json AF1E89EC -> 8A991C40: 137 paths changed, 0 positional [n] left, every other field identical. Proof: europa bodies 3/3 green on pint_terms 8D014481 (compile 0, run 0, ParserErrors 0, 362 rows / 195 terms / 24 sub-terms / 36 groups); GRANULAR 0 code overages after splitting row_path, row_effective, row_record, cells_of, row_of. Node Cells confirmation pending: reports-gate2 job-1793909634925 queued on laptop with src zip 61F5914D. Deferred findings left: (10) BT-11 tagging, (11) CFDI BT-1 Folio and BT-30 vs 31.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 35u32, "2026-11-05T23:07Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:1x local fiscal: review finding (11) FIXED. BT-1 for CFDI now binds the stamp's TimbreFiscalDigital/@UUID (the folio fiscal, always present once stamped) instead of the optional @Folio; this matches BT-25, which already references a preceding CFDI by CfdiRelacionado/@UUID. The stamp binding sits in cfdi_stamp_bindings and is reached against deps/corpus/mx/complements/TimbreFiscalDigitalv11.xsd; the reach test also requires cfdv40 to declare Comprobante/Complemento. BT-30/31 now follow one rule: BT-31 is the registration for the document's value-added tax. CFDI RFC stays BT-31 (IVA). NF-e CNPJ stays BT-30 (legal-entity register), and IE (the ICMS registration) is now BT-31 for emit and BT-48 for dest. Required census unchanged (11 of 24 bound for both). Stale test names _25_ renamed _24_. Proof on europa: canon_cfdi 517D3BD7 4/4 and canon_nfe 17334E64 4/4 green, ParserErrors 0; the mutants (stamp @NoSuchUuid, emit/NoSuchIE) fail naming BT-1 and BT-31. GRANULAR 0 code overages. Node Cells pending: reports-gate2 job-1793909634925 queued with src zip 123BE2C2. Deferred finding left: (10) BT-11 tagging.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 36u32, "2026-11-05T23:24Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:2x local fiscal: review finding (10) FIXED, data-driven. When the BIS structure leaves a term untagged for a document, canon_coverage::term_reach now falls back to PINT's binding for the same base term (pint_terms::document_terms, exact base_number match) and walks it with the qualifiers stripped (unqualified, which handles the 34 qualifiers that contain a slash). Such reaches show as a new reach case ReachedByPint, 'typed via PINT' in target/ci-metrics/canon-coverage.tsv. BT-11 in the credit note is reached at ubl:CreditNote/cac:AdditionalDocumentReference[cbc:DocumentTypeCode = 50]/cbc:ID. The coverage test now pins 0/0 misses and BT-11 (credit note) as the only PINT-sourced reach; a new path-walk assertion covers a slash inside a qualifier. Proof on europa: canon_coverage ED50F221 2/2 bodies green, 'canon coverage misses (invoice, credit note): 0, 0', ParserErrors 0; the mutant (no PINT match) fails 'every term reaches a typed field in both documents'. GRANULAR 0 code overages. Node Cells pending: reports-gate2 queued, src zip re-shipped. Every review finding is now fixed or recorded.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 37u32, "2026-11-06T08:17Z", "fiscal", "11-05: PINT reach case (ReachedByPint) + qualifier strip in canon_coverage ED50F221; cfdi stamp bindings (TimbreFiscalDigital/@UUID) 11/24; nfe IE terms 24. pint-terms.json 8A991C40.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 38u32, "2026-11-06T10:11Z", "fiscal", "CORRECTION 11-06 06:11: the 11-05 PINT reach work (canon_coverage ED50F221 + pint_terms) is NOT proven under the live package: node reports-gate2 shows canon_coverage cannot see pint_terms (FISCAL-CANON-PINT-UNBOUND). Treat the 04:17 note as drafted, not done.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 39u32, "2026-11-06T11:16Z", "fiscal", "07:15: the PINT reach code compiles in the live package (node probe A: canon_coverage check 0 / rust 0) and binds under a fresh Cells mount; the 11-05 red was a stale Cells mount (FISCAL-CANON-PINT-UNBOUND). Still drafted, not done, until the full fresh-mount re-gate passes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 40u32, "2026-11-06T14:50Z", "fiscal", "10:4x PINT reach PROVEN on the live package: gate3b (node, fresh stage) canon_coverage 2/2 green, pint_terms 3/3 green; the 11-05 drafted state is now done for the PINT terms.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 41u32, "2026-11-07T15:50Z", "fiscal", "11-07 groom DoD: every family is a typed projection of the EN 16931 + PINT term set with its measured loss (terms reached / terms in the family's documents) in reports.md; canon_coverage, pint_terms and the canon_* units green on a fresh stage; PINT reach is done (11-06 gate3b), CII profiles remain (FISCAL-CII-PROFILES, blocked on the user's Factur-X download).")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 42u32, "2026-11-07T16:47Z", "main", "main 11-07: linked to TFS-CONVERSION-LOSS-LAWS. This item's NotCarried losses and the 'reverse only where bijective' rule (UBL 192/192 lossless, NF-e/CFDI reverse not, BT-3 not bijective) are the hand-written form of that item's Lossy / Retraction / Iso marker; one canon pair is its third pilot. No change to this item's scope.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_model_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-MODEL", 43u32, "2026-11-10T10:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal groom 11-10 07:0x: no note since 11-07 and no next step, at 72% of a 1080 m estimate. What is left per the earlier notes: the canon pair's reverse direction only where bijective (UBL 192/192 lossless; NF-e and CFDI reverse not; BT-3 not bijective) and the NotCarried losses as the third pilot of TFS-CONVERSION-LOSS-LAWS. Tonight canon_document gained BT-13 order_ref (FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE, green 8/8). Next step: list which canon terms still lack a typed loss marker (NotCarried vs carried) for NF-e and CFDI, as a census test in canon.spi, so the remaining 28% is a counted list instead of an estimate.")
