inl claude_hooks_in_repo () = Task ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", "Claude Code hooks live in i574n.github (claude/hooks), settings.json points at the repo copy: reviewable in git diff, survive a profile wipe", Story, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:org,hooks,heal,workflow", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_claude_hooks_in_repo () = Planning ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_1 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 1u32, "2026-10-31T10:36Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 06:4x kit (filed during the user's 'fix hooks, memories' heal; hooks are main's, so main decides): the five Claude Code hooks (autonomous-gate, kit-tree-lease, kit-style-check, kit-work-in-repo, plus settings.json's wiring) live only in ~/.claude/hooks, outside any repo. The 10-28 profile wipe destroyed them and they were rebuilt from evidence (kit-hooks memory). Tonight alone they changed 5 times (gate wake-source text, the new work-in-repo hook, its string-form timeout that blocked a Write, style-check's $\" probe, lease narrowing by the regen), and each change was reviewable only through .bak files. Proposal: i574n.github/claude/hooks/*.ps1 becomes the single copy, and settings.json points at the repo paths directly (no install copy, so no second record to drift; work-in-the-repo memory). Every change then shows up in git diff for the user's review, and a wipe loses nothing that is committed. tree-lease-hook-test.ps1 already lives in i574n.github/scripts. Done = settings.json commands name repo paths, ~/.claude/hooks holds only archive/, and every hook's pipe test passes from the repo path.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_2 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 2u32, "2026-10-31T15:03Z", "main", "10-31 11:03 main: DECISION NEEDED FROM THE USER (batched into main's 18:00 report). The move only works as a whole: copy the five hooks to i574n.github/claude/hooks AND point ~/.claude/settings.json's hook commands at the repo paths. Changing settings.json is persistent configuration of the user's Claude Code setup, so main doesn't do it unasked; copying the hooks without repointing would create a second, drifting copy (worse than today). Ready to do in ~15 min on a yes: copy, repoint, run each hook once (gate dry run, tree-lease test, style-check probe), keep the old ~/.claude/hooks copies as .bak until the user commits.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_3 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:33Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Agent moves the hooks: copy ~/.claude/hooks/*.ps1 to i574n.github/claude/hooks (unstaged), back up settings.json to settings.json.bak-<stamp>, rewrite only the hook paths, then run every hook's pipe test from the repo path. KEEP iff all pass and a live PowerShell call succeeds; otherwise restore the .bak at once. Exception: the kit-tree-lease entry's command/onFailure shape is NOT changed, because the harness says that one is the user's. BACKUP/UNDO: settings.json.bak-<stamp>; the old hook files stay in ~/.claude/hooks. OWNER: kit.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_4 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. From resilience n5: the fleet-wide hook block (this lane's PowerShell was blocked twice on 11-02) comes from Claude Code not finding Git Bash. A scoop-only git is not at the standard path, so the hook runner times out and the tree-lease hook defaults to block. The fix is the env var CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH pointing at scoop's bash.exe, not a hook rewrite. That is resilience's/kit's settings step, with a settings.json.bak and the same keep/restore test as this item's record v2.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_5 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 5u32, "2026-11-07T22:07Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. The harness hook config is user-only (x decision record 11-02), so the move needs the user's word. DoD: hooks copied into i574n.github/claude/hooks with settings.json pointing at the repo copy (the user applies the settings change); hooks-test.ps1 passes against the repo copy. Next step: copy the current hooks into a drafts folder and diff them against what settings.json references, then ask the user to repoint.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_6 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 6u32, "2026-11-09T12:33Z", "org", "11-09 org: marked --wait user. The DoD requires repointing ~/.claude/settings.json's hook commands at the repo copy - that is harness hook config, which the harness itself and the governance ask-list reserve for the user (x decision record 11-02 + main 11-07 both concluded the settings change needs the user's word). The autonomous prep (copy hooks into i574n.github/claude/hooks) also risks leaking local C:\\Users paths / infra identity into a public tree (personal-data-never-in-public-trees, repos-never-name-infra), so that needs a path-scrub design first, not a verbatim copy. Clears when the user applies the settings.json repoint (or approves a scrubbed repo copy).")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_7 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 7u32, "2026-11-09T12:37Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:4x INVENTORY (next step done): settings.json wires 6 hook entries (PreToolUse x3: cmd.exe + 2 pwsh, PostToolUse, Stop, SubagentStop), all pointing at ~/.claude/hooks, which holds 6 live scripts: autonomous-gate.ps1 (11.5 KB, edited by rig 11-09 08:24 for AGILE-STALL-1109), kit-style-check.ps1, kit-tree-lease.ps1, kit-backlog-state-guard.ps1, subagent-hold.ps1, kit-work-in-repo.ps1, plus 15 dated .bak copies (the de-facto history the repo would replace). CONFLICT FOUND: the DoD copies these into i574n.github/claude/hooks, but every hook is a .ps1 and the standing rule is no new .ps1 in repos (Spiral-first). Options for the user: (a) allow hooks as the one .ps1 exception in i574n.github (thin launchers), (b) port each hook to a Spiral program built to a binary the settings point at (the gate already shells to kit, so it ports naturally into kit/rig as a verb, e.g. kit gate stop), (c) keep hooks out of git but snapshot them into the off-site backup (store-offsite-backup already covers ~/.claude memory; add hooks/). Recommendation: (c) now (one line in the backup set, wipe-proof today) + (b) for the gate over time; settings.json stays user-applied either way.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_8 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 8u32, "2026-11-09T12:39Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:4x option (c) first half applied regardless of the user's choice: store-offsite-backup.ps1's source set gains ~/.claude/hooks, so the 6 live hooks (and their dated .bak history) ride the next verified off-site snapshot; wipe-proof today. The repo question (a/b/c) stays the user's.")
