inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_1 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T12:22Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: found while landing SIM-IN-SPIRAL S5. 'kit standards C:\\home\\git\\x\\apps\\sim\\spi' reports files=23, but the package holds 29 .spi files; the 6 not checked are the entry notebooks in subfolders (simframes/simframes.spi, xsim_checks, xsim_events, xsim_flow, xsim_split, xsim_world; each declares '///- --package ..', so they belong to this package). simframes.spi had 4 lines of 121-129 columns that standards passed and only a plain length scan found (x wrapped them). Done = standards walks the package's subfolder entries (or every file whose ///- --package resolves to the package) and flags them; x's sim package stays at 0 findings.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_2 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T16:38Z", "kit", "10-31 12:4x kit: scoped, not built. The listing is kit_standards/standards.spi spiral_files, a raw-Rust read_dir blob (top-level .spi/.spir only, standards.spi excluded) feeding files_checked, which joins each name to the package folder and passes module_of(name) to kit_standards_scan's file findings. module_of only feeds two module rules (the float check in integer-only modules, and the test-block-needs-header rule), so a subfolder entry should pass its file STEM, not 'simframes/simframes'. AGENTS requires migrating a touched legacy blob, and the lib has no portable listing: file_system.directory_get_files is F#-only (null on other targets) and file_system.read_dir_names (file_system.spi:1702) is the Rust arm, returning result' (vec std_string) io_error. PLAN: replace spiral_files with Spiral over read_dir_names. Top-level entries as today, plus each subfolder (skipping target, .cache, node_modules) whose .spi files have first line '///- --package ..', named '<sub>/<file>' for the path and the stem for the module. Test block over a temp fixture: pkg/a.spi, pkg/sub/entry.spi with the header (checked), and pkg/other/loose.spi without it (not checked). Done = x's apps/sim/spi reports files=29 with 0 findings.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_3 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T16:56Z", "kit", "10-31 12:5x kit: BUILT (unstaged) per n2's plan; ships in TRAIN7. kit_standards/standards.spi spiral_files is now Spiral, no longer a raw-Rust read_dir blob (legacy migrated as AGENTS asks). sorted_names uses lib file_system.read_dir_names, then am'.from_vec_base, map_base sm'.from_std_string and am'.sort_by id (the kit_job_host idiom), guarded by directory_exists. names_where walks by index. The package's own .spi/.spir files are listed as before (standards.spi excluded), plus every subfolder file whose FIRST LINE is exactly '///- --package ..', named '<sub>/<file>'; target, node_modules and dot-folders are skipped. files_checked passes the file stem to module_of, so module rules see 'entry', not 'sub/entry'. CLI case subfolder_entries_of_the_package_are_checked_too (kit_standards/standards_cli.spi): pkg/sub/entry.spi with the header and a comment line is flagged ('sub/entry.spi:3  no-comment-lines'), pkg/other/loose.spi without the header is not, and files=2. Census ratchet ok; standards.rs had 572/1000 lines. Done = TRAIN7 green, then x's apps/sim/spi reports files=29.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_4 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 4u32, "2026-10-31T19:32Z", "kit", "10-31 15:3x kit: size check on the node (regen-sizes.ps1, read-only regen with cargo check on mirror kit-verify): standards.rs is 920/1000 with this change (it was 572; the Spiral listing plus the lib vec idiom costs about 350 generated lines), inside the gate. Other touched crates in the same run: agile_task_creation 990, agile_task_next 968, agile_todo_scan 1000 (exactly at the gate, KIT-TODO-SCAN-HEADROOM), kit_agile_mutation 831, kit_agile_routes 712, kit_do_file_steps 731, kit_machine_watch 898, kit_table_query 393, agile_task_revision 314. Cargo check passed for all.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_5 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 60 h ago by kit, progress kept at 75%. Resume from that note: t 968, agile_todo_scan 1000 (exactly at the gate, KIT-TODO-SCAN-HEADROOM), kit_agile_mutation 831, kit_agile_routes 712, kit_do_file_steps 731, kit_machine_watch 898, kit_table_query 393, agile_task_revision 314. Cargo check passed for all.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_6 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T13:03Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 09:1x microblog groom check, installed kit: the subfolder walk WORKS (scratch fixture pkg/sub/inner.spi with the header: files=2, inner.spi:3 no-comment-lines and :4 line-width 145 flagged). But the DoD case still FAILS: kit standards x/apps/sim/spi reports files=27, not 33, because the 6 sim subfolder entries now start with '///- --package .. --timeout 600000', and package_entry (standards.spi:41) accepts only an exact '///- --package ..' first line. FIX drafted (unstaged, rig told): package_entry also accepts the prefix '///- --package .. ' (the trailing space keeps ../sibling out). The CLI test adds pkg/timed/entry.spi (--timeout header, checked) and pkg/sibling/entry.spi ('///- --package ../sibling', not checked), so it expects files=3 findings=2. next: run the rig_standards CLI notebook on a node with a free slot, then kit standards x/apps/sim/spi must report files=33 findings=0.")
