inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_1 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T15:36Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: from main's note (LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP and LAMBDA-PARENS finished in lib today). (1) Notebook-era headings: x has 0 '/// #' lines in any apps/*.spi, so drop_name_headings.exs has nothing to do here (checked). (2) Redundant parens around trailing lambdas: about 28 candidate sites in x's apps/*.spi (rough grep for a '(\\ ... => ...)' ending a line). spiral/apps/cells/spi/lambda_parens_prove.ps1 proves per file through lib_gate.ps1 (a compile per file, BREAKS = keep the parens, -Site to bisect), and its -LiveLib defaults to spiral/lib/spiral; x's files belong to the apps/client and apps/sim packages, so the first step is checking that the gate compiles a consumer package (or passing x's package dir). Load medium: one compile per file, run as a single node job over the files with sites.")
inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_2 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 2u32, "2026-11-04T01:12Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:11 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP, x's corner: open x items with no note in 48 h). Owner x. Next step: run main's lambda-paren cleanup over x/apps/*.spi via the formatter (format --check now flags only drift, and today's lands were canonicalized), and close if 0 remain.")
inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_3 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 3u32, "2026-11-04T11:53Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:53 x: EXACT SITE COUNT with the prover's own finder (lambda_parens_prove.ps1's Get-TailSites, loaded via the AST without running the script: a '(\\ ... => ...)' closing at line end, scoped '=> \\*' or type-annotated tails excluded): 56 sites in 22 x files (the 10-31 rough grep said ~28). Top: sim/scheduler 9, sim/world 7, sim/sim_serve 6, client/reading 4, sim/schedule 4, client/wire 3, sim/scenario 3, personas 2, final_state 2, inbox 2. PLAN: the prover edits a copy and proves each file via lib_gate (one compile per file; BREAKS = keep the parens). Run it as ONE node job over the 22 files once the slot queue frees; files in x's queued stack (sim_serve, world, cells_executor, simframes) go LAST, after x-next8 lands, so the prover never races a pinned draft.")
inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_4 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 4u32, "2026-11-04T12:08Z", "x", "2026-11-04 08:08 x: 41 of 56 sites PROVEN to compile and QUEUED. Drafts (kit drafts x\\X-LAMBDA-PARENS, plan.json with base hashes) for the 19 files outside x's queued stack, made with the prover's OWN Get-TailSites + Remove-Parens (loaded from lambda_parens_prove.ps1 via the AST). Europa pack34 --check on a fresh stage of the live tree: 19/19 exit 0 (the prover's BREAKS test is a compile, which this is). They ride x-next7 (not launched; launcher + land updated, 23 files, every draft pinned): x-next7's pre-registered rule (sim/client builds 0, sim accept with every fixture BYTE-IDENTICAL, e2e RUST-OK, census SAME) proves the removal is purely syntactic (no codegen change). Remaining 15 sites in sim_serve, world, cells_executor and simframes follow after x-next8 lands.")
inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_5 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 5u32, "2026-11-04T13:46Z", "x", "2026-11-04 09:46 x: 14 MORE SITES drafted with the prover's own Get-TailSites + Remove-Parens: sim/world 7 (B4CDE32E0EA6 -> 6BC70304CB24, joins x-next7, now 26 files, pinned), x-next9's sim_serve 7 (587AE9BF2462 -> BDE70A884173) and route timeline_serve 1 (C2A6C2C0FFEB -> 82DD8227885E), x-next9 land re-pinned; simframes has 0. All format-clean, 0 cells over 272, europa --check 0 on the full x-next9 stage. Both runs' rules include byte-identical sim fixtures, which proves the removal is syntactic. Left: cells_executor (frozen in x-next6; after it lands).")
inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_6 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 6u32, "2026-11-06T08:19Z", "x", "2026-11-06 04:1x x: groom: Active -> Paused (untouched 43 h, P4). The 41+14 proven sites rode x-next7/x-next9/x-next10b/x-next11, which all landed on 11-05. Resume condition: a fresh prover sweep (lambda_parens_prove, CPU-light, the box is fine) reports the sites still left; if 0, close it Done.")
inl note_of_x_lambda_parens_7 () = Note ("X-LAMBDA-PARENS", 7u32, "2026-11-06T14:07Z", "x", "2026-11-06 10:07 x: resume check: the prover (lambda_parens_prove with Get-TailSites + Remove-Parens) is GONE. It was a scratch script, and only kit drafts x\\X-LAMBDA-PARENS\\plan.json (11-04) survives. The 'fresh prover sweep' resume step therefore needs a site finder first, as a kit or Spiral tool per the no-new-.ps1 rule rather than a scratch script. Stays Paused (P4); resume when a cell-budget or formatter pass can name redundant trailing-lambda parens.")
