inl planning_of_kit_pause_rule_rework () = Planning ("KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_pause_rule_rework_1 () = Note ("KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK", 1u32, "2026-10-31T20:27Z", "kit", "10-31 16:3x kit, user request relayed by compiler: rework the auto-pause rule. Evidence (compiler): 95 pause-by-rule notes on 93 items. Paused drops an item out of 'agile next' and out of the Stop gate's quoted rows, so 'resume when picked' never happens. P0s such as CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE, SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES, RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, XSD-FACET-TYPES and XSD-DECODE-RESULT sat hidden, along with the compiler lane's backend, Gleam and edition-3 work. DONE TODAY: (1) the dangling-backlog memory's R3 now says never auto-pause for silence: stale Active goes to Planned, and Paused only by an explicit decision with a reason AND a resume condition. (2) The Stop gate (~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1) names the team's Paused P0/P1 items with 're-decide each' (tested: team main sees CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE, SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES, RUST-NIGHTLY-...). (3) i574n.github/scripts/dangling-census.ps1 flags PAUSED-NO-RESUME (92 of 110 Paused) and PAUSED-BY-RULE (24, newest note a rule pause). (4) The repair census: 44 items still Paused with a rule note in their history (main 40, 33 of them P0/P1; kit 2; compiler 2). Kit's 2 (EOIE-MEMORY-MODEL, TODO-AS-SOURCE) were re-decided -> Planned with reasons. LEFT, kit code: 'agile set <id> <p> Paused' requires --reason \"<why>\" and --resume-on <event|yyyy-mm-dd> (stored on the item); 'agile next' resurfaces a Paused item once its date passes, or after 14 days with no condition; 'agile check' warns on any P0/P1 Paused without a resume condition. Main's 40 are main's to re-decide (the gate now shows them each fire).")
inl note_of_kit_pause_rule_rework_2 () = Note ("KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK", 2u32, "2026-10-31T21:11Z", "main", "10-31 17:11 main's share DONE (47 main-tagged rows flagged PAUSED-BY-RULE / PAUSED-NO-RESUME by dangling-census.ps1): 38 -> PLANNED (paused by the old silence/WIP rule with no blocker in their notes; a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing), incl. CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE, RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE, SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES, TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCE (it gates fiscal's live work), the granular heals, LIB-REACTORS, LIB-USAGE-DIAGNOSTICS, TOOLCHAIN-LATEST, KINO-HOT-PATHS; 6 stay PAUSED with a written Reason and Resume condition (DOTA, DOTA-FIRST-SCENARIO, DOTA-HEADLESS-WORLD, DOTA-LUA-BINDINGS: superseded by the user's WoW pivot, resume if the user asks for Dota; SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT: user-batch migration run; ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES: the user's in-Zed check); 1 -> DONE (LAB-SWEEP-GATE: spiral/lab no longer exists); 2 left as compiler re-decided them today (FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS Blocked, MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER Planned).")
inl note_of_kit_pause_rule_rework_3 () = Note ("KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK", 3u32, "2026-10-31T21:26Z", "kit", "10-31 17:2x kit: repair progress. kit re-decided 5 more silence pauses that used other wording ('Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued', a 10-28 groom), the Stop gate's new re-decide line surfaced them, all -> Planned with their next step kept: EOIE-JOBS (P0), WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB, EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC, EOIE-AGILE-FORMATTED-WRITER, CONVO-IN-SPIRAL. dangling-census.ps1's rule pattern now also matches 'nothing queued' and 'Paused. Last note'. Census now: Paused 62 (110 at 16:3x), PAUSED-NO-RESUME 51, PAUSED-BY-RULE 27 (mostly main's 40-item share in progress). kit has no Paused P0/P1 left.")
inl note_of_kit_pause_rule_rework_4 () = Note ("KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK", 4u32, "2026-11-09T06:29Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:0x local rig MEASURED on the live backlog: 59 Paused items (20 of them P0/P1); only 1 has no resume condition in any note (matching resume condition / resume when / resume if / resume on / resumes when / Resume:), and it is not P0/P1. So parts (a) and (b) of the DoD hold in practice: the stop gate's line Paused P0/P1 items for team <t> (re-decide each ...) resurfaces paused work on every stop (tonight it made rig re-decide KIT-REMOTE-SYNC with a reason and a resume condition). LEFT: (c) agile check warns on a Paused item with no resume condition (one warning per item naming it), with a CLI test; its baseline is that 1 item today. Code for TRAIN43. DoD: agile check prints the warning, test row, baseline recorded.")
inl note_of_kit_pause_rule_rework_5 () = Note ("KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK", 5u32, "2026-11-09T06:29Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Next step: the agile check warning for a Paused item without a resume condition. TypeFeatures: a pause_record union (PausedWith of reason * resume | PausedBare of reason) read from the notes, so check matches on the case instead of grepping prose.")
inl md_line_limit_120 () = Task ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", "Every Markdown file in the user's own repos keeps lines at 120 characters or less: a checker in kit standards plus a reflow tool that splits long prose lines (never joins authored lines), enforced on new edits", Story, P1, D3, 30u32, Active, "MD-LINES-COMPILER,MD-LINES-TIBIA,MD-LINES-X,MD-LINES-FISCAL,MD-LINES-KIT", "markdown,standards,formatting,main,kit,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_md_line_limit_120 () = Planning ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_1 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 1u32, "2026-10-31T20:27Z", "main", "10-31 16:27 main. USER REQUEST 10-31 ~16:2x: 'all md files should have the 120 char limit per line somehow'. CENSUS (tracked .md per repo; a line counts when over 120 chars): 1,094 md files, 656 with long lines, 39,663 long lines (36,948 prose, 1,094 table rows, 872 long URLs, the rest inside code fences). Own repos: spiral 11 files / 239 lines, kit 5/119, eoie 5/119, x 3/120, tibia 2/393 (332 table rows), i574n.github 5/84, polyglot 1/59, fiscal 1/25 (20 table), Spiral-s-ML-Library 3/90, dice 2/5, alphabet 1/5, azeroth 1/115, Trading-Journal 4/2,120, m4binder, fc1943s, blog, dir-tree-html, tapas2 and others 1-18 each. EXCLUDED (upstream forks; reflowing their docs only creates upstream diffs): zed 3,371, nearcore 514, wasmer 297, leptos 246, The-Spiral-Language 243 (fork checkout), ExplorerPatcher 192, plotters 83, cargo-outdated 76, livebook 52, atrium 28, rustix 19, otclient, forgottenserver. USER CALL: vault (Obsidian notes, 261 md, 30,865 long lines, mostly prose): Obsidian soft-wraps, so a hard 120 there changes how notes read; ask before including. DESIGN (memory formatter-keep-breaks: never join authored lines, only re-lay lines over 120): (1) checker: count lines over 120 outside code fences; exempt a table row (reflowing breaks the table: either shorten cells or accept) and a line that is only a URL/link target; (2) reflow tool: split prose lines at the last space before 120, keeping list/blockquote prefixes and indentation on the continuation line, never inside inline code, links or headings; (3) wire the checker into kit standards (the 1k-line gate's sibling) and the style hook, so new edits stay under 120; (4) run the reflow repo by repo, each team for its own repos, after a dry run shows only whitespace-at-break changes.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_2 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 2u32, "2026-10-31T22:12Z", "main", "10-31 18:12 main, SCOPE CORRECTED by the user ('why you're considering vault? stick to i574n'): only repos with an i574n remote. That is 19: azeroth, blog, cargo-outdated, dir-tree-html, dotfiles, eoie, fiscal, i574n.github, i574n.github.io, kit, tapas2, The-Spiral-Language, tibia, tictactoe, x (origin i574n), plus spiral, dice, alphabet, polyglot (remote github-i574n). OUT: vault and singularity (fc1943s only), and every third-party clone (zed, nearcore, wasmer, leptos, livebook, ...). n1's 'user call: vault' is withdrawn.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_3 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 3u32, "2026-11-05T23:21Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:2x CENSUS (tracked .md in the 13 i574n working repos, a line counts when over 120 chars; kinds: prose / table row / line with a 60+ char URL incl. badge links / inside a code fence): spiral 216/23/1/7, kit 85/24/1/9, x 47/43/1/29, tibia 61/331/1/1, i574n.github 73/10/1/0, fiscal 1/29/5/0, dice 5/1/1/2, regex 2/5/0/0, alphabet 2/2/1/0, html 1/0/0/1, blog 1/0/1/0, dotfiles 0/0/1/0, i574n.github.io 1/0/1/0. HEALED by hand (unstaged, soft breaks only: split at sentence or word boundaries, never inside a link, list continuations indented, nothing joined): regex 2, html 1, dice 5, alphabet 2, blog 1, i574n.github.io 1 -> prose 0 in those six (LF + trailing newline kept). RULE DESIGN for kit's checker: exempt table rows, code fences and lines whose only long token is a URL/badge (breaking those breaks rendering); flag prose only. LEFT: ~482 prose lines in spiral/kit/x/tibia/i574n.github/fiscal; that's the reflow tool's job (a kit verb), and each owning lane runs it. Census script: main scratchpad md-census.ps1 (fold into the kit verb).")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_4 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 4u32, "2026-11-05T23:24Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:2x i574n.github HEALED except the standard text: 9 long prose lines reflowed (unstaged) in docs/agents/agent-sync.md (151, 309), CONTRIBUTING.md (8, trailing two-space hard break kept on the last piece), README.md (65), profile/README.md (3, 5, 9, 11, 16; the user's own profile prose, words byte-identical). Method: split at the last space at or before col 120, never inside inline code, link text or link target; list continuations keep the item's indent; each line is rejoined and compared to the original before writing, and git diff --word-diff shows 0 changed words from the reflow. NOT touched: CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md (61 lines of the standard Contributor Covenant text; the reflow verb's job) and profile/README.md 38-40 (inline-HTML contact divs; breaking them risks the render, so the checker should exempt HTML block lines). Reflow script: main scratchpad md-reflow.ps1 -> drafts store beside md-census.ps1 (a model for the kit verb).")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_5 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 5u32, "2026-11-05T23:25Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:3x spiral MAIN SHARE healed (unstaged, same reflow + rejoin check, word diff 0): README.md 94/98/100 (contributing, license, the upstream MPL line), lib/spiral/bench/parsing/README.md 5/18/48, scripts/patched-crates/README.md 25. spiral's remaining long prose, by owner: compiler, apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md 78 + tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md 57 + samples READMEs 7 + tmp/README.md 2; x (Cells), apps/cells/README.md 65. Elsewhere: kit 85, x 47, tibia 61, fiscal 1, i574n.github's CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md 61 (standard text). Those wait on the reflow verb (model: drafts\\i574n.github\\MD-LINE-LIMIT-120\\md-reflow.ps1 + md-census.ps1) run by each owner, then kit's checker keeps it at 0.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_6 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 6u32, "2026-11-06T12:04Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:2x lint fill: DoD: 0 prose lines over 120 in the own repos' Markdown (md-census), each reflow word-identical to the original. Next step: hand the remaining about 482 lines to their owners as a reflow verb. TypeFeatures: none needed; this is text-only work.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_7 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 7u32, "2026-11-06T14:15Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:2x CENSUS (md-census.ps1, prose lines over 120): spiral 209, kit 85, tibia 61, x 47, i574n.github 64, fiscal 1, others 0 (regex, html, dice, alphabet, blog, dotfiles, i574n.github.io). Main's own repo: the 64 are 61 in CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md (the Contributor Covenant copied verbatim; kept as is so GitHub's community-profile check keeps recognizing it) and 3 raw-HTML icon lines in profile/README.md (length from icon URLs; splitting them risks the public page's layout). Rule amendment: verbatim third-party texts and raw-HTML lines are exempt, like tables, URLs and fences. Remaining actionable: spiral 209, kit 85, tibia 61, x 47, fiscal 1, owned by their lanes, via md-reflow.ps1 (word-identical check per line).")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_8 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 8u32, "2026-11-06T21:53Z", "main", "main 11-06 17:5x OWNER SPLIT for spiral's 211 (md-census -Repos spiral -List): compiler = apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md 80, tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md 57, samples READMEs 9 (mega_brzozowski_derivatives 5, tmp/README 2, samples/README 1, recursive_union_multi_case 1); x = apps/cells/README.md 65. Main's share is 0 (i574n.github's 64 are exempt: the verbatim Covenant and raw-HTML icons). Tool for owners: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\MD-LINE-LIMIT-120\\md-reflow.ps1 -File <f> -Lines <n,...> [-Apply] (splits only, word-identical check per line). kit 85, tibia 61, x 47, fiscal 1 are as in n-1. Next step: owners reflow at their next doc touch; kit's standards checker enforces new edits.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_9 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 9u32, "2026-11-09T11:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 microblog OWNER SHARE healed (unstaged; md-reflow.ps1 called in-process, because pwsh -File splits an -Lines array into separate strings and the binding fails). x README.md 5 lines and x apps/sim/spi/README.md 3, plus spiral apps/cells/README.md 63: whitespace-normalized text identical before and after, so 0 changed words. One long prose line stays in each of the two READMEs: the tool found no safe break (it never breaks inside inline code or link text); left as is. NOT touched: x apps/client/README.md, the e2e tutorial and thread file whose text the client e2e compares; reflow it only together with an -Accept client verify.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_10 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 10u32, "2026-11-09T16:06Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: org's own-repo share is DONE (i574n.github healed to 0 actionable prose; its remaining 61 CODE_OF_CONDUCT + 3 raw-HTML lines are the agreed exemptions). All remaining actionable lines are OTHER lanes' repos (spiral 209 = compiler, kit 85 = rig, tibia 61, x 47, fiscal 1) reflowed by each owner at their next doc touch via the md-reflow draft, and the ENFORCEMENT keystone is rig's standards checker (wire into kit standards so new edits stay <=120). Parking on lane:rig for the checker; per-owner reflow rides each lane. Clear when the checker lands.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_11 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 11u32, "2026-11-09T16:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 16:1x SPLIT BY OWNER (fresh md-census 16:0x, prose lines over 120): spiral 151 (almost all apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md -> compiler; 1 in apps/cells/README.md), kit 102 (rig), tibia 71, x 41 (microblog), fiscal 1. Filed one light child per owning lane with the proven method + census commands: MD-LINES-COMPILER, MD-LINES-TIBIA, MD-LINES-X, MD-LINES-FISCAL, MD-LINES-KIT; they are this item's deps now. Why: the floor census (rig's new gate line) shows compiler/fiscal/microblog/tibia at 0 ready light items while their share of this work sat in org's pool, invisible to them.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_12 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 12u32, "2026-11-09T16:16Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 15:0x local rig, CHECKER CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): src/rig_standards_md/width.spi (pure, HostFree, standards 0). md_line union Prose | FenceEdge | InFence | TableRow | RawHtml | LinkDefinition | Unbreakable (a line with no space, e.g. a long URL: no safe break); only Prose lines over 120 are findings, with \"path:line prose line is N columns, over 120\". Fences toggle on ``` or ~~~ and close correctly. CROSS-CHECK with the same rule in PowerShell over kit's 6 tracked .md files: 102 long prose lines (spec/one-call.md 49, FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md 34, README.md 10, AGENTS.md 7, infra/nodebench/README.md 2) vs org's 85 for kit: the md-reflow tool exempts a little more (likely blockquotes or link-only overflow); I will align the exemption list with md-reflow before wiring so the checker and the fixer agree. NEXT STEP after the probe: route it from kit standards (a markdown rule over git-listed .md files, ratchet mode first), then kit's own reflow with the md-reflow draft (spec/one-call.md expected blocks are fenced, so they stay byte-exact).")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_13 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 13u32, "2026-11-09T16:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 17:0x local rig, CHECKER ALIGNED with org2's live census (unstaged, in the probe batch): rig_standards_md/width.spi now mirrors md-census exactly: exempt = fence, table, heading (up to 3 leading spaces, 1-6 #, then a space, the census ^\\s{0,3}#{1,6}\\s), long URL (http(s):// followed by 60+ non-space chars, the census https?://\\S{60,}), and long inline code (a backtick span of 60+ chars, the census [^`]{60,}); raw HTML and link definitions are no longer exempt (the census does not exempt them). Tests cover each exemption, a 4-space indented \"heading\" (code, not exempt) and a 59-char span (not exempt). MD-LINES-KIT closed: kit reads prose 0. NEXT: route the checker from kit standards over git-listed .md, ratchet mode first.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_14 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 14u32, "2026-11-09T17:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 18:5x rig: restoring the lane:rig wait. Rig had re-pointed or cleared it after doing only part of the answer; this is another team's item, so the wait stays lane:rig until rig's whole share is done (progress is in rig's notes above).")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_15 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 15u32, "2026-11-09T20:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig progress (the lane:rig wait stays until the rule fires): rig's model for this item (rig_standards_md width (md-census exact)) is built and in rig's probe batch; its routing to every lane now has one carrier item, KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB (kit lint smells beside kit lint macros, ratchet mode with a per-repo baseline, a negative control per rule), which waits on TRAIN43 because the lint entry is shared code. rig clears this wait when the rule fires on your repo.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_16 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 16u32, "2026-11-09T21:25Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig progress: rig_standards_md is probe-green (Cells notebook gate on ganymede, off-train). The lane:rig wait stays until KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB wires the rule into kit lint smells after TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_md_line_limit_120_17 () = Note ("MD-LINE-LIMIT-120", 17u32, "2026-11-10T13:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 09:5x rig: the lane:rig wait is now item:KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB, the precise target every earlier rig note already named (that verb routes this rule to every lane, and it waits on train TRAIN43f, node-green 331/331 at 08:46 with the box install running). The wait clears itself when the verb is Done, so this item stops showing up as waiting on rig in the gate.")
inl org_scripts_home () = Task ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", "i574n.github/scripts holds only genuinely cross-repo glue: project-specific scripts move to their own repos, generic tooling becomes kit commands in Spiral, and the .py files are ported", Story, P1, D4, 30u32, Active, "KIT-FOLD-PROCESS-HEALTH,KIT-FOLD-JOB-RUNNING,KIT-FOLD-MIRROR-BACKUP,KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE,DELETE-ROOT-GUARD", "scripts,languages,cleanup,team:org,kit,resilience", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_org_scripts_home () = Planning ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_1 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 1u32, "2026-10-31T20:42Z", "main", "10-31 16:42 main. USER 10-31 ~16:3x: 'i574n.github is getting flooded with ps1 scripts, there are project specific ones there that probably should be in their own repos ... is this main lane's drift? a lot of py files also, i said we should prioritize other languages'. CENSUS i574n.github/scripts: 118 files (67 tracked, 51 untracked): 56 .ps1, 50 .py, 9 .spi, 1 .livemd, 1 .md, 1 .spiproj; subfolders wipe-recovery 47 (mostly .py), pins 11 (Spiral), spiral-independent 4. PROJECT-SPECIFIC (belong in their repo): spiral lib tooling land-lib-program, lib-guarded-do, lib-program-gate, lib-reanchor, respell-repo, bang-export-rewrite, slice-roundtrip-sweep, notebook-main-check, spiral-independent/; tibia tibia-mariadb-dump; x x-compat-census, x-node-verify; kit crate-gate-all, draft-regen-bundle, host-dupes-census. MAIN'S SHARE OF THE DRIFT: main wrote the rule (memory org-tooling-in-dot-github: cross-repo scripts in i574n.github/scripts) and added box-upkeep, node-temp-contain, node-archive-cleanup, safe-delete-test, scratch-archive-guard-test, resource-report-save, spiral-independent/ on 10-30/31; lanes over-applied the rule to project-specific scripts. PY: wipe-recovery/ (resilience's recovery toolkit) and profile-restore-drill-node.py break the existing no-.py-in-repos rule. PLAN: (1) classify every script: project-specific -> its repo (each team moves its own, callers updated, dangling check by stem); org-generic -> a kit command in Spiral (memories generic-tools-not-per-experiment, granular-style-discipline: logic in Spiral), PowerShell only for thin host glue; .py -> ported (A/B before retiring); (2) narrow org-tooling-in-dot-github to genuinely cross-repo, short-lived glue; (3) a kit standards check that flags new .py and project-named scripts under i574n.github/scripts.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_2 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 2u32, "2026-10-31T20:45Z", "kit", "10-31 16:4x kit: classifying kit's own 10-31 additions under the narrowed rule. (1) i574n.github/scripts/dangling-census.ps1 (moved from C:\\home\\data this morning) is GENERIC backlog tooling, so its end state is a kit verb ('kit agile census' with the flags DEPS-DONE, PAUSED-NO-RESUME, PAUSED-BY-RULE, STALE, WAITS-USER) written in Spiral; until then it stays as glue. (2) register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 (scheduled-task registration for the backup and the profile mirror) is machine glue that touches several repos: it stays in i574n.github/scripts. (3) node-kit-switch.ps1 is node glue for kit's rename: it belongs in kit/scripts (one project). Move it when it next changes, with its KIT-RENAME n62/memory pointers updated. kit/scripts gained release-train/launch-train changes plus train-hold.ps1, resume-train-if-starved.ps1, notebook-batch.ps1, regen-sizes.ps1 and candidate-build.ps1 (all kit-only, in kit's repo as the rule wants). Those three train helpers and notebook-batch are verb candidates too ('kit train hold|resume', 'kit notebooks <modules>'), filed on EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN. No .py was added.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_3 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 3u32, "2026-10-31T21:12Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 16:5x tibia's share (unstaged; deletions show as D in i574n.github). (1) lib-program-gate.ps1 MOVED to spiral/apps/cells/spi/lib_program_gate.ps1, hash-identical, beside lib_gate.ps1 and named in that folder's snake_case. No code caller (git grep across spiral, tibia, kit, x, fiscal, i574n.github; only backlog notes name it); the memories now point to the new path. (2) slice-roundtrip-sweep.ps1 RETIRED, not moved: it duplicated spiral's apps/cells/spi/lib_roundtrip.exs, which also writes the canonical bytes. A/B on the same good and bad drafts gave the same verdicts (good passes; a missing final newline fails both). Git history keeps the old file. (3) Left on purpose: tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 is tibia's project, but resilience wrote it and a daily 05:20 scheduled task calls it by this path, so moving it to tibia/scripts is resilience's call (task path and file together). recovered-drafts-census.ps1 is org-wide recovery tooling (resilience's area; a kit-command candidate), not tibia-specific. land-lib-program.ps1 and lib-guarded-do.ps1 are the shared lib-landing tools (x's and main's), also spiral lib tooling for their owners to move.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_4 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 4u32, "2026-10-31T22:51Z", "resilience", "10-31 18:2x resilience (git-51) DECISION on the scripts I added (user flagged the .py flood). SPLIT: (1) ARCHIVE as one-shot (the 10-28 wipe is recovered): i574n.github/scripts/wipe-recovery/ (46 .py forensic/undelete/restore scripts + recover.py + recovery_config.py + RUNBOOK.md, 98 KB). These ran once; not living org tooling. Archiving to the node remote-archive, restorable; memory undelete-bitlocker-trim + WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT point at it; if another wipe hits, restore the dir. (2) KEEP, but as PORT TARGETS for this item (scheduled-task entry scripts, run unattended daily, a recognized exception like kit's own .ps1 task): profile-mirror.ps1, profile-mirror-if-due.ps1, profile-restore-drill.ps1 (+ profile-restore-drill-node.py), config-baseline.ps1, tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1, register-scheduled-tasks.ps1. Under spiral-first-tooling these should become kit commands in Spiral; until ported they stay because the durability tasks depend on them. No NEW ad-hoc .py/.ps1 from this lane going forward; further resilience work is kit commands or notes.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_5 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 5u32, "2026-10-31T23:00Z", "x", "2026-10-31 19:00 x: x's share of the 10-31 .ps1 drift (main's all-lanes request), decided.\n(1) MERGED and MOVED: i574n.github/scripts/x-node-verify.ps1 and x-node-e2e.ps1 (both x-only) are now ONE project script, x/scripts/node-run.ps1 -Label -Mode verify|sim|parity [-Core -Part -NoAccept]. It reaches node-proof.ps1 and remote.ps1 through ../../i574n.github/scripts, parse-checked, and nothing in code called the old pair. The old files are archived (kit archive 20261031-185938). Git: x-node-verify shows ' D', and x-node-e2e shows 'AD' because the user had staged it mid-run, so the user's index still holds that add.\n(2) PORT TARGET, one command: x-compat-census.ps1 (i574n.github, cross-repo SpiralCompiler --x-compat overweight/mention counts) and x/scripts/postable-report.ps1 (xc post-thread --dry-run aggregated per repo) are two censuses of one fact, cell postability. End state: one Spiral 'xc postable census <repos>' subcommand in the x client (Spiral to Rust), reading the one typed postability source of POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE. Both scripts stay as glue until that lands, then go to the archive. No new .ps1 for it.\n(3) CELLS-IN-SPIRAL adds no .ps1. Today's two drafts were folded into notes (the lib-ref applier text in CELLS-SPI-LIB n2, the Kino-alias probe method in CELLS-CENSUS n3) and archived (kit archive 20261031-185252). The node probe dir C:\\home\\remote-stage\\x-kino-alias is removed.\nGeneric remainder for the kit team, a request only: 'read the node LOCALAPPDATA, launch node-proof with -RequireCore, retry 4 times printing the last 8 lines' is what every lane's node launcher repeats, so it belongs in a kit verb ('kit node proof --mirror --core --command-file').")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_6 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 6u32, "2026-10-31T23:10Z", "resilience", "10-31 19:1x resilience (git-51): executed tibia's request (PS1-TO-SPIRAL n17 classifies tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 as tibia-specific glue). Moved i574n.github/scripts/tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 -> C:\\home\\git\\tibia\\scripts\\tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 (its repo), and repointed the daily 05:20 scheduled task to the new path IN THE SAME CHANGE (register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 gains a \\ var = <git>\\tibia\\scripts; dry run: only tibia-mariadb-dump changes, 6 others unchanged). Proven: task action now the tibia path, test-run produced canary-20261031-190849.sql. So i574n.github/scripts no longer holds a tibia-specific script; the remaining durability scripts there are cross-machine infra (profile-mirror, restore-drill, config-baseline, register) still pending the Spiral port.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_7 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 7u32, "2026-11-03T07:45Z", "resilience", "11-03 03:4x resilience GROOM status: the .py FLOOD IS RESOLVED - 0 .py in i574n.github/scripts (was 50 per n1): wipe-recovery/ archived+removed, no profile-restore-drill-node.py left. Verified scripts/pins/dist .exe/.pdb/.rs (~9.7MB) are GITIGNORED local build output (git check-ignore confirms; not tracked) - not committed, no cleanup. REMAINING resilience share = port the durability scheduled-task .ps1 (profile-mirror, profile-mirror-if-due, profile-restore-drill, config-baseline, register-scheduled-tasks) to Spiral kit commands per spiral-first-tooling; box-gated (needs a compile + careful test since the daily tasks depend on them), tracked here + on PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT. NOTE: .ps1 count is 64 (up from n1's 56) - ongoing glue (de-leak node-env, etc.); the net goal is still fewer-via-Spiral-port, which waits on the box. Resilience's .py obligation under this item is DONE; the .ps1-to-Spiral port is the open piece.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_8 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 8u32, "2026-11-03T15:14Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:14 x: groom: x share verified NONE. No script in i574n.github/scripts is x-specific (name scan for x/xc/xsim/tweet/postable) or reads x's tree (content scan for git\\x\\ and apps/client). x's glue lives in x/scripts. x tag removed.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_9 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 9u32, "2026-11-03T16:17Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:3x tibia: tibia share checked, nothing to move. 10 of i574n.github/scripts mention tibia, all as one entry in a cross-repo list or org orchestration: build.ps1 and init.ps1 (org init/build calling tibia scripts/init.ps1 and build.ps1), crate-gate-all, pages-sweep, recovered-drafts-census (repo lists), config-baseline, hooks-test, profile-mirror, register-scheduled-tasks, resource-report (machine-wide). No tibia-only script lives there; tibia scripts are in tibia/scripts.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_10 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 10u32, "2026-11-04T11:21Z", "tibia", "11-04 07:3x tibia: dropped the tibia tag; tibia's share was checked on 11-03 12:3x with nothing to move (its 10 mentions are org-level cross-repo lists). The tag kept the item on the stop gate's list of ready tibia work.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_11 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 11u32, "2026-11-05T04:28Z", "resilience", "CLASSIFICATION (resilience, 62 .ps1 inventoried). Two sub-goals already DONE: (a) .py porting complete - 0 .py files remain in scripts/; (b) no project-specific stragglers - the dir is already cross-repo glue (app scripts already live in their repos, e.g. x\\scripts\\). Remaining reduction = fold GENERIC machinery that now duplicates kit verbs into kit commands, by cluster: PROCESS-HEALTH orphan-reaper/dangling-census/host-dupes-census/node-watch/node-utilization-monitor -> kit machine watch family; JOB-RUNNING serial-runner/queue-serial/live-wait/job-stop -> kit jobs; FS-GUARDS safe-delete -> rust_std_fs rooted policy (see DELETE-ROOT-GUARD); MIRROR/BACKUP profile-mirror*/critical-mirror/unstaged-backup -> kit archive/mirror verbs (profile-restore-drill already tracked as PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT); CENSUS/GATE memory-integrity-sweep/crate-gate-all/banned-words-scan/bang-export-rewrite/recovered-drafts-census/config-baseline -> kit verbs. THIN GLUE that legitimately stays .ps1 (pwsh wrapping kit/ssh): remote, node-env, watch-ids, register-scheduled-tasks. Each fold is kit-gated (needs the kit verb to exist first) and should carry its own small task; classification is the un-gated deliverable. resilience.")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_12 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 12u32, "2026-11-07T22:16Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: i574n.github/scripts holds only cross-repo glue; each of the 62 .ps1 is classified (keep / move to its repo / becomes a kit verb), and the classified moves are done; 0 .py (done). Next step: take resilience's 11-05 classification and file the kit-verb candidates as kit items. TypeFeatures: the classification as a union (CrossRepoGlue | ProjectScript of repo | KitVerb of name).")
inl note_of_org_scripts_home_13 () = Note ("ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME", 13u32, "2026-11-09T15:47Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:5x NEXT STEP DONE: resilience's 11-05 classification filed as one kit-verb fold item per cluster (team:rig, each with DoD/Next step/TypeFeatures): KIT-FOLD-PROCESS-HEALTH (orphan-reaper, dangling-census, host-dupes-census, node-watch, node-utilization-monitor), KIT-FOLD-JOB-RUNNING (serial-runner, queue-serial, live-wait, job-stop), KIT-FOLD-MIRROR-BACKUP (profile-mirror x3, critical-mirror, unstaged-backup; spec from KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR n5), KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE (memory-integrity-sweep, crate-gate-all, banned-words-scan, bang-export-rewrite, recovered-drafts-census, config-baseline); FS-GUARDS was already DELETE-ROOT-GUARD. Checked first: all 22 scripts still exist (none folded since 11-05) and no open item covered the four clusters. They are now this item's deps, so it leaves the ready pool honestly instead of sitting there un-actionable for org. Stays .ps1 by design: remote, node-env, watch-ids, register-scheduled-tasks (thin glue around kit/ssh).")
inl postability_one_source () = Task ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", "Postability data (the x profile JSON and the TLD list) has one typed source instead of byte-identical .txt/.json copies in x, spiral Cells (priv + test fixtures) and tibia; profiles are selected by name, not by a copied postability/ folder", Story, P1, D3, 70u32, Blocked, "", "team:microblog,cells,microblog,tibia,data,drift,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_postability_one_source () = Planning ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_postability_one_source_1 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 1u32, "2026-10-31T20:46Z", "main", "10-31 16:46 main. USER 10-31 ~16:3x: 'can we pivot this postability txt and json from the repos? seems like a major drift having these formats and copies'. CENSUS: the same two data files are copied byte-identical across repos: tlds.txt (7,516 B, 40806CDA1613) x4 = x/postability (tracked), spiral apps/cells/priv (tracked), spiral apps/cells/test/fixtures/postability (untracked), tibia/postability (untracked); x.json (1,251 B, CD95B0C1D176: profile x, weight_limit 280, link_weight 23, code-point weight ranges) x3 = x/postability (tracked), Cells test fixtures (untracked), tibia/postability (untracked); plus x/scripts/postable-report.ps1. ROOT CAUSE: Cells' x_compat.ex loads the TLD set from its own priv/tlds.txt and picks a profile by walking up from the checked file to the NEAREST postability/ folder (nearest_profile, x_compat.ex:51; SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE overrides), so every repo that wants postability checks carries its own copy. PIVOT: (1) one source of truth, as Spiral code rather than .txt/.json (the user prefers other languages over loose data files; memory no-py-txt-in-repos): the profile as a typed record and the TLD set as a lib module (or Cells-owned data generated from it), with a test that pins its digest; (2) profile selection by NAME (a project's spiral.toml or the env var), not by finding a copied folder; (3) delete every copy (archive first), x's postable-report reads the same source; (4) dangling check by stem (postability, tlds, x.json, x_compat) before removal. Owners: Cells (main) for the reader, x for the profile's content.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_2 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 2u32, "2026-10-31T21:18Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 17:1x tibia. A THIRD READER the census misses: the compiler's own --x-compat (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, postabilityProfilePath and postabilityProfileOfFile near line 34238, compiler lane). It takes SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE, else the nearest ancestor postability/*.json (first file after sort), then loads the TLD list from the file the JSON names in links.top_level_domains_file, relative to the JSON. tibia's build gate (tibia/scripts/build.ps1: --x-compat over src and apps) and x's --x-compat runs go through this reader, not Cells' x_compat.ex. So the pivot has to change both readers together, or tibia's gate breaks. Why tibia has a copy: tibia's CI has no x checkout, so on 10-30 build.ps1 got tibia/postability/ (x.json + tlds.txt) plus a drift check against a sibling ../x/postability when one exists. tibia's steps once both readers select the profile by NAME from a source tibia's deps/spiral already carries: build.ps1 names profile x (env or spiral.toml, whichever the pivot picks), its copy and drift check are deleted, and tibia/postability/ is archived. Until then tibia keeps the copy, which the drift check pins to x's bytes.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_3 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 3u32, "2026-10-31T21:26Z", "main", "10-31 17:26 main, first read of the reader (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/x_compat.ex, 234 lines): Cells' BUILT-IN default profile already IS the x profile. The Profile struct defaults (x_compat.ex:6-19) carry link_weight 23, default_weight 2, ranges {0,4351,1} {8192,8205,1} {8208,8223,1} {8242,8247,1}, short_domains t.co, and default_profile() adds the TLD set from priv/tlds.txt plus compiled hashtag/mention/cashtag/domain regexes. x.json's values match those defaults field for field (weight_limit 280, link_weight 23, default 2, the same 4 ranges), so every copied postability/x.json only reproduces the default. The copies exist because profile_for (x_compat.ex:51) prefers the env var, then the NEAREST postability/*.json walking up from the file. PLAN, simplest first: (1) a Cells test that loads x.json through cached_profile and asserts it equals default_profile() on every field (pins the equivalence, incl. the json's links/entities/posting sections); (2) if it holds, delete the copies in tibia and the Cells test fixtures (archive first) and keep x/postability/x.json only while x's postable-report.ps1 reads it; (3) one TLD source: Cells priv/tlds.txt, with x's report reading the same file or a generated Spiral module; (4) later, per the user's language preference, move the profile out of Elixir/JSON into a Spiral record that Cells and x both consume.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_4 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 4u32, "2026-11-01T03:05Z", "main", "main 23:05: copies removed. (1) Cells postability_profile_test.exs no longer reads a copied fixture: it builds x's profile inline from XCompat.default_profile plus the poster rule (defused_dot before [A-Za-z0-9_-], after [A-Za-z]) and copies priv/tlds.txt into a tmp dir at run time; same 4 assertions; landed green via cells_land_window (8/8 with x_compat_test, scratch proof without the fixture dir 8/8), test EC55DB487F84. (2) spiral/apps/cells/test/fixtures/postability and tibia/postability (both untracked, byte-identical to x's) archived to kit\\archive 20261031-230434 and 20261031-230438 and removed. (3) tibia/scripts/build.ps1: the hash-parity check against a local copy replaced by SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE pointing at ../../x/postability/x.json (the compiler's --x-compat honors it); verified: exit 0, 65 files, 0 unprofiled, 0 overweight, 17 mentions. Remaining sources: x/postability (the X profile, owner x), spiral/apps/cells/priv/tlds.txt (Cells' built-in default; spiral cannot depend on x), and x/apps/client/tlds.spi, a Spiral twin of x's tlds.txt held equal by a test: handed to x to generate one from the other or drop the txt.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_5 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 5u32, "2026-11-01T03:06Z", "x", "2026-10-31 23:06 x: answer to main's 23:05 note. ONE SOURCE = x/postability/tlds.txt. x/apps/client/tlds.spi becomes GENERATED from it by a Spiral step.\nWhy the txt and not the .spi:\n(1) The txt is the upstream shape: IANA publishes tlds-alpha-by-domain.txt as one label per line, so an update is a download and a diff, never a hand edit of Spiral string chunks.\n(2) The profile format is data-driven for every network: links.top_level_domains_file is read at runtime by spiral_compiler.fs:34143 (--x-compat) and by Spiral.Cells.XCompat. A future mastodon or bluesky profile names its own list the same way, so a list compiled into one client can't be the source.\n(3) tlds.spi exists only because xc's Rust/Gleam binary has no data file at runtime. It is a build artifact of the txt.\nPlan (x, CPU-light, not tonight):\n- tlds.spi keeps is_tld and its chunks, and gains a generator function: the source text of the chunk literals, built from the txt through the existing file_tlds parser.\n- A small Spiral program (spiral run, not a new .ps1) writes apps/client/tlds.spi from postability/tlds.txt.\n- the_list_is_postability_tlds_txt stays as the drift gate. It already fails on any difference, so after a txt update the fix is to rerun the generator.\n- gate.ps1:56 keeps listing the txt as a data file.\nThird copy, found while checking: spiral/apps/cells/priv/tlds.txt is hash-identical (40806CDA1613) and is x_compat.ex's @tlds_path default (lines 2-4) plus postability_profile_test's fixture. It's main's: drop it once XCompat always resolves the profile's file (or when CELLS-IN-SPIRAL ports XCompat), with the default pointing at ../x/postability/tlds.txt like tibia's build.ps1 does.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_6 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 6u32, "2026-11-01T03:10Z", "main", "main 23:1x: user disliked the Mix/OTP name priv; apps/cells/priv split by purpose: tlds.txt -> apps/cells/data/tlds.txt, new_project scaffold -> apps/cells/templates/new_project. Readers updated (x_compat.ex, new_project.ex, compiler_daemon.ex source_stamp, postability_profile_test.exs, README); new_project/postability_profile/warm_notebook/x_compat tests 14/14. Nothing used :code.priv_dir, so leaving the convention costs nothing.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_7 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 7u32, "2026-11-01T03:23Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 tibia: tibia's share DONE (unstaged in tibia). main removed the untracked tibia/postability copy. The CI gate comes back with x as the single source: gh-pages.yml's build job checks out i574n/x (public) into .x (sparse: postability) with the already-locked actions/checkout@v7.0.1, so actions.lock needs no refresh, and it sets SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE to .x/postability/x.json. build.ps1 takes that variable first, then a sibling ../../x/postability/x.json, else main's loud SKIPPED with a ::warning. Proof through build.ps1 -Files no-such-file: sibling -> every cell fits / 17 mentions; env -> a weight-100 copy -> throws (2776 over), so the env path is the one checked.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_8 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 8u32, "2026-11-01T03:24Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 tibia: CORRECTION. n7 is REVERTED on the user's direction (\"why the hell tibia is referencing x? spiral should be x compatible but in a generic way (cells), we shouldn't even know that x exists\"). gh-pages.yml is back to its committed state (no x checkout, no SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE). scripts/build.ps1 has NO x reference: the postable step is an unconditional LOUD skip (message plus GitHub ::warning) until Cells' generic check (mix spiral.x_compat --check, built-in defaults, no profile file) and tibia's :: respell (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SpiralCompiler format --spelling symbols) land. git grep finds 0 x references in tibia outside deps. Memory: postability-generic-no-x.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_9 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 9u32, "2026-11-01T03:32Z", "main", "main 23:3x, user direction 10-31 23:2x: 'spiral should be x compatible but in a generic way (cells), we shouldn't even know that x exists'; no repo references x. Done: Cells is the one checker with built-in defaults; mix spiral.x_compat --check adds the per-definition overweight rule (exit 1 only on overweight), the compiler's folder skip list, and a crash fix for non-ASCII next to a dot; parity with the compiler --x-compat under x's profile is exact on lib 1459, tibia 17, x 2 (landed 23:31, 9/9). tibia reverted every x reference (CI checkout and build.ps1); its postable step is skipped loudly until it respells. Measured: tibia respelled to :: (format --spelling symbols) under the default has autolinks 562 -> 9 (Lua inside macros) and overweight 51 -> 2. Remaining: (1) tibia respell + switch to the Cells check (tibia); (2) x's builds switch to the Cells check; (3) the compiler retires --x-compat, its XCompat section and the postability/*.json lookup, and Cells drops profile loading after (1)-(2); x/postability then serves only x's own poster; (4) every repo respells to :: (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX migration round), after which the TLD list and dot-defusing can go too.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_10 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 10u32, "2026-11-01T03:41Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 23:41 compiler, cadence groom: Step 3 SCHEDULED (main 23:33): retire --x-compat, the XCompat section and the postability/*.json lookup from the compiler. Cells owns the check now, with parity proven on lib/tibia/x. Starts only after x and tibia both switch their gates to the Cells check (resume condition: a note from each lane saying the old flag is unused); the compiler applier rides the next pack after that.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_11 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 11u32, "2026-11-01T03:43Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 tibia NEXT STEP (CPU-light, no window): (1) respell tibia src and apps in place with `SpiralCompiler format ../src ../apps --spelling symbols` (main's scratch: autolinks 562 -> 9, overweight 51 -> 2); (2) split the 2 near-limit cells, host/character.spi:116 (276 > 272) and host/world_port.spi:67 (274 > 272); (3) replace build.ps1's loud skip with `mix spiral.x_compat --check ../src ../apps` run from deps/spiral/apps/cells (exit 1 only on overweight). Proof: build.ps1 -Files no-such-file prints the check passing, plus one full test file to show the respell compiles.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_12 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 12u32, "2026-11-01T03:53Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 01:xx tibia: tibia's share LANDED in tibia (unstaged), with no x anywhere (git grep: 0 references). (1) Respell: SpiralCompiler format ../src ../apps --spelling symbols changed 61 of 65 files (x.y -> x::y, test -> :#). (2) The respell pushed lines past 120, so a plain format re-laid 10 files; that re-lay pushed 3 cells over a post, and 2 more were over before it. All split without behaviour change: gpu_sim hunt_and_clear_facts (local clears -> c), gpu_sim routed_hunt_matches (fixture for the WGSL routing test), search nudge_key (fixture), character expected_kit_where (fixture; same SQL bytes), world_port fake_log (fixture). (3) scripts/build.ps1's postable step is now Cells' generic check: from deps/spiral/apps/cells, mix spiral.x_compat --check <tibia src> <tibia apps> (scoop erlang/elixir prepended when present, as run_notebook.ps1 does), and it throws on a non-zero exit. Proof through build.ps1 -Files no-such-file: layout clean, then \"postable / x-compat report: 26 finding(s) in 65 file(s) (autolink 9, mention 17)\", 0 overweight; the arena and canary Lua builds compiled on the respelled sources. Negative: an overweight scratch cell makes the Cells check exit 1. PENDING: the full test suite on the respelled tree (node job queued behind the consumer regate, task b82qie3po). The 9 autolinks are Lua host text inside macros (warnings only).")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_13 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 13u32, "2026-11-01T04:38Z", "x", "2026-11-01 00:38 x: RE-DECIDED n5's generator, now DEFERRED with a written condition. Three facts since n5: (1) n9 step 4 retires the TLD list itself once every repo respells to :: (autolinks 562 -> 9 on tibia), so a generator would build tooling for a list slated for deletion. (2) The twin can't drift silently today: the_list_is_postability_tlds_txt fails on any difference between tlds.spi and tlds.txt, and gate.ps1:56 tracks the txt. (3) The generator isn't a copy: tlds.spi's 40 literals in groups of 6 exist so each definition stays under the per-post weight (271), so it has to re-pack under that limit. Decision: keep tlds.txt as the single source (n5) with the equality test as the enforcement. Write the generator ONLY IF tlds.txt has to change before n9 step 4 lands (an IANA update x needs). Otherwise x's share here closes when step 4 removes both files.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_14 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 14u32, "2026-11-01T04:52Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 01:xx tibia: the gate now uses the generic name (CELL-BUDGET-NAMING, landed 00:45). scripts/build.ps1's step is labelled \"cell budget\" and runs `mix spiral.cell_budget --check <tibia src> <tibia apps>` from deps/spiral/apps/cells; it reports over_budget lines and throws on a non-zero exit. No x_compat, postable, overweight or x left in build.ps1. Proof: the check on tibia gives \"cell-budget report: 26 finding(s) in 65 file(s) (autolink 9, mention 17)\", exit 0; the scratch negative gives over_budget 568 > 273, exit 1.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_15 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 15u32, "2026-11-01T05:11Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 02:xx tibia: CORRECTION to n12 and n14. The :: respell also respelled `test` to `:#`, and scripts/build.ps1 discovered test files with the pattern '^test ', so after the respell it matched 0 of 56 files: \"no test files matched\". A full run would have tested nothing, and CI would have failed or proven nothing. Found when the offscreen check reported \"no test files matched offscreen\". FIXED: the discovery pattern is '^(test|:#) ' (all 56 files found again); no other tibia script assumes the old spelling (27 scanned). The full suite on the respelled tree is rerunning on the node with the fixed script (tibia-respell-full-build2); until it passes, the respell is unproven beyond the Lua builds and the cell-budget and layout gates.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_16 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 16u32, "2026-11-01T06:07Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 02:07 compiler: STEP 3 DRAFTED (ready, lands in PACK-12 once x and tibia confirm the Cells check). One kit do program, 4 replacements in 2 files: core spiral_compiler.fs loses the whole '/// ## XCompat' section (243 lines, 34071-34313: XCompatKind/Finding, PostabilityProfile, postabilityProfile*, xCompat* incl. the postability/*.json lookup and SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE) and the 'xCompatWarnEntry file' hook in the build path (34976). Host tmp/compiler/host/Program.fs loses runXCompatReport (1251-1284) and the '--x-compat' CLI branch, and '--check' no longer warns (its xCompatWarnEntry call goes). Dry-applied on copies: 0 references left; every name the section defines is unused outside it (only the removed host fn and hook used them). Bases: spiral_compiler.fs C0990B2D590CE965, Program.fs 420E1452DB4B3194. CONSUMERS to tell at land time: tibia README.md:20 says 'measured with SpiralCompiler --x-compat' (doc to update), and apps/zed spiral_zed.rs:1749 parses XC00n warnings from --check stderr (its unit test uses a fixture string and stays green, but editor diagnostics for postability vanish unless Cells' check feeds zed; owner x). No other repo calls --x-compat (grep x, tibia, kit, fiscal, i574n.github, dice, polyglot).\nPROGRAM (kit do <dir holding spiral_compiler.fs and Program.fs> -):\nedit spiral_compiler.fs expect files 1 replacements 2\n  replace once <<<\n    /// ## XCompat\n    type XCompatKind =\n        | XCompatHashtag\n        | XCompatMention\n        | XCompatCashtag\n        | XCompatAutolink\n        | XCompatOverweight\n\n    /// ### XCompatFinding\n    type XCompatFinding = { kind : XCompatKind; line : int; column : int; text : string }\n\n    /// ### xCompatKindName\n    let xCompatKindName kind =\n        match kind with\n        | XCompatHashtag -> \"hashtag\"\n        | XCompatMention -> \"mention\"\n        | XCompatCashtag -> \"cashtag\"\n        | XCompatAutolink -> \"autolink\"\n        | XCompatOverweight -> \"overweight\"\n\n    /// ### xCompatCode\n    let xCompatCode kind =\n        match kind with\n        | XCompatHashtag -> \"XC001\"\n        | XCompatMention -> \"XC002\"\n        | XCompatCashtag -> \"XC003\"\n        | XCompatAutolink -> \"XC004\"\n        | XCompatOverweight -> \"XC005\"\n\n    /// ### xCompatHint\n    let xCompatHint kind =\n        match kind with\n        | XCompatHashtag -> \"X turns '#' before a letter into a hashtag link\"\n        | XCompatMention -> \"X turns '@' before a name into a mention\"\n        | XCompatCashtag -> \"X turns '$' before letters into a cashtag link\"\n        | XCompatAutolink -> \"X shortens what looks like a domain to a 23-character t.co link\"\n        | XCompatOverweight -> \"one post holds 280 weighted characters (CJK and emoji weigh 2, links 23), less the cell's cN k/n header line and 1 per defused link dot; split this definition\"\n\n    /// ### PostabilityProfile\n    type PostabilityProfile =\n        {\n            name : string\n            weightLimit : int\n            linkWeight : int\n            defaultWeight : int\n            weightRanges : (int * int * int) list\n            domainPattern : Text.RegularExpressions.Regex\n            topLevelDomains : Set<string>\n            shortDomainsLinked : Set<string>\n            twoLetterSecondLabelLongerThan : int\n            entityPatterns : (XCompatKind * Text.RegularExpressions.Regex) list\n            onePostHeader : string\n            headerSeparator : string\n            defusedBefore : Text.RegularExpressions.Regex\n            defusedAfter : Text.RegularExpressions.Regex\n            defusedExtraWeight : int\n        }\n\n    /// ### postabilityProfileOfFile\n    let postabilityProfileOfFile (path : string) : PostabilityProfile =\n        use document = Text.Json.JsonDocument.Parse (IO.File.ReadAllText path)\n        let root = document.RootElement\n        let at (element : Text.Json.JsonElement) (name : string) = element.GetProperty name\n        let text (element : Text.Json.JsonElement) (name : string) = (at element name).GetString ()\n        let number (element : Text.Json.JsonElement) (name : string) = (at element name).GetInt32 ()\n        let regex (pattern : string) = Text.RegularExpressions.Regex pattern\n        let post = at root \"post\"\n        let weights = at root \"code_point_weight\"\n        let links = at root \"links\"\n        let entities = at root \"entities\"\n        let posting = at root \"posting\"\n        let defused = at posting \"defused_dot\"\n        let domainsFile = IO.Path.Combine (IO.Path.GetDirectoryName (IO.Path.GetFullPath path), text links \"top_level_domains_file\")\n        {\n            name = text root \"profile\"\n            weightLimit = number post \"weight_limit\"\n            linkWeight = number post \"link_weight\"\n            defaultWeight = number weights \"default\"\n            weightRanges = [ for range in (at weights \"ranges\").EnumerateArray () -> range.[0].GetInt32 (), range.[1].GetInt32 (), range.[2].GetInt32 () ]\n            domainPattern = regex (text links \"domain_pattern\")\n            topLevelDomains = IO.File.ReadAllLines domainsFile |> Array.map (fun line -> line.Trim ()) |> Array.filter (fun line -> line <> \"\") |> Set.ofArray\n            shortDomainsLinked = [ for domain in (at links \"short_domains_always_linked\").EnumerateArray () -> domain.GetString () ] |> Set.ofList\n            twoLetterSecondLabelLongerThan = number links \"two_letter_tld_needs_second_label_longer_than\"\n            entityPatterns = [ XCompatHashtag, regex (text entities \"hashtag\"); XCompatMention, regex (text entities \"mention\"); XCompatCashtag, regex (text entities \"cashtag\") ]\n            onePostHeader = text posting \"budget_header_for_one_post\"\n            headerSeparator = text posting \"header_separator\"\n            defusedBefore = regex (\"^\" + text defused \"before\" + \"$\")\n            defusedAfter = regex (\"^\" + text defused \"after\" + \"$\")\n            defusedExtraWeight = number defused \"extra_weight\"\n        }\n\n    /// ### postabilityProfilePath\n    let postabilityProfilePath (file : string) : string option =\n        match Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable \"SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE\" with\n        | null | \"\" ->\n            let rec nearest (directory : string) =\n                if isNull directory then None\n                else\n                    let folder = IO.Path.Combine (directory, \"postability\")\n                    let found = if IO.Directory.Exists folder then IO.Directory.GetFiles (folder, \"*.json\") |> Array.sort |> Array.tryHead else None\n                    match found with\n                    | Some profile -> Some profile\n                    | None -> nearest (IO.Path.GetDirectoryName directory)\n            nearest (IO.Path.GetDirectoryName (IO.Path.GetFullPath file))\n        | path -> Some path\n\n    /// ### postabilityProfiles\n    let postabilityProfiles = Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentDictionary<string, PostabilityProfile> ()\n\n    /// ### postabilityProfileFor\n    let postabilityProfileFor (file : string) : PostabilityProfile option =\n        postabilityProfilePath file |> Option.map (fun path -> postabilityProfiles.GetOrAdd (IO.Path.GetFullPath path, postabilityProfileOfFile))\n\n    /// ### xCompatLinks\n    let xCompatLinks (profile : PostabilityProfile) (link : string) (topLevelDomain : string) =\n        if not (profile.topLevelDomains.Contains topLevelDomain) then false\n        elif profile.shortDomainsLinked.Contains (link.ToLowerInvariant ()) then true\n        elif topLevelDomain.Length = 2 then\n            let labels = link.Split '.'\n            labels.[labels.Length - 2].Length > profile.twoLetterSecondLabelLongerThan\n        else true\n\n    /// ### xCompatCodePointWeight\n    let xCompatCodePointWeight (profile : PostabilityProfile) (codePoint : int) =\n        match profile.weightRanges |> List.tryFind (fun (low, high, _) -> codePoint >= low && codePoint <= high) with\n        | Some (_, _, weight) -> weight\n        | None -> profile.defaultWeight\n\n    /// ### xCompatDefusedAt\n    let xCompatDefusedAt (profile : PostabilityProfile) (text : string) (i : int) =\n        i > 0 && i + 1 < text.Length && text.[i] = '.'\n        && profile.defusedBefore.IsMatch (string text.[i - 1]) && profile.defusedAfter.IsMatch (string text.[i + 1])\n\n    /// ### xCompatPostedLink\n    let xCompatPostedLink (profile : PostabilityProfile) (text : string) (found : Text.RegularExpressions.Match) =\n        let undefusedDot = seq { found.Index .. found.Index + found.Length - 1 } |> Seq.exists (fun i -> text.[i] = '.' && not (xCompatDefusedAt profile text i))\n        undefusedDot && xCompatLinks profile found.Value (found.Groups.[1].Value.ToLowerInvariant ())\n\n    /// ### xCompatPostWeight\n    let xCompatPostWeight (profile : PostabilityProfile) (post : string) =\n        let links = [ for found in profile.domainPattern.Matches post do if xCompatPostedLink profile post found then yield found ]\n        let unlinked = links |> List.rev |> List.fold (fun (rest : string) found -> rest.Remove (found.Index, found.Length)) post\n        let characters = unlinked.EnumerateRunes () |> Seq.sumBy (fun rune -> xCompatCodePointWeight profile rune.Value)\n        characters + profile.linkWeight * links.Length\n\n    /// ### xCompatTopLevelBlocks\n    let xCompatTopLevelBlocks (lines : string []) =\n        let lines = if lines.Length > 0 && lines.[lines.Length - 1] = \"\" then lines.[.. lines.Length - 2] else lines\n        let cells = Collections.Generic.List<int * string> ()\n        let current = Collections.Generic.List<string> ()\n        let mutable start = 1\n        let mutable blanks = 0\n        let mutable seen = false\n        let finish () = if current.Count > 0 then cells.Add (start, String.Join(\"\\n\", current).TrimEnd ())\n        for index in 0 .. lines.Length - 1 do\n            let line = lines.[index]\n            if line = \"\" then blanks <- blanks + 1\n            elif blanks > 0 && seen && not (line.StartsWith \" \" || line.StartsWith \"\\t\") then\n                finish ()\n                current.Clear ()\n                for _ in 2 .. blanks do current.Add \"\"\n                current.Add line\n                start <- index + 1\n                blanks <- 0\n            else\n                for _ in 1 .. blanks do current.Add \"\"\n                current.Add line\n                if not seen then start <- index + 1\n                blanks <- 0\n                seen <- true\n        finish ()\n        List.ofSeq cells\n\n    /// ### xCompatDefusedDots\n    let xCompatDefusedDots (profile : PostabilityProfile) (block : string) =\n        seq { 1 .. block.Length - 2 } |> Seq.filter (xCompatDefusedAt profile block) |> Seq.length\n\n    /// ### xCompatPostableLimit\n    let xCompatPostableLimit (profile : PostabilityProfile) (cell : int) (block : string) =\n        profile.weightLimit - xCompatPostWeight profile (profile.onePostHeader.Replace (\"{block}\", string cell) + profile.headerSeparator) - profile.defusedExtraWeight * xCompatDefusedDots profile block\n\n    /// ### xCompatOverweightFindings\n    let xCompatOverweightFindings (profile : PostabilityProfile) (lines : string []) =\n        [ for position, (row, block) in List.indexed (xCompatTopLevelBlocks lines) do\n            let weight = xCompatPostWeight profile block\n            let limit = xCompatPostableLimit profile (position + 1) block\n            if weight > limit then\n                yield { kind = XCompatOverweight; line = row; column = 1; text = $\"weight {weight} > {limit} ({profile.weightLimit} minus the c{position + 1} k/n header and defused dots)\" } ]\n\n    /// ### xCompatLineFindings\n    let xCompatLineFindings (profile : PostabilityProfile) (line : string) (row : int) =\n        let marks = profile.entityPatterns |> List.collect (fun (kind, pattern) -> [ for found in pattern.Matches line -> kind, found.Index, found.Value ])\n        let links =\n            [ for found in profile.domainPattern.Matches line do\n                if xCompatPostedLink profile line found then yield XCompatAutolink, found.Index, found.Value ]\n        marks @ links\n        |> List.sortBy (fun (_, start, _) -> start)\n        |> List.map (fun (kind, start, text) ->\n            { kind = kind; line = row; column = Globalization.StringInfo(line.Substring (0, start)).LengthInTextElements + 1; text = text })\n\n    /// ### xCompatFindings\n    let xCompatFindings (profile : PostabilityProfile) (source : string) =\n        let lines = source.Replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").Split '\\n'\n        let marks = lines |> List.ofArray |> List.mapi (fun index line -> xCompatLineFindings profile line (index + 1)) |> List.concat\n        marks @ xCompatOverweightFindings profile lines |> List.sortBy (fun finding -> finding.line, finding.column)\n    /// ### xCompatReportLine\n    let xCompatReportLine (path : string) (finding : XCompatFinding) =\n        $\"{path}:{finding.line}:{finding.column}: {xCompatKindName finding.kind}: {finding.text} ({xCompatHint finding.kind})\"\n\n    /// ### xCompatWarningLine\n    let xCompatWarningLine (path : string) (finding : XCompatFinding) =\n        $\"warning: {path}:{finding.line}:{finding.column}: {xCompatCode finding.kind} {xCompatKindName finding.kind}: {finding.text} ({xCompatHint finding.kind})\"\n\n    /// ### xCompatPackageEditionThree\n    let xCompatPackageEditionThree (file : string) =\n        let rec nearest (directory : string) =\n            if isNull directory then None\n            else\n                let toml = IO.Path.Combine (directory, \"spiral.toml\")\n                let project = if IO.File.Exists toml then toml else IO.Path.Combine (directory, \"package.spiproj\")\n                if IO.File.Exists project then Some project else nearest (IO.Path.GetDirectoryName directory)\n        match nearest (IO.Path.GetDirectoryName (IO.Path.GetFullPath file)) with\n        | Some project -> IO.File.ReadAllLines project |> Array.exists (fun line -> let t = line.Trim().Replace(\" \", \"\") in t = \"edition:3\" || t = \"edition=3\")\n        | None -> false\n\n    /// ### xCompatEnabled\n    let xCompatEnabled (file : string) =\n        Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable \"SPIRAL_X_COMPAT\" = \"1\" || (try xCompatPackageEditionThree file with _ -> false)\n\n    /// ### xCompatWarnedTexts\n    let xCompatWarnedTexts = Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentDictionary<string * string, unit> ()\n\n    /// ### xCompatWarnEntry\n    let xCompatWarnEntry (file : string) =\n        try\n            if xCompatEnabled file && IO.File.Exists file then\n                match postabilityProfileFor file with\n                | Some profile ->\n                    let text = IO.File.ReadAllText file\n                    if xCompatWarnedTexts.TryAdd ((file, text), ()) then\n                        for finding in xCompatFindings profile text do eprintfn \"%s\" (xCompatWarningLine file finding)\n                | None -> ()\n        with _ -> ()\n    /// ## SignalRSupervisor\n  >>> with <<<\n    /// ## SignalRSupervisor\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n                        if List.isEmpty entry_errors then dependency_warnings ()\n                        xCompatWarnEntry file\n                        let body() =\n  >>> with <<<\n                        if List.isEmpty entry_errors then dependency_warnings ()\n                        let body() =\n  >>>\nedit Program.fs expect files 1 replacements 2\n  replace once <<<\n    let private runXCompatReport (paths : string []) =\n        let extensions = set [ \".spi\"; \".spir\"; \".livemd\" ]\n        let files =\n            paths\n            |> Array.collect (fun path ->\n                if Directory.Exists path then\n                    filesUnder path (fun name -> List.contains name [ \"target\"; \"node_modules\"; \"deps\"; \"bin\"; \"obj\"; \"_build\"; \".git\"; \".history\" ])\n                    |> Array.ofSeq\n                    |> Array.filter (fun file -> extensions.Contains (Path.GetExtension file))\n                    |> Array.map (fun file -> file.Replace ('\\\\', '/'))\n                    |> Array.sort\n                elif File.Exists path then [| path |]\n                else [||])\n            |> Array.distinct\n        let profiled = files |> Array.map (fun file -> file, postabilityProfileFor file)\n        let unprofiled = profiled |> Array.choose (fun (file, profile) -> if profile.IsNone then Some file else None)\n        let findings =\n            [ for file, profile in profiled do\n                match profile with\n                | Some profile ->\n                    for finding in xCompatFindings profile (File.ReadAllText file) do yield file, finding\n                | None -> () ]\n        for file, finding in findings do printfn \"%s\" (xCompatReportLine file finding)\n        for file in unprofiled do\n            printfn \"%s: no postability profile (no postability/*.json in an ancestor directory and SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE unset)\" file\n        let byKind =\n            findings\n            |> List.countBy (fun (_, finding) -> xCompatKindName finding.kind)\n            |> List.sortBy fst\n            |> List.map (fun (kind, count) -> $\"{kind} {count}\")\n            |> String.concat \", \"\n        let unchecked = if unprofiled.Length = 0 then \"\" else $\", {unprofiled.Length} unchecked without a profile\"\n        printfn \"x-compat report: %d finding(s) in %d file(s)%s%s\" findings.Length files.Length (if byKind = \"\" then \"\" else $\" ({byKind})\") unchecked\n        if unprofiled.Length = 0 then 0 else 2\n\n    let reexecWithGen0Budget (rawArgv : string []) =\n  >>> with <<<\n    let reexecWithGen0Budget (rawArgv : string []) =\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n        elif argv.Length >= 2 && argv.[0] = \"--x-compat\" then\n            runXCompatReport argv.[1..]\n        elif argv.Length = 2 && argv.[0] = \"--check\" then\n            Spiral.spiral_compiler.xCompatWarnEntry argv.[1]\n  >>> with <<<\n        elif argv.Length = 2 && argv.[0] = \"--check\" then\n  >>>")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_17 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 17u32, "2026-11-01T07:23Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 03:23 compiler: step 3 program re-anchored on the post-PACK-12 core (796D343FB6E78D6E): still clean (4 replacements). Lives in the repo as apps/compiler/packs/pack13/2-retire-x-compat.kitdo, waiting for x and tibia to confirm they use the Cells check.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_18 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 18u32, "2026-11-01T07:45Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 03:45 tibia: the 61-file respell is proven on the node except for one regression of mine, character.spi's paren split, now fixed and green locally, and a node env gap (no wgsl runner) that is not caused by the respell. Detail: TIBIA-LIB-CONSUMER-REGATE, latest note. Build 3 is running on the node.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_19 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 19u32, "2026-11-01T12:40Z", "x", "2026-11-01 08:40 x: ITEM UPGRADE (round 4). Fields: tags gain team:x (it's a cross-lane item with main and tibia, and x owns the TLD half). DEFINITION OF DONE for x's half: either (a) n9 step 4 retires the TLD list, so x deletes tlds.txt and tlds.spi together and the equality test with them; or (b) tlds.txt must change before that, so tlds.spi is regenerated by a Spiral step and the_list_is_postability_tlds_txt passes. Artifact: the commit-ready diff. NEXT STEP: none until (a) or (b) triggers (n13). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN for (b): the generator packs labels into chunks typed 'chunk = { labels : list string; weight : i32 }' under the per-cell budget constant, never by counting characters in a joined string.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_20 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 20u32, "2026-11-01T17:14Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:12 compiler: DRAFT MOVED OUT OF THE REPO (user 11-01 13:0x rule: drafts live in the kit drafts store until ready as glue or types). retire-x-compat.kitdo now lives at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE\\retire-x-compat.kitdo (sha256 E405F44A0CDF..., byte-identical move, verified by hash). apps/compiler/drafts/ is gone (it was untracked, so git shows nothing). Gate unchanged: it ships in a pack only after x and tibia confirm the Cells check. When it ships, pass the store path to build-candidate.ps1 as the applier.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_21 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 21u32, "2026-11-02T01:22Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 21:2x tibia CONFIRMS its side of the gate on compiler's retire-x-compat (n: 'ships only after x and tibia confirm the Cells check'). git grep -i 'postab|x_compat|tld' over tibia src, apps, results and scripts finds 0 references. scripts/build.ps1 calls 'mix spiral.cell_budget --check' (under the erl memory guard), and its suite.spi decoder reads the 'cell-budget report' line typed (budget_report_of, with hashtag and cashtag kinds). Today's tibia CI runs 41350993071 (green) and 41366570407 (budget step green; red only in 4 unrelated test files) passed that check on both OS. Retiring --x-compat breaks nothing in tibia; only x's confirmation remains.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_22 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 22u32, "2026-11-02T17:17Z", "compiler", "11-02 13:20 compiler: STEP 3 (retire --x-compat) SCHEDULED for pack17. Gate status: tibia confirmed (n21). For x, a reader census today finds 0 references to x-compat / x_compat / xCompat in C:\\home\\git\\x and spiral/apps/cells; x was told it ships unless it objects before handover. retire-x-compat.kitdo (drafts store) still dry-applies on live (core 2 replacements at 34311/34972, host 2 at 1295/1351). It will be re-checked stacked on the pack16c list at pack time. CELL-BUDGET-NAMING closes when it installs (resilience routing 11-02).")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_23 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 23u32, "2026-11-02T17:19Z", "compiler", "11-02 13:25 compiler: x CONFIRMED step 3, on one condition, now met. The last live caller of --x-compat was i574n.github/scripts/x-compat-census.ps1:22 (tibia's POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS n142 census tool; 0 script callers, only backlog mentions, and its port target is x's `xc postable census`, POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS n160/n162). Archived to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261102-131918-x-compat-census\\ (hash 79A9D98719887909, verified equal) and DELETED from the worktree, unstaged (git status: \" D scripts/x-compat-census.ps1\"). The cell-budget check lives in Cells as `mix spiral.cell_budget --check`. Gate complete; retire-x-compat rides pack17.")
inl note_of_postability_one_source_24 () = Note ("POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE", 24u32, "2026-11-02T18:55Z", "compiler", "11-02 14:55 compiler: STEP 3 DONE. --x-compat is retired in the installed compiler (pack17, box 14:50). This closes the compiler side of CELL-BUDGET-NAMING (resilience routing 11-02); the cell-budget check is `mix spiral.cell_budget --check` in Cells.")
