inl node_always_fed () = Task ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", "The worker node never sits idle while heavy, node-runnable work exists: agile routes such items to the node, and an idle check pulls the next one (or alerts) when the node has no running or queued job", Story, P0, D3, 55u32, Active, "", "node,agile,scheduling,coordination,main,kit,remote,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_node_always_fed () = Planning ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_node_always_fed_1 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 1u32, "2026-10-31T21:48Z", "main", "10-31 17:48 main. USER 10-31 17:4x: 'why's the node idle? sign the lanes messed up coordination and agile'. MEASURED: at 17:42 the node had 0 running and 0 queued jobs; the last ones (kit verify-persist x2, compiler p11-speed x3, x parityprobe) had finished within the half hour. ROOT CAUSES: (1) no standing node queue: lanes send node jobs ad hoc while their current item needs them, so the node empties whenever no lane is mid-proof; (2) agile next ranks by priority/WSJF and load but knows nothing about machines, so heavy node-suitable items are never pulled to FILL the node; (3) 'keep the node busy' is only a memory (keep-node-busy), with no mechanism, and main itself left node-shaped work unqueued this afternoon (the Rust-lock re-measure, dice's lambda proof, a post-land lib sweep). IMMEDIATE (main): mirror synced (REMOTE-SYNC-OK, head fd70dccf) and job-1793483260661-main-lib-sweep queued: every lib file with tests gated on the node against today's lib (headings, lambda parens, F# retire, union rename), the day's strongest regression check. DESIGN: (a) a 'node' tag or field on items whose heavy step runs unattended on the node, plus 'kit agile next --machine node' that ranks them; (b) a node-idle check (kit schedule or the hourly containment) that, when the node has no running/queued job, starts the top node item's ready script or messages its team; (c) each team keeps at least one node-runnable item ready, the node analogue of 'always keep 2 light items ready'; (d) the resource report shows node idle minutes per day as the KPI.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_2 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 2u32, "2026-10-31T22:01Z", "kit", "10-31 17:5x kit: kit queued node work right after main's 17:42 report. job-1793483855773 kit-node-verify-wide runs 18 touched-module notebooks (CLI ones against candidate BB3616FB), and job-1793484065827 kit-node-train7-preview is chained after it: candidate-build over the 28 kit crates changed since the installed TRAIN5e snapshot, then all 30 changed modules with tests via notebook-batch -Bin. Roughly 3-4 h of node work, previewing TRAIN7's notebook phase off the box. kit's rule from here: before a kit wait, check 'remote.ps1 node job list' and queue a node-runnable kit step if the node is empty (the mirror kit-verify plus kit/scripts/notebook-batch.ps1, regen-sizes.ps1 and candidate-build.ps1 make that a single call).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_3 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 3u32, "2026-11-01T03:40Z", "kit", "10-31 23:5x kit groom, in kit's CPU-light top-3. NEXT CONCRETE STEP: make 'node idle' visible where lanes decide, without a new script: extend the existing kit_remote_status package so 'kit remote status' prints running/queued node jobs per lane plus an IDLE flag (no running job), then have the Stop gate hook (autonomous-gate.ps1, thin glue) add one line when the node is idle: 'node idle: start a node-runnable item (agile list --tag node)'. Node-runnable items get the tag 'node' so the gate can name one. Tonight's check (23:0x) showed the node saturated by 4 lanes, so the gap is the idle hours, not tonight.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_4 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 4u32, "2026-11-01T12:36Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: 'kit remote status' prints running and queued node jobs per lane and IDLE when none run (CLI test against a fake job list); the Stop gate adds 'node idle: start a node-runnable item' and names the top item tagged node when idle (pipe test); measured: node idle minutes per day reported by KIT-AGILE-CADENCE, target < 60 min idle while node-tagged items are ready. NEXT STEP: extend src/kit_remote_status with a node_activity union and the IDLE line; tag node-runnable items 'node' (KIT-SCALE, KIT-EXEC-METRICS, CELLS-RUST-OPT-LEVEL already). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: node_activity = Busy of list lane_job | Idle (closed union, no 'count = 0' sentinel); lane as a nominal; job state reused from kit_jobs' union, not parsed strings.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_5 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 5u32, "2026-11-01T19:44Z", "kit", "11-01 15:43 kit: FROZEN-BUSY FIX (main 15:3x: node-status.txt said BUSY from 10-30 to 15:29 because node-watch died). node-watch.ps1 (unstaged) now writes a stale_after=<now + max(5 min, 3 intervals)> field into every status line, with the rule in the line itself (\"past stale_after this file is UNKNOWN, never BUSY\"), plus machine= and one status file per machine (<machine>-status.txt; node-status.txt kept for node/laptop) and per-machine logs. remote.ps1 Linux status prints cpu N% from /proc/stat, so one watcher serves Windows and Linux. A cloud watcher is live: job-1793562109234 (europa-status.txt: cpu=4% AVAILABLE). Follow-up for kit: the reader side becomes a kit verb (kit machine status <machine>) that applies stale_after mechanically, part of PS1-TO-SPIRAL's watcher port.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_6 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 6u32, "2026-11-02T15:01Z", "kit", "kit 11-02: TRAIN-ON-NODE (P0) moves kit release trains (regen + notebooks, ~3 h of box CPU per train) to the node; first run TRAIN12.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_7 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:49Z", "main", "11-04 01:5x main: USER RULE (11-04 00:0x): 'prioritize long heavy runs in the node instead of here, we should be the last machine to get filled, battletest/dogfeed the train that way' (memory heavy-runs-node-first-box-last). Tonight's data: TRAIN18 ran its regen on the node, 295 crates published in 53 min, against about 3 h on the box for TRAIN17b; it failed only on one over-1000 crate (kit_heal_nameof). kit's s3 precheck took 7.4 min on the node. europa has only 2 CPUs and sat at load 10-16 when every lane routed checks there: --check attestations hit the 30 s default (VOID; --timeout-ms 150000), and 3 orphaned rustc builds stacked up after tool-moved ssh sessions. So the IDLE line should also report OVERSUBSCRIBED: load / nproc > 2 means route to the other machine, so the node-first rule doesn't just move the pile to europa.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_8 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 8u32, "2026-11-04T11:12Z", "main", "11-04 07:2x main: snapshot while the box and the node sat at 100%: europa load 0.81 on 2 CPUs (idle), so heavy checks should have gone there first. The box-side kernel gates this hour were main's own slip, because europa's earlier load was misread from a stale check. europa disk 97% (2.8 GB free of 94 GB): /data 50 GB (x-dumps /data/x/cache 40 GB, /data/enryu43 9 GB), /root/remote-stage/fiscal-check 8 GB; owners asked to trim to ~85%. Node disk 14.5 GB free after the 02:1x sweep. Rule for the gate text and for lanes: re-read load right before choosing a machine (cat /proc/loadavg on europa, LoadPercentage on the node).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_9 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 9u32, "2026-11-04T12:18Z", "main", "11-04 08:4x main OVERCORRECTION: europa load 26.9/22.4/20.6 on 2 CPUs (fiscal generator under pack27, two kit --check runs under pack34, main's html build, another compile), while the node also sits at 100%. Since the user's node-first rule lanes pile onto europa, and 13x oversubscription on 2 cores makes every europa run slow and flaky (main's html build: 22+ min for a ~8 min job). RULE PROPOSAL for the gate text and NODE-ALWAYS-FED: europa admits at most 2 concurrent heavy runs (one per CPU); above loadavg 4, queue on the node (4x more cores) or wait, never stack. kit's job host could enforce it with a per-host slot cap (MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS). Also seen: a kit test sleeper (/tmp/kit spiral test job kill on close ... sleeper child) alive 15.5 h at 0% CPU on europa, harmless but orphaned.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_10 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 10u32, "2026-11-04T15:16Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main: the n9 rule is now in the STOP GATE every lane reads (~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1): \"Before a heavy run, re-read the target's load (europa: cat /proc/loadavg; node: LoadPercentage): europa has 2 CPUs, so above loadavg 4 send it to the node instead of stacking.\" Seen live in main's next block. The job-host cap (MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS, kit) remains the durable fix; raw ssh runs bypass it until TRAIN22's dispatch.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_11 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 11u32, "2026-11-04T16:55Z", "main", "11-04 12:5x main SNAPSHOT (inverse of n8): node LoadPercentage 100 (TRAIN22 regen since 11:41, plus vmmem), europa loadavg 0.44/1.24/3.04 with only k3s/containerd/iggy resident: europa sat idle while the node was full. Acted at once: main's pending kernel gate for literal rounds 2-3 went to europa. Pattern of the day: the two machines alternate between saturated and idle, and lanes read the state late or not at all, so the rule in the stop gate (re-read load before choosing) is necessary but not sufficient. DURABLE FIX stays MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS + this item: a kit job host that knows both machines' free slots and places each queued heavy job on the freer one (europa 2 slots, node ~8), so lanes submit jobs, not ssh commands.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_12 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 12u32, "2026-11-04T17:02Z", "kit", "11-04 17:0x kit: DoD part 1 BUILT (unstaged): `kit window remote <alias> [--bin <kit>]` (kit_remote_status) now also runs `<kit> job list` on the machine and prints the node_activity union: NodeBusy jobs -> one line per lane \"kit remote status jobs machine=<m> lane=<lane> running=<r> queued=<q>\" (lane = label prefix, finished jobs ignored); NodeIdle queued -> \"kit remote status IDLE machine=<m> running=0 queued=<n> (start a node-runnable item: kit agile list --tag node)\". Test a_job_list_becomes_per_lane_activity_or_idle (2 lanes, idle with a queued job, lane_of). europa --check ok with bodies; box notebook job-1793811420520-kit-remote-status-tests. LEFT: the Stop-gate line (main's autonomous-gate.ps1: when IDLE, name the top node-tagged item) and the idle-minutes measure.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_13 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 13u32, "2026-11-04T21:40Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main INCIDENT for this item's health side: the node's C: hit 0 GB free about 17:28 (kit: 11 kit-regeneration staged workspaces of 0.7-1.25 GB piling up under spiral-bin\\kit-regeneration; compiler also cleared 20 finished review dirs under C:\\home\\remote-stage). It broke TRAIN24's regen, kit's size run and compiler's uniontag4 job; now 12.8 GB free, TRAIN25 relaunched. main's own footprint there is ~74 MB (mirror main-kernel 71 MB, 3 MB build dir). A \"node fed\" check needs a disk floor next to load: refuse new heavy jobs (or prune finished workspaces first) under ~10 GB free, since one train regen stages ~1 GB per workspace. Same day on europa the bottleneck was RAM (3.4 GB, a 2.4 GB cell OOM-killed k3s pods), so the dispatcher in MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS should weigh disk and memory, not only CPU slots.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_14 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 14u32, "2026-11-04T22:54Z", "kit", "11-04 19:0x kit: main's DISK FLOOR (17:4x incident note) BUILT (unstaged) in `kit window remote <alias>` (kit_remote_status): a third ssh call runs the machine's own `kit machine health --gate --min-disk-gb 0 --max-busy-pct 1000` (sysinfo disk_free_gb, already in every installed kit; verified live on the node: \"disk=10gb ram=5058mb busy=95pct\") and prints a typed node_disk: \"kit remote status disk machine=<m> free_gb=<n> floor_gb=10\", or under 10 GB \"kit remote status DISK-LOW machine=<m> free_gb=<n> floor_gb=10 (prune finished staged workspaces before a heavy job)\", or \"disk unknown ... reason=\" for an old kit. Floor 10 GB per main's note (one regen stages ~1 GB per workspace). The node sits AT 10 GB right now, during TRAIN25. Test a_health_gate_line_becomes_a_disk_state_against_the_floor (10gb ok, 0gb low, unknown verb). europa --check ok with bodies; box notebook kit-remote-disk-tests. Pairs with the launch-train.ps1 5 GB refusal (DISK-CLEANUP). LEFT: the auto-pull of the next node item when IDLE.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_15 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 15u32, "2026-11-04T22:59Z", "kit", "11-04 18:5x kit: disk floor PROVEN on the box (kit-remote-disk-tests 3/3, incl. a_health_gate_line_becomes_a_disk_state_against_the_floor). Node size run kit-size-argsdisk pending.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_16 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 16u32, "2026-11-04T23:00Z", "kit", "11-04 19:0x kit: the IDLE line now names the ranked command, \"(start the top node-runnable item: kit agile next <backlog root> --tag node --open 3)\"; `agile next --tag node` works in the installed kit (ready=18 today), while the old hint `agile list --tag node` was unranked. europa --check ok. The PULL half: proposed to main to fold `kit window remote laptop-ts` (IDLE / DISK-LOW + top 3 --tag node items) into autonomous-gate.ps1's stop message, since that gate is what every lane already reads when it stops; it is main's hook, so kit only proposed.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_17 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 17u32, "2026-11-04T23:05Z", "main", "11-04 19:1x main DECISION on kit's proposal: kit window remote <alias> (riding TRAIN26, not installed) prints node disk against a 10 GB floor (DISK-LOW) and an IDLE line pointing at kit agile next <root> --tag node --open 3 (18 ready node items today). The \"pull the next one when idle\" half goes into the stop gate (~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1) as a FOURTH parallel thread job (kit window remote laptop-ts) inside the existing 15 s kit budget, adding the IDLE or DISK-LOW line plus the top 3 node items to the block message. WIRE IT ONLY AFTER the installed kit has the verb (post TRAIN26): until then it would cost every lane's stop a failing call. Add hooks-test.ps1 cases for IDLE, DISK-LOW and a missing verb (fails open).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_18 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 18u32, "2026-11-04T23:12Z", "kit", "11-04 19:1x kit: HEADROOM SPLIT (unstaged, rides TRAIN27; TRAIN26's snapshot holds the 18:59 status.spi = 996 lines, checked): kit_remote_status was 4 lines under the gate, so the job-activity half moved to NEW linked crate kit_remote_activity (lane_job, node_activity, lane_of, job_of, activity_of, activity_lines + its test), exporting kit_remote_activity_text activity_text ((machine, output)) -> the joined lines and kit_remote_field_text field_text ((line, key)) (the disk parser reads disk= through it). status.spi keeps the windows/disk parts; package.spiproj links kit_remote_activity; Cargo.toml dep + workspace member + Cargo.lock entry; `cargo metadata --offline --locked` exit 0; europa --check ok on both (with bodies). Node size kit-size-remote-split and box notebooks kit-remote-split-tests pending.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_19 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 19u32, "2026-11-04T23:16Z", "kit", "11-04 19:2x kit: split PROVEN: node size kit_remote_status 996 -> 582, kit_remote_activity 476; box notebooks 2/2 (activity 1/1, status 2/2). Rides TRAIN27.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_20 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 20u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "main", "11-04 22:2x main STAR EXCHANGE: fiscal asks for a node DISK-FREE alarm (free swung 3.6-14 GB within hours; the 17:28 0-GB event half-broke fiscal's t1101 restore, killed TRAIN24 and compiler's uniontag4). Owners: main + resilience. kit already added the 10 GB DISK-LOW warning to kit window remote and a 5 GB refusal in launch-train (both unstaged, riding TRAIN26), so the alarm can reuse that check from resilience's hourly kit-machine-watch task once installed.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_21 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 21u32, "2026-11-05T04:35Z", "main", "11-05 00:35 main NODE DISK at 10.5 GB (alarm 15) diagnosed: no single new hog. Stage dirs are small (fiscal under 0.9 GB, all in use; main none). The biggest dirs: git mirrors spiral 6.1 / polyglot 4.3 (retired repo) / dice 3.3 GB; Temp\\spiral-cells-compiler 2.3 GB (11-04 11:34); r2r-cache 1.6 GB; Temp\\bgnajmgc 1.45 GB (11-03); Temp\\wsl-crashes 1.04 GB. LIVE FINDING: the node's WSL Ubuntu (Running since 10-25 15:16, vmmem 964 MB, older than the no-WSL-on-the-node rule) has WSLg's /usr/bin/weston crash-looping every ~105 s, each crash writing a 107 MB dump (rolling 10 kept). Asked resilience and x-dumps whether anyone uses it; one-shot at 01:47 runs `wsl --shutdown` if nobody claims it. Also: compiler pruned 578 r2r-old/replaced files (822 MB) from the node compiler dir, and main's pack-chain/swap-inplace now exclude and prune them on every ship.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_22 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 22u32, "2026-11-05T04:40Z", "main", "11-05 00:40 main NODE DISK reclaimed: deleted the node's retired polyglot mirror C:\\home\\git\\polyglot (4.31 GB) after a check: clean tree, 0 commits ahead of origin (github i574n/polyglot), no process using it (probe shells excluded), no scheduled task, not in remote.ps1's sync list; its 2 stashes (auto \"laptop pre-update 2026-10-25\": generated .dib.html/.ipynb renders plus a LICENSE) were kept as patches in the box's %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\node-polyglot-stashes-20261105. Node free 10.5 -> 14.7 GB. Also shipped pack38 to the node (host 08B00F25 / core 15FD51D7 = box) so kit can launch TRAIN27; resilience endorses the WSL shutdown (one-shot at 01:47).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_23 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 23u32, "2026-11-05T05:55Z", "main", "11-05 01:55 main WSL SHUT DOWN on the node (resilience endorsed; no lane claimed it, x-dumps included): wsl --shutdown, Ubuntu now Stopped, vmmem gone (~1 GB RAM back), the 10 weston crash dumps (1.04 GB) removed. Node C: 17.1 GB free (from 10.5 at the alarm). Separately, x asked that node compiler swaps be announced: the pack40/41 node ship waits for TRAIN27 AND x-next8 (job-1793858062706), then main announces before running pack-chain -SkipInstall.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_24 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 24u32, "2026-11-05T06:07Z", "main", "11-05 02:07 main NODE SHIPPED pack40 at 02:05 (host 895300935E291274 / core DDCA78971B4EAB36 = box; 41 archive entries; 5 old files pruned; launch ok) DURING TRAIN27, on x's GO: x-next8 died in 143 s because the live lib's reflection.spi:334 uses pack39's UnionCaseName op, and every node Gleam build compiling it failed on pack38. A node train pins its own compiler at launch (kit), so TRAIN27 is unaffected. pack-chain.ps1 gained -AllowTrain (ship despite a running train, saying so) and -SkipVultr (europa was thrashing from another lane's uncapped compile loop; it recovered on its own). kit and fiscal were told before the swap, x after. The europa Linux build of pack39/40 is still owed (pack38 is the last built there).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_25 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 25u32, "2026-11-05T14:10Z", "main", "11-05 10:10 main TRAIN UNBLOCK, status: TRAIN22-29 were all red; the last two died at regen on compiler Rust linked-shape bugs (TRAIN28 E0308: a struct import matched by field-type TEXT across crates with their own UH0; TRAIN29 E0425: a hand-written struct inside a mod taken as a linked shape). compiler fixed both (LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES 3 + 4) in pack48, and pack49 (same core, new host) followed. main shipped pack48 (09:21) and pack49 (09:39) to the node in x's named gaps, and built both on europa, so box = node = europa. kit's gate on pack48: full regen of 348 owners + cargo check --workspace --keep-going = ERRORS=0 CARGO-EXIT=0 (10:0x), the first clean regen in nine trains. TRAIN30 is cleared to launch.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_26 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 26u32, "2026-11-05T16:02Z", "main", "11-05 12:02 main TRAIN30 (pack49 core 0BA4A608, launched 10:25): REGEN PASSED, every owner regenerated and cargo check clean, the first train past regen since TRAIN21; compiler's linked-shape fixes 3+4 held in the field. It stopped at the 1000-line crate gate (11:59) on 4 generated crates: kit_job_slot 1311, kit_job_host 1090, kit_job_control 1105 (kit's morning heals; splits in the tree for TRAIN31) and agile_claim_rank 1025 (flagged to kit). Node shipped pack51 (core E190545B5F30A7B4) at 12:01 in x's gap, so box = node for TRAIN31; europa build queued. pack-chain now prunes main's old ship stages after each ship (pack49's pruned on first use).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_27 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 27u32, "2026-11-05T18:19Z", "main", "11-05 14:19 main TRAIN31 (pack51, launched 12:43): red at regen 14:18, on a KIT-SIDE link error, not a compiler one: E0433 in regenerated kit_cli_routes/routes.rs:195, kit_table_filter::kit_table_filter_kept called but kit_table_filter not linked (cargo suggests kit_table_logs::kit_table_filter_kept). Sent to kit with the regen tree path. TRAIN30's four size overs were fixed and stayed fixed; compiler fixes 3+4 held again (no E0308/E0425). Box = node = europa on pack51 (europa built 12:56).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_28 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 28u32, "2026-11-05T19:13Z", "main", "main 15:09 11-05: pack52 shipped to the node in place inside x's named gap (x-next10 kept its pinned pack51 copy). node SpiralCompiler.dll A1BF06EB9AD87F00 / Core A688EE5AD426A5A0 = box; launch ok; pack-chain pruned the pack51 stage. kit/x/compiler told. europa build retrying behind the 2100 MB headroom guard (pending).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_29 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 29u32, "2026-11-05T19:58Z", "resilience", "ALARM-DELIVERY FIXED (resilience, unstaged) - node-utilization-monitor.ps1:64 was calling `kit story note ... REMOTE-OFFLOAD-FIRST ... *> $null`: story is not a verb (renamed to agile), REMOTE-OFFLOAD-FIRST does not exist, and *> $null swallowed both failures - so every WASTE/DISK-LOW alarm since the rename was dropped silently (main found today DISK-LOW 13GB detected at 15:45 but never delivered). Fix: now `kit agile note <root> NODE-ALWAYS-FED \"...\" --as resilience` via Invoke-Bounded capturing rc, and on rc!=0 it appends \"NOTE FAILED rc=N\" to node-utilization-monitor.last.log instead of discarding - a guard that cannot deliver now says so. This note IS the proof the delivery path works. resilience 2026-11-05 15:5x.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_30 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 30u32, "2026-11-05T20:08Z", "main", "main 11-05 16:07: pack52 also built from source on europa (pack-chain retry attempt 13, once MemAvailable reached 2107 MB over the 2100 floor; 78.6 s; launch exit 0). The retries had waited ~1 h at 2070 MB (k3s + iggy baseline, ockam-iggy-edge restarted deliberately at 15:56). Box, node and europa are all on pack52 now. TRAIN32 runs on the node (job-1793906628967-kit-TRAIN32), verdict pending.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_31 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 31u32, "2026-11-05T23:27Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:2x NODE STATE: fed. 100% CPU, 8 GB RAM free, 5 running jobs (kit-TRAIN32 notebooks, x-next11, tibia-tf8-build, tibia-np5-gate-2, fiscal-twin2) + 2 queued behind them (tibia-tf8-sweep, fiscal-reports-gate2). DISK: 20 GB free at 15:5x after the .part sweep, now 17 GB, ~2 GB/h under this load, so the 15 GB floor comes around 20:3x. resilience's node-utilization-monitor alarm now DELIVERS (it notes here since its 16:2x fix), so the next DISK-LOW will reach this item; owners of the running jobs should delete their stage/regen dirs as each result is noted.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_32 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 32u32, "2026-11-05T23:49Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:5x INCIDENT: the node was unreachable from ~19:46 to 19:48:50 (about 3 min). Both routes timed out on port 22 AND ICMP got no reply (LAN <moon-lan-addr> and Tailscale <moon-ts-addr>; tailscale showed 'offline, last seen 1m ago', then 'direct <moon-lan-addr>'), so it was a network drop, not sshd starved by CPU. NO REBOOT: uptime 16,363 min (boot 10-25 11:06). Node jobs SURVIVED: kit-TRAIN32 notebooks, x-next11, tibia-tf8-sweep and fiscal-twin2 still running. Box-side casualties: waiters that called remote.ps1 during the window, e.g. TRAIN32's box half (job-1793906232412, exit 1 'no route') and main's watcher. kit is filing a retry for the box-side train poll; any box-side waiter should retry 'no route' a few times before failing. DISK: 14 GB free now, below the 15 GB floor, so resilience's fixed monitor should deliver a DISK-LOW note here on its next tick (first real test of the 16:2x delivery fix).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_33 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 33u32, "2026-11-05T23:58Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-05 ~15:0x resilience FIXED node-utilization-monitor fail-open (main caught it; unstaged, parse-clean, tested). BUG: all 3 probes returned -1 sentinel (root cause = $MirrorNode=$NodeRoutes[0]=laptop hostname which flakes to resolve moon; europa -1 = 15s bound under 100% box load) yet the run printed \"ok\" because $diskLow/idle/waste all require >=0, so a guard that could not MEASURE reported healthy while node was really <15GB. FIX: (1) route-fallback Invoke-NodeRoute loops $NodeRoutes first-that-answers (remote.ps1 pattern), mirror-CPU+disk combined into one probe; (2) FAIL-CLOSED: any -1 -> \"UNKNOWN: <probe> failed - cannot measure\" not ok; 2 consecutive UNKNOWN -> NODE-ALWAYS-FED note ([DELIVERED] marker dedups a long outage) + exit 1; (3) logs route + per-probe ms. Test: \"ok: box36% mirror100% compute252% node-free16GB [route=laptop mirror=4215ms compute=4918ms]\". Same fail-open-one-step-earlier shape as the guards-fail-closed rule. resilience-614162e5.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_34 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 34u32, "2026-11-06T00:43Z", "main", "main 11-05 20:4x TRAIN32 VERDICT (from kit): finished 20:42, notebooks 230/233, NOT installed. The 3 reds were all kit's own and are fixed in the tree (parents_cli argv, actor settle waits 20->60 s, mirror_cli argv). It was the first train since TRAIN21 past both regen and the crate gate. TRAIN33 launched 20:43 on the node (box job job-1793925783556-kit-TRAIN33-node; node and box on pack52; includes the launch-train ssh-blip retry), ETA ~01:00+, PENDING at main's run end 21:00. Next reader (kit lane or the next session): if it installs, the dogfood list is next --any (expect claimed=none), S7 edit --parent/list --tree, S10 coordinator dry run, M4 mirror proof, rename timing; then re-check LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE's strict JSON and PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS' kit repo scope.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_35 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 35u32, "2026-11-06T08:19Z", "main", "monitor state 11-06 04:14: UNKNOWN (route=none to mirror, node-free -1GB) - the mirror node IS the wifi node (moon) and its sshd is down (lockout during mesh-key setup), so no route answers. Fail-open rewrite correctly reported UNKNOWN not ok; a 2nd consecutive UNKNOWN will deliver a note here. Recovery = local Start-Service sshd on the wifi node (escalated to user); the box keeper already forwards SP:2247->wifi:22 so it re-feeds automatically once sshd is back.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_36 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 36u32, "2026-11-06T08:25Z", "resilience", "star-exchange consolidation 11-06 04:23: kit, tibia, compiler ALL reported the node unreachable (port 22, both routes) 04:16-04:21 and were about to treat it as down/relaunch blind. Reconciled with a fresh probe: wifi node <moon-ts-addr> ping=True, :135/:445 open, ONLY :22 down - the node is HEALTHY, just its sshd is locked out (my doing). LAN <moon-lan-addr> is dark (box off that segment). So the correct verdict is UNKNOWN-route, not node-down; recovery = local Start-Service sshd on the wifi node, after which SP:2247 and all node routes restore automatically. This is the top cross-lane finding of the round.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_37 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 37u32, "2026-11-06T08:44Z", "resilience", "repro probe: delivery path test 044426")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_38 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 38u32, "2026-11-06T08:50Z", "resilience", "node-utilization ALARM: node-utilization-monitor 2026-11-06 04:49 DISK-LOW: mirror node C: 14GB free (<15GB floor) - at risk [ARGTEST-B]")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_39 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 39u32, "2026-11-06T08:51Z", "resilience", "node-utilization ALARM: node-utilization-monitor 2026-11-06 04:51 DISK-LOW: mirror node C: 14GB free (<15GB floor) - mirror scp/retention + node sims at risk")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_40 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 40u32, "2026-11-06T08:56Z", "resilience", "alarm-delivery REAL root cause found+fixed 11-06 (the 15:58 \"fixed\" note was incomplete - alarms were STILL dropped): node-utilization-monitor delivered the note via Invoke-Bounded -> Start-Process -ArgumentList, which splits the alarm text (spaces + \"(<15GB floor)\") into 20 operands, so kit returned rc=2 and the alarm was logged NOTE FAILED and lost. ssh probes hid it (ssh rejoins split args; kit counts them). Fixed: note now sent via the call operator (& $kit agile note ... 2>&1), with retry for genuine CAS rejects and real stderr capture. VERIFIED: DISK-LOW now lands here (ALARM note count 0->2). See memory start-process-argumentlist-splits-args.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_41 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 41u32, "2026-11-06T10:48Z", "resilience", "SMART-DELEGATION/DELEG-ROUTER makes \"never idle\" real: offload-by-default sends heavy work to the idle lap twin instead of the saturated box (11-06: lap 19% CPU / 12GB free vs box 100% / 2.9GB free).")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_42 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 42u32, "2026-11-06T11:12Z", "resilience", "node-utilization ALARM: node-utilization-monitor 2026-11-06 07:11 DISK-LOW: mirror node C: 14GB free (<15GB floor) - mirror scp/retention + node sims at risk")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_43 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 43u32, "2026-11-06T13:25Z", "resilience-614162e5", "DISK TRAJECTORY WARNING 11-06 09:24: node C: free declining 14GB(07:11)->11GB(09:24) ~=1.3GB/h under the run. The DISK-LOW alarm DEDUPES on alarm TYPE not severity, so it fired once at 07:11 and will NOT re-alarm as the disk worsens - owners get no update as it approaches 0. At this rate the node disk could hit ~0 between ~16:30-20:30, BEFORE the 21:00 run end, which fails node jobs. ACTION: owners of the node jobs (kit TRAIN33, tibia tf9) should proactively clear completed stage/regen dirs NOW, not wait for a re-alarm that will not come. Resilience follow-up (deferred, risky to edit the live alarm path mid-run): DISK-LOW should re-alarm on each further N-GB drop below the last-alarmed level, not dedupe a worsening condition.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_44 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 44u32, "2026-11-06T13:49Z", "resilience", "node-utilization ALARM: node-utilization-monitor 2026-11-06 09:49 DISK-LOW: mirror node C: 10GB free (<15GB floor) - mirror scp/retention + node sims at risk")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_45 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 45u32, "2026-11-06T13:58Z", "resilience-614162e5", "DISK-LOW incident RESOLVING 11-06 10:1x: node C: recovered ~9GB -> 11GB. Contributions: resilience reclaimed 1.5GB (1.3GB stale >24h Cells temp + 163MB abandoned mirror .part turds); kit pruned 1.18GB (834MB staged regen workspaces + 350MB probe mirrors) AND fixed the ROOT CAUSE - each kit probe now deletes its own staged regen dir + mirror at job end, so kit is no longer a steady DISK-LOW source. Acute exhaustion risk (projected ~0 before 21:00) is averted. Watching: DISK-ALARM-REARM now re-alerts on each further 3GB drop (no more dedup-hides-worsening). Remaining steady contributor is x Cells temp (regenerates; resilience >24h stale-prune handles it as recurring upkeep). Good cross-lane close: alert -> owners acted + fixed at source.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_46 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 46u32, "2026-11-06T14:15Z", "resilience-614162e5", "DURABLE node-upkeep deployed 11-06: cells-temp-janitor (node-side scheduled task, daily 04:17, SYSTEM, Priority 5) auto-prunes Temp\\spiral_cells subdirs >24h + logs to C:\\ProgramData\\cells-janitor.log; never touches <24h (active run). Makes the manual stale-Cells prune RECURRING so the node disk will not refill with abandoned Cells temp on future days (the top 11-06 DISK-LOW contributor at 4.5GB). Informed x (owner) with an opt-out. Combined with kits per-probe self-clean (kit-regeneration) + DISK-ALARM-REARM, both top node-disk contributors now self-manage and worsening is re-alarmed - the disk-exhaustion failure mode is structurally addressed, not just patched for today.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_47 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 47u32, "2026-11-06T14:20Z", "resilience-614162e5", "node-disk failure mode FULLY structurally closed 11-06: both top contributors now have an owner root-cause fix + a resilience backstop. (1) Cells temp: x owns CELLS-TEMP-LEAK (P2) - File.rm_rf in the run after-block silently fails on Windows when cell.exe/.pdb are locked, and a killed BEAM skips the after-block; x fix sweeps the tmp root at Cells start. My cells-temp-janitor (daily >24h prune) is now the BACKSTOP for the killed-BEAM case that skips the sweep, not the only cleanup. (2) kit-regeneration: kit probes now self-clean regen+mirror at job end. Plus DISK-ALARM-REARM re-alerts on worsening. So: source fixes (x, kit) + backstops (janitor) + worsening-alarm (re-arm) = defense in depth, not a one-day patch.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_48 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 48u32, "2026-11-06T17:18Z", "resilience", "node-utilization ALARM: node-utilization-monitor 2026-11-06 13:14 DISK-LOW: mirror node C: 11GB free (<15GB floor) - mirror scp/retention + node sims at risk")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_49 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 49u32, "2026-11-06T20:45Z", "resilience", "node-utilization ALARM: node-utilization-monitor 2026-11-06 16:45 UNKNOWN: mirror,node-disk probe(s) failed - cannot measure (box 100%, mirror -1%, compute 54%, europa-tmp 24%, node-free -1GB [route=none mirror=0ms compute=3819ms])")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_50 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 50u32, "2026-11-06T20:57Z", "resilience-614162e5", "FALSE ALARM CORRECTION (resilience-614162e5, 11-06 16:5x): the 16:45 \"UNKNOWN: mirror,node-disk probe(s) failed ... node down\"-class alarm was FALSE - the node was UP the whole time (critical-mirror landed ok at 16:40 over the same link; my ssh sessions worked). CAUSE: node-utilization-monitors node probe (ssh + 3 CIM queries, 15s-bounded) cannot complete within 15s when the lap twin is at 100% CPU (both box+lap pinned all day), so all routes \"failed\" -> route=none -> UNKNOWN, and two consecutive (16:15 from my large scp saturating the link, 16:45 from lap-CPU) tripped the 2x-UNKNOWN=node-down alarm. The node was never down. FIX APPLIED: raised the node + compute probe timeouts 15s -> 40s (.bak, parse OK); verified - the probe now MEASURES (16:56 line = real \"DISK-LOW node C: 12GB\", not UNKNOWN), and the successful run reset the UNKNOWN streak. Lesson: a fail-closed guard must allow enough time to measure a loaded-but-healthy host, or it manufactures false down-alarms during the busy periods it most needs to be trusted. Node is healthy: 12GB free (post-prune), sshd Running, critical floor landing +wip. resilience-614162e5.")
