inl note_of_node_always_fed_65 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 65u32, "2026-11-09T05:10Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:1x rig: answered management's NO-BEACON finding for rig: rig now writes LOCALAPPDATA kit schedules autonomous-rig.last.log (first write 01:09:42) and its heartbeat cron (539b73e0, every 10 min to 21:00) refreshes it first on every wake with one line of current work, so idle-with-ready-alarm sees rig as Active or idle by beacon age instead of idle-blind. The other NO-BEACON lanes (compiler, fiscal, microblog, org, tibia) still need their own beacon writes; that is per-lane, so not done for them.")
inl note_of_node_always_fed_66 () = Note ("NODE-ALWAYS-FED", 66u32, "2026-11-09T06:12Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 02:5x local rig: the remaining scope (route heavy node-runnable items to a node, and pull the next or alert when a node has no running or queued job) is the executor design in KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR: the feeder that keeps queue depth per host, per-host policy (Always, Window, Parked, ShortOnly, NoBuilds), load admission that holds (item 5) and the KIT-JOB-HANDOFF lane print. Tonight's evidence for it: ganymede, moon and europa were all saturated by queued work from 6 lanes (no idle node), while the box held the lanes' sessions; the idle watch now has rig's beacon. Held on KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR so this item does not rotate through the gate as a second home for the same work.")
