inl cells_xcompat_spiral () = Task ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", "Cells in Spiral: the generic X check (x_compat.ex, 235 lines) as a typed Spiral module with a finding GADT, so the check needs no mix", Story, P1, D4, 20u32, Active, "CELLS-SPI-LIB", "cells,spiral,team:org,typefeatures,postability", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_xcompat_spiral () = Planning ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_1 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T03:37Z", "x", "2026-10-31 23:37 x: the CELLS-IN-SPIRAL slice where Cells and x meet (the user's 280-character synergy, 10-31). lib/spiral/cells/x_compat.ex (235 lines, census class a-pure) becomes a typed Spiral module in apps/cells/spi, so the generic X check runs without mix. x's builds (X-COMPAT-VIA-CELLS) then lose their last Elixir step. NEXT STEP (CPU-light, reading and drafting only): read x_compat.ex, the spiral.x_compat mix task, x_compat_test.exs and postability_profile_test.exs. Write the typed model into this item's note: a finding GADT indexed by kind (overweight, mention, hashtag, cashtag, autolink) so a report row can't pair a kind with the wrong payload; a weight function over code-point ranges; and the post weight as a record. Then draft the module (in the note, no file) under CELLS-SPI-LIB's lib reference (sm', listm). The oracle is x_compat_test plus byte-equal --check output over lib (1459), tibia (17) and x (2) against the Elixir check. The node runs it.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_2 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T06:43Z", "main", "main 02:4x: this item's new name is CELLS-CELL-BUDGET-SPIRAL (the module is Spiral.Cells.CellBudget since 00:45); the rename itself is parked because 'kit agile rename' ran 421 s and lost the CAS twice under groom-round writes (sent to kit as KIT-SCALE data). Scope, owner main (x's CELLS-IN-SPIRAL n3 M1): CellBudget as typed Spiral, with a finding union and the 280 limit as one constant, walking files with lstat and never following links (CELL-BUDGET-MEMORY), oracle cell_budget tests plus parity on lib/tibia/x.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_3 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 3u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "main", "main 08:3x TYPEFEATURESET PLAN (CellBudget in Spiral): finding = union Hashtag | Mention | Cashtag | Autolink | OverBudget, each case carrying exactly its payload (OverBudget: weight and limit as a phantom-typed weight 'unit so weights and byte counts can't mix); the 280 limit a single typed constant; the profile a record of compiled matchers with no optional string fields (today's defused_before: nil becomes a union NoDefusing | Defusing of matcher pair). File walk returns a typed tree visitor that never follows links (CELL-BUDGET-MEMORY's lesson) and streams per file. Model: kit's agile_cadence typed models. DoD: cell_budget_test + cell_budget_profile_test pass against the Spiral version via Cells, plus exact parity on lib 1459 / tibia 17 / x 2 findings. NEXT STEP: after CELLS-SPI-LIB lands, write cell_budget.spi beside cell_budget.ex and diff their outputs on the three corpora. FIELDS: estimate 240, load light, owner main.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_4 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-11-02T20:29Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:29 x: NOT moot after pack17 retired the compiler's --x-compat. This item ports Cells' own CellBudget check (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/cell_budget.ex, 219 lines), which x's builds still run through 'mix spiral.cell_budget --check'. Only the compiler flag is gone. It stays with main, off the critical path.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_5 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 5u32, "2026-11-09T10:19Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:4x PORT MAP after reading cell_budget.ex (185 lines today): the budget half is pure and ports directly: (a) top_level_blocks = blocks end only at blank line(s) followed by an UNINDENTED line (an indented line after a blank stays in the block), trailing whitespace trimmed; (b) weight = sum of per-code-point weights (1 inside the ranges 0-4351, 8192-8205, 8208-8223, 8242-8247, else 2); (c) limit = 280 - cell_weight(\"c<k> 1/1\\n\") - defused dots, i.e. 273 for cells 1-9, 272 for 10-99, 271 from 100; (d) cell_weight = weight - autolink weights + 23 per link. The rewrites half needs Unicode classes and lookbehind regexes (hashtag, mention, cashtag, domain) plus the TLD set from data/tlds.txt (now also lib tlds.spi, microblog's LIB-TLDS): that is the costly part of the port and the only part that needs more than lib string ops. Evidence the pure half is exact: an awk transcription of (a)+(c) for ASCII reproduces mix spiral.cell_budget weights on 51 findings across 9 files tonight. Next step: cell_budget.spi with (a)-(c) and a finding GADT (OverBudget weight limit first; Hashtag | Mention | Cashtag | Autolink later), tested against the Elixir cell_budget_test fixtures.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_6 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 6u32, "2026-11-09T10:30Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:5x DRAFT PARKED (unstaged, not gated): spiral/apps/cells/spi/cell_budget.spi holds the pure half (cell_weight nominal, finding union OverBudget {line; weight; limit}, code_weight ranges, text_weight over char codes, header limit 280 - weight(\"c<k> 1/1\\n\"), the blank-before-unindented block scanner, over_budget, 3 tests). Not yet in package.spiproj. Open before gating: scan_line (355) and over_from (364) exceed the cell budget, and the { s with ... } record update spelling is unverified in edition 3 (no lib example found); both to fix first. Next step: split those two cells, confirm the update spelling (or build full records), add to package.spiproj, gate on a node.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_7 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 7u32, "2026-11-09T10:47Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 11:0x DRAFT UNPARKED: cell_budget.spi rewritten without the unverified { s with ... } update (blank_seen / new_block / grown build full scan records) and with block_finding split out; 0 cells over budget by the exact oracle. Gating in a standalone dir on ganymede (/home/remote/stage/org2-cellbudget with its own spiral.toml), NOT via Cells' own package.spiproj, so a compile error cannot break the Cells tool doing the gating. Tests: the block rule (rows [1; 6]), code-point weights (abé 3, 中文 4, U+2010 1), the numbered header limit (273, 272, 271). Next step: green -> add the module to spi/package.spiproj and port cell_budget_test's over_budget fixtures.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_8 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 8u32, "2026-11-09T13:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09: gate job-1794225556357 (ganymede) = 2/3 pass, 1 red: code_points_weigh... got (4, 6, 3) want (3, 4, 1). Root cause: on rust sm'::to_char_list walks UTF-8 BYTES (length/index are byte-based), so every byte of a multibyte char weighs 1. Fix: weigh over unicode::code_points (lib, rust+gleam arms) with code_weight on i32; no hand-rolled UTF-8 decode. Budget oracle 0 findings. Restaged, gate resubmitted as org2-cellbudget. Next: green -> add cell_budget to apps/cells package.spiproj and compare its report against the awk oracle on the whole regex/src tree (both must list the same findings).")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_9 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 9u32, "2026-11-09T13:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:5x GREEN after the code-point fix: ganymede job-1794229567742-org2-cellbudget 3/3 passed (code_points_weigh... now (3, 4, 1); header limits 273/272/271; report path), cell-budget report 0 findings on itself. Next step: add cell_budget to apps/cells package.spiproj and diff its findings against the awk oracle over regex/src (both must list the same blocks).")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_10 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 10u32, "2026-11-09T13:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:5x HANDOFF: wiring cell_budget into apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj is microblog's call (Cells owner; 10 modified files in that dir now; package-order reds slip past --check). Asked microblog to wire it at its next Cells touch or name a window. Then: findings == awk oracle == cell_budget_ruled.ex over regex/src.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_11 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 11u32, "2026-11-09T13:52Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 10:0x microblog (Cells owner) on org2's pure-Spiral cell_budget port. (a) WIRED: apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj lists cell_budget before main (unstaged). (b) REFERENCE BUG FIXED, agreed with org2: Spiral.Cells.CellBudget.top_level_blocks padded a block opened after N>=2 blank lines with N-1 leading newlines, which weighed +N-1. A new block now starts as [line]. Discriminating asserts added to cell_budget_test.exs (a double gap: line 4 weight 293 > 273, where the old code gives 294; a 3-blank gap: {5, 'inl b = 2'}). The fix only lowers weights, and no stored budget baselines exist. CellBudgetRuled inherits it. (c) PORT GAP (org2's to fix): the reference weighs each autolink (domain-like token with a tlds.txt TLD) as 23; the port has no link weighting. PROOF STAGED: the moon slot runs the join-point A/B, then cells-budget-compare.ps1, which adds a mirror-only export cell_budget_findings and compares the port vs the fixed reference over regex/src (14 files), printing only_port/only_ref rows with each block's autolinks. The europa per-test suite mirror carries the wiring, the fixed .ex and the test. dod: the domain compiles with cell_budget wired; cell_budget_test green; port == reference over regex/src apart from the autolink rows until org2 lands (c). next: read both runs.")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_12 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 12u32, "2026-11-09T14:26Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 14:3x AUTOLINKS PORTED, green: ganymede job-1794233598593 5/5 (rust) and cell-budget report 0 findings on the port itself. Design: the reference domain regex reduced to a run scanner. Its lookbehind forbids [letter digit @ - _ . /] before a match, so a match can only start at a maximal [A-Za-z0-9_.-] run; greedy (label\\.)+ + backtracking = the largest j where parts 1..j-1 are labels and part j is a 2-63 letter TLD followed by a non-word char. Accept = TLD in the set, or t.co, or a 2-letter TLD with a second label > 2. Weight = code points - link points + 23 per link. The TLD set is DATA: over_budget/text_weight take tlds : tld_list (nominal), and the caller reads apps/cells/data/tlds.txt. Approximation: \\p{L}\\p{N} next to a domain = code point >= 128 outside General Punctuation and CJK punctuation. Cross-check: the reference's own autolink lint flagged exactly name.rs, foo.app, t.co in the test line and not x.rs, a@b.com, https://github.com, foo.com-bar, the same verdict the port's tests assert. The source now splits those literals (\"t\" ++# \".co\"), so the file has 0 findings. Reference bug (2), padding after >=2 blank lines, was fixed by microblog in cell_budget.ex. Wait: microblog's moon compare (findings == reference over regex/src).")
inl note_of_cells_xcompat_spiral_13 () = Note ("CELLS-XCOMPAT-SPIRAL", 13u32, "2026-11-09T23:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 18:4x moon after-sim: cells-budget-compare verdict=equal (exit 0, run joinpts/compare-20261109184246): the pure-Spiral cell_budget port and the fixed Elixir reference give identical per-cell weights over the compare corpus, so there are no only_port/only_ref rows to hand to org2. The earlier autolink-weight gap (reference weighs autolinks at 23) did not surface in this corpus.")
