inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_1 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:33Z", "kit", "11-01 00:3x kit, slice of EOIE-SCRUM-XP (user 00:2x via main: 'speed up the agile->scrum/xp migration'; slices of an hour or less). Spec: EOIE-SCRUM-XP M3 DESIGN note (10-30 13:5x) and the 10-22 typestate draft.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_2 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 2u32, "2026-11-01T12:38Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: 'kit backlog sprint show <root> [S-1]' prints goal, days left, committed vs done minutes and per-item status, and a burn-down of Done minutes per day equal to a hand count on a fixture (CLI test); exact dates once KIT-AGILE-CADENCE writes StatusChanged rows, labelled approximate before that. NEXT STEP: the verb reading sprints_of + task rows; burn-down via agile_cadence's done_dating. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: burn-down points as a record (day nominal, done minutes nominal); approximate vs exact as the done_dating union (ByLastNote | ByStatusChange) carried into the output type so an approximate chart can never print as exact.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_3 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 3u32, "2026-11-01T18:15Z", "kit", "11-01 14:15 kit: EMACS-STEALS fold: column totals (org column view). The board/sprint view prints per-column sums of estimate and actual minutes and item counts, computed from typed rows, not text.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_4 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 4u32, "2026-11-01T20:46Z", "kit", "11-01 16:46 kit: column totals (EMACS-STEALS org column view) are modeled and proven (unstaged), in src/agile_activity. board_item {id; status; estimate; actual} -> column_totals gives one column_total {column; items; estimate; actual} per status in board order, with empty columns as zeros. Test columns_total_their_items_and_standup_reads_typed_changes: Linux 4/4 for the package. NEXT: the board/sprint view prints these per column from the typed Task + ActualMinutes rows, not text.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_5 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:33Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 35 h ago by kit, progress kept at 40%. Resume from that note: the board/sprint view prints these per column from the typed Task + ActualMinutes rows, not text.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_6 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 6u32, "2026-11-04T09:16Z", "kit", "11-04 06:1x kit: `kit backlog sprint show <root> [<id>]` BUILT (unstaged, not wired yet). In kit_agile_sprint: SprintShow joins the typed sprint_verb union, and sprint_ran gives each verb its own argument shape. It prints `kit agile sprint show ok id= status= start= finish= days_left= goal=`, then `committed=Nm done=Nm`, then one line per item (task, minutes, task status from agile_task_census, committed/dropped). days_left = finish (lib date_time.days_from_civil) minus today. The linked state unit kit_agile_sprint_state gained sprint_head_of / sprint_items_of (array_base rows; id \"\" means the open sprint). europa pack34 + toml lib --check exit 0 (both crates, as-is and test bodies). Not yet: burn-down (needs KIT-AGILE-CADENCE StatusChanged rows), wiring and a node size run (with S3).")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_7 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 7u32, "2026-11-06T08:19Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 04:1x kit groom: parked Active to Planned, untouched since 11-04 (over 24 h; WIP cap: Active means touched within 48 h, and kit held 42 Active). Progress kept. Resume order unchanged; the next installable train (TRAIN33, link lost, result unread) carries no change to this item unless its last note says so.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_8 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 8u32, "2026-11-06T13:35Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 09:5x kit, dogfood with the TRAIN33 kit (6CEA882D) on a scratch backlog copy: sprint show <copy> S-PROBE-1 prints status, start, finish, days_left, goal, one line per item (minutes, task status, fate) and committed=90m done=0m. MISSING: the burn-down, which this item spec ties to KIT-AGILE-CADENCE recording StatusChanged rows; that dependency is now a dep, not prose (main 06:12 rule), so the item waits as Blocked. Resume when KIT-AGILE-CADENCE is Done: burn-down from Done stamps per day of the sprint.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s5_9 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S5", 9u32, "2026-11-06T13:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 09:5x kit: blocker: KIT-AGILE-CADENCE (StatusChanged rows give the per-day Done stamps the burn-down needs). Resume when it is Done.")
