inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:55Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 23:5x REVIEW (read-only; user asked to review fiscal's GADT/existential/HKT/prototype/reflection/phantom usage). FISCAL SRC (6,645 lines): gadt constructors 55, existentials 10, foralls 84, prototypes 6 + instances 11, phantoms 32, reflection 9, indexed unions 10 vs PLAIN unions 36 -> 18.5 constructs/1k excluding forall (31.2 with). Concentrated: profiles 212/1k, document 129, p2p 57, lifecycle 54, sunat 46 (22 percent of lines, 88 percent of constructs); generator, corpus_checks, canon*, modeling_ceiling, posting sit at 0-2/1k (the other 5,173 lines average 2.9/1k). Mega samples: omniledger 22.1/1k (existentials 14.5/1k, 58 indexed vs 30 plain unions), zeta 76.9/1k (84 vs 9). Biggest gaps: existentials (fiscal 1.5/1k) and the indexed:plain ratio (10:36). AGAINST THE RULE TODAY (fiscal's own lands): lib event_log R6/R9 types membership and audit use :: constructors with no index and int-coded discriminators (membership_code :122, audit_code :177, i64 0/1/2), append_outcome's uniform i64 cases, entry ev storing id/hash as raw strings although command_id/payload_hash nominals exist; xsd_emit's whitespace mode compared as strings 'preserve'/'replace'/'collapse' (:1113-1131, fed by xsd.spi WhiteSpace : string) was touched today and not migrated. TOP 5 MIGRATIONS: (1) money rounding -> regime-indexed rounding r GADT + a minor-units prototype per currency (money.spi:33, p2p.spi:165 hard-codes HalfEven 2); (2) sunat affectation -> \\? g. igv_affectation g, with tax_scheme and price_type indexed by affectation (sunat.spi:28/195/298); (3) unify the two regime vocabularies (lifecycle.spi:9 string nominals vs families.spi:714 phantoms), then buyer_response r GADT so PartlyAccepted under NF-e/DIAN does not type (lifecycle.spi:17); (4) event_log membership/audit as indexed types without i64 codes (event_log.spi:110/154); (5) purchase c s carrying money::amount c, and canon_document's currency tied to it (p2p.spi:13, document.spi:43). Others: sunat document_type d with note_reason d (:101/116/141), lifecycle event a with actor phantom (:138-156), canon term_id k / data_type d (:7/15/378), families family_root s with a gate-kind prototype (:12/690). TOOL BUG: kit standards --census reports lines=623 for fiscal/src where wc gives 6,645, so its per-1k figures for fiscal are about 10x too high (mega sample line counts are right); reported to rig.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:1x rig TRIAGE of the census line count (fiscal's report): ROOT CAUSE in kit src/rig_style_measure/measure.spi tests_from, which subtracts test lines from the denominator. It entered \"test region\" at a ///> marker and left it ONLY at a := main / inl main line. A package is measured as its top-level .spi files concatenated in ordinal order; fiscal/src has no main, so everything after the first file's first test block counted as tests. Replayed on the box: ordinal order gives exactly 623 (the installed census prints 623); the construct counts are unaffected (they scan all lines), as fiscal saw. It is not fiscal-only: 144 of kit's 651 packages are undercounted the same way (agile_task_next 43 instead of 876, rig_experiments 93 instead of 661), because in a multi-file package only the last module has a main. FIX (unstaged, rig_style_measure): a test block now ends at the next top-level line that is not its :# header (ends_test_block), plus a fixture for a test block followed by plain definitions and no main; kit standards 0 findings, ratchet 0 regressions (the fix only raises denominators). fiscal/src under the new rule: 6,482 lines (6,645 minus 163 test lines). Proof status: the algorithm is proven by the replay; the Spiral edit itself is UNPROVEN off-train (rig_style_measure links rig_style_probes, and the ganymede notebook harness does not build unit graphs); it rides TRAIN44. Until then divide fiscal's counts by about 6.5k lines, not 623.")
