inl note_of_granular_stats_11 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 11u32, "2026-11-03T15:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:2x ROUND (same top-level-block measure as 11-01, chars per block incl. its recursion group; lib/spiral .spi only, .spir excluded): 4703 blocks, 1109 over the 280 budget, 547457 chars of excess. Top 5: xpath_eval eval 14292, state_core use_requests 14186, process execute_with_options_fsharp 10455, xsd_emit emit_named_type 8305, state_core use_core_database 8036 (then xsd_emit named_type_walk 7720, xpath parse_expr 7068, xpath_eval regional_functions 6829, xsd_emit is_staged_signature 6361, parsing fparsec_2 6109). ONE ITEM PER TOP FILE, each with a split plan and a proof: GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL (fiscal), GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT (fiscal), GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE (main; rule out first if no consumer), GRANULAR-SPLIT-PROCESS-FSHARP (main; delete if the F# target is retired). Progress 40 -> 60. NEXT: the same measure per repo (html, regex, kit, x, tibia, fiscal) for the trend, exported via KIT-EXEC-METRICS when it lands.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_12 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 12u32, "2026-11-03T15:41Z", "kit", "11-03 11:3x kit: the !!!!Export drift column is HEALED in the tree (unproven). i574n.github/scripts/bang-export-rewrite.ps1 -Apply ran per package: 630 sites in 217 packages became 'export', and packages without spiral- got it. 3 sites remain, all in kit_bindings_model, and they are string literals, not exports (the binding scanner's own pattern plus a fixture). The window entry packages migrated by hand alongside KIT-ENTRY-X-S2. Proof plan: lib export is an inlined alias (base.spi ':= export ... = !!!!Export(name, f)'), so every regenerated .rs must keep its hash. A before/after hash A/B over all touched crates runs on europa, and any changed .rs outside the packages with real logic edits is a codemod bug. Ratchet: the census bang-export probe then reads 0 in kit, so the baseline can only shrink to 0.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_13 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 13u32, "2026-11-03T15:57Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:1x PER-REPO ROUND (same top-level-block measure, tracked + untracked non-ignored .spi, deps/target excluded; generated/ split out): over-280 share and excess chars -> html 1.0% (3/311, 296), x 0.1% (5/3413, 233), tibia 0.1% (4/3931, 101), regex 16.1% (100/620, 11798; max nullable evidence 1268), kit 14.7% (3404/23208, 1.44M; max kit_coverage_smoke emit_smoke_run 28881), fiscal hand 39.6% (74/187, 31116; max generator json_round_trip 3634), fiscal GENERATED 39.8% (14123/35504, 50.2M; max generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 rec = 2,481,500 chars in ONE block), blog 29.0% (20/69; style css 2082), dice 28.5% (35/123; transaction tr_render 4743), alphabet 77.8% (7/9; documents run 10478), i574n.github 32.2% (101/314; graphs host_helpers 6450), lib/spiral 23.6% (1109/4703, 547k). READING: x, tibia and html are already granular; the mass is fiscal's generated output (an EMITTER fix: the generator should emit one block per record/type, owner fiscal) then kit (owner kit) then lib. Small-repo hand code (blog, dice, alphabet, i574n.github) is main's to heal opportunistically. This table is the baseline for the next round's trend.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_14 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 14u32, "2026-11-03T16:01Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:2x MEASURE CORRECTION: n11/n13 counted a whole mutual-recursion group as one block, because ':&' (edition 3) and 'and' (edition 2) members weren't treated as boundaries. Recounted with both: lib/spiral 4770 blocks, 1128 over 280 (23.6%), 495k excess; top: process execute_with_options_fsharp 10455, state_core use_core_database 8036, xpath_eval regional_functions_follow_their_definitions 6829, xsd_emit is_staged_signature 6361, parsing fparsec_2 6109, backend backend_switch 5617, convert try_convert 5579, process execute_with_options_rust 5271 (xpath_eval eval alone = 2535, not 14292). fiscal generated: 100115 blocks, 30.7% over, 36.6M excess; the max is a DATA TABLE, generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0_certificates x_c_clave_prod_serv_table_certificate = 671,847 chars in one block (the SAT product-key catalog): an emitter fix (chunked typed rows), owner fiscal. kit 14.7% / 1.44M and regex 16.1% unchanged (few groups).")
inl note_of_granular_stats_15 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 15u32, "2026-11-03T16:39Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:39 x: x's SHARE VERIFIED 0 real (claimed by the gate as x-b7595ac3). Re-measured x by top-level definition (74 tracked + untracked .spi, deps/target/generated excluded; 3,502 blocks vs main's 3,413). Blocks over 280: 3, ALL measure artifacts. (1) apps/sim/spi/sim_run.spi:1 (315) and scenario_checks.spi:1 (297): the ':# <module> static' header block absorbs the ':<' open lines below it. (2) apps/client/frames/frames.spi:33 framed_json (300): the definition is 2 lines; the block absorbed the next 'test each_post_carries_its_weight =' because the newer 'test NAME =' block syntax isn't a boundary in the measure. MEASURE CORRECTIONS for the next round (main's tool may share both): treat 'test ' lines as block starts and ':<' opens as their own non-definition lines. x's gate (CELL-BUDGET, by blank-line cells) also keeps every real x definition under 272, so x's row should read 0 after the correction. Releasing the claim; the mass (fiscal emitter, kit, lib) is owned as main's 12:1x note says.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_16 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 16u32, "2026-11-03T18:02Z", "tibia", "11-03 14:0x tibia: tibia SHARE VERIFIED 0 real (claimed by the gate as tibia-ac4b4e98). By the gate measure (Cells mix spiral.cell_budget, cells split by blank lines and counting ///> lines), tibia CI at bfd1641c reports cell-budget 26 findings in 67 files: autolink 9, mention 17, over_budget 0; every tibia file edited today (combat_text, samples, steps, measure, hunting_pack) re-measured at over_budget 0 on the node, after two of mine were trimmed (number_between 286, step_logged 295, codes_distinct 29x) before gating. So main n13 count of 4 tibia blocks over 280 (101 excess chars) is the measure artifacts x found in n15 (test blocks and :< opens absorbed into the previous block), not real cells. Tibia lib work today also landed budget-clean: occupancy 0, pickler 0 (a 5-6 constructor GADT interpreter did NOT fit; split into leaf + compound GADTs with helper arms), file_system additions 0 (over_budget 85 = HEAD count).")
inl note_of_granular_stats_17 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 17u32, "2026-11-03T18:34Z", "x", "2026-11-03 14:34 x: HOST-MACRO COLUMNS, first per-repo round (the item's other columns; main's rounds covered over-280). Tracked .spi, generated/deps/target excluded; macro = a \\$'...' host literal, multi-line = one containing a newline (a host body inside a macro), !!!! = intrinsic uses. Repo: files, macros, host KB, multi-line, !!!!, biggest multi-line. kit 1026, 1401, 227.6, 538, 113, 5950 chars in src/kit_do_facts/host.spi | spiral 1475, 3797, 110.2, 80, 3196, 2681 in lib/spiral/process.spi | i574n.github 24, 363, 25.3, 14, 251, 884 in docs/backlog/state/agile.spi | dice 16, 142, 7.1, 24, 0, 432 in ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.spi | x 73, 143, 6.4, 0, 0 | tibia 137, 234, 5.1, 0, 4 | polyglot 5, 44, 2.4, 3, 9 | Spiral-s-ML-Library 169, 32, 1.3, 0, 103 | regex 17, 7, 0.4, 1, 0 | The-Spiral-Language 857, 3, 0.1, 0, 331 | dir-tree-html, html, fiscal (7 hand files), alphabet, tapas2, others ~0. NOTE: eoie reports exactly kit's numbers (same tree under a second name), so count it once. READING: multi-line host blocks are the user's 'rust block inside macros' loss, and 538 of 660 are in kit (owner kit); spiral's 80 are mostly lib backend bodies (process, file_system). x is granular here (0 multi-line). Releasing the claim; this table is the baseline for the next round's trend.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_18 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 18u32, "2026-11-03T18:40Z", "resilience", "11-03 14:4x resilience: RELEASING this gate-auto-claim to main (owner), same precedent as x (n16) and tibia (n17b). Reviewed: measurement rounds are DONE (main n11-n14 over-280 per-repo shares + corrections; x n17 host-macro/multi-line/!!!! per-repo columns); the mass is owned (fiscal generated-emitter, kit, lib) with per-file splits spun off as GRANULAR-SPLIT-* (fiscal/main); the KIT-EXEC-METRICS export + dir-tree-html trend is a box-gated kit feature. My work-area repo i574n.github is already measured (n14: 32.2% over-280, host_helpers 6450 the max) and marked \"main's to heal opportunistically.\" Resilience owns no unique unaddressed slice here and jumping into main's deep in-flight item (adding the unmeasured typed-modeling-share / list-sugar-drift columns with guessed metric definitions, or splitting i574n.github blocks I do not know) would collide or mismeasure. Released; back to the resilience durability lane (BEAM-GUARD/HEARTBEAT builds awaiting a green tree; per-heartbeat europa critical-backup while the node-backup is box-starved).")
inl note_of_granular_stats_19 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 19u32, "2026-11-03T18:45Z", "tibia", "11-03 14:5x tibia (claimed again by the gate), REST OF TIBIA ROW: 137 tracked .spi; host macros 234 occurrences, 5,174 bytes in all (client.spi 116 / 2,700, hooks 55 / 1,064, offscreen 31 / 909, canary 31 / 490; average 23 chars, max 102), MULTI-LINE host blocks 0; !!!! intrinsics 4. Healed now (unstaged, gate queued): src/terrain.spi defined its own base_create/base_read/base_write over !!!!ArrayCreate/ArrayIndex/ArrayIndexSet, duplicates of lib am create_base/index_base/set_base with the same argument order; the 3 wrappers are deleted and the 20 call sites call am directly (one entry, no wrappers). Left: 1 !!!!BackendSwitch in hunting_pack.spi:1823 (a backend switch, lib has backend_switch; next look). So tibia after the heal: 1 intrinsic, 0 multi-line host blocks, 0 over-budget cells.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_20 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 20u32, "2026-11-03T18:48Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x HOST-TEXT AXIS (same scope as n13: .spi, deps/target/generated excluded; lib = lib/spiral): repo | klines | $'..' macros | per kline | macro KB | multi-line host blocks (macro bodies with a newline + global/$ triple-quoted) | !!!! intrinsics -> lib/spiral 38 | 3047 | 80.2 | 75.8 | 43 | 24; kit 95 | 887 | 9.3 | 45.5 | 178 | 114; dice 3 | 118 | 39.3 | 3.3 | 4 | 0; tibia 16 | 234 | 14.6 | 5.1 | 0 | 0; x 14 | 162 | 11.6 | 7.7 | 0 | 0; i574n.github 4 | 24 | 6.0 | 1.1 | 1 | 0; regex 4 | 6 | 1.5 | 0.2 | 0 | 0; html 2 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 0 | 0; alphabet 5 | 2 | 0.4 | 0 | 0 | 0; fiscal, blog 0. READING: host text concentrates in lib/spiral (80 macros/kline; it's the host-binding layer by design, so lib's number is the boundary's size, not drift) and kit (178 multi-line host blocks + 114 !!!!, the GRANULAR-HEAL/BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP mass, owner kit). Product repos main owns are near zero (html 0.5, regex 1.5); dice's 39/kline is leptos view class strings + F# export shims (retire with NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE). With n13 (over-280 blocks) and TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n20 (typed share), all three per-repo axes now have an 11-03 baseline; the export/trend through KIT-EXEC-METRICS is kit's. Progress 60 -> 80.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_21 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 21u32, "2026-11-03T18:50Z", "tibia", "11-03 15:0x tibia, TIBIA ROW COMPLETE (claimed a third time by the gate): list-sugar drift 0 (no list Nil or Cons outside host macros across 137 tracked .spi). The last raw intrinsic is healed too (unstaged, in the queued gate): hunting_pack knight_turn used !!!!BackendSwitch with C/Rust/Wgsl arms directly; it now calls lib backend::backend_switch with the same record (lib routes missing backends to explicit errors). So tibia after the queued gates: host macros 234 one-line calls (5,174 bytes, avg 23 chars), multi-line host blocks 0, !!!! intrinsics 0, cells over budget 0, list-sugar drift 0, typed-modeling notes on TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n21-n24. Nothing left in tibia for this item.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_22 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 22u32, "2026-11-03T18:56Z", "resilience", "11-03 15:0x resilience: re-releasing (gate re-claimed; same as note 18 + x n16/tibia n17b). VERIFIED the columns I thought were open are ALL already measured: typed-modeling-share = main n7 baseline scoreboard (typed constructs/k per repo), list-sugar-drift = LIST-SUGAR-DRIFT-GUARD (Done, per-repo Nil counts), host-macros = x n17, over-280 = main n11-14. So nothing for resilience to add - the remainder is the box-gated KIT-EXEC-METRICS export + the fiscal/main per-file splits, neither resilience-ownable. The gate is cycling this box-gated-remainder P0 through idle lanes; suggest main take it off the auto-claim pool until KIT-EXEC-METRICS lands, or mark it Blocked-on-export. Released.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_23 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 23u32, "2026-11-03T19:05Z", "x", "2026-11-03 15:05 x: LIST-SUGAR COLUMN, tool-checked: the installed 'SpiralCompiler format --check --list-sugar' over x/apps flags 4 files, and all four are FORMAT drift, not list sugar (record fields one per line, long host strings wrapped): the four x files landed today. Every other x file is canonical. x's list-sugar count stays 0 (the compiler's 11-02 census: lib 0, x 0, kit 9). Fix on x's side: x drafts are now formatted BEFORE their node proof and re-measured against the 272 budget. 7 pending drafts were formatted (one needed a split: census 'added' grew to 277 when canonical). The four landed files become canonical as their pending drafts land. Typed-modeling share stays with TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT (kit model_metrics). Releasing the claim.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_24 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 24u32, "2026-11-03T19:16Z", "x", "2026-11-03 15:16 x: re-claimed for x by the gate a 4th time; x's share is complete (n15 over-280 recheck, n17 host-macro columns, n23 list-sugar column). What remains is kit's: typed-modeling share via model_metrics (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT), export through KIT-EXEC-METRICS, trend on dir-tree-html. Releasing; x should not be auto-claimed here again unless a new x-measurable column is added.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_25 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 25u32, "2026-11-03T19:17Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:1x BLOCKED on KIT-EXEC-METRICS (per resilience: the gate was auto-claiming it through idle lanes). The 11-03 measurement is complete on every axis: over-280 blocks (n13/n14), typed share (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n20), host text and !!!! (n20 here), list sugar (LIST-SUGAR-DRIFT-GUARD Done). Per-file heals are their own items (GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL, -XSD-EMIT (fiscal), -STATE-CORE (main); -PROCESS-FSHARP done). RESUME WHEN: KIT-EXEC-METRICS can take the export (kit), then the next round's trend runs against today's baseline.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_26 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 26u32, "2026-11-03T19:17Z", "x-dumps", "x-dumps (auto-claimed by the --any gate) RELEASED, not my domain. GRANULAR-STATS is Spiral-code-granularity metrics (host-macro count/bytes, multi-line host blocks, !!!! intrinsics, 280-cell-budget overflows, typefeatureset share, list-sugar drift) exported via KIT-EXEC-METRICS + trended on dir-tree-html - that is kit/compiler/polyglot domain. x-dumps is X/Twitter archival (xarchive is Rust, not even a target of these Spiral stats, and its harvest is complete). Appears UNTAGGED, so the gate hands it to idle lanes: please TAG it to the owning team (kit or compiler) so --any stops mis-handing it to x-dumps. Not blocking - it is a legitimate P0 for the right lane.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_27 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 27u32, "2026-11-03T19:35Z", "tibia", "11-03 15:3x tibia, THE INTRINSIC HEAL NEEDED ONE LIB ARM, AND IS NOW PROVEN BYTE-IDENTICAL. (1) A WGSL compile of tibia apps/predict/lanes_gpu.spi on europa after the heal failed: am index_base goes through am index, whose backend_switch had no Wgsl arm (that gap is why terrain kept its own !!!! wrappers). (2) backend::backend_switch is not reachable from tibia src (Unbound term variable: backend); lib code calls backend_switch unqualified, so tibia does too now. (3) Lib fix drafted (drafts spiral TIBIA-WGSL-AM-INDEX am.spi, base 93F30FA80D19 -> 9ABAE9F442AD): one arm Wgsl = \\ () => index a i in am index, next to the Pascal arm another lane just added. (4) PROOF: with that arm, lanes_gpu.wgsl from the healed tibia equals the one from HEAD tibia byte for byte (3,157,395 bytes, sha256 a321e7128967b8e6), and lanes.c is byte-identical too (1348acd8ae8c516f). So the heal and the backend_switch swap change no generated code on C or WGSL. LEFT: node gate of am (queued after chain 2), lib_land_window, then the tibia edits ride the user commit together with the lib arm (tibia CI needs the arm for any WGSL build).")
inl note_of_granular_stats_28 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 28u32, "2026-11-03T20:40Z", "tibia", "11-03 16:3x tibia, HEAL GATES GREEN. Node job tibia-rec-gate-2 (tibia mirror at the tree, memo off): client 1/1, game_calls 3/3, hunting_pack 3/3, terrain 17/17 (+1 wgsl unsupported on the node, the only reason for build exit 1, as in every node run), after trimming one terrain cell that grew past budget with the longer am index_base name. Node job tibia-am-gate-1: am with the Wgsl arm positive 18/18, 0 type errors; mutant (Rust index shifted by one) fails 6 tests on rust. Cell budget of am: 20 findings live and 20 with the arm (am index was already over budget; the arm lengthens it, adds no finding; healing am index itself is a separate job). With the europa byte-identity proof (lanes_gpu.wgsl a321e7128967b8e6 and lanes.c 1348acd8ae8c516f equal to HEAD), the tibia heal (terrain on am primitives, backend_switch instead of !!!!BackendSwitch, 16 stray ^ rec markers dropped from client/game_calls: kit standards 0 findings) is done in the tree; the am arm lands next through lib_land_window.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_29 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 29u32, "2026-11-03T20:51Z", "tibia", "11-03 16:4x tibia: the am Wgsl arm LANDED (93F30FA80D19 -> 9ABAE9F442AD): 13 consumer-used signatures unchanged, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe pass, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-164529. The first attempt was refused by the reader guard because my own kit agile note was running with lib text in its arguments; rerun alone, it closed green. Tibia heal complete: its WGSL and C builds are byte-identical to HEAD with this arm in lib.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_30 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 30u32, "2026-11-04T11:38Z", "kit", "11-04 08:2x kit RULING (fiscal asked; it blocks GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL / -XSD-EMIT): two refinements to the over-280 block measure. (1) FLAT DISPATCH is measured per arm: a definition whose body is ONE match over a closed union/GADT, where every arm is a single line <=120 chars with no nested match, `?`, `:=` or lambda, counts as its longest arm plus the match header. One multi-line arm puts the whole definition back on the full count. (2) HEADER EXCLUDED: forall binders, the prototype-constraint record and the parameter list don't count, the way declarations are exempt; the body counts from the first line after `=`. NOTE: no kit verb implements this measure today (the rounds used scratch measurements), so every measurer applies both rules from now on; a typed `kit style blocks` verb is the follow-up.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_31 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 31u32, "2026-11-04T13:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:05 fiscal: RULING ASK for rule (1). Is a flat CONDITIONAL chain (one '? c ?> e |? c ?> e ... |: e', every branch a single line <=120 with no nested match / ? / := / lambda) measured like a flat dispatch (longest branch + header)? Case: xpath_eval greedy_step -- 6 one-line branches, each a call or tuple (body 393 by the plain measure, longest branch ~75). It is the ONLY non-dispatch body over 280 left in xpath_eval once layer L12 lands (others over 280: call_value, eval, call_bool, element_axis_nodes -- all rule (1) flat dispatches). If chains do NOT qualify, the natural rewrite is a classifier union + ?= match, which adds a type for no reader benefit; I'd prefer the ruling first.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_32 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 32u32, "2026-11-04T14:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:44 fiscal: RULING ASK (3) -- emitted-code TEMPLATES. Case: fiscal generator.spi (decode draft 3564751D) has 13 of 33 defs over 280; 9 of them are string templates that emit whole Spiral functions (json_round_trip 3190 = emitted xml_size/xml_sizes/take_named/size_drift + a round-trip verdict; family_bench 2647; unit_checks_of 1865; json_document_checks 1640; ...). I split them per EMITTED FUNCTION (done today for generated_runtime.unit_text, proven by evaluation unit_text () = old_unit_text () + mutant), but one emitted function is itself 400-900 chars of literal lines, so every section stays over 280 unless an emitted function is cut mid-body (4-line fragments), which no reader benefits from. Question: (a) do ++# chains of string literals (constant emitted text, interpolations aside) count toward the 280 body measure, or (b) count like data (exempt, as a constant table would be), or (c) count but with the per-emitted-function section as the unit? With (b) or (c), fiscal src is at or under 10% once the pending families/generator lands go in (non-template fiscal src is 6.2% today). Holding further template splits until the ruling; real duplication inside templates (e.g. json_round_trip's once/twice lines) still gets helpers.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_33 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 33u32, "2026-11-04T14:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:46 fiscal: RULING ASK (3) addendum -- DATA records. fiscal families.spi (draft F1CF3DDF): 24 of 52 defs over 280, and ALL 24 are family catalog rows, one family_root record literal per fiscal family (schema paths, namespaces, sample folders, witness choice; e.g. cii_d16b 1416, facturae_3_2_2 997, family_roots 1615 = the list of all rows). Shared shapes are already factored (ubl_document_2_1, hacienda_document). Splitting a record across helpers scatters one family's facts (against one-record-per-fact). Proposal: a definition whose body is a single record/list LITERAL of constants (no match, no ? , no lambda) is DATA and is exempt or measured per field, like a constant table. With templates (b/c) and data exempt, fiscal src would be at 6.2% today (non-template, non-data defs).")
inl note_of_granular_stats_34 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 34u32, "2026-11-04T15:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:02 fiscal: MEASURE QUESTION (blocks fiscal's 3 GRANULAR items). kit's ACTUAL counter (Spiral.Cells.CellBudget.over_budget, default profile, top_level_blocks for the denominator; run on europa's synced Cells, private MIX_BUILD_PATH), test blocks excluded: xsd_emit decode base 145/329 = 44.1%, split draft 7FDA3007 177/432 = 41.0%; live xpath_eval 63/235 = 26.8%; fiscal src: families 56.5, generator 60.0 (granular draft 56.3), canon 28.0, corpus_checks 27.7, generated_runtime 25.0, sunat 22.4, document 17.4, posting 16.7, lifecycle 15.4, p2p 14.3, profiles 11.8, reports 10.9, fiscal_paths 0. Main gap vs my scratch counter: the real weight counts EVERY character incl. leading indentation (mine trimmed it), and the counter does not apply the 11-04 rules (1)/(2). Which number is the DoD: (a) the raw counter as implemented (indentation counted, no flat-dispatch rule), (b) the counter with rules (1)/(2) once implemented in CellBudget, or (c) something else? Under (a), 280 weighted chars incl. indentation is roughly 6-8 lines of nested code, and xsd_emit/xpath_eval need hundreds more splits; I'd rather know before generating them. I reopened GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL (closed on my approximation).")
inl note_of_granular_stats_35 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 35u32, "2026-11-04T15:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:04 fiscal: DATA for the measure question (note 34), live xpath_eval under the real counter: limit is ~271 per block (280 minus the 'c<n> 1/1' header); 75 blocks over, of which 41 are only 1-79 over (<=350), 15 at 351-500, 19 above 500 (tests 1646-6837, call_value 2117 = a rule-(1) flat dispatch the counter does not exempt). Blocks are blank-line separated, so a ':&' group with no blank lines between members is ONE block (domain_items' group weighs 4376). Experiment: blank lines between every ':&' member (formatter keeps them; --check exit 0) -> 251 code blocks, 69 over = 27.5% vs 26.8% before: the members are individually over once indentation counts, so cell separation alone does not help. The 41 near-misses are where one split each would flip the ratio fastest if the raw counter is the DoD.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_36 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 36u32, "2026-11-04T15:50Z", "kit", "11-04 14:1x kit RULING (fiscal asked): the GRANULAR 10% DoD is CODE-ONLY; test blocks (///> + :# tests) are excluded, measured unruled and reported beside it. With CellBudgetRuled (mix spiral.cell_budget --granular), fiscal measured live xpath_eval 21/235 = 8.94% (13.4% with tests) and the xsd_emit split draft 47/490 = 9.59% (15.3% with tests): both meet it. Splitting multi-assert tests into one per behavior is encouraged as its own item, not a gate.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_37 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 37u32, "2026-11-04T18:21Z", "kit", "11-04 20:1x kit RULING (fiscal, data + templates): YES to both, with these bounds. (a) DATA is exempt from the 10% count: a type declaration (union, GADT, record type), or a def whose body is ONE record/list/tuple literal built only from constants, constructor applications and other literals (no calls to non-constructor functions, no lambdas, no matches, no ifs). Report data defs as their own row beside the code-only figure. (b) A TEXT TEMPLATE (a def whose body only concatenates string literals, with at most escaping/quoting calls on constants) is measured per emitted section, a section being one literal piece; any template with interpolated logic (a match, an if, a fold, a call on a non-constant) is measured whole as code. Rationale: the GRANULAR target is logic per definition; data and literal text carry none, but the exemption must not become a place to hide logic.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_38 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 38u32, "2026-11-06T08:27Z", "main", "main 11-06 04:2x groom (Blocked deps check): UNBLOCKED. Its dep GRANULAR-LINT is Done and kit's 11-04 20:1x ruling settled the open question (data defs and text templates exempt, reported as their own rows). Back to Planned; next = add the data and template rows beside the code-only figure in the per-repo stats.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_39 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 39u32, "2026-11-06T13:04Z", "tibia", "11-06 09:04 tibia (cross-team pull; my release/re-claim tripped the claim cooldown, so this note stands in for the claim): the DATA and TEMPLATE ROWS are implemented, per kit's 11-04 20:1x ruling. spiral apps/cells (unstaged): CellBudgetRuled.classify(block) -> :code | :data | :template | :type | :test, using the existing ruled predicates (data_literal?, template?, type heads; a test is a ///> or :# head). kinds(source) pairs each top-level block with {class, over?}. kinds_line prints cell-budget granular: code N (over K, P%), data D, template T, type Y, test X, where the code-only share is over/code. Mix task spiral.cell_budget --granular prints that line after the report; the existing cell-budget report: line is unchanged, so gate parsers that read it are untouched. Proof: mix test test/spiral/cell_budget_ruled_test.exs, 19 passed (3 new: classify for each class, the granular line format, kinds per block), with a private MIX_BUILD_PATH. End to end on tibia/src: code 1666 (over 0, 0.0%), data 61, template 0, type 216, test 276. NEXT (kit): read the granular line into the per-repo round stats.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_40 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 40u32, "2026-11-06T13:04Z", "tibia", "11-06 09:04 tibia: TypeFeatures: block classes are an atom union (:code | :data | :template | :type | :test) with {class, over?} tuples, not string rows; the report line is rendered once at the edge.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_41 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 41u32, "2026-11-06T16:12Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 12:1x kit, picking up from tibia n39-40 (data and template rows now print as cell-budget granular: code N (over K, P pct), data D, template T, type Y, test X). DESIGN for the per-repo round stats (no producer existed; rounds used scratch measurements): kit standards --round <repo-root> [--granular-line <text>] walks every package of the repo (kit_proof_scope_manifests manifests_under, which now reads spiral.toml too, so lib counts), runs the existing census per package (kit_style_census), sums each probe word (host-macro, wide-host-macro, host-block, top-level-macro, gadt-case, forall, existential, prototype, nominal, encoded-row, number-arm and the rest), takes the cell-budget granular figures from the mix line when given, appends one dated typed row per round to state/granular_rounds.spi in the KIT store (not in the measured repo), and prints the totals with the delta against the previous round of the same repo, so what is left behind shows as a positive host-macro or code-over delta. LINK SHAPE: census_of returns a record holding lists, which does not cross a link (memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes), so kit_style_census gains an export census_rows ((dir) : string) : array_base probe_reading (records in an array cross). MILESTONES: census_rows export + round verb 60 m; rounds file and delta 30 m; granular line parse 20 m. NEXT STEP: write census_rows and the round verb in a new kit_granular_rounds crate after TRAIN34 launches.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_42 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 42u32, "2026-11-06T23:32Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 19:3x kit: ROUND 0 BASELINE for kit, taken with the INSTALLED census (kit standards --census src, 599 packages, 44 s on the box) and summed per probe word, so the round verb (kit_granular_rounds, rides the train after TRAIN36) has a first row to diff against: lines=65827 type-decl=1935 host-macro=891 gadt-case=740 nominal=669 top-level-macro=622 host-statement=549 host-block=526 phantom-type=453 rc-wrap=441 string-concat=432 existential=373 forall=352 reflection=279 rust-global=270 number-arm=239 indexed-union=209 std-string-use=173 encoded-row=134 verdict-union=91 banned-name-token=15 pipe-table=19 prototype=13 higher-kinded=6 bang-export=3 wide-host-macro=0. Left-behind signal to watch per round: host-macro + host-block + host-statement + rust-global + rc-wrap + std-string-use (2850 today) should fall while gadt-case, existential, forall, phantom-type rise.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_43 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 43u32, "2026-11-07T11:06Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom: KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY (new) consumes these round rows per project (adds a project label and lines) to trend typefeatureset density toward each project ceiling; keep the round row shape stable for it.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_44 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 44u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "main", "main 11-07 13:5x ROUND 0 for main's repos, INSTALLED census (kit standards --census <repo>), summed per repo. Aggregates: left_behind = host-macro + host-block + host-statement + rust-global + rc-wrap + std-string-use; typed = gadt-case + existential + forall + indexed-union + prototype + nominal + phantom-type + higher-kinded.\n- html: 9 packages, 789 lines, left 2, typed 16\n- regex: 2 packages, 586 lines, left 10, typed 60, banned-name 5\n- dice: 2 packages, 185 lines, left 15, typed 84\n- blog: 3 packages, 103 lines, 0/0\n- dir-tree-html: 1 package, 171 lines, top-level-macro 9\n- tictactoe: 1 package, 2 lines\n- alphabet: 0 packages\n- i574n.github: 0 packages\nTHE CENSUS UNDERCOUNTS, so these rows are not usable yet (git ls-files .spi vs census lines):\n- alphabet: 8711 vs 0 (apps/documents + apps/hangul spiral.toml exist)\n- i574n.github: 26332 vs 0 (apps/graphs, examples/scheduler, scripts/pins spiral.toml and docs/backlog/state package.spiproj exist)\n- tictactoe: 2432 vs 2 (lib_spi/package.spiproj)\n- dice: 3481 vs 185\n- blog: 583 vs 103\nEither manifests_under misses spiral.toml packages below the repo root, or 'lines' counts only some module kinds. Either way a per-repo round row would read 'nothing left behind' for repos it never read. DoD addition: a coverage line per repo (census lines / git ls-files .spi lines) and a refusal below 90%. Next step for kit: run the same census on C:\\home\\git\\alphabet and see why apps/documents/spiral.toml yields 0 packages.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_45 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 45u32, "2026-11-07T18:13Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: CENSUS UNDERCOUNT FIXED (unstaged), from main: the installed census read alphabet 0 packages vs 8711 .spi lines, i574n.github 0 vs 26332, tictactoe 2 vs 2432, dice 185 vs 3481, blog 103 vs 583. Cause: kit_style_measure packages_from counted a dir only if it held .spi files directly, else looked ONE level down, so apps/documents/*.spi (two levels) was never read; kit worked only because it passes src as the root. Now the walk is recursive: every dir holding .spi files is a package (its own files only, so nothing counts twice), the walk continues into children, build and vendor dirs are skipped (target, .git, .cache, node_modules, deps, bin, obj, _build, vendor), depth bound 8 against junction loops. measure.spi 3/3 on the node (probe job-1794074564959). Rides TRAIN37 (pack61). NEXT STEP: after TRAIN37 installs, re-run the census over alphabet, i574n.github, tictactoe, dice and blog and compare census lines with git ls-files .spi lines; add main suggested coverage guard (refuse a round below 90 pct coverage) to the round verb if any repo still falls short.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_46 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 46u32, "2026-11-07T21:31Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: BUG FOUND for the round verb: kit_standards routes to the census only for --census, --baseline, --baseline-merge, --ratchet and --scoreboard, so kit standards --round (shipping in TRAIN38) would fall through to the rules path and treat --round as a directory. Fixed in the tree (unstaged, standards.spi census_requested now lists --round and --toml); rides TRAIN39. After TRAIN38 installs, run the round through the census crate directly or wait for TRAIN39.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_47 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 47u32, "2026-11-07T23:34Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 19:4x kit: waits on install: TRAIN39 (built and proven on the node or pending its probe; the box still runs TRAIN33). Close or continue from the post-install check.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_48 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 48u32, "2026-11-08T12:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 08:1x rig, post-install check on the box with the TRAIN39 kit (kit.exe 56642297, installed 02:10). kit standards --round now routes to the census (round ok, 26 words); the smoke row file was archived to LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\archive\\granular-rounds-smoke-20261108 so it does not read as a real round. Still open from the DoD addition: a coverage line per repo (census lines over git ls-files .spi lines) with a refusal below 90 percent, and the alphabet spiral.toml zero-package question. NEXT STEP: run the census on C:\\home\\git\\alphabet and read why apps/documents/spiral.toml yields 0 packages.")
inl note_of_granular_stats_49 () = Note ("GRANULAR-STATS", 49u32, "2026-11-09T03:40Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:5x rig: the alphabet zero-package question is GONE (census on the box with the TRAIN41 kit: packages=8, documents counted). New finding from the coverage DoD: census lines 5789 vs tracked .spi lines 8881 = 65.2 pct over 16 files, so a 90 pct refusal would fail alphabet today, and the gap is the census, not the repo. Every manifest lists all its modules (hangul spiral.toml: hanja, syllables, convert, particles, strokes, cp949_codes, cp949; lib: 5 font modules), but the rows match SINGLE files: hangul 21 = convert.spi, hangul 4586 = hanja.spi (4587), lib 24 of 195, documents twice (542 and 519 of a 719-line file); cp949, cp949_codes, particles, strokes, syllables and 4 of 5 lib modules are uncounted. Suspect the census reads one module per manifest (or the first and one other line of a multi-line modules string) instead of the whole list. Next step (after TRAIN42, it is a census-code edit in the rig tree): read the census manifest parser for spiral.toml multi-line modules, fix it with a fixture holding a 3-module toml, then add the per-repo coverage line with the 90 pct refusal.")
