inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_1 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:43Z", "kit", "11-01 08:4x kit, slice of EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR (main 08:4x: slice it like SCRUM-XP; milestones M2-M5 from the 10-25 note, M1 shipped in TRAIN4c). DoD: zero calls to 'remote.ps1 node job' in kit and in the lanes' memories (stem grep, memory dangling-check-by-stem); remote.ps1's job verbs become a one-line shim printing the kit spelling for one release. NEXT STEP: grep callers, migrate memories and scripts, shim. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a beyond S1-S3 (glue removal); the shim emits the typed route's spelling, not a hand-copied string.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_2 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 2u32, "2026-11-03T16:14Z", "kit", "11-03 12:4x kit: stem grep done. kit/scripts, kit/src and i574n.github/scripts: 0 callers of 'remote.ps1 <machine> job'. Memories: 7 files (waiter-stop-leaves-job, status-files-need-age, keep-node-busy, node-lib-land-mirror-needs, remote-kit-worker-node, job-timeout-counts-queue-wait, node-launch-sync-minutes). Most use 'remote.ps1 node job list', and kit has NO 'job list --on' yet: JobList in kit_jobs/jobs.spi isn't placed, while start/status/wait/tail/stop already route. ORDER: (1) add JobList --on <alias> through kit_job_dispatch's forwarder, in the x shape (typed placement, no argument-index reads) and with a dispatch test; (2) rewrite the 7 memories: 'kit job start --on laptop ...' (the node's ssh alias is laptop), 'kit job wait|status|tail|stop <id>' (placement routes them), 'kit job list --on laptop'; (3) make remote.ps1's job verbs a one-line shim printing the kit spelling. Starts after the europa proof of the current kit_jobs WIP (process liveness), so two changes don't stack in one package mid-proof.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_3 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 3u32, "2026-11-03T17:30Z", "kit", "11-03 14:1x kit: step (1) in the tree (unproven): kit_job_dispatch.list_on_run (export kit_job_list_on) forwards 'kit job list --on <alias> [--bin <path>] [count]' over the same ssh options, now one ssh_to helper shared by start/forward/list. kit_jobs JobList routes '--on' to it; plain list stays local. Step (2) partly done: 3 memory instructions (node-launch-sync-minutes, node-lib-land-mirror-needs, remote-kit-worker-node) now say 'kit job start --on laptop' + 'kit job wait <id>'. The 4 'remote.ps1 node job list' sites switch to 'kit job list --on laptop' only after TRAIN16 installs it, so no memory names a verb that doesn't exist yet. Step (3), the remote.ps1 shim, follows the install.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_4 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 4u32, "2026-11-04T07:59Z", "kit", "11-04 04:3x kit PROBE: `kit job start --on laptop-ts --bin C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe <label> <ms> <cmd...>` works end to end with the installed kit (job-1793779134703-kit-on-probe: dispatched, then plain `kit job wait`/`tail` on the box routed by the recorded placement and returned the node output, exit 0). Two gaps stop it replacing remote.ps1 node job callers (launch-train's node half, precheck runs): (1) the default binary is bare `kit`, which is not on the node's PATH. Fix: a per-machine kit path in remote-machines.json read by dispatch (as remote.ps1 reads target.eoie), so --bin becomes optional. (2) remote.ps1 sets KIT_JOB_SLOTS from target.slots before `job start`; --on forwards no environment, so the node host would use its default slot count for a heavy train. Fix: dispatch prefixes the same env from the machine row. Then switch launch-train's three `$remote $Node job` calls to `kit job --on` (the launcher already holds the ssh host).")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_5 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 5u32, "2026-11-04T09:48Z", "kit", "11-04 07:4x kit: both probe gaps closed in the tree (unstaged). (1) Binary: kit_job_dispatch remembers --bin per alias in <jobs root>/machines/<alias>.bin; a later --on without --bin uses it (binary_of: given beats remembered, tests). list --on uses the same memory (list_on_run now takes the jobs root; entry passes it). (2) Slots: no forwarding needed. The remote host reads its own <jobs root>/slots (MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS), node = 6 is written. Proof: europa pack34 --check exit 0 for dispatch (with test bodies) and entry; box dispatch notebook queued. NEXT after the train installs it: switch launch-train's three `$remote $Node job` calls to `kit job start --on <ssh host> --bin C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe` once, then plain `kit job wait/tail <id>`.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_6 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 6u32, "2026-11-04T09:50Z", "kit", "11-04 08:0x kit: launcher switch DRAFTED, deliberately NOT applied: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\REMOTE-EXEC-S4-launch-train\\launch-train.ps1 (base sha 1860E666E19401C6, a 4-line diff; parses). The node half starts with `kit job start --on $SshHost --bin C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe`, then plain `kit job wait <id> 21600000` / `kit job tail <id> 40` (routed by the recorded placement). WHY PARKED: remote.ps1 prefixes KIT_JOB_SLOTS=6 on every node job start, and the node's shared job host takes its cap from whichever job starts it. A --on start forwards no env, and the installed node kit does not read <jobs root>/slots yet, so a train started this way could leave the node host uncapped for hours (MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS over-admission). APPLY when the node's C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe has the slots-file host (after the train that ships kit_job_host + kit_job_dispatch). Proof: `kit job list --on laptop-ts` with no --bin works, and a 7th node job queues. Box dispatch notebook: see the job.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_7 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 7u32, "2026-11-04T15:29Z", "kit", "11-04 13:4x kit: launcher draft REBASED on today's launch-train.ps1 (base sha 83ADC4009B3F0F09, which raises the node half to 10 h and the wrapper to 12 h): same 4-line change (node half via `kit job start --on $SshHost --bin C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe`, then plain `kit job wait <id> 43200000` and `kit job tail <id> 40`), CRLF kept (178), parses. Still parked until the node's kit has the slots-file host (TRAIN22).")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_8 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 8u32, "2026-11-04T19:28Z", "kit", "11-04 21:2x kit: TRAIN22 RED at the crate gate, partly on kit_job_dispatch dispatch.rs 1027 (the remembered --bin, binary_of + machine_binary inline). FIXED (unstaged): NEW linked crate kit_job_bin (export kit_job_machine_binary machine_binary ((jobs_root, machine, given))); dispatch keeps a one-line wrapper. Node size: kit_job_dispatch 968, kit_job_bin 170. The launcher draft stays parked until a train with this installs.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_9 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 9u32, "2026-11-04T22:49Z", "kit", "11-04 18:5x kit: launcher draft REBASED again, onto today's free-space-floor launch-train.ps1 (base sha 316F243DFCCE2529; the old draft kept as launch-train.ps1.base-83ADC400.bak beside it). Same 4-line change: $nodeKit, node half via `kit job start --on $SshHost --bin $nodeKit`, then `kit job wait <id> 43200000` and `kit job tail <id> 40`. CRLF kept (183), parses, diff against live = exactly those 4 hunks, $kit defined at line 20. Still parked until TRAIN25 (slots-file host + kit_job_bin) is installed on the node; then apply and prove with a 7th node job queuing.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_10 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 10u32, "2026-11-05T07:38Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:3x kit: S4 launch-train draft REBASED onto live BA23C6A309D51580 (live gained LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE's precheck block). The same 7-line block was inserted at the same anchor; the draft now differs from live by exactly S4's own hunks ($nodeKit, kit job start --on/--bin, kit job wait, kit job tail). Rebased draft 14A24741185F01B4; previous kept as launch-train.ps1.base316f in the draft dir. Still applies only after an install that carries --on/--bin (TRAIN28).")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_11 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 11u32, "2026-11-05T23:52Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 19:5x kit: live launch-train.ps1 changed again (KIT-TRAIN-WATCHER-RETRY wait loop, live hash 81841578748EB2B8), so the S4 draft (base BA23C6A3) needs one more rebase before it applies: its job wait call becomes the same retry loop.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_12 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 12u32, "2026-11-05T23:54Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 20:0x kit: S4 draft REBASED onto live 81841578 (with the KIT-TRAIN-WATCHER-RETRY loop): the same 4 S4 hunks (nodeKit, kit job start --on/--bin, kit job wait <id> 43200000 now inside the retry loop, kit job tail). Rebased draft D1F1F2A3, parse 0; previous kept as launch-train.ps1.baseBA23. Still applies only after an install that carries --on/--bin.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_13 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 13u32, "2026-11-06T13:15Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 09:2x kit: UNBLOCKED by the TRAIN33 install (kit.exe 6CEA882D carries --on/--bin). Dogfood on the box: kit job list --on node 3 fails ssh: Could not resolve hostname node, because the 11-06 mesh-key setup renamed the ssh aliases (laptop, laptop-ts, laptop-ip; there is no node alias any more), and kit job list --on laptop 3 runs a bare kit on the node, which is not on PATH there, until a job start --on laptop --bin C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe records the binary for that machine. So S4 call sites must pass the alias laptop and --bin, or better read both from remote-machines.json (sshAlias and the kit key, renamed from eoie today), which is KIT-NET-TOPOLOGY schema work. NEXT: rebase draft D1F1F2A3 onto the live launch-train.ps1, which changed again today (try/catch around the wait, UNKNOWN after 10 misses, -ResumeNodeJob), then apply.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_14 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 14u32, "2026-11-06T13:24Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 09:3x kit: draft REBASED onto live launch-train.ps1 992C546E (= HEAD 13b142b, which carries this morning try/catch wait, UNKNOWN after 10 misses and -ResumeNodeJob) by a 3-way merge from its base 81841578 (= 6c4df2e). One conflict, resolved by keeping the live loop shape and taking S4 calls. Rebased draft E97AC1FC in the kit drafts store (previous kept as launch-train.ps1.baseD1F1), parse 0, 4 hunks against live: nodeKit, kit job start --on $SshHost --bin $nodeKit, kit job wait $jobId 43200000 inside the try/catch loop, kit job tail. NOT applied to live on purpose: the next train should install today fixes over the proven remote.ps1 path. Apply plan: right after that train installs, apply E97AC1FC and launch the following train with -SshHost laptop (the node ssh alias since the 11-06 mesh-key rename) as its end-to-end proof; -ResumeNodeJob then needs a job that kit started with --on, since kit job wait reads local job records.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_15 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 15u32, "2026-11-06T20:51Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 16:5x kit: SMOKE on installed TRAIN33 kit: kit job start --on laptop --bin <node kit> kit-s4-smoke ... -> placement=remote, then box-local kit job wait and kit job tail resolved the remote id (exit=0, stdout returned): job-1793998183937-kit-s4-smoke. --on refuses quote characters in forwarded args (re-split guard); the node-half command has none. REBASED the stale draft onto todays launcher (base 87535985, which has the raw-block excuse and the 11 h retry): three lines change (node-half start via kit job start --on $SshHost --bin <kit path from remote-machines.json [$Node].kit, no hardcoded path>, wait via kit job wait, tail via kit job tail); parse 0. Draft at drafts/kit/REMOTE-EXEC-S4-launch-train/launch-train.ps1.rebased-87535985. APPLY only after TRAIN35s watcher exits (never patch a running launcher); the first train after that is its live proof.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_16 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 16u32, "2026-11-07T00:27Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 20:3x kit: APPLIED (unstaged) the rebased draft to scripts/launch-train.ps1 after stopping the TRAIN36 box watcher (TRAIN36 was already red; its node half keeps running for red discovery). Base 87535985 matched the tree; the copy before is archived beside the draft; parse 0. The node half now starts with kit job start --on $SshHost --bin <remote-machines.json [$Node].kit>, waits with kit job wait (12 h) and tails with kit job tail; no remote.ps1 job callers left in the launcher (remote.ps1 still does the repo syncs). The 11 h retry loop is unchanged and re-proven against the new call shape by the scratch harness (two misses then ok: backoff 60,120; spent window: UNKNOWN). Live proof: the next train launch.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_17 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 17u32, "2026-11-07T18:13Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: TRAIN37 (launched 14:12) is the first train whose node half starts through kit job start --on laptop --bin <remote-machines.json kit path>; live proof is the node half started line and a box-side kit job wait that resolves the remote id. Also fixed for node probes: compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1 now skips a top-level deps link in the kit workspace (node-proof.ps1 began linking deps/spiral into non-spiral repos at 13:03), which had made every kit regen probe throw Unexpected workspace link.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_18 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 18u32, "2026-11-07T18:22Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: LIVE PROOF for launch-train. TRAIN37 node half job-1794075557718-kit-TRAIN37 was started by kit job start --on laptop (its box job record says placement on laptop) and box-side kit job tail resolves the remote id; the watcher waits with box-local kit job wait. Left for this item: node-proof.ps1 (i574n.github scripts, main owns) still starts node jobs through remote.ps1 node job start; that caller moves under DELEGATE-1-VERB (kit delegate) rather than a script edit, so this item closes when DELEGATE-1 replaces node-proof. Progress 80.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_19 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 19u32, "2026-11-07T23:34Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 19:4x kit: waits on install: TRAIN39 (built and proven on the node or pending its probe; the box still runs TRAIN33). Close or continue from the post-install check.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_20 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 20u32, "2026-11-08T02:25Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 22:2x kit, BUG FOUND AND FIXED (for TRAIN40): the box judged a node-placed job dead. At 21:17 a kit job list on the box read job-1794098823854-kit-TRAIN39 (started on the node by kit job start --on laptop, so the box holds only a placement shadow: placement, remote-bin, label, started_ms) and job_state_now took its lost branch: no local supervisor, no heartbeat, no child, so it WROTE exit 125 lost (the memory-reaper text) for a job that was healthy on the node. Main saw it and asked whether TRAIN39 had died; kit job status forwards to the node and read running, kit job list read the local exit. Archiving the exit file did not help: the next list call wrote it again. FIX (kit_jobs/jobs.spi job_state_now): a record with a placement file is reported running locally and never written lost; the remote stays the authority (job status and job wait already forward). Proof pending: node probe ai (kit_jobs consumers kit_job_query and kit_job_state sizes). The false box exit file for that id stays until TRAIN40 installs. waits on install: TRAIN40")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_21 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 21u32, "2026-11-08T12:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 08:1x rig, post-install check on the box with the TRAIN39 kit (kit.exe 56642297, installed 02:10). The callers can only move to kit job --on once the box stops judging node-placed jobs lost; that fix (jobs.spi placement records never written as lost) is in TRAIN40, launched 08:09 as job-1794139763840-kit-TRAIN40-node. waits on install: TRAIN40")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_22 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 22u32, "2026-11-08T14:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 11:0x rig, post-install check with the TRAIN40 kit (kit.exe 6C4F076B, installed 10:52:57, pack61b core 65DEE79C; node notebooks 66/66 on candidate D5D22429). The TRAIN40 kit no longer writes a lost exit for a node-placed job. The one on the box (job-1794140052966-kit-TRAIN40 exit 125 lost, written 08:17 by the TRAIN39 kit before the fix) was archived to LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\archive\\false-lost-exit-20261108. Left: job list on the box shows a placed job as state=running with no forward to the node; it should read state=placed host=<host> or forward like job status does. NEXT STEP: that list line, then move the i574n.github remote.ps1 node job callers to kit job --on.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_23 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 23u32, "2026-11-08T15:19Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 11:2x rig: REGRESSION from the TRAIN40 fix, found by compiler: never writing a lost exit for a placement record meant a node-placed record whose box heartbeat stopped showed state=running forever, and install-when-clear skips any running *train* job, so 6 records (TRAIN37, TRAIN38, TRAIN39, TRAIN39r2, TRAIN40 node, s4-smoke) blocked pack62. Healed the data: kit job status forwarded to the node for each (all finished: exit 0 for TRAIN40, TRAIN39r2, s4-smoke; exit 1 for TRAIN37, TRAIN38, TRAIN39), the stale lost lines were archived to LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\archive\\false-lost-exit-20261108 and each record got the node's real exit line; pack62 then got its window at 11:09. CODE FIX for TRAIN41 (unstaged): job_live gains JobPlaced; a placement whose box heartbeat stopped is Live JobPlaced and lists as state=placed (not running), so a job running on another host never blocks a box install; the word parses back; new test line. Consumers match Live _ so nothing else changes; the 6 near-gate kit_jobs consumers measured after the change: kit_jobs_doctor 983, kit_job_summary 972, kit_job_gate 954, kit_machine_watch 947, kit_job_ticket 946, kit_window_run 944. NEXT STEP: job list forwards a placed record to its host (like job status), so it shows the real end.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_24 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 24u32, "2026-11-08T23:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:2x rig, TRAIN41 INSTALLED 19:12:49 (kit.exe 93BDD93F; release built on moon in the TRAIN41 mirror with pinned pack62 core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE, 583 s, schema and topology checks passed; copy-installed on the box after a sha256 match and a job list + agile next smoke; shipped manifest 1764 files). JobPlaced is installed: a node-placed record whose box heartbeat stops now lists as placed, never running, so remote jobs no longer block box installs.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_25 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 25u32, "2026-11-09T03:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 02:1x rig: CALLER INVENTORY for the remote.ps1 job retirement: only i574n.github node-proof.ps1:148 (remote.ps1 $JobMachine job [-RequireCore] start ...) plus guidance in docs/agents/agent-sync.md lines 213, 222, 248; no other repo calls remote.ps1 job. kit job start --on now resolves every routable alias: .bin files exist for ganymede, wifi, wifi-ts, wifi-ip, laptop, vultr, comet (wifi-ts and wifi-ip derived tonight from the registry kit field, both smoke-listed moon); a node.bin was derived too but archived, because node is a registry name and not an ssh alias (ssh: Could not resolve hostname node). TWO GAPS before node-proof can switch: (1) remote.ps1 maps registry name to sshAlias, kit --on takes the ssh alias, so node-proof must pass the alias (KIT-NET-TOPOLOGY M2 would let kit read the registry); (2) -RequireCore: remote.ps1 refuses a node whose compiler core differs, kit --on has no core check; add --require-core <hash> to job start --on, checked on the far side before the job is created. Next step: (2) as a typed refusal (exit 3 incomplete per the taxonomy), then switch node-proof and the doc lines in one change.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s4_26 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S4", 26u32, "2026-11-09T03:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 02:2x rig, refined plan for gap (2): do NOT port the core guard into kit. remote.ps1 Assert-NodeCore dot-sources the node Spiral env.ps1 and applies the det-root equivalence rule (L6); porting it is far past 45 minutes. Instead node-proof splits the step: remote.ps1 <machine> verify -RequireCore <hash> keeps the guard, then kit job start --on <sshAlias> creates the job, so the box holds a local record and kit job wait/tail work without ssh. Also carry over what remote.ps1 job adds today: it sets KIT_JOB_SLOTS from the registry slots field; with kit --on the host must have its jobs-root slots file (ganymede and comet need one written). node-proof is org tooling every lane uses, so the switch lands in a quiet window agreed with org, not mid-run. Next step: write the slots files where the registry has slots, then propose the node-proof diff to org.")
inl remote_exec_s5 () = Task ("REMOTE-EXEC-S5", "M4 remote jobs refuse on a source-tree mismatch, and live-tree writers stay local", TaskKind, P0, D3, 30u32, Planned, "DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", "kit,team:rig,remote,node,coordinator", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_remote_exec_s5 () = Planning ("REMOTE-EXEC-S5", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_remote_exec_s5_1 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S5", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:43Z", "kit", "11-01 08:4x kit, slice of EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR (main 08:4x: slice it like SCRUM-XP; milestones M2-M5 from the 10-25 note, M1 shipped in TRAIN4c). DoD: a remote job whose src slice manifest differs from the box's is refused before it starts (test with two fixture trees); a job declared as writing the live tree is never placed remote even with equal hashes (test). NEXT STEP: compare manifests from KIT-REMOTE-SYNC's deterministic bundle (eoie_bundle_manifest) inside the S2 dispatch. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: manifest as a set of (path nominal, sha256 nominal) compared as sets; write_scope = ReadsTreeOnly | WritesLiveTree (closed union declared by the job), so the live-tree rule is a pattern.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s5_2 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S5", 2u32, "2026-11-04T12:29Z", "kit", "11-04 09:5x kit: the DECISION is modelled (unstaged) in kit_coordinator_placement (S7's package). tree_need gains WritesLiveTree (placed only on the local machine, even when a remote one holds a tree) and ReadsSlice digest (local, or a remote whose machine_sample.slice equals the digest; machine_sample gains `slice : string`, \"\" from sample_of). New test a_remote_slice_must_match_and_live_tree_writers_stay_local: same slice -> the idle node; a stale slice is never used (local instead, or QueueUntilFree when local is full); writers stay local. europa check queued. REMAINING for the DoD: the digest itself (the box's src slice manifest via kit_mirror's walker + the remote's, answered by `kit mirror check` on the remote after TRAIN22) and the refusal line in kit_job_dispatch before ssh.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s5_3 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S5", 3u32, "2026-11-06T08:20Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 04:1x kit groom: parked Active to Planned, untouched since 11-04 (over 24 h; WIP cap: Active means touched within 48 h, and kit held 42 Active). Progress kept. Resume order unchanged; the next installable train (TRAIN33, link lost, result unread) carries no change to this item unless its last note says so.")
inl note_of_remote_exec_s5_4 () = Note ("REMOTE-EXEC-S5", 4u32, "2026-11-07T17:23Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit (user: generic delegation, any job to nodes with minimal friction; compiler asked): why compiler packs never built on the node: the node had the .NET 11 runtime but only 9.x SDKs. Installed SDK 11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 (the box version) into C:/Program Files/dotnet on the node as a node job (job-1794071797706); a net11.0 console builds. Compiler can build and review candidates on the node today through node-proof.ps1 (working-tree sync incl. unstaged, {mirror}/{stage} placeholders). This item (S5: refuse on tree or core mismatch, live-tree writers stay local) is the step that makes automatic sync safe for any job type; S11 and S12 then prove the two-machine queue. Friction list sent to compiler: full-tree resync per probe, GNU tar under Bash, node stage dirs filling disk, Cargo.lock locked on new crates, results only by tail plus scp, stale pins.")
