inl diamond_s2 () = Task ("DIAMOND-S2", "Mechanical feed: census, lint and crate gate facts become obligations, deterministically", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "DIAMOND-S1,TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT,GRANULAR-STATS", "kit,team:rig,gauge,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_diamond_s2 () = Planning ("DIAMOND-S2", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_diamond_s2_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S2", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: 'kit gauge src --mechanical' on kit prints per-package open mechanical obligations equal to the census and lint baselines (cross-check test on a fixture tree); two runs byte-identical. NEXT STEP: adapters from kit_style_census rows and kit_lint_model violations into obligations. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: census_fact = typed census row (package, metric union, count); each metric maps to an obligation family by a total match.")
inl note_of_diamond_s2_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S2", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:11Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit, refined: the mechanical feed reads model_metrics' 11 metrics through TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT's kit verb (compiler tokens, not regex: fiscal showed the regex version reads 0 definitions in generated units) and GRANULAR-STATS' columns (cell budget 280, host-macro bytes), so it now depends on both. Distance for M3/M5/M11 = gap to the mega samples' values (86.7 / 30.8 / 36.4 on 11-01); M7 string dispatch and M8 sentinels count absolutely (target 0). DoD addition: the mechanical scorecard for fiscal reproduces fiscal's 11-01 numbers (1.6 / 0 / 11.6, M7 6.5, M8 4.1) from the same tree.")
inl note_of_diamond_s2_3 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S2", 3u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit: Mechanical feeders now: GRANULAR-STATS (host-text drift, cell budget) and KIT-REUSE-METRICS (dup_ratio, lib_share, reuse_fanout). S2 consumes their rows, it does not re-walk the tree.")
inl diamond_s3 () = Task ("DIAMOND-S3", "Verdict ledger: adjudicated evidence keyed by unit hash + rubric version + model, replayable", TaskKind, P1, D3, 90u32, Blocked, "DIAMOND-S1", "kit,team:rig,gauge,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_diamond_s3 () = Planning ("DIAMOND-S3", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_diamond_s3_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: a ledger of typed verdict rows; replaying a score with the ledger and an unchanged tree gives identical output; changing one unit's content invalidates only that unit's verdicts (test); a rubric version bump invalidates all verdicts of that rubric (test). NEXT STEP: package kit_gauge_ledger with verdict rows in a '///- --no-respell' state module (agile-state style). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: verdict = { unit : unit_id; rubric : rubric_id * version nominal; model : model_id; answer : answer union per rubric }; answers are closed unions per rubric question (e.g. Beam | Native | EitherWithReason of reason), never free text.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 2u32, "2026-11-04T01:43Z", "kit", "11-03 21:4x kit: typed model DRAFTED in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S3\\src\\kit_gauge_ledger (not in the tree: an unproven test file would run in the next train's notebooks). Nominal ids rubric_id, rubric_version, model_id and content_hash as single-case unions over kit_gauge_model.unit_id. backend_answer is a closed union (Beam | Native | EitherWithReason : string), never free text. verdict is a record; verdict_standing is VerdictCurrent | VerdictStale. current_verdicts tree rubric version ledger keeps a verdict only when its unit's content hash is unchanged and its rubric version is current. Two tests encode the DoD: a content change stales only that unit; a rubric bump stales every verdict of that rubric and none of another's. LEFT: the '///- --no-respell' state module the ledger rows persist in (agile-state style), and a replay test (same ledger + unchanged tree -> identical score output). Prove on scratch (europa --check plus a Cells run) before landing. Record field renamed unit -> target (unit may be reserved).")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_3 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 3u32, "2026-11-04T07:58Z", "kit", "11-04 04:2x kit: kit_gauge_ledger LANDED in the tree (unstaged; module package, no crate; europa pack31 --check exit 0 as-is and all test bodies). Three tests cover the DoD: a content change invalidates only that unit's verdicts; a rubric version bump invalidates every verdict of that rubric (other rubrics stand); and replaying an unchanged tree with the ledger gives identical verdicts. Typed throughout: rubric_id/rubric_version/model_id/content_hash single-case unions, backend_answer closed union, verdict record, verdict_standing union. Remaining for Done: persistence of verdict rows as a state module (agile-state style) once the gauge verb (DIAMOND-S6, parked for size) has a home. Rides TRAIN21 notebooks.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_4 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 4u32, "2026-11-04T08:07Z", "kit", "11-04 05:0x kit: PERSISTENCE as a typed state module (unstaged). ledger.spi gains verdict_of (a full constructor: target, hash, rubric, version, model, answer) and ledger_source, which renders a ledger as Spiral source: `///- --no-respell`, `:< kit_gauge_ledger.ledger`, `:= ledger () : list verdict = [ verdict_of ... ]`, with strings escaped and EitherWithReason payloads quoted. Test the_ledger_persists_as_a_typed_state_module pins the exact text (escaped quotes included) and that a persisted row rebuilds an equal verdict. The rendered text was itself checked as a real module (kit_gauge_state/verdicts.spi on europa pack31: exit 0), so a program loads the ledger by compiling it, as agile.spi works. All DoD tests pass --check (as-is and bodies). Remaining for Done: the verb that writes state/verdicts.spi, which comes with the gauge verb's home (DIAMOND-S6, waiting on fiscal's split-or-program choice).")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_5 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 5u32, "2026-11-04T08:10Z", "kit", "11-04 05:2x kit: the answer is now a per-rubric union, verdict_answer = BackendAnswer backend_answer | XsdReading xsd_reading, where xsd_reading is {complete : bool; wildcards; modeled; declared : i32} (the row shape fiscal asked for: per schema set, keyed by unit hash + rubric version). The persistence test pins both shapes (booleans render as !+/!-), and a sample state module with an XsdReading row passes --check on europa. Remaining: the verb that appends a verdict row to state/verdicts.spi from a calibration run's output (fiscal's program on europa then hands kit the reading).")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_6 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 04:10 fiscal: will hand kit one XsdReading { complete; wildcards; modeled; declared } per schema set when the append verb lands, from the europa calibration program over lib xsd_census (the 11-03 run's readings are on DIAMOND-S6: NF-e, Chile DTE, myDATA, SAF-T and CII D16B complete; UBL 15 wildcards, all in signature/extension parts). Key: unit hash + rubric version + model, as kit's ledger defines.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_7 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 7u32, "2026-11-04T08:11Z", "kit", "11-04 05:3x kit: ledger_recorded (pure, latest wins): recording a verdict drops any earlier verdict for the same target + rubric + model and appends the new one last, while other rubrics keep their slots. Test recording_a_verdict_replaces_that_units_rubric_slot. europa --check exit 0 as-is and bodies. The append verb is then: read state/verdicts.spi's ledger (compile, or keep a sibling typed row list), ledger_recorded, ledger_source, write. That last I/O step waits for a caller; fiscal's calibration program is the first.")
