inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_3 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 3u32, "2026-11-04T11:38Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:38 x: PRECONDITION PROBE (claimed by x via the gate; this is main's item). The old runner exists ONLY on the box: dotnet tool list -g shows microsoft.dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001 and dotnet-repl 0.3.259 on the box; the NODE has neither (and x's node-first rule wants the bench there). spiral has no dib driver scripts left; the only .dib files are polyglot\\deps\\dotnet-interactive samples (27), not Spiral notebooks. So before the DoD's 3x2x5 runs: (1) install dotnet-interactive + dotnet-repl on the node (dotnet tool install -g, versions pinned to the box's 1.0.712001 / 0.3.259); (2) recreate the dib side of each of the 3 notebooks (small, lib physics, x client) as .dib run by 'dotnet repl --run <nb>.dib --exit-after-run' (the old invocation), with the same cells as the Cells notebooks; (3) the in-job A/A per runner. Releasing; next step owner main (or x on request).")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_4 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 4u32, "2026-11-04T11:45Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:45 x: PRECONDITION (1) TRIED and BLOCKED, the cause measured: 'dotnet tool install -g' of microsoft.dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001 and dotnet-repl 0.3.259 on the node both fail ('failed to install'). The node has only SDK 9.0.200 and runtimes 9.0.0-rc.2 / 9.0.2 / 11.0.0-rc.1, while the box carries 3.1, 6, 7.0.x, 8.0.x, 9, 10 and 11, and these old tool builds target an older runtime than the node has. So before the bench runs on the node: install the .NET 8 runtime there (or pick tool versions built for net9), then retry. Not done further by x: kit's claim guard marks this item declined-by-x for now; main owns the next step.")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_5 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 5u32, "2026-11-07T11:07Z", "x", "2026-11-07 07:07 x: GROOMED (user 11-07 via main: benchmarks on codespaces). This 360-min item overlaps compiler's CELLS-SCALING-BENCH. Both now share x's harness CELLS-BENCH-CODESPACE (120), and the questions split into x children CELLS-BENCH-PARALLEL (parallelism and CPU spread vs dib) and CELLS-BENCH-MEMO-LAYERS (memo layers, including single-flight/hopac and crate reuse). This item keeps the erl-vs-dotnet comparison on the old dib path, run on the same codespace harness, since the node can't install the old tool builds (n4).")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_6 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 6u32, "2026-11-08T17:47Z", "i574n", "USER 11-08 13:5x via tibia: 'schedule the dib cells bench somehow, that'll be installation bloat, gotta parallelize also, we can't rehearse it because it takes too long and there's the disk space issue'. The EPYC 9255 rental (RENT-REHEARSAL-EPYC9255, 11-08 ~14:45 local) removes the disk and install blockers (n4: the node can't install the old tool builds). DECISION 13:1x: the rental runs the INSTALLATION half only: install wall time and disk for .NET 8 + dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001 + dotnet-repl 0.3.259 (du of ~/.dotnet ~/.nuget), plus a cold/warm one-cell smoke on each runner (F# cell via dotnet repl; one trivial Spiral cell via Cells) as the VM-startup floor. Why not the full bench: a .dib of SPIRAL cells needs the old Spiral dotnet-interactive kernel extension (#!spiral), which no longer exists in spiral (n3). NEXT (i574n, before the next rental): find the polyglot Nov-2025 Spiral kernel (the CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT checkout), make it installable on Linux, write the 3 .dib (small, lib physics, x client) with the same cells as the Cells notebooks; then tibia's design runs: 3 notebooks x 2 runners x 5 reps in core-pinned matched pairs (taskset, disjoint core sets, symmetric contention) plus an A/A pair.")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_7 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 7u32, "2026-11-08T17:48Z", "i574n", "KERNEL LOCATED (i574n 11-08 13:5x). The dib-era 'spiral' kernel is NOT an extension: it lives in polyglot's PATCHED FORKS. (1) polyglot/deps/dotnet-interactive (fork of dotnet/interactive, last commit e65cb067 2026-09-27): src/dotnet-interactive/KernelBuilder.cs:56-59 registers new SpiralKernel() under the names spiral/Spiral (namespace Microsoft.DotNet.Interactive.Spiral; KernelExtensions.cs:319 UseNugetDirective for it). (2) polyglot/deps/dotnet-repl (fork, f8a86d0 2026-10-02): NotebookRunner.cs, CommandLineParser.cs and InteractiveDocumentExtensions.cs are patched for spiral. (3) The F# eval layer apps/spiral/Eval.fs + Eval.dib (1,311 lines; SignalR HubConnection to the Spiral compiler server, the Supervisor) and 17 .dib notebooks (lib/fsharp/*.dib, apps/spiral/Eval.dib, Supervisor.dib, scripts/init.dib) were DELETED in polyglot b8cb8392 (2026-10-06); take them from b8cb8392^. So the box's 'dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001 / dotnet-repl 0.3.259' are most likely these forks built locally, which is why a stock 'dotnet tool install' on the node can't reproduce them. The 'installation bloat' the user means = building both forks from source (.NET 8/9 SDK, a large repo) plus restoring Eval and the server. NEXT for the next rental: (a) build both forks on Linux from polyglot/deps (time + disk logged); (b) restore Eval.fs/Supervisor from b8cb8392^; (c) write the 3 .dib (small, lib physics, x client) with '#!meta defaultKernelName spiral' and the same cells as the Cells notebooks; then tibia's 3x2x5 core-pinned matched pairs + A/A. This rental (b-option) logs stock-tool install cost and a one-cell F# floor only.")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_8 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 8u32, "2026-11-08T19:30Z", "org2", "11-08 15:5x: the user SHELVED the CPU rental ('forget the cpu rental for now, we might go straight for gpu outside of europa later'); RENT-REHEARSAL-ENCKE is Paused. So this bench no longer waits for a rental. Its home is the codespace harness (CELLS-BENCH-CODESPACE): a codespace has the disk to build polyglot's two forks (deps/dotnet-interactive with SpiralKernel, deps/dotnet-repl) and run 3 notebooks x 2 runners x 5 reps with an in-job A/A, using tibia's core-pinned matched-pair design where cores allow. Prerequisites unchanged (note 7): restore Eval.fs/Supervisor from polyglot b8cb8392^, write the 3 .dib.")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_9 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 9u32, "2026-11-09T03:34Z", "microblog", "FINDING 11-09 (autonomous run): the dib side needs a Spiral kernel for dotnet-interactive, and the ONLY one is in polyglot's fork: polyglot/deps/dotnet-interactive/src/Microsoft.DotNet.Interactive.Spiral (Microsoft.DotNet.Interactive.Spiral.fsproj). spiral has none (only Cells' dib renderers and tests mention it). polyglot is slated for salvage-then-delete (org), so asked org to keep the kernel buildable in the salvage (kernel project + fork commit + the box's pinned tool versions dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001 / dotnet-repl 0.3.259). BLOCKER: the dib half of the bench until that salvage location exists. The Cells half and the comet bootstrap (codespace-spiral-setup.sh) do not depend on it.")
inl note_of_erl_vs_dib_bench_10 () = Note ("ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH", 10u32, "2026-11-09T05:03Z", "org", "DIB KERNEL REBUILD RECIPE (org salvage 2026-11-09): the only Spiral dib kernel lived in polyglot's fork. Rebuild = re-clone github.com/fc1943s/polyglot @ 053c128d (the WHOLE fork tool: the kernel opens Polyglot.Common + attaches to the fork's own dotnet-interactive build, so the kernel project alone is NOT buildable). Kernel at deps/dotnet-interactive/src/Microsoft.DotNet.Interactive.Spiral. Pinned global tools dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001, dotnet-repl 0.3.259. fc1943s is the frozen i574n backup remote; 053c128d on github-fc1943s/main-i574n (ls-remote confirmed). A redundant source-only copy sits at C:/home/data/archive/polyglot-spiral-dib-kernel (NOT buildable alone; C:/home/data is non-sanctioned drift per the Write hook). See memory polyglot-spiral-dib-kernel-salvage.")
inl perf_framework_study () = Task ("PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY", "Study every benchmarking approach we have, pre-vibecode (polyglot Perf, spiral perf notebooks) and since (compiler bench-pair and matrix, lib benchmark.spi, Cells phases_ms, kit bench, model_metrics, rebar plans), extract the best techniques, and design one benchmarking framework in Spiral", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "PERF-STUDY-1-INVENTORY,PERF-STUDY-2-TABLE,PERF-STUDY-3-DESIGN,PERF-STUDY-4-PORT,PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", "benchmark,perf,lib,kit,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_perf_framework_study () = Planning ("PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_perf_framework_study_1 () = Note ("PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:34Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user: 'we haven't even started exploring this edge yet. sad that we don't have cpus to iterate over and over here'). DoD: a comparison table (technique, where it lives, what it gets right: warmup, A/A, interleaving, quiet-core sampling, outlier policy, typed results) on this item; a framework design (API + typed result model) reviewed against it; one existing benchmark ported as proof. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a measurement as a GADT indexed by its unit; a benchmark as a record of setup/run/teardown with phantom-typed inputs; results as typed rows the exporter renders. NEXT STEP: locate the pre-vibecode polyglot Perf and spiral perf notebooks in git history (git log --all -- '*erf*').")
inl note_of_perf_framework_study_2 () = Note ("PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY", 2u32, "2026-11-09T12:47Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:5x PERF-STUDY-1 INVENTORY (paths, what each measures): SPIRAL: lib/spiral/benchmark.spi (the lib benchmarking module), lib/spiral/bench/parsing (bench_kit.spi + fparsec/pure_split arms + bench.ps1: parser throughput), apps/compiler/scripts/bench-pair.ps1 (compiler A/B pair timing), bench-native.ps1 (native backend run times), bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1 (Cells vs the sample matrix wall time), apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 + Cells notebook.ex phases_ms (per-phase compile/run timings per test), ci_gate.ps1 / lib_sweep.ps1 (gate timings), apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench*.ps1 + bench_backtrack/bench_derivative (fsx/spi/zig per-backend regex arms); KIT: infra/nodebench (Rust node benchmark + rate.ps1, the 0-1000 node rating), state/bench.spi (kit bench verb state); REGEX: bench/bench.spi (10 arms x 6 workloads, rotated arms, A/A band, 15 rounds x 25 passes, setup row, staged emitter); FISCAL: bench/acbr (Pascal ACBr), bench/dfe-net (C# DFe.NET), compare-roundtrip.ps1 (cross-library NF-e round trip); TIBIA: docs/BENCHMARK.md; I574N.GITHUB: examples/perf/Perf.spi (the pre-vibecode polyglot Perf port); RECOVERED (stroma, user review pending): bench_execution_gate, bench_promotion_decision, inference_benchmark_matrix, heldout_suite_bench. Next (PERF-STUDY-2): read each one's timing loop into the comparison table.")
inl note_of_perf_framework_study_3 () = Note ("PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY", 3u32, "2026-11-09T12:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 09:0x PERF-STUDY-2 COMPARISON TABLE (technique per approach, from reading the timing loops): REGEX BENCH (regex/bench/bench.spi): A/A YES (MinimalAgainArm; median ratio outside 0.95-1.05 turns every row of that table into a VOID verdict), interleaving YES (arms rotated every round), stats median + IQR of per-round ratios to a baseline arm, rounds 15 x 25 passes, typed results YES (sample / spread / time_verdict unions), warmup and outlier policy NO, quiet-core NO. COMPILER BENCH-PAIR (apps/compiler/scripts/bench-pair.ps1): interleaving YES (alternating A/B order per round), fresh process per compile, quiet-core YES (-QuietCores samples busy cores at each measurement and recomputes medians over quiet rounds only), stats median, A/A NO, typed NO (PS objects). LIB benchmark.spi: gc_collect before, then the N runs go through am'.parallel_map and only the TOTAL ms is kept, so it measures parallel throughput, not per-iteration latency; typed record test_case_result; no warmup, A/A, interleave, quiet or stats. LIB bench/parsing (bench_kit.spi + bench.ps1): repeated rounds, arms per parser, no A/A or quiet. CELLS model_metrics / phases_ms: typed per-phase timings per test (observability, not A/B). KIT nodebench + rate.ps1: one composite score per node, log-relative 0-1000 rating, outlier-aware rating only. POLYGLOT Perf.spi: interleaved arms, nothing else. FISCAL compare-roundtrip.ps1: cross-library round trip, correctness-first with times. BEST OF EACH for the design: regex's A/A band with VOID verdicts + rotation + median/IQR as typed unions; bench-pair's quiet-core gating + fresh process + alternating order. GAPS EVERYWHERE: an explicit warmup policy, an outlier policy (e.g. MAD), and recording the machine state (load, governor) WITH each sample. Next (PERF-STUDY-3): the typed design from these rows.")
inl note_of_perf_framework_study_4 () = Note ("PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY", 4u32, "2026-11-09T16:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:0x RE-ESTIMATED (gate: over 240 m): children 1-4 are Done (inventory, table, the bench_model design landed in lib, tibia's regex port); PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM (typed print unit, in proof on ganymede) is now a dep too. What is left on this parent is the closing review once 5 lands: 30 m. Next step: close when PERF-STUDY-5 is Done, citing each child's proof.")
inl blender_sample () = Task ("BLENDER-SAMPLE", "A minimal Spiral sample that drives Blender (revisiting the old polyglot Blender experiment) using the typefeatureset, rendered headless in GitHub Actions, with the image linked from dir-tree-html; the WGSL runner already works in GH", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "samples,blender,ci,gpu,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_blender_sample () = Planning ("BLENDER-SAMPLE", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_blender_sample_1 () = Note ("BLENDER-SAMPLE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:34Z", "main", "main 10:3x. DoD: a sample in spiral compiles to Python for Blender's bpy, a workflow step renders one image headless (blender -b), and the image is published as an artifact linked from dir-tree-html. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: scene objects as a GADT indexed by object kind (mesh/light/camera) so only valid properties apply; transforms with phantom coordinate spaces. NEXT STEP: find the polyglot Blender experiment in git history and check that a headless Blender install fits the Ubuntu runner time budget.")
inl note_of_blender_sample_2 () = Note ("BLENDER-SAMPLE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:26Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: 360m niche GPU/CI sample, over the light-round budget, and it REVISITS the old polyglot Blender experiment - but polyglot is HELD (deletion deferred until microblog confirms the dib-kernel salvage, memory polyglot-spiral-dib-kernel-salvage), so the source experiment is in a repo that is not to be churned yet. Also needs a headless-blender-fits-the-runner-budget check (CI). Parking on item:POLYGLOT-SPIRAL-DIB-KERNEL-SALVAGE (the Blender source lives in polyglot, whose status must settle first); re-pull when polyglot is resolved + the item is split to <=120m.")
inl package_model_standard () = Task ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", "Decide one packaging model for every repo by experiment: one manifest with many folders, one manifest per folder, or a main per .spi file (the compiler already takes main from each file), weighing Cells ergonomics and script-like execution (KIT-RUN-SPI); then a per-lane migration list for every repo that doesn't follow it", Story, P1, D4, 70u32, Active, "LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION,SPIPROJ-RETIRE", "packages,manifest,edition3,kit,main,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_package_model_standard () = Planning ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_package_model_standard_1 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:34Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user 11-01). DoD: three small repos-in-miniature, one per model, each running a test, a script-like main and a Cells notebook; a scored table (lines of config, rebuild time on one change, tooling paths that break); the decision written here; then one migration item per lane naming its repo's changes. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the package model as a union (SingleManifest of folder list | PerFolder | PerFile) in the manifest schema, so tools branch on a type, not on probing paths. NEXT STEP: census each repo's current style (spiproj and spiral.toml locations, how many folders per manifest).")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_2 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:04Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:2x, from the S0 study subagent's execution packet (aaf2a6f472dc70094). TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 is the candidate answer. The SingleManifest | PerFolder | PerFile union gains a fourth reading: linked units (a package is a unit; other units come in through link:, COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS). SPIPROJ-RETIRE settles the manifest file: spiral.toml only.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_3 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 3u32, "2026-11-04T08:56Z", "tibia", "11-04 05:0x tibia, INVENTORY FOR THE TIBIA STEP (after lib went prelude-only at 04:49): tibia has 9 packages (src, results, apps/arena, canary, host, map, offscreen, predict, suite), and each holds BOTH a package.spiproj and a spiral.toml whose modules list duplicates it (e.g. src: packageDir ../deps/spiral/lib, packages |core- spiral-, 21 modules in define-before-use order). RISK to settle in the standard before tibia moves: tibia/src also holds standalone programs that are deliberately NOT package modules (hunt_sim, gpu_sim, pack_sim; --check answers 'not declared in package', and build.ps1 compiles them by name under its long-gpu label). If prelude-only derives the module set from every .spi file present, those programs become package modules, which changes what Cells notebooks and consumer3 build. So the tibia step needs either an exclude list in the toml or the programs moved to their own app folder first. tibia will do the move after the standard says which; nothing changed in tibia yet.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_4 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 4u32, "2026-11-04T14:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:47 fiscal: INVENTORY FOR THE FISCAL STEP (input to the per-lane migration list; no change made). fiscal has 83 package.spiproj and 1 spiral.toml outside deps/target: (1) src/ -- BOTH package.spiproj and spiral.toml (edition 3, packageDir ../deps/spiral/lib, packages |core- spiral-, 16 modules in define-before-use order), the same duplication tibia reported; (2) generated/ -- 82 generated units, each its own one-module package.spiproj WRITTEN by the generator (src/generator.spi write_generated_module_with -> module_package dependencies module_name), listing its sibling-unit dependencies as packages ('../generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1-'); a generator test reads one back (the CFDI unit lists its complement units). So fiscal's migration is two steps: src to prelude-only spiral.toml (mechanical, like lib), and the generator's emitted manifest format (module_package) to whatever the chosen model is -- a one-function change plus one test, re-proven by a full regen identity run (all units, diff vs reference) on europa. README.md:145 documents the one-module-package-per-unit layout ('so a test cell type-checks only its own module'), which any model must keep.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_5 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 5u32, "2026-11-06T16:31Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:3x DECIDED (rule: follow what the repos already converged on and what EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL shipped, not a new experiment): ONE spiral.toml PER PACKAGE FOLDER, prelude-only (the compiler derives modules from the folder's .spi files), plus an explicit exclude list for standalone programs that must not become package modules (tibia's hunt_sim/gpu_sim/pack_sim case; the exclude field must exist in the manifest model before tibia relies on it). Per-file main stays available for script-like runs (KIT-RUN-SPI, installed with TRAIN33). MIGRATION LIST from tracked files (git ls-files, 11-06): DONE fiscal (84 toml, 0 spiproj), tibia (9 toml, 0 spiproj), spiral lib (spiral.toml only); x: 2 folders carry both (drop the spiproj); small repos, mechanical, owner main: regex 2, html 8 (linked units: check spiral.toml supports link: first), dice 2, alphabet 2, blog 1, i574n.github 4; kit 596 (generated crates, so kit's generator emits the manifest, like fiscal's generator change); spiral apps/compiler 1290 (test samples; compiler's call, since the harness reads them) plus apps 10. Next step: verify spiral.toml carries link: and an exclude field, then convert blog (1) as the pilot.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_6 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 6u32, "2026-11-06T16:43Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:5x PILOT DONE: regex (unstaged): src/ and bench/ package.spiproj -> spiral.toml (edition 3, same packageDir/packages, modules as a ''' block in the same order; old files backed up in the main scratchpad). PROOF: bench.rs generated by pack55d is byte-identical before and after the swap (B099B5E930A3, 275,255 B), and the Cells gate of src/charset.spi under the toml manifest passes 6/6. spiral.toml already supports link and an explicit modules list (compiler config fields: modules, packageDir, packages, link, edition, ...), so no exclude field is needed: a folder with standalone programs lists its modules explicitly (tibia does). Next: html (8, link: units), dice 2, alphabet 2, i574n.github 4, x's 2 doubles; blog waits, since the fork's post.ps1 reads blog's package.spiproj by text anchors.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_7 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 7u32, "2026-11-06T16:57Z", "main", "main 11-06 17:0x html CONVERTED (unstaged): all 9 package.spiproj -> spiral.toml (cli, html_model, html_inline, html_table, html_parse, html_render, html_pages, html_walk, markdown) via a converter in main's scratchpad (spiproj-to-toml.ps1; its regex output equals the hand-proven regex toml; arrays over 100 chars go one item per line, which tomlManifestText reads). PROOF: pack55d regenerates all 9 crates byte-identical before and after (0 of 9 differ; the link: units included), no html script reads package.spiproj, and old files are backed up in the scratchpad. The HTML-README-ANY-CASE Linux proof still holds, since the generated Rust is identical. Done so far: lib, fiscal, tibia, regex, html. Next: dice 2, alphabet 2, i574n.github 4, x's 2 doubles.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_8 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 8u32, "2026-11-06T17:11Z", "main", "main 11-06 17:2x dice CONVERTED (unstaged): root package.spiproj (lib/ + contract/ module tree) and ui/package.spiproj (nested src/ tree) -> spiral.toml with the hierarchy kept as an indented ''' block. PROOF: pack55d Rust for lib/dice.spi (497,695 B), contract/dice_contract.spi (130,533 B) and ui/src/dice_ui.spi (1,782,769 B) is byte-identical before and after (C32ADF070402, F0A1A6A44C27, F3115B16A3E8). Done: lib, fiscal, tibia, regex, html, dice. Next: alphabet 2, i574n.github 4; x's 2 doubles go to x.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_9 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 9u32, "2026-11-06T17:43Z", "main", "main 11-06 17:4x i574n.github: apps/graphs and scripts/pins CONVERTED and proven (pack55d Rust byte-identical: graphs 643,877 B 57AB3AAAF588, pins workflows 183,788 B 66C629571D80). CONVERTER BUG found and fixed first: it added 'edition = 3' even when the spiproj already had 'edition: 3', giving a duplicate key, so graphs and pins failed to compile on the first try; all five trial conversions were restored from backup before the fix, and only these two are kept. NOT converted (proof inconclusive): alphabet apps/documents (fails to compile on the box BEFORE the swap: fiscal's live xpath_eval land breaks it, sent to fiscal), alphabet apps/hangul and examples/scheduler (no main; --check attestation timed out under the box load). docs/backlog/state/package.spiproj is kit's (agile state) and is left to kit. Done: lib, fiscal, tibia, regex, html, dice, i574n.github graphs + pins.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_10 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 10u32, "2026-11-06T17:57Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:5x: the alphabet documents/hangul revert at 13:4x was for a FALSE red (my bad bisect; see the retraction on PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS). Re-running their byte-identical manifest proof against the live tree now.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_11 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 11u32, "2026-11-06T18:36Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:2x alphabet apps/documents CONVERTED to spiral.toml and proven: single-flight --backend Rust gave byte-identical output before and after (207D03252B07, 946405 B), with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR set and run from the app dir. The 13:4x red was my environment: without the package dir the lib loads twice, so you get 'Got T / Expected T' errors on identical types. No lib land was involved. hangul and examples/scheduler: --check printed only 'Attestation timed out' both times, so that proof is VOID; they stay package.spiproj (auto-reverted) and are being re-proven in Rust mode. Unstaged.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_12 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 12u32, "2026-11-06T19:01Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:5x alphabet apps/hangul and i574n.github examples/scheduler CONVERTED to spiral.toml and proven. Neither package defines main, so a --backend Rust compile emits only the prelude, and both gave the same 33920 B (CA5435AE6228), which is VOID as a comparison. Default --check (30 s budget) timed out on attestation. Proof used: --check --timeout-ms 600000 with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR set, run from each app dir. Each printed a real 'checked package <dir>' result, identical before and after the swap (hangul 25734D114EAD, scheduler 1959BD80EE1D). Unstaged. Conversions done today: alphabet documents/hangul, i574n.github graphs/pins/scheduler. Left: x's 2 doubles (x), kit's 596, compiler samples 1290, backlog state (kit).")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_13 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 13u32, "2026-11-06T21:55Z", "main", "main 11-06 17:5x MANIFEST COUNT (tracked package.spiproj still on disk / spiral.toml, deps excluded): spiral 1304 / 5 (compiler samples 1290 + apps), kit 596 / 0, x 2 / 2, fiscal 0 / 84, tibia 0 / 9, regex 0 / 2, html 0 / 9, dice 0 / 2, alphabet 0 / 2, blog 1 / 0, i574n.github 1 / 3 (the 1 is docs/backlog/state, kit's). Main's last one is blog's root package.spiproj: HELD because the fork's scripts/post.ps1 (34-39) reads it and patches it by text anchors to inject each post. The conversion must change post.ps1's anchor logic in the same change and re-prove both on a codespace (blog then fork push order). Next step for main: that blog+fork pair as one codespace-proven change. Owners: kit 596 + backlog state, compiler 1290 samples + apps, x 2.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_14 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 14u32, "2026-11-07T20:03Z", "main", "main 11-07 16:1x blog CONVERTED (unstaged), proof pending:\n- blog: package.spiproj deleted (backup: main scratchpad blog-package.spiproj.before) and spiral.toml added with the same packageDir, packages and module groups.\n- the fork's scripts/post.ps1 (spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language) now reads spiral.toml with TOML anchors `packageDir = '../spiral/lib'` and \"\\nposts/\\n\" (groups at column 0), injects the post as a root module before posts/, and writes the overlay spiral.toml.\nChecked locally: post.ps1 parses; both anchors match exactly once on the new toml; the injected manifest is well-formed. Only post.ps1 read blog's package.spiproj.\nPROOF STILL OWED: one codespace run with the box's spiral delta overlaid (it needs the tests-only Cells and pack61b's concat fix), blog's scripts/workflow.ps1 and the fork's post.ps1 on one post. Until then this pair is not push-ready.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_15 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 15u32, "2026-11-07T21:36Z", "main", "main 11-07 17:3x blog CODESPACE REHEARSAL GREEN, proof: origin i574n/spiral 7d9f7a5 + the box spiral delta (256 files, 2 deleted: tests-only Cells, pack61b, today's lib lands) + blog's 12-file delta with package.spiproj DELETED, on nightly-2026-11-05: blog scripts/workflow.ps1 exit 0, every engine notebook passing, 393 s, codespace deleted. In one run this proves the spiral.toml conversion, the 11-05 pin, the tests-only respell and the create_temp_directory fix. Still unproven: the fork's post.ps1 TOML anchors on a real post (checked locally: anchors match once, injected manifest well-formed). PUSH ORDER holds: spiral before blog.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_16 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 16u32, "2026-11-08T00:44Z", "main", "main 11-07 20:4x proof: blog REHEARSAL GREEN AGAIN with the deletion actually applied. The 17:3x run had kept package.spiproj (the CRLF delete-list bug), so it was valid only because Cells reads spiral.toml first. This run: 13 files + 1 deletion, git sees 14 changed; workflow exit 0, every engine notebook passing. So blog with ONLY spiral.toml is proven under CI conditions.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_17 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 17u32, "2026-11-09T15:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:4x OWN DRIFT HEALED: the two packages org2 created today used the retired package.spiproj, against this item's 11-06 decision (one spiral.toml per package folder): spiral/apps/registry (registry_model, registry_planner, registry_unit) and spiral/apps/plot (physics, from PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB). Both converted to spiral.toml with the same packageDir/packages/modules (form copied from html/html_model); old files backed up in drafts\\spiral\\PACKAGE-MODEL-OWN-DRIFT; nothing references the old filenames. Proof: Cells gates of physics, registry_planner and registry_unit under the toml manifests (ganymede job org2-toml; before: physics 43/43, registry_planner 14/14 under spiproj). Lesson for new packages: create spiral.toml, never package.spiproj; worth a kit standards rule (a new tracked package.spiproj outside compiler samples = finding).")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_18 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 18u32, "2026-11-09T16:05Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 16:0x PROOF for the own-drift heal: ganymede job-1794238423491-org2-toml, Cells gates under the new spiral.toml manifests (exact box spiral copy): apps/plot/physics.spi 43/43, apps/registry/registry_planner.spi 14/14, registry_unit.spi 3/3; the same counts as under package.spiproj before. Both packages now follow the standard (one spiral.toml per package folder).")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_19 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 19u32, "2026-11-09T16:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:0x RE-ESTIMATED (gate: over 240 m): the decision (11-06), the pilot and the conversions of lib, fiscal, tibia, regex, html, dice, alphabet, blog and i574n.github are done, plus today's two own-drift packages. What remains are other owners' migrations, now behind dep SPIPROJ-RETIRE: spiral compiler samples (~1290 spiproj, compiler), kit (~596, rig), x (2, microblog), apps/cells/spi (1, microblog). This parent keeps only the closing check (manifest census = 0 spiproj outside the exempt samples): 60 m. Next step: when SPIPROJ-RETIRE is Done, rerun the manifest census and close.")
inl note_of_package_model_standard_20 () = Note ("PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD", 20u32, "2026-11-09T17:00Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: the MODEL IS DECIDED (one spiral.toml per package folder, prelude-only, explicit modules list for standalone-program folders) and the migration is ~70pct DONE (lib, fiscal, tibia, regex, html, dice, alphabet, i574n.github graphs/pins/scheduler, blog unstaged). The REMAINING conversions are all OTHER lanes': kit 596 generated units (rig, via kit's generator emitting the manifest) + spiral apps/compiler 1290 test samples (compiler) + x 2 doubles (microblog). Plus the stated dep LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION. So it is not an over-240m item needing a split - it is decided + mostly done, waiting on the per-owner generator/sample conversions. Parking on item:LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION; the kit/compiler/x remainders are each owner's at their next train.")
