inl note_of_x_sota_model_84 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 84u32, "2026-11-05T09:51Z", "x", "2026-11-05 05:51 x: x-next7c's LAND is WAITING, not failed. Its lib step (date_time ECE2A9DD6806) passed the new round-trip precheck at 05:42, then lib_land_window waits for LIVE READERS: main's notebook gate on apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi (since 04:58, about 2 h of window left) compiles against the live lib. The wait is 30 min, then it throws (about 06:12) with nothing applied. CORRECTION: tonight's earlier land stalls were this same reader wait, not the RAM floor I blamed (main added -MinFreeMb anyway; harmless). Asked main for a gap or a per-file reader check. The levers run waits for this land (overlapping generated Rust).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_85 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 85u32, "2026-11-05T10:09Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:09 x: x-next7 LANDED (green run x-next7c): lib date_time ECE2A9DD6806 via lib_land_window (closed green, document_test 26/26, undo 20261105-055129; it first waited behind main's replay.spi reader); the x files landed, including the join-point fix (simframes 835CC894AF9B, sim_progress 5131B6D893A3), envoy manifests (frames gleam.toml 4811C1FFBCF0, manifest.toml FE8F552066A8), the X-NO-COMMENTS heal (posts 1D3DBF4AE0C2, run_signals, sim_publish, digest, prelude), lambda parens, the heading strip and requests; x/postability/tlds.txt removed (byte-identical to spiral apps/cells/data/tlds.txt). node-proof applied 27 generated outputs; 1 conflict, apps/client/README.md, correctly LEFT at the land's MIGRATE-TXT-FILES draft (F6BA371E172E, the new tlds path); the run's copy was the pre-migration README, because the node mirror never had that draft. x's live tree now has 1 comment line left (timeline_serve.spi:9, which x-next9 replaces). NEXT: x-levers1 LAUNCHED (job-1793873376874, node, pack44 core 657DA4B173F9D3D3): splitter with the long_form fix, plus lever-2 mimalloc.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_86 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 86u32, "2026-11-05T12:14Z", "x", "2026-11-05 08:2x x: SLICE (reflection codecs, the smallest piece): sim invariants' rule names are DERIVED, not hand-mapped (memory nameof-not-string-mapping). invariants.spi drops demand_rule_name and the 6-arm rule_name match (12 lines); rule_name r = reflection::typed_case_name r |> reflection::typed_name_snake, so SequentialEquivalence reads sequential_equivalence and a renamed case renames its finding. The strings are a protocol (runner findings lines, all_held), so a new test rule_names_are_the_snake_case_of_their_cases pins all 6 literally, including breaking_edits_fail, which no test covered before. Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\x\\X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES\\invariants.spi 16705919CAF4 on live 95CD1AC6975C: cell budget 0 findings, round trip canonical + fixpoint + byte-exact, europa --check exit 0 (pack44, live lib reflection.spi). --check does not run UnionCaseName codegen, so the rust + gleam tests ride x-next10 (its gate now runs invariants.spi besides sim_serve.spi; launch and land scripts updated and parse-checked; the dry run refuses only the expected sim_serve base, which x-next9 sets). Model status from the code today: platform prototype DONE (splitter.spi); open: post typestate, command GADT (cli.spi command is a plain union), invariant prototype, executor HKT, reflection codecs beyond names, iggy family.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_87 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 87u32, "2026-11-05T12:44Z", "x", "2026-11-05 09:1x x: GROOM of the target model against today's code, each part re-decided with its evidence. (1) POST TYPESTATE: DROPPED as written. Every post lifecycle in x is runtime-driven: scenario.spi draws edits from seeded randomness over a pool of rooted posts, sim_serve's writes come from requests, and final_state.spi folds a runtime event list (deleted : bool). A post s phantom can only guard code whose sequence is static, which in x is only test fixtures, so it would add ceremony without guarding a real path. The runtime stream stays nested unions (content | revision | reaction), as this item already said. (2) EXECUTOR HKT: MET without an HKT. executors.spi has executor = list string -> task_result, with fake_executor, leaking_executor and cells_executor as values, and runner_shell takes one. The pair-of-records indirection the model wanted gone is gone. An index \\* m. executor m would only add an effect index that every instance leaves unused, since all three are synchronous calls returning task_result. (3) INVARIANT PROTOTYPE: DROPPED in favour of the union plus derived names. The checks have different shapes (sequential_equivalence needs a baseline, commute takes two snapshots, the rest take one), so one ':? check i' signature cannot hold them without wrapping. The rule union already makes the finding list exhaustive, and its names are now derived by reflection (X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES, in x-next10). STILL OPEN: (4) command GADT, blocked: cli's command reaches xc's Rust main as the 15-field parsed_args tuple across a crate link, which is X-TYPED-UNITS' job, and that waits on TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 (Planned 0%); (5) reflection codecs beyond names (wire field lists); (6) iggy event family (LIB-IGGY-CLIENT). DONE: platform prototype (splitter.spi), auth phantom (sim_serve caller c), endpoint reads r / writes r (wire.spi).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_88 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 88u32, "2026-11-05T13:31Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:2x x: GROOM (5) REFLECTION CODECS for wire: DROPPED, like the case-name arms in posts.spi. The wire.spi field lists map EXTERNAL protocol keys, and those differ by platform for the same field: X 'text', 'author_id', 'created_at' (wire.spi:279-298, 353); Mastodon 'content' (402); Bluesky 'createdAt' and app.bsky.feed.post (414-422). A codec derived from record field names would force record names to equal one platform's keys and still need per-platform maps for the others. Reflection stays where the names are x's own: the invariant rule names (X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES, in x-next10). (6) IGGY FAMILY: its dependency moved today. LIB-IGGY-CLIENT's M3 gap (Gleam rd_str_utf8 stub) is drafted (LIB-IGGY-GLEAM-UTF8 92B9E9D4CFB3, rust + gleam round trips plus a NotUtf8 test, in x-next10's lib gates). Once it lands, the sim's event stream can map onto the family. Open now: (4) command GADT (blocked on typed links) and (6) the sim-to-iggy mapping.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_89 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 89u32, "2026-11-05T14:23Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:3x x: CORRECTION, scope of my europa --check claims today. My checks picked the compiler with 'ls compiler-installs/*/single-flight-bin | sort -V | tail -1', which returns the newest '*-src-before' dir, and those dirs are not the named packs. Measured cores: pack44-src-before ea36ca047fa29828, pack48-src-before 96df7d2a78a2469e, pack49-src-before dc49ffdc170199df (= europa's installed core). None equals the box or node pack cores (pack44 657DA4B173F9D3D3, pack48/49 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3). So where my notes say 'europa --check exit 0 on pack44' or 'on pack48', read 'on europa's older installed compiler (core shown above)'. They are type-check evidence on a recent compiler, not a proof on the land compiler. The node runs (pinned compiler, core read at launch) remain the proof, unchanged.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_90 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 90u32, "2026-11-05T18:44Z", "x", "2026-11-05 14:4x x: X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES RED in x-next10 (job-1793894849167, node, pinned pack51 core E190545B5F30A7B4): invariants.spi 10/10 tests FAILED on rust, including the 9 tests that predate the change, so the module does not compile for rust. The error text did not survive (stdout keeps only the last notebook's tail; the Cells work dirs were cleaned). The same draft built and ran fine on GLEAM: the sim build (sim accept 0, 0 fixtures changed) and e2e (RUST-OK) both used it. Every other notebook in the run passed: sim_serve, timeline_serve 17/17, remote_chunks, sim_progress, sim_publish, xsim_split, feed_merge 6/6, run_signals 2/2, census 4/4. HYPOTHESIS: !!!!UnionCaseName (reflection.case_name) is proven on rust only for STATIC values. reflection.spi's own ///> rust test names constants (Contract |> case_name), while rule_name in invariants runs on dynamic values (the tests use := ~s = ... snapshots, and findings_text maps rule_name over runtime findings). DECISION: drop this draft from the land; the pre-registered rule says no red notebook lands. Because x-next10's generated Gleam was built with the draft, its outputs cannot land without it, so the x side goes to a rerun, x-next10b, without invariants. That rerun also measures whether the LIVE invariants (hand-mapped names) passes rust on pack51. NEXT for this slice: confirm the hypothesis with a one-test rust probe (case_name on a ~dynamic union value). If confirmed, it is a compiler gap to file (UnionCaseName on a dynamic union in Rust); if not, find the real rust error. Until then, the hand-mapped rule_name stays.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_91 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 91u32, "2026-11-05T19:46Z", "x", "2026-11-05 15:3x x: (6) iggy family dependency moved: LIB-IGGY-CLIENT's Gleam UTF-8 decode is LANDED (iggy.spi 92B9E9D4CFB3, 7/7 rust + gleam). (5)/names: X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES stays OUT; its red was the pre-existing SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH, not the draft (the live and HEAD invariants fail the same 9/9 in a scratch tree).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_92 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 92u32, "2026-11-06T00:24Z", "x", "2026-11-05 20:1x x: X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES LANDED (green run x-next11, job-1793917404429, node, pinned pack52 core A688EE5AD426A5A0): sim invariants.spi 95CD1AC6975C -> 16705919CAF4. rule_name is derived (reflection::typed_case_name |> typed_name_snake); the 12-line hand-written demand_rule_name / rule_name match is gone; the new test pins all 6 protocol names. node-proof applied 38 generated outputs, 0 conflicts, 95 unchanged. Evidence: sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK, census SAME over 82 files with 0 cells over one post, invariants notebook 10/10 on rust + gleam (green now that SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH's Cells fix landed at 17:11; it was 0/9 for every version before). Model parts: (names) DONE; still open: command GADT (blocked on typed links) and the sim-to-iggy mapping (its codec dependency LIB-IGGY-CLIENT Gleam decode landed today).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_93 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 93u32, "2026-11-06T08:21Z", "x", "2026-11-06 04:2x x: NEXT STEP (CPU-light): write the sim-event -> iggy-message mapping table as a typed Spiral union draft (no compile needed to review it). The command GADT stays blocked on TYPED-LINK-SOTA.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_94 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 94u32, "2026-11-06T08:26Z", "x", "2026-11-06 04:2x x: follow-up (compiler star lesson 6): pack50 has !!!!UnionCaseName(x, \"snake\") and reflection case_name_snake. Swap invariants.spi rule_name (typed_case_name |> typed_name_snake) for it on the next invariants touch. Prove with one notebook gate.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_95 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 95u32, "2026-11-06T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-06 07:34 x: compiler's UnionCaseName follow-up EDITED in place (unstaged): invariants.spi rule_name is now reflection::case_name_snake r (pack50's !!!!UnionCaseName(x, \"snake\")), replacing typed_case_name |> typed_name_snake. 16705919CAF4 -> 1238B7C5FA99. Proof PENDING: the invariants notebook (rule_names_are_the_snake_case_of_their_cases compares against the hand list) rides the next x node run.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_96 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 96u32, "2026-11-06T13:35Z", "x", "2026-11-06 09:35 x: DRAFTED the sim-event to iggy-message mapping (kit drafts x\\X-SOTA-MODEL\\sim_iggy.spi E05E9624A7DC, not yet compiled). It has a typed topic union (RunProgress | SimEvents) whose names come from reflection::case_name_kebab, so the live 'run-progress' topic name the client posts to (client events.spi topic_url) is derived, not spelled. message = { topic; key; payload }. Every delivery is keyed by the post it touches (Posted/Framed, Edited/FrameEdited/Deleted, Liked/Unliked), so iggy's message key keeps one post's events ordered on one partition. The payload reuses the sim's compact stream line, object (fields_of at event), so a consumer decodes with the existing xsim-events v1 decoder. 4 tests. It uses sim_events (X-SIM-EVENTS-RENAME) and gates after x-cellsfix2c lands. Next: the client's events.spi publishes through topic_path instead of the hand URL.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_97 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 97u32, "2026-11-06T14:00Z", "x", "2026-11-06 10:00 x: LAYERING FIX to n96. The sim package depends on the client, not the reverse, so the topic type moves to a NEW client module topics.spi 119CE61A6FBB: topic = RunProgress | SimEvents, topic_name via reflection::case_name_kebab, topic_path stream t; 2 tests pin the live run-progress path. The client package gets topics after run_signals (client__package.spiproj E12D1C50B8E3 on A89E434ADDD0), and events/events.spi topic_url becomes s::base ++# topics::topic_path \"x\" topics::RunProgress (client__events__events.spi DD257DEF3CC6 on 0AB6A7981802), the same URL derived instead of spelled. sim_iggy.spi B7A250259A6F now uses topics::topic; 3 tests. Gate order: after X-SIM-EVENTS-RENAME lands (sim_iggy opens sim_events and joins the sim package after it), as one x node run: client build plus the topics notebook, sim build plus the sim_iggy notebook, and e2e. PENDING, not launched.")
