inl note_of_showcases_spiral_vs_rust_1 () = Note ("SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "main", "main 10:4x, second pass over the exported chat (user asked). Source: the archive's files/vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md and spiral_vs_phantomdata_prova_por_construcao.md (kit\\archive\\20261101-080304); the zip with the Rust attempts didn't survive, so the attempts get rewritten from the markdown. The report's rogue-route ranking: S4 strongest (Rust is removing generic_const_exprs), then S1 and S5; S3 weakest (its GAT test compiled in Rust). DoD: each showcase is a sample under apps/compiler/tmp/samples with a C/Rust row in the matrix; its Rust attempt is a file next to it whose rustc error text is checked by a test, re-run on the newest stable rustc (the report used 1.97; reviewers will ask for 1.99+); a doc page links them with the honest list of where Rust wins (linear typestate, GAT effects). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: each showcase must use the feature it advertises (GADT, existential, HKT, type literals, reflection) without stringly fallbacks; known limit, as a negative sample: existentials exist only at compile time ('Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var'). NEXT STEP: extract the six showcase code blocks from vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md into sample folders and compile them on pack14a.")
inl note_of_showcases_spiral_vs_rust_2 () = Note ("SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:32Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is DIRECTION-1031; recorded here instead of as a dep, because a dep on an unfinished parent epic hid this item from 'agile next' (backlog-wide sweep: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic).")
inl note_of_showcases_spiral_vs_rust_3 () = Note ("SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:42Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:4x SPLIT: one 60 m child per showcase (SHOWCASE-S1..S6), each with the shared DoD (sample + matrix row + checked rustc error of the best stable-Rust attempt); S4 first (the report's strongest). This parent keeps the summary page: 30 m. S7 (post-CIC proofs) stays vision, not split.")
inl note_of_showcases_spiral_vs_rust_4 () = Note ("SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST", 4u32, "2026-11-09T19:02Z", "compiler", "11-09 15:0x compiler, for all S1-S6 children (they waited on lane:compiler): the compiler ACCEPTS the showcase samples into apps/compiler/tmp/samples; the author writes them, and nothing waits on the compiler to start. House rules: one directory per sample (main.spi + package.spiproj, the same shape as other samples), every negative as its own <name>_negative sample (or a negatives/ subdir with an expect file, like -Suite tstypes), the Rust attempt as a plain .rs file next to it, and no personal paths. Rows appear in -Suite all by directory discovery. Before landing, run -Suite all -Backend C,Rust on ganymede (pack77) and quote the new rows. S4s blocker is resolved (see its note: type_arith is a core module, folded since pack75).")
