inl edition3_main_symbol () = Task ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", "Edition-3 symbol for the program entry instead of the English name main: pick :> (mirrors :< open; flows out), lexed as the entry declaration, plus a census of every other hardcoded English word the compiler requires", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", "team:compiler,edition3,language,lexer,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_edition3_main_symbol () = Planning ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_edition3_main_symbol_1 () = Note ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. PICK: :> for the entry (one operator token, like :#; 0 uses expected, the DOD checks it). CENSUS (step 1, recorded here): words the compiler hardcodes beyond keywords: main (entry lookup), test (done, :#), and the names it resolves by string in core/prelude (e.g. failwith, true/false, unit, the numeric type names); each gets a decision symbol/keep with a reason. DOD: :> lexes and the entry resolves through it on every backend (a sample entry_symbol with ///> on all backends), format --spelling symbols rewrites := main to :> and back (round trip byte-identical), and the census table is on this item. NEXT STEP: grep the lexer and the entry lookup (main string) in spiral_compiler.fs, and count :> uses in all repos. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: entry is a union EntryDecl = Named of name | Symbol, resolved once; no string comparison to main after the parser.")
inl note_of_edition3_main_symbol_2 () = Note ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:43Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:43 compiler, STEP 1 READ (CPU-light): (a) collision check for :> in all repos *.spi: 3 hits, all inside macro text emitting F# upcasts (lib/spiral/common.spi:24 $!x :> `u, mega_omniledger_erp_kernel/main.spi:11832-11833 inside a backend string), 0 as a Spiral token, so a column-0 :> is free. (b) the compiler finds the entry by the string main in 4 places in spiral_compiler.fs: 24852 (C: main is never static), 27155 (C++ host ArgsCppHost main), 35017 and 35086 (entry resolution via Map.tryFind main env.term, per backend). PLAN: same route as :# (lexed to TokVar test): the parser turns a column-0 :> definition into EntryDecl.Symbol and binds it under the internal entry name once, so those 4 sites read the EntryDecl and no longer compare strings; := main stays valid (EntryDecl.Named) for edition 2. Next: draft that as a .kitdo in apps/compiler/drafts plus the sample entry_symbol.")
