inl kit_drafts_store () = Task ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", "kit drafts put|list|promote: unfinished drafts live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\<repo>\\<ITEM>\\, always tied to a backlog item, and promote moves a draft into its repo only after a check (typed Spiral or thin glue, never .py/.tsv/.txt) (user rule 11-01 13:0x via main)", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,agile,drafts,standards,drift,typefeatureset,team:rig,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_drafts_store () = Planning ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_1 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T17:01Z", "kit", "11-01 13:1x kit. USER RULE (13:0x, relayed by main): unfinished drafts and tmp .py/.tsv junk leave the repos and live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\<repo>\\<ITEM>\\ until they are ready to commit as glue or typed Spiral; kit owns the store. Seeded by main: i574n.github\\SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (3 .py) and The-Spiral-Language\\UPSTREAM-FORK-PAGES (posts, scripts). VERBS: kit drafts put <repo> <ITEM> <path...> (moves files into the store, refuses an ITEM that is not in the backlog, appends a note on the item naming the files); kit drafts list [--repo r] [--item I] [--older-than Nd] (one typed row per draft: repo, item, path, bytes, age); kit drafts promote <repo> <ITEM> <draft> <repo-path> (runs the check, then moves the draft into the repo, unstaged, and notes the item). CHECK (promote refuses with the fix printed): the extension is not .py/.tsv/.txt/.csv/.rows; a .spi passes kit standards for its target package (ratchet, no regressions); a .ps1 is glue only (under 40 lines, calls kit or a repo script, no new parsing logic, per spiral-first-tooling); anything else is refused. QUALITY LINT HOOK: KIT-AGILE-QUALITY-LINT gains a rule flagging an open item whose drafts are older than N days (default 7) and a Done item that still owns drafts (promote or archive them). The store is outside every repo, so it also needs a backup line (backup-mirror-coverage-boundary: the profile mirror does not cover %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit). DoD: the three verbs plus CLI tests (put refuses an unknown item; promote refuses a .py and a .spi with a ratchet regression and accepts a clean .spi; list --older-than filters by age); the quality-lint rule with one test; kit drafts list over the store run live. NEXT: a typed model in a new HostFree package kit_drafts_model (draft row record, check_verdict union Promotable | RefusedKind ext | RefusedStandards findings | RefusedGlue reason, the age rule) with tests (CPU-light). TYPEFEATURES: check_verdict union; phantom markers :! InStore / :! InRepo on draft paths so promote is the only function that turns one into the other.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_2 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T17:16Z", "kit", "11-01 13:16 kit: the store's off-box copy is resilience's KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR (seeded 13:0x, 81 entries byte-exact). The dir-mirror --full snapshot mode the drafts need (edits and deletes) is specified there (kit builds the verb). kit drafts put/promote should trigger nothing remote themselves; the scheduled --full run picks the changes up.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_3 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T18:15Z", "kit", "11-01 14:15 kit: RULE NARROWED (user 14:0x via main): when we know where a file lands (a new app or lib module already decided), it starts at its FINAL path in the repo. The store holds only work whose landing is unknown. promote changes: its destination must be a decided landing (an existing package/app dir, or one named on the item), and every stray or committed-junk file (py/ps1/tsv/txt/md) gets a deliberate decision row (Land path | Draft item | Archive reason) instead of silently staying.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_4 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T09:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:1x local rig, first slice (unprobed): src/rig_drafts/model.spi, a pure package (HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0 findings, no Cargo yet so trains leave it out of regen; its notebook runs). draft_row record (repo, item, path, bytes, age_days) and draft_filter (repo, item, older-than days) with kept and a typed row line; file_kind union (SpiralSource, Manifest, Glue, Junk) by extension (a dot inside a directory name is not one); put_checked refuses an item not in the backlog (Task header in the raw state) and a path outside the repo; promote_checked implements the 11-01 14:15 narrowed rule: never Junk (py/ps1/tsv/txt/md...), only to a decided landing that exists. 3 test blocks. NEXT: probe on moon, then the entry (rig_drafts entry over lib file_system: put moves files and notes the item, list walks %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/<repo>/<ITEM>, promote moves to the landing) and the drafts direct verb. DoD: kit drafts put|list|promote with the refusals above, a note on the item for every put/promote, green notebook + CLI tests. TypeFeatures: file_kind and the two verdict unions.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_5 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T09:27Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:3x moon probe rig-probe1109k: src/rig_drafts/model.spi GREEN 3/3. Next: the entry and the drafts verb.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_6 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:4x local rig: entry src/rig_drafts/entry.spi written (lib file_system/env/console + workspace_primitives clock, no host macros; kit standards 0 findings on both modules). drafts put <repo root> <ITEM> <path...> --backlog <root>: put_checked per path, moves into %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/<repo leaf>/<ITEM>/<path relative to the repo>, receipt rig drafts put ok|failed moved=N, exit 1 on any refusal. drafts list [--repo r] [--item I] [--older-than Nd]: walks the store, one row per file (bytes, age from last write). drafts promote <repo root> <ITEM> <landing>: promote_checked per file (junk refused, landing must exist), moves to <repo>/<landing>/<file name>. Export rig_drafts_run. Not yet: the note on the item per put/promote (needs agile_task_notes), Cargo + route + CLI tests, a notebook probe of entry (no test blocks: regen only).")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_7 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:5x local rig: WIRED for TRAIN43: direct verb drafts (VerbDrafts + help line, route rig_drafts.entry.drafts_run through link), rig_drafts Cargo.toml (entry.spi -> entry.rs), workspace member, rig_cli dep, lock refreshed. Model probe green (1109k 3/3); entry is regen-checked in the train. After install: put/list/promote smoke on a scratch repo + the item note per move.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_8 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 8u32, "2026-11-10T04:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 00:4x rig: TRAIN43c's crate gate measured src/rig_drafts/entry.rs at 1196 lines (gate 1000), so rig_drafts is HELD OUT of TRAIN43d and TRAIN44 until it is split. 260 Spiral lines become 62 Rust fns. rig_cli/package.spiproj now lists rig_drafts under packages:/link: (it was inlined into kit.rs before). Plan: one linked unit per verb (list_run, put_run, promote_run each take words : list string, a shape that links), with entry keeping drafts_run as the dispatcher; measure with scripts/regen-sizes.ps1 on a free Windows node. Next step: after moon is free of TRAIN43d, split and measure; then it rides the next train.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_9 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 9u32, "2026-11-10T05:14Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 01:1x rig: SPLIT WRITTEN (unstaged; the pre-split package is archived under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\rig-drafts-before-split-20261110). rig_drafts (1196 lines in TRAIN43c's gate) becomes: rig_drafts_model (model.spi moved as-is, source package), rig_drafts_store (the shared path/flag/move helpers plus verb_words, source package), and three LINKED verb units rig_drafts_list / rig_drafts_put / rig_drafts_promote, each with its own Cargo crate and a unit-argument export (list_entry / put_entry / promote_entry () : i32, reading their own arguments), the shape that links per spiral-link-boundary-shapes; rig_drafts keeps only the drafts_run dispatcher and links the three. Model and store are separate packages so a verb unit never includes the dispatcher (no cycle). Workspace members + lock updated offline (cargo metadata --locked exit 0); kit standards 0 and ratchet 0 on all six packages; the train reference preflight over the whole tree: 0 unresolved. The model's tests in their new package are probing on ganymede (PENDING). UNPROVEN until measured: the crate sizes. Next step: when moon is free of TRAIN43d, scripts/regen-sizes.ps1 -Package rig_drafts,rig_drafts_list,rig_drafts_put,rig_drafts_promote, and grep the dispatcher .rs for rig_drafts_list:: calls to prove the links.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_10 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 10u32, "2026-11-10T05:16Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 01:2x rig: the moved model.spi is green in its new package (rig_drafts_model, Cells notebook gate on ganymede: exec=3 failed=0 passed=3). Still pending: the crate sizes (regen-sizes on a free Windows node). Next step: after moon is free of TRAIN43d, measure the four crates and prove the links.")
