inl openqasm_sim_spiral () = Task ("OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL", "Port the OpenQASM native-row simulator (openqasm-run/run.py) to Spiral", TaskKind, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "OPENQASM3-BACKEND", "compiler,openqasm,spiral,scripts,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_openqasm_sim_spiral () = Planning ("OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_openqasm_sim_spiral_1 () = Note ("OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T17:14Z", "compiler", "11-01 13:14 compiler: filed from the no-.py port-or-drop decision (PS1-TO-SPIRAL). WHAT: apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/openqasm-run/run.py (1502 lines, 46 KB) is the classical OpenQASM simulator behind every OpenQasm native row (test.ps1:626; C is the oracle). It is real logic, so it is ported, not dropped. DEFINITION OF DONE: (1) test.ps1's OpenQasm arm runs a Spiral-built simulator (Rust backend, compiled through the spiral CLI), and python is no longer an OpenQasm prerequisite; (2) `test.ps1 -Backend C,OpenQasm -Suite examples -Native` matches a run.py baseline taken in the same job row for row (same exit and stdout sha on every OpenQasm row, DISAGREE 0, no row lost); (3) run.py is archived and tmp/AGENTS.md's OpenQASM paragraph names the new runner. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: integer width is a closed union (w8 | w16 | w32 | w64) times signedness (signed | unsigned), replacing run.py's string kind tuples ('i8', 'u8', ...). A value is a union: int of width * signedness * u64 bits | f32 | f64 | bool | exact_literal of f64. exact_literal is the 'float literal stays exact until it meets a typed value' rule, made a constructor instead of a flag. The AST carries its scalar type as a phantom on typed expressions, so a f32-rounding step can only apply to f32 nodes. Errors are a union (parse | type | runtime of position) and become 'qasm error:' text only at the process boundary; no -1 sentinels and no exception strings. NEXT STEP: a construct census of run.py (each parser production and builtin, mapped to the emitted .qasm outputs of the 21 matrix samples), then the Spiral lexer and parser checked against those 21 files before any evaluator code.")
inl note_of_openqasm_sim_spiral_2 () = Note ("OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T18:03Z", "compiler", "11-01 14:04 compiler: CENSUS STEP 1 (structure of run.py, 1502 lines). Four layers map one-to-one onto Spiral modules. (1) LEXER: one lex function. (2) PARSER: a recursive-descent Parser class with 9 productions: program, func, block, stmt, type, ret, expr, unary, primary. (3) EVALUATOR: compile-to-closure, about 25 run_* forms (let, set, expr, if, while, output, checked, tuple and dyn-tuple, unit and dyn-unit, tagged, call, parts, source) plus runtime_converter. In Spiral this becomes a closure-producing compile over a typed AST, with the phantom scalar tag from n1's plan on each node. (4) NUMERIC CORE: as_i8/u8/i16/u16/i32/u32/i64/u64 (width wrap), f32 rounding, f64, idiv/imod (toward zero), int_ops_for(width), float_ops, and the math builtins sqrt, exp, log, sin, cos, pow and tanh. The numeric core is the riskiest part: C-exact wrap, shift-count masking and f32-after-every-op. It can be checked first and alone, against lib's existing integer and f32 ops, with the matrix samples' C outputs as the oracle. NEXT STEP: list the 21 OpenQasm matrix samples' emitted .qasm files and tally which productions and run_* forms they actually reach. Unreached forms are dropped from the port instead of carried over.")
inl note_of_openqasm_sim_spiral_3 () = Note ("OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL", 3u32, "2026-11-01T18:04Z", "compiler", "11-01 14:05 compiler: CENSUS STEP 2 (what emitted code reaches). There are 100 .qasm outputs under tmp/samples, more than the 21 matrix rows, and all 100 are the port's parse corpus. Construct counts (lines): def 163, if 223 / else 220, return 284, tuple return 29, tuple destructure 4, while(true) 15, continue 13, break 4, casts 10, shifts 14, math builtins 14, NaN/inf constant expressions 6. Types: bool 360, float[32] 85, float[64] 40, int[8]/int[16] 49, int[64] 21. The `(if c { 1 } else { 0 })` bool-to-int form has 0 uses in current outputs, but keep it in the parser because codegen still emits it. PORT ORDER (by reach): (1) numeric core (all widths and f32/f64; it touches every row); (2) parser over the 100 files (must parse all 100 with 0 errors before any evaluator code); (3) evaluator: def/call/return/if first, then while/continue/break, then tuples; (4) the 7 builtins. DoD unchanged (n1).")
inl note_of_openqasm_sim_spiral_4 () = Note ("OPENQASM-SIM-SPIRAL", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:09Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:17 compiler: GROOM (over 4 h). Scoped to the first two port steps of n3, numeric core + parser over the 100 .qasm files (240m). The evaluator and builtins become their own item once the parser parses all 100 files with 0 errors; filing it now would only duplicate this DoD.")
