inl note_of_dir_tree_lane_metrics_1 () = Note ("DIR-TREE-LANE-METRICS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T17:14Z", "main", "main 13:2x: 00:26 coverage pass found no item for the per-lane enrichment half (GRANULAR-STATS trends one metric there; TREE-PAGES-V2 is the publishing mechanics). DoD: each of spiral, kit, x, fiscal, tibia has at least one benchmark or metric view on its published page sourced from KIT-EXEC-METRICS rows produced in that CI run; git ls-files '*.tsv' in those repos is empty; each lane's last 3 pushes have green CI or a filed item for the red. Next: each lane picks its first view at the next groom round (compiler: per-backend compile time; fiscal: corpus pass counts; tibia: suite totals; x: sim parity; kit: exec metrics). Typefeatureset: a view is a typed record (Metric of name * unit phantom * rows), rendered by dir-tree-html, no string tables.")
inl note_of_dir_tree_lane_metrics_2 () = Note ("DIR-TREE-LANE-METRICS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "main", "main 19:2x (user 11-01 19:1x: 'gotta check the gh actions errors later to make sure we fix them in each lane also, so we always know what's bad from the dir-tree-html perspective'): add a CI status view, each repo's latest run per job (OS) with the failing step and a link, so a red Windows leg (alphabet's today: 60-min timeout, log lost) is visible on the page, not only in gh run list. Each lane checks its own repo's latest run at every groom.")
