inl note_of_heartbeat_staleness_guard_65 () = Note ("HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD", 65u32, "2026-11-05T20:07Z", "resilience", "SYSTEMIC FIX (resilience, unstaged; main + I converged independently). SIX resilience guards had broken+silenced alarm delivery since the kit story->agile rename: each called `kit story note <ID> ... *> $null` (dead verb + swallowed failure), so every scheduled alarm since the rename was dropped - the monitoring looked healthy while being DEAF. Fixed: node-utilization-monitor (full: agile note NODE-ALWAYS-FED + Invoke-Bounded rc + \"NOTE FAILED rc=N\" to .last.log), and story->agile + the same rc/NOTE-FAILED log line on profile-restore-drill (PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL), heartbeat-staleness-guard (HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD), memory-integrity-sweep (MEMORY-INTEGRITY-SWEEP), profile-mirror-monitor (PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL). config-baseline got verb-fix only (no $log var to append to). All 6 target IDs verified to exist first. All parse clean, unstaged. profile-mirror-if-due.ps1 confirmed FINE (schedule due is a real verb, reads LASTEXITCODE). This is the HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD principle - a guard that cannot deliver must say so - and HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD own script was one of the deaf ones. resilience 2026-11-05 16:0x.")
