inl note_of_heartbeat_staleness_guard_143 () = Note ("HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD", 143u32, "2026-11-07T19:40Z", "resilience", "FALSE ALARMS FIXED + guard now trustworthy (11-07 15:3x, surfaced by a groom of Blocked items). It was firing STALE on two EXPECTED-stale files: (1) autonomous-resilience.last.log (3973min) - the active run (this session) uses the cron-prompt heartbeat (fd939b13) and was not writing the liveness beacon the guard expects; FIX: I now maintain autonomous-resilience.last.log as a beacon each active turn (fresh while alive, correctly goes stale if the session dies). (2) profile-mirror.last.log (1410min) - the hot lane is intentionally DISABLED (MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST paused); FIX: the guard now skips a log whose producing scheduled task is Disabled/absent ($pausedLogTask map, auto-resumes monitoring if re-enabled). Re-run: \"all 12 watchers fresh\" exit 0. A genuine dead watcher still alarms (critical-mirror floor confirmed fresh <90min). parse OK. DoD: every status file age-checked, alarms only on REAL staleness, delivery rc-checked - working. Unblocked (the block was this false-alarm noise).")
