inl note_of_regex_skeleton_9 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 9u32, "2026-11-09T00:26Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 20:3x CELL BUDGET after compiler's pack63c fleet reformat (measured by compiler, confirmed with mix spiral.cell_budget --check): regex had +5 new over-budget definitions; all 5 fixed by hoisting a helper, no layout revert: agreement.spi visit -> queued helper; certificate.spi successors -> a probe_work type alias, so the signature fits one line; partition_from -> partition_class joins the existing :& group with partition_next; dfa.spi target_of -> with_state helper; table.spi empty_table -> next_base helper. html had +2: html_pages/tree.spi compare_from -> length_order helper (same results: both ended 0, a ended -1, b ended 1); file_views.spi -> a shorter test name. Re-check: only the PRE-EXISTING baseline remains (regex bench/bench.spi 15, html unit.spi x2 + walk_api.spi 1). Proof pending: Cells gate of the 6 changed notebooks queued on ganymede as job-1794183990021-org2-cellbudget-gate (mirror org2-cb, after tibia's chain; the box was at 90% CPU). Next step: read that job's verdict; on red, fix and re-queue.")
inl note_of_regex_skeleton_10 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 10u32, "2026-11-09T02:37Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 22:4x Proof (cell-budget splits): GREEN. Cells gate job-1794183990021-org2-cellbudget-gate on ganymede (mirror org2-cb = box tree, spiral 3739cfb7 + The-Spiral-Language 17654e07, pinned SPIRAL_CELLS_JOBS=2): 6 files, discovered 40, executed 40, passed 40, failed 0 (regex certificate 17, agreement 4, dfa 5, table 2; html tree 5, file_views 7). certificate's failed_targets entry is the test a_minimized_automaton_cannot_run_as_certified, which asserts that failure on rust; failed_tests is empty. The 7 reformat overruns are closed; only the pre-existing baseline remains (regex bench.spi 15, html unit.spi x2 + walk_api.spi 1). Unstaged; the user pushes.")
inl regex_syntax () = Task ("REGEX-SYNTAX", "regex typed syntax: AST and char-set unions (normalized code ranges, counted repeat with a typed upper bound, & and ~), similarity smart constructors, nullability as GADT evidence", Story, P1, D4, 95u32, Blocked, "-", "regex,automata,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_syntax () = Planning ("REGEX-SYNTAX", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_syntax_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:25Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DOD (n5 D1): code ranges are {low;high} u32 records in a sorted disjoint set built only by a normalizing constructor; repeat is Repeat (re, low, Bounded n | Unbounded), never unrolled; Owens-Reppy-Turon similarity (ACI alt, assoc seq, Nothing/Empty units, star idempotence, & and ~ units) in smart constructors; nullability returns accepts|rejects evidence values; test blocks per law (idempotence, commutativity order, units, evidence text) pinned to rust + gleam, 0 failures, cell budget 0 findings. NEXT STEP: write syntax/ (charset.spi, re.spi, nullable.spi) as notebooks and gate them on europa. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: phantom-indexed char sets (char_set normal vs raw) so only normalized sets reach the AST; nullable_evidence GADT indexed by accepts_empty/rejects_empty (xsd_regex shape, but the index never grows: constant index works at runtime); upper bound as a union, no -1; ordering of AST nodes via a comparison union (Below|Same|Above), not i32. FIELDS: estimate 300, load light, assignee agent.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 2u32, "2026-11-01T21:08Z", "regex", "regex 17:1x PROGRESS (unstaged in C:\\home\\git\\regex): src/ package (packageDir ../deps/spiral/lib) with 9 notebooks: charset (GADT char_set loose|normal, normalized code ranges), syntax (re union with And/Not/counted Repeat, order union, similarity smart constructors), nullable (GADT evidence accepts_empty|rejects_empty), derivative (Brzozowski + remainder theorem), dfa (classes, eager DFA, state nominal, Dead case, typed cap), minimal (Moore refinement, live analysis), certificate (distinguishing words checked on the derivative matcher, equivalence by product exploration), partial (Antimirov + support bound), agreement (keyed_rng corpus, 4 engines). Tests pinned rust+gleam. First Cells gate running on the node (job-1793566876167-regex-cells1, mirror regex-1; europa dropped per main's one-job rule). Scripts: drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SYNTAX\\{cells-gate,typecheck}.ps1. Cell budget NOT yet met (several definitions > 272).")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:27Z", "regex", "regex 17:3x CELL BUDGET (measured by block length, not yet by mix spiral.cell_budget): 35 definitions over ~267 chars, mostly full matches over the 9-case re union (derive 524, points_of 408, partials 543, alphabetic_width 403, order_re group 969, nullability_of group 1378, evidence GADT 1266). PLAN, decided: re-shape the AST so no match has more than ~4 arms: re = Leaf leaf (Nothing|Epsilon|Set) | Pair (pair_op = SeqOp|AltOp|AndOp, re, re) | Unary (unary_op = NotOp|StarOp, re) | Repeat; each engine then dispatches per family into a small helper. The evidence GADT splits by family the same way (leaf, pair, unary evidence). Do this after the first green Cells run so the shape change is the only diff.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:18Z", "regex", "regex 19:1x EVIDENCE node run3 job-1793571992048-regex-run3 (18:25-19:10, memo off, rust+gleam, 900 s budget; saved in drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SYNTAX\\run3-full.txt): total discovered 48 executed 48 passed 41 failed 7, mismatches {} in every file: all 7 reds are node infrastructure (charset: \"could not start the compiler on port 13977: lock_timeout\"; derivative: a cell main.spi missing in TEMP; dfa: \"compiler worker failed\"), not logic. syntax 7/7 and nullable 4/4 on rust and gleam (second run green in a row); charset 4/6 with both reds infra on gleam.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_5 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 5u32, "2026-11-04T12:24Z", "main", "11-04 08:4x main CELL BUDGET MEASURED by x (xc postable census, node build 11-04 07:07): regex/src 15 hand files, 548 cells, 96 over 272 chars (posts 672). Bands: 273-320 = 33 (trims), 321-544 = 51 (one split each), >544 = 12 (the real reshapes: language ends 1522, nullable evidence 1266 / nullability_of 1378 / accept_reason 1298, xsd class_body 1075 / alternation 1043, syntax order_re 969, semantics bt 905, dfa build_rows 661, lazy empty_store 646, certificate columns_sound 573, lazy grow_to 548); 17 of the 96 are test cells. Per file: certificate 16, lazy 13, xsd 9, semantics 8, minimal 7, partial 7, syntax 6, table 6, agreement 5, language 4, and 3 each in charset, derivative, dfa, laws, nullable. DECISION: split per measured cell (largest first, re-measured with xc) instead of n3's whole-AST reshape. The 12 big ones are where n3's 4-arm idea applies (the 9-case re matches). Re-measure: %TEMP%\\xc-node\\xc.exe postable census <files>.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_6 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 6u32, "2026-11-04T13:06Z", "main", "11-04 09:1x main CELL BUDGET 96 -> 61 over (xc postable census, box): charset 3->0, table 6->0, derivative 3->0, laws 3->0, syntax 6->0, dfa 3->0, agreement 5->0, partial 7->1 (reconstruction_from: its function-typed split parameter makes every helper header ~160 chars). KEY TECHNIQUE (proven; memory mutual-group-blank-line-splits-cells): a blank line may precede :& and the group still binds (europa --check, negative control fails ETY-UnboundVariable), and x confirmed xc counts each blank-separated :& block as its own cell. So recursive matches split into :& arm chains (derive -> derive_seq/derive_rest/derive_unary; normalize; order_re -> order_same/order_pair/order_unary/order_repeat_with; build_rows -> build_next/build_step; partials; alphabetic_width; agree_from/search_accepted/agree_on_words; assign) with every call fully applied: no closures, no eager evaluation. Non-recursive steps are plain helpers. Exceptions: charset order_ranges evaluates the tail comparison eagerly (after_tie), same result. VERIFIED: whole package --check clean on europa (planted-error control rejected). PENDING: the europa Cells gate (started on the 96->72 tree); the later splits need one more gate. LEFT: certificate 16, lazy 13, xsd 9, semantics 8, minimal 7, language 4, nullable 3, partial 1.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_7 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 7u32, "2026-11-04T13:17Z", "main", "11-04 09:2x main EUROPA GATE 1 GREEN: regex Cells (15 notebooks, rust+gleam) 86/86 passed, 0 failed, on the first-wave tree (charset, table, laws, derivative tests, first syntax/dfa/agreement splits). Since then: semantics 8->0, minimal 7->0, language 4->0, partial 7->1, and the :& chains in derivative/laws/syntax/dfa/agreement. 42 over left (certificate 16, lazy 13, xsd 9, nullable 3, partial 1). Package --check clean on europa after every file. GATE 2 (current tree) PENDING on europa.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_8 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 8u32, "2026-11-04T13:36Z", "main", "11-04 09:4x main CELL BUDGET 96 -> 2 over (xc census, box: 15 hand files, 729 cells). EUROPA GATE 2 GREEN: Cells 88/88 (wave 2: :& chains, semantics, minimal, partial, language). Wave 3 (nullable, xsd, lazy, certificate) package --check clean, Cells gate 3 PENDING. Techniques beyond n6: a type alias (:== seen_pairs = list (target * target)) to shorten headers; a sound_ctx record threading d/n/width/lows through rows_sound/columns_sound, with a generic first_of choosing the first violation (later checks now evaluate eagerly, same result, and a sound DFA checks every column anyway); existing eager_of and flip_accepting reused in place of inline copies; accessors nodes_of/steps_of/links_of plus a generic regrow/resized_copy in the array store (non-recursive helpers only on the hot path). LEFT (asked x): nullable evidence GADT declaration (1266, type, class question), partial reconstruction_from (375; its function-typed split parameter makes every helper header ~160 chars).")
