inl note_of_regex_spiral_deletion_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:26Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. PLAN (n5 D12). PHASE A paths: spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/ (README.md, main.spi, main.fsx, package.spiproj, bench.ps1, regex_crate_bench.rs, runtime_interned.spi, runtime_workload.spi, 67 subfolders: 27 positive incl. proof_suite/runtime_bench/runtime_native, 31 negative_*, 8 compiler_probe_*); its entries in apps/compiler/tmp/tests/matrix.psd1; then a single-flight -Accept so the oracle drops the rows. UNLOCK: REGEX-PUBLISH done (D1-D10 green in CI on a pushed commit) AND the user says go. BEFORE: dangling check by stem in every sibling repo; compiler lane keeps chosen compiler_probe_*/negative_* as minimal regression samples; MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps brzozowski for regex CI as canary. PHASE B: lib/spiral/xsd_regex.spi; consumers xsd_emit.spi (26 refs), xpath_eval.spi (14), fiscal generated units (table_matches), fiscal/src/corpus.spi. UNLOCK: REGEX-XSD parity + the user picks (i) fiscal/xpath consume regex as a package and xsd_emit leaves lib, or (ii) regex's engine lands in lib as the canonical copy. Agents never delete; the user runs or approves it. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a (deletion). FIELDS: estimate 90, load heavy (accept run), assignee pair.")
