inl cells_kit_merge_study () = Task ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", "Study merging Cells into kit (user 11-01 17:4x: 'consider merging cells and kit later, kit lane didn't like the idea but this might be the unavoidable direction, gotta experiment and philosophize, with a task so we don't forget'): one runner/job/notebook core across Gleam+Rust, now that iggy (Rust) and k3s join the balance", Story, P2, D5, 25u32, Active, "", "kit,cells,architecture,research,team:org,main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_kit_merge_study () = Planning ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_kit_merge_study_1 () = Note ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:48Z", "main", "main 17:4x: the user's framing. The balance equation now has Gleam and Rust (Spiral backends), iggy (Rust, adopted rather than rewritten), and k3s (adopted, memory-hungry but needed for Windows + WSL + Linux reuse). At SOTA we know what can be rewritten: early on we bound clap, and now lanes prefer from-scratch typefeatureset implementations. DoD: a written comparison (kit's job/window/agile core vs Cells' runner/daemon/notebook core): overlap measured in definitions and lines, the shared typed models (job, run, cell, verdict), the costs of merging versus not (startup, memory, BEAM vs native), and one prototype seam (e.g. kit running a Cells notebook through a typed job, or Cells using kit's job host), measured. Then a decision for the user with a recommendation. The kit lane's objection is recorded as an input, not a veto. Typefeatureset: the merged core's verdict and phase types as GADTs shared by both.")
inl note_of_cells_kit_merge_study_2 () = Note ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:09Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. Next step: list the duplicated runner/job/notebook surfaces between Cells (Elixir + Spiral port) and kit (Spiral/Rust) with line counts, as the input to the written study. TypeFeatures: the job/runner contract as one typed protocol both sides would implement.")
inl note_of_cells_kit_merge_study_3 () = Note ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:15Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:3x tibia (help pool): STEP 1 INVENTORY (note 2's next step). SIZES: Cells = 11242 lines of Elixir (apps/cells/lib) + 1441 lines of PowerShell drivers (spi/*.ps1); largest: notebook.ex 1446, compiler_daemon.ex 1261, cells.ex 1193, compiler_client.ex 834, targets.ex 728, memo.ex 603, mounts.ex 449, runner.ex 386. kit's runner/job surface (src): rig_jobs 1316, rig_process_observation 634, rig_process_table 579, rig_process 579, rig_job_host 525, rig_process_streaming 396, rig_do_jobs 393, rig_machine_watch(+model) 710, rig_notebook_progress 308, rig_job_after_model 293, rig_jobs_doctor_model 250, rig_job_dispatch 249 (about 6.2k). DUPLICATED SURFACE: OS process supervision. Cells runner.ex (Port.open with a watcher process, timeouts, capture files, cmd.exe quoting, tail reads) does what kit rig_process* + rig_job_host do natively (~2k lines vs 386). UNTYPED SEAM (the actual coupling today): kit learns a notebook's outcome by grepping Cells stdout for the text `spiral-tests total {json}` (rig_notebook_progress/model.spi:143, tests at :190-217); there is no shared type for the run/verdict, so a wording change in Cells silently breaks kit. UNIQUE (no counterpart): Cells notebook/compiler daemon+client/memo/targets/mounts (~5.3k, the notebook domain); kit agile/windows/queue. PRELIMINARY DIRECTION, not yet the decision: merge the SEAM, not the systems: (1) one typed run report (discovered/executed/passed/failed/not_run + per-test verdicts) defined once in lib, emitted by Cells and parsed by kit through the same type (replacing the grep); (2) the prototype the DoD asks for: kit job -> Cells notebook through that typed report, measured (it runs today, but untyped). A wholesale merge would mostly MOVE ~5.3k lines of unique notebook domain code without deduplicating it; the dedupe win is the ~400-line runner plus the protocol. Startup/memory costs (BEAM vs native) still to measure in step 2.")
inl note_of_cells_kit_merge_study_4 () = Note ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:16Z", "tibia", "Next step: step 2, measure the costs. Cells notebook cold start vs kit job start (wall + RSS, one trivial notebook, 5 runs each on an idle node), and how often the spiral-tests total text format changed in git history (the cost of the untyped seam). Then a typed run_report draft in lib for the seam prototype.")
inl note_of_cells_kit_merge_study_5 () = Note ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", 5u32, "2026-11-09T18:17Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:3x tibia: STEP 2 PART 1 (seam churn). git log -S \"spiral-tests total\": 3 commits in spiral apps/cells (fd70dccf, 0ec501fb, 59b477ba), 1 in kit src. So the untyped text seam has rarely broken in COMMITTED history. Caveats: -S only sees changes in how often the string occurs (new JSON fields inside the line do not show), and most lane work lives unstaged for days, so history undercounts churn. Reading for the decision: the seam's risk is real but low-frequency. The case for a shared typed run_report is correctness (kit's tests at rig_notebook_progress/model.spi:190-217 hard-code the line), not churn. STEP 2 PART 2 (start/RSS costs) needs an idle node, so it is queued for a quiet slot rather than measured on a shared ganymede (today's A/A showed 33 pct drift there).")
inl html_repo () = Task ("HTML-REPO", "New repo i574n/html (C:\\home\\git\\html), a from-scratch typefeatureset rewrite of dir-tree-html's roles (tree pages, markdown/README rendering, per-file viewers, notebook pages, later Spiral->TS/Wasm rendering with a leptos/tachys front end). Feature parity first, binaries built in GitHub Actions, then every repo switched to it, then the dir-tree-html repo retired (user 11-01 17:4x)", Epic, P0, D6, 50u32, Active, "", "html,pages,dir-tree-html,regex,blog,lib,dogfood,team:org,main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_html_repo () = Planning ("HTML-REPO", Minutes 1200u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_html_repo_1 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:49Z", "main", "main 17:4x, the user's words: 'since dir-tree-html deals also with markdown now and not only the tree, with probably having more roles in the future with rendering inner files with ts compiled from spiral or compiling to rust to use wasm in a leptos/tachys rewrite with the typefeatureset ... i created a new repo called html, we'll take this chance to start over instead of moving dir-tree-html's code, so we model things better considering the typefeatureset and the new lessons ... we gotta have feature parity with dir-tree-html asap, with the binaries being generated in gh actions etc, then adapting all repos, so we can delete the dir-tree-html repo without issues ... html will be another dogfeed challenge, with blog also, the reuse gotta be crazy, knowing what will be kept in lib and which repo will have which in deps, how many pre built binaries we can reuse'. PARITY CHECKLIST (dir-tree-html today, incl. 11-01 work): tree page with sizes and folder details, top README (GFM tables, ordered lists, inline code/links/images/badges/emphasis, \\\\| escape), --viewers per-file pages (.spi/.tsv/.md/.toml/.ps1/...) that never overwrite notebook pages, --self-test, a release binary, used by publish-tree.ps1 across 12 repos. DoD: (1) html renders every repo's Pages byte-equivalent or better (a diff report per repo); (2) GitHub Actions builds and publishes html's binaries (Linux + Windows), and repos download the release instead of building the renderer; (3) all 12 publish-tree callers switched; (4) dir-tree-html archived, with a redirect README. Lane tips: %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT\\lane-tips-20261101.md applies here too. Generic pieces (markdown, html escaping, file walk, size labels) are candidates for lib, decided by the reuse metrics (LIB-RESHAPE / KIT-REUSE-METRICS). Typefeatureset: a document model as unions/GADTs (Block, Inline, Viewer, Page), typed exports across crates, nameof instead of string maps.")
inl note_of_html_repo_2 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:38Z", "html", "html 21:3x STATE: C:\\home\\git\\html, unstaged on top of the user's f2dd71c. src/ has 7 Cells notebooks with 44 tests. They passed 44/44 at digest 22318F43 (node job html-cells-3). After the line-width re-lay (kit standards src: 0 findings), 42/44 passed (job html-cells-4). The 2 failures came from a parenthesised _assert_eq argument split over two lines. Moving those two expectations into fixture functions fixed it: render+pages 14/14 (job html-cells-6, digest F0A34AA5); the other 5 files passed 30/30 unchanged in cells-4. PARITY: byte-identical with dir-tree-html on 232/232 pages (HTML-PARITY n2). OPEN: the 1000-line gate (markdown/entry.rs 2169, cli/html.rs 1701 lines). The generated .rs files in the tree are stale box builds, and build.ps1 regenerates them. The first GitHub run needs the user's push and the Pages setting. LESSON: one of my box probes ran with C:\\home\\git\\alphabet as the cwd and left a stray file `x` there. Main moved it to drafts\\html\\HTML-REPO\\strays. From now on, probes run from the drafts folder and use absolute output paths. NEXT, in order: (1) split the markdown and cli crates (HTML-CLI n2); (2) the user pushes and we watch CI; (3) the release job (HTML-CI-RELEASE); (4) spiral/scripts/html.ps1 and the 12 callers (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS); (5) lib lands for html escaping and size labels (HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES).")
inl note_of_html_repo_3 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl note_of_html_repo_4 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:28Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Same rule as HTML-CI-RELEASE (Pages once the gh-pages branch exists, then 200). BACKUP/UNDO: Undo: gh api -X DELETE repos/i574n/html/pages. OWNER: main.")
inl note_of_html_repo_5 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 5u32, "2026-11-04T16:17Z", "main", "11-04 12:2x main ORPHAN SWEEP: Active with no note for 48 h, so back to Planned at 35% (WIP cap: Active means touched). Owner stays main; resume from the last note.")
inl note_of_html_repo_6 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 6u32, "2026-11-06T12:30Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: i574n/html replaces dir-tree-html in every caller (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS), CI green on both OSes, with the release binaries (HTML-CI-RELEASE). Next step: HTML-README-ANY-CASE lands with the user's push, then the shim switch draft from HTML-ADOPT-REPOS.")
inl note_of_html_repo_7 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 7u32, "2026-11-07T15:49Z", "main", "TypeFeatures: a typefeatureset rewrite by design: typed element/attribute nodes, the listing union and refusal union in html_walk, linked units exporting typed records.")
inl note_of_html_repo_8 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 8u32, "2026-11-09T03:19Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:2x STATUS vs DoD (read-only checks): (1) CI GREEN ON BOTH OSes: gh-pages.yml runs a matrix [ubuntu-24.04, windows-2025]; run 'tests' on the user's push 4ab01fc2 (02:31Z) completed/success, Pages deploys (02:46Z success); earlier pushes 37f633e4 and 549ebd90 were green too. (2) RELEASE BINARIES: none yet (gh release list is empty) -> HTML-CI-RELEASE stays open. (3) ADOPTION: HTML-ADOPT-REPOS (switch publish-tree.ps1 and its 12+ callers) not started, so dir-tree-html can't be deleted yet. Also done since the last note: parity byte-identical on 232/232 pages (HTML-PARITY), the typed-units/1 layout applied tonight (7 entries renamed to <unit>.spi, unique module stems; proof job-1794192253339-org2-html-units pending on ganymede), and the cell-budget splits from the reformat (gate 40/40 green). Progress 35 -> 50. Next step: HTML-CI-RELEASE (attach the cli binaries for both OSes to a release from the workflow), then the shim switch from HTML-ADOPT-REPOS.")
