inl fiscal_regen_incremental () = Task ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", "fiscal regen: per-family tests in parallel, and skip families whose input hashes did not change", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-2-FORMAT-CACHE,FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", "team:fiscal,fiscal,generator,ci,performance", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_regen_incremental () = Planning ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:57Z", "fiscal", "Found by fiscal 2026-11-01 (main's groom ask A). The consumer proof's generator.spi run regenerates all 81 units in one serial test (generates_every_family_version + the per-family tests in one process): 90+ min on the node, 100% CPU on 8 cores (shared). Per-family tests already exist (generates_chile_envio_dte_v10, generates_verifactu_registro, ... about 18), so: (1) a regen runner runs them as separate lib_gate -Test processes in parallel (cap = cores/2); (2) a family whose inputs are unchanged (sha of its schema closure + the lib files the generator imports + generator.spi itself) is skipped, with the previous output kept and a manifest row (family, input hash, output hashes) in target/ci-metrics. Proof of value: today's lib respell would have regenerated everything (lib hash changed), while an XSD fix touching 2 families regenerates 2.\nDONE: a regen of N changed families takes about N/cores of today's wall time; CI's build.ps1 uses the same runner; the manifest is published on the dir-tree-html page.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: \":== regen_row = { family : family_name; input_hash : content_hash; outputs : list (unit_name * content_hash) }\" with nominals (no raw strings), read and written as JSON through json_schema.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 2u32, "2026-11-04T04:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:13 fiscal: GROOM 11-04 (last note 11-01): owner fiscal. Evidence 11-03: one full regen proof = generator ~45 min + format 83 units 1523 s on the node, so the full-regen cost dominates every family proof. NEXT: skip families whose input closure hash is unchanged (hash the family row + its schema files), then run per-family gates in parallel on node + europa.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 3u32, "2026-11-04T07:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:01 fiscal: WHERE THE REGEN TIME GOES (measured 11-03/04), which re-aims this item. (1) GENERATION IS CHEAP: on europa the generator compiled to Rust in 36 s, rustc 180 s, and writing a family took under 1 s; the node's ~45 min 'generator' step is Cells compiling the generator's 24 tests, not generating. (2) FORMAT is a fixed 1,523 s for 83 units, and its cache (scripts/format-generated.ps1: key = sha256 of SpiralCompiler(Core).dll x raw unit hash, under target/format-cache) reports '0 from cache' every time. Not a bug: each lib change rewrites every unit, and the node's compiler core changed 7+ times in a day, each a new cache. (3) GATES: per-unit Cells gates run whether or not the unit changed. DONE IN JOB SCRIPTS (node-es-object.ps1): hash every generated unit before and after the regen and gate only the changed ones (plus the unit under proof). PROPOSALS, not applied: (a) build.ps1 / family-gates gate only units whose hash changed against the last green run's manifest (CI keeps full gates); (b) key the format cache on the formatter's BEHAVIOUR (hash of formatting a fixed probe set) instead of the dll bytes, so a core that does not change layout keeps the cache; risk: a probe set that misses a layout change leaves stale formatting, which CI's format check would catch. Skipping families by input hash (the original plan) saves under 1 s each, so it is dropped.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 4u32, "2026-11-06T12:45Z", "fiscal", "Split 11-06 08:4x (steps of 120 min or less), re-aimed by the 11-04 measurement (generation itself is cheap; the cost is Cells gating every unit + a fixed 1,523 s format): -1-CHANGED-GATES (90), -2-FORMAT-CACHE (90), -3-PARALLEL (120). The original 'skip families whose inputs did not change' is subsumed: comparing unit bytes after a cheap regen is exact and needs no input-closure hash. DoD: all three Done; a one-family XSD change regenerates everything (cheap) but formats and gates only that family. NEXT: step 1 (taken now).")
inl gate_heals_1101 () = Task ("GATE-HEALS-1101", "Gate heals from every lane's last 2 hours (user 11-01 17:4x: 'the lanes are sitting idle again instead of pulling, ask them what could be healed in the gates considering their last two hours and resource usage'): no lane waits on a gate it could have scoped, cached, offloaded or caught locally", Epic, P0, D5, 66u32, Planned, "SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH", "gates,ci,node,cells,kit,all-lanes,team:org,main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gate_heals_1101 () = Planning ("GATE-HEALS-1101", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_1 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: replies from compiler, x, tibia, fiscal, resilience, x-dumps (kit pending). Cross-lane themes: (1) box landings blocked for hours by heavy windows (x: 179 + 141 min held vs 1-5 min needed); (2) node saturation with 5 lanes (x: Cells suite 7.7x slower; tibia: 2 void gates, daemon start failures); (3) proofs rebuild everything (tibia consumer 129 min for 6 files; fiscal 81 units serial 90+ min; x verify ~3 h; compiler cold node builds 435-528 s, Gleam proofs 30 min); (4) stale or cold mirrors give false reds (fiscal 40 min chasing a stale corpus_checks; x cold Gleam false fails; resilience stale spiral); (5) cheap mistakes found only after a 14-min node cycle (resilience: parse error, a width-122 line). DONE NOW by main: lib_gate exits 1 when failed > 0 (x A5: erlang_map 0/3 had exited 0). Children: LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX, MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS, PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS, WARM-MIRROR-CACHES, MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD, CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS, PREDICT-PER-BACKEND, LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE, SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH, REMOTE-RUN-FILE. DoD: each child done, then a 2-hour lane-idle re-measure shows no gate wait over 15 min that a child should have removed.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_2 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:21Z", "main", "main 18:2x more replies. kit: (A1) node regen+proof runs take 20-28 min and the crate gate runs AFTER the full build, so 3 of 4 proofs found a 1000-line overrun only at minute ~20; heal = a seconds-fast size predictor (regen only the touched owner + line count) and the crate gate fail-fast before notebooks (fits LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE). (A2) the ratchet/standards check runs in seconds as gate 0. (A3) europa: KIT_JOB_SLOTS=1 plus Cells parallel=1. (A4) agile set/note take 1-66 s wall against 0.5-3.7 s internal, queueing on the 10.7 MB state; heal = KIT-SCALE's no-op short-circuit plus append-only segments. (A5) trains always snapshot. x-dumps: slot caps from remote-machines.json (MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS); a warm daemon per mirror (WARM-MIRROR-CACHES); a generated verb registry from [package.metadata.kit] so a lane can add a verb without touching kit's files; a node-singleton job that rebuilds Linux kit on europa whenever kit lands; remote.ps1 run -File (REMOTE-RUN-FILE); typed k3s manifests emit Namespaces first. NODE DISK (x-dumps 17:59, 4.4 GB free): main removed regenerable build outputs in idle mirrors (+2.36 GB, 6.6 GB free); resilience triages node TEMP (9.9 GB, a recovery source) and its 3.8 GB mirror; kit prunes kit-verify (6.75 GB). A heal to add: kit job host refuses or warns when the node has under 10 GB free.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_3 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:10Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 19:2x PARKED USER DECISION (resilience, node disk, for 22:00 batch): WSL ext4.vhdx compaction. The node WSL vhdx is 14.4 GB (C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\wsl\\{911b042f...}\\ext4.vhdx, distro Ubuntu, STATE=Running). Tonight's cleanup already got the node to 16.2 GB free (enough), so this is NOT urgent. RECOMMENDATION: defer; when more node headroom is wanted, compact in a quiet window: (1) confirm WSL is not actively hosting k3s/iggy for another lane, (2) wsl --shutdown, (3) Optimize-VHD -Path <vhdx> -Mode Full (needs Hyper-V module) OR diskpart select vdisk file=<vhdx> + compact vdisk. Reclaims the slack between the 14.4 GB allocated and WSL's actual used (unknown without df inside WSL while it ran). USER's machine call because wsl --shutdown stops WSL for everyone. Not doing it mid-run per main.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_4 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 4u32, "2026-11-02T00:20Z", "main", "main 20:2x FOUND + FIXED (unstaged remote.ps1): the route probe 'ssh -o ConnectTimeout=8 <alias> exit 0' can hang indefinitely, because ConnectTimeout covers only the TCP connect and not a stalled handshake (likely during europa's sshd PerSourcePenalties lockout at 19:3x, which remote.ps1's own probes triggered). Two of main's europa waiters sat in it for 1.5 h and 10 min, silently. The probe now adds -o BatchMode=yes -o ServerAliveInterval=5 -o ServerAliveCountMax=2, so it fails within ~20 s instead of blocking. Any lane job that looked stuck before reaching europa since 19:3x may have been this.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_5 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 5u32, "2026-11-02T00:54Z", "main", "main 20:5x HANGS ARE TODAY'S PATTERN (3 separate incidents): (1) remote.ps1's route probe (fixed 20:2x); (2) a remote.ps1 sync's Invoke-Remote ssh sat 22 min after the server side was gone (main's europa chain), because remote.ps1's ssh/scp had no keepalive; (3) resilience's profile-mirror: a hung remote-verify ssh held the overlap guard and silently skipped the primary backup for 6.2 h. FIX (unstaged remote.ps1): Get-HostOption, which every ssh and scp in remote.ps1 goes through, now always adds -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=4, so a dead link fails in ~60 s while long-running commands keep working (smoke: run hostname on node and europa OK). Resilience fixed profile-mirror the same way, plus a stale-run kill in its overlap guard. Rule for every tool that shells out to ssh: keepalives always; ConnectTimeout alone only bounds the connect.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_6 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 6u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: one more heal landed 11-02 (unstaged): apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 read GREEN when nothing ran (compiler's report: a mirror without the pascal alias made mix abort, the total was discovered 73 / executed 0, and the exit was 0). It now exits 2 on executed 0 of N>0 and on any \"** (Mix)\" line. Proven with a stub mix over 5 cases (abort and Mix-after-partial exit 2; clean pass and backend-gated not_run exit 0; a real failure exits 1).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_7 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 7u32, "2026-11-02T14:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Whether to compact the node's 14.4 GB WSL ext4.vhdx (wsl --shutdown + Optimize-VHD/diskpart). RULE (written before acting): Default is to defer, which is a no-op and so the safe choice: the node has 16.2 GB free after the cleanup (n3). Trigger to revisit: node free space under 10 GB at a kit health check. At that point the compaction becomes a UserBoundary, because Optimize-VHD and diskpart need elevation and wsl --shutdown stops WSL for everyone. BACKUP/UNDO: Nothing changes while deferred. OWNER: resilience. NEXT: Record the 10 GB trigger in the node health check and continue the item's own gate-heals survey across lanes. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_8 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 8u32, "2026-11-05T21:02Z", "main", "main 11-05 17:0x ROLLUP (the field read 0 since 11-01 although most themes were taken): (1) box landings held by heavy windows -> LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX 95 (lib two-step close proven; -MinFreeMb today; Cells -ProvenLog awaits one real land, asked x). (2) node saturation -> MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS 70 (kit), NODE-ALWAYS-FED 55 (kit; pack52 on box, node and europa today). (3) proofs rebuild everything -> PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS 50 (closure core proven, 'kit repo scope' wired by kit, not yet in the installed kit). (4) stale/cold mirrors -> MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD Done; CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER Done (no mid-gate compiler swap). (5) cheap mistakes found late -> LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE 55 (kit A1: TRAIN32 today is the first train since TRAIN21 past regen + crate gate before notebooks). kit A4 (agile write latency) -> KIT-SCALE 0 Planned, with NEW evidence today: 'agile rename' ran 14 min / 398 s CPU without writing, and plain note/set calls queued past 2 min at 14.86 MB. Hang heals (ssh keepalive/BatchMode in remote.ps1) and the vacuous-green lib_gate (exit 2 on executed 0) landed 11-02. Field = mean of the 8 owning items, ~66.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_9 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 9u32, "2026-11-06T10:10Z", "main", "main 11-06 06:1x groom: untouched 13 h, and it is a rollup whose themes live on their own items (LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX done, MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS, NODE-ALWAYS-FED, PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS). Active -> Planned; resume when SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH moves.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_10 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 10u32, "2026-11-07T15:47Z", "main", "TypeFeatures: none; an umbrella of per-lane gate heals, each child carries its own typed plan.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_11 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 11u32, "2026-11-09T15:59Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 last-2h reply (FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6A, refactor-only lib batches of xsd_emit.spi). MEASURED: the single-module lib_gate (37 tests) on moon took 78, 101 and 67+ min for batch 1-3 under shared moon load, against about 6 min for the full -PrivateLib proof and seconds for the copy-only box land: the gate is about 90 percent of each cycle, although every batch is local renames, one-line reflows and helper extractions. HEALS: (1) DONE by fiscal: stack batches, gating the newest draft only (b5 is built on b4, so one gate covers both; about 90 min of moon saved per skipped gate). (2) PROPOSED, needs compiler-lane input: a rename-only proof by codegen identity: compile the module's tests before and after and compare generated text; if identical, skip the test run. Open question: whether local binder names reach the generated code. (3) The box lib drifted under fiscal's proofs 3 times today (tlds plus 5 files; layers, process and the physics.spi removal). The rows diff plus exact resync (copy changed, delete moon-only) took about 1 min each time, a candidate for a lib_land_window -SyncFrom step. (4) On the saturated box, mix spiral.cell_budget plus lib_roundtrip took over 10 min per draft; the cell-budget awk oracle (exact, zero CPU) should replace the mix budget run, and only the round trip needs mix. (5) remote.ps1 node job status hung over 90 s once at 11:5x local and later returned normally.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_12 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 12u32, "2026-11-09T16:08Z", "tibia", "tibia 11-09 last-2h reply (lib land of env argv_view on moon, regex_xsd gates, BC steps 11-13 on ganymede). MEASURED: (1) a moon -PrivateLib proof took SIX attempts, every failure environmental and found only after the ~2 min tree copy: a PowerShell case clash (foreach $s clobbered $S, memory ps-variables-case-insensitive-clobber); a source-only lib pack that dropped lib/spiral/spiral.toml; and newer apps/cells sources forcing a Cells recompile that reads the spiral ROOT rust-toolchain.toml. HEAL (proposed, org tooling): one stage-tree builder that (a) replaces lib/spiral WHOLESALE including config files, (b) adds the spiral root files, and (c) runs a seconds preflight (lib/spiral/spiral.toml, root rust-toolchain.toml and every draft's base hash present) BEFORE the lander starts. That would have turned 5 failed proofs into 1 local error. (2) pack77 added a compiler stdout line (`outline: N arm(s)...`), which changed every content-sha filter that greps compile output away; a refactor looked like a behaviour change until diffed. HEAL: predict-style apps write result rows to a file (`-Out`) and gates hash THAT, never mixed stdout. (3) ganymede's 2 slots were both held by one lane for ~40 min while 2 tibia gates (xsd 4 min, BC step 13) queued. HEAL: none needed beyond MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS, but short gates could take a fast lane. (4) The rebench A/A on a shared ganymede drifted 33 pct, Void by design, so a quiet-slot window for timing arms is the remaining ask (PREDICT-BACKEND-REBENCH waits on it).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_13 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 13u32, "2026-11-09T16:13Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-09 last-2h reply (x client verify r2 cold + warm on moon, Cells timing read, europa per-test suite staging). MEASURED: (1) 20.3% of all Cells cell time in the r2-cold client verify was the 'mount' phase (4,680 of 23,111 s over 227 cells, about 20 s per cell; it was 0.3% on 10-21). The cause is not mounting: lib/spiral/spiral.toml has no module list, so every Manifest.read of lib starts 'dotnet SpiralCompiler.dll --resolve-manifest' (3.3-5.9 s each on loaded moon), 3-4 times per cell. HEAL (built, unstaged, test added): Manifest.cached memoizes per directory-listing stamp. Every lane's Cells gate that mounts the lib gets the ~20 s per cell back (CELLS-CELL-TIMINGS n28-29). (2) 3 of 48 client notebooks went VOID on the 300 s cell timeout while TRAIN42e shared moon (cpu 87%). HEAL (done): x-verify-client.ps1 -TimeoutScale (SPIRAL_CELLS_TIMEOUT_SCALE, recorded in inputs) for runs on a shared host. Its failed_lines now catch 'notebooks failed' and ': VOID, ', which the summary had missed. (3) 1 real red was mine: a module moved to lib while still listed in x's build.ps1 (rename-sweep memory point 6). (4) The phase data cost nothing: every Cells run with --output-path writes phases_ms per cell into its .ipynb. Read them before tuning (memory cells-mount-phase-is-manifest-resolve).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_14 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 14u32, "2026-11-09T16:17Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 16:2x on tibia's (1) stage-tree preflight: org2 hit the same class 3 times today on the ganymede route (a proof tree missing 236 ignored lib/spiral/bench/parsing/target/*.spi artifacts; a stale lib benchmark.spi kept by an overlay; xsd_emit.spi landed on the box between proof and land). What caught all three in seconds: Get-LibDigest raw digest of the box lib == of the node tree's lib before submitting, and again before the box land, plus the predicted post-land digest == the proof's lib digest line (recipe in memory lib-land-proof-on-node-copy-on-box). Durable form proposed to microblog (lib_land_window owner): a -DigestOnly switch reusing the window's own Get-LibDigest, so no new script and the digests agree with the window by construction. Wholesale lib replace (not an overlay) is tibia's (a) and org2's practice now.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_15 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 15u32, "2026-11-09T16:51Z", "compiler", "compiler 11-09 last-2h reply (all unstaged, spiral). HEALED: (1) Cells runner crash that HID the failing test (rig TRAIN42e notes_cli red, ErlangError invalid_byte 129: a failing test message carried an OEM-encoded byte, and JSON.encode! died; compiler_daemons rescue then replaced the real message with the encoding error). Spiral.Cells.Result.json_safe/1 (String.replace_invalid) at every JSON encode of child text: the per-file spiral-tests report line, the .ipynb write, the daemon error/void lines; raw runner output unchanged. 34/34 on ganymede incl. a test reproducing byte 129. Gate effect: a red names its test instead of dying. (2) formatter/candidate-gate.ps1 cached the kit consumer corpus FOREVER (if -not Test-Path), so after kit HEAD moved the gate compared against stale code; now every consumer corpus is re-extracted per run with one git archive (cheaper than the old per-file git show loop: dice 6 files, kit 1160, byte-identical to git show). (3) moon placement: a kit job wait --on busy-polls the node (memory), so the compiler heartbeat reads kit job list instead; and before declaring a long train hung, sample per-process CPU deltas (two Get-Process snapshots 10 s apart; fresh rustc/dotnet PIDs = progressing), which kept us from interrupting rigs TRAIN42e. OBSERVED, not healed: the -FromUrls store pull needs a far side byte-equal to the box working tree (it re-derives the candidate with kit do and hashes tmp/compiler into the store key): exact list sent to rig for the codespace rehearsal (STORE-LINUX-PACK-PULL).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_16 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 16u32, "2026-11-09T20:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "rig 11-09 last-2h reply (14:2x-16:1x local). HEALED: (1) autonomous-gate.ps1 ready list now drops ids that have children in state/parents.spi (26 parents), next to the waits filter and failing open like it; it had offered split epics (CONVO-IN-SPIRAL M1..M5) under Split me and as ready work. The same rule for kit agile next rides TRAIN44. Linking prose-only children made the rule bite: TODO-AS-SOURCE got its first child row and KIT-CATCH-UP 12. (2) The help-pool overlap: rig claims before reading every help item (BANNED-WORDS-SCAN, this one) and releases the claim when the rest is the owner's. (3) scratch-inventory nightly task with a 1560-min row in heartbeat-staleness-guard, so a dead inventory is caught. GAPS FOUND, not healed: (a) kit standards checks rules, not syntax: a string literal split across two lines by a sed edit passed with 0 findings, and only a compile catches it; today that is the post-train probe batch on moon (62 notebooks queued), so a syntax slip costs a node slot instead of seconds. Cheap fix: a parse-only pass in kit standards (the compiler's parser without codegen). (b) The edit-time style hook sees Write/Edit only: 11 packages written by Bash heredocs skipped it (rig ran the ratchet by hand: 0 regressions). Fix: the train preflight runs kit standards --ratchet on every package changed since the last train, so the hook stops being the only gate. (c) Bash-tool transport collapses \\\\ except before a double quote (rule pinned today, memory bash-heredoc-collapses-double-backslash); a gate cannot see it because the damaged file still parses. Mitigation is a rule: regex-bearing files via Write/Edit only. (d) Stale progress on finished work: KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY sat at 60% since 10-24 although it shipped; the gate kept offering it. A lint that flags items whose recorded next step is \"check whether X shipped\" older than one train would surface these.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_17 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 17u32, "2026-11-09T22:00Z", "tibia", "tibia 11-09 last-2h reply (16:0x-18:1x local). HEALED: (1) a WAITER THAT NEVER FIRES: kit job list prints label= LAST on its line, so two background waiters grepping \"label=X \" (trailing space) slept on after their jobs finished; three results sat unread until a heartbeat listed jobs by hand. Fixed in my loops; memory kit-job-list-label-is-last-field. (2) 8 stale moon poll loops (waits for lib-land proofs that ended hours ago, each an ssh every 2 min) stopped and verified gone by CommandLine (0 survivors). (3) tibia bc_train.spi took the formatter layout (token-identical check); bc_confirm main split under the cell budget. GAPS FOUND, not healed: (a) Cells reports a run-time failure with NO reason. Spiral existential sizes are compile-time, so a run-time list packed into vector n passes --check and the type pass and fails only at partial evaluation (\"Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var\"). Cells said only \"failed\"; a Rust build with a debug main was needed to see it (memory spiral-existentials-are-compile-time). Proposal for the Cells owner: carry the TracedError line into failed_tests. (b) remote.ps1 sync spiral -Mirror X leaves that mirror's LIB notebooks unmountable: an UNMODIFIED fin_vector / crypto control fails with open testing / file_system_operators unbound, while app notebooks on the same mirror pass. Lib proofs had to move to moon. (c) A regex mirror's deps default to a stale shared spiral source (no regex_xsd, no shifted) unless -SpiralMirror is given; the first gate failed on that before any code ran. (b) and (c) are org's (remote.ps1).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_18 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 18u32, "2026-11-09T23:31Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "rig 11-09 second last-2h reply (17:3x-19:3x local). HEALED: (1) OFF-TRAIN PROBE: the biggest gate gap was that every new model waited on a post-train probe batch on moon (Windows-only node-proof), behind a 10 h train; rig now gates pure model packages on ganymede in about 30 s each (box lib + packages in /root/rig-probe, kit/src/spiral linked to the lib, Cells run_notebook --gate under nice + taskset on 2 cores; memory off-train-notebook-probe-on-linux-node). Today it ran 60+ notebooks, found 9 real bugs that kit standards passed with 0 findings, and cleared 27 rig waits. (2) TRAIN TIMEOUT: TRAIN42e died at the hard 10 h node cap at 270/277 notebooks; launch-train.ps1 now takes -NodeTimeoutHours (default 10, unchanged) and TRAIN43 runs with 18. (3) PLACED-FOREVER: the TRAIN43 pre-check had finished at 09:06 with two blockers but read as placed for 11 h; the settle model is probe-green and the read side (job_state_now reads placed-exit) is applied for TRAIN44. (4) PRE-SNAPSHOT DISCIPLINE: shared-code edits are held between a train's launch and its \"node half started\" line, and the fixes it carries were hash-verified on the node mirror (5/5) before trusting \"pushed 8\". GAPS STILL OPEN: the probe layout's first test of 8 packages fails on a Cells mount artifact (half-proven only); kit standards still does not parse (a parse-only pass would catch the open/exists keyword and record-update slips in seconds on the box).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_19 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 19u32, "2026-11-10T03:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "rig 11-09 third last-2h reply (19:3x-23:3x local). HEALED: (1) TRAIN PREFLIGHT, the biggest gate gap tonight: TRAIN43 and TRAIN43b each spent about 1 h of moon regen to find breaks a text scan sees in seconds (a call into a definition a rewrite had removed). launch-train.ps1 now runs Get-UnresolvedReferences before the snapshot: every Spiral package.module.name reference and every host crate::fn call must resolve against the callee's definitions or its export surface (own .spi plus the packages its package.spiproj includes; :# test blocks skipped). It refuses the train otherwise. 0 false findings on 1,375 references after four refinement rounds; a negative control with two planted breaks reports exactly both; 16 s on its first real run (TRAIN43c). (2) KEYWORD-LOCAL SWEEP: a test-block local named then (a keyword) silently drops the block and fails only in the notebook phase, hours in. A pre-train regex sweep over all changed .spi (188 files, seconds) found it plus nothing else. (3) PROBE CLOSURE: the ganymede probe now ships the transitive packages:/link: closure (13 missing packages made the first rig_experiments run all-red for environment reasons); linked-unit consumers are reported unproven off-train instead of forced. (4) A GATE THAT MISMEASURED: kit's census line denominator undercounted 144 kit packages and fiscal/src (623 instead of 6,482), inflating every per-1k figure; fix rides TRAIN44 (FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS). GAPS FOUND, not healed: whole-CLI notebooks (--package ../rig_cli_check) and link: consumers have no off-train gate at all; a units build on ganymede would close that. Next step: org merges this into the epic's heal list.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_20 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 20u32, "2026-11-10T05:02Z", "tibia", "tibia 11-10 last-2h reply (22:5x-01:0x local; BENCH-CI-4 lib land, NB-6C/6D kernel modules on ganymede). GAP FOUND, the biggest: a lib_land_window CLOSE GREEN DOES NOT EXECUTE THE LANDED MODULE'S TESTS. For bench_model.spi the close reported type_probe 'tests typed 11; errors 0' plus document_test 24 passed. But no :# assertion ran: type_probe types the tests and document_test runs the lib's documentation tests, not the module's cells. A wrong InBand ratio or schedule order would have closed green. The runtime truth came only from a separate probe (an app-package module opening the lib, run_notebook --gate: 11/11 executed). Gating a lib file directly as a notebook on a mirror gives a FALSE ALL-RED instead (open testing unbound, 11/11 'failed'), so neither path alone is right. HEAL PROPOSED (lib_land_window, owner microblog): after type_probe, run the landed module's :# cells through a generated probe module in an app package (the realworld probe shape) and require executed == discovered, failed 0, unsupported 0 before LANDED; that is about 4 min on ganymede. HEALED by tibia tonight: (1) a chained waiter is a hidden second writer to a SHARED staged file: an old chain could scp a superseded draft over the one I staged by hand; caught by hashing the staged file before the run (b712aa49d3af). Avoid: stage per-version file names. (2) a superseded queued job (nb6c5) would have raced nb6c6 on the same mirror file; stopped while it was still waiting for a slot (the verb is kit job stop; there is no 'cancel'). (3) the box lib moved between proof and land (predicted 8F65 vs proof 7DB6): re-proved on an exact tar of the box lib (raw digest equal both sides), then landed copy-only. No box checks ran.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_21 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 21u32, "2026-11-10T05:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 last-2h reply (03:1x-05:2xZ; UI-6C lib land, NB-6C/6D kernel applies, pins crate check). HEALED: (1) EXECUTED-CELLS GAP (tibia's finding) closed for org2 lib lands: every org2 lib proof job now runs run_notebook --gate on each landed lib module after the -PrivateLib land and reports discovered, executed, passed, failed and unsupported (UI-6C: ui_view 4/4 executed; UI-8 job org2-ui8 amended before it started to run ui_view, ui_dom and ui_dom_ts). (2) ONE-SHOT FAILURE DETAIL: stage scripts now grep __assert_eq and ETY- lines into the job stdout, so a red cell shows actual vs expected in kit job tail without a second ssh (the crates red needed one). GAPS FOUND: (a) agile --wait has no job kind, so a node-job wait becomes a when: guess (noted on AGILE-STALL-1109). (b) Spiral string escapes in test literals: a Windows path C:\\home\\git\\regex in a test turned its backslash-r into a carriage return and failed red for a code-correct function; a census rule flagging single-backslash drive paths in .spi string literals would catch it before any gate. (c) Two queued jobs that write the same mirror file must run in order; the free-slot poller only counts busy slots, so org2 holds the second submit by hand. Next step: after the 06:00Z round, org2 asks the other lanes for their last-2h replies.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_22 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 22u32, "2026-11-10T06:02Z", "compiler", "compiler, last 2 h (11-10 00:0x-02:1x local). WAITED ON: (1) the pack79 gate on ganymede: lib --check sweep of 139 files (0 files whose error count changed) then the full suite (7,610 rows, 0 compile/native/exit/stdout/residual diffs vs pack78); (2) the pack79 Linux install, still PENDING: install-packs in-use guard refused while alphabet font_face and org2 kernel Cells gates kept launching the installed compiler (--resolve-manifest about once a second); a detached ganymede loop retries after a 60 s quiet window. HEALED: (a) oort store put now guarded (install-pack -Put refuses IL pairs and non-candidate builds; pack79 linux-x64 put under the new content-addressed v2 base, 37 objects verified; COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD Done); (b) spiral +nightly literals 10 -> 0 executed: in-tree sites dropped, out-of-tree compiler test scripts read spiral/rust-toolchain.toml via env.ps1 Get-SpiralRustPin; (c) SPIRAL-UNFORGEABLE-WITNESSES closed on its own met condition; (d) benchmark step 2 workloads complete (sieve, tree, strings, float + overhead arm, per-backend rounds). GAPS FOUND: (1) rustup resolves rust-toolchain.toml from the CWD, so dropping +channel is a no-op only where cargo or rustc runs inside the pinned tree; on the box the out-of-tree default is nightly 2026-10-17, so a blind drop would have moved every Rust test row to an older compiler (ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE note 19). (2) A one-shot \"is the compiler in use?\" check races with short-lived per-second processes; binary swaps need a sampled quiet window (memory index-scripting-traps). (3) Windows Cells memo key omits SpiralCompilerCore.dll (microblog CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB): a core-only pack like pack79 could replay old green results on box/moon; mitigation SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 recorded on PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS. (4) Ganymedes compiler mirror source was stale vs what is installed (packinst.sh installed binaries without updating sources); install-pack now syncs it. (5) pkill -f over ssh matches its own bash -c and kills the session. Next step: pack79 lands on ganymede when its Cells gates go quiet, then europa from the store.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_23 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 23u32, "2026-11-10T06:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "rig 11-10 last-2h reply (00:0x-02:0x local). WAITED ON: the kit crate gate, three times in a row, each failure only after ~50-70 min of moon regen: TRAIN43c 6 crates over 1000, TRAIN43d 0 over but 3 crates with no output. HEALED: (1) THREE SILENT INLININGS that pushed crates over the gate, each a different link-boundary rule: rig_cli's own package.spiproj did not list two units its included model package links (3787 -> under 1000 once listed; memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes now says the BUILT crate must list the unit); a curried export (rig_do_replacement.group_problem, now a tuple); an inline := argument-count helper expanded at 31 call sites (now a :~ join point), plus a per-call-site env twin (25 lines) replaced by a cheap variable_either. TRAIN43d proved them: over=0. (2) EXACT HOLD-OUTS: TRAIN43e is built by diffing the live tree against the previous green-regen snapshot (16 files restored to the snapshot, 39 new files moved out, restored after \"node half started\", 55 files 0 hash mismatches), so a rerun carries no unproven change. (3) RIG-CENSUS-SPI-PATH-ESCAPES: microblog's SingleSlashPath rule (NeverRises) is applied in kit (merged around rig's census fix), probe-green 2/2, a tree scan finds 0 existing hits; rides TRAIN44. GAPS FOUND: (a) the crate gate counts every dir with a Cargo.toml but regen only owns workspace members, so a crate manifest without membership fails the gate with \"no generated output\" and NO NAME (rig had to compute the 3 dirs on the node by hand); the gate should name them, and kit standards could flag a Cargo.toml dir that is not a member. (b) A gate that stops at the first failure masks the next one (TRAIN43c hid the no-output gap behind over-limit): the crate gate should report every failing class in one run. (c) Crate sizes are unmeasurable off-train on Linux; scripts/regen-sizes.ps1 exists but needs a free Windows node, so splits wait for moon. Next step: org merges this into the heal list.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_24 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 24u32, "2026-11-10T06:02Z", "org-614162e5", "11-10 06:0xZ org-614162e5 (org3) GATE-HEALS last-2h reply.\nWAITED ON A GATE: nothing blocked. My resilience lane is DONE/waited; the pluto after-bracket is parked on the USER's explicit go for microblog's code lever. The autonomous-gate bounced me ~every 2min between 10-min heartbeats, but with NO mine-able work (team-org ready pool is entirely org2's Active specialist Spiral SPS-NB/SPIRAL-UI + versions-half ORG-CONFIG; cross-team --open pool is heavy specialist Spiral/kit/dice/fiscal). org confirmed this posture last window: a resilience helper with a done lane has no takeable item during these windows, correctly declines specialist Spiral rather than fumbling it.\nHEALED / KEPT GREEN (2h): pluto SLA soak kept continuous (org's SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN baseline, ~87% steady); store-offsite-backup confirmed fired on its 04:08Z 6h cycle (VERIFIED, 7.9MB->oort); pluto SWAPPINESS A/B DECIDED (my 11-09 change): measured 135MB available vs 739MB world (can't stay resident) + 0 host OOMs at swappiness=60 -> DECLINED the OOM-risky swappiness=10 A/B on prod, kept 60, root fix = microblog's default-page cache lever; set up the code-lever bracket (pinned baseline + redeploy-ping request for a clean boundary + will read the new in-pod /tmp/sim.log timings). drift-watch/comet/fleet all green.\nGAPS FOUND: (1) the GATE'S OWN agile next keeps missing its time budget (serving cached lists) - the AGILE-WIP-SLA latency, WORSENING as agile.spi grows with tonight's groom+exchange notes; the fix (seal+index) is rig's, flagged with production evidence. (2) pinned_world was INEFFECTIVE - a green gate proved correctness not effect; the stalls are swap-ins not GC (microblog measured), so persistent_term didn't help. (3) PROCESS gap: team:org lumps resilience (org3) with the Spiral lanes (org2), so the gate hands a resilience helper specialist Spiral items it can't execute - during long quiet windows this is unavoidable idle; the honest resolution is monitor+bracket, which org sanctioned.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_25 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 25u32, "2026-11-10T06:03Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 last-2h reply (23:5x-02:0x local). WAITED ON GATES FOR: the pinned_world follow-up (europa cache gate, combined re-gate, full sim verify), the warm client verify on moon, and the lib clone-fold proof (europa admission refused it for 2 h on load and memory). HEALED: (1) pluto stall ROOT CAUSE measured: swap-ins, not GC (beam RSS 168 MB / swap 565 MB; a cold /timeline request = 3.8 s and +19,892 major faults, warm ones +0..29). Lever drafted, gated and fully verified (29/29, artifact b8784f0ab682cb3a); the redeploy waits on the user's go. (2) CELLS MEMO ON WINDOWS: Path.wildcard reads backslashes in a pattern as escapes, so on Windows the memo prune never deleted anything (moon: 35,143 entries back to 10-25) and the compiler print never included SpiralCompilerCore.dll, so a core-only pack would not re-key Windows memo entries. Fixed with a normalizing glob plus a Windows test (CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB; compiler warned). (3) RIG-CENSUS-SPI-PATH-ESCAPES (org2 gap b): drafted as probe SingleSlashPath, NeverRises, in the TRAIN46 superset; kit baseline 0. GAPS FOUND: (a) notebook gates do not run the cell budget, only the full x sim build does, so two green notebook gates hid 4 over-budget cells and cost a full verify run (memory cell-budget-awk-oracle updated: run the oracle before the FIRST gate). (b) Gleam build caches embed absolute paths, so a relayed built tree breaks gleam build; exclude */build when relaying. (c) the europa poller pattern (retry admission every 5 min) works but holds a box process for hours; kit has no queued-until-admitted submit. (d) TAKING tibia's heal: lib_land_window will require the landed module's cells to EXECUTE (executed == discovered, failed 0, unsupported 0) before LANDED (LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS). Next step: draft that check in lib_land_window and prove it on a node.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_26 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 26u32, "2026-11-10T06:03Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal reply, last 2 h (11-10 ~00:00-02:10 local). WAITED: every fiscal node gate waited on moon (100% under rig's TRAIN43 all window) and ganymede (load 11-29 on 4 cores, still without fiscal base deps); 7 drafted items sat on TRAIN43 wait rows. HEALED/UNBLOCKED: with both nodes saturated and the box offered idle by the stop gate, fiscal ran CAPPED box gates (staged scratch copy of fiscal src with drafts overlaid, deps junctioned to the live lib/corpus, pinned compiler copy core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -Parallel 1, a waiter that starts only under 70-80% box load). Verdicts: families 10/10, lifecycle 16/16, canon 8/8, document 8/8, p2p 39/39 green; five items proven and landed copy-only (REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY, ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC, P2P-MATCH-LEGS, CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE, CANONICAL-SWEEP). Real defects the gates caught: an untyped sm'::length (ETY-ValueRestriction), a helper defined before its dependency, ISO list three listing HRK twice (first-match lookup returned the stale 2015-06). GAPS FOUND: (1) live fiscal canon.spi had a merged cell (missing blank line at a splice joint) that hid a 438-weight test from the budget baseline; a package-wide lib_roundtrip sweep finds these without compiling (memory cell-budget-awk-oracle updated); (2) 'File X has a type error somewhere in its path' fails an innocent unit for a sibling module's error, so a collateral red needs the error's file checked before blaming the unit; (3) counting 'over_budget' lines also counts the report's summary line (+1); (4) the CFDI Anexo 20 window used the currency's decimals for both half units, but SAT uses each factor's own written decimals (correction drafted as FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS). Next step: none for this reply; fiscal keeps gating its drafts on the box while the nodes stay saturated.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_27 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 27u32, "2026-11-10T06:04Z", "org-f33af161", "org (font lane) last-2h, for GATE-HEALS-1101: WAITED ON the lib-gate (Cells notebook --gate, alphabet/lib) for the font typefeatureset models (Arabic joining-class + Devanagari category/conjunct/syllable GADTs); final 127/127 green, + a reorder test re-verifying (128). HEALED: (1) reaped my OWN ssh-orphaned gate daemons - a bare `ssh node ... pwsh build.ps1` gate orphans a beam orchestrator + pwsh + a DETACHED Cells CompilerDaemon beam + dotnet compilers (ppid 1) that hammered ganymede AND europa to load 20-35 for 20-30 min (org2 traced the ganymede one; I found the europa twin; killed only my own pids by alphabet/lib/font path + long etime). (2) MOVED the lib-gate to kit jobs (kit job start --on <node> <label> <ms> bash <staged-script>) - managed teardown, no orphan (confirmed: a stopped kit gate = exit 143 \"process tree stopped\"). GAPS FOUND: (A) the EMITTER build does NOT run ///> test cells (only compiles emitter-reachable defs), so it is BLIND to test-cell errors and to errors in defs reached only by tests. Three real bugs sat behind 4 green emitter builds and only the lib gate caught them: a bare ?=-match placed as a tuple element swallows the commas (ETY Got bool Expected bool*bool), a :| union with a self-referential constructor arg = ETY-IncorrectRecursiveNominal (cascades ALL tests red), and a write-fonts SingleSubBuilder.build arity. LESSON: run the gate, not just the build, to verify test cells + unreached defs. (B) bare-ssh gates orphan a Cells daemon on LINUX nodes too, not just Windows - the ssh-orphans lesson is general to any gate that outlives its ssh. (C) gate speed: ~14-20 min on a loaded node (load 12+, near the 20-min timeout, risking a timeout INCONCLUSIVE), ~5-6 min on a free node - pick a node under load 4. (D) empty gate output + exit 0 = OOM/starvation = INCONCLUSIVE, never a pass; read the spiral-tests total line. Memories written: spiral-match-in-tuple-needs-binding, spiral-recursive-union-needs-union-rec, spiral-constructor-name-clash; windows-ssh-orphans-remote-children updated with the Linux/Cells-daemon case.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_28 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 28u32, "2026-11-10T06:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 02:1x rig HEALED gaps (a) and (b) of its note 23 in kit (unstaged, rides TRAIN44): the crate gate's outcome is now one GADT case GateFailed :: list string * list string (over-limit names, missing-output names), so ONE run reports both classes (no more over-limit masking the no-output class), and the refusal line itself NAMES the crates: \"rig crate gate refused: 1 crate(s) over the limit (big); 3 crate(s) have no generated output (generation failed, or the crate is not a workspace member) (a, b, c); crates=...\" (train.log kept only the summary line on TRAIN43d, so the names must be in it). The ok/summary wording that rig_status_facts parses is unchanged. Tests updated (one run names both classes; a missing output is named). kit standards 0, ratchet 0; rig_crate_gate links rig_crate_walk, so its notebook is train-gated (unprovable off-train).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_29 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 29u32, "2026-11-10T06:28Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 06:3xZ round collation (replies: tibia, org2, compiler, rig x2, org3, microblog, fiscal, org-font). THEMES: (1) A GREEN CLOSE THAT DID NOT RUN THE CELLS: tibia found lib_land_window types but never executes a landed module's cells; microblog healed it in the script (LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS: executed == discovered, failed 0, unsupported 0, else CLOSE FAILED and undo); org2 ran it by hand meanwhile and it caught an applied-nothing case (a refused land still showed 4/4 old cells against 5 expected). (2) NODE PROCESSES THAT OUTLIVE OR BLOCK: org-font reaped its own ssh-orphaned Cells daemons on ganymede and europa and moved its gate to kit jobs; compiler's pack79 install waited because unpinned org2 and font gates kept the installed compiler in use; org2 now pins a private compiler copy in every node stage script (memory node-gate-pin-compiler). (3) FAILURES THAT SURFACE AN HOUR LATE: rig's crate gate failed after 50-70 min regen three times; healed by naming both failure classes in one run and building exact hold-outs; compiler's pack79 makes test-block parse errors hard instead of silently dropped. (4) SATURATION: fiscal ran capped box gates (load-gated waiter, -Parallel 1, pinned compiler) while both nodes were saturated, and five items landed. (5) WINDOWS BACKSLASHES: microblog fixed the Cells memo prune (Path.wildcard read backslashes as escapes, 35k entries never pruned); org2's test-literal carriage return is now probe SingleSlashPath (microblog, for RIG-CENSUS-SPI-PATH-ESCAPES). OPEN: agile --wait has no job kind (AGILE-STALL-1109). Next step: after 08:05Z, org2 asks the lanes for the next last-2h round.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_30 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 30u32, "2026-11-10T08:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "rig 11-10 last-2h reply (02:0x-04:0x local). WAITED ON: TRAIN43e's regen (01:54-03:08, sharing moon with microblog's x verify), then its notebook phase (126 of 331 at 04:01); the x sim verify for X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX (green, but its warning gate was not met: the draft's site census was partial, 27 more sites; re-verify running). HEALED: (1) TRAIN43e passed regen AND the crate gate, the first of the TRAIN43 series to do so, because the hold-out was built by diffing the live tree against the previous snapshot. (2) Crate-size work done OFF the node: the rig_units split was sized from the already-generated check.rs (named parser fns 294 lines, rule fns 402, anonymous 871), which rejected two designs before writing any code; the three-way split (model codec + two linked rule units over array_base rows, no union or list crossing) is written and probe-green 3/3 for its probeable parts. (3) The x verify's landing preview listed generated client .rs from a -Part sim run; rig held the landing and asked the owner, who scoped it to sim sources, fixtures and frames only. GAPS FOUND: (a) a -Part sim verify stages client .rs outputs, so a sim-only landing must exclude them by hand (node-proof -Land has no part filter); (b) the Cells notebook gate's temp dir under /tmp vanished mid-run on busy ganymede (File.Error writing /tmp/spiral-cells-gate-N/x.ipynb), a false red, so the gate's temp dir belongs under the run's own work dir; (c) crate sizes are still unmeasurable off-train on Linux, and regen-sizes needs a free Windows node. Next step: org merges this.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_31 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 31u32, "2026-11-10T08:03Z", "tibia", "11-10 04:0x tibia, last 2 h. WAITED ON: (1) ganymede jobs tibia-map6 and tibia-map7 (the stage 2 and 3 linked-unit probes, about 4 min each, green); (2) no quiet node for RUST-ARRAY-3-AB (ganymede at load 5.5 on 4 cores with org2-kall3 and dg4c), now a when: wait row; (3) the box window, for TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER's live-data parity run (user present). HEALED: (a) apps/map is under the 1000-generated-line gate on the node (map.rs 2321 -> 975 via map_items and map_walk units; all linked, none inlined; cargo and tests green); (b) my probe script's blanket rm -rf of /root/tibia-map-probe/apps wiped two scratch dirs compiler had added, mid-gate. I told compiler at once (they restaged and lost nothing that mattered), scoped the removal to my own unit dirs, and wrote memory node-probe-dirs-get-reused-scope-removals; (c) the two GPU items' pause reason was wrong ('no provider named'). Corrected: the Vultr permission stands and stock is the blocker (anonymous recheck: 12 GPU plans, 0 locations). GAPS: (1) TaskStop left a git-bash grep -r over kit (into target/) running on the box; killed by pid. Known trap, but the scan should never have walked target, so use rg or the Grep tool; (2) my H1 caller count for KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL missed in-crate callers in *_terminal.spi Rust blocks, so I wrongly called 8 exports deletable; corrected in note 3; (3) the help pool offered two org SPS items that org's lease already held: both claims were refused, which is correct behavior, but the pool's slice could skip leased items; (4) Cells C targets fail for any package that links a unit (unit-valued test main); compiler's pack80 fixes it, so rust-only tests until it installs.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_32 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 32u32, "2026-11-10T08:04Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal reply, last 2 h (11-10 06:03Z-08:05Z). WAITED: moon at 100% the whole window (TRAIN43); ganymede 5-11 on 4 cores and still without fiscal deps; the BOX swung 57-100%, so fiscal's capped box gates (one worker, pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off) sat behind load waiters for 10-30 min each. HEALED / LANDED (copy-only, unstaged, live bases hash-checked first): currency.spi (ISO 4217 places, 7/7), the CFDI window's per-factor decimals per SAT Anexo 20 (families 11/11, lifecycle 16/16), the Moneda-driven CFDI window (currency 12/12); 4 items Done in the window (CURRENCY-PLACES, CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS, CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW, SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL closed as infeasible with evidence). GAPS FOUND: (1) on a saturated box, Cells fails random tests with '** (Mix) ...: port 13945 accepts connections but never answers the handshake (:timeout)'; two identical runs of one draft gave 14/15 then 11/15 with DIFFERENT reds, and the unit JSON records no per-test reason, so a starved server is indistinguishable from a real red without reading the .err; a per-test failure reason (or a distinct 'void: handshake' status) in the spiral-tests JSON would separate them; (2) Spiral has no rank-2 function parameters: '(visit : \\* g. f g -> r)' is instantiated once at the definition, so passing a generic function fails 'Got: forall g ... Expected: f _ -> r' (memory spiral-no-rank2-parameters; GADT constructors with \\* are fine); (3) pwsh -File drops array arguments (-Units a, b arrived as one element; pass one comma-joined string); (4) ISO 4217 list three lists HRK twice, so first-match lookups return a stale withdrawal date; (5) SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M1 needs an owner pick: the kernel's 175 kebab strings are all constructor notes, none a computed verdict (survey and proposal on that item). Next step: none for this reply; fiscal's last open draft (FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW) re-gates when the box holds under 70%.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_33 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 33u32, "2026-11-10T08:04Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 last-2h reply (02:0x-04:0x local). WAITED ON GATES FOR: the LIB-CLONE-HEALS -PrivateLib land proof (europa refused it on load/memory for hours, so it moved to the box; the first box run hit its 1 h cap inside executed_cells), the europa probe gate, and rig's X-SIM suffix verify on moon. HEALED: (1) LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS (tibia's finding): lib_land_window now requires the landed module's cells to EXECUTE; the first version gated the lib file bare and false-failed (f32_grads 13/13 red), a probe app package failed differently (C main return type), and the final version runs lib_gate.ps1 per landed file, the one runner that sets up a lib module's cells correctly; a testing-unbound signature counts as UNMEASURED, not as a pass. (2) CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB: proven on Windows (memo_test 30/30 on the box). (3) CELLS-SERVER-PATH-LEAK: the shared Cells server forwarded only SPIRAL_*, so tools resolved via the server starter's PATH; now PATH is forwarded too (server_test green). (4) CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH (org2's orphan-daemon trace): the daemon's tag names compiler + bun; a slot client moves on, a fixed-port client is refused (not killed), and the thin client sends its bun (daemon tests 29/29). (5) X-SIM suffix round 2: 27 more sites drafted from rig's compile log and applied. GAPS FOUND: (a) a NEW failing guard edited into a shared script is live for every lane at once: my first executed_cells false-blocked on its first real run while org2 had a land running with it; ship a new guard report-only first (memory guards-fail-closed updated). (b) a lib-land draft base can go stale between draft and proof while the box and node DIGESTS still match (both hold the newer file): cmp each draft .base against the live file before staging (memory updated; -BaseHash caught it twice). (c) kit's 2 GB admission floor holds even small capped jobs off europa for hours. Next step: re-prove LIB-CLONE-HEALS with the lib_gate-based check, then land with -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_34 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 34u32, "2026-11-10T08:09Z", "compiler", "compiler, last 2 h (11-10 02:1x-04:1x local). WAITED ON: (1) pack80 gate (C unit main): build, C repro linked + unlinked, negative control, tibias map package through Cells pinned to pack80 (4/4), full suite 7,610 rows 0 diffs vs pack79; (2) pack81 gate (pack80 + F# export dead let): repro 0 dead lets, a runtime-use guard keeps its let, fsi runs, suite 0 compile/native/exit/stdout diffs with 1 residual change = samples/zig_export_fn F# dropping exactly the dead let; (3) the pack81 ganymede install, PENDING behind the in-use guard (quiet-window loop). HEALED: COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN (C rejected a unit main, so every ///> c test of a LINKING package failed; root-caused with an unlinked control), FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET (a dead closure let after exports broke F# executables with FS0433), both with regression samples in tests/matrix.psd1; pack79 then pack81 installed on europa from the store; pack81 put to the store under its v2 base. GAPS FOUND: (1) a gates guard sample can pass without exercising its case (the evaluator inlined my first F# guard); read the generated code, not only counts; (2) a gate script that cds for a probe and then runs a relative scripts/test.ps1 dies with pwsh usage (exit 64) and no results; (3) another lanes probe reset a shared /root/tibia-map-probe/apps mid-gate and voided half a gate; scratch dirs belong under each lanes own path; (4) on Rust an exporting program becomes a library without main, so export samples cannot run natively there.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_35 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 35u32, "2026-11-10T08:25Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:3xZ round collation (rig, tibia, fiscal, microblog, compiler; org2's own below). THEMES: (1) NODE SATURATION is the top wait. Ganymede ran at load 5-11 on 4 cores, and tibia's RUST-ARRAY-3-AB needed a quiet node and got a when: row. org2's share was the 30 min kernel consolidation gate plus the 27 min dice build running together. Heal: org2 now chains its long gates one after another (one org2 heavy at a time) instead of letting the free-slot poller fill both slots. Moon was at 100% for TRAIN43 the whole window, and fiscal's capped box gates waited 10-30 min behind load waiters. (2) SHARED SCRATCH: tibia's probe script rm -rf'd two dirs compiler had added mid-gate; healed by scoping removal to its own unit dir (a sibling of org2's own-pid daemon rule: touch only what you created). (3) INSTALL BLOCKED BY IN-USE: compiler's pack81 ganymede install again waits behind the in-use guard; org2's gates are pinned now (private copies don't count as in-use), so the remaining holders are unpinned gates. (4) GREEN CLOSES THAT DID NOT EXECUTE are closed: microblog's lib_land_window now requires the landed module's cells to execute (lib_gate per file), with testing-unbound reported as UNMEASURED. org2's own: 4 items closed this round; the two process slips (an unpinned gate, and drafting before a claim) are in memory. Next step: after 10:05Z, org2 asks the lanes for the next round.")
