inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_1 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:01Z", "main", "main 18:0x from resilience. DoD: kit's proof/sync path runs it by default and refuses to ship a draft that fails, in under 10 s for a typical change.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_2 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:00Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 groom (AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT): parent epic GATE-HEALS-1101. It was this item's only dep, which hid the item from agile next because an epic finishes after its children; parents are named in notes, deps are for real ordering only.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_3 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T20:41Z", "kit", "11-04 22:0x kit: FIRST SLICE BUILT (unstaged): `kit lint precheck <file.spi>...` (new linked crate kit_lint_precheck, routed through kit lint's own LintPrecheck case, so kit_cli (995) is untouched). Pure text checks, milliseconds per file: WidthOver (any line > 120) and OpenString (a line with an odd number of unescaped quotes outside host macros, a quote char literal and /// headers, i.e. a string literal broken across lines: exactly the \"\\\\n written through a heredoc becomes a real newline\" trap that hit kit 3 times on 11-04, once only caught by grep before a train). Prints one \"file:row: ...\" line per finding and \"kit lint precheck ok|refused files=N findings=M\", exit 1 on any finding. Tests: escaped quotes + a quote char are fine, a split string is 2 findings, a host-macro line is skipped, a 141-wide line. europa --check ok with bodies (precheck + lint cli); box notebooks kit-precheck-tests. NEXT slices: the parse check (compiler --check is ~20-60 s, so seconds-long needs the compiler server), kit standards on touched packages, the cell budget, and wiring into remote.ps1 sync as a default refusal.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_4 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T20:52Z", "kit", "11-04 22:3x kit: first slice PROVEN on the box: kit_lint_precheck precheck.spi 1/1 (escaped quotes + a quote char clean; a string split across two lines = 2 OpenString findings; a host-macro line skipped; a 141-wide line = WidthOver) and kit_lint_cli cli.spi 1/1 (precheck routes to LintPrecheck). The first run was RED on a rustc recursion limit, not on logic: sm'.replicate 120 \"x\" with a literal count unrolled into 120 nested format! calls (memory spiral-constant-replicate-unrolls); the fixture is now built from 10-char pieces. Ships with the next train after TRAIN23.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_5 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T22:29Z", "kit", "11-04 18:5x kit: a third precheck from today's failures (unstaged): `kit lint precheck` also takes Cargo.toml paths and refuses a crate whose output is build.rs, main.rs or lib.rs (\"output build.rs is a name Cargo reserves in a crate root (build.rs = build script); rename the module\"). TRAIN23 died 70 min into regen on exactly that (kit_run_build's module was named build); now it fails in milliseconds before any node run. Test a_crate_output_named_like_a_cargo_file_is_refused (build.rs refused, builder.rs fine). europa --check ok with bodies; box notebook kit-precheck-tests3.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_6 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T22:34Z", "kit", "11-04 18:4x kit: the reserved-output precheck is PROVEN on the box (kit-precheck-tests3 2/2: build.rs refused, builder.rs fine). Separately, node size run kit-size-post25 caught agile_task_listing at 1015 generated lines (OVER) after today's list_root change, which built the whole argument list just to read one value; list_root now calls a new kit_agile_list_root export in the linked kit_agile_list_args crate (argument_owned 1i32, the HEAD reader). europa --check ok on both; the re-size (kit-size-listing) is pending on the node. The other 6 sized fine: note_listing 832, task_inspection 679, lint_cli 211, lint_precheck 506, job_entry 421, kit_process 70.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_7 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T22:43Z", "kit", "11-04 18:4x kit: re-size GREEN on the node (kit-size-listing2): agile_task_listing 1015 -> 936, kit_agile_list_args 213. Every crate changed since TRAIN25's snapshot now sizes under 1000; the next train carries them.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_8 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T23:04Z", "kit", "11-04 19:0x kit: TRAIN25 RED at the crate gate on exactly the crate kit-size-post25 had already flagged: agile_task_listing task_listing.rs 1015 OVER (crates=337 over=1). Everything else passed: regen published 274 changed owners, 63 unchanged. The fix was already in the tree and node-sized (listing 936, kit_agile_list_args 295 with the typed root reader, kit_remote_status 996 = only 4 lines of headroom; split it before adding anything). TRAIN26 launched at 19:04 (job-1793833466593-kit-TRAIN26-node, same command as TRAIN25 reusing the train25 mirror; node at 100% load with 4 other jobs, 11.1 GB free). It carries everything since TRAIN25's snapshot (all kit's, all sized): listing/args fix, kit_process --timeout-ms, the reserved-output precheck, lease_corpus, the S10 re-lease fix, stop_cli checks, and the remote-status disk floor. It is the first train through the launcher's new 5 GB floor.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_9 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 9u32, "2026-11-05T00:14Z", "kit", "11-04 20:1x kit: TRAIN26 PAST THE GATE on the node: 20:09:20 regen ok (275 changed owners published, 62 unchanged, 0 errors), 20:09:22 crate gate ok (crates=337 over=0 limit=1000). First train today past regen + gate (TRAIN22 gate x3 crates, TRAIN23 build.rs, TRAIN24 disk full, TRAIN25 gate x1). Every crate it carries had been node-sized first. Now in the candidate phase (debug build of kit-cli and kit-dev); notebooks and release follow, so the install lands after 21:00 (pending).")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_10 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 10u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "kit", "11-04 22:1x kit (groom): TRAIN26 still PENDING on the node at 22:10: notebook phase 147/205 done, 4 RED so far, none in packages kit changed tonight: agile_task_notes notes_cli (agile_add_lands_a_groomed_item_in_one_call, cell exited 1; file unchanged since 10-25), command_spec_domain direct_verbs (shared_lines_print_once, cell exited 1; TRAIN26's 19:04 snapshot predates kit's 19:38 edit+exact revert), kit_bundle_manifest (archive_permissions_keep_executable_and_readonly_intent) and kit_do_verbs (2 tests), both \"File main has a type error\", both files last changed 11-04 00:31. If they stay red, TRAIN26 ends red and does not install. NEXT session: diagnose these four before any install or TRAIN27.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_11 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 11u32, "2026-11-05T05:27Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 01:2x kit: WIRING DRAFTED, not applied: launch-train.ps1 is the live launcher of TRAIN27 (memory never-patch-running-launcher). Draft: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE\\scripts\\launch-train.ps1 (base 316F243DFCCE2529, CRLF kept). Before kit job start it lists the touched src/*.spi and Cargo.toml (git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all) and runs kit lint precheck on them. A 'refused' verdict throws in seconds with the findings, so no node train starts on a width-121 line, a split string or a crate output named build.rs. An installed kit without the verb prints 'precheck unavailable in the installed kit; skipped' instead of refusing. DRY RUN on the box against the live tree: 13 touched files, installed kit = skipped path (correct; the verb ships with TRAIN26/27's tree). APPLY after TRAIN27 ends (it also carries the S4 draft's 4 hunks on the same base). Left after that: the parse slice (needs the compiler server) and the cell budget slice.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_12 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 12u32, "2026-11-05T07:37Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:3x kit: WIRING APPLIED (unstaged) to scripts/launch-train.ps1 now that TRAIN27 has ended and no launcher runs: live was exactly the draft's base 316F243DFCCE2529, and the only difference is the 7-line precheck block before kit job start (live now BA23C6A309D51580, CRLF kept, PowerShell parse errors 0). The next train launch runs kit lint precheck on the touched src .spi/Cargo.toml and refuses on findings. With the installed kit (no precheck verb yet) it prints 'skipped', so TRAIN28 itself still launches; from the install that carries the verb onward it enforces. The S4 draft (base 316F) now needs a rebase onto BA23 before it applies.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_13 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 13u32, "2026-11-07T15:52Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers + GUARD from the 11-07 star exchange (TRAIN36 went red on a :# block with no ///> target line; TRAIN34 on ++# unbound in a cli_check test). NEXT STEP: extend the launch-train precheck with two notebook checks over the touched .spi files: (1) every :# test block is preceded by a ///> line unless the file has a static prelude; (2) a file under package ../kit_cli_check that uses ++# opens sm'_operators. Both refuse the launch with file:line. The scan already exists as a scratch script (72 touched notebooks, 0 findings on 11-06). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: precheck_finding union (UntargetedTest, CliOperatorsUnopened, LineWidth, Raw) with file and line fields; verdict union Clean or Refused.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_14 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 14u32, "2026-11-07T18:13Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: the launch precheck now EXCUSES rows on lines UNCHANGED SINCE HEAD (git diff -U0 HEAD hunks per tracked file), besides rows inside raw blocks; untracked files and changed lines are still checked. Reason: x and compiler mass edits touched about a thousand legacy files with one-line changes, so the whole-file check refused TRAIN37 on old width violations it never introduced. First use: TRAIN37 launch excused 262 raw-block rows and 90 unchanged-line rows across 183 touched files, 0 real. The guard plan (untargeted test blocks, cli_check files using ++# without sm operators) still stands; a manual scan before TRAIN37 found 0 of each.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_15 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 15u32, "2026-11-07T20:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, GUARD BUILT (unstaged, scripts/launch-train.ps1): the launch precheck now also refuses the two notebook mistakes that each cost a whole train (TRAIN34: ++# in a kit_cli_check test without sm operators; TRAIN36: a :# block without its own ///> target line), over the touched .spi files only, with file:line. Proof: a dry run over today's 162 touched notebooks finds 0 (matching the manual scans); a synthetic kit_cli_check file with both mistakes is refused with both findings while its targeted block passes. Together with the unchanged-since-HEAD excusal (this morning), a launch now refuses only on new problems. First live use: the TRAIN38 launch. Progress 75.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_16 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 16u32, "2026-11-07T23:57Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:1x kit, THIRD GUARD BUILT (unstaged, scripts/launch-train.ps1): a lock precheck. Found tonight: a Cargo dependency added to a crate (kit_agile_sprint_show gained agile-status-changes) without refreshing src/Cargo.lock made the node regen fail under --locked in probes r, s and t, after the notebooks had already passed (cannot update the lock file because --locked was passed). The launch now runs cargo metadata --offline --locked in src (seconds, no build) and throws lock precheck refused with cargo's first lines and the fix (cargo update --workspace --offline in src). Proof on the box: parse 0; the extracted precheck passes on the current tree (lock exit 0, plus 268 raw-block and 92 unchanged-since-HEAD rows excused); negative case with the lock moved aside gives exit 101, and the lock was restored byte-identical. Also seen tonight and still open for this item: a local named open (a keyword) left only a ParserErrors warning, so the notebook passed and the regen failed; the parse step of this item would catch it. waits on install: none (a launch script, live at the next launch).")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_17 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 17u32, "2026-11-07T23:57Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:1x kit: this item is live work, not held for an install; the lock guard is active at the next launch. NEXT STEP: a parse-only check of touched .spi files in the precheck.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_18 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 18u32, "2026-11-08T00:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:4x kit, FOURTH GUARD (scripts/launch-train.ps1): the ++# check now covers every touched .spi, not only kit_cli_check tests. Found tonight: kit_job_env/env_adopt.spi used ++# without :< sm'_operators; the notebooks of other packages passed and the node regen failed with ETY-UnboundVariable ++# (probe y), the same class that cost TRAIN34. The guard ignores ++# inside string literals and // lines. Measured before widening: 0 findings over the 192 touched .spi and 0 over all 1109 src .spi files, so no false positives today. Proof on the box: parse 0; a synthetic env_adopt-like text (a ++# use, one inside a string, one in a comment) is flagged once; with the open added it passes; the full extracted precheck passes on the current tree (lock exit 0). Live at the next launch. NEXT STEP: a parse-only check of touched .spi files.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_19 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 19u32, "2026-11-08T01:19Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 21:2x kit, FIFTH GUARD (scripts/launch-train.ps1): a keyword used as a local or parameter name. Tonight a local named open in agile_team_lane passed its notebook (the parser only warned and dropped the block) and failed the node regen; earlier today real did the same in kit_style_measure. The guard flags := <kw> =, := <kw> :, lambda parameters and (~<kw> : parameters for the names proven reserved by a real failure: open, and, inl, let, type, union, nominal, prototype, instance, join, real (block is a valid name in compiled kit code, so it is not listed). Measured: 0 findings over all 1102 src .spi files; a synthetic := open and := real are flagged while opened and typed pass. Parse 0; the full extracted precheck passes on the current tree. This covers the parse step's most common miss in milliseconds; a real parse of touched files stays the open part of this item.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_20 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 20u32, "2026-11-08T01:51Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 21:4x kit, SIXTH GUARD (scripts/launch-train.ps1): a qualified reference pkg.module.name to a sibling package that the file's own package.spiproj does not list. Found tonight: kit_cli_model called kit_status_facts.facts.status_printed while only kit_cli (the crate) listed kit_status_facts, and the node regen failed with ETY-UnboundVariable kit_status_facts (probe ad). The check ignores string literals, host macros and // lines and only counts names that are real sibling package dirs. Measured: 0 findings over every src package once fixed. Proof on the box: parse 0; the extracted precheck passes on the current tree (lock exit 0); with kit_status_facts removed from kit_cli_model/package.spiproj it refuses with src/kit_cli_model/model.spi:31 uses package kit_status_facts, which this package.spiproj does not list, and the file was restored byte-identical. The same dry run also caught a 122-column line I had just written (fixed). The precheck now refuses six classes that each cost a node regen tonight or earlier: widths, untargeted tests, ++# without sm operators, keyword locals, a stale Cargo.lock, unlisted packages.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_21 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 21u32, "2026-11-08T04:33Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 00:3x kit, SEVENTH GUARD (scripts/launch-train.ps1): a := binding whose value starts on its own line and continues on the next line with ++#. The parser drops the binding and later uses read unbound. TRAIN39 lost its install to exactly this in agile_task_split/split_cli.spi (195/196); the same file with each piece bound first passed 1/1 on the same candidate. Measured 0 findings over 1155 src .spi files; the split_cli shape is flagged, while a value that starts on the next line (:= x = / value / ++# ...) is not. Parse 0. Edited while the TRAIN39 box half was running this script; pwsh had already parsed it at start and the edit sits in the precheck branch that -NodeStage skips, so the running job was unaffected, but the rule is still to wait.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_22 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 22u32, "2026-11-09T06:20Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:3x local rig, GUARDS 8-10 added to scripts/launch-train.ps1's notebook precheck (unstaged, parse 0), each from a moon probe that tonight cost 5-8 minutes: G8 a nested constructor pattern (| Void TimedOut =>), which drops the definition so callers see Unbound (rig_delegate, probe 1109k); G9 a record update whose subject is an application ({ default_request [ ... ] ?| ... }), a parse error that drops the block (rig_delegate, probe 1108h/i); G10 sm' or ++# in a package whose package.spiproj lacks spiral- (rust_std_env: 59 dependent crates failed regen, rig-r3b1108b). VALIDATED both ways: over all 1162 src .spi the three guards find 0 (no false positive can block a launch), and a 6-case regex table hits the bad shapes and passes the good ones (| Void cause =>, | Some n ?& ..., { base ?| ... }, { r ?| ... }). DROPPED a fourth guard on purpose: mixed plain/GADT union forms; the scan found toolchain_argument_domain/arguments.spi mixing them while it passes every train, so that is style, not an error (memory corrected). Guards now 10.")
