inl note_of_lib_move_read_text_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T16:32Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:4x tibia (help pool). LIB HALF DRAFTED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT\\file_system.spi (base 31DA42B6F518) adds read_text_under root relative = read_text_or_empty (root </> relative) and read_text_lf path = read_text_or_empty path |> sm'::replace \"\\r\\n\" \"\\n\", with one test (rooted read, CRLF -> LF, missing file -> \"\"). Gate: ganymede job-1794241863338-tibia-libgate-fs (format, --check, budget, file_system Cells) on a mirror re-synced to the box base. The typed read outcome is DEFERRED until a caller needs it: the 5 error-needing reads (owner_growth_runtime/growth:10, rating_guard_runtime/guard:13, rig_compiler_discovery/main:132, rig_handoff_render/render:24, rig_cli_model/argument_file:22) sit inside multi-statement host blocks that format the error themselves. KIT SITES re-mapped after the kit->rig renames (Grep std::fs::read_to_string over kit/src): exact read_text_or_empty: rig_experiments/ledger_host:10 file_text, proxy_text_replacement/text_replacement:30 file_text, rust_std_fs/model:126 (loaded_text wrapper). Rooted (read_text_under): rig_do_git_host/host:33, rig_do_write_host/host:46. read_text_lf: rig_guide/guide:11 text_of (strips \\r; equal for CRLF files). trim: agile_lease_terms/terms:50 (sm'::trim of read_text_or_empty). read_all_text: cold_proof_domain/native_binary_tests:6. Inline reads inside larger host blocks (jobs_watch:111, rig_adoption host:52, rig_cli_check:155, rig_do_facts host:83/143, coverage_prune) stay until their packages migrate. The kit switch is rig's window (rig owns those packages); tibia proposes the 8 one-line swaps after the lib land.")
inl note_of_lib_move_read_text_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT", 4u32, "2026-11-09T16:57Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:0x tibia: LIB HALF GATED (ganymede job-1794241863338-tibia-libgate-fs; mirror base = box base 31DA42B6F518, restored after): formatter unchanged, --check clean, Cells file_system discovered 45, executed 29, passed 29, failed 0 (16 unsupported on this host backend). The 91 over_budget cells are pre-existing. Fixed after the gate (layout only): a here-string dropped the blank line after the new test, which merged it with the next definition into one cell; the blank line is restored and the test renamed to fit (264 chars). NEXT: land it with lib_land_window via a moon -PrivateLib proof (driver proven today on LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-2-LIB), together with REGEX-LIB-4's regex_xsd if that gates in time; box post-land digest checked before the box copy.")
