inl note_of_lib_move_read_text_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT", 7u32, "2026-11-09T23:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:0x rig, KIT SWITCH APPLIED after TRAIN43's snapshot (unstaged; rides TRAIN44; 6 files, +6 -12 lines, host macros out): rig_experiments/ledger_host file_text and proxy_text_replacement/text_replacement file_text -> file_system.read_text_or_empty (its Rust arm is the same macro byte for byte); rig_do_write_host/host file_text -> file_system.read_text_under root path (lib </> is PathBuf::from(a).join(b), the same join as the macro, absolute paths included); rig_guide/guide text_of -> file_system.read_text_lf (CRLF -> LF; the old macro also dropped lone CR, which markdown guides do not carry); agile_lease_terms/terms trimmed_file_text -> sm'.trim (read_text_or_empty) (default trim set space, tab, CR, LF); cold_proof_domain/native_binary_tests read -> file_system.read_all_text (panics on a missing file like the old unwrap). NOT SWAPPED, with reasons: rust_std_fs/model read_text (its package does not reference the lib; adding the dependency to that legacy boundary is a separate decision), rig_do_git_host/host matching_lines (the read is inside a filter chain, not a one-liner). kit standards: no finding on any edited line (the 27 findings are pre-existing in undeclared legacy packages); ratchet 0 regressions. Proof: TRAIN44's regen and notebooks for these 6 packages.")
