inl note_of_lib_move_cli_prelude_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE", 7u32, "2026-11-07T22:14Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. Next step: list the ~45 kit packages' prelude copies with their argv offsets (kit owns those packages; x and tibia have already moved to lib env). TypeFeatures: one typed argv view (args : list string, offset fixed by the entry kind) in lib env, so off-by-one argv bugs become type errors.")
inl note_of_lib_move_cli_prelude_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T12:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:0x rig (LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-1-LIST), PRELUDE COPIES in kit/src (rg for top-level definitions of the CLI helpers, excluding the two source packages rust_std_env and workspace_primitives): 86 copies in 52 packages. argument_owned 20 copies (19 are the same one-line forward to rust_std_env.model.argument_owned, i.e. argv offset 2: args().skip(2).nth(i), the verb word at index 0): agile_task_next, agile_backlog_scaffold, agile_task_inspection, agile_task_creation, agile_planning_rollup, agile_todo_scan, agile_task_revision, agile_task_notes, agile_task_rename, agile_title_notes, patch_mutation_contract, agile_todo_record, agile_todo_roots, agile_planning_revision, agile_task_views, agile_planning_migration, rig_agile_routes, rig_agile_next_args, rig_agile_mutation, rig_agile_list_args. argument_count 17 copies with THREE different offsets: env.command_line_argument_count () + 1 (lib, 6: rig_do, rig_jobs, rig_table_query, ...), rust_std_env argument_count_after 0 (rig_machine_watch) / after 2 (agile verbs), and a text-based one (rig_cli_model argument_file). argument_byte 4 (task_creation, rig_agile_lease, rig_agile_routes, rig_agile_mutation). stdout_line 24 (16 = console.write_line forwards; 2 host println: rig_do_facts, rig_do_edit; 1 host write_all + i32: workspace_primitives source). stdout_text 4. decimal_of 10 with TWO semantics: optionm'.default_value 0 (convert.try_convert text) (lib, 7) vs host parse::<u64>().unwrap_or(0) with trim (rig_do_program, rig_do_edit decode) and an i32 fallback variant (rig_memory_model). Move plan implications: one lib cli_prelude with argument_owned/argument_count taking an explicit typed offset (VerbAt 0 | AfterVerb) kills the 3-offset drift; stdout_line = console.write_line; decimal_of = lib try_convert with trim (the host parse copies trim, the lib ones do not: unify on trim).")
inl lib_usage_verb () = Task ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", "kit lib usage: one verb that answers who calls which lib definition, how often, from which repo, as typed Spiral rows (usage nominal + verdict union), compiler-backed through SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT over each repo's consumer builds, replacing the three apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/lib-usage-*.ps1 and any side script", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "-", "kit,team:rig,lib,metrics,tooling,typefeatureset,main,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_usage_verb () = Planning ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_usage_verb_1 () = Note ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:54Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 11-01 19:0x. WHAT EXISTS (found first): the compiler's SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT recorder (spiral_compiler.fs ~7752, PrepassReferences: def/use rows with path+line, open-resolved names, nominal constructors and prototypes since pack 4) writes TSV rows at process exit; apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1, lib-usage-consumers.ps1, lib-usage-references.ps1 aggregate them (pwsh, untyped); kit has 'standards --census' (rule counts) and 'lint macros'/'lint shadows' (host macros, shadowing), none of which count calls; Cells reports test rows per file. Nothing yields per-definition call counts by repo. INTERIM TODAY (text census, a throwaway pwsh glue in the session scratchpad, not a repo tool): typed rows in %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\usage_census.spi, 4,056 rows, schema 'union repo = Spiral | Kit | X | Tibia | Fiscal | Dice | Alphabet | DirTreeHtml | Regex | Polyglot | Blog', 'union kind = Inl | Let | Type | Nominal | Union | Prototype', 'union verdict = UsedOutside | LibOnly | FileLocal | Unused', 'nominal usage = { module; name; kind; self_uses; lib_uses; outside_uses; by_repo : list (repo * i32); verdict }'. The verb should emit exactly these rows (the shape is the spec). DoD: (1) 'kit lib usage <spiral-root> <repo-root>...' builds each repo's consumer entry points with SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT set (on the node by default; one job), resolves every use row to a lib definition by the recorder's E identity, and writes the rows file plus a per-module summary (defs, unused, file-local, outside uses, repos); (2) tests with a fixture lib of 3 modules and 2 consumer packages: a qualified use, an open-resolved use, a type-position use, a prototype instance, and an operator each land in the right repo column, and an unused definition gets Unused; (3) the three lib-usage-*.ps1 scripts are deleted after one run agrees with them on the 10-18 baseline names; (4) LIB-RESHAPE and LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT cite its rows for keep/test/drop. TYPEFEATURESET: phantom-tagged paths (:! Lib / :! Consumer) so a lib row can't be counted as outside, the verdict union above, repo a closed union read from the roots' manifests, no string-keyed maps in the output.")
inl note_of_lib_usage_verb_2 () = Note ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:58Z", "main", "main 19:0x groom: NEXT STEP (kit, CPU-light): the typed row model (repo/kind/verdict unions, usage nominal) plus the use-row resolver as a HostFree kit package with the fixture tests from the DoD; the compiler-run half (SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT over each repo on the node) comes second. Owner kit, main reviews the rows against the 11-01 text census (usage_census.spi in the LIB-RESHAPE drafts dir). Estimate 480m, load medium.")
inl note_of_lib_usage_verb_3 () = Note ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", 3u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom: overlaps KIT-DEF-INDEX (new, child of KIT-REUSE-METRICS), which writes one typed row per definition with call sites in and out of lib. Build this verb as a query over those rows, not a second walker.")
inl lib_move_text_helpers () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", "Small text helpers re-implemented per package (number-to-text i32_text/u64_text/decimal_text/count_text in ~28 places, padded in 8, lines_joined in 10, unquoted in 8) switch to lib sm' (decimal_text, pad_left/pad_right exist); sm' gains the two missing ones (a newline join that skips empty sides, strip one surrounding quote pair) and a code-point-counting pad, since kit's padded counts chars while sm' pads by length", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT", "lib,generic,main,team:org,team:rig,typefeatureset,sm", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_move_text_helpers () = Planning ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:56Z", "main", "11-01 19:0x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (kit src/<pkg>/<file>:line unless marked, read in place). NUMBER TEXT (all = sm'.decimal_text, sm'.spi:2323, or sm'.show): i32_text agile_task_census/task_census:11, kit_standards/rules:45, kit_grep_query/search:90, agile_memory_links/links:8, kit_handoff_render/render:30, host-macro copies kit_table_query/cells:52, workspace_primitives/numbers:6, kit_experiments/ledger_host:29; u64_text kit_cli_check/cli:97, command_spec_domain/model:369, kit_adoption/run:9, agile_lease_terms/terms:84, kit_machine_watch/run:12, host-macro copies workspace_primitives/numbers:8, proxy_failure_classification/failure_classification:50; decimal_text kit_jobs/stop_cli:145, kit_lcov/lcov:66, kit_do_program/compiled:8, kit_receipt/receipt:15, kit_repo_state/repo:55, kit_jobs/host:16; count_text kit_process_table/model:58, kit_guide/guide:28, kit_memory_model/model:20, kit_resume/resume:16, kit_machine_watch/jobs_watch:7, kit_table_logs/logs:10, kit_style_census/census:7, x apps/client/posts.spi:121, lib xsd_regex.spi:756 (hand-rolled digit recursion). PADDING: identical host macro (pads to chars().count()) agile_planning_fields/planning_fields:7, agile_planning_rollup/planning_rollup:43, agile_task_listing/task_listing:42, agile_task_next/task_next:23; format!(\"{:<w$}\") kit_cli_check/cli:221, kit_process_table/listing:97; zero pad x apps/sim/spi/world.spi:305 (= sm'.pad_left w '0'); lib xsd_regex.spi:872 padded. NEWLINE JOIN skipping empty sides (? right = \"\" ?> left |? left = \"\" ?> right |: left ++ \"\\n\" ++ right): kit_do/run:57, kit_do_jobs/run:33, kit_do_lab/run:33, kit_do_read/run:40, kit_do_tables/run:20, kit_do_write/run:41, kit_do_facts/run:69, kit_do_git/run:41, kit_do_process/run:41, kit_do_edit/run:64. STRIP ONE QUOTE PAIR (byte_slice token 1 (len - 1)): agile_planning_gaps/gaps:20, agile_planning_rollup/planning_rollup:94, agile_planning_tally/planning_tally:34, agile_task_next/task_next:22, agile_task_listing/task_listing:40, agile_planning_migration/planning_migration:93, quote_stripped variants agile_note_model/model:134, agile_task_inspection/task_inspection:51. Not the same concept, left alone: kit_standards/rules:131 and kit_ci_model/tools:37 (remove every quote). LIB TARGET: sm' (existing). TYPED SHAPE: :! column_width = i32 counted in code points (unicode.code_point_count), pad_right_to (w : column_width) (fill : char) (s : string) and pad_left_to; the existing pad_left/pad_right keep their length semantics and say so in their test; line_joined (left : string) (right : string) : string; quote_pair_stripped (q : char) (s : string) : option string (None when s is not wrapped in q, so a caller cannot strip an unquoted token silently). DoD: (1) sm' definitions with :# blocks (pad of 'é' to 3 = 'é  ', pad of a longer text unchanged, line_joined with each side empty, quote_pair_stripped on '\"a\"', 'a', '\"', '') passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) every site above switched, proven by kit's touched notebooks + crate regen with byte-identical table output (agile list, kit do receipts), x's xsim build, and the lib xsd_regex gate; (3) the copies deleted. Overlap: EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY covers workspace_primitives/numbers as a package; this item covers the per-package copies.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:10Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:10 x: x's SHARE. (1) apps/client/posts.spi count_text is already a one-line call to sm'.obj_to_string (no re-implementation), so x leaves it; the call sites read better through the name. (2) apps/sim/spi/world.spi padded (a hand-rolled zero pad) becomes sm'::pad_left width '0' (sm'::obj_to_string n): pad_left is backend-neutral (replicate) and its twin pad_right is gated on gleam. Draft kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS\\world.spi, base 357D2B331A6A -> 561F876D817C. It rides the next x sim proof (the clock and date texts reach it through the sim e2e; the -Accept build checks the budget). Nothing else of x's is on this item's site list.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T20:17Z", "x", "2026-11-03 16:17 x: x's SHARE LANDED: apps/sim/spi/world.spi 357D2B331A6A -> 561F876D817C (padded = sm'::pad_left width '0' (sm'::obj_to_string n)), proven in x-next1b (sim accept 0 with no fixture changed, sim build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5), plus its 1 regenerated sim output. x has nothing else on this item's site list.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 4u32, "2026-11-04T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-04 08:24 x: dropped team:x (as with LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE). x's share landed 11-03 (x-next1b). Re-checked now over x/apps/*.spi for local i32_text/u64_text/decimal_text/count_text/padded/lines_joined/unquoted/pad_*: 3 definitions, all one-line wrappers over lib sm' (client posts count_text = sm'::obj_to_string; census count_text = label plus sm'::obj_to_string; sim world padded = sm'::pad_left width '0'), none re-implements a helper. The rest is kit's sites (team:kit/main).")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 5u32, "2026-11-07T22:15Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. TypeFeatures: none new; a dedup onto lib sm' (decimal_text, pad_left/pad_right). Remaining owners: kit and tibia packages (x's share landed 11-03).")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T18:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:1x LIB-HALF SCOPING (read before drafting): sm' today has pad_left/pad_right (by length), decimal_text, join' (array); none of the 3 missing helpers. (1) lines_joined (10 kit copies, e.g. kit/src/rig_do/run.spi:57: `? right = \"\" ?> left |? left = \"\" ?> right |: left ++# \"\\n\" ++# right`) is ONE semantics: lifts as-is into sm' (name: join_lines_skipping_empty). (2) unquoted (11 copies) is TWO semantics under one name: agile_note_model/model.spi:140 = quote_stripped THEN unescaped_from (a token reader that also unescapes), not just \"strip one surrounding quote pair\"; a single lib function would silently change the unescaping callers. So: lib gets strip_quote_pair (no unescape) and the unescaping copies keep their name until a per-copy audit marks which semantics each caller needs. (3) padded (8 copies) counts code points while sm' pads by length: the lib version needs a code-point count, which lives in lib unicode (unicode::code_points), a layer ABOVE sm'; so the code-point pad belongs in unicode (pad_points_left/right), not sm'. Next step: draft sm' join_lines_skipping_empty + strip_quote_pair and unicode pad_points_left with rust tests; prove via the ganymede lib route; the kit switches go to rig's train (team:rig).")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T18:05Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:1x LIB DRAFT (drafts\\spiral\\LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS\\sm'.spi, base DF110E397027): sm' gains join_lines_skipping_empty (kit's lines_joined semantics exactly) and strip_quote_pair (one surrounding pair, no unescape; a lone quote and inner quotes untouched), each with a rust test (empty sides; \"\\\"ab\\\"\" -> ab, \"\\\"\" stays, \"a\\\"b\\\"c\" stays, \"\\\"\\\"\" -> \"\"). Budget: the appended cells add no finding (sm' finding count unchanged vs live). Next: prove + land via the ganymede lib route after org2-swap4 frees the tree; then the code-point pad in lib unicode; then hand the kit call-site switches to rig.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 8u32, "2026-11-09T19:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "LANDED on the box 19:20Z (copy-only from ganymede proof, lib digest 0E9E54C1A17AEC9D = box prediction; re-proved after fin_vector/xsd_emit moved under us): sm' gains join_lines_skipping_empty + strip_quote_pair, unicode gains spaces_of + pad_points_right. Gates: unicode 10/10, sm' 80/80 (8 unsupported), document_test 26, 30 consumer signatures unchanged, 0 respell drift. Undo: spiral-bin/lib-land-undo/20261109-152011. Call-site switch handed to rig as KIT-TEXT-HELPERS-SWITCH.")
inl lib_move_dth_fs () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", "dir-tree-html shared.spi carries its own host bindings for path join, is-file, write, mkdir and temp dir plus a hand-rolled i64-to-text, all of which lib file_system and sm' already provide; switch its 40 call sites to lib and delete the copies (its write/mkdir return an error flag, so lib gains typed result-returning forms if write_all_text's unit return is not enough)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT", "lib,generic,main,team:main,typefeatureset,file_system,dir-tree-html", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_move_dth_fs () = Planning ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl agile_html_report () = Task ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", "i574n.github's GitHub Actions renders the agile state as an HTML report (the views the kit CLI prints: next/plan/wip/epic trees/burn-down, plus the TODO-comment scan across repos), published on its Pages and better than Jira (user 11-01 19:1x: 'better than jira with the todo comment scan (that we should've been exploring more by now, we barely use it)')", Story, P1, D4, 25u32, Planned, "", "kit,agile,pages,ci,todos,team:rig,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_agile_html_report () = Planning ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_agile_html_report_1 () = Note ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "main", "main 19:2x: the input is docs/backlog/state/agile.spi, read by kit in CI (kit agile ... --json); the TODO scan is 'kit agile todos <root> [paths] --json' (exists, barely used). Output: typed rows rendered to HTML by the new html repo's renderer once it has parity (HTML-REPO), dir-tree-html meanwhile. DoD: each push to i574n.github publishes an agile page with next per team, Active/Blocked with ages, epic trees with rolled-up estimate/actual, today's state changes, and TODOs linked to items; no .tsv committed; it renders in under 2 min of CI. Typefeatureset: view rows as unions (ItemRow, TodoRow, EpicNode GADT) shared with the CLI renderer, so the CLI and the page cannot drift.")
inl note_of_agile_html_report_2 () = Note ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:29Z", "kit", "11-01 19:29 kit GROOM. FIRST HURDLE: i574n.github's runner has no kit binary. Options: (a) the workflow checks out i574n/kit and builds kit-cli (about 3 min cold on CI, cached by Cargo target cache), or (b) kit's own gh-pages.yml publishes kit.exe/kit (linux) as a release asset or Pages file that i574n.github downloads by pinned hash (faster, one build per kit push). Decide (b) unless publishing binaries is a user decision (it is outward-facing, so it is PARKED for the user: \"may kit's CI publish its binary for other repos' CI?\"; (a) works meanwhile). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a HostFree package agile_report_model: report_section union (NextPerTeam team items | ActiveAging items | BlockedOn blocker items | EpicTree root | Burndown points | TodoSites findings), each item a typed record decoded from kit agile ... --json; one renderer from sections to HTML (the HTML-REPO renderer once it has parity, dir-tree-html meanwhile); phantom markers on sections that need the TODO scan input vs the state input, so a section cannot render without its source. NEXT STEP (CPU-light): the report_section model plus a test that decodes a small --json fixture into NextPerTeam and ActiveAging; then the workflow step running kit agile next/list/todos --json and the renderer. DoD unchanged (main 19:2x).")
inl note_of_agile_html_report_3 () = Note ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T00:00Z", "kit", "11-01 20:00 kit: typed model DONE (unstaged), new HostFree package src/agile_report_model. Phantom sources :! from_state / :! from_todo_scan on a section GADT: NextPerTeam, ActiveAging and BlockedOn are section from_state, TodoSites is section from_todo_scan, so a TODO section cannot be built from state items. The page is a report_page record with one typed list per source (no existential, because sections are built from runtime JSON and existentials are compile-time only, today's lesson). report_html renders one page with &/</> escaping. Test a_report_renders_typed_sections_and_escapes_text: Linux 1/1 (the first red was a stale copy after the cloud ssh lockout; re-pushed and verified). NEXT: decode kit agile next/list --json and agile todos --json into report_item/todo_site, then the i574n.github workflow step (blocked on the kit-binary-in-CI decision parked in n2).")
inl note_of_agile_html_report_4 () = Note ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", 4u32, "2026-11-02T13:59Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: May kit's CI publish its kit binary (release asset or Pages file) for other repos' CI to download by pinned hash? RULE (written before acting): Default = option (a): i574n.github's workflow checks out i574n/kit and builds kit-cli with a Cargo target cache. It publishes nothing new and is reversible, and the note itself says (a) works. Option (b) only comes back if (a)'s cached build passes 10 min median over 5 CI runs. Even then publishing a binary is an outward-facing step, so it would go to the user as a single commit. BACKUP/UNDO: Workflow and model edits stay unstaged for the user's review. The existing workflow stays in git HEAD. OWNER: kit. NEXT: Land the agile_report_model report_section union plus a test that decodes a small --json fixture into NextPerTeam and ActiveAging, then add a workflow step that builds kit from source (option a). VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_agile_html_report_5 () = Note ("AGILE-HTML-REPORT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:34Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 18 h ago by x, progress kept at 25%. Resume from that note: Land the agile_report_model report_section union plus a test that decodes a small --json fixture into NextPerTeam and ActiveAging, then add a workflow step that builds kit from source (option a). VETO: the user can reverse this at any time;")
inl ci_run_report_spi () = Task ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", "Recover the 'braggable' CI runtime history that the old dib/pwsh-notebook runs gave every repo (ipynb/html of each CI run on its Pages), now that workflow notebooks are retired: the pwsh->Spiral rewrite (KIT-RUN-SPI) emits a typed run report per CI run, rendered to HTML (user 11-01 19:1x: 'let's not bring it back, but we gotta study later how to make these runs export a similar report ... having these damn notebooks around just for that might not be good also, gotta deliberate')", Story, P2, D4, 70u32, Active, "KIT-RUN-SPI", "ci,pages,kit,reports,team:rig,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ci_run_report_spi () = Planning ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_ci_run_report_spi_1 () = Note ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "main", "main 19:2x: main retired i574n.github/scripts/workflow.livemd today (its 4 Invoke-Block calls now sit in workflow.ps1), which drops that run's notebook record; others (spiral apps/spiral export, polyglot) may follow. Deliberation inputs: per-step name, start, duration, exit, a log excerpt, and machine. As typed rows, a run report is just another page view (HTML-REPO), and nobody keeps notebooks only for this. DoD: a written decision (typed run report vs keeping one notebook per repo), and, if the report wins, one repo's CI publishes it next to its tree.")
inl note_of_ci_run_report_spi_2 () = Note ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", 2u32, "2026-11-09T20:52Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:2x tibia (help pool): DECISION INPUT, measured on the trees. RECOMMEND THE TYPED RUN REPORT; no notebook comes back. Most of it already exists: tibia's scripts/build.ps1 writes typed TSV rows every CI run into target/ci-metrics. (a) machine.tsv: platform, cpu, logical_cores, memory_gib, wgsl_runner, dx12_compiler, adapter_request. (b) files-<label>.tsv: File, Seconds, ExitCode per notebook file. (c) tests-<label>.tsv: File, Test, Target, Status, Ms, Memo per test. (d) wgsl-<label>.tsv, <name>.out logs, and tibia-<label>.prom gauges. gh-pages.yml uploads them as the ci-metrics-<os> artifact (always, 30 days), while the notebooks-<os> artifact is failure-only. So the deliberation inputs main listed (per-step name, duration, exit, a log excerpt, machine) are all recorded already; only per-step START times are missing. The record is lost because it never reaches Pages: it lives in a 30-day artifact. NO OTHER REPO writes rows (spiral, regex, html, i574n.github have no ci-metrics), so tibia is the natural pilot. PILOT PLAN (tibia, tibia's own repo): (1) the deploy job downloads both ci-metrics-<os> artifacts and copies the *.tsv (not .out, not .prom) into dist/runs/<run_id>/<os>/ with one run.tsv row (sha, run_id, os, started_utc). (2) Keep history: peaceiris publish replaces the site each deploy, so runs/ needs keep_files or a fetch of the previous runs/index.tsv; an index row is about 100 bytes per run. (3) Render the rows as HTML with a Spiral app (spiral-first; HTML-REPO's page view when it lands), one table per TSV plus a runs index. (4) PRIVACY: machine.tsv's wgsl_runner is an absolute path (on the box it holds a personal path), so the report keeps only its basename. Next step: draft (1)-(4) in tibia, unstaged; the CI proof needs a user push.")
inl note_of_ci_run_report_spi_3 () = Note ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:18Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:2x tibia: PILOT STEP (3) GREEN, the renderer. drafts\\tibia\\CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI\\apps\\report\\ (run_report.spi + spiral.toml, a new tibia app). Gate on ganymede (jobs tibia-round2/round3): --check clean, fmt same (the formatter's layout adopted), Cells 3/3: absolute paths keep only their file name (a Windows path with backslashes, a Linux path, a bare name); one header row and one body row per TSV line; markup in a cell escaped. REAL RUN: compiled to Rust, then run with files-short.tsv and machine.tsv as arguments, it prints a page with one <table><caption>file</caption> per TSV. The runner path /home/runner/.../spiral-wgsl renders as spiral-wgsl (step 4, privacy). LEFT: (1) the gh-pages.yml wiring: ubuntu build job runs the report over target/ci-metrics/*.tsv into dist/runs/<run_id>/index.html; history via a fetch of the previous gh-pages runs/ (force_orphan replaces the site each deploy); (2) a runs index page. Both are in tibia (tibia's repo) and need a user push for the CI proof.")
inl note_of_ci_run_report_spi_4 () = Note ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:19Z", "tibia", "TypeFeatures: the run report is typed rows (TSV with a header row) rendered by one Spiral function per shape; a later slice can lift each TSV into a record type per file kind (machine, files, tests) so a renamed column fails at compile time instead of rendering blank.")
inl note_of_ci_run_report_spi_5 () = Note ("CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI", 5u32, "2026-11-09T21:40Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:5x tibia: PILOT WIRED; the CI proof is owed. (1) TIBIA (tibia's repo, applied unstaged): apps/report/run_report.spi + spiral.toml (the green renderer); scripts/build.ps1 adds ../apps/report to the layout check (line 24/33) and to the notebook sources (line 97), so CI runs its 3 tests. (2) THE WORKFLOW IS GENERATED: tibia's gh-pages.yml comes from i574n.github scripts/pins/workflows.spi tibia (), so the step is a DRAFT for org's tooling repo: drafts\\i574n.github\\CI-RUN-REPORT-SPI\\workflows.spi (base 25A26307F25E). It adds tibia_run_report () and one ubuntu-only step run-report AFTER publish.ps1 (so publish cannot wipe it). The step compiles apps/report to Rust with the cached compiler, then runs target/report/report target/ci-metrics/*.tsv > dist/runs/<run_id>/index.html, which the existing gh-pages upload carries to Pages. HISTORY is deliberately left out of the pilot: the shared verified_pages_push_job uses force_orphan, so each deploy keeps only the latest runs/<id>; keeping earlier runs means changing that shared job for every repo (a follow-up for org). NEXT: org applies + regenerates (pins workflows generator), and a user push proves it on Pages at i574n.github.io/tibia/runs/<id>/.")
