inl note_of_html_ci_release_1 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml with the same uses: set as dir-tree-html (gh actions-lock --no-fix passes against a copied actions.lock), every run step pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1; green on ubuntu-24.04 and windows-2025 after the user pushes; then a release job (needs the user: a softprops/action-gh-release-style uses: means a new actions.lock entry, or gh release create with GITHUB_TOKEN, contents: write) publishing html-linux-x64 and html-windows-x64.exe with a sha256 manifest; spiral/scripts/html.ps1 downloads a pinned release tag instead of cloning + building. NEXT STEP: copy the workflow, verify the lock, user push. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a for yml; the release manifest is a typed .spi row module (asset, os, sha256), not a .txt. FIELDS: estimate 240m, load medium, assignee pair (push + Pages setting + release are the user's).")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_2 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:17Z", "html", "html 21:1x: .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml + actions.lock copied from dir-tree-html unchanged (same uses: set, every run step pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1); `gh actions-lock --no-fix` in C:\\home\\git\\html -> 'All 1 workflow valid'. Not run on GitHub yet: needs the user's push, and the Pages source setting (gh-pages branch) on i574n/html. The workflow will go red at the build.ps1 1000-line gate until HTML-CLI's crate split lands. NEXT STEP: release job (HTML-CI-RELEASE DoD) after the first green run.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_3 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:51Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x CI RED FOUND AND FIXED (unstaged, html tree was clean): run 41427447957 failed at build.ps1:16 because Cells' run_notebook.ps1:128 found no `mix` (the workflow copied from dir-tree-html has no BEAM setup, but html's build.ps1 runs Cells). Added erlef/setup-beam@v1.24.1 (otp 29, elixir 1.20, gleam 1.19.2, rebar3 3.28.0) before setup-dotnet and its actions.lock entry (copied from tibia/regex); `gh actions-lock --no-fix` -> All 1 workflow valid. Same shape is green in regex (run 41366627749). Pages for i574n/html can only be enabled once a green run creates the gh-pages branch.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_4 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_5 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:28Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: PRECONDITION: i574n/html has a gh-pages branch (checked 11-02: 404, so the deploy job has not pushed yet). When it exists, the agent runs gh api -X POST repos/i574n/html/pages (legacy, gh-pages, /) and passes iff the page returns 200 within 10 min. The precondition gate refused to enable Pages today, as designed. BACKUP/UNDO: Undo: gh api -X DELETE repos/i574n/html/pages. OWNER: main.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_6 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 6u32, "2026-11-02T17:06Z", "main", "main 11-02 13:0x WHY html CI IS RED (run 41444627861, ubuntu): not the tests (36 passed, 0 failed) but the 1000-line gate at build.ps1:36. CI generated markdown/entry.rs at 2,169 lines; locally markdown/entry.rs is 2,570 and cli/html.rs 2,105. Join points can't fix it: entry.rs holds 93 DISTINCT top-level fns with no inlined copies (largest block_html 164, group 149, string_slice 124, group 121). So the crate is simply too big: split into hand-modeled linked units (memory hand-modeled-build-units; link: units arrive with pack16c, queued). Plan: markdown -> inline (inline_parse) + block (render/markdown) units; cli -> tree + pages + file_views units; each under 1000 lines, typed exports. Second, smaller signal: markdown.spi executed 1 of 9 tests on CI with 8 \"unsupported\", so a target toolchain is missing in the CI job (memory ci-unsupported-means-tool-missing); check its ///> targets against the workflow setup. Owner main; next run after pack16c installs, compiled on the node.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_7 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 7u32, "2026-11-02T19:55Z", "main", "main 11-02 16:0x BLOCKED ON A REAL PREREQUISITE: the 1000-line fix needs linked units with CROSS-UNIT CALLS. html's layout is one shared src/ package (7 modules) plus two thin entry crates: markdown/entry.spi is 6 lines but emits 2,570 because it inlines markdown, inline_parse, render and model; cli/html.spi is 123 lines and emits 2,105 by inlining tree, pages, file_views, render and model. Splitting src/ into link: units only helps if markdown/cli can CALL those units' functions. pack17's Step A links types (unions) only; Step B, typed cross-unit calls, is COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS (P0, 0%). The interim alternative, host-string crate calls or kit bindings, is the drift we are removing, so: dep added; resume when Step B lands. Plan then: units model, inline_parse, render, markdown, tree, pages, file_views; entry crates link them; each under 1000 lines.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_8 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 8u32, "2026-11-03T09:41Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:5x RESUMING: its dep COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS is at 90%, and compiler measured the boundary rules on installed pack23 (lu6-lu8): arrays, tuple args (flattened), and records inside arrays cross; a record taken or returned DIRECTLY crosses only with all-primitive fields; CURRIED exports are not linked but inlined, silently. html CI is still red only on the gate (run 07:43: markdown/entry.rs 2,339 lines; --self-test passed). PLAN, mirroring kit_grep_query/kit_grep_found (sibling package under packages: plus link:, its own Cargo lib crate, callers import package.module): units html_model (unions), html_parse (markdown + inline_parse: text -> list block), html_render (render: list block -> string), then html_pages (tree + pages + file_views); markdown/entry and cli/html link them. Each export has a single tuple argument, never curried. OPEN QUESTION, asked of compiler as an lu9 probe: does a recursive union list (list block with list inline inside) cross linked, or get inlined? If it is inlined, the fallback is string -> string exports per unit. NEXT: compiler's lu9 verdict, then the split, gated on the node after MIRROR-RESYNC-1103.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_9 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 9u32, "2026-11-03T09:53Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:5x compiler (answer to main's lu9 request): measured on pack23 Rust (details COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS n12). (1) The parse/render split LINKS: parse_parse and render_blocks_html are pub fns with the model unions in their signatures, imported by use model::{inline, block}. (2) But list block does NOT lower to a shared type: each crate re-emits core list instantiations, so rustc E0308. With array_base instead of list at the boundary, all 4 crates build and the html is correct, PROVIDED every crate (parse, render AND the entry/app) lists the model unit under link:. (3) Lib question: a union defined in a lib module (any non-linked package) is re-emitted per crate (measured: model used as a package without link: gave the app its own US0 -> E0308). So keep the markdown model in a linked html_model unit that every crate links, with array_base containers, and keep lib to escape and the markup builders. Gap filed: LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES (list across units).")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_10 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 10u32, "2026-11-03T09:54Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:0x DESIGN SETTLED by compiler's lu9 (n9). The split LINKS (pub fns with the recursive model unions in their signatures), but 'list block' cannot cross: every crate re-emits list instantiations (E0308), and lib-defined types are re-emitted per crate. array_base crosses when EVERY crate on the path, the entry crate included, lists the model unit under link:. DECISION, by rule (the model is immutable data, and array_base is a mutable Rc<RefCell<Vec>>, which weakens the typefeatureset): keep 'list' and take compiler's LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES (the defining unit owns list/option instantiations) as a prerequisite. FALLBACK if it has not landed by 11-04 06:00: array_base containers in the model only, behind conversion helpers. LAYOUT (ready to prepare now): html_model (unions: inline, block, page parts), html_parse (markdown + inline_parse: text -> list block), html_render (render: list block -> markup), html_pages (tree, pages, file_views); markdown/entry and cli/html list them under packages: AND link:; each a Cargo lib crate with path deps, like kit_grep_found. Each export takes one tuple argument (curried exports are not linked).")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_11 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 11u32, "2026-11-03T11:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:0x THE SPLIT WORKS (scratch %TEMP%\\html-split, box, installed pack24; the live repo is untouched until the gates pass). 8 crates, every generated file UNDER 1000: html_model 586, html_inline 596, html_table 230, html_parse 837, html_render 480, html_pages 887, markdown/entry 12, cli/html 901 (was markdown/entry 2339 + cli 2105). cargo release build OK. The new binary's --self-test passes (nested fixture plus the new viewer/no-overwrite case). Page parity vs the old 11-01 binary (byte-identical to dir-tree-html) with --viewers: regex 30/30 pages identical; dice and tibia still running. SHAPE: units are packages beside each other ('../html_x-' under both packages: and link:); each unit's main exports one-tuple-argument functions; the model unit exports blocks_of/nodes_of/aligns_some/viewer_same to ANCHOR the shared types (a union crosses only if a model export mentions it: viewer gave E0308 until viewer_same existed) plus level_of/level_tag/escape/trim, so consumers link instead of inlining them. Small curried builders (wrap, anchor, quoted, digit, show_i64, at_is, trim's helpers) moved into model and are inlined, which is cheap. Size wins beyond the split: digit_value as char-code arithmetic, digit as a slice of '0123456789', level_of linked. NEXT: dice/tibia parity, then apply to the live repo (folders html_model, html_inline, html_table, html_parse, html_render, html_pages; src/ goes; build.ps1 builds the 8 crates in order and gates the 6 notebook folders), and a node gate of every notebook.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_12 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 12u32, "2026-11-03T11:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:4x SCOPE DECIDED by rule (the smallest change that retires dir-tree-html wins): RELEASE BINARIES are NOT a prerequisite for adoption. The shim (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS n3) consumes html the way dir-tree-html has always been consumed: clone at a pinned commit, init -fast 1, build.ps1 -fast 1 (now skips the notebook gate; it still builds, self-tests and gates line counts). So this item is DONE when html's CI is green on a pushed commit with the split: the 8-crate build, notebooks green, every generated file under 1000. Published release binaries (Linux + Windows) become a later, optional speed-up for the shim, with no deadline; they publish GitHub releases, which is outward and needs no decision now.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_13 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 13u32, "2026-11-03T12:16Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:2x PROVEN ON THE BOX: html's full build.ps1 on the live repo (the 8-crate split) is GREEN. Cells notebooks 49/49 (the 6 unit folders; markdown's 9 tests now carry explicit rust targets, after an untargeted run defaulted to zig and failed; table.spi and pages_api.spi gained the package header plus 3 new tests: row cells with an escaped pipe, alignment reading, md/digit/show_i64), every crate built, --self-test passes (nested fixture + viewer/no-overwrite), largest generated file 901 lines (cli/html.rs), HTML-OK. REMAINING: the user's push of html, then CI green on GitHub (ubuntu + windows). Progress 50 -> 85.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_14 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 14u32, "2026-11-03T17:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:2x GENERATED UNITS REFRESHED to pack26 output (unstaged): all 8 committed .rs copied from europa's fast build of the same sources (backups %TEMP%\\html-rs-before-pack26). The diffs are pack26's move-on-last-use (e.g. markdown/entry.rs: 'v1.clone()' -> 'v1') plus the HTML-TREE prototype sort in pages.rs (887 -> 890); line counts otherwise unchanged (cli/html.rs 962 the largest). Europa build of exactly these: HTML-OK, tree 5/5, pages 5/5.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_15 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 15u32, "2026-11-03T18:31Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x BLOCKED (not idle): the split, the lint heal, the pack26 refresh of the generated units and the europa/box proofs are done; the only step left is the GitHub run after the user pushes html. RESUME WHEN: html HEAD moves past 05a1a436.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_16 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 16u32, "2026-11-05T05:53Z", "main", "11-05 01:53 main UNBLOCKED (the resume condition held: html HEAD 68ccb00f, the user's 11-04 23:21 push, contains 05a1a436). The CI half of the DoD is PROVEN: html's gh-pages run on 68ccb00f is green on build (windows-2025), build (ubuntu-24.04) and push. LEFT: the release job (html-linux-x64, html-windows-x64.exe plus a typed sha256 manifest), which the DoD already marks as needing the user (a new actions.lock entry for an action-gh-release uses:, or gh release create with GITHUB_TOKEN and permissions contents: write in gh-pages.yml). It is not on the adoption critical path: HTML-ADOPT-REPOS n3 consumes html like dir-tree-html (clone at a pinned commit, build -fast). Also today: HTML-PARITY n4, html at parity or better on 11 repos.")
inl note_of_html_ci_release_17 () = Note ("HTML-CI-RELEASE", 17u32, "2026-11-06T08:21Z", "main", "main 11-06 04:2x groom (untouched >12 h): BLOCKED on the user: the CI half is proven green (68ccb00f); only the release job (html-linux-x64, html-windows-x64.exe + typed sha256 manifest) is left, and the DoD marks it as needing the user. Resume when the user okays the release job.")
inl html_adopt_repos () = Task ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", "html adoption: switch publish-tree.ps1 and its 12+ repo callers (spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, regex, blog, dice, polyglot, i574n.github, fork-spiral-patch, dir-tree-html) from dir-tree-html to the html release", Story, P1, D4, 85u32, Blocked, "HTML-CI-RELEASE,HTML-PARITY", "html,pages,dir-tree-html,typefeatureset,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_html_adopt_repos () = Planning ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_1 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 resolves the renderer through a new spiral/scripts/html.ps1 (release download, pinned tag + sha256) with dir-tree-html.ps1 kept as a fallback for one release; every caller's Pages run green with a per-repo diff report showing byte-equal or explained differences (HTML-PARITY); no repo builds the renderer in CI any more. Callers today (grep 11-01): spiral, regex, fiscal, blog, fork-spiral-patch, tibia, kit, x, i574n.github, dice, polyglot, dir-tree-html (scripts/publish.ps1 in each). NEXT STEP: html.ps1 in spiral/scripts once the first release exists. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a (glue); the per-repo parity verdicts are typed rows rendered on html's own page. FIELDS: estimate 300m, load medium (12 CI runs), assignee pair (pushes are the user's).")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_2 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 2u32, "2026-11-03T08:49Z", "main", "main 11-03 04:1x CALLER LIST CORRECTED from the 11-03 git grep. polyglot and dir-tree-html are no longer callers (out of the org), and spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, regex and blog have no direct call: they all publish through spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1, which goes through the SHIM spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1. Direct shim callers: alphabet scripts/init.ps1, dice scripts/init.ps1 + publish-bin.ps1, tapas2 scripts/init.ps1 + publish.ps1, mechahaze-album1 scripts/publish.ps1. Own clone: i574n.github scripts/init.ps1 + build.ps1. So adoption is ONE change (the shim downloads and verifies html's release binary instead of cloning and building dir-tree-html), plus i574n.github init/build. Proof: every repo's next gh-pages run renders identically (HTML-PARITY), and a fresh clone (no local dir-tree-html) works.")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_3 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T11:06Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:1x SHIM SWITCH DRAFTED, without waiting for release binaries: html is consumed exactly like dir-tree-html (clone at a pinned commit, scripts/init.ps1 -fast 1, build), since html's init.ps1 is identical to dir-tree-html's. Draft: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\HTML-ADOPT-REPOS\\dir-tree-html.ps1, a 6-line diff against spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (repo dir-tree-html -> html, exe dist/html, clone html.git, build.ps1 -fast 1, pin placeholder). html's build.ps1 gained a working -fast that skips the Cells notebook gate (publishing only needs the binary; --self-test and the 1000-line gate still run). ORDER, which is why this is a draft and not in live spiral: (1) the user pushes html with the unit split, (2) main sets rendererCommit to that pushed SHA and lands the shim in spiral, (3) the user pushes spiral, (4) every repo's next gh-pages run proves it (HTML-PARITY: 276 pages across regex/dice/tibia identical to the old renderer, except tibia's README fix). If spiral were pushed first with this shim, every gh-pages run would clone a pre-split html that fails its own gate. FOLLOW-UP: rename the shim to html.ps1 and update its 5 callers (alphabet, dice x2, tapas2 x2, mechahaze-album1, publish-tree).")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_4 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T04:22Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 00:3x STEP 2 OF THE 11-03 ORDER DONE (unstaged): step 1 held (the user pushed html; GitHub main = 4ab01fc231e621ed53c363e1a037e5300959678d, verified via ls-remote + gh api; CI green on both OSes). spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (the shim every repo's publish-tree goes through) now clones i574n/html, pins rendererCommit = 4ab01fc2..., builds with 'build.ps1 -fast 1' (skips the Cells gate; the pinned build.ps1 still copies dist/html and runs --self-test) and runs dist/html. The live shim was unchanged since 10-25, so the 11-03 draft applied as its 4 hunks; the old live copy is saved as drafts\\HTML-ADOPT-REPOS\\dir-tree-html.ps1.live-before-20261109; parse 0. PRE-PUSH PROOF queued: job-1794198133061-org2-html-shim-proof on ganymede (a fresh 'git clone --depth 1 i574n/spiral', the new shim overlaid, the shim run end to end: html clone at the pin, init -fast, build -fast, self-test), the closest stand-in for a gh-pages runner. (I tried comet first as the most runner-like host, but kit can't reach it after its restart; reported to rig.) Next: on green, steps 3-4 are the user's spiral push and every repo's next gh-pages run (HTML-PARITY: identical output); then i574n.github init/build (its own clone) and the 4 direct shim callers (alphabet, dice, tapas2, mechahaze-album1) need no change, since they call the shim.")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_5 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T06:43Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: ganymede job-1794198133061 org2-html-shim-proof exit 1 after 138 min, INCONCLUSIVE for the shim. html build reached the spiral CLI bootstrap (deps/spiral apps/spiral/build.ps1) which compiled fine in 3m08s, then its run check failed 9 of N: cuda + protocol-level-* + protocol-child-exception + protocol-cuda-driver all panic at spiral.process_cuda child failed, No such file or directory (os error 2), i.e. ganymede has no cuda child runtime. Not an html or shim defect. Next step: rerun the shim proof on a host with the cuda child present (moon) or with the CLI run check scoped to non-cuda backends; also decide whether html CI should require the cuda run check at all.")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_6 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T07:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 03:2x ROOT CAUSE of the inconclusive shim proof (compiler): apps/spiral/spiral.spi cuda_python() spawned the executable python; Linux nodes ship only python3, so the child spawn hit ENOENT and process_cuda panicked in all 9 run-check cases. Fix (compiler, unstaged in spiral: SPIRAL_PYTHON, else python on Windows, else python3) is proven on ganymede (build.ps1 exit 0 with no python and SPIRAL_PYTHON unset). Until the user pushes spiral, the shim rerun (step 5 of the ganymede org2-regex-chain) puts a python -> python3 symlink dir first on PATH. Blocker for the clean (no workaround) proof: the user pushing spiral.")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_7 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T08:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 05:1x CALLER MAP (git grep dir-tree-html over every C:\\home\\git repo, tracked files): own callers = spiral (scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 = the shim, publish-tree.ps1 + workflow.ps1 call the shim), dice (scripts/init.ps1 and publish-bin.ps1: pwsh ../deps/spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, then runs the last output line with --dir . --html index.html), alphabet (scripts/init.ps1, same shim). So dice and alphabet adopt html THROUGH the spiral shim with no edits of their own, once spiral is pushed and their deps/spiral moves. Contract check: the shim still prints the binary path as its last line ($exe = <html>/dist/html), and html's CLI parses the same operands (options { dir; html } + --viewers): dist/html.exe --dir . --html index.html on a 3-file scratch tree exits 0 and writes index.html listing every entry. Not ours (fc1943s): fc1943s.github, mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault, polyglot keep dir-tree-html; the dir-tree-html repo itself is fc1943s. Next step: the shim rerun on ganymede (python3 alias), then the user's spiral push; dice/alphabet CI green after their deps/spiral bump closes this.")
inl note_of_html_adopt_repos_8 () = Note ("HTML-ADOPT-REPOS", 8u32, "2026-11-09T08:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: GREEN. ganymede job-1794207704602 step org2-shim-proof (08:29-08:41Z, exit 0): fresh clone of pushed spiral bf5cc30a + the unstaged shim (scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 -> html) -> the shim cloned html at the pinned rendererCommit 4ab01fc2, bootstrapped the spiral CLI (run check passed, no FAILED rows, with a python -> python3 PATH alias until compiler's cuda_python fix is pushed), built html, and printed /home/remote/org2-shim/html/dist/html as its last line in shim_secs=696 (SHIM-PROOF-DONE). Together with the 05:1x caller map (dice + alphabet adopt through this shim, same CLI contract) the adoption is proven end to end on Linux. Blocker: the user's spiral push (shim + compiler's python3 default); then dice/alphabet CI after their deps/spiral bump closes this.")
