inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T00:14Z", "fiscal", "Found by fiscal 2026-11-01 judging the dir-tree-html page after the first fully green run (41351043040). The page lists everything, but the reports are raw TSV (bench.tsv, examples.tsv, files.tsv, tests.tsv). The regex repo's rule (main 11-01: results shown on the dir-tree-html page as HTML, no committed .tsv) is the bar.\nDONE: (1) target/ci-metrics gets rendered HTML views generated in CI (an index with the examples table, Messages per family plus the first message; the bench table with parse/write medians per unit and OS; the slowest files; the tests table filterable by status) linked from the page root; (2) both OS jobs publish their metrics under os-labelled names (examples-windows-2025, bench-ubuntu-24.04, ...), and the index compares them; (3) the page shows the commit id, run id and build time; (4) the README \"Reports\" section links the views.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the TSV rows become typed records (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH bench_row, an example_row with \":| example_verdict = | Valid | Invalid : i32 | NotWritten | SchemaUnloadable\"), written as JSON through json_schema and rendered from the typed rows, never by regex over text.\nNEXT STEP: check whether dir-tree-html renders .html files next to TSVs; emit the index from a Spiral cell in build (no new .ps1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 2u32, "2026-11-03T19:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:07 fiscal: DoD (1), (3) and (4) WRITTEN, unstaged in fiscal. (1)+TYPEFEATURESET: NEW src/reports.spi F198DEF3 (registered last in package.spiproj and spiral.toml): the TSVs become typed rows (test_row with ':| test_status = Passed | Failed | Static | Skipped | Unsupported | NotRun | TimedOut' parsed by lib case_labels.case_of_label, so no status string table; ':| reported_status = Known | Unknown' keeps an unexpected label; file_row with decimal seconds; bench_row; example_row with the planned ':| example_verdict = Valid | Invalid : i32 | NotWritten | Unmeasured'), rendered to target/ci-metrics/reports.md: stamp, status counts, every test that did not pass, the 10 slowest files, the bench, the example verdicts (cells escape '|'). Rendering goes through MARKDOWN tables on purpose: the page renderer (dir-tree-html now, html's HTML-CLI drop-in next) turns markdown into HTML, so fiscal adds no HTML code of its own and moves with the html repo (the 11-03 'finish html, retire dir-tree-html' priority). (3) the stamp: commit GITHUB_SHA, a run link from GITHUB_RUN_ID, build time from FISCAL_BUILD_TIME (build.ps1 sets it); a local build says so. (4) README Reports links reports.md first. Glue (no new .ps1): build.ps1 +4 lines (the stamp, 'reports' excluded from the main pass and run after the TSVs are written with FISCAL_METRICS_SUFFIX), publish.ps1 includes 'reports.md'. PROVEN on europa: --check with bodies exit 0; all 3 bodies as Rust exit 0; a real render of the box's regen7 TSVs printed the expected tables (19 failed generator tests of that red run listed, bench rows, slowest file). OPEN: DoD (2) the windows job's metrics on the page (only ubuntu publishes today; needs the push job to merge both artifacts), and the html renderer's view of .md files under target/ (verify on the first green page).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T19:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:11 fiscal: DoD (2) DESIGN, not applied today: fiscal's push job is the shared org helper verified_pages_push_job (i574n.github/scripts/pins/workflows.spi:217; YAML is generated from it, never hand-edited), and scripts/pins/{pins.ps1,workflow.spi,workflows.spi} carry another lane's unstaged edits right now. The change: a push-job variant taking extra artifact names, downloading ci-metrics-ubuntu-24.04 and ci-metrics-windows-2025 (actions/download-artifact@v8.0.2, already in fiscal's actions.lock, so the lock does not change) into gh-pages/target/ci-metrics-<os>/ before the deploy; each OS's reports.md then sits under its own os-labelled folder. Apply when the pins WIP lands (regenerate with pins.ps1, verify with gh actions-lock --no-fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T20:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:24 fiscal: REUSE: build.ps1's GitHub step summary no longer builds its own markdown tables in PowerShell (slowest 8 files, bench); it writes the heading line (label, file count, minutes) and appends target/ci-metrics/reports.md minus its title, so the summary and the published report come from the same typed rows (-5 PowerShell lines). Parse check 0 errors; the block was simulated with a sample reports.md (heading + report body).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T22:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:03 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793732410948-fiscal-confirm-landed2, t1101, pinned compiler core 2ABF22D79E6B6943 start and end, the landed files placed over the mirror and restored after): money 3/3, ledger 9/9, event_log 7/7, durable_file 3/3, lifecycle 10/10, document 6/6, p2p 14/14, posting 2/2, reports 3/3 -- every prediction met, every 'fails' negative recognized by Cells.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 6u32, "2026-11-04T05:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:28 fiscal: DoD (2) APPLIED (unstaged). The 11-03 blocker was another lane's pins WIP, untouched since 11-03 06:16, i.e. settled, so it is built on top: i574n.github/scripts/pins/org_jobs.spi gains artifacts_download (pattern) (path) and verified_pages_push_job_with (extra : list step), which inserts steps after the pages download; verified_pages_push_job = the [] case, so the other 6 workflows on the helper stay BYTE-IDENTICAL (checked: of all 11 org workflow files only fiscal's gh-pages.yml changed). workflows.spi fiscal (): the push job downloads pattern 'ci-metrics-*' into gh-pages/target, so each OS's metrics + reports.md land under gh-pages/target/ci-metrics-<os>/ (a pattern download does not fail when one OS's artifact is missing, unlike a by-name download). Regenerated with pins dist/workflows.exe --write: fiscal gh-pages.yml +5 lines (actions/download-artifact@v8.0.2, already in actions.lock); gh actions-lock --no-fix: valid. NOTE: the same --write also rewrote tibia's gh-pages.yml (pre-existing drift at line 73, not fiscal's); restored byte-identical and reported to tibia. PENDING: proof on CI at the user's next fiscal push (pages show target/ci-metrics-ubuntu-24.04/reports.md and ...-windows-2025/).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 7u32, "2026-11-05T07:41Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:4x compiler (ask from the SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL census, no action needed from compiler): fiscal/src/reports.spi:117 has 2 match arms that map union cases to their own names as string literals. They can become reflection::case_name x (or sm'::to_lower of it) over the !!!!UnionCaseName op (pack39+, box and node since 03:10). Example heals: spiral cells daemon.spi request_line, lib doc_blocks.spi level_tag (green 11-05). Your call when.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 8u32, "2026-11-05T13:50Z", "fiscal", "11-05 09:5x local fiscal: NAMEOF HEAL APPLIED in fiscal src (in place, unstaged; backup reports.before-nameof-8987026C.spi in the session scratchpad), answering compiler's 07:41 ask. src/reports.spi 8987026C -> E0F37B27: verdict_text keeps the Invalid n arm (payload, own text) and maps every other case through case_labels::label_of_name \"\" \" \" (reflection::case_name v), so NotWritten still prints 'not written' and Valid/Unmeasured print 'valid'/'unmeasured' byte-identically. case_labels::case_label could not be used: it enumerates get_union_fields_untag, which needs payload-less unions, and example_verdict has Invalid : i32. New assertion in tsv_rows_read_into_their_typed_columns pins all four outputs. Also healed the file's 4 respell-drift literals (true/false -> !+/!- in is_unknown, failing_lines, writes_the_ci_reports). Box checks with a pinned compiler copy (core 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3): format --check --respell-drift exit 0, --check exit 0 (29 s). PENDING: the Cells run of reports.spi's 4 rust tests on the NODE, job-1793886615820-fiscal-reports-gate, queued after the facet regen job (one Cells run per node), scratch tree only, mirror untouched.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 9u32, "2026-11-05T13:54Z", "fiscal", "11-05 09:5x local fiscal (follow-up): a whole-src format --check --respell-drift (14 files) found 2 more, both at HEAD bb1ebad, now fixed in place and unstaged (backups document.before-fmt-249C56E6.spi and generated_runtime.before-fmt-2F02F888.spi in the session scratchpad): document.spi 249C56E6 -> 667309A1 (3 true/false -> !+/!- literals in its tests) and generated_runtime.spi 2F02F888 -> D899E5DE (one formatter line wrap of sample_path_text; the emitted unit text is unchanged). Result: all 14 fiscal src files formatter- and respell-clean (exit 0), package --check exit 0 (box, pinned core 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3). This also removes a formatter-drift red that CI would have shown at HEAD. PENDING on the NODE: job-1793886615820-fiscal-reports-gate, widened before its start to gate reports.spi and document.spi from a fresh src zip 0A8C6282.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 10u32, "2026-11-05T14:00Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:0x local fiscal: TWO MORE NAMEOF HEALS in fiscal src (in place, unstaged; backups canon.before-nameof-8457C66F.spi, corpus_checks.before-nameof-2AC1F2A4.spi in the session scratchpad), from a src sweep for match arms that map a case to its own name (the SUNAT catalog codes and MyInvois versions are real code tables and stay literal). (1) canon.spi ubl_document_name = \"ubl-\" ++# case_labels::case_label \"Ubl\" \"\" document (prefix cut, no separator: UblCreditNote -> creditnote), new test each_ubl_document_is_named_by_its_case. (2) corpus_checks.spi kind_label = sm'::to_lower (sm'::replace \"Kind\" \"\" (reflection::case_name kind)), new test each_ubl_kind_names_its_manifest (pins kind_label for all 3 kinds and one full ubl_manifest path). Box: format --check --respell-drift exit 0 for both, package --check exit 0. PENDING on the NODE in the same queued job-1793886615820-fiscal-reports-gate (cap amended 1 h -> 3 h; script 743233C6, src zip 94D86AEA): reports + document + canon all tests, corpus_checks filtered to the new pin plus the two real-manifest tests (myinvois 22/22, sunat 28/15/15). BYTE CHECK for (1): the canon gate rewrites canon/en16931-terms.json, which keys 379 entries by these names; the node output must hash 12A85C78 like the repo's.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 11u32, "2026-11-05T14:35Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:5x local fiscal CORRECTION to my 10:0x note: the committed canon/en16931-terms.json (12A85C78) is pretty-printed CRLF, not the Spiral writer's compact LF output, so the node byte check must compare with the 11-02 Spiral baseline 9DBC4B63F0CA (52,597 bytes), not 12A85C78. The canon nameof heal is in fact ALREADY byte-proven: europa eff-1793888925 ran the healed ubl_document_name (in the same src) and its JSON, with the separate additive 'effective' field stripped, hashes 9DBC4B63F0CA exactly, so all 379 'ubl-invoice'/'ubl-creditnote' keys are unchanged.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 12u32, "2026-11-05T15:30Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:3x local fiscal: RUST BODY RUN ON EUROPA (chain eff-*1793892466; self-contained stage = box core + box lib + live fiscal src + the corpus parts these modules read (pe/ and the root ubl manifests); pinned copy of europa's installed compiler core dc49ffdc170199df; every non-'fails' test body compiled --backend Rust into one main, rustc -O, run): reports 4 bodies, document 3, lifecycle 7, posting 2, profiles 2, sunat 8 -- compile, rustc and run exit 0 for all six. The harness fails on a wrong pin (mutants earlier today on canon and pint_terms exited 1 with the exact message). The node Cells run (job-1793886615820, queued) stays as confirmation; it now also copies the gitignored oracle files (src/corpus.txt, patterns.txt, pattern_probes.txt, pattern_expected.txt) from the mirror into its tree, without which its corpus gate would have been VOID (a src zip never carries them). Here: reports.spi E0F37B27 (nameof heal + respell) 4 bodies incl. the new verdict pin, document.spi 667309A1 (respell) 3 bodies green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 13u32, "2026-11-05T15:35Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:3x local fiscal: corpus_checks heal FIXED + PROVEN. My 10:0x pin test each_ubl_kind_names_its_manifest had a parse error (its '? cond' continued on a line starting '||' at the same indent as '?'), and the compiler silently LEFT THE BLOCK OUT of the module: format --check and --check were both green on the box; only the europa --backend Rust compile warned (ParserErrors, 'Expected: then'). Fixed in place (labels bound first, continuation indented): corpus_checks.spi -> EFD329A3, format clean. EUROPA eff-cc1793892778 (filter: the pin + every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes + every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit, which exercise kind_label on all three kinds against the real manifests): compile, rustc, run exit 0. No other module run today printed ParserErrors. Node zip re-shipped (BE4D67E0) while job-1793886615820 is still queued.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 14u32, "2026-11-05T18:58Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:0x local fiscal: the CI report gains a CANON CENSUS section (reports.spi A135648B, unstaged): after the examples table, reports.md shows per family how the 25 required EN 16931 terms are covered: NF-e 4.00 13 bound / 2 implied / 3 derived / 3 national code / 4 not carried; CFDI 4.0 13 / 1 / 4 / 3 / 4. Built from the typed tables in canon_nfe / canon_cfdi (a ':== census' record per family, gap kinds counted from canon_coverage's ':| gap'), not from text. Test the_canon_census_counts_each_family pins both rows. EUROPA: all 5 reports bodies (incl. writes_the_ci_reports, which renders it) compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; GRANULAR 0 code overages. In the queued node Cells job-1793886615820 (zip re-shipped).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 15u32, "2026-11-05T20:15Z", "fiscal", "11-05 16:1x local fiscal: two node runs came back VOID (environment, not code), both from the t1101 mirror's STALE lib/spiral: it lacks the box-only lib modules ledger / money (landed unstaged on the box 11-03), xml.first_difference_by (landed today) and xsd_emit.dereferenced_parts, and it still orders modules by package.spiproj, so an xml_codec copied in ahead of decimal cannot see decimal. (1) src Cells job-1793886615820: every module failed together (the package type check needs posting -> ledger / money and canon_coverage -> dereferenced_parts); stopped by me. (2) MyInvois twin job-1793895376229: the regen compile failed (xml_codec: Unbound decimal; document_syntax: Unbound read_text / decoded_by / present). FIX: both now unpack the BOX lib/spiral (lib.zip 1C36B453, toml-ordered, the lib every europa proof used) into their scratch trees. RE-QUEUED in priority order behind the running facet-extra gates job-1793908968483 (which uses the facet gate's proven setup and is unaffected): job-1793909583928-fiscal-twin2 (script FE325247), then job-1793909634925-fiscal-reports-gate2 (script 89E28B5A, src zip D742F390). The europa Rust body runs of every module stay the landing evidence; these are the Cells confirmations, pending on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 16u32, "2026-11-05T23:20Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:2x local fiscal: pages now also publish fiscal's Cells notebook pages (main's PAGES-NOTEBOOK-PUBLISH ask): scripts/publish.ps1 -Include adds '*.spi.html','*.spi.ipynb','*.spi.livemd' (as tibia; publish-tree lists untracked files without --exclude-standard, so the gitignored notebooks/ is picked up; 19 html + 19 ipynb present locally). gh-pages.yml already runs publish.ps1 after build.ps1 under !cancelled() on ubuntu, so no workflow edit. Unstaged. STILL OPEN for Done: DoD (2) 'the index compares them' (each OS lands its own reports.md under gh-pages/target/ci-metrics-<os>/, nothing compares the two yet), plus the CI proof of every DoD at the user's next fiscal push (none since bb1ebad0).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 17u32, "2026-11-06T08:17Z", "fiscal", "11-05/06: node reports-gate2 (job-1793909634925, lib A14FBC87, src 7EACA360) result UNKNOWN: laptop node unreachable on <moon-lan-addr> and <moon-ts-addr> since ~22:40. DoD (2) cross-OS comparison still open. Next step: one job status once the node is back, then delete my node stage dirs.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 18u32, "2026-11-06T08:24Z", "fiscal", "Star exchange 11-06: (main #6) run the Linux half of the cross-OS comparison on a codespace, not a capped europa (ld bus error under MemoryMax = VOID); (kit #1) on 'no route' read the node-side job log before any relaunch. Dep on NODE-LAPTOP-DROPS-OFF-NETWORK for the node half.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 19u32, "2026-11-06T10:11Z", "fiscal", "11-06 06:11 reports-gate2 VERDICT: RED (executed > 0, failed > 0), one root cause = package type error FISCAL-CANON-PINT-UNBOUND; not 70 separate test failures. Node raw outputs are in C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fiscal-reports\\*.txt (to delete once fixed).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 20u32, "2026-11-06T10:13Z", "fiscal", "Groom 06:13 (compiler 06:12 #1): spiral gh-pages cells-gate runs only on schedule/dispatch, so the post-push proof comes from the next SCHEDULED run log. (x-dumps #1) the report check must cover the render path: a field in the typed rows but absent from the page type is a silent drop. (tibia #2) full node stdout is at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\jobs\\<id>\\stdout.log on the job host.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 21u32, "2026-11-06T14:49Z", "fiscal", "10:4x PROOF GREEN, node: gate3 (job-1793964046801, core A688EE5A) + gate3b (job-1793967659042, core 24D39673, the 5 modules gate3 left VOID, now staged with fiscal/canon, samples and the box eu/peppol-pint incl. syntax pages): ALL 15 report/canon modules pass on fresh Cells stages: reports 5/5, document 6/6, canon 5/5, pint_terms 3/3, canon_coverage 2/2, canon_nfe 4/4, canon_cfdi 4/4, canon_codes 2/2, canon_derived 3/3, lifecycle 13/13, posting 3/3, sunat 9/9, profiles 4/4, corpus 1/1, corpus_checks 3/3 = 72 tests, 0 failed. Note the node's compiler core changed between the two runs (A688 -> 24D3). Remaining for DoD (2): the cross-OS comparison on a codespace (Linux) vs these Windows results. Node stage dirs deleted.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 22u32, "2026-11-06T20:52Z", "fiscal", "16:5x CI PROOF read (GitHub, fiscal gh-pages deploy f6f01e99 @ 2026-11-06T05:00Z, run 42146976275 green): DoD (2) MET: gh-pages target/ci-metrics-ubuntu-24.04/ and target/ci-metrics-windows-2025/ both published (309 entries each, reports.md + examples.tsv + bench.tsv in each). DoD (3) MET: the windows reports.md opens with commit f6f01e99, run link 42146976275, built 2026-11-06 02:04 UTC, Tests 193 passed 0 failed. DoD (4): README Reports links reports.md (11-03). DoD (1) GAP, named: the page root index.html (dir-tree-html) LINKS reports.md but does not render it (no table in the page; .nojekyll serves the .md as plain text). By the 11-03 design fiscal emits markdown and the shared page renderer turns it into HTML, so the remaining step belongs to the renderer: the html repo's HTML-CLI drop-in rendering .md files under target/. Resume when: that renderer is on the pages job; then re-read the page. 90%.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 23u32, "2026-11-06T20:54Z", "fiscal", "DoD: (1) rendered HTML report views (examples, bench, slowest files, tests by status) linked from the page root; (2) both OS jobs publish metrics under os-labelled folders; (3) the page shows commit, run and build time; (4) README Reports links the views. Status 16:5x: (2)-(4) met on CI f6f01e99; (1) waits on the page renderer turning reports.md into HTML.\nNEXT: re-read the pages once the HTML-CLI renderer runs in the pages job.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 24u32, "2026-11-07T21:24Z", "fiscal", "11-07 17:2x DoD (1) re-checked against both renderers (read-only): fiscal's pages render through spiral scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, which pins the dir-tree-html repo at a643950e. Both the pin and dir-tree-html HEAD (7 commits later) render markdown ONLY for the page root README.md (shared.spi readme_html options.dir; dtl_markdown), never per directory or per file, so target/ci-metrics-<os>/reports.md stays plain text and a README.md rename would not help. The html repo's html_pages/file_views.spi DOES render any .md as prose (viewer_of maps c.md to the markdown viewer; test a_markdown_file_renders_as_a_readme_section). So nothing remains on fiscal's side: reports.md is already the typed, rendered-to-markdown output (and gains the Modeling ceiling section with FISCAL-MODELING-CEILING-1-TABLE). Resume when: the org page tool renders per-file .md (dir-tree-html.ps1 moves to html's pages tool, or dir-tree-html gains a .md file viewer and its pin is bumped); then check gh-pages target/ci-metrics-ubuntu-24.04/reports.md renders as HTML and close.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 25u32, "2026-11-09T05:45Z", "fiscal", "11-09 RE-READ (read-only): the pages serve index.html (200), but target/ci-metrics/reports.md (and any .html of it) is 404. Not a renderer issue: fiscal CI has been RED since 11-07 and fails at family-gates.ps1 BEFORE the reports unit runs (FISCAL-MANIFEST-DRIFT-GUARD n3/n4), so no reports.md is produced or published. Meanwhile target/ci-metrics/modeling-ceiling.tsv IS published (an earlier run). Blocker: the CI-red fix (generated/family-gates.tsv missing at family-gates.ps1; repro in flight on ganymede). NEXT STEP: once CI is green, re-read reports.md on the pages (the DoD's renderer question then applies).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 26u32, "2026-11-09T07:17Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 UNBLOCKED in the tree (unstaged, takes effect on the user's next push): (1) the CI red's ubuntu cause is fixed (generator writes_the_family_gate_table now creates generated/ first; Linux control/fix proof on ganymede, FISCAL-MANIFEST-DRIFT-GUARD n6); (2) build.ps1 8505AA3C+ catches a family-gates.ps1 throw into the problems list, so even a RED run now continues to the reports unit (build.ps1 runs it before the final problems throw) and publishes reports.md plus every metrics table. NEXT STEP unchanged: after the next push, re-read target/ci-metrics/reports.md on the pages and apply the DoD's renderer question.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 27u32, "2026-11-09T08:36Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 RENDERER CHECK on the live pages (i574n.github.io/fiscal, deploy 518c4abe): the dir-tree-html index LINKS target/ci-metrics/reports.md, but that file is 404 (the red run's reports unit never ran; the build.ps1 catch now lets it run on red), and markdown is NOT rendered: README.md is served raw (200, 18829 bytes) and README.md.html is 404. So the DoD's 'renderer turns markdown into HTML' does not hold today: dir-tree-html links .md files as-is. Options: (a) html's HTML-CLI drop-in (the planned renderer) renders .md to HTML; (b) build.ps1 also writes reports.html via a lib markdown renderer, if one exists. NEXT: check whether lib or html has a markdown-to-HTML function before choosing; otherwise the gap waits on the html repo's renderer, not fiscal.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 28u32, "2026-11-09T08:38Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 RENDERER ANSWER: no fiscal-side HTML needed. The html repo's page renderer (html_pages/file_views.spi) already has typed viewers: Prose for .md (test a_markdown_file_renders_as_a_readme_section: '# T' renders as a README section), Delimited for .tsv (a header + rows table), Source for .spi (pre/code, escaped), Picture and Diagram (.mmd). So reports.md AND every target/ci-metrics/*.tsv (gate-cost, growth, tests, modeling-ceiling) render as pages the moment fiscal's pages job switches from dir-tree-html (which links .md raw: README.md is served as plain text, README.md.html is 404) to html's renderer, the DoD's planned 'HTML-CLI drop-in'. The remaining step is outside fiscal: the shared push job (org's verified_pages_push_job) adopting html's CLI. Fiscal side complete once a run publishes reports.md, which the build.ps1 catch now ensures even on a red run.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 29u32, "2026-11-09T11:36Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Wait: when the user pushes fiscal (reports.md publishes even on red) and lane org (shared push job switches dir-tree-html to html renderer)")
inl kit_train_snapshot_pin () = Task ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", "launch-train always snapshots kit AND pins the lib: the train copies the kit tree (existing -Snapshot) and a lib snapshot (passed as release-train -Lib), so lib lands and lane edits never mix versions inside a running train (main 11-01 20:2x)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,release,train,lib,team:rig,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin () = Planning ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kit_no_escaped_daemons () = Task ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", "No process started through kit may escape its session: kit process start-under-shell parents to the caller's owner session (not explorer) and stays in the job; Cells' compiler servers die with their daemon (user 11-01 20:4x: \"check why kit let all these processes dangle without a parent\")", Story, P1, D3, 65u32, Active, "", "kit,jobs,processes,cells,resilience,team:rig,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons () = Planning ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_1 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T00:47Z", "kit", "11-01 20:46 kit ANALYSIS (box, 20:4x): 14 processes had a dead parent. Kit's share: two Cells compiler servers (dotnet SpiralCompiler.dll --server-tcp ... --stall-seconds 120, started 10-30 22:06 and 10-31 12:40, idle 2 MB) whose parent, the Cells BEAM daemon, was gone; both STOPPED by kit (no established connections). CHAIN: (1) Cells starts its compiler DAEMON through kit (compiler_client.ex daemon_start: kit process start-under-shell); (2) kit_os_launch kit_parented_start uses CREATE_BREAKAWAY_FROM_JOB (flags 0x0900_0220) and, with no owner, parents to GetShellWindow's process = EXPLORER, so the daemon leaves the caller's kit job (whose container allows breakaway, limits 0x2800 = KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE|BREAKAWAY_OK) and outlives every session; (3) the daemon spawns --server-tcp servers and, when it exits, does not stop them; (4) the server has no idle exit or parent watch (--stall-seconds only bounds an outstanding compile, Program.fs:983). This contradicts the rule that kit processes belong to their session (memory kit-live-parent-every-process: never explorer-parent). Others' orphans (not touched): idle interactive pwsh shells, a claude-boost-watcher, a codespaces ssh, a 20:19 europa probe ssh without BatchMode (fixed in remote.ps1 since), and a 20:26 pwsh loop syncing linux-1101. FIX PLAN: (a) kit: kit_shell_parented_start passes the caller owner (kit_caller_owner) instead of 0, so the parent is the session, never explorer; drop CREATE_BREAKAWAY_FROM_JOB from the tries so the process stays in the caller's job and KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE reaps it with the session; keep BREAKAWAY_OK only if a proven caller needs it (audit first); (b) compiler host: --server-tcp exits when its parent pid is gone or after N idle minutes without a session (compiler lane); (c) Cells: the daemon stops its servers on exit (x lane). DoD: after a notebook batch and the end of its session, no SpiralCompiler --server-tcp or Cells BEAM survives (a process census before/after); a kit job end leaves 0 descendants; tests for the owner choice (owner pid used, explorer never). NEXT: (a) in kit_os_launch (rides TRAIN9) plus the census check as a kit machine watch rule (orphan = dead-parent process whose image is in a kit-launched family).")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_2 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:56Z", "kit", "11-01 20:56 kit: compiler's side (b) is drafted for the next pack (CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL): serveSessions exits after SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS with no session (opt-in; it never fires mid-session; it deletes the socket/.pid/.bridge files). A parent watch ALREADY exists behind SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID, but the leaked servers were spawned without it. So the spawner (the Cells daemon, x lane) must set BOTH SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID=<daemon pid> and SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS (for example 600) when it starts a --server-tcp server. Added to (c).")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_3 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:01Z", "kit", "11-01 21:01 kit: x confirms Cells has set SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID on every spawned --server-tcp since 7a4c960e (11-01 09:48, compiler_daemon.ex:1162 port_env = the daemon's os pid), so the stopped pair (10-30/10-31) predates the fix; x adds SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=600 to the same port_env. Cells does not need the daemon to outlive its session (cross-session reuse only saves warm-up, and the daemon already idle-retires), so (a) the kit change is unblocked for TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_4 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:23Z", "kit", "11-01 21:23 kit: (a) DONE in the tree (unstaged, TRAIN9). kit_os_launch: kit_shell_parented_start passes the caller's owner (kit_caller_owner) as the parent; kit_parented_start no longer falls back to GetShellWindow (explorer) when the owner is 0, so the child stays a plain child of its caller; CREATE_BREAKAWAY_FROM_JOB is dropped from the creation tries (0x0900_0220 -> 0x0800_0220), so the process stays inside the caller's kit job and KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE reaps it with the session; the unused user32 externs are removed; the help texts (direct_verbs.spi, run.spi) now say \"the caller's session as its live parent, inside the caller's kit job\". Ratchet ok. Remaining: TRAIN9 regen and install, then the DoD census (a notebook batch plus session end leave no Cells BEAM or --server-tcp behind).")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_5 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 5u32, "2026-11-02T12:26Z", "resilience", "11-02 08:1x resilience post-analysis census (pre-TRAIN9-install): the pattern persists -- box had 15 dead-parent orphans incl 3 spiral-bin dotnet (57h/43h/6h), CLAUDE_CODE_SHELL_LAUNCHER pwsh, gh codespace logs, ssh codespaces; all reaped. Added a box-side JANITOR complementing kit's upstream fix: i574n.github/scripts/orphan-reaper.ps1 (dead-parent, class-tiered grace compiler/remote 60m vs shells 12h, preserves boost-watcher/mirror singletons, -DryRun lists live orphans). Use orphan-reaper -DryRun as the DoD census tool. Verification signal: once TRAIN9 installs and the Cells daemon sets PARENT_PID+IDLE_EXIT, the janitor should trend to 0 finds.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_6 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T00:50Z", "resilience", "11-02 20:48 resilience: DoD CENSUS VERIFIED POSITIVE (the signal n5 predicted: \"once TRAIN9 installs the janitor trends to 0\"). Ran the designated census (orphan-reaper -DryRun = 0 past-grace, + a direct dead-parent census of ANY age): 22 dead-parent procs total, ZERO kit-launched family - no dotnet, no SpiralCompiler --server-tcp, no erl/beam/epmd with a dead parent. BEFORE/AFTER: n5's 08:1x census found 3 escaped spiral-bin dotnet daemons (57h/43h/6h); NOW 0, AND it holds DURING a live 59-notebook batch (TRAIN13c running as measured) - so kit-launched compiler servers no longer escape their session. TRAIN9 parenting fix (a: caller-owner parent, no explorer, no CREATE_BREAKAWAY, KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE) + Cells PARENT_PID/IDLE_EXIT (c) are confirmed WORKING post-install (current kit is TRAIN11-era, so TRAIN9 shipped). The 22 dead-parent procs are all NON-kit families, correctly out of this item's scope: 3 git (Claude-Code Fork-lineage, reaper 3m short-grace - the KIT-ORPHAN-SIM short tier, NOT kit-launched), 2 pwsh (by-design detached shells, 720m grace), 1 waitfor (subagent background-waitfor, legit), ~16 Windows service-manager-parented OS/app services (tailscale/rustdesk/mariadbd/gfx/audio - parentless by design, never orphans). REMAINING to close: the owner-choice unit tests (owner pid used, explorer never) + (b) compiler --server-tcp idle-exit fully landed/verified. The census-based DoD (no SpiralCompiler/BEAM survives a batch) PASSES. Bump 40->65.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_7 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 7u32, "2026-11-03T23:07Z", "resilience", "11-03 19:05 resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON AUDIT (box-independent; read the fresh 18:57 resource-report + tied to the live 100%-CPU starvation). FINDING: the invariant currently HOLDS. resource-report.ps1's section \"box processes by name, outside any live kit job's tree and any Claude session, >=200MB WS (candidates for dangling)\" is EMPTY - zero escaped daemons. All box CPU is legitimate lane work under live claude.exe session trees (kit 25 procs/302 CpuSec incl TRAIN17, compiler 14/50, fiscal 16/70, main/x/tibia). So: (a) the no-escaped-daemons invariant is satisfied right now; (b) resource-report.ps1 is ALREADY the live monitor for this (its dangling-candidates section is the detector) - the item's \"make orphans simulable\" (cf KIT-ORPHAN-SIM) is the gap, not detection; (c) the current critical-mirror backup-failure starvation is genuine fleet load (TRAIN17 + compiles), NOT reapable orphans - it eases when TRAIN17 finishes, no CPU to reclaim. Evidence baseline for the item; no enforcement change needed today.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_8 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 8u32, "2026-11-04T11:27Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-04 ~07:3x resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON RE-AUDIT (under today's heavy churn: SI retune, multi-lane builds, a 90pct-CPU BEAM run). Census: 0 kit-launch-type procs (dotnet/pwsh/erl/beam.smp/mix/escript/SpiralCompiler/node/cargo/rustc) with a DEAD parent AND outside any live claude.exe or kit job root. INVARIANT HOLDS - no kit-launched daemon escaped its session. The box's dead-parent procs are all legit non-kit (firefox, rustdesk, mariadbd, git fsmonitor--daemon [by-design --detach], ms-teams, winlogon, igfx). Resilience-audit half stays green; remaining enforcement (kit process start-under-shell parenting) is team:kit. Re-run each groom via the process-health sweep.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_9 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 9u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "resilience", "11-04 star-exchange ASK (resilience->kit): kit job wait should EXIT when its controlling shell dies. Today a backgrounded `kit job wait <id> | tail` left the kit-job-wait process ALIVE after TaskStop (it reparented to a harness process) and orphaned a tail.exe (user flagged dangling procs). This extends the no-escape invariant to the job-wait waiter specifically.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_10 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 10u32, "2026-11-05T04:07Z", "resilience", "DETECTION signature from real lineage (resilience, frame 2026-11-04 23:38, traced all 61 kit-relevant procs to root): an escaped process is one whose parent chain roots at explorer/wininit/sh (shell or session-manager) instead of the kit job host or the owning lane session. Evidence: ZERO kit-adjacent trees root at a claude owner session; the BEAM/Elixir daemons are the concrete escapees - dotnet<erl<erl<sh, erl<erl<sh, erl<sh all root at a bare git-bash sh, not a kit job object, which is exactly the Cells compiler-servers-should-die-with-their-daemon case (a shell that can exit out from under them). No kit.exe/job-host tree existed in the frame (kit CLI is short-lived), so the escape SURFACE is the long-lived BEAM/compiler daemons, not kit's own process. Also: Claude tool pwsh children root at windowsterminal<explorer not at the claude process, so lane tool-subprocs are not reapable via claude lineage. Detection is un-gated and now specified; the FIX (kit process start-under-shell must parent to the owner session + enroll the tree in a kit job object so it dies with the daemon) is kit-team gated. Pairs with KIT-ORPHAN-SIM proc-frame.v1. resilience.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_11 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 11u32, "2026-11-05T20:22Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-05 ~12:2x resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON RE-AUDIT (resilience-audit half; point-in-time, box). INVARIANT HOLDS: 0 kit-launched-family procs (dotnet/erl/beam.smp/epmd/mix/escript/SpiralCompiler/cargo/rustc/node) with a DEAD immediate parent. All 6 live kit-family procs have LIVE parents: erl 8852<-22316, dotnet 21380/20532/18980<-17904, erl 3816<-23836, erl 5972<-3816. No daemon escaped its session. Fast-screen method: dead-immediate-parent is the necessary condition; 0 hits means the fuller root-lineage trace (note 77: chain rooting at sh/explorer) is not needed this tick. Latent escape surface (BEAM under a still-alive git-bash sh that orphans on shell-exit) unchanged + kit-tree gated. Half stays green.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_12 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 12u32, "2026-11-06T02:18Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-05 ~22:2x resilience WIFI-NODE JOB VALIDITY AUDIT (user ask). Checked all 500 kit jobs on moon (wifi node). ALL VALID (consistent records, no corrupt/phantom states; kit heartbeat reclassifies dead-supervisor jobs as lost, so no silent zombies). States: 435 finished, 50 stopped, 7 timed-out (clean wall-clock, tree stopped), 3 lost (exit125 memory-reaper kills, trees ended), 2 spawn-failed (exit125 \"spawn -File: program not found\" = kit-size-tablelogs/noteedit launcher bad path), 2 running (supervisors beating), 1 queued. ESCAPED-DAEMON INVARIANT HOLDS on wifi node: 0 kit-family procs (dotnet/erl/beam/epmd/mix/escript/SpiralCompiler/cargo/rustc/node) with a dead parent; the lost jobs leaked nothing (job tree ended with the supervisor). SURFACED (other lanes): fiscal-twin2 running ~6h with stdout frozen at 667B + fiscal-reports-gate2 queued behind it ~6h (fiscal to judge legit-long vs hung; not an orphan); 2 spawn-failed kit-size jobs = kit launcher -File path bug. Did not touch other lanes jobs. resilience-614162e5.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_13 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 13u32, "2026-11-06T08:27Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 04:27 kit groom, CPU-light fix from the x-dumps star lesson: scheduled task kit-machine-watch-hourly was Priority 7 (below normal) with ExecutionTimeLimit PT72H and MultipleInstances IgnoreNew, so one stalled run would have silently skipped every hourly sweep for up to 72 h. Set to Priority 5 and PT50M (limit below the hourly cadence; normal priority so a busy box does not starve it into the limit, task result 267014). Last result before the change: 0 at 04:17. Revert: Priority 7, PT72H.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_14 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 14u32, "2026-11-06T10:14Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 06:1x kit groom 2, star exchange consolidation: two false orphans from resilience: git fsmonitor--daemon is parentless by design and respawns when killed (disable core.fsmonitor per repo instead), and a harness stop of a bash watcher leaves the git-bash launcher and its child alive (kill the tree by pid). The sweep should classify both rather than flag or kill them.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_15 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 15u32, "2026-11-06T11:27Z", "resilience-614162e5", "empirical catalog from resilience 11-06 orphan sweep (data, not a claim) - four distinct \"escaped daemon\" classes, each a DIFFERENT fix (do not treat parentless uniformly): (1) git fsmonitor--daemon = parentless BY DESIGN (--detach) and churns on Windows; not a leak, killing respawns it - heal = disable per-repo core.fsmonitor. (2) ssh ProxyJump -W helpers = orphan when the outer ssh is killed by external timeout; the -W stdio-forwarder clings to an already-dead session (looks bound, refuses) - heal = trap-EXIT cleanup, carry key via -i through -J (no agent), bound with ssh ConnectTimeout not external timeout. (3) a bash/pwsh watcher survives a harness/background STOP (TaskStop ends the task record, NOT the OS process; git-bash launcher+child keeps running) - heal = kill the process TREE by pid, verify gone. (4) memory-reaper 125-lost = the supervisor killed under box memory pressure (3GB+ job on a box with <3GB free). DETECTION that worked: parent-DEAD AND no ESTABLISHED tcp AND age>Nmin = leaked; parent-DEAD but detached-daemon or live-child = valid. Refs in resilience notes on NODE-ALWAYS-FED/ssh-chain-orphans.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_16 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 16u32, "2026-11-07T15:52Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: turn resilience's 11-06 catalog of four escaped-daemon classes into kit job doctor findings, one per class, each with its own heal text (git fsmonitor: disable per repo, never kill; ssh ProxyJump -W helpers: trap-exit cleanup; plus the other two), building on the UnwatchedJob finding added 11-06. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: escaped_class union with one case per catalog class, each finding carrying pid, parent chain and heal; no string classes.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_17 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 17u32, "2026-11-08T05:11Z", "resilience", "11-08 ~01:08 resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON SWEEP (box at 100pct CPU, healthy multi-lane fleet). INVARIANT HOLDS: orphan-reaper -DryRun=0 past-grace; direct any-age fast-screen = 15 live kit-family procs (dotnet/erl/beam/escript/rustc/cargo/node) ALL with LIVE parents (erl<-pwsh, rustc+cargo<-rustup, escript<-gleam chains = legit build+BEAM trees), 0 dead-parent kit-family. The 100pct CPU is legit lane contention (box is the user current laptop; top consumers are the lane claude.exe sessions + their gate/build .ps1 jobs: box-law-gate, launch-train, lib_gate, node-proof), NOT reapable orphans. Resilience-audit half stays green; remaining job-doctor-findings + owner-choice unit tests = team:kit.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_18 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 18u32, "2026-11-09T11:24Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:4x local rig, the recorded next step as a pure model (unprobed, probe batch after TRAIN42e): src/rig_job_escaped/escaped.spi (HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0): process_facts record (name, command, parent_alive, live_child, established_tcp, age_minutes) and escaped_class union with one case per resilience 11-06 catalog class plus the two valid outcomes: GitFsMonitor (never reaped; heal: disable core.fsmonitor), SshForwarder (-W helper left by a timed-out ssh), StoppedWatcher (a bash/pwsh outliving its stopped task), Leaked (dead parent, no child, no connection, past a 60 min grace), Attached (live parent), Detached (parentless but working or still young). class_of follows the catalog's detection rule (dead parent AND no ESTABLISHED tcp AND old = leaked; a live child or connection = valid); heal_of gives one heal text per class; reapable is true only for SshForwarder, StoppedWatcher and Leaked. Catalog class 4 (memory-reaper 125-lost) is a JOB state, not a process, and is already reported by job list (lost, exit 125). Next: job doctor reads the facts (process table + parent liveness + tcp state) and prints one finding per escaped process with its class and heal. TypeFeatures: escaped_class union, process_facts record.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_19 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 19u32, "2026-11-09T23:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate on ganymede, off-train (rig_job_escaped/escaped.spi 2/2 (the escaped-class catalogue and the reap scope); Cells run_notebook --gate, rust target, rig's probe layout). The first full off-train batch had shown this package half-proven (first test 'spiral not loaded'); a warm re-run passed every test, so that was a cold-start artifact of the first batch, not the package. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_20 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 20u32, "2026-11-09T23:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:4x rig: parked on train:TRAIN44. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step is a walk, a store fed by a heartbeat, or wiring into shared kit code (agile next / todo scan / job host), which goes into TRAIN44 with its own regen and crate-gate proof.")
inl kit_hidden_verb_flags () = Task ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", "Hidden or internal kit verbs (job host, supervise ...) refuse unknown flags such as --help instead of starting the real thing (x-dumps 11-01 23:0x: kit job host --help started a real job host over ssh)", TaskKind, P2, D1, 85u32, Planned, "", "kit,cli,jobs,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags () = Planning ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_1 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T03:09Z", "kit", "11-01 23:09 kit. WHY: on europa, kit job host --help started a real job host (it supervised nothing and was killed), right next to the pod's single host, which risks the single-host rule. DoD: every internal verb (job host, job supervise, the host's run entry) refuses any argument it does not define with exit 2 and a one-line usage, and --help/-h prints usage without side effects; a CLI test runs kit job host --help and asserts exit 2 plus no host.pid written. NEXT: find the job host entry's argument parse (kit_job_host host_run.spi host_run reads argument 3/4 for owner pid/start) and add an unknown-flag refusal. TYPEFEATURES: a typed internal_args union (HostArgs owner start | HelpAsked | Unknown flag) instead of positional decimal_u64 reads.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_2 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T04:57Z", "kit", "IN TREE (TRAIN9): kit_jobs/jobs.spi JobHost refuses when argument 3 starts with \"-\" (\"job host is started by kit itself and takes no flags\"), so `kit job host --help` no longer starts a shared host. Found while there: job_command_of in kit_jobs/model.spi is a hand-written word->case map (13 arms). reflection.union_try_pick matches case names or their lowercase, so the migration means renaming JobStart.. to bare verbs, which collide with other unions wherever kit_jobs.model is opened. Deferred to its own change, with a census of the colliding names first.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_3 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:24Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 10:2x job_command_of MIGRATED to reflection (unstaged, src/kit_jobs/model.spi): optionm'.default_value JobUnknown (reflection.union_try_pick (\"job\" ++# word)). union_try_pick matches a case name exactly or its lowercase, so 'start' -> 'jobstart' = lower(JobStart); the Job prefix stays, so the bare-verb collision census that deferred this (n2) is moot: no case renamed. New test every_job_verb_is_its_case_name_without_the_job_prefix: all 13 verbs, 'Start', 'restart' and '' -> JobUnknown. NODE (job-1793628460234): kit_jobs model 9/9. COST, measured: jobs.rs 553 -> 637 (+84): union_try_pick builds the field list twice (exact + lowercased). Kept anyway: the user's no-hand-written-string<->case-map rule outranks my own no-growth rule while the crate is far under the 1000 gate. Follow-up for lib: a lower-only pick (one list) would recover most of the +84 for every caller. Also in this train: the job-host flag refusal message ('job job host') fixed in kit_jobs/jobs.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_4 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T07:34Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 17 h ago by kit, progress kept at 60%. Resume from that note: e while the crate is far under the 1000 gate. Follow-up for lib: a lower-only pick (one list) would recover most of the +84 for every caller. Also in this train: the job-host flag refusal message ('job job host') fixed in kit_jobs/jobs.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_5 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 5u32, "2026-11-04T20:19Z", "kit", "11-04 20:5x kit: half verified on the INSTALLED kit: `kit job host --bogus` refuses (\"job host is started by kit itself and takes no flags; see job --help\") and starts nothing. `kit job supervise --bogus` exits 125 with NO message: it does not appear to start a supervisor, but it does not name the problem either. LEFT: supervise (and the other internal verbs) print the same refusal line as host.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_6 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 6u32, "2026-11-04T20:21Z", "kit", "11-04 21:1x kit: supervise half BUILT (unstaged): kit_job_entry JobSupervise now refuses an empty operand or any operand starting with \"-\" with \"kit error: job supervise is started by kit itself for one job id and takes no flags; see job --help\" (the same rejected path and wording as host), instead of the silent exit 125 seen on the installed kit; the real callers (kit_job_host host_run, kit_job_host_request) always pass a job-... id, so they are unaffected. europa --check ok. Rides the next train after TRAIN23 (proof: `kit job supervise --help` prints the refusal and starts nothing). With host and supervise covered, the remaining internal verbs (run-serial is a --flag OF chain, not a verb) need no guard.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_7 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 7u32, "2026-11-04T22:02Z", "kit", "11-04 18:0x kit: CLI check WRITTEN (unstaged) in kit_jobs/stop_cli.spi, internal_job_verbs_refuse_flags_instead_of_starting: `job supervise --help` and `job supervise` (no id) exit 2 with \"supervise is started by kit itself for one job id and takes no flags\", and `job host --help` exits 2 with the host refusal (rejected returns 2). The existing refused_adoption check passes a job id to supervise, so it is unaffected. Rides the next train after TRAIN25 (TRAIN25's snapshot predates the supervise guard).")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_8 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 8u32, "2026-11-06T08:21Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 04:1x kit groom: parked Active to Planned, untouched since 11-04 (over 24 h; WIP cap: Active means touched within 48 h, and kit held 42 Active). Progress kept. Resume order unchanged; the next installable train (TRAIN33, link lost, result unread) carries no change to this item unless its last note says so.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_9 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 9u32, "2026-11-06T10:14Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 06:1x kit groom 2, star exchange consolidation: second case, from compiler and tibia independently: kit job tail <id> --lines 60 returns ok with 0 lines, while kit job tail <id> 60 works. An unknown flag on a public verb silently changes the result. DoD widened: every verb refuses an unknown flag with exit 2 and names the valid form; job tail also accepts --lines n and --all. Resilience adds the caller side: Start-Process -ArgumentList split an alarm text into 20 operands and kit refused with rc 2 for a week unnoticed, so strict verbs must print the refused argv in the error.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_10 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 10u32, "2026-11-08T04:19Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 00:2x kit: job tail FIXED for TRAIN40 (kit_job_control/control.spi): the line count was read as decimal_u64 of argument 4, so --lines 60 parsed as 0 and printed 0 lines with an ok receipt. Now tail_count accepts no argument (20), a plain count, --lines <n> and --all, and anything else exits 2 naming the valid forms. Test a_tail_count_is_a_number_lines_or_all_and_nothing_else. The rest of this item (every verb refuses unknown flags) stays open. Proof pending: node probe ai.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_11 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 11u32, "2026-11-09T06:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:2x local rig, a --help sweep with the TRAIN41 kit over 8 verbs: standards, agile edit, job, metrics, lint, window, memory, schedule. Six answer with usage (as a kit error line, acceptable). TWO STILL WRONG: (1) kit standards --help reads --help as a PACKAGE PATH (prints --help:0 package not a directory) and still ends with a kit standards ok receipt (packages=0 findings=1), so a mistyped argument reads as success, the exact class this item exists for; (2) kit agile edit --help prints a metadata line (name=agile effect=mutate handler=agile) instead of usage, and the agile edit usage text elsewhere omits the flags it actually accepts: --parent <EPIC>, --wait <kind>:<value>|--clear, --split milestones (tonight rig found each only by reading source). Fix: standards refuses an argument that starts with -- and is not a known flag (exit 2, naming the valid forms); agile edit --help prints the full usage including those three flags; a test row each. Code for TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_12 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 12u32, "2026-11-09T14:34Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 10:3x microblog recheck of rig's n10 two defects on the installed kit (11-08). (2) agile edit --help: now prints the agile usage line (summary=... then 'usage: kit agile: init ...'). Improved; whether it lists --parent/--wait/--split is rig's to confirm. (1) standards --help: STILL reads --help as a package path ('--help:0 package not a directory'). The exit is now 1, so a script sees failure, but the receipt still says 'kit standards ok packages=0 ... findings=1', so a reader of the text sees ok. Remaining fix as n10 says: refuse an unknown --flag with exit 2 and a usage line, before any package scan.")
