inl feature_parity_table () = Task ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", "Feature-by-backend parity table in tests/matrix.psd1 + a compiler warning when a feature is used on a backend whose cell says no + rule: a feature landing on one backend files <FEATURE>-PARITY-<BACKEND> items in the same change", Story, P1, D4, 15u32, Planned, "BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY", "team:compiler,compiler,parity,backend-balance,standards", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_feature_parity_table () = Planning ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_feature_parity_table_1 () = Note ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:49Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x filed from kit-session Explore subagent aaf2a6f472dc70094 (11-02, read-only; report relayed by kit to main). Parent per the report: extend, don't fork the plan.")
inl note_of_feature_parity_table_2 () = Note ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:54Z", "compiler", "11-02 06:55 compiler: GROOM. DESIGN CONSTRAINT: the compiler cannot read tests/matrix.psd1 at compile time (test data, not shipped). So the source of truth for the warning is a typed table IN the compiler: one record per backend with a feature set (union of a Feature case type: Export, LinkedUnits, PrimToString, Bigint, Float32, ...). The warning fires in the backend dispatch, where the backend is known and the op is seen. matrix.psd1 then gets a generated or checked view, not a second hand-kept list (one record per fact). A test asserts every Feature with a `no` cell has a `Known` matrix entry and every `yes` cell has a passing sample. Starting rows from what exists: Export is yes on F#/Rust/Gleam/TS and no on Zig and the rest (verified 11-02 by grep of TyOp(Export)); PrimToString is yes on 12 matrix lists after pack15d. The process rule (feature on one backend files <FEATURE>-PARITY-<BACKEND> items in the same change) belongs in the standards doc next to the regression-sample rule.")
inl note_of_feature_parity_table_3 () = Note ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-05T09:59Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:0x compiler: FIRST DATA for the in-compiler table: a census of Op x backend from the live core (pack44 source), computed rather than hand-kept. Method: 140 Op cases (spiral_compiler.fs:1724-1917); an op counts as handled by a backend when its name appears as a match arm ('| Op' / '| Op.Op') inside that backend's codegen section (codegenFsharp ... CodegenPython, 19 backends). 97 ops never reach codegen (compile-time peval ops: HashSet*/HashMap*, type-level ...). 43 reach codegen; 19 of them on all 19 backends. Gaps (columns F R Pa Z Le B G Lu Wa Wg Ca K Sw Q E TS C Cp Py): ToPythonRecord/ToPythonNamedTuple 1 (Python only, by design); Assign 4 yy.....y........y..; MonotonicDelayMs 6 .yy............yyyy; ArrayIndexSet 11 yy....yyyy.yy...yyy; UnionTag 12 yyyyy.yyy......yyyy; Printf 13 yyyy..yyy..yy..yyyy; StaticStringConcat 14 yyyyyyyyy..yy..yy.y; PrimToString 14 yyyyyyyyy..yy..yy.y; Sqrt 14 yyyyyyyyy....y.yyyy; StringSlice 14 yyyyy.yyy..yy..yyyy; StdoutFlush 15 .yyyy...yyyyyyyyyyy; StringIndex 15 yyyyyyyyy..yy..yyyy; ArrayIndex 15 yyyyy.yyyy.yy..yyyy; Log 15 yyyyyyyy...yyy.yyyy; Cos/Sin/Exp/Pow/Tanh 16 yyyyyyyyy..yyy.yyyy; TypeToVar 17 yyyy..yyyyyyyyyyyyy; BoolOr/BoolAnd 18 yy.yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy; NanIs 18 yyyyyyyyyy.yyyyyyyy. CAVEATS: a pattern census. (a) A backend that maps an op through a generic table, not a '| Op' arm, shows a false gap; Pascal BoolAnd/BoolOr are likely such cases, so each '.' needs a probe before it becomes a 'no' cell. (b) Wgsl/Calyx/OpenQasm/Ebpf are deliberately narrow backends, so their gaps are mostly by design and become Known rows. NEXT: turn this into the typed Feature x Backend record in the compiler (the 11-02 design: one record per backend, Feature union), with each 'no' cell carrying a matrix Known entry, and a test that every 'yes' cell has a passing sample.")
inl note_of_feature_parity_table_4 () = Note ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", 4u32, "2026-11-05T10:00Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:0x compiler: CORRECTED CENSUS (supersedes the note above). The first pass required the op right after '|' and missed grouped patterns like Pascal's '| (BoolAnd | BitwiseAnd), _'. With '[|(]\\s*Op', 47 ops reach codegen and 21 are on all 19 backends (BoolAnd/BoolOr/ArrayIndexSet etc. move to yes). Remaining gaps (F R Pa Z Le B G Lu Wa Wg Ca K Sw Q E TS C Cp Py): PragmaUnrollPush/Pop 1 (Cpp only); ToPythonRecord/ToPythonNamedTuple 1 (Python only); Export 5 yy.y..y........y... (F#, Rust, Zig, Gleam, TS: the linked-unit backends); Assign 6 yyyy...y........y..; MonotonicDelayMs 6 .yy............yyyy; UnionTag 12 yyyyy.yyy......yyyy; PrimToString / StaticStringConcat 14 yyyyyyyyy..yy..yy.y; StdoutFlush 15 .yyyy...yyyyyyyyyyy; Printf / StringIndex / StringSlice 15 yyyyyyyyy..yy..yyyy; Sqrt/Pow/Tanh/Log/Exp/Sin/Cos 16 yyyyyyyyy..yyy.yyyy; ArrayIndex / ArrayIndexSet 16 yyyyyyyyyy.yy..yyyy; TypeToVar 17 yyyy..yyyyyyyyyyyyy; Global 18 yyyyy.yyyyyyyyyyyyy; NanIs 18 yyyyyyyyyy.yyyyyyyy. Most remaining '.' sit on the narrow backends (Wgsl, Calyx, OpenQasm, Ebpf), which become Known rows by design. Each '.' on a general backend still needs a probe before it becomes a 'no' cell.")
inl note_of_feature_parity_table_5 () = Note ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", 5u32, "2026-11-05T10:41Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:4x compiler: FIRST GAP PROBED, Assign (!!!!Assign(target, value), a mutable dyn local): ':= ~x = 1i32; !!!!Assign(x, 41i32); x + 1' compiled with installed pack44. OK: Rust, C (exit 0; C was a FALSE gap in the census: its handler sits outside the section bounds I used, so the pattern census undercounts C). REAL gaps, explicit errors: Python ('Assign with 2 args not supported'), Kotlin ('doesn't support the operation Assign yet'), Swift (same), Wasm ('not supported in the Wasm backend'), Cpp ('Assign with 2 args not supported'). By design: Gleam (immutable locals), so a 'no' cell with a Known row. Lesson for the table builder: a census row is a hypothesis, and the compile probe is the evidence; each general-backend '.' gets one 20-line probe like this before it becomes a cell. Filed ASSIGN-PARITY for the 5 real gaps.")
inl note_of_feature_parity_table_6 () = Note ("FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE", 6u32, "2026-11-05T10:42Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:5x compiler: second probe, UnionTag: real gaps on Bend, Kotlin, Swift (explicit 'doesn't support the operation UnionTag yet'); Wasm, Gleam, Lean compile, as the census said. Filed UNIONTAG-PARITY.")
