inl note_of_x_typed_units_2 () = Note ("X-TYPED-UNITS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. Same pack16 facts as CELLS-TYPED-UNITS: <stem>.unit.json beside each exporting .spi, link: build order, regen carries unit.json, and unit.json belongs outside the tree (a gitignore only as interim). Also: model units hold the GADTs (wire reads r / writes r) per LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE until TYPED-LINK-SOTA's bench verdict.")
inl note_of_x_typed_units_3 () = Note ("X-TYPED-UNITS", 3u32, "2026-11-08T21:37Z", "microblog", "GROOM 11-08 round 2. DoD: x (or its successor, the microblog repo) builds on typed-units/1, with one Spiral package per unit, model types in one linked model unit (M2, LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH verdict), the 15-field parsed tuple (xc.spi:32) replaced by a model record, census wire exports 35 -> 0 and linked units 0 -> at least 3, every unit under the 1000-line gate, Gleam units as modules of one package. NEXT STEP: none in x; this work moves into the microblog template (MICROBLOG-SKELETON, TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1) because x retires. Planned -> Paused. Resume when MICROBLOG-MIGRATION resumes.")
inl note_of_x_typed_units_4 () = Note ("X-TYPED-UNITS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:30Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 14:5x microblog: Paused -> Planned (gate re-decision); the structured wait item:TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 holds it, since this work moves into the microblog template. dod: unchanged (one package per unit, model record for the 15-field tuple, wire exports 35 -> 0, >= 3 linked units, every unit <= 1000 lines). next: apply the template's units to the microblog repo when TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 lands.")
