inl note_of_org_versioning_1 () = Note ("ORG-VERSIONING", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:50Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x from the kit-session Explore report aaf2a6f472dc70094 (section 6, with sources: Zed DeltaDB, Anthropic Scion write-up, NEAR upgrade docs). Scion/DeltaDB are version-control systems, not numbering schemes. USER DECISION: adopt per-project semver + org template edition? Rec: yes; calendar versioning fits fixed-schedule products, not us.")
inl note_of_org_versioning_2 () = Note ("ORG-VERSIONING", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Adopt per-project semver plus one org-wide integer template edition. RULE (written before acting): Default is to adopt, per main's recommendation in n1. Calendar versioning fits fixed-schedule products, not this org. It is reversible because nothing is tagged yet: write the scheme as a typed module (version = nominal {major; minor; patch}; edition = union of integer editions) and per-lane <REPO>-1-0-DOD items. Creating and pushing tags stays a later UserBoundary, part of the user's push. BACKUP/UNDO: Docs and items only, unstaged; no tags are created OWNER: main. NEXT: Write the typed version/edition module and file the per-lane 1.0 DoD items. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_org_versioning_3 () = Note ("ORG-VERSIONING", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:59Z", "main", "main 11-02 ADOPTED on the backlog (was a draft). RULE (fixed before looking, per the user via fiscal 11-02: \"those things can be decided autonomously\"; technical calls are ours, decided by a pre-stated rule with rule and outcome recorded). Rule: a backlog convention that is reversible and touches no public artifact is ours to adopt; anything that PUBLISHES (pushing tags, a release, a crates.io name) stays the user's go. Outcome: per-project semver with <REPO>-1-0-DOD items (5 lanes already drafted theirs) and one org template edition integer are the working convention. No tag is pushed until the user says so.")
inl note_of_org_versioning_4 () = Note ("ORG-VERSIONING", 4u32, "2026-11-07T22:16Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: per-project semver tags at 1.0 when the <REPO>-1-0-DOD holds (typed units, gates green, CI green), plus one org-wide integer template edition recorded in i574n.github; the first project (html) tagged.")
inl note_of_org_versioning_5 () = Note ("ORG-VERSIONING", 5u32, "2026-11-09T04:41Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 00:4x Its dep TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 is Done (11-08 23:3x), so this is unblocked. TEMPLATE EDITION RECORDED (unstaged; DoD part 2): the org-wide template edition is 1, named typed-units/1, declared once in i574n.github at examples/typed-units/Cargo.toml as [workspace.metadata.spiral] template = typed-units/1 (the reference); html, the first adopter, carries the same line in its root Cargo.toml. Cargo ignores workspace.metadata; cargo metadata parses both. Later adopters (microblog SKELETON, fiscal/tibia/x) add the same line; a future typed-units/2 bumps the integer. DoD parts 1/3 (tag html 1.0): PUBLISHING = the user's go per the 11-02 rule, and an HTML-1-0-DOD must hold first. Existing 1.0 DoDs: SPIRAL-COMPILER 30, TIBIA 20, X-DUMPS/X/FISCAL/REGEX 0; none for html, so I filed HTML-1-0-DOD from tonight's facts. Progress 0 -> 40.")
inl note_of_org_versioning_6 () = Note ("ORG-VERSIONING", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:08Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:2x per-project DoD status: HTML-1-0-DOD 80 Blocked (shim proof green; waits on the user's release-job OK + spiral push, then the user's tag); REGEX-1-0-DOD 0 -> 10 with a 5-line checklist and a keep-or-cut question to compiler on BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT + SOTA (proposal: 1.0 = correct + typed + certified, the SOTA product = 2.0). The other lanes' DoDs (SPIRAL-COMPILER 30, TIBIA 20, X-DUMPS/X/FISCAL 0) are theirs.")
