inl note_of_zig_parallel_units_battle_test_1 () = Note ("ZIG-PARALLEL-UNITS-BATTLE-TEST", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:02Z", "kit", "Filed by kit 11-02 07:1x from the S0 study subagent's execution packet (aaf2a6f472dc70094; the user resumed it and asked that everything go to execution). USER asked for this explicitly. Corpus: kit's agile_todo_model/paths/scan/merge slice (already measured under Step A, KIT-TYPED-CRATES n10-n12) or a mega sample split into units. Measure: wall time at 1 vs N workers, generated lines per unit, cold build and warm rebuild after a one-unit change, on Zig, Rust and Gleam. Runs on the node or europa (one job at a time there), never the box. DoD: the scored table in this item; each regression filed as its own item.")
inl note_of_zig_parallel_units_battle_test_2 () = Note ("ZIG-PARALLEL-UNITS-BATTLE-TEST", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:08Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:20 compiler: GROOM. Blocked by LINKED-UNITS-ZIG (including its step 0: Zig has no Export arm today). The build order comes from the unit graph (program 2's <stem>.unit.json links field): a topological level runs in parallel, and build.zig modules are generated from the same graph. Measure 1 vs N workers over one corpus, with the same corpus as Rust crates (cargo -j) and Gleam modules, with an A/A arm in the same job (wall time and peak RSS per arm). Run on the node, never the box. Corpus candidate: the linked_unit_union sample family scaled to ~20 units, plus kit's agile_todo trio once it moves to link:.")
