inl note_of_spiral_compiler_1_0_dod_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-COMPILER-1-0-DOD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:08Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:20 compiler: DRAFT (ORG-VERSIONING is a proposal waiting on the user; nothing here is adopted). What stands between the Spiral compiler and 1.0: (1) linked units complete: COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS second cut + EXTERN-CALLS (Step B), IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE, LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX, LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE; Rust and Gleam as unit backends, Zig after LINKED-UNITS-ZIG. (2) spiral.toml is the only manifest the compiler reads (SPIPROJ-RETIRE host part: the 5 package.spiproj-only readers in tmp/compiler/host/Program.fs). (3) FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE in place, with the compiler warning live and every no-cell carrying a matrix Known entry. (4) CI green on the backends the table marks yes (matrix single-flight -Suite all -Native), with no new Known rows. (5) typed-units/1 applies to the Spiral code this lane owns (samples and lib packages it touches), not to the F# core; the 1000-generated-lines gate is measured on samples. (6) A tagged release built by install-pack from a named program stack. Not 1.0 blockers: self-hosting, GADT phantom-index erasure, hopacsota.")
inl note_of_spiral_compiler_1_0_dod_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-COMPILER-1-0-DOD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:03Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Adopt ORG-VERSIONING, the proposal this 1.0 DoD draft depends on? RULE (written before acting): Default: adopt ORG-VERSIONING provisionally as the working scheme (semver, 1.0 = the drafted DoD). The DRAFT DoD becomes the lane's working checklist. This is reversible because it only shapes backlog text and gates. The tag in step (6) remains a user git action. BACKUP/UNDO: Keep the DRAFT text as a note before rewording. Revert = re-tag the item draft (kit state-backups hold the prior agile.spi). OWNER: compiler. NEXT: Drop the draft tag, keep the 6 criteria, and link each to its item so 'agile next --team compiler' hands them out. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_spiral_compiler_1_0_dod_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-COMPILER-1-0-DOD", 3u32, "2026-11-05T09:56Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:0x compiler: applied x's 11-02 ByDefault decision NEXT (draft text kept above as the backup): draft tag and 'DRAFT:' dropped; the 6 criteria stay; open ones linked as deps so agile next hands them out. STATUS per criterion today: (1) linked units complete: DONE, all items closed: COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS, COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS (step B), IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE, LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX, LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE, LINKED-UNITS-ZIG; Rust, Gleam and Zig are unit backends (tonight: pack41 Gleam prelude types, pack42 Rust field visibility). (2) spiral.toml the only manifest the compiler reads: OPEN -> dep SPIPROJ-RETIRE (Planned 0%). (3) feature parity table + compiler warning: OPEN -> dep FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE (Planned 0%). (4) CI green on the table's backends with no new Known rows: no own item; it is read from the CI run after the user's push, so it stays a criterion checked at release time. (5) typed-units/1 on the lane's Spiral code: no item exists under that name; it is checked per sample and package at review. (6) a tagged release built by install-pack from a named program stack: dep SPIRAL-CI-COMPILER-BINARIES (Planned) plus ORG-VERSIONING; the tag itself stays the user's git action. Packs today run as named program stacks (pack38-pack44 each = a listed kitdo set), so the 'named program stack' half already holds.")
inl x_dumps_1_0_dod () = Task ("X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD", "X-DUMPS 1.0 definition of done (DRAFT, waits on ORG-VERSIONING adoption): xarchive on typed-units/1 as 5 units (xarchive_model, xarchive_boundary, xarchive_harvest, xarchive_history, xarchive bin) with every gate green; all harvested accounts at archive+X+context completion with lost/tombstone accounting; a cache-only rerun reproduces byte-identical outputs; europa pods rendered by kit k3s render from xarchive.k3s.spi; a backup restore proven on a scratch box; repo home + git decided by the user; tagged 1.0", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "ORG-VERSIONING,TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1,X-DUMPS,X-DUMPS-SPIRAL-REWRITE", "team:org,management,release", "current", "current")
