inl note_of_x_dumps_1_0_dod_1 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:08Z", "x-dumps", "Drafted for the main groom round 11-02 (ORG-VERSIONING asks each lane for <REPO>-1-0-DOD). Planned only; not started until the user adopts ORG-VERSIONING. Units: model = records/kinds/identity types; boundary = HTTP+sha256 cache+rate/backoff+fs (fetch.rs and all file IO); feature harvest = cdx/snaps/live/context/media + parse; feature history = identity/timeline/merge/summary/md+html render (timeline.rs is the 1000-line risk; split render if it crosses); bin = run orchestration (lanes, finisher) + CLI.")
inl note_of_x_dumps_1_0_dod_2 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T22:28Z", "x-dumps", "Backup RESTORE PROVEN 11-02 (DoD criterion met). Restored the live 6 GB backup (x-20261102T171138Z.tar.zst) to a scratch dir via cygwin `zstd -dc | tar -x` (cmd pipe, binary-safe): 16 files out, all 4 people/ summaries intact and readable (@juhondacivic 1450651554340642818, @fc1943s 1637273636049498112, @stewshka 1819115209170276352, @fc1943s+@i574n 72784485). So the 6-hourly backups are genuinely restorable, not just zstd-valid. Extract took ~16 min because people/ sits late in tar order so tar reads the full 6 GB; a full DR restore is similar. Trap: `bash -lc` on a fresh cygwin triggers skeleton-profile setup and swallowed the script - use a cmd pipe (zstd.exe -dc | Windows tar -xf -), not cygwin bash login. Exit 1 was cosmetic (geygey summary.md not in the backup yet - account unfinished).")
inl note_of_x_dumps_1_0_dod_3 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD", 3u32, "2026-11-02T22:32Z", "x-dumps", "Byte-identical cache-rerun PROVEN 11-02 (DoD criterion met). Re-ran juhondacivic merge from the live cache into a scratch root /tmp/repro on europa and sha256-compared the people output against live: timeline.ndjson AND summary.md both BYTE-IDENTICAL (3df37fae...). So the pipeline is deterministic - a cache-only rerun reproduces the same bytes. Two of the DoD criteria now proven: backup-restore (note 2) + byte-identical repro (this). Remaining DoD: the 5-unit typed-units/1 port (gated on TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 + downloads finishing), kit k3s render of the manifests, repo home + git (user), tag 1.0.")
inl note_of_x_dumps_1_0_dod_4 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD", 4u32, "2026-11-06T11:53Z", "x-dumps", "1.0 readiness map 11-06 (which DoD criteria today's work moved): (1) typed-units/1 5-unit restructure + gates green = PENDING (waits ORG-VERSIONING). (2) all accounts at archive+X+context completion with lost/tombstone accounting = ADVANCING: enrichment re-harvest (running on europa) refreshes live+context with likes/replies/entities/lang/author/dims; completeness settled (3 reachable 100% ref-complete, 121 suspended confirmed gone, 4981 unrecoverable accounted). (3) cache-only byte-identical rerun = PROVEN 11-02. (4) europa pods rendered by kit k3s from xarchive.k3s.spi = PENDING (infra). (5) backup restore proven on scratch box = PARTIAL (archives integrity-verified restorable; explicit scratch-box restore still to prove). (6) repo home + git decided by user = PENDING USER. (7) tag 1.0 = PENDING. Net: 1 proven, 1 advancing, rest gated on user/org/infra. Not x-dumps-authorable now; stays Planned 0% behind ORG-VERSIONING.")
inl note_of_x_dumps_1_0_dod_5 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD", 5u32, "2026-11-07T15:57Z", "x-dumps", "next: adopt ORG-VERSIONING, then define the xarchive 1.0 acceptance test on typed-unified output (one gate per stage).")
