inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:11Z", "tibia", "DRAFT (ORG-VERSIONING is a proposal awaiting the user). What stands between tibia and 1.0, from the tree 11-02:\n(a) typed-units/1 split, none done: model = src rules (geometry..policy, views, quantity); feature = sim (search, network, hunting_pack, combat) + results/ (+ rows/); boundary = apps/host + offscreen + canary (all hand host code outside arena: 62 of 231 $' lines); bin = suite + predict. apps/arena (114+55 $' lines in client/hooks) stays whole-program: the arena sandbox bans require (TIBIA-MAP-TYPED-UNITS after v1). apps/map gets the template layout.\n(b) SPIPROJ-RETIRE: 9 package.spiproj (src, results, 7 apps) beside spiral.toml; readers scripts/predict.ps1:21-22 (patches it), live/paths.ps1:14 (hashes .spiproj), README.md:25-26. Waits on the compiler host reader.\n(c) gates unmeasured: 1000 generated lines/unit, union-to-code at a boundary (purpose_code instances live in model, labels via case_labels reflection), concrete export signatures, typefeatureset score.\n(d) CI green: red on 1f40e7d; fixes (offscreen, arena_rows, secondary_hits, publish.ps1) node-green, waiting on the user's commit.\n(e) open lanes feeding 1.0: MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV 55%, TIBIA-RUN-METRICS 75%, LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS 75%.\n(f) tag.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:04Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Adopt ORG-VERSIONING, the proposal this tibia 1.0 DoD draft depends on? RULE (written before acting): Default: adopt ORG-VERSIONING provisionally, so the draft becomes tibia's working 1.0 checklist. It is reversible (backlog text only), and the tag (f) stays a user git action. Item (d), the user's commit of the CI fixes, is already met: tibia is in sync at 89ce0d4 (2026-11-02 06:13) with only README.md modified. BACKUP/UNDO: Keep the DRAFT note as is; kit state-backups hold the prior agile.spi; revert = re-tag draft. OWNER: tibia. NEXT: Mark (d) as committed, check tibia CI on 89ce0d4, and drop the draft tag. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 3u32, "2026-11-03T10:32Z", "tibia", "11-03 06:3x tibia, CHECKLIST STATE (n1 items, from the tree and today's runs). (a) typed-units/1 split: not started; unchanged. (b) SPIPROJ-RETIRE: unchanged; tibia's own readers already accept spiral.toml (predict.ps1 Set-Manifests, LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION n7). (c) gates: typefeatureset moved tonight (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n16-n17: every found-flag record in the arena is an option, offscreen flags and competitor's targeting/mover are unions); the scoreboard rerun is still owed. (d) CI green: NOT met today: tibia's gh-pages Windows job went red at 07:42 (bfd1641c) on spiral/scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1's LunarG 'latest' Vulkan zip 404; main fixed it in spiral (ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT n1), green after the user pushes spiral; no tibia change needed. (e) feeding lanes: MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV 95% (last step = one live block; blocked 11-03 by box memory: kit needs 4 GB free for live-gui, 2.4 GB free with 8 lanes open), TIBIA-RUN-METRICS 85% (c and rust series live; quiet C/Rust = 2.65x), LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS 75% unchanged. (f) tag: user git action. Full-suite regression in flight on the node (memo-off, all 60+ files); its red rows so far are infrastructure (spiral lua host 0xC0000005 crashes, a compiler-port lock timeout, map under contention), with solo reruns queued before any verdict.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 4u32, "2026-11-03T13:42Z", "tibia", "11-03 09:2x tibia, (d) CI GREEN: TWO separate reds, not one. Windows (bfd1641c): spiral init-wgsl-run.ps1 LunarG 1.4.363.1 zip 404, fixed in spiral by main, waits on the spiral push. UBUNTU: red since d4ad52ad (11-02 21:59); last green c97cc9e6 (11-02 14:38); no failed tests, but build.ps1 counts unsupported as not green: combat_text 5/5 unsupported, game_calls 3/3, samples 1, ground_trace 1 (its notebook main defaults to Zig and the generated main.zig fails: main.zig:160:25 expected semicolon), plus competitor 1 in bfd1641c. These are Lua-only files (combat_text 5x lua, game_calls 3x lua) that did NOT change between the green and red commits; Zig is 0.17.0 via setup-zig in both runs. What changed in d4ad52ad: scripts/init.ps1 stopped cloning polyglot and running polyglot's init.ps1 and now runs spiral's scripts/init-app-build.ps1 (scripts/build.ps1 and workflow.ps1 switched core.ps1 to spiral too). So the polyglot-to-spiral bootstrap switch changed what the CI environment provides (most likely the spiral CLI build and its Lua host, by analogy with the node runner incident today). NEXT: read one unsupported reason from the CI cells output (download the ci-metrics artifact or rerun one file with verbose) and compare init-app-build's spiral CLI build with polyglot's.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 5u32, "2026-11-03T13:57Z", "tibia", "11-03 09:5x tibia, UBUNTU RED ROOT CAUSE FOUND (supersedes the guess in n4): the CI notebooks artifact of run 41598147028 says, for every unsupported test, unsupported on this machine: spiral lua --lua-path /tmp/spiral_cells/.../main.lua was not found. Cells runs every lua target through the Spiral CLI (builders.ex dispatch -> spiral lua), resolved at deps/spiral/workspace/target/release/spiral, and nothing builds it since d4ad52ad: polyglot init.ps1 line 151 ran deps/spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1, spiral init-app-build.ps1 does not. ALL lua targets are unavailable on CI (arena_host etc. still pass via their other target and log lua unavailable); files whose only target is lua (combat_text 5, game_calls 3, samples 1, ground_trace 1, competitor 1) turn unsupported, so the gate is red. FIX (unstaged, tibia scripts/init.ps1 +4): after the lua5.1 block, build the CLI with deps/spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1 when neither spiral nor spiral.exe exists in deps/spiral/workspace/target/release (guard keeps local inits from rebuilding a runner other lanes use). Parse-checked; guard tested present/missing. Proof = the next CI run after the user push: 0 unsupported and no lua unavailable lines. The ground_trace Zig main error is non-gating (executed 1 passed 1) and separate.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 6u32, "2026-11-03T14:06Z", "tibia", "11-03 10:0x tibia, n5 fix MOVED: main fixed it in one place, spiral scripts/init-app-build.ps1 (unstaged) builds the CLI via apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1 when workspace/target/release/spiral[.exe] is missing. Tibia init.ps1 runs init-app-build first, so the tibia copy was dead and is removed (tibia init.ps1 back to HEAD). Goes live with the user spiral push; proof = the next tibia Ubuntu CI run shows 0 unsupported and no lua unavailable lines.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 7u32, "2026-11-05T05:26Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:26 tibia, CHECKLIST UPDATE. (d) CI GREEN: MET. tibia 'tests' run 41960766319 on 3d8e815 (11-05 03:18Z) passed on windows-2025 and ubuntu-24.04, and the pages deploy followed. (b) SPIPROJ-RETIRE, tibia's share, now probing. Every tibia toml/spiproj pair is equal (normalized edition, packageDir, packages and module tree) except apps/predict, where gpu_plan (registered 11-04) is only in the toml and still compiles inside the package, so the toml is what gets read and the spiproj is already stale. Cells' manifest.ex tries spiral.toml first. The compiler host still names spiproj directly in relatedClosure (diagnostic scoping) and applyPackageDefaults (edition/default-int), so the proof is empirical, not a code read: europa probe sr1 runs --check on the last module of all 9 packages with both manifests, then toml-only, then a toml-only negative (src minus geometry, arena minus client) that must fail. Running.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 8u32, "2026-11-05T05:28Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:28 tibia, (c) GATES, SOURCE-SIDE BASELINE (installed kit standards --census src apps results, 2 s): src 8657 lines, gadt-case 27, existential 4, forall 46, 0 host-macro, 0 rust-global, 0 bang-export, 0 string-concat; arena 3141 lines, host-macro 21, top-level-macro 148 (the Lua sandbox host, whole-program by design); canary 411 (host-macro 1, top-level-macro 30); host 1050 (clean); map 914 (clean); offscreen 450 (host-macro 12, rust-global 18, top-level-macro 19: the FFI boundary); predict 213 (host-macro 1, encoded-row 4); suite 304 (clean); results 911 (gadt-case 3, encoded-row 2). CAVEAT: prototype reads 0 everywhere although src has 2 ':?' prototypes (network judge, typed_network width) and tibia has 7 ':+' instances. That is the known census probe gap (EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET n45-46, kit), so the typefeatureset score for prototypes must be counted by grep until it lands. Still unmeasured: the 1000 generated lines/unit gate (needs a compile per unit, a node job).")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 9u32, "2026-11-05T05:33Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:33 tibia, (b) SPIPROJ-RETIRE, COMPILER HALF PROVEN on europa (sr1; full tibia src/results/apps tree from the live box, current lib, europa compiler; --check type-checks every top-level def): A, both manifests: the last module of all 9 packages (src/hunting_pack, results/map_grids, arena/steps, canary/lead_trace, host/world_executor, map/map, offscreen/offscreen, predict/gpu_plan, suite/suite) exit 0 with 0 diagnostics. B, toml-only (all 9 package.spiproj deleted, 0 left): the same 9, exit 0 with 0 diagnostics. C, negative, toml-only minus one module: src without geometry exits 5 with 2277 diagnostics (terrain.spi:5 Unbound geometry); arena without client exits 5 with 3113 (probe.spi:6 Unbound client). So the host's relatedClosure does not hide diagnostics in toml-only packages, and edition 3 resolves without the spiproj. CELLS HALF queued: node job tibia-sr2-toml-cells moves the 9 spiproj files out of mirror tibia-np1 (per-file backup and hash), runs build.ps1 -Files coins,cooldowns and predict -Module gpu_plan, then restores each file. After it is green, the live deletion follows (unstaged), with README lines 25-26/243 updated. (c) NOTE: kit crate gate C:\\home\\git\\tibia --limit 1000 reads crates=0 (tibia has no committed generated crates), so it is vacuous here, not a pass; the per-unit generated-lines measure needs compiles.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 10u32, "2026-11-05T06:01Z", "tibia", "11-05 02:01 tibia, (c) generated-lines probe gl1: VOID, and it overloaded europa. Design faults: it compiled every module with a main to both C and Rust. src and results have no main entries (skipped silently), and the arena probes are Lua-targeted, so their C COMPILE-FAILED rows (parity, bot_prelude, bot_dofile, bot_env, scan) and bot_env's Rust failure say nothing about the code; the few Rust line counts (parity 389, scan 408, bot_dofile 68, bot_prelude 53) are not the backend arena ships. Worse, the back-to-back compiles ran under a 2300M scope when only about 2.2 GB was free. Together with the other lanes' load, europa thrashed (load 47, sshd banner timeouts for every lane, k3s pods restarting) until kit flagged it and I stopped the loop at 05:59Z (load 47 -> 13 within a minute). REDO on the node: compile each package's entries for its OWN backend (arena -> Lua, map -> Rust, host and offscreen per their ///> targets, the src/results test blocks through the notebooks), one compile at a time.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 11u32, "2026-11-05T07:19Z", "tibia", "11-05 03:19 tibia, (b) SPIPROJ-RETIRE FOR TIBIA: DONE (unstaged). CELLS HALF PROVEN on the node (job tibia-sr2-toml-cells-2: 9 package.spiproj moved out of mirror tibia-np1 with per-file hash-checked backups, 0 left): build.ps1 -Files coins,cooldowns ran layout clean and budget clean; coins 5/5; cooldowns 8/9, where the one red is spiral-wgsl exit 0xC0000005, the node WGSL runner crash also seen WITH the spiproj present (gate tibia-np2-gate-2 draft arm, green in its next arm), so an environment fault, not a manifest one. predict.ps1 -Module gpu_plan compiled and ran toml-only. All 9 restored with matching hashes. With sr1's compiler proof (9/9 --check toml-only, negative control bites), tibia drops the 9 files: git ls-files plus git diff HEAD confirmed each tracked and unmodified first, so HEAD restores them. Also: README manifest lines (25-26, 243) now name spiral.toml only; scripts/predict.ps1 Set-Manifests is toml-only (the spiproj branch is gone); live/paths.ps1 no longer hashes .spiproj. Both scripts parse 0.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 12u32, "2026-11-05T07:38Z", "tibia", "11-05 03:38 tibia, (c) 1000-GENERATED-LINES GATE, MEASURED (node job tibia-gl2-gen-lines-2; mirror tibia-np1 = live tree; the mirror's own compiler; every entry with a main, each compiled for the backend it ships on, one at a time). OVER 1000: apps/arena (Lua) competitor 4362, measure 1611, random 1474, steps 1373, nexbot 1219; apps/predict (C) predict 82,505 and lanes 60,510, lanes_gpu (WGSL) 60,043; apps/map (Rust) 2383. WITHIN: arena bot_dofile 69, bot_env 8, bot_prelude 48, parity 431, path 635, scan 442, summon 551, vbot 868; predict gpu_plan 382; offscreen (Rust) 694; canary lead_trace 724 Lua / 770 Rust, ground_trace 548 / 606. (sweep: not registered in apps/predict's toml, which predict.ps1 adds on the fly, so it is a probe artifact, not a failure.) READING: the sim entries (predict, lanes, lanes_gpu) are whole-program single files 60-80x over; meeting the gate there IS (a), the typed-units split into packages with exports (hand-modeled units), not a splitter. The arena probes are 1.2-4.4x over and run in the OTClient sandbox, which bans require, so they stay whole-program by design (n1: TIBIA-MAP-TYPED-UNITS after v1); they need a documented exemption or a sandbox-compatible split. map is 2.4x over (Rust can take units). So (c) is measured: 9 of 23 entries over.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 13u32, "2026-11-05T07:40Z", "tibia", "11-05 03:40 tibia, (a)/(c) PLAN FOR apps/map (2383 generated Rust lines, the cheapest OVER entry: Rust takes linked units, no sandbox). Seams in map.spi (914 source lines): (1) a protobuf-style field reader (varint_from, varint, field_at, fold_fields with a visitors record), (2) the appearances parser on top of it (flag_seen, bank_seen, appearance -> item_kinds), (3) the items.xml scanner (item_tags, id_names, matches_from, find_from, digits_from), (4) the OTBM tree reader, (5) the region and walkability writers plus the generated terrain definitions. Units by the link-boundary rules (memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes): a map_model unit owning the shared records (item_kinds as arrays of primitives), with anchor exports for every type that crosses; proto and xml as leaf units exporting primitive or array-shaped functions (closures can't cross, so fold_fields' visitors stay inside the proto unit and the appearances parse moves in with it). COST BEFORE STARTING: map builds as ONE rustc file (apps/map/run.ps1), so units need a Cargo workspace in tibia (Cargo.toml per unit with [package.metadata.spiral], path deps, a lockfile), and the proof (run.ps1 with its terrain/region parity) needs the live Canary data under TibiaWorld, which only the box has. Not started tonight; it needs a box window and is a planned slice, not wait-filler.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 14u32, "2026-11-06T08:20Z", "tibia", "11-06 04:19 tibia (groom): SPIPROJ-RETIRE is done on tibia's side. All 9 package.spiproj files are deleted (unstaged), proven on the compiler and Cells, with README and live/paths.ps1 updated; the item still waits on main's repo-wide close. Generated lines: 9 of 23 entries are still over 1000, and apps/map (2383 Rust lines) is the cheapest. NEXT: split map.spi's field reader per the 11-05 03:40 plan.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 15u32, "2026-11-07T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (lint markers). DoD: tibia 1.0 is tagged when CI is green on both OSes with the pushed spiral, SPIPROJ-RETIRE is closed, the typed-units split (TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1) is in, and apps/map is under the 1000-generated-line gate; proof is the green CI run and the tag.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 16u32, "2026-11-10T07:33Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:3x tibia: (a) apps/map under the 1000-generated-line gate is MET ON THE NODE via TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER's three linked units (map.rs 975, map_walk 659, map_items 354, map_kinds 349; cargo green; tests green). Remaining for that DoD row: the box parity run (live Canary data), then applying the draft. Next step: after the box window opens, run the parity run for TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER and apply the draft.")
inl note_of_tibia_1_0_dod_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-1-0-DOD", 17u32, "2026-11-10T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-10 10:5x tibia: the apps/map row is MET and APPLIED (unstaged): four linked units, every generated file under 1000 lines (map.rs 975), with byte-identical output to the original on the real Canary map (see TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER, now Done). Remaining 1.0 rows per note 15: CI green on both OSes with the pushed spiral, SPIPROJ-RETIRE closed, the typed-units split in.")
inl fiscal_1_0_dod () = Task ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", "DRAFT (ORG-VERSIONING is a proposal, not adopted): what stands between fiscal and 1.0 = typed-units/1 layout + all its gates green + CI green on its backends + tagged", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1,ORG-VERSIONING", "team:fiscal,fiscal,release,standards,draft", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_1_0_dod () = Planning ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_fiscal_1_0_dod_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:12Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 07:12 DRAFT DOD (main groom round 11-02, point 3), measured on the tree today.\nUNITS (typed-units/1): fiscal_model (model: canon + lifecycle types and pure fns); fiscal_host (boundary: fiscal_paths + every file_system read/write); fiscal_corpus (feature: corpus + corpus_checks); fiscal_generator (feature: generator over lib xsd_*); fiscal_regen (bin: writes generated/, samples/, canon/en16931-terms.json). The 81 generated/<family> units stay one generated model package each, joined by link: (FISCAL-TYPED-UNITS, filed when TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 v1 is green).\nBLOCKERS: (1) 1000-line gate: 68 of 81 generated units are over 1000 lines (UBL Invoice 57,667); needs per-closure split + shared runtime: XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS, FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB, FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES. (2) boundary: 67 file_system calls outside a boundary (corpus_checks 37, generator 25, canon 4, corpus 1) move into fiscal_host; canon's JSON write moves to the bin. (3) no union-to-code mapping at the boundary: canon ubl_document_name/term_id_text stay model show_ fns, the host only writes text. (4) concrete export signatures + parity clean: checked once the template gates exist. (5) typefeatureset never down: baseline from FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS before the split. (6) SPIPROJ-RETIRE: generator.spi:6 module_package + :37 writes 81 package.spiproj, :998 test reads one, README.md:142, src/package.spiproj duplicates src/spiral.toml; the generator writes spiral.toml with link: instead. (7) CI green on its backends: ubuntu-24.04 + windows-2025 green today on the Rust path (c8830d7, run 41366612730); Delphi blocked on DELPHI-CASE-INSENSITIVE-NAMES; USER/MAIN DECISION which backends fiscal 1.0 requires (rec: Rust only for 1.0, Delphi for 1.1). (8) open P0s close: XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES (85%, waits on the spiral push), FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE, FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH. (9) no tracked junk: src/corpus.txt (FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND). (10) tag v1.0.0 after all of it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_1_0_dod_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:50Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 07:51 DECIDED (user 11-02 07:5x: \"those things can be decided autonomously\"), replacing n1's \"USER/MAIN DECISION\" on backends. RULE, fixed first: fiscal 1.0 requires every backend that has a CI row in the fiscal workflow and is green today. A backend with an open blocker item joins in a minor release once that item closes. OUTCOME: 1.0 = Rust Cells on ubuntu-24.04 + windows-2025 (green at c8830d7, run 41366612730). Delphi/Pascal = 1.1, gated on DELPHI-CASE-INSENSITIVE-NAMES + FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH. ORG-VERSIONING adoption itself stays main's/the user's (org-wide direction), so this item stays draft.")
inl note_of_fiscal_1_0_dod_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:59Z", "main", "main 11-02 DECIDED, no longer a user decision. RULE (fixed before looking, per the user via fiscal 11-02: \"those things can be decided autonomously\"; technical calls are ours, decided by a pre-stated rule with rule and outcome recorded). Rule: a 1.0 requires the backends that (a) already run its consumer path green in CI and (b) are its declared primary target; others come in the next minor. Outcome: Rust for 1.0 (generated units already build and test there); Delphi for 1.1 (DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY 78%, not CI-green yet). Matches fiscal's own recommendation.")
inl note_of_fiscal_1_0_dod_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:06Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 11:01 from the 11-02 star exchange (compiler #13, kit #8): pack16 link: units write <stem>.unit.json beside the .spi, and an importer of an unbuilt link: unit fails 'build X first'. Add to the typed-units/1 blockers: (11) gitignore *.unit.json in fiscal; (12) build.ps1 and any staged regen build link: units in link: order, units first; a staged copy-back must carry the .unit.json files too, not just .rs. CORRECTION (main 11-02 13:5x): *.unit.json files are TEMPORARY (pack17 moves them out of the tree), so blocker (11) is \"never commit *.unit.json\", NOT a permanent gitignore entry. Blocker (12), building in link: order, stands. pack16c (core B640F761890510F7) is the first compiler that writes them; the :: drift lint finds 0 in fiscal.")
inl note_of_fiscal_1_0_dod_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", 5u32, "2026-11-07T15:53Z", "fiscal", "11-07 groom DoD: typed-units/1 layout adopted (TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1), every typed-units/1 gate green, fiscal CI green on its backends on a pushed commit, and a 1.0 tag cut under ORG-VERSIONING once that proposal is adopted. NEXT: none of fiscal's to take; it waits on ORG-VERSIONING's adoption (the user's yes) and TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_1_0_dod_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-1-0-DOD", 6u32, "2026-11-09T22:47Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 18:5x wait moved from prose to a wait row (user: ORG-VERSIONING adoption, then TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1). BLOCKER: ORG-VERSIONING is a proposal the user has not adopted. NEXT STEP for fiscal once it is adopted: map today's gates onto the typed-units/1 layout and cut the tag only on a pushed commit with CI green on every backend.")
inl typed_transformer_lab () = Task ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", "Typed transformer at spiral/apps/transformer: llama2.c-style stories15M/42M/110M inference in one Spiral source with type-level tensor shapes, token-identical to run.c, C/Rust/CUDA/WGSL, faster than llama2.mojo; generic shape/op-graph/memory-plan code in lib, reused by tibia", Epic, P1, D8, 45u32, Active, "TIBIA-AGENT", "ml,transformer,benchmarks,typefeatureset,lib,compiler,team:tibia,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_typed_transformer_lab () = Planning ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", Minutes 4800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_1 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:14Z", "regex", "regex 07:2x FILED for the user (11-02 07:0x: \"put in the backlog so we start the llama2/transformer experiment later while talking to tibia to see his plans in leveraging mrakgr's ml library's graph code ... we lost in the wipe the conversations about this, maybe we have in agile history\"). HISTORY CHECKED: no llama/transformer item or note exists in the backlog or in the git history of i574n.github, kit, spiral, tibia or eoie (git log -S). The only surviving source is the 10-29..31 share (DIRECTION-1031 n1 lists typed_llama as a gated candidate): artifact cccab1fd section D.2 and the \"typed_llama\" row (score 21, the top GPU challenge), 4edd442c #3, d05f9cdd naming. TIBIA ANSWERED (ML-LABS n11): tibia takes nothing from the graph code (its policy is an integer 8-6-3 net, integer-only so WGSL and C agree bit for bit; targets C, Rust, WGSL, Lua; corebase arrays are C++/CUDA-only); it WILL consume a typed shape/dimension core from lib if one lands with C/Rust/WGSL arms and a generic element type. GOAL: a llama2.c-style inference (stories15M first, maybe GPT-2 small) in one typed Spiral source with tensor shapes as type-level dimensions, emitting C, Rust, CUDA and WGSL. DOD (from cccab1fd D.2, numbers the authors published, re-measure on our machines before citing): greedy output token-identical to llama2.c run.c on stories15M/42M/110M with a fixed seed and checkpoint; logits max abs diff <= 1e-4 in fp32; tok/s >= llama2.c runfast single-thread and >= its OpenMP build on the same machine; CUDA and WGSL tok/s published per model size; a \"one source, five backends\" table; benchmarks in CI rendered on a dir-tree-html page like regex. ARENA (incumbents, re-measure): llama2.c ~110 tok/s (M1 Air), llama2.mojo 1,025-1,283 parallel vs 730 llama2.c OpenMP and 890 llama.cpp, llama2.zig 660 single-thread vs 548 runfast, llama2.rs ~215 vs ~220 C; candle, burn, dfdx as Rust references (dfdx abandoned computed shapes: the narrative). PLAN: (1) read Spiral-s-ML-Library ml/ (layers, matmul kernel, models, primitives) and corebase/tensorm for the typed op graph, dimension propagation and storage planner, as design input only (C++/CUDA macros do not port); (2) a shape/dimension core in lib (type-level naturals per the mega samples' idioms, MEGA-SAMPLES-AS-MODELS n1) with C/Rust/WGSL arms, which tibia can consume; (3) CPU reference matmul/attention/rmsnorm/rope/softmax with oracle tests against run.c dumps; (4) GPU kernels. NAMING: never put \"llama\" in a product name (Meta trademark); compatibility can be cited. DEPENDS ON: ML-LABS (Tensor Lab), compiler Rc/FBIP premise (cccab1fd: without Perceus/FBIP timeboxes double). NEXT STEP when started: pin llama2.c + stories15M checkpoint + tokenizer as CI downloads (never committed), write the run.c oracle dump test first.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_2 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:24Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x CORRECTION from tibia (via main): tibia DID plan graph reuse: TIBIA-AGENT (Done, 53 notes, \"Agent from mrakgr's graph code\"). 10-22/23: M1 port of CEM + memory plan to C failed twice (TIBIA-AGENT n47); M2e typed per-agent view failed (n52); M3 = a typed graph with sizes as type indices and a raw -> planned -> frozen typestate, drafted green but never landed (n49), draft at tibia/target/predict/agent-m3/src/typed_network.spi (tibia is moving it; read its new path from TIBIA-AGENT). ML-LABS n11 is rewritten with the details. DECISION: the shared ground is ONE typed-graph/shape core in lib with a generic element type, designed together with the lib vec/fin module the regex absorption map needs (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB (b)); run the 3-line shadowing repro (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type) before naming it. Deps now ML-LABS,TIBIA-AGENT. FIRST STEP when started: read the M3 draft and TIBIA-AGENT n47/n49/n52 for why M1/M2e failed.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_3 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 3u32, "2026-11-02T13:09Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: OWNERSHIP moves to the tibia lane, by the user 11-02: 'so yeah you're saying tibia isn't enough and we need the transformer effort, let's go with that (spiral/apps/transformer), with the generic code in lib, and tibia reusing it as much as it can ... we'll need compiler backend changes too to beat mojo's speed'. P2 to P1; '(later)' dropped. Also mine the ML library graph and its modeling for every nugget, our fork commits included. Children are filed from two inventories: the original deliberation (DIRECTION-1031 share, archive 20261101-080304) and an ML-library nugget sweep. GPU runs use the standing Europa permission (rent, run, DELETE right away).")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_4 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 4u32, "2026-11-02T13:40Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, ORIGINAL DELIBERATION re-read: share eab494f1 / conversation d21da8dc, archive %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261101-080304, full extraction in scratchpad llama2-deliberation.md. Findings that correct n1:\n(1) The user's 10-30 ask was \"something derived from the graph in mrakgr's ml library\" (conv:887). llama2 was the assistant's proposal (R1-4edd #3). The user only asked \"can the model started in the tibia repo yield good gpu results ... or the llama idea is the best for this niche?\" (conv:908). The user CHOSE it on 11-02: \"let's go with that (spiral/apps/transformer)\".\n(2) DoD as written (R2-cccab D.2/F#4): greedy output token-identical to run.c on stories15M/42M/110M; logits max abs diff <= 1e-4 fp32; tok/s >= llama2.c runfast single-thread and >= its OpenMP build on the same machine; CUDA and WGSL tok/s published per size; a backends table. Oracle: diff against ./run stories15M.bin -t 0. Timebox 6 weeks, doubling without Perceus/FBIP. Only gate: WGSL < 50% of CUDA on the same GPU means CPU + CUDA only. New on top, from the user 11-02: beat llama2.mojo (1,025-1,283 tok/s parallel by its author).\n(3) Never designed in the deliberation, so filed here as gaps: op graph/IR and layer-by-layer type plan (only matmul : t [m,k] -> t [k,n] -> t [m,n] and reshape via mult were given); matmul tiling; SIMD codegen; emitted-code threading; KV-cache layout; tokenizer.bin BPE; mmap checkpoints; int8/q8 quantization (runq.c); a CPU-speed failure gate; and the ML library graph itself (only \"a alavanca e a linhagem tensor1..14/ml1..3\", which lives in the fork's Spiral Compilation Tests/cuda_experiments).\n(4) Advice kept: compile-time shapes are the differentiator against stable Rust (generic_const_exprs #76560); Rc is fine at load time, never in matmul; publish compile time beside run time; no inflated Mojo-style claims; same-machine comparisons only; never put \"llama\" in the product name (Meta trademark; citing compatibility is fine); keep runtime model-size dispatch outside existentials (one specialization per checkpoint).\n(5) The deliberation's tibia line (\"second GPU front\", a Craftax-Classic port bit-identical to JAX at >= 405k SPS) is noted for TIBIA, not adopted.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_5 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:07Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, CHILDREN FILED from both inventories (research saved at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\: llama2-deliberation.md and ml-library-nuggets.md). App: TRANSFORMER-ORACLE, -CPU-REFERENCE, -TOKENIZER, -CHECKPOINT-LOAD, -CPU-SPEED, -GPU, -QUANT-Q8, -MOJO-STUDY, -BENCH-PAGE. Lib (generic, also reused by tibia): LIB-TYPE-SHAPES, LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS, LIB-ARENA-PLANNER, LIB-OP-GRAPH, LIB-ROW-OPS, LIB-PICKLER-GADT, LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES. Compiler: COMPILER-EMIT-PARALLEL-LOOPS, COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN, COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP, COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES, COMPILER-CUDA-TENSOR-CORES. GPU: GPU-STACKED-RUNS (20 USD cap). tibia side: TIBIA-TYPED-NETWORK, TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION, TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS. Every nugget in the inventory is a KEEP or REMODEL row folded into one of these, or a DROP with its reason in the file. LESSONS to hold to (inventory section 6): the batch dim stays free of the launch shape; plan shared memory explicitly (nvcc never reuses static smem); sync tiled kernels before async/Cutlass; read ptxas -v before restructuring for registers; golden deterministic tests and per-thread rng from day one; watch generated size and compile time; add a backend arm before relying on any core module; probe hardware, never hardcode it. Suggested order: ORACLE, then LIB-TYPE-SHAPES, then CPU-REFERENCE on LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS, ARENA-PLANNER and ROW-OPS, then the compiler speed items, then GPU.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_6 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 6u32, "2026-11-02T14:45Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MINGLED: tibia decomposed this item on 11-02 (TRANSFORMER-ORACLE, -CPU-REFERENCE, -TOKENIZER, -CHECKPOINT-LOAD, -CPU-SPEED, -GPU, -QUANT-Q8, -MOJO-STUDY, -BENCH-PAGE in spiral/apps/transformer; lib cores LIB-TYPE-SHAPES, LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS, LIB-ARENA-PLANNER, LIB-OP-GRAPH; compiler COMPILER-EMIT-PARALLEL-LOOPS, COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN, COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP). Those replace the PLAN steps of n1; n1's DoD and arena numbers stand. The regex lane's LIB-VEC-FIN builds on LIB-TYPE-SHAPES.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_7 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 7u32, "2026-11-02T15:03Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia groom from the star exchange. (1) Start spiral/apps/transformer on typed-units/1 from day one (TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1): model = shapes/config, feature = forward pass and sampling, boundary = checkpoint IO, the host and every target-language macro, bin = the CLI. A unit with exports writes <stem>.unit.json: gitignore it and build in link: order (compiler pack16). (2) Cells targets are a closed list (rust fsharp typescript python cuda cpp gleam lua c delphi pascal zig lean wgsl, no wasm); one bad ///> line aborts the whole file. (3) Never emit bulk data (weights, oracle dumps) as code: rustc hit 10 GB on 16k string cells (MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV n13); weights load at runtime and oracles are compared at runtime. (4) A/B the generated size per variant before choosing a granular shape (kit: +230 vs +16 generated lines). (5) Require executed > 0 per file in every gate (compiler: \"passed 0 of 73\" exited 0).")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_8 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 8u32, "2026-11-03T05:39Z", "tibia", "11-03 01:3x tibia, GENERIC KERNELS MOVED TO LIB (unstaged in spiral): new lib/spiral/f32_kernels.spi (registered after heap_scope) holds the transformer's offset-based array-f32 kernels unchanged: sum_squares/scale_into/rmsnorm, dot, matmul_rows/matmul, copy_into, add_into, axpy, max_from/exp_from/divide_from/softmax, zero_from, plus floats_of and near for tests. apps/transformer/transformer.spi opens f32_kernels, drops its copies, and moves its matmul and softmax tests to lib. Lib tests (c + rust): matmul, softmax order and sum, rmsnorm (3,4 with weights 1,2 gives 0.84852, 2.26274), axpy at offsets. PROOFS (node job chain3-1, memo off): lib positive 4/4, type errors 0; mutant (softmax denominator + 1) fails exactly softmax_keeps_the_order_and_sums_to_one; transformer 5/5 on top of lib (greedy tokens equal to run.c, logits within 1e-4, prompt encode, top-p, raw bytes), so the move changed no output. Two test cells were over the cell budget (289, 304), so they now use a near helper and a binding; the re-gate is queued (chain5). Relation: sized_array keeps the type-level dot/matmul; f32_kernels is the runtime-shaped twin that the transformer uses, since checkpoint dims arrive at runtime.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_9 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 9u32, "2026-11-03T05:59Z", "tibia", "11-03 01:59 tibia: lib/spiral/f32_kernels.spi GATE GREEN (node job chain7-1, spiral digest 0DC2227B86AEA6FB, file D6819F8E8B480D21): positive 4/4, type errors 0, cell budget 0 (test checks moved into the helpers ordered_unit and near_pair), mutant fails exactly softmax_keeps_the_order_and_sums_to_one. With chain3-1's transformer 5/5 on top of it, the kernel move is done.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_10 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 10u32, "2026-11-03T21:32Z", "tibia", "11-03 17:5x tibia, 15M RE-BENCH WITH THE LANDED LIB IS INCONCLUSIVE (no claim): 16 rounds alternating order on europa, runfast vs the typed transformer (map_f32s zero-copy, landed file_system 4360A1E93B85). The script waited for load < 0.5, but other lanes started mid-run: 11 of 32 rows ran at load > 1.5; means runfast 1366.9 / typed 1452.7 ms. Quiet rows only (load <= 1.0, 7 paired rounds): runfast 1090 / typed 1201 ms, paired runfast/typed 91.8 percent, consistent with this morning (about 93 percent on 15M) but the absolute times are about 33 percent above this morning quiet ones (runfast 822 ms), so the host itself was slower (steal). Kept as a trend point only; the 11-03 morning squares stay the reference. Rerun when europa is idle for 10+ minutes.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_11 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 11u32, "2026-11-03T21:38Z", "tibia", "11-03 17:5x tibia, 15M CLEAN RE-RUN WITH THE LANDED LIB (europa, waited for load < 0.5, max row load 0.97, 0 rows above 1.5): 16 alternating rounds, runfast 987.1 ms vs typed 1060.1 ms mean; paired runfast/typed per round mean 93.3 percent (min 77.7, max 109.5). Same as this morning (about 93 percent on 15M), so landing the zero-copy loader as a lib module (file_system map_f32s, split into small C helpers for the cell budget) cost nothing measurable. The host is about 20 percent slower than this morning in absolute terms (runfast 822 then), so only the paired ratio compares across sessions. Per-round spread is wide (78-110), so a 2 percent claim would need more rounds; none is made.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_12 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 12u32, "2026-11-03T21:52Z", "tibia", "11-03 18:0x tibia, 42M and 110M with the landed lib (same 16-round alternating protocol, load gate < 0.5): 42M CLEAN (max row load 0.99, 0 rows above 1.5): runfast 2464.9 vs typed 2558.2 ms, paired runfast/typed 96.4 percent (min 89.7, max 106.6), consistent with this morning 97.4-97.8. 110M CONTAMINATED (9 of 32 rows above load 1.5, peak 4.21, another lane started): runfast 8104.9 vs typed 8057.6 ms, paired 100.6 percent: not usable, no claim; this morning 96.8 stays the reference. Summary with the landed zero-copy lib: 15M 93.3, 42M 96.4 percent of runfast; the gap still shrinks with model size (fixed per-token overhead dominates the small model).")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_13 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 13u32, "2026-11-03T22:08Z", "tibia", "11-03 18:1x tibia: 110M second attempt also CONTAMINATED (waited 540 s for load < 0.5, then 24 of 32 rows above load 1.5, peak 6.41; paired 97.8 percent with a 70-121 spread): no claim, and no further 110M attempts tonight while other lanes keep europa busy; this morning 96.8 percent stays the 110M reference.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_14 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 14u32, "2026-11-03T22:45Z", "tibia", "11-03 18:4x tibia, 110M THIRD ATTEMPT, near-clean (started at load 0.38; 5 of 32 rows just above 1.5, peak 1.64): runfast 7795.1 vs typed 7941.6 ms; paired runfast/typed 98.3 percent over all 16 rounds (min 92.0, max 109.8), 98.0 percent over the 12 rounds with both runs at load <= 1.5. So with the landed lib: 15M 93.3, 42M 96.4, 110M about 98 percent of runfast (this morning 93 / 97.4-97.8 / 96.8); 110M within noise of this morning, no regression from landing the loader.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_15 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 15u32, "2026-11-04T04:20Z", "tibia", "11-04 00:20 tibia, from the star exchange (compiler #8): the runtime_bench hot-loop ranking is Zig 71, Wasm 114, C 210, Lua 7563 ms (mega_brzozowski); examples-only timings had measured start-up. NEXT, CPU-light for the box: build the typed transformer on the Zig backend on the node, and time stories15M greedy on europa against the C build (same tokens, 16 rounds, load-gated) as BACKEND-METRICS-MODEL's second compute sample. Node and europa first, box last (user 11-04).")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_16 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 16u32, "2026-11-06T08:18Z", "compiler", "11-06 04:1x compiler GROOM: Active 52 h untouched -> Planned (WIP cap). tibia can re-activate it; the live transformer work is TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION / TRANSFORMER-CPU-SPEED.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_17 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 17u32, "2026-11-06T08:20Z", "tibia", "11-06 04:19 tibia (groom, untouched 52 h): the lab's live work moved into its children. TRANSFORMER-CPU-REFERENCE is Done. TRANSFORMER-CPU-SPEED shows v6 at 96.9% / 98.4% of runomp8, and the chunk lever is refuted. TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION (compiler) has the v8 sweep pending on the node. The lab stays Active only as the umbrella. NEXT: close it once CPU-SPEED reaches a verdict (beat runomp8 or record the gap), and keep GPU work under TRANSFORMER-GPU (blocked: 0 Cloud GPU locations).")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_18 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 18u32, "2026-11-06T10:12Z", "compiler", "11-06 06:1x compiler: REVERTED my 04:1x Active -> Planned move. This is a team:tibia item. I picked it from `kit agile list --team compiler`, which matches the plain compiler tag loosely (x star 06:12 #1: 329 rows, 151 truly team:compiler). The status is tibia's call; I restored Active, and my 04:1x next-step note stands as a suggestion only.")
inl note_of_typed_transformer_lab_19 () = Note ("TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB", 19u32, "2026-11-07T15:47Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (lint markers). DoD: stories15M/42M/110M token-identical to run.c on C and Rust (done for C), CUDA and WGSL arms, and faster than llama2.mojo on the same host (TRANSFORMER-BEAT-MOJO). TypeFeatures: type-level tensor shapes everywhere (sized dims), speed only from codegen levers, no shape erasure.")
