inl note_of_regex_sota_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SOTA", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:15Z", "regex", "regex 07:3x FILED for the user (11-02 07:0x: \"iterate enough so we beat the performance with spiral, even if we have to patch the compiler backends to optimize codegen, while still emitting crates limited to 1k loc\"). STARTING POINT (REGEX-BENCH-PAGE n7, n9): our list-backed minimal DFA takes 1/0.068 = ~15x the regex crate's time on 4 x 4000 bits; on tiny anchored words the crate's per-call cost makes it 5-7x slower than ours. DOD: on the CI page (ubuntu-24.04 and windows-2025, in-job A/A passing), for every throughput workload of REGEX-BENCH-CATALOGUE the best Spiral engine's median per-round ratio vs the regex crate is <= 1.00 with IQR printed and counts equal; the same tables also beat regex-automata dense::DFA where the workload is DFA-only; every generated file <= 1000 lines; no workload is dropped to win (losses stay on the page). ORDER: REGEX-DFA-TABLE (data layout, biggest lever), REGEX-CRATE-UNITS (keeps the 1k rule), REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES (compiler), prefilters/AOT from REGEX-AOT-TARGETS, then rebar (REGEX-REBAR GATE 1: geomean <= 2.0x continue). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: engines stay prototype instances over typed workloads; speed never comes from erasing types in Spiral, only from what codegen emits.")
inl note_of_regex_sota_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SOTA", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:29Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x HANDOFF (START HERE if the regex subagent is gone; user 11-02 07:0x asked for a backlog main can continue from). STATE: i574n/regex CI is GREEN at 1a9668b (run 41366627749: 50/50 Spiral tests on ubuntu + windows, bench ran, page pushed to gh-pages) but GitHub Pages is NOT enabled (user setting), so the page 404s. Unstaged on top: src/table.spi (array-backed DFA table + 2 tests, not yet run in Cells), src/package.spiproj, bench/bench.spi (TableArm, VOID rows print the unverified median); proven: the bench compiles and every arm returns equal counts (box run 07:2x). ORDER OF WORK: 1 REGEX-DFA-TABLE (push the unstaged files; read the CI table vs n2 prediction), 2 REGEX-CRATE-UNITS (kit's link: plan, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE n12), 3 REGEX-BENCH-CATALOGUE (workloads as typed records; regex-automata dense/sparse, aho-corasick, fancy-regex, resharp arms), 4 REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES (4 measured candidates in n2), 5 REGEX-BYTES-UTF8 -> REGEX-SPANS -> REGEX-PREFILTER, 6 REGEX-RUST-DIALECT -> REGEX-REBAR (GATE 1), in parallel the absorption items REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE, REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED (also a speed win), REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE, REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES, LIB-VEC-FIN (shared with tibia TIBIA-AGENT M3 and TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB) -> REGEX-TYPED-CORES; then REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION (archive, gate in its n2). Later: REGEX-AOT-TARGETS, REGEX-LEAN-VALIDATION, REGEX-PRETOK, REGEX-MASK, TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB. HOW TO PROVE: Cells on the node takes ~45 min (drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SYNTAX\\cells-gate.ps1 via remote.ps1 node job; one job at a time, retry after memory kills); bench-only on the node ~6 min (drafts\\regex\\REGEX-BENCH-PAGE\\bench-build.ps1); a user push gives CI in ~10 min with quiet-runner numbers (CI is the reference for timing). USER DECISIONS PENDING: enable Pages, crate name, license (spiral is AGPL v3; regex has none), go for the archive.")
inl note_of_regex_sota_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SOTA", 3u32, "2026-11-02T12:27Z", "regex", "regex 08:3x LESSONS FOLDED FROM THE OTHER REWRITES (11-02 research on ERP, CIC, zeta): (1) prototypes are mandatory (the user: mega samples are not the bar without them); dispatch a runtime choice once at the boundary, never instances packed in records of functions (583 -> 1,549 Rust lines in fiscal); (2) refusing constructors for every certificate/witness; (3) negatives as fails blocks; (4) every rewrite gets an absorption map + archive gate (regex is the template, ERP/CIC/zeta copy it); (5) false passes: polyglot's zeta tests checked mpmath, not Spiral: every regex test asserts on the Spiral value, never only on the oracle; (6) a runtime kernel is needed for Lean-as-oracle (the CIC sample's Lean row returned 0): regex likewise must keep engines computing at run time for benchmarks, with staged engines as a separate AOT category.")
