inl note_of_regex_crate_units_2 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T04:50Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 00:5x UNBLOCKED in practice: its dep COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS' auto-export child LINK-AUTO-EXPORT shipped in pack59d (11-07: AE1 monomorphic one-group, AE2 curried via a tuple wrapper, AE3 every module of a unit's package, AE2B skips polymorphic/wildcard shapes), and compiler's scratch proof split rx_syntax into a linked unit: bench.rs 6,934 -> 5,965 lines with all 17 deterministic bench facts identical. Its last step for Done is 'main's (org's) real split of regex', i.e. this item. CHANGED SINCE 11-06: syntax/charset/nullable/derivative/language moved into lib as regex_*, and lib links as ONE unit per the template decision, so the engine families left in regex/src are dfa+minimal+certificate+table, lazy, partial, semantics(+backtracking), agreement, laws, typed, xsd. STEP 1 queued: job-1794199751574-org2-regex-measure on ganymede (build.ps1 -fast = regen + cargo, no Cells gate; it prints every generated .rs size) to get today's bench.rs size under pack63c. Next: the :~ join-point pass over bench.spi's multi-use helpers (the workload_report/facts_of builders), then units per engine family with typed entries, measured by kit crate gate --limit 1000.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_3 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T04:54Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 01:0x FINDING (measured on the committed bench.rs, 4,777 lines, 150 fns; the fresh pack63c size comes from job-1794199751574): the 11-02 plan's step 1 (':~ join-point pass over bench.spi helpers') buys almost nothing. Every one of bench.spi's 23 ':=' helpers has 1-2 call sites (size_text and all_arms 2, all others 1), so inlining doesn't multiply them. The largest generated fns are library/engine code inlined into the single crate: group_12 293 lines (the order_re group from lib regex_syntax), prepare_2 209 (builds every engine), workload_report_1 192, facts_of_120 166, agree_from_132 116, time_row_143 108, partials_107 103, derive_35 87, nullability_of_41 80. So the only route under 1000 is UNITS: (a) the regex_* lib modules out of bench.rs into their own linked unit (the order_re group, derive and nullability alone are ~460 lines), (b) one unit per engine family in regex/src (dfa+minimal+certificate+table; lazy; partial; semantics), (c) bench keeps only workloads + the report. Precondition to check first: can a repo link (part of) lib as a unit today? The template decision says 'lib = ONE link unit', but I found no repo that links lib as a unit yet; that's the design question to settle with compiler before cutting. Next: read the measurement, then ask compiler about a lib link unit vs a regex_model unit inside regex holding the regex_* imports.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_4 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T05:50Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 02:1x DESIGN SETTLED with compiler (owner of auto-export): OPTION B. Under AE1-AE3 a unit auto-exports only the top-level, annotated, single-group (or curried, via a synthesized __uncurried), forall-free definitions of ITS OWN package's modules; opened lib modules are NOT candidates. So: (1) regex/src/regex_model/ becomes a unit package (auto-export: monomorphic in its manifest), listed AFTER the lib packages under packages so its names shadow correctly; (2) its modules hold THIN MONOMORPHIC WRAPPERS for exactly what bench and the engine units call (e.g. derive_regex (r : re) (c : u32) : re = derive c r; nullable_regex; the order_re group entry; ...), every parameter annotated (a polymorphic or partially applied call still inlines, and the build warns if a call reaches a lambda-wrapped export); (3) the lib bodies are then emitted once in regex_model's crate, and consumers link to regex_model_<name>. OPTION A (lib as a linked unit) is NOT available: lib stays ONE unit and nothing builds a linked unit from a subset of lib. Expected: bench.rs drops by the ~460 lib-derived lines; if still over 1000, split bench's own drivers into a second unit. Next step: once job-1794199751574 gives today's sizes, list the lib functions bench and the engines call (the wrapper set), then write regex_model.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_5 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T05:52Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 02:2x WRAPPER SET for regex_model (grep of the 119 top-level defs in lib regex_charset/syntax/nullable/derivative/language against bench.spi + dfa/minimal/certificate/table/lazy/partial/semantics/agreement): the CODE-SIZE drivers are the derivative group (derive, 6 call sites), nullable (6), the order_re group behind same_re (8) + insert_leaf (3) + order_re (1), the smart constructors seq (11), star (10), repeat (6), alt (5), both (5), negate (5), language_answer (the oracle, 5), matches (4), and the charset helpers contains / single / range / of_ranges. High counts on ends_in_zero (25), fourth_from_end (24), word (19), zero_runs (10) are test FIXTURES, not size drivers (wrap them only if bench's drivers need them). So regex_model's modules wrap: derive_regex, nullable_regex, same_regex, seq_regex / alt_regex / both_regex / star_regex / repeat_regex / negate_regex, language_regex, matches_regex, contains_set, single_set, range_of, of_ranges_set, each fully annotated, monomorphic (re, u32, char_set normal, list u32). COST NOTE: consumers must CALL the wrapper names (regex_model_<name> through the link), so bench + every engine module's call sites switch from the lib names to the wrappers; that's the bulk of the edit (~110 call sites by the counts above), mechanical but wide, best done one engine family per step with a regen measurement after each. Next step: today's bench.rs size from job-1794199751574, then regex_model + bench's call sites first (bench alone carries the headline number).")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_6 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T07:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 04:3x SCOPE NOTE: with REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX/-DERIVATIVE closed as superseded (their modules are lib now) and REGEX-UNIT-AUTOMATA waiting on REGEX-LIB-3, this item owns the split of everything that stays in regex: partial, lazy, agreement, laws, witness, semantics, typed, xsd + the bench, per the Option B regex_model design.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_7 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:0x measurement (ganymede job-1794213011274): the only generated crate in regex today is bench/bench.rs at 7065 lines (the 1000-line gate is OPEN for it: build.ps1 warns and keeps it uncommitted until REGEX-BENCH-PAGE splits bench.spi by hand); regex/src produces no committed .rs (Cells tests only). So the unit split that matters first is the bench: bench.spi -> per-arm/per-workload units under 1000 generated lines each, linking the lib regex_* modules once REGEX-LIB-3/4/5 land. Next step: list bench.spi's definitions by arm to size the split.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_8 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 8u32, "2026-11-09T11:05Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 11:3x SPLIT SIZING (next step done): bench.spi is only 461 lines (largest definitions: answer 19, prepare 16, all_arms 14, arm_name 13, one_pass 12) yet bench.rs is 7065 generated lines, so the crate is dominated by the ~14 opened regex modules compiled INTO it (lib regex_charset/syntax/derivative/language + src dfa, minimal, table, certificate, partial, agreement, semantics, lazy, table_emit), not by the bench's own code. Splitting bench.spi alone cannot reach the 1000-line gate. Plan in order: (1) the engine as linked typed units following html's typed-units/1 layout (Option B regex_model + thin monomorphic wrappers per unit): regex_core (lib regex_* + dfa/minimal/table/certificate after REGEX-LIB-3 moves them to lib), regex_lazy (lazy + partial), regex_oracle (agreement + semantics), regex_staged (table_emit + the generated staged_tables), each with `link` entries in spiral.toml so its code is compiled once per unit instead of inlined into the bench; (2) then the bench in 3 small units: bench_workloads (workload, names, regexes, crate patterns, expected sizes, words), bench_arms (arm, answer, one_pass, *_accepted, timed, rounds), bench_report (spread, milli_text, time_row, facts_head, setup_line, stamp, main). Measure after (1): if each linked unit and the bench crate are under 1000 generated lines, the gate closes. Next step: after REGEX-LIB-3 lands, write regex_core's Cargo.toml + spiral.toml (link) using html's unit layout as the sibling to copy.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_9 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 9u32, "2026-11-09T15:27Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:2x STEP 1 (de-duplicate before splitting): regex/src's own dfa/minimal/certificate/table copies are REMOVED in favor of the lib modules REGEX-LIB-3 landed. Checked first: each lib module equals its src twin modulo the module renames, layout (static block position, a --timeout header), certificate's probe -> pending_pair, and regex_dfa's new sound cap. Edits (unstaged; backups drafts\\regex\\REGEX-CRATE-UNITS-SWAP): src/spiral.toml drops the 4 modules; 23 open lines repointed to regex_* in agreement, lazy, partial, semantics, typed, core_emit, table_emit, bench.spi, staged_check/tables/time (git grep missed the untracked ones; plain grep found 9 more); bench.spi's staged emitter template now writes :< regex_table, so the regenerated staged_tables.spi still matches. Budget oracle clean on every gated file. Proof: full regex build.ps1 on ganymede (job org2-swap) against a regex tree linked to the exact box spiral copy (lib 0CCCB6163BFA0636). Effect on the 1000-line gate: the 4 modules now come from lib, so the next step (the typed linked units) can link them once instead of inlining per crate.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_10 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 10u32, "2026-11-09T15:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:5x COVERAGE GAP found mid-proof and fixed: the swap run's Cells gate shows 51/51 over 11 files (was 87/87 over 15): the 36 tests of dfa/minimal/certificate/table moved to lib with them, and NOTHING executes lib regex_* tests on a recurring basis (lib/spiral/build.ps1's notebook list has no regex_* module; land windows only type-probe; regex's gate covered src/ only). The same was already true of regex_charset/syntax/derivative/nullable/language. Fix (regex/build.ps1, unstaged): the gate list is DERIVED from regex's own sources: every `:< regex_*` open in src/bench/staged maps to deps/spiral/lib/spiral/<m>.spi (throw if missing), so today = 9 lib modules, and a future move into lib is gated automatically. Parse clean. A second full run after org2-swap proves it.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_11 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 11u32, "2026-11-09T15:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:5x STEP 1 PROVEN: ganymede job-1794238049801-org2-swap, full regex build.ps1 on the swapped tree (no src dfa/minimal/certificate/table; opens -> lib regex_*), linked to the exact box spiral copy (lib 0CCCB6163BFA0636): Cells 51/51 over 11 files (the moved modules' 36 tests now live in lib; the derived lib gate restores them, run 2 below), bench compiled (RUST-COMPILED bench.rs 20 s), \"staged_tables.spi matches the emitter\" (the :< regex_table template change and the generated file agree), REGEX-OK. bench.rs 7861 lines (was 7741: the lib modules are still compiled INTO the crate, so the 1000-line gate needs step 2, the linked units). Setup rows unchanged in shape (certified build 0.014 ms .. 1414.9 ms vs staged pass 0.007-0.119 ms). Run 2 (org2-swap2): same tree + the derived lib gate in build.ps1.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_12 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 12u32, "2026-11-09T16:46Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 16:4x STEP 1 DONE incl. the coverage fix: ganymede job-1794240598692-org2-swap2 (same swapped tree + the derived lib gate): \"lib regex modules gated here: regex_certificate regex_charset regex_derivative regex_dfa regex_language regex_minimal regex_nullable regex_syntax regex_table\", Cells 118/118 over 20 files (was 87/87 over 15 before the swap, 51/51 over 11 right after it): the 36 moved tests run again AND 31 tests of charset/syntax/derivative/nullable/language that had no recurring gate before now run on every regex build; staged match; REGEX-OK; bench.rs 7861 lines. Next step (step 2): the linked typed units, so bench.rs links the lib regex modules once instead of compiling them in (the 1000-line gate).")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_13 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 13u32, "2026-11-09T17:27Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:3x STEP 2 DESIGN (from memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes + html's 8-unit split): a union crosses crates only through a LINKED model unit that every crate on the path links, never through lib (a lib union in an export signature gets copied per crate -> rustc E0308). The engines' types (re, dfa, built, verdict, prepared) now live in lib, so the bench cannot be cut by module. Cut by ARM instead: one unit per arm family, each owning its engine end to end (builds the workload's pattern + prepared state internally) and exporting only PRIMITIVE TUPLED signatures, exported by name (not wrapped in a lambda, which silently inlines): arm_pass ((workload, salt, n) : i32 * u32 * u32) : i32 (matches over the generated corpus, the deterministic row) and arm_nanos (same args) : u64. Units (bench.spi arm union, 10 arms): rx_derivative (BrzozowskiArm, AntimirovArm), rx_automata (EagerArm, MinimalArm, MinimalAgainArm, TableArm), rx_lazy (LazyArm, LazyStoreArm), rx_external (RegexCrateArm, BacktrackingArm); bench keeps orchestration, rotation (bench_model.rotated), spreads and the HTML report, so its own crate holds no engine code. Layout per html: regex/units/<unit>/{spiral.toml (packages + link), Cargo.toml [package.metadata.spiral], <unit>.spi}, workspace member, cargo update --offline --workspace. PROOF per unit: grep bench.rs for `<unit>::` calls (linked, not inlined) and every generated .rs < 1000 lines; then REGEX-BENCH-GATE-THROW flips the warning to a throw. Next step: build rx_external first (smallest: crate regex + backtracking oracle), measure its .rs, then rx_lazy.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_14 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 14u32, "2026-11-09T17:46Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:5x STEP 2, FIRST UNIT DRAFTED (unstaged; backups drafts\\regex\\REGEX-CRATE-UNITS-STEP2): (1) src/workloads.spi (new, gated): the workload union, names, regexes, crate patterns, expected_minimal and the corpus helpers moved out of bench.spi verbatim, plus workload_of_index/index_of_workload (round-trip test); the 3 six-arm matches split into 3-arm halves to fit the cell budget (they were over budget already in bench.spi, ungated there). (2) units/rx_external/ (new crate, workspace member): host.spi (only the regex-crate bindings), rx_external.spi exporting BY NAME external_nanos ((code, workload, salt, n) : i32 * i32 * u32 * u32) : u64 * i32, which prepares outside the clock and times 25 passes inside, exactly the bench's old loop (code 0 = Rust regex crate, 1 = backtracking). (3) bench: prepared drops crate_regex and gains workload/salt/n; timed routes RegexCrateArm/BacktrackingArm to external_nanos, the other 8 arms unchanged; bench/spiral.toml lists ../units/rx_external- under packages AND link; bench Cargo depends on it by path. (4) build.ps1 builds the unit before the bench and reports its .rs size. Proof pending: full build after org2-swap3 frees the tree; check bench.rs for rx_external:: calls (linked, not inlined) and both sizes.")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_15 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 15u32, "2026-11-09T18:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:3x FIRST LINKED UNIT PROVEN: ganymede job-1794247180988-org2-swap4 (full regex build.ps1, box-equal tree): REGEX-OK (Cells gate green; staged match), rx_external compiled as its own crate and regex-bench linked it (\"Compiling rx_external ... Compiling regex-bench ... Finished\"), bench.rs has exactly 1 `rx_external::` call (cross-crate, not inlined: the tupled-primitive export by name works), and bench.rs went 7911 -> 7533 lines (-378, the two external arms). NEW PROBLEM: rx_external.rs is 1939 lines, itself over the 1000-line gate, because the unit compiles in workloads (6 patterns), the corpus generator (agreement random_word/letters) and the backtracking oracle (semantics). Next step: measure which part dominates rx_external.rs (grep its fn sizes); candidate fixes: (a) give the corpus its own unit that exports texts by (workload, salt, n) as list of strings (a list of primitives should cross), (b) split rx_external into rx_crate and rx_backtrack. Then the next arm units (rx_lazy, rx_automata, rx_derivative).")
inl note_of_regex_crate_units_16 () = Note ("REGEX-CRATE-UNITS", 16u32, "2026-11-09T18:57Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 19:0x STEP 2b DRAFTED (unstaged): rx_external.rs was 1939 lines because the unit rebuilt the workload pattern AND the corpus (agreement generator + regex_dfa classes) inside. Fix = pass data instead of rebuilding it, since the bench already holds the corpus in prepared: (1) NEW units/rx_crate: crate_nanos ((pattern, texts) : string * list string) : u64 * i32, only the host regex binding + the 25-pass loop (no lib regex at all); (2) units/rx_external is now backtracking-only: external_nanos ((i, ws) : i32 * list (list u32)) : u64 * i32 rebuilds just workload_regex for the oracle; no host, no regex crate dep. bench external_sample routes RegexCrateArm -> crate_nanos (crate_pattern w, texts), BacktrackingArm -> external_nanos (index, words); bench/spiral.toml lists both units under packages AND link; workspace members + bench path deps updated; build.ps1 builds and size-reports rx_crate. Open question the next build answers: do list string / list (list u32) arguments cross (memory: core lists cross since pack24) or silently inline? Proof: the build after org2-swap5 (grep bench.rs for rx_crate:: and rx_external::, all three .rs sizes).")
inl regex_codegen_patches () = Task ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", "Compiler backend patches driven by the regex hot loop: profile generated Rust/C, patch codegenRust/CodegenC (state dispatch, Rc clones, bounds checks, closures) with in-job A/A + A/B, suite oracle unchanged", Story, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "REGEX-DFA-TABLE", "regex,automata,benchmark,compiler,team:compiler,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_codegen_patches () = Planning ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", Minutes 900u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_codegen_patches_1 () = Note ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:15Z", "regex", "regex 07:3x FILED for the user (\"even if we have to patch the compiler backends to optimize codegen\"). DOD per patch: a pre-registered question and prediction on this item; a minimal regression sample under samples/ (one per codegen change); -Suite all single-flight with no REGRESSED/DISAGREE and every residual change explained; the regex bench ratio moves outside its A/A band on CI; crates stay <= 1000 lines. CANDIDATES (verify by reading the generated bench.rs first, drafts\\regex\\REGEX-BENCH-PAGE\\bench-probe.rs): Rc<str>/Rc list clones inside join-point loops; union-match dispatch on the state emitted as nested if/else instead of a match/jump table; per-call thread_local string literals; bounds-checked array_base indexing where the index is a proven class/state nominal; closures from eta-reduced helpers (memory spiral-eta-reduction-makes-closures). Owner: compiler lane with regex measurements. NEXT STEP: annotate the hottest 5 functions of bench.rs (run, step, class_index, derive, matches) with their generated shape and file the first patch candidate.")
inl note_of_regex_codegen_patches_2 () = Note ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:15Z", "regex", "regex 07:3x EVIDENCE READ from the generated bench.rs (drafts\\regex\\REGEX-BENCH-PAGE\\bench-probe.rs, 4228 lines, 11-01 compiler). Hot loop shape per DFA step: run_from_94 -> step_96 -> row_at_69 + class_index_98 + target_at_97, all walking Rc lists. FOUR codegen candidates, each needs a minimal sample + A/A-gated bench before claiming: (1) LOOP-INVARIANT CLONES: a self-tail-call loop reassigns every parameter, so unchanged ones are cloned each iteration: run_from_94 does `(v0, v1, v2, v3, v4, v5) = (v0.clone(), v1.clone(), v2.clone(), v3.clone(), v8.clone(), v7.clone())` (4 Rc increments + decrements per symbol for arguments that never change); emit only the changed slots. (2) PATTERN-BOUND CLONES: every match arm clones each bound field (`let v4: Rc<UH3> = v4.clone();`) even when the value is used once or only borrowed; move or borrow instead. (3) NON-TAIL ROW LOOKUP: row_at_69 returns a (US6, Rc<UH5>) tuple through real recursion (the record row is flattened into a tuple, which blocks the tail-call loop), so lookup depth = state index on the stack; a tuple-returning self tail call should still become a loop. (4) CONSTANT CASES behind thread_local!: `UH5::UH5_Nil` is fetched through a thread_local Rc on every fallback. (1) and (2) are backend-wide (C/Zig have refcounts too: check them). The data-layout fix (REGEX-DFA-TABLE) removes the list walks; these patches still matter for derivative/Antimirov engines, which are Rc trees by nature.")
inl note_of_regex_codegen_patches_3 () = Note ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x COMPILER BLOCKERS named by the share re-read (item 21, via main): the runtime GADT-index bug (FOR-D, compiler_probe_gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime; main sent the sample to compiler), the --check silent block drop (CHECK-SILENT-DROP), and timer/static helpers that must be :~ join points (seen here: an inlined OnceLock timer gave each call site its own clock, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE n4).")
inl note_of_regex_codegen_patches_4 () = Note ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", 4u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 21 (verbatim): 21. NEW compiler blockers. Fix the runtime GADT-index bug (compiler_probe_gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime); E puts it in M0, the backlog currently works around it. Fix the --check silent drop. Perceus/FBIP must come after partial evaluation, with a DoD of benchmarks against the current version on at least 2 native backends. Add a rule from this session: timer and static helpers must be :~ join points (an inlined := made a separate OnceLock per call site). Source: E §7 M0, §4; S row 11 and tier T3; REGEX-BENCH-PAGE n4.")
inl note_of_regex_codegen_patches_5 () = Note ("REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:45Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MINGLED with the compiler/tibia 11-02 grooms: COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP (Rc reuse; the share's premise that timeboxes double without it), COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN and COMPILER-EMIT-PARALLEL-LOOPS (tibia's transformer needs), FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE and BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY (backend coverage) are the compiler-side homes; this item stays the regex-measured list (the 4 candidates of n2) and each candidate that becomes a compiler patch moves to one of those items with the regex bench as its A/B evidence.")
