inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_1 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:3x ABSORPTION MAP of spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives vs C:\\home\\git\\regex (read-only audit by subagent a7821856091a39bf1 for the user's 11-02 ask \"make sure we're reusing all the modeling goodies from that sample ... don't know how much our new regex repo is absorbing/assimilating that, if it's coming line by line or if we only rewrote parts\"). VERDICT: from-scratch rewrite, 0 legacy identifiers, no line-by-line reuse. 71 items (32 concepts, 31 negatives, 8 compiler probes): 9 ABSORBED, 20 PARTIAL, 42 MISSING. Algorithms and runtime cross-checks carried over; most TYPED modeling did not (Vec/Fin indices, typestate, sealing, indexed DFA cores, the independent language oracle, 3 of 4 engines). Landing: (a) regex module, (b) spiral lib, (c) compiler regression sample, (d) drop.\nCONCEPTS: 1 nominal alphabets + symbol_compare prototype + regex generic over alphabet PARTIAL -> (d) code points make mixing impossible. 2 Peano finite_length, length-indexed finite_symbol_vector, finite_symbol_index (Vec/Fin) total lookup MISSING -> (b) lib vec/fin, compile-time only. 3 finite_alphabet authority/descriptors/cardinality/inventory laws/certified_alphabet_inventory/indexed descriptor (+generic_indexed_alphabet_authority, finite_inventory_adversarial, indexed_dfa_probe) PARTIAL -> (a) checkers in charset.spi/dfa.spi that Normal is normalized and classes partition the code points, plus swapped/short adversarial cases. 4 AST + smart constructors ABSORBED (syntax.spi), missing x*.x* -> x* -> (a). 5 nullable ABSORBED+improved (GADT evidence). 6 derivative/canonical_derivative/accepts ABSORBED. 7 unnormalized reference_derivative/reference_accepts + semantic triangle MISSING -> (a) laws.spi. 8 language_remainders independent oracle MISSING -> (a) semantics.spi; route certificate.check_witnesses through it. 9 law suites (remainder, idempotence, nullable preserved, coherence, step certificate, remainder_theorem, derivative_universal_witness) PARTIAL -> (a) laws.spi with exhaustive depth-2 corpora. 10 static_* twins + compile-time discharge MISSING -> (a) staged.spi. 11 DFA closure BFS ABSORBED. 12 bounded closure 2^(positions+1) budget PARTIAL (fixed cap 4096) -> (a) dfa.spi test against the bound. 13 closure soundness (closed, distinct, total, keys distinct, formula-consistent, normalized, order-coherent; indexed_closure_certificate forged/swapped rows) MISSING -> (a) certificate.check_dfa + forged-row tests. 14 minimization ABSORBED (Moore instead of bisimulation). 15 quotient coverage/representative origins/quotient closed PARTIAL -> (a) check the block map, prove eager ~ minimal. 16 constructive minimality ABSORBED (checked vs derivatives; item 8 makes it independent). 17 GADT typestate (bit_matcher_state, matcher_state, derivative_runtime_gadt, derivative_pipeline) PARTIAL -> (a) automaton phase built -> minimal -> certified. 18 existentials sealed after verification PARTIAL -> (d) existentials compile-time only; result unions refuse instead. 19 higher-ranked capabilities/capability_program/matcher_batch MISSING -> (d) covered by contract_existential_batch, contract_higher_rank_hot_swap. 20 indexed DFA incl. indexed_dfa_state_cardinality compiled core (acceptance vector, Fin-target matrix, coverage/origin counts) PARTIAL -> (a) typed.spi on (b). 21 inventory_indexed_model/proof_suite/inventory_closed_dfa_runtime PARTIAL -> fold into typed.spi. 22 antimirov_certificate reconstruction law PARTIAL -> (a) partial.spi test. 23 antimirov_typed_slot_bound PARTIAL -> (a) runtime injective origin assignment; shape GADT (d). 24 canonical_form_certificate (+_edition3) PARTIAL -> (a) syntax.is_canonical asserted on every DFA state; edition3 duplicate (d). 25 matcher profiles/head shapes MISSING -> (d). 26 ternary examples incl. tri_cyclic_nonminimal PARTIAL -> (a) minimal.spi test. 27 LCG workloads vs regex crate ABSORBED. 28 backtracking baseline MISSING -> (a) semantics.spi + bench arm. 29 staged DFA MISSING -> (a) staged.spi + bench arm. 30 interned memoized lazy DFA (interned_regex/bit_slot nominals) MISSING -> (a) lazy.spi + bench arm. 31 runtime_bench/native/smoke across C/Rust/Delphi PARTIAL -> (a) ///> c or zig targets. 32 bench_* x8, bench.ps1, regex_crate_bench.rs ABSORBED except arms 28-30.\nNEGATIVES (31): alphabet plumbing MISSING (d) [alphabet_mix, missing_compare, missing_alphabet_symbols, missing_finite_inventory_witness, derivative_program_missing_symbols, antimirov_missing_finite_authority, missing_rank_lookup, indexed_descriptor_local_cardinality]; raw_inventory_bypass PARTIAL -> (a) one negative (char_set loose vs normal); length MISSING -> (a) typed.spi after (b) [truncated_canonical_vector, indexed_row_length, finite_index_out_of_range, inventory_length_mix (fails today for the wrong reason)]; cardinality MISSING -> (a) typed.spi [indexed_dfa_quotient_coverage_count, indexed_dfa_representative_origin_count]; typestate MISSING -> (a) with 17 [phase_use, derivative_runtime_phase_use, raw_generic_state_seal, seal_unverified_derivative, derivative_skip_normalization; generic technique also in contract_illegal_transition]; HKT MISSING (d) [hkt_batch_predicate_specific, hkt_requires_capability_capture]; witness forgery: forge_constructive_minimality_witness + raw_representatives_not_minimality_witness PARTIAL (runtime Forged check exists; the first fails for the wrong reason and would compile since nominal constructors are public), exact_rows_not_soundness_witness + raw_quotient_not_semantic_witness MISSING -> (a) runtime forgery tests with 13 and 15; Antimirov MISSING -> (a) runtime forgeries with 23, type-level (d) [antimirov_slot_shape, antimirov_support_assignment_count, forge_structural_support_bound, raw_indexed_not_structural_support_bound, raw_regex_not_positioned_bound].\nCOMPILER PROBES (8): gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime MISSING (open FOR-D bug) -> (c) samples/gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime; gadt_rank_matrix MISSING (guards the 2026-10-06 C/C++ GADT tag-numbering fix) -> (c); gadt_runtime ABSORBED (byte-identical to samples/gadt_specialized_case_rank) (d); existential_helper_control, recursive_indexed_definition, finite_vector_rank PARTIAL -> (b) unit tests of lib vec/fin; generic_inventory_pack, generic_matcher_state MISSING (d). Main already sent the two (c) samples to compiler.\nCOUNTS: concepts 32 = 8/14/10, negatives 31 = 0/3/28, probes 8 = 1/3/4, all 71 = 9/20/42 (absorbed/partial/missing).\nCONSTRAINTS: items 2, 20, 21 and the length/cardinality negatives stay COMPILE-TIME (a let rec over a runtime finite_symbol_index hits the open FOR-D GADT bug; compiled cores run on i32 state). Existentials compile-time only on every backend. Cells test blocks cannot assert \"must not type-check\", so regex negatives need a small negative/ package set that build.ps1 checks. Before naming the lib vec/fin module: the 3-line repro from memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type.\nESTIMATES: (a) ~510 min (semantics 40, laws 40, certificate soundness/coverage/forgeries 35, typestate 30, Antimirov reconstruction+slots 40, canonical checker + x*x* 20, charset/class invariants 20, bound + ternary tests 15, lazy 60, staged 60, bench arms 20, backend targets 10, typed.spi + negatives 120); (b) ~60; (c) ~20 + a matrix accept; (d) ~10.\nDELETE GATE (archive, never delete): the legacy sample goes once (a) items 7, 8, 9, 13, 17, 28, 29, 30 plus (b) and (c) have landed.\nCITATIONS legacy main.spi: symbol_compare 12, finite_length 75, finite_symbol_vector 78, finite_symbol_index 84, indexed descriptor 179, finite_alphabet 155, certified_alphabet_inventory 287, nullable 330, normalize 448, derivative 457, reference_derivative 483, language_remainders 565, semantic triangle 625, step certificate 732, static_* 910-1056 and 1575-1944, indexed_dfa_capability 1058, dfa_closure 1192, bisimulation 1359, constructive distinguishing 1449-1502, dfa_minimize_states 1532, sealed_minimized_dfa 1946, state_budget 1967, position bound 2007, indexed transition vector 2120, dfa_run 2290-2416, dfa_surface_certificate 2423, sealed_dfa_surface 2437, matcher_state 2634, bit_matcher_state 2671, sealed_match 2685, profiles 2705-2717, capability_program 2722, matcher_batch 2910, tri_cyclic_nonminimal 2993; antimirov_typed_slot_bound/main.spi position tree 63, origin slot 119; remainder_theorem/main.spi proof 7; canonical_form_certificate/normalization_derivation.spi 10; indexed_dfa_state_cardinality/main.spi state vector 4, quotient coverage 188, origins 248, acceptance vector 402, target matrix 415. New regex: charset.spi char_set 10; syntax.spi seq 76, alt 119; nullable.spi evidence 12; derivative.spi derive 15, remainder_holds 46; dfa.spi build_rows 97, state_cap 110; minimal.spi moore 103, minimize 140; certificate.spi certify 67, check_minimality 81, forged 96; partial.spi partials 33, support_bound 125; agreement.spi all_agree 63; bench.spi arms 79. Existing compiler samples: gadt_specialized_case_rank, contract_existential_batch, contract_higher_rank_hot_swap, contract_illegal_transition.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_2 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 2u32, "2026-11-02T12:27Z", "regex", "regex 08:3x COVERAGE CHECK (user 11-02: \"make sure we didn't leave anything behind\"): every (a) row of n1 now has an owning item: 3, 4 (x*.x*), 12, 13, 15, 22, 23, 24, 26 + the witness/Antimirov forgeries -> REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES; 7, 8, 9, 28 -> REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE; 10, 29, 30, 32 arms -> REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED; 17 + typestate negatives + raw_inventory_bypass -> REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE; 20, 21 + length/cardinality negatives -> REGEX-TYPED-CORES; (b) 2 + probes existential_helper_control, recursive_indexed_definition, finite_vector_rank -> LIB-VEC-FIN; 31 (c/zig targets) -> REGEX-AGREEMENT (n4 today); (c) gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime + gadt_rank_matrix -> compiler lane (sent by main 11-02); (d) rows recorded with reasons in n1. LESSON FROM THE OTHER REWRITES (ERP/CIC research 11-02): negatives become `:# name fails ETY-TermError \"msg\" =` blocks beside the code (TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC is Done; tibia readiness.spi:81 uses it), not a negative/ package set: REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE is updated accordingly.")
