inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_4 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:37Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MIGRATION DONE RULE (user 11-02: \"make sure all these mega sample migrations have a definition of done so they don't spin forever again, and so we remove their code from the repo asap so we keep only latest code following the new style with test cells etc ... gotta transfer all the goodies before though, different than what regex did, only implemented a sliver then called it done\"). APPLIES TO all five: brzozowski (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB / REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION), lean_cic (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB / CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE), zeta (ZETA-TYPED-ARITH + ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE / ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE), omniledger (FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP / OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE), spiral_proves_spiral (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT + SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). (1) A migration is DONE only when the old sample is ARCHIVED out of the repo; a new home that works (regex published, CI green) is NOT done while absorption rows remain (the regex lesson: 9 of 71 legacy items absorbed at \"publishable\"). (2) Before the archive, every absorption-map row is resolved: (a) absorbed = a passing test in the new home in CI on both OSes, citing the legacy line; (b) lib = landed with lib tests; (c) compiler = a minimal regression sample with a matrix row; (d) dropped = a reason the map states. No row is left \"partial\". (3) ANTI-SPIN: the map is written first (one item, <= 4 h), then every (a)/(b) row is worked in priority order with the row count reported on the parent each groom round (absorbed / total); a week with no row closed raises the parent to P0 for the next round; a row blocked only by a compiler bug becomes its (c) regression sample plus a compiler item, and the archive may proceed with that row recorded as blocked-in-compiler (the goodie survives as the repro, in the new style). (4) The archive step runs in the SAME groom round the last row closes (scratch-archive.ps1, hash-verified, restore command in a note, dangling check by stem, user go), and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps its canary to the new home. (5) The parent item is set Done only after the archive note exists.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_5 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:44Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x (c) ROWS DONE by the compiler lane (GADT-UNINHABITED-PAYLOAD-RUNTIME n-last, 11-02 07:35): samples/gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime runs on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (4 ran, agree 3, DISAGREE 0) and samples/gadt_rank_matrix guards the 10-06 C/C++ GADT tag-numbering fix over three case orders (7 ran, agree 6, DISAGREE 0); compiler_probe_gadt_runtime is byte-identical to samples/gadt_specialized_case_rank and goes with the archive. Both rows are \"new\" until the next full -Suite all accept. Remaining before the archive: the (a) and (b) rows (n2 coverage list).")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_6 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 6u32, "2026-11-04T13:54Z", "main", "11-04 10:0x main ROW (b) DONE via LIB-VEC-FIN: the legacy finite_length / finite_symbol_vector / finite_symbol_index modeling (main.spi 75-97) is in lib as fin_vector.spi (LANDED 11-04, two-step land green): nat_zero/nat_succ, vector n el, fin n with a TOTAL two-arm lookup exactly like finite_symbol_vector_lookup, plus the three probes as tests (existential_helper_control = some_vector/of_list; recursive_indexed_definition = mapped; finite_vector_rank = rank). Also landed: sized_array's literal-indexed bounded n. Remaining before the archive: the (a) rows on their owning items (n2 list).")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_7 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 7u32, "2026-11-06T12:30Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: the 42 missing cases from mega_brzozowski_derivatives are covered by regex tests (or recorded as out of scope), so the sample can be archived. Next step: list the 42 by name against regex's test names.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_8 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 8u32, "2026-11-09T03:09Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:1x PARTIAL RE-AUDIT (read-only, by module and test names in regex/src; NOT a full 71-row re-map): the 11-02 audit is STALE; much of what it called MISSING has landed since (commits 53b31ae..47dfc04 'tests'). Now present: concept 7 (unnormalized vs normalized + semantic triangle) and 9 (law suites): laws.spi checks raw r, normalize r, the production Brzozowski matcher and regex_language's independent oracle over EVERY regex of depth 1 (1,320 checks) and depth 2 (241,560 checks, rust) on all short words, with laws Constructors / Idempotence / Nullability / Remainder / Brzozowski. An oracle triangle is stronger than the unnormalized reference_derivative the audit proposed, so concept 7 is absorbed differently, not missing. Concept 8 (independent language oracle): semantics.spi + lib regex_language, agreeing with every engine on a seeded corpus. ENGINES (the audit said 3 of 4 missing): lazy.spi (a lazy DFA agreeing with the eager one, interning only visited states, answering where the eager cap refuses, overflow answered), partial.spi (Antimirov partial derivatives, within the bound), semantics.spi (backtracking baseline + a ReDoS shape). CERTIFICATES (13/15/23): certificate.spi, 18 tests incl. distinguishing words for every state pair and forgery detection. TYPED + negatives (2, 20, 21, length): typed.spi, a typed core agreeing with derivatives up to length 6, plus 'fails Unification failure' negatives (a core one row short, a target past the last state). Still unverified from names alone: alphabet plumbing (d), HKT (d), typestate negatives, static_* twins (10), the x*.x* -> x* constructor (4), the 2 compiler probes (c). Progress 0 -> 50 as a conservative estimate. Next step: a full 71-row re-map against today's regex/src + lib regex_* (read-only), marking each ABSORBED/PARTIAL/MISSING with the file:test that proves it; then only the true gaps stay open.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_9 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 9u32, "2026-11-09T03:27Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:3x FULL RE-MAP (read-only subagent audit of all 71 items against regex 47dfc04 + lib regex_* at spiral bf5cc30a, each with file:line or test-name evidence): ABSORBED 38 / PARTIAL 12 / MISSING 2 / DROPPED-BY-DESIGN 19 (was 9/20/42/0 on 11-02). Concepts 21/5/2/4; negatives 11/7/0/13; probes 6/0/0/2. Absorbed in new forms: Vec/Fin via lib fin_vector; the alphabet as a class partition checked in certificate.spi; x*.x* -> x* via starred_twice (test two_equal_stars_in_a_row_collapse_to_one); the oracle triangle in laws.spi; typestate via automaton built|minimal|certified (table_of accepts only certified); Moore minimization + quotient and minimality certificates; Antimirov reconstruction + bound; lazy interned DFA; backtracking + ReDoS; the GADT probes as samples in apps/compiler/tmp/samples. DROPPED by design: alphabet-generic plumbing (code points make mixing impossible), HKT, sealed existentials (compile-time only), type-level Antimirov position trees, matcher profiles. MISSING (2): item 10 static_* twins/compile-time discharge and item 29 staged DFA (both owned by REGEX-STAGED-TABLES, P2 0%). TRUE GAPS, most valuable first: (1) a phase-skipping negative (one 'fails Unification failure' test, e.g. certified (Eager (eager_of r))), which closes 3 partial negatives, cheap; (2) closure-certificate completion: an order_re coherence law (antisymmetric + transitive over the depth-2 corpus; the lazy store's intern relies on it and nothing checks it) + forged-row tests for NotTotal / WrongTransition / DuplicateKey + a swapped-rows forgery; (3) a raw_inventory_bypass negative (loose char_set where normal is required), cheap; (4) generate the typed core from the certified DFA instead of hand-typing it (+ indexed row width, coverage/origin counts), expensive; (5) staged DFA + compile-time discharge; (6) the derivative universal witness; (7) use the 2^(positions+1) bound instead of the fixed 4096 cap; (8) C targets on the lazy/table/semantics/typed tests; (9) partition coverage padding. Decided limits, not gaps: a certified automaton is forgeable through its public constructor (REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE n4), and existentials are compile-time only. Progress 50 -> 80 ((38 + 19) of 71 settled). Next step: gaps (1) and (3), cheap negatives in regex/src, gated on a node.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_10 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 10u32, "2026-11-09T03:38Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:5x GAPS 1, 2 (order part) and 3 WRITTEN, proofs PENDING (unstaged, regex/src). Gap 1, certificate.spi: an_eager_automaton_cannot_skip_minimizing_on_its_way_to_a_certificate fails 'Unification failure' = certified (Eager (eager_of (ends_in_zero ()))): certified accepts only automaton minimal_phase; the positive twin certified (minimized (Eager ...)) already passes inside certified_of, so the failure can only come from the skipped phase. It closes raw_generic_state_seal / seal_unverified_derivative / derivative_skip_normalization. Gap 3, certificate.spi: a_loose_set_cannot_become_a_class_without_normalizing fails 'Unification failure' = Set (loose_of [...]) (Set needs char_set normal; of_ranges, the normalizing path, passes everywhere); this closes raw_inventory_bypass. Gap 2 (order part), laws.spi: order_coherent checks reflexive (order_re a a = Same), antisymmetric (order_re a b = flip of order_re b a) and transitive (a<b, b<c => a<c) over depth_one (60 regexes, 3,600 pairs, ~108k triple checks) on rust + gleam; it returns Coherent or the exact counterexample. The lazy store's binary-tree intern relies on that coherence and nothing checked it. Proofs queued on ganymede (pinned to 2): job-1794195164150-org2-regex-negatives (certificate.spi), then job-1794195492298-org2-regex-order-law (laws.spi). Still open from gap 2: forged-row tests for NotTotal / WrongTransition / DuplicateKey + a swapped-rows forgery.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_11 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 11u32, "2026-11-09T03:46Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:5x GAP 2 (forged rows) WRITTEN too, certificate.spi. 4 forgeries of the 2-row ends_in_zero eager DFA, each expected violation derived from check_dfa's order (per row: accepting flag, then width, then each column; duplicate keys only after all rows pass): (a) a_row_missing_a_column_is_named: drop the first target of every row -> NotTotal 0; (b) a_transition_to_the_wrong_state_is_named: every target -> state 0; column 0 (codes 0-47) truly goes to Dead -> WrongTransition (0, 0); (c) a_repeated_state_key_is_named: append state 0's key -> DuplicateKey (0, 2); (d) swapped_rows_are_caught_by_their_accepting_flags: row 0 carries the accepting flag of the state after reading '0' -> AcceptingMismatch 0. Helpers next to escape_row / flip_accepting: drop_first_target, shorter_row, start_only_row, swapped_rows (no name clashes in regex/src or lib regex_*). The ganymede mirror was re-synced while job-1794195164150-org2-regex-negatives was still pending, so that job gates certificate.spi with all 6 new tests (2 negatives + 4 forgeries); the laws.spi order law follows in job-1794195492298. With these, item 13's open tests are written; only the closure-budget wiring (item 12) and the expensive items (4-9) remain.")
inl note_of_regex_legacy_absorb_12 () = Note ("REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB", 12u32, "2026-11-09T05:26Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 01:4x SPLIT (the gate flagged 600 m, which never fits a round; this kit build has no edit --split verb, so children were filed by hand, each <= 120 m and taken from the 11-08 re-map's true gaps): REGEX-ABSORB-NEGATIVES 60 m (gaps 1-3, written, proofs pending), REGEX-ABSORB-TYPED-CORE 120 m (item 20 + cardinality negatives), REGEX-ABSORB-UNIVERSAL-WITNESS 90 m (item 9), REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET 60 m (item 12), REGEX-ABSORB-C-TARGETS 60 m (item 31), REGEX-ABSORB-PARTITION-COVERAGE 30 m (item 3 padding); the 2 MISSING concepts (10 static twins, 29 staged DFA) stay with the existing REGEX-STAGED-TABLES. deps now = the 6 children + REGEX-STAGED-TABLES; the parent's own estimate is 30 m (the closing rollup). Next step: the children; the parent closes when they and REGEX-STAGED-TABLES are Done or explicitly declined.")
