inl note_of_regex_bytes_utf8_1 () = Note ("REGEX-BYTES-UTF8", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:27Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x FILED from the share re-read (contradiction (a): M1 was parked behind GATE 1 in REGEX-AOT-TARGETS, but GATE 1 cannot be measured fairly without it). Source C (cccab1fd) §B.2 M1. DOD: byte equivalence classes (<= 256 classes per DFA) and \\pL, \\w, \\d, . compiled to UTF-8 byte automata; states <= 1.5x regex-automata's minimized DFA on 50 patterns; 0 divergences on 10^7 fuzz inputs vs the code-point engine and the regex crate; bench arms over &[u8]. CUT: blowup > 3x on \\w/\\pL -> adopt regex-automata's UTF-8 construction as the reference and continue. NEXT STEP: a byte-class table built from code-point classes for ASCII patterns, then the UTF-8 range splitter. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: phantom alphabet index (bytes vs code_points) on the table so a byte table never runs on code points.")
inl note_of_regex_bytes_utf8_2 () = Note ("REGEX-BYTES-UTF8", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 8 (verbatim): 8. NEW REGEX-BYTES-UTF8: byte alphabet and UTF-8 automata, before GATE 1 (M1). Byte equivalence classes as a [u8;256] map to class ids; \\pL, \\w, \\d and . compiled to UTF-8 byte automata. DoD: state count <= 1.5x regex-automata's minimized DFA on 50 patterns, and 0 divergences on 10^7 fuzz inputs. Cut: more than 3x on \\w/\\pL means adopting regex-automata's construction as the reference. Timebox 2 weeks. Source: C §B.2 M1. These criteria currently sit in REGEX-AOT-TARGETS (see contradiction a).")
inl regex_spans () = Task ("REGEX-SPANS", "regex unanchored search with spans: forward DFA for match ends, reverse DFA for starts, leftmost-longest then leftmost-first (M3), counts identical to rebar", Story, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "REGEX-BYTES-UTF8", "regex,automata,benchmark,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_spans () = Planning ("REGEX-SPANS", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_spans_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SPANS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x FILED from the share re-read (contradiction (a): M3 was parked behind GATE 1). Source C §B.1 \"Semântica\", §B.2 M3. DOD: unanchored search reporting (start, end) spans; leftmost-longest first, then leftmost-first via priority derivatives (Frisch-Cardelli greedy); counts identical to rebar on every selected count/count-spans/grep benchmark; CUT: if leftmost-first needs > 2 extra weeks, publish leftmost-longest with per-engine counts like RE#. NEXT STEP: a reverse-regex function (reverse of re) and the two-pass search over the table engine. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: match semantics as a union (LeftmostLongest | LeftmostFirst) selecting a prototype instance at compile time; span as a record of two nominal byte offsets.")
inl note_of_regex_spans_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SPANS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 9 (verbatim): 9. REGEX-REBAR (or NEW REGEX-SPANS): unanchored search (M3). A forward DFA finds the match end and a reverse DFA finds the start, as regex-automata does; count-spans and per-line grep are built on top. DoD: counts identical to rebar's. Timebox 3 weeks. Source: C §B.2 M3.")
inl regex_prefilter () = Task ("REGEX-PREFILTER", "regex prefilters (M5): memchr/memchr2/3, rare byte, literal sets (Teddy-style via memchr/aho-corasick in generated code) plus the prefilter-necessity certificate L <= S*.Lits.S*", Story, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "REGEX-SPANS", "regex,automata,benchmark,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_prefilter () = Planning ("REGEX-PREFILTER", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_prefilter_1 () = Note ("REGEX-PREFILTER", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x FILED from the share re-read (contradiction (a): M5 was parked behind GATE 1). Source C §B.2 M5, §A.1 #3 (\"I did not find this in any engine\"). DOD: literal extraction from re; prefilter arms chosen per pattern; a certificate that every match contains one of the literals, checked by inclusion L(r) <= L(S*.(lit1|...|litn).S*) through the product/inclusion machinery; geomean <= 1.5x rust/regex on the intersection and literals <= 1.2x; FREEZE if < 30% gain over the plain DFA. NEXT STEP: literal extraction + inclusion check as a Cells test, then a memchr arm. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a prefilter value is only constructible with its necessity certificate (certified_prefilter built by the checker).")
inl note_of_regex_prefilter_2 () = Note ("REGEX-PREFILTER", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 12 (verbatim): 12. NEW REGEX-PREFILTER: prefilters as their own item (M5), split out of AOT-TARGETS because M5 is GATE 1's 2-4x branch. memchr/memchr2/memchr3, rare byte, and a Teddy-style literal set via memchr/aho-corasick in the generated code; a necessity certificate L ⊆ Σ*·Lits·Σ*. DoD: geomean <= 1.5x rust/regex on the intersection, and the literal benchmarks <= 1.2x (both thresholds missing from the backlog today). Cut: freeze if the gain over M4 is under 30%. Timebox 2 weeks. Source: C §B.2 M5.")
