inl note_of_zeta_parity_anthropic_1 () = Note ("ZETA-PARITY-ANTHROPIC", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:13Z", "regex", "regex 08:1x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a68d3a7d7a786b1d7 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\zeta-report.md; external facts (Anthropic paper, OpenAI quasi-RH release, Liu arXiv 2610.12234) come from its web search and are UNVERIFIED here: re-read the primary sources before relying on a number. PAPER (per the agent; verify): ''More than two thirds of the zeros of the Riemann zeta function are simple and on the critical line'' (Claude, 2026-08-11; announcement anthropic.com/research/riemann-zeta; Lean repo github.com/anthropics/zeta-23-lean). Theorem A: N0s(T,2T) >= (2/3 - o(1)) N(T,2T) (previous 5/12) and Nd >= (5/6 - o(1)) N (previous 0.6603); Montgomery-Taylor window c_MT^-1 = 1/2 + (1/sqrt2) cot(1/sqrt2) giving 2 - c_MT^-1 = 0.67250... and (3 - c_MT^-1)/2 = 0.83625...; R(psi0) = 4/3; ceiling over bandwidth-one certificates ~0.682 (section 7.2); Theorem B for primitive Dirichlet L(s,chi); method: a d x d compression G~ of Weil''s explicit-formula Hermitian form over windows equispaced in [T,2T] plus the rank-trace inequality rank P1 >= 2 tr P1 + 4 tr Q'' - 4b - ||P1+Q''||^2_HS, inputs Lambda(n) sums, Stirling for Gamma''/Gamma, Montgomery-Vaughan; ''thousands of numerical checks against known zeta zeros''. DOD: the constants reproduced to 1e-12 and R(psi0) = 4/3; G~ built from computed zeros for windows in [T,2T] up to T = 10^4..10^6; tr G~/N -> 1, the decompositions and inequality (1.1) checked with N0s/N >= 2/3 observed; numeric check count >= the paper''s ''thousands''; a Theorem B check for at least one chi; the statement emitted through Spiral''s Lean backend and cross-referenced with anthropics/zeta-23-lean (a proof is OUT of scope: say so). NEXT STEP: fetch the paper PDF and the Lean repo (downloads are a standing OK), confirm every number above.")
inl note_of_zeta_parity_anthropic_2 () = Note ("ZETA-PARITY-ANTHROPIC", 2u32, "2026-11-07T13:42Z", "main", "main 11-07 PRIMARY SOURCE NOW LOCAL AND READ (recovery sweep, ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107). The user's work PC (work-hub) Downloads\\spiral-samples held the paper, its companion volume and the Lean repo; copied byte-exact (sha256 checked against work-hub) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\ZETA-PARITY-ANTHROPIC\\from-des073\\ (third-party, kept out of the public repo): zeta-two-thirds.pdf (631,785 B, sha256 6792988e...), zeta-transcript-explanation.pdf (1,058,230 B, 271aba2d..., Anthropic: How the two-thirds argument was found, two agent runs; its own caveat: the runs' math is unverified, the paper is not affected), zeta-23-lean-main.zip (1,557,537 B, 6bea7314..., github.com/anthropics/zeta-23-lean, lean-toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0-rc2, 329 .lean files, AUDIT.md, LICENSE, NOTICE). VERIFIED against the PDF (replaces the n1 UNVERIFIED web summary): title MORE THAN TWO THIRDS OF THE ZEROS OF THE RIEMANN ZETA FUNCTION LIE ON THE CRITICAL LINE, author Claude, dated 2026-08-10 (n1 said 08-11); Jarred Sumner posed and guided, Ralph Furman and Levent Alpoge took responsibility for communication. (1.3) H(lambda) = 2 - 1/lambda - lambda/3, H_d = (1+H)/2, F(lambda) = lambda/(1+lambda^2/3); H(1) = 2/3, H_d(1) = 5/6, F(1) = 3/4; H >= 0 iff lambda >= 3 - sqrt6 = 0.5505. Theorem A: N0*(T,2T) >= (H(lambda) - c loglogT/logT) N(T,2T), so liminf N0*/N >= 2/3 (distinct zeros on the line); Lean names two_thirds_on_critical_line (N0star), thmB0_mult (2/3 for NOsimple) and thmC0_mult (5/6 for Ndist), in Zeta23/Unconditional.lean and FinalMult.lean, Mathlib 51e6992efd06, tag v1.0, only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound. Optimized test family: 0.6725, 0.6725, 0.83625; c_MT = sqrt2 tan(1/sqrt2)/(1+(1/sqrt2)tan(1/sqrt2)). Prior records the paper cites: kappa > 5/12 (PRZZ20), distinct 0.6603 (Wu15). PARITY TARGETS from section 8 (numerical illustrations, not used in the proofs), ready to become test rows: (1) window I=[600,1200], X=95.5, d=436, Kaiser taper: C_prime=351.3 vs C_zero=351.4, N(I)=472, C/N=0.744 vs F(1)=0.750, all 436 eigenvalues positive (min 0.205); prime-side vs zero-side G within 1e-6..1.1e-8 using the first 2000-3700 zeros; (2) the R_S table, e.g. [9000,10000] lambda=1: L=7.32, X=1510, d=1162, C/N=0.766, cert +0.50; [998000,10^6] lambda=1: C/N=0.757; (3) T=2000, I=[2000,4000], 3700 zeros, N(I)=1957: C_pred 1436.03 vs C_zero 1436.41 (lambda=1, eta=0.05), agreement 3e-4; (6) rank-trace certificate from 10^5 zeros at T=1000: +0.49 N(I) (lambda=1, eta=0.1), ||A||_F^2/tr A = 1.387 vs 4/3. DoD addition: reproduce these rows within their printed digits from ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE zeros. NEXT STEP unchanged (after ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE); the Lean repo is the statement reference, the PDF section 8 the numeric one.")
