inl note_of_zeta_mega_retire_4 () = Note ("ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-11-10T11:23Z", "org3", "org3 ROLE-REPLACEMENT + DELETION-PRECONDITION (KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS org3 part; org2 mega-sample split). mega_zeta_structural_laboratory, VERIFIED on disk 11-10:\nMIGRATED (with test cells): NONE yet. No lib/spiral/zeta exists (verified: find lib -iname *zeta* empty; no \"zeta\" in lib/spiral/*.spi). The absorption items ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE + ZETA-TYPED-ARITH are both 0%. The other source is polyglot's lib/math (local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot; polyglot left the org 11-03, so that copy is DELETED after a check per the 11-03 rule, not archived). So zeta is the OPPOSITE of brzozowski: brzozowski's engine is already in lib, zeta's is not started.\nLEFT (as items): ZETA-TYPED-ARITH, ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE (the deps), ZETA-FINAL (absorb the mega sample + polyglot lib/math into lib/spiral/zeta).\nDELETION PRECONDITION: 58 matrix.psd1 rows (verified count); 39 zeta ExpectedErrors pins must move to the lib zeta package rows (compiler canary); family files = main.spi/fsx/zig, package.spiproj, all_terminals + the many negative_* subdirs; CONSUMERS (verified) = apps/compiler/tmp/tests/matrix.psd1 + apps/compiler/scripts/bench-native.ps1. Gate = lib/spiral/zeta absorbs (ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE + ZETA-TYPED-ARITH done) AND the 39 ExpectedErrors relocated AND canary kept AND user go. Archive (never delete).\nROLE-REPLACEMENT per compiler's template (SAME constraint as brzozowski: compiler's SPS/CIC decision keeps native coverage on \"brzozowski/omniledger/ZETA runtime rows\", so zeta is also currently-retained native coverage and cannot drop runtime rows until relocated): (1) compile entry -> the lib zeta package ONCE IT EXISTS; (2) runtime_native/all_terminals/Backends rows -> KEEP until lib zeta + a bench home exist; (3) bench-native.ps1 zeta runtime dir -> BACKEND-BENCH-CI; (4) canary: keep one per this item's DoD + the 39 ExpectedErrors in lib zeta. Next step (org3/math lane): zeta is BLOCKED on ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE/ZETA-TYPED-ARITH -- no archive is possible until the lib absorption even starts, unlike brzozowski which only needs REGEX-PUBLISH + absorb-completion. This is the long pole of the 5-mega deletion.")
