inl note_of_x_dumps_spiral_rewrite_1 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-SPIRAL-REWRITE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:16Z", "x-dumps", "Groomed 11-02 from the user directives relayed by resilience: (1) rewrite the entire x-dumps project in Spiral, (2) move it to the x repo as another generic project, (3) START ONLY AFTER the test accounts are fully downloaded. Gate = X-DUMPS dep; at 11-02 08:1x juhondacivic is in media (3,800/5,322) and geygey_hadid is at ~7,500/62,770 snaps per shard (~1.5 d). Plan: M1 model unit (record/kind/identity/tombstone GADTs + codecs for the existing ndjson shapes, round-trip tests on real lines); M2 boundary (HTTP + sha256 cache, per-host rate/backoff, fs, clock: one-expression primitives); M3 harvest feature (cdx/snaps/live/context/media + api_v2/HTML parse); M4 history feature (identity, timeline, merge, summary, md/html render; split render if past 1000 generated lines); M5 bin (run lanes + finisher) + spiral.toml packages per the x README; M6 replay acceptance: cache-only run on a frozen copy, diff every output byte-for-byte against the Rust outputs; M7 iggy events + k3s render, swap the europa pod, archive the Rust crate. x repo conventions: spiral.toml edition 3, one Rust crate per entry under apps/archive/<crate>, scripts/build.ps1 names the app.")
inl note_of_x_dumps_spiral_rewrite_2 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-SPIRAL-REWRITE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:25Z", "x-dumps", "Concrete unit->module map (execution-readiness grooming, from the current Rust source): UNIT xarchive_model (model): record-kind union (tweet/reply/quote/retweet/lost/mention), Capture (cdx.rs), Person + account identity/holder rules (merge.rs), tombstone; codecs for each ndjson shape (wayback, live, context, timeline) as round-trippable GADTs. UNIT xarchive_boundary (boundary, only host code): fetch.rs whole (Client/Opts/Cache/Fetched, sha256 http cache, per-host rate halving + backoff, write_atomic) + every scattered std::fs read/write pulled in as named one-expression primitives + clock + the iggy HTTP codec from events.rs. UNIT xarchive_harvest (feature): cdx.rs (CDX crawl, captures_by_id, candidates, clear_stale_shards, wayback_lines, tweet_ids), snaps.rs, live.rs (profile/live/context), media.rs, parse.rs (api_v2 + HTML extract). UNIT xarchive_history (feature): timeline.rs (md/html/ndjson render) + merge.rs (Person grouping, absorb, summary_of); split render into its own unit if generated Rust >1000 lines (timeline.rs is the big one at 17.5KB source). UNIT xarchive (bin): main.rs arg parse + run orchestration (archive lanes + X lane + finisher, sharding via --shards/--set) + archive/merge/follow commands + the iggy event routing (producer/follow) over the boundary codec. Gate still: start only after all 5 test accounts finish + TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 ready.")
inl note_of_x_dumps_spiral_rewrite_3 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-SPIRAL-REWRITE", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:57Z", "x-dumps", "dod: xarchive reimplemented as a generic Spiral x app that passes every test account end-to-end. next: start gated only after every test account passes; begin by porting the cdx+profile stages.")
inl cic_app_scaffold () = Task ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", "spiral/apps/kernel scaffold: src/package.spiproj (packageDir ../../../lib), build.ps1 cloned from regex, wired into spiral scripts/workflow.ps1, Cells gate total line in CI on both OSes", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "-", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_app_scaffold () = Planning ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl cic_syntax () = Task ("CIC-SYNTAX", "kernel syntax: name nominal, level union (Zero/Succ/Max/IMax/Param), term union (Sort/BVar/FVar/Const/App/Lam/Pi/Let), binder info, structural equality via prototype, size/hash", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_syntax () = Planning ("CIC-SYNTAX", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl cic_scope () = Task ("CIC-SCOPE", "kernel scope: locally nameless open/close/instantiate/abstract under the loose|closed phantom, lift/lower, with round-trip laws", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "CIC-SYNTAX", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_scope () = Planning ("CIC-SCOPE", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl cells_port_targets () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", "Cells in Spiral C5: targets.ex (859), builders.ex (486) and toolchain.ex (173), 1,518 Elixir lines, become typed Spiral over the existing targets.spi. The target -> builder map is a GADT 'target b' indexed by builder, and the tool table is one record per tool, so no string tool names. DELPHI-TO-PASCAL step 3 renames ride along (PascalTarget, delphi_compiler/run_delphi). Oracle: builders_test, targets_test, targets_test_name_test and notebook_targets_test pass unchanged", Story, P1, D5, 55u32, Paused, "CELLS-HTML-PARITY", "team:microblog,cells,cells-in-spiral,typefeatureset,beam", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_port_targets () = Planning ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:19 x: added by the Cells groom. The Elixir line counts come from the live tree census at 2026-11-02 08:19 (44 .ex files, 11,380 lines in all).")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. From compiler n2: Cells test targets are a closed list (rust fsharp typescript python cuda cpp gleam lua c delphi pascal zig lean wgsl, no wasm), and one bad ///> name aborts the WHOLE file's tests. The port's target b GADT makes the list a closed typed union. An unknown name becomes a typed per-block error row (\"unknown target X; known: ...\"), never a file-wide abort. Oracle addition: a file with one bad ///> line still runs its other blocks.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T21:39Z", "x", "2026-11-02 17:39 x: SCOPED a pure slice for later: present/2 with output_field, trace_text, result_map(_line), decode_result, shown_output, command_result and json_map (about 90 lines, output text to shown text; typed as a closed union Field | Trace | Empty | Raw), plus strip_gleam_warnings. BLOCKER: it decodes arbitrary JSON lines (command_result may be a string or an object). lib json's decode is a typed reflection decode into a known record, so it doesn't fit. Erlang json:decode via erlang_term would match Elixir's JSON (the same OTP module) exactly, but it raises on invalid input, and the Gleam boundary has no try/catch yet. NEEDS a lib erlang_json with a typed result (Ok of a dynamic json value | Error) built on a rescue wrapper, then this slice is a corpus parity port.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T21:56Z", "x", "2026-11-02 17:56 x: SAFE-JSON ENABLER drafted (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-JSON-VALUE). Rule (decided by the rule, no question for the user): a primitive goes to lib when lib can run it on the consumer's backend. Here it can't: lib json_schema's json_value reader is lenient, and xml::code_point_width has no Gleam arm. So the strict parser lives in Cells spi as json_value.spi, using text:: byte ops: a recursive union json (JNull | JBool | JNum raw text | JStr | JArr | JObj member list); a total parse : string -> option json (RFC 8259: no raw controls, only the JSON escapes, paired surrogates, well-formed UTF-8, no trailing commas or leading zeros); field lookups where the first member wins (matching JSON.decode, probed: {a:1,a:2} -> 1); and a compact canonical text. Export json_canonical. Oracle, PRE-REGISTERED for x-cells-json1: json_value.spi blocks 1/1; 'json value parity: F files, N texts compared (A accepted), 0 differ' with F > 20 and 20 < A < N, over every tracked .json up to 256 KB plus 7 malformed variants of each and 52 edge cases; acceptance and the decoded value both match JSON.decode; mix 0 failures. Promotion: when lib sm' gets a portable byte_at with a Gleam arm, move json into lib (one type, unifying json_schema's json_value) and delete the Cells copy.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_5 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 5u32, "2026-11-02T22:05Z", "x", "2026-11-02 18:05 x: PRESENT SLICE phase A drafted in the same store folder, and proven in the same job (x-cells-json1, one package compile for both). apps/cells/spi/builder_output.spi opens json_value. It reproduces targets.ex's present/failure_trace chain: a Unicode White_Space utrim, matching String.trim (probed: 9-D 20 85 A0 1680 2000-200A 2028 2029 202F 205F 3000); result maps, whole or as the line's trailing {...}, matching the regex (\\{.*\\})\\s*$ with an ASCII-only \\s, probed; \\r?\\n lines; ANSI SGR stripping; command_result's output first. Exports builder_present and builder_failure_trace ('' for nil). ADDED PRE-REGISTERED RULE: builder_output.spi blocks 1/1; 'builder output parity: N texts compared (D distinct shown), 0 present differ, 0 failure traces differ' with N > 1500, against a verbatim copy of the Elixir chain over 10x17x9 synthetic outputs plus every tracked .json up to 64 KB in 3 framings; mix 0 failures. Phase B (after the land): targets.ex present/failure_trace delegate, and output_field, trace_text, result_map, result_map_line, decode_result, result?, shown_output, command_result and json_map are deleted.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_6 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 6u32, "2026-11-02T22:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 18:24 x: x-cells-mdjson1 (json, builder and markdown in one job), NOT GREEN by its rule. (1) JSON: 0 differ over 142 texts (29 accepted), but only 13 tracked .json exist across spiral, dice and alphabet, so the pre-registered F > 20 was unreachable. AMENDED RULE, set before the rerun (reason: the tracked-json floor can't be met): docs = 13 tracked .json plus JSON documents encoded from up to 300 tracked .spi files in 3 framings (compact JSON.encode!, :json.format pretty, and an ASCII \\\\uXXXX-escaped form with surrogate pairs for astral characters); each doc gets 7 malformed variants, plus the edge list; pass = 0 differ with files > 10, docs > 300 and 20 < accepted < texts. (2) BUILDER: parity 1569 texts, 119 distinct shown, 0 present differ, 0 failure traces differ, but builder_output.spi's own block failed 0/1. The Elixir oracle agrees with all 6 block expectations (checked locally), so it's a Spiral literal or harness issue, not the port. The rerun prints the block's raw tail. Rerun: x-cells-mdjson2.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_7 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 7u32, "2026-11-02T23:06Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:06 x: PHASE A LANDED (unstaged, tree-write window win-1793660548148): apps/cells/spi json_value.spi 0AFA4C77E400, builder_output.spi D66085FF75B9, html_markdown.spi 372121A33A3C; main.spi 61F876646A00 (exports markdown_html, json_canonical, builder_present, builder_failure_trace); package.spiproj 4861747CF1C9; domain.ex B4670B18B36C; plus 3 parity tests. PROOF x-cells-mdjson3 (core 8960CAB701FEF46E): blocks 3/3; json 6442 texts (13 files + 900 encoded docs, 929 accepted) 0 differ; builder 1569 texts 0/0 differ; markdown 111 texts 0 differ; mix 10 passed. PHASE B PRE-REGISTERED (x-cells-pb1, A/B on one mirror, drafts kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-PHASE-B-MD-PRESENT): targets.ex 859 -> 760 (present and failure_trace delegate; 9 helpers deleted); html.ex 231 -> 181 (Html.markdown delegates). Tests: html_test, html_markdown_parity_test, targets_test, targets_test_name_test, notebook_report_test, builder_output_parity_test. Pass = A base and B draft both exit 0 with equal passed counts and 0 failures, and the same domain hash in A and B (no Spiral change).")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_8 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 8u32, "2026-11-02T23:50Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:50 x: BUILDERS PARSE phase A drafted (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-BUILDERS-PARSE, combined with M3.3 into one job, x-cells-bm1). apps/cells/spi/builders.spi models the ///> header as types: tool (13 cases), tool_choice (SkipTool | Tool), field, flag_kind (TakesOptional | TakesOne | TakesDeps | TakesCleanup), inline (Bare | Inline), dep_version (NoVersion | AnyVersion | Version), and records dep, builder_values and builder. Errors are a result string carrying the exact ArgumentError text. Elixir's inspect is reproduced from a full code-point sweep: the <<bytes>> form for C0 except \\\\a-\\\\r and \\\\e, C1, U+FFFE/FFFF and invalid UTF-8; \\\\uXXXX for A0 34F 61C 2000-200F 2028-202E 205F-2064 2066-2069 FEFF FFF9-FFFC; named escapes; \\\\#{. Graphemes (tokenizer, short clusters, unquote slices) go through Gleam string.pop_grapheme/length/slice, matching String.graphemes. The wire is length-prefixed fields; Builders.split_spiral decodes it next to the old split. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-cells-bm1): builders.spi blocks 1/1 and manifest.spi 3/3; 'builders parity: F files, H headers, N texts compared (E errors), 0 differ' with F > 500, H > 50 and 100 < E < N (tracked .spi files, every ///> line alone, and a 20-tool x 54-argument grid plus extras); the M3.3 rule as registered on CELLS-MANIFEST-SOURCEMAP-SPIRAL; builders_test, crates_section_test, manifest_test and notebook_report_test 0 failures.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_9 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 9u32, "2026-11-02T23:53Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:53 x: x-cells-pb1 base (A, unmodified tree) came back 67/68. Failing: 'a Gleam cell runs from the notebook's directory, so relative fixture paths resolve' (TargetsTest), an environment failure on the mirror that exists without any draft. RULE AMENDMENT, recorded before B's result is known (B was applied 19:40 and is still running): the pre-registered '0 failures' can't hold when the base itself fails. Pass = B's passed count equals A's (67) and B's failing set is exactly A's (that one test), and nothing else differs. That test is still not evidence for the port either way; the present/failure_trace coverage comes from the command_result, trace, empty-output and plain-text tests, plus the 1569-text parity. If B fails anything else, phase B is red.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_10 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 10u32, "2026-11-03T00:12Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:12 x: PRESENT SLICE phase B LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793664081831): targets.ex 859 -> 760 (B3BC3F2315BA; present and failure_trace delegate to Domain.builder_present/builder_failure_trace; output_field, trace_text, result_map, result_map_line, decode_result, result?, shown_output, command_result, json_map and failure? deleted). PROOF x-cells-pb1, judged by the n9 amendment: A base 67/68 and B draft 67/68 with the same single environment failure (the Gleam fixture-path test) and the same domain 1E1A12F94F30. Retired parity test builder_output_parity_test.exs archived to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261102-200215-cells-retired-parity-tests and removed (unstaged). json_value_parity_test stays as the permanent oracle against JSON.decode. NEXT: x-cells-bm1 (builders parse phase A plus M3.3) is launched.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_11 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 11u32, "2026-11-03T00:33Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:33 x: BUILDERS phase B drafted (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-BUILDERS-B): builders.ex 486 -> 198 lines. The old split, take_line, parse_command!, parse_args/tokens/long/short/cluster, apply_flag, short_kind!, consuming?, cluster_inline, flag_token?, parse_bool, tokenize, join, flags and the @tools/@expected/@*_flags tables are deleted; split_spiral becomes split. parse_dep, unquote_value and quoted? stay for with_crates. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-cells-bb1, A/B on one mirror after bm2 lands): tests builders_test, crates_section_test, directives_test and notebook_targets_test; pass = A base and B draft exit 0 with equal passed counts and the same domain hash (no Spiral change). builders_parity_test.exs is archived at the phase B land (it calls the removed split_spiral) and left out of the suite.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_12 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 12u32, "2026-11-03T00:42Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:42 x: x-cells-bm2 verdict. M3.3 GREEN by its rule (manifest.spi blocks 3/3; manifest declares parity 3914 texts, 12 declare modules, 0 differ; manifest_test and notebook_report_test passed). BUILDERS NOT GREEN by its rule: blocks 1/1 and parity 0 differ over 2612 texts (1479 files, 952 errors), but the pre-registered H > 50 failed: there are only 44 distinct ///> lines across all tracked .spi. I don't lower a floor after seeing the data and call that run green. Instead x-cells-bm3 adds independent evidence: every pair of the 54 arguments under rust, gleam, py and ts (11,664 two-argument headers, exercising flag interplay, consumption and clusters across tokens). RULE for bm3, set before it runs: 0 differ, with files > 500, H > 40 (the real corpus, measured), pairs > 10000 and errors between 1000 and N; plus the M3.3 rule again. Both slices land together, since they share main.spi and domain.ex.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_13 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 13u32, "2026-11-03T01:05Z", "x", "2026-11-02 21:04 x: GLEAM PROJECT slice drafted (phase A in kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-GLEAM-PROJECT, layered on the bm drafts; phase B in \\CELLS-GLEAM-PROJECT-B: targets.ex 760 -> 723, gleam_manifest and strip_gleam_warnings delegate, @gleam_deps and gleam_warning_line? move to Spiral). apps/cells/spi/gleam_project.spi: strip_warnings (warning blocks, gutters, Hint and box lines) and manifest (the fixed 7-dependency set plus the cell's own deps, versions cleaned of backslashes and outer quotes, values rendered with builders::inspect); the wire in is length-prefixed fields; Path.basename stays in Elixir. PRE-REGISTERED RULE, phase A (x-cells-gp1): gleam_project.spi blocks 1/1; 'gleam project parity: M manifests (S dep sets), O outputs compared, 0 manifests differ, 0 outputs differ' with M > 500 and O > 5000 (deps of every tracked gleam ///> header, a name x version grid, 4 paths x 3 targets, and every 3-line combination of 14 warning-shaped lines, LF and CRLF), against the public Targets functions. Phase B (x-cells-gp2, A/B): targets_test.exs at lines 282, 292, 302, 321 and 349 (the gleam manifest, lock, warm-package and warning tests); pass = equal passed counts in A and B, and B's failing set equal to A's.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_14 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 14u32, "2026-11-03T01:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 21:08 x: BUILDERS PARSE phase A LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793668036743): spi/builders.spi 996D20CFA669, main.spi E95191D7E9F0, package.spiproj 4AF4499F6246, domain.ex B150D47B7D6B, builders.ex 29A693A8AB65 (split_spiral plus the wire decoder next to the old split), builders_parity_test.exs EDC06C76E61B. PROOF x-cells-bm3, green on every pre-registered condition: blocks 1/1; builders parity 14276 texts (1479 files, 44 headers, 11664 argument pairs; 11566 errors, so ArgumentError text matched byte for byte), 0 differ; Result 47 passed. NEXT: x-cells-gp1 (gleam project phase A) is launched; then bb1 (builders phase B).")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_15 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 15u32, "2026-11-03T01:31Z", "x", "2026-11-02 21:31 x: bb1 and gp phase B MERGED into one A/B job, x-cells-pbb1, after gp2 lands (both are Elixir-only changes on disjoint files, so one sync and one compile cover both; drafts in kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-PHASE-B-BUILDERS-GLEAM). Tests: builders_test, crates_section_test, directives_test, notebook_targets_test, plus targets_test.exs:282:292:302:321:349. Pass = the two pre-registered rules together: equal passed counts in A and B, B's failing set equal to A's, and the same domain hash in A and B. builders_parity_test.exs is archived at that land.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_16 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 16u32, "2026-11-03T01:40Z", "x", "2026-11-02 21:40 x: GLEAM PROJECT phase A LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793669945955): spi/gleam_project.spi DCA06993EEB2, main.spi F41C223DEA9A, package.spiproj 8E3379568FE5, domain.ex 4D13304B9F3A, gleam_project_parity_test.exs 647A63DAA7FC. PROOF x-cells-gp2, green on every pre-registered condition: blocks 1/1; parity 3624 manifests (302 dep sets: deps of every tracked gleam ///> header plus a name x version grid, over 4 paths and 3 targets) and 5488 outputs (every 3-line combination of 14 warning-shaped lines, LF and CRLF), 0 differ against the public Targets functions. gp1 failed honestly first: an unannotated lambda parameter read d::name, so it was inferred as a function (now a memory). The merged phase B, x-cells-pbb1, is launched.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_17 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 17u32, "2026-11-03T01:44Z", "x", "2026-11-02 21:44 x: BUILDERS DEPS drafted (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-BUILDERS-DEPS, layered on the merged phase B). builders.spi gains deps_wire (each crate token through the landed dep_of and dep_text), exported as builder_deps. with_crates declares crates through it, and parse_dep, unquote_value and quoted? leave builders.ex (198 -> 174). PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-cells-bd1, after x-cells-pbb1 lands): builders.spi blocks 1/1; 'builders deps parity: B builder sets, R real dep tokens, N cases compared, 0 differ' with B > 20 and N > 1000 (every tracked file's builders x single crates from 16 synthetic and all real dep tokens, plus both lists whole), against a verbatim copy of the old parse_dep chain; crates_section_test and builders_test 0 failures.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_18 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 18u32, "2026-11-03T01:58Z", "x", "2026-11-02 21:58 x: MERGED PHASE B LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793671097611): builders.ex 486 -> 198 (0A967A6EFAD5; the Elixir ///> parser, tokenizer and flag tables are gone, and split decodes the Spiral wire) and targets.ex 760 -> 723 (EF5A8DA0979D; gleam_manifest and strip_gleam_warnings delegate, and @gleam_deps and gleam_warning_line? are gone). PROOF x-cells-pbb1: A base 30 passed (19 excluded by the targets_test line filter) = B draft 30 passed, domain 0B663C971A83 in both. builders_parity_test.exs is retired (it called the removed split_spiral), archived to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261102-215819-cells-builders-parity-test and removed (unstaged). x-cells-bd1 (builders deps) is launched.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_19 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 19u32, "2026-11-03T02:00Z", "x", "2026-11-02 22:00 x: TARGETS HOST drafted (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-TARGETS-HOST, layered on bd1). targets.spi gains a closed host union (FsiHost | PythonHost | LuaHost | JavascriptHost | PowershellHost) with host_of, host_name, host_file_extension and is_cl (repeated .exe suffixes trimmed, as String.trim_trailing does). targets.ex 723 -> 709: host_key's language table, host_extension's clauses and cl? delegate; Path.basename stays Elixir. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-cells-th1, after bd1 lands): 'targets host parity: C cells, 5 hosts, P paths, 0 differ' against verbatim copies of the old host_key, host_extension and cl? (26 language spellings including case, spaces, Unicode and dotted-I, 14 compiler paths); mix 0 failures.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_20 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 20u32, "2026-11-03T02:09Z", "x", "2026-11-02 22:09 x: compiler's CELLS-TYPED-TARGETS edits read and kept (peer heads-up). targets.spi C9FF077924D0 (21:55: target_of returns option target, no UnknownTarget) is the exact base of the x-cells-th1 draft, and its land guard pins that hash. notebook.ex CAC37061E0E0 (21:39: with_builders rescues an unknown backend as :builder_error) and notebook_targets_test.exs 2ABBFF79E520 aren't touched by any x draft, and x-cells-pbb1 ran with them in both A and B. PascalTarget is noted as x's to add, as part of this item's builder/target model. builders.spi's ForDelphi already maps 'delphi' and 'pascal', so a target-side Pascal case would sit next to DelphiTarget.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_21 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 21u32, "2026-11-03T02:11Z", "x", "2026-11-02 22:11 x: BUILDERS DEPS LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793671833275): builders.spi 1F8F9D626538 (deps_wire), main.spi C28B5A8CF738 (builder_deps), domain.ex 77B26ECBA062, builders.ex 486 -> 174 tonight in all (E40498F38AAC; with_crates declares crates through Spiral, and parse_dep, unquote_value and quoted? are gone), builders_deps_parity_test.exs D1038D158BA0. PROOF x-cells-bd1: blocks 1/1; parity 3320 cases (79 builder sets, 21 real dep tokens), 0 differ against the old parse_dep chain; Result 9 passed. builders.ex now holds only dispatch, argv and the wire decoder.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_22 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 22u32, "2026-11-03T04:36Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:36 x: TARGETS HOST LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793680554553): targets.spi 7B98288DC0CC (host union FsiHost | PythonHost | LuaHost | JavascriptHost | PowershellHost, host_of, host_name, host_file_extension, is_cl), main.spi AE2FCBD33CDF, domain.ex BBBCE6E60BB1, targets.ex 723 -> 709 (0B9585081D64; host_key's table, host_extension and cl? delegate), targets_host_parity_test.exs EA65F6E5F56A. PROOF x-cells-th1 on core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF: 'targets host parity: 29 cells, 5 hosts, 14 paths, 0 differ', Result 8 passed. targets.ex went 859 -> 709 tonight; what's left there is process running, toolchain lookup and IO.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_23 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 23u32, "2026-11-03T04:37Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:37 x: NEXT STEPS, groomed from the tree after tonight's 8 lands. DONE in Spiral: builder output presenter, ///> parser (the builders model plus Elixir inspect), deps wire, gleam manifest and warning filter, host languages and the cl check. LEFT, by value: (1) targets.ex process running (run_program, run_status, normalize, budget, timeout_error, format_ms): typed with a run_outcome union over lib erlang_port once process exits are typed there (LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB); (2) toolchain.ex (173): env and path lookup, which waits for a typed lib env/path module, so do it with C8's mounts; (3) PascalTarget (compiler's 22:3x heads-up): add it when a distinct Pascal builder exists (today 'pascal' maps to Delphi in builders.spi); (4) builders.ex's wire decoder and dispatch/argv stay at the Elixir boundary until LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS lets Gleam records cross. Each next slice keeps tonight's pattern: phase A with a corpus parity test against the live Elixir, then an A/B phase B, every rule pre-registered, and land scripts with base hashes recorded at draft time.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_24 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 24u32, "2026-11-03T15:32Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:32 x: groom: step (1)'s blocker is now DRAFTED in lib (LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB note, erlang_port run_collect -> run_outcome Finished | TimedOut), gated in x-cells-mpath1. Once it lands, targets.ex run_program/run_status/normalize become a typed slice over run_outcome, and format_ms plus the timeout message (3 lines of pure text) ride along in the same slice rather than costing their own node run. Steps (2)-(4) still wait as listed in the last note.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_25 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 25u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:13 x: GROOM (user 11-04 00:1x via main). Active -> Planned (WIP cap). Step (1) waits on LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB's run_collect landing, which is gated in the queued node run x-cells-mpath1 (launcher ready). Resume when that lands.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_26 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 26u32, "2026-11-04T04:21Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:21 x: back to Active at 55 under the user's 11-04 00:2x rule (Active = a note within 48 h, relayed by kit). My 11-04 groom parked it under the old 12 h cap; its last real note is under 48 h old, so the parking is undone. Next step unchanged.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_27 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 27u32, "2026-11-05T10:45Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:45 x (Cells owner): compiler's DELPHI-TO-PASCAL Cells rename LANDED (cells window, 58 passed, undo cells-20261105-064025): DelphiTarget -> PascalTarget, ForDelphi -> ForPascal, console.spi arms, targets.ex pascal_compiler/run_pascal (fpc keeps -Mdelphi), builders.ex :pascal; '///> delphi' still accepted as an alias (test). This port's targets.spi/builders.spi now carry the Pascal names.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_28 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 28u32, "2026-11-05T13:39Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:5x x: RE-GROOM of n-next (11-03 00:37) against today's tree. (3) PascalTarget: DONE by compiler's DELPHI-TO-PASCAL Cells rename (06:40 land). (1) targets.ex process running: its dependency LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB is Done, but a slice now would mostly move format strings. run_program, run_status and normalize decide on Elixir exception structs (ProcessError reason :not_found -> :tool_missing, TimeoutError) and on Runner.run's {:ok, %{exit_status, output}} | {:error, {:timeout, info}} maps, so the typed part would be the message texts (timed out after <budget_text>, failed (exit N), was not found [at path], could not start) while every decision stays in Elixir. Each Cells land costs a full suite run on the node. DECISION: (1) moves when the runner itself does, i.e. with C8's runner.ex port (CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS) over lib erlang_port: a run_outcome union (Ran exit output | TimedOut budget | NotFound | CouldNotStart reason) with budget as Unbounded | Within ms, decided in Spiral at the port boundary, then the messages come along. Not before. (2) toolchain.ex: unchanged, waits on a typed env/path lib module (none exists). (4) builders.ex wire/dispatch: waits on LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS (compiler, Blocked 85%). So this item's next step is the C8 runner port; progress stays 55.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_29 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 29u32, "2026-11-06T08:19Z", "x", "2026-11-06 04:1x x: groom: Active -> Paused (untouched 19 h). (3) PascalTarget is done (compiler, 11-05 06:40). Next step: (1) a targets.ex process-running slice on LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB (Done). Medium load; it needs a cells_land_window -ProvenLog close on the node. Resume when CELLS-HTML-PARITY clears the node queue.")
