inl note_of_cells_port_memo_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 2u32, "2026-11-02T20:17Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:17 x: C6.1 LANDED (unstaged), the FIRST ELIXIR REMOVED by CELLS-IN-SPIRAL. Memo's reach analysis (strip_line_comment, the identifier scan, block_shape for all four header regexes, the unreached-definition graph walk, and the row drop) is now apps/cells/spi/memo.spi (AAAF5ECD43DA, exported as reached_program). Memo.reached_program delegates to it; the Elixir reached_program body, unreached_definitions and reach_blocks are deleted (memo.ex 642 -> 603). PROOFS on pack17: x-cells-c6a2, the corpus PARITY ORACLE: 134 tracked .spi files (lib plus every app's spi) compared between the Elixir and Spiral reached_program, 0 differ, mix 51 passed, memo.spi blocks 4/4. x-cells-c6c1 (the switch, A/B): memo, memo_deps, notebook and document tests 63 -> 63. The parity test then retired (archive 20261102-161639): after the switch it would compare Spiral with itself. Earlier runs failed honestly first: c6a1 had listm::exists missing from core, and c6b1 used the keyword 'instance' as a record field (memory spiral-keywords-not-identifiers). LEFT in memo.ex: the package-print side (package_index, shaped_blocks/block_shape/references for package prints) and the IO (key, fetch, store, prune, stamps) for later C6 slices. Cells lib Elixir now totals 11344 lines (census was 11,380).")
inl note_of_cells_port_memo_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 3u32, "2026-11-02T20:17Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:17 x: ORDERING for the rest of C6, read from memo.ex: the package-print side (package_prints, package_index, compiled_blocks, package_print_for, reached_package_print, reach_package_blocks, resolve_references, with_stable_ids) reads manifests (Spiral.Cells.Manifest, i.e. M3 CELLS-MANIFEST-SOURCEMAP-SPIRAL) and mount dependencies (Spiral.Cells.Mounts, i.e. C8 CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS) and builds the term that key/3 hashes. So it ports after M3 and C8. Its oracle changes too: keys hash an Elixir term today, so a Spiral canonical print changes every key once by design. The proof is behavioral (memo_test and memo_deps_test: an unreached edit keeps the key, a reached edit changes it), not byte-equal keys.")
inl note_of_cells_port_memo_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:28 x: groom (WIP cap: Active means touched within 12 h): Active -> Paused at 25%. Not touched since yesterday, because today's node time goes to Cells-on-html, the sim-erlang slice, the iggy probe and the real-profile replay (four x jobs queued serially). RESUME CONDITION: x's node queue drains (x-events2, x-replay1, x-cells-mpath1, x-html-gleam6 done) or CELLS-HTML-PARITY lands its Cells half; its next step stays n-last (the package-print side first: package_prints, package_index, compiled_blocks).")
