inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:19 x: added by the Cells groom. The Elixir line counts come from the live tree census at 2026-11-02 08:19 (44 .ex files, 11,380 lines in all).")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:58Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:58 x: MODEL RULE (groom): linked-unit exports must be monomorphic (LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE). request r stays inside cells_model, and cells_boundary exports one concrete function per reply type or an existential. Processes use GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT's concurrency interface where it exists; otherwise otp_actor sits only in cells_boundary. The message GADT is defined once so IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE can reuse it. Oracle addition: the typefeatureset census never goes down (CELLS-TYPED-UNITS n1 baseline).")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T16:34Z", "x", "2026-11-02 12:34 x: SLICE PLAN, revised from the code. Domain exports to Elixir are string -> string with unions flattened to text, so C7a's protocol parsing can't move out through another string export (that would ADD encoded wire). Instead the client itself moves into Spiral over a typed socket boundary.\nC7a.1 (proving now on node xcells1, x-cells-c7a1): apps/cells/spi/client.spi, with one generic transact : port -> stamp -> request r -> result r client_failure. The GADT makes Hello, Status, Pool and Compile share one exchange, with the reply type fixed by the request. client_failure = Unreachable : string | Stale | WaitedOut | Lost : string, mirroring compiler_client.ex's error shapes. The test blocks run a fake daemon on a spawned BEAM process. daemon.spi's compile_of/failed_of now match the Elixir edge cases (exactly 1-2 fields after ok; a sole numeric queue after timeout; a bare 'error' is unexpected; the message after the queue keeps its tabs). Both ride in the drafts store (CELLS-IN-SPIRAL-C7A), since live Cells is shared.\nC7a.2 DONE: lib erlang_tcp.spi LANDED 12:24 (AD74CCCA5A8C; package.spiproj 9A65F56D4191). It provides the typed socket boundary (connect_local/send_line/receive_line/close/listen_local/accept, tcp_failure = Refused | TimedOut | Closed | Failed, tcp_wait = Forever | WithinMs). Proof x-lib-tcp2: closed green, document_test 22, lib_gate 3/3 executed (x-lib-tcp1 failed honestly on a pattern-syntax error, which lib_gate's new Mix-abort guard caught).\nNEXT: C7a.3 is the first Elixir deletion. Cells' BEAM side calls client.transact through a Gleam export once CELLS-TYPED-UNITS defines cells_boundary; until then the daemon process tier (C7b) is the next consumer.")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 4u32, "2026-11-02T16:47Z", "x", "2026-11-02 12:47 x: C7a.1 LANDED in live Cells (unstaged, hash-guarded, tree-write window): spi/client.spi B4D57D56DBA2 (new), spi/daemon.spi CBD50642E10E (Elixir-parity parsing), spi/package.spiproj F9E7265AE7A6 (client after daemon). PROOF x-cells-c7a2 (node xcells1, eoie path): daemon.spi 6/6 executed and passed, client.spi 4/4 (compile round trip through a spawned fake daemon, Status typed by its request, stale stamp, unreachable port), no Mix abort. x-cells-c7a1 failed first on ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous: WithinMs exists in both daemon and erlang_tcp, so client.spi writes erlang_tcp.WithinMs. No export yet, so domain.gleam is unaffected and no Elixir test can change. NEXT: C7b's daemon process tier is the first consumer of client.transact.")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_5 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:28 x: groom (WIP cap: Active means touched within 12 h): Active -> Paused at 45%. Not touched since yesterday, because today's node time goes to Cells-on-html, the sim-erlang slice, the iggy probe and the real-profile replay (four x jobs queued serially). RESUME CONDITION: x's node queue drains (x-events2, x-replay1, x-cells-mpath1, x-html-gleam6 done) or CELLS-HTML-PARITY lands its Cells half; its next step stays C7a.2 after the landed C7a.1 (client.spi, daemon.spi).")
