inl note_of_cells_scaling_bench_1 () = Note ("CELLS-SCALING-BENCH", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:20 compiler: filed from the user's directive (relayed by resilience 11-02): \"benchmark dib vs cells once and for all ... more cells => exponentially slower\"; it also helps define DoDs across projects. PLAN: one generated notebook family (N = 1, 2, 4 ... 128 cells, each a small typed cell over one shared prefix), run under Cells (daemon compiler, memo off and on) and under the dib path (dotnet-repl / fsi_chain, KINO-FSI-CLEANUP), with an A/A arm in the same job and wall time, CPU and RSS per phase. Fit the curve (linear vs quadratic in N). The deliverable is the ranked list of causes (e.g. each cell recompiles its whole prefix => O(N^2)). Existing tool to extend, not duplicate: apps/compiler/scripts/bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1. Runs on the nodes, never the box.")
inl note_of_cells_scaling_bench_2 () = Note ("CELLS-SCALING-BENCH", 2u32, "2026-11-07T11:07Z", "x", "2026-11-07 07:07 x: GROOMED with ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH (user 11-07): per-cell cost vs cell count runs on x's codespace harness CELLS-BENCH-CODESPACE; the parallel and memo questions live in CELLS-BENCH-PARALLEL / CELLS-BENCH-MEMO-LAYERS. This item keeps the 1..128-cell scaling curve per phase, which is compiler's. Codespace instead of the 3 nodes, for quiet CPUs.")
inl note_of_cells_scaling_bench_3 () = Note ("CELLS-SCALING-BENCH", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:56Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler (groom): DoD: a table of per-cell cost for 1, 8, 32 and 128 cells, per phase (parse, prefix compile, codegen, native build, run), for dib and for Cells on the node, median of 3 on a quiet node, plus the ranked fix list (each phase whose per-cell cost grows with cell count gets an item). typefeatureset plan: none; measurement only. next step: generate the 1..128-cell notebooks from one template cell, after LARGE-INPUT-SCALING's script so both share the timing harness.")
