inl note_of_dcolon_migration_lint_1 () = Note ("DCOLON-MIGRATION-LINT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:20 compiler: filed from the user's directive (relayed by resilience 11-02: \"why hasn't all code migrated to `::` yet, including open support? heal the drift\"). WHY IT DRIFTED: no gate flags `module.member`, so new code keeps copying the old spelling (kit's model.spi:41 `sm'.trim`). MEASUREMENT (regex over a lib-module name followed by `.`, strings/macros/comments stripped, so approximate): see title. CUT: same shape as LIST-SUGAR-DRIFT-GUARD. The formatter already has the compiler's tokens and parse; the finding is \"module-qualified access spelled with .\" -> \"::\", resolved against actual module names (never a regex), with --fix rewriting in place. \"open support\": verify that every open/import form accepts and prints `::` (e.g. `:< sm'` + qualified uses) and fix any parser gap first. Then the lint goes into lib's land gate, and each lane heals its repo with counts handed over (kit, dice, alphabet, x/cells).")
inl note_of_dcolon_migration_lint_2 () = Note ("DCOLON-MIGRATION-LINT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:59Z", "compiler", "11-02 10:55 compiler (groom): program DCOLON-MIGRATION-LINT\\1 (`format --check --respell-drift`) rides pack16c. On lib it reports 65 in 5 files, and that is exactly the set `format --spelling symbols` fixes: lint 67 -> fixer -> 0 on a scratch copy. The 2 extra hits were `:# forall`/`:# exists` test names, now excluded because findings come only from lines the converter changes. NEXT after install: hand counts to kit (src), dice, alphabet, x/cells and fix lib's 5 files (bench/parsing x4, json.spi) through land-lib-program; add the lint to the lib land gate.")
inl note_of_dcolon_migration_lint_3 () = Note ("DCOLON-MIGRATION-LINT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T17:58Z", "compiler", "11-02 14:05 compiler: LINT INSTALLED (pack16c). LIB HEAL READY: 5 programs in the drafts store (DCOLON-MIGRATION-LINT\\2..6-lib-respell-*.kitdo, 38 hunks for the 65 findings; land plan with base/target sha256 in lib-respell-land-plan.csv there). They were generated from `format --spelling symbols` output on scratch copies and verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to the formatter output after a kit-do apply on a full lib copy, every file equal. Files: bench/parsing/{bench_kit,fparsec,main,pure_split}.spi and json.spi. Order: node lib gate on json.spi (control vs heal), after the pack17 review frees the node mirror (one gate per mirror); then land-lib-program per file once kit-TRAIN11 releases the heavy window, closing with document_test. Lane counts were handed to main's broadcast 14:00.")
inl note_of_dcolon_migration_lint_4 () = Note ("DCOLON-MIGRATION-LINT", 4u32, "2026-11-02T19:03Z", "compiler", "11-02 15:15 compiler: LIB HEALED. The 5 programs landed through land-lib-program (undo copies under kit\\undo\\2..6-lib-respell-*): json.spi AE971545AA5C38DC (node lib gate 16/16 in both arms, executed > 0, 0 type errors), bench/parsing bench_kit 14B13FA5, fparsec 3FFC0859, main 96639CAB, pure_split 3FC31A46. The installed lint now reports 0 for lib, and document_test passes (Result: 22 passed). TOOL FIX on the way: land-lib-program.ps1 never created the undo copy's parent folder, so every lib file in a subfolder failed (safely, before writing). It now creates it (one line, parse-checked). Left: each lane heals its own repo (counts in main's broadcast); then the lint joins the lib land gate.")
