inl note_of_sps_notebooks_1 () = Note ("SPS-NOTEBOOKS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x FILED. SOURCE: research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"the only mega sample left is spiral proves spiral, which i don't know what we could do with yet, but still groom what's needed to at least migrate it to the new project style with test cells etc.\" LEGACY: 11,186 lines (631 KB), 487 :=, 66 unions, 38 nominals, 64 :==, 146 GADT cases, 423 existential sites, 71 terminals, 89 negative_* packages (matrix.psd1 ExpectedErrors from ~372), all_terminals 11; Peano meta_add relation GADT; an exact-linear/affine STLC (Unit/Bool/False/Tensor/Arrow) over context-indexed usage vectors; proven by construction: merge without Used-Used, renaming, outer weakening, open/closed beta, capture-avoiding substitution, strengthening, canonical forms, closed progress, closed-Bool normalization; open: universal progress, general application progress, beta congruence, confluence, strong normalization; False eliminator quarantined (empty match). It is a compiler canary for type-layout sensitivity (formatter G3, MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER n3), so it stays frozen as an oracle until archive. Children: SPS-PURPOSE, SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT, SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS, SPS-TYPEFEATURES, SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE.")
inl note_of_sps_notebooks_2 () = Note ("SPS-NOTEBOOKS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:19Z", "main", "main 11-02: dep MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER moved from this epic to SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE. Splitting the sample into notebooks (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT) does not need the five-sample retirement map; only the archive step must respect it. Flagged by the Lean/CIC research agent (add9e665535617d64).")
inl note_of_sps_notebooks_3 () = Note ("SPS-NOTEBOOKS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:38Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MIGRATION DONE RULE (user 11-02: \"make sure all these mega sample migrations have a definition of done so they don't spin forever again, and so we remove their code from the repo asap so we keep only latest code following the new style with test cells etc ... gotta transfer all the goodies before though, different than what regex did, only implemented a sliver then called it done\"). APPLIES TO all five: brzozowski (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB / REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION), lean_cic (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB / CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE), zeta (ZETA-TYPED-ARITH + ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE / ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE), omniledger (FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP / OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE), spiral_proves_spiral (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT + SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). (1) A migration is DONE only when the old sample is ARCHIVED out of the repo; a new home that works (regex published, CI green) is NOT done while absorption rows remain (the regex lesson: 9 of 71 legacy items absorbed at \"publishable\"). (2) Before the archive, every absorption-map row is resolved: (a) absorbed = a passing test in the new home in CI on both OSes, citing the legacy line; (b) lib = landed with lib tests; (c) compiler = a minimal regression sample with a matrix row; (d) dropped = a reason the map states. No row is left \"partial\". (3) ANTI-SPIN: the map is written first (one item, <= 4 h), then every (a)/(b) row is worked in priority order with the row count reported on the parent each groom round (absorbed / total); a week with no row closed raises the parent to P0 for the next round; a row blocked only by a compiler bug becomes its (c) regression sample plus a compiler item, and the archive may proceed with that row recorded as blocked-in-compiler (the goodie survives as the repro, in the new style). (4) The archive step runs in the SAME groom round the last row closes (scratch-archive.ps1, hash-verified, restore command in a note, dangling check by stem, user go), and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps its canary to the new home. (5) The parent item is set Done only after the archive note exists.")
inl note_of_sps_notebooks_4 () = Note ("SPS-NOTEBOOKS", 4u32, "2026-11-07T22:19Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. Next step: work happens in the children (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT first, then SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS and SPS-TYPEFEATURES); this epic rolls them up.")
inl note_of_sps_notebooks_5 () = Note ("SPS-NOTEBOOKS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T18:29Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: EPIC (1200m), mis-tagged light; its own title says 'purpose decided by the USER' and user 11-02 said he does not yet know what to do with spiral-proves-spiral, only to groom it. Children SPS-PURPOSE / SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT / SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-TYPEFEATURES / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE are the leaves (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT already waits on SPS-PURPOSE). The mega sample stays FROZEN as a compiler type-layout oracle until archive. Re-tagged heavy; parking on user (purpose is the user's call, per the title + 11-02).")
