inl note_of_sps_notebook_split_7 () = Note ("SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT", 7u32, "2026-11-10T07:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 FINAL ACCOUNTING (each of the 71 terminal bodies checked against the 119 kernel test bodies, read-only): 57 covered firmly, 10 WEAK, 1 aggregate (active_indexed_surface), 3 NONE. CORRECTION to note 5: all_used_usage_vector, context_indexed_lambda and indexed_variable_renaming_composition were listed as covered there; no kernel test asserts them. NONE: all_used_usage_vector (all-used derived from a context shape: 3 cells, used 3, bitmap 7); context_indexed_lambda (domain to domain tensor domain wrapper: tags 2, slots 1, lengths 4, used 2, bitmap+resources 5); indexed_variable_renaming_composition (renaming plans have no compose; direct = sequential at slot 3, steps 3 = 1+2). WEAK (same construct, narrower fact): conditional (only outer tag 7, not guard 3 / branches 2,2); identity_substitution (no closed Unit-Bool tensor case); open substitution variable (replacement is a closed constant, not an open Unit variable); tensor_right_general_congruence (right child steps by identity beta, the sample's point is a conditional step); closed_recursive_beta_progress (only the deep derivation is opened); closed_composite_ready_beta (identity ready beta only at Unit, not the composite Unit-Bool source); open_identity_beta_reduction (Unit instance only, not Bool); recursive application argument congruence depth 2 and depth 3 (no Unit to Unit-tensor-Unit layer); argument trace (progress and endpoint projections unasserted). Split: SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS carries the 3 NONE and 10 WEAK; this parent closes when it does.")
