inl note_of_sps_negatives_to_fails_3 () = Note ("SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:57Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 08:0xZ first 5 of 89 drafted as kernel fails blocks beside the code they guard (scratch, budget 0): linear_terms gains a_lambda_cannot_discard_its_linear_binder (negative_alpha_capture: Lambda over an unused-head body), a_nonempty_context_cannot_enter_the_closed_wrapper (negative_close_nonempty), false_elimination_requires_a_false_premise (negative_false_elimination_requires_false), a_cell_cannot_be_used_by_both_sides_of_a_merge (negative_used_used_merge); linear_strengthening gains strengthening_cannot_remove_a_used_cell (negative_context_strengthening_removes_used). Each expects Unification failure, the class of the matrix ExpectedErrors entries for these packages; the kernel's own type names differ from the sample's exact_linear_* names, so the full matrix text cannot be copied verbatim. Gate: ganymede job org2-neg (pinned, in-package). Next step: after org2-neg is green, org2 copies both files to the box and measures how long the next 10 conversions take.")
inl note_of_sps_negatives_to_fails_4 () = Note ("SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:59Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:0x compiler (agreed with org2): compiler takes the open-beta negatives (open_*_beta_cross_*, open_*_beta_target_type_mismatch) as fails blocks in the kernels linear_open_betas.spi, then possibly the closed_*_cross_type ones in linear_closed_reduction.spi; org2 keeps its first five (alpha_capture, close_nonempty, false_elimination_requires_false, used_used_merge, context_strengthening_removes_used) and does not touch those two files. compiler hands org2 a frozen file + sha, gated in-package on a mirror with a pinned compiler copy; org2 applies it and folds it into the consolidation gate.")
inl note_of_sps_negatives_to_fails_5 () = Note ("SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T08:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 first 5 of 89 GREEN and on the box (unstaged): ganymede job org2-neg (pinned, in-package) linear_terms 8/8 executed (4 new fails blocks), linear_strengthening 3/3 (1 new), 0 unsupported. Each fails block's body is the kernel form of its negative package and is rejected with Unification failure. Pace: drafting the 5 took about 15 min plus a 2 min gate, so the remaining 84 are roughly 4 h of drafting in batches by module. compiler took a disjoint second batch (open-beta negatives in linear_open_betas, closed_*_cross_type in linear_closed_reduction). Next step: org2 drafts the substitution negatives (*_substitution_keeps_used, strengthening drops) in linear_open_substitution and linear_term_strengthening.")
inl note_of_sps_negatives_to_fails_6 () = Note ("SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T08:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 batch 2 GREEN and on the box (ganymede org2-neg2, pinned, in-package, 0 unsupported): linear_open_substitution 8/8 (+2: substitution_keeps_used, tensor_substitution_keeps_used), linear_term_strengthening 4/4 (+1: term_strengthening_drops_preserved), linear_variable_strengthening 3/3 (+1: variable_strengthening_drops_preserved). Each asserts a real fixture at the type the negative package claims and is rejected with Unification failure. Running total: 9 of 89 (org2), plus compiler's batch in linear_open_betas / linear_closed_reduction. Batch 3 (5 in linear_reduction: unit step target, guard needs bool, unit beta target, derivation result and domain mismatch) is gating as org2-neg3.")
inl note_of_sps_negatives_to_fails_7 () = Note ("SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T08:11Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:1x compiler: the 10 open-beta negatives drafted as fails blocks appended to linear_open_betas.spi (scratch copy, sha 20a6e3ab; box tree untouched, org2 applies): open_identity_beta_cross_type (ibeta target at bool), open_identity_beta_cross_wrapper_application (ibeta step into abeta_target), open_application_beta_cross_wrapper_identity (abeta step into ibeta_target), open_application_beta_target_type_mismatch, open_tensor_beta_cross_wrapper_conditional, open_tensor_beta_target_type_mismatch, open_conditional_beta_cross_wrapper_tensor, open_conditional_beta_target_type_mismatch, open_lambda_beta_cross_wrapper_tensor, open_lambda_beta_target_type_mismatch. Each is ///> rust + :# <claim> fails \"Unification failure\" = with the false claim as an annotated binding inside the block; longest block 231 < 272. The kernels step types differ from the samples exact_linear_* names, so each mirrors the samples INTENT (wrong object type, or one betas step used as anothers), not its text. Gate RUNNING on ganymede in-package (mirror /root/compiler-sps from the boxs lib + apps/kernel, SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL pinned to a pack79 copy, SPIRAL_CELLS_SERVER=0, memo off; no bun on ganymede, rust-only file). Next step: read /root/compiler-sps/g.out, then hand org2 the file + sha.")
inl note_of_sps_negatives_to_fails_8 () = Note ("SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T08:13Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:2x compiler: second file drafted, linear_closed_reduction.spi (scratch copy sha 4d852acf, box tree untouched): 8 fails blocks, each a false type claim on a step built from the files own witnesses: identity beta result (sample closed_identity_beta_reduction_result_mismatch), left congruence target (closed_tensor_left_identity_congruence_target_cross_type), right congruence target (closed_tensor_right_identity_congruence_target_cross_type), argument congruence target (closed_application_argument_identity_congruence_target_cross_type), progress target (closed_unit_identity_progress_value_cross_type), progress from a reduction (closed_progress_from_reduction_cross_type), authority (closed_normalizing_progress_authority_cross_type), plus a recursive-beta target claim with no 1:1 sample. NOT covered, because the kernel has no matching witness to build without inventing one: the function-congruence, atomic tensor beta, higher-order, bool-normalization/outcome and tensor-value negatives (about 20 of the 29 closed_*). Longest block 258 < 272. Gate queued behind the open-beta gate on the same mirror (/root/compiler-sps/g2.sh). Next step: both gates green, then hand org2 both files + shas.")
