inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 13u32, "2026-11-08T19:55Z", "fiscal", "11-08 LANDED (fiscal side unstaged, lib side via lib_land_window). LIB: FISCAL-ERP-FIELD-META closed green 15:47: xsd_emit 673807F2 + xml_codec BD3C251F, lib digest 0FB176F529463A4B; consumer signatures 0 changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type probes 2/2 PASS (37 + 9 tests typed), respell drift 0; undo at spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261108-154723. (The first apply was refused by the live-reader guard on org2's note text, a false positive filed to rig by org2.) FISCAL: generator 5FA6A206, families 2ACF1F66, lifecycle 4C061E89, family-gates.ps1 A6B1FD05 and the new modeling_ceiling 6AEEA43B copied in, 5/5 at recorded hashes; generated/ replaced from the node regen, 167/167 matching the node manifest (45 changed + family-gates.tsv new, 0 extra); build.ps1 kept at live DE68F406. Pre-existing staged files (scripts/init.ps1, src/spiral.toml) left untouched. Evidence rows: Downloads\\relay-lab\\logs\\fiscal\\20261108-node-gate.*.tsv (101 unit rows). NEXT STEP: update FAMILY-MANIFEST, LAW, LIFECYCLE, CEILING, REGIME-INDEX, DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES; then XSD-FACET-DIGITS, MONEY (R5 draft), LEDGER; gate the R2 p2p draft.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 14u32, "2026-11-08T21:33Z", "fiscal", "11-08 GROOM: Planned 0% -> Active 45%. The combined landing (lib field-meta + generator, families, lifecycle, family-gates, modeling_ceiling + regenerated generated/) is done (n13). NEXT STEP: update FAMILY-MANIFEST (closed today), LAW, LIFECYCLE, REGIME-INDEX, DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES; gate the R2 p2p quorum draft; land the R5 money ceiling draft via lib_land_window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 15u32, "2026-11-09T03:56Z", "fiscal", "11-08 POST-LANDING GATE on pack63c (moon job-1794183825019 + merge rerun job-1794196190120). The whole landed tree (lib field-meta + R2 + the p2p budget split, staged 20:22; pinned compiler core 7A2B8AD55B7D48BB; cell timeouts x2): 100 units reported, 99 green. Merge: every example validates; reports 6/6. The ONE failure, generated_fiscal_runtime 1 of 3, is a live-Cells mount regression, not fiscal code: a mounted test resolves the unit's relative packageDir '../../deps/spiral/lib' against cells-mounts/<hash>/ ('Package .../cells-mounts/deps/spiral/lib/spiral is not loaded'). It passed with the 11-07 Cells mirror; reported to microblog (the Cells owner) with the timeline. The first merge also failed on a fiscal STAGING gap: .gitignore:9 ignores *.tsv, so the git ls-files stage list skipped generated/family-gates.tsv. Rule for future stages: copy generated/ from the filesystem, not from git ls-files. 82 green verdict rows went to oort (STORE-FISCAL-VERDICTS). Since then R1, R3 (p2p) and R5 (money, lib) also landed.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 16u32, "2026-11-09T04:25Z", "fiscal", "11-09 LANDED TREE 100/100 GREEN on pack63c. The one failure in the 11-08 post-landing gate, generated_fiscal_runtime (a Cells mount regression), passes 3/3 on moon (job-1794197871827, -Parallel 1, a stage restaged 00:1x from live Cells with microblog's mount fix: a mounted unit whose relative packageDir escapes is shadowed with the path expanded against its original dir, never junction-linked; an empty --resolve-manifest stdout now counts as failure). One shadow mount, no :link (microblog verified). SCOPE: at P1 the flaky path didn't recur, so the guard isn't stress-proven; the next full parallel gate is that test. That stage also has generated/family-gates.tsv (the stage list now takes generated/ from the filesystem, closing the *.tsv-gitignore gap).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 17u32, "2026-11-09T04:44Z", "fiscal", "11-09 SPLIT (stop-gate ask: 2430 m never fits a round; this kit has no 'edit --split' verb). The umbrella's estimate double-counted work already filed as child items, so the children are now its deps: FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX, -MONEY, -DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES, -ADAPTERS-ALL, -P2P-TYPESTATE, -LEDGER, -EVENT-LOG, -ALL-FAMILIES-PIPELINE, -NEW-COUNTRY-DRILL (each carries its own estimate). The umbrella's own remaining work is 90 m: the closing DoD check (one canonical document model, every family adapted, the P2P/ledger/event-log flows over it, the mega sample retired via OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE). NEXT STEP: pull the children in order (P2P R4 gating, then EVENT-LOG R7, DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES R8); this item closes when its deps do.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 18u32, "2026-11-10T10:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal groom 11-10 07:0x: this umbrella 'closes when its deps do'; after tonight MONEY, P2P-TYPESTATE and EVENT-LOG are Done, and the remaining open children are FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES (R8, on XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ), FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (now ready), FISCAL-ERP-ADAPTERS-ALL, FISCAL-ERP-ALL-FAMILIES-PIPELINE, FISCAL-ERP-NEW-COUNTRY-DRILL and FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX. An umbrella with no work of its own should not read as pullable, so it now waits on its next gating child (item:FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES). Next step: pull FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER, then R8 once 3-READ lands.")
