inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: :! br = () and the like; :| ^ regime_witness r; family r k indexed by regime and kind; dispatch at the boundary. DOD: an M7 (stringly dispatch) = 0 check; a negative showing a BR adapter cannot be applied to a UBL family. Deps on FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST S1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T12:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 08:05 fiscal: FIRST TYPED SLICE IN THE TREE (unstaged, src/families.spi on top of the FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST move): phantom regimes ':! brazil = ()', ':! europe_ubl = ()', ':! mexico = ()'; a regime witness GADT ':| regime_witness r = | Brazil :: regime_witness brazil | EuropeUbl :: regime_witness europe_ubl | Mexico :: regime_witness mexico'; a regime-indexed family ':! regime_family r = family_root' with family_root_of; brazilian_families (16: the 12 NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e roots + NF-e 4.00 + 3 events), ubl_families (6), mexican_families (1); families_of \\* r. (witness : regime_witness r) : list (regime_family r), dispatch at the boundary by GADT refinement, no strings (M7 = 0 for this slice); a Brazil-only adapter access_key_digits (_ : regime_family brazil) : i32 = 44. Tests: every_regime_lists_its_own_families (16 / 6 / 1, and every Brazilian family maps through the adapter) and the DoD NEGATIVE a_ubl_family_takes_no_brazilian_access_key fails \"Unification\". Proven on idle europa (pack24): families and generator type-check, and the same misuse as a top-level definition fails 'ETY-TermError: Unification failure. Got: list (regime_family europe_ubl)'. The Cells run of all three families tests rides job-1793707217418 (its inbox copy was updated to 0AB7E110). Still open from the DoD: 'family r k' (the document-kind index) and registry rows dispatched at the boundary for every regime.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 3u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 22:15 fiscal: GROOM 11-04 21:3x: still Active, waiting, not stale: its typed slice lives in src/families.spi, which the joint decode land replaces with the FISCAL-CII-PROFILES draft (F1CF3DDF); the land is blocked by the decode gate's MDF-e reds (XSD-DECODE-RESULT note 33). Resume after that land: re-apply the regime-index slice on top of the landed families.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 4u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 22:16 fiscal: CORRECTION to note 3: the FISCAL-CII-PROFILES families draft F1CF3DDF already carries the regime slice (regime_witness: 5 uses in the draft, 5 in live), so nothing needs re-applying; the land keeps it. The item's next step stays the remaining regimes after the decode land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 5u32, "2026-11-06T08:19Z", "fiscal", "Groom 11-06: next step = waits on FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST close; then family_id nominal from the manifest rows.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:20Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 WAIT RESOLVED (lint ProseWait): FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST closed 11-08/09, so the 11-06 groom's next step is open: family_id as a nominal derived from the manifest rows. Starting the read of families.spi for the design.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:32Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 RESCOPED BY THE BUDGET. Tried completing the index with 10 more regimes (Costa Rica, Chile, Spain, Italy, Poland, Portugal, Greece, Hungary, India, Europe-CII) plus a partition test (every one of the 45 families in exactly one regime). The cell budget forbids it: a 13-case regime_witness GADT is 534 weighted chars (a union cannot be split across cells), and the split dispatch (families_of/_elsewhere/_further) and names_by_regime added 4 more overages: families.spi went 35 -> 40, and baselines only shrink. More to the point, a regime witness pays only when an operation is regime-specific (today access_key_digits for brazil); none exists yet for the other countries, so their phantoms would be speculative. KEPT, the real gap: Mexico's regime listed only CFDI 4.0, while the TFD 1.1 stamp and Pagos 2.0 complements are Mexican families too: mexican_families now lists all 3, and every_regime_lists_its_own_families expects 3 (src/families.spi 6A44ED14, HEAD + 3/-2 lines, over-budget 35 = HEAD). Test running on ganymede. RULE for future regimes: add a country's witness together with its first regime-specific operation (e.g. a Chile folio range, a Costa Rica clave), never alone; past ~5 cases the witness needs a two-level shape (region witness indexing a country witness) to stay under 272.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 8u32, "2026-11-09T09:35Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 GREEN: every_regime_lists_its_own_families passed on ganymede (run_notebook --test, 25 s) with src/families.spi 6A44ED14 (Mexico = CFDI 4.0 + TFD 1.1 + Pagos 2.0); tree restored after. Unstaged in fiscal.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 9u32, "2026-11-10T23:34Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 20:5x GROOM per the 11-09 rule (add a country's witness with its first regime-specific operation): Peru now HAS a regime-specific operation (SUNAT's submitted file name RUC-TT-SERIE-NUMERO.xml, rule 1034; being typed in FISCAL-PE-SUNAT-FILE-NAME), but a Peru witness still does not fit: SUNAT documents are UBL 2.1 documents whose family roots EuropeUbl already lists, and a family belongs to exactly one regime, so families_of Peru would duplicate UBL roots or be empty. So the operation lives in sunat.spi over its own document_type, not behind a regime phantom. If a regime witness for Peru is ever wanted, it needs a customization layer (UBL root x SUNAT customization 2.0) rather than new family roots. Next step: none until another regime gains a regime-specific operation over its own family roots.")
