inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 10u32, "2026-11-07T21:15Z", "fiscal", "11-07 17:1x re-decided: stays Paused. Reason: money rounding needs XSD-FACET-DIGITS, whose lib draft (xml 57AB7497 + xsd_emit B1178DE4) is stacked on the unlanded field-meta xsd_emit, and no lib lands tonight (lib_land_window closes red on the consumer gate until pack61b is fleet-wide; europa is still on pack61). Resume when: XSD-FACET-DIGITS is Done (after the field-meta set lands and its node regen + Cells gate pass).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 11u32, "2026-11-08T12:57Z", "fiscal", "11-08 CORRECTION to the 11-07 note: its premise (no lib lands until pack61b is fleet-wide) was false; fiscal landed two lib sets 11-07 23:12 and 23:32. The real blocker is gate cost: the field-meta set needs its regenerated units gated, and the full gate no longer fits 6 h. Resume path: the combined landing in FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC n8 (started 11-08), gated by sharding (FISCAL-GATE-SHARD).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 12u32, "2026-11-08T13:45Z", "fiscal", "11-08 OMNILEDGER absorption row owned here (OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n8): R5 safe-ceiling rounding (sample main.spi:649-693), next to the floor/half-up/half-even modes in money.spi:33-49, with a test.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 13u32, "2026-11-08T14:40Z", "fiscal", "11-08 R5 DRAFTED (absorption row from OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n8; independent of the field-meta stack, since money.spi is not in it): kit drafts spiral\\FISCAL-ERP-MONEY-R5-CEILING\\v1\\money.spi FE2F3675 over live 0D68320D. New rounding case Ceiling (the sample's safe ceiling, main.spi:649-693: an exact quotient stays, any positive remainder rounds up, so a conversion never under-collects). Test ceiling_rounds_up_and_never_undershoots: 2.1 -> 3, exact 2.0 stays 2, -2.5 -> -2, 1.651 -> 1.66 at 2 places where half up gives 1.65. GRANULAR: the live file had 2 code overages (rounded 498, converted 333); the draft splits rounded_units and route_value out, so it has 0 (baseline shrinks), with the same arithmetic. Consumers: ledger.spi passes money::rounding through (revalued, 2 HalfUp call sites) and has no exhaustive match on it, so the new case breaks nothing. NEXT STEP: lib_land_window dry run, then -Apply, when the box has a compile window (today it is at 100 percent with TRAIN40's box half and pack62 queued). Resume condition for the rest of this item is unchanged: XSD-FACET-DIGITS (field-meta landing).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 14u32, "2026-11-09T02:49Z", "fiscal", "11-08 RESUMED (autonomous run). The pause waited on the combined landing, which closed green 15:47. R5 safe-ceiling rounding: the draft is rebased onto live money.spi A74A7DC9 (pack63c layout) as v2 74C60F7E by formatting v1 with pack63c; its diff against live is exactly the R5 change (Ceiling case, rounded_units + route_value extracted, converted simplified, ceiling test). lib_land_window dry run green (round trip OK). BLOCKER: the cell budget is 6 over in v2 vs 4 over in live, so it must not grow before -Apply. NEXT STEP: split the 2 new overages (find them with mix spiral.cell_budget --check on v2), then -Apply with -BaseHash A74A7DC9.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 15u32, "2026-11-09T03:16Z", "fiscal", "11-08 R5 LANDED via lib_land_window, closed green at ~22:57: lib/spiral/money.spi 881A2AEB over live A74A7DC9 (lib digest EB40FCBCEFCBD471; consumer apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type probe PASS, respell drift 0; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261108-225711). OMNILEDGER R5 (safe-ceiling rounding, sample main.spi:649-693) is ABSORBED: a Ceiling mode next to floor, half-up and half-even, with ceiling_rounds_up_and_never_undershoots. Cell budget held at live's 4 over (rounded 590 -> 359; converted no longer over) by extracting half_even_units, rounded_units, via_value and route_value. Rebase lesson: when a draft's base moved only by a formatter respell, run the draft through the same formatter, then diff against live; only the semantic change should remain. NEXT STEP: the last OMNILEDGER rows owned here are done; DOD check against OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n8.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 16u32, "2026-11-09T21:00Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 16:5x the blocker moved: XSD-FACET-DIGITS's LIB half LANDED (xml FCE8DD3E with total_digits/fraction_digits; xsd_emit 070FB8C4 makes totalDigits/fractionDigits restrictions validated nominals), so money amounts read from schemas now carry their digit bounds. What is left before MONEY can close: DIGITS's family proof (cfdi_v4_0 plus a Hacienda unit on a fresh node gate after the next fiscal regen). Then FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (deps MONEY + P2P-TYPESTATE, P2P already Done) becomes ready.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 17u32, "2026-11-09T22:43Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 18:4x UNBLOCKED: XSD-FACET-DIGITS is Done (lib landed and family-proven on cfdi_v4_0 and cr_factura_4_4). The 11-06/11-07 pause said resume when DIGITS is Done and nothing else blocks it. Next step: re-check this item's DoD against what is live (currency-indexed amounts, the FX route GADT, rounding per regime incl. R5 Ceiling) and either close it or name the last gap; FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER follows once this is Done.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 18u32, "2026-11-09T22:44Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 18:5x DoD RE-CHECKED against live money.spi 881A2AEB. MET: (1) currency-indexed amounts over lib decimal (amount c = decimal::decimal; plus is same-currency only; negative test brl_plus_eur_does_not_type); (2) the FX route GADT with an existential middle currency (Via :: \\* a b. (\\? m. rate a m * rate m b) -> fx_route a b, Direct for one hop; converted takes a route). GAP: (3) 'rounding as an evidence-carrying union PER REGIME': rounding is a plain 4-case union (HalfUp, HalfEven, Floor, Ceiling) passed as a value, so nothing ties a regime to its legal mode. Shape of the fix: a regime-indexed GADT in fiscal (not lib), e.g. regime_rounding r with one constructor per regime that fixes the mode and places (NF-e: HalfUp at 2; a HalfEven regime; Ceiling for safe conversions), and converted taking that evidence instead of a free rounding value, so a wrong mode for a regime does not type. It needs the regime phantom indices from FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX, so MONEY now waits on that item instead of on DIGITS. 95 percent.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 19u32, "2026-11-09T22:46Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "NEXT STEP: when FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX provides the regime phantoms (its wait row is on this item), draft regime_rounding r in fiscal with one constructor per regime fixing mode and places, change converted to take that evidence, and add a negative test where a wrong mode for a regime is rejected; then close MONEY and pull FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 20u32, "2026-11-10T03:44Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 00:5x DESIGN CORRECTED BY SOURCES. SOURCED 11-10 (web research, official sources): NO regime prescribes a tie-handling rounding MODE. Brazil NF-e 4.00: vProd/vICMS 2 decimals (TDec_1302), vUnCom 0-10, qCom 0-4; per item vProd = round2(vUnCom x qCom) within +-0.01 else rejection 629/630 (NT 2011/004 s4.4 p10); ABNT NBR 5891 NOT found mandated in MOC 7.00 (Anexo I unchecked). Mexico CFDI 4.0 (Anexo 20 DOF 2022 + guia de llenado Apendice 7 Q37/39/41): line Importe and tax Importe validated against a WINDOW, lower = (Cantidad - 10^-dec/2)(ValorUnitario - 10^-dec/2) truncated, upper = (Cantidad + 10^-dec/2 - 10^-12)(ValorUnitario + 10^-dec/2 - 10^-12) rounded up; lines at full precision (t_Importe up to 6 decimals), round only at the end; SubTotal/Total/tax summary use the currency's decimals from c_Moneda (0-4, MXN 2). EN 16931 / Peppol BIS 3.0: all amounts max 2 decimals (BR-DEC-01..28), VAT rounded per category (BR-CO-17, method unstated), CEN schematron uses XPath round() with +-1 unit tolerance on BR-CO-17/BR-S-09, Peppol R120/R040 tolerance 0.02; unit price and quantity unbounded. CONSEQUENCE: the gap is NOT 'a regime-indexed rounding mode' (that would encode law that does not exist). It is (a) per-currency minor units (a prototype or table from the c_Moneda catalog: decimals per currency, MXN 2, others 0-4), replacing callers passing places by hand; and (b) regime-indexed ACCEPTANCE WINDOWS that return evidence: accepted_within (a certificate carrying the bounds) or rejected with the bound it broke, per regime (NF-e +-0.01 per item; CFDI computed lower/upper per line from the currency decimals; EN 16931 2-decimal amounts with per-category VAT). Next step: draft the currency-decimals table from the c_Moneda catalog (fiscal deps corpus mx) and an amount_window r GADT with the three regimes, in fiscal src.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 21u32, "2026-11-10T10:05Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 06:3x DoD (3) MET IN ITS SOURCED FORM, closing. Note 11-10 03:44Z established from official sources that no regime prescribes a tie-handling MODE; each regime prescribes a WINDOW. That window is now live and gated green: families.spi amount_window r indexed per regime (NfeItem : amount_window brazil, CfdiLine : cfdi_decimals -> amount_window mexico, En16931Amount : amount_window europe_ubl) with window_check returning an evidence-carrying window_verdict r (Within/Outside with the bounds), and a Brazilian window cannot check a Mexican line (negative test, Unification). proof: box gates 11-10, families 11/11 + lifecycle 16/16 (FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY, FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS) and currency 15/15 (ISO 4217 places, the Moneda-driven window, and a real SAT-stamped CFDI line inside its window while strict rounding would reject it). (1) and (2) were met 11-09. Next step: none; Done (FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER can now pull).")
