inl note_of_fiscal_erp_document_prototypes_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES", 14u32, "2026-11-09T05:28Z", "fiscal", "11-09 SEQUENCING. R8 (typed codecs for the ERP operation payloads through the fiscal_document prototype) needs descriptor READS: XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ (a reading instance walking the existential '<ty>_fields' lists). Step 2 is Done (the hoist is emitted, 44/44 units; corrected 11-09). Steps 3+ are xsd_emit changes, and xsd_emit is now the bottleneck file for three fiscal lines that must land one at a time: (1) FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-0-LIB-STAGED (draft 7A6892B9, lib test gate queued on ganymede), (2) FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6-EMIT (241 code overages, in batches), (3) XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ, which unblocks R8. Order: 1, then 3 (it unblocks ERP depth), then 2 in batches between other lands. NEXT STEP: after step 0 lands, draft descriptors step 3 (the reading instance), then R8 over it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_document_prototypes_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES", 15u32, "2026-11-09T11:03Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 SEQUENCING UPDATE: of the xsd_emit queue in n?, (1) step 0 LANDED (7A6892B9) and (3)'s first half LANDED (xsd_emit 0888893E: every derived record now gets its base-part witness, so <ty>_field/<ty>_fields exist for ~all record writers). Still needed for R8: the READ half of XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ (the reading instance walks the existential <ty>_fields list instead of record_texts' string-keyed part walk). That is the next xsd_emit draft after the GRANULAR 6A batch now gating on moon (v3 790F6F6B), keeping one xsd_emit draft at a time. NEXT STEP unchanged: R8 once the reader reads through <ty>_fields.")
