inl note_of_omniledger_archive_1 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:26Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". PARITY GATE: every (a)/(b)/(c) row of FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP landed; each compiler behaviour the sample guards has a regression sample or a covering row; references repointed or removed: matrix.psd1 lines 22, 53-54, 58, 80, 85, 238 and ExpectedErrors from 331; apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md:138 and :146; hopacsota/PLAN.md:965; the GLEAM-ABYSSAL-SCALE brief and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER; a stem grep across sibling repos finds nothing. THEN scratch-archive.ps1 (never delete).")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_2 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:27Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 12:24 the map is in FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP's 11-02 note (33 concepts, 43 negatives, 77 terminals, each classed with lines). The parity gate's (a)/(b)/(c) owners: FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE, -LEDGER, -EVENT-LOG, -MONEY, -REGIME-INDEX, XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES, XSD-DECODE-RESULT, LIB-VEC-FIN, LIB-DURABLE-APPEND, GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES; (d) rows point at WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_3 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 12:57 fiscal: TRANSFER INVENTORY (the DONE rule: archive only after every useful part moved). Source: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_omniledger_erp_kernel, 12,080-line main.spi with 830 top-level definitions, 106 tracked files, 43 negative_* dirs + all_terminals + runtime_native. MAPPING, definitions by prefix: erp_p2p (249) + erp_issue/receive/match/reserve/collect (53) -> FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE draft p2p.spi (stage typestate + three-way match + authorized-document witness DONE in draft; STILL TO MOVE: budget reservation tokens, partial receipts by quantity, approval quorum); typed_fx (193) + settlement_fx / existential_typed / typed_usd (20) -> FISCAL-ERP-MONEY draft money.spi (fx_route with existential middle currency, rounding modes DONE; STILL TO MOVE: epoch-indexed settlement routes and the ratio certificate); typed_fx stream position / hashed statement log / identity collision (part of the 193) -> FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG draft event_log.spi (as RUNTIME evidence outcomes, deliberately not type-level successor chains); raw-byte position codec + checksummed persisted log -> LIB-DURABLE-APPEND; erp_net + opposed_mirror (18) -> FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER draft ledger.intercompany; erp_close (9) -> ledger (STILL TO MOVE: close certificate per entity/period/standard); erp_add/mul/nat/rate + v65 (45) -> lib decimal/money (type-level naturals are compiler stress, see below). NEGATIVES (43): p2p stage/version/outbox (10: p2p_*, erp_step_detached_result, unit_event_multistep_plan) -> p2p.spi's 10 fails tests + event_log outbox typestate; hash/identity collisions and reapply (5) -> event_log Replayed/Collided outcomes (runtime); history/observation (4) -> event_log; event_payload_codec_cross_family -> event_log's a_log_of_one_event_type_takes_no_other; net_intercompany_detached_mirrors -> ledger.intercompany returns both mirrors at once (detachment cannot be expressed); fences, multiprocess endpoints, takeover, lock receipts, WAL/crash recovery (14) -> LIB-DURABLE-APPEND (lib, not fiscal); owner-lineage/fixed-depth nat forcing (5) -> NOT fiscal: type-level arithmetic stress. COMPILER VALUE (decide before archiving): the sample is 5 rows of the compiler's mega suite and runtime_native carries the DeadPureLetElision notes in apps/compiler/AGENTS.md; archiving removes that coverage, so the compiler lane must accept the loss or keep a trimmed stress copy. Pair item, user go stays required.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_4 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T19:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:33 fiscal: STILL-TO-MOVE list from n3, now: period close (ledger open/closed period) MOVED; close certificate per standard (ledger certificate s e p c) MOVED; epoch-indexed settlement FX (ledger quote a b p + revalued) MOVED; budget reservation, approval quorum, partial receipts (p2p reserved state, quorum approve, receive_more) MOVED; durable outbox (event_log append_durably over lib durable_file) MOVED. All landed unstaged, runtime-proven as Rust on europa, node Cells confirmation queued (confirm-landed2). Remaining before archiving: the compiler-value decision (the sample's 5 mega-suite rows and the runtime_native AGENTS.md notes) and the user's go (pair item).")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_5 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T05:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:29 fiscal: COMPILER-VALUE DECISION, with evidence (spiral apps/compiler/tmp): the sample is wired into the compiler suite as 3 run rows (main.spi ERP mega row, all_terminals, runtime_native), 2 F#/Windows platform entries, 2 timeout entries, bench-native.ps1's runtime_native, AGENTS.md notes (:142, :150), and 41 matrix.psd1 negative rows (43 negative_* dirs), each pinning an exact ETY-TermError unification message over nat-indexed GADT typestate (fence histories, commit trees, recursive takeover programs, versioned event stores). Across ALL other samples only 5 negative rows involve nat_succ, so this 12,080-line sample is the compiler's main nat-indexed GADT negative coverage. Those shapes are compiler stress, not fiscal concepts; fiscal deliberately did not port them. FISCAL SIDE COMPLETE: every business concept moved (n3/n4: p2p typestate + reservation/quorum/partial receipts, money + FX routes, ledger + periods + certificates + revaluation, durable event log/outbox), landed and Cells-confirmed 11-03. RECOMMENDATION: do NOT archive; the sample stays in the compiler suite as a GADT stress/regression asset (the user, 11-03: GADT bugs mean 'only now we're scratching the surface of the complex-enough models'). Archiving needs the user's go and would delete 41 of the 46 nat-indexed negatives; keeping needs none. Parked with that recommendation; reopen only if the user still wants it archived, after GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES gives equivalent coverage.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_6 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T06:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:54 fiscal: PAUSED (re-decided, stop-gate groom). REASON: the archive would delete the compiler suite's main nat-indexed GADT negative coverage (41 of 46 matrix.psd1 negatives with nat_succ, plus 3 run rows and the native bench) while fiscal's absorption is already complete, so archiving now loses value and gains nothing. RESUME WHEN: (a) GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES (or another compiler sample) carries equivalent nat-indexed negatives AND (b) the user still wants the sample archived (archiving needs the user's go). Until then the sample stays where it is; nothing for fiscal to do.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_7 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T07:23Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:23 fiscal: priority P1 -> P3: nothing is actionable until the n6 resume condition (equivalent nat-indexed compiler negatives AND the user's go); fiscal's absorption is complete, and the recommendation is to keep the sample.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_8 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 8u32, "2026-11-08T13:45Z", "fiscal", "11-08 REGROOM (user 11-08 via i574n: keep reaching the SOTA model while expanding countries and the generic ERP so we retire the old mega sample; archive-only is dropped, retire = DELETE once absorbed). CORRECTIONS to n5: (i) fiscal's side was NOT complete: a read-only audit today (sample spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_omniledger_erp_kernel, main.spi 12,080 lines) finds 14 of 23 business rows ABSORBED with tests and 9 PARTIAL or GAP; (ii) the sample carries 43 negative dirs, 41 with matrix.psd1 rows (:343-383); 21 contain nat_succ out of 26 suite-wide (not 41 of 46); 2 dirs have no row and never run. ABSORPTION CHECKLIST (DoD part A, each row needs a fiscal or lib test): ABSORBED: P2P stage typestate (p2p.spi:15, 9 tests), budget reservation, partial receipts (amount), tax-authority witness at match, three-way match, intercompany mirror pair (ledger.spi:42), currency-indexed money (money.spi:15), FX route with middle currency, FX tied to a period, rounding floor/half-up/half-even, balanced journal (ledger.spi:30 + posting.spi), ledger per entity and currency, period close + certificate + GAAP projection, append at expected position, payload-hash collision, proven retry, durable outbox (event_log.spi:59 + durable_file.spi). REMAINING (fiscal or lib): R1 plan composition ErpStep/ErpThen (S:167) -> FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE; R2 quorum of 3 DISTINCT roles (S:102-111; p2p.spi:32 only counts) -> P2P-TYPESTATE; R3 P2P payment through an FX route (S:149) -> P2P-TYPESTATE; R4 quantities with unit of measure on partial receipts -> P2P-TYPESTATE; R5 safe-ceiling rounding (S:649-693) -> FISCAL-ERP-MONEY; R6 history, facts and membership queries with tests (S:1438, :3638-3860) -> FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG; R7 P2P transitions written to the event log or outbox (S:6008-6117) -> EVENT-LOG; R8 typed codecs for the ERP operation payloads (S:6590-8974) -> FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES; R9 checksummed frames (S:1634-1721; durable_file.spi has none) -> lib (WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB). DoD part B (compiler side, not fiscal's call): the 5 compiler-stress negatives and type-level naturals get a home in GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES; the 16 durability negatives and 33 terminals (CAS races, fencing, WAL recovery) in WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB; the runtime_native codegen rows (11 backends) and bench-native.ps1:5 rehomed or retired by compiler. DoD part C: delete the sample dir, its matrix.psd1 rows (:22, :54-55, :59, :83, :88, :245, :343-383, :764, :908 and the runtime_native lists), bench-native.ps1:5 and AGENTS.md :156/:164 in one change, with the compiler suite green after. NEXT STEP: R1-R4 inside P2P-TYPESTATE once the combined landing unblocks it; compiler is told about part B today.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_9 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 9u32, "2026-11-08T13:45Z", "fiscal", "DoD: (A) all 23 business rows of the n8 checklist ABSORBED, each with a named fiscal or lib test (today 14 of 23); (B) compiler has rehomed the sample's compiler-stress and durability negatives and the runtime_native rows (GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES, WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB); (C) the sample dir and every suite reference deleted in one change, with the compiler suite green after.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_10 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 10u32, "2026-11-09T04:33Z", "fiscal", "11-09 CHECKLIST UPDATE (part A, the business rows; ref n8). ABSORBED 11-08/09 with tests: R1 plan composition -> fiscal p2p_plan (a GADT with an existential middle stage, then_/run_plan, out-of-order composition does not type; p2p.spi 6A1E28B3); R2 quorum of distinct roles AND distinct people -> fiscal p2p (bare names do not type; 16/16); R3 P2P payment through an FX route -> fiscal settled_amount/pay_in over money::fx_route (direct + middle currency, wrong-currency route does not type; p2p.spi 0425DBE0, 22/22); R5 safe-ceiling rounding -> lib money.spi 881A2AEB (Ceiling mode + ceiling_rounds_up_and_never_undershoots; lib_land_window closed green). IN FLIGHT: R4 quantities with a unit of measure (fiscal partial_receipt over lib units::amount, each/kilogram phantoms, refusing receive beyond the order, kilograms-vs-each does not type): draft A3573EB9, gate queued on ganymede. REMAINING: R6 history/facts/membership queries over the event log, R7 P2P transitions written to the log/outbox (FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG); R8 typed codecs for the ERP operation payloads (DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES); R9 checksummed frames (lib WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB). Parts B (compiler-stress negatives rehomed) and C (delete) unchanged.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_11 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 11u32, "2026-11-09T06:29Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 CHECKLIST: R4 (partial receipts by unit of measure) and R7 (purchase events in an idempotent event log) ABSORBED into fiscal p2p with tests (p2p.spi 715E5792, 28/28 on ganymede 06:14 UTC). Absorbed now: R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R7. Remaining: R6, R8 (needs XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ, after the xsd_emit step-0 lib gate now running on ganymede), R9. NEXT: R6 draft.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_12 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 12u32, "2026-11-09T06:52Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 R6 (history, facts and membership queries over the event log) DRAFTED and GREEN as a lib event_log change (LIB-EVENT-LOG-R6 6701B3BE, 12/12 on ganymede), landing with xsd_emit step 0 in one moon land window. After that land: absorbed R1-R7; remaining R8 (typed codecs, after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ) and R9 (checksummed frames, lib WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB), then parts B and C.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_13 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 13u32, "2026-11-09T08:05Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 R9 DESIGN (checksummed frames, sample S:1634-1721). The sample seals each persisted command as a frame carrying a checksum derived from its content, sums frames and checksums over the persisted log, and audits a frame by recomputing (stored vs recomputed, then a validation union). Business core for fiscal: lib event_log's durable line (entry_line: position, command id, payload hash, event text; written by append_durably) gains a trailing Adler-32 of the line's own text, reusing lib wire (adler_of; published-vector test adler32_of_wikipedia already in lib), and a reader audit_lines returns a typed verdict: an audit union Intact of i64 (frames read) | Corrupt of i64 * u32 * u32 (first bad position, stored, recomputed), plus a frame_count. Tests: a written log audits Intact with its frame count; flipping one byte of an event reports Corrupt at that position; a frame whose checksum column is missing is Corrupt (fail closed). The sample's type-level persisted-log index stays compiler stress (part B), not business. SEQUENCING: this is a draft on lib event_log, which holds the R6 draft (6701B3BE) waiting for the step-0 + R6 land (moon proof v2 running), so R9 is drafted right after that land, never stacked on it.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_14 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 14u32, "2026-11-09T08:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 R6 LIVE in lib event_log (land from a proven close, see FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG). Absorbed now: R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7. Remaining business rows: R8 (typed codecs, after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ, now unblocked) and R9 (checksummed frames, n13 design, drafting next). Then parts B (compiler-stress negatives rehomed) and C (delete).")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_15 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 15u32, "2026-11-09T08:29Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 R9 DRAFTED on live lib event_log 6701B3BE (no stack): kit drafts spiral LIB-EVENT-LOG-R9 v1 event_log.spi DB33ED2E (280 lines). ADDITIVE: line_codes + line_checksum (lib wire::adler_of over the line's code points, which equals Adler-32 over UTF-8 on ASCII lines such as fiscal's command/hash/stage lines, and stays an integrity checksum otherwise; named line_checksum, not adler32, for that reason); framed_line (entry_line's body + TAB + its checksum); framed_text (oldest first); audit union (Intact :: i64 | Corrupt :: i64 * string * string = frame, stored, recomputed); frame_verdict splits at the LAST tab (event text may hold tabs); audit_frames walks lines and stops at the first bad frame (fail closed); audit_code. Tests: a_framed_log_audits_intact (2 frames), a_changed_event_is_corrupt_at_its_frame (cancelled -> cancelleD: Corrupt at 2), a_frame_without_its_checksum_is_corrupt (a bare entry line: Corrupt at 1). NOT changed: append_durably still writes plain entry lines; switching the durable format to framed lines is a separate decision (it changes the on-disk shape that lib's only_a_real_append_reaches_the_file and fiscal lifecycle's outbox test pin). Gate queued on europa after the step-3 xsd_emit gate.")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_16 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 16u32, "2026-11-09T08:47Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 R9 LIVE in lib event_log 08687CF1 (line_checksum, framed_line, framed_text, audit union, audit_frames, 15/15 on moon). LANDED 11-09 04:4x local from a proven close, copy-only on the box (moon job-1794213782003-fiscal-libland-proof5: round trip, 0 consumer signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type probe PASS for both, respell drift 0, lib digest 2306F0893534A3AF = the box digest after the land). Proof v4 had stopped at the round trip: the R9 draft lacked a final newline (a PowerShell here-string drops it); the canonical bytes from lib_roundtrip.exs fixed it (08687CF1). Absorbed now: R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7, R9. Remaining business row: R8 (typed codecs for the ERP operation payloads), which follows XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ (its step-3 draft 0888893E is canonical and gating on europa). Then parts B (rehome the compiler-stress negatives) and C (delete the sample).")
inl note_of_omniledger_archive_17 () = Note ("OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE", 17u32, "2026-11-10T02:54Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 23:4x REVIEW (read-only, against the code; user asked to review the mega samples). Sample S = spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_omniledger_erp_kernel/main.spi (12,080 lines). CORRECTIONS to the R list: R4 is PARTIAL (fiscal p2p.spi partial_receipt over units::amount exists, :187-194, but receive/receive_more :58/:62 still take a bare decimal); R7 is PARTIAL (p2p_event :205-209 has 4 payload-free events reserved/approved/ordered/received, no matched/paid/netted/closed, and the 'payload hash' :222 hashes the event name; S's events carry the whole operation, S:6008-6117); R2 is absorbed but weaker (approvals not bound to their document, S:59); R1, R3, R5, R6, R9 confirmed with file:line. R8 is open AND mis-scoped: S's R8 (S:6590-8974) is a typed encode/decode round trip of the 8 ERP operations with truncation and cross-family negatives; the backlog mapped it to family decoding through fiscal_document, which has one instance today (canon_of manual_invoice, document.spi:118). GAPS NOT ON THE LIST: G1 hash-chained outbox (S:5788-5957; lib crypto has SHA-256, nothing chains); G2 match legs indexed by entity/currency/item/document (S:57-88; fiscal purchase s is indexed by stage only, three_way :66 compares amounts); G3 P2P never reaches the ledger or period close (S:157-160), no intercompany-netting stage; G4 currency minor-unit scale (S:1009-1019; lib money takes places from callers); G5 per-aggregate identity in the event log (S:1401-1418, :4312). PART B: 43 negative_* dirs, 41 matrix rows (matrix.psd1 :349-389), 2 dirs unregistered; runtime_native rows need a home. PART C references: matrix.psd1 (many lines), scripts/bench-native.ps1:5, tmp/AGENTS.md:498/:515, lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md:1220. VERDICT: NOT READY. NEXT STEP: split R8 into R8a (typed encode/decode round trip of p2p events WITH payloads for every stage, covering R7 and the cross-family negative; can start now) and R8b (family decoding through canon_of instances, after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ's reader); add G1-G5 as rows (G2 and G1 first); finish R4 by indexing receive by unit.")
inl rec_marker_heal () = Task ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", "Remove ^ (rec) from every definition that is in no recursion cycle (96 on 11-02: kit 28, regex 33, lib 22, fiscal 7, x 5, cells 1), then a kit standards rule that refuses ^ outside a cycle so LLMs stop adding it by convention", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "team:org,main,kit,standards,drift,spiral-style", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rec_marker_heal () = Planning ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_1 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 (user: \"kit changed a lot of functions to recursive lately, seemed mechanical, we gotta heal from this drift so the llms don't start putting the ^ on every function by convention\"). ROOT CAUSE found: main's own memory join-points-shrink-generated said \"make multi-use helpers `:~ ^`\", and lanes copied it. The lexer maps `:=` to inl, `:~` to let (join point) and `^` to rec (spiral_compiler.fs:1260-1261), so a join point is `:~` alone; lib already has 132 plain `:~` defs. Memory corrected 11-02. MEASURED (per-file call graph over top-level defs; flagged = no path back to itself, so mutual recursion is kept): kit/src 28 of 588 ^defs, lib/spiral 22 of 461, regex/src 33 of 125, fiscal/src 7 of 30, x client 3 of 42 + sim 2 of 45, cells/spi 1 of 100, tibia/src 0 of 38. Lists: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\GROOM-1102-MAIN\\rec-scc-out.txt (scanner rec-scc.ps1 beside it). The scanner bounds bodies by column-0 lines, so verify each before removing; a cross-file cycle would be missed. DoD: every flagged def is either un-^'d with its package gate green (generated output identical or smaller) or recorded as a real cycle; then a GRANULAR-LINT/standards row \"rec outside cycle\" ratchets at 0 per repo. Each lane heals its own repo (kit, regex, fiscal, x); main does lib and cells.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_2 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:47Z", "main", "main 11-02 09:xx CORRECTED COUNTS (n1 overcounted). fiscal found the blind spot: the scanner skipped ':& :~ name' group members, so a ^ that opens a :& mutual-recursion group looked cycle-free (fiscal canon.spi:113 visit_element + :127 read_children). Fixed (':&' members join the call graph) and rerun: kit 28 of 588, lib 4 of 461 (was 22), x 0 (was 5), fiscal 6 of 30 (matches fiscal's own hand check exactly), regex 31 of 125 (was 33), cells 1 of 100, tibia 0. Total 70 (was 96). The list in drafts\\i574n.github\\GROOM-1102-MAIN\\rec-scc-out.txt is replaced. Owners: kit 28 (with the standards rule), fiscal 6 (in progress), main lib 4 + regex 31 + cells 1. x has none.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_3 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-11-02T15:18Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 12:0x HEALED + RULE (unstaged; ships in the next kit train). (1) Heal: 28/28 kit `^` sites outside any cycle removed by one hash-checked kit do program, each site verified first: the line reads ':~ ^ <name>' and the name is not called in its own body (case-sensitive; -match had faked a self-call on the Rendered constructor). 25 in k3s_manifest/manifest.spi, 3 in kit_k3s/k3s.spi; 8 genuinely recursive ^ remain. k3s_manifest tests 5/5. kit_k3s cannot be notebook-compiled alone (unbound package import), before AND after the heal, identical errors. (2) Rule: new crate kit_rec_cycle (typed: definition record, site = RecSite | PlainSite, cycle_verdict = InCycle | NoCycle; per-file call graph from tokenised bodies, DFS back to the definition; `:&` group members included; over-approximated edges can only miss, never falsely refuse), called from kit_standards_scan through the binding package kit_rec_cycle_api (interim until COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS Step B). Finding: '<path>:<line>  rec-outside-cycle  ^ on <name> but it is in no recursion cycle'. Placement decided by size: inside kit_standards_scan it made scan.rs 651 -> 1252 (OVER); as its own crate scan.rs 653 + rec_cycle.rs 625, gate ok (274 crates). Type lesson: the first draft used a GADT site m + existential any_site and the compiler refused it ('Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var'): existentials are compile-time only, so runtime-parsed data uses a plain union. EQUIVALENCE with main's scanner: on the exact pre-heal files (manifest.spi rebuilt by reversing the heal program, hash cda88b64 = the original base) the rule reports 28 at the same 28 lines; on the healed tree 0 over 490 packages (node job-1793632486186). Tests 2/2 (self-call cycle, stray ^, mutual pair with a :& member). Census baseline merged for kit_rec_cycle, kit_rec_cycle_api, kit_standards_scan; ratchet 0 regressions.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_4 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 4u32, "2026-11-02T16:04Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 12:04 fiscal HEALED (unstaged): dropped ^ from canon.spi ubl_document_name, child_text, is_group, structure_terms, term_order and lifecycle.spi key_of. Kept visit_element ^ (its :& read_children group is real mutual recursion; main's scanner fix). Node gate t1101 (job-1793635216854-fiscal-rec-heal): canon 1/1 (160 terms, 30 groups), lifecycle 6/6 with both negative tests. canon keeps 10 ^ defs, all self-recursive; lifecycle 0.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_5 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 5u32, "2026-11-02T16:37Z", "main", "main 11-02 12:4x SECOND CORRECTION, a grammar rule: a `^` that OPENS a `:&` group must stay, even when the group has no cycle, because `:&` requires a rec opener. Removing it gives \"Invalid `and` statement\" (regex dfa.spi:151, minimal.spi:29 on the node) and fails every module compiled after that file in the path (main's lib heal type_probe failed json_schema, xsd_regex and xsd_certificate, all from json_schema.spi's json_value_at alone; auto-undone). The scanner now skips group openers too. Of main's heals, 4 were openers: regex dfa state_count, minimal live_after, xsd codes_of (restored to ^) and lib json_schema json_value_at (dropped from the land). Corrected main totals: regex 28, lib 3, cells 1. kit (28) and fiscal (6): re-check yours for a following `:&` line.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_6 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 6u32, "2026-11-02T16:47Z", "main", "main 11-02 12:36 LANDED GREEN (lib_land_window): lib xsd_certificate row_sound + certified_table, xsd_regex add_move, and apps/cells/spi/text.spi take_tilde_word lost their needless ^. Close: signatures unchanged, apps/spiral + apps/wasm compile, document_test 22 passed, type_probe xsd_certificate + xsd_regex PASS. Undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261102-123646. lib json_schema json_value_at keeps ^ (it opens a :& group). Unstaged. Main's remaining share: regex 28 (node proof rerunning).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_7 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 7u32, "2026-11-02T16:50Z", "main", "main 11-02 12:5x regex PROVEN ON THE NODE: 28 needless ^ removed from regex/src (9 files; the 3 :& openers dfa state_count, minimal live_after and xsd codes_of keep ^). build.ps1 on the node: 52 discovered, 52 executed, 52 passed, 0 failed (11 files; sync digest 75D4704E2FE70A2E). Unstaged. Main's share is DONE: regex 28, lib 3, cells 1. Node fix on the way: the node's regex checkout lacked the deps\\spiral link, so main junctioned it to the node's freshly synced C:\\home\\git\\spiral.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_8 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 8u32, "2026-11-03T00:48Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:48 x: x's share VERIFIED 0 in the current tree, so no edit is needed. Method: every ':= ^' and ':~ ^' definition (including ':& :~ ^') in the 73 x/apps .spi files (91 marked) was checked for its own name, with string literals blanked, in its head body and its indented body, and for opening a ':& group'. None is outside a cycle, so the 11-02 count of 'x 5' was healed before now or counted something else. The same scan over Cells spi plus tonight's Cells and lib drafts (23 files, 179 marked) also finds 0, so the new json_value, builder_output, builders, gleam_project and unix_clock code adds none. x has nothing left for this item; the kit standards rule half stays with kit.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_9 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 9u32, "2026-11-03T01:04Z", "main", "main 11-02 20:5x regex CI RED on the user's 17:59 push d7aa16be (gh-pages): src/nullable.spi 1/4, 'TracedError: Pattern miss' on the evidence GADT (3 tests). The node reproduces it under pack18 with core identical to the box. NOT this item's heal: the only nullable.spi change since green fab456a1 is ':~ ^ nullable' -> ':~ nullable', and an in-job A/B (^ restored vs as committed) fails 1/4 in BOTH arms. regex was 52/52 on the node ~12:30 under pack16c, so the suspect is pack17/18 (GADT join points). Sent to compiler with the repro. The other 27 regex heals pass: every other regex file is green in the same gate.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_10 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 10u32, "2026-11-03T03:06Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:2x regex RED RESOLVED under pack20: node core 4E48590A5408C14B, regex nullable.spi 4/4 (3/4 failed under pack18/19). With the earlier full gate (65/68, the 3 being nullable) regex src is 68/68 green on the node; regex CI turns green on the next push now that the compiler fix (GADT-ERASE-ONLY-GROWING, pack20) is in spiral's live source.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_11 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 11u32, "2026-11-03T12:35Z", "x", "2026-11-03 08:35 x: groom: team:x and x tags removed, since x's share is verified 0 (n8) and nothing is left for x. The item stays with main (heals) and kit (the standards rule).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_12 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 12u32, "2026-11-04T06:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:31 fiscal: fiscal's share VERIFIED 0 (11-02 had 7). Method: every top-level ':~ ^' / ':= ^' definition in fiscal src (27 today) is checked for a self-call with identifier boundaries on both sides (so model_census does not count as calling census), on the head line and the body, and for a following ':&' member (a mutual-recursion group); 0 flagged. The scan was validated on a probe (a non-recursive '^' one-liner flagged, a self-recursive one not). As with x (n8), fiscal can drop its tag; the item stays with main (lib/kit/regex heals) and kit (the standards rule).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_13 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 13u32, "2026-11-05T22:39Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:4x HEAL HALF DONE: re-scanned with fiscal's method (a top-level ':~ ^'/':= ^' definition is flagged only when neither its head nor its body calls its own name with identifier boundaries, counting ' and _ as identifier characters, and it isn't in a ':&' group; the body ends at the next column-0 construct, so a following test block can't count as a self-call). Probe-validated: plain one-liner flagged; self-recursive kept; model_census vs census flagged; go vs go' flagged; even/odd group kept; a ^ def called only by a later test flagged. RESULT, 0 flagged everywhere: regex 186 kept (was 33 non-recursive on 11-02), spiral/lib 532 kept (was 22), spiral/apps/cells 171 (was 1), kit/src 661 (was 28); x and fiscal verified 0 by their owners (n8, fiscal 11-04). Drift healed. LEFT: kit's standards rule refusing ^ outside a cycle (this scan's predicate is the spec: self-call by identifier boundary on head+body, or a :& group). Scanner: main's scratchpad rec-scan.ps1 (move to a kit lint verb with the rule).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_14 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 14u32, "2026-11-05T22:41Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:4x: the scanner (the rule's spec) is now durable at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\REC-MARKER-HEAL\\rec-scan.ps1 (-Root <dir>, dry by default; -Apply removes ^ from flagged defs, keeping line endings), not the session scratchpad named in n13.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_15 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 15u32, "2026-11-05T22:46Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:4x REMAINING REPOS (scanner now enumerates via git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard, so it skips deps/ junctions and build output, and fails closed on 0 files; it reproduces regex's 186): x 94 kept, fiscal 38, html 30, dice 4, alphabet 17, blog 13, i574n.github 20: 0 flagged. tibia 133 kept, 1 flagged: src/hunting_pack.spi:1920 ':~ ^ knight_turn_shared ... = knight_turn_inline b t p', non-recursive BY DESIGN. knight_turn's backend_switch calls the _shared one for C and Rust and _inline for Wgsl, so here ^ marks 'emit one shared function, don't inline'. NOT healed. FOR KIT'S RULE: ^ has a second, legitimate use (a non-inlined shared function), so the rule needs an explicit escape (a dedicated no-inline marker, or an allow comment/attribute), not a blanket refusal. A naked refusal would break tibia's C/Rust codegen size choice.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_16 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 16u32, "2026-11-06T12:46Z", "main", "main 11-06 10:5x CENSUS (rec-scan.ps1 from the drafts store, git ls-files based): flagged ^ with no self-call and no :& group: kit 0 (665 kept), regex 0 (186), lib/spiral 0 (535), fiscal 0 (42), x 0 (94), tibia 1 (138), spiral outside lib 68 = apps/compiler 66 (all in tmp/samples contract_* files, terminal_label and kin) + apps/spiral 1 + apps/wasm 1. Was 96 on 11-02, so every lib and product repo is clean. Remaining: the 66 compiler samples (compiler's call: samples feed expected outputs, and ^ is sometimes kept on purpose to emit a shared function rather than inline), plus 3 single sites. DoD: 0 flagged outside sites recorded as deliberate (no-inline) with a reason; each heal compiled on every backend and byte-compared against HEAD. Next step: hand the 66 sample sites to compiler as one batch.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_17 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 17u32, "2026-11-06T12:46Z", "main", "TypeFeatures: none; this removes rec markers and adds no types.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_18 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 18u32, "2026-11-06T18:00Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:0x HEALED the 2 single sites: apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1472 run and apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.spi:38 run lost their needless ^ (each has one call site and no cycle). Proof: the single-flight compiler, --backend Rust, before vs after, gave BYTE-IDENTICAL output (spiral CBD54E65F5E1, 22604 lines; spiral_wasm E10C2BB46AF9, 3726 lines). Rust is the only backend either app builds. Unstaged. Left: the 66 apps/compiler sample sites (compiler's call, a batch) and tibia's knight_turn_shared (deliberate: the no-inline shared function for C/Rust). That makes kit's rule escape necessary.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_19 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 19u32, "2026-11-06T22:25Z", "main", "main 11-06 18:2x RECOUNT (rec-scan over spiral, git ls-files): flagged 66, kept 1661. All 66 are in apps/compiler/tmp/samples, now that main's apps/spiral and apps/wasm heals have landed. HANDED TO COMPILER as one batch: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\REC-MARKER-HEAL\\compiler-samples-flagged-20261106.tsv (path:line name per row). Compiler's call per site: drop the ^ and re-accept that sample's expected outputs, or keep it as a deliberate no-inline shared function, with a reason. Every non-compiler repo is at 0, except tibia's deliberate knight_turn_shared. kit's rule needs the no-inline escape before it can refuse ^ outside a cycle.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_20 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 20u32, "2026-11-08T21:40Z", "org", "Next (org verify 11-08, NOT closeable): 2 gaps remain - (a) compiler owns the 66 apps/compiler/tmp/samples flagged ^ sites (batch tsv in kit drafts), (b) kit standards rule still needs an explicit NO-INLINE escape before it can refuse ^ outside a cycle, because ^ has a legit second use (shared non-inlined fn per backend_switch, e.g. tibia knight_turn_shared). Close only when both land + each heal byte-compares vs HEAD per backend.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_21 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 21u32, "2026-11-09T09:16Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:1x compiler: taking (a), the 66 apps/compiler/tmp/samples ^ sites. Decision rule per site: DROP the ^ when the definition has exactly one call site (inlining one call cannot duplicate code; the ^ is then a pure non-inline request with no sharing benefit) and re-accept the sample; KEEP it when there are 2+ call sites AND the body is non-trivial (deliberate shared non-inlined function -- the no-inline escape kit needs), with the reason written into the batch tsv. Names cluster: terminal_label 23, parallel_terminal 9, multihost_terminal 7, v36_terminal 5, v36b/terminal_row/terminal/final_row/antimirov_insert_unique 2 each, 9 singles (mega erp/zeta/brzozowski). Call-site scan running; then one edit batch + a -Suite all -Accept on a node (re-accept is full-suite only) and a per-backend byte-compare of the changed samples vs HEAD to confirm only the inlined function moves.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_22 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 22u32, "2026-11-09T09:31Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:3x compiler: call-site census of the 66 sites: 57 have exactly ONE call site; 9 have 2-17 (antimirov_insert_unique x2, derivative_*_proof_symbol/suffix x3, erp_p2p_fence_history_value 17 / _owner 13, erp_p2p_physical_owner_lineage_current_owner 2, zeta ..._run_product_value 2), and every one of those 9 bodies is a trivial case projection or a one-line normalize-and-insert, so none is a deliberate shared function. DROPPED all 66 ^ (38 sample files, unstaged in spiral). Validation chain staged on ganymede (~/remote-stage/recheal, starts after the pack70 gate): control = HEAD sources, treatment = healed sources, both -Suite all -Filter <the 38 sample ids> -Native -TimeoutSec 900 with the installed compiler; compares compile/exit/verdict/stdout per row + the largest compile_ms increases (a mega blow-up restores that marker with a reason = the kit no-inline escape case), tars the regenerated outputs, then restores the mirror sources.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_23 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 23u32, "2026-11-09T09:42Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:3x compiler: (a) DONE pending landing -- all 66 ^ dropped (38 files) and the heal is BYTE-IDENTICAL: ganymede control (HEAD sources) vs treatment (healed), -Suite all -Filter <38 ids> -Native, installed compiler: 38 rows, compile-status diffs 0, exit diffs 0, stdout diffs 0, generated residual diffs 0 (largest compile_ms change < 0.9 s, noise). Reason: since pack63 the compiler infers recursion and a ^ on a definition that never refers to itself no longer changes codegen, so no sample needs re-accepting and none needed a no-inline escape. The 38 healed files are unstaged in spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples. (b) remains kits: the explicit no-inline escape; note that the 66-site evidence shows a stray ^ is now codegen-neutral, so the rule can refuse ^ outside a cycle without breaking output -- the escape is only needed if a real no-inline use exists (tibia knight_turn_shared).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_heal_24 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-HEAL", 24u32, "2026-11-09T13:28Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:4x CLOSE. (a) compiler: all 66 apps/compiler/tmp/samples ^ dropped, byte-identical control vs treatment on ganymede (n22), unstaged for the user's push. (b) rig's rule EXISTS and is wired: kit/src/rig_rec_cycle/rec_cycle.spi (139 lines; site/cycle_verdict typed; 3 tests: self-call vs stray mark, mutual recursion + :& members, a group opener stays) is appended to every file's findings by rig_standards_scan::file_findings. The no-inline escape that org's 11-08 verify asked for is NOT needed: compiler's pack63 finding is that a ^ on a self-free definition changes no codegen, and `:~` alone is already the shared non-inlined join point, so ^ carries no no-inline meaning to escape. The only live flagged site is tibia's knight_turn_shared (hunting_pack.spi:2130), which keeps its intent without ^: handed to tibia as TIBIA-KNIGHT-TURN-REC (byte-compare per backend). Proof: rec_cycle.spi tests + scan.spi wiring (read 11-09), compiler's byte-identical run (n22), rec-scan census 0 flagged in every non-compiler repo except that tibia site (n16).")
