inl note_of_physics_out_of_lib_3 () = Note ("PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB", 3u32, "2026-11-09T14:25Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 14:3x MOVE PROVEN ON THE NODE, box land pending a digest match. Census: 0 code consumers of physics in any repo (git grep over 12 repos); its only lib ties were lib/spiral/build.ps1's notebook list and layers.spi's layer_of_physics row (the layers rule checks import direction only). Destination: apps/plot (NOT a new app): plot is the Rust renderer whose run check takes exactly physics's series shape [\"square\",\"x\",\"y\",[...]], and Cells finds the renderer at workspace/target/release/plot, which plot/build.ps1 builds. So: apps/plot/physics.spi (byte-identical, 7BB0E347EB65) + apps/plot/package.spiproj (packageDir ../../lib; |core- spiral-; modules physics) + plot/build.ps1 exports the notebook right after building the renderer and FAILS when the ipynb holds 0 svg (on ganymede, without the renderer, all 6 outputs fell back to \"plot tool not found\" text: environmental, and exactly what that check now catches). Lib drafts (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB): build.ps1 without \"physics\", layers.spi without the row; physics.spi removed via -Remove. Proofs: (1) ganymede job-1794232069853 physics from apps/plot with a lib lacking physics.spi: 43/43; (2) job-1794233594361 lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply: signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26/26 (alphabet + dice staged as siblings; 24/26 without them), type_probe PASS, respell 0, LANDED and closed green, lib digest 93B32F3D47AF5848. Box land: copy-only needs an exact digest; the node tree's lib differs from the box (ignored bench target artifacts; diff running), and lib_land_window's -ProvenLog digest does not exclude -Remove files, so a land with a removal can never match exactly. Next: fix both, then the copy-only box land.")
inl note_of_physics_out_of_lib_4 () = Note ("PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB", 4u32, "2026-11-09T14:35Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 14:3x LANDED on the box, copy-only, DONE. Node proof rerun on an EXACT copy of the box lib (raw digest A2C00E110B93EDD8 both sides; the first proof tree lacked 236 ignored bench/parsing/target artifacts and kept a stale benchmark.spi): ganymede job-1794234587677 lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS, respell 0, LANDED and closed green, lib digest 3649D80B2DB8DA32. Box: lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply with microblog's new -Remove exclusion in Get-LibDigest: \"LANDED from a proven close\" with no fast-check rerun (exact digest), tree-write window held 0.3 s; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-103446. Verified after: lib/spiral/physics.spi gone, apps/plot/physics.spi 7BB0E347EB65 (byte-identical), box lib digest 3649D80B2DB8DA32 = the proof's, no physics left in lib build.ps1/layers.spi. Unstaged: M apps/plot/build.ps1, M lib/spiral/build.ps1, M lib/spiral/layers.spi, D lib/spiral/physics.spi, ?? apps/plot/package.spiproj, ?? apps/plot/physics.spi. Proof: the two logs above. Pages: the published notebook path moves from lib/spiral/physics.spi.* to apps/plot/physics.spi.* (publish globs *.spi.ipynb from the repo root), and plot/build.ps1 now fails if that ipynb holds 0 svg.")
