inl gpu_stacked_runs () = Task ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", "A rehearsed, stacked GPU run queue that saturates one rented L40S for 1-2 h: tibia lane sims (evolution at 100x budget, held-out windows, seed sweeps) plus transformer benchmarks (stories15M/42M/110M tok/s on CUDA and WGSL, the run.c oracle), each dry-run locally on WGSL first, packed so the GPU never idles, results copied back and the instance DELETEd in the same script", Story, P1, D5, 30u32, Active, "TIBIA-GPU-RENTAL", "tibia,transformer,gpu,benchmarks,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gpu_stacked_runs () = Planning ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_1 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:32Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: filed from the user's 11-02 budget rule (TIBIA-GPU-RENTAL n9). DoD: one script that provisions, runs the queue at measured 100% GPU utilization (nvidia-smi sampled throughout), copies results back, DELETEs, and verifies the instance is gone, with the total cost recorded. Before the first rental, the queue's local WGSL dry run predicts at least 60 min of saturated GPU work. Saturation design input: mrakgr's CUDA/UPMEM strategies from the ML-library nugget inventory.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_2 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:07Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, SATURATION PLAN from mrakgr's CUDA work (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md section 7). (1) Probe the device at start (SMs, regs/SM, smem/SM, CC) and size the grid from occupancy (LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES), never a hardcoded GPU. (2) Precompile every sm_89 kernel before renting so no nvcc time is billed. Load weights and sim states with one arena copy from pinned memory (the UPMEM arena lesson). (3) Sims: one sim per thread, the population as a leading dim, resident loops with no host traffic, lockstep ticks with masks, >= 2-4 blocks/SM at <= 128 regs, independent batches on multiple streams, grid sync only for population updates. (4) Inference: batch many sequences on a free batch dim, fuse norm/softmax/sample per row, tensor-core GEMM for prefill and batched decode. (5) Judge 100% by the binding resource: his H100 profile showed 12.5% occupancy yet 80% DRAM (2.69 TB/s) thanks to 16-byte loads. Sample nvidia-smi dmon SM% and DRAM% throughout. The L40S has no thread block clusters. UPMEM gave nothing measured to reuse: one simulated DPU, one tasklet.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_3 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T15:03Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia groom from the star exchange, rules for the rental script. (1) Europa injects SSH keys only at provision: pass sshkey_id in the create call (x-dumps). (2) Use a unique name per transient unit or run, and guard globs under set -e or use a trap, so cleanup and the DELETE always run (x-dumps). (3) Judge the box from outside: confirm the DELETE with a list call, never by the script's exit 0 (resilience/main: a mirror died 19 h while its task reported 0). (4) Keep the space before the host var after any ssh -o (resilience). (5) Pull checkpoints from one client per host and IP; rate limits are per IP (x-dumps).")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_4 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T23:06Z", "tibia", "11-02 19:0x tibia, READINESS CHECK (no rental yet, by the $20-cap rule: rent only when the stacked queue can keep the GPU busy). Ready to stack today: nothing GPU-side has passed parity. (1) Tibia lanes: apps/predict/lanes_gpu.spi compiles to WGSL (59,803 lines); on the node's Quadro the device is lost, on europa lavapipe the pipeline compiles (~9 min on 2 vCPU) and the first run hit the runner's 120 s completion limit (rerun with SPIRAL_WGSL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800 in flight). Lane parity with the C lanes 0-3 is the gate before any rented run. (2) Transformer on GPU: not started. The wgsl-run runner takes only a shader (no input buffers), so a WGSL forward pass needs runner support for a read-only storage buffer (the checkpoint) plus a lib shape for it; CUDA is not started either. (3) CPU-side work that could ride along on a rented box (parallel C transformer, stories110M A/B) waits for pack19 (atomic refc) and the ParamEscape pack. Order to make it rentable: lane parity on lavapipe, a lane throughput number (lanes/s at chunk 1024) so the 1-2 h queue is sized from measurement, then the runner's input-buffer support for the transformer.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_5 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T03:59Z", "tibia", "11-02 23:5x tibia, READINESS UPDATE (still no rental, by the $20-cap rule). Moved since n4: (1) WGSL lane correctness is now PROVEN with a checker, not by luck: the compiler lane's overflow-checking runner and shader (WGSL-LANE-HEAP-OVERFLOW) fail any run whose lanes overflow, and after tibia's two allocation cuts (network decide/inputs without arrays; terrain path windows released by a WGSL heap mark/release) 64 lanes run at the default 1 MB/lane with no overflow and lanes 0-3 equal to C (TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION n13). (2) Throughput on europa lavapipe (2 vCPU, contended): 16 lanes in 3.3 s, 64 lanes in 193 s at load ~2 (tiny plan). Still missing before a rental is worth it: the full 8x64x100 plan's per-lane heap and lanes/s (one long lavapipe run, or the first minutes of the rental itself), the compiler lane's heap fix landing in a pack (so the rented box runs the checked runner), and a transformer GPU path (runner input buffers, TRANSFORMER-GPU n2). Order unchanged: full-plan measurement first, then size the 1-2 h queue from lanes/s.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_6 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T09:12Z", "tibia", "11-03 05:1x tibia, READINESS + AVAILABILITY (no rental). Gaps from n5 that are now closed: full-plan per-lane heap fits the default 1 MB (no overflow) and full-plan lanes equal C (TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION n16; the lib heap_scope shader is byte-identical, n18); sized_array runs on WGSL (LIB-TYPE-SHAPES n11). So tibia lanes alone could saturate a GPU (thousands of independent 1 MB lanes; the sweep's per-lane cost is about 219 s on one C core). Still missing: a measured GPU lanes/s (only a rental can give it; lavapipe 2 lanes = 1,789 s says nothing about an L40S), and the transformer GPU path. AVAILABILITY 09:1xZ via the Cloud-provider API (read-only; key never printed): account credit about 103 USD (balance -103.01, pending 2.08); type=vcg lists 3 plans, vcg-l40s-16c-180g-48vram 1.54 USD/h, vcg-l40s-32c-375g-96vram 3.08 USD/h, vcg-l40s-64c-750g-192vram 6.15 USD/h, and ALL THREE have an empty locations list, so no region offers an L40S on demand now. DECISION: no rental today; recheck availability at the start of the next run window. When a region opens, the first rental is a 1 h, 20-lane-chunk measurement (provision, build the checked runner, full-plan lanes at increasing SPIRAL_WGSL_LANES, nvidia-smi dmon throughout, copy back, DELETE, list to verify) capped at about 2 USD, which sizes the real 1-2 h queue.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_7 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 7u32, "2026-11-03T11:40Z", "tibia", "11-03 07:4x tibia: availability recheck (Cloud-provider API, read-only): all three vcg-l40s plans (1.54 / 3.08 / 6.15 USD/h) still list NO locations; no rental possible. Readiness since n6: the transformer CPU side reached ~97% of llama2.c runfast on 42M/110M (TRANSFORMER-CPU-SPEED n20-n21), and the sized_array/heap_scope WGSL paths are proven on lavapipe, so a rental's first hour can measure tibia lanes/s on real hardware once a region opens.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_8 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 8u32, "2026-11-04T11:29Z", "tibia", "11-04 07:29 tibia, availability recheck (Cloud-provider API, read-only; key from ~/.secrets/europa.env, not printed): type=vcg lists 3 plans and all 3 have NO locations, so still no rental possible, as on 11-03. Readiness grew since n7: lib occupancy now probes a real device through the CUDA driver at run time (LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES slice 5, with a compute-capability fallback for old drivers), so a rental's first minute can print its own launch plan (occupancy::described (planned target (probed 0) kernel)); TRANSFORMER-ZIG-BACKEND gives a third compute backend for the same model. Next check: on the next groom, or when a lane reports a GPU region opening.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_9 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 9u32, "2026-11-04T14:53Z", "tibia", "11-04 10:53 tibia: availability recheck (read-only API, no spend): Europa /v2/plans?type=vcg lists 3 GPU plans and none has a location, so on-demand GPUs are still unavailable on Europa. Spend so far: 0 USD of the 20 USD cap.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_10 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 10u32, "2026-11-04T15:30Z", "tibia", "11-04 11:30 tibia, CONSUMER SLICE IN THE TREE: tibia/apps/predict/gpu_plan.spi (new module, registered in apps/predict/spiral.toml after lanes_gpu; unstaged) is the GPU run's first command: occupancy::probed 0 through the CUDA driver at run time; on Some d it prints the device line and the launch plan of the lanes kernel (64 threads = the WGSL runner's workgroup, smem 0, registers not counted since WGSL reports none), exit 0; on None it prints 'no CUDA device: probed 0 is None', exit 1. Proof: box (Quadro K1100M): 'device sms 2, threads/sm 2048, blocks/sm 16, regs/sm 65536, smem/sm 49152' and 'blocks/sm 16, grid 32, occupancy 50%', exit 0, compiled inside tibia's package (12,826 B C); europa (no GPU), the same C: 'no CUDA device', exit 1. LEFT: the same command on a rented L40S as the first step of GPU-STACKED-RUNS (no Cloud GPU region yet).")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_11 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 11u32, "2026-11-05T02:09Z", "tibia", "11-04 22:09 tibia: WHY NO CLOUD GPU (read-only API + web, no spend). (1) It is not our account: the same queries WITHOUT an API key (GET /v2/plans is public) give the identical result, 3 vcg plans, all NVIDIA L40S (vcg-l40s-16c/32c/64c, 1.671/3.342/6.684 USD/h, deploy_ondemand true, deploy_preemptible false), each with locations: []. (2) GPU bare metal is the same: A100x4, A100x8, H100x8, L40x8, GH200, MI300X, MI325X, MI355X and B200 plans all show 0 locations, while 14 of 15 non-GPU bare-metal plans list 1-24 locations. (3) GET /v2/regions/{id}/availability?type=vcg returns available_plans [] in ewr, ord, lax, sjc, atl, ams, fra and sea, both with and without a key, while ?type=vbm in ewr returns non-GPU metal. (4) The fractional A16/A40/A100 cloud GPU plans are gone from the catalog entirely, not just empty. (5) External trackers agree: GetDeploying lists Europa's L40S out of stock in all configurations, checked 11-03 and 11-04. No Europa statement explains it; Europa's API reference and product pages answer 403 to automated fetches, and docs.europa.com describes a normal console flow with no access step. CONCLUSION: on-demand GPU capacity on Europa is currently zero for everyone through the public API; it is a supply state, not an account gate we can lift with a parameter. Options: keep the read-only recheck; ask Europa sales about reserved or contract capacity (needs the user, it is an outward contact); or the user decides on another provider, which the 11-02 rental permission does not cover.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_12 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 12u32, "2026-11-05T05:03Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:03 tibia: availability recheck (anonymous GET /v2/plans?type=vcg and /v2/plans-metal): still 3 L40S cloud plans and 9 GPU metal plans, every one with 0 locations. No rental possible; the queue keeps growing on CPU meanwhile (node runs offspring per thread at 3.2x on 8 threads, TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION).")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_13 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 13u32, "2026-11-06T10:10Z", "tibia", "GPU parked 11-06 06:10 tibia (close-ratio groom): this will not close this week. Europa lists 0 GPU locations on every plan (LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES is Blocked), and the $20 rental can't start. Unpark when a GPU location appears.")
