inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_17 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 17u32, "2026-11-07T19:24Z", "tibia", "11-07 15:2x tibia: pause re-checked, stays Paused. Reason: Europa's public plan list (GET https://api.europa.com/v2/plans?type=vcg, no key) still shows 0 locations on all 3 GPU plans (L40S 16c/32c/64c) at 15:2x, so the $20 rental cannot start. Resume when: a vcg plan lists a location.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_18 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 18u32, "2026-11-09T03:16Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:1x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused. Reason: the provider refused every rental on 11-08 (deposit, monthly fee limit, no GPU locations). The user then shelved the CPU rental and said a GPU rental may go OUTSIDE that provider later. A non-provider GPU is a direction, not a permission (gpu-rental-permission). Resume when: the user names the GPU provider, cap and account, OR the current provider lists a GPU location and its account gates (deposit, fee limit) admit a $20 run.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_19 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 19u32, "2026-11-09T21:01Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:0x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused. Reason: unchanged since 11-08. The user shelved the CPU rental and named no GPU provider; a non-provider GPU is a direction, not a permission. Resume when: the user names a GPU provider, cap and account.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_20 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 20u32, "2026-11-10T07:47Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:5x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused, with the reason CORRECTED. The standing user permission (memory gpu-rental-permission, 11-02) still covers Vultr GPUs up to $20; what blocks is stock, not a missing provider. An anonymous recheck now (GET /v2/plans?type=vcg and /v2/plans-metal, no key): 3 cloud GPU plans and 9 bare-metal GPU plans, 0 with any location, the same as on 11-04. A non-Vultr GPU is still a direction, not a permission (user 11-08). Resume when: a Vultr GPU plan lists a location in the anonymous query, or the user names another provider, cap and account.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_21 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 21u32, "2026-11-10T10:41Z", "tibia", "11-10 06:4x tibia GPU PROVIDER SURVEY (user asked: browse from the Edge extension and find clouds that rent GPUs autonomously by API key, like Vultr, with price ranges). Research only: nothing signed up, nothing rented. Read through Edge from each provider's own pricing page; Vast.ai from its public offer API. On-demand USD per GPU-hour, read 11-10: RunPod (REST/GraphQL API + runpodctl, per-second billing): A40 0.59, L40S 1.09, A100 PCIe/SXM 1.79, H100 PCIe 2.89, H100 NVL 3.19, H100 SXM 3.99, H200 5.29, B200 7.99. Vast.ai (marketplace, CLI + API; anonymous sample of 64 verified offers, so indicative): RTX 3090 0.21, RTX 4090 0.49-0.61, RTX 5090 0.50-0.67, A100 0.43-1.14, H100 PCIe 2.85-3.53, H100 SXM 3.84, B200 about 12. Hyperstack (API): A4000 0.15, A6000 0.50, L40 1.00, A100 1.35-1.60, H100 2.50, H100 SXM 3.20, H200 3.99, B200 6.00 (spot from 0.40 for A6000). TensorDock (marketplace API): RTX 4090 from 0.35, A100 SXM from 1.80, H100 SXM from 2.25. Lambda (API; list prices from 11-16, the 1x tab showed the same per-GPU rates): V100 0.79, A100 40GB 1.99, A100 80GB 3.19, H100 4.59, B200 7.69. DigitalOcean GPU Droplets (API + doctl): RTX 4000 Ada 0.76, L40S 1.57, RTX 6000 Ada 1.57, MI300X 2.59, H100 4.41, H200 4.47; spot B300 6.17. The user's DO key (saved 11-10 in ~/.secrets/digitalocean.env) sees NO GPU sizes, so GPU access must be enabled on the account first, and the droplet limit is 3. Verda, formerly DataCrunch (API): A6000 0.85, RTX 6000 Ada 1.54, L40S 1.98, A100 80GB 2.32, H100 5.04, H200 6.44. Not read: getdeploying.com's aggregator (Cloudflare bot check, not bypassed). For this item's 1-2 h saturated runs, the cheapest fits are RunPod L40S 1.09 or A100 1.79, Hyperstack A100 1.35, and Vast or TensorDock RTX 4090 about 0.35-0.6 for the transformer benches; H100-class is 2.25-4.60. A non-Vultr provider still needs the user's yes (provider, cap, account; memory gpu-rental-permission). Resume when: the user names a provider, cap and account, or Vultr GPU stock returns.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_22 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 22u32, "2026-11-10T11:06Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:1x tibia: RESUMED. The resume condition is met: the user named the provider (RunPod), gave the account key (~/.secrets/runpod.env) and authorized up to the  balance today (user 11-10: pick the best GPU for tibia and transformer work no matter the price; it becomes fleet node 12, reused on and off for weeks; settle in, run the full CPU+GPU nodebench, turn off, record cost and time; rehearse in k3s first). In flight: a nodebench GPU build in an ubuntu:22.04 k3s pod on ganymede (job tibia-nb12-build), the rental runner draft (drafts\\tibia\\GPU-RUNPOD-K3S-REHEARSAL\\runner.sh + pod-bench.sh), and org3 asked how row 12 joins the rating. GPU: H200 SXM, community cloud (.59/h; secure has no H200 stock), falling back to H100 SXM secure (.99/h). Next step: after the build is green and org3 answers (or 30 min pass), create the pod with a box-side stop watchdog, run pod-bench.sh, pull and verify the results, stop the pod, and record cost and duration.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_23 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 23u32, "2026-11-10T11:25Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:2x tibia FIRST RENTAL DONE (RunPod, user-authorized): node 12 'titan' (provisional), pod fsouc1ubw5nyrp, H200 SXM 141GB, SECURE cloud .29/h, IS. The H200 community offer at .59 had no instance with a public IP. TIMELINE: create 11:14:02Z; container up about 11:14:11; SSH published by 11:16:25 (first poll); upload of nodebench 5.5MB plus the script, and the run started 11:17:24 (42 s); the software-GPU guard aborted the first pass at 11:17:4x (llvmpipe); Vulkan debugging 11:18-11:20:50 (the NVIDIA ICD is present but vkCreateInstance is refused, also with the LunarG 1.4.313 loader, so no Vulkan on this pod); the CPU passes plus CUDA ran 11:20:53-11:21:13 (20 s: 3 idle nodebench, 1 saturated, a torch microbench); results pulled and sha-verified (64ac516b3e34) in 31 s; podStop at 11:23:27 = 9 min 25 s, about .83. Stopped, not terminated: the 20GB volume keeps billing .006/h for reuse. Balance 15 -> 14.50 so far (billing may lag). Watchdog: a detached pwsh process that stops the pod at T+58 min was armed, then disarmed by file after the manual stop; both watchdogs exited. RESULTS: CPU quota 10.2 of 96 Xeon 8568Y+ cores; idle best ST 47.07 ms, MT 51.82 ms, MEM 19.64 GB/s, DWR 3452 MB/s, DSYNC 0.156 ms, DIOPS 15512. CUDA (torch 2.4.1+cu124): bf16 matmul 813.9 TFLOPS, fp32 51.5 TFLOPS, HBM copy 4301 GB/s. Raw lines sent to org3 for the 12-node re-rate (GPU dimension NOT MEASURED, CUDA as unranked annotations). LESSONS for the next rental: (1) container env is NOT in SSH sessions (read /proc/1/environ); (2) datacenter Hopper exposes no Vulkan here, so GPU work must use CUDA, which means the WGSL lanes path needs a CUDA backend or another provider image; (3) 9 of the 9.4 billed minutes were setup and debugging, against 20 s of work, so the next rental should run a k3s-rehearsed runner with a CUDA probe first. Next step: after org3 posts the re-rated table, plan the CUDA path for tibia lanes and the transformer, rehearsed in k3s before the next rental.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_24 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 24u32, "2026-11-10T11:30Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:3x tibia: NODE 12 RATED (org3, relay-lab/bench/scores.tsv; backup scores.tsv.bak-before-titan-20261110). titan is #2 of 12 at 918.9 (par 1000, the new fleet max from its 10-core MT 51.82 ms; sgl 903, mem 880, disk 865; gpu omitted, because GPU_CLASS=software fails rate.ps1's discrete|integrated gate, and the rating renormalizes over the 4 measured dimensions). New order: jupiter 930.5, titan 918.9, venus 725.1, ganymede 614.3, europa 595.0, neptune 580.7, pluto 449.7, mercury 431.1, saturn 388.9, comet 358.6, moon 241.1, earth 171.7. The CUDA fields are recorded as unranked annotations (bf16 813.9 TFLOPS is the transformer-relevant figure, not the 918.9). Next step: after the next CUDA-path rehearsal in k3s, restart this stopped pod (fsouc1ubw5nyrp) for the first stacked tibia/transformer run.")
inl note_of_gpu_stacked_runs_25 () = Note ("GPU-STACKED-RUNS", 25u32, "2026-11-10T13:09Z", "tibia", "11-10 09:0x tibia: rentals 2 and 3 (detail on TIBIA-LANES-CUDA notes 5-6). Resuming the stopped node-12 pod FAILED (pinned to a host whose GPUs are now taken); a fresh H100 hung 19 min with no container (terminated, .26 lost); a scripted retry (create, wait with a 6 min abort, upload, run, terminate, verify) ran the CUDA probe OK on an H100 in 95 s for .11. The scripted one-unit rental is now the pattern, and reuse should go through a network volume, not a stopped pod. Balance 12.73. Next step: after the lanes CUDA kernel passes its k3s rehearsal, run the stacked lanes rental with this scripted pattern.")
inl transformer_oracle () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-ORACLE", "Transformer oracle first: pin llama2.c (commit), stories15M/42M/110M checkpoints and tokenizer.bin as CI downloads (never committed), and record run.c greedy outputs (tokens plus fp32 logits per step) as typed Spiral row modules; the first test diffs against ./run stories15M.bin -t 0", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "transformer,benchmarks,oracle,team:tibia,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_oracle () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-ORACLE", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl transformer_cpu_reference () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-CPU-REFERENCE", "Transformer CPU reference: fp32 forward pass (embedding, rmsnorm, RoPE, multi-head attention with KV cache, SwiGLU FFN, softmax, greedy and top-p sampling) in spiral/apps/transformer over the lib shape core, token-identical to run.c on stories15M/42M/110M on C and Rust", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "TRANSFORMER-ORACLE", "transformer,lib,typefeatureset,team:tibia,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_cpu_reference () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-CPU-REFERENCE", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl transformer_tokenizer () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-TOKENIZER", "Typed BPE tokenizer for llama2.c tokenizer.bin: vocab scores, merge-based encode, decode with byte fallback; identical token ids to run.c encode on a fixed prompt set", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TRANSFORMER-ORACLE", "transformer,team:tibia,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_tokenizer () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-TOKENIZER", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl transformer_checkpoint_load () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-CHECKPOINT-LOAD", "Load llama2.c checkpoints by reflection over a typed config/weights record (the S5 idea): header to config, weight tensors as typed views over one mmap or read buffer, shared-classifier flag, with no per-field hand parsing", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TRANSFORMER-ORACLE,LIB-BINARY-IO", "transformer,typefeatureset,team:tibia,tibia", "current", "current")
