inl note_of_transformer_gpu_1 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-GPU", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:42Z", "tibia", "Filed 11-02 by tibia under TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB (n4, from the original deliberation, share eab494f1). Reuses tibia's WGSL pipeline. GPU spend comes out of the 20 USD cap (TIBIA-GPU-RENTAL).")
inl note_of_transformer_gpu_2 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-GPU", 2u32, "2026-11-02T23:13Z", "tibia", "11-02 19:1x tibia, prerequisite found for the WGSL half: the native runner (spiral apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/wgsl-run/src/main.rs, wgpu 30) takes only `spiral-wgsl <file.wgsl>`; it binds three read-write storage buffers it creates itself (SpiralIo code + lanes, and the spiral_heap words) and loads no input data, so a forward pass cannot get the checkpoint. Needed: an optional read-only storage binding filled from a file (e.g. `SPIRAL_WGSL_INPUT=<path>` -> binding 3, `array<u32>` words, f32 by bitcast), plus the lib/compiler side that names that binding from Spiral (an input array of the WGSL backend). Owner of the runner: the compiler lane (native shims). The WGSL lane path itself is proven on lavapipe (TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION n6: C and WGSL lanes bit-identical), so this binding is the only missing piece for a WGSL transformer.")
