inl note_of_compiler_simd_codegen_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:42Z", "tibia", "Filed 11-02 by tibia under TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB (n4, from the original deliberation, share eab494f1). The deliberation's only line: 'desempenho depende de BLAS/SIMD'. Design input: the Mojo study and mrakgr's CUDA tiling (nugget inventory).")
inl note_of_compiler_simd_codegen_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN", 2u32, "2026-11-02T21:23Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, design input from TRANSFORMER-MOJO-STUDY (done; report mojo-zig-study.md in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102). Shape to build: (1) a lane vector whose width is a type literal, default 16 f32 (Mojo measured wider as slower on 288-wide rows), lowered to gcc vector extensions in C (`typedef float v16 __attribute__((vector_size(64)))`, portable across SSE/AVX2/AVX-512), std::simd or chunked arrays in Rust, vec4 groups in WGSL; (2) lane-wise mul-add + horizontal reduce + scalar tail as lib functions over it; (3) several independent accumulators (zig uses 8, 4 when fused) to break the FMA chain; (4) fused matmul over a type-level output count (QKV n=3, w1/w3 n=2) as an inl recursion over the type literal, in lib. GATE CHANGE: reordered float sums mean greedy byte-identity with run.c is no longer required; the gate is the logits script (max abs diff <= 1e-4, equal non-zero counts), the same one runfast/-Ofast already passes.")
inl note_of_compiler_simd_codegen_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN", 3u32, "2026-11-02T23:05Z", "tibia", "11-02 19:0x tibia, NEGATIVE RESULT for source-level accumulators (node job transformer-acc-1, stories15M, gcc -O3 -march=native, no fast-math, node at 100% load): a dot4 join point with 4 independent f32 chains plus a scalar tail (scratch variant of apps/transformer) keeps greedy tokens identical on stories260K and stories15M, but is not faster: rounds run-O3 / spiral-c (current) / spiral-acc = 7,428/7,463/7,553, 6,775/7,175/8,562, 8,089/8,406/8,867 ms. gcc still sees a generic while(1) self-loop, not a counted loop it can vectorize, so ILP from explicit chains alone does not pay; the lever stays real vector codegen (this item's vector type) or -Ofast. Also confirms the reordered-sum tokens can stay identical on these checkpoints, which supports the logits-gate plan in n2.")
inl note_of_compiler_simd_codegen_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-SIMD-CODEGEN", 4u32, "2026-11-07T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (lint markers). DoD: a typed vector-lane type with width as a type literal lowered to C vector extensions, Rust std::simd and WGSL vec4, a golden test per backend, and matmul in lib written on it. Next step: wait for TRANSFORMER-TYPED-SIMD-DOT's measurement (the auto-vectorized lib form); start this only if it leaves a gap to llama2.mojo. TypeFeatures: lanes as a type-level literal; a width that does not divide the row is a compile error.")
