inl cells_typed_units () = Task ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", "Cells on typed-units/1: split apps/cells/spi (8 files, 2,334 lines) into link: units so no unit generates more than 1000 lines. Today the domain is ONE generated module, src/spiral_cells/domain.gleam, at 18,622 lines (1.05 MB). Units: cells_model (types only: text, document, directives, cell, targets, the daemon protocol GADT), cells_boundary (the only home of host code: Erlang/Kino/OS externals, today text.spi's 5 host macros), cells_feature (notebook, memo, runner, mounts, daemon/pool processes), cells_beam (Gleam bin: the BEAM runtime and Kino facades) and cells_cli (Rust bin: the C11 CLIs). Exports are monomorphic: request r stays inside cells_model, and the boundary exports one concrete function per reply type or an existential. Retire the single domain.gleam and never use x's post-hoc text splitter. DoD: every unit at most 1000 generated lines, the typefeatureset census never down from the 11-02 baseline, and the Cells suite equal before and after", Story, P1, D5, 30u32, Active, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS,LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS", "team:microblog,cells,cells-in-spiral,linked-units,typefeatureset,line-gate", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_typed_units () = Planning ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_1 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:58Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:58 x: added by the 10-min groom (user: check that Cells modeling nails the typefeatureset, the Gleam/Rust/iggy balance, and the new 1k split model). BASELINE census of apps/cells/spi at 2026-11-02 09:58: unions 29, GADT cases 10 (daemon 6, cell 3, directives 1), records 7, forall 4, existentials 0, nominal/phantom 0, prototypes 0. Tab-wire sites 32 (daemon codec 17, document 8; expected until the Elixir callers go), 0/1 flags 14, host macros 5 (text.spi).")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_2 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. From compiler n13 and kit n8: pack16 writes <stem>.unit.json beside each exporting .spi; an importer of an unbuilt link: unit fails \"build X first\"; and staged regen must carry .unit.json back with the .rs. So build units in link: order, and the Cells build carries unit.json. Per the user's no-outputs-in-repo rule (memory derive-baselines-not-stored), unit.json belongs in a build dir; a gitignore is only the interim. x asked compiler about the location in its star-exchange message.")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_3 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T13:14Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 09:2x microblog, CPU-light design step (reads only). (1) SIZE NOW: generated apps/cells/src/spiral_cells/domain.gleam (gitignored) is 37,002 lines / 1.94 MB, double the 18,622 at filing; 528 fns, 100 types. (2) THE UNIT SPLIT ALONE CANNOT MEET THE 1000-LINE GATE: single generated functions exceed it: spi_walk_65 1966 lines (document.spi:858, a 32-line source), parse_tokens_366 1599 (builders.spi), open_step_67 1207 (document.spi:798), search_top_9 1126 (cell.spi), cluster_371 950 (builders), walk_99 932, test_block_go_62 866 (document), code_at_339 741. Cause for spi_walk: := inliners. close_mode (document.spi:779) inlines code_cell 4 times plus doc_cell and test_cell_of, and spi_walk expands those at 5 sites (inside it: find_from_1 x33, rev_rows x13, join_rows x10). So STEP 0 = join points before units (memory join-points-shrink-generated, size-every-inliner). Draft A (not applied; the tree is shared and a red Cells blocks every lane): code_cell, doc_cell, test_cell_of and close_mode go from := to :~. Patch at drafts/i574n.github/CELLS-TYPED-UNITS/document.spi; base sha256 915571ac21b7a1f, 4-line diff. Same audit next for parse_tokens/cluster (builders.spi) and search_top (cell.spi). (3) REFERENCE GRAPH (qualified uses, files under apps/cells/spi): a star around text. cell->text 76, directives->text 24 + cell 3, document->text 178, notebook->text 40 + cell 4, targets->text 4, daemon->text 11, client->daemon 11 + text 1, memo->text 34, source_blocks->text 11 + memo 3, verdicts->text 5, manifest->text 32, source_map->text 16, json_value->text 8, builder_output->text 13, builders->text 26 + json_value 6 + builder_output 2, html_markdown->none. No cycles, so the units fall out as: base (text) <- model (cell, directives, targets, daemon protocol) <- features (document, notebook, memo, source_blocks, verdicts, manifest, source_map, json_value, builder_output, builders, gleam_project, mount_text, run_result) <- cli/beam bins. next: prove draft A on a node mirror (regen domain.gleam, measure spi_walk, run the Cells suite), then the builders/cell audit.")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_4 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T13:14Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "dod: every generated Cells module (domain units) is at most 1000 lines with no function over the gate (join points first, then link: units base/model/features/bins as in note 3), the Cells suite is green on a node at the same pass count as before, and x client + sim verifies stay green on the new Cells. typefeatures: the units follow the existing unions/GADTs (cell kinds, daemon protocol GADT); join points change only generated shape, never the types.")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_5 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T13:19Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 09:3x microblog: STEP 0 drafts complete, and the proof is staged on moon (C:/home/remote-stage/joinpts). Drafts B and C add to A: builders.spi apply_flag := -> :~ (it inlines optional/one/deps/cleanup_flag, expanded 3x in cluster and 2x via long_step/short_step into parse_tokens: quoted_from/printable_from/bytes_from x6 there); text.spi starts_at and is_value_binding := -> :~ (starts_at is inlined at every starts_with, about 1000 sites org-wide in Cells; search_top shows skip_spaces x14); cell.spi declaration and binding_keyword := -> :~ (12 starts_with each, inlined into search_top). Total 9 one-token changes in 4 files, none applied to the tree. PROOF SCRIPT cells-joinpoints-ab.ps1: a fresh copy of cellsmd1's spiral lib + apps/cells at C:/home/remote/cellsju1. Two arms, base (the box's current apps/cells/spi) and joined (base + the 4 drafts). Each arm regenerates domain.gleam via mix compile, measures total lines, fn count, fns over 1000 and the top 12, then runs builders_test, cell_test, directives_test, document_test and targets_test. Expect joined: same test results, spi_walk/parse_tokens/search_top/cluster far below 1000, a smaller domain.gleam. Placement: moon's order is TRAIN42e, then compiler's post-train window, then org2 REGEX-LIB-3 and my sim verify; this A/B goes after those, as a plain job in a free slot.")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_6 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T23:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 18:4x moon after-sim (job-1794264025297-x-night-chain), JOIN-POINT A/B on the Cells spi drafts (drafts store i574n.github/CELLS-TYPED-UNITS, run joinpts/run-20261109184026): generated Gleam 37,008 lines (base) -> 30,269 (joined), -18.2%; the largest definition parse_tokens 1,599 -> 473 lines. Both arms compile (exit 0). Both arms fail the SAME 3 tests, all mirror gaps not caused by either arm: DocumentTest dice + alphabet corpus (that mirror's Cells predates the :dice_corpus/:alphabet_corpus tags) and the CLI export (spiral CLI not built there). Equal red sets = no regression from join points. NEXT STEP: land the 4 join-point drafts (document, builders, text, cell .spi) into apps/cells/spi after a box-tree diff against their .base copies (the base may have moved since).")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_7 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T23:09Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 19:1x microblog: JOIN POINTS LANDED in the box tree (unstaged): apps/cells/spi/{document,builders,text,cell}.spi replaced by the drafts after each .base was checked equal to the live file (so the drafts sit on the current tree, including today's text.spi flattening). Proof = the moon A/B in n6 (both arms compile; identical mirror-gap test reds; generated Gleam -18.2%). Shas: document 41a25c204a61, builders 607406bd109d, text d708251558c9, cell 4dc8a6fceab4; 0 lines over 120. The generated src/spiral_cells/domain.gleam is gitignored and regenerates on the next Cells compile, so nothing committed drifts. NEXT STEP: the next node Cells run (any lane) recompiles the domain; read its gleam line count to confirm the ~30.3k figure on the box tree, then continue typed units (link: units split) from this smaller base.")
inl note_of_cells_typed_units_8 () = Note ("CELLS-TYPED-UNITS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T09:39Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:4x GROOM: the 4 join-point drafts are landed; the remaining measurement (gleam line count of the recompiled domain) needs the next node Cells notebook run, which compiles the domain (todays europa mix test run does not). Wait row: when:next-node-cells-notebook-run.")
inl lib_type_shapes () = Task ("LIB-TYPE-SHAPES", "lib: type-level shapes for every backend: type_arith (add/sub/mult/div/divup over type literals, plus nominal_recreate normalization), length-indexed static arrays sa n el (scan, tree reduce typed sa (divup n 2), merge : sa a -> sa b -> sa (add a b)) and tuple_list n el, backend-neutral (C/Rust/WGSL/Lua arms), with tlit for literal configs and a dim_of shape witness", Story, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,typefeatureset,transformer,tibia,team:tibia", "current", "current")
