inl lib_tensor_views () = Task ("LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS", "lib: struct-of-arrays tensors with type-level dims and a zero-cost compile-time view algebra (zip, unzip, rezip, reorder, apply, view, split, flatten, reshape, factorize, apply_proj), bounds checks that are type errors when index and size are literals and runtime only for dynamic dims, and reorder proven by term-var set equality", Story, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-TYPE-SHAPES,COMPILER-TYPE-ARITH-NORMALIZE", "lib,typefeatureset,transformer,tibia,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_tensor_views () = Planning ("LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_tensor_views_1 () = Note ("LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:03Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md section 2 (tensorm/tensor_main.spi:4-409, tensorm/utils.spir:4-22, real_core assert_term_vars_are_equal_under_set_equality:133-146, factorize_sizeof_16 at :277). The ML library's version had Python/CUDA arms only (apply_ptr:139-142); this one needs C/Rust/WGSL first.")
inl note_of_lib_tensor_views_2 () = Note ("LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (lint markers). DoD: struct-of-arrays tensors with type-level dims and the view algebra (zip, reorder, split, flatten, reshape) with compile-error tests for mismatched literals. Next step: blocked in practice on TYPE-ARITH-3's redesign (computed dims); until then views with literal dims only. TypeFeatures: dims as type-level literals; reorder proven by term-var set equality.")
inl lib_arena_planner () = Task ("LIB-ARENA-PLANNER", "lib: typed static memory planning: partitions over byte arenas (*. side by side, +. overlapping for phase reuse), 16-byte and element-size alignment, typed tensor views from (ptr, size), one arena per memory space (spaces as a union, never int ids), liveness-based scratch reuse, and one bulk copy per arena", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS", "lib,transformer,tibia,gpu,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_arena_planner () = Planning ("LIB-ARENA-PLANNER", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_arena_planner_1 () = Note ("LIB-ARENA-PLANNER", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:03Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md sections 2 (partitionm.spi:1-126), 1.1 (pass_calculate_partitions layers.spi:124-169, space ids :6-12), 1.3 (overlapping smem partition kernel.spi:32-38) and 7.2 (UPMEM: one 64 MiB MRAM arena, 8-byte-aligned offsets, args from free_vars). New: liveness reuse (the library gave every intermediate its own slot) and a persistent KV-cache space.")
inl note_of_lib_arena_planner_2 () = Note ("LIB-ARENA-PLANNER", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (lint markers). DoD: a lib partition type over byte arenas with alignment, typed views from (ptr, size), liveness-based reuse, and golden tests on C and Rust that views never overlap when live. Next step: wait for LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS (its dep); meanwhile list the transformer's buffers with their lifetimes as the first fixture. TypeFeatures: memory spaces as a union, partitions as *. and +. type operators, views typed by their element and sized dims.")
inl lib_op_graph () = Task ("LIB-OP-GRAPH", "lib: typed op graph: a GADT indexed by each node's output tensor type with the kernel hidden in an existential, shape checking by types instead of asserts, a layout pass on LIB-ARENA-PLANNER, separate extract (views) and run (emit) interpreters, typed nominal keys with exactly-one extraction, a layer_filter union, an output placement union (Fresh | Into) instead of op_/op'/op triples, per-layer init closures, phantom-tagged checkpoint handles, and an ensemble/batch dim kept free of the launch shape", Feature, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-ARENA-PLANNER", "lib,typefeatureset,transformer,tibia,team:tibia", "current", "current")
