inl lib_device_capabilities () = Task ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", "lib/compiler: a probed device capability record (SMs, regs/SM, smem/SM, warp size, compute capability, threads/SM), an occupancy calculator, and a compile-time tile planner parameterized by it, replacing hardcoded GPU unions", TaskKind, P1, D4, 90u32, Blocked, "", "lib,compiler,gpu,transformer,tibia,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_device_capabilities () = Planning ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_1 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md sections 3 (corecuda/base.spi:6-53 hardcoded gpu() = RTX5080), 1.2 (frame/frame_iter :17-33), 1.3 (max_blocks_per_sm.py formula) and failure 12 (H100 move needed source edits). Feeds GPU-STACKED-RUNS: print device, grid, regs and smem once at start and fail fast below the occupancy target.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_2 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:07Z", "tibia", "11-03 11:3x tibia, SLICE 1 DRAFTED (drafts spiral LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES occupancy.spi, new lib module, not in live lib). Typed records per_sm {threads; blocks; regs; smem}, device {sms; per_sm; smem_per_block; smem_reserved}, kernel {threads; regs per thread; smem per block}. Presets by compute capability: cc_89 (1536 threads, 24 blocks, 65536 regs, 100 KB smem per SM) for rtx4060 (24 SMs) and l40s (142 SMs); cc_90 (2048, 32, 65536, 228 KB) for h100_sxm (132 SMs); per-block smem 99 KB / 227 KB, 1 KB reserved per block. Occupancy goes beyond the ML library formula (max_blocks_per_sm.py): registers allocated per warp in units of 256, smem in 128-byte units plus the per-block reserve, threads rounded to warps, and fits (threads 1..1024, regs <= 255, smem <= per-block limit) gives 0 blocks. API: blocks_per_sm, occupancy_percent, grid (persistent grid = sms x blocks). 4 C tests (h100 48 KB -> 4 blocks, 50 percent; rtx4060 42 regs -> 10 not the naive 12; over-limit smem -> 0; l40s grid 852). europa probe: all 5 values right, and the whole calculation folds at compile time (133-byte C main), so a compile-time tile planner can take it as a parameter. Mutant (no 256-register rounding): probe fails as it should. NEXT: node lib gate with package.spiproj = live + occupancy, round trip, lib_land_window; then slice 2 = probe a real device (cudaGetDeviceProperties) into the same record, slice 3 = corecuda gpu() union replaced by a device value.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_3 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T15:26Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:0x tibia: slice 1 (occupancy.spi 070EE8AF0F83) GATED on the node mirror: positive 4/4, 0 type errors, cell budget 0 findings; mutant (no 256-register rounding) fails exactly registers_are_allocated_per_warp_in_units_of_256; lib_roundtrip canonical true fixpoint true (draft bytes = canonical). Lands after file_system (land running). SLICE 2 drafted in drafts LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES slice2: typed launch record {blocks_per_sm; grid; occupancy}, launch d k, and planned target d k which fails fast when the kernel cannot launch or sits below the occupancy target (the GPU-STACKED-RUNS start-of-run check). Tests: a_plan_at_its_target (h100 -> 4, 528, 50) and a fails test below target 75. europa probe: at-target exit 0 (folded to a 133-byte main), below-target exits 1 with the message.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_4 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:47Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:4x tibia, SLICE 1 LANDED via lib_land_window (new file + package.spiproj line after keyed_rng, base 8FB24F8AD13A): occupancy.spi 070EE8AF0F83, package.spiproj now 2BF4B4159278; closed green: apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe occupancy PASS (4 tests typed, 0 errors), 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-113740. Unstaged for the user. Slice 2 (launch record, meets, planned): first node gate showed fails tests are COMPILE-error tests in Cells (README Expected compile errors), so a run-time failwith cannot be tested that way; reworked to a pure meets predicate tested directly, planned keeps the fail-fast failwith; re-gate running (occ-gate-3).")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_5 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T16:20Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:4x tibia, SLICE 2 LANDED (base 070EE8AF0F83 -> C9A8E50BB549): launch record {blocks_per_sm; grid; occupancy}, launch d k, meets target l, planned target d k (fail-fast). Closed green: consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 6 tests typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-121449. The first try was undone at close for one respell-drift finding (false must be written !-), memory lib-respell-bool-literals. Next slices: probe a real device (cudaGetDeviceProperties) into a device record, then feed GPU-STACKED-RUNS (print launch once at start, planned with the occupancy target).")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_6 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T20:43Z", "tibia", "11-03 16:4x tibia, SLICE 3 LANDED (described : launch -> string, e.g. blocks/sm 4, grid 528, occupancy 50%, the one line GPU-STACKED-RUNS prints at start): occupancy C9A8E50BB549 -> E69324077D19 and package.spiproj moved occupancy after sm_operators (it now opens sm_operators; the first node gate was VOID with Unbound module sm_operators, the define-before-use order trap); package re-derived from live at land time (82E29239D38D, another lane had landed meanwhile) -> E11B322C8801. Node gate: positive 7/7, 0 type errors, budget 0; mutant fails exactly the register-rounding test. Close green: consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 7 typed, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-163038.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_7 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:09Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:09 tibia, SLICE 4 DRAFTED (drafts LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES v4, base E69324077D19): the typed model of a device probe. A union attribute (Sms, ThreadsPerSm, BlocksPerSm, RegsPerSm, SmemPerSm, SmemPerBlock, SmemReserved), cuda_code mapping each one to its cudaDeviceAttr value, and device_from (query : attribute -> i32) : device. A real GPU becomes device_from (cudaDeviceGetAttribute on ordinal 0 . cuda_code), and the planner never sees raw attribute numbers. The codes 16/39/106/82/81/97/111 are VERIFIED against NVIDIA's own header (driver_types.h in the nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12 12.9.79 wheel, lines 1937-2025, unzipped on europa). NVIDIA's API page lists the enumerators without values. Tests: a_probed_device_is_built_from_its_attribute_answers (c, rust: device_from rtx4060_answers = rtx4060 (), and its launch prints blocks/sm 10, grid 240, occupancy 83%) and each_attribute_asks_its_own_cuda_code (c). respell-drift 0. The europa --check was VOID (30 s attestation cap, europa at load 8 from other lanes). Proof goes to the node gate tibia-pk7-occ4-gate-1 (mutant: per_sm_from reads SmemPerBlock for smem), queued after tibia-zig-gate-1. NEXT after the land: the C binding cuda_query ordinal a via cudaDeviceGetAttribute, proven on the first GPU box (rental or the box's rtx4060), feeding GPU-STACKED-RUNS.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_8 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T05:47Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:47 tibia, SLICE 4 LANDED (base E69324077D19 -> 52430D9393A9): attribute union + cuda_code (codes checked against NVIDIA driver_types.h 12.9.79) + device_from. Proof: box gate in a test-suite window on a scratch lib (-Compiler process), positive 9/9 with 0 type errors; mutant (per_sm_from reads SmemPerBlock for smem) fails exactly a_probed_device_is_built_from_its_attribute_answers; cell budget 0; respell 0; europa --check --timeout-ms 150000 exit 0, with the negative twin exit 5. Close green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 9 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261104-013458. (A first land attempt refused itself: the generated land script's single-file spec flattened, @(@(...)), and lib_land_window rejected the draft argument; nothing was written. The land scripts now fail closed with ErrorActionPreference Stop.) NEXT: the C binding cuda_query (cudaDeviceGetAttribute) proven on a GPU box, feeding GPU-STACKED-RUNS.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_9 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T06:24Z", "tibia", "11-04 02:2x tibia, SLICE 5 DRAFTED AND PROVEN ON A REAL GPU (drafts LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES v5, base 52430D9393A9): probed ordinal : option device through the CUDA DRIVER API loaded at run time (LoadLibraryA nvcuda.dll / dlopen libcuda.so.1; cuInit, cuDeviceGet, cuDeviceGetAttribute), so no CUDA toolkit is needed to build. Every failure (no library, missing symbol, init or device error) answers -1, and probed is None when Sms <= 0, so a GPU-less CI runner gets None. The C side is split into one small global per C function (c_cu_win_lib/sym, c_cu_posix_lib/sym, types, ready, device, attr_fn, find, ask, attribute) for the cell budget. FIRST REAL PROBE (box, mingw gcc): the box GPU is NOT the rtx4060 preset but an NVIDIA Quadro K1100M (Kepler, cc 3.0, driver 25.21.14.2678 = R426, pre-CUDA-11): sms 2, threads/SM 2048, regs 65536, smem/SM 49152, opt-in smem/block 49152, while attributes 106 (blocks/SM) and 111 (reserved smem) answered -1 (they arrived in CUDA 11). So v5 adds CcMajor/CcMinor (codes 75/76, checked in NVIDIA driver_types.h 12.9.79) and filled: an unsupported attribute falls back to blocks_by_cc (Kepler 16, Volta 32 / Turing 16, A100 32 / GA10x 16 / Ada 24, others 32) and reserved_by_cc (1024 from cc 8, else 0). After that the live probe prints blocks 16, reserved 0, launch blocks/sm 10, grid 20, occupancy 62, and equals device_from (filled k1100m_answers) (exit 0). Tests: an_old_driver_falls_back_to_the_compute_capability (c, rust: 16, 0, 10) and a_probe_finds_no_device_without_a_driver_and_whole_sms_with_one (c). respell 0, budget 0. NEXT: box Cells gate with a mutant, then the land.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_10 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 10u32, "2026-11-04T07:56Z", "tibia", "11-04 03:5x tibia, SLICE 5 LANDED (52430D9393A9 -> BE410DF8161A): probed ordinal : option device through the CUDA driver API loaded at run time (nvcuda.dll / libcuda.so.1), with the compute-capability fallback (filled, blocks_by_cc, reserved_by_cc) for drivers older than CUDA 11. Proof: a REAL-GPU run on the box (Quadro K1100M, cc 3.0, R426): sms 2, threads 2048, blocks 16 (fallback), regs 65536, smem 49152, reserved 0 (fallback); launch blocks/sm 10, grid 20, occupancy 62; equal to device_from (filled k1100m_answers). Node gate tibia-occ5-gate-1 (mirror synced): positive 11/11 with 0 type errors (the probe test also passed on the node's own K1100M); mutant (reserved_by_cc answers 1 below cc 8) fails exactly an_old_driver_falls_back_to_the_compute_capability; cell budget 0 over (hashtag and autolink findings only, from the C #ifdef text); respell 0. Close green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 11 typed 0 errors, 0 respell; undo lib-land-undo 20261104-035117. LEFT for 100%: GPU-STACKED-RUNS prints described (planned target (the probed device) kernel) once at start; that is the consumer slice, next when a GPU run is planned.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_11 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T15:30Z", "tibia", "11-04 11:30 tibia, CONSUMER SLICE IN THE TREE: tibia/apps/predict/gpu_plan.spi (new module, registered in apps/predict/spiral.toml after lanes_gpu; unstaged) is the GPU run's first command: occupancy::probed 0 through the CUDA driver at run time; on Some d it prints the device line and the launch plan of the lanes kernel (64 threads = the WGSL runner's workgroup, smem 0, registers not counted since WGSL reports none), exit 0; on None it prints 'no CUDA device: probed 0 is None', exit 1. Proof: box (Quadro K1100M): 'device sms 2, threads/sm 2048, blocks/sm 16, regs/sm 65536, smem/sm 49152' and 'blocks/sm 16, grid 32, occupancy 50%', exit 0, compiled inside tibia's package (12,826 B C); europa (no GPU), the same C: 'no CUDA device', exit 1. LEFT: the same command on a rented L40S as the first step of GPU-STACKED-RUNS (no Cloud GPU region yet).")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_12 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 12u32, "2026-11-05T05:16Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:16 tibia: Active -> Blocked at 90. Everything CPU-side is landed and proven (slices 1-5 plus the gpu_plan consumer on the box K1100M). The last 10% is running gpu_plan on a rented L40S, and Europa shows 0 locations on every GPU plan (anonymous recheck today at 01:03, GPU-STACKED-RUNS n12). Unblocks when a GPU plan has a location or the user picks another provider.")
