inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_14 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 14u32, "2026-11-08T21:39Z", "tibia", "11-08 17:4x tibia groom (re-verify the premise): the stated resume condition \"a Cloud vcg plan lists a location\" is now TRUE in the catalog (vcg-a16-12c-120g-32vram, NVIDIA A16 32 GB, $0.942/h, ewr), but the account monthly fee limit refuses it ($688/mo list; memory europa-rental-account-gates), and the user shelved rentals and may go to a GPU outside Europa. So still Blocked; the BLOCKER is now the account limit / provider choice, not stock. The CPU-only half (core count, cache sizes, SIMD width) needs no GPU and can run on box, node and ganymede today.")
inl compiler_gpu_backend_primitives () = Task ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", "Compiler: the GPU/fast-CPU primitives the ML library used through CUDA macros, as typed ops on every backend that has them: WGSL workgroup memory, barriers, subgroup collectives and atomics; an unroll pragma (union NoUnroll | UnrollAll | UnrollBy) on C/Rust/WGSL; restrict emission in C; f16/bf16 types; a noinline attribute instead of the noinline_ name prefix; 16-byte vector loads", Feature, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "", "compiler,backends,wgsl,gpu,transformer,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives () = Planning ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", Minutes 2400u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md section 5 (capability table: missing in our compiler: unroll outside CodegenCpp, restrict 0 hits, f16 0 hits, WGSL shared memory/barriers/subgroups/atomics) and 3 (pragma.spi -1/0/n codes, models.spi:8-9 name convention). Coordinate with WGSL-BACKEND and the compiler lane.")
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:46Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:4x tibia groom (lint markers). DoD: each named primitive (WGSL workgroup memory, barriers, subgroup ops, atomics, the unroll union, restrict in C, f16/bf16, a noinline attribute, 16-byte vector loads) as a typed op with a golden test on every backend that has it and a compile error on the others. Next step: list which of these already exist in lib/compiler (grep the WGSL backend) and split the rest into 120-min steps. TypeFeatures: the unroll pragma as the union NoUnroll | UnrollAll | UnrollBy, memory spaces as a union, never int ids.")
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:54Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:5x tibia: the D1 inventory is done (see the child): 7 of 9 primitives are absent as typed ops; unroll and noinline exist only on Cpp/CUDA in untyped form; the Cpp backend has CudaHost/CudaDevice targets. Next step: compiler lane picks the order of S1-S8 (WGSL workgroup memory + barriers first, for tibia lanes' shared state).")
