inl tibia_learning_nuggets () = Task ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", "tibia: adopt the ML library's learning machinery that fits integer, bit-exact sims: CEM ensemble update (elites at or above the mean, resampling from elite statistics) as a batched trainer option, ensemble action sampling with importance weights, log-space path probabilities, tabular CFR+ and VR-MCCFR baselines before any NN policy, LSH sign-bit hashing of features into a policy table, a game-node union state machine with one step call site, bitmask decks/bitsets, bounded histories pickled into features, and on-device state encoding", Story, P1, D5, 80u32, Blocked, "TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE,TIBIA-NUGGET-TABULAR-CFR,TIBIA-NUGGET-IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING,TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS", "tibia,ml,typefeatureset,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_learning_nuggets () = Planning ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md sections 1.4 (cem.spi:38-146, models.spi:37-76, path_probs.spi, cfr.spi:144-253, cem_models.spi:86-95 select_id_from_mask), 1.2 (local_binarize :817-821), 3 (game/leduc state machine, train_cfr.spi:129-134 single site, deckm bitmask, hd enumerative CFR+), and failures 1 and 7 (neural CFR/CEM failed on NL Hold'em: start from tabular baselines known to converge; golden deterministic tests and rng per thread from day one). Remodel the int action ids with failwith decoders and the bool mode flags (is_train, is_current) into unions; the elite rule becomes selection = TopK : n | AboveMean; ratio accumulators become a running_mean nominal.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 2u32, "2026-11-05T04:26Z", "tibia", "11-05 00:26 tibia: SLICE 1 DRAFTED, CEM ensemble update as a batched trainer option (scratch np2 = src/network.spi base 707e7157dc1e + COMPILER-EMIT-PARALLEL-LOOPS' evolve_par_by + this; draft ab5b42043d78). The nugget's elite rule is a union, as the inventory asked: elites = TopK : i32 | AboveMean. AboveMean compares score * n >= total in i64 (lane fitness sits near -1e9, so an i32 sum of 32 children overflows); TopK uses a stable rank (strictly better children plus equal-scored EARLIER children), so ties go to the lower child id, deterministically. The next parent is the clamped per-weight integer mean of the elite children (each child re-derived by mutate, so no per-child weight storage); scores come from scores_by (parallel::for_index, one child per thread on C). CEM moves the mean, so climb_cem_by carries a kept_best and never returns worse than its start; width keeps next_weight_round's shrink (elite-variance width is the next refinement). Tests (c, rust): tied_elites_keep_the_earlier_child_and_the_mean_counts_ties (scores 5,5,3,1: TopK 1 = child 0 only, TopK 2 and AboveMean = 0 and 1), the_mean_rule_does_not_overflow_on_large_scores (-1e9 scores), cem_never_ends_below_its_start (c). europa probe, C t1/t2 and Rust identical: heal judge seed 5, climb 17, cem AboveMean 17, cem TopK 3 = 13. Node gate tibia-np2-gate-1 queued: draft, then a double mutant (fold '>=', tie rank 'i <= child'). Rest of the inventory (importance-weighted ensemble sampling, CFR+ baselines, LSH features) stays open.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 3u32, "2026-11-05T05:12Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:12 tibia: SLICE 2 DRAFTED (np3 = 3c8136221511, supersedes np2): CEM's spread comes from elite statistics too. cem_rule = { pick : elites; spread : spread }, spread = Shrink | EliteSpread. EliteSpread sets the next width to max 4 ((width + elite mean-absolute-deviation from the elite mean) / 2), averaged over all weights; Shrink keeps next_weight_round's schedule. One elite_pass per round feeds both the mean and the deviation pass. Regression on europa (C at OMP 2 and Rust, identical): AboveMean+Shrink and TopK 3+Shrink give 17 and 13 at seed 5, the same as np2; the heal judge is too coarse to tell EliteSpread apart (17/13, 13/13 at seeds 5/9), so the real comparison is the lanes objective. First node gate on np2 (tibia-np2-gate-2): 10/12 green; the two reds were the node GPU runner crashing (spiral-wgsl 0xC0000005 on the unchanged network_decides_on_gpu, green in the next arm) and my test line 'a >= b |> _assert_eq' parsing as a >= (b |> ...) (fixed with parens, memory spiral-pipe-binds-tighter-than-comparison). Mutant arm: parallel_climb and tied_elites fail exactly as targeted. Gate 3 (draft only, np3) is queued on the node.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 4u32, "2026-11-05T06:35Z", "tibia", "11-05 02:35 tibia, SLICE 1 RESULT ON THE REAL OBJECTIVE (node job tibia-cl1-cem-lanes, 6023 s, OMP 8, i7-4810MQ; lanes.spi PF1 objective = worth CheapClearWithin 94934 on the arena-spot cyclops camp; full plan 8 generations x 64 offspring x 100 training seeds; held-out = the same worth on seeds 1001-1100). Columns: lane, method (0 climb via evolve_par_by, 1 CEM AboveMean+Shrink, 2 CEM TopK 8+Shrink), train / held. Lane 0: -67400/-67350, -99450/-99700, -75650/-75250. Lane 1: -67600/-67700, -432700/-441200, -69000/-68750. Lane 2: -68200/-82950, -398850/-420400, -101950/-101300. Lane 3: -66900/-81250, -135500/-134750, -73450/-73700. VERDICT for slice 1 (Shrink width): the CEM mean update LOSES to the elitist hill climb on training in 4/4 lanes for both elite rules. AboveMean is far worse: half the population is elite, so the mean drifts toward mediocre children. TopK 8 is closer (1-50% worse) and generalizes more evenly (train ~ held in all 4 lanes), beating the climb on held-out only in lane 3 (-73700 vs -81250), where the climb overfit (train -66900, held -81250); the climb overfits lanes 2 and 3 by about 14k. So CEM is no improvement for this objective at this budget. The next test is slice 2's EliteSpread (elite-statistics width) at TopK 8, queued on the node; europa is out for compiles tonight.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 5u32, "2026-11-05T06:49Z", "tibia", "11-05 02:49 tibia: PLACED in live tibia/src/network.spi (707e7157dc1e -> 3c8136221511, unstaged). It adds evolve_par_by (offspring per thread via parallel::for_index), the CEM trainer evolve_cem_by with cem_rule = { pick : TopK n | AboveMean; spread : Shrink | EliteSpread }, and 4 tests. PROOF: node gate tibia-np2-gate-3 (tibia's own build.ps1 -Files network on the synced mirror, the draft swapped in and restored): layout clean, cell budget clean, discovered 12, executed 12, passed 12 (c, rust and wgsl): parallel_climb_keeps_the_sequential_winner c+rust, tied_elites_go_to_the_earlier_child c+rust, the_mean_rule_does_not_overflow_on_large_scores c+rust, cem_never_ends_below_its_start c, plus the 6 existing tests. Mutant kills (gate 2, np2: fold '>=' and tie rank '<=') fail exactly the parallel and tie tests; np3 left those definitions unchanged. Mirror restored to 707E7157DC1E.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 6u32, "2026-11-05T08:15Z", "tibia", "11-05 04:15 tibia, SLICE 2 RESULT (node job tibia-cl2-cem-lanes-2, 2827 s, OMP 8; the same objective, full plan and seeds as slice 1; np3 compiled on the node with the mirror's compiler). EliteSpread (width = mean of the old width and the elites' mean absolute deviation): AboveMean, lanes 0-3 train/held: -99450/-99700, -276950/-284350, -398850/-420400, -269850/-277800. Lanes 0 and 2 are identical to Shrink, consistent with the best weights being found before the two width rules diverge. TopK 8: -67950/-82450, -203050/-208050, -68250/-68250, -72400/-72150. COMBINED VERDICT (slices 1-2, 4 lanes): the elitist climb wins TRAINING in every lane. On HELD-OUT, the medians are climb -74,475, TopK 8 Shrink -74,475 (a tie) and TopK 8 EliteSpread -77,300. EliteSpread is the best variant on lanes 2 and 3 (lane 2 held -68,250 vs the climb's -82,950, with no overfit) but collapses on lane 1 (-208k); AboveMean is bad with either spread. So no CEM variant beats the climb robustly at this budget (8 x 64). The climb stays the default; evolve_cem_by stays in network.spi as an option, gated and tested. If CEM is revisited: elitism inside CEM (carry the best child into the next mean) and a held-out-scored kept_best, since its edge is generalization, not training fit. The rest of the inventory (importance-weighted ensemble sampling, tabular CFR+ baselines, LSH features) is untouched.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 7u32, "2026-11-06T08:20Z", "tibia", "11-06 04:19 tibia (groom): verdicts to fold in from TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION. Held out over 8 lanes, x4 seeds per candidate beats x1 (median -68,350 vs -74,475; worst lane -71,900 vs -114,200), and x8 is flat, so seeds generalize. Extra offspring overfits even with a validation selector. CEM (TopK/AboveMean x Shrink/EliteSpread) does not beat the climb. lanes.spi already has robust_plan (seeds = 4 x training_count). NEXT (CPU-light): write these as nugget rows and point full runs at robust_plan.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 8u32, "2026-11-06T12:17Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:17 tibia: SPLIT (main: over 240 min). Slice 1 (CEM: elites TopK/AboveMean, spread Shrink/EliteSpread) is done and placed in src/network.spi; verdict: it does not beat the elitist climb on held-out data. The remaining nuggets became children: TIBIA-NUGGET-LSH-TABLE, -TABULAR-CFR, -IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING, -BITSETS (each 120 min with a DoD). The game-node state machine and the bounded histories ride along inside TABULAR-CFR''s abstraction. The parent closes when the 4 children close. NEXT: TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS' module (CPU-light).")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 9u32, "2026-11-06T12:18Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:18 tibia: DoD: all 4 children Done, each with its own proof (golden tests on c and rust plus the measured comparison its DoD names).")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 10u32, "2026-11-07T15:53Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:5x tibia groom round 2 (stale Active, no note in 12 h): Planned. A parent waiting on its children: TABULAR-CFR (reopened, waits on TIBIA-CFR-RETREAT-MODEL), LSH-TABLE (PR-29 VOID) and BITSETS (box live window). IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING is Done.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 11u32, "2026-11-08T16:21Z", "tibia", "11-08 tibia groom: 3 of 4 children Done (LSH-TABLE, TABULAR-CFR, IMPORTANCE-SAMPLING). BLOCKER: TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS (90 pct, Blocked): its code and 5 Cells tests are green; only run.ps1's terrain and region parity is left, and that needs the box's live Canary data in a free box live window. NEXT STEP: none on this parent; it closes when BITSETS closes. Resume when: kit window list shows a free live slot on the box, then run BITSETS' parity.")
