inl note_of_link_split_invariance_23 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 23u32, "2026-11-05T14:52Z", "compiler", "11-05 10:5x compiler: SPLIT ORACLE GREEN for the LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES closed-shapes fix (box, pack47 candidate = pack44 + program 3 + UnionTag; run 08:29-10:50 at box load 83-100%): test.ps1 -Suite split, full 34-sample list, 616 cuts, REACH 333 legal, 0 fail (no DIFFERS, no native build-fail) on Zig and Rust, run single-flight-20261105-082940 in the scratchpad pack47 cache. Same reach as pack37 (333 legal), so the narrower struct import loses no legal cut. pack48's program 4 only drops non-generated (hand-written) structs from the shape set; the split samples have none, so the result carries to pack48/49 (now on box, node and europa).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_24 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 24u32, "2026-11-05T18:06Z", "compiler", "11-05 14:0x compiler: SPLIT ORACLE GREEN on the INSTALLED compiler directly (box; installed pack50 at start 11:05, pack51 from 11:58: Rust output byte-identical, so the swap cannot change a row): 616 cuts, REACH 333 legal, 0 fail (no DIFFERS, no native build-fail) on Zig and Rust, run spiral-bin\\runs\\single-flight-20261105-110510. This checks LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES' fixes 3 + 4 directly rather than by carrying the pack47 result: reach is unchanged at 333.")
