inl note_of_link_split_invariance_26 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 26u32, "2026-11-06T15:49Z", "compiler", "11-06 11:4x compiler: NEXT STEP TAKEN: the split oracle on the CURRENT shipped core, node first. job-1793980081661-compiler-split-oracle: test.ps1 -Suite split in an isolated mirror (C:\\home\\remote\\compiler-split, tree c0e77c3f + this box's unstaged digest 932AF956), SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL = the node's installed compiler, core 257DB91886B97811 (pack55d, which adds the linked-unit stale-graph error, the lambda-export warning and Gleam named records since the last green run on pack47/48). Private cache; 6 h cap; node at 100% load (correctness run, not timing). DoD for this step: 616 cuts, REACH 333 legal, 0 fail, as on pack47. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: no code (oracle run).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_27 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 27u32, "2026-11-06T17:28Z", "compiler", "11-06 13:2x compiler: split oracle job-1793980081661 (node, core 257DB91886B97811) is PENDING, not hung: its stdout stays at the header because the runner keeps only test.ps1's last 40 lines, but the run dir (compiler-split-cache\\runs\\single-flight-20261106-115336\\split) holds 317 cut dirs across 20 samples at 13:27, still writing (contract_schema_indexed_codec Rust cut6), node load 100%. At that rate about 90 more minutes. The node route dropped once (remote.ps1 NoRoute on <moon-lan-addr> and <moon-ts-addr> at 13:22, back at 13:26). The shard measurement job-1793981352933 is queued after it.")
