inl todo_vs_agile_bench () = Task ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", "Benchmark the decentralized TODO-in-source model against the single agile.spi file model (write latency, lost updates, lock races, rename cost, read/query speed, lane concurrency), then decide TODO-AS-SOURCE scope from the numbers", Story, P1, D5, 60u32, Planned, "KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", "team:org,main,kit,todo,agile,bench", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_todo_vs_agile_bench () = Planning ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_1 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 1u32, "2026-11-02T16:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 (user: \"we also should review why the task about spreading todo comments everywhere is parked, we gotta benchmark this decentralized approach vs the agile.spi file model\"). WHY PARKED: TODO-AS-SOURCE (P1 epic, 50%) was Paused only by silence; kit moved it back to Planned on 10-31, noting it is \"a deliberate destructive migration ... not abandoned work\" that needs a fresh scope decision. Its prototype migrate-prototype.py is archived (kit\\archive\\20261030-232045). The scanner KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS is 80%. No benchmark existed, so the decision had nothing to stand on. TODAY'S EVIDENCE FOR AGILE.SPI'S COST: every write rewrites the whole 11.7 MB file (1-8 s per note under load); one `kit agile rename` ran 15 min and 424 s of CPU, then lost an optimistic-lock race (KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST); lost updates re-opened at least 2 items (FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE, LIB-RESHAPE status); batch writes hit \"file changed since read\" (tibia #8). PRE-REGISTERED BENCH (fixed before running): on a scratch copy of the backlog plus a scratch tree with the same items as TODO markers, measure p50/p95 latency of note/add/edit/rename/list/next with 1, 4 and 8 concurrent writers; lost-update count over 1,000 interleaved writes; full-text query time; and the git diff size per change. A/A on each side first (ab-needs-in-job-aa). Run on the node, not the box. DECISION RULE: adopt the source model for a class of items (code TODOs) if it wins p95 write latency and lost updates with no loss of query ability; keep agile.spi for epics and cross-repo items either way.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_2 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 2u32, "2026-11-02T18:20Z", "main", "main 11-02 14:4x FIRST RESULTS (node moon at ~99% CPU from other lanes, so latencies are loaded-box numbers; kit TRAIN11 AD5A8A62; scratch copy of the 11.3 MB backlog + a 925-file .spi tree; scripts and raw output in kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH and on the node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\todo-bench).\nHARNESS LESSONS (two VOID runs before the valid one): (1) a copied backlog carries its LEASE record, so the scratch copy started 608 h expired and EVERY write was refused (\"lease authority blocked ... should_wrap=1\"); fix: `kit agile begin <root> '<3-7 words>'` on the copy. (2) `kit agile add` refuses `--as` without `--note`; the target item was never created and the first run's \"write latency\" was refusal latency. Every sample now checks ok/refused/stored.\nVALID: agile.spi note writes, 24 per row: 1 writer p50 1.5 s / p95 2.9 s; 4 writers p50 2.0 s / p95 10.2 s; 8 writers p50 4.3 s / p95 8.6 s; 24/24 stored, 0 LOST at every width (kit's write lock serializes correctly). TODO-in-source marker write: p50 1-2 ms, p95 3-18 ms (A/A B/B2), no shared file, so no contention by construction. QUERY: agile.spi list --words 8.4 s, show 3.1 s, next 5.8 s; `kit agile todos` over 925 files 17.4 s (SLOWER than list). Diff size: agile.spi rewrites 11.3 MB per note; a marker adds 1 line to 1 file.\nDECISION RULE (pre-registered): adopt source TODOs for code items if they win p95 write latency AND lost updates with no loss of query ability. Write latency: source wins about 1000x. Lost updates: tie (0 vs 0). Query: source LOSES (17.4 s vs 8.4 s). VERDICT: NOT YET. The blocker is the todos scanner, not the model. Gate to adopt: make `agile todos` answer within agile list's time (an index or prefilter over changed files; KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS), then re-run this bench. Open anomaly: the todos query found 80 BENCH markers where 40 were written (double count in the output or the scan); check before the re-run. Note: production lost updates today (2 items) did NOT reproduce for concurrent notes, so they come from another write path (status set / edit), worth its own probe.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_3 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 3u32, "2026-11-03T03:12Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:1x RE-TIMED with kit AF229BEC (TRAIN13c, 22:21) on the box, same backlog root: 'agile todos' 114,435 ms then 94,407 ms (roots=6, files=14,076, scanned=4,707, todos=9; skipped generated 6,241 + syntax 3,123), vs 'agile list' 2,476 ms. The scan is SLOWER than the 17.4 s of n2 because it now walks 6 roots / 14k files. VERDICT: still NOT YET, the gate (todos fast enough to replace the parked TODO list) is further away. For kit: the 9 todos cost a 14k-file walk each call; an mtime-keyed cache per root (the agile_todo_cache crate exists) or an index written at commit time would bring it under the list's 2.5 s.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_4 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 4u32, "2026-11-05T08:10Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:1x kit groom (WIP cap: Active means a note within 48 h): Active -> Planned, last note 2026-11-03T03:12Z (53 h ago), progress kept at 60%. Resume from that note; nothing was lost, it just isn't being worked.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_5 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 5u32, "2026-11-06T13:09Z", "main", "main 11-06 11:5x DoD backfill (kit lint): DoD: a measured table (write latency, lost updates, lock races, rename cost, query time) for TODO-in-source vs agile.spi at today's size, with a recommendation. Next step: rerun the agile side after TRAIN33 (rename is now 1.6-3 s per item, was minutes).")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_6 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 6u32, "2026-11-07T22:19Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. TypeFeatures: benchmark rows typed { model : TodoInSource | AgileFile; metric : WriteLatency | LostUpdates | LockRaces | RenameCost | QuerySpeed; value }.")
