inl note_of_kit_edition3_respell_1 () = Note ("KIT-EDITION3-RESPELL", 1u32, "2026-11-02T20:20Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 16:2x SIZED with pack17's own checker on europa: `SpiralCompiler format --check --respell-drift src` over kit reports 10,017 respell-drift sites in 641 files (main counted 3,313 with strings stripped). The top packages are kit_lint_model 207, agile_todo_model 191, kit_standards 183, kit_machine_windows 173, agile_task_next 153, kit_coverage_smoke 150, rust_std_fs_mutation 142 and kit_bindings_model 124. PLAN: the fixer is `format --spelling symbols <files>` (the checker and fixer agree exactly, per main). Scope it to kit/src only, never the repo root; state/ spelling is guarded separately by KIT-STATE-SPELLING-GUARD. Run it in its own train after TRAIN13: (1) apply on a scratch copy of src, (2) regenerate every owner and require byte-identical generated .rs except for spelling-invariant noise (the respell must not change semantics), (3) all notebooks green, (4) re-check 0 drift, (5) census ratchet 0 regressions. It's one mechanical change, landed as one unstaged changeset for the user to commit separately from feature work.")
