inl note_of_x_dumps_translate_2 () = Note ("X-DUMPS-TRANSLATE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "x-dumps", "COST MODEL 11-03 (settles the cost side; a paid run still needs the user budget/go per the standing rule). Corpus = 4 completed accounts: 26,988 UNIQUE narratable segments (deduped via translate_input.ndjson), 1,675,902 source chars. Spec needs 2 renditions per segment: the opposite of EN/PT, plus KO. Token estimate: input ~0.45M tok (Latin ~3.7 char/tok); output ~1.2M tok (EN/PT ~0.46M + KO ~0.6-0.77M; KOREAN OUTPUT TOKENS DOMINATE and are the main uncertainty). Prices (third-party 2026, confirm at anthropic.com/pricing; Batch API = 50 pct off, prompt-cache the instruction once): Haiku 1/5 -> batch ~$3; Sonnet 3/15 -> batch ~$10; Opus 5/25 -> batch ~$16, for the 4 accounts. geygey_hadid roughly doubles it (narratable count unknown until it is narrated). TOTAL incl geygey (batch): Haiku ~$6-10, Sonnet ~$20-30, Opus ~$35-50. RECOMMEND Sonnet (strong multilingual quality per WMT, best quality/cost) with a Haiku quality spot-check. DRY-RUN READY but NOT run (needs user go): 50-segment sample from the smallest account on Haiku+Sonnet (~$0.20-0.50) to validate quality AND the real token/char ratios (especially KO) before committing the full run. Free levers already in place: dedup, plus prompt-caching the system instruction and the Batch API.")
