inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:16Z", "x-dumps", "VALIDATED 11-03: juhondacivic has ~1,260 lost ids (Wayback capture = tombstone 404 \"account no longer exists\"), and an archive.today sample found 0/5 elsewhere - very likely GENUINELY UNRECOVERABLE. These are the canonical case for this item: keep every such id in the internal index, FILTER from the joined display timeline (no gaps while scrolling), per the user 11-03 directive. The index already exists implicitly (captures.tsv has all ids; timeline marks lost/removed/no-text); this item wires the display filter into the frontend (X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND) and, with XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI, the typed text_lost flag.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:57Z", "x-dumps", "Index emitter built 2026-11-04 into xarchive `world`: emits joined/unrecoverable.ndjson (id, account_id, username, utc, kind, reason) for every lost==true post - the internal index of what did NOT survive, kept in data while the scroll filters it out (phantom-state render). Compiles clean on box. Deploy to europa + run world to produce it AFTER recovery PASS-2 completes, so the index reflects the post-recovery (smaller) lost set. Display-filter half is x (timeline_serve lost==true drop).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:00Z", "x-dumps", "Index emitted + verified 2026-11-04: joined/unrecoverable.ndjson, 4896 entries. Emitter half DONE. Display-filter half (render-time lost==true drop) is x in timeline_serve.spi.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_5 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 5u32, "2026-11-04T09:59Z", "x-dumps", "Index now content-accurate 2026-11-04: 4860 entries (was 4896) after the content-based lost fix - recovered tweets with text/media no longer counted as unrecoverable. By account: 72784485=49, juhondacivic=1259, geygey=3417, stewshka=61, 1637=74. Emitter half done+verified (0 lost-with-content, 0 empty-content-shown); display-filter half is x.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_6 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 6u32, "2026-11-04T11:20Z", "x-dumps", "INDEX half DONE 2026-11-04: xarchive world now emits BOTH the machine index (joined/unrecoverable.ndjson, 4860 ids) AND a readable internal index (joined/unrecoverable-summary.md: per-account count + date range + by-reason, kept on purpose, hidden from the scroll per the directive). Per account: fc1943s(1637) 74, fc1943s(72784485) 49, geygey 3417, juhondacivic 1259, stewshka 61 (all 2012-2026 ranges). By-reason all \"not-captured\" (per-tweet lost reason is the archive-fetch failure; account-level suspension e.g. geygey is separate context). DISPLAY-FILTER half (hide lost==true from the joined scroll) is x render in timeline route/sim — the remaining dependency. Emitter fully verified (compiles, regen clean).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_7 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 7u32, "2026-11-04T11:40Z", "x-dumps", "Display-filter half landing 2026-11-04: x-next5c LANDED the sim lost filter (sim_serve user_posts drops lost==true), so the X-API mock no longer serves lost entries. The joined-scroll render filter rides x-next6 (route page_of phantom). Index half fully done (machine unrecoverable.ndjson + readable unrecoverable-summary.md). Item complete once the x-next6 route filter lands.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_8 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 8u32, "2026-11-04T12:57Z", "x-dumps", "DISPLAY-FILTER half now implemented (pending train, not yet live) 2026-11-04: X-TIMELINE-ROUTE/timeline_serve.spi drops lost==true in page_of via surviving/visible, and my GET /timeline entry (feed_reply, integrated by x via serve_with + feed_or_api) consumes it - so the joined scroll hides the 4860 unrecoverable while unrecoverable.ndjson keeps them. Index re-verified CURRENT against the 11:19Z sim world: 4860 ndjson entries = 4860 lost posts in joined.world.json, exact match. BOTH halves implemented+verified; item completes when the X-TIMELINE-ROUTE draft trains to live (route --check 0 already).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_9 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 9u32, "2026-11-04T23:14Z", "x-dumps", "DISPLAY-FILTER half PROVEN LIVE 2026-11-04: the demo sim UI (localhost:58151/timeline, x scratch build) hides the 4860 lost posts in the served joined timeline via the route visible/surviving filter, confirming BOTH halves work end-to-end on real data (emitter index 4860 + render-time drop). Still pending x-next9 train for the production landing.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_10 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 10u32, "2026-11-05T03:53Z", "x-dumps", "Live-build (8787) validation note 2026-11-04: inspected the served page HTML - each article carries byline (@handle, account_id, timestamp), authorship class (post/reply/repost/quote) and text, but NOT individual post ids. So the display-filter cannot be validated by cross-checking rendered ids against the 4860-id index from the rendered HTML. Filter correctness is route-level: timeline_serve surviving/visible drop lost==true before render (confirmed in source), and the 23:14Z end-to-end proof stands; count-level validation would need a full scroll (~3169 pages at budget 50) = not CPU-light. Item stays 95% pending route-filter train landing. Releasing claim to work the now-unblocked P1 codec gate (kit supplied the draft path).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_11 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 11u32, "2026-11-05T04:18Z", "x-dumps", "INDEX COMPLETENESS GAP found+characterized 2026-11-05: a reference-graph check surfaced 121 ids (juhondacivic 48, geygey_hadid 73) referenced by our own posts (reply_to/quote.id), authored by our own SUSPENDED accounts, but NOT in the crawl, NOT context-cached, and NOT in this 4860-id index (0 overlap). Phantom ids: known to exist only via the reference, so the crawl never had a capture to mark lost. Direct by-id syndication probe = 121/121 tombstone (confirmed gone). They SHOULD be indexed (true unrecoverable 4860+121=4981). The emitter (xarchive world) builds the index from lost==true POSTS only; to include these it must also fold in referenced-but-absent self-ids (reply_to/quote.id whose author is one of ours and that have no post record). List saved europa:/data/x/joined/reference-gap-own-accounts.tsv. Follow-up: emitter enhancement OR a supplementary index file.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_12 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 12u32, "2026-11-05T04:25Z", "x-dumps", "Index data completed to true count 2026-11-05: built europa:/data/x/joined/unrecoverable-refs-supplement.ndjson (121 rows, schema-matched {account_id,id,kind:lost,reason,username,utc}; utc derived EXACTLY from each snowflake id via bash 64-bit (id>>22)+1288834974657 - not awk/jq, which would lose the high bits of ids >2^53 as doubles). Combined with the existing 4860-id unrecoverable.ndjson = 4981 unique ids (0 overlap reconfirmed). By account: geygey_hadid 73, juhondacivic 48; all syndication-tombstoned = confirmed gone. This supplement is a stopgap AND a spec/fixture for the DURABLE fix: xarchive world emitter should fold referenced-but-absent self-ids (reply_to/quote.id authored by one of ours with no post record) into the index so a re-emit regenerates all 4981 deterministically - a hand-built supplement would drift on the next xarchive world run. Progress held at 95%: data complete, durable emitter change is the remaining work (well-specified).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_13 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 13u32, "2026-11-05T04:48Z", "x-dumps", "Emitter enhancement ATTEMPTED+verified on europa 2026-11-05, then REVERTED (not landed - exposed a nuance). Added referenced-self-id phantom emission to xarchive world (local draft C:\\home\\git\\xarchive\\src\\world.rs: compiles, built on europa 20s, world ran clean exit 0). RESULT: naive emitter emits 130 phantom (index 4990) vs my earlier jq probe 121; 115 common. Diagnosed EXACTLY: (a) all 15 emitter-extra are in accounts/*/context.ndjson = cross-account self-refs (our A replies to our B -> B fetched into A context, we HAVE a snippet) -> should be EXCLUDED; emitter lacks context subtraction. (b) 6 probe-extra are refs on non-reply/quote records that the emitter skips (it gates extraction on kind==reply/quote) - emitter kind-gating is arguably MORE correct (0 of 6 in timelines or context). So TRUE unrecoverable ~115, not a clean number; hinges on 2 semantics: do context-snippet-only ids count? do non-reply/quote refs count? REVERTED europa world.rs to backup (known-good; index stays 4860). Local draft kept pending: add context.ndjson subtraction + confirm the 2 semantics. The 121 supplement itself needs the same reconciliation. NET: reachable accounts still 100% complete; suspended-account missing self-refs all tombstoned on X (a handful have context snippets).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_14 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 14u32, "2026-11-05T05:02Z", "x-dumps", "Emitter enhancement COMPLETE + VERIFIED 2026-11-05 (local unstaged; shared node reverted to pristine). Added referenced-self-id phantom emission WITH context subtraction to xarchive world (C:\\home\\git\\xarchive\\src\\world.rs, unstaged for user review+commit per never-commit). VERIFIED on europa: index 4975 = 4860 + 115 phantom self-ids (geygey 72, juhondacivic 43), 0 of 115 in context. Two definitional calls baked in (flagged for review): (Q1) an id whose FULL text we hold via the context stage (embed endpoint) is RECOVERED -> context-held self-ids EXCLUDED (drops 15 vs the naive 130); (Q2) only reply/quote records yield refs (kind-gated, consistent with refs_of/post_of) -> drops 6 non-reply/quote anomalies the earlier kind-agnostic probe had. Proven-correct unrecoverable count = 4975 (was 4860). europa REVERTED to committed-source (4860) to keep the shared node pristine; verified change is local-unstaged for the user to commit+redeploy (then index becomes 4975 durably). This supersedes + is the durable form of the earlier hand-built 121 supplement.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_15 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 15u32, "2026-11-05T05:19Z", "x-dumps", "Emitter FULLY RECONCILED + VERIFIED 2026-11-05 (two independent methods agree exactly). Resolved both semantic questions WITH EVIDENCE: (Q1) subtract context ids - context holds FULL text via the embed endpoint = recovered, not lost; (Q2) KIND-AGNOSTIC extraction, NOT kind-gated - found 462 records (288 tweet, 174 retweet) carrying reply_to/quote.id; the tweet-kinded ones are mis-kinded self-replies referencing our own accounts (e.g. a \"tweet\" with reply_to_user=geygey_hadid), so gating on kind==reply/quote wrongly drops ~6 real self-refs. Final kind-agnostic + context-subtracting emitter emits 121 phantom self-ids -> index 4860+121 = 4981, and it reproduces my original jq probe EXACTLY (identical=121, emitter_only=0, probe_only=0; geygey 73 + juhondacivic 48). So the correct unrecoverable count is 4981. Local xarchive/src/world.rs has the verified change (unstaged, for user commit -> durable 4981). europa reverted to pristine committed-source (4860, known-good binary). Durable fix is landing-ready; this supersedes the earlier 130/115 attempts and the hand-built supplement.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_16 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 16u32, "2026-11-06T08:28Z", "x-dumps", "Groom 11-06 04:28: re-checked per fiscal #9 - zero deps, so not dependency-blocked; the only gate is USER action (commit the verified-unstaged xarchive/src/world.rs emitter change -> durable 4981 index). Status stays Active 97 until that commit; europa left pristine at 4860. Nothing for x-dumps to unblock here; flagged as awaiting-user.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_17 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 17u32, "2026-11-06T10:15Z", "x-dumps", "Blocked 11-06 06:14: emitter deliverable DONE+verified (produces 4981; two independent methods agree id-for-id). The only remaining step is NOT x-dumps work: USER commits the staged xarchive/src/world.rs change to make the 4981 index durable. RESUME CONDITION: user commits world.rs. Set Blocked so the user queue is listable (main #4).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_18 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 18u32, "2026-11-07T15:57Z", "x-dumps", "blocker: blocked on the USER committing the verified-unstaged xarchive/src/world.rs emitter change (durable 4981 index). waits on user git commit; resume when world.rs is committed. No x-dumps work remains.")
