inl x_timeline_frontend () = Task ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", "Minimal Spiral frontend: joined X-like scrollable timeline across all collected accounts, built on the sim, in the x repo", Feature, P2, D5, 75u32, Active, "X-CLIENT,SOCIAL-TRANSPORT-SIM", "team:microblog,microblog,frontend,timeline,sim", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_timeline_frontend () = Planning ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", Minutes 360u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_1 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: build a minimal frontend to see a joined timeline of all collected accounts, using the sim code, in Spiral; grow it when appropriate like lib. The X-simulating scroll UI is generic (even if somewhat temporary) so it lives in the x repo/projects (C:\\home\\git\\x, apps/). Filters unrecoverable no-text entries per XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_2 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:20Z", "x", "2026-11-03 03:20 x: INTAKE (filed by x-dumps; team:x and assignee added). PLAN: a minimal Spiral frontend in x apps/ over the client's typed pool (posts.spi post/account/medium/reference), merging every collected account's timeline newest first. Its merge is the k-way merge NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW already prototyped (a resumable typed cursor), so that logic lands here, generic, with no NEAR dependency. Rendering is a static HTML page over the html repo's typed markup model (HTML-MODEL), not a new renderer (the drift-watch rule on CELLS-HTML-PARITY). Sequenced after X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES, so the frontend is proven against real-shaped data in the sim first.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_3 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:20Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:20 x: STEP 1 drafted, the generic merge (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\feed_merge.spi, 37709C86D9E7), restored from NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW's archived edition-2 probes (kit archive 20261030-232045: paged_merge, paged_offsets, paged_exhausted_negative) and rewritten in today's syntax with a typed cursor. feed_cursor t is a nominal over list (list t) (the erl_map pattern). merged_page newer budget cursor returns one page plus the resumed cursor: each step takes the newest head across feeds (better and head_better pick it; equal heads keep the earlier feed, so ties are stable), pops it (popped), and stops at the budget or when all feeds are empty. The order is a parameter (newer : t -> t -> bool), so one merge serves posts by (created_at, id) as well as plain ids. Blocks: pages resume from the cursor (3 then the rest, [90;80;75] then [70;60;20;10;5]), an exhausted or zero-budget page is empty, and equal heads keep feed order. Every cell is under 272 with headroom. NEXT: register it in x (apps/client or a new apps/timeline unit) once x-events3 has landed spiral.toml/package.spiproj, then a page renderer over the html units for the joined real-profile timelines. The NEAR consumer half stays Paused on NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_4 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 4u32, "2026-11-03T16:21Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:21 x: STEP 2 decided from the tree: the order is posts.spi's existing 'newer (a : entry) (b : entry)' (created_at second, then later_id, the rule its same-second block tests), so the joined timeline is feed_merge::merged_page posts::newer budget (cursor_of feeds), where each feed is one account's entries through posts' newest_first. No new ordering code. The page renders those entries with posts' entry fields through the html units (html_model nodes, html_render), and the real-profile worlds on europa (X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES n6) are the first input, read in place.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_5 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 5u32, "2026-11-03T16:27Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:27 x: STEP 3 drafted (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\timeline_page.spi): the page over the html units (opens model and render). byline = Paragraph [Strong [@user]; ' · ' time], then Paragraph [text], then Rule per entry, under an H1 title, rendered by render::blocks_html |> markup_text. merged = feed_merge::merged_page posts::newer, so joined_page title budget feeds is one page of the newest entries across accounts. Rust blocks: the byline and rule show, entry text is escaped (a <b> & c -> &lt;b&gt; &amp;), and a 2-entry page over two accounts takes a3 and b2 but not a1. Cells within budget. Packaging decided at registration: it needs the client root (posts) plus the html units as packages, so it is likely its own apps/timeline unit linking html like Cells will. The CELLS-HTML-PARITY CI note (html cloned beside the repo) applies to x's CI too, so registration waits for that pattern to settle.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_6 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:33Z", "x", "2026-11-03 13:33 x: STEP 1 REGISTRATION folded into x-next2: feed_merge joins the client root package (spiral.toml 2301C5DD40E4 -> 445B3F065EAF, package.spiproj 122B06832D93 -> 15692AC85DCB, 'feed_merge' after 'posts'; bases are x-events3's landed manifests), and feed_merge.spi 37709C86D9E7 lands as apps/client/feed_merge.spi. Its 3 rust blocks run in the client build, and CELL-BUDGET covers it. timeline_page.spi (step 3) stays a draft until the html-link pattern lands with CELLS-HTML-PARITY, since it opens html's model and render.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_7 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 7u32, "2026-11-03T21:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 17:30 x: STEP 1 LANDED in x-next2 (job-1793737559206, pinned pack27 core 6F83B94FE33167CC; the installed core moved to D1854B99FD3FA940 mid-run): lib gate 23/23, sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0 (CELL-BUDGET, xc.rs 992), e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME over 76 files with 0 over one post. apps/client/feed_merge.spi E3A4CD239079 registered in spiral.toml and package.spiproj; its 3 rust blocks pass in the client build. Step 3 (timeline_page) waits on the html-link pattern.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_8 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 8u32, "2026-11-04T04:06Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:06 x: SPLIT agreed with x-dumps (the user re-scoped them onto the joined timeline). x-dumps: an 'xarchive world' emitter (5 real ndjson timelines -> one joined world.json with lost:true flags; it stays on europa/node, never in a repo), then battle-testing sim+xc on it. x: the human HTML route in a new apps/sim/spi/timeline_serve.spi (sibling of sim_serve, reuses its HTTP helpers), rendered on the server with feed_merge::merged_page + the timeline_page draft. Merge and lost-filter in the serve module, not xc (xc fetches 5 per account, no per-account paging). CURSOR: stateless URL '?f=<feed order>&c=<raw offsets>', offsets count raw positions including lost, so the cursor survives filter changes. sim_serve.spi is reserved for x's pending tie-break draft (X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES); x-dumps won't edit it without telling x first. Built in the next run the user starts.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_9 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 9u32, "2026-11-04T05:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 01:03 x: ROUTE CURSOR drafted (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\feed_merge.spi, base E3A4CD239079 -> EB3A98054CC9, 104 lines, max cell 256, widest 120): offsets_of all cursor = items consumed per feed (original length - remaining), and resumed all offsets = the cursor rebuilt by dropping that many. That is the agreed URL cursor (?f=<feed ids>&c=<raw offsets>, lost included). Helpers are tail-recursive with accumulators (length_from, dropped), since one real feed holds 125k posts; consumed/resumed_from recurse only per FEED. 3 new tests: offsets_count_each_feed_consumed ([1;2;0] after a 3-post page), resumed_offsets_page_like_the_cursor (the resumed page equals the cursor's), offsets_past_the_end_or_missing_resume_safely (offset 9 on a 1-item feed empties it, a missing offset counts as 0). Rides x-next5. PRE-REGISTERED addition to x-next5's rule: feed_merge notebook gate exit 0 with spiral-tests failed=0 over all 6 tests (3 existing + 3 new); else exit 8 = FAIL. Next: the text codec (?f/&c parse and print) and timeline_serve.spi on top.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_10 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 10u32, "2026-11-04T06:25Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:25 x: DESIGN BLOCKER found before building the route's render bridge. The timeline_page draft (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\timeline_page.spi) opens html's 'model' and 'render' units, but apps/client declares packages = ['|core-', 'spiral-'] only, so html's units aren't visible and the draft can't compile as is. (Its package.spiproj and spiral.toml drafts equal live, leftovers of the landed feed_merge registration.) THREE OPTIONS: (a) client depends on the html repo package: a cross-repo dep, so x's CI must also check out html; (b) html's block model + renderer move to lib (lib-first; any repo could render pages); (c) the sim route emits its own minimal HTML (no dependency, but a second renderer to keep escaped and correct). Leaning (b), by the lib-first rule and since html's units already gate on Gleam. But it moves another lane's code, so it's a decision to record, not to take silently. Until decided, the route's pure parts stand (feed_merge cursor, timeline_serve query codec, both in queued runs), and the bridge waits.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_11 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 11u32, "2026-11-04T06:43Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:43 x: RENDER UNBLOCKED by main's (b) decision (html's block model + renderer move to lib; see HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES). timeline_page now opens lib markup + doc_blocks + doc_render (+ protocol for post_id, which the old draft never opened: a latent ETY-UnboundVariable that the first europa check caught). Registered after run_signals in both client lists, on x-next6's (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-PAGE). Europa pack33 --check on the stacked context (x-next5b + x-next6 drafts + the lib doc overlay): exit 0. Lands after the doc move lands in lib and x-next6 lands; its 3 tests then run in that run's notebook gate. Remaining for the route: timeline_serve's handler (world feeds -> merged_page -> page html), the next draft.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_12 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 12u32, "2026-11-04T06:49Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:49 x: timeline_page draft final = E9FEA5CE9BED (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-PAGE): sample_entry now puns the record like posts' entry_at (params named after the fields; the record fixes their types), 302 -> under 272; 0 over-272 cells; respell clean; europa --check exit 0 in the stacked context. Client lists B7E2FD8F33F1 / EB5EE0B3BC2F (timeline_page after run_signals).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_13 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 13u32, "2026-11-04T06:55Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:55 x: ROUTE CORE drafted (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-ROUTE\\timeline_serve.spi F00540CC8A4E, on x-next5b's frozen 6E893B50869E): feed_item = username * post term; page_of feeds cursor budget = feed_merge::merged_page over feed_merge::resumed (raw offsets), with newer_item = strictly newer by sim_serve::newer_or_same (the id tie-break), then visible drops lost posts and renders via timeline_page::plain_entry. It returns the next raw offsets. Test a_page_hides_lost_posts_but_counts_them: a lost post mid-page is hidden ([t4; t2]) yet counted ([1; 2]). timeline_page gains plain_entry id username created_at text (sample_entry is now a one-liner over it; 2F0208B46FE8). Europa --check exit 0 for both in the full stacked context. Next: the HTTP side (GET /timeline?f=..&c=.. -> page_of -> timeline_html plus a next link with cursor_query), with feeds sorted ONCE at boot.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_14 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 14u32, "2026-11-04T08:00Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:00 x: TYPEFEATURESET in the route (main relayed kit's census: x/apps trails every typed-modeling column, GADT 1.3/kloc, existential 0). 'Never render a lost post' is now a TYPE guarantee, not a convention: a phantom-indexed GADT feed_post kind = ShownPost :: term -> feed_post shown_kind | LostPost :: term -> feed_post lost_kind (index bound explicitly per constructor, the safe form against the implicit-existential export-erasure bug; mirrors html's page index_page/file_page). Only 'surviving' builds a shown_item (alias string * feed_post shown_kind); entry_of and so the renderer accept ONLY shown_item, so a lost post can't reach the page by type. visible = fold kept + rev + each entry_of. Draft 7EAFD8EEC78E (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-ROUTE), max cell 267, europa --check exit 0. The first importer (the HTTP entry) will be the export-erasure check. Next typed candidates in x per the census: feed_cursor indexed by its feed count; run_signal as a GADT indexed by kind (step vs finished).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_15 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 15u32, "2026-11-04T10:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:02 x: route feed_of added (draft 891E13B89C3D): a user's posts raw (lost included, so the cursor's raw offsets stay valid), with_author, sorted ONCE with lib list_sort::sorted_by newer_post (landed 05:4x), paired with the username. Checked with the page and the full x-next5b/6 stack on a NEW-layout lib stage (spiral.toml, modules from files): timeline_page and timeline_serve both --check exit 0. (On the old-layout stage, list_sort was unregistered; that was the stage, not the draft.)")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_16 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 16u32, "2026-11-04T10:39Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:39 x: COORDINATION with x-dumps (the user directed them to finish the joined-timeline items). Split sent: x-dumps takes the posts.spi typed-model extension now (in none of x's drafts). The sim fixes, timeline_serve, feed_merge, world, cells_executor, build/sim-shell and the sim lists are IN FLIGHT in x-next5c (hash-guarded, with 3 runs stacked on them), and the page, route core, codec split, publisher and hook are queued in x-next6..8 on those bases, so those stay with x until they land. Then each landed file is free for x-dumps. Offered x-dumps the route's HTTP entry after x-next6.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_17 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 17u32, "2026-11-04T10:41Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:41 x: AGREED with x-dumps: x-dumps owns (1) the posts.spi typed-model extension now (sends x the landed hash; x rebases later drafts on it) and (2) the route's GET /timeline HTTP entry, starting AFTER x-next6 lands (it sits on that base). x OWES x-dumps two pings: when x-next5c lands (posts consumers ready to rebase) and when x-next6 lands (the HTTP entry can start). x keeps the in-flight and queued stack (x-next5c..8, page, route core).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_18 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 18u32, "2026-11-04T11:02Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:02 x: GROOM. Rendering input (x-dumps, real corpus): fate removed = 153,437 of 163,307 posts (geygey suspended), standing 5,010, lost 4,860. So the page's removal note must be ONE compact line per post (not a block), since nearly every scrolled post carries it. Lost posts never render (the route's GADT). Next for the page: a compact removal marker in entry_blocks once posts' fate reaches the entry (after x-next6 lands posts.spi's survival model).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_19 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 19u32, "2026-11-04T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:34 x: x-next5c (job-1793782508291, pinned core 0758BAF4, 2 h 32 min) PASSED its pre-registered rule and LANDED (9 hash-guarded drafts + 42 regenerated outputs, 0 conflicts): sim accept 0 with NO fixture changed, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, all Rust units under 1k, census SAME over 77, notebook gate one fresh process per file: feed_merge 6/6, timeline_serve 4/4 (x-next5b's 3/4 was the stale warm server). LANDED for this item: feed_merge.spi EB3A98054CC9 (offsets_of/resumed) and the new timeline_serve.spi 6E893B50869E (page_cursor URL codec), registered in the sim lists. Next: x-next6 (launching), then the page/route core.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_20 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 20u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "x", "2026-11-04 22:16 x: GROOM, progress 30 -> 70 with evidence. Tonight's /timeline work belongs here (it was recorded on X-SOTA-MODEL notes 11-04 18:4x-21:3x). LIVE for the user via x-dumps on the real 5-account joined world: one newest-first timeline; the two fc1943s accounts split by id; cursor pagination; feeds cached in the world (0.03-0.15 s per page); natural-run sort (feed build 12.2 -> 2.6 s); a preconnect crash found and fixed. Built in demo xprobe12 and handed to x-dumps: SIM_PORT stable port, infinite scroll, authorship labels (Reply / Repost of, muted / Quoting + blockquote), parser bounds checks. PENDING (not landed): all of it sits in x-next9 drafts (X-TIMELINE-PAGE/ROUTE/ENTRY plus lib LIB-HTTP-SERVER-BOUNDS and LIB-ERLANG-RAW-TCP), behind x-next7 (job-1793840045834, pending on the node) and x-next8. The remaining 30 pct: land x-next8/9 through node proofs, browser-confirm the scroll, and per-request isolation (needs compiler support for a try/catch in generated Gleam).")
