inl org_exit_fallout () = Task ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", "CI and link fallout from the user moving dir-tree-html and polyglot out of the i574n org (11-03: 'this way we can eventually finish all tasks til the end while fixing errors while they appear, in ci etc'). dir-tree-html is now fc1943s/dir-tree-html (the i574n URL redirects); polyglot is fc1943s/polyglot (NO redirect from i574n/polyglot). Local copies stay at C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html and C:\\home\\git\\polyglot as sources until their absorption items close. SITES (git grep 11-03, tracked files): (a) clones through the redirect: spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (used by publish-tree.ps1 for every gh-pages run, and directly by alphabet init, dice init/publish-bin, tapas2 init/publish, mechahaze-album1 publish) and i574n.github scripts/init.ps1 + build.ps1. They work while the redirect holds; the real fix is HTML-ADOPT-REPOS (the shim switches to html's release); if a run fails first, pin the clone to fc1943s/dir-tree-html at a643950e. (b) dead link: i574n.github profile/README.md -> i574n.github.io/polyglot/lib/math/math.spi.html; point it at zeta's page in spiral once ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE lands, or drop the line. (c) docs: i574n.github docs/agents/agent-sync.md lists polyglot as a core repo. (d) workspaces: i574n.code-workspace and i574n-deps.code-workspace include ../polyglot. (e) inventory scripts that still list polyglot: spiral apps/compiler/scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1, parser-corpus-gate.ps1, apps/compiler/tmp/formatter/extract-corpus.ps1; i574n.github pins.ps1, pages-sweep.ps1, recovered-drafts-census.ps1. (f) spiral apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1:141 falls back to polyglot/deps for the VS Code plugin; apps/compiler/AGENTS.md says 'the polyglot builder'. (g) dotfiles dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1 calls polyglot's Supervisor (dead). (h) watch each repo's next CI run (gh run list) after the user's pushes; every red caused by the move is fixed here. OUT OF SCOPE: the fc1943s and fc1943s.github repos (dump org, polyglot is theirs now), singularity's data, the upstream fork's conditional fsproj path, and compiler source comments that record history. DONE: (a)-(g) fixed or ruled out with a reason, and one green CI run per affected repo.", Story, P0, D3, 90u32, Blocked, "", "ci,org,polyglot,dir-tree-html,drift,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_org_exit_fallout () = Planning ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_1 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 1u32, "2026-11-03T09:30Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:3x FIXED (unstaged), from reading each red CI run:\n(1) i574n/.github CI RED since the user's 23:17 push (runs at 23:17 and 07:43): scripts/workflow.ps1:13 dot-sourced ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 ('The term ... is not recognized'). That was main's own 11-02 regression: init.ps1 stopped cloning polyglot, but workflow.ps1 still read it. Now '. ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1', like build/outdated/publish.ps1 (init clones spiral first). Parses.\n(2) d: i574n.code-workspace drops the polyglot folder and polyglot/workspace/Cargo.toml from rust-analyzer.linkedProjects; i574n-deps.code-workspace points at ../spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language. Both parse as JSON.\n(3) c: docs/agents/agent-sync.md no longer lists polyglot as a core repo or a deps clone.\n(4) b: profile/README.md's math link now points to https://fc1943s.github.io/polyglot/lib/math/math.dib.html (HEAD 200; the old i574n URL and math.spi.html are 404). It moves to zeta's page under ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE.\n(5) e (i574n.github half): pins/pins.ps1 orgRepos now matches the org (gh repo list i574n): dir-tree-html and polyglot out, html and regex in. pins/workflows.spi drops the dir_tree_html and polyglot workflow definitions plus their 7 target rows (306 -> 275 lines; backup %TEMP%\\workflows.spi.before-org-exit). Node compile: RUST-FAILED for workflows AND the untouched pins_check, so it is the node's stale spiral checkout (MIRROR-RESYNC-1103), not this edit; it is re-run after the resync. html's gh-pages.yml is not modelled in pins yet (add with HTML-CI-RELEASE).\nSTILL OPEN: e (pages-sweep.ps1 and recovered-drafts-census.ps1 default repo lists; spiral apps/compiler scripts lib-usage-census, parser-corpus-gate, extract-corpus, env.ps1:141 and AGENTS.md, which are compiler's tree); g (dotfiles' appdata build uses polyglot's Supervisor); scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1 (a finished one-off, deletion candidate after a stem grep).\nOTHER REDS, NOT FROM THE MOVE: html (the 1000-line gate, markdown/entry.rs 2339 lines; HTML-CI-RELEASE) and tibia (LunarG 'latest' = 1.4.363.1 has no Windows runtime zip, 404). The tibia one is fixed in spiral/scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1: it tries 'latest', then the published versions newest first (vulkan.lunarg.com/sdk/versions/windows.json). Tested end to end on the box: it picks 1.4.363.0, and the zip carries x64/vulkan-1.dll. Lands when the user pushes spiral.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_2 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:34Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:4x MORE FIXED (unstaged): e, i574n.github half: scripts/pages-sweep.ps1 and recovered-drafts-census.ps1 default repo lists match the org (polyglot and dir-tree-html out, html and regex in; both parse). scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1 DELETED: a finished one-off migration (SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT Done), referenced only by backlog notes and itself (stem grep over every repo); git history keeps it. g: dotfiles dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1 now builds appdata.spi -> appdata.py through spiral's BuildSpiral -Backend Python instead of polyglot's Supervisor (parses). Its PROOF (compile + python run + same .appdata.toml.txt as before) runs after MIRROR-RESYNC-1103, on the node, or on the box once kit's TRAIN14c heavy window ends. e/f in spiral apps/compiler (5 sites) are handed to compiler (its tree). LEFT: the dotfiles proof, the pins compile re-run, compiler's 5 sites, and green runs after the user's pushes (.github: the workflow.ps1 fix; tibia: the Vulkan fallback in spiral).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_3 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 3u32, "2026-11-03T09:38Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:4x compiler: apps/compiler sites FIXED (unstaged, each .ps1 parse-checked). scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1 default repos: polyglot dropped, eoie -> kit. scripts/parser-corpus-gate.ps1 repo loop: polyglot -> kit. scripts/env.ps1 Get-SpiralPackageDir: the polyglot/deps fallback is gone; it still resolves spiral's deps/The-Spiral-Language (checked). tmp/formatter/extract-corpus.ps1 'user' corpus: now read from a bare cache clone of https://github.com/fc1943s/polyglot (LOCALAPPDATA/spiral-bin/corpus-src/polyglot.git, cloned on first use) at the same pinned bb856d13, which is on fc1943s/main (checked with branch -r --contains), so it survives POLYGLOT-RETIRE without vendoring 86 files / 577 KB. AGENTS.md: the stale 'build.ps1 in this directory packages ... with the polyglot builder' line is removed (no such file; the build is scripts/build.ps1). Also fixed beyond the five: tmp/AGENTS.md (core fallback wording) and tmp/README.md Upstream (the fork lives at spiral's deps/The-Spiral-Language). Left as history: tmp/AGENTS.md formatter note about dice's deps\\polyglot loop, and the contract sample name contract_cross_abi_polyglot_lowering.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_4 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 4u32, "2026-11-03T10:18Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:4x .github CI, second blocker found and FIXED (unstaged): workflow.ps1 also runs pins/pins.ps1, which now compiles (it had been failing on the node only because of the stale lib) and reported 3 workflow files differing from the typed source (scripts/pins/workflows.spi). The lanes had edited committed workflows without the model: i574n.github gh-pages.yml (an apps/graphs/build.ps1 step, if ubuntu, continue-on-error), spiral gh-pages.yml (the cells-gate job's transformer model cache step plus ci_gate -Roots lib/spiral,apps/transformer), and kit gh-pages.yml (env CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=0). Modelled all three: workflow.spi run_step gained continue_on_error (rendered after the body) plus a soft_run_if constructor; workflows.spi has the graphs step, a transformer_model_cache step and the kit env. pins.ps1 on the box: 'workflows: 0 workflow files differ from the typed source', exit 0. Backups %TEMP%\\pins-workflow.spi.bak, pins-workflows.spi.bak2. RULE for lanes: a workflow edit goes through scripts/pins/workflows.spi, or .github CI turns red.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_5 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T10:19Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:5x g RESOLVED BY DELETION, not a port. The box proof of the ported dotfiles build failed in the compiler, not the port: appdata.spi is edition-2 Spiral against an old lib backend union (ETY-UnionsCannotBeApplied on 'Rust None' / 'Rust (Wasm |> Some)', and ETY-UnboundVariable 'Python'). CHECK before deleting: nothing reads its output .appdata.toml.txt (git grep over dotfiles, spiral, kit, i574n.github, x and tibia; the only mention was main's own note), its builder was polyglot's dead Supervisor, it was last touched 2025-11-28, and it carried tracked .py files (no-py rule). So it is STALE by the 11-03 rule: DELETED dist/appdata/spiral (5 tracked files, unstaged; git history keeps them). The rest of dist/appdata (FancyZones, rider, vscode, read by src/windows/install-sudo.ps1) is untouched.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_6 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:50Z", "tibia", "11-03 13:5x tibia: one more fallout site of the polyglot exit, found in tibia CI and FIXED by main in spiral (unstaged, lands with the user spiral push): polyglot scripts/init.ps1 line 151 built the Spiral CLI (deps/spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1), and spiral scripts/init-app-build.ps1, which every app switched to, did not. Cells runs every lua target through that CLI (spiral lua --lua-path), so on CI every lua target became unavailable; files whose only target is lua turned unsupported and the gate went red (tibia Ubuntu since d4ad52ad: combat_text, game_calls, samples, ground_trace, competitor). Fix: init-app-build.ps1 builds the CLI with apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1 when workspace/target/release/spiral[.exe] is missing (main). Affects every app on init-app-build (fiscal, blog, kit, x, dir-tree-html, html, regex, tibia). Proof = the first app CI run after the push with 0 unsupported lua rows. Details: TIBIA-1-0-DOD n5, POLYGLOT-RETIRE n25-n26.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_7 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 7u32, "2026-11-03T18:31Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x BLOCKED (not idle): every site from the move is fixed in the tree (i574n.github workflow.ps1/pins/workspaces/README/scripts, compiler's apps/compiler sites, dotfiles' dead build deleted, spiral init-wgsl-run fallback for tibia, init-app-build CLI build; i574n.github init/build no longer clone dir-tree-html; no workflow references either repo). Remaining: confirm CI green after the user's pushes of i574n.github, spiral and html. RESUME WHEN: any of those HEADs moves (i574n.github 5245678, spiral 98e51d32, html 05a1a436).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_8 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 8u32, "2026-11-05T04:13Z", "main", "11-05 00:13 main CI RED from main's own init-app-build CLI step (n7), found from fiscal's report. spiral faf422c9 (user push 11-04 23:18, run 41960731928) and fiscal bb1ebad (run 41960782740) are both red, with two causes and no change in the CLI itself (apps/spiral and its committed spiral.rs are identical to the last green, 98e51d32). (1) Ordering: init.ps1 line 14 runs init-app-build.ps1, which now builds the CLI and its run check, but sccache was only installed at init.ps1:78, while the CLI hard-sets RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache (spiral.spi:256). Result: \"could not execute process sccache ... rustc -vV\" on ubuntu (rust, protocol-rust-build). (2) Layout: fiscal clones spiral to deps/spiral and runs init-app-build. file_system.get_workspace_root maps .../deps to its parent and then needs a sibling spiral/workspace checkout (the old polyglot layout), which a runner lacks, so every backend panics \"Option does not have a value\" (spiral.rs 19405/20376/20669/21359). FIX (unstaged; scripts only, no CLI regen): init-app-build.ps1 installs cargo-binstall and sccache BEFORE the CLI build (the block moved out of init.ps1, which still installs trunk after it), and sets SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT to its own checkout when unset, which get_workspace_root honors before any walk. Both parse clean. PENDING: CI on the user's next spiral push, then fiscal's. Follow-up: later CLI uses in a deps layout (fiscal's Cells lua runs) need SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT in the job env too, or a lib fallback in get_workspace_root (deps search fails -> use the deps/spiral checkout itself).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_9 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 9u32, "2026-11-05T04:48Z", "main", "11-05 00:48 main LIB FALLBACK (fiscal's choice over a per-step env var): draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-WORKSPACE-ROOT-DEPS\\file_system.spi (AB1B2AFC5F06, base A981A5951BF8). New deps_workspace_root: a found root named deps still prefers an outer spiral/workspace checkout (unchanged), else it returns the deps dir itself, so the root becomes deps/spiral instead of panicking; SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT still wins first. Test a_deps_root_without_an_outer_checkout_keeps_its_own_spiral. Round trip clean (lib_land_window dry run). First notebook gate VOID twice: once in a bare lib copy (packages unbound outside a repo), once cgroup-killed during mix setup while another lane's 1.5 GB rustc ran on europa; it is re-armed to start after that build, in a -Mirror main-ws copy. Then the two-step land (node proof + box -ProvenLog). Ships with the user's next spiral push, together with the init-app-build sccache/SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT fix (n8).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_10 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 10u32, "2026-11-05T06:42Z", "main", "11-05 02:42 main LANDED (unstaged, rides the user's next spiral push): lib/spiral/file_system.spi A981A5951BF8 -> AB1B2AFC5F06 (deps_workspace_root: a found root named deps still prefers an outer spiral/workspace checkout, else uses deps/spiral itself instead of panicking; SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT still wins first). Two-step land: node proof (mirror main-proven, Windows) control 40/42 with the 2 failures being 300 s cell TIMEOUTS (VOID, node at 100% under TRAIN27), draft 43/43; node close green (signatures 13 unchanged, spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26/26, type_probe 43 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift); box close green from -ProvenLog (lib had moved, so fast checks reran; document_test taken from the proof), undo %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-023639. With the init-app-build fix (n8), the fiscal deps-layout panic and the sccache ordering are both fixed in the tree; a fresh-runner test of init on a codespace is running now.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_11 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 11u32, "2026-11-05T06:50Z", "main", "11-05 02:50 main FRESH-RUNNER PROOF of the init fix (before the user's push): codespace miniature-meme-x7jqqp6pp3v957 (Ubuntu 24.04, 4 cores, no Rust, no sccache, no cargo-binstall), spiral HEAD faf422c9 cloned with the box's fixed scripts/init-app-build.ps1 (886B46344C30) and init.ps1 dropped in; rustup + nightly-2026-10-18 minimal installed first, as setup-rust does in CI. init.ps1 -> init-app-build: cargo-binstall --self-install, then \"cargo binstall sccache\" (sccache v0.19.0 -> ~/.cargo/bin, 2.7 s), THEN apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1: run check rust exit 0 \"spiral-check-rust 42\" (the CI red case), cuda/lua/gleam 42, protocol cases as expected, no FAILED / RUST-FAILED line; init continued (trunk via binstall). So the sccache-ordering red is fixed for every repo whose CI runs spiral init. The deps/spiral panic fix is the file_system.spi land (n10). PENDING: CI on the user's next push.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_12 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 12u32, "2026-11-06T12:04Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:2x lint fill: Blocked on the user's spiral push (the init-order fix proven on a fresh codespace 11-05); resume when the push lands, then check each repo's CI.")
inl scheduler_model_move () = Task ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", "Move polyglot's scheduler model (apps/scheduler/Tasks.spi, 214 lines, last edited 10-25) to i574n.github/apps/scheduler, as decided by POLYGLOT-RETIRE n21 (polyglot left the org 11-03; the local copy is the source). It is a typed task-scheduling model: task_id/task_name nominals, manual_scheduling, recurrency_offset, fixed_recurrency and scheduling unions over date_time, action events, plus a terminal calendar printer. STEPS: (1) respell to edition 3: 'test x =' becomes ':# x =' with distinct names; the '/// ##' heading comments go (no-comment rule); field access becomes '::'; module calls follow the current lib spelling; (2) keep its 4 tests (get_actions, get_actions_2, cols, lines) on their zig target, adding rust; (3) a package.spiproj next to it, the way apps/graphs has one; (4) gate it on the node with memo off (after MIRROR-RESYNC-1103); (5) then rule out the polyglot copy. DONE: every test is green on the node, the file follows kit standards, and POLYGLOT-RETIRE notes the move.", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", "polyglot,migration,typefeatureset,i574n.github,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_scheduler_model_move () = Planning ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl node_versioned_spiral_source () = Task ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", "Versioned spiral source on the nodes, so the shared lib can be updated while lanes' jobs run (memory deploys-never-wait-for-idle). TODAY: every node mirror links deps to the node's C:\\home\\git\\<repo>\\deps, and those link spiral to the ONE mutable checkout C:\\home\\git\\spiral. A sync either waits for a node that is never idle (MIRROR-RESYNC-1103 waited 2 h behind 5+ jobs) or swaps files under running jobs. DESIGN: sync spiral into C:\\home\\remote\\spiral-src\\<head-digest> (immutable once built, runner included); remote.ps1 sync links each NEW mirror's spiral to the current version directory, so a job keeps the version it started with; a 'current' pointer moves atomically; old versions are deleted when no running job's mirror links them (kit job list plus a junction scan). The same on europa. DONE: a sync under 3 running jobs changes none of their inputs (proven by hashing their mirror's lib before and after), and new jobs see the new head.", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "node,europa,mirror,remote,deploy,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_node_versioned_spiral_source () = Planning ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl linked_units_shared_instances () = Task ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", "Linked units re-emit generic union instantiations per crate: a core list (or option) instantiated over a linked unit's union (list inline, list block) is emitted as its own enum in every crate that uses it, so a list crossing a link: boundary fails rustc E0308. The defining linked unit should own the instantiation (pub) and every linking crate should import it, like the user unions it already imports", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", "team:compiler,compiler,linked-units,rust,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_linked_units_shared_instances () = Planning ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl html_lint_heal () = Task ("HTML-LINT-HEAL", "Heal html's kit standards findings (73 on 11-03, after kit's new lint rule). 64 x rec-outside-cycle ('^ on a definition in no recursion cycle'; '^' means rec, not join point): inline_parse 15, markdown 15, render 12, tree 8, model 7, pages 4, file_views 3. HTML-MODEL wrote ':~ ^' on non-recursive helpers, believing '^' marked join points. 9 x line-width (file_views 61/63, inline_parse 112, markdown 145, pages 82/84, tree 30/112/119), all predating 11-03. RULE for each '^' removal: html src stays green, and the generated markdown/entry.rs and cli/html.rs line counts must not grow (a '^' change can alter inlining). Measure before and after on the node. Do it after HTML-MARKDOWN's raw-item fix lands and before the unit split, so each file churns once. DONE: kit standards on html/src reports 0.", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "html,lint,standards,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_html_lint_heal () = Planning ("HTML-LINT-HEAL", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl cells_lua_host_crash () = Task ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", "Cells: 'spiral lua' host exits 0xC0000005 (access violation) intermittently under node load; plus compiler port lock_timeout", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,lua,flaky,node,team:compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_lua_host_crash () = Planning ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl spiral_nameof_typed () = Task ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", "Typed names beyond the met nameof DoD: case_name returns a phantom-tagged name t (not a bare string) so names of different unions do not mix, name styles (exact/lower/snake/kebab) applied at compile time, qualified module::case names, and a GADT-indexed case table whose length is known at compile time", Story, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-NAMEOF", "team:compiler,compiler,typefeatureset,nameof", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_nameof_typed () = Planning ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl kit_heal_nameof () = Task ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", "kit heal nameof <repo>...: drive lib nameof_heal over git-tracked .spi and heal kit's hand-kept case<->string maps by reflection", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,team:rig,granular,typefeatureset,reflection", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_heal_nameof () = Planning ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_heal_nameof_1 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", 1u32, "2026-11-03T12:50Z", "kit", "Filed 11-03 09:0x from compiler (SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL n5): lib/spiral/nameof_heal.spi has findings (source) (tokens) : list finding {kind ToName|OfName; first_line; arms; cases}. Census: 30 findings / 144 arms across 7 repos, 20 of them (108 arms) in kit (kit_adoption_habits 17, window_model 9, command_spec_domain 8, toolchain receipt 8), plus kit's own new kit_style_probes probe_word (19 arms; it was untracked at census time). PLAN: (1) the verb kit heal nameof <repo>... in a typed entry crate (x shape): list git-tracked .spi (skip samples/state/deps), run SpiralCompiler tokens <file> through lib process, call nameof_heal.findings, print typed rows file/line/kind/arms and a count per repo; (2) heal kit's rows with reflection (union_case_suffix + sm'.to_lower or a kebab helper), probe_word first (its words are kebab: gadt-case, wide-host-macro). Parent: KIT-CATCH-UP.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_nameof_2 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", 2u32, "2026-11-03T16:02Z", "kit", "11-03 11:5x kit: HEALED in the tree (unproven) now that lib sm'.kebab_of has landed. A scan found every match whose arms all return kebab(case name minus a shared prefix), checked CASE-SENSITIVELY: the first pass was case-insensitive and passed rust_tool_environment's RUSTC wrongly. 16 maps became 'sm'.kebab_of (union_reflection.cases.union_case_suffix PREFIX x)': kit_style_probes.probe_word (21 arms), lease_phase_text, legacy_word, sort_word, effect_name, toolchain_action_name, rust_tool_identity, ceremony_word, program_family_word, amendable_word, settled_word (payload cases too), lint class_word, verdict_word, standard_word, toolchain_action_name_label; plus window_model class_word/window_event_word under S2. rust_tool_environment is now to_upper (rust_tool_identity tool), not a second map. Kept as-is: query_filter_text (computed strings), phase_word (snake_case output). Proof: probes.spi 2/2 on europa; the healed packages' 10 test files and the regen of their 86-package consumer closure run in the europa round-2 job.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_nameof_3 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", 3u32, "2026-11-09T06:54Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:4x local rig: the verb EXISTS in the TRAIN41 kit (kit heal nameof <dir>...) and the 11-03 heal turned 16 hand maps into reflection, so most of this item is done; but running it on the rig tree PANICS after 130 s: rig_nameof_findings findings.rs:795 start byte index 12 is not a char boundary (inside é). Root cause in the LIB: lib/spiral/nameof_heal.spi token_of line 38 takes sm'.substring from (near - from) of a source line, where from/near are the compiler tokens' CHARACTER columns, while sm'.substring on the Rust backend slices BYTES; any line with a multi-byte character before a token panics. Handed to compiler (lib owner of nameof_heal) with two fix options (char-indexed substring for token columns, or byte offsets from tokens). Blocked on that lib fix; then rerun the verb on rig and count the remaining maps.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_nameof_4 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", 4u32, "2026-11-09T06:58Z", "compiler", "11-09 03:0x compiler: LIB FIX for rig's report (kit heal nameof panicked: findings.rs:795 'start byte index 12 is not a char boundary; it is inside é'): nameof_heal.spi token_of sliced compiler token columns (CHARACTER columns) with sm'::substring, which slices BYTES on Rust. New char_slice: Rust arm chars().skip(from).take(count) into Rc<str>, default arm the old byte substring; token_of uses it. Proof (ganymede, pack64): lib --check rc 0, format --check rc 0, a Rust build of char_slice on a line starting with é returns the right token (exit 42). Regression test added (///> rust) token_columns_count_characters_not_bytes. Unstaged; rides kit's next regen.")
