inl note_of_granular_split_state_core_1 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE", 1u32, "2026-11-03T15:11Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:2x (GRANULAR-STATS): 2nd and 5th largest lib definitions, both leptos UI hooks with step-by-step log lines (198-line use_core_database). FIRST: stem-grep consumers across repos (dangling-check-by-stem); if none is live, rule out with bold removal. Otherwise PLAN: each logged step becomes a named function, the hook composes them.")
inl note_of_granular_split_state_core_2 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:18Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:3x CONSUMER CHECK (tracked .spi/.spir/.ps1/.toml/.spiproj in 12 repos): LIVE consumer = dice ui (ui/src/state.spi, ui/src/hooks/use_transactions.spi, ui/src/components/home.spi); kit only mentions it in lint baselines/evidence. So NOT a rule-out: split. Proof path for the split: dice ui's wasm/leptos build compiles and its pages render the same (dice CI's gh-pages), plus the lib state_core notebook if it has tests; land via drafts + lib_land. Heavy-ish build -> run it on a remote machine.")
inl note_of_granular_split_state_core_3 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE", 3u32, "2026-11-07T22:12Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. DoD: use_requests and use_core_database each split into named steps under the 280-char cell budget, with dice ui (the live consumer) building and its notebooks green. Next step: list use_requests' branches as candidate step names. TypeFeatures: request states as a union (Idle | Loading | Loaded of data | Failed of string) instead of string flags.")
inl note_of_granular_split_state_core_4 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:4x NEXT STEP DONE (step names from the hooks' own log labels; lib/spiral/state_core.spi 648 lines). use_requests (330-648, runs to EOF): (1) entry + use_database, (2) database_memo, (5) state_data_func, plus the unlabeled tail that maps requests -> result vec; candidate named steps: requests_database_memo, requests_state_data, requests_results. use_core_database (113-329): (1) entry, (4) effect core_state_heap, (7)-(10) four signal_update effects (dark_mode, debug, url_hash, data: one generic signal_sync step applied 4x), (11) loading memo, (13) set_core_state_heap_action, (18) effect new_core_state_heap; candidate steps: core_heap_effect, signal_sync (x4), loading_memo, heap_action, new_heap_effect. The gaps in the numbering ((3), (6), (12), (14)-(17)) are steps whose log lines were removed earlier; their code still sits between the labeled ones. Constraint: each step is a closure over the hook's signals, so the split passes those signals as a record (a typed hook_context) rather than 6-8 positional args. Proof: dice ui's wasm/leptos build + render (heavy: a node or CI run), then lib_land_window. Next step: write the hook_context record and lift signal_sync first (4 identical blocks, the biggest budget win).")
inl note_of_granular_split_state_core_5 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T17:32Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09 DECOMPOSITION PLAN (next-step done: branches listed from the log-delimited steps in state_core.spi). Both hooks already self-document their steps via leptos::log \"state_core.<hook> (N) / <what>\" markers = natural split boundaries.\nuse_requests (lines 335+, 20 log steps) -> candidate named steps the hook composes: database_memo_step (2); request_resource_step (3, state_data_resource new_local_resource); state_data_func_step (4-6, the func + result); requests_signal_step (7,13); state_data_signal_step (8-9); url_effect_step (10,12); set_data_error_step (11); result_finalize_step (18,20).\nuse_core_database (lines 113+, 18 log steps) -> database_resource_step (2-3, incl error); core_state_heap_effect_step (4-6); signal_updates_step (7-10: dark_mode/debug/url_hash/data signal_update); loading_memo_step (11-12); loaded_heap_step (13-15: database=None / loaded / new_core_state_heap); finalize_loaded_step (16-17: dark_mode_loading, set_loaded).\nTYPED SHAPE (per DoD): request/data state as a union Idle | Loading | Loaded of data | Failed of string replacing the string-flag logs. Each step a named function under the 280-char cell budget; the hook = a short composition calling them.\nIMPLEMENTATION (the heavy, remaining part, NOT done here): write the step fns + compose, then VERIFY the live consumer (dice ui src/state.spi, hooks/use_transactions.spi, components/home.spi) builds (wasm/leptos, a heavy remote build) and its gh-pages notebooks stay green, landed via lib_land_window (a shared-lib edit - do not touch outside the window, per the file_system.spi lesson). That is a dedicated lib-land effort with a node build, not a light-round task; org owns it.")
inl note_of_granular_split_state_core_6 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T19:56Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 15:5x: STEP-1 DRAFT done (signal_sync lift = the biggest budget win, note 4). Draft at LOCALAPPDATA/kit/drafts/spiral/GRANULAR-SPLIT-STATE-CORE/signal_sync_lift.patch.md: a generic top-level inl signal_sync forall a. (label) (sig) (v) that logs + signal_updates, replacing the 4 near-identical signal_update blocks (steps 7-10 dark_mode/debug/url_hash/data, lines 188-206) with 4 one-liners (~20 lines to helper+4 calls). Field value types differ (bool/bool/std_string/core_state_data) so generic over a; helper reads only its args so top-level reusable, not hook-local. UNVERIFIED: authored only, NOT applied to the live shared lib state_core.spi (do not edit outside the lib_land_window per the file_system.spi lesson; a train snapshots WIP). Box zero compute (text only). NEXT (window-gated + heavy): apply signal_sync + the other candidate steps + the typed Idle|Loading|Loaded of data|Failed of string union, then dice-ui wasm/leptos build + gh-pages notebooks green, land via lib_land.")
