inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_1 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 1u32, "2026-11-03T17:07Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x SPLIT from REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED. Why separate: the bench's timed region already excludes table construction (TableArm 'minimal DFA as an array table' runs at 0.06x of the minimal DFA from a prepared table), so a compile-time table can only win on SETUP. DoD: a bench row for prepare time (certified_of + table_of) per workload vs a staged table produced by Spiral's partial evaluation for a literal pattern, A/A in band; plus the same match verdicts as the runtime table on the agreement words.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_2 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 2u32, "2026-11-07T22:17Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. Next step: measure the setup time of 5 literal patterns with lazy DFA vs a compile-time staged table on the regex bench, as the go/no-go number.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_3 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T05:50Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 02:1x SCOPE GROWS (from the 11-08 legacy re-map + REGEX-ABSORB-TYPED-CORE): besides the setup-time staged table for literal patterns, this item now owns the two MISSING legacy concepts, item 10 (static_* twins + compile-time discharge) and item 29 (staged DFA), and the typed core GENERATION: typed.spi's 16-state core is typed by hand because its size is a type (Peano n16, fin n16 targets), so generating it from certified_of r can only be compile-time staging (partial evaluation emitting the vector n bit_row), never a runtime step. Keep the 11-03 go/no-go first: measure the setup time of 5 literal patterns (certified_of + table_of vs a staged table) on a node; if staging wins nothing on setup, record the typed-core generation as the one remaining reason to stage. Estimate 150 m stays for the measurement slice; the generation slice gets its own child if the measurement says go.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_4 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T07:00Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 03:1x GO/NO-GO MEASUREMENT WRITTEN (regex/bench/bench.spi, unstaged): per workload the report now prints a setup line under the facts head: setup_ms = mean of 25 certified_of r + table_of builds (the dead index summed so the builds cannot be dropped), next to the median of one array-table pass over the 400 words (TableArm nanos / 25 over the 15 rounds). A compile-time staged table can save at most the setup number, so the decision rule is: if setup is under one table pass on every workload, staging wins nothing on setup and the only remaining reason to stage is the typed-core generation (REGEX-ABSORB-TYPED-CORE); if setup dominates (expected for EighthFromEnd at 256 states), staging is a go for those shapes. The 6 bench workloads stand in for the 5 literal patterns; the build runs on ganymede, not the box. Proof: pending in step 1 (org2-regex-measure, full build.ps1: cells + bench) of the ganymede org2-regex-chain, mirror synced sha 1b48ed17; the step greps the h2 + setup lines from report.html. Next step: read those lines and record the verdict.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_5 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T07:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 04:5x Proof MOVED: step 1 of org2-regex-chain stopped at the cells gate (lazy.spi c-only builder crash, now untagged), so build.ps1 never reached the bench and printed no setup rows. The measure reruns at the end of the ganymede org2-registry-gate job (submitted by an idempotent box poller into a free slot). Next step: read its == setup rows.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_6 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:04Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:1x GENERATION SLICE (the typed-core half): compile-time types from runtime DFAs are not reachable directly (minimal_of is runtime :~ code; real-level computed nominals like tuple_list build types only from type literals), so staging = TWO-PHASE CODEGEN: a Spiral function emits the typed core as Spiral source, a gate writes it to a module and compiles it, and the existing bisim proof checks the compiled rows against minimal_of. Written (unstaged): regex/src/core_emit.spi (registered in spiral.toml after typed): emitted_core prefix d : option string emits <p>n1..<p>nN Peano aliases, the <p>bit_row alias, <p>q0..q(N-1) fin values, one <p>r<i> row per state (verdict_at + step on 48/49; a Dead target makes it None since a bit core has no dead row), <p>v1..vN vectors in the hand core's order, and <p>start (from d::start), blank-line separated so each emitted definition is its own cell. Test (rust): the 2-state ends_in_zero core is emitted exactly (10 definitions). All cells within budget by the exact oracle; names clash-checked. Proof: added to the pending ganymede org2-regate. Next step after green: a gate step that writes emitted_core \"g\" (minimal_of (fourth_from_end ())) to a generated module and proves bisim (16, 16) on it, replacing the hand rows.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_7 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:37Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:4x core_emit RED in the regate (job-1794216118751): ETY-UnboundVariable minimal_of at core_emit.spi:98 - minimal_of lives in certificate.spi, not minimal.spi. Fixed: core_emit opens certificate (names clash-checked against certificate/minimal/dfa: none). Re-gate: ganymede org2-core-emit (idempotent box poller, next free slot).")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_8 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 8u32, "2026-11-09T09:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof + GO/NO-GO VERDICT: GO. ganymede job-1794213011274 bench setup rows (mean of 25 certified_of + table_of builds vs the median array-table pass over the workload's words): (0|1)*0 0.015 ms vs 0.009 ms (1.7x); (0|00)*1 0.023 vs 0.008 (2.9x); (0|1)*1(0|1){3} 0.831 vs 0.009 (~90x); [a-z]{1,64} 217.254 vs 0.007 (~31,000x); fourth-from-end on 4 x 4000-bit texts 0.963 vs 0.125 (7.7x); (0|1)*1(0|1){7} 1441.759 vs 0.010 (~144,000x). Setup exceeds one table pass on EVERY workload, by 4-5 orders of magnitude where the minimal DFA is large (256 states, 65 states), so a compile-time staged table removes the dominant cost for literal patterns. Next step: the staged path = core_emit (gating now in ganymede org2-core-emit) generalized from the bit core to the array table (emit the table_of rows as a static array literal per literal pattern), with the same agreement words as the runtime table.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_9 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 9u32, "2026-11-09T10:00Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:1x STAGED ARRAY TABLE slice written (unstaged): regex/src/table_emit.spi (registered after core_emit). table_lines prefix t emits Spiral source that rebuilds the certified table with NO derivatives or minimization at run time: each array (lows u32, next i32, accepting bool) becomes a chain of definitions <p>lows0..k, each listm::append-ing a 24-item chunk to the previous one (so every emitted definition stays a small cell however large the DFA), then <p>table () : table = { width; dead; start; lows = array_of (<p>lowsK ()); ... }. The run-time side it relies on is shared code: array_of (list -> array_base), base_list (array_base -> list), rebuilt t. Tests (rust): a table rebuilt from its lists answers exactly like the certified one on every word up to length 6 (fourth_from_end); the emitted module has one definition per chunk plus the table. 0 budget findings, names clash-checked. Proof: ganymede org2-table-emit (idempotent box poller). Next step after green: a gate step that writes table_lines \"s\" (minimal_table r) for the 6 bench patterns to a generated module and adds a StagedTableArm to the bench, so the setup row compares staged vs certified directly.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_10 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 10u32, "2026-11-09T10:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: core_emit GREEN (ganymede job-1794217968006): the emitted 2-state ends_in_zero typed core matches the predicted text exactly (10 definitions: gn1, gn2, gbit_row, gq0, gq1, gr0 Rejected/gq1/gq0, gr1 Accepted/gq1/gq0, gv1, gv2, gstart = gq0). table_emit gating now (job-1794218421212).")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_11 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 11u32, "2026-11-09T10:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: table_emit GREEN (ganymede job-1794218421212, 48 s): 2/2 - a table rebuilt from its lists (array_of over base_list) answers exactly like the certified table on every word up to length 6 for fourth_from_end, and table_lines emits one definition per 24-item chunk plus the table. Both emitters (typed core, array table) are now proven. Next step: the generated-module gate: write table_lines \"s\" (minimal_table r) for the 6 bench patterns into a generated module, add a StagedTableArm to the bench (prepare = the emitted <p>table (), no certified_of), and put its setup next to the certified build in the setup row.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_12 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 12u32, "2026-11-09T10:07Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:2x GENERATED-MODULE PIPELINE written (unstaged): (1) bench.spi opens table_emit and gains an emit mode: with REGEX_EMIT_STAGED set, main prints a complete generated module staged_tables (header + table_lines \"s<k>_\" for the 5 distinct bench patterns: s1 (0|1)*0, s2 (0|00)*1, s3 fourth-from-end, s4 [a-z]{1,64}, s5 eighth-from-end) instead of the report; otherwise it runs the bench as before (run_bench). (2) new regex/staged/ package (spiral.toml: ../src- linked; modules staged_tables (generated) + staged_check): staged_check proves s1/s2/s3 answer like the certified tables on every word up to 6 and s4/s5 keep 65/256 states. (3) ganymede stage org2-staged.sh: rebuild only the bench (BuildSpiral + cargo, no cells), run it with REGEX_EMIT_STAGED=1 > staged/staged_tables.spi, cell_budget over the generated module, Cells gate staged_check. Queued via idempotent box poller (label org2-staged). Next step after green: copy the generated staged_tables.spi back to the box tree and add a StagedTableArm whose prepare uses s<k>_table () so the setup row times staged vs certified.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_13 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 13u32, "2026-11-09T10:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: STAGED PIPELINE GREEN end to end (ganymede job-1794218838628, 168 s): bench rebuilt with the emit mode -> REGEX_EMIT_STAGED=1 regex-bench wrote staged/staged_tables.spi (194 lines, 5 staged tables s1..s5) -> mix spiral.cell_budget 0 findings over the generated module + staged_check -> staged_check 3/3: s1 (0|1)*0 and s2 (0|00)*1 answer like the certified tables on every word up to 6, s3 fourth-from-end likewise, s4 [a-z]{1,64} and s5 eighth-from-end keep 65 / 256 states. The generated module is copied back to the box tree at regex/staged/staged_tables.spi (unstaged; e.g. s1 = lows [0, 48, 49, 50], next 12 entries, accepting [!-, !+, !-]). Setup cost of a staged table at run time = array fills from literal lists (no derivatives, no minimization) vs 1441.759 ms certified build for s5. Next step: a StagedTableArm in the bench (prepare = s<k>_table ()) and a staged setup column next to the certified one, plus build.ps1 regenerating staged_tables.spi and failing on a diff (the generated file stays reproducible).")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_14 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 14u32, "2026-11-09T10:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: STAGED vs CERTIFIED SETUP MEASURED (ganymede job-1794221131334, staged_time over the generated module, mean of 25 builds each): s1 (0|1)*0 1 us vs certified 15 us (~15x); s2 (0|00)*1 1 us vs 23 us (~23x); s3 fourth-from-end 9 us vs 831 us (~92x); s4 [a-z]{1,64} 31 us vs 217,254 us (~7,000x); s5 eighth-from-end 155 us vs 1,441,759 us (~9,300x). With staged_check's agreement (s1-s3 answer like the certified tables on every word up to 6; s4/s5 keep 65/256 states), the 11-03 DoD holds: a prepare-time row per workload certified vs staged, the staged table giving the same verdicts. Left for 100: build.ps1 regenerates staged_tables.spi and fails on a diff (the generated file stays reproducible), and the staged column printed by the bench itself rather than a side program.")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_15 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 15u32, "2026-11-09T10:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 11:1x REPRODUCIBILITY WIRED (unstaged): regex build.ps1 now (1) gates staged/staged_check.spi with the src notebooks, so CI proves the committed staged tables answer like the certified ones, and (2) after the bench run, re-runs regex-bench with REGEX_EMIT_STAGED=1 and compares the output with staged/staged_tables.spi; on any difference it rewrites the file and fails (\"stale ... commit the regenerated file\"), so the generated module can never drift from the emitter. Parse clean; synced to the ganymede mirror. Proof: the next full regex build (it also exercises both new steps). Left: the staged column inside the bench report itself (today staged_time.spi is a side program).")
inl note_of_regex_staged_tables_16 () = Note ("REGEX-STAGED-TABLES", 16u32, "2026-11-09T13:31Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:5x REPRODUCED, CLOSE. ganymede job-1794227421877-org2-regex-full (full regex build.ps1, cells + bench + staged diff): spiral-tests total discovered 87, executed 87, passed 87, failed 0 over 15 files (staged/staged_check.spi 3/3 included); \"build.ps1 / staged / staged_tables.spi matches the emitter\" (the regenerated module is byte-identical to the committed one); REGEX-OK. Setup rows (certified table build mean of 25 vs one array table pass median): 0.013/0.009, 0.027/0.009, 0.948/0.010, 202.288/0.008, 0.838/0.125, 1427.912/0.009 ms, the same GO shape as the verdict note (staged pass ~10 us flat vs certified build up to 1.43 s). Generated bench.rs 7741 lines (1000-line gate stays the known REGEX-BENCH-PAGE warning). Proof: the job above, REGEX-OK + the staged match line.")
