inl note_of_kit_remote_status_compiler_probe_1 () = Note ("KIT-REMOTE-STATUS-COMPILER-PROBE", 1u32, "2026-11-04T11:47Z", "x-dumps", "remote.ps1 node status shows \"node runner (SPIRAL_EXE unset or missing)\" + \"node compiler (missing)\" because the status snippet reads the bare ssh environment, but the node DOES compile/run (run_notebook.ps1 resolves the compiler from spiral-bin/compiler-installs; main ran Lean 198/198 on the node 11-04). Fix: the status probe should resolve the compiler/runner the same way run_notebook does, so node vs box gate-comparability lines are accurate. Found by x-dumps validating REMOTE-CLOUD; corrected by main. kit owns remote.ps1.")
inl note_of_kit_remote_status_compiler_probe_2 () = Note ("KIT-REMOTE-STATUS-COMPILER-PROBE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:36Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:4x tibia (help pool): REPRODUCED + FIX DRAFTED (rig applies; remote.ps1 base 79A11107626F). Repro: `remote.ps1 ganymede status` printed `node compiler (missing)` although ganymede compiled ~25 tibia gates today. ROOT CAUSE (remote.ps1:177): the status snippet looks for spiral-bin under [Environment]::GetFolderPath('LocalApplicationData'), which on Linux is ~/.local/share; ganymede's compiler lives in /root/.cache/spiral-bin. Cells (run_notebook.ps1:47, lib_land_window.ps1) resolve $env:LOCALAPPDATA ?? $env:XDG_CACHE_HOME ?? $HOME/.cache, and the node jobs set SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR. FIX (one expression): $core = Join-Path ($env:SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR ?? (Join-Path ($env:LOCALAPPDATA ?? $env:XDG_CACHE_HOME ?? (Join-Path $HOME '.cache')) 'spiral-bin')) 'bin' 'single-flight' ... Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\KIT-REMOTE-STATUS-COMPILER-PROBE\\remote.ps1: parse 0 errors; run against ganymede it prints `node compiler 9EF0395BF5D9782D 2026-11-09 14:13` (pack77's core, installed 14:13 per compiler). Windows nodes keep LOCALAPPDATA, so nothing changes there. Out of scope, left as is: `node runner (SPIRAL_EXE unset)` is accurate (nodes run through run_notebook, not the box spiral.exe).")
inl note_of_kit_remote_status_compiler_probe_3 () = Note ("KIT-REMOTE-STATUS-COMPILER-PROBE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "proof: 11-09 21:4x rig APPLIED tibia's draft (unstaged): i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1 line 177 now resolves the compiler core through SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR, then LOCALAPPDATA, XDG_CACHE_HOME or ~/.cache (the same order as install-pack's cacheRoot) instead of the Windows-only LocalApplicationData folder; tibia proved it against ganymede (remote status prints pack77's core 9EF0395B instead of \"missing\"). The draft's base hash 79A11107626F matched the live file (which carries other lanes' unstaged edits), so the copy changes exactly 1 line (Compare-Object), parse 0 errors; the pre-apply copy is kept beside the draft as remote.ps1.live-before-apply.")
