inl note_of_cic_env_index_1 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 1u32, "2026-11-04T19:28Z", "main", "11-04 15:3x main FILED from CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY: replay runtime grew from ~5 min to ~20 min as more of the Prelude was admitted (each accepted declaration grows the list every later lookup scans). DOD: same verdicts (oracle pins, kernel tests, replay tally byte-identical), replay of Init.Prelude under 5 min on europa.")
inl note_of_cic_env_index_2 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-04T19:59Z", "main", "11-04 16:0x main SCOPE: env.spi's find_decl is a linear scan (decl_name d = n per element); 17 lookups call it, 107 signatures carry `list decl`, and about 6 sites extend it (d :: env in typing admit/admit_quotient_decls, recursor :: env in inductive, the fvar axiom in conversion's bodies_defeq and context_env). PLAN: one nominal environment = { decls : list decl; index : <persistent name map> } with find_decl/extended as the only accessors; the 107 signatures change mechanically (list decl -> environment) and the extension sites go through `extended`. Measure first: time one replay with a counter of find_decl steps to confirm lookups dominate before the refactor.")
inl note_of_cic_env_index_3 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 3u32, "2026-11-04T22:58Z", "main", "11-04 18:5x main RATIONALE CORRECTED: the 20-minute replays that motivated this item were NOT lookup cost. They were the u64 overflow in Nat.pow 2 64 falling back to structural unfolding (fixed by decimal bignum arithmetic, CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY n16). With that fixed, Init.Prelude (1837 decls) replays in 33 s and Init.Core (3479 decls) in 89 s on europa, so the DoD target (< 5 min) already holds. Lowered to P4 and kept Planned: revisit only if a larger module replay (Init.Data.*, Std) shows find_decl dominating, and measure that first (a step counter in find_decl) before any refactor of the 107 signatures.")
inl note_of_cic_env_index_4 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 4u32, "2026-11-04T23:25Z", "main", "11-04 19:3x main NEW EVIDENCE (memory, not speed): Init.Data.Array.Basic (lean4export v4.35.0, 274585 lines, 15.6 MB, sha FED98694, pinned in the kit drafts store under CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES) was killed at 132 s under a 1.8 GB systemd cap on europa (exit 143, no tally), while modules up to 180k lines replay in <= 158 s. The replay holds at once: every export line as a string, three id-indexed arrays sized to the line count, every decoded row, and the full decl list with terms. Cheaper first steps than an index: stream lines instead of materializing the list, drop rows after storing them, size the arrays per table (names/levels/exprs counts) instead of by line count; then measure RSS per module. Run Array.Basic on the node (more RAM) to get its verdict meanwhile.")
inl note_of_cic_env_index_5 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 5u32, "2026-11-04T23:32Z", "main", "11-04 19:3x main MEASUREMENT CAVEAT: /usr/bin/time -v around the Nat.Basic (115 s) and List.Basic (164 s) replays reported a max RSS of ~139 MB, but that is the pwsh/mix wrapper, NOT the Rust test cell: the cell is reaped by the BEAM, so time's rusage never sees it. The 20:30 UTC OOM showed the cell itself at 2.4 GB RSS (dmesg). To measure properly: run under a NAMED transient unit (systemd-run --unit=main-replay-N --scope ...) and read /sys/fs/cgroup/system.slice/main-replay-N.scope/memory.peak before the scope exits, or sample ps rss of the \"cell\" process every few seconds.")
inl note_of_cic_env_index_6 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 6u32, "2026-11-07T22:11Z", "main", "main 11-07 groom. Next step: replace find_decl's list scan with lib dict keyed by name (admission order kept in a parallel list), then rerun the Init.Prelude export replay on europa and compare against the 20 min baseline.")
inl note_of_cic_env_index_7 () = Note ("CIC-ENV-INDEX", 7u32, "2026-11-09T20:15Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:1x: waiting - not currently warranted. Note 3 corrected the rationale: the 20-min replays were a Nat.pow u64 overflow (since fixed), not find_decl lookup cost; Init.Prelude replays 33s now, DoD under-5min already holds. P4, revisit-only-if a larger-module replay shows find_decl dominating, and MEASURE FIRST (a find_decl step counter) before touching the 107 signatures. Waits on evidence of need.")
