inl note_of_kit_agile_crate_headroom_1 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-CRATE-HEADROOM", 1u32, "2026-11-05T02:19Z", "kit", "11-04 22:2x kit, from the 11-04 star exchange (resilience ask 4). Evidence: today kit split agile_claim_lease (1059), agile_claim_cli (1450), agile_task_listing (1015) and earlier agile_quality_state (1230), each only after a train or size run failed; KIT-TODO-SCAN-HEADROOM (agile_todo_scan at 1000/1000) is the same pattern. Root cause: the source-only agile models (agile_claim_model, agile_task_text, agile_note_model ...) inline into every agile_* crate, so one model change grows many crates at once. DoD: (1) a size report listing each agile_* crate's generated lines from the last regen, with those over 900 flagged; (2) the heaviest shared model functions moved behind ONE linked agile crate with tuple/array_base exports, so consumers call it instead of inlining it; (3) every agile_* crate <= 900 after a train. NEXT: rank inlined model functions by how many agile crates pull them in (grep consumers' package.spiproj). TYPEFEATURES: the report rows as a typed crate_size record; the linked boundary keeps typed exports (no joined strings).")
inl note_of_kit_agile_crate_headroom_2 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-CRATE-HEADROOM", 2u32, "2026-11-09T06:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:0x local rig, DoD (1) SIZE REPORT from the generated .rs outputs in the live tree (72 agile_* crates with an output file): 13 over 900, 0 over 1000. Closest to the gate: agile_task_creation 983, agile_claim_lease 983, agile_task_next 983 (17 lines of headroom each), agile_todo_scan 959, agile_task_waits 944, agile_task_asks 943, agile_claim_queue 941, agile_task_tree 930, agile_task_notes 930, agile_todo_merge 923, agile_todo_lines 917, agile_quality_state 914, plus one more over 900. Caveat: these are the outputs in the tree; TRAIN42's regen (with compiler's pack63c reformat and tonight's edits) will rewrite them, so re-read the report from that regen before acting. The pattern holds: three crates sit at 983 because each was last trimmed to just pass. DoD (2) is code: move the heaviest shared model functions (the source-only agile models inlined into every crate) behind ONE linked agile crate, so a model change grows one crate, not 13. Next step: after TRAIN42, rerun this report from its regen and name the 3 shared functions with the most inlined lines.")
