inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_1 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 1u32, "2026-11-05T03:07Z", "x", "2026-11-04 23:07 x: filed after the user's 11-04 night correction ('you started adding comments, code should be self explanatory, i thought we had memories and other stuff enforcing that'). Today ONLY memory enforces it: kit-style-check.ps1 checks host strings, not comments, and only on Edit/Write, and scripted writes bypass it. BASELINE, measured 11-04 22:5x (pattern ^\\s*///(?![>-]) or ^\\s*//(?!/) over .spi, excluding target/e2e/_build/build/deps/node_modules): spiral lib 389 lines in 68 files (benchmark 86, iggy 32, sm' 30, physics 23, date_time 17); Cells spi 35 in 9; x 13 in 7 (all stripped in queued x drafts); kit src 5 in 3. DoD: one checker (a kit lint or a ratchet in kit standards) that allows only ///> and ///- directives and the TODO form, wired into (1) the PostToolUse hook for .spi on Edit/Write, (2) lib_land_window and cells_land_window closes, (3) each repo gate, ratcheted so counts only shrink (memory baselines-only-shrink). Interim: x's land scripts refuse drafts with comment lines (11-04).")
inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_2 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 2u32, "2026-11-05T10:59Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:59 x: HEALED the Cells part of the baseline. Cells spi: 35 lines in 9 files -> 0, through cells_land_window (closed green, 58 passed: document_test, builders_test, targets_test; undo cells-20261105-065317). Files: builder_output, builders, gleam_project, html_markdown, json_value, manifest, memo, source_map, targets (all .spi under apps/cells/spi). Each diff removes only comment and blank lines, and each file round-trips byte-exact; manifest.spi also gained its missing blank line before a :# test and its missing final newline (both pre-existing in live). Baseline now: lib 389, Cells 0, x 1 (timeline_serve.spi:9, healed by x-next9), kit 5. The gate itself (hook, land closes, repo gates) is still kit's to build.")
inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_3 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 3u32, "2026-11-05T12:25Z", "x", "2026-11-05 08:3x x: HEALED the free part of the spiral lib baseline. 38 lib files, 164 comment lines removed, through lib_land_window (closed green: 55 consumer-used signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe 38/38 PASS, 0 respell drift; lib digest E2F9F654E6655672; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-073406). It waited first behind the kit lane's scope_run.spi notebook (a live lib reader). Only lines matching ^\\s*///(?![>-]) or ^\\s*//(?!/) were removed, then double blank lines were collapsed. 0 unexpected diff lines, and every draft round-tripped byte-exact before the land. The files were chosen as having no git WIP and no pending kit draft (list: scratchpad lib-no-comments-files.txt). LIB NOW: 199 comment lines in 26 files (from 363 at 06:59, 389 at the 11-04 baseline). Every one of the remaining 26 has git WIP or a pending draft from another lane (for example reflection.spi's /// ### headings), so they heal when those lands clear. Baseline: lib 199, Cells 0, x 1 (timeline_serve.spi:9, healed by x-next9), kit 5. The enforcing gate (hook, land closes, repo gates) is still kit's to build.")
inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_4 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T08:27Z", "main", "main 11-06 04:2x from x's star exchange (11-06 04:22, lesson 9): comments landed through scripted and draft-dir edits, which the Write/Edit style hook never sees (memory scripted-edits-bypass-style-hook). The gate needs a land-side half: lib_land_window and the drafts apply scripts refuse a draft with comment lines, a regex check beside the hash guard, so the hook is not the only enforcement point.")
inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_5 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T09:21Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:2x local rig, EDIT-TIME HALF LIVE: ~/.claude/hooks/kit-style-check.ps1 (the PostToolUse Write|Edit hook every lane runs) now checks EVERY .spi, not only kit src: an added line matching ^\\s*///(?![>-]) or ^\\s*//(?!/) (the regex x used for the 11-05 lib heal) is reported with exit 2 (the model sees it at once); ///> targets and ///- notebook directives pass; lines already in the Edit old_string are not counted, so existing comments never block an unrelated edit. Pipe-tested 3 payloads: added comment -> exit 2 naming the line; directives -> 0; pre-existing comment kept -> 0. Same session: the hook's host-macro check no longer fires on $\" inside string literals (false positives on literals like \"$\"). LEFT (per main 11-06): the land-side half, lib_land_window and the drafts apply scripts refusing a draft with comment lines (Cells/microblog script), and repo gates ratcheted from the baseline. DoD: edit hook + land refusal + per-repo ratchet, each with a negative control. Next step: ask microblog for the lib_land_window refusal (regex beside the hash guard). TypeFeatures: none (script gates).")
inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_6 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:27Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:3x LAND-SIDE HALF DONE by microblog (live spiral tree, apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1, unstaged): right after the -BaseHash guard, Get-AddedComments diffs each .spi/.spir draft against its live file as a line multiset (a new file counts every line), prints ADDED COMMENT: <file>:<line>: <text> for any added line matching the hook regex and throws before any write or window. Controls run ad hoc on the box: unchanged old comment 0; added ///> and ///- 0; added // note 1; /// doc 1; new file with a comment 1; //// banner 1; real LIB-TLDS draft 0. Not yet run inside a full land. Left: repo gates ratcheted from the baseline (kit standards no-comment-lines already covers kit packages that declare it).")
inl note_of_comment_lint_gate_7 () = Note ("COMMENT-LINT-GATE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T18:11Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:4x local rig, RATCHET BASELINE measured (third leg: per-repo gates), the same regex as the edit hook and the land refusal (^\\s*///(?![>-]) or ^\\s*//(?!/)), over git-tracked .spi/.spir that exist (tracked files deleted in unstaged work are skipped), target/deps/tmp/_build excluded: spiral 271 lines in 36 of 243 files (top lib/spiral/benchmark.spi 86, apps/spiral/spiral.spi 43), kit 28 in 5 of 1205 (state/consolidation_fixtures.spi 22, agile_todo_model/model.spi 3), dice 18 in 2 (lib/dice.spi 10, contract/dice_contract.spi 8), alphabet 9 in 1 (apps/documents/documents.spi), and x, tibia, fiscal, regex, html at 0. NEXT: record these as per-repo ratchet rows (a comment-lines word in the census, so kit standards --ratchet refuses growth in any repo, the way the edit hook already refuses added lines), with a negative control per repo.")
