inl note_of_assign_parity_1 () = Note ("ASSIGN-PARITY", 1u32, "2026-11-05T10:41Z", "compiler", "11-05 06:4x compiler, from FEATURE-PARITY-TABLE's first probe. The !!!!Assign(target, value) intrinsic (peval spiral_compiler.fs:12262; a dyn local bound with := ~x or dyn) compiles on F#, Rust, Pascal, Zig, Lua, TypeScript and C, but fails explicitly on Python ('Assign with 2 args not supported'), Kotlin and Swift ('doesn't support the operation Assign yet'), Wasm ('not supported in the Wasm backend') and Cpp ('Assign with 2 args not supported'). Gleam/Lean/Bend have immutable locals, so those are 'no' by design (Known rows). Fixture: package |core-, main.spi ':= main () : i32 = / := ~x = 1i32 / !!!!Assign(x, 41i32) / !!!!Add(x, 1i32)', expected exit 42. DoD: each of the 5 backends either emits the assignment (Python: a plain rebind, with nonlocal where the local is captured; Kotlin/Swift: the dyn local declared var; Cpp: x = v; Wasm: local.set) with the fixture exiting 42 natively, or the cell is recorded as 'no' with its reason in the parity table; plus a regression sample listed on those backends.")
