inl tibia_map_field_reader () = Task ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", "tibia: split apps/map/map.spi's protobuf-style field reader (varint_from, varint, field_at, fold_fields) into its own module with its own tests, cutting apps/map's 2383 generated Rust lines toward the 1000-line gate; plan in TIBIA-1-0-DOD 11-05 03:40", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1", "tibia,team:tibia,granular,lines", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_map_field_reader () = Planning ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 1u32, "2026-11-06T10:13Z", "tibia", "11-06 06:13 tibia: split from TIBIA-1-0-DOD (main's close-ratio groom). This part needs neither TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 nor SPIPROJ-RETIRE, which block the parent. DoD: the reader module passes run_notebook on rust, apps/map's Cells tests stay green, and the generated-line count for apps/map drops (before 2383, after quoted). The proof runs on the node.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:13Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:13 tibia: NEXT: move varint_from/varint/field_at/fold_fields into apps/map/fields.spi with test blocks for each. DoD: as in note 1.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 3u32, "2026-11-06T11:22Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:22 tibia: CORRECTION to note 1 (\"needs neither TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 nor SPIPROJ-RETIRE\"), which was wrong. Re-reading TIBIA-1-0-DOD's 11-05 03:40 plan: apps/map builds as ONE rustc file (run.ps1), so moving the reader into another module of the same package does not cut a single generated line. Only a LINKED unit (its own crate) does. That needs a Cargo workspace in tibia (a Cargo.toml per unit with [package.metadata.spiral], path deps, a lockfile), which is TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1's convention, and the proof (run.ps1 terrain/region parity) needs the live Canary data, which only the box has. Fixes: dep TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 restored, estimate 240. NEXT: wait for TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 or a box live window. DoD: as in note 1, plus the reader as a linked proto unit (visitors stay inside it, since closures can't cross the link).")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:03Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:0x tibia: THE SPLIT IS PROVEN ON THE NODE (draft drafts\\tibia\\TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER\\, not yet in the repo). tibia's first linked unit, following html's typed-units/1 shape: a root Cargo.toml workspace (members apps/map + apps/map_kinds, workspace.metadata.spiral template typed-units/1); apps/map_kinds = kinds.spi (bytes, the field reader varint/field_at/fold_fields with its visitors record, item_kinds, the appearances parser, item_kinds_of; plus the moved varint test) + entry map_kinds.spi exporting map_kinds_rows = kinds_rows : bytes -> array item_kinds (a ONE-ROW array, because a direct non-primitive record return silently inlines) + spiral.toml + Cargo.toml [lib]; apps/map's spiral.toml links ../map_kinds-, map.spi opens kinds, and main reads index (kinds_rows ...) 0. MEASURED (ganymede jobs tibia-map1..5): generated map.rs 2321 (baseline on this compiler) to 1981 lines, -340; kinds.rs 349; map.rs makes exactly 1 map_kinds:: call (linked, not inlined); cargo build --release green; kinds test 1/1 and map tests 4/4 on rust. TRADEOFF: the C targets were dropped from both test files, because Cells' C test builds fail ('return type of main ... 32-bit int') once a package links a unit; reported to the compiler lane, and it matches html's rust-only linked units. run.ps1 draft: compile both units, then cargo build --release -p map, exe at target/release/map. Generated .rs and Cargo.lock are tracked, per html's convention. map.rs at 1981 is still over the 1000 gate, so the next seams (items.xml scanner, OTBM reader, region) follow as further units. Next step: after the user is away (box window), run the drafted run.ps1 on the box against the live Canary data, require the walkability dump to match results/rows/arena_region_r45.spi, then apply the draft to the repo (unstaged).")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 5u32, "2026-11-10T07:33Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:3x tibia: apps/map IS UNDER THE 1000-LINE GATE ON THE NODE (draft drafts\\tibia\\TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER\\, three linked units). Stage 2: apps/map_items (the items.xml scanner, exported as a tuple-argument ids_of ((text, needle) : bytes * string) : array bool, since curried exports inline; plus a test over an id, a fromid/toid range and a self-closing item). Stage 3: apps/map_walk (the OTBM walker, links map_kinds; exported as walk_rows over a one-row array item_kinds returning a one-row array grid, since direct record args and returns inline). map keeps the constants, emitters, listings and main. MEASURED (ganymede job tibia-map7): generated lines map.rs 975 (was 2321), map_walk 659, map_items 354, map_kinds 349, so EVERY unit is under 1000; links in map.rs: kinds 1, items 3, walk 1 (all linked, none inlined); cargo build --release green; tests kinds 1/1, items 1/1, map 4/4 (rust). run.ps1 draft builds the four units then cargo; the workspace has members apps/map, map_items, map_kinds, map_walk. The C targets are temporarily off: compiler's pack80 (COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN) fixes the unit-main C emit, after which they can return. Next step: after the user is away (box window), run the drafted run.ps1 on the box against the live Canary data, require the walkability dump to match results/rows/arena_region_r45.spi, then apply the draft to the repo (unstaged).")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 6u32, "2026-11-10T09:35Z", "tibia", "11-10 05:4x tibia: C TARGETS RESTORED. compiler's COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN (pack81) is on ganymede, so the draft's tests list ///> rust plus ///> c again, as in the repo (map 4 tests, kinds 1, items 1). Probe tibia-map8 on ganymede: compiled map_kinds 349, map_items 354, map_walk 659, map 975 lines; links kinds 1, items 3, walk 1; cargo green; Cells kinds 1/1, items 1/1, map 4/4 with failed_targets empty (before pack81, the c target of a linking package failed here, so empty means c passed). The box compiler is still pre-fix until compiler's win-x64 build installs, so the box parity run must run the CELLS tests after that install, or skip them (run.ps1 itself runs no tests). Next step: after the user is away (box window) and the box compiler has pack81 or later, run the drafted run.ps1 against live Canary data, require the walkability dump to match results/rows/arena_region_r45.spi, then apply the draft to the repo (unstaged).")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 7u32, "2026-11-10T11:48Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:5x tibia: the user is AFK until 21:00 (box free of the user), but the box CPU is at 100% from other lanes, so the live-data parity run (a cargo release build with lto plus a full Canary map pass) waits for the box to calm down (the courtesy rule: under 70% CPU for 3 min). Next step: after the box is under 70% CPU, copy the draft over a scratch tibia tree (deps/spiral is a SYMLINK to C:\\home\\git\\spiral, so recreate it, never copy through it), run apps/map/run.ps1, require the dump to match results/rows/arena_region_r45.spi and src/terrain.spi to match, then apply the draft to the repo unstaged.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_field_reader_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-FIELD-READER", 8u32, "2026-11-10T14:54Z", "tibia", "11-10 10:5x tibia: APPLIED to the tibia repo (unstaged, never staged). Files: root Cargo.toml (workspace: apps/map, map_items, map_kinds, map_walk; typed-units/1), apps/map {Cargo.toml, map.spi, spiral.toml, run.ps1}, apps/map_kinds, apps/map_items, apps/map_walk (each Cargo.toml + sources + spiral.toml), .gitignore + 'apps/map*/*.rs' and '/Cargo.lock' (tibia does not track generated code; the old run.ps1 wrote under target/). Base check: HEAD apps/map/map.spi = 1ea5e47d87b3, unchanged since 11-08, so the draft was cut from it. PARITY proof (ganymede, the box CPU was at 100% from other lanes, so the live Canary inputs (28 MB public server data, sha-checked) were copied to the node): (1) the SPLIT and the unsplit ORIGINAL (repo map.spi -> 2321-line map.rs, rustc O3) produce byte-identical output on the real Canary map, all 1137 lines, sha 4cb20a8caec8 (jobs tibia-map-parity, tibia-map-orig); (2) the walkability dump EQUALS the committed arena_region_r45.spi content (8984 chars). FIXED a latent run.ps1 bug: it compared a raw module against a formatter-reflowed file (the working tree's arena_region_r45.spi is now the multi-line Table form), so it failed even for the unchanged map; the check now compares the joined string literals with the escaped dump (tested: the real output matches, the old check differs, an all-walkable negative control differs). PRE-EXISTING, not from this item: 143 of 308 generated terrain definitions (arena_spot_bits_*) are not verbatim in src/terrain.spi with the original map as well, filed as TIBIA-TERRAIN-SPI-STALE. Generated sizes: map.rs 975, map_walk 659, map_items 354, map_kinds 349 (all under 1000); tests kinds 1/1, items 1/1, map 4/4 on rust and c.")
