inl note_of_kit_job_tail_lines_flag_1 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-TAIL-LINES-FLAG", 1u32, "2026-11-06T10:15Z", "compiler", "11-06 compiler (tibia 06:12 #2 hit it too): `kit job tail <id> --lines 60` printed \"stdout (last 0 lines)\" with an ok header; `kit job tail <id> 60` printed 60. Two lanes read that as an empty log. Fix: accept --lines N, or fail with the usage line; never ok with 0.")
inl note_of_kit_job_tail_lines_flag_2 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-TAIL-LINES-FLAG", 2u32, "2026-11-09T13:55Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "proof: 11-09 10:0x microblog groom check, installed kit (11-08) on the box, over the settled job job-1794225846973-kit-unstaged-backup (34 stdout lines). 'job tail <id> --lines 3' prints the last 3 lines; 'job tail <id> 2' prints the last 2; '--all' prints all; '--bogus' exits 2 with 'expects a line count, --lines <n> or --all after the id, got --bogus'. This is the fix rig recorded on KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS n8 (kit_job_control/control.spi tail_count, test a_tail_count_is_a_number_lines_or_all_and_nothing_else), now installed. DoD met: --lines is honored and anything else is rejected, never printing 0 lines with an ok receipt. pass.")
