inl note_of_type_arith_4_pack_6 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-4-PACK", 6u32, "2026-11-09T14:50Z", "compiler", "11-09 14:5x compiler: the REDESIGNED fold (TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD/3-lazy-fold-over-pack73b) ships in pack77: single-flight core source 2cc4470f2b4aee59, host 79070d91ca070828; linux-x64 SpiralCompilerCore.dll 9ef0395b, SpiralCompiler.dll c51a27a4 (oort store, manifest round-trip verified). INSTALLED on ganymede + europa 14:13Z (guarded, rollback pre-pack77-*). pack77 gate: -Suite all 7610 rows vs pack76, 0 compile-status / 0 residual diffs (pack75, which first carried the fold, gated likewise vs pack73). PENDING: the box + moon (win-x64 pair builds on moon after TRAIN42e and microblogs r2w end); then tibia reruns probe3 incl. sized_array on the box and closes. Wait: train:TRAIN42e.")
inl note_of_type_arith_4_pack_7 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-4-PACK", 7u32, "2026-11-09T21:49Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:0x tibia: DONE. Run on ganymede, not the box (no box compute while the user is present); ganymede runs the same redesigned fold, installed core 3ab85d76 / SpiralCompiler c51a27a4. STEP-2 SAMPLE (type_arith_literal_unify, the DoD sample; job tibia-step2): positive compiles and exits 4; neg and neg_user_add stay \"Unification failure\" (a dim that does not fold still refuses). PROBE3 (drafts\\spiral\\LIB-TYPE-SHAPES\\probe3; job tibia-probe3; exits are mod 256): spelled exit 166 = 678 (mult 2 3 used as sized 6) as on pack58c; twostep exit 73 = 585; the SINGLE-LET form exit 73 = 585 too. That form FAILED on pack58c with \"Got sized (add 2i32 3i32) i32, Expected sized 5i32 i32\", so the unify-time fold (3B) is live in this pack. neg still a type error. LIB sized_array.spi (the module pack58c broke): --check clean on the box lib. Every pre-registered outcome holds.")
