inl note_of_type_arith_5_reshape_3 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T11:31Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:31 tibia: TypeFeatures: reshape/flatten with computed dims typed end to end (sized (mult heads head_dim)), with the nominal_recreate escape removed.")
inl note_of_type_arith_5_reshape_4 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE", 4u32, "2026-11-06T20:46Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:5x tibia: PROBE 3 on the BOX with pack58c (single-flight core 1524D5D56E6A11D5, sourceSha ef757b710be39cfa = compiler's reviewed candidate; drafts store drafts\\spiral\\LIB-TYPE-SHAPES\\probe3, LIB-TYPE-SHAPES probe 2 with resized removed). (1) SPELLED computed dims FOLD: q0 : sized (type_arith::mult 2 3) i32 used as sized 6 i32 compiles and runs (exit 678 = count 6 x 100 + physical 6 x 10 + total 18, as predicted). (2) INSTANTIATED arithmetic does NOT fold: u : sized 5 i32 = merged v w, with merged : sized a el -> sized b el -> sized (type_arith::add a b) el and v : sized 2, w : sized 3, fails with \"Unification failure. Got sized (add 2i32 3i32) i32, Expected sized 5i32 i32\". The negative (sized 6) fails with the same shape, as it should. Cause: the fold runs in visit_t over written types; add a b only becomes all-literal after a and b are substituted during unification, and unify compares the unnormalized TyApply against TyLit. So shape-changing functions still need probe 2's resized relabel, which means reshape is NOT typed end to end yet. Blocked on: TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD (fold the reserved ops in unification after substitution). Resume when: a pack carries it; rerun probe3 (positive should exit 567 + 18 = 585 without resized, negative should stay a type error).")
inl note_of_type_arith_5_reshape_5 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE", 5u32, "2026-11-06T20:49Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: INTERIM until 3b: binding the shape-changing call first and annotating on the next let works on pack58c (probe3\\twostep exits 585, no resized). So lib code can drop nominal_recreate/resized where the call and the annotation are on separate lets; the single-let form waits on TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD (deferral, not a new fold).")
inl note_of_type_arith_5_reshape_6 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T12:33Z", "tibia", "11-09 08:5x tibia: UNBLOCKED. Its blocker (the single-let fold, TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD, merged into TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD) shipped in pack75 (installed on ganymede/europa; box and moon after rig's TRAIN42e), and TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD is Done on probe3 evidence. NEXT STEP: rerun the reshape probe in the single-let form on pack75 (Linux), then drop nominal_recreate/resized from the lib reshape helpers where the call and its annotation share one let.")
inl note_of_type_arith_5_reshape_7 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T12:43Z", "tibia", "11-09 09:0x tibia: STEP PRE-REGISTERED (the DoD run). LIB-TYPE-SHAPES probe2 with the escape REMOVED: `:= u : sized 5 i32 = resized (merged v w)` becomes `:= u : sized 5 i32 = merged v w` (single let, the computed dim sized (type_arith::add 2 3) unified with 5 by the pack75 fold). On the installed pack75 (ganymede, Linux), compile and run on BOTH c (gcc -O2) and rust (rustc --edition 2024 -O). Expected: both compile and both exit 567 = count 5*100 + physical 5*10 + total 17 (shown as 55 = 567 mod 256 on Linux). The original probe2 (with resized) runs as control and must also give 567. A compile error on the no-resized variant means the fold does not cover merged's return type: record it, do not reintroduce resized.")
inl note_of_type_arith_5_reshape_8 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T13:06Z", "tibia", "Evidence: 11-09 09:0x tibia, ganymede job-1794228244154-tibia-shape-probe2 exit 0 on the INSTALLED pack75 (SpiralCompilerCore 830bada0): LIB-TYPE-SHAPES probe2 WITHOUT the escape (`:= u : sized 5 i32 = merged v w`, no resized, no nominal_recreate) compiles and runs on c (gcc -O2) and rust (rustc --edition 2024 -O); both exit 567 (55 mod 256), the same as the control with resized on both backends. So the computed dim sized (type_arith::add 2 3) unifies with 5 in one let; the DoD (green on c and rust, workaround removed) is met. Lib code may now drop resized/nominal_recreate in single-let shape changes; no live lib or product site uses them (grep 11-09: only an old fpga sample under polyglot deps).")
