inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_4 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 4u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "tibia", "11-07 13:4x tibia: STARTED on a QUIET node (load 2 percent at launch): job-1794072902743-tibia-rust-array-ab, with a waiter. Arms by compiler, both from the box's install undo copies so neither is a fresh build: BEFORE = core 8F0094967068FC85 (pack57, compiler-installs\\pack58b-20261106-173716\\single-flight-bin.before), AFTER = core 712FA1815A484F1D (pack58b = pack57 + RUST-ARRAY-2 + compiler's liveness follow-up + RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE, from pack59d-20261107-073231\\...before). Each arm gets its own SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR on the node (bin unzipped, toolchains junctioned to the node's), same tibia tree 9CC54C59CF13 and same lib (np1s). 3 interleaved rounds x {before, after} x {c, rust} of predict.ps1 -Module sweep -SkipChecks, recording load, wall ms, the .prom hunts/s and a hash of the output rows (parity). C arms double as a noise control (these changes are Rust-only). The A/B attributes the change to pack58b as a whole, not to RUST-ARRAY-2 alone.")
inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_5 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 5u32, "2026-11-07T19:50Z", "tibia", "11-07 15:5x tibia: RUN 1 READ IN FULL (job-1794072902743-tibia-rust-array-ab, exit 0, 131 min). PARITY HOLDS: rows_hash D2D7CF050F3B in all 12 runs (3 rounds x {before 8F0094967068FC85, after 712FA1815A484F1D} x {c, rust}). TIMING VOID against the DoD (\"at least 3 QUIET rounds per arm\"): the node was quiet only at launch. Load at the start of each run: round 1 39/39/84/7, round 2 35/85/100/90, round 3 100/100/100/100 percent (other lanes' jobs started meanwhile), and the script sampled load only at the start of a run. Quoted only as void data, Rust/C wall ratio: before 2.89 / 4.04 / 3.37, after 3.41 / 4.68 / 2.47; hunts/s rust before 26 / 8 / 5, after 24 / 7 / 12. The noise is as large as any effect, so no claim either way. The C arms, which act as the control, also moved 42 -> 16 hunts/s across rounds. Lesson: a quiet launch does not keep a 2-hour A/B quiet; every run needs its own gate. RERUN QUEUED: job-1794080988202-tibia-rustab-quiet (after the PR-35 chain, 10 h cap), the same arms, tree and caches, with a quiet gate before EVERY run (3 consecutive 10 s samples under 30 percent, up to 20 min; VOID after 12 failed waits), arm order alternating by round, load recorded before and after each run, and a waiter. BLOCKER: that job. NEXT STEP: read it in full; the verdict is the Rust/C hunts/s ratio, median of 3 quiet rounds per arm, before vs after, with parity.")
inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_6 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 6u32, "2026-11-07T22:20Z", "tibia", "11-07 18:3x tibia: RERUN STOPPED by me, VOID, no timing taken. job-1794080988202-tibia-rustab-quiet waited 6 times x 20 min at calm 0 (node load 100 pct from other lanes all evening, with not one quiet window) and was holding one of the node's few job slots while 4 of my own jobs queued behind it. Stopped at 18:3x (exit 143, 0 timed rows). The node is the wrong host for a quiet A/B on a busy evening; europa does go quiet, but the arms are Windows compiler copies plus tibia's predict pipeline, so moving it is a port, not a rerun. BLOCKER: a quiet node window (overnight, or a hold reserved with the other lanes). NEXT STEP: requeue rustab-quiet.ps1 unchanged (scratch rustab/, caches and tree already on the node) when a quiet window is agreed; parity is already established (D2D7CF050F3B, 12 of 12 runs).")
inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_7 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 7u32, "2026-11-08T21:29Z", "tibia", "11-08 17:3x tibia groom (re-verify the blocking premise): the blocker \"no quiet node window\" has a new answer: ganymede (Europa vc2-4c-8gb, Miami, 24/7, ours, idle; memory ganymede-node). It has shared vCPUs, so an A/A arm decides whether a window is quiet enough. NEXT STEP: run the C vs Rust sweep A/B on ganymede with an A/A arm once org registers it and its toolchains are copied from europa (same Ubuntu 26.04 / glibc 2.43).")
inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_8 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 8u32, "2026-11-08T21:39Z", "tibia", "11-08 17:4x tibia: ganymede is REGISTERED (org3: remote-machines.json, 2 slots, validated byte-identical to europa on all 3 DLLs). Placement: one compiler build at a time there (8 GB). Ready to run with the A/A arm.")
inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_9 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 9u32, "2026-11-08T23:14Z", "tibia", "11-08 19:3x tibia: PLACEMENT RULE update (user direction relayed by fiscal; memory k3s-build-test-substrate). Once org has k3s on ganymede (install order ganymede -> comet -> WSL last), run the timed arms as k3s wrapper pods: memory request == limit, CPU limit = workers, cpuset-pinned; NEVER overlap a measurement with any compilation on the same node (compile first, then measure with the node otherwise idle). ganymede has 2 slots, so take both, or check that the other slot is idle, and keep the A/A arm. Toolchain image pinned by digest; caches on the capped hostPath /cache. A WSL run never counts as a Linux result. Until k3s lands, a plain ganymede job is fine for SMOKE only (no timing claims).")
inl note_of_rust_array_3_ab_10 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-3-AB", 10u32, "2026-11-10T07:47Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:5x tibia: still blocked on a quiet node. At 03:47 ganymede had k3s Ready (v1.37.2+k3s1) but load 5.5 on 4 cores, running org2-kall3 and org2-dg4c. The note 9 placement rule (k3s pods, never overlapping a compile) needs both slots idle. Next step: after ganymede's slots are both free, with load under 0.5, start the A/A + A/B arms as k3s pods per note 9.")
