inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_1 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:01Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:1x tibia: Split from COMPILER-RUST-ARRAY-HOT-LOOP. DoD: the transformer's Rust tok/s is quoted before and after, parity holds against the C build, and the regen byte-compare limits the change to that array kind.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_2 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:14Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:14 tibia: NEXT: after step 4, implement SpiralCell for f32 arrays and measure the transformer's Rust build. DoD: as in note 1.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_3 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 3u32, "2026-11-06T11:16Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:1x tibia: CONDITIONS from step 4's review, part of the DoD. (1) The pack gate runs the Rust rows plus the lib Rust tests in the debug std-RefCell build (SPIRAL_RUST_CHECKED_ARRAYS); 0 Borrow panics proves the invariant. (2) am' 491/498/620 borrow PER ELEMENT (clone the element, drop the guard, call f, re-read len), not by cloning the Vec, because a push under a live &T is the UB shape. (3) Add a failure test for a[i] <- a[j] on the same array, alongside the 5 tests in step 4's note.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_4 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 4u32, "2026-11-06T11:31Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:31 tibia: TypeFeatures: the array type stays array el in Spiral; only the Rust representation of the backend changes, and the checked build keeps the aliasing invariant testable.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_5 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 5u32, "2026-11-06T11:42Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:42 tibia: DESIGN GAP found while drafting; step 4 missed it. Arrays CROSS linked-unit boundaries (records inside arrays cross at any depth; lib array crosses like array_base: memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes, pack23/24 proofs). A SpiralCell struct defined in each generated crate's prelude would make every crate's Rc<SpiralCell<Vec<T>>> a DIFFERENT type, so every array that crosses a link fails with E0308. FIX, keeping compiler's 3 conditions: use the std type Rc<std::cell::UnsafeCell<Vec<T>>>, which is identical in every crate, and give each crate a private extension trait `SpiralBorrow` (borrow(&self) -> &T, borrow_mut(&self) -> &mut T, via UnsafeCell::get) implemented for UnsafeCell<T>. Codegen's 6 sites and lib's .borrow()/.borrow_mut() snippets then compile unchanged, because method syntax resolves to the trait. Only CONSTRUCTORS respell, RefCell::new -> UnsafeCell::new at the array-typed sites: am' 468/491/498/618/620, crypto 246, sm'_real.spir 132/148/152, sm' 1607/1660/1753, seq 429, listm' 792, process 49 (15 sites). Not touched: parsing's String buf and process's Command/Child (non-array RefCells), rust.spi's explicit std::cell::RefCell, and HeapMutable records (14377/14604). Checked build: SPIRAL_RUST_CHECKED_ARRAYS swaps the emitted alias back to RefCell in every crate at once, since the flag is global per build. NEXT: compiler confirms the UnsafeCell plus trait variant (asked), then the draft.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_6 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 6u32, "2026-11-06T11:46Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:46 tibia: compiler OK'd the UnsafeCell plus SpiralBorrow variant (08:2x) with 3 more checks, now part of the DoD. (a) Grep the generated Rust and the lib snippets for Ref/RefMut used as TYPES and for drop(guard) on a borrow; respell them or the variant fails. (b) std::borrow::Borrow must never be in scope next to SpiralBorrow (E0034): the pack gate greps the emitted crates for `use std::borrow::Borrow`. (c) The trait is `use`d from the per-crate prelude in every module that borrows, linked consumers included, plus a linked sample whose array crosses a unit boundary and is mutated on both sides (the E0308 case). Earlier conditions (1)-(3) stand; the checked flag builds the RefCell alias in all crates for the gate. NEXT: census for (a), then the draft.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_7 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 7u32, "2026-11-06T11:52Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:52 tibia: CENSUS for check (a), read only, run over spiral, kit, regex, alphabet, dice, tibia, x and fiscal. (1) Ref/RefMut as types: only rust.spi (58-67, 114-116, 221, 318-347: ref_cell, cell_ref, ref_leak). Those are explicit std::cell::RefCell host nominals over `rc (ref_cell t)`, never Spiral arrays; the only other user is the dead tictactoe repo. They stay. (2) drop(guard): only process.spi 666-704, on Command/Child host RefCells, not arrays. They stay. (3) Array-typed RefCell::new constructors to respell: the 15 lib sites listed in n5, plus 2 outside lib, apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1787 and apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.spi:223 (args as array string). kit's 11 RefCell::new sites are all on host nominals (`:! pending_writes = $'std::rc::Rc<std::cell::RefCell<Vec<..>>>'` and so on), not Spiral arrays, so they stay. (4) `use std::borrow::Borrow`: 0 hits in the lib and the compiler's Rust emitter. Total respell: 17 constructor sites in spiral; 0 in other repos.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_8 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 8u32, "2026-11-06T11:56Z", "tibia", "11-06 07:56 tibia: STAGED PLAN plus compiler DRAFT v1. Order, so no step breaks the installed lib: (S1, compiler pack) emit `pub type SpiralArrayCell<T>` in every crate's prelude, defaulting to RefCell (no behavior change), and spell arrays through it (type 14386, literal 14633, create 14649). SPIRAL_RUST_ARRAY_CELL=unsafe switches every crate to `std::cell::UnsafeCell` plus the private SpiralBorrow trait, which is identical across linked crates because the alias expands to the std type. Draft v1: kit store drafts\\spiral\\RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL\\v1\\spiral_compiler.fs, 98F63E5A0CD4 on base A5FF832751C3, +10/-3. (S2, lib land after S1 is installed) respell the array-typed `RefCell::new(` to `SpiralArrayCell::new(` at 20 sites. That is the n7 census plus 3 more found now: am' 225, 232 (from_vec) and 481 (growable), so am' 225/232/468/481/491/498/618/620, crypto 246, sm'_real 132/148/152, sm' 1607/1660/1753, seq 429, listm' 792, process 49, apps/spiral 1787, apps/wasm 223. am' 498 (skip_while) and 620 (sort keys) become per-element Spiral loops (compiler condition 2). (S3) gate with =unsafe plus the checked RefCell default, the 4 failure tests, a[i] <- a[j], and the linked cross-unit sample, then flip the default. S3 RISK to census first: committed .rs outputs in kit (171), spiral samples (108) and x (27) change text on regen; any HAND-written Rust that spells Rc<RefCell<Vec<..>>> at a boundary with generated arrays breaks on the flip. Check kit infra/a/iggy-client before S3.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_9 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 9u32, "2026-11-06T12:01Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:01 tibia: S2 LIB DRAFT ready, to land only after S1 is installed. Kit store drafts\\spiral\\RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL\\lib-v1: am' 9ABAE9F442AD -> 40C7011CC4C9, crypto A39E787FBBDF -> 7DC71DAF6FD8, sm'_real.spir 1E643BE2F38C -> 88066930DBA1, sm' 0A15625F655D -> 88E948F32DD1, seq 81C2168D9B71 -> 806125669A34, listm' 2E75EDF3AA9E -> EDC3BA12581A, process B68E3B9F02E5 -> F8F3412F182D, apps/spiral 0C9A13AA8AC8 -> 43C863CE825C, apps/wasm 3AFD8EB4B32F -> CDDDDC8E8B01. 18 RefCell::new( respelled to SpiralArrayCell::new( (each line asserted to hold exactly one). am' skip_while became a Spiral per-element loop (mut index plus loop::while', then skip), and sort_by's Rust keys became arraym::map fn a (the same as its Python/TypeScript arms), so neither calls a user closure under a borrow (compiler condition 2). The round trip is clean on all 6 lib .spi files (sm' with its _real.spir): canonical true, fixpoint true.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_10 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 10u32, "2026-11-07T15:52Z", "tibia", "11-07 11:5x tibia groom round 2 (stale Active, no note in 12 h): Paused. Reason: drafts only (S1 alias, S2 lib respell, S3 flip, 35 pct); the compiler lane takes type-level packs one at a time, and TYPE-ARITH-3's redesign (ta3b) is in front. Resume when: ta3b is installed or dropped, then ask compiler for the next pack slot.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_11 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 11u32, "2026-11-07T19:25Z", "tibia", "11-07 15:2x tibia: pause re-checked, stays Paused. Reason: the compiler lane takes type-level packs one at a time, and the TYPE-ARITH-3 redesign (ta3b) is still in front; its candidate DLL path has not arrived. RUST-ARRAY-3-AB (job-1794072902743, which measures the pack58b array change this builds on) is still running on the node. Resume when: ta3b is installed or dropped AND the RUST-ARRAY-3-AB verdict is read; then ask compiler for the next pack slot.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_12 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 12u32, "2026-11-09T03:16Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:1x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused. Reason: its base, RUST-ARRAY-3-AB, still has no verdict. The item is Planned and its timed arms now wait for k3s wrapper pods on a quiet ganymede (placement rule, note 9 there), so no A/B number exists to build step 5 on. Resume when: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB records a verdict from those pods (or the user moves the timed arms elsewhere).")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_13 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 13u32, "2026-11-09T13:29Z", "tibia", "11-09 09:4x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused. Half of the condition is now met: ta3b is installed (pack75, core 830bada0; TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD and TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE Done). The other half is not: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB is still Planned with no verdict. Its timed arms need an otherwise idle ganymede (note 9 there), and ganymede is busy with tibia compile jobs until about 11:00. Resume when: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB records a verdict.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_14 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 14u32, "2026-11-09T21:01Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:0x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused. Reason: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB is still Planned with no verdict. Its timed arms need an otherwise idle ganymede (k3s wrapper pods per note 9 there), and ganymede has been running tibia/org gate jobs back to back all afternoon. Resume when: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB records a verdict.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_15 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 15u32, "2026-11-10T07:47Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:5x tibia: pause re-decided, stays Paused. Reason: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB still has no verdict. Its blocker RUST-ARRAY-2-WIDE-MERGE is Done and k3s is Ready on ganymede, but the timed arms need ganymede otherwise idle, and at 03:47 it was at load 5.5 on 4 cores, running org2-kall3 and org2-dg4c. Resume when: RUST-ARRAY-3-AB records a verdict.")
inl note_of_rust_array_5_refcell_impl_16 () = Note ("RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL", 16u32, "2026-11-11T01:05Z", "tibia", "11-10 21:0x tibia: REBASE NOTE for the resume. The draft drafts\\spiral\\RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL\\lib-v1\\sm'.spi (11-06, sha 88e948f32dd1) is behind the live lib\\spiral\\sm'.spi (8f62db1e387d): org2 reformatted sm'.spi tonight (LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION, whitespace-only), and the draft already predated other lib changes. lib_land_window's base-hash check would refuse it as is. When this resumes, redo the change on the current box file instead of applying the old draft. Pause unchanged: resume when RUST-ARRAY-3-AB records a verdict.")
