inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_5 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 5u32, "2026-11-06T12:41Z", "main", "main 11-06 10:3x spiral apps/zed (unstaged): server.rs read EOIE_SPIRAL_COMPILE / EOIE_DOTNET as fallbacks, names nothing sets since kit moved to KIT_SPIRAL_COMPILE / KIT_DOTNET (kit README, compiler-contracts). Renamed to the KIT_ names, test sample paths C:\\home\\git\\eoie -> C:\\home\\git\\kit, README example likewise; cargo test 23/23 passed (11 + 12), 0 eoie left in apps/zed src/README. extension.wasm (tracked, 10-12) is stale and Zed rebuilds it on dev install. Kept: lib/spiral/iggy.spi's 'eoie' in frozen wire-format fixtures (the hex encodes the 4 bytes; renaming changes the fixture, not product naming).")
inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_6 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 6u32, "2026-11-06T12:49Z", "compiler", "11-06 08:5x compiler (owner of the Delphi keys): respelled every backend_switch `Delphi =` key in spiral apps/compiler to `Pascal =`: 20 sites in 19 files (18 tracked samples incl. samples/core/sm.spi, plus the new untracked backend_switch_missing_arm_site). No record had both keys. Recount: git -C C:\\home\\git\\spiral grep -c -E \"^\\s+Delphi = \" -- apps/compiler -> 0 (exit 1 = no match). apps/cells: 0 sites in that form. The compiler maps Delphi -> Pascal (backend_key_canonical, spiral_compiler.fs 9816), but BackendSwitch evaluates arms in key order and validation can emit globals, and core/sm.spi feeds most samples. So PENDING proof: a compile-only -Suite all on installed pack52, then git diff on samples outputs must show 0 changed output files. Runs on the box after the record-update census. Not touched yet: the sample folder name delphi_uses_units (renaming moves a matrix id) and the scripts' -eq 'Delphi' aliases (probe, bench-pair, test.ps1 ConvertTo-BackendName and ValidateSet, mega bench.ps1); next, after a caller grep.")
inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_7 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 7u32, "2026-11-06T13:33Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:3x compiler: the 4 command-line Delphi aliases are REMOVED (unstaged, all parse 0): probe.ps1 (ValidateSet and the -eq 'Delphi' line), bench-pair.ps1 (the -eq line), test.ps1 ('Delphi' dropped from -Probe's ValidateSet), mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 (the per-backend alias). Callers checked across spiral, kit, fiscal, x, tibia and i574n.github: none pass Delphi to these scripts (kit README names a different script, spiral.ps1). KEPT on purpose: test.ps1's ConvertTo-BackendName, which also normalizes STORED data (the box baseline EXPECTED.tsv still has 444 Delphi rows); it goes after the next single-flight -Accept rewrites the baseline as Pascal. Output proof for the key respell: the full compile-only suite was too slow (test.ps1 picked 1 worker on a memory-short box), so I stopped it. The proof now compiles only the 28 samples that can change: the 18 edited plus every sample reaching samples/core sm.spi's byte_to_i32 through its utf8/codepoint functions; their outputs must equal HEAD. Side finding: the stopped run rewrote 19 mega_brzozowski outputs with the CURRENT compiler's clone elision (v11.clone() -> v11). That is pre-existing drift from earlier packs, not this change; those outputs are correct for pack53c and are the user's to commit.")
inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_8 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 8u32, "2026-11-06T13:34Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:3x compiler: PROOF: the Delphi -> Pascal key respell is byte-neutral. Installed pack53c (core 24D3967377735A37), test.ps1 -Suite all -Filter over the 28 affected samples (single-flight-20261106-093130): 216 jobs, examples 212 (208 ok at parity with the baseline, 4 error = the new backend_switch_missing_arm_site rows), frontier 4 (the expected-error frontier_hopacsota_deferred_validation_mismatch rows); git status shows 0 changed output files among the 28 samples. The compiler's share of the delphi term is done: 0 `Delphi =` keys in apps/compiler, 0 command-line aliases. Legitimate and kept: the sample folder name samples/delphi_uses_units (a matrix id; FPC's Delphi-mode units are its subject), test.ps1's stored-data normalization until the next -Accept, and FPC's {$mode delphi}. Recount: git -C C:\\home\\git\\spiral grep -n -E \"^\\s+Delphi = |-eq 'Delphi'\" -- apps/compiler -> only test.ps1:26 ConvertTo-BackendName (kept, stated reason).")
inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_9 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 9u32, "2026-11-06T19:45Z", "main", "main 11-06 15:4x RECOUNT. Command: for each of the 11 own repos, git grep -i -I -c <term>, excluding docs/backlog/state and kit state/agile.spi. Result: eoie spiral 5, kit 558, x 1, i574n.github 1508; kino spiral 2111, tibia 1, i574n.github 362; delphi spiral 550, kit 2, fiscal 3, i574n.github 120; harness kit 9, tibia 1, i574n.github 124; postab spiral 2, kit 1, x 21, tibia 1, i574n.github 76; dir-tree-html spiral 8, html 1, dice 2, alphabet 1, i574n.github 44; bless tibia 35, i574n.github 106. i574n.github is almost all HISTORICAL or GENERATED: docs/backlog/archive/done-notes.spi (741 eoie) plus apps/graphs/out/backlog.{mmd,svg,graphml}, which are rendered from the backlog and regenerate on the next graphs build. main's live share, FIXED (unstaged): scripts/remote.ps1:42 dropped the dead $target.eoie fallback (all 4 machines in remote-machines.json carry kit; parse 0; a live 'remote.ps1 europa job list' resolves kit). scripts/resource-report.ps1 dropped the 'eoie' team prefix. apps/graphs/compiler_model.spi renamed the backend node NBDelphi -> NBPascal (key b_pascal, title Pascal); proof: --backend Kotlin before vs after differs in exactly those 5 lines (US44_NBPascal, key, title), same 880741 B. graphs.kt is regenerated by build.ps1 before kotlinc and its tracked copy is already 4 days stale, so it was not hand-edited. LEGITIMATE and kept: graphs agile.spi area_of_word 'eoie'/'kino'/'harness' (classifies historical titles), remote.ps1 'kino' (the real Kino dep folder), banned-words-scan 'harness' (the scanner's own word), agent-sync history lines. Left for owners: kit 558 (state/owner_growth, FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md, coverage lcov), spiral kino 2111 (apps/cells kino_text_* sidecar names; APPS-GRANULAR-HEAL slice 2 replaces them with lib grapheme ops), spiral delphi 550 (compiler: FPC mode + the delphi_uses_units sample, per their n7), x postab 21 (x).")
inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_10 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 10u32, "2026-11-06T19:45Z", "main", "Next step: kit rules whether its 558 eoie hits (state history, FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW, coverage) are historical; APPS-GRANULAR-HEAL slice 2 removes the kino_text_* sidecar names; then recount with the command in n9.")
inl note_of_rename_leftovers_1106_11 () = Note ("RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106", 11u32, "2026-11-06T23:06Z", "main", "main 11-06 19:0x the eoie arm is GONE from i574n.github apps/graphs/agile.spi:72 (now: w =. \"kit\" ?> Kit). My n9 kept it as historical, but area_of_word only ever reads TAGS (first_team, first_lane, first tag), and kit retagged all 73 backlog items eoie -> kit today, so the arm was dead. proof: graphs --backend Kotlin compiles; the diff vs the previous build is confined to area_of_word (its eoie branch removed, locals renumbered). graphs.kt and out/backlog.* regenerate on the next graphs build. i574n.github now has 0 live eoie references outside history (the done-notes archive and note texts).")
