inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_1 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 1u32, "2026-11-06T11:25Z", "fiscal", "DoD: xsd_emit gate green; regen of 2 families (nfe_v4, ubl_invoice_2_1) changes only their reader text; their unit Cells gates green on a fresh stage. NEXT: after step 2 lands. TYPEFEATURES: exists v. field owner v.")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_2 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 2u32, "2026-11-06T11:28Z", "fiscal", "Rescoped by the step-1 design: DoD adds a measured coverage target. Record writers with a field GADT are 4969 of 8745 = 56.8% today (census: union <ty>_field r count vs and let <ty>_children count over fiscal/generated); this step makes attribute_step and derived_prefix base parts produce witnesses, target >= 95%, and the reader reads through <ty>_fields.")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_3 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:59Z", "fiscal", "17:0x DESIGN REFINED by a census (box fiscal/generated, 83 units, today's committed text; scratchpad gadt-census.ps1): 8176 record writers (choice unions, 274, counted apart: the 11-06 07:2x 56.8% mixed them in), 3128 with union <ty>_field r = 38.3%. The 5048 without: 4976 (98.6%) are derived wrappers whose whole body is '<base>_children x.base', 66 are base + own parts, 6 are empty bodies, 0 staged owners. CORRECTION to the step-1 design: attribute_step does NOT block a GADT (attributes go to attribute_parts, which all_witnessed never sees); the blocker is derived_prefix writing (step-6 draft xsd_emit 673807F2 :2493) mapping base_children through plain (no witness), so all_witnessed sees a None part. CHANGE for this step: derived_prefix gives the base part a witness {case = case_name (owner ++# '_field') 'base'; t = <base type>; field = 'base'; fragment = '<base>_children v'; tag = ''; occurs = {1; Some 1}} (its prototype needs the owner name, as element_witness has), so base-only and base + own records get <ty>_field / <ty>_get / <ty>_fields; expected coverage ~99.9% (8170/8176); then the reader reads through <ty>_fields. DoD unchanged (xsd_emit gate; regen of nfe_v4 + ubl_invoice_2_1 changes only reader/witness text; their unit gates green on a fresh stage). NEXT: draft on top of the step-6 xsd_emit once the field-meta set lands (one xsd_emit stack at a time).")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_4 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 4u32, "2026-11-09T07:34Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 CHANGE MAP on the step-0 draft xsd_emit 7A6892B9 (the base this step stacks on once step 0 lands; drafting now would make a 2-deep stack on one file). The witness-less base part is derived_prefix writing (:2528): parts = listm::map plain (base_children kinds base). The prototype (:2194, ':? derived_prefix f : \\* form. f -> list (string * type_kind) -> type_reference form -> walked') has no owner name, and the base witness's case needs one (case_name (owner ++# '_field') 'base', as element_witness builds at :~2520). So: (1) add an owner string to the prototype; (2) update its 6 instances: reading :2319, staged_reading :2424, writing :2528, staged_writing :2631, exampling :2699, staged_exampling :2762 (the staged ones delegate, so they only pass the owner through); (3) update the 2 dispatch sites :2851 and :2875; (4) writing's base part becomes { text = base_children ...; witness = Some { case = case_name (owner ++# '_field') 'base'; t = <base type>; field = 'base'; fragment = '<base>_children v'; tag = ''; occurs = once } } so all_witnessed (:2090) succeeds for base-only and base + own records. Records: witness (:2072), part (:2074), plain (:2076). Expected census 38.3% -> ~99.9% (8170 of 8176). DoD unchanged (xsd_emit gate; regen of nfe_v4 + ubl_invoice_2_1 changes only reader/witness text; their unit gates green). Step 0 + R6 land is queued on the box (waiting for CPU under 60%).")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_5 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 5u32, "2026-11-09T08:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 UNBLOCKED: step 0 is live (xsd_emit 7A6892B9), so this step drafts directly on live with no draft stack. The n4 change map applies to the live file line for line (derived_prefix prototype :2194, its 6 instances, dispatch :2851/:2875, writing's base-part witness).")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_6 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 6u32, "2026-11-09T08:26Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 DRAFTED on live xsd_emit 7A6892B9 (no stack): kit drafts spiral XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ v1 xsd_emit.spi 0888893E. Changes: (1) the derived_prefix prototype takes the owner name (f -> string -> kinds -> type_reference -> walked); (2) its 6 instances take it, and the staged ones pass it through; (3) the one call with arguments (record dispatch, live :3044) passes the record name, which is the owner element_content_walk already uses for element witnesses; (4) new base_fragment and base_witness (before emit_element_witness, define-before-use checked): case = case_name (owner ++ _field) base, t = reference_type base (the record's declared base field type, :1310), field = base, tag = empty (base content has no element), occurs = once, fragment = the base_children expression over v (record: <base>_children v; enum/validated: xml.text_children (to_text v); text: xml.text_children v); writing's derived_prefix now gives its base part that witness, so all_witnessed succeeds for derived records. Gate: xsd_emit lib gate (all tests) running on europa against the box's live lib (event_log 6701B3BE) plus this draft. NEXT: regen of nfe_v4 + ubl_invoice_2_1 to confirm only witness/reader text changes, and the coverage census (union <ty>_field r over record writers, 38.3 % -> target ~99.9 %).")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_7 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 7u32, "2026-11-09T10:43Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 LANDED. Gate: xsd_emit 37/37 on moon (job-1794215186106, type errors 0; europa's duplicate was stopped, starved by another lane's processes). Land: moon proof job-1794219151415 closed green on a byte-identical box copy incl. microblog's new tlds.spi (round trip, 0 consumer signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type probe PASS 37 tests typed, respell drift 0, digest C144C1B7950BD0EF); the box lib had moved again before the box land, so lib_land_window reran the fast checks on the box (its designed fallback) and closed green: live xsd_emit 0888893E, box lib digest 138AC55BB63B1A0B. Derived records now give their base part a witness (base_witness), so all_witnessed succeeds for them. NEXT for this item: measure the coverage census on the next regen (union <ty>_field r over record writers, 38.3 % before; target ~99.9 %), then the reader reads through <ty>_fields. Unblocked by this land: OMNILEDGER R8, FISCAL-TYPED-UNITS SCC emission, the GRANULAR 6A-6C slices (one xsd_emit draft at a time).")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3_read_8 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ", 8u32, "2026-11-10T23:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 20:3x GROOM: both remaining steps touch lib xsd_emit (the coverage census needs a regen on a landed emitter; 'the reader reads through <ty>_fields' is an xsd_emit edit), and xsd_emit already carries two stacked drafts in flight: FISCAL-TYPED-UNITS-D1 (SCC, in proof on ganymede) and FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D2 (staged versioned families, checked on europa). One xsd_emit draft line at a time, so this queues behind them. Next step: after both land, measure the census on a regen, then draft the reader over <ty>_fields on top of the landed emitter.")
