inl formatter_join_lone_then () = Task ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", "Formatter rule: join a lone '?>' (edition-3 then) onto its '? cond' line, and a lone 'then' onto its 'if cond' line, whenever the joined line fits in 120 columns; today the formatter keeps authored breaks, so 'then laid below its if' (the user's 10-24 review) survives in edition-3 form: 76 lone '?>' lines in spiral (apps/compiler 33, lib 23, apps/cells 20; 66 of 67 joinable), 238 in kit, 73 in fiscal, 1-3 in x/dice/alphabet/tibia", Story, P1, D3, 90u32, Blocked, "", "formatter,compiler,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_join_lone_then () = Planning ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:12Z", "main", "main 11-06 09:4x filed from FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW (main): edition-2 lone 'then' lines are at 0 in spiral after the 10-24 heal, but the respell to edition-3 symbols re-created the same layout as a lone '?>'. DoD: 'spiral format' joins them (token-neutral: parse-same on the lib corpus, 0 lines over 120 created), a formatter test row for both spellings, and a census per repo after each lane formats its tree. Next step: add the join to the formatter's if/then layout pass beside the existing keep-breaks rule.")
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_2 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T13:24Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:2x compiler: CAUSE (read at the tree core after pack53c, f4621c37): FormatterLayout's if-branch joiner mergeThen (spiral_compiler.fs ~33080) matched only the literal text \"then\" / \"then \", but edition-3 files print SpecThen as \"?>\" (FormatterConvert ~31218), so a lone ?> could never join. On top of that, thenStaysOnCondition kept every AUTHORED break before then (authoredBreaks) and otherwise followed a per-file ThenHabit vote, which preserved exactly the then-below-if layout of the 10-24 review. FIX: kitdo 1-join-then-both-spellings.kitdo (kit drafts FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN, 5 replacements, dry run ok on a copy). A then keyword always joins its condition line when the joined line fits; both spellings go through thenWord/isThenWord/startsWithThen; the now-dead ThenHabit type, thenHabit, thenHabitOf and its assignment, and keywordLine/keywordLines/writtenOnOneLine are removed. NEXT STEP: candidate build (joins pack55 with RECORD-UPDATE-TYPE-CHANGE 1), then format-corpus format over lib (G1 parse-same, G7 comments-same, over120-created 0) and the census of lone ?> / then lines per repo before and after. DoD: lone-then count drops to 0 where the join fits, the guard rows stay at 141/141, and a formatter test row covers both spellings. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: none (formatter layout text).")
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_3 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:25Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:2x compiler: BASELINE census before the fix (git grep over tracked .spi/.spir, excluding docs/backlog and compiler samples). A line that STARTS with the then keyword, alone or followed by its body (both join under the fix when they fit): spiral ?> 638 / then 5; kit ?> 873 / 0; fiscal ?> 109 / then 1096 (edition-2 generated units); x 10 / 0; dice 19 / 0; alphabet 27 / 0; tibia 215 / 0. Main's 76 for spiral counts only the bare lone ?> lines; this count is wider on purpose. Command: git -C <repo> grep -n -E \"^\\s*\\?>( |$)\" -- *.spi *.spir (and the same with then).")
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_4 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 4u32, "2026-11-06T13:39Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:4x compiler: TEST FIXTURES added (unstaged) to the formatter synthetic corpus, which candidate-gate.ps1 checks for stability and parse-same: tmp/formatter/synthetic/then_below_condition_e3.spi (? cond / ?> 1i32 / |: 2i32, plus a lone ?> with its body indented below) and then_below_condition_e2.spi (if cond / then 1i32 / else 2i32). Baseline, installed pack53c `format --stdin`: both files come back unchanged, the then keyword still below its condition (the reported bug, reproduced). Expected on pack55: \"? x < 3i32 ?> 1i32\" and \"if x < 3i32 then 1i32\" on one line, and the lone ?> joined as \"? x < 3i32 ?>\" with its body kept indented below.")
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_5 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 5u32, "2026-11-06T13:44Z", "compiler", "11-06 09:4x compiler: pack55 (first program version) left both fixtures UNCHANGED. The reason: the relayout joiner (mergeThen) only runs for blocks that do NOT fit as written; a block whose lines all fit 120 columns takes the AsWritten path (FormatterFormat ~33915), which applies only the textHabits text passes, accepted when sameParse. So the fix belongs in textHabits too. Program extended (6th replacement): a then-join text pass at the end of textHabits. A line starting with ?> / then joins the previous line when that line is a one-line condition head (`? `, `|? `, `if `, `elif `) at the same indent, has no // comment, both lines are quote-safe, and the joined line fits 120. The existing sameParse guard drops the whole habit pass if the parse changes. Dry run ok (6 replacements). Rebuilding as pack55b.")
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_6 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 6u32, "2026-11-06T14:19Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:1x compiler: pack55b (core C4791083C75098CB) JOINS both fixtures (\"? x < 3i32 ?> 1i32\", \"if x < 3i32 then 1i32\", lone ?> -> \"? x < 3i32 ?>\" with the body below). lib corpus (format-corpus format, 154 files), installed vs pack55b: parse-same 154/154 both, comments-same 154, over120-layout-created 0 both, files-unchanged 121 -> 87 (34 files gain then-joins). One regression found and FIXED: G1 non-idempotent 1 -> 2. A stdin re-format of every output pins it to lib/spiral/file_system.spi: the relayout path (mergeThen) joined an outer lone ?>, and the nested `? recursive / ?> ...` was joined only on the second pass, because the text join ran only on the as-written path. The program now makes the join a standalone joinThenLines, applied after textHabits AND to the relaid result (each guarded by sameParse); 8 replacements, dry run ok. The 5 other stdin-non-idempotent lib files (convert, erlang_process, metrics, resultm, sm') are equally non-idempotent on the INSTALLED formatter (a global-string layout, pre-existing, not this item). Rebuilding as pack55d (4 programs).")
inl note_of_formatter_join_lone_then_7 () = Note ("FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN", 7u32, "2026-11-06T14:32Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:4x compiler: pack55d (core 257DB91886B97811; this program now 8 replacements) is GREEN on the formatter gates. Fixtures: both spellings join, the lone ?> joins with its body kept below. lib corpus (154 files): parse-same 154, comments-same 154, over120-layout-created 0, files-unchanged 87 (34 files gain joins), G1-not-idempotent 1 = the installed baseline (the 1 -> 2 regression from pack55b is fixed: file_system.spi now reaches its fixed point in one pass). proof: format-corpus exit 0; the stdin second pass over file_system.spi is byte-identical. Remaining before Done: pack55d's compiler review (running), install, and the per-repo recount after the lanes format their trees.")
