inl c_closure_called_loop_inline () = Task ("C-CLOSURE-CALLED-LOOP-INLINE", "codegenC: small self-tail leaf loops called from a closure body (parallel::for_index lambdas) stay __attribute__((noinline)); measure first whether inlining them pays (transformer v8 dot_l30/32/34/45, dot57, row_q859), then extend C-BORROWED-LOOP-INLINE's rule to closure bodies only if it does", Story, P3, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "compiler,team:compiler,codegen,c,performance,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_closure_called_loop_inline () = Planning ("C-CLOSURE-CALLED-LOOP-INLINE", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_c_closure_called_loop_inline_1 () = Note ("C-CLOSURE-CALLED-LOOP-INLINE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:13Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:11 tibia: found closing COMPILER-C-BORROWED-PARAMS (see its last note). DoD: an A/B on transformer v8 42M, the same source with a sed-removed noinline on those six functions, 5 quiet rounds per arm under tf9-sweep.ps1''s skip-not-run harness, parity checked. If the median gain is >= 2%, extend the inline rule to closure bodies and re-measure; otherwise close as measured-no-gain. NEXT: the sed A/B on the node. TypeFeatures: codegen-only, no source type changes.")
inl note_of_c_closure_called_loop_inline_2 () = Note ("C-CLOSURE-CALLED-LOOP-INLINE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:16Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:16 tibia: A/B QUEUED on the node: job-1793967335894-tibia-tf-inline-ab, after the 15M sweep. Script tibia-tf6\\inl-ab.ps1: v8-regen.c (core A688EE5AD426) against v8-inl.c, which drops __attribute__((noinline)) from exactly the 6 closure-called loops (the swap count is asserted). Both are built with -Ofast -march=native -fopenmp and the unaligned-vector-move flag, with the building gcc's bin first on PATH. Parity is gated against v3 at OMP 1 and 8 on 42M; then 5 quiet rounds (skip-not-run), alternating order, 8 threads. Pending.")
inl note_of_c_closure_called_loop_inline_3 () = Note ("C-CLOSURE-CALLED-LOOP-INLINE", 3u32, "2026-11-06T19:55Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:0x tibia: job-1793967335894-tibia-tf-inline-ab STOPPED by me after its quiet gate could not pass (same node load that voided job-1793965243889-tibia-tf9-quiet-15m: 0 of 8 calm windows), so it would only have held PR-29's hashed-lanes job for ~2 h. Its non-timing results stand: inline swaps 6 of 6 applied; stories42M parity v8r and v8i at OMP 1 and 8 == v3 (749 chars). The A/B itself is NOT measured: rerun on a quiet host (europa has 2 CPUs, too few for OMP 8; the node after the fleet's trains).")
