inl note_of_tibia_nugget_bitsets_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:17Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:17 tibia: split from TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS (main: steps of 120 min or less). Source: inventory 3 (deckm bitmask). DoD: a bitset module with set/test/count tests on c and rust; apps/map's item_kinds switched over with the terrain/region parity of run.ps1 unchanged (needs the box's live Canary data); generated-line count for apps/map quoted before and after. NEXT: the bitset module with its tests. TypeFeatures: modes and decisions are unions, not int ids or bool flags (the nugget inventory's remodel rule).")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_bitsets_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:23Z", "tibia", "11-06 08:22 tibia: LIB DRAFT (lib first: no bitset exists in lib/spiral). New module lib/spiral/bitset.spi, kit store drafts\\spiral\\TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS\\v1, 80CDCA12BBC6: the record bitset = { words : array u32; size : i32 }, with empty/has/put/remove/count_set (Kernighan popcount) and 3 tests on c and rust: bits set and cleared across words, a new set empty at every word edge (31/32/64, 3 words for 65 bits), the top bit counted once. The round trip is clean (canonical, fixpoint). PENDING on the node: job-1793967698581-tibia-bitset-gate, after the v8 Cells run. It adds the file to the mirror lib, runs the draft and a mutant (remove keeps the bit, so the first test must go red), then deletes the file. NEXT after green: lib_land_window, then switch apps/map item_kinds (box data for the parity).")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_bitsets_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:47Z", "tibia", "11-06 09:47 tibia: LIB LANDED. lib/spiral/bitset.spi (new, 80CDCA12BBC6, unstaged) via lib_land_window. Closed green: 0 consumer signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (3 tests typed, 0 errors), respell_drift 0; lib digest FECE83845C67116A; undo at spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261106-094148. Proof before landing: node job-1793967698581-tibia-bitset-gate, where the draft passed 3/3 on c and rust (6 rows) and the mutant (remove keeps the bit) went red on exactly bits_are_set_and_cleared_across_words c. NEXT: switch apps/map item_kinds (5 arrays of 65536 bool/i32) to bitset for the bool ones; the parity proof needs the box's live Canary data (run.ps1).")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_bitsets_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS", 4u32, "2026-11-06T14:03Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:03 tibia: apps/map SWITCHED (unstaged; -ChecksOnly green). item_kinds' unpassable/sight_blocking/ground/height are bitset::bitset (2048 u32 words each, instead of 65536-entry bool arrays), built by no_items (). Writers use bitset::put, the height read uses bitset::has, copy_bit copies a kinds bit into the per-depth tile stack (copy_mark stays for exits/teleports, which are still bool arrays from ids_with), and merge_from writes into a bitset. GENERATED LINES (honest): Rust map.rs is 2306 -> 2376 (+70; same installed compiler, HEAD vs this tree), because the bitset ops inline. The memory saving is real (4 x 64 KiB of bools -> 4 x 8 KiB), but line count does not drop, so this does not move apps/map toward the 1000-line gate (that stays with the linked-unit split). PENDING: map.spi's own Cells tests on node job-1793973814751-tibia-mapbits-cells (mirror tibia-map, which has bitset); the run.ps1 terrain/region parity needs the box's live Canary data.")
inl note_of_tibia_nugget_bitsets_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUGGET-BITSETS", 5u32, "2026-11-06T14:20Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:20 tibia: map.spi's Cells tests are GREEN with bitsets (node job-1793973814751-tibia-mapbits-cells, mirror tibia-map whose lib has bitset.spi; map 13B00E7E0319, the same bytes as the local tree): exit 0, discovered 5, executed 5, passed 5 on rust and c (varint, signed labels, the word mask, row spans x2). Left for the DoD: run.ps1's terrain/region parity, which needs the box's live Canary data (TibiaWorld), i.e. a box live window. Resume when: the box has a free live window.")
