inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:33Z", "fiscal", "DoD: regen writes the MDF-e pair as one closure module + two thin version roots; both unit Cells gates green on a fresh stage; the repeated-line share drops from the 11-06 baseline 60.6% (census: scratchpad repeat-census.ps1 (identical top-level definitions in >= 5 units, by line)). NEXT: read generate_versioned_family (xsd_emit) and the demo test, then draft the families/generator change. TYPEFEATURES: payload-free nominal version tags, exists v. version_witness v.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:35Z", "fiscal", "08:4x DESIGN READ (live lib xsd_emit D00BE390, live generator 3B3D0A0E; text only). LIB: generate_versioned_family members core (xsd_emit:3504) returns (core_text, version_texts, family_text); split_family puts identical types in the core, each version opens it, and family_text (3466) emits one nominal per version, union version_witness v, and version-indexed unions with one reader matching the witness (demo test versioned_families_read_through_one_witness :3574). GAP 1 (blocking): its parts come from member_parts -> module_parts (3083) = module_parts_with Reading, the READER-ONLY walk; regular units come from the staged walk (staged_walk_texts :3064: readers + writers + examples) plus certificates and per-unit checks. Adopting it now would drop MDF-e's writers, examples and tests. GAP 2 (spec): tags carry a string payload (nominal v1 = string; V1 :: string -> version_witness v1), against the title's 'payload-free'; keep the string (it is the @versao text the dispatching reader needs) and retitle. FISCAL SIDE (ready): generator already writes unit dependencies (write_generated_module_with deps, module_package '../<unit>-' entries, as CFDI complements do), so core / version / family units can be wired that way. SPLIT of this step: 1a (lib, 120): generate_versioned_family over module_parts_staged (the full staged walk) with a lib test that a version module keeps its writer and example; 1b (fiscal, 120): families.spi gains an MDF-e group, the generator writes core + 2 version units + family unit with deps, unit gates on a fresh stage. NEXT: 1a draft.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T22:51Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 19:0x STEP 1b HELD: reading for the wiring found a gap in the landed lib step 1a (mine). staged_member_parts runs module_parts_staged but does NOT apply staged_items, and the versioned core gets no staging_prelude, whereas staged_units (what standalone signed units use) does both. So versioned MDF-e units would carry staged writers over unstaged types and most likely not compile; the 1a test only checked that the writer text is present. Certificates would also stay inline in the core or version units instead of a separate unit (compiles; recorded as a known difference). Fix sliced as FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D2 (lib, light). Wiring facts kept for 1b: only src/families.spi names generated_mdfe_* in source (the rest is target/ output), so the version units keep the names generated_mdfe_v1_00 / generated_mdfe_v3_00 and CI metric history stays continuous; the gate table is schema/example driven and does not change. Next step: D2, then 1b.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE", 4u32, "2026-11-10T23:12Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 19:5x STEP 1b DRAFTED: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE\\generator.spi 0C311E88 over live BC710324 (.base kept). write_family_modules skips the two MDF-e roots (written_unless_versioned); write_versioned_family writes the core unit (deps: runtime), each version unit (deps: runtime + core; its text plus that root's unit checks) with its certificates unit kept, and the family unit (deps: runtime + core + both versions) through generate_versioned_family_staged ['Signature']; write_every_family = the ungrouped roots + write_mdfe_family, so generates_every_family_version still counts 12. MDF-e roots stay in the families.spi tables, so the gate table is unchanged. New tests: writes_mdf_e_as_one_versioned_family (2 written), the_mdf_e_family_unit_depends_on_its_core, an_mdf_e_version_opens_the_core. Budget 49 -> 49. RISKS for the gate: (1) version texts start 'open <core>' without their own codec prelude, so the gate will show whether opening the core is enough to reach xml_codec; (2) the certificates unit is regenerated from the standalone path, so certificate items also sit inline in the version text (duplicate definitions, separate modules). Next step: once D2 lands, gate the generator on ganymede with a fresh stage (build.ps1 -Files generator, then the MDF-e units).")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE", 5u32, "2026-11-11T01:57Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 21:5x LIB FIX LANDED (D2: live xsd_emit 3AF2661A013F, 47/47). Step 1b is unblocked: the generator draft drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE\\generator.spi 0C311E88 (over live BC710324) writes generated_mdfe_core, generated_mdfe_v1_00 / v3_00 (open the core) and generated_mdfe through generate_versioned_family_staged. Next step: gate it on a node with a fresh stage (fiscal-gate-on-ganymede recipe: build.ps1 -Files generator, then the MDF-e units); the two recorded risks (version units reaching xml_codec through the core; certificates inline and in their own unit) are what that gate settles.")
