inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3_parallel_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:44Z", "fiscal", "DoD: build.ps1 gates N changed units with at most cores/2 lib_gate processes at once, each with its own -BuildPath; wall time for 6 changed units measured against the serial run on the node. NEXT: after step 1; heavy-gate lessons apply (per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3_parallel_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:00Z", "fiscal", "13:5x DRAFT in place (fiscal/scripts/build.ps1 4D70767E -> C47F6C6E, unstaged; backup scratchpad build.before-parallel-4D70767E.ps1): new -Parallel <n> (default 1 = today's serial path unchanged; 0 = max(1, cores/2)). Invoke-TestFile split into Start-TestFile (launch, cache skip) + Complete-TestFile (collect rows/problems/gate-cache key); Invoke-TestFiles runs the middle unit group as a pool with true worker slots 0..n-1, each child started with Start-Process -Environment @{ MIX_BUILD_PATH = target/mix-workers/<slot> } (never a process-wide env: memory heavy-gate-lessons); generator and reports stay serial. Box pool test (stub notebook, CPU-light): 7 units at -Parallel 3 = max concurrent 3, exactly 3 build paths (0,1,2), the planted failure reported as a problem, rows 7/7; -Parallel 1 = serial, no MIX_BUILD_PATH override. PENDING (node laptop): job-1793987979366-fiscal-parallel-measure, queued after libgran5: 6 units (cr_factura_4_4, es_facturae_3_2_2, cfdi_v4_0, fatturapa_1_2_3, hu_nav_3_0, mdfe_v3_00) on a stage copy of the t1101 fiscal mirror, runs parallel-cold (-Parallel 4), serial, parallel-warm; wall time per run + per-unit verdicts. NEXT: read the job's stdout.log; keep -Parallel only if every unit stays green in the parallel runs.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3_parallel_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", 3u32, "2026-11-06T23:38Z", "fiscal", "19:4x MEASUREMENT VOID (node laptop, core 8F0094967068FC85, job-1793987979366-fiscal-parallel-measure; stopped by me at 19:4x, exit 143, stage removed junctions-first, t1101 mirror deps untouched). parallel-cold (-Parallel 4) ran the 6 units in 2662 s wall (per-unit 619-957 s, sum 4881 s), but EVERY test failed at compile time, identically: '** (Mix) ...generated_cfdi_v4_0.spi: FatalError ... cells-mounts/c652c0db298b28fc/generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0/generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0.spi:2:6: ETY-UnboundModule: Unbound module. In the definition: open xml_codec' (same in all 6). Cause: the stage borrowed the t1101 mirror's spiral tree (deps junctions), whose lib lacks box-only modules (memory node-repo-mirrors-use-the-base-spiral-lib) and whose Cells still has the old mount key (mounts.ex 85B259B5A1D0, the stale-mount bug x fixed on the box), so the serial run would fail the same way and the timings measure failures; stopped instead of letting it hold the node past 21:00. The -Parallel mechanics did run 4 at once on the node with per-slot MIX_BUILD_PATH (no 'Waiting for lock' line in the log). NEXT: rerun with the box's lib staged as lib.zip under the stage (as the lib gates do) and a fresh stage path, serial vs -Parallel 4 vs -Parallel 4 warm; keep -Parallel 1 the default until then.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3_parallel_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", 4u32, "2026-11-07T17:45Z", "fiscal", "11-07 13:5x PENDING (node laptop): job-1794073518766-fiscal-full-build, a FULL fiscal build.ps1 -Parallel 4 on a fresh mirror f1107 (spiral REMOTE-SYNC-OK head f6000cfa digest 8114FD197F1FA09B; fiscal REMOTE-SYNC-OK head 6b82ad5c digest 7A1CA4A555B8485C, incl. the unstaged init.ps1 fix + guard), init.ps1 run there first for the corpus, pinned compiler copy, with these drafts overlaid: src/families.spi 2ACF1F66 + src/generator.spi 9670695D (FISCAL-LAW-MISSING-REPORTED, stacked on FISCAL-LIFECYCLE-EVENTS (b') and FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST S3), src/lifecycle.spi 4C061E89 ((b')), scripts/family-gates.ps1 A6B1FD05 (S3). One run proves all three drafts (generated units regenerate with the new law and lifecycle tests, every unit's Cells gate, the examples step through the S3 family-gates TSV) and measures -Parallel 4 for FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL. Expected problem: generated drift vs HEAD (the law adds a test to every XSD unit), to be copied back with the proof. Launched plain, not --heavy (the node's kit could not find spiral's scripts/heavy.ps1; the node had no other job).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3_parallel_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", 5u32, "2026-11-08T00:13Z", "fiscal", "11-07 20:1x PARALLEL TIMING (node laptop, job-1794073877397-fiscal-full-build2, build.ps1 -Parallel 4, full fiscal incl. regen, 13:5x-20:0x): the run did NOT fit the 6 h job cap: 98 test files finished, then the cap stopped it with generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 at 1926 s and generated_ubl_receiptadvice_2_1 at 792 s still running. The tail is dominated by the big generated units run 4 at a time: generated_nfe_v4 alone ran > 2225 s (and VOIDed 2 tests on the cell timeout), and each UBL document unit took ~2800-3240 s (despatchadvice done in 3239 s). So -Parallel 4 on the laptop does not make a full gate fit one job: the gate set must be split by unit family (Brazilian DFe, UBL, rest) into separate jobs, each well under 6 h, and the UBL units given the widest cell timeout. Log kept in the session scratchpad (fullbuild\\build2.log).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3_parallel_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL-3-PARALLEL", 6u32, "2026-11-10T23:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 20:3x GROOM: the 11-08 next step ('split the gate set by unit family into separate jobs, each under 6 h') must NOT become YAML jobs: the user rejected multi-job CI on 11-08 as drift, so CI stays one job running pwsh scripts/build.ps1 and scale lives in the entry script over our machines. That is now FISCAL-GATE-SHARD: build.ps1 -Shards/-ShardSet/-ShardWeights plus today's -ShardMaxUnitKB (a capped shard takes only small generated units, e.g. europa's 13 certificate units) split the gate across moon / ganymede / europa, each shard well under 6 h, and -MergeShards rebuilds the one verdict. Next step: none separate; this item closes when FISCAL-GATE-SHARD's 3-host sharded gate finishes inside the cap with -MergeShards equal to the unsharded unit set.")
inl xsd_facet_digits () = Task ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", "xsd_emit: generated readers reject values over totalDigits / fractionDigits (read by lib xsd today, never enforced)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-2-GADT", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,lib,facets", "current", "current")
