inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_1 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:52Z", "fiscal", "Found 11-06 09:0x (XSD-FACET-TYPES remainder census, live lib xsd D?, xsd_emit D00BE390): xsd reads TotalDigits/FractionDigits (xsd.spi:140-141) but xsd_emit enforces only Length/MinLength/MaxLength (length_checks :548, lengths_accept :997), Pattern (DFA), Enumeration and WhiteSpace; TotalDigits appears only in one example test (:3794). DoD: the validated-nominal reader for a restriction with totalDigits/fractionDigits rejects a value with too many digits (Invalid with its path), and its example stays valid; lib test plus one fiscal family whose schema uses them (find one with grep totalDigits in deps/corpus) green on a fresh-stage node gate. NEXT: grep the corpus for totalDigits/fractionDigits use and pick the family. TYPEFEATURES: none new (validated nominal).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_2 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T12:53Z", "fiscal", "09:0x CORPUS CENSUS: 20 XSDs use totalDigits/fractionDigits: cr/hacienda 9, cl/dte 2, hu/nav 2, mx/cfdi 2, pl/ksef 2, gr/mydata 1, mx/complements 1, tr/ubltr 1 (none in SEFAZ, which uses patterns). Proof family: generated_cfdi_v4_0 (cfdv40 + tdCFDI t_Importe-style decimals) plus one Hacienda unit. ORDER: draft after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-2's xsd_emit draft lands (same file, base D00BE390), so the two lib drafts never race.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_3 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:32Z", "fiscal", "16:3x DRAFT (kit drafts spiral\\XSD-FACET-DIGITS\\v1, stacked on the not-yet-landed field-meta + step-6 xsd_emit so the drafts never race): xml 57AB7497 over live EE1DC7C7 gains fraction_digits / total_digits (XSD 1.1 value i x 10^-n: sign and leading integer zeros are not digits, trailing fraction zeros are not significant, n counts toward totalDigits so 0.05 has 2) + test digit_counts_follow_xsd; xsd_emit B1178DE4 over step-6 673807F2: digit_checks emits 'xml.total_digits s <= n' / 'xml.fraction_digits s <= n' conjuncts into <type>_is_valid, has_digit_facet makes a totalDigits/fractionDigits restriction a validated nominal (is_constrained), the builtin decimal example '1' stays valid. CHECKS: format --check 0 (xsd_emit; xml's 5 format diffs are inherited base lines), GRANULAR 0 code overages both (europa counter); europa (core e6a3e4d0e7336508) --check exit 0 for xml, xsd_emit and the field-meta xml_codec it needs; digit_counts_follow_xsd as a single body: first run FAILED on my own wrong expectation (0.05 -> 1), corrected per XSD 1.1, rerun PASS. EXPECTED DRIFT: about 20 schemas' digit-faceted types (cr/hacienda 9, cl/dte 2, hu/nav 2, mx/cfdi 2, pl/ksef 2, gr/mydata 1, mx/complements 1, tr/ubltr 1) become validated nominals, so the generated units change. NEXT: after the field-meta set lands, a node full regen + Cells gate of xsd_emit/xml (proof family generated_cfdi_v4_0 + one Hacienda unit), then land.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_4 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T17:07Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 13:1x REBASED as v2 (kit drafts spiral\\XSD-FACET-DIGITS\\v2), the unblock for FISCAL-ERP-MONEY's last 10 percent and so FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (P2P-TYPESTATE is Done, MONEY R5 landed 11-08). v1 was stacked on a pre-11-09 xsd_emit (673807F2) and xml EE1DC7C7; both moved. xml.spi v2 3D08A402 over live 76E11AA1: the 5 digit helpers (xml_digits_unsigned/split/parts, fraction_digits, total_digits) and the digit_counts_follow_xsd test ported by anchor, blank lines added so they stay separate cells (v1 merged total_digits into is_space_character's cell). xsd_emit.spi v2 over 6A batch 5 (86826209, the next expected live, so this lands right after b5 and never races it): digit_checks + new facet_checks helper (length + digit conjuncts) before pattern_conjuncts, has_digit_facet before has_length_facet, is_constrained also counts digit facets; validator_text uses facet_checks with c/cs locals, so it gets SHORTER (was 21 over) instead of growing. No name clashes across lib; sm trim_start/trim_end/index_of/starts_with still exist. Budget and round trip running. NEXT: gate v2 (xml + xsd_emit) after b5 lands, then the cfdi_v4_0 family proof per the DoD.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_5 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T17:23Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 13:5x v2 CHECKED: xml.spi FCE8DD3E (the ported xml_digits_split was 284 > 272, so its parameter unsigned is now u; xml code overages 32 = live 32), xsd_emit.spi 070FB8C4 (202 = b5's 202, no growth); both round trips canonical. Ready to gate right after 6A batch 5 lands (v2 xsd_emit is built on b5).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_6 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T20:59Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 16:5x LIB LANDED: live xml.spi FCE8DD3E (over 76E11AA1) and xsd_emit.spi 070FB8C4 (over 86826209), copy-only on the box from proof job-1794257249532 (document_test 26 passed, type probe PASS for both modules, respell 0, digest 8515D6789EBB44B5). Gate on moon: xml 17/17 (digit_counts_follow_xsd included), xsd_emit 37/37, 0 type errors. RACE HANDLED: proof job-1794256573571 closed green, but layers.spi moved on the box during it, so it was not landed; the 3 differing files were re-synced, digests matched again (3C5B7A931082183F), and the re-proof was landed by a chained waiter within seconds of closing. Generated readers now reject values over totalDigits/fractionDigits (validated nominals via has_digit_facet). Remaining DoD: one fiscal family that uses the facets (cfdi_v4_0, plus a Hacienda unit) green on a fresh-stage node gate after the next fiscal regen.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_7 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T21:14Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 17:1x FAMILY PROOF STARTED on moon (the box is CPU-light only; moon had 53 percent CPU and 7.3 GB free): job-1794258829658 runs erp-node.ps1 regen with a fresh lib.zip (box lib incl. the landed xml FCE8DD3E and xsd_emit 070FB8C4) and fiscal.zip (box fiscal, git ls-files -co minus deps), then -Phase unit for generated_cfdi_v4_0 and generated_cr_factura_4_4 (Hacienda). regen waits for moon load under 70 percent, so it does not stack on the 6A b6 gate. Log: fiscal-erp-in\\digits-family.log.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_digits_8 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-DIGITS", 8u32, "2026-11-09T22:42Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 18:4x DONE. Family proof green on moon (job-1794258829658, 86 min, pinned compiler core B62490C34FD69070): regen against the landed lib (xml FCE8DD3E, xsd_emit 070FB8C4) passed the generator 28/28, formatted 83/83 units, wrote 167 generated files, every example validates; then generated_cfdi_v4_0 green in 484 s and the Hacienda unit generated_cr_factura_4_4 green in 216 s. DoD met: the lib test digit_counts_follow_xsd plus two fiscal families whose schemas use totalDigits/fractionDigits, green on a fresh-stage node gate. The regenerated tree is at fiscal-erp\\out\\regen.zip on moon (the box fiscal generated/ is unchanged; refreshing it is a separate step that feeds the user's next commit).")
inl xsd_facet_bounds () = Task ("XSD-FACET-BOUNDS", "lib xsd reads minInclusive/maxInclusive/minExclusive/maxExclusive and xsd_emit's readers enforce them (today the four facets are dropped at read)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 45u32, Active, "XSD-FACET-DIGITS", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,lib,facets", "current", "current")
