inl note_of_xsd_facet_bounds_1 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-BOUNDS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T12:52Z", "fiscal", "Found 11-06 09:0x: xsd_facet (xsd.spi:6-13) has no bound cases and the facet reader (134-141) drops minInclusive/maxInclusive/minExclusive/maxExclusive. DoD: xsd_facet gains the four bounds (decimal text), the reader keeps them, xsd_emit's validated reader for numeric/date restrictions enforces them, a lib test covers each, and examples stay inside the bounds; fresh-stage node gate green, regen diff limited to the families that use bounds. NEXT: after XSD-FACET-DIGITS (same emitter path). TYPEFEATURES: none new.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_bounds_2 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-BOUNDS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T08:42Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:0x (help pool, fiscal item, claimed microblog-b7595ac3): DRAFTED in the drafts store spiral/XSD-FACET-BOUNDS, 5 lib files, each with a .base. (1) xml.spi (base 3487D66E3B2B = LIB-CLONE-HEALS xml draft, which lands first): is_decimal_text, decimal_order (sign, whole length, then text; arbitrary width, so 20-digit fiscal bounds work without i64), and min_inclusive / max_inclusive / min_exclusive / max_exclusive (bound s): decimal order when the bound is decimal-shaped, text_order otherwise (dates 1970-01-01, year-months 2025-01); a non-decimal value never meets a decimal bound; test bound_facets_order_decimals_by_value_and_other_text_lexically (14 asserts). (2) xsd.spi: xsd_facet gains MinInclusive/MaxInclusive/MinExclusive/MaxExclusive : string; reader xsd_facet_bound keeps them (they were OtherFacet); test bound_facets_are_typed. (3) xsd_census.spi: the four map to BoundsCeiling directly; the string-matching ceiling_bound/ceiling_other are removed. (4) json_schema.spi: minimum/maximum/exclusive* go through xsd_facet_bound, so JSON bounds are typed too; its test now matches MaxInclusive/MinInclusive. (5) xsd_emit.spi: bound_checks emits xml.min_inclusive \"<b>\" s etc. into the validator; is_constrained includes has_bound_facet (bounded simple types become validated nominals, as digits did); simple_example keeps examples inside the bounds (moves to the first inclusive bound that passes pattern, length, digits and bounds); test bound_facets_validate_and_keep_examples_inside. Survey: 36 fiscal .xsd files use the facets (minInclusive 1 x54, 0 x36, maxInclusive 9999999999999.99999 x8, 99999999999999999999 x6, dates, year-months). PROOF QUEUED: box job-1794300131818-x-libland-proof-bounds waits for box2 to settle, then lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply on the same private copy (all 5 bases match it). NEXT STEP: read the proof; if green, land with -ProvenLog after LIB-CLONE-HEALS, then a fiscal regen family proof (cfdi_v4_0 + one Hacienda unit) on a node. TYPEFEATURES: the facet union stays a plain union; bounds are text by design (decimal or lexical decided by the bound).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_bounds_3 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-BOUNDS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T08:47Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:5x proof RE-QUEUED as box job-1794300438256-x-libland-proof-bounds2 (the first, job-1794300131818, stopped by me before it started work): it now also waits until the box holds under 70 percent CPU for 3 consecutive minutes, the rule fiscal uses for its gates, since fiscal saw Cells handshake timeouts with the box at 97-100 percent (FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW notes). Order unchanged: after box2 settles. NEXT STEP: read its tail.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_bounds_4 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-BOUNDS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T08:52Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:5x proof moved into ONE staged chain, box job-1794300687658-x-libland-proof-chain: quiet box -> LIB-CLONE-HEALS re-proof (its xml.spi is this draft's base) -> only if green, quiet box again -> this proof. bounds2 (job-1794300438256) stopped by me before it did any work: box2 closed red and was undone, so this draft's xml base would have been refused. NEXT STEP: read the chain tail.")
inl dice_pages_404 () = Task ("DICE-PAGES-404", "dice's published site links two pages that 404 (https://i574n.github.io/dice/lib/dice.spi.html and /dice/ui/dist), from its README, its index page and the org profile: scripts/publish.ps1 calls publish-tree without -Include, so the generated notebook (lib/dice.spi.ipynb from lib/build.ps1) is never published, and ui/build.ps1 writes the web UI to ui/dist, which .gitignore excludes, so the UI is never published either", Story, P1, D2, 90u32, Blocked, "", "dice,pages,ci,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_dice_pages_404 () = Planning ("DICE-PAGES-404", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_dice_pages_404_1 () = Note ("DICE-PAGES-404", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:01Z", "main", "main 11-06 11:2x found while checking the org profile's links (curl: dice/ 200, dice/lib/dice.spi.html 404, dice/ui/dist 404). Fix: publish.ps1 passes -Include '*.spi.html,*.spi.ipynb' -Exclude 'target,deps,_build,node_modules' as spiral's publish does, the notebook step also writes the .spi.html, and after publish-tree ui/dist is copied into dist/ui/dist. alphabet mirrors dice, so check it the same way. DoD: after the user's push, both URLs answer 200 and the UI loads. Proof: a codespace run of dice's workflow.ps1 + publish.ps1 counting the two paths in dist. Next step: write the publish.ps1 change and check whether lib/build.ps1 already emits the .spi.html.")
inl note_of_dice_pages_404_2 () = Note ("DICE-PAGES-404", 2u32, "2026-11-06T13:03Z", "main", "main 11-06 11:3x FIX IN THE TREE (dice, unstaged): scripts/publish.ps1 now passes -Include '*.spi.html','*.spi.ipynb' -Exclude 'target','deps','_build','node_modules' (spiral's publish shape), and after publish-tree copies ui/dist (trunk + rna output, gitignored) into dist/ui/dist. Notebook runs already write the .spi.html beside the .ipynb (only gate runs pass --no-html), so lib/dice.spi.html exists once lib/build.ps1 runs. Parse 0 errors. Proof running: codespace with dice main + this file, workflow.ps1, then a check that dist/lib/dice.spi.html, dist/lib/dice.spi.ipynb and dist/ui/dist/index.html are present. Next step: read that proof; alphabet's publish has the same no-Include call, so check whether alphabet links any generated page.")
inl note_of_dice_pages_404_3 () = Note ("DICE-PAGES-404", 3u32, "2026-11-06T13:17Z", "main", "main 11-06 12:1x README link audit (curl every https://i574n.github.io link in the 11 own READMEs + the org profile): non-200 were dice (3: lib/dice.spi.html, contract/dice_contract.spi.html, ui/dist, all covered by this item's publish fix), spiral 1 and i574n.github 1, both pages that are no longer generated. Fixed in place (unstaged): spiral README 'Spiral CLI notebook' (spiral.spi.html, 404) -> 'Spiral CLI source' (spiral.spi, 200); i574n.github README 'Full workflow output' (workflow.livemd.html, retired with .livemd) -> 'Workflow script' (scripts/workflow.ps1, 200); org profile polyglot math link -> spiral's math.spi.html (POLYGLOT-RETIRE). alphabet's README link answers 200.")
inl note_of_dice_pages_404_4 () = Note ("DICE-PAGES-404", 4u32, "2026-11-06T14:40Z", "main", "main 11-06 14:4x proof attempts so far are VOID (setup gaps, not dice): run 1, the codespace had bun but no bunx, so ui/build failed; run 2, bunx was linked but dice's Playwright webServer hard-codes ~/.bun/bin/bunx (CI's setup-bun location), so e2e timed out after 60 s before publish ran. Run 3 is running now with ~/.bun/bin/{bun,bunx} linked like CI, and publish.ps1 called directly after the workflow, so the dist check happens whatever e2e does. Run 2b (publish + NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS' contract cell) is also running for the contract notebook's result.")
inl note_of_dice_pages_404_5 () = Note ("DICE-PAGES-404", 5u32, "2026-11-06T16:12Z", "main", "main 11-06 16:1x PROVEN on a codespace (dice main + scripts/publish.ps1, lib/build.ps1, contract/build.ps1, contract/dice_contract.spi): init 0, lib build 0, publish 0 -> publish-tree copied 72 tracked + 3 regenerated files; dist/lib/dice.spi.html 137,252 B, dist/lib/dice.spi.ipynb 67,350 B, dist/lib/dice.spi.livemd 33,474 B, dist/ui/dist/index.html (14 UI files). The run-3 failure was MY bug, found by this proof: pwsh-invoked publish-tree got -Include 'a', 'b' as stray positional arguments (fiscal's 06:12 lesson); fixed to comma-joined strings like spiral's publish. The ui build's exit 1 is its Playwright e2e on the codespace (browser launch closed), after the UI is built. Blocked on the user's push of dice; then curl the 3 URLs for 200.")
