inl note_of_fiscal_cii_profiles_1_pin_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CII-PROFILES-1-PIN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:08Z", "fiscal", "DoD: init.ps1 fetches or copies both zips into deps/corpus/eu/factur-x pinned by sha256 (throws on change); a note lists the five profile XSD roots (MINIMUM, BASIC WL, BASIC, EN 16931, EXTENDED) and the example invoices per profile. NEXT: after the user request.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cii_profiles_1_pin_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CII-PROFILES-1-PIN", 2u32, "2026-11-10T02:45Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 22:5x DONE. proof: the user downloaded ZUGFeRD_2.5.2_EN.zip (FeRD, 29.7 MB, sha256 03C335F0B898A66A14D2548EE5DFE72504D0138A732C4E67E805866F45FC5EBF, 348 entries). fiscal scripts/init.ps1 (unstaged) gains a deps/corpus/eu/factur-x block that COPIES it from FISCAL_FACTURX_ZIP or ~/Downloads, throws on any sha256 change, and skips with a message where the zip is absent (CI), since the source is email-gated; placed locally with the pin verified (git-ignored). PROFILE XSD ROOTS (Factur-X 1.09.2): Schema/0_Factur-X_1.09.2_MINIMUM/Factur-X_1.09.2_MINIMUM.xsd, 1_..._BASICWL/Factur-X_1.09.2_BASICWL.xsd, 2_..._BASIC/Factur-X_1.09.2_BASIC.xsd, 3_..._EN16931/Factur-X_1.09.2_EN16931.xsd, 4_..._EXTENDED/Factur-X_1.09.2_EXTENDED.xsd, each with its own urn_un_unece type modules plus schematron (.sch) and xslt; the unrestricted base is Schema/5. CII D22B XSD/CrossIndustryInvoice_100pD22B.xsd (the D16B -> D22B move). EXAMPLES per profile (xml/pdf): MINIMUM 2/2, BASIC WL 2/2, BASIC 3/3, EN16931 25/26, EXTENDED 25/29, plus XRECHNUNG 4/8. One zip holds both schemas and examples, so the two-zip wording of the DoD collapses to one pin.")
