inl note_of_fiscal_cii_profiles_3_lattice_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CII-PROFILES-3-LATTICE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T02:51Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 23:1x DoD ALREADY MET BY LIVE CODE (fiscal src/profiles.spi C0390CA5): phantom levels minimum < basic_wl < basic < en16931 < extended_ctc_fr < extended; profile p GADT; step a b (one constructor per adjacent pair, upward only); recursive path a b with Here / Then (\\? b. step a b * path b c), so a path is evidence of an upward chain; widen takes the path as evidence. Tests: a_basic_invoice_widens_to_en16931_and_extended (positive, BASIC -> EN16931 and -> EXTENDED through CTC-FR), a_path_never_narrows and a_widened_invoice_has_its_target_profile (both fail 'Unification failure' as required). The real remaining gap is elsewhere: profiled p = profile p * string, so a BASIC-indexed value can hold any XML text. Once step 2's five families exist, profiled p should carry the generated typed document of profile p (a prototype from the phantom level to its generated root type), which is the natural scope of -4-EXAMPLES. Also open: profile_urn has None for EXTENDED-CTC-FR; read its guideline URN from the 1.09.2 spec in the package (Documentation/) rather than guessing. NEXT STEP: confirm the three tests green at the next fiscal gate, then close this step.")
