inl kit_standards_test_targets_roots () = Task ("KIT-STANDARDS-TEST-TARGETS-ROOTS", "kit standards TestTargets stops flagging modules that run through a package root or a static prelude (79 false positives on spiral lib)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,standards,cpu-light,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_standards_test_targets_roots () = Planning ("KIT-STANDARDS-TEST-TARGETS-ROOTS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_standards_test_targets_roots_1 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-TEST-TARGETS-ROOTS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:10Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 09:1x kit, filed from main 09:0x: kit standards rule TestTargets (a test block in a module without a notebook header never runs) flags 79 spiral lib modules that DO run: physics.spi 43/43 via run_notebook.ps1 --path lib/spiral/physics.spi, file_system.spi 23/0 in the 11-04 scheduled cells-gate. Lib modules run with the lib package as context (lib/spiral/build.ps1 notebook list, ci_gate -Roots lib/spiral) and need no ///- --package line. DoD: the rule counts a module as running when its package is a runner root (lib/spiral, a ci_gate -Roots entry) or it carries a :# <module> static = prelude; real orphans still warn; kit standards C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral reports 0 for physics.spi and file_system.spi and keeps a fixture orphan red. MILESTONES: rule change + fixture test 45 m; recount on lib 10 m; install 5 m. NEXT STEP: read the TestTargets probe in kit_standards and add the root and prelude cases. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a closed union test_reach (NotebookHeader | PackageRoot | StaticPrelude | Orphan) decides the verdict, never a boolean chain.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_test_targets_roots_2 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-TEST-TARGETS-ROOTS", 2u32, "2026-11-06T18:25Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 14:2x kit: FIX BUILT (unstaged, rides TRAIN35): in kit_standards/rules.spi the scan treats a :# <module> static = prelude line as a notebook header, so lib modules like physics.spi (which open with :# physics static = and run with the lib package as context) stop being flagged, while a module with tests and neither header nor prelude still is. New test case lib_style in a_test_block_needs_a_notebook_header_to_run; two pre-existing over-width lines in the file wrapped so the precheck stays clean. PROOF node probe job-1793982955768: rules.spi 8/8. Chosen over the package-root idea because the prelude is a property of the file itself, so no runner configuration has to be read. DoD left: after install, kit standards C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral reports 0 test-targets findings for physics.spi and file_system.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_test_targets_roots_3 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-TEST-TARGETS-ROOTS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "proof: 11-09 20:1x local rig, installed kit standards C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral (150 files, 5.6 s): physics.spi 0 findings; file_system.spi has no ''never runs'' finding (its one test-targets row is the newer target-placement rule: a ///> target not directly above a test block); the 79 false positives of 11-06 are gone. Real orphans still warn, as the DoD asks: 7 modules carry tests with neither a notebook header nor a :# <module> static = prelude: float_native.spi:56, layers.spi:177, lustre.spi:135, metrics.spi:71, nameof_heal.spi:265, testing.spi:57, xml.spi:132. Other test-targets rows on lib (11) are the placement rule (9 targets not directly above a test, 2 above a static block), outside this item. DoD met.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_test_targets_roots_4 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-TEST-TARGETS-ROOTS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:11Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:4x rig CORRECTION of note 3: its \"physics.spi 0 findings\" was measured on a file that is NOT in the live tree: lib/spiral/physics.spi is deleted in another lane's unstaged work (moved to apps/plot/physics.spi), so that line proved nothing. proof (replaces it): over the lib files that exist, 102 carry test blocks AND a :# <module> static = prelude (the case the fix covers), and 0 of them are flagged \"never runs\"; every one of the 7 flagged files (float_native, layers, lustre, metrics, nameof_heal, testing, xml) has no prelude, so the rule still catches real orphans; file_system.spi (tests + prelude) is not flagged. The DoD stands on this measurement.")
inl run_target_args_postable () = Task ("RUN-TARGET-ARGS-POSTABLE", "GRANULAR cell budget measures a flat run_target_args \\| dispatch per arm, as it does flat backend_switch (BACKEND-SWITCH-POSTABLE)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 85u32, Active, "", "team:rig,kit,cells,granular,postability,lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_run_target_args_postable () = Planning ("RUN-TARGET-ARGS-POSTABLE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_run_target_args_postable_1 () = Note ("RUN-TARGET-ARGS-POSTABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-06T13:18Z", "x", "2026-11-06 09:18 x: filed with the measurement in BACKEND-SWITCH-POSTABLE n4. lib env.spi with every arm moved to a one-line helper call (draft 11B45711ED8D) still weighs 744/510/461 for get/set/remove_environment_variable, because the counter weighs the run_target_args dispatch whole. DoD: (1) a flat run_target_args dispatch weighs its heaviest arm; (2) a CellBudgetRuled test row with a 10-target one-line dispatch is under budget; (3) the europa ~/cell-budget snapshot is refreshed. Then x re-measures and lands env (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS).")
inl note_of_run_target_args_postable_2 () = Note ("RUN-TARGET-ARGS-POSTABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:53Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "proof: (microblog, spiral tree unstaged). Cells CellBudgetRuled rule 1 now also covers a body that is exactly one run_target_args dispatch: head line `run_target_args (...) \\|` followed by arms that are each `| Target => \\ params => <call>` on one line of at most 120 chars, with no ?=, \" ? \", ?>, := or a second lambda in the call. It weighs head line + heaviest arm, mirroring flat_switch; any multi-line or logic arm still counts the whole body. Tests (cell_budget_ruled_test.exs): a 10-target one-line dispatch weighs head + heaviest arm and stays under 272 (DoD 2); the counter-example with a multi-line or logic arm counts in full. Result 21/21 pass. CONTROL: the same tests against HEAD cell_budget_ruled.ex fail exactly the new positive test (20/21), so the test discriminates; the file was restored and hash-checked. DoD 3 is left: refresh the europa ~/cell-budget snapshot (GRANULAR counter copy), owner rig/kit. Then x re-measures lib env.spi (get/set/remove_environment_variable were 744/510/461) and lands it under POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS.")
inl note_of_run_target_args_postable_3 () = Note ("RUN-TARGET-ARGS-POSTABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:54Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "NEXT STEP: rig/kit refreshes the europa ~/cell-budget GRANULAR snapshot from this Cells (DoD 3), then x re-measures lib env.spi. TYPEFEATURES: none new; the rule is a string-shape predicate over the cell body, like flat_switch.")
inl note_of_run_target_args_postable_4 () = Note ("RUN-TARGET-ARGS-POSTABLE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T11:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:4x microblog took this (rig team item) and did rule 1 in Cells CellBudgetRuled: a flat run_target_args dispatch counts as head line + heaviest arm, mirroring flat backend_switch; arms must be one-line | T => \\ a => call (<= 120 chars, no logic), else the whole body counts; 21/21 tests incl. a 10-target dispatch under 272 and a counter-example; HEAD's counter fails exactly the new test (spiral tree, unstaged). LEFT for rig (GRANULAR counter owner): DoD 3, refresh the europa ~/cell-budget snapshot, then re-measure lib env.spi get/set/remove_environment_variable (744/510/461). After TRAIN43.")
