inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_6_emit_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6-EMIT", 5u32, "2026-11-08T21:33Z", "fiscal", "11-08 UNBLOCKED: this item's own draft (FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6-EMIT v1, xsd_emit 673807F2) landed today through lib_land_window, closed green (lib digest 0FB176F529463A4B, type probe 37 tests typed). Its ORDER condition (field-meta and twin drafts first) is met, because they were the same land. NEXT STEP: count the landed xsd_emit's code overages with the europa GRANULAR counter (budget 272); 0 means Done, anything else is the remaining list.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_6_emit_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6-EMIT", 6u32, "2026-11-09T05:14Z", "fiscal", "11-09 REAL BASELINE (mix spiral.cell_budget --check, current counter, live xsd_emit 0B24BF7D after the pack63c respell): 278 over-budget definitions = 241 CODE + 37 tests (plus 17 autolink findings), not the '39 code overages' this item was opened with. The counter and the respell changed the picture. Worst code definitions by weight: carriers (:592, 1005), several ':&' mutual groups at :3215/:3071/:3241/:3266/:3155/:3046/:3179 (739-893 each), complement_case_dispatch (:4218, 804), emit_record_walk_texts (:2904, 796), builtin_kinds (:572, 745), dereferenced_in (:1663, 709). The 11-08 R5-style split (extract helpers, keep the layout) applies. Blocker: FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-0-LIB-STAGED's xsd_emit draft (7A6892B9) is in flight on the same file; two drafts on one lib file collide. NEXT STEP: once step 0 lands, split in batches of ~10 definitions per lib land (largest first, the :& groups need care: a blank line before :& splits the group, per memory), each batch type-probed and landed through lib_land_window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_6_emit_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6-EMIT", 7u32, "2026-11-09T07:01Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 MEASURED on the step-0 draft xsd_emit 7A6892B9 (mix spiral.cell_budget on ganymede, budget 272): 278 over-budget = 241 CODE + 37 tests, identical to the 05:14 live baseline, so step 0 adds no overage. Code by weight: 273-300: 50, 301-350: 84, 351-450: 56, 451-600: 26, over 600: 25 (the :& mutual groups, carriers, builtin_kinds, complement_case_dispatch, emit_record_walk_texts, dereferenced_in). Real size about 600 m, not 120 m, so SPLIT into 3 slices of at most 240 m: 6A (the 134 definitions at 273-350, one or two helper extractions each), 6B (the 56 at 351-450), 6C (the 51 above 450, restructuring incl. the mutual groups). ORDER: after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ lands (step 0 lands first, then step 3), because each slice is a draft on xsd_emit and stacking a third draft on one file is the C4 degradation shape. Row list (weight, line, kind, head) is regenerable from the counter; no stored baseline.")
inl note_of_fiscal_lib_granular_6_emit_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-LIB-GRANULAR-6-EMIT", 8u32, "2026-11-10T10:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal groom 11-10 07:0x: the ordering rule in the last note ('after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ lands; one xsd_emit draft at a time') is a real dependency, so it moves from prose to a wait row (item:XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-3-READ). 6A's batch-6 re-gate keeps its own TRAIN43 wait. Next step: when 3-READ lands, draft 6B (the 56 cells at 351-450) as the single xsd_emit draft.")
inl c_operator_function_names () = Task ("C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES", "codegenC: a non-inlined operator definition (lib file_system's (</>)) is emitted as a C function literally named `</>2`, so any C program that calls it fails to compile (\"expected identifier or '(' before '<'\"); emit a sanitized name (op_lt_slash_gt2) the way other backends mangle", Story, P2, D2, 60u32, Active, "", "compiler,team:compiler,codegen,c,bug,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_operator_function_names () = Planning ("C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_c_operator_function_names_1 () = Note ("C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:04Z", "tibia", "11-06 10:04 tibia: found while gating LIB-FILE-SYSTEM-TEST-DEBRIS. Repro (box, installed compiler): package with lib, main.spi = `:< file_system` then `:= main () : i32 = sm'::length (get_temp_path () </> \"probe.bin\")` (after the C arm of get_temp_path from that draft); --backend C emits `String * </>2(String * v0, String * v1){` at main.c:135, and gcc rejects it. Rust and Zig rows using </> passed in the same gate. The lib draft works around it with ++# \"/name\" in its C tests. DoD: a sample with an operator definition called from main compiles and runs on C; a regen byte-compare shows only names that were invalid change. NEXT: find the C function-name emitter and reuse the mangling other backends use for symbol characters. TypeFeatures: codegen-only.")
inl note_of_c_operator_function_names_2 () = Note ("C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:26Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:3x compiler: DRAFTED drafts\\spiral\\C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES\\1-c-identifier-names.kitdo (3 replacements; applies both on the live core and on the pack93 chain). codegenC gets cIdent: a name that is already a C identifier passes through unchanged, so only names that never compiled can change; a pure operator becomes op_<tokens> (</> -> op_lt_slash_gt, so the method is op_lt_slash_gt<tag>); a mixed name replaces each bad char with _<token> (f -> f_prime). Applied where codegenC builds MethodRecC and ClosureRecC names, so the forward declaration, definition, loop table and call sites all agree. Sample samples/c_operator_function_name (:~ (</>) a b = a*10 + b on run-time x=4, y=2; expect exit 66; registered under Fsharp,C,Rust,Pascal). pack94 = pack93 + this (core f6756924), probe queued on ganymede after pack93: C codegen + gcc + run under pack93 (expect the gcc error on </>) and pack94 (expect exit 66). Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack94/g.log at \"p94 done\"; then a C regen byte-compare over the suite to confirm only invalid names changed.")
inl note_of_c_operator_function_names_3 () = Note ("C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES", 3u32, "2026-11-11T00:26Z", "compiler", "DoD: a sample with a non-inlined operator definition called from main compiles and runs on C (gcc), and a C regen byte-compare over every sample shows only names that were invalid C identifiers change. TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_c_operator_function_names_4 () = Note ("C-OPERATOR-FUNCTION-NAMES", 4u32, "2026-11-11T01:10Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:1x compiler: pack94 run 1 FAILED TO BUILD (FS0010 \"Unexpected quote symbol in pattern matching\" at the new token match): the kitdo text collapsed the F# char literal backslash-backslash into a single backslash, so the character pattern for the backslash became invalid. The repro side worked: pack93 emits \"int32_t </>0(int32_t v0, int32_t v1)\" and gcc rejects it (\"expected identifier or ( before < token\"). Program rewritten to match backslash and apostrophe by character code (int c: 92, 39), so no escaped literals remain; reapplied on pack93 (core 51615c42) and re-queued on ganymede after the chains last job (log g.log, first attempt kept as g1.log). Next step: read pack94/g.log at \"p94b done\" (want exit 66 from op_lt_slash_gt).")
