inl link_auto_export () = Task ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", "link: units export every top-level monomorphic definition a consumer calls, curried functions included, without a hand-written unit.spi export list or single-argument wrappers; today each linked call needs export '<name>' <definition> on a one-argument definition, so splitting an existing package into units means wrapping every cross-unit function and rewriting its call sites", Story, P1, D5, 95u32, Active, "AUTO-EXPORT-1-MONOMORPHIC,AUTO-EXPORT-2-CURRIED", "compiler,linked-units,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_link_auto_export () = Planning ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_link_auto_export_1 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 1u32, "2026-11-06T14:19Z", "main", "main 11-06 13:3x motivating case: regex's bench.rs is 4777 lines (the 1000-line gate is only a warning there) because bench compiles the whole engine: 150 functions, 150 distinct names, so nothing is duplicated and only linking can split it. regex's syntax module alone has about 55 definitions used across 15 modules plus bench (charset 161 lines, syntax 371, nullable 184). Hand-written wrappers for every unit boundary would cost more than the split itself. DoD: a package listed under link: exposes its called top-level definitions to the consumer's link calls automatically (curried arity handled), proven on regex's rx_syntax split with bench.rs shrinking by that unit's share. Next step: compiler judges feasibility against today's export mechanism (unit graph + export table).")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_2 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 2u32, "2026-11-06T14:21Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:2x compiler FEASIBILITY (read at the pack53c core): (1) FEASIBLE: auto-export of top-level definitions whose inferred type has no forall and whose argument and result have a link-boundary form. The unit build synthesizes export \"<unit>_<name>\" <name> per definition, opt-in per unit via a manifest flag; consumers match by definition identity already (definitionSources -> ExternCalls.lookup), so no consumer change. (2) NEW WORK, curried definitions: today inlined with the \"curried\" warning (peval ExternCalls fallthrough); needs an uncurried tuple export plus consumer-side collection of a fully applied chain. (3) IMPOSSIBLE as specified, polymorphic definitions: a unit cannot know at its own build which instantiations consumers need without consumer-to-unit feedback, which is a cycle in the post-order unit build. They stay inlined unless annotated monomorphic or exported at chosen types. NEXT STEP (offered to main): census of regex syntax.spi + 14 modules' cross-module definitions by class 1/2/3 (inference only). DoD for the feature, if taken: opt-in flag; class-1 definitions link with no export lines; a linked sample with 3 auto-exported functions and Calls checks; unit.json unchanged for units without the flag.")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_3 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 3u32, "2026-11-06T14:27Z", "compiler", "11-06 10:3x compiler: CENSUS (main's decision rule 10:2x). Method: build regex bench to Rust on the installed pack53c with SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT (prepass def/use rows, 32,632 rows; --check alone skips prepass), keep uses whose use file and definition file are both in regex src/bench and DIFFER, and classify each used definition by its head text (scratchpad link-census.ps1; per-definition table link-census.tsv). Result: 115 cross-file definitions, 418 uses. Types (union/nominal constructors, type aliases): 23 defs, 104 uses (cross by the unit graph already, not calls). Calls: 314 uses. CLASS 1 (monomorphic, one argument group or ()): 50 defs, 174 uses = 55%. CLASS 2 (monomorphic, curried): 40 defs, 137 uses. CLASS 1+2 = 311 = 99%. CLASS 3 (polymorphic): 2 defs, 3 uses, both phantom-index helpers (certificate.automaton_dfa \\* p., semantics.verdict_of_oracle \\* k.), annotatable or exportable at their few instantiations. CAVEATS: (a) this counts cross-FILE calls, a superset of the cross-UNIT calls for the planned rx_syntax | rx_derivative | rx_automata | rx_certificate split; the module-to-unit map applies to link-census.tsv directly; (b) classes come from head text, not inferred types; (c) boundary form is not checked per signature (0 function-typed parameters seen). VERDICT under the rule: class 1 alone = 55% < 80%, class 1+2 = 99% >= 80%. So regex splits on auto-export once the uncurried-export pack exists. Steps to file as children: AUTO-EXPORT-1 (manifest flag + class-1 export synthesis) and AUTO-EXPORT-2 (uncurried export + consumer chain collection).")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_4 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 4u32, "2026-11-06T21:09Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:1x compiler: steps 1 and 2 are DONE and shipped (AUTO-EXPORT-1 + AUTO-EXPORT-2 on pack57, all three hosts). FIELD PROOF started on a scratch copy of regex (scratchpad regex-split.ps1, nothing written to the regex repo): unit rx_syntax = charset + syntax + nullable with auto-export: monomorphic, src = the other 13 modules, bench links rx_syntax. Base bench.rs on today's core: 6,934 lines. FINDING: the unit exported NOTHING (trace: 'unit rx_syntax own 1 [main:fun] candidates []'), although it synthesized 5 curried wrappers in its modules: AUTO-EXPORT-1 folds 'own' definitions from the ENTRY file's prepass stream only, so a multi-module unit exports only its entry module (fine for every one-module sample, useless for a real split). With no exports, no unit graph is written, so bench failed 'has no unit graph'. FIX drafted as AUTO-EXPORT-3-MULTI-MODULE\\1-every-module-of-the-unit.kitdo (1 replacement, dry run ok on pack58c's source): before LinkAutoExport.main, fold in the definitions of every other file of the entry's package from prepass.files.uids_file (fulfilled streams only, so it can never block; the entry's own names win a clash). Candidate ae3a building; next step: rerun the regex proof on it and read bench.rs's line count.")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_5 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 5u32, "2026-11-06T21:10Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:1x compiler: typefeatureset plan: exports stay monomorphic by rule (no forall crosses the boundary); the unit's export set is a Map from definition name to its prepass E, and the curried arity is carried by the synthesized tuple wrapper's own type, so no new untyped keys are introduced.")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_6 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 6u32, "2026-11-06T21:33Z", "compiler", "11-06 17:3x compiler: FIELD PROOF on candidate ae3a (core 8A98D347D8FD1C9C = pack58c tree + AUTO-EXPORT-3-MULTI-MODULE; the AE3 program applies the same on pack57's tree, re-dry-run before its pack) over a scratch copy of regex (scratchpad regex-split.ps1; the regex repo is untouched): unit rx_syntax (charset + syntax + nullable, auto-export: monomorphic) now exports from ALL its modules (trace: own 171, 5 curried wrappers synthesized), unit rx_syntax.rs = 3,908 lines; bench.rs drops 6,934 -> 5,965 lines (-969, -14%) with 71 rx_syntax:: cross-unit calls; both crates build with cargo 1.99.0 (bench depends on regex 1 + the rx_syntax path crate). Running both benches to completion now (idle priority, box; the node is relaunching kit's train) to compare exit codes and certification facts. Remaining for DoD: that behavior check, then AE3 in a pack gated with smoke + linked + the lib type probe.")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_7 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 7u32, "2026-11-06T22:10Z", "compiler", "11-06 18:1x compiler: the behavior check of the split regex bench is PENDING, not run: the base bench did not finish within 30 min at idle priority on the saturated box (killed at 1800 s; it runs 6 workloads x 15 rounds x 400 words x 25 passes), so the box cannot give that comparison today. Both cargo builds exist in the compiler scratchpad (regex-cargo\\target-*). next step: run base and split benches on the node after kit's TRAIN35 (~19:50) or tomorrow and compare exit codes (failure counts) and the certification facts; then this item closes with AUTO-EXPORT-3 shipped.")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_8 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 8u32, "2026-11-06T23:22Z", "compiler", "11-06 19:2x compiler: BEHAVIOR CHECK PASSED for the regex split (box, Normal priority, both benches to completion): base bench (single package, 6,934-line bench.rs) exit 0 in 846 s, split bench (rx_syntax unit + bench linking it, 5,965-line bench.rs, built on candidate ae3a) exit 0 in 873 s; 0 failures on both, and all 17 deterministic facts are identical across the 6 workloads (states built / minimal: 2/2, 4/2, 16/16, 65/65, 16/16, 256/256; certified pairs 1, 1, 120, 2080, 120; agree on 40 words everywhere). Only the timing-table rows differ (ratios and VOID noise markers, run to run). So the split shrinks bench.rs by 14% with unchanged results. Remaining for Done: AUTO-EXPORT-3 shipped (pack59, after kit's TRAIN36), then main splits the real regex (REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX).")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_9 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 9u32, "2026-11-07T11:44Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: every compiler step is shipped (pack59d SHIPPED (main 07:4x): box core AAD93F1E9CB86319 (07:32), node the same in place 07:41 (fresh launch exit 0), europa Linux build from 04123021555F0DE9 / 9452B1A2EBD761EB (core 9eddee63e40fd6ac, launch exit 0); main's sized_array probe passes under it.). Auto-export now covers monomorphic one-group definitions (AE1), curried ones through a tuple wrapper (AE2), every module of a unit's package (AE3), and skips polymorphic/wildcard/unannotated shapes safely (AE2B); the scratch regex proof shrank bench.rs 6,934 -> 5,965 lines with identical results. Remaining for Done: main's real split of regex (REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX, resumed on main's side).")
inl note_of_link_auto_export_10 () = Note ("LINK-AUTO-EXPORT", 10u32, "2026-11-09T06:24Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:5x compiler: compiler side unchanged-complete (AE1/AE2/AE2B/AE3, shipped since pack59d, carried in pack63c/pack64). The one remaining DoD step, the REAL regex split, is owned by org (REGEX-CRATE-UNITS); compiler answered its design question 11-09 01:4x: Option B, a regex_model unit inside regex/src with auto-export: monomorphic AND thin annotated monomorphic wrappers around the regex_* lib calls bench/engine use (auto-export only considers the unit package's OWN modules, never opened lib modules), listed after lib under packages:; Option A (lib as a linked unit) is not available today. Close when org posts the real split's bench.rs line count with identical results.")
