inl note_of_kit_reformat_after_pack55_1 () = Note ("KIT-REFORMAT-AFTER-PACK55", 1u32, "2026-11-06T15:40Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-06 11:3x kit, from compiler owner notice (pack55d on box and node: spiral format joins a then / ?> line onto its condition line when the join fits 120, FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN): kit has about 873 lines starting with ?>, so layout and style checks report would change on files nobody edited. RULE until the user pushes spiral with this core: do NOT reformat kit with the new formatter (CI formats with the committed compiler and would go red); treat then-join diffs as expected noise in style checks and train logs. DoD: after that push, one reformat pass over kit src with the pushed formatter, regen, a train, and the CI run green on both OSes. MILESTONES: reformat pass + regen 30 m; train 15 m attended; CI check 15 m. NEXT STEP: wait for the spiral push carrying pack55d core, then run the pass. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: none (layout only); the pass must leave the census unchanged, checked by kit standards --ratchet before and after.")
inl kit_unstaged_retention () = Task ("KIT-UNSTAGED-RETENTION", "kit-unstaged-backup store grows unbounded - add a retention rule", Story, P2, D2, 80u32, Active, "", "kit,backup,retention,wipe,resilience,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_unstaged_retention () = Planning ("KIT-UNSTAGED-RETENTION", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_unstaged_retention_1 () = Note ("KIT-UNSTAGED-RETENTION", 1u32, "2026-11-06T15:55Z", "resilience-614162e5", "kit\\backups\\unstaged grows unbounded: 82MB on 11-03 -> 327MB / 42 timestamped snapshots on 11-06 (every 2h, never pruned). The store rides the off-box mirror; unbounded growth bloats both the store and (now) the critical-mirror WIP inclusion over time. ASK (kit): add a retention rule to kit-unstaged-backup - keep the newest N (e.g. 12 = 24h) plus one-per-day for M days, prune the rest; same pattern as other kit stores. Found during the 11-06 hot-lane-stall incident (MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST) when routing WIP to the critical lane. resilience-614162e5.")
inl note_of_kit_unstaged_retention_2 () = Note ("KIT-UNSTAGED-RETENTION", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:48Z", "resilience", "IMPLEMENTED + PROVEN + RAN (11-07 13:3x). unstaged-backup.ps1 gains age-tiered retention: keep all <=3d, 1/day <=21d, 1/week <=90d, + a floor of newest 12 + always newest&oldest. Gated behind -Prune (DryRun lists only); the scheduled task does NOT pass -Prune, so default stays never-delete until proven. Dry-run on the real store: 55 runs -> keep 43 / prune 12, newest+oldest kept, no day loses coverage (only redundant intraday dupes >3d pruned). Ran -Prune once: 56->44 runs, pruned 12 (102.9MB), 536->460MB. DoD: store bounded, no day gap, wipe-depth history kept. REMAINING (user-batch): add -Prune to the kit-unstaged-backup task args in register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 (SCHEDULED-TASKS-CONFIRM) to make it continuous.")
inl note_of_kit_unstaged_retention_3 () = Note ("KIT-UNSTAGED-RETENTION", 3u32, "2026-11-07T17:49Z", "resilience", "NEXT STEP: add -Prune to the kit-unstaged-backup task Arguments in register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 (user-batch, SCHEDULED-TASKS-CONFIRM) so retention runs every 2h. DoD: the store stays bounded (age-tiered keep-set) with no day-gap and wipe-depth history, deletion gated behind -Prune and dry-run-proven before first use. TYPEFEATURES: keep-set as a HashSet[string] of run names; retention tiers (all/daily/weekly + floor + newest/oldest) as explicit age predicates, so a run is kept iff it matches a named tier.")
inl note_of_kit_unstaged_retention_4 () = Note ("KIT-UNSTAGED-RETENTION", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 21:3x rig, MEASURED for the pending user decision: the store is back to 1,244 MB in 69 runs (oldest 10-29, newest 11-09 14:09), from 460 MB right after the one-off -Prune on 11-07: about 390 MB per day while the scheduled task runs without -Prune, and today's large unstaged volume across lanes will raise it. The retention code is proven (dry-run and one real prune on 11-07); only the scheduled-task argument change remains, which is the user's batch call (SCHEDULED-TASKS-CONFIRM). Parked as a user wait.")
