inl kit_codespace_run () = Task ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", "kit codespace run: one verb that creates a codespace, installs the pinned toolchain, overlays the box delta, runs marker-polled steps, fetches logs and always deletes, with per-run core-hour usage rows", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,codespaces,ci,compute,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_codespace_run () = Planning ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_codespace_run_1 () = Note ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", 1u32, "2026-11-06T20:01Z", "main", "Filed by main 11-06 16:0x from CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS (its next step). SPEC, from 9 proven scratch drivers now in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS (plots-cs, fork-cs, blog-cs, dice-cs4, ci-rehearsal-*; each is drive.ps1 + remote.sh). `kit codespace run <repo> --steps <file> [--machine standardLinux32gb] [--overlay <dir|tgz>] [--fetch <glob>] [--step-max-min 150]` does: (1) gh codespace create -R <repo> -b main -m <machine> --idle-timeout 120m --retention-period 1h, refusing on a non-name result; (2) a TOOLS step from one pinned table (pwsh 7.6.9, OTP 29.1.2, elixir 1.20.5, gleam 1.19.2, rebar3 3.28.0, zig 0.17.0, bun 1.4.4 incl. ~/.bun/bin/{bun,bunx}, rust nightly-2026-10-18 + rust-src) that ends with a per-tool ok/MISSING line and ABORTS on any MISSING the steps need; (3) shallow clone plus overlay of the box's unstaged delta, printing git status --porcelain; (4) each step launched with nohup and polled for its DONE marker every 60 s up to step-max-min, its full .out printed; (5) fetch logs/artifacts; (6) delete in a finally, then verify that 'gh codespace list' no longer shows it. It records wall seconds x cores per run into a usage row (quota 120 core-hours a month). Lessons the verb must encode: pwsh-invoked scripts take comma-joined strings, not arrays; the CI layout needs ~/.bun/bin; a stuck driver must still delete in finally; a run's verdict must name the targets it exercised (zig etc.), so a stale-ordered '43/43' can't stand in for a later change.")
inl note_of_kit_codespace_run_2 () = Note ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", 2u32, "2026-11-06T20:01Z", "main", "DoD: kit codespace run reproduces one of the scratch drivers end to end (create, tools, overlay, steps, fetch, delete verified gone) with a usage row written. Next step: kit reads the dice-cs4 and plots-cs pairs and writes the verb. TypeFeatures: a step outcome union (Done of marker | TimedOut | Missing of tool) and a typed usage row, not strings.")
inl note_of_kit_codespace_run_3 () = Note ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", 3u32, "2026-11-08T19:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 16:0x rig: RE-RANKED UP (user 11-08 asked whether codespaces created on demand then deleted already exist as rig work; two lanes hand-rolled one this week: org3 for the nodebench sweep, microblog nearly for CELLS-BENCH-CODESPACE). Slot: right after TRAIN42 content (R3b, RIG-LANES-GENERIC slice 1, RIG-UNITS-U1), BEFORE RIG-PACK-SHIP (pack63 waits on the fleet respell and the user push anyway, so pack shipping has slack). Inputs: the 9 proven drivers in LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS plus microblog's CELLS-BENCH-CODESPACE driver on the dice-cs4 pair as the 10th reference; shared memory codespace-on-demand-pattern. Until the verb lands, lanes reuse the drafts drivers rather than writing new ones. NEXT STEP: after TRAIN42 launches, the verb skeleton (create, pinned tools with the MISSING abort, overlay, marker-polled steps, fetch, always delete, core-hour rows).")
inl note_of_kit_codespace_run_4 () = Note ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", 4u32, "2026-11-09T05:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 02:3x rig, what the comet round (11-08 19:5x -> 11-09 00:4x) taught the verb, as requirements (the verb itself is not written yet): (1) TRANSPORT: --on through gh's ssh proxy needs a connect timeout of 60-90 s (gh answers in 12-28 s even when the codespace is awake); per-machine jobs/machines/<alias>.connect landed in the tree for TRAIN42 (comet = 90), and only Windows OpenSSH works (git-bash ssh mangles the gh.exe ProxyCommand). (2) PERSISTENCE: a restart wipes /tmp but keeps $HOME, so the kit binary, gitRoot and stage live under /home/codespace/remote/... (moved tonight; registry and comet.bin updated). (3) IDLE COST: an idle stop that counts only kit jobs killed compiler's detached job; the stop rule must count load >= 0.5 or an unreadable load as busy, and only probe when gh already reports Available (any ssh wakes it). (4) TEARDOWN: a one-shot scheduled delete (comet-auto-delete 01:30) plus an every-5-min idle stop proved workable; the verb must own both and log core-hours per run (org3 tracked ~34 of 120 free left). (5) SETUP: kit Linux binary from ganymede (stripped, glibc 2.39 compatible with Ubuntu 24.04), pwsh tarball into $HOME. These five become the verb's steps; the step outcome union in the DoD gains Unreachable (connect timeout) and Wiped (missing path after restart). Next step unchanged: write the verb from the dice-cs4 and plots-cs drivers plus these five.")
inl note_of_kit_codespace_run_5 () = Note ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", 5u32, "2026-11-09T05:39Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:4x rig, lesson (6) from the live teardown: the 01:30 auto-delete watchdog MISFIRED. In the scheduled-task context its first gh codespace list took 2.5 min and returned nothing, so the script logged already gone and skipped the delete while comet stayed Available (its own final list showed it). Caught at 01:35, deleted by hand at ~01:37 (comet idle, load 0.13); every layer verified gone (gh list [], comet.bin, registry entry, ssh Include, both tasks; comet.connect and comet.config archived to LOCALAPPDATA kit archive comet-teardown-20261109). RULE for the verb: a teardown treats an empty or failed list as UNKNOWN, retries, and only reports gone after a successful list that lacks the name; then it verifies each layer, as teardown-sweeps-every-layer says.")
inl note_of_kit_codespace_run_6 () = Note ("KIT-CODESPACE-RUN", 6u32, "2026-11-09T11:37Z", "tibia", "11-09 07:4x tibia (STAR-UNBLOCK contribution, reference driver #10 for this verb): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS\\tibia-cs\\ (drive.ps1 + remote.sh). New in it, each one a requirement for the verb: (1) EXACT-TREE mode: fetch the pushed HEAD sha into `git init` WITH `git remote add origin <url>` first (a bare fetch-by-URL leaves no origin, and repo init scripts then clone github.com//X), overlay a working-tree tar of `git ls-files -m -o --exclude-standard`, and pin deps/The-Spiral-Language to the box commit; (2) STALE-PIN guard: abort exit 64 when the pinned sha differs from the box HEAD or any overlaid file is newer than its delta tar; (3) per-run evidence: core DLL sha256 plus CORE PACKAGE MISSING detection plus the full layout diff for any \"would change\" file; (4) machine default basicLinux32gb (2 cores; free quota about 34 core-h); (5) a delete-then-verify `gh codespace list` in finally. Traps found tonight: detached nohup work dies on the idle stop; oomd SIGTERMs (rc 143) builds over ~6 GB on 8 GB; git-bash cannot use the gh.exe ProxyCommand (use Windows OpenSSH, ConnectTimeout 60); ziglang.org timed out (pull toolchains from oort's keyless bundle instead).")
