inl type_arith_3b_unify_fold () = Task ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", "type arith step 3b: compiler change: when unify compares a reserved type_arith op whose operands are still unresolved metavars against a literal (an annotation pushed into an application before its arguments bind), DEFER that comparison and re-run it after the definition is inferred, instead of failing; the fold itself already handles resolved operands", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD", "compiler,team:compiler,tibia,team:tibia,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_type_arith_3b_unify_fold () = Planning ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", Minutes 120u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_type_arith_3b_unify_fold_1 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", 1u32, "2026-11-06T20:46Z", "tibia", "11-06 16:5x tibia: split from TYPE-ARITH-5-RESHAPE after probe 3. 11-06 16:5x tibia: PROBE 3 on the BOX with pack58c (single-flight core 1524D5D56E6A11D5, sourceSha ef757b710be39cfa = compiler's reviewed candidate; drafts store drafts\\spiral\\LIB-TYPE-SHAPES\\probe3, LIB-TYPE-SHAPES probe 2 with resized removed). (1) SPELLED computed dims FOLD: q0 : sized (type_arith::mult 2 3) i32 used as sized 6 i32 compiles and runs (exit 678 = count 6 x 100 + physical 6 x 10 + total 18, as predicted). (2) INSTANTIATED arithmetic does NOT fold: u : sized 5 i32 = merged v w, with merged : sized a el -> sized b el -> sized (type_arith::add a b) el and v : sized 2, w : sized 3, fails with \"Unification failure. Got sized (add 2i32 3i32) i32, Expected sized 5i32 i32\". The negative (sized 6) fails with the same shape, as it should. Cause: the fold runs in visit_t over written types; add a b only becomes all-literal after a and b are substituted during unification, and unify compares the unnormalized TyApply against TyLit. So shape-changing functions still need probe 2's resized relabel, which means reshape is NOT typed end to end yet. DoD: a kitdo program in drafts\\spiral\\TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD reusing TypeArithReserved's ops table and fold, called where unify compares a TyApply of a reserved op (after substitution), same range and zero-divisor rules as step 3; probe3 positive exits 585 without resized and the negative stays a type error; suite compare with 0 residual cells; then a compiler pack. NEXT: find the unify site that compares TyApply against TyLit. TypeFeatures: the fold stays keyed on GlobalIds from the reserved module, no name matching.")
inl note_of_type_arith_3b_unify_fold_2 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", 2u32, "2026-11-06T20:48Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:0x tibia: CAUSE CORRECTED by a two-step probe (probe3\\twostep on pack58c): `:= m = merged v w` then `:= u : sized 5 i32 = m` compiles and runs to 585 (count 500 + physical 50 + totals 17 + 18). So visit_t already folds sized (add a b) once a and b are bound; the earlier failure is ORDERING: with the annotation on the same let, unify_gadt's loop (spiral_compiler.fs ~5697-5772) compares the return type sized (add ?a ?b) against sized 5 before the arguments bind ?a and ?b, so visit_t cannot fold and the TyApply-vs-TyLit pair falls to er (). DESIGN: in loop, for a reserved-op TyApply (TypeArithReserved.ops) whose operands visit to metavars, against a TyLit or another reserved op, push (r, got, expected) to a deferred list instead of er (); re-unify the list where the top-level definition finishes inference, and report the original TermError if it still does not fold. DoD unchanged: probe3 positive (single let) exits 585, the negative stays a type error, suite compare 0 residual cells.")
inl note_of_type_arith_3b_unify_fold_3 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", 3u32, "2026-11-06T20:50Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: DESIGN (read from the box tree spiral_compiler.fs with pack58c; line numbers from that tree). Everything lives inside `infer package_id module_id ...` (5365), where `errors` is declared (5368). (1) STATE: next to `let errors = ResizeArray()` add `let deferredArith = ResizeArray<VSCRange * T * T>()`. (2) DETECT: inside unify_gadt (5611) a local `reservedPending t`: t visits to TyApply(TyApply(op, a), b) with visit_t op = TyNominal i, `TypeArithReserved.ops.ContainsKey i`, and visit_t a or visit_t b is a TyMetavar. (3) DEFER: in `loop` (5697), just before the final `| _ -> er ()` (5772), add `| a, b when gadt_links.IsNone && (reservedPending a || reservedPending b) -> deferredArith.Add((r, a'', b''))`, so GADT pattern unification keeps today's behavior. (4) FLUSH: `generalize` (5550) is defined BEFORE unify (5779), so the flush cannot live in it. Add after `let unify range got expected = ...` (5779) a `flushArith ()`: snapshot and clear deferredArith, `unify r a b` each (an item still pending re-defers itself), then turn whatever is left into errors.Add(r, TermError(a, b)) and clear. Call it right before each generalize call site: inl (6235), rec_block with foralls (6264) and without (6276), plus the top-level statement paths that read `0 = errors.Count` (6644-6802) for anything generalize does not reach. (5) WHY THIS IS SOUND: a deferred pair only exists while an operand is an unbound metavar; by the enclosing definition's generalize every argument of the application has been inferred, so visit_t folds it (proven by probe3\\twostep, which compiles to 585); if it still does not fold, the original TermError is reported at the original range, so no program that fails today starts passing except through the fold. RISKS for review: error ORDER changes (deferred errors appear after later ones in the same definition), and deferral must not hide an occurs-check or kind error, so it only applies to the TyApply-vs-anything fallthrough case. NEXT: write drafts\\spiral\\TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD\\1-defer.kitdo with those 5 sites, dry-run on the pack58c tree core, then a private-cache Debug build plus probe3 (single-let positive 585, negative still TermError) on the node once the tibia chain frees it.")
inl note_of_type_arith_3b_unify_fold_4 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", 4u32, "2026-11-06T20:55Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:1x tibia: PROGRAM drafted: kit store drafts\\spiral\\TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD\\1-defer.kitdo (883534ADBC13, 7 replacements). DRY-RUN applies clean on the box tree core EF757B710BE3 (= pack58c reviewed source) -> B60EC4FECCE6. Sites: deferredArith next to errors; reservedPending before unify_gadt's loop (anchored on the loop's first match line, because blank-line anchors lose their trailing spaces in drafts); the deferral arm before the final er (); flushArith (strict) after unify; flushArith (scope = 1) before each of the 3 generalize calls (inl, and rec_block with and without foralls). Top-level statements run at scope 0 and both inl and rec_block increment first, so scope = 1 is exactly \"a top-level definition\": strict there (leftovers become the original TermError), lenient for local definitions (leftovers stay deferred). NOT COMPILED: next is a private-cache Debug build (SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR + build.ps1 -Configuration Debug -CoreSource) with probe3 (single-let positive exits 585, negative stays a TermError) and a suite compare, on the node once the tibia chain frees it, or handed to compiler for a pack review.")
inl note_of_type_arith_3b_unify_fold_5 () = Note ("TYPE-ARITH-3B-UNIFY-FOLD", 5u32, "2026-11-06T21:23Z", "tibia", "11-06 17:2x tibia: MERGED into TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD's redesign (pack58c rolled back: the eager visit_t fold broke sized_array.spi's probe). The deferral in 1-defer.kitdo stays the second half of that redesign; this item closes into TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD once the combined program exists.")
