inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_1 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 1u32, "2026-11-06T21:59Z", "main", "Split from DICE-GRANULAR-HEAL (360 min > 240; census 11-06 18:0x: 148 sites, up from 79). rpc.spi only. DoD: each site healed to lib functions/typed records or recorded as a deliberate host binding with a reason; dice ui build + e2e green on a codespace. Next step: classify the 82 sites (serde record shapes vs call glue vs JS interop). TypeFeatures: typed records for RPC payloads instead of host struct macros.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_2 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 2u32, "2026-11-06T22:04Z", "main", "main 11-06 18:0x CLASSIFIED (read of rpc.spi): the macros bind hand-written Rust serde structs in crate::model::near::rpc. (a) 15 nominal aliases ':! rpc_input' = $'crate::model::near::rpc::RpcInput' (lines 5-33); (b) 15 record-construction macros building those structs field by field (lines 163-236); (c) the rest are field reads ('$0.id', '.name', '.jsonrpc') and call glue. The heal is one design move: define the 15 shapes as Spiral records (TypeFeatures: records + an error union for RpcError/ErrorCause), and decode/encode JSON with lib json (json_value/json_quote), so the Rust structs, (a) and (b) disappear together and (c) becomes record field access. Gate: dice ui build + its e2e (transactions view reads these) on a codespace. Next step: list the Rust struct file and its serde attributes (rename/skip/option) that the decoder must honor.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_3 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 3u32, "2026-11-10T23:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 NEXT STEP DONE (read dice ui/src/model/near/rpc.rs, 166 lines: 15 serde structs + fetch_transaction_status). What a Spiral decoder must honor, checked against lib json_real decode_at: SUPPORTED already: String, i32, f64, Option, nested records, Vec<record> via array_base; Vec<String> (RpcInput.params, logs, receipt_ids, input_data_ids, output_data_receivers) as list once JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS lands (org2, gating now; until then array_base string). GAPS (4): (1) unsigned widths: Metadata.version u8 and OutcomeDetail.gas_burnt u64 have no decode_at arm (only u32); add u8/u64 arms, since NEAR gas_burnt (~1e14) must not go through f64. (2) maps that are really tagged unions: OutcomeDetail.status HashMap<String,String> is NEAR externally tagged {SuccessValue: ...} / {SuccessReceiptId: ...} / {Failure: ...}, and ActionDetail.actions Vec<HashMap<String,TransferDetail>> is [{Transfer: {...}}, {FunctionCall: {...}}]; TYPEFEATURES: model both as Spiral unions (case name = JSON key), which is exactly the lib generic union path, and that path unrolled at compile time on run-time input for list (EJP0040, fixed for list only), so decoding a union field from a run-time body needs its own probe first. (3) rename: ReceiptDetail has serde rename_all = PascalCase, so its one field action is the JSON key Action; the decoder has no rename, so either a field named with the JSON spelling or a rename map. (4) call glue: fetch_transaction_status posts RpcInput (EXPERIMENTAL_tx_status, params [hash, bowen]) to mainnet then the archival URL, retrying only on error code -32000 (unknown tx); that stays a deliberate host binding (reqwest_wasm in the browser) unless lib gains a wasm http. Next step: probe lib json on a run-time body for a union-valued field ({status: {SuccessValue: x}}) on ganymede; if it unrolls, file the union arm beside the list arm (same fix shape) before drafting the 15 records and 2 unions")
inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_4 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 4u32, "2026-11-10T23:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 GAP (2) CLOSED without a probe: lib json.spi already has decode_reads_unions_by_case_name, green on c and rust, decoding union-valued fields from a run-time (~) reply in exactly the NEAR externally tagged shape ({\"TargetCity\":\"Recife\"}, unit cases as bare strings, record payloads as objects). The list case unrolled only because list is a RECURSIVE union; NEAR status and actions unions are not recursive, so OutcomeDetail.status and ActionDetail.actions model directly as Spiral unions (status: SuccessValue : string | SuccessReceiptId : string | Failure : ...; action element: Transfer : transfer_detail | FunctionCall : ... ). Remaining decoder gaps: (1) u8/u64 arms, (3) the PascalCase Action key. Next step: draft rpc_model.spi (the 15 records + 2 unions, decode via lib json) in kit drafts dice/DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC with a decode test over a recorded EXPERIMENTAL_tx_status reply, keeping version/gas_burnt as f64 until the u64 arm exists")
inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_5 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 5u32, "2026-11-10T23:58Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 DRAFT (kit drafts dice/DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC/rpc_model.spi, budget 0): the 15 serde structs as Spiral records plus two unions (action = Transfer | FunctionCall over transfer_detail; outcome_status = SuccessValue | SuccessReceiptId), decoded by lib json (arrays as array_base until JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS lands; version and gas_burnt as f64 until a u64 arm exists). Three rust tests on run-time (~) replies in the NEAR wire shape: a receipt outcome with its status union, an action list with tagged actions, and the PascalCase receipt key decoding into a field literally named Action (the cheapest answer to gap 3, if Spiral accepts an upper-case field name). Gate queued on ganymede as org2-rpcm (scratch app over lib, after org2-both). Consumers (components/dice_view.spi, hooks/use_transactions.spi) are untouched: the swap and the dice ui build + e2e on a codespace stay the item gate")
inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_6 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 6u32, "2026-11-11T00:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 first gate org2-rpcm: 1/3 green. a_receipt_outcome_decodes_its_status_union_from_a_run_time_reply PASSED on rust, so a NEAR externally tagged status union decodes from a run-time reply. The other two failed with TracedError \"Typecase miss. Got: action\": lib json decode_at array_base arm handles only i32, string and record elements, not union elements (a further decoder gap, number 5). Fix in the draft: actions is now list action, since the list arm JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS landed tonight calls decode_at per element and that handles unions. Regate org2-rpcm2 chained after org2-rwf2")
inl note_of_dice_granular_1_rpc_7 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC", 7u32, "2026-11-11T00:28Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 rpc model GREEN: ganymede org2-rpcm2 rpc_model 3/3 on rust, 0 unsupported: the outcome status union, a tagged action list (actions as list action, through the JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS list arm) and the PascalCase receipt key decoding into a record field literally named Action (so gap 3 needs no rename support) all decode from run-time replies. Draft stays in kit drafts dice/DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC/rpc_model.spi (not landed: dice ui consumers still use the Rust structs). Remaining gaps: (1) u8/u64 decode arms (version, gas_burnt kept f64 meanwhile), (4) fetch_transaction_status stays a host binding. Next step: swap components/dice_view.spi and hooks/use_transactions.spi onto rpc_model records, then the dice ui build + e2e on a codespace (the item gate)")
inl dice_granular_2_nearblocks () = Task ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", "Heal dice ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.spi host macros (33 sites) to granular Spiral", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "granular,macros,dice,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks () = Planning ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_1 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 1u32, "2026-11-06T21:59Z", "main", "Split from DICE-GRANULAR-HEAL (360 min > 240; census 11-06 18:0x: 148 sites, up from 79). nearblocks.spi only, after slice 1 settles the shared record pattern. DoD: as slice 1. Next step: reuse slice 1 classes. TypeFeatures: typed records for RPC payloads instead of host struct macros.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_2 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 07:4xZ CLASSIFIED (nearblocks.spi, 33 sites, all one kind): they bind hand-written Rust serde structs in crate::model::near::nearblocks: 7 nominal aliases (:! block' = crate path), 7 struct-construction macros (Block { block_height: ... } and so on) and 19 field reads (.block_height and so on), i.e. a box/unbox layer between serde-decoded Rust structs and the Spiral records that already exist in the same file (block, action, actions_agg, outcomes, outcomes_agg, txn, root). HEAL (same move as DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC note 2): decode the nearblocks response text straight into the Spiral root record with lib json.decode (typed, json_real.spir), so the Rust structs and all 33 macros go together. PREREQUISITE in lib: json_real decodes i32, string, bool, records, arrays, tuples, options and unions, but not u32 (block_height) or f64 (deposit, transaction_fee); and the records use sm'.std_string where json.decode yields string. DoD: json_scan number span + json_real f64 and u32 cases with Cells tests; nearblocks records switched to Spiral string and the json.decode path; dice ui build + e2e green on a codespace. TYPEFEATURES: the records stay the typed source of truth; no host struct remains. Next step: org2 adds f64 and u32 decoding to json_scan/json_real with tests (lib land via ganymede proof).")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_3 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:36Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 07:4xZ second prerequisite found: the response is decoded generically by lib state_core.use_requests (lib/spiral/state_core.spi:330; serde over the Rust type u, then the Spiral map, here root_unbox), called from dice ui hooks/use_transactions.spi:103. So the heal needs a text variant in state_core (the same request cache, handing the body text to a Spiral decoder string -> t) and then nearblocks decodes with json.decode into root. That variant also unblocks DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC, which has the same serde-struct pattern. Order: (1) json number decoding (lib, proving now as ganymede job org2-json); (2) state_core text variant (lib); (3) nearblocks records to Spiral string + use_transactions mapping; (4) dice ui build + e2e on a codespace. Next step: after org2-json is green and landed, org2 drafts the state_core text variant.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_4 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:42Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 07:5xZ step 2 drafted: state_core.use_requests_with requests decode map (decode : string -> result' u std_string, applied where the body called sm'::deserialize) plus use_requests as a one-line wrapper passing sm'::deserialize, so existing callers are unchanged (draft drafts/spiral/DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS/state_core.spi 08689ad75a10). Proof queued as org2-sc after org2-json: dice ui main.rs regenerated before and after a private land, normalized diff must be empty (callers: only dice ui use_transactions.spi:103 and :229). Step 3 ripple measured: nearblocks records switch sm'.std_string to string and optionm'.option'/array_base std_string to Spiral option/array string; consumers to adapt: use_transactions.spi:151 (sort by block_timestamp), :182 (transaction_hash into the rpc params, add to_std_string while rpc stays serde), components/transaction.spi tr_render (field display). It needs a real dice ui Rust build (cargo check wasm32 + trunk + e2e) on a codespace, not only a regen. Next step: after org2-json and org2-sc land, org2 drafts step 3 and gates it in one codespace run.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_5 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T08:08Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:1xZ results. (1) org2-json: json_scan cells 3/3 (parse_f64, parse_u32 and number_end correct), but the json record decode cell FAILED (amount 0.0, height 0): value positions point at the space after a colon, and the new parsers did not skip it. Fixed in the draft (parse_f64 and parse_u32 now skip spaces, moved after skip_spaces); re-proof org2-json2 queued. (2) org2-sc: the state_core private land closed green; the dice ui main.rs regen differs by 236 normalized lines, all one relocation: decode is now threaded as a closure argument (use_requests_with_N gains a parameter) and the identical serde_json::from_str body moves into a thread_local closure. Not text-identical, so rustc is the judge: org2-scchk runs cargo check -p dice_ui --bin dice_ui_bin --target wasm32-unknown-unknown on the before and after main.rs on ganymede. Next step: after both are green, org2 lands json_scan/json_real/json and state_core on the box.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_6 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T08:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:2xZ json GREEN (ganymede org2-json2): json_scan 3/3 and json 17/17 executed (the spaced record decode now gives amount 0.0025 and height 4000000000), lib digest 9B8B00376B047FCF. Box land order (each proof was made on the mirror state left by the one before): (1) json_scan/json_real/json v1 with the org2-json log, (2) state_core with the org2-sc log, (3) json_scan v2 with the org2-json2 log, each behind the digest guard. Step 2 waits for the dice ui cargo check org2-scchk, so all three land together after it.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_7 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T08:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:3xZ state_core seam PROVEN for its callers: dice ui main.rs before and after, post-processed exactly like build.ps1 (Add-RustDerives plus pub mod model), both cargo check -p dice_ui --bin dice_ui_bin --target wasm32-unknown-unknown with 0 errors and the same 3 warnings (ganymede org2-scchk2). The first check (org2-scchk) skipped that post-processing and drowned in unresolved crate::model errors, so it was not a verdict. Box land: replaced the three-step plan with one combined proof (org2-jsc): the mirror is reset to the box's json_scan/json_real/json/state_core, then all four drafts land privately in one step with executed cells for json_scan and json, giving one proof log for one digest-guarded box land.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_8 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T08:46Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 steps 1 and 2 LANDED on the box (copy-only from the combined ganymede proof org2-jsc: close green, lib digest 9B8B00376B047FCF, json_scan 3/3 and json 17/17 executed; dice ui cargo check 0 errors before and after in org2-scchk2): lib/spiral/json_scan.spi de5a52524122 (number_end, parse_f64 via convert::parse_f64, parse_u32 via an i64 digit fold, both skipping leading spaces), json_real.spir b85e359b4651 (f64 and u32 decode cases), json.spi 59d8919c7acb (a typed record decode test with both), state_core.spi 08689ad75a10 (use_requests_with requests decode map; use_requests unchanged for callers). Left: step 3 (nearblocks records to Spiral string, decode with json.decode via use_requests_with, consumers in use_transactions and transaction.spi) and step 4 (dice ui build + e2e on a codespace). Next step: org2 drafts step 3.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_9 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 9u32, "2026-11-10T08:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:5xZ step 3 drafted (drafts/spiral/DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS/dice): nearblocks.spi keeps the 7 records the UI consumes and replaces all 33 host macros (7 crate-path aliases, 7 struct constructors, 19 field reads) with Spiral wire records (action_wire, txn_wire, root_wire: plain string, option, array_base), the typed conversions action_of, logs_of and txn_of (sm'.to_std_string per field), and decode_root (json.decode into root_wire, then map). use_transactions.spi:103 calls state_core.use_requests_with txns_requests model.near.nearblocks.decode_root id. The Rust serde structs (model/near/nearblocks.rs) and their pub mod line go away; rpc.rs stays for DICE-GRANULAR-1-RPC. Proof running as ganymede org2-nb: a lib-only probe decoding a realistic two-txn nearblocks page (u32 height, 1.5e24 deposit, bool status, a method and a null method, logs present and absent), then dice ui regen with build.ps1's post-processing and cargo check for wasm32.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_10 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 10u32, "2026-11-10T09:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 ganymede org2-nb (pinned, mirror restored after): dice ui regen rc=0 with the drafts (nearblocks.spi typed wire records + decode_root over json.decode, use_transactions via state_core.use_requests_with, near.rs without pub mod nearblocks, nearblocks.rs removed); cargo check wasm32 0 errors 3 warnings; 3 serde_json::from_str sites remain in main.rs (other modules). The probe went red only on its own literal 1.5e24 (Spiral lexes e24 as a variable): sample deposit changed to 1.5e3 asserted as 1500.0f64, so exponent parsing stays covered; probe-only rerun org2-nb2 queued. Next step: on nb2 green copy the three drafts to the box, delete dice/ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.rs, then the codespace UI build + e2e")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_11 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 11u32, "2026-11-10T09:14Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 probe rerun org2-nb2: test 1 GREEN (typed records decode, deposit 1.5e3 exponent read as 1500.0); test 2 RED with a real lib bug: an explicit \"method\":null decodes as Some \"ull}\" because the json_real option arm returns None only for a missing key (at < 0) and otherwise runs the string reader, which skips the n as an opening quote. Fix drafted in kit drafts DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS/lib: json_scan gains absent (missing key, or the value after spaces starts with n, which in JSON can only be null), the option arm uses it, and json.spi gains decode_reads_null_options_as_none (days null, units with a space before null, score 55). Land proof org2-jnull queued (bases DE5A52524122, B85E359B4651, 59D8919C7ACB). Next step: on green copy-land on the box, rerun the probe")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_12 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 12u32, "2026-11-10T09:36Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 null-option fix LANDED on the box from a proven close (ganymede org2-jnull: lib_land_window LANDED and closed green, 26 passed, post-land digest 002B62DF357BD5F8 = box DigestOnly; json_scan 3/3, json 18/18 with the new decode_reads_null_options_as_none). Box lib: json_scan.spi cba2e551b2f6 (absent helper), json_real.spir 28eaeb2793d6 (option arm uses json_scan::absent), json.spi 3f96e1ca72f8. Undo: spiral-bin/lib-land-undo/20261110-053403. Next step: rerun the nearblocks probe (org2-nb3) against the landed lib, then copy the three dice drafts to the box")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_13 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 13u32, "2026-11-10T09:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 probe GREEN against the landed json lib (ganymede org2-nb3: nearblocks_probe 2/2 executed, 0 failed: typed records with the 1.5e3 deposit, and a null method plus missing logs decode as absent). Dice drafts now on the box (unstaged), bases verified equal to the proof's originals: ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.spi 51dc4a16e666 (wire records + decode_root over json.decode), ui/src/hooks/use_transactions.spi 4142896d4ab7 (state_core.use_requests_with), ui/src/model/near.rs ffd1fc1191fc (no pub mod nearblocks), ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.rs deleted (git keeps it). Regen + wasm cargo check were green in org2-nb. Next step: step 4, the codespace UI build plus e2e on the dice tree with the landed json lib")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_14 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 14u32, "2026-11-10T09:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 step 4 replanned onto ganymede instead of a codespace: the proven dice codespace driver builds the COMMITTED spiral from init.ps1, which lacks the unstaged lib this change needs (json.decode, use_requests_with, the null fix), and dice e2e is one title check (toHaveTitle dice) that does not touch nearblocks. Job org2-nbui (pinned compiler, 60 min) installs trunk 0.21.14 and Playwright chromium on the node, overlays the three drafts and runs the full ui/build.ps1 (regen, cargo check, e2e, css, release trunk bundle, rna); green keeps the drafts in the mirror (= box), red restores")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_15 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 15u32, "2026-11-10T10:30Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 ganymede org2-nbui2 (pinned, drafts overlaid, hyperui cloned as dice init.ps1 does): ui/build.ps1 got through regen, cargo check, CSS, the release trunk bundle (RUST-OK dice_ui-*_bg.wasm 1276646 B, wasm-bindgen 0.2.130) and rna (dist/index.html + popup.html), then stopped at e2e. The e2e failure was the node, not dice: ganymede had no Node, so playwright test ran under bun and its TS config transform never ran (bun parsed playwright.config.ts as JS). org2 installed Node v26.13.0 (the box's version) at ganymede spiral-bin/toolchains/node; e2e against that dist then passed 1/1 (org2-e2e2). A clean single-entry rerun with Node on PATH is gating as org2-nbui3")
inl note_of_dice_granular_2_nearblocks_16 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-2-NEARBLOCKS", 16u32, "2026-11-10T10:37Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: ganymede org2-nbui3 (pinned compiler, Node v26.13.0, the three drafts overlaid on the mirror, landed json lib): dice ui/build.ps1 rc=0 in one run: regen, cargo check ok, release trunk bundle RUST-OK dice_ui-*_bg.wasm 1276646 B (wasm-bindgen 0.2.130), rna dist/index.html + popup.html, e2e 1 passed. The mirror keeps the drafts (= box). On the box (unstaged): ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.spi 51dc4a16e666, ui/src/hooks/use_transactions.spi 4142896d4ab7, ui/src/model/near.rs ffd1fc1191fc, nearblocks.rs deleted; lib json_scan cba2e551b2f6 / json_real.spir 28eaeb2793d6 / json.spi 3f96e1ca72f8 (null options). Node upkeep: ganymede now has Node at spiral-bin/toolchains/node and trunk 0.21.14 in /root/.cargo/bin")
