inl note_of_dice_granular_4_core_3 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-4-CORE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T06:39Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 06:4xZ sites by kind. lib/dice.spi (5, HEAL): the five Fsharp arms were raw export shims (let rotate_numbers x = !rotate_numbers' x, likewise create_sequential_roller, roll_progressively, roll_within_bounds, main); drafted as the typed lib export (export name f) inside the same Fsharp arms, so Rust/TypeScript/C output is unchanged; codegenFsharp supports Export for capture-free closures (the primed locals compile to closureN()). Proof running: ganymede job org2-dg4, pinned compiler, dice/lib/build.ps1 -SkipTs -SkipPy (notebook cells, document round trip, F# compile, publish, run with the result assertion) plus a before/after diff of the five generated F# let lines. contract/dice_contract.spi (8 host sites, DELIBERATE, reason each): 462 State struct needs #[near_sdk::near(contract_state)] and PanicOnDefault; 469 OldState needs borsh derives over near_sdk::store::vec::Vector; 476 From<OldState> migration walks the near_sdk store vector; 488/514/535 #[near_sdk::near] impl blocks are the contract ABI and only delegate to the Spiral exports dice_contract_*; 390 testing_env! builds the mocked chain context; 440 env::used_gas() reads the VM gas counter. None is expressible as Spiral and none carries logic beyond delegation, so they stay host. Next step: after org2-dg4 is green, org2 copies dice.spi and the regenerated dice.fsx to the box.")
inl note_of_dice_granular_4_core_4 () = Note ("DICE-GRANULAR-4-CORE", 4u32, "2026-11-10T08:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: ganymede job org2-dg4c (pinned compiler, dice/lib/build.ps1 -SkipTs 1 -SkipPy 1): notebook 28/28 executed, 0 unsupported; FSHARP-OK (published, ran, result in range) and RUST-OK. On the box (unstaged): dice/lib/dice.spi 5fae2fc8ef9d with rotate_numbers, create_sequential_roller, roll_progressively and roll_within_bounds as the typed lib export (dice.fsx e24d3f417f2b now has typed let rotate_numbers (v0 : int64) : ... and so on). main stays a macro shim, recorded reason: Export hoists the function above the closure bindings it came from, so an exported [<EntryPoint>] main is not the last declaration and dotnet publish fails FS0433 (org2-dg4b). compiler's pack81 (FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET) drops that dead let; retry export main after it installs. contract/dice_contract.spi: 8 deliberate host sites, each reason in note 3.")
