inl planning_of_large_input_scaling () = Planning ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_1 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:04Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: filed from the user 11-07 via main direction ('the compiler should handle files of indefinite size'; find superlinear spots in memo, cache, single-flight vs hopacsota). Extends COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE (whose step 2 found the 16 MB file linear, parse + tokenize about 3/4). DoD: a table (input, size, phase times, peak MB, exponent per phase) for agile.spi slices, fiscal's largest generated units, upstream's largest files and 2 project graphs, on both cores, on a quiet node; every phase above exponent 1.2 named with its code site and a follow-up item. next step: list fiscal's largest generated units and upstream's largest files. typefeatureset plan: none; measurement only.")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_2 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:05Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: STEP 1 DONE, the inputs. Largest single files: docs/backlog/state/agile.spi 16,271,813 bytes; fiscal's generated UBL units about 3.9 MB each (generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 3,908,125; creditnote 3,890,257; debitnote 3,888,072; despatchadvice 3,870,221); lib/spiral's largest module xsd_emit.spi 197,826; upstream's largest file only 23,132 (Spiral Compilation Tests/cuda_experiments/*/tensor_main.spi), so upstream has no large-file pressure: the scaling question is entirely ours. Plan for the table (a node job, quiet node, median of 3): (a) agile.spi in 1/8, 1/4, 1/2, 1/1 slices (header + the first k-th of its binding lines, as in the shard tool); (b) the 4 UBL units plus 1/4 and 1/2 slices of the biggest; (c) per phase (tokenize, parse, typecheck, prepass, peval for a --backend Rust build where it compiles) wall time and peak MB, from SPIRAL trace timings; (d) the same on the hopacsota core if one is installed on the node (else noted as not available); (e) the exponent per phase as log(t2/t1)/log(n2/n1) between slices, flagging any above 1.2. next step: the measurement script (scratchpad) and a node job when x's verify frees it. Watch: scripted recursive scans of C:\\home\\git must avoid Get-ChildItem -Recurse (it walks target/ and node_modules, taking hours); use rg-backed lookups or named folders.")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_3 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 3u32, "2026-11-07T21:03Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:1x compiler: STEP 2 READY (scratchpad scaling-cmd.ps1 + a 16 MB snapshot tar of docs/backlog/state): a node job slices agile.spi to 1/8, 1/4, 1/2, 1/1 at top-level block boundaries (as a copy of its self-contained state package) and generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 to 1/4, 1/2, 1/1 (inside the fiscal mirror so its packageDir/runtime resolve), and measures per input tokenize (--test-blocks), parse+typecheck (--check) and the formatter (format --check): median of 3 wall seconds and peak working set, then the exponent log(t2/t1)/log(n2/n1) per phase between slices. hopacsota: no installed hopacsota core on the node, recorded as not available. NEXT STEP: launch after pack62's node gates (the node is saturated by 5 lanes' jobs right now, one of them tibia's quiet bench), quiet node per the DoD.")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_4 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 4u32, "2026-11-08T03:57Z", "compiler", "11-07 23:5x compiler: NOT RUN tonight, by the DoD's quiet-node condition: the node sat at 100% load all evening (kit TRAIN38/39, tibia qat/rustab benches, x verify/crates, fiscal full builds, plus this lane's pack gates). Inputs and script are ready (scratchpad scaling-cmd.ps1, state.tar snapshot). NEXT STEP: launch in the first quiet node window (after TRAIN39 and before the morning respell), then COMPILER-LOAD-ALL right after it.")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_5 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 5u32, "2026-11-08T04:25Z", "compiler", "11-08 00:3x compiler: AGILE TABLE MEASURED on europa (quiet: loadavg 0.2; installed pack61b Linux core 79a209d7eb6c5540; each run in a 1500 MB systemd scope; median of 3; /usr/bin/time wall s / max RSS MB). Slices of the 16,787,463-byte state/agile.spi snapshot cut at top-level block boundaries: 1/8 2.13 MB: tokenize 0.62 s/146, check 1.64/170, format --check 9.65/303 | 1/4 4.28 MB: 0.94/125, 2.52/232, 15.29/441 | 1/2 8.67 MB: 1.29/222, 3.73/367, 26.17/736 | 1/1 16.79 MB: 2.22/365, 6.72/582, 47.05/1164. EXPONENTS log(t2/t1)/log(n2/n1): tokenize 0.60, 0.45, 0.82; check (parse+typecheck) 0.62, 0.56, 0.89; format 0.66, 0.76, 0.89. NONE above 1.2 (none above 1.0): the compiler and the formatter scale linearly or better on the largest input we have; process start dominates the small slices. Memory is linear: check ~35 MB per MB of input, format ~70 MB per MB. The formatter is the costliest phase (~7x check), the place to look for a speedup, not a superlinear spot. Not yet measured: fiscal's UBL units (need a fiscal mirror) and the peval/codegen phase (a --backend build). NEXT STEP: the UBL slices + a Rust build phase on the node's next quiet window.")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_6 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 6u32, "2026-11-08T04:36Z", "compiler", "11-08 01:0x compiler: FISCAL UNITS MEASURED on europa (same setup; lib = the box's current lib incl. unstaged, shipped with the units). (a) generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 slices (0.93 / 1.95 / 3.91 MB): tokenize 0.88/1.35/2.00 s (exp 0.63, 0.57); format 2.15/3.92/8.57 s, 196/390/672 MB (exp 0.87, 1.13: the highest exponent seen, under 1.2); check on a prefix slice is invalid (a generated unit's prefix cuts forward references: ETY-UnboundVariable), so (b) check uses WHOLE units as the size axis: nfe_v4_certificates 0.88 MB 6.96 s/516 MB, nfe_v2_00 1.21 MB 7.49 s/551 MB, nfe_v4 2.13 MB 10.19 s/760 MB, ubl_invoice 3.91 MB 13.89 s/1,090 MB: exponents 0.23, 0.54, 0.51 (0.46 over the whole 4.4x range): sublinear, with a ~5 s fixed cost (lib load + startup). Memory per input MB is ~8x agile's (generated XML codecs: many nominals and unions per byte); peak 1.1 GB at 3.9 MB is the number to watch on the 3.4 GB europa. RESULT: no phase above exponent 1.2 on our largest inputs (agile state 16.8 MB, fiscal units 3.9 MB); the formatter (exp up to 1.13 on generated code, ~7x check's time on the state) is the place for speed work. Remaining for the DoD: the peval/codegen phase (a --backend Rust build of these units) and the hopacsota core (not installed on any node).")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_7 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 7u32, "2026-11-09T06:26Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:5x compiler: REMAINING-DoD PLAN (CPU-light prep done; the run needs a QUIET node, which ganymede is not tonight at load 10-25, so timings there would be invalid). (1) peval+codegen phase: --backend Rust on the 4 whole fiscal units already used as the size axis (nfe_v4_certificates 0.88 MB, nfe_v2_00 1.21, nfe_v4 2.13, ubl_invoice_2_1 3.91), median of 3, /usr/bin/time wall + max RSS, minus the matching --check time = peval+codegen; (2) the same 4 on the hopacsota core (build.ps1 -Mode hopacsota in a private cache); (3) upstream's 3 largest .spi from The-Spiral-Language as a third family; (4) 2 project graphs: apps/spiral and kit/src (load-all rerun job-1794205438229 on moon gives per-root times as a by-product). Placement: europa only with a 1536M cap, too tight for ubl Rust codegen (check already peaks 1.1 GB); prefer moon in a quiet window (org's window order) or ganymede after k3s pods idle. Next step: ask org for a quiet slot on moon, run (1)+(2) there as one job.")
inl note_of_large_input_scaling_8 () = Note ("LARGE-INPUT-SCALING", 8u32, "2026-11-09T09:52Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:5x compiler: timed window SUBMITTED on moon as step 1 of job-1794217919229-compiler-moon-post-train (TRAIN42c finished, team org released moon). Same protocol as staged 11-09: hopacsota built untimed in a private cache, then the CPU<15%-for-2-min quiet gate (max 40 min; fiscal-step3-gate was running at submit, so the gates log line records the CPU at timing start), then 4 fiscal generated units x (3 single-flight runs, median + 1 hopacsota run) with peak MB, exit and output-identity per unit. PENDING.")
