inl note_of_compiler_load_all_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:04Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: filed from the user 11-07 via main direction (battle-test loading everything at once). DoD: one --server-tcp instance is fed lib/spiral and every package root of spiral, x, tibia, kit, fiscal, regex, dice (the census roots); recorded per root: load time, cumulative working set, and a second pass's time (memo reuse ratio); failures named; run on the node. next step: reuse the census root list (scratchpad census-pkgs*.txt) and the server client used by Cells. typefeatureset plan: none; measurement only.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 2u32, "2026-11-07T21:09Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:2x compiler: READY to run (scratchpad loadall-cmd.ps1 + loadall-roots.txt): 126 package roots with an existing entry file each (lib/spiral first, spiral 22, x 2, tibia 9, kit 5, fiscal 84, regex 2, dice 2; from the census root list plus dice's two manifests), fed to ONE --server-tcp instance as C builds (a 'Cannot find main' reply counts as loaded: parse+infer ran), two passes; per root: seconds, server working set; per pass: total seconds, failures, peak MB. Needs a node mirror of spiral,x,tibia,kit,fiscal,regex,dice (node-proof links deps to the spiral snapshot). NEXT STEP: run after LARGE-INPUT-SCALING on a quiet node.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 3u32, "2026-11-08T04:44Z", "compiler", "11-08 01:1x compiler: RUN on europa (quiet; installed pack61b Linux core; ONE --server-tcp instance in a 2600 MB scope; europa's clones of spiral, x, kit, regex, dice, so tibia and fiscal roots are not covered; 33 roots, C builds, two passes). LOADED (parse + typecheck done): 27 of 33: 3 ok, 3 'no main', 9 codegen errors, 11 'main must return i32 on C' / 'no C arm' (C is the wrong backend for them, which only runs after load). 1 intentional failure (zed bad fixture's type error). 5 ENVIRONMENT failures: PackageErrors from europa's clones (dice package.spiproj line 3 and kit's typed_predicate packages reference deps/ links the clones lack). MEMORY: server RSS 153 MB at the first root, 1.73 GB with lib plus all 28 loaded packages resident; no OOM under the cap. TIME: pass 1 63.6 s, pass 2 56.5 s, only 11% faster: the warm server keeps parse/typecheck (iggy encode 8.20 -> 0.91 s, regex bench 2.17 -> 0.18, agreement 6.32 -> 3.25) but re-runs partial evaluation + codegen on every request, so big entries do not get faster (apps/spiral 8.29 -> 11.30 s, wasm 4.77 -> 5.20). FINDING for COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS: in server mode an unchanged (source-graph fingerprint, backend, entry) should return the previous output, as the batch host's CompilationCache already does; that, not loading, is what the second pass is missing. Remaining for the DoD: the box/node run with tibia + fiscal roots and kit's deps (node-proof links them).")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 4u32, "2026-11-08T04:52Z", "compiler", "11-08 01:2x compiler: CORRECTION to note 3's FINDING: the server host DOES reuse whole outputs (Program.fs:1111 CompilationCache(true); keyed by uri + backend + source-graph fingerprint, only when the revision is unchanged). The successful builds hit it on pass 2 (regex bench 2.17 -> 0.18 s, iggy encode 8.20 -> 0.91). The big entries did not get faster because their C builds ENDED IN ERRORS (main must return i32 on C), and errors are never cached, so they re-ran partial evaluation. So the second-pass number mostly measures this run's wrong backend choice, not a missing cache. Rerun the timing part with each root's own backend (Rust/Gleam per its manifest or a ///> line) on the node run that adds tibia + fiscal.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 5u32, "2026-11-09T06:24Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:4x compiler: RERUN QUEUED with each root's OWN backend (the 11-08 europa run compiled everything to C, so most big entries ended in 'main must return i32 on C' errors, and errors are never cached, which made pass 2 look only 11% faster). Root list: 126 roots over spiral, kit, regex, dice, x, tibia, fiscal; backend = the file's first ///> target, else the repo default (Rust 116, C 6, Lua 3, Zig 1). Driver: a PowerShell TCP client to ONE --server-tcp instance on moon (has all repos incl. tibia + fiscal), two passes, per-request ms + server working set. Job: moon job-1794205438229-compiler-load-all-own-backends (after the 15-file test run). Next step: read pass 1 vs pass 2 per root; the DoD wants the warm reuse proven on successful builds and the peak memory with everything resident.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 6u32, "2026-11-10T10:37Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:3x compiler (groom with fiscal; rig mapped TRAIN42e to TRAIN43f \"or clear if no train is needed\"): CLEARED, not re-pointed. This item never needed a rig train: the wait stood for its pack content reaching the Windows hosts, and pack78 (containing pack67-pack77) is installed on all four nodes (box/moon Core f4148639; Linux now pack82 Core c495bc57). Remaining DoD is a measurement (warm reuse on successful builds, peak memory with everything resident), a medium run for ganymede, which org provisioned 06:05 local. Next step: rerun the 126-root load on ganymede with each root''s own backend.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 7u32, "2026-11-10T11:12Z", "compiler", "11-10 07:3x compiler: the 11-09 queued rerun on moon (job-1794205438229-compiler-load-all-own-backends) NEVER RAN: exit 143, stopped on request while waiting for job-1794203526984-compiler-split-tests-15files. Rerun needs moon (the only node with all 7 repos incl. tibia + fiscal; ganymede has lib/deps since 06:05 local but not every repo) when it is quiet (TRAIN43f running now). Note for the rerun: tonights COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN (pack80+) makes unit-returning mains compile on C, which removes the \"main must return i32 on C\" errors that skewed the 11-08 europa pass-2 numbers; moon still runs pack78 until its win-x64 pack83, so either run after that install or pin a pack83 win-x64 copy. Next step: when moon is quiet, rerun the 126-root two-pass driver with each roots own backend.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 8u32, "2026-11-10T23:07Z", "compiler", "11-10 19:1x compiler: RERUN RUNNING on moon (quiet, idle since the BSOD): job-1794351993986-compiler-moon-loadall-p89b, the same 126-root two-pass driver (C:\\home\\remote-stage\\loadall\\loadall-p89.ps1 = loadall-moon.ps1 with only the compiler pinned) against the Windows pack89 build (sourceSha16 962ba558, built on moon tonight; it includes COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN, so unit mains no longer error on C). Pass 1 rows are arriving (some roots fail with their own PackageErrors / type errors, recorded as errors, never cached). Next step: compare pass 1 vs pass 2 ms on the ok rows and take the max working set as peak memory.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 9u32, "2026-11-10T23:13Z", "compiler", "11-10 19:2x compiler: moon run DONE (job-1794351993986-compiler-moon-loadall-p89b, pack89 win build core F66E14AF, one --server-tcp instance, two passes). WARM REUSE PROVEN on successful builds: the 22 roots that compiled ok took 160.0 s in pass 1 and 0.98 s in pass 2 (pass totals 218 s -> 46 s incl. errors; biggest: spiral/apps/spiral/spiral.spi 42.5 s cold, regex/bench/bench.spi 19.8 s, spiral_wasm 14.9 s, x exsss 13.1 s; every pass-2 ok row <= 147 ms). 11 roots error (their own PackageErrors/type errors, never cached, same in both passes), 3 load with no main. TWO GAPS, so not Done: (1) 90 of 126 roots are MISSING on moon: 84 fiscal paths in roots.tsv no longer exist (fiscal restructured its tree; the repo itself is present), plus 4 tibia, 1 kit, 1 spiral; (2) the memory column reads 19 MB throughout, i.e. the PID the driver samples is not the process holding the compiled state, so peak memory is unmeasured. Next step: regenerate roots.tsv from todays trees (first ///> target, else repo default) and sample the working set of the servers whole process tree, then rerun on moon.")
inl note_of_compiler_load_all_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-LOAD-ALL", 10u32, "2026-11-10T23:41Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:0x compiler: the corrected rerun (job-1794352866622-compiler-moon-loadall-p89c: fiscal/tibia/kit clones fast-forwarded on moon, process-tree memory sampling) CRASHED: exit -1073741819 (0xC0000005, access violation in pwsh) while moon was starved (org2: sshd resetting connections; rig TRAIN43f release build on moon). No result; not retried tonight. Next step: rerun on moon when it is quiet (it is still the only node with every repo), same script C:\\home\\remote-stage\\loadall\\loadall-p89.ps1.")
