inl rec_marker_infer () = Task ("REC-MARKER-INFER", "Recursion marker ^: make it unnecessary in the i574n dialect (infer self/mutual recursion from the definition's own references) while upstream's spelling keeps working; compare F# rec, OCaml let rec, Scala, Haskell", TaskKind, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,syntax,dialect", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rec_marker_infer () = Planning ("REC-MARKER-INFER", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_1 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:04Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: filed from the user 11-07 via main direction (drop it, infer it, or at least make it a no-op unless needed; the user suspects it is an F# let-rec copy; LLM drift put it on every function, REC-MARKER-HEAL removes the 96 unneeded sites). DoD: (1) a short comparison (F# rec scoping, OCaml let rec, Scala/Haskell implicit recursion) and what ^ actually controls in our compiler (name visibility only, or also join points / mutual groups); (2) in the i574n dialect a recursive definition without ^ compiles (recursion detected from references, mutual groups from the reference graph) and an unneeded ^ is a warning; (3) upstream dialect unchanged; samples on every backend unchanged byte-for-byte. next step: read how the parser and prepass use the rec flag. typefeatureset plan: the inferred recursion groups as a typed SCC result, not a flag per name.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_2 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 2u32, "2026-11-07T11:11Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: STEP 1 DONE, what ^ controls (read at the live tree): the parser keeps ^ as TopRecInl (spiral_compiler.fs ~3530), inl_or_let_process (~2682) puts the definition's OWN NAME in scope of its body only when is_rec (and requires a function body: ExpectedFunctionAsBodyOfRecStatement), the bundler groups a ^ block with the following :& blocks into one BundleRecInl (~3870, ~4025), and inference (~6602) runs rec_block over the group: every name of the group in scope, monomorphic inside the group, generalized after. Without ^, a name in the body resolves to an EARLIER top-level definition of that name (shadowing), exactly ML's let vs let rec. So it is not just an F# copy: it is OCaml/F# 'let rec' semantics, which exist because ML allows redefinition with shadowing (Haskell and Scala make every top-level definition recursive because they forbid shadowing at the top level). DESIGN for the i574n dialect, upstream-compatible: (a) a definition whose body references its own name while NO earlier top-level definition of that name is in scope is unambiguous, so infer rec; (b) if an earlier same-named definition exists, keep the upstream reading (shadowing) and warn that ^ is needed for recursion; (c) mutual recursion: a forward reference from a definition to a LATER top-level definition is unbound today, so form groups from the reference graph's strongly connected components among consecutive definitions and infer them like a :& group; (d) an unneeded ^ (no self or group reference) becomes a warning, which also gives REC-MARKER-HEAL a compiler-side detector; upstream's dialect keeps today's rules unchanged. next step: implement (a)+(d) behind the i574n dialect switch in inl_or_let_process / the bundler, with samples: a recursive definition without ^ compiles; a shadowing redefinition keeps its old meaning.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_3 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 3u32, "2026-11-07T19:38Z", "compiler", "11-07 15:4x compiler: STEP (a) DRAFTED (kit\\drafts\\spiral\\REC-MARKER-INFER\\1-infer-self-recursion.kitdo, 5 replacements, stacks on LITERAL-SUFFIX-WARN's InferResult field).\nKEY PROPERTY: recursion is inferred ONLY when a top-down definition's inference fails with its OWN name unbound (InferResult.self_unbound, a typed check on UnboundVariable (UnboundTermName own)). Then typecheck re-infers the same definition as a one-element BundleRecInl (exactly what `^` produces). A self-reference that resolves to an earlier same-named definition never fails, so shadowing keeps its meaning (rule b) with no extra check, and every program that compiles today compiles to the same bytes: the change can only turn today's 'Unbound term variable: f' errors into recursive definitions. The stream keeps the ORIGINAL bundle beside the rec result, so the incremental diff (reference equality on bundles) still reuses it. Upstream-dialect packages are excluded (upstreamDialectPids, filled where autoExportPids is, from package_default_env's edition).\nSAMPLES (unstaged): samples/rec_inferred_self (count_down without ^, exit 17; today: unbound error) and samples/rec_shadowing_keeps_meaning (`:= step n = n + 1` then `:= step n = step (step n)`, exit 42 today and after).\nNot in this step: (c) mutual groups from the reference graph, (d) the unneeded-^ warning (needs a free-variable walker over RawExpr; the cheap double-infer would cost every ^ definition a second inference).\nNEXT STEP: gate as pack63 after pack62 (smoke + examples byte identity, both samples on C/Zig/Rust).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_4 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 4u32, "2026-11-07T21:21Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:2x compiler: STEP (d) DRAFTED in the same kitdo (now 6 replacements): for a single-definition top-down ^ group in an i574n package whose name has no earlier definition, infer runs validate_bound_vars over the body (a syntax walk, no inference) and, when the body never refers to its own name, warns 'WTY-UnneededRecMarker: <name> never refers to itself, so its ^ is not needed; drop the ^'. upstreamDialectPids moved before infer so infer can read it (one dictionary, filled where autoExportPids is). This gives REC-MARKER-HEAL a compiler-side detector. pack62 (gating on the node now) carries step (a) only; (d) rides the next pack. Still open: (c) mutual groups from the reference graph.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_5 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 5u32, "2026-11-07T21:48Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:5x compiler: (c) mutual groups, DESIGN ONLY (not drafted): today a reference to a LATER top-level definition is 'Unbound term variable', so inferring mutual recursion means typecheck must look ahead in the bundle stream: when a top-down definition fails only on names that later definitions of the same module define, and those later definitions (transitively) refer back, group the consecutive run into one BundleRecInl and infer it as a :& group. Cost: lookahead on the promise stream (blocks are fulfilled lazily) and a new forward-reference semantics, which upstream ML scoping never had; the user's ask ('drop it, infer it, or at least make it a no-op unless needed') is met for self-recursion by (a) and for the marker by (d), so (c) waits for a user request with a real mutual pair that :& makes awkward.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_6 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 6u32, "2026-11-07T22:41Z", "compiler", "11-07 18:3x compiler: PACK62 GATED GREEN on the node (job-1794086340458-compiler-p62; core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE; sources = live + 6 programs, re-applied byte-identical 986A4912DA0970C7): smoke residuals 0/159 differ vs pack61 (DISAGREE 0; 10 Swift = node vcvars gap); Rust compile -Suite all vs pack61b 542 rows, only rec_inferred_self differs (base error -> ok, the feature); linked 20/20 (incl. linked_literal_suffix_redundant / _needed); lib type probes 3/3; apps/spiral consumer ok; fixtures: --test 7/31/unbound-before, duplicate-package hint names both package dirs, rec samples C+Rust 17/42. Install on the box is WAITING for kit's TRAIN38 (a mid-train box install would mix compilers); then hashes to main.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_7 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 7u32, "2026-11-07T23:07Z", "compiler", "11-07 19:0x compiler: STEP (d) PROVEN on the node (p63a): ':= ^ unneeded (x : i32) : i32 = x + 1' warns 'WTY-UnneededRecMarker: unneeded never refers to itself, so its ^ is not needed; drop the ^'; ':= ^ needed n = ... needed (n - 1)' does not; the build still compiles. Draft split for clean gating: 1-infer-self-recursion.kitdo (step a, in pack62) and 2-unneeded-marker-warning.kitdo (step d, pack63).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_8 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 8u32, "2026-11-08T03:08Z", "compiler", "11-07 23:1x compiler: PACK63 GATED GREEN on the node (job-1794105487479-compiler-p63; core 82C0AC66450A66B5 = pack62 sources + 3-static-block-opens + REC 2-unneeded-marker-warning + FORMATTER 3-hand-if-then-rule-over-pack62): S2b 15/10/99 + leak refused; WTY-UnneededRecMarker on the fixture; type probes 3/3; consumer ok; smoke residuals 0/159 vs pack62 (DISAGREE 0); linked 20/20; Rust -Suite all 542 rows equal to pack62 except 5 rows where pack62/pack61b timed out under node load (3 negative samples error identically; portable_convert_parse and portable_math_rounding recompiled on the box: residual-equal). NOT INSTALLED: per main and the user's approved plan, pack63 installs the morning after the user's push, followed at once by one fleet respell window (rule A v2 makes unrespelled files red in formatter checks).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_9 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 9u32, "2026-11-09T02:44Z", "compiler", "11-08 23:0x compiler: pack63c (= gated pack63 + the user HEAD 3739cfb7 Pascal shl/shr fix + FORMATTER 4) INSTALLED on box/moon/vultr/ganymede 11-08 (box 19:14 copy-install, pair 9011B777/7A2B8AD5; Linux core 5c92e46c byte-identical on vultr and ganymede). Moon -Suite all -Native on pack63c (job-1794182365680, private cache, 22 min): 7586 rows, compile ok 7048, native 6714 ran, 10 build-fail, oracle agree 5949, DISAGREE 0. Vs the 10-31 accepted baseline: compile changes only gadt_growing_index_runtime error->ok (x3); one exit change (dynamic_array_tuple_managed C 0->-1) whose C is byte-identical under pack62 and pack63c (B075ECF24EA2C45C), so it predates pack63c. europa lib --check 82/82 reformatted lib files ok. The installed compiler now infers self-recursion and warns WTY-UnneededRecMarker (DoD 2 partly). Next step: mutual groups from the reference graph (DoD 2 rest), then REC-MARKER-HEAL's 66 compiler sample sites.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_10 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 10u32, "2026-11-09T06:30Z", "compiler", "11-09 03:1x compiler DESIGN for DoD 2's remaining half (mutual groups without :&). Where: typecheck (spiral_compiler.fs ~29733) walks a module's bundle stream in order; today a top-down BundleInl whose inference fails ONLY because its own name is unbound is retried as a one-definition BundleRecInl (x.self_unbound, ~29740). Extension: (1) infer reports forward_unbound, the term names unbound in env (never a shadowing case: a name already bound keeps its meaning, as rec_shadowing_keeps_meaning requires); (2) when a BundleInl fails only on forward_unbound names, typecheck looks AHEAD in the same module's stream for the bundles defining them; if they are all top-down BundleInl and reachable within a contiguous run, it infers the whole run [f .. g] as ONE BundleRecInl (contiguous, so top-down order and the definitions in between keep their scope), emits that group's result in place of the run, and skips the consumed bundles; (3) anything else (a forward name defined by a type, prototype, open or another module) is a normal unbound error, unchanged; (4) upstream-dialect packages are untouched (upstreamDialectPids), and every program that compiled before compiles to the same bytes, because the retry only fires where inference already failed. Tests: rec_inferred_mutual (even/odd without :&, exit 42 on C/Rust/Zig), rec_inferred_mutual_with_between (a non-recursive def between the two), rec_mutual_upstream_refused (dialect upstream still needs :&), plus the full suite residual-identical to pack64. Next step: draft it as a kitdo over pack66, build on ganymede, run the 3 fixtures + -Suite all.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_11 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 11u32, "2026-11-09T06:31Z", "compiler", "11-09 03:2x compiler: DESIGN CONSTRAINT found before implementing (read at pack66 source ~29795-29830): diff walks typecheck's RESULT stream in lockstep with the INPUT bundle stream (one result per input bundle), so the mutual-group retry must NOT shorten the stream. Instead: the group's result goes on the FIRST bundle of the run, and every consumed later bundle gets a placeholder result (its own bundle, no errors, no top_env additions, since the group already added every name) so diff stays 1:1 and the incremental server path keeps working. The retry is kept only if the group infers with zero errors; otherwise the original per-bundle results stand (no behavior change for code that compiled or failed before). The lookahead forces at most the next 64 stream cells (a Hopac job, inside typecheck's existing Job). Implementation deferred to a focused pass with fixtures: it touches the Hopac stream plumbing that the editor/server path also uses, so it needs the -Suite all + server-mode incremental check, not a blind kitdo.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_12 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 12u32, "2026-11-09T08:30Z", "compiler", "11-09 08:3x compiler: mutual groups IMPLEMENTED as draft 3-infer-mutual-groups.kitdo (over pack70 = pack71 candidate). InferResult gains unbound_only (the unbound term names when EVERY error is an unbound term name). typecheck: a top-down BundleInl that fails only on unbound names (own name filtered; not upstream dialect; not an autoExport package in v1) looks ahead up to 64 stream cells for top-down BundleInl defining them (None cells skipped, any other bundle kind aborts); the whole contiguous run is inferred as ONE BundleRecInl; kept only with zero errors, otherwise the original per-bundle result stands. Stream stays 1:1: the group result rides the first bundle, each consumed bundle gets a placeholder (FRecInl [] filled_top, AInclude empty, no errors) so diff/prepass keep lockstep reuse (prepass of FRecInl [] adds nothing). Note: lockstep was already loose (auto-export emits an extra result and diff then falls back to tc()). Fixtures staged: rec_inferred_mutual (even/odd, exit 42), rec_inferred_mutual_with_between (non-recursive decrement between), rec_mutual_undefined_negative (forward name never defined stays ETY-UnboundVariable). Build + C run queued on europa behind a loadavg<3 guard (ganymede load 24/4 cores). v1 limits: autoExport packages keep needing :&; upstream fixture deferred (needs upstream-syntax source).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_13 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 13u32, "2026-11-09T09:34Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:4x compiler: MUTUAL GROUPS WORK (pack71 = pack70 + 3-infer-mutual-groups.kitdo, core be24a339, built + run on europa, C via gcc). Rule TIGHTENED before the build: a lookahead group is formed only when every forward name the failing definition needs can reach it again through the members references (validate_bound_vars over each member body, restricted to group names) -- a real cycle. Definitions between the cycle members ride along in the group; a plain forward reference to a later non-recursive definition stays an error, so top-down meaning is unchanged outside cycles. Fixtures landed as samples (unstaged): rec_inferred_mutual (even/odd, no :&) exit 42; rec_inferred_mutual_with_between (decrement between, used only after its definition) exit 42; rec_mutual_undefined_negative ETY-UnboundVariable is_odd; rec_forward_reference_negative (twice_plus -> later plus_one, no cycle) ETY-UnboundVariable plus_one. First try of with_between used decrement BEFORE its definition and was correctly refused under the tightened rule. Next: -Suite all on pack71 (residual-identical expected: the path only fires where inference already failed) + a server-mode incremental check.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_14 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 14u32, "2026-11-09T09:45Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:5x compiler: INCREMENTAL STALENESS found by reading the server path (no server-mode harness exists) and fixed in the draft: diff reuses a typecheck result when its stored bundle equals the input bundle; the group result was stored under the FIRST members bundle, so editing a LATER member would reuse the group (old member body inside) and re-typecheck only the edited member alone -- stale codegen in the editor/server path. Fix: the group result is stored under a synthetic key Some (BundleRecInl(group, true)), which never equals an input bundle, so any edit recomputes from the group head (only grouped definitions lose incremental reuse). Verified the stored bundle has no other reader (prepass, error collection and HoverAt ignore it). Placeholders now also carry the groups hovers, since HoverAt picks the last result at or before the cursor line and a cursor inside a later member lands on its placeholder. CLI output is unaffected (no previous result to diff), so the running pack73 gate stays valid; the final build gets the fixtures again.")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_15 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 15u32, "2026-11-09T10:12Z", "compiler", "pack73 (with REC 3) suite on ganymede: 7586 rows vs pack70, compile-status diffs 0, residual diffs 0 -- the mutual-group path changes nothing that compiled or failed before; new rows: rec_* samples as designed. pack73b (final draft: synthetic group key + placeholder hovers) fixtures all as designed. Rolling out as pack73b (europa installed).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_16 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 16u32, "2026-11-10T10:13Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:1x compiler (groom, prompted by fiscal): the train:TRAIN42e wait was stale (it stood for the box/moon install of pack73b, delivered later by pack78 to all four nodes; TRAIN42e is dead). DoD met: (1) the comparison and what ^ controls (11-07 11:11Z note: name visibility of the definitions own name, function-body requirement, :& grouping); (2) i574n dialect: recursion without ^ compiles, mutual groups from the reference graph (REC 3 in pack73b: synthetic group key, placeholder results keep the stream in lockstep) and an unneeded ^ is WTY-UnneededRecMarker (pack63); (3) upstream dialect unchanged and samples unchanged (pack73 suite vs pack70: 7586 rows, compile-status 0, residual 0; new rows only the rec_* samples).")
inl note_of_rec_marker_infer_17 () = Note ("REC-MARKER-INFER", 17u32, "2026-11-10T10:16Z", "compiler", "Evidence: pack63 gate (WTY-UnneededRecMarker on the fixture, residuals 0/159), pack73 suite on ganymede 11-09 10:12Z (7586 rows, 0 status/residual diffs vs pack70, rec_* samples as designed), installed fleet-wide in pack78 and later (box/moon Core f4148639, Linux pack82 Core c495bc57).")
inl literal_suffix_warn () = Task ("LITERAL-SUFFIX-WARN", "Warn when a number literal's explicit suffix is unnecessary (10u64 where inference already gives u64), with the suggested spelling", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,diagnostics,dialect", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_literal_suffix_warn () = Planning ("LITERAL-SUFFIX-WARN", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl formatter_pre_hopac_audit () = Task ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", "Formatter vs the hand-written era: check every org repo's code from before the vibecoding/hopac-sota phase against the formatter for hand rules, type-modeling techniques and naming/style preferences, and fix what drifted", TaskKind, P1, D4, 80u32, Active, "", "team:compiler,formatter,style,audit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit () = Planning ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:04Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: filed from the user 11-07 via main direction (go back to before ~November 2025 in every org repo). DoD: per repo, the last pre-phase commit, the formatter run over its .spi files with the diff classified (formatter rule missing / formatter wrong / old style intentionally replaced), each 'missing' or 'wrong' fixed or filed. next step: find the pre-phase commit per repo with git log. typefeatureset plan: none.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_2 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T19:29Z", "compiler", "11-07 15:3x compiler: STEP 1 (pre-phase commits, last commit before 2025-11-01, which is where each repo's 'tests' burst starts): spiral ef1398e6 (2025-10-29), polyglot 8d8b136e (10-29), dice 8fb6fc7 (10-29), alphabet e9dbcac (10-28), tictactoe a473452 (2023-03-14). i574n.github 25c350f, vault 218f6e4e and singularity 9286c97 hold no Spiral at those commits; The-Spiral-Language and Spiral-s-ML-Library are upstream (excluded). The hand-written era lived mostly in .dib notebooks: extracted every `#!spiral` cell (spiral 1903 cells in 43 notebooks, polyglot 56, dice 44, alphabet 16) into <notebook>.dib.spi beside the era's .spi files (spiral 77, dice 16, tictactoe 54): 198 files, 2.2 MB, tar 77d580e67797.\nSTEP 2 running on europa (load 1.2; installed pack61 formatter, Linux core 65d6bb6a; systemd scope MemoryMax=1600M): `format` over a copy, then `diff -ru` original vs formatted for classification (formatter rule missing / formatter wrong / old style intentionally replaced).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_3 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 3u32, "2026-11-07T20:16Z", "compiler", "11-07 16:2x compiler: STEP 2 RESULT (europa, installed pack61 formatter, 11 s; corpus tar 77d580e67797). 189 of 198 files change, 782 hunks:\n- 316 over-120 splits: the hand era wrote lines past 120 columns; the formatter's 120 limit (LineWidth rule) is the user's later decision. CLASS: old style intentionally replaced.\n- 207 whitespace-only (trailing blanks; `rc( mutable t)` -> `rc ( mutable t)`; `!!!!SymbolToString (x)` -> `!!!!SymbolToString(x)`). CLASS: intentional normalization.\n- 285 if/then JOINS: `if cond` / `then x` (then on its own line) becomes `if cond then x`. CLASS: FORMATTER RULE WRONG vs the hand rule. Census of the hand corpus: spiral 309 split-before-then vs 78 `if c then` with a block body after and only 2 whole one-liners; alphabet 32 split / 0; dice 28 / 9; tictactoe 14 / 20 (2023, older); polyglot 4 / 8. THE HAND RULE (spiral, the user's own code): a then-branch that is one line goes on its own `then` line under `if` (`else` on the next line); `if c then` ends the line only when a block body follows; one-line if/then/else almost never.\n- 13 other joins + 4 unclassified (to read with the formatter change).\nDECISION NEEDED BEFORE ANY RESPELL (memories mass-respell-show-sample-first, formatter-change-ripples-fleet): flipping the formatter to the hand rule respells every formatted repo; compiler will show the user a sample diff first. Edition 3's `? c` / `?> a` / `|: b` is the same shape, so the rule carries to both dialects.\nNEXT STEP: draft the formatter rule on a candidate, run it over lib + one repo, and put the sample diff in front of the user.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_4 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 4u32, "2026-11-07T20:50Z", "compiler", "11-07 16:5x compiler: DRAFT (option B, no respell): kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT\\1-keep-authored-then-line.kitdo. The join comes from mergeThen's first case (core ~33349: a one-line 'then x' is pulled onto the condition line whenever it fits). B keeps that merge only when 'then' was authored on the condition's line (authoredBreaks has every lexeme that starts a source line); a 'then x' written on its own line stays there, a bare 'then' before a block still joins ('if c then' + block, the hand rule's other half). Code formatted since November has no own-line 'then x' (the formatter joined them), so B changes no formatted file, while hand-era files keep their style. Option A (force the hand rule everywhere, respelling every formatted file) is the user's call with a sample diff (memory mass-respell-show-sample-first). NEXT STEP: ride pack62's candidate; prove 0 changes on lib format --check and 0 if/then joins on the pre-phase corpus.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_5 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 5u32, "2026-11-07T21:23Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:3x compiler: CLASSIFICATION COMPLETE. The remaining 17 hunks are blank-line trims (dice contract/ui) and redundant statement parentheses dropped ('(join listm.init_series ...)' -> 'join ...', polyglot math): intentional normalizations. So of 782 hunks the only 'formatter wrong' class is the 285 if/then joins; the 316 over-120 splits and 224 whitespace/paren normalizations are the user's later rules. Fix drafted as option B (keep an authored own-line 'then x'); option A (force the hand rule fleet-wide) waits on the user with a sample diff. NEXT STEP: pack62's node gate proves B (lib --check unchanged, split-before-then kept in the corpus).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_6 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 6u32, "2026-11-07T21:27Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:3x compiler: option A's footprint (estimate by line scan of lib/spiral, spiral/apps, x/apps, kit/src, tibia/src, fiscal/src): 5,144 one-line 'if c then x' / '? c ?> x' lines with no else on the same line, in 648 files, would move 'then x' to its own line. That is the size of the user's decision (A respells them; B keeps them as written and keeps hand-era files as written).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_7 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 7u32, "2026-11-07T21:38Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:4x compiler: USER DECISION (asked directly): FORCE THE HAND RULE (option A): a one-line then-branch always goes on its own 'then' (or '?>') line under its condition; 'if c then' ends the line only before a block body. Sample diff to the user BEFORE any respell (memory mass-respell-show-sample-first); install together with one fleet respell window coordinated with x/kit (5,144 lines / 648 files estimated). pack62 keeps option B (no ripple: authored own-line 'then x' stays) as the safe intermediate; A ships in pack63 with the respell.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_8 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 8u32, "2026-11-07T21:47Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:5x compiler: pack62's node gate measured option B: lib format --check unchanged (76 would-change files on both pack61b and the candidate, so no ripple), but on the hand-era corpus it keeps only 38 of the 387 own-line 'then' layouts: the formatter's other path, 'a whole if that fits goes on one line' (core ~33326), joins most of them before mergeThen runs (127 of the 171 short three-line if/then/else in spiral's hand code fit in 120 columns). So the user's option A must drop both (kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT\\2-hand-if-then-rule.kitdo does: removes the whole-if one-line case and never merges 'then x'). NEXT STEP: A's sample diff over lib/spiral from the next node job (not for install), shown to the user before the respell.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_9 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 9u32, "2026-11-08T02:05Z", "compiler", "11-07 22:0x compiler: USER SAMPLE ROUND 1 (rule A v1 over lib/spiral + spiral/apps): only 12 files change (lib 3 +11/-5, apps 9 +50/-24, all one-line '? c ?> a |: b'; the 5,144-line estimate was a raw line scan that counted inline ifs the formatter never re-lays). v1 gave '? c ?> a' / '|: b' because a text pass, joinThenLines (core ~34115), glued any 'then x' / '?> x' line onto its condition. USER (asked directly): 3 lines like if/then/else ('? c' / '?> a' / '|: b'), and 'keep one liners if too small, don't fantomas have a threshold for that? can we do even better?'. Fantomas: fsharp_max_if_then_else_short_width (60 by default) keeps a short if/then/else on one line. Hand corpus: 171 split vs 2 one-liners, even 'if x > 0i32 / then 1 / else 0' was split, so a character threshold alone over-joins. RULE A v2 (draft 2-hand-if-then-rule.kitdo, 4 replacements): one line only when every then/else branch is a single token (literal or name) AND the whole if is at most 40 characters (structural, stricter than Fantomas' width); otherwise 3 lines; mergeThen never pulls 'then x' up; joinThenLines joins only a bare 'then'/'?>' before a block. NEXT STEP: node job compiler-fmta2 gives the v2 sample + hand-corpus fidelity for the user.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_10 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 10u32, "2026-11-08T02:34Z", "compiler", "11-07 22:2x compiler: USER APPROVED rule A v2 for ONE coordinated fleet respell (asked directly with the sample: 'Approve, respell fleet'). Sample (node job compiler-fmta2, base pack61b vs v2 over the same trees): lib/spiral 52 files +527/-260, spiral/apps 54 files +695/-334; fidelity on the 2025 hand corpus: 382 of 387 own-line 'then' layouts kept, 4 whole one-liners (hand had 2). PLAN: pack63 = S2b + REC step d + rule A v2 (rebased over pack62, whose option-B line it replaces); install; then one respell window where each owner runs the installed formatter over its repos (spiral: compiler; x, kit, tibia, fiscal, dice/alphabet/regex/blog per owner), a per-repo diff count posted before applying, kit's style/census checks and Cells notebooks gating each repo after. NEXT STEP: pack62 install after TRAIN39's box half, then pack63's gate.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_11 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 11u32, "2026-11-08T03:08Z", "compiler", "11-07 23:1x compiler: PACK63 GATED GREEN on the node (job-1794105487479-compiler-p63; core 82C0AC66450A66B5 = pack62 sources + 3-static-block-opens + REC 2-unneeded-marker-warning + FORMATTER 3-hand-if-then-rule-over-pack62): S2b 15/10/99 + leak refused; WTY-UnneededRecMarker on the fixture; type probes 3/3; consumer ok; smoke residuals 0/159 vs pack62 (DISAGREE 0); linked 20/20; Rust -Suite all 542 rows equal to pack62 except 5 rows where pack62/pack61b timed out under node load (3 negative samples error identically; portable_convert_parse and portable_math_rounding recompiled on the box: residual-equal). NOT INSTALLED: per main and the user's approved plan, pack63 installs the morning after the user's push, followed at once by one fleet respell window (rule A v2 makes unrespelled files red in formatter checks).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_12 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 12u32, "2026-11-08T11:48Z", "compiler", "11-08 compiler: SEQUENCE CHANGE (main, 11-08): the fleet respell (rule A v2) waits for rig's TRAIN41 to install, because rig's kit->rig source respell (R3, on TRAIN41) and this respell both rewrite every kit .spi. The order is TRAIN40 -> TRAIN41 (R3) -> fleet respell -> R4/R5 (KIT-NEXT-NAME note 4). The respell still needs, in order: the user's push, pack63 on the box, and the sample diff shown to the user. Rig tells compiler when TRAIN41 is installed. pack62 and pack63 installs are unaffected.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_13 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 13u32, "2026-11-08T22:34Z", "compiler", "11-08 18:2x compiler: USER (direct): \"we should never wait on pushes ... make sure the updated compiler is everywhere then reformat where we drifted\". Drift cause: pack62 joinThenLines glued `?> x` onto `? c` even with `|:` on the next line (tibia/apps/arena/scan.spi), and blocks that fit 120 columns are kept AsWritten, so pack63 alone never heals that drift. FIX = program 4-split-joined-then-before-else.kitdo (textHabits splitThenLines: a condition line with a top-level ?>/then followed by a same-indent |: / |? / else / elif line splits into three; sameParse-guarded). pack63c = user HEAD 3739cfb7 core (incl. Pascal QWord shl/shr) + CELLS 3 + REC 2 + FORMATTER 3 + FORMATTER 4. Probes: j1/j2/elif/nested/string-?>/no-else/one-liner/three-line all correct; scan.spi heals to HEAD layout byte-for-byte. INSTALLED: moon (pair 9011B777/7A2B8AD5, backup compiler-installs\\pack63c-20261108-181727), europa + ganymede (Linux build, byte-identical, core 5c92e46c2001dc2b). BOX: held until TRAIN41 box half installs (rig: the train pins the live compiler). Next step: fleet reformat with the candidate DLL (dry run running), then box install on rigs signal.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_14 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 14u32, "2026-11-08T23:51Z", "compiler", "11-08 19:5x compiler: pack63c INSTALLED EVERYWHERE: box 19:14 (copy-install, live core 4521428F31ABC748 unstaged, backup compiler-installs\\pack63c-20261108-191403), moon (pair 9011B777/7A2B8AD5), vultr + ganymede (Linux core 5c92e46c, byte-identical). FLEET REFORMAT APPLIED (unstaged), formatted on ganymede with the installed pack63c, box only wrote files: 853 files over spiral 118, kit 546, tibia 115, x 32, regex 12, fiscal 11, html 7, alphabet 5, dice 3, blog 1. Excluded: kit state/, spiral apps/compiler/tmp + scripts + zed fixtures, fiscal generated/ (owner regenerates). 381 files are pure then-splits; the rest also carry 120-column splits and blank cleanup; every output passed sameParse. 9 files edited by lanes after the snapshot were re-formatted from live (a blind write would have reverted tibia bc_run.spi). Next step: moon A/B pack62 vs pack63c on generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 (fiscal reports pack62 7 s/unit vs over 10 min under pack63c on loaded ganymede); lanes run their gates (rig regen before TRAIN42, tibia layout gate, microblog Cells).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_15 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 15u32, "2026-11-09T00:00Z", "compiler", "11-08 20:0x compiler: perf A/B on idle moon: NO regression. generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 (4.3 MB): pack62 57 s / pack63c 57 s / pack62 again 57 s, peak 1.6-2.0 GB; pt_saft (1.2 MB) 18/19/17 s. The over-10-min times on ganymede were load (16.9 on 4 cores). QUEUED: moon job-1794182365680-compiler-suite-pack63c-moon (-Suite all -Native, mirror compiler head 3739cfb7 + pack63c live core, private cache); ganymede job-1794182370625-compiler-linux-suite-sizing (Linux -Suite all -Native under /usr/bin/time, for k3s sizing). Next step: read both results on wake, then close CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS / REC-MARKER-INFER with evidence if residuals match pack62.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_16 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 16u32, "2026-11-09T01:04Z", "compiler", "11-08 21:1x compiler: CELL-BUDGET FALLOUT of the fleet reformat (microblog caught it): the non-granular counter weighs newlines + indentation, so the three-line if and 120-column wraps pushed cells over 272. Measured with my snapshot before vs live after: lib +26, cells/spi +6, kit +28, tibia +15, regex +5, fiscal +2, html +2, x +5. USER DECISION (asked directly): split definitions, keep the budget and the layout. DONE: tibia, regex, html (org2), fiscal, x (microblog); compiler split lib + cells/spi to 0 new (keccak lanes_of as 2 rows; helpers hoisted; 6 tests split per target), --check clean on ganymede for lib/spiral and apps/cells/spi. Mistake: live-lib edits red for ~10 min (metrics annotation, xpath :& group split), fixed. OPEN: kit 28 (rig, TRAIN42); moon job-1794186278301-compiler-budget-split-tests runs the touched modules tests after the suite. FORMATTER BUG: pack63c is not idempotent: a second format pass changed schematron.spi (2 joined ifs, one with a \"\\\\\" literal) and builders.spi (an over-120 string split) that the first pass left. Next step: reproduce on a fixture and fix in the next pack.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_17 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 17u32, "2026-11-09T01:07Z", "compiler", "11-08 21:3x compiler: FORMATTER ENV HAZARD (tibia, comet): a pack63c build from the reviewed source (core-src 4521428f31abc748) reported tibia apps/arena/observer.spi would change (the `? c ?>` guard + block) when deps/The-Spiral-Language was missing; the same file is a no-op under pack63c on ganymede with the core package present. So format output can depend on whether |core- resolves, presumably through the sameParse/blockShapes guard. Next step: a fixture that formats a file with and without SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR and asserts identical output; until then, gates must fail closed when the core package is missing instead of formatting.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_18 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 18u32, "2026-11-09T03:59Z", "compiler", "11-09 00:4x compiler: the \"not idempotent\" finding re-read. (a) builders.spi: NOT idempotency but a MODE difference. The fleet pass ran format-corpus format, whose literal splitting is off unless --split-literals, while the format command lanes gates run splits over-120 literals with ^^ by default. So the fleet is not yet canonical under the format command. (b) schematron.spi: a real one-pass gap. A block re-laid because a line exceeded 120 goes through joinThenLines only, so an inline `? c ?> a` that wraps keeps its then on the condition line until a second pass meets the block AsWritten and splitThenLines splits it. FIX DRAFTED: kit drafts spiral FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT 5-split-then-on-relaid-blocks.kitdo (the LaidOut path also calls splitThenLines). (c) The comet env hazard did NOT reproduce: tibia observer.spi with no core package on ganymede gave format --check rc 0, so the comet diff likely came from its broken checkout, not the formatter; keep tibia fail-closed guard anyway. QUEUED: ganymede job-1794196704735-compiler-fleet-canonical-format-3 runs the installed format command to a fixed point (max 3 passes; core package + manifests present) over a fresh 1707-file snapshot; apply with the live==snapshot guard after. Next step: pack64 candidate = pack63c + program 5 (+ the env fixture), built on ganymede.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_19 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 19u32, "2026-11-09T05:43Z", "compiler", "11-09 01:1x compiler: CANONICAL PASS APPLIED (unstaged): ganymede job-1794196704735 ran the installed pack63c `format` command (which splits over-120 literals with ^^, unlike format-corpus) to a fixed point (pass 1 -> 2 changed, pass 3 none; core package + 2060 manifests present; 0 format errors; ~1 min/pass for 1707 files). Applied only where live == snapshot: 110 files (tibia 64, kit 28, spiral 14, alphabet 2, dice 1, x 1); 1 stale skipped (alphabet font-emit, org). Cell budget per file live vs snapshot: +2 total, both fixed: lib crypto.spi (hex_of_vec macro -> rust_hex_of_vec; --check + format --check clean on ganymede), x timeline_serve.spi (scroll_import split out; byte-identical JS; budget 0, format clean). Measurement traps: whole-repo counts pick up dist/ copies, and mix.bat silently drops findings when 110 long paths exceed cmd 8191 chars (use a short junction). Next step: pack64 (program 5) result on ganymede; then the fleet is canonical AND one-pass stable.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_20 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 20u32, "2026-11-09T05:52Z", "compiler", "11-09 01:5x compiler: budget-split TEST verdicts so far (moon, lib_gate): sm'.spi 245 of 247 rows agree. The 2 others are not mine: CONTROL A/B on the pre-edit snapshot (job-1794196004651) shows replace_agrees_on_c Pascal disagrees identically (Pascal console prints UTF-8 as mojibake, pre-existing), and show_floats Lean passed in both arms (the first run cells-failed = flake). The remaining 15 touched lib files (incl. crypto.spi hex_of_vec) are queued: job-1794203526984-compiler-split-tests-15files after the pack64 Windows pair. Note: pwsh -File flattens an array argument, so -Files must be passed in-process (& script -Files $files).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_21 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 21u32, "2026-11-09T06:10Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:1x compiler: PACK64 = pack63c + FORMATTER program 5 (split-then on re-laid blocks). Gate: (a) a schematron-shape fixture: pack63c NOT idempotent, pack64 splits in pass 1 and is idempotent; (b) ganymede job-1794203166457: pack64 format over the 1707-file canonical fleet is a NO-OP (tree 1b95045db9ce90ec unchanged, 0 format errors). Builds: Linux core 2be9257dfdeb6780 (ganymede), Windows pair 9011B777/B62490C34FD69070 (moon job-1794203222791). Both in oort (rid-win-x64, rid-linux-x64; round-trip equal). INSTALLED: box via install-pack -FromStore (first real store install, 31 files, live core c2db952e unstaged, backup compiler-installs pack64-20261109-020510), vultr (pair copy). PENDING: ganymede (waits for idle compiler), moon (the first copy hit two Zig compiles holding the core DLL: the in-use guard matched backslash paths only while those jobs used Local/spiral-bin/... forward slashes; moon stayed consistent on pack63c because the host DLL is identical; install-pack.ps1 guard fixed to normalize slashes; retry waits up to 30 min).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_22 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 22u32, "2026-11-09T06:39Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:4x compiler: PACKAGE CHECK under pack64 on europa (job-1794206284797, vultr mirror synced at head bf5cc30a + today's unstaged edits): --check passes (rc 0) for lib/spiral, apps/cells/spi, apps/kernel/src, apps/transformer and apps/spiral, i.e. every spiral package the two reformat passes and the cell-budget splits touched; about 11 s / 450 MB each. Test-block execution for the 15 split lib files is still running on moon (job-1794203526984).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_23 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 23u32, "2026-11-09T07:26Z", "compiler", "moon job-1794203526984-compiler-split-tests-15files (cell-budget splits in 15 lib files, live tree) finished exit 0 in 87 min: 244 test-block rows, 234 agree, 4 DISAGREE, 6 not run. Clean: crypto, doc_parse, doc_table, fin_vector, json_scan, metrics, pickler_derive, schematron, schematron_run, unicode, xpath, xsd_emit (37/37), xsd_regex. PENDING (not green): keccak Zig x3 (keccak512_matches_the_reference_digests, keccak512_pads_across_the_block_boundary, every_variant_comes_from_one_typed_sponge; 32s/31s/11s) and process split_args TypeScript (30.0s) -- run under 4 concurrent rustc on a 93% CPU moon, durations at the 30 s mark suggest timeouts, not semantics (the keccak split only re-rows lanes_of). keccak gleam/pascal not_run x6 = no runner. Recheck: keccak.spi + process.spi split vs HEAD control on quiet moon after TRAIN42.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_24 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 24u32, "2026-11-09T10:15Z", "compiler", "keccak recheck DONE on ganymede (10:04/10:10Z, load ~3.5, Cells gate, installed compiler): HEAD keccak.spi vs the cell-budget split version give IDENTICAL results: 6 discovered, 6 executed, 4 passed, the same 2 failing tests in both arms, failed_targets {} (no Zig failures). So the moon Zig DISAGREEs under 4 concurrent rustc were load timeouts, and the split is behaviour-neutral. The 2 failures that both arms share are pre-existing, independent of the split (moon listed them as a_digest_cannot_be_read_as_a_shorter_array and a_padding_without_a_domain_cannot_hash). Still pending: process split_args TypeScript (needs bun; moon after TRAIN42d).")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_25 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 25u32, "2026-11-09T10:55Z", "compiler", "11-09 10:5x compiler: FORMATTER REGRESSION FOUND + FIXED (draft 6-fails-clause-as-written.kitdo): FormatterSpacing.respaceLine treated the `-` in a test headers `fails ETY-TermError \"msg\"` clause as a binary operator and wrote `fails ETY - TermError \"msg\"`. Cells expectation parser (notebook.ex: one code token, then a quoted message) then lost the expectation, so the fails test ran as an ordinary test and FAILED. Hit: lib keccak.spis 2 fails tests (respelled in the 11-08 canonical pass and committed in bf5cc30a); they also lacked ///> lines, and the static block carried ///> zig (NoTargetOnStatic). Fixes (unstaged): keccak spelling restored + ///> c on both + static target dropped; program 6 keeps every gap after `fails` on a test-header line as written. pack74 = pack73b + program 6 (core 919ca84f, built on ganymede): the two-header probe file is unchanged by format; lib format --check flags keccak under the installed formatter but not under pack74. microblog also made Cells accept the spaced form (normalized), as a second guard. Separate finding: 8 lib files have drifted from canonical since 11-08 (bytes, convert, erlang_process, metrics, near, resultm, schematron, sm; 82 diff lines, all long raw $.. macro literals the formatter would split with backslash continuations). Not reformatting mid-day while lanes edit lib; proposing one quiet-time pass, checked for byte-identical emitted code per backend.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_26 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 26u32, "2026-11-09T10:56Z", "compiler", "keccak.spi with the restored fails spelling + ///> c targets + no static target: Cells gate on ganymede 6/6 PASS (was 4/6 in both HEAD and the split; the two fails tests now prove ETY-TermError / ETY-ConstraintError again). lib/spiral/keccak.spi unstaged on the box.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_27 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 27u32, "2026-11-09T13:44Z", "compiler", "process.spi recheck DONE on ganymede (bun 1.4.4 for TypeScript): the cell-budget split version and HEAD give IDENTICAL results, 18 executed, 10 passed, the same 8 failing, and split_args on TypeScript PASSES in both (the moon DISAGREE was a load timeout). The 8 shared failures are a pre-existing Linux bug, not the split: the Rust process tests spawn \"python\", and Linux nodes have only python3. Fix (unstaged, lib/spiral/process.spi): python_program () = \"python\" on Windows else \"python3\", used at all 8 spawn sites; gate of the fixed file running on ganymede. With keccak (6/6 after the fails-header fix) the 15-file split audit is closed: every split file is behaviour-identical to HEAD.")
inl note_of_formatter_pre_hopac_audit_28 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT", 28u32, "2026-11-09T13:51Z", "compiler", "process.spi python fix GATED on ganymede (Cells gate, in-mirror swap with EXIT trap; mirror restored 4861fa81): 18 executed, 18 passed, 0 failed (was 10/18 on Linux in both HEAD and the split). lib/spiral/process.spi unstaged on the box: python_program () helper + 8 spawn sites. Windows behaviour unchanged by construction (still \"python\" there); moon/box confirm on the next Windows gate.")
