inl note_of_kit_def_index_1 () = Note ("KIT-DEF-INDEX", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 1 (mental plot metrics). DoD: kit code index <roots> writes typed rows per definition (repo, file, name, kind, type parameters, call sites in and out of lib, lines) for kit, spiral lib and the other own repos; a second run diffs against the stored rows; under 60 s on europa for the org. MILESTONES: definition rows from the parser 90 m; call sites and lib-vs-app reuse 60 m; stored rounds and diff 30 m. NEXT STEP: reuse kit_style_measure package walk and the lint walk to emit one row per top-level definition. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: definition_kind union, reuse as a GADT indexed by in-lib or app, rows as records; no joined strings.")
inl note_of_kit_def_index_2 () = Note ("KIT-DEF-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-07T11:16Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: per main KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY n3, the index is searchable FTS-style (token postings over names, signatures and doc words, in the ai-memory manner), so kit code index answers find queries without a rescan; rows stay typed and the postings are derived from them.")
inl note_of_kit_def_index_3 () = Note ("KIT-DEF-INDEX", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:16Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:4x local rig, first slice (model only, unprobed; probe batch after TRAIN42e lands): src/rig_code_index/index.spi (HostFree + LibReferenced): definition_kind union (Inline, JoinPoint, Recursive, Union, Record, Test), definition_row record (repo, file, name, kind, line), kind_rules by top-level prefix (:~ ^, :~, :=, :| ^, :|, :==, :#; most specific first), definition_of parsing one line into an optional row (locals and opens are not rows), reuse GADT InLib n | InApps n with counted and generic (used by apps and more than once). 2 test blocks. Next: the walk (reuse the rig_style_measure package walk) emitting rows per repo, then call sites by name with lib-vs-app attribution, then the stored rounds and diff, then FTS postings per KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY n3.")
inl note_of_kit_def_index_4 () = Note ("KIT-DEF-INDEX", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate on ganymede, off-train (rig_code_index/index.spi 2/2; Cells run_notebook --gate, rust target, rig's probe layout). The first full off-train batch had shown this package half-proven (first test 'spiral not loaded'); a warm re-run passed every test, so that was a cold-start artifact of the first batch, not the package. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_def_index_5 () = Note ("KIT-DEF-INDEX", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:4x rig: parked on train:TRAIN44. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step is a walk, a store fed by a heartbeat, or wiring into shared kit code (agile next / todo scan / job host), which goes into TRAIN44 with its own regen and crate-gate proof.")
inl kit_modeling_topology () = Task ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", "typefeatureset topology per project trended toward a ceiling", Story, P1, D4, 50u32, Active, "", "kit,metrics,typefeatureset,code-map,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_modeling_topology () = Planning ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_1 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 1: how far fiscal or zeta is from its modeling ceiling. DoD: per project per day, typefeatureset use (gadt-case, existential, forall, phantom, nominal, indexed-union, reflection) per 1000 lines from the census rounds (GRANULAR-STATS), a ceiling estimate from the best package in each project, and a typed history file that is training-ready (one row per project per day, never rewritten). MILESTONES: per-project density from census rounds 90 m; ceiling estimate and distance 90 m; history rows plus trend line 60 m. NEXT STEP: extend kit_granular_rounds rows with a project label and lines, then compute density. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: feature union with reflection for names, density as a nominal per-kloc number, history rows typed.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_2 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T11:12Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, ROW SCHEMA agreed with fiscal (FISCAL-MODELING-CEILING-1-TABLE): two ceilings. Hand-written code: kit computes density itself from census rounds, ceiling = best package in the project (unchanged). Generated families: the schema defines the ceiling, so the project emits typed rows, one per family x construct: CeilingRow (project : string, family : string, construct : string, expressible : i32, typed : i32, day : string), construct from a closed word list (choice, enumeration, pattern, length-facet, digits-facet, bounds-facet, occurs, record, signature, schematron-rule, version), each row under a no-respell union header in a derived file target/ci-metrics/modeling-ceiling.spi (never committed). Percent and distance are DERIVED by kit, never stored. kit reads the rows by the CeilingRow marker like its other typed rows and models construct as a union, unknown words reported, never guessed. DoD amended: distance to ceiling uses the schema-defined ceiling where a project emits CeilingRow rows, else the best package.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_3 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 3u32, "2026-11-07T11:15Z", "main", "main 11-07 SCION / DELTADB / AI-MEMORY, mapped to this metric (the user asked whether they relate to a trainable modeling topology from the code's history). All three are external products: Scion = Anthropic's Git replacement (server-held authority, partial fetch); Zed's Delta(DB) = checkpoints plus incremental deltas that keep the agent conversation behind each change; akitaonrails/ai-memory = a git-versioned markdown wiki with SQLite FTS5 handover across agents. Fit: DeltaDB's idea is the core of 'trainable'. Write each daily typed row with the change set it measures plus lane, session id and transcript offset (proposed in KIT-TWO-HUBS n2), so metric deltas join to the decisions behind them. Today's git history can't, since commit messages are all 'tests'. Scion's idea suits the INDEX: one long-lived authority holding every repo parsed, answering reuse/duplicate queries (the same shape as compiler's COMPILER-LOAD-ALL). ai-memory: prior art to beat with typed records; worth taking its FTS-style cheap index over lib symbols and call sites. Reuse the compile/Cells memo content hashes (reach graph) as the cheap periodic input instead of re-parsing.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_4 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 4u32, "2026-11-07T11:16Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit: folding main n3 (scion/deltadb/ai-memory) into the DoD: each daily history row also carries its provenance: the change set it measured (repo head plus a hash of the dirty tree), the lane, the session id and the transcript offset that produced it (DeltaDB idea, see KIT-TWO-HUBS n2), so a later learner can join a density change to the work that caused it. Cheap input: reuse the memo reach hashes to skip unchanged packages. Fiscal row schema already sent (CeilingRow, note 2).")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_5 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 5u32, "2026-11-09T09:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:4x handoff from fiscal (the CeilingRow input agreed 11-07): fiscal's generated-family ceiling table is live on fiscal's pages under target/ci-metrics/modeling-ceiling.tsv (fiscal checked 11-09: HTTP 200, 318 rows, 45 families). Tab-separated with header: family, construct, expressible, typed, emitted; one row per family x construct; no project/day column (project = fiscal; day = the CI run date from the deploy commit / reports.md stamp). Republished on every push, red runs too; build.ps1 reads the previous published copy first, so a trend is one pull away. fiscal offers an explicit day column on request.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_6 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 06:2x fiscal: the day column is in (fiscal src/modeling_ceiling.spi 49F4D223, unstaged): modeling-ceiling.tsv columns family, construct, expressible, typed, emitted, day (UTC yyyy-mm-dd from FISCAL_BUILD_TIME), day LAST so positional readers keep working; proven on ganymede (both modeling_ceiling tests pass; sample row nfe_v2_00 signature 1 1 1 2026-11-09, 0 malformed). Reaches the pages on the user's next push. Reader keys on (project, day, family, construct), project = fiscal from the URL.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_7 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 7u32, "2026-11-09T19:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:0x local rig, READER CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_modeling_topology/topology.spi (pure, HostFree) over fiscal's modeling-ceiling.tsv as agreed (columns family, construct, expressible, typed, emitted, day; day LAST). ceiling_row { project; day; family; construct; expressible; typed } keyed (project, day, family, construct), project from the caller (the URL); row_of reads by position and returns HeaderRow, Row, or Malformed line (a non-number cell is Malformed, never a zero); per_mille = typed / expressible x 1000 summed over families; trend rows construct = one day_coverage per day in first-seen order, which is the \"trended toward a ceiling\" line per construct. Test: header, four rows over two days, the per-day coverage (500 then 1000 for signature), and a malformed number. NEXT: the IO half fetches the published TSV (current + the previous copy fiscal keeps) and prints the per-construct trend; a second project joins by publishing the same columns.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_8 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 8u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_modeling_topology_9 () = Note ("KIT-MODELING-TOPOLOGY", 9u32, "2026-11-09T23:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x rig, CHECKED THE READER AGAINST THE LIVE FILE and fixed a real mismatch (unstaged): the published table at fiscal's Pages (<owner>.github.io/fiscal/target/ci-metrics/modeling-ceiling.tsv, HTTP 200, 10,856 bytes, 320 lines = header + 318 rows + trailing) still has FIVE columns (family, construct, expressible, typed, emitted): fiscal's day column (49F4D223) has not reached the pages yet (it lands on the user's next push). The 11-09 reader required six fields, so every live row would have read as Malformed. Now row_of project run_day line accepts both shapes: six columns take their own day, five columns take run_day (the CI run date, fiscal's original contract); counted builds the row once for both. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (topology 1/1, re-gated after the last edit): header, the four 6-column rows and their per-day trend, a non-number cell malformed, and a live 5-column row (nfe_v2_00 choice 18 18 18) taking the run day. NEXT: the IO verb (fetch the TSV, keep the previous copy, print the per-construct trend), a new CLI verb, so TRAIN44.")
inl duplicate_code_shingles () = Task ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES", "duplicate code by normalized token shingles across repos", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,duplicates,code-map,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_duplicate_code_shingles () = Planning ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_duplicate_code_shingles_1 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 2, milestone 1 of DUPLICATE-CODE-TOOL. DoD: kit dup <roots> reports clone pairs whose token shingles match after identifier and literal normalization, across kit, lib and own repos, with a ranked list and a known-pairs baseline that only shrinks. MILESTONES: normalized tokenizer 60 m; shingle index and pair ranking 90 m; baseline and report 30 m. NEXT STEP: tokenize .spi with the lint scanner, replace identifiers by role tokens. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: token union, clone_pair record, verdict union New or Known.")
inl note_of_duplicate_code_shingles_2 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:5x local rig, milestone 1 (normalized tokenizer) as a pure model, unprobed (probe batch after TRAIN42e): src/rig_code_dup/dup.spi (HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0, census ratchet 0 regressions after dropping a tab literal the census reads as row encoding): token union (Ident, Literal, Keyword word, Operator symbol), tokens_of (identifiers -> I, numbers -> L, a fixed keyword list kept, every other symbol an operator), shingles size text (k-token windows over the normalized stream), overlap (shared windows). Tests: renamed copies normalize to the same tokens; a renamed copy shares every window, a different operator shares only the I = I window. Known gap: string literals are split into words rather than one L (the scanner has no string state yet). Next: the per-file index and pair ranking (milestone 2) over the rig_code_index walk.")
inl note_of_duplicate_code_shingles_3 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T23:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate on ganymede, off-train (rig_code_dup/dup.spi 2/2; Cells run_notebook --gate, rust target, rig's probe layout). The first full off-train batch had shown this package half-proven (first test 'spiral not loaded'); a warm re-run passed every test, so that was a cold-start artifact of the first batch, not the package. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_duplicate_code_shingles_4 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:4x rig: parked on train:TRAIN44. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step is a walk, a store fed by a heartbeat, or wiring into shared kit code (agile next / todo scan / job host), which goes into TRAIN44 with its own regen and crate-gate proof.")
inl duplicate_code_semantic () = Task ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC", "same logic under different names found by structure", TaskKind, P1, D4, 35u32, Planned, "", "kit,duplicates,code-map,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_duplicate_code_semantic () = Planning ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_duplicate_code_semantic_1 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 2, the sneaky kind: same logic, different names. DoD: alpha-renamed and reordered-binding clones are found by a structural hash of the parsed definition (binders numbered, commutative ops sorted, lib aliases resolved), with a precision sample of 20 hand-checked pairs before it feeds heals. MILESTONES: structural normal form 120 m; hash index across repos 60 m; precision sample and report 60 m. NEXT STEP: pick the Spiral parse output the compiler exposes for formatting and hash its tree. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: normal-form expression GADT, binder indices as a nominal, match evidence as an existential over the two sources.")
inl note_of_duplicate_code_semantic_2 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:38Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "PROTOTYPE (microblog, 11-09, read-only, CPU-light): token-level alpha-renaming census (no compiler parse yet): per top-level := / :~ definition, the body is tokenized, parameters, := locals and lambda binders are renumbered v1..vN, self-recursion becomes SELF, and groups of 25+ tokens with equal keys are clones. Over spiral/lib/spiral + kit/src .spi: 52 clone groups, 29 with different names (alpha-renamed). Hand-checked 10 pairs, 10 true clones: xml has_pair = has_attribute_pair; f32_grads softmax_of = probs_of; xsd_emit digits_text = xsd_regex count_text; bytes copy_from = sized_array put_from (monomorphic vs generic, keep generic); bench_kit show_i64/show_i32; am vec_for_each prime/double-prime; xml attribute_of = xpath table_lookup. Biggest: 23 kit definitions are the same two-guard 0/1 binding (bool_pair_binding) under 23 names across 14 contract/domain modules; 6 + 4 + 3 more mask/binding families. Not covered yet: commutative-op sorting, lib alias resolution, and the 20-pair precision sample (10 done). Script + output in the drafts store: kit/DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC/clones.awk, clones.txt. NEXT: rig decides whether the 23 bindings fold into one shared bool_pair_binding; the lib pairs (xml, f32_grads, xsd, bytes) are lib-lane heals via lib_land_window.")
inl note_of_duplicate_code_semantic_3 () = Note ("DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:53Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig decision on microblog's n2 census (52 clone groups, 29 under different names, 10/10 sampled pairs true clones): YES, fold the largest family (23 identical two-guard 0/1 bindings across 14 contract/domain modules) into one shared definition, after TRAIN43 snapshots and checked by that train's regen; rig applies it in the post-TRAIN43 change set with the other cross-package rewrites. The rest of the groups get a per-group decision then.")
inl kit_tfs_rewrite_detect () = Task ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", "detect code a typefeatureset rewrite would improve", Story, P1, D4, 70u32, Active, "", "kit,typefeatureset,heal,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_tfs_rewrite_detect () = Planning ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_tfs_rewrite_detect_1 () = Note ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 3. DoD: kit tfs candidates <roots> lists definitions where typefeatureset modeling fits better (string-tag matching, bool flag pairs, parallel arrays, number tables, untyped id strings crossing functions, host macros with a lib equivalent), old and new code alike, ranked by expected gain, and writes a typed queue that autonomous heals and lib or cross-repo moves consume without the user's approval, each move gated by tests and byte-compare. MILESTONES: detectors over census probes 120 m; ranked typed queue 60 m; move proposals into lib or the owning repo 60 m. NEXT STEP: start from census probes encoded-row, number-arm and string-concat, add string-tag compare. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: candidate GADT indexed by detector, gain score nominal, queue rows typed.")
inl note_of_kit_tfs_rewrite_detect_2 () = Note ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:29Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 21:2x local rig, FIRST RANKED CANDIDATES (the recorded next step: start from the census words). Installed census over kit/src (635 packages), score = 4 x encoded-row + 3 x number-arm + string-concat + std-string-use: 111 packages carry a signal. TOP: rig_machine_windows 91 (14 encoded rows, 32 concat; 357 lines), agile_todo_model 82 (37 concat, 45 std-string uses; 752 lines), rig_machine_watch 73 (10 rows, 30 concat), agile_note_model 50, agile_task_creation 41, rig_memory_model 35, rig_jobs 35, rig_do_program 35, agile_task_next 34 (8 number arms), binary_install_negative_probe 30 (10 number arms in a 33-line probe), rig_memory_save 29, rig_do_process 28. FOURTH DETECTOR measured (string-tag compare: a value compared to a lower-case word literal inside a guard, test lines excluded, a union belongs there): 133 sites in 78 packages; top rig_do_jobs 8, k3s_manifest 6, rig_delegate 5, agile_todo_model 5, rig_do_edit 5, rig_machine_watch_model 4. agile_todo_model shows on three detectors at once, so it is the first heal target. NEXT: the typed candidate queue (candidate GADT indexed by detector, gain score nominal) with string-tag compare as a census word, then move proposals.")
inl note_of_kit_tfs_rewrite_detect_3 () = Note ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:2x local rig, MILESTONE 2 CORE BUILT (ranked typed queue; unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_tfs_queue/queue.spi (pure, HostFree). detector EncodedRow | NumberArm | StringConcat | StdStringUse | StringTagCompare, each with its census weight (4, 3, 1, 1, and 2 for the new string-tag word) and its heal (RecordRows | UnionArms | LibStringCalls | TagUnion); signal { package; detector; count } is one census cell; ranked signals builds one candidate per package { detectors; score; heals } and orders by detector COUNT first, then weighted score (the recorded rule: agile_todo_model shows on three detectors, so it heals first), and a zero count is no signal. Test: a three-detector package (score 92) above a two-detector one (88), heals deduplicated in signal order, zero-count package absent. NEXT (M3): the IO half reads kit standards census rows into signals, writes the queue as rows the heal loop consumes, and adds string-tag-compare as a census word.")
inl note_of_kit_tfs_rewrite_detect_4 () = Note ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_tfs_rewrite_detect_5 () = Note ("KIT-TFS-REWRITE-DETECT", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, M3 FIRST HALF BUILT (unstaged): src/rig_tfs_queue/census.spi reads standards/census.spi rows CensusCount (\"package\", \"word\", count, lines) into signal rows for the five scored words (encoded-row, number-arm, string-concat, std-string-use, string-tag-compare; detector_of maps the spelling, every other census word scores nothing), so ranked runs on the real census. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (census 1/1): four scored rows out of six lines (the union header and host-block skipped), ranking by detectors then score (88 over 82 when both have two), and the count read as the first number. REAL QUEUE today (same rule over the 14,014-row census, a text pass): 110 packages with a signal; head = rig_machine_windows (3 detectors, 92), rig_machine_watch (3, 74), agile_task_next (3, 66), agile_note_model (3, 54), rig_jobs (3, 45), rig_memory_model and rig_do_program (3, 35), rig_table_query (3, 27). agile_todo_model is NOT at the head only because string-tag-compare is not a census word yet (its 5 sites are invisible to the census); adding that word is the remaining M3 step and edits the shared census code, so it rides TRAIN44 with COMMENT-LINT-GATE's word.")
inl kit_txn_review_pause () = Task ("KIT-TXN-REVIEW-PAUSE", "kit transactions pause for an LLM review before commit", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,saga,review,typefeatureset,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_txn_review_pause () = Planning ("KIT-TXN-REVIEW-PAUSE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_txn_review_pause_1 () = Note ("KIT-TXN-REVIEW-PAUSE", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 4. DoD: a kit CLI transaction is a typed saga (steps with compensations, bidirectional); a review step pauses it, writes a review request to a queue, and kit txn approve or compensate resumes it; an operating LLM can answer the queue autonomously; a CLI test drives pause, approve and compensate. MILESTONES: saga model with compensations 120 m; pause point, queue file and resume verbs 120 m. NEXT STEP: model the saga over an existing multi-step verb (agile split: add children, link parents, note) so compensation removes what was added. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: step GADT indexed by phase (Pending, Paused, Committed, Compensated), compensation as a paired existential, review verdict union.")
inl note_of_kit_txn_review_pause_2 () = Note ("KIT-TXN-REVIEW-PAUSE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:2x local rig, MILESTONE 1 CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_txn_saga/saga.spi (pure, HostFree), modelled over the item's own worked example (agile split: add child, link parent, note). saga_step AddChild | LinkParent | AddNote, each with an exact compensation (RemoveChild | UnlinkParent | RemoveNote) from undo_of; saga_phase Running | PausedForReview n | Committed | Compensated undos; advanced runs steps until the review point, approved resumes to Committed, rejected compensates the done steps NEWEST FIRST (bidirectional, per the DoD), and only a paused saga can be approved or rejected. Test covers pause after two steps, approval running the rest, rejection undoing in reverse, a saga with no review point, and rejecting an unpaused saga (no effect). TypeFeatureSet note: the phase is a plain union here; the step GADT indexed by phase from the plan stays for milestone 2, once the probe shows this shape compiles. NEXT (M2): the review queue file and the txn approve / txn compensate verbs.")
inl note_of_kit_txn_review_pause_3 () = Note ("KIT-TXN-REVIEW-PAUSE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_txn_review_pause_4 () = Note ("KIT-TXN-REVIEW-PAUSE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig: parked on train:TRAIN43. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step adds a CLI verb or wires into shared kit code (rig do / job host / job list / proxy fs / agile entry), and TRAIN43 snapshots the live tree about 19:30 local, so shared-code edits wait until it has snapshotted and go into a post-TRAIN43 train with their own regen and crate-gate proof.")
