inl kit_useless_abstraction () = Task ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", "score useless wrapper abstractions instead of a rigid rule", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,quality,granular,standards,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_useless_abstraction () = Planning ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_1 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 6, example :~ present (path : string) : bool = file_system.file_exists path. DoD: a score per definition, not a rule: pure forwards or renames with one call site, single-expression wrappers that add no type, name or invariant, and parameter re-orderings score high; wrappers that add a type, a nominal, a guard or several call sites score low; kit lists the top offenders per repo and the hook mentions a new high scorer. MILESTONES: forward and rename detection 60 m; scoring with call-site counts from KIT-DEF-INDEX 90 m; report and hook line 30 m. NEXT STEP: detect a body that is one call passing its parameters through unchanged. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: wrapper_shape union (Forward, Rename, Reorder, Adds), score nominal.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_2 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 2u32, "2026-11-07T11:15Z", "main", "main 11-07: the user's example is HEALED at its source (it was main's own, from the html_walk split, and existed TWICE: html/cli/html.spi:20 and html/html_walk/walk.spi:15). Lib file_system.file_exists is already a :~ join point, so the local wrapper added no type, guard or inlining barrier. Both definitions are removed and the 6 call sites call file_system.file_exists directly; the resulting 124-column guard chain is split one branch per line. proof: europa, html synced (head 549ebd90), build.ps1 -fast: all units + cli compile, cargo build, html --self-test pass, HTML-OK exit 0. Unstaged. Score hint for the detector: a forward to a definition that is already :~ is the clearest 'useless' case.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_3 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 3u32, "2026-11-07T16:47Z", "main", "main 11-07: linked to TFS-CONVERSION-LOSS-LAWS (the user's 'nothing can be fully transparent' thread). A pure forward is a conversion with no bending: its conversion_shape would be Iso with an identity body, which is exactly this detector's highest score. When both items land, the scorer can read the marker instead of re-deriving forward-ness from the body.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_4 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 4u32, "2026-11-07T20:03Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, MILESTONE 1 BUILT (unstaged): a forward-wrapper census word. kit_style_probes gains ForwardWrapper (probe drift, direction MayNotRise): a one-parameter definition whose whole body is one qualified call on one identifier, e.g. the user example :~ present (path : string) : bool = file_system.file_exists path. Rust regex has no backreferences, so the probe cannot prove the parameter passes through unchanged; it catches the common shape and is a measured signal, not a rule, per the user (score it, no rigid rule). Safe to install: the census ratchet treats a word missing from the stored baseline as count -1 (not ratcheted), so existing wrappers do not block edits until a baseline records the word. Tests: probes word list gains forward-wrapper; measure.spi asserts the user example matches and a wrapper with real logic (an && guard) does not. Node proof: probe job-1794081778285-kit-probe1107h. NEXT STEP: milestone 2, the score: join the probe hits with KIT-DEF-INDEX call-site counts (one caller plus pure forward scores high; a wrapper that adds a type, nominal or guard scores low). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: wrapper_shape union (Forward, Rename, Reorder, Adds), score nominal.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_5 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 5u32, "2026-11-07T22:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 18:3x kit, MILESTONE 2 BUILT (unstaged, rides TRAIN39): the score, without waiting on KIT-DEF-INDEX. New crate src/kit_wrapper_score (model.spi pure + wrappers.spi IO), routed as kit standards --wrappers <repo> [--top n] (census FlagWrappers). It parses one-line definitions (:~, :=, inl, with ^) whose parameters are plain (x : T) groups and classifies the body: wrapper_shape GADT Forward (a qualified call passing the parameters through in order, or x |> qualified.f), Rename (the same with an unqualified callee), Reorder (the same parameters in another order); anything else (a guard, a literal, a repeated argument, a tuple parameter) is not a wrapper. Call sites are a word-bounded count of the name over every .spi/.spir that git lists in the repo (qualified m.name counts), minus the definition. Score: Forward or Rename 3, Reorder 2; +2 with at most one caller, -1 with three or more; +1 when the callee is qualified (lib). The report lists the top n (default 20) as score path:line name shape callers=n -> callee and a summary files= wrappers= high= (score 5 or more); exit 0, a score not a rule (user 11-07). Tests: the user example present scores 6 with one caller; a guard and a duplicated argument are not wrappers; references are word-bounded. Proof pending: node probe n. NEXT STEP: milestone 3 after proof: run it over kit, x and html for the first top lists, and have the edit hook mention a NEW high scorer in the text just added.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_6 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 6u32, "2026-11-07T23:34Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 19:4x kit: waits on install: TRAIN39 (built and proven on the node or pending its probe; the box still runs TRAIN33). Close or continue from the post-install check.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_7 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 7u32, "2026-11-07T23:40Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 19:4x kit: MILESTONE 3 PLAN, no new hook code needed. The edit hook (kit-style-check) already runs the installed census ratchet on the edited package, and milestone 1 added the forward-wrapper census word (direction MayNotRise). Today the stored baseline has no forward-wrapper row, so the word reads -1 and is not ratcheted. After TRAIN39 installs: (1) a sanctioned baseline merge records forward-wrapper counts per package (old code newly detected, allowed by the baselines-only-shrink rule); (2) from then on the hook names a package whose forward-wrapper count rises in the text just added, which is the new-high-scorer mention the DoD asks for; (3) kit standards --wrappers <repo> gives the ranked list for the top-offender report. Proven parts: the wrappers model notebook 2/2 (probe n), census flag test (probe p). waits on install: TRAIN39")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_8 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 8u32, "2026-11-08T00:43Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:5x kit: NOT in TRAIN39. The wrappers score is built and proven (model notebook 2/2), but even after a model/IO split (kit_wrapper_score 709 linked to kit_wrapper_score_model) the model half generates 1227 lines. Both crates are parked in the kit drafts store under TRAIN40-layers-wrappers with the census routing removed. The forward-wrapper census word (milestone 1) is unaffected and stays in TRAIN39. NEXT STEP: cut the model (definition_rest unrolls a 5-start fold; shape_of and uses_in carry several closures), re-wire, and probe. waits on install: TRAIN40")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_9 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 9u32, "2026-11-08T12:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 08:1x rig: the wrappers model is cut under the gate by reading the generated Rust per function. shape_of was 356 of 1056 lines because a failed guard on the piped arm copied the whole next arm into each failing branch; that arm is now its own join point (called_shape) and the shared Forward/Rename choice is passed_shape. Model 1056 to 847 lines. Node probe job-1794139008804-kit-probe1108a: model notebook 2/2 pass, 10 TRAIN40 packages 0 over 1000, kit_wrapper_score 827 linked. Census routing re-wired; rides TRAIN40, launched 08:09 as job-1794139763840-kit-TRAIN40-node. waits on install: TRAIN40")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_10 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 10u32, "2026-11-08T14:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 11:0x rig, post-install check with the TRAIN40 kit (kit.exe 6C4F076B, installed 10:52:57, pack61b core 65DEE79C; node notebooks 66/66 on candidate D5D22429). The wrappers census is installed: kit standards --wrappers src\\kit_path_first gives wrappers files=3 wrappers=0 high=0. NEXT STEP: milestone 3, a sanctioned baseline merge that records forward-wrapper counts per package, so the edit hook starts ratcheting them.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_11 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 11u32, "2026-11-09T13:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:1x local rig, TOP-OFFENDER REPORT (installed kit standards --wrappers src --top 12, 5.3 s): files=1190 wrappers=144 high=9. Score 6 (pure forward, one caller): agile_sprint_rows/rows.spi:13 fate_word -> reflection.union_to_string; agile_todo_scan/todo_scan.spi:42 path_is_directory -> file_system.directory_exists and :43 path_is_file -> file_system.file_exists (the user's 11-07 example shape exactly); rig_agile_mutation/agile_mutation.spi:83 state_lock_taken -> rig_agile_lock.lock.lock_taken; rig_bundle_retention/series.spi:33 ascii_digits -> sm'.all_digits; rig_coordinator_table/decision.spi:36 decision_word -> reflection.union_to_string. Score 5 (one-caller renames): agile_note_listing segments_of, rig_table_query listed_line, rust_std_fs original_body. Score 4 (two callers): agile_activity_rows status_of_word, command_spec_domain direct_verb_usage, rig_do_facts query_word. Heal plan: the 9 high ones are one-line removals with their single call site retargeted, per package, each with its package's notebook probe; agile_todo_scan and rig_agile_mutation sit near the 1000-line gate, so their heal must not grow them (removing a forward is neutral or shrinks). Milestone 3 (sanctioned forward-wrapper baseline so the hook ratchets) still open: it needs a census re-measure, not a hand edit (baselines only shrink).")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_12 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 12u32, "2026-11-09T13:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:2x local rig, HEALED two score-6 forwards (unprobed; in the post-train probe batch): rig_bundle_retention/series.spi ascii_digits (its one caller now calls sm'.all_digits directly) and agile_sprint_rows/rows.spi fate_word (its one caller now binds reflection.union_to_string item.fate). Left on purpose: rig_coordinator_table decision_word (its only caller is its own test: an API question, not a pure forward), agile_todo_scan path_is_file/path_is_directory and rig_agile_mutation state_lock_taken (crates near the 1000-line gate: heal with a size check in a train), rig_bundle_retention and the score-5 renames next.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_13 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 13u32, "2026-11-09T15:14Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 12:2x local rig, ROUND 2 HEALED (unstaged; notebooks queued): agile_todo_scan path_is_directory and path_is_file (callers now call file_system.directory_exists / file_exists), rig_agile_mutation state_lock_taken (state_lock_held calls rig_agile_lock.lock.lock_taken), rig_table_query listed_line (its one caller in rig_table_diff/diff.spi uses appended, already in scope). Re-score: wrappers 144 -> 139, high 9 -> 4; ratchet ok. The 4 left are deliberate: decision_word (only caller is its test), and two FALSE POSITIVES the scorer should learn: agile_note_listing segments_of is a linked-unit export name (export \"rig_agile_segments_of\" is its caller; the boundary needs the name), and rust_std_fs original_body constructs the nominal original_text (it adds a type, the DoD's low-score case). NEXT STEP: teach the shape classifier those two (an export site is not a call; a body that applies a nominal constructor is Adds), then milestone 3 (sanctioned forward-wrapper baseline).")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_14 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 14u32, "2026-11-09T16:31Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 16:3x CROSS-REPO BREAK healed: lib file_system.spi lost the alias read_dir_names (edited 11:45 local, outside lib_land_window: no undo dir), but html/html_walk/walk.spi:29 and alphabet/apps/documents/documents.spi:287 still called it. org2 repointed both to read_directory_names (identical signature; unstaged; backups drafts\\i574n.github\\READ-DIR-NAMES-ALIAS). Rule for the remaining rounds: before deleting a lib definition, plain-grep its name across every repo (git grep misses untracked), because the land window's consumer check compiles only apps/spiral.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_15 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 15u32, "2026-11-09T16:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 16:3x CORRECTION to note 14: the read_dir_names removal was NOT this item's work (rig confirms no edits under spiral/lib today; its rounds touched kit packages only). The lib edit came from another lane at 15:45Z; the html/alphabet callers are repointed regardless. Note 14's grep rule still stands for any lib definition removal.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_16 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 16u32, "2026-11-09T17:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:2x PROOF for the two repointed callers (read_dir_names -> read_directory_names): SpiralCompiler --check with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin (the core package's parent; pointing it at the app dir leaves |core- unresolved): \"checked package .../html/html_walk\" rc=0 and \"checked package .../alphabet/apps/documents\" rc=0 (parse + type inference). An earlier \"exit 0\" for the same checks was a bash $? read after $(basename ...) in the same echo (fail-open; memory bash-dollar-question-after-substitution).")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_17 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 17u32, "2026-11-09T18:21Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:2x tibia (help pool): FIELD DATA for the scorer, from tibia (owned, so healed in place). (1) kit standards --census ../tibia reports no forward-wrapper hits because it finds no package.spiproj (tibia, like regex, uses spiral.toml); the probe never sees those repos, so worth fixing. (2) A direct scan of the probe's shape (one-param body = one qualified call on the param) over tibia src+apps found 8. LOW (keep, they add something): quantity.spi hp/ms/tile_count/gp (each adds a phantom unit type, units::amount hitpoints etc.): a TYPE-ADDING forward the scorer must not flag; competitor.spi finish -> gauge::finish_reporting_parity (~20 call sites, a much shorter name). HIGH (healed, unstaged): summon.spi order_count = am'::length (1 call site, inlined); bc_intick.spi student_of = bc_eval::student_tactic (2 sites in-module, inlined); bc_run.spi pair_count = listm::length (5 sites in 5 modules, inlined; every site got SHORTER). Gate: ganymede job-1794248465186-tibia-forwards. Scoring lessons: a forward whose return type differs from the callee's (a phantom/nominal) = Adds; call-site count alone mislabels pair_count (5 sites but a pure rename that is longer than its body).")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_18 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 18u32, "2026-11-09T18:42Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:4x tibia: CORRECTION to note 17, from the gate (ganymede job-1794248465186-tibia-forwards). Inlining pair_count BROKE type inference: ETY-ValueRestriction (\"Metavars that are not part of the enclosing function's signature are not allowed\") at every site where the length feeds `++#?` (bc_run:157, bc_dagger:44, bc_intick:37). listm::length is generic in its integer type, and pair_count's declared `: i32` is what fixed it. So pair_count was NOT a pure rename: it PINS A TYPE, exactly the low-score Adds case. Restored (definition + 5 call sites). order_count and bc_intick's student_of stayed inlined (no errors there). SCORER LESSON, stronger than note 17's: a forward whose declared return type is narrower than the callee's inferred/generic type is an Adds (type pinning), even when the names alone look like a rename; the scorer has to compare declared vs callee types, not just the body shape. Re-gate: job tibia-forwards2. The shadow heal (KIT-OPEN-SHADOW-LINT) gated green (job tibia-shadow: fmt same, --check clean, budget at the 67 baseline).")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_19 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 19u32, "2026-11-09T18:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:0x rig, SCORER RULES to add (from tibia notes 17-18 and rig's round 2): a forward is NOT useless (score it as Adds) when (a) its declared parameter or return type narrows the callee's generic or inferred type (tibia: pair_count = listm::length with : i32 pins the integer; inlining it broke inference with ETY-ValueRestriction), (b) it is a linked-unit export name, (c) it applies a nominal constructor, or (d) it wraps a phantom-type value; and the census must also walk spiral.toml repos (tibia, regex), which it skips today. rig's 6 heals of 11-09 were re-checked against (a): each returns bool or string from a concretely typed callee, so none pinned a generic.")
inl note_of_kit_useless_abstraction_20 () = Note ("KIT-USELESS-ABSTRACTION", 20u32, "2026-11-09T19:12Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:0x tibia: re-gate GREEN after restoring pair_count (ganymede job-1794249725545-tibia-forwards2): the 6 touched files are formatter-unchanged, --check is clean (the ETY-ValueRestriction lines are gone), and over_budget is at the 67 baseline. Final tibia outcome: 2 useless forwards removed (summon order_count, bc_intick student_of), 1 kept as a type-pinning forward (bc_run pair_count : i32), 5 kept as type-adding or many-site forwards (quantity hp/ms/tile_count/gp, competitor finish). Unstaged.")
inl kit_number_drift () = Task ("KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT", "find hardcoded number literals better modeled with types", TaskKind, P2, D2, 45u32, Planned, "", "kit,quality,typefeatureset,standards,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_number_drift () = Planning ("KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_number_drift_1 () = Note ("KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 7, example lib iggy.spi literal constants. DoD: an org-wide census row counts magic numbers (repeated literals, hex frames, offsets and sizes outside a named definition) per package, with a candidate list for typed modeling (nominal sizes, frame GADTs); the baseline only shrinks. MILESTONES: literal probe with context 60 m; candidate list and baseline 60 m. NEXT STEP: extend kit_style_probes with a literal-number probe that skips 0, 1 and test blocks. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: literal_kind union, candidate rows typed.")
inl note_of_kit_number_drift_2 () = Note ("KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:23Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 14:2x microblog (help pool), FIRST CENSUS to size the baseline (one gawk pass over kit/src/*.spi, test blocks (:# and ///>) and string literals skipped, literals of 3+ digits or hex, excluding 100 and 1000, counted per package, reported when one value repeats >= 3 times): 46 packages, 89 repeated values, 862 uses. TOP: agile_task_next 504 uses / 26 values (180 x88), but ranking.spi:322 onward is a replay FIXTURE TABLE inside an ordinary definition, i.e. data. The probe must exempt data-literal definitions the way Cells' CellBudgetRuled.data_literal? does, or this one package swamps the baseline. Real candidates for typed modeling: rust_std_process 65535 x16 (an exit/port mask, a nominal u16 width), state_receipt_codec_model 18446744073709551615 x13 (u64 max as a sentinel, better an option or a 'none' case), toolchain_argument_domain 1073741823 x12 (2^30 - 1 cap, a named limit), 1024 across cold_proof_domain x17, agile_state_runtime x26, rig_coverage_prune x12, evidence_currentness_domain x10 and rig_cold_rebuild_matrix x8 (KiB/MiB scaling, a 'bytes' nominal with kib/mib constructors), 60000 in process_batch_plan_domain x8 and rig_machine_windows x4 (ms per minute, a duration type), 512 in rig_bundle_manifest x13. Census script: microblog scratchpad numbers.awk. next: the literal probe in kit_style_probes with data-literal and test-block exemptions; baseline per package from it.")
inl note_of_kit_number_drift_3 () = Note ("KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:49Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 14:5x microblog (help pool), PROBE DRAFT (drafts store kit/KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT, probes.spi + measure.spi with .base copies, sha CFAB871961F5/456389FBC742, NOT in the kit tree, rig applies). Typed as one more drift case: probe side gains MagicNumber :: probe drift, direction MayNotRise, word magic-number, pattern (^|[^\\w.])(\\d{3,}|0x[0-9A-Fa-f]+)(u8|u16|u32|u64|i8|i16|i32|i64|f32|f64)\\b (typed literals only, so strings and identifiers like x1000i32 and decimals like 2.500f64 do not count; 0 and 1 never match). each_probe gains the step; the words test gains magic-number; measure.spi's regex test gains a 4-line sample expecting 2 (checked with grep -P: 2). Sizing over kit/src: 1603 matching lines; agile_task_next 320 (the replay fixture table), rig_machine_windows 74, rig_jobs 50, agile_claim_model 28, state_receipt_codec_model 27. A package with no census row is skipped by the baseline (None => kept), so the new word lands without a ratchet red; rows appear on the next census regen and only shrink after. Known gap vs the DoD: matching_lines counts test-block lines too (true for every probe), so test literals sit in the baseline; exempting data-literal definitions is left for later. Not compiled (no box compute while the user is present); rig proves it with the rig_style_probes and rig_style_measure notebooks.")
inl note_of_kit_number_drift_4 () = Note ("KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:54Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig: microblog's MagicNumber probe draft (n3; drafts kit/KIT-NUMBER-DRIFT, probes.spi + measure.spi with .base copies) is accepted; applied after TRAIN43 snapshots, so its census change rides a train of its own with a node compile (it is uncompiled; the box takes no compute while the user is present).")
inl kit_land_harden () = Task ("KIT-LAND-HARDEN", "multi-lane lib lands that never stumble on live drafts", Story, P0, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,lib,landing,resilience,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_land_harden () = Planning ("KIT-LAND-HARDEN", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_land_harden_1 () = Note ("KIT-LAND-HARDEN", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 8: i thought kit is smart enough to handle that by now. DoD: a land takes a content-hashed snapshot of every draft at start and refuses if a draft or its base changes mid-land; compiler pins are fresh per run (KIT-TRAIN-STALE-PIN); lock waits name the holder and inherit for child writes (done 11-06); a land queue serializes lanes per touched file set; a rehearsal of 3 lanes landing overlapping lib files in one window passes. MILESTONES: draft snapshot and base check 90 m; per-file-set land queue 90 m; 3-lane rehearsal 60 m. NEXT STEP: list the fragile cases from this week lands (live-written drafts, stale pins, lock waits) with their logs. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: land phase GADT, draft snapshot record with hash nominal, conflict verdict union.")
inl note_of_kit_land_harden_2 () = Note ("KIT-LAND-HARDEN", 2u32, "2026-11-09T05:47Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 02:1x rig, fragile cases from this week (the NEXT STEP list), tonight's three: (1) BASE MOVED MID-RUN: compiler applied the pack63c reformat to 541 kit .spi files at about 20:00 while rig was syncing a mirror and editing the same tree; only remote.ps1 digests (REMOTE-SYNC-OK ... digest) and per-file archives kept the two apart, and compiler re-formatted 5 rig-touched files from their current content to avoid overwriting WIP. (2) FILES REWRITTEN UNDER AN EDITOR: at 00:5x several rig files (rust_std_env model, rig_jobs stop_cli, rig_job_create create) changed on disk between rig's read and its next edit (formatter or a user staging), caught only because the edit tool compares; a land without a pre-write hash check would have clobbered them. (3) A STALE SNAPSHOT VERIFIED THE WRONG TREE: rig's TRAIN42 regen check ran on a mirror synced before later edits, so it had to be stopped and re-synced twice (rig-r3b1108b, rig-r3b1108c). All three are the same DoD clause: snapshot every input by content hash at start, and refuse or re-snapshot when a draft or its base changes before the write. The split verb refused (already-small at exactly 240 m), so the three milestones stay in this item.")
inl note_of_kit_land_harden_3 () = Note ("KIT-LAND-HARDEN", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:38Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 fiscal adds 4 fragile cases from today's 7 lib lands (6 from proven closes), each with what saved it: (4) LIB MOVED BETWEEN PROOF AND LAND: microblog's tlds.spi landed between fiscal's moon-copy sync and its proof; then the box lib moved AGAIN between proof 8 and the box land (digest 63F6E0FE -> A61580D1 -> landed 138AC55B). Saved by lib_land_window's ProvenLog digest check (non-exact -> rerun fast checks on the box). Want: the land queue records the box lib digest at proof start and refuses or re-proves on change, instead of silently paying box CPU. (5) DRAFT NOT BYTE-EXACT AFTER NODE WORK: a PowerShell here-string dropped a draft's final newline; the proof job ran the round trip first, so it failed in 28 s, not after document_test. Want: 'kit lib draft check' = lib_roundtrip + cell budget + parse, BEFORE submitting a proof. (6) ROUND TRIP AND BUDGET PASS A NON-PARSING BLOCK: a record update on a call ({ f x ?| ... }) round-tripped canonical and passed the counter, then the gate died at ParserErrors (the block is dropped from the module). Want: the draft check includes a parse (spiral --check on the one file) since format leaves unparsable blocks as-is. (7) STOPPING A GATE SKIPS ITS RESTORE: 'kit job stop' on a moon gate that swapped a draft into a shared proof tree skipped the script's finally, leaving the draft in the tree; caught only by a hash check before the next run. Want: proof trees are per-run copies (or the land queue re-verifies the tree digest before each proof). Recipe that worked for every case: moon -PrivateLib proof on a byte-identical copy (+ siblings dice lib/contract, alphabet documents, SPIRAL_CELLS_SKIP_CLI_EXPORT=1), digest both sides immediately before proof and before land, box -ProvenLog = copy only. Memory: lib-land-proof-on-node-copy-on-box.")
inl kit_repo_graph () = Task ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", "org repo dependency graph that flags upward references", Story, P1, D3, 40u32, Active, "", "kit,repos,dependencies,ci,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_repo_graph () = Planning ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_repo_graph_1 () = Note ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "user 11-07 via main point 9: spiral should not reference x, tibia etc. without losing what the pipelines achieved. DoD: kit repo graph <roots> derives who references whom (paths, packages, scripts, CI workflows) across own repos, prints the graph, and flags references from base repos (spiral, lib) up into product repos with the file and line; main owns the org CI design (TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET, ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME), so each flagged edge gets a proposed home agreed with main. MILESTONES: reference extraction 90 m; layering rules and flags 60 m; report and proposals 30 m. NEXT STEP: grep spiral for x, tibia, fiscal and kit path references as the first edge list. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: repo layer union (Base, Tool, Product), edge record, verdict union Allowed or Upward.")
inl note_of_kit_repo_graph_2 () = Note ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:3x local rig, FIRST EDGE LIST (the recorded next step: rg over spiral, excluding deps/target/_build/.git, for home/git/<repo> and ../<repo> references to x, tibia, fiscal, kit, rig, microblog, html, regex, dice, alphabet): 27 hits in 9 files. UPWARD (base -> tool/product): (1) apps/compiler/scripts/machine-watch.ps1:3 runs ../../../../kit/kit.exe (spiral needs the tool at runtime) -> proposed home: the watch belongs to kit/rig (or calls rig from PATH, never a sibling path). (2) apps/compiler/scripts/formatter/candidate-gate.ps1:22-31 reads dice, alphabet and kit HEAD to gate the formatter on consumers, and (3) apps/compiler/scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1:3 lists spiral, kit, dice, alphabet, x, tibia -> both are ORG-level gates: proposed home i574n.github org tooling (org-tooling-in-dot-github), with spiral keeping only a hook to call them. PERSONAL PATHS in a public tree (repos-never-name-infra rule): apps/zed/src/server.rs:305-346 test fixtures use C:\\home\\git\\kit paths, apps/zed/README.md:172 names C:\\home\\git\\kit, apps/cells/test/spiral/cells/mounts_name_test.exs:7 uses C:/home/git/tibia/... -> neutral fixture paths (C:/work/app). SAME LAYER (allowed): apps/cells document_test.exs and directives_test.exs reach ../dice and ../alphabet, the lib siblings Cells mounts. Next: the same pass over lib/spiral (expect 0) and over kit -> products, then the layer union (Base: spiral+lib+dice+alphabet; Tool: rig; Product: x, tibia, fiscal, html, regex, microblog) as code (repo graph verb), each upward edge sent to its owner with the proposed home (compiler owns apps/compiler scripts, microblog owns Cells tests, zed is compiler's).")
inl note_of_kit_repo_graph_3 () = Note ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:14Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:3x local rig, SECOND PASS kit -> others (src .spi + scripts + compiler-contracts): 24 hits, 0 UPWARD: every kit -> spiral edge is downward (tool uses base: init/publish/workflow/release-train/workspace.ps1 resolve ../../spiral core.ps1, cells and the compiler bundle), and ../x hits are path-escape fixtures (rig_evidence, rig_mirror_unpack, rig_schedule, rig_proof_scope_manifests). PERSONAL PATHS to neutralize in kit: scripts/release-acceptance.ps1:30-138 hard-codes C:/home/git/{kit,i574n.github,spiral} and the backlog root (should take -Repos/-Backlog with no default), src/rig_machine_windows/window_model.spi:168 help text e.g. C:/home/git/spiral/lib and :422-434 test paths (neutral C:/work/lib). Layer table so far: spiral = Base with 3 upward edges (machine-watch, candidate-gate, lib-usage-census) + 3 personal-path fixtures; rig = Tool, clean direction, 2 personal-path sites. Next: lib/spiral, then the products' own deps (x, tibia, fiscal, html via deps/ junctions are downward by construction), then the repo graph verb.")
inl note_of_kit_repo_graph_4 () = Note ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", 4u32, "2026-11-09T11:55Z", "tibia", "11-09 08:0x tibia (third pass, offered by rig; tibia's ready pool was empty). Same rg pass as notes 2-3 (patterns home/git/<repo>, ../<repo> for x, tibia, fiscal, kit, rig, microblog, html, regex, dice, alphabet, plus C:\\home and kit.exe/rig.exe calls; deps/target/_build ignored). LIB/SPIRAL (Base): 0 UPWARD edges (rig expected 0: confirmed). 1 PERSONAL-PATH fixture: lib/spiral/file_system.spi:1738 test delete_target_is_protected \"C:\\\\home\\\\git\\\\kit\\\\.cache\\\\x\" -> proposed neutral C:\\\\work\\\\app\\\\.cache\\\\x (the case asserts an ordinary deep path is NOT protected, so any non-system path keeps the meaning). PRODUCTS: x 0, fiscal 0, html 0, regex 0 (code and md). dice: 1 SAME-REPO edge, dice/contract/dice_contract.spi -> ../dice (self, allowed). alphabet: 3 SAME-REPO edges, apps/documents/documents.{spi,rs} -> ../alphabet (self, allowed). tibia: 5 Product -> Tool runtime calls of kit.exe (allowed direction; tool resolution = Get-Command kit, then %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\kit\\\\bin\\\\kit.exe). 3 of them carried a PERSONAL-PATH fallback 'C:\\\\home\\\\git\\\\kit\\\\kit.exe' (scripts/score.ps1:11, live/block.ps1:14, live/arena-summary.ps1:4): HEALED by tibia just now (fallback dropped; LOCALAPPDATA kit verified present on the box; 3 scripts parse clean; unstaged). tibia now has 0 C:\\\\home\\\\git references in tracked code. LAYER TABLE (rig's union): Base spiral = 3 upward + 3 personal fixtures (note 2); Base lib = 0 upward + 1 personal fixture; Tool rig = clean + 2 personal sites (note 3); Products x/tibia/fiscal/html/regex/dice/alphabet = 0 upward (only self and Product -> Tool edges), 0 personal after the tibia heal. Remaining for the DoD: the repo-graph verb itself (rig, after TRAIN43) and the 4 proposed homes agreed with org.")
inl note_of_kit_repo_graph_5 () = Note ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", 5u32, "2026-11-09T15:42Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:3x local rig, KIT SIDE HEALED (unstaged): every personal path in kit's Spiral sources and scripts is gone (rg over src/**/*.spi, scripts, compiler-contracts and spec: 0 hits for C:\\home\\git or the user profile). (1) scripts/release-acceptance.ps1 no longer copies the user's real memory directory (a personal-data path in a public tree) as test input: it builds a two-file fixture (fixture.md + MEMORY.md; the forget/restore check only needs the index before the save), and every repo path comes from a new mandatory -GitRoot (nothing calls the script, it runs by hand). (2) compiler-contracts test-window-holder, test-window-holder-detail and test-read-verb default to $PSScriptRoot-relative kit.exe paths. (3) Test fixtures neutralized with their meaning kept: agile_claim_cli anchored path, rig_delete_guard cache path (C:\\work\\app\\.cache\\x: still an ordinary deep path), rig_machine_windows tree tests. FOUND A BUG doing (3): this morning's neutralization of rig_machine_windows changed lib to C:/work/repo/lib but missed the backslash spelling of the reader's path, so a_tree_write_waits_for_readers... would have FAILED (\"a held read below\" was no longer below); fixed to C:\\work\\repo\\lib\\spiral (the notebook is in the probe batch). LEFT for other lanes (not edited): spiral's 3 upward edges (apps/compiler machine-watch.ps1 calling ../../../../kit/kit.exe; formatter candidate-gate and lib-usage-census reading dice/alphabet/kit/x/tibia: proposed home = org tooling in i574n.github) and the lib/spiral/file_system.spi:1738 fixture path: compiler's call. NEXT STEP: the graph tool itself (repo layer table + edge scan as a kit verb) from these three passes.")
inl note_of_kit_repo_graph_6 () = Note ("KIT-REPO-GRAPH", 6u32, "2026-11-09T16:03Z", "compiler", "11-09 compiler: spiral side DONE (unstaged, nothing staged). (1) apps/compiler/scripts/machine-watch.ps1 RETIRED: the hourly task kit-machine-watch-hourly already runs the native kit machine watch from %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin, no file in any repo referenced the .ps1 (HEAD keeps it). (2) formatter/candidate-gate.ps1 names no sibling repo: new -Consumers name=<repo dir>:<path>[,<path>...] (repeatable per name; git archive HEAD, .spi only, re-extracted every run, so the old stale kit cache is gone) and -ComplaintCorpus (default dice, skipped when absent). Proven equal to the old extraction: dice 6 files, kit 1160 (= ls-tree), dice.spi byte-identical to git show. Old default = -Consumers dice=<git>\\dice:lib/dice.spi,ui/src/model/near/rpc.spi,ui/src/model/near/nearblocks.spi,ui/src/components/content.spi,ui/src/components/menu_tabs.spi dice=<git>\\alphabet:apps/documents/documents.spi kit=<git>\\kit:src. parser-corpus-gate.ps1 likewise: -ConsumerRepos <dir>... (old list tibia x dice alphabet kit). (3) lib-usage-census.ps1 MOVED to i574n.github/scripts (repo names under $gitRoot, the crate-gate-all.ps1 convention; body identical; no new file net). (4) lib/spiral/file_system.spi fixture -> C:\\work\\app\\.cache\\x (still !- unprotected). ALSO swept spiral for personal paths: 7 self-references in apps/compiler/scripts and apps/cells/spi now $PSScriptRoot-relative (parse 0, every resolved path exists; daemon_collision_proofs second spelling derived, byte-identical to the old literal), cells README example neutral. REMAINING personal paths in spiral = test fixtures needing a test run: apps/cells/test/.../compiler_daemon_test.exs (4 lines), mounts_name_test.exs (2), apps/zed (README 5, server.rs 14).")
