inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:06Z", "fiscal", "11-07 fiscal: the lib side of the regex reuse (FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP's proposal, once main decides which side absorbs which). DoD: lib xsd_regex re-expressed over the canonical engine with its public API unchanged for xsd_emit / xpath_eval / generated units / fiscal corpus; every xsd_regex test green; the cross-engine agreement on fiscal's pinned pattern corpus shows 0 disagreements; the generator identity arm 0 differing on the node; landed via lib_land_window. Splits by layer if over 120 min (engine, parser, tables). TYPEFEATURES: none new. Deps: FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP, main's decision, REGEX-XSD parity.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 2u32, "2026-11-07T11:12Z", "fiscal", "11-07 unblocked in part: main decided option (ii) and takes the regex side (moving regex's core into lib through land windows). The pair map and the API to keep are on FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP (Done; drafts fiscal\\FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP\\map.txt). Start when the core is in lib; gate = regex agreement.spi vs lib xsd_regex on fiscal's pinned corpus, then the node identity arm 0 differing.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:45Z", "fiscal", "NEXT: when main reports regex's core landed in lib, re-express xsd_regex's nullability layer first (same design and names on both sides, map layer 4), run the ouroboros agreement on fiscal's pinned corpus, then the derivative and parser layers.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 4u32, "2026-11-09T07:26Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 STARTED (premise re-checked: regex's core IS in lib: regex_syntax, regex_charset, regex_nullable, regex_derivative, regex_language). LAYER 4 (nullability) DRAFT: kit drafts spiral FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER v1 xsd_regex.spi 6BF9F440 over live DB60F33F (1165 -> 1102 lines). Adds to_re (rx -> regex_syntax::re: RxNone Nothing, RxEps Epsilon, RxClass Set of a normalized char_set (complemented when negated), Seq, Alt, Star, RxRepeat Repeat with Bounded high: xsd_regex never builds an unbounded RxRepeat, {n,} is seq (counted n n) (star atom)), class_set, repeat_bound (clamps a negative i32 to 0u32; rx nullability tested low <= 0, regex tests low = 0). nullability_of, nullable and nullability_text now delegate to regex_nullable; xsd_regex's own evidence GADT (EpsAccepts/NoneRejects/ClassRejects ...), its 3 mutual helpers and both reason printers are DELETED (the two algorithms agree case for case and both evidence types carry no terms). API: the one outside consumer, xpath_eval.spi:821, uses only nullable (bool), unchanged; the internal users (derivative :318, matcher :631/:643, DFA accepting :790) keep the same bool, so every DFA/matching test exercises the adapter. Only visible change: the one nullability test's TEXT now uses regex's spellings (seq(star,repeat-from-zero) and alt(set,seq-right(nothing))). GATING on ganymede now: xsd_regex.spi and xpath_eval.spi lib gates (ganymede's regex modules are byte-identical to the box's). NEXT: on green, the cross-engine agreement on the pinned pattern corpus, then layers 2-3 (charset, smart constructors), then derivative.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 5u32, "2026-11-09T08:36Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 LAYER 4 PROVEN on ganymede (lib = box live + the adapter): xsd_regex 8/8 (nullability text plus every DFA, matcher and derivative test, all of which go through nullable), xpath_eval 27/27 (the one outside consumer of nullable), type errors 0. CROSS-ENGINE AGREEMENT on fiscal's pinned corpus (336 patterns x every trial vs .NET's recorded answers, fiscal corpus_checks draft 51578A19 over lib draft 6F570A3A): the_canonical_engine_matches_like_dotnet_on_every_trial PASSED (29 s), and the 3 existing engines refactored onto the new trial_disagreements helper still pass: derivative 196 s, DFA 63 s, in-place table 63 s. The canonical regex engine (regex_derivative over to_re) is the fastest of the four on this corpus. Drafts: lib xsd_regex 6F570A3A (adapter + canonical_disagreements), fiscal corpus_checks 51578A19 (helper + canonical test; it needs the lib draft first). NEXT: land the lib draft (proof on moon, copy-only box land), then the fiscal corpus_checks draft, then layers 2-3 (charset, smart constructors) and the derivative layer.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 6u32, "2026-11-09T08:47Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 LAYER 4 LIVE: lib xsd_regex 6F570A3A (to_re, class_set, repeat_bound; nullability_of/nullable/nullability_text delegate to regex_nullable; probe_codes, canonical_matches, canonical_disagreements). LANDED 11-09 04:4x local from a proven close, copy-only on the box (moon job-1794213782003-fiscal-libland-proof5: round trip, 0 consumer signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type probe PASS for both, respell drift 0, lib digest 2306F0893534A3AF = the box digest after the land). Proof v4 had stopped at the round trip: the R9 draft lacked a final newline (a PowerShell here-string drops it); the canonical bytes from lib_roundtrip.exs fixed it (08687CF1). Fiscal side landed in the working tree (unstaged): src/corpus_checks.spi 51578A19 over base DAC14D90 (trial_disagreements helper; the derivative, DFA and table tests rewritten onto it; new the_canonical_engine_matches_like_dotnet_on_every_trial), proven on ganymede (4 engine tests passed vs .NET on all 336 pinned patterns). NEXT: layer 2 (charset: in_ranges/insert_range/complement over regex_charset) as the next draft on the now-live xsd_regex.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 7u32, "2026-11-09T08:53Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 LAYER 2 (charset) STUDIED, not a drop-in. Differences vs regex_charset: (a) xsd_regex in_ranges scans an UNNORMALIZED list (any order, overlaps) while regex contains_in assumes a normalized sorted set and exits early; a per-call adapter would normalize on every call, and in_ranges is the hot path (derive, matcher, DFA build: once per character per class); (b) xsd_regex complement_ranges returns gaps in REVERSE order (it prepends), regex complement returns them ascending, and range order feeds rx_compare, the canonical forms and the DFA tables that xsd_emit embeds in generated validators, so a swap can change generated text. PLAN for this slice: change RxClass to carry a normalized regex_charset::char_set normal (built once by the parser and by class_set), so in_ranges becomes regex_charset::contains (logarithmic early exit, no per-call normalize) and complement is regex's; keep rx_compare's order by comparing normalized ranges; PROOF = the 8 xsd_regex tests + xpath_eval 27 + the 4 corpus engines vs .NET + the generator IDENTITY arm (regen 166 files, 0 differing) because generated validators embed these ranges. Estimate ~150 m incl. the identity regen on a node. Not started.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 8u32, "2026-11-10T23:47Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 21:1x Slice D1 DONE and lib-proven: xsd_regex 48B13BA45027 (RxClass carries its normalized regex_charset set, built once; membership and to_re go through it; order kept on the written form), europa proof green, log at scratchpad xsdproof\\regex-proof.log. Next step: the generator IDENTITY regen on a node (regenerate the 166 generated files with the draft lib; expect 0 differing files because rx_compare's order is unchanged), then land copy-only on the box with lib_land_window -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 9u32, "2026-11-11T00:07Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 21:5x IDENTITY ARM RECIPE (not started: ganymede at load 8 on 4 cores with 6 of 7 GB used, europa too small for the big families, moon starved). Use the generator's own tests, not a hand harness (memory: a scratch harness silently skipped 9 families on 11-05): one ganymede job in the fiscal-gany mirror runs build.ps1 -Files generator twice, A with the live lib and B with lib xsd_regex = the D1 draft 48B13BA45027, hashing every file under fiscal/generated after each pass, and reports the differing files. A/B rather than against the committed generated/, because the committed units may predate other lanes' emitter changes. Expect 0 differing (rx_compare still orders classes by their written form). Then land copy-only on the box: lib_land_window -Draft xsd_regex.spi=<draft> -BaseHash 6F570A3ACBDE -ProvenLog scratchpad xsdproof\\regex-proof.log -Apply. Next step: run the A/B when a node has about 3 GB free and load under its core count.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 10u32, "2026-11-11T01:08Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 21:1x REBASED onto org2's lib reformat (LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION, layout only): box xsd_regex is now AC2037C46214 (was 6F570A3ACBDE). The reformat wrapped one signature (canonical_disagreements) onto 4 lines; lib_roundtrip leaves the old base unchanged, so it was a different formatter and I did not guess its layout. git merge-file (ours = draft, base = old box, theirs = new box) merged with 0 conflicts; verified that my 40 changed lines are identical on the old and new base and that the merge adds only the 5-line wrap. Rebased draft drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER-D1\\xsd_regex.spi B175055B5C73 over .base AC2037C46214 (pre-rebase copies kept); budget 54 -> 54. The europa proof (regex-proof.log) proved the OLD bytes, so the -ProvenLog land needs a re-proof of B175055B5C73 against the reformatted lib (tar staged at scratchpad xsdproof\\lib4.tgz f590bb088127; about 10 min on europa). Next step: re-prove on europa when microblog's bench ends, run the identity A/B regen, then land with -BaseHash AC2037C46214.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER", 11u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-11 heads-up for fiscal (status unchanged, your item): the user ruled that the regex engine lives in the regex repo's own lib, not lib/spiral (REGEX-LIB-HOME). The adapter's API goal stands, but its target becomes the regex package reached through deps/regex; lib xsd_regex itself may move to fiscal's lib (XML-STACK-HOME). Hold new lib/spiral regex lands until REGEX-LIB-HOME has its package path.")
