inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_11 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 11u32, "2026-11-09T16:13Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: the canonical taplo config IS done (ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE note: i574n.github/.taplo.toml, TAPLO_CONFIG env, 11 per-repo copies deleted); main-owned repos formatted. The only remaining work is ENFORCEMENT: wire taplo fmt --check into kit standards so every repo's spiral.toml/Cargo.toml is gated, plus each owner applies in its repo. The checker is rig lane (kit standards sibling of the 1000-line gate). Parking on lane:rig; clear when kit standards runs the taplo check.")
inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_12 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 12u32, "2026-11-09T17:45Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:0x local rig, PROGRESS (the lane:rig wait stays until the check runs from kit standards): (1) MEASURED kit with the canonical config (TAPLO_CONFIG = i574n.github/.taplo.toml): taplo fmt --check over its 379 tracked .toml exits 0, kit is clean. (2) FOUND the hazard the checker must close: this session's shell had started before TAPLO_CONFIG was set at user level, so taplo silently used its DEFAULTS and reported 2 false \"not properly formatted\" files (src/Cargo.toml, rig_patch_transaction_contracts/Cargo.toml). (3) BUILT the verdict core (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi (pure, HostFree): toml_verdict TomlFormatted n | TomlUnformatted paths | ConfigMissing | TaploMissing; verdict_of refuses when TAPLO_CONFIG is empty (never a default run) and reads each path from taplo's \"the file is not properly formatted path=...\" lines. NEXT: the IO half in kit standards (git ls-files *.toml, spawn taplo fmt --check with the env, feed the output here), ratchet mode first.")
inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_13 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 13u32, "2026-11-09T20:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig progress (the lane:rig wait stays until the rule fires): rig's model for this item (rig_standards_toml (refuses without TAPLO_CONFIG)) is built and in rig's probe batch; its routing to every lane now has one carrier item, KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB (kit lint smells beside kit lint macros, ratchet mode with a per-repo baseline, a negative control per rule), which waits on TRAIN43 because the lint entry is shared code. rig clears this wait when the rule fires on your repo.")
inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_14 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 14u32, "2026-11-09T21:25Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig progress: rig_standards_toml (after pinning listm.length to i32) is probe-green (Cells notebook gate on ganymede, off-train). The lane:rig wait stays until KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB wires the rule into kit lint smells after TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_15 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 15u32, "2026-11-10T00:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:3x rig CORRECTION to notes 20:23 and 21:25Z: the \"rig_standards_toml model (refuses without TAPLO_CONFIG)\" those notes call probe-green was a rewrite over the SHIPPED src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi and removed its toml_run entry point; it broke TRAIN43's regen (rig_style_census) and is reverted to HEAD (archived, not deleted). The shipped check already does what this item needs (git ls-files *.toml, taplo fmt --check --config, typed Formatted/Unformatted/NoConfig/NoTaplo, exit 0/1/2, refusing when no config resolves). The one behavior worth keeping from the model is now an edit to the shipped file: TAPLO_CONFIG WINS whenever it is set, and a repo .taplo.toml is only the fallback when it is unset (before: a stray repo copy overrode the canonical config, against the one-source rule); test renamed the_shared_config_wins_and_a_repo_copy_is_only_the_fallback; kit standards 0 findings; probe on ganymede PENDING. The lane:rig wait stays until the rule fires from kit lint smells (KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB).")
inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_16 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 16u32, "2026-11-10T00:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:33 rig: the TAPLO_CONFIG-first edit to the shipped src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi is probe-green: Cells notebook gate on ganymede, exec=2 failed=0 passed=2 in 53 s (node copy hash 8b97cf186527 = box). Unstaged, rides TRAIN44. The lane:rig wait stays until KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB routes the rule to every lane.")
inl note_of_toml_format_taplo_17 () = Note ("TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO", 17u32, "2026-11-10T13:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 09:5x rig: the lane:rig wait is now item:KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB, the precise target every earlier rig note already named (that verb routes this rule to every lane, and it waits on train TRAIN43f, node-green 331/331 at 08:46 with the box install running). The wait clears itself when the verb is Done, so this item stops showing up as waiting on rig in the gate.")
