inl note_of_regex_core_into_lib_1 () = Note ("REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:14Z", "main", "Decided 11-07 by main (regex owner) on fiscal's FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP (map: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP\\map.txt). User 11-07: everything should reuse from everything; lose the fear of big lib changes. Gaps the core needs before the switch (fiscal): longest_match; class_end/escape_end/brace_end; block-list parity (regex 7 vs lib 4); dfa_of_values; example_with printable-choice; byte-stable dfa_table_text + table_matches (19 generated units, 61 calls). DoD: the core lives in lib (land windows, scratch type_probe first), regex src re-points at it with its bench facts identical, the ouroboros agreement check (regex agreement vs lib xsd_regex on fiscal's pinned corpus) green; then fiscal's FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER. Next step: split into children per layer (charset+syntax, nullable+derivative, dfa+minimal, xsd parser), each <=240 min. TypeFeatures: the re union, nullability evidence GADT and typed refusals stay as in regex.")
inl note_of_regex_core_into_lib_2 () = Note ("REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB", 2u32, "2026-11-07T16:47Z", "main", "main 11-07: TFS-CONVERSION-LOSS-LAWS depends on this item: the xsd_regex adapter it creates is that item's second pilot pair (expected Retraction: xsd syntax into the lib AST and back is a law, the reverse loses lib-only constructs). Declare the direction when the adapter is written.")
