inl note_of_html_md_svg_dedup_1 () = Note ("HTML-MD-SVG-DEDUP", 1u32, "2026-11-07T11:14Z", "main", "User 11-07: same thing with html and markdown stuff, svg etc. (everything should reuse from everything). Known copies: html repo html_render/html_inline/markdown units; lib markup.spi + doc_render.spi; lib physics.spi chart/frame JSON feeding Cells display.ex SVG rendering; Cells html.ex page rendering (Elixir; x's ELIXIR ratchet applies). DoD: a definition-pair map like fiscal's FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP, then one canonical lib layer (escape, element/attribute builders, markdown blocks, SVG path/axis) that the html repo and Cells call, with outputs byte-identical (html --self-test, Cells html_test/display_test, physics notebook SVG count). Next step: the pair map (kit's DUPLICATE-CODE-SHINGLES can seed it once it exists). TypeFeatures: typed element/attribute nodes rather than string concatenation.")
inl note_of_html_md_svg_dedup_2 () = Note ("HTML-MD-SVG-DEDUP", 2u32, "2026-11-07T20:25Z", "main", "main 11-07 16:3x PAIR MAP (git grep over html, spiral (lib + Cells) and blog):\nESCAPE:\n- canonical: lib markup.escape (typed markup); blog engine/html.spi already calls it.\n- copy: spiral/apps/cells/spi/html_markdown.spi:7 `escape` (chained text::replace).\n- lib xml escape_text_xml / escape_attribute_xml stay: the XML spec's set, used by fiscal.\n- the other '&amp;' hits are test expectations.\nRENDER (markdown blocks -> HTML):\n- canonical: lib doc_render.blocks_html over lib doc_blocks types; the html repo already calls it (html_render/render.spi:17 markdown_html = blocks_html (parse_markdown s)).\n- the identical `inline_fixture` in html_render/render.spi:21 and lib doc_render.spi:135 is a duplicated TEST, not duplicated code.\nPARSE (markdown text -> blocks):\n- NOT in lib: html/html_parse/markdown.spi (277 lines, parse_markdown) + html/html_inline/inline_parse.spi (169).\n- That gap is why Cells grew a THIRD implementation (html_markdown.spi, 126 lines: its own inline parser, renderer and escape) and why blog keeps its own block union.\nBLOG:\n- engine/post.spi has its own block union (Heading, Paragraph, Code, Terminal, Table, Note) rendered by string concat.\n- Heading/Paragraph/Code/Table overlap doc_blocks + doc_render (code_html, table_html); Terminal and Note have no lib case.\nSVG: one producer only (Cells display.ex, Elixir, from lib physics JSON frames); no duplicate yet. When the ELIXIR ratchet ports it, it lands as a lib svg module, not in Cells.\nPLAN as children:\n(1) HTML-MD-PARSER-TO-LIB (main): move parse_markdown + inline_parse into lib as doc_parse; html calls lib; html --self-test byte-identical.\n(2) CELLS-MD-ON-LIB (x): html_markdown.spi -> lib doc_parse + doc_render + markup.escape; Cells html tests byte-identical, or the differences listed.\n(3) BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB (main): blog renders through doc_render; Terminal/Note become lib block cases or stay blog-local with a reason.")
inl note_of_html_md_svg_dedup_3 () = Note ("HTML-MD-SVG-DEDUP", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:4x STATE: children (1) HTML-MD-PARSER-TO-LIB Done (lib doc_parse); (2) CELLS-MD-ON-LIB 85% (microblog; apps/cells/spi/html_markdown.spi down to 11 lines); (3) BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB 35%, step (a) landed 11-07, steps (b)+(c) wait on the user's pick of the showcase before/after sample (now a wait row, not just prose). SVG: still one producer (Cells display.ex via the apps/plot renderer; physics moved to apps/plot today). Next step: none for org until the blog sample decision; microblog finishes (2).")
inl xdumps_string_media_normalize () = Task ("XDUMPS-STRING-MEDIA-NORMALIZE", "Normalize string-media (bare URL arrays) to path/type/alt objects in the xarchive media stage so the world is single-shape (retires the serve-side is_map filter)", Story, P3, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:org,management,media,harvest,xarchive", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xdumps_string_media_normalize () = Planning ("XDUMPS-STRING-MEDIA-NORMALIZE", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xdumps_string_media_normalize_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-STRING-MEDIA-NORMALIZE", 1u32, "2026-11-07T12:22Z", "x-dumps", "Filed 2026-11-07 from the media-quote serve finish. 83 posts in joined.world.json store the media field as an array of bare URL strings (e.g. pbs.twimg.com/media/HQKcPyaWEAAhKpi.jpg) instead of path/type/alt_text objects; 15,849 posts use proper object-media. The serve crashed with badmap on the URL binary until timeline_serve media_terms added an is_map filter (hash 6B62FAFA05FA, gated 28/28) that SKIPS string-media (no local file to serve). Permanent fix: the xarchive media stage / timeline.rs should normalize string-media into path/type/alt objects and localize the files (fetch like other media) so the world is single-shape and these 83 posts media actually renders, letting the serve-side filter retire. Same spirit as XDUMPS-BIN-MEDIA-TYPE forward-fix (sniff_ext) and the context-promotion permanent fix. Not blocking: serve stable with the filter. See memory xdumps-world-fields-multishape.")
inl note_of_xdumps_string_media_normalize_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-STRING-MEDIA-NORMALIZE", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:57Z", "x-dumps", "dod: xarchive media stage emits every post media[] as path/type/alt objects (no bare URL strings) and the 83 current string-media posts localize and render in the UI, making the serve-side is_map filter redundant. next: in xarchive media.rs detect array-of-string media, fetch+localize each URL like object-media and emit a path/type/alt entry, re-run media->timeline->world, confirm the 83 render.")
inl note_of_xdumps_string_media_normalize_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-STRING-MEDIA-NORMALIZE", 3u32, "2026-11-07T19:22Z", "x-dumps", "Investigated 11-07. media_of (xarchive/src/world.rs:45-54) ALWAYS wraps r[media] string elements into {path,type,alt_text,media_key} objects, so a world built by current world.rs has NO bare-string media. Yet the deployed world still has 83 bare-string media:[http...] posts (vs 15,849 object-media) - they BYPASSED world.rs::media_of (recovery/enrichment overlay wrote raw posts without re-running media_of, or an older build). KEY: wrapping via media_of would NOT fix rendering - path would = the raw twimg URL and the /media route only serves LOCAL files (media_root/rel), so /media/https://... = 404. REAL fix = LOCALIZE the 83 URLs (fetch via media.rs -> media.tsv -> timeline local paths; may 404 for old tweets) then rebuild world + re-sync to node (disruptive to the live deploy). It is 0.05% of posts (83/163,348) and the SERVE already SKIPS them gracefully (is_map filter in timeline_serve, no crash, text shows). Deferring the disruptive localize+rebuild. next: fold a media.rs \"post-media URL not in media.tsv -> fetch\" pass into the NEXT scheduled world rebuild; serve-skip is the graceful interim. Staying P3.")
inl note_of_xdumps_string_media_normalize_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-STRING-MEDIA-NORMALIZE", 4u32, "2026-11-07T22:33Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "INVESTIGATED 11-07T22:3xZ — the 83 bare-URL-media posts ARE fixable (recoverable media), not a dead end. All 83 are account 72784485 (fc1943s, the USER'S OWN). Their media is stored as bare external URL arrays (e.g. \"media\":[\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/EQY-K7AW4AEXaap.jpg\"]) instead of the normal {path,media_key,type,alt_text} objects, so the serve's map-shape guard skips them (83 posts render without their images). The files are NOT cached in /data/x/accounts (never downloaded during harvest). BUT recoverable: sampled URLs return HTTP 200 on pbs.twimg.com live AND are in Wayback (CDX 2020 capture, 200, ~139KB each). So the complete fix = fetch the 83 (~11MB total) into the media tree + normalize those posts' media to {path,...} objects + rebuild world + redeploy; then they render self-contained. Alternative (no fetch): serve could emit the external pbs URL directly (renders now, but external dep + leaks viewer requests to Twitter + fragile if later deleted) — not preferred for a self-contained archive. BLOCKED ON USER: fetching is paused ('only code deploys now'); 83 images is a tiny targeted completion of the user's own media, not a re-harvest — surfaced to the user to approve the small fetch. Until then the serve correctly skips them (no crash).")
