inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_1 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 1u32, "2026-11-07T13:01Z", "main", "main 11-07 RECOVERED + COMPILABLE, unstaged in C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\recovered\\ for the user's review (user 11-07: sweep for stroma/pdf2stroma/espiral comum/W43/tritcritnet/zeta+mamba; else work-hub's Downloads; iterate until compilable; put in i574n.github). Sources (fetched read-only from work-hub = the work PC, <user>@<work-hub-addr>, through rustdesk -> 244:2244; also on the box where noted):\n(1) tritcritnet/ = bundle_tritcritnet_v20260618-alpha9252 (the NEWEST, Rust: core + tritcritnet crates, 161 src files incl. ternary_zeta_*, local_w43*, w43_*): cargo check clean on nightly-2026-10-18.\n(2) tritcritnet-cpp/ = from bundle_eoie_v20260530-alpha834: tritcritnet.cpp (1.3 MB, g++ -std=c++23 -D_USE_MATH_DEFINES -fsyntax-only: 0 errors) + readme_tritcritnet*.md + joint_rust_workspace (the early Rust port tcn-core/eoie-core; cargo check clean).\n(3) stroma/ = bundle_stroma_v20260618-alpha9252 (Rust PDF parser: core + stroma + its tritcritnet dep): cargo check clean.\n(4) pdf-indexing/ = the untracked files of C:\\home\\git\\stroma (github stewshka/stroma has only an Initial commit): pdf2stroma_raw_v2-alpha4.ps1, pdf2stroma_libs.ps1, pdf2mdc.c (POSIX: compiles and links with gcc on Linux/europa; MinGW lacks strndup/sysconf), pdf2md.cpp (g++ -fsyntax-only 0 errors).\n(5) agile_eoie dump -> kit (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-EOIE-DUMP-GROOM).\nNOT placed (found, available on request): W43.py + W43.kml and stroma.md, inside C:\\home\\git\\singularity\\temp\\ingest_old(1).zip -> old_workspace_v2-alpha3.zip; the BitNet+zeta Gemini PDF in the same archive; espiral comum notes (vault\\data\\espiral-comum, Writingway Projects\\EspiralComum); older combined bundles alpha9118-9237 on work-hub (eoie\\old). NOT FOUND anywhere: any Mamba code (only a prior-art mention in tibia PRIOR_ART.md). Lost: the 10-17 notes' Downloads\\bundle-cleanup-backup-20260926, dev1, files-2026-05 (~2,565 zips) are on neither machine; the box Downloads bundles are 0-byte/700-byte undelete stubs. Note: pdf-indexing holds 2 .ps1 files, against the no-new-.ps1 rule, kept because the user asked to review the originals as they were.")
