inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_3 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 3u32, "2026-11-07T13:43Z", "main", "main 11-07 (recovery subagent) ADDED to recovered/, unstaged, after the user's 11-07 follow-up (extract everything useful, latest versions, W43 too, organized for review): (a) recovered/README.md, a review index (folder, version, source, check status, pre-commit cautions); (b) recovered/w43/W43.py (16,241 B, great-circle geodesy over lon/lat, 39 defs) and W43.kml (29,376 B, 29 placemarks: dragon1, dragon/sirius, cloverleaf/orion, 817, ...), from ingest_old(1).zip -> old_workspace_v2-alpha3.zip; (c) recovered/pdf-indexing/stroma.md (23,427 B, the 2026-01-07 pt-BR summary of the indexing and query pipeline); (d) recovered/tritcritnet/docs/Gemini-BitNet e Funcao Zeta_ Potenciais Conquistas.pdf (6,242,434 B, sha256 0bfd6616..., matches the bundle stub). Third-party zeta sources stay off the public repo, in kit drafts (ZETA-PARITY-ANTHROPIC n2). Cautions written in the README: the repo is public; W43.kml holds real coordinates and the Gemini PDF is a personal chat; W43.py breaks the no-.py rule (kept as an original). Latest-version check: no newer tritcritnet, stroma or pdf2stroma exists on either machine (work-hub zip-entry scan of 2,347 zips); the 05-16 pdf2stroma alpha207..303 bundles survive only as undelete stubs or noise. The dragon line (W43.kml, dragon_v20260125-alpha24.kml, W6.zip with the signed W66/W5D/W5G PDFs) gets its own catalog item.")
inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_4 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 4u32, "2026-11-07T13:46Z", "main", "main 11-07 09:4x: the resumed sweep agent added recovered\\README.md (review index), w43\\W43.py, pdf-indexing\\stroma.md, W43.kml and the Gemini BitNet+zeta PDF. main MOVED the two personal files (W43.kml with real coordinates 2B176E0A3029, the Gemini chat export 0BFD66163A5C) OUT of the public i574n.github tree into %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107\\private\\, so an unstaged-tree push can't publish them, and pointed the README at the private copies. W43.py stays for review (it breaks the no-.py rule, kept as an original like the .ps1 files). Dragon line: DRAGON-LINE-CATALOG.")
inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_5 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 5u32, "2026-11-07T14:17Z", "main", "main 11-07 10:0x (sweep subagent, user 11-07: copy the dragon stuff and every pending file from work-hub into i574n.github in one place for review in Fork, none to be committed, dedup later). recovered/ now also holds, unstaged and untracked: dragon/ (README with the version analysis, from-des073/{dragon_v20260125-alpha24.kml, W6.zip, HPOW.md, ДЕНЬ_ПОБЕДЫ_W43.md}, W6/ unzipped, w43/{W43.py, W43.kml}, vault-Untitled-1.md); espiral-comum/ (EC20251231-pre.md 5.1 MB from work-hub plus the vault and Writingway notes); agile-eoie/ (eoie-consolidated/ 16 files, the 08-11 legacy agile_eoie.md, the 07-22 agile_eoie 1.md); bundles/from-des073/ (14 files, 59 MB: eoie alpha834/9247/9252, tritcritnet/stroma/spiral/mechahaze alpha9252, combined alpha9118/9119/9220/9237, cot and roadmap logs). Every copy's sha256 matches work-hub. README.md rewritten as the index. This follows the user's explicit 11-07 ask over the 09:4x private move: W43.kml is back in the tree (dragon/w43) because the user wants the dragon files visible in Fork; the private drafts copies stay too. Not copied (named in the README): MECHAHAZE_full_album_mp3_320 (231 MB, too big for the SP relay that carries RustDesk); the eoie alpha70xxx and spiral-bin/samples/brzozowski bundles (kit and compiler history, mined by BUNDLE-WISDOM) and the work PC's own project folders.")
inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_6 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 6u32, "2026-11-07T14:32Z", "main", "main 11-07 TRITCRITNET REUSE ASSESSMENT (user 11-07: is the code reusable given the transformer etc., and would we be better off had it not been parked?). CORRECTION to n1 (NOT FOUND any Mamba code): tritcritnet-cpp\\tritcritnet.cpp (19,878 lines) is a real tiny byte-level language model trainer: embedding, per layer an SSM-style gated recurrent block (SSMParams: conv kernels K0..K2, Wz/Ws/Wo gates, 4d FFN), local attention islands (M=8, H=32, every 32 tokens) switched on only above a criticality threshold (0.70, credit budget), layernorm, softmax, Adam and AdamW, hash-split train/val/test byte windows, a JSONL event log per step, checkpoints. Its own audit (lines 4413-4416) says the Mamba part is not real yet: selective scan and input-dependent transitions absent (GRU/conv drift), ternary only as fake-quant, packed trits absent. The Rust alpha9252 (161 files, about 16k lines) is mostly plan, receipt and gate records (426 static string literals); its only learner is a one-layer ternary linear model (ternary_autograd_min.rs). REUSABLE NOW: (1) packed ternary weights with add/sub kernels, filed as TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY (shared with tibia's ternary policy option); (2) the training pieces (backprop through attention and FFN, AdamW, deterministic data splits) if the transformer or tibia ever trains rather than only infers; (3) the audit-table habit of naming which claims are not yet earned. NOT REUSABLE: the zeta, W43 and Lenia curricula (synthetic, dropped by tibia PRIOR_ART) and the Rust critic and gate modules (kit agile next already ranks tasks, tibia BENCHMARK holds the promotion rule). COUNTERFACTUAL: little would have been gained by absorbing it into the Rust-to-Spiral migrations earlier. The Rust half is the same receipts-without-a-yardstick drift kit is still healing from (it grew in the same eoie bundles), so absorbing it would have added drift. The C++ half had real pieces, but its numbers were self-graded with no external benchmark; the transformer took the opposite route (llama2.c outputs as the oracle, tok/s against named incumbents), which is the reason it advanced. The one real loss from parking: the packed-trit kernel could have been measured months ago against a public BitNet checkpoint.")
inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_7 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 7u32, "2026-11-08T21:40Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 17:4x VERIFY (round-2 groom split): NOT closable by a lane. The DoD is the user's review of i574n.github/recovered/ (keep / where / which leftovers to pull), and every lane-side step is done (copies sha256-matched to work-hub; personal files also kept privately under kit/drafts). Status Active 90% -> Blocked, so the autonomous run doesn't pull it. Next step: the user's review in Fork; then a lane moves each kept piece to its home.")
inl note_of_archive_recovery_1107_8 () = Note ("ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107", 8u32, "2026-11-08T21:41Z", "org2", "Blocker: waits on the user's review of i574n.github/recovered/ in Fork (keep / where / which leftovers to pull).")
