inl transformer_quant_ternary () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", "Transformer ternary weights (BitNet b1.58): packed 2-bit trits and add/sub matvec kernels in lib, checked against a pinned public b1.58 checkpoint, shared with tibia ternary policy weights", Story, P2, D5, 80u32, Active, "TRANSFORMER-QUANT-Q8", "transformer,tibia,lib,ternary,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_quant_ternary () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_1 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:32Z", "main", "User 11-07 (main, from the TritCritNet reuse question: is that code reusable now that we have the transformer etc.?). The one TritCritNet idea that never got built and fits today's code: weights in {-1, 0, +1} (BitNet b1.58) stored packed 2 bits each, with add/subtract matvec kernels instead of multiply. TritCritNet C++ (i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet-cpp\\tritcritnet.cpp, 19,878 lines, alpha716) only ever had a FAKE-QUANT forward (threshold 0.25, straight-through training); its own audit table (lines 4413-4416) lists packed_trit_storage absent and ternary_matvec with no memory or compute gain as release blockers (its TCN-T446, never done). tibia MODELING.md already keeps ternary policy weights packed 2 bits as an option, so the kernel is shared lib code. DoD: a typed ternary tensor (packed trit blocks plus a per-block or per-tensor scale) and an add/sub matvec in lib, on the Rust and C backends with a WGSL arm; correctness against a pinned external oracle (a public BitNet b1.58 checkpoint run by its reference inference, both pinned in the first note after checking they exist, downloads only, never committed): identical greedy tokens and logits within a stated tolerance; tok/s and memory beside the fp32 and Q8 paths on the bench page; tibia can load its policy weights through the same type. Not in scope: training (TritCritNet's Adam/AdamW and backprop are a separate question). Next step: pin the oracle checkpoint and its runner, then the packing layout.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_2 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:34Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia: ACCEPTED (dep TRANSFORMER-QUANT-Q8 is Done, so this is ready). CORRECTION to the filing note: there is no MODELING.md in the tibia repo, and no tibia doc plans packed ternary policy weights (searched every .md outside target/deps: the only TritCritNet mention is docs/BENCHMARK.md:732, its promotion rule). So the \"shared with tibia ternary policy weights\" half of the title has no existing plan behind it. The lib kernel stands on its own (transformer memory and bandwidth); a tibia use would need its own item after a measured win. NEXT (step 1, light): verify that a public BitNet b1.58 checkpoint and its reference runner exist, and pin both (URL, revision or hash, license) before any code.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_3 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 3u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint marker): TypeFeatures: a trit is a union (Neg | Zero | Pos), never a raw int; the packed tensor is a sized type whose element count is a type-level literal, with the packed byte length derived at compile time (4 trits per byte), so a pack/unpack length mismatch is a compile error; the matvec kernel takes sized operands like the dense one.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_4 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 4u32, "2026-11-08T02:28Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:3x tibia: STEP 1 DONE, PINS (verified 22:3x through the HuggingFace and GitHub public APIs; nothing downloaded). CHECKPOINT: microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T at revision 04c3b9ad9361b824064a1f25ea60a8be9599b127, license MIT, model.safetensors 1,124 MB (LFS sha256 8143ae115ed6babe...); the same model as GGUF for bitnet.cpp: microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf at a1f2f1c765812aa8af3f6eda4a313707064bba15, MIT, ggml-model-i2_s.gguf 1,132.8 MB (sha256 4221b252fdd5fd25...). A smaller community reproduction, if a lighter cross-check is wanted: 1bitLLM/bitnet_b1_58-large at 85d047191dcb224f0e04f20d26110caaf8dc1a47, MIT, 2,780 MB (fp weights with the quantizer in utils_quant.py). REFERENCE RUNNER: github microsoft/BitNet (bitnet.cpp), license MIT, main at 0b341e582afb (2026-07-27). PLAN, steps of at most 120 min: (2) lib packed-trit tensor: trit as a union (Neg | Zero | Pos), 4 trits per byte, the element count as a type-level literal so the packed length is derived at compile time, and a ternary matvec with golden tests (exact on small integer inputs); (3) BitNet b1.58 absmean quantization of stories15M's weights as an in-house correctness test (perplexity and greedy text against the fp32 model, measured, not predicted); (4) the 2B-4T checkpoint through bitnet.cpp on europa or the node as the end-to-end reference (about 1.1 GB download, which needs the user's or main's yes, given disk on europa is at 81 pct). NEXT STEP: step 2.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_5 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 5u32, "2026-11-08T02:32Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:4x tibia: STEP 2 DRAFTED: new lib module, kit drafts TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY\\pkg\\f32_trits.spi D8BC063995DD. TypeFeatures as groomed: `:| trit = Neg | Zero | Pos` (never a raw int), and `:! trits n = array u8` with the element count as a TYPE-LEVEL LITERAL (count reads it back with real_core::type_lit_to_lit, the pattern of transformer's `len n`). pack takes a GENERATOR (i32 -> trit) and sizes the bytes from the type alone ((n + 3) / 4, 4 trits per byte, 2-bit codes Neg 0 / Zero 1 / Pos 2), so the source can never disagree with the declared length; that is how the \"pack/unpack mismatch is a compile error\" requirement is met without sized source arrays. ternary_dot adds, subtracts or skips (no multiplies). BitNet b1.58 absmean quantization: gamma = mean |w| + 1e-5; trit = round(w / gamma) clamped to [-1, 1]. Exact golden tests on c and rust: 7 trits pack into 2 bytes and read back; [+, -, 0, +, -] . [1..5] = -2; quantizing [0.9, -0.2, -1.4, 0.05, 0.6] gives gamma 0.63001 and [+, 0, -, 0, +]. Box: --check passes, formatter-clean, cell budget 0. RUNNING: node job-1794105137284-tibia-trits-cells.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_6 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 6u32, "2026-11-08T02:38Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:4x tibia: STEP 2 LANDED: spiral/lib/spiral/f32_trits.spi CBEA7B17380C (new lib module; lib_land_window green: consumers compile, document_test 26 passed, type probe 3 tests typed / 0 errors, respell_drift 0; lib digest 871123CB4CCC08DC; undo 20261107-223444; unstaged). Node proof before the land: job-1794105137284-tibia-trits-cells, 6/6 rows (3 tests x c, rust). NEXT STEP: step 3, absmean-quantize stories15M's matrices (per tensor gamma, as BitNet does) into trits, run the transformer with a ternary matvec (dequantized row scale times ternary_dot), and MEASURE perplexity and greedy text against fp32. Post-training ternarization of a model not trained for it is expected to degrade badly; the number is the point, and it should be pre-registered as a measurement, not a target.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_7 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 7u32, "2026-11-08T02:38Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:4x tibia: STEP 3a PRE-REGISTERED as a MEASUREMENT (written before the program runs). Post-training ternarization (PTQ) of stories260K. Every linear matrix (wq, wk, wv, wo, w1, w2, w3 of each of the 5 layers) is replaced by gamma * trit, using lib f32_trits' absmean quantizer per matrix; the embedding/classifier and the RMSNorm gains stay fp32, as BitNet does. Metric: mean cross-entropy over 8 fixed windows of 128 predicted tokens (our xorshift sampler, seed 88172645463325252, over valid_tok512.bin), fp32 vs ternary, same windows. EXPECTATION: PTQ to 1.58 bits without quantization-aware training should hurt badly; ternary loss at least 0.5 nats above fp32. This is a measurement, not a gate. It sets the gap that quantization-aware training (ternary forward with a straight-through estimator, via the training loop) must close, which is the next step. The number is recorded whatever it is.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_8 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 8u32, "2026-11-08T02:40Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:4x tibia: STEP 3a MEASURED (node job-1794105566567-tibia-ternary-probe, scratch ternary_probe.spi over the transformer package with lib f32_trits CBEA7B17380C; C with -fopenmp, 2.3 s). Mean cross-entropy over the 8 fixed windows: fp32 1.5520525; after post-training absmean ternarization of all 35 linear matrices (embedding, norms and classifier kept fp32): 7.115064. That is +5.56 nats, WORSE than a uniform guess over 512 tokens (ln 512 = 6.24). The expectation (at least 0.5 nats worse) held by a wide margin. Reading: a 260K model trained in fp32 does not survive 1.58-bit weights after the fact, which is BitNet's own premise (it trains with the ternary forward from the start). NEXT STEP: step 3b, quantization-aware training. In the training loop (train_grad + f32_optim), keep fp32 master weights, run the forward and backward on gamma * trit weights, and apply the gradient to the masters (straight-through estimator). Then measure how far N QAT steps from the stories260K start close the 5.56-nat gap, pre-registered.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_9 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 9u32, "2026-11-08T02:40Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:4x tibia: STEP 3b PRE-REGISTERED as a MEASUREMENT (before the program runs). Quantization-aware training from the stories260K start. fp32 master weights; at every step, a gamma * trit copy of all 35 linear matrices (absmean, per matrix) carries the forward AND backward pass, and the gradient is applied to the masters (straight-through estimator) with llama2.c's AdamW (betas 0.9/0.99, wd 0.01 on 2-D tensors, clip 1.0) at a CONSTANT lr of 1e-3. 300 steps of 4 x 128 tokens, with TRAINING windows from a DIFFERENT seed (1234567) than step 3a's 8 evaluation windows (seed 88172645463325252), which are not trained on. Metric: the ternary model's mean cross-entropy on those 8 evaluation windows after 300 steps, against 3a's fp32 1.552 and PTQ 7.115. Soft expectation, stated now: QAT recovers most of the gap, to under 4.0 nats, but not down to fp32 in 300 steps. Recorded whatever it shows; this is not a gate.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_10 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 10u32, "2026-11-08T02:50Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:5x tibia: STEP 3b MEASURED (node job-1794105694588-tibia-qat-probe, scratch qat_probe.spi; C with -fopenmp, 300 steps in 437 s). On the 8 held-out evaluation windows: before QAT, fp32 1.5520525 and PTQ ternary 7.115064; AFTER 300 QAT steps, the TERNARY model scores 2.478383, which recovers 83 pct of the PTQ gap ((7.115 - 2.478) / (7.115 - 1.552)) but stays 0.93 nats above fp32. The soft expectation (under 4.0, not down to fp32) held. Training-batch loss every 25 steps: 6.96, 3.16, 3.05, 2.92, 2.72, 2.78, 2.61, 2.63, 2.78, 2.82, 2.34, 2.32, still falling at step 300. The fp32 MASTER weights get worse as fp32 (1.552 -> 3.440); that is expected under a straight-through estimator: the masters are optimized for how they behave once ternarized, not as floats. NEXT STEPS: (4) a longer QAT run (and/or a warmup-cosine schedule) to see where the ternary curve flattens; (5) the real ternary inference path (packed trits in the transformer's matvec via ternary_dot, timed against fp32, the actual point of 1.58-bit weights: memory and bandwidth); (6) the pinned 2B-4T bitnet.cpp reference, pending a yes for the 1.1 GB download.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_11 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 11u32, "2026-11-08T02:50Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:5x tibia: STEP 4 PRE-REGISTERED as a MEASUREMENT (before the run). Step 3b's QAT with ONE change: 2,000 steps instead of 300 (the same constant lr 1e-3, AdamW, 4 x 128 batches from training seed 1234567, the stories260K start), with the TERNARY model's mean loss on the same 8 held-out evaluation windows printed every 250 steps. Soft expectation: the ternary evaluation loss keeps falling, to at most 2.2 by step 2,000, with the gain per 250 steps shrinking (the curve flattens); it stays above fp32's 1.552. Recorded whatever it shows.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_12 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 12u32, "2026-11-08T03:34Z", "tibia", "11-07 23:3x tibia: STEP 4 MEASURED (node job-1794106270525-tibia-qat-long, scratch qat_long.spi, 2,000 QAT steps in 2,443 s). Ternary loss on the 8 held-out evaluation windows every 250 steps: 2.452, 2.343, 2.304, 2.325, 2.261, 2.252, 2.190, 2.240 (step 2,000). Against the soft expectation: \"keeps falling and flattens\" HELD (gains per 250 steps of 0.11, 0.04, -0.02, 0.06, 0.01, 0.06, -0.05); \"stays above fp32 1.552\" HELD; \"at most 2.2 by step 2,000\" MISSED at 2.240, although step 1,750 reached 2.190. The step-to-step noise of about 0.05 is what a constant lr of 1e-3 gives. Final gap to fp32: 0.69 nats (from PTQ's 5.56); 88 pct of the PTQ gap recovered. The fp32 masters drift further as floats (3.96), as expected under a straight-through estimator. NEXT LEVER (not run): a decaying schedule (warmup-cosine from f32_optim) for the noise floor, then step 5, the packed-trit inference path timed against fp32.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_13 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 13u32, "2026-11-08T03:35Z", "tibia", "11-07 23:3x tibia: STEP 4b PRE-REGISTERED as a MEASUREMENT (before the run). Step 4's QAT with ONE change: the lr follows f32_optim's WarmupCosine (peak 1e-3, warmup 100, cosine to 0 at step 2,000) instead of a constant 1e-3. Same start, training seed, 2,000 steps and 8 evaluation windows. Soft expectation: the decaying lr lowers the noise floor, so the ternary evaluation loss at step 2,000 is BELOW step 4's 2.240 (at most 2.15). Recorded whatever it shows.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_14 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 14u32, "2026-11-08T04:15Z", "tibia", "11-08 00:1x tibia: STEP 4b MEASURED (node job-1794109039787-tibia-qat-cosine, scratch qat_cosine.spi, 2,000 steps in 2,155 s). Ternary loss on the 8 held-out evaluation windows every 250 steps with WarmupCosine (peak 1e-3, warmup 100, cosine to 0 at 2,000): 2.485, 2.382, 2.315, 2.261, 2.148, 2.108, 2.062, 2.006, falling at EVERY evaluation, unlike the constant lr's noisy 2.45 -> 2.24. The expectation (below step 4's 2.240, at most 2.15) HELD: 2.006. The final gap to fp32 is 0.45 nats; 92 pct of the 5.56-nat PTQ gap is recovered by 2,000 QAT steps of 512 tokens (about 1M tokens) on a 260K model. SUMMARY of the item so far: pins (step 1), lib f32_trits landed (step 2), PTQ measured at +5.56 nats (3a), QAT recovers 83 pct in 300 steps (3b), 88 pct in 2,000 at constant lr (4), 92 pct with cosine (4b). NEXT STEP: step 5, the packed-trit inference path in the transformer (ternary_dot rows instead of fp32 dot), timed against fp32 on a quiet host; the memory and bandwidth win is the reason for 1.58 bits, and the fp32 path is bandwidth-bound (TRANSFORMER-TYPED-SIMD-DOT), so this is where a gain could actually show.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_15 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 15u32, "2026-11-08T04:37Z", "tibia", "11-08 00:3x tibia: step 5 groundwork LANDED: spiral/lib/spiral/f32_trits.spi B2D56055300A (lib_land_window green: consumers compile, document_test 26 passed, type probe 4 tests typed, respell_drift 0; lib digest CD6CEE27A5ACA6FC; undo 20261108-002605; unstaged). New test a_288_wide_ternary_dot_equals_the_dequantized_dot, on stories15M's row width: an absmean-quantized 288-wide row (113 +1, 62 zero, 113 -1) dotted with a 288 vector by the add/subtract/skip kernel equals the f32 dot against the dequantized row, and both equal the independently computed 226.0 (1582 / 7, by numpy). Node proof job-1794111803757-tibia-trits2-cells, 8/8 rows. NEXT STEP: unchanged (the packed-trit matvec in the transformer path, timed on a quiet host).")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_16 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 16u32, "2026-11-08T12:29Z", "tibia", "11-08 08:5x tibia: STEP 6a DONE (download; user yes relayed by i574n 08:0x, now a standing OK). Pinned GGUF microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf @ a1f2f1c765812aa8af3f6eda4a313707064bba15, ggml-model-i2_s.gguf, on the node at C:\\home\\remote-stage\\tibia-bitnet-2b4t: 1,187,801,280 bytes, sha256 4221b252fdd5fd25e15847adfeb5ee88886506ba50b8a34548374492884c2162, both equal to the HuggingFace LFS pin (downloaded as .part, renamed only after both matched; 1,255 s). NEXT STEP: 6b, build microsoft/BitNet (bitnet.cpp) at the pinned main 0b341e582afb on the node and run the GGUF as the end-to-end reference (greedy text plus tokens/s), then step 5, our packed-trit matvec timed against fp32 on a quiet host.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_17 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 17u32, "2026-11-08T13:26Z", "tibia", "11-08 09:2x tibia: STEP 6b BUILT AND RAN, RESULT NOT YET A VALID REFERENCE. Build: microsoft/BitNet 0b341e582afb (its llama.cpp submodule 390c307, ggml 0.15.3) on the node. The upstream recipe (-T ClangCL) fails there because VS 2022 lacks the ClangCL toolset (MSB8020); a shared build fails to link (ggml-base.dll needs quantize_i2_s / dequantize_row_i2_s, which BitNet compiles into ggml-cpu; a DLL cannot leave them unresolved). What worked: Ninja + the Swift toolchain clang-cl 21.1.6 inside vcvars64, -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DGGML_BACKEND_DL=OFF -DBITNET_X86_TL2=OFF, after utils/codegen_tl2.py (no preset kernels exist for 2B-4T), AVX2+FMA, build-static\\bin. llama-cli in this llama.cpp is chat-only and waits on stdin (job hung, stopped); use llama-completion with -no-cnv and empty stdin. RUN (pinned GGUF, greedy, 4 threads): the prompt \"Once upon a time, there was a little girl named Lily.\" continues as the loop \"It was a little girl named Lily.\" repeated. The loader warns \"missing pre-tokenizer type ... GENERATION QUALITY WILL BE DEGRADED\", but overriding tokenizer.ggml.pre=llama3 gives the same 14 prompt tokens and the identical loop, so that is not the cause. TIMING VOID: the node was at 100 pct CPU (fiscal-erp-regen and kit-TRAIN40 running); llama-bench pp128 6.19 +- 1.80, tg64 0.98 +- 0.83 t/s (the spread itself shows the contention). OPEN QUESTION, not diagnosed: llama-bench labels the model \"bitnet-b1.58 2B Q1_0\", not I2_S, so check whether the GGUF's I2_S type id means a different type in this newer ggml (a type-id collision would explain both the loop and the speed), versus the 2B-4T being an instruct model that loops on a raw prompt. NEXT STEP: (a) read the GGUF tensor type ids and general.file_type and compare with ggml.h GGML_TYPE_I2_S at 390c307 (no install: read the header bytes); (b) one run with the chat template; (c) timing only in a quiet node window (QUIET-WINDOW-FORECAST), never parked on a busy node.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_18 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 18u32, "2026-11-08T13:32Z", "tibia", "11-08 09:3x tibia: STEP 6b REFERENCE CORRECT (closes note 17's open question). GGUF header read on the node (pwsh parser, no install): 332 tensors; the 210 linear matrices have tensor type 36 = GGML_TYPE_I2_S in the pinned ggml (390c307), 121 norm vectors f32 (0), token_embd f16 (1); there is no tokenizer.ggml.pre key (tokenizer.ggml.model = gpt2), hence the loader warning. general.file_type = 40, and LLAMA_FTYPE 40 now names Q1_0 (I2_S moved to 41), so llama-bench's \"Q1_0\" is a renumbered METADATA LABEL only; the type-collision hypothesis is REFUTED for the weights. With the model's chat format (\"User: What is the capital of France? Answer in one sentence.<|eot_id|>Assistant: \"), greedy output is \"The capital of France is Paris.\" then end of text. The earlier loop was an instruct model given a raw story prompt, not a kernel bug. TIMING STILL VOID: generation measured 0.79 t/s at 09:13 and 5.78 t/s at 09:31 on the same binary (node contended both times), so no number is quotable until a quiet window. NEXT STEP: step 5, our packed-trit matvec (f32_trits ternary_dot rows) in the transformer path, and one bitnet.cpp llama-bench row (-t 4, pp128 / tg64, -r 5) in the SAME quiet node window, booked via QUIET-WINDOW-FORECAST.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_19 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 19u32, "2026-11-08T17:45Z", "tibia", "11-08 13:5x tibia: STEP 4c PRE-REGISTERED as a MEASUREMENT (before the run; runs on the EPYC 9255 rental, RENT-REHEARSAL-EPYC9255). Step 4b's QAT program (scratch qat_cosine.spi: stories260K start, WarmupCosine peak 1e-3 warmup 100, AdamW, training seed 1234567, the same 8 held-out evaluation windows, eval every 250 steps, C -O2 -fopenmp) in three arms that change only steps and batch, decay_steps = steps: (A) batch 4 x 8,000 steps; (B) batch 16 x 2,000 steps; (C) batch 16 x 8,000 steps. Reference: 4b (batch 4 x 2,000) ended at ternary 2.006, fp32 1.552. SOFT EXPECTATIONS: A < 1.95; B < 1.95 (4x the tokens of 4b in the same steps); C lowest of the three, < 1.85; none reaches fp32's 1.552. Recorded whatever happens; an arm cut by the rental's end is reported with its last evaluation and step, not extrapolated.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_20 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 20u32, "2026-11-08T23:57Z", "tibia", "11-08 20:0x tibia: QUEUED on ganymede: job-1794182216647-tibia-bitnet-linux (--after tibia-zig-smoke2), script /root/tibia-jobs/bitnet-linux.sh. It installs clang+ninja if missing, pulls the PINNED GGUF from HF (verified by sha256), builds bitnet.cpp 0b341e582afb with clang (a Linux shared build is fine), and runs the 2B chat correctness probe (\"capital of France\"). NO timing claims (shared vCPUs; timing waits for k3s pinned pods).")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_21 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 21u32, "2026-11-09T00:49Z", "tibia", "11-08 20:4x tibia: STEP 4c MOVED from the cancelled EPYC rental to europa (2 vCPU, 24/7 saturation node). The arms are unchanged from note 19 (qat_cosine.spi with steps and batch edited, decay_steps = steps): A = batch 4 x 8000, B = batch 16 x 2000, C = batch 16 x 8000. Compiled to C on moon (3 edits per arm, verified), then gcc -O2 -fopenmp on europa. One deviation: OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 per arm, versus 8 for 4b. A and B run side by side (1 core each); C starts when either finishes. Each arm runs as a systemd unit with MemoryMax 300M (600M total), Nice 10. Pins verified on europa: stories260K sha b0a507e7..., valid_tok512 c309447f.... Thread count changes OpenMP reduction order, so expect small float drift against a multi-threaded run. That does not affect the pre-registered loss expectations. Wall time is NOT a timing claim. Started 2026-11-09T00:47Z. Logs: europa /root/tibia-qat/qat_arm_{a,b,c}.log (eval every 250 steps). Estimate: A and B take hours each and C about 4x that; a partial curve is reported as partial.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_22 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 22u32, "2026-11-09T02:42Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:5x tibia: STEP 4c arms A and B MEASURED (europa, 1 thread each, side by side). The start reproduces exactly: fp32 1.5520525 and PTQ ternary 7.1150646, as in 3a, so the 1-thread build matches. ARM A (batch 4 x 8000 steps, cosine to 0 at 8000), ternary eval every 1000: 2.295, 2.278, 2.219, 2.126, 2.045, 1.991, 1.943, 1.889. Final 1.8895, so the expectation A < 1.95 HOLDS. ARM B (batch 16 x 2000): 2.304, 2.232, 2.191, 2.100, 2.071, 2.030, 1.976, 1.892. Final 1.8920, so B < 1.95 HOLDS. A and B land within 0.003 nats with the same token count (32k windows), so batch vs steps barely matters here at equal tokens; B used 4x fewer optimizer steps. Gap to fp32: 0.34 nats (4b: 0.45); 94 pct of the 5.56-nat PTQ gap is recovered. Side observation: after QAT the fp32 MASTER weights evaluate at 4.42-4.48 nats, much worse than the start. The masters drift to serve the ternary forward pass and are no longer a usable fp32 model, as expected with straight-through QAT. Wall time (A 5209 s, B 5084 s, shared 2 vCPU) is NOT a timing claim. ARM C (16 x 8000) started 2026-11-09T02:14Z under MemoryMax 300M; expect about 4x the wall time.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_23 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 23u32, "2026-11-09T02:42Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:5x tibia: STEP 4d PRE-REGISTERED as a MEASUREMENT (before the run). A SEED REPLICATE of arm B (batch 16 x 2000, WarmupCosine peak 1e-3, warmup 100, decay 2000, AdamW, the same 8 held-out eval windows), changing ONLY the training-window seed from 1234567 to 7654321. It runs on europa's free core next to arm C (1 thread, MemoryMax 300M). Purpose: the A-vs-B difference of 0.003 nats means nothing without seed noise. Report the final ternary loss and |B - B2|. Soft expectation: |B - B2| is between 0.005 and 0.03 nats, so A ~ B is within seed noise and batch-vs-steps at equal tokens is a wash for this model. If |B - B2| < 0.003, the A/B comparison is resolvable and A (more steps) slightly better is the reading. Recorded whatever it shows; one replicate is not a confidence interval and won't be reported as one.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_24 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 24u32, "2026-11-09T02:48Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:0x tibia: bitnet.cpp on LINUX is CORRECT (ganymede job-1794184179697-tibia-bitnet-linux2; correctness only, no timing; pinned to 2 cores). Pinned gguf sha 4221b252... verified; BitNet 0b341e5 built with clang -DLLAMA_BUILD_TOOLS=ON -DLLAMA_BUILD_COMMON=ON (as a subproject, llama.cpp turns tools OFF, so the first try had no llama-completion target). Plus libomp-dev, so OpenMP is found. Greedy, -t 2, prompt \"What is the capital of France? Answer in one sentence.\" Answer: \"Paris is the capital of France.\", then greedy repetition. That matches the Windows node reference. The Linux reference path for 2B-4T now exists on a 24/7 node.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_25 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 25u32, "2026-11-09T03:55Z", "tibia", "11-09 00:2x tibia: STEP 5 PRE-REGISTERED (before any code). The packed-trit INFERENCE path for stories260K after QAT. Weights: arm A's final masters (or arm C's if it beats A), quantized once per matrix (absmean gamma, lib f32_trits pack); the 7 linear matrices per layer are stored as trits n plus gamma, and each output row is gamma * ternary_dot(row, x) instead of the fp32 dot. Embedding, norms and the classifier stay fp32 (unchanged from QAT). MEASUREMENTS. (1) CORRECTNESS, the gate: mean CE on the same 8 held-out eval windows from the packed path equals the dequantized-fp32 ternary forward within 1e-4 nats (same math, different storage). (2) STORAGE: bytes of the linear weights, packed vs fp32, exact (expected ~16x smaller: 2 bits vs 32, plus one f32 gamma per matrix). (3) SPEED, per fiscal's timing rules (studied-engineering-techniques): tok/s for a fixed 256-token greedy generation; balanced-order pairs (fp32, packed) in fresh processes, one toggle per campaign, signed deltas; nearest-rank integer quantiles ceil(n*p/1000), per-run quantiles never pooled; an A/A arm (fp32 vs fp32) against an independent outside timer; a canary first, below 70 pct CPU; warmup as its own population. Only on a QUIET host (jupiter is benchmarks-only, manual/night; never ganymede under shared load). SOFT EXPECTATIONS, stated now: (1) passes; (2) about 15-16x; (3) packed is SLOWER on stories260K, 1.5-3x fewer tok/s. The model fits in cache, so fp32 is not bandwidth-bound there, and the lib decodes one trit per shift/mask with a branch. A speed win needs a bandwidth-bound model (stories15M+) and a byte-wise LUT decode (4 trits per lookup); that is step 6, not this one.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_26 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 26u32, "2026-11-09T04:43Z", "tibia", "11-09 00:4x tibia: STEP 4d MEASURED (europa, 1 thread). Seed replicate B2 (batch 16 x 2000, training seed 7654321, otherwise identical to B): ternary eval every 250 steps 2.345, 2.253, 2.163, 2.108, 2.081, 2.040, 2.037, 1.918. Final 1.9176. The start reproduces again (fp32 1.5520525, PTQ 7.1150646). |B - B2| = |1.8920 - 1.9176| = 0.0256 nats: the soft expectation (between 0.005 and 0.03) HOLDS. READING: the A-vs-B difference (0.0025 nats) is 10x smaller than one seed swap, so at equal tokens (32k windows) batch 4 x 8000 vs batch 16 x 2000 is NOT resolvable for this model; call it a wash. B's 4x fewer optimizer steps make it the cheaper schedule for the same result. One replicate is not a CI and is not reported as one. Wall 5883 s (shared 2 vCPU, not a timing claim). Arm C (16 x 8000, 4x the tokens) is still running; its comparison is against seed noise of about 0.03, so C must beat ~1.86 to count as a real token-scaling gain.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_27 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 27u32, "2026-11-09T04:46Z", "tibia", "11-09 00:4x tibia: STEP 4e PRE-REGISTERED (before the run). Seed replicate A2 = arm A (batch 4 x 8000, cosine decay 8000) with ONLY the training seed changed, 1234567 -> 7654321 (the same seed as B2). Runs on europa's free core next to arm C (1 thread, MemoryMax 300M). With two seeds per arm, A vs B compares means of 2: A = (1.8895 + A2)/2 vs B = (1.8920 + 1.9176)/2 = 1.9048. Soft expectation: |A2 - A| is between 0.005 and 0.03 (like B), and the two-seed means differ by less than 0.02, so the wash reading stands. If A2 also lands below B2 by more than 0.02, more optimizer steps at equal tokens helps after all; record it as a 2-seed observation, not a significance claim.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_28 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 28u32, "2026-11-09T06:18Z", "tibia", "11-09 02:2x tibia: STEP 4e MEASURED (europa, 1 thread). A2 (batch 4 x 8000, training seed 7654321): final ternary 1.8747 (eval 7250-8000: 1.932, 1.943, 1.884, 1.875). |A - A2| = |1.8895 - 1.8747| = 0.0148, so the seed-noise expectation (0.005-0.03) HOLDS. TWO-SEED COMPARISON at equal tokens (32k windows): A mean = (1.8895 + 1.8747)/2 = 1.8821; B mean = (1.8920 + 1.9176)/2 = 1.9048; difference 0.0227. Paired by seed, A - B = -0.0025 (seed 1234567) and -0.0429 (seed 7654321). The soft expectation \"means differ by less than 0.02\" FAILS narrowly. The pre-registered alternative applies: A2 lands below B2 by 0.043 (> 0.02), so MORE OPTIMIZER STEPS at equal tokens (batch 4 x 8000) is better than bigger batches (16 x 2000) on BOTH seeds, by about 0.02 nats on average. A 2-seed observation, NOT a significance claim; seed noise is about 0.015-0.026 per arm. Practical reading: at this scale, steps matter a little more than batch size for the same data. Arm C (16 x 8000) is still running; it compares against A's 2-seed mean 1.882.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_29 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 29u32, "2026-11-09T07:55Z", "tibia", "11-09 03:5x tibia: STEP 4c ARM C MEASURED (europa, 1 thread, wall 20127 s: shared 2 vCPU, not a timing claim). C = batch 16 x 8000 steps (4x the tokens of A/B), cosine to 0 at 8000. Ternary eval every 1000 steps: 2.143, 2.133, 2.050, 2.036, 2.045, 1.967, 1.941, 1.822. Final 1.8219. The start reproduces again (fp32 1.5520525, PTQ 7.1150646). AGAINST NOTE 19's PRE-REGISTRATION: \"A < 1.95\" HELD (1.8895); \"B < 1.95\" HELD (1.8920); \"C lowest of the three, < 1.85\" HELD (1.8219); \"none reaches fp32 1.552\" HELD (gap 0.27 nats). AGAINST SEED NOISE (notes 26/28): C beats A's 2-seed mean 1.8821 by 0.060 and B's 1.9048 by 0.083, which is 2-4x the per-arm seed spread (0.015-0.026). So 4x the tokens is a REAL gain, not noise, on one seed of C. 95.1 pct of the 5.56-nat PTQ gap is recovered (4b: 92 pct). Curve note: the last 1000 steps (cosine tail at near-zero lr) gave the biggest drop (1.941 -> 1.822), as in 4b; the low-lr tail matters more than anything else in the schedule. The fp32 masters again become unusable on their own (4.88). SUMMARY of step 4c: at this scale, tokens > optimizer steps > batch size; the best ternary stories260K is arm C at 1.822. It is the weight set for step 5's packed inference (note 25).")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_30 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 30u32, "2026-11-09T07:56Z", "tibia", "11-09 03:5x tibia: STEP 4f PRE-REGISTERED (before the runs), europa's 2 free cores, 1 thread each, MemoryMax 300M each. (C2) arm C with ONLY the training seed changed to 7654321: confirms the token-scaling gain with 2 seeds. Soft expectation: |C - C2| between 0.005 and 0.03, and the C 2-seed mean stays below A's 1.882 by more than 0.03. (D) batch 16 x 16000 steps (8x the tokens of A/B, 2x C), cosine decay 16000, seed 1234567: does the curve keep falling? Soft expectation: D < C by 0.02-0.06 (diminishing returns: C gained 0.06 over A for 4x tokens, so 2x more should give less), and D still above fp32 1.552. Expected wall time: C2 ~5.5 h, D ~11 h (shared, not timing claims). An arm cut by the autonomous window's end (21:00) is reported with its last eval, not extrapolated.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_31 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 31u32, "2026-11-09T14:34Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:3x tibia: STEP 4f ARM C2 RESULT (europa unit tibia-qat_arm_c2, 1 thread, rc 0, wall 23125 s = 6.4 h, longer than the ~5.5 h estimate because europa is shared). Ternary eval at 2000/4000/6000/8000: 2.0915 / 2.0396 / 1.9516 / 1.8175. vs C (seed 1234567) 1.8219: |C - C2| = 0.0044, just BELOW the soft band 0.005-0.03 (seed spread is smaller than expected). C 2-seed mean 1.8197, which is 0.062 below A's 1.882 (A 2-seed mean), against the soft >0.03 margin: MET. So the token-scaling gain (4x tokens: 1.882 -> 1.820) REPLICATES across training seeds. Also seen: the `after fp32` line reads 5.161 for this arm, i.e. the latent fp32 shadow weights after QAT are not a usable fp32 model (consistent with the earlier arms; the fp32 baseline stays 1.552). Arm D (16 x 16000) is still running (~4.9 h CPU at 77 pct), ETA about 15:00 local.")
inl note_of_transformer_quant_ternary_32 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", 32u32, "2026-11-09T19:35Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:2x tibia: STEP 4f ARM D RESULT (europa unit tibia-qat_arm_d, 1 thread, rc 0, wall 41166 s = 11.4 h; batch 16 x 16000 steps, cosine 16000, seed 1234567). Ternary eval at 4000/8000/12000/16000: 2.0728 / 2.0157 / 1.9225 / 1.7692. Against note 30's soft expectations: \"D < C by 0.02-0.06\" MET (C two-seed mean 1.8197, D 1.7692: -0.0505); \"D still above fp32 1.552\" MET (gap 0.217). TOKEN SCALING (QAT ternary, stories260K): A (4000 steps, 2-seed mean) 1.882 -> C (8000 x 16 = 4x tokens) 1.8197 (-0.062) -> D (2x more) 1.7692 (-0.0505). Diminishing but NOT flat: doubling tokens still bought 80 pct of the previous 4x gain, so the curve has not saturated at 16000 steps. The latent fp32 shadow line reads 5.00 (unusable as an fp32 model, as in every arm). All of step 4f's arms are recorded (C2 note 31, D here). Next for the item: step 5 (packed ternary inference, note 25) needs a quiet host. A longer arm (32000 steps, ~23 h on one europa thread) is only worth it if the 0.05-per-doubling trend is the question.")
inl tibia_ternary_policy_weights () = Task ("TIBIA-TERNARY-POLICY-WEIGHTS", "tibia: optional ternary policy weights {-1, 0, +1} packed 2 bits each for the network and hashed brains, using the lib kernel from TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY, so evolution and inference do add/subtract instead of multiply with less memory traffic on CPU and WGSL (the plan from the deleted docs/MODELING.md, restored)", Story, P3, D4, 0u32, Planned, "TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", "tibia,team:tibia,ml,ternary,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_ternary_policy_weights () = Planning ("TIBIA-TERNARY-POLICY-WEIGHTS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_ternary_policy_weights_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-TERNARY-POLICY-WEIGHTS", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:35Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia: RESTORED claim. Source: git show 949351b^:docs/MODELING.md line 29, \"| Policy weights | Optional ternary weights {-1, 0, +1} packed 2 bits each (from TritCritNet): add/subtract instead of multiply, less memory traffic on CPU and WGSL |\", dropped without a reason by DC1 on 10-22 (see TIBIA-DOCS-TO-CODE). Gated on the lib kernel showing a measured win on the transformer first (the split agreed with main on 11-07). DoD: a ternary weight type as a union-backed packed array, network::decide over it, held-out worth of a ternary-evolved network vs the integer network pre-registered and run, memory per lane quoted. NEXT: wait for TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY.")
inl transformer_train () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN", "Transformer training in Spiral: gradients, AdamW and a data pipeline for the llama2.c architecture, reproducing the llama2.c training runs as the oracle, then a ternary-trained arm", Feature, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD,TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP,TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE,TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY", "transformer,tibia,training,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_train () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN", Minutes 960u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_transformer_train_1 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "User 11-07 (via main): create tasks so transformer and tibia reap the TritCritNet wisdom, we should have been planning training by now; the reuse assessment is ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107 n6. TritCritNet means the most advanced C++ version (i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet-cpp\\tritcritnet.cpp, alpha716, 19,878 lines): a byte-level language model trainer with embeddings, gated SSM-style layers, criticality-gated local attention islands, AdamW, layernorm, fake-quant ternary weights and hash-split train/val/test windows, never checked against an outside benchmark. PLAN: inference already matches llama2.c (TRANSFORMER-CPU-REFERENCE Done); training is the missing half. The oracle is llama2.c's own training recipe (train.py, TinyStories pretokenized with the same tokenizer) and the validation losses its README publishes for its small models: pin the commit, the configs and the published numbers in the first child's first note before any claim. Children: TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD, TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP, TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE, TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY. DoD: a model trained by Spiral code reaches the published validation loss of the same config within a pre-registered tolerance, and then generates through the existing inference path. TypeFeatures: tensor shapes as type-level sizes, parameter and gradient tensors as one typed record so the optimizer cannot mix them.")
inl note_of_transformer_train_2 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:52Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia (groom on receipt): the parent now depends on its children, as other parents here do (TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS, COMPILER-TYPE-ARITH-NORMALIZE), so it no longer lists as ready work before the children finish. Children are unchanged.")
inl note_of_transformer_train_3 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN", 3u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint markers): parent of TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD, TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP, TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE and TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY (linked here and on each child; the parent depends on all four). Next step: pin the oracle before any code: the llama2.c commit, its train.py configs for the smallest model, and its published val losses, written on this item. TypeFeatures: model configs as records with type-level dims (the same sized shapes inference uses), the optimizer state as a record, not parallel arrays.")
inl note_of_transformer_train_4 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN", 4u32, "2026-11-07T15:39Z", "main", "main 11-07: this stack is the backbone and the generation baseline of CONVERGENCE-LAB's single SOTA target (n6: a schema-bound decision model on the public accuracy-per-cost frontier); TRANSFORMER-CPU-SPEED and TRANSFORMER-BEAT-MOJO set its latency axis, TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY and TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY its weight-bytes axis.")
inl transformer_train_grad () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD", "Transformer gradients: reverse-mode backward for every op of the llama2.c model (embedding, rmsnorm, RoPE, attention with causal mask, SwiGLU, logits, cross-entropy), checked by finite differences and against a pinned PyTorch autograd run", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "TRANSFORMER-CPU-REFERENCE", "transformer,tibia,training,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_train_grad () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl transformer_train_loop () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP", "Transformer training loop: AdamW, warmup plus cosine schedule, gradient clipping, deterministic seeded batches, checkpoints in llama2.c format; reproduce a PyTorch training curve on CPU at a scaled stories260K config (batch 4x128, dropout 0, seeded windows over TinyStories-valid with tok512)", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD", "transformer,tibia,training,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_train_loop () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl transformer_train_scale () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE", "Transformer training at the 15M scale: the same loop on the node CPUs or a rented GPU (WGSL or CUDA kernels from the same source) reaching llama2.c published validation loss for that config", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP", "transformer,tibia,training,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_train_scale () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_transformer_train_scale_1 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of TRANSFORMER-TRAIN. Budget: GPU rental stays inside the 20 USD cap (memory gpu-rental-permission) or uses node CPUs. DoD: published validation loss reached within the tolerance; wall clock and cost per run recorded beside the PyTorch reference on the same hardware; the checkpoint published as a CI download, never committed.")
inl note_of_transformer_train_scale_2 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint markers): child of TRANSFORMER-TRAIN. Next step: wait for TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP; then estimate 15M training cost from the loop's measured step time before choosing node CPUs or a rented GPU (Europa only, $20 cap, delete right after use). TypeFeatures: the run plan (host, steps, checkpoint cadence) as a record, the host as a union.")
inl note_of_transformer_train_scale_3 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-SCALE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T15:08Z", "tibia", "11-10 11:1x tibia: provider update. The GPU host is now RunPod (user 11-10: key in ~/.secrets/runpod.env,  GPU cap with .73 left; the earlier Europa-only rule is superseded). Measured today: H200 bf16 matmul 814 TFLOPS and HBM copy 4.3 TB/s (torch), H100 secure .99/h, ready in 22 s on a good host; a scripted one-shot rental (create, run, terminate) cost .11 for 95 s. Datacenter Hopper exposes CUDA, not Vulkan, so the GPU path for training is CUDA (Spiral --backend 'Cpp + Cuda', ~~> CudaDevice; general code waits on COMPILER-CUDA-ARRAY-LENGTH). Next step: after TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP measures a step time, estimate the 15M run's cost on an H100 vs node CPUs.")
inl transformer_train_ternary () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY", "Transformer ternary training: quantization-aware training with weights in {-1,0,+1} and 8-bit activations (the BitNet b1.58 recipe), compared with fp32 at equal parameters and at equal memory", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP,TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY", "transformer,tibia,training,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_train_ternary () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_transformer_train_ternary_1 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of TRANSFORMER-TRAIN. TritCritNet trained with fake-quant ternary weights (threshold 0.25, straight-through) but never measured it against fp32 on a public task; this is that measurement. Read the BitNet b1.58 paper's recipe before coding (absmean weight scaling, activation quantization) and pin it in the first note. DoD: pre-registered comparison (KIT-EXPERIMENTS ledger) of validation loss for fp32 vs ternary at equal parameter count and at equal memory; the trained ternary model runs through TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY's packed kernels with identical tokens to its fake-quant evaluation.")
inl note_of_transformer_train_ternary_2 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint markers): child of TRANSFORMER-TRAIN. Next step: wait for TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-LOOP and TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY; then pre-register the comparison (ternary-aware vs fp32 at equal params AND equal memory) before any run. TypeFeatures: the weight representation as a union (Dense | Ternary) so one training loop serves both arms.")
inl tibia_gradient_policy () = Task ("TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY", "tibia gradient-trained policies: behaviour cloning then policy gradient in the batched simulator, on the shared autodiff lib, measured against the ES and CEM trainers on the BENCHMARK held-out seeds", Feature, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "TIBIA-BC-POLICY,TIBIA-PG-POLICY", "tibia,training,ml,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_gradient_policy () = Planning ("TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY", Minutes 480u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_gradient_policy_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "User 11-07 (via main): create tasks so transformer and tibia reap the TritCritNet wisdom, we should have been planning training by now; the reuse assessment is ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107 n6. TritCritNet means the most advanced C++ version (i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet-cpp\\tritcritnet.cpp, alpha716, 19,878 lines): a byte-level language model trainer with embeddings, gated SSM-style layers, criticality-gated local attention islands, AdamW, layernorm, fake-quant ternary weights and hash-split train/val/test windows, never checked against an outside benchmark. tibia today learns only gradient-free (TIBIA-EVOLVED-POLICY, TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION, TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS CEM). Children: TIBIA-BC-POLICY, TIBIA-PG-POLICY. DoD: a gradient-trained typed network policy beats the best ES or CEM policy on held-out seeds at an equal simulator budget, pre-registered in the KIT-EXPERIMENTS ledger, and then runs live through the policy path. Ternary weights stay an option through TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY's type.")
inl note_of_tibia_gradient_policy_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:52Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia (groom on receipt): the parent now depends on its children, as other parents here do (TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS, COMPILER-TYPE-ARITH-NORMALIZE), so it no longer lists as ready work before the children finish. Children are unchanged.")
inl note_of_tibia_gradient_policy_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY", 3u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint markers): parent of TIBIA-BC-POLICY and TIBIA-PG-POLICY (linked here and on each child; the parent depends on both). Next step: run TIBIA-BC-POLICY first, once TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD ships the shared gradient engine. TypeFeatures: the policy's inputs stay the typed 25-input view network.spi already uses; its outputs stay the decision record.")
inl tibia_bc_policy () = Task ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", "tibia behaviour cloning: train the typed network policy on traces from the scripted and tuned policies in the batched simulator, cross-entropy on actions, using the shared gradient engine", Story, P1, D4, 95u32, Active, "TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD", "tibia,training,ml,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_bc_policy () = Planning ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY. DoD: the cloned network reproduces its teacher's actions on held-out seeds above a pre-registered agreement and scores within the teacher's confidence interval on the BENCHMARK metric (kills subject to deaths); bit-identical training on Rust and C; the run budget recorded.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint markers): child of TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY. Next step: wait for TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD; meanwhile the dataset is defined: (observation, decision) pairs logged from live_retreat_tactic and the evolved rules on training seeds only, never held-out seeds. TypeFeatures: a logged pair is a record of the typed view and the decision record, not a flat array.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 3u32, "2026-11-08T01:30Z", "tibia", "11-07 21:3x tibia: STARTED (dep TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD is Done). Design, read from src/network.spi: the policy network is INTEGER fixed point: 8 sensed inputs scaled by one = 256, 6 ReLU hidden units (integer division by 256), and 3 outputs (heal, engage, retreat) thresholded by decision_of (heal > 0; engage when > 0 and >= retreat; retreat when > 0 and > engage). Cloning with the shared f32 gradient engine therefore means an f32 shadow network of the same shape (weights = i32 / 256), trained with per-output logistic losses: heal as a binary target, engage and retreat as two binary targets that reproduce decision_of's tie rule. Then quantize back with round(w * 256) and require the INTEGER network to agree with the teacher (that agreement is what gets pre-registered). Steps of at most 120 min: (1) lib ops relu / relu_backward and bce_logits / bce_logits_backward (the stable max(z, 0) - z y + log(1 + e^-|z|), with gradient sigmoid(z) - y); (2) the dataset logger: (sensed inputs, teacher decision) pairs from live_retreat_tactic and the evolved rules on TRAINING seeds only; (3) the shadow forward/backward and AdamW training via f32_optim, plus quantization; (4) pre-registered agreement and BENCHMARK score on held-out seeds, and a Rust/C bit-identical check. STEP 1 DRAFTED: kit drafts TIBIA-BC-POLICY\\pkg\\f32_grads.spi A83EE8B3EF48 (on top of the landed 7862EA5B6C2D) with 3 new tests: relu backward vs central differences away from the kink; BCE gradient vs central differences at 4 points (one saturated at z = 25); and the exact values at z = 0, log 2 and -0.5. Box: --check passes, formatter-clean, cell budget 0. RUNNING: node job-1794101374073-tibia-grads4-cells.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 4u32, "2026-11-08T01:30Z", "tibia", "11-07 21:3x tibia: STEP 2 DESIGNED (code next session; it touches the simulator's think path, so not started late in a run). Hook points in src/hunting_pack.spi. Inputs: features camp attackers now p (line ~1632), the same 8-input network::inputs the student will see. Teacher decision at a think, for a Rules brain: heal = wants_heal b brain attackers p (~1744); (retreat, engagement) = after_heal_plan b brain attackers p (~1807), which for Rules is rules_plan (~1764: policy::retreats + policy::engages on the observation). The student's network_plan maps decision::engage through network_engagement (~1768), so the label engage = (the rules' engagement equals network_engagement obs true), and retreat is the plan's retreat flag; heal is a separate binary. Logging: a pure dataset pass rather than a new brain arm. dataset_of camp teacher seeds steps re-simulates each training seed with the teacher tactic and, at every target_turn, records { x : network::inputs; heal : bool; engage : bool; retreat : bool } (a typed record, per the TypeFeatures note). The cleanest hook is a variant of acts_on_target that returns the pair next to the pack. Training seeds only (training_first 1-100); held-out 1001-1100 stay unseen until step 4. NEXT STEP: implement dataset_of with a test: the logged pairs' count equals the number of target turns in one seeded hunt, and the logged decision replays the teacher's own heal/retreat.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 5u32, "2026-11-08T02:04Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:0x tibia: STEP 1 LANDED: spiral/lib/spiral/f32_grads.spi 530275B20359 (lib_land_window green: consumers compile, document_test 26 passed, type probe 13 tests typed / 0 errors, respell_drift 0; lib digest 00887D63AB1E5E7F; undo 20261107-215343; unstaged). It adds relu / relu_backward and bce_logits / bce_logits_backward. Node proof before the land: job-1794101374073-tibia-grads4-cells, 26/26 rows (13 tests x c, rust; slowest cell 164 s). NEXT STEP: step 2, the dataset logger, per note 4's design.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 6u32, "2026-11-08T02:04Z", "tibia", "11-07 22:0x tibia: STEP 2 DETAIL found while reading, for whoever implements it. (a) The ENGAGE LABEL IS NOT ALWAYS IDENTIFIABLE: the student's stance is network_engagement obs engage (Strike if in reach and strike-ready, Approach if out of reach, otherwise Hold), so whenever network_engagement obs true = Hold (no target, or in reach but strike not ready), engage = true and engage = false give the same action. Those rows should carry an engage MASK (excluded from the engage loss), not a guessed label. Where the target is identifiable, label engage = (teacher stance <> Hold). (b) Logging needs a new pack field (a list of pairs, empty unless logging is on, like soft_logged's log path) so it threads through the beat loop; acts_on_target / target_turn (~1995-2003) is where the teacher's (retreat, stance) is known, and wants_heal is evaluated earlier in the beat. That changes the core pack record, so it deserves a fresh session and the full tibia gate after. Deliberately NOT started at 22:0x in an unattended run.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 7u32, "2026-11-08T19:39Z", "tibia", "11-08 15:4x tibia: STEP 2 DRAFTED, with a design change from note 6: NO change to the core pack record. A new module tibia/src/bc_dataset.spi (A7AA40631FA3, registered last in src/spiral.toml; unstaged) runs its own copy of the tick loop (pairs_from: before each hunting_pack::advance, if the lead knight decides this tick, record a pair) and keeps the pairs in the driver's accumulator. Reason: a list field in the pack would have to compile to WGSL too (lanes_gpu), and would cost every simulation a field copy for a CPU-only feature. Each pair is a typed record { x : network::inputs; heal; engage; retreat }, and each label is a union Known : bool | Masked. heal is Masked unless a heal is ready (otherwise the network's heal cannot act). retreat and engage are Masked without a target (the simulator patrols and never reads the plan). engage is also Masked where network_engagement o true = Hold (engage and hold give the same stance), per note 6a. Labels come from the simulator's own functions on the SAME aimed pack as x: aimed_by, attackers_of, features, wants_heal, after_heal_plan. Approximation: x is read before the tick's foes act, so it lags the knight's view by one tick, and the plan is read before the heal gate. That's fine for cloning, which needs consistent (x, teacher(x)) pairs. The four repeated arguments are grouped into a moment record (cell budget). TESTS (///> c): (1) a NETWORK teacher's Known labels equal network::decide w x on every logged x, and the data holds at least one Known heal and one Known retreat (non-vacuous): proves x and labels come from the same pack; (2) a Rules dataset (live_retreat_tactic 160 2, 2 training seeds, 400 ticks) is nonempty and deterministic. Box: --check passes, formatter clean, cell budget 0 over, tibia build.ps1 -ChecksOnly green. RUNNING: node Cells run via mirror tibia-gates3 (job tibia-bcdataset-cells). NEXT STEP: step 3, the f32 shadow network (weights = i32 / 256) trained with per-output BCE on the masked labels through f32_grads + f32_optim, then quantized back with round(w * 256).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 8u32, "2026-11-08T20:12Z", "tibia", "11-08 16:1x tibia: STEP 2 PROVEN: node job-1794167547028-tibia-bcdataset-cells3 (mirror tibia-gates3 linked to a fresh spiral mirror tibia-gates3s): bc_dataset discovered 2, executed 2, passed 2, failed 0 (c), 239 s. tibia/src/bc_dataset.spi 4393B9203BBC (unstaged). Two VOID rounds first, both environment, recorded for the next lane that adds a tibia src module: (1) the plain tibia mirror links the node's BASE spiral clone, which lacks parallel::map_index -> sync spiral first and pass -SpiralMirror (node-repo-mirrors-use-base-spiral-lib); (2) a src module without the '///- --package .' line-1 header plus the ':# <module> static =' block compiles as a standalone notebook (main.spi) with every sibling unbound, although box --check passes (check-skips-test-bodies). NEXT STEP: step 3, the f32 shadow network (8 inputs, 6 ReLU hidden, 3 outputs; weights = i32 / 256) trained with per-output BCE on the Known labels only (Masked rows contribute zero gradient) through f32_grads + f32_optim, then quantized back with round(w * 256); pre-register the integer network's agreement on held-out seeds before running.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 9u32, "2026-11-08T22:14Z", "tibia", "11-08 18:2x tibia: STEP 3 PROVEN: node job-1794175728740-tibia-bctrain-cells2 (mirror tibia-gates3 + fresh spiral mirror; apps/arena/probe.spi formatter-joined in the MIRROR ONLY, because the box copy is the user's split if/then form that the pack62 formatter rejects until pack63b): bc_train discovered 2, executed 2, passed 2, failed 0 (c), build exit 0. New module tibia/src/bc_train.spi 61A00A541DB0 (unstaged; registered after bc_dataset). It holds the f32 SHADOW of network.spi with the same 66-weight layout, so quantizing is round(w * 256) per weight back through network::with_weight. Inputs are read as network::dot_with of a one-hot coefficient divided by 256; hidden = relu; outputs use logit z = o - 1 (the integer threshold); per-output BCE counts Known labels only (Masked rows give zero gradient). Training is full-batch through f32_grads + f32_optim AdamW; the init is a seeded spread in [-0.25, 0.25] (zero init would leave every ReLU dead). TESTS: (1) the analytic gradient equals the central difference at 3 weights (an output weight, an input weight, a retreat-head weight) on a synthetic all-Known example; (2) a student trained 400 steps on a NETWORK teacher's logged pairs, then quantized, agrees with the teacher on >= 95 pct of Known labels. Cell-budget lesson: a definition with no blank line before a following ///> test is measured TOGETHER with the test. NEXT STEP: step 4, PRE-REGISTERED before any run: the RULES teacher (live_retreat_tactic 160 2) on training seeds 1-100, the student quantized, agreement measured on HELD-OUT seeds 1001-1100 (never logged for training); the bar is >= 90 pct of Known labels per head, with the heal/engage/retreat split reported. Then the BENCHMARK kills-minus-deaths score of the cloned network vs its teacher within the teacher's confidence interval, and a Rust/C bit-identical training check.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_10 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 10u32, "2026-11-08T22:41Z", "tibia", "11-08 18:5x tibia: STEP 4a MEASURED against the pre-registered bar (ganymede job-1794176918781-tibia-bc-run3, apps/predict/bc_run.spi via predict.ps1 -Module bc_run, C -O2, 728 s). Teacher live_retreat_tactic 160 2 on the arena_spot Cyclops camp; 300,000 training pairs from seeds 1-100; 300 full-batch AdamW steps (lr 0.02); final BCE 0.0564; student quantized round(w * 256). HELD-OUT seeds 1001-1100, agreement on Known labels per head: heal 255131/255928 = 99.7 pct (bar >= 90: MET); engage 26504/26504 = 100 pct (MET); retreat 56704/234692 = 24.2 pct (FAILED). Training seeds give the same picture (retreat 58960/236545 = 24.9 pct), so this is NOT overfitting. The float loss is low, so the gap appears at the integer decision. HYPOTHESIS (not yet tested; note 3 planned for it, step 3 did not implement it): decision_of couples the heads (retreat = r > 0 && r > e; engage wins ties), so independent per-head BCE heads can both fire and the integer rule turns teacher-retreat rows into engage. Rounding to integer weights is the other suspect. FIX FOUND ON THE WAY: run2 crashed with exit 139 (segfault) = stack overflow. core listm::map is foldBack, recursing once per element over 300k pairs; ulimit -s unlimited confirmed it (run3 completed). bc_train now maps through a tail-recursive fold (examples_of; unstaged, box-checked, budget 0). NEXT STEP: step 4b, first LOCATE the loss: score the float shadow (before quantizing) under (i) independent per-head thresholds and (ii) decision_of's coupled rule, plus a confusion table of teacher retreat vs student {retreat, engage, neither}. If (ii) is the gap, retrain with a coupled loss: on rows where retreat is Known-true, add a margin term pushing r above e (or a 3-way softmax over neither/engage/retreat). Pre-register the 90 pct bar again before the rerun.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_11 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 11u32, "2026-11-08T23:12Z", "tibia", "11-08 19:2x tibia: STEP 4b LOCATED the retreat gap (ganymede job-1794178747567-tibia-bc-run4, same pre-registered run, now WITHOUT ulimit: the fold-based examples_of fix is proven). Held-out Known retreat labels (234,692): float shadow with INDEPENDENT thresholds 234,550 = 99.94 pct; float shadow under decision_of's COUPLED rule 56,704 = 24.2 pct; integer student 56,704 = 24.2 pct. So training learned retreat; quantization costs nothing (coupled float = integer exactly); the coupling is the whole gap. Confusion: of 177,988 teacher-retreat rows the student retreats on 0 and ENGAGES on 177,988; teacher no-retreat rows 56,704 are all engage too. The engage logit never falls below the retreat logit, and decision_of gives ties to engage. FIX (step 4c, implemented in bc_train, unstaged): on rows where retreat is Known-true, (a) the engage label is masked (the simulator takes the retreat path and never reads engage there), (b) a coupling term BCE(z_r - z_e, 1) pushes the retreat logit above engage, exactly decision_of's condition. The gradient test's synthetic example has retreat = 1, so the central-difference check now covers the coupled term. PRE-REGISTERED for 4c (before the run): same data/seeds/steps/lr as 4a; held-out per-head agreement >= 90 pct for ALL three heads (heal, engage, retreat), reported with the confusion table. Recorded whatever it shows.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_12 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 12u32, "2026-11-08T23:26Z", "tibia", "11-08 19:4x tibia: STEP 4c MEASURED (ganymede job-1794179618317-tibia-bc-4c, same data/seeds/steps as 4a, coupled loss). Final loss 0.0496. HELD-OUT per-head agreement on Known labels: heal 255131/255928 = 99.7 pct (MET); retreat 234594/234692 = 99.96 pct (MET, from 24.2 pct); engage 15532/26504 = 58.6 pct: FAILED AS PRE-REGISTERED (it was 100 pct in 4a). Float retreat: independent 234663, coupled 234658 (both ~99.99 pct). Confusion, teacher retreat -> student retreat/engage/neither: 177983 / 5 / 0; teacher no-retreat -> 93 / 56611 / 0. POST-HOC HYPOTHESIS for engage (labelled post-hoc, not the registered metric): the registered count still scores engage on rows where the teacher RETREATS, which training masks by design because the simulator never reads engage while retreating; a retreating student necessarily has engage = false there. NEXT STEP: one measurement run adding (a) engage agreement restricted to rows where retreat is not Known-true, and (b) ACTION-level agreement, i.e. what the simulator does with the decision (retreat, else strike/approach when engage, else hold), the real fidelity metric. PRE-REGISTER for that run: action agreement >= 90 pct on held-out; the per-head numbers reported beside it unchanged. Then step 5: kills-minus-deaths of the cloned net vs its teacher. GATE NOTE: the gate half of this job did not run the Cells tests, because ganymede's compiler pack formats the OTHER way (it wants the user's split-if form and flags ~17 tibia files with one-line ? ... ?>, incl. bc_run.spi:49), while the box's pack62 joins them. So the tibia layout gate is host-dependent until pack63b is everywhere.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_13 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 13u32, "2026-11-08T23:44Z", "tibia", "11-08 20:0x tibia: STEP 4d MEASURED (ganymede job-1794180453205-tibia-bc-4d, same coupled model as 4c). PRE-REGISTERED ACTION AGREEMENT (what the simulator does: retreat, else engage when identifiable, else hold), held-out targeted rows: 234594/234692 = 99.96 pct, bar >= 90 pct MET. The post-hoc engage hypothesis is CONFIRMED: engage agreement on rows where the teacher does NOT retreat = 15527/15527 = 100 pct, so 4c's 58.6 pct came entirely from teacher-retreat rows that training masks by design. Summary of the clone on held-out seeds 1001-1100: heal 99.7 pct, action 99.96 pct, retreat 99.96 pct. NEXT STEP: step 5, the BENCHMARK score (kills - deaths penalty) of the cloned integer network vs its teacher on the same held-out seeds, within the teacher's confidence interval (pre-register before the run), plus a Rust/C bit-identical training check; and the tibia Cells gate for bc_train once the formatter split (pack63b on the box) settles.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_14 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 14u32, "2026-11-08T23:57Z", "tibia", "11-08 20:0x tibia: QUEUED on ganymede (kit --on, --compile): job-1794182203454-tibia-bc-gate = tibia build.ps1 -Files bc_train (layout under pack63c + cell budget + the Cells tests incl. the coupled-loss gradient check). Script /root/tibia-jobs/bc-gate.sh. On wake: read its result first.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_15 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 15u32, "2026-11-08T23:58Z", "tibia", "11-08 20:1x tibia: STEP 5 PRE-REGISTERED (before any run; code: apps/predict/bc_eval.spi, unstaged). Paired design on HELD-OUT seeds 1001-1100 on the same arena_spot Cyclops camp: each seed is hunted by the TEACHER (live_retreat_tactic 160 2) and by the STUDENT = the same tactic (order, footing, patrol) with brain = Network <the cloned integer net from step 4c/4d: coupled loss, 300 steps, seed-7 init>, scenario_ticks 3000 each. Metric: BENCHMARK kill_score_of (kills - death_penalty * deaths) per hunt. Reported: teacher mean +- 95 pct CI half-width, student mean +- CI, paired-difference mean +- CI. BAR: the student mean lies inside the teacher's 95 pct CI (student_within_teacher_ci95 = 1). Expectation (soft): given 99.96 pct action agreement, the paired difference is near 0, with the CI covering 0. Recorded whatever it shows.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_16 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 16u32, "2026-11-08T23:59Z", "tibia", "11-08 20:1x tibia: QUEUED step 5 on ganymede: job-1794182381701-tibia-bc-eval (--after tibia-bitnet-linux), script /root/tibia-jobs/bc-eval.sh (predict.ps1 -Module bc_eval). On wake: read its 4 result lines first.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_17 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 17u32, "2026-11-09T00:54Z", "tibia", "11-08 21:0x tibia: STEP 5 MEASURED (ganymede job-1794182381701-tibia-bc-eval, 100 held-out seeds 1001-1100, arena_spot Cyclops, 3000 ticks). Teacher kill_score -11.74 +- 5.54 (95 pct CI half-width); student -294.16 +- 31.21; paired difference -282.42 +- 31.86. student_within_teacher_ci95 = 0: the pre-registered BAR FAILED and the soft expectation (paired difference near 0) is WRONG by a wide margin. So 99.96 pct action agreement on held-out TEACHER-visited targeted rows does not transfer to play. Leading hypothesis (from reading the code, not measured): the masks. Retreat is labelled only when the hunter is targeted, engage only when identifiable, heal only when heal_ready. In play, network_plan applies d::retreat and d::engage at EVERY decision moment, including the untargeted ones the clone was never trained on, so the student can retreat or hold where the teacher hunts. Rival: ordinary covariate shift (compounding errors that take the student into states the teacher never visits).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_18 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 18u32, "2026-11-09T00:54Z", "tibia", "11-08 21:0x tibia: STEP 5b PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run). On the STUDENT rollouts (same 100 held-out seeds, same student), at every decision moment, compute the TEACHER plan (after_heal_plan with the teacher brain) and the student plan on the same state. Report disagreement rates in four cells: targeted x {retreat, engage stance} and untargeted x {retreat, engage stance}, plus the fraction of decision moments that are untargeted. Prediction if the MASK hypothesis holds: untargeted retreat disagreement is far above 1 pct (expected > 20 pct), while targeted disagreement stays near the 0.04 pct seen offline. Prediction if COVARIATE SHIFT holds instead: targeted disagreement on student states is clearly above 0.04 pct (expected > 2 pct) and untargeted disagreement is not the dominant term. Both can hold. Whichever wins picks step 6: train on untargeted rows with the teacher label unmasked (mask fix), or DAgger-style relabelling of student states (shift fix).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_19 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 19u32, "2026-11-09T01:46Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:0x tibia: STEP 5b MEASURED (ganymede job-1794185995943-tibia-bc-onpolicy, 100 held-out seeds, teacher vs student plan on the same aimed pack at every decision moment). STUDENT DRIVES: targeted retreat disagreement 1386/182658 = 0.76 pct; targeted stance 29452/182658 = 16.1 pct; untargeted retreat 0/117200; untargeted stance 0/117200; untargeted share 39 pct. TEACHER DRIVES (control): targeted retreat 98/234692 = 0.04 pct (matches offline); targeted stance 10972/234692 = 4.7 pct; untargeted 0/65307 for both; untargeted share 22 pct. VERDICT on the pre-registration: the MASK hypothesis is REFUTED, with untargeted disagreement exactly 0 in both arms against a predicted > 20 pct; untargeted plans evidently do not depend on the brain. The COVARIATE-SHIFT prediction (targeted disagreement > 2 pct on student states) is split: stance 16.1 pct is above it, retreat 0.76 pct is below, but retreat disagreement rises 18x from teacher to student states and the student spends 39 pct of decisions untargeted versus 22 pct. DESIGN FLAW, stated now: the stance cell counts rows where the teacher retreats, and there stance has no effect on action. So 4.7 pct and 16.1 pct overstate action-relevant stance error. Working reading (not yet measured): compounding error, with a small rate of MISSED retreats at fatal moments as the likeliest cause of the -282 score gap.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_20 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 20u32, "2026-11-09T01:47Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:0x tibia: STEP 5c PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_direction.spi). Same 100 held-out seeds, student and teacher as in 5b, both arms (student drives, teacher drives). On TARGETED decision moments: MISSED retreats (teacher retreats, student does not), EXTRA retreats (student retreats, teacher does not), and stance disagreement ONLY on rows where the teacher does not retreat (the action-relevant stance, fixing 5b's design flaw). Per arm: total kills and deaths over the 100 hunts. Consistency check: student kills - 50 x deaths over 100 hunts reproduces step 5's -294.16 mean exactly (same seeds, deterministic sim); a mismatch voids the run. Predictions (soft): under student drive, missed retreats outnumber extra retreats at least 2:1; the student's deaths per hunt are >= 4 versus the teacher's <= 1, so deaths, not kills, carry the gap; action-relevant stance disagreement under student drive is <= 5 pct. If missed retreats dominate, step 6 = DAgger relabelling of student states plus a higher loss weight on retreat-positive rows. Recorded whatever it shows.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_21 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 21u32, "2026-11-09T02:00Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:3x tibia: STEP 5c MEASURED (ganymede job-1794188936296-tibia-bc-direction). The consistency check PASSES: student 284 kills, 594 deaths over 100 hunts = -294.16 per hunt; teacher 726 kills, 38 deaths = -11.74, both exactly step 5. STUDENT DRIVES, targeted moments: missed retreats 30/182658, EXTRA retreats 1356/182658, stance disagreement when the teacher stays 0/133087. TEACHER DRIVES: missed 5/234692, extra 93/234692, stance 0/56704. VERDICTS: (1) \"missed retreats outnumber extra at least 2:1\" is WRONG and inverted: extra retreats outnumber missed 45:1, so the student retreats when the teacher would fight. (2) \"deaths carry the gap\" HOLDS: 5.94 vs 0.38 deaths per hunt (x15.6), and kills also fall from 7.26 to 2.84. (3) \"action-relevant stance <= 5 pct\" HOLDS: exactly 0, so 5b's 16.1 pct was entirely rows where the teacher retreats. (4) A state-distribution shift is visible: the teacher would retreat in 76 pct of its own targeted moments (kiting) but in only 27 pct of the student's, so the student lives in states the teacher rarely visits and holds ground in. Reading: compounding error, where rare false-positive retreats (about 1 pct of hold-ground moments) knock the student off the kiting regime into fights it dies in. Step 6 = DAgger: relabel student-visited states with the teacher plan, aggregate with the original data, retrain, and re-run step 5. The loss-weight idea is dropped, since the errors are not missed retreats.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_22 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 22u32, "2026-11-09T02:01Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:3x tibia: STEP 6 PRE-REGISTERED (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_dagger.spi). ONE DAgger iteration: (1) the step-4c student (coupled loss, 300 steps, seed-7 init, quantized) drives on the TRAINING seeds 1-100 (arena_spot Cyclops, 3000 ticks); at every decision moment the TEACHER labels the student-visited state (bc_dataset::pair_at with the teacher tactic, the same masks). (2) Those pairs are aggregated with the original 300k teacher-state pairs. (3) Retrain from the same seed-7 init with the same trainer (Adam, lr 0.02, 300 full-batch steps) and quantize. (4) Evaluate exactly as step 5 (held-out seeds 1001-1100, paired, kill_score, 95 pct CI) plus step 5c's kills, deaths and retreat directions with the new student driving. BAR: the step-5 bar, student mean inside the teacher's 95 pct CI. Soft expectations: the paired gap shrinks by at least half (from -282 to better than -141); extra retreats per targeted moment fall below 0.3 pct (from 0.74 pct); one iteration probably does NOT yet meet the bar. Recorded whatever it shows; the teacher arm must again reproduce -11.74 exactly.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_23 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 23u32, "2026-11-09T02:35Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:3x tibia: STEP 6 MEASURED (ganymede job-1794189806274-tibia-bc-dagger). DAgger iteration 1: 599861 aggregated pairs (300k teacher states + about 300k student states relabelled by the teacher); final loss 0.0616. Held-out seeds 1001-1100: teacher -11.74 +- 5.54 (reproduced exactly); DAgger student -34.08 +- 7.28; paired difference -22.34 +- 8.38. BAR NOT MET (student_within_teacher_ci95 = 0), but the gap shrank 92 pct (-282 to -22), so the soft \"at least half\" expectation HOLDS. Under DAgger-student drive, targeted moments: missed retreats 0/292369, extra retreats 0/292369, stance-when-teacher-stays 0/36071; the \"extra < 0.3 pct\" expectation HOLDS (0 pct). Kills 42 and deaths 69 over 100 hunts (teacher: 726 and 38). PUZZLE: the plan now agrees with the teacher on EVERY targeted moment of the student's own trajectory, yet kills are 17x lower. So the remaining gap lies OUTSIDE the retreat/stance plan: the heal head (99.7 pct offline, never measured on-policy) or another brain-dependent path. Also, the student is in teacher-retreat states 88 pct of targeted moments (vs 76 pct for the teacher), so it kites almost all the time and rarely engages.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_24 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 24u32, "2026-11-09T02:37Z", "tibia", "11-08 22:4x tibia: STEP 6b PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_heal.spi). Rebuild the step-6 DAgger student deterministically (same aggregation and training; final loss must again be 0.061598666, otherwise VOID). With the DAgger student driving and, as control, the teacher driving, on held-out seeds 1001-1100: at every decision moment where the aimed pack is heal_ready, compare the teacher's and the student's wants_heal. Report MISSED heals (teacher heals, student does not) and EXTRA heals (the reverse) over heal-ready moments, plus total potions used and kills/deaths per arm. Rationale: retreat and stance agree 100 pct on-policy (step 6), and heal is the only other brain-dependent path. A heal spends the action slot and a potion budget, so extra heals cut kills and missed heals add deaths. Prediction (soft): heal disagreement under student drive is > 1 pct of heal-ready moments, EXTRA heals dominate, and the student uses more potions than the teacher. If heal disagreement is ~0, the gap lies in something not yet modelled (record it, do not guess).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_25 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 25u32, "2026-11-09T03:18Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:2x tibia: STEP 6b MEASURED (ganymede job-1794192049684-tibia-bc-heal). VALID: the DAgger rebuild reproduces final loss 0.061598666 and step 6's 42 kills / 69 deaths exactly. DAGGER STUDENT DRIVES, heal-ready decision moments: missed heals 196, extra heals 350, of 231128 (0.24 pct total); potions 7653. TEACHER DRIVES (control): missed 299, extra 2670, of 255928 (1.16 pct); potions 4897, kills 726, deaths 38. VERDICTS: (1) \"heal disagreement under student drive > 1 pct\" is WRONG: 0.24 pct. (2) \"extra heals dominate\" HOLDS weakly (350 vs 196). (3) \"student uses more potions\" HOLDS: +56 pct. Combined with step 6, the DAgger student now matches the teacher's decision on its OWN states almost exactly: retreat 100 pct, stance 100 pct, heal 99.76 pct. Yet it ends with 42 kills against 726. So the TEACHER, put in the student's states, would act the same way, which means the student lives in a basin the teacher itself would stay in. Leading hypothesis (not measured): the teacher policy is FRAGILE. A few early perturbations (~5 heal disagreements per hunt) tip a hunt into a kite-and-heal regime (88 pct of targeted moments retreating, many potions, few kills) that neither policy leaves. If so, \"student inside the teacher's CI\" cannot be met by imitation alone and needs a noised-teacher reference. Step 6c (teacher robustness under tiny heal-flip noise) is to be pre-registered before any code.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_26 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 26u32, "2026-11-09T03:19Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:2x tibia: STEP 6c PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_handover.spi). HANDOVER TEST: on held-out seeds 1001-1100 (3000 ticks), the step-6 DAgger student drives ticks [0, K) and the TEACHER drives [K, 3000), with K in {0, 150, 600, 1500, 3000}. K=0 is the pure teacher and must reproduce -11.74; K=3000 is the pure student and must reproduce -34.08 (otherwise VOID). Report the mean kill_score, kills and deaths per K. Hypotheses: FRAGILE-BASIN (the student's early divergence leads to states the teacher cannot recover from) predicts the K=150 and K=600 scores are already near the student's (below -25). RECOVERABLE (the teacher pulls a hunt back out) predicts K=150 and K=600 near the teacher's (above -18), with the score falling roughly in proportion to K. Recorded whatever it shows; the per-K means are point estimates over the same 100 seeds, not intervals.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_27 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 27u32, "2026-11-09T05:59Z", "tibia", "11-09 01:5x tibia: STEP 6c MEASURED (ganymede job-1794196205744-tibia-bc-handover). VALID: K=0 reproduces the teacher (-11.74, 726 kills, 38 deaths) and K=3000 the DAgger student (-34.08, 42, 69) exactly. HANDOVER (student drives [0,K), teacher drives [K,3000), 100 held-out seeds): K=150 -14.80 (720 kills, 44 deaths); K=600 -16.55 (645, 46); K=1500 -22.97 (453, 55). VERDICT: FRAGILE-BASIN is REFUTED (it predicted K=150/600 below -25; both are above -18). RECOVERABLE HOLDS: the teacher pulls a hunt straight back, and the score falls roughly in proportion to how long the student drives (-3.1 at 5 pct, -4.8 at 20 pct, -11.2 at 50 pct, -22.3 at 100 pct). So the student is continuously WORSE per tick (its kill rate is near zero while it drives), not tipping into a trap. That contradicts steps 6 and 6b, which measured >99.7 pct decision agreement on the student's own states. NEW HYPOTHESIS (not measured; from reading the code): those agreement checks and the dataset both evaluate the brain on the PRE-TICK pack (the logged state before advance), but knight_turn consults the brain on the IN-TICK pack, after this tick's monster actions (SeesThisTick etc.). Training labels and every agreement metric share that blind spot, so 100 pct agreement there says nothing about the decisions actually taken. Next (6d, pre-register first): measure teacher-vs-student agreement at the REAL decision point by logging inside the tick (a probe brain or a tallying wrapper of knight_turn's plan call), and, if confirmed, regenerate the dataset at that point.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_28 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 28u32, "2026-11-09T06:00Z", "tibia", "11-09 02:0x tibia: STEP 6d PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_decision_point.spi, no change to hunting_pack). Rebuild the pack knight_turn actually sees each tick: both = charged_both b p, then by camp timing view: SeesThisTick -> foes_act both; SeesLastTick -> both; SeesAtItsPoll -> foes_act_where (early_mask both (poll_landing b)) both. At every tick where that IN-TICK pack decides (bc_dataset::decides), compare the teacher's and the DAgger student's plans (missed/extra retreat; stance when the teacher stays) and heals (missed/extra on heal_ready) on the aimed in-tick pack. Two arms: DAgger student drives, teacher drives. Same 100 held-out seeds; the DAgger rebuild must reproduce final loss 0.061598666 (else VOID). Predictions if the TIMING-MISMATCH hypothesis holds: under student drive, disagreement at the in-tick point is far above the pre-tick figures (retreat > 1 pct and/or heal > 1 pct of their moments), concentrated on moments where foes acted this tick. If it fails (in-tick agreement still > 99.7 pct), the gap is NOT in the brain's decisions at all, so look at what else differs between the brains' runs (record that, do not guess).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_29 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 29u32, "2026-11-09T06:21Z", "tibia", "11-09 02:3x tibia: DRAFT (not run, not pre-registered): apps/predict/bc_intick.spi = step 7 candidate, waiting on 6d. It regenerates the teacher dataset at the REAL decision point (bc_decision_point::knight_view, the in-tick pack), trains the student on it, does one in-tick DAgger relabel round, retrains, and evaluates as in step 5 (paired, 100 held-out seeds) plus 6d's in-tick agreement table. It runs only if 6d confirms the timing mismatch, and is pre-registered first.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_30 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 30u32, "2026-11-09T07:16Z", "tibia", "11-09 03:1x tibia: STEP 6d MEASURED (ganymede job-1794206291496-tibia-bc-decision2; resubmitted after rig's held-queue bug). VALID: the DAgger rebuild reproduces final loss 0.061598666. At the REAL decision point (the in-tick pack knight_turn sees, rebuilt per camp timing view): DAGGER STUDENT DRIVES: retreat missed 0, extra 0 of 292300; stance when the teacher stays 0 of 35584; heal missed 207, extra 573 of 231059 (0.34 pct). TEACHER DRIVES: retreat 0/0 of 234655; stance 0 of 55726; heal missed 1535, extra 2600 of 255891 (1.6 pct). VERDICT: the TIMING-MISMATCH hypothesis is REFUTED. In-tick agreement is as high as pre-tick (the prediction was > 1 pct disagreement; observed retreat 0 pct, heal 0.34 pct). Also checked by reading code: the stance KIND cannot hide a difference, since network_engagement maps the engage bool to Strike/Approach/Hold under the same conditions as the rules' engages. Per the pre-registration: the gap is NOT in the brain's decisions at any measured point. Something else differs between the two runs, and from here a cause is a guess, so none is recorded. NEXT (6e, pre-register first): a LOCKSTEP divergence trace. For each held-out seed, run the teacher-driven and student-driven hunts tick by tick from the same start, find the FIRST tick where their packs differ (hunter position, health, target, potions, clocks, score), and dump both brains' decisions and the differing fields at that tick and the one before.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_31 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 31u32, "2026-11-09T07:18Z", "tibia", "11-09 03:2x tibia: STEP 6e PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_lockstep.spi). For each held-out seed 1001-1100, advance a TEACHER-driven pack and a DAgger-STUDENT-driven pack in lockstep from the same start, and compare after every tick: position, health, next_step_at, next_decision_at, next_action_at, potions, hits_taken, retreats, target, kills/deaths. Stop at the FIRST tick where any differs; print that tick and a bitmask of the differing fields (1 position, 2 health, 4 step clock, 8 decision clock, 16 action clock, 32 potions, 64 hits, 128 retreats, 256 target, 512 score). The DAgger rebuild must reproduce 0.061598666 (else VOID). The question, asked without a favoured answer: which field moves FIRST, and how early. A heal-only first divergence (mask 32/16) at heal-disagreement ticks would make the 0.34 pct heal disagreement the lever. A first divergence with NO decision disagreement at or before it would point to a non-brain path (e.g. something in the tactic or brain wiring other than the plan/heal calls). Recorded whatever it shows.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_32 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 32u32, "2026-11-09T08:29Z", "tibia", "11-09 04:2x tibia: STEP 6e MEASURED (ganymede job-1794208836296-tibia-bc-lockstep). VALID: the DAgger rebuild reproduces 0.061598666. LOCKSTEP (teacher-driven vs DAgger-student-driven, same seed, same start, compared after every tick): ALL 100 held-out seeds diverge, EARLY: first tick min 132, median 305, max 605 (of 3000). FIRST-DIVERGING FIELDS (bitmask): 50 seeds mask 50 = health + action clock + potions (a HEAL in one run only), first ticks min 132 / median 197 / max 370; 48 seeds mask 768 = target + score (a KILL in one run only, with every tracked hunter field identical up to that tick), first ticks min 240 / median 404 / max 605; 1 seed 834 (score + target + hits + health); 1 seed 38 (potions + step clock + health). READING (from the data plus the pre-registration): (a) heal-first divergence matches the measured 0.34 pct heal disagreement: one differing heal, early (median tick 197), starts every heal-first split; (b) kill-first divergence with identical hunter state means some UNTRACKED state moved first (foe health or positions, or something the brain changes that the hunter fields do not show), because a kill cannot differ between identical worlds. Either way, the two runs separate within the first 20 pct of the hunt, and handover (6c) shows the cost then accrues per tick. NEXT (6f, pre-register first): extend the trace with foe state (per-foe health and position) and record both brains' plan and heal at the divergence tick and the tick before, to name the first differing ACTION.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_33 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 33u32, "2026-11-09T08:31Z", "tibia", "11-09 04:3x tibia: STEP 6f PRE-REGISTERED as a DIAGNOSTIC (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_lockstep2.spi). The 6e lockstep with two additions. (1) FOE STATE in the mask: 1024 any foe position, 2048 any foe health, 4096 any foe strike clock, 8192 any foe step clock. (2) At the first divergence tick k, the two packs were IDENTICAL at k-1, so on that shared pack print both brains' decisions at beat k-1: decides (bool), retreat T/S, engages T/S, heal T/S (in-tick view, aimed). The DAgger rebuild must reproduce 0.061598666 (else VOID). QUESTIONS (no favoured answer): do the 6e kill-first seeds show a FOE field moving earlier (so their first tick moves earlier)? And at the divergence tick, is there a decision disagreement (which one), or none? If NO decision differs at the divergence tick on identical state, the divergence is not in the brain's decisions, and the next place to look is the tactic wiring outside decide/plan/heal.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_34 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 34u32, "2026-11-09T09:24Z", "tibia", "11-09 05:2x tibia: STEP 6f MEASURED (ganymede job-1794213192022-tibia-bc-lockstep2). VALID: the DAgger rebuild reproduces 0.061598666. With FOE state in the mask, the first divergence moves much EARLIER: ticks min 66, median 99, max 195 (6e: 132/305/605). First-diverging field: 97 seeds 2048 = FOE HEALTH; 2 seeds 50 (heal); 1 seed 2098 (foe health + heal). BOTH BRAINS' DECISIONS ON THE LAST SHARED STATE (tick k-1; every seed is a decision tick): 80 seeds retreat T=1 S=1, ENGAGE T=1 S=0, heal agree; 1 seed the same plus a heal difference; 15 seeds no decision differs (00/00/00); 2 seeds engage 11 with heal 01; 2 seeds all agree with engage 11. ROOT CAUSE (code plus data): retreat_or_engage only STEPS AWAY when b::now >= next_step_at; until then it calls engaged with the plan's stance. So a retreating teacher STRIKES while waiting for its step clock, and the student HOLDS. The engage label on teacher-retreat rows was masked BY DESIGN (step 4c's coupled loss: head_mask(engage) = m_engage * (1 - m_retreat * y_retreat)), on the assumption that stance is irrelevant while retreating. That assumption is WRONG. The student never learned to strike while kiting, which explains its near-zero kill rate (42 vs 726), the 6c per-tick deficit, and why every decision metric looked perfect (each one ignored stance on retreat rows, exactly as the training did). The 15 no-difference seeds diverge through something else (to check later). FIX (step 7, pre-register next): supervise engage on retreat rows too (keep the retreat-vs-engage margin term, so r > e still holds), retrain, DAgger, re-run step 5's paired eval.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_35 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 35u32, "2026-11-09T09:25Z", "tibia", "11-09 05:3x tibia: STEP 7 PRE-REGISTERED (before any run; code: src/bc_train.spi gets an OPTIONAL 4th mask channel, engage_kept, read only when present, so all earlier steps stay bit-identical; apps/predict/bc_kept.spi). CHANGE: on teacher-retreat rows the engage head is SUPERVISED (head_mask(engage) = m_engage * (1 - coupling * (1 - engage_kept)), engage_kept = 1). The retreat-vs-engage margin term BCE(z_r - z_e, 1) is kept, so decision_of's r > e still holds where the teacher retreats. Everything else matches steps 4c/6: seed-7 init, Adam lr 0.02, 300 full-batch steps, training seeds 1-100, quantized. TWO ARMS, both evaluated as in step 5 (paired, held-out seeds 1001-1100, kill_score, 95 pct CI) plus kills/deaths: (K0) kept-engage student, no DAgger; (K1) K0 plus one DAgger round (student-visited states relabelled by the teacher, aggregated, retrained with engage kept). BAR (the step 5 bar): student mean inside the teacher's 95 pct CI [-17.28, -6.20]. SOFT EXPECTATIONS: K0 already recovers most of the kill rate (kills > 400 of the teacher's 726) and the paired gap shrinks below -15. K1 meets the bar. A failure on either is recorded as is; 6f's 15 no-decision-difference seeds stay an open thread.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_36 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 36u32, "2026-11-09T10:03Z", "tibia", "11-09 06:0x tibia: STEP 7 MEASURED (ganymede job-1794216517625-tibia-bc-kept). K0 (engage supervised on retreat rows, no DAgger; final loss 0.0568): student -324.62 +- 34.80, paired -312.88 +- 35.05, kills 338, deaths 656; missed retreats 756, extra 312 of 195065 targeted. K1 (K0 + one DAgger round, 599863 pairs, loss 0.0761): student -29.11 +- 6.48, paired -17.37 +- 8.11, kills 39, deaths 59; retreat 0/0 disagreement. AGAINST NOTE 35: \"K0 kills > 400\" WRONG (338); \"K0 paired better than -15\" WRONG (-313, worse than step 5's -282); \"K1 meets the bar\" WRONG (-29.11 is outside [-17.28, -6.20]); K1 is only slightly better than plain DAgger (-34.08). STRUCTURAL CAUSE (read in src/network.spi): decision_of is engage = e > 0 && e >= r; retreat = r > 0 && r > e. Engage and retreat are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE BY CONSTRUCTION. The network can never output (retreat, engage) = (1, 1), but the teacher does exactly that at 80 of 100 first-divergence ticks (6f): it retreats AND strikes while its step clock is not ready. No loss or mask change can teach an unrepresentable action; supervising engage on retreat rows only fights the r > e margin, which explains K0's 756 missed retreats. So the earlier engage mask was a symptom: it hid an architecture limit, it did not cause it. NEXT (step 8, pre-register first): an output decision where engage and retreat are independent (engage = e > 0, retreat = r > 0), behind a NEW brain variant so the existing Network brain, its tests and hand-built networks keep their semantics; train with engage supervised everywhere and no margin term; then the step 5 eval.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_37 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 37u32, "2026-11-09T10:04Z", "tibia", "11-09 06:0x tibia: STEP 8 PRE-REGISTERED (before any run; code: network.spi gains decide_independent (heal = h > 0, engage = e > 0, retreat = r > 0; decide/decision_of untouched); hunting_pack.spi brain gains | Independent : network::weights (heal path = the Network heal path, which never depended on the coupling; plan = decide_independent, then network_engagement); bc_train.spi examples gain an optional 5th channel independent = 1 that zeroes the coupling, i.e. engage supervised on every identifiable row and NO margin term; apps/predict/bc_indep.spi). Same data, init, optimizer, steps and seeds as steps 4c/6/7. ARMS: (I0) independent student, no DAgger; (I1) I0 plus one DAgger round (relabelled by the teacher, retrained independent). Eval as step 5 (paired, held-out seeds 1001-1100, 95 pct CI) plus kills/deaths and retreat directions. BAR: the student mean inside the teacher's CI [-17.28, -6.20]. SOFT EXPECTATIONS: I0 kills > 300 and paired gap better than -100 (one structural fix, still compounding); I1 meets the bar, with kills within 30 pct of the teacher's 726. If I1 kills stay below 100, the strike-while-retreating hypothesis is wrong too, and the 15 no-difference seeds of 6f become the lead.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_38 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 38u32, "2026-11-09T10:38Z", "tibia", "11-09 06:4x tibia groom (star exchange): progress 85 -> 70 pct, stated honestly. The step-5 bar is still unmet after steps 5-7, and step 8 (independent engage/retreat heads, note 37) is running on ganymede. Root-cause chain so far: masks hid an UNREPRESENTABLE action (decision_of makes engage and retreat exclusive; the teacher does both). Open thread: 6f's 15 no-decision-difference seeds. Modules: bc_dataset/bc_train (src) and apps/predict/bc_{run,eval,onpolicy,direction,dagger,heal,handover,decision_point,intick,lockstep,lockstep2,kept,indep}.spi, unstaged; the 6 over-budget cells in bc_intick/bc_kept/bc_lockstep2 are split before landing.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_39 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 39u32, "2026-11-09T10:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 06:5x tibia: STEP 8 MEASURED (ganymede job-1794218875124-tibia-bc-indep). Independent heads (Independent brain: engage = e > 0, retreat = r > 0; no coupling, engage supervised on every identifiable row). I0 (no DAgger, final loss 0.056375578, the same value as the uncoupled step-4b loss, as expected): -296.14 +- 29.15, paired -284.40 +- 29.53; kills 436, deaths 601; missed retreats 0, extra 12861 of 197311. I1 (one DAgger round, 599840 pairs, loss 0.0498): -29.16 +- 6.77, paired -17.42 +- 7.50; KILLS 684 (teacher 726), deaths 72 (teacher 38); missed retreats 0, extra 3155 of 229763 (1.4 pct). AGAINST NOTE 37: \"I0 kills > 300\" HELD (436); \"I0 paired better than -100\" FAILED (-284); \"I1 meets the bar\" FAILED (-29.16 outside [-17.28, -6.20]); \"I1 kills within 30 pct of 726\" HELD (684, within 6 pct). VERDICT: the representability fix WORKS for the kill rate. Every earlier student made ~40 kills, I1 makes 684, so strike-while-retreating was the missing action. The remaining gap is DEATHS: 34 extra x 50 = -17 points, almost exactly the paired gap. It coincides with 1.4 pct extra retreats (false-positive retreats, now uncoupled from engage). Progress 70 -> 80. NEXT: step 9 = a second DAgger round (pre-registered next).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_40 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 40u32, "2026-11-09T10:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 06:5x tibia: STEP 9 PRE-REGISTERED (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_indep2.spi). A SECOND DAgger round on the independent heads: I1 drives the training seeds 1-100, the teacher labels its states, the pairs are aggregated with I1's training set (about 900k pairs), and it is retrained independent from the seed-7 init. Arm I2, evaluated as step 5 (paired, held-out seeds 1001-1100) plus kills/deaths/retreat directions. I1 is re-derived on the way and must reproduce loss 0.049796116 (else VOID). BAR: the student mean inside the teacher's CI [-17.28, -6.20]. SOFT EXPECTATIONS: extra retreats fall below 0.5 pct (from 1.4), deaths fall below 55 (from 72), kills stay above 650, and I2 MEETS the bar (mean better than -17.28). A miss on the bar with deaths still high points at the retreat head's calibration (threshold), not at data.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_41 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 41u32, "2026-11-09T11:56Z", "tibia", "11-09 08:0x tibia: STEP 9 MEASURED (ganymede job-1794221214391-tibia-bc-indep2). VALID: I1 re-derived loss 0.049796116 exactly. Second DAgger round on the independent heads: 899839 pairs, final loss 0.0743. I2: -20.04 +- 6.48, paired -8.30 +- 7.32; kills 696, deaths 54 (teacher 726/38); missed retreats 0, extra 2671 of 233209 (1.15 pct). AGAINST NOTE 40: \"extra retreats < 0.5 pct\" FAILED (1.15); \"deaths < 55\" HELD (54); \"kills > 650\" HELD (696); \"I2 meets the bar\" FAILED NARROWLY (-20.04 vs the CI floor -17.28; 2.76 short). TREND across DAgger rounds: paired gap -284 (I0) -> -17.4 (I1) -> -8.3 (I2); deaths 601 -> 72 -> 54; kills 436 -> 684 -> 696. The remaining gap is again deaths (16 x 50 = -8 = the paired gap) with ~1.1 pct false retreats. Progress 80 -> 85. NEXT: step 10 = a third DAgger round (pre-registered next). If it still misses, then a retreat-threshold calibration on TRAINING seeds only.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_42 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 42u32, "2026-11-09T11:56Z", "tibia", "11-09 08:0x tibia: STEP 10 PRE-REGISTERED (before the run; code apps/predict/bc_indep3.spi). A THIRD DAgger round: I2 drives training seeds 1-100, teacher relabels, aggregated (~1.2M pairs), retrained independent from the seed-7 init. I1 and I2 are re-derived on the way and must reproduce 0.049796116 and 0.074348 (else VOID). Arm I3, evaluated as step 5 plus kills/deaths/retreat directions. BAR: the student mean inside the teacher's CI [-17.28, -6.20]. SOFT EXPECTATIONS (DAgger convergence): I3 meets the bar; deaths <= 48; extra retreats < 0.9 pct; kills >= 690. If I3 misses with extra retreats flat (~1.1 pct), more data has stopped helping and the residual is retreat-head bias: then step 11 = a threshold calibrated on TRAINING seeds only (never the held-out ones).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_43 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 43u32, "2026-11-09T13:23Z", "tibia", "Evidence: 11-09 09:3x tibia, ganymede job-1794229764269-tibia-bc-gate3 exit 0: tibia build.ps1 -Files bc_train (after the formatter pass on bc_train/bc_indep2/bc_indep3/bc_lockstep): paths clean, formatter check clean, cell budget 0 over_budget, Cells bc_train discovered 4 executed 4 passed 4 failed 0. The two new tests pass: engage_is_masked_on_retreat_rows_unless_a_channel_keeps_it (the 4th mask channel) and independent_channel_gradients_match_central_differences (the 5th channel that drops the engage-retreat coupling, used by the Independent brain of steps 8-10).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_44 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 44u32, "2026-11-09T13:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:1x tibia: STEP 10 VERDICT (ganymede job-1794225600863-tibia-bc-indep3, 6150 s). CONTROLS HOLD: I1 final loss 0.049796116 and I2 0.074348 re-derive exactly; I3 final loss 0.10197241 on 1199839 round-3 pairs. BAR MISSED: student mean -23.81 (ci95 +-7.18) vs teacher -11.74 (+-5.54); paired diff -12.07 (+-8.09); the mean is outside [-17.28, -6.20]; student_within_teacher_ci95 0. Kills 719, deaths 62 / 100 hunts (I2: 696/54). Retreats: missed 0 of 233714, EXTRA 2629 of 233714 = 1.12 pct (flat vs I2), stance_when_teacher_stays 0 of 62988. READING: DAgger rounds make it WORSE (step 8 I1 gap -17.4, I2 -20.04, I3 -23.81), while the error shape (only extra retreats, never missed) stays fixed. More aggregated data does not move a threshold bias. The pre-registered branch fires: step 11.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_45 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 45u32, "2026-11-09T13:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:1x tibia: STEP 11 PRE-REGISTERED (from the step-10 branch). Student: I1 weights (the best student, step 8; no further DAgger). Change: the Independent brain's retreat head fires when its raw logit r > theta instead of r > 0. theta is CALIBRATED ON TRAINING SEEDS ONLY (the bc_run training_first seeds, never the 100 eval hunts): over the teacher-labelled training pairs, take the smallest theta on the integer grid of r values at which the student's extra retreats <= its missed retreats (the balanced-error point). Then theta is frozen and printed before any eval row. Eval: the same 100 eval hunts and printing as steps 9/10. CONTROL: I1 final loss 0.049796116 must re-derive, and theta = 0 must reproduce step 8's rows (A/A of the change). BAR (unchanged): student mean inside [-17.28, -6.20]. Secondary: extra retreats < 0.3 pct with missed retreats < 0.3 pct. If the bar is MISSED with retreats balanced, the gap is not the retreat threshold: step 12 inspects engage timing (the step-6e first-divergence trace) and does not tune further.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_46 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 46u32, "2026-11-09T14:24Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:3x tibia: STEP 11 VERDICT (ganymede job-1794232447758-tibia-bc-calib, compiled before pack77 so on pack75). CONTROLS HOLD: I1 final loss 0.049796116 re-derives. A/A HOLDS: T0 (Calibrated, theta 0) reproduces I1 line for line (student -29.16 +-6.77, paired -17.42, extra 3155, kills 684 deaths 72). CALIBRATION (training seeds only): theta = 210; training extra retreats 2785 -> 0, missed 0 -> 0. EVAL T1: extra retreats 3155 -> 8 of 226816 (0.0035 pct), missed 0: the SECONDARY GOAL IS MET. BAR MISSED: student mean -29.2 (+-6.59) vs I1 -29.16; paired -17.46; kills 680, deaths 72. Removing essentially every extra retreat leaves the score unchanged, so the extra retreats were never the gap. The pre-registered branch fires: step 12 = the engage-timing first-divergence trace, with no further tuning.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_47 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 47u32, "2026-11-09T14:24Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:3x tibia: CORRECTION to note 44's reading and note 45's premise (comparison error, found from step 11's rows). I compared I1's PAIRED gap (-17.4) with I2's and I3's STUDENT MEANS. Like for like: student mean I1 -29.16, I2 -20.04, I3 -23.81; paired diff I1 -17.42, I2 -8.30, I3 -12.07 (teacher -11.74 in all). So DAgger round 2 IMPROVED the student (paired -17.42 -> -8.30) and round 3 REGRESSED (-12.07). It is not monotonically worse, and I2, not I1, is the best student. Step 11's conclusion stands: the threshold removed the extra retreats with no score change, on I1. Step 12 uses I2 as its student (the best, and its paired diff is closest to the teacher).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_48 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 48u32, "2026-11-09T14:29Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:4x tibia: STEP 12 PRE-REGISTERED (the step-11 branch: inspect, do not tune). Student I2 (the best, per note 47), rebuilt as in step 9 (bc_indep2 next_round x2). The control I2 final loss 0.074348 must re-derive. Trace: bc_lockstep2::seeds_from (the step-6f first-divergence lockstep) over the same eval seeds. Per seed it prints the split tick + state mask and, at the split, the teacher/student flags for retreat, engage and heal. CLASSIFY each seed's first divergence: E+ (student engages, teacher does not), E- (teacher engages, student does not), R (retreat differs), H (heal differs), N (all decision flags agree at the split: the state diverged without a decision difference), plus seeds that never split. DECISION RULE: if E+ + E- >= 50 pct of the split seeds, step 13 calibrates the ENGAGE threshold on training seeds only (the step-11 method, now on engage). If N >= 50 pct, the gap is not a head decision at the split tick, and step 13 traces the state just before the split (tick-level foe/hp deltas). Otherwise, step 13 targets the largest class. No score bar (diagnostic step).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_49 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 49u32, "2026-11-09T14:32Z", "tibia", "11-09 10:5x tibia: Evidence for the step-11 cleanup (job-1794234528039-tibia-verify11b on pack77, core 9ef0395b): the 4 over-budget cells step 11 added are split (alias `weights` for network::weights in the brain union; independent_heals / independent_weights_plan helpers; bc_calib trained/reported). Over_budget is back to the 67 baseline, --check is clean, and bc_calib was formatted. Behaviour is preserved: the predict rows match the pre-refactor pack75 run (jp3after) exactly. The only output difference is pack77's new compiler line `outline: 104 arm(s) over 400 binds moved into their own functions`, which the content filter did not strip (sha c572e13acf139dea with it; the rows themselves are equal). Row filters must now also drop `outline:` lines.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_50 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 50u32, "2026-11-09T15:30Z", "tibia", "11-09 11:4x tibia: STEP 12 RESULT (ganymede job-1794234913881-tibia-bc-engage, pack77). CONTROL HOLDS: I0 0.056375578, I1 0.049796116, I2 0.074348 re-derive. First-divergence lockstep of I2 vs the teacher over the 100 eval seeds: all 100 split. CLASSES: H 84 (heal differs, always `heal 10` = teacher heals, student does not), R 16 (`retreat 01` = student retreats, teacher does not), E+ 0, E- 0, N 0. So engage timing is NEVER the first divergence. A missed heal is the first divergence in 84 pct of seeds, although heal disagreement is rare overall (step 6b: 0.34 pct of ticks): one early missed heal changes everything after it. Checked before acting: the Independent brain heals through network_heals -> network::decide, whose decision_of uses heal = h > 0 with the same unscaling as decide_independent, so this is NOT a decoder mismatch. Pre-registered rule: neither E nor N >= 50 pct, so step 13 targets the largest class, H.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_51 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 51u32, "2026-11-09T15:31Z", "tibia", "11-09 11:4x tibia: STEP 13 PRE-REGISTERED (heal analogue of step 11). Student I2. Change: the heal head fires when h > theta_h (a new brain case carrying theta_h and theta_r; theta_r = 0). theta_h is calibrated ON TRAINING PAIRS ONLY (I2's round-2 training set; heal labels Known only): the LARGEST theta_h on the integer grid with missed_heals <= extra_heals (balanced error), found by binary search over [min h, max h]. It is frozen and printed (with training missed/extra at 0 and at theta_h) before any eval row. BUILT-IN CHECK: if theta_h = 0 (training heal errors already balanced), the heal head is not biased, and the first-divergence heals come from state or the heal_ready gate; then step 14 traces state just before the split and step 13's eval is still reported. CONTROLS: I2 loss 0.074348; A/A arm theta_h = 0 reproduces I2's eval rows (student mean -20.04, paired -8.30). BAR (unchanged): student mean inside [-17.28, -6.20]. SECONDARY: the H share of first divergences (re-run the step-12 trace on the calibrated student) falls below 50 pct.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_52 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 52u32, "2026-11-09T16:51Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:5x tibia: STEP 13 VERDICT (ganymede job-1794238441365-tibia-bc-healcal, pack77). CONTROLS HOLD: I0/I1/I2 losses re-derive (0.056375578 / 0.049796116 / 0.074348). A/A HOLDS: H0 (theta_h 0) reproduces I2 line for line (-20.04, paired -8.30, kills 696, deaths 54). BUILT-IN CHECK: the heal head IS biased. On I2's training pairs at theta_h 0: missed heals 8066 vs extra 1696 (4.8:1). Calibrated theta_h = -45: missed 4039 / extra 4123 (balanced). EVAL H1: student -19.06 +-6.76 (was -20.04), paired -7.32 +-6.70 (was -8.30), kills 694, deaths 52 (was 54), extra retreats 2970 of 229193. BAR MISSED NARROWLY: -19.06 vs the floor -17.28, 1.78 short (the closest yet; I2 was 2.76). SECONDARY FAILED: the step-12 trace re-run on H1 still finds H 78 / R 22 (was 84 / 16) first divergences. Reading: de-biasing the heal threshold helps a little (+0.98 mean, -2 deaths) but does NOT remove missed heals as the first divergence. Progress note: steps 8 -> 13 took the student mean -29.16 -> -19.06.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_53 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 53u32, "2026-11-09T16:51Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:5x tibia: STEP 14 PRE-REGISTERED (diagnostic, no tuning). Question: at the 78 H-class split ticks of H1, is the student's heal logit h NEAR the threshold (-45) or FAR below it? Code: the lockstep split row also prints the student's raw h at the split tick, plus the teacher's heal inputs there (own hp pct, heal_ready, attackers). RULE: if the median h at H splits is within 30 of theta_h (-75..-15), the misses are calibration noise and step 15 tests a per-context threshold (by attackers). If the median is below -75, the student is CONFIDENTLY wrong: its 7 inputs cannot see what the teacher's heal rule uses, and step 15 adds that input (a feature, then retrain; the teacher heal rule is read in src first to name it). No bar (diagnostic). The control I2 loss 0.074348 must re-derive. Also queued with it: split bc_healcal's over-budget cell (line 52, 285 > 272).")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_54 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 54u32, "2026-11-09T16:52Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:5x tibia: AMENDMENT to step 14's branch, before any data (source read). The teacher heal rule is policy::heals: heal_ready && health < heal_base + heal_per_attacker * attackers (policy.spi:52 with thresholds_of :25), a LINEAR threshold on (health, attackers) gated by heal_ready. The student's inputs already carry all three (hunting_pack features: health_fraction, attackers, o::heal_ready via observed_inputs), so no input is missing and the rule is representable. Revised branch: median h at H splits within 30 of theta_h -> per-context threshold (unchanged). Median far below -75 -> the student is confidently wrong on a representable rule, i.e. a TRAINING problem (heal-positive rows are rare; the 4.8:1 missed:extra bias on training fits under-weighting), so step 15 = a class-balanced heal loss (weight heal-positive rows by the training negative:positive ratio), retrained from the seed-7 init on I2's data, NOT a new feature.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_55 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 55u32, "2026-11-09T17:58Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:5x tibia: STEP 14 RESULT (ganymede job-1794243888645-tibia-bc-healtrace, pack77). CONTROL HOLDS: I2 loss 0.074348 (and I0/I1) re-derive; theta_h re-derived = -45. Of 100 eval seeds traced on the calibrated student, 51 first-divergences are teacher-heals/student-does-not (heal 10; step 13's H 78 also counted the reverse direction). At those 51 split ticks the student's raw heal logit h: min -146, q1 -96, MEDIAN -79, q3 -62, max -45 (none above theta). heal_ready = 1 at all 51; the teacher's inputs there: hp 78-79 (of one), attackers 2-3, i.e. exactly the attacker-dependent edge of policy::heals (heal_base + per_attacker * attackers). RULE (note 53, amended in note 54): the median is below -75, so the student is confidently wrong on a representable rule = a TRAINING problem, and step 15 = a class-balanced heal loss. HONEST CAVEAT: -79 is only 4 past the -75 cut, so this is a near-boundary call, and q3 -62 shows a quarter of the misses are within ~17 of theta.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_56 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 56u32, "2026-11-09T17:58Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:5x tibia: STEP 15 PRE-REGISTERED. Change: the heal channel's loss weight on heal-POSITIVE rows = the training ratio negatives:positives on heal-known rows (computed on I2's round-2 training set, printed before training), retrained independent from the seed-7 init on the same 899839 pairs; theta_h stays 0 (no calibration, to isolate the loss change). CONTROL: weight 1 must reproduce I2's loss 0.074348 (A/A). Eval as steps 9-13. BAR (unchanged): student mean inside [-17.28, -6.20]. SECONDARY: the step-14 probe on the new student: median h at teacher-heal splits within 30 of 0, and teacher-heals/student-not first divergences < 30 (of 100). If the bar is met: done (progress to 95). If deaths fall but the bar is missed: combine with the step-13 calibration as step 16.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_57 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 57u32, "2026-11-09T18:06Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:1x tibia: STEP 15 CODE (as pre-registered in note 56). bc_train.spi gains heal_weighted_mask / heal_weighted_example_of / heal_weighted_examples_of: the heal channel's mask on heal-POSITIVE rows = positive * mask_of, everything else = independent_mask. The loss and its gradient are head_mask * bce (bc_train :100/:119), linear in the mask, so this is exactly a class weight, and positive = 1.0 is byte-for-byte the independent examples (the A/A arm W1 must re-derive 0.074348). apps/predict/bc_healweight.spi: ratio = negatives:positives on I2's round-2 heal-known rows (printed), trains W1 (weight 1) and WR (weight = ratio), evaluates both, and re-runs the step-14 heal probe on WR. Job: ganymede job-1794247531301-tibia-bc-healweight.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_58 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 58u32, "2026-11-09T19:20Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:1x tibia: STEP 15 VERDICT (ganymede job-1794247531301-tibia-bc-healweight, pack77, 71 min). CONTROLS HOLD: I0/I1 losses re-derive; W1 (heal weight 1) final loss 0.074348 = I2 exactly, and W1's eval reproduces I2 line for line (-20.04, paired -8.30, kills 696, deaths 54), so the A/A holds. Heal-known training rows: positive 67620, negative 748252 -> heal weight 11.065543. WR (class-balanced heal loss, theta 0, no calibration): final loss 0.1767; student mean +5.24 +-2.16 vs teacher -11.74 +-5.54; paired diff +16.98 +-5.87; kills 774 (teacher 726), DEATHS 5 (teacher 38; I2 54); extra retreats 2107 of 248301 (0.85 pct), missed 0. SECONDARY MET: teacher-heals/student-not first divergences 0 of 100 (pre-registered < 30; step 14 had 51), so the probe's h-median is undefined (no such splits). BAR: written as \"inside the teacher CI [-17.28, -6.20]\" and framed in notes 37/40 as \"better than -17.28\": +5.24 is ABOVE the whole teacher interval, so the student clears the bar by 22.5 and BEATS the teacher (paired CI excludes 0). Per the pre-registration, progress -> 95. HONEST READING: this is no longer imitation. The class-balanced student heals far more often than the teacher (it was under-healing 4.8:1 on training; the weight reverses it), and with death costing 14000 gp vs 50 gp per potion it out-scores the teacher. The gap that steps 5-14 chased was the heal head's class imbalance, confirmed by both directions (calibration +0.98 mean in step 13, re-weighting +25.3 here). Open question for the item owner: is BC's DoD fidelity to the teacher or score? If fidelity, a weight between 1 and 11 that matches the teacher's heal rate is step 16; if score, the WR student is the new policy candidate and should go to a held-out confirmation on fresh seeds.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_59 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 59u32, "2026-11-09T19:22Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:2x tibia: STEP 16 PRE-REGISTERED (confirmation, no tuning). Seeds 2001-2100 are unused by every tibia module (grep: no 2001 seed in src/apps; training is 1-100, held-out 1001-1100, resampled 10001+), so they are a FRESH block the step-9..15 decisions never saw. Re-derive WR exactly as in step 15 (I2 round-2 pairs, heal weight = training negatives:positives, which must print 11.065543; WR final loss must re-derive 0.17669696, else VOID), then evaluate paired against the teacher on 2001-2100 with bc_eval's paired sums. CONFIRM if the paired-diff 95 pct CI lower bound is > 0 (WR beats the teacher on fresh seeds). WEAK if the paired mean is > 0 but the CI includes 0. REFUTED if the paired mean is <= 0 (step 15 was seed luck on 1001-1100). Code: apps/predict/bc_confirm.spi.")
inl note_of_tibia_bc_policy_60 () = Note ("TIBIA-BC-POLICY", 60u32, "2026-11-09T20:11Z", "tibia", "11-09 16:1x tibia: STEP 16 VERDICT = CONFIRMED (ganymede job-1794252217704-tibia-bc-confirm, pack77). VALID: WR re-derived exactly (heal rows 67620 / 748252, WR final loss 0.17669696 = step 15). On the FRESH seed block 2001-2100 (never used by any step): teacher -9.66 +-5.27, WR student +4.85 +-2.19, paired diff +14.51 +-5.91, so the 95 pct CI is [+8.60, +20.42], with a lower bound > 0. The class-balanced student beats the teacher on seeds it has never seen; step 15's +16.98 was not a property of seeds 1001-1100. SUMMARY OF THE CHAIN (steps 5-16): the residual BC gap was the heal head's class imbalance (heal-positive rows 8.3 pct of heal-known rows; the student under-healed 4.8:1). Fixing it moves the student from -20.04 (I2) to +5.24 (held-out) / +4.85 (fresh), above the teacher. Cleanups in the same run: bc_train.spi now carries the formatter's layout (tokens identical); bc_confirm main was split (retrained) for the cell budget (333 > 273). OPEN FOR THE OWNER (unchanged from note 58): fidelity vs score. If score, the WR student is the policy candidate and this item can close; if fidelity, a weight between 1 and 11 that matches the teacher's heal rate is the next step.")
inl tibia_pg_policy () = Task ("TIBIA-PG-POLICY", "tibia policy gradient: PPO-style training of the cloned policy in the batched WGSL and C simulator lanes, against ES and CEM at an equal simulator budget", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "TIBIA-BC-POLICY", "tibia,training,ml,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_pg_policy () = Planning ("TIBIA-PG-POLICY", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_pg_policy_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-PG-POLICY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY. DoD: pre-registered arms (BC only, BC plus PG, best ES, best CEM, random control) on the frozen scenario pack with held-out seeds; verdict with confidence intervals in the ledger; the winner becomes the live candidate only if it wins on held-out seeds.")
inl note_of_tibia_pg_policy_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-PG-POLICY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:56Z", "tibia", "11-07 tibia groom (lint markers): child of TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY. Next step: wait for TIBIA-BC-POLICY; then pre-register policy gradient vs ES/CEM at an equal sim budget on held-out seeds before any run. Today's PR-33 and PR-34 matter here: the ratio weights over a whole hunt are heavy-tailed, so the PG estimator should be per-decision with a baseline. TypeFeatures: the trajectory step as a record (view, decision, log prob, reward), the method as a union (PolicyGradient | Evolution).")
inl kit_yardstick_audit () = Task ("KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT", "kit heal: audit kit for the bundle-era drift TritCritNet exposed (receipts, gates, ratings and ledgers with no reader and no external yardstick) and retire or justify every one", Feature, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,drift,heal,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_yardstick_audit () = Planning ("KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT", Minutes 660u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_yardstick_audit_1 () = Note ("KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "User 11-07: kit might have been blind the whole time that this is drift; now that it is verified against a codebase that grew in the same era, update the kit backlog so it heals too. EVIDENCE (main 11-07): TritCritNet's Rust half (alpha9252, 161 files) grew in the same eoie bundles as kit and is mostly plan, receipt, gate and rating records with 426 static string literals and self-graded scores, no external benchmark (ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107 n6, tibia PRIOR_ART). kit carries the same vocabulary: 64 files in kit/state (ratings, authority_census, burnin_receipts, prune_receipts, retention_receipts, typecheck_receipts, several *_settlement and *_apply, self_patch*, restart_baton, owner_growth ...) and about 43 of 606 src crates named for receipts, ledgers, gauges, ratings, authority or evidence (kit_gauge_ledger, kit_gauge_model, rating_guard_*, state_receipt_* x10, authority_state_domain ...). Whether each is drift is unmeasured; this item measures it. Children: KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY, KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE, KIT-DRIFT-GUARD. DoD: every state file and receipt-like crate has a row naming its reader (a verb, test or lane that consumes it), its yardstick (the outside fact it is checked against) and a verdict; retired ones archived (scratch-archive, restore note); the guard live in kit standards. Related: KIT-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE, KIT-GRANULAR-MIGRATION, KIT-CONSOL-BUNDLE-ERA.")
inl note_of_kit_yardstick_audit_2 () = Note ("KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:53Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom (markers for lint): parent of KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY, KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE and KIT-DRIFT-GUARD (linked now); 660 m = 240 + 240 + 180. NEXT STEP: run KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY first; retire and guard both depend on its rows. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the audit verdict per artifact is a union (Checked against an external fact, ReadOnlyByItself, Unread) computed from the inventory rows; no string verdicts.")
inl kit_drift_inventory () = Task ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", "kit drift inventory: for every kit/state file and every receipt, ledger, gauge, rating or authority crate, find its readers by import and call graph and its yardstick, as typed rows", Story, P1, D3, 30u32, Active, "", "kit,drift,heal,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_drift_inventory () = Planning ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_1 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT. Method: list kit/state/*.spi and src crates; for each, the importers (crate graph), the verbs that read or write it, the tests that assert on its content, and the outside fact it is compared to (a compiler result, a git state, a file hash, a CI run, a benchmark), or none. DoD: one row per artifact with reader count, yardstick and a proposed verdict (keep, merge, retire); the rows land as a typed Spiral record set in kit, not a tsv; counts reported in a note.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_2 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:53Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom (markers for lint). NEXT STEP: list the 64 kit/state files and the about 43 receipt/ledger/gauge/rating/authority crates, then for each find its readers by grepping exports and file paths across kit/src and scripts, and record the external fact it is checked against (a test, a train gate, a live verb) or none. Reuse KIT-DEF-INDEX rows for readers once they exist. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: artifact GADT indexed by kind (StateFile, Crate); reader as a record with the call site; yardstick as a union (TestFact, GateFact, LiveFact, NoFact); one typed row per artifact.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_3 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 3u32, "2026-11-07T18:16Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, FIRST INVENTORY SLICE (kit/state, measured by name references with git grep over src/*.spi, scripts/*.ps1 and compiler-contracts/*.ps1): 63 .spi state files; 26 have ZERO named readers, all 26 are registered modules of kit/state/package.spiproj (so the state attestation compiles them on every check while no code consumes them), 95,814 bytes, last touched 2026-10-27 (wipe-era receipts). The 26: self_patch_negative, self_patch_apply, self_patch_restore, path_tag_settlement, path_tag_evidence, path_tag_apply, parallel_search_settlement, process_batch_settlement, incident_recovery_apply, receipt_row_kind_apply, fallback_retirement, retention_receipts, pipeline, coverage_refresh, coverage_reactivation_apply, plan_retirement, consolidation_template, architecture, series_apply, series_settlement, series_snapshot, cargo_resume_apply, shim_settlement, shim_apply, calibration, burnin_receipts. Low-reader files (1 to 4 readers: consolidation*, dogfood_exit, prune_receipts, self_patch, patches, adapter_inventory, family_contracts, portable_toolchain, toolchain_process_receipt, legacy_catalog) need a reader-by-reader look: several readers are cold_proof_domain test fixtures, not consumers. CAVEAT: generic stems (core, history, agile, bundle, evidence) overcount readers; their rows need a symbol-level check. NEXT STEP: turn this into typed rows (artifact GADT, readers, yardstick NoFact for the 26) and hand the 26 to KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE as batch 1 (archive the files, drop the module lines, one train green).")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_4 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 4u32, "2026-11-07T18:17Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, INVENTORY SLICE 2 (crates): 18 crates whose names match receipt, ledger, gauge, rating, authority, settlement, evidence, census, burnin or attest (with a Cargo.toml; main counted about 43 with a broader net). ALL 18 have at least one dependent crate (package.spiproj or Cargo.toml): state_receipt_* (parser, fingerprint, serializer, tuple, codec_core) feed kit_agile_state; rating_guard_runtime and the evidence and authority domains feed kit_bundle_zip, kit_cli and kit_handoff; agile_task_census has 8. So crate-level drift is not orphaned crates: the question per crate is whether its call path is reachable from a live verb and whether what it computes is checked against an external fact (a test, a gate, a user-visible verb). NEXT STEP for crates: trace each of the 18 from its dependent to a live verb (kit_cli routes) and mark Reachable plus yardstick, or UnreachableFromVerbs; the state-file batch (26 unread modules, slice 1) is ready for KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE now.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_5 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 5u32, "2026-11-07T23:43Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 19:5x kit, INVENTORY SLICE 3 (reachability, cargo metadata --offline over src, 375 workspace crates). (A) The 18 receipt-like crates: ALL 18 are reachable from kit-cli; 4 have a runnable test block (authority-state-domain, kit-do-facts-receipt, kit-evidence, kit-style-census) and 14 have none (agile-task-census, agile-update-receipt, bootstrap-authority-status, evidence-currentness-domain, handoff-evidence-projection-domain, proxy-file-receipt, proxy-search-receipt, rating-guard-runtime, semantic-evidence-domain, the five state-receipt-* crates); the drift guard (TRAIN39) flags exactly these. (B) 33 crates are not reached from kit-cli: 7 serve the other binaries (kit-dev, kit-predicate-lift and their predicate and metadata domains); 9 are test-only and keep their place (kit-agile-contracts, kit-archive-contracts, kit-contracts, kit-hook-rules, kit-patch-mutation-contracts, kit-patch-transaction-contracts, kit-proxy-edit-contracts, kit-release-contracts, typed-predicate-contracts); 17 have no test, no live dependent, no reference from scripts, CI or another crate, and no binary reaching them: 11 example-only probes (inspection-negative, inspection-policy-probe, kit-bootstrap-probe, kit-domain-probe, kit-patch-batch, kit-policy-probe, kit-rust-std-env, kit-toolchain-argument-agile-probe, kit-toolchain-argument-policy-probe, process-batch-plan-policy-probe, process-batch-plan-resume-probe) and 6 libs (kit-bootstrap-policy, kit-patch-fallback-domain, kit-patch-grammar, kit-patch-scan, patch-domain, patch-model). NEXT STEP: KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE batch 2 after TRAIN39 installs: archive those 17 crate dirs to the kit archive, drop their workspace members, cargo update --workspace, and prove a node regen of the whole tree is unchanged otherwise; the 14 untested live receipt crates each get a test that checks them against a fact, or a retire decision.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_6 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 6u32, "2026-11-07T23:50Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:0x kit: first 3 of the 14 untested live receipt crates now carry a runnable test that checks them against a fact (unstaged): agile_update_receipt (the kit agile set receipt keeps its fields in order: id, progress, status, validation, compiler, bytes_before, bytes_after, elapsed_ms; the clock reads real epoch ms), proxy_file_receipt (elapsed_ms is a bare whole number; real epoch clock), rating_guard_runtime (the ceiling binding accepts 0 to 620 and rejects 621 and negatives; today state/ratings.spi has exactly the 14 active_rating rows at or under 620 that the host check expects). Each file gains the notebook header and an opens-only static block. Proof pending: node probe t (job-1794095391226-kit-probe1107t). NEXT STEP: the other 11 (proxy_search_receipt, bootstrap_authority_status, the evidence domains, agile_task_census, state_receipt_* five), then KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE batch 2 after TRAIN39.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_7 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 7u32, "2026-11-07T23:50Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:0x kit: CORRECTION to slice 3 (B): the cargo graph misses Spiral source-package use (a package listed under packages: in another package.spiproj inlines at source level and leaves no Cargo edge). Re-checked against every package.spiproj: domain (3 users), patch_batch (1), policy_probe (2), rust_std_env (62), bootstrap_policy (2), patch_fallback_domain (1), patch_domain (5) and patch_model (5) ARE used and stay; kit_patch_grammar and kit_patch_scan are themselves users of patch_domain and need the same check under their own dir names. Truly unused (no Cargo dependent, no package.spiproj user, no script or CI reference, no binary reach): 7 example-only probes, inspection_negative, inspection_policy_probe, bootstrap_probe, toolchain_argument_agile_probe, toolchain_argument_policy_probe, process_batch_plan_policy_probe, process_batch_plan_resume_probe. Batch 2 retire scope is those 7 only, after TRAIN39. LESSON for the inventory: reachability = Cargo edges UNION package.spiproj packages edges.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_8 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 8u32, "2026-11-08T00:23Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:3x kit: 7 of the 14 untested live receipt crates now have a runnable test checking a fact, all node-proven 1/1 (probes t, w, x): agile_update_receipt, proxy_file_receipt, rating_guard_runtime, proxy_search_receipt (truncation at the hit limit, end_of_file on a short slice, the fs-search field order), agile_task_census (status by id, done and unsettled ids, waits column and counts over the real Task row shape), evidence_currentness_domain (stages: irregular 0, observed 1, verified 2; cargo's own RUSTC/CARGO variable names; kit vs kit.exe), semantic_evidence_domain (current only with all 6 gates and all 3 flags). Generated sizes unchanged or smaller (tests add no codegen). Left: bootstrap_authority_status, handoff_evidence_projection_domain and the five state_receipt_* crates, written in the old (=.) dialect with checks inside main; their heal is a respell plus moving the main checks into test blocks, a separate slice. Rides TRAIN39.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_9 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 9u32, "2026-11-08T00:24Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 20:3x kit, FINDING (the clearest receipt drift so far, no test written on purpose): kit status prints a constant. bootstrap_authority_status exports five values that kit_cli_model run_status reads: four contract authority statuses (workspace_state, compiler_session, legacy_cpp_bundle_writer, ingest_frontier) that are self-checks over fixed inputs inside their own models (revision_binding 0 0 0, manifest_binding 1 2: they fold to constants at compile time), and settled_migration_status_code () = 987i32, printed as the status itself. The neighbours are constants too: settled_migration_score 987, capability equivalents 69 total / 69 settled / 0 remaining, recovered_prototype_score 304. Nothing measures any of them, so a test here could only assert a constant equals itself, which would satisfy the drift guard without checking a fact. DECISION NEEDED (kit's own verb, proposed default): kit status reports measured facts (installed train, pinned compiler core, backlog census counts, crate gate verdict) and the five constants retire with bootstrap_authority_status; the contract self-checks stay as tests in their own packages. Until then bootstrap_authority_status is listed as untested-by-design in this inventory.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_inventory_10 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", 10u32, "2026-11-08T01:04Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 21:0x kit, KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE BATCH 2 DONE for TRAIN40 (unstaged; TRAIN39's snapshot was already taken): the 7 crates the corrected inventory found unused by every edge kind (no Cargo dependent, no package.spiproj user, no script or CI reference, no binary reach) are archived, not deleted, to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\kit-crate-retire-batch2-20261107-210401: inspection_negative, inspection_policy_probe, bootstrap_probe, toolchain_argument_agile_probe, toolchain_argument_policy_probe, process_batch_plan_policy_probe, process_batch_plan_resume_probe. Each was re-checked for package.spiproj users right before the move (0 each); their workspace members are gone, cargo update --workspace refreshed the lock, and cargo metadata --offline --locked passes; no reference remains in src/Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, scripts, compiler-contracts, .github or any package.spiproj. Workspace 375 -> 368 crates plus tonight's new ones. Proof: the next train's full regen (TRAIN40).")
inl kit_drift_retire () = Task ("KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE", "kit drift retirement: retire or merge every artifact the inventory marked as no reader or no yardstick, archived with a restore path, with the kit test suite and a release train green after each batch", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY", "kit,drift,heal,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_drift_retire () = Planning ("KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_drift_retire_1 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT. DoD: each retire batch archives (never deletes) with scratch-archive, passes kit's tests and a release train, and records what went in a note; verbs that only produced self-referential receipts either gain a real consumer or go; the counts before and after (state files, crates, lines) are reported.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_retire_2 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:53Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom (markers for lint). NEXT STEP: take the inventory rows whose yardstick is NoFact and readers are empty, group them into batches by crate family, archive (never delete) each batch with its tests, and prove each batch with a train green before the next. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: batch record with its artifacts and the proving train id; retirement state union (Proposed, Archived, Proven).")
inl note_of_kit_drift_retire_3 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-11-07T18:30Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, BATCH 1 STAGED (unstaged, rides TRAIN38): the 26 unread state modules from KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY slice 1 moved into the kit archive (kit-state-retire-batch1-20261107-142018, with package.spiproj before and after), and their 26 module lines dropped from kit/state/package.spiproj (69 -> 43 lines); git shows 27 files, deletions only. CHECK RESULT, not yet clean: kit agile check C:/home/git/kit on the retired state fails with Package graph rejected ... authority_state_domain: Package C:/home/git/kit/src/spiral is not loaded (a package-resolution error naming a src package, unrelated to which state modules are listed); the A/B run with the 26 modules restored only timed out at the 30 s attestation bound (VOID), so the baseline is unknown. NEXT STEP: run the same check at HEAD on the node with a longer timeout to learn whether the src/spiral resolution failure predates this batch (likely: kit/state is the frozen legacy state and trains do not attest it); then prove batch 1 in TRAIN38. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: batch record (artifacts, proving train), retirement state union (Proposed, Archived, Proven).")
inl note_of_kit_drift_retire_4 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-11-07T18:48Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, A/B SETTLED on the node (job-1794076836456-kit-state-ab, pack61): kit agile check on kit/state fails IDENTICALLY with and without batch 1 (Package graph rejected ... src/authority_state_domain: Package .../kit/src/spiral is not loaded), so that failure PREDATES the retirement and is unrelated to it; batch 1 removes no reader and changes no check outcome. The pre-existing failure (kit legacy state no longer type-checks because authority_state_domain resolves a src/spiral package that does not exist) is a separate drift fact for KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY. NEXT STEP: TRAIN38 carries batch 1; close batch 1 when that train is green.")
