inl note_of_kit_drift_guard_1 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "Child of KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT. DoD: the rule runs in the kit gate and the style hook, with a positive and a negative fixture; it reports the artifact, the missing reader or yardstick, and the fix; documented in kit's standards output.")
inl note_of_kit_drift_guard_2 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:53Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom (markers for lint). NEXT STEP: add a kit standards rule that flags a new package or state file whose name says receipt, ledger, gauge, rating or authority unless the same change adds its reader and a test that checks it against an external fact; wire it into the style hook report. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: drift_word union for the suspicious names, finding rows typed, verdict union (Guarded, MissingReader, MissingCheck).")
inl note_of_kit_drift_guard_3 () = Note ("KIT-DRIFT-GUARD", 3u32, "2026-11-07T21:48Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, GUARD BUILT (unstaged): a measurable proxy for reader-and-check-land-together, since that cannot be read statically. kit standards (TestTargets, a default standard) now flags a package whose name says receipt, ledger, gauge, rating, authority, settlement or burnin and that has no runnable test block anywhere in its Spiral files: package.spiproj:1 test-targets a receipt-like package with no test that checks it against a fact. Pure helpers drift_named and has_test_block in kit_standards/rules.spi with test a_receipt_named_package_needs_a_test_that_checks_it. Preview over kit/src: 23 receipt-named packages, 18 with no runnable test (state_receipt_codec_core/model, fingerprint domain and probes, parser, serializer, tuple, rating_guard_contract and runtime, proxy file and search receipts, patch_compat_receipts, patch_authority_probe, agile_update_receipt, bootstrap_authority_status), which is the next KIT-DRIFT-INVENTORY slice. kit standards findings are report-only (the edit hook runs only the census ratchet), so nothing blocks. NEXT STEP: prove in a node probe (rules.spi notebook plus kit_standards regen), ride TRAIN39, then decide per package: add a check, or hand it to KIT-DRIFT-RETIRE.")
inl convergence_lab () = Task ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", "Convergence lab: one SOTA target from the incomplete work, a small Spiral-built, schema-bound, calibrated, ternary-capable decision model (Jev-shaped) on the public accuracy-per-cost frontier of its size class, every absorbed seed an ablation arm", Epic, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "", "ml,research,curricula,training,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_convergence_lab () = Planning ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", Minutes 2220u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_convergence_lab_1 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:50Z", "main", "User 11-07: couldn't we start over from all the techniques and curricula gathered over the last month, considering benchmarks and definitions of done, not limited to BitNet checkpoints, something stronger that emerges from what we're attempting (TritCritNet = the C++ model; the old hope was that combining it with W43 and zeta would make intelligence converge). The difference this time: every curriculum is generated with an independent checker (our own engines decide the answer), every claim is a pre-registered hypothesis with controls, and language quality is measured on a public yardstick. TECHNIQUES as arms: transformer (TRANSFORMER-TRAIN), a true selective-scan SSM block (the piece TritCritNet's audit said was missing), a hybrid with criticality-gated attention islands (TritCritNet's idea), fp32 vs Q8 vs ternary QAT, gradient vs ES/CEM. CURRICULA, each with an exact checker and length or depth splits for out-of-distribution tests: TinyStories text; regex (membership, derivative, equivalence, checked by the regex engines); zeta typed arithmetic (primality, factorization, von Mangoldt, checked by lib); CIC typing judgments (checked by the lean_cic sample's checker); tiny Spiral programs and their values or types (checked by the compiler); great-circle geometry from W43.py's operations (distances, intersections, checked numerically); tibia next-state prediction (checked by the simulator). HYPOTHESES (registered in CONV-PREREG before any run): H1 a model trained on the mixed curriculum beats single-curriculum models of equal compute on each family's held-out OOD split (transfer); H2 ternary QAT at equal memory beats fp32 at its smaller size; H3 SSM or hybrid beats the transformer at equal parameters on the longest splits; H4 gated attention reaches the same loss with less compute; controls: shuffled-answer curricula and the untrained model. Children: CONV-PREREG, CONV-CURRICULA, CONV-SSM-BLOCK, CONV-RUNS, CONV-REPORT. DoD: each hypothesis has a verdict with confidence intervals in the ledger; the best model and its benchmark table are on a Pages site; the report says plainly whether anything converged. Budget: node CPUs and the 20 USD GPU cap unless the user raises it.")
inl note_of_convergence_lab_2 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:54Z", "main", "Next step: CONV-PREREG (register H1-H4 before any run), then CONV-CURRICULA.")
inl note_of_convergence_lab_3 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:10Z", "main", "main 11-07 AMENDMENT (user 11-07: wasn't I trying to do some kind of jev? will these tasks yield something better? if not, why not suggest it). Read as JEPA (joint embedding predictive architecture: predict the representation of a hidden part from its context in latent space, no token reconstruction); the word jev or JEPA appears nowhere in the recovered material, so this reading is main's and the user can correct it. Why it fits: the original vision (i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet-cpp\\readme_tritcritnet.md) says TritCritNet is NOT a tiny homemade ChatGPT but a learned validator over typed evidence: a four-lane encoder (exact symbolic W43/base-43, numeric phase from zeta, dynamical Lenia, semantic EC text) on a shared selective-state trunk, unifying the lanes into one compact latent space where the kinds of object become distinguishable coordinates. That is a joint-embedding, latent-prediction design with a critic head, not next-token language modeling. The first version of this epic (n1) planned next-token training plus transfer tests, which is the thing the vision rejected; main anchored on the transformer pipeline because it already has an external oracle, and did not read the vision's architecture section before filing. CHANGES: (1) new H0, registered first: JEPA-style pretraining (context encoder, slowly updated target encoder, latent predictor, an anti-collapse term) on the typed lanes beats next-token pretraining at equal compute, measured by frozen-encoder probes trained on checker labels (is this answer correct, which family, how hard) on the held-out OOD splits, plus a shuffled-label control; (2) the primary product is the critic or validator the vision describes, scored by the independent checkers, with language generation as a secondary arm; (3) the lanes follow the vision (symbolic, numeric, dynamical, semantic) plus a tibia simulator lane, and the curricula of n1 become the lanes' data; (4) new children CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE and CONV-WORLD-MODEL. Kept from n1: independent checkers, pre-registration, OOD splits, public yardsticks.")
inl note_of_convergence_lab_4 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 4u32, "2026-11-07T15:35Z", "main", "main 11-07 GROOM: TRITCRITNET-ABSORB feeds this epic its seeds (the multi-lane encoder, the mixed-radix tokenizer, the validator role, criticality-gated compute, ternary training, the selective-scan gap) through TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP rows, the same absorption-map discipline as the mega sample to regex; the TritCritNet codebases are deleted only at that epic's delete gate.")
inl note_of_convergence_lab_5 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 5u32, "2026-11-07T15:36Z", "main", "main 11-07 CORRECTION (user 11-07: you're still researching jepa, i said jev). The n3 JEPA reading was wrong. Jev (TypeSafe AI, launched 2026-09-15, Hacker News launch thread of about 1,800-1,900 points; built by Diogo Almeida, ex-OpenAI; a16z-led round reported at a 7.5B USD valuation): a non-generative System One decision model. The caller defines the question and the allowed answers (a schema, up to 255 options), the model scores every allowed answer at once instead of writing tokens, it can never answer outside the schema, and it is trained by RLCD (reinforcement learning for calibrated decisions) so its probabilities match how often it is right. Uses: classification, routing, scoring, extraction, guardrails. Caveats from coverage: benchmarks self-published (speedups of 40-500x cited), internals undisclosed (non-autoregressive, parallel evaluation; whether it is a transformer is unknown), weak at math, counting and long context. Sources are secondary (DigitalOcean, eesel, byteiota, gopenai, Bloomberg Law); pin TypeSafe's own post before relying on any number. WHY IT IS WHAT TRITCRITNET WAS REACHING FOR: the original readme says TritCritNet is not a tiny ChatGPT but a learned validator that decides what kind of object it is looking at (exact arithmetic, symbolic fever, executable code, dynamical pattern, false proof, useful route, hallucinated bridge); that is a schema-bound decision model, the Jev shape, built before Jev existed. Spiral fits it better than most stacks: the answer schema is a typed union, derived from the types (nameof, typefeatureset), so out-of-schema answers are unrepresentable by construction. CHANGES: H0 becomes the decision-model hypothesis (CONV-PREREG n4); CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE is retitled to the decision objective (its id kept, kit rename is not safe on this backlog), with JEPA-style latent pretraining demoted to an optional encoder-pretraining arm; CONV-WORLD-MODEL stays as a tibia arm, not the headline. Why main did not suggest it: Jev launched 2026-09-15, after main's training data, and main guessed JEPA instead of searching the word first.")
inl note_of_convergence_lab_6 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 6u32, "2026-11-07T15:39Z", "main", "main 11-07 ONE TARGET (user 11-07: what we absorb must converge into something SOTA, not loose samples; fiscal has a measurable end, tibia does not, the transformer at least does; the aim is to see what SOTA can be made from all this incomplete work done with less capable models). THE CONVERGENCE TARGET, replacing the open-ended framing of n1: a small Jev-shaped decision model built entirely in Spiral, schema-bound (the answer set is a typed union), scoring every allowed answer in one parallel pass, calibrated, ternary-capable and CPU-native, compiled from one source to Rust, C and WGSL, that reaches the published accuracy-per-cost frontier of open models of its size class on a pinned public suite of fixed-answer benchmarks. MEASURABLE END: on every benchmark of the suite pinned in CONV-SOTA-TARGET, our model sits on or beyond the Pareto frontier of accuracy against CPU latency per decision and weight bytes, measured on the same machine against the pinned comparison models, with calibration (expected calibration error, Brier) reported beside accuracy; the frontier page publishes it from GH Actions (CONV-FRONTIER-PAGE). If the frontier is not reached, the epic still closes with the published gap and the best point reached, so it cannot spin forever. HOW EVERYTHING CONVERGES: every absorbed piece is an arm in one ablation table on that frontier, and stays only if it moves the frontier or is required by something that does: the transformer training stack (TRANSFORMER-TRAIN) is the backbone and the generation baseline; the transformer speed work (TRANSFORMER-CPU-SPEED, TRANSFORMER-BEAT-MOJO) sets the latency axis; ternary (TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY, TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-TERNARY) sets the weight-bytes axis; TritCritNet's seeds (selective-scan trunk, criticality-gated compute, the multi-lane typed encoder, the mixed-radix tokenizer, the validator role) are arms via TRITCRITNET-ABSORB; Jev's schema-bound parallel scoring and calibration training are the head (CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE, now the decision objective); the checker-labelled curricula (regex, zeta, CIC, Spiral programs, W43 geometry, tibia) are extra training data whose value is measured on the public suite, plus our own verifiable track as a second table; tibia next-action and kit routing are dogfood consumers, not the yardstick. H0-H4 (CONV-PREREG) become the pre-registered ablations inside this table.")
inl note_of_convergence_lab_7 () = Note ("CONVERGENCE-LAB", 7u32, "2026-11-11T01:57Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 cross-ref (2026-11-10 window close): child CONV-CURRICULA now has ALL 6 curriculum families SPECCED (authoring half done) — regex, tibia-next-state, W43-exactness, zeta/phase, Lenia, EC-routing — in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CONV-CURRICULA\\ (5 files). Each has an independent non-model oracle (engine/sim/op/math/CIC), the shared TRITCRITNET-alpha001 row format, length/depth/magnitude OOD held-out splits, test blocks, no committed data. Also: TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP seed sources fully enumerated with destinations routed here (CONV-FRONTIER-PAGE arms: model-arch/ternary/criticality/MoE; CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE: claim-gate decision objective + curricula). These feed the frontier ablation table when the build gate (port specs to Spiral generators+checkers) runs.")
