inl note_of_conv_prereg_3 () = Note ("CONV-PREREG", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:10Z", "main", "main 11-07 AMENDMENT: register H0 first (JEPA-style latent-prediction pretraining vs next-token pretraining at equal compute, scored by frozen-encoder probes on checker labels over the OOD splits, shuffled-label control), see CONVERGENCE-LAB n3.")
inl note_of_conv_prereg_4 () = Note ("CONV-PREREG", 4u32, "2026-11-07T15:36Z", "main", "main 11-07 AMENDMENT, replaces n3: H0 is now the decision-model hypothesis (see CONVERGENCE-LAB correction note). A schema-bound decision model (typed answer unions, every allowed answer scored at once, trained for calibration) on the checker-labelled lanes beats, at equal compute and on the OOD splits, (a) next-token generation constrained to the same schema and (b) a linear probe on a frozen next-token encoder, on accuracy AND calibration (expected calibration error, Brier score); controls: shuffled labels and the majority class. JEPA-style pretraining enters only as an encoder arm under H0.")
inl note_of_conv_prereg_5 () = Note ("CONV-PREREG", 5u32, "2026-11-09T15:43Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:4x DONE: 8 experiments registered with kit experiment register in a new ledger, i574n.github/docs/ledger/convergence/ (one <ID>.registration file each, unstaged), all stamped registered=2026-11-09T15:42Z, before any CONV run exists. CONV-H0-ACC (decision vs constrained_gen, ood_accuracy) and CONV-H0-ECE (ood_ece, 15 equal-mass bins; Brier reported, not tested): H0 per the 11-07 amendment (Jev-shaped decision model). CONV-H1-TRANSFER (mixed vs single, analyzed --where family=X; holds on >= 4 of 6 checker families). CONV-H2-TERNARY (ternary_qat vs fp32_small at equal weight bytes +-5 pct). CONV-H3-SSM and CONV-H3-HYBRID (each vs transformer at equal params +-5 pct, longest_split_accuracy). CONV-H4-GATED (compute_to_target = counted training FLOPs to the dense arm's median final loss; never-reached runs scored at budget). CONV-CTRL-SHUFFLED (one-sample: accuracy minus majority-class rate = 0; a failing lane is excluded from H0-H4 and disclosed). Every test: Welch two-sided unless noted, 5 seeds per arm, confidence 0.95, an MDE stated in the decision rule (3 accuracy points; 0.02 ECE; 15 pct compute). Changes from now on go through kit experiment amend (recorded with a reason), never edits. Proof: the 8 registration files (registered= lines).")
inl conv_curricula () = Task ("CONV-CURRICULA", "Convergence lab curricula: generators and independent checkers in Spiral for the seven families (TinyStories, regex, zeta arithmetic, CIC typing, Spiral programs, great-circle geometry, tibia next state), with in-distribution and OOD splits", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "ml,research,curricula,training,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_conv_curricula () = Planning ("CONV-CURRICULA", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_conv_curricula_1 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 1u32, "2026-11-07T14:51Z", "main", "Child of CONVERGENCE-LAB. Each family is a typed generator plus a checker that is not the model (the regex engines, lib primes and Lambda, the CIC checker, the compiler, the W43 operations re-implemented in Spiral, the tibia simulator); splits by length, depth or magnitude so OOD means harder, not just different. DoD: per family a fixed-seed dataset spec, a checker with test blocks, and a size and difficulty table; no dataset files committed, generated in CI.")
inl note_of_conv_curricula_2 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 2u32, "2026-11-07T14:54Z", "main", "Next step: build the first two curricula, each with its independent checker and a harder held-out split: regex (the regex engines decide) and tibia next-state (the simulator decides); the rest follow the same row format.")
inl note_of_conv_curricula_3 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:52Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 drafted the first curriculum SPEC (regex), the authoring half of \"build the first two curricula\": %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CONV-CURRICULA\\regex-curriculum-spec.md. Row format reuses the TRITCRITNET alpha001 shape (id,split,family,pattern,input,expected_match,expected_caps,difficulty_depth,difficulty_len,seed); CHECKER = the regex engine itself (never the model), with a cross-engine DISAGREE oracle if the repo has >1 backend. 7 typed generator families (literal/char_class/quantifier/alternation/anchor/group_capture/backref), each with a difficulty knob. Size/difficulty table L0-L3 + two OOD held-out splits (depth 4-5 and input<=128 = harder, same families). Test blocks assert engine-reproduces-row + OOD-still-decided + polarity balance. NEXT: port to a Spiral generator+checker in the regex repo (19 .spi, engine is the oracle); then tibia next-state (simulator decides) in the same row format; no data committed, CI generates.")
inl note_of_conv_curricula_4 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 4u32, "2026-11-11T01:53Z", "org-f33af161", "Second curriculum SPEC drafted (tibia next-state): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CONV-CURRICULA\\tibia-nextstate-curriculum-spec.md. Checker = the tibia SIMULATOR (deterministic next-state replay oracle), never the model. Row: id,split,family,state,action,expected_next_state,difficulty_entities,difficulty_steps,seed. 5 families (movement/combat/item_use/multi_entity/sequence); table L0-L3 + OOD held-out (9-12 entities, k 4-6 steps = harder, same sim rules). Test blocks assert sim-reproduces-row + determinism + multi-step=folded-single-steps. BOTH first-two curricula specs now authored (regex + tibia), each with engine/simulator-as-oracle + length/depth/magnitude OOD + no committed data. Next (parent, BUILD gate): port both to Spiral generator+checker with test blocks (regex repo + tibia sim), CI-generated; the remaining families (W43 ops, CIC, compiler, lib primes/Lambda) reuse the same row-format + independent-checker pattern.")
inl note_of_conv_curricula_5 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 5u32, "2026-11-11T01:54Z", "org-f33af161", "Third curriculum spec drafted (W43 exactness, the foundational skeleton beyond the required first two): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CONV-CURRICULA\\w43-exactness-curriculum-spec.md. Checker = W43 ops re-implemented in Spiral (deterministic arithmetic oracle, per the DoD list). 8 op families (year/date_mjd encode-decode, next/prev_code, cycle43, boundary_year, offset_ablation, wrong_offset_detect); table L0-L3 + OOD far-from-epoch magnitudes & unseen offset subtleties; test blocks assert op-reproduces-row + round-trip identity + boundary/leakage detection. Three specs now authored (regex, tibia, W43), each engine/sim/op-as-oracle, same row format, length/depth/magnitude OOD, no committed data. Remaining families (zeta/phase via lib primes+Lambda, Lenia dynamics, EC-route via CIC checker, the compiler) follow the identical pattern. Parent gate = port to Spiral generator+checker, CI-generated.")
inl note_of_conv_curricula_6 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 6u32, "2026-11-11T01:55Z", "org-f33af161", "Fourth curriculum spec drafted (zeta/phase, TRITCRITNET Layer 2, phase literacy not mysticism): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CONV-CURRICULA\\zeta-phase-curriculum-spec.md. Checker = lib primes + Lambda deterministic math (mod/phase/eta ops), never the model. 6 families (epoch_mod, phase_golden/prime, eta_alt/radix, zeta_signal_bucket, criticality_label, modular_clock); OOD = larger magnitudes + near-threshold criticality; test blocks assert math-reproduces-row + bucket stability + partition completeness. FOUR of ~6 curriculum families now specced (regex, tibia, W43, zeta/phase) — all engine/sim/op-as-oracle, same row format, length/depth/magnitude OOD, no committed data, CI-generated. Remaining: Lenia dynamics (sim checker) + EC corpus routing (CIC checker). Parent gate = port specs to Spiral generators+checkers. All specs in the CONV-CURRICULA draft dir.")
inl note_of_conv_curricula_7 () = Note ("CONV-CURRICULA", 7u32, "2026-11-11T01:56Z", "org-f33af161", "ALL 6 CURRICULUM FAMILIES NOW SPECCED (authoring half of the item complete). Final two drafted: Lenia dynamics (sim checker: predict {mass,entropy,com,stability-class oscillator/dissipates/explodes/glider} from compressed rollouts) + EC corpus routing (CIC checker: route into the 10-label EC arc taxonomy, LLM labels frozen as oracle, claim-gate/anti-delusion tie-in). File: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\CONV-CURRICULA\\lenia-and-ec-curriculum-specs.md. Full set = regex, tibia-next-state, W43-exactness, zeta/phase, Lenia, EC-routing — each with an INDEPENDENT non-model oracle (engine/sim/op/math/CIC), the shared row format, length/depth/magnitude OOD held-out splits, test blocks, no committed data (CI-generated), matching the DoD per-family (fixed-seed spec + checker with test blocks + size/difficulty table). PARENT BUILD GATE remains: port each spec to a Spiral generator+checker, starting regex (DoD-named pilot). 5 spec files in the CONV-CURRICULA draft dir.")
