inl conv_jepa_objective () = Task ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", "Convergence lab decision objective (Jev-style): a schema-bound typed decision model that scores every allowed answer at once, trained for calibration on checker labels, on the multi-lane encoder; JEPA-style latent pretraining only as an optional encoder arm", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "TRANSFORMER-TRAIN-GRAD,CONV-CURRICULA", "ml,research,curricula,training,jev,decision-model,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_conv_jepa_objective () = Planning ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_conv_jepa_objective_1 () = Note ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", 1u32, "2026-11-07T15:10Z", "main", "Child of CONVERGENCE-LAB (n3 amendment). Read the primary JEPA papers before coding and pin them in the first note (the image, video and language variants and how each avoids representation collapse). DoD: the encoder trains stably (no collapse: representation variance and rank tracked per step); frozen-encoder probes for correctness, family and difficulty beat the same probes on a next-token-pretrained encoder of equal compute, or the note says they do not; both arms registered under H0 in the ledger.")
inl note_of_conv_jepa_objective_2 () = Note ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:11Z", "main", "Next step: read and pin the primary JEPA papers (I-JEPA, V-JEPA, and LeCun's position paper), then specify the multi-lane encoder's latent-prediction loss, the slowly updated target encoder and the anti-collapse term, before writing code. Caveat: the user's word was 'jev', read as JEPA by the agent but unconfirmed; confirm with the user before building.")
inl note_of_conv_jepa_objective_3 () = Note ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:35Z", "main", "main 11-07: the user confirmed JEPA is meant (the HN-hyped one: LeCun's AMI Labs, 1.03B USD seed in March 2026, V-JEPA 2.1 in March 2026, Causal-JEPA predicting object states from interactions, LLM-JEPA for language). Read these primary sources first and pin them in a note; Causal-JEPA's object-interaction prediction is the closest match to the tibia world model, LLM-JEPA to the semantic lane. Seeds from TritCritNet that land here (TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP gives the rows): the four-lane typed-evidence encoder, the mixed-radix tokenizer (bytes, base-43 symbols, small numeric tokens), the validator role, and criticality-gated compute as an arm.")
inl note_of_conv_jepa_objective_4 () = Note ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", 4u32, "2026-11-07T15:36Z", "main", "main 11-07 RETARGET (user: i said jev, not JEPA). Jev (TypeSafe AI, launched 2026-09-15, Hacker News launch thread of about 1,800-1,900 points; built by Diogo Almeida, ex-OpenAI; a16z-led round reported at a 7.5B USD valuation): a non-generative System One decision model. The caller defines the question and the allowed answers (a schema, up to 255 options), the model scores every allowed answer at once instead of writing tokens, it can never answer outside the schema, and it is trained by RLCD (reinforcement learning for calibrated decisions) so its probabilities match how often it is right. Uses: classification, routing, scoring, extraction, guardrails. Caveats from coverage: benchmarks self-published (speedups of 40-500x cited), internals undisclosed (non-autoregressive, parallel evaluation; whether it is a transformer is unknown), weak at math, counting and long context. Sources are secondary (DigitalOcean, eesel, byteiota, gopenai, Bloomberg Law); pin TypeSafe's own post before relying on any number. DoD now: answer schemas are Spiral unions per curriculum family (verdict correct or wrong, family, difficulty bucket, next action for tibia); the model returns a calibrated distribution over exactly those cases in one parallel pass; trained first by cross-entropy on checker labels, then by a calibration objective in the RLCD spirit (pin the method from TypeSafe's own material when it is public, otherwise a proper scoring rule); reported: accuracy, expected calibration error and Brier score per family on OOD splits, latency per decision, against constrained next-token generation at equal compute. Seeds from TritCritNet (TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP): the four-lane typed-evidence encoder, the mixed-radix tokenizer, the validator role, criticality-gated compute. The n1 and n2 JEPA notes remain as history.")
inl note_of_conv_jepa_objective_5 () = Note ("CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE", 5u32, "2026-11-07T16:47Z", "main", "main 11-07: linked to TFS-CONVERSION-LOSS-LAWS. A decision over a typed answer set is a Lossy conversion by construction (input to one of N options); calibration (ECE, Brier) is how this lane names that loss honestly. No scope change; record the answer-set mapping as Lossy with the named loss when the objective is written.")
inl conv_world_model () = Task ("CONV-WORLD-MODEL", "Convergence lab world model: an action-conditioned latent predictor of the tibia simulator (next latent state from state and action) used for planning by search in latent space, against the gradient and evolution policies", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE,TIBIA-BC-POLICY", "ml,research,curricula,training,jepa,team:org,main", "current", "current")
