inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_1 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T15:22Z", "x", "2026-11-07 11:22 x: split out of CELLS-TARGET-REQUIRED (11-07) after NoTestTarget landed for test cells. Two inherited defaults remain, both deliberate until measured: (1) non-test steps (code cells, the plan_tests whole-file step) still build on default_builders: the prelude's ///> lines, else SPIRAL_CELLS_DEFAULT_TARGET / default_target:, else ///> zig. The ~391 test-free self-check files compile on zig this way, and the Cells suite's test_helper sets the env to rust. (2) Notebook.inherit_deps merges the prelude's -d crates into a test's own same-tool builder. Plan: census which files rely on each (the zig default for the whole-file step; prelude -d reaching own ///> rust); decide where the whole-file target comes from (explicit ///> on the entry or code cell, or derived from the file's own test targets, i.e. inferred from explicit lines rather than a convention); move needed crates into package manifests (as x did); then remove default_builders' prelude/env/zig chain and inherit_deps, and update test_helper. Prove it with an org census plus a node Cells suite and a control.")
inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_2 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:23Z", "x", "2026-11-07 11:23 x: raised to P2 at main's direction (11-07). The user's 'keep everything explicit, no env vars prelude etc.' covers code cells, the whole-file step and inherit_deps too, not only tests. Per-kind censuses come first, as planned.")
inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_3 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:27Z", "x", "2026-11-07 11:27 x: CENSUSES DONE (box, cache-free walk of C:\\home\\git skipping .cache/tmp/polyglot; 4157 .spi files with code cells). (A) inherit_deps: only 39 files rely on it, ALL x's own (26 client, 13 sim), and every crate they inherit (serde_json, base64, jiff, sha2, unicode-segmentation, unicode-normalization) is already declared in x's package manifests since today. So removing inherit_deps is a no-op for the org; it needs its own Cells gate plus an x verify. (B) The non-test target default: 4063 files' code cells and whole-file check fall back to the hardcoded zig (kit 1210 + its eoie mirror 1210, The-Spiral-Language 857, spiral 199, Spiral-s-ML-Library 168, tibia 148, fiscal 103, tictactoe 49, i574n.github 24, html 20, regex 18, dice 16, blog 10, alphabet 8, dir-tree-html 7, x 7, ...). 90 more take the prelude's targets (x 75, spiral 14, i574n.github 1). OPTIONS for where a non-test step's target comes from: (1) a ///> on each file's code/entry cell: a respell of about 4153 files (heavy churn); (2) a per-package declaration in the manifest, like crates (e.g. cells_targets = ['zig'] in spiral.toml / cells_targets: in package.spiproj): explicit, stated once where it belongs, and a few dozen manifests instead of thousands of files [x recommends]; (3) derive it from the file's own explicit test targets (covers the 90 prelude files and any file with tests; test-free files still need (1) or (2)). Either way the env var, default_target: and the hardcoded zig go.")
inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_4 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 4u32, "2026-11-07T16:42Z", "x", "2026-11-07 12:42 x: APPLIED (unstaged), the user's (B) per-file choice relayed by main. 1906 files in our 18 repos got their effective non-test target as line 1, above any ///- --package row (1821 ///> zig; the rest copy their prelude's ///> lines). Per-file proof: the header resolves to exactly today's prelude/zig default, runnable tests' own targets are unchanged, nothing attached to a test, and a hash-guarded write with originals backed up in the scratchpad. Cells: Notebook.file_targets (the ///> lines among the first cell's leading directive rows) replaces default_builders (prelude/SPIRAL_CELLS_DEFAULT_TARGET/default_target:/zig removed); inherit_deps removed; test_helper's env default removed. A non-test step without targets fails with 'NoFileTarget: <path> names no target for its code cells: add a ///> <lang> line at its top'; empty (inferred-skip) steps are exempt. About 40 Cells fixtures now name ///> rust at their top. Node: Cells suite 386/394 (6 VOID mirror gaps; 2 parity tests that timed out under load and pass alone). Final census of our repos: 1914 files, 1913 ok, plus 1 flag: cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd, a Livebook smart-cell demo on the single-cell eval! API, ungated. REMAINING implicit default: Cells.run/eval! single-cell Builders.default() = rust (the Livebook smart-cell UX); a decision for main/the user. Owners told: kit, tibia, fiscal, compiler; main routes the rest.")
inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_5 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 5u32, "2026-11-07T16:47Z", "x", "2026-11-07 12:47 x: follow-up from fiscal. A generator that writes .spi units must emit the target line too, or the next regeneration drops it and the drift check fails. fiscal's generator.spi capped_unit_text now writes '///> zig' above its '///- --package . --timeout N' header (FD8B21FA, 83 units byte-identical on regeneration). Org search: no other emitter writes .spi headers, and fiscal's build.ps1 is the only generated-drift check.")
inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_6 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 6u32, "2026-11-07T18:06Z", "x", "2026-11-07 14:06 x: FINAL (user, via compiler, 11-07 afternoon): TESTS ONLY. This supersedes the per-file header and the (b) union. Cells runs only test cells (test / fails / build_only), each on its own ///> lines with its own -d crates. Code cells and main never run, and the plan_tests whole-file step is removed (notebook.spi whole_file and last_def deleted; scope renamed TestsOnly). A non-test step with no target of its own is planned empty. file_targets/union, NoFileTarget, inherit_deps, default_builders and the env/default_target/zig fallbacks are all removed; test_cell_names covers fails and build_only, so NoTestTarget applies to them too. Node Cells suite 387/393 (6 VOID mirror gaps). Undo of the line-1 headers: compiler's cleanup did the 759 files with tests; I restored kit 917 + spiral 75 + tibia 73 + fiscal 2 byte-exact from my backups (routes.spi by kit); main restored its 100. document_test fixed: removing ///> _ had left a non-canonical blank line before main in 7 files, now normalized (dice/documents/near_wallet round trips 0 differing). keccak's fails test got ///> zig; main's dice fails tests too. Crates: x manifests' crates lists removed; each x rust test carries a -d list again (39 files, 152 lines). A node job is minimizing each list to the crates the test's generated Rust actually references (job-1794074601477-x-crates1, core E3F33F3766EE6EDA). Coverage loss sent to compiler: 390 test-free work mains; 8 with explicit check lines (MAIN-CHECKS-TO-TESTS candidates).")
inl note_of_cells_nontest_targets_explicit_7 () = Note ("CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT", 7u32, "2026-11-09T13:08Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "proof: 11-09 09:1x microblog groom. The item's goal (no inherited targets for code cells or the whole-file check, and inherit_deps dropped) was met by the 11-07 TESTS ONLY change recorded in note 6: code cells and main never run, the whole-file step is removed, and a non-test step with no target is planned empty. Re-checked in today's tree (spiral/apps/cells, *.spi/*.ex/*.exs): 0 matches for inherit_deps, default_builders, NoFileTarget, file_targets, whole_file, last_def and default_target, while TestsOnly/NoTestTarget are live in notebook.spi (3), notebook.ex, mix spiral.targets and notebook_targets_test.exs. Green evidence: the node Cells suite at the change was 387/393 (6 VOID mirror gaps, n6), and the 11-09 client verify runs on this Cells. Dep CELLS-TARGET-REQUIRED is Done. Closing as done by the tests-only change; nothing left.")
inl tritcritnet_absorb () = Task ("TRITCRITNET-ABSORB", "TritCritNet absorption: a seed map of the C++ and Rust codebases into the forward items, with a delete gate (every seed preserved, every code seed absorbed or dropped) before both codebases go", Epic, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "tritcritnet,recovery,ml,absorb,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tritcritnet_absorb () = Planning ("TRITCRITNET-ABSORB", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tritcritnet_absorb_1 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-ABSORB", 1u32, "2026-11-07T15:34Z", "main", "User 11-07: by jev I mean the thing hyped on HN these last months (JEPA: LeCun's AMI Labs, 1.03B USD seed in March 2026, V-JEPA 2.1, Causal-JEPA, LLM-JEPA; CONVERGENCE-LAB n3 already reads it this way). Groom so we get the best of everything as move-forward plans, like the old mega sample to regex, and define a metric for when both TritCritNet codebases (C++ and Rust) can be deleted without losing the seeds. RULE, the same as the mega-sample migrations (ZETA-FINAL n2): a migration is done only when the old code is gone, and before that every row of an absorption map is resolved; a new home that merely works is not done. INPUTS: i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet-cpp (tritcritnet.cpp 19,878 lines: about 313 functions and 45 structs; readme_tritcritnet.md, README_TRITCRITNET_VISION.md 16 sections, readme_tritcritnet-eoie.md 43 sections; joint_rust_workspace 9 crates; reports) and i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet (Rust alpha9252: 161 src files plus core, mostly plan, receipt and gate records); the source zips in recovered\\bundles\\from-des073; ARCHIVE-RECOVERY-1107 n6 (reuse assessment). FORWARD HOMES already filed: TRANSFORMER-TRAIN (+GRAD, LOOP, SCALE, TERNARY), TRANSFORMER-QUANT-TERNARY, TIBIA-GRADIENT-POLICY (+BC, PG), CONVERGENCE-LAB (+PREREG, CURRICULA, SSM-BLOCK, JEPA-OBJECTIVE, WORLD-MODEL, RUNS, REPORT), KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT (the Rust half is the drift evidence). Children: TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP, TRITCRITNET-RETIRE.\nTHE SEED METRIC. A seed is one idea, technique, recipe, result or piece of code worth keeping, one row each: every C++ component group (model blocks, optimizer, data split, criticality lane and islands, quantization and straight-through training, event log and checkpoint schema, CLI experiment switches, the audit table rows), every Rust module family, every claim-bearing section of the three readmes (the four-lane typed-evidence encoder, the mixed-radix tokenizer of bytes, base-43 and numeric tokens, the validator role, forcedness as a metric, optionality), every recorded run result, and every curriculum generator. Each row has a source (file and line range), the seed's text written INLINE in the map (so the file can go), a destination item, and one resolution: ABSORBED (a passing test in the new home in CI names the legacy file and line), PLANNED (the destination item's notes hold the seed text verbatim), or DROPPED (a reason). Two hard rules: (1) a CODE seed, whose value is in the code itself (a kernel, the backprop, AdamW, the data split, the island gating, the quantizer, the event schema), may only be ABSORBED or DROPPED, never just PLANNED, because the idea alone would lose it; (2) every number from TritCritNet runs is copied inline with its label (self-graded, no external benchmark). Track two numbers on the epic: preserved = (absorbed + planned + dropped) / seeds, and absorbed = absorbed / code seeds. DELETE GATE: preserved = 100 percent AND absorbed = 100 percent of code seeds (or each remaining one dropped with a reason) AND recovered\\stroma no longer builds against the recovered tritcritnet crate (stroma's own map decides its copy). Until then both codebases stay. DoD of the epic: the gate met, the two folders and the tritcritnet-only bundle zips removed by TRITCRITNET-RETIRE, and the map left in the backlog as the record.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_absorb_2 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-ABSORB", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:35Z", "main", "DoD: every TritCritNet seed row is resolved (absorbed with a passing CI test naming its source file and line; planned with its text verbatim on the destination item; or dropped with a reason), code seeds only absorbed or dropped, preserved = 100% and absorbed-of-code = 100%, and the recovered stroma no longer depends on the recovered tritcritnet crate. Next step: TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_absorb_3 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-ABSORB", 3u32, "2026-11-07T15:36Z", "main", "main 11-07 CORRECTION to n1: jev is Jev (TypeSafe AI's non-generative, schema-bound, calibrated decision model, 2026-09-15), not JEPA; details on CONVERGENCE-LAB's correction note. The metric and the delete gate are unchanged; the seeds land on CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE, now the Jev-style decision objective.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_absorb_4 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-ABSORB", 4u32, "2026-11-07T15:39Z", "main", "main 11-07 CONVERGENCE RULE added to the metric (user 11-07: absorb into something SOTA, not loose samples): ABSORBED now means the seed is an arm in CONVERGENCE-LAB's frontier ablation table (CONV-FRONTIER-PAGE) with a measured delta, or a component an arm needs; a seed that never moves the frontier is DROPPED with its measured delta as the reason. The delete gate is unchanged.")
