inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_1 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 1u32, "2026-11-07T15:35Z", "main", "Child of TRITCRITNET-ABSORB. Build the seed map as typed Spiral rows (no tsv in repos) plus the seed texts inline in this item's notes, one note per family so no note is huge: C++ model and training, C++ data and logging, C++ criticality and quantization, C++ audit table, Rust module families (most expected DROPPED as drift, each with the reason, feeding KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT), the three readmes' claims, run results. For each seed name the destination item and post the seed text on that item too. MILESTONES: inventory and grouping 120 m; texts, destinations and first resolutions 120 m. DoD: every seed has a row, a destination and a resolution or an explicit open status; the two metric numbers computed and written on TRITCRITNET-ABSORB. Next step: list tritcritnet.cpp's structs and function groups by section header, then the Rust src files by name family.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_2 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 2u32, "2026-11-11T01:26Z", "org-f33af161", "D1 inventory slice done (half of the inventory+grouping 120m milestone): structural map at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP\\inventory.md. Next step: turn the inventory into seed rows (C++ by 5 section-families; Rust by model-bearing prefixes neural/ternary/inference/sota/baseline vs governance-drift suffixes critic/gate/guard), name each seeds destination (CONVERGENCE-LAB/CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE for model, KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT for drops), post seed text on the destination. Then the two metrics on TRITCRITNET-ABSORB.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_3 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:30Z", "org-f33af161", "D2 grouping slice done: inventory+grouping milestone now complete (seed-rows.md = 11 code seeds, destinations, first resolutions). Next step (milestone 2, 120m): add readme-claims + run-results seeds (under recovered/ readmes + runs/), post each seed text verbatim on its destination item (one note per family), then compute preserved% + absorbed-of-code% on TRITCRITNET-ABSORB. Drafts: inventory.md + seed-rows.md in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP\\.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_4 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 4u32, "2026-11-11T01:31Z", "org-f33af161", "Milestone-2 started (readme-claim seeds): appended 9 claim seeds from readme_tritcritnet.md (the SOTA vision digest) to seed-rows.md. KEY ALIGNMENT found: TritCritNet core novelty = the \"claim gate\" (is the system allowed to say this? reject/suspend/promote), a NON-generative critic of representations = exactly a Jev-style decision model (jev-is-typesafe-decision-model), so claim-gate + multi-head-epistemic + curriculum seeds land on CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE, the model-arch/ternary/MoE seeds on CONV-FRONTIER-PAGE, ops/memory-ecology on KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT. Still pending: eoie (1603L) + VISION (638L) readme claims not yet extracted (digest covers core); NO runs/ dir found under recovered trees (record as no recovered run-results or locate bench tsvs). Then post seed texts on destinations + compute the two metrics on TRITCRITNET-ABSORB.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_5 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 5u32, "2026-11-11T01:32Z", "org-f33af161", "Run-results seed RESOLVED: no recovered run DATA exists (no runs/results/scores dir under any recovered tree; the ~16 *_scoreboard.rs/*_score.rs are source logic already in the Rust governance families; only .tsv are joint_rust_workspace/reports tooling reports). Run-results seed = DROPPED (no data survived the wipe). So the seed SOURCES are now fully enumerated: C++ 5 section-families + Rust 6 name-families (inventory.md) + 9 readme claims + run-results(dropped) (seed-rows.md). Remaining for milestone 2: eoie+VISION readme claim extraction, post seed texts on destinations, compute metrics on ABSORB.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_6 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 6u32, "2026-11-11T01:33Z", "org-f33af161", "VISION readme seeds added (integration/role theme, distinct from SOTA arch): claim-eoie-policy-critic (rank next actions avoiding overclaiming = Jev shape -> CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE + EOIE as first consumer), claim-depend-on-inference, claim-receipt-learning-loop, claim-forcedness-metric. RECONCILED with the 11-07 convergence rule: the decision objective is a CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE arm; EOIE action-ranking is an APPLICATION/eval of it, not a competing destination; forcedness/optionality = governance -> yardstick. Only eoie readme (1603L) claims left for milestone 2; seed-rows.md now covers 2 of 3 readmes + all code + run-results(dropped).")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_7 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 7u32, "2026-11-11T01:34Z", "org-f33af161", "eoie readme seeds added (superset of VISION; lines 1-611 duplicate it). DISTINCT: 6-product list (TritCritBench->CONV-FRONTIER-PAGE as the ablation table; anti-apophenia->CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE as concrete claim-gate; W43-codec-lib + cpp->rust-migration + watchmen-audit->KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT) + 5-layer dataset recipe (W43/zeta/Lenia/EC-routing/anti-delusion -> CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE curriculum) + roadmap sequencing notes. SEED-SOURCE ENUMERATION NOW COMPLETE: all code families + all 3 readmes + run-results(dropped) in inventory.md + seed-rows.md. Remaining milestone-2 (parent, full-context judgment): post seed texts verbatim on destinations + compute the two metrics on ABSORB.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_8 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 8u32, "2026-11-11T01:46Z", "org-f33af161", "eoie readme detail (760-942) read: CONFIRMS the recorded seeds, no NEW distinct ones. The 5-layer dataset recipe has concrete feature lists (L1 W43 codec: year/date_mjd encode-decode, next/prev_code, cycle43, boundary_year, offset_ablation; L2 zeta: epoch_mod_574/57400, phase_golden/prime, eta_alt, criticality_label; L3 Lenia descriptors; L4 EC routing taxonomy = spiral-runtime/tooling/governance-funding/product-physical/identity-myth-sanity/w43-numeric/jyotish-symbolic/risk-warning/execution-plan/archive-index; L5 anti-delusion training ex: \"this proves destiny\"->risk=high, \"oracle not learner\"->claim_block=true). L5 IS the claim-gate training data (\"Page 0 defending against Page 1\"). These are verbatim seed TEXT for the posting step, not new seeds. READisME-SOURCE ENUMERATION DEFINITIVELY COMPLETE (all 3 readmes + code + run-results). Milestone-1 done + milestone-2 inventory done; only cross-item posting + metric computation remain (parent, full-context).")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_seed_map_9 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP", 9u32, "2026-11-11T01:47Z", "org-f33af161", "Final eoie seed (concrete MVP build-first, line 1085): seed-mvp-alpha001 = one dataset file tritcrit_mix_alpha001.tsv, columns [id,split,source,task_kind,input,target,basis,route,myth_level,epistemic_risk,execution_value,tags], rows from W43/W60/offset-ablation/Lenia/zeta/EC-route/danger-claim-block, trained input->multi-head labels (labels matter more than next-token). This is the concrete ENTRY POINT for the decision-model arm -> CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE (first training set). Canonical role line from the doc: \"a ternary criticality router for symbolic/dynamical archives\". TRITCRITNET SEED SOURCES NOW FULLY EXTRACTED (all code families + all 3 readmes incl. details + run-results dropped). Clean handoff: parent milestone-2 remainder = post the verbatim seed texts (now all located) on CONV-JEPA-OBJECTIVE / CONV-FRONTIER-PAGE / KIT-YARDSTICK-AUDIT, then compute preserved%% + absorbed-of-code%% on TRITCRITNET-ABSORB.")
