inl note_of_tritcritnet_retire_1 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-11-07T15:35Z", "main", "Child of TRITCRITNET-ABSORB. Runs only when the delete gate on the epic is met (preserved 100 percent, code seeds 100 percent absorbed or dropped, stroma off the recovered tritcritnet crate). Then: delete i574n.github\\recovered\\tritcritnet and recovered\\tritcritnet-cpp and the tritcritnet-only bundle zips (bundle_tritcritnet_v20260618-alpha9252, bundle_eoie_v20260530-alpha834) after a dangling check by stem across the repos; the combined bundles stay until the stroma, mechahaze and eoie maps say otherwise; the work-hub originals are the user's. DoD: the folders are gone, nothing references them, and a final note lists what was deleted with sha256 values.")
inl note_of_tritcritnet_retire_2 () = Note ("TRITCRITNET-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-11-07T15:35Z", "main", "Next step: after TRITCRITNET-SEED-MAP reaches the delete gate, check both percentages on the epic, then delete recovered/tritcritnet, recovered/tritcritnet-cpp and the two TritCritNet-only zips (bundle_tritcritnet alpha9252, eoie alpha834), keeping the map in the backlog.")
inl conv_sota_target () = Task ("CONV-SOTA-TARGET", "Convergence lab SOTA target: pin the public fixed-answer benchmark suite, the comparison models of the same size class with their published numbers, the frontier axes and the measuring harness, before any training", TaskKind, P1, D3, 55u32, Active, "", "ml,research,sota,decision-model,jev,team:org,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_conv_sota_target () = Planning ("CONV-SOTA-TARGET", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_conv_sota_target_1 () = Note ("CONV-SOTA-TARGET", 1u32, "2026-11-07T15:39Z", "main", "Child of CONVERGENCE-LAB (n6). Candidate suite: the standard zero-shot fixed-answer tasks small-model papers report (for example ARC Easy and Challenge, HellaSwag, PIQA, BoolQ, WinoGrande), plus classification and routing sets with calibration labels; choose by what the comparison models publish. DoD: suite, splits, metrics (accuracy, expected calibration error, Brier, CPU latency per decision on a named machine, weight bytes) and the comparison set pinned with sources; the comparison models re-measured on our machine for latency; the frontier computed and written as the bar to beat. No claim of SOTA without this pinned set. Next step: list which small open models publish numbers on which tasks.")
inl note_of_conv_sota_target_2 () = Note ("CONV-SOTA-TARGET", 2u32, "2026-11-10T23:52Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 NEXT STEP DONE (which small open models publish numbers on which tasks; web sources read 11-10). (A) 1B-2B class, ONE harness, the best anchor: BitNet b1.58 2B4T tech report (arXiv 2504.12285 v2, Table 1) re-ran LLaMA 3.2 1B, Gemma-3 1B, Qwen2.5 1.5B, SmolLM2 1.7B, MiniCPM 2B and BitNet b1.58 2B (ternary; all instruct) with lm-evaluation-harness: ARC-C 0-shot acc_norm 37.80/38.40/46.67/43.52/44.80/49.91; ARC-E 63.17/63.13/76.01/62.92/72.14/74.79; OpenbookQA 34.80/38.80/40.80/46.00/40.20/41.60; BoolQ 0-shot acc 64.65/74.22/78.04/75.78/80.67/80.18; HellaSwag 60.80/57.69/68.28/71.71/70.81/68.44; PIQA 74.21/71.93/76.12/76.12/76.66/77.09; WinoGrande 0-shot acc 59.51/58.48/62.83/68.98/61.80/71.90; plus CPU TPOT latency 48/41/65/67/124/29 ms on a named machine (i7-13800H) and non-embedding memory 2/1.4/2.6/3.2/4.8/0.4 GB. (B) sub-500M class: SmolLM2 model cards (lighteval, 0-shot, base models): SmolLM2-360M vs Qwen2.5-0.5B vs SmolLM-360M: HellaSwag 54.5/51.2/51.8, ARC avg 53.0/45.4/50.1, PIQA 71.7/69.9/71.6, CommonsenseQA 38.0/31.6/35.3, WinoGrande 52.5/54.1/52.8, OpenBookQA 37.4/37.4/37.2; SmolLM2-135M vs SmolLM-135M: HellaSwag 42.1/41.2, ARC avg 43.9/42.4, PIQA 68.4/68.4, WinoGrande 51.3/51.3, OpenBookQA 34.6/34.0 (no BoolQ, no ARC E/C split, no latency). (C) Not yet read: Pythia (70M-12B, per-checkpoint lm-eval results) and MobileLLM (125M/350M) as further sub-500M anchors. FINDINGS for the DoD: (1) published numbers are NOT comparable across harnesses (SmolLM2-1.7B HellaSwag is 68.7 base/lighteval in its paper vs 71.71 instruct/lm-eval in the BitNet table), so the frontier must be re-measured on our machine with one harness, as the DoD already says; (2) NO source publishes calibration (ECE, Brier), the target model defining property, so the calibration axis of the frontier is ours to measure for every comparison model; (3) the suite every 1-2B anchor shares under one harness is ARC-E, ARC-C, OpenbookQA, BoolQ, HellaSwag, PIQA, WinoGrande (0-shot), which matches the candidate suite in note 1. TYPEFEATURES: none (research). Next step: pin that 7-task suite with lm-eval task names and splits, read Pythia and MobileLLM numbers for the sub-500M anchors, then choose the 3-4 comparison models to re-measure (latency, ECE, Brier) on a named node")
inl note_of_conv_sota_target_3 () = Note ("CONV-SOTA-TARGET", 3u32, "2026-11-10T23:53Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 SUITE PINNED + COMPARISON SET PROPOSED. (C) read: MobileLLM (arXiv 2402.14905, Table 3, zero-shot, baselines run from their Hugging Face weights; harness not named) reports the SAME 7 tasks (+SIQA) for 125M and 350M: MobileLLM-125M ARC-E 43.9 ARC-C 27.1 BoolQ 60.2 PIQA 65.3 HellaSwag 38.9 OBQA 39.5 WinoGrande 53.1; Pythia-160M 40.0/25.3/59.5/62.0/29.9/31.2/50.9; MobileLLM-350M 53.8/33.5/62.4/68.6/49.6/40.0/57.6; Pythia-410M 47.1/30.3/55.3/67.2/40.1/36.2/53.4. SUITE (pinned, the 7 tasks every anchor shares, lm-evaluation-harness task names with their default splits): arc_easy and arc_challenge (test), boolq (validation), piqa (validation), hellaswag (validation), openbookqa (test), winogrande (winogrande_xl validation); all 0-shot; metric acc_norm for ARC, OBQA, HellaSwag, PIQA and acc for BoolQ and WinoGrande (the BitNet table convention), plus our own axes per task: expected calibration error (15 equal-width bins over the top-answer probability), Brier score over the answer set, CPU time per decision on a named node, and weight bytes. COMPARISON SET (proposed, one per size class, all with public weights): Pythia-160M (the common baseline in every small-model table), SmolLM2-360M and Qwen2.5-0.5B (the strongest sub-500M open models), BitNet b1.58 2B4T (ternary, CPU-native, the direct analogue of our target); MobileLLM-125M/350M as published-only reference rows if their weights license blocks a re-run. Next step: write the measuring harness spec (lm-eval invocation per model plus the ECE/Brier pass over its per-answer log-likelihoods), then run it on a node (moon or ganymede, never earth), which is the heavy part this item gates on")
inl note_of_conv_sota_target_4 () = Note ("CONV-SOTA-TARGET", 4u32, "2026-11-10T23:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 HARNESS SPEC (no repo is named for the lab yet, so the spec lives here; code lands once CONVERGENCE-LAB names its home). (1) ACCURACY, third-party tool run on a node, never committed: lm_eval --model hf --model_args pretrained=<hf id>,dtype=float32 --tasks arc_easy,arc_challenge,boolq,piqa,hellaswag,openbookqa,winogrande --num_fewshot 0 --device cpu --batch_size 8 --log_samples --output_path <node stage>/<model>; report acc_norm for arc_easy, arc_challenge, openbookqa, hellaswag, piqa and acc for boolq, winogrande (the BitNet table convention). Pin the lm_eval version and each model revision hash in the result file, since a harness version change moves scores. (2) CALIBRATION, a Spiral program over the --log_samples jsonl (Spiral-first; it needs lib json to decode records with list fields from run-time input, which is exactly JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS, gating now): per doc, the per-choice log-likelihoods give p = softmax over the choices (raw, not length-normalized: calibration is of the model probabilities); ECE = sum over 15 equal-width bins of (bin size / N) * |accuracy - mean top probability|; Brier = mean over docs of sum over choices of (p_k - y_k)^2. (3) LATENCY: wall time of a fixed 200-doc slice per task divided by docs, on ONE named node with pinned threads (taskset to 4 cores, OMP/torch threads 4), median of 3 runs; record the CPU model. Caveat: BitNet b1.58 runs in transformers only as a reference (no ternary kernels), so its accuracy comes from the hf run but its latency must come from bitnet.cpp, recorded separately. (4) SIZE: weight bytes on disk as loaded (safetensors total; GGUF for bitnet.cpp). Next step: CONVERGENCE-LAB names the repo for the lab; then write the Spiral calibration pass there (blocked only on JSON-DECODE-LIST-FIELDS landing) and run (1)+(3) for the 4 comparison models on moon or ganymede")
