inl note_of_cells_livemd_explicit_target_1 () = Note ("CELLS-LIVEMD-EXPLICIT-TARGET", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:08Z", "main", "main 11-07: flagged by x at the end of CELLS-NONTEST-TARGETS-EXPLICIT (1913 of 1914 files ok). The one left is spiral/apps/cells/notebooks/spiral.livemd: its smart cells run through Spiral.Cells.eval!, whose Builders.default() = rust is the LAST implicit default in Cells. DECIDED by main from the user's 11-07 direction ('nah let's keep everything explicit, no env vars prelude etc.'): retire it. DoD: eval!/run with no ///> line fails with the same NoFileTarget/NoTestTarget wording; the smart cell UI shows a target picker (or writes ///> rust into new cells) so the demo keeps working; spiral.livemd's cells name their targets; the census reports 1914/1914; node Cells suite no new reds vs the 386/394 baseline. TypeFeatures: target selection as a required value of the eval!/run request type (no default constructor), not an optional with a fallback. Next step: list every caller of Builders.default() in apps/cells and the Kino smart cell, and decide picker vs written line.")
inl note_of_cells_livemd_explicit_target_2 () = Note ("CELLS-LIVEMD-EXPLICIT-TARGET", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:14Z", "main", "main 11-07 13:2x RE-SCOPE: since this item was filed, the user decided TESTS ONLY (in compiler's session, relayed by x): Cells runs only test cells, code cells and main never run, no file-level line-1 target, no ///> on static blocks, whole-file check dropped. The DoD's census goal is void. What's left is whether the Livebook smart cell's single-cell eval!/run counts as a runnable test cell (then it must name its ///>, no rust default) or as a code cell (then it doesn't run and Builders.default() goes away). x owns that call.")
inl note_of_cells_livemd_explicit_target_3 () = Note ("CELLS-LIVEMD-EXPLICIT-TARGET", 3u32, "2026-11-09T14:55Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 10:5x microblog (x owns the call per n2): DECIDED that a Livebook smart cell's eval!/run is a runnable cell, so it must name its ///> target like a test, with no rust default. BUILT (unstaged, spiral/apps/cells): (1) Spiral.Cells.run: an empty builder list returns {:error, %SpiralError{message: untargeted_cell_message()}}, i.e. 'NoTestTarget: the cell names no target: add a ///> <lang> line to it' (the same tag as Notebook.untargeted_message), before any mount or compile; eval! raises it. run's body moved into run_targeted (no behavior change for targeted cells). (2) run_host_rust labels its chunk with the builder actually run, not Builders.default(). (3) Builders.default/0 is DELETED (0 callers left in apps). (4) smart_cell.ex @default_source starts with '///> rust', so a new smart cell keeps working. (5) notebooks/spiral.livemd: all 4 smart cells carry '///> rust' in both the attrs source and the generated ~S heredoc. (6) README example and one sentence on the rule. (7) Tests: 27 untargeted run/eval! call sites in cells_test, cells_live_test, display_test, notebook_report_test and slots_test gain '///> rust\\n' (the parsed builder equals the old default, blank(:rust, 'rust')); the timeout-validation and empty-code cases are unchanged since they return before the check; new test a_cell_that_names_no_target_is_refused_before_it_compiles (a compile stub that flunks if reached; run returns the error, eval! raises); smart_cell_test asserts the default carries ///> rust. PROOF: the files were pushed into the europa per-test suite mirror (cells.ex hash 5c46ef4ba306 matches the box) before its start, so the one full suite run covers this too. dod: full suite with no new reds vs the 386/394 baseline; the refusal test green. typefeatures: the target list is required data of the run request: an empty list is a refusal, not a default.")
inl note_of_cells_livemd_explicit_target_4 () = Note ("CELLS-LIVEMD-EXPLICIT-TARGET", 4u32, "2026-11-09T20:51Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 16:5x microblog HEAL: the moon sim verify's compile printed 'warning: function blank/2 is unused' (builders.ex:116). The private blank/2 map builder was called only by the Builders.default/0 this item retired, so it was dead code. Removed (unstaged), with the doubled blank line the deletion had left. No caller can exist (defp). Riding: the after-sim r3 client verify recompiles Cells on xqueue1 (re-synced before submit), where the warning must be gone.")
