inl cells_module_scope_tests () = Task ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", "Tests compile in their own module's scope: package inferred from the nearest manifest (no '///- --package .') and the module's own opens (no static prelude)", Story, P0, D5, 80u32, Active, "", "team:compiler,cells,standards,dialect", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_module_scope_tests () = Planning ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_1 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:13Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler (user 11-07: \"can't we get the same functionality without requiring '///- --package .'? why was that invented?\"). WHY IT EXISTS: Cells compiles each cell as a standalone program, so a notebook inside a package has to mount its own directory with '///- --package .' to see sibling modules (apps/cells/README.md:72), and a file's first test also needs a ':# x static =' prelude repeating the file's top-level ':<' opens, because only that prelude reaches the standalone cells (memory notebook-main-default-zig, 11-04 rule). Both are boilerplate produced by compiling cells OUTSIDE their module, and they contradict the user's 10-12 direction (SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES): the .spi itself is the notebook, with compiler-understood test blocks. DESIGN: Cells compiles each test in the scope of its own module: (1) the package is the nearest manifest (package.spiproj / spiral.toml), which the compiler already resolves for every file (file_package_dir), so '///- --package .' becomes unnecessary and is removed; (2) a test sees the module's own top-level opens and definitions, so the static prelude becomes unnecessary and is removed. DoD: both inferred in Cells (x) with no directive and no prelude; every repo's '///- --package .' lines and opens-only static preludes respelled away mechanically in one window (excluding docs/backlog/state/** and archive/**); a census before/after (0 left); all notebook gates green. Explicit '///- --package <other dir>' (mounting a DIFFERENT package) stays valid. typefeatureset plan: none; resolution reuses the compiler's manifest lookup. next step: x confirms how Cells assembles a cell's program today (where the opens come from) and whether the module-scope compile can reuse the compiler's --test-blocks boundaries.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_2 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:40Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: COMPILER-SIDE DESIGN (x takes the Cells side; x confirmed today a test program is `program packages opens defs body`, defs = every kept code cell + static block in order, the opens param never filled).\nTODAY IN THE CORE: blockParsingParse (spiral_compiler.fs ~3671) returns Error [] for any `test`/`:#` block, so tests never reach a module; the build entry is `Map.tryFind \"main\" env.term` over the entry file's final env (~36597).\nPLAN (core, no text patching anywhere):\n1. Parse tests as a top statement `TopTest(name, modes, body)` instead of dropping them; prepass ignores TopTest by default, so module terms, residuals and lib builds are unchanged (gate: lib as a package compiles to the same C with and without tests, as today, plus -Suite all byte-identical).\n2. A build request carries an entry selector: Main (default) | Test name. Host flag `--test <name>` (all modes: --backend, build-file, --batch column, server). For Test name, prepass of the ENTRY FILE ONLY includes that one test as an anonymous entry term at the test's position (sees exactly the definitions above it, like today's 'file up to the block plus body'), and the entry lookup reads that term instead of \"main\". The file's own main is never compiled or run (user 11-07: main is code generation, never a check). Names cannot collide: the entry term has no source name (default_value test vs := default_value in optionm'.spi).\n3. The package is the entry file's nearest manifest exactly as for any build, so sibling modules resolve with no `///- --package .`; the file's own top-level opens apply, so no static prelude is needed for them.\n4. `--test-blocks` already reports bounds/modes/targets per test; Cells calls `--test <name> --backend <lang>` per (test, ///> target) and keeps owning modes (ignore, fails, no_agree, print_code, build_only) and the ///> crates.\nOPEN QUESTION FOR THE USER (not decided between lanes, per [[cells-tests-only-main-is-codegen]]): where `:< testing` comes from once there is no prelude: (a) a top-level `:< testing` in the file (module-wide open), (b) `:< testing` inside each test body, or (c) the compiler opens testing implicitly in test entries. (c) is inheritance, so it is not the default; compiler will ask before x respells.\nSlices: S1 TopTest parse + prepass skip (byte-identical gate), S2 entry selector + --test flag + host plumbing, S3 sample tests under tests/families proving sibling-module access with no --package and no prelude, S4 Cells switch (x).")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_3 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 3u32, "2026-11-07T18:56Z", "compiler", "11-07 15:0x compiler: S2 PROVEN ON THE NODE (job-1794076685837-compiler-mst1, CLI mode). Drafts: kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS\\1-core-test-entry.kitdo (10 replacements: DefaultEnv.test_entry, a path-keyed test_entry_selection, blockParsingParse promotes ONLY the selected non-static test of the selected file into TopInl named \"\\u0001test <name>\" (unreferenceable, so `:# helper` next to `:= helper` never collides), file_default_env applies the selection, FileOpen/loader reparse fresh when a file's selection changes, the build entry reads the test term instead of main) and 2-host-test-flag.kitdo (10: `--test <name>` with --backend; server-tcp `compile<TAB>B<TAB>in<TAB>out<TAB>test<TAB>name`; a selection change forgets the revision so the file reopens; the previously promoted file is reopened unpromoted when another file is selected; no compile cache for test builds).\nFixture (package with model + main, `:< model` at main's top, NO --package ., NO prelude), C backend, gcc, run:\n- --test before_helper: ETY-UnboundVariable helper, \"In the definition: test before_helper\" (a test sees only the definitions above it, as today's Cells semantics)\n- --test helper_sees_sibling: exit 7 (sibling module through the file's own open)\n- --test qualified_member: exit 15 (model::triple)\n- --test helper (named like `:= helper`): exit 31, no collision\n- --test prelude (static): refused \"Cannot find test `prelude` ... (a static test is a prelude, not an entry)\"; --test missing: same refusal\n- no --test: main, exit 99 (main untouched)\nOther files' tests still parse to Error [], so builds without --test are unchanged (byte gate in the next job).\nNEXT STEP: job mst2 (with LITERAL-SUFFIX-WARN): warm server-tcp switching (same file, cross-file revert, recovery after an error), smoke residual byte-identity vs pack61; then ship as pack62 and hand x the protocol for the Cells switch (S4).")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_4 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-11-07T19:25Z", "compiler", "11-07 15:3x compiler: WARM MODE + BYTE GATE PROVEN (node job-1794078321752-compiler-mst2; candidate = live + this item's 2 drafts + LITERAL-SUFFIX-WARN; SpiralCompilerCore CEFBA8F98D854C82).\nserver-tcp, ONE process, 10 requests: main 99 / test helper_sees_sibling 7 / test qualified_member 15 / main 99 (revert in place) / extra.spi test extra_triple 12 (cross-file: main reverted, extra promoted) / main test helper 31 / test before_helper -> the ETY-UnboundVariable error / test helper_sees_sibling 7 (recovery after an error) / extra test 12 / main 99. All correct.\nByte gate: smoke with the candidate, residual hash differs 0 of 159 vs the box's pack61 smoke (builds without --test are unchanged); native DISAGREE 0 (the 10 Swift build-fails are the node's vcvars gap, NODE-SWIFT-VCVARS).\nNEXT STEP: mst3 (linked suite, Rust compile -Suite all base vs candidate, lib type probes, apps/spiral consumer); then install as pack62 and hand x S4.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_5 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-11-07T21:38Z", "compiler", "11-07 17:4x compiler: USER DECISION (asked directly): test-only opens like ':< testing' stay in an opens-only STATIC block with NO ///> target, as in the dib days (the user: 'why can't it be inside a open only or static test block like it were on the dib days?'; the earlier 'weird' was the target on it, not the block). Design S2b: in a --test build, the static blocks ABOVE the selected test in the same file are compiled as module statements (their opens apply to the test), and in every other build they stay skipped, so 'testing' never enters the module's normal scope. Implementation: blockParsingParse returns a new TopStatic(statements) for such a block when the file is the selected one (its body rows re-parsed as top statements), the bundler flattens it. x's respell then drops only targets on static blocks and '///- --package .', keeping the opens-only static blocks. pack62 (gating now) has S2 without S2b; S2b rides pack63 before x's switch.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_6 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-11-07T22:41Z", "compiler", "11-07 18:3x compiler: PACK62 GATED GREEN on the node (job-1794086340458-compiler-p62; core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE; sources = live + 6 programs, re-applied byte-identical 986A4912DA0970C7): smoke residuals 0/159 differ vs pack61 (DISAGREE 0; 10 Swift = node vcvars gap); Rust compile -Suite all vs pack61b 542 rows, only rec_inferred_self differs (base error -> ok, the feature); linked 20/20 (incl. linked_literal_suffix_redundant / _needed); lib type probes 3/3; apps/spiral consumer ok; fixtures: --test 7/31/unbound-before, duplicate-package hint names both package dirs, rec samples C+Rust 17/42. Install on the box is WAITING for kit's TRAIN38 (a mid-train box install would mix compilers); then hashes to main.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_7 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-11-07T23:07Z", "compiler", "11-07 19:0x compiler: S2b PROVEN on the node (job-1794091261706-compiler-p63a, sample candidate core 84D0A12DCA0A0A86 = pack62 programs + 3-static-block-opens + REC step d + formatter rule A): main.spi with ':# prelude static =' / ':< model' and NO top-level open: --test uses_static_open (triple 5) exit 15, --test helper_and_open (helper (triple 1)) exit 10, main (no --test) exit 99; a separate package whose normal module code uses 'triple' under the same static block fails ETY-UnboundVariable triple (the static opens never reach normal module scope). Draft: kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS\\3-static-block-opens.kitdo (TopStatic, parsed only for the selected file in --test builds, flattened by the bundler). NEXT STEP: pack63 = pack62 + this + REC step d (formatter rule A stays out until the user's respell); then x switches Cells.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_8 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 8u32, "2026-11-08T03:08Z", "compiler", "11-07 23:1x compiler: PACK63 GATED GREEN on the node (job-1794105487479-compiler-p63; core 82C0AC66450A66B5 = pack62 sources + 3-static-block-opens + REC 2-unneeded-marker-warning + FORMATTER 3-hand-if-then-rule-over-pack62): S2b 15/10/99 + leak refused; WTY-UnneededRecMarker on the fixture; type probes 3/3; consumer ok; smoke residuals 0/159 vs pack62 (DISAGREE 0); linked 20/20; Rust -Suite all 542 rows equal to pack62 except 5 rows where pack62/pack61b timed out under node load (3 negative samples error identically; portable_convert_parse and portable_math_rounding recompiled on the box: residual-equal). NOT INSTALLED: per main and the user's approved plan, pack63 installs the morning after the user's push, followed at once by one fleet respell window (rule A v2 makes unrespelled files red in formatter checks).")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_9 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 9u32, "2026-11-09T02:44Z", "compiler", "11-08 23:0x compiler: pack63c (= gated pack63 + the user HEAD 3739cfb7 Pascal shl/shr fix + FORMATTER 4) INSTALLED on box/moon/vultr/ganymede 11-08 (box 19:14 copy-install, pair 9011B777/7A2B8AD5; Linux core 5c92e46c byte-identical on vultr and ganymede). Moon -Suite all -Native on pack63c (job-1794182365680, private cache, 22 min): 7586 rows, compile ok 7048, native 6714 ran, 10 build-fail, oracle agree 5949, DISAGREE 0. Vs the 10-31 accepted baseline: compile changes only gadt_growing_index_runtime error->ok (x3); one exit change (dynamic_array_tuple_managed C 0->-1) whose C is byte-identical under pack62 and pack63c (B075ECF24EA2C45C), so it predates pack63c. europa lib --check 82/82 reformatted lib files ok. Next step: microblog switches Cells to the compile ... test <name> protocol (told 23:0x); rig adds NoPackageDot; then the DoD closes on a Cells notebook run without '///- --package .'.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_10 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 10u32, "2026-11-09T02:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:5x rig, handoff from compiler: pack63c with --test <name> is installed everywhere; microblog is switching Cells to the per-test protocol. AFTER that lands, rig adds a NoPackageDot lint that flags a ///- --package . header line (NOT NoStaticPrelude). Known instances include rig_delegate/model.spi and rig_job_remote_gate/gate.spi (both start with ///- --package .); the lint lands with a census count and the files migrate in the same change, so the baseline only shrinks. Next step: wait for microblog's Cells landing, then the lint rule plus fixtures.")
inl note_of_cells_module_scope_tests_11 () = Note ("CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS", 11u32, "2026-11-09T09:58Z", "compiler", "11-09 10:0x compiler: COMPILER SIDE PROVEN for NoPackageDot, on ganymede with the installed pack67 and the compilers own --test <name>: apps/cells/spi/mount_text.spi in the TARGET shape (opens-only `:# mount_text static = / :< testing` block, NO `///- --package .` line) compiles all 3 of its tests for Gleam (exit 0), with sibling-module names such as text::find_from resolving through the files own package. The fully header-less HEAD version fails only on `_assert_eq` unbound (no :< testing opens), which is the users standard (static block = the place for test-only opens), not a module-scope gap. So microblogs flag-ON failure on that file was the missing opens block. Remaining for Done: microblogs Cells per-test protocol landing (Cells passes --test with the files package), then rigs NoPackageDot lint + migration, then one Cells notebook run without the ///- line.")
inl main_checks_to_tests () = Task ("MAIN-CHECKS-TO-TESTS", "Convert whole-file 'checks' (mains that assert) into explicit test cells; main stays code generation only", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,cells,standards", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_main_checks_to_tests () = Planning ("MAIN-CHECKS-TO-TESTS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl project_standard_heal () = Task ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", "Heal the drift from the project standard: encode it as enforced kit-standards checks (module-scope tests, per-test ///> + crates, no --package . / prelude / header, main = codegen)", Story, P0, D4, 50u32, Active, "", "team:compiler,standards,cells,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_project_standard_heal () = Planning ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_1 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:14Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler (user 11-07: \"each project is following a standard, we did studies about this before, gotta learn how we drifted again to heal\"). THE STANDARD (from the user's 10-12 design session, SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES, and today's decisions): a package is a manifest (spiral.toml or package.spiproj; dialect implicit) plus modules; each module carries its own inline test cells, compiled in the module's scope; every test names its own language and crates on its ///> line; main is only the code-generation entry (one per program); libraries are auto-export units with no main; no prose files, expectations inline. HOW WE DRIFTED, this week's evidence: Cells compiled cells outside their module, so lanes added '///- --package .', then opens-only static preludes, then prelude targets, an env default, a hardcoded zig fallback, a per-file target header and manifest-level crates, each a local fix by one lane that nobody checked against the standard, because the standard was a design note and memory, never a CHECK. Two lanes respelling the same files with two models (11-07) is the same failure. HEAL: (1) encode the standard as an enforced check, a 'kit standards' notebook rule set run in the train and CI: no '///- --package .', no opens-only static prelude, every test has its own ///> with its crates, no target header, no main that asserts; (2) finish CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS and MAIN-CHECKS-TO-TESTS so the rules hold without boilerplate; (3) any NEW notebook mechanism gets a user question before it lands (memory cells-tests-only-main-is-codegen). DoD: the rule set exists in kit standards, runs in kit's train and spiral CI, and reports 0 findings fleet-wide after the respells. typefeatureset plan: the standard's rules as typed findings (code, file, line), not grep text. next step: list kit standards' current notebook rules and diff them against the standard above.")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_2 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-07T18:41Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: STEP 1 DONE (diff kit standards vs the standard). kit/src/kit_standards/rules.spi knows NoCommentLines, LfOnly, TestTargets, HostFree, LibReferenced, LineWidth, IntegerOnly. The TestTargets rule CONTRADICTS today's standard in two places:\n(a) it accepts a target \"in the file header\" (scan.header_targets): the user ruled per-test only, no file header;\n(b) it REQUIRES '///- --package .' and a ':# <module> static =' prelude (\"a test block in a module without a notebook header never runs; start the file with ///- --package ...\"): the exact boilerplate the user asked to remove. The rule set itself enforced the drift.\nMISSING rules: NoTargetOnStatic (a ///> line above a static block), NoTargetHeader (///> before the first block of a file), CratesOnTest (crates only on a test's ///> line, never in spiral.toml/package.spiproj), MainIsCodegen (no test-like check lines in a test-free file's main; the census showed real checks live in exported Rust #[test]s, so this rule may be informational).\nSEQUENCING: (a) can change now (no header fallback; x already stripped the headers); (b) and NoPackageDot/NoStaticPrelude wait for CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS (the --test entry) plus the Cells switch, otherwise tests stop running. Kit owns kit_standards (team:kit files); sent the list to kit.\nNEXT STEP: kit edits TestTargets (drop the header fallback) and adds NoTargetOnStatic + NoTargetHeader + CratesOnTest as typed rules; then, after the Cells switch, flips (b) into NoPackageDot + NoStaticPrelude.")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_3 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-11-07T23:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 19:5x kit -> compiler: the kit standards side of step 2 is BUILT and node-proven (rules.spi notebook 11/11 on probes n and o, kit_standards trimmed under the gate), riding TRAIN39 (waits on install). TestTargets now flags, in order: a retired ///> _ line; a test without a notebook header; crates (-d) on a ///- package line; a test block without its own ///> line directly above it (per-test only); a stray target, with one message for a ///> above a static block (NoTargetOnStatic) and one for a ///> not directly above a test (covers the file-level header, NoTargetHeader). Package level: crates in package.spiproj or spiral.toml are flagged (CratesOnTest), and a receipt-like package with no runnable test is flagged (the drift guard). Per (b) in note 2, the package-dot and static-prelude requirement is KEPT until CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS and the x Cells switch land; MainIsCodegen is not built. NEXT STEP for kit: drop the notebook-header requirement when compiler says the --test entry is live in Cells.")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_4 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 4u32, "2026-11-08T04:03Z", "compiler", "11-08 00:0x compiler: CORRECTION from the user's 11-07 17:4x decision (asked directly): an opens-only STATIC block with NO ///> target stays the standard place for test-only opens (':# m static =' / ':< testing'), honored by the compiler in --test builds (pack63). So the planned 'NoStaticPrelude' rule is WRONG and must not be added. The standard's rules become: NoPackageDot (no '///- --package .', after pack63 + x's Cells switch), NoTargetOnStatic (a ///> above a static block), NoTargetHeader, TestTargets per test (no header fallback, kit landed it), CratesOnTest (no crates: / crates = in manifests, x removed the feature), and the formatter's hand if/then rule enforced by format --check after the morning respell. Told kit.")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_5 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 5u32, "2026-11-09T06:21Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:4x compiler: STATUS against the standard's rules. DONE on the compiler side: (1) --test <name> compiles a test inside its own module and package with the file's top-level opens and an opens-only static block honored (pack63, installed fleet-wide 11-08 as pack63c, now pack64); (2) the formatter's hand if/then rule: the fleet is CANONICAL (two passes 11-08, 963 files total, unstaged), and pack64 makes format one-pass stable, so ormat --check can now gate (pack64 format over all 1707 fleet files is a no-op). REMAINING, owned elsewhere: microblog's CELLS-PORT-PER-TEST-PROTOCOL (Cells compiles tests via --test; then '///- --package .' is unnecessary), then rig's NoPackageDot lint (told 11-08), and turning format --check on in the style hook/CI (kit). NoStaticPrelude must NOT be added (user 11-07). Next step for compiler: none until the Cells port lands; then verify CI green on async.spi (the live symptom of the missing module scope).")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_6 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 6u32, "2026-11-09T08:49Z", "compiler", "11-09 08:5x compiler: (a) microblog proved the async.spi acceptance: SPIRAL_CELLS_PER_TEST=1 makes its 3 Rust tests pass 3/3 (0/3 with the flag off). (b) apps/cells/spi/mount_text.spi (committed 11-08 without the ///- --package . header and opens-only static block) was red 3/3 in BOTH arms; fixed by adding the standard header (3/3 gleam on ganymede, unstaged). The flag-ON failure on a header-less file is a gap in the per-test port for NoPackageDot; told microblog, with the old header-less file as a repro.")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_7 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:04Z", "compiler", "11-09 09:0x compiler: header sweep of app packages (test files with ///> but no ///- line that call sibling modules) found 3 more besides mount_text, all red since their 11-08 commit: apps/cells/spi run_result (had a static block, lacked ///- --package .), source_blocks and verdicts (lacked both). Control run before the fix: 10/10 fail. After adding the standard header: verdicts 5/5. Two had a SECOND, independent defect exposed once they compiled: source_blocks test_headers_are_split_out... expected b5/l5 for the 6-byte text `:= a =` (the field encoder writes the byte length; the literal was evidently respelled after the counts were written) -> fixed to b6/l6/b6; run_result tagged ///> zig but reaches the Gleam-only Cells text module (raw @external(erlang..) globals leaked into main.zig) -> retargeted to ///> gleam (its transitive FFI reach). Result: 13 previously-red Cells tests now 13/13 green on ganymede (mount_text 3, verdicts 5, source_blocks 2, run_result 3), all unstaged. apps/compiler/spi/tokens.spi is header-less but uses no sibling module, so left alone.")
inl note_of_project_standard_heal_8 () = Note ("PROJECT-STANDARD-HEAL", 8u32, "2026-11-09T09:58Z", "compiler", "CORRECTION to note 6 (11-09 10:0x compiler): the flag-ON failure on the header-less mount_text was NOT a per-test port gap. That file lacked BOTH the ///- line and the :< testing static block; under the compilers --test, module scope resolves (text::find_from ok) and only _assert_eq is unbound. In the NoPackageDot target shape (static opens block kept, ///- removed) all 3 tests compile (CELLS-MODULE-SCOPE-TESTS note 11).")
inl node_candidate_pipeline () = Task ("NODE-CANDIDATE-PIPELINE", "Build and gate compiler candidates on the node (byte comparison, review suites), install on the box from the returned, hash-verified candidate", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION", "team:compiler,infra,node,performance", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_node_candidate_pipeline () = Planning ("NODE-CANDIDATE-PIPELINE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl generic_node_delegation () = Task ("GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION", "Any kind of work delegates to nodes with minimal friction: one command, automatic live-tree sync (incl. unstaged), automatic pre/post checks, placement by load, results returned", Epic, P0, D6, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR,DELEGATE-1-VERB,DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT,DELEGATE-3-DEPS-LINK,DELEGATE-4-CORE-PIN,DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT,DELEGATE-6-RESULTS,DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP,DELEGATE-8-COMPLETION,DELEGATE-9-MEMO,DELEGATE-10-NEVER-LIST,DELEGATE-11-NODE-IDENTITY,DELEGATE-12-QUIET-SLOT,DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH,DELEGATE-14-WARM-ORG-MIRROR,DELEGATE-15-LANE-MIGRATIONS,DELEGATE-16-PROOF", "team:compiler,team:rig,team:org,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_generic_node_delegation () = Planning ("GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION", Minutes 2400u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_generic_node_delegation_1 () = Note ("GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:22Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler, filed from the USER's direction: \"coordinate with resilience and kit so we don't have these gaps anymore, any kind of work should be able to be delegated to nodes with minimal friction, automatic syncs/checks etc so we don't drift with stale stuff like kit's been dealing with jobs processes for weeks. ask each lane how such generic delegation could help their pipelines then groom.\" TRIGGER: on 11-06/07 all 6 compiler packs built and gated on the box at 100% CPU while the node (the laptop) idled at 1-3% with 12 GB free; resilience's WASTE alarm fired nearly every peak hour. Cause: box-only pipeline scripts, not capacity. BASE TO EXTEND (no parallel system): kit's KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR (P0, 15%: a supervised coordinator per machine, typed slot/lease/job typestate, the Rust job runner, SSH + Tailscale fallback, placement by free slot) and its REMOTE-EXEC-S* steps (S4 Active: retire remote.ps1 node job callers; S5: refuse on a source-tree mismatch; S11/S12: two heavy jobs one per machine, node >= 90% CPU while the queue is not empty), plus WARM-MIRROR-CACHES (shared node build cache and Cells memo store). ADDED by this epic: (1) ANY job type, compiler candidates and gates, notebook batches, trains, censuses, benchmarks, through one command; (2) automatic sync of the live tree INCLUDING unstaged files and kitdo programs, so no job runs on a stale tree; (3) automatic pre-checks by resilience's rules (route probe >= 40 s, disk floor 15 GB, PATH/toolchain parity, core and tree hash match) and post-checks (orphan cleanup, results and artifacts returned to the box, hashes verified); (4) placement by measured load, the box last; (5) a never-delegate list (the box's install pin, kit's live state files, the RustDesk node). DoD: every lane's top box-bound pipeline runs through it once with the box idle; the WASTE alarm is quiet for a full working day; each lane's answers (asked 11-07 13:3x) are groomed into child steps of 240 min or less. typefeatureset plan: a job as a typed record {kind; inputs (tree hash, program hashes); placement; checks; artifacts}, never an ad-hoc command line. next step: groom the lanes' answers (due about 14:15) with kit and resilience into child steps.")
inl note_of_generic_node_delegation_2 () = Note ("GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:23Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: LANE ANSWERS, part 1 (tibia, fiscal, x-dumps).\nTIBIA. On the box: build.ps1 -ChecksOnly (formatter + cell budget, about 2.5 min each, about 10x in 2 days), --check scratch checks, format diffs, arena Lua probe builds. Friction: every node job hand-built (zip, scp, unpack OUTSIDE the mirror since a sync prunes scratch inside it, junction deps/spiral); np1s lib stale and its core ahead of the box (formatter), so a layout gate was VOID; load gave lock_timeout and 300 s cell VOIDs with no quiet window for benches; results read back by ssh -EncodedCommand; started_ms counts queue time; a queued job reads its inputs at START (useful, undocumented); laptop-ts timed out, so a second route was needed. Wants: 'kit job run --tree <repo> --core <pin> -- <cmd>' that snapshots the working tree incl. unstaged (hashed) into scratch outside any mirror, links the SAME lib + core as the box, refuses on a mismatch, and returns stdout + tests.tsv + per-file verdicts (pass/red/VOID with cause) keyed by snapshot hash; plus a local --check before queueing, a per-job quiet gate for benches, and route failover. Never: live game/GUI windows, stored secrets (Cloud key, GPU rental), commits/pushes/staging, and reading the verdict (the agent reads the full log, never a summary line).\nFISCAL. On the box or waiting: lib_land_window close (consumer compile + document_test + type_probe, 10-15 min under load, one wait of 30 min on another lane's window); the full regen of 83 units + the drift check (only CI runs it); harness compiles (rustc 160 s); format checks. The node handled Cells gates and generator identity arms, but SERIALLY: one Cells run per node meant a hand-reordered 6-job chain. Friction: a hand stage script per job (zip core/lib/src, scp with retries, hash verify, junctions, disk gate, junctions-first cleanup); stale t1101 lib (a VOID run on 'Unbound module xml_codec'); stale Cells mount key; the core changed 3 times mid-chain; results via ssh into stdout.log, truncated by own filters twice. Wants: 'kit node run --tree <paths> -- <cmd>' snapshotting named box paths (content-hashed), syncing incrementally, pinning the current core, running on a fresh stage, returning stdout + exit + tests.tsv into a local job dir, deleting the stage, memoizing results by input hash, and a priority queue instead of after-chains; lib_land_window's close checks from the same snapshot on the node, with only the hash-checked apply on the box. Never: the write into the live lib/repo (land/apply), git commit/stage, anything behind the user's identity (email-form downloads, credentials), the keep-or-undo decision (the node reports, the box applies).\nX-DUMPS. Placeable: xarchive harvest/re-harvest stages (cdx, profile, snaps, live, context, media) and timeline/merge/world builds, pinned to europa today, movable to any Linux node with network + account inputs; the sim serve (:8787) is movable but must stay co-located with the world + media it serves. Friction: moving the 146 MB world + media is slow and truncation-prone (europa transfers > 2.5 GB silently truncate); re-harvests must MERGE, then the rebuilt world must be re-transferred, so drift between copies is the main staleness risk; media.tsv / world path coupling; node identity is ambiguous (ssh rustdesk and ssh europa both report hostname 'europa'). Wants: stages shipped with inputs auto-synced and outputs pulled back content-hash-checked, a versioned world with atomic swap, a 'current core + current world hash' precheck before any run or serve, and stable per-node identity (not hostname). Never: ANY compute on pluto (relay-only for the user's RustDesk; zero placement, never degrade, never restart sshd); swapping the serve's world/media root without a hash check; the user's X-account data and API credentials leaving private trees.")
inl note_of_generic_node_delegation_3 () = Note ("GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION", 3u32, "2026-11-07T17:33Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: LANE ANSWERS, part 2 (kit, resilience, main, x).\nKIT. Heavy work already on the node: regen sizes, notebooks, CLI tests vs the candidate, trains' node half. Box-only: the train's box half (release + install into the box's kit) and the census. Friction: a full-tree resync per probe (minutes on a busy box); GNU tar under Bash breaks sync; regen stage dirs fill the node disk (hand cleanup); Cargo.lock --locked fails on new crates; results only via stdout tail + scp; a stale compiler pin on a same-name relaunch; the node lacked the .NET 11 SDK (FIXED 11-07: SDK 11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 installed, matches the box). Wants: 'kit job start --on auto --sync spiral,kit <label> <cmd>' with content-hash sync of the live tree, refusal when the node's core or tree hash differs (S5), load placement (S7 done), declared outputs copied back with hashes, stage auto-cleaned. Never: writes to live backlog state (kit-locked), installs into the box's bin, anything editing the box's working tree. Today's path: i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1 -MirrorName -Label -Repos -Command ({mirror}/{stage} tokens), then -Remove.\nRESILIENCE. Pre-checks: route (Invoke-NodeRoute, >=40 s probe, first answering), disk floor (target >=15 GB free), toolchain/PATH parity (rustc/zig/SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR visible on the NON-INTERACTIVE ssh PATH), tree/core freshness (pin hash = box), memory headroom. Post: capture the result, verify scp landing by HASH, prune the stage, reap leftover ssh/pwsh children. Existing code: scripts/node-env.ps1 (Invoke-NodeRoute, Invoke-Bounded with child-tree kill, rc124 = timeout, Sync-RoboTree, ConvertTo-EncodedCommand), node-utilization-monitor.ps1 placer predicates (15 GB $diskLow, europa /tmp 85%, box>=85%/node<=35%/lap free>=3000 MB, orphan reaper). MISSING: the toolchain/PATH parity probe and a tree-freshness HASH check (robocopy mirrors bytes, never verifies a pin). Budgets: lap C: 15 GB floor, mirror lanes have priority on that disk; europa 3.4 GB HARD cap, every heavy job in a systemd scope (silent 137/143 = OOM), /tmp is a 1.7 GB RAM tmpfs; fiscal peaks 3-5 GB so lap only when free > 6 GB. Never: the install/pin step, the critical/profile mirror writers, builds needing box-only lib modules absent from the node base lib, sshd restart / stateful swaps on a remote-only node, WSL bash.\nMAIN. Node-takeable: lib_land_window's gates (consumer apps/spiral, document_test, type_probe, respell_drift; only the final swap needs the live tree; today the window held a 55-min tree-write slot just to gate), downstream notebook gates, cross-repo --check/consumer proofs. Friction: non-spiral mirrors link deps\\spiral to the node's stale BASE clone (ETY-UnboundModule twice: 11-04 and 11-07; fixed in node-proof.ps1, but 'remote.ps1 sync' alone still defaults to base); the node compiler lags silently (node 11-06 vs box 11-07) unless -RequireCore; gitignored deps/ not mirrored (hand junctions); kit path differs on the node; results need a hand-rolled remote run (stdout/stderr split, 5 KB JSON lines); node disk 11.9 GB free, mirrors removed by hand; no completion push (background ssh job wait). Wants: 'kit delegate <repos> [--keep] -- <cmd>' snapshotting repos incl. unstaged + box lib, pinning (and shipping) the box's installed core, linking every repo's deps to that snapshot, refusing below a disk floor, returning a typed summary (exit, per-file JSON line, first N error lines), auto-removing the mirror, landing produced files via a hash-guarded manifest (node-proof -Land exists). Never: writes to the live box tree, backlog writes, git, anything on RustDesk Sao Paulo, credentials, decisions/approvals, box deletions.\nX. Box-bound: cell_budget checks, org censuses (mix run over ~5k files), dry-run/apply respells, every document_test round trip, because they need ALL repos + the box's unstaged state while mirrors carry spiral+x only. Friction: a 156-path ssh command line silently returned nothing; mirrors missing dice/alphabet/spl2spi + lib package.spiproj made 6 Cells tests VOID every run; a mid-run core swap made one verify mixed-core; a reused mirror kept generated .etf files that tripped the line gate; hand hash-diff + scp of changed Cells files every iteration; results only via job tail with a line cap. Wants: 'kit delegate <repos...> -- <cmd>' syncing unstaged trees by digest into a fresh or clean mirror, pinning and printing the core, shipping stdout.log + a named outputs dir back, auto-cleaning; plus an all-org-repos mirror kept warm for censuses and round trips. Never: writes to box live state (backlog state, :8787 serve, installed binaries/trains), tree edits beyond read-only proofs, credentialed X posts.\nCONVERGENCE (all 7 lanes): one verb; snapshot incl. unstaged by content hash into a FRESH stage; deps linked to the same snapshot; the box's core pinned + refused/shipped on mismatch and locked for the job; pre-checks (route, disk, toolchain PATH, memory caps); typed results + full log + declared outputs back by hash; stage auto-clean; completion push; memo by input hash; box keeps every apply/install/git/state write. Groomed into DELEGATE-* children (next note).")
inl delegate_1_verb () = Task ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", "kit delegate <repos...> [--on auto|<machine>] [--keep] -- <cmd>: one verb over kit job start --on, printing job id, machine, core hash and snapshot hash", TaskKind, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "REMOTE-EXEC-S5", "team:rig,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_1_verb () = Planning ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_1_verb_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: one call runs an arbitrary command on a placed node with no hand staging; {stage}/{repo} tokens resolve on the node; works from PowerShell AND Bash (no GNU tar dependency: kit and x hit it). node-proof.ps1 becomes a thin wrapper or is retired. Asked by all 7 lanes (epic notes 2-3).")
inl note_of_delegate_1_verb_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: wrap what exists (kit job start --on, box-side job wait/tail by remote id, proven 11-06) behind kit delegate: parse <repos> [--on auto|machine] [--keep] -- <cmd>, call the snapshot (2) and start the job; the first cut runs the command through the same staged run.ps1 shape node-proof.ps1 uses, so lanes can switch with one line. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: delegate_request record, placement union (Auto, OnMachine), outcome union shared with kit_job_dispatch.")
inl note_of_delegate_1_verb_3 () = Note ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", 3u32, "2026-11-07T17:53Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit, from resilience (DELEGATE-11 done, DELEGATE-5 in progress): the verb composes resilience predicates from scripts/node-env.ps1 (dot-sourced). FIRST refusal before any upload: Test-NodeIdentity -Route <r> -ForCompute -> ok, refusal (no-identity, identity-mismatch, relay-only), identity; node_id comes from ~/.node-identity (key=value: node_id, name, role, os, relay_only, site, created) because hostnames collide (rustdesk-sao reports europa). Then Test-NodePreflight (coming): ordered verdicts over route failover, disk floor 15 GB, toolchain PATH parity (rustc, cargo, zig, dotnet SDK, SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR), memory headroom with a Win32 Job Object commit cap, europa systemd scope cap; short-circuits on the first refusal. kit keeps the verb, snapshot, pin, results, memo and never-list.")
inl note_of_delegate_1_verb_4 () = Note ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", 4u32, "2026-11-09T00:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 21:0x rig, adopting the studied techniques (memory studied-engineering-techniques, relayed by fiscal at the user's ask). EXIT-CODE TAXONOMY for the verb and every rig job verdict: 0 ok, 2 policy failed, 3 incomplete, 64 bad input, 70 runner error, 74 output error, 124 timeout, 130 cancelled. rig_delegate model today: verdict Pass | Fail of i32 | Void of void_cause (TimedOut, OutOfMemory, NoRoute, NotRun), notebook 3/3 green on moon 11-08 (rig-probe1108j). Map: Refused request -> 64, Void TimedOut -> 124, NotRun -> 3, NoRoute -> 70, Fail n -> 2 when a gate said no, runner crash -> 70, fetch-back write failure -> 74. DoD: verdict_code is a total match over the union with a test row per code. TypeFeatures: exit_class union with one case per taxonomy code. Next step: add exit_class and verdict_code to rig_delegate model.spi with the table test.")
inl note_of_delegate_1_verb_5 () = Note ("DELEGATE-1-VERB", 5u32, "2026-11-09T01:19Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 21:2x rig PROOF: exit_class (8 cases) with code_of_class, class_of_cause and class_of_verdict landed in rig_delegate model.spi (live tree, unstaged); moon notebook 4/4 green, job-1794186862359-rig-probe1108l. Mapping as in the note before: Refused 64, TimedOut 124, NotRun 3, other void 70, Fail 2, Pass 0; Output 74 and Cancelled 130 exist for the fetch-back and stop paths still to wire. Next step: the verb execution path (sync, staged script, job start --on, full-log fetch-back) returning these codes; it rides TRAIN42.")
inl delegate_2_snapshot () = Task ("DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", "delegate snapshot: named repos incl. unstaged + the box lib, content-hashed, incremental sync into a FRESH stage outside any mirror", TaskKind, P0, D5, 0u32, Planned, "DELEGATE-1-VERB", "team:rig,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_2_snapshot () = Planning ("DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_2_snapshot_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: second run of an unchanged tree sends ~0 bytes (kit: full resync per probe took minutes); a stage is never reused (x: stale .etf from a reused mirror tripped a line gate; tibia: sync prunes scratch inside mirrors); paths list goes by file, not argv (x: a 156-path ssh command line silently returned nothing). Reuse or fold KIT-REMOTE-SYNC; snapshot hash = hash of the sorted (path, content-hash) list.")
inl note_of_delegate_2_snapshot_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: absorb KIT-REMOTE-SYNC (same intent: native non-git transport on the deterministic tar writer in kit_archive_tar_runtime): hash the working tree by content (unstaged included, box lib included), send only changed files as a path list by file (never argv), unpack into a FRESH stage per job; reuse the manifest walk remote.ps1 sync does today, in kit. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: snapshot record (repo, head, dirty hash, file count), file delta union (Added, Changed, Removed), snapshot hash nominal used as the memo key part.")
inl note_of_delegate_2_snapshot_3 () = Note ("DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T00:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 21:0x rig, adopting the studied techniques (memory studied-engineering-techniques, relayed by fiscal at the user's ask). HASH RECHECK: record the source tree digest and the binary sha256 at snapshot, copy inputs into the evidence dir, and RECHECK both right before the live phase, because peers change the tree mid-run (seen tonight: compiler reformatted 541 files while rig had a mirror syncing). A mismatch ends the run as incomplete (exit 3), never as a pass. DoD: a fixture that edits a file between snapshot and live phase gets exit 3. Next step: reuse remote.ps1 digest semantics (REMOTE-SYNC-OK digest) as the recorded value.")
inl delegate_3_deps_link () = Task ("DELEGATE-3-DEPS-LINK", "delegate links every repo's deps (deps\\spiral and declared sibling repos) to the SAME snapshot, never the node's base clone; refuse when a declared dep repo is missing", TaskKind, P0, D3, 0u32, Planned, "DELEGATE-2-SNAPSHOT", "team:rig,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_3_deps_link () = Planning ("DELEGATE-3-DEPS-LINK", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_3_deps_link_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-3-DEPS-LINK", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: a non-spiral repo test that opens a lib module added today passes on the node (main: ETY-UnboundModule on 11-04 and 11-07; fiscal: Unbound module xml_codec VOID); x's 6 Cells VOIDs from missing dice/alphabet/spl2spi + lib package.spiproj become a refusal naming the missing repo before any run. remote.ps1 sync stops defaulting to the base clone.")
inl note_of_delegate_3_deps_link_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-3-DEPS-LINK", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: read each named repo manifest for declared sibling repos (deps\\spiral and package paths) and include them in the same snapshot; refuse with the missing repo name when a declared repo is not in the snapshot. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: repo_dependency record, verdict union (Linked, MissingRepo).")
inl delegate_4_core_pin () = Task ("DELEGATE-4-CORE-PIN", "delegate pins the box's installed compiler core: ships it when the node differs, refuses or waits on a mid-job core swap, prints the core in the result", TaskKind, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "DELEGATE-1-VERB", "team:rig,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_4_core_pin () = Planning ("DELEGATE-4-CORE-PIN", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_4_core_pin_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-4-CORE-PIN", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: a job never runs on a compiler other than the box's installed one (main: node 11-06 vs box 11-07 silently; fiscal: core changed 3x mid-chain; x: a mid-run swap made a verify mixed-core; kit: stale pin on same-name relaunch, KIT-TRAIN-STALE-PIN). The core hash is part of the result key. Shipping reuses pack-chain -SkipInstall; the box install itself stays on the box.")
inl note_of_delegate_4_core_pin_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-4-CORE-PIN", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: at delegate start read the box installed core hash (the same files launch-train parity hashes), compare with the node, ship via pack-chain -SkipInstall when it differs, and pin a copy in the job stage so a mid-job swap cannot change it (the KIT-TRAIN-STALE-PIN lesson); put the core hash in the result key. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: core_hash nominal, pin verdict union (Matched, Shipped, Refused).")
inl delegate_5_preflight () = Task ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", "delegate pre-checks: route failover, disk floor, toolchain PATH parity on the non-interactive ssh PATH, memory headroom and europa systemd-scope cap", TaskKind, P0, D4, 70u32, Blocked, "DELEGATE-1-VERB", "team:org,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_5_preflight () = Planning ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: each check is a typed refusal before any upload. Reuse node-env.ps1 (Invoke-NodeRoute >=40 s, Invoke-Bounded) and the monitor's placer predicates (15 GB $diskLow, europa /tmp 85%, lap free >= 3000 MB, fiscal-class jobs only when free > 6 GB). NEW: the toolchain probe (rustc, cargo, zig, dotnet SDK version = box's, SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR) run the way jobs run (kit and compiler: the node had the .NET 11 runtime but no SDK; resilience: rustc installed but not on the ssh PATH). Mirror lanes keep priority on lap C:.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:48Z", "resilience", "MEMORY-CAP preflight check (motivated by the 11-07 x-roundtrip BEAM blow-up: 35.6GB committed on a 16GB node, pagefile-thrashed, starved every lane). Before upload the placer checks free memory headroom (already in the monitor), AND the launch wrapper must run the remote job under a COMMITTED-MEMORY CAP = the Windows analog of europa systemd-scope ([[europa-heavy-jobs-cap-memory]]): a Win32 Job Object with JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_JOB_MEMORY so a blow-up gets OOM-killed as ONE process cleanly, never thrashes the node. Typed refusal: reject placement if (free_mb - job_budget_mb) < floor. Linux side keeps the systemd-scope. Contract to post to kit for the verb to call.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_3 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 3u32, "2026-11-07T17:49Z", "resilience", "NEXT STEP: implement the 5 preflight predicates in node-env.ps1 as typed refusals returning @{ok;refusal}, each wrapped in Invoke-Bounded: (1) route failover (Invoke-NodeRoute >=40s, first-answering), (2) disk floor (target free >=15GB, lap mirror lanes keep priority), (3) toolchain PATH parity (rustc/cargo/zig/dotnet SDK on the NON-interactive ssh PATH + SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = box version), (4) memory headroom + Job-Object committed cap, (5) europa systemd-scope cap. Compose into Test-NodePreflight that short-circuits on first refusal. DoD: no job uploads unless all 5 pass; each failure is a named typed refusal, not a silent skip. TYPEFEATURES: refusal as @{ok;refusal;check}; preflight result as an ordered list of per-check verdicts.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_4 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 4u32, "2026-11-07T17:55Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom markers (lint). NEXT STEP: resilience writes the predicate contracts in node-env.ps1 (route, disk floor, toolchain PATH parity run through the non-interactive ssh shell, memory headroom, europa scope) as inputs -> typed refusal/ok, then posts them to kit for DELEGATE-1-VERB to call.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_5 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 5u32, "2026-11-07T18:01Z", "resilience", "IMPLEMENTED + LIVE-VERIFIED (11-07 14:0x). node-env.ps1 gains Invoke-PreflightSsh/Invoke-NodeProbeWin + 5 typed-refusal predicates (Test-RouteFailover, Test-DiskFloor, Test-ToolchainParity, Test-MemoryHeadroom, Test-VultrScopeCap) composed by Test-NodePreflight -Route <r> [-ForCompute], short-circuiting on first refusal, returning @{ok;refusal;verdicts}. Verified live: laptop -ForCompute PASSES all 5 (identity/route/disk/toolchain/memory); rustdesk REFUSES relay-only at identity. CORRECTION: toolchain parity PASSES on laptop via pwsh (Get-Command rustc succeeds from the non-interactive ssh pwsh - .cargo\\bin IS on the pwsh PATH); the earlier empty rustc was a cmd-shell PATH artifact, so pwsh-launched node builds DO find the toolchain. parse OK. REMAINING (the systemic heal from the BEAM incident): the committed-MEMORY CAP at launch - a Win32 Job Object (JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_JOB_MEMORY) wrapping the node-side job so a blow-up OOM-kills one process not the node (Linux = systemd-run scope). That is launch-time and belongs with kit the verb owner; preflight only CHECKS headroom. parse OK. No commit, no stage.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_6 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 6u32, "2026-11-07T18:20Z", "resilience", "SWIFT added to the toolchain parity surface (compiler 11-07, after the GREEN first node pack gate: node pack61 byte-identical to box, 0/159 residual). node-env.ps1 gains $CompilerToolchain = rustc,cargo,dotnet,swiftc,zig (the verb passes this for a candidate build; Test-ToolchainParity default stays rustc,cargo so a non-compiler job is not over-constrained). SWIFT CAVEAT captured in code: swiftc is PRESENT on the node but real builds fail \"exception 1033\" = Windows.sdk + Swift runtime not on PATH, so Get-Command swiftc PASSES falsely - true Swift parity needs a swiftc SMOKE-COMPILE. FLAGGED to compiler; the repair (install Swift SDK+runtime per tmp/AGENTS.md Swift section) is node provisioning, surfaced to them. NEXT STEP: add a swiftc smoke-compile to Test-ToolchainParity for Swift-class jobs.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_7 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 7u32, "2026-11-07T18:41Z", "resilience", "SWIFT 1033 ROOT-CAUSED (11-07, read-only probe, no compile): on the laptop non-interactive ssh pwsh, swiftc is FOUND + SDKROOT set + UCRT present, but link.exe and cl.exe are NOT on PATH. VS 2022 is installed (vctip.exe runs), so the MSVC toolchain is not missing from disk - the VS DEVELOPER ENV (vcvars) is not LOADED in the non-interactive session, so cl/link + MSVC/SDK INCLUDE/LIB are absent; swiftc frontend uses the clang importer for the Windows SDK modulemaps and dies without them = exception 1033 (frontend crash). Same impoverished-non-interactive-session class as rustc-via-cmd. FIX (compiler build side): load vcvars in the node Swift job (cmd /c vcvars64.bat && swiftc, or Enter-VsDevShell). IMPLICATION for this item: Test-ToolchainParity for a Swift/C++ node job must check cl.exe + link.exe ON PATH (= vcvars loaded), not just swiftc presence - a presence-only check passes while the build fails. Reported to compiler.")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_8 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 8u32, "2026-11-07T18:51Z", "resilience", "CLARIFICATION on the Swift cl/link parity check (avoids a false-refuse trap): do NOT add cl/link to the bare-PATH toolchain probe. The preflight runs in a PLAIN ssh session with NO vcvars loaded, but the actual build job DOES load vcvars (compiler fixed test.ps1 Swift tier to import vcvars64; NODE-SWIFT-VCVARS). A bare cl/link Get-Command check in the preflight session would therefore FALSE-REFUSE every compiler job (rustc/dotnet build fine via their own linkers without vcvars - proven by the GREEN byte-identical node pack61). The correct Swift/C++ parity check must either run WITH vcvars loaded (mirror the build env) or be a swiftc SMOKE-COMPILE - not a bare-PATH probe. $CompilerToolchain stays rustc,cargo,dotnet,swiftc,zig (no cl/link).")
inl note_of_delegate_5_preflight_9 () = Note ("DELEGATE-5-PREFLIGHT", 9u32, "2026-11-07T20:16Z", "resilience", "BLOCKER: resilience part done+verified (5 typed-refusal predicates + Select-OffloadTarget, live-proven). Remaining is OTHER-LANE: the proactive Job-Object/systemd-scope committed-memory cap is kit launch-verb work (DELEGATE-1-VERB / KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR); the Swift smoke-compile needs a node build-env (vcvars) window. RESUME: when kit lands the launch cap, or for a node Swift smoke when a build window opens. Nothing resilience-side actionable now.")
inl delegate_6_results () = Task ("DELEGATE-6-RESULTS", "delegate returns typed results into a local job dir: exit, full stdout.log, tests.tsv, per-file verdict lines (pass/red/VOID+cause), declared outputs dir, all hash-verified", TaskKind, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "DELEGATE-1-VERB", "team:rig,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_6_results () = Planning ("DELEGATE-6-RESULTS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_6_results_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-6-RESULTS", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: no ssh -EncodedCommand / job tail / scp by hand (tibia, fiscal, main, x, kit); no line or 5 KB cap; the FULL log always lands (tibia: the agent reads the full log, never a summary line; fiscal: own filters truncated results twice); landing is verified by hash, not size (resilience). Produced files the box should keep go through the hash-guarded -Land manifest; the apply stays on the box.")
inl note_of_delegate_6_results_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-6-RESULTS", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: on job end copy back the stage outputs dir, stdout.log, tests.tsv and per-file verdicts into the local job dir with hashes verified, and record a VOID cause per file when a verdict is missing; today results come back only by tail plus manual scp. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: result record, verdict union (Pass, Fail, Void of cause), cause union (Timeout, Oom, NoRoute, NotRun).")
inl note_of_delegate_6_results_3 () = Note ("DELEGATE-6-RESULTS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T00:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 21:0x rig, adopting the studied techniques (memory studied-engineering-techniques, relayed by fiscal at the user's ask). RUN-EVIDENCE PROTOCOL for job/delegate results: a fresh, empty, create-new-only run directory per run; each step under its own timeout that kills the tree (exit 124) with its own stdout/stderr logs and elapsed_ms; summary.json rewritten after EVERY step; scope and limitations fields in every summary with a render test that they survive; totals typed exact / at_least / unknown, never a silent 0; contradictory evidence fails and is never repaired; failed run dirs are kept; no automatic retries, no relaxed verdicts. DoD: a delegate run leaves that directory shape, proved by a fixture run that times out one step. TypeFeatures: a total union (Exact of u64 | AtLeast of u64 | Unknown); a consuming step recorder whose finish seals the summary. Next step: the summary model in rig_delegate beside verdict.")
inl delegate_7_cleanup () = Task ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", "delegate auto-removes the stage after results land (--keep opts out) and a node janitor prunes orphaned stages and leftover ssh/pwsh children", TaskKind, P0, D2, 60u32, Blocked, "DELEGATE-6-RESULTS", "team:org,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_7_cleanup () = Planning ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:35Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: node free disk never drops because of delegated stages (kit: regen stage dirs filled the disk; main: 11.9 GB free, mirrors removed by hand); janitor ages stages > 24 h; reaps child trees per [[reap-spares-kit-jobwaits-and-trains]] rules (never a live job-wait or train).")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:49Z", "resilience", "NEXT STEP: a node janitor (reuses Invoke-Bounded child-tree kill + orphan-reaper age gate): on result-landing remove that job stage immediately; on a scheduled sweep remove stage dirs older than 24h and reap orphaned child trees whose launching ssh session is gone (check parent cmd first, spare kit job-waits/trains per the reaper rules). DoD: no stage dir outlives its results by >24h and no orphaned child tree survives its parent; a dry-run lists before deleting. TYPEFEATURES: a stage entry as {path;landed;age}; janitor verdict per entry = keep|prune|reap.")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_3 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 3u32, "2026-11-07T17:55Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom markers (lint). NEXT STEP: resilience lists C:\\home\\remote and C:\\home\\remote-stage on the node with age and in-use state (111 mirrors on 11-07), then adds the age-gated prune to the standing orphan reaper; the delegate verb deletes its own stage after results land.")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_4 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 4u32, "2026-11-07T18:05Z", "resilience", "STAGE SWEEP DONE (11-07 14:0x; extended the existing node-disk-cleanup.ps1, no new script). Added a 24h-gated sweep of C:\\home\\remote-stage (per-job upload stages outlive the 6h temp scratch): prune stage dirs whose LastWriteTime is >StageAgeHours old (default 24), so a long-running job keeps its stage fresh and is never pruned mid-flight; gated behind -Apply (dry-run by default). parse OK. DoD progress: no stage dir outlives its results by >24h = covered by the age sweep. REMAINING: (1) auto-remove a stage the MOMENT results land = the delegation verb trigger (kit owns the verb), not an age sweep - noted for kit. (2) orphaned child process TREES whose launching ssh is gone = orphan-reaper.ps1 already owns that (cross-ref, not duplicated here). NEXT STEP: hand kit the on-landing stage-removal hook; confirm node-disk-cleanup runs on a node schedule with -Apply (user-batch). No commit, no stage.")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_5 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 5u32, "2026-11-07T18:20Z", "resilience", "spiral-bin-candidates sweep ADDED (compiler 11-07): node-disk-cleanup.ps1 now keeps the newest $KeepCandidates (default 2) %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\<name> dirs by LastWriteTime and prunes older - a keep-N rule, not age, because candidates are REUSED across packs (nodepack61 is queued for the next pack; an age cut could delete an active one). -Apply gated, parse OK. node-disk-cleanup now covers: temp scratch >6h, remote-stage stages >24h, spiral-bin-candidates keep-newest-2.")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_6 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 6u32, "2026-11-07T18:51Z", "resilience", "LOGIC VERIFIED against real laptop-node dirs (11-07, read-only dry-run). spiral-bin-candidates keep-newest-2: KEEPS mst1 (14:41) + nodepack61 (13:58 - compiler needs it), WOULD-PRUNE the 11 superseded 10-29/10-30 packs (p3br,crd,p3tr,pack8,p3hc,pack7h,pack7,p3speed,pack7full,p3d4,pack7check) = multi-GB reclaim. remote-stage 24h sweep: keeps every fresh stage (todays fiscal-full-*, dice-pack61, cpipe1, x-roundtrip, main-ship-pack61, kit-probe1107*) and selects only multi-day-stale (backups 272h, ex/gc/pr/r9 ~298h, metrics 104h, xcells1 122h, tibia-gates 74h, kit-toml-lib 83h, x-media1/2-out 32/25h, etc.). So the rule spares active work and targets abandoned dirs correctly. Node has 25GB free now (not urgent); enabling the scheduled -Apply is the coordinated/user-batch step (it prunes other lanes stale stages - 24h-untouched = safe, but coordinate). parse OK.")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_7 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 7u32, "2026-11-07T19:01Z", "resilience", "CANDIDATE RECLAIM EXECUTED (11-07 14:5x, compiler-authorized keep-newest-2): pruned 11 stale spiral-bin-candidates dirs (the 10-29/10-30 superseded packs) on the laptop node, freed 754MB, KEPT mst1 + nodepack61 (compilers active/queued packs). Node C: 25->26GB. This realizes the spiral-bin-candidates keep-2 rule once, manually; the scheduled node-disk-cleanup -Apply will keep it bounded. The remote-stage 24h sweep is NOT auto-applied yet (prunes other lanes stale stages - coordinate before enabling -Apply on a schedule, per the commitment to x-dumps/peers).")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_8 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 8u32, "2026-11-07T20:17Z", "resilience", "BLOCKER: resilience part done (stage 24h-sweep + spiral-bin-candidates keep-2 in node-disk-cleanup.ps1, verified; 754MB reclaimed). Remaining is OTHER-LANE/coordination: on-landing stage removal = DELEGATE-6-RESULTS (kit verb); enabling the scheduled -Apply (prunes other lanes stale stages) needs coordination + is user-batch task-reg. RESUME: kit lands the results hook, or a coordinated maintenance window to enable -Apply.")
inl note_of_delegate_7_cleanup_9 () = Note ("DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP", 9u32, "2026-11-09T23:11Z", "org-614162e5", "11-09 19:1x org-614162e5 CURRENT NODE STALE-STAGE DIAGNOSIS (read-only, serves the user ask 'stale jobs in nodes'). moon C:\\home\\remote-stage now holds 139 stage dirs; ~15 are STALE 5-14 DAYS old and still present: 10/26 ex,gc,pr,gf,r9; 10/27 backups; 11/02 xcells1; 11/03 metrics,group-part-units,realshape; 11/04 kit-toml-lib,tibia-tf-out. These are the SAME abandoned dirs the 11-07 dry-run flagged (backups 272h, ex/gc/pr/r9 ~298h) - 2 days later they persist. Node disk = 15.2 GB free, right AT the 15GB alarm floor (was ~25GB on 11-07, ~16GB earlier today: slow downward pressure). spiral-bin-candidates = 6 dirs (keep-newest-2 would prune 4). CONFIRMS the predicted consequence of leaving the scheduled -Apply DISABLED: the verified node-disk-cleanup.ps1 janitor (24h stage sweep + candidates keep-2, proven 11-07, reclaimed 754MB once manually) is NOT running on a schedule, so stale stages accumulate and disk creeps toward the floor. RECOMMENDATION (becoming time-sensitive as disk nears 15GB): enable the scheduled node-disk-cleanup -Apply on the node (the coordinated/user-batch step this item deferred) OR do one coordinated apply pass. I did NOT unilaterally prune - the stale stages are OTHER LANES' dirs (tibia,xcells,kit,metrics) and the commitment is to coordinate before -Apply deletes peers' stale stages; the candidates keep-2 is compiler-pre-authorized but best run via the script's safe keep-newest logic, not by hand. The on-landing auto-remove half stays blocked on DELEGATE-6-RESULTS (kit verb). This is current evidence that the deferred -Apply enablement should move up.")
