inl note_of_delegate_12_quiet_slot_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-12-QUIET-SLOT", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:36Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD: tibia's bench and cell-budget timing runs stop going VOID on lock_timeout / 300 s under co-load; the exclusive job waits for the slot instead of failing; priority order replaces hand-built after-chains (fiscal: a hand-reordered 6-job chain).")
inl note_of_delegate_12_quiet_slot_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-12-QUIET-SLOT", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-07 kit groom markers. NEXT STEP: add --exclusive to delegate: the placement waits for a machine with no other kit job and holds the slot until the job ends; a priority order (exclusive first, then by item priority) decides the queue. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: slot_mode union (Shared, Exclusive), priority nominal.")
inl delegate_13_drift_watch () = Task ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", "automatic drift watch: a scheduled tick compares every node's installed core, base lib and toolchain to the box and heals (re-ship/resync) or alarms", TaskKind, P0, D3, 92u32, Active, "DELEGATE-11-NODE-IDENTITY", "team:org,infra,node,delegation", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delegate_13_drift_watch () = Planning ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_1 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:36Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom of GENERIC-NODE-DELEGATION (user: any work delegates to nodes with minimal friction). DoD (user 11-07: \"automatic syncs/checks etc so we don't drift with stale stuff\"): a lagging node core or base lib is detected within one tick and healed by the owning step (pack-chain for cores), never silently used; status file has an age ([[status-files-need-age]]); the alarm reaches a lane ([[alarm-detects-but-never-delivers]]).")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_2 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 2u32, "2026-11-07T17:49Z", "resilience", "NEXT STEP: a scheduled tick that hashes each node (keyed by node_id from DELEGATE-11, not hostname) for core pin + base lib + toolchain versions and diffs against the box (role=origin); on drift, heal via the owning step (re-sync/re-pin) or alarm through a DELIVERY-VERIFIED channel (probe the deliver verb+target, never detect-only). DoD: drift on any node is caught within one tick and either auto-healed or alarmed with the node_id + which dimension drifted; a planted mismatch fires exactly one verdict, 0 false positives on an in-sync node. TYPEFEATURES: node fingerprint as {node_id;core;lib;toolchain} record; drift verdict = InSync|Drifted(dimension)|Unreachable.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_3 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 3u32, "2026-11-07T17:56Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler groom markers (lint). DoD: within one tick a node whose installed compiler core, base spiral lib or toolchain differs from the box is reported in a status file with an age and through a channel a lane actually receives, and the owning step heals it (pack-chain for cores, resync for the base lib). NEXT STEP: resilience adds a core-hash and base-lib-hash comparison to the existing node-utilization monitor tick, keyed by DELEGATE-11 ids.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_4 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 4u32, "2026-11-07T18:28Z", "resilience", "PROVEN DRIFT found (subagent probe 11-07, concrete input for this item): rustc box 8006091eb (10-17) vs europa f9ceb4a4d (10-31); dotnet box rc.1.26425.128 vs europa rc.3.26522.148; zig MATCHED (0.18.0-dev.738+ae9a8acc7). So the node is NOT toolchain-identical to the box today - a node build could diverge. Probe commands: rustc --version, dotnet --version, zig version per host + the spiral core-pin hash + base-lib hash (pin-file path TBD). Drift verdict keys on node_id (DELEGATE-11). This is exactly the signal drift-watch must catch + heal (re-sync) or alarm.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_5 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 5u32, "2026-11-07T18:38Z", "resilience", "TOOLCHAIN-DRIFT DIMENSION IMPLEMENTED + LIVE-VERIFIED (11-07 14:3x). node-env.ps1 Get-ToolchainFingerprint <route> + Test-NodeDrift <route> fingerprint rustc(commit)/dotnet/zig per host (OS-aware, prefixed output so a missing tool does not misalign) and diff the node vs the box (role=origin). Live run vs europa returned ok=False with the EXACT proven drift: rustc box 8006091eb vs europa f9ceb4a4d; dotnet box rc.1.26425.128 vs europa rc.3.26522.148; zig matched (not flagged). So the detector correctly catches real drift and ignores matches. DoD progress: drift on a node is detected + named per dimension - met for the toolchain dimension. REMAINING: (1) the CORE/base-lib PIN-HASH dimension (needs the pin file path - ask compiler/kit), (2) the scheduled tick + a DELIVERY-VERIFIED alarm/heal channel (probe the deliver verb+target, not detect-only), (3) auto-heal via re-sync. FINDING: europa is AHEAD of the box on rustc+dotnet - flagged to compiler (a cloud build is not toolchain-identical to the box).")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_6 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 6u32, "2026-11-07T19:06Z", "resilience", "SCHEDULED-TICK + DELIVERY-VERIFIED ALARM done + live-verified (11-07). node-env.ps1 Invoke-DriftWatch [-Routes] [-NoteOnDrift] fingerprints each node (keyed by node_id) vs the box, writes a typed report to node-drift-watch.last.log and READS IT BACK to confirm delivered (not detect-only, per the alarm-detects-but-never-delivers trap); -NoteOnDrift also files an rc-checked backlog note. Live run (delivered=True) found drift on BOTH nodes: laptop zig 0.17.0 vs box 0.18.0-dev.738 (laptop zig is a MAJOR version behind - flagged to compiler, matters if a node build links via zig cc); europa rustc 8006091eb->f9ceb4a4d + dotnet rc.1->rc.3. DoD progress: a scheduled tick catches drift per node + alarms through a verified channel - MET for the toolchain dimension. REMAINING: core-pin + base-lib dimension (pin path pending compiler/kit; base-lib compare must handle node-uses-base-lib design), auto-heal (re-sync), and wiring Invoke-DriftWatch -NoteOnDrift into a schedule (user-batch).")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_7 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 7u32, "2026-11-07T19:13Z", "resilience", "DRIFT-WATCH is BOX-AUTHORITATIVE (confirmed per compiler 11-07: box versions are the baseline; installs/accepts happen on the box; native memo keys on tool stamps). Test-NodeDrift already compares node-vs-box so \"drift\" = node differs from box - correct as-is. ZIG-BUMP SCOPED + DEFERRED: compiler wants the laptop zig bumped 0.17.0 -> 0.18.0-dev.738+ae9a8acc7 (zig is the FIRST oracle -Oracle Zig,C, so the gap shifts native row verdicts box-vs-node). Method discovered: both use scoop, but the box zig is NON-STANDARD - scoop/shims/zig.shim points to apps\\zig-dev\\current (0.18.0-dev.738) while apps\\zig\\current is stock 0.17.0, so `scoop update zig` would NOT bump it (and would revert the box). Exact-738 match = COPY box %USERPROFILE%\\scoop\\apps\\zig-dev\\current (~361MB) -> laptop + replicate the zig.shim -> zig-dev. DEFERRED because: laptop is mid-build (4 rustc now - must not swap zig under a live build) + the 361MB transfer wants an idle link (floor protection). Execute when laptop idle + link quiet.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_8 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 8u32, "2026-11-07T19:19Z", "resilience", "AUTO-HEAL SPEC (the remaining heal dimension, fully specified so it is ready to wire when a node is idle + link quiet). Heal = make the drifted node match the BOX (authoritative) per tool - each mechanism is TOOL-SPECIFIC, not a generic copy: (1) ZIG: copy box %USERPROFILE%\\scoop\\apps\\zig-dev\\current -> node scoop apps\\zig-dev\\current + replicate scoop\\shims\\zig.shim (path=...\\zig-dev\\current\\zig.exe); verify `zig version`==box. NOT `scoop update` (box zig is a shim-indirected manual dev install; update reverts it). (2) RUSTC (nightly commit, e.g. box 8006091eb 2026-10-17): `rustup toolchain install nightly-2026-10-17` on the node then set default; verify the commit hash in `rustc --version` matches box. (3) DOTNET (e.g. box 11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 vs europa rc.3): install the box exact SDK via dotnet-install --version 11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128; verify `dotnet --version`. Each heal is GATED: run only when the node has NO active build (never swap a toolchain under a live build - the laptop was dotnetx5/rustcx4 at 100% at 19:1x) and the link is idle (floor protection). After any heal, re-run Invoke-DriftWatch to prove in-sync. Heal POLICY: match box, never let a node run ahead (native memo keys on box tool stamps - compiler 11-07).")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_9 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 9u32, "2026-11-07T21:22Z", "resilience", "ZIG-BUMP DEFERRAL REFINED (11-07 17:2x, per compiler): the laptop node is at 100% from FIVE lanes jobs side-by-side (fiscal-full-build2 200+min, x-crates2 120+min, x-cells-full6, 2 tibia jobs, compiler-p62) - healthy contention, not a loop, and it will not clear for hours. DECISION: do NOT chase a slot (would mean asking fiscal/x to pause 200-min jobs) for the zig bump - it is LOW-URGENCY (laptop zig 0.17 works for those lanes builds; the 0.17->0.18-dev.738 drift only matters for compilers native-oracle byte-identical checks, which compiler manages + builds authoritative artifacts on the box). The laptop zig-dev bump waits for a NATURAL node-quiet window (overnight or whenever the stack clears); I stopped polling the node every heartbeat for it. Compiler will ping if a node build specifically needs 0.18-dev.738 on the laptop. So DELEGATE-13 toolchain-drift detection+alarm+auto-heal-spec are DONE; the one execution (laptop zig heal) is deferred-by-choice, not blocked-urgently.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_10 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 10u32, "2026-11-07T21:41Z", "resilience", "RUSTC DRIFT BEING RESOLVED FLEET-WIDE (11-07, user decision via main): spirals nightly rustc pin moves 10-18 -> 11-05 in ONE coordinated pass tonight, and nightly-11-05 is ALREADY installed on box, node AND europa. So the rustc drift my drift-watch flagged (box 8006091eb/10-17 vs europa f9ceb4a4d/10-31) converges - all three hosts to nightly-11-05 after the pin-move. This is exactly the kind of coordinated heal the drift-watch is meant to confirm (vs the ad-hoc per-host bump I spec`d). AFTER the pin-move, Invoke-DriftWatch should show rustc IN-SYNC across hosts; I will re-run it to verify once the pass completes tonight. REMAINING drift after the rustc pin-move: zig (laptop 0.17 vs box 0.18-dev.738, deferred to a node-quiet window) + dotnet (europa rc.1 vs rc.3, compiler to decide direction). The nightly pin-move covers rustc only. Note: resilience .ps1 scripts are NOT affected by the Spiral formatter change (item 2) - different toolchain.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_11 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 11u32, "2026-11-08T05:05Z", "resilience", "DELIVERY-VERIFIED hardened (session 614162e5): Invoke-DriftWatch note emission now uses the fleet CAS-retry loop @(0,2,5,10) via the call operator (was a single & kit note that would silently break the delivery guarantee on a transient CAS reject). node-env.ps1 parse-clean. Scheduled-tick wiring held back: the drift routes default to laptop(node)+europa and the user flagged the alias node status 11-08 (\"not using that alias anymore for that\"), so the node roster needs confirmation before a drift schedule is registered - not assuming it autonomously.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_12 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 12u32, "2026-11-08T05:51Z", "resilience", "DRIFT-WATCH CORRECTNESS FIX + accurate convergence verify (11-08, resilience). BUG: Get-ToolchainFingerprint read the AMBIENT rustc (box default nightly-2026-10-18 / 8006091eb) but spiral BUILDS use spiral/rust-toolchain.toml which pins nightly-2026-11-05 (rustc in-repo = 2d20b42b8) - so the rustc \"drift\" it flagged (box 10-17 vs europa 10-31) was a FALSE POSITIVE on a toolchain builds never use. FIX (node-env.ps1, parse-clean): read the pin channel from rust-toolchain.toml and fingerprint \"rustc +<pin>\" on EVERY host (a host lacking the pinned toolchain returns empty = correctly flagged real drift). dotnet/zig stay ambient (no toml pin). VERIFIED: box fp rustc now 2d20b42b8; full Invoke-DriftWatch (28s, hardened cached probe, under 100pct box CPU) shows rustc CONVERGED on nightly-2026-11-05 across box+laptop+europa. ACCURATE remaining drift (for the 02:00 report): laptop zig 0.17.0 vs box 0.18.0-dev.738 (deferred to a node-quiet window) + europa dotnet rc.1.26425.128 vs rc.3.26522.148 (compiler to decide direction). So the rustc pin-move DID land for builds; the standing \"box rustc still 10-17\" worry was the ambient default, not what builds use.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_13 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 13u32, "2026-11-08T21:33Z", "org", "Next: fold NODE-BENCH-METRIC perf-drift (nodebench-metric-and-rating, built by org3) into Invoke-DriftWatch so a node slower than its baseline alarms, not just a toolchain mismatch.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_14 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 14u32, "2026-11-08T21:43Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 17:4x, from org3's HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD verify: node-drift-watch.last.log is STALE 952 min (~16 h) at 17:4x, so the drift watcher is DEAD. Next step: find why it stopped (scheduled task state + last log tail), then restart it or retire it in favor of lane-reconcile; the heartbeat guard will confirm freshness after.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_15 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 15u32, "2026-11-08T22:07Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 18:0x ROOT CAUSE (found and fixed by org3, confirmed by org2): the watcher was not dormant. scripts/node-env.ps1 failed to PARSE, so every function in it was dead (node routing, Invoke-PreflightSsh, Invoke-DriftWatch, the lane helpers). Cause: line 402's bash load-check used backslash-dollar inside a PowerShell double-quoted string, so PowerShell evaluated the bash subexpression and choked on ||. Fix: backtick-dollar. Proof: Parser.ParseFile gives 0 errors; dot-sourcing loads 22 functions, including Invoke-DriftWatch and Invoke-PreflightSsh; every scripts/*.ps1 parses clean; org3 ran Invoke-DriftWatch by hand and the heartbeat refreshed (drift none; moon transiently unreachable). node-env.ps1 is UNTRACKED, so git can't show who added line 402. Next step: confirm the NEXT scheduled run refreshes node-drift-watch.last.log on its own (HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD green without a hand run), then close.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_16 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 16u32, "2026-11-09T02:50Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 22:5x autonomous-run check: node-drift-watch.last.log is 279min stale (last line 2026-11-08 18:05 = the line-402 hand run, NOT a scheduled fire). ROOT CAUSE: Get-ScheduledTask *drift* returns NONE - the scheduled tick was NEVER registered; the 05:05 hold (pending laptop-vs-wifi roster) was never lifted into a registration. Roster IS now resolved (node route=wifi, 11-08 standardization) so this is UNBLOCKED. The 18:05 run still routed to deprecated laptop (UNREACHABLE no identity) + vultr-sjc (in-sync). NEXT: register a drift tick by cloning the WORKING idle-with-ready-alarm scheduled task (conhost --headless hidden-window) calling Invoke-DriftWatch -Routes wifi,vultr,ganymede -NoteOnDrift; frequency ~3h, NOT folded into the frequent node-util tick (the 28s ssh-fingerprint is too heavy). Deferred from 22:5x to a focused beat to get the task XML right (scheduled-watchdog-silently-refused). NOT closeable until it self-refreshes with no hand run.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_17 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 17u32, "2026-11-09T03:03Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 23:0x LANDED (CPU-light): scripts/node-drift-watch.ps1 wrapper (parse-clean, UNTRACKED) + scheduled task node-drift-watch registered (conhost --headless hidden-window, Priority 5, ExecTimeLimit 12M, first fire 23:07 then every 3h, State=Ready). Wrapper owns RISING-EDGE delivery: calls Invoke-DriftWatch log-only and files a DELEGATE-13 note ONLY when drift state changes - avoids 3h note-spam on europa standing dotnet drift (-NoteOnDrift at line 431 notes every drifted run, so NOT used). ROUTES=vultr only: identity probe showed wifi/laptop=the BOX (b4c8f166, self-check pointless), vultr=europa (vultr-sjc 85944c7a, valid), ganymede+moon+comet=NO node-identity -> HARD DEP on DELEGATE-11; extend the wrapper Routes when they register. PENDING: confirm the 23:07 fire self-refreshes node-drift-watch.last.log with NO hand run (next heartbeat verifies); then staleness-guard stays green + the vultr dimension is closeable.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_18 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 18u32, "2026-11-09T03:08Z", "org3", "DRIFT-WATCH edge 2026-11-08 23:08: [ok] -> [DRIFT: vultr] | drift-watch vultr-sjc [85944c7a-b987-4bf5-94a4-633c4af92c8f]: DRIFT dotnet(box=11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 node=11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148)")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_19 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 19u32, "2026-11-09T03:11Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 23:09 VERIFIED end-to-end UNDER THE SCHEDULER (no hand run): the 23:07 scheduled fire self-refreshed node-drift-watch.last.log (age 1min, stamp 23:08) - the open DoD blocker org2 flagged is MET. It correctly caught the real europa dotnet drift (vultr-sjc 85944c7a: dotnet box=rc.1.26425.128 node=rc.3.26522.148) and the wrapper filed EXACTLY ONE rising-edge note [ok]->[DRIFT: vultr], delivery-verified (rc=0, no NOTE FAILED). So the vultr dimension is proven: tick + self-refresh + detect-with-node_id+dimension + rising-edge deliver. REMAINING for full close: ganymede/moon coverage (DELEGATE-11 identity dep) + auto-heal re-sync (later step). The europa dotnet rc.1-vs-rc.3 drift is now LIVE-TRACKED; compiler still owns the direction call.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_20 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 20u32, "2026-11-09T03:19Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 23:1x GANYMEDE COVERAGE ADDED (unblocks the ganymede dep): wrote ~/.node-identity on ganymede (node_id 0fa5a15e-...=machine-id as UUID, name=ganymede role=compute os=linux site=mia) - it was simply never onboarded when DELEGATE-11 ran 11-07. Added ganymede to node-env.ps1 NodeIdentityOs(linux)+ExpectedNodeIds; Test-NodeIdentity -ForCompute now ok=True; Get-NodeIdentity resolves. Extended node-drift-watch.ps1 Routes to @(vultr,ganymede), parse-clean. Drift-watch now covers the primary cloud compute; the ganymede line appears on the next scheduled fire (02:07). REMAINING: moon identity (still none) + auto-heal. NOTE node-env.ps1 co-edited with org2 Get-LaneSessions this session - both coexist + parse clean.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_21 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 21u32, "2026-11-09T03:30Z", "org3", "DRIFT-WATCH edge 2026-11-08 23:30: [DRIFT: vultr] -> [ok] | drift-watch vultr,ganymede: UNREACHABLE (no identity)")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_22 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 22u32, "2026-11-09T03:32Z", "org3", "DRIFT-WATCH edge 2026-11-08 23:32: [ok] -> [DRIFT: vultr,ganymede] | drift-watch vultr-sjc [85944c7a-b987-4bf5-94a4-633c4af92c8f]: DRIFT dotnet(box=11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 node=11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148) | drift-watch ganymede [0fa5a15e-0766-47d2-9d1a-cc24f0cd20ea]: DRIFT dotnet(box=11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 node=11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148)")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_23 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 23u32, "2026-11-09T03:33Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 23:3x CORRECTION (hand-run artifacts, disregard the two 23:30/23:32 edge notes): verifying ganymede coverage, I hand-ran the wrapper with '-Routes vultr,ganymede' via pwsh -File, which passes the comma-list as ONE string so it looked up a route literally named 'vultr,ganymede' -> UNREACHABLE -> false state 'ok' -> a false '[DRIFT: vultr]->[ok]' edge note; the corrective re-run (default array) then filed '[ok]->[DRIFT: vultr,ganymede]'. LESSON: pass -Routes only via -Command or rely on the default; -File never splits a comma array. The scheduled task runs with NO args so its default @(vultr,ganymede) is correct and unaffected. VERIFIED TRUE STATE: node-drift-watch covers vultr+ganymede end-to-end; BOTH cloud nodes carry the SAME standing dotnet drift box=11.0.100-rc.1.26425.128 vs node=rc.3.26522.148 (ganymede 0fa5a15e confirmed, same as europa 85944c7a) - the cloud hosts are AHEAD of the box on dotnet; compiler owns the direction call. Next scheduled fire 02:07 reads 'DRIFT: vultr,ganymede' unchanged -> no further note.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_24 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 24u32, "2026-11-09T03:40Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 23:4x HARDENED (implements the item's typed verdict InSync|Drifted|Unreachable): fixed the flaw my hand-run exposed - an UNREACHABLE node (no identity / probe failed) was folded into 'ok', so a failed probe masqueraded as a cleared drift (the false edge note earlier). Now Invoke-DriftWatch (node-env.ps1) collects an $unreachable set, the log head carries 'UNREACHABLE: <routes>' as a first-class part (never 'ok' when a node couldn't be probed) and returns it; the wrapper's rising-edge state matches, so a lost probe reads as lost-visibility, never 'drift resolved'. VERIFIED: Invoke-DriftWatch -Routes @('nonexistent-test') -> drifted=[], unreachable=[nonexistent-test], head='UNREACHABLE: nonexistent-test' (not ok). Both scripts parse clean + coexist with org2's Get-LaneSessions; log restored to the true 'DRIFT: vultr,ganymede' so the 02:07 fire sees a matching prior.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_25 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 25u32, "2026-11-09T04:30Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 00:3x MOON TAIL RESOLVED (it was a category error, not missing work): ~/.ssh/config groups 'Host moon wifi laptop' = all aliases of the SAME host (the box DESKTOP-6E8C14G). So 'moon' is NOT a separate node needing an identity - it's the box's fleet alias, already covered by the 'local' identity. DRIFT-WATCH COVERAGE IS COMPLETE for what matters: the box-ssh-reachable REMOTE compute nodes where builds must match the box = europa(vultr) + ganymede, both now covered + verified. pluto(rustdesk) is relay_only (no builds, not a drift target); the work-lab night nodes (venus/mercury/saturn) are deep-relay via ssh chains, out of a box-direct drift-watch's scope (they'd need their own identity + chain-reach, a separate effort if ever wanted). So the ONLY remaining open tail is the AUTO-HEAL, blocked on compiler's dotnet-direction call (box rc.1 vs both cloud nodes rc.3; asked compiler 00:2x). Everything else (scheduled tick, self-refresh, 2-node detect, rising-edge deliver, unreachable-verdict hardening) is done + verified.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_26 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 26u32, "2026-11-09T04:42Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 00:4x DOTNET FALSE-POSITIVE FIXED (compiler caught it, same class as the rustc fix): the drift-watch fingerprinted the SYSTEM dotnet (dotnet --version = box rc.1) but the compiler builds with the spiral CACHE SDK (<cache>/spiral-bin/toolchains/dotnet, Resolve-SpiralDotnet) which is rc.3 on ALL hosts, and the oort compiler store keys by that SDK. So the 'DRIFT: dotnet rc.1 vs rc.3' was a false positive on a toolchain builds never use. FIX (node-env.ps1 Get-ToolchainFingerprint, local + linux-remote branches): dotnet now reads the cache SDK - %LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/toolchains/dotnet/dotnet.exe (win) and HOME/.cache/spiral-bin/toolchains/dotnet/dotnet (linux), ambient fallback. VERIFIED: box fp now = cache rc.3.26522.148; Test-NodeDrift vultr + ganymede both ok=True drift=[]; drift log cleared to 'ok / vultr-sjc in-sync / ganymede in-sync' (rising-edge filed the [DRIFT]->[ok] clear note). AUTO-HEAL must NOT touch the box system dotnet (compiler: user-workstation install, not byte-identity). Windows-remote branch still reads ambient but is harmless/unused (no windows remote node; moon/wifi/laptop=box=local). Remaining real drift: zig only (laptop 0.17 vs box 0.18-dev, deferred). So drift-watch is now ACCURATE across rustc/dotnet/zig/mimalloc; the only open tail is auto-heal wiring (direction = forward to rc.3 per compiler, enforce on nodes only).")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_27 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 27u32, "2026-11-09T04:51Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 00:4x GROOM -> Active 92%: the DoD ('drift caught within one tick and EITHER auto-healed OR alarmed with node_id + which dimension drifted; planted mismatch fires exactly one verdict, 0 false positives on in-sync') is MET via the accurate ALARM path: scheduled 3h tick, self-refresh, europa+ganymede coverage (the only build-relevant remote nodes; moon=box, pluto=relay), rising-edge delivery with node_id+dimension, unreachable-as-first-class, and accurate fingerprints (rustc toml-pin, dotnet cache-SDK after compiler's catch, zig/mimalloc). 0 false positives confirmed (both nodes in-sync). Remaining 8% = AUTO-HEAL wiring, which is a BEYOND-DoD enhancement (the DoD is satisfied by 'alarmed') + needs a REAL drift to test the per-tool install safely (compiler: forward to rc.3, nodes-only, NEVER the box) - deferred rather than ship untested toolchain-install logic. Not Done only because that enhancement + the deferred zig heal (laptop 0.17->0.18-dev) remain.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_28 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 28u32, "2026-11-09T06:53Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 03:0x CORRECTION to the 00:3x MOON TAIL note: moon is NOT the box. The ssh config line groups moon/wifi/laptop as aliases of ONE host, DESKTOP-6E8C14G, but the box is a different machine (Win32_ComputerSystem.Name on the box = ALIAS; over ssh moon answers DESKTOP-6E8C14G). Both have 8 logical CPUs; moon is the Windows twin node. So moon is a remote Windows compute node that takes kit jobs (compiler timing window, microblog chains) and needs drift coverage: a node identity + the Windows-remote fingerprint branch (currently reads ambient dotnet, i.e. the cache-SDK fix is missing there). Next step: add moon to the drift targets with the Windows-remote branch reading %LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/toolchains/dotnet, then a planted-mismatch check on moon.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_29 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 29u32, "2026-11-09T07:01Z", "org3", "DRIFT-WATCH edge 2026-11-09 03:01: [ok] -> [DRIFT: wifi] | drift-watch vultr-sjc [85944c7a-b987-4bf5-94a4-633c4af92c8f]: in-sync | drift-watch ganymede [0fa5a15e-0766-47d2-9d1a-cc24f0cd20ea]: in-sync | drift-watch laptop [b4c8f166-3608-4028-8a75-4ad3cf12d95f]: DRIFT dotnet(box=11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148 node=11.0.100-rc.2.26504.105); zig(box=0.18.0-dev.738+ae9a8acc7 node=0.17.0)")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_30 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 30u32, "2026-11-09T07:02Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 03:0x MOON CORRECTION + COVERAGE ADDED (org2 note 28 was RIGHT; my 00:3x/00:4x moon=box claims were WRONG). Verified directly: box = ALIAS (MachineGuid 2b2c714b), moon = DESKTOP-6E8C14G (MachineGuid 26fe0dc3, 8 CPUs) = a SEPARATE Windows node. ssh aliases moon/wifi/laptop all point to that remote node (identity b4c8f166 name=laptop), NOT the box - so I'd WRONGLY excluded moon from drift coverage. FIXED: (1) Get-ToolchainFingerprint WINDOWS-REMOTE branch now reads the cache SDK (%LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/toolchains/dotnet/dotnet.exe, ambient fallback) - was still ambient; (2) added 'wifi' to node-drift-watch.ps1 default routes @(vultr,ganymede,wifi). Parse-clean, coexists with org2 Get-LaneSessions. VERIFIED the wrapper now covers moon + found REAL drift my error had HIDDEN: moon dotnet CACHE SDK=rc.2.26504.105 (BEHIND box+cloud rc.3.26522.148) + zig 0.17 (vs box 0.18-dev); vultr+ganymede stay in-sync. The SCHEDULED task (default routes) now covers moon automatically. moon rc.2 is a REAL byte-identity risk (moon takes kit jobs) - per compiler's forward-to-rc.3 direction, moon's cache SDK needs updating to rc.3 (node-provision heal, deferred). My moon=box error was ONLY in the drift-watch; saturation-monitor correctly treats wifi as a node.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_31 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 31u32, "2026-11-09T07:08Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 03:1x moon SDK drift is COMPILER-OWNED (compiler confirmed, owns + will heal it): compiler installs rc.3 into moon's %LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/toolchains/dotnet via install-dotnet.ps1 AFTER rig's TRAIN42 moon half + compiler's moon links finish, BEFORE building the pack67 Windows pair on moon (the pair's oort key embeds sdk-<version>, must be rc.3 to match box+store). rc.1+rc.2 stay side by side (not deleted); nothing broken meanwhile (pack64 runtimeconfig targets runtime rc.1 with rollForward Major, so the installed compiler runs fine on rc.2). Recorded by compiler on COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS. The drift-watch correctly keeps flagging moon rc.2 (rising-edge = filed once) until the rc.3 heal, then shows in-sync (clear-edge) - so it tracks the heal automatically. DESIGN NOTE for the deferred AUTO-HEAL: it must NOT auto-heal LANE-OWNED drifts - compiler explicitly said 'don't auto-heal moon'. So the auto-heal spec needs an OWNERSHIP/opt-out model (a drift a lane owns + is actively healing is not the auto-heal's to touch) ALONGSIDE the 'never touch the box' rule. A drift-watch that auto-heals is only safe if it knows what it's allowed to heal.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_32 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 32u32, "2026-11-09T09:47Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 05:4x HARDENED edge-detection against state-aliasing (unstaged, scripts/node-drift-watch.ps1). BUG: the rising-edge note keyed ONLY on the head route-summary (priorState vs newState = 'DRIFT: wifi'). If an already-drifting node acquired a NEW drift dimension (e.g. moon, already dotnet-rc.2+zig, also drifts rustc), the summary stays 'DRIFT: wifi' and NO edge note fired - a real change silently swallowed (same couldn't-distinguish-from-known class as monitor-failure-not-clean-value, one level up: the detector's state key was coarser than the signal). FIX: read prior DETAIL from the log body (lines filtered to 'drift-watch *', so an appended NOTE-FAILED line can't masquerade as drift) before Invoke-DriftWatch overwrites it; edge now fires when the route-summary OR the detail content changes; note/fail-log tag the edge 'state change' vs 'detail change (same routes)'. VERIFIED: parse OK + 5/5 edge unit tests (A unchanged=no-fire [proves NO re-alarm spam on the stable known moon drift], B new-dimension-same-route=FIRE [the bug], C route-change=FIRE, D first-run-empty=no-fire, E drift-cleared=FIRE). Did NOT execute the live probe (would ssh + overwrite the log mid another-capture); AST parse + isolated logic test instead. node-env.ps1 Invoke-DriftWatch unchanged.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_33 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 33u32, "2026-11-09T12:24Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 DoD MET at 92% - driving to its terminal state for resilience. The DoD (drift caught within one tick + alarmed with node_id+dimension + 0 false positives on in-sync) is fully satisfied via the accurate ALARM path: 3h scheduled tick + self-refresh, coverage of every build-relevant remote node (europa+ganymede+moon, all identity-onboarded), rising-edge delivery, unreachable-as-first-class, accurate fingerprints (rustc toml-pin, dotnet cache-SDK, zig/mimalloc) + the edge-aliasing hardening (detail-keyed edge, 5/5 tests). The remaining 8% is AUTO-HEAL, which the groom marks BEYOND-DoD, and the HEAL itself is COMPILER's domain: compiler owns the toolchain install + the rc.3 direction call (moon's live dotnet-rc.2/zig-0.17 drift is the real test case, which drift-watch already DETECTS correctly - the detect half is done). So the detect side is complete; the heal side waits on compiler. Wait: lane:compiler for the auto-heal (toolchain install direction + execution). Resilience keeps the drift DETECTION running.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_34 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 34u32, "2026-11-09T13:34Z", "compiler", "compiler ANSWER 11-09 13:4x (heal side, as dotnet-pin owner). DIRECTION: the fleet pin is the BOX: spiral cache SDK 11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148, the installed compiler pair, the spiral deps clone at the box HEAD (17654e07 today); rustc follows each repos rust-toolchain.toml (rustup heals it on use, so report only); zig is pinned by whoever ships zig (not compiler). HEAL RECIPES you may run automatically when the node has NO running compiler/train/gate job (check kit job list) and log each heal: (1) dotnet drift -> `pwsh apps/compiler/scripts/install-dotnet.ps1 -Version <box SDK>` (new -Version flag, unstaged: installs that exact SDK side by side and throws unless it is listed afterwards; never the channel default, which can pass the pin); (2) compiler pair drift -> install-pack.ps1 -FromUrls <minted list> (box mints with -MintUrls; nodes need no keys) or the guarded pair copy; the in-use guard must pass, else defer to the next tick; (3) deps clone drift -> restore from a box tar of deps/The-Spiral-Language at the box HEAD, after removing junctions with cmd /c rmdir (PS 5.1 Remove-Item follows them). Never heal moon while rigs train or compilers timed window runs. moons dotnet rc.2 is healed by compilers queued moon job (step 2 = the exact rc.3 install), so keep it EXPECTED until that job reports. Wait on compiler cleared.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_35 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 35u32, "2026-11-09T13:36Z", "org3", "org3 11-09: compiler answered the heal side (note 34, cleared its wait). AUTO-HEAL RECIPE captured (box=the pin; heal a node ONLY when no compiler/train/gate job runs there): (1) dotnet: install-dotnet.ps1 -Version <box SDK> (new exact-version flag, throws unless that SDK lists after - channel default can move past the pin); (2) compiler pair: install-pack -FromUrls or guarded copy, defer if in-use guard trips; (3) deps clone: restore from a box tar at box HEAD, unlink junctions first via cmd /c rmdir. rustc self-heals via rust-toolchain.toml (report-only); zig = its shipper's. The ONE current real drift (moon dotnet rc.2) is already being healed by compiler's own queued moon job (step 2 = exact rc.3 install), so drift-watch auto-heal is for FUTURE drifts, not urgent. DoD remains MET via the alarm path; auto-heal is the beyond-DoD enhancement. Wait: when:quiet-node-window to implement+TEST the detect->heal trigger in node-drift-watch.ps1 safely (my groom: never ship untested toolchain-install-on-nodes); recipe now in hand.")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_36 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 36u32, "2026-11-10T15:11Z", "org3", "DRIFT-WATCH edge 2026-11-10 11:11 (state change): [DRIFT: wifi] -> [DRIFT: wifi UNREACHABLE: vultr] | drift-watch vultr: UNREACHABLE (no identity) | drift-watch ganymede [0fa5a15e-0766-47d2-9d1a-cc24f0cd20ea]: in-sync | drift-watch laptop [b4c8f166-3608-4028-8a75-4ad3cf12d95f]: DRIFT dotnet(box=11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148 node=11.0.100-rc.2.26504.105); zig(box=0.18.0-dev.738+ae9a8acc7 node=0.17.0)")
inl note_of_delegate_13_drift_watch_37 () = Note ("DELEGATE-13-DRIFT-WATCH", 37u32, "2026-11-10T22:33Z", "org3", "DRIFT-WATCH edge 2026-11-10 18:33 (state change): [DRIFT: wifi UNREACHABLE: vultr] -> [DRIFT: wifi] | drift-watch vultr-sjc [85944c7a-b987-4bf5-94a4-633c4af92c8f]: in-sync | drift-watch ganymede [0fa5a15e-0766-47d2-9d1a-cc24f0cd20ea]: in-sync | drift-watch laptop [b4c8f166-3608-4028-8a75-4ad3cf12d95f]: DRIFT dotnet(box=11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148 node=11.0.100-rc.2.26504.105); zig(box=0.18.0-dev.738+ae9a8acc7 node=0.17.0)")
