inl xdumps_timeline_nav () = Task ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", "Timeline navigation: direction toggle (oldest-first + scroll upward) + date start-from jump, bidirectional infinite scroll", Story, P2, D3, 85u32, Active, "", "team:org,management,ui", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xdumps_timeline_nav () = Planning ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xdumps_timeline_nav_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", 1u32, "2026-11-07T17:39Z", "x-dumps", "User 11-07: infinite scroll alone is not enough to navigate. Add (1) a direction toggle so you can start at the bottom/oldest and infinite-scroll UPWARD (newer), as well as top/newest-down; (2) a date \"start from\" input that seeks the merged cursor to that date and scrolls either direction. Touches timeline_serve (/timeline dir+from params, reversed feed_merge cursor seek by created_at) + timeline_page (scroll script fetches in the active direction; toggle + date UI). next: design the reversed cursor + from-date seek over feed_merge, add tests, gate on the sim notebook (coordinate with x who owns the gated files; run rule is Cells TESTS ONLY so land via gate). dod: user can pick a start date and a direction and infinite-scroll both ways without gaps/dupes, tests green.")
inl note_of_xdumps_timeline_nav_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", 2u32, "2026-11-07T19:05Z", "x-dumps", "Date start-from increment authored 11-07 (scratchpad/nav-draft/timeline_serve.spi on base A8BBFD705CAF + nav_from control in the ui-faithful timeline_page draft). SERVER: parse ?from=<date>; feeds are newest-first so per-feed seek offset = count of posts with created_at > (from++\"T9\") (lexical ISO bound incl the whole from-day); seeded() applies the seek only on the first page (empty cursor), continuations use the carried c= offsets + existing next-link/scroll. CLIENT: a <form method=get action=/timeline> with <input type=date name=from> + submit (pure HTML, no JS). So you pick a date and the timeline starts there and scrolls older (down) via the existing infinite scroll. next: the harder half = reverse direction (dir=up: start at oldest, scroll UP to newer) - needs an older_item comparator + reversed feeds + reverse-prepend scroll; defer until clean. budget-check running; both drafts rebase onto x final hashes then tests+gate+redeploy :30087. dod: pick a start date + direction and infinite-scroll both ways without gaps/dupes, tests green.")
inl note_of_xdumps_timeline_nav_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", 3u32, "2026-11-07T19:22Z", "x-dumps", "Server-side COMPLETE + validated 11-07 (nav-draft/timeline_serve.spi base A8BBFD705CAF): date start-from (seeded/from_of/seek_offsets) + bidirectional dir=up/down (dir_of/older_item/oriented/cmp_of/page_dir; next_link+page_html thread d=dir so continuations/scroll keep direction; seeded skips from-seek for up). Granular budget 0 over_budget, parses, signatures consistent. Client date-input in the ui-faithful timeline_page draft. REMAINING: reverse-scroll chat-style CSS (column-reverse) pending user UX confirm + a direction-toggle UI link. Pending x stable hashes -> rebase + tests + sim-gate + redeploy :30087.")
inl note_of_xdumps_timeline_nav_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", 4u32, "2026-11-07T19:56Z", "x-dumps", "LIVE + functionally verified 11-07 on :30087. timeline_serve applied (D226FBAC56BD; fixed seek_feed to erlang_term::text_at_least). VERIFIED: ?from=2020-06-01 seeks to 2020-06-01; ?d=up returns oldest-first (2017-01-15) vs newest default (2026-10-18); date-input + Newest/Oldest toggle render. Date start-from + direction toggle DELIVERED. REMAINING: chat-style reverse-scroll CSS (column-reverse) pending user UX confirm; formal rust gate (3 new cells staged) blocked by the spiral/apps/cells main.spi error. ~85%.")
inl note_of_xdumps_timeline_nav_5 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", 5u32, "2026-11-07T20:18Z", "x-dumps", "Handed timeline_serve 4C5108538B78 to x for the -d pass. Date start-from + direction toggle LIVE + verified (?from=2020-06-01->2020, ?d=up->2017-01-15, next-link threads d=up). REMAINING: reverse-scroll chat-style column-reverse CSS pending USER UX confirm (chat-style vs ascending; browser-untestable here so not shipping blind); formal tests-green = x -d-pass result.")
inl note_of_xdumps_timeline_nav_6 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TIMELINE-NAV", 6u32, "2026-11-07T22:19Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "INFINITE-SCROLL REPEAT BUG FIXED + DEPLOYED LIVE 11-07T22:2xZ (user: 'scroll repeating tweets when pressing end/scrolling fast'). ROOT CAUSE: two inconsistent selectors in the scroll JS. last() picked the DOM-last a[href^=/timeline?] (correctly the bottom next-link), but scroll_append did d.querySelector('a[href^=/timeline?]') = the FIRST match in the fetched page = the nav 'Oldest first' link (/timeline?d=up, which also starts with /timeline?). So after page 1, the sentinel href got set to /timeline?d=up and every further fetch reloaded that same oldest-first page => repeating tweets (worse on End/fast-scroll firing many more() calls). FIX: gave the next-link a distinct class=\"more\" and switched both last() and the fetched-page selector to 'a.more' (nav links are class=\"dir\", so no collision). timeline_serve.spi 4C5108538B78 -> 8AB01D598FE2 (timeline_page unchanged C7A0006B4A7B). Added regression cell the_next_link_and_scroll_target_the_more_class (asserts class=more + a.more present, href^= absent). Built+deployed via the same europa isolated build (HEAD + my 2 files, respell stashed). VERIFIED LIVE: next-link has class=more, scroll uses querySelector('a.more'), href^= gone; pagination advances cleanly c=0.0.0.0.50 -> 0.0.0.0.100, page2 older (18:02 vs 19:51), NO overlap; decode fix + d=up/from/video all intact.")
