inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 1u32, "2026-11-07T19:08Z", "compiler", "11-07 compiler: split from COMPILER-MEMO-DESIGN (candidate a). Measured: Cells' warm daemon took the sm' gate 537 -> 217 s; a cold lib-importing compile is 5.7-6.0 s, about 75% re-reading lib. DoD: the four clients reuse one warm process (spawned on demand, retired on core-hash change or idle), with before/after wall times on the same inputs, and byte-identical outputs. NEXT STEP: measure test.ps1 -Suite linked cold vs through a server-tcp session (it compiles every unit in a fresh process today), then factor the client into test.ps1 first. typefeatureset plan: none new.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 2u32, "2026-11-08T04:07Z", "compiler", "11-08 00:1x compiler: CLIENT MAP (read at the live tree): (1) spiral/apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 runs the consumer gate as one COLD 'dotnet <compiler> --backend Rust' per consumer (line 210) and type_probe.ps1 as separate processes; only document_test goes through the Cells daemon (warm). (2) apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1 -Suite linked runs one cold process per unit (line ~145) and depends on each compile's own stderr for Warns/NoWarns, which a server-tcp session sends to the SERVER's stderr. (3) kit's release-train pins a DLL copy (release-train.ps1:51-59); its regen path is kit's to map. PREREQUISITE found: a per-request diagnostics channel in the server protocol: an opt-in request field (e.g. a trailing 'warnings') that makes the host capture Console.Error for that request (one request at a time per session, so a scoped Console.SetError is safe) and send 'spiral-session<TAB>warning<TAB><text>' lines before the ok/error line; opt-in because the Cells daemon (compiler_daemon.ex:846) parses the first reply line as ok/error. ORDER: S1 the warning channel (host, after pack63), S2 test.ps1 linked through one server per run (measure cold vs warm on the same rows), S3 lib_land_window's consumer gate, S4 ask kit about regen. NEXT STEP: draft S1 as a host kitdo after the morning pack63 install.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 3u32, "2026-11-08T04:09Z", "compiler", "11-08 00:0x compiler: S1 DRAFTED (kit\\drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS\\1-server-warning-channel.kitdo, 2 replacements over pack62's host): a server-tcp request whose last field is 'warnings' has its compile's Console.Error captured (TextWriter.Synchronized, restored in finally; one request at a time per session) and its 'warning:' lines sent as 'spiral-session<TAB>warning<TAB><text>' BEFORE the ok/error line; requests without the field are byte-for-byte unchanged, so the Cells daemon is unaffected. NEXT STEP: gate it with pack63's follow-up pack, then S2 (test.ps1 linked through one server per run, Warns/NoWarns read from the warning lines).")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T06:18Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:2x compiler: S1 (server-tcp per-request warnings channel) REBASED: it applies cleanly over pack66's host (pack65 dialect + census edits), and is now FOLDED INTO pack66 (host 74b08e7b, core 2d2d13ac), restaged on ganymede before job-1794204862068 runs, so it is built and checked with pack66. Caveat recorded for S2: Console.SetError is process-wide, so two concurrent sessions in ONE server could interleave captured warnings; S2 must run one session per server, as test.ps1 linked does, or move to a per-request diagnostic sink in the core. Next step: S2, test.ps1 -Suite linked through one server-tcp session per run, reading Warns/NoWarns from the spiral-session warning lines, measured cold vs warm on the same 20 cases.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T06:20Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:3x compiler: S2 DRAFTED (unstaged, apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1 linked suite): with SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM=1 a linked case compiles all its units in dependency order in ONE warm process via the host's existing --batch jobs.tsv/results.tsv mode (absolute entry paths, per-unit status from results.tsv, warnings from the batch stderr log for Warns/NoWarns); the default stays the cold per-unit path, so the change is opt-in until the A/B proves it. This avoids needing S1's server channel for test.ps1 (S1 stays for kit regen and lib_land consumer gates, which keep a server across many cases). QUEUED: ganymede job-1794205228949-compiler-linked-warm-ab, three arms cold / warm / cold2: verdicts, wall time, and every generated unit file (rs/zig/gleam) hash-compared cold vs warm. Next step: if the outputs are identical and warm is faster, make warm the default and record the before/after.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T07:03Z", "compiler", "11-09 03:0x compiler: S2 A/B RESULT (ganymede, pack64, -Suite linked, 21 rows): cold 230 s, warm 103 s, cold2 147 s (host load varied; warm about 1.4-2.2x faster); verdicts identical in all arms (8 pass, 13 fail). The 13 Linux failures are a test.ps1 bug, not compiler: the rustc --extern path was joined with a backslash, so extern location does not exist on Linux; FIXED with Join-Path (unstaged). OUTPUTS: cold vs cold2 byte-identical, but warm differs in ONE case (linked_rust_list_over_model app.rs/render.rs): only the ORDER of names in use model::{...}, because codegenRust builds the linked-import list in a process-state-dependent order. FIX DRAFTED: 2-sort-rust-linked-uses.kitdo (sort unit groups and names), applies over pack66; it changes linked Rust residual text once, to a deterministic order. Warm stays OPT-IN until that fix is installed and the A/B is byte-identical.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T07:05Z", "compiler", "11-09 03:0x compiler: pack67 = pack66 + 2-sort-rust-linked-uses (core 777c218a, host 74b08e7b) STAGED on ganymede as chain3 (starts when chain2 = CLI proof + pack66 gate is done): Linux build in a private cache, then -Suite linked COLD vs WARM with the fixed test.ps1 (Join-Path extern path), hashing every generated unit file. Pass condition for making warm the default: 21/21 rows, cold vs warm byte-identical. Next step: read chain3; if identical, flip test.ps1 linked to warm by default (keep SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM=0 as the cold escape) and record the before/after wall.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 8u32, "2026-11-09T07:23Z", "compiler", "pack67 (pack66 + 2-sort-rust-linked-uses) A/B on ganymede 2026-11-09 07:06-07:12Z, core 777c218a host 74b08e7b: -Suite linked cold wall 146s vs warm (SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM=1) 100s = 1.46x; generated linked unit files cold vs warm BYTE-IDENTICAL (34 files, sha256 lists equal) -- the nondeterministic use-order is fixed by sorting units + names. Both arms 18/21 pass; the 3 fails are Zig build-fail exit 13 (linked_records, linked_union, linked_zig_alloc_export) on zig 0.18.0-dev.738, pre-existing in the pack64 baseline (LINKED-UNITS-ZIG). Next: roll pack67 out (Linux via oort now; win-x64 pair on moon after TRAIN42 + rc.3 SDK), then flip test.ps1 warm to default once the installed compiler sorts.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 9u32, "2026-11-09T07:50Z", "compiler", "pack67 ROLLOUT linux-x64 DONE 11-09 07:47-07:49Z: oort pair key compiler/pack/v1/core-777c218a.../host-74b08e7b.../sdk-11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148/rid-linux-x64 put + verified round-trip; installed (in-use guard clean, prior pair backed up under compiler-installs/pre-pack67-*) on ganymede and europa (= the vultr VM, same host): SpiralCompiler 3b1da458, Core 1ff0ea21; smoke compile ok. PENDING: win-x64 pair on moon after TRAIN42 (job-1794209289968-kit-TRAIN42) + moon cache SDK rc.2 -> rc.3, then box -FromStore and moon install; then tell microblog (edition years) and flip SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM default.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 10u32, "2026-11-09T09:32Z", "compiler", "moon post-TRAIN42 job STAGED (C:\\home\\remote-stage\\moon-post\\post-train.ps1, not yet submitted): (1) the timed scaling window (its own CPU<15%-for-2-min quiet gate, so it waits out org2-lib3-landproof if that overlaps); (2) moon cache SDK pinned EXACTLY to 11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148 via dotnet-install -Version (install-dotnet.ps1 takes the newest preview, which may already be past the fleet pin); (3) the pack67 win-x64 pair from the byte-identical pack67 sources (core 777c218a, host 74b08e7b) in a private cache. Then: oort put win-x64, box install-pack -FromStore, moon copy-install with the in-use guard, flip SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM default, tell microblog. Submit on rig TRAIN42c DONE.")
