inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_14 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 14u32, "2026-11-09T11:34Z", "compiler", "11-09 11:4x compiler: client 2 of 4 WIRED (opt-in): apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 consumer gate runs every -Consumer through ONE `--batch` process when SPIRAL_LAND_WARM=1 (same per-consumer report lines; default stays the cold per-consumer loop; unstaged). A/B on ganymede (installed pack73b, load ~9): 3 consumers (apps/spiral/spiral.spi, apps/lisp/spl2spi.spi, apps/transformer/transformer.spi) -> cold one-process-each 123.5 s vs one warm batch 64.2 s = 1.92x, all 3 .rs outputs BYTE-IDENTICAL. Client 1 (test.ps1 -Suite linked) proven 11-09 (1.46x, identical); its default flips with the Windows pack73b install. Remaining: kit regen (rig, kit code) and the 4th client named in the DoD. Wait: job wifi:TRAIN42e (moon pair -> box/moon install -> flip linked warm default).")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_15 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 15u32, "2026-11-09T12:00Z", "compiler", "pack75 ASSEMBLED as the rollout target if its gate is green before moon frees (else pack73b ships first): core de5db728, host 79070d91 = box live (c2db952e / bd09b4f1) + 14 programs IN ORDER (kit drafts spiral/): DIALECT-IDENTITY/1-dialect-and-edition-year-fields, TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG/1-features-out, COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS/1-server-warning-channel, COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS/2-sort-rust-linked-uses, TS-TYPEFEATURESET-PROBES/1-types-out, TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG/2-count-project-modules, C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV/1-null-safe-incref, TS-TYPEFEATURESET-PROBES/2-gadt-encoding, REC-MARKER-INFER/3-infer-mutual-groups, TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD/3-lazy-fold-over-pack73b, FORMATTER-PRE-HOPAC-AUDIT/6-fails-clause-as-written, PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS/1-keyword-as-name, TS-TYPEFEATURESET-PROBES/3-bool-literal-no-narrowing, LINK-WITHOUT-MANIFEST/1-derived-links-flag. Candidate dirs staged: box %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack75\\source, moon C:\\home\\remote-stage\\moon-post\\*.p75.fs. Gate staged on ganymede (~/remote-stage/pack75/p75.sh). Wait: job ganymede:pack75 gate.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_16 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 16u32, "2026-11-09T12:24Z", "compiler", "pack75 GATED GREEN + LINUX ROLLOUT DONE (11-09 12:24Z): -Suite all vs pack73: 7606 rows, compile-status diffs 0, residual diffs 89 (TypeScript only = the expected bool-literal `as boolean`), new rows only keyword_as_local_name_negative; fixtures (REC x4, c_array slot 42, keyword message), format keeps fails headers, tstypes 3/3; tibia probe3 green on ta3b. oort put linux-x64 OK (round-trip verified). Installed with guard on europa (12:23:53Z) and ganymede (12:23:57Z): SpiralCompiler c51a27a4 / Core 830bada0, rollback points pre-pack75-*. Windows: moon post-train job now builds the pack75 win-x64 pair (sources staged). Wait: job wifi:TRAIN42e.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_17 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 17u32, "2026-11-09T14:18Z", "compiler", "ROLLOUT TARGET -> pack77 (11-09 14:1xZ): core 2cc4470f, host 79070d91 = pack75 + TS-TYPEFEATURESET-PROBES/4-reserved-word-names + ZIG-OUTPUT-SIZE-BLOWUP/1-outline-large-arms (default 400 binds, C+Zig). Gates: pack76 vs pack75 0/0, pack77 vs pack76 7610 rows 0/0; outlining stress 0 exit/stdout diffs. Box re-derivation list = the 14 programs of note 15 + those 2, in that order (16). oort put linux-x64 OK; INSTALLED with guard on europa + ganymede (SpiralCompilerCore 9ef0395b; rollback pre-pack77-*). Moon post-train staged for the pack77 win-x64 pair (p77 sources, cache77); box candidate %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack77\\source. Wait: train:TRAIN42e.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_18 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 18u32, "2026-11-09T19:30Z", "compiler", "ROLLOUT TARGET -> pack78 (11-09 19:3xZ): core 1f2c48f6, host 79070d91 = pack77 (16 programs) + FORMATTER-TAB-LINES/1-check-reports-tab-kept-lines.kitdo (17 programs, in that order). Gate: -Suite all vs pack77, 7610 rows, 0 compile-status / 0 residual diffs. oort put linux-x64 OK; INSTALLED with guard on europa + ganymede (SpiralCompilerCore 3ab85d76; ganymede first refused while another lanes --resolve-manifest was running, then installed; rollback pre-pack78-*). Moon post-train re-staged for the pack78 win-x64 pair (p78 sources verified on moon, cache78); box candidate %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack78\\source. Wait: train:TRAIN42e.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_19 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 19u32, "2026-11-09T21:38Z", "compiler", "pack78 FLEET-WIDE 11-09 21:3xZ (core 1f2c48f6, host 79070d91, 17 programs). ganymede + europa: linux-x64 ReadyToRun pair (Core 3ab85d76). MOON: win-x64 pair built on moon (job-1794258111432, exit 0, private rc.3 SDK via SPIRAL_DOTNET in moon-post\\dotnet-rc3, shared toolchain untouched under fiscals gate; moons shared runtime already had rc.3), guarded copy-install: SpiralCompiler 99eadcd9 / Core f4148639, launch check True. BOX: install-pack -FromStore reproduced the candidate (live c2db952e + 17 programs -> 1f2c48f6/79070d91), then a guarded copy of the SAME final pair as moon (99eadcd9 / f4148639, launch True; rollback pre-pack78r2r-*). STORE CAVEAT: the oort pack78 win-x64 entry holds the IL-only pair (8e0be9fa / 1bec06f0), because I fetched at 17:19 between build.ps1s IL build and its in-place ReadyToRun step (17:29-17:30); oort keys are immutable (rclone --immutable), so it stays: valid, same reviewed sources, not precompiled (slower start). Lesson: fetch only after the job exits and check Test-ReadyToRunImage before oort put. The timed scaling window did NOT run (moon not quiet); still pending. SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM default NOT flipped: it needs a post-install byte-identical warm A/B first.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_20 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 20u32, "2026-11-09T21:59Z", "compiler", "11-09 17:5x local, TWO things. (1) FIX of my pack78 Windows install: org2 found the boxs lib_land_window round trip failing with Method not found ListModule.emptyListError. Cause: the pair was built with moons rc.3 SDK, which bundles a NEWER FSharp.Core (49b00056) with that method, but my copy-installs (box + moon) replaced ONLY SpiralCompiler(Core).dll and kept the older FSharp.Core (c235edbd). Both report assembly version 11.0.0.0, and --capabilities never hits the method, so the launch check passed. FIXED: box + moon now carry the builds complete 35-file set (0 mismatches after copy), and the guard now runs a REAL smoke (--check lib/spiral/process.spi --timeout-ms 300000, exit 0) with whole-bin rollback; backups pre-pack78full-*. Linux unaffected (installed FSharp.Core = builds, 631d3ddb). (2) SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM DEFAULT FLIPPED in test.ps1 (unstaged; warm unless SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM=0), after the byte-identical A/B on installed pack78 (ganymede, -Suite linked, 21 rows): 0 compile / native / exit / stdout / residual diffs; cold 131 s, warm 85 s (1.54x). Both arms exit 1 on the same failing rows (verdicts identical).")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_21 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 21u32, "2026-11-10T10:37Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:3x compiler (groom with fiscal; rig mapped TRAIN42e to TRAIN43f \"or clear if no train is needed\"): CLEARED, not re-pointed. This item never needed a rig train: the wait stood for its pack content reaching the Windows hosts, and pack78 (containing pack67-pack77) is installed on all four nodes (box/moon Core f4148639; Linux now pack82 Core c495bc57). The warm linked default is flipped (unstaged test.ps1). Next step: the remaining DoD measurement on ganymede, then close.")
inl note_of_compiler_warm_clients_22 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS", 22u32, "2026-11-10T11:01Z", "compiler", "11-10 07:1x compiler: SPLIT by client, because three of the four DoD clients are other lanes tools. Done here: test.ps1 -Suite linked warm by default (1.54x, byte-identical). Children: WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT (compiler, light), WARM-CLIENT-KIT-REGEN (rig), WARM-CLIENT-LIB-LAND-WINDOW (microblog), WARM-CLIENT-NODE-PROOF (fiscal), each carrying the proven pattern and the same DoD. This parent closes when its children do.")
