inl note_of_cells_md_on_lib_1 () = Note ("CELLS-MD-ON-LIB", 1u32, "2026-11-07T20:26Z", "main", "main 11-07 (child of HTML-MD-SVG-DEDUP). spiral/apps/cells/spi/html_markdown.spi (126 lines: own inline parser, renderer and escape) is a third markdown implementation. Once HTML-MD-PARSER-TO-LIB lands, Cells renders through lib doc_parse + doc_render + markup.escape. DoD: html_markdown.spi deleted or reduced to a call; Cells html/notebook render tests byte-identical, or every difference listed and accepted; the ELIXIR ratchet does not grow. Next step: diff html_markdown.spi's output against lib doc_render on Cells' own markdown fixtures, to measure the gap before switching. TypeFeatures: typed blocks instead of string pieces.")
inl note_of_cells_md_on_lib_2 () = Note ("CELLS-MD-ON-LIB", 2u32, "2026-11-08T05:19Z", "x-b7595ac3", "2026-11-08 01:2x microblog (ex x): NEXT STEP DONE, the gap measured. Harness (scratchpad mddiff, box, pack61b): a Spiral package with a copy of Cells html_markdown.spi beside lib doc_parse + doc_render + markup.markup_text, compiled to Gleam and run on the BEAM over 8 fixtures. SAME on 3: Cells' own test string (heading, inline code, link, list, fenced code, paragraph), escaping of < > & quotes, and paragraph breaks. DIFF on 5, each a feature the lib has and Cells lacks: **bold** -> <strong>; '1. one\\n2. two' -> <ol>; pipe tables -> <table>; ![img](p.png) -> <img> (Cells emitted !<a>); a fenced block's language is kept. Neither renders *em*. So switching Cells to the lib only adds features: Cells' pinned test output is byte-identical. NEXT STEP: replace html_markdown::markdown's body with markup_text (blocks_html (parse_markdown s)), delete the 120 lines of the private parser, and keep Cells' test as the regression.")
inl note_of_cells_md_on_lib_3 () = Note ("CELLS-MD-ON-LIB", 3u32, "2026-11-09T05:15Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 SWITCHED (spiral tree, unstaged): apps/cells/spi/html_markdown.spi went from 133 lines (a private inline parser, block state machine and escape) to markdown = markup::markup_text (doc_render::blocks_html (doc_parse::parse_markdown source)), plus its pinned gleam test kept as the regression. The 11-08 harness measured that test's output byte-identical through the lib path (the lib only adds bold, ol, tables, img and fence language). Caller: main.spi export markdown_html (unchanged). Proof queued: job-1794200929269-cells-md-gate on moon (mirror cellsmd1, file D4CD3F78D7A8 hash-pinned), notebook --gate html_markdown.spi. The Cells Gleam domain beam (main.gleam) picks it up on the next domain build; the notebook render tests in the next full Cells suite close the DoD.")
inl note_of_cells_md_on_lib_4 () = Note ("CELLS-MD-ON-LIB", 4u32, "2026-11-09T08:45Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 file gate GREEN: job-1794212718688-microblog-head2 step cells-md-gate (run cells-md-gate-20261109043616, mirror cellsmd1, html_markdown.spi D4CD3F78D7A8): its pinned gleam test passes 1/1 through lib doc_parse/doc_render/markup, which proves the 11-08 'byte-identical' measurement. DoD left: Cells' html/notebook render tests in the next full Cells suite (they exercise main.spi's markdown_html export through the rebuilt domain).")
inl note_of_cells_md_on_lib_5 () = Note ("CELLS-MD-ON-LIB", 5u32, "2026-11-09T11:34Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "Wait: job moon:job-1794221637538-x-verify-client-r2")
inl blog_blocks_on_lib () = Task ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", "blog renders its post blocks through lib doc_render (Heading/Paragraph/Code/Table) instead of its own string concatenation", TaskKind, P3, D3, 35u32, Planned, "HTML-MD-SVG-DEDUP", "blog,markdown,dedup,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_blog_blocks_on_lib () = Planning ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_blog_blocks_on_lib_1 () = Note ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", 1u32, "2026-11-07T20:26Z", "main", "main 11-07 (child of HTML-MD-SVG-DEDUP). blog engine/post.spi renders its own block union (Heading, Paragraph, Code, Terminal, Table, Note) by string concatenation. Heading/Paragraph/Code/Table map onto lib doc_blocks + doc_render (code_html, table_html); Terminal and Note have no lib case. DoD: blog renders through doc_render; Terminal/Note either become lib block cases (if html or Cells can use them) or stay blog-local with the reason in a note; blog's rss/style/post tests and the generated site byte-identical, or the differences listed. Next step: compare blog's render_block output with doc_render for the four overlapping cases on the showcase post. TypeFeatures: blog's posts are written as typed doc_blocks values.")
inl note_of_blog_blocks_on_lib_2 () = Note ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", 2u32, "2026-11-07T21:07Z", "main", "main 11-07 17:2x MEASURED (blog engine/post.spi render_block vs lib doc_render.block_html), case by case:\n- Heading: blog `<h2>` from plain text; lib level-tagged, inline-markdown content, trailing \"\\n\".\n- Paragraph: blog plain escaped text; lib inline markdown + \"\\n\".\n- Code: blog `<pre><code class=\"language-X\">`; lib CodeBlock has NO language field (`<pre><code>` + lines).\n- Table: blog has no newlines and no alignment; lib newline-separated, align attributes.\n- Rule: blog `<hr class=\"section-rule\">`; lib `<hr>\\n`.\n- Terminal, Note: no lib case.\nSo byte-identity is impossible without lib changes. PROPOSED (decide in the work, not now):\n(a) lib CodeBlock gains an optional language (doc_blocks change; html's renderer then emits the class when present, since html's own markdown fences carry a language too);\n(b) Terminal and Note stay blog-local blocks rendered around lib markup;\n(c) the blog accepts lib's newline layout and plain `<hr>` (style.css targets hr instead of .section-rule), and blog's post tests are updated to lib output.\nNext step: (a) as a draft, with html --self-test showing no change for language-less fences.")
inl note_of_blog_blocks_on_lib_3 () = Note ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", 3u32, "2026-11-07T22:03Z", "main", "main 11-07 18:1x: step (a) is IN A LAND WINDOW now (lib CodeBlock gains a language, `CodeBlock : string * list string` with \"\" = none; doc_parse captures the fence language; doc_render emits class=\"language-X\" only when non-empty, so language-less fences render unchanged). The blog switch itself (b + c) changes the user's visible site HTML (heading levels, newline layout, plain <hr>), so per the sample-first rule it waits for the user to see a before/after of one post page. resume when: the user approves a sample diff of posts/showcase rendered both ways.")
inl note_of_blog_blocks_on_lib_4 () = Note ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", 4u32, "2026-11-07T22:21Z", "main", "main 11-07 18:2x SAMPLE for the user's decision, from posts/showcase.spi blocks; BEFORE = blog render_block, AFTER = lib doc_render (both read from the code):\n- Heading \"Text\": BEFORE `<h2>Text</h2>` (the site adds a section anchor + TOC entry); AFTER `<h2>Text</h2>\\n`, with NO anchor/TOC support in lib -> a FEATURE LOSS unless lib heading_html gains an id.\n- Paragraph \"Paragraphs escape their text, so <tags> & ampersands print as written.\": the same visible text either way (`&lt;tags&gt; &amp;`); AFTER, inline markdown is parsed, so a `*` or backtick in a paragraph would become emphasis/code.\n- Code (\"spiral\", ...): BEFORE `<pre><code class=\"language-spiral\">...`; AFTER the same once code-block-language lands (now in its window).\n- Table: BEFORE one line `<table><thead><tr><th>...`; AFTER newline-separated, with alignment attributes.\n- Rule: BEFORE `<hr class=\"section-rule\">`; AFTER `<hr>\\n` (style.css would target hr).\n- Note, Terminal: blog-local either way.\nRECOMMENDATION: keep blog's Heading (anchors + TOC are blog features), Note and Terminal blog-local; route Paragraph/Code/Table through lib. Or first give lib headings an optional anchor id, then route them too. Waiting for the user's pick.")
inl note_of_blog_blocks_on_lib_5 () = Note ("BLOG-BLOCKS-ON-LIB", 5u32, "2026-11-07T23:25Z", "main", "main 11-07 19:2x step (a) LANDED, proof: green. lib_land_window code-block-language closed green (undo 20261107-191156): doc_blocks.spi 1D39D3640E04 (`CodeBlock : string * list string`, language first, \"\" = none), doc_parse.spi E01DC62B918F (the fence line captures its language; new test a_fence_keeps_its_language), doc_render.spi 9D261664FAE3 (emits class=\"language-X\", escaped, only when non-empty, so language-less fences render unchanged); respell drift 0. An html rebuild on europa is running to refresh html's generated .rs. Step (b)+(c) still wait for the user's pick of the sample (note 4).")
