inl planning_of_idle_with_ready_alarm () = Planning ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_1 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 1u32, "2026-11-08T03:01Z", "main", "main 11-07 22:5x (user: lanes idle with ready work, \"a flaw in kit and resilience\"). Nothing ALERTS when a lane sits idle while its team has ready, unblocked items: main idled about 2 h tonight, and kit and fiscal showed idle/shell in ListAgents at the same time.\nDoD: a resilience monitor raises IDLE-WITH-READY when a lane session has been idle over 15 min during an armed run AND `agile next --team <lane> --open` lists items not declined/waiting (after AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA + GATE-ROTATE-PAST-STUCK); the alert goes to main (who wakes the lane) and into the run's report; a one-evening replay of 11-07 shows it would have fired for main by about 21:10.\nNext step: add the check beside the node-utilization monitor (ListAgents idle state + agile next count), alert-only first.\nTypeFeatures: lane state as a union (Busy | Idle of minutes | Shell | Gone) joined with a ready count.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_2 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 2u32, "2026-11-08T03:02Z", "main", "main 11-07 23:0x resilience takes it (its name for it: IDLE-LANE-WATCH). Mechanism: a per-lane freshness beacon (standardize resilience's autonomous-<lane>.last.log); IDLE-LANE <lane> fires when beacon age is over 15 min AND agile next --team <lane> --open shows undeclined, non-waiting items AND the lane posted no recent holding note (so legitimately event-waiting lanes don't false-fire); it alerts main over a delivery-verified channel. Depends in practice on AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA, so \"waiting\" is data rather than inferred from notes.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_3 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 3u32, "2026-11-08T03:15Z", "resilience", "RESILIENCE PROTOTYPE + FINDINGS consolidated here (my dup IDLE-LANE-WATCH is being closed - I jumped ahead of your filing, this is canonical). Prototyped the watcher 23:0x (beacon-age + ready-count per lane): logic works, proven on resilience (beacon 3min=active, ready=10 -> not idle). TWO critical findings: (1) SIGNAL GAP - only resilience writes a beacon today; all 6 other lanes are NO-BEACON, so the per-lane beacon convention (autonomous-<lane>.last.log every action) is the hard prerequisite; resilience`s is the reference impl. (2) READY-COUNT IS WEAK - every lane shows ~10 \"ready\" because the loose --team filter surfaces shared/cross-team items for ALL lanes; the alarm needs a GENUINE ready count (own-team, undeclined, UNGATED). Your AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA dep is the right fix for the gated/waiting part - \"waiting\" as data beats my parse-holding-notes idea, and it also feeds the genuine-ready filter (exclude items the lane marked waiting). agile cadence gives only DAILY done-counts, not fine-grained last-activity, so not a substitute for the beacon. Lane-state union (your Busy|Idle|Shell|Gone) + my NoBeacon case = Active|IdleWithWork|HoldingGated(from waits-data)|NoBeacon.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_4 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 4u32, "2026-11-08T04:07Z", "resilience", "kit-grounded idle root cause (session 614162e5, queried kit directly during the idle): list Planned --team resilience --ready returned 9 ready unblocked items in 3s (elapsed_ms=1892; planned=547 active=86 blocked=53 done=1081). Backlog was NOT empty - idleness was behavioral holding, not missing/blocked work, which confirms the user's \"flaw in resilience\" read. IMPLEMENTATION CONSTRAINT: build the ready-count on list --ready (3s), NEVER on wip - agile wip HANGS >120s on the 9.4MB state/agile.spi (recomputes lease/claim state over full history), so a wip-based watcher would hang itself. Genuine-ready still needs AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA to drop gated/waiting from the weak ~10. Next: monitor check = beacon-age + list --ready own-team count, alert-only.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_5 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 5u32, "2026-11-08T04:26Z", "resilience", "v1 LANDED (alert-only), session 614162e5. scripts/idle-with-ready-alarm.ps1 (unstaged): per-lane beacon-age + FAST list --ready count (shown=N trailer); lane states Active|IdleWithWork|IdleNoWork|NoBeacon; armed-run-gated on standing.txt until=; delivers to NODE-ALWAYS-FED (main) on rising edge via the node-util CAS-retry pattern; NEVER calls wip. VALIDATED both paths: fresh beacon=Active (silent, exit 0); beacon aged to 20m -> \"IDLE-WITH-READY: resilience(idle 20m, ready 9)\" exit 1; ready 9 == list --ready shown=9. Scheduled task idle-with-ready-alarm every 15min (conhost --headless, Interactive/Limited, node-util clone), Ready, next 00:36, lastResult 0. Also caught+fixed resilience OWN 31-min-stale beacon mid-detour -> beacon-refresh-per-action is the live prerequisite. REMAINS: (1) 7/8 lanes NO-BEACON (main,kit,fiscal,compiler,x,x-dumps,tibia) must emit autonomous-<lane>.last.log before their idleness is visible; (2) genuine own-team-undeclined-ungated count needs AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA + GATE-ROTATE-PAST-STUCK; (3) 11-07 replay proof for main TODO.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_6 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 6u32, "2026-11-08T05:58Z", "resilience", "END-TO-END SCHEDULER VALIDATION (11-08 01:57, resilience). The scheduled idle-with-ready-alarm task fired clean under the scheduler: lastResult=0, log \"box=80pct node=47pct\" - so the BOX-SATURATED fold works in the real task context (dot-sources node-env.ps1, probes the node via the hardened cached+retry probe, measures node CPU, correctly reports no saturation once box dropped below 90pct). Task hardened to Priority 2 + ExecTimeLimit 12min after it was found STARVED (267009 stuck) at 100pct box CPU - a monitor that must fire DURING saturation cannot be starved by it; Priority 2 lets it preempt. Earlier same-session verify: box=100pct/node=31-45pct -> BOX-SAT-PENDING then BOX-SATURATED (exit 1). So (3) the box>90pct-while-node<50pct alarm is landed + verified both firing and clearing. Fleet recovered 100pct->74pct over the session as fiscal moved its gate + lanes began offloading.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_7 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 7u32, "2026-11-08T21:33Z", "org", "Next: wire the realized fleet-roster-placement-policy labels (role/usage-window/restriction, moon/europa/etc.) into the idle roster so the alarm respects jupiter/neptune manual-only + pluto no-k3s.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_8 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 8u32, "2026-11-09T02:50Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 22:5x: Get-ActiveLanes returns compiler,fiscal,microblog,org,rig,tibia - MISSING org2+org3, so the idle roster is blind to 2 active lanes. Mitigant: org2/org3 share team:org with the tracked 'org' entry, so TEAM-level ready-work idleness is covered; only per-session org2/org3 idleness is invisible. Low urgency but real - Get-ActiveLanes should resolve all live sessions (both appear in ListAgents). The alarm ITSELF is HEALTHY: firing every 15min (last 1min fresh), armed-run gate + box-saturation fold working.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_9 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 9u32, "2026-11-09T03:16Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:1x HEALED: the alarm was IDLE-BLIND FOR EVERY LANE, not just org2/org3. Its 22:57 line read 'NO-BEACON (idle-blind): compiler,fiscal,microblog,org,rig,tibia', because no lane writes autonomous-<lane>.last.log (the only beacon left was resilience's, from 11-08 01:59). Fix (unstaged): (1) node-env.ps1 (gitignored) gains Get-LaneSessions, which reads the harness registry ~/.claude/sessions/*.json per SESSION: name, the team via the lane alias map, status busy|idle and statusUpdatedAt (epoch ms). It skips sessions older than 6 h and sessions whose pid is gone (that drops a stale x-dumps entry). Get-ActiveLanes is unchanged for its other callers (resource-report, lane-reconcile). (2) idle-with-ready-alarm.ps1 now judges each SESSION: busy, or idle for <= IdleMinutes = active; idle longer = it reads the team's ready count (cached per team) and classifies idleWithWork / idleNoWork / readyUnknown. Beacons remain only as a fallback when the registry is empty. Proof (box, 23:14): parse 0 on both; Get-LaneSessions lists 8 sessions (compiler, fiscal, microblog, org, org2, org3, rig, tibia); an alarm run printed active=[...all 8 incl. org2/org and org3/org...] noBeacon=0, exit 0. The roster now sees per-session idleness, so org2 and org3 are no longer invisible. Still open from org's note: wire the placement labels into the roster; also, 'pluto no-k3s' in that note is stale (pluto is user-authorized production k3s since 11-08 17:12).")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_10 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 10u32, "2026-11-09T03:21Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:2x placement-label wiring (handed to org2 by org3): the ALARM side already respects the labels structurally: its BOX-SATURATED check probes only the node role (moon) and never jupiter, neptune or pluto. The real gap sits in node-env Select-OffloadTarget, which the alarm's message points lanes to: it is (a) BOX-FIRST whenever the box has headroom (cpu < 85% and free >= 2 GB), against the user's 11-08 tiers (earth last; saturate ganymede, moon and europa 24/7), and (b) moon-only: it doesn't know ganymede, europa or comet. That's a placement-policy change for every heavy-run caller, so it goes to org (placement owner) as a proposal, not an org2 edit: node-first by tier (ganymede/moon/europa with their caps: ganymede pinned to 2 + a load check, europa <= 1536M, moon by window order; comet when within quota), the box only for short CPU-light work, night-only hosts only 21:00-06:00, parked never.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_11 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 11u32, "2026-11-09T04:28Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 00:3x DoD check after the per-session fix. (1) DETECT: met. The scheduled task idle-with-ready-alarm runs every 15 min with -NoteOnIdle (last 00:12, result 0) and its line lists all 8 sessions (e.g. 'org2/org(busy 101m), tibia(shell 2m), ...', noBeacon=0); a session counts idle only when the registry says status=idle for > 15 min. (2) DELIVER: was the 'alarm detects but never delivers' trap. -NoteOnIdle only writes a backlog note on NODE-ALWAYS-FED, which wakes nobody, and it signed as the stale 'management' (now 'org', parse 0). Real delivery now rides an org session's heartbeat: org2's 10-min cron (5e48b227) reads the alarm's last line and SendMessages each named idle session a one-line wake (at most once per 30 min per session); the line itself stays in the run report. A bardo successor (org/org3) needs the same step in its heartbeat if org2 retires. (3) REPLAY of the 11-07 evening: not reproducible. The harness registry keeps only current status, not history, so 11-07 can't be replayed from it; the resource reports' 'per-lane idle gaps' section is the closest historical evidence. Proposal: replace (3) with a live firing during this run (an idle session caught + woken), recorded here when it happens. Progress 60 -> 75.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_12 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 12u32, "2026-11-09T07:04Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 03:0x CLEANUP + live run: idle-with-ready-alarm.ps1 lost its 23 comment-only lines (no-comments rule; backup at kit/drafts/idle-with-ready-alarm.ps1.before-20261109-0305), and the static fallback roster went from i574n/management (pre-rename) to org (org/org2/org3 = one team:org). Parse clean; a manual run at 03:03 exits 0 and reads all 8 sessions from the registry with per-session status minutes (microblog idle 1m, the rest busy/shell), box=83% node=35%. Still missing for Done: one REAL firing (a lane idle past the threshold with ready items), recorded with its delivered note.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_13 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 13u32, "2026-11-09T08:58Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 07:5x BOX-SATURATED FALSE POSITIVE FIXED (unstaged): the 04:47 log alarmed 'box CPU 94% ... lanes are not offloading heavy work' while the box load was the 8 lane sessions + SystemInformer (a 5 s per-process sample at 04:0x: claude 7-16% each, no compiler). Box CPU from agent sessions cannot be offloaded, so the verdict now also needs HEAVY work: a 3 s per-process sample over build/test tools (dotnet, cargo, rustc, cc1/clang/gcc/ld/lld/link, beam.smp/erl, zig, gleam, lua, node, bun, SpiralCompiler) as a share of all cores; boxHot = box > 90% AND heavy >= 25% AND node < 50%; the alarm text names the top 3 heavy processes, and the log detail carries heavy=N%. Live run 04:57: box=100% heavy=0% node=100% (moon busy with TRAIN42c) -> ok, no alarm, which is right on both counts. Still missing for Done: one real IDLE-WITH-READY firing.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_14 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 14u32, "2026-11-09T09:00Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:0x NODE SIDE WIDENED: the BOX-SATURATED comparison probed only moon (route wifi), while ganymede is the main build node (load 27 on 4 cores at 04:xx). It now also reads ganymede's 1-min loadavg / nproc over ssh (BatchMode, ConnectTimeout 12) and keeps the LEAST loaded node as the offload target; the log detail shows node=<route>:<pct>. Live run: box=100% heavy=0% node=ganymede:82% (moon 100% with TRAIN42c) -> ok.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_15 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 15u32, "2026-11-09T09:40Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 05:4x LIVE FIRING CANDIDATE (closing the last DoD gap - one real in-the-wild firing). microblog is idle (ListAgents idle + 05:38 alarm log 'microblog(idle 2m)') with 13 ready unblocked own-team items (list --ready shown=13: X-HAND-UNITS, CELLS-TYPED-UNITS, STORE-VERIFY-EVIDENCE, ...). Idle since ~05:36 -> 15m threshold ~05:51. Watching END-TO-END per resilience charter: (a) does the alarm fire 'IDLE-WITH-READY: microblog(idle ~15m, ready 13)', and (b) does org2's delivery heartbeat (cron 5e48b227) actually WAKE microblog (the alarm-detects-but-never-delivers check). Coordinated with org2 to not pre-empt the natural firing. Will record fired/delivered + timestamps next beat. If alarm fires but microblog stays idle = real delivery-gap finding, will wake + flag.")
inl note_of_idle_with_ready_alarm_16 () = Note ("IDLE-WITH-READY-ALARM", 16u32, "2026-11-09T09:58Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 05:5x LIVE CAPTURE outcome: NO firing - candidate self-resolved. microblog was idle 7m@05:42 and idle 0m@05:57 (resumed ~05:51-57, before the 15-min threshold), so the 05:57 alarm run correctly read 'no idle-with-ready lane'. This is a TRUE-NEGATIVE validation (useful, not the DoD firing): the alarm did NOT false-fire on a ~7-14min transient idle - its 15m threshold properly filters brief lulls, so it is not trigger-happy. It did NOT exercise org's delivery relay (cron 4a9dc3d0) either, because microblog resumed on its OWN before any firing - the relay had nothing to wake. So the open DoD gap is UNCHANGED: still need one real firing = a lane idle PAST 15min WITH ready unblocked own-team work, caught AND woken by the relay. Will keep watching opportunistically (a lane crossing 15m idle is the trigger; most idles self-resolve first, as this one did). org2 coordinated + did not touch microblog as agreed.")
