inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_1 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 1u32, "2026-11-08T03:05Z", "main", "Child of REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB (main 11-07 23:0x split, rule: children <=240 min). Lib copies take a regex_ prefix: lib already has xsd (XML Schema) and generic names like table. Method as in HTML-MD-PARSER-TO-LIB: bodies byte-identical except headers/opens and lib respell (sm'::), landed with lib_land_window; regex's modules then open the lib copy and are deleted; proof by regex CI rehearsal on a codespace (cs-pair driver; europa OOMs regex's Cells tests at 950 MB) with tests and bench facts identical. TypeFeatures: the re union, nullability evidence GADT and typed refusals move unchanged. DoD: the three landed; regex re-pointed; rehearsal green, with bench facts identical. Next step: drafts after step 2.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_2 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 2u32, "2026-11-08T04:57Z", "main", "main 00:5x SCOPE: table opens certificate (uses automaton, automaton_dfa, certificate, certified_of, certified_phase: the typed phase automaton), so step 3 carries certificate (484) too: regex_dfa, regex_minimal, regex_certificate, regex_table. Drafts ready at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\REGEX-LIB-3 (bodies verbatim; only line 1, the opens and the :# name change). Next step: land after REGEX-LIB-2 lands; then re-point agreement, lazy, partial, semantics, bench and delete the four.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_3 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 3u32, "2026-11-09T03:02Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 23:0x DRAFTS REFRESHED (they predated compiler's pack63c fleet reformat and org2's 11-08 cell-budget splits, so landing the 00:5x drafts would have reverted both). The 4 drafts in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\REGEX-LIB-3 are regenerated from the CURRENT regex/src (dfa, minimal, certificate, table) with the lib transform: header '///- --package .' (no --timeout), sibling opens renamed (dfa/minimal/certificate -> regex_*), static blocks named after the lib module (:# regex_dfa static), and lib's header order (opens, blank, static block), matching the landed regex_derivative.spi. LF endings like lib. The old drafts are kept in REGEX-LIB-3\\before-pack63c-20261108\\. No qualified sibling references exist (0 'dfa::' etc.), so open renames suffice. The diff old -> new is the reformat's wrapped signatures + the 5 helper splits (queued in agreement, which stays in regex; probe_work alias + partition_class in certificate; with_state in dfa; next_base in table) + the static-block move. Source proof: the regex/src gate is 40/40 green on ganymede (job-1794183990021). NEXT STEP: land through lib_land_window (gates: signatures, consumers, document_test, type_probe, respell_drift) in a box lib-queue slot when the box isn't saturated, or as a node job if lib_land_window can target one; then regex/src imports regex_dfa etc. and drops its copies, which also unblocks REGEX-NERODE.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_4 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 4u32, "2026-11-09T06:27Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 02:2x DRAFTS REFRESHED AGAIN, now from regex/src AFTER tonight's proven changes (old drafts in REGEX-LIB-3\\before-refresh-20261109-0225\\). Same transform as 11-08 23:0x (header without --timeout, sibling opens -> regex_*, static blocks named after the lib module, lib's header order opens/blank/static). Contents: regex_dfa 229 lines / 5 tests (the with_state split), regex_minimal 203 / 4, regex_certificate 573 / 25 tests (+8 tonight: 2 phase/loose-set negatives, 4 forged rows, 2 partition; gate job-1794195164150 25/25 green on ganymede), regex_table 147 / 2 (the next_base split; its new ///> c tags are pending job-1794202463652, test metadata only). READY TO LAND via lib_land_window when the box lib queue is free and box CPU allows. That land is also PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS' scoped-land timing proof and unblocks REGEX-NERODE + REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET. Progress 30 -> 50.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_5 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 5u32, "2026-11-09T08:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 05:1x LANDING ROUTE that keeps the box light: lib_land_window.ps1 takes -ProvenLog <log> (a log that records lib digest, LANDED and closed green, and each <live> <hash12>); with it the box reruns only the fast checks and takes document_test from the proof. The proving run must be on a WINDOWS node (the script reads Get-CimInstance; ganymede is Linux), i.e. moon via remote.ps1 moon run, which the script already treats as a scratch reader. Box CPU sat at 100% from 03:xx to 04:0x (8 lane sessions + SystemInformer, no heavy job), so the direct land stays deferred. Order: moon is TRAIN42's node half now, then compiler's quiet timing window; the moon land proof goes after both. Next step: when moon frees, sync the 4 drafts there and run the land window with -Apply under remote.ps1 moon run, then -ProvenLog on the box.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_6 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 6u32, "2026-11-09T08:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 07:3x PRE-LAND CHECKS on the 4 drafts (kit/drafts/spiral/REGEX-LIB-3, 02:26): fresh (no regex/src dfa/minimal/certificate/table edit since) and 0 cells over the 272 budget (exact awk oracle, same weights as mix spiral.cell_budget). Ready for the moon land proof once TRAIN42c and compiler's timed window clear moon; microblog's LIB-TLDS land proof (job-1794214024263, moon) is the recipe template it will hand over.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_7 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:4x MOON LAND RECIPE (from microblog's green LIB-TLDS land, job-1794214427244): (1) pwsh remote.ps1 node sync spiral -Mirror <m> + sync alphabet + sync dice (document_test reads ../alphabet and ../dice beside the mirror's spiral); (2) scp the drafts to moon + a wrapper that sets SPIRAL_CELLS_SKIP_CLI_EXPORT=1 and runs pwsh <m>\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\spi\\lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft \"a.spi=<d1>,...\" -Label <ITEM> -Lib <m>\\spiral\\lib\\spiral -PrivateLib -Apply *> land.log; (3) kit job start --on wifi <label> 3600000 pwsh -NoProfile -File C:/home/remote-stage/<wrapper>.ps1 into a free slot; (4) scp land.log back (must hold 'LANDED and closed green' + one '<file> <hash12>' line per draft); (5) on the box: lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft <same> -Label <ITEM> -ProvenLog <land.log> -Apply (tree-write window; the fast checks re-run on the box, only document_test comes from the proof).")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_8 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 8u32, "2026-11-09T09:14Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:5x STAGED on moon (C:\\home\\remote-stage\\org2-lib3): the 4 drafts, sha256 prefixes regex_dfa 6E9D25121530, regex_minimal FD28BD757DFC, regex_certificate ECBE135901C5, regex_table 4EF9C00CAA02 (match the box drafts). Wrapper ready in org2 scratch (org2-lib3-land.ps1: SPIRAL_CELLS_SKIP_CLI_EXPORT=1, -BaseHash new x4, -PrivateLib -Apply, log to land.log). moon slots right now: kit-TRAIN42c + fiscal-step3-gate (CPU 100%), and only 12 GB free on C:, so I asked microblog to let me reuse its land mirror instead of syncing a new spiral+alphabet+dice copy. Next step: mirror name -> resync spiral into it -> start in the next free moon slot (before compiler's timed window, never during it) -> carry land.log back -> box -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_9 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 9u32, "2026-11-09T09:25Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 09:2x MIRROR READY + ARMED: moon mirror cellspt1 (reused with microblog's OK) re-synced from the box: REMOTE-SYNC-OK head bf5cc30a digest 1E1DF034BDFCBFE1 (tlds.spi C10D96111D4C on both sides; regex_dfa absent = new). Wrapper C:\\home\\remote-stage\\org2-lib3-land.ps1 points at it. A box poller (scratchpad lib3-when-free.sh, idempotent on label org2-lib3-landproof) submits ONE kit job start --on wifi only while TRAIN42c still runs, moon < 2 running jobs and no compiler job running; if TRAIN42c ends first it stands down (the slot belongs to compiler's timed window). compiler + rig told. Next step: read land.log (scp from moon) and run -ProvenLog on the box.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_10 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 10u32, "2026-11-09T09:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 09:5x poller STOOD DOWN as designed: TRAIN42c ended (09:50Z) before a moon slot freed, and the slot after TRAIN42 belongs to compiler's quiet timed window. Placement after the window (told compiler + microblog): the LIB-3 land proof takes ONE slot first (~30 min), microblog's long tail may run in the other. Everything is staged (cellspt1 synced, drafts + wrapper on moon). Next step: when compiler posts the timed window DONE, re-run scratchpad lib3-when-free.sh with the TRAIN42 guard dropped (guard = no compiler job running).")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_11 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 11u32, "2026-11-09T09:52Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:0x RE-ARMED: compiler's moon job job-1794217919229-compiler-moon-post-train = (1) timed window (waits for CPU < 15% for 2 min) (2) SDK pin to rc.3 (3)(4) pair builds. The land proof waits for the WHOLE job, not just the timed phase, because step (2) swaps moon's cache SDK (rig: a mid-run SDK swap breaks running jobs); and no --after-ok (a link submitted into full slots goes to jobs/held and never wakes). Box poller lib3-when-free.sh (rewritten, idempotent) submits org2-lib3-landproof when no compiler job is running/queued and moon has < 2 running jobs. Bonus: the proof then runs on the rc.3 SDK the box and cloud nodes use.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_12 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 12u32, "2026-11-09T10:10Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:3x POLLER KILLED before it fired: rig started TRAIN42d on moon (05:55) and compiler stopped its post-train job (never left its quiet gate), so the poller's guard (no compiler job running) would have let the land proof jump ahead of compiler's timed window. Nothing was submitted (no org2 job on moon). Order: TRAIN42d -> compiler's timed window + pair builds (new job id on rig's DONE) -> LIB-3 land proof -> microblog's tail. Next step: submit org2-lib3-landproof by hand (one kit job start --on wifi into a free slot) when compiler posts its DONE; everything stays staged on cellspt1. Lesson: a guard keyed on another lane's job label is fragile when that lane restarts its job; key on the explicit DONE message instead.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_13 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 13u32, "2026-11-09T10:45Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:5x from the star exchange (fiscal, 6 off-box lands today): the box lib MOVES during a proof, so (1) re-sync cellspt1 and compare its lib digest with the box lib right before submitting the moon proof, and (2) compare again right before the box -ProvenLog land (lib_land_window prints the digest; a mismatch means the fast checks rerun on the box, which is fine, but a draft-file mismatch means re-prove). Also confirmed: the 4 drafts add no comment lines (the new COMMENT-LINT gate would refuse them), and their here-string-free copies are byte-exact.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_14 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 14u32, "2026-11-09T10:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Blocker: moon's C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\deps\\The-Spiral-Language is MISSING (microblog found it 11-09 07:0x; every moon compile using the default core fails with \"core is not loaded\", exit 5), and cellspt1\\spiral\\deps is a junction to that same deps dir, so the land proof would fail the same way. compiler + rig are told and own the restore. Next step: once restored (and the core hash re-checked), the moon order resumes and the land proof is submitted by hand after compiler's DONE.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_15 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 15u32, "2026-11-09T10:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 11:2x moon core RESTORED (rig: its own 06:42 cleanup had deleted the shared spiral deps through a junction; restored + verified): C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\deps\\The-Spiral-Language and cellspt1's junctioned copy both present. Blocker cleared; back to the moon ORDER: moon now runs TRAIN42e + fiscal g6a-gate3 + x verify-client-r2; then compiler's timed window + pair builds; then this land proof (submitted by hand on compiler's DONE, with the lib-digest checks from fiscal's lesson).")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_16 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 16u32, "2026-11-09T14:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 14:4x ROUTE CHANGE: the land proof moves OFF moon's queue (it was 3rd behind TRAIN42e + compiler's window; no moon job had been submitted, so nothing to cancel) onto ganymede, using the Linux-node route proven an hour ago on PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB (private tree /home/remote/org2-phys, raw lib digest 3649D80B2DB8DA32 = the box's, checked just before staging). ONE window lands 5 new lib files: regex_dfa, regex_minimal, regex_certificate, regex_table + bench_model (PERF-STUDY-3, green 5/5), -BaseHash new x5. Folded in: RENAME-1108's last site, regex_certificate's probe record -> pending_pair (probe_work -> pending_work; 9 whole-word sites, diff = only the rename, budget clean; backup drafts\\REGEX-LIB-3\\before-rename-20261109). Job: org2-lib3land. Then: copy-only box land with -ProvenLog after predicting the box digest.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_3_dfa_17 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", 17u32, "2026-11-09T15:05Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:0x LANDED on the box, DONE. Proof (ganymede, private tree re-synced after xsd_emit.spi landed on the box mid-way, so raw lib digest 4F55A7C588BF586E on both sides before the re-proof): job-1794236396731-org2-lib3land, 5 drafts round-trip, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe 5/5 PASS (regex_certificate 22 tests typed incl. its expected-fail typing tests), respell 0, LANDED and closed green, lib digest F91E5CEE8102BACD. Box: box digest re-checked = 4F55... right before, then lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply: \"LANDED from a proven close\", no fast-check rerun; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-110436; box lib now F91E5CEE8102BACD = the proof. Landed (new, unstaged): lib/spiral/regex_dfa.spi 6E9D25121530, regex_minimal.spi FD28BD757DFC, regex_certificate.spi A47D96C94982 (probe -> pending_pair), regex_table.spi 4EF9C00CAA02, plus bench_model.spi 2D56BEE1AA08 (PERF-STUDY-3). Proof: those two logs.")
