inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_1 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T03:06Z", "main", "Child of REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB (main 11-07 23:0x split, rule: children <=240 min). Lib copies take a regex_ prefix: lib already has xsd (XML Schema) and generic names like table. Method as in HTML-MD-PARSER-TO-LIB: bodies byte-identical except headers/opens and lib respell (sm'::), landed with lib_land_window; regex's modules then open the lib copy and are deleted; proof by regex CI rehearsal on a codespace (cs-pair driver; europa OOMs regex's Cells tests at 950 MB) with tests and bench facts identical. TypeFeatures: the re union, nullability evidence GADT and typed refusals move unchanged. DoD: lib regex_xsd covers every function fiscal's 19 generated units call (61 calls), with byte-stable dfa_table_text; the ouroboros agreement (regex vs lib xsd_regex on fiscal's pinned corpus) green. Next step: list fiscal's call surface from map.txt (drafts fiscal\\FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP).")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_2 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:22Z", "tibia", "11-09 11:3x tibia (handed over by org2; UNIT items stay with org2). CALL SURFACE: already listed in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-REGEX-DUP-MAP\\map.txt \"CONSUMER API\": generated units 61x table_matches only; xsd_emit dfa_state x13, pattern_matches x4, dfa_move x3, dfa_table_text x2, example_with x2, repeated x2, table_matches x2, compile_pattern, dfa_of_pattern(_within), dfa_of_values; xpath_eval rx x4, class_end x2, compile_pattern x2, escape_end x2, longest_match x2, brace_end, matches_from, nullable; plus fiscal corpus_checks (census layer). STEP 1 (this note): lib regex_xsd as a byte-identical MOVE of regex/src/xsd.spi (live sha 95AD63868334, 386 lines). The opens already name lib modules (regex_charset/regex_syntax/regex_derivative), and xsd is a leaf in regex (no regex module opens it). The REGEX-LIB-3 shape: opens first, then `:# regex_xsd static`. Draft: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS\\regex_xsd.spi. Gate: ganymede job-1794237706422-tibia-xsdgate (format, --check, cell budget, its own 7+ Cells tests, on a spiral mirror synced from the box at 15:3xZ). NEXT STEPS, one gap at a time, each a regex_xsd addition with a test, keeping xsd_regex's adapter API byte-stable: (a) longest_match, (b) class_end/escape_end/brace_end positions, (c) the 7 named blocks vs lib's 4, (d) dfa_of_values, (e) example_with/repeated, (f) dfa_table_text + table_matches.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_3 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:28Z", "tibia", "Evidence (step 1): ganymede job-1794237706422-tibia-xsdgate on pack77, run against a spiral mirror synced from the box at 15:3xZ (with REGEX-LIB-3 + bench_model). regex_xsd.spi (the byte-identical move of regex/src/xsd.spi) gives: formatter unchanged, --check clean, cell budget 0 findings, Cells discovered 8 executed 8 passed 8 failed 0 (rust + gleam rows). The mirror was cleaned afterwards (0). Steps 2a (longest_match over code points) and 2b (syntax spans: brace/escape/class with nested subtraction) are drafted in the same file and gate next.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_4 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:35Z", "tibia", "11-09 11:5x tibia: STEPS 2a+2b GATED (job-1794238112101-tibia-xsdgate2): Cells discovered 11 executed 11 passed 11 failed 0 (8 moved + 3 new: longest_match; brace/escape spans incl. \\p{..}; class span through nested subtraction and escapes), --check clean. Two layout fixes were applied after it: the formatter wanted class_step one branch per line, and the cell budget flagged longest_from at 288 > 272 (now split with a `seen` helper). STEP 2c (gap: named blocks): the map said 7, but regex has 6 (typed union: + GeneralPunctuation, CurrencySymbols), a strict SUPERSET of lib's 4 with the SAME names and ranges (0-127, 128-255, 256-383, 384-591). A test pins that, so the adapter switch cannot change any accepted \\p{Is..} pattern. One adapter difference to keep in mind: regex REFUSES an unknown block (typed UnknownBlock), while lib returns an unparsable position. Re-gate of 2a-2c: job-1794238527001-tibia-xsdgate3.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_5 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T15:39Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:0x tibia: STEPS 2d + 2e DRAFTED (gate after xsdgate3). 2d dfa_of_values: no hand-built DFA in the canonical core. values_re folds alt over word (codes_of v) from Nothing, and regex_dfa + regex_minimal already give the unique minimal DFA of that finite language (lib's builder becomes an adapter detail). Test: [MYR; SGD; \"\"] accepts exactly its members and rejects MY, MYRR, USD. 2e example_with/repeated: example_of on re over code points, with lib's choice rule (class low if >= 33, else the first of [A, a, 1, Z, z] in the set, else low), repeated_codes for Star (stars) and Repeat (low). Test: [0-9]{8} -> 00000000, [^@]{2} -> AA, a*b with stars 2 -> aab. TWO KNOWN DIVERGENCES from lib's example_with, for the ouroboros gate (xsd_emit examples must stay byte-identical, so the adapter keeps lib's generator until the gate shows 0 diffs on fiscal's corpus): (i) regex normalises alt into canonical (sorted) order, so `b|a` yields `a` where lib takes the first WRITTEN branch `b`; (ii) regex has no negation flag (it stores the complement set), so a negated class excluding all of A, a, 1, Z, z yields its lowest member where lib yields `~`. Possibly a third: whether `+` desugars as Repeat(a,1,..) (lib) or Seq(a, Star a) (regex) changes the repeat count; the test avoids `+` until checked.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_6 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T15:40Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:0x tibia: divergence (iii) from note 5 RESOLVED by reading both parsers: `+` is NOT a divergence. lib xsd_regex regex_parse_quant_at turns 43u32 into seq atom (star atom), and regex_syntax plus a = seq a (star a), so the example of x+ is x then x repeated `stars` times in both. Related: lib parses x? as alt_written RxEps atom (example = empty, the first written branch). regex's optional sorts Epsilon first by rank, so it should also give empty; this is folded into divergence (i) for the corpus gate to confirm. The known divergences stay (i) alt order and (ii) all-excluded negated classes.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_7 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T15:41Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:1x tibia: GAP 2f (dfa_table_text + table_matches) DECIDED, with no core change: they STAY in the xsd_regex adapter as a stable ABI. Reason: table_matches/table_run/table_step (xsd_regex.spi:1067-1083) interpret a STRING table only (cp_at over the text plus regex_table_row), with no dependence on rx or any regex engine type. The 61 calls in fiscal's 19 generated units read tables that xsd_emit wrote with dfa_table_text. Re-emitting them from regex_dfa (different state numbering) would change every generated unit, which is what the DoD's \"byte-stable dfa_table_text\" forbids. So the canonical core supplies the DFA (via values_re / regex_dfa), and the adapter keeps the text format. A later switch can feed regex_dfa rows into the same dfa_table_text, gated by the generator identity arm (0 differing units). GAP LIST COMPLETE: a longest_match, b syntax spans, c blocks (superset, test), d values_re, e example_of (2 known divergences), f adapter ABI. Remaining for DoD: (1) gate 2d+2e; (2) land regex_xsd via lib_land_window (moon or ganymede proof, digest check first); (3) the ouroboros agreement: regex vs lib xsd_regex on fiscal's pinned corpus, green.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_8 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 8u32, "2026-11-09T15:53Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:2x tibia: LANDING CUT PRE-REGISTERED, after org2's trap note (lib notebook list skips new modules, the land window only type-probes, and regex/build.ps1 now gates exactly the lib regex_* modules that regex/src OPENS). xsd is a leaf (no regex module opens it), so landing regex_xsd while deleting regex/src/xsd.spi would leave its 13 tests running NOWHERE. SAME CUT therefore includes: (1) lib regex_xsd lands; (2) regex/src/xsd.spi is deleted and `xsd` leaves regex/src/spiral.toml; (3) regex/src/agreement.spi gains `:< regex_xsd` (the ouroboros check opens it anyway: regex_xsd vs lib xsd_regex on fiscal's pinned corpus), so regex/build.ps1's derived list covers regex_xsd. CHECK (org2's): regex's gate total = 87 (today) + the lib regex_* modules' tests, including regex_xsd's. If the total drops by xsd's count, the trap fired and the cut is not done. The regex-side edits (2)-(3) are org2's repo: tibia drafts them, org2 applies.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_9 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 9u32, "2026-11-09T15:54Z", "tibia", "11-09 12:2x tibia: the regex-side half of the cut is DRAFTED (org2 applies; regex is org2's repo) in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS\\. agreement.spi (base ADA30FE3BCA9) adds `:< regex_xsd` after `:< regex_certificate`. spiral.toml (base 139D7BAA3FEC) drops the `xsd` module line, leaving lazy, partial, agreement, semantics, laws, witness, typed, core_emit, table_emit. Plus deleting src/xsd.spi (live 95AD63868334). Order: the lib land of regex_xsd first; then these three in one apply; then regex/build.ps1, whose total must be 87 + the lib regex_* tests including regex_xsd's.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_10 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 10u32, "2026-11-09T16:58Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:0x tibia: the regex-side drafts are REBASED on org2's green base (regex build 118/118 incl. the 9 lib regex modules). agreement.spi live ADA30FE3BCA9 (unchanged): the draft adds `:< regex_xsd` after the last lib regex_ open (regex_certificate). src/spiral.toml live 64E750526AAF (now lists ssv_graph): the draft drops only the `xsd` line. src/xsd.spi live is still 95AD63868334, so lib regex_xsd remains a byte-identical move of it. The full 2a-2e lib gate is xsdgate4. Then the order is: one moon proof lands regex_xsd (with LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT's file_system), the box copy after a digest match, org2 applies the 3 regex-side edits, and regex/build.ps1 total = 118 + regex_xsd's tests (the trap check).")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_11 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 11u32, "2026-11-09T17:05Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:1x tibia: FULL 2a-2e GATE GREEN (ganymede job-1794243328611-tibia-xsdgate4, pack77): --check clean, Cells discovered 14 executed 14 passed 14 failed 0 (rust + gleam rows; incl. values_re membership and example_of on [0-9]{8}, [^@]{2}, a*b). Formatter-only changes were taken from the gate's format output (tokens identical). One over-budget cell (example_of, 360) was split into a mutual :~ ^ example_of / :& :~ repeat_example pair, the same shape as xsd_regex's class_end; a dropped blank line was restored. Re-gate: job-1794243731439-tibia-xsdgate5. Then the moon proof for regex_xsd + file_system.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_12 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 12u32, "2026-11-09T17:22Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:2x tibia: re-gate xsdgate5: fmt same, --check clean, Cells 14/14, cell budget 1 finding = the merged repeat_example + example_text cell from the pre-fix file it copied (the blank line was restored right after; local measure: every cell <= 264). LAND PROOF launched on moon (job tibia-libland7) together with LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT's file_system: drafts regex_xsd.spi FA6BE524EC72 (new) + file_system.spi C9BB02D1FDD6 (base 31DA42B6F518), the tree = the box lib as packed (aca413b4 tgz), hashes verified on both ends before launch.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_13 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 13u32, "2026-11-09T17:57Z", "tibia", "Evidence: lib regex_xsd LANDED 11-09 13:53 local on the box lib by lib_land_window from a proven close, together with LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT's file_system. PROOF: moon -PrivateLib (job tibia-libland7; the tree = the box lib packed at 13:2x): round trip, consumers, document_test, type_probe, respell_drift; \"LANDED and closed green\", regex_xsd.spi FA6BE524EC72 (new), file_system.spi C9BB02D1FDD6, lib digest C799304325951906. BOX: the post-land digest was recomputed locally first (both drafts overridden) = C799304325951906, an exact match, so the box only copied (tree-write window win-1794246777284-27116, waited 0 ms): \"LANDED from a proven close\", undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-135257. Unstaged. NEXT (the same cut, org2's repo): apply the rebased regex-side drafts (delete regex/src/xsd.spi; drop xsd from src/spiral.toml; agreement.spi opens regex_xsd), then regex build total = 118 + regex_xsd's 14 (the trap check). Then the ouroboros agreement in fiscal's corpus checks.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_14 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 14u32, "2026-11-09T18:06Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:1x tibia: org2 APPLIED the regex-side cut (unstaged; backups drafts\\regex\\APPLY-1109-TIBIA): src/xsd.spi deleted, `xsd` dropped from src/spiral.toml (applied by intent, since the toml had gained ssv_graph/workloads after my base), agreement.spi opens regex_xsd, README points at lib regex_xsd.spi. The trap check is pending org2's next full regex build (expected total = 122 + regex_xsd 14 - xsd's own tests + 13 new absorb tests); org2 sends the exact number.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_15 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 15u32, "2026-11-09T20:23Z", "tibia", "11-09 16:3x tibia: TRAP CHECK PASSED (org2 ganymede job-1794251871681-org2-swap5, 19:53Z, exit 0): the regex gate ran 131/131 over 22 files, failed 0. RECONCILED FILE BY FILE against the box tree (static count of :# tests minus each file's prelude): 21 product files = 128 (lib regex_certificate 25, regex_xsd 14, regex_syntax 10, regex_dfa 7, regex_derivative 6, regex_charset 6, regex_nullable 4, regex_minimal 4, regex_language 3, regex_table 2; regex/src typed 10, partial 9, semantics 5, lazy 5, ssv_graph 4, agreement 4, witness 3, laws 3, table_emit 2, workloads 1, core_emit 1), + org2's staged/staged_check.spi 3 = 131, an exact match. So every lib test regex opens is EXECUTED by the consumer gate, including regex_xsd's 14 (the lib-move-drops-tests trap did not fire), and the absorb tests are in (typed 9->10, witness 2->3). My earlier formula (122 + 14 - xsd + 13) was wrong in its last term (the absorb slices added 2 regex tests, not 13; fin_vector's tests run in lib's own gate); the per-file reconciliation replaces it.")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_16 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 16u32, "2026-11-10T10:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 10:1xZ clearing the lane:org2 wait: the trap check was answered 11-09 19:53Z (ganymede org2-swap5: regex gate 131/131 over 22 files, reconciled file by file by tibia above). Box still has the cut: regex/src/xsd.spi absent, no xsd module in regex/src/spiral.toml")
inl note_of_regex_lib_4_xsd_gaps_17 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS", 17u32, "2026-11-10T12:24Z", "org3", "org3 triage 11-10: claimed, read the full history, released -- this is NOT a fresh-driver item. lib regex_xsd LANDED 11-09 (tibia, moon proof) and org2 APPLIED the regex-side cut (src/xsd.spi deleted, agreement.spi opens regex_xsd). The only remaining DoD -- the trap-check total AND the ouroboros agreement (regex_xsd vs lib xsd_regex on fiscal's pinned corpus, which runs as agreement.spi cells) -- is confirmed by org2's NEXT FULL REGEX BUILD, which org2 said it would run and report the exact number of. So the next step waits on org2's build, not on a new driver. Setting a wait so it leaves the ready pool (it was falsely-ready: 15% Active, no wait, so the gate kept offering it while it is actually pending org2's build).")
