inl microblog_migration () = Task ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", "Migrate x into the microblog repo (generic client, BEAM server, x-archive) and retire x", Epic, P2, D7, 0u32, Paused, "MICROBLOG-UI-LANDING,MICROBLOG-SKELETON,MICROBLOG-LIB-MODEL,MICROBLOG-CLIENT,MICROBLOG-SERVER,MICROBLOG-DATA-CENSUS,MICROBLOG-CUTOVER,MICROBLOG-RETIRE-X", "microblog,migration,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_microblog_migration () = Planning ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", Minutes 4800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_microblog_migration_1 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 1u32, "2026-11-08T04:03Z", "main", "USER DECISION (11-07, via x-dumps' /btw fork): migrate x into C:\\home\\git\\microblog (blank clone on disk) and eventually delete x. Owner lane: x (x-dumps drives its UI landing and the archive question). Layout: deps/spiral vendored like html; lib/ = one post+timeline model; apps/client (Spiral->Rust, protocol-generic reader from x/apps/client: read-only adapters for activitypub (Mastodon, Threads via fediverse, opt-in/partial), atproto (Bluesky), x-archive (static dump), x-syndication); apps/server (Spiral->Gleam/BEAM+iggy from x/apps/sim); apps/x-archive (from the xarchive Cargo repo; fold in OR keep xarchive as source of truth + vendored: x-dumps decides). Data: event-sourced merge-patch store with per-field provenance (source + fetch time), merge-not-replace. One manifest topology, TypeFeatures: all-code and Cells tests-only from commit 1. SEQUENCING (hard): (1) x-dumps lands its in-flight x UI work (timeline_page E78F29A0EC1D, timeline_serve 97F4088FE596) permanently first; (2) client migrates first; (3) the live europa serve stays on x until microblog's server is green; (4) server + cutover last. Lib-first: the shared post/timeline model and any html_render/markdown/blog-engine reuse go through lib (doc_* is already in lib since 11-07), not repo-to-repo deps. DoD: client migrated and green with live reads vs Mastodon, Bluesky and x-archive; server migrated, europa deploy green, live serve re-pointed x->microblog, iggy healthy; the archive question settled; the patchable store live with all x data migrated losslessly with provenance (row counts + hashes before/after); nothing unique left only in x (file-level census); TypeFeatures/cells/granular/budgets green; x, x-dumps and main sign off; the USER runs the delete of x (never an agent). Next step: x (owner) splits this into children MICROBLOG-1-SKELETON, -2-MODEL-LIB, -3-CLIENT, -4-ADAPTERS, -5-STORE, -6-SERVER, -7-DATA-MIGRATION, -8-CUTOVER, -9-RETIRE-X, chained by deps; the first pull is SKELETON after x-dumps' UI lands.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_2 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 2u32, "2026-11-08T04:10Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "XARCHIVE FOLD-VS-VENDOR DECISION (x-dumps drives, per i574n) 11-08T00:0xZ: RECOMMEND VENDOR (keep xarchive as a separate source-of-truth repo), NOT fold-in. Grounding (on disk): xarchive/ is a 617MB standalone Cargo-RUST repo - src/ = cdx, events, fetch, live, media, merge, narrate, parse, snaps (2267 LOC) + deploy/ + target/. It is the HARVESTER: it fetches tweets/media + builds the archive dump. microblog/apps/client is a Spiral->Rust READ-ONLY reader whose x-archive adapter CONSUMES that dump. These are different concerns (produce vs read) and different build systems (Cargo-Rust vs Spiral-in-microblog); folding a Cargo app into a Spiral repo mixes toolchains + bloats the day-one slate with 617MB of harvest state. CLEANER: xarchive stays the harvest source-of-truth; microblog reads its OUTPUT via the x-archive adapter (same pattern as the activitypub/atproto adapters reading their sources). If grooming wants a single repo later, the harvester can move as its own Cargo workspace member under microblog/ without being rewritten - but that is a convenience, not a day-one need. Open for confirmation; flag if the data-migration proof (before/after row counts + hashes) argues for co-location.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_3 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 3u32, "2026-11-08T04:18Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "DATA-MIGRATION LOSSLESS-PROOF PROTOCOL (x-dumps, drafting the DoD proof i574n flagged) 11-08T00:2xZ. The x world entities to census (from the sim world / xarchive dump): accounts (by id+handle; note the dup-handle case, two fc1943s accounts 72784485 and 1637273636049498112 must both survive), posts by KIND (original / reply / quote / repost), media files (images+videos, by content hash), the reference graph (reply-to + quote-of edges), and per-post engagement (like/reply/repost counts). PROOF = two-sided census: BEFORE (frozen x world, captured right before cutover) and AFTER (microblog world post-import) must match on (1) per-type ROW COUNTS and (2) a CONTENT hash. The content hash must be over canonical CONTENT fields only (id, author, created_at, text, media content-hashes, ref edges, engagement) sorted by id — NOT over provenance/fetch-time metadata, since the patchable store adds provenance that has no before-image; a per-entity hash rolled into a sorted-concatenation digest per type lets a mismatch localize to the offending ids. LOSSLESS = counts equal + content digests equal; any intentional transform (e.g. normalizing multi-shape fields) is recorded as a named exception with its own before/after count. Capture discipline: freeze harvest before the before-census (no re-harvest mid-migration) so the two sides are comparable. This is a protocol design only; the actual census runs at migration time when the data is final. Ties to [[xdumps-world-fields-multishape]] (multi-shape normalization is the likely named transform) and the provenance store.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_4 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 4u32, "2026-11-08T04:25Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "UI-LANDING DoD line status (x-dumps) 11-08T00:2xZ: the two verifies that prove my in-flight UI are RUNNING on the budget-fixed hashes (box reads timeline_page 79E375431143, timeline_serve 97F4088FE596). Jobs: client job-1794111824846-x-verify-1108a-client (node xqueue1 pack61b) + sim x-verify-1108b-sim (node xqueue3 pack61b). Note: the earlier sim run job-1794110090990 never started because the cell-budget PRE-GATE checks the client tree for every part, so the timeline_page budget red blocked the sim part too; that is now cleared by the split. A full part took ~3h tonight, so both will still be PENDING at 02:00 — the microblog/x lane reports them pending-with-ids, not landed. Their GREEN closes DoD item 5 (nothing unique left only in x: UI landed+proven). These jobs outlive this bg autonomous run (ends 02:00), so the microblog lane owns tracking them to green; no action left on my side but to hand the state over.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_5 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 5u32, "2026-11-08T04:44Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "UI-landing hash update (x-dumps) 11-08T00:4xZ: timeline_serve had a second non-granular budget red (scroll_track, the URL-on-scroll JS, line 244 weight 371 - a 3-piece concat cell that granular under-counts but the gate sums). Split into 3 functions (scroll_track/scroll_track_scan/scroll_track_apply); re-verified 0 over_budget on both files with the gate counter. NEW hashes for the UI-landing DoD line: timeline_page 79E375431143 + timeline_serve CE8CD524A6E2 (was 97F4088FE596). microblog lane relaunching client+sim verifies on these. Lesson reinforced: ALWAYS check landing budget with the non-granular mix spiral.cell_budget (no --granular) on every touched tree before handing a hash - granular 0-over does not clear the gate for multi-piece ++# string cells.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_6 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 6u32, "2026-11-08T05:02Z", "x-dumps-ec368ac8", "UI-LANDING: budget gate CLEARED, verifies RUNNING (x-dumps) 11-08T00:5xZ. microblog lane confirmed the box tree (timeline_page 79E375431143 + timeline_serve CE8CD524A6E2) shows over_budget 0 across BOTH client + sim with the gate command; box defuse/digest/glyphs clean (the overruns were only in the europa mirrors respell WIP, not the box). Both parts are now PAST the budget pre-gate and running on the node: client job-1794113772611-x-verify-1108c-client (xqueue1 pack61b) + sim x-verify-1108d-sim (xqueue3). ~3h each so still pending at 02:00; microblog lane reports them pending-with-ids and owns tracking to green past this bg runs end. Their GREEN closes DoD item 5 (UI landed+proven). My active UI-landing work is COMPLETE - nothing left but the verify wall-clock.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_7 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 7u32, "2026-11-08T05:17Z", "main", "USER 11-08 01:0x: lane renames: the x lane is now 'microblog' (owner of this epic) and x-dumps is 'management'. Most remaining x-archive work is done (node GB download, server deploy setup), so microblog can carry this alone; after the frontend work, management teaches microblog to keep the deploy hot (MANAGEMENT-LANE-CHARTER). xarchive: vendor, not fold (management's 11-08 analysis: xarchive is a 2267-LOC Cargo harvester that PRODUCES the archive; microblog's x-archive adapter consumes it). The polyglot chat contract sample is absorbed here (POLYGLOT-SALVAGE-AUDIT).")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_8 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 8u32, "2026-11-08T05:37Z", "management-f33af161", "UI-landing hash correction (management) 11-08T01:3xZ: the sim verify caught that my label_of change (Repost-of-X only, Reply label removed) left two STALE sim test cells I missed when updating the timeline_page cell tests - timeline_serve.spi:449/453 (label_for -> label_of). Fixed (449 asserts Repost of @gfixler; 453 renamed a_reply_has_no_label asserts empty), budget re-checked 0 over. NEW UI-landing hashes: timeline_page 79E375431143 + timeline_serve ABEE1D0C960F (was CE8CD524A6E2). The CLIENT e2e RED (17->1->1) looks SEPARATE from my changes (client detects repost/reply via structural enums, not label text; no old-label strings in apps/client) - awaiting the failing check names from the full log. LESSON: when a shared helper (label_of) changes, grep EVERY tree for its assertions, not just the file I edited - label_for in the sim reached it.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_9 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 9u32, "2026-11-08T07:42Z", "management-f33af161", "UI-landing: sim verify RED fixed again (management) 11-08T02:3xZ. The sim verify on ABEE1D0C960F red exit 1 (1/29 notebooks): TWO more rust cells reached Erlang FFI - dir_of_reads_the_d_param + from_of_reads_the_from_param, both calling dir_of/from_of -> dotted_in -> sim_serve::query_first -> erlang_http_server::query_value (Erlang-only), generating Gleam into the Rust build. I had WRONGLY cleared these earlier as \"string-only dotted_in, rust-safe\" without tracing dotted_in to its FFI. Switched both to ///> gleam; 0 ///> rust cells now remain in timeline_serve.spi. NEW hashes: timeline_page 447BE46DA675 (Lights-Out #000 + Inter font, the user x-faithfulness fix) + timeline_serve 02F9E1DC2DA0. LESSON REINFORCED: do not ASSUME a helper is backend-neutral - TRACE every rust cell call chain to the actual FFI; dotted_in looked like a string op but hit an Erlang http helper two hops down.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_10 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 10u32, "2026-11-08T12:08Z", "microblog", "Paused 11-08 (user): finish the Cells Elixir rewrite and the typed-boundary work first, so microblog starts on settled modeling instead of carrying drift. Resume when CELLS-PORT-CLIS (last Elixir), LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH (M1/M2/M3 verdict) and TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 (org template) are Done. x and the live serve stay as they are; MICROBLOG-UI-LANDING continues in x.")
inl note_of_microblog_migration_11 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-MIGRATION", 11u32, "2026-11-08T12:29Z", "microblog", "Gate update: LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH Done (compiler, M2 GADT facade is the default: safety 100% vs 0%, ~40% smaller, round trips on Rust and BEAM incl. iggy; works on installed pack61b; an M3 win would never need a source change). Remaining gates: CELLS-PORT-CLIS (team:microblog, deps CELLS-PORT-NOTEBOOK + CELLS-PORT-KINO-FACADES) and TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 (team:i574n, dep PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD). Resume when both are Done.")
