inl note_of_kit_next_name_1 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 1u32, "2026-11-08T04:40Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "Filed 11-08 by kit from the user's naming question (subagent review, user-resumed): rated 0-1000, kit 620, rig 730, yard 780 (a rail yard: trains assembled, held on sidings, signaled and dispatched, matching trains, gates, waits and placement), loom 700, depot 690, helm 650. DECISION NEEDED from the user first: rig or yard (the plan below is name-agnostic; R1 asks). DoD: the tool, its crates, binary, config dirs, env vars, backlog IDs, team tag, lane names, hooks, scripts, docs and CI use the new name, with a one-release compatibility shim, then the shim retires; history keeps old names. SEQUENCING: start after TRAIN39 installs and after pack63 plus the fleet formatter respell (two fleet respells must not overlap); close or fold KIT-RENAME (eoie to kit, 90 percent) first. NEXT STEP: R1 inventory and the name decision. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a rename_target union over the categories (Crate, CargoName, Export, Binary, ConfigDir, EnvVar, BacklogId, TeamTag, LaneName, Hook, Script, Doc, Ci) with a count per category, so progress is a typed table.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_2 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 2u32, "2026-11-08T05:00Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 01:0x USER DECISION (the user's words via the naming fork): rig. 'i'm ready to fully commit with renaming to rig now, don't care about the cost' and 'i already renamed the repo and fixed local's origin'. Verified: origin = https://github.com/i574n/rig.git; the local checkout is still C:\\home\\git\\kit. This epic is the RIG-RENAME epic the user asked for (kept under its filed id to avoid an expensive id rename tonight; R5 renames every KIT-* id to RIG-* anyway). R1 no longer needs the name decision. Sequencing unchanged: after TRAIN39's box half installs (it runs from C:\\home\\git\\kit, so the folder must not move before it ends), and after pack63 plus the fleet formatter respell. Fold in KIT-RENAME (eoie to kit, 90 percent) when R1 starts.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_3 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 3u32, "2026-11-08T05:19Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 01:2x RIG-RENAME CHECKLIST (user 01:0x via main: full rename to rig, pass every lesson of the eoie to kit rename). Lessons from KIT-RENAME, RENAME-LEFTOVERS-1106 and KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST, mapped to steps:\n1. IDs AND TAGS (R5). On 11-06 the 169 ids were renamed but 73 items kept the old TAG until a recount found them; rename team:kit and every kit tag in the same pass, then recount tags as well as ids. Old ids stay in older note text as history, and each renamed item gets a note naming its old id.\n2. RENAME COST (R5). agile rename was quadratic (14 min, 398 s CPU on 14.8 MB; fixed 11-05). The state is now 9.45 MB after tonight's seal. Batch it under the agile lock with a backup and a set-hash proof like the seal's.\n3. MACHINES (R4). Last time the node needed junctions (kit\\jobs -> eoie\\jobs, kit\\windows) and remote-machines.json keys pointing old to new, plus the old binary kept by hash (kit-<hash>.exe). Do the same for rig on box, node (C:\\home\\bin) and europa; switch only when no job host process of the old name is left.\n4. CONFIG AND ENV (R2). %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\{bin,jobs,drafts,archive}, %APPDATA%\\kit\\{target_limits.spi,path_first.spi,fleet.spi,lease-policy}, jobs\\machines\\europa.gate, and env KIT_CONFIG_HOME, KIT_RELEASE_HOME, KIT_STYLE_ROOT, KIT_STYLE_KIT, KIT_SPIRAL_TIMEOUT_MS, KIT_BIN_UNDER_TEST, KIT_SPIRAL_BUNDLE: new first, old fallback, one-shot copy.\n5. HOOKS AND SCHEDULED TASKS (R4). ~/.claude/hooks (autonomous-gate.ps1, kit-style-check.ps1 defaults C:\\home\\git\\kit and kit.exe), and kit-machine-watch-hourly plus every kit-* scheduled task, re-registered with FULL paths (scheduled-task full-path trap) as a user batch.\n6. SOURCE (R3). Crate names also live inside raw host strings ($'kit_style_census::kit_census_run()', $\"bootstrap_authority_status::...\") and export names (\"kit_...\"); the respell must cover string-embedded names, not only Spiral identifiers. Run on a train with the 7 precheck guards, ONE model crate diff shown to the user first.\n7. FOLDER (R4). C:\\home\\git\\kit -> C:\\home\\git\\rig only when no job runs from it (no kit-TRAIN* job; tonight's TRAIN39 install runs from it). Node mirrors (C:\\home\\remote\\*\\kit) and node-proof/remote.ps1 repo names follow.\n8. OTHER REPOS (R1/R6). Dead arms elsewhere: last time i574n.github apps/graphs agile.spi kept an eoie arm that read only tags. Recount with git grep -i -I -c kit over all 11 own repos, excluding the history list (backlog state, archive, kit state, recorded history files).\n9. CI AND PINS (R7). The repo rename is done; workflow names, actions.lock and pins_check references follow.\n10. MEMORY AND LANES (R6). Memory files and MEMORY.md name kit paths and kit-<hash> lanes; lanes announce rig-<hash>; claims rows carry lane names.\nWINDOW: a quiet window, never during a train install; after pack63 and the fleet formatter respell. DoD as KIT-RENAME's: git grep -i kit gives 0 tracked hits outside the history list in every own repo, and 0 items carry a kit tag.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_4 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 4u32, "2026-11-08T11:47Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 07:5x rig, RE-SEQUENCED (user via management: the lane and the tool must be renamed to rig asap). The LANE half is done: team:rig on 247 live items and the session is rig. R1 is Done with the inventory. Checked the old premise: pack62 and pack63 are NOT installed (every job this morning reports core 65DEE79C, pack61b), so waiting for pack63 plus the fleet formatter respell would park the rename for an unknown time. The real constraints are narrower: (a) the source respell must not OVERLAP the fleet formatter respell (both rewrite every kit .spi), (b) the folder move needs no job running from C:\\home\\git\\kit, (c) one train at a time. NEW ORDER: TRAIN40 (built: waits as data, status facts; two model crates still being trimmed) launches first; R3 (the source respell, with R2's shim folded in: one startup copy of each KIT_* to RIG_* when unset, so a single place holds the fallback) is prepared in parallel, one model crate diff goes to the user first, then it rides TRAIN41; the fleet formatter respell follows TRAIN41 (main and compiler asked to hold it until then). R4 (folder, junctions, hooks, scheduled tasks, node and europa) right after TRAIN41 installs, R5 (302 KIT-* ids, the 62 Done team:kit tags and 420 bare kit tags) under the agile lock with a set-hash proof, then R6-R8. NEXT STEP: trim the two TRAIN40 model crates and launch it; draft the R3 model crate diff.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_5 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 5u32, "2026-11-08T12:26Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 08:5x rig, TRAIN41 SEQUENCE (compiler and i574n agreed): TRAIN40 node half (pack61b) then its box install; then compiler's pack62 install-when-clear fires on the box (8 h wait, gated core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE); i574n pack-chains pack62 to node and europa; TRAIN41 launches only after pack62 is live on the box AND the node (launch parity check). TRAIN41 carries R3 (after the user's yes on r3-sample.diff), the config-dir choice already in the tree (kit_path_first config_choice: rig if it exists or no kit dir exists, else kit; 4-case test plus a test that a pipe binds tighter than ||, node proof pending as kit-probe1108b), the gleam build/zig-out skip, the explicit taplo --config and the status-change no-op skip. Compiler is told directly when TRAIN41 installs, then the fleet formatter respell goes. waits on install: TRAIN40")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_6 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 6u32, "2026-11-08T14:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 11:0x rig, post-install check with the TRAIN40 kit (kit.exe 6C4F076B, installed 10:52:57, pack61b core 65DEE79C; node notebooks 66/66 on candidate D5D22429). TRAIN40 is installed. TRAIN41 (R3 respell plus the fixes in the tree) now waits only on pack62 live on the box and the node (compiler install-when-clear polls every 2 min; i574n chains it to node and europa). Recorded as a resume-when row.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_7 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 7u32, "2026-11-08T21:32Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 17:3x rig GROOM: progress fixed from 12 to 35 (R1 Done; R3 applied to the tree and riding TRAIN41, relaunched 15:43). Next step unchanged: TRAIN41 green, then R3b (env, output, binary, paths) with R4 in TRAIN42.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_8 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 8u32, "2026-11-08T22:10Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 18:1x rig: compiler is rolling pack63c (formatter fix, user directive: never wait on pushes, update the compiler everywhere, then reformat drift). Agreed: kit live tree included in the fleet reformat now (R3 edits complete; TRAIN41 runs from its 15:43 snapshot; TRAIN42 carries the reformat; kit state/*.spi and FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md excluded). Condition: pack63c on the BOX waits until TRAIN41 box half installs, because release-train pins the live compiler at the box half first step and a pack63c pin over pack62 code would mislabel TRAIN41; moon is safe (node half pinned its copy at start). rig messages compiler at TRAIN41 install. waits on install: TRAIN41")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_9 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 9u32, "2026-11-08T23:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:2x rig, TRAIN41 INSTALLED 19:12:49 (kit.exe 93BDD93F; release built on moon in the TRAIN41 mirror with pinned pack62 core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE, 583 s, schema and topology checks passed; copy-installed on the box after a sha256 match and a job list + agile next smoke; shipped manifest 1764 files). R3 Done and installed; next R3b + R4 (binary name, env names, output prefix, LOCALAPPDATA paths, hooks, scheduled tasks, folder move) in TRAIN42, built on moon and copy-installed.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_10 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 10u32, "2026-11-08T23:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:5x USER DIRECTION (directly in the rig session): \"we're still using the kit term too much\" and \"groom so this gets prioritized without waiting for my approvals\". So: every remaining rename slice is P0 and NO slice waits on a user approval; the user chose rig and asked for the full rename (11-08 01:0x), so each step proceeds on its own proof (tests, train, hash-verified install, lossless backlog proof). Peer conditions still hold where they protect others: R4 announces its machine window to all lanes and checks no job runs from C:\\home\\git\\kit before moving folders; compiler is told directly when a train installs.\nMEASURED 11-08 19:4x (rig repo, history excluded): 3101 kit words in 675 files: KIT_ env 513 hits / 207 files, output prefix \"kit <verb>\" 1433 / 432, kit.exe 124 / 58, kit- labels and bin names 403 / 217, package.metadata.kit 19 / 18, LOCALAPPDATA/APPDATA kit paths 13 / 11, kit_ identifiers 1. Machine: LOCALAPPDATA\\kit and APPDATA\\kit dirs, repo folder C:\\home\\git\\kit, 4 kit-*.ps1 hooks, 2 kit-* scheduled tasks, the eoie junction. Backlog: 307 KIT-* ids, 67 team:kit tags, 1125 kit-* note authors. Memory: 300 files. Other repos about 200 hits (kit.exe callers).\nORDER: R2 (now the R3b scope) in the tree now, ships in TRAIN42 with R4's code side (built on moon, copy-installed); R4 machine window right after the install; R5 backlog ids under the agile lock with a lossless proof right after R4; R6 memory and docs; R7 workflow names (the GitHub repo is already renamed); R8 retires the KIT_/kit.exe fallbacks after about 7 clean days. Rename slices go ahead of KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR where they compete for the same train.\nDoD: git grep -i kit gives 0 hits in rig and the other own repos outside the history list; 0 KIT-* ids and 0 team:kit tags in the backlog; the binary is rig.exe (kit.exe a one-release copy); hooks, tasks and config dirs named rig. Next step: R2 file edits in the tree. TypeFeatures: the rename_target union (Crate, CargoName, Export, Binary, ConfigDir, EnvVar, OutputPrefix, BacklogId, TeamTag, Hook, Task, Doc) with a count per case as the progress table.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_11 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME", 11u32, "2026-11-10T02:51Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 21:3x rig: waits re-pointed to the train that will actually carry the rename. TRAIN42e never installed, and TRAIN43 and TRAIN43b stopped at regen (rig causes, fixed; see KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN 245/249). KIT-NEXT-NAME, R2 (rig.exe) and R4 (machine move, which needs rig.exe installed) now wait on train:TRAIN43c. Before relaunching: the 21:04 fix plus a test-block keyword trap (a local named then, in experiment_gates.spi) are being probed on ganymede, and a keyword-local sweep over all 188 changed/new .spi found nothing else.")
