inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_1 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 1u32, "2026-11-08T04:40Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "DoD: both names run every verb identically for one release window; env and config read new first, old second; a test per fallback. NEXT STEP: the alias binary and env fallback in the boundary package. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: name_source union (NewName, LegacyName) on every lookup.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_2 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 2u32, "2026-11-08T23:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:5x rig GROOM: re-scoped to R3b (the parts R3 deferred because they couple to the running machine and to callers outside rig): 513 KIT_ env hits, 1433 output-prefix hits, 124 kit.exe, 403 kit- labels and bin names, 19 package.metadata.kit, 13 config-dir paths. P0, no user approval needed (user 11-08). DoD: those counts at 0 outside the one-release fallbacks; every KIT_ read falls back from RIG_ for one release; scripts and parsers outside rig accept both prefixes; TRAIN42 green. Next step: env names with the fallback helper first, then the output prefix with dual-accepting parsers. TypeFeatures: a legacy_name union (Env, Binary, Prefix, Dir) for the fallback table.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_3 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 3u32, "2026-11-09T00:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 20:3x rig PROGRESS, env-name slice written in the live tree (unstaged, originals archived per file under LOCALAPPDATA kit archive r3b-env-before-20261108). Rule for one release: READ RIG_X first then KIT_X; WRITE both; REMOVE both; test runners twin every KIT_ drop and set (rig_cli_check twinned). Mechanical pass: 147 files, 198 Rust reads, 77 Rust .env writes, 10 env_remove, 39 PowerShell sets as RIG = KIT = value chains, 21 PowerShell reads as RIG ?? KIT. Hand edits: 12 Spiral env reads (let pairs, or a file-local variable_of), rust_std_env variable_or_empty (accepts either spelling, RIG first; the host primitive stays one expression as variable_named, style hook clean), agile_lease_terms environment_text, the forward list in legacy_terminal, 5 writes split across raw continuations, RIG_DOTNET in native_compiler.rs. EXCEPTION KIT_JOB_* job-steering names stay write-KIT-only this release: the lib env.environment_restored keeps one prefix, so dual writes would reset RIG_JOB_* to the parent job values in nested jobs; readers still try RIG_ first; the doctor ignores both prefixes. Left as KIT pairs (self-contained, R8): coordinator spool/kit, agile lock holder, dogfood REAL_PYTHON/SHELL overrides, pwsh text embedded in Rust test strings. Proof queued: ganymede job-1794184264456-rig-r3b1108 (regen + cargo check) after job-1794182386809-rig-regen1108 (reformat-only regen), and job-1794184394999-rig-cellbudget1108. Next step: parsers in every repo accept rig and kit output prefixes (lands without a train), then the prefix flips in the train after.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_4 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 4u32, "2026-11-09T00:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 20:5x rig PROGRESS, OUTPUT PREFIX flipped in the live tree for TRAIN42 (was planned for a later train; safe now because every parser accepts both first). Parsers widened to (kit|rig): node-proof.ps1 and idle-with-ready-alarm.ps1 (i574n.github), the kit-style-check hook, launch-train.ps1 (5) and release-acceptance.ps1 (4), tibia pz-in-traces.ps1 (tibia did it), and in the binary rig_remote_activity (job list from older remote kits), rig_status_facts (crate gate log), rig_machine_watch (error lines); dispatch reads the id= token so it was already prefix-free. Flip: 1448 string literals starting with kit plus a verb, in 429 .spi/.rs files, originals archived under LOCALAPPDATA kit archive r3b-prefix-before-20261108. Untouched on purpose: usage text, hints and (kit job <id>) labels that sit mid-literal (producer and parser both unflipped, so consistent; they flip with the binary name), 166 bare kit team names in fixtures, documented commands in guide fixtures (R6). TRAP met and fixed: the flip respelled the old-prefix side of the new dual parsers; restored by hand. Proof: ganymede job-1794184264456-rig-r3b1108 mirror re-synced to this tree (digest 829B37DC), regen + cargo check. Next step: its verdict, then the cell-budget splits, then TRAIN42 on moon.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_5 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 5u32, "2026-11-09T03:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:0x rig, pre-train catches from moon probes and static scans: (1) rust_std_env lacked spiral- in package.spiproj, so the new variable_or_empty (sm' plus ++#) broke regen of 59 dependent crates (rig-r3b1108b partial: 149 ok, 59 errors, all through rust_std_env); fixed by adding spiral- (AGENTS.md rule); r3b1108b stopped and rerun as job-1794193603310-rig-r3b1108c on mirror digest 76A7E304. (2) ASYMMETRIC prefix-flip misses: rig_jobs model label_safe test (input flipped to rig regen, expected kit_regen stayed) -> expected now rig_regen__batch_1_7; rig_job_dispatch remote_line and forward_line tests had their COMMAND expectations flipped to rig job, but those lines invoke the remote binary, which stays named kit until R4 -> reverted to kit job. Static scans found no other same-line asymmetry, no unflipped kit-verb samples in triple-quoted blocks, no concatenated kit prefix. rig_jobs model 9/10 then fixed (probe 1109b); re-probe of rig_jobs + rig_job_dispatch running (rig-probe1109c). RULE for the binary rename (R4/TRAIN43): command lines that invoke the remote binary flip together with the remote installs, not with output text.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_6 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 6u32, "2026-11-09T07:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:0x local rig PRE-CHECK GREEN: ganymede job-1794193603310-rig-r3b1108c (mirror digest 76A7E304: the env-name slice, the output-prefix flip, rig_delegate, the rust_std_env lib fix, compiler's pack63c reformat, the heavy-refusal fix and machine defaults.env): KIT regeneration passed for 374 selected owners, then cargo check finished in 3m 25s (only warning: an unused rig-window-admission dependency in rig-window-wait), exit 0, about 3.6 h at parallel 1 under org's ganymede pins. Edits after that digest (per-machine connect timeout, job metrics labels and peak, wait backoff, launcher guards 8-10, layer Prim, two test-expectation fixes) are covered by moon notebook probes (green: rig_job_bin, rig_exec_metrics, rig_exec_jobs, rig_standards_layers_model, rig_jobs; rig_job_dispatch rerun plus rig_net_crossing running as rig-probe1109h) and by TRAIN42's own node regen. NEXT: TRAIN42 node half on moon when org gives the window (compiler's chain is running there now).")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_7 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 7u32, "2026-11-09T07:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:1x local rig, TRAIN42 LAUNCH PLAN: org approved the moon window after compiler's current link and before its queued timing links (never beside a timing run); waiting on compiler to hold scaling-timed-window, which is chained --after the current link. SDK drift flagged by org3 (moon's cache .NET SDK rc.2 vs rc.3 elsewhere): launch-train's parity gate pins compiler DLL, core and rustc (what fixes the generated code and binary), not the SDK that hosts the compiler; drift check in this train: ganymede's rc.3 regen of the same tree changed 0 .rs outputs, so any regenerated output on moon beyond what post-digest edits explain = SDK drift, stop before install. Not bumping moon's SDK tonight (compiler's moon chain uses it). Follow-up for KIT-TRAIN parity: add the SDK version to the parity line as a logged field.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_8 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 8u32, "2026-11-09T07:07Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:2x moon, local rig: probe1109h (job-1794207689491-rig-probe1109h) GREEN 15/15: rig_job_dispatch 3/3 (ssh_with connect seconds), rig_net_crossing 1/1, rig_jobs model 11/11. Every edit since TRAIN42's pre-check digest is now probed; launch gate left: compiler-split-tests-15files ending on moon (compiler stopped its 3 queued links for the window).")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_9 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 9u32, "2026-11-09T07:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:5x local rig, TRAIN42 running (moon job-1794209289968-kit-TRAIN42, regen phase since 03:28; box coordinator job-1794209054794-kit-TRAIN42-node). Mirror fix while in regen: src/rig_units (unprobed U1 WIP, no manifests, its earlier version failed both tests in TRAIN41) moved out of train25 into the moon archive train42-snapshot-rig-units, so the notebook phase does not run it. Lesson stands: a train snapshots the whole live tree; new packages written after the sync (rig_agile_gap) are not in TRAIN42.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_10 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 10u32, "2026-11-09T07:52Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:0x local rig, launch-train.ps1: the snapshot copy now leaves out every src dir that holds .spi files but no package.spiproj (robocopy /XD per dir, and a Say line names them). Today that is exactly rig_units (tracked in HEAD, unprobed U1 WIP: TRAIN41 failed on it, TRAIN42's mirror had it until moved out by hand). Parse check 0 errors; dry run lists rig_units only. Takes effect from TRAIN43 (TRAIN42's coordinator parsed the old script). Box watcher swapped from kit job wait (busy-poll, org flagged it holding box CPU) to a 5-min check of the coordinator exit file.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_11 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 11u32, "2026-11-09T08:20Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:2x local rig, TRAIN42 FAILED at the crate gate (moon job-1794209289968, exit 1 at 04:06): regen ok (33 changed owners), then agile_task_notes 1043 and agile_task_creation 1012 lines (gate 1000). Cause mine: rust_std_env.variable_or_empty (an inline) gained the KIT_/RIG_ twin branch (prefix test, substring, two reads), about 40 Rust lines at EVERY call site; task_notes read 4 variables through it. Not SDK drift. Fix: rust_std_env.variable_twin <rest> (RIG_ then KIT_, no prefix test; variable_or_empty reuses it), task_notes reads the author once and AI_AGENT/CLAUDECODE plainly, task_creation reads variable_twin AUTHOR (sm'.trim, legacy trim migrated). The ganymede pre-check was green but never ran kit crate gate: next pre-check runs it on the regenerated outputs. Unprobed new packages (rig_agile_gap, rig_do_replacement) held out to drafts TRAIN43-HOLD with their wiring reversed (lock back to HEAD). TRAIN42b launched 04:15 (box coordinator job-1794212127113-kit-TRAIN42b-node); its snapshot left out rig_units by the new rule.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_12 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 12u32, "2026-11-09T08:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:5x local rig: TRAIN42b FAILED in regen (04:32): 19 units with The link: unit X has no unit graph. Root cause in compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1 -Incremental: an unchanged unit is skipped by copying its old .rs, which writes no *.unit.json, so a changed consumer that links it cannot compile (agile_task_annotation, agile_quality_facts, rig_do_model, rig_path_first, rig_heal_nameof skipped at 0 ms; 14 consumers failed, cascading). TRAIN42 had passed only because those linked units had changed inputs then. Fix: a unit any other unit links never takes the skip ($linkedUnits from the link sections). TRAIN42c launched 04:47 (box coordinator job-1794214036006-kit-TRAIN42c-node) with a snapshot = TRAIN42b's tree + this fix: my 12 post-snapshot files (gap verb wiring, rig_do_replacement wiring, toml declared order, read U+FFFD note) and 2 new packages were swapped out to drafts TRAIN43-HOLD for the copy and restored after the snapshot line (04:48:03). Moon probe rig-probe1109j failed twice before starting: node-proof spiral sync tar failed (box-side), not yet diagnosed.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_13 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 13u32, "2026-11-09T09:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 06:3x local rig, TEAM TAG SWEEP (rename slice, P0): 98 tasks still carried pre-rename team tags; retagged with agile edit <id> tags: team:kit and team:eoie -> team:rig, team:management, team:resilience and team:i574n -> team:org (the 11-08 one-team:org rule); other tags untouched, duplicates dropped. 98 of 98 ok, re-scan finds 0 stale team tags. Found while measuring shard sizes for KIT-AGILE-PER-REPO.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_14 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 14u32, "2026-11-09T09:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 06:0x local rig: TRAIN42c passed regen (the linked-unit fix works: 0 no-unit-graph errors) but the crate gate stopped it at 05:49: agile_task_creation 1076. Cause: when the style hook made me migrate the author line to lib sm'.trim, the Rust backend emitted sm'.trim as Spiral code (two scan helpers + a 95-line string_slice, about 170 lines) where rust_std_string.model.trim was one host call. Restored HEAD's rust_std_string.model.trim around variable_twin AUTHOR (the hook objects; justified: lib trim costs ~170 generated lines and breaks the gate; expected size ~HEAD 983 + the twin read). TRAIN42d launched 05:55 (box coordinator job-1794218125277-kit-TRAIN42d-node) = TRAIN42c tree + that one line; my post-42c work (gap, replacement, units + drafts verbs, shards, toml, read note, 16 files + 5 dirs) swapped out for the snapshot and restored after the mirror push (05:58:18).")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_15 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 15u32, "2026-11-09T10:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 06:1x local rig, TRAIN43 PRE-CHECK submitted on ganymede (job-1794218773195-rig-regen1109, free slot 2 of 2, load ~4.7/4 cores so it is slow): mirror rig-regen1108 synced (spiral 156 changed, kit 113 changed, digests 0C0C053B / 50A95A42), stage script rig-regen1109.sh = the 11-08 full regen (parallel 1, 900 s per owner) PLUS kit crate gate . --limit 1000 on the regenerated src (the step the 11-08 pre-check lacked), printing OVER rows and every crate at 950+ lines. Near-gate crates to watch: rig_agile_mutation (992 before the gap arm), do_read (967 + 1 branch), rig_do_edit (951 + link call), rig_cli (905 + 2 routes), agile_task_creation (~983 + twin).")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_16 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 16u32, "2026-11-09T10:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:0x local rig: TRAIN42d died in regen at 06:45 (34 units: Package .../The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin/core is not loaded) because MY moon cleanup at 06:42 (powershell 5.1 Remove-Item -Recurse of 17 rig-probe mirrors + stage dirs + 9 old regen workspaces) followed the mirrors' spiral\\deps junction and deleted the shared C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\deps\\The-Spiral-Language; microblog's verify went VOID on the same gap. Restored from the box's clean checkout (tar sha 62EABCE06088 both ends, 3321 files, HEAD 17654e07, core present), blast radius checked (other shared deps and train25 untouched), all-clear sent to microblog + compiler, memory mirror-delete-follows-deps-junction saved. Moon free disk 11.4 -> 16.4 GB. TRAIN42e launched 06:54 (box coordinator job-1794221691845-kit-TRAIN42e-node) = TRAIN42d's tree (+ rig_agile_shards, probe-green 3/3, no Cargo member, which could not be moved out); held work restored after the 06:58 mirror push. The launcher's node wait is now a 2-min job list poll (org2: the old remote kit job wait busy-polled moon); it takes effect for the coordinator launched after this edit, i.e. TRAIN42e.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_17 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 17u32, "2026-11-09T11:31Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:3x local rig, EARLY READ of the TRAIN43 pre-check on ganymede (rig-regen1109, mirror synced 06:05, so it predates the do_read receipt and job-host nap edits): 233 of ~380 units done, 0 non-ok rows. Generated sizes so far: agile_task_creation 992 (the TRAIN42d/e text: variable_twin + host trim; under the gate, 8 lines of headroom, so TRAIN42e should pass the gate), agile_task_notes 927, rig_agile_gap 949 (agile_add inlined through agile_task_creation). Still pending: rig_agile_mutation (992 before the gap arm, the tightest), rig_do_edit, rig_do_read, rig_cli, rig_units, rig_drafts, rig_do_replacement, rig_read_query.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_18 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 18u32, "2026-11-09T12:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:5x local rig, TRAIN43 PRE-CHECK RESULT (ganymede rig-regen1109, 2 h 20 m, mirror of 06:05): regen exit 1 from ONE root error, rig_drafts/entry.spi:72 ETY-NominalInPatternUnbox (matched Ok/Error on file_system.rename's result' nominal), which also failed rig_cli (it links rig_drafts); every other unit regenerated (378 rows). FIXED: resultm.is_err (file_system.rename into from). The crate gate in that log read the mirror's committed .rs (regen did not publish), so its agile_task_creation 1076 is TRAIN42c's fetched copy, not the new code (the regen output measured 992 earlier). Other crates at 950+ in that gate: rig_agile_mutation 992 (pre-gap-arm), rig_standards_layers_model 996, rig_lint_growth 975, rig_memory_query 976, agile_task_next 983. Next pre-check after TRAIN42e lands, with the post-train probe batch green.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r2_19 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2", 19u32, "2026-11-11T04:38Z", "rig", "11-11 00:4x rig: rig.exe IS INSTALLED (user 11-11: why are we still using kit instead of rig). The TRAIN44b binary D80FDBD7 now sits under both names: %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/bin/rig.exe and kit.exe, and the repo root rig.exe and kit.exe (/rig.exe added to .gitignore). Smoke under the rig name: job list, agile list, lint precheck ok. Every self-call uses current_exe and the gate reads installed-train.txt from the binary's own folder, so both names run every verb identically (the R2 DoD). release-train.ps1 now refreshes rig.exe and kit.exe together in the repo and lane copies, each retired by name. Left for the Cargo slice (rides a train): [[bin]] name kit to rig and kit-dev to rig-dev, then build.ps1 release/rig, release-train and candidate-build target/debug/rig.exe, 7 compiler-contracts test defaults, coverage_run --bin, 5 contract drivers' rig_binary file name, selected_tests CARGO_BIN_EXE_rig-dev. Callers may switch to rig.exe now; kit.exe stays one release (R8 retires it).")
