inl note_of_kit_next_name_r4_2 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R4", 2u32, "2026-11-08T05:01Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 01:0x kit: scope addition from the user's decision: R4 also renames the local folder C:\\home\\git\\kit to C:\\home\\git\\rig, after no job runs from it (check kit job list for a running kit-TRAIN* first), and updates every path that names it (scripts, hooks, remote-machines.json, memories).")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r4_3 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R4", 3u32, "2026-11-08T23:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:5x rig GROOM: P0, no user approval needed (user 11-08). Runs right after TRAIN42 installs, in one window announced to all lanes, after checking no job runs from C:\\home\\git\\kit: folder C:\\home\\git\\kit to rig (junction kit -> rig for one release), LOCALAPPDATA/APPDATA kit to rig with junctions, 4 hooks and 2 scheduled tasks renamed and re-registered with full paths, node/europa/ganymede installs and the registry kit field, the eoie junction removed. Next step: write the window checklist as a dry run.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r4_4 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R4", 4u32, "2026-11-09T00:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 20:4x rig WINDOW CHECKLIST (dry run, inventoried on the box 20:4x). PRE: TRAIN43 installed (rig.exe plus a kit.exe copy); kit job list shows nothing running or queued from C:\\home\\git\\kit; no kit job host alive (idle exit or stop); window announced to all lanes; RustDesk untouched. 1 REPO: move C:\\home\\git\\kit to C:\\home\\git\\rig, junction kit -> rig for one release; the eoie junction (C:\\home\\git\\eoie -> kit) removed, it is only a link. 2 CONFIG: LOCALAPPDATA kit (24 entries: bin, jobs, archive, reports, schedules, retired, windows ...) and APPDATA kit (fleet.spi, lease-policy, path_first.spi, target_limits.spi) move to rig, each with a kit junction, so paths baked into scripts keep working (the comet watchdog script lives under LOCALAPPDATA kit reports); the stale APPDATA eoie folder goes to the archive. 3 HOOKS: kit-backlog-state-guard, kit-style-check, kit-tree-lease, kit-work-in-repo become rig-*.ps1 and settings.json hook entries are updated in one edit; autonomous-gate.ps1 has kit paths inside, respelled; old files archived. 4 TASKS: kit-machine-watch-hourly and kit-unstaged-backup exported to XML in the archive, re-registered as rig-* with full exe paths, each run once and checked, then the old ones unregistered. 5 NODES: moon C:\\home\\bin rig.exe plus kit.exe, ganymede and comet kit paths, the registry kit field and jobs machines .bin files. 6 VERIFY: rig job list and rig agile next answer, kit.exe still answers, each hook fires once, each task ran, git grep finds no C:\\home\\git\\kit path in scripts. Next step: TRAIN42 then TRAIN43, then this window.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r4_5 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R4", 5u32, "2026-11-10T11:27Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 07:3x rig, checklist addition: once a rig config dir exists, config_dir prefers it over the legacy kit dir, so move %APPDATA%\\kit\\.taplo.toml (the bundled TOML-check fallback, TAPLO-KIT-BUNDLED-FALLBACK) and %APPDATA%\\kit\\target_limits.spi into it in the same step, and the same on every node.")
