inl note_of_kit_next_name_r5_2 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R5", 2u32, "2026-11-08T23:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:5x rig GROOM: P0, no user approval needed (user 11-08). 307 KIT-* ids to RIG-*, 67 team:kit tags (Done history included per the DoD), under the agile lock with a set-hash proof like the seal; each renamed item gets a note naming its old id; lanes told once (alias rig=kit already in lane-aliases.txt). Next step: the id map and a dry run on a copy of the state.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r5_3 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R5", 3u32, "2026-11-09T03:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:0x rig DRY RUN on a copy of the backlog (scratchpad r5-dry, live state untouched). ID MAP: 1947 items, 307 KIT-* ids, 13 RIG-* ids, ONE collision: KIT-RENAME (the eoie to kit rename) would land on the existing RIG-RENAME (Done epic), so map it to RIG-RENAME-EOIE; all other 306 map KIT-X to RIG-X. RENAME VERB: kit agile rename is exact (KIT-NEXT-NAME renamed its task row plus 11 note rows, items=12; children KIT-NEXT-NAME-R2..R8 untouched), about 60 s cold then about 6 s per id, so 307 ids take about 30 min under the lock. GAP FOUND: agile rename rewrites state/agile.spi only. parents.spi, claims.spi and waits.spi keep the old id (after renaming KIT-NEXT-NAME: parents 8 refs left, waits 1; after KIT-DRIFT-GUARD: parents 1, claims 1), so a bulk rename would orphan parent links, claims and waits. Side-file totals today: parents 23 KIT ids, claims 23, waits 3. FIX before R5 (TRAIN43): agile rename also rewrites exact quoted ids in parents, claims and waits in the same locked write, with a fixture per file. PROOF for R5: the multiset of ids in every state file, mapped through the table, equals the multiset after (the seal set-hash pattern), and agile check passes. Next step: the side-file rewrite in the rename verb.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r5_4 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R5", 4u32, "2026-11-10T02:55Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:5x rig, R5 PRECONDITION PROGRESS (the side-file gap from the dry run): new pure package src/rig_agile_side_rename/side.spi (HostFree, unstaged) rewrites one id across parents.spi, claims.spi and waits.spi exactly: quoted ids are replaced with their quotes, so KIT-X never touches KIT-X-Y; a row whose FIRST field is the old id also gets its binding renamed (wait_of_kit_x -> wait_of_rig_x, parent_of_, claim_<slug>__declined_<lane> keeps its suffix), while a row that only points at the id (a parent field, an item wait) keeps its own binding; row_change is a GADT (Untouched | Pointing | Owned) and a tally counts rows and bindings for the proof. Probe-green 3/3 on ganymede. Today the side files hold 293 KIT- id occurrences (parents 97, claims 79, waits 117). NEXT: call it from agile rename inside the same locked write (agile_task_rename is legacy host code, so that change migrates the verb per AGENTS.md); rides TRAIN44; then the 307-id run with the set-hash proof.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r5_5 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R5", 5u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:2x rig groom. Next step: call rig_agile_side_rename from agile_task_rename inside the same locked write (migrating that legacy verb per AGENTS.md), with a fixture per side file; then the 307-id run with the set-hash proof.")
inl note_of_kit_next_name_r5_6 () = Note ("KIT-NEXT-NAME-R5", 6u32, "2026-11-10T03:51Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 00:0x rig, R5 WIRING WRITTEN (unstaged, rides TRAIN44). agile rename now renames the id in parents.spi, claims.spi and waits.spi too. Design: the side pass runs BEFORE the agile.spi write, through the new HostFree package (rig_agile_side_rename.side.renamed_sides, read and write passed in as functions, so the pass is testable without IO); the verb supplies the lib file reader and its existing compare-and-replace state_written per side file. A refused side write stops the rename with \"side files not finished (<file>: <reason>); run it again\": a rerun is safe because rows already renamed no longer hold the old id and the old id is still in agile.spi, so no repair mode is needed (a repair mode could wrongly re-point orphan references to an unrelated id). Output gains side_rows=N side_bindings=N. PROOF: side package probe-green 4/4 on ganymede (adds a fake-IO test: claims.spi absent and skipped, a refused write named, the others still written); agile_task_rename and agile_task_notes kit standards 0 findings, ratchet 0 regressions; the train's reference preflight run now: 0 unresolved (the verb's 3 qualified names resolve); crate 408 of 1000 lines before the change. UNPROVEN off-train: the verb itself and the CLI notebook (agile_task_notes/notes_cli.spi now sets a wait on ID-A before the rename and asserts wait_of_id_z with ID-Z and no ID-A left); both run in TRAIN44. Next step: after TRAIN44 is green and installed, run the R5 map (306 KIT-X -> RIG-X plus KIT-RENAME -> RIG-RENAME-EOIE) with the multiset proof per state file.")
