inl org_config_single_source () = Task ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", "One source for org-wide config: no .taplo.toml committed per repo, and no tool/toolchain version duplicated between scripts, settings and workflows", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "org,standards,toml,pins,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_org_config_single_source () = Planning ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_1 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 1u32, "2026-11-08T05:16Z", "main", "USER 11-08 01:0x: 'can we get the same benefits without having to commit .taplo.toml in every repo? same thing about duplicated versions between scripts settings and workflows, gotta reuse somehow with sota (or invented) ways'. Facts: i574n.github/scripts/pins (pins.spi typed source, workflows.spi generator, pins_check) already generates every org workflow channel and x/tibia rust-toolchain.toml; tonight pins_check found exactly the 5 workflow lines a manual bump missed. But scripts (init.ps1, build.ps1 +nightly-..., cells.ex @rust_toolchain, lib rust_testing.spi) repeat the version by hand: 13 spiral files plus lib for one bump. Candidates: (a) the formatter config ships inside rig (kit standards passes taplo --config <rig-owned file> or the equivalent options), so no repo carries .taplo.toml; (b) pins.spi emits ONE generated versions file per repo (or lib exports typed constants) that scripts and cells read, so a bump is one typed edit plus regeneration; (c) the rust-toolchain.toml file is the single pin for cargo/rustc and scripts drop explicit +nightly-... (cargo honors the file), with CI reading the channel from it. TypeFeatures: the typed tool union in pins.spi stays the source; generated artifacts carry a provenance header check. DoD: a toolchain bump is one edit in pins.spi plus one generator run; pins_check covers scripts and cells as well as workflows; .taplo.toml removed from repos with formatting unchanged (fleet diff empty). Next step: inventory every version literal (git grep for nightly-, OTP-, elixir, gleam, zig, bun versions) across org repos and pick (a)/(b)/(c) per tool.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_2 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 2u32, "2026-11-08T12:02Z", "i574n", "USER 11-08 08:0x: 'about the taplo files, yeah advance in a way that we don't need them in the repos'. DONE for taplo (box): option (a) variant. The canonical config is i574n.github/.taplo.toml (the org tooling repo; it is UNTRACKED there and must be committed by the user to become the CI source). User env TAPLO_CONFIG now points at it; taplo 0.10.0 honors TAPLO_CONFIG and --config. PROBE: with an external config, exclude globs (deps/**, **/target/**) match relative to the CWD of the run, so per-repo behavior is unchanged (scratch repo: deps and target skipped, src flagged). The 11 per-repo copies (alphabet blog dice fiscal html regex spiral tibia tictactoe x kit; eoie is a junction to kit) were hash-identical to the canonical and untracked: deleted. Check after: dice fmt --check exit 0 using the canonical; fiscal 1 error = the known generated_cfdi_v4_0/spiral.toml (generator fix rides fiscal's next landing). LEFT: (1) kit standards passes --config <canonical> explicitly (no env dependence, works in old shells and CI) -> rig; (2) CI: workflows that format TOML check out i574n/.github and set TAPLO_CONFIG; (3) node and europa: set TAPLO_CONFIG in User env / profile when they run fmt; (4) versions half (pins) unchanged, see deps audit.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_3 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 3u32, "2026-11-08T12:12Z", "i574n", "Audit 11-08 12:2x (read-only agent; registries queried 11-08; inventory scratchpad cargo-deps.csv + latest.json), the VERSIONS half. pins.spi already single-sources CI tools and action pins (every workflow but tictactoe's matches). Drift outside it: (1) the Rust nightly literal nightly-2026-11-05 is hand-written in about 20 script files (alphabet apps/documents/build.ps1, dice lib/build.ps1, html build.ps1, regex build.ps1, spiral apps/{lisp,wasm,spiral,plot}/build.ps1, apps/compiler/scripts/{try,test,export-check-rust}.ps1, scripts/init-app-build.ps1, init.ps1 x3, init.sh, lib bench/parsing/bench.ps1, i574n.github pins.ps1); trunk 0.21.14 in spiral init.ps1 AND the workflows.spi cache key. (2) Crate drift between repos: regex in 4 spellings (~1.7, 1, 1.10, 1.13.1), serde_json in 3 (kit disagrees with itself), sha2 prerelease ~0.11.0-pre.4 in alphabet/spiral vs 0.11.1 in kit, rayon, clap, tokio, mimalloc, base64, near-sdk =5.11.0 (spiral wasm) vs 5.30.1 (dice), near-workspaces 0.11.1 vs 0.24.0. kit has no [workspace.dependencies]: 287 crates pin alone. (3) .NET: every workflow installs SDK 9.0.202 while the spiral compiler and fiscal bench target net11.0. DECISION (i574n): (a) scripts stop writing +nightly-DATE: cargo honors rust-toolchain.toml, which pins.spi already generates per repo; the scripts that need a channel name read it from that file. (b) Each Rust repo declares versions once in [workspace.dependencies] and members use dep.workspace = true; an org version catalog generated from pins.spi (typed crate -> version) feeds every repo's workspace table, and pins_check fails on any member pinning its own version. (c) Open ranges that already admit breaking releases get upper bounds (mlua >=0.11.4, leptos >=0.8.11, uuid *, and the <1 ranges on 0.x crates: getrandom, gloo-net, rexie, near-sandbox-utils, base64). Next step: (a) first, since it removes 20 hand edits per nightly bump; owners: spiral scripts -> compiler, kit -> rig, rest -> i574n.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_4 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T12:13Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 Cells share of decision (a) DONE (microblog, Cells owner; spiral tree unstaged). spiral apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells.ex no longer hard-codes @rust_toolchain \"+nightly-2026-11-05\". It reads the channel at compile time from spiral/rust-toolchain.toml (which pins.spi generates), with @external_resource, so a bump recompiles Cells, and it exposes Spiral.Cells.rust_channel/0. It raises at compile time if the file has no channel line. The 3 test literals in cells_test.exs (rustc_args, prepare_rust_toolchain listed and install message) now read rust_channel(), plus a shape assertion ^nightly-YYYY-MM-DD$. proof: 2 targeted tests pass (2/2) after the recompile. A bump is now one pins.spi edit + generator run for Cells too. Fixture path text in rustup_proxy_test.exs:7 is sample data, not a pin; left alone. LEFT for the other owners: the ~20 script literals listed in note 3 (alphabet, dice, html, regex, spiral apps + compiler scripts + init, i574n.github pins.ps1).")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_5 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T12:22Z", "org", "11-09 org: decision (a) DONE for the rest->i574n repos. Removed the redundant hand-written +nightly-2026-11-05 from alphabet/apps/documents/build.ps1, html/build.ps1 (x2: build + metadata), regex/build.ps1 (x2), dice/lib/build.ps1 - cargo now resolves the toolchain from each repo's root rust-toolchain.toml (all four pin channel=nightly-2026-11-05, so removal is a PROVABLE no-op: cargo searches up to the root toolchain file and an explicit +toolchain equal to it leaves the resolved toolchain identical). A future nightly bump is now one edit per repo (rust-toolchain.toml) instead of two. Unverified-by-rebuild (documents/html/regex/dice builds not set up on europa) but no-op by cargo's documented override rules; the font build (apps/font-emit/build.ps1) never used +nightly and is unaffected. FOLLOW-UPS: (1) alphabet dist/apps/documents/build.ps1 has a STALE 2025-11-01 literal (generated tree, rides regen not hand-edit); (2) dir-tree-html/build.ps1 uses +nightly-2026-10-18 (different date - check its own rust-toolchain.toml before removing); (3) spiral apps/{wasm,spiral,plot}/build.ps1 and polyglot are compiler's; kit is rig's. Decision (b) workspace.dependencies catalog + (c) open-range upper bounds not started.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_6 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T12:59Z", "org", "11-09 org: decision (a) is now complete for the clean rest->i574n repos (alphabet html regex dice). dir-tree-html is the one remaining rest repo and is a DOCUMENTED EXCEPTION: its build.ps1 uses +nightly-2026-10-18 which matches its OWN rust-toolchain.toml (channel nightly-2026-10-18), so removal there is also a provable no-op - BUT (1) it is the known stale-fork (DIR-TREE-HTML-CI-STALE-FORK: CI red since 11-02, resolves to fc1943s), and (2) it is on an OLD nightly (2026-10-18 vs the fleet's 2026-11-05) = separate drift. Deferring the pin removal there until the fork/CI item is resolved, to avoid touching a problematic fork for a low-value change. So decision (a) 'scripts drop +nightly where the toolchain file pins it' is DONE for every clean org Rust repo; spiral is compiler's, kit is rig's, dir-tree-html deferred. Decisions (b) workspace.dependencies catalog + (c) open-range upper bounds remain.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_7 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T16:26Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09 decision (c) INVENTORY (ripgrep over org Cargo.toml, gitignored deps/target auto-skipped; vendored polyglot/deps/Fable + polyglot temp/extension EXCLUDED as third-party/generated):\nUNBOUNDED (no upper bound - must add one):\n- spiral/apps/spiral/Cargo.toml:31  mlua = \">=0.11.4\"  -> \">=0.11.4,<0.12\"   [owner: compiler]\n- dice/ui/Cargo.toml:31  leptos = \">=0.8.11\"  -> \">=0.8.11,<0.9\"   [owner: dice lane]\n- dice/ui/Cargo.toml:44  uuid = \"*\"  -> \"1\"  (pin major)   [owner: dice lane]\nBOUNDED AT <1 but still admit 0.x-minor breakage (audit wants these tightened to the next 0.x+1):\n- dice/ui:25 base64 \">=0.22,<1\" -> \",<0.23\"; :29 gloo-net \">=0.6,<1\" -> \",<0.7\"; :36 rexie \">=0.5,<1\" -> \",<0.6\"; :43 getrandom \">=0.3,<1\" -> \",<0.4\"\nAPPLICATION: per-owner with a build check (the bound must not exclude the currently-resolved version; uuid 1.x / leptos 0.8.x / mlua 0.11.x are all current, so these are safe no-ops to resolution). near-sandbox-utils from the original audit was not found in current org source (dropped or in deps). This completes the decision-(c) inventory; decision (b) [workspace.dependencies catalog generated from pins.spi] remains unstarted and is the larger piece. org did not edit peer Cargo.tomls (lane boundaries + build-verify needed).")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_8 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T19:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 19:5x decision (c) APPLIED for dice/ui/Cargo.toml (unstaged). CORRECTION to note 7: its proposed bounds would have excluded 4 of the versions dice_ui resolves today (Cargo.lock: base64 0.23.1, gloo-net 0.7.0, rexie 0.6.2, getrandom 0.4.3), so they were not applied as written. Used a caret on the resolved 0.x minor instead (in 0.x every minor is breaking): base64 '0.23', gloo-net '0.7', rexie '0.6', getrandom '0.4', leptos '0.8.11' (caps <0.9), uuid '1' (was '*'). Proof: cargo metadata --locked rc=0 on the box and Cargo.lock untouched, so resolution is identical. Left for (c): spiral apps/spiral mlua '>=0.11.4' -> '0.11.4' is compiler's. Decision (b) (workspace.dependencies catalog generated from pins.spi) still unstarted.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_9 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 9u32, "2026-11-09T19:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 19:5x decision (b) first repo: regex now declares versions once. Root Cargo.toml gains [workspace.dependencies] (regex = '1', rx_external/rx_crate paths); bench and units/rx_crate use { workspace = true }. bench drops its direct regex dependency: its host.spi kept 3 regex bindings duplicated from units/rx_crate plus 2 dead ones (os_name, arch_name, no uses anywhere), all removed, so only the rx_crate unit links the regex crate. cargo metadata rc=0; the end-to-end proof is regex build 6 (after swap5). Survey so far: dice has [workspace.dependencies] (18 refs, 42 own pins left), html none (9 members, 65 own pins), regex done; kit's 287 crates are rig's.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_10 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 10u32, "2026-11-09T20:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof (regex slice of decision b): ganymede job org2-b6 exit 0 at 20:5x: REGEX-OK, Cells 131/131 over 22 files, bench.rs calls rx_external:: 2x and rx_crate:: 2x (the linked units), and cargo tree -p bench --depth 1 shows 0 direct regex crate deps; only units/rx_crate (84-line rs) links regex, through [workspace.dependencies]. Next for (b): html (9 members, 65 own pins) and dice's remaining 42, then a pins.spi-generated catalog.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_11 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 11u32, "2026-11-09T21:29Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 21:3xZ decision (b) for dice: borsh (3 members) and serde_json (2) moved into root [workspace.dependencies]; members use { workspace = true } (ui keeps its extra borsh features additively). Root chrono/futures tightened from >=0.x,<1 to caret '0.4'/'0.3' (resolved 0.4.45 / 0.3.34). Proof: cargo metadata --locked rc=0, Cargo.lock untouched. html checked: 0 registry deps (all 34 member deps are path links between its own units), so nothing to centralize there. Org Rust repos now single-source their crate versions per repo: regex, dice; html has none. Left for (b): the pins.spi-generated org catalog across repos; kit (rig) and spiral apps (compiler).")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_12 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 12u32, "2026-11-09T22:36Z", "org-614162e5", "11-09 18:3x org-614162e5 (resilience, node-config half - cross-team, read-only probe). The taplo item-(3) LEFT loose-end (node + europa set TAPLO_CONFIG when they run fmt) is UNMET, quantified: BOX ok (TAPLO_CONFIG=C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\.taplo.toml, canonical present). MOON (wifi) TAPLO_CONFIG UNSET + no canonical at C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\.taplo.toml (moon has no i574n.github checkout at that path). EUROPA TAPLO_CONFIG UNSET + taplo NOT INSTALLED at all + no canonical. PRACTICAL IMPACT is LOW right now: europa cannot run taplo fmt (binary absent) so it formats no TOML; moon runs fmt only if a lane drives it there, unverified. So this is a real-but-low-urgency DoD loose-end, not a live drift source. To CLOSE it properly when wanted: a node needs BOTH the canonical .taplo.toml present (ship it or checkout i574n.github) AND TAPLO_CONFIG pointing at it in the non-interactive env (User env on Windows twins; profile/env on Linux) - the same non-interactive-PATH-parity discipline as DELEGATE-5 toolchain checks (a var set only in an interactive shell is absent to an ssh-launched fmt). Until then the box + CI remain the only places the single config is honored. Not claiming this item (org2 active on the versions half); flagging the node half as measured + open for whoever closes node/CI.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_13 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 13u32, "2026-11-09T22:55Z", "org-614162e5", "11-09 18:5x org-614162e5 (resilience, taplo/CI half audit - read-only, distinct from org2 versions half). AUDITED how kit standards resolves + uses the taplo config (kit/src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi + generated toml.rs toml_verdict_of_5). FINDINGS: (1) GOOD - the toml check is TYPED + FAIL-CLOSED: verdict_of with config=empty returns ConfigMissing ('no config is a refusal, never a default run', message 'toml refused: TAPLO_CONFIG is unset'), with a test asserting it. So kit standards NEVER silently formats with taplo's wrong defaults when the canonical config is absent - it REFUSES. That is the right discipline (a missing config is not a clean pass). (2) RESOLUTION ORDER: local <root>/.taplo.toml if present -> else TAPLO_CONFIG env -> else empty=refuse. Since the per-repo .taplo.toml were all deleted (item done), org repos now rely on the TAPLO_CONFIG env. (3) GAP for note-1 item (1) 'pass --config explicitly, no env dependence, works in old shells and CI': PARTIALLY met - the resolved config IS passed to taplo, and absence fail-closes (safe), BUT resolution still DEPENDS on the env (or a local file); there is NO kit-bundled canonical fallback. So any host running kit standards WITHOUT TAPLO_CONFIG (CI job, node, fresh shell) REFUSES the toml check (red), rather than drifting - safe but blocks the check. CONCRETE CLOSE (rig, who owns rig_standards_toml): ship the canonical .taplo.toml INSIDE kit's install tree and fall back to it when both local-file and env are absent -> kit standards then always has the canonical config with ZERO env setup on any host, fully delivering 'no env dependence'. Pairs with my node-env finding (note 12): nodes lack both the env AND the file; a kit-bundled fallback closes both at once. Not claiming (org2 active on versions half); taplo/CI half audited + the one concrete rig step named.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_14 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 14u32, "2026-11-10T00:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:4x rig, progress for the taplo leg (no claim, no wait change): kit's TOML check (src/rig_standards_toml/toml.spi, kit standards --toml <repo>) now resolves the config TAPLO_CONFIG-FIRST: when the env var names the canonical i574n.github/.taplo.toml it always wins, and a repo-local .taplo.toml is only a fallback when the variable is unset (before 11-09 a stray repo copy silently overrode the canonical one). It refuses (exit 2, NoConfig) when neither resolves, never running taplo's defaults. Probe-green 2/2 on ganymede, unstaged, rides kit TRAIN44. Not done for this item: flagging a committed repo .taplo.toml as a finding (the check ignores it rather than reporting it).")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_15 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 15u32, "2026-11-10T04:30Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 04:3xZ decision (b) catalog DRAFTED (unstaged, not yet registered): i574n.github/scripts/pins/crates.spi, a typed crate union (Regex, Borsh, SerdeJson, Chrono, Futures) with crate_name / crate_version / crate_features, crate_line and workspace_dependencies (list crate) emitting a repo's [workspace.dependencies] block; dice_crates/regex_crates list each repo's set. Org versions resolved: regex '1.10' (regex repo had '1', dice '1.10'; regex resolves 1.13.1, so both are satisfied), borsh 1.5, serde_json 1.0 + arbitrary_precision, chrono 0.4, futures 0.3. 2 rust tests (a line with features; the regex repo block). Budget 0. Next step: gate it on a node mirror of scripts/pins (packageDir ../../../spiral/lib), register it in scripts/pins/spiral.toml only after green, then extend pins_check to compare each repo's root Cargo.toml table with the generated block.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_16 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 16u32, "2026-11-10T04:36Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 04:4xZ decision (b) catalog GREEN and registered: scripts/pins/crates.spi gated on a ganymede mirror of scripts/pins (job org2-crates rc=0 2/2), then added to scripts/pins/spiral.toml before pins_check (registered only after green). Next step: ORG-CONFIG-PINS-CHECK-CRATES wires pins_check to compare dice's and regex's root [workspace.dependencies] with workspace_dependencies (dice_crates / regex_crates); after that, switch regex's root table to regex '1.10' to match the catalog.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_17 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 17u32, "2026-11-10T05:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 05:2xZ found 2 unsourced toolchain files: html/rust-toolchain.toml and regex/rust-toolchain.toml pin nightly-2026-11-05 by hand, outside workflows.spi targets, so a pins.spi bump would skip both repos. Drafted (scratch, not on box yet): workflows.spi adds html, regex and i574n.github rust-toolchain.toml targets (rendered = rust_toolchain []), and pins.ps1 drops its own hand-written rustc +nightly-2026-11-05 (rustup reads the new i574n.github/rust-toolchain.toml). End-to-end proof: ganymede job org2-pins4 runs pins.ps1 on the mirror with these edits, plus the dice/regex crate table check. Next step: after org2-pins4 is green, org2 copies workflows.spi, pins.ps1 and i574n.github/rust-toolchain.toml to the box.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_18 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 18u32, "2026-11-10T05:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 applied on the box after the green end-to-end run (org2-pins4 plus a resynced dist/workflows rerun: 0 differ): workflows.spi 37555c91c091 adds html, regex and i574n.github rust-toolchain.toml targets, so all 9 org toolchain files (alphabet blog dice spiral tibia x html regex i574n.github) now come from pins.spi; pins.ps1 221cc9aab063 dropped its own rustc +nightly-2026-11-05 (rustup reads the new i574n.github/rust-toolchain.toml 9c3cb929f7cc, not ignored, unstaged). A nightly bump is now one pins.spi edit plus one pins.ps1 run for every org repo. LEFT outside org: spiral apps scripts (compiler), kit (rig), dir-tree-html stale fork (deferred), taplo node env + kit-bundled fallback (rig). Next step: org2 asks compiler and rig whether their remaining +nightly literals can read the generated toolchain file the same way.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_19 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 19u32, "2026-11-10T05:48Z", "compiler", "11-10 02:0x compiler: spiral literals 10 -> 2 (unstaged). DROPPED where cargo/rustc runs inside spiral/ (rust-toolchain.toml applies): apps/{plot,spiral,wasm}/build.ps1 (-Location ../../workspace), apps/lisp/build.ps1 and scripts/init.ps1 (both Set-Location $PSScriptRoot). NOT a no-op for apps/compiler/scripts/{test,try,export-check-rust}.ps1: they compile generated code in cache dirs OUTSIDE the tree (test.ps1 Invoke-Native ... $dir), where rustup uses its default toolchain; on the box that is nightly 2026-10-17, not the pinned 11-04 build, so a plain drop would have silently moved every Rust test row to another compiler. Those now call a new env.ps1 Get-SpiralRustPin, which READS the channel from spiral/rust-toolchain.toml (so pins.spi stays the single source) and returns +<channel> only when a rustup executable sits next to the rustc (replaces the old \".cargo/bin in the path\" test, which missed /usr/local/cargo/bin installs). Proven on the box from %TEMP%: helper -> +nightly-2026-11-05; rustc in the try/export form and the test.ps1 form both report nightly 2026-11-04 (the pinned build); a non-rustup rustc path gives no pin; 9 edited scripts parse with 0 errors. LEFT for lib (lib code, generated commands whose cwd is the crate dir, likely outside the tree): lib/spiral/rust_testing.spi:36 and lib/spiral/bench/parsing/bench_kit.spi:125; same trap applies. Next step: lib replaces those two with the toolchain-file channel or a crate-local rust-toolchain.toml.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_20 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 20u32, "2026-11-10T05:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 checked compiler's cwd correction (note 19: rustup reads the toolchain file from the working directory, so a +channel drop is a no-op only where cargo or rustc runs under the pinned tree) against org's drops: pins.ps1 runs rustc in i574n.github/scripts/pins under the generated i574n.github/rust-toolchain.toml (ganymede printed the pinned 2026-11-04 build there); alphabet/apps/documents, html, regex and dice/lib build.ps1 run cargo in their own repo root or deps/spiral/apps/cells, never a cache dir. All hold. LEFT: lib/spiral/rust_testing.spi and lib/spiral/bench/parsing/bench_kit.spi (out-of-tree crate dirs, need the env.ps1 Get-SpiralRustPin pattern or the same read of spiral/rust-toolchain.toml); kit 0 literals; dir-tree-html deferred; taplo node env (rig). Next step: after lib owners move those two lib files to the read-the-pin pattern, org2 closes this item.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_21 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 21u32, "2026-11-10T05:59Z", "compiler", "11-10 02:1x compiler (answers the lane:compiler wait on the two lib files): lib/spiral/rust_testing.spi DROPPED (unstaged, string-only edit, no typing effect): its cargo test runs in file_system::get_source_directory (), which is CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR on Rust and __SOURCE_DIRECTORY__ on F#; the only caller is apps/spiral/spiral.spi (rust_testing.run_tests), whose crate builds in spiral/workspace via apps/spiral/build.ps1, so both dirs sit under spiral/rust-toolchain.toml (no fsharp dir exists in the tree) and the drop is a no-op. lib/spiral/bench/parsing/bench_kit.spi:125 is NOT a pin: the string is benchmark INPUT for the command-line parser bench (case cli_cargo beside quoted-argument cases, with fake C:/repo paths) and is never executed; editing it would only change the bench data, so it stays and does not count against the single source. spiral now has 0 executed +nightly literals; a nightly bump is one pins.spi edit.")
inl note_of_org_config_single_source_22 () = Note ("ORG-CONFIG-SINGLE-SOURCE", 22u32, "2026-11-10T06:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 CLOSE: org's DoD is met. All 9 org rust-toolchain.toml files are generated from pins.spi (workflows.spi), every org workflow pin is checked by pins_check, dice and regex [workspace.dependencies] are checked against crates.spi, and spiral's tracked +nightly literals are gone or read the generated pin via env.ps1 Get-SpiralRustPin (compiler notes 19 and 21; rust_testing dropped as a no-op, bench_kit:125 is parser bench input, not a pin). A nightly bump is one pins.spi edit plus one pins.ps1 run. Per-repo .taplo.toml removed 11-08. Correction: org2 re-added a lane:compiler wait after note 21 had already answered it; cleared. Outside org and tracked elsewhere: kit-bundled taplo fallback and node TAPLO_CONFIG (rig, notes 13-15), dir-tree-html's own +nightly-2026-10-18 (DIR-TREE-HTML-CI-STALE-FORK).")
