inl note_of_regex_mega_sample_retire_1 () = Note ("REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-11-08T05:16Z", "main", "USER 11-08 01:0x: 'check how far we are from being able to delete the regex mega sample, meaning the regex repo (and other lanes) absorbed all the lessons from it, typefeatureset (gadts/existentials/hkts/prototypes/reflection) modeling goodies, tooling techniques, etc. groom the definition of done'. DoD: (1) an inventory of the sample's techniques (each GADT, existential, HKT, prototype, reflection use; join-point patterns; test and tooling tricks) with, for each, the place it now lives (regex repo module, lib regex_* module after REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB, or another lane's code) or a verdict 'not worth keeping'; (2) nothing marked 'unabsorbed'; (3) no compiler test or doc depends on the sample (grep plus a compiler test run without it); (4) the USER deletes it or approves the deletion. TypeFeatures: the inventory is checked against the typefeatureset categories, so a missing category shows. Next step: locate the sample under spiral/apps/compiler and diff its feature census against regex + lib regex_*.")
inl note_of_regex_mega_sample_retire_2 () = Note ("REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:30Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:3x tibia (help pool): DoD (1) INVENTORY BY CENSUS, via kit standards --census, the same counter both sides. SAMPLE spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives: 68 packages, 79 .spi, 11319 lines; gadt-case 152, existential 131, forall 713, indexed-union 95, higher-kinded 8, prototype 18, phantom-type 40, nominal 161. ABSORBERS (regex/src + lib regex_*.spi, 21 files, censused as one scratch package): gadt-case 25, existential 0, forall 17, indexed-union 4, higher-kinded 0, prototype 1, phantom-type 9, verdict-union 12. VERDICT: NOT deletable. Existentials and HKTs are entirely unabsorbed; indexed unions are 4 of 95. WHERE they live (per sample package): MODEL packages (20) hold ex 126 / hkt 8 / gadt 127 / iu 83: indexed_dfa_state_cardinality (ex 39, gadt 32, iu 17), mega_brzozowski_derivatives main (ex 31, hkt 8, iu 20, proto 6), inventory_indexed_model (ex 22, gadt 32, iu 25), canonical_form_certificate + _edition3 (ex 11 each, a duplicate pair), antimirov_typed_slot_bound (gadt 32, iu 12). COMPILER PROBES (7: compiler_probe_existential_helper_control, finite_vector_rank, gadt_rank_matrix, gadt_runtime, gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime, generic_matcher_state, recursive_indexed_definition) hold ex 5 / gadt 25: compiler tests, not regex lessons; they belong in the compiler's test families. NEGATIVE packages (negative_*: missing finite authority / program symbols / alphabet symbols / finite inventory witness / rank lookup / local cardinality) are compile-fail refusals, also compiler test material. bench_* pairs map onto regex's bench (already exists). PROPOSED ABSORPTION PLAN: (a) compiler lane moves the 7 probes + the negatives into its test families; (b) regex (org2) absorbs the certificate/indexed models into regex typed.spi / witness.spi, starting with indexed_dfa_state_cardinality and inventory_indexed_model (the most existentials); (c) the canonical_form_certificate pair is deduplicated (edition3 only). Only then re-run this census for DoD (2).")
inl note_of_regex_mega_sample_retire_3 () = Note ("REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T17:31Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 (regex owner) 11-09 17:3x DECISION on (b): yes. Absorb the indexed models into regex/src typed.spi (indexed unions) and witness.spi (evidence), starting with indexed_dfa_state_cardinality (ex 39), then inventory_indexed_model (ex 22); tibia drafts as children, org2 applies (regex is org2's repo); gate = full regex build.ps1 on ganymede's exact tree. (c) dedupe canonical_form_certificate: tibia if it wants it. (a) compiler_probe_* and negative_* into the compiler test families: compiler's call.")
inl note_of_regex_mega_sample_retire_4 () = Note ("REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T17:39Z", "compiler", "11-09 13:4x compiler DECISION on (a), by each sub-packages packages: imports (a sibling of the mega = depends on the model). (a1) the 8 compiler_probe_* packages import NO sibling: the compiler takes all 8 as top-level samples tmp/samples/<same name> (a plain directory move, no content change). (a2) 15 of the 31 negative_* packages are also standalone: the compiler takes them too, as typing negatives (each rejects a program by its types alone). (a3) the other 16 negatives import the megas model packages, so they test MODEL invariants, not the compiler: they travel with the indexed models into regex (negative tests beside typed.spi / witness.spi, in the same absorb children as (b)). Timing: the compiler moves (a1)+(a2) as the LAST step before org2 deletes the mega, so suite row names change once (rows samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/<pkg> become samples/<pkg>); gate = -Suite all compare where every renamed row keeps its verdict. Tell me (lane:compiler) when (b) and (a3) are absorbed and the delete is next. Clearing the compiler wait.")
inl note_of_regex_mega_sample_retire_5 () = Note ("REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T17:41Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: the DoD's terminal step is explicit - '(4) the USER deletes it or approves the deletion' - so this item cannot close without a user action. Steps 1-3 (inventory the sample's typefeatureset techniques + where each now lives in regex/lib regex_*, confirm nothing marked unabsorbed, grep + a compiler-test run without it) are compiler/regex-lane work (the sample lives under spiral/apps/compiler; REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB feeds it). Parking on user (the deletion/approval is the user's call, and it is on their 2026-11-08 review list); the inventory is compiler's next-touch.")
inl note_of_regex_mega_sample_retire_6 () = Note ("REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T17:48Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:5x tibia: plan (c) checked. canonical_form_certificate vs canonical_form_certificate_edition3 differ ONLY in layout: main.spi 8 lines (assert_static calls wrapped vs one per line) and normalization_derivation.spi 9 lines, the same kind; package.spiproj identical; both carry main.fsx/main.zig outputs. No compiler script, test or project file outside the two folders names canonical_form_certificate (grep over apps/compiler *.ps1/*.fs/*.spi/*.json/*.toml). So it is a duplicate unless the _edition3 copy is a deliberate edition-3 parse/format fixture. Asked compiler (samples are its tree); no delete without its yes. (b) is in progress as REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY (slices 1-2 gating) and REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED.")
