inl note_of_rig_next_product_census_1 () = Note ("RIG-NEXT-PRODUCT-CENSUS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T05:17Z", "main", "USER 11-08 01:0x: the x -> microblog migration teaches how organic growth went wrong (client, then xsim outside, absorption, Spiral rewrite, archive). The same will happen to kit: a new repo with a new product name, rewritten bit by bit, most-used features first (or newly invented ones), iggy plus a Gleam/Rust balance from day one, typefeatureset everywhere, never lazily copying files. DoD: a census table of every rig verb and module with use counts (hooks, lanes' transcripts and scripts, schedules) and a keep/drop/redesign verdict each, plus a ranked first-slice list for the rewrite. Next step: rig drafts the census source (command-usage counts from logs and transcripts) after RIG-RENAME.")
inl note_of_rig_next_product_census_2 () = Note ("RIG-NEXT-PRODUCT-CENSUS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T19:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, PREMISE RE-CHECKED: the wait-for was RIG-RENAME, which is Done (100%), so this is unblocked. CENSUS SOURCE, STATIC HALF (hooks, repo scripts, scheduled tasks; 74 files plus every task action; pattern kit|rig[.exe] <verb>): agile 11 (2 hooks, 9 scripts), job 9 (2 hooks, 5 scripts, 2 tasks), window 3, do 3, schedule 2, lint 1, standards 1, crate 1, machine 1 (the hourly watch task); the other 29 top-level verbs have NO static caller: status, ci, process, env, backlog, story, standup, evidence, heal, hook, mirror, resume, guide, adoption, run, experiment, kill, ps, edit, grep, lines, read, table, repo, proxy, bundle, patch, memory, metrics. CAVEAT: lower bounds, since callers through a variable ($kitExe agile ...) are missed (kit-style-check runs standards yet counts 0 here); the backlog/story/standup aliases duplicate agile by design. So static use cannot drop anything: the deciding signal for those 29 is interactive use in transcripts, which kit adoption --days N already computes. NEXT: run kit adoption --days 14 --out <tsv> when the box is free (it walks every transcript: box compute, not while the user is present) or on a node copy, then join both halves into the keep/drop/redesign table.")
inl cells_html_outputs_all_repos () = Task ("CELLS-HTML-OUTPUTS-ALL-REPOS", "Every repo's useful test-cell outputs are generated as HTML and reachable from html's dir tree (the nbdev vision via test asserts)", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "cells,html,dir-tree,docs,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_html_outputs_all_repos () = Planning ("CELLS-HTML-OUTPUTS-ALL-REPOS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_html_outputs_all_repos_1 () = Note ("CELLS-HTML-OUTPUTS-ALL-REPOS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T05:17Z", "main", "USER 11-08 01:0x: check all repos for important HTML files missing from generation by test-cell output and from html's dir tree. No comments or docs in repos, but useful test assert outputs (like the handcrafted lib of the pre-vibecoding era) may be the SOTA way to reach the original nbdev vision, better than the dib attempt. DoD: per repo, a list of test files whose cell output HTML is generated and linked from the dir tree; missing ones fixed or justified; a census check fails CI when a test file has no generated page. TypeFeatures: the page set is derived from the test index (document test_index), not a hand list. Next step: census the generated HTML per repo vs the test files (Cells test_index), starting with spiral lib and regex.")
inl note_of_cells_html_outputs_all_repos_2 () = Note ("CELLS-HTML-OUTPUTS-ALL-REPOS", 2u32, "2026-11-11T01:50Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 census first-probe (2026-11-10 21:50, bounded — full census left for a timed pull): regex has 19 .spi files but NO .html / test_index / dist|docs|html output dir at repo depth<=3. So the census structure is NOT per-repo-local for regex — either regex generates no HTML pages yet (then every regex test file is \"missing\" = the gap the item hunts), OR the generated pages live centrally in html/ dir-tree (the item tags include dir-tree). SHARPENED NEXT STEP: first establish WHERE generated test-cell HTML lands (grep html repo dir-tree for regex/spiral page links, and check Cells document test_index output path) BEFORE counting per-repo; the census is \"test_index entries\" vs \"pages the dir-tree links\", and TypeFeatures wants the page set derived from test_index not a hand list. Start: locate html dir-tree generation + one repo Cells test_index, then diff.")
inl note_of_cells_html_outputs_all_repos_3 () = Note ("CELLS-HTML-OUTPUTS-ALL-REPOS", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:51Z", "org-f33af161", "SCOPING FINDING (bounded probe, 21:51): per-test-file HTML generation LARGELY DOES NOT EXIST yet. spiral/lib has 9 .html but all are APP artifacts (near/wallet dist/index.html, playwright-report), not test-cell pages; regex has 0; html_pages/html_walk/cli .spi show no test_index/cell-output HTML scanning. So this item is more BUILD than AUDIT: the \"missing\" set ~= every test file, and the DoD \"missing ones fixed or justified + census CI check\" means (1) STAND UP the test-cell -> HTML page pipeline (Cells document test_index -> a generated page per test block), (2) have html dir-tree link them, (3) a census CI that fails when a test_index entry has no page. Revised next step: design the test_index -> page emission first (one repo, e.g. regex, as the pilot), not an audit of non-existent pages. This likely raises the item estimate (build, not audit) — flag for the owner to re-size.")
inl lane_work_model () = Task ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", "Typed model for lane vs non-lane work so the management lane knows what it can pull (no 'others' bucket)", Story, P1, D4, 35u32, Active, "", "rig,backlog,lanes,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lane_work_model () = Planning ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lane_work_model_1 () = Note ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", 1u32, "2026-11-08T05:17Z", "main", "USER 11-08 01:0x: rig should model task management for lane vs non-lane work; the management lane must know what it can pull, without sloppily calling something an 'others' bucket. Sketch: every item has an owner kind as a closed union (Lane name | Role capability, e.g. Coordination, NodeOps, Grooming, Resilience) plus the required capabilities (CpuHeavy, NodeAccess, WindowsDesktop, LibLand); a lane declares its capabilities, and next/gate offer items whose requirements it satisfies. TypeFeatures: owner and capability unions; next derives pullability from them. DoD: agile next --as management returns only items it can do; no 'others'/'misc' tag remains; lint flags items with no owner kind. Next step: rig drafts the union with AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA (same field family).")
inl note_of_lane_work_model_2 () = Note ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", 2u32, "2026-11-08T05:27Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-08 01:3x kit SKETCH (main 01:0x: typed lane vs non-lane work, no others bucket, same field family as AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA). DATA: a state module beside waits.spi, owners.spi, one row per item: inl owner_of_<slug> () = Owner (\"ID\", kind, value), kind in lane | role | user | machine. kit maps it onto owner_kind = LaneOwned of lane | RoleOwned of capability | UserOwned | MachineOwned of machine (a GADT; an unknown kind word is reported, never bucketed). CAPABILITIES: requires.spi rows Requires (\"ID\", capability) with capability = Compiler | Gpu | NodeHeavy | BoxOnly | UserDecision | Network, so main sees what a lane CAN pull: an item is pullable by a lane when its owner is that lane or a role the lane holds and every required capability is one the lane holds (lane capabilities come from config rows, not code). VERBS: rig agile edit <root> <ID> --owner <kind:value> and --requires <cap,cap> (the --wait shape). NEXT AND GATE: agile next --as <lane> ranks only pullable, non-waiting items; the gate's ready line uses the same predicate, and items owned by UserOwned or needing UserDecision go to a user line instead of any lane. MIGRATION: today team:<t> tags map to LaneOwned t; user-batch tags map to UserOwned; untagged items are listed by lint (ProseWait's sibling, OwnerMissing), not silently pooled. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: owner_kind and capability as GADTs; pullable as one predicate (lane, item) shared by next, gate and lint. NEXT STEP: after TRAIN40 ships the waits module, add owners.spi with the same writer and reader shape, then the predicate.")
inl note_of_lane_work_model_3 () = Note ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:47Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:1x local rig, PREDICATE CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch) from the 11-08 sketch: src/rig_lane_work/work.spi (pure, HostFree). owner_kind LaneOwned lane | RoleOwned role | UserOwned | MachineOwned machine; capability Compiler | Gpu | NodeHeavy | BoxOnly | UserDecision | Network; lane_profile { lane; roles; holds } (from config rows, not code); owner_of word value reads an Owner row and returns UnknownOwner for any other word, so \"others\" is reported, never bucketed (the user's ask); pullable profile owner requires is true only when the lane owns it or holds its role AND holds every required capability, and never for a user item or one needing UserDecision (those go to the user line). Test covers own lane, held role with and without the capability, another lane's item, the user cases, and the unknown-owner refusal. NEXT: owners.spi and requires.spi rows (the waits.spi shape) with agile edit --owner/--requires, then agile next --as <lane> and the gate's help pool using pullable instead of the team tag.")
inl note_of_lane_work_model_4 () = Note ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_lane_work_model_5 () = Note ("LANE-WORK-MODEL", 5u32, "2026-11-09T22:11Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, STATE ROW CODEC BUILT (unstaged): src/rig_lane_work/rows.spi, the recorded next step's first half: owner rows inl owner_of_<slug> () = Owner (\"ID\", kind, value) and requires rows inl requires_of_<slug>_<capability> () = Requires (\"ID\", \"Gpu\"), one row per capability, slug and quote rules copied from waits.spi so the files read like the waits state. owners_of_text / requires_of_text read rows back; capability_of maps the closed six words and reports anything else as UnknownCapability word, and an unknown owner kind reads as UnknownOwner (no bucket). proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (rows 1/1): the written owner row exactly, reading it back among other lines, two capability rows, an unknown capability and an unknown owner kind both named. kit standards 0, ratchet clean. NEXT: agile edit --owner/--requires writing these rows into state/owners.spi and state/requires.spi, then agile next --as <lane> and the gate's help pool calling pullable; both edit the shared agile entry, so after TRAIN43 snapshots.")
