inl note_of_microblog_server_3 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-SERVER", 3u32, "2026-11-08T12:39Z", "microblog", "Design constraint (user 11-08): the server is not Gleam-only. Every server part that needs rayon-style data parallelism (world build and merge, feed building, the lossless import census, search) is a Rust bin, called from the Gleam/OTP serve through a typed boundary: M2 (LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH verdict), model types in one linked model unit, concrete exports only, no string-in/string-out wires. Placement per component follows BACKEND-BALANCE and GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT, recorded as a typed placement row. TYPEFEATURES: backend placement union (Gleam for OTP/subjects, Rust for rayon/crossbeam) per component.")
