inl note_of_deps_refresh_compiler_1 () = Note ("DEPS-REFRESH-COMPILER", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:12Z", "i574n", "USER 11-08 08:0x 'also check for updated versions in the deps for the org's repos'. Audit 11-08 12:2x (read-only agent; registries queried 11-08; inventory scratchpad cargo-deps.csv + latest.json). Declared in spiral compiler Packages.props: FSharp.Control.AsyncSeq 3.2.1 (latest 4.15.0), System.Reactive 6.0.1-preview.1 (7.0.0), System.Reactive.Linq 6.0.1-preview.1 (6.1.0 stable), Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR.Client 7.0.0 (10.0.14; 11.0 rc.3 matches net11.0), System.Management 9.0.4 (10.0.14), Argu 6.2.4 (6.2.5). Also: CI installs dotnet SDK 9.0.202 (pins.spi) while the compiler targets net11.0. A pack ships it (compiler cache and packs). DoD: compiler builds and the pack gates pass on the refreshed packages; prereleases replaced by stable where one exists. Next step: check which of these are still referenced at all (SignalR, AsyncSeq) before bumping; delete unused ones instead.")
inl note_of_deps_refresh_compiler_2 () = Note ("DEPS-REFRESH-COMPILER", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:28Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:3x compiler: DRAFTED drafts\\spiral\\DEPS-REFRESH-COMPILER\\1-compiler-packages.kitdo (6 replacements in apps/compiler/tmp/compiler/lib/Packages.props; applies cleanly): Argu 6.2.4 -> 6.2.5, FSharp.Control.AsyncSeq 3.2.1 -> 4.15.0 (major), Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR.Client 7.0.0 -> 10.0.14 (the latest STABLE; the 11.0 rc stays out under the items stable-over-prerelease rule), System.Management 9.0.4 -> 10.0.14, System.Reactive 6.0.1-preview.1 -> 7.0.0 (major, prerelease -> stable), System.Reactive.Linq 6.0.1-preview.1 -> 6.1.0 (stable). GATE PLAN: build.ps1 -CoreSource reads Packages.props from the tree it runs in, so the gate needs a scratch copy of the node mirrors apps/compiler with the props applied, then build there plus the suite against the same core without the bump (the AsyncSeq/Reactive majors are where API breaks would show). The CI SDK pin (9.0.202 in pins.spi vs net11.0) is a separate org item. Next step: run that gate on a node with a free slot.")
