inl note_of_microblog_profile_avatars_1 () = Note ("MICROBLOG-PROFILE-AVATARS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:15Z", "management-f33af161", "User 11-08: fetch the latest avatar image we can find for each profile/account (fc1943s and the rest) and serve them, so the timeline avatar-gutter (currently a gray placeholder circle from the 516px-column layout work) shows the real avatar. Approach options: (a) the avatar URL may already be in the harvested account/profile data; (b) else fetch via the x syndication/profile path (see syndication-returns-engagement-and-entities, x-tweet-recovery-syndication). Download + serve under media_root (same symlink-into-media_root pattern just used for the Chirp fonts, e.g. /media/avatars/<account>.jpg), and wire the .avatar div to <img src> per account. Pick the LATEST available image per profile. Dedup the two fc1943s accounts (dup-handle-fc1943s-two-accounts) - each account id gets its own avatar.")
