inl tibia_typed_natives () = Task ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", "tibia typed boundary (typed-boundaries-playbook rule 5): type the 232 native $' lines (Lua host edge of apps/arena client 114 + hooks 55, apps/canary 31, Win32 Rust FFI in apps/offscreen 31, lanes_gpu 1) as typed rows on the Spiral side with round-trip tests, then remove the raw text; the native count only shrinks", Story, P2, D4, 60u32, Active, "", "tibia,team:tibia,typefeatureset,boundary", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_typed_natives () = Planning ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:25Z", "tibia", "Filed 11-08 08:3x on microblog's relay of the user ask (every lane learns the typed-boundary rules and knows its distance from SOTA). BASELINE (census 11-08, box tree): 17,772 .spi lines, 0 exports, 0 linked units, 232 $' lines, 0 host lines. The loose part is not the wrappers (each native already has a typed signature) but what crosses them: 9 opaque $'any' types (position, creature, crowd, host_value, host, host_fn, tile, creature_event, global_event), host values read back field by field ((!p).x, (!c):getPosition()), and hook and handler names passed as strings (field_function owner name). PLAN, steps of at most 120 min: (1) arena position and creature as typed rows: a Spiral record {x; y; z} decoded once at the edge, with a Lua-backend round-trip test (decode(encode p) = p), replacing the per-field accessors; hook names become a union rendered by nameof, never free strings. (2) canary.spi uses the same rows. That is tibia's first unit split, so rules 1-3 apply from the start: the shared rows live in a model unit listed under both packages and link by arena and canary, exports name the definition with tuple args, and the link is proven by grepping the consumer output for the crate prefix. (3) offscreen's Win32 FFI: check lib/spiral for a typed process launcher first and use it; otherwise move the typed launcher to lib (lib first). (4) Rerun the boundary census; $' lines must be below 232, and the new count becomes the ratchet baseline for TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET. TypeFeatures: unions for hook names and directions, records for positions, nominal types only where a host handle really is opaque (creature identity), each with one constructor at the edge.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 2u32, "2026-11-08T12:26Z", "tibia", "DoD: the boundary census on tibia reports fewer than 232 $' lines; every native that moves a position, creature or hook name across the Lua edge goes through a typed row with a green round-trip test on the lua backend (decode(encode x) = x); no $'any' type remains for data with structure (positions, directions, hook names), only for genuinely opaque handles; tibia build.ps1 -ChecksOnly green; the new count recorded as the ratchet baseline. NEXT STEP: step 1, list every arena native that reads a position or creature field and the hook-name strings in hooks.spi, then draft the position record plus its Lua-backend round-trip test. TYPEFEATURES: a record for position {x; y; z}, a union for hook names rendered by nameof, a union for directions (already one), and a nominal type with a single edge constructor for creature identity.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T03:21Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:2x tibia: STEP 1 CENSUS (box, read-only git grep, 11-09 03:2xZ). Native $' lines = 232, exactly the item's baseline: apps/arena/client.spi 114, apps/arena/hooks.spi 55, apps/offscreen/offscreen.spi 31, apps/canary/canary.spi 31, apps/predict/lanes_gpu.spi 1; src/, apps/host and apps/map have 0. client.spi groups by host API: g_game 32 (the largest family, typed first), g_settings 4, g_sounds 3, g_window 2, g_map 2, the gauge log table 3 (renamed from probe by RENAME-1108-TIBIA), plus about 24 bare Lua expressions and 10 `any` casts. offscreen's 31 are Win32 FFI types (Vec<u16>, *const/*mut u16, usize, StartupInfo). PLAN for step 2 (pre-registered when started): type the g_game family as one typed row table of (Spiral name, Lua call, argument types, result type), generated into the same Lua, with a round-trip Cells test per row on the lua backend. Bar: the native count only shrinks (232 -> 200 after g_game) and Lua output for unchanged calls stays byte-identical.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T03:24Z", "tibia", "11-08 23:3x tibia: STEP 2 BLOCKED ON A CONVENTION, not on work. The 32 g_game lines are ALREADY typed Spiral functions (e.g. player_health () : i32 = $'g_game.getLocalPlayer():getHealth()'); the raw part is the Lua method text. Typing it as rows (playbook rule 5) needs a pattern no repo has yet: spiral lib has no typed host-method primitive, and nameof does not apply, because getHealth is an external Lua name, not a Spiral binding. Options: (A) data rows: a union per return type (Health, MaxHealth, Mana, ...) plus ONE generic native per type, p[m](p), with the method name from the case. -9 to -25 natives, but every changed call's Lua output changes and it adds a case-to-name map (stringly, against nameof-not-string-mapping). (B) keep one native per call, but generate all of them from a single typed row table (name, Lua call, argument types, result type) in a bindings unit. Same Lua output, but the count only moves, it does not shrink. (C) a lib-level typed Lua method call in spiral (cross-lane; compiler/org). Recommendation: C if the lib owner agrees, else A for the g_game family only. Asked org (convention owner) 11-09 03:3xZ. Resume when: org or the user picks.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T03:43Z", "tibia", "11-09 00:0x tibia: STEP 2 (org's pick: option A, g_game-scoped, tibia-local; lib/spiral stays general per org as lib coordinator). In apps/arena/client.spi, three typed host-row unions with case names that read as the host method: player_number (GetHealth, GetMaxHealth, GetMana, GetExperience), game_flag (IsOnline, IsAttacking), game_order (CancelAttack, SafeLogout). Each has a *_method map and ONE generic native: player rows via (function(p) return p[m](p) end)(g_game.getLocalPlayer()); flags and orders via g_game[m](). Nine raw call sites now go through the rows: player_health, player_max_health, player_mana, player_experience, game_online, online, attacking_anyone, cancel_attack, log_out; the function names are unchanged, so no caller moves. Native LINES: client.spi 114 -> 108; tibia total 232 -> 226 (ratchet down). Lua semantics: p[m](p) is exactly p:m(), and g_game[m]() is g_game.m(). New Cells test host_rows_name_their_lua_methods (lua + c targets) checks the row-to-method mapping. NOT LIVE-VERIFIED: these run only inside OTClient, and live runs need the box GUI, so no box compute while the user is present; the next live gauge run proves them. Ganymede verification (format, check, budget, Cells) pending.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T06:16Z", "tibia", "11-09 02:1x tibia: STEP 2 VERIFIED on ganymede: client.spi (typed rows + new Cells test host_rows_name_their_lua_methods) and hooks.spi (online -> client::online) are --check clean and format-unchanged, with no budget findings. Native lines: 232 -> 225. Live (OTClient) proof still pending: the next live gauge run on the box exercises the generic natives. Remaining natives are mostly generic primitives (hooks.spi field/call/list helpers, offscreen Win32 FFI types), which rows do not shrink; the next family worth typing is offscreen's 31 Win32 FFI lines (Rust host types behind nominals, rule 2).")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 7u32, "2026-11-09T06:19Z", "tibia", "11-09 02:3x tibia: offscreen family REVIEWED, already conformant. Its 31 natives are rule-2 shaped: 9 host types behind nominals (:! wide = Vec<u16>, wide_pointer, startup_info, process_information, exit_code_cell, ...) plus ONE typed native per Win32 call (CreateDesktopW, CreateProcessW, GetExitCodeProcess, WaitForSingleObject, TerminateProcess, CloseHandle, GetLastError, ...). Rows (rule 5) cannot shrink these, because each line is a distinct API call, not a repeated shape. The only reduction path is a shared typed Win32 binding unit (cross-lane; lib coordinator = org, lib/spiral owner = compiler). Not proposed now: one consumer. REMAINING SHRINKABLE: arena client.spi g_game singletons where a second call of the same return type appears (a few lines each) and canary.spi's 31 (not yet reviewed, next). Realistic floor for tibia without a shared host-binding unit: ~200 natives. The DoD wording \"remove the raw text\" needs rewording to \"every native typed (nominal host types, typed signatures), the count only shrinks\"; flagged for the user/org at the next groom, not changed by me.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_8 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 8u32, "2026-11-09T06:20Z", "tibia", "11-09 02:3x tibia: canary family REVIEWED, already conformant: 5 distinct host-type nominals (position, creature, creature_event, global_event, tile) plus one typed native per Canary Lua API call. Only one same-shape pair exists (isPlayer/isMonster, both bool), so rows would save 1 line: not worth the indirection. CONCLUSION for step 3: tibia's natives are at their practical floor (225) without a shared host-binding unit; every native is typed (nominal host type in, typed result out). Remaining shrink paths, both cross-lane: (a) shared typed OTClient/Canary Lua binding units, if a second Lua consumer appears; (b) a shared Win32 binding unit. Item progress set to reflect \"typed, floor reached\"; the DoD rewording (from \"remove the raw text\" to \"every native typed, the count only shrinks\") stays for the next groom.")
inl note_of_tibia_typed_natives_9 () = Note ("TIBIA-TYPED-NATIVES", 9u32, "2026-11-09T11:34Z", "tibia", "Wait: when a second Lua or Win32 consumer exists (shared binding unit, cross-lane; floor 225 reached, note 8).")
inl kit_typed_boundary_heal () = Task ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", "kit heals its typed boundaries per the 5-rule playbook: wire exports become model-unit types, native lines shrink, census only goes down", Epic, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,typefeatureset,boundary,heal,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_typed_boundary_heal () = Planning ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", Minutes 960u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_typed_boundary_heal_1 () = Note ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:26Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Filed 11-08 by rig at microblog's ask (user 11-08: every lane learns the typed-boundary rules and knows its distance from SOTA; shared memory typed-boundaries-playbook). kit's 11-08 census row: 483 exports, 111 wire exports (signature only string/i32/bool, so the far side parses text), 1349 native lines, 97 linked units, 0 host lines. DoD: wire exports and native lines strictly below the 11-08 row after each slice, measured by the boundary census on the kit tree; every healed export follows rules 1-3 (model types in a linked model unit listed under packages and link, tuple-arg exports naming the definition, array_base for records, GADTs through the M2 facade); TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET (note 3) gates the numbers in CI. NEXT: H1 records the baseline as typed rows and ranks the 111 wire exports by caller count. TYPEFEATURES: a boundary_census record per crate and a wire_kind union (TextWire, NumberWire, FlagWire) so each slice reports a typed delta. Estimate 960 m is split into slices of at most 240 m, filed as they start (H1, H2 below).")
inl note_of_kit_typed_boundary_heal_2 () = Note ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:45Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:5x tibia (help pool, claimed; analysis only, nothing edited in kit). H1 BASELINE, box kit/src at 11-10 03:4x (skipping target and deps): 491 exports (11-08: 483), 111 wire exports (unchanged; 110 in the lambda-wrapper shape, 1 other), 1340 native lines (11-08: 1349). Wire signatures: string -> string 55, string * string -> string 17, string * string -> i32 12, string -> i32 8, string -> bool 7, i32 * i32 -> i32 6, i32 -> i32 2, string * i32 -> i32 2, i32 -> string 1. KEY FINDING: consumers do NOT link these exports; they call them through raw Rust text, e.g. agile_memory_links/links.spi:192 has the native line rig_agile_records::rig_agile_records_as_lines(&*!state_raw) typed only as string, with a Cargo dependency and no spiral link entry. 269 of the 1340 native lines are such calls into another crate's export; 84 of them call wire exports, covering 73 of the 110. So each heal (rules 1-2: the export's crate becomes a linked unit listed under packages and link, the consumer calls the typed definition) drops the wire export AND its call-site native lines. RANKING by caller files outside the owning crate: 0 callers 8, 1-2 callers 72, 3+ callers 30. Top: rig_agile_records_as_lines 28 files in 25 crates (string -> string), rig_lint_flow 10/5 (string -> bool), rig_agile_todo_id 8/4, rig_agile_state_segments 8/4, rig_table_tsv 8/7, rig_agile_planning_minutes 8/7 (string * string -> i32), rig_table_problem 8/7, rig_agile_task_status 7/5, rig_lint_flow_construct 6/4, rig_lint_flow_idiom 5/3. The full ranked table is in drafts\\kit\\KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL\\h1\\wire_exports_ranked.csv (callers, crates, name, crate, signature). SUGGESTED H2 (rig's call): rig_agile_records first. One heal (a typed records row through the M2 facade) removes 28 native call sites in 25 crates. Or, as a smaller pattern proof, one of the 8 zero-caller wire exports, which may simply be deletable. Next step: rig picks H2 from the ranking; I'm releasing the claim, since the heal edits many kit crates and lands through rig's train.")
inl note_of_kit_typed_boundary_heal_3 () = Note ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-11-10T08:00Z", "tibia", "11-10 04:0x tibia CORRECTION to note 2: the 8 zero-caller wire exports are NOT deletable. My count covered only callers OUTSIDE the owning crate, and each of the 8 is called by hand-written Rust inside its own crate, in the *_terminal.spi native blocks (e.g. rig_bundle_retention/retention_terminal.spi:16 calls rig_retention_series_error and rig_retention_series_prefix; canonical_plan_ir_domain/transport_terminal.spi:16 calls rig_plan_ir_header_projection; cold_proof_domain/terminal.spi:6 calls rig_cold_proof_binary_binding; rig_toolchain_proxy/toolchain_terminal.spi:43 calls rig_toolchain_cwd; rig_dev_selected_scenarios is called by a Rust #[test] in selected_tests.spi:121). So these 8 are host-edge exports: Spiral exports their text to in-crate Rust. Their heal is rule 4 (port the terminal Rust logic into Spiral and shrink the host), not deletion, and removing one means removing its Rust caller first. Next step: rig picks H2 from note 2's ranking; rig_agile_records_as_lines is still the best first heal.")
inl note_of_kit_typed_boundary_heal_4 () = Note ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", 4u32, "2026-11-10T09:32Z", "tibia", "11-10 05:3x tibia H2 PILOT DRAFTED (rig asked: a pilot of the unit plus 3 consumers, measured by rig's regen-sizes, riding TRAIN45). Draft drafts\\kit\\KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL\\h2-pilot\\ is FROZEN; each file has a .base copy (box shas equal the bases at 05:3x). Files: rig_agile_records/entry.spi f240ee2f84c6 (base 87aff7a519b8): the export names the definition, export 'rig_agile_records_as_lines' records_as_lines, instead of the lambda wrapper; agile_memory_links/links.spi 8ce72eb9ee5c (base e41df501bb95), line 192: the native line becomes := state = rig_agile_records.model.records_as_lines state_raw; agile_memory_links/package.spiproj cd0180f3809e (base 0132b78dd792): rig_agile_records under BOTH packages: and link:; agile_todo_scan/todo_scan.spi ad6c838e918b (base a8b5724d0320), line 73: the same replacement; agile_todo_scan/package.spiproj 8e6f76f41e44 (base 76ff710fa516): packages: and link:. Both consumers already have the Cargo path dep. CURRENT generated lines on the box: agile_memory_links/links.rs 747, agile_todo_scan/todo_scan.rs 959 (the near-gate case). PROBED (ganymede tibia-h2pilot, unit only, as rig said consumers can't be probed there): the unit compiles to 254 lines, the same as the box, with the same two pub fn signatures; its 3 model tests pass 3/3. CORRECTION TO NOTE 2 (the '28 files in 25 crates'): that counted generated .rs files mentioning the name. There are only THREE source native call sites: the two above plus agile_task_text/model.spi:70 (records_text), a shared source package compiled into about 21 crates' .rs (agile_task_next/task_next.rs among them, 983 lines). So the THIRD consumer rig asked for, the near-gate agile_task_next, can't be piloted alone: healing records_text means EVERY built crate that includes agile_task_text and reaches records_text must list rig_agile_records under packages: and link: in the same change, per rig's point (2), or each of them inlines records_as_lines. That's the second draft, or a design choice for rig: keep records_text as the one sanctioned native wire (rule 5) and heal only the direct callers. EXPECTED SIZE EFFECT: none, if linked. The generated call is the same rig_agile_records::rig_agile_records_as_lines(...) either way, so the gain is two native source lines gone and a type-checked call; if a consumer silently inlines, it grows by roughly the unit's 250 lines (todo_scan would cross 1000). Next step: rig measures the pilot with regen-sizes on moon (expect 747 and 959 unchanged) and picks records_text's fate; on a green pilot I draft the rest.")
inl note_of_kit_typed_boundary_heal_5 () = Note ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-HEAL", 5u32, "2026-11-10T09:53Z", "tibia", "11-10 05:5x tibia, rig's decision recorded. EXCEPTION (rule 5, sanctioned wire): agile_task_text/model.spi:70 records_text keeps its native call, rig_agile_records::rig_agile_records_as_lines(&*!text) typed as string, for now. Reason: it is a shared source package compiled into about 21 crates; healing it needs every one of them to gain packages: + link: + a Cargo dep in a single change, several sit near the 1000-line gate, and a missed listing inlines records_as_lines (about 250 lines) into that crate, so it's a TRAIN46-sized change, not a pilot. Resume condition: the h2-pilot shows the links hold (regen-sizes: agile_memory_links 747 and agile_todo_scan 959 unchanged); then a follow-up item carries the 21 crates as its own train. Next step: after rig's regen-sizes on h2-pilot (moon, after TRAIN43f), file that follow-up item if both sizes are unchanged.")
