inl note_of_kit_typed_boundary_h1_2 () = Note ("KIT-TYPED-BOUNDARY-H1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T06:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:2x local rig, DoD done except the typed-rows form. CENSUS RERUN (playbook boundary_census.ps1, copied to the rig scratchpad) on the kit tree: .spi files 1170, lines 107,896, exports 481, wire exports 111, $' lines 1,349, linked units 97, host lines 0. Against the 11-08 row (100,752 / 483 / 111 / 1,349 / 97 / 0): the boundary did not drift; the +7,144 lines are compiler's pack63c reformat (three-line ternaries, about +6.2k) plus tonight's new modules; exports -2. WIRE EXPORTS RANKED (grep with the census wire signature finds 125 lines because it also counts test-only exports; callers = other files naming the export): rig_agile_records_as_lines 28; rig_lint_flow 11; rig_agile_state_segments, rig_table_tsv, rig_agile_planning_minutes, rig_table_problem, rig_agile_todo_id 9 each; rig_agile_task_status 8; rig_lint_flow_construct 7; rig_lint_flow_idiom 6. By family: agile (agile_task 33, rig_agile 31, agile_todo 29, agile_planning 21, about 114 callers), rig_do 47, rig_lint 33. TOP FAMILY FOR H2: the agile records-as-text boundary, led by rig_agile_records_as_lines (28 callers each parsing joined text lines back into records); H2 replaces it with a typed record list across the link (array_base of a record, the shape that links per spiral-link-boundary-shapes). Next step: H2 on rig_agile_records_as_lines.")
