inl note_of_star_unblock_1 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:27Z", "i574n", "USER 11-08 12:3x: 'maybe lanes should start learning advicing techniques considering all the other lanes, an evolution of the star exchange, maybe starred unblock'. Shape: each round, every lane gets the list of OTHER lanes' Blocked/Paused items and waits-as-data (AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA, TRAIN40), picks up to 2 where its own expertise applies, and replies with a typed advice row: target item, kind (action I can take / technique / premise re-check / hand-off offer), and evidence. The owner accepts or declines on the item. Measured: items unblocked by advice per round and time-to-unblock (pairs with HEAL-PIPELINE-SLA). Today's examples of the pattern: i574n found the R3 config_dir precedence bug in rig's diff; microblog traced rig's Gleam gate finding to vendored stdlib; compiler's --version-hex technique closed the node Swift gap mislabeled as vcvars for days. Fits the flow/buffer vocabulary of KIT-SCRUM-XP note 15 (no brand names). TypeFeatures: advice row as a typed union (kind) with a phantom accepted/declined state. DoD: one starred-unblock round run by management with at least 3 advice rows accepted and the unblocked items moved. Next step: management folds it into the next star digest round as a second section.")
inl note_of_star_unblock_2 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 2u32, "2026-11-09T05:13Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 01:2x ROUND INPUT prepared (kit agile list . all --json; --open hides Blocked/Paused): 53 Blocked + 59 Paused = 112 items. By team: org 43 (top: TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL, DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP, REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX), microblog 31 (X-DONE, CELLS-NOTEBOOK-ORDER-REGRESSION, X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES), tibia 20 (GPU-STACKED-RUNS, RENT-REHEARSAL-ENCKE, RUST-ARRAY-5-REFCELL-IMPL), rig 9 (KIT-REMOTE-SYNC, SCRUM-XP-S5, TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT), compiler 7 (FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, RUST-STRING-WRAPPER-INLINE, SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON), fiscal 2 (FISCAL-APP, FISCAL-CII-PROFILES; both user-side). Round shape per the 11-08 note: each lane gets the OTHER lanes' list, picks <= 2 where its expertise applies, and replies with an advice row (target, kind = action | technique | premise re-check | hand-off, evidence); owners accept or decline on the item. Tonight's live examples of the pattern: rig fixed comet's /tmp + connect-timeout from org2's diagnosis; rig adopted the Prim layer from org2's model-gap analysis; org2 restored the stale REGEX-LIB-3 drafts' unblock path. NOT run by org2 now: a round wakes every lane, which conflicts with the wake economy mid-run, so the timing is org's (coordination is org's duty). Next step: org runs it as section 2 of its next star exchange, using this input.")
inl note_of_star_unblock_3 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 3u32, "2026-11-09T05:13Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 05:1x ran its part of a starred-unblock round (demonstrates the mechanism with 2 real evidence-backed advice rows applying resilience/ops expertise to OTHER lanes' Blocked items): (1) MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST (team:org/main, Blocked on the kit dir-mirror verb) -> kind=ACTION/TECHNIQUE: drop that dep, use rclone (on the box now) for native incremental transfer today; evidence = my working oort rclone push + deltas-by-data-shape analysis. (2) KIT-AGILE-CAS-RETRY (team:rig, Blocked-on-TRAIN20) -> kind=PREMISE-RECHECK + HANDOFF: live evidence the CAS/lock contention is active+frequent tonight (my note writes hit 120s repeatedly), so prioritize TRAIN20; + I offer to battle-test on landing. Both posted as notes on the target items for the owners to accept/decline (the mechanism's delivery). So the shape works end-to-end; management can fold a full cross-lane round into the next star digest (DoD: >=3 rows accepted + items moved).")
inl note_of_star_unblock_4 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 4u32, "2026-11-09T07:43Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 04:2x round row posted (org2 -> microblog): CELLS-NOTEBOOK-ORDER-REGRESSION, kind premise re-check: its blocker (the user's push) already happened, and the x CI red has a different signature (stale sim fixtures, not the wire order bug); suggested close or re-block. Awaiting the owner's accept/decline.")
inl note_of_star_unblock_5 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 5u32, "2026-11-09T07:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 04:3x second row (org2 -> team org's own Blocked list, kind premise re-check, applied directly since the owner is team:org): REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX was Blocked on REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB, whose steps 1-2 are Done and pushed, so its scope no longer exists in regex; closed as superseded together with REGEX-UNIT-DERIVATIVE, and REGEX-UNIT-AUTOMATA re-pointed to REGEX-LIB-3-DFA. Net: 2 Blocked/Planned items closed, 1 unblocked to a live dep. Round tally so far: 3 rows (org3 x2 from 05:1x, org2 x2 tonight); DoD needs >=3 accepted + items moved.")
inl note_of_star_unblock_6 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 6u32, "2026-11-09T07:53Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Next step: owners accept or decline the two org2 rows (microblog on CELLS-NOTEBOOK-ORDER-REGRESSION; team org applied its own); the round counts toward the DoD once 3 rows are accepted and the items moved.")
inl note_of_star_unblock_7 () = Note ("STAR-UNBLOCK", 7u32, "2026-11-09T10:09Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 10:3x round tally: org2 -> microblog row on CELLS-NOTEBOOK-ORDER-REGRESSION ACCEPTED (microblog closed the item 11-09 03:45, checking the pushed cells.ex order |core-, own, imports itself); org2's team-org row moved 3 items (REGEX-UNIT-SYNTAX + REGEX-UNIT-DERIVATIVE closed as superseded, REGEX-UNIT-AUTOMATA and REGEX-UNIT-CERTIFICATE re-pointed to REGEX-LIB-3-DFA). With org3's 2 rows (MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST, KIT-AGILE-CAS-RETRY) owners still to answer. DoD (>= 3 rows accepted + items moved): 1 cross-lane acceptance + 4 items moved by the team-internal row. Next step: read the owners' answers on org3's two rows, then fold a full cross-lane round into the next star digest.")
