inl planning_of_cells_to_rig_repo () = Planning ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_1 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:40Z", "microblog", "GROOMING (user 11-08: groom with the lanes so the Cells code moves to the rig repo already; continue the migration from there). Proposed ownership, open to the lanes: rig owns the HOME (repo, gate, trains, installs); microblog owns the PORT (all CELLS-PORT-* items are team:microblog and this lane has capacity while MICROBLOG-MIGRATION is paused); compiler is consulted on CELLS-PORT-MEMO (memo techniques); management is not involved. Open questions per lane: rig: target path in the rig repo, and how cells_land_window, the Elixir ratchet and kit installs follow the move. i574n: the spiral-side callers and docs that point at apps/cells (Livebook/Kino, lib gates, nightly). compiler: the daemon/memo protocol paths Cells reads. DoD: Cells builds and its full gate (mix test --max-cases 4 --timeout 900000, node) is green from the rig repo; nothing in spiral still imports apps/cells; the .ex line count is unchanged by the move (the ratchet baseline moves with it). NEXT STEP: collect each lane objection or constraint as a note here, then cut the move.")
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_2 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 2u32, "2026-11-08T12:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 09:2x rig GROOM (home owner). No objection to the split: rig owns the home (repo, gate, trains, installs), microblog owns the port (CELLS-PORT-*), compiler is consulted on memo.\nTARGET PATH: apps/cells at the rig repo root (beside src, scripts, compiler-contracts), so C:\\home\\git\\rig\\apps\\cells. WHEN: after TRAIN41 installs and R4 has moved C:\\home\\git\\kit to C:\\home\\git\\rig, so Cells moves once, not into kit and then again; and never while a train runs, because every train runs its notebooks through Cells.\nWHAT FOLLOWS THE MOVE (measured on the box 11-08):\n1. The notebook runner path is hard-coded in two places: kit_job_coordinator/coordinator.spi:47 (spiral ++ /apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1) and scripts/release-train.ps1:154. Both become the rig-relative path, and the runner hash pin in launch-train (RunnerHash) then pins the Cells copy inside the train snapshot, so a Cells change is gated by the next train like any kit change.\n2. cells_land_window.ps1 defaults -Cells to PSScriptRoot/.., so it moves without edits; its Elixir ratchet (Get-ElixirDrift) compares .ex lines before and after each land, with no stored baseline, so it moves with the script; the CELLS-PORT- and CELLS-ELIXIR-HEAL label exemption stays.\n3. kit scripts/init.ps1:25-27 runs mix local.hex, local.rebar and deps.get in ../../spiral/apps/cells: it points at apps/cells in the repo.\n4. kit_tracked_text/text.spi:18 allows apps/cells/data/tlds.txt as upstream data: the path stays valid repo-relative once Cells lives in the rig repo (today it describes a spiral path).\n5. i574n.github remote.ps1:328 checks apps\\cells\\deps in the node mirror (MIRROR-DEPS-MISSING): it must read the rig mirror. pins/workflows.spi:126 runs apps/cells/spi/ci_gate.ps1 inside spiral's CI with -Roots lib/spiral,apps/transformer: spiral CI would need to check out the rig repo, or the gate moves to rig's CI and spiral lib lands call it. That is i574n's call.\n6. apps/cells/spi also holds spiral-lib tooling (lib_gate.ps1, lib_land.ps1, lib_land_window.ps1, lib_land_queue.ps1, lib_sweep.ps1, lib_program_gate.ps1). They gate spiral lib lands, not Cells, so they either move with Cells (and spiral lands depend on the rig checkout) or stay in spiral. Decide before the cut.\n7. Mirrors: node and europa mirrors gain the rig copy of Cells (deps under apps/cells/deps, about the same size), and the spiral mirror loses it once nothing imports it.\nESTIMATE: 240 m is low with points 1-7; split at the cut into M1 move plus runner path (rig, 120 m), M2 callers and CI (i574n, 90 m), M3 node and europa mirrors and the full Cells gate from the rig repo (rig, 90 m).")
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_3 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 3u32, "2026-11-08T12:44Z", "microblog", "microblog on rig note 2: accepted. Order: after TRAIN41 installs and R4 renames the kit folder to rig, never during a train. Slices at the cut: M1 move + runner path (coordinator.spi:47, release-train.ps1:154, RunnerHash pin; rig 120 m), M2 callers + CI (remote.ps1:328, pins/workflows.spi:126; i574n 90 m), M3 mirrors + full Cells gate green from rig (rig 90 m). Open question, microblog view: the lib land tooling in apps/cells/spi (lib_gate, lib_land*, lib_sweep) should MOVE with Cells, because it runs lib through the Cells gate and the land window. i574n decides, since spiral lib is theirs. Estimate raised to 300 m.")
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_4 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 4u32, "2026-11-08T12:46Z", "i574n", "i574n inventory 11-08 12:5x (git grep of TRACKED files for apps/cells or a 'cells' path, every org repo; 66 files outside apps/cells; full list in i574n scratchpad cells-refs.txt). SPIRAL side (12): .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml; scripts/core.ps1 and scripts/init.ps1; lib/spiral/build.ps1, lib/spiral/bench/parsing/bench.ps1 (nightly bench), lib/spiral/near/wallet/build.ps1; apps/kernel/build.ps1 (Livebook/Kino kernel); apps/compiler/scripts/{test-blocks, lib-usage-consumers, bench-cells-vs-matrix}.ps1 plus tmp/AGENTS.md and tmp/tests/matrix.psd1. i574n.github: scripts/pins/workflows.spi (the generated org workflows call Cells), scripts/remote.ps1 (node/europa stage trees), apps/graphs (backlog chart outputs, text only). Every repo's build runs Cells through deps/spiral/apps/cells: html/build.ps1, regex/build.ps1, dice/lib/build.ps1 + dice/contract, blog/scripts/common.ps1, alphabet apps/hangul + apps/documents, fiscal scripts/{build, box-gate, pascal-reach}.ps1, tibia scripts/build.ps1, kit scripts/{release-train, notebook-batch, init}.ps1 + 6 kit/src files, x apps/sim (15) + apps/client (3) + scripts {sim-shell, sim-run, common}.ps1. Box schedules and ~/.claude hooks: 0 refs. Node and europa: stage trees mirror spiral including apps/cells (remote.ps1), and the europa x sim runs Cells. NO OBJECTION to the move, with three conditions. (1) LIB TOOLING: the lib landing path lives in apps/cells/spi (lib_land_window, lib_land, lib_land_queue, lib_gate, lib_program_gate, lib_sweep, lib_roundtrip). Lib stays in spiral, so either those become rig verbs in the same move or spiral keeps a thin entry; every lane lands lib through them daily, so no gap day. (2) CI COST: today each repo's CI clones spiral and gets Cells for free. After the move each repo needs rig too, or rig publishes a Cells release artifact that workflows fetch by a pinned version (pins.spi gains a cells pin; preferred: one download instead of a second clone and build). (3) ONE CUTOVER: the deps/spiral/apps/cells path is hardcoded in about 25 build scripts; ship one resolver (env or pins-generated) that every script calls, land it BEFORE the move, then flip it in one edit. Mirrors (remote.ps1) and the Cells runner build (apps/spiral/build.ps1 appends mimalloc and builds release-unwind) move with it.")
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_5 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 5u32, "2026-11-08T12:47Z", "microblog", "GROOMED 11-08 (rig note 2, i574n inventory note, compiler on memo): every lane agrees on the move and the ownership (rig home, microblog port, compiler consulted on memo, management not involved). Scope: 66 tracked files outside apps/cells point at Cells (12 in spiral, ~25 build scripts across repos via deps/spiral/apps/cells, pins/workflows.spi, remote.ps1 stage trees, node and europa mirrors, the Kino kernel). i574n conditions, now part of the DoD: (1) the lib landing tooling in apps/cells/spi (lib_land_window, lib_gate, lib_land_queue and the rest) moves as rig verbs in the same step, with no gap day; lib stays in spiral. (2) CI uses a pinned Cells artifact published by rig (a cells pin in pins.spi), not a clone-and-build of rig per repo. (3) M0, before the move: one resolver for the Cells path lands, so the flip is one edit. Order: M0 resolver, then after TRAIN41 + R4 the cut: M1 move + runner path (rig), M2 callers + CI pin (i574n), M3 mirrors + full gate green from rig (rig). NEXT STEP: rig or i574n files M0 (the Cells path resolver) and claims it.")
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_6 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 6u32, "2026-11-08T13:00Z", "microblog", "x callers DONE (microblog, unstaged): scripts/common.ps1 defines $CellsRoot = $env:SPIRAL_CELLS_ROOT ? $env:SPIRAL_CELLS_ROOT : (Join-Path $SpiralRoot apps/cells), next to $SpiralRoot; common.ps1 (erl_memory_limit, mix push-location, run_notebook runner), sim-run.ps1, sim-shell.ps1 and apps/sim/build.ps1 use it (every x script dot-sources common.ps1, so apps/client/build.ps1 and node-run.ps1 inherit it). Proof: 0 parse errors in all 4; unset resolves to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\apps\\cells (exists), set resolves to the env value; the only literal apps/cells left in x scripts is the fallback. NOT covered by the env var (data, not scripts): postability/x.json:34 and the test apps/client/tlds.spi:202 read spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt by relative path. Decide before M1 whether tlds.txt moves with Cells or gets a stable home (e.g. spiral lib data); the x side then changes those 2 lines. i574n count of 15 sim files: on the box, outside build output, only apps/sim/build.ps1 and the README mention apps/cells.")
inl note_of_cells_to_rig_repo_7 () = Note ("CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO", 7u32, "2026-11-08T13:00Z", "microblog", "tlds decision (i574n 11-08): the TLD list gets a stable home in lib as a Spiral module (LIB-TLDS, team:microblog, filed). data/tlds.txt moves with Cells as a private Cells asset until cell_budget.ex is ported and opens lib tlds, then it is deleted. So the tlds references do NOT block M1.")
inl gleam_records_regen_proof () = Task ("GLEAM-RECORDS-REGEN-PROOF", "x regen proof that unblocks LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS: one node run (sim accept, sim build Gleam, client build, e2e, census) with the generated .gleam diffed against the same tree on pack53c 24D3967377735A37; send compiler every changed hunk", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:microblog,gleam,linked-units,node", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gleam_records_regen_proof () = Planning ("GLEAM-RECORDS-REGEN-PROOF", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl agile_waits_resolve () = Task ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", "waits clear themselves and reach the acting lane: an item wait ends when its item is Done, a train wait when that train is installed, and a lane wait shows up in that lane's next as an unblock line", TaskKind, P0, D3, 90u32, Active, "", "agile,gate,idle,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_agile_waits_resolve () = Planning ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_1 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Filed 11-08 by rig from microblog's report (user 11-08: why do Cells tasks keep waiting with nobody pulling them). AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA (TRAIN40) stores waits as Waits rows and agile next hides any id with a row, but (1) nothing clears a wait: a WaitsItem stays after its item is Done, a WaitsTrain after the install; (2) a WaitsLane names the lane that must act, yet that lane never sees it (LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS is Blocked on x's regen proof, and no microblog item exists for it); (3) a ResumeWhen in prose is never re-checked. DoD: a wait is resolved when its item is Done or its train is the installed last-installed train, and the item returns to next; agile next --team T lists one unblock line per WaitsLane T row (waiting item, action text, age); ResumeWhen stays manual but agile gate lists it with its age; CLI tests for each case. NEXT: in agile_task_next, replace the substring test with a typed read of waits.spi plus the Done set and the installed train. TYPEFEATURES: a wait_state union (Holding, Resolved of reason, Routed of lane) computed per wait.")
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_2 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 2u32, "2026-11-08T14:07Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 10:5x rig, PART 1 BUILT (unstaged, rides TRAIN41): waits clear themselves. New crate agile_waits_hold (644 generated lines; workspace member added, Cargo.lock refreshed offline): an item wait holds until its item is Done; a train wait holds until the installed train number reaches it (TRAIN41 installed clears a TRAIN40 wait); lane, user and when waits hold. The installed train is read from installed-train.txt beside the running kit binary. agile next links it (agile_waits_hold.hold.holding_ids (root, text)) and only scans the Done set when waits.spi has rows. Kept agile_task_waits at its TRAIN40 size (944) and agile_task_next at 977 by moving the logic out instead of growing them (first try was 1196 and 1149). proof: node probe job-1794145797443-kit-probe1108e exit 0, hold.spi 1/1 pass, regen sizes 8 packages 0 over 1000 with cargo check, links agile_task_next to agile_waits_hold 1. LEFT: (2) release-train writes installed-train.txt beside the installed binary at install (after TRAIN40's box half, which runs that script from the live tree); (3) WaitsLane rows routed to the acting lane as unblock lines in its next. NEXT STEP: (3) in agile_next_print, then (2) after TRAIN40.")
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_3 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 3u32, "2026-11-08T14:17Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 10:2x rig, PART 3 BUILT (unstaged, rides TRAIN41): a WaitsLane row reaches the team that must act. agile_waits_hold lane_waits_printed reads --team T from the next filters and prints one line per lane wait routed to T (team: prefix accepted): unblock  ITEM  waits on team T: answer or pull it; skipped under --json; agile next links it (983 lines, hold crate 811). proof: node probe job-1794147246310-kit-probe1108f, hold.spi 2/2 pass (routing, team prefix, team flag). New CLI test an_item_wait_clears_when_its_item_is_done_and_a_lane_wait_reaches_that_team in next_cli.spi needs the candidate binary, so it first runs in TRAIN41. LEFT: release-train writes installed-train.txt beside the installed binary, after TRAIN40 box half. NEXT STEP: that edit once job-1794147257405-kit-TRAIN40 ends.")
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_4 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 4u32, "2026-11-08T14:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 11:0x rig, post-install check with the TRAIN40 kit (kit.exe 6C4F076B, installed 10:52:57, pack61b core 65DEE79C; node notebooks 66/66 on candidate D5D22429). PART 2 BUILT: release-train.ps1 now writes installed-train.txt beside the lane binary (LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\bin) at install (parse 0); seeded with TRAIN40 now. All three parts are built and node-proven; they ship together in TRAIN41.")
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_5 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 5u32, "2026-11-08T19:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 15:5x rig: GAP found live: LIB-LAYERS-2-RATCHET went Done (org landed lib/spiral/layers.spi, 172 rows; the installed --layers gives modules=172 unassigned=0 violations=2252 baseline=2252) but its lane wait row stayed, and lane waits never self-clear, so after TRAIN41 the org lane would still see an unblock line for a Done item. Cleared by hand (agile edit --wait --clear). FIX for TRAIN42: unblock_lines and holding_of skip a wait whose OWN item is Done (any kind), using the same done_ids pass; CLI test case: a Done item with a lane wait prints no unblock line.")
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_6 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 6u32, "2026-11-08T21:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 18:0x rig: the Done-item routing gap is FIXED in the tree (rides TRAIN42; TRAIN41 snapshot already taken): unblock_lines takes the Done set and skips a wait whose own item is Done; lane_waits_printed now gets (root, filters, state text) from agile next, so the Done set reuses the text next already read (no second 9.6 MB read) and is only computed with a team filter and a non-empty waits file. New test line: a Done item routes no unblock line. Box codegen: agile_waits_hold 845 lines, agile_task_next 983, both links present. First try hit the keyword-local trap (a local named open); renamed. Node notebook proof waits for TRAIN41 to leave the node.")
inl note_of_agile_waits_resolve_7 () = Note ("AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE", 7u32, "2026-11-08T23:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:2x rig, TRAIN41 INSTALLED 19:12:49 (kit.exe 93BDD93F; release built on moon in the TRAIN41 mirror with pinned pack62 core 4524F0D8D0AABDEE, 583 s, schema and topology checks passed; copy-installed on the box after a sha256 match and a job list + agile next smoke; shipped manifest 1764 files). Self-clearing waits and lane routing are installed (agile next answers with the hold crate linked). The Done-item routing fix is in the tree for TRAIN42.")
inl cells_path_resolver () = Task ("CELLS-PATH-RESOLVER", "M0 of CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO: one resolver for the Cells path (rig verb plus the spiral-side lookup) that every caller uses, so the move is a one-line flip", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:rig,cells,rig,paths", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_path_resolver () = Planning ("CELLS-PATH-RESOLVER", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl fiscal_gate_shard () = Task ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", "fiscal gate sharded across hosts and CI jobs: cost-balanced unit shards from one regen, merged reports", Story, P0, D4, 85u32, Active, "", "team:fiscal,fiscal,gate,scale,horizontal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_gate_shard () = Planning ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:57Z", "fiscal", "11-08 opened by fiscal. Design: build.ps1 -Shards N -ShardSet a,b (the xarchive --shards/--set convention, X-DUMPS n28). One regen step writes generated/ once; each shard then tests the units assigned to it by longest-processing-time over a weight (the unit's last measured seconds from target/ci-metrics files tsv when present, else its byte size: the 3.8 MB UBL units are the slowest), so shards balance without a stored baseline. Examples and reports run in a merge step that joins the shard tsv files. Placement: node and europa shards as kit node jobs under the memory caps; CI as a matrix (regen job, shard jobs, merge job; public-repo minutes are free). DoD: (1) build.ps1 -Shards 4 -ListOnly over today's tree prints 4 disjoint unit sets that cover every unit; (2) one real sharded gate over node + box (+ europa for the small units) finishes with every shard green and the slowest shard named; (3) the CI matrix runs the shards on the next push. Estimate 240 m provisional (D4 base).")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 2u32, "2026-11-08T12:58Z", "fiscal", "11-08 NEXT STEP: add -Shards / -ShardSet / -ListOnly to scripts/build.ps1 (with the SPIRAL_CELLS_ROOT resolution CELLS-PATH-RESOLVER asks for in the same edit), print the 4-shard dry-run list over today's tree, then use it as the gate of the combined ERP-unblock landing (FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC n8) on node + box + europa.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 3u32, "2026-11-08T13:33Z", "fiscal", "11-08 CORRECTION to n1 DoD (3), user 11-08 via i574n: CI stays ONE job per repo calling the entry script (memory one-entry-no-native-wrappers; PIPELINES-GREEN rejected multi-yml map-reduce for drift). A regen + 8x2 shard + merge workflow was drafted, then fully reverted (pins.ps1 reports fiscal identical to the typed source again). Horizontal scale lives in scripts/build.ps1 only: (a) the same -Shards N -ShardSet command fanned over our machines through kit's remote executor, then -MergeShards; (b) inside the single CI job, parallel unit processes on the runner's cores: build.ps1 now defaults -Parallel to cores/2 when $env:CI is set (1 locally), with largest units first, so the unchanged CI step pwsh scripts/build.ps1 stops being serial. DONE SO FAR: -Shards/-ShardSet/-ListOnly/-MergeShards, deterministic size-balanced assignment (4 shards over 99 units, disjoint and covering, within 1 KB of each other), SPIRAL_CELLS_ROOT resolution. RUNNING (node laptop, (a) in practice): job-1794143424823-fiscal-erp-regen, then job-1794143449207-fiscal-erp-shardsA (shards 0-4 of 12), then job-1794143456335-fiscal-erp-shardsB (5-9); the box takes 10-11. DoD (3) is now: one CI run of the single job green with the parallel default, and its wall time recorded against the 420-min serial runs.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 4u32, "2026-11-08T19:40Z", "fiscal", "11-08 NEXT SLICE: weighted shards for mixed hosts (org3 fleet order: moon > comet > venus for fiscal). Get-ShardOwners' LPT split assumes equal-capacity shards, so a 1-slot codespace (comet, 8 GB) would get as many bytes as the 4-slot node (moon, 16 GB). DoD: build.ps1 -ShardWeights 4,1,1 (one weight per shard, default all 1). LPT assigns each unit, largest first, to the shard with the least load/weight. Every host still computes the same split from the same weights. Units over a host's memory slot are pinned to shards whose weight >= 2 (ubl_invoice_2_1 and the 4 other UBL units stay on moon). Evidence for need: node rows (moon P4: 645 unit-min, critical unit 4325 s); Linux path proven on europa 11-08 (gate-cost rows written). NEXT STEP: implement and -ListOnly dry-run '-Shards 3 -ShardWeights 4,1,1' on the box.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 5u32, "2026-11-08T19:55Z", "fiscal", "11-08 IMPLEMENTED: build.ps1 -ShardWeights (live DE68F406, unstaged). Weighted LPT: each unit, largest first, goes to the shard with the least (load + size) / weight. A weight count other than -Shards, or a non-positive weight, throws. Dry run on the box, '-Shards 3 -ShardWeights 4,1,1 -ListOnly': 62 units 42,178 KB / 19 units 10,544 KB / 18 units 10,544 KB (exact 4:1:1); '4,1' is rejected. Each 1-slot shard gets one big UBL unit (despatchadvice, receiptadvice), which fits an 8 GB host's single slot at ~5 GB peak. Fleet plan from org3: moon weight 4 (P4), comet and venus weight 1, mercury after venus. NEXT STEP: the first mixed-host gate: -Shards 3 -ShardWeights 4,1,1 with ShardSet 0 on moon, 1 on comet, 2 on venus, then -MergeShards.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 6u32, "2026-11-08T20:48Z", "fiscal", "11-08 FLEET UPDATE (org3): ganymede (Europa Miami, 4 Skylake cores, 8 GB, .NET 11, kit-worker, 2 kit slots) joins the one-slot pool. FISCAL WEIGHT 1, not 2: fiscal is memory-bound (unit peak 3-5 GB, rule free > peak + 1.5 GB), so 8 GB holds one unit. Revisit only when gate-cost rows show peaks under ~3 GB there. Until KIT-NET-TOPOLOGY M2, launch with kit job start --on ganymede --bin /home/remote/git/kit/src/target/debug/kit. First mixed-gate plan: -Shards 4 -ShardWeights 4,1,1,1: moon ShardSet 0 at P4, then ganymede, comet and venus ShardSet 1/2/3 at P1; then -MergeShards.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 7u32, "2026-11-08T21:33Z", "fiscal", "11-08 GROOM: 55% -> 75%. Sharded gate green end to end on the node (12 shards, merge coverage), single-host 2-shard form proven on europa, -ShardWeights implemented and dry-run (4:1:1 exact). NEXT STEP: the first mixed-host gate, -Shards 4 -ShardWeights 4,1,1,1 (moon P4, then ganymede, comet and venus at P1), then -MergeShards (n6).")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 8u32, "2026-11-08T21:40Z", "fiscal", "11-08 groom r2 PLAN, ganymede first (moon stays with TRAIN41; org owns the window order). Step 1: copy the local rental bundle (scratchpad rental/fiscal-rental.tgz + run.ps1, smoke-proven on europa Linux) to ganymede and run its timing row on the small unit generated_nfe_v2_00_certificates via kit job start --on ganymede --bin /home/remote/git/kit/src/target/debug/kit, -Parallel 1. That proves pwsh + dotnet 11 + pack62 + rust there. Step 2: the weighted gate. -Shards 4 -ShardWeights 4,1,1,1: ganymede ShardSet 1, comet 2, venus 3 at P1, run as soon as each host is proven; moon ShardSet 0 at P4 in its window after TRAIN41; then -MergeShards on one host with all four units-shard*of4 tables. Logs: gate-cost and files rows to relay-lab/logs/fiscal/<stamp>.*. Step 1 is CPU-light and needs no moon window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 9u32, "2026-11-08T21:53Z", "fiscal", "11-08 STEP 1 RESULT (ganymede smoke, bundle 97067b81): NOT yet a fiscal host. Two causes. (1) ganymede has no Erlang/Elixir, and the Cells runner launches every test through mix (run_notebook.ps1:157), so the unit failed in 2 s with \"'mix' is not recognized\"; europa has OTP 29 + Elixir 1.20.5. Asked org (owner of ganymede) to provision the same. (2) systemd-run transient units get an empty HOME, which breaks core.ps1's paths: pass -E HOME=/root (memory systemd-run-empty-home). Everything else checks out: pwsh, dotnet 11, rust, compiler pack E24C992685D603EC, 6.7 GB free, 4 cores. The bundle stays staged at ganymede:/root/remote-stage/fiscal-gany/fr. NEXT STEP: once org confirms Elixir, rerun the timing + p2p rows under systemd-run -E HOME=/root -p MemoryMax=6G; green means ganymede joins the weighted pool at weight 1. Blocker: OTP/Elixir on ganymede (org).")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 10u32, "2026-11-08T23:13Z", "fiscal", "11-08 STEP 1 DONE: ganymede is a proven fiscal Linux host after Elixir was provisioned and the launcher was fixed (systemd-run -E HOME=/root + bash -lc for the login PATH). generated_nfe_v2_00_certificates 1/1 green; the p2p gate 16/16 green, 277 s. NEXT STEP: per the user's k3s direction (11-08), the weighted gate moves onto k3s. fiscal installs k3s on ganymede (org's rollout order) and runs one unit as a pod through the node-side wrapper (memory request == limit == unit peak; see memory k3s-build-test-substrate); then shards become pods.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 11u32, "2026-11-09T00:24Z", "fiscal", "11-08 QUEUED (on wake, check these first): moon job-1794183825019-fiscal-erp-gate-live (--after-ok compiler's job-1794182365680 suite). It gates ALL units of the landed tree in one host-local sharded run (-Shards 2 -ShardSet 0,1, P4, gate cache ON, so the first real green rows go to the node's out\\green.tsv for STORE-FISCAL-VERDICTS), then merges. Stage: node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fiscal-erp (staged by job-1794183751799 at 20:22: pinned compiler core 7A2B8AD55B7D48BB = pack63c, 83 units with cell timeouts x2, p2p 687F334A, build.ps1 DE68F406). K3S PODS on ganymede (user direction: k3s as the build substrate): k3s v1.37.2 installed, 6.08 GiB allocatable; build-base:2 image (ubuntu 26.04 + build tools + ICU) built by a BuildKit pod in 69 s, pinned by digest; wrapper proven: admission, digest check, cancel = exit 124, timing rows (pod start 4-5 s after admission). OPEN: the pattern oracle segfaults (exit 139) inside a 3 GiB pod, cumulatively, at the 600th XSD (catCFDI parses fine alone). A 5 GiB retry could not admit because ganymede never had 5.6 GB free for 15 min. NEXT STEP: rerun the oracle in a 5 GiB pod when ganymede drains; fiscal's full pod gate stays LAST in ganymede's chain (overnight).")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 12u32, "2026-11-09T03:18Z", "fiscal", "11-08 EUROPA PROVEN for fiscal's small units: job-1794192284023-fiscal-eur-certs, all 37 *_certificates units green (each discovered 1 executed 1 passed 1), 1924 s wall under vultr.gate's 1536M MemoryMax scope, pack63c core 5C92E46C2001DC2B. Load was ~5.4 on 2 vCPU, so the per-unit seconds are correctness-only, NOT bench rows (relay-lab logs/fiscal/20261108-europa-certs.*.loaded-not-bench). Fleet for fiscal now: moon (all units, Windows, P4), ganymede (Linux, 1 big unit at a time), europa (Linux, small certificate units, <=1.5G). NEXT STEP: as a weighted gate, europa's shard takes only the certificate units: a per-shard unit filter by peak memory (the size-class split), since -ShardWeights alone would hand it UBL units it can't hold.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 13u32, "2026-11-10T23:22Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 20:2x SIZE-CLASS SPLIT LANDED in fiscal scripts/build.ps1 (unstaged; was 3661CCEF, now 51CE90A5; .base in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GATE-SHARD): new -ShardMaxUnitKB (one cap per shard in KB, 0 = none); Get-ShardOwners only offers a unit to shards whose cap admits its source size, keeps the weighted greedy among those, and throws '<unit> (<KB>) fits no shard' when none does; a wrong cap count throws. VERIFIED with -ListOnly on the box (light): without caps the 3-shard 4,1,1 assignment is byte-identical to before (64/19/18 units); with -ShardMaxUnitKB 0,0,64 shard 2 gets 32 units totalling 489 KB and no unit over 64 KB, while every UBL and NF-e unit moves to the uncapped shards; impossible caps and a wrong count fail loudly. CAVEAT: source size is a good memory proxy for generated units only; small hand-written units such as families and canon run generation-heavy tests, so a europa shard should also be restricted (or measured) by kind, not by size alone. Next step: measure peak RSS per unit once on ganymede (the gate's per-unit rows) and either add a kind filter for the europa shard or feed measured peaks instead of source size.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_shard_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SHARD", 14u32, "2026-11-10T23:22Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 20:3x REFINED (live build.ps1 now 23E8E973, unstaged, mirrored in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GATE-SHARD\\build.ps1 over .base 3661CCEF): a capped shard takes only GENERATED units under its cap, so hand-written units (whose small sources run generation-heavy tests) always go to uncapped shards. Re-verified with -ListOnly: uncapped assignment unchanged (64/19/18); -Shards 3 -ShardWeights 4,1,1 -ShardMaxUnitKB 0,0,64 gives shard 2 exactly 14 units / 235 KB, 13 of them *_certificates, 0 hand-written. That is the europa shape from the 11-09 note (europa held all 37 certificate units under its 1536M cap). Next step: one real sharded gate across moon (shard 0, all big units), ganymede (shard 1) and europa (shard 2, -ShardMaxUnitKB cap) when the fleet is quiet, then -MergeShards to check the union equals the unsharded unit set.")
