inl planning_of_fiscal_gate_cache_reach () = Planning ("FISCAL-GATE-CACHE-REACH", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl fiscal_gate_budget () = Task ("FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET", "fiscal gate cost as typed rows: per-unit and per-phase seconds with host, core and load; growth flag and slowest-shard budget", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:fiscal,fiscal,gate,scale,healing", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_gate_budget () = Planning ("FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl fiscal_gate_scale () = Task ("FISCAL-GATE-SCALE", "fiscal gate wall time independent of family count: adding a family adds a shard, never wall time", Epic, P0, D7, 0u32, Planned, "FISCAL-GATE-SHARD,FISCAL-GATE-CACHE-REACH,FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET,FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", "team:fiscal,fiscal,gate,scale,horizontal,healing", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_gate_scale () = Planning ("FISCAL-GATE-SCALE", Minutes 1040u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_scale_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SCALE", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:57Z", "fiscal", "11-08 opened by fiscal (user 11-08: pull the healing of the long compilation window; we need to scale indefinitely; healings automatic; scaling mostly horizontal). DIAGNOSIS (box tree 11-08): (1) build.ps1 tests every unit on ONE host with -Parallel slots, and CI runs the whole build once per OS under timeout-minutes 420, so gate wall time grows linearly with families; the 11-07 node full build (-Parallel 4, 83 units) hit the 6 h job cap and was VOID. (2) The gate cache key holds the digest of ALL of lib/spiral. (3) Units repeat their closures: the six UBL 2.1 units are 3.78-3.82 MB each (22.7 MB, the cac/cbc library copied six times), the four CT-e family v4 units 1.68 MB each, and 60.6 percent of 1.36 M lines sit in definitions repeated in 5 or more units (FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES n5). One law test alone took 241-3991 s per unit (FISCAL-LAW-MISSING-REPORTED n8-10): compile per unit dominates, not test count. PLANNING GAP: the repeat census was tracked as tidiness (target under 5 percent) and nothing tracked gate wall time, so each new family added cost silently until the cap broke, and then every ERP resume condition waited on a gate that no longer fit. CHILDREN: FISCAL-GATE-SHARD (horizontal), FISCAL-GATE-CACHE-REACH (re-test only what a change reaches), FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET (automatic detection and ratchet), FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES (closures compiled once; UBL common records become linked model units per typed-boundaries rule 1). DoD: adding a family adds a shard, never wall time: a full fiscal gate with the slowest shard at or under 60 min on today's hosts plus CI runners, a lib change re-tests only the units that reach it, and the gate-cost ratchet runs on every build.")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_scale_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SCALE", 2u32, "2026-11-08T12:59Z", "fiscal", "NEXT STEP: FISCAL-GATE-SHARD (Active, fiscal) first, since the ERP-unblock landing needs it today; then CACHE-REACH and BUDGET; VERSIONED-FAMILIES follows the field-meta landing (its step 0 waits on XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS-2-GADT). Estimate 1040 m = open children's remaining work (SHARD 240 x 95 percent = 228, CACHE-REACH 120, BUDGET 120, VERSIONED-FAMILIES steps 1-5 = 570 per its n5 split; step 0 unsized).")
inl note_of_fiscal_gate_scale_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-GATE-SCALE", 3u32, "2026-11-08T13:41Z", "fiscal", "11-08: nested under FISCAL-BUILD-HOURS (the user's P0 epic for the same problem, filed by i574n) as its horizontal and cache lever. CI stays one job per repo (the user rejected YAML sharding 11-08); horizontal means more hosts running build.ps1 -Shards. NEXT STEP unchanged: FISCAL-GATE-SHARD's node run, then FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET's rows.")
inl agile_degrade_detect () = Task ("AGILE-DEGRADE-DETECT", "detect degrading items automatically: coordination signals (stale premises, draft stacks, churn without progress) and resource signals (cap VOIDs, gate-time trends, host hogs) open typed heal incidents", Feature, P0, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,agile,healing,degradation,scheduling,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_agile_degrade_detect () = Planning ("AGILE-DEGRADE-DETECT", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_agile_degrade_detect_1 () = Note ("AGILE-DEGRADE-DETECT", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:57Z", "fiscal", "Filed 11-08 by fiscal for rig (user 11-08: rig needs a way to detect when tasks are degrading because of coordination incompetence or resource hog, which we will keep dealing with; scaling will be mostly horizontal; healings must be automatic). SEED CASE: fiscal's ERP items, stalled since 11-04: 29 FISCAL-ERP notes on 11-03, then only groom and re-decided-stays-Paused notes, progress frozen on 5 Paused items while notes kept accruing. SIGNALS, each computable from backlog state plus job receipts. COORDINATION: (C1) progress flat for 48 h or more while notes grow; (C2) the same Paused reason re-decided twice or more; (C3) a machine-checkable blocking premise that is false (fiscal wrote until-pack61b-is-fleet-wide on 3 items 11-07 for about 4 h while every host already ran that core); (C4) draft stack depth of 2 or more (a draft built on an unlanded draft: fiscal's digits draft sits on field-meta, which sits on step-6); (C5) the age of a wait on another team's item that nobody pulls (AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE clears waits; this flags their age). RESOURCE: (R1) a job VOID at its cap (fiscal full build, 6 h, 11-07); (R2) a gate's wall time trending toward its cap (FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET rows); (R3) queue time over run time for a team's jobs; (R4) a host hog: one process holding a host's CPU or memory while other teams' jobs wait (fiscal launched onto another lane's 100 percent train 11-07; a fiscal gate was the box's largest memory consumer 11-08 01:xx). ACTION: each hit opens a typed incident for the owning team (HEAL-PIPELINE-SLA measures time to heal) and shows as an unblock line in that team's agile next; for C3 the detector re-checks the premise itself and posts the correction. DoD: over the live backlog and the job store, the detector flags the fiscal ERP items (C1, C2, C3, C4) and the 11-07 fiscal full build (R1), flags nothing on 3 healthy active items, runs on a schedule, and its hits reach the owning lane's next. Estimate 480 m provisional (D5 base); rig re-sizes on pickup.")
inl note_of_agile_degrade_detect_2 () = Note ("AGILE-DEGRADE-DETECT", 2u32, "2026-11-08T13:12Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 10:1x rig GROOM: accepted as rig's. Re-sized from 480 m to five slices of at most 240 m (sum 900 m), filed as children. Shared pieces stay in one place: C5 (age of an unpulled cross-team wait) and the hit reaching the owning team's next both ride AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE's routing (one unblock-line mechanism for waits and for degradation hits), and C1 overlaps KIT-AGILE-STALE-ACTIVE (stale Active is the no-notes case, C1 is the many-notes-no-progress case; one detector computes both). R2 reads FISCAL-GATE-BUDGET rows when fiscal writes them. ORDER: AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE first (the routing), then D1, D2, D3, D4, D5. DoD unchanged (fiscal ERP items trip C1-C4, the 11-07 fiscal full build trips R1, 3 healthy items trip nothing, scheduled, hits in the owning next). NEXT: AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE, then D1. TYPEFEATURES: a degradation GADT indexed by its source (Coordination and Resource signals as separate case families, each carrying its evidence record), so an incident cannot be opened without the evidence its signal needs.")
inl fiscal_cn_efapiao () = Task ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", "China fully digitalized e-fapiao as fiscal's first data-dictionary family (STA e-invoice business data standard, parts 1-2)", Story, P2, D5, 30u32, Active, "FISCAL-GENERIC", "team:fiscal,fiscal,generic,country,china", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao () = Planning ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", Minutes 420u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 1u32, "2026-11-08T12:57Z", "fiscal", "Opened 11-08 by fiscal (user 11-08: are we contemplating china yet?). Until now China appeared only in FISCAL-GENERIC n1 (the 10-22 survey). Facts (web, 11-08): fully digitalized e-invoices are national since 2024-12-01 (STA notice); the XML message carrying the digital signature is the accounting original, PDF and OFD only render it; the official structure lives in the e-invoice business data standard (part 1 basic elements, part 2 specific elements, cited by the MOF e-voucher accounting guide of 2025-05), published as documents; no official downloadable XSD was found; a third-party XML spec V3.0 circulates but is unverified. So China is fiscal's first DATA-DICTIONARY family, a front end FISCAL-GENERIC lists but no family uses yet: field tables (name, type, length, cardinality) feed the same typed schema model the XSD front end feeds. NEXT (light): fetch the official data standard parts and the Leqi direct-connection developer docs if public (downloads standing OK), record source URLs and versions here, and write a one-page front-end design. DoD: one official sample e-fapiao XML decodes into the generated typed model and round-trips; the family is a manifest row plus the data-dictionary input, with 0 per-country generator lines. Estimate unsized until the first step names 3 milestones.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 2u32, "2026-11-08T12:59Z", "fiscal", "NEXT STEP: fetch the official e-invoice business data standard parts 1-2 and any public Leqi developer docs, record URLs and versions here, and write the one-page data-dictionary front-end design. Estimate 480 m is PROVISIONAL (D5 base rule), to be replaced by 3 sized milestones after this step.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 3u32, "2026-11-08T13:45Z", "fiscal", "11-08 RESEARCH (read-only web, 11-08). (1) The data standard is national standard GB/T 42965-2023 (part 1 basic elements, GB/T 42965.1; part 2 specific elements, GB/T 42965.2), issued and effective 2023-08-06, listed at openstd.samr.gov.cn (std_list p.p2=42965); whether the full text is free to read is unverified. (2) No official XSD for the STA-issued e-fapiao XML was found. The MOF publishes, per voucher type, an XBRL taxonomy package (schema files, linkbases, an element list with data types and labels, an instance document): for the fully digitalized e-invoice, P020250617561583232009.zip on kjs.mof.gov.cn (page t20250519_3964020, 2025-05-19), entry schema einv_entry_point_2023-12-31.xsd, namespace http://xbrl.mof.gov.cn/taxonomy/2023-12-31/einv. It models the accounting-entry record derived from the invoice, not the invoice XML itself. (3) Leqi direct-connection docs are registration-only (approved taxpayers, credit grade A/B, revenue threshold), not public. (4) No official sample e-fapiao XML was found. DECISION for the first slice: the MOF XBRL taxonomy is fiscal's first XBRL front end and a real XSD set; it gives the accounting projection of a Chinese e-invoice (useful for the generic ERP), while the invoice XML itself waits on GB/T 42965 field tables. NEXT STEP: download the MOF zip (downloads standing OK), list its xsd files and element list, and decide whether the XSD front end reads the XBRL schemas as-is.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 4u32, "2026-11-09T03:48Z", "fiscal", "11-08 FETCH ATTEMPT (autonomous run). Both reconstructed MOF URLs return the site's 404 page (HTML, about 7 KB): http://kjs.mof.gov.cn/zhengcefabu/202505/P020250617561583232009.zip and the announcement page t20250519_3964020.htm under that path; HTTPS fails at the TLS layer from the box. A web search confirms the context (nine departments are rolling out the XML/XBRL-based electronic voucher accounting data standards nationally; software providers must support full digital voucher workflows by 2028: xbrl.org news 'china accelerates e invoicing with xbrl based electronic voucher standards'), but not the zip's real URL. NEXT STEP: find the exact attachment link from the MOF accounting division's standards page (kjs.mof.gov.cn, the electronic voucher accounting data standard section) or a mirror that names einv_entry_point_2023-12-31.xsd; then download into an isolated scratch dir, list the XSDs, and decide whether the XSD front end reads the XBRL schemas as-is. Downloads are standing OK.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 5u32, "2026-11-09T05:55Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 FOUND AND FETCHED (autonomous run, downloads standing OK). The real announcement page is http://kjs.mof.gov.cn/zt/kuaijixinxihuajianshe/dzpzkjsjbzshsd/sjbz/202505/t20250519_3964020.htm (HTTP 200; HTTPS gives 502 from the box; mirror www.xbrl-cn.org/2025/0519/271451.shtml). Note 4's zhengcefabu path was wrong. It lists 9 attachments (full-digital e-invoice, its rail and air ticket variants, fiscal bill, non-tax payment, bank receipt, bank statement, VAT e-invoice, treasury payment). The e-invoice zip is .../sjbz/202505/P020250617561583232009.zip: 196786 bytes, sha256 prefix eb75e173c1315742, 20 entries. It holds the guide docx, the element list xlsx, taxonomy einv-20231231 (einv_cor-20231231.xsd, roles xsd, entry point einv_entry_point_2023-12-31.xsd, label cn/en and presentation linkbases) AND 2 OFFICIAL INSTANCE DOCUMENTS: einv_ord_20220326_22442000000005170034.xml (ordinary, 36 facts, 5 monetary with unitRef CNY and decimals 0) and einv_spcl_20231231_22442000000921291350.xml (special VAT). Note 3's claim that no official sample exists is CORRECTED: these 2 instances are the DoD round-trip samples. SHAPE: XBRL item style. 58 elements: 47 substitutionGroup xbrli:item, 2 xbrli:tuple (InformationOfAccountingDocumentsTuple and InformationOfDebitAndCreditEntryTuple, each a complexType sequence of element refs, minOccurs 0 maxOccurs unbounded); item types 27 stringItemType, 8 booleanItemType, 5 monetaryItemType, 4 gYearMonthItemType, 2 gYearItemType, 1 dateItemType; imports xbrl-instance-2003-12-31.xsd and the dtr numeric/nonNumeric schemas by remote URL. GAP vs the XSD front end: lib xsd.spi:258 already reads element ref as the name, but nothing reads substitutionGroup or the xbrli item types. DECISION: no new front end. The XSD front end gets (a) a fixed xbrli prelude mapping the 6 item types to existing primitives (monetary = decimal plus unitRef and decimals attributes) instead of fetching the remote imports; (b) substitutionGroup xbrli:item or xbrli:tuple makes a global element a fact the root xbrli:xbrl may hold, beside context and unit records. LICENSE: the taxonomy header says all rights reserved, no reproduction without MOF written permission, so fiscal FETCHES the zip at build time (corpus manifest row with url + sha256), never commits it. MILESTONES (replace the provisional 480 m): M1 corpus row + xbrli prelude, cor xsd generates (120 m); M2 substitutionGroup facts + context/unit records, both instances decode (180 m); M3 round-trip both instances, family manifest row, 0 per-country generator lines (120 m). GB/T 42965 field tables stay a later family for the invoice XML itself. Files in the box scratch cn-efapiao dir (local only). NEXT: M1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 6u32, "2026-11-09T06:46Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 M1 PART 1 DONE: fiscal scripts/init.ps1 (D2D63253, unstaged) fetches the MOF zip with Expand-Pinned (http URL; HTTPS gave 502 from the box; pin EB75E173C1315742; entries carry the zip UTF-8 name flag 0x0800, so no code page) into deps/corpus/cn/einv, which /deps/ in .gitignore keeps out of git (license: all rights reserved). DRIFT-NEUTRAL, checked against each whole-corpus scan: init's root scan writes manifests only for UBL kinds and 3 named roots (HU NAV, GR myDATA, MX CFDI), and the MOF XMLs have roots xbrli:xbrl and link:linkbase; pattern-oracle.ps1 reads xs:pattern facets from every corpus xsd, and the 3 MOF xsds have 0; no generated unit embeds the new paths. M1 PART 2 DESIGN (lib, the next draft): xsd_resolve::is_builtin is PREFIX-based (xs or xsd only). Make it namespace-based through the existing namespace_for (XMLSchema namespace or the xbrli instance namespace http://www.xbrl.org/2003/instance), and extend xsd_emit builtin_kinds with the 6 xbrli item types: stringItemType StringBuiltin, monetaryItemType DecimalBuiltin, booleanItemType BooleanBuiltin, dateItemType DateBuiltin, gYearMonthItemType and gYearItemType OtherBuiltin (text). The remote xbrl.org imports are then never fetched. Then M2: substitutionGroup xbrli:item/xbrli:tuple facts under an xbrli:xbrl root with context and unit records.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 7u32, "2026-11-09T08:52Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 M1 PART 2 DRAFTED, simpler than n6's plan: NO xsd_emit change. lib xsd_resolve draft 4405043F (kit drafts spiral FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO-M1 v1, over live 0A4CBB93, canonical per lib_roundtrip) maps an XBRL item type to its XML Schema builtin AT QUALIFICATION: xbrli_item_builtin resolves the reference's prefix through the schema's own namespace declarations (namespace_for) and, only when it is the XBRL instance namespace http://www.xbrl.org/2003/instance, maps the local name via a 6-row table (stringItemType string, monetaryItemType decimal, booleanItemType boolean, dateItemType date, gYearMonthItemType gYearMonth, gYearItemType gYear); qualify_reference then returns xs:<base>, and everything downstream (is_builtin, xsd_emit builtin_kinds by local name) sees an ordinary builtin. The old body is kept as qualify_plain. The remote xbrl.org imports are never fetched. Test an_xbrli_item_type_resolves_to_its_xml_schema_builtin: xbrli:monetaryItemType -> xs:decimal, xbrli:stringItemType -> xs:string, the namespace decides (x:dateItemType with x bound to the instance namespace -> xs:date), and other:monetaryItemType in another namespace is NOT mapped. Gating on moon (job-1794214275368-fiscal-cn-gate). OPEN for M2: confirm the MOF schema's references go through qualify_reference (it runs in rename_schema during catalog resolution), then substitutionGroup facts + context/unit records.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 8u32, "2026-11-09T08:56Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 M1 PART 1 EXECUTED (not just parsed): init.ps1's own Save-Pinned and Expand-Pinned (extracted by AST) ran the CN block against a scratch deps dir on the box: the pin EB75E173C1315742 verified, Expand-Archive unpacked 13 files with the Chinese folder names intact (UTF-8 flag), 3 xsd (einv_entry_point_2023-12-31, einv_cor-20231231, einv-20231231_rol) and both official instances (einv_ord_*, einv_spcl_*). xsd_resolve part 2 is green on moon (7/7) and its land proof is running.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 9u32, "2026-11-09T09:05Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 M1 PART 2 LIVE: lib xsd_resolve 4405043F (XBRL item types resolve to their xs: builtins through the schema's own namespace binding). LANDED copy-only on the box from a proven close (moon job-1794214487335-fiscal-libland-proof6: round trip, signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type probe PASS 7 tests, respell drift 0, lib digest 99ED43B950E2005F, equal to the box digest after the land). M1 is complete on both halves: the corpus fetch (init.ps1, executed and verified) and the type mapping (lib). NEXT: M2, substitutionGroup xbrli:item / xbrli:tuple facts under an xbrli:xbrl root with context and unit records, and first confirm that the MOF schema's references pass through qualify_reference (rename_schema during catalog resolution).")
inl note_of_fiscal_cn_efapiao_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-CN-EFAPIAO", 10u32, "2026-11-09T09:08Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "11-09 M2 PREMISE CHECKED (read-only): the MOF schema's type references DO pass through the new mapping. fiscal's generator loads XSD families via xsd_resolve::load_schema_tree_with (generator.spi:541) -> load_tree -> resolve_read_schema, which runs qualify_schema (declared_namespaces attributes []) with the schema ROOT's xmlns declarations (xsd_resolve.spi:455-461); einv_cor-20231231.xsd's root declares xmlns:xbrli=http://www.xbrl.org/2003/instance, so xbrli:*ItemType references become xs: builtins at load. (The qualify_schema [] calls in xsd_emit/json_schema are test helpers with no namespaces; the mapping correctly does nothing there.) M2 scope stays: a manifest family row for cn/einv (Xsd entry over einv_cor-20231231.xsd), then substitutionGroup xbrli:item/xbrli:tuple facts as root-level elements of an xbrli:xbrl document with context and unit records, decoding both official instances.")
inl lib_tlds () = Task ("LIB-TLDS", "lib/spiral/tlds.spi: a generic TLD module (typed literal chunks plus is_tld) for link detection; lib, rig and Cells never name x or any network", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:microblog,lib,cells,cell-budget,generic", "current", "current")
