inl note_of_lib_tlds_1 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T13:00Z", "microblog", "Decided by i574n 11-08 during the CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO grooming: the stable home of the TLD list is a lib Spiral module, not a .txt (no-.txt rule) and not a Cells asset; postability is generic and x and microblog both consume it. Steps: (1) round-trip the lib draft, then land through lib_land_window (draft form tlds.spi=<path>, -Apply); (2) x client opens lib tlds; the 2 data references stop reading the file; (3) Cells cell_budget.ex keeps data/tlds.txt as a private asset until its budget logic is ported to Spiral and opens lib tlds, then tlds.txt is deleted. Not a blocker for M1 of CELLS-TO-RIG-REPO. NEXT STEP: draft lib/spiral/tlds.spi from x apps/client/tlds.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_tlds_2 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 2u32, "2026-11-08T13:18Z", "microblog", "CORRECTED by the user 11-08: generic only. Spiral and rig must not know x exists (CELL-BUDGET-NAMING, user 11-01: 280 is a phantom constant kept in ONE place, @weight_limit in Cells CellBudget.Profile; no X nomenclature). So: (1) lib tlds is plain link-detection data with generic names; no x, post or network wording in lib, rig or Cells. (2) Cells cell_budget opens lib tlds when its budget logic is ported (then data/tlds.txt is deleted). (3) The x side does not repoint anything: x client drops its own TLD list and opens lib tlds; the tlds.spi:202 test that compared x list vs the Cells file is deleted (one source, nothing to compare); postability/x.json is NOT updated, it retires with the profile loader (POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE). X-only layers (t.co weight, dot defusing, poster header) stay in x/microblog. (4) Code-side autolink collisions are already solved by the dot-to-:: spelling migration, so no lib rule exists for dotted names. microblog inherits these generic configs from lib/rig. NEXT STEP: draft lib/spiral/tlds.spi with generic names, round-trip it, then the land window.")
inl note_of_lib_tlds_3 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 3u32, "2026-11-08T13:30Z", "microblog", "Draft READY (microblog 11-08, CPU-light while job-1794144215181-x-regen-1108a runs): %USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-TLDS\\in\\tlds.spi, 192 lines. From x apps/client/tlds.spi with: no ///- package line (lib files have none); no :< prelude (lib never opens it): spread id -> listm'::collect id, has -> listm'::exists' (both forms already in lib: parallel.spi, cursor_walk.spi); the test example post -> dev; the Cells-file comparison test and its listed_tlds/file_tlds helpers removed (lib is the one source). No network, x or Cells wording. ROUNDTRIP tlds.spi: canonical true fixpoint true (lib_roundtrip.exs, private MIX_BUILD_PATH); canonical bytes equal the draft. TRAP for the land: x apps/client/tlds.spi is ALSO module tlds, and x builds with spiral lib packages, so land lib tlds and delete x's copy in the same step (x callers then resolve to lib tlds::is_tld). DoD: lib tlds landed via lib_land_window with its test green on rust and gleam; x copy deleted, its tlds.spi:202 file test gone; 0 network or x wording in lib. NEXT STEP: lib_program_gate proof of common_and_generic_tlds_are_known on the node, then lib_land_window -Apply (draft form tlds.spi=<path>) with the x delete in the same window.")
inl note_of_lib_tlds_4 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T04:41Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 proof queued: job-1794199295529-lib-tlds-gate on moon, after job-1794198981519-cells-per-test-ab. It copies mirror cellspt1's lib/spiral (bf5cc30a + live edits, digest BCB3B8A8), adds the draft tlds.spi (C10D96111D4C, hash-pinned in the wrapper), and runs cellspt1's lib_gate.ps1 -File tlds.spi with a private build path. Evidence lands in C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-tlds-gate-<ts>\\summary.json. Green opens lib_land_window (tlds.spi=<draft>, -Apply) in the same step as deleting x apps/client/tlds.spi and its file-comparison test. The next client verify covers the x side.")
inl note_of_lib_tlds_5 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T08:44Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 lib proof GREEN: job-1794212718688-microblog-head2 step lib-tlds-gate (run lib-tlds-gate-20261109043547), lib_gate.ps1 on a cellspt1 lib copy plus the draft tlds.spi C10D96111D4C: tests passed 1 of 1, type errors 0. Next: the land, in ONE step: lib_land_window (draft tlds.spi=<path>, -Apply; box copy-only via a node -PrivateLib proof + -ProvenLog when the box is saturated), and in the same step delete x apps/client/tlds.spi and its file-comparison test, so x callers resolve to lib tlds::is_tld.")
inl note_of_lib_tlds_6 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T08:48Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 land in progress: proof job-1794214024263-lib-tlds-landproof on moon (org-approved; lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply on the cellspt1 mirror lib, draft C10D96111D4C). x-side step, checked on the box, to apply right after the box copy-only land: (1) delete x apps/client/tlds.spi; (2) remove the 'tlds' module line from BOTH x manifests, apps/client/package.spiproj:9 and spiral.toml:7 (dual manifests). The callers (splitter.spi:8, domains/domains.spi:7, defuse.spi:8) use ':< tlds' and then resolve to lib tlds. The definitions x has and the draft lacks are only listed_tlds and file_tlds, the file-comparison test helpers, with 0 caller uses. postability/x.json:34 still names Cells data/tlds.txt, and that retires with the profile loader (POSTABILITY-ONE-SOURCE), unchanged here. The proof of the x side is the next client verify.")
inl note_of_lib_tlds_7 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T09:12Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 LANDED. Moon proof job-1794214427244-lib-tlds-landproof2: lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply on the cellspt1 mirror lib, with the alphabet and dice siblings synced and SPIRAL_CELLS_SKIP_CLI_EXPORT=1 because the mirror has no spiral.exe. Result: round trip, 0 signature drift, consumer spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26/26, type-probe PASS, 0 respell drift; LANDED and closed green; mirror digest 5EED4DBE85EF04ED. Run 1 failed only on those environment gaps and undid itself. Box: the land.log was scp'd back, then lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply: kit tree-write window, fast checks re-run (the box lib differed from the mirror), document_test taken from the proof; LANDED and closed green; live lib tlds.spi C10D96111D4C, lib digest 63F6E0FEF0448055, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-050708. Same step in x (unstaged): apps/client/tlds.spi deleted (202 lines with the file-comparison test) and the 'tlds' module line removed from package.spiproj and spiral.toml; the callers' ':< tlds' now resolves to lib. DoD left: the next x client verify (it rides the long tail).")
