inl note_of_lib_tlds_11 () = Note ("LIB-TLDS", 11u32, "2026-11-09T16:04Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 12:0x microblog, per org2's lib-move lesson (memory lib-move-drops-test-execution): after the move, lib/spiral/tlds.spi's test (common_and_generic_tlds_are_known, rust + gleam) ran in NO recurring gate. lib/spiral/build.ps1's curated notebook list did not name it, and x's client gate only covers x's own files. Fixed (unstaged): build.ps1 lists 'tlds' at the end (it composes with org2's unstaged removal of physics from the same list). The test was already green 1/1 in the 11-09 lib-tlds node gate, so spiral CI gains one cheap notebook. This is the lib owning its module's tests, which beats making each consumer derive a lib list.")
