inl note_of_agile_degrade_d2_1 () = Note ("AGILE-DEGRADE-D2", 1u32, "2026-11-08T13:12Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "DoD: premises the detector can check (an installed pack or train, an item status, a host core) are re-checked and a false one posts a correction note; draft stacks are read from the drafts store and depth 2 or more is a hit; fiscal 11-07 until-pack61b premise and the digits/field-meta/step-6 stack trip them. NEXT: list the premise words already machine-checkable (train, pack, item status). TYPEFEATURES: a premise union (InstalledTrain, InstalledPack, ItemStatus, HostCore) with a checked verdict.")
inl note_of_agile_degrade_d2_2 () = Note ("AGILE-DEGRADE-D2", 2u32, "2026-11-09T05:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:2x rig C3 DRY RUN on the live backlog: 108 Paused or Blocked items; a regex for TRAIN or pack numbers near wait/until/after/blocked on/install in each item's LAST note, compared with what is installed (TRAIN41, pack63c), flagged 5. Read by hand: 1 true (FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, waits on the fleet respell after TRAIN41, both done; correction note posted to its owner compiler), 1 likely (FORMATTER-JOIN-LONE-THEN, waits on the user's spiral push with pack55d's core; the fleet is on pack63c but the push itself is not checkable from here), 3 false (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT really waits on TRAIN42, pack63 was a side mention; TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD waits on a compiler candidate built on pack57, not on pack57; MICROBLOG-MIGRATION says works on installed pack61b, a statement, not a premise). Precision 2 in 5 means the detector must read only the Blocked on: or Waits: clause, split it into premises, and require ALL premises met before calling it false; version numbers elsewhere in a note are not premises. Better still, premises belong in waits.spi rows (train/item kinds already self-clear), so C3 for free text is the migration path into rows. TypeFeatures unchanged: premise union (InstalledTrain, InstalledPack, ItemStatus, HostCore) with a checked verdict.")
