inl note_of_agile_degrade_d3_1 () = Note ("AGILE-DEGRADE-D3", 1u32, "2026-11-08T13:12Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "DoD: hits computed from kit job receipts on box and node; the 11-07 fiscal full build (6 h cap) trips R1; R3 reports per team with the numbers; CLI tests on fixture job dirs. NEXT: read the exit and timeout files kit job writes. TYPEFEATURES: the Resource case family with job evidence records.")
inl note_of_agile_degrade_d3_2 () = Note ("AGILE-DEGRADE-D3", 2u32, "2026-11-09T04:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:1x rig, first evidence before code (job list on each host, last 300 or fewer records): box 300 jobs, 1 void at cap (kit-coordinator-dry2), 0 lost; ganymede 55 jobs, 2 void at cap (rig-regen1108, my own: 374 outputs at 20 s serial outgrew a 90 min cap; x-pluto-build2), 3 lost (compiler's refused --heavy records, fixed by KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR item 2 in TRAIN42); moon 300 jobs, 4 void at cap (x-cells-full6, x-crates2, fiscal-full-build2 ...), 6 lost; europa 234 jobs, 0 void, 3 lost. DESIGN: R1 = a job whose state is timed-out or memory-capped (exit 124/137) is a degradation row naming label, host, cap and elapsed, deduplicated per label stem (the trailing digits and letters of reruns stripped, so x-cells-full6 and x-cells-full7 are one stem) so a rerun under a wider cap closes it; R3 = per team (label prefix to team via lane aliases) the median queue wait (started_ms minus created) over median run time above 1.0 in the window. Typed: a degradation union (VoidAtCap of label * host * cap_ms | QueueOverRun of team * ratio_x100) feeding AGILE-DEGRADE-D5 incidents. Sources: local job dirs plus job list --on per host (no remote waiters). Code in TRAIN43 (TRAIN42 scope frozen).")
