inl note_of_rename_1108_i574n_2 () = Note ("RENAME-1108-I574N", 2u32, "2026-11-09T12:31Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:3x DONE FOR i574n.github (unstaged; backups in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\RENAME-1108-I574N): by meaning per the lexicon map. Our own content hash -> fingerprint: remote.ps1 (Get-TreeDigest/Get-CoreDigest -> Get-TreeFingerprint/Get-CoreFingerprint, all vars and messages incl. the function text shipped to the node; consumers node-proof.ps1 and kit launch-train.ps1 match only the REMOTE-SYNC-OK <repo> prefix, so nothing parses the renamed word), node-ship.ps1. Liveness -> ping: linux-worker.ps1 $probe. Test scratch -> trial: hooks-test lease prefix, safe-delete-test scratch dir. Control sample -> control: banned-words-scan probe.txt. Instruments -> gauge: node-utilization-monitor message. docs/agents/agent-sync.md: probe -> trial. All parse clean. KEPT as external names: dice + alphabet keccak/sha2 digests (sha2::Digest, the digest crate, the lib digest module), compiler's lib_land_window \"lib digest\" (spiral, not this item). DEFERRED: regex certificate.spi's probe type (a state pair under exploration) is copied verbatim into REGEX-LIB-3's drafts, so renaming it now would break the staged land; rename after REGEX-LIB-3 lands (in the lib copy). html and blog had none. Left: identifiers with Probe inside a word (Invoke-NodeProbeWin, NodeProbeTimeoutMs) across node-env consumers, a separate sweep.")
