inl note_of_store_no_dangling_1 () = Note ("STORE-NO-DANGLING", 1u32, "2026-11-08T18:35Z", "tibia", "oort (rented 11-08 14:31: Oort Object Storage sjc1, bucket oort-bucket, private, lifecycle abort-incomplete-multipart-2d; keys ~/.secrets/cloud-s3.env, never printed; box measured 4.5 Mbit/s up, 8.6 down; memory oort-object-store). Lane answers + prior-art survey: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\remote-store-20261108. resilience: incomplete multipart uploads bill invisibly and are likely on a 6 Mbit link (oort has abort-after-2d already); forgotten objects/versions; leaked keys; public misconfig. tibia's Encke lesson: a refused vx1 create left a 400 GB boot volume billing (found by a list call, deleted). DoD: one check command reports multipart uploads, lifecycle presence per bucket, key-pattern grep over repos, unattached volumes/snapshots, and month-to-date storage cost, green on today's state. NEXT STEP: write the check against oort and the Cloud-provider API. TYPEFEATURES: none (operations).")
inl note_of_store_no_dangling_2 () = Note ("STORE-NO-DANGLING", 2u32, "2026-11-09T12:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:1x FIRST SLICE (read-only checks, no deletions): (1) oort incomplete multipart uploads: 0 (rclone backend list-multipart-uploads -> []); the bucket also carries the abort-incomplete-multipart-2d lifecycle rule (tibia 11-08), so leftovers self-clear. (2) inventory: 185 objects, 1.139 GiB, top prefixes backups/ compiler/ fiscal/ i574n/ results/ toolchains/ (all expected owners). (3) no S3 key in any repo file: an in-process scan (keys loaded from OORT_ENV_FILE into memory, never on a command line, never printed) over 52,601 tracked + untracked-not-ignored files across every C:\\home\\git repo found 0 files containing either key. (4) the two box scripts that use the keys (store-offsite-backup.ps1, compiler's install-pack.ps1) read bucket and secrets path from env since tonight. Left for DoD: a monthly cost-drift alarm over the inventory (size + object count as a time series), provider orphans after failed creates (volumes, snapshots, IPs), and a recorded lifecycle-rule read (rclone cannot show it; needs the provider API).")
inl note_of_store_no_dangling_3 () = Note ("STORE-NO-DANGLING", 3u32, "2026-11-09T12:07Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 08:1x COST-DRIFT ALARM wired: store-offsite-backup.ps1 (already scheduled) now appends rclone size --json for the bucket to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\schedules\\oort-inventory.tsv (iso, objects, bytes) on every run, and its log line carries oort=<objects>obj/<GiB>; when the bucket is over 2x its earliest size within the last 30 days the line adds WARN:oort-size-doubled-in-30d(a->b GiB); a failed size query reads oort-inventory=UNKNOWN, never a clean value. Live run 12:04Z: exit 0, LOCKED, VERIFIED, oort=187obj/1.15GiB, first TSV row written. Left: provider orphans after failed creates (volumes, snapshots, IPs; needs the provider API, read-only) and a recorded lifecycle-rule read.")
inl note_of_store_no_dangling_4 () = Note ("STORE-NO-DANGLING", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:36Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:4x LAST PIECE needs the user: provider orphans after failed creates (volumes, snapshots, reserved IPs) can only be listed through the provider API, and no provider CLI or key is configured on the box (no vultr-cli, no config). Configuring one means entering an API key, which agents never do. Ask: either the user runs a read-only listing (e.g. the provider console's block storage / snapshots / reserved IPs pages) once and pastes the counts, or installs a read-only-scoped key for a CLI themselves. Everything else in the DoD is done (oort multipart 0 + lifecycle rule, inventory + 30-day doubling alarm wired, no S3 key in any repo).")
