inl note_of_rig_pack_ship_1 () = Note ("RIG-PACK-SHIP", 1u32, "2026-11-08T18:44Z", "i574n", "USER 11-08 14:4x: 'is management ready to absorb/assimilate/take over i574n and resilience? rate 0-1000, then groom what's missing' (handover blocker). Today pack shipping depends on %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\pack-chain.ps1, a DRAFT in i574n's folder with no committed home, run by hand by i574n (pack62 11-08: box verify, node in-place swap with undo TSV, europa Linux source build needing 2.1 GB headroom and a serve pause). Shape: one rig verb that (a) verifies box DLL + source hashes against compiler's quote, (b) refuses while a train runs unless told, (c) ships to the node in place per file with an undo list and a fresh-process smoke, plus a core-hash check (the script only checked the host DLL), (d) for Linux hosts PULLS the pack from oort (STORE-LINUX-PACK-PULL: packs/linux-x64/sha256-<sha>.tgz, by-source index) and source-builds only when no object exists, uploading the result, (e) prints the broadcast line for every lane. Then any lane, management first, can ship. DoD: pack63 shipped to node + europa by management with this verb; europa never source-builds a pack that already has an object. Next step: lift pack-chain.ps1's steps into kit typed jobs after TRAIN41.")
