inl note_of_rig_lanes_generic_1 () = Note ("RIG-LANES-GENERIC", 1u32, "2026-11-08T19:13Z", "org2", "USER 11-08 15:0x: renamed management->org, i574n->org2, resilience->org3; 'groom the backlog properly ... kit should rework everything needed to keep things generic, also gotta revisit the typefeatureset. throughout the days the three lanes should be indistinguishable pull wise while org retaining all responsibilities so org2 and org3 can be retired at any time'. Context: 3 sessions (org, org2, org3) now share team org; earlier renames (x->microblog, kit->rig, main->i574n->org2, resilience+management->org) each needed hand fixes in scripts and rosters. SHAPE: (1) rig reads lanes from ONE source (today lane-aliases.txt; later a typed lanes model in rig, LANE-WORK-MODEL) and has no hardcoded lane/session names (grep rig for main, i574n, management, resilience, x-dumps, kit as lane tokens; derive or delete); (2) agile next/list --team T resolves T through the alias map, so --team management or --team i574n still lands on org; (3) claims and notes record the SESSION (author), while routing, WIP, close ratios and reports group by TEAM; (4) any session of a team can pull, claim or release any team item (pull-wise indistinguishable), and a stale claim by a closed session expires by TTL; (5) lane-reconcile's learn-alias and enforce steps become a rig verb (rig lanes reconcile) instead of an i574n.github script. TypeFeatures: team and session as distinct nominal types (phantom-indexed ids) so a session id can't be passed where a team is expected. DoD: grep of rig shows 0 hardcoded lane names; --team with an old name resolves; a claim from org3 on an org item and a release from org works; per-team close ratio printed by rig. Next step: grep rig for lane tokens and list them.")
inl type_feature_census_flag () = Task ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", "compiler --features-out: per-file counts of gadt, existential, hkt, prototype, reflection and phantom type parameters from the typed AST, so rig's census reads facts instead of grepping text", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,census,rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_type_feature_census_flag () = Planning ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_1 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 1u32, "2026-11-08T19:17Z", "compiler", "11-08 compiler, filed from org2's star-exchange ask (user 11-08: revisit the type features as a PER-FEATURE census, separate counts, no umbrella word in code). PLAN: a '--features-out <file.json>' flag on --check writes per-file FACTS, so rig's census reads compiler output instead of grepping text. Counted separately: gadt (union constructors whose result type refines a type index), existential (TyExists in definition signatures + pack sites), hkt (type parameters of a non-* kind, i.e. TyInl-kinded), prototype (prototype declarations and instances), reflection (uses of a fixed, listed set of reflective primitives), phantom (declared type parameters that occur in no field). The typed AST already separates these (TyForall, TyExists, TyInl, nominal/union declarations, the prototype env), so this is a read-only pass after infer. SCOPE CAVEAT: --check skips test bodies, so counts cover definitions; the JSON states its scope. DoD: one fixture per feature with exact expected counts plus a zero-count negative file; output schema versioned (type-features/v1); rig's census consumes it on one repo. TYPEFEATURES: the per-file record is a typed record of six i32 counts plus scope, not a string map. NEXT STEP: list the reflective primitives (union_reflection, the record/union reflection functions) and the exact AST shapes for each count, then write the fixtures first.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_2 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 2u32, "2026-11-08T19:21Z", "compiler", "11-08 compiler, SCHEMA AGREED with org2 (consumer: rig's TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT, retitled 'per-feature census'; RENAME-1108-RIG drops the umbrella marker). No umbrella word in the flag name, the JSON keys or the title. Flag: --features-out <file.json> on --check. Per file, one object with seven i32 counts under exactly these keys: gadt, existential, hkt, prototype, prototype_instances, reflection, phantom, plus 'scope': 'definitions only; test bodies are skipped by --check' and 'schema': 'features/v1'. Rig reads these facts first and falls back to its own source scan per feature when a key is missing.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_3 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 3u32, "2026-11-09T01:04Z", "compiler", "11-08 fiscal study (studied-engineering-techniques) asks of compiler: (1) a rejection-class tally per gate (indexed/consumed/brand/family/privacy/distinct/shape) counted from the compiler error text over every fails cell, so typefeatureset promises are counted; (2) a payoff row before any new encoding (error, bug stopped, consumer, cost); (3) build cost = size-weighted critical path; model units take plain fields, not feature evidence; (4) count cells within 10% of the 272 budget (pile-up watch); (5) differential rewrites on 100k+ generated inputs with golden hashes. Next step: fold (1) and (4) into the --features-out schema as extra CensusCount keys once rig lands features/v1.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_4 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 4u32, "2026-11-09T04:05Z", "compiler", "11-09 00:5x compiler DESIGN (rig keys features/v1, accepted verbatim): a PrepassFeatures module beside PrepassReferences (spiral_compiler.fs ~7963), gated by SPIRAL_FEATURES_OUT (the host flag --features-out <file> sets it), enqueues rows path<TAB>key<TAB>count and flushes once at process exit like the references rows; rig aggregates path -> package with the manifest it already reads, so CensusCount rows are (package, key, count). Counting at the Bundle stage (after parse, before inference; Bundle type ~3921): feature-prototype = BundlePrototype; feature-instance = BundleInstance; feature-gadt-case = union cases whose RawTExpr uses the signature form (range_of_texpr_gadt_constructor already detects it); feature-existential = RawExists + RawTExists occurrences in every bundle body; feature-hkt = a HoVar with an arrow kind in a bundle head, or a type variable applied to arguments; feature-phantom = a BundleType/Nominal/NominalRec HoVar with no free occurrence in its RawTExpr (exact, not token-based); feature-reflection = PrepassReferences use rows whose target path is union_reflection.spi or reflection.spi, plus nameof. feature-law-test stays rig-only (a test-name convention, invisible to the compiler); feature-phantom-rust comes from codegenRust PhantomData emission (a separate counter at codegen). Acceptance: the per-package diff of compiler vs rig token counts on lib/spiral + kit/src, every nonzero cell explained. Next step: draft the kitdo (PrepassFeatures + the host flag), build on ganymede after pack64.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_5 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 5u32, "2026-11-09T06:14Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:2x compiler: IMPLEMENTED (draft): kit drafts spiral TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG 1-features-out.kitdo (core 7 + host 1 replacements) over pack65 -> pack66 source core 2d2d13ac / host caa270f0. Design as built: a FeatureCensus module (thread-local counters, active only while walking); the existing fold_offset_ty/fold_offset_term visitors call hit on union cases with is_gadt (feature-gadt-case), RawTExists/RawExists (feature-existential), forall binders with an arrow kind (feature-hkt), and collect RawTVar names; FeatureCensusBundles.countModule walks the module's bundle stream after load_module's parse and adds feature-prototype, feature-instance, arrow-kinded HoVars (feature-hkt) and nominal/type parameters no body mentions (feature-phantom); rows path<TAB>key<TAB>count append to SPIRAL_FEATURES_OUT at exit; the host sets it from --features-out <file>. Dropped: a type-variable-applied heuristic (it cannot tell a type variable from a type constructor name syntactically). Not in the compiler: feature-law-test, feature-reflection (rig token census), feature-phantom-rust (later, codegenRust). QUEUED: ganymede job-1794204862068-compiler-pack66-features (build + --features-out over a lib --check, per-key totals). Next step: diff per package against rig's token census once rig lands features/v1.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_6 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 6u32, "2026-11-09T06:46Z", "compiler", "11-09 02:5x compiler: pack66 BUILT (Linux core 17b9efc5dff83ba0, host 3b1da458) and --features-out WORKS: one lib --check (28 s) wrote 82 rows (path, key, count) over lib/spiral + core. Totals: feature-gadt-case 179 in 19 files, feature-instance 168 in 16, feature-prototype 54 in 15, feature-phantom 32 in 21, feature-existential 13 in 8, feature-hkt 5 in 3. Top: xsd_emit instances 90, xpath gadt cases 83, leptos instances 24, regex_nullable gadt 18. Next step: the per-package diff against rig's token census (features/v1) once rig wires it; pack66 gate then rollout.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_7 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 7u32, "2026-11-09T07:09Z", "compiler", "pack66 gate GREEN on ganymede (2026-11-09): suite -All exit 0 in 8m39s; vs pack63c run single-flight-20261109-032210: 7586 common rows, residual diffs 0, compile-status diffs 23 = all old timeouts now finishing (15 timeout->ok, 8 timeout->error on routes_negative_* expected-error samples). pack67 (pack66 + sorted rust linked uses) building on ganymede chain3.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_8 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 8u32, "2026-11-09T07:55Z", "compiler", "BLIND SPOT FOUND + FIXED (draft 2-count-project-modules.kitdo, 11-09): the census hook sat only in loader_package, but a projects own modules are parsed in the supervisor FileOpen branch, so the 11-08 numbers (gadt-case 179, instance 168, ...) are PACKAGE MODULES ONLY. Program 2 (applies after TS-TYPEFEATURESET-PROBES/1-types-out) defers counting to process exit for every module (countLater on both paths, countAtExit registered before the row flush; no Hopac.run inside the supervisor loop). Proven on ganymede as pack69 (core 955146f8): the probe project module now emits main.spi feature-phantom 1 (quantity unit), package rows unchanged, types.d.ts byte-identical to pack68. Rerun the per-package census after this lands.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_9 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 9u32, "2026-11-09T08:34Z", "compiler", "pack69 (pack67 + types-out + census project-module fix) suite gate on ganymede 07:56-08:31Z under load 24-27 on 4 cores (35 min vs 8.6 idle): 7586 rows, residual diffs 0 vs pack66; compile-status diffs 106 ALL into timeout (ok->timeout 85, error->timeout 21) across 12 samples = load artifacts, so PENDING not green. Recheck of exactly those 12 samples with -TimeoutSec 600 behind a load<8 guard is phase 0 of ~/remote-stage/pack70/p70gate.sh.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_10 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 10u32, "2026-11-09T09:06Z", "compiler", "pack69 GATE GREEN (11-09 09:00Z): the 12 samples whose 106 rows timed out under load were rechecked with -TimeoutSec 600 at load < 8: 106 common rows vs pack66, compile-status diffs 0, residual diffs 0. With the full run (7586 rows, residual diffs 0), pack69 (pack67 + TS-TYPEFEATURESET 1-types-out + CENSUS 2-count-project-modules) is residual-identical to pack66 on every row. Rollout rides the next pack after pack70 (C NULL-safe incref) clears its gate.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_11 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 11u32, "2026-11-10T10:37Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:3x compiler (groom with fiscal; rig mapped TRAIN42e to TRAIN43f \"or clear if no train is needed\"): CLEARED, not re-pointed. This item never needed a rig train: the wait stood for its pack content reaching the Windows hosts, and pack78 (containing pack67-pack77) is installed on all four nodes (box/moon Core f4148639; Linux now pack82 Core c495bc57). pack69''s content (TS-TYPEFEATURESET 1-types-out + CENSUS 2-count-project-modules) is in every installed pack since. Next step: confirm the census flag on an installed compiler and close.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_12 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 12u32, "2026-11-10T10:42Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:4x compiler: CONFIRMED on an installed compiler. ganymede (pack83, Core 2c6efed9, which carries pack66s 1-features-out program): --check --features-out on apps/compiler/tmp/samples/empty_match_false_eliminator writes the agreed rows path<TAB>key<TAB>count: main.spi feature-gadt-case 2 (UnitValue, BoolValue refine value ty), samples core operators.spi feature-prototype 4 and feature-instance 4; check rc 0. Format = rigs accepted features/v1 TSV design (11-09 00:05 note), superseding the first JSON sketch.")
inl note_of_type_feature_census_flag_13 () = Note ("TYPE-FEATURE-CENSUS-FLAG", 13u32, "2026-11-10T10:45Z", "compiler", "Evidence: pack66 lib --check wrote 82 rows over lib/spiral + core (gadt-case 179, instance 168, prototype 54, phantom 32, existential 13, hkt 5); pack69 gate residual-identical to pack66 on 7586 rows; installed ganymede pack83 run 11-10 06:4x local wrote the expected 3 rows for the GADT sample.")
