inl iggy_ca_reissue () = Task ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", "Reissue the iggy CA and server cert on europa: ECDSA P-256 instead of Ed25519 (Windows Schannel and LibreSSL cannot handshake with Ed25519, rc 35), and keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign on the CA (Python >= 3.13 rejects a CA without it)", TaskKind, P3, D2, 40u32, Active, "", "team:microblog,iggy,europa,tls,serve", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_iggy_ca_reissue () = Planning ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_iggy_ca_reissue_1 () = Note ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", 1u32, "2026-11-08T20:38Z", "microblog", "Found by tibia 11-08 while battle-testing the public iggy HTTPS API on europa:3000: Python/OpenSSL handshakes, Schannel and LibreSSL fail; Python 3.13 strict mode rejects the CA (no keyUsage), so the bench relaxes only that flag. Not urgent: a reissue restarts iggy under the live :30087 serve. Do it in a serve maintenance window per the runbook (memory xsim-serve-deploy-runbook): new CA + server cert, update the iggy-tls secret, rollout restart iggy, re-hand the new public ca.crt to clients (tibia moon/ganymede, the serve), verify /ping from Windows curl (Schannel) and Python strict. DoD: curl.exe from the box gets 200 on https://<europa-addr>:3000/ping without -k when given the CA; Python 3.13 verifies without relaxing flags.")
inl note_of_iggy_ca_reissue_2 () = Note ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", 2u32, "2026-11-08T20:43Z", "microblog", "PROVEN by tibia 11-08 (IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS, user: \"there's gotta be a way to make it work on windows\"), on ganymede, since torn down: a stunnel front with an ECDSA P-256 chain (CA keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign; server SAN IP plus EKU serverAuth) forwarding with full verification to iggy :3000; Windows' own System32 curl.exe (Schannel) gets /ping = pong, HTTP 200; the wrong CA gives rc 60, so verification is real. EXTRA REQUIREMENT for the reissue: Schannel then fails rc 60 with CERT_TRUST_REVOCATION_STATUS_UNKNOWN, because a private CA has no CRL/OCSP. So the reissued certs carry crlDistributionPoints pointing at a served CRL (the chosen form), or every Windows client passes --ssl-no-revoke (chain and IP still verified). Updated DoD: Windows curl.exe gets 200 with the CA and WITHOUT --ssl-no-revoke. NO-RESTART BRIDGE if the serve window stays far off: route B, a small ECDSA front (stunnel) on a second port, proven to work; opening that port is a new public exposure and needs the user's yes first.")
inl note_of_iggy_ca_reissue_3 () = Note ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T05:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 PREPARED (nothing applied). iggy now runs on PLUTO (11-09 cutover), not europa, so the window is the planned pluto serve redeploy, bracketed by org3's soak. Generator: microblog scratchpad iggy-ca-reissue.sh <public-addr> <crl-url> [outdir], run ON pluto so ca.key never leaves the node. It makes:\n- an EC P-256 CA (basicConstraints critical CA:true pathlen 0; keyUsage critical keyCertSign,cRLSign);\n- a P-256 server cert (SAN IP, EKU serverAuth, crlDistributionPoints = the served CRL);\n- an empty CA-signed CRL (365 days, DER ca.crl).\nIt self-checks with openssl verify plus extension dumps and prints sha256 of ca.crt, server.crt and ca.crl.\nCRL HOSTING with no new exposure and no code change: timeline_serve's /media/ route serves any safe relative path under media_root (safe_rel refuses .., absolute paths and drives), so ca.crl goes to <media_root>/pki/ca.crl and the URL is http://<pluto-addr>:30087/media/pki/ca.crl, on the already-public serve port. Renewal: regenerate the CRL yearly (nextUpdate 365 d; put the date in the runbook).\nWindow steps:\n1. Generate on pluto.\n2. Update the iggy-tls secret with server.crt + server.key and roll out iggy (a brief iggy restart; the serve is untouched).\n3. Copy ca.crl to the media root.\n4. Hand the new public ca.crt to tibia (moon, ganymede) and the serve config.\n5. Verify the DoD: the box's System32 curl.exe with the CA and WITHOUT --ssl-no-revoke gets 200 on /ping, Python 3.13 strict verifies, and the wrong CA gives rc 60.\nCoordinate with tibia (validator) and org3 (soak bracket).")
inl note_of_iggy_ca_reissue_4 () = Note ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T10:45Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "NEXT STEP: in the next planned pluto window (org brackets it, tibia validates), run iggy-ca-reissue.sh on pluto, update the iggy-tls secret, roll out iggy, place ca.crl under the media root at pki/ca.crl, and hand the new ca.crt to clients. DoD: box System32 curl.exe gets 200 on /ping with the CA and without --ssl-no-revoke, and Python 3.13 strict verifies.")
inl note_of_iggy_ca_reissue_5 () = Note ("IGGY-CA-REISSUE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T11:34Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "Wait: when org brackets the next pluto redeploy (tibia validates)")
inl iggy_windows_clients () = Task ("IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS", "Windows clients talk to our iggy over verified TLS with Windows-native tooling (curl.exe, Invoke-RestMethod, .NET) and with a typed Spiral/Rust client, not only through Python: today every Windows TLS stack fails the Ed25519 chain (rc 35)", Story, P1, D3, 40u32, Blocked, "", "team:tibia,tibia,iggy,windows,tls,microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_iggy_windows_clients () = Planning ("IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_iggy_windows_clients_1 () = Note ("IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T20:41Z", "tibia", "User 11-08 17:0x: \"there's gotta be a way to make it work on windows, we need this on the backlog\". MEASURED 11-08 (memory iggy-http-bench-and-tls): our iggy CA AND server cert are Ed25519. Windows Schannel has no Ed25519 certificate support, so every Windows curl (System32 8.0.1, Git/scoop ucrt64 8.23) and PowerShell's web cmdlets (.NET on Windows also uses Schannel) fail the handshake with curl rc 35. The official curl.se Windows build (LibreSSL 4.4) fails too. CURL_SSL_BACKEND=openssl doesn't help: no MultiSSL build on the box. What works today on Windows: Python's ssl (OpenSSL 1.1.1t on moon, 3.0.16 on the box), so the bench client is Python.\nROUTES, cheapest-to-live first:\n(A) ROOT FIX: IGGY-CA-REISSUE (microblog): CA + server cert re-minted as ECDSA P-256 with keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign. Schannel, LibreSSL, .NET and Python >= 3.13 strict mode all accept it. Cost: an iggy restart under the live serve, plus a new ca.crt for every client. Deferred by microblog for that reason.\n(B) NO-RESTART BRIDGE: a TLS-terminating sidecar with its own ECDSA P-256 cert from a new CA, on a second hostPort (e.g. 3443), forwarding to iggy's existing listener. Candidates: stunnel, or a tiny Caddy/nginx/haproxy; the serve's k3s already runs traefik-less, so a plain sidecar container. Windows-native clients use :3443, everything else keeps :3000. Removable once (A) lands.\n(C) TYPED CLIENT, Spiral-first: a rig unit that speaks the iggy HTTP API (shapes verified live on 0.9.0, see the memory), compiled to Rust with rustls, which supports Ed25519. It works on Windows with today's cert and serves as the typed boundary IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE wants (one GADT message model). The official iggy Rust SDK (TCP/QUIC, rustls) is the alternative transport: check that its 0.9.0 crate matches our server.\nDoD: on moon (Windows), with full chain + hostname verification, never -k: (1) curl.exe and Invoke-RestMethod GET /ping and the bench flow succeed (via A or B); (2) the route C client (or the iggy Rust SDK) runs the bench flow (login, topic, produce, poll, delete) and prints the same one-line IWR/IRD/ILAT/ICLEAN; (3) an A/A against the Python client on moon, so the client language isn't the variable. NEXT STEP: ask microblog for a reissue window for (A); meanwhile prototype (B) as a stunnel sidecar on ganymede first (our own node, no live serve), pointed at europa's :3000, to prove an ECDSA front works for Windows curl before touching europa. TYPEFEATURES: route C: a GADT over iggy requests indexed by response type (Login -> token, CreateTopic -> topic, Send -> confirmations, Poll -> polled), the transport backend as a closed union (Http | Tcp), credentials as a phantom-sealed record never rendered to argv.")
inl note_of_iggy_windows_clients_2 () = Note ("IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS", 2u32, "2026-11-08T20:43Z", "tibia", "11-08 17:1x tibia: ROUTE (B) PROVEN on ganymede, then torn down. stunnel (apt stunnel4) on ganymede: [windows-front] accept :3443 with a fresh ECDSA P-256 chain (a 30-day test CA with keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign; server cert SAN IP:<ganymede-addr>, EKU serverAuth), then plaintext 127.0.0.1:3444, then [to-iggy] client mode -> <europa-addr>:3000 with verifyChain + CAfile = the iggy CA + checkIP. Result: Windows System32 curl.exe 8.0.1 (Schannel, no OpenSSL) GET https://<ganymede-addr>:3443/ping = pong, HTTP 200, 0.77 s, with --cacert front-ca.crt. NEGATIVE CONTROL: the same curl with the WRONG CA = rc 60, so verification is real. TWO TRAPS FOUND: (1) Europa Ubuntu images ship ufw ACTIVE with only 22/tcp, so a new listener times out (rc 28) until `ufw allow <port>`; (2) Schannel then fails rc 60 with CERT_TRUST_REVOCATION_STATUS_UNKNOWN, because a private CA has no CRL/OCSP. Fix: curl --ssl-no-revoke (chain + IP still verified), or give the reissued CA a CRL distribution point. Teardown verified: unit stopped, 0 listeners on 3443/3444, ufw 3443 rule removed; test CA files kept in ganymede /root/front (30-day test chain, no live use). IMPLICATIONS: (A) CA-REISSUE as ECDSA P-256 will work for Windows natively, once the revocation point is handled (CRL DP or --ssl-no-revoke). (B) needs a permanent home with its own ufw/hostPort and is removable after (A). STILL OPEN: Invoke-RestMethod/.NET with a private CA (needs the CA in the Windows store, or a custom validation callback); route (C) the typed Spiral/Rust (rustls) client. NEXT STEP: share the result with microblog for the IGGY-CA-REISSUE window; then a .NET probe through the same front recreated on demand.")
inl note_of_iggy_windows_clients_3 () = Note ("IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS", 3u32, "2026-11-08T21:41Z", "tibia", "11-08 17:5x tibia: PLAN AGREED with microblog for route (A). microblog reissues the iggy CA + server cert itself on pluto (iggy moved there 17:26; pluto is user-authorized k3s production), but only AFTER its serve is stable there: ~230 MB free and swap in use, so no iggy restart stacked on the serve's first 2 GB-peak start. Spec: ECDSA P-256; CA keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign; server SAN IP + EKU serverAuth; CRL distribution point -> a public-read CRL-only object in oort (microblog/pki/ca.crl, nextUpdate ~1 year; the rest of the bucket stays private). BLOCKER: microblog's reissue (IGGY-CA-REISSUE), gated on the pluto serve being stable. Resume when: microblog sends the new public ca.crt + endpoint. Then tibia runs 3 validations: (1) Windows System32 curl.exe /ping with --cacert and NO --ssl-no-revoke; (2) a wrong-CA negative control (rc 60); (3) Python 3.14 in default strict mode with NO verify-flag relaxation (proves keyUsage). Route (C), the typed Spiral/Rust rustls client, stays open and independent of (A).")
inl note_of_iggy_windows_clients_4 () = Note ("IGGY-WINDOWS-CLIENTS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T10:38Z", "tibia", "11-09 06:4x tibia groom: premise re-checked. Still Blocked, now on microblog's IGGY-CA-REISSUE, which is PREPARED (ECDSA P-256 CA, keyUsage critical, SAN IP, EKU serverAuth, CRL DP served from the existing /media/pki/ca.crl) and waits for a planned pluto window. Resume when: microblog reports the reissue live; then tibia validates that Windows curl.exe gets 200 with the CA and WITHOUT --ssl-no-revoke, and that Python 3.13 strict verifies.")
inl serve_to_pluto () = Task ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", "Move the text serve to pluto (SP/Brazil k3s) for BR latency, stood up fresh, validated, then cut over with europa as hot fallback; media served from oort public-read URLs fetched by the browser", Story, P1, D5, 90u32, Active, "", "team:microblog,serve,pluto,oort,k3s,sla", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_serve_to_pluto () = Planning ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_1 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 1u32, "2026-11-08T21:10Z", "microblog", "User decision 11-08 (relayed by org3; the media part confirmed directly by the user: oort public-read prefix). MEASURED on europa 11-08: serve RSS steady ~760 MB (beam anon 745 MB, file cache 13 MB), peak 2,030 MB at world load; world = joined.world.json 141 MB (+ a 169 MB .etf beside it); media = ~25 GB under /data/x (accounts, fonts), streamed from DISK per request, so offloading media saves ~0 RAM. The blocker on pluto is DISK (3.7 GB), and RAM (948 MB + 4.3 GB swap) is hit by the TEXT world. Plan: (1) MEDIA-TO-OORT: seed from europa in-DC, keys microblog/media/<sha256>.<ext>, public-read on that prefix only, Cache-Control public, max-age=31536000, immutable, correct Content-Type; the serve rewrites media URLs to oort. (2) SERVE-WORLD-RSS: shrink the text world to fit pluto. (3) Stand up fresh on pluto (rig k3s), with iggy reached on europa over TLS 8090 (no second iggy, since 512Mi Guaranteed cannot fit beside the serve on 948 MB); validate /timeline, media, iggy; cut over the route; europa stays the hot fallback until org3's SLA probe is green for a soak period. DoD: pluto serves /timeline with org3's probe p95 recorded, media loads from oort in the browser, europa fallback verified by a forced failover.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_2 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 2u32, "2026-11-08T21:13Z", "microblog", "CORRECTED by the user 11-08: (1) the 2 GB load peak is handled with SWAP + CONFIG on pluto, slow is acceptable, the goal is UPTIME; SERVE-WORLD-RSS is NOT a prerequisite. (2) europa hosts NO services from now on (saturation compute only): no europa hot fallback, and iggy moves off europa too. Plan details come from what the user already agreed with org3; ask org3, do not invent. Owner requirements for the pluto config: the serve's memory limit must let the 2 GB peak go to swap without a cgroup OOM kill; a long startupProbe budget (world load under swap is slow); liveness must NOT kill a slow-but-alive pod (a 5 s timeout on a swapping beam means a restart loop, which is the worst case for uptime), so relax it a lot or rely on readiness; iggy's placement and its 512Mi Guaranteed reservation are re-decided for pluto.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_3 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 3u32, "2026-11-08T21:16Z", "microblog", "Agreed plan (org3 11-08, from the user): pluto is the sole production host, no fallback; kubelet failSwapOn=false + NodeSwap swapBehavior=LimitedSwap with 4.3 GB swap; iggy on pluto at 256Mi. MANIFEST drafted (microblog scratchpad xsim-serve-pluto.yaml, client dry-run OK, sent to rig): Burstable 512Mi request / 640Mi limit (LimitedSwap gives Guaranteed pods no swap; Burstable gets ~request/node x swap, about 2.3 GB here), startup budget 60 min, readiness 30 s, liveness only after ~20 min of total silence, NodePort 30087, hostPath /data with frames (19 MB) + the world as a real file (141 MB). FACTS: the serve does not use iggy (only sim_publish.spi progress posting does). Media URLs come from timeline_page.spi:84 media_src, so the oort switch is a one-function change (TODO, microblog). CAUTION: /media/fonts serves X's proprietary Chirp fonts (timeline_page.spi:182-188); they must not go to the public oort prefix, so drop Chirp for Inter (already the substitute) and seed only accounts/*/media. NEXT STEP: media base URL + drop Chirp in timeline_page, then verify on pluto once rig's k3s is up.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_4 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 4u32, "2026-11-08T21:18Z", "microblog", "Code changes specified (sent to org, owner of timeline_page.spi, which moved 46A542536225 -> D2EA26F372D3 today, so no edit under them): (1) media base: timeline_page.spi:84 media_src is the single point for img/video src (87, 92); on pluto it emits <MEDIA_BASE_URL><sha256>.<ext> from a path->sha256 manifest loaded at serve start; with the env unset it stays /media/ (europa and tests unchanged). (2) drop Chirp: remove chirp_400..800 (182-188) from page_style (192) and Chirp from font-family (142); Inter (190) remains. Both need client + sim verifies (the sim imports client). org3 marks /media expected-404 in the SLA probe until (1) lands.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_5 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 5u32, "2026-11-08T21:20Z", "microblog", "Chirp DROPPED (microblog, unstaged, org-approved: the file was free): timeline_page.spi font-family starts at Inter; chirp_400..800 and their page_style refs removed; grep chirp in x = 0. The file hash returned EXACTLY to 46A542536225 (D2EA26F372D3 was 46A542536225 plus org's Chirp experiment), so sim verify job-1794136408919-x-verify-1108h-sim (GREEN on 46A542536225 + 02F9E1DC2DA0) already covers it; the client verify stays gated on 46A542536225. format --check reports a reformat that is pre-existing in 46A542536225; left alone to keep the verified hash. Disk cleanup of the Chirp woff2 files (/data/x/fonts and the /data/x-serve/media/fonts symlink on europa) is org's at cutover, after the Chirp-free page is live. NEXT: (1) the media base URL + path->sha256 manifest.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_6 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 6u32, "2026-11-08T21:41Z", "microblog", "DEPLOY STATE 11-08 17:5x: the user confirmed k3s on pluto directly (\"k3s is OK on pluto now\"); pluto = pluto, ssh rustdesk, k3s v1.37.1 (RustDesk + iggy + coredns), LimitedSwap live. Pluto now: 231 MB available, swap 351 MB used, disk 2.8 GB free, no /data yet. ARTIFACT: do NOT copy from the node's xqueue3 mirror (a 16:45 sync left its timeline_page at D2EA26F372D3, the Chirp version, so the mirror diverged from the verified build); build fresh on a Linux host from the current tree (timeline_page 46A542536225, timeline_serve 02F9E1DC2DA0), pinned pack62, under the runbook memory cap. NEXT STEPS: (1) sim build on europa (compute) -> build/dev/erlang; (2) stage /data/x-serve/frames/erlang (~19 MB) + /data/x-serve/joined.world.json as a real file (141 MB, from europa /data/x/joined) on pluto, relayed through the box; (3) apply xsim-serve-pluto.yaml; watch the first start and memory.swap.max (rig); (4) org3's probe on /timeline; (5) then IGGY-CA-REISSUE on pluto (tibia validates).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_7 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 7u32, "2026-11-08T21:43Z", "org3", "org3 11-08 17:4x (written by org2 for org3; org3 couldn't locate the backlog root) SLA SAMPLER STATE, bardo-handoff: tool = relay-lab/bench/sla-probe.sh; data = relay-lab/logs/sla/; restart from the relay-lab root = for i in $(seq 1 N); do bash bench/sla-probe.sh [serve_url]; sleep 20; done (anyone can restart it). State at 17:4x: rustdesk + iggy green on pluto's k3s (user-authorized production since 17:12). The serve waits on rig's serve skeleton; microblog deploys the Burstable serve next. Next step: point the sampler at the serve URL once it answers, and harden whichever layer strains first.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_8 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 8u32, "2026-11-08T21:57Z", "microblog", "HOLD 11-08 21:5x: (1) ganymede build attempt job-1794174925296-x-pluto-build refused correctly (the guard requires a beam newer than the job): build.ps1 failed in 2 s because the isolated mirror /home/remote/xpluto has no deps/The-Spiral-Language; fix = SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR pointing at the ganymede spiral checkout's deps. (2) BLOCKER: local timeline_serve.spi is now BD1C5BF309F5 (+263/-39 vs HEAD, mtime 08:04, older than when 02F9E1DC2DA0 was hashed, so likely a copy or restore that kept an old mtime), not the verified 02F9E1DC2DA0. Asked org whether BD1C is the intended serve (then it needs a sim verify) or where 02F9 lives. Nothing deployed to pluto.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_9 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 9u32, "2026-11-08T23:16Z", "microblog", "STOOD UP on pluto (soak, not cutover; production stays on europa). Artifact: frames-erlang.tgz sha 3c90c6d9e2165c28 (8 packages), built on ganymede from page 46A542536225 + serve BD1C5BF309F5 (org's confirmed serve), relayed byte-exact; the world is joined.world.json sha 27d1c0e556be5a1b, 146,368,363 bytes, relayed from europa (gzip through Git Bash: a long binary pipe through PowerShell truncated). First apply was Pending: Insufficient memory (allocatable ~885 Mi, 454 Mi already requested, the pod asked 528 Mi), so the serve request went 512Mi -> 400Mi (limit 640Mi; LimitedSwap share ~400/948 x 4.4 GB ~1.9 GB). Running 23:07; the first 8 min show RAM 150-310 MB + swap ~0.8-1.1 GB while the world loads; /timeline not yet up (startup budget 60 min). The pod-slice memory.swap.max reads 0 while swap.current is ~1.1 GB: the allowance is per container. Gate: full sim verify job-1794179080877-x-pluto-verify on ganymede (4 h budget; the first run passed 10/10 notebooks before its 60 min cap). Background watcher on /timeline. NEXT STEP: /timeline 200 -> ping org3 for the SLA probe; verify green -> cutover.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_10 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 10u32, "2026-11-08T23:24Z", "microblog", "UP on pluto 11-08 23:2x (soak): 2/2 Running, 0 restarts; /timeline 200 reached at ~16 min after start (one startup-probe timeout absorbed by the 60-min budget, no kill). Steady state: /timeline 200 in 42-61 ms on-node (23,849 B), 170-280 ms from the box over the public path; node 301 MB available, swap 1.3 GB used; RustDesk hbbs/hbbr 1/1 throughout. Handed to org3 for the SLA probe. Proof: Running 2/2, five on-node /timeline 200s, three public 200s. NEXT STEP: cutover after org3's soak is green AND the full sim verify job-1794179080877-x-pluto-verify passes; then media base URL (media 404 until then) and IGGY-CA-REISSUE.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_11 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 11u32, "2026-11-09T00:02Z", "microblog", "Media step 1 queued on europa: job-1794182550567-x-media-manifest (sha256 of every accounts/*/media file -> path<TAB>sha256 manifest in the europa stage dir, MemoryMax 512M, nice/ionice; Chirp fonts excluded by path). Upload to oort waits on rig's typed store unit; the serve's media base change follows the cutover.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_12 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 12u32, "2026-11-09T00:08Z", "microblog", "Media manifest DONE and verified (job-1794182550567-x-media-manifest, europa, exit 0, 138 s): 19,153 entries = all 19,153 media files, 35.09 GB by file size, 15,378 unique sha256. ~3,800 duplicates are stored once on disk (du 24G), so the fast run is cache plus SHA throughput, not a short set. The content-addressed upload to oort is 15,378 objects. Manifest stays in the europa stage dir (it lists account paths, so it is never pushed). NEXT STEP for media: upload via rig's typed store unit (public-read prefix, keys <sha256>.<ext>, immutable cache headers), then the serve's media base change after the cutover.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_13 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 13u32, "2026-11-09T00:57Z", "microblog", "Technique adopted (memory studied-engineering-techniques): the CUTOVER takes a verified-deploy CERTIFICATE that only the checks can mint: artifact sha (3c90c6d9e2165c28) + the green sim verify job id + org3's soak-green sampler window + the same source hashes (page 46A542536225, serve BD1C5BF309F5) rechecked at cutover time. No certificate, no route switch. TypeFeatures: a certificate record with a private constructor, minted only by the verify+soak reader and taken as the cutover step's argument.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_14 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 14u32, "2026-11-09T01:07Z", "microblog", "Proof: full sim verify GREEN on the deployed pair, job-1794179080877-x-pluto-verify (ganymede, exit 0, 123 min): page 46A542536225 + serve BD1C5BF309F5, build.ps1 exit 0, \"all 29 notebooks passed\" (0 failed). Cutover certificate, part 1 of 2 (artifact sha 3c90c6d9e2165c28 was built from these sources by job-1794175396322-x-pluto-build2). Part 2: org3's soak-green window. NEXT STEP: when org3 reports soak green, recheck the pluto pod (2/2, 0 restarts) and switch the route; then scale the europa serve to 0 (europa hosts no services) and ping org for the Chirp font removal.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_15 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 15u32, "2026-11-09T01:14Z", "microblog", "CUTOVER DONE 11-09 ~01:15Z. Certificate: sim verify green (job-1794179080877-x-pluto-verify, all 29 notebooks) + org3 SOAK GREEN 23:25:25Z..01:11:27Z (151 samples: /timeline on-node avail 99.3% p50 72 ms p95 1.3 s p99 2.6 s; ext p50 319 ms; one 6 s host-level swap/GC stall, self-healed; iggy and RustDesk 100%) + recheck at cutover (pluto pod 2/2, 0 restarts in 126 min, artifact sha 3c90c6d9e2165c28 and world sha 27d1c0e556be5a1b on disk, /timeline 200 86 ms). Switch: no route layer existed (no proxy or DNS on europa), so the europa serve was scaled to 0 (deployment 0/0, europa :30087 refused externally; europa gained ~760 MB for saturation); pluto :30087 200 in 0.18-0.21 s from the box. Rollback: kubectl -n xsim scale deploy xsim-serve --replicas=1 on europa. Org pinged for the Chirp font removal. REMAINING: media to oort (manifest ready, 15,378 objects, via rig's store unit) + the serve's media base change (media 404 until then), then IGGY-CA-REISSUE.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_16 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 16u32, "2026-11-09T01:16Z", "microblog", "Chirp fully retired (org 11-09): /data/x-serve/media/fonts symlink and /data/x/fonts (the 4 Chirp woff2) removed on europa after the serve went 0/0; nothing else touched (media root and accounts symlink intact). Chirp is now neither served (pluto page is Chirp-free) nor stored on europa, and the oort seed excludes fonts.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_17 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 17u32, "2026-11-09T01:25Z", "microblog", "org3 hardening 11-09: pluto vm.swappiness 10 -> 60 (persisted /etc/sysctl.d/99-pluto-uptime.conf), so the serve (RAM ~228 MB + swap ~758 MB) swaps cold pages instead of being OOM-biased. RustDesk is unaffected: Guaranteed pods get no swap under LimitedSwap. Folded into the manifest for the NEXT planned redeploy (the media base change, which restarts the pod anyway; a cold start is ~16 min of downtime, so no restart just for these): socat TCP-LISTEN ...,max-children=64 (done in the scratchpad manifest); a mid PriorityClass below rustdesk-critical (to add). Latency-tail lever = the BEAM resident set (SERVE-WORLD-RSS, P3), not RAM.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_18 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 18u32, "2026-11-09T04:22Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "org3 11-09 SLA finding: the >6 s /timeline stalls (cluster 01:17-01:25Z) are BEAM major GCs over a swap-backed heap (~228 MB RAM + ~758 MB swap), not node pressure or restarts (iggy 0.6 ms, rustdesk 12 ms throughout, 0 restarts in 5 h). Lever analysis: ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER already defaults to 65535, so raising it barely helps; the copying major GC must touch every live word of the process heap that holds the world, which pages it back in. Real lever for the next redeploy: move the read-mostly world out of process heaps into ETS (read_concurrency) or persistent_term, which process GC never scans, and keep per-request heaps small (spawn per request, or hibernate idle holders). Measure with org3's running soak: p99 /timeline and stall count before and after. Optional tail-latency work, not fix-now (98.7% over a 2.1 h soak is the accepted slow-but-up tradeoff).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_19 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 19u32, "2026-11-09T04:45Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 GC-stall fix DRAFTED in x (unstaged, not yet checked or verified): sim_serve.spi world_of now pins the parsed world JSON with persistent_term (pinned_world: put under key xsim_world, erlang:garbage_collect, get), using lib erlang_term::apply, so no new FFI. Why it works: the serve is ONE process (served/handled loop) holding api_world, and its indexes (by_handle, by_id, by_post) and lazily built feeds are dict and list skeletons whose values are subterms of raw. With raw in the literal area, process GC copies only those skeletons and never pages the world in from swap. Load peak: the heap copy of the parsed JSON dies at the explicit GC right after put, so the transient is about one extra world copy before the indexes are built, comparable to today's 2 GB peak (watch it on the redeploy; the Burstable swap envelope is about 2.9 GB). Writes (with_created, counted, dropped) build new heap nodes that share literal subterms, which is safe. Output is unchanged by construction. Proof plan: sim verify (all notebooks) plus a europa-free soak on pluto bracketed by org3 (before: p99 3.1 s, >6 s stalls clustered; after: expect no >6 s stalls). Rides the redeploy with media-to-oort, the PriorityClass and socat max-children.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_20 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 20u32, "2026-11-09T04:54Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 pinned_world --check GREEN: job-1794199756663-sim-serve-check (moon, mirror cellspt1, x digest 498F4C08, 61 s, exit 0). It checked the whole apps/sim/spi package (parse + inference only; partial evaluation, codegen and tests not run). The sim verify remains the proof.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_21 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 21u32, "2026-11-09T11:25Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 Chirp replacement font: org's sans.ttf is ready (69 glyphs: Latin both cases, 0-9, 7 punctuation; OS/2 v4 + name tables; lib Cells gate 54/54; source alphabet lib/font_glyph.spi + apps/font-emit). Decisions (microblog): org emits sans.woff2 from the emitter, and TTF is the fallback meanwhile. org delivers both with a sha256. Integration: the files go to the serve media root as fonts/sans.woff2 (the existing /media/ route, no new port). timeline_page page_style gets @font-face { font-family: \"XSans\"; src: url(/media/fonts/sans.woff2) format(\"woff2\"), url(/media/fonts/sans.ttf) format(\"truetype\") }, with XSans first in font-family ahead of Inter. The CSS alias is independent of the font's placeholder internal name (the public name is the user's call). Lands after the warm verify arm; rides the next pluto redeploy with pinned_world, the PriorityClass and socat max-children; org brackets it.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_22 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 22u32, "2026-11-09T11:30Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 font DELIVERED and verified: europa /home/remote/stage/fonts (org; woff2 by Google's reference woff2_compress, out of the x pipeline). Fetched to the microblog scratchpad fonts/: sans.woff2 2076 B sha256 8c0a0e6960edac3dfb61b426d894ef03ff0203e8c2e11218061e678f383b25bb and sans.ttf 5592 B sha256 875cca71564b26698933fed8dca55e64045eea88058a3733be1d57f1c0969a8d; both match org's .sha256 files. At redeploy: copy both into the serve media root under fonts/, recheck the hashes on pluto, add the XSans @font-face to timeline_page. Fonts are generated glyph art, not personal data, so they are fine to serve publicly.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_23 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 23u32, "2026-11-09T11:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "font v2 supersedes v1 (org: double-story lowercase a; otherwise identical). Re-fetched to scratchpad fonts/ and verified: sans.woff2 2096 B sha256 53c55755a8f3451d4647d70715d7b36ca7186f397bc44e141901bd32daaa1ad7, sans.ttf 5620 B sha256 3462d72b2eac3ee63bc51fffe0d9794912b7c06288d1b3cf4518b755e9f22101. Pin THESE at the redeploy; the v1 hashes in note 22 are retired.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_24 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 24u32, "2026-11-09T12:54Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 08:5x microblog: XSans font CSS DRAFTED in x (unstaged, not yet --checked): timeline_page.spi gains font_face () = @font-face{font-family:'XSans';src:url(/media/fonts/sans.woff2) format('woff2'),url(/media/fonts/sans.ttf) format('truetype');font-display:swap}, placed right after the Inter @import (an @import must stay first in a stylesheet); body_css font-family now leads with 'XSans' ahead of 'Inter', so any glyph outside XSans's 69 falls back to Inter per character. page_style's 134-char line became style_text () (one ++# per line), so the file is back to 0 lines over 120. No e2e fixture holds page CSS (grep of apps/client/e2e/*.json for font-family and style finds none), so the client expectations stay unchanged and only the client hash moves. Safe for the running r2 verify: the warm arm reuses the frozen xqueue1 mirror, not C:\\home\\git\\x. Fonts at redeploy are the v2 pair from org (sans.woff2 sha256 53c55755...), superseding the v1 hashes in the 07:30 note. Also removed a stale ignored apps/client/e2e/__pycache__ (a 10-26 .pyc of the retired Python social_stub). next: --check the client on a node with a free slot, then ride the redeploy.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_25 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 25u32, "2026-11-09T16:53Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 12:5x microblog: SIM VERIFY STARTED on moon in the slot my stopped r2-warm freed (org2 yes; compiler may stop it if TRAIN42e ends and its window wants moon): job-1794243181261-x-verify-sim3, x-verify-sim.ps1 -Arm accept -TimeoutScale 3 on cellsmd1, re-synced from the box at 12:5x (spiral bf5cc30a fingerprint 6753E11050908E1E, x 9bb9749d fingerprint ED6D99B225B533DF; both match the box tree). It carries the unstaged pinned_world GC fix, and its Cells carries the unstaged memo-on, Manifest.cached and explicit-target fixes (hashes in summary inputs). On green: the regenerated e2e world fixtures (sim-*.world.json etc.) are copied back to the box x tree after a diff review; that heals x CI's fixture drift. pinned_world gets its proof line here, then ORG is pinged that the redeploy set (pinned_world + XSans font + PriorityClass + socat max-children) is ready.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_26 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 26u32, "2026-11-09T19:04Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 15:1x microblog: REDEPLOY REQUEST from org (org3 soak: stall rate rose to 3/30 samples, avail ~90%, serve-GC-specific: serve-ext and serve-local both 6 s, iggy and rustdesk fine). This is what pinned_world fixes. FACT: pluto 948 MB RAM / 270 MB available / 1.4 GB swap used; xsim-serve strategy=Recreate, 1 replica, so no surge pod fits next to RustDesk and the redeploy is stop + cold start (~16 min down). GATES: (1) sim verify job-1794243181261 green (running; past its stress step); (2) a fresh Linux build from the verified sources; (3) stage with the v2 fonts, PriorityClass, socat max-children=64. Asked org to pick (a) a ~16 min planned window bracketed by its soak or (b) a europa bridge (breaks europa-no-services, needs org's yes). Nothing on pluto changed.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_27 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 27u32, "2026-11-09T19:08Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09 DECISION (answering microblog's window request; also sent direct): METHOD = option (a), the planned ~16min Recreate outage. DECLINED option (b) scaling europa to bridge - 'europa hosts no services' is a user-agreed policy and breaking it (even 20min) is not warranted to fix a DEGRADED-but-up serve (org3: uptime held, accepted SLA-vs-uptime tradeoff). URGENCY LOW: intermittent slowness, not downtime, so do NOT rush. Finish all 3 guards first (sim verify green, FRESH Linux build from verified sources per never-copy-a-mirror, staged with XSans v2 + PriorityClass + socat max-children=64). TIMING: once guards green, pick the quietest window; if staged + quiet before ~20:00 local, ping org and I bracket before/after p99 + stall-count on org3's pinned soak baseline; if guards not green by then, DEFER past my autonomous window (ends 21:00) and hand bracketing to org3 rather than rush unbracketed. Nothing on pluto changes until guard (1) green + microblog pings.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_28 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 28u32, "2026-11-09T19:11Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 15:2x microblog: ORG DECIDED: option (a), a planned ~16 min Recreate window at LOW urgency; NO europa bridge (europa-no-services is user policy). All 3 guards first. If the artifact is staged and a quiet window lands before ~20:00 local, ping org to bracket p99 + stall count; otherwise defer past org's window and hand the before/after to org3 (soak baseline pinned). GATE 2 STARTED: fresh build job-1794251474256-x-pluto-build-1109 on ganymede in a dated copy /home/remote/xpluto-1109 (xpluto untouched) overlaid with box x + spiral lib/scripts. The 127 authored apps/sim+client sources equal the verified sim snapshot (cellsmd1) byte for byte, checked on box, moon and ganymede. 2 stale files (lib physics.spi, client tlds.spi) moved to xpluto-1109-stale. Acceptance: the generated sim/frames/src gleam hashes (frames-src.sha256) must equal moon's verified-run output, so the artifact is the tested code.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_29 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 29u32, "2026-11-09T19:17Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 15:3x microblog: GATE 2 GREEN. job-1794251474256-x-pluto-build-1109 (ganymede, exit 0, ~3 min): page A2B5E6C274F7, serve FE1F0B1C7DD9, sim_serve 877325805CC0 (carries pinned_world); xsim_frames.beam rebuilt by the job; artifact /home/remote/stage/pluto-serve-1109/frames-erlang.tgz 2,756,103 B sha 7D0FD0C6F9111070. EQUIVALENCE: all 42 generated sim/frames/src gleam files are byte-identical to the moon cellsmd1 copy that the running sim verify regenerated at 15:07 local, so the artifact is the code under proof. GATE 3 PREPARED, not run (org: nothing on pluto before gate 1): staging script relays the tgz byte-exact through the box into /data/x-serve/frames-1109 (dated; frames/ kept for rollback) and the v2 fonts into /data/x-serve/media/fonts (the serve's media_root = world dir + /media), every sha rechecked on pluto; manifest xsim-serve-pluto-1109.yaml (sha 12e061956d6075c3): PriorityClass xsim-serve-standard value 100000 preemptionPolicy Never (below rustdesk-critical 1000000; can never evict iggy), socat max-children=64, frames-1109 path, serve port renamed so the duplicate-name warning is gone; kubectl apply --dry-run=server clean on pluto. Rollback = re-apply the 11-08 manifest (frames/ path), also a ~16 min Recreate.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_30 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 30u32, "2026-11-09T21:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 17:1x microblog: GATE 1 NOT GREEN (pending). Sim verify job-1794243181261 (moon) hit its 4 h wall-clock cap (exit 124, 12:53-16:53) INSIDE the final 'sim build' step's notebook phase (exsss and sim_events passed, final_state was running; ~27 notebooks left). What it did prove: 'x verify / sim accept exit 0', so the full sim run plus both stress steps passed with pinned_world in the serve, and 11 fixtures were accepted (e2e sim-small/stress/lost/gap world+expected, thread-oauth1, prelude events/final). FIXTURE REVIEW (box vs moon, 7 changed e2e files, fetched to scratch, NOT yet copied to the box): every change follows the 11-08 formatter respell of the sim's own posted source (nested ifs split onto ?> lines, reference_as split into reposted_as), so 145 -> 147 posts in stress. Copy them only with gate 1 green. PER ORG'S RULE (not green by ~20:00): the redeploy DEFERS past org's window, and the before/after bracketing goes to org3 (soak baseline pinned). REMAINING GATE 1: verify.ps1 -Part sim WITHOUT -Accept on the same cellsmd1 mirror (unchanged since the run, so the pluto artifact equivalence still holds), 12 h cap, chained before after-sim in one staged script (night-chain.ps1) that a box poller submits when moon is free (fiscal g6a-b6-gate and compiler moon-pack78-pair are on moon now; deadline 20:50). Gates 2 and 3 stay ready (artifact 7D0FD0C6F9111070 staged on ganymede, manifest dry-run clean). Nothing on pluto changed.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_31 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 31u32, "2026-11-09T21:30Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 17:3x microblog: GATE 1 MOVED TO EUROPA (idle, one-off compute; moon has 3 live jobs from other lanes). job-1794259774071-x-gate1-europa: verify.ps1 -Part sim WITHOUT -Accept, SPIRAL_CELLS_TIMEOUT_SCALE=3, MemoryMax 2560M, 7 h cap, in /home/remote/xgate1 = ganymede's xpluto-1109 relayed byte-exact (deps = the shared europa symlink) plus moon's 11 accepted fixtures. PRE-CHECKS: 124 authored x sources identical to the verified moon set; the 2 spot fixtures match moon (stress world f8527b4a8818c0d1, prelude final d98bc75f6584e901). The run also hashes the regenerated sim/frames/src gleam, so the artifact equivalence (42 files vs moon) is checked again on its output. The runner Cells is the 11-08 copy that ran the green 11-08 Linux verify. The moon night chain is now after-sim only (no duplicate gate-1 run).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_32 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 32u32, "2026-11-09T22:54Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 18:5x microblog: ALL 3 GATES GREEN, apply waits on org's bracketing. GATE 1: europa job-1794260188582-x-gate1-europa3, verify.ps1 -Part sim (no accept) exit 0, 29/29 sim notebooks passed (incl. sim_serve = pinned_world, timeline_serve), on the exact artifact sources (page A2B5E6C274F7, serve FE1F0B1C7DD9, sim_serve 877325805CC0) with moon's 11 accepted fixtures; together with moon's 'sim accept exit 0' (full sim run + both stress steps) this is the full sim verify. The 42 regenerated frames gleam files are byte-identical to moon's verified run, so the artifact is the proven code. Two false starts on europa were relay snags (gleam build caches carrying ganymede's absolute paths, moved to xgate1-aside; verify -Out needs robocopy, dropped). GATE 3 STAGED on pluto (additive, live pod untouched, 23 h, 0 restarts, /timeline 200 0.14 s): /data/x-serve/frames-1109 (8 packages from frames-erlang tgz sha 7d0fd0c6f9111070, rechecked on pluto; a copy is kept as frames-erlang-1109.tgz) and /data/x-serve/media/fonts/sans.{woff2,ttf} (v2 shas rechecked; /media/fonts/sans.woff2 already serves 200, 2096 B). The old frames/ stays for rollback. FIXTURES: the 11 accepted files are copied into the box x tree (unstaged; heals x CI's fixture drift once pushed). APPLY = kubectl apply of xsim-serve-pluto-1109.yaml (sha 12e061956d6075c3, server dry-run clean): Recreate, ~16 min down. Waiting for org to confirm its before-baseline (pinged 18:5x).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_33 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 33u32, "2026-11-09T22:55Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 19:0x microblog: USER DECISION NEEDED, the only thing left. Org (rightly) declines to be the trigger: a ~16 min planned outage of user-authorized production needs the user's explicit go, and peer messages are never user approval, so microblog won't apply it either (pluto: never stop without the user). DECISION FOR THE USER: apply the pinned_world redeploy to pluto. WHAT: kubectl apply of xsim-serve-pluto-1109.yaml (Recreate, frames-1109, PriorityClass xsim-serve-standard 100000 / preemptionPolicy Never, socat max-children=64, XSans v2 fonts). COST: ~16 min of /timeline downtime (cold start of the world). GAIN: org3's soak shows serve-GC stalls rising (3/30 samples at 6 s, availability ~90% this evening vs ~99%); pinned_world moves the world out of the process heap so major GCs stop scanning it. EVIDENCE: all 3 gates green (n32). ROLLBACK: re-apply the 11-08 manifest (frames/ kept), also ~16 min. When the user says go: org or org3 captures the before-baseline, microblog applies in a quiet window, org/org3 capture the after-bracket (p99 + stall count).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_34 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 34u32, "2026-11-10T02:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 02:0xZ USER GO given in org2's session (user: 'run the deploy'); org2 applied per n32/n33. Pre-flight: manifest sha 12e061956d6075c3 matched on the box and on pluto; frames-1109/erlang 8 packages present; server dry-run clean (priorityclass create, deployment configured, ns/service unchanged); live pod xsim-serve-6d8c675c86-gqgwn 26h 0 restarts. BEFORE-BASELINE (org2, 10 x /timeline from pluto localhost:30087): 6 x 200 at 0.08-0.13 s, 1 x 200 at 11.66 s, 3 x timeout at 15 s = the stall pattern. APPLIED 02:01:36Z (kubectl apply -f xsim-serve-pluto-1109.yaml); Recreate in progress, watcher on the box. Rollback if needed: re-apply xsim-serve-pluto.yaml (11-08, frames/ kept).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_35 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 35u32, "2026-11-10T02:07Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 02:0xZ CUTOVER LIVE: new pod xsim-serve-589b885d97-tdrt6 2/2 Running at 02:06:35Z (~5 min after apply, well under the 16 min budget), 0 restarts, no OOM/kill events; startup budget is 360 x 10 s = 60 min, never at risk. Fonts /media/fonts/sans.woff2 200 2096 B. AFTER-READINGS (pluto localhost:30087/timeline): 02:06:53Z 10 req = 1 timeout at 15 s (first request right after ready), 9 x 200 typically 0.04 s (baseline typical 0.08-0.13 s), one 1.8 s; 02:07:25Z 15 req = 15 x 200, 14 at 0.04-0.63 s, ONE at 8.4 s. Memory available 139 -> 201 MB (948 total; was 261 before). VERDICT SO FAR: the steady-state latency halved and there were no timeouts in the second sample, but stalls are reduced, NOT gone (1/15 at 8.4 s vs the baseline's 4/10 over 11 s). org3's soak after-bracket over a longer window is the real comparison; rollback stays the 11-08 manifest if the soak shows no gain.")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_36 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 36u32, "2026-11-10T02:08Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 02:0xZ microblog AFTER-CHECK of org2's cutover (applied 02:01:36Z on the user's direct 'run the deploy' to org2): new pod xsim-serve-589b885d97 2/2, 0 restarts; first /timeline 200 at ~02:06Z, under 5 min (the 11-08 cold start was ~16 min). Live spec as staged: priorityClassName xsim-serve-standard, socat max-children=64, frames-1109. RustDesk 2/2 untouched (28 h). XSans present in the page, /media/fonts/sans.woff2 200 2096 B. AFTER-SAMPLE at +6 min, 10 x /timeline with 15 s cap: 10/10 200; 7 fast (0.04-0.11 s), 3 slow (3.4 / 8.4 / 8.5 s), 0 timeouts. org2's before-baseline: 6 fast, 1 at 11.7 s, 3 timeouts. Early and small: the world may still be paging in after the cold start, so org3's soak over hours (p99 + stall count vs the pinned baseline) is the real verdict. Memory 646 MB used, 1.28 GB swap. Rollback stays available (11-08 manifest, frames/ kept).")
inl note_of_serve_to_pluto_37 () = Note ("SERVE-TO-PLUTO", 37u32, "2026-11-10T03:15Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 23:15 local microblog WATCH (+72 min after the cutover; pod 2/2, 0 restarts, RustDesk untouched): 10 x /timeline (15 s cap): 10/10 200; 8 fast (0.04-0.06 s), 1 at 3.6 s, 1 at 12.5 s. Memory 785 MB used, swap 1.17 GB. So stalls are FEWER than org2's before-baseline (3 timeouts + 1 at 11.7 s in 10) but NOT gone. Not conclusive at n=10: org3's soak p99 and stall count over hours decide. If the soak still shows >= 6 s stalls, the next lever is the per-request heap (spawn per request, or hibernate idle holders) from the 11-09 04:22Z analysis, since the world now sits in persistent_term. NEXT STEP: read org3's soak bracket in the window and compare.")
inl serve_world_rss () = Task ("SERVE-WORLD-RSS", "Shrink the serve's text-world RAM so it fits pluto (948 MB RAM): today steady ~760 MB, peak 2,030 MB at load, from a 141 MB JSON world", Story, P3, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:microblog,serve,beam,memory,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_serve_world_rss () = Planning ("SERVE-WORLD-RSS", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_serve_world_rss_1 () = Note ("SERVE-WORLD-RSS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T21:10Z", "microblog", "Levers, each measured before and after with peak and steady RSS: (a) load the binary .etf (binary_to_term) instead of parsing JSON, which should cut the load peak (check which file cli_serve reads today); (b) keep post bodies off the process heap: ETS with compressed, or an index (ids, timestamps, feed offsets) in RAM with bodies read from an on-disk binary per page, targeting <= 300 MB steady; (c) GC tuning (fullsweep_after, a heap cap only after (b), since the runbook forbids capping today's heap). Typed: the world index and page reads as model-unit types, not string wires. DoD: steady <= 300 MB and peak <= 600 MB on the same world, /timeline output byte-identical to today.")
inl note_of_serve_world_rss_2 () = Note ("SERVE-WORLD-RSS", 2u32, "2026-11-08T21:13Z", "microblog", "Deprioritized P1 -> P3 (user 11-08): uptime on pluto is reached with swap + config, slow is fine; this item is a later efficiency gain, not a gate for SERVE-TO-PLUTO.")
inl note_of_serve_world_rss_3 () = Note ("SERVE-WORLD-RSS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:06Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 11:0x microblog, lever (a) checked by reading code: ALREADY BUILT. sim_serve.spi json_file (95-115): etf_of path = path.etf; when the .etf is newer than the JSON (modified_at compare), etf_read returns binary_to_term of it; otherwise the JSON is decoded once (erlang_term::json_decoded of read_all_text) and written back as term_to_binary (etf_written). Test a_newer_etf_answers_for_its_json (1033) pins the freshness rule. So after the first start the serve never parses the 141 MB JSON, and the measured 2,030 MB peak is NOT JSON parsing on warm starts (on a cold start without .etf it is). Related, unstaged: pinned_world (175) puts the decoded world into persistent_term, so process GC stops copying it (the stall fix in SERVE-TO-PLUTO); its effect on steady RSS is to be measured on the redeploy. Remaining levers: (b) bodies off-heap (ETS compressed, or an index in RAM with page reads from disk), (c) GC flags. next: on the redeploy (SERVE-TO-PLUTO), record steady and peak RSS with pinned_world as the new baseline before starting (b). typefeatures: world index record (ids, timestamps, feed offsets) as a model-unit type.")
inl infra_names_out_of_repos () = Task ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", "Repos never name infra: no provider, host nickname, IP, region, bucket or personal path in anything pushed; code speaks roles (node, worker, object-store) that local config maps to machines", Story, P1, D3, 80u32, Active, "RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL,TIBIA-RESULT-ROWS-RELPATHS,X-NODE-RUN-ROLE", "team:org,standards,privacy,heal,repos", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_infra_names_out_of_repos () = Planning ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_1 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 1u32, "2026-11-08T22:25Z", "org2", "USER 11-08 18:1x: 'scripts and code have reference to words like europa, the gh repos shouldn't know about these details, gotta heal similar stuff'. CENSUS 11-08 (org2, our 19 repos, .gitignore respected; false positives europa.eu links and SVG digits removed). TRACKED leaks: i574n.github docs/backlog agile.spi (932) + archive/done-notes.spi (736); apps/graphs/out/backlog.{svg,mmd,graphml} (derived from backlog titles); scripts/node-utilization-monitor.ps1 (20); tibia/results 18 rows with absolute personal log paths; x/scripts/node-run.ps1 (hard-coded laptop machine key). UNTRACKED (heal before first push): rig infra/nodebench, infra/a/iggy-client, infra/k3s-iggy, scripts/node-kit-switch.ps1 (default alias laptop), src fixtures in rig_job_placement / rig_job_dispatch / rig_ci_verdict / rig_net_topology / rig_coordinator_placement. PATTERN (already in the repo): tracked code names roles; ~/.config/remote-machines.json (has a node key) and the gitignored scripts/node-env.ps1 map roles to real hosts; memory holds the human context. DoD: a census over every org repo finds 0 infra tokens in pushable files (deny-list read from LOCAL config, never stored in a repo), each lane's slice is Done, and the user has decided the backlog's home. Next step: owners heal their slices (children); the user decides the backlog question. TypeFeatures: Role as a closed union (Node | Worker | ObjectStore | ProductionHost) resolved through a local map; a test that a role resolves and an unknown name is refused.")
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_2 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 2u32, "2026-11-08T22:25Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 18:2x ORG SLICE (scripts) HEALED, unstaged. node-utilization-monitor.ps1 now speaks only roles: node and worker variables; alarms WORKER-TMP/DISK/OOM/MEM instead of the provider-named ones; machine sizes and regions dropped from messages; thresholds became params; comments removed. The timeseries header became node_cpu,node_free_mb,worker_cpu and is MIGRATED IN PLACE when the shape matches (the old code wiped history on a header change); proof: 176 rows -> 177, header rewritten. idle-with-ready-alarm.ps1 calls Invoke-NodeProbeWin 'node'; the gitignored node-env.ps1 accepts 'node' as the role for the route chain. Proof: 0 parse errors on all three; a live run exit 1 = a real WASTE alarm (box 100%, node idle). Remaining org slice: apps/graphs/out/backlog.* follows the backlog decision. Memory: repos-never-name-infra.")
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_3 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 3u32, "2026-11-08T22:42Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 18:4x USER REFINEMENT: 'these things on the backlog aren't a big of a deal. also you can keep things like the planet aliases to ease understanding things'. So: (1) the planet aliases (moon, europa, ganymede, pluto, oort, jupiter, ...) are ALLOWED and preferred in code and notes; (2) NO mass scrub of the backlog (a respell was measured on copies only, about 3,600 hits, then dropped; the live backlog is untouched). What stays out of PUSHED code, scripts, fixtures and result rows: the provider name, IPs, real hostnames, regions, the bucket name, personal paths, work-network names and usernames. The deny-list lives locally at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config\\infra-aliases.tsv (replacements go to planet aliases or placeholders), never in a repo. DoD revised: the children are Done, plus a census of pushable code (not the backlog) that finds 0 deny-list tokens. Next step: the children (rig, tibia, microblog).")
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_4 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 4u32, "2026-11-08T22:57Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 18:5x BACKLOG CLEANUP DONE, GENTLY (user: 'do the cleanup, just not as abrupt'). Four staged passes, each one: preview + sampled word-diff, then apply under kit's agile.spi.lock (held 2.8-9.8 s), originals archived first under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\backlog-infra-scrub-<stamp>-<stage>, then verify (kit reads 1941 items before and after, lint unchanged). Stage 1 identity: 523 replacements (personal paths -> %USERPROFILE%, IPs -> <host-addr> placeholders, real hostnames -> planet aliases, work-network names -> work-hub/work-host, usernames -> <user>, bucket/endpoint/key names). Stage 2 provider: about 2,180 (host uses -> europa; provider uses (account/credit/plan/...) -> cloud-provider; hardware nouns (VM/instance/location/GPU) and 'a ...' -> cloud; object storage -> oort). Stage 3: the sao host alias -> pluto (Sao Paulo untouched), 'europa sjc' collapsed; datacenter code lists left as is (public catalog codes). Stage 4: kit agile rename VULTR-DISK-HEAL -> EUROPA-DISK-HEAL, KIT-VULTR-LAUNCH-MEM-GATE -> KIT-EUROPA-LAUNCH-MEM-GATE, XDUMPS-SJC-K3S-DEPLOY -> XDUMPS-EUROPA-K3S-DEPLOY (deps intact); alarm names in notes VULTR-OOM/DISK/MEM/TMP -> WORKER-* to match the healed monitor. KEPT on purpose: planet aliases; 23 residuals that are names of real artifacts (a memory file, job ids, a backup file name, the node-env function Test-VultrScopeCap, the binding machine_of_des_073), which change only when the artifact is renamed. apps/graphs/out regenerates from the backlog on its next run. Progress 25 -> 60.")
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_5 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 5u32, "2026-11-09T00:26Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 20:3x (unrelated to infra names; recorded here only because no item owns this yet; see the note on REGEX-SKELETON): fixed the pack63c reformat's cell-budget overage in org-owned regex (+5) and html (+2).")
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_6 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 6u32, "2026-11-09T07:35Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 04:0x TRACKED-CODE SWEEP (git grep, tracked files only, word rows with -w, over i574n.github spiral regex html kit fiscal x tibia; backlog + generated graphs excluded): 9 hits left in code. FIXED: i574n.github docs/agents/agent-sync.md named moon's real hostname -> moon (unstaged). ROUTED to compiler: spiral apps/compiler/scripts/install-pack.ps1 (tracked) names the real bucket (lines 40-41) and a provider-named secrets file (line 46); suggested env-var heal. KEPT: fiscal 'Sao Paulo' x4 is a city in NF-e fixtures, not infra (the word row over-matches; tighten it to the host alias form). Kit, regex, html, x, tibia: 0. BACKLOG REGROWTH since the 11-08 scrub: about 220 hits in state/agile.spi (provider word 78, others 2-40; mostly new notes written by lanes, org3 included). Low priority per the user; next gentle pass = the same staged preview/apply as 11-08. Also apps/graphs/out (generated from the backlog) carries the old names until regenerated. Next step: compiler's install-pack heal, then the deny row tightening, then a staged backlog re-pass.")
inl note_of_infra_names_out_of_repos_7 () = Note ("INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS", 7u32, "2026-11-09T07:46Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 04:3x spiral HEALED by compiler (unstaged): install-pack.ps1 store keys are bucket-free (compiler/base/v1/..., compiler/pack/v1/...); the bucket comes only from $env:OORT_BUCKET (Get-OortPath throws when unset), the secrets file from $env:OORT_ENV_FILE ?? ~/.secrets/oort-s3.env; real values live in box user env only; verified by minting pack67 linux-x64 URLs (33) from local config. git grep over spiral tracked files: 0 provider/bucket hits. Tracked-code state now: spiral 0, i574n.github 0 (agent-sync.md fixed), kit/regex/html/x/tibia 0, fiscal only the Sao Paulo fixture city (kept). Left: backlog regrowth (low priority, staged re-pass) + apps/graphs/out regeneration.")
