inl note_of_rig_infra_names_heal_1 () = Note ("RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-08T22:25Z", "org2", "Child of INFRA-NAMES-OUT-OF-REPOS (user 11-08). Files (all untracked, so heal before the first push): infra/nodebench/README.md, rate.ps1, src/main.rs (relay-lab and node names); infra/a/iggy-client/review-box-follow.ps1 + node-*.ps1 (ssh laptop, laptop-last-ip.txt); infra/k3s-iggy/iggy.yaml, node-wsl.ps1, verify.ps1; scripts/node-kit-switch.ps1 (default -Alias laptop); src/rig_job_placement/placement.spi and rig_job_dispatch/dispatch.spi fixtures (laptop, laptop-ts); rig_ci_verdict/verdict.spi (a fixture fn named laptop); rig_net_topology/topology.spi; rig_coordinator_placement/placement.spi. Fixtures use neutral names (node-a, worker-1); scripts take the role (node) and resolve it via ~/.config/remote-machines.json. DoD: 0 infra tokens in rig's pushable files, plus a census verb or check that reads its deny-list from LOCAL config (never a repo file; the list itself is infra detail) and runs in the style hook as a ratchet. Next step: the fixture renames + node-kit-switch default, then the census check. TypeFeatures: the census row as a closed union of token classes (Provider | Host | Address | Region | Bucket | PersonalPath).")
inl note_of_rig_infra_names_heal_2 () = Note ("RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-08T22:42Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 18:4x USER REFINEMENT: planet aliases are FINE, so fixtures may say moon / europa / ganymede instead of laptop / laptop-ts; only raw identity must go (the provider name europa, IPs, real hostnames such as DESKTOP-... and europa, regions, the bucket, personal paths). The census deny-list is %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config\\infra-aliases.tsv (literal|word, token, replacement); read it from there, never copy it into the repo. The backlog is out of scope.")
inl note_of_rig_infra_names_heal_3 () = Note ("RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-11-08T22:42Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 18:5x rig: FILES HEALED (all untracked, before the first push): src fixtures to neutral names (rig_ci_verdict local stub laptop to stub_host; rig_coordinator_placement europa sample to worker-1; rig_job_dispatch laptop-ts and C:/home/bin to node-a and C:/opt/bin; rig_job_placement laptop to node-a, its placement= expectation in step); infra/a/iggy-client/review-box-follow.ps1 takes -Machine node (a ROLE) and resolves the ssh alias and address from ~/.config/remote-machines.json like node-proof (parse 0); scripts/node-kit-switch.ps1 (the completed eoie-to-kit migration, on the KIT-RENAME history list) archived out of the repo to LOCALAPPDATA\\kit\\archive\\completed-scripts-20261108; infra/nodebench README, rate.ps1 and src/main.rs reworded to roles (fleet coordinator, the smallest 1 GB node, the largest 28-core node, the object store, object-store credentials; no provider, region, bucket, store nickname or credentials path). proof: git grep --untracked over the whole rig repo minus history (state/*.spi, FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md, evidence) for providers, host nicknames, IP prefixes, region and bucket gives 0 lines. Node probe kit-probe1108g of the 4 changed notebooks running. LEFT: the census check with its deny-list read from LOCAL config (never a repo file). NEXT STEP: the census row as a closed union (Provider, Host, Address, Region, Bucket, PersonalPath) and the reader of a local deny-list file, wired into the style hook as a ratchet.")
inl note_of_rig_infra_names_heal_4 () = Note ("RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL", 4u32, "2026-11-08T22:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-08 19:0x rig: user refinement (via org2, 18:4x): planet aliases are FINE (\"keep things like the planet aliases to ease understanding\"); only raw identity must go (provider names like europa, IPs, real hostnames such as DESKTOP-... or provider instance names, regions, the bucket, personal paths); the backlog is out of scope. The neutral wording already applied stays valid (aliases are allowed, not required). Census deny-list source decided: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config\\infra-aliases.tsv with rows (literal|word, token, replacement), read at run time and NEVER copied into a repo. NEXT STEP: the census row as a closed union of raw-identity classes (Provider, Address, Hostname, Region, Bucket, PersonalPath; planet aliases are not a class) reading that file, wired into the style hook as a ratchet.")
inl note_of_rig_infra_names_heal_5 () = Note ("RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL", 5u32, "2026-11-08T22:57Z", "org2", "org2 11-08 18:5x, from tibia (its slice is Done): a census pattern for personal paths must require / or an escaped \\\\ after the drive colon; tibia's first pattern false-positived on a \\n escape (wall:\\nscan). Suggestion: 'kit table logs --root <dir>' emitting root-relative paths would make relative paths structural for every lane's tables. Also, the node-env function Test-VultrScopeCap and job ids named -vultr-watch still carry the provider name; rename them when convenient (the backlog notes keep the old names until then).")
inl note_of_rig_infra_names_heal_6 () = Note ("RIG-INFRA-NAMES-HEAL", 6u32, "2026-11-09T06:26Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 03:5x local rig RE-VERIFIED after tonight's ~600 edited files (env names, prefix flip, new packages, scripts): 0 deny-list hits in the rig tree (history excluded: state, evidence, target, lock files, FIRST-COMMIT-REVIEW.md), checking all 31 entries of the local deny-list (LOCALAPPDATA kit config infra-aliases.tsv, never copied into a repo). MATCHING RULE for the census check this item still owes, learned the hard way tonight: the file has 3 columns (kind, raw name, alias); match column 2, with kind literal = case-insensitive fixed string and kind word = case-insensitive WHOLE word (a bare substring match on a short region code produced 438 false hits); print only the alias and the location, never the raw name. Next step unchanged: that census check reading the deny-list at run time.")
