inl note_of_nodebench_spiral_rewrite_1 () = Note ("NODEBENCH-SPIRAL-REWRITE", 1u32, "2026-11-08T23:07Z", "org3", "DoD: nodebench reimplemented in Spiral (kit/infra or lib), feature-gated via typefeatureset (lean default vs gpu), granular style, self-explanatory code with NO comments, emits the same one-line key=value metric; builds+runs across the fleet. Next step: study kit/infra/nodebench/src/main.rs (Rust v0.2) + the granular/typed-boundaries conventions, scope Spiral modules (cpu/mem/disk/gpu), decide the typefeatureset split. TypeFeatures: lean|gpu. Proof: a Spiral-built nodebench produces a metric line matching the Rust one on >=2 nodes. Blocker: none (later / non-urgent, user 11-08).")
inl note_of_nodebench_spiral_rewrite_2 () = Note ("NODEBENCH-SPIRAL-REWRITE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:40Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:4x tibia (help pool): SLICE 1 GREEN, the pure model, as a new kit package draft drafts\\kit\\NODEBENCH-SPIRAL-REWRITE\\handoff-1\\ (nodebench.spi sha a3a73726cd23, package.spiproj, standards.spi copied from agile_claim_model: no comments, width 120, LF, test targets, lib referenced; FROZEN). Models kit/infra/nodebench/src/main.rs v0.2: node_state (Idle|Saturated), disk + disk_result (DiskMeasured|DiskFailed with the -1 sentinels), gpu_result (GpuSkipped|GpuMeasured), the metric record, metric_line (the exact key=value line via sm'.format_fixed for Rust's {:.N}), best_of (min), median (upper middle), the deterministic wrapping LCG offset stream and slot_of, and the rate helpers. Tests 5: the whole line byte for byte (CORES=4 ST_MS=812.25 MT_MS=1234.50 MEM_GBPS=12.00 DWR_MBPS=456.5 DRD_MBPS=1024.0 DSYNC_MS=0.500 DIOPS=1500 GPU_CLASS=skip STATE=idle); failed disk + saturated (-1.0/-1.0/-1.000/-1, STATE=sat); best_of/median; the LCG (first value 3236661110929538048, slots 48128 and 36175, computed independently: the generated Rust's u64 math wraps like Rust's wrapping_mul/add); rates. Gate: off-train probe on ganymede (kit/src/nodebench next to a kit/src/spiral link, run_notebook --gate): 5/5, 0 unsupported. Trap on the way: |> listm.append ys puts ys FIRST; a diagnostic probe whose expect message carried the actual line localized it. Packaging is rig's call (kit still uses package.spiproj everywhere). TypeFeatures: lean|gpu is modeled as gpu_result; the gpu probe itself stays a feature-gated host primitive. Next step: after rig agrees the package placement, add the measurement slice: timers, threads, memory copy and the fsync'd disk probe as named one-expression primitives in kit's OS boundary package, per AGENTS.md.")
inl note_of_nodebench_spiral_rewrite_3 () = Note ("NODEBENCH-SPIRAL-REWRITE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T06:43Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:5x tibia: rig answered placement. Home: src/rig_nodebench (rig_ prefix for every new kit package; package.spiproj, since kit has 0 spiral.toml packages and regen finds owners from package.spiproj); the model stays HostFree with standards.spi copied from a HostFree + LibReferenced sibling. Same model, staged as drafts\\kit\\NODEBENCH-SPIRAL-REWRITE\\handoff-2\\rig_nodebench\\ (nodebench.spi a3a73726cd23, unchanged from handoff-1). Host side: a NEW boundary package src/rig_os_bench next to src/rig_os_machine, which REUSES rig_os_machine's logical_cpus and is_windows. It uses named one-expression primitives at most 120 chars, host types behind :! nominals, and no blocks or statements: a nominal Instant + elapsed_ns; a worker-count thread primitive with the loop body in the same crate; a nominal buffer + copy; and open/write/sync_all/remove as separate disk primitives. No HostFree there. rig applies the slices from tibia's drafts after TRAIN43e installs. OPEN DECISION (user or org, NOT rig's): should nodebench become a rig verb, so every benchmarked node needs rig.exe, or stay a standalone binary, giving rig_nodebench its own Cargo bin target so lean, offline nodes still run it? Next step: after the user or org picks verb vs standalone, draft rig_os_bench and the measurement slice on that entry shape.")
inl fleet_node_saturation_24_7 () = Task ("FLEET-NODE-SATURATION-24-7", "Keep ganymede/moon/europa saturated 24/7 (tiered node scheduling + wake-economy)", Epic, P2, D6, 0u32, Planned, "", "scheduling,nodes,saturation,rig", "current", "current")
inl note_of_fleet_node_saturation_24_7_1 () = Note ("FLEET-NODE-SATURATION-24-7", 1u32, "2026-11-08T23:28Z", "org3", "GOAL (user 11-08): keep the always-on compute nodes continuously busy, autonomous-run or NOT. TIERS: SATURATE-24/7 = ganymede, moon, europa (long queues, append jobs, never idle). QUOTA-DOGFOOD = comet (use as hard as possible to discover when the codespace quota ends; track usage). NIGHT-ONLY 9pm-6am = venus, mercury, saturn (work-lab, off-hours only). PARKED/MANUAL/BY-REQUEST = neptune, jupiter. EARTH(box) = short jobs OK, NO long compilations. pluto = production/services, no builds. WAKE-ECONOMY: lanes+gates must NOT over-wake lanes (preserve the autonomous on/off-toggle balance we landed); when a lane IS woken, it first checks the results of its last queued/pending runs, THEN grooms the backlog = another dimension to battletest/dogfood rig scheduler. DoD: a durable per-lane job-queue keeps ganymede/moon/europa busy 24/7 with appended work; comet usage tracked toward quota; tier windows enforced; wake-economy respected. Next step: rig designs queue+append+smart-wake into the executor/gate; org encodes tiers in placement; org3 tracks saturation + comet quota + tier-window enforcement. Blocker: KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR land (queuing needs the funnel); ramps as it lands.")
inl node_saturation_monitor () = Task ("NODE-SATURATION-MONITOR", "org3 saturation monitor: per-node depth + comet quota + tier-window compliance (feeds the feeder)", Feature, P2, D4, 30u32, Active, "FLEET-NODE-SATURATION-24-7", "scheduling,monitoring,saturation,org3", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_node_saturation_monitor () = Planning ("NODE-SATURATION-MONITOR", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_node_saturation_monitor_1 () = Note ("NODE-SATURATION-MONITOR", 1u32, "2026-11-08T23:30Z", "org3", "DoD: a monitor (org3) that reports (a) per-node QUEUED DEPTH for the 24/7 tier (ganymede/moon/europa) vs their floor (KIT_JOB_SLOTS+2) and emits a per-node depth TARGET that rig feeder consumes; (b) comet codespace-hours used toward quota, alert near the limit (quota-discovery dogfood); (c) tier-window COMPLIANCE: night-only (venus/mercury/saturn) only run 21:00-06:00, parked (neptune/jupiter) only by request, earth no long-compiles, pluto no builds. Next step: v1 reads `kit job list`/host spools for depth + `gh codespace` usage for comet + wall-clock vs tier windows; wire the depth-target output to the feeder once DELEGATE-1-VERB + the per-node policy-union land (rig order: executor -> KIT-JOB-HANDOFF wake-line -> policy-union -> feeder). Blocker: KIT-REMOTE-EXECUTOR/feeder for the target-consumer side; standalone monitoring works now. TypeFeatures: n/a.")
inl note_of_node_saturation_monitor_2 () = Note ("NODE-SATURATION-MONITOR", 2u32, "2026-11-09T00:04Z", "org3", "REQUIREMENT (org/microblog fleet warning 11-08): the wake-line + monitor must classify cell-budget REFUSALS SEPARATELY from genuine pass/fail. compiler 853-file pack63c reformat pushed 5+ cells over budget (alphabet fonts likely too); an over-budget tree REFUSES every verify (not a regression). So: mark over-budget trees refuse-expected and HOLD queued gates against them instead of spending a 24/7 slot; the check-pending-on-wake summary buckets refusals apart so a woken lane does not re-queue a tree that will just refuse. Budget-check-before-gate = fleet default this round.")
inl note_of_node_saturation_monitor_3 () = Note ("NODE-SATURATION-MONITOR", 3u32, "2026-11-09T00:13Z", "org3", "v1 LANDED at relay-lab/bench/saturation-monitor.sh (box-light): reports 24/7-tier depth (ganymede/moon/europa vs floor slots+2) flagging DRAINS, + comet codespace core-hours vs the 120 free (alert at 110), + a daytime night-only reminder. First run flagged europa depth=0 (drained), moon=1, ganymede=3; comet 81.8/120 used. Next: feed the per-node depth TARGET to rig feeder once the executor lands; refine per-node floors from actual KIT_JOB_SLOTS; add refuse-expected tree holds.")
