inl note_of_kit_exec_metrics_m1_1 () = Note ("KIT-EXEC-METRICS-M1", 1u32, "2026-11-09T04:43Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-EXEC-METRICS by kit agile split (milestone 1). DoD: job receipts become samples per label and machine with elapsed and peak memory, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_exec_metrics_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-EXEC-METRICS-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T04:54Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:3x rig: most of M1 already existed (rig_exec_jobs: kit metrics export --jobs [--since ms] turns settled job dirs into rig_job_duration_ms samples per lane; run live on the box: 32 lines for the last 24 h). DEFECT FOUND in that live output: several series shared one label set (rig_job_duration_ms{machine=\"box\",lane=\"kit\"} repeated), which Prometheus rejects as duplicate series. FIX (live tree, unstaged): JobDuration carries (lane, job id, ms) and prints a job label, so every series is unique; new JobPeak (lane, job id, bytes) from each job's peak_private_mb file prints rig_job_peak_bytes{machine,lane,job}; peak_mb_of parses the file (absent or unparsable = no sample). Tests updated (unique series, a 192 MB peak becomes 201326592 bytes, no peak no sample). Probe rig-probe1109f on moon (metrics + jobs notebooks). Left for M2: the machine union is Box | Node only, remote hosts need their own word.")
inl note_of_kit_exec_metrics_m1_3 () = Note ("KIT-EXEC-METRICS-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-09T04:55Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "DoD: kit metrics export --jobs prints one unique series per settled job (duration, plus peak bytes when recorded) with machine, lane and job labels, and the notebooks of rig_exec_metrics and rig_exec_jobs pass. Next step: the moon probe verdict, then M2 (more machines). TypeFeatures: the metric GADT indexes units by phantom (JobDuration -> metric unit_ms, JobPeak -> metric unit_bytes), so a peak can never print as a duration.")
inl note_of_kit_exec_metrics_m1_4 () = Note ("KIT-EXEC-METRICS-M1", 4u32, "2026-11-09T05:25Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 01:5x rig PROOF: moon notebooks green, rig-probe1109f (job-1794200700858): rig_exec_metrics 1/1 and rig_exec_jobs 1/1, covering the job label (unique series) and peak bytes (192 MB -> 201326592). Left for Done: run kit metrics export --jobs --since <24 h> with the TRAIN42 binary and check no two lines share a label set.")
