inl regex_absorb_closure_budget () = Task ("REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET", "regex: use the 2^(positions+1) bound as the closure budget instead of the fixed 4096 cap in dfa.spi (re-map item 12)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "REGEX-LIB-3-DFA", "team:org,regex,automata,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_absorb_closure_budget () = Planning ("REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_absorb_closure_budget_1 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET", 1u32, "2026-11-09T05:26Z", "org2", "Child of REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB (split 11-09 by org2; source: the 11-08 full re-map, note 9). DoD: build derives its state cap from the pattern positions (2^(p+1), clamped), and a test shows a pattern that exceeds 4096 but stays within its bound builds. Next step: read dfa.spi:139 and certificate.spi:480-512 (the bound is already measured there).")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_closure_budget_2 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET", 2u32, "2026-11-09T05:31Z", "org2", "org2 11-09 01:5x OVERLAP found before editing: REGEX-NERODE (paused until REGEX-LIB-3-DFA lands) already designs the cap change for lib regex_dfa: 10k states or 2 MB of table, a typed build error, a fallback to the interned lazy DFA, and the (a|b)*a(a|b){n} test. Changing dfa.spi's fixed 4096 cap now would be redone in lib right after (the same reason NERODE paused). So this child now depends on REGEX-LIB-3-DFA, and its 2^(positions+1) bound should land as the DERIVED part of NERODE's cap: the cap = min(2^(p+1), the 10k/2 MB ceiling), one change in lib regex_dfa. Next step: after REGEX-LIB-3-DFA lands, do it together with REGEX-NERODE's cap.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_closure_budget_3 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:1x DESIGN CORRECTION before editing: 2^(positions+1) is NOT a sound cap for this engine. lib regex_certificate's check_closure only MEASURES it on the 4 sample patterns (none with counted repeats, And or Not). positions_of counts Repeat(x, ...) once, so a{1000} (really 1001 states, lib test a_thousand_counted_letters...) has bound 2^2 = 4; And(r, s) derivatives reach D(r)*D(s) > 2^(p+1). An unsound cap REFUSES valid patterns, worse than the fixed 4096. So the cap is REGEX-NERODE's resource ceiling, sound by construction: table_cap classes = min(10000 states, 2 MB / (8 B * classes)); build r = build_within (table_cap (length (classes_of r))) r; the typed StateCapReached error stays; 2^(p+1) stays the certificate's diagnostic. Draft drafts\\spiral\\REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET\\regex_dfa.spi (base 6E9D25121530) with 2 new tests: a run past the old 4096 cap builds (a{5000} -> States 5001, rust) and the cap values (table_cap 3/200/0 = 10000/1310/10000). The lazy-DFA fallback NERODE wants lives in regex/src (lazy.spi is not lib), so it is not part of this lib change. Proof: ganymede job org2-capland = lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply + an executing gate of the landed module.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_closure_budget_4 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-CLOSURE-BUDGET", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:19Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:1x LANDED, DONE. Proof (ganymede, exact box-lib tree F91E5CEE8102BACD): job-1794237120092-org2-capland, lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply: apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26, type_probe PASS, respell 0, LANDED and closed green, lib digest 0CCCB6163BFA0636; then an EXECUTING gate of the landed lib regex_dfa.spi: 7/7 passed (incl. a_run_past_the_old_4096_cap_builds_under_the_table_ceiling: a{5000} -> States 5001; the_cap_is_the_smaller_of_10000_states_and_2_mb_of_table: 10000/1310/10000; the old 4-cap refusal and a{1000} tests unchanged). Box: pre-land digest re-checked F91E..., lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply \"LANDED from a proven close\", undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-111815, box lib now 0CCCB6163BFA0636 = the proof. regex_dfa.spi E7ED5A6942A0 (unstaged). DoD met in its corrected form (note 3): the cap is derived (from the class count) and sound, and a pattern past 4096 states builds. regex/src/dfa.spi keeps its legacy 4096 copy until REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB swaps regex/src onto the lib modules. Proof: the logs above.")
