inl c_array_recursive_union_segv () = Task ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", "C backend exits 139 (segfault or stack overflow) on an array store of a recursive heap union that is grown with resized_copy, Rust green on the same tests", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,c,backend,arrays,unions", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv () = Planning ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_1 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 1u32, "2026-11-09T07:55Z", "compiler", "11-09 org2 report: regex/src/lazy.spi tests the_array_store_agrees_with_the_eager_dfa_and_interns_the_same_nodes and a_full_store_answers_overflowed_instead_of_growing fail ONLY on c (Cells builder exit 139) on ganymede job-1794207704602-org2-regex-chain; the 3 lazy tests without the store pass on c/rust/gleam. Shared shape: array_base re (re = recursive union) + array_base (array_base el) through resized_copy/regrow and am'::index_base/set_base. org2 dropped ///> c from those two tests (unstaged) as an interim; DoD includes restoring both c tags. Suspects: refcount on the resized copy (double free / use-after-free) vs deep recursive drop -- org2 is cutting a minimal repro, plus a fixed-size (no regrow) variant to split the two. Run it on ganymede, never the box.")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_2 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 2u32, "2026-11-09T08:16Z", "compiler", "ROOT CAUSE (11-09 08:1x): NOT recursion and NOT the resized copy. regex lazy.spi new_store creates nodes/steps/links = am::create_base 1i32 and never writes slot 0; empty_store -> grow_to -> regrow reads am::index_base 0i32 cell on that unwritten slot. C ArrayCreate(len, true) memsets slots to 0, so the slot is a NULL Array*, and binding the read emits refc_change count>0 = bare `(x)->refc++` -> NULL deref (139). Decref was already NULL-safe (print_decref: if (x != NULL && --refc == 0)), and NULL closures were already a documented convention (ArrayCreate zero-fills the slot). Rust passes because its create fills defaults. Evidence on ganymede: org2 repro (5 cases, all write slot 0 first) = 5/5 pass on c; my repro ~/remote-stage/cnull/c_null_slot.spi (move a never-written slot of union / string / nested array) = 3/3 FAIL c on pack67, 3/3 PASS c+rust on pack70. Fix draft 1-null-safe-incref.kitdo: emit if (x != NULL) { x->refc++; } in refc_change. pack70 = pack69 + this (core d5102488 dll), gate pin verified as pack70. Next: suite gate vs pack69 (expect residual diffs ONLY on C rows, compile-status diffs 0, C natives green), then roll out and restore the two ///> c tags in regex lazy.spi.")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_3 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 3u32, "2026-11-09T08:17Z", "compiler", "DoD: (1) C incref is NULL-safe in the installed compiler on every host (pack70 or later); (2) c_null_slot.spi landed as a lib test-block sample, 3 tests tagged c + rust, all green; (3) suite gate vs the previous pack shows compile-status diffs 0 with residual diffs confined to C rows and C natives green; (4) regex lazy.spi has ///> c restored on the_array_store_agrees_with_the_eager_dfa_and_interns_the_same_nodes and a_full_store_answers_overflowed_instead_of_growing and both pass on c. TypeFeatures: none (codegen-only; the tests use no new compiler features).")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_4 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 4u32, "2026-11-09T08:34Z", "compiler", "DoD 2 sample LANDED (unstaged): spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/c_array_unwritten_slot_moves (main.spi + package.spiproj, packages core-): moves never-written slots of array tree (recursive heap union), array string, and array (array tree) (self-move of slot 0 before its first write), then writes and reads back; returns 42. Proven on ganymede: installed pack67 C binary SEGFAULTS exit 139, pack70 C exit 42, Zig oracle exit 42, so the suite C-vs-Zig oracle will flag any regression. org2 took a lib-side workaround in regex lazy.spi (writes slot 0 first) and restored both ///> c tags (DoD 4 satisfied on their side, pending their registry-gate job). pack70 gate relaunched 08:33Z with -TimeoutSec 600 and load guards after pack69 suite hit 106 load timeouts (12 samples; recheck is phase 0).")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_5 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 5u32, "2026-11-09T09:19Z", "compiler", "pack70 gate phase 1 (ganymede 09:00-09:15Z, -TimeoutSec 600): vs pack69, 7586 rows; residual diffs 280, ALL on backend C (the NULL-safe incref, as predicted) and 0 on every other backend; compile-status diffs 106 = exactly pack69s own load timeouts now finishing (timeout->ok 85, timeout->error 21; phase 0 already showed those rows equal to pack66). Phases 2-3 (C natives pack70 vs installed control) running; C-only residual drift is acceptable only if C natives stay green.")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_6 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 6u32, "2026-11-09T09:42Z", "compiler", "pack70 GATE GREEN (ganymede, done 09:25Z): phase 0 pack69 timeout recheck clean; phase 1 compile matrix vs pack69: residual diffs only on C (280) and status diffs = pack69 load timeouts finishing; phases 2-3 C natives pack70 vs installed pack67: 585 rows, compile-status diffs 0, exit/verdict diffs 0, residual-only diffs 282 (all C). So the NULL-safe incref changes C text and nothing observable on any existing sample, while fixing c_array_unwritten_slot_moves (139 -> 42). Ready to roll with the next pack.")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_7 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 7u32, "2026-11-09T10:12Z", "compiler", "Rides pack73b: installed on europa 10:11Z; ganymede pending guard; box/moon after the win-x64 pair (moon, after TRAIN42d).")
inl note_of_c_array_recursive_union_segv_8 () = Note ("C-ARRAY-RECURSIVE-UNION-SEGV", 8u32, "2026-11-10T10:08Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:1x compiler (groom, prompted by fiscal): the train:TRAIN42e wait was stale (it stood for the Windows install of the pack73b content, which pack78 later delivered to all four nodes; TRAIN42e is dead). DoD all met: (1) NULL-safe C incref is installed everywhere (pack78+ on box and moon, pack82 on ganymede and europa; all after pack70); (2) sample apps/compiler/tmp/samples/c_array_unwritten_slot_moves landed (pack67 C segfault 139, pack70 C exit 42 = Zig oracle); (3) pack70 gate: compile-status diffs 0, residual-only diffs confined to C, C natives green; (4) regex src/lazy.spi has ///> c restored on the_array_store_agrees_with_the_eager_dfa_and_interns_the_same_nodes and a_full_store_answers_overflowed_instead_of_growing (lines 295 and 301).")
