inl rig_gap_do_replace_pattern () = Task ("RIG-GAP-DO-REPLACE-PATTERN", "gap: do replace pattern with a group reference to a group that does not exist ($1000ms) replaces the match with nothing and exits 0", TaskKind, P1, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "rig,gap,do,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_gap_do_replace_pattern () = Planning ("RIG-GAP-DO-REPLACE-PATTERN", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_gap_do_replace_pattern_1 () = Note ("RIG-GAP-DO-REPLACE-PATTERN", 1u32, "2026-11-09T08:02Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "FAILED CALL: verb=do edit replace pattern exit=0 cwd=- argv=edit src/jobs.spi / replace pattern all \"timeout (\\d+)s\" with \"timeout $1000ms\". Both lines became timeout followed by nothing; the regex crate reads $1000ms as the named group 1000ms, which the pattern lacks, and expands it to empty. Found writing spec/one-call.md case 53 (11-09 04:0x, installed kit 5B9082C1). DoD: a replacement that names a group the pattern does not define is refused before any write, with intent, usage, the valid groups and a corrected example (${1}000ms). Next step: validate replacement group names against the compiled regex capture names in the do edit validation pass, add a rig_do_edit test. TypeFeatures: a replacement_part union (Literal, Group index, Group name) parsed once.")
inl note_of_rig_gap_do_replace_pattern_2 () = Note ("RIG-GAP-DO-REPLACE-PATTERN", 2u32, "2026-11-09T08:30Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 04:4x local rig, FIX WRITTEN (unprobed, rides TRAIN43): new pure linked package src/rig_do_replacement (HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0 findings): pattern_groups scans the pattern text for capture groups (skips escapes, character classes incl. a leading ], non-capturing (?:, flags, lookarounds (?= (?<! ; counts (?P<n> and (?<n> as index + name), references_from reads the replacement like the regex crate ($$ literal, ${name}, $name = longest run of letters/digits/_), replacement_problem names the first unknown group with the valid list and a ${N}rest hint when the reference starts with a known index. rig_do_edit run.spi: a Pattern rule with a valid regex now also checks group_problem, so the edit fails validation and nothing is written (no new host code: the census ratchet refused a capture_names host primitive in rig_do_edit, 14/66 -> 15/67). Tests: 3 blocks in replacement.spi, CLI test a_replacement_naming_a_missing_group_writes_nothing in rig_do_edit/edit_cli.spi. Wiring: link + Cargo dep + workspace member, lock refreshed. After it ships: update spec case 53 prose (today it says the reference expands to nothing).")
inl note_of_rig_gap_do_replace_pattern_3 () = Note ("RIG-GAP-DO-REPLACE-PATTERN", 3u32, "2026-11-09T09:27Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 05:3x moon probe rig-probe1109k (job-1794215686927): src/rig_do_replacement/replacement.spi GREEN 2/2 after fixing the hint (1109j had caught it: digits_end took the whole 1000 in $1000ms; known_prefix now offers the longest digit prefix that is a known group, ${1}000ms). Left: TRAIN43 regen + the rig_do_edit CLI test a_replacement_naming_a_missing_group_writes_nothing; then spec case 53 prose.")
inl rig_job_host_linux_upkeep () = Task ("RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP", "Linux job host upkeep on ganymede: the systemd kit-worker host is mis-rooted and redundant, and the live host burns about 12 pct CPU while idle", TaskKind, P1, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "rig,jobs,linux,node,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_job_host_linux_upkeep () = Planning ("RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_job_host_linux_upkeep_1 () = Note ("RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP", 1u32, "2026-11-09T10:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "FOUND 11-09 06:4x (org2 sweep, verified by rig): ganymede runs two kit job hosts. (a) pid 33312 = kit-worker.service MainPID: ExecStart /home/remote/git/kit/src/target/debug/kit job host (a DEBUG build from a dev checkout), Environment KIT_JOB_HOST_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=0 KIT_JOB_SLOTS=2, no HOME, cwd / (the empty-HOME trap: its jobs root resolves where no submission lands; 0 pct CPU, 14 h). (b) pid 38734 = /root/.cache/kit/supervisor/kit-<hash> job host, auto-started by job start --on, HOME=/root, serves every real job (supervising rig-regen1109 now), and holds about 12 pct of one core while idle for 12 h (org2 measured). DoD: one host per machine: the unit runs the installed release kit with HOME=/root (or RIG_JOBS_HOME set) so it IS the host that submissions use, the auto-start path finds it instead of spawning a second, and an idle host sleeps (under 1 pct CPU). Next step: read the host idle loop (rig_job_host) for a missing sleep/backoff on Linux, then switch the unit in a quiet window (never while it supervises a job). TypeFeatures: none yet.")
inl note_of_rig_job_host_linux_upkeep_2 () = Note ("RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:07Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:1x local rig, IDLE LOOP read (src/rig_job_host/host_run.spi host_served): every 500 ms, whatever the load, the host lists the requests dir, checks the owner, lists held entries, rewrites the live-children record and counts held jobs; on a small VM that is the steady ~12 pct. FIX (rides TRAIN43, model probe rig-probe1109p running): host_model gains busy_nap_ms 500 and next_idle_nap (doubling to a 4 s cap) with test an_idle_host_naps_longer_and_longer_up_to_four_seconds; host_served carries the nap: any request or live child resets it to 500 ms, an idle KeepServing tick sleeps the nap and doubles it, draining keeps 500 ms. Cost: an idle host notices a new request up to 4 s later. Left for this item: the systemd unit (release binary + HOME) in a quiet window, one host per machine.")
inl note_of_rig_job_host_linux_upkeep_3 () = Note ("RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:17Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 07:4x moon probe rig-probe1109p: src/rig_job_host/host_model.spi GREEN (exit 0, incl. an_idle_host_naps_longer_and_longer_up_to_four_seconds). host_run.spi carries the nap (regen-checked in TRAIN43).")
inl note_of_rig_job_host_linux_upkeep_4 () = Note ("RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP", 4u32, "2026-11-09T13:57Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:5x local rig, DIAGNOSED (read-only, prompted by microblog's sweep). ganymede runs two job hosts, both parent 1. (a) pid 33312 = the ENABLED systemd unit kit-worker.service (\"kit job host (rig worker, no k3s)\", since 11-08 20:45:59Z), ExecStart /home/remote/git/kit/src/target/debug/kit job host: a debug build, cwd /, no HOME in its environment, so its jobs root falls back to a dir that does not exist; it serves nothing (no shell-host/pid names it, no job names it), 0% CPU, 29 s CPU in 17 h, stdout to journald. (b) pid 38734 = /root/.cache/kit/supervisor/kit-424426336-1794170559 job host, left by an abandoned ssh session scope (session-118, 11-08 21:55Z), cwd /tmp, HOME=/root: THIS is the canonical host (jobs/shell-host/pid = 38734, rewrites shell-host/live every tick) and serves the open jobs (2 now: org2 physics, tibia bc-calib). Its steady 13.8% CPU is the idle busy-poll fixed by the rig_job_host idle backoff (busy_nap 500 ms, doubling to 4 s; unprobed, rides TRAIN43). PLAN, when ganymede has no open job and after TRAIN43 installs: write a drop-in for kit-worker.service with ExecStart = the installed release binary and Environment=HOME=/root, systemctl daemon-reload + restart, verify shell-host/pid names the unit's pid and live advances, then stop 38734 by pid and verify it is gone. Never kill 38734 while jobs are open.")
