inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_1 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 1u32, "2026-11-09T10:56Z", "compiler", "rig 11-09 star exchange: both cost a train round. DoD: (1) a local binding named open is a hard parse error naming the line and suggesting a rename; (2) Some { record } either parses as Some ({ record }) or fails with an error that says to parenthesize; negative samples for both. TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_2 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:11Z", "compiler", "11-09 11:1x compiler: REPRO on the installed pack73b: (1) a local `:= open = x + 1i32` -- the CLI already fails (exit 5) and names the line, but only as the generic \"Expected one of: lowercase variable, _, ~, (, {, ;, [, exists\" plus a knock-on \"Unbound term variable: f\", and the per-block warning repeats it; it never says open is a keyword. (2) `Some { x = x }` is NOT a parser bug: it parses as Some applied to a record and the type error is correct; what bites is `Some { .. } |> r`, which is `(Some { .. }) |> r` by ordinary precedence (application binds tighter than |>). No grammar change for (2). FIX for (1), draft 1-keyword-as-name.kitdo (9 edits): new ParserErrors case KeywordAsName, returned by all six read_small/type_var fallbacks when the token is a keyword; rendered (word keywords only) as \"Keyword `open` cannot be used as a name here; rename it (for example open_).\" under Other error messages. Built on ganymede over pack73b, no FS0025 incomplete-match warnings; the repro now prints that sentence. Next: a negative sample (keyword_as_local_name_negative) + suite gate, ride the next pack.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_3 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "compiler", "groom 11-09 23:2x (star digest: \"keyword-named locals in a test block silently drop the block\"). pack78 (fleet-wide) carries 1-keyword-as-name.kitdo, which makes a keyword used as a local name a hard error. Open question: does that cover locals INSIDE a test block, or is the whole test block still dropped before the check runs? Next step: on ganymede (installed pack78), --check a file with a test block holding := type = 1 (and one with match / open as names) and confirm a hard error naming the line; if the block is still silently dropped, extend the program to test-block bodies.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_4 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T03:28Z", "compiler", "11-09 23:4x compiler, VERIFIED on installed pack78 (ganymede): (1) plain code `:= type = 1` -> --check rc 5, \"Keyword `type` cannot be used as a name here; rename it (for example type_)\". (2) The same local inside a TEST block: --check rc 0 and --backend C rc 0, because both skip test bodies by design (memory check-skips-test-bodies); --test-blocks still LISTS the block (extraction no longer drops it). (3) The test body compiled as its own program (what Cells per-test protocol does per test, default-on since microblogs 11-09 change) -> rc 5 with the keyword error. So the digests silent drop is real only for runs that never compile test bodies (--check, --backend builds, the old whole-notebook protocol); a per-test Cells gate surfaces it. GAP: a pre-train sweep needs a Cells run to see it. Next step: make --check PARSE test-block bodies (parse only, no inference, so it stays cheap) and report parse errors per block with file:line, as a kitdo program for the next pack, proven by a test-block keyword sample whose --check must fail.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_5 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T03:32Z", "compiler", "ROOT CAUSE (11-09 23:3x): blockParsingParse sends every test block through blockParsingTestEntryStart, which returns None unless default_env.test_entry selects exactly that test; the result is Error [] (an error with NO messages), so the block is dropped silently and its body is never parsed. FIX DRAFTED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS\\2-check-parses-test-bodies.kitdo: when NO test is selected (--check, normal builds), parse each non-static test body and return its real parse errors (still no entry); when a test IS selected (Cells per-test), other tests stay skipped, so a broken test B cannot fail test As run; tests with a fails mode are skipped too (some may expect parse errors on purpose). Candidate pack79 = pack78 + this program, core 089d8707. Gate launched on ganymede 23:3x (~/remote-stage/pack79/g.log): the repro must fail --check with the keyword error; --check over all lib/spiral files old vs new lists newly visible errors (= real broken tests hidden until now); -Suite all vs pack78. Next step: read g.log, triage any newly visible lib errors with their owners, then decide pack79.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_6 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T04:48Z", "compiler", "pack79 install caveat (microblog 11-10, CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB): on Windows hosts the Cells memo key never includes SpiralCompilerCore.dll (the glob in Memo.compiler_binaries_print fails on backslash paths), and pack79 changes ONLY the core (host Program.fs unchanged), so Windows Cells gates after installing pack79 on box/moon could replay pre-pack79 cell results as green. Until microblogs glob fix deploys: run every Windows Cells gate after pack79 with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0. Linux is unaffected (forward-slash paths). Next step unchanged: after the gate, install pack79 (Linux via install-pack -FromDir, the COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET proof).")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_7 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T05:07Z", "compiler", "11-10 01:0x compiler: pack79 gate on ganymede, phase 1 GREEN: lib sweep --check over all 139 lib/spiral files, pack78 vs pack79, files whose error count changed: 0 (so no lib test block hides a parse error; the fix exposes nothing new in lib). Repro still hard-errors (rc=5, Keyword `type` cannot be used as a name). Phase 2 PENDING: full suite (frontier, examples, contracts, mega: 7,610 jobs, 2 workers, timeout 600 s) started 01:01, log ~/remote-stage/pack79/suite.log; g.sh diffs results.tsv against pack78. Next step: read the suite diff when g.log says p79 done.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_8 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T06:08Z", "compiler", "11-10 02:0x compiler: pack79 INSTALLED on ganymede (06:04Z, Core 9f1ef997) and the installed compiler hard-errors on the repro: --check of a test block with := type = ... exits 5 with Keyword `type` cannot be used as a name (pack78 returned Error [] silently). Gate: lib 139 files 0 error-count changes, suite 7,610 rows 0 diffs. Store: linux-x64 put (v2 base). REMAINING: win-x64 pack79 for box + moon (a moon build, then -Put win-x64 under a v2 base, which also replaces the stale v1 Windows base) and europa from the store. Windows Cells gates after that install run with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 until CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB lands. Next step: build pack79 win-x64 on moon when moon is quiet.")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_9 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 9u32, "2026-11-10T06:15Z", "compiler", "11-10 02:1x compiler: pack79 INSTALLED on europa FROM THE STORE (first Linux store install end to end): install-pack -FromUrls (45 min presigned urls minted on the box, url file deleted on both hosts right after), store hit on the v2 base files-9d42858d + pair pack79, every file matched its manifest, 35 files copied with 0 mismatches, launch True, smoke --check process.spi ok; installed Core 9f1ef997 / host c51a27a4 = ganymede = the gate build. Backup ~/.cache/spiral-bin/compiler-installs/pack79-20261110-061530. Linux fleet (ganymede, europa) on pack79. REMAINING: win-x64 pack79 for box + moon (moon build when quiet, -Put win-x64 under a v2 base). Next step unchanged (wait when:moon-quiet).")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_10 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 10u32, "2026-11-10T13:14Z", "compiler", "11-10 09:0x compiler: moon is QUIET (0 jobs, 1% CPU at 08:53 local): the pack83 win-x64 pair build is RUNNING as kit job job-1794316277859-compiler-moon-pack83-pair (pair83.ps1 in C:/home/remote-stage/moon-post: private rc.3 SDK dotnet-rc3, cache83, sources spiral_compiler.p83.fs c3742c88 / Program.p83.fs). pack83 = pack79 parser fix + C unit main + F# export dead-let (both fixes) + empty match. Next step: when the job EXITS (never on DLL presence: R2R rewrites in place), fetch the 35-file bin, install-pack -Put win-x64 (new v2 base replaces the stale v1 one), install box + moon with -FromDir (Windows Cells gates after it with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 until CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB lands).")
inl note_of_parser_silent_drops_hard_errors_11 () = Note ("PARSER-SILENT-DROPS-HARD-ERRORS", 11u32, "2026-11-10T13:54Z", "compiler", "11-10 09:4x compiler: DONE fleet-wide via pack83 (contains this fix plus C unit main, F# export dead-let (both fixes) and empty match). win-x64 pair built on moon (job-1794316277859, exit 0, 92 s, R2R done; Core de4ee5a2), put to the store (base v2 files-046a0947, replaces the stale v1 Windows base), INSTALLED box (09:39 local: 6 programs reproduce pack83 from the boxs live pack78 source; 35 files, 0 mismatches, smoke ok) and moon (job-1794318330252: 35 files, 0 mismatches, smoke ok, Core de4ee5a2). Linux: ganymede + europa on pack83 (Core 2c6efed9). Windows Cells gates should run with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 until CELLS-MEMO-WINDOWS-GLOB lands (core-only change, same host hash).")
