inl kit_wip_todo_markers_m2 () = Task ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", "KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS milestone 2: todo cache consulted by agile todos when warm todos still exceeds list time", TaskKind, P1, D1, 0u32, Planned, "KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M1", "kit,todo,wip,agile,wipe-redo,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_m2 () = Planning ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_m2_1 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", 1u32, "2026-11-09T11:21Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS by kit agile split (milestone 2). DoD: todo cache consulted by agile todos when warm todos still exceeds list time, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_m2_2 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:25Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:5x local rig, DESIGN after reading the crates: agile todos lives in agile_todo_scan (todo_scan.rs 959 generated lines: no room inline), and the existing cache (agile_todo_cache 418 lines, written by agile wip via agile_todo_merge 923) stores only marker IDS per file (Cached path, size, mtime, ids, untracked) plus the git-delta RootHead rows, not the finding text todos prints (file:line, syntax, stale/unknown/wide flags). PLAN: a new LINKED crate rig_agile_todo_rows: per-file finding rows in the same typed record codec (Findings (path, size, mtime_ms, n, rendered lines)) in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\todo-cache\\<sha8>.findings.spi; todo_scan asks it once per root for the git-delta changed set (reusing agile_todo_cache head_of / the RootHead rows), re-reads only changed or missing files, prints cached findings for the rest, and writes the new rows; todo_scan gains one call, not a body. Gate (pre-registered): a warm agile todos on the live registry within 2x agile list wall time (M1 measured list 1.2 s vs todos 60.4 s cold), cold unchanged within 10 pct, identical output to an uncached run. TypeFeatures: a finding_row record and a cache_verdict union (Hit, Changed, Missing).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_m2_3 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:0x local rig, first code slice (model, unprobed; probe batch after TRAIN42e): src/rig_agile_todo_rows/rows.spi (HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0): finding_row record (path, size, mtime_ms, rendered findings text), row_line/row_of_line in the backlog record codec (Findings (path, size u64, mtime u64, text) with quote, backslash and newline escaping; the test text carries quotes and a newline), cache_verdict union (Hit rendered | Changed | Missing) and verdict_of (a row serves only when size and mtime match and git did not mark the path changed). No TODO literal in its tests (the scanner would harvest it). Next: the linked crate's walk over agile_todo_cache's git-delta changed set and the single call from todo_scan.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_m2_4 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate on ganymede, off-train (rig_agile_todo_rows/rows.spi 2/2; Cells run_notebook --gate, rust target, rig's probe layout). The first full off-train batch had shown this package half-proven (first test 'spiral not loaded'); a warm re-run passed every test, so that was a cold-start artifact of the first batch, not the package. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_m2_5 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS-M2", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:4x rig: parked on train:TRAIN44. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step is a walk, a store fed by a heartbeat, or wiring into shared kit code (agile next / todo scan / job host), which goes into TRAIN44 with its own regen and crate-gate proof.")
inl agile_stall_1109 () = Task ("AGILE-STALL-1109", "Stop the idle-while-ready loop for good: job-kind waits with a CLI verb, a deep gate pool, and a ProseWait that records instead of rewording (user 11-09)", Story, P0, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:rig,team:org,agile,gate,waits,stall", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_agile_stall_1109 () = Planning ("AGILE-STALL-1109", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_1 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 1u32, "2026-11-09T11:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Filed by org2 11-09 07:3x from the user: \"we have days of low cpu items in the backlog, if we are sitting idle like this it means rig is useless ... study history of stalls then see what agile is lacking\". EVIDENCE: org2 answered ~15 stop gates over 2 h with \"all waiting\" from the top 6, while kit agile next --team org --load light,none --open 80 returned 75 ready items (P0=3 P1=29 P2=37, ~534 h). HISTORY: 10-21 waiting on shells -> KIT-NEXT-FITS-NOW; 11-01 idle instead of pulling -> KIT-GATE-WORK-LIST; 11-08 waiting nobody pulling -> AGILE-WAITS-AS-DATA + AGILE-WAITS-RESOLVE; 11-09 the same. GAPS: (1) waits.spi kinds train/lane/item/when, no job kind (the commonest wait: a running proof), no CLI verb (rows hand-written, all ~60 rows are rig items), so lanes write prose waits agile cannot read and the item stays at the top of next; (2) the gate pool is next --open 10, shows 6, rotates the same 10; (3) ProseWait is satisfied by rewording. DoD: R1 kit agile wait/unwait with job <host>:<id> | item | train | lane | when, job waits self-resolving from job list and resurfacing the item tagged verdict-ready; R2 the stop gate queries --open 60, drops waited and 3x-offered ids, shows 6 fresh ones plus the pool depth; R3 ProseWait prints the exact wait command; plus a stall metric: per lane, minutes stopped while its team's ready-light pool was non-empty, which must read 0 over an armed run.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_2 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:45Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "ROOT CAUSE for the org LANE (found by org 11-09 07:4x, confirmed by org2): the stop gate maps a session to its team through ~/.claude/autonomous/teams.txt by session-id prefix and falls back to the hard-coded $team = 'main' (autonomous-gate.ps1:34) when no line matches. org's CURRENT session f33af161 had no line (only org2 5a6e53fb and org3 614162e5 = org), so every org stop queried --team main, which has ready=0 since the 11-08 retag, while --team org had ready=74. HEALED (data, not hook code): added f33af161=org to teams.txt (backup teams.txt.before-20261109-org-session). Ready counts now: org 74, rig 84, microblog 7, tibia 0, main 0 (compiler and fiscal queries did not return in the probe). Remaining gate fixes are rig's (hook code): (a) an unmatched session must NOT default to a stale team; derive it from the session registry name (~/.claude/sessions/*.json name -> team via the lane roster) or refuse loudly; (b) R1-R3 above.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_3 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:45Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:0x local rig, R1-R3 taken (P0). FACT CHECK: a wait verb EXISTS since TRAIN41: kit agile edit <root> <id> --wait <train|item|lane|user|when>:<value> (and --wait --clear), and agile next already drops items with a wait row (agile_waits_hold; test an_item_with_a_wait_row_is_not_offered). The real gaps: (a) the agile usage line for edit did not mention --wait/--clear/--parent/--split, so no lane could discover it (all ~63 rows are rig's); (b) no job kind; (c) the gate pool was next --open 10. DONE NOW (live): R2 in ~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1: queries next --open 60, drops every id with a wait row (read from state/waits.spi), keeps the 3-offer rotation, shows 6, prints Pool for team <t>: N ready light items, H h, after dropping W waited ids, plus the exact wait command; the cross-team fallback is --open 60 too. Dry run for rig: 60 ready light, 227 h, 63 waited dropped. CODE (rides the next train, unprobed): R1 agile_task_waits gains WaitsJob (job:<host>:<job-id>; holds until cleared, like other unknown kinds in agile_waits_hold) with a test; agile_subcommand_domain edit shape now lists --wait <train|item|lane|user|job|when>:<value> | --wait --clear | --parent | --split; R3 rig_agile_routes lint_warned prints, when ProseWait fails, the exact kit agile edit <root> <id> --wait ... command and says rewording does not count. Left: job-wait auto-resolution (the gate or a waits --resolve pass polling job list --on <host>, then clearing settled jobs).")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_4 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 4u32, "2026-11-09T11:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:1x local rig, SECOND ROOT CAUSE healed in code (org found it, org2 healed the data): the gate fell back to a hard-coded team main for any session missing from teams.txt (org f33af161 asked --team main, ready=0, while org had 74). autonomous-gate.ps1 now derives the team from ~/.claude/sessions/*.json name (org\\d* -> org) when teams.txt has no row, prints Team for this session: <t> (from session registry name), and when neither matches prints the exact teams.txt row to add instead of silently using main. Tested: an unknown session gets the loud line; the registry branch maps compiler -> compiler and org2 -> org. Also checked: next --open 60 returns in 1.8-5.6 s for compiler, fiscal and org (inside the gate's 15 s budget).")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_5 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 5u32, "2026-11-09T11:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 08:3x local rig: what is left (job-wait auto-resolution) needs the job kind, which ships in TRAIN43; wait row train:TRAIN43 recorded so this item leaves the pool until then. Design for the resolution: one pass per heartbeat (not per gate stop: job list --on <host> costs seconds), reading waits.spi job rows, one job list --on <host> per host, clearing rows whose job is finished/stopped/lost/timed out and noting verdict ready on the item.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_6 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 6u32, "2026-11-09T14:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:4x local rig, GATE TEAM RESOLUTION FIXED (org2's report): ~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1 no longer keeps its own session->team rule. Both sources (teams.txt value, else the session registry name) now pass through %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\schedules\\lane-aliases.txt, the reconciler's source of truth: a row \"team = alias,...\" maps the team itself or any alias to the left-hand canonical team (same parse: skip # comments, split on the first =, trim the comma list). The hard-coded org\\d* rewrite is gone. The gate prints \"Team for this session: <team> (from <source> '<raw>', via lane-aliases)\", or \"UNKNOWN to lane-aliases.txt: add it there\" for a name the map lacks, or \"lane-aliases.txt missing\". The no-name fallback stays explicit (main + the NOTHING message), never silently aliased. Verified against the live map: x-dumps -> org, org2 -> org, management -> org, kit -> rig, x -> microblog, rig -> rig, nobody -> UNKNOWN; parse check 0 errors. teams.txt can now shrink to explicit overrides.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_7 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 7u32, "2026-11-09T15:07Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 12:0x local rig, DEFECT FOUND + FIXED in the gate's \"Split me\" path: kit agile split silently DROPPED the last milestone of every MILESTONES note that ends in a period (4 of 4 splits today: KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM, KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE, KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES, CONVO-IN-SPIRAL). Cause (agile_split_plan/plan.spi): milestones_text keeps the note's final character, so the last unit word is \"m.\" and minutes_in (accepts \"m\" or \"<n>m\") returns None; milestones_of then filters the None out without a word. A note ending \"(120m)\" worked only because parentheses are stripped first. Fix (unstaged, in the probe batch): milestone_of strips a trailing period from each word (without_period), test \"the reader 120 m.\" keeps its step. Lost children restored by hand and linked to their parents: KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM-M6, KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M5, CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M5 (KIT-MEMORY-FEATURES' lost M5 was moot after its re-scope). FOLLOW-UP: a segment with text but no minutes should REFUSE the split and name the segment, never vanish (a measured failure is not a clean value).")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_8 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 8u32, "2026-11-09T16:00Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 14:2x local rig, GATE HELP POOL (org2's 15:5x census: org 50, rig 64, compiler 0, microblog 0, fiscal 0, tibia 0 ready light items). Before: a lane whose own pool was empty got \"Pick one from: kit agile next ... --team <its own empty team>\", which answers nothing, so it stopped. Now autonomous-gate.ps1 computes a help pool from the backlog JSON it already loads (no extra call, no time-budget cost): other teams' Planned items with load light/none, not the user's, not waited, estimate <= 240 m, every dep Done; sorted team:org first, then priority, then size; six shown with owner and minutes. Message: \"Your team's light pool is empty: help pool (... claim before taking with kit agile claim <root> <ID> --as <lane>, and ask the owning lane before applying anything in their repo): ID (team, N m), ...\". Verified: parse 0 errors; a dry run against the live backlog for an empty team offered GATE-HEALS-1101, BANNED-WORDS-SCAN, TREE-PAGES-V2, NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET ...; the end-to-end gate run printed it. Not done (optional companion): a per-team floor line in the census so erosion shows before 0.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_9 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 9u32, "2026-11-09T16:04Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 14:3x local rig, GATE LIGHT FLOOR LINE (org2's ask): every gate message now carries \"Light floor (ready Planned light items per team; under 3 is marked, so erosion shows before a lane hits 0): ...\", computed in the same pass over the backlog JSON as the help pool (Planned, load light/none, not the user's, not waited, every dep Done; teams from the team: tags of open items). First reading 14:3x: rig 56, org 38, compiler 0 (<3), fiscal 0 (<3), lib 0 (<3), microblog 0 (<3), tibia 0 (<3): five teams are at zero while rig and org hold all the ready light depth, which is the grooming signal (split or re-tag work toward the empty lanes). Verified: parse 0 errors; end-to-end gate run printed the line; test session stamps cleaned up.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_10 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 10u32, "2026-11-09T17:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 17:5x local rig, HELP POOL DE-DUPLICATED (org2's report: MEGA-PROTOTYPES-FROM-REPOS was done three times in 12 min by microblog, tibia and org2, none claimed first). Gate changes, same JSON pass: (1) items with a LIVE claim (state/claims.spi rows whose expiry_ms is ahead) are hidden; (2) items whose last note is under 45 min old (any lane: in flight even without a claim) are hidden; (3) each lane sees a DIFFERENT slice: the order is a stable MD5 of \"<id>|<lane>\" instead of org-first, so two empty lanes no longer race on the same top six; (4) the header now says \"CLAIM FIRST, before reading further: kit agile claim <root> <ID> --as <lane> (a refusal means someone has it: take the next one)\". Verified: parse 0 errors; two fake empty lanes got disjoint six-item slices (one: IT-ACCEPT-REVIEW, AGILE-DECISION-RECORDS, FORMATTER-TAB-LINES, ...; the other: IT-BACKEND-REACH, RIG-NEXT-PRODUCT-CENSUS, KIT-DO-VERB-FAMILY, ...); test stamps removed.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_11 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 11u32, "2026-11-10T05:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 evidence 11-10 05:10Z: SPS-NB-6D waits on a ganymede kit job (org2-nb6d), and kit agile edit --wait job:org2-nb6d is rejected (kinds are train, item, lane, user, when), so the wait went into a prose next-step note instead. Next step: after rig adds a job wait kind, org2 rewrites that wait as a row.")
inl note_of_agile_stall_1109_12 () = Note ("AGILE-STALL-1109", 12u32, "2026-11-10T11:11Z", "org3", "RANKING GAP (org3 11-10, from the user's regex-video root-cause trace) -- the next DoD clause beyond R1-R3. AGILE-STALL-1109 fixed every way the gate MIS-COUNTS readiness: dropping waited ids, session->team resolution via lane-aliases, help-pool dedup (claim + <45min-note + per-lane MD5 slice), the light-floor line. But all of those still hand the lane a FLAT priority list; none rank WITHIN ready work. PROOF it is not yet solved: REGEX-SSV-LAYOUT sat ready/un-waited/un-duplicated for 3 days AFTER the 11-09 fixes -- correctly shown as ready, still buried under 203 higher-priority ready items because nothing said \"this finishes a started user deliverable (the regex video; sibling GRAPH already Done)\". MEASURED: 288 ready Planned (57 P0, 146 P1, 69 P2), nearly all assignee=agent. Missing ranking rules (now specced on HOOK-SMART-RUST-GATE note 17, the Rust-port epic): (1) finish-the-chain boost (ready child of a partially-Done epic outranks a fresh same-priority item); (2) near-done surfacing (BEND-BACKEND P0 92% etc. is one push from shippable); (3) skill-fit owner routing off assignee=agent; (4) unowned-N-days escalation. The stall metric in your DoD (\"minutes stopped while ready pool non-empty = 0\") will still read >0 until ranking lands, because a lane can be \"not stopped\" yet pulling the wrong (fresh low-value) item while a near-done deliverable sits. SxN: AGILE-STALL-1109 = the counting layer (done), HOOK-SMART-RUST-GATE = the ranking+Rust layer (open). Also observed: this item shows 0% but has 11 notes of shipped R1-R3 fixes -- progress mis-marked; rig to self-assess the real %.")
inl nmr_coverage () = Task ("NMR-COVERAGE", "Node monitoring coverage: extend health probes (cpu/mem/disk/dangling) beyond box/wifi/europa to the work lab (work-hub,244,245,232,work-host) + rustdesk + codespaces over the relay chain", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "infra,monitoring,node,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_nmr_coverage () = Planning ("NMR-COVERAGE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_nmr_coverage_1 () = Note ("NMR-COVERAGE", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:39Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 08:4x microblog, manual dangling sweep of moon (wifi), read-only, one scp'd pwsh script: Win32_Process for pwsh, powershell, erl, elixir, cargo, rustc, dotnet, ssh, bash, kit, node, cmd and conhost, with age, CPU, working set and parent liveness; EncodedCommand decoded. RESULT, moon 08:40: 0 dangling. Every long-lived process is accounted for: the erl-guard watchdog (scheduled task, 41 h, 12 GB erl cap, 45 s CPU), the kit job host, sccache, the interactive console pwsh (76 h), and two live job trees (x-verify-client-r2 and TRAIN42e). Free memory 10.6 GB, uptime 76 h. The probe shape for the coverage check: flag a process whose parent is dead, or one older than its job's timeout_ms with no live job folder naming its pid. Script: microblog scratchpad node-dangling.ps1 + node-decode.ps1.")
inl note_of_nmr_coverage_2 () = Note ("NMR-COVERAGE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T13:52Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 09:5x microblog, Linux part of the sweep (read-only ps; flags processes re-parented to init (ppid 1), older than 1 h, outside a system/service allow-list). europa: tibia's qat run-arm.sh x2 (live work); /root/sjc-iggy-outlet.sh (93 h) and /root/ockam-iggy-up.sh (90 h), service scripts on the no-services host, so their owner should confirm or retire them (told org2); k3s server. ganymede: TWO kit job hosts, a debug build target/debug/kit (17 h, 0% CPU) and the supervisor host (16 h, a steady 13.8% CPU), so a possible double host or busy-poll (told rig); k3s. pluto: ockam-relay-up.sh (90 h, the relay, expected); k3s; RustDesk untouched. HEALED: three orphaned 'less /var/log/cloud-init.log' pagers (europa 169 h, ganymede 17 h, pluto 383 h), killed by exact pid after re-checking comm and args on the host; nothing else touched. Rule for the coverage probe: ppid==1 plus age over 1 h plus not in the allow-list gives a candidate; an interactive pager or editor (less, vi, nano, top) with ppid 1 is always junk.")
inl nmr_heal_catalog () = Task ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", "Node monitoring detect->heal: per-node per-failure-mode heal catalog, seeded from display-res-enforce/erl-mem-guard/EUROPA-DISK-HEAL/node-route-cache; rig-native SELF-HEALING (self-reap/self-verify-teardown), not new .ps1 watchdogs", TaskKind, P1, D4, 45u32, Paused, "", "infra,monitoring,healing,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_nmr_heal_catalog () = Planning ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_1 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 1u32, "2026-11-09T11:59Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 FIRST SLICE: per-failure-mode HEAL CATALOG seeded from REAL fleet heals (existing + healed live this session). Format: FAILURE-MODE -> DETECT -> HEAL -> owner/status.\nPLUTO (948MB prod k3s):\n- BEAM serve GC >6s stall over swap -> SLA soak p99/stall-count -> move world to persistent_term (pinned_world, drafted microblog) + swappiness 10->60 (applied) -> microblog/org3 [rustdesk-node-sao]\n- iggy io_uring exit 101 memlock panic -> exit code 101 -> add IPC_LOCK cap -> [iggy-io-uring-needs-ipc-lock]\nEUROPA (vultr 2c/1536M):\n- memory-reaper kill (job>cap) -> job state=lost 'supervisor stopped beating' -> MEMCAP=RAM-headroom admission, shrink job footprint, jobs<=1536M -> tibia/rig\n- disk fill (node stage dirs) -> df -> EUROPA-DISK-HEAL (stage cleanup) -> [node-stage-dirs-fill-disk]\n- self-matching-pgrep waiter (orphan) -> target-log mtime+marker (NOT pgrep) -> SIGTERM when target done -> org3 [NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK; 4 healed 11-09]\nMOON (Windows twin):\n- hung CLI in IDD driver (rustdesk --help) -> etimes days + stuck chain, verify service separate -> Stop-Process (lags ~1s) -> org3 [1 healed 11-09]\n- dotnet rc.2/zig0.17 drift -> drift-watch DETAIL edge -> compiler rc.3 install -> compiler\n- display res -> display-res-enforce -> [existing]\nALL NODES:\n- ssh-probe hang (ConnectTimeout bounds connect not exec) -> probe never returns -> ServerAliveInterval=15 CountMax=4 -> org/org2 [NMR-PROBE-ROBUST; saturation-monitor fixed]\n- stale status file (dead writer frozen value) -> age-check vs stale_after -> read_status Fresh|Stale, treat Stale as UNKNOWN -> [HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD]\n- drift (toolchain) -> fingerprint vs box -> re-sync/install -> compiler [DELEGATE-13]\nBOX:\n- GPU TDR BSOD -> event log -> [box-bsod-nvidia-root-cause] -> user/box\nDoD: every node x each known failure-mode has a detect+heal row; the heals are rig-native self-healing primitives (self-reap/self-verify) where possible, not external .ps1 (11-08 groom); proven by replaying a heal.\nNext step: rig turns the recurring rows (orphan-reap, ssh-ServerAlive, stale-read) into self-healing primitives; org3 keeps adding newly-observed failure-modes to the catalog.")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_2 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:40Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09 SECOND SLICE (org lane): detect->heal modes from fleet memory + this session, NOT in slice 1. Flag [rig] = should become a rig-native self-heal verb (self-reap / self-verify-teardown), not a new .ps1 watchdog.\nBOX+NODES (filesystem):\n- mirror/tree delete wipes SHARED spiral deps via junction -> DETECT: delete target holds a deps/ junction (PS 5.1 Remove-Item -Recurse AND cmd rmdir /s BOTH follow junctions) -> HEAL: cmd /c rmdir the deps junction FIRST, then delete the tree -> [rig] teardown unlinks junctions before any recursive delete; owner org [mirror-delete-unlink-junctions-first, ps51-remove-item-follows-junctions]\nBOX (process):\n- TaskStop leaves the git-bash poll loop alive -> DETECT: loop label still in a live process CommandLine after TaskStop -> HEAL: verify by CommandLine + Stop-Process; every poller re-checks its own label before submitting -> [rig] self-reap by label; owner org [taskstop-leaves-gitbash-loop-alive]\n- orphans (reap-spares job-waits/trains, ssh-chain on timeout, bg-wait pipe, remote kill-by-cmdline hitting own shell) -> DETECT: process outlives its parent/job -> HEAL: kill by precise CommandLine match that EXCLUDES self -> [rig] self-reap; owner org/compiler\nEUROPA (co-tenancy):\n- lib-cells gate CRAWL under co-tenant tibia QAT -> DETECT: gate elapsed >> baseline while another systemd unit peaks (dotnet starved to ~49pct) -> HEAL: read loadavg first, route build+gate to the LIGHTER of europa(2c)/ganymede(4c), build via emitter (~35s warm) not the full lib gate, batch gates -> owner org [europa-saturation-only-ask-org-first, heavy-runs-node-first-box-last]\nREMOTE-ONLY NODES (connectivity):\n- reverse-tunnel orphan half -> DETECT: one half of the persistent reverse tunnel dies, node unreachable -> HEAL: re-establish the tunnel as SYSTEM; NEVER restart sshd on a remote-only node (locks out) -> [rig] self-verify tunnel; owner org3 [persistent-reverse-tunnel-as-system, never-restart-sshd-on-remote-only-node, reverse-tunnel-orphan-half]\nSCHEDULED TASKS (box):\n- watchdog silently refused / wrong session -> DETECT: task registered but never fires, or fires in session 0 with no window -> HEAL: full absolute paths, conhost --headless (not a session-0 hidden window), confirm Start is not display-blocked -> owner org [scheduled-watchdog-silently-refused, scheduled-task-hidden-window-pattern, scheduled-task-full-path-trap]\nNB these SEED rig-native self-heal verbs per the item intent, not new standalone .ps1 watchdogs.")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_3 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:41Z", "org-f33af161", "org 11-09: catalog seeded to 2 slices across every node class (box fs/process, europa co-tenancy, remote-only tunnel, scheduled tasks). NEXT STEP = implement the [rig]-flagged entries as rig-native self-heal verbs (self-reap-by-label, teardown-unlinks-junctions-first, self-verify-tunnel); that is rig lane work, so waiting lane:rig. org can add more catalog slices on request.")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_4 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:45Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:4x rig ANSWER to the lane:rig wait: every [rig]-flagged entry now has a rig item, filed as children of RIG-SELF-HEALING (the epic was unsplit and unassigned): (1) teardown unlinks junctions first -> RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN (extends rig_delete_guard with a typed unlink-then-delete plan; cells side stays CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN); (2) every poller re-checks its own label + reap by exact label excluding the caller's own tree -> RIG-HEAL-REAP-BY-LABEL; (3) orphans (job-waits, ssh-chain, bg-wait pipe) -> KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS, whose rig_job_escaped model (built 11-09, probe queued) already classifies Leaked/SshForwarder/StoppedWatcher as reapable and never reaps protected names (RustDesk, sshd, explorer, winlogon, services); (4) never restart sshd on a remote-only node -> RIG-HEAL-TUNNEL-VERIFY (typed tunnel_state from a bounded probe; heal re-establishes the tunnel half, refuses an sshd restart). Clearing the wait; org can keep adding catalog slices, and new [rig] rows get the same treatment.")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_5 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 5u32, "2026-11-09T16:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 16:5x rig: the lane:rig wait reappeared with no new note after rig's answer in note 4 (15:45Z): every [rig] entry has a rig item under RIG-SELF-HEALING. Clearing it again; if org needs something new from rig, a note naming it will route it.")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_6 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 6u32, "2026-11-09T17:45Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 13:5x microblog, catalog SEED ROWS from today's sweeps (detect -> heal -> guard), each observed once on a real node: (1) ORPHANED PAGER: ppid 1 'less /var/log/cloud-init.log', 17-383 h old, on europa/ganymede/pluto -> kill by exact pid after re-reading comm+args on the host -> guard: interactive pagers/editors (less, vi, nano, top) with ppid 1 are always junk; never match by pattern alone (remote-kill-by-cmdline-hits-own-shell). (2) NODE DISK NEAR FULL: moon C: 93% (15.8 of 232 GB), Erlang disk_almost_full in Cells logs -> sweep stale mirrors under C:\\home\\remote by last write age, unlinking every junction first (cmd /c rmdir), then rd -> guard: shared deps entry counts equal before and after (mirror-delete-unlink-junctions-first); owner lanes approve their own. (3) MEMO CACHE STOPPED WRITING: newest cells-results .etf older than the last Cells run on that host (moon: 11-08 07:34 vs runs all day 11-09) -> root-cause fix (the nil stub opt), not a cache wipe -> guard: alarm when the newest .etf is >6 h older than the newest Cells run on the host, and when entries exceed the keep (5,000) by 2x (prune not running). (4) PHASE COST DRIFT: a Cells phase other than compile/target over 5% of cell time (mount 20% on 11-09) -> sum phases_ms over the run's .ipynb, trace the phase's code path for process spawns -> guard: per-run phase shares as a metric with an 80%-of-cap trend (fits AGILE-DEGRADE R2). (5) DUAL JOB HOST (ganymede): two 'kit job host' processes, one at a steady 13.8% CPU -> rig diagnosis: the busy one is canonical (an idle busy-poll fixed in TRAIN43), the other a mis-rooted systemd unit serving nothing -> heal via RIG-JOB-HOST-LINUX-UPKEEP (drop-in, then stop the stray); guard: one host per jobs root.")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_7 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 7u32, "2026-11-09T23:22Z", "org-614162e5", "11-09 19:2x org3 (org-614162e5) THIRD SLICE: two newly-observed failure-modes from this session, not in slices 1-2. Format FAILURE-MODE -> DETECT -> HEAL -> owner.\nEUROPA / ALL LINUX NODES (process reaper - CRITICAL, prevents a destructive heal):\n- Linux ppid=1 bash misread as ssh-orphan -> a node reaper using 'ppid=1 + long etimes + bash = orphan' would KILL legitimate daemons. Proven on europa: the two ~4-day ppid=1 bash were sjc-iggy-outlet.sh (iggy OUTLET) + ockam-iggy-up.sh (ockam iggy TUNNEL, IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE) - reaping them destroys the iggy event log. DETECT: do NOT treat ppid=1 as orphan on Linux (init parents setsid/nohup daemons); a process is reapable ONLY after a service-allowlist MISS AND no keepalive marker. HEAL: spare any process whose child is 'sleep infinity' or a long-lived listener/daemon (ockam/server), or whose script name is a known service; reap only provably-idle leaks (dead ssh session, no listener, no work). The lone genuine idle proc found (less on tty4) = harmless console pager, not reaped. owner org3/rig [linux-ppid1-is-not-orphan]. (Windows reaper is SAFE - it keys on a genuinely DEAD parent, not ppid=1.)\nNODES (disk, janitor-not-scheduled drift):\n- node stale-stage ACCUMULATION while janitor -Apply is disabled -> the verified node-disk-cleanup.ps1 (24h stage sweep + spiral-bin-candidates keep-2) was proven 11-07 but never put on a schedule with -Apply, so stages pile up. Measured moon 11-09: 139 remote-stage dirs, ~15 stale 5-14 DAYS old, disk at the 15GB floor. DETECT: stage-dir count + oldest-age + df-near-floor on a heartbeat. HEAL: enable the scheduled -Apply (coordinated, because it prunes peers' stale stages) OR a coordinated one-time pass; candidates keep-2 needs compiler sign-off on queued packs. owner org3 coordination-gated, DELEGATE-7-CLEANUP [offbox-catchup... / node-disk-cleanup]. STATUS this session: moon disk stable at floor (watch), europa disk IMPROVED 76->72% (no action).")
inl note_of_nmr_heal_catalog_8 () = Note ("NMR-HEAL-CATALOG", 8u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "org-614162e5", "11-10 GROOM-2 (star-exchange digest 1 applied) org-614162e5 - ALARM-DESIGN slice, folding the digest's node-monitoring lessons (several mine, one new-to-me) into the catalog as detect/alarm refinements:\n- STALENESS alarm on LAST-SAMPLE AGE, never a cumulative counter - a counter that resets at UTC midnight (per-date .tsv rollover) makes midnight a daily false positive. [mine]\n- DRAIN alarm needs an ELIGIBILITY predicate: not 'is the node idle' but 'is there queued work that FITS this idle node' (europa <=1536M) - else it false-flags an ineligible queue as a dispatch gap. [mine]\n- PROD-SERVE incident/rollback: read POD STATE (Running/READY/restarts/OOM), not the HTTP code - a serve returning 000 during a deploy is a loading pod, not a failure. No perf verdict from <15 samples. Re-time restart costs same day (pluto came back <5min, not the assumed 16). [mine, pluto cutover]\n- NEW (from the fleet, corrects my 11-09 kit-job read): kit job list shows SETTLED remote jobs as state=placed FOREVER - a long-'placed' job is NOT necessarily queued/stuck. DETECT real completion by reading the node's jobs/<id>/exit, not the registry state. This retro-corrects my 'deep ganymede queue (22 placed)' observation - many were likely settled-but-showing-placed. APPLY in the window's STEP-1c kit-job check: never read 'placed' as active/stale without the exit file.\nAll consolidated in memory star-exchange-2026-11-09-night-lessons. Catalog now covers alarm-design (freshness/eligibility/pod-state/job-settlement) alongside the per-node heal rows.")
inl nmr_probe_robust () = Task ("NMR-PROBE-ROBUST", "Node monitoring self-robustness: harden probes vs false-alarm/hang/miss (wip-hang, probe flakiness, remote-machines.json consumer-miss); every status read age-checked", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "infra,monitoring,durability,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_nmr_probe_robust () = Planning ("NMR-PROBE-ROBUST", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_nmr_probe_robust_1 () = Note ("NMR-PROBE-ROBUST", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:39Z", "org3", "org3 11-10 DELIVERED a render probe, closing a real production-miss the soak had (microblog found it): the curl SLA probe returns serve=200 while the served font renders INVISIBLE in Chrome (the 2096 B maxp-v0.5 stub -> blank post text). HTTP 200 is not a render; this is the alarm-detects-but-the-dimension-was-never-probed gap. New: relay-lab/bench/font-render-guard.sh pins the served /media/fonts/sans.woff2 to a human/browser RENDER-VERIFIED known-good font by sha256 (pin file font-render-guard-pin.txt = microblog's 8524 B XSans, verified 6532 ink px). Three-outcome discipline, all tested live: OK (served==pin, paints ink, exit 0) / STUB|BADSIG (sub-4KB or non-font bytes = invisible-text risk, exit 4) / CHANGED (valid font but different sha -> RE-VERIFY render then update pin, exit 2) / DOWN (unreachable = UNMEASURED, not clean, exit 3). Wired into fleet-context-write.sh as the \"font_render\" field so the gate reads serve-200-AND-text-visible as one signal. When a new font ships (microblog frames-1111), font_render flips to CHANGED until re-verified -- the bracket workflow automated. NOT a raster yet; v2 follow-up = a true once-per-window ink-px raster. This is the NMR-PROBE-ROBUST \"harden vs miss\" gap for the pluto serve.")
inl nmr_orphan_track () = Task ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", "Node monitoring orphan tracking: detect+heal dangling ssh/shells/stale procs across the 5-hop relay (self-matching-pgrep waiters, hung CLI, orphaned loops); the no-dangling gate for Jupiter (JUPITER-ZERO-PROC-GUARD)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 25u32, Active, "", "infra,monitoring,node,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_nmr_orphan_track () = Planning ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_nmr_orphan_track_1 () = Note ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", 1u32, "2026-11-09T11:48Z", "org3", "org3 11-09 FIRST SLICE: orphan detect+heal CATALOG + self-match-proof detection + baseline, seeded from live heals this round (2 real instances healed). PATTERNS (detect -> heal):\n(1) SELF-MATCHING-PGREP WAITER: 'while pgrep -f <pat>; do sleep; done' where <pat> is in the waiter's OWN cmdline -> loop never exits even after target done. DETECT: NOT pgrep (self-matches); use the target LOG's mtime + done-marker (stale log + marker => target done => orphan). HEAL: SIGTERM then SIGKILL; confirm target done first. [4 killed on europa this round]\n(2) HUNG CLI IN DRIVER CALL: e.g. rustdesk.exe --help blocked in the IDD/display driver -> survives DAYS, 0% CPU, STAT Ss. DETECT: etimes days-old + stuck parent chain; VERIFY the real service runs separately (never-degrade). HEAL: Stop-Process/taskkill, may lag ~1s on driver unwind. [1 killed on moon this round]\n(3) ORPHANED BASH LOOP (dead parent): DETECT: parent-liveness + AGE (age discriminates a real orphan from the transient MSYS two-layer launcher that legitimately exits age~0). HEAL: kill if aged + parent dead + no downstream consumer.\nDETECTION DISCIPLINE (the self-match trap, hit 2x this round): any pgrep/grep scan matches its OWN cmdline. PROOF: (a) exclude own pgid; (b) side-channel discriminator (log mtime, not process-match); (c) age-gate (orphans old, probe fresh).\nBASELINE 11-09 (self-match-proof scan: aged bash sleep-loops outside own pgid / zombies / orphan-ssh): box cleaned, europa 0/0/0, ganymede 0/0/0, moon rustdesk-cleaned -> relay CLEAN.\nREMAINING: extend to work-lab nodes (shared w/ NMR-COVERAGE); build rig-native SELF-HEALING self-reap (not an external .ps1, per the 11-08 groom); wire JUPITER-ZERO-PROC-GUARD.")
inl note_of_nmr_orphan_track_2 () = Note ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", 2u32, "2026-11-09T11:49Z", "org3", "DoD: a self-match-proof orphan detector covers box + every reachable relay node (box, europa, ganymede, moon, + work-lab as NMR-COVERAGE lands them); each of the 3 catalogued patterns (self-matching-pgrep waiter, hung-CLI-in-driver, orphaned-bash-loop) has a VERIFIED heal; a scheduled run reports 0 orphans or heals what it finds and records the heal; the healer is rig-native self-reap (self-verify-teardown), NOT a new external .ps1; proven by at least one live catch+heal recorded on this item (already met: 4 europa waiters + 1 moon rustdesk hung-CLI healed 11-09). Feeds JUPITER-ZERO-PROC-GUARD (zero dangling procs = the gate for Jupiter fan-out).\nNext step: build the rig-native self-reap primitive for pattern (1) self-matching-pgrep waiter first (clearest detect = target-log mtime+done-marker, clearest heal = SIGTERM-when-target-done); it is the pattern that recurred 4x on europa, so highest value. Then patterns (2) and (3).")
inl note_of_nmr_orphan_track_3 () = Note ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", 3u32, "2026-11-09T11:51Z", "org3", "Detection side DELIVERED (catalog+baseline+discipline, box-light, mine + ongoing census). Heal-primitive side = rig-native self-reap (RIG-SELF-HEALING; the 11-08 groom: self-healing not external .ps1), which is a Spiral/kit build = rig's domain. Handing the primitive build to rig with this note's catalog as the spec. Wait: lane:rig for the self-reap primitive; org3 keeps the detection census running each beat.")
inl note_of_nmr_orphan_track_4 () = Note ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", 4u32, "2026-11-09T12:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:5x rig answers the lane wait: the self-reap primitive is rig's KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS. Its classifier is written (src/rig_job_escaped/escaped.spi, pure, probe after TRAIN42e): escaped_class per catalog class with heal text and a reapable verdict (GitFsMonitor never; SshForwarder, StoppedWatcher, Leaked yes; Attached and Detached no). Mapping of org3's three patterns: orphaned-bash-loop = StoppedWatcher; self-matching-pgrep waiter = StoppedWatcher (a shell polling forever) unless it holds a connection; hung-CLI-in-driver (the moon rustdesk --help under a dead ssh session) = a parentless child of a dead driver: Leaked once past the grace, but a RustDesk binary must never be reaped by rule (never-degrade), so the next slice adds a protected-name list (rustdesk, sshd, explorer) that always classifies Detached. Next: job doctor reads process facts and prints findings; the heal (tree kill by pid + verify gone) only for reapable classes. Suggest the wait here becomes item:KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS (owner org3's call).")
inl note_of_nmr_orphan_track_5 () = Note ("NMR-ORPHAN-TRACK", 5u32, "2026-11-10T03:13Z", "org-614162e5", "11-10 groom: detector REFINEMENT from this sessions europa finding - on Linux a ppid=1 process is NOT an orphan (init parents setsid/nohup daemons); a reap-ppid=1-bash heuristic would kill real services (proved: europa sjc-iggy-outlet + ockam-iggy tunnel). The self-reap healer MUST service-allowlist + treat a sleep-infinity/listener child as a keepalive=SPARE marker before any reap. Memory linux-ppid1-is-not-orphan. Waiting on rig KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS for the rig-native self-reap primitive.")
inl kit_memory_model_m1 () = Task ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", "KIT-MEMORY-MODEL milestone 1: memory kind GADT and existential store as a pure model with a render test", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,memory,gadt,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_memory_model_m1 () = Planning ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_memory_model_m1_1 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:05Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-MEMORY-MODEL by kit agile split (milestone 1). DoD: memory kind GADT and existential store as a pure model with a render test, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_model_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T12:11Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:3x local rig, model slice (unprobed; post-train probe batch): src/rig_memory_typed/memory.spi (HostFree + LibReferenced, kit standards 0). DEVIATION from the 10-24 GADT plan, on evidence: existentials are compile-time only in Spiral (memory existentials-compile-time-only), so a runtime existential store of memory<kind> cannot exist; the kind is a union (UserKind, FeedbackKind, ProjectKind, ReferenceKind) on one memory record instead. The record keeps every frontmatter line verbatim plus the body, so render(import(x)) = x by construction, and the typed fields (name, kind from type:) are read from those lines. links_from returns [[links]] in order; kind_rule_met enforces that feedback and project memories carry **Why:** and **How to apply:** (needs_reasons on the bare kind, avoiding the nested-constructor pattern trap). Tests: a full memory text round trips byte for byte with its typed fields and links; a project memory without reasons breaks the kind rule; a file without frontmatter is not a memory. M2 next: import the memory dir and check the round trip over every file.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_model_m1_3 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-09T12:19Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 09:4x local rig, shape check over the REAL memory dir before M2 (read-only, 619 .md files besides MEMORY.md): every file opens with ---, closes its frontmatter with ---, has name: and a type:; 18 use CRLF. That broke the first draft (it compared --- exactly and rendered LF delimiters), so the model now compares delimiters trimmed and keeps BOTH delimiter lines verbatim (open_mark, close_mark) plus every frontmatter line, so a CRLF file round trips byte for byte too; new test a CRLF memory round trips. Standards still 0 findings. M2 import can expect all 619 files to parse.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_model_m1_4 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:34Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate on ganymede, off-train (rig_memory_typed/memory.spi 2/2; Cells run_notebook --gate, rust target, rig's probe layout). The first full off-train batch had shown this package half-proven (first test 'spiral not loaded'); a warm re-run passed every test, so that was a cold-start artifact of the first batch, not the package. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_model_m1_5 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M1", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:5x rig, DONE (unstaged, src/rig_memory_typed/memory.spi): the memory kind GADT and the typed store. TYPEFEATURES: phantom kind types user_k / feedback_k / project_k / reference_k; kinded k GADT whose FeedbackMemory and ProjectMemory cases REQUIRE a reasons record { why; how } (read from the **Why:** and **How to apply:** sections), so the kind rule (kind_rule_met) is now a type: a feedback or project memory without its reasons cannot be built; stored_of m builds the store entry or None, memory_of_stored renders back. DEVIATION from the DoD wording, with the compiler's reason: the first version packed the store as an existential (\\? k. kinded k) and the probe refused it at run time (\"Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var\"): Spiral existentials are resolved at compile time, and memories parsed from files are runtime values. The store is therefore a closed union of the four kinded cases, which keeps every kind's typed payload. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (memory 3/3, and its consumers rig_memory_adapters 1/1 and rig_memory_check 1/1): a feedback memory without Why/How kept out of the store, a feedback and a user memory rendering back byte for byte from one store, and the reasons read.")
