inl note_of_rig_derived_links_regen_1 () = Note ("RIG-DERIVED-LINKS-REGEN", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:13Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "From compiler's LINK-WITHOUT-MANIFEST note 7 (handoff 11-09): derived links ride pack75 behind SPIRAL_DERIVED_LINKS=1. DoD: compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1 derives the build order and the linked-unit set (the 11-09 never-skip-linked rule included) from packages deps with non-empty exports in <stem>.unit.json, Cargo path deps follow, and a full regen with the flag shows exactly the census's 86 new extern edges and no other change. Next step: when pack75 is installed, read one unit.json and write the derivation in test-regeneration.ps1. TypeFeatures: none (regen script).")
inl lib_complex_from_polyglot () = Task ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", "lib: move polyglot lib/math complex arithmetic (complex, re, im, add/sub/mult/div, powc, sin, conj; rust num-complex) into lib/spiral as complex.spi with its rust test; zeta via pyo3 stays dead", TaskKind, P4, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "lib,polyglot,team:lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot () = Planning ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot_1 () = Note ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:26Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "From POLYGLOT-SALVAGE-AUDIT 11-09: polyglot/lib/math/math.spi (560 lines) has no lib/spiral counterpart (no num_complex anywhere in spiral/lib or i574n.github/examples). DoD: dod: lib/spiral/complex.spi with the rust complex test green under lib_gate, polyglot math.spi verdict flips to moved. Next: next: copy the complex section only, respell to edition 3, run lib_gate on a node. typefeatures: none needed.")
inl note_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot_2 () = Note ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:11Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 11:1x microblog (filer), before any copy: polyglot's complex section is 100% raw Rust host macros: !\\((a, b), $'\"$0 + $1\"') for add/sub/mult/div/eq, $0.re, $0.im, $0.sin(), $0.conj(), num_complex::Complex::new/powc, over a nominal $'num_complex::Complex<t>'. Copying it as written would put logic in macros (the LIB-MACRO-HEAL drift) and make the module rust-only with a num-complex dependency, against lib's rules (host code only as named one-expression primitives in boundary modules; a generic helper is backend-agnostic). RE-SCOPED proposal (team:lib decides): lib/spiral/complex.spi as a PURE Spiral record :== complex = { re : f64; im : f64 } with add/sub/mult/div/conj/eq written in Spiral arithmetic. These need no host code and run on every backend. sin and powc use lib float primitives (sin, cos, sinh, cosh, exp, log, atan2) if lib has them; check the float_native/math modules first and add any missing one as a boundary primitive with a lib test. zeta (pyo3) stays dead. dod (revised): complex.spi pure Spiral, tests on rust + gleam + c giving the same values (for example (1+2i)(3-i) = 5+5i, and sin(i) = 1.1752i to 1e-12), lib_gate green on a node. next: inventory lib float primitives (sin/cos/sinh/cosh/exp/log/atan2) per backend.")
inl note_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot_3 () = Note ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:14Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 11:2x microblog, inventory step DONE: every primitive the pure module needs already exists on every backend. core.spi (The-Spiral-Language core): log, exp, tanh, sqrt, sin, cos (lines 84-98, !!!! intrinsics, forall t {float}); lib math.spi: atan2 (a per-backend backend_switch, with Gleam via erlang math), log_base, e, floor/ceil/round. Missing as named functions, but derivable in Spiral with no host code: sinh x = (exp x - exp (-x)) / 2, cosh x = (exp x + exp (-x)) / 2. So complex.spi needs ZERO new host primitives: sin (a+bi) = sin a cosh b + i cos a sinh b; abs = sqrt (re^2 + im^2); arg = atan2 im re; powc z w = exp (w * log z), with log z = log |z| + i arg z. next: write lib/spiral/complex.spi (record, add/sub/mult/div/conj/eq/abs/arg/exp/log/powc/sin) with rust+gleam+c tests, then lib_gate on a node.")
inl note_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot_4 () = Note ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", 4u32, "2026-11-09T15:20Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 11:3x microblog: DRAFT written, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT\\complex.spi (sha256 5E414983CA38). It goes to the drafts store, not the lib tree: a new file in the box lib would change every lane's lib digest and break copy-only -ProvenLog lands; it lands through lib_land_window. Content: :== complex = { re : f64; im : f64 }; complex, complex_add/sub/mult/div, conj, norm_sqr, complex_eq, complex_abs (sqrt), complex_arg (math::atan2), sinh/cosh via exp, complex_exp, complex_log, powc z w = exp (w * log z), complex_sin; no host code. Tests (each ///> rust + gleam + c): a_product_is_exact ((1+2i)(3-i) = 5+5i), a_division_undoes_the_product ((5+5i)/(3-i) = 1+2i, exact in binary), the_sine_of_i_is_i_times_the_hyperbolic_sine_of_one (0 + 1.1752011936438014i), i_to_the_power_i_is_real (0.20787957635076193), exp_of_i_pi_is_minus_one (re -1, |r| 1). Every block passes the awk budget oracle (the first test was split after weighing 298); 0 lines over 120; no name collision in lib. PROOF queued: lib-complex-gate.ps1 (lib_gate on a cellsmd1 lib copy plus the draft, with a hash pin) runs in my moon slot job after the sim verify.")
inl note_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot_5 () = Note ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 18:46 moon after-sim: lib-complex-gate verdict ok (run C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-complex-gate-20261109184633): tests passed 5 failed 0 of 5, type errors 0, draft sha 5E414983CA38 on a copy of the cellsmd1 lib. NEXT STEP: land complex.spi via lib_land_window -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_lib_complex_from_polyglot_6 () = Note ("LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT", 6u32, "2026-11-09T23:07Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "NEXT STEP (precise, per memory lib-land-proof-on-node-copy-on-box): my green gate ran lib_gate.ps1, which -ProvenLog does not accept (it wants a lib_land_window close log: 'LANDED and closed green' plus a '<lib file> <hash>' line per draft). So: (1) on a free node mirror, run lib_land_window.ps1 -PrivateLib -Lib <mirror lib> -Draft <file>=<draft> -Label LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT -Apply to get that close log; (2) on the box, run lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -Label LIB-COMPLEX-FROM-POLYGLOT -ProvenLog <that log> -Apply, which only copies under the tree-write window (no box compute).")
inl kit_job_placed_settle () = Task ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", "kit job list on the box folds a remote job's settled state into its placed record: --on jobs stay state=placed exit=- forever after they end on the node", TaskKind, P2, D2, 35u32, Active, "", "kit,jobs,remote,stability,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_job_placed_settle () = Planning ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_1 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:37Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "Found 11-09 08:3x by microblog (star-exchange stale-jobs sweep, CPU-light reads only). Box kit job list shows x-verify-pk67-warm, x-verify-pk67-cold and x-verify-sim2 as state=placed exit=- elapsed 2.4 h, and TRAIN42c/d the same. Their box folders hold only label, placement (on wifi), remote-bin, started_ms. On the node the same ids are settled: pk67-warm exit=143 stopped, pk67-cold exit=2 finished, sim2 exit=125 skipped (after-ok). kit job doctor on the box does not flag them either (it reported only an unwatched live TRAIN42e-node). Effect: every lane reading job list sees phantom live remote jobs and has to ssh to learn the truth. dod: job list prints the node's exit, state and reason for a placed id once the node has settled it (one batched read per host per call, or a placed-settled file written when job status --on fetches it), and doctor flags a placed record whose node folder is settled or missing. next: read how job list renders placement records (placement file, remote-bin), add the per-host batched exit read. typefeatures: none needed; a placed record gains a settled variant.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_2 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:24Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 14:3x microblog (filer), the first step, read: WHY it sticks. kit/src/rig_jobs/jobs.spi:49-61 job_state_now. A remote job's box folder has no 'exit' file, so job_state_of reads it as Settled JobLost, and the branch at :58 ('file_exists (job_file id \"placement\") ?> Live JobPlaced') turns that into a permanent Live JobPlaced. No code path ever brings the node's exit back (rig_job_placement only renders ' placement=<machine>', placement.spi:40). MINIMAL DESIGN, 2 slices: (1) READ SIDE, a pure change at :58. Before answering Live JobPlaced, read job_file id \"placed-exit\"; if present, parse it with the same exit_line format the node writes and return its Settled state (finished/stopped/skipped plus exit and reason), so job list and doctor print the node's verdict. (2) FILL SIDE, one ssh per host per call. A 'kit job settle-placed [--on <host>]' (also run by job list when any placed record is older than N min) sends the placed ids in ONE remote command; the node prints '<id><TAB><contents of jobs/<id>/exit or MISSING>' (an exit line, a still-running marker, or MISSING = held or never started); the box writes placed-exit for the settled ones and leaves the rest. MISSING beyond the job's timeout becomes a doctor finding (lost remote job). Evidence it works without new node code: the node's exit files hold the whole line (seen today: '143<TAB>ms<TAB>stopped<TAB>stopped on request ...', '125 ... skipped --after-ok ...', '2 ... finished'). typefeatures: placed_outcome union (PlacedRunning | PlacedSettled of exit_record | PlacedMissing) for the fill side; the read side reuses job_state.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_3 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:16Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:5x local rig, FILL-SIDE CORE BUILT on microblog's design (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_job_settle/settle.spi (pure, HostFree). placed_outcome PlacedRunning | PlacedSettled exit_fields | PlacedMissing | PlacedUnreadable line (the planned union plus Unreadable, so a garbled reply is never read as settled); outcome_of parses the node's exit-file text in rig_jobs' exit_record format (code, ended ms, word, detail) and KEEPS THE RAW LINE so placed-exit is written byte for byte (an empty detail's trailing tab survives; only the RUNNING / MISSING marker compare trims); settle_plan now reply_text jobs gives one settle_action per placed job: WritePlacedExit (id, line) | LeavePlaced | LostRemoteJob (id, age) when MISSING past placed + timeout (the doctor finding) | NoReply id when the node's reply has no line for that id (a failed or partial ssh is never read as settled or clean). Test: settled, running, missing-old (lost), missing-young (left), no reply, unreadable, and a non-number code. NEXT: slice 1 (the read side at rig_jobs/jobs.spi:58, read placed-exit before answering Live JobPlaced) rides with TRAIN44's rig_jobs touch after TRAIN43 snapshots; then the settle-placed verb sends the one remote command and applies this plan.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_4 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T19:26Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 15:3x microblog, LIVE EVIDENCE (user direction: diagnose stale jobs on the nodes): box 'kit job list' shows 3 compiler jobs as state=placed exit=- at elapsed ~45.6M ms (12.6 h): job-1794206010492-compiler-linked-warm-ab-2 and job-1794206003863-compiler-pack66-features-2 (placement=ganymede), job-1794206134100-compiler-scaling-timed-window (placement=wifi). On the nodes, all three SETTLED ~12.5 h ago: exit file = 143 'stopped on request while waiting for ...', pid dead. So nothing is running or stuck; the box record never folds the node's exit in. Each such row reads as a 12 h hang to any lane auditing jobs. Fixture for the fix: a placed record plus a node exit file with code 143 and reason 'stopped' must render state=settled exit=143.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_5 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T20:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, LIVE COST of this bug: rig's TRAIN43 pre-check (job-1794218773195-rig-regen1109, --on ganymede) finished this morning with exit 1 (\"1<TAB>1794227200423<TAB>finished<TAB>\") and carried two train blockers (a type error and a crate over 1000), but the box record kept placement=on ganymede with no exit for ~11 h, so nothing surfaced them until a hand read of /root/.cache/kit/jobs/<id>/exit. Note for the fill side: on Linux nodes the job folder is /root/.cache/kit/jobs/<id> (not LOCALAPPDATA), so the settle-placed remote command must ask the node's own kit for its jobs root rather than assume a path.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_6 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The first probe was red and is fixed (unstaged): a record update on a call result (job \"d\") did not parse; bound first; re-probed green. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_7 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T22:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, SLICE 1 (READ SIDE) DRAFTED for TRAIN44 (not applied: TRAIN43 is mirroring the live tree): drafts\\kit\\KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE\\jobs-read-side.spi replaces src/rig_jobs/jobs.spi:58-59 (the |? file_exists (job_file id \"placement\") ?> Live JobPlaced branch of job_state_now) with: read <job>/placed-exit; empty -> Live JobPlaced as today; otherwise job_state_of { record ?| exit_text = settled_text }, so the node's own exit line goes through the SAME parser the box uses for local jobs (finished / stopped / skipped / timed-out with code and detail) and job list and doctor print the node's verdict. The fill side (settle.spi, probe-green) writes placed-exit byte for byte, so the two halves meet on that file. Proof plan: the rig_jobs notebooks in TRAIN44 plus one placed fixture with a placed-exit file.")
inl note_of_kit_job_placed_settle_8 () = Note ("KIT-JOB-PLACED-SETTLE", 8u32, "2026-11-09T22:55Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 18:5x rig: slice 1 (read side) APPLIED to src/rig_jobs/jobs.spi after TRAIN43's snapshot (unstaged; rides TRAIN44): job_state_now reads <job>/placed-exit for a placed job and settles through job_state_of. Its proof is TRAIN44's rig_jobs notebooks (rig_jobs needs the kit tree, so the off-train probe layout cannot gate it). The wait stays train:TRAIN43 until TRAIN44 is cut.")
