inl note_of_perf_study_3_design_1 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-3-DESIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:41Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: a typed .spi draft with the model and its tests, reviewed against the table. Next step: start from the best-scoring rows of PERF-STUDY-2.")
inl note_of_perf_study_3_design_2 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-3-DESIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-09T12:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 09:1x DESIGN DRAFT (lib draft, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\PERF-STUDY-3\\bench_model.spi, budget-clean): the best-of rows from PERF-STUDY-2 plus the 3 gaps, typed. plan {rounds; passes; warmup_passes (gap: warmup policy); quiet_cores (bench-pair's gate); aa_low/aa_high (regex's A/A band); outliers : outlier_rule = KeepAll | MadCutoff k (gap: outlier policy)}; sample {arm; round; nanos; state : machine_state {busy_cores; load}} (gap: machine state recorded WITH each sample); spread {low; middle; high} = quartiles + median; aa_verdict = InBand ratio | Void ratio (a table outside the band is VOID, never reported); rotated k arms (regex's per-round rotation); quiet plan sample (drop loud samples); kept rule xs (MAD trimming). 5 rust tests: quartiles of [5;1;3;9;7] = (3, 5, 7); MadCutoff 3 drops a 90 among 10-12 while KeepAll keeps 6; aa 1.02 InBand vs 1.2 Void; rotation by one; busy-core sample not quiet. Wait: job ganymede:org2-benchmodel (box poller). Next: green -> land as lib bench_model via lib_land_window (moon/proven route), then PERF-STUDY-4 ports the regex setup row onto it.")
inl note_of_perf_study_3_design_3 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-3-DESIGN", 3u32, "2026-11-09T13:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:5x gate 1 RED 5/5 from ONE type error: listm::filter does not exist (core listm has map/append/length; filter lives in lib listm'). Fixed to listm'::filter, restaged, resubmitted (org2-benchmodel). Wait row unchanged.")
inl note_of_perf_study_3_design_4 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-3-DESIGN", 4u32, "2026-11-09T14:13Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 14:1x GREEN: ganymede job-1794231507592-org2-benchmodel 5/5 passed (rust): quartiles (3, 5, 7); MadCutoff 3 keeps 5 of 6 vs KeepAll 6; aa 1.02 InBand / 1.2 Void; rotation by one; a busy-core sample is not quiet. Design DoD met: the typed model of the best-of rows + the 3 gaps (warmup, MAD outliers, machine state per sample) exists with tests. Proof: that job. Next (PERF-STUDY-4): land bench_model.spi as lib via lib_land_window and port regex's setup row onto it.")
