inl note_of_ci_k3s_1_manifests_2 () = Note ("CI-K3S-1-MANIFESTS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T13:13Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:3x DONE. Headless-service census (repos now): spiral's compiler host --server-tcp is the ONE service without manifests (iggy already has kit/infra/k3s-iggy; the Cells compiler daemon is a client-spawned child, not a service; everything else is CLI or static site). Placement: spiral/infra/k3s-compiler/, NOT deploy/k3s (the 10-30 call predates kit's sibling convention infra/k3s-<name>; followed the sibling). Files (unstaged, LF, no comments): Dockerfile (2-stage; sdk 11.0.100-rc.2 and runtime 11.0.0-rc.2 pinned tag@digest, verified via MCR manifest HEAD; publish host -p:SpiralCore=single-flight; build-stage assert --capabilities lists server-tcp; non-root APP_UID; DOTNET_GCgen0size=0x4000000 preset so --server-tcp does NOT re-exec itself, keeping the server as PID 1 for SIGTERM), Dockerfile.dockerignore (allowlist: spiral_compiler.fs, runtime, tmp/compiler = ~2.4 MB of the 303 MB apps/compiler context), compiler.yaml (Deployment + ClusterIP Service on 7470, namespace-less for a throwaway -n; SPIRAL_SERVER_BIND=0.0.0.0:7470; readiness + liveness tcpSocket; requests==limits memory 4Gi (admission by memory), cpu 1/2; readOnlyRootFilesystem, drop ALL, seccomp RuntimeDefault, no SA token; emptyDir /work (socket/pid/bridge + HOME) and /tmp). Proof: kubectl apply --dry-run=server -n default on ganymede k3s v1.37.2 -> deployment.apps/spiral-compiler created (server dry run), service/spiral-compiler created (server dry run), exit 0.")
inl ci_k3s_2_workflow () = Task ("CI-K3S-2-WORKFLOW", "CI k3s 2: one GitHub Actions job that starts a throwaway k3s, applies the manifests, waits ready, probes health", TaskKind, P1, D2, 70u32, Active, "CI-K3S-1-MANIFESTS", "ci,kubernetes,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ci_k3s_2_workflow () = Planning ("CI-K3S-2-WORKFLOW", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_ci_k3s_2_workflow_1 () = Note ("CI-K3S-2-WORKFLOW", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:43Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: the job runs green on push via the repo's entry script (one job, no YAML sharding). Next step: after CI-K3S-1.")
inl note_of_ci_k3s_2_workflow_2 () = Note ("CI-K3S-2-WORKFLOW", 2u32, "2026-11-09T13:13Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 handoff from CI-K3S-1 (protocol facts the job MUST respect, read from host Program.fs): (1) the server is one-client-sequential: accept, one request line, reply, next accept. So probes are tcpSocket (handshake completes from the backlog even mid-compile); never an exec probe that sends a request. (2) compile takes FILE PATHS on the server filesystem (compile<TAB>backend<TAB>input<TAB>output), so the smoke must kubectl cp a tiny no-lib sample into /work in the pod, then send in-pod paths over port-forward and assert a spiral-session<TAB>ok line; test-blocks<TAB>path is a cheaper round trip with no compile. (3) quit ends the server (pod restarts). Build: docker build -f infra/k3s-compiler/Dockerfile apps/compiler (context apps/compiler; BuildKit honors Dockerfile.dockerignore), tag spiral-compiler:local, k3s ctr -n k8s.io images import, reference by TAG (ctr-import trap). ganymede cannot prove the image yet: fiscal's ~/node-build/node-image-build.sh copies only the Dockerfile (no context) and caps BuildKit at 2Gi (compiler cold compile ~3 GB); extending it is fiscal's/rig's call, so the runner (16 GB) is the builder. Next step: add the k3s target to i574n.github/scripts/pins/workflows.spi (pinned INSTALL_K3S_VERSION) driven by spiral's entry script.")
inl note_of_ci_k3s_2_workflow_3 () = Note ("CI-K3S-2-WORKFLOW", 3u32, "2026-11-09T13:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 13:4x BUILT (unstaged, needs the user's push to run). spiral/scripts/workflow.ps1 gains -K3s (ONE entry, no new script): Linux-only guard; k3s v1.37.2+k3s1 binary downloaded from the release and sha256-checked against its sha256sum-amd64.txt (no curl|sh installer); k3s server --disable traefik,metrics-server in the background; wait node Ready (4 min); docker build -f infra/k3s-compiler/Dockerfile apps/compiler -> docker save -> k3s ctr import; throwaway namespace k3s-smoke-<pid>; apply compiler.yaml; rollout status 600s; source piped into /work via kubectl exec; port-forward svc 17470:7470; TCP test-blocks round trip asserting spiral-session<TAB>test-blocks with >=1 block; finally: kill forward, delete ns --wait, FAIL if anything is left, kill the server. Parse-checked (0 errors); $args passthrough of --no-headers/-n/--timeout= verified. YAML: one guarded_run always() step in the existing compiler job (scripts/pins/workflows.spi spiral_compiler_job) so a red matrix never hides the k3s result; spiral .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml hand-applied in the generator's exact render (next pins run confirms byte-identical); no new action, actions.lock untouched. Base images re-pinned to rc.3 (newest on MCR, = ganymede's SDK): sdk 11.0.100-rc.3@sha256:59d092a8..., runtime 11.0.0-rc.3@sha256:2484f504.... Proof pending: (a) ganymede job org2-k3sproto proves the protocol half (--server-tcp + SPIRAL_SERVER_BIND + gen0 preset = no re-exec child + test-blocks reply shape); (b) the full path proves only on the first scheduled/dispatched compiler run after the push.")
inl note_of_ci_k3s_2_workflow_4 () = Note ("CI-K3S-2-WORKFLOW", 4u32, "2026-11-09T13:39Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 14:0x PROTOCOL HALF PROVEN on ganymede (job-1794231459300-org2-k3sproto, net11.0 SpiralCompiler.dll): --capabilities prints \"server-tcp test-blocks source-blocks resolve-manifest\" (the Dockerfile build-stage assert holds); SPIRAL_SERVER_BIND=127.0.0.1:17471 honored (\"spiral-session-ready port=17471\"); with DOTNET_GCgen0size preset the server has 0 child processes (no gen0 re-exec, so it is PID 1 in the pod and gets SIGTERM directly); test-blocks reply \"spiral-session<TAB>test-blocks<TAB>1507484<TAB>10<TAB>0\" (fields[3]=10 passes the script's >=1 check on unicode.spi); quit -> \"spiral-session<TAB>quit\", server exit 0. Remaining: the k3s + image half proves only on the first compiler run (schedule or dispatch) after the user pushes spiral + i574n.github.")
