inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_2_lib_2 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-2-LIB", 2u32, "2026-11-09T13:17Z", "tibia", "11-09 09:2x tibia: TAKING this (tibia pool empty; READY org item, CPU-light). Design from LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE note 8: lib env gets `argv_view = Whole | User | AfterVerb` (Whole: index 0 = the executable slot, the 11 \"+1\" copies; User: index 0 = first user argument, today's command_line_argument; AfterVerb: index 0 = the argument after the verb word, rust_std_env's skip(2) used by the 20 agile copies) with view_argument / try_view_argument / view_count, so the offset is a type, not a constant in each copy. decimal_of unifies on trim (convert try_convert of the trimmed text, default 0). stdout_line needs no lib code: the switch step calls console.write_line. Tests as Cells rows in env.spi; gate on ganymede, land via lib_land_window.")
inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_2_lib_3 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-2-LIB", 3u32, "2026-11-09T13:18Z", "tibia", "TypeFeatures: the argv base is a union argv_view (Whole | User | AfterVerb) passed to every accessor, so the three hand-copied offsets (+1, 0, skip 2) become a typed choice and an off-by-one is a different constructor, not a silent constant; decimal_of returns u64 by try_convert of the trimmed text.")
inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_2_lib_4 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-2-LIB", 4u32, "2026-11-09T13:34Z", "tibia", "Evidence: 11-09 09:5x tibia, ganymede job-1794230634014-tibia-env-argv exit 0, run on a copy of lib env.spi in the spiral mirror (restored afterwards, verified 0). The draft was present (5/5 definitions). --check env.spi was clean. Cells env.spi: discovered 19, executed 19, passed 19, failed 0, which includes the 3 new tests argv_views_shift_the_user_arguments, argv_views_read_the_same_slots and decimal_of_trims_and_falls_back_to_zero. The formatter asked for one wrap (try_view_argument), now applied in the box tree. Cell budget: 13 over_budget in env.spi, all in pre-existing definitions (none in the new 304-345 range). Draft: spiral/lib/spiral/env.spi, unstaged, adding argv_view (Whole|User|AfterVerb), view_shift, try_view_argument, view_argument, view_count, decimal_of. NEXT: land it via lib_land_window (consumer compile + document_test). Then LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH points the 86 kit copies at these.")
inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_2_lib_5 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-2-LIB", 5u32, "2026-11-09T16:47Z", "tibia", "Evidence: LANDED 11-09 12:45 local on the box lib by lib_land_window from a proven close. PROOF: moon -PrivateLib (job tibia-libland6, tree = fiscal-libland base + the box lib replaced wholesale + box apps/cells + apps/spiral + spiral root files): round trip ok, signatures, consumers (apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles), document_test, type_probe, respell_drift 0; \"LANDED and closed green\", env.spi 4B73AC37A53E, lib digest 529E4B908CD4A5A5. BOX: the post-land digest was recomputed locally first (Get-LibDigest rows with env.spi overridden) = 529E4B908CD4A5A5, an exact match, so the box only copied: round trip ok, tree-write window win-1794242754610-32244 (waited 2 ms), \"LANDED from a proven close\", undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-124553. lib env.spi now carries argv_view (Whole|User|AfterVerb), view_shift, try_view_argument, view_argument, view_count, decimal_of + 3 test blocks (Cells 19/19 on ganymede, note 4). Unstaged. NEXT is LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH (rig's packages): point the kit copies at these. Took 6 proof attempts: see GATE-HEALS-1101 tibia note for the stage-tree preflight that would have made it 1.")
