inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_3_switch_1 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH", 1u32, "2026-11-09T12:43Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: no package-local prelude copies left; kit train green. Next step: after LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-2, coordinated with rig's trains.")
inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_3_switch_2 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:28Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:3x HANDED TO RIG (claimed first, then released by this note): the lib half is landed (tibia 12:45 local: lib env.spi argv_view Whole|User|AfterVerb, view_shift, try_view_argument, view_argument, view_count, decimal_of; box lib digest 529E4B908CD4A5A5 at that land). The switch rewrites ~86 prelude copies in 52 kit packages (table: LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE n8; argument_count has 3 argv offsets -> Whole/User/AfterVerb, decimal_of 2 semantics -> trim vs no trim) and its DoD is a green kit train, so it rides rig's train cadence in rig's repo; a parallel org2 edit would race the train snapshot (memory train-snapshot-takes-peer-wip). The two non-kit sites stay with their owners: x oauth1 process_id (microblog), tibia offscreen arguments_from (tibia). Next step: rig maps each copy to its argv_view and switches per package in the next train.")
inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_3_switch_3 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH", 3u32, "2026-11-09T17:36Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 18:2x rig ACCEPTED. Sequencing: NOT edited before TRAIN43 snapshots, because train snapshots take the whole live tree (train-snapshot-takes-peer-wip) and TRAIN43 already carries ~40 unprobed rig models; an 86-site rewrite in 52 packages gets its own train (TRAIN44) so a red points at it alone. Plan from LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE n8: argument_owned/argument_count by offset -> view_argument/view_count with Whole (env.command_line_argument_count + 1 users: rig_do, rig_jobs, rig_table_query ...), User (argument_count_after 0: rig_machine_watch) or AfterVerb (the agile verbs, skip 2); stdout_line copies -> console.write_line (no wrapper); decimal_of -> lib decimal_of (the 2 host parse copies that trim keep trimming at the call site: lib try_convert does not trim). Each package's copy removed in the same edit (no new forwards). x and tibia sites stay with microblog and tibia.")
inl note_of_lib_cli_prelude_3_switch_4 () = Note ("LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig: KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE-M1's re-measure shows the agile family holds 20 of the 25 kit packages with positional argument reads and all 6 strict string-compare verb sites; this switch (argument_owned -> view_argument AfterVerb) closes most of that P0's remainder, so do them as one change in the post-TRAIN43 train.")
inl tibia_knight_turn_rec () = Task ("TIBIA-KNIGHT-TURN-REC", "tibia hunting_pack.spi:2130 knight_turn_shared: drop the stray ^ that rig's rec-cycle standards rule now flags", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,team:tibia,standards,spiral-style", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_knight_turn_rec () = Planning ("TIBIA-KNIGHT-TURN-REC", Minutes 20u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_knight_turn_rec_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-KNIGHT-TURN-REC", 1u32, "2026-11-09T13:28Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: hunting_pack.spi:2130 reads `:~ knight_turn_shared ...` (no ^), and the C, Rust and Wgsl outputs for the knight_turn tests are byte-identical before vs after. Next step: drop the ^ and byte-compare per backend. Why it is safe: `:~` is already a join point, i.e. a shared, non-inlined function. `^` only adds rec, and compiler measured on 11-09 (REC-MARKER-HEAL n22) that since pack63 a ^ on a definition that never refers to itself changes no codegen. So the no-inline intent lives in `:~`, not in the ^. Filed by org2 from REC-MARKER-HEAL.")
inl note_of_tibia_knight_turn_rec_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-KNIGHT-TURN-REC", 2u32, "2026-11-09T14:48Z", "tibia", "Evidence: 11-09 10:5x tibia, ganymede job-1794234831503-tibia-knight-rec on pack77 (core 9ef0395b). hunting_pack.spi now reads `:~ knight_turn_shared (b : beat) (t : tactic) (p : pack) : pack = knight_turn_inline b t p` (no ^; the body never refers to itself). The same compiler session built apps/predict/predict.spi (which runs knight_turn every tick) with and without the ^: C IDENTICAL (sha 839ba1ae4cfe7f5b, 4310295 bytes), Rust IDENTICAL (sha b2a1e565cdaed0d6, 3843994 bytes). WGSL: no tibia test targets wgsl with knight_turn (grep: hunting_pack.spi has no ///> wgsl rows; nothing outside it calls knight_turn), and knight_turn's Wgsl arm calls knight_turn_inline, so knight_turn_shared (the only changed definition) cannot appear in any Wgsl output. The job's wgsl line compared lanes_gpu.spi, which is not a Wgsl entry (TyArrayLiteral unsupported), so it produced no files and is not evidence either way.")
inl note_of_tibia_knight_turn_rec_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-KNIGHT-TURN-REC", 3u32, "2026-11-09T14:51Z", "tibia", "Proof: ganymede job-1794234831503-tibia-knight-rec, C and Rust byte-identical with vs without the ^ (note 2).")
inl rig_ci_status_contract () = Task ("RIG-CI-STATUS-CONTRACT", "rig CI red on every push since at least 11-06: contract test typed_handoff_is_readable_and_versionless expects kit status to print spiral_first=true, but status now prints train/gate facts", TaskKind, P1, D2, 70u32, Active, "", "kit,ci,contracts,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_ci_status_contract () = Planning ("RIG-CI-STATUS-CONTRACT", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_ci_status_contract_1 () = Note ("RIG-CI-STATUS-CONTRACT", 1u32, "2026-11-09T14:06Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "Found 11-09 10:1x by microblog (groom; read-only gh plus local runs). i574n/rig gh-pages workflow: the last 4 push runs failed (11-06 02:12, 11-06 10:29, 11-08 23:07, 11-09 02:30); both OS jobs fail in 'pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1' -> build.ps1 -Test -CompilerContracts -> 'Native Spiral developer workflow failed (exit 101)'. Failing test (ubuntu, run 42551351888): typed_handoff_is_readable_and_versionless panicked at rig_contracts/contracts.rs:427 (source src/contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi:523): assert surface.contains(spiral_first=true) && !surface.contains(alpha=) && help contains 'usage: kit' && unknown fails; 14 passed, 1 failed. Clause check on the installed kit (11-08): help has 'usage: kit' (ok); 'kit unknown' exits 2 (ok); 'kit status' prints 'kit status missing train source=...', 'missing gate source=...', 'kit status ok facts=0 missing=2', with NO spiral_first=true. That is the failing clause. HEAD still has the old surface in src/rig_cli/kit.rs:44/82/83 and rig_cli_routing/routing_terminal.spi:42 ('rig status ok migration=... spiral_first=true ...'), but the routed status verb is now the train/gate facts one. dod: the contract matches the status verb that ships (assert the facts receipt, or route the legacy surface under its own word), CI green on both OS. next: decide which status surface is canonical; update cli_driver.spi:523 and regenerate contracts.rs. typefeatures: none needed.")
inl note_of_rig_ci_status_contract_2 () = Note ("RIG-CI-STATUS-CONTRACT", 2u32, "2026-11-09T14:12Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 10:1x local rig, DECIDED + FIXED (unstaged, unproven). Canonical status surface = the routed rig_status_facts verb (receipt \"rig status ok facts=N missing=M\" plus one \"rig status missing <fact> source=<path>\" line per missing fact; exit 0 even when facts are missing, which is why only the substring clause failed). The spiral_first=true line in rig_cli_routing/routing_terminal.spi (42, 80-81) is the old eoie migration receipt; nothing routes to it. Fix: contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi:523 typed_handoff_is_readable_and_versionless now asserts surface.contains(\"status ok facts=\") (holds under both the kit and rig output prefixes and on a CI runner with no train facts); the help \"usage: kit\" and unknown-exits-nonzero clauses are unchanged. Proof: the CI compiler-contracts leg (build.ps1 -Test -CompilerContracts) on the next push; nothing compiles on the box while the user is present. Follow-up for removal: the unrouted legacy status code in routing_terminal.spi (bold removals wanted) once CI is green.")
inl rig_task_creation_split () = Task ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", "split agile_task_creation (992/1000 generated lines) into a pure model and its IO entry, then switch its 4 host trims to lib sm'.trim", TaskKind, P2, D3, 80u32, Active, "RUST-STD-STRING-LOWERING", "kit,agile,granular,team:rig", "current", "current")
