inl note_of_rig_task_creation_split_1 () = Note ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", 1u32, "2026-11-09T14:07Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "DoD: task_creation crates both under 900 generated lines after the switch; the notes_cli/creation notebooks green. Next step: read task_creation.spi and move the pure flag/extras parsing (lines 60-160) into a model module.")
inl note_of_rig_task_creation_split_2 () = Note ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", 2u32, "2026-11-09T14:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 10:2x rig, compiler MEASURED on ganymede: lowered sm'.trim is 17 lines one-time program overhead + ~2 lines per extra call site (1 call 17, 4 calls 23; old lib trim 98 and 218). Switching task_creation's 4 host trims costs about +4 to +8 lines on 992/1000: 996-1000, at the gate edge that stopped TRAIN42 and TRAIN42c. ORDER: split first (margin), then switch in the same train.")
inl note_of_rig_task_creation_split_3 () = Note ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", 3u32, "2026-11-10T23:08Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal (help pool) 11-10 19:4x DESIGN READ, nothing drafted: the split needs rig's call. kit/src/agile_task_creation/task_creation.spi (242 lines) separates cleanly. PURE: task_binding, add_flag + flag_word/flag_words/flag_of_word, add_extras + no_extras/extras_with, flag_parse/extras_read unions, task_line, extras_receipt, task_id_byte_allowed + the i32 predicates. IO: extras_from (argv), author_settled/extras_checked (env RIG_AUTHOR/KIT_AUTHOR), agile_add (state file), agile_add_entry/main. The 4 host trims are at extras_with (note, author), author_settled and extras_receipt; trim_end_matches in agile_add is a 5th host string call. BLOCKER: the DoD says both task_creation CRATES stay under 900 generated lines, but a source-only model package (the agile_task_text pattern: model.spi + package.spiproj, no Cargo.toml) compiles INTO the consumer crate, so it would not shrink task_creation.rs. A real second crate means the entry calls it through a new host call (the agile_task_notes::rig_agile_groomed pattern plus a Cargo path dep), which kit's AGENTS.md forbids outside the OS boundary package. Options: (a) a model crate exported through a sanctioned boundary primitive; (b) a source-only model plus cutting generated size another way (the trims through lib sm'.trim, whose one-time 17 lines rig measured); (c) relax the per-crate DoD to the entry crate. Next step: rig chooses a, b or c; fiscal can then draft the pure model (light) if rig wants help.")
inl note_of_rig_task_creation_split_4 () = Note ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", 4u32, "2026-11-10T23:16Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal (help pool) 11-10 20:0x DRAFT READY for rig to apply, per rig's linked-unit ruling. PROFILE of the current task_creation.rs (991 lines): agile_add_entry_0 = 567 (agile_add, task_line, extras_receipt and the success text all inline into it), extras_from 105, string_concat 96, flag_of_word 59, extras_checked 50, task_id_bytes_allowed 42. So the text building is what to move. DRAFT %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT\\: NEW linked unit agile_task_creation_text (Cargo.toml lib text.rs, package.spiproj core+spiral only, standards.spi copied from rig_units_edges = HostFree + LibReferenced, text.spi) exporting task_line and add_receipt, each one tuple of strings to string (tuple args link), built only on lib sm' and ++# (its own spi_quoted / spi_escaped, since agile_task_text.model has host calls), with tests a_task_line_quotes_its_texts and a_receipt_names_only_the_given_extras. ENTRY (.base kept for each): task_creation.spi 242 -> 200 lines, rust_std_string uses 23 -> 6; task_line now builds a row and calls the unit; extras_receipt removed; agile_add_success uses add_receipt; agile_add's append migrated from concat5 to ++#; the three host trims (extras_with note and author, author_settled) now lib sm'.trim; sm'_operators opened. package.spiproj lists the unit under packages AND link; Cargo.toml gains the path dep; workspace-Cargo.toml adds the member. NOT VERIFIED: no build or gate ran (generated line counts need a cargo build on a node), and the trim_end_matches in agile_add stays host (its lib form needs a char list). OPEN for rig: which BUILT crate must also list the unit (rig_agile_mutation depends on agile_task_creation; rig_agile_gap lists it as a package). Next step: rig applies, builds, and reads both crate sizes against the 900 DoD.")
inl note_of_rig_task_creation_split_5 () = Note ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", 5u32, "2026-11-10T23:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal (help pool) 11-10 20:1x per rig: only rig_agile_gap also needs the unit, because it INLINES agile_task_creation (packages without link) while rig_agile_mutation only has a Cargo dep on the built crate. Added drafts\\kit\\RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT\\rig_agile_gap\\package.spiproj (agile_task_creation_text under packages and link) and Cargo.toml (path dep), each with .base. The draft set is complete; fiscal hands the item back to rig. Next step: rig applies the set, measures both crate sizes on moon, and it rides TRAIN44.")
inl note_of_rig_task_creation_split_6 () = Note ("RIG-TASK-CREATION-SPLIT", 6u32, "2026-11-10T23:27Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 19:4x rig: fiscal's draft APPLIED to the kit tree (unstaged; all 6 bases equal the live files, 10 files copied and hash-checked, pre-apply copies archived at kit\\archive\\rig-task-creation-split-pre-apply-20261110) plus Cargo.lock (the agile-task-creation-text package and its edges from agile-task-creation and rig-agile-gap). Proof so far: the new linked unit agile_task_creation_text/text.spi passes 2/2 on the Cells notebook gate (ganymede); regen-sizes on moon (job-1794353037149): agile_task_creation 896 (was 991), agile_task_creation_text 123, rig_agile_gap 790 (was 858), 0 over 1000, so the DoD under 900 for both task_creation crates is met. The consumers (agile_task_creation, rig_agile_gap link the unit) are provable only on a train: TRAIN44. Thanks to fiscal for the profile (agile_add_entry_0 567 of 991 lines) and the draft.")
