inl note_of_kit_standards_ecosystem_m1_1 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM-M1", 1u32, "2026-11-09T14:29Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM by kit agile split (milestone 1). DoD: RepoEntry rule init.ps1 + workflow.ps1 are the only CI entries, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_ecosystem_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T14:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:2x local rig, CENSUS (read-only, every git repo under the box's git root; forks and upstream mirrors such as atrium, leptos, zed, nearcore, wasmer, rustix, plotters, livebook, forgottenserver, otclient keep their own CI and are OUT of scope: the rule applies only where a root standards.spi opts in). COMPLIANT (scripts/init.ps1 + scripts/workflow.ps1, single gh-pages.yml): 19 = alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, eoie, fc1943s.github, fonts, fork-spiral-patch, html, i574n.github, kit, mechahaze-album1, polyglot, regex, spiral, tapas2, tibia, vault, x. PARTIAL (init.ps1 but no workflow.ps1; YAML calls init/build/publish directly): fiscal (init, build, publish), currency_converter (init, build, flyctl deploy). LEGACY (neither script): azeroth, fc1943s.github.io, i574n.github.io (echo set-output pages-only, deprecated ::set-output), calc-parser (pwsh test.ps1 at repo root), cumbuquia (inline mix deps.get/credo/dialyzer), dotfiles (echo build), tictactoe (root init.ps1 + dotnet paket; dist.yml with inline perl). NO CI: microblog. RULE SHAPE (one finding union, each with the fix printed): MissingInit, MissingWorkflow, StepBypassesWorkflow (file, command); a repo opts in by its root standards.spi. Rollout order by drift: fiscal and currency_converter are one-file fixes (a workflow.ps1 that runs the existing init/build/publish), then the legacy pages repos.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_ecosystem_m1_3 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-09T14:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:3x local rig, RULE MODEL BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): new package src/rig_standards_repo (repo_entry.spi, pure, HostFree; separate from rig_standards, which microblog holds for KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS). repo_facts { has_init; has_workflow; steps : list workflow_step { file; command } } -> entry_finding list: MissingInit | MissingWorkflow | StepBypassesWorkflow step (a run step that does not go through scripts/workflow.ps1, either slash); finding_text names the rule and the fix. Test covers the compliant shape and the fiscal shape from the census. NEXT STEP after the probe: the IO half (read .github/workflows/*.yml run: lines and the two script paths) and the opt-in by root standards.spi, routed from kit standards <repo>.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_ecosystem_m1_4 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM-M1", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The first probe was red and is fixed (unstaged): its test literal lost a backslash to the Bash transport (scripts\\workflow.ps1 became scripts<w>orkflow); fixed with Edit; re-probed green. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_ecosystem_m1_5 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ECOSYSTEM-M1", 5u32, "2026-11-09T21:42Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, IO HALF BUILT and proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (repo_io 1/1, repo_entry 1/1): src/rig_standards_repo/repo_io.spi (HostFree; files through the rig_os_files boundary, entry_names, and lib file_system). steps_of file text turns a workflow file into workflow_step rows: a \"- run: cmd\" or \"run: cmd\" line is one step, and a \"run: |\" (or >) block becomes ONE step whose command is its more-indented lines joined by \"; \" (blank lines inside the block skipped); recursion over lines is join points (:~ ^), per today's EJP0011 lesson. repo_facts_of root reads scripts/init.ps1 and scripts/workflow.ps1 presence and every .github/workflows/*.yml|yaml. Test: a three-step workflow (a run line, a run block, an echo) gives the three commands and entry_findings names the two that bypass scripts/workflow.ps1. NEXT STEP: route it from kit standards <repo> behind the opt-in row in the root standards.spi; that edits the shared standards entry, so after TRAIN43 snapshots.")
