inl note_of_kit_do_slop_gate_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T14:37Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:0x local rig, BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): new linked-unit package src/rig_do_slop (slop.spi, pure, HostFree, standards 0 findings), shaped like rig_do_replacement because do_edit.rs is 951/1000 generated lines and cannot take the check inline. slop_finding union ConsNilSpelled line | LineTooWide (line, width); judges ONLY lines the edit adds (a line of the new text not present in the old text), so untouched legacy lines are never refused; only .spi/.spir paths; width 120 (the kit standards width; M2 can read the package standards.spi). Cons/Nil match whole words only (NilLike, Consensus pass). Exported as rig_do_slop_problem (path, before, after) -> \"\" or \"line 3 spells Cons/Nil: write :: and []; line 4 is 127 columns, over 120\". NEXT STEP after the probe: wire it into rig_do_edit file_result_of beside group_problem (link + Cargo dep + workspace member + lock) as a refusal, and the accept row in M4.")
inl note_of_kit_do_slop_gate_m1_3 () = Note ("KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_do_slop_gate_m1_4 () = Note ("KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M1", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE: the milestone is the added-text checks for Cons/Nil spelled out and long lines (src/rig_do_slop/slop.spi): proof: its notebook gate passed on ganymede (whole-word Cons/Nil, NilLike and Consensus pass, width over 120 named per line). Wiring into rig_do_edit as a refusal is the next milestone's step.")
inl note_of_kit_do_slop_gate_m1_5 () = Note ("KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M1", 5u32, "2026-11-09T21:36Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:4x tibia (help pool), THE IO HALF DRAFTED for rig's train (kit is rig's; not applied): drafts\\kit\\KIT-DO-SLOP-GATE-M1\\. (1) rig_do_edit\\run.spi: new slop_refusal path before after = rig_do_slop.slop.slop_problem (path, before, after), prefixed 'slop in <path>: ' when non-empty. file_result_of binds it once and refuses AFTER the existing checks (problem, untouched, emptied), so a clean edit, an untouched file and a non-.spi path behave exactly as before; only added .spi/.spir lines are judged (the model's rule). (2) rig_do_edit\\package.spiproj: rig_do_slop under packages and link. (3) rig_do_edit\\Cargo.toml: rig-do-slop = { path = ../rig_do_slop }. (4) src\\Cargo.toml: rig_do_slop as a workspace member after rig_do_replacement (it was not a member). Bases: rig_do_edit\\run.spi base B846A617119D; rig_do_edit\\package.spiproj base 9AAA339ED999; rig_do_edit\\Cargo.toml base 56D200A37E21; Cargo.toml base 29E20D48878A. LEFT for rig: regen + Cargo.lock + the do_edit.rs generated-line count (it was 951/1000; the call adds about 6 lines) + the train.")
