inl note_of_node_proof_linux_target_1 () = Note ("NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET", 1u32, "2026-11-09T15:01Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 11:5x rig REQUEST with evidence: node-proof.ps1 hard-codes Windows-style stage paths and syncs through the Windows node alias (-JobMachine only changes where the job starts), so every notebook probe queues on moon. Today moon held TRAIN42e (277 notebooks, ~4 h) plus two other lanes' jobs at 100 pct CPU, while ganymede sat at load 2.4 of 4 cores; rig's probe batch (26 notebooks of unprobed models) waited the whole morning. DoD: node-proof -JobMachine ganymede runs a one-notebook probe end to end (sync, run, summary) with the same Pattern verdict lines. Next step: map the stage and mirror roots per machine (Windows: C:\\home\\remote\\<name>; Linux: /home/remote/<name>) from the existing node aliases.")
inl note_of_node_proof_linux_target_2 () = Note ("NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET", 2u32, "2026-11-09T16:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 12:2x DRAFT (scratch, not applied): node-proof.ps1 with -JobMachine selecting the machine for sync, staging, hash checks, fetch, summary and remove; paths from the machine's remote-machines.json entry (mirrorBase, stage, kind=linux for the / separator); node keeps the node-env values. Linux: no scoop PATH line; -Summary reads XDG_CACHE_HOME or ~/.cache/kit/jobs (kit's Linux job dir, verified on ganymede); -Remove uses Get-Process CommandLine plus rm -rf (no symlink following); scp drops HostName when nothing resolves. Parses clean, +35/-20. Tested from scratch: -Summary on ganymede and node (node output unchanged), -Remove on an absent ganymede mirror. Untested: sync + job start (needs the real scripts dir). No caller passes -JobMachine today. Asked org to approve applying it and running the DoD one-notebook probe on ganymede.")
inl note_of_node_proof_linux_target_3 () = Note ("NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET", 3u32, "2026-11-09T16:58Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 12:4x APPLIED with org's approval (unstaged, scripts/node-proof.ps1 8D1CC868751F) and run end to end on ganymede: sync REMOTE-SYNC-OK, staging and hash checks ok, kit job start ok (held on full slots, then woke and ran 278 s), -Summary read ~/.cache/kit/jobs, -Remove deleted the mirror (109 GB free). The one-notebook probe (lib_gate doc_text.spi) exited 2, nothing ran, for an ENVIRONMENTAL reason: ganymede's base /home/remote/git/spiral is an empty git-init repo (only .git), so remote.ps1 sync has no deps to link; the mirror lacked deps/The-Spiral-Language and apps/cells/deps (mix: kino missing). Fix options sent to org: provision base deps once by copy, or a per-machine deps source in remote-machines.json. Second gap on both OSes: -Remove leaves the worktree registration (prunable); pruned on ganymede by hand, proposed a prune step. DoD remaining: rerun the probe after deps are provisioned.")
inl note_of_node_proof_linux_target_4 () = Note ("NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET", 4u32, "2026-11-10T10:11Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 cleared the lane:org wait: ganymede is provisioned (europa deps copied via box relay - deps/The-Spiral-Language 90M with VS Code Plugin, apps/cells/deps 5.5M, lib/spiral 2.2M/131 spi, worktree pruned). fiscal signaled to rerun the one-notebook DoD probe for end-to-end confirmation.")
