inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m1_2 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:10Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 12:1x local rig, REBUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch) the record/replay store lost in the 10-28 wipe, as src/rig_convo_replay/replay.spi (pure, HostFree, standards 0). turn union System | User | Assistant | Call (name, arguments) | Result value; record folds a transcript with a stack of open calls (Call pushes a call_key, Result pops the innermost: LIFO, as the 10-19 design), producing exchanges in order plus typed record_problem rows: OrphanResult at-turn and UnansweredCall key (the type-indexed protocol that rejects these at compile time still waits on GADT-GROWING-INDEX-HANG, so this is the runtime form). replay exchanges key returns the latest recorded result or None. Test: two calls split by a user turn replay exactly, other arguments miss, nested calls pair innermost first, an orphan result and an unanswered call are both named. NEXT (M2): persist exchanges as JSON lines through lib json.")
inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m1_3 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
