inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m2_2 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-09T21:58Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:1x tibia (help pool): GREEN, ready for rig's train (kit is rig's; not applied). drafts\\kit\\CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M2\\replay.spi (base A15C03951C04; the package is otherwise unchanged) appends: exchange_row { name; arguments; result }; exchange_line (json.quote per field, one object per line); to_lines; exchange_of (a TYPED json.decode straight into exchange_row, the first json.decode use in kit); of_lines (blank lines skipped in a fold). Test: two exchanges, one whose arguments hold escaped quotes and a newline, round-trip to_lines |> of_lines equal to the input, a replay after the round trip finds the escaped call, and blank input holds no exchanges. Gate on ganymede in rig's probe layout (job tibia-convo, rig-probe's box lib): Cells 2/2 passed (M1's test + this one). Widths <= 120, no comments (package standards). NEXT (M3 or the IO half): read/write the lines file through file_system at the kit boundary.")
inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m2_3 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M2", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:58Z", "tibia", "TypeFeatures: a JSON line decodes straight into the exchange_row record type (json.decode \\* t. typed by the binding), so a renamed or missing field fails in the decoder instead of yielding an empty string.")
inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m2_4 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M2", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:03Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig APPLIED tibia's draft (drafts\\kit\\CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M2\\replay.spi; a pure append to src/rig_convo_replay/replay.spi, no existing line changed, unstaged; hash equal after copy; kit standards 0 findings). DONE: exchanges persist as JSON lines through the lib json codec: to_lines writes {\"name\",\"arguments\",\"result\"} with json.quote, of_lines reads each line with a typed json.decode into exchange_row, blank lines hold nothing. proof: tibia's gate 2/2 on ganymede in rig's probe layout (job tibia-convo), a round trip with escaped quotes and a newline, and replay still finding the escaped call after loading. Caveat for later: json.decode has no failure case, so a malformed or torn line is not reported as such; KIT-TABLE-JSONL's framing model (probe-green) is the check to put in front of of_lines when real transcripts are loaded.")
