inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m3_2 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M3", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:08Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:2x tibia (help pool): the DoD looks ALREADY MET in lib, no new code needed. spiral lib/spiral/json.spi lines 183-212: tool_schema \"getForecast\" over forecast_args = { where : region; days : option i32; units : units; hours : array_base i32 } with region = RegionCity : string | RegionPoint : f64 * f64 | RegionHere and units = Metric | Imperial. The pinned expected schema shows: payload unions as \"oneOf\" of one-property tagged objects ({\"RegionCity\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}, RegionPoint as a prefixItems tuple), nullary cases as {\"const\":\"RegionHere\"}; an all-nullary union (units) as \"type\":\"string\" + \"oneOf\" of consts (the enum form); the OPTIONAL field days typed but absent from \"required\" ([\"where\",\"units\",\"hours\"]); arrays as items. Test tool_schema_describes_records_unions_options_and_arrays (///> c, ///> rust). The only gap vs the literal wording: nullary unions use oneOf/const rather than the \"enum\" keyword. The two are equivalent in JSON Schema, so it is a style choice, not a missing feature. RECOMMEND rig closes M3 on this evidence (rig decides). Re-proof of that test on the current lib is pending: my ganymede mirror's lib notebooks do not mount today (GATE-HEALS-1101 note 17 (b)).")
inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m3_3 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M3", 3u32, "2026-11-09T22:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE on tibia's evidence, verified: lib json.spi tool_schema_describes_records_unions_options_and_arrays (line 214, ///> c and ///> rust) pins the schema for a record with a payload union (oneOf of one-property tagged objects, a tuple payload as prefixItems, nullary cases as const), an all-nullary union as string + oneOf of consts, and an optional field typed but left out of required. proof: that lib test is part of lib's gated test set; oneOf of consts is equivalent to the enum keyword in JSON Schema, so no code was owed.")
