inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m4_2 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M4", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:32Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE (unstaged, src/rig_convo_replay/replay.spi): the decoder is now type-directed INTO THE SAME RECORD. M2 decoded each JSON line into a flat exchange_row and copied fields into exchange; now exchange_line writes the record's own nested shape {\"call\":{\"name\":...,\"arguments\":...},\"result\":...} and exchange_of is just json.decode line : exchange (the lib decoder follows the record's type, nested records included, as lib json.spi decode_reads_nested_records shows), and exchange_row is gone. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (replay 2/2): the round trip with escaped quotes and a newline in the arguments, and replay still finding the escaped call after loading. Still open for real transcripts: json.decode has no failure case, so the JSONL framing check (KIT-TABLE-JSONL) goes in front of of_lines; noted on M2.")
