inl note_of_convo_in_spiral_m5_2 () = Note ("CONVO-IN-SPIRAL-M5", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:43Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE (unstaged; inside src/rig_convo_replay/replay.spi): the .convo surface syntax reader for the MVP the corpus mining fixed (> user 270 files, > assistant 215, > system 75, > define 94, recorded > call 30 / > result 29, @tags such as @model / @time / @tokenUsage). blocks_of text reads each \"> role\" header and its body up to the next header (blank edges trimmed) into block_reading = TurnBlock (turn, tags) | DefineBlock (body, tags) | UnknownHeader (line, header); \"> call name(args)\" becomes Call (name, body), @tag lines attach to the block after them, an unknown header is named with its line number (never dropped). turns_of feeds the store's own turn union, so record + replay run straight on a .convo file. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (replay module 3/3): five turns from a seven-block file, the call's name and body, a define kept apart, an unknown header at line 15, a tag on the call block, and replay answering the recorded call. Notes: it lives in the replay module because a separate surface module could not open replay (ETY-UnboundModule, the module name collides with its replay function); the first probe also caught an eager substring on short headers, fixed by computing the call name only in the call branch.")
inl perf_study_5_print_quantum () = Task ("PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", "bench_model: a plan field for the print unit, so sub-10 us rows print in ns instead of sitting at the 3-decimal ms quantum", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "team:org,perf,bench,lib,regex", "current", "current")
