inl note_of_perf_study_5_print_quantum_1 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", 1u32, "2026-11-09T15:15Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: lib bench_model.spi gains a typed print unit chosen from the spread (e.g. unit_of spread = Ns | Us | Ms by magnitude, at least ~1000 quanta per printed value), regex's setup row prints through it, and a test pins 0.009 ms -> 9 us style output. Next step: add the unit union + unit_of to bench_model (a lib draft, landed via the node-proof route), then switch regex's setup_line. Source: tibia's PERF-STUDY-4 timed A1/B/A2 run, where sub-10 us rows sit at the print quantum.")
inl note_of_perf_study_5_print_quantum_2 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:30Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 15:3x DRAFTED (drafts\\spiral\\PERF-STUDY-5\\bench_model.spi, base 2D56BEE1AA08, budget clean): time_unit = Nanos | Micros | Millis; unit_of ms = Millis when >= 1 ms, Micros when >= 1 us, else Nanos (the largest unit where the value is >= 1, so a 3-decimal print keeps >= 1000 quanta); in_unit, unit_name; 2 rust tests on binary-exact values (1.5/0.5/0.0005 -> Millis/Micros/Nanos; 0.5 ms -> 500 us, 0.25 ms -> 250 us, 0.0005 ms -> \"ns\"). Then regex setup_line prints milli_text (in_unit u x) ++ unit_name u. Wait: its lib proof uses the ganymede exact-copy tree, which the running regex build (org2-swap) reads, so it proves right after that job.")
inl note_of_perf_study_5_print_quantum_3 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", 3u32, "2026-11-09T15:30Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "TypeFeatures: a closed union (time_unit = Nanos | Micros | Millis) chosen by magnitude, so a print unit is a typed choice, not a string suffix.")
inl note_of_perf_study_5_print_quantum_4 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", 4u32, "2026-11-09T17:20Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 17:2x LIB LANDED + consumer applied. Proof (ganymede exact tree, raw lib 6E2065C9D353B452 both sides after syncing env.spi + xsd_emit.spi that other lanes landed mid-way): job-1794244038842-org2-batch, lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply: apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26, type_probe PASS (7 tests typed), respell 0, LANDED and closed green, lib digest 085560A3E14B39D0 (= the box prediction from -DigestOnly); executing gate of the landed lib bench_model.spi 7/7 (incl. the_print_unit_keeps_a_thousand_quanta_per_value, a_value_scales_into_its_unit). Box: \"LANDED from a proven close\", undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261109-131817, box lib now 085560A3E14B39D0. bench_model.spi 73353E54D603 (unstaged). Consumer: regex/bench/bench.spi setup row now prints timed_text = milli_text (in_unit u ms) + unit_name u (live base 6cf7a8f9db7 matched; 8 diff lines; the ratio columns keep milli_text). Proof of the consumer: the next full regex build (org2-swap3).")
inl note_of_perf_study_5_print_quantum_5 () = Note ("PERF-STUDY-5-PRINT-QUANTUM", 5u32, "2026-11-09T17:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:0x CONSUMER PROVEN, DONE: ganymede job-1794244806602-org2-swap3 (full regex build.ps1 on the box-equal tree with the landed bench_model): REGEX-OK, Cells 122/122 over 21 files, and the setup rows now print through the typed unit: \"setup 14.086 us per certified table build (mean of 25), one array table pass 7.746 us (median)\" ... \"setup 189.070 ms ..., one array table pass 7.166 us\" ... \"setup 1473.284 ms ..., 8.294 us\" (before: 0.014 ms / 0.009 ms, i.e. 9 quanta). Every printed value now has >= 1000 quanta. Proof: that job's setup rows.")
inl rig_heal_junction_teardown () = Task ("RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN", "rig teardown unlinks junctions before any recursive delete: the delete guard detects a junction or reparse point inside the target (PS 5.1 Remove-Item -Recurse and cmd rmdir /s both follow them) and unlinks each with a non-following rmdir first, then deletes the tree", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,healing,self-healing,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_heal_junction_teardown () = Planning ("RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_heal_junction_teardown_1 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN", 1u32, "2026-11-09T15:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "filed 11-09 by rig from org''s NMR-HEAL-CATALOG [rig] entries. DoD: rig_delete_guard gains a typed junction_plan (Unlink paths, then Delete) and refuses to recurse while any junction remains; a test on a fixture tree with a junction to a sibling keeps the sibling intact. Seed: the 11-09 moon loss of the shared spiral deps (memory mirror-delete-follows-deps-junction). Related: CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN (the cells side).")
inl note_of_rig_heal_junction_teardown_2 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 13:5x local rig, PLAN MODEL BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): src/rig_delete_plan/plan.spi (pure, HostFree, standards 0; its own package because rig_delete_guard generates 810 lines). tree_entry PlainEntry | JunctionEntry (path); teardown_plan Teardown steps | RefusedTeardown reason; teardown_step UnlinkJunction path | RemoveTree path. teardown_of guard_refusal target entries: the delete guard's refusal comes first; a target that is itself a junction is ONLY unlinked; otherwise every junction inside is unlinked before RemoveTree. INVARIANT that catches the 11-09 moon loss: if the walk reports any entry below a junction, the walker followed the junction, so the plan REFUSES (\"the walk entered a junction and would delete through it\"); a sibling with a shared prefix (deps vs depsx) is not inside. Paths normalized to forward slashes. NEXT STEP after the probe: the IO half (a walker that lists reparse points without descending, the non-following unlink, then the remove) wired into proxy fs-remove-tree and the mirror teardown.")
inl note_of_rig_heal_junction_teardown_3 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The first probe was red and is fixed (unstaged): the test paths lost their backslashes to the Bash transport; fixed with Edit; re-probed green. The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_rig_heal_junction_teardown_4 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-JUNCTION-TEARDOWN", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig: parked on train:TRAIN43. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step adds a CLI verb or wires into shared kit code (rig do / job host / job list / proxy fs / agile entry), and TRAIN43 snapshots the live tree about 19:30 local, so shared-code edits wait until it has snapshotted and go into a post-TRAIN43 train with their own regen and crate-gate proof.")
inl rig_heal_reap_by_label () = Task ("RIG-HEAL-REAP-BY-LABEL", "rig self-reap by label: a poller or watcher re-checks that its own label still owns the job before submitting, and a leftover with a dead owner is reaped by exact label, never by a command-line match that can hit the caller's own shell", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,healing,self-healing,team:rig", "current", "current")
