inl note_of_rig_heal_reap_by_label_1 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-REAP-BY-LABEL", 1u32, "2026-11-09T15:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "filed 11-09 by rig from org''s NMR-HEAL-CATALOG [rig] entries. DoD: one typed label_owner check used by job pollers before every submit, and job reap --label <l> that excludes its own process tree; test: a stale poller stops instead of resubmitting. Seed memories: taskstop-leaves-gitbash-loop-alive, remote-kill-by-cmdline-hits-own-shell. Shares classes with KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS (rig_job_escaped).")
inl note_of_rig_heal_reap_by_label_2 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-REAP-BY-LABEL", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:3x local rig, MODEL BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_heal_reap/reap.spi (pure, HostFree). (1) submit_decision me registry: a poller may submit only while the registry row for its label is its own (same pid and start time); a newer owner gives StopTakenOver owner, and a missing row gives StopUnregistered, never a blind resubmit (the TaskStop-leaves-the-loop-alive lesson). (2) reap_targets label processes own: EXACT label equality (rig-probe never matches rig-probe-2) and never any pid in the caller's own process tree (tree_of walks children from the caller), the remote-kill-by-cmdline-hits-own-shell lesson. Test covers all three submit verdicts and a reap that spares the caller's child and the similarly named label. NEXT: the IO half: label rows from the job registry, process rows with their job labels from rig_jobs, and a job reap --label verb.")
inl note_of_rig_heal_reap_by_label_3 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-REAP-BY-LABEL", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_rig_heal_reap_by_label_4 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-REAP-BY-LABEL", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:08Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig: parked on train:TRAIN43. The model is probe-green; the recorded next step adds a CLI verb or wires into shared kit code (rig do / job host / job list / proxy fs / agile entry), and TRAIN43 snapshots the live tree about 19:30 local, so shared-code edits wait until it has snapshotted and go into a post-TRAIN43 train with their own regen and crate-gate proof.")
inl rig_heal_tunnel_verify () = Task ("RIG-HEAL-TUNNEL-VERIFY", "rig self-verifies a remote-only node's tunnel before and after any change and never restarts sshd there: a probe of the reverse tunnel decides Healthy | Degraded | Down and the heal is to re-establish the tunnel half, not the daemon", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,healing,self-healing,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_heal_tunnel_verify () = Planning ("RIG-HEAL-TUNNEL-VERIFY", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_heal_tunnel_verify_1 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-TUNNEL-VERIFY", 1u32, "2026-11-09T15:44Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "filed 11-09 by rig from org''s NMR-HEAL-CATALOG [rig] entries. DoD: a typed tunnel_state from a bounded probe (ConnectTimeout) and a refusal of any sshd restart on a node marked remote-only; test with a fake probe. Seed memories: never-restart-sshd-on-remote-only-node, reverse-tunnel-orphan-half. Related: KIT-NET-LINK.")
inl note_of_rig_heal_tunnel_verify_2 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-TUNNEL-VERIFY", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:2x local rig, MODEL BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): src/rig_heal_tunnel/tunnel.spi (pure, HostFree, standards 0). node_access RemoteOnly | LocalConsole; probe_result { connected; exit_code; elapsed_ms } from a bounded probe -> tunnel_state Healthy | Degraded ms (connected but over 15 s: reported, not healed) | Down reason; heal_for maps Down to ReestablishTunnel only; decided access action makes the never-restart-sshd rule a TYPE decision: RemoteOnly + RestartSshd is Refused (\"it is the only way in\"), a node with a console may restart it, and the tunnel heal is always allowed. Test covers each state and both refusal sides. NEXT: the IO half: the probe through the node alias with ConnectTimeout (the connecttimeout memory: 12 s or more under box starvation), and the reverse-tunnel re-establish as SYSTEM (persistent-reverse-tunnel-as-system).")
inl note_of_rig_heal_tunnel_verify_3 () = Note ("RIG-HEAL-TUNNEL-VERIFY", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
