inl note_of_kit_fold_process_health_1 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-PROCESS-HEALTH", 1u32, "2026-11-09T15:46Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: each of the 5 scripts has a kit machine verb with the same output fields (or a superset), its scheduled task points at the verb, and the .ps1 is archived. Next step: diff each script's output columns against kit machine watch's and list the missing ones. TypeFeatures: a process finding as a union (Orphan | Duplicate | Stale of age) instead of text lines.")
inl note_of_kit_fold_process_health_2 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-PROCESS-HEALTH", 2u32, "2026-11-09T15:55Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 14:1x local rig, OUTPUT DIFF DONE (the recorded next step; read-only over i574n.github/scripts). Mapping, script -> kit home -> what kit lacks: (1) orphan-reaper.ps1 (54 lines; kills processes of classes dotnet/node/cargo/rustc/erl/beam/epmd older than 60 min whose parent is dead, with their children) -> rig_job_escaped (KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS, built 11-09): its Leaked class is the same rule (dead parent, past the grace, no live child or connection) and it never reaps protected names (RustDesk, sshd, explorer, winlogon, services). LACKS: the toolchain class allowlist (kit reaps any Leaked name; the script only toolchains: kit should adopt the allowlist as a typed reap_scope, the safer default) and the IO reap verb. (2) dangling-census.ps1 (39; open items flagged BLOCKED / PAUSED / PAUSED-NO-RESUME / PAUSED-BY-RULE, StaleDays 3) -> kit agile lint already checks BlockerNamed and PauseResume per item; LACKS: a one-line census summary (\"open N; flagged M\") and the staleness-by-days flag: a lint --census mode. (3) host-dupes-census.ps1 (26; host-macro definitions whose bodies repeat across packages) -> rig_code_dup (built 11-09, unprobed) finds duplicate definitions; LACKS a host-macro-only filter. (4) node-watch.ps1 (37; every 75 s logs cpu=N% node-jobs=N plus idle/under flags for one machine) -> kit machine watch + job list --on; LACKS: a --log interval mode on a remote machine. (5) node-utilization-monitor.ps1 (135; box saturated pct vs node idle pct, CSV time series, notes NODE-ALWAYS-FED when the node is wasted; its only kills are its own timed-out child) -> KIT-EXEC-METRICS (samples per label and machine) + machine watch; LACKS the cross-machine saturation verdict (Saturated | Wasted | Balanced) and the note-on-waste action. TypeFeatures as planned: process_finding Orphan | Duplicate | Stale age; plus reap_scope and fleet_balance unions. Next step: the reap_scope allowlist on rig_job_escaped (smallest, safety-positive), then the lint --census summary.")
inl note_of_kit_fold_process_health_3 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-PROCESS-HEALTH", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:09Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:3x local rig, THE RECORDED NEXT STEP DONE (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): reap_scope on rig_job_escaped/escaped.spi, the smallest safety-positive piece. reap_scope = OwnLabels labels | EveryOwner; in_scope refuses an empty owner under OwnLabels (an unlabelled process is never \"mine\"); may_reap scope owner facts = in scope AND not protected (rustdesk, sshd, explorer...) AND reapable by the existing class (SshForwarder | StoppedWatcher | Leaked). Test: own leaked process reaped, another lane's and an unlabelled one refused, the explicit fleet scope, and a process still inside the 60-min grace refused even under EveryOwner. NEXT: the lint --census summary (process_finding Orphan | Duplicate | Stale age), then the reap verb takes --scope mine by default and --scope fleet only for org.")
