inl note_of_kit_fold_job_running_2 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-JOB-RUNNING", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:59Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:3x local rig, CALLERS FOUND (the recorded next step): repos: only 2 org scripts call them: i574n.github/scripts/pause-plan.ps1:46 (job-stop.ps1) and pause-requeue.ps1:26 (queue-serial.ps1); scheduled tasks: none (Get-ScheduledTask action scan); memory: 6 files mention them (bg-shell-reap-off, lane-renames-2026-11-08, MEMORY.md, node-job-queued-for-slot, serial-runner-not-job-chains, test-ps1-mutex-per-cache-dir), to update when the scripts are archived. MAPPING (55 lines total): (1) serial-runner.ps1 (23; runs a JSON manifest of steps in order, heavy steps via spiral heavy.ps1 Invoke-Heavy after waiting out a live-gui block, logs, summary) -> kit job chain [--ok] --serial -- <label> <timeout> <program> ... -- ... (shipped; the memory serial-runner-not-job-chains already names it the one-call form). LACKS: a per-link heavy flag that routes the link through the heavy gate and waits out a live block. (2) queue-serial.ps1 (7; job start [--after] <label> <timeout> pwsh serial-runner.ps1 <manifest>) -> one job chain --serial call; pause-requeue.ps1 switches to it directly. (3) live-wait.ps1 (16; polls kit window list every 20 s for a live-gui row) -> belongs inside the heavy-link admission above, not a separate poller (no remote busy-poll, per the DoD). (4) job-stop.ps1 (9; kit job stop <id> guarded by an org-only label regex) -> kit job stop exists; LACKS the ownership refusal (ps kill --mine has one; job stop does not): a typed owner check (job author vs caller, --theirs to override) belongs in kit job stop, then pause-plan.ps1 calls it directly. NEXT: the heavy-link flag on job chain --serial, then the job stop owner check, then switch the 2 callers and archive the 4 scripts.")
