inl note_of_kit_fold_census_gate_2 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:52Z", "compiler", "11-09 compiler (help pool), STEP 1 DONE: ranked by callers. Method: git grep over spiral, kit, i574n.github, x, tibia, fiscal, regex (backlog text excluded), ~/.claude/hooks, and box scheduled-task arguments. RANK: (1) config-baseline (78 lines): scheduled task config-baseline-check (registered in register-scheduled-tasks.ps1:42), its log watched by heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1:11, and its output dir %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config-baseline mirrored by profile-mirror.ps1:25. (2) memory-integrity-sweep (67 lines): scheduled task memory-integrity-sweep, log watched by heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1:10. (3-6) crate-gate-all (18), banned-words-scan (41), bang-export-rewrite (118), recovered-drafts-census (70): ZERO callers in any repo, hook or scheduled task; run by hand from backlog notes only (banned-words-scan is BANNED-WORDS-SCANs tool). So: fold config-baseline and memory-integrity-sweep as kit verbs FIRST (callers to switch: one scheduled-task registration each plus the staleness-guard log names); the 4 zero-caller scripts are candidates to RETIRE with a reason (bang-export-rewrite = a one-shot migration if no ! exports remain; crate-gate-all = superseded if kits crate gate covers every repo) rather than fold. Nothing applied in rigs or orgs tree. Releasing my claim; rig owns the verbs.")
inl note_of_kit_fold_census_gate_3 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T18:01Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:0x local rig, FOLD #1 CORE BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch), following compiler's ranking: config-baseline first. src/rig_config_baseline/baseline.spi (pure, HostFree): baseline_row union FileRow (path, sha) | EnvRow (name, value) | DirSetRow (dir, names) | CompilerRow (kind, hash); config_drift union Changed | Missing | EnvChanged (name, before, now) | DirSetChanged | CompilerUnsanctioned; check_of baseline live newer_install -> { drift; sanctioned; checked }, keeping the script's rule that a compiler hash change is SANCTIONED when a newer compiler install exists, else unsanctioned drift. GENERIC by design: the script hard-codes this machine's personal paths (~/.ssh/config, scoop persist, Zed, Terminal), so the kit verb will read its target list from typed rows in the USER's config dir (never the repo, per repos-never-name-infra), and the snapshot store stays under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config-baseline so the profile mirror keeps working. DECISIONS on the 4 zero-caller scripts (compiler: no repo, hook or scheduled-task callers): RETIRE, not fold, each with its reason once checked: crate-gate-all (kit crate gate covers it if it runs per repo), bang-export-rewrite (a one-shot migration if no ! exports remain), banned-words-scan (the census banned-name-token word already counts it), recovered-drafts-census (a one-off recovery tool). NEXT: the IO verb rig config baseline snapshot|check, switch the scheduled task and the staleness guard's log name, then memory-integrity-sweep.")
inl note_of_kit_fold_census_gate_4 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE", 4u32, "2026-11-09T18:57Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:4x local rig, FOLD #2 MAPPED: memory-integrity-sweep.ps1 (67 lines; the second live script: scheduled task, log read by heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1:10). Its checks, mapped to kit: (a) per file: NO-FRONTMATTER, NO-NAME, NAME-MISMATCH (name: differs from the file stem), NO-DESCRIPTION, NO-TYPE -> rig_memory_typed's memory_of_text + kind_rule_met already parse these into a typed memory record; (b) index: INDEX-DEAD-LINK (a MEMORY.md link to a missing file) and ORPHAN (a file not linked from MEMORY.md), plus [[name]] links that resolve to no memory -> exactly KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M3 (dangling and orphan link report from the typed store), so this part is NOT new work; (c) NEW: DUP-CANDIDATE, 6-word shingle Jaccard >= 0.35 between two memories, and (d) the citation line it shells out to kit agile links --memory for. Fold plan: one rig memory check <dir> verb = memory_typed records + M3's link report + a shingle-similarity model for (c), emitting typed findings (the script's nine finding words as one union); then the scheduled task and the staleness guard's log name switch to it, and the .ps1 is archived. With config-baseline (fold #1, core built) that covers both live scripts; the 4 zero-caller scripts retire with reasons (note 3).")
inl note_of_kit_fold_census_gate_5 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE", 5u32, "2026-11-09T19:05Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 23:1x local rig, FOLD #2 NEW PART BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_memory_dupes/dupes.spi (pure, HostFree) = memory-integrity-sweep's DUP-CANDIDATE check, same numbers as the script: words = lower-cased [a-z0-9] runs, shingles = distinct 6-word runs, per-cent shared = intersection / union x 100, a pair is a DupCandidate (name, other, per-cent) at >= 35; bodies with no 6-word run are skipped (the script's Count -gt 0 guard). Test: the word split, two shingles from 7 words, a and b sharing 2 of 4 runs (50) found while an unrelated memory is not, and a too-short body forming no pair. Cost note for the IO half: contains-over-lists is quadratic per pair; at ~330 memories x ~150 shingles that is fine for a daily task, and the verb can switch to a sorted merge if it shows in the timing. Remaining for fold #2: the rig memory check verb that joins rig_memory_typed (per-file findings), KIT-MEMORY-MODEL-M3 (index and link findings) and this model, then the scheduled task switch.")
inl note_of_kit_fold_census_gate_6 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE", 6u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_fold_census_gate_7 () = Note ("KIT-FOLD-CENSUS-GATE", 7u32, "2026-11-09T22:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, FOLD #2 LOGIC JOINED (unstaged): src/rig_memory_check/check.spi (HostFree; packages rig_memory_typed + rig_memory_dupes). memory_finding union carries memory-integrity-sweep.ps1's finding kinds: NoFrontmatter | NoName | NameMismatch (file, declared name) | NoDescription | NoType (per file, from memory_of_text and field_in) | IndexDeadLink | Orphan (MEMORY.md links vs files on disk, only flat name.md links counted, as the script does) | Duplicate (a, b, per-cent) (from dup_candidates); memory_check index files returns them all in one list. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (check 1/1): a name/stem mismatch, a missing description, a file without frontmatter, a dead index link, an orphan, and a linked file not reported as orphan. kit standards 0, ratchet clean. NEXT: the rig memory check <dir> verb (read dir + MEMORY.md, print the findings and the citations line), then the scheduled task and the staleness guard switch to it and the .ps1 is archived; the verb edits the shared CLI entry, so after TRAIN43 snapshots.")
