inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:07Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 17:1x local rig, BASELINE (installed kit standards --census src, 629 packages, 93.9 s, 72,622 lines). Legacy constructs (total, largest package): rust-global 270 (contracts_entry 45), host-block 522 (rig_cli_check 25), host-statement 545, host-macro 891 (rust_std_fs 32), string-concat 427 (agile_todo_model 37), rc-wrap 440 (rig_cli_check 26), std-string-use 171 (agile_todo_model 45), top-level-macro 611 (rig_cli_model 43), encoded-row 134 (rig_machine_windows 14), forward-wrapper 97. Typed constructs: gadt-case 909 (bootstrap_policy 27), existential 373, verdict-union 101, nominal 669, type-decl 2036. TREND vs the 10-22 text counts: rust_global 386 -> 270 (-30 pct), Rc wraps 616 -> 440 (-29 pct); contracts_entry still holds the largest rust_global cluster (48 on 10-14 -> 45), so M6 targets it. Targets for M2-M5 from this table: the do statement algebra should move rig_cli_check's host blocks and agile_todo_model's string concat / std-string use, the top two non-contract clusters.")
