inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m2_1 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M2", 1u32, "2026-11-09T16:25Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE by kit agile split (milestone 2). DoD: statement effect GADT for the pure_read family in a model crate, indexed by receipt type, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m2_2 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 19:1x local rig, PURE_READ FAMILY BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the post-TRAIN42e probe batch): src/rig_do_algebra/read.spi (pure, HostFree). The statement GADT is indexed by its receipt type, following kit's own precedent (agile_task_query query_flag value): read_statement receipt = Show (path, first, last) -> read_statement shown | Search pattern -> read_statement found | Files suffix -> read_statement listed, with receipt records shown { path; first; lines }, found { pattern; hits : list hit { path; line; text } } and listed { suffix; paths }, and the existential any_read = \\? receipt. read_statement receipt for heterogeneous programs. run_read \\* receipt. files statement : receipt returns the receipt the statement's type names (so a Show can never yield a search receipt), over an in-memory tree_file list so it is testable without IO; statement_word gives the receipt verb. Test covers each case. The probe answers the open question: whether Spiral refines the return type per GADT arm here (the design depends on it). NEXT (M3): the staged_write family (Edit/Write/Copy with a staged_write receipt).")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m2_3 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M2", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m2_4 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M2", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:33Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE: the milestone is the statement effect GADT for the pure_read family in a model crate (src/rig_do_algebra/read.spi): proof: its notebook gate passed on ganymede (run_read returns the receipt each Show/Search/Files statement's type names), which also answers the design question this milestone carried: Spiral refines the return type per GADT arm. M3 (staged_write) continues in its own item.")
inl kit_idiomatic_core_m3 () = Task ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M3", "KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE milestone 3: the staged_write family with its receipts", TaskKind, P0, D1, 100u32, Done, "KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M2", "kit,one-call,adoption,team:rig", "current", "current")
