inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m4_1 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M4", 1u32, "2026-11-09T16:25Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE by kit agile split (milestone 4). DoD: the external_effect family with existential process and job handles, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_idiomatic_core_m4_2 () = Note ("KIT-IDIOMATIC-CORE-M4", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:01Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE (unstaged): src/rig_do_algebra/external.spi, the external_effect family beside read and write. TYPEFEATURES: job_handle = JobHandle of an EXPLICIT existential (\\? h. h * (h -> string)), so a process pid (u64) and a kit job id (string) live in one list of handles and only their rendering escapes; external_statement receipt GADT: RunProgram -> ran { program; code; output }, StartJob -> started { label; handle }, WaitJob handle -> settled, StopJob handle -> stopped; run_external host statement interprets through an external_host capability record { run; start; wait; stop }, so the real process boundary (rig_os_launch / rig_os_run) plugs in as one host and tests use a fake one. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (external 1/1): a run receipt, a pid handle and a job-id handle rendered from one list, a settled wait, a stop. Trap found: Spiral has no implicit existentials (ETY-GadtImplicitExistential: a :: case binding a type its result does not mention drops the whole union); the payload must be packed as (\\? h. ...) and opened with := \\? h. ... = payload.")
