inl regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality () = Task ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", "regex absorbs the mega sample's indexed_dfa_state_cardinality model (39 existentials, 32 GADT cases, 17 indexed unions): indexed unions into regex typed.spi, evidence into witness.spi", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "regex,typefeatureset,mega-sample,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality () = Planning ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_1 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 1u32, "2026-11-09T17:38Z", "tibia", "Child of REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE (plan (b), approved by org2 11-09 13:3x). DoD: the model's typed techniques live in regex/src typed.spi (indexed unions) and witness.spi (evidence), drafted under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY and applied by org2; regex build green on ganymede (/home/remote/org2-phys/regex, total = 118 + the new tests); every new cell within the 272 budget; no new module unless the concern is new. TypeFeatures: existentials and indexed unions move from the sample into the product repo.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_2 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 2u32, "2026-11-09T17:43Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:5x tibia: SLICE 1 DRAFTED (the compiled core). Reading the model (indexed_dfa_state_cardinality main.spi:402-470) against lib fin_vector shows its bespoke GADTs are instances of lib's generic vector n el / fin n: indexed_dfa_target_row s r = vector s (fin r), indexed_dfa_target_matrix s src r = vector src (vector s (fin r)), indexed_dfa_acceptance_vector n = vector n bool, and packed_* = an existential over the state count (lib some_vector's shape). So the absorption reuses lib generics instead of copying ~1500 lines. Draft (regex typed.spi base 08EB59597B2C, which already opens fin_vector and uses n1..n16): `:== sized_dfa s n = { start : fin n; accepting : vector n bool; targets : vector n (vector s (fin n)) }` (a transition can only name a state the DFA has), `:| some_sized_dfa s = SomeSizedDfa : (\\? n. sized_dfa s n)` (the size hidden, the model's packed form), sized_run (item over the matrix), sized_states (rank through the existential), and the (0|1)*0 DFA as sized_dfa n2 n2 with a test: 10 accepted, 01 rejected, the packed DFA reports 2 states. Gate: ganymede job-1794246163572-tibia-absorb-dfa (regex mirror re-synced; base checked). NEXT SLICES: the minimization certificate (quotient coverage + representative origins, model :188-300) as vector-indexed evidence in witness.spi.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_3 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 3u32, "2026-11-09T17:43Z", "tibia", "Next step: read the gate (job-1794246163572-tibia-absorb-dfa); if green, draft slice 2 (the minimization certificate as vector-indexed evidence in witness.spi) and hand slice 1 to org2 to apply.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_4 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 4u32, "2026-11-09T17:46Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:5x tibia: SLICE 2 DRAFTED (the minimization certificate, model main.spi:188-260). The model's indexed_dfa_quotient_coverage c r = vector c (fin r) (each closure state names its representative) and indexed_dfa_representative_origins r c = vector r (fin c) (each representative names a closure state it came from); their *_validation unions are Certified/Rejected. In regex witness.spi (base 14083D4CD22C, + `:< fin_vector`): `:== quotient_certificate c r = { cover : vector c (fin r); origin : vector r (fin c) }` and certified = every representative i satisfies cover[origin[i]] = i (the origins are a SECTION of the cover, so the quotient is onto and each class has a witness), by sections_from over the origin vector. Test: 3 closure states merged into 2 representatives with origins [0; 1] is certified; origins [0; 0] is refused. Gate: ganymede job-1794246355577-tibia-absorb-witness.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_5 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 5u32, "2026-11-09T17:59Z", "tibia", "11-09 13:5x tibia: SLICE 2 GREEN (ganymede job-1794246355577-tibia-absorb-witness): witness.spi + quotient_certificate: --check clean, cell budget 0, Cells discovered 3 executed 3 passed 3 failed 0; the formatter wants merged_cover wrapped (layout only). SLICE 1 FAILED its first gate on ONE type error: SomeSizedDfa d => rank d::accepting does not type, because the payload is an existential package (exists n. {...}), not a record; and since the module failed to type, 5 of typed.spi's existing tests failed with it. Fixed with lib fin_vector's idiom: pack with `SomeSizedDfa (\\? d)`, unpack with `:= \\? n. d = packed`. Re-gate: job tibia-absorb-dfa2. Compiler confirmed canonical_form_certificate_edition3 is a leftover duplicate (not a fixture): keep ONE, formatter layout, plain name, when it travels to regex.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_6 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 6u32, "2026-11-09T18:02Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:0x tibia: SLICE 1 GREEN on re-gate (ganymede tibia-absorb-dfa2): typed.spi --check clean, cell budget 0, Cells discovered 10 executed 10 passed 10 failed 0 (9 existing + the sized-DFA test). Both slices now carry the formatter's layout (adopted only where the token stream is identical). READY FOR org2 TO APPLY (regex is org2's repo): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY\\typed.spi (base 08EB59597B2C: + sized_dfa, some_sized_dfa, sized_run, sized_states, the (0|1)*0 sized DFA and test) and witness.spi (base 14083D4CD22C: + `:< fin_vector`, quotient_certificate, sections_from, certified and test). After the apply, regex build total = 118 + 2. What the model has beyond these two slices: the bisimulation capability / representative lookup (main.spi:144-186) and the compiled runner surface (:501-640), which are the next slices of this item.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_7 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 7u32, "2026-11-09T18:09Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:1x tibia: org2 APPLIED slices 1-2 to live regex (typed.spi + witness.spi; org2 bound one 290-weight cell, since cells numbered 100+ have a 271 limit). SLICE 3 DRAFTED, in LIB because it is generic: the model's representative lookup (main.spi:162-186, IndexedDfaRepresentativeIndexFound (FiniteSymbolIndexSucc index) | Missing) is \"the first element of a vector n el satisfying a predicate, as an option (fin n)\". lib fin_vector.spi (base 36E6617D2A32) gains shifted (option (fin n) -> option (fin (nat_succ n))), find_fin (holds) (v) : option (fin n), found_at, and a test (c/rust/lua like its siblings: 20 is found at 1 in [10;20;30], 99 gives -1). Gate: ganymede job-1794247730445-tibia-libgate-finvec. SLICE 4 next: pack regex_dfa's list DFA into some_sized_dfa (rows found with find_fin), so a DFA built by the existing pipeline becomes the bound-checked form, which the model's compiled runner certifies.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_8 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 8u32, "2026-11-09T18:10Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:2x tibia: SCOPE DECISION. With slices 1-3 the model's typed techniques are absorbed: the length-indexed transition matrix (sized_dfa over lib vector/fin), existential packing of the state count (some_sized_dfa), the minimization certificate (witness quotient_certificate, a section check) and the bounded representative lookup (lib find_fin). The remaining model surface, the compiled runner that converts a built DFA, is engineering on top and needs a sink-state design, so it moved to its own item REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT (filed with the design). This item closes when slice 3's lib land is green.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_9 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 9u32, "2026-11-09T18:39Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:4x tibia: SLICE 3 GREEN (ganymede job-1794247730445-tibia-libgate-finvec, mirror base = box base 36E6617D2A32, restored after): fin_vector --check clean, cell budget 0, Cells discovered 6 executed 6 passed 6 failed 0 (c/rust/lua rows incl. find_fin). The formatter only wraps the test tuple (applied). LAND PROOF launched on moon (job tibia-libland8; draft fin_vector.spi 591821D6DE6D, base 36E6617D2A32; tree = the box lib repacked now). Then the box digest check and a copy-only land close this item.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_10 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 10u32, "2026-11-09T18:55Z", "tibia", "Evidence (slice 3): lib fin_vector find_fin / shifted / found_at LANDED 11-09 14:48 local on the box lib by lib_land_window from a proven close. Moon -PrivateLib proof job tibia-libland8: \"LANDED and closed green\", fin_vector.spi 591821D6DE6D, lib digest 7C295499BC75A0C4. The box post-land digest was recomputed first = 7C295499BC75A0C4 (an exact match), so the box only copied (window win-1794250437661-26080, waited 1 ms); undo in spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo. STATE: all three slices are in (typed.spi + witness.spi applied by org2; find_fin in lib). Remaining DoD line: the full regex build on ganymede counting the new tests (org2's next build, the same one as REGEX-LIB-4's trap check). Then Done.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_dfa_cardinality_11 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", 11u32, "2026-11-09T20:23Z", "tibia", "11-09 16:3x tibia: last DoD line MET. TRAP CHECK PASSED (org2 ganymede job-1794251871681-org2-swap5, 19:53Z, exit 0): the regex gate ran 131/131 over 22 files, failed 0. RECONCILED FILE BY FILE against the box tree (static count of :# tests minus each file's prelude): 21 product files = 128 (lib regex_certificate 25, regex_xsd 14, regex_syntax 10, regex_dfa 7, regex_derivative 6, regex_charset 6, regex_nullable 4, regex_minimal 4, regex_language 3, regex_table 2; regex/src typed 10, partial 9, semantics 5, lazy 5, ssv_graph 4, agreement 4, witness 3, laws 3, table_emit 2, workloads 1, core_emit 1), + org2's staged/staged_check.spi 3 = 131, an exact match. So every lib test regex opens is EXECUTED by the consumer gate, including regex_xsd's 14 (the lib-move-drops-tests trap did not fire), and the absorb tests are in (typed 9->10, witness 2->3). My earlier formula (122 + 14 - xsd + 13) was wrong in its last term (the absorb slices added 2 regex tests, not 13; fin_vector's tests run in lib's own gate); the per-file reconciliation replaces it. DONE.")
inl regex_absorb_inventory_indexed () = Task ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", "regex absorbs the mega sample's inventory_indexed_model (22 existentials, 32 GADT cases, 25 indexed unions) into typed.spi / witness.spi", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", "regex,typefeatureset,mega-sample,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed () = Planning ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_1 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 1u32, "2026-11-09T17:38Z", "tibia", "Child of REGEX-MEGA-SAMPLE-RETIRE (plan (b)); after REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY, the same method and gates.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_2 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:57Z", "tibia", "11-09 14:5x tibia: SCOPE from reading the model (inventory_indexed_model, 1633 lines, 2 files). ALREADY COVERED by the DFA-cardinality slices: inventory_dfa_state_vector / acceptance_vector / target_vector / closed_rows are vector/fin instances (= typed.spi sized_dfa); inventory_dfa_state_index_search_result = lib find_fin; packed_* = the some_sized_dfa existential. GENUINELY NEW (this item's real content): (1) inventory_regex length: a regex over a FINITE SYMBOL INVENTORY, so symbols are fin n indices instead of u32 code points (the alphabet becomes a type-level size; finite_symbol_search_result length is its lookup); (2) CAPABILITY RECORDS (finite_symbol_equality_capability, inventory_canonical_derivative_capability, inventory_acceptance_capability, inventory_raw_dfa_closure_capability): explicit dictionary-passing of the engine's operations instead of prototypes, which lets a program be checked against a reference acceptance (the model's reference vs fast acceptance pair). Plan: slice 1 = an inventory alphabet (vector n code_range + symbol_of : u32 -> option (fin n)) in typed.spi; slice 2 = the capability record + an agreement test (reference derivative acceptance vs sized_dfa run over every word up to length 5). Starts when REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY closes (its dep).")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_3 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:26Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig (help pool), SLICE 1 DRAFT for tibia (not applied; regex is tibia's): drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED\\inventory_alphabet.spi, a block to append to src/typed.spi (it uses only what typed.spi already opens: fin_vector's vector, fin, find_fin, found_at, to_list, and n3). code_range = u32 * u32 (inclusive, tuples like bit_row); symbol_of alphabet c = find_fin (in_range c) alphabet, so an alphabet of n ranges gives fin n symbols (the type-level alphabet size the plan names; first matching range wins); word_of turns a code list into option (list (fin n)), None as soon as one code is outside the inventory; disjoint alphabet checks no two ranges overlap (so \"first match wins\" never hides a second meaning). Test: an ident alphabet [a-z][0-9][_] as vector n3 maps q, 5, _ to symbols 0, 1, 2 and ! to -1; a word in and a word out of the inventory; disjoint true for it, false for [a-z] with [d-n]. UNCOMPILED (box takes no compute while the user is present); tibia's usual node proof applies. Slice 2 (capability record + reference-vs-sized_dfa agreement over words up to length 5) builds on symbol_of.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_4 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 4u32, "2026-11-09T20:29Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig correction to note 3: the draft now reuses the lib's code_range record ({ low; high }, regex_charset.spi:5, built with range low high) instead of a local u32 * u32 alias, which would have clashed with regex_dfa's code_range that typed.spi already sees; the block starts with :< regex_charset because opening regex_dfa does not re-export it.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_5 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 5u32, "2026-11-09T20:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:0x tibia: REVIEWED rig's slice 1 and adapted it for the gate: drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED\\inventory-block.spi. Changes: symbol_of -> inventory_symbol (it would clash with the conversion block's symbol helper in the same file); word_of reuses the conversion block's cons_found instead of a tuple match on two options; `:< regex_charset` moves to typed.spi's top opens; the one 460-char test becomes three tests within the 271 budget (codes -> symbols 0/1/2/-1; a word in = 3 symbols, a word with ! = none; disjoint true for [a-z][0-9][_], false for [a-z]+[d-n]); no lambdas. It appends AFTER the conversion block (it needs cons_found). Gate: job tibia-dfaconv2.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_6 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 6u32, "2026-11-09T21:27Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:3x tibia: SLICE 1 GREEN and STANDALONE (no lib change needed: it uses find_fin, which is already in lib). READY FOR org2 TO APPLY: drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED\\typed.spi (603E2EA41AE1; base = regex src/typed.spi CF407962354F). The whole file, with the formatter's layout adopted after a token-identical check. Changes vs base: + :< regex_charset (for code_range), + cons_found, + rig's inventory block as reviewed (in_range, inventory_symbol, word_of, overlaps_any, disjoint_ranges, disjoint, ident_alphabet, symbol_at, word_length) and 3 rust tests. Gate (ganymede job tibia-inventory): --check clean, budget 0, Cells 12/13; the 3 new tests pass. The single red is the_typed_core_answers_like_the_derivatives..., which also fails on an UNMODIFIED typed.spi on my mirror (its lib predates the 21:1xZ lands), and org2's own gate on the current lib passes it 10/10 (job org2-typed). Not a regression from this slice. NEXT SLICES (note 2): capability records (finite_symbol_equality / acceptance / derivative capabilities as explicit dictionary records) and the reference-vs-fast acceptance check.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_7 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 7u32, "2026-11-09T21:28Z", "tibia", "DoD: the model's inventory_indexed techniques live in regex src typed.spi / witness.spi (inventory alphabet as fin n symbols, capability records, reference-vs-fast acceptance check), each slice gated green on ganymede (budget 0, its tests passing) and applied by org2. Next step: org2 applies slice 1 (typed.spi draft, note 6); then tibia drafts slice 2, the capability records.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_8 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 8u32, "2026-11-09T21:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 21:3xZ slice 1 APPLIED: tibia's drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED\\typed.spi over regex src/typed.spi (base CF407962354F matched; additive: :< regex_charset, cons_found, the inventory alphabet block). Proof on org2's ganymede mirror (lib = box current, digest 436296D1C783788F): job org2-typed2, Cells gate of src/typed.spi rc=0 13/13 (10 existing + 3 new); budget oracle 0 on the box copy. Unstaged.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_9 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 9u32, "2026-11-10T10:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 10:1xZ clearing the lane:org2 wait: slice 1 was applied 11-09 21:33Z (note above) and the box regex/src/typed.spi is still 603e2ea41ae1 = tibia's draft (unstaged). Next step is tibia's slice 2, the capability records")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_10 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 10u32, "2026-11-10T11:48Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:5x tibia: SLICE 2 GREEN, READY FOR org2 TO APPLY (frozen): drafts\\regex\\REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED\\slice2\\typed.spi cbd1c3726a0d (base = live regex src/typed.spi 603e2ea41ae1, copy at slice2\\typed.spi.base). ADDS the model's capability records as explicit dictionary-passing: a nominal acceptance_capability over list u32 -> verdict; answer_with (unwraps by constructor match, as the model does); instances reference_acceptance (derivative matches), core_acceptance (the typed bit-row DFA), indexed_acceptance (the class-indexed rows); engines (a pair alias); agree and misses_between (the reference-vs-fast agreement check); the helpers words_to_six and fourth_reference. 3 tests: the core and the indexed capability each answer like the reference on all 127 words up to six (0 misses); a capability that rejects everything misses exactly the 56 accepted words (8+16+32), so the check bites. One layout fix: the base's doubled blank line at 359-360 (from the slice-1 splice) is squeezed to one, which is canonical. GATE (ganymede, exact copy of the box's regex src + spiral lib, pack81): base control 13/13 (job tibia-rxslice2); final draft 16/16, 0 unsupported (job tibia-rxslice2c). Budget: the awk oracle shows every cell <= 270 (an earlier version had 2 test cells at 365/273, so they were split before the final gate). TypeFeatures: capabilities are a nominal type, never strings; the engines are typed values. DoD remaining after this applies: the model's other capability records (symbol equality, derivative, raw DFA closure) as needed. Next step: after org2 applies slice 2, close this item if the remaining model techniques are already covered (note 2's census), else draft slice 3.")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_11 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 11u32, "2026-11-10T11:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 11:5xZ slice 2 APPLIED on the box (unstaged): tibia's drafts regex/REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED/slice2/typed.spi over regex src/typed.spi (base 603e2ea41ae1 matched; now cbd1c3726a0d). Diff reviewed: additive (nominal acceptance_capability, reference/core/indexed capabilities, agree/misses_between over words up to six, 3 tests incl. the all-rejecting negative control at 56 misses) plus the 359-360 blank-line squeeze; budget oracle 0 on the box copy. Proof is tibia's ganymede gate on an exact copy of the box regex (pack81): base 13/13, draft 16/16. Next step: tibia's slice 3 or the item's close")
inl note_of_regex_absorb_inventory_indexed_12 () = Note ("REGEX-ABSORB-INVENTORY-INDEXED", 12u32, "2026-11-10T11:59Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:5x tibia: DONE. Both slices of note 2's plan are applied on the box (unstaged): slice 1, the inventory alphabet as fin n symbols (applied 11-09 21:33Z), and slice 2, the capability records plus the reference-vs-fast acceptance check (applied by org2 11-10 11:5xZ; box regex src/typed.spi = cbd1c3726a0d, verified by hash). The DoD's three techniques (inventory alphabet, capability records, reference-vs-fast check) now live in regex typed.spi. proof: ganymede gates on an exact copy of the box's regex src + lib, slice 1 13/13 (org2-typed2), slice 2 16/16 green (tibia-rxslice2c), budget oracle 0. The model's remaining parts were already covered by the DFA-cardinality slices (note 2's census: state/acceptance/target vectors = sized_dfa, search = find_fin, packed = some_sized_dfa).")
inl regex_sized_dfa_convert () = Task ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", "regex: a validating conversion from regex_dfa's list dfa into typed.spi's some_sized_dfa (Dead -> an explicit sink state, every index checked once), so pipeline-built DFAs run without row_at/target_at's silent fallbacks", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY", "regex,typefeatureset,mega-sample,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert () = Planning ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:10Z", "tibia", "Follow-up of REGEX-ABSORB-DFA-CARDINALITY (the model's compiled runner, main.spi:501-640). WHY: regex_dfa row_at/target_at (regex_dfa.spi:154-163) map an out-of-range index to Dead / { accepting = Rejected; next = [] } SILENTLY; the sized form makes that unrepresentable. DESIGN: (1) lib fin_vector fin_at (i : i32) (v : vector n el) : option (fin n) (the int -> bounded index step); (2) count states = rows + 1 sink, and build the acceptance and target vectors from ONE existential size n (of_list on the rows, then map each target through fin_at, Dead -> the sink's fin); (3) return a validation union Converted (some_sized_dfa s) | Malformed (reason), the model's Certified/Rejected shape; (4) a test: build (0|1)*0 through regex_dfa build, convert, and sized_run agrees with run_unchecked on every word up to length 6. DoD: that agreement test green in regex typed.spi, budget-clean, applied by org2. TypeFeatures: an existential size shared by two vectors, a total transition function with no fallback.")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 2u32, "2026-11-09T20:29Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig (help pool), STEP 1 DRAFT (not applied; lib/spiral is org's, regex is tibia's): drafts\\spiral\\REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT\\fin_vector-fin_at.spi, a block to append to lib fin_vector.spi after find_fin (it reuses shifted and the three () fixture): fin_at i v : option (fin n), None for a negative index or one past the end, so the int -> bounded-index check happens ONCE at conversion and never again at run time; test in fin_vector's style (c, rust, lua targets): indexes 0 and 2 found, 3 and -1 not. FINDINGS for steps 2-4 (from reading regex_dfa.spi in the lib): row = { accepting : verdict; next : list target }, target = Dead | To state, dfa.classes : list code_range; the silent fallbacks are target_at (past the end -> Dead) and row_at (past the end -> a rejecting empty row), lines 154-163. The conversion needs TWO sizes: n (states = rows + 1 sink, from of_list) and s (symbol classes, from dfa.classes); sized_dfa s n fixes s outside the existential, so either the caller passes s as a vector s code_range of the classes (Malformed when its rank differs from the dfa's), or the result packs both sizes (\\? s n.). Recommend the first: it matches some_sized_dfa s as typed.spi declares it, and the agreement test can build the (0|1)*0 classes vector by hand (n2, like ends_in_zero_sized). Each row's next list must have exactly s targets; a short row is Malformed (today target_at would quietly read it as Dead). UNCOMPILED (box: no compute while the user is present).")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:0x tibia: STEPS 2-4 DRAFTED: drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT\\convert-block.spi (to append to regex src/typed.spi, which also gains `:< regex_charset` for code_range). to_sized classes d : converted s (Converted (some_sized_dfa s) | Malformed reason). The caller passes the class vector, as rig recommended, but builds it with of_list d::classes, so s is the dfa's real class count. Note: (0|1)*0 has 4 classes, not 2, because classes_of splits the whole code-point range. Dead -> one explicit sink state (index = row count, a rejecting row whose every target is itself); each target is checked once by lib fin_at; a short or long row -> Malformed. Test: minimal_of (fourth_from_end ()) converts, and sized_run agrees with run_unchecked on every word up to 6 (0 misses) and on two words outside {0,1} (0 misses); a first row cut to [] -> Malformed (-1). FIRST GATE (tibia-dfaconv): stale lib on the mirror (no shifted, no regex_xsd) + code_range unbound; both fixed (spiral mirror re-synced to the box lib 591821D6DE6D, regex_charset opened). Budget re-split for the 271 limit (cells past 100). Re-gate: job tibia-dfaconv2 (lib fin_vector + rig's fin_at, then typed.spi with this block and the inventory slice).")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 4u32, "2026-11-09T20:50Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:1x tibia: GATE 2 (tibia-dfaconv2): typed.spi budget 0 findings; 2 type errors fixed. (1) Recursive functions with foralls must be fully annotated, so sized_rows needs its return type back (now the sized_targets s n m alias). (2) The class_symbol rename had not applied. LIB: rig's fin_at checks clean, but fin_vector's 7 C-target tests ALL failed, including the 6 that were already there, and its test cell was 283 > 272 (now two tests). Gate 3 runs an unmodified fin_vector as the control first, to tell a C-toolchain problem on ganymede from a fin_at problem; it saves the logs.")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_5 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 5u32, "2026-11-09T20:54Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:2x tibia: GATE 3 (tibia-dfaconv3): budget 0; ONE type error left: the nested pattern VectorCons ((_, next), rest) against a vector of concrete tuples unifies the payload with a rigid var ('tc vs _ * list i32). witness.spi matches VectorCons on a concrete element fine, so it is the nested tuple pattern; fixed with a row_next projection. LIB CONTROL: an UNMODIFIED fin_vector fails the same way on this mirror (open testing unbound under --livemd from the lib dir, after today's spiral re-sync), so the lib notebook failures are the mirror's, not fin_at's; fin_at --check is clean. Its real proof is the moon -PrivateLib lib land. Gate 4: job tibia-dfaconv4.")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_6 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 6u32, "2026-11-09T21:00Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:3x tibia: GATE 4 (tibia-dfaconv4): typed.spi --check CLEAN, budget 0, Cells 12/14 passed. Failed: (a) the_typed_core_answers_like_the_derivatives_on_every_word_up_to_six, an EXISTING test, with \"FatalError: the return type of main in the C backend should be a 32-bit int\" (not yet known whether it fails without the drafts on this re-synced mirror); (b) my a_built_dfa_converts... (rust). The Cells log carries no per-test reason, so job tibia-dfadebug runs the unmodified typed.spi as a control and builds the draft with a temporary main that prints the three counts.")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_7 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 7u32, "2026-11-09T21:08Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:1x tibia: CONTROL (job tibia-dfadebug): the UNMODIFIED typed.spi on this mirror also fails the_typed_core_answers_like_the_derivatives_on_every_word_up_to_six (9 of 10 pass; the C-backend \"main must return a 32-bit int\" fatal), so that red belongs to the mirror's current lib + typed.spi, not to the drafts. Worth a look by whoever owns the typed core test, since the box's lib moved today. The draft's only own red is the conversion test; the debug build failed only on ++# (typed.spi does not open sm'_operators), fixed in the debug copy. Rerun: job tibia-round2.")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_8 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 8u32, "2026-11-09T21:22Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:3x tibia: ROOT CAUSE FOUND, and it changes the design (job tibia-dfadebug4, the conversion built to Rust with a debug main). The partial evaluator stops with \"TracedError: Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var\", traced through to_sized -> lib of_list ([] => SomeVector (\\? VectorEnd)). Spiral's existential sizes are COMPILE-TIME types: of_list can pack a list into vector n only when the evaluator knows the list's length. A pipeline-built DFA (minimal_of / build over a regex, computed at run time) has a run-time-length rows and classes list, so it CANNOT be lifted to sized_dfa s n. The hand-written sized DFAs in typed.spi work because their sizes are literal. So the item's premise (\"pipeline-built DFAs run without row_at/target_at's silent fallbacks\" via some_sized_dfa) does not hold in this form. Everything else in the draft is sound: --check clean, budget 0, fin_at (lib) type-checks. OPTIONS: (A) a run-time VALIDATED form: validate once (every target < row count, every row has the class count), then run a checked_dfa whose only constructor is the validator, so the silent fallbacks can only be reached on unvalidated input. That is a smart constructor, weaker than a type-level size; Spiral has no module privacy, so the guarantee is by convention unless the constructor is hidden behind a nominal. (B) keep the sized form for compile-time-known DFAs only (generated tables, like fiscal's pinned regexes) and convert at compile time. (C) close as infeasible-as-designed with this finding. Recommend (B) + (A): (B) covers the generated-table case at full strength; (A) covers run-time DFAs honestly. Owner call (tibia team item, regex applied by org2).")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_9 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 9u32, "2026-11-10T03:12Z", "tibia", "11-09 23:1x tibia groom. Next step: once the user picks a design from note 8, draft the conversion on that design and gate it on ganymede. Until then it waits on the user (wait row).")
inl note_of_regex_sized_dfa_convert_10 () = Note ("REGEX-SIZED-DFA-CONVERT", 10u32, "2026-11-10T03:17Z", "tibia", "11-09 23:1x tibia groom 2. Next step: after the user picks a design from note 8, draft the conversion on it and gate it on ganymede.")
inl spiral_ui_1_restore () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI-1-RESTORE", "Restore the archived SPIRAL-UI lab drafts (ui.spi, ui_tracking.spi, probe_main.spi, probe_tracking.spi) into their real place as incomplete drafts, or record why the library starts over", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:org,spiral,ui,lib", "current", "current")
