inl note_of_spiral_ui_1_restore_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-1-RESTORE", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: each of the 4 archived files is either restored into spiral (lib module draft) or recorded as superseded, with the reason. Next step: run the restore command in SPIRAL-UI n2 into a scratch dir and diff the 4 files against lib leptos.spi/state_core.spi. TypeFeatures: none (triage). Parent: SPIRAL-UI (split by org2 11-09: 1680 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_1_restore_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-1-RESTORE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:31Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:3x DONE (triage). Restored the 4 archived files (archive 20261030-232045, scratch-archive.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab -Restore ... -Only SPIRAL-UI\\*) into the drafts store %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI\\ (not into lib: all 4 are EDITION-2 syntax: type/union/inl/match/mut, while lib is edition 3). Verdicts: (1) ui_tracking.spi (44 lines) = the signal design to keep: automatic dependency tracking through a tracker (reactive_graph style), lazy memo with a dirty flag set by the tracked reads -> SEED for SPIRAL-UI-2 (respell to edition 3, signals as typed handles). (2) ui.spi (92 lines): its signals (manual subscribe closures) are SUPERSEDED by (1); its view union (Text | Element of tag*attrs*children | Reactive | Fragment), attribute union (Class | Href | OnClick) and render_html/count_elements are the SEED for SPIRAL-UI-3 (upgrade view to a GADT keyed by element kind). (3) probe_main.spi + probe_tracking.spi = the test specs for -2/-3: render_html of div.app[button \"+\", span \"n\"] == \"<div class=\\\"app\\\"><button>+</button><span>n</span></div>\", count_elements = 3, memo computes exactly 2x (initial + one set), doubled after set 3 = 6; and setting an UNRELATED signal must NOT recompute the memo (values 0, 0, 6, 6; computes stays 2) = the fine-grained property SPIRAL-UI-2's DoD names. Proof: the restore log (4 files) + the files in the drafts store.")
inl spiral_ui_2_signals () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", "Spiral reactive core: signal t as a typed handle, create/get/set, memo and effect over a dependency graph, with rust tests and no DOM", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-UI-1-RESTORE", "team:org,spiral,ui,lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_ui_2_signals () = Planning ("SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_ui_2_signals_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: a lib module (ui_signals) whose tests show a set propagating to a memo and an effect exactly once, and an unchanged set propagating to nothing. Next step: model the graph as nodes with typed handles and a dirty set. TypeFeatures: signal t / memo t as typed handles (phantom over the value type). Parent: SPIRAL-UI (split by org2 11-09: 1680 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_2_signals_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:3x DESIGN QUESTION FIRST (found while starting): the seed (drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI\\ui_tracking.spi, edition 2) is built on `mut` cells (cell <- value, *cell), and edition-3 lib has no plain mutable-cell spelling; the only mut in lib is host Rust (rust::mut' over vec). Two routes: (a) a host-backed cell nominal per backend (Rust Rc<RefCell>, TS let) in a boundary module, keeping the seed's tracker design; (b) a pure graph value threaded explicitly (set g s v : graph; get g m : t * graph) with signal t / memo t as typed ids, heterogeneous values via an existential store. (b) fits the typefeatureset + pure-lib rule and tests without a host; (a) is closer to leptos semantics and the TS DOM mount (-4). Next step: a 20-line probe of (b) over two signals of different types (i32, string) to see if the existential store stays cheap, then decide. Tests to carry from the probes: memo computes exactly 2x across one set; an unrelated set does not recompute (0, 0, 6, 6).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_2_signals_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Design picked: route (b) without an existential store. Signals are typed lenses into the user's own model record (signal model t = {id; read; write}), so the record is the heterogeneous store and every value keeps its type. Memo = deps + compute + cache/store lenses (an option t slot in the model); the graph keeps homogeneous rows only (deps, clear : model -> model) and reactions (deps, run). set compares with the current value (unchanged = no-op), clears the dependent caches, then runs the dependent reactions. Probe drafted at drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI\\ui_signals.spi, budget clean, 2 rust tests carrying the (6, runs 2, effects 1) and unrelated/unchanged = nothing cases; gate job org2-ui queued on ganymede.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_2_signals_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T20:17Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 20:1x. lib/spiral/ui_signals.spi LANDED on the box (copy-only from the ganymede -PrivateLib proof, lib digest E294E4FCF7BC1BB4 = box prediction; undo spiral-bin/lib-land-undo/20261109-161646) with its layers.spi row (ui_signals, Std). Proof: land checks green (26 document tests, consumers compile, type-probe ui_signals PASS 2 tests typed, 0 respell drift); Cells gate of ui_signals rc=0, 2/2 rust tests: a set recomputes the memo once and runs its effect once (6, runs 2, effects 1); unrelated and unchanged sets do nothing (runs 1, effects 1). DoD: met. Design: signals are typed lenses into the user's model record (no existential store, no host cells), memo caches live in the model as option slots, the graph keeps only homogeneous (deps, clear) rows and reactions. Found on the way: layers.spi's own test was already red (no testing prelude), filed as LIB-LAYERS-TEST-PRELUDE. Next: SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE.")
inl spiral_ui_3_view_tree () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE", "Typed view tree: element nodes as a GADT keyed by element kind, static render to an HTML string, signal-bound text nodes", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-UI-2-SIGNALS", "team:org,spiral,ui,lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_ui_3_view_tree () = Planning ("SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_ui_3_view_tree_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: a view of nested elements renders byte-identical to a hand-written HTML string, and a signal-bound text node renders the signal's current value. Next step: define view kinds as a GADT (Element of kind * attrs * children | Text | Bound of signal). TypeFeatures: GADT view nodes indexed by element kind. Parent: SPIRAL-UI (split by org2 11-09: 1680 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_3_view_tree_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T20:21Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig (help pool), DRAFT for org (not applied; org owns lib/spiral): drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI\\ui_view.spi, next to org2's ui_signals draft. Built on what is already in the lib: ui_signals (landed today) and markup.spi (escape, attributes, element, concat), so no new escaping code. element_kind closed union Div | Span | Para | Items | Item | Button | Break (tag_of; void_kind: Break renders <br> with no children or close tag); view model (recursive) = Element (kind, attrs, children) | Text s | Bound (ui_signals::signal model string), indexed by the same model type as the signals, so a bound node can only read a signal of this view's model; render g v reads Bound through ui_signals::get, escapes Text and Bound alike. Tests (DoD): a nested view renders byte-identical to the hand-written string <div class=\"card\"><p>a &lt; b &amp; c</p><ul><li>one</li><li>hi</li></ul><br></div>, and a bound node renders the signal's current value after a set, escaped (<span>&lt;new&gt;</span>). UNCOMPILED (the box takes no compute while the user is present); it needs org's ganymede -PrivateLib proof like ui_signals. Open choice for org: element kinds as a closed union (this draft) versus a type index per kind (the title's \"GADT keyed by element kind\"), which would let attrs be typed per element; the union keeps render one match and is enough for the static-render DoD.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_3_view_tree_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:33Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 20:3x. lib/spiral/ui_view.spi LANDED on the box (copy-only from the ganymede -PrivateLib proof, lib digest C81406D99326DDB5 = box prediction; undo spiral-bin/lib-land-undo/20261109-163247) with its layers.spi row (ui_view, Std). Proof: land checks green (26 document tests, consumers compile, type-probe PASS 2 tests typed, 0 respell drift); Cells gate rc=0 2/2 rust tests: nested Div/Para/Span render byte-identical to '<div><p>a &lt; b: 0</p><p><span>label </span></p></div>' (text escaped), and after set a 7 / label x the same view renders the new signal values. DoD: met. Design: view m k is a GADT keyed by content kind (phrasing vs flow), so a Div inside a Span or Para is a type error; leaves are a plain union leaf m = Text | Bound (graph m -> string); bound s show reads ui_signals::get. Attributes and events were not in this DoD; they ride SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM with the DOM mount.")
inl spiral_ui_4_ts_dom () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", "Mount the typed view tree in the browser through the TypeScript backend, with signals updating DOM nodes in place", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-UI-3-VIEW-TREE", "team:org,spiral,ui,lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom () = Planning ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:12Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: one dice ui component renders the same DOM as its leptos version in a headless browser check. Next step: pick the smallest dice ui component and write its view in the new tree. TypeFeatures: DOM handles as nominal host types. Parent: SPIRAL-UI (split by org2 11-09: 1680 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", 2u32, "2026-11-09T20:41Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig (help pool), THE RECORDED NEXT STEP (pick the smallest dice ui component, write its view in the new tree): dice ui components are Spiral files generating Leptos (ui/src/components/*.spi). Smallest = lists_view.spi (255 B): its Leptos DOM is ONE bare text node \"???\" in a fragment (leptos.text_view), no wrapper element. In the landed lib ui_view that is exactly a top-level text \"???\" (Leaf is view m phrasing and renders unwrapped), so it is the first byte-identical target. DRAFT (not applied; dice is yours): drafts\\dice\\SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM\\lists_view_ui.spi, view + a render test asserting \"???\". GAP FOUND for the next component: home.spi (647 B) renders <div class=\"flex flex-1\" class:dark=(signal dark_mode)> around content. ui_view as landed has NO attributes (Leaf/Span/Para/Div only), so home cannot be written in it yet. Proposal for org: Div (and Span, Para) take a list (attr m) first, attr m = Static of name * value | ClassWhen of class name * (graph m -> bool), rendered static attrs first then the toggled classes, escaped like text; ClassWhen is what class:dark needs and what the TS mount will update in place when the signal changes. UNCOMPILED (box: no compute while the user is present).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 20:5x started. Base is landed: lib ui_signals (typed-lens signals, memo, reactions) + lib ui_view (view m k GADT, phrasing/flow, static render). Probe: ui_view's 2 tests with an added ///> typescript target line gated rc=0 2/2 on ganymede (job org2-uits), BUT the gate summary has no per-target breakdown, so TypeScript execution is UNCONFIRMED; first step next round: rerun with the Cells per-target output (or a ts-only test) to prove the render compiles and agrees on TS. Then: a TS-only module (backend_switch TypeScript arm) with document.createElement/textContent/appendChild macros; mount walks view m k once, records (signal id, text node) pairs for Bound leaves, and a reaction per Bound leaf rewrites that node's textContent on set (reuses ui_signals react, so in-place updates need no diffing). DoD proof idea: a headless check (jsdom or node) that after set the same node object holds the new text.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", 4u32, "2026-11-09T21:20Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 21:2xZ progress. (1) TypeScript CONFIRMED: Cells needs bun (SPIRAL_BUN); ganymede has it cached at spiral-bin/toolchains/bun/bun-linux-x64/bun (1.4.4) but not on PATH, so the earlier TS target was silently 'unsupported'. With SPIRAL_BUN set, ui_view's tests run 2/2 on typescript. (2) LANDED lib/spiral/ui_dom.spi (+ layers row; box digest 436296D1C783788F, undo lib-land-undo/20261109-172000): a pure mount that walks view m k once and emits typed dom_op (Create, CreateText, Append, SetText) plus one binding per Bound leaf; refresh emits SetText only for bindings whose text changed (in-place update, no diffing). Gate rust+typescript 2/2: mounting counter_view emits 16 ops headed by Create (1, div); after set a 7, refresh yields exactly [SetText (4, 7)]. LEFT for DoD: a TS-only applier (backend_switch TypeScript arm, document.createElement/createTextNode/appendChild/textContent over an id->node array) and a headless proof that after set the SAME node object holds the new text (needs a DOM in bun: happy-dom or a minimal fake document, a download to approve).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", 5u32, "2026-11-09T21:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 21:4xZ DoD proof GREEN, land held. lib draft ui_dom_ts.spi (TypeScript-only host boundary: dom_table = Map<number, any>, apply_op runs Create/CreateText/Append/SetText through document.createElement/createTextNode/appendChild/textContent). Headless proof in bun with a fake document installed on globalThis: mount counter_view, apply the ops, hold node 4, set a 7, apply refresh's patch: the SAME node object now has textContent '7' (gate 1/1 typescript, ganymede org2-domts3). Land proof green on ganymede (org2-domtsland: type-probe PASS, consumers compile, 0 drift, lib digest C326D7A4BCEB56EB = box prediction). Box -Apply REFUSED by the box's round trip: '(Mix) Method not found: ListModule.emptyListError()' = FSharp.Core mismatch in the box pack78 install (reported to compiler); nothing written. Next step: re-run the copy-only land once compiler confirms the box install; then close (DoD met by the proof).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_4_ts_dom_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", 6u32, "2026-11-09T22:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 22:0xZ. lib/spiral/ui_dom_ts.spi LANDED on the box after compiler fixed the pack78 FSharp.Core mismatch (copy-only from the ganymede proof, lib digest C326D7A4BCEB56EB = box prediction; undo lib-land-undo/20261109-180136), layers row (ui_dom_ts, Host, typescript). Proof: the TypeScript gate in bun (ganymede org2-domts3, 1/1): mount -> apply ops to a document -> set a 7 -> apply refresh's patch -> the SAME text node object holds '7'; land checks green (type-probe PASS, consumers compile, 0 drift). DoD: met (the typed view tree mounts through the TypeScript backend and signals update DOM nodes in place). The SPIRAL-UI stack in lib: ui_signals -> ui_view -> ui_dom (pure ops + in-place patches, rust+typescript) -> ui_dom_ts (browser applier). Note: Cells needs SPIRAL_BUN to run typescript targets on ganymede (bun cached at spiral-bin/toolchains/bun, not on PATH).")
inl kit_memory_adapters_m1 () = Task ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M1", "KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS milestone 1: the client adapter interface as a typed record with import and export, plus the Claude instance over the memory dir and MEMORY.md", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,memory,team:rig", "current", "current")
