inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m1_1 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M1", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:13Z", "kit-split", "split from KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS by kit agile split (milestone 1). DoD: the client adapter interface as a typed record with import and export, plus the Claude instance over the memory dir and MEMORY.md, proven in the parent item notes. NEXT STEP: read the parent latest note for this milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:53Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 22:3x local rig, BUILT (unstaged, unprobed; in the probe batch): src/rig_memory_adapters/adapter.spi (pure, HostFree), built ON rig_memory_typed (11-09) instead of a second parser. memory_client union ClaudeCode | Codex | Zed | OpenCode; store_file { name; text }; import_of client files returns Imported (memories, unreadable file names) or ImportRefused reason; the Claude instance reads every *.md except MEMORY.md through memory_of_text and NAMES each unreadable file rather than dropping it; claude_export renders each memory back with text_of_memory (byte for byte: the raw frontmatter lines are kept) plus a MEMORY.md index line per memory (\"- [name](name.md) - description\"); the other clients are refused with \"no adapter yet for <client>\", never an empty import. Test: one memory read, the index skipped, one unreadable named, byte-exact render-back, the index line, and a Codex refusal. NEXT: M2 (Codex and Zed over AGENTS.md).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m1_3 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: the model passed its notebook gate (run_notebook --gate, rust target) on ganymede, outside the TRAIN42e train, which timed out on moon: rig shipped the box lib and today's 41 self-contained model packages to /root/rig-probe and gated each (nice, 2 pinned cores). The probe wait is answered; next step is the item's IO half per its last note.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m1_4 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M1", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:13Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:3x tibia (help pool): the DoD reads as MET. Note 2 BUILT src/rig_memory_adapters/adapter.spi: memory_client union + import_of / claude_import / claude_export over store_file, the Claude instance (every *.md except MEMORY.md through memory_of_text, unreadable files named, byte-exact render-back, the index line). Note 3: its notebook gate passed on ganymede. Note 2's own NEXT is M2, so no IO step is owed inside M1. One wording gap for rig to rule on: the DoD says \"interface as a typed RECORD with import and export\", but the build dispatches on a client UNION (import_of client files). A record of functions { import : list store_file -> import_result; export : list memory -> list store_file } per client would be the HKT-style instance the parent names; the union is simpler and refuses unknown clients by construction. RECOMMEND rig closes M1 as built (or asks for the record form). A live import of the real memory dir was NOT run: it needs box compute or copying personal memory files to a node.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m1_5 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M1", 5u32, "2026-11-09T22:26Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE on tibia's reading plus the wording fix: the DoD asks for the interface \"as a typed record with import and export\", so adapter.spi now also has memory_adapter { client; import_files : list store_file -> import_result; export_files : list memory -> list store_file } and adapter_of client : option memory_adapter (Some for ClaudeCode built from claude_import / claude_export, None for clients without an adapter, so unknown clients are still refused by construction); field names avoid the export keyword. proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (adapter 1/1), now also importing and exporting through the record (a file plus the index) and None for Zed. A live import of the real memory dir stays for M2's IO step (box compute or a node copy of personal files, neither done here).")
