inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m2_2 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:44Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:4x tibia (help pool): GREEN, ready for rig's train (kit is rig's; not applied). drafts\\kit\\KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2\\adapter.spi (base 77299BF3DD5C, rig's M1 file incl. the memory_adapter record) adds the AGENTS.md adapter shared by Codex (~/.codex/AGENTS.md) and Zed (%APPDATA%\\Zed\\AGENTS.md), per the parent's format notes 3 and 6 (plain markdown, no frontmatter, one ## section per rule). Import: split on '## ', each section becomes a memory through the existing memory_of_text (frontmatter synthesized: name = slug of the title, description = the title, type feedback); a non-blank preamble before the first section is NAMED in unreadable ('AGENTS.md preamble'), never dropped; no AGENTS.md -> ImportRefused. Export: '## <description>' + body per memory, which round-trips the file byte for byte. import_of / adapter_of now cover Codex | Zed; OpenCode stays refused (the old Codex/Zed refusal assertions moved to OpenCode). Tests: two sections -> commit-message / tests-first, byte-exact export; a preamble named. Gate in rig's probe layout on ganymede (job tibia-memad, with the box's rig_memory_typed): Cells 3/3. NOT in this slice: the Zed threads DB (read-only per the item) is IO-side and needs a sqlite reader; the IO half reads/writes the real AGENTS.md files.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m2_3 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2", 3u32, "2026-11-09T22:44Z", "tibia", "TypeFeatures: every client is one memory_adapter record { import_files; export_files } chosen by adapter_of over the memory_client union; AGENTS.md sections become typed memory values through the same frontmatter parser as Claude's, so all clients share one memory type.")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m2_4 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:54Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 18:5x rig APPLIED tibia's draft after TRAIN43's snapshot (drafts\\kit\\KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M2\\adapter.spi; unstaged; hash equal after copy; kit standards 0, ratchet clean; it rides TRAIN44). DONE: an AGENTS.md adapter shared by Codex and Zed: each \"## \" section becomes a memory through memory_of_text, export writes the file back byte for byte, a preamble before the first section is named in the unreadable list instead of dropped; the only removed lines are the two refusal assertions that named Codex and Zed (now adapted), moved to OpenCode, the remaining client without an adapter. proof: tibia's gate 3/3 on ganymede in rig's probe layout (job tibia-memad).")
