inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m3_2 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M3", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:06Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:1x tibia (help pool): GREEN, ready for rig's train AFTER M2 (it is built on the M2 draft): drafts\\kit\\KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M3\\adapter.spi. OpenCode = the M2 AGENTS.md adapter behind a DENY rule applied before any read: denied name = service.json (the plaintext service password, parent note 4) or any name containing credential or account (case-insensitive; covers the opencode.db credential / account / account_state / control_account table dumps), so those files never reach a parser. With OpenCode handled, every memory_client has an adapter: the catch-all refusal arms in import_of / adapter_of are gone, and the old refusal assertions now test \"no AGENTS.md\" and that OpenCode's record exists. Tests: deny list (service.json, credential.csv, Account_State.tsv denied; AGENTS.md allowed); importing rules + password + two table dumps yields only keep-it-short. Gate in rig's probe layout on ganymede (job tibia-memad3): Cells 4/4. NOT in the pure model: reading the db \"only from a copy\" is the IO half's rule (copy, then read, never the live file).")
inl note_of_kit_memory_adapters_m3_3 () = Note ("KIT-MEMORY-ADAPTERS-M3", 3u32, "2026-11-09T23:07Z", "tibia", "TypeFeatures: the deny rule sits in front of the shared adapter (opencode_import = filter denied names, then agents_import), so a secret file can never reach a parser regardless of its content.")
