inl note_of_kit_entry_x_shape_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:18Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:5x local rig, RE-MEASURED against the live kit/src (the slice DoD metrics of 11-03). proof: string-compare verb dispatch (an argument read compared to a word literal): 41 sites in 16 packages by the broad pattern, 6 by the strict one (argument_owned/argument_at/argument_byte N = \"...\"), down from 126 in 29 on 11-03; packages with positional argument reads (argument_owned/argument_at with an integer index): 25, down from 56; packages still using !!!!Export: 2 (one in the style family, one in bindings). BY FAMILY (strict sites / positional packages / bang files): agile 6 / 20 / 0, contract probes 0 / 4 / 0, job 0 / 1 / 0, style 0 / 0 / 1, bindings 0 / 0 / 1; every other family is at 0 / 0 / 0. FINDING: the remainder is the agile family's argument_owned prelude copies, the very sites LIB-CLI-PRELUDE-3-SWITCH (accepted by rig 11-09, rides after TRAIN43) replaces with lib's typed argv_view (AfterVerb); so M2-M5 of this item should be re-sized after that switch lands, and the two run as one change. The 4 contract-probe packages read fixed argv on purpose (test drivers): candidates for an explicit exemption rather than a rewrite.")
