inl realworld_1_spec () = Task ("REALWORLD-1-SPEC", "RealWorld (Conduit) API as types: every endpoint of the official spec as a typed route union with request/response shapes, plus the home decision for the app", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:org,spiral,app", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_realworld_1_spec () = Planning ("REALWORLD-1-SPEC", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_realworld_1_spec_1 () = Note ("REALWORLD-1-SPEC", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:16Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: a route union covering every endpoint of the RealWorld API spec (users, profiles, articles, comments, tags), each with typed request/response records, and a recorded repo location (e.g. spiral/apps/realworld). Next step: list the spec's endpoints from the official Postman collection. TypeFeatures: routes as a GADT indexed by the response type. Parent: SPIRAL-REALWORLD (split by org2 11-09: 2400 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_realworld_1_spec_2 () = Note ("REALWORLD-1-SPEC", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:19Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:2x DRAFT + one open design question. Home decided: spiral/apps/realworld (new package, spiral.toml per PACKAGE-MODEL-STANDARD). Draft realworld_api.spi (unstaged, not yet gated): the 19 RealWorld endpoints as conduit_route r, a GADT indexed by the response type (Login/Register/CurrentUser/UpdateUser -> conduit_user; GetProfile/Follow/Unfollow -> conduit_profile; ListArticles/Feed -> article_list; GetArticle/Create/Update/Favorite/Unfavorite -> conduit_article; DeleteArticle/DeleteComment -> no_content; AddComment -> conduit_comment; GetComments -> list conduit_comment; GetTags -> list string), conduit_* records named to avoid bare-open clashes, and route_method / route_path / route_auth_of (Required | Optional | Anonymous) per the spec, with 2 rust tests. OPEN: the 19-case GADT alone weighs 1183 (cell budget 272) and a type cannot span cells, so the budget-clean shape is sub-GADTs (user / profile / article-read / article-write / comment / favorite routes, 2-4 cases each) under a wrapper whose constructors carry a polymorphic index; that constructor shape needs a compile proof before it is the design. Next step: gate the draft as-is on a node to prove the GADT + forall functions compile, then restructure into sub-GADTs and re-gate.")
inl note_of_realworld_1_spec_3 () = Note ("REALWORLD-1-SPEC", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:29Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Gate 1 failed (real bug): or-patterns joined GADT constructors with different response indices (Login|Follow = conduit_user vs conduit_profile). Restructured: plain sub-unions per response type (or-patterns legal), 2-level GADT conduit_route r = Account (account r) | Content (content r) with comments r sub-GADT, http_method union, route_spec record + spec builder; budget oracle clean. Gate 2: index-passing constructors need an explicit forall (| Account :: \\* r. account r -> conduit_route r). Gate 3 queued as org2-rw3.")
inl note_of_realworld_1_spec_4 () = Note ("REALWORLD-1-SPEC", 4u32, "2026-11-09T19:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 19:5x. Proof: ganymede job org2-rw3, Cells gate of spiral/apps/realworld/realworld_api.spi rc=0, 2/2 rust tests passed (a route names its method, path and auth; public and profile routes follow the spec). Covers all 19 RealWorld endpoints (users 4, profiles 3, articles 5 + favorite 2, listings 2, removals 2, comments 2, tags 1) with typed request/response records; routes are conduit_route r indexed by the response type (2-level: Account/Content over account r / content r, comments r sub-GADT). Budget oracle clean. Lessons: GADT or-patterns must share an index; index-passing constructors need an explicit forall. Location: spiral/apps/realworld (spiral.toml, unstaged).")
inl realworld_2_model () = Task ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", "Conduit domain model and in-memory store: users, follows, articles, favorites, comments, tags, with tests", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "REALWORLD-1-SPEC", "team:org,spiral,app", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_realworld_2_model () = Planning ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_1 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:16Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: store operations for each spec action with rust tests (create/get/list/update/delete, follow/favorite toggles, tag listing). Next step: the user/article records and an id-keyed store. TypeFeatures: phantom ids per entity (id user vs id article). Parent: SPIRAL-REALWORLD (split by org2 11-09: 2400 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_2 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 2u32, "2026-11-09T20:11Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:1x: FIRST INCREMENT authored + budget-clean; compile-gate RUNNING on ganymede (bg task bsg7cnnt0, notifies on completion). New module spiral/apps/realworld/realworld_model.spi (added to spiral.toml modules, unstaged). Phantom-typed ids as a result-indexed GADT: id t with Id :: forall t. i32 -> id t, so id user and id article are DISTINCT types (the typefeatureset point) + id_raw + id_eq. Stored entities user/article/comment, distinct from the api wire shapes conduit_* (user holds password_hash not token; article/comment carry id user / id article authorship). Id-keyed store record (users/articles/comments/follows/favorites assoc lists + next_id) with empty_store + create_user (threads next_id). 3 helper-free rust tests: phantom-id distinctness, empty_store next_id=1, create advances the counter. Cell-budget oracle clean (max 218 of 272). Box zero compute (authored on box; gate off-box). NEXT increment: get_user/list/update/delete + follow/unfollow + favorite/unfavorite toggles + tag listing (listm try_find + optionm map), each with a rust test, per the DoD.")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_3 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:15Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:1x: GATE GREEN off-box on europa (Cells gate, SPIRAL_CELLS_GATE_WINDOW=0 on a quiet node load 0.15). spiral-tests: discovered 3, executed 3, passed 3, failed 0, GATE-EXIT=0. The phantom-id GADT + entities + store + create_user compile and the 3 rust tests pass: phantom-id distinctness (id user vs id article distinct types, erasing to i32), empty_store next_id=1, create advances the counter. First increment VERIFIED. Progress 0 to 25pct. Box zero compute. Next increment (unblocked, helpers pinned - listm try_find + optionm map): get_user/list_users/update/delete + follow/unfollow + favorite/unfavorite + tag listing, each with a rust test.")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_4 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 4u32, "2026-11-09T20:26Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:2x: SECOND INCREMENT green off-box europa (6/6: discovered 6 executed 6 passed 6 failed 0, GATE-EXIT=0). Added store ops: pair_key/pair_val (tuple-match accessors; no fst/snd in lib/spiral), get_user (listm try_find by id + match), create_article, follow + is_following (directional via the (id user,id user) follows relation - phantom-id pairs working), favorite. 3 new tests green: get_user finds a created user; follow is directional (1to2 true, 2to1 false); create_article advances the counter. Facts pinned: listm try_find returns standard Some/None; bare-tuple match (a,_)/(_,b) works; record-update with and cons-vs-field :: spacing all compile. Budget clean, box zero compute. Progress ~50pct. NEXT: list_users + update_user/delete_user, unfollow, unfavorite + is_favorited, get_tags (dedup over article tag_lists), comments CRUD, each with a rust test, to complete the DoD.")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_5 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 5u32, "2026-11-09T20:32Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:3x: THIRD INCREMENT green off-box europa (10/10: discovered 10 executed 10 passed 10 failed 0). Added removal/update ops, all listm filter + ternary + try_find (no new helpers): is_favorited, unfollow, unfavorite, delete_user, update_user (filter-out old + cons new). 4 new tests green: unfollow removes the edge, favorite toggle round-trips (fav then unfav: true then false), update_user replaces in place (jake to neo via get_user), delete_user removes it (get_user gone). Store CRUD + both relation toggles (follow/favorite) complete. Progress ~75pct. PINNED for the last piece: list and list-prime are DISTINCT types with listm box : list to list-prime and unbox : list-prime to list, and listm map is on list-prime - so list_users/get_tags map via unbox (map fn (box xs)). REMAINING DoD: comments CRUD (add/get/delete, proven cons/try_find/filter), list_users (box/unbox map pair_val), get_tags (flatten article tag_lists + dedup - needs concat/distinct, the one unpinned bit).")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_6 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 6u32, "2026-11-09T20:37Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:3x: FOURTH INCREMENT green off-box europa (13/13: discovered 13 executed 13 passed 13 failed 0). Added comments CRUD (add_comment cons+next_id, get_comment try_find, delete_comment filter) + list_users via the list/list-prime box-unbox map idiom (listm unbox (map pair_val (box s::users))) - list and list-prime are DISTINCT types. 3 new tests green: add then get comment (body nice), delete_comment removes it, list_users returns created (head match jake). Progress ~90pct. get_tags (collect over article tag_lists + a str_distinct dedup helper using listm collect:16 flatMap + contains:829) is gating now (btyfbub8f) - the last DoD op (tag listing). On green REALWORLD-2-MODEL covers every DoD store op: create/get/list/update/delete, follow/favorite toggles, tag listing, each with a rust test.")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_7 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 7u32, "2026-11-09T20:41Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:4x: DONE - get_tags fixed + green, 14/14 (discovered 14 executed 14 passed 14 failed 0). FIX: (pair_val p)::tag_list hit ETY-TermError - field access on the generic pair_val's type variable v cannot resolve (the earlier ops were pinned by id_eq's signature; get_tags had nothing to pin v). Replaced with a concrete-typed accessor: article_tag_list (p : id article * article) : list string = match p | (_,a) => a::tag_list, so the article type is known at the field access. get_tags = str_distinct (listm collect article_tag_list s::articles); collect:16 is flatMap on plain list, str_distinct dedups via contains:829 + a curried recursive loop. DoD MET: every store op has a rust test - create (user/article/comment), get (user/comment), list (list_users), update (update_user), delete (user/comment), follow+favorite toggles (is_following/is_favorited), tag listing (get_tags distinct); phantom-typed ids throughout (id user != id article). 14 tests green off-box europa; box zero compute, unstaged. Article/comment listing are trivial repeats of list_users for the later route->store layer (REALWORLD-3).")
inl note_of_realworld_2_model_8 () = Note ("REALWORLD-2-MODEL", 8u32, "2026-11-09T20:49Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 11-09 16:4x: POST-DoD model-completeness increment green off-box (17/17). Added the read ops the api endpoints need + REALWORLD-3-AUTH (rig) will consume: get_article (try_find by id), list_articles (box/unbox map pair_val), list_comments (filter by comment_of_article predicate matching c::article, then box/unbox map). 3 new tests green: get_article finds a created article, list_articles returns created, list_comments filters by article (sample comment on article 2, head body nice). Fills the GetArticle/ListArticles/GetComments read side the model lacked. Item stays Done (DoD was met at 14 tests); this is downstream-consumer completeness. 17 tests total, box zero compute.")
