inl note_of_showcase_s1_gadt_rules_2 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S1-GADT-RULES", 2u32, "2026-11-09T19:50Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 16:0x DRAFTED (scratch, not in tmp/samples yet): source = archive 20261101-080304 blob A43822B6 (vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md section 1, fiscal rules as typed data). showcase_gadt_rules: edition-3 rewrite following the gadt and contract siblings (a recursive rule t GADT, constructors bind their own vars, inl rec eval over money/rate nominals; main returns 108 for a dynamic base of 12000) plus showcase_gadt_rules_negative (When (Base, ...): rule money where rule bool belongs). Rust attempt (enum Rule<T> + fn eval<T>, Copy derived so only the GADT failure remains): stable rustc 1.99.1 gives exactly 3 errors, all E0308 'expected type parameter T, found Money/Money/bool' with 'the caller chooses a type for T which can be different from Money'; rust_attempt.expect holds the first error line and that note. Ganymede has only nightly rustc (1.102.0-nightly), so the stable check ran on the box (one 40-line compile). OPEN: the Spiral side (test.ps1 -Suite all -Backend C,Rust -Filter showcase_gadt_rules) needs a tree with apps/compiler and deps; asked compiler which tree to use before copying the dirs in.")
