inl note_of_showcase_s2_hidden_stages_2 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S2-HIDDEN-STAGES", 2u32, "2026-11-09T19:41Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Samples written: hidden_stages (policy = | Policy :: \\* s. s * (s -> i32 -> s * i32) -> policy; a spend cap with i32 state and a dedupe with list i32 state run from one list, expected exit 180 = cap 110 + unique 70 over [40; 30; 40]) and hidden_stages_escape_negative (leak returns the hidden state as i32). Rust attempt hidden_stages/rust_attempt.rs on ganymede rustc 1.102.0-nightly: error[E0191] the value of the associated type State in Policy must be specified, at Vec<Box<dyn Policy>>. Next step: rows from job org2-s4b (filter now decimal_scales|reflection_diffs|hidden_stages).")
inl note_of_showcase_s2_hidden_stages_3 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S2-HIDDEN-STAGES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:09Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 20:1x. -Suite all -Filter hidden_stages -Backend C,Rust -Native on ganymede (run single-flight-20261109-200353): samples/hidden_stages C ok exit 180, Rust ok exit 180 oracle agree (cap policy with i32 state 110 + dedupe policy with list i32 state 70, both behind one policy type). Negative hidden_stages_escape_negative: single typed error 'Got: i32 Expected: s In the definition: leak' (the hidden state cannot leave its pack), now an ExpectedErrors row in tests/matrix.psd1. Rust attempt rust_attempt.rs, rustc 1.102.0-nightly: error[E0191] the value of the associated type State in Policy must be specified (Vec<Box<dyn Policy>>). Spiral fact found: GADT existentials must be explicit, | Policy :: (\\? s. ...) -> policy, packed with Policy (\\? (...)) and opened with := \\? s. state, step = payload; an implicit \\* s. is ETY-GadtImplicitExistential.")
