inl note_of_showcase_s3_hkt_rule_1 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S3-HKT-RULE", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:42Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Next step: write S3; note the report says its GAT test COMPILED in Rust, so the showcase must state honestly what Rust can do. TypeFeatures: HKT. DoD: a sample under spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples with a C/Rust row in the matrix, plus its best stable-Rust attempt as a file next to it whose real rustc error text is checked by a test (re-run on the newest stable rustc). Source: archive 20261101-080304 files/vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md (the Rust attempts get rewritten from it). Parent: SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST (split by org2 11-09: 360 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_showcase_s3_hkt_rule_2 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S3-HKT-RULE", 2u32, "2026-11-09T19:38Z", "compiler", "11-09 15:5x compiler: SAMPLE WRITTEN + RUN (unstaged): spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/showcase_hkt_one_rule/ (main.spi + package.spiproj with core-). One rule, reserve_and_bill \\* (m : * -> *) {(>>=); on_succ}., over cores monad prototypes (option + list instances from core/monad.spi) plus a NEW effect in 3 lines: :! audited a = { value; trail } with :+ (>>=) and :+ on_succ. Built for C on ganymede (installed pack78): compile rc 0, C program 1,406 bytes, exit 7 = 300/100 + 2 scenarios + 2 trail entries. The generated C keeps ONLY the runtime stock branch; the scenario count and trail length are compiler-computed constants (v13 = v12 + 2l; v14 = v13 + 2l), the claim of the 11-01 doc. Rust backend compiles too. RUST, honestly: rust_attempt.rs (fn reserve_and_bill<M> ... -> M<i32>) fails with error[E0109]: type arguments are not allowed on type parameter `M` (checked text in rust_attempt.expect); rust_gat_emulation.rs (trait Effect { type Of<T>; ... }) COMPILES and exits 7 for Option + Vec, so the page must say Rust can do this with GATs, and the Spiral win is: no per-effect trait impl boilerplate, effects resolved at compile time, the async-without-Box case still needing an unstable feature (doc). PENDING for the DoD: (1) the rustc check ran on ganymedes default rustc 1.102.0-nightly 2026-11-07, but the DoD says newest STABLE: rerun with stable and pin the expect text; (2) wire rust_attempt.expect into a test (a -Suite row or a test.ps1 check that runs rustc and greps the expect line); (3) first -Suite all with the new sample (-Accept its row). Releasing my claim; org owns the showcase page.")
inl note_of_showcase_s3_hkt_rule_3 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S3-HKT-RULE", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:41Z", "compiler", "11-09 15:4x compiler, DoD item (1) BLOCKED BY POLICY, not by work: ganymede has NO stable rustc (rustup toolchains: nightly default + nightly-2026-11-05), by design: RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE (P0, user) puts every Rust build on one dated nightly. The DoDs \"re-run on the newest stable rustc\" contradicts that. Options for org: (a) accept the pinned nightly as the reference rustc (E0109 for the direct form is a long-standing stable error too, so the verdict is not nightly-only), or (b) check stable in a throwaway container (rust:stable image) so no node gains a second default toolchain. Not installing stable on a node without a decision. Evidence so far: nightly 1.102.0 2026-11-07: rust_attempt.rs -> error[E0109] (x3, one per M<i32>), rust_gat_emulation.rs compiles, exit 7.")
