inl note_of_showcase_s4_decimal_scales_1 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S4-DECIMAL-SCALES", 1u32, "2026-11-09T18:42Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Next step: write S4 first, the report's strongest case, and the Rust attempt with generic_const_exprs on stable. TypeFeatures: type-level numbers. DoD: a sample under spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples with a C/Rust row in the matrix, plus its best stable-Rust attempt as a file next to it whose real rustc error text is checked by a test (re-run on the newest stable rustc). Source: archive 20261101-080304 files/vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md (the Rust attempts get rewritten from it). Parent: SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST (split by org2 11-09: 360 m never fits a round).")
inl note_of_showcase_s4_decimal_scales_2 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S4-DECIMAL-SCALES", 2u32, "2026-11-09T18:45Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 18:5x SOURCE READ + BLOCKER. Source restored (archive 20261101-080304, files/_home_claude_showcase_deliverables_vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md, section \"## 4.\", lines 156-189): nominal amount currency scale = i64, nominal qty uom scale = i64; times : qty u s1 -> amount c s2 -> amount c (add s1 s2); rescale reads s_from via real_core.type_lit_to_lit; the claimed Rust output is wrapping_mul, + 5e11, / 1e12 (half-up from scale 14 to 2); 3 negatives must fail to compile (no rescale: Got amount brl (add 4i32 10i32) / Expected amount brl 2i32; BRL + USD; scale 2 + scale 4); the Rust attempt Amount<C, { S1 + S2 }> -> \"generic parameters may not be used in const operations\". BLOCKER: the sample `open type_arith`, and no type_arith module exists in today's lib (type_lit_to_lit does: sized_array, pickler, keccak, f32_trits use it), and the compiler has no type-level arithmetic of its own (the only \"add\" in spiral_compiler.fs is a codegen combinator). Next step: find type_arith (memory polyglot-spiral-dib-kernel-salvage: fc1943s/polyglot @ 053c128d, or the archive's other files) and port it to lib as an edition-3 module with tests; only then write the S4 sample.")
inl note_of_showcase_s4_decimal_scales_3 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S4-DECIMAL-SCALES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:02Z", "compiler", "11-09 15:0x compiler: the BLOCKER is not real. type_arith is a CORE module, not a lib one: deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin/core/type_arith.spir (listed in core/package.spiproj:5, so every |core- package sees it): nominal add/sub/mult/div/divup over type_lit_to_lit. Since pack75 (pack77 now, installed on ganymede + europa), inference FOLDS those ops over literals to a type literal before unify (TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD, Done; tibia probe3 green on the installed pack, incl. a negative with ETY-TermError Unification failure). Working lib example: lib/spiral/sized_array.spi (merge : sized a el -> sized b el -> sized (type_arith::add a b) el; test at 137: sized (type_arith::add 2 3) i32). So the S4 sample can write amount c (type_arith::add s1 s2) today; no port needed. Expect the negatives message to show the FOLDED literal (Got amount brl 14 ...), not add 4 10, because the fold runs before unify: write the expected text from a real run, not from the 11-01 markdown. Build/check S4 on ganymede or europa (pack77); box and moon still run the pre-fold pack until moon frees.")
inl note_of_showcase_s4_decimal_scales_4 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S4-DECIMAL-SCALES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T19:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 19:0x CORRECTION to note 2 (thanks compiler): the \"blocker\" was wrong. type_arith EXISTS as a CORE module, deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin/core/type_arith.spir (core/package.spiproj:5), nominal add/sub/mult/div/divup, and since pack75 inference folds them over literals before unify (TYPE-ARITH-3-FOLD, Done); working example lib/spiral/sized_array.spi (sized (type_arith::add a b) el). My search covered lib and the compiler only, not core. So `amount c (type_arith::add s1 s2)` works today (pack77). Gotcha: a negative's expected text shows the FOLDED literal (e.g. 14i32), not `add 4 10`, so take it from a real run. House rules for the sample: SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST note 4. Next step: write the S4 sample in apps/compiler/tmp/samples with the 3 negatives, run it on a node to capture the real messages.")
inl note_of_showcase_s4_decimal_scales_5 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S4-DECIMAL-SCALES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T19:17Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Samples written: decimal_scales (exit 7374) + 3 negatives (unrounded, currency, scale), budget clean. Rust attempt decimal_scales/rust_attempt.rs on ganymede rustc 1.102.0-nightly: 2x 'error: generic parameters may not be used in const operations' at Amount<C, { S1 + S2 }> (help: add generic_const_exprs). Next step: suite job org2-s4 (-Suite all -Filter decimal_scales -Backend C,Rust -Native) then ExpectedErrors rows with the real negative messages.")
inl note_of_showcase_s4_decimal_scales_6 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S4-DECIMAL-SCALES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T19:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 20:0x. -Suite all -Filter decimal_scales -Backend C,Rust -Native on ganymede (run single-flight-20261109-195652, compiler 76ef79e3ab87 = box): samples/decimal_scales C ok exit 206, Rust ok exit 206 oracle agree (206 = 7374 mod 256: 4.25 L x 1.7350000000 BRL = 73.74 BRL at scale 2). Negatives, each a single typed error, now ExpectedErrors rows in tests/matrix.psd1: currency 'Got: amount brl 2i32 Expected: amount usd 2i32'; scale 'Got: amount brl 2i32 Expected: amount brl 4i32'; unrounded 'Got: add 4i32 10i32 Expected: 2i32' (times yields scale 4+10 and the type refuses it as scale 2 without rescale). Rust attempt rust_attempt.rs, rustc 1.102.0-nightly: 2x 'generic parameters may not be used in const operations' at Amount<C, { S1 + S2 }>. Trap fixed on the way: samples need packages |core- (bundled core with type_arith and operators), not core- (local samples/core).")
