inl note_of_showcase_s6_six_languages_2 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES", 2u32, "2026-11-09T19:45Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:4x tibia (help pool). KERNEL PICKED: showcase 1's IBS/CBS rule GADT (source: archive 20261101-080304, extract files/_home_claude_showcase_deliverables_vitrines_spiral_vs_rust.md, sections 1 + 6), which section 6 says compiled to Rust 21 / F# 12 / TS 16 / Delphi-FPC 32 / Python 29 / C 20 lines. Ported from the old syntax (union rec / inl / match) to edition 3 in the showcase_hkt_one_rule layout: nominal money/rate, `:| ^ rule t` with Base/Const/RateBp/Apply/Above/When, a GADT-refined `eval \\* t`, cbs_rule = When (Above (Base, Const 10000), Apply (Base, RateBp 90), Apply (Base, RateBp 36)), and main reading the base through a host literal $\"20000\" (expected 20000*90/10000 = 180). Draft: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES\\showcase_fiscal_kernel\\ (compiler samples are compiler's tree, so the draft lives in drafts until compiler takes it). BACKENDS today (SpiralCompiler --help): Fsharp|C|Rust|Pascal|Zig|Wasm|Wgsl|Calyx|Kotlin|Swift|OpenQasm|Ebpf|Lean|Bend|TypeScript|Lua|Gleam|Cpp+Cuda|Python+Cuda, so all six of section 6 exist (Pascal = Delphi/FPC, Python via \"Python + Cuda\"). Gate: ganymede job-1794253524587-tibia-s6 (compile all six; run C and Rust, expecting exit 180; Python/Pascal/TS run only if their toolchain is present). The Rust-attempt half of the DoD (rust_attempt.rs + an .expect checked against the newest stable rustc, E0308 per section 1) is next.")
inl note_of_showcase_s6_six_languages_3 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T19:55Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:5x tibia: RUST HALF VERIFIED (ganymede job-1794253618989-tibia-s6rust): rust_attempt.rs (enum Rule<T> { Base, Const(T), RateBp(i32), Apply, Above, When } + fn eval<T>) fails as section 1 says: `error[E0308]: mismatched types` at `Rule::Base => Money(it.base.0)`, \"expected type parameter `T`, found `Money`\"; rust_attempt.expect (that header line) MATCHED. CAVEAT: ganymede's rustc is 1.102.0-nightly (2026-11-07), not stable; E0308 is the same on every channel, but the DoD says the newest STABLE rustc, so that run is still owed (europa or a codespace with stable). SIX-BACKEND GATE first run: all six failed BEFORE the code, with \"Package /root/s6/core is not loaded\", because the template's `packages: core-` only resolves inside compiler's samples tree (the mirror lacks apps/compiler/tmp). The gate copy now names packageDir = the compiler package dir (which holds core); the draft keeps the template form. Rerun: job tibia-s6b.")
inl note_of_showcase_s6_six_languages_4 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T19:57Z", "tibia", "11-09 15:5x tibia: the stable-rustc run is still OWED, and no node has stable today: ganymede has 1.102.0-nightly, and europa has only nightlies (1.101.0-nightly active; nightly-2026-10-18 / -11-05). Installing a stable toolchain on europa is an infra change there (org agrees europa plans first), so it was not done. Options: a codespace (rig's driver installs stable rustup), or org approves `rustup toolchain install stable` on europa. The E0308 itself does not vary by channel.")
inl note_of_showcase_s6_six_languages_5 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T19:58Z", "tibia", "11-09 16:0x tibia: SIX-BACKEND GATE GREEN (ganymede job-1794254128017-tibia-s6b, pack77). One Spiral source -> C 20 lines, Rust 21, F# 12, TypeScript 16, Pascal (Delphi/FPC) 34, Python 30. The first four REPRODUCE the archived doc's section-6 counts exactly (C 20 / Rust 21 / F# 12 / TS 16); Pascal +2 and Python +1 vs 32/29. RUN: C exit 180, Rust exit 180, Python exit 180 = 20000*90/10000, the GADT interpreter fully erased (C output 396 bytes). Pascal and TypeScript are compile-verified only (no fpc or bun on ganymede). Rust attempt: E0308 as expected (note 3), the stable-rustc run owed (note 4). REMAINING DoD (compiler's tree): copy %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES\\showcase_fiscal_kernel\\ (main.spi, package.spiproj in the template form, rust_attempt.rs, rust_attempt.expect) into spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/ and add its C/Rust row to the matrix; then the expect test on stable rustc.")
inl note_of_showcase_s6_six_languages_6 () = Note ("SHOWCASE-S6-SIX-LANGUAGES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T20:00Z", "compiler", "11-09 16:0x compiler: LANDED in the samples tree (unstaged): apps/compiler/tmp/samples/showcase_fiscal_kernel/ (tibias draft, read in full: main.spi, package.spiproj core-, rust_attempt.rs, rust_attempt.expect). Suite rows: every samples/ dir with an entry is an examples row with the default backends F#, C, Rust, Pascal (test.ps1 Get-ExampleBackends), so C + Rust need no matrix edit; I ADDED it to tmp/tests/matrix.psd1 AlsoTypeScript and Python (one line each; the matrix parses, both lists contain it), so its rows cover all 6 languages the showcase claims (F#, C, Rust, Pascal, TypeScript, Python). The first -Suite all on ganymede records them (next compiler pack gate). Still owed: the stable-rustc expect run. No node has stable (RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE); fiscal ran S1s on the boxs stable 1.99.1, the same route for this one, or the container option on SHOWCASE-S3. Wait: train:TRAIN42e (next pack gate).")
