inl note_of_sps_nb_3_renaming_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-3-RENAMING", 2u32, "2026-11-09T20:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig (help pool, claimed), DRAFT + GATE RUNNING. Located the sample's renaming/weakening section (main.spi ~880-1200: weaken_exact_linear_indexed_variable, the exact_linear_indexed_variable_renaming GADT with Identity/Weaken, the two apply functions for membership and single-use, the runtime depth walk, the three-step plan and their terminals). PORTED against NB-2's landed names per tibia's mapping (MembershipThere / SingleUseThere, Variable (VariableAt (\\? (m, u, note))), extend / unused / used / zero / meta_succ, one_unit, empty_usage, term_label): drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-3-RENAMING\\linear_renaming.spi, its own module after linear_terms (NB-2's file untouched). Shapes: renaming sc ss su tc ts tu d = RenameIdentity note | RenameWeaken (prefix, note) moving to (extend mc h) (meta_succ ms) (unused mu); renamed_membership / renamed_single_use apply one plan in lockstep; renamed_variable rebuilds the term; renaming_depth replaces the sample's reflected runtime counter with a plain i32; weaken = the one-step plan. Terminals as :# tests with ///> rust: weakening keeps the variable (term_label \"variable\"); a three-step plan (concrete heads bool, unit, bool) renames in lockstep with depth 3. Gate on ganymede (tibia's nb2.sh recipe, 2 pinned cores, box kernel src + the draft): /root/rig-jobs/nb3.sh, output nb3.out.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_3_renaming_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-3-RENAMING", 3u32, "2026-11-09T20:53Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, proof: GREEN on ganymede (tibia's nb2 recipe, 2 pinned cores; box apps/kernel/src incl. NB-2's linear_terms + the draft, linear_renaming registered after linear_terms): package --check rc 0; run_notebook --gate rc 0, spiral-tests discovered 2 executed 2 passed 2 failed 0. CELL BUDGET 0 findings (the awk oracle from memory cell-budget-awk-oracle, limit 273 for cells 1-9 and 272 after): 19 cells, largest 268; the first version had 5 over (the GADT head 329, the three apply/rebuild cells 287-309, three_steps 494) and passed the gate anyway, so the budget was fixed by short type-variable names, short notes and four type aliases (three_heads, three_slot, three_usage, three_plan), then the gate re-run on the final text (same green). Final draft: drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-3-RENAMING\\linear_renaming.spi (sha below). DoD status: notebook shape yes, tests yes with ///> rust, names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_ yes, budget 0 yes, gate green yes; NOT done by rig: the comparison with the mega sample's typecheck output for the moved definitions, and the apply (spiral is org's: copy to apps/kernel/src/linear_renaming.spi and add linear_renaming after linear_terms in package.spiproj, the way org2 applied NB-2).")
