inl note_of_sps_nb_4_substitution_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4-SUBSTITUTION", 1u32, "2026-11-09T19:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Next step: locate this module's definitions in the mega sample (grep its section) and move them with their terminals as tests. DoD: the module is a notebook (///- --package ., static prelude for opens only) whose terminals are :# tests with ///> targets (static/build_only only where compile-time), names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, cell budget 0 findings, Cells gate green; its typecheck output matches the mega sample's for the moved definitions. Template: regex/html notebooks. Source: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency/main.spi (11,835 lines). Parent: SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT (split by org2 11-09: 480 m never fits a round). TypeFeatures: keeps the sample's GADTs/existentials as they are.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_4_substitution_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4-SUBSTITUTION", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:11Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 22:1xZ slice 1 (unstaged): spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_substitution.spi, registered after linear_renaming in apps/kernel/src/package.spiproj. idsub (the sample's exact_linear_indexed_identity_substitution) over NB-2's term/intro/elim as an inline recursive group (:= ^ idsub + :& := idsub_intro / idsub_elim), plus a structural size group. Gate (ganymede org2-ls5): rc=0 2/2 (identity_term size 2 -> 2, kind intro; closed_unit_conditional size 4 -> 4, kind elim); budget 0. Lessons: recursion over terms with existential packs must be INLINE (:= ^), since a :~ join point fails with 'Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var'; a :& group needs a ^ head. Next: the strengthening half (sample ~4400+), then the open typed substitution (sample 4075-4300).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_4_substitution_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4-SUBSTITUTION", 3u32, "2026-11-09T22:20Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 22:2xZ (scope: the substitution core + context strengthening; the rest split to SPS-NB-4B-OPEN-SUBST-STRENGTHEN). Unstaged in spiral/apps/kernel/src, registered in package.spiproj after linear_renaming: (1) linear_substitution.spi: idsub over term/intro/elim (inline := ^ group) + structural size; gate org2-ls5 rc=0 2/2. (2) linear_strengthening.spi: strengthen sc su tc tu (StrengthenHere | StrengthenThere with the tail usages packed explicitly (\\? b e. ...)) + mark_step (KeepUnused | KeepUsed), which folds the sample's ThereUnused/ThereUsed into one case for the cell budget with the same indices; the sample's tail/context plans; gate org2-lst4 rc=0 2/2 (removed one cell down; the newer used Unit kept). Budget 0 on both. Spiral facts: an opened existential must not reuse the function's forall names (ETY-ShadowedExists).")
