inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 1u32, "2026-11-09T19:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Next step: locate this module's definitions in the mega sample (grep its section) and move them with their terminals as tests. DoD: the module is a notebook (///- --package ., static prelude for opens only) whose terminals are :# tests with ///> targets (static/build_only only where compile-time), names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, cell budget 0 findings, Cells gate green; its typecheck output matches the mega sample's for the moved definitions. Template: regex/html notebooks. Source: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency/main.spi (11,835 lines). Parent: SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT (split by org2 11-09: 480 m never fits a round). TypeFeatures: keeps the sample's GADTs/existentials as they are.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:29Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:3x tibia: SLICE 1 GREEN, ready for org2 to apply (spiral is org's): drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION\\linear_reduction.spi (259B1074EB17) -> apps/kernel/src/linear_reduction.spi, registered after it gates (org2's new rule). Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5d; box kernel src incl. NB-2..4 + the draft): package --check rc 0; Cells linear_reduction 3/3; linear_terms 4/4 as the control. (The first run was red only because the box's linear_variable_strengthening.spi was mid-edit; org2 has since fixed it.) Budget: every cell <= 264. SCOPE = the sample's small_step core (main.spi:728-822) + the conditional step terminals (2093-2166): small_step = Branch (branch_step: TrueStep | FalseStep over one branch_parts alias, \\? g.) | Guard (guard_step: GuardStep, \\? gs gt b., recursive through small_step via a :& mutual group); step_source / step_target as inline recursive groups (:= ^ + :& :=, NB-4's lesson); step_preservation = step_target (as in the sample). Tests: a True step starts at an if-True and ends at its then branch; a False step ends at its else branch; a guard step rewrites only the guard (source is an elim, target's guard is the inner step's target BoolFalse). Deviation: the step terminals' notes are shortened for the budget; shapes and indices as in the sample. NOT IN SLICE 1 (about 230 more reduction definitions): beta steps (closed identity/tensor/application beta relations, main.spi:1961+), runtimes, the rest -> SPS-NB-5 slice 2+.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 3u32, "2026-11-09T22:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 22:3xZ slice 1 APPLIED: tibia's drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION\\linear_reduction.spi copied to spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_reduction.spi and registered after linear_variable_strengthening in package.spiproj (unstaged), only after a green gate on org2's mirror with the full kernel package (job org2-lred rc=0 3/3; budget 0 on the box copy). tibia's own proof: tibia-nb5d package --check rc 0, 3/3. Slice 2+ (about 230 beta/runtime definitions) remains.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:14Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:1x tibia: SLICE 2 GREEN, in the same draft (now 36FB72D1185E; supersedes note 2's hash, one file for org2 to apply). Adds the closed identity BETA step (sample main.spi:1961-2050): generic_variable / identity_term_for \\* y. (the generic identity lambda over NB-2's Variable/Intro), beta_relation y = BetaRelation of a closed argument, beta_source = Elim (Apply (identity, argument, empty merge)), beta_target = the argument, beta_step = BetaStep (\\? y. beta_relation y * string) packing the type. Tests (6 total now): + an identity beta redex steps to its argument (source elim, target the unit argument); the same relation works at Bool; a packed step still rebuilds the redex. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5e on the box's CURRENT kernel incl. org2's fixed linear_variable_strengthening): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 6/6; linear_terms 4/4. Budget: every cell <= 266. Deviation as before: shortened notes. LEFT (slice 3+): tensor beta (2353+), the generic closed_beta_relation over applications (2445+), and the runtime/terminal counterparts.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 5u32, "2026-11-09T23:19Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:2x tibia: SLICE 3 GREEN in the same draft (now C531D8A19F2A; one file for org2 to apply). Adds the closed TENSOR beta step (sample main.spi:2296-2388): unit_tail (Unit over (extend empty y) with the binder unused), left_only (NB-2's MergeStep over LeftOnly: only the left child uses the binder), tensor_lambda_for \\* y. = Lambda of Tensor (generic_variable, unit_tail, left_only), tensor_beta_source = Apply (tensor_lambda, argument), tensor_beta_target = Tensor (argument, Unit) (capture-avoiding substitution replaces only the left child), tensor_beta_step = TensorBetaStep (\\? y. closed y * string). Tests (8 now): + a tensor redex steps to the pair of its argument and Unit (source elim, the target's left child is the argument); a packed tensor step keeps its argument on the left. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5f, current kernel): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 8/8; linear_terms 4/4. Every cell <= 266. LEFT: the generic closed_beta_relation over applications (main.spi:2445+) and the runtime/terminal tags.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_6 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 6u32, "2026-11-09T23:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 23:1xZ slices 1+2 file APPLIED over spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_reduction.spi after a green gate on org2's mirror with the full kernel package (job org2-lred2 rc=0, 8/8 executed); tibia's own: package --check rc 0, 6/6.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_7 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 7u32, "2026-11-09T23:28Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:3x tibia: SLICE 4 GREEN in the same draft (now A2063C774B25; one file for org2). Adds the sample's UNIFIED closed beta relation (main.spi:2445-2490): closed_beta r = IdentityBeta (\\* y. closed y -> closed_beta y) | TensorBeta (\\* y. closed y -> closed_beta (tensor_type y unit_type)), closed_beta_source / closed_beta_target dispatching to slices 2-3, closed_beta_step = ClosedBetaStep (\\? r. closed_beta r * string). The module now also opens linear_substitution (NB-4) for its structural size. FIDELITY CHECK against the sample's own runtime assertions (main.spi:2510-2517): step_sizes gives identity (4 -> 1) and tensor (6 -> 3), the sample's exact numbers, so the NB-2 shape split did not change term sizes. Tests 10. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5g): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 10/10; linear_terms 4/4. LEFT: closed_recursive_beta_derivation (main.spi:2525+) and later reduction runtimes.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_8 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 8u32, "2026-11-09T23:58Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:0x tibia: SLICE 5 GREEN in the same draft (now 66FB7350E09C; one file for org2). Adds the first three cases of the sample's closed_recursive_beta_derivation (main.spi:2526-2540): derivation d r = Bound (a closed argument: derivation d d) | LeftUnit (derivation d r -> derivation d (tensor r unit)) | RightUnit (derivation d r -> derivation d (tensor unit r)); derivation_argument recovers the bound argument through any nesting; open_body builds the open lambda body (Bound = the generic variable; LeftUnit / RightUnit = a tensor of the inner body with a Unit tail, using left_only / a new right_only merge, NB-2's RightOnly). Tests (12 now): the bound argument survives nested tensors; the open body of RightUnit (LeftUnit (Bound b)) has structural size 5 (predicted before the run: two tensors + two Units + the variable). Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5h): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 12/12; linear_terms 4/4. Every cell <= 266. LEFT for NB-5: the derivation's remaining six cases (LeftBoolTrue, RightBoolFalse, the three conditional cases, ApplicationIdentity) and the runtime/terminal counterparts.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_9 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 9u32, "2026-11-10T00:03Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:1x tibia: SLICE 6 GREEN in the same draft (now 1CAF76ED611F; supersedes slice 5's hash, one file for org2). Adds the derivation's Bool-tail cases (main.spi:2541-2548: TensorLeftBoolTrue, TensorRightBoolFalse). The 6-case GADT no longer fit one cell, so derivation is now Bound | Units (unit_derivation: LeftUnit / RightUnit) | Bools (bool_derivation: LeftBoolTrue / RightBoolFalse), the two halves in a :& mutual group, and derivation_argument / open_body each became a three-part inline recursive group (:= ^ + :& :=). Same indices as the sample. Shared body_of / body_tail aliases; left_pair / right_pair take the tail, so Unit and Bool tails share one builder. Tests 13: slice 5's two (nested_derivation rewrapped in Units) + Bools (RightBoolFalse (Bools (LeftBoolTrue (Bound unit)))) keeps its argument and has open-body size 5. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5i): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 13/13; linear_terms 4/4. LEFT for NB-5: the three conditional derivation cases and ApplicationIdentity (main.spi:2550-2561), then runtimes.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_10 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 10u32, "2026-11-10T00:06Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:1x tibia: SLICE 7 GREEN in the same draft (now 078CC5C9EABD; one file for org2, superseding note 9's hash). Adds two more derivation cases from main.spi:2550-2561 as a third mutual sub-union (derivation = Bound | Units | Bools | Steps; step_derivation = IfTrue | ApplyIdentity, both derivation d r -> derivation d r): IfTrue's open body is if True then body else body with the guard over an unused binder (true_guard via tail_unused) and the guard-unused / branch-used merge (right_only, the sample's MergeUnusedUsed); ApplyIdentity's is an identity lambda living in the outer binder's context (its own binder newest, the outer one unused) applied to the body, the same merge. derivation_argument and open_body each gained a :& step part. Tests 14: + both keep the argument; predicted open-body sizes If (guard + 2 branches + If) = 4 and Apply (Apply + Lambda + 2 variables) = 4 held. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5j): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 14/14; linear_terms 4/4. Every cell <= 266. LEFT for NB-5: ConditionalTrueRightApplicationIdentity and ConditionalFalseDistinctBool (both compose the cases above), then the runtime/terminal counterparts.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_11 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 11u32, "2026-11-10T00:07Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:0xZ slices 1-5 APPLIED over spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_reduction.spi after org2's mirror gate with the full kernel package: rc=0, 13/13 executed, 0 unsupported (tibia: 12/12). Already registered after linear_substitution (via linear_variable_strengthening's position).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_12 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 12u32, "2026-11-10T00:12Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:2x tibia: SLICES 7+8 GREEN; the recursive beta derivation is now COMPLETE (all 9 sample cases, main.spi:2526-2561). The draft (AAD0EF0E2A02) supersedes the copy org2 applied at slice 6 (13/13). It adds step_derivation (IfTrue, ApplyIdentity, Forks) and fork_derivation (IfTrueRightApply: if True then body else identity applied to body; IfFalseDistinct: if False then (if True then body else body) else body), each in the :& groups for derivation_argument and open_body; shared if_with / true_guard / false_guard / if_body / apply_body builders; the guard-unused, branch-used merge is right_only (the sample's MergeUnusedUsed). Tests 15: + IfTrue and ApplyIdentity keep the argument with open-body sizes 4 and 4; the composed cases keep the argument with sizes 7 and 7. My pre-registered 6 for the right-apply body was a miscount (the application adds 4 nodes, not 3); the run's 7 is explained node by node and the expectation was corrected. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5l, the current kernel): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 15/15; linear_terms 4/4. Every cell <= 266. LEFT for NB-5: the runtime/terminal tag functions (outer_tag + step runtimes) only; the reduction relations themselves are all ported.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_13 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 13u32, "2026-11-10T00:14Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:2x tibia: DoD MET in draft (EB85BE858757), ready for org2's final apply over the slice-6 copy. Adds the sample's runtime tag check: outer_tag over NB-2's split term (Variable 0, Apply 1, Unit 2, BoolTrue 3, BoolFalse 4, Tensor 5, Lambda 6, If 7, the sample's exact_linear_indexed_term_outer_tag numbering, main.spi:2080-2088). TWO FIDELITY CHECKS against the sample's own runtime assertions now pass: (1) closed beta tags identity (1, 2) and tensor (1, 5), with sizes identity 4 to 1 and tensor 6 to 3 (main.spi:2510-2517); (2) the closed unit conditional's tag 7 (main.spi:2104). So the budget-forced shape split of NB-2/NB-5 preserves both the sample's term shapes and its node counts. Tests 17; gate (ganymede job tibia-nb5m, current kernel): package --check rc 0; linear_reduction 17/17; linear_terms 4/4; every cell <= 266. Scope delivered: small_step (+ source/target/preservation), identity and tensor beta, the unified closed_beta relation and step, the full 9-case recursive beta derivation (argument + open body), runtime tags. The sample's string-returning *_terminal wrappers are replaced by these :# tests, per the DoD.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_5_reduction_14 () = Note ("SPS-NB-5-REDUCTION", 14u32, "2026-11-10T00:22Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-10 00:2xZ (tibia's work, applied by org2). Final file applied over spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_reduction.spi (unstaged) after org2's mirror gate with the full kernel package: rc=0, 17/17 executed (job org2-lred3). Proof: tibia 17/17, with runtime tags matching the sample's own assertions (beta tags (1,2) and (1,5), the conditional's 7, sizes 4->1 and 6->3); budget 0. DoD: met.")
