inl note_of_sps_nb_6_progress_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", 1u32, "2026-11-09T19:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Next step: locate this module's definitions in the mega sample (grep its section) and move them with their terminals as tests. DoD: the module is a notebook (///- --package ., static prelude for opens only) whose terminals are :# tests with ///> targets (static/build_only only where compile-time), names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, cell budget 0 findings, Cells gate green; its typecheck output matches the mega sample's for the moved definitions. Template: regex/html notebooks. Source: spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency/main.spi (11,835 lines). Parent: SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT (split by org2 11-09: 480 m never fits a round). TypeFeatures: keeps the sample's GADTs/existentials as they are.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6_progress_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T00:30Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:3x tibia (claimed from the help pool), SCOPE MEASURED: NB-6 is not one 80 m notebook. The sample has 71 _terminal defs (the parent's count); by line: before 2600 (the NB-1..5 range) 20; 2600-7999 (open substitution/strengthening/open betas) 20; 8000-9499 (general reduction family + values + closed progress) 10; 9500+ (normalization) 21. So 51 terminals and 463 top-level defs remain after line 2600. Progress (main.spi:8874) is stated over the GENERAL reduction family (8061, 13 constructors: Conditional, ClosedAtomic, ClosedTensorLeft/Right, ClosedApplicationFunction/Argument, ClosedRecursiveBeta, Beta, Open{Identity,Tensor,Application,Lambda,Conditional}Beta), and the five open betas live in 6500-7999, a range no NB item names (NB-4/4B's modules cover part of 2600-7999 but cite no line ranges, so coverage there is unmeasured). PROPOSED SPLIT for org (not applied, org's item): NB-6A values + canonical forms (8803-8870, no reduction dependency; tibia starting it now as a slice); NB-6B open betas (6500-7999) after mapping NB-4/4B's coverage of 2600-7999; NB-6C the general reduction family + closed progress (8000-9499, 10 terminals); NB-6D normalization (9500+, 21 terminals).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6_progress_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T00:34Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:3x tibia: SLICE 6A GREEN, a NEW module drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS\\linear_values.spi (DC0C3AF07CEA; opens linear_types, linear_terms, linear_substitution; register after linear_open_substitution). Ports main.spi:8803-8870: the value judgment, its embedding value_term, the unit canonical form, and bool_canonical (CanonicalTrue/False). SHAPE (forced by the budget, mirrors NB-2's term split): the sample's ValueUnit/BoolTrue/BoolFalse share one payload, so they become ValueConstant over NB-2's constant family; the non-recursive ValueLambda joins it in leaf_value; value = Leaf | ValueTensor (the only recursive case). The canonical-form lemmas are partial matches the checker accepts only because the index rules out the other cases (unit_leaf, bool_constant). Tests 2: closed pair and identity embed with sizes 3 and 2; canonical forms read back (unit size 1; true and false). Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6b, current kernel + this module registered on the mirror only): --check rc 0; linear_values 2/2, 0 unsupported. The first shape (job tibia-nb6a) was also 2/2 but had 3 cells over budget. NEXT: 6B/6C/6D per note 2 (closed progress needs the general reduction family, main.spi:8061, which needs the open betas at 6500-7999).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6_progress_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T00:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 (org) 11-10 00:4xZ DECISION: tibia's measured 6A-6D split ACCEPTED. 6A APPLIED: spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_values.spi (value judgment, value_term, unit/bool canonical forms), registered after linear_open_substitution only after org2's mirror gate (job org2-lv rc=0 2/2; budget 0; tibia's own 2/2). Remaining parts opened as SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS, SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION, SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION. On coverage of 2600-7999: org2's NB-4/4B modules ported recursive_open_typed_substitution (~4075-4300), context/variable/term strengthening (~4881-5430) and identity substitution (~3624); 6B should first diff the sample's defs in 6500-7999 against those names.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6_progress_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T00:39Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "Proof: 6A linear_values gated rc=0 2/2 on org2's mirror with the full kernel package, budget 0, applied + registered. DoD for this item (re-scoped by the accepted split): 6A done; 6B/6C/6D carry the rest as their own items.")
