inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_1 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 1u32, "2026-11-09T19:14Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 15:3x microblog, from the DUPLICATE-CODE-SEMANTIC census (n2): two same-file lib clones folded, drafts in the kit drafts store spiral/LIB-CLONE-HEALS (with .base copies): f32_grads.spi probs_of (identical to softmax_of after alpha-renaming) deleted, its 2 callers (cross_entropy, cross_entropy_backward) now call softmax_of; xml.spi has_attribute_pair (identical to has_pair) deleted, missing_attribute calls has_pair. Grep over every repo .spi: no caller outside these files (tibia's soft_policy probs_of is its own definition). DoD: lib_gate.ps1 green for both files on a lib copy, then land via lib_land_window -ProvenLog. Gate staged on moon (joinpts/libclones/lib-clones-gate.ps1, draft hashes 446B5F93AC56 / FB782AACDF58, mirror bases 530275B20359 / 76E11AA15A87 checked), appended to run-moon-slot.ps1 so it rides the after-sim slot.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_2 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:01Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "NEXT STEP: when the moon after-sim slot (job-1794264025297-x-night-chain) reports, read joinpts/libclones/lib-clones-gate run summary: verdict ok -> land both drafts through lib_land_window with -ProvenLog; a red gate -> read its gate.log tail per file. TYPEFEATURES: none new; both folds delete a duplicate definition and keep the existing typed signature (floats -> floats; string -> string -> list (string * string) -> bool).")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_3 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T23:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 18:48 moon after-sim: lib-clones-gate verdict ok (run C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-clones-gate-20261109184803): lib_gate green for f32_grads.spi and xml.spi with both drafts applied on a lib copy whose bases matched (530275B20359 / 76E11AA15A87). NEXT STEP: land via lib_land_window -ProvenLog with that run's summary, after re-checking the box lib still equals the draft bases.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_4 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:07Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "NEXT STEP (precise, per memory lib-land-proof-on-node-copy-on-box): my green gate ran lib_gate.ps1, which -ProvenLog does not accept (it wants a lib_land_window close log: 'LANDED and closed green' plus a '<lib file> <hash>' line per draft). So: (1) on a free node mirror, run lib_land_window.ps1 -PrivateLib -Lib <mirror lib> -Draft <file>=<draft> -Label LIB-CLONE-HEALS -Apply to get that close log; (2) on the box, run lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -Label LIB-CLONE-HEALS -ProvenLog <that log> -Apply, which only copies under the tree-write window (no box compute).")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_5 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 groom 2 (digest: gate the exact bytes you apply): the land must carry exactly the gated drafts, f32_grads 446B5F93AC56 and xml FB782AACDF58 (lib_land_window's -BaseHash with the bases 530275B20359 / 76E11AA15A87 refuses a moved base). NEXT STEP unchanged: the -PrivateLib close on a node mirror, then the box -ProvenLog copy.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_6 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T03:55Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:1x microblog: PROOF STAGED per lib-land-proof-on-node-copy-on-box. (1) Round trip on the box: both drafts canonical true, fixpoint true. (2) Exact europa copy /home/remote/libland-1110/spiral: the tracked tree plus every git-ignored lib .spi/.spir/.spiproj (419 = box 419), deps = the shared symlink; the raw lib digest on europa equals the box's, 566F65D3485BD784, and the predicted post-land digest is FC38F0AB8FBBD35B on both. (3) Proof job x-libland-clone-proof: lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply with -BaseHash 530275B20359,76E11AA15A87, drafts 446b5f93ac56 / fb782aacdf58, SPIRAL_CELLS_SKIP_CLI_EXPORT=1, nice 19; a box poller submits it when europa admits it. Next step: when the proof log says LANDED and closed green with lib digest FC38F0AB8FBBD35B, recompute the box prediction (other lanes land meanwhile) and, if equal, run the box land with -ProvenLog; on a mismatch, refresh the europa tree from the newer box files and re-prove.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_7 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T06:13Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 02:1x: the proof REFUSED TWICE, correctly: lib_land_window's -BaseHash guard reported xml.spi changed since its draft was proven (now FCE8DD3E560D). Another lane landed additive xml_digits_* helpers into the box xml.spi at 11-09 16:58, after my .base was cut (76E11AA15A87). The earlier europa digest check matched only because both sides held the NEWER file, while the draft was built on the OLD one, so landing it would have silently reverted that lane's change. The guard caught it. REBASED: the same fold reapplied to the current xml.spi (the duplicate has_attribute_pair is removed and missing_attribute calls has_pair; the diff is exactly that), draft 3487D66E3B2B on base FCE8DD3E560D, round trip canonical + fixpoint; f32_grads unchanged (446B5F93AC56 on 530275B20359). Stale draft and base kept beside the new ones. Europa drafts and the proof script updated (-BaseHash 530275B20359,FCE8DD3E560D). Also fixed the submit poller: the old one re-submitted after a job that started and failed, so it would have looped; the new one exits on any job id. Next step: the x-libland-clone-proof2 run (it also carries LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS): read executed_cells and LANDED, then re-predict the box digest and land with -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_8 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T07:29Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 03:3x: the first box proof (job-1794291471630) TIMED OUT at its 1 h cap inside executed_cells (f32_grads's 13 cells compile for c and rust on a box at 100%; the testing-unbound false red only appears after the whole gate), so the undo never ran: only the PRIVATE copy kept the drafts (restored from .base); -PrivateLib takes no tree-write window and never touches the box lib; no leftover processes. The box lib moved twice meanwhile (other lanes' lands: leptos.spi, ui_dom.spi ...), so the private copy was refreshed from the box and its digest re-matched (9DFC1430F38FAC4F); both draft bases still equal the live files. RERUN: job-1794295760745-x-libland-proof-box2, 3 h cap, with the interim window script (a testing-unbound gate counts as UNMEASURED, not a failure). Next step: on LANDED, re-predict the box digest and land with -ProvenLog; if the box moved again, refresh and land right after a fresh proof.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_9 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 9u32, "2026-11-10T08:51Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:5x box2 proof (job-1794295760745, 79 min) CLOSED RED and was undone: document_test 26 passed, type_probe 2/2 PASS, consumers compile, but executed_cells xml.spi discovered 17 executed 17 FAILED 3. That run used the OLD direct-gate executed_cells (it started before the switch to lib_gate.ps1) and kept no raw output, so which 3 is unknown. The draft cannot change behaviour: has_pair (xml.spi:622) has the same body as the removed has_attribute_pair, and fiscal's lib gate had live xml 17/17 on moon, so the 3 most likely come from the direct-gate path (the same family of false reds that hit f32_grads). RE-PROVING with the lib_gate-based check: box job-1794300687658-x-libland-proof-chain waits for the box to hold under 70 percent CPU for 3 minutes (fiscal's rule), then lib_land_window -PrivateLib on the private copy, refreshed from live first (json.spi, json_scan.spi, state_core.spi, json_real.spir had moved). The undo dir holds no raw gate output; the new script writes it to <undo>/executed-cells/xml.spi.raw.txt, so a red now names its cells. NEXT STEP: read the chain tail; LANDED in the copy -> land on the box with -ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_10 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 10u32, "2026-11-10T09:14Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:2x RE-PROOF CLOSED RED AGAIN, now with a named cell (box job-1794300687658, lib_gate-based check, quiet box 05:00-05:03): document_test 26 passed, type_probe 2/2 PASS, executed_cells xml.spi 17 executed, 16 passed, 1 FAILED: code_points_step_through_utf8 on the PASCAL target only (builder exit 8192); undone. box2 had 3 failures on the same bytes, so the count moves between identical runs. The draft cannot reach that cell: it only swaps has_attribute_pair for the identical has_pair (xml.spi:622), nothing near the code_points path (code_point_at / pascal_code_point_at). Hypothesis: live xml.spi fails or flakes on that pascal cell too, which would make executed_cells block a land on a defect that already exists (a new fail-closed guard in a shared script should ship report-only, or compare against the live baseline). CONTROL RUNNING: box job-1794302047845-x-xml-control runs the same lib_gate.ps1 on the restored copy (xml.spi = live FCE8DD3E560D). NEXT STEP: control red on the same cell -> executed_cells counts only reds that the live baseline does not have (fix in lib_land_window), then re-prove; control green -> the pascal failure is real for the draft and gets traced.")
inl note_of_lib_clone_heals_11 () = Note ("LIB-CLONE-HEALS", 11u32, "2026-11-10T22:50Z", "microblog", "11-10 11:51 box BSOD killed my box gate (job-1794302397769 proof chain / job-1794302635550 pascal detail; both lost, no verdict). The user is present after the crash, so box stays light: relaunch when the box is quiet (pin SPIRAL_FPC to freepascal 3.3.1-20261025 in-process; the user env has no pin).")
