inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_m2_2 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-10T09:55Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 06:0x rig: the PLACEMENT MODEL is written and probe-green (src/rig_scratch_place/place.spi, new pure package, HostFree, unstaged; Cells notebook gate on ganymede 1/1). A scratch file is AlreadyPlaced when its content hash equals a repo file (no proposal), Diverged :: repo * path when only the name matches (a proposal addressed to the repo's owning lane, from an owners table passed in as data), or Unplaced (a proposal with no target, for triage); proposal_line renders one draft row per proposal. Not done: the IO verb that hashes the inventory's 154,808 deliverable-looking files and the repos, which is box IO beyond the CPU-light rule while the user is present, so it should run in the scratch-inventory's 03:40 idle slot or on a node copy. Next step: after TRAIN44 installs, wire a rig scratch place verb into the 03:40 schedule (read-only, writes the proposals as drafts).")
