inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_m3_2 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH-M3", 2u32, "2026-11-10T14:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 10:2x rig: the RULE is written and probe-green with its negative controls (new pure package kit src/rig_scratch_cited/cited.spi, HostFree, unstaged, hash 977cbf8d1394; Cells notebook gate on ganymede 2/2). note = { item; text } with the text normalized once (backslashes and every path boundary, space quote bracket comma = < > tab CR LF, become /, lower-case, // collapsed); a folder is KeptCited :: name * item when a note holds /<root>/<name>/ or, for names of 16+ characters (session ids), /<name>/ alone; otherwise Removable. Negative controls in the tests: a PREFIX of a cited folder (pack6 when a note cites pack6c/run.log) and a SHORT bare name (tmp) stay Removable. fates, removable_names and fate_line give the archive one line per folder. M2 is NOT a real precondition of this rule (the chain order came from kit agile split), so it was built while M2 waits on TRAIN44. Next step: the IO side, a rig verb (rig scratch cited <backlog> <scratch root>) that reads the notes from state/agile.spi, lists the folders and prints the fates; then the archive script (i574n.github scripts/scratch-archive.ps1, org-owned: rig asks before touching it) consults it before its -Apply removal. Both ride a train after TRAIN44.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_m3_3 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH-M3", 3u32, "2026-11-10T14:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 10:2x rig markers. TYPEFEATURES: a record (note), a union with a payload per case (folder_fate: Removable :: string, KeptCited :: string * string), option for the first citing item, inline string params; no joined-string rows (fate_line renders at the edge only). DoD: the archive keeps every folder a backlog note cites, proven by the negative controls in cited.spi plus one live dry run of the verb on the box scratch root. NEXT STEP: author the rig scratch cited verb (IO unit beside the pure model).")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_m3_4 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH-M3", 4u32, "2026-11-10T14:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 10:5x rig: VERB WRITTEN, rides TRAIN44 (unstaged). (1) rig_scratch_cited/cited.spi gained notes_of_state: every state line starting inl note_of_ is one note named by its first quoted field (the item id), so claims, waits and tasks never count; probe on ganymede 3/3 (hash fe3122e7ba7d), the third test proves a stored ESCAPED Windows path (C:\\\\t\\\\pack6c) still cites and its prefix still does not. (2) new package rig_scratch (entry.spi, HostFree): rig scratch cited <backlog root> <scratch root> reads every .spi under <backlog>/state (agile.spi plus the note segments), lists the directories under the scratch root and prints one fate line per folder plus rig scratch cited ok notes=N folders=N kept=N. It FAILS CLOSED: 0 notes read (a wrong backlog path) is exit 2, never all-removable. (3) wiring: VerbScratch in command_spec_domain/direct_verbs.spi (+ help line), rig_cli_model dispatch, rig_cli and rig_cli_model packages + link, Cargo member + rig_cli dependency + lock; bases archived at kit\\archive\\rig-scratch-verb-bases-20261110. Proof: the live dry run on the box scratch root after TRAIN44 installs.")
