inl note_of_kit_lint_smells_verb_1 () = Note ("KIT-LINT-SMELLS-VERB", 1u32, "2026-11-09T20:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Created 11-09 by rig to carry the wiring four other-team waits name. Models built and probe-queued: rig_lint_catalogue (DeepIf, OptionPresenceMatch; NESTED-IF-TOOL, LIST-SUGAR-SCAN), rig_test_placement (TestsClusteredAtEnd, >50pct trailing; SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES), rig_standards_md (md-census width; MD-LINE-LIMIT-120), rig_standards_toml (TOML-FORMAT-TAPLO). DoD: kit lint smells <root> [--paths] prints one finding per site with the model's fix text, ratchet mode against a baseline row per repo so existing sites read as baseline and growth fails, a negative control per rule, and each waiting item cleared by its owner once its rule fires. Shape: a new linked unit beside GRANULAR-LINT's kit lint macros (rig_standards is at 906 of 1000 generated lines, so the rules cannot go inline there); md and toml rules read git-listed files of their extension. NEXT STEP: after TRAIN43 snapshots and the probe batch passes the four models, add the lint smells subcommand in the lint entry and the linked unit. TYPEFEATURES: smell union per model, one finding record.")
