inl note_of_x_sim_redundant_suffix_1 () = Note ("X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX", 1u32, "2026-11-09T20:53Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 16:5x microblog, found in the moon sim verify's compile log (job-1794243181261): 50 compiler warnings WTY-RedundantLiteralSuffix in x's own sources, 31 in apps/sim/spi/exsss.spi (lines 18-108) and 19 in apps/sim/spi/sim_events.spi (lines 153-173). The compiler names each fix ('the context already gives this literal the type i32, so its suffix is redundant; write 0'). DO NOT APPLY YET, for 3 reasons: (1) both files feed the sim build, so an edit breaks gate 2's proof that the staged pluto artifact (sha 7D0FD0C6F9111070) is the verified source; (2) the sim posts its own source text, so the just-reviewed e2e fixtures would drift again; (3) a 50-site respell needs a sample shown first (user rule 11-07). DoD: the warnings at these 50 positions are gone (the compiler's own count is 0 for both files), with a sample of 5 shown before the rest, and the sim fixtures re-accepted in the same change. After the pluto redeploy.")
inl note_of_x_sim_redundant_suffix_2 () = Note ("X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:00Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-09 19:1x microblog: DRAFT READY, not applied (structured wait item:SERVE-TO-PLUTO). Drafts store x/X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX: exsss.spi + sim_events.spi with .base copies (sha 5901530609B0/7682220D1209). A perl drafter took the 50 sites straight from the compiler's warnings (file, line, column, 'write N'), asserted at each column that the source reads exactly <N><suffix>, and rewrote right to left per line: 50 applied, 0 refused (exsss 20 lines, sim_events 9). SAMPLE (5 of 50): exsss:18 'shl64 1u64 bits - 1u64' -> 'shl64 1 bits - 1' (2 sites); exsss:20 'low_bits 58i32' -> 'low_bits 58'; exsss:25 'x0 + 11400714819323198485u64' -> 'x0 + 11400714819323198485'; exsss:26 'shr64 x 30i32' -> 'shr64 x 30'. NEXT STEP: once the pluto cutover is done, copy the 2 drafts into x, compile (0 WTY-RedundantLiteralSuffix on both files), and re-accept the sim fixtures in the same change, since the sim posts its own source.")
inl note_of_x_sim_redundant_suffix_3 () = Note ("X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX", 3u32, "2026-11-10T02:08Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 02:1xZ microblog: wait cleared, the pluto cutover is done (SERVE-TO-PLUTO n34+). The draft in n2 can be applied now; NEXT STEP unchanged (copy the 2 drafts, compile to 0 warnings, re-accept the sim fixtures in the same change; that is node compute).")
