inl note_of_x_sim_redundant_suffix_11 () = Note ("X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX", 11u32, "2026-11-10T14:20Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 14:2xZ ROUND 3 DRAFTED (drafts x\\X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX\\round3, .base beside each file; live untouched). Source: the compiler's own capped list in the frames-1112 build log on europa (the compiler prints the first 50 per package; it reports 552 more). The drafter (round3\\draft.js) takes file:line:col plus the compiler's 'write N', asserts the source at that column reads exactly N plus a type suffix, and strips only the suffix, right to left per line: 50 applied, 0 refused (personas.spi 21 lines, scenario.spi 8, final_state.spi 4). SAMPLE (before | after): < has (\\ b => sm'::ends_with b s) [ \" \"; \"\\t\"; \"\\n\"; \"\\r\"; char_of 11i32; char_of 12i32 ]|> has (\\ b => sm'::ends_with b s) [ \" \"; \"\\t\"; \"\\n\"; \"\\r\"; char_of 11; char_of 12 ]|< { seed users = 8i32; edits = 3i32; breaking = 0i32; churn = 0i32; personas = []; branch_|> { seed users = 8; edits = 3; breaking = 0; churn = 0; personas = []; branch_tests = !- }|< := opened_levels () : i32 = 4i32|> := opened_levels () : i32 = 4. NEXT STEP: copy into x, run the sim build on a node (0 WTY-RedundantLiteralSuffix at these 50 positions; the next 50 surface for round 4), and re-accept the sim fixtures only if the posted source text changed.")
