inl lib_crypto_auth_primitives () = Task ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", "lib crypto: HMAC-SHA256, a password KDF and a constant-time compare, so auth stops needing a toy MAC", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "team:lib,lib,crypto,realworld", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives () = Planning ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_1 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-09T21:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: lib/spiral/crypto.spi (or a new auth_crypto module) exports hmac_sha256 (key, message -> bytes/hex, checked against RFC 4231 vectors), a password KDF (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with RFC 7914/6070-style vectors, or argon2id via the host crate per backend) and constant_time_equal over bytes; each with rust tests and the vectors as rows. Found by tibia 11-09 on REALWORLD-3-AUTH: apps/realworld/auth.spi takes an auth_crypto record { mac; same } and ships only toy_crypto for tests; register/login need the KDF. lib today has sha256 (host) and hmac_sha1_base64 only. Next step: decide host-crate (Rust hmac/sha2/pbkdf2, TS crypto.subtle) vs pure Spiral per backend via backend_switch. TypeFeatures: phantom key/digest nominals (secret, mac) so a MAC is never compared with a plain string. Proof: Cells gate green on the vector tests.")
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_2 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 2u32, "2026-11-09T21:29Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:3x tibia (claimed): DECISION on the recorded next step: HOST PRIMITIVES per backend, the pattern crypto.spi already uses for hmac_sha1_base64, NOT pure Spiral (hand-rolled crypto is where originality is most dangerous). Rust: hmac + sha2 + pbkdf2 + subtle crates; Gleam: Erlang crypto (crypto:mac, crypto:pbkdf2_hmac, crypto:hash_equals). DRAFT: drafts\\spiral\\LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES\\crypto.spi (the whole lib file; block inserted before hash_to_port). Adds hmac_sha256_hex, pbkdf2_sha256_hex (32-byte key, rounds as u32) and constant_time_equal; every backend arm is its own small function, so each cell is <= 270. Tests with published vectors, rust + gleam: RFC 4231 case 2 (Jefe); PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 password/salt at 1, 2 and 4096 rounds; constant_time_equal on equal / differing / shorter strings. Gate: ganymede job tibia-crypto, with an unmodified-crypto.spi control first (my spiral mirror's lib notebooks were red today for mirror reasons).")
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_3 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 3u32, "2026-11-09T21:34Z", "tibia", "11-09 17:4x tibia: GATE 1 (ganymede job tibia-crypto). Package --check of the draft is CLEAN. The notebook could NOT run on my mirror: the UNMODIFIED crypto.spi control fails identically (open file_system_operators unbound; every test red), so lib notebooks on that mirror are broken since today's spiral re-sync, not by this draft. Budget: the mix gate counted one new cell at 360 that the awk oracle missed. The Gleam global's triple-quoted string held a blank line followed by an indented line, which the gate keeps in one block. Fixed by splitting crypto_gleam_auth into crypto_gleam_pbkdf2 + crypto_gleam_hash_equals, with no blank lines inside the globals. Every new cell is now <= 271/272, and the remaining over_budget findings are crypto.spi's existing cells (hash_text, hmac_sha1_base64, hash_to_port...). Draft now F11CA5A319A8, base 8753CC4D5346 (= box). NEXT: the real proof is the moon -PrivateLib lib-land proof (round trip + consumers + every crypto test incl. the 4 vectors), then the box copy-only land. moon is at 91 pct load now, so it waits.")
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_4 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:12Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:2x tibia: ganymede lib notebooks stay unmountable on my mirror after three tries (manifest mtime bump; SPIRAL_LIB set; rig's exact --gate invocation from apps/cells). Every run fails identically on the UNMODIFIED crypto.spi too (open file_system_operators unbound), so it is the mirror, not the draft. Likely cause: the spiral sync left the mirror's deps on a \"shared source\". The draft's package --check is clean in every run. PROOF MOVED TO MOON (load 51 pct at launch): moon -PrivateLib lib-land proof, job tibia-libland-crypto (box tree packed 18:2x: lib/spiral, apps/cells, apps/spiral, root tomls; draft crypto.spi over base 8753CC4D5346). Then the box copy-only land with the digest check.")
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_5 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 5u32, "2026-11-09T22:33Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:4x tibia: MOON PROOF 1 (job tibia-libland-crypto) closed GREEN: round trip, signatures, consumers, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (tests typed 13, 0 errors), respell_drift 0; crypto.spi F11CA5A319A8, lib digest 1B5F0ADD94D0BFEF. BUT the box post-land digest is 74F836C912DBAA8D, because my pack's --exclude=target dropped the lib's 236 git-ignored bench/parsing/target/*.spi artifacts, which the digest counts (the trap org2 named in GATE-HEALS-1101 note 14). Landing on a mismatched digest would make the window rerun checks ON THE BOX, so: REPACKED with every lib file (419 = box 419) and re-proving: job tibia-libland-crypto2. Also owed after the land: the 13 crypto tests EXECUTED (the window types them but does not run them; the RFC vectors are not proven until a Cells run on a node with working lib notebooks).")
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_6 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 6u32, "2026-11-09T22:43Z", "tibia", "11-09 18:4x tibia: LANDED on the box lib (unstaged) from a proven close. Moon -PrivateLib re-proof (job tibia-libland-crypto2, full lib: 419 files) closed GREEN: round trip, signatures, consumers, document_test 26 passed, type-probe PASS (tests typed 13, errors 0, control ok), respell_drift 0; crypto.spi F11CA5A319A8, lib digest 74F836C912DBAA8D. Box: base 8753CC4D5346 unchanged, predicted post-land digest 74F836C912DBAA8D = the proof (exact), so the box only copied (tree-write window, waited 8 ms): \"LANDED from a proven close\", undo in spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo. lib crypto.spi now exports hmac_sha256_hex, pbkdf2_sha256_hex (32-byte key) and constant_time_equal on Rust and Gleam. STILL OWED for the DoD: EXECUTING the 4 vector tests (RFC 4231 case 2; PBKDF2 1/2/4096 rounds) and the constant-time test. The window types them but does not run them, and my mirror cannot mount lib notebooks today. Next: a Cells run of lib crypto.spi on a node whose lib notebooks mount (moon's private tree), then REALWORLD-3-AUTH swaps toy_crypto for these.")
inl note_of_lib_crypto_auth_primitives_7 () = Note ("LIB-CRYPTO-AUTH-PRIMITIVES", 7u32, "2026-11-09T23:17Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:2x tibia: DONE. The vectors are EXECUTED and pass against the LANDED lib crypto.spi (F11CA5A319A8), on ganymede (job tibia-rw-crypto5), through app notebooks on the spiral mirror synced to the box lib: crypto_vectors 4/4 (hmac_sha256_hex RFC 4231 case 2 = 5bdcc146...3843; pbkdf2_sha256_hex password/salt at 1 round = 120fb6cf...e17b, 2 rounds = ae4d0c95...4c43, 4096 rounds = c5e478d5...134a; constant_time_equal equal / differing / shorter = true / false / false), each on ///> rust with its crates (sha2 hmac / sha2 pbkdf2 / subtle). The lib file's own 13 tests were type-probed by the land window; the Gleam arms are typed, not executed. Why it took four runs: Cells builds Rust-with-crates through the spiral CLI found at SPIRAL_EXE or <spiral>/workspace/target/release/spiral; ganymede's mirror had neither, and SPIRAL_EXE alone did not reach the run, so compiler's built CLI was symlinked at the default path. DoD met: hmac_sha256 against RFC 4231, a KDF (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256) against published vectors, constant_time_equal, with rust tests and the vectors as rows.")
