inl note_of_kit_resume_compiler_m1_2 () = Note ("KIT-RESUME-COMPILER-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:06Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, DONE (unstaged): src/rig_handoff_degrade/inputs.spi turns the three sources into the degrade model's inputs: handoff_rows_of text reads inl ... = HandoffSection (\"title\", \"body\") rows (the legacy fixture shape) and returns None for an empty file, which the model treats as an absent handoff; waits_of reads state/waits.spi rows into \"ID (kind:value)\" lines; active_of_listing takes the Active ids from kit agile list output; state_of assembles typed_state with the receipts. Fields come from the same split-on-quote codec as the owner rows (the writers replace inner quotes). proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (inputs 1/1): a handoff row with other rows ignored, an empty file as absent, a wait row, Active ids only (a Planned row and the receipt line skipped), and the projection with no missing part. The file reads themselves (handoff.spi, waits.spi, the listing) are one-line calls in M2's kit resume verb. Note: no handoff.spi exists in the backlog root today, the absent case this model was built for.")
