inl note_of_kit_resume_compiler_m2_2 () = Note ("KIT-RESUME-COMPILER-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:10Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 rig, RENDERER BUILT (unstaged, src/rig_handoff_degrade/inputs.spi): projection_text prints one line per part, \"<title> [handoff|derived|missing]: <text or reason>\", then \"missing: <titles>\" (or \"missing: none\") and, when a handoff repeats a title, \"repeated titles: ...\". proof: notebook gate green on ganymede (inputs 2/2): a derived part, a missing part with its reason, and the missing line naming every gap. NEXT (wiring, for TRAIN44): kit resume (src/rig_resume, a legacy host-macro package with a resume_section union) gains a Handoff section whose body is projection_text over inputs read from <root>/handoff.spi, state/waits.spi and the agile list output; that adds rig_handoff_degrade to rig_resume's packages plus a Cargo path dependency, so the lock update and regen run on a node (the box takes no compute while the user is present).")
