inl note_of_sps_nb_4b_open_subst_strengthen_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4B-OPEN-SUBST-STRENGTHEN", 1u32, "2026-11-09T22:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: like NB-1..4 (notebook in spiral/apps/kernel/src, :# tests with ///> rust, names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, budget 0, Cells gate green). Scope from the mega sample: variable_strengthening (main.spi ~4935) and term_strengthening (~5072) over linear_strengthening's strengthen/mark_step, the open_unit strengthening plans (~5250-5430), and the recursive_open_typed_substitution (~4075-4300, ~5769). Next step: port variable_strengthening onto membership/single_use from linear_terms. TypeFeatures: GADT plans with explicit existential packs. Proof: gate rc=0. Split from SPS-NB-4-SUBSTITUTION by org2 11-09.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_4b_open_subst_strengthen_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4B-OPEN-SUBST-STRENGTHEN", 2u32, "2026-11-09T22:29Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 22:3xZ slice 1 green (unstaged): spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_variable_strengthening.spi (registered after linear_strengthening). The sample's 3-case 7-index variable_strengthening is split for the budget into vbase (VRemove | VUsedHere, payloads as :== aliases) + recursive vstr (VBase | VUnused), same indices; vsource/vtarget return linear_terms' variable directly (no partial match on terms); shifted = the There step. Plans: remove_plan (drop the newer unused cell) and the sample's used_here_plan. Gate ganymede org2-lvs3 rc=0 2/2: removing the newer cell puts the source slot at 1 and the target at 0; the used head survives at slot 0 on both sides; budget 0. Process lesson (tibia saw it): a kernel module entered package.spiproj before its first green gate turned every kernel notebook's package check red for minutes; register only after green. Next: term_strengthening (sample ~5072) over vstr, then the open typed substitution.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_4b_open_subst_strengthen_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4B-OPEN-SUBST-STRENGTHEN", 3u32, "2026-11-09T22:34Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 22:3xZ slice 2 green (unstaged): spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_term_strengthening.spi, registered after linear_reduction only after its gate. tstr sc su tc tu y with the leaf cases: TVariable (variable plan packed with its two slots, \\? s t.) and TConstant, where the sample's Unit/BoolTrue/BoolFalse fold into one case over const_kind y (KindUnit | KindTrue | KindFalse) with the same strengthen + all_unused x2 evidence. tsource/ttarget rebuild linear_terms' term (Variable / Constant). Gate ganymede org2-lts rc=0 2/2 (the unit plan keeps a constant on both sides; the replacement variable stays a variable); budget 0. Next (slice 3): the Tensor/Lambda/If/Apply cases as an intro/elim group over tstr, then the open typed substitution.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_4b_open_subst_strengthen_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4B-OPEN-SUBST-STRENGTHEN", 4u32, "2026-11-09T22:43Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 22:4xZ slice 3 green: linear_term_strengthening.spi now covers ALL eight of the sample's term_strengthening cases. Structure by depth for the cell budget: tleaf (TVariable | TConstant over const_kind) outside the group; recursive tstr = TLeaf | TIntro | TElim with a :& group of tintro (TTensor | TLambda), ttensor (Pair), telim (TIf | TApply), tif (Branch), tapply (Call); merges = the paired source/target usage_merge. tsource/ttarget are inline groups (one small function per form) that rebuild linear_terms' term/intro/elim on each side. Gate ganymede org2-lts5 rc=0 3/3 (constant keeps its kind; the variable stays a variable; strengthening passes under a lambda binder); budget 0. Edited as a scratch copy, gated on the mirror, then copied over the registered box file (kernel package never red). Left: the open typed substitution (sample ~4075-4300, ~5769).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_4b_open_subst_strengthen_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-4B-OPEN-SUBST-STRENGTHEN", 5u32, "2026-11-09T22:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-09 22:5xZ. Final slice: spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_open_substitution.spi (registered after linear_term_strengthening only after its green gate), the sample's recursive_open_typed_substitution, ALL nine cases: OVar (membership + single_use + selected + replacement term, slot packed) and the 8 composites layered for the budget: ointro (OTensor over otensor = TLeftSide/TRightSide | OLambda) and oelim (OApp = OFun/OArg | OIf = OGuard/OBranches), each part a single-case union with its existentials packed and merges for the source/target merge pair. selected folds the sample's ThereUnused/ThereUsed via a one-sided mark relation. osource rebuilds the term with the variable in place; otarget puts the replacement at the selected slot. Gate ganymede org2-los2 rc=0 2/2 (variable -> constant at the slot; a tensor-left substitution keeps size 3 and the held right part, with real LeftOnly/Neither merges); budget 0. NB-4B totals: linear_variable_strengthening (2/2), linear_term_strengthening (3/3, 8 cases), linear_open_substitution (2/2, 9 cases). DoD: met.")
inl spiral_ui_5_attrs_events () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI-5-ATTRS-EVENTS", "Typed attributes and events on ui_view elements (class, href, on_click) through the dom_op stream", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-UI-4-TS-DOM", "team:org,spiral,ui,lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_ui_5_attrs_events () = Planning ("SPIRAL-UI-5-ATTRS-EVENTS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_ui_5_attrs_events_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-5-ATTRS-EVENTS", 1u32, "2026-11-09T22:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: ui_view elements carry typed attributes (Class, Href, plus a typed OnClick that runs a ui_signals set) and ui_dom emits them as dom_op rows (SetAttr, Listen); ui_dom_ts applies them, and a bun test clicks a fake button and sees a bound text node rewritten in place. Gap found by org2 11-09: dice/ui (the first consumer, 52 leptos bindings) needs element_to_view/text_fragment/div/td/th/tr (covered by ui_view), signal_get/set/memo (covered by ui_signals), but also attributes, on_click and use_context, which today's stack lacks. Next step: add an attrs list to the element cases of view m k (phantom kind keeps phrasing/flow), extend mount with SetAttr. TypeFeatures: attribute GADT indexed by element kind (href only on anchors). Proof: Cells gate rust+typescript (SPIRAL_BUN) green.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_5_attrs_events_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-5-ATTRS-EVENTS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:45Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-09 23:4xZ phase 1 LANDED (attributes): lib ui_view / ui_dom / ui_dom_ts updated together (box digest 76E6DC0952527E2D, undo lib-land-undo/20261109-194447). ui_view: view m k = Leaf | Element (\\? e c. element e k c * list (attr e) * list (view m c)), where element is a tag GADT indexed by attribute kind e, own kind k and child kind c (SpanTag, LinkTag, ParaTag, DivTag) and attr e = Class (any) | Href (anchor only), so href on a div and a div inside a span are type errors; render escapes attribute values. ui_dom emits SetAttr (id, name, value) after Create; ui_dom_ts applies it with setAttribute. Proof: land green on ganymede (type-probe 3/3 PASS, consumers compile, 0 drift), gates rust+typescript (SPIRAL_BUN, 0 unsupported): ui_view 2/2 (exact HTML with class/href, escaped &amp;), ui_dom 2/2 (23 ops incl. 3 SetAttr; the patch stays [SetText (4, 7)]), ui_dom_ts 2/2 (classes and the raw href land on the right DOM nodes; in-place text update kept). Lesson: render/mount over views with existential packs must be inline (:= ^), not :~. Phase 2 (on_click) next.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_5_attrs_events_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-5-ATTRS-EVENTS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T00:02Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-10 00:0xZ. Phase 2 (events) LANDED: lib ui_view / ui_dom / ui_dom_ts (box digest A0A55232728B441B, undo lib-land-undo/20261109-200225). ui_view: Clickable (graph m -> graph m) * view m k with on_click; render ignores the handler. ui_dom: Listen (node, index) op on the clickable's root node, handlers kept as (index, handler) pairs, click g m i applies handler i (pure, no failure path), so a click followed by refresh yields the in-place patch. ui_dom_ts: app_state {g, m, t}; start_app applies the ops and wires each Listen to a DOM click listener that runs click, refresh, applies the patch and stores the new state. Proof: land green on ganymede (type-probe 3/3 PASS, consumers compile, 0 drift); gates with SPIRAL_BUN, 0 unsupported: ui_view 2/2, ui_dom 3/3 rust+typescript (a click patches exactly [SetText (3, 1)] with [Listen (4, 0)] emitted), ui_dom_ts 3/3 typescript (a DOM click on the span runs the Spiral handler and the SAME text node now reads 1; attributes; in-place set). DoD: met (typed Class/Href attributes and a typed on_click through the dom_op stream, applied in the browser applier, with a click test).")
