inl note_of_lib_quoted_fields_1 () = Note ("LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS", 1u32, "2026-11-09T23:19Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Created 11-09 by rig. The same 4-line reader (split on the double quote, keep the odd-indexed pieces) now exists in four kit packages written today: rig_lane_work/rows.spi, rig_handoff_degrade/inputs.spi, rig_tfs_queue/census.spi, rig_experiment_ledger/rows.spi, plus the older nth_quoted loop in agile_task_waits/waits.spi. It is exact for kit's state files because their writers replace inner quotes with an apostrophe. AGENTS.md: a missing generic helper goes into lib/spiral. DRAFT (lib style, sm' module, rust + gleam test): drafts\\spiral\\LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS\\sm-quoted_fields.spi. DoD: quoted_fields in sm' with its test, landed by the lib owner; then rig switches the four kit copies (one line each) in a later train. NEXT STEP: the lib owner reviews the draft and lands it. TYPEFEATURES: none (a total string function).")
inl note_of_lib_quoted_fields_2 () = Note ("LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS", 2u32, "2026-11-09T23:31Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:4x tibia (lib, claimed): REVIEWED rig's draft, correct for kit state rows: split on the double quote, keep the odd pieces; total; the writers replace inner quotes with an apostrophe, so no escaping is needed. One edge, recorded not changed: an unterminated trailing quote (a \"b) still yields b as a field; kit's writers never produce one. LAND DRAFT = the whole lib file: drafts\\spiral\\LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS\\sm'.spi (96FC9E71DD67; base box sm'.spi 54DECAB14E3A; rig's block appended at the end). TESTS EXECUTED: an app notebook on ganymede (job tibia-quoted) with the draft overlaid on my spiral mirror (restored to 54decab14e3a after) calls sm'::quoted_fields: a state row gives [A; train; TRAIN44]; no quotes give [] and an empty pair gives [\"\"]. 2/2 passed. LAND: the moon -PrivateLib proof + box copy, as for crypto today; the full-lib pack is ready (419 files). Moon is running TRAIN43 at 85 pct, so it waits.")
inl note_of_lib_quoted_fields_3 () = Note ("LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS", 3u32, "2026-11-09T23:53Z", "tibia", "11-09 19:5x tibia: DONE. sm'::quoted_fields LANDED on the box lib (unstaged) from a proven close: sm'.spi 96FC9E71DD67 (base 54DECAB14E3A). PROOF on a LINUX node (ganymede, job tibia-quoted-land3, lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply in my spiral mirror): signatures 30 unchanged, consumers compile, document_test 24 passed, type-probe pass, respell drift 0, lib digest 47244681BBA43FBE; the box's predicted post-land digest equalled it exactly, so the box only copied (tree-write window waited 0 ms; undo in spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo). Tests executed earlier from an app notebook (2/2). Two exactness traps on the way, both recorded: (1) a mirror synced by remote.ps1 lacks the lib's 236 git-ignored bench/parsing/target artifacts the digest counts, so I copied the box's whole lib/spiral over it; (2) the box lib moved (ui_dom/ui_dom_ts/ui_view) between my first prediction and the proof, so the prediction must be recomputed right before the land. NEXT (rig, later train): switch the four kit copies (rig_lane_work, rig_handoff_degrade, rig_tfs_queue, rig_experiment_ledger) and agile_task_waits' nth_quoted to sm'.quoted_fields.")
inl note_of_lib_quoted_fields_4 () = Note ("LIB-QUOTED-FIELDS", 4u32, "2026-11-09T23:58Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-09 20:0x rig: the kit switch is DONE in the live tree (unstaged, rides TRAIN44): rig_lane_work/rows.spi fields_of, rig_handoff_degrade/inputs.spi, rig_tfs_queue/census.spi and rig_experiment_ledger/rows.spi now call sm'.quoted_fields and carry no local copy (3 definitions and 1 inline fold removed). proof: notebook gate green on ganymede against the landed lib (sm'.spi 96FC9E71DD67 on the node, hash equal to the box): rows 1/1, inputs 2/2, census 1/1, ledger rows 1/1; kit standards 0, ratchet clean. Three MORE copies of the same reader exist inside legacy Rust host blocks (cold_proof_domain cold_quoted_fields, semantic_evidence_domain closeout_quoted_fields, patch_control_domain patch_quoted_fields): they go when those packages migrate off host blocks.")
