inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T00:08Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: ui_view's element GADT gains the tags dice/ui and lib leptos/ui actually use, with child-kind indices that make misuse a type error (td/th only inside tr, tr only inside thead/tbody, thead/tbody only inside table); input gets a typed value attr + an on_input event through the dom_op stream; rust+typescript gates (SPIRAL_BUN) green and a lib land. Measured by org2 11-09 over dice/ui + lib/spiral/leptos/{ui,svg} (37 files): div 24, td 19, th 19, path 11, span 7, tr 4, svg 4, button 2, label 2, select/pre/nav/input/table/thead/tbody 1 each; signals: signal_get 4, on_click 2, arc_memo 1, for 1. Next step: add table_kind/row_kind/cell_kind phantom kinds and TableTag/TheadTag/TbodyTag/TrTag/TdTag/ThTag to element e k c. TypeFeatures: GADT element tags indexed by parent/child kinds. Proof: gates + land green.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T00:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:2xZ slice 1 LANDED (box digest 5F4263633C71367C, undo lib-land-undo/20261109-201950): ui_view's element GADT is now three tag families, Basic (span/a/p/div), Tabular (table/thead/tbody/tr) and Extra (td/th/pre/button), over new phantom kinds table_part / row_part / cell_part, so td/th only fit inside tr, tr only inside thead/tbody, thead/tbody only inside table (misuse = type error). Call sites wrap the tag in its family (el (Basic DivTag) ...). ui_dom follows. Gates (SPIRAL_BUN, 0 unsupported): ui_view 3/3 incl. a typed table rendering escaped cells, ui_dom 3/3, ui_dom_ts 3/3 unchanged. Left for DoD: input with a typed value attr + on_input event, select/label/nav, inline svg/path, then leptos-style helper names.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T00:27Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:2xZ slice 2 (input) DRAFTED, not landed: drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI-6B\\{ui_view,ui_dom,ui_dom_ts}.spi. Design: ui_view Input (graph m -> string) * (string -> graph m -> graph m) with input_of (signal m string) helper, render <input value=...>; ui_dom dom_op gains SetValue (id, v) and ListenInput (id, i), binding gains value : bool so refresh patches an input with SetValue and text with SetText, mounted gains inputs (index, handler), type_in g m i text applies handler i; test expects typing 'hi' to patch [SetValue (3, hi); SetText (4, hi)]. First gate (ganymede org2-ui6b): ETY-UnboundVariable with_node in input_node = define-before-use (move input_node after leaf_node); budget oracle: view union 323, render 328, input_node 469, bind_leaf 275, refresh_one 303, so split input_node into with_binding / listen_input helpers and move Input into the mount_click group member. Next step: those two fixes, gate rust+typescript (SPIRAL_BUN), then the ui_dom_ts wiring (node.value = v for SetValue, an input listener passing e.target.value) and a lib land of the three files.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T00:37Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:3xZ slice 2 (input) GREEN in the probe, NOT landed: drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI-6B\\{ui_view,ui_dom,ui_dom_ts}.spi. Gate ganymede org2-ui6e with SPIRAL_BUN: ui_view 3/3, ui_dom 4/4 (typing 'hi' patches [SetText (4, hi); SetValue (3, hi)], newest binding first), ui_dom_ts 3/3; 0 unsupported. Fixed on the way: define-before-use (input_node below leaf_node), Input now wraps a single-case input_view (InputOf read/handler). Before landing: budget oracle still has ui_view's view union at 283 and render at 287 (over 272), plus the ui_dom cells input_node/bind_leaf/refresh_one; then the ui_dom_ts wiring for SetValue (node.value = v) and ListenInput (input listener passing e.target.value) with a bun test, then one land of the three files.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T00:45Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:4xZ slice 2 drafts now within budget (0 findings in ui_view and ui_dom) and green: ganymede org2-ui6f, SPIRAL_BUN, ui_view 3/3, ui_dom 4/4, ui_dom_ts 3/3, 0 unsupported. Compaction: handler alias, view m k, render_more :& member for Clickable/Input, new_binding / with_binding / listen_input / patch_of helpers. NOT landed on purpose: ui_dom_ts still ignores SetValue/ListenInput, so a land now would ship inputs whose DOM value never updates. Next step: in ui_dom_ts, SetValue -> node.value = v and wire ListenInput to an input listener passing e.target.value through type_in + refresh (like on_dom_click); a bun test typing into a fake input; then one land of the three files from drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI-6B.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T00:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:5xZ ui_dom_ts input wiring drafted in drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI-6B\\ui_dom_ts.spi (set_value, on_dom_input via type_in + refresh, wire_input on ListenInput, fake input with type(v)); first gate (org2-ui6g) failed: ETY-TermError at the new typed_text test (line ~156: the inline String(t.get(3).value) macro is a 3-tuple element of the wrong type, bind it with :=), and wire / install_fake_events / typed_text are over budget. Note: the draft file changed on disk after org2's last edit (not by org2), so re-read it before the next edit. The ui_view + ui_dom input slice is green and budget-clean (org2-ui6f) and waits for this applier piece before one land.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T00:53Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:5xZ input slice GREEN END TO END in the probe (ganymede org2-ui6h, SPIRAL_BUN, 0 unsupported): ui_view 3/3, ui_dom 4/4 (rust+typescript), ui_dom_ts 4/4 incl. typing 'hi' into a DOM input: the Spiral handler runs via type_in + refresh, the SAME bound text node reads 'hi' and the input's value is 'hi'. Fix: bind the inline value macro with := before the tuple. Before the land (next round): budget oracle still flags ui_dom_ts wire 295, install_fake_events 284, typed_text 337 (ui_view and ui_dom are 0); split wire's Listen arm into wire_click like wire_input, split the fake input methods into their own install step, move typed_text's setup into a helper. Then one land of drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-UI-6B\\{ui_view,ui_dom,ui_dom_ts}.spi through lib_land_window (re-predict digests first; the box lib moves often).")
