inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 12u32, "2026-11-10T05:34Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 05:3xZ consumer port moved onto keyed lists (draft dice_table2.spi 435a3c81b605, org2 scratch; probe package apps/dice_table_probe on the mirror): the ledger model holds the txn list, tbody is each (txns_signal) keyed by txn hash, and a third cell asserts a new txn list emits Remove of the dropped hash row first and 19 ops total (one removal plus one 18-op row mount), while the render and note-patch cells keep their slice-0 expectations (ids unchanged). Next step: after SPIRAL-UI-8-KEYED-LIST lands, org2 gates dice_table2 in the probe package (rust and typescript).")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 13u32, "2026-11-10T06:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 keyed consumer proof GREEN: dice_table2 (435a3c81b605) in probe package apps/dice_table_probe on the ganymede mirror over the UI-8 lib (job org2-dt2): 3 cells executed and passed, 0 unsupported (render like the dice markup; note set patches only the status text; a new txn list removes the dropped hash row first, 19 ops). The transaction table is now a typed keyed list. Next step: after SPIRAL-UI-8-KEYED-LIST closes, org2 decides where the consumer port lives (a lib sample next to ui_dom) and closes UI-6.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_6_tables_forms_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS", 14u32, "2026-11-10T06:30Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE: every tag family in the title is landed in lib/spiral/ui_view.spi (tables 6A, form controls and pre 6B, label/select/option/nav and inline svg/path 6C), and the consumer proof is green: the dice transaction table ported onto the stack as a typed keyed list (drafts/spiral/SPIRAL-UI-6-TABLES-FORMS/dice_table.spi 435a3c81b605; ganymede job org2-dt2: 3 cells executed and passed, 0 unsupported). Moving dice/ui itself onto Spiral is a separate migration decision, not part of this item.")
inl sps_nb_6b_open_betas () = Task ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", "spiral-proves-spiral notebook 6B: the five open betas (sample main.spi 6500-7999)", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", "team:org,spiral,proofs,mega-samples", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas () = Planning ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T00:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: like NB-1..5 (notebook in spiral/apps/kernel/src, :# tests with ///> rust, names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, budget 0, Cells gate green, registered only after its own green gate). Scope: OpenIdentity/Tensor/Application/Lambda/Conditional betas; first map NB-4/4B coverage of 2600-7999 by def name. Next step: list the sample defs in that line range and port the first GADT. TypeFeatures: GADT plans with explicit existential packs, inline (:= ^) recursion. Proof: gate rc=0. Split from SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS per tibia's measured note 2, accepted by org2 11-10.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T00:39Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:4xZ coverage map for whoever holds 6B (tibia does): sample lines 6500-7999 hold 126 top-level defs, ALL in the open-beta families, none ported by NB-4/4B (whose modules cover identity substitution ~3624, recursive_open_typed_substitution ~4075-4300/5769, strengthening ~4881-5430). GADTs in range: open_identity_beta_step ty, open_tensor_beta_step ty, open_beta_body_step ty result_type, open_application_beta_step ty, open_beta_body_application_step ty result_type, open_lambda_beta_target_witness, open_lambda_beta_step, open_beta_body_lambda_step ty result_type, open_conditional_beta_step, open_beta_body_conditional_step ty result_type. Def counts by family (stems): open_lambda_beta 9 (+ _step 4, _inner 4), open_conditional_beta 7 (+ _step 3), open_application_beta 5 (+ _step 3), open_tensor_beta 3 (+ _step 3), open_identity_beta_step 3, open_beta_body_* 3 each. Suggested order: identity -> tensor -> application -> lambda -> conditional (the beta_body steps per family alongside), building on linear_open_substitution's osub for the substitution inside each beta.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T00:39Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:4x tibia COVERAGE MAP of the 20 sample terminals in 2600-7999, against the kernel modules' tests (org2's ranges plus a read of each module's :# tests). (1) COVERED as tests, 5: closed_recursive_beta_derivation 2921 (linear_reduction, NB-5); identity_substitution 3696 (linear_substitution); recursive_open_typed_substitution_variable 4419 and _tensor_left 4495 (linear_open_substitution); context_strengthening 4929 (linear_strengthening). application_lambda_substitution_preservation 3571 is inside org2's ~3624 range but has no test of its own: verify. (2) DEFINITIONS PORTED, TERMINAL MISSING, 4: recursive_open_typed_substitution _lambda_outer 4642, _tensor_right 4706, _application_argument 4786, _application_function 4872. linear_open_substitution already implements OLambda, OApp (OFun, OArg) and OIf in osource/otarget but tests only the variable and tensor_left cases, so these are 4 cheap :# tests in org2's module (ask org2 first). (3) UNCOVERED, 10: the open betas proper, beta_step 6332 and open_beta_body_family 6804 / _application_family 7141 / _lambda_family 7692 / _conditional_family 7971, which are this item; and 5 substitution-era terminals no item names: nested_lambda_substitution 3194, application_lambda_substitution 3414, total_bool_literal_replacement 3848, conditional_bool_literal_replacement 3919, bool_negation_involution 4032. Suggest an NB-6E for those 5 plus group (2), or fold them in here. Method: grep of _terminal defs in main.spi, each module's :# list, and the O* match arms in linear_open_substitution. tibia's run ends 21:00, so this claim lapses unworked past the map.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T00:42Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:4x tibia: 1 of the 4 group-(2) terminals is now a test. recursive_open_typed_substitution_tensor_right (main.spi:4706) is drafted over org2's module at drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS\\linear_open_substitution.spi (B9856420E979): the applied file plus right_merge (RightOnly), right_plan (TRightSide over var_plan, held unit on the left) and the test a_tensor_right_substitution_keeps_the_shape_and_the_held_left_part. Predicted (3, 3, intro) mirrors tensor_left; it held. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6r): --check rc 0; linear_open_substitution 3/3, 0 unsupported; budget 0 findings. For org2 to apply (their module). STILL MISSING from group (2): lambda_outer, application_function, application_argument. Each needs a substituted variable under a binder or at an arrow type, so the one_cell (unit) fixtures don't reach them: they need an arrow-typed or two-cell context fixture first. tibia's run ends 21:00; the claim lapses.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T00:46Z", "tibia", "11-09 20:4x tibia: CORRECTION to note 4's hand-off. tibia edited the handed-off draft afterwards, so org2's gate at ~20:43 (job org2-los3) caught an in-progress, failing file. Restored: drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS\\linear_open_substitution.spi is now exactly the tensor_right version (sha256 b9856420e979, 3/3 in job tibia-nb6r). NEW, optional, at a separate frozen path with-lambda-outer\\linear_open_substitution.spi (03168a15b021): adds recursive_open_typed_substitution_lambda_outer (main.spi:4642) as a test via a two-cell fixture: the lambda body pairs the substituted outer variable (slot 1, SelectedThere + MarkUnused) with its own binder (slot 0); RightOnly merges over the existing left_merge/none_merge tails. Predicted sizes 4 and 4 with label intro held. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6m): --check rc 0; 4/4; budget 0. Trap: an untyped SelectedThere (\\? (SelectedHere ..., MarkUnused ...)) fails ETY-ExistsShouldntHaveMetavars; giving the selection its own annotated helper fixes it. LEFT from group (2): application_function and application_argument (they need an arrow-typed cell). Lesson: a handed-off draft path is frozen; new work goes in a new path.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_6 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T00:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 00:5xZ APPLIED tibia's frozen with-lambda-outer\\linear_open_substitution.spi (sha256 03168a15b021) over spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_open_substitution.spi after org2's mirror gate with the full kernel package: rc=0, 4/4 executed (job org2-los4), budget 0. Adds the tensor_right and lambda_outer terminals as tests. Still untested in the module: application_function and application_argument (need an arrow-typed fixture), plus the 5 open betas this item owns.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_7 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T03:44Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 03:4xZ slice 1 (open identity beta) green and applied: spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_open_betas.spi, registered after linear_values only after its gate (ganymede org2-lob rc=0 2/2, budget 0). ibeta y over concrete indices as the sample has them (body in [y; y] used-bound / unused-outer, argument in [y] used, RightOnly merge), so the merge of the identity's unused usage with the argument's usage is the argument's usage and source/target share the term c s y index. Every indexed witness is bound through a typed helper (tibia's ExistsShouldntHaveMetavars lesson). Tests: source is an elim (application of the lambda), target is the argument variable; size 4 -> 1, matching the sample's own assertion. Next step: the open tensor beta (sample ~6560+), then application, lambda and conditional.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_8 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T03:52Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 03:4xZ slice 2 (open tensor beta) green and applied over linear_open_betas.spi (edited as a scratch copy, gated on the mirror, then copied; job org2-lob2 rc=0 4/4, budget 0). (\\x. <x, true>) arg -> <arg, true>: tbeta y carries the tensor body, the argument, the application merge and the target's parts (true's all_unused in [y], the LeftOnly target merge); source is the elim redex, target the rebuilt intro pair; size 6 -> 3, matching the sample's assertion. Next step: the open application beta (sample ~6800+), then lambda and conditional.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_9 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 9u32, "2026-11-10T03:57Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 03:5xZ slice 3 (open application beta) green and applied (job org2-lob3 rc=0 6/6, budget 0). (\\x. id x) arg -> id arg with the inner identity preserved: abeta y reuses body_term/identity_fn from slice 1; id_in builds a closed identity in any context from an all_unused proof (here_slot/here_use typed helpers, no inline witnesses). Pre-registered sizes 7 -> 4 (Elim + Intro-lambda over a 4-node body + arg; Elim + 2-node id + arg) reproduced exactly. Next step: the open lambda beta (sample: open_lambda_beta_step + target witness + inner), then the conditional beta.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6b_open_betas_10 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6B-OPEN-BETAS", 10u32, "2026-11-10T04:07Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DONE 11-10 04:0xZ. spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_open_betas.spi holds all FIVE open betas, each with a source/target pair and a pre-registered size check: identity (\\x.x) arg -> arg, 4 -> 1; tensor (\\x.<x,true>) arg -> <arg,true>, 6 -> 3; application (\\x. id x) arg -> id arg, 7 -> 4; lambda (\\x.\\y.<x,y>) arg -> \\y.<arg-lifted,y>, 7 -> 4 (the lifted argument sits at slot 1 under y, so capture-avoidance is in the types); conditional (\\g. if g then () else ()) b -> if b then () else (), 7 -> 4. Proof: ganymede org2-lob5 rc=0 10/10, budget 0; edited as scratch copies, each gated before replacing the registered box file. The sample's beta_body_* step families (identity/application/lambda/conditional bases) are the wrappers that feed the general reduction family, so they move to SPS-NB-6C. Proof: gate rc=0 10/10.")
inl sps_nb_6c_general_reduction () = Task ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", "spiral-proves-spiral notebook 6C: the general reduction family + closed progress (sample 8000-9499)", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS", "team:org,spiral,proofs,mega-samples", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction () = Planning ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 1u32, "2026-11-10T00:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: like NB-1..5 (notebook in spiral/apps/kernel/src, :# tests with ///> rust, names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, budget 0, Cells gate green, registered only after its own green gate). Scope: the 13-constructor reduction family at main.spi:8061 and progress at 8874, 10 terminals; needs 6B. Next step: list the sample defs in that line range and port the first GADT. TypeFeatures: GADT plans with explicit existential packs, inline (:= ^) recursion. Proof: gate rc=0. Split from SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS per tibia's measured note 2, accepted by org2 11-10.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 groom 2 (lesson: a split child carries its terminal count): DoD adds 'all 10 sample _terminal defs in 8000-9499 present as :# tests'. Next step: grep -n _terminal main.spi in 8000-9499 to list the 10 names, then port the 13-constructor reduction family at main.spi:8061 after 6B lands.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:08Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 04:0xZ: 6B DONE (linear_open_betas: all five open betas, 10/10). Scope added from 6B: the sample's open_beta_body_* step families (identity/application/lambda/conditional bases, about 3 defs each) that wrap the five betas, built over linear_open_betas' ibeta/tbeta/abeta and the lambda/conditional pairs. Next step: list 6C's 10 _terminal defs in 8000-9499 and port the 13-constructor reduction family at main.spi:8061.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:25Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:2x tibia (help pool): SLICES 1+2 GREEN as a NEW module drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION\\handoff-1\\linear_closed_reduction.spi (sha 57487d33507f, FROZEN; register after linear_values; it opens linear_reduction + linear_values). PORTS: (1) recursive-beta derivation_source (Apply of the Lambda over open_body to the argument) and derivation_target (main.spi:2754-2888: the closed term built case by case over NB-5's derivation unions as one inline mutual group). The sample's own runtime size assertions hold EXACTLY: open/source/target for identity 1/4/1, left_unit 3/6/3, right_unit 3/6/3, deep 7/10/7 (main.spi:2890-2997). (2) Closed atomic reduction (8000): AtomicBeta over NB-5's closed_beta (identity + tensor), AtomicStep over small_step, plus AtomicRecursive. (3) The CLOSED reduction family (8061, closed constructors): reduction = ReduceAtomic | ReduceTensor (ReduceLeft/ReduceRight congruences) | ReduceApply (ReduceFun/ReduceArg congruences), with source/target. (4) Closed progress (8874): ProgressValue (linear_values value) | ProgressStep, source/target, and the derivation authority (8925-8990): one derivation yields the closed Lambda value and its progress step. SHAPE (budget): reduction is indexed by type only, because these constructors are all closed. The sample's open-context constructors (Beta, Open*Beta) go in a separate open family when NB-6B lands; recursive beta lives under atomic, since it never contains a reduction. Tests 6: sample sizes; left congruence 6 to 3; argument congruence 7 to 4; recursive step 10 to 7; value progress 3 = 3; authority lambda 8 / source 10 / target 7. Gate (ganymede jobs tibia-nb6c1..3): --check rc 0, 6/6, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Next step: after org2 applies this module, port ready-beta progress (9513-9612) as slice 3; the open betas join after NB-6B.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 5u32, "2026-11-10T04:45Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:4x tibia: SLICE 3 GREEN; handoff-2\\linear_closed_reduction.spi (sha b712aa49d3af, FROZEN) SUPERSEDES handoff-1 (same module, a strict superset). Adds main.spi:9166-9612: the closed-source phantom indices (source_unit/true/false/pair/identity/lambda, and the ready redexes source_ready_identity and source_tensor_beta); the value-source family vsource = SourceLeaf (Unit/True/False) | SourceFn (SourceIdentity | SourceLambda) | SourcePair (recursive), with source_value/source_term/source_progress; the ready-beta witness ready_beta = ReadyIdentity | ReadyTail (both a function value and an argument value, indexed by the redex shape), ready_relation into NB-5's closed_beta, ready_progress, and the relation+progress bundle (9557-9600). Tests 10 (6 + 4): value sources embed (pair 3, identity 2); a value source is its own progress (3 = 3); ready identity: relation source 4, progress 4 to 1; ready tail: 6, 6 to 3. Trap fixed on the way: SourceIdentity left its type var unresolved in a test (ETY-ValueRestriction); a typed helper pins it. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6c6): --check rc 0, 10/10, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Next step: after org2 applies handoff-2, port the recursive-beta ready opening (9001-9055) and the value-source canonicity terminals (9213-9330).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_6 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 6u32, "2026-11-10T04:49Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:4x tibia: SLICE 4 GREEN; handoff-3\\linear_closed_reduction.spi (FROZEN, a strict superset of handoff-2). Adds main.spi:9001-9055 and 9237-9330: ready_opened (derivation, its closed lambda value, source, target, note) via open_ready, and opened_shape; the lambda-value canonicity readers lambda_leaf_tag/lambda_tag (through two projection helpers, never a nested GADT pattern); identity_at, the identity value at any type. Tests 13 (10 + 3), all pre-registered from NB-5's outer_tag numbering: the opened deep redex reads (lambda 6, application 1, sizes 10 and 7); the tensor-tail lambda body is a Tensor (5) and the bool identity body a Variable (0); the identity body at unit*bool is also a Variable (0). Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6c7): --check rc 0, 13/13, 0 unsupported, budget 0. NB-6C now covers every CLOSED part of main.spi:8000-9612. Remaining: the five open-context constructors (Beta, Open{Identity,Tensor,Application,Lambda}Beta, plus OpenConditionalBeta), which need NB-6B's open betas. Next step: after NB-6B lands its open betas, add them as a separate open family joined to this closed one.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_7 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 7u32, "2026-11-10T05:10Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 applied handoff-3 on box: apps/kernel/src/linear_closed_reduction.spi sha 4cf52623ad02, ganymede mirror gate 13/13 green; registered in package.spiproj after linear_open_betas, before linear_bool_normalization (753509ea270e box+mirror). Next step: after NB-6D handoff-2 gates green in-package (job org2-nb6d), tibia closes 6C.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_8 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 8u32, "2026-11-10T05:16Z", "tibia", "11-10 01:1x tibia: OPEN PART GREEN; NB-6C's reduction family is now COMPLETE (closed + open). NEW module drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION\\handoff-open-1\\linear_general_reduction.spi (sha 53f560331bba, FROZEN; register after linear_closed_reduction; it opens linear_closed_reduction and reaches linear_open_betas by qualified name, because opening both would collide on lambda_source, a type in one and a function in the other). Ports main.spi:8061's open constructors over the landed linear_open_betas: open_family (OpenIdentity / OpenTensor / OpenApply over ibeta/tbeta/abeta) and open_fixed (OpenLambda, OpenConditional over the fixed lambda/cond betas), joined as open_beta; general c s t y = AnyClosed (closed reduction) | AnyStep (small_step in any context) | AnyOpen (open beta, both usages used), with general_source / general_target. Tests 3, all pre-registered from linear_open_betas' own numbers and all held on the first run: families 4 to 1, 6 to 3, 7 to 4; fixed lambda 7 to 4, conditional 7 to 4; a closed recursive-beta step through general 10 to 7. Gate (ganymede jobs tibia-gen1 / tibia-gen2): --check rc 0, 3/3, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Remaining for 6C: none in the reduction family. Next step: after org2 applies this module, close NB-6C with the parent's terminal count.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_9 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 9u32, "2026-11-10T05:26Z", "tibia", "11-10 01:2x tibia: ARGUMENT TRACE GREEN; handoff-open-2\\linear_general_reduction.spi (sha 7cdf1a962199, FROZEN) SUPERSEDES handoff-open-1 (a strict superset; same position right after linear_closed_reduction). Adds main.spi:8187-8240: trace = TraceBase (a closed reduction) | TraceMore (a closed function over an inner trace); trace_reduction (nests argument congruences); trace_depth; argument_depth over a reduction (through apply_depth, a projection rather than a nested GADT pattern). Tests 5 (3 + 2), pre-registered: a depth-3 trace has trace depth 3 = reduction depth 3 and sizes 13 to 10 (base 4 to 1, plus 3 per identity wrap); at depth 4 both depths read 4 (the sample's depth-four runtime assertion). Gate (ganymede job tibia-gen3): --check rc 0, 5/5, 0 unsupported, budget 0. NB-6C now covers ALL of main.spi:8000-9612 plus the open constructors. Next step: after org2 applies handoff-open-2, close NB-6C.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_10 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 10u32, "2026-11-10T05:54Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 applied on the box: apps/kernel/src/linear_general_reduction.spi handoff-open-2 7cdf1a962199, registered right after linear_closed_reduction (package.spiproj b77b8111b791, box = mirror). In-package ganymede gates: open-1 3/3 (org2-nb6d3), open-2 5/5 (org2-nb6d4), with linear_closed_reduction 13/13 earlier. Per tibia the reduction family is complete; tibia closes 6C.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6c_general_reduction_11 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION", 11u32, "2026-11-10T05:55Z", "tibia", "11-10 01:5x tibia: CLOSED. On the box (org2-nb6d4 green in-package): linear_closed_reduction 4cf52623ad02 (13/13) and linear_general_reduction 7cdf1a962199 (5/5), package.spiproj b77b8111b791. Coverage of main.spi:8000-9612: closed atomic + general reduction (closed and open constructors), the argument trace, closed progress, value sources and canonicity, the ready-beta witness/bundle/opening, and the recursive-beta source/target with the sample's runtime size assertions. 18 tests across the two modules, every number pre-registered.")
