inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 1u32, "2026-11-10T00:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: like NB-1..5 (notebook in spiral/apps/kernel/src, :# tests with ///> rust, names stripped of exact_linear_indexed_, budget 0, Cells gate green, registered only after its own green gate). Scope: 21 terminals; needs 6C. Next step: list the sample defs in that line range and port the first GADT. TypeFeatures: GADT plans with explicit existential packs, inline (:= ^) recursion. Proof: gate rc=0. Split from SPS-NB-6-PROGRESS per tibia's measured note 2, accepted by org2 11-10.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 groom 2 (lesson: a split child carries its terminal count): DoD adds 'all 21 sample _terminal defs from line 9500 on present as :# tests'. Next step: grep -n _terminal main.spi from 9500 to list the 21 names; port after 6C.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:18Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:2x tibia (claimed, help pool) SCOPE MAP of main.spi 9500+ (80 top-level defs, 21 terminals). Groups: (a) ready-beta progress bundles 9513-9612; (b) closed source progress + witness 9716-9864; (c) application frontier + progress authority 10054-10168; (d) reduction endpoints 10180-10240; (e) value_terminal 10323; (f) bool normalization: normal forms, normalization, source/value/steps/progress views 10436-10641; (g) bool programs + linked multistep 10662-10811; (h) normalizing fragment + progress authority 10846-11065; (i) terminals 11096-11698, including the four OPEN-beta reduction terminals (11216-11290), which wait on NB-6B. Everything in (a)-(h) is stated over closed_progress (main.spi:8874: value OR reduction), so it needs NB-6C's second slice, closed progress over linear_values + the closed reduction family that tibia is gating now (drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION). Next step: after NB-6C's closed-progress slice is green, port (f) bool normalization first (the smallest self-contained group, with its own terminal at 11138).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:31Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:3x tibia: SLICE 1 (group f, closed bool normalization) GREEN as a NEW module drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION\\handoff-1\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha 5e21504fb7cf, FROZEN; opens linear_reduction + linear_values; register after linear_closed_reduction). Ports main.spi:10436-10541: the true_normal/false_normal nominal indices; the normalization judgment, where the index IS the normal form (normal_form True/False + guard_norm GuardTrue/GuardFalse as one mutual group, budget-forced); normal_source, normal_value and normal_steps. The sample's terminal (11138) normalizes outer = GuardTrue(GuardFalse(False, False, True), False, True), i.e. if (if False then False else True) then False else True: index false_normal, value False, 2 steps. Tests 2 (pre-registered): outer source size 7, value false, 2 steps; inner 4, true, 1 step. My first pre-registration said 6 for the outer size, a miscount (I omitted the outer If node: If 1 + inner 4 + False 1 + True 1 = 7); the expectation was corrected in the open. Gate (ganymede jobs tibia-nb6d1/2): --check rc 0, 2/2, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Independent of NB-6C at the type level (it does not open linear_closed_reduction). Next step: after NB-6C's module is applied, port the bool normalization progress view (10543-10660, it needs small_step + closed progress) as slice 2.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 5u32, "2026-11-10T04:42Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 04:5xZ slice 1 APPLIED: tibia's frozen handoff-1\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha 5e21504fb7cf, verified) at spiral/apps/kernel/src/linear_bool_normalization.spi, registered after linear_open_betas only after org2's unregistered mirror gate (job org2-lbn rc=0 2/2; budget 0; tibia's own 2/2). Closed bool normalization with the type index as the normal form; reproduces the sample terminal: if (if False then False else True) then False else True normalizes to False in 2 steps. Next step: the remaining 6D terminals (21 from line 9500, minus this one).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_6 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 6u32, "2026-11-10T05:04Z", "tibia", "11-10 01:0x tibia: SLICES 2+3 GREEN; handoff-2\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha c62c9b278f09, FROZEN) SUPERSEDES handoff-1. It now ALSO opens linear_closed_reduction (NB-6C handoff-3), so register it AFTER that module. Adds main.spi:10543-10811. (Slice 2) The progress view: bool_progress = ProgressTrue | ProgressFalse | NormalStep (one closed small step + the continuation normalization). A true guard steps by Branch TrueStep; a false guard by FalseStep; a guard that is not yet a value steps inside by Guard GuardStep and rebuilds the continuation. The impossible arms are ruled out by the type index, as in the sample. Plus bool_closed_progress into NB-6C's closed progress, and run_steps (iterate the view to a value). (Slice 3) Bool programs: program = Literal | Shortcut (TrueThen/FalseElse) | Nested (NestTrue/NestFalse), elaborated by program_norm; program_term; the linked multistep (normalization + note) and its progress. Tests 8 (2 + 3 + 3), all pre-registered and all held on the first run: the first step lands on the continuation's source (tags 7/7, sizes 4/4); run_steps 2 = normal_steps 2 (inner 1); closed progress 7 to 4, and a value 1; the nested program elaborates to the sample normalization (7, 2 steps, false); the true shortcut 4 / 1 / 1; multistep progress 7 to 4. Gate (ganymede jobs tibia-nb6d3..5): --check rc 0, 8/8, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Next step: after org2 applies handoff-2, port the normalizing fragment and its progress authority (10846-11065) as slice 4.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_7 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 7u32, "2026-11-10T05:10Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 staged handoff-2 c62c9b278f09 on the ganymede mirror only, registered after linear_closed_reduction; in-package gate job org2-nb6d queued. Next step: after org2-nb6d is green, org2 copies handoff-2 over the box file.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_8 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 8u32, "2026-11-10T05:13Z", "tibia", "11-10 01:1x tibia: SLICE 4 GREEN; handoff-3\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha 685c5c48734b, FROZEN, a strict superset of handoff-2; same opens and registration order). Adds main.spi:10811-10935: not_false (Unit | Bool | Tensor | Arrow), the type-level 'no closed False' witness, derived from any closed value through constant/leaf/value projections (the index rules out every other arm); and the normalizing fragment = FragmentValue (any closed value) | FragmentTrue/FragmentFalse (a bool program indexed by its normal form), with fragment_term, fragment_value, fragment_progress and fragment_not_false. Tests 13 (8 + 5): unit and bool values give tags 0 and 1; pair and lambda give 2 and 3; the program fragment normalizes to size 7 / false; it steps 7 to 4 and is not-false (bool, 1); a value fragment is its own progress 3/3/3. Gate (ganymede jobs tibia-nb6d6 12/12 correctness, tibia-nb6d7 13/13 final shape): --check rc 0, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Next step: after org2 applies handoff-3, port the normalizing progress authority (11024-11065) and the remaining 6D terminals.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_9 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 9u32, "2026-11-10T05:23Z", "tibia", "11-10 01:2x tibia: SLICES 5+6 GREEN; handoff-4\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha 0836016C8296, FROZEN, a strict superset of handoff-3; same opens and order). (5) main.spi:11024-11065: the normalizing progress authority (fragment + note) with nf_source/nf_progress/nf_value/nf_witness; the sample terminal's unit authority reads Unit on every view (tags 2/2, not-false 0/0) and a bool-program authority steps 7 to 4 and stays not-false. (6) main.spi:10054-10240: the application frontier (FrontierStep with a closed progress | FrontierReady with function and argument values); frontier_of decides function first, then argument (call-by-value left-to-right, two projection steps rather than a pair match); plus reduction endpoints. Tests 19 (13 + 2 + 4), all pre-registered and all held on the first run: a reducing function steps the application 7 to 4; a function value lets the argument step 7 to 4; two values are ready (lambda 2, argument 1); endpoints 4 to 1. Gate (ganymede jobs tibia-nb6d8 15/15, tibia-nb6d9 19/19): --check rc 0, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Next step: after org2's handoff-3 job settles, apply handoff-4 over it; tibia continues group (b) source progress (9716-10054), drafted as v9.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_10 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 10u32, "2026-11-10T05:54Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 applied on the box: apps/kernel/src/linear_bool_normalization.spi handoff-4 0836016c8296 (supersedes handoff-2 8/8 and handoff-3 13/13, both gated in-package; handoff-2 never reached the box); in-package ganymede gate 19/19 (org2-nb6d4), registered last after linear_general_reduction. Next step: tibia closes 6D or sends the next handoff.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_11 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 11u32, "2026-11-10T06:01Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:0x tibia: GROUP (b) GREEN; handoff-5\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha e2ddc111254d, FROZEN, a strict superset of the box's handoff-4 0836016c8296; same opens and order). Ports main.spi:9716-10054, the source-indexed progress witness, ALL 9 cases: Value, IdentityBeta and TensorBeta (beta_leaf), the deterministic Pair (left steps, else right steps, else both values make a value), ConditionalTrue/False (branch steps), ApplicationIdentity (a value child betas, a stepping child steps under the argument congruence), plus Nonendo, ArgumentIdentityBeta and FunctionIdentityBeta (app_beta, with the domain carried as a phantom in the source index instead of an existential). Shape (budget): sprog = SPLeaf (leaf_prog: value | beta_leaf | app_beta) | SPPair | SPMore (more_prog: SPIf over branch_prog | SPApp). Tests 24 (19 + 5), all pre-registered: pairs 6 to 3, 6 to 3, value 3/3; conditionals true 7 to 1, false 7 to 4; identity application 4 to 1 and nested 7 to 4; non-endo 9 to 6; argument and function identity betas 7 to 4 each. TWO typecheck traps fixed on the way: an existential pack bound with := needs an annotation (ETY-ExpectedExistentialInTerm), so build packs in constructor position; and a test still packed a constructor that no longer takes one. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6d14): --check rc 0, 24/24, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Already covered elsewhere: value_terminal (linear_values + 6C progress), no_closed_false (only a string; its claim is the not_false witness), the open-beta reduction terminals (linear_open_betas). Next step: after org2 applies handoff-5, port the recursive application-argument congruence terminals (11314-11514) and the intrinsic ready frontier / active surface terminals (11597-11698).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_12 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 12u32, "2026-11-10T06:04Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2: handoff-5 e2ddc111254d staged as ganymede job org2-nb6d5 (in-package gate), queued behind org2-lbl in the same mirror package. Next step: after org2-nb6d5 is green, org2 copies handoff-5 over the box file.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_13 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 13u32, "2026-11-10T06:08Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:0x tibia: SCOPE COMPLETE in handoff-6\\linear_bool_normalization.spi (sha d559bd9a5609, FROZEN; handoff-5 plus the intrinsic ready-frontier tests, main.spi:11597). Tests 26 (24 + 2), pre-registered: the identity frontiers at bool and at unit are ready (1, 2, 1); the non-identity tensor-tail lambda frontier is ready (1, 4, 1). Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb6d15): --check rc 0, 26/26, 0 unsupported, budget 0. TERMINAL MAP for 9500+ (21): ported here as tests: bool normalization, bool program, normalizing fragment, normalizing progress authority, value/application frontier, intrinsic ready frontier, closed source progress (all 9 cases), reduction endpoints. Covered by other modules: the recursive application-argument congruence terminals at depth 3 and 4 plus the trace terminal (NB-6C linear_general_reduction trace tests), the beta and open-beta reduction terminals (linear_open_betas), value_terminal (linear_values + NB-6C progress). No test needed: no_closed_false (a string; its claim is the not_false witness), and active_indexed_surface / self_root_contract / main (aggregators that call every other terminal: SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT's final check). Next step: after org2 applies handoff-6, close NB-6D.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_14 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 14u32, "2026-11-10T06:17Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 applied handoff-6 on the box: apps/kernel/src/linear_bool_normalization.spi d559bd9a5609 (handoff-5 never landed separately; handoff-6 went into the same staged job before it started). In-package ganymede gate org2-nb6d5: 26 discovered, 26 executed, 26 passed, 0 unsupported. Per tibia this completes 6D's scope; tibia closes 6D.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_6d_normalization_15 () = Note ("SPS-NB-6D-NORMALIZATION", 15u32, "2026-11-10T06:18Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:2x tibia: CLOSED. On the box: apps/kernel/src/linear_bool_normalization.spi d559bd9a5609 (org2-nb6d5 in-package: 26/26 executed, 0 unsupported). Coverage of main.spi:9500+: every non-aggregate terminal is a test here or in a named module (note 13 map); no_closed_false is the not_false witness; active_indexed_surface/self_root_contract/main are aggregators for SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT's final check.")
inl backend_bench_ci () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", "All-backend speed benchmark run through Cells and in GitHub Actions, iterated until faithful, with metrics published per run", Epic, P1, D6, 50u32, Active, "", "performance,benchmark,backends,cells,ci,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", Minutes 1500u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:42Z", "compiler", "User 11-09 21:1x: a benchmark measuring the speed of ALL backends, run through Cells, iterated until it is faithful; reuse what is useful from the perf code around (apps/compiler/scripts bench-native.ps1, bench-pair.ps1, alternating-ab.ps1, profile-speedscope.ps1; lib/spiral/bench_model.spi plan type with warmup passes, quiet cores, A/A bounds and MAD outliers, benchmark.spi; mega_brzozowski_derivatives runtime_bench + bench_* + regex_crate_bench.rs; kit/infra/nodebench) plus techniques from BenchmarkDotNet (pilot/warmup/target phases, overhead subtraction, outlier rules, confidence intervals), Rust criterion (bootstrap CI, change detection vs saved baseline, black_box) and hyperfine (warmup runs, shell-overhead correction, min/median/MAD); runs in the gh-pages workflow so every scheduled run publishes the metrics. Children 1-7 split it by owning lane. FAITHFUL = defined in child 5.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:25Z", "org3", "org3 cross-ref 11-10: this epic is a DELETION BLOCKER for two mega samples. REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION (brzozowski) and ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE (zeta) cannot drop their runtime_native / bench_* matrix rows until BACKEND-BENCH-CI absorbs those workloads as the durable native-at-scale bench home -- because compiler's KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS decision keeps SPS/CIC native coverage ON brzozowski/zeta/omniledger runtime rows. So the chain is: BACKEND-BENCH-CI absorbs brzozowski runtime_bench + bench_sieve/tree/strings/float (and the zeta runtime workload) -> THEN brzozowski/zeta can archive without losing large-program native coverage. Please make the brzozowski/zeta bench_* workloads an explicit input to whichever child owns the workload catalogue, and note the two retire items as downstream. Details in REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION note 5 + ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE note 4.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", 3u32, "2026-11-10T23:43Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:0x compiler (groom): steps 1 (inventory), 2 (workloads: 5 self-checking samples, 60/60 rows on 12 backends on moon, Lua cap fixed by pack87) and 4 (stats layer) are Done. Step 3 (Cells notebook, team:microblog) is unblocked and microblog was told 11-10 19:0x; step 5 (faithful, heavy) needs 3; step 6 (Actions step, team:org) needs 3. Progress 50% by steps. Next: microblogs step 3.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", 4u32, "2026-11-10T23:43Z", "compiler", "DoD (from the users request 11-09): a benchmark measuring the speed of ALL backends, (1) run through Cells (step 3), (2) iterated until faithful: A/A within bounds, rankings stable across runs, the CI numbers agree with node runs (step 5), (3) reusing the perf code and BenchmarkDotNet/criterion techniques (steps 1 + 4, Done), (4) running in GitHub Actions inside the existing workflow and publishing the metrics there: step summary table, raw rows artifact, gh-pages page (step 6). Responsible lanes decided per step (compiler 1/2/4/5, microblog 3, org 6). TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", 5u32, "2026-11-11T00:23Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:4x compiler: FAITHFULNESS FIX (microblogs step-3 split-build run showed C float at 21 ms for 8 Mandelbrot rounds vs Rust 400 ms: gcc hoisted the repeated pure call). Decision (b), a data dependency: each rounds input carries the previous rounds result through an opaque zero, work(input + last / MAX). The term is 0 for every real result but unprovable, and it chains the rounds. Applied to bench_float/sieve/tree/strings (box, unstaged); checks and exits unchanged. Verified ganymede gcc -O2: float 21 -> 270 ms; sieve 198, tree 2166, strings 105 ms; exits 197/246/241/166. microblog mirrors it in bench_cells. Rule for step 5: every new workload must chain its rounds the same way, and an A/A plus a \"rounds 1 vs 8 scales ~8x\" check flags any remaining hoisting.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_6 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI", 6u32, "2026-11-11T00:55Z", "microblog", "microblog answers its wait: step 3 (BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS) is Done. 20-cell Cells notebook at apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_cells, opaque rounds, memo off, build/run split on rust/c/zig(ReleaseFast)/gleam, receipt rows via SPIRAL_CELLS_PHASE_ROWS. Steps 5 (compiler) and 6 (org) can start; recipe on the step 3 item note 12.")
inl backend_bench_ci_1_inventory () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", "Backend bench step 1: inventory every perf tool and technique, decide reuse vs retire, write the harness design", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "-", "performance,benchmark,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_1_inventory () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_1_inventory_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:42Z", "compiler", "DoD: a note listing each existing perf script/module (see the epic) with keep / fold-in / retire, and the chosen technique per concern (warmup, iteration count, overhead, outliers, CI, change detection) citing its source (BenchmarkDotNet / criterion / hyperfine / bench_model.spi).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_1_inventory_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", 2u32, "2026-11-10T02:46Z", "compiler", "rig 11-09 input on kit/infra/nodebench (it measures HARDWARE, not backends): carry the METHOD, not the code. KEEP: (1) best-of-N (minimum) with nanosecond timers: it removed most cross-machine run-to-run noise; integer ms hid real differences. (2) PIN build flags per backend and RECORD them on every row: nodebench measured plain rustc -O (opt-level 2) ~1.9x slower than opt-level=3 + lto=fat + codegen-units=1 on the same box (the hot loop stops vectorizing), so a table mixing flag sets ranks flags, not backends. (3) Measure-only runs printing one fixed metrics line; rating/compare run separately over stored rows (nodebench rate.ps1), which keeps step 7 cheap. DROP: hardware metrics, the wgpu GPU path, rate.ps1s log-scale rating (step 7 uses CI comparison instead). Inventory verdict for nodebench: method kept (1-3), code retired from this harness.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_1_inventory_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "compiler", "Next step: list every perf script and module named in the epic note (apps/compiler/scripts bench-native/bench-pair/alternating-ab/profile-speedscope, lib bench_model.spi + benchmark.spi, mega_brzozowski runtime_bench + bench_* + regex_crate_bench.rs, kit/infra/nodebench method per note 2) with a keep / fold-in / retire verdict each, then the technique per concern.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_1_inventory_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", 4u32, "2026-11-10T03:32Z", "tibia", "11-09 23:4x tibia (help pool) INVENTORY, read from the files themselves (git ls-files + each script's param block and measurement lines; nothing was run). VERDICTS: (1) apps/compiler/scripts/bench-native.ps1 (113 lines; every backend dir per sample, Stopwatch, Runs=7, keeps the min): FOLD-IN as the step-3 runner's compile-then-run loop over backends; drop its own min-only statistics. (2) bench-pair.ps1 (103; compiler build A vs B, interleaved rounds, median, drops rounds whose LoadPercentage >= QuietCores): FOLD-IN; its quiet-round filter and alternation are the noise method, and its statistics move to bench_model. (3) alternating-ab.ps1 (65; compiler self-build variants w1/w8 x cw, rotated per round, median): FOLD-IN as a consumer of the same interleaved runner (compiler throughput is a second workload family, not a second harness). (4) profile-speedscope.ps1 (111; summarizes speedscope busy time per thread): KEEP, outside the harness; profiling explains a delta, it doesn't measure one. (5) bench-cells-vs-matrix.ps1 (127; test-runner wall time + sampled machine load) and (6) ebpf-dual-profile.ps1 (31; eBPF sample dual build): KEEP, out of scope (test infra and eBPF codegen, not backend runtime). (7) lib/spiral/bench_model.spi (129 lines, 8 tests; plan = rounds/passes/warmup_passes/quiet_cores/A-A band/MAD outlier rule, rotating arms, quiet-sample test, print units): KEEP as the statistics core that step 4 extends; zero consumers today (git grep), so step 3 is its first. (8) lib/spiral/benchmark.spi (355 lines; run' = integer-ms Stopwatch around am'::parallel_map over the repetition count, so repetitions run CONCURRENTLY and contend with each other; gc_collect once before): RETIRE as a measurement method; zero consumers (git grep), so removing it is a lib change for the lib lane to decide. (9) mega_brzozowski_derivatives/runtime_bench (main.spi plus 13 hand-written language ports) + regex_crate_bench.rs: FOLD-IN as the first step-2 workload; main.spi is already self-checking (four engines must agree; expect_counts 93/97/16) and prints one result line. (10) kit/infra/nodebench: method kept, code retired (note 2, rig).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_1_inventory_5 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", 5u32, "2026-11-10T03:32Z", "tibia", "11-09 23:4x tibia TECHNIQUE PER CONCERN + HARNESS DESIGN. Incumbent defaults are cited from their docs as known, not re-fetched tonight: verify any number before it goes into code. WARMUP: discarded warmup passes, fixed per workload (bench_model.warmup_passes). Sources: BenchmarkDotNet's warmup stage; criterion warm_up_time 3 s; hyperfine --warmup N. ITERATION COUNT: a pilot sizes the inner repeat so one measured pass takes >= ~100 ms, then a fixed number of interleaved ROUNDS (BenchmarkDotNet's pilot stage, IterationTime 500 ms; hyperfine's floor of 10 runs and 3 s). Whole-process timing for every backend, because in-process timers don't exist on all of them. OVERHEAD: an empty-workload arm per backend, i.e. the same binary with N=0 (hyperfine measures and subtracts shell spawn time; BenchmarkDotNet subtracts an overhead method), so start-up never counts as speed. NOISE + PLACEMENT: interleave and rotate arms every round (bench-pair, alternating-ab, bench_model rotation); drop rounds taken above the quiet-core threshold (bench-pair QuietCores, bench_model machine_state); pin and RECORD build flags per backend on every row (nodebench, note 2: opt-level 2 vs 3+LTO = 1.9x); nanosecond timers. OUTLIERS: MAD cutoff, and report how many were dropped (bench_model MadCutoff; hyperfine warns via a MAD-based modified z-score; BenchmarkDotNet removes upper Tukey-fence outliers). STATISTIC: median per arm, plus best-of-N on a separate hardware-only line (nodebench). CI: bootstrap CI on the median (criterion: 100k resamples, 95%); this is step 4. CHANGE DETECTION: paired per-round ratios with a bootstrap CI that must exclude 1, plus an A/A arm that must sit inside bench_model's aa band or the table is VOID (criterion: significance 0.05 + noise threshold 1%; tibia's runs use the same A/A-gated paired CI). DESIGN: workloads are self-checking Spiral samples (runtime_bench shape: engines agree + expected counts) compiled per backend with recorded flags. One measure-only runner (bench-native's loop + bench-pair's quiet filter) writes one fixed row per (workload, backend, round, arm). Statistics (bench_model + step 4) and the table/page run separately over the stored rows, so re-analysis never re-runs. Placement: node first (ganymede pinned cores), never overlapping a compile on the same node.")
inl backend_bench_ci_2_workloads () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", "Backend bench step 2: a self-checking workload set that every backend compiles and runs with identical output", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "BACKEND-BENCH-CI-1-INVENTORY", "performance,benchmark,backends,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:42Z", "compiler", "DoD: 4-6 workloads (seeded from runtime_bench and the mega runtime_native samples: CPU-bound loops, allocation/union-heavy, string, array) that run on every backend in the matrix (C, Rust, Zig, F#, TypeScript, Python, Gleam, Lua, Pascal, Kotlin, Swift, ... as each backend supports them), each printing a checksum so the harness rejects a fast-but-wrong run; per-backend support listed explicitly, no silent skips.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T02:46Z", "compiler", "Constraint from step 1 (rig, nodebench): each backend gets ONE pinned optimization flag set (e.g. Rust opt-level=3, lto=fat, codegen-units=1; C -O3 with a named compiler; Zig ReleaseFast; .NET Release + ReadyToRun or not, stated), recorded on every result row. Mixing flag sets ranks the flags, not the backends (rustc -O vs full release measured ~1.9x on one box).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:59Z", "compiler", "11-10 00:2x compiler: WORKLOAD 1 of the new set = apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_sieve (unstaged; core-only package): sieve of Eratosthenes to n = 2,000,000, repeated 8 rounds, every round self-checked against 148,933 primes (failwith otherwise), exit = total mod 256 = 40. Written with self-tail recursion (:~ ^) instead of !!!!While/!!!!Assign, because the Python and TypeScript backends reject Assign (\"Assign with 2 args not supported\"); n and rounds are ~ runtime values so partial evaluation cannot fold the work. Compiles on C, Rust, Zig, Python, TypeScript, F#, Lua, Gleam (8/8). Ran on ganymede (installed pack78, loaded node, single runs): C 154 ms, Rust 220 ms (opt-level 3 + lto fat + cgu 1), Zig 303 ms (ReleaseFast), Python 84.7 s; all exit 40. Not run yet: TypeScript (no bun on ganymede), Lua (no luajit), F#, Gleam, Pascal. DESIGN CONSEQUENCE for steps 3-5: one fixed size cannot serve every backend (Python is ~550x C, so 15 samples = 21 min per workload); the harness needs a per-backend size (a pilot that picks rounds so one pass is >= ~100 ms and <= a cap) instead of a size baked into the program. Next step: make rounds come from a per-backend input (backend switch on a runtime size, or an env/arg read where the backend has one), then workloads 2-4 (allocation-heavy union tree, string building + hashing, float n-body) from runtime_bench and the mega runtime_native samples.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:24Z", "compiler", "11-10 00:5x compiler: 4 SELF-CHECKING WORKLOADS in apps/compiler/tmp/samples (unstaged): mega_brzozowski_derivatives/runtime_bench (regex derivatives, 4 engines must agree; tibias seed), bench_sieve (int arrays, exit 197), bench_tree (recursive union allocation, exit 246), bench_strings (substring slicing + byte reads, exit 241). The three new ones share one convention: identical per-round work everywhere, rounds chosen per backend by !!!!BackendSwitch (8 compiled, 1 interpreted), each round self-checked, exit = one rounds checksum (2C). SUPPORT (compile, ganymede pack78): all 3 new workloads compile on C, Rust, Zig, Python, TypeScript, F#, Lua, Gleam. RAN + agree: C, Rust, Zig, Python. NOT RUN YET: TypeScript (no bun on ganymede), Lua (no luajit), F# (fsi), Gleam (erlang), Pascal, Kotlin, Swift, Wasm (moon/box toolchains). Next step: run the 4 workloads through test.ps1 -Suite examples -Native on moon (it has every native toolchain) once moon is free, list each backend x workload as agrees / build-fail / unsupported, then close this item.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_5 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T09:12Z", "compiler", "11-10 05:1x compiler: CORRECTION to the workload samples (unstaged): apps/compiler/tmp/samples packages resolve core- to the SAMPLES core (tmp/samples/core: dotted operators +. -. *. /. %. =., undotted comparisons, no failwith), not the language core. I had validated bench_* in a staging dir whose core symlinked the FULL core, so in the real suite they would have failed with ETY-UnboundVariable +. All rewritten: arithmetic in dotted operators (type products like tree * tree untouched) and a one-line local failwith helper (:= failwith \\* t. (msg : string) : t = !!!!FailWith(`t, msg)). Re-validated INSIDE the ganymede mirrors samples tree with pack82: C and Rust exits unchanged, bench_sieve 197, bench_tree 246, bench_strings 241, bench_float 166, bench_overhead 197.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_6 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T14:34Z", "compiler", "11-10 10:4x compiler: moon is quiet; the all-backend run is RUNNING (job-1794321248002-compiler-moon-bench-all-backends, installed pack83): the 5 bench samples (rewritten for the samples core: dotted operators, local failwith) registered in tests/matrix.psd1 for Zig, Python, Lua, Gleam, Kotlin, Swift, Wasm and AlsoTypeScript (box, unstaged; same lines applied to moons mirror), plus the default Fsharp/C/Rust/Pascal; test.ps1 -Suite examples -Filter bench_ -Native on moon, which has every native toolchain. Next step: read moons results.tsv and list each backend x workload as agrees / build-fail / unsupported, then close.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_7 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T14:45Z", "compiler", "11-10 10:5x compiler: DONE. Moon run (job-1794321248002, installed pack83, test.ps1 -Suite examples -Filter bench_ -Native): 5 workloads x 12 backends = 60 rows, ALL compile and run: C, Fsharp, Gleam, Kotlin, Lua, Pascal, Python, Rust, Swift, TypeScript, Wasm, Zig. Exits identical everywhere (overhead 197, sieve 197, tree 246, strings 241, float 166); 59 rows agree with the Zig oracle (the Zig rows are the oracle). ONE exception: Lua bench_strings timed out at 900 s (1 round) -> filed LUA-BENCH-STRINGS-TIMEOUT. Not run: Bend, Lean, Cpp, Wgsl/Calyx/OpenQasm/Ebpf (no strings/f64 or no runner for these programs); unsupported by design for this set. The set is ready for step 3 (the Cells benchmark notebook, microblog) and step 5 (CI job).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2_workloads_8 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T14:48Z", "compiler", "Evidence: moon results.tsv C:/home/remote-stage/moon-post/cache-bench/runs/single-flight-20261110-103409/results.tsv: 60 rows, compile ok 60, native ran 60, 59 exits agree, Lua strings timeout; ganymede C/Rust/Zig/Python runs earlier tonight.")
inl backend_bench_ci_3_cells () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", "Backend bench step 3: run the workloads through Cells (one notebook, per-test cells, timing rows in the receipt)", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS", "performance,benchmark,cells,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:42Z", "compiler", "DoD: a Cells notebook whose per-test cells build each workload per backend and record build time and run time as typed receipt rows; Cells memo forced OFF for timed cells (a memo hit is not a measurement); phases separated (compile, native build, run).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T02:43Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 microblog (Cells owner) ACCEPTS this slice; no other split needed. What Cells already has for it: (1) memo off: SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 turns off both the notebook memo and the cell-code memo (Memo.enabled?), so timed runs can set it per job; the bench should assert memo_hits = 0 in its spiral-tests totals rather than trust the flag. (2) Per-test compile is default-on since 11-09 (SPIRAL_CELLS_PER_TEST=0 opts out), so each test cell compiles alone: that is the unit to time. (3) Each .ipynb already records phases_ms per cell (mount, compile, native build, run). The receipt rows should be derived from those, not from a second stopwatch. Since 11-09, mount is no longer dominated by dotnet --resolve-manifest (Manifest.cached). (4) Compiler binaries: on Linux before 11-09 the memo never re-keyed on a compiler change (lowercase lookup bug, fixed), so compare only runs whose Cells carries that fix. (5) Explicit targets: every timed cell needs its ///> <backend> line; untargeted cells are refused (NoTestTarget). DoD addition: an A/A pair of the same notebook on one host, to size noise before any backend comparison (CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD showed ~15% wall slowdown under concurrency). NEXT STEP: once BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2-WORKLOADS lands, write the notebook with one test cell per workload x backend and a receipt row type { workload; backend; compile_ms; native_ms; run_ms; memo_hit : bool }. TYPEFEATURES: the backend as a union indexed by its toolchain (Rust | Gleam | C | Lua | Python | Fsharp ...), the receipt row typed, and memo_hit asserted false before a row is accepted.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T23:53Z", "microblog", "microblog 19:5x status for the epic: D1 (sieve on rust/c/zig/gleam) is rerunning on ganymede (job-1794353800982, queued behind other lanes) after the dotted-operator fix. D2 is drafted in drafts\\spiral\\BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS-D2\\bench_cells (all 5 workloads x 4 backends = 20 per-test cells): run-time sizes (~n, ~depth, ~copies, ~width/~height/~limit); the strings text is built at run time (195 copies = 4095 chars) instead of the 4 KB literal; each cell asserts the sample's own self-checks; overhead_<backend> gives the per-cell startup baseline. The receipt reads phases_ms (mount / compile / native build / run) and reports queue separately (42-44 s of node daemon queue in run 1). D2 runs after D1 proves the shape.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 4u32, "2026-11-11T00:11Z", "microblog", "D2 run 1 on europa failed: bench_cells package.spiproj listed only core-, and that Cells copy does not resolve 'open testing' implicitly. Added spiral- to the D1 and D2 manifests; D2 rerun job-1794355775523. D3 (c/gleam native build vs run split in phases_ms) landed.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_5 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 5u32, "2026-11-11T00:14Z", "microblog", "D2 PASS on europa (job-1794355775523): 20/20 per-test cells (5 workloads x rust/c/zig/gleam), memo_hits 0, 71 s wall. Landed (untracked) at spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_cells/{bench_cells.spi,package.spiproj} beside the bench_* workloads. phases_ms (ms; this run predates the D3 split, so c/zig/gleam show one fused build+run): rust build/run overhead 419/6, sieve 2316/272, tree 834/1797, strings 1402/147, float 674/293; c fused overhead 513, sieve 267, tree 3686, strings 446, float 227; zig fused 3725/3334/9771/4273/2710; gleam fused 1306/5675/1852/3164/2240. Compile 0.9-3.0 s, mount 0.04-1.5 s, node daemon queue 0-14 s reported separately. Next (step 3 remainder): rerun on the D3 build so c/gleam split build vs run, decide zig build-exe vs run, then the typed receipt rows (phases_ms -> one row per cell x backend) for step 5's faithfulness loop.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_6 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 6u32, "2026-11-11T00:18Z", "microblog", "Rerun on the split build (europa job-1794356124533): 20/20, memo_hits 0. c and gleam now report build vs run. Run ms: sieve rust 125 / c 157 (8 rounds) / gleam 6452 (1); tree 1908 / 2577 / 994; strings 276 / 218 / 2640; float 400 / 21 (!) / 1639. Build ms: rust 611-2637, c 253-369, gleam 573-1236; zig still fused 2.9-9.2 s. FAITHFULNESS FLAG for step 5: float_c runs 8 rounds of a 480x360x200 Mandelbrot in 21 ms, so gcc is very likely hoisting the repeated pure mandel call out of the round loop (the result is only compared with the first). The round loop needs an opaque dependency (feed r into the inputs, or a volatile/escape sink) before the C numbers mean anything; rust may be partly affected too.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_7 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 7u32, "2026-11-11T00:19Z", "microblog", "Step 3 state: the notebook (20 cells), the memo-off run and the phases_ms split are done (80%). Left: (1) opaque round loops so C/Rust can't hoist the repeated pure workload, which needs compiler's choice of mechanism (a black_box/opaque primitive in core, or feeding the round index into the inputs with a matching checksum); (2) typed receipt rows (cell x backend -> queue/compile/build/run) once (1) fixes what a run means. Waiting on compiler for (1).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_8 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 8u32, "2026-11-11T00:23Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:4x compiler, ANSWER to the lane:compiler wait (hoisting in float_c): decision (b), a data dependency chaining rounds, work(input + last / MAX), already applied to the 4 bench_* samples (exits unchanged; ganymede gcc -O2 float 21 -> 270 ms for 8 rounds). Exact forms sent to microblog; bench_cells mirrors them. Wait cleared.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_9 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 9u32, "2026-11-11T00:26Z", "microblog", "STEP-5 BASELINE (europa job-1794356634611, opaque rounds, split phases): 20/20, memo_hits 0. Run ms [rust / c (8 rounds) / gleam (1 round)]: sieve 252/93/5130, tree 1941/2348/995, strings 253/199/3604, float 351/450/2420 (float_c was 21 before the opaque chain, so hoisting is gone). Build ms: rust 423-2034, c 113-447, gleam 687-939. zig is fused: 2.5-7.9 s. Landed: apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_cells/bench_cells.spi (opaque form) + package.spiproj (core- + spiral-). Left for step 3: typed receipt rows; zig build/run split decision.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_10 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 10u32, "2026-11-11T00:26Z", "microblog", "compiler chose (b): every round feeds the previous result in through an opaque zero (x + last / MAX). Mirrored in bench_cells (sieve n + last/2147483647; tree depth + last/MAX; strings start index last/4294967295; float width + last/MAX; last starts at the first result). Step-5 baseline rerun: europa job-1794356634611.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_11 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 11u32, "2026-11-11T00:40Z", "microblog", "D4 landed: the bench runs with SPIRAL_CELLS_ZIG_RELEASE=1 so zig reports ReleaseFast build vs run like c/rust/gleam (europa: sieve 1479/235, tree 1492/2195, strings 1349/157, float 905/259 ms). Step 3 is functionally complete: 20-cell notebook, memo off, opaque rounds, build/run split on all 4 backends. Left only: typed receipt rows for step 5.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_3_cells_12 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-3-CELLS", 12u32, "2026-11-11T00:48Z", "microblog", "STEP 3 DONE. The bench runs through Cells: apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_cells (5 workloads x rust/c/zig/gleam, per-test cells, opaque rounds), memo off, build vs run split on every backend (zig via SPIRAL_CELLS_ZIG_RELEASE=1), and typed receipt rows via SPIRAL_CELLS_PHASE_ROWS=<file> (name, backend, queue, mount, compile, build, run, fused). Recipe: SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 SPIRAL_CELLS_ZIG_RELEASE=1 SPIRAL_CELLS_PHASE_ROWS=rows.tsv pwsh spi/run_notebook.ps1 --path <bench_cells.spi> --no-memo. Baseline numbers in notes 9-11. Step 5 (faithful, compiler) and step 6 (Actions, org) can start.")
