inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_4_stats_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-4-STATS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:42Z", "compiler", "DoD: lib bench_model.spi extended (or reused as is) so a plan yields median, MAD and a bootstrap confidence interval per backend x workload, rounds interleaved across backends (ABAB, not AAAA BBBB) so drift hits every arm alike, plus an A/A arm (same binary twice) whose ratio must sit in the plan's aa_low..aa_high; results as typed rows, not text.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_4_stats_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-4-STATS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:03Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:0x tibia (help pool): DRAFT drafts\\lib\\BACKEND-BENCH-CI-4-STATS\\bench_model.spi (sha 122739B30C3B over base 73353E54D603), extending lib bench_model.spi per the DoD. ADDS: schedule/schedule_from (every round runs every arm, with the order rotated one place per round, so drift and position hit each arm alike); percentile; a bootstrap CI on the median (bootstrap_ci, resample, boot_medians, pick), with resample indices from keyed_rng::mix32 so the CI is deterministic on every backend; typed row { workload; backend; arm; round; nanos } and summary { workload; backend; arm; count; mad; ci : spread (low = 2.5%, middle = median, high = 97.5%) } via cell_samples (MAD outlier rule applied) and summary_of; aa_ratio (twin median / base median, then aa_of into the plan's band). TESTS 11 (7 kept + 4 new): the schedule order for 2 rounds x 3 arms; the interval brackets the median (6 rows, the 500 outlier dropped, count 5, median 100); a twin at ratio 1.01 is InBand; a twin at 1.2 voids. EVIDENCE: (1) lib_land_window -PrivateLib -Apply on ganymede (job tibia-bench4q): round trip, signatures, consumer apps/spiral compiles, document_test 24 passed, type probe 11 typed / 0 errors, respell 0. One fix along the way: the lib spells record update { p ?| ... }, not with. (2) RUNTIME probe (job tibia-bench4r): the 11 tests run from a realworld probe module against the swapped-in draft: executed 11, passed 11, 0 unsupported. Box land pending: the box lib moved since the mirror copy (box predicts 8F656314800F8D9A, the proof had 7DB629FBF3A27952), so a re-proof on an exact copy of the box lib is running (job tibia-bench4s). Next step: after tibia-bench4s, land copy-only on the box if its lib digest equals the box prediction.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_4_stats_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-4-STATS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:04Z", "tibia", "TypeFeatures: typed records (row, summary, plan, spread) and the aa_verdict union carry every result; the outlier rule stays a union (KeepAll | MadCutoff); no string-typed results. Next step: after job tibia-bench4s, land copy-only on the box if its lib digest equals the box prediction.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_4_stats_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-4-STATS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:12Z", "tibia", "11-10 00:1x tibia: LANDED on the box lib (unstaged; lib/spiral/bench_model.spi is untracked in git), sha 122739B30C3B, copy-only from the proven close (lib_land_window -ProvenLog; undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261110-001156). PROOF CHAIN: (1) private-lib close on ganymede over an EXACT copy of the box lib (job tibia-bench4s: raw digest 566F65D3485BD784 equal on both sides, 419 lib files), with post-land digest 8F656314800F8D9A = the box's own -DigestOnly prediction, re-checked seconds before landing. Checks: signatures unchanged, consumer apps/spiral compiles, document_test 24 passed, type probe 11 typed / 0 errors, respell 0. (2) RUNTIME: 11/11 executed and passed, 0 unsupported (job tibia-bench4r, realworld probe over the same bytes). DoD MET: a plan yields median (ci.middle), MAD and a bootstrap CI per backend x workload cell (summary_of over typed rows); rounds interleave every arm with rotation (schedule); the A/A twin's ratio must sit in the plan's band (aa_ratio -> InBand | Void); results are typed rows/summaries, not text. Step 3's runner is the first consumer (bench_model had none before).")
