inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL", 1u32, "2026-11-10T02:42Z", "compiler", "FAITHFUL = all three, measured: (a) the A/A ratio stays within 0.97-1.03 on GitHub runners and 0.99-1.01 on a quiet node; (b) the backend ranking per workload is identical across 3 consecutive runs; (c) per-backend ratios vs the C baseline agree between a GitHub run and a quiet-node run within their confidence intervals. Report relative numbers (ratio to C in the same run) as the headline, since absolute times on shared runners drift. Iterate on round count, warmup and workload size until all three hold; record each iteration.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "compiler", "groom 11-09 (star digest, org3/microblog): no perf verdict from fewer than 15 samples. Each backend x workload cell needs >= 15 measured rounds (after warmup) before step 5 judges A/A bounds or rankings; fewer is reported as \"insufficient samples\", never as a result.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:03Z", "microblog", "microblog 21:0x: running compiler's aa.sh x5 on europa (job-1794359006334), m= repointed to /home/remote/xcache/spiral with tonight's landed Cells, notebook = landed bench_cells, out /tmp/mb-aa. Summary lines will follow here.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL", 4u32, "2026-11-11T01:46Z", "microblog", "microblog A/A x5 (europa job-1794359006334) is INVALID, a receipt bug on my side, not a measurement. (1) The phase rows had an EMPTY test name: notebook code cells don't carry the ':# name =' line, which is a markdown header, so aa.sh grouped all 20 cells into 4 per-backend buckets ('0 of 4 within 10%', spreads 380-1180% are workload mixing). Fixed and landed: keep_phase_row now takes the name from the run report's test entry. A real europa run (job-1794361489101) gives 20/20 rows with names (sieve_rust rust queue mount compile build run fused). (2) Runs 4 and 5 wrote no TSV although both passed 20/20: still open, maybe the ipynb render path is skipped on unchanged repeat runs. The next A/A should check rows=20 per run. Rerun aa.sh after 22:00; europa /tmp/mb-aa keeps runs 1-3 (nameless).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_5 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL", 5u32, "2026-11-11T01:47Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:5x compiler: the first A/A x5 (microblog, europa) is INVALID: the receipt rows had an empty test name (code cells do not carry the :# name), so aa.sh grouped 20 cells into 4 per-backend buckets (\"0 of 4 within 10%\", 380-1180% spreads from mixing workloads). microblog fixed the row name (from the run reports test entry; e.g. \"sieve_rust rust 14963 1306 1967 717 153 0\") in their tree. aa.sh now takes the tree and expected row count as arguments and retries a run once when it writes fewer rows than expected (runs 4 and 5 had passed 20/20 but written no TSV). RERUN STARTED: europa ~/remote-stage/aa2 (tree /home/remote/xcache/spiral, notebook bench_cells_aa, 5 runs, 20 rows each, quiet-window gated); it will finish after 22:00, so the verdict is the next sessions. Next step: read ~/remote-stage/aa2/g.log (per-cell median, spread, \"A/A: X of 20\").")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_6 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL", 6u32, "2026-11-11T01:47Z", "microblog", "microblog answers its wait: the receipt-row name bug is fixed and landed (named rows verified on europa, 20/20), and compiler's aa.sh now retries short runs. The rerun is back with compiler (europa tree m=/home/remote/xcache/spiral is ready).")
