inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_6_actions_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-6-ACTIONS", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 DRAFTED (kit drafts i574n.github/BACKEND-BENCH-CI-6-ACTIONS/workflows.spi over scripts/pins/workflows.spi, the typed source the spiral gh-pages.yml is generated from; YAML is never hand-edited). Two steps added to spiral_cells_gate_job (the scheduled/dispatch cells-gate job; no new job), between ci_gate.ps1 and the existing always() artifact upload: (1) bench_cells_step runs microblog step-3 recipe from apps/cells: SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 SPIRAL_CELLS_ZIG_RELEASE=1 SPIRAL_CELLS_PHASE_ROWS=<runner.temp>/cells-gate/bench_rows.tsv pwsh spi/run_notebook.ps1 --path apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_cells/bench_cells.spi --no-memo, with || echo BENCH-FAILED so a bench failure is visible but does not fail the job until BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL; (2) bench_summary_step turns the rows into a markdown table (test, backend, compile ms, build ms, run ms: columns 1, 2, 5, 6, 7 of notebook.spi phase_row, which has no header) appended to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY. The rows file lands in the cells-gate dir, so the EXISTING upload-artifact step carries the raw rows: no new action, actions.lock unchanged. Not yet: the gh-pages metrics page (needs the pages push job to receive the rows; follow-up). Next step: regenerate the YAML from the draft with pins.ps1 on a node, diff it against gh-pages.yml (only the 2 new steps may change), then land both")
