inl note_of_compiler_install_full_set_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:10Z", "compiler", "From 11-09: copying only SpiralCompiler(Core).dll left a stale FSharp.Core (same assembly version 11.0.0.0, different bytes) and broke every lane's lib land on the box (Method not found ListModule.emptyListError); --capabilities did not catch it. DoD: ~/remote-stage/packinst.sh (Linux) and the Windows guarded copy install the full build output (35 files on Windows; Linux currently differs in 26 files IL vs ReadyToRun), back up the whole bin, and gate on --check <lib file> --timeout-ms 300000 with whole-bin rollback; NEXT STEP: port the scratchpad inst78-full.ps1 logic into packinst.sh and a repo-side Windows equivalent (no new .ps1 in repos: extend install-pack.ps1 with a -FromDir mode instead).")
inl note_of_compiler_install_full_set_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:41Z", "compiler", "11-09 23:4x compiler: BUILT + PROVEN on the box (unstaged, spiral apps/compiler/scripts/install-pack.ps1; no new script). New -FromDir <build output dir>: refuses a dir without SpiralCompilerCore.dll + build-identity.json, and refuses unless build-identity.jsons sourceSha16 equals the reviewed candidate core; then installs EVERY file through the existing full-set copy, verifies 0 hash mismatches after the copy, runs the launch check, then a REAL smoke (new -Smoke, default lib/spiral/process.spi, --check --timeout-ms 300000, package dir from Get-SpiralPackageDir when unset) that fails on exit != 0 or Method not found / MissingMethod / TypeLoad / FileNotFound and ROLLS BACK the whole bin from the backup. The smoke also runs for -FromStore / -FromUrls installs. Proof (box, same-pack reinstall of moons pack78 output): \"from dir ... built from the reviewed candidate core 1f2c48f6\", 35 files, mismatches 0, launch True, smoke exit 0 ok True, INSTALLED. Note: after an install, live already IS the candidate, so a reinstall passes no -Programs. Next step: after pack79 gates, install it on ganymede + europa with pwsh install-pack.ps1 -Name pack79 -FromDir <build dir> -Apply (the Linux proof), then retire ~/remote-stage/packinst.sh.")
inl note_of_compiler_install_full_set_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:43Z", "compiler", "TypeFeatures: none in Spiral (a PowerShell install script); the typed boundary is build-identity.jsons sourceSha16 checked against the reviewed candidate core before any copy, so a bin from another build cannot install. Next step: after pack79 gates, the Linux proof with pwsh install-pack.ps1 -FromDir on ganymede + europa.")
inl note_of_compiler_install_full_set_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET", 4u32, "2026-11-10T05:34Z", "compiler", "11-10 01:4x compiler: Linux proof IN PROGRESS on ganymede. Mirror synced to pack78 live source (core 1f2c48f6, host 79070d91) + the new install-pack.ps1 (old copies in ~/remote-stage/inst79/mirror-before); candidate ~/.cache/spiral-bin-candidates/pack79/source; KIT_BIN = the nodes kit debug build (has kit do). First -Apply attempt: the candidate reproduced, then the in-use guard REFUSED (an alphabet Cells gate launches the installed compiler for --resolve-manifest about every second), the guard working as designed. A detached loop (~/remote-stage/inst79/w.sh, log w.log, 6 h cap) retries -FromDir -Apply only after a 60 s quiet window (no installed-compiler process and no run_notebook.ps1 across 12 samples); every attempt also re-runs the guard, the full-set copy check and the real --check smoke with rollback. Next step: read w.log / apply.log; on INSTALLED record files, mismatches and smoke, then europa from the store via -MintUrls + -FromUrls.")
inl note_of_compiler_install_full_set_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET", 5u32, "2026-11-10T06:07Z", "compiler", "11-10 02:0x compiler: DONE, Linux proof landed. ganymede 06:04Z: pwsh install-pack.ps1 -Name pack79 -Programs <parser kitdo> -FromDir <pack79 gate build output> -Apply (KIT_BIN = node kit build): candidate reproduced from live (1F2C48F6 + program -> 089D8707 = reviewed), whole-bin copy 35 files with 0 mismatches, launch check True under the resolved dotnet, real smoke --check process.spi exit 0 ok, Cells domain stamp removed, backup ~/.cache/spiral-bin/compiler-installs/pack79-20261110-060353. Installed Core 9f1ef997 / host c51a27a4 = the gate build. The in-use guard refused while Cells gates ran; the quiet-window loop installed at the first 60 s quiet stretch. packinst.sh is superseded (install-pack covers Linux; retire it from remote-stage when no lane references it). Windows half proven 11-09 23:4x on the box (pack78 -FromDir, 35 files, smoke ok).")
inl note_of_compiler_install_full_set_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-INSTALL-FULL-SET", 6u32, "2026-11-10T06:08Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede ~/remote-stage/inst79/apply.log 06:04Z (35 files, mismatches 0, launches True, smoke exit 0 ok, install exit=0) + installed SpiralCompilerCore.dll sha 9f1ef997 = gate build; box 11-09 23:4x pack78 -FromDir proof (35 files, mismatches 0, smoke ok).")
inl compiler_store_put_r2r_guard () = Task ("COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD", "oort pack put refuses a non-ReadyToRun pair and a still-running build", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,packs,oort,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_store_put_r2r_guard () = Planning ("COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_store_put_r2r_guard_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:10Z", "compiler", "From 11-09: the pack78 win-x64 store entry is the IL pair because I fetched between build.ps1's IL build and its in-place ReadyToRun step; oort keys are immutable, so it stuck. DoD: the put path checks Test-ReadyToRunImage (build.ps1) on both DLLs and refuses otherwise, and the fetch step waits on kit job list state=finished exit=0, not on DLL presence. NEXT STEP: move the scratchpad oort-put-pack.ps1 check into install-pack.ps1 as a -Put mode (no new repo .ps1), with the R2R check before rclone copy.")
inl note_of_compiler_store_put_r2r_guard_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:49Z", "compiler", "11-09 23:5x compiler: BUILT (unstaged, install-pack.ps1, no new script) + a ROOT CAUSE found on the way. ROOT CAUSE of tonights box FSharp.Core break: the store base key is compiler/base/v1/deps-<hash of the fsproj files>/sdk-<label>/rid-<rid>, so the win-x64 rc.3 base was put once from a build whose SDK was not really rc.3 (it holds FSharp.Core c235edbd), and every win-x64 store install pairs a rc.3-built compiler with that stale FSharp.Core; immutable, so it cannot be fixed in place. FIX: new -Put -FromDir <build output> -TargetSdk <exact> [-TargetRid]: refuses unless build-identity.json sourceSha16 = the reviewed candidate core, refuses unless BOTH DLLs are ReadyToRun images (the PE ManagedNativeHeader test copied from build.ps1s Test-ReadyToRunImage), then puts a v2 BASE keyed by CONTENT (compiler/base/v2/files-<sha256 of the sorted name+sha rows of every non-pair file>/rid-<rid>, manifest schema compiler-base/v2) and the pair with a new manifest field base = that key; rclone --immutable for both. READER: Get-StoreInstall fetches the pair first and follows pair.base when present (falls back to the v1 key for old entries); -MintUrls likewise reads the pair manifest (rclone cat) to mint the right base. A pair can no longer meet deps from another build. PROOF so far (box): parse 0; -Put on a dir whose 2 DLLs are the IL copies refused with \"IL only ... wait for the build job to EXIT\"; the final pair tests as ReadyToRun. Next step: the real round trip with pack79 (put linux-x64 from ganymedes build output via -Put, then install it on europa with -FromStore / -FromUrls, smoke exit 0). TypeFeatures: none in Spiral (PowerShell); the typed boundaries are the content-hash base key and the pair manifests base field.")
inl note_of_compiler_store_put_r2r_guard_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD", 3u32, "2026-11-10T05:32Z", "compiler", "11-10 01:4x compiler: DONE. install-pack.ps1 -Put (unstaged, no new script) PUT pack79 linux-x64 to the store from the finished ganymede build output: refused nothing because build-identity sourceSha16 = 089d8707 = the reviewed candidate and Test-ReadyToRunImage passed on both DLLs; base is the NEW content-addressed key compiler/base/v2/files-9d42858d.../rid-linux-x64 (33 files, manifest schema compiler-base/v2), pair compiler/pack/v1/core-089d8707.../host-79070d91.../sdk-11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148/rid-linux-x64 with manifest.base naming that v2 key, rclone --immutable. Completeness checked from the box with -MintUrls (10 min expiry, file deleted right after): 37 objects = base 34 + pair 3. The refusal side was proven 11-09 23:5x (the pack78 IL pair was refused as IL only). A still-running build cannot pass: until build.ps1 exits, the DLLs are IL (R2R rewrites them last). Windows store installs still read the stale v1 base for pack78 until a win-x64 v2 put (next Windows pack).")
inl note_of_compiler_store_put_r2r_guard_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-STORE-PUT-R2R-GUARD", 4u32, "2026-11-10T05:34Z", "compiler", "Evidence: box 11-10 01:4x, pwsh scripts/install-pack.ps1 -Name pack79 -Put -FromDir <ganymede pack79 bin copy> -TargetSdk 11.0.100-rc.3.26522.148 -TargetRid linux-x64 printed PUT ... both DLLs ReadyToRun; build-identity matches the reviewed candidate; -MintUrls listed 37 objects (base 34, pair 3); IL refusal proven 11-09 23:5x on pack78.")
inl fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec () = Task ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", "fiscal p2p events carry their payloads and round-trip through a typed codec (OMNILEDGER R8a, also finishes R7)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,erp,mega-samples,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec () = Planning ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:10Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "From the 11-09 mega-sample review (OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n17). Sample S = mega_omniledger_erp_kernel main.spi:6590-8974: each ERP operation encodes to a length-prefixed payload, decodes back to a typed operation, and truncated or wrong-family payloads are rejected. Fiscal p2p.spi:205-222 today: 4 payload-free events (reserved, approved, ordered, received) and a payload hash over the event name. DoD: p2p_event s indexed by the purchase stage, one event per stage incl. matched, paid, closed, each carrying its operation data; encode/decode round trip for every event; negatives for a truncated payload and a payload of the wrong event family; event_log payload hashes over the encoded payload. NEXT STEP: draft p2p_event s in fiscal src/p2p.spi from S's operation shapes, then the codec over lib event_log's framed lines. TypeFeatures: stage-indexed GADT for events, existential over the stage in the log.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Groom 2 (star exchange 1 digest, memory star-exchange-2026-11-09-night-lessons): (a) ported is not tested: before estimating, map the sample's own tests for this behaviour (S negative_event_payload_codec_cross_family and the payload round-trip :# tests) to their _terminal definitions and measure the scope; (b) the log's existential over the stage: never build the indexed witness inline inside \\? (...), bind it through a typed helper first (ETY-ExistsShouldntHaveMetavars). NEXT STEP: the test map, then draft p2p_event s.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:43Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 00:4x TEST MAP (ported is not tested): the sample's tests are its _terminal definitions plus negative_* dirs. Codec core S:6590-6830 (NetIntercompany): payload_frame_terminal :6648 (encode the typed op to a length-prefixed field frame, base64; bytes > 0, SHA-256 digest 32 bytes), payload_decode :6681 returning a decision union ErpNetIntercompanyPayloadDecoded proof | ErpNetIntercompanyPayloadRejected reason (a decision that carries its reason, not a bool), payload_decode_typed_operation :6726 (rebuilds the fully indexed op: invoice_match entity/currency/item/location/jurisdiction/document + opposed mirror pair), typed_decode_authority_from_bytes :6770 (asserts encode (decode bytes) = bytes), payload_codec_terminal :6789 (accepts the canonical frame and rejects a truncated one); downstream terminals settle_payment_from_decoded :6905, close_period_from_decoded :6874, five..eight event store terminals :6949-7113 (the log grows one typed event per stage, version counted by type-level naturals nat_add). Negatives: negative_event_payload_codec_cross_family, negative_p2p_{two,three,four}_event_* (wrong version, skipped middle, wrong final stage). The sample frames with F# string macros; fiscal's version must be portable Spiral over lib event_log framed lines (line_checksum) and xml/wire helpers. SCOPE for fiscal (estimate 180 m, was 120): (1) p2p_event s with a payload per stage incl. matched/paid/closed (fiscal p2p.spi has purchase s stages already); (2) encode/decode with a decode_decision union carrying the reason; (3) round-trip + truncation + cross-family negatives; (4) record_step hashes the encoded payload. The type-level event-count (nat_add) part stays out; fiscal's log head is an i64. Next step: draft (1) and (2) in kit drafts fiscal\\FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC over live p2p.spi 715E5792.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:34Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 04:5x DRAFT p2p.spi BB91B98F over live 715E5792: cell budget neutral (live 7 -> draft 7 over), lib_roundtrip canonical 1/1. The private p2p_event carries payloads (WasReserved item*amount, WasApproved names, WasOrdered number, WasReceived amount, WasMatched key, WasPaid reference), built from typed purchases (reserved_event .. paid_event); encode_event frames tag|len:field..., decode_event returns event_decision (Decoded | Rejected reason) via fields_from/next_field/event_of; step_hash hashes the full frame, so a changed payload for a logged stage collides. Tests: ordering events round-trip, matched and paid round-trip, truncated frame rejected, other family rejected, reservation needs two fields, changed received payload Collided at 4. Fixed on the way: field_length used a type annotation as an i64->i32 conversion; now convert::i32. Not compiled yet. FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS stacks on this draft. Next step: node gate of p2p.spi with a pinned compiler once moon leaves TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", 5u32, "2026-11-10T05:15Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:2x box gate 11-10 00:57-01:12 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib, -Parallel 1, 943 s). The stacked p2p (codec + match legs + order ref) did not typecheck; both errors were this draft's: framed_field passed sm'::length straight to obj_to_string, leaving its integer type open (ETY-ValueRestriction; now annotated : i32), and logged_ordering was placed before ordering_events (ETY-UnboundVariable; moved below). Codec draft now 17FA4639 (7 over = live, canonical). Next step: the box re-gate of the stacked p2p decides this draft too.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_event_codec_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC", 6u32, "2026-11-10T05:35Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:3x PROVEN AND LANDED. box re-gate 11-10 01:22-01:34 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib, document DE4BB79E + canon AA43331F overlaid): p2p.spi DD5BDC7E GREEN, discovered 39 executed 39 passed 39 failed 0 in 631 s; document and canon were green 8/8 each in the 00:57 gate. LANDED copy-only into C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\src (unstaged, never committed) after the live bases matched (document DFE711A4, canon ADA23785, p2p 715E5792); undo in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE\\undo-20261110-013454. the payload-carrying p2p_event, its frame codec (encode_event / decode_event with event_decision) and step_hash over the full frame are live; round-trip, truncation, other-family and collision tests pass. Next step: none; Done.")
