inl note_of_fiscal_eventlog_indexed_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:11Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "From the 11-09 type-usage review (FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS n1): fiscal's own 11-09 R6/R9 lands broke the modeling rule. lib event_log.spi: membership and audit use :: constructors with no index, membership_code (:122) and audit_code (:177) encode cases as i64 0/1/2, append_outcome's Replayed/Collided/Stale are uniform i64 cases, entry ev stores id and hash as raw string although command_id and payload_hash nominals exist. DoD: membership m and audit a indexed by phantom outcome (or the codes removed in favour of the constructors), entry fields typed by the existing nominals, the R6/R9 tests unchanged and green through lib_land_window. NEXT STEP: draft in kit drafts spiral\\FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED over live 08687CF1 and check cell budget + round trip. TypeFeatures: phantom-indexed outcomes, nominal ids.")
inl note_of_fiscal_eventlog_indexed_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:46Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:0x draft AAC5B4F3 checked: over-budget cells 11 = live 11 (membership_of no longer over; the rewritten audit test with its Corrupt match is), round trip canonical. Fiscal companion 01F2BBAF (lifecycle.spi test compares send ... <> event_log::Replayed 1i64). Next step: on a free node, lib_gate event_log.spi with the draft, then a proof landing both files (lib via lib_land_window, fiscal companion copied after).")
inl note_of_fiscal_eventlog_indexed_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED", 3u32, "2026-11-10T05:11Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:1x local BASE MOVED: fiscal lifecycle.spi is now 76449093 (FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY landed: system_regime, line_verdict, issued_nfe_doc, nfe_line_verdict and two tests). This item's fiscal companion drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED\\lifecycle.spi (01F2BBAF) was built on 4C061E89; its only change there is the test line '? send (event_log::appended_log first) <> event_log::Replayed 1i64', so the rebase is that one edit over 76449093. Next step: re-apply that edit over the new live lifecycle.spi, recheck budget and round trip.")
inl note_of_fiscal_eventlog_indexed_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED", 4u32, "2026-11-10T05:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:3x companion REBASED: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED\\lifecycle.spi E590F259 over the newly landed live lifecycle 76449093 (the one test line now compares the union, 'send (event_log::appended_log first) <> event_log::Replayed 1i64'); cell budget 13 -> 13, lib_roundtrip canonical. The old companion is kept as lifecycle.old-companion-01F2BBAF.spi. The lib half (event_log.spi AAC5B4F3) still goes through lib_land_window, and the companion must land in the same window because it drops outcome_code. Next step: prove event_log + the fiscal companion together on a node (or the box when the nodes stay saturated), then land lib copy-only and the fiscal companion together.")
inl note_of_fiscal_eventlog_indexed_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED", 5u32, "2026-11-10T10:36Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 07:2x WAIT ANSWERED: this waited on 'a node lib gate + proof (moon after TRAIN43, or ganymede once base deps exist)'; ganymede's base deps now exist and a node-proof notebook probe ran green there (NODE-PROOF-LINUX-TARGET, tests passed 1/1). Next step: prove lib event_log.spi AAC5B4F3 + the fiscal lifecycle companion CF106BDA on ganymede via lib_land_window with a pinned compiler, then land lib copy-only and the companion together.")
inl note_of_fiscal_eventlog_indexed_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED", 6u32, "2026-11-10T11:03Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 07:5x PROOF RUNNING on ganymede: job-1794308453537-fiscal-evlog-proof (node-proof mirror fiscal-evlog, spiral + dice synced, alphabet documents.spi placed by hand because its bundle fetch failed; node lib replaced wholesale by the box's exact lib tar, 419 files; pinned compiler copy; lib_land_window -Draft event_log.spi=AAC5B4F3 -BaseHash 08687CF1780A -PrivateLib -Apply). Box prediction: lib digest 002B62DF357BD5F8 now, post-land 11687AFCF8D33A6A. Removed functions (outcome_code, membership_code, audit_code) have no caller outside fiscal lifecycle.spi, which the rebased companion CF106BDA replaces. Next step: on a green close with post-land digest 11687AFCF8D33A6A, land lib copy-only on the box with -ProvenLog and copy the companion into fiscal src together.")
