inl fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify () = Task ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", "fiscal: one regime phantom vocabulary shared by lifecycle, families and money (the prerequisite of regime-indexed rounding and buyer_response r)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,erp,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify () = Planning ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:11Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "From the 11-09 type-usage review: fiscal has two regime vocabularies, lifecycle.spi:9-13 (:! nfe = string style nominals) and families.spi:714 (:! brazil = () phantoms with regime_witness r). DoD: one phantom set used by regime_witness, the response/cancellation prototypes in lifecycle.spi and (next) a regime-indexed rounding r; no behaviour change; fiscal unit tests green at the next gate. NEXT STEP: list every use of both vocabularies (grep lifecycle.spi, families.spi, canon_*), pick the families.spi phantoms as the survivors, draft the lifecycle side in fiscal src. Unblocks FISCAL-ERP-MONEY's last gap and FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX. TypeFeatures: phantom regime index shared across modules.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:31Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-09 23:5x RESCOPED after reading the code: the two vocabularies are two AXES, not duplicates. lifecycle.spi:9-13 nominals (:! nfe = string etc.) are the document SYSTEM and carry the layout version (nfe '4.00', stored as a::regime and used for prototype dispatch of cancellation/correction/response events); families.spi:714 phantoms (brazil, europe_ubl, mexico) are the country REGIME (Brazil covers NF-e, CT-e, MDF-e). Merging them would lose the version and contradict the 11-09 rule on FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX (add a regime witness only with its first regime-specific operation). Right shape: a relation GADT system_regime s r in lifecycle.spi (families comes first in module order, lifecycle references families::), e.g. NfeIsBrazil :: system_regime nfe families::brazil, CfdiIsMexico, UblIsEurope, introduced together with its first cross-axis operation: the regime-indexed rounding that closes FISCAL-ERP-MONEY (a document's system picks its regime's legal rounding mode and places). The legal rules are being sourced first (NF-e/ABNT NBR 5891, CFDI Anexo 20 per c_Moneda, EN 16931 BR-DEC) so no mode is encoded from memory. Next step: after the sourced rules arrive, draft system_regime s r plus regime_rounding r in fiscal src and gate on a node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:44Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 00:5x sourced rules arrived (see FISCAL-ERP-MONEY latest note): regimes define tolerance windows and decimals, not rounding modes. The first cross-axis operation is therefore amount validation: a document's system (nfe, cfdi, ubl) selects its regime's acceptance window, which is where system_regime s r pays. Next step: draft system_regime s r in lifecycle.spi together with the amount_window r draft on FISCAL-ERP-MONEY, and gate both on a node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 4u32, "2026-11-10T03:50Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:3x DRAFTED from the sourced rules (kit drafts fiscal\\FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY). families.spi 0C0D8683 over 6A44ED14: amount_window r (NfeItem :: brazil; CfdiLine :: i32 currency places -> mexico; En16931Amount :: europe_ubl), window_verdict r (Within / Outside, each carrying the lower and upper bounds, a decision with its evidence instead of a bool), window_bounds (NF-e round2(q x v) +-0.01 per NT 2011/004 s4.4; CFDI Anexo 20: Floor at the currency places of (q - half unit)(v - half unit) and Ceiling of (q + half unit)(v + half unit); EN 16931 round2 +-0.02 per Peppol R120), window_check; tests a_cfdi_line_is_checked_against_its_anexo_20_window (q 3, v 10.00, 2 places -> 29.93..30.07, 30.00 within, 30.08 outside), an_nfe_item_allows_one_centavo_either_way, and the negative a_brazilian_window_cannot_check_a_mexican_line. KNOWN DEVIATION: SAT's upper bound also subtracts 10^-12 from each factor; lib decimal's i64 units overflow at scale 24, so the draft omits it; it only changes the result when the exact product lands less than ~1e-11 above a grid point. lifecycle.spi F687307B over 4C061E89: system_regime s r (NfeIsBrazil, CfdiIsMexico, UblIsEurope) linking the document system to the country regime, and line_verdict, which takes the link, the regime's window and a document s st, so a NF-e document cannot be checked against the CFDI window (negative test an_nfe_document_cannot_use_the_cfdi_window). MERGE NOTE: the event_log companion draft 01F2BBAF also edits lifecycle.spi over the same base; land them as one merged file. Next step: after budget + round trip, gate families and lifecycle on a free node, then close FISCAL-ERP-MONEY's gap (c_Moneda places table next).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 5u32, "2026-11-10T04:27Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 04:3x DRAFTS BUDGET-NEUTRAL AND CANONICAL (families 12F8BF31, lifecycle 76449093; bases families 6A44ED14, lifecycle 4C061E89). Cell budget on the box: families live 35 -> draft 35, lifecycle 14 -> 14; lib_roundtrip canonical 2/2. Changes: cfdi_bounds split into cfdi_low/cfdi_high over a cfdi_half, the NF-e and EN 16931 arms share tolerance_window, verdict_of builds the verdict; CFDI tests split (bounds, inside, outside), the NF-e window test split into low and high edges; lifecycle gets an nfe_line_verdict fixture. Known deviation stays: SAT's -10^-12 term is omitted (i64 overflow at scale 24). Merge note: the FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED companion edits lifecycle.spi too. Next step: node gate of families.spi + lifecycle.spi with a pinned compiler once moon leaves TRAIN43 (or ganymede gets fiscal deps); then hand CfdiLine its places from FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 6u32, "2026-11-10T05:05Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:0x local BOX GATE (nodes saturated: moon 100% under TRAIN43, ganymede ~11 on 4 cores; the run is autonomous and the gate offered the idle box, so one capped run at -Parallel 1): staged copy of fiscal src in the session scratchpad with the drafts overlaid, deps junctioned to the live spiral lib and corpus, pinned compiler copy core F414863971EB2A2C, SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0, build.ps1 -Files ... -NoGateCache. families.spi 12F8BF31: GREEN, discovered 10 executed 10 passed 10 failed 0, 159 s (CFDI Anexo 20 bounds/inside/outside, NF-e one-centavo edges, and the Unification negative). lifecycle 76449093 still running in the same gate. Next step: record lifecycle's verdict when the gate ends, then clear the TRAIN43 wait if both are green (box proof stands in for the node gate; lib untouched).")
inl note_of_fiscal_regime_phantoms_unify_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY", 7u32, "2026-11-10T05:11Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:1x local PROVEN AND LANDED. Box gate (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib): families.spi 12F8BF31 green 10/10 in 159 s; lifecycle.spi 76449093 green 16/16 in 176 s. Live bases matched (families 6A44ED14, lifecycle 4C061E89), so both copied into C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\src (unstaged, never committed); undo copies in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY\\undo-20261110-011123. The fiscal FISCAL-EVENTLOG-INDEXED companion (lifecycle.spi 01F2BBAF over base 4C061E89) must now be rebased onto 76449093. Next step: rebase the event_log companion; the CFDI window's ISO places land with FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES (currency.spi still in this gate).")
inl fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential () = Task ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", "fiscal sunat: affectation becomes an existential over igv_affectation g; tax scheme and price type are indexed by the affectation", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,pe,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential () = Planning ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:11Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "From the 11-09 type-usage review: sunat.spi:28 affectation (Taxed | Exempt | Unaffected) is a hand-written existential around the phantom-indexed igv_affectation g, with three duplicated dispatchers (:241, :247, :290); tax_scheme (:195/232) is a plain union ending in a catch-all, and expected_price_type (:298) picks by a bool. DoD: affectation = \\? g. igv_affectation g, the three dispatchers collapse to one, tax_scheme and price_type indexed so a scheme or price type that contradicts the affectation does not type (negative tests), rule (b) and the 58 homologation cases still green. NEXT STEP: draft in fiscal src/sunat.spi and check budget + round trip. TypeFeatures: existential over the affectation index, GADTs for scheme and price type.")
inl note_of_fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Groom 2 (star exchange 1 digest): pack each affectation through a typed helper (\\* g. igv_affectation g -> affectation) instead of building the indexed witness inline inside \\? (...), which fails ETY-ExistsShouldntHaveMetavars. NEXT STEP: draft the helper plus the existential in fiscal src/sunat.spi, then budget + round trip.")
inl note_of_fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:39Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 00:2x RESCOPED after reading the code. The review's existential is WRONG here: affectation_of picks the index from a runtime catalog-07 code, and Spiral existentials are compile-time packs (a runtime branch that packs different indices fails 'Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var'), so the hand-written union affectation (Taxed | Exempt | Unaffected over igv_affectation g) is the correct staged design for runtime-chosen indices. A second onerous/free index on igv_affectation is also out: taxed_cases () mixes onerous and free constructors in one runtime list, which cannot hold mixed indices. The real smell was the 3 duplicated dispatchers. DRAFT (kit drafts fiscal\\FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL\\sunat.spi 43ADBA25 over live 330CB163, 462 -> 456 lines): one eliminator on_affectation \\* r. (visit : \\* g. igv_affectation g -> r) (a : affectation) : r (rank-2 visitor, the shape of the contract_* samples' visit parameters), and code_of, affectation_scheme, affectation_is_onerosa become one-liners over it. Budget + round trip running. Next step: after the checks, gate sunat.spi on a node (catalog 07 round trip, scheme and price tests, the 58 homologation cases) and land in the tree.")
inl note_of_fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", 4u32, "2026-11-10T03:48Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:1x draft 43ADBA25 checked: over-budget cells 21 = live 21, round trip canonical. Next step: on a free node, run fiscal's sunat.spi tests with the draft (catalog 07 round trip, scheme/price tests, the 58 homologation cases), then land it in the tree.")
inl note_of_fiscal_sunat_affectation_existential_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-SUNAT-AFFECTATION-EXISTENTIAL", 5u32, "2026-11-10T06:05Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:1x NOT FEASIBLE AS DESIGNED, closed with evidence. proof: box gate (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, live lib, draft sunat.spi 43ADBA25) failed typechecking at all three call sites of the eliminator: sunat.spi:101 'Got: forall g. igv_affectation g -> string Expected: igv_affectation _ -> string In the definition: code_of', and the same at 243 (affectation_scheme) and 290 (affectation_is_onerosa). on_affectation itself typechecks, but Spiral instantiates the forall in a parameter annotation '(visit : \\* g. igv_affectation g -> r)' once at the definition, so the parameter is monomorphic and a polymorphic function cannot be passed: Spiral has no rank-2 function parameters. The cited 'contract_* precedent' is GADT constructors (\\* inside constructor types), which are a different thing. The live sunat.spi 330CB163 keeps its explicit three-arm matches, which are correct; the draft stays in drafts\\ for reference. Next step: none; a dedupe of those matches would need a prototype per behaviour, which buys nothing over three arms.")
inl serve_stalls_after_pin () = Task ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", "pluto /timeline still stalls after the pinned_world cutover: find the remaining cause", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "serve,pluto,sla,performance,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_serve_stalls_after_pin () = Planning ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_1 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:18Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 groom 2 (microblog), from org3's soak after the cutover: 16 samples show ~87.5% availability vs ~90% before, so the stalls are NOT reduced yet (early, but n >= 15). My own n=10 samples agree (12.5 s at +72 min). DoD: find why /timeline still stalls with the world in persistent_term, and either fix it with a gated change or record why pinned_world can't help. NEXT STEP: (1) read what the running pod IS: confirm pinned_world is active in xsim-serve-589b885d97 (the serve's /tmp/sim.log startup lines, and the beam's process memory: the request handler's heap should be small if the world is pinned); (2) code-read sim_serve.spi / timeline_serve.spi request path for whatever still copies or traverses the world per request (building the timeline list, JSON encoding the whole feed); (3) correlate stall times with node swap-in (vmstat si) to tell GC from paging. TYPEFEATURES: a stall_cause union (MajorGc | SwapIn | Socat | Unknown) per sampled stall.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_2 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:30Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 23:4x microblog STEP 1 RESULT (read-only on pluto): (a) the live beam (pod xsim-serve-589b885d97) has VmRSS 168 MB, VmSwap 565 MB, VmHWM 605 MB: the world is mostly PAGED OUT. persistent_term keeps the GC from scanning the world, but it does not keep the kernel from swapping it. (b) Correlation, 15 x /timeline at 2 s spacing alongside vmstat 1 s: the one stall (6.3 s at epoch 1794281345) coincided with swap-in of 18-28 MB/s for ~6 s (~150 MB paged in); fast requests ran at 1-5 MB/s background si. A second burst (~1378-1386) had no request of mine and is likely another client (org3's soak). So the remaining stalls are page-ins of the world, not GC; pinned_world fixed the wrong half for this host. (n=1 stall: a supported hypothesis, not proven.) (c) /tmp/sim.log is not where the serve logs; its log path is still to find. NEXT STEP: (1) confirm with the beam's major-fault counter (/proc/<pid>/stat field majflt) before and after a stall, n >= 3 stalls; (2) code-read sim_serve.spi / timeline_serve.spi: does /timeline walk the WHOLE world per request (then every request pages it all in) or only the recent slice? If whole, the lever is an index so a request touches only the page it renders; alternatives are a larger memory request (pluto has ~300 MB available, tight next to RustDesk) or shrinking the world (SERVE-WORLD-RSS).")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_3 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 3u32, "2026-11-10T03:33Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 23:5x microblog STEP 1b, ROOT CAUSE MEASURED (read-only): the beam's own major-fault counter (/proc/573475/stat field 12) around 15 x /timeline at 2 s spacing. Request 1, the first after an idle gap: 3.8 s and +19,892 major faults (~78 MB of the world paged in from swap). Requests 2-15 back to back: 0.03-0.44 s and +0..29 faults. RSS rose 168 -> 315 MB, swap fell 565 -> 424 MB. So the remaining stalls are the first request after a quiet gap paging ~80 MB of the world back in, and memory pressure on the 948 MB node pushes it out again between requests. NOT GC, which is why pinned_world left availability unchanged. Code read: each request walks the whole users list (cursor_ids via sim_serve::users_in w::raw) and merges every user's feed head (page_dir / feed_merge); from= queries fold over every feed, so a request touches records scattered across the whole world. LEVERS, cheapest first: (1) vm.swappiness. org3 raised it 10 -> 60 on 11-09 to bias away from OOM; 60 also swaps the idle world out more eagerly. A soak A/B (60 vs 10) needs no outage and is reversible, but it is org3's hardening call, so proposed to org3, not changed. (2) Cache the default page: the served world is a read-only snapshot, so /timeline with no query renders the same HTML every time; render it once into persistent_term and a default request touches tens of KB instead of ~80 MB. Needs code + verify + another restart, so it is a user decision. (3) Shrink the world (SERVE-WORLD-RSS). NEXT STEP: after org3 answers on (1), draft (2) in timeline_serve.spi with a notebook test (default page = the cached binary; any query still renders live), gated on a sim verify.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_4 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 4u32, "2026-11-10T03:43Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:0x microblog: org3 DECLINED the swappiness 60 -> 10 arm (rightly): pluto has 135 MB available and 194 MB droppable cache against 425 MB of world swapped out, so even 10 can't keep the world resident (~96 MB short) and it would remove the OOM bias on a production node. swappiness stays 60; org3 keeps the soak and a pinned pre-lever baseline. LEVER 2 DRAFTED (drafts store x/SERVE-DEFAULT-PAGE-CACHE, sim_serve.spi + timeline_serve.spi with .base copies; the bases equal the deployed sources 877325805cc0 / fe1f0b1c7dd9; drafts 52eb2699afe9 / 122e966d2646): api_world gains default_page : string (blank_world sets it to empty); timeline_reply returns the remembered page for a /timeline request with an empty query, else renders it with feeds, remembering it only for the empty query. A big binary lives off-heap, so GC never copies it, and a default request no longer walks users or feeds. Two new gleam tests: the default page is rendered once then served from the world; a query renders live and is not remembered. The page is a pure function of the read-only world (no time-relative text in labeled_html), so the cache never goes stale. GATE: sim_serve + timeline_serve + simframes/simframes notebooks on europa (/home/remote/xcache, a clean relay of the verified tree, no build caches, drafts overlaid), job label x-serve-cache-gate, nice 19; europa's admission refused it (MemAvailable 1267 MB < cap 1536 + floor 500), and a box poller retries every 5 min until admitted. NEXT STEP: after the gate is green, run the full sim verify on the drafts (they change the deployed artifact), then put the redeploy to the user with the before/after plan: org3's soak n >= 15 and the beam's major faults per default request (cold request: ~19,892 faults now, target: hundreds).")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_5 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 5u32, "2026-11-10T04:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:0x microblog: CACHE GATE GREEN, job-1794282557985-x-serve-cache-gate on europa (run cache-gate-20261110034918, drafts 52eb2699afe9 / 122e966d2646 on the deployed sources): sim_serve 9/9, timeline_serve 35/35 (incl. both new cache tests), simframes/simframes 1/1 (the whole frames package compiles with the new api_world field). The timing row (SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING) was added to the same draft after this gate, so the combined draft d48d3fdd99e5 re-gates as x-serve-cache-gate2 (poller, europa load 17 now). Next step: combined gate green -> full sim verify on the drafts -> put the redeploy to the user with the bracket (org3's soak n >= 15 + the beam's major faults per default request + the new server-side timing rows).")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_6 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 6u32, "2026-11-10T04:19Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:2x microblog: COMBINED GATE GREEN, job-1794283539239-x-serve-cache-gate2 on europa (run cache-gate-20261110040539, drafts 52eb2699afe9 / d48d3fdd99e5 = default-page cache + timing row on the deployed sources): sim_serve 9/9, timeline_serve 36/36 (incl. the 2 cache tests and the row-format test), simframes/simframes 1/1. NEXT GATE queued: the full sim verify on the drafts (verify.ps1 -Part sim, no accept, moon's 11 accepted fixtures overlaid on /home/remote/xcache), job label x-serve-cache-verify, 7 h cap, nice 19; a box poller submits it when europa admits it (load 12 now). Next step: after that verify is green, put the redeploy to the user: cost = one Recreate (~5 min measured 11-10); gain = a default request touching KBs instead of ~80 MB of swapped world; bracket = org3's soak n >= 15, the beam's major faults per default request (now ~19,900 on a cold request), and the new server-side timing rows.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_7 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 7u32, "2026-11-10T04:28Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:4x microblog: the full verify x-serve-cache-verify went RED in its cell-budget step (exit 1 in 2 min, before any build): 4 over-budget cells, all mine. api_world 294 > 272 and blank_world 281 > 272 (the new field; api_world was already at ~271), timed_timeline 326 > 271, the cache test 314 > 271. The notebook gates never run the budget check, only the full sim build does. FIXED in the drafts (now sim_serve 574f466ddb8f, timeline_serve 2ebb9e33c39c; 0 over budget by the exact awk oracle, bases clean too; 0 lines over 120): a type alias feed_lists for the feeds type, the field renamed to front, page_size = 100 (the compiler flags the i32 suffix as redundant there), logged_timing split out of timed_timeline, a shared default_get () request for the test. Rerun queued: x-serve-cache-verify2 (poller, europa). Next step: verify2 green -> put the redeploy to the user with the bracket.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_8 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 8u32, "2026-11-10T05:48Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 01:5x microblog: ALL GATES GREEN, the redeploy is a USER DECISION. Full sim verify on the drafts: job-1794284861716-x-serve-cache-verify2 (europa, run cache-verify-20261110042742) exit 0, sim build exit 0, 29/29 sim notebooks passed (incl. sim_serve and timeline_serve), against the 11 accepted fixtures with no fixture drift (the cache and the timing rows change no rendered output). Inputs: timeline_serve 2ebb9e33c39c, sim_serve 574f466ddb8f (both drafts now copied into the box x tree, unstaged, after their bases were checked equal to the live files). ARTIFACT = that verify run's own frames build: frames-erlang-1110.tgz, 8 packages, 2,758,804 B, sha b8784f0ab682cb3a (on the box scratchpad and in europa /home/remote/stage). MANIFEST xsim-serve-pluto-1110.yaml (sha 3ec4ac07abb2bef7) = the live 1109 one with frames-1110 as the only change; server dry-run clean on pluto. DECISION FOR THE USER: the apply is one Recreate (~5 min measured on 11-10). GAIN: a default /timeline request renders from the cached page instead of walking ~80 MB of swapped world (cold request today: 3.8 s and ~19,900 major faults); plus server-side timing rows in /tmp/sim.log. BRACKET: org3 soak n >= 15 against the pinned pre-lever baseline, the beam majflt per default request, and the new timing rows. ROLLBACK: the current 1109 manifest (frames-1109 kept), also ~5 min. Next step: on the user's go, stage frames-1110 on pluto (additive, sha rechecked there), org3 takes the before-baseline, microblog applies, org3 brackets.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_9 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 9u32, "2026-11-10T05:51Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "org3 11-10 01:5x: the pre-lever baseline is pinned (soak continuous, steady state ~87% availability, 21 of 161+ samples are 6 s swap-in stalls). Bracket protocol agreed: org3 compares soak stall count + availability before vs after over a steady window (first 200 after the restart, then n >= 15), reads the new in-pod /tmp/sim.log timing rows, and org interprets. Next step: on the user's go, stage frames-1110 on pluto, apply the 1110 manifest, and SEND org3 the exact cutover timestamp (apply time and first 200) so the restart transient stays out of the after-window; then read the beam major faults per default request.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_10 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 10u32, "2026-11-10T08:28Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:2x (08:27Z) pluto watch: pod xsim-serve-589b885d97-tdrt6 2/2 Running, 0 restarts, 6h26m. A COLD /timeline took 19.35 s (HTTP 200) and the next one 0.054 s; node swap used 1,270 MB of 4,447, RAM free 75 MB, available 279 MB. That is 5x the 3.8 s cold stall measured earlier and just under a 20 s client timeout, so the idle swap-out is getting worse as the soak ages. The default-page cache (frames-1110, sha b8784f0ab682cb3a, verify 29/29) is the fix ready to ship; it waits on the user go (wait user:pluto-cache-redeploy-go). Read-only check; nothing was changed on pluto.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_11 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 11u32, "2026-11-10T09:06Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:0x (09:05Z) pluto watch: pod 2/2 Running, 0 restarts, 7h03m. /timeline 10.92 s then 5.67 s back to back (both HTTP 200); swap used 1,300 MB (was 1,270 at 08:27Z). NEW SHAPE: at 08:27Z the repeat request was 0.054 s; now the repeat is slow too, so the beams pages are evicted between consecutive requests, not only after idle. The default-page cache keeps each request to one stored string instead of a render over the world, which cuts the pages a request must fault in; it is ready (frames-1110 b8784f0ab682cb3a, verify 29/29) and waits on the user go. Read-only; nothing changed on pluto.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_12 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 12u32, "2026-11-10T09:39Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:4x GROOM: lint ProseWait fixed by this note; the structured wait row stays user:pluto-cache-redeploy-go. org3 brackets the cutover with its soak baseline.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_13 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 13u32, "2026-11-10T09:46Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:4x (09:43Z and 09:45Z) pluto: pod 2/2, 0 restarts, 7h43m. 09:43Z: 10.68 s then 0.086 s. 09:45Z, only 2 MIN LATER: 11.56 s then 2.03 s. So a warm page is evicted again within about 2 minutes: the stall is not only idle-driven (it was the reading of the 08:27Z and 09:17Z pairs). Memory pressure on pluto is now continuous, so request rate alone will not keep the page resident. The cache lever still applies (one stored string per default request instead of a render over the world, so far fewer pages to fault in), and its value grows with this. Read-only.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_14 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 14u32, "2026-11-10T11:37Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:3xZ: user 06:5x pre-authorized the pluto cache redeploy (\"stop asking me for decisions ... until our font is finished and live on pluto with all the pending items around it\"). The default-page cache now ships with the timeline CSS as frames-1111 (sim_serve 574f466ddb8f, timeline_serve 2ebb9e33c39c, timeline_page 3b703fc082d2), building on ganymede (job-1794309940701-x-pluto-build-1111g2). NEXT STEP: stage frames-1111 on pluto, apply xsim-serve-pluto-1111.yaml, org3 brackets it, read the timing rows and the cold /timeline stall after.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_15 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 15u32, "2026-11-10T11:56Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:5xZ CACHE LIVE (frames-1111, applied 11:41:34Z): the default /timeline answers in 2-5 ms from the stored page (3 back-to-back: 4.5, 2.0, 2.3 ms; first hit after start 3.7 ms), against 10-19 s cold stalls this morning. Query pages still render the world: ?d=up 13.5 s (timing row \"timeline rendered 13514\"). NEXT STEP: org3 soak samples across idle windows decide whether the default stall is gone (n >= 15 per org3s rule); the query path is a separate lever (cache the first page per direction, or a lighter world), to file if the soak shows users hit it.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_16 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 16u32, "2026-11-10T14:50Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~14:4xZ: AFTER-BRACKET CLOSED -> RESOLVED, attributed to SERVE-DEFAULT-PAGE-CACHE (cutover 11:41:34Z). Evidence (org3 soak): TWO independent clean 30-sample windows post-cutover -- W1 11:55-12:36Z and W2 13:46:45-14:39:35Z (W2 measured entirely after the frames-1112 pod-recreate recovery, so no deploy-downtime contamination) -- both 30/30 serve OK, 0 stalls (0 codes 000, 0 responses >6s), mean latency 0.26/0.31s, slowest 1.85/1.50s. Versus the pinned-world baseline ~83-87% avail / 2-5 stalls per 30. The ~2h span includes a pod Recreate (1112) whose downtime org3 excluded; the only coincident serve-path change bracketed is the default-page-cache lever (font swaps in-window are static-asset, not serve-path). CAVEAT ON RECORD: observational inference-to-best-explanation, not a controlled rollback A/B -- but a clean 83-87%->100% before/after with the cache as the sole serve-path change is strong enough to close. Soak wound to 180s normal cadence; stall_count_30 gauge stays live as the regression tripwire. No rollback signal.")
inl note_of_serve_stalls_after_pin_17 () = Note ("SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN", 17u32, "2026-11-11T01:34Z", "microblog", "11-10 21:34 local data point: one /timeline took 4.9 s (pod up 11 h, no restarts), and three immediate repeats took 2-4 ms. Pluto memory is tight: 948 MB total, 69 MB free, about 225 MB available; load 0.4. A single slow first request after idle is consistent with the earlier stall pattern (GC or page-in under memory pressure). Next probe: log the serve's own per-request ms and the beam RSS around a stall.")
inl font_complex_scripts () = Task ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", "Arabic and Devanagari complex-script support for the Spiral grotesque font, seamless with the typefeatureset", Story, P1, D4, 90u32, Active, "", "team:org,font,spiral,typefeatureset,lib", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_font_complex_scripts () = Planning ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_1 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:45Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-09 night org-f33af161: tracks the complex-script font work the user directed (Arabic, then Hindi/Devanagari), seamless with the typefeatureset. STATE: Arabic typed joining-class GADT done (ar_initial/ar_medial are dual-joining only, so a contextual form a right-joining letter lacks is a COMPILE error) with lib gate 124/124. Devanagari typed category GADT done (DevaCons/DevaVow/DevaMatra; deva_base takes deva cons_c so a matra can never be a syllable base = compile error; matra carries MPre/MPost/MAbove/MBelow) with emitter at 265 glyphs render-verified (ka shows the shirorekha headline) and the lib-gate 125-count re-running on ganymede after two europa OOM inconclusives. Phase 1 (isolated/base forms + typed models) done for both scripts. Trap hit+fixed: a constructor named Cons clashes with the prelude list cons (see memory spiral-constructor-name-clash). Memories: spiral-font-arabic-marathon, spiral-font-devanagari-marathon. All unstaged; off-box builds (europa/ganymede run-build.sh + lib build.ps1). Next step: confirm the Devanagari lib-gate 125-count, then add the next Devanagari base consonants and start the Arabic Phase-2 GSUB joining scratch prototype (rustybuzz shaping-verify first).")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_2 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T03:55Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-09 night org-f33af161 PROGRESS: Devanagari Phase-1 base set extended off-box on europa (emitter builds green). Consonants now ka ma na ta ra la sa pa va da ya ha (12), plus independent vowel a and matras aa/i, all cmapped via deva_glyph and render-verified with the shirorekha headline (na: headline+left-vertical+bottom-cup+right-stem; ra: central stem+left arm; pa: open-top box; va: ellipse loop). Emitter reached 270 glyphs on the first 5; the pa/va/da/ya/ha batch is building to 275. Glyph skeletons are crude rect+arch_down+ellipse placeholders, structurally plausible but not final forms. The typed category model (deva c GADT, matra-cannot-be-base invariant) is unchanged and compiles in every emitter build. STILL PENDING: the lib-gate 125-count (confirms the devanagari_category_is_typed ///> cell executes) OOM-inconclusive twice on memory-tight europa and lost on ganymede at load 32 - waiting for a node under load 4 with >1.8GB free; the heartbeat retries it. Next step: confirm the 275-glyph build + 125-count, then the Arabic Phase-2 GSUB joining scratch prototype (rustybuzz shaping-verify first).")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_3 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:04Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-09 ~23:58 local org-f33af161: NODE-GATED. 275-glyph emitter build GREEN (12 Devanagari consonants ka ma na ta ra la sa pa va da ya ha + vowel a + matras aa/i; FONT-EMIT-OK, render.txt 7700 lines). Remaining steps all need a node under load 4, but all three Linux nodes are saturated by the window lanes (europa load ~20, ganymede ~32, moon unreachable); stacking is counterproductive. Local Phase-2 groundwork done: drafted the Arabic rustybuzz shaping harness (Cargo.toml + src/main.rs under the session job tmp arabic-shape/) that shapes beh+beh / beh+teh / alef+beh / 3x beh and prints the gids - with no GSUB it confirms the isolated baseline, and it becomes the Phase-2 pass/fail verifier once init/medi/fina + a GSUB arab table exist. Setting a when-wait; the 10-min heartbeat retries. Next step when a node is under load 4: run the lib-gate 125-count, scp+cargo build the rustybuzz harness against sans.ttf (rustybuzz not cached - cargo fetches), then build the GSUB SingleSubst init/medi/fina for beh/teh.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_4 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:11Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~00:10 local org-f33af161: Phase-2 shaping harness STAGED on europa at /home/remote/git/arabic-shape/ (Cargo.toml, src/main.rs, sans.ttf copied from apps/font-emit). When europa (or any node) is under load 4: cd there, cargo build --release (cargo fetches rustybuzz, not cached), ./target/release/arabic-shape sans.ttf -> prints the shaped gids for beh/beh+beh/beh+teh/alef+beh. Expect all gids = isolated bases (no GSUB yet) = the Phase-2 baseline. Then the GSUB SingleSubst (isol->init/medi/fina) work. ALSO still node-gated: the lib-gate 125-count for the devanagari_category_is_typed cell. Heartbeat aa4e365b retries both. Fleet node state at wait-time: europa ~20, ganymede ~32, moon down - all 7 window lanes competing.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_5 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T04:16Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~00:18 local org-f33af161: Devanagari set extended (local edits, verify next build): added independent vowels aa i u (DevaVow) and e/o matras (DevaMatra, MAbove/MPost) via the typed model. Hindi base now 12 consonants + 4 independent vowels (a aa i u) + 4 matras (aa i e o) = 20 Devanagari glyphs; emitter will reach ~280 when built. Pending verifications (node-gated, nodes easing): (1) lib-gate 125-count running on ganymede job b28lblz06 (ganymede eased to load 4); (2) emitter build of the new vowels/matras - do it on ganymede right after b28lblz06 frees it, or europa when it drops under 4. Next after those: the Arabic Phase-2 shaping harness (staged at europa:/home/remote/git/arabic-shape/) then the GSUB joining. Heartbeat aa4e365b armed.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_6 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T04:18Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~00:20 local org-f33af161: lib-gate 125-count DEFERRED, not failed. Three attempts produced empty output (no spiral-tests total line) - europa OOM (avail <1.9GB), then ganymede twice starved (load spiked 4->35 mid-run as window lanes piled on). This is node starvation during the window peak, treated as INCONCLUSIVE per failed-measurement discipline, never a pass OR a fail. The emitter build (lighter) compiles font_glyph.spi including the deva GADT + renders every glyph, so the typed model is sound; the 125-count just confirms the ///> cell executes. Setting a when-wait; heartbeat retries when the lanes ease (their first heavy runs started ~23:25 local). Node-gated queue for the next genuinely-free window: (1) lib-gate 125-count, (2) emitter build of the new vowels/matras (~280 glyphs), (3) cargo build the arabic-shape harness. Do NOT stack on a node above load 4.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_7 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T04:23Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~00:25 local org-f33af161: Arabic Phase-2 GSUB builder DRAFTED + staged. europa:/home/remote/git/arabic-shape/ now has src/gsub.rs (build_arabic_gsub: SingleSubBuilder isol->init, wrapped Lookup -> SubstitutionLookupList, Feature init, LangSys, Script arab, ScriptList, Gsub::new; roundtrip_check serializes via dump_table and reparses with read-fonts to self-check the API) + main.rs calling it, Cargo.toml adds write-fonts 0.55 + read-fonts 0.37. API signatures are best-effort from research and will need iteration on first compile (expected). Node-independent work for this item is now EXHAUSTED: typed models done (Arabic joining-class + Devanagari category GADTs), 3 Arabic + 20 Devanagari glyphs added, shaping harness + GSUB builder drafted+staged. Everything remaining is node-gated and the fleet is saturated (all nodes spiking to load 20-35). Heartbeat aa4e365b retries this queue when a node is genuinely under load 4: lib-gate 125-count, emitter build (~280 glyphs, new vowels/matras), cargo build the arabic-shape crate (fix write-fonts API + rustybuzz), then port the GSUB into the emitter finish() FFI with the contextual forms as real gids.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_8 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T04:49Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~00:50 local org-f33af161: ROOT CAUSE of the 4 lib-gate \"failures\" = MY OWN ORPHANS, not the model. Each off-box lib-gate run as a bare ssh (ssh europa/ganymede ... pwsh build.ps1) orphaned a beam+pwsh orchestrator + a detached Cells CompilerDaemon beam + dotnet compilers when the ssh timed out / the bg task returned; they kept gating for 20-30 min, starving the node (org2 traced the ganymede one; I found the europa twin). REAPED both: ganymede pwsh 2367659 + beam 2367681; europa pwsh 717231 + beam 717318 + daemon 717673 + dotnet 723188/723202. Killed only my own pids (alphabet/lib/font --path, long etime); left org2/tibia/compiler gates alone. LESSON (memory windows-ssh-orphans-remote-children updated): the off-box lib-gate MUST run as a kit job (managed teardown), never a bare ssh. EMITTER build is unaffected (it is a cargo build + one emit, no Cells daemon) and is 4x green: 284 glyphs now = 16 Devanagari consonants (ka ma na ta ra la sa pa va da ya ha ga ja ba cha) + 4 independent vowels (a aa i u) + 4 matras (aa i e o) + 3 Arabic, all render-verified with the shirorekha. So the typed model + all glyphs compile and render. REMAINING node-gated (run as KIT JOBS when a slot + a node under load 4 are free; heartbeat drives): lib-gate 125-count (confirms the ///> test cell executes - low risk since it compiles), arabic-shape crate build (de-risk the write-fonts GSUB API), then the GSUB port into the emitter finish() FFI.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_9 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 9u32, "2026-11-10T04:56Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~01:05 local org-f33af161: added 6 more consonants (kha gha tha dha pha bha) -> 22 Devanagari consonants (near-complete base), 30 Devanagari glyphs total (+ 3 Arabic), font ~290 when built. These 6 are UNVERIFIED: fleet still saturated (ganymede load 12, europa 22 / 661MB free - no node under load 4), so no emitter build can run without stacking. Stopping glyph additions here: 22 consonants + 4 vowels (a aa i u) + 4 matras (aa i e o) is a usable Hindi base, and further value is in VERIFICATION + Phase-2 shaping, both node-gated. NODE-GATED QUEUE (heartbeat drives as the fleet eases; run the lib-gate as a KIT JOB not bare ssh): (1) emitter build to verify the last 6 consonants -> ~290 glyphs, (2) lib-gate 125-count, (3) arabic-shape crate build (GSUB API de-risk), (4) GSUB port into the emitter. All glyphs unstaged; emitter builds are 4x green through 284 glyphs; the typed Arabic+Devanagari GADT models are proven to compile and render.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_10 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 10u32, "2026-11-10T05:06Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~01:15 local org-f33af161: added the Devanagari CONJUNCT typed model (Phase-2 typefeatureset scaffolding, not churn). deva_cluster GADT: Base :: deva cons_c -> deva_cluster | Join :: {head : deva cons_c; tail : deva_cluster} -> deva_cluster, with cluster_len (:~ ^ recursive). INVARIANT: only consonants (deva cons_c) can be in a cluster, so a conjunct containing a matra or independent vowel is a COMPILE error - the correct-by-construction form of Devanagari's C+virama+C conjunct rule, mirroring the Arabic joining-class model. Test devanagari_conjunct_is_typed builds ka+sa (len 2) and ka+ta+sa (len 3). UNVERIFIED yet: the running lib-gate kit job (job-1794286724377-font-lib-gate-125, bg wait b9c0150nf) is on source from just before this, so it confirms the 125-count (category + joining tests); the conjunct test (-> 126) + the last 6 consonants need the NEXT gate/emitter build. Phase-2 now has: typed joining (Arabic) + typed conjunct+category (Devanagari) + the GSUB builder + rustybuzz harness staged. Next: GSUB generation driven by these typed clusters/forms.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_11 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 11u32, "2026-11-10T05:09Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~01:22 local org-f33af161: TYPED MODEL MILESTONE - the Devanagari typefeatureset scaffold is complete: category (deva: DevaCons/DevaVow/DevaMatra, matra-cant-be-base) -> cluster (deva_cluster: Base/Join, consonants-only conjuncts) -> syllable (deva_syllable: Inherent/WithMatra, a matra attaches only to a consonant cluster, never a bare vowel or alone). With the Arabic joining-class GADT (initial/medial dual-only) that is 4 correct-by-construction illegal-states-unrepresentable models answering the users \"seamless with the typefeatureset\". UNVERIFIED (next lib-gate on latest source -> count 127 = 123 + arabic_joining + devanagari_category + devanagari_conjunct + devanagari_akshara): the conjunct + akshara test cells + the last 6 consonants. The running kit job (job-1794286724377-font-lib-gate-125, bg wait b9c0150nf) is on source from before the conjunct/akshara adds, so it confirms the 125 baseline; a fresh gate verifies 127 after. REMAINING (node-gated, kit jobs via heartbeat): verify 127 + emitter build (~290 glyphs), then Phase-2 GSUB generation DRIVEN BY these typed clusters/forms (Arabic init/medi/fina from the joining class; Devanagari conjunct/reorder from deva_cluster + matra_pos), rustybuzz shaping-verify, then port into the emitter finish() FFI.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_12 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 12u32, "2026-11-10T05:16Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~01:30 local org-f33af161: FIRST real lib-gate result (kit job, no orphan) + a REAL BUG CAUGHT. job-...-125: discovered 125, passed 124, FAILED 1. The failure was devanagari_category_is_typed: two inline `?= matra_position x ?| | MPost => true | _ => false` matches placed directly as tuple elements did NOT group (ETY-TermError Got: bool Expected: bool * bool) - the match arms swallowed the tuple commas. The 4x-green EMITTER builds never caught it (they do not run ///> test cells), so the lib gate earns its place. FIX: bind each match to a local (:= aa_post = ?= ... ; := iv_pre = ?= ...) before the tuple - the Spiral idiom for complex tuple elements. The Arabic model is CONFIRMED (the 124 passed include arabic_joining_forms_are_typed). Resubmitted the gate on the fixed+complete source: job-1794287691906-font-lib-gate-127 on ganymede (bg wait b84hhw5ar) - expect 127 (123 + arabic_joining + devanagari_category[fixed] + devanagari_conjunct + devanagari_akshara). Also added 4 matras (u uu ai au, exercising MBelow) -> 8 matras total, 34 Devanagari glyphs, font ~294 (glyph verify via the next emitter build when a node frees - europa 449MB now). LESSON worth memory: never place a bare `?=`-match as a tuple element; bind it first.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_13 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 13u32, "2026-11-10T05:21Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~01:45 local org-f33af161 (heartbeat depth step): added the Devanagari PRE-BASE MATRA REORDERING - the hard Indic shaping concept, typed. syllable_visual_order (s : deva_syllable) -> list (outline quadratic): for a WithMatra syllable it dispatches on matra_position of the sign - MPre (i-matra) is consed to the FRONT (rendered left of the consonant, the pre-base reorder), every other position appends after. Helpers: cluster_glyphs (deva_cluster -> glyph list, recursive) + outl_append (safe recursive list append). Test devanagari_reorder_prebase_matra asserts ki (ka + i-matra, MPre) has the i-matra glyph FIRST while ka+aa-matra (MPost) has ka first - proving the reorder. Applied the tuple-match lesson (bound the ?= matches to locals ki_first/kaaa_first, not inline). This is the typed logic a GSUB/reorder pass will drive. UNVERIFIED (node-gated, fleet saturated: europa 650MB, ganymede running the 127-gate). Verifies in the next gate -> 128 (adds devanagari_reorder_prebase_matra). The running job-...-127 (bg wait b84hhw5ar) is on source before this; it confirms the core 127; a follow-up gate covers the reorder.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_14 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 14u32, "2026-11-10T05:37Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~02:05 local org-f33af161: 2nd real bug caught by the gate. job-...-127 went ALL 127 red from one root cause: :| deva_cluster with Join tail : deva_cluster is a self-referential (recursive) union, which :| forbids (ETY-IncorrectRecursiveNominal), cascading UnboundVariable/CasePatternNotFound across every def+test in font_glyph (so the whole module + all 5 files red). Again the emitter build could not catch it (deva_cluster is reached only from test cells). FIX: made deva_cluster NON-recursive - a record { lead : deva cons_c; more : list (deva cons_c) } with a :~ ^ recursive FUNCTION over the list (recursive functions are fine; only recursive TYPES under :| fail; genuine recursive ADTs need `union rec`). Updated the conjunct + akshara tests to record literals. REMOVED the reorder block (cluster_glyphs/syllable_visual_order/reorder test) to get back to green first; will re-add it verified. Resubmitted: job-1794288640592-font-lib-gate-126 on ganymede (load eased to 7), bg wait bn8twe8u8, expect 126 (123 + arabic + category + conjunct + akshara). Saved the trap to memory spiral-recursive-union-needs-union-rec. Released the NODEBENCH-SPIRAL-REWRITE cross-team claim (kit repo too large to search efficiently; font is the priority). Glyph emitter build (verify the 16 newest glyphs -> ~294) deferred, nodes loaded.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_15 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 15u32, "2026-11-10T05:49Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~02:20 local org-f33af161 (heartbeat): GLYPHS VERIFIED to 294 (emitter build on europa, FONT-EMIT-OK, render.txt 8232 lines = 294 glyphs). All 22 Devanagari consonants + 4 independent vowels + 8 matras + 3 Arabic forms compile and render; font_glyph.spi compiles at the emitter-reachable level (the deva GADT, deva_glyph, every glyph function). PENDING: the 126-gate on ganymede (models: record-based conjunct/syllable fix) is near its 20-min timeout on the loaded node - if it times out that is INCONCLUSIVE, re-run on now-free europa. DEPTH STEP: launched the arabic-shape crate build on europa (be8cej500) to de-risk the write-fonts 0.55 GSUB API (my gsub.rs was drafted blind) + the rustybuzz harness - the Phase-2 critical path. Next: fix the GSUB API from the compiler errors, then the shaping-verify (shape beh+beh, confirm init+fina gids), then port GSUB into the emitter finish() FFI.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_16 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 16u32, "2026-11-10T05:56Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~02:30 local org-f33af161: GSUB de-risk build (arabic-shape crate, europa) compiled rustybuzz + write-fonts + read-fonts but surfaced 3 real API mismatches in my blind gsub.rs - the de-risk working as intended. CORRECTED write-fonts 0.55 API (from the source at /root/.cargo/registry/.../write-fonts-0.55.0): (1) SingleSubBuilder implements Builder; .build takes `&mut VariationStoreBuilder` and returns a Vec of subtables - not nullary (my call had no arg). (2) SubstitutionLookupList = LookupList<SubstitutionLookup> (type alias); lookups assemble via LookupBuilder<T> in tables/layout/builders.rs, not raw ::new everywhere - one of my ::new calls had wrong arity. (3) Reading back: use read_fonts FontRead::read(FontData), NOT Gsub::read (no such assoc fn on the write TableRef). DECISION: the full GSUB build is a focused write-fonts task (the builder flow with VariationStoreBuilder) - DEFER to a dedicated session; it is Phase-2, non-urgent (user said Arabic shaping is later). The de-risk value is captured: the real API path is now known. Meanwhile the 126-gate (record-based conjunct/syllable models fix) is re-running on FREE europa (job-1794289994067-font-lib-gate-126e, bg wait b05xuvc88) after the ganymede one was stopped past timeout (kit reaped its tree cleanly, exit 143 - no orphan, confirming the kit-job fix). Glyphs already verified to 294.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_17 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 17u32, "2026-11-10T06:00Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~02:35 local org-f33af161: GREEN MILESTONE - lib gate 127/127 PASSED (FONT-LIB-OK) on free europa (job-...-126e, discovered 127 executed 127 failed 0 passed 127). The record-based deva_cluster fix resolved the recursive-nominal bug. So the complete \"seamless with the typefeatureset\" deliverable the user asked for is now VERIFIED: 4 illegal-states-unrepresentable models - Arabic joining-class (initial/medial dual-only), Devanagari category (matra-cant-be-base), conjunct (consonants-only clusters), syllable/akshara (matra attaches only to a cluster) - all green, over 294 render-verified glyphs (22 Devanagari consonants + 4 vowels + 8 matras + 3 Arabic). Both verification layers green: emitter build 294 glyphs + lib gate 127/127. Everything unstaged. REMAINING: (1) re-add the pre-base matra reordering (record-based, on this green base, verified) - next depth step; (2) Phase-2 GSUB generation (deferred, deep write-fonts builder API task, non-urgent); (3) glyph-shape refinement + remaining consonants (later). Progress 55%.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_18 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 18u32, "2026-11-10T06:10Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~02:50 local org-f33af161 (heartbeat): FULL TYPED MODEL VERIFIED - lib gate 128/128 PASSED (FONT-LIB-OK, europa). The record-based pre-base matra reordering (syllable_visual_order: MPre matra consed to the visual front, others appended; via cons_glyphs + outl_append over the cluster list) passes - so the hardest Indic shaping concept is now typed correct-by-construction AND verified. All 5 models green: arabic_joining + devanagari_category + devanagari_conjunct + devanagari_akshara + devanagari_reorder_prebase_matra. This completes the users \"seamless with the typefeatureset\" deliverable at the type level. DEPTH STEP: added the Devanagari retroflex row (Ta ttha dda ddha nna = U+091F-0923) - emitter build running on europa (ber6rdl7f) to verify -> ~299 glyphs, 27 Devanagari consonants. Progress 60%. Remaining: finish the consonant set (~6 more: nga nya chha jha sha Sha), the Phase-2 GSUB shaping (deferred, deep write-fonts builder task), glyph-shape refinement. Both layers green: lib gate 128/128 + emitter build (294, retroflexes verifying). All unstaged, off-box.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_19 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 19u32, "2026-11-10T06:16Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~03:05 local org-f33af161 (heartbeat): HINDI ALPHABET COMPREHENSIVELY COMPLETE. Complete 33-consonant Devanagari alphabet verified (emitter build 305, FONT-EMIT-OK) - all rows: ka-varga (ka kha ga gha nga), cha-varga (cha chha ja jha nya), Ta-varga retroflex (Ta Tha Da Dha Na), ta-varga (ta tha da dha na), pa-varga (pa pha ba bha ma), ya ra la va, sha Sha sa ha. Added the 4 common independent vowels (e ai o au) -> 8 vowels (a aa i u e ai o au), building (bxf3nw4xo -> 309). So Hindi now has: 33 consonants + 8 vowels + 8 matras (aa i e o u uu ai au) = 49 Devanagari glyphs, over the verified typed model (128/128: category + conjunct + syllable + reorder). Plus Arabic (3 forms + joining model). All glyph shapes are crude rect+arch_down+ellipse placeholders - structurally plausible, to refine. Progress 65%. REMAINING: Phase-2 GSUB shaping (deferred, deep write-fonts builder task - the real payoff for rendered words), glyph-shape refinement, the long vowels ii/uu/ri (minor). Both layers green: lib gate 128/128 + emitter build 305 (309 building). Unstaged, off-box.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_20 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 20u32, "2026-11-10T06:20Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~03:15 local org-f33af161 (heartbeat): 309 glyphs verified (emitter build, FONT-EMIT-OK, 8652 lines). The 4 common vowels (e ai o au) render. SO THE USER DELIVERABLE IS COMPREHENSIVELY COMPLETE + VERIFIED: Arabic (3 forms + typed joining-class model) + Hindi/Devanagari (complete 33-consonant alphabet + 8 independent vowels + 8 matras + the typed category/conjunct/syllable/reorder models), all 5 typefeatureset models green (lib gate 128/128) over 309 render-verified glyphs (emitter build). Glyph shapes are crude rect/arch_down/ellipse placeholders (known Phase-1 limitation, refine later). GSUB (Phase-2 shaping - makes rendered WORDS actually join/reorder) is DEFERRED: the write-fonts 0.55 builder API is deep (SingleSubBuilder.build needs &mut VariationStoreBuilder; LangSys::new fewer args than I guessed; read via FontRead not Gsub::read) and blind source-greps keep failing on the crate structure - it needs a docs-based focused session (docs.rs/write-fonts), which fits the user noting shaping is \"later\". The de-risk value is captured (3 API mismatches found + the real path). REMAINING: GSUB (focused/deferred), glyph-shape refinement, the long vowels ii/uu/ri + more matra positions (minor polish). Progress ~65%. Unstaged, off-box, both verification layers green.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_21 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 21u32, "2026-11-10T06:26Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~03:30 local org-f33af161: GSUB DE-RISK DONE (not deferred after all - cracked it). The arabic-shape crate COMPILES + RUNS on europa. (1) rustybuzz harness works + confirms the no-GSUB baseline: beh+beh -> [258,258] both isolated (no joining), beh+teh -> [259,258], alef+beh -> [258,257] RTL - every gid is the cmap base, no contextual forms yet. (2) write-fonts 0.55 GSUB builder assembles + serializes a valid 68-byte GSUB (arab / init feature / SingleSubst 258->300). PROVEN API (the 3 blind-draft errors fixed): use write_fonts::tables::layout::builders::Builder (trait must be in scope for .build); vs = VariationStoreBuilder::new(0) from tables::variations::ivs_builder; SingleSubBuilder::default().insert(GlyphId16,GlyphId16); subtables = single.build(&mut vs); Lookup::new(LookupFlag::empty(), subtables); SubstitutionLookupList::new(vec![lookup.into()]); Feature::new(None, vec![0]); FeatureList::new(vec![FeatureRecord::new(Tag::new(b init), feature)]); LangSys::new(vec![0]) (ONE arg, no required-feature); Script::new(Some(langsys), vec![]); ScriptList::new(vec![ScriptRecord::new(Tag::new(b arab), script)]); Gsub::new(scripts, features, lookups); dump_table(&gsub). Crate at europa:/home/remote/git/arabic-shape. REMAINING Phase-2 integration (now unblocked): emit the Arabic init/medi/fina contextual forms as glyphs (gids) in the emitter, build the init/medi/fina GSUB in finish() FFI referencing those gids, rustybuzz-verify beh+beh -> [beh.init, beh.fina]. Alphabet also 100% complete: 312 glyphs (33 consonants + 11 vowels + 8 matras + Arabic), lib gate 128/128. Progress 70%.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_22 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 22u32, "2026-11-10T06:39Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~03:45 local org-f33af161: ARABIC CURSIVE JOINING WORKS END-TO-END (Phase 2 DONE for beh/teh). The emitter finish() FFI now builds a GSUB (init/medi/fina features, arab script) that rustybuzz applies on the Spiral-generated sans.ttf. VERIFIED (rustybuzz, RTL visual order): beh+beh -> [260,261] = [beh.fina, beh.init] (joined! not [258,258]); 3x beh -> [260,262,261] = [beh.fina, beh.medi, beh.init] (initial-medial-final in RTL order); beh+teh -> [263,261] = [teh.fina, beh.init]; alef+beh -> [258,257] = [beh.isol, alef.isol] (alef right-joining correctly does NOT join the following). HOW: (1) emitted the 6 Arabic contextual forms (beh/teh init/medi/fina) as glyphs cmapped to Arabic Presentation Forms-B U+FE90-FE98 (via ar_initial/ar_medial/ar_final typed accessors - dual-only, so this is type-safe); (2) ported the proven write-fonts GSUB builder into finish() FFI with no-string-literal Tags ([105,110,105,116]=init etc.) + .to_vec() not vec! + VariationStoreBuilder::new(0); fg() looks up gids from the cmap vec by codepoint; b.add_table(&gsub). FONT-EMIT-OK, font builds. So the full pipeline works: typed joining model -> contextual-form glyphs -> GSUB -> rustybuzz joining. The user deferred shaping to \"later\" - it is now DONE for the first letters. Progress 80%. NEXT: extend to all dual-joining letters (design their init/medi/fina forms), then Devanagari GSUB (conjuncts + the matra reorder, using syllable_visual_order). Everything unstaged, off-box.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_23 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 23u32, "2026-11-10T06:42Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~03:55 local org-f33af161: DEVANAGARI MATRA REORDERING WORKS (automatically, via rustybuzz/HarfBuzz Indic machine - no custom reorder GSUB needed). Verified: ka+i-matra (U+0915 U+093F) -> [270, 266] = [i-matra, ka] - the i-matra (typed AFTER) renders BEFORE ka, the pre-base reorder; ka+aa-matra (U+093E) -> [266, 269] = [ka, aa-matra] post-base stays after; ma+i-matra -> [270, 267] reordered. KEY INSIGHT: HarfBuzz handles the pre-base matra reorder from Unicode properties given just the glyphs + cmap + script=DEVANAGARI; my typed syllable_visual_order (MPre -> front) models the SAME behavior, confirming it matches the shaper. SO BOTH SCRIPTS NOW SHAPE: Arabic cursive joining (my emitter-built init/medi/fina GSUB) + Devanagari matra reordering (HarfBuzz automatic). Progress 82%. REMAINING Devanagari shaping: CONJUNCTS (ka+virama+sha -> ligature) need a cjct GSUB (half-forms) - the Indic machine applies the font cjct feature; that is the next Devanagari GSUB piece, built the same way as the Arabic init/medi/fina (proven path). Plus extending Arabic joining to more letters (design their forms). Harness at europa:/home/remote/git/arabic-shape (now tests both scripts). Everything unstaged, off-box.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_24 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 24u32, "2026-11-10T06:49Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~04:05 local org-f33af161: added the virama glyph (U+094D, halant, advance 0) -> 319 glyphs; cluster shaping confirmed at BASELINE: ka+virama+sha -> [266,318,309]=[ka,virama,sha] and ka+virama+ta -> [266,318,272]=[ka,virama,ta] - readable with an explicit virama, no conjunct ligature yet (expected, no cjct GSUB). SO THE COMPREHENSIVE SHAPING STATE: Arabic cursive joining WORKS (emitter GSUB), Devanagari matra reordering WORKS (HarfBuzz auto), Devanagari conjuncts render at baseline (explicit virama). NEXT for full conjuncts: design a conjunct glyph (e.g. ksha) + build a LigatureSubst GSUB (akhn/cjct feature: [ka,virama,sha]->ksha) in the emitter finish() - extends the proven SingleSubst path via SingleSubBuilder.promote_to_ligature_sub()/LigatureSubBuilder; may also need GDEF glyph classes (mark=virama). That is the remaining Devanagari-shaping piece; plus init/medi/fina forms for the rest of the Arabic alphabet (only alef/beh/teh designed). Harness (europa:/home/remote/git/arabic-shape) now tests Arabic joining + Devanagari reorder + conjunct clusters. 319 glyphs, lib gate 128/128, both layers green, unstaged, off-box. Progress 82%.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_25 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 25u32, "2026-11-10T06:51Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~04:10 local org-f33af161: LigatureSubst API found for conjuncts (ready to implement). LigatureSubBuilder::default() (or SingleSubBuilder::promote_to_ligature_sub()); .insert(target: Vec<GlyphId16>, replacement: GlyphId16) maps a component sequence -> a ligature glyph; builds via the Builder trait (.build(&mut vs)) like SingleSubst. CONJUNCT PLAN: (1) design a conjunct glyph (ksha); (2) emit it cmapped to a PUA codepoint (U+E000) so it gets a gid (conjuncts have no Unicode codepoint); (3) in the emitter finish() GSUB, add a dev2/deva ScriptRecord with a cjct FeatureRecord -> a LigatureSubst lookup inserting [ka_gid, virama_gid, sha_gid]->ksha_gid (gids via the fg() cmap lookup; .to_vec() not vec!); (4) test ka+virama+sha -> [ksha]. RISK: HarfBuzz Indic cjct may need GDEF glyph classes (virama=mark) to apply - if the simple cjct does not fire, add a minimal GDEF. This is the remaining Devanagari-shaping gap; the Arabic alphabet extension (init/medi/fina for the other 25 letters) is the other remaining piece. COMPREHENSIVE STATE unchanged: both scripts shape the core cases (Arabic joining + Devanagari reorder), 319 glyphs, lib gate 128/128. Pacing the conjunct + Arabic extension via heartbeats.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_26 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 26u32, "2026-11-10T06:58Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~04:25 local org-f33af161: DEVANAGARI CONJUNCT LIGATURE WORKS - ALL THREE SHAPING BEHAVIORS NOW LIVE. ka+virama+sha (U+0915 U+094D U+0936) -> [319] = a SINGLE glyph (the ksha conjunct)! The cjct LigatureSubst GSUB ([ka,virama,sha]->ksha, under a dev2 Devanagari script) + HarfBuzz Indic machine ligated the cluster. No GDEF needed. ka+virama+ta -> [266,318,272] stays unligated (only ksha built - correct). HOW: designed the ksha glyph (cmapped to PUA U+E000 for a gid), added a LigatureSubBuilder lookup via .insert([ka,virama,sha gids], ksha gid) + a cjct FeatureRecord + a dev2 ScriptRecord to the emitter finish() GSUB (now 4 lookups: 3 SingleSubst init/medi/fina + 1 LigatureSubst cjct; 2 scripts arab + dev2). (Fixed a paren bug: a plain-outline glyph ends ]) not ]) ) - only DevaCons-wrapped ones have the extra paren.) SO THE SPIRAL-GENERATED FONT NOW DOES: Arabic cursive joining (init/medi/fina) + Devanagari matra reordering (i-matra pre-base) + Devanagari conjunct ligatures (ksha) - all verified with rustybuzz. 320 glyphs, lib gate 128/128. The shaping the user deferred to \"later\" is comprehensively demonstrated for all 3 behaviors. EXTENSIBLE: more conjuncts = +glyph +ligature insert; more Arabic letters = +forms +SingleSubst. Progress 88%. Unstaged, off-box.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_27 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 27u32, "2026-11-10T07:04Z", "org-f33af161", "2026-11-10 ~04:35 local org-f33af161: conjunct pattern SCALES - 3 conjuncts now ligate: ka+virama+sha->[319] ksha, ta+virama+ra->[320] tra, ja+virama+nya->[321] jna; unbuilt kta correctly stays [ka,virama,ta]. Each conjunct = +1 glyph (PUA) + 1 lg.insert([C1,virama,C2], conj) in the one cjct LigatureSubBuilder - trivially extensible. 322 glyphs. SO THE FONT IS COMPREHENSIVELY SHAPING both scripts with every pipeline proven: Arabic cursive joining (init/medi/fina SingleSubst), Devanagari matra reordering (HarfBuzz auto, matches the typed syllable_visual_order), Devanagari conjunct ligatures (cjct LigatureSubst, 3 built). The users deferred shaping is done + demonstrated to extend. All typed-model work verified (lib gate 128/128). REMAINING is pure mechanical extension of proven patterns (user can prioritize): the rest of the ~1000 common Devanagari conjuncts, init/medi/fina for the other 25 Arabic letters (needs the Arabic alphabet designed first), and refining the crude placeholder glyph shapes. Pacing light extensions via heartbeat. Unstaged, off-box, nothing committed. Progress 90%.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_28 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 28u32, "2026-11-10T08:15Z", "org-f33af161", "Arabic COMPLETE: 28-letter cursive-joining alphabet all rustybuzz-verified off-box europa (alef beh teh theh noon yeh dal thal reh zain lam meem jeem hah khah seen sheen sad dad tah zah ain ghain feh qaf kaf heh waw). Each via the typed arabic GADT (dual_j 4 forms / right_j 2 forms), isolated cmapped U+06xx + contextual forms to Presentation-Forms-B + GSUB init/medi/fina SingleSubst. 3-way joining proven (meem+lam+meem to meem.fina/lam.medi/meem.init). Hindi: 33 consonants + 11 vowels + 8 matras + virama + 7 conjuncts + pre-base matra reorder. Font ~416 glyphs. CODEGEN SCALING WALL: emitter single giant main hit rustc 10m19s/1GB at 416 glyphs (was 130-322s); further growth needs emitter codegen split, so 28 letters is the natural stop. Shapes are crude placeholders (system is the deliverable; refinement is user aesthetic call). All UNSTAGED.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_29 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 29u32, "2026-11-10T08:31Z", "org-f33af161", "CODEGEN WALL FIXED (join points): converted 326 pure glyph builders in lib/font_glyph.spi from := (inl) to :~ (join point), leaving the 18 GADT accessors (ar_initial/deva_glyph etc, identified by ?= match) as := for totality. Generated spiral_main 50143 to 2989 lines, 328 fns, build 619s to 251s (10m19s to 4m11s). Shaping byte-identical (join points semantics-preserving, verified: every gid matches pre-refactor). Scales for future scripts now. Safe transform rule: convert a top-level := block only if its body has no ?= match. All UNSTAGED, backup kept.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_30 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 30u32, "2026-11-10T09:51Z", "org-f33af161", "4 GADT negative tests added to font_glyph.spi + VALIDATED (minimal Cells notebook, passed 4/4): illegal typefeatureset states are COMPILE ERRORS - ar_initial/ar_medial reject a right-joining letter (no initial/medial form), deva_base rejects an independent vowel and a dependent matra (only a consonant is a syllable base). Strongest proof of the seamless-with-typefeatureset ask (illegal states unrepresentable). NOTE: the full font_glyph recurring Cells gate times out at 132 cells; negatives validated via a minimal notebook; full-gate fix filed as FONT-CELLS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT (microblog took it).")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_31 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 31u32, "2026-11-10T10:27Z", "org-f33af161", "Arabic extended to 32 letters: added teh marbuta (U+0629, feminine ending - very common) + 3 alef variants (madda U+0622, hamza-above U+0623, hamza-below U+0625), all right-joining, built+rustbuzz-verified off-box europa (247s with the join-point-fixed build). beh+teh-marbuta to [357,261], beh+alef-madda to [359,261], correct final forms. 28 core consonants + these 4 = the common Arabic letter set.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_32 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 32u32, "2026-11-10T11:16Z", "org-f33af161", "CRITICAL production bug FIXED (maxp v0.5 -> v1.0). microblog found XSans glyphs render INVISIBLE in Chrome-on-Windows (DirectWrite) while skrifa+FreeType render them fine - because the emitter wrote maxp table version 0.5 (CFF-style, no maxPoints/maxContours); glyf fonts REQUIRE maxp v1.0. DirectWrite reads maxPoints=0 and allocates zero outline storage = blank. This had shipped to pluto prod (real visitors saw blank posts). Fix in font_emit.spi finish() FFI: set maxp max_points=512 max_contours=64 + the other v1.0 fields, write-fonts compute_version() then emits v1.0. Verified maxp version=0x10000; FreeType ink o=488px. Fixed woff2/ttf delivered to microblog render dir. Deploy to pluto is the USER's call (surfaced, not self-deployed). Lesson recorded: skrifa+rustbuzz verification is lenient and does not prove glyphs PAINT in a strict rasterizer. All UNSTAGED.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_33 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 33u32, "2026-11-10T15:39Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~15:3xZ: DEPLOYED-FONT COMPLEX-SCRIPT VERIFICATION (systematic fonttools check of the live sans.ttf). ARABIC: fully correct - distinct init/medi/fina glyphs (beh.init/fina=3 contours, medi=4, vs base 2 = real connecting strokes), GSUB arab script with init/medi/fina features, all 3 single-sub lookups (22/22/31 maps) resolve base->positional with ZERO .notdef targets. DEVANAGARI: 12 base consonants present (ka kha ja ta da na ma ra sha sa nya ya, 4-5 contours), all 7 conjuncts (ksha nta tra sta dya jna shra -> distinct PUA E000-E006, 5-7 contours, no notdef), virama + aa/i/e/o matras present. GAP FOUND: U+0940 ii-matra (long-ii ी) was MISSING -> tofu for की etc. FIXED (additive, built green on europa, U+0940 now cmap-mapped, distinct right-stem+top-bar glyph = mirror of i-matra). DELIVERED to a VERIFY path (drafts/x/TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY/verify/sans-iimatra-verify.*), NOT the live render dir; microblog asked to render क+ी vs a reference before promoting. DEEPER FINDING (for a future enhancement): this font's matra model is MPre/MPost reorder + advance with NO GPOS mark attachment, so a post-base matra (ii) sits to the RIGHT of the consonant rather than its flag reaching over it - proper Devanagari matra positioning (and reph, nukta, etc.) needs GPOS mark/mark+mark attachment. i-matra works only because MPre + its bar overlaps the following consonant. Pending: microblog render verdict on the ii-matra partial fix.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_34 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 34u32, "2026-11-10T15:46Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~15:4xZ: COMPLEX-SCRIPT COVERAGE CHECK (cmap vs standard base sets) found more gaps beyond ii-matra. DEVANAGARI: consonants 33/37 (missing U+0929 ऩ, U+0931 ऱ, U+0933 ळ lla, U+0934 ऴ - 0933 is the common one, Marathi/some Hindi; others rare); matras 8/10 (missing U+0940 ii [being fixed now] + U+0943 ृ vocalic-r matra, common: कृ संस्कृत); MISC missing U+0902  anusvara ं [VERY common - nasalization, in हिंदी itself], U+0901 chandrabindu ँ, U+0903 visarga ः; indep vowels 7/7 complete. ARABIC: base 29/36 (missing U+0649 alef-maksura ى [common, word-final], U+0640 tatweel [elongation, not a letter], U+063B-063F [rare/non-standard]). TRIAGE: the CONSONANTS (ळ 0933) and ARABIC LETTER (alef-maksura 0649) are addable as regular cmapped glyphs like the existing ones (low risk). The COMBINING MARKS (anusvara 0902, chandrabindu 0901, r-matra 0943 which is BELOW-base, visarga 0903) need above/below positioning the font lacks - same GPOS-mark-attachment gap as note 33. Without GPOS, an above mark like anusvara placed MPost sits to the RIGHT not above the consonant, so it is NOT a clean additive fix (unlike ii-matra which is legitimately right-placed per microblog render verify). RECOMMEND: add ळ + alef-maksura as regular glyphs (quick); the combining marks are a Phase-2 GPOS deliverable. anusvara is the highest-value missing glyph (nasalization is pervasive in Hindi) - prioritize GPOS for it.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_35 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 35u32, "2026-11-10T22:52Z", "microblog", "microblog 22:51Z: ii-matra build live on pluto (woff2 682c9b27, ttf c2174609; backup fonts-before-iimatra-20261110). Chrome check before the drop: advance 330 / ink 0..281, no collision in कीक, all other scripts metric-identical to 5dc8b6e1. org3 told to move the soak sha pin.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_36 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 36u32, "2026-11-10T23:01Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~19:0xZ GROOM (post-BSOD recovery, box-light): font complex-script status. LANDED LIVE: ii-matra U+0940 (pluto 22:51Z). DELIVERED (microblog verify dir, pending render+promote): alef-maksura U+0649 (dotless-yeh, right_j isol+FEF0 final, GSUB lfn 0649->FEF0 confirmed; common word-final in على إلى حتى). STRATEGIC CONCLUSION from microblog's fallback finding (missing glyph -> correct SYSTEM face for the cluster, not tofu): only CONFIDENT-design glyphs are worth adding, because a blind-designed glyph that is slightly wrong REGRESSES vs the correct system fallback. ii-matra (exact mirror of matra_i) and alef-maksura (exact yeh-minus-dots) qualify. The remaining gaps do NOT: ळ 0933 is blind Devanagari design (no exact reference -> fallback is better); anusvara 0902 / chandrabindu 0901 / r-matra 0943 are above/below combining marks that NEED GPOS mark-to-base (the fallback positions them correctly meanwhile, so no rush). So the font deliverable (typed Arabic+Devanagari model, deployed, pixel-faithful Latin, Arabic cursive + Devanagari conjuncts verified correct, ii-matra live) is at a clean completion; the real remaining enhancement is GPOS Phase-2 (anusvara the highest-value target) — a focused multi-step piece, not a quick add. NO new blind glyph adds recommended.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_37 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 37u32, "2026-11-10T23:36Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~19:4xZ: GPOS ANUSVARA PLAN (de-risked - confirmed the API, ready to execute fresh). The font has NO GPOS today; anusvara 0902 / chandrabindu 0901 / r-matra 0943 are above/below marks that sit WRONG without mark-attachment (worse than the Windows system-face fallback), so they are GPOS-gated. write-fonts 0.55 HAS a clean MarkToBaseBuilder (src/tables/gpos/builders.rs:837), analogous to the SingleSubBuilder already in finish(): insert_mark(GlyphId16, class:&str, AnchorBuilder), insert_base(GlyphId16, class, AnchorBuilder), impl Builder -> Vec<MarkBasePosFormat1>. PLAN: (1) add an anusvara glyph (small filled dot above the shirorekha, ~y 720-800, in font_glyph.spi) + emit it cmapped at 0902 (advance 0 or small). (2) In finish() build a Gpos exactly like the Gsub: a MarkToBaseBuilder, class \"top\"; insert_mark(fg(0x0902), \"top\", AnchorBuilder at the anusvara mark point ~ (0, its-bottom)); insert_base(fg(cp), \"top\", AnchorBuilder at (consonant top-center, ~720)) for every Devanagari consonant gid (ka..ha). Build -> Vec<MarkBasePosFormat1> -> Lookup (LookupType 4 gpos / mark-base) -> PositioningLookupList -> Gpos::new(scripts, features, lookups) with an abvm FeatureRecord under the dev2 Script; b.add_table(&gpos). (3) Verify: rustbuzz shape क+0902 (U+0915 U+0902) -> anusvara positioned ABOVE ka, not to its right; then microblog raster-compares हिं. NOTE: base anchor x must track each consonant advance (center = advance/2); a single shared anchor misplaces wide/narrow consonants - may need per-consonant x. NOT STARTED: a new GPOS table in the 650-line FFI string is error-prone to author at session-end depth during the BSOD-recovery window; best done fresh. This note makes it a ~1-2 hour execute, not a research task. Highest-value remaining Hindi gap (anusvara is in हिंदी हैं में etc.).")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_38 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 38u32, "2026-11-10T23:54Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~19:5xZ: GPOS ANUSVARA IMPLEMENTED (note 37s plan executed - now wired, not deferred). The font has its FIRST GPOS table. Built green on europa, delivered to verify (sans-anusvara-verify.*), pending microblog render-check of क+ं positioning. STRUCTURE (fonttools-confirmed): GPOS LookupType 4 MarkToBase under abvm feature / dev2 script, markCount 1 (anusvara 0902) + baseCount 19 consonants; mark anchor (0,712), base anchor (280,712) -> dot centers above the consonant y 712-808, above the ~655 headline. THE WORKING FFI IDIOM (for the next GPOS - chandrabindu, matras): write_fonts 0.55 MarkToBaseBuilder in finish() like the GSUB: let mut mb = MarkToBaseBuilder::default(); mb.insert_mark(GlyphId16::new(fg(0x0902)), topc, AnchorBuilder::new(0,712)).unwrap() [returns Result]; mb.insert_base(gid, topc, AnchorBuilder::new(280,712)); then PositionLookup::MarkToBase(Lookup::new(LookupFlag::empty(), mb.build(&mut vs).into_iter().map(MarkBasePos::Format1).collect::<Vec<_>>())) -- the ONE gotcha: build() returns Vec<MarkBasePosFormat1> but Lookup::new wants Vec<MarkBasePos>, so map(MarkBasePos::Format1). Then PositionLookupList::new([pl].to_vec()); Gpos::new(scripts, features, pll); b.add_table(&gpos). FFI constraints held: no bang (used >0 not !=0), no quote string literals (topc = std::str::from_utf8(&[116u8,111,112]) for \"top\"; tags as byte arrays). KNOWN LIMIT: base anchor x fixed 280 (ok for ~560-advance consonants; per-consonant advance/2 if microblog flags off-center). Reuses the GSUB imports (Lookup, Tag, FeatureList, Script, VariationStoreBuilder, GlyphId16 all in finish scope). Pending microblog positioning verdict.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_39 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 39u32, "2026-11-11T00:19Z", "microblog", "microblog 00:19Z: anusvara GPOS v3 live on pluto (woff2 326300fd, ttf 5cfab53e; backup fonts-before-anusvara-20261110). The font's first GPOS: MarkToBase (anusvara over 19 consonants + ी/ा stems; े/ै as zero-advance marks) and MarkToMark (ं right of े/ै). Verified with HarfBuzz across 3 rounds of fixes: v1 dot off-center and े/ै spacing beside the consonant; v2 matra+dot collided in में/हैं (70x50 units); v3 clear (में dot 330..426 vs matra 140..300). Every other text shapes to identical gids and advances; maxp v1.0.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_40 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 40u32, "2026-11-11T00:21Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-11 ~00:2xZ: ANUSVARA GPOS LIVE on pluto (00:19:41Z, woff2 326300fd). microblog HarfBuzz-verified the full stack: mark-to-base (कं/हिं dot centered above) + mark-to-mark (में dot 330-426 right of e-matra, हैं dot 350-446 right of ai, both inside the 560 advance, no collision). नहीं attaches to ी over its stem. े/ै are zero-advance marks (है/मे/के correct). All non-Devanagari text identical gids/advances, maxp v1.0. So the font now renders है/में/हैं/नहीं in-font instead of Nirmala fallback. This is the first GPOS table in the font, built this session from zero (write-fonts 0.55 MarkToBaseBuilder + MarkToMarkBuilder, 2 lookups type 4+6 under abvm, idiom in notes 37/38). REMAINING (reuse the SAME lookups/idiom per microblog): chandrabindu 0901 + r-matra 0943 (r-matra is BELOW-base = a new blwm feature + below anchor) + ळ 0933 (plain consonant, needs reference). Extending to chandrabindu next (above-mark, same abvm lookups, just a crescent+dot glyph).")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_41 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 41u32, "2026-11-11T00:44Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-11 ~00:4xZ: CHANDRABINDU 0901 v2 delivered to verify (both microblog fixes: anchor 0,712 to center; glyph = shallow U-cup x-120..120 y690..760 ~28 stroke 180 hollow + 50-dia dot y815, per microblog raster spec), pending microblog re-raster of हाँ/चाँद/माँ/कँ/मेँ. Reuses the anusvara mark-base + mark-mark lookups (added as a mark in both, L0 now 4 marks, L1 2 mark1s). REMAINING GAPS + the de-risked plan: (1) r-matra 0943 ृ = BELOW-base, the one new direction. NOT a copy of the above-marks: needs its OWN MarkToBase lookup (L2) with a bottom mark class + base anchors at the consonant BOTTOM (~280, 0) and the r-matra mark anchor at its top, under a NEW blwm (below-base marks) FeatureRecord (tag [98,108,119,109]) referencing lookup index 2; Script LangSys then lists both abvm (above: anusvara/chandrabindu/matra lookups 0,1) and blwm (below: 2). Plus the hook glyph (a small curl hanging below the baseline, y negative). HarfBuzz applies blwm for Devanagari below marks; verify क+ृ (0x0915 0x0943) shapes the hook BELOW ka. Best done FRESH (below-base + the blwm feature-application has subtleties worth verifying carefully, not rushing at session-end depth). (2) ळ 0933 = plain consonant, needs a reference shape from microblog to design (render-gate like the glyphs). The GPOS builder idiom (MarkToBaseBuilder/MarkToMarkBuilder, notes 37/38) covers r-matra; only the blwm feature wiring + the hook glyph are new.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_42 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 42u32, "2026-11-11T00:55Z", "microblog", "microblog 00:54Z: chandrabindu v3 live (woff2 057d3b75, ttf 31affc31; backup fonts-before-chandrabindu-20261110). Root cause of the anchor offsets in v1/v2: the emitter normalizes each glyph's xMin to 0, so a mark anchor must be the stored half-width (anusvara 48, chandrabindu 120), not 0. Shape: a U-cup 240 wide plus a 50 bindu; verified by raster plus HarfBuzz across कँ हाँ माँ मेँ, other texts identical.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_43 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 43u32, "2026-11-11T00:57Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-11 00:54Z: CHANDRABINDU 0901 LIVE on pluto (woff2 057d3b75). कँ centered 280, हाँ/माँ over the aa stem, मेँ right of the e-matra, reads as proper candra+bindu, anusvara set unchanged, maxp v1.0. So BOTH Devanagari above-marks (anusvara 0902 + chandrabindu 0901) are now DEPLOYED via the full GPOS stack (mark-base L0 + mark-mark L1, abvm, 4 marks + 21 bases + 2 mark1s), built from zero this session. KEY REUSABLE RULE (cost 2 iterations, now in memory): the emitter normalizes each glyph xMin->0, so a mark glyph drawn centered at x=0 (ink -W..W) stores at 0..2W, and its GPOS mark-base anchor x = W (stored center), NOT 0 (anusvara W=48, chandrabindu W=120); mark-mark-for-right-stack uses x=0 (stored left edge). REMAINING: r-matra 0943 (below-base, the ONE new direction: needs L2 MarkToBase with a bottom class + blwm feature + a hook glyph hanging below the baseline; plan in note 41) + ळ 0933 (plain consonant, needs a reference). HOLDING r-matra for a fresh pass: below-base blwm application is unverified and session depth is extreme; everything else is deployed. All my font builds ran off-box single-slot on europa; box light; all source UNSTAGED.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_44 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 44u32, "2026-11-11T01:20Z", "microblog", "microblog 21:2x verify review: r-matra (U+0943) per-consonant bot anchors PASS: right-stem consonants put the hook at 472 (28 in from the ink's right edge, under the stem), with क 280 / ग 300 / र 230; blwm fires, hook y -137..-13, all other texts identical. ळ (U+0933) first pass reads as two separate tall zeros '00' (the loops overlap only 10); asked for a shared middle stroke (centers 220/470). The r-matra font is in verify, built together with ळ; it drops as soon as a ळ-fixed or r-matra-only build is green.")
inl note_of_font_complex_scripts_45 () = Note ("FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS", 45u32, "2026-11-11T01:30Z", "microblog", "microblog 01:29Z: r-matra + ळ live (woff2 5f64b39b, ttf 8967d600; backup fonts-before-rmatra-lla-20261110). r-matra: blwm + per-consonant stem anchors (472 right-stem, 280/300/230 क/ग/र), hook y -137..-13. ळ: joined double loop (shared middle wall, x60..630, adv 690) after the first pass read as '00'. Tonight's drops on pluto: ii-matra, alef-maksura, @ and ·, anusvara+e/ai GPOS, chandrabindu, r-matra+ळ. Each was HarfBuzz-additive with maxp v1.0; Chrome ink proof is still pending (the box Chrome can't reach my loopback since the reboot).")
inl serve_timeline_timing () = Task ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", "pluto serve: log a server-side duration row per /timeline request (cached vs rendered)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "serve,pluto,sla,observability,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_serve_timeline_timing () = Planning ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_1 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 1u32, "2026-11-10T03:59Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:2x microblog: found while diagnosing SERVE-STALLS-AFTER-PIN. The production serve keeps NO server-side record of /timeline latency: sim_serve's logged writes only the sim's X-API routes (reply_as), and pluto serves only /timeline and /media, so /tmp/sim.log never exists in the pod. Every stall number so far was measured from outside the pod (curl, soak). DoD: each /timeline request appends one row 'timeline <cached|rendered> <ms>' to the serve's log (the existing log path, /tmp/sim.log on the pod's emptyDir), timed with erlang monotonic_time in milliseconds; a gleam test pins the row format; it rides the same restart as the default-page cache, so the before/after bracket gets server-side durations. Next step: draft now_ms, timing_row and timed_timeline in the SERVE-DEFAULT-PAGE-CACHE timeline_serve.spi draft, route feed_or_api's /timeline through it, add the row-format test.")
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_2 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:02Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:3x microblog: DRAFTED in the SERVE-DEFAULT-PAGE-CACHE timeline_serve.spi draft (now sha d48d3fdd99e5; sim_serve draft unchanged, 52eb2699afe9): now_ms () reads erlang:monotonic_time(millisecond) through erlang_term::apply + cast; timing_row cached ms gives 'timeline cached|rendered <ms>'; timed_timeline times timeline_reply and appends the row to the serve's log through erlang_file::file_appended (the same call sim_serve's logged uses); feed_or_api routes /timeline through it. New gleam test pins the row format ('timeline cached 12', 'timeline rendered 3400'). 0 lines over 120. The running europa gate (x-serve-cache-gate) tests the earlier draft 122e966d2646, so this needs its own gate run. Next step: after x-serve-cache-gate settles, overlay this draft on /home/remote/xcache and rerun cache-gate.sh (same 3 notebooks), then the full sim verify before the redeploy goes to the user.")
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_3 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:19Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:2x microblog: COMBINED GATE GREEN, job-1794283539239-x-serve-cache-gate2 on europa (run cache-gate-20261110040539, drafts 52eb2699afe9 / d48d3fdd99e5 = default-page cache + timing row on the deployed sources): sim_serve 9/9, timeline_serve 36/36 (incl. the 2 cache tests and the row-format test), simframes/simframes 1/1. NEXT GATE queued: the full sim verify on the drafts (verify.ps1 -Part sim, no accept, moon's 11 accepted fixtures overlaid on /home/remote/xcache), job label x-serve-cache-verify, 7 h cap, nice 19; a box poller submits it when europa admits it (load 12 now). Next step: after that verify is green, put the redeploy to the user: cost = one Recreate (~5 min measured 11-10); gain = a default request touching KBs instead of ~80 MB of swapped world; bracket = org3's soak n >= 15, the beam's major faults per default request (now ~19,900 on a cold request), and the new server-side timing rows.")
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_4 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:28Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 00:4x microblog: the full verify x-serve-cache-verify went RED in its cell-budget step (exit 1 in 2 min, before any build): 4 over-budget cells, all mine. api_world 294 > 272 and blank_world 281 > 272 (the new field; api_world was already at ~271), timed_timeline 326 > 271, the cache test 314 > 271. The notebook gates never run the budget check, only the full sim build does. FIXED in the drafts (now sim_serve 574f466ddb8f, timeline_serve 2ebb9e33c39c; 0 over budget by the exact awk oracle, bases clean too; 0 lines over 120): a type alias feed_lists for the feeds type, the field renamed to front, page_size = 100 (the compiler flags the i32 suffix as redundant there), logged_timing split out of timed_timeline, a shared default_get () request for the test. Rerun queued: x-serve-cache-verify2 (poller, europa). Next step: verify2 green -> put the redeploy to the user with the bracket.")
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_5 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 5u32, "2026-11-10T05:48Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "11-10 01:5x microblog: ALL GATES GREEN, the redeploy is a USER DECISION. Full sim verify on the drafts: job-1794284861716-x-serve-cache-verify2 (europa, run cache-verify-20261110042742) exit 0, sim build exit 0, 29/29 sim notebooks passed (incl. sim_serve and timeline_serve), against the 11 accepted fixtures with no fixture drift (the cache and the timing rows change no rendered output). Inputs: timeline_serve 2ebb9e33c39c, sim_serve 574f466ddb8f (both drafts now copied into the box x tree, unstaged, after their bases were checked equal to the live files). ARTIFACT = that verify run's own frames build: frames-erlang-1110.tgz, 8 packages, 2,758,804 B, sha b8784f0ab682cb3a (on the box scratchpad and in europa /home/remote/stage). MANIFEST xsim-serve-pluto-1110.yaml (sha 3ec4ac07abb2bef7) = the live 1109 one with frames-1110 as the only change; server dry-run clean on pluto. DECISION FOR THE USER: the apply is one Recreate (~5 min measured on 11-10). GAIN: a default /timeline request renders from the cached page instead of walking ~80 MB of swapped world (cold request today: 3.8 s and ~19,900 major faults); plus server-side timing rows in /tmp/sim.log. BRACKET: org3 soak n >= 15 against the pinned pre-lever baseline, the beam majflt per default request, and the new timing rows. ROLLBACK: the current 1109 manifest (frames-1109 kept), also ~5 min. Next step: on the user's go, stage frames-1110 on pluto (additive, sha rechecked there), org3 takes the before-baseline, microblog applies, org3 brackets.")
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_6 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 6u32, "2026-11-10T11:37Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:3xZ: user 06:5x pre-authorized the pluto cache redeploy (\"stop asking me for decisions ... until our font is finished and live on pluto with all the pending items around it\"). The default-page cache now ships with the timeline CSS as frames-1111 (sim_serve 574f466ddb8f, timeline_serve 2ebb9e33c39c, timeline_page 3b703fc082d2), building on ganymede (job-1794309940701-x-pluto-build-1111g2). NEXT STEP: stage frames-1111 on pluto, apply xsim-serve-pluto-1111.yaml, org3 brackets it, read the timing rows and the cold /timeline stall after.")
inl note_of_serve_timeline_timing_7 () = Note ("SERVE-TIMELINE-TIMING", 7u32, "2026-11-10T11:55Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:5xZ DONE, live: frames-1111 writes one timing row per /timeline to /tmp/sim.log in the serve container: \"timeline cached 0\" for the default page, \"timeline rendered 13514\" for a query render (?d=up, 13.5 s). proof: kubectl exec tail of /tmp/sim.log right after the cutover, plus curl times (default 2-5 ms, query 13.54 s).")
inl backend_bench_ci_2a_tree () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2A-TREE", "Bench workload 2: allocation-heavy recursive union tree (build, fold, checksum) on every backend", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "performance,benchmark,backends,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_2a_tree () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2A-TREE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2a_tree_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2A-TREE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:00Z", "compiler", "Shape: build a complete binary tree of depth d (runtime ~ value) as a recursive union, fold it to a checksum, repeat; self-check the node count (2^(d+1)-1) and checksum; exit = checksum mod 256. Same conventions as bench_sieve (core-only package, self-tail recursion, no !!!!Assign). Next step: write apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_tree, compile on the 8 backends, run C/Rust/Zig/Python on ganymede, compare exits.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2a_tree_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2A-TREE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:06Z", "compiler", "11-10 00:3x compiler: DONE. apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_tree (unstaged, core-only): recursive union tree (:| ^ tree = Leaf : i32 | Node : tree * tree), built to runtime depth 20 (2^20 leaves, ~2M nodes), leaf count self-checked, checksum folded mod 1000003, 4 rounds, exit = 149. Lesson: recursive functions over a runtime value must be :~ ^ (join points); := ^ inlined build into itself until EJP0040 (1000 nested dynamic ifs). Compiles on C, Rust, Zig, Python, TypeScript, F#, Lua, Gleam (8/8). Ran on ganymede (pack78, loaded, single runs): C 1195 ms, Rust 1270 ms, Zig 621 ms, Python 40 s; all exit 149. Zig at ~half of C is a real allocation-strategy gap (C/Rust refcount + malloc/free per node), exactly what the benchmark should surface; profile it once step 5 says the numbers are faithful.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2a_tree_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2A-TREE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:08Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede 11-10 00:3x, installed pack78 (SpiralCompilerCore 3ab85d76), ~/remote-stage/benchw/bench_tree: --backend C/Rust/Zig/Python/TypeScript/Fsharp/Lua/Gleam all compile; native C (gcc -O3), Rust (opt-level 3, lto fat, cgu 1), Zig (ReleaseFast) and python3 each exit 149 (= checksum mod 256 after the leaf-count self-check passes in every round). Sample in tree: apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_tree.")
inl backend_bench_ci_2b_strings () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2B-STRINGS", "Bench workload 3: string building and hashing (FNV-1a over generated strings) on every backend", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "performance,benchmark,backends,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_2b_strings () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2B-STRINGS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2b_strings_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2B-STRINGS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:00Z", "compiler", "Shape: generate k strings by concatenation from a runtime seed, FNV-1a hash each over its bytes (string index), xor-fold to a checksum; self-check a precomputed checksum; exit = checksum mod 256. Next step: write apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_strings and run it across backends like bench_sieve.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2b_strings_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2B-STRINGS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:16Z", "compiler", "11-10 00:4x compiler: DONE. apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_strings (unstaged, core-only). SHAPE CHANGED from the plan: core has NO runtime string concatenation (+ on strings is a ConstraintError; only !!!!StaticStringConcat over literals; libs ++# is per-backend macros) and NO char-to-integer conversion (!!!!Conv refuses char -> i32), so the workload measures what core strings do have: a runtime 4,095-byte string; for every offset k, !!!!StringSlice(text, k, n-1) (a substring allocation) hashed with 32-bit FNV-1a over !!!!StringIndex reads, chars mapped by !!!!EQ to small codes; 4 rounds; ~8M byte reads + 4,095 substring allocations per round; length self-checked; exit = checksum mod 256 = 4. Compiles on C, Rust, Zig, Python, TypeScript, F#, Lua, Gleam (8/8). Ran on ganymede (pack78, loaded, single runs): C 106 ms, Rust 67 ms, Zig 115 ms, Python 71 s; all exit 4. Ranking differs from bench_tree (there Zig was fastest), which is why the set needs several shapes.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2b_strings_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2B-STRINGS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:17Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede 11-10 00:4x, installed pack78 (Core 3ab85d76), ~/remote-stage/benchw/bench_strings: all 8 backends compile; native C (gcc -O3), Rust (opt-level 3, lto fat, cgu 1), Zig (ReleaseFast) and python3 each exit 4. Sample in tree: apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_strings.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2b_strings_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2B-STRINGS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:17Z", "compiler", "Evidence: see note 3 (ganymede 11-10 00:4x, pack78: 8/8 backends compile; C, Rust, Zig, python3 all exit 4); sample at apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_strings.")
inl backend_bench_ci_2c_size_input () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2C-SIZE-INPUT", "Bench workloads take a per-backend size so one pass is >= 100 ms everywhere without 20-minute interpreter runs", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "performance,benchmark,backends,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_2c_size_input () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2C-SIZE-INPUT", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2c_size_input_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2C-SIZE-INPUT", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:00Z", "compiler", "From bench_sieve: Python runs ~550x C, so a size baked into the program cannot serve every backend. Next step: decide between (a) a !!!!BackendSwitch on the rounds value (sizes chosen per backend in the source, simplest, no I/O) and (b) reading rounds from argv or an env var where a backend can; measure (a) on bench_sieve first because it keeps the workload pure.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2c_size_input_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2C-SIZE-INPUT", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:23Z", "compiler", "11-10 00:5x compiler: DONE (option a). DECISION: identical per-round work on every backend (same n / depth / text), and !!!!BackendSwitch picks only the ROUND COUNT (8 for compiled backends: C, Cpp, CppHost, Rust, Zig, Fsharp, Pascal, Wasm, Kotlin, Swift; 1 for Python, Lua, Gleam, TypeScript, Bend, Lean), so the reported metric is time per round = (whole-process time - overhead) / rounds, directly comparable across backends with no work-normalization guess (sieve work is n log log n, not n). Exits made round-independent: each round is self-checked against the first round (or the known prime count), and the exit is ONE rounds checksum: bench_sieve 197, bench_tree 246, bench_strings 241 on every backend. All 3 rewritten in apps/compiler/tmp/samples (unstaged). For step 3: the overhead arm needs a 0-round binary per backend (an env or arg override of rounds, or a sibling sample with rounds 0); interpreters at 1 round x 15 samples cost ~2.5-5 min per workload, within a scheduled job.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2c_size_input_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2C-SIZE-INPUT", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:23Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede 11-10 00:5x (pack78, load 26), C 8 rounds vs python3 1 round give the same exit per workload: bench_sieve 197/197, bench_tree 246/246, bench_strings 241/241 (C 339 ms / 2527 ms / 114 ms; Python 12 s / 9 s / 19 s, inflated by load).")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2c_size_input_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2C-SIZE-INPUT", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:24Z", "compiler", "Evidence: note 3 above (same exits at 8 vs 1 rounds on all three workloads); samples bench_sieve, bench_tree, bench_strings in apps/compiler/tmp/samples.")
inl fiscal_currency_places () = Task ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", "fiscal: per-currency decimal places from the official SAT c_Moneda catalog, so money amounts and CFDI windows stop taking places from callers", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,erp,mx,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_currency_places () = Planning ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:08Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "From the sourced rounding research (FISCAL-ERP-MONEY n20): CFDI 4.0 SubTotal/Total/tax summary use 'the decimals the currency supports' from the c_Moneda catalog (0-4, MXN 2); today money and p2p callers pass places by hand (p2p.spi:165 hard-codes 2). DoD: a typed table or prototype from the pinned catCFDI c_Moneda column (not hand-typed), places_of for the currencies fiscal models, the CFDI window draft (FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY) taking places from it, a test that MXN is 2 and a 0-decimal currency (e.g. JPY or CLP) is 0, all read from the catalog. Next step: locate c_Moneda in the pinned catCFDI.xsd/xls under deps/corpus/mx and decide generated enumeration vs a census at gate time. TypeFeatures: currency phantom to places, generated from the catalog.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:10Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:2x SOURCE DECIDED AND PINNED. The pinned SAT catCFDI.xsd lists c_Moneda codes only (no decimals; SAT keeps 'Decimales' in its catCFDI.xls). SAT's decimals follow ISO 4217 minor units, so the source is the official ISO 4217 list one from SIX (the maintenance agency): https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/financial-information/data-center/iso-currrency/lists/list-one.xml, published 2026-09-17, 280 entries, sha256 33139B438657D1CEE116BA737807EA71D19D6DE4B90F799A09C56F0CC6A1B0FF, pinned in fiscal scripts/init.ps1 (unstaged, deps/corpus/iso4217) and placed locally. Checked: MXN 2, JPY 0, CLP 0, BHD 3, EUR/BRL/USD 2. CAVEAT: the URL is SIX's latest copy, so the pin throws when ISO amends the list (by design: re-pin after review). Next step: a generator-style reader of CcyNtry (Ccy, CcyMnrUnts) into a typed places_of for the currencies fiscal models, plus a check that every c_Moneda code in catCFDI.xsd has an ISO entry (flagging SAT-only codes such as MXV/CNH, if any lack minor units).")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:12Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:3x CENSUS c_Moneda (catCFDI.xsd, 183 codes) vs ISO 4217 list one (178 codes): 156 codes have numeric minor units (0 places: 17, 2: 131, 3: 7, 4: 1). 14 c_Moneda codes are ABSENT from current ISO list one: ANG, BGN, BYR, CNH, CUC, ESD, HRK, MRO, NIC, SLL, STD, UYP, VEF, ZWL (withdrawn or superseded currencies SAT still lists, plus offshore CNH, which is not ISO). 13 are present with minor units N.A.: XAG, XAU, XBA, XBB, XBC, XBD, XDR, XPD, XPT, XSU, XTS, XUA, XXX (metals, funds, testing). So ISO list one alone cannot answer places_of for 27 SAT codes; a silent default of 2 would be wrong. DESIGN: places_of returns a decision (Places n from ISO | NoMinorUnit for N.A. codes | Unlisted code) rather than an i32; for the 14 withdrawn ones, pin ISO list three (historic, same SIX folder, carries the withdrawn currencies' minor units) or SAT's catCFDI.xls Decimales column. Next step: fetch and pin ISO list three, re-run this census, then draft the reader in fiscal src.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 4u32, "2026-11-10T04:14Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:4x ISO list three pinned too (same SIX folder, published 2026-01-01, 137 historic codes, sha256 98FDE2423CDB916D...; fiscal scripts/init.ps1 unstaged, placed locally). Of the 14 c_Moneda codes missing from list one, 12 are WITHDRAWN with dates: ANG 2025-03, BGN 2026-01, BYR 2017-01, CUC 2021-06, HRK 2023-01, MRO 2017-12, NIC 1990-10, SLL 2023-12, STD 2017-12, UYP 1993-03, VEF 2018-08, ZWL 2024-09; CNH (offshore yuan) and ESD are not ISO codes at all. Historic entries carry NO minor-units field (CtryNm, CcyNm, Ccy, CcyNbr, WthdrwlDt only), so ISO cannot give their places. DESIGN FIXED: places_of returns a decision with its evidence: Places n (list one) | NoMinorUnit (list one N.A.: metals, funds, test codes) | Withdrawn date (list three) | NotIso (CNH, ESD); a CFDI in a withdrawn currency is then a visible finding instead of a silent 2 places. Next step: draft the reader over both pinned XMLs in fiscal src (xml helpers already in lib) with tests for MXN 2, JPY 0, BHD 3, XAU NoMinorUnit, BYR Withdrawn 2017-01, CNH NotIso.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 5u32, "2026-11-10T04:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 03:1x DRAFT written: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES\\currency.spi (new fiscal module; spiral.toml discovers files, so no registration edit). Typed half: places_of and iso_code_of over lib money::currency c (Brl, Eur, Usd, Mxn), proven by a test against ISO list one (canon_codes' pattern: a small typed table whose test reads the pinned source). Wire half: minor_unit_of (code) : minor_unit = Places n (list one) | NoMinorUnit (N.A.) | Withdrawn date (list three) | NotIso, reading both pinned XMLs with xml::read_xml and sunat::child_named/child_text. Tests: BRL/MXN/EUR/USD 2 from ISO, JPY/CLP 0, BHD 3, XAU/XDR NoMinorUnit, BYR Withdrawn 2017-01, HRK 2023-01, CNH NotIso. Budget and round trip running on the box (CPU-light). Next step: settle budget and canonical form, then hand the CFDI window's places to places_of in the FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY draft (CfdiLine i32 becomes the currency's places) and queue the node gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 6u32, "2026-11-10T04:30Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 04:4x DRAFT currency.spi F84A5E45, cell budget 0 over (iso_table split into iso_root + iso_table, the typed test split into BRL/MXN and EUR/USD), lib_roundtrip canonical 1/1. 7 tests: typed BRL/MXN/EUR/USD = 2 from ISO list one, JPY/CLP 0, BHD 3, XAU/XDR NoMinorUnit, BYR Withdrawn 2017-01 / HRK 2023-01, CNH NotIso. Reuses sunat::child_named/child_text and xml::read_xml; i64->i32 via convert::i32. Not compiled yet (node gate). Next step: node gate of currency.spi (new module, so the fiscal package gate picks it up) with a pinned compiler once moon leaves TRAIN43; after green, the CFDI window callers pass places_of money::Mxn into CfdiLine.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 7u32, "2026-11-10T04:50Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 05:4x currency.spi 76303E4C: added the DoD's CFDI link, peso_window (families::CfdiLine (places_of money::Mxn)) and test a_peso_cfdi_line_takes_its_places_from_iso_4217 (3.00 x 10.00 at MXN's ISO places gives 29.93 to 30.07). Cell budget 0 over, lib_roundtrip canonical. The draft now STACKS on the FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY families draft (window_bounds, CfdiLine), so both gate together. Next step: one node gate of families + lifecycle + currency with a pinned compiler once moon leaves TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 8u32, "2026-11-10T05:15Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:2x box gate 11-10 00:57-01:12 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib, -Parallel 1, 943 s). currency.spi 76303E4C failed 7/7 as COLLATERAL: 'File currency has a type error somewhere in its path' with the error in p2p.spi framed_field (the package typechecks every module on the path), so currency's own code is not yet judged. families (which currency stacks on) is green and landed. Next step: the box re-gate of p2p + currency.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 9u32, "2026-11-10T05:52Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:5x box gate of currency.spi 76303E4C (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, live lib now carrying the landed families/p2p): typechecks; 6 of 7 tests pass; FAILED sat_codes_iso_withdrew_carry_their_withdrawal. Cause (data, not code): ISO list three lists HRK TWICE, CROATIA 2015-06 and CROATIA 2023-01; entry_for returned the first (2015-06), while the kuna's real withdrawal is 2023-01 (euro). The 11-10 census missed it because its hashtable kept the last entry. FIX (draft 015AAD95, 0 over, canonical): historic_unit takes the LATEST withdrawal over all of a code's list-three entries, keyed year*100+month via decimal::parse on fixed substrings (ISO also writes ranges such as '1978 to 1981' and '1990-07 to 1990-09', which key by their leading year-month); the test message now states the double listing. Re-gate of currency + the SUNAT draft queued on the box (waits for load under 80%). Next step: record that verdict; on green, land currency.spi (new module) and close.")
inl note_of_fiscal_currency_places_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", 10u32, "2026-11-10T06:34Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:3x PROVEN AND LANDED. box gate 11-10 02:23-02:34 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib): families.spi 33AF4D84 GREEN 11/11, lifecycle.spi BB993E13 GREEN 16/16, currency.spi E7867E9F GREEN 7/7. LANDED copy-only into C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\src (unstaged, never committed) after the live bases matched (families 12F8BF31, lifecycle 76449093, currency absent); undo in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES\\undo-20261110-023433 (currency.spi is new, so its undo is deleting it). currency.spi is live: places_of/iso_code_of over money::currency, minor_unit_of reading the pinned ISO 4217 lists one and three (Places | NoMinorUnit | Withdrawn latest date | NotIso), the HRK double listing resolved to 2023-01, and the MXN CFDI window taking its places from ISO. Next step: none; Done.")
inl fiscal_p2p_match_legs () = Task ("FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS", "fiscal p2p: the three-way match checks order reference, currency and supplier, not only amounts (OMNILEDGER gap G2)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,erp,mega-samples,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_p2p_match_legs () = Planning ("FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_p2p_match_legs_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:08Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "From the 11-09 mega-sample review (OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n17, G2): in the sample the order, receipt, invoice and payment share entity, currency, item and document indices (S:57-88); in fiscal, purchase s is indexed only by stage and three_way (p2p.spi:66) compares three decimals. DoD: match_invoice also requires the invoice's order reference, currency and supplier to agree with the purchase (from canon_of's terms), with a typed mismatch reason instead of None, and negative tests for a wrong currency, a wrong supplier and another order's invoice. Next step: list which of those terms canon_document already carries (document.spi) and draft the match decision union. TypeFeatures: a match decision carrying its evidence; currency phantom on the purchase is FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS top-5 item 5 (later).")
inl note_of_fiscal_p2p_match_legs_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:20Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 03:0x READ + DESIGN. canon_document (document.spi:43) carries number, issued, currency (CodeValue), seller and buyer (TextValue) and three amounts, but NOT the purchase-order reference (EN 16931 BT-13 / NF-e xPed); only one canon_of instance exists (manual_invoice, document.spi:118) and canon_document is built in canon_from_values only, so widening it later is contained (document.spi plus posting.spi fixtures). The purchase side holds only { item; amount } plus the order number string, so neither currency nor supplier is checkable today. SLICE 1 (this item, p2p.spi only): an order_terms record { number; supplier; currency } replaces the bare order-number string in Ordered/Received/Matched/Paid (place_order takes it); a match_decision union (MatchedInvoice purchase matched | AmountsDiffer ordered received billed | CurrencyDiffers ordered billed | SupplierDiffers ordered billed) from decide_match; match_invoice stays option-typed as matched_of (decide_match ...) so p2p_plan Steps keep their shape; negative tests for a USD invoice on a BRL order and another seller. SLICE 2 (later): BT-13 order_ref in canon_document so the third leg checks the invoice's order reference. BASE: the draft stacks on the FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC draft (both edit the Ordered/Received patterns), so it is built after that draft's budget check settles. Next step: copy the codec draft as the base and write the order_terms + decide_match block.")
inl note_of_fiscal_p2p_match_legs_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:40Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 05:0x DRAFT p2p.spi 893D375E (stacked on the FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC draft BB91B98F): over-budget cells SHRINK live 7 -> draft 6 (the old 429-weight match_invoice is gone), lib_roundtrip canonical. Slice 1: order_terms { number; supplier; currency } replaces the bare order string in Ordered/Received/Matched/Paid and in place_order/ordering; match_decision = MatchedInvoice | AmountsDiffer ordered*received*billed | CurrencyDiffers ordered*billed | SupplierDiffers ordered*billed; decide_match (generic, canon_of) -> received_decision (non-generic) -> legs = currency_leg then supplier_leg then amounts_decision; match_invoice = matched_of (decide_match ...), so p2p_plan Steps and existing tests keep their shape. Fixtures po_terms (Seller Ltda, BRL, matching invoice_for), invoice_from seller currency, decision_for. New tests: USD invoice on a BRL order -> CurrencyDiffers (BRL, USD); another seller -> SupplierDiffers; short receipt -> AmountsDiffer. Event-log command keys stay strings. Not compiled yet. Next step: node gate together with the codec draft (same file) once moon leaves TRAIN43; slice 2 (OrderDiffers from BT-13) is FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE.")
inl note_of_fiscal_p2p_match_legs_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T05:37Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:3x PROVEN AND LANDED. box re-gate 11-10 01:22-01:34 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib, document DE4BB79E + canon AA43331F overlaid): p2p.spi DD5BDC7E GREEN, discovered 39 executed 39 passed 39 failed 0 in 631 s; document and canon were green 8/8 each in the 00:57 gate. LANDED copy-only into C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\src (unstaged, never committed) after the live bases matched (document DFE711A4, canon ADA23785, p2p 715E5792); undo in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE\\undo-20261110-013454. order_terms in the purchase GADT and match_decision (CurrencyDiffers, SupplierDiffers, AmountsDiffer) are live; match_invoice wraps decide_match, so plan steps keep their shape. Next step: none; Done.")
inl backend_bench_ci_2d_float () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2D-FLOAT", "Bench workload 4: f64 arithmetic (n-body style integration) on every backend", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "performance,benchmark,backends,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_2d_float () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2D-FLOAT", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2d_float_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2D-FLOAT", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:25Z", "compiler", "Shape: a few bodies integrated for k steps in f64 (sqrt, mult, add), energy summed and compared to the first round within an exact bit match (deterministic order), exit = a quantized checksum mod 256; same per-backend rounds convention as 2C. Note Wgsl/Calyx/OpenQasm/Ebpf have no f64; list them unsupported. Next step: write apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_float and run C/Rust/Zig/Python on ganymede.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2d_float_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2D-FLOAT", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:30Z", "compiler", "11-10 01:1x compiler: DONE, shape changed from n-body to a MANDELBROT escape count, because its result is an exact integer (pure f64 mult/add/compare, no sqrt; identical under IEEE double without FMA contraction, the default on x86-64), so the self-check and exit need no float tolerance. apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_float (unstaged, core-only): 480x360 grid, limit 200, every round must equal the first, exit = count mod 256 = 166; rounds per backend by the 2C BackendSwitch convention. Compiles on C, Rust, Zig, Python, TypeScript, F#, Lua, Gleam (8/8). ganymede (pack78, loaded, single runs, 8 rounds compiled / 1 interpreted): C 337 ms, Rust 313 ms, Zig 386 ms, Python 11 s; all exit 166. Backends without f64 (Wgsl, Calyx, OpenQasm, Ebpf) are unsupported for this workload by design. The workload set is now 5: runtime_bench, bench_sieve, bench_tree, bench_strings, bench_float, plus bench_overhead.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2d_float_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2D-FLOAT", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:31Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede 11-10 01:1x pack78: apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_float compiles on 8 backends; native C, Rust, Zig and python3 each exit 166.")
inl backend_bench_ci_2e_overhead () = Task ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2E-OVERHEAD", "Bench overhead arm: an empty-workload program per backend so start-up never counts as speed", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "performance,benchmark,backends,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_bench_ci_2e_overhead () = Planning ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2E-OVERHEAD", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2e_overhead_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2E-OVERHEAD", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:26Z", "compiler", "From the step-1 design (hyperfine subtracts shell spawn, BenchmarkDotNet an overhead method): each backend needs a program that starts, does a trivial runtime-dependent step and exits, timed the same way as the workloads; per-round time = (workload time - overhead time) / rounds. Next step: write apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_overhead (core-only, a ~runtime value returned so nothing folds) and compile it on the 8 backends.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2e_overhead_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2E-OVERHEAD", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:27Z", "compiler", "11-10 01:0x compiler: DONE. apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_overhead (unstaged, core-only): main returns !!!!Mod of a ~ runtime seed (197), so the program does one runtime step (the literal stays a runtime variable in main.c, nothing folds) and exits 197 like bench_sieve. Compiles on C, Rust, Zig, Python, TypeScript, F#, Lua, Gleam (8/8). ganymede (pack78, loaded): C best-of-5 10.2 ms whole-process, python3 125 ms. Step 3 times this the same way as each workload and reports per-round = (workload - overhead) / rounds.")
inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_2e_overhead_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-2E-OVERHEAD", 3u32, "2026-11-10T04:28Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede 11-10 01:0x pack78: --backend C/Rust/Zig/Python/TypeScript/Fsharp/Lua/Gleam all compile apps/compiler/tmp/samples/bench_overhead; native C and python3 exit 197.")
