inl note_of_fiscal_canon_order_reference_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:30Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Slice 2 of FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS (n2): canon_document (document.spi:43) has number, issued, currency, seller, buyer and three amounts but no order reference; EN 16931 BT-13 (Purchase order reference, cac:OrderReference/cbc:ID in UBL, 0..1) and NF-e compra/xPed (0..1) both carry it, and CFDI has no standard field. DoD: an order_ref term (0..1, so an option of term_value identifier_data) in canon_document, filled by canon_from_values/manual_canon (manual_invoice grows an optional order reference, or a second builder keeps the 7-tuple callers unchanged), BT-13 asserted present in the pinned canon term table, and the p2p match gains an OrderDiffers leg that only fires when the invoice names an order. Next step: confirm BT-13's row in canon.spi's 162-term table and decide whether manual_invoice grows a field or a with_order_ref builder wraps it (fewer caller edits in posting.spi). Uses: option-typed term, match decision carrying its evidence.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_order_reference_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:46Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 05:3x DRAFTS SETTLED (document DE4BB79E, canon AA43331F, p2p F935735C; bases document DFE711A4, canon ADA23785, p2p = the FISCAL-P2P-MATCH-LEGS draft over the codec draft). Cell budget on the box: document 7 -> 7, canon 22 -> 22, p2p 7 -> 6; lib_roundtrip canonical 3/3. document.spi: canon_document gains order_ref : option (term_value identifier_data) (None from canon_from_values, the only literal record, so the 7-tuple manual_invoice callers in posting/p2p are untouched); identifier_in accessor; with_order_ref (record update) and order_ref_of; tests a_manual_invoice_names_no_order and the_order_reference_is_bt_13. canon.spi: test bt_13_is_the_optional_order_reference asserts BT-13 binds ubl:Invoice|CreditNote/cac:OrderReference/cbc:ID at 0..1 (checked in both pinned Peppol structure files), via order_reference_binding; ALSO repairs the live merged cell found by FISCAL-CANONICAL-SWEEP and splits the exposed legacy cardinality test (nested_text). p2p.spi: OrderDiffers case and order_leg (fires only when the invoice names an order, BT-13 being 0..1), legs = order then currency then supplier then amounts; tests: an invoice for PO-8 against PO-7 gives OrderDiffers, an invoice naming PO-7 matches. Not compiled yet. Next step: one node gate of document + canon + p2p (with the codec and match-legs drafts it stacks on) with a pinned compiler once moon leaves TRAIN43.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canon_order_reference_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T05:15Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 01:2x box gate 11-10 00:57-01:12 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib, -Parallel 1, 943 s). canon.spi AA43331F GREEN 8/8 (BT-13 binding, the repaired merged cell, split cardinality tests) and document.spi DE4BB79E GREEN 8/8 (order_ref, with_order_ref, the two BT-13 tests). p2p.spi (top of the codec -> match legs -> order ref stack) FAILED to typecheck: framed_field's sm'::length had no fixed integer type (ETY-ValueRestriction) and logged_ordering came before ordering_events (unbound); both are codec-draft lines, fixed in all three stacked drafts (order-ref p2p now DD5BDC7E, budget unchanged, canonical). Next step: re-gate p2p + currency on the box once its load is under 70% (waiter running), then land document + canon + p2p together.")
