inl note_of_fiscal_canonical_sweep_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANONICAL-SWEEP", 1u32, "2026-11-10T04:43Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Found 11-10 while drafting FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE: live fiscal/src/canon.spi (ADA23785) is NOT canonical; a blank line is missing before ///> rust test a_cardinality_within_its_ancestors_is_their_product, so the cell tool counts it inside the previous test's cell and its own weight (438, over 271) never shows. A missing blank at a splice joint is a known here-string trap. DoD: lib_roundtrip over every fiscal/src/*.spi on the box (CPU-light, no compile); every non-canonical file listed with its diff; each fix drafted (canonical bytes) with its cell-budget delta stated, since fixing a merge can EXPOSE hidden over-budget cells (then split them in the same draft, baselines only shrink). Next step: run the round trip over all fiscal src files and list the non-canonical ones.")
inl note_of_fiscal_canonical_sweep_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CANONICAL-SWEEP", 2u32, "2026-11-10T04:45Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 05:2x SWEEP DONE on the box (lib_roundtrip over all 21 fiscal/src/*.spi, no compile): 19 canonical, 2 not. canon.spi (ADA23785): blank line missing before test a_cardinality_within_its_ancestors_is_their_product at L439, so two tests counted as ONE cell and the hidden test's own weight (438 > 271) never showed; repaired in the FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE canon draft, where that legacy test is split (nested_text helper; presence test and bounds test) and the file stays budget-neutral 22 -> 22. p2p.spi (715E5792): one extra blank line at L242 (a double blank never merges cells, so budget-neutral); every p2p draft in flight (codec, match legs, order reference) emits canonical bytes and repairs it. No other file differs. proof: ROUNDTRIP total 21, canonical 19, both differences accounted for. Next step: none for this item beyond those drafts landing; mark Done when FISCAL-CANON-ORDER-REFERENCE and FISCAL-ERP-P2P-EVENT-CODEC land.")
