inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T05:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 split from SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT note 5 (tibia asked for one item covering both the split and SPS-NB-6B note 3 coverage map). DoD: each terminal below has a :# cell in an apps/kernel/src linear_* notebook asserting its result, gated in-package on a node mirror with budget 0: open substitution application_argument and application_function; weakened family (unit_bool_closed_tensor, unit_bool_weakened_tensor, bool_application_weakened, weakened_identity_lambda, two_step_weakened_identity_lambda, arbitrary_outer_lambda, outer_weakening_composition, outer_weakening_associativity); total and conditional bool literal replacement; bool_negation_involution; nested_lambda_substitution, application_lambda_substitution and its preservation; conditional_guard_preservation, reduction_preservation; closed_recursive_beta_conditional, shared_argument_counterexample; nonidentity_lambda_canonicity, atomic_tensor_beta_progress, bool_application_atomic_congruence; all_membership_spine. Slices go through org2 for box apply. Next step: tibia takes the first slice (open substitution application cases).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:03Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:0x tibia (the open-substitution application slice, per org2): GREEN; drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE\\handoff-1\\linear_open_substitution.spi (FROZEN; the box module 03168a15b021 plus two fixtures and two tests). Covers recursive_open_typed_substitution_application_function (main.spi:4872) and _application_argument (4786). Function position: fun_plan applies the existing lambda_plan (a substitution under a binder) to a held unit, so OFun reaches the outer variable inside the applied lambda; source Apply(lambda (x, z), u) is size 6, and so is the target. Argument position: arg_plan applies a closed identity in the one-cell context (cell_identity, built from binder_var) to var_plan; source Apply(id, x) is size 4, and so is the target Apply(id, Unit). Both merges reuse left_merge/right_merge/none_merge. Tests 6 (4 + 2), pre-registered (6, 6, elim) and (4, 4, elim), both held on the first run. Gate (ganymede job tibia-nb7a): --check rc 0, 6/6, 0 unsupported, budget 0. With this, all 4 group-(2) cases from NB-6B note 3 are tests. Next step: after org2 applies it, tick these two terminals off the note-5 map.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T06:09Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 2 (bool) DONE: apps/kernel/src/linear_bool_literals.spi e5e4e56a887a, gated alone on the ganymede mirror (job org2-lbl: 4 discovered, 4 executed, 4 passed, 0 unsupported; budget 0), then registered last in package.spiproj (box b1fff4fb5ec9; mirror after org2-nb6d5 settles). Covers total_bool_literal_replacement (true,false tensor to false,false, size 3 kept), conditional_bool_literal_replacement (guard and both branches to false, size 4 kept), bool_negation_involution (nested 5-node tensor, once flips every literal, twice restores the literal list, size kept) plus negation leaving a conditional unchanged as in the sample. Slice 1 (tibia, open substitution application cases, handoff-1 efb88cc2cb03) is gating in-package as org2-nb6d5. Claims: org2 the weakened family (8), tibia nested/application lambda substitution (3). Next step: org2 drafts the weakened family notebook.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 4u32, "2026-11-10T06:14Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 3 (weakened family, all 8) drafted as apps/kernel/src/linear_weakened.spi 6b23f940dfe6 (budget 0), queued as ganymede gate org2-lw after org2-nb6d5. 3a: unit_bool_closed_tensor (two variables over Unit,Bool, merge LeftOnly then RightOnly, closed by all_used: slots 1,0, size 3), unit_bool_weakened_tensor (weaken both under a new Unit head, Neither step: slots 2,1), bool_application_weakened (function,argument slots 1,2). 3b: a typed outer_plan (OuterSame/OuterMore, each step adds one unused outer cell) applied to the identity's all_unused proof: weakened_identity_lambda (slot 0, 1 unused), two_step (0, 2), arbitrary_outer_lambda (a 2-step plan weakens like two steps), outer_weakening_composition (compose = plan concatenation; direct equals sequential), outer_weakening_associativity (both bracketings of three plans give 3 steps and 3 unused cells). Next step: after org2-lw is green, org2 registers linear_weakened after linear_bool_literals.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_5 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 5u32, "2026-11-10T06:15Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:1x tibia: LAMBDA-SUBSTITUTION SLICE GREEN as a NEW module drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE\\handoff-lambda-1\\linear_lambda_substitution.spi (sha b0e2443dda14, FROZEN; opens linear_reduction, so register it after linear_reduction). Covers nested_lambda_substitution (main.spi:3194), application_lambda_substitution (3414) and application_lambda_substitution_preservation (3571). The sample's source and target terms are built exactly: nested (lambda x. lambda y. (x, y)) () to lambda y. ((), y); application (lambda f. lambda b. f b) (lambda z. z) to lambda b. (id' b), where id' is the identity weakened under b. older_var/newer_var/both_merge are generic over the two cell types, so both cases share them. Tests 3, all the sample's own runtime numbers (3179, 3396, 3555), held on the first run: nested tags 1 to 6, sizes 7 to 4; application 1 to 6, 8 to 5, body an Apply (tag 1) of size 4; both shrink by exactly 3. Preservation's closed-source and closed-target conditions hold by construction (both endpoints are typed closed). Gate (ganymede job tibia-lam1): --check rc 0, 3/3, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Next step: after org2 applies it, tick 3194/3414/3571 off the note-5 map.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_6 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 6u32, "2026-11-10T06:16Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 06:2xZ claim map, settled with tibia. org2: bool slice (3, linear_bool_literals, landed), weakened family (8) + all_membership_spine (linear_weakened 6e0d14d46892, gating as org2-lw). tibia: open substitution application cases (linear_open_substitution handoff-1 efb88cc2cb03, gating as org2-nb6d5), nested/application lambda substitution + preservation (linear_lambda_substitution b0e2443dda14, gating as org2-lw, registers after linear_reduction), and porting closed_recursive_beta_conditional, shared_argument_counterexample, bool_application_atomic_congruence, conditional_guard_preservation, reduction_preservation. Already asserted in 6C handoff-3 linear_closed_reduction: nonidentity_lambda_canonicity (lambda_values_keep_their_body_shapes, the_identity_body_is_a_variable_at_a_composite_type), atomic_tensor_beta_progress (a_ready_tail_steps_to_the_pair). Next step: after tibia's last five land, org2 runs the SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT final accounting.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_7 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 7u32, "2026-11-10T06:17Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 applied tibia's slice 1 on the box: apps/kernel/src/linear_open_substitution.spi efb88cc2cb03 (over 03168a15b021, same registration spot); in-package gate org2-nb6d5 6/6 executed, 0 unsupported. Mirror package.spiproj synced to the box (b1fff4fb5ec9, includes linear_bool_literals).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_8 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 8u32, "2026-11-10T06:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 landed on the box after unregistered in-package gates (job org2-lw): apps/kernel/src/linear_weakened.spi 6e0d14d46892 (9 discovered, 9 executed, 9 passed: the 8 weakened-family terminals plus all_membership_spine) registered after linear_bool_literals; tibia's linear_lambda_substitution.spi b0e2443dda14 (3/3 executed) registered right after linear_reduction. package.spiproj 8d3b4002e990 on box and mirror. Covered now: 16 of the 20 note-5 entries plus the 2 already asserted in 6C. Left: tibia's five ports in progress. Next step: after those land, org2 runs one consolidation gate of every kernel notebook against the full package order (the --check misses package-order reds), then the SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT final accounting. Correction to the count above: note 5 lists 24 entries; 17 now have kernel tests (open substitution application 2, weakened 8, bool 3, lambda substitution 3, membership spine 1) plus 2 already asserted in 6C = 19 of 24, and tibia's five ports are the rest.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_9 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 9u32, "2026-11-10T06:22Z", "tibia", "11-10 02:2x tibia: THE LAST FIVE note-5 TERMINALS GREEN in drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION\\handoff-open-3\\linear_general_reduction.spi (sha 00d81b745b06, FROZEN; the box's 7cdf1a962199 plus additions only, same position). Covers closed_recursive_beta_conditional (main.spi:8447: ApplyIdentity over IfTrue over Bound, an Application on both ends, 10 to 7); shared_argument_counterexample (8469: IfTrueRightApply over Bound, Application to Conditional, 10 to 7); bool_application_atomic_congruence (8592: identity and conditional steps in function and argument position, all four with an Application on both ends; sizes 7/4, 7/4, 8/4, 7/4); conditional_guard_preservation (2241: a guard step keeps a Conditional, 7 to 4); reduction_preservation (8745: the five open betas preserve their typed target shapes, Variable 0, Tensor 5, Apply 1, Lambda 6, If 7). Tests 12 (5 + 7), all pre-registered and all held on the first run. Gate (ganymede job tibia-gen4): --check rc 0, 12/12, 0 unsupported, budget 0. Also counted as already-tested in NB-6C handoff-3 (on the box): nonidentity_lambda_canonicity (lambda_values_keep_their_body_shapes, the_identity_body_is_a_variable_at_a_composite_type) and atomic_tensor_beta_progress (a_ready_tail_steps_to_the_pair). With this, all seven reduction-family note-5 terminals org2 handed tibia are accounted for. Next step: after org2 applies handoff-open-3, tibia's NB-7 share is done.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_7_terminal_coverage_10 () = Note ("SPS-NB-7-TERMINAL-COVERAGE", 10u32, "2026-11-10T06:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: consolidation gate org2-kall2 on ganymede (pack79, mirror = box by hash-diff after syncing export.spi and lean.spi) ran every kernel linear_* notebook in package order: 119 discovered, 119 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported (types 2, terms 4, renaming 2, substitution 2, strengthening 2, variable_strengthening 2, reduction 17, lambda_substitution 3, term_strengthening 3, open_substitution 6, values 2, open_betas 10, closed_reduction 13, general_reduction 12, bool_normalization 26, bool_literals 4, weakened 9). It included tibia's last five ports (linear_general_reduction handoff-open-3 00d81b745b06, now on the box). All 24 note-5 entries have kernel cells (22 in NB-7 slices, 2 already in 6C).")
inl fiscal_cfdi_moneda_window () = Task ("FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", "fiscal: a CFDI line picks its Anexo 20 window from its Moneda code, and codes without ISO minor units get no window instead of a guessed 2 places", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES", "fiscal,mx,cfdi,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_cfdi_moneda_window () = Planning ("FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_moneda_window_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", 1u32, "2026-11-10T05:53Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Payoff of FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES' decision union: CFDI 4.0 rounds line amounts to the decimals of the currency in Moneda (c_Moneda, 183 codes; 27 lack ISO minor units: 13 N.A. metals/funds/test codes, 12 withdrawn, CNH and ESD not ISO). DoD: moneda_window = WindowFor (families::amount_window families::mexico) | NoWindow minor_unit, cfdi_window_for (moneda : string) built on minor_unit_of; tests MXN gives 29.93 to 30.07 for 3 x 10.00, JPY (0 places) gives a whole-unit window, XAU gives NoWindow NoMinorUnit, HRK gives NoWindow (Withdrawn 2023-01), CNH gives NoWindow NotIso. Next step: draft the block beside the currency draft and splice it after the currency gate's verdict. Uses: a GADT-indexed window carried in a decision union.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_moneda_window_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:09Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:2x BLOCK DRAFTED: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW\\moneda-block.spi.txt, to splice into currency.spi after its gate. moneda_window = WindowFor (families::amount_window families::mexico) | NoWindow minor_unit; cfdi_window_for moneda cantidad valor builds CfdiLine { importe = ISO places of the Moneda; cantidad; valor }, so the written decimals of Cantidad and ValorUnitario are explicit parameters (deliberately NOT read from decimal::scale, because decimal::parse normalizes 3.00 to scale 0, the bug class FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS fixes); moneda_bounds returns option amount_pair. Tests: MXN 3.00 x 10.00 gives 29.93 to 30.07; JPY 3 x 1000 (0 decimals each) gives 2498 to 3502 (2.5 x 999.5 floor, 3.5 x 1000.5 ceil); XAU NoWindow NoMinorUnit, HRK NoWindow (Withdrawn 2023-01), CNH NoWindow NotIso. Every cell under 271 by the oracle (largest 265). Next step: splice after the currency + own-decimals box gate is green, recheck budget and round trip, gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_moneda_window_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", 3u32, "2026-11-10T06:36Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:4x SPLICED over the now-live currency.spi E7867E9F: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW\\currency.spi 1E226E7A (moneda_window, cfdi_window_for, amount_pair, moneda_bounds and 5 tests); cell budget 0 over (live 0), lib_roundtrip canonical. Box gate of currency queued (starts under 80% box load, pinned core, memo off). Next step: record the gate's verdict; on green, land currency.spi and close.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_moneda_window_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", 4u32, "2026-11-10T06:53Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:5x PROVEN AND LANDED. box gate 02:46-02:53 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib): currency.spi 1E226E7A GREEN 12/12 (the 7 currency tests plus a_peso_line_window_comes_from_its_moneda, a_yen_line_window_is_in_whole_yen, a_metal_code_gets_no_window, a_withdrawn_code_gets_no_window, a_code_outside_iso_gets_no_window). Copied over live E7867E9F (unstaged); undo in C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW\\undo-20261110-025337. A CFDI line now picks its Anexo 20 window from its Moneda, and codes without ISO minor units get NoWindow with the reason. Next step: none; Done.")
inl fiscal_cfdi_window_own_decimals () = Task ("FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS", "fiscal: the CFDI line window takes each factor's half unit from its own written decimals (NumDecimalesCantidad, NumDecimalesValorUnitario), not the currency's", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "fiscal,mx,cfdi,correctness,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_cfdi_window_own_decimals () = Planning ("FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_window_own_decimals_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T05:54Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "CORRECTION to the landed FISCAL-REGIME-PHANTOMS-UNIFY window (families.spi 12F8BF31, cfdi_low/cfdi_high): SAT's Anexo 20 v4.0 additional validations give lower = (Cantidad - 10^-NumDecimalesCantidad/2) * (ValorUnitario - 10^-NumDecimalesValorUnitario/2) truncated to the Importe's decimals, upper = the same with + (and -10^-12) rounded up (gncys.com transcription of the SAT validations; ValidaCFD thread on the SAT example; error CFDI40169). The landed code uses the CURRENCY places for both halves, which is right only when Cantidad and ValorUnitario are written with the currency's decimals (its test, 3.00 x 10.00 MXN, is such a case). lib decimal normalizes 3.00 to {3, scale 0}, so the written counts cannot come from the parsed values and must travel with the window. DoD: CfdiLine carries cfdi_decimals { importe; cantidad; valor }; cfdi_line places is the all-equal shorthand; a test where Cantidad is written '3' (0 decimals) x 10.00 at MXN gives 24.98 to 35.02. Next step: draft families.spi over 12F8BF31 and splice it with the currency draft after the currency gate's verdict.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_window_own_decimals_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:03Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:1x DRAFT drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS\\families.spi 33AF4D84 + lifecycle.spi BB993E13 over live 12F8BF31 / 76449093: cfdi_decimals { importe; cantidad; valor } carried by CfdiLine; cfdi_low/cfdi_high take each factor's half unit from its own decimals and round to importe's; cfdi_line places is the all-equal shorthand used by the existing tests and the lifecycle negative; new test a_cfdi_window_uses_each_factors_decimals over the quantity_without_decimals fixture (3 written with 0 decimals x 10.00 at MXN: 24.98 to 35.02, checked by hand: 2.5 x 9.995 = 24.9875 floor, 3.5 x 10.005 = 35.0175 ceil). Cell budget families 34 -> 34, lifecycle 13 -> 13; lib_roundtrip canonical. The SAT -10^-12 upper term stays a documented deviation. The currency draft's peso_window must switch to families::cfdi_line. Next step: after the running currency + SUNAT box gate reports, splice the cfdi_line rename into currency and gate families + lifecycle + currency together.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_window_own_decimals_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T06:10Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:2x GATE QUEUED: the box gate of currency + families + lifecycle (own-decimals drafts overlaid: families 33AF4D84, lifecycle BB993E13, currency E7867E9F with peso_window on families::cfdi_line) runs once the box is under 80% load, in the same run as FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES. Next step: record that run's verdict; on green, land families + lifecycle + currency together.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_window_own_decimals_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-WINDOW-OWN-DECIMALS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T06:35Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:3x PROVEN AND LANDED. box gate 11-10 02:23-02:34 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib): families.spi 33AF4D84 GREEN 11/11, lifecycle.spi BB993E13 GREEN 16/16, currency.spi E7867E9F GREEN 7/7. LANDED copy-only into C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\src (unstaged, never committed) after the live bases matched (families 12F8BF31, lifecycle 76449093, currency absent); undo in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CURRENCY-PLACES\\undo-20261110-023433 (currency.spi is new, so its undo is deleting it). the CFDI line window now takes each factor's half unit from its own written decimals (cfdi_decimals { importe; cantidad; valor }); a 3 written with 0 decimals x 10.00 at MXN gives 24.98 to 35.02, per SAT's Anexo 20 validation. Next step: none; Done.")
inl lib_land_executed_cells () = Task ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", "lib_land_window: a close must EXECUTE the landed module's cells (executed == discovered), not just type them", TaskKind, P1, D2, 70u32, Active, "", "cells,lib-land,gates,heal,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_land_executed_cells () = Planning ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_1 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T06:07Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "From tibia's GATE-HEALS-1101 finding (11-10 05:02Z): a lib_land_window close could be green without running one assertion of the landed module (type_probe only types the tests; document_test runs the lib's doc tests, not the module's cells). org2 compensates by hand in every proof job. DoD: the close requires, for every landed .spi, run_notebook --gate with executed == discovered, failed 0, unsupported 0, else CLOSE FAILED and undo; the ProvenLog path checks the proof's executed_cells lines; a false all-red from gating a lib file directly (testing unbound) fails closed with a hint naming the app-package probe. Next step: prove it on a node inside the LIB-CLONE-HEALS -PrivateLib proof.")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_2 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:08Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 02:0x: IMPLEMENTED (box tree, unstaged; lib_land_window.ps1 sha 52d0c770a023, parse 0): new Get-ExecutedVerdict reads run_notebook's spiral-tests total and requires executed == discovered, failed 0, unsupported 0; a new === executed_cells section runs after type_probe for every landed .spi (the same $probe list), prints one executed_cells line per file into the proof log, and a miss sets CLOSE FAILED and undoes the land. On the ProvenLog path it echoes the proof's executed_cells lines, or says the proof predates the check (no failure, so lands in flight keep working). Local unit check of the verdict on four outputs: green passes; typed-not-run (executed 0 of 11) fails; the false all-red (testing unbound) fails with the app-package-probe hint; no totals fails with the gate exit. The new script is swapped into the europa proof tree (/home/remote/libland-1110), so the pending LIB-CLONE-HEALS -PrivateLib proof (x-libland-clone-proof, poller) runs the new check on f32_grads.spi and xml.spi. Next step: read executed_cells in that proof log; if both lines are green and LANDED, the heal is proven.")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_3 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:08Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 03:1x FIRST REAL RUN (box -PrivateLib proof for LIB-CLONE-HEALS, job-1794291471630-x-libland-proof-box): document_test ran, type_probe passed 2/2, then executed_cells f32_grads.spi gave discovered 13, executed 13, FAILED 13, testing unbound. That is exactly tibia's predicted false all-red: a lib file gated directly cannot open testing. As first written, the check would therefore FAIL every land of such a module, a false block. My edit sits unstaged in the shared box tree and org2 had a box land running with it, so I warned org2 at once. INTERIM FIX (parse 0; verdict cases rechecked): that exact signature is now UNMEASURED, printed loudly, and does not fail the close (the close falls back to type_probe alone, the pre-change guarantee); a real red (failed > 0 without the signature) and typed-not-run (executed < discovered) still fail closed. So the heal currently catches modules that gate directly and must still grow the probe path for the rest. Next step: generate the realworld probe in a scratch app package (spiral.toml with the lib package; a module that opens testing and the landed module, plus a verbatim copy of its :# blocks with their ///> lines), run run_notebook --gate on THAT, and require executed == discovered there; prove it on f32_grads (13 cells).")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_4 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:33Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 03:4x PROBE PATH IMPLEMENTED (box tree, unstaged; parse 0). Why direct gating is a false red: a lib module can open only modules declared before it in the lib package, so f32_grads's own static :< testing is unbound when the file is gated as a lib notebook; inside an APP package that depends on the whole lib, testing resolves. New New-ExecutedProbe: for each landed .spi it writes a scratch app package under the land's undo dir (executed-probes/<name>/spiral.toml with packageDir = the lib's parent, packages = [|core-, <lib>-], one module) holding a VERBATIM copy of the landed file, with a ///- --package . --timeout 900000 header and its first static block renamed to the probe module's name (as apps/realworld names its own). executed_cells now gates that probe, so the cells run against exactly the landed text. The UNMEASURED fallback stays for a probe that still shows testing unbound. Checked offline: probes generate correctly for f32_grads.spi (482 -> 483 lines, header + renamed static) and sm'.spi (the quote sanitized to _q). Not yet gated: the running box proof (x-libland-proof-box2) started before this edit and still uses direct gating. Next step: gate one probe for real (f32_grads, 13 cells, expect executed 13 failed 0) as a node job, then the next land proof uses the probe path end to end.")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_5 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 5u32, "2026-11-10T07:34Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 03:4x: real probe gate staged on europa (/home/remote/stage/probe-gate.sh: the same probe shape, built with europa paths, for f32_grads.spi = base 530275b20359, then run_notebook --gate on it), label x-probe-gate; europa admission refuses it for now (MemAvailable 1804 < 2036), and a box poller retries every 5 min. Next step: after x-probe-gate settles, expect discovered 13, executed 13, failed 0; that proves the probe path the next land proof uses.")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_6 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 6u32, "2026-11-10T08:04Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:0x PROBE PATH DROPPED, lib_gate.ps1 used instead (box tree, unstaged; lib_land_window.ps1 sha 6267D60A5DC5, parse 0). The europa probe gate (job-1794297616927-x-probe-gate) also went 13/13 red, with a different error: FatalError: The return type of main in the C backend should be a 32-bit int. So neither a bare run_notebook --gate nor an app-package probe sets up a lib module's cells correctly. lib_gate.ps1 does (it ran f32_grads.spi green in last night's moon lib-clones gate): it gates the lib file directly but first sets SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR to the real core package, SPIRAL_CC on Windows, memo off, plus an isolated build path and compiler port for lib copies. That missing setup most likely explains tibia's testing-unbound false red too. executed_cells now runs lib_gate.ps1 -File <rel> -Lib $Lib -RawOut <undo>/executed-cells/<rel>.raw.txt per landed .spi and reads spiral-tests total from the raw file (executed == discovered, failed 0, unsupported 0); New-ExecutedProbe is removed; the UNMEASURED fallback stays for a testing-unbound signature. Next step: the next -PrivateLib land proof (LIB-CLONE-HEALS re-proof) exercises this path; expect executed_cells f32_grads 13/13 and xml 17/17 green.")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_7 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 7u32, "2026-11-10T09:17Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:3x BASELINE COMPARE added (spiral/apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1, unstaged, parse 0): executed_cells now treats reds the way type_probe already does ($baseFail): only NEW reds block. Why: the LIB-CLONE-HEALS re-proof closed red on xml.spi code_points_step_through_utf8@pascal, a cell its one-line rename cannot reach, and the count moved between identical runs (3 then 1), so a fail-closed guard with no baseline would block every lanes xml.spi land on a defect that already exists. HOW: Get-FailedPairs reads the spiral-tests file line into test@target pairs (failed_targets, plus failed_tests with no target as test@all); Compare-ExecutedBase runs ONLY on a red with executed == discovered and unsupported 0: it holds the landed file aside, puts the undo copy back, runs lib_gate.ps1 on it to <raw>.base.txt, restores the landed bytes in a finally, and passes when every red pair is red on the base too (\"every red is red on the base too: ...\"), else fails naming the NEW reds. Green runs cost nothing extra; UNMEASURED (testing unbound) stays as it was. Checked: Get-FailedPairs on the real raw file gives code_points_step_through_utf8@pascal; a fixture gives a@rust | a@pascal | b@all; no line gives 0. NEXT STEP: read the xml control (box job-1794302047845); then re-prove LIB-CLONE-HEALS with this script.")
inl note_of_lib_land_executed_cells_8 () = Note ("LIB-LAND-EXECUTED-CELLS", 8u32, "2026-11-10T09:20Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:3x CONTROL CONFIRMS the hypothesis: live xml.spi FCE8DD3E560D fails the same cell under the same gate (code_points_step_through_utf8@pascal, builder exit 8192; filed as LIB-XML-PASCAL-CODE-POINTS for team lib). Without the baseline compare, executed_cells would have blocked every xml.spi land on that existing red. Proof chain RESTARTED with the baseline-compare script: box job-1794302397769-x-libland-proof-chain2 (quiet box -> LIB-CLONE-HEALS -> XSD-FACET-BOUNDS). Expected: xml.spi 'every red is red on the base too: code_points_step_through_utf8@pascal' and a green close.")
inl spiral_ui_9_change_keyup () = Task ("SPIRAL-UI-9-CHANGE-KEYUP", "Spiral UI change and keyup events: a select reports its chosen value and a keyup reports its key, typed in ui_view and wired in ui_dom and ui_dom_ts", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral,ui,lib,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_ui_9_change_keyup () = Planning ("SPIRAL-UI-9-CHANGE-KEYUP", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_ui_9_change_keyup_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-9-CHANGE-KEYUP", 1u32, "2026-11-10T06:19Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 06:2xZ measured dice/ui leptos events (git grep on:): click 5, change 4, keyup 2; the stack has click and input. DoD: ui_view gains a change view over a select (signal of the chosen option value) and a keyup handler (key name to graph update); ui_dom emits ListenChange and ListenKey ops and dispatches them like type_in; ui_dom_ts wires change and keyup listeners; rust and typescript cells green with executed equal to discovered. Drafts stack on drafts/spiral/SPIRAL-UI-8-MOVES until that lands. Next step: org2 drafts the view and dom side.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_9_change_keyup_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-9-CHANGE-KEYUP", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:25Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 TYPEFEATURES: change and keyup are typed view cases Changed and KeyUp carrying string -> graph -> graph handlers; dom_op gains ListenChange and ListenKey, both registering into the existing typed inputs table so dispatch is type_in. Drafted at drafts/spiral/SPIRAL-UI-9 (ui_view, ui_dom, ui_dom_ts over the landed bee757f9f044 / aeaee461da41): op cell (select listened as handler 0 at node 3, keyup input as handler 2 at node 8, both patch the bound text and the input value) in rust and typescript, plus a fake-DOM cell (choose b, press Enter reach the bound text). Next step: org2 proves the drafts on the ganymede mirror after the kernel consolidation job.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_9_change_keyup_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-9-CHANGE-KEYUP", 3u32, "2026-11-10T06:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 proof status, NOT green yet: job org2-ui9 closed the private lib land green (digest 04D6B213A4654846) with ui_view 5/5 and ui_dom 7/7 executed (the new change/keyup op cell included), but ui_dom_ts reported 7 discovered, 0 executed, 7 unsupported. Each cell's reason (run_notebook --output-path) was that bun was not found. Root cause: org2's own detached Cells CompilerDaemon on ganymede, spawned by an earlier org2 job without SPIRAL_BUN, survived that job's stop and was reused (memory cells-daemon-env-from-first-job). Fix queued: once org2-ui8n and org2-kall2 finish, kill that daemon (org2's own, -pa org2-phys Cells) and rerun ui_view, ui_dom and ui_dom_ts (job org2-ui9ts2, SPIRAL_BUN + pinned compiler + SPIRAL_CELLS_SERVER=0). Nothing reaches the box until executed equals discovered.")
inl note_of_spiral_ui_9_change_keyup_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-UI-9-CHANGE-KEYUP", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:22Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: after org2's stale Cells daemon was killed, the isolated rerun org2-ui9ts2 (pinned compiler, SPIRAL_BUN, SPIRAL_CELLS_SERVER=0) executed every cell: ui_view 5/5, ui_dom 8/8, ui_dom_ts 7/7, 0 unsupported. Landed on the box copy-only from the org2-ui9 proof (lib digest 04D6B213A4654846): lib/spiral/ui_view.spi d51c1166c43d (Changed and KeyUp views, on_change and on_keyup), ui_dom.spi c8af752690fc (ListenChange and ListenKey into the typed inputs table), ui_dom_ts.spi d54b38823d34 (change and keyup listeners, fake-DOM choose and press). dice/ui's three event kinds (click, change, keyup) now all exist on the stack.")
inl fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window () = Task ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", "fiscal: every Concepto of the pinned stamped CFDI 4.0 falls in its Anexo 20 window, with decimals read from the attribute text", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-CFDI-MONEDA-WINDOW", "fiscal,mx,cfdi,corpus,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window () = Planning ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", 1u32, "2026-11-10T06:37Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Real-data check of the CFDI window: deps/corpus/mx/stamped/cfdiutils-cfdi40-valid.xml (Moneda MXN) has a Concepto with Cantidad='4' (0 decimals) x ValorUnitario='956.04' (2 decimals) and Importe='3824.15', while round2(4 x 956.04) = 3824.16, so a strict rounding check would REJECT this SAT-valid CFDI; the Anexo 20 window with each factor's own decimals ((3.5 x 956.035) floor to (4.5 x 956.045) ceil, about 3346.12 to 4302.20) accepts it. DoD: written_decimals from the attribute text (never decimal::scale, which parse normalizes), the concept read via sunat::child_named and xml::element_attributes, a test that the stamped concept is Within its window, and a contrast test that the strict round2 product differs from Importe. Next step: draft the block beside the Moneda draft and splice it after that gate's verdict. Uses: the moneda_window decision and the GADT-indexed amount_window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:39Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 02:5x BLOCK DRAFTED: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW\\stamped-block.spi.txt (appends to currency.spi after the Moneda block). written_decimals counts digits after the dot in the attribute TEXT; attribute_text/attribute_amount over xml::element_attributes; child_of chains sunat::child_named (Comprobante > Conceptos > Concepto); concept_window builds the window from the Moneda plus each factor's written decimals; billed_within checks Importe with families::window_check (peso_window alias). Tests: written decimals 0/2/6 from '4', '956.04', '1.500000'; the stamped concept (4 x 956.04 billed 3824.15, MXN) is Within; and the contrast: round2(4 x 956.04) = 3824.16 is NOT the billed 3824.15, so a strict rounding check would reject this SAT-valid CFDI. Every cell under 271 by the oracle (largest 264). Next step: splice after the Moneda gate's verdict, recheck budget and round trip, gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:08Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 03:1x box gate 02:58-03:06 local (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, currency.spi ADEF83E0): 14 of 15 passed, INCLUDING written_decimals_come_from_the_text, the_stamped_concept_falls_in_its_anexo_20_window and strict_rounding_would_reject_the_stamped_concept. The one red, offshore_yuan_is_not_an_iso_code (green in both earlier gates on unchanged code), is VOID, not a verdict: '** (Mix) ...currency.spi: port 13945 accepts connections but never answers the handshake (:timeout)', the Cells compiler server missing its handshake on a box at about 97% CPU. Re-gate started. Next step: record the re-gate; on green, land currency.spi ADEF83E0 and close.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:22Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 03:2x re-gate 03:08-03:17 local on the same draft ADEF83E0 with the box at 100%: 11 of 15 passed; reds sat_codes_iso_withdrew_carry_their_withdrawal, offshore_yuan_is_not_an_iso_code, a_code_outside_iso_gets_no_window, strict_rounding_would_reject_the_stamped_concept. The unit JSON records no per-test reasons, and the only error in currency.out.err is again 'port 13945 accepts connections but never answers the handshake (:timeout)'. The red SET changes between identical runs (run 1 only offshore_yuan), and every red test was green in the 02:23 and 02:46 gates, so this reads as Cells-server starvation on a saturated box, NOT a verdict on the code; not landing on that inference. Next step: re-gate when the box holds under 70% for 3 consecutive minutes; land only on a clean 15/15.")
inl note_of_fiscal_cfdi_stamped_window_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW", 5u32, "2026-11-10T08:39Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 04:4x PROVEN AND LANDED. box gate 04:31-04:39 local, started only after the box held under 70% for 3 consecutive minutes (pinned core F414863971EB2A2C, memo off, -NoGateCache, live lib): currency.spi ADEF83E0 GREEN 15/15 in 364 s, the SAME bytes that gave 14/15 and 11/15 with different reds on a saturated box, which confirms those were Cells handshake starvation, not the code. Copied over live 1E226E7A (unstaged); undo in C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CFDI-STAMPED-WINDOW\\undo-20261110-043931. The pinned stamped CFDI 4.0's Concepto (4 written with 0 decimals x 956.04, billed 3824.15, MXN) is Within its Anexo 20 window, while round2(4 x 956.04) = 3824.16 shows a strict rounding check would reject this SAT-valid CFDI. Next step: none; Done.")
inl cells_server_path_leak () = Task ("CELLS-SERVER-PATH-LEAK", "Cells server: requests resolve tools against the server starter's PATH (only SPIRAL_* is forwarded)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,server,toolchain,bug,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_server_path_leak () = Planning ("CELLS-SERVER-PATH-LEAK", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_server_path_leak_1 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-PATH-LEAK", 1u32, "2026-11-10T06:44Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "From org2 11-10 06:3xZ (ganymede org2-ui9: ui_dom_ts TS cells 7 unsupported, \"bun was not found\", while a Rust-only gate without SPIRAL_BUN ran at the same time). microblog code read of the box server.ex: accept is a SEQUENTIAL loop (accept, recv, run_request, send, close), so two requests cannot overlap and clobber each other's SPIRAL_* mid-run; the compiler daemon slot is keyed by the served DLL (served_dll_tag), so compiler pins do not cross requests either. The REAL leak: try_execute forwards only SPIRAL_* variables, so PATH (and every other variable) is the one the server's FIRST starter had. The server is one per user name, which on root nodes means one for every lane, so Toolchain's System.find_executable fallbacks (bun when SPIRAL_BUN is unset, python, lua, gleam ...) resolve against another lane's PATH. DoD: the client forwards PATH (Path on Windows) along with SPIRAL_*, run_request applies and restores it the same way, plus a test that PATH is forwarded and a non-forwarded name is not. Next step: patch server.ex and add the test.")
inl note_of_cells_server_path_leak_2 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-PATH-LEAK", 2u32, "2026-11-10T06:46Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 02:5x PATCHED (box tree, unstaged) + test GREEN on the box (Windows): server.ex gains forwarded?(name) = SPIRAL_* or PATH (any case, so Windows Path too), used both by try_execute (what the client sends) and run_request (what the server saves, applies and restores). Requests stay sequential, so applying and restoring PATH per request is safe. New test/spiral/cells/server_test.exs: forwards SPIRAL_BUN, SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL, PATH, Path; not HOME, MIX_ENV; Result 1 passed (24 s). Caveat for org2's exact case: when SPIRAL_BUN IS set, the forwarded env already carried it; if that rerun still said bun not found, check which Cells tree started the ganymede server (its source stamp must equal the client's, else the client runs locally). Next step: the change reaches nodes on the next mirror sync; org2 can then drop SPIRAL_CELLS_SERVER=0.")
inl note_of_cells_server_path_leak_3 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-PATH-LEAK", 3u32, "2026-11-10T09:03Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:1x DONE. LINUX proof: europa job-1794299368632-x-cells-linux-test exit 0 (box Cells lib/test/spi tar 2b363c70c9038a81 in my xcache tree, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, nice 10, pwsh present): memo_test, compiler_daemon_test, server_test, notebook_report_test, compiler_gate_pin_test = 99 passed, rc=0. server_test green on Linux as on the box. DoD met: server.ex forwarded?/1 takes SPIRAL_* plus PATH (any case, so Windows Path), run_request saves and restores it like the SPIRAL_ names, and server_test asserts SPIRAL_BUN, SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL, PATH and Path are forwarded while HOME and MIX_ENV are not. All unstaged.")
inl cells_daemon_env_match () = Task ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", "Cells compiler daemon: refuse or respawn when a client's SPIRAL_BUN / compiler pin differs from the daemon's starter", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,daemon,toolchain,bug,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_daemon_env_match () = Planning ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_daemon_env_match_1 () = Note ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", 1u32, "2026-11-10T06:56Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "From org2 11-10 06:5xZ, traced on ganymede: a detached Spiral.Cells.CompilerDaemon (beam, ppid 1), spawned by org2's first consolidation gate with NO SPIRAL_BUN and the installed compiler, outlived its job (kit job stop does not reach it) and was REUSED by every later org2 job, so their TS cells could not find bun and their compiler pins never applied. Code read (compiler_client.ex base_port): when SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_PORT is set the client uses that fixed port and never checks the daemon's compiler (served_dll_tag is checked only in build_slot_port, the unset-port path), and nothing compares SPIRAL_BUN at all. DoD: the daemon's banner carries the starter's identity (compiler DLL tag and the resolved bun path, and any other env that changes cell results); a client whose values differ refuses that daemon (one clear error line) or takes a fresh slot, on both the fixed-port and the slot paths; a test with two clients whose SPIRAL_BUN differ sees two daemons or one refusal, never a silent reuse. Next step: read CompilerDaemon's banner/handshake (banner_dll, pick_slot) and extend it with the bun tag.")
inl note_of_cells_daemon_env_match_2 () = Note ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:07Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 03:0x IMPLEMENTED (box tree, unstaged) + TESTED on the box. compiler_daemon.ex: the served tag now names the toolchain, served_dll_tag = served_compiler_tag (the old DLL-stamp tag) <> \"~\" <> tool_tag(resolved bun) (a phash2 of the path with slashes normalized, \"none\" when unresolved). The banner, pick_slot (slot path) and the new refusal use the combined tag; other_build? and the warm-port FILE keep the compiler-only tag, because run_notebook.ps1 computes that file name itself from the DLL stamps. compiler_client.ex ensure: same code stamp but a foreign tag -> {:error, \"the compiler daemon on port N was started with another toolchain (compiler or bun) than this client's; stop that daemon or set another SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_PORT\"}. It REFUSES rather than kills, because on a fixed port the daemon may be another lane's. On the slot path pick_slot already moves past a foreign tag to a fresh slot. New test: tool_tag is slash-insensitive, differs for another bun, \"none\" for nil, and served = compiler <> \"~\" <> bun. Runs of compiler_daemon_test.exs: first 26/29 (3 queue-time/stall timing tests timed out with the box at 100%), rerun 29/29 with the same code, so the 3 are load flakes, not this change. Gap left: the run_notebook.ps1 thin client sends only the DLL, so a thin-client request is checked for the compiler, not for bun. Next step: carry bun in the thin-client request (a \"bun\" field next to \"dll\" in notebook_reply), then a Linux run of the same file on a node.")
inl note_of_cells_daemon_env_match_3 () = Note ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:51Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:0x THIN-CLIENT GAP CLOSED (box tree, unstaged): run_notebook.ps1 now sends bun (SPIRAL_BUN, else the first bun on its PATH, else empty) next to dll in the notebook request; the daemon's notebook_reply answers stale (\"the daemon resolves another bun than this client\") when other_bun?/1 differs, exactly like the existing other compiler build check, so the thin client falls back instead of running TS cells without bun. An empty client value counts as no bun. tool_tag now lowercases on Windows: Elixir resolved bun as c:/Users/... while PowerShell's Get-Command gives C:\\Users\\..., which would otherwise flag every Windows request stale. Tests: compiler_daemon_test.exs 29/29 on the box (incl. case-insensitive tags on Windows, other_bun? false for the daemon's own bun and for nil, true for another path). Running now: one real thin-client gate on the box (digest.spi) to confirm matching resolutions produce no false stale line. Next step: read that run, then a Linux run of compiler_daemon_test on a node.")
inl note_of_cells_daemon_env_match_4 () = Note ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", 4u32, "2026-11-10T08:06Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:1x WINDOWS SPELLING CHECKED with the real paths on the box (mix run in the test build): PowerShell's Get-Command gives C:\\Users\\i574n\\.bun\\bin\\bun.exe, Elixir's Toolchain.bun gives c:/Users/i574n/.bun/bin/bun.exe, and other_bun? reads them as the SAME bun (false), so a matching thin client gets no false stale; an empty client value reads as different (stale -> local fallback), the conservative choice, since cell results should match the client's own env. The end-to-end thin-client gate (digest.spi) was stopped: it had blocked 25 min with no Elixir child (a build lock while the box proof compiled), and the direct check above answers the question. Next step: a Linux run of compiler_daemon_test.exs on a node, then done.")
inl note_of_cells_daemon_env_match_5 () = Note ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", 5u32, "2026-11-10T08:30Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:3x Linux run QUEUED: europa job-1794299368632-x-cells-linux-test (pending behind a peer rustc; nice 10, private MIX_BUILD_PATH) extracts the boxs whole Cells lib/test/spi (tar sha 2b363c70c9038a81, 170 entries) into my xcache tree and runs memo, compiler_daemon, server, notebook_report and compiler_gate_pin tests. Box: the same five files = 98/98 (server_test separately green earlier). NEXT STEP: read its Result line from the heartbeat (job list --on europa, never job wait).")
inl note_of_cells_daemon_env_match_6 () = Note ("CELLS-DAEMON-ENV-MATCH", 6u32, "2026-11-10T09:03Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:1x DONE. LINUX proof: europa job-1794299368632-x-cells-linux-test exit 0 (box Cells lib/test/spi tar 2b363c70c9038a81 in my xcache tree, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, nice 10, pwsh present): memo_test, compiler_daemon_test, server_test, notebook_report_test, compiler_gate_pin_test = 99 passed, rc=0. Box: compiler_daemon_test 30/30 (with the capability retry test). DoD met: the served tag = compiler tag ~ bun tag (slash- and case-insensitive on Windows); the slot path skips a foreign tag, the fixed port refuses one with a clear error, and the thin client gets 'stale' from a daemon that resolves another bun; the real Windows spellings were checked to match (no false stale). All unstaged.")
inl sps_nb_8_terminal_gaps () = Task ("SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS", "Kernel tests for the last 3 untested mega-sample terminals and tighter assertions for 10 weak ones (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT note 7)", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral,proofs,kernel,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_sps_nb_8_terminal_gaps () = Planning ("SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_sps_nb_8_terminal_gaps_1 () = Note ("SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T07:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 split from SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT note 7 (final accounting). DoD: new :# cells for all_used_usage_vector, context_indexed_lambda and indexed_variable_renaming_composition (a compose on renaming plans with direct = sequential), and tightened cells for the 10 WEAK rows so each asserts the terminal's own numbers or shapes; every kernel linear_* notebook green in package order with executed equal to discovered (consolidation gate, pinned compiler, SPIRAL_BUN). TYPEFEATURES: renaming composition as a typed plan concatenation like outer_plan compose in linear_weakened. Next step: org2 takes the 3 NONE rows first (renaming composition in linear_renaming; all_used vector and context-indexed lambda in linear_terms or a new notebook).")
inl note_of_sps_nb_8_terminal_gaps_2 () = Note ("SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:15Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 07:1xZ drafted its six rows into linear_weakened (scratch v3 c2f6f20a6e40, budget 0; opens linear_reduction and linear_open_substitution too). NONE to covered: all_used_usage_vector (usage_vector from a shape: used 3/3 bitmap 7, unused 3/0/0); context_indexed_lambda (indexed_at with Free and Lambda cases over the Unit,Bool shape; the lambdas at both cells sum to tags 2, slots 1, lengths 4, used 2, bitmap+resources 5, the sample's numbers); indexed_variable_renaming_composition (compose_renaming as plan concatenation; direct slot 3 = sequential slot 3, steps 3 = 1 + 2). WEAK to firm: conditional (if_tags 7, 3, 2, 2: outer, guard, both branches); identity_substitution (the closed Unit-Bool tensor keeps size 3 and tags 5, 2, 3); open substitution variable case (an OPEN Unit variable replacement: source slot 0, target slot 1). Gates: org2-lw2 (first three) running, org2-lw3 (all six) chained after it, both pinned with SPIRAL_BUN. tibia has the seven weak rows in its reduction modules. Next step: after org2-lw3 is green, org2 copies linear_weakened to the box and reruns the consolidation gate once tibia's superset lands.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_8_terminal_gaps_3 () = Note ("SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:16Z", "tibia", "11-10 03:1x tibia: the SEVEN WEAK ROWS in tibia's modules are now firm, in drafts\\spiral\\SPS-NB-6C-GENERAL-REDUCTION\\handoff-open-4\\linear_general_reduction.spi (sha 651f2aa12c8b, FROZEN; the box's 00d81b745b06 plus additions, and it now also opens linear_values). Each one's exact sample case is now a test: (1) tensor_right_general_congruence (main.spi:8553): the right child is a conditional step (False, if True then () else ()), 6 to 3, Tensor on both ends. (2) closed_recursive_beta_progress (9055), the shallow derivations: Bound(Unit) progress 4 to 1; IfFalseDistinct(Bound) opened (lambda 6, apply 1, 10 to 7); composed ApplyIdentity(IfFalseDistinct) opened (6, 1, 13 to 10); the bool LeftUnit(Bound True) authority: lambda 4, progress 6 to 3. (3) closed_composite_ready_beta (9612): the ready identity over the Unit-Bool pair source, relation 6, progress 6 to 3. (4) open_identity_beta_reduction (11216): the BOOL instance, built from linear_open_betas' generic id_body/here_slot/here_use by qualified name, tags (Apply 1, Variable 0), 4 to 1. (5) application-argument congruence at depth 2 and 3 (11314/11371) under the Unit to Unit-tensor-Unit tail lambda: depth 2 is 12 to 9, depth 3 is 15 to 12. (6)+(7) the trace's progress and endpoint projections: 13 to 10 both. Tests 21 (12 + 9), all pre-registered; gate (ganymede job tibia-gen7): --check rc 0, 21/21, 0 unsupported, budget 0. One fix on the way: value_term needed :< linear_values, since opens are not transitive through linear_closed_reduction. Next step: after org2 applies handoff-open-4, mark these seven rows firm in the parent's note-7 accounting.")
inl note_of_sps_nb_8_terminal_gaps_4 () = Note ("SPS-NB-8-TERMINAL-GAPS", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:51Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: consolidation gate org2-kall3 on ganymede (pinned pack79 copy, SPIRAL_BUN, SPIRAL_CELLS_SERVER=0) ran every kernel linear_* notebook in package order: 134 discovered, 134 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported. On the box (= mirror by hash): linear_general_reduction.spi 651f2aa12c8b (tibia's open-4, the seven weak rows: 21/21) and linear_weakened.spi b27a81536df8 (org2's six rows: the three untested terminals plus conditional tags, the identity-substitution tensor and the open variable replacement: 15/15). All 3 NONE and all 10 WEAK rows of SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT note 7 now assert the sample's own numbers or shapes.")
inl compiler_c_unit_main () = Task ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", "C backend: a main (or test entry) that returns unit runs and exits 0 instead of FatalError", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,c,codegen,cells,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_c_unit_main () = Planning ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_c_unit_main_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", 1u32, "2026-11-10T07:18Z", "compiler", "From tibia 11-10 (apps/map + linked apps/map_kinds): every ///> c test of a package that LINKS a unit fails with FatalError: The return type of main in the C backend should be a 32-bit int. Root cause (traced on ganymede, pack79): Cells compiles a linked package's tests in place through the compiler's test entry, whose value is unit (an _assert ends it), while a standalone notebook test goes through Cells' wrapper that appends 0i32; Rust accepts a unit main, C rejects anything but i32. Control: the same test in an UNLINKED package compiled with --test fails identically, so linking only changes which path Cells takes. Fix: codegenC emits a unit main body as static void spiral_unit_main(void) plus int32_t main(){ spiral_unit_main(); return 0; }; any other non-i32 main keeps the error. TypeFeatures: none (codegen text). Next step: kitdo on pack79, build + gate on ganymede (repro + C rows of the suite).")
inl note_of_compiler_c_unit_main_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:22Z", "compiler", "11-10 03:2x compiler: program drafted at %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN/1-c-unit-main.kitdo (one replacement in codegenCs main match: a [||] arm that prints the body as static void spiral_unit_main(void) and int32_t main(){ spiral_unit_main(); return 0; }; the fallback message now says 32-bit int or unit). Candidate pack80 = pack79 + this program, core a29ccab1 (scratchpad p80). Gate RUNNING on ganymede (~/remote-stage/pack80/g.sh, log g.log): build; the varint test on C through --test in the linked unit (map_kinds) and the unlinked control (ctl_nolink) must compile, gcc-build and exit 0; a NEGATIVE control (expected value changed to 151) must exit nonzero, so a pass is not just an empty main; tibias mapc copy (1 c + 3 rust tests) through Cells with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL pinned to pack80; full suite diffed against pack79. Next step: read g.log when it says p80 done.")
inl note_of_compiler_c_unit_main_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:24Z", "compiler", "DoD: (1) a unit-valued main or test entry compiles on C and exits 0 (linked unit and unlinked control), (2) a failing assertion in such a test still exits nonzero (negative control), (3) tibias ///> c test of a linking package passes through Cells, (4) the full suite shows 0 diffs vs pack79. Next step: read the ganymede gate log.")
inl note_of_compiler_c_unit_main_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:33Z", "compiler", "11-10 03:3x compiler: pack80 gate on ganymede, DoD (1)-(3) MET, (4) PENDING. (1) varint test entry on C: linked unit map_kinds compile 0 / gcc 0 / exit 0 (run before tibias probe reset its apps dir); unlinked control (restaged in my own /root/compiler-pack80-probe) compile 0 / gcc 0 / exit 0. (2) NEGATIVE control, expected value changed to 151: exit 1, so the assertion runs inside spiral_unit_main. (3) tibias map package (links map_kinds, map_items, map_walk) with one test switched to ///> c, through Cells run_notebook --gate with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL pinned to pack80: discovered 4, passed 4, failed 0 (pack79: the c test FatalError). (4) full suite vs pack79 running (~/remote-stage/pack80/g.log). The first mapc gate run was void (tibias probe removed the scratch dirs mid-gate; restaged outside their tree).")
inl note_of_compiler_c_unit_main_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-C-UNIT-MAIN", 5u32, "2026-11-10T07:37Z", "compiler", "11-10 03:3x compiler: DoD (4) MET: pack80 full suite on ganymede vs pack79, rows 7610, compile/native/exit/stdout diffs 0, residual changed 0. All four DoD points met on the candidate. NOT installed yet: pack81 (= pack80 + FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET) is gating behind it and ships both; install Linux via install-pack -FromDir like pack79, Windows with the pending win-x64 build on moon. Next step: install pack81 when its gate is green, then close.")
