inl fsharp_export_dead_let () = Task ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", "F# backend: the binding behind an Export stays as a dead statement after the exports, so an exported main is not the last declaration (FS0433)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,fsharp,codegen,export,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fsharp_export_dead_let () = Planning ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_1 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 1u32, "2026-11-10T07:27Z", "compiler", "From org2 11-10 (dice/lib/dice.spi, ganymede pack79, job org2-dg4b): export \"rotate_numbers\" rotate_numbers' emits the right top-level let rotate_numbers (v0 : int64) ... = closure0 () v0, but the source binding remains as let v0 : (int64 -> (UH0 -> UH0)) = closure0() AFTER all exports; when main is also exported, [<EntryPoint>] let main is no longer the last declaration and dotnet publish fails with FS0433. Fix direction: DeadPureLetElision (or the F# export pass) drops a pure let whose only use is the Export op. TypeFeatures: none (codegen). Next step: reproduce with a two-export sample (one main) on the F# backend on a node, then the elision rule + an apps/compiler/tmp/samples regression sample.")
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_2 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:33Z", "compiler", "11-10 03:3x compiler: REPRODUCED on ganymede pack79 (2-line package: export \"double\" double in main): the fsx ends with let double ... = closure0 () v0 and then the dead let v0 : (int64 -> int64) = closure0(). FIX drafted at %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET/1-skip-export-only-closure-let.kitdo (2 replacements in codegenFsharp): export_only_closures = top-level Export targets minus every var any other top-level bind uses (DeadPureLetElision.markOp/markData, which count join-point args, applies and nested blocks; the lets own binding is not counted); binds then records closure_of_var for such a TyLet(v, JPClosure, no args) and emits nothing. Candidate pack81 = pack80 + this (core d79c9266). Gate queued on ganymede behind pack80 (~/remote-stage/pack81/g.sh): repro must show 0 dead lets; a guard sample whose closure is ALSO called must keep its let; dotnet fsi runs both; full suite vs pack80. TypeFeatures: none (codegen text). Next step: read pack81/g.log.")
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_3 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 3u32, "2026-11-10T07:33Z", "compiler", "DoD: (1) a closure whose only use is an Export emits no let in F# (repro shows 0 dead lets), (2) a closure also used elsewhere keeps its let (guard sample), (3) both fsx files run under dotnet fsi, (4) full suite 0 diffs vs pack80; then org2 can try export \"main\" for dice. Next step: read the pack81 gate log.")
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_4 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 4u32, "2026-11-10T07:50Z", "compiler", "11-10 03:5x compiler: pack81 gate on ganymede: build 0; repro (export only): 0 dead lets, dotnet fsi exit 0. GUARD corrected: the first guard (call double seed) was inlined by the evaluator, so it never used the closure; export refuses a runtime variable (needs a compile-time function and makes its own closure at the export site), so the only real shared-use risk is a later runtime value of the same function. Guard sample: export \"double\" double; := ~f = double; f seed. pack79 emits let v0 = closure0() (dead) + let v1 = closure1() (used by v1 v2); pack81 emits only v1 (kept, the runtime use gets its own closure var) and drops the dead v0; both run under fsi exit 0. DoD (1)-(3) met. (4) suite PENDING: the first suite run was void (g.sh had cdd into the probe dir, so pwsh could not find scripts/test.ps1 and printed usage, exit 64); rerunning from apps/compiler (~/remote-stage/pack81/s.log).")
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_5 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 5u32, "2026-11-10T07:56Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:0x compiler: REGRESSION SAMPLE apps/compiler/tmp/samples/fsharp_export_closure_shared_use (unstaged, core-only): !!!!Export of double plus a later runtime use (:= ~f = double; f seed) self-checked to 42, registered under Backends Fsharp (Rust turns an exporting program into a library crate without main, identical on pack79, so it cannot run natively there). pack81 F#: exit 0, keeps let v1 = closure1() (the used closure) and drops the export-only one. It guards the dangerous direction (eliding a USED let breaks the F# build); the dead-let direction is invisible under fsi, which the gates repro covers.")
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_6 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 6u32, "2026-11-10T09:23Z", "compiler", "11-10 05:2x compiler: DONE on Linux. pack81 suite: 0 compile/native/exit/stdout diffs, the 1 residual change is samples/zig_export_fn F# dropping exactly the dead let. Installed ganymede pack81 (09:13Z), europa pack82 (09:20Z). org2 can retry export \"main\" for dice on these nodes.")
inl note_of_fsharp_export_dead_let_7 () = Note ("FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET", 7u32, "2026-11-10T09:23Z", "compiler", "Evidence: pack81 repro 0 dead lets; guard (export plus a later runtime use) keeps let v1 = closure1() and runs under fsi; zig_export_fn F# diff is the single removed dead let; sample fsharp_export_closure_shared_use F# exit 0; installed ganymede pack81 Core f3552f75, europa pack82 Core c495bc57.")
