inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m1_2 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T07:57Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 04:1x SURVEY (fiscal took this from the help pool, then released it pending one owner decision). In apps/kernel/src the kebab strings (175 across 17 files: linear_reduction 45, linear_open_betas 30, linear_weakened 27, linear_terms 14 ...) are ALL constructor notes: the trailing string every derivation constructor carries (MergeStep (\\? (LeftOnly 'Unit-only-left', ..., 'older-cell')), SingleUseHere (..., 'argument-used-once'), BetaRelation (argument, 'bool-beta')). No function COMPUTES a kebab verdict (searched for match arms and ?> / |: branches returning a kebab literal: none), and readers mostly ignore the note (BetaRelation (argument, _)). Notes also flow across files (IdentityBeta's note feeds BetaRelation; IdentityBeta is built in linear_bool_normalization, linear_closed_reduction and linear_general_reduction), so retyping one widely-used note ripples. PROPOSAL for the pattern: BetaRelation's string is the one that names a RULE ('bool-beta', 'unit-beta'), so make it :| beta_rule = | IdentityRule | ... with the rule as a value the step can be checked against, and keep free-text notes elsewhere for now; or, if 'certificate' means something else (e.g. a verdict the oracle notebooks return), name it. Next step: org picks the target constructor; then the conversion is about 40 lines in linear_reduction plus its 3 tests.")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m1_3 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M1", 3u32, "2026-11-10T08:10Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: ganymede job org2-m1 (pinned, in-package): linear_terms 8/8 and linear_weakened 15/15 executed, 0 unsupported. Pattern: the kebab certificate strings carried by Closed and FullyUsed (closedness-is-carried-by-the-same-usage-index-as-the-term and so on) are now a typed union closure_reason (UsageIndexCarriesClosedness, AllUsedConsumesTheContext); closed_note/fully_used_note became closed_reason/fully_used_reason, and the tests assert the union cases. On the box (unstaged): apps/kernel/src/linear_terms.spi 3f5dee682161 (also carries the four SPS-NEGATIVES fails blocks; the close_nonempty one now uses the union so it fails for the usage reason only), linear_weakened.spi 3a5dc6dfe212. TYPEFEATURES: the verdict is a type, so a misspelled certificate is a compile error, not a passing string compare. M2 applies this to the remaining certificate strings.")
