inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m2_2 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M2", 2u32, "2026-11-10T08:13Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:1xZ census (kernel linear_* tests that assert a kebab string): 10 sites. 1 is a CERTIFICATE, linear_types one_plus_zero_is_one (asserted the proof notes one-plus-zero-is-one and zero-plus-right-preserves-the-exact-usage-index). Drafted: a typed add_rule (ZeroCase, SuccessorCase) with rule_of and add_steps, and the test now asserts (SuccessorCase, 1, ZeroCase); the unused add_label is gone (scratch 913da6a0c346, gating as org2-m2). 9 are PROVENANCE labels, kept with reason: linear_reduction asserts constant_note values (the-unit-argument, the-bool-argument, the-tensor-argument, the-packed-argument, the-bound-argument, the-if-argument, the-fork-argument) to show WHICH argument a beta step or derivation carries into its target; a tag or shape compare would let a wrong argument of the same type pass, so these labels are identity, not verdicts. Next step: after org2-m2 is green, org2 lands linear_types and closes M2.")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m2_3 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M2", 3u32, "2026-11-10T08:18Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE (org handed over the lease: take it), proof: ganymede job org2-m2 (pinned, in-package) linear_types 2/2 executed, 0 unsupported. On the box (unstaged): apps/kernel/src/linear_types.spi 913da6a0c346, with the typed add_rule (ZeroCase, SuccessorCase), rule_of and add_steps; the meta_add test asserts (SuccessorCase, 1, ZeroCase), and add_label is removed. Census closed: the only kebab certificate left in kernel tests was this one; the 9 linear_reduction provenance labels stay as free-text identity notes (agreed with org: type the strings that name a rule, keep the notes that name a value).")
