inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m3_2 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M3", 2u32, "2026-11-10T08:20Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:2xZ first slice drafted (linear_weakened scratch fe5e809ce008, budget 0): one prototype ? steps_of p : p -> i32 with instances for renaming (renaming_depth) and outer_plan (plan_steps), tested on three_steps (3), both_steps (2) and the composed renaming (3). It probes whether a prototype instance can head a multi-parameter GADT type, which the shared interface needs. Gating as ganymede org2-m3. Next step: if green, add instances for strengthen (removed_depth) and the term strengthening plan, then a shared source/target pair.")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m3_3 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M3", 3u32, "2026-11-10T08:38Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 08:4xZ two syntax findings for prototypes in a kernel .spi (recorded for the next slice): (1) the edition-3 short forms ? and + used in lib/doc_render are rejected here (Expected one of: inl, let, union, nominal, prototype, type, instance), so kernel notebooks write prototype steps_of p : p -> i32 and instance steps_of <type> ... = ...; (2) an instance must bind as many forall variables as its type's arity minus the prototype's (ETY-InstanceCoreVarsShouldMatchTheArityDifference), so renaming (7 indices) is instance steps_of renaming sc ss su tc ts tu d = ... and outer_plan (4) is instance steps_of outer_plan sc su tc tu = .... Retry gating as ganymede org2-m3c (scratch 9b4f0e8178eb).")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m3_4 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M3", 4u32, "2026-11-10T08:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 1 GREEN and on the box (ganymede org2-m3c, pinned, in-package: linear_weakened 16/16 executed, 0 unsupported): apps/kernel/src/linear_weakened.spi 9b4f0e8178eb declares prototype steps_of p : p -> i32 with instance steps_of renaming sc ss su tc ts tu d (renaming_depth) and instance steps_of outer_plan sc su tc tu (plan_steps); one cell dispatches steps_of over a three-step renaming (3), a two-step weakening plan (2) and a composed renaming (3). That's the first prototype in the kernel (census prototype > 0). Next step: org2 adds instances for strengthen (removed_depth) and the term-strengthening plan, then a shared source/target pair for the substitution plans.")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m3_5 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M3", 5u32, "2026-11-10T08:58Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 2 GREEN and on the box (ganymede org2-m3d, pinned, in-package: linear_weakened 16/16 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported): apps/kernel/src/linear_weakened.spi 46be56494079 imports linear_strengthening and adds instance steps_of strengthen sc su tc tu = removed_depth, so one prototype now spans renaming, outer_plan and strengthen; the test asserts (3,2,3,1). Box = mirror hash. Next step: slice 3 adds a substitution instance from linear_open_substitution, then the item closes")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m3_6 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M3", 6u32, "2026-11-10T09:08Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 3 GREEN and on the box (ganymede org2-m3e, pinned, in-package: linear_weakened 17/17 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported): apps/kernel/src/linear_weakened.spi b38208aa59f9 adds osub_steps (a mutual group over osub/ointro/oelim mirroring otarget: OVar 0, each descent 1 plus its sub-plans, a branch adds both arms) and instance steps_of osub c u v r y = osub_steps; the test asserts var_plan 0, arg_plan 1, lambda_plan 2, fun_plan 3. One prototype steps_of now spans renaming, outer_plan, strengthen and open substitution, which meets the DoD (prototypes for the shared renaming and substitution interface over the kernel modules). Box = mirror hash. Kernel finding: no if/max in the kernel edition, so a sum measure replaces a depth max")
inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m3_7 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M3", 7u32, "2026-11-10T09:09Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 correction to the previous note: the kernel edition does have a conditional (? c ?> a |: b, used by bool_of in linear_reduction); only an if keyword and a max helper are absent. The sum measure stands as chosen (a total count of descents), not as a workaround")
