inl note_of_sps_typefeatures_m4_7 () = Note ("SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M4", 7u32, "2026-11-10T09:47Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE: the False eliminator is GREEN under pack82 and on the box (ganymede org2-m4, pinned pack82, scratch copy of the kernel package with the box's proven modules: linear_values 5/5 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported). apps/kernel/src/linear_values.spi ef1e51a986b0: false_constant is a zero-arm match over constant c u false_type, false_leaf and false_absurd peel leaf_value and value with only their reachable arms, false_count : i32 and false_label : string both instantiate it, and the fails block the_false_eliminator_rejects_a_bool_value holds. The ganymede mirror copy follows once the negatives chain leaves the package")
inl cells_memo_silent_whole_keys () = Task ("CELLS-MEMO-SILENT-WHOLE-KEYS", "Cells memo: a failed --capabilities probe is cached for the whole Cells process (persistent_term []), so source bounds go :unavailable and every memo key silently switches to whole-source mode; those keys never match a healthy run's reached-block keys (best explanation for STORE-VERIFY-EVIDENCE's cold to warm 0/47 memo hits)", Story, P1, D3, 90u32, Active, "", "cells,memo,bug,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_memo_silent_whole_keys () = Planning ("CELLS-MEMO-SILENT-WHOLE-KEYS", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_memo_silent_whole_keys_1 () = Note ("CELLS-MEMO-SILENT-WHOLE-KEYS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T08:25Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 04:4x FOUND + FIXED (unstaged, box). CAUSE: CompilerDaemon.host_capabilities cached a FAILED dotnet --capabilities probe as [] in persistent_term for the life of the Cells process, so SourceBlocks.of_texts (and Manifest's resolve-manifest) returned :unavailable for every later notebook; Memo then keyed every step on the whole source (whole = bounds == :unavailable), and those keys can never meet a healthy run's reached-block keys. EVIDENCE on moon (read-only, job x-memo-kinds, its memo store classified by entry kind and local hour): during STORE-VERIFY-EVIDENCE's cold arm (11-09 19h-20h) 180 result entries and ZERO bounds entries were written; the warm arm (11-10 00h-02h) wrote 280 NEW bounds entries for the same unchanged sources. If the cold arm had had bounds they would already be stored, so it ran unbounded and wrote whole-mode keys: this explains the warm arm's 0/47 hits. FIX: compiler_daemon.ex caches the capability list only on exit 0 (a failure is retried on the next call); memo.ex gains whole_keys?/1; notebook.ex adds report field memo_keys=whole ONLY on a degraded run (healthy reports byte-identical). TESTS: new compiler_daemon_test 'a failed capabilities probe is retried...' is RED on the old code (left: [], right: [source-blocks, resolve-manifest]) and green on the fix; new memo_test 'a context without source bounds keys on whole sources...'; box memo + gate_pin + notebook_report + compiler_daemon = 98/98, no warnings. Next step: ships with the next Cells mirror sync, then a Linux run of the two touched test files.")
inl note_of_cells_memo_silent_whole_keys_2 () = Note ("CELLS-MEMO-SILENT-WHOLE-KEYS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T08:26Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "DoD: (1) a failed --capabilities probe is never cached (red-before/green-after test); (2) a run without source bounds says memo_keys=whole in its report; (3) both changes in the Cells mirror and green on Linux too (memo_test + compiler_daemon_test); (4) the next warm verify arm on moon shows memo_hits on its notebooks with no memo_keys=whole. TYPEFEATURES: none; this is Elixir in apps/cells, outside Spiral code. NEXT STEP: the next Cells mirror sync carries the 4 touched files (compiler_daemon.ex, memo.ex, notebook.ex, plus the two tests), then the Linux run.")
inl note_of_cells_memo_silent_whole_keys_3 () = Note ("CELLS-MEMO-SILENT-WHOLE-KEYS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T09:03Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 05:1x DoD (3) met. LINUX proof: europa job-1794299368632-x-cells-linux-test exit 0 (box Cells lib/test/spi tar 2b363c70c9038a81 in my xcache tree, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, nice 10, pwsh present): memo_test, compiler_daemon_test, server_test, notebook_report_test, compiler_gate_pin_test = 99 passed, rc=0. DoD (4) remains: the next warm verify arm on moon must show memo_hits with no memo_keys=whole.")
inl spiral_empty_match () = Task ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", "Spiral: a zero-arm match over a GADT value whose index no constructor can produce, so a typed False eliminator can be written", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral,compiler,typefeatureset,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_empty_match () = Planning ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 1u32, "2026-11-10T08:16Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10 filed for SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M4. Sample: drafts/spiral/SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH/empty_match_probe.spi (value ty with UnitValue at unit_ty and BoolValue at bool_ty; absurd (x : value false_ty) : t = ?= x ?| with no arms). Today (pack79, ganymede job org2-emp): Unexpected end of block past this token at the empty arm list, so the whole block is left out of its module. The mega sample hit the same wall and quarantined its no-closed-False eliminator. DoD: the parser accepts a match with zero arms; the type checker accepts it only when no union case's index unifies with the scrutinee type (absurd over value false_ty compiles, the same body over value unit_ty is a type error naming UnitValue); the zero-arm match lowers to an unreachable on every backend; a frontier sample with both cases. Next step: compiler decides whether a zero-arm match fits the parser and the case-refinement check.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 2u32, "2026-11-10T08:22Z", "tibia", "11-10 04:3x tibia (help pool, claimed; a code read of the box's vendored compiler at spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language, nothing edited). FEASIBLE, in three small pieces. (1) PARSER: BlockParsing.fs:1216, the match clauses parser is (optional bar >>. sepBy1 (root_pattern_when .>>. (skip_op '=>' >>. next)) bar). sepBy1 is exactly why ?= x ?| with no arms gives 'Unexpected end of block'; a zero-arm form needs sepBy for SpecMatch only, keeping sepBy1 for function so a bare 'function' stays an error. (2) TYPE CHECK: Infer.fs:1493, RawMatch(_,body,l) -> f body_var body; List.iter (match_clause (body_var,s)) l. With l = [] it adds NO constraint, so relaxing only the parser would make ANY scrutinee type-check (unsound). The emptiness check reuses PatUnbox's refinement (Infer.fs:1782-1797): take ho_index (visit_t body_var) to get the nominal; for each case, a non-GADT case means reachable; a GADT case runs gadt_extract scope v, then trial unify_gadt (Some links) r scrutinee specialized_constructor in a try; success means reachable, and the error names that case. Two cautions: dispose_gadt_links undoes only the TyVar links, while unify_gadt also binds TyMetavars permanently (Infer.fs:1155-1160), so the trial must run on a metavar-free scrutinee, either required by annotation (as in the sample's (x : value false_ty)) or with a metavar snapshot and restore; and a scrutinee that isn't a known nominal union is an error too. (3) LOWERING: Prepass.fs:980 folds the clauses over the seed EPatternMiss(EV id), so [] already lowers to EPatternMiss, and PartEval.fs:1238 turns that into a COMPILE-TIME 'Pattern miss' type error. That is fine when absurd is never reached during partial evaluation, but a dyn branch that PE does evaluate would fail the build, so the DoD's 'unreachable on every backend' needs a distinct node (or EPatternMiss on a dyn scrutinee emitting the backend's unreachable/abort, as the exhaustive-match fall-through near PartEval.fs:1314 avoids). TESTS for the DoD: absurd over value false_ty compiles; the same body over value unit_ty fails naming UnitValue; over value t (t a forall var) fails, since t could be unit_ty; and a dyn call site inside a runtime if compiles to unreachable. Next step: compiler decides on (1)-(3); I'm releasing the claim, since compiler changes ship in compiler's packs.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 3u32, "2026-11-10T08:26Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:3x compiler (claimed after tibia released; follows tibias note 2): program drafted at %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH/1-zero-arm-match.kitdo, candidate pack82 = pack81 + it (core ebcbc29b). (1) PARSER: the shared clauses parser takes allow_empty; match uses sepBy (zero arms ok), function keeps sepBy1 so a bare function stays an error. (2) INFER: a new RawMatch(r,body,[]) arm: the scrutinee must be a metavar-free nominal union (else ETY-EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion); every non-GADT case is reachable; every GADT case gets a TRIAL unify_gadt of the scrutinee against its specialized constructor (gadt_extract at scope+1) inside try, links disposed after; a case that unifies is reported as ETY-EmptyMatchReachableCase naming it. The metavar-free requirement is tibias caution: unify_gadt binds metavars permanently, so the trial only runs on an annotated scrutinee. (3) LOWERING unchanged for now (zero arms already fold to EPatternMiss); the gates absurd_dyn_closure probe measures what a runtime closure that reaches it does before deciding on a distinct unreachable node. Gate RUNNING on ganymede (~/remote-stage/pack82/g.log): probes absurd_false (must compile and run), absurd_unit (must name UnitValue), absurd_forall (value ty: must name a case), absurd_prim (i32: known-union error), function_empty (still a parse error), absurd_dyn_closure; full suite vs pack81. TypeFeatures: zero-arm match = typed False elimination over a GADT index no constructor produces.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 4u32, "2026-11-10T08:30Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:3x compiler: first pack82 probe run (core ebcbc29b): parser OK (only function_empty still fails to parse, as intended); absurd_unit named UnitValue, absurd_forall named both cases, absurd_prim gave EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion. BUG FOUND in my trial: unify_gadt does NOT throw on a mismatch, it catches its own InferTypeErrorException and appends to errors, so try/with saw every case as reachable and leaked the failed trials TermError (absurd_false wrongly named UnitValue). FIX: snapshot errors.Count, run the trial, unreachable iff the count grew, and RemoveRange the trials errors so nothing leaks. Candidate rebuilt as core 83df216b; the superseded gate was stopped by pid (its suite workers too) and restarted clean (~/remote-stage/pack82/g.log; first run kept as g1.log).")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 5u32, "2026-11-10T08:37Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:4x compiler: second probe run (core 83df216b) PASSED the type side: absurd_false compiles and runs (C and Rust exit 5 = mains value), absurd_unit names only UnitValue (1 EmptyMatch error, 0 leaked TermErrors), absurd_forall names both, absurd_prim gives EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion, function_empty still a parse error. absurd_dyn_closure confirmed tibias point (3): a runtime closure over value false_ty made PE evaluate the empty match and fail the build with Pattern miss. LOWERING added: inference records the matchs result type (annotations.Add, like RawMacro), and the fill pass rewrites a zero-arm RawMatch to RawOp(FailWith, [RawType(annot); \"unreachable: a match with no arms was reached\"]), which PE turns into TyFailwith at that type: a runtime abort on every backend, no new E node. The scrutinee is dropped, sound because the checker proved no value reaches it. Candidate core 57232a80; gate restarted (~/remote-stage/pack82/g.log).")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 6u32, "2026-11-10T08:41Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:5x compiler: pack82 (core 57232a80) probes ALL as intended on ganymede: absurd_false compiles, C/Rust exit 5; absurd_unit ETY-EmptyMatchReachableCase naming UnitValue only; absurd_forall names UnitValue and BoolValue; absurd_prim ETY-EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion; function_empty still a parse error; absurd_dyn_closure (a runtime closure over value false_ty) now COMPILES and runs, C/Rust exit 7, and the generated C carries the abort text \"unreachable: a match with no arms was reached\". DoD (1)-(3) met by probes; the frontier sample is next, the full suite vs pack81 is running.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 7u32, "2026-11-10T08:47Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:5x compiler: SAMPLES (unstaged) apps/compiler/tmp/samples/empty_match_false_eliminator (absurd over value false_ty plus a runtime closure reaching it plus a self-checked describe; Backends Fsharp,C,Rust; pack82: C exit 0, Rust exit 0) and empty_match_reachable_case_negative (ExpectedErrors: ETY-EmptyMatchReachableCase ... the UnitValue case of value can produce). EXISTING sample samples/empty_match_parse_error (zero arms over i32) used to expect the parse error; it is still an error, now ETY-EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion, so its expected text is updated in tests/matrix.psd1 (same id). SECOND GAP FOUND by the F# run: value false_ty specializes to a ZERO-CASE union, and the F# backend printed type [<Struct>] US0 = with no body (FS0547). Program 2-fsharp-empty-union.kitdo prints a zero-case union as US<n> = struct end / UH<n> = class end. Not named frontier_* because frontier samples always also run Pascal, and an empty union on Pascal (its case x.tag of with no arms) is unverified here (no fpc on ganymede). Final candidate core e0607258 (pack81 + program 1 + program 2); final gate queued behind the running one (~/remote-stage/pack82/g3.log): samples on C/Rust/F#, both negatives, suite vs pack81.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 8u32, "2026-11-10T08:50Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:5x compiler: first pack82 suite (core 57232a80) vs pack81: rows 7610, compile/native/exit/stdout diffs 0, residual changed 0; test.ps1 exit 1 from exactly ONE row, samples/empty_match_parse_error [C] WRONG-ERROR (the mirrors matrix still expected the old parse error; it now gets ETY-EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion as intended). Applied ONLY my own matrix rows to the ganymede mirror (expected text update, the new negative row, Backends rows for empty_match_false_eliminator / c_unit_main_self_check / fsharp_export_closure_shared_use; pre-edit copy at ~/remote-stage/pack82/matrix.psd1.before) plus those sample dirs, before the final gates suite starts, so the final gate exercises the new samples and expectations.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 9u32, "2026-11-10T08:51Z", "compiler", "11-10 04:5x compiler: FINAL candidate pack82 (core e0607258 = pack81 + programs 1 and 2) on ganymede: empty_match_false_eliminator compiles and exits 0 on C, Rust AND F# (the F# empty-union fix works: US<n> = struct end); empty_match_reachable_case_negative gives ETY-EmptyMatchReachableCase; empty_match_parse_error gives ETY-EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion. Full suite vs pack81 running (~/remote-stage/pack82/suite3.log). DoD (1)-(4) met on the candidate except the suite; install follows with the pack81 rollout.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 10u32, "2026-11-10T09:23Z", "compiler", "11-10 05:2x compiler: final gate GREEN (core e0607258: suite vs pack81 rows 7610, 0 compile/native/exit/stdout/residual diffs, test.ps1 exit 0, with the updated matrix rows on the mirror). Store: pack82 linux-x64 put. INSTALLED on europa from the store (09:20Z, 35 files 0 mismatches, smoke ok, Core c495bc57). ganymede: quiet-window loop running (~/remote-stage/inst82). Next step: ganymede installed, then close; Pascal tracked on PASCAL-EMPTY-UNION.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 11u32, "2026-11-10T09:27Z", "compiler", "11-10 05:3x compiler: org2s SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M4 (three zero-arm matches over constant / leaf_value / value at false_type, scrutinee annotated, c u forall-bound) waits on pack82 reaching GANYMEDE (org2 does not use europa). Rigid forall vars are fine for the checker (it rejects only metavars; TyVars go through the gadt links and are disposed). Next step on install: kit agile edit <root> SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M4 --wait --clear, then close this item.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 12u32, "2026-11-10T09:36Z", "compiler", "11-10 05:3x compiler: DONE on Linux. pack82 INSTALLED on ganymede (09:35Z, install-pack -FromDir after the quiet-window loop, 35 files 0 mismatches, smoke ok, Core c495bc57) and europa (09:20Z from the store, same Core). DoD: (1) parser accepts zero arms for match only; (2) the checker accepts them only when no cases index unifies (absurd over value false_ty compiles; over value unit_ty names UnitValue; over value ty names both); (3) lowering is a runtime abort at the matchs type on every backend (C, Rust, F# run; Pascal tracked on PASCAL-EMPTY-UNION); (4) samples empty_match_false_eliminator + empty_match_reachable_case_negative (not frontier_* because frontier always includes Pascal). Org2s SPS-TYPEFEATURES-M4 wait cleared. Windows follows with the win-x64 build.")
inl note_of_spiral_empty_match_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-EMPTY-MATCH", 13u32, "2026-11-10T09:38Z", "compiler", "Evidence: pack82 final gate on ganymede (core e0607258): probes absurd_false C/Rust exit 5, absurd_unit names UnitValue only, absurd_forall names both, absurd_prim EmptyMatchNeedsKnownUnion, function_empty still a parse error, absurd_dyn_closure C/Rust exit 7 with the abort text in main.c; samples C/Rust/F# exit 0 and both negatives give their exact codes; suite 7610 rows 0 diffs vs pack81, exit 0; installed ganymede + europa Core c495bc57.")
