inl note_of_sps_open_typed_substitution_1 () = Note ("SPS-OPEN-TYPED-SUBSTITUTION", 1u32, "2026-11-10T09:55Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 filed from SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS: about 13 of the 89 negatives (the *_choice_substitution_keeps_used family, recursive_closed_bool_substitution_keeps_used, recursive_open_bool_*, recursive_open_typed_*, application_argument_function_branch_mismatch, closed_bool_*_right_beta_result_mismatch) are rejected in the mega sample as exact_linear_indexed_recursive_open_typed_substitution mismatches, and the kernel's osub (linear_open_substitution) has no recursive typed variant. DoD: a recursive open typed substitution union beside osub, with source/target functions and at least one positive cell green, then the listed negatives as fails blocks beside it. Next step: read negative_choice_substitution_keeps_used and negative_recursive_open_typed_substitution_type_mismatch in apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency, and draft the union in a new kernel module after linear_open_substitution")
inl note_of_sps_open_typed_substitution_2 () = Note ("SPS-OPEN-TYPED-SUBSTITUTION", 2u32, "2026-11-10T09:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 finding after reading the sources: the mega sample's ExactLinearIndexedRecursiveOpenTypedSubstitutionVariable packs exactly what the kernel's OVar packs (membership, single_use, selected, replacement term, note), so osub in linear_open_substitution already is the open typed substitution, not a missing witness. The choice negatives assert a valid two-cell plan with target usage = source usage; linear_weakened's open_var_plan (context unit_unit) is that two-cell plan. Scope narrows to: map these negatives onto osub fixtures, adding two-cell tensor/application plans where a negative needs them. First slice drafting now: choice_substitution_keeps_used and recursive_open_typed_substitution_type_mismatch beside open_var_plan")
