inl note_of_sps_open_typed_substitution_8 () = Note ("SPS-OPEN-TYPED-SUBSTITUTION", 8u32, "2026-11-10T11:27Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 5 first try was RED in its scratch package (ETY-ExistsShouldntHaveMetavars in nest3 / ub_pick: unannotated helpers left metavariables inside \\? packs); fixed by annotating every helper (slot1/slot2 aliases, ub_use/ub_pick/ub_older/ub_member/ub_repl, concretely typed lambda_src/lambda_tgt merges) and re-gating together with slice 6 as org2-ots6b. Slice 6: a_right_choice_keeps_its_pair_result = closed_bool_right_beta_result_mismatch (+ closed_bool_nested_right_beta_result_mismatch, same body), a_function_choice_keeps_its_pair_result = application_argument_function_branch_mismatch. LAST SLICE (7): recursive_open_typed_substitution_strengthening_drops_replacement and its _lambda_ twin use the sample's fused substitution-then-strengthening relation (target context differs from the source), which the kernel does not have: osub and tstr exist separately. Either a new ostr union beside osub (Variable / TensorLeft / Lambda with three merges, plus fixtures), or account for both by composition of the existing blocks (substitution keeps the target usage + term strengthening cannot drop a preserved used cell). NEXT STEP: after ots6b, decide slice 7 by size")
