inl note_of_fsharp_dead_let_record_use_1 () = Note ("FSHARP-DEAD-LET-RECORD-USE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T09:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 evidence (ganymede org2-dmain, pinned pack81, 11-10 09:56Z): dice/lib/dice.spi 5fae2fc8ef9d with line 806 Fsharp = export main main builds the notebook green (28/28) but dotnet publish fails: dice.fs(703,27) error FS0039 The value or constructor v4 is not defined. In new_trace_state_24 the shim build has let v4 : (string -> unit) = closure15() then let v5 : Mut3 = {l0 = v4}; the export build drops the v4 let and keeps the use. Files on ganymede: /home/remote/stage/org2-dmain-failing-dice.fs (failing), org2-dmain-before.fsx (shim build), org2-dmain-dice.spi (source). The [<EntryPoint>] main export itself is emitted correctly. DoD: the dice export build publishes, plus a regression sample with a closure let read only through a record field. Next step: reproduce with that minimal sample")
inl note_of_fsharp_dead_let_record_use_2 () = Note ("FSHARP-DEAD-LET-RECORD-USE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T10:02Z", "compiler", "11-10 06:0x compiler: ROOT CAUSE (my bug, from FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET in pack81/pack82): export_only_closures held var TAGS computed from mains top-level binds, but the skip test lived in binds, which also prints every method and closure body, and var tags are numbered PER BODY. So a method-local let whose tag equals a top-level export-only closures tag was skipped too (dice: new_trace_state_24s v4 = closure15(), read via {l0 = v4}). Not a record-use issue as such; any same-numbered closure let in any body of an F# program that uses export. Blast radius: F# programs with export only (without exports the set is empty). FIX (program %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/FSHARP-DEAD-LET-RECORD-USE/1-skip-top-level-let-objects-only.kitdo): the set now holds the top-level TyLet OBJECTS (HashIdentity.Reference) and binds tests the bind object, so other bodies can never match. Candidate pack83 = pack82 + it (core c3742c88). Gate running on ganymede (~/remote-stage/pack83/g.log): dice draft F# with pack82 (must reproduce the missing v4 let) vs pack83 (must keep it), the export repro/guards, full suite vs pack82. TypeFeatures: none (codegen).")
