inl note_of_timeline_pixel_fidelity_1 () = Note ("TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:18Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "USER 11-10 06:0x: 'use the C:\\Users\\i574n\\OneDrive\\Desktop images to make sure our sans font is faithful, with the timeline css also, try ripping off everything to the pixel level, paddings, colors, alignments, etc. coordinate with the org lane so we keep holding the timeline and cells items'. Split: microblog holds the timeline CSS (this item, x/apps/client/timeline_page.spi), org holds the font (SANS-FONT-FIDELITY). Scope boundary: layout, spacing, colors and type metrics are matched; X's logo and trademarked icons are not copied. First measurement (profile screenshot, 1:1 CSS px since the avatar measures 40 px): center column 331..930 (600 px), right column 350 px, avatar 40 px at 12 px top and 16 px left padding, text column starts 8 px after the avatar (ours: gap 12 px). DoD: our rendered page, screenshotted at the same width, matches the reference within 1 px on every measured box edge and exactly on every sampled color. TYPEFEATURES: none; CSS text in timeline_page.spi. NEXT STEP: sample the screenshots' pixels (colors, edges) with a script, then render ours at the same width and diff.")
inl note_of_timeline_pixel_fidelity_2 () = Note ("TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY", 2u32, "2026-11-10T10:37Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 06:3x MEASURED AND DRAFTED (drafts x\\TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY\\timeline_page.spi, base A2B5E6C274F7; live file untouched). REFERENCE (1:1 profile screenshot, pixel-scanned with a System.Drawing script): column borders x=331/930 (600 px); rows 125 px single-line, 145 px two-line = 12 pad + 20 name + 4 + 20 label + 4 + 20 per text line + 12 + 20 action bar + 12 pad + 1 border; avatar 40x40 at +16/+12; text column 8 px after the avatar; colors bg #000000, border #2f3336, text #e7e9ea, secondary #72767b (= rgb 113,118,123), links and badge #419bef (solid pixels; we used rgb 29,155,240). DRAFT: .row gap 12 -> 8 px; article p margin 2px 0 -> 0; head line 14 -> 15 px with margin 0 0 4px; counts line-height 20px and margin-top 12px; link color rgb(65,155,239); labeled rows use head_line (@user · date, no post id, which made the header wrap to 2 lines) and drop the trailing <hr> (rows already have the bottom border); new test a_post_row_is_one_head_line_and_no_rule. VERIFIED IN CHROME (local render of the live page with the draft applied, served at 127.0.0.1:8765): 0 header wraps in 50 rows, header at 12 px, text at 36 px, row height = 12+20+4+20n+12+1. OPEN: (1) X always shows a 20 px action bar 12 px below the text; ours shows counts only when nonzero (test engagement_counts_hidden_when_zero), a semantics decision; (2) the date is ISO, X shows \"27 de out\"; (3) the font is SANS-FONT-FIDELITY (org): the deployed sans.woff2 is a 2 KB stub; org ships the x-height raise and the current build path next. NEXT STEP: gate the draft (timeline_page.spi cells) on a node, then the client verify with -Accept for the changed page fixtures.")
inl note_of_timeline_pixel_fidelity_3 () = Note ("TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:01Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:0xZ LANDED ON THE BOX + BUILDING FOR PLUTO (user 06:5x: iterate autonomously until live on pluto). x/apps/client/timeline_page.spi = the draft (3b703fc082d2; base a2b5e6c274f7 checked equal before copy). europa job-1794308433984-x-pluto-build-1111 syncs the whole box x tree (242 tracked + untracked files, tar sha af7766be98cf08b1; the deleted apps/client/tlds.spi removed there too), gates timeline_page.spi (Cells, memo off), then builds frames-erlang-1111 (default-page cache from SERVE-DEFAULT-PAGE-CACHE + this CSS/markup) with the same refusals as 1109 (beam must be rebuilt by the job). NEXT STEP: read the build; stage frames-1111 on pluto, write xsim-serve-pluto-1111.yaml (the 1110 one with frames-1111), tell org3 the cutover time, apply, watch pod + /timeline, roll back to frames-1109 on red.")
inl note_of_timeline_pixel_fidelity_4 () = Note ("TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY", 4u32, "2026-11-10T11:26Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:2xZ BUILD MOVED to ganymede. The europa build (job-1794308433984) thrashed europa (load 60 on 2 cores, a 700 MB beam from build.ps1s sim notebooks), so I stopped it; its tree is gone and europa is back for orgs font build. The first ganymede try (job-1794309700258) refused cleanly: xsim_split type error, because ganymedes spiral lib (11-08) predates LIB-TLDS (tlds.spi moved from the client into lib). Rerun job-1794309940701-x-pluto-build-1111g2 first syncs the box lib sources (tar 416661 B, has tlds). The fixed XSans font is live since 11:15Z (PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE Done). NEXT STEP: read the g2 build; stage frames-1111 (stage script fetches from the node that built it), apply xsim-serve-pluto-1111.yaml, bracket with org3.")
inl note_of_timeline_pixel_fidelity_5 () = Note ("TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY", 5u32, "2026-11-10T11:54Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:5xZ LIVE ON PLUTO: frames-1111 (tgz dd9b95831dd5ae8d, built on ganymede from the whole box x tree + box lib; frames beam 11:28:37Z) applied 11:41:34Z, serving from 11:48-11:49Z (org3: ~4 min downtime, render guard OK). VERIFIED on the live page (fetched from pluto, rendered in Chrome with the live XSans): 50 posts, avatar at +16/+12, text column 8 px after the avatar, head line at 12 px and 20 px tall, body at 36 px, 0 head-line wraps, 0 inner <hr>, link color rgb(65,155,239), font XSans loaded. Matches the 1:1 reference on every measured edge. OPEN (the remaining 15%): (1) X always shows a 20 px action bar 12 px below the text, ours only when counts are nonzero; (2) dates are ISO, X shows \"27 de out\"; (3) glyph fidelity rides SANS-FONT-FIDELITY (org: c/C/G/e/S/z/digit normalization, then x-height 535). NEXT STEP: draft the always-present action bar and the short date, gate, ship as frames-1112 together with orgs tuned font.")
inl note_of_timeline_pixel_fidelity_6 () = Note ("TIMELINE-PIXEL-FIDELITY", 6u32, "2026-11-10T13:51Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 13:4xZ DONE, LIVE: frames-1112 (tgz be3f5ff3c91be3d7; round 2: always-present 20 px action bar 12 px below the text, pt-BR short dates \"18 de out\", the two new tests; gate 18/18) applied 13:36:05Z, serving from 13:43:13Z. proof (live page fetched from pluto, measured in Chrome): every row = 12 pad + 20 head + 4 + 20 per text line + 12 + 20 action bar + 12 pad + 1 border (a 5-line row is 181 px, exactly the reference formula); 50/50 rows carry div.actions; 0 inner <hr>; dates \"18 de out\". Together with frames-1111 (8 px avatar gap, 15 px head, rgb(65,155,239) links, 16/12 avatar offsets) every measured edge of the 1:1 reference matches. NOTES, not defects: (a) the sim appends a USER id to a handle held by more than one user record (timeline_serve label_of), so \"@fc1943s · 1637273636049498112\" is sim-world disambiguation, a data question; (b) a non-English post adds the lang badge row (X has none). Glyph fidelity is SANS-FONT-FIDELITY.")
