inl note_of_answered_waits_and_jobs_1 () = Note ("ANSWERED-WAITS-AND-JOBS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:27Z", "org-f33af161", "Filed by org-f33af161 per org3's HOOK handoff (parent HOOK-SMART-RUST-GATE). Pure-local backlog reads the current pwsh gate already does - NO Rust core. fiscal's 4 predicates (note 3 on parent, data in fiscal scratchpad groom/waits.csv): (a) drop waits on Done items; (b) clear item: waits whose LEADING id is Done; (c) clear elapsed when: timestamps; (d) flag dead-train waits (fiscal counted 97 on TRAIN42/42e/43/43c/43d). deps.csv there is also the fixture for a why-the-floor-is-low field (per-team top blocking deps unblocking N items). DoD: a verb/pass that applies a-d over the live backlog, with a dry-run count, run from the heartbeat. fiscal already did a manual sweep (20 waits on Done cleared); this makes it a repeatable predicate.")
inl rig_layers_prim_full_arms () = Task ("RIG-LAYERS-PRIM-FULL-ARMS", "kit standards --layers: a Prim macro is allowed only inside a backend switch with an arm for every target backend (PartialBackendBinding finding)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 80u32, Active, "", "kit,standards,layers,team:rig", "current", "current")
