inl note_of_rig_layers_prim_full_arms_1 () = Note ("RIG-LAYERS-PRIM-FULL-ARMS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Filed 11-10 from the LIB-LAYERS n11 ruling: Prim exists (n12) but allows any macro. DoD: rig_standards_layers_model reports PartialBackendBinding for a macro in a Prim module that is not inside a backend_switch covering every target backend, with a fixture pair (full arms clean, one arm missing flagged). Next step: read how kit standards scans macros (scan.spi) and where backend_switch arms are visible in the text.")
inl note_of_rig_layers_prim_full_arms_2 () = Note ("RIG-LAYERS-PRIM-FULL-ARMS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T10:48Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 06:5x rig: IMPLEMENTED in rig_standards_layers_model/model.spi (unstaged): a prim_binding GADT (RawMacros :: i32 | MissingArms :: i32 * list string) from a line scan of the module's code (tests and comments already stripped by code_of): a backend_switch block is tracked by indentation and its arms are the capitalized words before \" = \"; a macro outside any switch counts as raw, and a switch lacking a backend that another switch in the SAME module binds is MissingArms. So the rule needs no per-package backend list: a module's own switches define what full means. Prim modules report one \"partial backend binding: ...\" row per finding; violation_count now counts those rows one each instead of mistaking them for the macro row. Tests: full arms clean, a short switch names Gleam, a raw macro counted, a Prim report counts 1. kit standards 0, ratchet 0; probe-green 3/3 on ganymede. Rides TRAIN44 (the layers model in TRAIN43f has Prim without this check). Next step: after TRAIN44, re-run kit standards --layers over lib with the binding modules mapped to Prim and read the partial-binding count (lib's sm' first switch has only a Rust arm, so findings are expected and are the point).")
inl note_of_rig_layers_prim_full_arms_3 () = Note ("RIG-LAYERS-PRIM-FULL-ARMS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T10:49Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "TypeFeatures: GADT cases (prim_binding: RawMacros :: i32, MissingArms :: i32 * list string), records (switch_scan), no existentials.")
