inl rig_slice_on_demand () = Task ("RIG-SLICE-ON-DEMAND", "rig backlog slice <ID>: turn a ready medium/heavy item whose next step is authoring into a light draft child, the parent keeping its gate step", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,backlog,drafts,light-floor,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_slice_on_demand () = Planning ("RIG-SLICE-ON-DEMAND", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_slice_on_demand_1 () = Note ("RIG-SLICE-ON-DEMAND", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:45Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "USER 11-10 06:0x (relayed by microblog): split on demand; experiments and blocked items advance in drafts without losing progress, learning from the lab folders, careful about drift. Microblog measured the cause: load describes the GATE, so 20 medium + 8 heavy microblog items (21 for tibia) whose next step is CPU-light authoring never reach a light pool. DoD: (a) rig backlog slice <ID> creates child <ID>-D<n> \"draft: <next step>\" load=light, deps none, output under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\<repo>\\<ID>\\ with a .base per touched file; the parent gets wait item:<child> and keeps its medium/heavy gate step; (b) the autonomous gate calls it for the top ready medium/heavy item when a team's light floor is under 3 (one slice per pause, never more than the floor deficit); (c) a fixture pair: a heavy item with an authoring next step slices, an item whose next step is a run does not. Next step: model the slice decision (next step kind: authoring vs gate) as a pure Spiral module with tests.")
inl note_of_rig_slice_on_demand_2 () = Note ("RIG-SLICE-ON-DEMAND", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:11Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 07:1x rig, per the USER 06:5x message (relayed; \"days of elixir work to migrate ... something is wrong with rig or these tasks\"): SHIPPED A LIVE STEP TODAY, no train needed. The autonomous gate hook (rig-owned infra, backup .bak-rig-<ts>, parse 0) now, when a team has NO ready light item, prints \"Slice on demand\" with the team's top 3 ready medium/heavy items (Planned, not waited, not claimed, not parents, deps Done, not user-assigned, P0 first) and the exact commands to slice one: kit agile add <ID>-D1 TaskKind P2 D1 'draft: <next step>' 'team:<team>' --load light ... then --wait item:<ID>-D1 on the parent. The lane checks that the last note's Next step is authoring (the JSON carries no note text, and an agile show per item would blow the gate's time budget). Replayed on live data: microblog gets X-HAND-UNITS, WARM-CLIENT-LIB-LAND-WINDOW, X-BACKEND-SWITCHES; tibia gets three compiler epics. The pure decision model (src/rig_backlog_slice) is written for the kit verb, which rides TRAIN44, where the authoring check becomes automatic. TypeFeatures: GADT cases (step_kind, slice_verdict), records (slice_input).")
inl note_of_rig_slice_on_demand_3 () = Note ("RIG-SLICE-ON-DEMAND", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:56Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 08:0x rig, first live use of the gate's slice suggestion (rig's own pauses): it offered AGILE-WIP-SLA, IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE, KIT-AGILE-CLAIM-QUEUE and KIT-EDITION3-ROUND; none had an explicit authoring Next step in its last note (one was a measurement, one a respell run), so all correctly stayed whole. GAP: the gate re-offered the same 3 every pause. FIXED in the live hook (backup .bak-rig-<ts>, parse 0): slice candidates rotate like ready items, through a per-session slice-offers.json; each is offered at most 3 pauses running, then the next candidates surface, and the counter clears once all are rotated past. Simulated over 6 pauses with 4 candidates: A,B,C x3, then D x3. The kit verb (TRAIN44) should keep the judgement instead: a KeepWhole verdict recorded on the item stops it being offered until its next note.")
inl rig_drafts_drift_check () = Task ("RIG-DRAFTS-DRIFT-CHECK", "rig drafts check: every drafts dir maps to a live item, every file has a matching .base, stale drafts and orphan dirs are listed (the lab-folder lesson)", Story, P1, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,drafts,drift,groom,team:rig", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_drafts_drift_check () = Planning ("RIG-DRAFTS-DRIFT-CHECK", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_drafts_drift_check_1 () = Note ("RIG-DRAFTS-DRIFT-CHECK", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:45Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "USER 11-10 06:0x direction (relayed): sandboxes are fine if they cannot drift. Lesson (memory lab-in-repo): the lab folders drifted because they sat for weeks unattached to a live item. DoD: rig drafts check lists (1) drafts dirs whose item is Done, absent, or without a note for 3+ days; (2) files without a .base; (3) STALE drafts whose .base no longer matches the live file (the base moved under the draft, as with X-SIM-REDUNDANT-SUFFIX round 1 vs rig's census fix); (4) the same owner+hash rule for node sandboxes (mirrors such as xqueue*, rig-probe trees): each has an owner item and a whole-tree hash diff before use. Nothing stays by default: the groom prints archive candidates (archive, never delete). Builds on the rig_drafts store (KIT-DRAFTS-STORE). Next step: a pure model of a draft dir's state (live item, bases match, age) with tests.")
inl note_of_rig_drafts_drift_check_2 () = Note ("RIG-DRAFTS-DRIFT-CHECK", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:17Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 07:2x rig: PURE MODEL written and probe-green 1/1 on ganymede (src/rig_drafts_drift/drift.spi, HostFree, unstaged). GADTs: owner_state (OwnerLive days | OwnerDone | OwnerAbsent), base_state (BaseMatches | BaseMoved | BaseMissing | LiveGone), drift (DoneOwner | AbsentOwner | SilentOwner days | NoBase | StaleDraft | TargetGone); owner findings are archive candidates (archive, never delete), file findings name the draft. The real store today: 466 item dirs across 15 repos (spiral 299, kit 43, x 36, fiscal 33), a misfiled top-level RENAME-1108-I574N dir, and rig's own TRAIN43d/e/f hold dirs (they will show as AbsentOwner once their trains land, which is right). Next step: the IO reader (walk the store, map dirs to items from the backlog, hash each file against its .base and the live file), CPU-light enough for the box (reads and hashes about 466 dirs), as a kit verb in TRAIN44. TypeFeatures: GADT cases (owner_state, base_state, drift), records (draft_file, draft_dir).")
inl cic_negatives_map () = Task ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", "map the 40 negatives of mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel one by one onto apps/kernel tests (runtime Rejected refusals or fails blocks), filling the gaps", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,mega-samples,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_negatives_map () = Planning ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cic_negatives_map_1 () = Note ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:49Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 groom 11-10 (user: groom the mega-sample migrations until the old samples can go). CIC-MEGA-ABSORB closed the 77 terminals, but the 40 negatives (matrix ExpectedErrors, samples/mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel/negative_*) were only parked on CIC-TYPING n8, and the CIC modules (syntax..typing, inductive, lean, export) carry 92 tests and 0 fails blocks. By the shared typefeatureset rule (CIC-TYPING n1: runtime-checked terms with typed refusals), most map to a runtime Rejected test, not a compile-time fails block. DoD: a table of all 40 (negative -> kernel test name, or a new Rejected test, or dropped with a reason) in this item's notes, the new tests green on a ganymede gate. Next step: list the 40 negative_* dirs with their matrix Expected text and match each against the typing.spi/conversion.spi refusals")
inl note_of_cic_negatives_map_2 () = Note ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", 2u32, "2026-11-10T10:56Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 MAP of the 40 (read from each negative_*/main.spi body). A, term typing mismatches (20) -> runtime refusals. COVERED by typing.spi the_legacy_negative_families_are_refused_at_runtime: capture (loose bound), dependent_pi_domain_mismatch and general_pi_binder_body_mismatch (not a type), legacy_let_codomain_mismatch (let mismatch), general_dependent_application_argument_mismatch, legacy_application_codomain_mismatch and dependent_result_type (check mismatch). COVERED by conversion.spi distinct_sorts_differ_and_a_divergent_side_reports_no_fuel: atomic_defeq_sort_mismatch, conversion_constraint_sort_mismatch. COVERED by inductive.spi reduction_preserves_the_type_of_beta_delta_and_iota_redexes plus the subst.spi lemmas: whnf_sort_mismatch, ordinary_identity_beta_source_sort_mismatch, ordinary_identity_beta_target_sort_mismatch, total_substitution_domain_mismatch. NEED A NEW TEST (slice 1, typing.spi): general_dependent_lambda_binder_body_mismatch, dependent_cross_pair, indexed_dependent_application_result_mismatch, indexed_unary_constructor_application_result_mismatch, programmed_dependent_application_result_mismatch, programmed_endpoint_cross_codomain, recursive_codomain_application_depth_mismatch (a lambda checked against a Pi with another codomain; applications checked against the wrong instantiated codomain; a double application typed as a single one). D, iota categories (3) NEED A NEW TEST (slice 2, inductive.spi): iota_indexed_action_reduction_cross_category, iota_indexed_conclusion_cross_category, iota_indexed_recursor_component_cross_category (a recursor applied with a minor premise or motive of the wrong type is refused). C, metavariables (8) DROPPED, the same reason CIC-MEGA-ABSORB dropped the 7 metavariable terminals (metas belong to an elaborator, the kernel has none): context_sort_indexed_membership_sort_mismatch, meta_assignment_future_dependency, meta_authority_forged_solved, two_meta_assignment_sort_mismatch, two_meta_duplicate_first_assignment, two_meta_second_self_reference, unification_assignment_sort_mismatch, unification_constraint_context_mismatch. B, forged authorities (9) DROPPED WITH A TYPEFEATURESET NOTE: intrinsic_constraint_raw_relation, nondefeq_authority_not_intrinsic_application, nondefeq_authority_not_scoped_pi_authority, nondefeq_not_defeq_pair_authority, scalar_decision_authority_not_intrinsic, scalar_defeq_cannot_be_pair_authority, scoped_application_obstruction_not_intrinsic, membership_identity_authority_not_scalar, typed_meta_identity_decision_not_scalar. The old sample made a verdict carry its subject terms in its type, so forging one was a type error; the new kernel verdicts (conversion defeq = Same | Different | NoFuel, typing inferred = Typed | Rejected) are public unions without their subjects, so they are trusted by convention (only conversion/infer build them). An LCF-style fix needs either verdicts indexed by their subject terms (the SPS discipline) or constructors private to the module. TYPEFEATURES: kept as an open equilibrium question on LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS, not a blocker for the archive. Totals: 13 covered, 10 new tests, 17 dropped with reasons = 40. NEXT STEP: draft slice 1 (7 application/lambda cases as one runtime test in typing.spi)")
inl note_of_cic_negatives_map_3 () = Note ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:09Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 slice 1 GREEN and on the box (ganymede org2-cicn1, pinned, scratch package = box kernel: typing 12/12 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported): apps/kernel/src/typing.spi a8eac1aa4416, mirror synced. a_lambda_or_partial_application_keeps_its_codomain (a Prop lambda and poly_id Prop both refused against a Prop-to-Type Pi) and a_full_application_keeps_its_result (poly_id Prop p refused at a one-level Pi and at p, accepted at Prop as the control) cover general_dependent_lambda_binder_body_mismatch, dependent_cross_pair, indexed_dependent_application_result_mismatch, indexed_unary_constructor_application_result_mismatch, programmed_dependent_application_result_mismatch, programmed_endpoint_cross_codomain, recursive_codomain_application_depth_mismatch. Map now: 20 covered, 3 left (the iota slice), 17 dropped with reasons. NEXT STEP: slice 2 in inductive.spi, a recursor applied with a minor premise or motive of the wrong type is refused")
inl note_of_cic_negatives_map_4 () = Note ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", 4u32, "2026-11-10T11:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: slice 2 GREEN and on the box (ganymede org2-cicn2, pinned, scratch package = box kernel: inductive 21/21 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported): apps/kernel/src/inductive.spi a974e6a53951, mirror synced. a_recursor_refuses_methods_from_the_wrong_category: Nat.rec on zero is Typed with the right motive and methods (control) and Rejected with the minor premises swapped (iota_indexed_recursor_component_cross_category), with a succ step returning a Prop where the motive demands Nat (iota_indexed_action_reduction_cross_category), and with a motive that is not a type family (iota_indexed_conclusion_cross_category). FINAL MAP of the 40: 23 covered by green kernel tests (13 pre-existing + 7 slice 1 + 3 slice 2), 17 dropped with reasons (8 metavariable negatives: no metas in a kernel; 9 forged-authority negatives: verdicts are public unions, kept as the TYPEFEATURES equilibrium question on LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS). CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE's map dependency is met")
inl note_of_cic_negatives_map_5 () = Note ("CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP", 5u32, "2026-11-10T13:26Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 follow-up: CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY is Done, so the 9 forged-authority negatives (intrinsic_constraint_raw_relation, nondefeq_authority_not_intrinsic_application, nondefeq_authority_not_scoped_pi_authority, nondefeq_not_defeq_pair_authority, scalar_decision_authority_not_intrinsic, scalar_defeq_cannot_be_pair_authority, scoped_application_obstruction_not_intrinsic, membership_identity_authority_not_scalar, typed_meta_identity_decision_not_scalar) move from dropped to covered by inductive.spi's three verdict-forgery fails blocks. Final map: 32 covered, 8 dropped (the metavariable negatives only)")
