inl note_of_kernel_as_compiler_corpus_1 () = Note ("KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:50Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 groom 11-10: matrix.psd1 holds 107 rows for mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency (89 negatives + runtime_native/all_terminals/Backends/Timeouts) and 59 for mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel (40 negatives + the same roles); apps/compiler/scripts/bench-native.ps1 lists both runtime_native dirs; SPS-NOTEBOOKS n2 calls the SPS sample a type-layout oracle and SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE says keep one minimal type-layout canary. The proofs moved to apps/kernel (30 modules, 300+ tests), but the samples' codegen-stress role has no replacement yet. DoD: compiler names what replaces each role (the kernel notebooks as a gate family, a kept minimal canary, or nothing with a reason) and the matrix/bench edits are drafted; deletion of the rows themselves stays in the archive items. Next step: compiler decides the replacement per role")
inl note_of_kernel_as_compiler_corpus_2 () = Note ("KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T10:56Z", "compiler", "11-10 07:0x compiler DECISION per role (SPS = mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency, CIC = mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel; both have proofs in apps/kernel now). (1) MEGA SUITE compile entries (matrix Mega: CIC, Self): REPLACE with apps/kernel as ONE compile-only Mega entry; large-program compile stress needs a program of that scale, and the kernel package is the same code. (2) runtime_native / all_terminals rows, their Backends rows (matrix ~735-772, AlsoTypeScript ~245-247) and the four 180 s Timeouts: DROP; the semantics are proven by the kernels tests, and native backend coverage at scale stays with brzozowski / omniledger / zeta runtime rows and the new bench_* workloads. (3) bench-native.ps1 runtime_native dirs for SPS and CIC: DROP; mega_brzozowski_derivatives/runtime_bench + bench_sieve/tree/strings/float take over (BACKEND-BENCH-CI). (4) Type-layout canary: KEEP ONE as SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE asks: samples/mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency/all_terminals on C ONLY (1 row) until a small extracted canary sample replaces it; CIC keeps no canary. The 89 negative_* packages follow SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS (36 of 89 moved). Next step: compiler makes the matrix + bench-native.ps1 edits (1)-(4) once org archives the sample dirs, gated by one suite run; org/org3 apply the same rule to regex + zeta.")
inl note_of_kernel_as_compiler_corpus_3 () = Note ("KERNEL-AS-COMPILER-CORPUS", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:23Z", "org3", "org3 11-10: the \"org/org3 apply the same rule to regex + zeta\" part is DONE. Role-replacement + deletion-precondition notes written on REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION (note 5, brzozowski) and ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE (note 4, zeta), each applying compiler's 4-role template with a verified-on-disk inventory. KEY CONSTRAINT I surfaced for compiler: your SPS/CIC decision drops their native-at-scale rows BECAUSE coverage \"stays with brzozowski/omniledger/zeta runtime rows\" -- so brzozowski and zeta are the CURRENTLY-RETAINED native coverage and must NOT drop their own runtime rows until BACKEND-BENCH-CI absorbs the bench_* workloads (brzozowski) and lib/spiral/zeta exists (zeta). Don''t delete brzozowski/zeta by analogy to SPS/CIC or the fleet loses its only large-program native coverage. The lane:org wait STAYS open: it still needs the org (org2) side -- archive the SPS/CIC sample dirs -- before you make the matrix + bench-native.ps1 edits (1)-(4). org3''s sub-part is the only part I could close.")
inl pluto_font_invisible () = Task ("PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE", "pluto timeline: the served XSans (/media/fonts/sans.woff2, 2096 B) paints letters and digits invisible in browsers; the page CSS lists XSans first, so browser visitors see blank post text", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "serve,pluto,font,bug,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_pluto_font_invisible () = Planning ("PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_pluto_font_invisible_1 () = Note ("PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T10:51Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "Found by microblog 11-10 06:5x in Chrome (local render served at 127.0.0.1:8765; nothing changed on pluto). The live stub fetched from pluto loads (FontFace status loaded, advances present: a 27, H 27, 5 25 at 48px) but letters and digits paint NO ink; only unmapped chars ('@', apostrophe) show, via fallback. org's current build (8560 B woff2 / 36176 B ttf) has the same defect, so this is the font emitter, not the deploy. Evidence: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude-chrome-screenshots-ZUZMsF\\screenshot-1794307829844-2.png (live stub) and screenshot-1794307677268-1.png (new build vs Arial). The soak is curl-only (HTTP status/latency), so no gate saw it. FIX OPTIONS for the USER's decision on pluto: (a) drop 'XSans' from the served font-family until the font paints (one CSS string in timeline_page.spi; text then uses Inter or the system sans); (b) wait for org's fixed font and ship both together with the frames-1110 cutover. Font fix: SANS-FONT-FIDELITY / org (asked for a raster check in the font gate). DoD: a browser render of the pluto timeline shows ink for every post's text, checked by a render probe. TYPEFEATURES: none.")
inl note_of_pluto_font_invisible_2 () = Note ("PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T10:57Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 10:56Z STOP-GAP APPLIED (user 06:5x: 'stop asking me for decisions like this, iterate autonomously until our font is finished and live on pluto'). Moved the served fonts aside on pluto: /data/x-serve/media/fonts/{sans.woff2,sans.ttf} -> /data/x-serve/media/fonts-invisible-20261110/ (sha 3462d72b2eac3ee6, 53c55755a8f3451d). No pod/yaml change. Both URLs now 404 and /timeline stays 200 (0.076 s), so @font-face fails and browsers use the Inter/system fallback: text visible. org3 told the cutover time. NEXT STEP: org's fixed font (raster-verified in Chrome by me) goes into the same path, and the item closes with a browser render showing ink.")
inl note_of_pluto_font_invisible_3 () = Note ("PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:17Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 11:15Z FIXED AND LIVE. Root cause (org): the emitter wrote a maxp table version 0.5 (CFF-style, no maxPoints/maxContours) into a glyf font; DirectWrite (Chrome on Windows) read maxPoints=0 and painted nothing, while FreeType/skrifa recompute and showed ink, so the font's own harness passed. org emits maxp 1.0 (maxPoints 512, maxContours 64). VERIFIED IN CHROME by canvas ink count of 'stewshka Hno 56' at 64px: new woff2 6532 px, new ttf 6532 px, old live stub 0 px, Arial 7919 px. DEPLOYED to pluto 11:15:00Z (user 06:5x pre-authorized): /data/x-serve/media/fonts/{sans.woff2 f9d9a61fe495b034, sans.ttf f9242398ae3a4fe2}, sha checked on both ends; copies in drafts x\\PLUTO-FONT-INVISIBLE; the stop-gap backup of the broken fonts stays in /data/x-serve/media/fonts-invisible-20261110. proof: the font pluto SERVES (fetched back, sha f9d9a61fe495b034) paints 6532 ink px in Chrome; /timeline 200. org adds a raster ink>0 check to the font gate; org3 adds a render probe to the soak.")
inl warm_client_test_split () = Task ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", "Warm compiler client: test.ps1 -Suite split reuses one resident server-tcp compiler like -Suite linked", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,performance,warm,team:compiler", "current", "current")
