inl note_of_warm_client_test_split_1 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:00Z", "compiler", "Child of COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS. Pattern proven by test.ps1 -Suite linked (11-09, now default): one resident --server-tcp compiler per (core hash, root), jobs/results TSV, retired on core-hash change; ganymede A/B on 21 rows: cold 131 s vs warm 85 s (1.54x), 0 compile/native/exit/stdout/residual diffs. DoD: this client reuses one warm process, before/after wall times on the same inputs, byte-identical outputs. TypeFeatures: none (script). Next step: read how -Suite split compiles each unit (test.ps1) and reuse the linked suite''s warm.jobs.tsv path.")
inl note_of_warm_client_test_split_2 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:06Z", "compiler", "11-10 07:2x compiler: IMPLEMENTED (unstaged, apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1 -Suite split): per (case, backend) the cuts are created first (split-units, unchanged), then every cuts model + app unit compiles in ONE --batch process (jobs in cut order, model before app), and each cuts verdict is evaluated exactly as before; SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM=0 keeps the old one-process-per-unit path (same switch as -Suite linked). Batch errors arrive flattened onto one line (Program.fs cleanProtocolText), so the warm \"refused\" message starts at the first ETY-/TracedError/FatalError match instead of being a whole line; verdicts, result kinds and generated files are what must match. A/B RUNNING on ganymede (staged copy /root/compiler-warmsplit, installed pack83 pinned, -Filter array_i32|closure_array, both backends): wall times, verdict/result-kind diff, sha256 of every generated app unit file. TypeFeatures: none (script).")
inl note_of_warm_client_test_split_3 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:11Z", "compiler", "11-10 07:3x compiler: first A/B VOID (cold 57 s / warm 27 s, 18 rows, 0 verdict diffs, but every cut was refused in BOTH arms with PackageErrors): -Suite split links each cuts core with New-Item -ItemType Junction, which does not exist on Linux, so no cut found core and the arms compared identical failures. Two findings: (1) -Suite split has never really run on Linux; FIX (unstaged, test.ps1): SymbolicLink when not $IsWindows. (2) a cut refused for an ENVIRONMENT reason (PackageErrors) still counts as verdict pass, so a broken environment reports green while testing nothing; follow-up: a refusal must carry an ETY-/TracedError diagnostic from the split model to count. A/B rerunning with the symlink fix.")
inl note_of_warm_client_test_split_4 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", 4u32, "2026-11-10T11:15Z", "compiler", "11-10 07:4x compiler: DONE. A/B on ganymede (staged copy, installed pack83 pinned, -Filter array_i32|closure_array, Zig + Rust), with the Linux symlink fix: cold (SPIRAL_LINKED_WARM=0, one process per unit) 81 s vs warm (one --batch per case and backend) 37 s = 2.2x; 18 rows each, verdict/result-kind diffs 0; generated unit files 36 vs 36, sha256-identical (0 differing). Both arms exit 1 identically from the native build step on Linux, filed as SPLIT-SUITE-LINUX-NATIVE. Also in test.ps1 (unstaged): a cut refused because its packages did not load now FAILs with result \"environment (...)\" instead of passing as a refusal.")
inl note_of_warm_client_test_split_5 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", 5u32, "2026-11-10T11:16Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede /root/compiler-warmsplit/ab.out 11-10 11:12Z: cold 81 s, warm 37 s, rows 18/18, verdict diffs 0, unit files 36/36 identical; results LEGAL 2, native build-fail identical in both arms.")
inl note_of_warm_client_test_split_6 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT", 6u32, "2026-11-10T11:55Z", "compiler", "STRONGER evidence after SPLIT-SUITE-LINUX-NATIVE: the same A/B with working native builds: cold 82 s vs warm 39 s (2.1x), both exit 0, 18/18 rows pass LEGAL in each arm, verdict diffs 0, 36/36 generated unit files sha256-identical.")
