inl note_of_warm_client_kit_regen_1 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-KIT-REGEN", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:00Z", "compiler", "Child of COMPILER-WARM-CLIENTS. Pattern proven by test.ps1 -Suite linked (11-09, now default): one resident --server-tcp compiler per (core hash, root), jobs/results TSV, retired on core-hash change; ganymede A/B on 21 rows: cold 131 s vs warm 85 s (1.54x), 0 compile/native/exit/stdout/residual diffs. DoD: this client reuses one warm process, before/after wall times on the same inputs, byte-identical outputs. TypeFeatures: none (kit Rust). Next step: rig measures kit regen cold on one root, then routes it through a --server-tcp session.")
inl note_of_warm_client_kit_regen_2 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-KIT-REGEN", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:09Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:2x rig: COLD BASELINE measured (both on moon, kit train25 tree, TRAIN43f pin): TRAIN43f node regen 376 owners compiled cold in 59 min at -Parallel 3 (0 skipped); the incremental A/B compiled 127 owners (the linked units and their consumers) in 23 min at -Parallel 2, i.e. about 11 s per cold compile per lane under load. CLIENT DESIGN read from the compiler host (tmp/compiler/host/Program.fs runTcpServer/serveSessions): start dotnet <pinned SpiralCompiler.dll> --server-tcp <session path> per lane with SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID = the regen pid (the server dies with its client) and the same SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT / SPIRAL_BUILD_BUDGET_MS the cold path sets; read the ready line spiral-session-ready port=N pid=P from stdout; per owner send compile<TAB>Rust<TAB><input><TAB><output> and read lines until spiral-session<TAB>ok<TAB>pid<TAB>bytes... or spiral-session<TAB>error<TAB>pid<TAB>message (warning lines come first). The per-owner timeout maps to --stall-seconds. Retire a server when the pinned core hash changes, and keep the cold path for a server that died (rerun that owner in a fresh process, as test.ps1 -WarmRecycle does). The scheduler in test-regeneration.ps1 (the $running list, ~line 262) only swaps Process start/exit for a session request/answer. ORDER: this edits compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1, which KIT-TRAIN-INCREMENTAL-REGEN already drafts (linked-unit graph restore); landing two drafts of one file in parallel collides, so this waits on that item, then drafts on top of its landed file. DoD (unchanged): before/after wall time on the same inputs, byte-identical outputs.")
