inl note_of_warm_client_node_proof_2 () = Note ("WARM-CLIENT-NODE-PROOF", 2u32, "2026-11-10T22:58Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 19:2x DEFERRED, not sliced: the next step is a measurement (one node-proof job cold vs through a --server-tcp session), not authoring, and an A/B timing needs a quiet node. ganymede has 4 cores and sits at loadavg 3-5 under fiscal's own xsd_emit SCC proof (executed_cells) plus the D2 check and microblog's memo proof, so wall times now would measure contention, not the warm client. Next step: run the cold/warm pair on ganymede once fiscal-scc-proof and fiscal-mdfe-d2-check have exited and loadavg is under 1.")
inl regex_ssv_render_ci () = Task ("REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI", "regex video: the gh-pages ffmpeg render pipeline, proven on dummy frames before LAYOUT lands (the non-gated half of REGEX-SSV-RENDER)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 85u32, Active, "", "regex,video,ci,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_ssv_render_ci () = Planning ("REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_ssv_render_ci_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Sliced 11-10 by rig (delegation for REGEX-STATE-SPACE-VIDEO, org3 plan note 4): REGEX-SSV-RENDER waits on LAYOUT only for real frames; the workflow (gh-pages.yml, ffmpeg encode, artifact upload) is testable on generated dummy frames now. DoD: the workflow encodes N dummy frames into a video artifact in one CI run, frame count and duration checked. REGEX-SSV-RENDER then only swaps dummy frames for LAYOUT's. Next step: draft gh-pages.yml with a dummy-frame step.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_render_ci_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:34Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 claimed 11-10. Design, following the repo rules: no YAML edit (workflows are generated from i574n.github scripts/pins/workflows.spi, and gh-pages.yml already runs the one entry scripts/workflow.ps1 and uploads dist as the artifact), no new action (actions.lock unchanged), no new script. The stage lives in regex scripts/publish.ps1 after publish-tree.ps1 (which rebuilds dist): the frame interface is a raw RGB24 file (320x180, 24 fps, 48 frames); a dummy producer (ffmpeg lavfi testsrc2) writes it now and REGEX-SSV-RENDER swaps in the Spiral rasterizer later; the encoder turns it into dist/ssv/state-space.mp4 (libx264, yuv420p, faststart); checks: raw byte count = w*h*3*frames, ffprobe frame count, size, duration within 0.05 s, file under 5 MB; installs ffmpeg with apt on Linux when missing. Draft at kit drafts regex/REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI/publish.ps1. The block alone is gating on ganymede as org2-ssv (Linux, pwsh, apt ffmpeg)")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_render_ci_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 stage PROVEN on Linux and applied on the box (unstaged): regex/scripts/publish.ps1 c4a62ebca9d4 (+19 lines after publish-tree.ps1). Proof: ganymede org2-ssv ran the block alone (pwsh, core.ps1 Invoke-Block, apt ffmpeg): VIDEO-OK regex/ssv / state-space.mp4 48 frames 320x180 2 s 56144 B, raw RGB file 320*180*3*48 B checked and removed, dist/ssv/state-space.mp4 present. gh-pages.yml needs no change: its ubuntu leg runs scripts/workflow.ps1 (which runs publish.ps1) and uploads dist, so the mp4 rides in the existing artifact; the windows leg runs it too when ffmpeg is on PATH (installed only on Linux). DoD left: one CI run on a pushed commit (the user's push). REGEX-SSV-RENDER then replaces the testsrc2 producer with the Spiral rasterizer writing the same raw RGB24 file")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_render_ci_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-RENDER-CI", 4u32, "2026-11-10T11:42Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 amendment: the windows-2025 leg also runs publish.ps1, so a host without ffmpeg that is not Linux now prints VIDEO-SKIPPED regex/ssv and returns instead of failing (Linux still installs ffmpeg with apt and must produce VIDEO-OK). Box regex/scripts/publish.ps1 36bdcf345176, parse-checked; the Linux path is unchanged from the org2-ssv proof")
inl regex_ssv_determinism () = Task ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", "regex video: determinism gate, two runs over the same GRAPH rows give identical frame hashes", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "regex,video,determinism,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_ssv_determinism () = Planning ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Sliced 11-10 by rig (delegation, org3 plan note 4): runs on REGEX-SSV-GRAPH's rows (Done) and dummy frames now, and on real frames once LAYOUT lands. DoD: a harness renders twice and compares per-frame hashes, failing on the first differing frame; a negative control (a seeded random jitter) must fail it. Next step: write the two-run hash compare over dummy frames.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:57Z", "org3", "org3 11-10 DRAFTED (claimed, lease to 13:12Z). Wrote the determinism gate as 3 ///> rust cells + helpers added to regex/src/ssv_graph.spi (all symbols in scope -> lowest-risk; could split to ssv_determinism.spi once export semantics are confirmed). Draft + .base in drafts/regex/REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM/; also applied UNSTAGED to src/ssv_graph.spi.\nDESIGN (per DoD + rig note): frame_of(state)=index*4+kind_code (overflow-safe small ints, no hash needed at the dummy stage); frames(g)=per-state digest in discovery order; first_diff(a,b,i) recurses and returns Same | DiffAt <first differing frame index> (fails on the FIRST diff, per DoD). THREE cells: (1) two renders of the same graph -> Same (determinism); (2) a single jittered frame (bump_at f 1) -> DiffAt 1 (the negative control the DoD asks for -- a seeded perturbation MUST be caught, at its index); (3) different graphs -> DiffAt 0 (the digest discriminates -- a digest that can't tell frames apart would pass determinism trivially and be worthless).\nHAND-VERIFIED arithmetic against the existing GRAPH cells: seq(zero,one) kinds [Live;Live;Accepting] -> frames [1;5;10]; both(...) kinds [DeadEnd;DeadEnd] -> frames [0;4]; first_diff[1;5;10][1;5;10]=Same; bump idx1 -> [1;6;10] -> DiffAt 1; vs [0;4] -> DiffAt 0. Cell budget: 7 cells total (was 4), awk oracle clean.\nNOT GATED -- I will NOT claim it compiles without the Cells rust gate (compiler not built here; build.ps1 runs the full heavy suite). NEXT STEP: run the Cells rust gate node-first (cd regex; pwsh build.ps1), confirm the 3 new cells pass; residual DIALECT risks to watch = _assert_eq on a bare nullary union (Same), the ?= a, b ?| tuple-match arms, and :~ ^ recursion on first_diff/bump_at (all mirrored from existing ssv_graph.spi code but unverified). After green: split to its own module if desired + register. edges/rounds in the digest are a v2 enrichment (states-only is enough for the first gate).")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:59Z", "org3", "org3 correction: src/ssv_graph.spi RESTORED to its green 110-line base (I will not leave unverified Spiral in src poisoning the regex gate -- restore-on-red discipline). The determinism draft (147 lines, 7 cells) lives ONLY in drafts/regex/REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM/ssv_graph.spi (with .base). To land: cp the draft over src/ssv_graph.spi, run the Cells rust gate node-first (cd regex; pwsh build.ps1), fix any dialect reds, then it's green. Not gating this pass (heavy, node-first, compiler not built here; I've delivered the design + hand-verified arithmetic). Lease auto-expires 13:12Z -- a Spiral-fluent lane can apply+gate it, or I will next pass. The design is the value-add; the gate run is mechanical.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 4u32, "2026-11-10T12:09Z", "org3", "org3: waiting on REGEX-SSV-GRAPH-BLOCKS (org2) -- my determinism cells land in ssv_graph.spi which org2 is actively editing, so I rebase my draft onto org2's landed ssv_graph (then layer first_diff + jitter negative control over ssv_layout's digest(layout g f)). org2 will send the landed hash. Draft frozen in drafts/regex/REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM/.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_5 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 5u32, "2026-11-10T12:14Z", "org3", "org3: GRAPH-BLOCKS landed (org2, ssv_graph.spi 691476fa35a5 green on ganymede) + ssv_layout landed (me) -> wait cleared, DESIGN CORRECTED. The determinism gate should consume the REAL frames: ssv_layout.digest(layout g f), NOT the states-only graph proxy I first drafted. New home = a NEW module ssv_determinism.spi (:< ssv_layout, ssv_graph, testing, regex_derivative) -- additive, so it does not re-touch ssv_graph/ssv_layout while org2's combined gate (org2-glay) is in flight. Shape: frame_digests g = [digest(layout g 0)..digest(layout g (n-1))]; :~ ^ first_diff (a b : list i64) (i) : diff_at returns Same | DiffAt <first differing frame> (fail on first diff, per DoD); cells = (1) two renders -> Same; (2) bump_at one frame's i64 digest -> DiffAt 1 (the JITTER NEGATIVE CONTROL ssv_layout's own cell lacks -- a seeded perturbation MUST be caught); (3) two different graphs -> differs=!+. NOT AUTHORED yet: blind cross-module Spiral authoring is high-risk unverified (the import resolution of fourth_from_end/tri_cyclic across testing/regex_derivative is the main unknown) -- author it when it can be gated (after org2-glay confirms the package green). The states-only draft in drafts/regex/REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM/ is superseded by this layout-based design. NEXT STEP: after org2-glay is green, write ssv_determinism.spi consuming layout, gate it with the regex package node-first.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_6 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 6u32, "2026-11-10T12:59Z", "org3", "org3: parking on org2-glay (the combined ssv_layout+ssv_graph gate org2 is running). The determinism module authoring should go against a confirmed-green regex package base, not mid-gate -- org2 posts the glay result on REGEX-SSV-GRAPH-BLOCKS. Design is final (note 5: new ssv_determinism.spi consuming ssv_layout.digest(layout g f), first_diff + jitter negative control). Author + gate once the package is green.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_7 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 7u32, "2026-11-10T13:28Z", "org3", "org3 11-10 AUTHORED the determinism gate (package now green: org2-mlay 8/8 ssv_layout 9370fc9b + ssv_graph 691476fa). Draft: drafts/regex/REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM/ssv_determinism.spi (NEW module, 47 lines, 3 cells x4 lines = budget-clean). Consumes ssv_layout: frame_digests g = [digest(layout g 0)..digest(layout g (n-1))] (the real coordinate frames, not the states-only proxy). diff_at = Same | DiffAt; first_diff fails on the FIRST differing frame (per DoD). Cells: (1) two renders -> Same (determinism); (2) bump_at one frame's i64 digest -> DiffAt 1 (the JITTER NEGATIVE CONTROL -- ssv_layout's own cell only tests positive stability, never discrimination); (3) fourth_from_end vs tri_cyclic -> differs=!+ (the digest discriminates). Imports match ssv_layout (testing, regex_derivative, regex_minimal, ssv_graph) + ssv_layout -> resolves fourth_from_end/tri_cyclic/digest/layout (my earlier import-uncertainty is retired). NOT GATED here (heavy node gate). NEXT STEP: register ssv_determinism in regex/src/spiral.toml AFTER org2's ssv_parity line lands (coordinated, no toml collision), copy the draft to src/, then gate on a node with the package (Cells rust, like org2-mlay). merge_frame frames can fold into frame_digests as a v2 once this gates. Wait cleared (package green + draft authored).")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_8 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 8u32, "2026-11-10T13:33Z", "org3", "org3: ssv_parity landed in spiral.toml (org2) so the toml-collision wait is answered. Draft ssv_determinism.spi is ready to register (append after ssv_parity) + gate. Keeping it OUT of src/ for now so it does not poison org2's in-flight package gate with unverified code. Next step: gate it on a node with the package (Cells rust) -- either org2/compiler include it in the next regex package gate on the ganymede mirror (3 cells, consumes ssv_layout.digest/layout, imports match ssv_layout), or I set up a dedicated node gate next pass. Not urgent: it is a quality gate, RENDER does not depend on it. Parking on the gate.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_determinism_9 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-DETERMINISM", 9u32, "2026-11-10T13:47Z", "org3", "org3 11-10 GATED GREEN + LANDED. org2 ran job org2-det on the ganymede regex mirror (scratch copy of the box package: ssv_graph 691476fa + ssv_layout 9370fc9b + ssv_parity 9933ffc5 + my ssv_determinism 85d3d11a registered after ssv_parity, pinned compiler): ssv_determinism 3/3 executed, 0 failed, 0 unsupported; budget oracle 0. LANDED node-proof/box-copy: appended ssv_determinism after ssv_parity in regex/src/spiral.toml + copied src/ssv_determinism.spi (47 lines, 3 cells). The determinism gate consumes the REAL layout frames (ssv_layout.digest(layout g f)), fails on the first differing frame (first_diff), with the jitter negative control ssv_layout's own positive-only cell lacks + graph discrimination. DoD met (LAYOUT landed = real frames, not dummy). Closing. FOLLOW-UP (v2, not blocking): fold merge_frame frames into frame_digests so the gate also covers the merge animation (currently layout-growth frames only). The whole regex-video layout+determinism chain (GRAPH->LAYOUT->MERGE->DETERMINISM) is now landed + gated.")
