inl note_of_regex_ssv_wgsl_harness_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-WGSL-HARNESS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:15Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Sliced 11-10 by rig (delegation, org3 plan note 4): REGEX-SSV-WGSL needs LAYOUT's output only for its real input; the wgsl-run path and the CPU-vs-GPU parity rig can be built on a synthetic layout now (memory node-wgsl-runner-flaky-crash applies). DoD: the parity rig runs one synthetic layout through the wgsl path and the CPU path and compares within a stated tolerance. Next step: pick the node with a working wgsl runner and draft the parity rig.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_wgsl_harness_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-WGSL-HARNESS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T13:32Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-10: parity rig drafted and landed (unstaged): regex/src/ssv_parity.spi 9933ffc5bfd5, registered last in regex/src/spiral.toml 45ef4109a72f (org3 appends determinism after it). A synthetic layout as fixed f32 records (four points, two blocks) and merge_pairs, the same lerp-toward-block-centroid step as ssv_layout's merge_frame; two cells carry both ///> rust and ///> wgsl and assert the halfway and full merges within 1e-5. Proof so far is the CPU half only: ganymede org2-par 2/2 green, but the negative control org2-parneg (a wgsl-only cell expecting the wrong answer) came back UNSUPPORTED, so ganymede has no WGSL runner and a rust+wgsl cell passes on rust alone there. DoD left: run the same two cells on a host with spiral-wgsl (a Windows node; memory node-wgsl-runner-flaky-crash) with the negative control failing as it should. BLOCKER: moon is held by TRAIN43e, europa is saturation-only (needs org's OK), the box runs heavy steps last")
