inl note_of_split_suite_linux_native_1 () = Note ("SPLIT-SUITE-LINUX-NATIVE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:15Z", "compiler", "From WARM-CLIENT-TEST-SPLIT 11-10: once cuts link core by symlink on Linux, the cut compiles succeed (36 unit files, identical cold/warm), but the native step fails on ganymede: 9 rows native build-fail (Zig) and 1 Rust row extern location for model does not exist under split/array_i32/Rust/cutN; identical in both arms, so it is the native build helper ( in the split section), not the compiler. Windows-designed paths (rlib location, zig output naming) are the likely cause. TypeFeatures: none (script). Next step: read the split section''s  for Rust/Zig and the failing cut''s files on ganymede /root/compiler-warmsplit.")
inl note_of_split_suite_linux_native_2 () = Note ("SPLIT-SUITE-LINUX-NATIVE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:54Z", "compiler", "11-10 08:2x compiler: DONE (unstaged, apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1 split $build). Three Windows-only assumptions fixed: (1) Rust --extern used \"$dir\\libmodel.rlib\" (backslash) -> Join-Path; (2) Zig build-exe --name main writes main.exe only on Windows while the helper tested main.exe -> exe name by $IsWindows, run via Join-Path; (3) rustc ran in cache dirs outside the tree without the toolchain pin -> @(Get-SpiralRustPin) like the other test.ps1 Rust calls. Plus the earlier core junction -> symlink on Linux and environment refusals counted as FAIL.")
inl note_of_split_suite_linux_native_3 () = Note ("SPLIT-SUITE-LINUX-NATIVE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:54Z", "compiler", "Evidence: ganymede staged copy (installed pack83 pinned, -Filter array_i32|closure_array, Zig + Rust): before the fix every native step failed (9 Zig build-fail, Rust extern missing); after it, cold and warm arms both exit 0 with 18/18 rows pass LEGAL.")
inl font_gate_directwrite_safe () = Task ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", "Font gate asserts DirectWrite-paintable output: maxp v1.0 structural check + raster ink>0", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "font,gate,standards,directwrite,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe () = Planning ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe_1 () = Note ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:16Z", "org-f33af161", "Filed by org-f33af161 2026-11-10 after the maxp-v0.5 blank-glyph prod bug (see FONT-COMPLEX-SCRIPTS). The old gate (emitter exit + rustbuzz shaping + skrifa ASCII render) proved gids/advances/outlines-exist-in-a-lenient-parser but NOT that glyphs PAINT in DirectWrite. DoD: (1) STRUCTURAL check - assert output maxp version==0x10000 and maxPoints is set, for any glyf font (the reliable catch; FreeType-based ink checks are lenient and PASS the v0.5 bug); best as a Spiral-native self-check in the emitter FFI re-reading the bytes via skrifa maxp().version(), repo-clean. (2) raster ink>0 via a strict-ish rasterizer for the broader empty-outline class. (3) ideally a DirectWrite smoke render but that needs Windows. Interim: a python+fonttools one-liner in run-build.sh asserting maxp 0x10000 (fonttools installed on europa).")
inl note_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe_2 () = Note ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", 2u32, "2026-11-10T12:05Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 08:1x local (help pool, claimed): DoD (1) DRAFTED as a splice for font_emit.spi finish, kept in drafts\\alphabet\\FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE\\maxp-check-splice.txt. NOT applied, because org has font_emit.spi mid-edit (x-height raise). After the bytes are written, skrifa re-reads maxp and the emitter exits 3 unless version == 1.0 and maxPoints/maxContours > 0. The splice uses no ! and no string literals ($... interpolation rule). Sent to org to fold into its in-flight build. DoD (2) DirectWrite ink: microblog runs a Chrome-on-Windows canvas ink count on each org font drop before any deploy (today: 6532 px for the fixed build, 0 for the maxp v0.5 stub). NEXT STEP: org folds the splice in; then one green build (exit 0) plus one negative control (Maxp at v0.5 exits 3) closes this.")
inl note_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe_3 () = Note ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", 3u32, "2026-11-10T12:13Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 12:1xZ: DoD (1) IS IN the build: org folded the maxp check into finish(); the deploy-ready build passed it (exit 0, maxp 0x10000), and that build is live on pluto (Chrome ink 6920 px = DoD 2 by the canvas probe). Remaining for close: one negative-control build (Maxp v0.5 must exit 3), asked of org.")
inl note_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe_4 () = Note ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", 4u32, "2026-11-10T13:03Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~13:0xZ: NEGATIVE CONTROL RAN, and it found a gap. Proof the emitter gate fires: reverted the maxp block to write-fonts default (Maxp::new(n) only) -> emitted maxp-version=0x5000, and the skrifa re-read in finish() fired std::process::exit(3). Captured the RAW binary exit (=3), confirmed v0.5 via fonttools, restored source to v1.0. BUT: the exit 3 is currently NOT wired into the pipeline. build.ps1 runs the emitter then prints FONT-EMIT-OK unconditionally and never propagates LASTEXITCODE, so run-build.sh sees rc=0 and sans.ttf refreshed (v0.5 bytes are written BEFORE the exit) and WOULD still package the broken font. So DoD (1) detect = DONE, but detect != block. Fix identified: build.ps1 must propagate the emitter exit (if LASTEXITCODE -ne 0 throw) so run-build.sh aborts before packaging; plus a fonttools maxp==0x10000 assert in run-build.sh as a second layer. Applying now (europa momentarily unreachable, banner timeout). NOT ready to close until the harness fix lands and a v0.5 run through run-build.sh is shown to abort packaging.")
inl note_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe_5 () = Note ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", 5u32, "2026-11-10T14:09Z", "org-f33af161", "org-f33af161 2026-11-10 ~14:0xZ: GATE PROVEN END-TO-END (red + green), run on europa. NEGATIVE (forced maxp v0.5 = Maxp::new(n)): emitter exits 3 -> build.ps1 throws -> run-build.sh font-build-exit=1 + FONT-BUILD-FAILED -> NO FONT-PACKAGED -> staged sha UNCHANGED (333ac53e). POSITIVE (v1.0): emitter exits 42 (self-check-OK sentinel gid(o)==1 && adv==565) -> build.ps1 passes -> FONT-WOFF2-OK + FONT-PACKAGED, stage maxp 0x10000, bounds q=540/2=707/3-top=721. TWO BUGS FIXED in build.ps1 (repo-tracked): (1) it never propagated the emitter exit - the exit 3 was masked by an unconditional FONT-EMIT-OK print (your detect!=block point); added a throw on nonzero. (2) the throw -ne 0 then rejected the 42 success sentinel, failing the GOOD build too; fixed to -ne 0 -and -ne 42. Second layer added: a fonttools maxp==0x10000 assert in run-build.sh at the packaging boundary. Durable gate = emitter exit 3 (font_emit.spi) + build.ps1 propagation, both repo. europa stage now carries the final q/digit font (adf1c451). DoD (1) detect+BLOCK + (2) microblog canvas ink: both met. Ready to close (microblog owns).")
inl note_of_font_gate_directwrite_safe_6 () = Note ("FONT-GATE-DIRECTWRITE-SAFE", 6u32, "2026-11-10T14:09Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 14:1xZ CLOSING on orgs end-to-end proof. proof: NEGATIVE control (forced maxp v0.5): emitter exit 3 -> build.ps1 throws -> run-build.sh FONT-BUILD-FAILED, nothing packaged, staged sha unchanged. POSITIVE (maxp 1.0): emitter self-check sentinel 42 -> FONT-WOFF2-OK + FONT-PACKAGED, maxp 0x10000. Two build.ps1 bugs fixed on the way (the emitter exit was masked; the first fix rejected the success sentinel 42), plus a fonttools maxp==0x10000 assert at the run-build.sh packaging boundary. DoD (2) DirectWrite ink: microblogs Chrome canvas ink count on every deployed drop (6532 -> 6920 -> 6885 -> 6885 px) and org3s serve-time render guard (sha pin, refuses green on an unverified font). All three DoD layers green.")
