inl note_of_cells_port_memo_d1_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:35Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 07:3x local DRAFTED (drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-PORT-MEMO-D1, .base beside each live file): memo.spi gains shape_row (kind tab names tab operators, names space-joined: identifiers and operators never contain whitespace) + kind_word + spaced, and the gleam test shape_rows_carry_kind_names_and_operators; main.spi exports block_shape (string * string -> string, the established wire shape); domain.ex passthrough block_shape: 2; memo.ex block_shape is now a 4-line parse of the Spiral row (the 20-line regex cond is GONE from lib: the host shrinks) and public with @doc false; new test memo_shape_parity_test.exs keeps the old regexes as the ORACLE and compares them with Memo.block_shape over every top-level block of every tracked .spi in all repos (asserts > 1000 blocks, 0 differences). NEXT STEP: run it in a private Cells copy (domain rebuild = compiler CPU; the box is at 100%, so on a quiet box or a free node), then land via cells_land_window.")
