inl compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_d1 () = Task ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES-D1", "draft: inventory which GPU primitives (workgroup memory, barriers, subgroups, atomics, unroll, restrict, f16/bf16, noinline, 16-byte loads) already exist per backend (WGSL, Cpp/CUDA, C, Rust), then split the rest into 120-min steps", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_d1 () = Planning ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES-D1", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_d1_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:38Z", "tibia-ac4b4e98", "Slice of COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES: drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES\\ with a .base per touched file; the parent keeps its gate step. Context 11-10: the rented H200 (node 12) exposes CUDA but NOT Vulkan, so the inventory must also say what the Cpp/CUDA backend (CodegenCpp.fs + corelib.cuh) already offers, as the route for tibia's GPU lanes there. DoD: a per-backend table of the 9 primitives with file:line evidence, and the missing ones split into child steps of at most 120 min.")
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_d1_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T11:52Z", "tibia", "11-10 07:5x tibia INVENTORY (code read of the fork's merged compiler spiral/apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, 36,226 lines; the vendored 'The Spiral Language 2' dir is the OLD upstream with only C/Cpp/Fsharp/Python codegens, so it is the wrong tree for this question). Per primitive, with evidence: (1) WGSL workgroup memory: ABSENT (0 hits for var<workgroup>). (2) Barriers: ABSENT on WGSL (no workgroupBarrier/storageBarrier); no __syncthreads emitted by the Cuda backend either. (3) Subgroups: ABSENT everywhere. (4) Atomics: only internal, not typed ops: WGSL emits atomic<u32> heap_overflow with atomicAdd (22908, 22920) for the heap checker, and C emits __atomic_fetch_add/__atomic_sub_fetch for threaded refcounts (26754, 26758). (5) Unroll: PRESENT on the Cpp/CUDA backend only, as an int code (28424-28425: 0 gives #pragma unroll, i gives #pragma unroll i), not the NoUnroll|UnrollAll|UnrollBy union; absent on C/Rust/WGSL. (6) restrict: ABSENT. (7) f16/bf16: ABSENT. (8) noinline: by NAME PREFIX on Cpp/CUDA (28642: a fun_name starting with noinline gives __noinline__), plus a C __attribute__((noinline)) for borrowed loops only (27434), so not an attribute users can set. (9) 16-byte vector loads: ABSENT. KEY FOR TIBIA: the Cpp backend has CudaHost/CudaDevice targets (28057-28058, 28478-28479: __trap() on device), so a CUDA route to the H200 (node 12, no Vulkan) already exists. SPLIT of the missing work, each at most 120 min, all compiler-pack work for the compiler lane: S1 WGSL workgroup memory as a typed address space plus workgroupBarrier; S2 typed atomics (WGSL atomic<T> + C11/CUDA atomics) as one op family; S3 the unroll union replacing the int code, emitted on C/Rust/CUDA; S4 restrict on C pointer params; S5 f16/bf16 scalar types on C/CUDA/WGSL (enable f16); S6 a noinline attribute replacing the name prefix; S7 16-byte vector loads (vec4 / float4 / uint4); S8 subgroup collectives (WGSL subgroups extension, CUDA __shfl). Not filed as 8 items yet: the parent decides the order with the compiler lane. DoD met for this slice.")
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_d1_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES-D1", 3u32, "2026-11-10T11:56Z", "tibia", "proof: code read of spiral_compiler.fs with file:line evidence per primitive (note 2); an analysis-only slice, no runtime claim.")
