inl note_of_regex_ssv_graph_blocks_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-GRAPH-BLOCKS", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:45Z", "compiler", "From REGEX-SSV-LAYOUT 11-10: merge_round carries only {round; blocks} (a count), so the layout cannot know WHICH states merge. ssv_graph''s rounds already replay regex_minimal''s Moore refinement (refine_rows over blocks); keep each round''s blocks as a list i32 indexed by state (block id per state). TypeFeatures: none new. Next step: add members : list i32 to merge_round from the refined blocks, with a test that the final round''s distinct ids = minimal_size.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_graph_blocks_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-GRAPH-BLOCKS", 2u32, "2026-11-10T12:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 claimed and drafted (kit drafts regex/REGEX-SSV-GRAPH-BLOCKS/ssv_graph.spi, base = box regex/src/ssv_graph.spi 882d552139d0): merge_round becomes { round; blocks; members : list i32 }, members being the block id per DFA state (regex_minimal's Block id, DeadBlock as -1) read off each round's refined blocks (round 0 from initial_blocks, later rounds from refine_once via round_on k r). Test the_final_round_names_one_block_per_minimal_state: on tri_cyclic_nonminimal and fourth_from_end the final round's distinct live ids equal minimal_size and members has one entry per state. Budget 0. Gating in place on the ganymede regex mirror as org2-gblk (restore on red; mirror regex tree hash-equal to the box after syncing typed.spi). org3 told about the shared file (its DETERMINISM apply is not in the box file)")
