inl note_of_regex_ssv_merge_layout_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-MERGE-LAYOUT", 1u32, "2026-11-10T11:45Z", "compiler", "Merge half of REGEX-SSV-LAYOUT''s DoD. After the discovery frames, each merge round r gets frames where every state moves toward the centroid of its round-r block (linear interpolation, same IEEE-only arithmetic, so it stays deterministic); a round''s end positions are its block centroids. TypeFeatures: none new. Next step: once REGEX-SSV-GRAPH-BLOCKS lands, add merge_frames to ssv_layout.spi with a test that a fully merged block''s members coincide at the last frame.")
inl note_of_regex_ssv_merge_layout_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SSV-MERGE-LAYOUT", 2u32, "2026-11-10T12:50Z", "compiler", "11-10 08:5x compiler: DRAFTED + GATED, frozen at %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/regex/REGEX-SSV-MERGE-LAYOUT/ssv_layout.spi (9370fc9b) over ssv_layout.spi.base (b1836bf2 = the box file org3 applied). Adds :< regex_minimal and merge frames: merge_frame g k t steps = the final discovery layout, rounds before k fully merged, round k interpolated by u = t/steps; merged moves every live state (members >= 0) toward the centroid of its round block with lerp (dead states, -1, stay); centroids and lerp use only + - * / so frames stay bit-deterministic. Tests (tri_cyclic_nonminimal): after the last round each block sits at one point (spread 0.0 against final_members), step 0 of round 0 = the discovery layout (digest equal), merge frames deterministic across two graph builds. GATE: ganymede in-package Cells with the boxs current ssv_graph (691476fa, members per round) and installed pack83 pinned: 8/8 passed (5 layout + 3 merge), 0 failed. Largest cell 257 < 272. Next step: org applies the frozen file on the box (copy-only, confirming gate), then close.")
