inl note_of_backend_primitive_parity_d2_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY-D2", 1u32, "2026-11-10T12:02Z", "compiler-88a146f8", "Slice of BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY (inventory D1: base.spi is the biggest portable gap). (=.) / (<>.) have arms for Gleam Lua Fsharp Python Rust TypeScript Zig Lean Kotlin but not C or Pascal. Add C = \\ () => !!!!EQ(a, b) and Pascal = ... (NEQ for <>.): the core op''s own codegen handles prims and strings on those backends, and an unsupported composite t becomes that backend''s clear codegen error instead of the no-arm failure. Plus ///> c and ///> pascal test targets on the existing i32 tests and a string test. Drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY/ with a .base per touched file; the parent keeps its gate step. TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_backend_primitive_parity_d2_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY-D2", 2u32, "2026-11-10T12:36Z", "compiler", "11-10 08:3x compiler: DRAFT 6 written: %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY/6-structural-equality-c-pascal.kitdo (5 replacements in lib/spiral/base.spi, over base 3e762c0a): C/Pascal arms for (=.) = !!!!EQ(a, b) : bool and (<>.) = !!!!NEQ(a, b) : bool; ///> c + ///> pascal on join_body_unit_6/7; new test structural_equality_compares_runtime_strings (c, pascal, rust; runtime ~ strings, = true, <> true, = false). First gate FAILED every test: without the : bool annotation the arm type is () -> _ (ETY-ValueRestriction, an unbound metavar), which the other arms avoid with : bool; fixed. GATE on ganymede (lib mirror, installed pack83 pinned, run_notebook --gate on base.spi): CONTROL (unmodified base.spi) 27/27 passed; DRAFT 28/28 passed, 0 failed. CAVEAT: ganymede has NO Free Pascal (no fpc anywhere), so the ///> pascal targets cannot have built there, yet the summary shows unsupported 0: Cells did not report the missing toolchain as unsupported (worth a Cells look). C and Rust are proven; Pascal waits for moon (fpc). Budget: the (=.) / (<>.) definition blocks grow 701->772 and 720->793 chars (they were already over 272, like 20 other base.spi definitions); the new test cell is 186.")
inl note_of_backend_primitive_parity_d2_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY-D2", 3u32, "2026-11-10T12:38Z", "compiler", "DoD: draft 6 applies cleanly to lib/spiral/base.spi; base.spis Cells gate passes on every target it already had plus c and pascal for (=.) / (<>.) and the runtime-string test; the control and draft runs differ only by the added rows. Next step: on moon (has fpc) when quiet, run base.spis gate with draft 6 applied and confirm the pascal rows execute and pass, then hand the program to the lib landing.")
inl note_of_backend_primitive_parity_d2_4 () = Note ("BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY-D2", 4u32, "2026-11-10T14:17Z", "compiler", "11-10 10:1x compiler: DONE and LANDED (unstaged): kit do applied draft 6 to the boxs lib/spiral/base.spi (3e762c0a -> 287db793). Pascal now PROVEN on moon (has fpc): base.spi gate with draft 6 on installed pack83, 28/28 passed, 0 failed (the pascal targets ran there, unlike on ganymede). Combined with ganymede (C + Rust + the existing targets, 28/28 vs a 27/27 control), every target of (=.) / (<>.) is proven.")
