inl cic_verdict_authority () = Task ("CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY", "typefeatureset equilibrium for the CIC kernel: make typing and conversion verdicts unforgeable (LCF-style), so the 9 dropped forged-authority negatives of the old CIC sample get a typed home", TaskKind, P3, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_verdict_authority () = Planning ("CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cic_verdict_authority_1 () = Note ("CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY", 1u32, "2026-11-10T12:06Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 groom 11-10 from CIC-NEGATIVES-MAP: the old sample made a verdict carry its subject terms in its type (corrected_cic_structural_defeq_pair_authority ctx sort and similar), so forging one was a type error; the kernel's verdicts (conversion defeq = Same | Different | NoFuel; typing inferred = Typed | Rejected) are public unions without their subjects, trusted by convention. Two designs: (a) verdicts indexed by phantom subject codes, as the SPS half does with GADT indices (cost: runtime terms are untyped, so the index would be a nominal stamp, not the term); (b) constructors private to their module, if Spiral can hide a constructor (a compiler question). TYPEFEATURES: the outcome decides whether the 9 negatives become fails blocks. DoD: a recorded decision with its reason, and either a gated draft of the chosen design with at least one forged-verdict fails block, or a note that the equilibrium stays runtime-trusted. NEXT STEP: ask compiler whether a module can export a type without its constructors")
inl note_of_cic_verdict_authority_2 () = Note ("CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY", 2u32, "2026-11-10T12:45Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 decision (compiler 11-10: Spiral has private unions, :| private name =; outside the module constructing a case fails with ETY-ModuleIndexFailed qualified or ETY-UnboundVariable after an open, while matching still works): design (b). Drafted: conversion.spi defeq and typing.spi inferred become private (grep shows no construction of Same/Different/NoFuel or Typed/Rejected outside their own modules; inductive and nested only match), and inductive.spi gains three fails blocks: a_defeq_verdict_cannot_be_forged_outside_conversion (Same [] -> UnboundVariable), a_typing_verdict_cannot_be_forged_outside_typing (Typed (Sort Zero) -> UnboundVariable), a_qualified_defeq_constructor_is_not_exported (conversion::Same [] -> ModuleIndexFailed). They stand for the 9 dropped forged-authority negatives (each forged an authority value the checker did not produce). Gating as org2-cva (inductive, typing, conversion, nested in a scratch package)")
inl note_of_cic_verdict_authority_3 () = Note ("CIC-VERDICT-AUTHORITY", 3u32, "2026-11-10T13:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 DONE, proof: ganymede org2-cva (pinned, scratch package = box kernel + the three drafts): inductive 24/24, typing 12/12, conversion 7/7, nested 5/5, 0 unsupported. On the box and mirror (unstaged): conversion.spi 1b080377b641 (:| private defeq), typing.spi f45988499d9e (:| private inferred), inductive.spi e467a1cce429 (+3 fails blocks: a_defeq_verdict_cannot_be_forged_outside_conversion and a_typing_verdict_cannot_be_forged_outside_typing fail with UnboundVariable, a_qualified_defeq_constructor_is_not_exported fails with ModuleIndexFailed). Matching outside the owning module still works (inductive and nested match Same/Typed and stay green). Decision recorded: the kernel's verdicts are now LCF-style, buildable only by the checker that owns them, which gives the old CIC sample's 9 forged-authority negatives a typed home")
