inl note_of_cells_port_cell_budget_d1_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-CELL-BUDGET-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T12:10Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 08:3x found in the migration audit: spi/cell_budget.spi (235 lines, a typed port of the X default profile: code-point weights, TLD-aware autolinks, top-level block scan, OverBudget findings, 5 rust tests) has NO consumer anywhere (no .spi imports it, no domain export), while lib/spiral/cells/cell_budget.ex (219) still does all of it. DoD: domain export text_weight green on the Gleam domain build; CellBudget.cell_weight(text) with the default profile returns the Spiral weight; a parity test over every top-level block of every tracked .spi shows 0 differences; cell_budget_test and cell_budget_ruled_test unchanged and green. TYPEFEATURES: cell_weight stays a nominal inside the Spiral module; the wire is an i32. NEXT STEP: after CELLS-PORT-MEMO-D1 proves the domain-export pattern on the node, draft the export and the delegating cell_weight.")
inl note_of_cells_port_cell_budget_d1_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-CELL-BUDGET-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T13:07Z", "microblog-b7595ac3", "microblog 11-10 13:0xZ first proof (ganymede job-1794314298484): the domain export builds and cell_budget_test + cell_budget_ruled_test + the new gleam wire test pass (26/27), but the 134735-text parity test TIMED OUT at 900 s. CAUSE (design, not semantics): every call shipped and re-split the full ~1500-entry TLD list and checked membership by linear scan, against Elixirs MapSet. FIX in the draft: CellBudget.cell_weight passes only the TLDs that occur as words in that text (one regex scan, downcased, MapSet filter, usually 0-3 entries). Semantics unchanged: a TLD absent from the text cannot match. RERUN: ganymede job-1794315972035-x-cb-d1-proof2.")
