inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_d1_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T12:27Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "Slice of FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE: drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE\\ with a .base per touched file; the parent keeps its gate step (regen of the MDF-e pair + both unit Cells gates + the repeated-line census). Lib side is live since 11-09 (FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-0-LIB-STAGED: staged walk, per-version witnesses, codec instances). Next step: read the live MDF-e family rows in families.spi and generate_versioned_family's signature in lib xsd_emit, then draft the families entry (core + v1.00 + v3.00 units wired by module dependencies, as CFDI complements are).")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_d1_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T12:45Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 09:5x RESCOPED BY A CODE READ: the slice is NOT pure fiscal authoring. Live lib xsd_emit's generate_versioned_family (:4128) still builds versions through member_parts -> module_parts = module_parts_with Reading (READER-ONLY), with no signatures or staging; MDF-e is a signed family whose unit today comes from generated_units_signed (staged_type_names + staged_units: signing-stage nominals, staged writers and examples, certificates). Routing MDF-e through it now would drop its writers, examples and signing stage. 0-LIB-STAGED (Done 11-09) added witnesses + codec instances to the versioned texts but not the staged walk. The lib already has the pieces: module_parts_staged staged signatures schema (:3650, staged_walk_texts = readers + staged writers/examples) and staged_type_names. DRAFT PLAN (lib, via lib_land_window, provable on ganymede): member_parts_staged signatures members + generate_versioned_family_staged signatures members core_module, reusing split_family / family_third; a test on a two-version signed demo family asserting the version unit carries the staged writer and the signing nominal. The fiscal wiring (families group + generator branch) follows once that lands. Next step: read split_family/family_third and the demo test at xsd_emit:4200, then draft the two functions and the test.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_d1_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D1", 3u32, "2026-11-10T14:24Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 11:3x LIB DRAFT + PROOF. Draft drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D1\\xsd_emit.spi (base live 070FB8C455DD) adds staged_member_parts, versioned_from and generate_versioned_family_staged so a versioned family keeps each member's staged writers (signatures in, writer per signed document), with tests a_signed_versioned_family_keeps_its_staged_writers and the control a_reader_only_versioned_family_has_no_staged_writer. Budget-neutral by the oracle (239 -> 239). PROOF 1 (job-1794318647761-fiscal-xsd-proof, ganymede, exact box lib tar, -PrivateLib -Apply) RED and auto-undone: type error at the fixture signed_versions, annotated xsd_schema final while read_schema returns xsd_schema written (the phase index is a phantom, so the annotation must name the phase the reader produces). Fixed in one token (final -> written), draft now FEE124468E4F, predicted box post-land digest 219CE68B16EA64C8. PROOF 2 (job-1794319762092-fiscal-xsd-proof2): node raw digest = box 11687AFCF8D33A6A, consumers compile, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (39 tests typed, control ok); executed_cells running. Next step: on a green close, land copy-only on the box with lib_land_window -ProvenLog (expect post-land 219CE68B16EA64C8), then hand the parent FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE its fiscal wiring step.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_d1_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D1", 4u32, "2026-11-10T15:18Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 11:2x PROOF GREEN, BOX LAND BLOCKED (not by this draft). ganymede job-1794319762092-fiscal-xsd-proof2 closed 'LANDED and closed green' on box lib 11687AFCF8D33A6A: consumers compile, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (39 typed), executed_cells 39/39 failed 0, respell 0; log at session scratchpad xsdproof\\proof2.log. The box lib then moved to 51EFFBD7FD7352E1 (xsd_emit still 070FB8C455DD) and lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply refused at its round trip with nothing written: 'no ROUNDTRIP row (VOID)', trace base.spi:275:15 (C = \\ () => !!!!EQ(a, b)). CONTROL: the UNCHANGED live xsd_emit gives the same VOID, so every box lib round trip fails since an unstaged base.spi change at 10:17 that adds C/Pascal arms the box's installed compiler does not resolve. Told the compiler lane. Next step: when the box round trip works again, rerun the same -ProvenLog -Apply land (post-land digest is re-predicted then).")
