inl compiler_cuda_switch_fallback () = Task ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", "Compiler: a backend_switch evaluated under CudaDevice/CudaHost with no arm for it falls back to its Cpp/CppHost arm, so lib code (run_target and friends) works inside ~~> CudaDevice kernels", Story, P1, D2, 70u32, Active, "", "compiler,cuda,backend,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_cuda_switch_fallback () = Planning ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_cuda_switch_fallback_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", 1u32, "2026-11-10T13:39Z", "tibia", "Filed 11-10 09:3x by tibia. Repro: tibia apps/predict cuda_lanes.spi (drafts\\tibia\\TIBIA-LANES-CUDA) calls lane_score inside ~~> CudaDevice under --backend 'Cpp + Cuda'; partial eval fails with 'Cannot find the backend CudaDevice in the backend switch op.' because lib backend_switch records have Cpp/CppHost keys but no CudaDevice/CudaHost (backend.spi run_target_args', is_rust, is_zig, and more). The lookup (spiral_compiler.fs PartEval BackendSwitch, about 11701-11750) only aliases Delphi to Pascal (backend_key_canonical). The draft patch (drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK\\patch.md) picks a current arm with a fallback (CudaDevice to Cpp, CudaHost to CppHost, only when the switch has no own arm), keeps s.backend unchanged so nested switches fall back too, and applies the same rule to UnsafeBackendSwitch. DoD: 3 tests (fallback taken; an explicit CudaDevice arm still wins; the cuda_lanes repro emits a __global__ kernel that nvcc links). Context: a minimal Spiral kernel already runs on a RunPod H100 (cuda_probe sum 2016 OK, 11-10), so this is what unblocks tibia lanes on the GPU. Next step: compiler reviews the patch, builds it into the next pack, and runs the 3 tests.")
inl note_of_compiler_cuda_switch_fallback_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", 2u32, "2026-11-10T14:24Z", "compiler", "11-10 10:2x compiler: IMPLEMENTED per tibias patch.md as %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/drafts/spiral/COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK/1-cuda-switch-fallback.kitdo (4 replacements): a shared cudaFallbackBackend helper after backend_key_canonical (CudaDevice -> Cpp, CudaHost -> CppHost, only when the switch has no arm of its own and has the Cpp/CppHost arm); BackendSwitch picks if backend = current (s.backend stays CudaDevice/CudaHost so nested switches fall back the same way, and every arm is still validated for its type); UnsafeBackendSwitch uses the same current. Candidate pack84 = pack83 + it (core 3d79bd59). GATE running on ganymede (~/remote-stage/pack84/g.log): two probes compiled with --backend \"Cpp + Cuda\": fallback (switch with only Cpp/CppHost inside ~~> CudaDevice: pack83 must fail with Cannot find the backend CudaDevice, pack84 must emit the Cpp arm 7001) and explicit (a CudaDevice arm 7003 must win on both); full suite vs pack83. No GPU on ganymede: the device run stays tibias H100 step. TypeFeatures: none (partial evaluation).")
inl note_of_compiler_cuda_switch_fallback_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", 3u32, "2026-11-10T14:29Z", "compiler", "11-10 10:3x compiler: PROBES PASS on ganymede (pack84 built, core 3d79bd59): fallback probe (switch with only Cpp/CppHost inside ~~> CudaDevice, --backend \"Cpp + Cuda\"): pack83 rc 5 \"Cannot find the backend CudaDevice\" (tibias bug reproduced), pack84 rc 0 and the device code carries the Cpp arm (= 7001); explicit probe (switch with its own CudaDevice arm): pack83 and pack84 both emit = 7003, so an explicit arm still wins. Full suite vs pack83 running. Next step: suite diff, then put + install pack84 (Linux first), then tibia reruns cuda_lanes on the H100.")
inl note_of_compiler_cuda_switch_fallback_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", 4u32, "2026-11-10T14:48Z", "tibia", "11-10 10:4x tibia: pack84 (compiler's implementation) VERIFIED on the tibia repro (job tibia-cuda-lanes3, pinned pack84 on ganymede): the CudaDevice error is gone. The next blocker: 'This program reaches a lib/spiral backend_switch that has no arm for the CppHost backend'. Lib census: 241 backend_switch blocks lack CppHost, 236 of them lack Cpp and C too (sm' 32, date_time 27, near 22, base 21, am' 17, convert 12 ...). Asked compiler to (1) name the switch in the FatalError and (2) extend the chain to CppHost -> Cpp -> C and CudaHost/CudaDevice through C. Next step: after compiler names the switch or extends the chain, rerun the tibia lanes gate.")
inl note_of_compiler_cuda_switch_fallback_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-CUDA-SWITCH-FALLBACK", 5u32, "2026-11-10T14:56Z", "compiler", "11-10 10:5x compiler: pack84 GATED (suite 7640 rows 0 diffs vs pack83; probes as designed) and INSTALLED on ganymede 14:42Z (quiet-window loop); store linux-x64 put (base v2 files-3fffae25). tibia confirmed on the real repro: the CudaDevice error is gone; next stop was the lib wrappers \"no arm for the CppHost backend\" marker. Two follow-ups per tibia: (a) LIB program 2-lib-cpp-falls-back-to-c.kitdo: backend.spis backend_switch wrapper routes Cpp and CppHost through cpp_or_c (records Cpp arm, else its C arm, else the old markers); (b) COMPILER program 3-fallback-chain-to-c.kitdo: op-level chain CudaDevice -> Cpp -> C, CudaHost -> CppHost -> Cpp -> C, CppHost -> Cpp -> C (first arm present wins, explicit arms still win). pack85 = pack84 + (b), core ca04c6bc; gate running on ganymede (probes fallback / explicit / conly (switch with only a C arm inside ~~> CudaDevice must emit 7004) + suite vs pack84). The lib program lands after tibias repro passes with both.")
inl cells_port_compiler_client_d1 () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT-D1", "draft: the compiler daemon line codec through Spiral: export daemon.spi's typed request encoding and reply decoding (compile ask, status, hello, pool) to the domain; compiler_client.ex builds request lines and parses replies through it instead of hand-built tab strings; parity test over a table of requests and recorded daemon replies; drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT-D1 with a .base per file", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,cells-in-spiral,daemon,typefeatureset,team:microblog,split-on-demand", "current", "current")
