inl note_of_hook_smart_rust_gate_d1_1 () = Note ("HOOK-SMART-RUST-GATE-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T15:23Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Slice of HOOK-SMART-RUST-GATE: org3 11-10 note 17 lists the four rules and says HOOK-GATE-RUST-CORE carries them, but no item has that id, so this slice is the carrier. Drafts go to kit src as a new pure package (no tracked file touched); the parent keeps its gate step (the Rust gate binary reads the precomputed ranking).")
inl note_of_hook_smart_rust_gate_d1_2 () = Note ("HOOK-SMART-RUST-GATE-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T15:38Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 11:5x rig: DONE, probe-green (new pure package kit src/rig_ready_rank/rank.spi, HostFree, unstaged, hash adb876ef56b9; Cells notebook gate on ganymede 2/2). TYPEFEATURES: item_priority union, reason union with payloads (FinishChain :: epic id, NearDone :: progress, Unowned :: idle days), records epic, ready_item, weights, ranked; weights are DATA (band 100, finish_chain 150, near_done_at 80 / near_done 120, unowned_days 2 / unowned 60), so tuning needs no code change. Rules of org3 note 17: (1) finish-the-chain: a ready child of a STARTED epic (a Done sibling or progress > 0) gets +150, which beats fresh work of its own band AND the band above (the regex-video fixture: SSV-LAYOUT P1 under a started epic ranks above a fresh P0), an unstarted epic gives nothing; (2) unowned N days: flagged as a reason (+60), never silent; (3) skill-fit: the first route whose tag the item carries names the lane; (4) near done: progress >= 80 gets +120 (BEND P0 92% -> score 480). Ranking is a stable merge sort (lib list_sort, STRICT predicate: a non-strict one breaks stability), ties keep the input order. rank_line renders one explained row (BEND score=480 -> compiler (near done 92%, unstarted 3 days)). Proof: the two tests pin the fixture order and every reason.")
inl compiler_perceus_fbip_d1 () = Task ("COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP-D1", "draft: a design note on where Perceus reuse analysis (FBIP) runs relative to partial evaluation, read against today's compiler (refcount prepass, PartEval, codegen)", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_perceus_fbip_d1 () = Planning ("COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP-D1", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_perceus_fbip_d1_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T15:23Z", "tibia-ac4b4e98", "Slice of COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP: drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP\\ with a .base per touched file; the parent keeps its gate step. DoD: the note names the pass order (PE, then refcount insertion, then reuse), the IR it reads, the ownership union (Owned | Borrowed | Reusable), which backends get reuse first, and the samples and benchmarks that prove byte-identical output; with file:line evidence from spiral_compiler.fs.")
inl note_of_compiler_perceus_fbip_d1_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T15:26Z", "tibia", "11-10 11:3x tibia: DESIGN NOTE DONE: drafts\\spiral\\COMPILER-PERCEUS-FBIP\\design.md. Read against spiral_compiler.fs. Partial evaluation (PartEvalEngine 8921 on) yields typed TypedBind[]; refc_prepass' (26617) runs per backend on it and already computes the drop points (g_decr via refc_used_vars), initial ownership (g_incr), call and constructor ownership (g_op, g_op_decr) and per-join-point borrowing (borrowed key i); consumers are CodegenC (26972, 27011-27034, 27298), the Pascal refc variant and Python del (29372); Rust uses Rc with no prepass. DECISION: the order is partial evaluation, then refc_prepass, then a NEW backend-independent reuse pass (a token table keyed by TypedBind), then codegen. It goes after PE because FBIP pairs (an unbox arm rebuilding the same shape) only become visible and sized after specialization and inlining; it goes after refc because reuse needs exactly g_decr's drop points. Ownership as a union Owned | Borrowed | Reusable of size; no tokens across TyWhile or join points in v1. Backends: C first, then Pascal refc, then Rust (Rc::try_unwrap), then Cuda after COMPILER-CUDA-ARRAY-LENGTH. Proof plan: byte-identical sample output with reuse on and off (C, Rust), a negative test where an rc 2 scrutinee is never reused, and benchmarks (listm samples, tibia lanes, transformer CPU) on a quiet node. proof: code read with file:line evidence; analysis-only slice.")
