inl note_of_kit_release_train_d1_1 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T15:46Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "Slice of KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN (notes 263-264: TRAIN43f r1 release timed out at 1 h on a loaded box, r2 refused -Resume after the 09:24 pack). The draft shares %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\TRAIN-ON-NODE\\scripts\\release-train.ps1 (+ .base) with TRAIN-ON-NODE-D1, so one file lands once; the parent keeps its gate step (TRAIN44 runs it).")
inl note_of_kit_release_train_d1_2 () = Note ("KIT-RELEASE-TRAIN-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T15:50Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 12:0x rig: DONE as a draft in the shared file %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\TRAIN-ON-NODE\\scripts\\release-train.ps1 (base = live, verified; PowerShell parse 0 errors). (1) RESUME AND PIN: when the live core moved after the pin, -Resume now continues ON THE PIN with a line saying so (every earlier phase of the train used it), and refuses only when no pin exists, the case where copying the live compiler would really mix. This is what r3 did by hand with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL. (2) RELEASE TIMEOUT: when build.ps1 fails and release.log holds command timed out after, the first log is kept as release-timed-out.log and build.ps1 runs once more (cargo keeps the crates built, as r1 to r3 showed); a second failure still stops. Residual, not in this draft: a FIRST box-half launch pins whatever compiler is live then, which can differ from the node half when a pack lands between them; the box pin should be checked against the core the node logged (compiler at end ... core X) before the release. DoD: both changes drafted and reviewed in this note; proof is TRAIN44 (it lands with TRAIN-ON-NODE-D1, one file).")
