inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1_mdfe_d2_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D2", 2u32, "2026-11-10T22:55Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 19:1x DRAFT drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES-1-MDFE-D2\\xsd_emit.spi 3AF2661A013F over .base 05ED9255E232 (the FISCAL-TYPED-UNITS-D1 SCC draft, in proof). Changes: staged_of (the record update staged_units already does inline) and staged_member_parts now stage the signed types; family_core_text takes a prelude placed where main_unit_text puts it (after the codec and carrier preludes); the prelude threads emit_family_split / emit_split_shared / emit_split_first into split_family_with, and split_family = split_family_with with an empty prelude, so generate_family and generate_versioned_family are unchanged; versioned_from takes it and generate_versioned_family_staged passes staging_prelude. Tests: a_signed_versioned_family_stages_its_signed_types (versions contain 'nominal x_t_doc s ='), control a_reader_only_versioned_family_stays_unstaged, a_signed_versioned_core_opens_the_staging_types_once, control a_reader_only_versioned_core_has_no_staging_prelude. Cell budget held at 239 -> 239 (two renames, the staged_of helper, tests split into positive and control). Known difference kept: certificate items stay inline in the core or versions rather than a separate unit. Next step: ganymede round trip and type probe (job label fiscal-mdfe-d2-check, mirror fiscal-xsd2), then a lib proof after the SCC draft lands.")
