inl note_of_fiscal_regex_lib_adapter_d1_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T23:28Z", "fiscal-84b53718", "fiscal 11-10 20:4x DRAFT drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER-D1\\xsd_regex.spi 48B13BA45027 over live 6F570A3ACBDE (.base kept). DESIGN, chosen to keep generated text identical: RxClass now carries (negated, written ranges, normalized regex_charset set); the set is built ONCE by the new smart constructor rx_class (via class_set) at every construction site (parser classes, escapes, properties, dot, single). Membership and the canonical-engine conversion go through the set: derive uses regex_charset::contains (was in_ranges over raw ranges xor negated) and to_re passes the set to regex_syntax::Set (was class_set renormalizing on EVERY to_re call, and nullable calls to_re on every derivative step). ORDER is untouched: rx_compare still compares (negated, written ranges), so alternative sorting and DFA state dedupe, and therefore generated validator text, should not change; the identity regen proves that. No RxClass pattern outside xsd_regex (checked all lib). class_example and range_points still read the written ranges. New tests: a_class_keeps_its_written_order, a_class_matches_through_its_normal_set. Budget 54 -> 54. Next step: europa round trip + type probe (job label fiscal-regex-adapter-check), then the parent's proof: the 8 xsd_regex tests + xpath_eval 27 + the 4 corpus engines vs .NET + the generator identity regen (0 differing files) on a node.")
