inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_1 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-10T23:27Z", "compiler-88a146f8", "Slice of RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION: drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION\\ with a .base per touched file; the parent keeps its gate step. TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_2 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-10T23:27Z", "compiler", "DoD: a self-checking sample (samples core: dotted operators) with a 4-way or-pattern into one non-trivial body, its Rust/C outputs showing how many times that body is emitted, and the source location of the duplication with a proposed fix shape. TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_3 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 3u32, "2026-11-10T23:32Z", "compiler", "11-10 19:3x compiler: DRAFTED. Finding first: bound OR-patterns are already deduplicated (OrPatternJoin.lift turns the body into a join point; or_pattern_bound_alternatives main.rs emits the body once as method1). The remaining shape is the WILDCARD STAIRCASE: an earlier clause with >= 2 refutable tests (Red, Red) makes every later clause body reachable from several failure paths, and peval copies it per path (3x in wildcard_pair_dyn, 11-05). Program drafts\\spiral\\RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION\\1-lift-shared-fail-continuations.kitdo (3 replacements in OrPatternJoin): count refutable tests per pattern; a non-trivial clause body after an earlier clause with >= 2 tests is lifted into a join point the same way or-pattern bodies are; nothing is lifted when any clause in the match is type-directed (a join point would lose type refinement). Sample samples/match_wildcard_shared_fallback (self-checking, samples core, expected exit 57; registered under Fsharp,C,Rust,Pascal). pack90 = pack89 + this (core 9b0d944f), gating on ganymede: body copies pack89 vs pack90 on Rust and C, C run, suite vs pack89. Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack90/g.log at \"p90 done\".")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_4 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 4u32, "2026-11-10T23:36Z", "compiler", "11-10 19:4x compiler: pack90 PROBES PASS (ganymede, sample match_wildcard_shared_fallback): Rust: wildcard body copies pack89 3 -> pack90 1, 64 -> 59 lines; C: 90 -> 85 lines, both runs exit 57 (expected). Suite vs pack89 running. Next step: \"p90 done\" verdict (only output shrink may change, exits identical); then the parent gates the Rust byte comparison over every sample.")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_5 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 5u32, "2026-11-11T00:32Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:3x compiler: pack90 suite RED, draft WITHDRAWN. vs pack89: 216 compile diffs (ok -> error) on 18 backends (Zig 39, Fsharp 19, Rust 15, C/Gleam/Kotlin/Pascal/Python/Swift/TypeScript 13 each, ...), all type errors after lifting, e.g. contract_full main.spi:25:5 \"Unification failure. Got: .xml -> string Expected: (nfe_signed : *)\": a match that branches on SYMBOL patterns (resolved statically, so they refine types) had its fallback lifted into a join point, which loses that refinement. My typeDirected guard did not count PatSymbol (nor static PatValue). Packs 91-94 rebased onto pack89 without this program (ganymede sources replaced before their builds started). Next step: redo the lift with a stricter guard, lifting only when every refutable test in the earlier clauses is a run-time union-case test (PatUnbox on a dynamic scrutinee), and treat any PatSymbol/PatValue/typeDirected clause as a stop; re-gate on the full suite.")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_6 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 6u32, "2026-11-11T00:40Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:4x compiler: REDRAFTED stricter as drafts\\spiral\\RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION\\2-lift-shared-fail-union-only.kitdo (3 replacements against the live core; program 1 stays withdrawn). New guard: a non-trivial fallback body is lifted only when EVERY clauses pattern is structural (PatVar, wildcard PatE, unit PatB, PatPair, PatUnbox union-case tests, nothing else: no PatSymbol, PatValue, PatAnnot, PatWhen, records, arrays) and an earlier clause makes >= 2 union-case tests. A failed union-case test adds no type information, so the join point cannot lose a refinement, which is exactly what broke contract_fulls symbol-pattern match in pack90. pack97 = pack89 + this (core d97e67ca), queued on ganymede after pack96: probe match_wildcard_shared_fallback (Rust body copies 3 -> 1, C exit 57) and the full suite vs pack89 (the bar is 0 compile diffs). Open question the probe settles: whether nullary cases like Red parse as PatUnbox(..., PatB); if they parse otherwise the sample is not lifted and the copies stay 3.")
inl note_of_rust_match_duplication_d1_7 () = Note ("RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION-D1", 7u32, "2026-11-11T01:25Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:2x compiler: pack97 PROBE PASS (stricter union-only guard): match_wildcard_shared_fallback Rust body copies 3 -> 1 (64 -> 59 lines), C 90 -> 85 lines, both C runs exit 57. So nullary cases (Red, Green) do parse as union-case tests and the structural guard admits this sample. The deciding check is the suite (pack90 broke 216 rows); running now.")
