inl note_of_codegen_readable_2_c_1 () = Note ("CODEGEN-READABLE-2-C", 1u32, "2026-11-10T23:54Z", "compiler-88a146f8", "Step (2) of CODEGEN-READABLE-2, C first (the oracle). TypeFeatures: none. DoD: every C output names unions by source (US_<name> / UH_<name>, _<tag> only on a same-name collision, the old US<tag> form only when no source name exists); C native run over the whole suite with no new build-fail and no new DISAGREE vs the C oracle; outputs differ only in names.")
inl note_of_codegen_readable_2_c_2 () = Note ("CODEGEN-READABLE-2-C", 2u32, "2026-11-10T23:54Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:0x compiler: DRAFTED drafts\\spiral\\CODEGEN-READABLE-2\\1-c-union-source-names.kitdo (26 replacements, generated from the live cores exact lines with automatic context for non-unique anchors). UnionRecC gains name; codegenCs union memo takes a prefix (US / UH, since stack and heap count tags separately) and mints the name once from unionSourceNames (sanitized to ASCII letters/digits/_), adding _<tag> on a collision and falling back to US<tag>; all 24 mint lines (type names, typedefs, case constructors, incref/decref and their bodies, and the refcount calls emitted for nested unions) read it. Helpers become <name>_incref / _decref / _incref_body / _decref_body. 0 old-style mint strings left in codegenC. pack91 = pack90 + this (core 8590ee7d), queued on ganymede after HOPACSOTA-P3: build, or_pattern_bound_alternatives on C (gcc build + run), then test.ps1 -Backend C -Native over the whole suite. Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack91/g.log at \"p91 done\".")
inl note_of_codegen_readable_2_c_3 () = Note ("CODEGEN-READABLE-2-C", 3u32, "2026-11-11T01:07Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:1x compiler: PROBE (ganymede pack91, rebased on pack89): or_pattern_bound_alternatives on C emits typedef ... US_shape, constructors US_shape_Circle / US_shape_Square / US_shape_Triangle, gcc builds, exit 41. Whole-suite C native: 554 ran, 5 build-fail (all abi_external_* negatives or mismatch samples, which are meant to fail at the C build), 40 compile errors (top-level samples, consistent with expected-error rows). PENDING, not green: there is no pack89 C-native run to diff against, so \"no new build-fail / DISAGREE\" is not shown yet. Next step: the same C-native run with pack89 on ganymede, then diff native/exit per row.")
