inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-11T00:00Z", "compiler-88a146f8", "Slice of LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP: drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP\\ as a kitdo against the live core; the parent keeps its linked_* row gate. TypeFeatures: none new (nominal records/unions cross as types defined once in the owning unit).")
inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:00Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:0x compiler: ENTRY POINTS located (live core pack89). (1) spiral_compiler.fs build_many (~37677): ExternCalls.wrapped is set only for Rust/Gleam/Zig, and ExternCalls.current gets one Call row per backend: Rust {call = unit::e; borrow_strings; struct_records}, Gleam {call = unit.e; import_text = import unit; flat_records}, Zig {call = unit.e; import_text = const unit = @import(...)}. F# falls to Map.empty, so a linked F# consumer has no calls. (2) ExternCalls (~10226): the Call records ABI flags (struct_records, flat_records, multi_ranges, copy_tuples, pascal_records) decide how records/tuples cross; callable/blocker refuse functions and macros. (3) F# exports already exist (codegenFsharp export path; samples fsharp_export_closure_shared_use, FSHARP-EXPORT-DEAD-LET). DRAFT PLAN: add Fsharp to the wrapped condition; add an F# row {call = Unit.e; import_text = None (fully qualified); borrow_strings = false; unit_path = Unit.; struct_records = true (records cross as the owning units nominal type); flat_records = false; multi_ranges = true (F# tuples); copy_tuples = false}. Then the driver: test.ps1 linked_* on Fsharp compiles one .fs per unit in dependency order into one fsproj (Compile Include order), the later per-unit assemblies step being the parents. Next step: write the kitdo and probe it on one 2-unit linked sample.")
inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 3u32, "2026-11-11T00:03Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:0x compiler: DRAFTED both halves. (1) Compiler drafts\\spiral\\LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP\\1-fsharp-extern-call-row.kitdo: build_many gets an Fsharp Call row: call = <Unit>.<export> with the unit name capitalized (fsi names a #load-ed model.fsx module Model), import_text None, borrow_strings false, struct_records/flat_records false (first step: scalars, strings and tuples cross; records are refused at the boundary by ExternCalls.blocker until a later step decides the record ABI), multi_ranges true, copy_tuples false. (2) Harness 2-linked-fsharp-runner.kitdo for scripts/test.ps1 (3 replacements; parses): unit extension fsx, a run.fsx that #loads every non-root unit in build order before the root plus the same exit pipe as single-file F#, run with dotnet fsi --exec. pack92 = pack91 + (1) (core cc621ca4), queued on ganymede after pack91: compile linked_records model + app on F#, list the Model.* calls, run the #load chain with fsi (want exit 13, as Zig and Gleam). The shared mirrors test.ps1/matrix are NOT touched by the probe. Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack92/g.log at \"p92 done\"; then add Fsharp to the linked rows Backends and land (2).")
inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 4u32, "2026-11-11T00:03Z", "compiler", "DoD: linked_records builds on F# as two units (model.fsx + app main.fsx) and the #load chain exits 13 like Zig and Gleam, with the app calling Model.* (not inlined); the harness program applies and parses. TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 5u32, "2026-11-11T01:07Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:1x compiler: PROBE PARTIAL (ganymede pack92 rebased on pack89): model and app both compile on F#, and the #load chain runs with exit 13 (want 13), BUT the app contains no Model.* call: the export was inlined into the app, so the F# Call row was never used. Likely cause: ExternCalls.current is filled from file_linked_units, whose calls map for F# is empty when the unit build has not produced an F# interface (the wrapped/units graph is computed for Rust/Gleam/Zig paths). Next step: trace why l.calls is empty for an F# consumer (SPIRAL_AUTO_EXPORT_TRACE=1 on the app compile) and feed the F# units exports into the link graph.")
inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_6 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 6u32, "2026-11-11T01:37Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:3x compiler: ROOT CAUSE of the inlined Model calls found by reading the dispatch (spiral_compiler.fs ~37705-37740): only the Gleam, Rust and Zig branches call writeUnitGraph; F# used the plain build helper, so an F# unit never writes its <stem>.unit.json, readUnitCalls finds nothing, the consumers ExternCalls map is empty and the export is inlined. Program 3 drafts\\spiral\\LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP\\3-fsharp-writes-unit-graph.kitdo replaces the F# dispatch with the Rust-shaped branch (file_linked_units, DeadPureLetElision, writeUnitGraph, codegenFsharp, UnusedGlobals.prune). pack101 = rebased pack92 (Call row) + program 3 (core 6b2b4c77), queued on europa (load gate): linked_records model then app on F#, expect Model.* calls in the app and the #load chain exit 13. Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack101/g.log at \"p101 done\".")
inl note_of_linked_units_fsharp_d1_7 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP-D1", 7u32, "2026-11-11T01:46Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:4x compiler: PROBE PASS for step 1 (europa pack101 = pack89 + 1-fsharp-extern-call-row + 3-fsharp-writes-unit-graph): linked_records on F#, model unit and app both compile; the app now CALLS Model.model_pair across the unit boundary (pack92 inlined everything), and the #load chain runs with exit 13 (want 13). Only model_pair crosses: the samples other exports (model_norm, model_make, model_label_len) involve records, which step 1 deliberately keeps from crossing (struct_records = false), so they are still inlined, as designed. Remaining for the parent LINKED-UNITS-FSHARP: (a) the record ABI on F# (records crossing as the owning units nominal type), (b) landing the harness program 2 and adding Fsharp to the linked rows Backends, (c) per-unit assemblies later. Programs 1 + 3 are a coherent first landing.")
