inl note_of_stable_entry_points_d1_1 () = Note ("STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS-D1", 1u32, "2026-11-11T00:13Z", "compiler-88a146f8", "Slice of STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS: drafts go to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS\\ as a kitdo; the parent keeps its gate (the 3 linked_rust_auto_export samples with their dummy mains removed, then kits 126 export-carrier mains). TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_stable_entry_points_d1_2 () = Note ("STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:13Z", "compiler", "Design (11-10 20:1x compiler, read from the live core): the refusal is spiral_compiler.fs build body() (~37638): Map.tryFind \"main\" env.term -> | _, None -> \"Cannot find main\". The auto-export path (| _, Some main when file_auto_export ... = Some \"monomorphic\") already WRAPS an existing main with the export calls, so a library unit only needs an entry to hang them on. Option A (rejected): synthesize EFun in env.term; env.term holds lowered E whose EFun carries Scope (free-variable data computed by the prepass), so a hand-built node is fragile. Option B (chosen): at the source level, when the files package has autoExport = monomorphic, no test_entry and no main, add a synthetic block := main () : i32 = 0i32 to that files module before prepass, so scopes are computed normally; emitted outputs must be byte-identical to todays dummy-main units. Next step: find the per-file block list feeding prepass (blockParsing / module load for the built file) and draft option B.")
inl note_of_stable_entry_points_d1_3 () = Note ("STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS-D1", 3u32, "2026-11-11T00:16Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:2x compiler: DRAFTED option B: drafts\\spiral\\STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS\\1-no-main-library-unit.kitdo (1 replacement). The typecheck streams end case gets a guarded arm: in an auto-export package (autoExportPids, the same set AutoExportCurried.synthesize uses), a module whose env.term has no main gets a synthetic BundleInl main = \\ () => (0i32 : i32), inferred and appended to the stream like AutoExportCurrieds extra bundle, so prepass sees ordinary source and computes scopes itself; then the plain end case runs. pack93 = pack92 + this (core b3d42986), queued on ganymede after pack92: for each of the 3 linked_rust_auto_export model units, Rust output with the dummy main kept (pack92 vs pack93: must be identical) and with the dummy removed (pack92 must refuse with Cannot find main; pack93 output must equal todays dummy-main output). Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack93/g.log at \"p93 done\".")
inl note_of_stable_entry_points_d1_4 () = Note ("STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS-D1", 4u32, "2026-11-11T00:16Z", "compiler", "DoD: an auto-export package with no main builds as a library unit, with Rust output byte-identical to the same unit with its dummy main; units that keep their main are unchanged; pack92 still refuses the no-main unit (proves the arm is what changed). TypeFeatures: none.")
inl note_of_stable_entry_points_d1_5 () = Note ("STABLE-ENTRY-POINTS-D1", 5u32, "2026-11-11T01:07Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:1x compiler: PROBE (ganymede pack93, rebased on pack89): linked_rust_auto_export and linked_rust_auto_export_curried PASS every check: with the dummy main kept, pack92 and pack93 Rust outputs are identical; with the dummy removed, pack92 refuses (\"Cannot find main in file model\") and pack93 builds the unit with output byte-identical to todays dummy-main output. The third sample (linked_rust_auto_export_modules) was mis-probed: its model units entry is not the first *.spi (the probe compiled arith.spi, which has no main either way), so it says nothing. DoD met on 2 of 3; the third needs its real entry file. Next step: rerun the third with the right entry, then the suite vs pack89.")
