inl note_of_store_typed_cas_d1_2 () = Note ("STORE-TYPED-CAS-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:28Z", "rig-fc1568a6", "11-10 20:3x rig: model WRITTEN (kit src/rig_store_key/key.spi, new pure package, unstaged), probe queued on ganymede. TYPEFEATURES: entry_kind union, key_spec and input records, matrix_row union with a payload per outcome (Misses | StaleHit | HitsOutside | Overkeyed :: input name). key_of keeps only the spec's fields and length-frames every name and value (n:text), so two different input splits can never share a key. matrix edits each input once: an input in the build's reach that leaves the key unchanged is a StaleHit (fiscal's forgotten-prelude case), an input outside the reach that moves the key is Overkeyed; failures lists only those. DoD: three tests green (forgotten/complete/greedy specs, framing, run-time names). Not in this slice: the entry GADT with phantom tier and sealing, the backend union, reflection over typed input records (the matrix is what proves a hand-listed spec today).")
