inl note_of_mega_stale_negatives_1 () = Note ("MEGA-STALE-NEGATIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-11T00:51Z", "compiler", "Found 11-10 20:5x (MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER census): 247 mega negative dirs, 236 ExpectedErrors rules; the 11 without a rule were recompiled on ganymede (installed pack89, Zig): at least 8 fail with ETY-UnboundVariable on names that no longer exist, e.g. brzozowski negative_antimirov_missing_finite_authority (Unbound constraint symbol_compare; Unbound term RegexChar), omniledger negative_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority_wrong_endpoint (Unbound type erp_p2p_three_owner_physi...), zeta negative_descent_unavailable_divisor_wrong_child (Unbound type certified_interval_positive_position...). Stale negatives pass as failures without checking anything. List: brzozowski negative_antimirov_missing_finite_authority, negative_forge_constructive_minimality_witness, negative_forge_structural_support_bound; omniledger negative_recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch, negative_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority_wrong_endpoint; spiral_proves negative_beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport (fails 'Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var'); zeta negative_descent_unavailable_divisor_wrong_child, negative_legacy_completion_raw_classification, negative_mixed_contradiction_obligation_not_rejection, negative_mixed_rejected_obstruction_not_found_consistency, negative_recursive_divisor_refusal_wrong_child. Logs: ganymede ~/remote-stage/negs/*.log. TypeFeatures: none. DoD: each repaired negative fails with its INTENDED type error (Got/Expected on the property it names) and has an ExpectedErrors rule with that text; a negative that cannot be repaired is archived with a reason. Next step: for each, find the renamed definition (git log -S on the old name) and rewrite the negative's body against it.")
inl note_of_mega_stale_negatives_2 () = Note ("MEGA-STALE-NEGATIVES", 2u32, "2026-11-11T00:53Z", "compiler", "11-10 20:5x compiler: CLASSIFIED (git grep over tracked mega sources + git log -S). Class A, property no longer modeled (8): every name the omniledger, zeta and spiral_proves stale negatives need (erp_p2p_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority, certified_interval_positive_positional_legacy_completion_refusal, certified_arithmetic_rooted_ordered_prime_power_nf_uniqueness_mixed_second_prime_*) was last touched in 1eb2ecfd (2026-09-27) and exists in 0 non-negative files today: the definitions were removed from the megas, so these negatives guard nothing. Decision rule (archive-never-delete): archive each with a hash-verified kit archive and a restore line, reason \"property removed from the mega in 1eb2ecfd\". Class B, import drift (3, brzozowski): their names still exist, but bit_alphabet / bit_finite_length now live only in sample compiler_probe_finite_vector_rank and RegexChar / symbol_compare come through antimirov_certificates own deps; repair by importing the defining package (or defining the alphabet locally) and confirming the INTENDED error. spiral_proves negative_beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport fails \"Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var\", which may be its real intent; check against its name before classifying. Next step: Class B repairs first (3 small spiproj/import edits, validated on a node), then the Class A archive in one batch.")
inl note_of_mega_stale_negatives_3 () = Note ("MEGA-STALE-NEGATIVES", 3u32, "2026-11-11T00:55Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:0x compiler: CORRECTED split after checking all 11 individually (ganymede ~/remote-stage/negs, installed pack89, Zig): 3 are REAL negatives that only lacked a rule, now registered in tests/matrix.psd1 (box, unstaged; 434 ExpectedErrors; both TermError texts confirmed against the logs): negative_forge_structural_support_bound (Contains \"Got: antimirov_support_slot_assignment shape (finite_length_succ\", fresh type-variable names left out), negative_recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch (\"Expected: erp_p2p_event_outbox (nat_succ (nat_succ (nat_succ nat_zero)))\"), negative_beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport (\"Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var\", which matches its name). 8 are STALE (fail only on ETY-UnboundVariable): brzozowski negative_antimirov_missing_finite_authority and negative_forge_constructive_minimality_witness (import drift: names live in other packages now), omniledger negative_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority_wrong_endpoint and zeta negative_descent_unavailable_divisor_wrong_child, negative_legacy_completion_raw_classification, negative_mixed_contradiction_obligation_not_rejection, negative_mixed_rejected_obstruction_not_found_consistency, negative_recursive_divisor_refusal_wrong_child (definitions removed in 1eb2ecfd, 2026-09-27). Next step: repair the 2 brzozowski imports; archive the 6 removed-property negatives with the kit archive tool and a restore line.")
inl note_of_mega_stale_negatives_4 () = Note ("MEGA-STALE-NEGATIVES", 4u32, "2026-11-11T01:06Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:1x compiler: brzozowski import repair TRIED in a scratch tree on ganymede (~/remote-stage/negfix: symlinks to the mirrors mega children plus a modified copy of negative_antimirov_missing_finite_authority; the mirror was not touched). The negative needs root definitions (symbol_compare in mega_brzozowski_derivatives/main.spi, RegexChar) AND the sub-package function antimirov_certificate; modules do not re-export, and every two-package spelling is refused: packageDir ../.. + \"mega_brzozowski_derivatives/antimirov_certificate-\" (no slash in a package path); \"|mega.../antimirov_certificate-\" (same); packageDir .. + \"../mega_brzozowski_derivatives-\" (resolves under packageDir: \"not loaded\"); packageDir .. + \".-\" (\"Self referential links are not allowed\"). No mega negative imports two packages today. So the repair is structural: either (a) the root package lists the antimirov_certificate module (the root package.spiproj modules are main, runtime_workload, runtime_interned), or (b) the negative is rewritten against antimirov_certificates own exports with a locally defined lone alphabet and regex value. Next step: pick (b) if antimirov_certificate exposes a regex builder, else (a), and confirm the intended \"missing finite authority\" error.")
