inl note_of_backend_bench_ci_5_faithful_d1_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL-D1", 2u32, "2026-11-11T01:01Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:1x compiler: PROTOCOL v1 (drafts\\spiral\\BACKEND-BENCH-CI-5-FAITHFUL\\aa.sh, bash -n ok). Inputs: microblogs bench_cells notebook and receipt rows (SPIRAL_CELLS_PHASE_ROWS: name, backend, queue, mount, compile, build, run, fused). Runs: R=5 consecutive runs on one node, each started only after a 60 s quiet window (load < 0.8 for 12 samples x 5 s), memo off, Zig ReleaseFast split. Verdict per cell (workload x backend): median run ms over R, spread = (max - min) / median; A/A ok when spread <= 10% (or <= 5 ms absolute for tiny cells). Faithful when (1) >= 90% of cells are A/A ok, (2) per workload the backend ranking by median is identical in >= 4 of 5 runs, (3) the opaque-round chain holds (C float stays ~270 ms, not 21) and (4) later, CI medians agree with node medians within a stated factor per backend (step 6). The bootstrap CI from lib bench_model.spi (BACKEND-BENCH-CI-4-STATS) replaces the min/max spread in v2. TypeFeatures: none.")
