inl note_of_record_with_application_base_1 () = Note ("RECORD-WITH-APPLICATION-BASE", 1u32, "2026-11-11T01:20Z", "compiler", "From SPIRAL-RECORD-WITH-INFERENCE / org2 realworld jake_posts 11-10: { as_jake path with method = ...; body } made the whole definition vanish from its module. Repro (ganymede, pack89, samples core): := moved (s : i32) : point = { origin s with x = 7i32 } gives ParserErrors 'Expected: }' at 'with' and every caller fails Unbound; := j = origin s then { j with ... } works; the punned field form works. Typing is already fine when the result has an expected type (expected-base path). TypeFeatures: none. DoD: the application-base form parses and type-checks under an expected type, with a regression sample (application base + punned field) on the default backends; a base that still cannot be typed reports the existing ETY-MetavarsNotAllowedInRecordWith. Next step: find the record-with base parser (RawRecordWith construction) and widen its base from a simple term to an application.")
inl note_of_record_with_application_base_2 () = Note ("RECORD-WITH-APPLICATION-BASE", 2u32, "2026-11-11T01:21Z", "compiler", "11-10 21:2x compiler: DRAFTED drafts\\spiral\\RECORD-WITH-APPLICATION-BASE\\1-record-with-application-base.kitdo (1 replacement). The base parser was (read_small_var |>> rawv) <|> rounds next, so a parenthesized base { (origin s) with ... } already worked and only the bare application failed. Now a variable base takes any number of plain-variable or parenthesized arguments, folded into RawApply with a range spanning the call; with and the field accessors are not plain variables, so the argument loop stops where the update begins. pack99 = pack89 + this (core b470e209), queued last on ganymede: probes app (want exit 8), both (12), pun (12) on C, then the suite vs pack89 (a parser change must show 0 diffs). Next step: read ~/remote-stage/pack99/g.log at \"p99 done\".")
