inl xsans_shape_fidelity () = Task ("XSANS-SHAPE-FIDELITY", "XSans letterforms, spacing, coverage and weight match the user X screenshots (SANS-FONT-FIDELITY matched only vertical bands)", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE,XSANS-SIDEBEARINGS,XSANS-ADVANCES,XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS,XSANS-CURVE-QUALITY,XSANS-STEM-WEIGHT,XSANS-BOLD-FACE,XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_shape_fidelity () = Planning ("XSANS-SHAPE-FIDELITY", Minutes 900u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_shape_fidelity_1 () = Note ("XSANS-SHAPE-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "USER 11-10 22:1x: \"make the fonts even more faithful with the screenshots, they are still weird\". SANS-FONT-FIDELITY matched only VERTICAL bands (x-height 531, round 547/16, caps 710/735); shapes, spacing, coverage and weight were never compared. Measured 11-10 22:2x on the live font (woff2 5f64b39b, ttf 8967d600) vs the reference crop ref-crops/zoom-lowercase-conductor-line1.png, our line rendered with HarfBuzz at the matched 45 px: ink columns 1111 ref vs 907 ours (glyph bodies ~18% narrow), in-word letter gap mean 4.18 px ref vs 5.83 ours (~40% loose), gaps of 9 px or more 15 ref vs 24 ours, stems 4-5 px ref vs 3-4 ours. Root causes are split into the child items: XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE, XSANS-SIDEBEARINGS, XSANS-ADVANCES, XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS, XSANS-CURVE-QUALITY, XSANS-STEM-WEIGHT, XSANS-BOLD-FACE, XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE. Glyph drawings stay our own; Chirp is only a local measurement reference, never shipped. DoD: every child Done and XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE green on the deployed font: letter-gap mean and ink-column ratio within 5% of the reference crop, 0 missing ASCII, and a side-by-side sheet of the reference crops vs ours reviewed with the user. NEXT: XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE first (visible in nearly every post), then sidebearings and advances.")
inl xsans_ascii_coverage () = Task ("XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE", "XSans covers all printable ASCII and common text punctuation (26 ASCII missing today: comma, apostrophe, quotes, parens, question mark, slash ...)", TaskKind, P0, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_ascii_coverage () = Planning ("XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_ascii_coverage_1 () = Note ("XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "The live font misses 26 of 95 printable ASCII: double quote, $ % &, apostrophe, ( ) * +, comma, / ; < = > ?, [ backslash ] ^ _, backtick, { | } ~. It also misses common text punctuation: U+00A0 nbsp, U+00A9, U+00AB and U+00BB, U+00B0, U+2013 and U+2014 dashes, U+2018 U+2019 U+201C U+201D curly quotes, U+2026 ellipsis, U+2022 bullet, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2192, U+00BF and U+00A1. Chrome draws each from the next family in the stack (Segoe UI on Windows), so a post like \"faster, buys\" mixes two faces mid-line. This is the most frequent weirdness: comma and apostrophe appear in most posts. Measure each from the reference crops (height, width, baseline offset) before drawing; a wrong glyph regresses vs a correct fallback (lesson from the @ v1). DoD: the coverage check (HarfBuzz collectUnicodes over 0x20-0x7E plus the list above) prints missing 0; each new glyph is raster-compared vs a reference crop at 15 px and 45 px; maxp v1.0; all existing advances unchanged (additive). NEXT: crop comma, apostrophe, quotes, parens, question mark and slash from the 06:04 and 06:05 screenshots and author them in lib/font_glyph.spi.")
inl xsans_sidebearings () = Task ("XSANS-SIDEBEARINGS", "XSans glyphs carry real left sidebearings (today lsb = 0 on every glyph, all spacing on the right)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "XSANS-ASCII-COVERAGE", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_sidebearings () = Planning ("XSANS-SIDEBEARINGS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_sidebearings_1 () = Note ("XSANS-SIDEBEARINGS", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "Every glyph has left sidebearing 0: the emitter normalizes each outline xMin to 0 (the same step behind the GPOS mark-anchor gotcha), so all spacing sits on the right. Measured lsb/rsb: n 0/142, o 0/165, e 0/200, a 0/195, g 0/230, i 0/145, H 0/142, M 0/144. Letters sit flush on the left and float apart on the right, so the spacing looks uneven. Fix: emit a real lsb per glyph (balanced, or from the Chirp lsb/rsb table measured once from the local copy) and keep the advance. RISK: the GPOS anchors were authored against the normalized coords (mark anchor = stored half-width: anusvara 48, chandrabindu 120; per-consonant bottom anchors 472/280/300/230), so re-derive them in the same change and re-run the Devanagari shaping set (the mark.js words). DoD: lsb/rsb for a-z A-Z 0-9 within 10 units of the target table; HarfBuzz shaping of the Devanagari and Arabic sets places every mark within 5 units of its pre-change ink position; letter-gap mean on the conductor crop within 10% of 4.18 px at 45 px. NEXT: read the xMin normalization in apps/font-emit/font_emit.spi finish() and list every anchor that depends on it.")
inl xsans_advances () = Task ("XSANS-ADVANCES", "XSans advance and ink widths match the Chirp table per glyph (n -83, H -167, M -173, period -67 units today)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "XSANS-SIDEBEARINGS", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_advances () = Planning ("XSANS-ADVANCES", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_advances_1 () = Note ("XSANS-ADVANCES", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "Advances differ from Chirp (units per 1000; Chirp values from the 11-08 one-off measure in SPIRAL-GROTESQUE-FONT n4): n 480 vs 563 (-83), H 560 vs 727 (-167), M 690 vs 863 (-173), w 680 vs 734 (-54), period 250 vs 317 (-67), e 560 vs 539 (+21), a 560 vs 543 (+17), g 560 vs 515 (+45), t 400 vs 356 (+44); o, i, l and space already match. Ink is narrower than the advance on most glyphs (o ink 400 in 565), which is why the bodies look ~18% narrow. Fix the BODY widths, not only the advance: widening the advance alone just adds gap. Step 1: measure the full Chirp table once (advance, lsb, xMin, xMax for every ASCII glyph) from the local copy, kept in a local file outside every repo. DoD: advance within 5 units and ink width within 15 units of the table for every ASCII glyph; total width of the conductor line within 1% of the reference crop. NEXT: locate the local Chirp copy (management measured it 11-08) and write the table.")
inl xsans_letterform_joins () = Task ("XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS", "XSans glyphs are single connected strokes: b d p q j k N M S G f y come apart or misassemble at display size", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_letterform_joins () = Planning ("XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_letterform_joins_1 () = Note ("XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "Rendered at 110 px (HarfBuzz outlines, nonzero fill), several glyphs come apart or misassemble: b d p q stems detached from their bowls (a visible gap in \"play\"), j and k disconnected, a gap in the N diagonal, M broken, S reads as a 5, the G inner bar misplaced, the f hook floating, y a straight v with a stick tail, @ boxy. First confirm the cause per glyph: a contour with the wrong winding cancels an overlap under nonzero fill (Chrome and FreeType fill the same way), as opposed to a real coordinate gap; dump the contour directions with skrifa. DoD: connected ink components per glyph equal the expected count (1 for most letters, 2 for i j ! ? ; : and similar), checked by XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE; a 110 px sheet of a-z A-Z 0-9 shows no gaps and is reviewed against the screenshot crops. NEXT: render each listed glyph alone, count its components, and log the winding of each contour.")
inl xsans_curve_quality () = Task ("XSANS-CURVE-QUALITY", "XSans bowls and arcs are smooth (c o e s n u read angular or squared today)", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_curve_quality () = Planning ("XSANS-CURVE-QUALITY", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_curve_quality_1 () = Note ("XSANS-CURVE-QUALITY", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "Curves read angular: c renders close to a < shape, the o u n bowls look squared, and s looks angular. The arc helpers lower each quarter arc into few quadratic segments, and the bowls flatten at the shoulders. Compare at 45 px and 110 px against the conductor and out-of-fuel crops. DoD: max deviation of each bowl from a true ellipse arc under 4 units (segment count raised where needed); c o e s a n u look round in the side-by-side sheet; quad-count growth per glyph recorded. NEXT: measure how far arc_ring_c and ellipse_contour lowering deviate from a true arc in lib/font_glyph.spi.")
inl xsans_stem_weight () = Task ("XSANS-STEM-WEIGHT", "XSans regular stem weight matches Chirp (ours is ~10-15% light)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "XSANS-ADVANCES", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_stem_weight () = Planning ("XSANS-STEM-WEIGHT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_stem_weight_1 () = Note ("XSANS-STEM-WEIGHT", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "Stems measure 3-4 px on ours vs 4-5 px on the reference at 45 px (most frequent horizontal ink run: 4 px x368 ours; 4 px x281 and 5 px x256 ref), so the regular face is ~10-15% light. Measure the Chirp n and H stem widths in units once, then set the stem constants in lib/font_glyph.spi. DoD: stem width of n, l and H within 5 units of the measured target; the run-length histogram on the conductor crop matches the reference mode within 0.5 px. NEXT: measure the Chirp stem widths together with the XSANS-ADVANCES table.")
inl xsans_bold_face () = Task ("XSANS-BOLD-FACE", "XSans bold 700 face for display names and headers (today Chrome fakes bold from the 400 face)", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "XSANS-STEM-WEIGHT,XSANS-LETTERFORM-JOINS", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_bold_face () = Planning ("XSANS-BOLD-FACE", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_bold_face_1 () = Note ("XSANS-BOLD-FACE", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "The timeline declares one @font-face (weight 400) but uses font-weight 700 for display names (article strong) and 800 for h1, so Chrome synthesizes a faux bold by smearing the regular outlines; the reference names use a real bold. Build a 700 face (stroke-offset embolden in the emitter, or bolder stems, with per-glyph advance growth measured from the local Chirp bold) and add a second @font-face at weight 700 in x/apps/client/timeline_page.spi (microblog). DoD: sans-bold.woff2 served on pluto, the page requests it for names, name widths in the name-handle-date crop within 2 px of the reference, maxp v1.0. NEXT: measure the Chirp bold stems and advances from the local copy.")
inl xsans_fidelity_gate () = Task ("XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE", "Font build gate in Spiral asserts XSans coverage, advances, sidebearings, components and stems against targets", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "font,alphabet,timeline,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsans_fidelity_gate () = Planning ("XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsans_fidelity_gate_1 () = Note ("XSANS-FIDELITY-GATE", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:44Z", "microblog", "Every fidelity number in XSANS-SHAPE-FIDELITY was measured by hand with scratch scripts. Make it a gate written in Spiral (spiral-first; no new .ps1, .py or .js in repos): test cells in apps/font-emit that read the built TTF through skrifa and assert (1) cmap coverage of the ASCII and punctuation list, (2) per-glyph advance and lsb vs the target table, (3) the connected-component count per glyph, (4) the stem width of n, l and H. The Chirp table stays a local file outside the repos; only our own targets are written in the test. The reference-crop raster compare stays a manual review step. DoD: the gate runs in the font build on a node, fails today on coverage and lsb, and turns green as the child items land. NEXT: list the skrifa calls the existing finish() round-trip uses and add the coverage assertion first.")
