inl note_of_cells_parity_tests_in_spiral_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PARITY-TESTS-IN-SPIRAL", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:45Z", "microblog", "Since 11-08 the port slices added 13 Elixir parity tests (601 lines: memo_shape_parity 187, compiler_compile_parity 67, compiler_banner_parity 62, compiler_pool_parity 45, compiler_status_parity 40, targets_manifest_parity 35, cell_weight_parity 32, targets_zig_release 29, memo_shim_parity 29, targets_phase_split 27, result_json_safe 24, server_test 14, phase_rows 10). Each keeps the old Elixir implementation alive as an oracle inside the test, so the old code never dies. New rule for every slice: prove parity ONCE against the corpus on a node (record the counts in the item note, e.g. memo D2-D6 0 differences over 134,735 blocks), then delete the oracle and keep golden cases as Spiral test cells in spi/*.spi next to the ported function. DoD: the 13 files are gone or reduced to a thin integration test that calls Spiral.Cells.Domain only; the same cases run as ///> gleam test cells in spi/memo.spi, spi/daemon.spi, spi/gleam_project.spi and spi/notebook.spi; the Cells gate is green on a node; .exs lines at or below the 11-08 count. NEXT: start with memo_shape_parity_test.exs (largest): extract its golden blocks into memo.spi tests and delete the regex oracle.")
