inl note_of_cells_retroport_11_10_1 () = Note ("CELLS-RETROPORT-11-10", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:45Z", "microblog", "New behavior added in Elixir since 11-08 that belongs in spi/*.spi with only a passthrough left in Elixir. MICROBLOG (this lane, 11-10): targets.ex phase split (target_build_ms, target_run_ms) and run_zig_release behind SPIRAL_CELLS_ZIG_RELEASE; notebook.ex keep_phase_row and the phase-key wire; cells.ex timed made public; the compiler_client.ex wrappers around status_row, compile_row, pool_row and hello_row. OTHER LANES (grow since 11-08; owners to be confirmed in the agent sync, then each gets its own slice): manifest.ex +33, cell_budget_ruled.ex +25, directives.ex +23, cell_budget.ex +15, compiler_daemon.ex +14, mounts.ex +8, result.ex +6, server.ex +4. Each port keeps the shell effects (File, System.get_env, ports) in a thin Elixir call and moves every decision (env parsing, phase math, row building, flag choice) into Spiral. DoD: each listed function decision lives in a Spiral export, and apps/cells .ex lines are at or below the 11-08 count (11,221) as CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET reports; Cells gate green on a node. NEXT: port the targets.ex zig-release flag choice and the phase-split arithmetic into spi/targets.spi first (the smallest, already parity-covered).")
inl cells_elixir_ratchet_2 () = Task ("CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET-2", "Cells Elixir ratchet without holes: HEAD-derived, counts .ex .exs .ps1, runs on every landing path, no CELLS-PORT exemption (grew +128/+748/+134 since 11-08)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 0u32, Planned, "CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET", "cells,kit,spiral,ratchet,team:microblog", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_elixir_ratchet_2 () = Planning ("CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET-2", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_elixir_ratchet_2_1 () = Note ("CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET-2", 1u32, "2026-11-11T03:46Z", "microblog", "USER 11-10 22:3x: \"we are still adding a lot of new ex and exs code instead of going spiral first, this way the migration will never finish\" (the second time after 11-07, which produced CELLS-ELIXIR-RATCHET, Done). The 11-07 ratchet did not hold. MEASURED in spiral/apps/cells vs the last commit bf5cc30a (11-08), staged plus unstaged: .ex 11,221 -> 11,349 (+128), .exs 7,637 -> 8,385 (+748, 13 new test files), .ps1 1,413 -> 1,547 (+134), .spi 5,315 -> 5,809 (+494). Grew: manifest.ex +33, cells.ex +31, notebook.ex +27, cell_budget_ruled.ex +25, directives.ex +23, targets.ex +20, cell_budget.ex +15, compiler_daemon.ex +14, compiler_client.ex +14, domain.ex +12; shrank: fsi_chain.ex -60, memo.ex -26, builders.ex -19. HOLES in the 11-07 ratchet: (1) it lives only in cells_land_window.ps1, and lanes (microblog included, 11-10) land slices by direct copy after a base check, so it never ran; (2) it counts lib .ex only, so .exs tests and .ps1 are free; (3) it exempts every CELLS-PORT-* label, which is exactly where the growth came from; (4) it measures the land delta, so a no-op applier reads 0. FIX: a check written in Spiral as a kit check (no new .ps1 or .py) that derives the baseline from git HEAD per file touched by the slice, counts .ex, .exs and .ps1 lines under apps/cells, and refuses growth with NO label exemption; the only allowed .ex addition is one domain.ex passthrough line per new Spiral export. It runs in every landing path: cells_land_window, the lane base-check copy (kit lane land or its equivalent), and the gate summary, so a direct copy cannot skip it. TYPEFEATURES: verdict is a union (Shrunk | Flat | Grew of list of file deltas), never a bool or exit string; the file kind is a union (Ex | Exs | Ps1). DoD: the check refuses the current tree and names the grown files; it passes after CELLS-RETROPORT-11-10 and CELLS-PARITY-TESTS-IN-SPIRAL; a fixture test covers grow, shrink, new file, passthrough allowance and no exemption for CELLS-PORT-*; proof is its output on both trees. NEXT: find where kit hosts its census checks and add the per-file HEAD line counter there.")
inl compiler_warn_surface () = Task ("COMPILER-WARN-SURFACE", "Compiler warnings reach the lanes: a SPIRAL_WARNINGS_OUT TSV (code, path, line, col, message, fix span) beside SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT, per-repo warning counts in the census with a baseline that only shrinks, Cells/rig gate lines and the CI job summary print them; today WTY-* go to stderr only, for the entry package only, capped at 50 with a suffix-specific overflow line, and are dropped whenever there is any error, so lanes clean them by grep", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,warnings,diagnostics,ci,census", "current", "current")
