inl note_of_compiler_warn_surface_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARN-SURFACE", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:12Z", "compiler", "DoD: (1) SPIRAL_WARNINGS_OUT writes one TSV row per warning across ALL packages built, not just the entry; (2) warnings are kept when other blocks have errors; (3) the 50 cap and the suffix-specific overflow line become per-code; (4) census/Cells gate line prints warnings=N per code with a baseline that only shrinks; (5) CI job summary lists counts. Evidence of need: printing at spiral_compiler.fs ~37616-37635 (literal_warnings, gated on List.isEmpty entry_errors). TypeFeatures: warning_code union + warning_row nominal on the rig side. Next step: read the references recorder (~8427) and mirror its exit-time writer for warnings.")
inl compiler_warn_unused_open () = Task ("COMPILER-WARN-UNUSED-OPEN", "WTY-UnusedOpen: warn on a top-level open (:< in the i574n dialect, open upstream) from which the module resolves no name, with the open line as fix span; resolution data already exists in the references recorder (open-resolved names); edge cases: opens used only for types, operators, union cases, prototype instances or only by test cells", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,warnings,diagnostics,lint", "current", "current")
