inl note_of_compiler_warn_unused_open_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARN-UNUSED-OPEN", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:12Z", "compiler", "DoD: fixtures positive (open of a module whose names are all unused) and negatives (open used only for a type, an operator, a union case in a pattern, a prototype instance, only from a test cell); suite 0 compile-status diffs; a census over lib, rig, x, fiscal, tibia with the count recorded as the baseline. Prior art: eoie_job_supervise dropped an unused open of rust_std_string.model by hand (KIT-LIB-REUSE note 31). TypeFeatures: none (compiler-side check). Next step: confirm the references recorder sees every name kind above, then draft the check over its open-resolved rows.")
inl compiler_warn_rec_marker_local () = Task ("COMPILER-WARN-REC-MARKER-LOCAL", "WTY-UnneededRecMarker beyond top-level single definitions: today it fires only for a top-level BundleRecInl outside upstream dialect and outside shadowing (spiral_compiler.fs infer ~5776); extend it to local recursive bindings (:~ ^ inside a body), :& group members outside the cycle, and autoExport packages, so the editor flags what rig_rec_cycle finds by text", TaskKind, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "REC-MARKER-INFER", "team:compiler,compiler,warnings,diagnostics,rec", "current", "current")
