inl note_of_compiler_warn_rec_marker_local_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARN-REC-MARKER-LOCAL", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:12Z", "compiler", "DoD: fixtures for a local :~ ^ that never calls itself (warns), one that does (silent), a :& member outside the cycle (warns), an autoExport package (warns); suite 0 diffs; rig_rec_cycle findings and the compiler warning agree on a census of rig, lib and tibia. TypeFeatures: none. Next step: find where local recursive bindings are inferred and reuse the validate_bound_vars self-reference test from the top-level arm.")
inl compiler_warn_unused_binding () = Task ("COMPILER-WARN-UNUSED-BINDING", "WTY-UnusedBinding: warn on a local := binding or a match/lambda pattern variable that is never read (a leading underscore opts out), like F# 1182 and Rust unused_variables; type-level and effect-only bindings need a rule, measured on the suite before landing", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,warnings,diagnostics", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_warn_unused_binding () = Planning ("COMPILER-WARN-UNUSED-BINDING", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_warn_unused_binding_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARN-UNUSED-BINDING", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:13Z", "compiler", "DoD: rule for what counts as unused (a binding read only at type level counts as read; effect-only := needs a _ name); fixtures both ways; suite measured before landing (count per sample, no compile-status change); heal plan for the top repos via RIG-WARNINGS-FIX. Related: X-DONE note 16 measured 183 dead lets in generated Rust (1.6%), the codegen side of the same drift. TypeFeatures: none. Next step: census-only mode first (count, do not print), over the suite.")
inl compiler_warn_unreachable_arm () = Task ("COMPILER-WARN-UNREACHABLE-ARM", "WTY-UnreachableArm: warn on a match arm that an earlier arm already covers (after a catch-all variable or _, or a repeated union case with no guard), from the source patterns only, not from partial-evaluation pruning; today no source-level unreachable or redundant-arm diagnostic exists", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,warnings,diagnostics,patterns", "current", "current")
