inl note_of_compiler_warnings_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-WARNINGS", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:12Z", "compiler", "11-11 compiler groom (user: warnings for unused opens, unnecessary recursive marks, etc.; cleanups happen often, by grep). Found first: WTY-UnneededRecMarker (pack63, REC-MARKER-INFER Done; top-level only) and WTY-RedundantLiteralSuffix are the only compiler warnings; rig_rec_cycle (REC-MARKER-HEAL) refuses stray ^ by text; KIT-OPEN-SHADOW-LINT covers shadowing opens; no unused-open, unused-binding, unreachable-arm or unused-definition diagnostic exists anywhere. Gap is twofold: missing warnings, and the existing ones are invisible (stderr, entry package, cap 50, dropped on any error), which is why fixes stay manual. DoD: every child Done; census shows per-repo warning counts that only shrink; lanes stop filing grep cleanups. TypeFeatures: warning code union and row nominal on the rig side; none in the compiler core. Next step: COMPILER-WARN-SURFACE first, since every other child is only useful once warnings are counted.")
inl rig_new_id_prefix_guard () = Task ("RIG-NEW-ID-PREFIX-GUARD", "agile add and agile rename refuse a NEW id starting KIT- or EOIE- (hint: use RIG-), and agile lint reports any KIT- id whose first note is after 2026-11-08T23:40Z; pulled forward from KIT-NEXT-NAME-R8 so the rename stops regrowing while trains are red", TaskKind, P0, D1, 80u32, Active, "", "team:rig,rig,rename,naming,agile", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rig_new_id_prefix_guard () = Planning ("RIG-NEW-ID-PREFIX-GUARD", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rig_new_id_prefix_guard_1 () = Note ("RIG-NEW-ID-PREFIX-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:18Z", "compiler", "11-11 compiler groom (user 11-11: why are we still using kit instead of rig? heal this also). Measured in state/agile.spi: about 40 items with a KIT- id were filed after the 11-08 rig decision (kit-split M-slices 11-09, KIT-HELP-POOL-HIDES-LEASES 11-10, rig D1 slices 11-10/11, and compiler KIT-WARNINGS-FIX 11-11, already renamed to RIG-WARNINGS-FIX); 378 KIT- ids vs 28 RIG- ids today. Cause: the only guard (R8 census word) is P2 and last in the chain behind R7, a user action, while R2/R4/R5 wait on trains that have been red since TRAIN41 (11-08), so lanes copy the dominant prefix. DoD: a new KIT-/EOIE- id is refused by add and as a rename target, with the RIG- hint; the lint row exists; tests in Spiral blocks; installed in the next green train. TypeFeatures: id_prefix_verdict union (Allowed | LegacyPrefix). Next step: rig lane drafts it for the train after TRAIN44b; until then every lane files RIG- ids by hand.")
inl note_of_rig_new_id_prefix_guard_2 () = Note ("RIG-NEW-ID-PREFIX-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-11-11T04:58Z", "rig", "11-11 00:5x rig: WRITTEN and node-green (unstaged; rides the next train). New linked unit src/rig_agile_id_prefix (prefix.spi: retired_prefix union KitPrefix/EoiePrefix in GADT form; new_id_refusal gives 'the KIT- id prefix is retired ...; use RIG-<rest>'; late_ids reads note 1 of every KIT-/EOIE- item and keeps those after 2026-11-08T23:40Z; retired_report gives the lines plus a count line; exports rig_agile_new_id_refusal and rig_agile_retired_report). agile add refuses before parsing the rest; agile rename refuses a retired NEW id (KIT-X to RIG-X still passes); agile lint prints the retired-prefix rows and 'rig agile lint retired-prefix ids=N' after its summary line. Moon (TRAIN44b pin, train25 mirror): prefix.spi 4/4, regen and cargo check exit 0 for the unit plus agile_task_creation, agile_task_rename, rig_agile_lint, rig_agile_mutation. Sizes: prefix 434, task_creation 912 (896 before), task_rename 870 (861), lint_cli 266 (263). The first, inlined version measured 981, 939 and 600, so the guard moved into a unit. Cargo.toml workspace member and three path deps added, Cargo.lock refreshed offline. Takes effect when the next train installs.")
inl lib_home_census () = Task ("LIB-HOME-CENSUS", "Census every lib/spiral module by consumer repo and give each single-repo cluster a placement verdict (stay generic in spiral lib, or move to the owner repo lib)", Story, P0, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "lib,dedup,org-structure,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_home_census () = Planning ("LIB-HOME-CENSUS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_home_census_1 () = Note ("LIB-HOME-CENSUS", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: one typed census row per lib/spiral module (lines, consumer repos with file counts, lib-internal users) regenerated by a kit standards finding, plus a verdict per cluster; the finding flags any lib module whose only consumers sit in one repo. Seed (org2 11-11 00:2x, git ls-files .spi/.spir of dice fiscal x tibia html regex blog alphabet spiral-apps, token scan for M:: / :< M / open M, lib-internal uses not counted): 154 modules. ZERO outside consumers (lib-internal or dead): ui_signals, ui_view, ui_dom, ui_dom_ts, xpath_eval 1930 lines, xsd_certificate, xsd_constraints, near_workspaces, erlang_port, otp_supervisor, keccak, iggy and lib infrastructure (testing, trace, common, seq, stream...). ONE consumer repo: regex cluster (regex_charset 7 files, regex_syntax 7, regex_derivative 7, regex_dfa 6, regex_certificate 4, regex_language 4, regex_minimal 3, regex_nullable 3, regex_table 1, regex_xsd 1, bench_model 1, fin_vector 1) = regex only; fiscal cluster (xsd_emit 5121 lines, xsd_regex 1116, xsd 771, xsd_resolve 683, json_schema 654, schematron 607, xml_codec 437 in 45 fiscal files, schematron_run, xsd_census, ledger, event_log, money, decimal, durable_file, round_trip, xpath 1038) = fiscal only, about 13k lines; dice: near, sm'_real, digest; tibia: occupancy, step_runtime, heap_scope, fixed_views, bitset, pickler, platform, json_scan; x: wire 18 files, tlds, erlang_http(_server), erlang_map, erlang_text, cursor_walk, oauth, crypto, unix_clock, json; spiral apps: parsing 1330, reactors, math, clap, store. Rule for the verdict: a module is generic (stays) when its concept is language-level (collections, text, json, process, testing); it moves when it is a product's domain (an engine, a standard's stack, a protocol) even if generic-looking. Next step: write the finding in rig (kit standards) so the census is a command, not a scratch script. TypeFeatures: verdict as a closed union (Generic | OwnerRepo repo | Dead) indexed by module, consumers as typed rows.")
inl regex_lib_home () = Task ("REGEX-LIB-HOME", "The regex engine lives in the regex repo as its own lib package (reverses REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB): regex_* and bench_model leave lib/spiral, consumers reach them through deps/regex", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-HOME-CENSUS", "regex,lib,dedup,org-structure,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_lib_home () = Planning ("REGEX-LIB-HOME", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_lib_home_1 () = Note ("REGEX-LIB-HOME", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:1x: \"same thing about regex wtf, each repo need its own lib when appropriate\". The 11-07 decision (REGEX-CORE-INTO-LIB n1, read from \"everything should reuse from everything\") moved regex's core INTO spiral lib; the user's rule is that reuse goes through the owning repo's lib package, not into one shared lib. Census (LIB-HOME-CENSUS): every regex_* module and bench_model are used by the regex repo alone; lib xsd_regex and fiscal are the only other link. Mechanism already exists: repos carry deps/<repo> junctions (dice has deps/polyglot and deps/hyperui), and spiral.toml packages take relative paths, so fiscal gets deps/regex and a package entry for regex's lib folder. DoD: regex/lib (spiral.toml, one package) holds charset, syntax, nullable, derivative, dfa, minimal, table, language, certificate, xsd (bodies byte-identical except headers/opens; regex_ prefix dropped inside its own repo if the names stay clear); regex/src, units and bench open it; lib/spiral copies archived (never deleted) with their layers rows; fiscal and lib xsd_regex reach the engine through deps/regex or xsd_regex moves to fiscal (decided in XML-STACK-HOME); regex CI and fiscal CI clone the dep the way they clone spiral; regex tests green on a node, fiscal xsd_regex suite green. Next step: draft regex/lib/spiral.toml and the fiscal deps/regex junction on a node copy, gate regex tests. Supersedes REGEX-LIB-4-XSD-GAPS and REGEX-LIB-5-SWITCH (paused); FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER keeps its API goal but points at the regex package. TypeFeatures: unchanged engine; the package boundary is a typed linked unit (rx_syntax precedent).")
inl ui_lib_home () = Task ("UI-LIB-HOME", "The reactive UI stack (ui_signals, ui_view, ui_dom, ui_dom_ts) moves from lib/spiral to the html repo, on ONE html model: ui_view renders through typed markup instead of its own escape and string tags", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-HOME-CENSUS", "ui,html,lib,dedup,org-structure,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ui_lib_home () = Planning ("UI-LIB-HOME", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_ui_lib_home_1 () = Note ("UI-LIB-HOME", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:1x: \"ain't the new ui files in lib conflicting with the html repo? which lane did this?\". Answer: org2 (this session) drafted ui_signals/ui_dom/ui_dom_ts and landed all four (rig drafted ui_view) on 11-09/11-10 under SPIRAL-UI, into lib/spiral. Conflicts found: (1) HTML-REPO's own title names the html repo as the home of the leptos/tachys front end, so the stack sits in the wrong repo; (2) ui_view.spi:139 has its own escape and attribute/tag string rendering next to lib markup.spi (typed markup, entity) that html_render already uses, so there are two HTML models and two escapers; (3) zero consumers outside lib (census), the dice table proof was a lib test. DoD: html/ui (spiral.toml package) holds signals, view, dom, dom_ts; view renders to markup (no raw string HTML, no second escape); lib/spiral copies archived with their layers rows; html and its CI green; nothing in lib imports them. Next step: diff ui_view render against html_render/markup and write the unified render on a node copy of the html repo. TypeFeatures: view stays a GADT indexed by content model; markup is the only trusted-text type.")
inl physics_home () = Task ("PHYSICS-HOME", "Physics gets the right home: generic numerics (derivative, integration, euler, euler-cromer, runge-kutta steppers) go to lib, mechanics to its own physics package, and plot keeps only the renderer", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-HOME-CENSUS", "physics,lib,plot,org-structure,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_physics_home () = Planning ("PHYSICS-HOME", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_physics_home_1 () = Note ("PHYSICS-HOME", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:1x: \"why was physics lib moved to plot? is it really the best move?\". It was org2's call on 11-09 (PHYSICS-OUT-OF-LIB n3), and it is not the best move: the DoD said \"its own app package\", and org2 put it in apps/plot because plot's renderer takes the same series shape. physics.spi is 1185 lines of a physics course: generic numeric methods (derivative variants, integration, euler, euler_cromer, runge_kutta shifts, vec sums) plus mechanics (state_1d, forces, velocity models) plus 3 plot series demos. Putting it under plot couples a domain to its renderer. DoD: lib gets the numeric methods as a typed module (after a lib grep for math/derivative duplicates), generic over a state prototype; spiral/apps/physics (own spiral.toml) holds mechanics on top of it; apps/plot holds only plot.rs and its series contract, and the physics series demos call it as a consumer; the 43 Cells tests still pass, split across the two packages. Next step: map each of physics.spi's definitions to numeric / mechanics / demo. TypeFeatures: a prototype for the state space (vector ops), stepper as a function over it, units as phantom-indexed f64 (mass, time, position, velocity are bare f64 aliases today).")
inl xml_stack_home () = Task ("XML-STACK-HOME", "Decide the home of the fiscal-only XML stack in lib/spiral (xsd, xsd_emit, xsd_resolve, xsd_regex, xsd_census, xsd_certificate, xsd_constraints, xpath, xpath_eval, schematron, schematron_run, xml_codec; about 13k lines)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-HOME-CENSUS", "xml,xsd,fiscal,lib,org-structure,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xml_stack_home () = Planning ("XML-STACK-HOME", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xml_stack_home_1 () = Note ("XML-STACK-HOME", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: one verdict, recorded here and applied: (a) the stack stays in spiral lib as generic XML-standards code, (b) it moves to fiscal's own lib package, or (c) it becomes its own repo with its own lib (a NEW REPO is the user's call). Facts: fiscal is the only consumer of every module (xml_codec in 45 fiscal files); xpath_eval, xsd_certificate and xsd_constraints have zero outside consumers; the stack implements W3C standards, so it is generic in kind but single-product in use. org2 recommendation: (b) now, fiscal/lib, since a repo split can follow later without touching consumers twice. Next step: ask the user only if (c) is wanted; otherwise draft fiscal/lib on a node copy. TypeFeatures: unchanged; a move.")
inl note_of_xml_stack_home_2 () = Note ("XML-STACK-HOME", 2u32, "2026-11-11T05:01Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-11 01:2x VERDICT (b) fiscal's own lib package, agreed by fiscal (cross-session 11-11): the XML stack (xsd*, xpath*, schematron*, xml_codec) moves to a fiscal lib package, which also lets its land proofs gate inside fiscal. A separate repo was not wanted by either lane, so no user decision is needed. Next step: fiscal drafts fiscal/lib on a node copy when its next window opens; FISCAL-REGEX-LIB-ADAPTER re-proofs draft B175055B5C73 against deps/regex, not the old lib home.")
inl lib_home_per_repo () = Task ("LIB-HOME-PER-REPO", "Each repo owns its domain lib (user 11-11): spiral lib keeps language-generic code only; a product domain (regex engine, UI stack, XML stack, physics) lives in its owner repo as that repo's lib package, reached through deps/<repo>", Epic, P0, D6, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-HOME-CENSUS,REGEX-LIB-HOME,UI-LIB-HOME,PHYSICS-HOME,XML-STACK-HOME", "lib,dedup,org-structure,team:org", "current", "current")
