inl note_of_lib_home_per_repo_1 () = Note ("LIB-HOME-PER-REPO", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:21Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:1x verbatim: \"groom properly so we're sota org wise ... same thing about regex wtf, each repo need its own lib when appropriate, wth are you guys doing\". This refines lib-first: generic code still goes to spiral lib and is never copied into a consumer, but a product's engine stays in the product's repo and other repos reuse it as a package dependency. Precedent: dice already reaches polyglot and hyperui through deps junctions. DoD: every child closed; a kit standards finding refuses a NEW lib/spiral module whose census shows one owner repo, unless the land note gives the generic reason. Next step: LIB-HOME-CENSUS finding, then REGEX-LIB-HOME and UI-LIB-HOME in parallel on node copies. TypeFeatures: placement verdict as a closed union; package edges as typed manifest rows.")
inl ui_sota_matrix () = Task ("UI-SOTA-MATRIX", "Feature matrix of our UI stack against Leptos/tachys and reactive_graph (current release), row by row, with the typed-Spiral answer and its test for each row", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "UI-LIB-HOME", "ui,html,sota,team:org", "current", "current")
