inl note_of_ui_sota_matrix_1 () = Note ("UI-SOTA-MATRIX", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11: \"if we're going advanced things need to be even better than leptos/tachys considering the typefeatureset\". DoD: a typed matrix (one row per capability: fine-grained signals with automatic dependency tracking, memos, effects and batching, owner/cleanup scopes, async resources and Suspense/Transition, context, typed views, attributes, events with typed payloads, class/style directives, keyed lists, SSR string and streaming, hydration, islands, server functions, router), each row with Leptos's status read from its source (not from memory), ours, and the test that proves ours. Rows where we must WIN, because the typed model allows it and tachys does not do it: HTML content model checked by the view index (a div inside a span is a type error), per-tag attribute sets in the attr GADT, event payload typed by the event, and static subtrees staged at compile time. Next step: read leptos/tachys and reactive_graph in C:\\home\\git\\leptos at its latest tag and fill the Leptos column. TypeFeatures: the matrix itself is typed rows (capability union, status union).")
inl ui_sota_reactive () = Task ("UI-SOTA-REACTIVE", "Signals at reactive_graph parity or better: typed handles with automatic dependency tracking (no hand-listed deps ids), glitch-free ordered propagation, batching, owner scopes with cleanup, async resources", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "UI-SOTA-MATRIX", "ui,html,sota,team:org", "current", "current")
