inl granular_bone () = Task ("GRANULAR-BONE", "Granular to the bone: a written rule for new and touched definitions (one concept each, no control flow in any host text including shell scripts, typed ids instead of bare ints and strings), enforced on the lib land path, starting with the code landed 11-10", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "granular,lib,lint,team:org", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_granular_bone () = Planning ("GRANULAR-BONE", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_granular_bone_1 () = Note ("GRANULAR-BONE", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:1x: \"also we're still adding non fully granular code, it needs to go to the bone\". Evidence from org2's own 11-10 lands: (1) process.spi descendants_shell is a recursive shell function inside a Spiral string, so the tree walk, the loop and the recursion live in host text; to the bone means children_of pid (ONE host call: ps --ppid, parsed in Spiral), a Spiral recursion for descendants, and one kill call per pid; (2) kill_command and kill_args repeat the same platform decision; (3) pids are bare i32 and DOM node ids are bare i32 with string tag names in ui_dom dom_op; (4) long definitions remain in touched files: process.spi execute_with_options_rust 87 lines, split_args 47, stdio_line 46; json_real.spir decode_at 41. DoD: the rule written once (memory and the rig lint, not repo prose), with measurable checks (host text holds no loop, branch, recursion or pipe of commands; a definition does one thing and fits the cell budget; ids crossing a module are nominal types); the lib land path (lib_land_window) refuses a land whose NEW or CHANGED definitions fail them (ratchet on the diff only, so old debt never blocks); the 4 cases above healed and landed. Next step: heal (1)-(2) in process.spi on a node copy (org2 owns the regression), then the lint rule in rig. TypeFeatures: pid and node_id as nominal phantoms; host call kinds as a closed union in the lint.")
