inl note_of_rename_1111_tally_rig_1 () = Note ("RENAME-1111-TALLY-RIG", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:23Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:2x: \"also put in the backlog to rename tally in addition to probe, pick alternatives accordingly\". Replacements by meaning, picked by org2 (collision-checked with git grep in kit, tibia, spiral, x: breakdown 0 hits anywhere; counts and totals already carry the same meaning): (a) a record of named counts, e.g. kit claim tally {leased; lived}, tibia swing_tally {landed; total}, links_tally -> COUNTS (claim_counts, swing_counts, link_counts); (b) the fold step that adds one observation, e.g. tally_with, tallied_swing, tally_bump, tally_step -> COUNT verb (count_finding, counted_swing, count_step); (c) a per-kind histogram, e.g. tally_kind, tally_of over kinds -> BREAKDOWN; (d) an end-of-run totals line or print, e.g. compiler printTally, layoutTally -> TOTALS (printTotals, layoutTotals). Hard cut, no aliases; backlog history is not rewritten; external names stay. Ride the same cut as the open probe/digest rename where that item is still open. DoD: git grep -iw tally in kit returns 0 outside external names; kit builds and its tests pass. Next step: classify each tally identifier into (a)-(d). TypeFeatures: none; a rename.")
