inl note_of_rig_new_harvest_1 () = Note ("RIG-NEW-HARVEST", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:4x: the template \"should be sota considering the typefeatureset and the goodies from all projects\". DoD: a typed table (pattern, source repo and file, template slot, test that proves it) covering at least: x (typed command union entry points in the client shape; one GADT message family with byte-identical Rust and Gleam codecs; caller witnesses as phantom indices), fiscal (runtime choice dispatched into a generic per branch as in model_census; versioned persisted unions; event_log), rig (standards census per construct; typed agile rows; ratchets that only tighten), html (7-unit typed-units proof; content-model typed nodes), regex (linked unit with one exported union; laws and certificate tests), tibia (C oracle tests; gauge and trial split; occupancy-style dense models), Cells (test blocks per declared backend, executed-cells gate, a run-time data test beside every literal test), realworld (http request and response spine), alphabet and dice (whatever their census shows best), plus the mega samples as the construct-density target (M-scores). Each kept row names its GADT, existential, HKT, prototype, reflection or phantom use. Next step: rig drafts the row list from memories and the census, org lanes fill their own repo rows. TypeFeatures: rows typed by a pattern union and a construct union.")
inl note_of_rig_new_harvest_2 () = Note ("RIG-NEW-HARVEST", 2u32, "2026-11-11T04:54Z", "rig", "11-11 01:0x rig: DRAFT ROWS WRITTEN as a typed package, kit/src/rig_new_harvest/patterns.spi (unstaged, probe pending on moon). row v is a GADT over phantom kept/left_out: Kept :: pattern_fact * slot -> row kept; the scaffold will take only list (row kept), and a fails-Unification test proves a left-out row cannot reach it. 18 kept rows over 7 slots (ModelUnit, BoundaryUnit, FeatureUnit, BinUnit, OwnLib, TestBlocks, Ratchets), each with repo, file, proving test, constructs and the invariant it enforces; 12 of 18 use a typed construct, and a test holds that share at two thirds or more. Sources: x cli command union, wire.spi phantom caller witness, sim_events two-backend codec (plain unions; there is NO GADT codec family in x yet, so the template adds the GADT form itself); fiscal corpus_checks model_census; lib xsd_emit versioned witness and event_log; rig_boundary_census ratchet and run-time data test; html model page kind and render prototype; lib ui_view typed children; regex typed.spi certificate and laws.spi; tibia gpu_sim C oracle; realworld reply-indexed routes; dice phase-indexed plan; alphabet font_outline; typed-units one exported union. LEFT OUT: occupancy (GPU-only), mega samples (density target for the ratchet floor, not a file), and tibia's held-out seeds, held until the tibia lane names the proving test (the seed_block phantom is in src/hunting_pack.spi). Not found: a regex unit exporting a union. Next: the probe, then the org lanes confirm their rows, then SCAFFOLD splits per the RIG-NEW note.")
