inl note_of_rig_new_scaffold_1 () = Note ("RIG-NEW-SCAFFOLD", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "DoD: the command is Spiral (no .ps1 or text templates; spiral-first tooling) and writes: spiral.toml per unit and link: edges; a model unit that USES each construct for a real invariant (GADT with phantom indices, an existential pack chosen at compile time, a prototype with instances, nameof reflection), never as decoration; a boundary unit with a typed refusal union and one codec family generated for Rust and Gleam; a bin with a typed command union entry; a lib package for the repo's own domain reached by consumers through deps/<repo> (LIB-HOME-PER-REPO rule); test blocks on every declared backend with a run-time data test; CI as one entry with actions.lock; .gitignore covering target/ and build/ checked with git check-ignore; formatter clean; ratchets wired in from day one: at most 1000 generated lines per unit, construct census baseline that can only rise, granular rule on new definitions (GRANULAR-BONE), naming lexicon. Absorbs CELLS-NEW-PROJECT's DoD (a new project passes its own gate on the first run). Next step: after RIG-NEW-HARVEST, write the generator for the model unit first. TypeFeatures: the template itself is typed: unit kind as a closed union, link edges as typed rows, generated files as a GADT indexed by unit kind.")
