inl note_of_rig_new_1 () = Note ("RIG-NEW", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:40Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 00:4x on i574n.github/examples/typed-units: \"yeah groom with rig so this goes there. also it should be sota considering the typefeatureset and the goodies from all projects\". Today typed-units/1 exists only as prose in TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 notes plus a 119-line toy example that no tool references, so html and tibia follow it by hand and it can drift. DoD: all four children Done; no example folder remains in the org repo; a new repo starts from rig new and is green on its first build. Folds in: CELLS-NEW-PROJECT (scaffold), X-REPO-TEMPLATE (x's recorded template decisions feed RIG-NEW-HARVEST), TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET (ships inside the template). Next step: RIG-NEW-HARVEST. TypeFeatures: see children.")
inl note_of_rig_new_2 () = Note ("RIG-NEW", 2u32, "2026-11-11T04:41Z", "rig", "11-11 00:5x rig GROOM (owner now rig). Order stands: HARVEST then SCAFFOLD then GOLDEN then ADOPT. Corrections: (1) HARVEST's typed table is a rig package, src/rig_new_harvest (pattern union, construct union, row record of pattern, repo, proof file, template slot, constructs, proving test), not a markdown or joined-string table, because AGENTS.md's ratchet refuses joined-string rows; its tests check every row names at least one construct and one existing proof file read at run time. (2) SCAFFOLD (D5, 600m) splits after HARVEST lands, into M-slices: the edition model (the typed slot tree of typed-units/2 as data), the writer (rig new <dir> <name> through the fs boundary, no text templates), ratchets and census wired, the repo's own lib package plus deps/<repo> (LIB-HOME-PER-REPO). Each slice ships by train, so GOLDEN waits on the train that carries the verb. (3) The template's construct use must be load-bearing: each construct row names the invariant it enforces (the user's meaning: GADTs, existentials, HKTs, prototypes, reflection, phantom indices; never decoration). The current examples/typed-units has 4 units and about 119 .spi lines (tu, tu_model, tu_io, tu_feature; Rust and Gleam outputs); user-staged, so left untouched until GOLDEN archives it.")
