inl note_of_rig_crash_dump_watch_1 () = Note ("RIG-CRASH-DUMP-WATCH", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 01:0x: \"erl_crash.dump files are being left alone for days without being diagnosed then healed\". Found on the box 11-11 00:5x and diagnosed by org2 (dumps archived at LOCALAPPDATA kit archive crash-dumps-20261111):\n(1) C:\\home\\git\\erl_crash.dump, 11-07 13:40, OTP 29: boot failed scanning an -eval argument that reached erl as io:format(OTP... with its quotes stripped (not_character): an ad-hoc version check typed through a shell. No product bug; heal: version checks go through one rig toolchain gauge, never a hand -eval.\n(2) spiral/apps/cells/erl_crash.dump, 11-10 10:58, OTP 29: an Elixir Cells run died while printing its own error, because standard_error was gone (the device does not exist): the parent that owned its pipes had exited, so the real error (an ErlangError :terminated) reached no log. Heal: job-started Cells runs write stderr to a file in the job dir, not an inherited pipe; find the 10:58 job in the job list.\n(3) x/erl_crash.dump, 11-04 21:25: the sim server panicked in lib erlang_http_server request_of on a partial request (spiral string slice out of range, xsim_frames request_of_451). Already HEALED on 11-05 21:54 (lib test an_empty_or_partial_request_still_parses), but the dump sat for 6 days. after_prefix still slices with a computed length; GRANULAR-BONE covers the guard.\n(4) livebook/erl_crash.dump, 10-01, OTP 26: load_failed for kernel modules at boot, a runtime started against a missing OTP lib dir; stale, no action.\nOut of scope: cumbuquia and currency_converter dumps from 2024 (old repos outside the fleet).\nDoD: kit jobs set ERL_CRASH_DUMP to the job's own dir; a user-level ERL_CRASH_DUMP on every machine points ad-hoc runs at one crash folder; rig machine watch scans repos and that folder on the box, moon, ganymede and europa, extracts Slogan, Calling Thread and the top frames, archives the dump and writes a typed row (machine, time, class, owner lane, item) into the backlog within the hour; erl_crash.dump is in every repo's .gitignore through the template (RIG-NEW-SCAFFOLD). Next step: the slogan classifier as a typed union (BootArgs, LostStdio, Panic module fn line, LoadFailed, Oom) with these 4 dumps as its test fixtures. TypeFeatures: dump class as a closed union; per-class owner routing as a prototype.")
inl note_of_rig_crash_dump_watch_2 () = Note ("RIG-CRASH-DUMP-WATCH", 2u32, "2026-11-11T05:03Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "org2 11-11 01:3x microblog's check of dump (2), the Cells crash at 11-10 10:58: no kit job matches it, since every job started 10:30-11:00 ran on ganymede or wifi, not the box, and microblog's session ran no box Cells or mix run at 14:55-14:59Z. The dump died at boot, so it holds no notebook path or env. Most likely a box-local mix or run_notebook.ps1 started outside kit jobs whose parent pwsh exited first. So the heal must cover BARE starts too: run_notebook and mix entry points send stderr to a temp file themselves, not only kit jobs. Without a job dir the dump also needs the machine-level ERL_CRASH_DUMP folder to be found at all.")
