inl note_of_ledger_typed_home_1 () = Note ("LEDGER-TYPED-HOME", 1u32, "2026-11-11T04:59Z", "org-5a6e53fb", "User 11-11 01:0x: \".registration files in .github, geez\". They are org2's (CONV-PREREG, 11-09): 8 files in i574n.github/docs/ledger/convergence written by kit experiment register as key=value text (id, registered, question, test, metric, arms, runs, decision). Two drifts: untyped text where the backlog itself is typed Spiral data, and the wrong repo (the org tooling repo, not the lab). The registration itself (timestamped before any run) stays valuable and must survive with its original stamps. DoD: rig experiment register writes and reads typed rows (a registration record with a test union welch/one-sample/binomial/wilson and an arms list) in a .spi state file; the 8 registrations converted with their registered stamps unchanged; they live with the convergence lab (CONVERGENCE-LAB's home, per LIB-HOME-PER-REPO); the .registration files archived; analyze refuses a run that predates its registration as today. Next step: rig defines the row type; org2 converts and moves the 8. TypeFeatures: registration as a record with a statistical-test GADT indexed by its metric kind.")
